पुष्पवेणी
पुष्पवेणी f. (-णी) A garland of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशकटी
पुष्पशकटी f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. Raining flowers, on any great occasion of rejoicing<BR>in earth and heaven.<BR>	 2. A heavenly voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशय्या
पुष्पशय्या f. (-य्या) A flowery bed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशर|पुष्पशरः
पुष्पशर m. (-रः) KĀMADEVA, the god of love.<BR> E. पुष्प, and शर an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशरासन|पुष्पशरासनः
पुष्पशरासन m. (-नः) KĀMADEVA,<BR> E. पुष्प, and शरासन a quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशून्य|पुष्पशून्यः
पुष्पशून्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Not bearing flowers, flowerless.<BR>	 m. (-न्यः)<BR>The glomerous fig-tree.<BR> E. पुष्प, शून्य void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पशालिन्
पुष्पशालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Flowery.<BR> E. पुष्प, and शालिन् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पश्री
पुष्पश्री f. (-श्रीः) Abundance, or beauty of flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प, श्री wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पसमय|पुष्पसमयः
पुष्पसमय m. (-यः) Spring.<BR> E. पुष्प, and समय a season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पसायक|पुष्पसायकः
पुष्पसायक m. (-कः) The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पसार|पुष्पसारः
पुष्पसार m. (-रः) The nectar, or honey of flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प. and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पस्वेद|पुष्पस्वेदः
पुष्पस्वेद m. (-दः) The nectar, or honey of flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प, and स्वेद<BR>sweat, or exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पहासा
पुष्पहासा f. (-सा) A woman during menstruation.<BR> E. पुष्प, and हास who smiles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पहीन
पुष्पहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Flowerless, not flowering.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. The<BR>glomerous fig-tree.<BR>	 2. A woman whose menstruation has ceased<BR>a barren woman.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, &c. and हीन abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पा
पुष्पा m. (-ष्पा) The district of Bhāgalpur or the name of its capital<BR>champā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पागम|पुष्पागमः
पुष्पागम m. (-मः) The Spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाजीव|पुष्पाजीवः
पुष्पाजीव m. (-वः) A flowerman, a maker of garlands.<BR> E. पुष्प, and आजीव livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाजीविन्
पुष्पाजीविन् m. (-वी) A flowerman, a maker of garlands.<BR> E. पुष्प, आजीव<BR>livelihood, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाञ्जन|पुष्पांजन|पुष्पाञ्जनं
पुष्पाञ्जन n. (-नं) The calx of brass used as a collyrium.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, and अञ्जन collyrium. “कोम काजल” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाञ्जलि|पुष्पांजलि|पुष्पाञ्जलिः
पुष्पाञ्जलि mf. (-लिः-ली) Presenting a nosegay or flowers, held in both<BR>hands opened, and hollowed.<BR> E. पुष्प, and अञ्जलि the hands joined<BR>and opened; also similar compounds, as कुसुमाञ्जलि, प्रसूनाञ्जलि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पानन|पुष्पाननः
पुष्पानन m. (-नः) A kind of Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाम्बुज|पुष्पांबुज
पुष्पाम्बुज n. (-जं) The Sap of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पायुध|पुष्पायुधः
पुष्पायुध m. (-धः) The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पावचय|पुष्पावचयः
पुष्पावचय m. (-यः) Gathering flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प, and अवचय collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पावचायिन्
पुष्पावचायिन् mf. (-यी-यिनी) A flower-gatherer.<BR> E. पुष्प, and अवचायिन्<BR>who collects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाभिषेक
पुष्पाभिषेक m. (-कः) Bathing with flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पासव|पुष्पासवं
पुष्पासव n. (-वं) Honey.<BR> E. पुष्प, and आसव spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पासार|पुष्पासारः
पुष्पासार m. (-रः) A shower of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पास्त्र|पुष्पास्त्रः
पुष्पास्त्र m. (-स्त्रः) KANDARPA, the Hindu Cupid.<BR> E. पुष्प, and अस्त्र a wea-<BR>pon; pointing his darts with flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पाहर
पुष्पाहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Who or what takes flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प, and आहर who or what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिका
पुष्पिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The tartar of the teeth.<BR>	 2. The mucus of the<BR>glans penis, or urethra.<BR>	 3. The concluding words of a chapter.<BR>E. पुष्प a flower, कन् aff. of comparison, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिणी
पुष्पिणी f. (-णी) A woman in her courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पित|पुष्पितः
पुष्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Flowered, in flower.<BR>	 2. Florid, flowery.<BR>3. Completely manifested, fully developed.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A woman<BR>during menstruation.<BR> E. पुष्प, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिताग्रा
पुष्पिताग्रा f. (-ग्रा) A form of metre, a mixed kind and a variety of<BR>the Aupachandasika; the line consisting of four or six short<BR>syllables, a pyrrhic or a dactyl, two trochees and a spondee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पिन्
पुष्पिन् mfn. (-ष्पो-ष्पिणी-ष्पि)<BR>	 1. Flowering, bearing flowers.<BR>	 2. A bound-<BR>ing in flowers.<BR> E. पुष्प, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पेषु|पुष्पेषुः
पुष्पेषु m. (-षुः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. पुष्प, and इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पोद्गम|पुष्पोद्गमः
पुष्पोद्गम m. (-मः) The appearance of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पोद्यान
पुष्पोद्यान n. (-नं) A flower-garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्पोपजीविन्
पुष्पोपजीविन् m. (-वी) A florist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्प्य
पुष्प्य r. 4th. cl. (पुष्प्यति) To blossom. विकशने कण्ड्रा० पाठान्तरम् सक० सेट् ।.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्य|पुष्यः
पुष्य mf. (-ष्यः-ष्या)<BR>	 1. The eighth lunar asterism, comprising three<BR>stars, of which one is the Cancer.<BR>	 2. The month Pous, (Dec.<BR>and Jan.)<BR>	 3. The Kali, or fourth age.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish, aff. क्यप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्यरथ|पुष्यरथः
पुष्यरथ m. (-थः) Any sort of car or carriage, except a war chariot. E.<BR>पुष्य the asterism, and रथ a car; also पुष्परथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुष्यलक|पुष्यलकः
पुष्यलक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The musk-deer.<BR>	 2. A pin, a bolt, stake.<BR>	 3. A<BR>naked mendicant. It is read in some places पुष्कलक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस
पुस r. 10th cl. (पोषयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To rub.<BR>	 2. To damage, चुरा० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्त|पुस्तं
पुस्त r. 10th cl. (पुस्तयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To respect.<BR>	 2. To disregard, to treat<BR>with disrespect.<BR>	 3. To bind.<BR>	 4. To smear. चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्त|पुस्तं
पुस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Filled.<BR>	 2. Covered.<BR>	 n. (-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Smearing, anoin-<BR>ting, painting, plastering, &c.<BR>	 2. Any thing made of metal, wood<BR>or clay, &c.<BR>	 nf. (-स्तं-स्ती) A book, a manuscript.<BR> E. पुस्त to bind,<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तक|पुस्तकं|पुस्तकः
पुस्तक nf. (-कं-की) A book, a manuscript.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तकमुद्रा
पुस्तकमुद्रा f. (-द्रा) A particular position of fingers in religious worship.<BR>The posture is thus defined in Tantra sāra. viz.--“वाम मुष्टिं<BR>स्वाभिमुखीं कृत्वा पुस्तकमुद्रिका” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्तकर्म्मन्|पुस्तकर्मन्
पुस्तकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Plastering, painting, &c. see पुस्त.<BR> E. पुस्त as above, कर्म्मन् business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्ती
पुस्ती f. (-स्ती) A manuscript.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पुस्फुस
पुस्फुस m. (-सः) The lungs; also पुप्फुस and फुप्फुस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पू
पू(ङ)पूङ् r. 1st cl. (पवते)शोधे भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् । (ञ)पूञ् r. 9th cl. (पुनाति-<BR>पुनीते)<BR>	 1. To purify, to cleanse, physically or metaphorically.<BR>	 2. To<BR>clean from chaff, to winnow.<BR>	 3. To Discriminate, to discern.<BR>	 4. To<BR>invent, to think out, to contrive. क्र्यादि० प्वा० उभ० सक० सेट् । r. 4th cl.<BR>(पूयते) To grow or become pure. दिवा० आत्म० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूग|पूगं|पूगः
पूग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>heap, a quantity, a multitude.<BR>	 3. Disposition, property, nature.<BR>4. The Jack-tree.<BR>	 5. An association, a corporation.<BR>	 n. (-गं) The<BR>fruit of the faufel, the betel-nut.<BR> E. पू to cleanse, गन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगकृत
पूगकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Assembled, collected.<BR> E. पूग, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपात्र|पूगपात्रं
पूगपात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A betel-box.<BR>	 2. A spitting-spot.<BR> E. पूग, and पात्र a<BR>vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपीठ|पूगपीठं|पूगपीठः
पूगपीठ n. (-ठं) A spitting-pot.<BR> E. पूग betel, and पीठ a stool; chewing<BR>the pān producing an increased excretion of saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगपुष्पिका
पूगपुष्पिका f. (-का) Flowers and betel presented to the principal guests<BR>at a marriage festival.<BR> E. पूग, and पुष्प a flower, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगफल|पूगफलं
पूगफल n. (-लं) The Areca-nut.<BR> E. पूग, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगरोट|पूगरोटः
पूगरोट m. (-टः) The marshy date tree, (Phænix or Elate paludosa.) E.<BR>पूग Areca, and रुट् to shine, to resemble, aff. घञ; also with कन्<BR>added पुगरोटक. “हिन्ताल वृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूगवैर
पूगवैर n. (-रं) Enmity against a number of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्
पूज् r. 10th cl. (पूजयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To adore, to reverence, to worship.<BR>	 2. To<BR>present with. With सम्, 1. To pay respect to.<BR>	 2. To present with.<BR>चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजक|पूजकः
पूजक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Worshiping, a worshiper.<BR> E. पूज् to worship, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजत्
पूजत् mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्) Worshiping, reverencing.<BR> E. पूज् to wor-<BR>ship, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजन|पूजनं
पूजन n. (-नं) Worship, worshiping: see पूजा.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A sparrow.<BR> E. पूज् to worship, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजनीय
पूजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be worshiped or revered.<BR> E. पूज्, and<BR>अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजयितव्य
पूजयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be worshiped.<BR> E. पूज् to worship, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजयितृ
पूजयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Worshiping, a worshiper.<BR> E. पूज् to wor-<BR>ship, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजा
पूजा f. (-जा) Worship, culture, respect, homage of superiors or adora-<BR>tion of the gods.<BR> E. पूज् to worship, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजार्ह|पूजार्हः
पूजार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Worshipful, venerable, respectable, sacred. E.<BR>पूजा worship, अर्ह fit, deserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजित|पूजितः
पूजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Worshiped, adored, reverenced.<BR>	 2. Ac-<BR>knowledged.<BR>	 3. Endowed.<BR> E. पूज् to worship, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूजिल|पूजिलः
पूजिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Venerable, respectable, worshipful, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः) A deity.<BR> E. पूजा, and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्य|पूज्यः
पूज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) Worshipful, venerable, fit for or deserving<BR>adoration, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ज्यः) A father-in-law.<BR> E. पूज् to worship, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूज्यमान
पूज्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being reverenced or respected.<BR> E. पूज् to<BR>worship, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूण्
पूण् r. 10th cl. (पूणयति-ते) To accumulate, to collect or heap together. चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्
पूत् Ind. An imitative word expressive of hard breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=463-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्कारी
पूत्कारी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. The capital of the Nāgas.<BR>	 2. A name of SARASWATI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत|पूतं|पूतः
पूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pure, purified.<BR>	 2. Threshed, winnowed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Cleaned, cleansed.<BR>	 4. Speaking the truth, sincere, honest.<BR>5. Foul-smelling, stinking, putrid.<BR>	 6. Guarded, defended.<BR>	 7.<BR>contrived, composed.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Truth, speaking truth.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>conch-shell.<BR>	 2. White Kusa grass.<BR>	 m. du. (-तौ) The buttocks. E.<BR>पू to purify, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतक्रतायी
पूतक्रतायी f. (-यी) The wife of INDRA.<BR> E. पूतक्रतु INDRA, ङीप् aff; in place<BR>of उ, ऐच् is inserted, and then changed before ई to आय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतक्रतु|पूतक्रतुः
पूतक्रतु m. (-तुः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. पूत, pure, and क्रतु sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूततृण
पूततृण n. (-णं) White Kusa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतद्रु|पूतद्रुः
पूतद्रु m. (-द्रुः) The bread-fruit tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. पूत, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतधान्य|पूतधान्यं
पूतधान्य n. (-न्यं) Sesamum.<BR> E. पूत, and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतना
पूतना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>name of a female demon killed by KṚṢṆA, when he was but an<BR>infant on her attempting to take his life.<BR>	 3. A disease, atrophy<BR>and wasting in a child, ascribed to the malignant operations of<BR>the female fiend PŪTANĀ.<BR> E. पूत् to be pure, nominal verb, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतनारि|पूतनारिः
पूतनारि m. (-रिः) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. पूतना a female fiend, and अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतनासूदन|पूतनासूदनः
पूतनासूदन m. (-नः) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. पूतना, and सूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतनाहन्
पूतनाहन् m. (-हा) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. पूतना, and हन् who kills: see the<BR>three words preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतपाप
पूतपाप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Purified, freed from sin.<BR> E. पूत, and पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतपाप्मन्
पूतपाप्मन् mfn. (-प्मा-प्मा-प्म) Purified from sin.<BR> E. पूत, and पाप्मन् sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतफल|पूतफलः
पूतफल m. (-लः) The jack-tree.<BR> E. पूत fetid, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतात्मन्
पूतात्मन् m. (-त्मा)<BR>	 1. A saint, an ascetic, a pure or purified person.<BR>2. A man of a cleanly person, or purified by ablution.<BR>	 3. An<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR> E. पूत purified, आत्मन् spirit or self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूति|पूतिः
पूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Purity, purification.<BR>	 2. A stench, a stink, putrefac-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Civet.<BR>	 n. (-ति)<BR>	 1. Filthy water.<BR>	 2. Pus, matter. Adj. Putr-<BR>id, Stinking, ill-smelling.<BR> E. पू to be pure, or पूय to stink, aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूति|पूतिः
पूति(ती)क m. (-कः) Grey bonduc, (Cæsalpinia bonducella, Rox.)<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>1. A potherb, “पुंइशाक” (Basella lucida &c.)<BR>	 2. A civet or pole-<BR>cat. Adj. Foul.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Ordure, excrement.<BR> E. पूति a stink, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिकरज|पूतिकरजः
पूतिकरज m. (-जः) A plant, (Cæsalpinia bonducella.)<BR> E. पूतिक the<BR>same, रञ्ज् to colour, aff. अण्; also with the nasal retained, पूतिकरञ्ज<BR>“नाटाकरम्जा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिकर्णक|पूतिकर्णकः
पूतिकर्णक m. (-कः) Fetid ulceration of the ear.<BR> E. पूति, and कर्ण the ear, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिकामुख|पूतिकामुखः
पूतिकामुख m. (-खः) A bi-valve-shell<BR> E. पूतिका a potherb, and मुख face,<BR>appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिकाष्ठ|पूतिकाष्ठं
पूतिकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A sort of pine, (P. devadāru.)<BR> E. पूति purity, काष्ठ<BR>wood; also with कन् added पूतिकाष्ठक m. (-कः) The Sarala tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिकीट
पूतिकीट m. (-टः) The winged-bug. “गंँधोपोका” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिगन्ध|पूतिगंध|पूतिगन्धं|पूतिगन्धः
पूतिगन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Ill-smelling.<BR>	 n. (-न्धं)<BR>	 1. Sulphur.<BR>	 2. Tin.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-न्धः) Stench, fetid odour.<BR> E. पूति a stink and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिगन्धि|पूतिगंधि|पूतिगन्धिः
पूतिगन्धि mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि) Ill-smelling. Adj. Stinking.<BR> E. पूति stink-<BR>ing, गन्ध smell, and इन् substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिगन्धिक|पूतिगन्धिकः
पूतिगन्धिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Ill-smelling, fetid.<BR> E. पूति a stink, गन्ध smell, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतितैला
पूतितैला f. (-ला) Heart-pea, (Cardiospermum halicacabum.)<BR> E. पूति<BR>stink, तैल oil. “लताकट्की” इति भाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिनस्य|पूतिनस्यः
पूतिनस्य n. (-स्यं) Fetid exhalation from the nostrils.<BR> E. पूति, and नस्य nostril.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिनासिक
पूतिनासिक Adj. Having a fetid nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिपुष्पिका
पूतिपुष्पिका f. (-का) A variety of the common citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR>E. पूति stinking, and पुष्प a flower, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिफला
पूतिफला f. (-ला) A plant, (Psoralea corilifolia.)<BR> E. पूति stinking, फल<BR>fruit. “सोमराज्याम्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिफली
पूतिफली f. (-ली) A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR> E. पूति stink, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिमयरिका
पूतिमयरिका f. (-का) The common carroway. “अजमोदायाम्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिमांस
पूतिमांस n. (-सं) Dead or decayed flesh.<BR> E. पूति, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिमेद|पूतिमेदः
पूतिमेद m. (-दः) The khayar tree, (mimosa catechu.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिवक्त्र
पूतिवक्त्र Adj. Having offensive breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिव्रण
पूतिव्रण n. (-णं) A foul ulcer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिवात|पूतिवातः
पूतिवात m. (-तः) The Bel, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>	 2. Foul air.<BR> E. पूति a<BR>stink, वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिवृक्ष|पूतिवृक्षः
पूतिवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. पूति a foul smell, and वृक्ष a tree. “श्योनाक वृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतिशारिजा
पूतिशारिजा f. (-जा) The pole or civet-cat. “खटाश” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूती
पूती(ति)क m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Cæsalpinia bonducella.)<BR>	 2. The pole-cat<BR>or civet-cat.<BR>	 f. (-का) A potherb, (Basella rubra, and lucida.)<BR> E. पूति<BR>a stink or purity, कन् added, and the penultimate optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूतीकरज
पूतीकरज m. (-जः) A plant, (Cæsalpinia bonducella) Also पूतीक,<BR>पूतिक, पूतिकरज पूतीकरञ्ज, or पूतिकरञ्ज. “नाटाकरम्जा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूत्यण्ड|पूत्यंड|पूत्यण्डः
पूत्यण्ड m. (-ण्ड)<BR>	 1. The musk deer.<BR>	 2. An insect with a fetid smell,<BR>the winged-bug. “गंँधोपोका”<BR> E. पूति a stench, and अण्ड the testicle<BR>or any egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूथिका
पूथिका f. (-का) A potherb; see पूतीक and पूतिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पून|पूनः
पून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Lost, destroyed.<BR> E. पू to purify aff. क्त, deriv. irr.<BR>“पूञो विनाशे” पा० क्तस्य नः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूप|पूपः
पूप m. (-पः) A cake.<BR> E. पू to purify, aff. पक् or यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपला
पूपला f. (-ली) A sort of sweet cake, fried with Ghee or oil.<BR> E. पूप a cake,<BR>ला to get or be, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपशाला
पूपशाला f. (-ला) A baker's or confectioner's shop.<BR> E. पूप, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपाली
पूपाली f. (-ली) A sort of cake or biscuit, made of meal or barley, half-<BR>baked or fried.<BR> E. पूप cake, आङ् before, ला to be or resemble, aff.<BR>क, fem. aff. ङीप्; also with कन् added पूपालिका; or पूपाय अलति, अल्-<BR>अच० गौरा० ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूपिका
पूपिका f. (-का) A sort of cake, half-baked or fried in oil or Ghee. E.<BR>पूप a cake, कन् aff. of comparison, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूय|पूयं|पूयः
पूय(ई)पूयी r. 1st cl. (पूयते)<BR>	 1. To split or cleave.<BR>	 2. To stink. दुर्गन्धे<BR>अक० भेदने विशरणेच सक० दिवा० आत्म० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूय|पूयं|पूयः
पूय n. (-यं) Pus, matter, discharge from an ulcer, sore or wound,<BR>E. पूय् to stink, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयन|पूयनं
पूयन n. (-नं) Pus, discharge from a wound or sore.<BR> E. पूय to stink, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयरक्त|पूयरक्तः
पूयरक्त n. (-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Ichor, sanies.<BR>	 2. Discharge of sanies from the nostrils.<BR>m. (-क्तः) A kind of disease of the nose.<BR> E. पूय, and रक्त blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयशोणित
पूयशोणित n. (-तं) Ichor, sanies.<BR> E. पूय, and शोणित blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयारि|पूयारिः
पूयारि m. (-रिः) The Nimba tree, (Melia azadirachta.)<BR> E. पूय pus, and<BR>अरि inimical; the leaves being used to produce discussion, or the<BR>absorption of matter that has formed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूयालस|पूयालसः
पूयालस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Suppuration at the joints, white swelling.<BR>	 2. Mat-<BR>ter in the eye.<BR> E. पूय, and अलस idle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर|पूरं|पूरः
पूर r. 4th cl. (ई) पूरी (पूर्य्यते) 1. To satisfy.<BR>	 2. To fill.<BR>	 3. To be satisfied.<BR>4. To be full. दिवा० आत्म० सक० सेट् । r. 10th cl. (पूरयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>satisfy.<BR>	 2. To fill out.<BR>	 3. To fill with wind, to blow.<BR>	 4. To cover,<BR>to surround.<BR>	 5. To fill with sound, to make resonant.<BR>	 6. To inten-<BR>sify, to strengthen. चु० उभ० सक० सेट् । With आ 1. To fill, to make<BR>full.<BR>	 2. To blow.<BR>	 3. To cover, to envelop, to intertwine. With<BR>परि To fill completely. With प्र, 1. To fill.<BR>	 2. To enrich, to load<BR>with riches. With सम, To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर|पूरं|पूरः
पूर mfn. subst. (-रः-रा-रं) A sort of unleavened cake, fried with Ghee<BR>or oil.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A piece of water, a large quantity of water,<BR>a lake.<BR>	 2. The healing or cleansing of ulcers.<BR>	 3. Making content,<BR>satisfying.<BR>	 4. Filling.<BR>	 5. Supply.<BR>	 6. Swelling of a river or the<BR>sea.<BR>	 7. A stream, a flood.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A kind of incense. Adj.<BR>(-रः-रा-रं) Full, filled.<BR> E. पूर् to fill, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरक|पूरकः
पूरक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Filling, completing, or that which fills or<BR>completes.<BR>	 2. Filling up.<BR>	 3. Satisfying.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A citron, (Citrus<BR>medica.)<BR>	 2. The multiplier. (In arithmetic.)<BR>	 3. Closing the right<BR>nostril, and drawing up air through the left, a religious cere-<BR>monial.<BR>	 4. The funeral cake or cakes that must be given to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">Page465-a+ 60</a>]<BR>complete the obsequial rites.<BR> E. पूर् to fill, aff. कुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरकृत
पूरकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Filled<BR> E. पूर्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरण|पूरणं|पूरणः
पूरण mfn. (-णः-णा-णी-णं) Filling, completing.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Act of filling,<BR>completing or making up.<BR>	 2. The final obsequial ball or cake.<BR>	 3.<BR>Multiplication, (in arithmetic)<BR>	 4. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus<BR>rotundus.)<BR>	 5. Rain, raining.<BR>	 nf. (-णं-णी) The cross threads in<BR>weaving a piece of cloth, m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A bridge, a causeway.<BR>	 2. The<BR>ocean.<BR>	 3. A medicinal oil or embrocation.<BR>	 f. (-णी) The silk-cotton<BR>tree.<BR> E. पूर् to fill, aff. ल्युट् or युच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरणप्रत्यय|पूरणप्रत्ययः
पूरणप्रत्यय m. (-यः) An affix forming an ordinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरयितृ
पूरयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Filling.<BR> E. पूर् to fill, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरयित्क
पूरयित्क Ind. Having filled.<BR> E. पूर् to fill, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरिका
पूरिका f. (-का) A sort of unleavened cake, fried with Ghee or oil.<BR> E. पूरी,<BR>as above, aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरित|पूरितं
पूरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Filled, full, complete.<BR>	 2. Multiplied.<BR>	 3. Over-<BR>spread.<BR> E. पूर् to be full, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूरुष|पूरुषः
पूरुष m. (-षः) Man, male, mankind.<BR> E. पूर् to be full, (the world,) aff.<BR>उषन्; it is also written, पुरुष &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ण|पूर्णः
पूर्ण r. 10th cl. (पूर्णयति-ते) To accumulate, to collect or heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ण|पूर्णः
पूर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Full, filled, complete.<BR>	 2. All, entire.<BR>	 3. Strong,<BR>powerful, able.<BR>	 4. Selfish, self-indulgent.<BR>	 f. (-र्णा)<BR>	 1. Fifth, tenth, or<BR>fifteenth day of the half month.<BR>	 2. Full moon.<BR> E. पूर् to be full, aff.<BR>क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णक|पूर्णकः
पूर्णक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cock.<BR>	 2. A kind of tree.<BR>	 f. (-र्णिका) A sort of bird,<BR>described as having a double or cleft beak; also नासाच्छिन्नी. E.<BR>पूर्ण full, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णककूद
पूर्णककूद Adj. Full-humped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णकाम|पूर्णकामः
पूर्णकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Satisfied, satiated.<BR> E. पूर्ण fulfilled, काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णकुम्भ|पूर्णकुंभ|पूर्णकुम्भः
पूर्णकुम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. A water vessel, one filled with holy water, used at<BR>the consecration of a king.<BR>	 2. A full cup or jar.<BR> E. पूर्ण full, and कुम्भ<BR>a water jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णपात्र|पूर्णपात्रं
पूर्णपात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A full cup or vessel.<BR>	 2. A vessel filled with clothes or<BR>ornaments, which are scrambled for by the guests and relations<BR>at a festival.<BR>	 3. A vessel full of rice, presented at a sacrifice to the<BR>superintending and officiating priests; the Pūrṇa Pātra is pro-<BR>perly a measure of 256 handfuls of rice; it may also be composed<BR>of as much as will satisfy one great eater.<BR> E. पूर्ण full, and पात्र a<BR>vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णमा
पूर्णमा f. (-मा) The day of full moon.<BR> E. पूर्ण full, मा the moon; also<BR>पूर्णिमा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णमास|पूर्णमासः
पूर्णमास m. (-सः) A monthly sacrifice, performed on the day of full<BR>moon; also पौर्णमास.<BR>	 f. (-सी) Day of full moon.<BR> E. पूर्ण complete,<BR>मास the month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ण|पूर्णः
पूर्ण(वी)बीज m. (-जः) The citron.<BR> E. पूर्ण, and बीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णानक
पूर्णानक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A vessel full of clothes, &c. at a feast: see पूर्णपात्र.<BR>2. The sound of a drum.<BR>	 3. A moon-beam.<BR> E. पूर्ण full, अन् to go,<BR>or be, aff. बुन्; also read पूर्णालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णालक|पूर्णालकं
पूर्णालक n. (-कं) A vessel of clothes or ornaments to be scrambled for.<BR>E. पूर्ण full, अल् to ornament, aff. ण्वुल्; also sometimes written<BR>पूर्णानक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णिमा
पूर्णिमा f. (-मा) Day of full moon.<BR> E. पूर्ण full, (the moon,) इमक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णेन्दु|पूर्णेंदु|पूर्णेन्दुः
पूर्णेन्दु m. (-न्दुः) The moon, the full moon.<BR> E. पूर्ण, and इन्दु the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्णोपमा
पूर्णोपमा f. (-मा) A complete simile, in which the four requisites, namely<BR>उपमेय, उपमान, साधारणधर्म्म, and उपमावाचक must all be expressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्त्त|पूर्त|पूर्त्तं|पूर्त्तः
पूर्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Filled, full, complete.<BR>	 2. Covered, concealed.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-र्त्त)<BR>	 1. An act of pious liberality, as digging a well, planting a<BR>grove, building a temple, &c.<BR>	 2. Nourishing, cherishing. It is<BR>thus defined in Vāchaspatya:--“वापीकूपतडागादि देवता यतनानि च । अन्न<BR>प्रदानमारामः पूर्तमित्यभिघीयते” ॥<BR> E. पृ to cherish or fill, aff. क्त, and<BR>the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्त्ति|पूर्ति|पूर्तिः|पूर्त्तिः
पूर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Fullness, completion.<BR>	 2. Satisfaction.<BR> E. पॄ to satisfy or<BR>fill, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्त्तिन्|पूर्तिन्
पूर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) Filling, completing.<BR>	 2. Effective.<BR> E. पॄ to satisfy, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्ब|पूर्ब|पूर्ब्बः
पूर्ब्ब r. 1st cl. (पूर्ब्बति) To fill. 10th cl. (पूर्ब्बयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To dwell.<BR>	 2. To<BR>invite: the root is written either पूर्ब्ब or पूर्व्व । निमन्त्रणे सक० निवासे<BR>अक० चु० उभ० सेट् । अन्तस्थात्नु भ्वा० प० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्व|पूर्व|पूर्वः|पूर्व्वः
पूर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वी-र्व्वं)<BR>	 1. First, former, prior, preceding, initial.<BR>	 2. East,<BR>eastern.<BR>	 3. All, entire.<BR>	 4. Before, in front of.<BR>	 m. plu. (-र्व्वाः)<BR>Ancestors, forefathers.<BR>	 f. (-र्ब्बा) The east.<BR>	 n. (-र्व्वं) An ancient tradi-<BR>tion.<BR> E. पूर्ब्ब or पूर्व्व to fill, to dwell, &c. aff. अच्; hence to derivative<BR>and its compounds may be written either with व or व; the second<BR>of the duplicate consonants may also be rejected, making it पूर्ब<BR>or पूर्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्बक
पूर्ब्बक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Prior, before, preceding.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A forefather.<BR>E. पूर्ब्ब, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्बकल्प
पूर्ब्बकल्प m. (-ल्पः) Former times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्बकाल
पूर्ब्बकाल n. (-लं) Former time.<BR> E. पूर्ब्ब, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वकालीन|पूर्वकालीन
पूर्व्वकालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Ancient, belonging to former times.<BR> E. पूर्ब्बकाल and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्बकाष्ठा
पूर्ब्बकाष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा) The east, the eastern quarter.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and काष्ठा quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्बकृत
पूर्ब्बकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done formerly, or in a prior existence.<BR> E. पूर्ब्ब,<BR>and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वकोटि|पूर्वकोटि|पूर्वकोटिः
पूर्व्वकोटि f. (-टि) The starting point, the first statement of a debatable question.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वगङ्गा|पूर्वगङ्गा|पूर्वगंगा
पूर्व्वगङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) The Narmada river.<BR> E. पूर्ब्ब formerly, (called) गङ्गा<BR>the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वचोदित|पूर्वचोदित
पूर्व्वचोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Formerly stated, before-mentioned, aforesaid.<BR>E. पूर्व्व, and चोदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्बज|पूर्बज
पूर्ब्बज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Born or produced before, either in time or<BR>place.<BR>	 2. Eastern, born in the east.<BR>	 3. Elder.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. An elder<BR>brother.<BR>	 2. The son of the elder wife, even though last born.<BR>	 m.<BR>plu. (-जाः)<BR>	 1. The deified progenitors of mankind.<BR>	 2. Ancestors,<BR>forefathers in general.<BR> E. पूर्ब्ब formerly or first, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्बजिन|पूर्बजिन
पूर्ब्बजिन m. (-नः) A Bauddha teacher; also MANJUGHOSHA.<BR>	 m. plu.<BR>(-नाः) The twenty-four Jinas or Jaina saints of a former æra. E.<BR>पूर्ब्ब, and जिन a Jina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वतन|पूर्वतन
पूर्व्वतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Former.<BR> E. पूर्ब्ब, and तनट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्बदिक्पति|पूर्बदिक्पति
पूर्ब्बदिक्पति m. (-तिः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. पूर्ब्ब east, दिश् quarter, and<BR>पति regent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदिश्|पूर्वदिश्
पूर्व्वदिश् f. (-दिक्) The eastern region.<BR> E. पूर्ब्ब, and दिश् a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदृष्ट|पूर्वदृष्ट
पूर्व्वदृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Formerly seen.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदेव|पूर्वदेव|पूर्वदेवः|पूर्व्वदेवः
पूर्व्वदेव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. An Asura or demon.<BR>	 2. A Pitṛ, or progenitor.<BR> E. पूर्व्व<BR>before, देव a god; the first being the elder offspring of KĀSYAPA,<BR>the parent of both gods and demons, and the second being the<BR>progenitor of gods and men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदेवता|पूर्वदेवता
पूर्व्वदेवता f. (-ता) A primeval deity, a Pitṛ or progenitor of gods as<BR>well as men.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and देवता a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्ब्बदेश|पूर्बदेश
पूर्ब्बदेश m. (-शः) The eastern country, or eastern part of India.<BR> E. पूर्व्व<BR>eastern, देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वदेह|पूर्वदेह
पूर्व्वदेह m. (-हः) A former body, a prior existence.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and देह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वपक्ष|पूर्वपक्ष|पूर्वपक्षः|पूर्व्वपक्षः
पूर्व्वपक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A proposition, an assertion; the first part of an<BR>argument, to which assent or refutation is necessary.<BR>	 2. The first<BR>half of a lunar month.<BR> E. पूर्व्व first, पक्ष argument, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वपक्षपाद|पूर्वपक्षपाद|पूर्व्वपक्षपादः
पूर्व्वपक्षपाद m. (-दः) The first division of legal proceeding, the plaint. E.<BR>पूर्व्वपक्ष, and पाद quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वपद|पूर्वपद|पूर्व्वपदं
पूर्व्वपद n. (-दं) The first member of a compounded word, of a sentence,<BR>a verse. &c.<BR> E. पूर्व्व preceeding, and पद a ward, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वपदिक|पूर्वपदिक
पूर्व्वपदिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Relating to the first member of a compound<BR>term.<BR> E. पूर्व्वपद, and इकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वपर्व्वत|पूर्वपर्वत|पूर्वपर्वतः|पूर्व्वपर्व्वतः
पूर्व्वपर्व्वत m. (-तः) The eastern mountain, behind which to sun is suppo-<BR>sed to rise.<BR> E. पूर्व्व eastern, and पर्व्वत a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वप्रवृत्त|पूर्वप्रवृत्त
पूर्व्वप्रवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Formerly fixed, or done.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and प्रवृत्त undertaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=465-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वफल्गुनी|पूर्वफल्गुनी
पूर्व्वफल्गुनी f. (-नी) The eleventh lunar asterism; the first Phalguni,<BR>the twelfth Nakshatra, being termed Uttara or subsequent; this<BR>asterism figured by a couch contains two stars, one of which is<BR>the Leonis.<BR> E. पूर्व्व first, and फल्गुनी the name of the two asterisms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वफल्गुनाभव
पूर्व्वफल्गुनाभव m. (-वः) The planet Jupiter.<BR> E. पूर्व्वफल्गुनी as above, and भव<BR>being born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वभाद्रपदा|पूर्वभाद्रपदा
पूर्व्वभाद्रपदा f. (-दा) The first of the two lunar asterisms, called Bhādra-<BR>padā, and twenty-sixth, of the whole, containing two stars. E.<BR>पूर्व्व first, भाद्रपदा the asterism so named; it is also read<BR>पूर्व्वभद्रपदा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वभाषिन्|पूर्वभाषिन्
पूर्व्वभाषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Polite, complaisant, condescending to<BR>speak first.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and भाषिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वभुक्ति|पूर्वभुक्ति|पूर्वभुक्तिः
पूर्व्वभुक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Prior possession.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and भुक्ति enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वमारिन्|पूर्वमारिन्
पूर्व्वमारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Dying first.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, मृ to die, घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वमीमांसा|पूर्वमीमांसा
पूर्व्वमीमांसा f. (-सा) An inquiry into the ritual portion of the Veda. It is<BR>called पूर्व्वमीमांसा in contradistinction to the Vedānta system which<BR>is considered to be a sequel to Jaimini's system and is styled उत्तर<BR>मीमांसा; there is however very little in common between the two<BR>systems.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वयक्ष|पूर्वयक्ष|पूर्व्वयक्षः
पूर्व्वयक्ष m. (-क्षः) One of the Jinas or Jaina teachers.<BR> E. पूर्व्व formerly,<BR>यक्ष a demi-god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वरङ्ग|पूर्वरङ्ग|पूर्वरंग|पूर्वरङ्गः|पूर्व्वरङ्गः
पूर्व्वरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The commencement of a drama, or the prelude to<BR>to instrumental or vocal performance; a prologue, an overture.<BR>E. पूर्व्व first, रङ्ग a stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वराग|पूर्वराग|पूर्वरागः|पूर्व्वरागः
पूर्व्वराग m. (-गः) Affection arising from some cause before the parties<BR>meet.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and राग passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वरात्र|पूर्वरात्र|पूर्वरात्रः|पूर्व्वरात्रः
पूर्व्वरात्र m. (-त्रः) The first part of the night.<BR> E. पूर्व्व preceding, रात्रि night,<BR>and the final changed to अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वरूप|पूर्वरूप|पूर्व्वरूपं
पूर्व्वरूप n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. Indication of some approaching change.<BR>	 2. Retention<BR>of the first of two concurrent vowels or consonants.<BR>	 3. Symptom<BR>of occurring disease.<BR> E. पूर्व्व previous, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वलक्षण|पूर्वलक्षण
पूर्व्वलक्षण n. (-णं) Indication of something about to occur, as sickness, &c,<BR>E. पूर्व्व, and लक्षण sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्ववत्|पूर्ववत्|पूर्ववन्त्
पूर्व्ववत् Ind. As before, as aforesaid, &c.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्ववाद|पूर्ववाद|पूर्ववादः|पूर्व्ववादः
पूर्व्ववाद n. (-दं) A former plaint or averment.<BR> E. पूर्व्व former, and वाद<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्ववादिन्|पूर्ववादिन्
पूर्व्ववादिन् m. (-दी) One who has made a former plea or complaint. E.<BR>पूर्व्ववाद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वशैल|पूर्वशैल|पूर्वशैलः|पूर्व्वशैलः
पूर्व्वशैल m. (-लः) The eastern mountain, behind which the sun is sup-<BR>posed to rise.<BR> E. पूर्व्व eastern, शैल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वसर|पूर्वसर|पूर्व्वसरः
पूर्व्वसर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Preceding, going before.<BR> E. पूर्व्व first, सृ to go, aff. ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वसन्ध्या|पूर्वसन्ध्या
पूर्व्वसन्ध्या f. (-न्ध्या) Dawn, daybreak.<BR> E. पूर्व्व prier, and सन्ध्या junction, (of<BR>the day.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वसार|पूर्वसार|पूर्व्वसारः
पूर्व्वसार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Going eastwards.<BR> E. पूर्व्व east, and सृ to go, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वसाहस|पूर्वसाहस|पूर्वसाहसः
पूर्व्वसाहस n. (-सं) The first or heaviest of the three fines, or punishment.<BR>E. पूर्व्व, and साहस infliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाचरित|पूर्वाचरित
पूर्व्वाचरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done or followed formerly.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and<BR>आचरित observed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाद्रि|पूर्वाद्रि|पूर्वाद्रिः|पूर्व्वाद्रिः
पूर्व्वाद्रि m. (-द्रिः) The eastern mountain.<BR> E. पूर्व्व eastern, and अद्रि<BR>mountain: see पूर्व्वशैल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वापर|पूर्वापर
पूर्व्वापर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) First and last, prior and subsequent.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>Proof, and thing to be proved.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and अपर after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाभ्यास|पूर्वाभ्यास|पूर्वाभ्यासः
पूर्व्वाभ्यास m. (-सः) Former practice, or experience.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and अभ्यास<BR>practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वार्द्ध|पूर्वार्ध|पूर्वार्धः
पूर्व्वार्द्ध n. (-र्द्धं) The first or east half of any thing.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वावतर
पूर्व्वावतर m. (-रः) First accession or attack, (of any passion, disease, &c.)<BR>E. पूर्व्व, and अवतर befalling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वावेदक|पूर्वावेदक|पूर्वावेदकः
पूर्व्वावेदक m. (-कः) A plaintiff, one who has made a complaint before<BR>another.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and आवेदक who represents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाषाढा|पूर्वाषाढा
पूर्व्वाषाढा f. (-ढा) The first of two constellations, each called Āshāḍhā,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">Page466-b+ 60</a>]<BR>and the 20th of the lunar asterisms, containing two stars of<BR>which one is Sagitarii.<BR> E. पूर्व्व first, आषाढा Āshāḍhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाह्ण|पूर्वाह्ण|पूर्वाह्णः|पूर्व्वाह्णः
पूर्व्वाह्ण m. (-ह्णः) The first part of the day, the forenoon.<BR> E. पूर्व्व first,<BR>and अहन् day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वाह्णेतन|पूर्वाह्णेतन|पूर्व्वाह्णेतनः
पूर्व्वाह्णेतन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Belonging or relating to the forenoon. E.<BR>पूर्व्वाह्ण as above, द्यु aff. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वेण|पूर्वेण
पूर्व्वेण Ind. In the east, easterly, eastward.<BR> E. पूर्व्व the east, and the form<BR>of the 3rd case used as a participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वेद्युस्|पूर्वेद्युस्
पूर्व्वेद्युस् Ind.<BR>	 1. A former day, yesterday.<BR>	 2. The morning, dawn, the<BR>first part of the day.<BR>	 3. A day or portion of a day on which<BR>religious ceremonies are to be performed.<BR> E. पूर्व्व former or first,<BR>and एद्युस् aff. for द्यु a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वोक्त|पूर्वोक्त
पूर्व्वोक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Said formerly, before-mentioned, aforesaid. E.<BR>पूर्व्व, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वोत्तर|पूर्वोत्तर
पूर्व्वोत्तर nf. (-रं-रा) The north-east.<BR> E. पूर्व्व east, and उत्तर north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूर्व्वोदित|पूर्वोदित
पूर्व्वोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Aforesaid, afore-mentioned.<BR> E. पूर्व्व, and उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूल्
पूल् r. 1st and 10th cls. (पूलति पूलयति-ते) To accumulate, to collect or<BR>heap. चु० उभ० पक्षे भ्वा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूष्
पूष् r. 1st cl. (पूषति)<BR>	 1. To increase or grow.<BR>	 2. To nourish. see पुष्<BR>अक० भ्वा० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूष|पूषः
पूष m. (-षः) The mulberry. (Morus Indica.)<BR> E. पूष् to grow, aff. क. “तुंँत् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषन्
पूषन् m. (-षा) The sun.<BR> E. पूष् to nourish, aff. कनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषभासा
पूषभासा f. (-षा) The capital of INDRA.<BR> E. पूष the sun, भास् light, aff.<BR>टाप्, splendid as the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पूषासुहृत्
पूषासुहृत् m. (-हृत्) SĪVA.<BR> E. पूष the sun, and सुहृत् a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृ
पृ r. 3rd cl. (पिपर्त्ति)<BR>	 1. To protect, to nourish.<BR>	 2. To fill. जुहो० पर० सक०<BR>अनिट् वा दीर्घे सेट् । 5th cl. (पृणोति) To satisfy, to please or content.<BR>प्रीतौ अक० प्रीणने सक० स्वादि० पर० अनिट् । r. 1st and 10th cls. (परति<BR>पारयति-ते) To fill, as the stomach or a vessel. चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR>r. 6th cl. (But with वि and आङ् prefixed, and ङ aff.) व्यापृङ्<BR>(व्याप्रियते) To be busy or active, to labour, to make exertions;<BR>तु० आत्म० अक० अनिट्ः see पृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्का
पृक्का f. (-क्का) A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR> E. स्पृश् to<BR>touch, कन् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्त|पृक्तं
पृक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Touched, mixed, in contact or combination<BR>with.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं) Wealth, possessions.<BR> E. पृच् to mix, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्ति|पृक्तिः
पृक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Touch, contact.<BR> E. पृच् to touch, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृक्थ|पृक्थं
पृक्थ n. (-क्थं) Property, wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्
पृच्(ई)पृची r. 2nd cl. (पृक्ते) r. 7th cl. (पृणक्ति) To touch, to be or bring<BR>in contact. r. 1st and 10th cls. (पर्चति पर्चयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To hinder or<BR>restrain.<BR>	 2. To touch. सम्पर्के अदा० आत्म० अक० सेट् । संयमने सक० सम्पर्के<BR>अक० चु० उभ० पक्षे भ्वा० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छक|पृच्छकः
पृच्छक m. (-कः) An inquirer, an investigator, an inquisitive person. E.<BR>प्रच्छ् to ask, वुन् aff. र changed to ऋ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छन|पृच्छनं
पृच्छन n. (-णं) Asking, inquiring.<BR> E. पृच्छ् to ask, ल्युट् aff., र changed to ऋ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृच्छा
पृच्छा f. (-च्छा) Asking, questioning a question or inquiry.<BR> E. प्रच्छ् to<BR>inquire, affs. अङ् and टाप्, the semi-vowel changed to the corres-<BR>ponding vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृज्
पृज्(ई)पृजी r. 2nd cl. (पृक्ते) To touch, to be in contact with. अदा० आ० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृड्
पृड् r. 6th cl. (पृडति) To delight. तु० पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृण्
पृण् r. 6th cl. (पृणति) To please or gratify. तुदा० पर० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृत्
पृत् f. An army. This word has no form, for the first five cases; accord-<BR>ing to some it is an optional substitute for the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतना
पृतना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. An army.<BR>	 2. A small army or division consisting of<BR>243 elephants, as many chariots, 729 horse, and 1215 foot.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fight, encounter.<BR> E. पृ to fill, तनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतनासाह्
पृतनासाह् m. (-षाट्) INDRA.<BR> E. पृतना an army, सह् to bear or be equal to, ण्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्
पृथ् r. 10th (पर्थयति-ते) To throw or cast, to send or direct. चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्
पृथक् Ind.<BR>	 1. Without, except.<BR>	 2. Separately, severally.<BR> E. पृथ् to throw<BR>or dismiss, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=466-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्करण
पृथक्करण n. (-णं) Separating, distinguishing, analysing.<BR> E. पृथक्, and करण<BR>making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्कृत
पृथक्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Separated, sundered, made distinct.<BR> E. पृथक्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्क्षेत्र
पृथक्क्षेत्र m. plu. (-त्राः) Children of one father by wives of different<BR>classes.<BR> E. पृथक् separately, and क्षेत्र a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथकत्व
पृथकत्व n. (-त्वं) Individuality, separateness, severalty.<BR> E. त्व added to<BR>पृथक्; also with तल्, पृथक्ता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्त्वचा
पृथक्त्वचा f. (-चा) A plant, commonly Mūrvā, (Sanseviera zeylanica.) E.<BR>पृथक् separately, त्वच् skin; having a fibrous bark from which<BR>bows-strings are made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्पर्णी
पृथक्पर्णी f. (-र्णीं) A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia Rox.)<BR> E. पृथक् separate,<BR>पर्ण a leaf, aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्पिण्ड|पृथक्पिण्डः
पृथक्पिण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A relation connected by ablation of water only. E.<BR>पृथक्, and पिण्ड obsequial cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथगात्मता
पृथगात्मता f. (-ता) Discrimination, judgment.<BR> E. पृथक् severally, आत्मन्<BR>real nature, तल् aff.; distinguishing the different nature of different<BR>things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथगात्मन्
पृथगात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Several, separate, individual.<BR>	 m. (-त्मा)<BR>Individualised spirit, or that of an individual, as detached from<BR>universal spirit, or the soul of all.<BR> E. पृथक्, and आत्मन् self or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथगात्मिका
पृथगात्मिका f. (-का) Individuality, separate or individual state of being.<BR>E. पृथक् separately, आत्मन् self, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथग्गुण
पृथग्गुण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Having distinct properties.<BR> E. पृथक्, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथग्जन|पृथग्जनः
पृथग्जन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. An ignorant man, a fool.<BR>	 2. A man of a low cast.<BR>3. A sinner, a wicked or vicious man.<BR>	 m. plu. (-नाः) Children of<BR>one father by different mothers.<BR> E. पृथक् separate, away from,<BR>(virtue &c.) and जन a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथग्विध|पृथग्विधः
पृथग्विध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Various, diversified, multiform.<BR> E. पृथक् several, विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथवी
पृथवी f. (-वी) The earth: see पृथिवी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथा
पृथा f. (-था) KUNTĪ, the wife of PĀṆḌU.<BR> E. प्रथ to be famous, affs. अङ्<BR>and टाप, the semi-vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथाज|पृथाजः
पृथाज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The son of KUNTĪ, “ARJUNA,” &c.<BR>	 2. Name of a tree.<BR>E. पृथा, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथापति|पृथापतिः
पृथापति m. (-तिः) PĀṆḌU, the nominal father of the Pāṇḍava<BR>princes.<BR> E. पृथा KUNTI, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिका
पृथिका f. (-का) A centipede.<BR> E. पृथ् to throw, aff. क्वुन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवि|पृथिविः
पृथिवि f. (-विः) The earth: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवी
पृथिवी f. (-वी) The earth.<BR> E. प्रथ् to be famous, Unādi aff. षिवन्, fem.<BR>aff. ङीप्, and the vowel substituted for the semi-vowel; also with<BR>the anti-penultimate vowel changed to अ, पृथवी; or dropped alto-<BR>gether, पृथ्वी; or without the fem. aff. पृथिवि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीक्षित्
पृथिवीक्षित् m. (-क्षित्) A king.<BR> E. पृथिवी, and क्षित् who rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीतल
पृथिवीतल n. (-लं) The surface of the ground.<BR> E. पृथिवी, and तल surface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीपति|पृथिवीपतिः
पृथिवीपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A king, a sovereign.<BR>	 2. A drug, commonly<BR>Rishabha.<BR>	 3. YAMA, regent of the dead.<BR> E. पृथिवी the earth, and<BR>पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीपाल|पृथिवीपालः
पृथिवीपाल m. (-लः) A king, a sovereign, a ruler.<BR> E. पृथिवी the earth, and<BR>पाल who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवीशक्र|पृथिवीशक्रः
पृथिवीशक्र m. (-क्रः) A king.<BR> E. पृथिवी the earth, and शक्र INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथु|पृथुः
पृथु mfn. (-थुः-थुः-थ्वी-थु)<BR>	 1. Large, great.<BR>	 2. Smart, clever.<BR>	 m. (-थुः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>fifth monarch of the solar dynasty in the second age.<BR>	 2. A name<BR>of Agni or fire.<BR>	 f. (-थुः)<BR>	 1. A pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A medicinal substance, commonly Hingupatri.<BR>	 3. Opium.<BR> E. प्रथ्<BR>to be famous, aff. कु, and र changed to ऋ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुक|पृथुकं|पृथुकः
पृथुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) The young of any animal.<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं) Rice or<BR>grain flattened.<BR>	 f. (-का) Hingupatri: see पृथु.<BR> E. प्रथ् to be famous,<BR>aff. कुकन् or पृथु as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुरोमन्
पृथुरोमन् m. (-मा) A fish in general.<BR> E. पृथृ large, and रोमन् hair of the<BR>human body, to which the scales of the fish may be considered<BR>analogous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुल|पृथुलं
पृथुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Great, large.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A medicinal substance,<BR>“Hingupatri.”<BR> E. पृथु, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुशेखर|पृथुशेखरः
पृथुशेखर m. (-रः) A mountain.<BR> E. पृथु large, and शेखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुस्कन्ध|पृथुस्कंध|पृथुस्कन्धः
पृथुस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) A boar.<BR> E. पृथु large, स्कन्ध shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथूदर|पृथूदरः
पृथूदर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Large-bellied, stout, corpulent.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A ram.<BR>E. पृथु, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्वी
पृथ्वी f. (-थ्वी)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. A pungent seed. (Nigella Indica.)<BR>	 3.<BR>A medical substance and condiment, perhaps the leaf of the<BR>asafœtida plant, “Hingupatri.” 4. The mother of the seventh Jina,<BR>or Jaina deified teacher, SUPĀRSWA.<BR>	 5. Cardamoms.<BR>	 6. Name of a<BR>metre. E. The feminine form of पृथु, or पृथु the king so named, and<BR>ङीप् aff.; the domain of king PṚTHU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्वीका
पृथ्वीका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Large cardamoms.<BR>	 2. Small cardamoms.<BR>	 3. A small<BR>pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.)<BR> E. पृथ्वी as above. कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्वीभर|पृथ्वीभरः
पृथ्वीभर m. (-रः) A species of the Atyasti metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृदाकु|पृदाकुः
पृदाकु m. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. A scorpion.<BR>	 3. A tiger.<BR>	 4. A leopard or<BR>the small hunting leopard.<BR>	 5. An elephant.<BR>	 6. A tree.<BR> E. पर्द to<BR>fart, Unādi aff. काकु; the vowel substituted for the semi-vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्नि|पृश्निः
पृश्नि mfn. (-श्निः-श्निः-श्नि)<BR>	 1. Small, short, thin.<BR>	 2. Delicate, feeble.<BR>	 f. (-श्निः)<BR>1. A ray of light.<BR>	 2. A queen, the wife of SUTAPĀ, who being<BR>regenerated after death, became DEVAKĪ the mother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>3. The earth.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, नि Unādi aff., and the initial<BR>rejected; also पृष्णि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्नि|पृश्निः
पृश्नि(ष्णि)का f. (-का) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निगर्भ|पृश्निगर्भः
पृश्निगर्भ m. (-र्भः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. पृश्नि the wife of a saint<BR>incarnate in DEVAKĪ, and गर्भ the embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निधर|पृश्निधरः
पृश्निधर m. (-रः) KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निपर्णी
पृश्निपर्णी f. (-णी) A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia,) according to some of<BR>its synonymes, but in ROXBURGH'S Catalogue, Hedysarum lagopo-<BR>dioides.)<BR> E. पृश्नि small, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निभद्र|पृश्निभद्रः
पृश्निभद्र m. (-द्रः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. पृश्नि DEVAKĪ and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निशृङ्ग|पृश्निशृंग|पृश्निशृङ्गः
पृश्निशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU, in that incarna-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. A name of GANEŚA.<BR> E. पृश्नि small, and शृङ्ग a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्नी
पृश्नी f. (-श्नी) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. पृष् to sprinkle,<BR>नि, aff. and ङीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्
पृष्(उ)पृषु r. 1st. cl. (पर्षति)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle.<BR>	 2. To weary.<BR>	 3. To hurt,<BR>to injure.<BR>	 4. To Give. भ्वा० आ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत्|पृषन्त्
पृषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Sprinkling.<BR>	 n. sing. (-षत्) du. (-षती) plu. (-षन्ति)<BR>A drop of water or any liquid.<BR>	 mf. (-षन्-षती) The porcine deer. E.<BR>पृष् to sprinkle, Unādi aff. अति, or participial aff. शतृ; also पृषत्<BR>and पृषन्ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत|पृषतः
पृषत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A drop of water.<BR>	 2. The porcine deer.<BR> E. पृष् to<BR>sprinkle, Unādi aff. अतच्; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषताम्पति|पृषतांपति|पृषताम्पतिः
पृषताम्पति m. (-तिः) Air, wind, or its deified personification.<BR> E. पृषत् a<BR>deer, in the second case plural, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषताश्व|पृषताश्वः
पृषताश्व m. (-श्वः) Air, wind.<BR> E. पृषत् the porcine deer, and अश्व a horse:<BR>see पृषदश्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत्क|पृषत्कः
पृषत्क m. (-त्कः) An arrow<BR> E. पृषत् a deer, and कन् added; swift as a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषदश्व|पृषदश्वः
पृषदश्व m. (-श्वः) The god of air, or wind divinely personified.<BR> E. पृषत्<BR>the porcine deer, or a drop of rain, and अश्व a horse; whose steeds<BR>are like deer, or may be considered as the drops of rain, accom-<BR>panying a gale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषदाज्य|पृषदाज्यं
पृषदाज्य n. (-ज्यं) Ghee mixed with curds, forming an oblation.<BR> E. पृषत्<BR>sprinkling, and आज्य Ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषद्वल|पृषद्वलः
पृषद्वल m. (-लः) A horse of the wind.<BR> E. पृषत् a deer, वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषन्ति|पृषंति|पृषंतिः|पृषन्तिः
पृषन्ति n. (-न्ति) A drop of water.<BR> E. पृष् to sprinkle, aff. झिच्; according<BR>to the best authorities, however, this word is the plural inflection<BR>of पृषत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषभाषा
पृषभाषा f. (-षा) See पूषभाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषाकरा
पृषाकरा f. (-रा) A small stone used as a weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=467-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषातक|पृषातकं
पृषातक n. (-कं) An oblation of Ghee and curds.<BR> E. पृष् sprinkling, अत्<BR>to go or be, अच् and कन् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषोदर|पृषोदरः
पृषोदर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having a spot or circle on the belly. According<BR>to Professor Turkabāchaspati:--पृषः दिवोदरं यस्य पृषो० तलोपः 1. Small-<BR>bellied, and पृषन्ति उदरे यस्य.<BR>	 2. Air, wind. But in his other works<BR>this word is taken as a type of such irregular compounds. Accor-<BR>ding to others:--E. पृषत् a drop of any thing liquid, and उदर the<BR>belly, form irregular and special; the word is most commonly in<BR>use as a grammatical term, being the leading word of a class in<BR>which the formation of each is peculiar to itself, and being thence<BR>applied to designate the rule which comprehends the whole of<BR>the series.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषोद्यान|पृषोद्यानं
पृषोद्यान n. (-नं) A small garden.<BR> E. पृषत्, and उद्यान a garden, त rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ट
पृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Asked, inquired, interrogated.<BR>	 2. Sprinkled. E.<BR>प्रच्छ् to ask, क्त aff. and the vowel substituted for the semi-vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्टहायन|पृष्टहायनः
पृष्टहायन m. (-नः) A species of grain.<BR>	 mf. (-नः-ना) An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्टि|पृष्टिः
पृष्टि m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. A ray of light.<BR>	 2. Touch.<BR> E. पृष् to touch, &c. aff. क्तिन्.<BR>when it is derived from प्रच्छ्-क्तिन् it means “Inquiry” and when<BR>formed from पृष् कर्तरि क्तिच् it signifies “the back” or “at the<BR>side of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ट्वा
पृष्ट्वा Ind. Having asked.<BR> E. प्रच्छ् to ask, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठ|पृष्ठं
पृष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. The back.<BR>	 2. The rear, the last, the back or hinder part<BR>of any thing.<BR>	 3. The surface or superficies.<BR>	 4. The back or the<BR>other side, (as of a document.)<BR>	 5. The flat roof of a house.<BR> E. पृष् to<BR>sprinkle, Unādi aff. थक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठगोप|पृष्ठगोपः
पृष्ठगोप m. (-पः) A soldier who protects the rear of a warrior while he<BR>is fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठग्रन्थि|पृष्ठग्रंथि|पृष्ठग्रन्थिः
पृष्ठग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) A hump on the back.<BR> E. पृष्ठ the back, ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठचक्षुस्
पृष्ठचक्षुस् m. (-क्षुः) A crab. According to Vāchaspatya:--A bear.<BR> E. पृष्ठ<BR>the back, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठतल्पन
पृष्ठतल्पन n. (-नं) The exterior muscles on the back of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठतस्
पृष्ठतस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Behind, at the back of.<BR>	 2. Backwards.<BR>	 3. Secretly, covert-<BR>ly.<BR> E. पृष्ठ the back, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठदृष्टि|पृष्ठदृष्टिः
पृष्ठदृष्टि m. (-ष्टिः) A bear.<BR> E. पृष्ठ and दृष्टि sight, looking behind him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठफल
पृष्ठफल n. (-लं) Superficial contents of any figure.<BR> E. पृष्ठ and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठमांस
पृष्ठमांस n. (-सं) A fleshy protuberance on the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठमांसाद|पृष्ठमांसादः
पृष्ठमांसाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) A backbiter, a talebearer, a slanderer.<BR> E. पृष्ठ<BR>the back, मांस the flesh, अद् to eat, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठमांसादन|पृष्ठमांसादनं
पृष्ठमांसादन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) A backbiter.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Backbiting, slandering.<BR>E. पृष्ठमांस and अदन eating: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठयान
पृष्ठयान n. (-नं) Riding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठवंश|पृष्ठवंशः
पृष्ठवंश m. (-शः) The back-bone.<BR> E. पृष्ठ the back, and वंश a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठवास्तु
पृष्ठवास्तु n. (-स्तु) The upper story of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठवाह्
पृष्ठवाह् m. (-वाट् or वाड्) An ox of burthen, or one in training.<BR> E. पष्ठ<BR>and वाह् who bears: also प्रष्ठवाह् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठवाह्य|पृष्ठवाह्यः
पृष्ठवाह्य m. (-ह्यः) An ox of burthen, carrying any thing on his back. E.<BR>पृष्ठ the back, वह् to bear, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठरक्ष|पृष्ठरक्षः
पृष्ठरक्ष m. (-क्षः) See पृष्ठगोप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठशय
पृष्ठशय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Sleeping on the back.<BR> E. पृष्ठ and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठशृङ्ग|पृष्ठशृंग|पृष्ठशृङ्गः
पृष्ठशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A wild goat.<BR> E. पृष्ठ the back, and शृङ्ग a horn, whose<BR>horn bends over towards the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठशृङ्गिन्|पृष्ठशृंगिन्
पृष्ठशृङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A buffalo.<BR>	 2. An eunuch.<BR>	 3. A name of BHIMASENA.<BR>4. A ram.<BR> E. पृष्ठ the back, शृङ्ग a horn, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठास्थि
पृष्ठास्थि n. (-स्थि) The back bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठ्य|पृष्ठ्यं|पृष्ठ्यः
पृष्ठ्य mfn. (-ष्ठ्यः-ष्ठ्या-ष्ठ्यं) Relating or belonging to the back.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठ्यः) A<BR>pack-horse.<BR>	 n. (-ष्ठ्यं) A multitude of back bones.<BR> E. पष्ठ the back,<BR>यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्णि|पृष्णिः
पृष्णि mfn. (-ष्णिः-ष्णिः-ष्णि) Small, short or thin: see पृश्नि.<BR>	 f. (-ष्णिः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>heel: see पार्ष्णि.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR> E. पृष् to sprinkle, नि Unādi aff.<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पॄ
पॄ r. 3rd. cl. (पिपर्त्ति)<BR>	 1. To fill.<BR>	 2. To blow 3. To satisfy. जुही०<BR>पर० सक० सेट् । 9th cl. (पृणाति) To rear, to bring up, &c. क्य्र० भ्वा० पर०<BR>सक० सेट् । r. 10th cl. (पारयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To nourish, to protect.<BR>	 2. To fill.<BR>चु० उभ० सक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचक|पेचकः
पेचक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An owl.<BR>	 2. The root of an elephant's tail.<BR>	 3. The tip<BR>of it.<BR>	 4. A cloud.<BR>	 5. A bed.<BR>	 6. A louse.<BR> E. पच् to spread, Unādi aff.<BR>वुन्, इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचकिन्
पेचकिन् m. (-की) An elephant.<BR> E. पेचक the root of an elephant's tail, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचिल|पेचिलः
पेचिल m. (-लः) An elephant.<BR> E. पेच for पेचक as above, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचु
पेचु m. (-चुः) An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR> E. पिच् to hurt, उ aff.;<BR>also with उलट् aff. पेचुल, fem. पेचुली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचुली
पेचुली f. (-ली) An esculent root: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेञ्जूष|पेंजूष|पेंजूषः|पेञ्जूषः
पेञ्जूष m. (-षः) The wax of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेट|पेटः
पेट mf. (-टः-टा or -टी) A basket, a bag, a chest, a large basket.<BR>	 m. (-टः)<BR>The open hand with the fingers extended.<BR> E. पिट् to collect, घञ् and<BR>टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटक|पेटकं|पेटकः
पेटक mn. (-कः-कं) A basket for holding clothes, books, &c.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>Multitude, quantity.<BR> E. पिट् to collect, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटाक|पेटाकः
पेटाक m. (-कः) A basket.<BR> E. पेटा, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटिका
पेटिका f. (-का) A box, a basket.<BR> E. पेटा and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटी
पेटी f. (-टी) A small basket.<BR> E. पिट्, aff. अच्, ङीप् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेडा
पेडा f. (-डा) A basket, a large basket.<BR> E. पिड् to collect, affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेण
पेण(ऋ)पेणृ r. 1st cl. (पेणति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To embrace.<BR>	 3. To grind: it<BR>is more usually read पैणु; गतौ पेषेच सक० श्लेषे अक० भ्वा० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेत्व|पेत्वं|पेत्वः
पेत्व m. (-त्वः) A small part.<BR>	 n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Nectar.<BR>	 2. Ghee or clarified<BR>butter.<BR> E. पा to drink, इत्वन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेपीयमान
पेपीयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) To be drank repeatedly.<BR> E. पा to drink, reit. v.,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेय|पेयं
पेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Drinkable, drink.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Milk.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>1. Rice gruel.<BR>	 2. Decoction of any thing after straining.<BR>	 3. Any<BR>drink with a small quantity of boiled rice.<BR>	 4. Anise, (Pimpinella<BR>anisum.)<BR> E. पा to drink, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेयु|पेयुः
पेयु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. The sea.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेयूष|पेयूषं|पेयूषः
पेयूष mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>	 1. The milk of a cow, which has calved within seven<BR>days.<BR>	 2. Fresh Ghee.<BR>	 3. Amrita or nectar.<BR> E. पीय Sautra root, for<BR>पा to drink, ऊसुन् Unādi aff., and the vowel changed; otherwise<BR>पीयूष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरा
पेरा f. (-रा) A kind of musical instrument.<BR> E. पि वा रे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरु|पेरुः
पेरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. The golden mountain.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 4. Fire.<BR>E. पा to drink, Unādi aff. रु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरोज|पेरोजं
पेरोज n. (-जं) The turquoise: it is the Persian word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेल|पेलं|पेलः
पेल(ऋ)पेऌ r. 1st cl. (पेलति) To go or move. r. 10th cl. (पेलयति-ते) To<BR>shake, to tremble. कम्पे अक० गतौ सक० भ्वा० पर० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेल|पेलं|पेलः
पेल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A small part.<BR>	 2. Going.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A testicle.<BR> E. पिल् to send,<BR>aff. घञ्, or पेल् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलव|पेलवं
पेलव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Delicate, fine.<BR>	 2. Thin, slim, slender.<BR>	 3. Soft. E.<BR>पेल, वा to get, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलि|पेलिः
पेलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. One who goes.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR> E. पेल, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलिन्
पेलिन् m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR> E. पेल going, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेव
पेव(ऋ)पेवृ r. 1st cl. (पेवते) To gratify by service, to serve, to attend on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशल|पेशलः
पेशल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Dexterous, clever.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, agreeable,<BR>3. Fraudulent, crafty.<BR>	 4. Soft, smooth.<BR>	 5. Tender, delicate.<BR>	 6.<BR>Thin, slender.<BR> E. पिश् to be a component part, अलच् aff.; also पेषल<BR>and पेसल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशस्कत्
पेशस्कत् m. (-कृत्) A sort of insect, a kind of wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशि|पेशिः
पेशि m. (-शिः) The thunderbolt.<BR>	 f. (-शिः or -शी)<BR>	 1. An egg.<BR>	 2. Split pease.<BR>E. पिश् to be a part, Unādi aff. इन्; also with ङीप् added in the<BR>fem, form पेशी, as below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशी
पेशी f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. The egg of a bird.<BR>	 2. A blown bud.<BR>	 3. Spikenard,<BR>(Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>	 4. A ball of flesh or meat.<BR>	 5. A sheath, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">Page469-a+ 60</a>]<BR>scabbard.<BR>	 6. A muscle.<BR>	 7. The fetus shortly after conception.<BR>8. A kind of musical instrument.<BR>	 9. The name a river.<BR>	 10.<BR>The name of a female imp or demon.<BR> E. पिश् to be a component<BR>part, aff. इन् and ङीप् added; also पेशि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=468-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशी
पेशी(शि)कोष(श) m. (-षः or शः) A bird's egg. “अण्डकोषेच” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेश्वर
पेश्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Who or what grinds.<BR> E. पिश् to grind, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेष|पेषः
पेष(ऋ)पेषृ r. 1st cl. (पेषते) To resolve or endeavour diligently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषण|पेषणं
पेषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Grinding, pulverising, reducing to dust or powder.<BR>	 2.<BR>A hand mill, a stone and muller, any apparatus for grinding or<BR>pounding.<BR>	 3. A plant, (a sort of Euphorbia with three lobes, com-<BR>monly Teṇkātāsij.)<BR> E. पिश् to grind, aff. ल्युट्; also पेषणि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषणि|पेषणिः
पेषणि f. (-णिः or -णी) A stone slab on which condiments, &c. are ground<BR>with a muller.<BR> E. पिश् to grind, aff. अनि and ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषल|पेषलः
पेषल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Dexterous, clever.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, handsome:<BR>see पेशल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषाक|पेषाकः
पेषाक m. (-कः) A small slab for grinding any thing upon.<BR> E. पिष् to grind, Unādi aff. आकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेस
पेस(ऋ)पेसृ r. 1st cl. (पेसति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेसल|पेसलः
पेसल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Dexterous.<BR>	 2. Handsome, see पेशल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेस्वर
पेस्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Destructive.<BR>	 2. Moving, going.<BR>	 3. Splendid.<BR> E. पिस्<BR>to hurt, &c. वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पै
पै r. 1st cl. (पायति) To dry, to wither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैङ्गि|पैंगि|पैंगिः|पैङ्गिः
पैङ्गि m. (-ङ्गिः) A patronymic of Yāska.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैञ्जूष|पैंजूष|पैंजूषः|पैञ्जूषः
पैञ्जूष m. (-षः) The ear.<BR> E. पिजि to injure, aff. ऊषन्, and the radical<BR>vowel augmented, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैठर|पैठरं
पैठर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Boiled in a pot, (flesh, &c.)<BR> E. पिठर a vessel, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैठीनसि|पैठीनसिः
पैठीनसि m. (-सिः) A Muni, author of a system of laws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैण्
पैण्(ऋ)पैणृ r. 1st cl. (पैणति)<BR>	 1. To go or approach.<BR>	 2. To command or<BR>direct, (an act.)<BR>	 3. To touch or embrace.<BR>	 4. To pound or grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैण्डिन्य|पैंडिन्य|पैंडिन्यं|पैण्डिन्यं
पैण्डिन्य n. (-न्यं) Mendicity, living upon alms.<BR> E. पिण्ड a ball of meat or<BR>rice, इनि poss. aff., यञ् aff. of condition: Also पैण्डिक्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतामह|पैतामहं
पैतामह mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>	 1. Belonging or relating to the grand-father,<BR>inherited from him, (property, &c.)<BR>	 2. Relating to Brahmā.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>plu. Ancestors, forefathers.<BR> E. पितामह, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृक|पैतृकं
पैतृक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Paternal, ancestral, belonging or relating to the<BR>father or to progenitors.<BR>	 2. Sacred to the manes.<BR>	 n. (कं) A Śhrā-<BR>ddha performed in honor of the manes.<BR> E. पितृ a father, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृकभूमि|पैतृकभूमिः
पैतृकभूमि f. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. Father-land, the country of one's ancestors.<BR>	 2. A<BR>paternal estate.<BR> E. पैतृक, भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृकष्वसेय
पैतृकष्वसेय m. (-यः) A paternal aunt's son.<BR>	 f. (-यी) The daughter of a<BR>paternal aunt.<BR> E. पितृ a father, स्वसृ a sister, aff. ढक् whence the<BR>vowel of स्वसृ is rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृमत्य|पैतृमत्यः
पैतृमत्य m. (-त्यः) The son of an unmarried woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृस्वस्रीय
पैतृस्वस्रीय mf. (-यः-या) The son or daughter of a father's sister.<BR> E. पितृ<BR>a father, स्वसृ a sister, छण् aff. whence the ऋ of स्वसृ is changed to<BR>री ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्ति
पैत्ति mfn. (-त्तः-त्ती-त्तं) Biliary, bilious.<BR> E. पित्त, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्तिक|पैत्तिकः
पैत्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bilious, biliary.<BR> E. पित्त, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्र|पैत्रं
पैत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Paternal, ancestral, relating or belonging to a<BR>parent or progenitor.<BR>	 2. Sacred to the manes.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The part<BR>of the hand between the thumb and forefinger, or according to<BR>some the root of the forefinger.<BR>	 2. A year, month, day, &c. of the<BR>Pitṛs.<BR> E. पितृ a parent, aff. अण् । Also पैत्र्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्राहोरात्र|पैत्राहोरात्रः
पैत्राहोरात्र m. (-त्रः) A day and night of the Pitṛs, or progenitors, equal<BR>to a month of mortals.<BR> E. पैत्र relating to the manes, अहन् a day,<BR>and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्रिक्
पैत्रिक् mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Paternal, ancestral.<BR> E. पितृ, and ठञ् aff. and the<BR>vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैल|पैलः
पैल m. (-लः) A Sage, the promulgator of the Rig-Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैलव
पैलव Adj.<BR>	 f. (-वी) Made of the wood of the pilu tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशल्य|पैशल्यं
पैशल्य n. (-ल्यं) Mildness, affability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाच|पैशाचः
पैशाच mfn. (-चः-ची-चं) Infernal, demoniacal, relating or belonging to a<BR>Pīśacha or goblin.<BR>	 m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. A mode of marriage the ravishment<BR>of a girl by her lover; it is the last of the eight forms of marriage<BR>in Hindu law, in it the lover defiles a damsel without her consent<BR>when she is sleeping or intoxicated or deranged in intellect.<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of demon.<BR>	 f. (-ची)<BR>	 1. A present to a friend, or to secure friendly<BR>regard made at a religious ceremony.<BR>	 2. Night.<BR>	 3. The lowest Prā-<BR>krita dialect spoken on the stage by demons in Hindu dramatical<BR>representations.<BR> E. पिशाच an imp, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाचिक
पैशाचिक Adj.<BR>	 f. (-की) Infernal, demoniacal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुन|पैशुनं
पैशुन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Information, reporting evil of others.<BR>	 2. Roguery.<BR>3. Backbiting.<BR> E. पिशुन a spy, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुन्ध
पैशुन्ध n. (-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Information, espionage, &c.<BR>	 2. Depravity, wickedness.<BR>E. पिशुन a spy, a rogue, aff. यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्ट|पैष्टः
पैष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टी-ष्टं) Ground or made up into a cake.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टी) Spiritu-<BR>ous liquor distilled from meal.<BR> E. पिष्ट ground, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्टिक|पैष्टिकं
पैष्टिक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A quantity of cakes.<BR>	 2. Spirituous liquor distilled from<BR>meal.<BR>	 f. (की) Made of flour.<BR> E. पिष्ट, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोगण्ड|पोगंड|पोगण्डः
पोगण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Deformed, having a redundant or defective<BR>member.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः) A boy one from his fifth to his sixteenth year,<BR>E. अपि certainly, गडि to be a part of the cheek., अच् affs the अ<BR>of the prefix is rejected, and the इ changed to ओ; otherwise,<BR>अप depreciative prefix, गम् to go, and the deriv. irr.; also<BR>अपोगण्ड; in the second sense it also occurs पौगण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोट|पोटः
पोट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The foundation of a house, &c.<BR>	 2. Uniting, mixing.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-टा)<BR>	 1. A woman having a beard.<BR>	 2. A female servant or slave.<BR>	 3.<BR>A masculine woman, an amazon.<BR>	 4. A hermaphrodite. (-टी) A.<BR>large alligator.<BR> E. पुट् to shine, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटगल|पोटगलः
पोटगल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A reed, (Arundo tibialis, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A sort of grass,<BR>(Saccharum spontanium.)<BR>	 3. A fish.<BR> E. पोट uniting, (with the<BR>wind,) गल् to go, aff. अच्, waving in the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोट|पोटः
पोट(ट्ट)लिका f. (-का) A bundle or packet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटिक|पोटिकः
पोटिक m. (-कः) A boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोट्टली
पोट्टली f. (-ली) A bundle, a parcel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोडु|पोडुः
पोडु m. (-डुः) The lower surface of the parietal bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत|पोतः
पोत mf. (-तः-ती) The young of any animal.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A young elephant<BR>of ten years old.<BR>	 2. A vessel, a ship, a boat.<BR>	 3. The site of a<BR>house or dwelling.<BR>	 4. Cloth, a garment.<BR>	 5. The young shoot of a<BR>plant.<BR> E. पूञ् to purify, तन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतक|पोतकः
पोतक m. (-कः) The young of an animal.<BR>	 2. A young plant.<BR>	 3. The scite of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतकी
पोतकी f. (-की) A potherb, (Basella lucida.)<BR> E. पूत nominal verb, from<BR>पूत a stench, वुञ् aff. ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतज|पोतजः
पोतज m. (-जः) An animal that produces young at once without the<BR>intervention of any medium: elephants and some other animals<BR>being supposed in Hindu physiology to carry the young without the<BR>aid of an ovarium or uterus.<BR> E. पोत young, and जन् to bear, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतवणिज्
पोतवणिज् m. (-णिक्) A voyaging merchant.<BR> E. प्रोत a boat, and वणिक् a<BR>trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतरक्ष|पोतरक्षः
पोतरक्ष m. (-क्षः) The rudder of a boat, or large oar used as one.<BR> E. पोत<BR>a boat, रक्ष to preserve, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतलकप्रिय|पोतलकप्रियः
पोतलकप्रिय m. (-यः) One of the Jinas or Jaina deified teachers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतवाह|पोतवाहः
पोतवाह m. (-हः) A rower, a boatman, a steersman, a towman, or one<BR>of the crew that keeps watch and the mast-head.<BR> E. पोत a boat,<BR>वह् to bear, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोताच्छादन|पोताच्छादनं
पोताच्छादन n. (-नं) A tent.<BR> E. पोत a cloth, आच्छादन covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोताधान|पोताधानं
पोताधान n. (-न) Small fry, a shoal of young fish.<BR> E. पोत, and आघान<BR>taking; being caught in bags.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतास|पोतासः
पोतास m. (-सः) A sort of camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतिका
पोतिका f. (-का) A potherb, (Basella rubra and lucida.)<BR> E. पूत nominal<BR>verb, to stink, aff. वुन्, fem. aff. टाष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=469-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोतृ
पोतृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. One of the Sixteen officiating priests at a sacrifice.<BR>2. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. पू to make pure, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्र|पोत्रं
पोत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The snout of a hog.<BR>	 2. The share of a plough.<BR>	 3. The<BR>thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>	 4. A boat, a ship.<BR>	 5. A garment.<BR>	 6. The<BR>office of the Hotri.<BR> E. पू to make pure, त्र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्रायुध|पोत्रायुधः
पोत्रायुध m. (-धः) A hog.<BR> E. पोत्र a snout, आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्रिदंष्ट्राज
पोत्रिदंष्ट्राज m. (-जः) A gem, supposed to be found in the tooth of a hog.<BR>E. पोत्रि a hog, दंष्ट्रा a tooth, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्रिन्
पोत्रिन् m. (-त्री) A hog.<BR> E. पोत्र the snout, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोत्रिरथा
पोत्रिरथा f. (-था) One of the Śaktis or the female divinities of the<BR>Jainas.<BR> E. पोत्रि a hog, and रथ a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोथकी
पोथकी f. (-की) Red pimples on the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोपुव
पोपुव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Purifying or cleansing much or repeatedly.<BR> E. पू<BR>to purify, intents. v., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोल|पोलः
पोल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Magnitude, bulk.<BR>	 2. A heap, a quantity.<BR> E. पुल् to be great, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोलिका
पोलिका f. (-का) Flat cakes made of barley or wheat, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोलिन्द|पोलिंद|पोलिंदः|पोलिन्दः
पोलिन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. A part of a boat supporting the deck, (the knees or<BR>ribs of a boat.)<BR>	 2. The mast of a ship.<BR> E. पोल magnitude, इदि to be<BR>supreme, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष|पोषः
पोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>	 2. Increase, growth.<BR>	 3. Plenty,<BR>abundance.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish, aff. घञ्; also with ल्युट् aff. पोषण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषण|पोषणं
पोषण n. (-णं) Nourishing, cherishing.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषणीय
पोषणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be cherished or protected.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish,<BR>अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषयित्रु
पोषयित्रु mfn. (-त्रुः-त्रुः-त्रु) Nourishing, cherishing.<BR>	 m. (त्रुः) The Kokila or<BR>Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish, in the causal form, इत्रुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोषितव्य
पोषितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be cherished or protected.<BR> E. पुष्, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्टृ
पोष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Who or what nourishes, cherishes, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टा)<BR>1. Grey bonduc.<BR>	 2. A protector, a cherisher.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish,<BR>aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्टृवर|पोष्टृवरः
पोष्टृवर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Who or what nourishes best.<BR> E. पोष्टृ and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्य|पोष्यः
पोष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. To be cherished or taken care of.<BR>	 2. A class of<BR>relatives who claim compulsory maintenance.<BR> E. पुष् to nourish,<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्यत्व
पोष्यत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Cherishing dependents.<BR>	 2. Being taken care of.<BR> E. पोष्य, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्यपुत्त्र
पोष्यपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) An adopted son.<BR> E. पोष्य and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोष्यवर्ग|पोष्यवर्गः
पोष्यवर्ग m. (-र्गः) A class of persons or objects to be cherished as<BR>parents, children, guests, and the sacred fire.<BR> E. पोष्य and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौश्चल्य
पौश्चल्य n. (-ल्यं) Female incontinency, harlotry.<BR> E. पुंश्चली a lewd woman,<BR>यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौंसवन|पौंसवनं
पौंसवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. One of the Sanskāras or essential ceremonies of the<BR>Hindu religion; a religion; a religious observance held on a woman's perce-<BR>iving the first signs of a living conception.<BR>	 2. fetus.<BR>	 3. milk. E.<BR>पुंसवन, q. v., with अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौस्न
पौस्न mfn. (-स्नः-स्नी-स्नं) Virile, manly, relating to or good for man.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-स्नं) Manhood.<BR> E. पुं man, स्नञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौगण्ड|पौगंड|पौगण्डं
पौगण्ड f. (-ण्डी) Boyish.<BR>	 n. (-ण्डं) Boyhood, (from the 5th to the 16th year.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्डर्य्य|पौण्डर्य|पौंडर्यं|पौण्डर्य्यं
पौण्डर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) A drug, commonly Pūndarīya.<BR> E. अण् added to पुण्डर्य्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्र|पौंड्र|पौंड्रः|पौण्ड्रः
पौण्ड्र m. (-ण्ड्रः)<BR>	 1. A country, extending from Rangpur across the<BR>Ganges to the Jungle Mahals and part of south Behar, including<BR>therefore the greater part of Bengal.<BR>	 2. The Native of that<BR>country.<BR>	 3. A king of that country.<BR>	 4. A sort of sugar-cane of<BR>a pale straw colour.<BR>	 5. Name of the conch-shell of Bhīma.<BR> E. पुण्ड्र<BR>the same, aff. अण्; also with कन् added पौण्ड्रक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रक|पौंड्रक|पौंड्रकः|पौण्ड्रकः
पौण्ड्रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The pale straw-coloured species of sugar-cane.<BR>2. A man of a mixed caste, from the Vaiśya and female of the<BR>distiller caste, whose business it is to boil sugar.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to पौण्ड्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रवर्द्धन
पौण्ड्रवर्द्धन m. (-नः) A country, one of the divisions of central India,<BR>(Behar,)<BR> E. पौण्ड्र the sugar-cane, and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौण्ड्रिक|पौंड्रिक|पौंड्रिकः|पौण्ड्रिकः
पौण्ड्रिक m. (-कः) A pale straw variety of the sugar-cane.<BR> E. पुण्ड्र the<BR>same, aff. ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतव|पौतवं
पौतव n. (-वं) Measuring, a measure.<BR> E. पु to be made pure or correct, तन्<BR>aff. and अण् added; also यौतव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौतिनासिक्य
पौतिनासिक्य n. (-क्यं) Fœtor of the nostrils.<BR> E. पुतिनासिका a foul nose, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्तिक|पौत्तिकं
पौत्तिक n. (-कं) Honey of a pale colour.<BR> E. पुत्तिका a small bee, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्त्र
पौत्त्र mfn. (-त्त्रः-त्त्री-त्त्रं) Relating to a son.<BR>	 m. (-त्त्रः) A son's son, a grand-<BR>son.<BR>	 f. (-त्त्री) A grand-daughter, either in the male or female line,<BR>though more usually implying a son's daughter.<BR> E. पुत्त्र or पुत्त्री a son<BR>or daughter, अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्त्रिक
पौत्त्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging to a son or a grandson.<BR> E. पुत्त्र or<BR>पौत्त्र, and ठञ् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्त्रिकेय
पौत्त्रिकेय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A daughter's son.<BR>	 2. The son of a daughter<BR>appointed to raise issue for her father.<BR> E. पुत्त्रिका, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्त्रिन्
पौत्त्रिन् mfn. (-त्त्री-त्त्रिणी-त्त्रि) Having a grandson.<BR> E. पौत्त्र and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनःपुनिक|पौनःपुनिकः
पौनःपुनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Repeated, reiterated, again and again. E.<BR>पुनर, again, repeated, aff. ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनःपुन्यं|पौनःपुन्य
पौनःपुन्यं n. (-न्यं) Reiteration, repetition.<BR> E. पुनर् again, repeated, aff. यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनरुक्त|पौनरुक्तं
पौनरुक्त n. (-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Tautology.<BR>	 2. Superfluity, uselessness.<BR> E. पुनरुक्त, and<BR>अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनर्भव|पौनर्भवः
पौनर्भव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Repeated, additional.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The son of a<BR>widow remarried, one of the twelve sons or heirs admitted by the<BR>old Hindu law; the son of a twice-married woman.<BR>	 2. The second<BR>husband of a woman.<BR> E. पुनर्भव, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर|पौरं|पौरः
पौर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) City, citizen, relating to or produced in a town or<BR>city.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A fragrant grass.<BR> E. पुर a city, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरक|पौरकं|पौरकः
पौरक n. (-कं) A garden round a house.<BR> E. पौर citizen, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरजन|पौरजनः
पौरजन m. (-नः) A citizen.<BR> E. पौर, जन person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरन्दर
पौरन्दर n. (-रं) The luner asterism called Jyeshthā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरव|पौरवः
पौरव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Of the race of Puru, descended from Puru.<BR> E. पुरु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरसख्य
पौरसख्य n. (-ख्यं) Connexion or equality by inhabiting the same city<BR>for ten years, fellow-citizenship.<BR> E. पौर relating to a city, सख्य<BR>friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरस्त्य|पौरस्त्यः
पौरस्त्य mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं)<BR>	 1. Prior, first, initial.<BR>	 2. Foremost.<BR>	 3. Eastern.<BR>E. पुरस् formerly, अण् aff. of relation, पौरस् and त्यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरस्त्री
पौरस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) A woman residing in a town or city.<BR> E. पौरा, and स्त्री a<BR>female; also similar compounds, as पौरयोषित, पौराङ्गना, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराण
पौराण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Relating to the past, or Purānas.<BR> E. पुराण, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराणिक|पौराणिकः
पौराणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of or belonging to the Purānas, Paurānic.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) A Brāhman, well read in the Purānas, a mythologist. E.<BR>पुराण, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुष|पौरुषं|पौरुषः
पौरुष mfn. subst. (-षः-षी-षं) The measure of a man, equal to the height<BR>to which he reaches with both arms elevated, and the fingers<BR>extended. Adj. Manly, of or belonging to man.<BR>	 n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. The<BR>property of manhood, virility, manliness.<BR>	 2. Action, or action<BR>incidental to the state of humanity.<BR>	 3. Semen virile.<BR>	 4. Strength,<BR>power, vigour, heroism.<BR>	 5. The Penis.<BR>	 6. A Sundial.<BR> E. पुरुष a<BR>man, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषता
पौरुषता f. (-ता) Manhood, manly strength or spirit.<BR> E. तल् added to पौरुष;<BR>also with त्व, पौरुषत्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरषेय
पौरषेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Made by, derived from, or relating to man,<BR>human, manly, virile, &c.<BR>	 2. Spiritual.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A crowd or<BR>number of men.<BR>	 2. Manslaughter, murder.<BR>	 3. Law, as affecting<BR>persons.<BR>	 4. A Day-labourer.<BR> E. पुरुष a man, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुष्य|पौरुष्यं
पौरुष्य n. (-ष्यं) Manliness, courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोगव|पौरोगवः
पौरोगव mf. (-वः-वी) Overseer or superintendent of the royal kitchen. E.<BR>पुरुस् first, गौ the eye, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोडाश|पौरोडाशः
पौरोडाश m. (-शः) A prayer, recited upon making an oblation of clarified<BR>butter.<BR> E. पुरोडाश butter offered to fire, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=470-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोडाशिक|पौरोडाशिकः
पौरोडाशिक m. (कः) A priest who recites the prayer used in offering an<BR>oblation of clarified butter.<BR> E. पौरोडाश, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोभाग्य|पौरोभाग्यं
पौरोभाग्य n. (-ग्यं) Ill-luck, censoriousness, fault-finding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोहित्य|पौरोहित्यं
पौरोहित्य n. (-त्यं) The character or functions of family priest.<BR> E. पुरोहित<BR>and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमास|पौर्णमासः
पौर्णमास m. (-सः) A ceremony performed at the full of the moon, by<BR>persons maintaining a perpetual fire.<BR>	 f. (-सी) Day of full-moon. E.<BR>पुर्णमास a rite, &c. aff. अण्. ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णिम|पौर्णिमः
पौर्णिम m. (-मः) An ascetic.<BR>	 f. (-सा) Day of full-moon.<BR> E. पूर्णिमा, and अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्त्तिक|पौर्तिक
पौर्त्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Sacrificial, ceremonial.<BR>	 2. Relating to meritor-<BR>ious deed.<BR> E. पूर्त्त, and aff. ठक्. ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्व|पौर्व
पौर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वी-र्व्वं) Relating, or belonging to the past, to the east,<BR>&c.<BR> E. पूर्व्व and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्वदे
पौर्व्वदे(दै)हिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging to a former body or existence.<BR>E. पूर्व्वदेह, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्वपदिक|पौर्वपदिक
पौर्व्वपदिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to the first member of a compound.<BR> E. पूर्व्वपद and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्वार्द्धिक|पौर्वार्धिक
पौर्व्वार्द्धिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Dwelling or being in the eastern division of<BR>town, &c.<BR> E. पूर्व्वार्द्ध eastern half or part, and ठञ् aff.; also with<BR>घञ्, पौर्व्वार्द्ध; and with यत्, पूर्व्वार्द्ध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्वापर्य्य|पौर्वापर्य|पौर्वापर्यं|पौर्वापर्य्य
पौर्व्वापर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Priority and subsequence.<BR>	 2. Context.<BR> E. पूर्व्वापर<BR>first and last, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्वाह्णिक|पौर्वाह्णिक|पौर्व्वाह्णिकः
पौर्व्वाह्णिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging or relating to or produced in the<BR>forepart of the day.<BR> E. पूर्व्वाह्ण forenoon, aff. ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व्विक|पौर्विक
पौर्व्विक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Prior, primary, former.<BR>	 2. Ancestral.<BR> E. पूर्व्व<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलस्त्य|पौलस्त्यः
पौलस्त्य m. (-स्त्यः)<BR>	 1. KUVERA.<BR>	 2. RĀVAṆA.<BR>	 3. Either of the brothers of<BR>RĀVANA, VIBHĪṢAṆA or KUMBHAKARṆA.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR>	 f. (-स्त्यी)<BR>The sister of RĀVANA, ŚŪRPANAKHĀ.<BR> E. पुलस्त्य a saint so named,<BR>and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलि|पौलिः
पौलि mf. (-लिः-ली) Grain half dressed, or scorched or fried with Ghee,<BR>and made into a sort of cake.<BR> E. पौल a heap, इञ् aff. and ङीप्<BR>added for the fem.; also with कन् added पौलिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलिका
पौलिका f. (-का) A sort of cake: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलोमी
पौलोमी f. (-मी) Sachi, the Daughter of Puloman and wife of INDRA.<BR>E. पुलोमन् a saint, the father of the goddess, अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलोमीसम्भव|पौलोमीसंभवः
पौलोमीसम्भव m. (-वः) An epithet of Jayanta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष|पौषः
पौष m. (-षः) The month Pausha, in which the moon is in the Pushya<BR>asterism, (December-January.)<BR>	 f. (-षी) Day of full moon in the<BR>month of Pausha.<BR> E. पुष्य the asterism in which the moon is full in<BR>this month, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्कर|पौष्करं
पौष्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Relating to a pond, to a lotus, to fragrant Costus,<BR>&c.<BR> E. पुष्कर, q. v., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पष्करिणी
पष्करिणी f. (-णी) A large pond or reservoir, a lotus-pool.<BR> E. पुष्करिणी the<BR>same, and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्कल्य|पौष्कल्यं
पौष्कल्य n. (-ल्यं) Maturity, complete development.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्टिक|पौष्टिकं
पौष्टिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Preservative, protective, nutritive, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Nutritious, fattening.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A cloth worn when the ceremony of<BR>tonsure is performed.<BR> E. पुष्टि nourishing, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्ण|पौष्णं
पौष्ण n. (-ष्णं) The last of the twenty-eight lunar asterisms; also REVATĪ.<BR>E. पूषन् the sun, in this name regent of the asterism, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्प|पौष्पं
पौष्प mfn. (-ष्पः-ष्पी-ष्पं) Flowery, floral, relating or belonging to flowers,<BR>&c.<BR> E. पुष्प, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्पक|पौष्पकं
पौष्पक n. (-कं) The oxid of brass, considered as a collyrium.<BR> E. पुष्पक<BR>the same, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्पी
पौष्पी f. (-ष्पी)<BR>	 1. A name of Palibothra or mordern Patna.<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>spirituous liquor.<BR> E. पुष्प a flower, अण् aff. and ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ना
प्ना f. (-प्ना) Sivās braided hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्याट्
प्याट् Ind. A particle of calling, ho ! hola !<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्याय्
प्याय्(ओ)(ई)ओप्यायी r. 1st cl. (प्यायते) To grow or increase, to enlarge or<BR>swell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यायन
प्यायन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Increased.<BR>	 2. Growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यायित
प्यायित f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Increased.<BR>	 2. Grown fat.<BR>	 3. Refreshed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्युष्
प्युष्(इर)प्युषिर r. 4th cl. (प्युष्यति)<BR>	 1. To burn.<BR>	 2. To share or divide.<BR>r. 10th cl. (प्युषयति-ते) To relinquish, to part with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्युस्
प्युस् r. 4th cl. (प्युष्यति)<BR>	 1. To divide.<BR>	 2. To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यै
प्यै(ङ)प्यैङ् r. 1st cl. (प्यायते)<BR>	 1. To grow or increase.<BR>	 2. To swell. Caus.<BR>(प्याययति-ते) With आ to make comfortable.<BR>	 2. To enlarge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्र
प्र Ind. A particle and prefix, implying.<BR>	 1. Progressive motion, (forth,<BR>forward, away, &c.)<BR>	 2. Excess or excellence, (very, much, excee-<BR>ding.)<BR>	 3. Appearance, manifestation. It corresponds with the Latin<BR>particles Pro and Præ, as in प्रकर्त्तुं To do much or well; प्रक्रमितुं To<BR>go forth or over; प्रकर्षितुं To excel; प्रकाशितुं To display; प्रस्थातुं To<BR>go forth, set out; प्रकमम् Very willingly; प्रमृगम् When the deer go<BR>forth, (the time, &c.) See the following compounds.<BR> E. प्रथ् to be<BR>famous, &c. aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकट|प्रकटं
प्रकट mfn. (-टः-टी-टं) Displayed, unfolded, manifest, apparent.<BR> E. प्र im-<BR>plying manifestation, and कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटम्
प्रकटम् Ind. It is also used as an indeclinable in the sense of:--1. Clear,<BR>evident.<BR>	 2. Undisguished, public.<BR>	 3. Visible: see the above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटन|प्रकटनं
प्रकटन n. (-नं) The act of manifesting or disclosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटित|प्रकटितं
प्रकटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Manifested, displayed.<BR>	 2. Evident, apparent.<BR>3. Opened, expanded.<BR> E. प्र before, कट् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटीकरण
प्रकटीकरण n. (-णं) Making visible or apparent, displaying, manifesting.<BR>E. प्रकट, and करण making, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटीकृत
प्रकटीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made manifest, open, or visible.<BR> E. प्रकट, and कृत made, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्प|प्रकंप|प्रकंपः|प्रकम्पः
प्रकम्प m. (-म्पः)<BR>	 1. Shaking, trembling.<BR>	 2. Violent motion.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>कपि to tremble, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पन|प्रकंपन|प्रकम्पनः
प्रकम्पन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Trembling violently.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Wind, air, (gener-<BR>ally violent.)<BR>	 2. A hell.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Violent or excessive motion, great<BR>trembling.<BR> E. प्र implying excess, कम्पन trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पमान
प्रकम्पमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shaking, trembling violently.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>कपि to tremble, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकम्पयत्
प्रकम्पयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Shaking, agitating.<BR> E. प्र before, कपि to<BR>tremble, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर|प्रकरं|प्रकरः
प्रकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who or what does much or well.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>heap a, quantity.<BR>	 2. A bundle of flowers, a nosegay.<BR>	 3. Aid, assis-<BR>tance, friendship.<BR>	 4. Usage, custom, continuance of a similar<BR>practice.<BR>	 5. Respect.<BR>	 6. Seduction, abduction.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Aloe wood,<BR>(Agallochum.)<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Theatrical dress or disguise, as wearing<BR>a woman's garb, &c.<BR>	 2. An episodical incident in a drama.<BR>	 3. An<BR>open piece of ground, the meeting of four roads, or the proper<BR>scite of any magical operations.<BR> E. प्र before कृ to make, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरण|प्रकरणं
प्रकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. An introduction, a prologue or prelude.<BR>	 2. A poetical<BR>fiction or poem, in which the story and principal persons are<BR>wholly imaginary; the term is especially applied to a dramatic<BR>poem.<BR>	 3. A chapter, a section, a book, a place of pausing or<BR>stopping.<BR>	 4. Treating with respect.<BR>	 5. Doing much or well.<BR>	 6. Op-<BR>pertunity, occasion.<BR>	 7. Subject, topic.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A minor drama of<BR>the same character as the prakarana, but of less extent; also<BR>प्रकरणिका.<BR> E. प्र before, कृ to make, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकश
प्रकश m. (-शः) Hurting, killing.<BR> E. प्र, कश् to hurt, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्ष|प्रकर्षः
प्रकर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Excellence, eminence, superiority.<BR>	 2. Speciality, intensity,<BR>universality.<BR>	 3. Absoluteness, definitiveness.<BR>	 4. Strength, power.<BR>5. Length, protractedness.<BR>	 6. (In grammar.) The effect of the<BR>prefix “प्र” upon roots; (the inst. and abl. Singulars viz:--प्रकर्षेण<BR>and प्रकर्षात् are used as indeclinables in the sense of “eminently,”<BR>“exceedingly,” “In a high degree.)”<BR> E. प्र before, कृष् to attract, aff.<BR>घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षगमन
प्रकर्षगमन n. (-नं) Going absolutely or finally, departure.<BR> E. प्रकर्ष, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षण
प्रकर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Drawing, attracting.<BR>	 2. Ploughing, drawing furrows.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">Page472-a+ 60</a>]<BR>3. Excellence, superiority.<BR>	 4. Realizing by the use of a pledge<BR>more than interest of the loan.<BR> E. प्र before, कृष् to attract, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=471-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षित
प्रकर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Drawn, drawn out.<BR>	 2. Exceeded in profit,<BR>(the interest of the loan.)<BR>	 n. (-तं) Profit on a pledge beyond interest<BR>of a loan.<BR> E. प्र before, कृष् to make furrows, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकला
प्रकला f. (-ला) A minute portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्पना
प्रकल्पना f. (-ना) Settlement, allotment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्पित
प्रकल्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Done, made.<BR>	 2. Settled f. (-ता) A kind of<BR>riddle.<BR> E. प्र before, कृप् to be able, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाण्ड|प्रकांड|प्रकांडं|प्रकांडः|प्रकाण्डः
प्रकाण्ड mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. The stem of a tree, the part between the root<BR>and the branches.<BR>	 2. A branch, a shoot.<BR>	 3. Excellence, happiness,<BR>(or used as an attributive without admitting variation of gender,)<BR>excellent, best, happy.<BR> E. प्र implying excess or superiority, कम् to<BR>desire, aff. ड, and the penultimate vowel made long by special<BR>rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाण्डर|प्रकांडर|प्रकांडरः|प्रकाण्डरः
प्रकाण्डर m. (-रः) A tree.<BR> E. प्रकाण्ड a stem, रा to get, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाम|प्रकामं|प्रकामः
प्रकाम f. (-मा) Adj.<BR>	 1. Much, excessive, to the heart's content.<BR>	 2. Am-<BR>orous.<BR>	 m. (-मः) Desire, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकामम्
प्रकामम् Ind. Voluntarily, willingly.<BR>	 2. To the heart's content.<BR>	 3. Ex-<BR>ceedingly.<BR> E. प्र implying much, very, काम desire, will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकार|प्रकारः
प्रकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Difference.<BR>	 2. Similitude.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Sort, kind, species.<BR>2. Way, mode, manner.<BR>	 3. Property, quality, speciality,<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>कृ to do, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाश|प्रकाशं|प्रकाशः
प्रकाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शी-शं)<BR>	 1. Like, resembling.<BR>	 2. Open, manifest,<BR>blown, expanded.<BR>	 3. Famous, celebrated.<BR>	 4. Public.<BR>	 n. adv. (-शं)<BR>1. Openly, publicly.<BR>	 2. (In dramatic language), Aloud.<BR>	 f. (-शा)<BR>1. Visible.<BR>	 2. Shining.<BR>	 3. Open.<BR>	 4. Renowned.<BR>	 5. Expanded.<BR>	 6.<BR>Denuded of trees.<BR>	 7. Looking like, (at the end of compounds.)<BR>m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Sunshine, lustre, light.<BR>	 2. Expansion, diffusion, mani-<BR>festation; the word being equally applicable to physical or moral<BR>subjects, as the blowing of a flower, diffusion of celebrity, the<BR>publicity of an event, or the manifestation of a truth.<BR>	 3. A<BR>laugh, a smile.<BR>	 4. Publicity.<BR>	 5. An open spot.<BR>	 6. A golden mirror.<BR>7. The chapter of a book.<BR>	 8. Elucidation, (at the end of titles of<BR>works.)<BR>	 n. (-शं) White or bellmetal, brass.<BR> E. प्र implying<BR>motion or eminence, काश् to shine. aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशम्
प्रकाशम् Ind. It is used as an indeclinable in the Sense of:--1. Openly,<BR>publicly.<BR>	 2. Aloud, audibly, (used as a Stage-direction in this<BR>Sense.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशक|प्रकाशकः
प्रकाशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What irradiates, what makes open or apparent,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An illuminator, an expounder, an illustrator.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Sun.<BR> E. प्रकाश to make light or evident, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशकज्ञातृ
प्रकाशकज्ञातृ m. (-ता) A cock.<BR> E. प्रकाशक illuminator, (the sun), and ज्ञातृ<BR>who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशक्रय|प्रकाशक्रयः
प्रकाशक्रय m. (-यः) An open purchase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशता
प्रकाशता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Manifestation, visibility.<BR>	 2. Luminousness.<BR> E. प्रकाश,<BR>and तल् aff.; also with त्व प्रकाशत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशन|प्रकाशनः
प्रकाशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Illuminating, giving light.<BR>	 2. Making clear or manifest.<BR>3. Displaying.<BR> E. प्र before, काश् to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशनारी
प्रकाशनारी f. (-री) A public woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशमान
प्रकाशमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Splendid, brilliant, radiant.<BR> E. प्र before, काश् to shine, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशात्मक
प्रकाशात्मक Adj. Shining, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशात्मन्
प्रकाशात्मन् m. (-त्मा)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. An epithet of Śiva.<BR> E. प्रकाश light, आत्मन्<BR>self; light itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशित|प्रकाशितं
प्रकाशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Evident, apparent, manifest, visible.<BR>	 2. Pub-<BR>lished, promulgated.<BR>	 3. Illuminated, enlightened.<BR> E. प्रकाश manifes-<BR>tation, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकिरण|प्रकिरणं
प्रकिरण n. (-णं) Scattering, Strewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्ण|प्रकीर्णं|प्रकीर्णः
प्रकीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Spread abroad, published, promulgated.<BR>	 2.<BR>Expanded, opened.<BR>	 3. Miscellaneous, mixed.<BR>	 4. Scattered, disper-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">Page472-b+ 60</a>]<BR>sed, disordered, confused.<BR>	 5. Agitated, excited, wild.<BR>	 6. Waved, wav-<BR>ing.<BR>	 n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. A Chowri, a cow-tail used as a fan.<BR>	 2. A chapter,<BR>a section.<BR>	 3. A collection of miscellaneous rules.<BR> E. प्र before, कृ<BR>to throw or cast, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्णक|प्रकीर्णकं|प्रकीर्णकः
प्रकीर्णक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A Chowri, the tail of the Bos grunniens, used as a<BR>whisk or fan, a fly-flap.<BR>	 2. The section or chapter of a book.<BR>3. Extent, length, especially of a stanza or book.<BR>	 4. (In law,) A<BR>case not provided for by the Śhastras, and to be decided by the<BR>authority of the judge or king.<BR>	 5. A miscellany.<BR>	 6. Any collection<BR>of heterogeneous objects not arranged under any distinct classes<BR>or heads.<BR>	 f. (-का) Scattered about.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A horse.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to प्रकीर्ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्त्तन|प्रकीर्तन|प्रकीर्तनं
प्रकीर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Proclaiming, announcing.<BR>	 2. Praising, extolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्त्ति|प्रकीर्ति|प्रकीर्तिः
प्रकीर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Fame, celebrity.<BR>	 2. Declaration.<BR>	 3. Praise.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, कॄ to scatter, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्त्तित|प्रकीर्तित|प्रकीर्त्तितं
प्रकीर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Declared, explained, said, revealed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Celebrated, renowned.<BR> E. प्र before, कॄ to scatter, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्य्य|प्रकीर्य|प्रकीर्यः|प्रकीर्य्यः
प्रकीर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be spread abroad or about to be diffused,<BR>promulgated, expanded, or extended.<BR>	 m. (-र्य्यः) A plant, (Cæsal-<BR>pinia bonducella.)<BR> E. प्र progressive motion, कॄ to throw or cast,<BR>aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुञ्च|प्रकुंच|प्रकुंचः|प्रकुञ्चः
प्रकुञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) A particular measure of capacity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुपित
प्रकुपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Enraged, incensed.<BR>	 2. Disordered.<BR>	 3. Stimula-<BR>ted.<BR> E. प्र before, कुप् to be angry, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुर्व्वत्|प्रकुर्वत्
प्रकुर्व्वत् mfn. (-र्व्वन्-र्व्वती-र्व्वत)<BR>	 1. Behaving respectfully to, waiting upon,<BR>serving, honouring.<BR>	 2. Doing much or well.<BR> E. प्र before, कृ to do,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुर्व्वाण|प्रकुर्वाण
प्रकुर्व्वाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Attending, or behaving to with respect.<BR>2. Doing much or well.<BR> E. प्र, and कृ to make, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुल|प्रकुलं
प्रकुल n. (-लं) A handsome or excellent body.<BR> E. प्र excellent, कुल the<BR>body aff. क; also read प्रह्वल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकूष्माण्डी|प्रकूष्मांडी
प्रकूष्माण्डी f. (-ण्डी) An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृत|प्रकृतः
प्रकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made, completed, accomplished.<BR>	 2. Com-<BR>menced.<BR>	 3. Continuing or engaged in what has been begun.<BR>	 4.<BR>That which is under consideration, the Subject in hand, (In<BR>this Sense it is often used for the “Upameya” in works of<BR>rhetoric).<BR>	 5. Genuine, real.<BR>	 6. Appointed, charged.<BR>	 7. Wished,<BR>expected.<BR>	 8. Important, interesting.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The original subject.<BR>E. प्र before, कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृति|प्रकृतिः
प्रकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Nature; in philosophy the passive or material cause<BR>of the world, as opposed to the active or spiritual; and in my-<BR>thology, a goddess, the personified will of the Supreme in the<BR>creation identified with Māyā or illusion, and in an especial<BR>manner the prototype of the female sex; hence it is the same<BR>with the Śakti or personified energy or bride of a deity, as LAKṢMĪ,<BR>DURGĀ, &c. in some systems Prakriti is considered the same<BR>with the Supreme Being.<BR>	 2. The natural state or condition of<BR>any thing.<BR>	 3. A radical form or predicament of being, an illusion,<BR>intelligence, consciousness, and the five elements, or Ākās, fire,<BR>air, earth, and water.<BR>	 4. The five elements collectively.<BR>	 5. Cause,<BR>origin.<BR>	 6. A woman or womankind.<BR>	 7. A mother.<BR>	 8. An animal.<BR>9. The male organ of generation.<BR>	 10. The female organ of genera-<BR>tion.<BR>	 11. An uninflected word; the radical form of a word, before<BR>the affixes forming cases, &c. are subjoined.<BR>	 12. A requisite of<BR>regal administration, of which seven are enumerated; the king,<BR>the minister, an ally, treasure, territory, fortresses, and an army:<BR>the corporations or companies of citizens are sometimes added,<BR>making an eighth class.<BR>	 13. A form of metre, consisting of a stanza<BR>of four lines, each line containing twenty-one syllables.<BR>	 14. (In<BR>arithmetic,) A given coefficient. (In anatomy,) Temperament,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">Page473-a+ 60</a>]<BR>the predominance of one of the humours at the time of generation.<BR>E. प्र implying priority or precedence, कृ to make aff. क्तिन् or क्तिच्;<BR>being the first step towards creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=472-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतितरल
प्रकृतितरल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Volatile, fickle.<BR> E. प्रकृति nature, and तरल changing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतिपुरुष|प्रकृतिपुरुषः
प्रकृतिपुरुष m. (-षः) A minister of State.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतिमण्डल|प्रकृतिमंडल
प्रकृतिमण्डल n. (-लं) The entire kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतिसिद्ध
प्रकृतिसिद्ध n. (-द्धं) Natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतिसुभग
प्रकृतिसुभग Adj. Naturally agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतिस्थ
प्रकृतिस्थ mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Natural, genuine, unmixed.<BR>	 2. Inherent,<BR>innate.<BR>	 3. In good health.<BR>	 4. Stripped of everything.<BR>	 5. Come to<BR>oneself.<BR> E. प्रकृति, and स्थ what is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृशित
प्रकृशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Thin, emaciate.<BR> E. प्र before, कृश् to be thin, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृष्ट|प्रकृष्टं
प्रकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Chief, principal, pre-eminent.<BR>	 2. Remote, far,<BR>long, (as a road).<BR>	 3. Drawn out, lengthy, long.<BR>	 4. Disquieted. E.<BR>प्र eminently, कृष् to attract, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृष्टत्व
प्रकृष्टत्व n. (-त्वं) Eminence, superiority.<BR> E. प्रकृष्ट, and त्व aff.; also with<BR>तल् aff. प्रकृष्टता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॢप्त
प्रकॢप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Made, prepared.<BR>	 2. Mixed.<BR> E. प्र before, कृप् to<BR>make, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोथ|प्रकोथः
प्रकोथ m. (-थः) Putrefaction, putridity.<BR> E. प्र-कुथ्-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोप|प्रकोपः
प्रकोप m. (-पः) Irritation, provocation, enraging.<BR> E. प्र before, कुप् to be<BR>angry, causal v. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपणीय
प्रकोपणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be incensed or enraged.<BR> E. प्र before, कुप्<BR>to be angry, causal v., अनीयर् aff.; and the न optionally changed;<BR>also प्रकोपनीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपन
प्रकोपन n. (-नं) Irritating, provoking.<BR> E. प्र before, कुप् to be angry, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपित
प्रकोपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Irritated, provoked.<BR> E. प्र before, कुप् to be<BR>angry, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोष्ठ|प्रकोष्ठः
प्रकोष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. The fore-arm.<BR>	 2. Part of the frame of a door.<BR>	 3. A<BR>court in the house, or open space surrounded by buildings.<BR>	 4. A<BR>room near the gate of a Palace.<BR> E. प्र before, कुष् to draw, स्थन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्खर|प्रक्खरः
प्रक्खर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A horse's armour.<BR>	 2. A dog.<BR>	 3. A mule. also प्रखर<BR>and प्रक्षर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रन्तृ|प्रक्रंतृ
प्रक्रन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>	 1. Who proceeds or goes.<BR>	 2. Conquering, over-<BR>powering, surpassing.<BR>	 3. Who begins, a beginner.<BR> E. प्र before, क्रम्<BR>to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रम|प्रक्रमः
प्रक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Proceeding, going.<BR>	 2. Leisure, opportunity.<BR>	 3. Begin-<BR>ning.<BR>	 4. Surpassing, overcoming.<BR>	 5. A step, a stride.<BR>	 6. A place<BR>considered as a measure of distance.<BR>	 7. Proportion, order, method.<BR>E. प्र first, क्रम् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रमणीय
प्रक्रमणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be gone or proceeded.<BR> E. प्र before, क्रम् to go,<BR>अनीयर् aff.; also प्रक्रमितव्य and प्रक्रम्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रमभङ्ग|प्रक्रमभंग|प्रक्रमभङ्गः
प्रक्रमभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Want of regularity in expression considered as a<BR>fault of composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रममाण
प्रक्रममाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Proceeding.<BR>	 2. Beginning.<BR>	 3. Overcoming.<BR> E. प्र before, क्रम् to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकान्त
प्रकान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Gone, proceeded.<BR>	 2. Gone beyond, surpassed.<BR>3. Begun.<BR>	 4. Under discussion, in hand.<BR>	 5. Valorous.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, क्रम् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रिया
प्रक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Bearing royal insignia.<BR>	 2. Way, manner, conduct.<BR>3. High position.<BR>	 4. Chapter or section of a book.<BR>	 5. Etymological<BR>formation, (In gram.)<BR> E. प्र principal, क्रिया business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीडित
प्रकीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Playing, sporting.<BR> E. प्र before, क्रीड् to play, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्लिन्न|प्रक्लिन्नः
प्रक्लिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Satisfied.<BR>	 2. Wet, soaked.<BR> E. प्र excess, क्लिद्<BR>to wet, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्वण|प्रक्वणः
प्रक्वण m. (-णः) The sound of the Vīnā or lute.<BR> E. प्र principal, क्वण् to<BR>sound, aff. अप्; also प्रक्वाण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्वाण|प्रक्वाणः
प्रक्वाण m. (-णः) The sound of the Vīṇa or lute.<BR> E. प्र before, क्वण् to sound, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षय|प्रक्षयः
प्रक्षय m. (-यः) Ruin, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षर|प्रक्षरः
प्रक्षर m. (-रः) Iron armour for the defence of a horse or elephant.<BR> E. प्र<BR>best, क्षर to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षरण|प्रक्षरणं
प्रक्षरण n. (-णं) Trickling, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालक
प्रक्षालक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what washes.<BR> E. प्र before, क्षल् to cleanse, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालन|प्रक्षालनं
प्रक्षालन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Bathing.<BR>	 2. Anything used for purifying.<BR>	 3. Water<BR>for washing.<BR>	 4. Cleaning, washing.<BR> E. प्र thoroughly, क्षल् r. 10 cl. to<BR>clean, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालित|प्रक्षालितः
प्रक्षालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Washed, cleansed.<BR> E. प्र before, क्षल् r. 10th cl. to clean, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षिप्त
प्रक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Thrown, cast, hurled.<BR>	 2. Interpolated, spurious.<BR>E. प्र before, क्षिप् to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षिप्तवत्
प्रक्षिप्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Throwing, having thrown.<BR> E. प्र before, क्षिप्<BR>to throw, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षीण
प्रक्षीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Decayed, wasting.<BR>	 2. Destroyed.<BR>	 3. Disappeared.<BR>E. प्र before, क्षि to waste, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षीवित
प्रक्षीवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Intoxicated.<BR> E. प्र before, क्षीव् to be drunk, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षुण्ण
प्रक्षुण्ण f. (ण्णा) Adj.<BR>	 1. Crushed.<BR>	 2. Incited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेप|प्रक्षेपः
प्रक्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Throwing, casting, projecting.<BR>	 2. Throwing into or upon.<BR>3. Anything added, or thrown into drugs when in course of<BR>decoction.<BR>	 4. A throw, a cast.<BR>	 5. Interpolation.<BR>	 6. The sum<BR>deposited by every member of a commercial corporation.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, क्षिप् to throw, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेपण|प्रक्षेपणं
प्रक्षेपण n. (-णं) Throwing, casting.<BR> E. प्र before, क्षिप् to throw, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षोभण|प्रक्षोभणं
प्रक्षोभण n. (-णं) Exciting, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेडन|प्रक्ष्वेडनः
प्रक्ष्वेडन mf. (-नः-ना)<BR>	 1. An iron arrow.<BR>	 2. Clamour, a loud indistinct<BR>noise.<BR> E. प्र especially, क्ष्विद् to sound indistinctly, aff. ल्यु, deriv.<BR>irr.; otherwise प्रक्ष्वेदन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेदन|प्रक्ष्वेदनः
प्रक्ष्वेदन mf. (-नः-ना)<BR>	 1. An iron arrow.<BR>	 2. Calling aloud, clamour: E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेदित
प्रक्ष्वेदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Clamorous, shouting, making loud indistinct<BR>noise.<BR>	 2. Unctuous.<BR> E. प्र before, क्ष्विद् to sound, क्त aff.; also read<BR>प्रक्ष्वेडित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेदितवत्
प्रक्ष्वेदितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Noisy.<BR>	 2. Unctuous.<BR> E. प्र before, क्ष्विद्<BR>to make a noise, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रखर|प्रखरः
प्रखर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Very hot or acrid.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Iron armour, for the<BR>defence of a horse or elephant.<BR>	 2. A dog.<BR>	 3. A mule.<BR> E. प्र very<BR>much, खन् to hurt, aff. रक, derive. irr, or प्र before, खर an ass,<BR>or hot, sharp. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्य|प्रख्यः
प्रख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>	 1. Like, resembling, (in composition.)<BR>	 2. Visible,<BR>distinct.<BR>	 f. (-ख्या)<BR>	 1. Visibility, perceptibility.<BR>	 3. Fame, renown.<BR>	 3.<BR>Similarity, similitude.<BR> E. प्र before, ख्या to say, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यात|प्रख्यातः
प्रख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Celebrated, famous.<BR>	 2. Pleased, happy.<BR>	 3.<BR>Bespoken, forestalled, claimed by right of pre-emption.<BR> E. प्र much,<BR>ख्यात famed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यातभाण्ड
प्रख्यातभाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A commodity that is to be first offered for sale to<BR>some person, (as the Raja, &c.)<BR> E. प्रख्यात claimed, भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यातवप्तृक|प्रख्यातवप्तृकः
प्रख्यातवप्तृक m. (-कः) A gentleman, a Hidalgo, the son of some eminent<BR>person.<BR> E. प्रख्यात known, वप्तृ a father, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्याति|प्रख्यातिः
प्रख्याति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Publicity, celebrity.<BR>	 2. Praise, eulogium.<BR>	 3. Fame. E.<BR>प्र pre eminence, &c. and ख्याति reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यानीय
प्रख्यानीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be celebrated or made known.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>ख्या to say, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगण्ड|प्रगंड|प्रगंडः|प्रगण्डः
प्रगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The upper arm, (from the elbow to the shoulder.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ण्डी) An outer wall or rampart.<BR> E. प्र principal, गण्ड part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगत
प्रगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Separate, apart.<BR>	 2. Gone with difficulty.<BR>	 3.<BR>Gone forward.<BR> E. प्र, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगतजानु|प्रगतजानुः
प्रगतजानु mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु) Bandy-legged, having the knees far apart. E.<BR>प्रगत separated, and जानु the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगतजानुक|प्रगतजानुकः
प्रगतजानुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bandy-legged, bow-legged, having the knees<BR>far apart.<BR> E. प्र away, गत gone, जानु the knee, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगदित
प्रगदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Speaking, beginning to speak.<BR> E. प्र before, गद्<BR>to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगम|प्रगमः
प्रगम m. (मः) The first advance in love-making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगमन|प्रगमनं
प्रगमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Progress, advance.<BR>	 2. The first advance in love-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">Page474-a+ 60</a>]<BR>making.<BR>	 3. Difficult progress.<BR>	 4. Going afar or apart.<BR>	 5. Disputing<BR>words.<BR> E. प्र, and गम् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=473-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगर्जन|प्रगर्जनं
प्रगर्जन n. (-नं) Roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगल्भ|प्रगल्भः
प्रगल्भ mfn. (-ल्भः-ल्भा-ल्भं)<BR>	 1. Bold, confident.<BR>	 2. Prompt, ready.<BR>	 3.<BR>Resolute, energetic.<BR>	 4. Illustrious, eminent.<BR>	 5. Strong, able.<BR>	 6.<BR>Shameless, impudent, audacious.<BR>	 7. Mature.<BR>	 8. Developed,<BR>great.<BR>	 m. (-ल्भः) The fire used for oblations at the birth of a child.<BR>f. (ल्भा)<BR>	 1. A woman who courts her husband's caresses.<BR>	 2. A Scold-<BR>ing woman, a shrew.<BR>	 3. A bold woman experienced in love-matters<BR>considered as a character in poetic composition.<BR> E. प्र much, गल्भ<BR>to be proud, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगलभता
प्रगलभता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Energy, resolution.<BR>	 2. Confidence, boldness.<BR>3. Audacity, arrogance.<BR>	 4. Power, eminence, consequence.<BR>	 5.<BR>Perverseness, wilfulness.<BR> E. तल् aff. of the abstract, added to the<BR>last; also with त्व, प्रगल्भत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगाढ|प्रगाढं
प्रगाढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Much, excessive.<BR>	 2. Hard, difficult.<BR>	 3. Firm.<BR>n. (-ढं) Pain, Privation, penance.<BR>	 n. adv. (-ढं)<BR>	 1. Much, exceed-<BR>ingly.<BR>	 2. Tightly, firmly.<BR> E. प्र before, गाढ much, exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगाढम्
प्रगाढम् Adj. It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of “exceedingly”<BR>“firmly”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगातृ
प्रगातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) A capital singer.<BR> E. प्र excellent, and गातृ who sings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगीत
प्रगीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sung, vocal.<BR> E. प्र, and गीत sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगुण|प्रगुणः
प्रगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Straight.<BR>	 2. Honest, upright, straight in<BR>morals.<BR>	 3. Clever, skilful.<BR> E. प्र excellent, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगुणित
प्रगुणित f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Made straight.<BR>	 2. Made Smooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगुण्य
प्रगुण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. More, exceeding.<BR>	 2. Excellent.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>गुण a quality or quantity and क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगृहीत
प्रगृहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Collected, strung together.<BR>	 2. Accepted,<BR>admitted.<BR>	 3. (In gram.) Pronounced separately without observing<BR>the rules of Sandhi: see the next<BR> E. प्र, and गृहीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगृह्य|प्रगृह्यं
प्रगृह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be taken, accepted, admitted, &c.<BR>	 mn. (-ह्यः-ह्यं)<BR>The class of letters or syllables not subject to the rules of euphony,<BR>as the final ई or ऊ of the dual number. &c. As हरी एतौ, विष्णू इमौ,<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगे
प्रगे Ind. Dawn, morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगेतन|प्रगेतनः
प्रगेतन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Relating, or belonging to the morning.<BR> E. प्रगे<BR>morning, and द्यु aff., तन् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगोपन|प्रगोपनं
प्रगोपन n. (-नं) Protection, preservation, salvation.<BR> E. प्र especially, गोपन preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगथन
प्रगथन n. (-नं) Stringing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रह|प्रग्रहः
प्रग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Taking, seizing.<BR>	 2. Confinement, restriction, restraint,<BR>captivity.<BR>	 3. A prisoner, a captive, either man or beast in confine-<BR>ment.<BR>	 4. A rein, a rope or halter for horses, and cattle.<BR>	 5. The<BR>string suspending a balance.<BR>	 6. Favour, kindness.<BR>	 7. An arm.<BR>	 8. A<BR>ray of light.<BR>	 9. The commencement of an eclipse.<BR>	 10. A vowel not<BR>subject to the rules of Sandhi.<BR>	 11. A sort of Cassia, (C. fistula.)<BR>E. प्र before, ग्रह् to take or seize, aff. अप्; otherwise with घञ् aff.<BR>प्रग्राह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रहण|प्रग्रहणं
प्रग्रहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking, seizing.<BR>	 2. Assuming.<BR>	 3. The commencement<BR>of an eclipse.<BR>	 4. A rein, a bridle.<BR> E. प्र before, ग्रह to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्राह|प्रग्राहः
प्रग्राह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Seizing.<BR>	 2. Taking, taking up, bearing, carrying.<BR>	 3.<BR>The string of a balance.<BR>	 4. A rein, &c.<BR> E. प्र before, ग्रह् to take,<BR>घञ् aff.; see प्रग्रह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रीव|प्रग्रीवः
प्रग्रीव mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>	 1. A window, a lattice, a balcony.<BR>	 2. A summer<BR>house, a pleasure house.<BR>	 3. A building on the top of a palace, a<BR>painted turret.<BR>	 4. A wooden balustrade or fence on the edge of<BR>a building.<BR>	 5. A stable.<BR>	 6. The top of a tree.<BR> E. प्र excessive or<BR>excellent, and ग्रीवा a neck; the neck as it were of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्ल
प्रग्ल mfn. (-ग्लः-ग्ला-ग्लं) Wearied, fatigued, exhausted.<BR> E. प्र before, ग्लै to<BR>be weary, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

घटक|घटकः
घ टक m. (-कः) A rule, a doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघटा
प्रघटा f. (-टा) The first principles of a science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघटाविद्
प्रघटाविद् m. (-विद्) A general reader, but not a profound one.<BR>E. प्रघटा said to imply novelty, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघण|प्रघणः
प्रघण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A terrace before a house.<BR>	 2. A copper pot.<BR>3. An iron crow or club.<BR> E. प्र before हन् to strike, aff. अप्,<BR>and the radical letter changed; also प्रघाण प्रघन, and प्रघान ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघन|प्रघनः
प्रघन m. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A covered terrace before a house.<BR>	 2. A sort of bean,<BR>(Phaseolus mungo.)<BR> E. प्र before, हन् to strike or hurt, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघस|प्रघसः
प्रघस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Voracious.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Eating much.<BR>	 2. A<BR>Daitya, a demon.<BR> E. प्र much, वस for अद् to eat, aff. अप् or अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघाण|प्रघाणः
प्रघाण m. (-णः) A covered terrace or small portico before the<BR>door of house.<BR> E. प्र before, हन् to strike, (with the feet,)<BR>aff. अप्, and the radical vowel changed optionally; also प्रघण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघात|प्रघातः
प्रघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Combat, battle.<BR>	 2. Killing.<BR> E. प्र violently, घात striking;<BR>also प्राघात ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघान|प्रघानः
प्रघान m. (-नः) A covered terrace before the door of a house,<BR>a porch, a portico: see प्रघन, and प्रघण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघुण|प्रघुणः
प्रघुण m. (-णः) A guest; It is another form of प्राघुण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघूर्ण|प्रघूर्णः
प्रघूर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Turning round or rolling violently.<BR>2. Wandering, roaming.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) A guest, a visitor.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, घूर्ण to turn round, aff. अच्ः Also प्राघूर्ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघोषक|प्रघोषकः
प्रघोषक m. (-कः) Sound, noise.<BR> E. प्र much, घोष sound, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचक्र|प्रचक्रं
प्रचक्र n. (-क्रं) An army in motion, or as sometimes explained,<BR>foraging.<BR> E. प्र before, चक्र a division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचक्षस्
प्रचक्षस् m. (-क्षाः)<BR>	 1. The regent of Jupiter, VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, चक्ष् to speak. Unādi aff. असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचण्ड|प्रचंड|प्रचण्डः
प्रचण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Excessively hot or burning.<BR>2. Intolerable, insupportable.<BR>	 3. Bold, confident, presuming.<BR>4. Wrathful, passionate.<BR>	 5. Violent, strong.<BR>	 6. Furious.<BR>	 7. Terrible.<BR>m. (-ण्डः) A sort of Nerium with white flowers.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा) One<BR>of DURGĀ'S emanations or attendants.<BR> E. प्र very, चण्ड hot, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचण्डघोण|प्रचंडघोण
प्रचण्डघोण Adj. Large-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचण्डमूर्त्ति|प्रचण्डमूर्ति|प्रचण्डमूर्त्तिः
प्रचण्डमूर्त्ति m. (-र्त्तिः) A tree, (Tapia cratæva.) “वरुण वृक्षे.”<BR> E. प्रचण्ड Ne-<BR>rium, and मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचय|प्रचयः
प्रचय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A heap, a quantity, a number.<BR>	 2. Gathering,<BR>(as fruit or flowers, but especially by means of a stick or<BR>other implement.)<BR>	 3. Slight union or aggregation.<BR>	 4. Growth,<BR>increase.<BR> E. प्र before, चि to gather, aff. अच्; also with घञ् aff.<BR>प्रचाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचयण
प्रचयण n. (-णं) Collecting, gathering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचर|प्रचरः
प्रचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A road, a path.<BR>	 2. Usage, custom, currency.<BR>3. Going well or widely.<BR> E. प्र before, चर् to go, aff. अप्; also<BR>with घञ् aff. प्रचार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचरण|प्रचरणं
प्रचरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going, proceeding.<BR>	 2. Circulating, being current.<BR>E. प्र before, चर् to go. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचरत्
प्रचरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Going well, quickly, widely, &c.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, चर् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचरित
प्रचरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone, going.<BR>	 2. Pursued, practised,<BR>(as an art or business.)<BR> E. प्र before, चर् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचल|प्रचलः
प्रचल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. What goes much or widely.<BR>	 2. Current,<BR>circulating, customary.<BR>	 4. Shaking, trembling.<BR> E. प्र before, चल्<BR>to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलत्
प्रचलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>	 1. Going, proceeding far or much.<BR>2. Prevailing, circulating, being customary or current.<BR>	 3. Being<BR>recognised, (as authority or law, &c.)<BR> E. प्र before, चल् to<BR>go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलन|प्रचलनं
प्रचलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Moving, going much or widely 2. Circulating,<BR>being customary or current.<BR> E. प्र before, चल् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलाक|प्रचलाकः
प्रचलाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A peacock's tail.<BR>	 2. Archery, shooting with<BR>arrows.<BR>	 3. A snake.<BR> E. प्र before, चल् to go, aff. आकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=474-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलाकिन्
प्रचलाकिन् m. (-की)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. A peacock.<BR> E. प्रचलाक a peacock's<BR>tail, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलायित|प्रचलायितं
प्रचलायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rolling about, tossing, tumbling, (as in<BR>sleep.); Nodding the head, while asleep in a sitting posture.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, चल् to go, in the causal form, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलित
प्रचलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone far or wide, wandering, roving.<BR>2. Sct in motion, shaken.<BR>	 3. Current, customary, circulating,<BR>prevailing.<BR>	 4. Recognised, received, (as authority or law, &c.)<BR>5. Rolling (as the eye).<BR> E. प्र before, चल् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचाय|प्रचायः
प्रचाय m. (-यः) Gathering anything with the hand.<BR> E. प्र, चि to collect,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचायिका
प्रचायिका f. (-का) Gathering in turn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचार|प्रचारः
प्रचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Going, proceeding.<BR>	 2. Custom, usage, 3. Conduct.<BR>4. Currency.<BR>	 5. Appearance, manifestation.<BR>	 6. A Pasture-ground.<BR>	 7.<BR>A play-ground.<BR>	 8. A path, a foot-path.<BR> E. प्र before, चर् to go,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचाल|प्रचालः
प्रचाल m. (-लः) The stick or body of the Vīṇa or lute.<BR> E. प्र before, चर् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचालन|प्रचालनं
प्रचालन n. (-नं) Stirring, moving, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचित
प्रचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Collected, gathered together.<BR>	 f. (ता) Plucked.<BR>2. Amassed, accumulated.<BR>	 3. Covered.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A species of the<BR>Dandaka metre.<BR> E. प्र before, चि to assemble, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुर|प्रचुरं|प्रचुरः
प्रचुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Much, many.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Abundant, plentiful.<BR>	 2. Rep-<BR>lete with, abounding in, (at the end of a compound.)<BR>	 m. (-रः) A<BR>thief.<BR> E. प्र before, चुर् to steal, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरपुरुष|प्रचुरपुरुषः
प्रचुरपुरुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Abounding with men, populous, numerous.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-षः) A thief.<BR> E. प्रचुर, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरीकरण|प्रचुरीकरणं
प्रचुरीकरण n. (-णं) Adding to, augmenting, increasing.<BR> E. प्रचुर and करण<BR>making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरीकृत
प्रचुरीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Augmented, in quantity or number.<BR> E. प्रचुर, and<BR>कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेतस्
प्रचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः) Happy, delighted.<BR>	 m. (-ताः)<BR>	 1. VARUṆA, the<BR>regent of water.<BR>	 2. The name of a saint and law-giver.<BR>	 m. plu. (-सः)<BR>The ten sons of PRACHĪNAVARHI by the daughter of VARUṆA,<BR>and the progenitors of DAKṢA.<BR> E. प्र best, first, चेतस् the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेतृ
प्रचेतृ m. (-ता) A charioteer.<BR> E. प्र before, चि to collect, (the reins,)<BR>aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेल|प्रचेलं
प्रचेल m. (लः) A yellow fragrant wood.<BR> E. प्र before, चेल् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पचेलक
पचेलक m. (-कः) A horse.<BR> E. प्र well, fast, चेल् to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोद|प्रचोदः
प्रचोद m. (-दः) Inciting, instigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोदन|प्रचोदनं
प्रचोदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Saying, enjoining, prescribing.<BR>	 2. Sending, directing.<BR>3. A rule or law.<BR> E. प्र before, चुद् to direct, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोदित|प्रचोदितः
प्रचोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Prescribed, directed.<BR>	 2. Sent.<BR>	 3. Determined.<BR>4. Instigated, incited.<BR> E. प्र thoroughly, चुद् to direct, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोदिनी
प्रचोदिनी f. (-नी) A prickly nightshade, (Solanum jacquini)<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>चुद् to send, affs. ल्यु and ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्युत
प्रच्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fallen from, deviated from.<BR> E. प्र before, च्यु to fall, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छ
प्रच्छ(औ)प्रच्छौ r. 6th cl. (पृच्छति)<BR>	 1. To ask or inquire.<BR>	 2. To desire, to<BR>know. With अनु to question about; with आ 1. To ask.<BR>	 2. To take<BR>leave of. With परि to ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छद|प्रच्छदः|प्रछद
प्रच्छद m. (-दः) A cover, a wrapper.<BR> E. प्र completely, छद् to cover, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छदपट|प्रच्छदपटः
प्रच्छदपट m. (-टः) A cover, a wrapper, either of a person or thing, as<BR>a cloak, a veil, a sheet, a curtain, &c.<BR> E. प्रच्छद a cover, and पट<BR>cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छना
प्रच्छना f. (-ना) Asking, addressing, inviting.<BR> E. प्रच्छ् to ask, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छन्न|प्रच्छन्नं
प्रच्छन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Covered, clothed.<BR>	 2. Unavowed, disguised.<BR>3. Private, concealed, secret.<BR>	 n. (न्नं)<BR>	 1. A private door within a<BR>house.<BR>	 2. A lattice, a loop hole.<BR>	 3. Any private door.<BR> E. प्र before, छद्<BR>to hide, aff. क्त, what is concealed or secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छन्नम्
प्रच्छन्नम् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of “Secretly,” “covertly.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छर्द्दन|प्रच्छर्दन|प्रच्छर्दनं
प्रच्छर्द्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Vomiting.<BR>	 2. An emetic.<BR> E. प्र, छर्द-ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छर्दिका|प्रच्छर्द्दिका
प्रच्छर्दिका f. (-का) Vomiting, sickness.<BR> E. प्र violently, छर्द to vomit,<BR>aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादन|प्रच्छादनं
प्रच्छादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. An upper or outer garment.<BR>	 2. Covering, concealing.<BR>E. प्र completely, छद् to cover, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादित|प्रच्छादितं
प्रच्छादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Covered, clothed, hidden, concealed.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, छद् to cover, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छाय|प्रच्छायं
प्रच्छाय n. (-यं) Thick shade, a shadowy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छिल
प्रच्छिल f. (-ला) Dry.<BR> E. प्रच्छ्-वा० इलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यव|प्रच्यवः
प्रच्यव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Fall, ruin.<BR>	 2. Improvement, growth.<BR> E. प्र-च्यु-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यवन|प्रच्यवनं
प्रच्यवन n. (-नं) Dropping, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्युत
प्रच्युत f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Fallen from.<BR>	 2. Displaced, degraded.<BR>	 3. Put to flight, routed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्युति|प्रच्युतिः
प्रच्युति f. (-ति)<BR>	 1. Fall, ruin.<BR>	 2. Loss, deprivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज|प्रजः
प्रज m. (-जः) A husband.<BR> E. प्र before, जन् to be born, ड aff. who is<BR>re-born in his children: see प्रजा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजन|प्रजनः
प्रजन mn. (नः-नं)<BR>	 1. Impregnating, begetting.<BR>	 2. Impregnation or<BR>pregnancy of cattle in general.<BR>	 3. The season for a cow's taking<BR>the bull, &c.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A progenitor, an impregnator.<BR>	 2. Bringing<BR>forth, bearing.<BR> E. प्र before, जन् to be born, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनन|प्रजननं
प्रजनन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The vulva.<BR>	 2. Birth, production.<BR>	 3. Going well or<BR>quickly.<BR>	 4. Procreation.<BR>	 5. Semen.<BR> E. प्र before, जन् to be<BR>born, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनार्थम्
प्रजनार्थम् Adv. Ind. For the sake of procreation.<BR> E. प्रजन, and अर्थ on account of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनिका
प्रजनिका f. (-का) A mother.<BR> E. प्र before, जन् to be born, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनिष्णु
प्रजनिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Being born or produced.<BR>	 2. Producing,<BR>generating.<BR>	 3. Growing or standing, (as corn.)<BR> E. प्र before, to जन्<BR>be born, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनुक|प्रजनुकः
प्रजनुक m. (-कः) The body.<BR> E. प्र-जन्-वा० उक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्प|प्रजल्पः
प्रजल्प m. (-ल्पः)<BR>	 1. Prattle, gossip.<BR>	 2. Talking heedlessly to a lover. E.<BR>प्र and जल्प talking. It is thus described in Vāchaspatya. “असूयेर्ष्या-<BR>मदयुता योऽवधीरणमुद्रया । प्रियस्य कौशलोद्गारः प्रजल्पः स तु कथ्यते ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्पन|प्रजल्पनं
प्रजल्पन n. (-नं) Talking, speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजव|प्रजवः
प्रजव m. (-वः) Great speed.<BR> E. प्र before, जव quickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजविन्
प्रजविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Swift, speedy.<BR>	 m. (-वी) A runner, a courier,<BR>an express.<BR> E. प्र before, जव speed, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजा
प्रजा f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. Progeny, offspring.<BR>	 2. People, subjects.<BR>	 3. Propagation,<BR>generation.<BR>	 4. Semen.<BR>	 5. Mankind.<BR> E. प्र before, जन् to be born, affs.<BR>ड and टाप्. This word changed with प्रजस् when used as the<BR>last member of a Bahubrihi compound with अ, दुस् or सु as the<BR>first member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाकाम
प्रजाकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Desirous of offspring.<BR> E. प्रजा, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजागर|प्रजागरः
प्रजागर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Waking, watching.<BR>	 2. A guardian.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>Krishṇa.<BR> E. प्र before, जागर wakefulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजातन्तु|प्रजातंतु|प्रजातन्तुः
प्रजातन्तु m. (-न्तुः) A race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाता
प्रजाता f. (-ता) A woman who has born a child.<BR> E. प्र before, जात born,<BR>(from whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाति|प्रजातिः
प्रजाति f. (-ति)<BR>	 1. Procreation, propagation.<BR>	 2. Delivery.<BR>	 3. Procreative power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाद
प्रजाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Who or what gives offspring.<BR>	 2. What removes<BR>barrenness, (as a medicine, &c.)<BR> E. प्रजा, and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजादान|प्रजादानं
प्रजादान n. (-नं) Silver.<BR> E. प्रजा people, and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाधर्म्म|प्रजाधर्म
प्रजाधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) The duty of children or of subjects.<BR> E. प्रजा and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजानत्|प्रजानन्त्
प्रजानत् mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्)<BR>	 1. Sensible, intelligent.<BR>	 2. Knowing, under-<BR>standing.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती) A sensible woman.<BR> E. प्र before, ज्ञा to know,<BR>aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजानिषेक|प्रजानिषेकः
प्रजानिषेक m. (-कः) Impregnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाप|प्रजापः
प्रजाप m. (-पः) A king.<BR> E. प्रजा people, subjects, and प who protects, from पा with क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजापति|प्रजापतिः
प्रजापति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. The epithet common to<BR>the ten divine personages, who were first created by BRAHMĀ;<BR>they are also termed Brahmādikas, and their names are MARICHI,<BR>ATRI, ANGIRAS, PULASTYA, PULAHA, KRATU, PRACHETAS,<BR>VASIṢṬHA, BHRIGU, and NĀRADA: some authorities make the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">Page476-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Prajāpatis only seven in number, others reduce them to three,<BR>such as DAKṢA, NĀRADA, and BHRIGU, and others make them<BR>twenty-one.<BR>	 3. A king, a sovereign.<BR>	 4. A father.<BR>	 5. A son-in-law, a<BR>daughter's husband.<BR>	 6. The sun.<BR>	 7. Fire.<BR>	 8. A name of VISWA-<BR>KARMĀ, the architect of gods.<BR> E. प्रजा people or the world, and<BR>पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=475-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजायिनी
प्रजायिनी f. (-नी) A mother, or bearer of children.<BR> E. प्र before, जन् to be born, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजावत्|प्रजावन्त्
प्रजावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Having progeny.<BR>	 2. Having subjects.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ती)<BR>	 1. A brother's wife 2. The wife of an elder brother.<BR>	 3. A<BR>mother.<BR> E. प्रजा offspring, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजावृद्धि|प्रजावृद्धिः
प्रजावृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Increase of progeny.<BR> E. प्रजा and वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजाहित|प्रजाहितं
प्रजाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Favourable or good for children or subjects,<BR>&c. kind to them, useful to them, &c.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Water.<BR> E. प्रजा people<BR>and हित friendly, useful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजिन|प्रजिनः
प्रजिन m. (-नः) Air, wind.<BR> E. प्र before, जि to surpass or overcome, क्त aff. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजीवन|प्रजीवनं
प्रजीवन n. (-नं) Livelihood, subsistence.<BR> E. प्र, and जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजुष्ट
प्रजुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Strongly attached to, devoted to, intent on. E.<BR>and जुष् to serve, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजेश्वर|प्रजेश्वरः
प्रजेश्वर m. (-रः) A king.<BR> E. प्रजा subject, and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञ|प्रज्ञः
प्रज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Wise, learned; also प्राज्ञ.<BR>	 2. Bandy-legged,<BR>having the knees for apart: see प्रज्ञु.<BR>	 f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>	 1. A clever or<BR>sensible woman.<BR>	 2. Understanding, wisdom, knowledge.<BR>	 3. The<BR>goddess of arts and eloquence, SARASWATĪ.<BR>	 4. Discrimination,<BR>judgment.<BR>	 5. Power of device or design.<BR> E. प्र before, ज्ञा to know,<BR>aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञप्ति|प्रज्ञप्तिः
प्रज्ञप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. An appointment, an agreement, an engagement.<BR>	 2.<BR>Teaching doctrine. (-प्ती) One of the Vidyā Devīs of the Jainas.<BR>E. प्र before, ज्ञा to know, causal v., aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाकाय|प्रज्ञाकायः
प्रज्ञाकाय m. (-यः) A Bauddha saint; also MANJUGHOSHA.<BR> E. प्रज्ञा<BR>knowledge, कै to sound, अङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाचक्षुस्
प्रज्ञाचक्षुस् m. (-क्षुः) A name of DHRITARĀSTRA. Adj. Blind, having<BR>the understanding as the only eyes.<BR> E. प्रज्ञा and चक्षुस् the eye:<BR>being physically blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञात
प्रज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, understood.<BR>	 2. Famous, notorious.<BR>3. Distinct, clear.<BR> E. प्र, and ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञान|प्रज्ञानं
प्रज्ञान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wise, learned.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>	 2.<BR>A mark, a sign, a token.<BR> E. प्र exceeding, ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाल
प्रज्ञाल f. (-ला) Wise, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञावत्|प्रज्ञावन्त्
प्रज्ञावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Wise, intelligent.<BR> E. प्रज्ञा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञावृद्ध
प्रज्ञावृद्ध Adj. Old in wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाहीन
प्रज्ञाहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Silly, unwise, ignorant.<BR> E. प्रज्ञा, and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञिन्
प्रज्ञिन् m. (-ज्ञी) A sage, a scholar, a wise or learned man.<BR> E. प्रज्ञा<BR>wisdom, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञिल
प्रज्ञिल f. (-ला) Prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञु|प्रज्ञुः
प्रज्ञु mfn. (-ज्ञुः-ज्ञुः-ज्ञु) Bandy-legged, having the knees far apart.<BR> E. प्र<BR>separate, जानु the knee, and ज्ञु substitude also प्रज्ञ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वलन|प्रज्वलनं
प्रज्वलन n. (-नं) Blazing up, flaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वलित|प्रज्वलितः
प्रज्वलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Blazing, radiant.<BR>	 2. Burnt.<BR> E. प्र implying<BR>excess, ज्वलित burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वालित
प्रज्वालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Lighted, kindled.<BR> E. प्र before, ज्वल् to blaze, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रडीन|प्रडीनं
प्रडीन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Flying, rapidly, or flying in every direction.<BR>	 2. Taking<BR>flight, beginning to fly.<BR> E. प्र intensitive, डीन flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रण|प्रणः
प्रण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Old, ancient.<BR> E. प्र substituted for पुराण, and न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणख|प्रणखः
प्रणख m. (-खः) The point of a nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणत|प्रणतः
प्रणत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bending, bowed, humble, stooping, inclined.<BR>2. Skilful, clever.<BR> E. प्र before, नम् to bow, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणतवत्
प्रणतवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Bowing, bent, bowed.<BR> E. प्र before, णम् to bow<BR>down, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणताशिरस्
प्रणताशिरस् mfn. (-राः-राः-रः) Inclined, stooping, having the head or top<BR>bowed.<BR> E. प्रणत, and शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणति|प्रणतिः
प्रणति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Salutation, reverence, obeisance.<BR>	 2. Courtesy.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, नम् to bow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणदन|प्रणदनं
प्रणदन n. (-नं) Sounding, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणदित
प्रणदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounded, sounding.<BR> E. प्र before, णद् to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणमत्
प्रणमत् mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्) Bowing to, saluting with reverence or res-<BR>pect.<BR> E. प्र before, णम् to bow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणमित
प्रणमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bending.<BR> E. प्र before, णम् to bow, क्त aff. with इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणय|प्रणयः
प्रणय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Affection, friendly or fond regard.<BR>	 2. Acquaintance.<BR>3. Asking, begging.<BR>	 4. Affectionate solicitation.<BR>	 5. Final eman-<BR>cipation or beatitude.<BR>	 6. Trust, confidence.<BR>	 7. Reverence, obeisance,<BR>8. Favour, kindness.<BR> E. प्र before, नी to get, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयत्
प्रणयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Leading, conducting.<BR>	 2. Dispensing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Decreeing, awarded.<BR> E. प्र and णी to lead, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयन्
प्रणयन् n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Leading, conducting.<BR>	 2. Dispensing, distributing.<BR>3. Sentencing, awarding.<BR>	 4. Bringing.<BR>	 5. Executing.<BR>	 6. Writing,<BR>composing.<BR> E. प्र before, णी to guide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयमान|प्रणयमानः
प्रणयमान m. (नः) Lover's quarrels.<BR> E. प्रणय and मान indignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयवत्|प्रणयवन्त्
प्रणयवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Attached to, loving.<BR> E. प्रणय, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयविमुख
प्रणयविमुख Adj. Declined to friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयविहति|प्रणयविहतिः
प्रणयविहति f. (-तिः) Denial, refusal, non-compliance.<BR> E. प्रणय requiring, विहति rejecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयापराध|प्रणयापराधः
प्रणयापराध m. (-धः) An offence against love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयिन्
प्रणयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिणी-यि)<BR>	 1. Affectionate, kind.<BR>	 2. Intimate, familiar.<BR>3. Beloved, dear.<BR>	 4. Desirous of.<BR>	 m. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A husband or lover.<BR>2. A favourite 3. A suitor.<BR>	 f. (-यिणी) A wife or mistress.<BR> E. प्रणय<BR>affection, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयोन्मुख
प्रणयोन्मुख Adj. Impatient through love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणर्त्तन
प्रणर्त्तन n. (-नं) Dancing.<BR> E. प्र before, नृत् to dance, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणव|प्रणवः
प्रणव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The mystical name of the Deity, or syllable “Om.”<BR>2. A small kind of drum or tabor.<BR>	 3. A name of Viṣṇu.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, नु to praise, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणवक|प्रणवकः
प्रणवक m. (-कः) The mystical name of the Deity.<BR> E. प्रणव, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणश्यत्
प्रणश्यत् mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्)<BR>	 1. Perishing, falling away.<BR>	 2. Endeavour-<BR>ing to escape.<BR> E. प्र before, नश् to destroy, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणस
प्रणस f. (-सा) Adj. Having a prominent nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाडी
प्रणाडी f. (-डी) Intervention, interposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाद|प्रणादः
प्रणाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A loud noise, especially expressing approbation<BR>or delight, a huzza, a shout.<BR>	 2. A low sound expressive of great<BR>pleasure, a murmur or sigh of rapture.<BR>	 3. A cry for help.<BR>	 4.<BR>Neighing, bringing.<BR>	 5. A disease of the ear, a noise or buzzing in<BR>the ear from thickening of the membranes, &c.<BR> E. प्र much, and<BR>नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाम|प्रणामः
प्रणाम m. (-मः) Respectful or reverential salutation, addressed especial-<BR>ly to a Brahman or deity.<BR> E. प्र before, णम् to bow, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणायक|प्रणायकः
प्रणायक m. (-कः) A leader, a chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाय्य|प्रणाय्यः
प्रणाय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं)<BR>	 1. Devoid of passion or desire.<BR>	 2. Disobedient,<BR>disagreeing.<BR>	 3. Upright, straight, in rectitude.<BR>	 4. Beloved.<BR> E. प्र<BR>away, णी to go, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाल|प्रणालः
प्रणाल mf. (-लः-ली)<BR>	 1. An issue from a pond, drain, a watercourse.<BR>	 2.<BR>An uninterrupted series.<BR> E. प्र before, नल् to bind, aff. घञ्; also<BR>with कन् added in the fem. form प्रणालिका f. (-का)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाश|प्रणाशः
प्रणाश m. (-शः) Loss, destruction.<BR> E. प्र before, णश् to be destroyed, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशन|प्रणाशनं
प्रणाशन n. (नं) Destruction, annihilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशिन्
प्रणाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Destroying.<BR> E. प्र before, णश् to be destroyed,<BR>causal v., घिणुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिघ्नत्
प्रणिघ्नत् mfn. (-घ्नत्-घ्नती-घ्नत्) Preparing or threatening to strike.<BR> E. प्र and<BR>नि before, हन् to strike, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिंसित
प्रणिंसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Kissed.<BR> E. प्र, णिसि to kiss, क्त aff.; also read<BR>प्रनिंसित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिंसितव्य
प्रणिंसितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be kissed, what may or ought to be<BR>kissed.<BR> E. प्र before, णिसि to kiss, तव्य aff.; also read प्रनिंसितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=476-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधान|प्रणिधानं
प्रणिधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Great effort, stress, energy.<BR>	 2. Profound religious<BR>meditation.<BR>	 3. Access, entrance.<BR>	 4. Respectful behaviour.<BR>	 5.<BR>Application, use.<BR>	 6. Renunciation of the fruits of actions.<BR> E. प्र and<BR>नि and prefixed to धा to have, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधि|प्रणिधिः
प्रणिधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. A spy, a secret agent or emissary.<BR>	 2. Asking, solici-<BR>tation or request.<BR>	 3. Care, attention.<BR>	 4. A follower.<BR> E. प्र and नि<BR>before, धा to have, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिनदत्
प्रणिनदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्) Sounding deep or like thunder.<BR> E. प्र and<BR>नि before, नद् to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिनाद|प्रणिनादः
प्रणिनाद m. (-दः) A deep sound, that of thunder or its like.<BR> E. प्र and नि<BR>before, नद to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतन|प्रणिपतनं
प्रणिपतन n. (-नं) Saluting, bowing or doing homage to.<BR> E. प्र and नि<BR>before, पत् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतित
प्रणिपतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bowed down in reverence, saluting.<BR> E. प्र and नि before, पत् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपत्य
प्रणिपत्य Ind. Having bowed down or in reverence, having saluted<BR>respectfully.<BR> E. प्र and नि before, पत् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनिपात
प्रनिपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Salutation, reverence, obeisance.<BR>	 2. Falling at one's<BR>feet, prostration.<BR> E. प्र and नि before, पत् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपातरस
प्रणिपातरस m. (-सः) A magical formulæ pronounced over weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिहित|प्रणिहितं
प्रणिहित mfn. (-तः-ता-त)<BR>	 1. Delivered, entrusted, consigned.<BR>	 2. Obtained,<BR>received, acquired.<BR>	 3. Acknowledged, admitted.<BR>	 4. Placed, fixed,<BR>deposited.<BR>	 5. Prudent, advised, careful, wary.<BR>	 6. Determined, deci-<BR>ded.<BR>	 7. Having the mind concentrated.<BR>	 8. Spied out.<BR>	 9. Stretched<BR>forth.<BR> E. प्र and नि before, धा to have, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीत|प्रणीतं|प्रणीतः
प्रणीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dressed, (as food.) cooked, &c.<BR>	 2. Made, done.<BR>constructed.<BR>	 3. Thrown, cast. sent.<BR>	 4. Entered, approached.<BR>	 5.<BR>Proper, fit.<BR>	 6. Said, declared.<BR>	 7. Delivered, given, presented.<BR>	 8.<BR>Decreed, sentenced, awarded.<BR>	 9. Advanced, promoted.<BR>	 10. Execu-<BR>ted, accomplished.<BR>	 11. Taught.<BR>	 12. Composed, written.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>Fire consecrated by prayers or mystical formulæ.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A vessel<BR>used at sacrifices, a sort of cup.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Condiment.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>नी to get, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणु
प्रणु(णू)त mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Praised, celebrated.<BR> E. प्र before, णु to praise, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुत्त
प्रणुत्त f. (-ता) Adj. Driven away, repelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुद्
प्रणुद् mfn. (-णुत् or -णुद्) Enjoining, directing, who or what commands or<BR>enjoins.<BR> E. प्र before, णुद् to command, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुन्न
प्रणुन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Shaking, trembling.<BR>	 2. Sent, despatched.<BR>	 3.<BR>Driven away.<BR>	 4. Set in motion.<BR> E. प्र before, णुद् to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणेतृ
प्रणेतृ m. (-तृः)<BR>	 1. A leader.<BR>	 2. The promulgator of a doctrine.<BR>	 3. An<BR>author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणेय|प्रणेयः
प्रणेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Docile, submissive, agreeable.<BR>	 2. To be accomplished.<BR>3. To be settled.<BR> E. प्र before, नी to lead, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणोद|प्रणोदः
प्रणोद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Directing, ordering.<BR>	 2. Guilding, driving, (as horses.)<BR>E. प्र before, णुद् to send, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणोदित
प्रणोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ordered, directed.<BR>	 2. Driven, guided.<BR> E. प्र before, णुद् to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतत
प्रतत f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Spread over, covered.<BR>	 2. Stretched out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतति|प्रततिः
प्रतति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Spreading, expansion.<BR>	 2. A creeping plant.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>तन् to spread, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतती
प्रतती f. (-ती) A creeping plant.<BR> E. ङीप् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतन|प्रतनः
प्रतन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Old, ancient.<BR> E. प्र prior, with द्युल् aff. and तन्<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतनु
प्रतनु mfn. (-नुः-न्वी-नु)<BR>	 1. Thin, delicate, minute.<BR>	 2. Small, puny.<BR>	 3.<BR>Slender, emaciated.<BR>	 4. Insignificant.<BR> E. प्र, and तनु thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतपन|प्रतपनं
प्रतपन n. (-नं) Making warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतप्त
प्रतप्त f. (-प्ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Heated.<BR>	 2. Tortured, tormented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर|प्रतरः
प्रतर m. (-रः) Crossing, crossing over.<BR> E. प्र + तॄ-अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्क|प्रतर्कः
प्रतर्क m. (-र्कः) Congecture, supposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्कण|प्रतर्कणं
प्रतर्कण n. (-णं) Reasoning, discussion, doubt, logic.<BR> E. प्र before, तर्क् to reason, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्द्दन|प्रतर्दन|प्रतर्दनः
प्रतर्द्दन n. (-नं) Repelling.<BR> E. प्र + तृद्-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतल|प्रतलं|प्रतलः
प्रतल m. (-लः) The open hand with the fingers extended.<BR>	 n. (-लं) One<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">Page477-b+ 60</a>]<BR>of the seven principal divisions of the lower regions.<BR> E. प्र excee-<BR>ding, तल lowness, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतान|प्रतानः
प्रतान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Spreading, expansion.<BR>	 2. A shoot, a tendril.<BR>	 3. A low<BR>spreading creeper.<BR>	 4. A disease, fainting, epilepsy.<BR>	 5. Ramifi-<BR>cation.<BR> E. प्र before, तन् to spread, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतानिन्
प्रतानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Spreading, extending.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A spreading<BR>creeper.<BR> E. प्र before, तन् to spread, aff. ल्युट्, and इनि and ङीप्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रताप|प्रतापः
प्रताप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Majesty, dignity, glory, possession of rank and power.<BR>2. Spirit, valour, energy.<BR>	 3. Splendour, brilliancy.<BR>	 4. Warmth,<BR>glowing, Heat.<BR> E. प्र before, तप् to shine, aff. घञ् । “अर्क वृक्षे च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापन|प्रतापनं|प्रतापनः
प्रतापन m. (-नः) Name of a hell.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Inflicting pain or punish-<BR>ment, burning, consuming.<BR>	 2. Paining, distressing.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>तप् to heat, aff. णिच्-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापवत्|प्रतापवन्त्
प्रतापवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Majestic, glorious.<BR>	 2. An epithet of Sīva.<BR> E. प्रताप and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापस|प्रतापसः
प्रतापस m. (-सः) A species of gigantic Asclepias, with white flowers.<BR>E. प्रताप heat, षो to destroy, aff. क । “शुक्लार्क वृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापिन्
प्रतापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>	 1. Shining, splendid.<BR>	 2. Dignified, powerful.<BR>3. Burning.<BR>	 4. Distressing.<BR> E. प्रताप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रताम्
प्रताम् mfn. (-तान्)<BR>	 1. Desiring.<BR>	 2. Being afficted.<BR> E. प्र before, तम् to desire, ण्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतार|प्रतारः
प्रतार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Crossing over.<BR>	 2. Carrying over, bearing over.<BR>	 3.<BR>Deceit, fraud.<BR> E. प्र before, तृ to cross, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारक|प्रतारकः
प्रतारक m. (-कः) A cheat.<BR> E. प्र before, तृ to cross, aff. णिच्-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारण|प्रतारणं
प्रतारण nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>	 1. Fraud, cheating, deceit, over-reaching, trick.<BR>	 2.<BR>Carrying over.<BR> E. प्र before, तॄ to cross, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारित|प्रतारितः
प्रतारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cheated, deceived, tricked.<BR> E. प्र before, तॄ to<BR>pass over, (to overreach,) aff. णिच्-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रति
प्रति Ind. As a prefix to verbal themes it means,--1. In the<BR>direction of, towards.<BR>	 2. In opposition to.<BR>	 3. Back, in return.<BR>4. Down upon. As a prefix to nouns not immediately derived<BR>from verbs it means,--1. Likeness, resemblance.<BR>	 2. Rivalry.<BR>As a particle and prefix it means. --I. Substitution,<BR>(instead, in lieu;) as प्रद्युम्नः केशवात् प्रति.<BR>	 2. Several order,<BR>(severally, each by each;) as वृक्षं प्रति सिञ्चति; प्रतिवेद each<BR>Veda; प्रतिदिनं every day; प्रतिछिद्रं each opening; प्रतिगर्भ<BR>every birth; प्रत्येक one by one.<BR>	 3. Direction, (to, towards,<BR>upon;) as वृक्षं प्रति विद्योतते विद्युत्.<BR>	 4. Beloning to, (as a part or<BR>portion.)<BR>	 3. Exchange, return, (again, back again,) as तिलेभ्यः प्रति<BR>माषान् यच्छति.<BR>	 6. A little, &c. as शाकप्रति, सूपप्रति.<BR>	 7. Opposition, in<BR>place, as प्रतिसूर्य्यं against the sun, प्रतिवात against the wind.<BR>	 8. With<BR>respect to, अनेकभार्य्यं, प्रत्याह.<BR>	 9. In proportion to, as त्वं सहस्राणि प्रति<BR>10. In the vicinity of, by the side of, as गङ्गां प्रति.<BR>	 11. At the time<BR>of, as फाल्गुनं प्रति.<BR>	 12. Concerning, as वह्निर्विवाहं प्रति कर्म्मसाक्षी.<BR> E. प्रथ् to<BR>be famous, डति aff.; in the following compounds the final इ of<BR>प्रति is optionally long, before derivatives formed with घञ्, as<BR>प्रतिहार or प्रतीहार &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक|प्रतिकः
प्रतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Worth sixteen Pans of Cowries.<BR> E. प्रति substituted for कार्षापण, and यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकञ्चुक|प्रतिकंचुक|प्रतिकञ्चुकः
प्रतिकञ्चुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकण्ठम्|प्रतिकंठम्
प्रतिकण्ठम् Ind.<BR>	 1. Severally, one by one.<BR>	 2. Near the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकर|प्रतिकरः
प्रतिकर m. (-रः) Requital, compensation.<BR> E. प्र + कृ-अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकर्तृ
प्रतिकर्तृ f. (-र्त्री) Requiting, compensating.<BR>	 m. (-र्ता) An opponent, an<BR>adversary.<BR> E. प्र + कृ-तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकर्म्मन्|प्रतिकर्मन्
प्रतिकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Dress, decoration, personal embellishment.<BR>	 2.<BR>Retaliation, requital.<BR>	 3. Remedy, redress.<BR>	 4. Opposition.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>belonging to, (the body.) and कर्म्मन् business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकर्ष|प्रतिकर्षः
प्रतिकर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Aggregation.<BR>	 2. Anticipation, (of a word,) occurring<BR>later.<BR> E. प्रति + कृष्-भावे-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक|प्रतिकः
प्रतिक(ष्क)श m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A leader.<BR>	 2. An assistant.<BR>	 3. A messenger. E.<BR>प्रति + कश्-अच्-मुट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकष|प्रतिकषः
प्रतिकष Adj. Not obeying the whip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=477-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकाय|प्रतिकायः
प्रतिकाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A butt, a mark; the effigy of a man, for archers<BR>to practise at.<BR>	 2. An effigy, an image, a picture.<BR> E. प्रति again, and<BR>काय the body; a repetition or reflection of the form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकार|प्रतिकारः
प्रतिकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Revenge, requital, retribution, retaliation.<BR>	 2. Reme-<BR>dying, counteracting.<BR>	 3. Remedy, prevention.<BR>	 4. Opposition.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>again, against, and कार making; also प्रतीकार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकाश|प्रतिकाशः
प्रतिकाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Like, resembling, (used in composition.)<BR>	 m.<BR>(-शः)<BR>	 1. Look, appearance.<BR>	 2. Reflection.<BR> E. प्रति to or again, and<BR>काश or कास what shines: also प्रतीकाश, प्रतिकास, and प्रतीकास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकास|प्रतिकासः
प्रतिकास mfn. (-सः-सा-स) Like, (in composition:) see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकितव|प्रतिकितवः
प्रतिकितव m. (-वः) An opponent in a game.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकुञ्चित|प्रतिकुंचित
प्रतिकुञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bent, curved.<BR> E. प्रति, and कुचि to be curved, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकुञ्जर|प्रतिकुंजर|प्रतिकुञ्जरः
प्रतिकुञ्जर m. (-रः) A hostile elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूप|प्रतिकूपः
प्रतिकूप m. (-पः) A moat, a ditch.<BR> E. प्रति implying little, and कूप a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूल|प्रतिकूलं
प्रतिकूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Contrary, adverse, cross-grained, reverse,<BR>inverted.<BR>	 2. Contradictory, cross, perverse.<BR>	 3. Inauspicious.<BR>	 4.<BR>Unpleasant, disagreeable.<BR> E. प्रति for प्रतीप averted, and कूल a<BR>bank or shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूलम्
प्रतिकूलम् Ind.<BR>	 1. Contrarily.<BR>	 2. Inversely, in an inverted order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकूलता
प्रतिकूलता f. (-ता) Opposition, hostility.<BR> E. प्रतिकूल, and तल् aff.; also<BR>with त्व, प्रतिकूलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकृत
प्रतिकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Requited, returned.<BR>	 2. Counteracted.<BR>	 3. Re-<BR>medied.<BR> E. प्रति, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकृति|प्रतिकृतिः
प्रतिकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. An effigy, a figure, an image, a picture, a<BR>reflection, a shadow, a reflected image.<BR>	 2. Retaliation, return,<BR>revenge.<BR>	 3. A substitute.<BR> E. प्रति again, &c. and कृति making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकृष्ट|प्रतिकृष्टं
प्रतिकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Inferior, low, vile.<BR>	 2. Twice ploughed, or<BR>ploughed back again.<BR>	 3. Repulsed, rejected.<BR>	 4. Hidden, con-<BR>cealed.<BR> E. प्रति against, and कृष्ट drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्रम|प्रतिक्रमः
प्रतिक्रम m. (-मः) Inverted order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्रिया
प्रतिक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Return, requital.<BR>	 2. Retaliation.<BR>	 3. Remedying,<BR>counteracting.<BR>	 4. Embellishment, decoration.<BR>	 5. Protection.<BR>	 6.<BR>Help, succour.<BR> E. प्रति, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्रष्ट
प्रतिक्रष्ट f. (-ष्टा) Adj. Miserable, poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्रीध
प्रतिक्रीध m. (-धः) Anger in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षण|प्रतिक्षणं
प्रतिक्षण Adv.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Momentarily, every moment.<BR> E. प्रति, several order, and क्षण an instant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षय|प्रतिक्षयः
प्रतिक्षय m. (-यः) A guard, an attendant.<BR> E. प्रति against, क्षय injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षिप्त|प्रतिक्षिप्तः
प्रतिक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Dismissed, rejected, turned away.<BR>	 2. Sent,<BR>despatched.<BR>	 3. Opposed, repelled, resisted.<BR>	 4. Abused, reviled.<BR>5. Calumniated, falsely accused.<BR> E. प्रति again, against, and क्षिप्त<BR>thrown, sent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षुत|प्रतिक्षुतं
प्रतिक्षुत n. (-तं) Sneezing, wheezing.<BR> E. प्रति repeatedly, क्षुत sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षेप|प्रतिक्षेपः
प्रतिक्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Rejection.<BR>	 2. Contradiction.<BR>	 3. Contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगत|प्रतिगतं
प्रतिगत fn. (-ता-तं) Flying backwards and forwards, wheeling in flight.<BR>E. प्रति repetition, and गत gone; going and coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगमन|प्रतिगमनं
प्रतिगमन n. (-नं) Returning, going back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगर्ज्जत्|प्रतिगर्जत्
प्रतिगर्ज्जत् mfn. (-र्ज्जन्-र्ज्जन्ती-र्ज्जत्)<BR>	 1. Echoing, reverberating.<BR>	 2. Murmuring,<BR>rebelling.<BR> E. प्रति before, गर्ज्ज to growl, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगर्जना
प्रतिगर्जना f. (-ना) Roaring against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगर्हित
प्रतिगर्हित f. (-ता) Adj. Blamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगात्रम्
प्रतिगात्रम् Ind. In every limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगिरि|प्रतिगिरिः
प्रतिगिरि m. (-रिः) Any inferior mountain, or any thing like a moun-<BR>tain.<BR> E. प्रति, and गिरि a hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगृहीत
प्रतिगृहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken, accepted.<BR>	 2. Admitted.<BR>	 3. Married.<BR> E. प्रति, ग्रह् to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगृहीतृ
प्रतिगृहीतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who takes or accepts, an accepter, a receiver.<BR>E. प्रति before, ग्रह् to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगृह्य
प्रतिगृह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be taken, what may be accepted, &c.<BR>Ind.<BR>	 1. Having taken.<BR>	 2. Bringing up the rear.<BR> E. प्रति, and<BR>ग्रह् to take, क्यप् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रह|प्रतिग्रहः
प्रतिग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Acceptance, assent.<BR>	 2. Proper donation to Brāh-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">Page478-b+ 60</a>]<BR>mans, whatever is a fit present to a Brāhman at suitable periods.<BR>3. The acceptance of such a gift.<BR>	 4. Friendly reception.<BR>	 5. Favor.<BR>6. Marrying.<BR>	 7. A spitting-pot.<BR>	 8. The reserve of an army, ā<BR>detachment posted with the general four hundred yards in the<BR>rear of the line.<BR>	 9. The sun near the moon's node.<BR> E. प्रति again,<BR>&c. and ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रहण|प्रतिग्रहणं
प्रतिग्रहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Receiving presents.<BR>	 2. Marrying.<BR> E. प्रति, and ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रहणीय
प्रतिग्रहणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be taken or accepted.<BR> E. प्रति, ग्रह् to<BR>take, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्राह|प्रतिग्राहः
प्रतिग्राह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A spitting-pot.<BR>	 2. Accepting gifts.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>ग्रह् to take, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्राह्य
प्रतिग्राह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be accepted or taken.<BR> E. प्रति, and ग्रह् to<BR>taken, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगेहम्
प्रतिगेहम् Ind. In every house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघ|प्रतिघः
प्रतिघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं) Adverse, inimical.<BR>	 m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. Wrath, rage.<BR>	 2.<BR>Mutual beating, combat, fighting.<BR>	 3. Fainting.<BR>	 4. An enemy.<BR>	 5.<BR>Opposition.<BR> E. प्रति again, severally, and घ striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रति
प्रति(ती)वात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A return blow, repulse, rebound.<BR>	 2. Warding<BR>off a blow.<BR>	 3. Preventing, prohibiting.<BR> E. प्रति before, हन् to kill,<BR>aff. निच्-भावे-अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघातन|प्रतिघातनं
प्रतिघातन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Repulsing.<BR>	 2. Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. प्रति mutually, हन् to kill, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघातिन्
प्रतिघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>	 1. Repelling, repulsing.<BR>	 2. Hostile,<BR>opposed to.<BR> E. प्रतिघात, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघ्न|प्रतिघ्नं
प्रतिघ्न n. (-घ्नं) The body.<BR> E. प्रति again, घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघ्नत्
प्रतिघ्नत् mfn. (-घ्नन्-घ्नती-घ्नत्)<BR>	 1. Opposing, impeding.<BR>	 2. Destructive.<BR>	 3.<BR>Hostile.<BR> E. प्रति before, हन् to kill, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिचन्द्र|प्रतिचंद्र|प्रतिचन्द्रः
प्रतिचन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A mock-moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिचरणम्
प्रतिचरणम् Ind. In every Vedic school or branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिचिकीर्षा
प्रतिचिकीर्षा f. (-र्षा) Desire of retaliation or revenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिचिन्तन|प्रतिचिंतन|प्रतिचिंतनं
प्रतिचिन्तन n. (-नं) Thinking repeatedly, considering, meditating upon.<BR>E. प्रति, and चिति to think, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिच्छन्द|प्रतिच्छंद|प्रतिच्छंदः|प्रतिच्छन्दः|प्रतिछन्द
प्रतिच्छन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. A reflected image, any image, a picture, a statue.<BR>2. A substitute.<BR> E. प्रति again, छदि to cover, aff. अच्; also with कन्<BR>added प्रतिच्छन्दक n. (-कं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिच्छन्दन|प्रतिच्छंदन
प्रतिच्छन्दन n. (-नं) A cover, a piece of cloth for a covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिच्छन्न|प्रतिछन्न
प्रतिच्छन्न f. (-न्ना) Adj.<BR>	 1. Covered, enveloped.<BR>	 2. Hidden, concealed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Furnished with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिच्छाया|प्रतिछाया
प्रतिच्छाया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. An image, a statue, a bas-relief, a picture.<BR>	 2. A<BR>reflected image, a shade or shade or shadow.<BR> E. प्रति again, छाया a shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिच्छेद|प्रतिच्छेदः|प्रतिछेद
प्रतिच्छेद m. (-दः) Opposition, resistance.<BR> E. प्रति, and छेद cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजङ्घा|प्रतिजंघा
प्रतिजङ्घा f. (-ङ्घा) The forepart of the leg, the thigh.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>and जङ्घा the thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजल्प|प्रतिजल्पः
प्रतिजल्प m. (-ल्पः) A reply, an answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजल्पक|प्रतिजल्पकः
प्रतिजल्पक m. (-कः) Reply in assent, respectful concurrence.<BR> E. प्रति, and जल्पक talking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजागर|प्रतिजागरः
प्रतिजागर m. (-रः) Attention, watchfulness.<BR> E. प्रति towards, and जागर<BR>watchful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजिह्वा
प्रतिजिह्वा f. (-ह्वा) The uvula, or soft palate.<BR> E. प्रति again, or like, जिह्वा<BR>the tongue; also with कन् added in the fem. form, प्रतिजिह्विका (-का) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजीवन|प्रतिजीवनं
प्रतिजीवन n. (-नं) Resuscitation.<BR> E. प्रति again, नीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञा
प्रतिज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>	 1. Promise, agreement, engagement, assent.<BR>	 2. Admi-<BR>ssion, acknowledgment.<BR>	 3. Declaration, affirmation.<BR>	 4. (In logic,)<BR>The proposition, the assertion to be proved.<BR>	 5. A plaint, (in law.)<BR>E. प्रति mutually, ज्ञा to know, aff. अङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञात|प्रतिज्ञातं
प्रतिज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Promised, agreed.<BR>	 2. Admitted, acknowledged.<BR>3. Propounded, asserted.<BR> E. प्रति mutually, ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञातव्य
प्रतिज्ञातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be promised.<BR>	 2. To be assented to. E.<BR>प्रति before, ज्ञा to know, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञान|प्रतिज्ञानं
प्रतिज्ञान n. (-नं) Promise, agreement, assent.<BR> E. प्रति before, ज्ञा to know, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञान्तर
प्रतिज्ञान्तर n. (-रं) A subsequent proposition on failure of the first, (in<BR>logic.)<BR> E. प्रतिज्ञा, and अन्तर difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=478-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञापत्रक
प्रतिज्ञापत्रक n. (-कं) A bond, a written contract.<BR> E. प्रतिज्ञा agreement, and<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाय
प्रतिज्ञाय Ind. Having promised.<BR> E. प्रति before, ज्ञा to know, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाविरोध|प्रतिज्ञाविरोधः
प्रतिज्ञाविरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Denial of a logical proposition.<BR>	 2. Acting<BR>contrary to promise or agreement.<BR> E. प्रतिज्ञा, and विरोध opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाविवाहित
प्रतिज्ञाविवाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Promised in marriage, betrothed. E.<BR>प्रतिज्ञा, and विवाहित married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञासन्न्यास|प्रतिज्ञासंन्यास|प्रतिज्ञासंन्यासः
प्रतिज्ञासन्न्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Abandonment of the original proposition, (in<BR>logic.)<BR>	 2. Breaking a promise.<BR> E. प्रतिज्ञा, and सन्न्यास quitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञाहानि
प्रतिज्ञाहानि f. (-निः) Giving up the argument.<BR> E. प्रतिज्ञा, and हानि<BR>abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञेय|प्रतिज्ञेयः
प्रतिज्ञेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be promised or accepted.<BR>	 m. (-यः) The reciter<BR>or pronouncer of a panegyric, the proclaimer of rank and titles,<BR>a herald, a bard, a panegyrist.<BR> E. प्रति before, ज्ञा to know, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतितत्त्वसिद्धान्त
प्रतितत्त्वसिद्धान्त m. (-न्तः) Conclusion or notion adopted by each disputant<BR>severally.<BR> E. प्रति severally, तत्त्व truth, and सिद्धान्त conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतितन्त्र
प्रतितन्त्र Adv.<BR>	 n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. According to each Tantra.<BR>	 2. According to<BR>each opinion, &c.<BR> E. प्रति and तन्त्र a doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतितर|प्रतितरः
प्रतितर m. (-रः) An oarsman, a sailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिताल|प्रतितालः
प्रतिताल m. (-लः) A kind of air or melody.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The key of a door<BR>or padlock, or an instrument to open a door.<BR> E. प्रति relating to,<BR>ताल tune, or a lock, fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदर्शन|प्रतिदर्शनं
प्रतिदर्शन n. (-नं) Seeing, perceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदान|प्रतिदानं
प्रतिदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The return or re-delivery of a deposit.<BR>	 2. Barter,<BR>exchange.<BR>	 3. Giving back or in return for.<BR> E. प्रति again, दान a<BR>giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदारण|प्रतिदारणं
प्रतिदारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Splitting.<BR> E. प्रति reciprocally,<BR>and दारण tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदिन|प्रतिदिनं
प्रतिदिन Adv.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Every day, day by day.<BR> E. प्रति severally, and दिन a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदिवन्
प्रतिदिवन् m. (-वा)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The day.<BR> E. प्रति severally, दिव् to<BR>shine, Unādi aff. कनिन्; also with the vowel lengthened, प्रतिदीवन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदिशं
प्रतिदिशं Adv.<BR>	 n. (-शं) Every where, all around.<BR> E. प्रति, and दिश् a<BR>quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदृष्ट
प्रतिदृष्ट f. (-ष्टा) Adj. Come in sight, become visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदेय|प्रतिदेयं
प्रतिदेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be returned, to be given back, or as an equi-<BR>valent.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A pledge, a pawn.<BR>	 2. An article purchased and<BR>given back.<BR> E. प्रति again, देय to be given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदैवतम्
प्रतिदैवतम् Ind. For every deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिद्वन्द्व|प्रतिद्वंद्व|प्रतिद्वन्द्वः
प्रतिद्वन्द्व n. (-न्द्वं) Opposition, hostility.<BR>	 m. (-न्द्वः)<BR>	 1. An opponent, an<BR>adversary, a rival.<BR>	 2. An enemy.<BR> E. प्रति against, द्वन्द्व a couple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिद्वन्द्विन्|प्रतिद्वंद्विन्
प्रतिद्वन्द्विन् mfn. (-न्द्वी-न्द्विनी-न्द्वि) Hostile, an enemy.<BR> E. प्रतिद्वन्द्व, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधावन|प्रतिधावनं
प्रतिधावन n. (-नं) Assailing, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधुर|प्रतिधुरः
प्रतिधुर m. (-रः) A horse harnessed by the side of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वनि|प्रतिध्वनिः
प्रतिध्वनि f. (-निः) Echo, reverberated sound.<BR> E. प्रति, and ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वस्त
प्रतिध्वस्त f. (-स्ता) Adj. Down cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वान|प्रतिध्वानं|प्रतिध्वानः
प्रतिध्वान m. (-नः) Echo, reiterated or repeated sound.<BR> E. प्रति again, ध्वान sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनन्दन|प्रतिनंदन|प्रतिनंदनं
प्रतिनन्दन n. (-नं) Greeting, congratulating.<BR> E. प्रति + नन्द्-भाव-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनप्तृ
प्रतिनप्तृ m. (-प्ता) A great grandson, a son's grandson.<BR> E. प्रति again,<BR>repeated, and नप्तृ a grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनव|प्रतिनवं
प्रतिनव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. New, young, fresh, recent.<BR>	 2. Newly blown<BR>or budded.<BR> E. प्रति intensitive prefix, and नव new.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनाडी
प्रतिनाडी f. (-डी) A branch-vein.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनाद|प्रतिनादः
प्रतिनाद m. (-दः) Echo, resonance.<BR> E. प्रति, and नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनादित
प्रतिनादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Echoing, re-sounding.<BR> E. प्रतिनाद, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनायक|प्रतिनायकः
प्रतिनायक m. (-कः) The adversary of the hero of a poetic composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रति
प्रति(ती)नाह m. (-हः) A flag, a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिधि|प्रतिनिधिः
प्रतिनिधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. A resemblance of a real form, an image, a statue,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A surety.<BR>	 3. A substitute.<BR> E. प्रति again, धा to have, with<BR>नि prefix, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिनद|प्रतिनिनदः
प्रतिनिनद m. (-दः) An echo, a reverberation.<BR> E. प्रति, and निनद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनियम|प्रतिनियमः
प्रतिनियम m. (-मः) A general rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिर्जित
प्रतिनिर्जित f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Rescinded.<BR>	 2. Vanquished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिर्देश्य
प्रतिनिर्देश्य f. (-श्या) Adj. That which, though stated before, is repeated<BR>in order to give some further information about it, viz:--(The<BR>attribute ताम्रत्व in “उदेति सविता ताम्रस्ताम्र एवास्तमेति च”)<BR> E. प्रति + निर्-<BR>दिश-कर्म्मणि-ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिर्यातन|प्रतिनिर्यातनं
प्रतिनिर्यातन n. (-नं) Retaliation, retribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिवर्त्तन|प्रतिनिवर्तन|प्रतिनिवर्तनं
प्रतिनिवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Turning back or away from 2. Returning. E.<BR>प्रति, and नि before, वृत् to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिविष्ट
प्रतिनिविष्ट f. (-ष्टा) Adj.<BR>	 1. Hardened.<BR>	 2. Obstinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिविष्टमूर्ख|प्रतिनिविष्टमूर्खः
प्रतिनिविष्टमूर्ख m. (-र्खः) A confirmed blockhead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिवृत्त
प्रतिनिवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Turned away from, desisted from,<BR>leaving, withdrawn from.<BR>	 2. Come back, returned.<BR> E. प्रति and नि<BR>before, वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिश
प्रतिनिश Adv.<BR>	 n. (-शं) By night, every night.<BR> E. प्रति, and निशा a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनोद|प्रतिनोदः
प्रतिनोद m. (-दः) Repelling, repulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रति
प्रति(ती)प m. (-पः) A king of the lunar race, father of SĀNTANU, and<BR>grandfather of BHĪṢMA &c.: See प्रतीप.<BR> E. प्रति severally, and प<BR>who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपक्ष|प्रतिपक्षः
प्रतिपक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. An enemy, (figuratively used in the sense of “equal”<BR>“similar.”)<BR>	 2. A respondent, an opponent.<BR>	 3. A defendant. E.<BR>प्रति against, and पक्ष a part, a party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपक्षित
प्रतिपक्षित Adj.<BR>	 1. Containing a contradiction.<BR>	 2. Nullified by a<BR>contradictory premiss, (as a Hetu.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपक्षिन्
प्रतिपक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) An adversary, an opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्ति|प्रतिपत्तिः
प्रतिपत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Fame, renown, reputation.<BR>	 2. Gaining, getting,<BR>obtaining, acquirement.<BR>	 3. Action, wordly practice or activity, as<BR>opposed to religious contemplation.<BR>	 4. Use, application, profit.<BR>5. Arrogance, audacity, confidence.<BR>	 6. Knowledge, perception,<BR>observation, determination, ascertainment.<BR>	 7. Elevation, exalta-<BR>tion, promotion, acquirement of rank or dignity.<BR>	 8. Acknowledg-<BR>ment, assent, admission, acceptance.<BR>	 9. Inspiring trust or confi-<BR>dence, satisfying, showing in proof.<BR>	 10. Respectful or affectionate<BR>behaviour.<BR>	 11. Purpose, design.<BR>	 12. Comprehending, includ-<BR>ing.<BR>	 13. Distribution, disposal.<BR>	 14. Giving, presentation.<BR>	 15. Inte-<BR>llect, intelligence.<BR>	 16. Inclination, tendency.<BR>	 17. Method, means.<BR>18. Promotion, preferment.<BR>	 19. Proof, conviction.<BR>	 20. Under-<BR>taking, commencement.<BR>	 21. Resolution.<BR>	 22. Procedure, act of<BR>proceeding.<BR>	 23. Knowledge of what to do.<BR>	 24. Blinding, mislead-<BR>ing, deceiving.<BR>	 25. Throwing Ghee on the fire, or images into<BR>a sacred stream, or any similar rite from which no advantage<BR>is expected.<BR> E. प्रति severally or towards, &c. पद् to go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिपटह|प्रतिपत्तिपटहः
प्रतिपत्तिपटह m. (-हः) A large drum; the state drum allowed only to<BR>chiefs of a certain rank.<BR> E. प्रतिपत्ति celebrity, and पटह a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिपराङ्मुख
प्रतिपत्तिपराङ्मुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Obstinate, unyielding.<BR> E. प्रतिपत्ति,<BR>and पराङ्मुख averse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिमत्|प्रतिपत्तिमन्त्
प्रतिपत्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Active, prompt.<BR>	 2. Celebrated.<BR>	 3.<BR>High in rank.<BR> E. प्रतिपत्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिविशारद
प्रतिपत्तिविशारद Adj. Knowing what is to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तूर्य्य|प्रतिपत्तूर्य|प्रतिपत्तूर्य्यं
प्रतिपत्तूर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) A kettle-drum.<BR> E. प्रतिपद् rank, and तूर्य्य a musical<BR>instrument. “दगड् काडा”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपथन्
प्रतिपथन् Ind. Along the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपद्
प्रतिपद् f. (-पद्-पत्)<BR>	 1. The first day of a lunar fortnight, the first of<BR>the moon's increase or wane.<BR>	 2. Beginning, commencement.<BR>	 3.<BR>Understanding, intellect.<BR>	 4. Rank, consequence.<BR>	 5. A kettle<BR>drum.<BR> E. प्रति severally, पद् to go, and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपद
प्रतिपद Ind. or n. adv. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Step by step.<BR>	 2. At every word.<BR>	 3.<BR>Continually, every moment.<BR> E. प्रति, and पद step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपदा
प्रतिपदा (-दी) f. (-दा or दी) The first day of a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपन्न|प्रतिपन्नं
प्रतिपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Known, understood, ascertained, determined.<BR>2. Promised, engaged, assented to, accepted.<BR>	 3. Overcome,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">Page480-a+ 60</a>]<BR>conquered, subdued.<BR>	 4. Obtained, gained.<BR>	 5. Done, effected,<BR>accomplished.<BR>	 6. Undertaken.<BR>	 7. Replied.<BR>	 8. Acknowledged,<BR>admitted.<BR>	 9. Proved, demonstrated.<BR> E. प्रति again, and पद् to<BR>go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=479-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपाण|प्रतिपाणः
प्रतिपाण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Stake, gage, the thing played for.<BR>	 2. A counter-<BR>pledge, the thing staked against another.<BR> E. प्रति, and पण् to have<BR>price, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपात्रम्
प्रतिपात्रम् Ind. As regards each character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादम्
प्रतिपादम् Ind. In each quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादक|प्रतिपादकः
प्रतिपादक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. What produces effects, causes, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Explanatory.<BR>	 f. (-दिका)<BR>	 1. Granting, bestowing.<BR>	 2. Establishing,<BR>demonstrating.<BR>	 3. Explaining, illustrating.<BR>	 4. Furthering, pro-<BR>moting.<BR> E. प्रति, and पद् to go, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादन|प्रतिपादनं
प्रतिपादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. Ascertaining, proving, establi-<BR>shing, determining, rendering clear or intelligible.<BR>	 3. Action,<BR>worldly conduct or interest.<BR>	 4. Accomplishing, effecting.<BR>	 5. Pro-<BR>ducing, causing.<BR>	 6. Expounding, explaining.<BR>	 7. Repeated action,<BR>practice.<BR> E. प्रति severally, and पद् to go, causal v., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादित
प्रतिपादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Delivered, given.<BR>	 2. Caused, produced.<BR>3. Proved, explained, established.<BR> E. प्रति before, पद् to go, causal<BR>form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादुक
प्रतिपादुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Determining, ascertaining.<BR>	 2. Making<BR>manifest or clear.<BR>	 3. What causes or effects.<BR> E. प्रति before, पद् to<BR>go, causal v., उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपाप
प्रतिपाप Adj. Recompensing evil for evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालक|प्रतिपालकः
प्रतिपालक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what protects or defends.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. A king.<BR>	 2. A protector.<BR> E. प्रति before, पाल् to protect, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालन|प्रतिपालनं
प्रतिपालन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Protecting, defending, guarding, cherishing.<BR>	 2.<BR>Following, practising.<BR> E. प्रति and पाल् to cherish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालनीय
प्रतिपालनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be cherished or protected.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>observed or followed.<BR> E. प्रति, and पाल् to cherish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालित
प्रतिपालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cherished, protected.<BR>	 2. Practised, follow-<BR>ed.<BR> E. प्रति before, पाल् to cherish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपाल्य|प्रतिपाल्यं
प्रतिपाल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) To be cherished or protected.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>पाल् to cherish, यत् aff.; also प्रतिपालितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपीडन|प्रतिपीडनं
प्रतिपीडन n. (-नं) Oppressing, molesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपुरुष|प्रतिपुरुषः
प्रतिपुरुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A deputy, a substitute.<BR>	 2. A companion.<BR>	 3. The<BR>effigy of a man which thieves push into a house to ascertain<BR>whether any body is awake.<BR>	 n. adv. (-षं) Every man, man by<BR>man.<BR> E. प्रति, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजक
प्रतिपूजक m. (-कः) A reverer, one who does homage.<BR> E. प्रति, and पूजक who worships.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजन|प्रतिपूजनं
प्रतिपूजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Exchange of civilities, mutual obeisance or rever-<BR>ence.<BR>	 2. Offering homage or respect.<BR> E. प्रति, and पूजन worship-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजित
प्रतिपूजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Treated with reverence or respect.<BR>	 2.<BR>Exchanged as civilities.<BR> E. प्रति, and पूजित worshiped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूज्य
प्रतिपूज्य Ind.<BR>	 1. Having offered homage to.<BR>	 2. Having exchanged<BR>respectful salutation.<BR> E. प्रति, and पूज् to worship, ल्युप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूरण|प्रतिपूरणं
प्रतिपूरण n. (-णं) Filling, filling up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूर्वाह्णम्
प्रतिपूर्वाह्णम् Ind. Every forenoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रणाम|प्रतिप्रणामः
प्रतिप्रणाम m. (-मः) A bow in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रदान|प्रतिप्रदानं
प्रतिप्रदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Returning, restoring.<BR>	 2. Giving in marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रयाण|प्रतिप्रयाणं
प्रतिप्रयाण n. (-णं) Return, retreat.<BR> E. प्रति, and प्रयाण who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रश्न|प्रतिप्रश्नः
प्रतिप्रश्न m. (-श्नः)<BR>	 1. A question in return.<BR>	 2. An answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रसव|प्रतिप्रसवः
प्रतिप्रसव m. (-वः) Precept for an act which under other circumstances<BR>is forbidden, a counter-exception or the application of the<BR>general rule to a case covered by an exception.<BR> E. प्रति, and प्रसव<BR>birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रसूत|प्रतिप्रसूतः
प्रतिप्रसूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Re-enjoined, after having been forbidden. E.<BR>प्रति, and प्रसूत born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपतन
प्रतिपतन n. (-नं) Leaping back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफल|प्रतिफलं|प्रतिफलः
प्रतिफल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. An image, a shadow, a reflection.<BR>	 2. Return<BR>requital, retaliation.<BR> E. प्रति, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफलन|प्रतिफलनं
प्रतिफलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A reflected image.<BR>	 2. Requital, return.<BR> E. प्रति,<BR>and फल to bear fruit, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफलित|प्रतिफलितं
प्रतिफलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Represented, reflected, shadowed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Requited, returned.<BR> E. प्रति, and फल् to bear fruit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफुल्लक|प्रतिफुल्लकः
प्रतिफुल्लक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Flowered, blossoming, having. flowers.<BR>	 2.<BR>Full blown flowered.<BR> E. प्रति severally, फुल्ल blown, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबद्ध|प्रतिबद्धः
प्रतिबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Disappointed, thwarted, crossed, vexed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Obstructed, opposed, kept at a distance, prevented.<BR>	 3. Set, inlaid,<BR>4. Bound, tied.<BR>	 5. Connected with, furnished with, entangled.<BR>	 6.<BR>Inseparably connected, (In phil.)<BR> E. प्रति against, and बद्ध bound,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबधक
प्रतिबधक m. (-कः) An opposer, an injurer.<BR> E. प्रति, बघ् to kill, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्ध|प्रतिबंध|प्रतिबंधः|प्रतिबन्धः
प्रतिबन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Obstacle, impediment.<BR>	 2. Disappointment.<BR>	 3.<BR>Resistance, opposition.<BR>	 4. Blockade, siege.<BR>	 5. Inseparable connec-<BR>tion.<BR> E. प्रति against, बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धक|प्रतिबंधक|प्रतिबन्धकः
प्रतिबन्धक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Impeding, obstructing, an obstructor or<BR>opposer.<BR>	 2. Binding.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A branch, a shoot.<BR>	 n. (-कं) An im-<BR>pediment.<BR> E. प्रतिबन्ध obstacle, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धकारिन्
प्रतिबन्धकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Who or what hinders, obstructs, &c.<BR>E. प्रतिबन्ध, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धन|प्रतिबंधन|प्रतिबंधनं
प्रतिबन्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Obstructing, impeding.<BR>	 2. Binding, confinement.<BR>E. प्रति, and बन्ध् to bind, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिब
प्रतिब(न्दि)न्दी f. (-न्दी) An argument equally applicable to the opposite side.<BR>E. प्रति + बन्ध-इन् or ङीप् optionally added; also प्रतिबन्धि and प्रतिबन्धी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धि|प्रतिबंधिः|प्रतिबन्धिः
प्रतिबन्धि m. (-न्धिः or -न्धीः) Contradiction.<BR> E. प्रति, and बन्ध्, to blind. इन्<BR>aff. see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबन्धु|प्रतिबंधु|प्रतिबन्धुः
प्रतिबन्धु m. (-न्धुः)<BR>	 1. The sons of a daughter.<BR>	 2. Equal in rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबल|प्रतिबलः
प्रतिबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Able, adequate, powerful.<BR>	 2. On equal stren-<BR>gth.<BR>	 n. (-नं) An hostile army.<BR> E. प्रति intensitive prefix, and बल<BR>strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबाधन|प्रतिबाधनं
प्रतिबाधन n. (-नं) Repelling, keeping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबाहु
प्रतिबाहु m. (-हुः) The forepart of the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबि
प्रतिबि(वि)म्ब(म्ब) n. (-म्बः-म्बः)<BR>	 1. A reflection.<BR>	 2. A picture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिम्बन|प्रतिबिंबन|प्रतिबिंबनं
प्रतिबिम्बन n. (-नं) Correspondence, comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिम्बित|प्रतिबिंबित
प्रतिबिम्बित f. (-ता) Reflected, mirrored.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबुद्ध
प्रतिबुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Exalted, rendered prosperous or great.<BR>	 2.<BR>Known, celebrated.<BR>	 3. Wakened, awake.<BR> E. प्रति and बुध् to know,<BR>aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोध|प्रतिबोधः
प्रतिबोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Waking, awaking.<BR>	 2. Instructing.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>बुध् to know, घञ् aff.; also with ल्युट् प्रतिबोधन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधित
प्रतिबोधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Instructed, taught.<BR>	 2. Awakened.<BR> E. प्रति,<BR>and बोधित taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभट|प्रतिभटः
प्रतिभट m. (-टः) A rival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभणित
प्रतिभणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Answered, replied.<BR> E. प्रति, and भणित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभय|प्रतिभयं
प्रतिभय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Formidable, fearful, frightful.<BR>	 n. (-य) Fear. E.<BR>प्रति completely, and भय fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभा
प्रतिभा f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. Understanding, intellect, especially as opening<BR>or expanding.<BR>	 2. Sharpness, brilliancy of conception.<BR>	 3. Genius,<BR>especially poetic genius.<BR>	 4. Light, splendour.<BR>	 5. Reflected light.<BR>6. Audacity, boldness, confidence, consequence.<BR>	 7. An image. E.<BR>प्रति before, भा to shine, affs. ड and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाग|प्रतिभागः
प्रतिभाग n. (-गं) A share of small articles, as fruit, flowers, &c. paid<BR>daily to the Rājā for household expenditure.<BR> E. प्रति, and भाग<BR>a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभात
प्रतिभात f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Known, understood.<BR>	 2. Luminous, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभान|प्रतिभानं
प्रतिभान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Boldness, audacity.<BR>	 2. Brilliancy, light.<BR>	 3. Intellect,<BR>understanding.<BR>	 3. Presence of mind.<BR> E. प्रति before, भा to shine,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=480-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभानवत्|प्रतिभानवन्त्
प्रतिभानवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Bold, prompt, audacious.<BR>	 2. Bright,<BR>brilliant.<BR> E. प्रतिभान and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभान्वित|प्रतिभान्वितः
प्रतिभान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Confident, bold, audacious.<BR>	 2. Acquir-<BR>ing knowledge or experience.<BR>	 3. Endowed with genius.<BR> E. प्रतिभा<BR>confidence, अन्वित joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभामुख|प्रतिभामुखः
प्रतिभामुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Confident, bold, arrogant.<BR> E. प्रतिभा con-<BR>fidence, मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाव|प्रतिभावः
प्रतिभाव m. (-वः) Corresponding character or disposition.<BR> E. प्रति, and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभावत्|प्रतिभावन्त्
प्रतिभावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Confident, bold.<BR>	 2. Knowing, shrewd.<BR>3. Bright, luminous.<BR>	 m. (-वान्)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR>E. प्रतिभा light, lustre, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाववत्
प्रतिभाववत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Social.<BR> E. प्रतिभाव, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाषा
प्रतिभाषा f. (-षा) An answer, a reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभासन|प्रतिभासनं
प्रतिभासन n. (-नं) Look, appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभासा
प्रतिभासा m. (-साः)<BR>	 1. Occurring to the mind at once.<BR>	 2. Illusion.<BR>	 3. Look, appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाहानि|प्रतिभाहानिः
प्रतिभाहानि f. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Loss or absence of knowledge, want of sense.<BR>2. Dulness, darkness.<BR> E. प्रतिभा knowledge, and हानि abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभिन्न
प्रतिभिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Separated, divided.<BR>	 2. Pierced through.<BR>	 3.<BR>Closely connected.<BR> E. प्रति before, भिद् to break, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभू
प्रतिभू m. (-भूः) A surety, a bail.<BR> E. प्रति implying substitution, भू to be,<BR>aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभेदन|प्रतिभेदनं
प्रतिभेदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Piercing, cutting, penetrating.<BR>	 2. Separating.<BR>dividing.<BR>	 3. Putting out, (as the eyes.)<BR> E. प्रति before, भिद् to<BR>break, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभोग|प्रतिभोगः
प्रतिभोग m. (-गः) Enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिम|प्रतिमः
प्रतिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Like, resembling, (In composition)<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1.<BR>A resemblance, a figure, an image, a picture.<BR>	 2. An idol.<BR>	 3.<BR>The part of an elephant's head between the tusks.<BR>	 4. Similarity,<BR>Similitude.<BR>	 5. Measure, extent.<BR> E. प्रति against, मा to measure, अङ्<BR>and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमण्डल|प्रतिमंडल
प्रतिमण्डल n. (-लं) An eccentric orbit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमता
प्रतिमता f. (-ता) Reflection, image, shadow.<BR> E. प्रतिम, and तल् aff.;<BR>also with त्व, प्रतिमत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमन्दिरम्|प्रतिमंदिरम्
प्रतिमन्दिरम् Ind. In every house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमल्ल|प्रतिमल्लः
प्रतिमल्ल m. (-ल्लः) An antagonist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमान|प्रतिमानं
प्रतिमान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Resemblance, an image, picture.<BR>	 2. An idol.<BR>	 3. A<BR>model.<BR>	 4. Likeness, similarity.<BR>	 5. A reflection.<BR>	 6. A weight.<BR>	 7.<BR>The part of an elephant's head between the tusks.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>मा to measure, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमानभाग
प्रतिमानभाग m. (-गः) The part of an elephant's head between the tusks.<BR>E. प्रतिमान, and भाग part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमाया
प्रतिमाया f. (-या) Counter spell, counter-charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमार्ग्गक|प्रतिमार्गक|प्रतिमार्गकः
प्रतिमार्ग्गक m. (-कः) The city of HARIŚ CHANDRA.<BR> E. प्रति contrary, मार्ग<BR>a road, and कन् aff.; having come back part of the way to earth,<BR>after being raised to heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमाला
प्रतिमाला f. (-ला) An exercise analogous to capping verses, reciting<BR>verse for verse, (as a trial of memory or skill.)<BR> E. प्रति against, माला<BR>a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमासम्
प्रतिमासम् Ind. Every month, monthly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमित्र
प्रतिमित्र n. (-त्रं) An enemy, an adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुक्त|प्रतिमुक्तः
प्रतिमुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Clothed, put upon, worn, armed, accoutred.<BR>2. Thrown mutually or at one another.<BR>	 3. Loosed or liberated re-<BR>peatedly.<BR>	 4. Released.<BR>	 5. Hurled, flung.<BR> E. प्रति against, मुच् to<BR>loosen, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुख
प्रतिमुख n. (-खं) (In dramatic composition), A secondary plot or inci-<BR>dent, calculated either to promote or obstruct the catastrophe, adv.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. In front, before, in presence.<BR>	 2. Near.<BR> E. प्रति, and मुख<BR>the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुखागत
प्रतिमुखागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Come before, or in front of.<BR>	 2. Run<BR>against.<BR> E. प्रतिमुख and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुद्रा
प्रतिमुद्रा f. (-द्रा) A counter-seal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुहूर्त्तम्|प्रतिमुहूर्तम्
प्रतिमुहूर्त्तम् Ind. Every moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमूर्त्ति|प्रतिमूर्ति|प्रतिमूर्तिः
प्रतिमूर्त्ति f. (-र्त्ति) An image, a likeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमूषिका
प्रतिमूषिका f. (-का) A kind of rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमेन्दु
प्रतिमेन्दु m. (-न्दुः) The image, reflection or resemblance of the moon. E.<BR>प्रतिमा and इन्दु the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमोक्ष|प्रतिमोक्षः
प्रतिमोक्ष m. (-क्षः) Liberation, deliverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमोचन|प्रतिमोचनं
प्रतिमोचन n. (-नं) Loosening, 2. Retaliating, retribution.<BR>	 3. Liberation, release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियत्न|प्रतियत्नः
प्रतियत्न mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं) Active, vigorous, diligent, making effort or<BR>exertion.<BR>	 m. (-त्नः)<BR>	 1. Desire, wish.<BR>	 2. Taking prisoner, making<BR>captive.<BR>	 3. Comprehension.<BR>	 4. Acting well or properly.<BR>	 5. Acquiring<BR>a new virtue or accomplishment.<BR>	 6. Making complete or perfect.<BR>7. A making or preparing.<BR>	 8. Retaliating, recrimination, revenge.<BR>9. Opposition, counteraction.<BR> E. प्रति much or against and यत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियातन|प्रतियातनं
प्रतियातन n. (-नं) Requital, retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियातना
प्रतियातना f. (-ना) A resemblance of real forms, a picture, a statue, &c. E.<BR>प्रति against, यातना an applying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियान|प्रतियानं
प्रतियान n. (-नं) Return, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियूथप|प्रतियूथपः
प्रतियूथप n. (-पः) The leader of a hostile herd of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोग|प्रतियोगः
प्रतियोग n. (-गं)<BR>	 1. Opposition, contradiction, controversy.<BR>	 2. Co-operation,<BR>association.<BR>	 3. Existing, as the counterpart of anything.<BR>	 4. A re-<BR>medy, an antidote.<BR> E. प्रति against, युज् to join, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिता
प्रतियोगिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Mutual cooperation.<BR>	 2. Opposition.<BR>	 3. Existence<BR>as a counterpart.<BR>	 4. Dependent existence.<BR> E. प्रतियोगिन्, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिन्
प्रतियोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>	 1. Who or what impedes or opposes.<BR>	 2.<BR>What cooperates with.<BR>	 m. (-गी)<BR>	 1. An opponent.<BR>	 2. A partner,<BR>an associate.<BR>	 3. A counterpart.<BR>	 4. Any thing or object dependent<BR>upon another and not existing without it.<BR> E. प्रतियोग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोध|प्रतियोधः
प्रतियोध m. (-धः) An adversary in fight, an antagonist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरक्षण|प्रतिरक्षणं
प्रतिरक्षण n. (-णं) Preserving.<BR> E. प्रति, and रक्षण keeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरथ|प्रतिरथः
प्रतिरथ m. (-थः) An opposite fighter in a war-chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरम्भ|प्रतिरंभ|प्रतिरंभः|प्रतिरम्भः
प्रतिरम्भ m. (-म्भः) Passion, rage, violent or passionate abuse.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>before, रभि to sound, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरव|प्रतिरवः
प्रतिरव m. (-वः) Quarrel.<BR> E. प्रति + रु-अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिराज|प्रतिराजः
प्रतिराज m. (-जः) A hostile king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरात्र
प्रतिरात्र n. (-त्रं) Every night.<BR> E. प्रति repeatedly, and रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरुद्ध
प्रतिरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Impeded, hindered.<BR>	 2. Obstructed, opposed.<BR>3. Surrounded, invested, blockaded.<BR>	 4. Impaired.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>रुध् to oppose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरुरूषु
प्रतिरुरूषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to speak or tell.<BR> E. प्रति, and रु to cry, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरूप|प्रतिरूपं
प्रतिरूप n. (-पं) A picture, an image, the counterpart of any real form.<BR>Adj. Corresponding, suitable, proper.<BR> E. प्रति against, रूप form;<BR>also with कन् added, प्रतिरूपक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोद्धृ
प्रतिरोद्धृ mfn. (-द्धा-द्ध्री-द्धृ) Who or what opposes, hinders, prevents, &c. E.<BR>प्रति before, रुध् to obstruct तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोध|प्रतिरोधः
प्रतिरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Opposition, impediment.<BR>	 2. An opponent.<BR>	 3. Con-<BR>cealing, hiding.<BR>	 4. Siege, blockade.<BR>	 5. Theft, robbery.<BR>	 6. Abuse,<BR>censure.<BR> E. प्रति before, रुध् to oppose, and घञ् aff.; also with ल्युट्,<BR>प्रतिरोधन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधक|प्रतिरोधकः
प्रतिरोधक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A thief, a robber.<BR>	 2. An obstacle.<BR>	 3. An opponent.<BR>E. प्रति severally, रुध् to obstruct, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधिन्
प्रतिरोधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि) Who or what obstructs, opposes, impedes,<BR>controverts, &c.<BR>	 m. (-धी)<BR>	 1. A thief, a robber, 2. An opponent.<BR>E. प्रति against, रुध् to hinder, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलक्षण
प्रतिलक्षण n. (-णं) A mark, a sign, a token.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलम्भ|प्रतिलंभः|प्रतिलम्भः
प्रतिलम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Obtaining, getting.<BR>	 2. Censure, reviling, abuse. E.<BR>प्रति before, लभि to sound, aff. घञ्; also with ल्युट् aff. प्रतिलम्भन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलाभ|प्रतिलाभः
प्रतिलाभ m. (-भः) Taking back, obtaining back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलिपि|प्रतिलिपिः
प्रतिलिपि f. (-पि) A transcript, a copy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलोम|प्रतिलोमः
प्रतिलोम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Left, not right.<BR>	 2. Reverse, inverted, contrary<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">Page482-a+ 60</a>]<BR>to the natural course or order, against the hair or grain.<BR>	 3. Hos-<BR>tile.<BR>	 4. Low, vile, base, depraved.<BR>	 5. In law, contrary to caste, (ap-<BR>plied to the issue of a woman higher in caste than her husband.) E.<BR>प्रति reverting, and लोमन् hair of the body, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=481-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलोमक
प्रतिलोमक n. (-कं) Inverted order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलोमज|प्रतिलोमजः
प्रतिलोमज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born in the inverse order of the classes, as<BR>of a Kṣatriya father and Brāhman mother, of a Vaiśya father<BR>and Kṣatriya or Brāhman mother, &c.<BR> E. प्रतिलोम, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवचन|प्रतिवचनं
प्रतिवचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A reply, an answer, a rejoinder.<BR>	 2. An echo.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>again, back again, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवचस्
प्रतिवचस् n. (-चः)<BR>	 1. An answer, a reply.<BR>	 2. An echo.<BR> E. प्रति again and<BR>वचस् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवत्सरम्
प्रतिवत्सरम् Ind. Every year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवसथ|प्रतिवसथः
प्रतिवसथ m. (-थः) A village.<BR> E. प्रति before, वस् to abide, अथच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवस्तु
प्रतिवस्तु n. (-स्तुं)<BR>	 1. An equivalent.<BR>	 2. A parallel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवस्तूपमा
प्रतिवस्तूपमा f. (-मा) A figure of Speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाक्य|प्रतिवाक्यं
प्रतिवाक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं) Answerable, admitting or requiring an an-<BR>swer.<BR>	 n. (-क्यं) A reply, an answer.<BR> E. प्रति before, वाक्य a speech, or<BR>वाक् speech, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाच्
प्रतिवाच् f. (-वाक्) An answer, a reply.<BR> E. प्रति again, वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाणि|प्रतिवाणिः
प्रतिवाणि f. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. An answer.<BR>	 2. A rejoinder.<BR> E. प्रति before, वाणि<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवात|प्रतिवातः
प्रतिवात n. adv. (-तं) To leeward, against the wind.<BR> E. प्रति, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाद|प्रतिवादः
प्रतिवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A rejoinder, a reply.<BR>	 2. Refusal.<BR> E. प्रति + वद-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवादिन्
प्रतिवादिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A defendant, a respondent, (in law.)<BR>	 2. An oppon-<BR>ent.<BR> E. प्रति again and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाप|प्रतिवापः
प्रतिवाप m. (-पः) Addition of substance to medicines, either during or<BR>after decoction.<BR> E. प्रति and वप् to sow, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवार|प्रतिवारः
प्रतिवार m. (-रः) Warding off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवारण|प्रतिवारणं|प्रतिवारणः
प्रतिवारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Keeping back, warding off.<BR> E. प्रति + वारि-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवार्त्ता|प्रतिवार्ता
प्रतिवार्त्ता f. (-र्त्ता) Account, news, information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवासर|प्रतिवासरः
प्रतिवासर n. adv. (-रं) Day by day.<BR> E. प्रति severally, and वासर a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवासिन्
प्रतिवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) A neighbour, neighbouring.<BR> E. प्रति near,<BR>about, and वासिन् who resides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविघात|प्रतिविघातः
प्रतिविघात m. (-तः) Striking back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधान|प्रतिविधानं
प्रतिविधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Arrangement, array.<BR>	 2. Counteracting, taking<BR>measures against.<BR>	 3. Subsidiary, or substituted ceremony.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>and विधान precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधि|प्रतिविधिः
प्रतिविधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Retaliation.<BR>	 2. A remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविम्ब|प्रतिविंब|प्रतिविम्बं|प्रतिविम्बः
प्रतिविम्ब n. (-म्बं) A resemblance or counterpart of real forms, as a<BR>picture, an image a shadow, &c.<BR> E. प्रति back again, and विम्ब an<BR>image; or प्रति + आचारे क्विप् नामधातुः पर० अक० सेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविम्बात
प्रतिविम्बात m. (-तः) A mirror.<BR> E. प्रतिविम्ब and अत what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविशिष्ट
प्रतिविशिष्ट f. (-ष्टा) Adj. Most excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविषा
प्रतिविषा f. (-षा) A plant, commonly Ātāich or Atis, (Betula.)<BR> E. प्रति<BR>against, and विष venom; an antidote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविष्णु
प्रतिविष्णु Ind. (-ष्णु) To or in place of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. प्रति, and विष्णु the deity so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविष्णुक|प्रतिविष्णुकः
प्रतिविष्णुक m. (-कः) The muchukunda tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविहित
प्रतिविहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Arranged, arrayed.<BR> E. प्रति and वि before, धा to have, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवीर्य
प्रतिवीर्य n. (-र्यं) Being a match for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेलम्
प्रतिवेलम् Ind. On every occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेश|प्रतिवेशः
प्रतिवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The residence of a neighbour, a neighbouring house<BR>or neighbourhood.<BR>	 2. A neighbour.<BR> E. प्रति against, विश् to enter,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेशवासिन्
प्रतिवेशवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Neighbouring, a neighbour.<BR> E. प्रतिवेश, and वासिन् who dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेशिन्
प्रतिवेशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) A neighbour, neighbouring,<BR> E. प्रतिवेश<BR>neighbourhood, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेश्य|प्रतिवेश्यः
प्रतिवेश्य m. (-श्यः) A neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेष्टित
प्रतिवेष्टित Adj.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Surrounded.<BR>	 2. Rolled back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिव्यूह|प्रतिव्यूहः
प्रतिव्यूह m. (-हः) The array of an army against an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशङ्कनीय
प्रतिशङ्कनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be ever held in fear or doubt.<BR> E. प्रति and<BR>शङ्कनीय to be apprehended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशङ्का
प्रतिशङ्का f. (-ङ्का) Constant fear or doubt.<BR> E. प्रति and शङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशब्द|प्रतिशब्दः
प्रतिशब्द m. (-ब्दः)<BR>	 1. Echo.<BR>	 2. A roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशम|प्रतिशमः
प्रतिशम m. (-मः) Cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशयन|प्रतिशयनं
प्रतिशयन n. (-नं) Laying down without food before any deity for the<BR>attainment of an object.<BR> E. प्रति + शी-भावे ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशाप|प्रतिशापः
प्रतिशाप m. (-पः) Curse for curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशासन|प्रतिशासनं
प्रतिशासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sending a servant on a message, ordering or<BR>dispatching an inferior after calling him to attend.<BR>	 2. Giving<BR>orders.<BR>	 3. Counter-authority.<BR> E. प्रति severally, शासन ruling; also<BR>प्रतिशास्ति f. (-स्तिः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशिष्ट|प्रतिशिष्टं
प्रतिशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Celebrated, famous.<BR>	 2. Sent, ordered, dis-<BR>patched.<BR>	 2. Dismissed.<BR> E. प्रति intensitive, and शिष्ट celebrated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशीन
प्रतिशीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Melted, fluid, dropping, oozing.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>श्यै to drop, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्या
प्रतिश्या f. (-श्या) Catarrh.<BR> E. प्रति before, श्यै to go, to run, affixes अङ् and टाप्; also प्रतिश्याय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्याय|प्रतिश्यायः
प्रतिश्याय m. (-यः) Catarrh.<BR> E. प्रति before, श्यै to go, to drop, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रय|प्रतिश्रयः
प्रतिश्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. An assembly.<BR>	 2. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 3. An asylum,<BR>a place of refuge.<BR>	 4. Help, assistance.<BR>	 5. Promise.<BR>	 6. A place of<BR>sacrifice, the room or building where the sacrifice is performed.<BR>7. A place where food, &c. is given away.<BR> E. प्रति completely, श्री<BR>to serve, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रव|प्रतिश्रवः
प्रतिश्रव m. (-वः) Promise, assent, agreement.<BR> E. प्रति before, श्रु to hear, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रवण|प्रतिश्रवणं
प्रतिश्रवण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Assenting to, listening to, (with attention and<BR>obedience.)<BR>	 2. Promising, agreeing.<BR> E. प्रति, श्रु to hear, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुत्
प्रतिश्रुत् f. (-श्रुत्)<BR>	 1. Repeated sound, echo.<BR>	 2. Promise.<BR> E. प्रति before, श्रु<BR>to hear, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुत|प्रतिश्रुतः
प्रतिश्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Promised, assented, agreed, accepted.<BR> E. प्रति mutually, श्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुति|प्रतिश्रुतिः
प्रतिश्रुति f. (-तिः) A reverberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषिद्ध|प्रतिषिद्धः
प्रतिषिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Forbidden, prohibited, disallowed.<BR>	 2. Con-<BR>tradictory.<BR> E. प्रति against, सिद्ध granted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषिद्धसेवन
प्रतिषिद्धसेवन n. (-नं) Doing what is prohibited.<BR> E. प्रतिषिद्ध and सेवन following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषिद्धसेविन्
प्रतिषिद्धसेविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Following or doing what is forbidden.<BR>E. प्रतिसिद्ध, and सेविन् who serves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेद्धृ
प्रतिषेद्धृ mfn. (-द्धा-द्ध्री-द्धृ) A prohibitor or prohibitive, prohibiting or<BR>forbidding.<BR> E. प्रति before, सिद्ध to make complete, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेध|प्रतिषेधः
प्रतिषेध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Prohibition, forbidding, exception, contradiction.<BR>2. Denial, refusal.<BR> E. प्रति before, सिद्ध to be perfect, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधक|प्रतिषेधकः
प्रतिषेधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what forbids, preventive, prohibitive.<BR>E. प्रति before, सिध् to complete, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधन|प्रतिषेधनं
प्रतिषेधन n. (-नं) Prohibiting, prohibition.<BR>	 2. Denial, refusal.<BR> E. प्रति, सिद्ध<BR>to complete, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधाक्षर
प्रतिषेधाक्षर n. (-रं) Denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधोक्ति|प्रतिषेधोक्तिः
प्रतिषेधोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Denial, refusal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधोपमा
प्रतिषेधोपमा f. (-मा) A kind of Simile thus explained by Dandin:--<BR>“न जातु शक्तिरिन्दोस्ते मुखेन प्रति गर्जितुम् ।<BR>कलङ्किनो जडस्येति प्रतिषेधोपमैव सा ॥”<BR>But according to modern writers this would be a व्यतिरेक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्क|प्रतिष्कः
प्रतिष्क m. (-ष्कः) A spy, an emissary.<BR> E. प्रति before, कष् to strike, aff.<BR>डं, and सुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कश|प्रतिष्कशः
प्रतिष्कश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A spy, a secret emissary, a Harkarā.<BR>	 2. A companion.<BR>3. A leader, a preceder.<BR>	 4. A whip, a leather thong.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>कश् to hurt or kill, aff. अच् and सुट् augment; if it is used attributively<BR>to imply the application of a whip, the augment is not inserted, as<BR>प्रतिकशाश्वः a horse that is whipped on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कष|प्रतिष्कषः
प्रतिष्कष m. (-षः) A whip, a leather thong.<BR> E. प्रति before, कष् to hurt, aff.<BR>अच्, and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कस|प्रतिष्कसः
प्रतिष्कस m. (-सः) A spy, a messenger, an emissary.<BR> E. प्रति before, कस् to<BR>go, aff. अच् and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=482-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्टब्ध
प्रतिष्टब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Obstructed, impeded, stopped.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>ष्टभि to hinder, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्टम्भ|प्रतिष्टंभ|प्रतिष्टंभः|प्रतिष्टम्भः
प्रतिष्टम्भ m. (-म्भः) Obstacle, impediment, opposition.<BR> E. प्रति before, ष्टभि<BR>to hinder, aff. अच्; or प्रति + स्तम्भ-भावे घञ् षत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठ|प्रतिष्ठः
प्रतिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Famous.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>	 1. Fame, celebrity.<BR>	 2. The<BR>earth.<BR>	 3. The accomplishment of a religious ceremony or any set<BR>of rites, especially those instituted for the attainment of super-<BR>natural and magical powers.<BR>	 4. A form of metre, consisting of a<BR>stanza of four lines, of four syllables each: it is also applied to a<BR>form of the Gāyatrī, being a triplet of 8, 7, and 6 syllable lines,<BR>making altogether 21 syllables.<BR>	 5. Place, scite.<BR>	 6. Staying, stand-<BR>ing, fixation.<BR>	 7. Limit, boundary.<BR>	 8. Accomplishment, completion,<BR>(in general.)<BR>	 9. Consecration of a monument erected in honour of<BR>a deity, or of the image of a deity.<BR>	 10. Endowment of a temple,<BR>portioning or marrying a daughter, &c.<BR>	 11. Fixity, Strength, firm<BR>foundation 12. Prop, support, Stay.<BR>	 13. Rest, tranquility.<BR>	 14. A<BR>receptacle.<BR>	 15. High authority, par-eminence.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः) The father<BR>of SUPĀRSWA, the seventh Jaina pontiff.<BR> E. प्रति before, स्था to stay<BR>or stand, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठान|प्रतिष्ठानं
प्रतिष्ठान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Site, situation.<BR>	 2. Foundation.<BR>	 3. Celebrity.<BR>	 4. The<BR>capital of the early kings of the lunar dynasty, opposite to Allā-<BR>hābād.<BR>	 5. The capital of SĀLIBĀHANA on the Godāvery, in the<BR>Dakshin.<BR> E. प्रति and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठापन|प्रतिष्ठापनं
प्रतिष्ठापन n. (-नं) Fixing, placing, locating.<BR> E. प्रति before, स्था to stay, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठापित
प्रतिष्ठापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Set up, located, fixed, erected.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>स्था to stay, causal v. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठासु
प्रतिष्ठासु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Wishing or intending to stay or remain.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>before, स्था to stay, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठित|प्रतिष्ठितः
प्रतिष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Famous, celebrated.<BR>	 2. Completed, finished.<BR>3. Consecrated.<BR>	 4. Endowed, portioned.<BR>	 5. Established in life,<BR>married, &c.<BR>	 6. Placed, situated.<BR>	 7. Established, fixed.<BR>	 8. Appli-<BR>cable or applied to.<BR>	 9. Comprised or included in, 10. Prized,<BR>valued.<BR>	 11. Secured, acquired.<BR> E. प्रतिष्ठा as above, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्णात
प्रतिष्णात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pure, (as a thread.)<BR> E. प्रति before, ष्णा to<BR>bathe, क्त aff., in any other sense प्रतिस्नात ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंङ्क्रम
प्रतिसंङ्क्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Reflection.<BR>	 2. Reabsorption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंख्या|प्रतिसङ्ख्या
प्रतिसंख्या f. (-ख्या) Consciousness.<BR> E. प्रति + सम + ख्या-भावे अङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंविद्
प्रतिसंविद् f. (-वित्) An accurate knowledge of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहार|प्रतिसंहारः
प्रतिसंहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Compression, diminution.<BR>	 2. Comprehension,<BR>inclusion.<BR>	 3. Withdrawing, taking back.<BR> E. प्रति, and सम् before,<BR>हृ to take, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहृत
प्रतिसंहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Comprehended, included.<BR>	 2. Compressed,<BR>reduced in bulk.<BR> E. प्रति and संहृत collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसञ्चर|प्रतिसंचर|प्रतिसंचरः
प्रतिसञ्चर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Reabsorption.<BR>	 2. Reabsorption of the world in<BR>Prakriti or in other words, the destruction of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसन्देश|प्रतिसंदेश|प्रतिसंदेशः
प्रतिसन्देश m. (-शः) A message sent in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसन्धान|प्रतिसंधान|प्रतिसंधानं
प्रतिसन्धान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Self-command, suppression of feeling for a time.<BR>3. Praise, panegyric.<BR>	 3. Meditating upon.<BR>	 4. Joining together.<BR>	 5.<BR>The period of transition between two ages.<BR>	 6. A remedy, a means.<BR>E. प्रति and सम् before, धा to have, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसन्धि|प्रतिसंधि|प्रतिसंधिः
प्रतिसन्धि m. (-न्धिः)<BR>	 1. Reunion.<BR>	 2. Cessation.<BR>	 3. The period of transi-<BR>tion between two ages.<BR> E. प्रति + सम् + धा-कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसम
प्रतिसम Adj. A match for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसमाधान|प्रतिसमाधानं
प्रतिसमाधान n. (-नं) A remedy, a cure.<BR> E. प्रति, सम and आङ् before, धा<BR>to have, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसमासन|प्रतिसमासनं
प्रतिसमासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Resisting, withstanding.<BR>	 2. The being a match for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसर|प्रतिसरः
प्रतिसर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) A servant, servile, dependent.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>rear of an army.<BR>	 2. A garland, a wreath.<BR>	 3. A bracelet.<BR>	 4. Cicatri-<BR>zing or healing, (as a sore.)<BR>	 5. A form of magic or incantation.<BR>	 6.<BR>Daybreak, morning.<BR>	 mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. A string worn round the hand<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">Page483-b+ 60</a>]<BR>at nuptials, &c.<BR>	 2. Ornament, adorning.<BR>	 3. The junction of the<BR>frontal sinuses of an elephant.<BR> E. प्रति before, सृ to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसर्ग|प्रतिसर्गः
प्रतिसर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. The portion of a Purāṇa, which treats of the des-<BR>truction and renovation of the world.<BR>	 2. Secondary creation, or<BR>the creation of the world by the agency of BRAHMĀ. and other<BR>divine beings regarded as the agents of one Supreme Being.<BR>	 2.<BR>Dissolution.<BR> E. प्रति severally, सर्ग going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसव्य|प्रतिसव्यं
प्रतिसव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Inverted, reverse.<BR> E. प्रति intensitive and सव्य the left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसान्धानिक|प्रतिसांधानिक|प्रतिसांधानिकः|प्रतिसान्धानिकः
प्रतिसान्धानिक m. (-कः) A bard, a panegyrist.<BR> E. प्रतिसन्धान praise, and<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसायम्
प्रतिसायम् Ind. Every-evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसारण|प्रतिसारणं
प्रतिसारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Repelling, repulsion.<BR>	 2. Applying remedies to<BR>a wound.<BR>	 3. An instrument for anointing a wound.<BR> E. प्रति, सृ to go,<BR>causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसारित
प्रतिसारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Repelled, repulsed.<BR>	 2. Dressed, as a wound.<BR>E. प्रति before, सृ to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसीरा
प्रतिसीरा f. (-रा) An outer tent, a screen or wall of cloth.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>षिञ् to bind, affs. रक् and टाप्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसूर्य्य|प्रतिसूर्य|प्रतिसूर्यः|प्रतिसूर्य्यः
प्रतिसूर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A lizard, a chameleon.<BR>	 n. adv. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Opposite to the<BR>sun.<BR>	 2. A mock sun.<BR> E. प्रति before, सूर्य्य the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसूर्य्यक|प्रतिसूर्यक|प्रतिसूर्यकः|प्रतिसूर्य्यकः
प्रतिसूर्य्यक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A lizard, a chameleon.<BR>	 2. The sun's disk.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>before or about, सूर्य्य the sun, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसृष्ट|प्रतिसृष्टः
प्रतिसृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Sent, dispatched.<BR>	 2. Repulsed.<BR>	 3. Celebrated.<BR>4. Given.<BR>	 5. Intoxicated.<BR> E. प्रति before, सृज् to create, &c. aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्कन्ध
प्रतिस्कन्ध n. adv. (-न्धं) Upon the shoulders.<BR> E. प्रति, and स्कन्ध shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्नात
प्रतिस्नात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bathed, washed.<BR> E. प्रति before, ष्णा to bathe,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्नेह|प्रतिस्नेहः
प्रतिस्नेह m. (-हः) A requital of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पन्दन|प्रतिस्पंदन|प्रतिस्पंदनं
प्रतिस्पन्दन n. (-नं) Throbbing, vibration.<BR> E. प्रति, and स्पन्दन throbbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पर्द्धा
प्रतिस्पर्द्धा f. (-र्द्धा) Emulation, rivalry, the wish or effort to excel or<BR>overcome.<BR> E. प्रति definitive prefix, and स्पर्द्धा emulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पर्द्धिन्
प्रतिस्पर्द्धिन् mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि)<BR>	 1. Envious, emulous, a rival.<BR>	 2. Refractory,<BR>rebellious.<BR> E. प्रतिस्पर्द्धा, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्याय
प्रतिस्याय m. (-यः) Catarrh.<BR> E. प्रति before, श्यै to drop, aff. अच्; see प्रतिश्याय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्रोतस्
प्रतिस्रोतस् n. adv. Against the stream.<BR> E. प्रति, and स्रोतस् current.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्वन|प्रतिस्वनः
प्रतिस्वन m. (-नः) Echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्वर|प्रतिस्वरः
प्रतिस्वर m. (-रः) Reverberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहत|प्रतिहतः
प्रतिहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Disappointed.<BR>	 1. Opposed, obstructed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fallen, overthrown.<BR>	 4. Sent, despatched.<BR>	 5. Hated, disliked.<BR>	 6.<BR>Tied, bound.<BR>	 7. Struck, hurt, killed, especially in return or<BR>requital.<BR>	 8. Repulsed, repelled.<BR>	 9. Reflected.<BR> E. प्रति before, हत<BR>hurt or killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहतमति
प्रतिहतमति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Averse to hating, disliking.<BR> E. प्रतिहत, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहति|प्रतिहतिः
प्रतिहति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Repulse, rebound, beating back or again.<BR>	 2. Disa-<BR>ppointment.<BR>	 3. Rebound.<BR>	 4. Anger, wrath.<BR> E. प्रति, and हति<BR>striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहनन|प्रतिहननं
प्रतिहनन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Striking again, returning a blow, &c.<BR> E. प्रति, and हनन striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहन्यमान
प्रतिहन्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being failed or disappointed.<BR> E. प्रतिहन् to<BR>disappoint, pass, v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहरण|प्रतिहरणं
प्रतिहरण n. (-णं) Avoiding, shunning.<BR> E. प्रति before, हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहस्त|प्रतिहस्तः
प्रतिहस्त m. (-स्तः) A deputy, a substitute.<BR> E. प्रति, and हस्त<BR>the hand; also with कन् added प्रतिहस्तक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहस्तिन्
प्रतिहस्तिन् m. (-स्ती) The keeper of a brothel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रति
प्रति(ती)हार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A door.<BR>	 2. A doorkeeper.<BR>	 3. A Juggler.<BR>	 4. Trick,<BR>disguise.<BR> E. प्रति against, हृ to take, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारक|प्रतिहारकः
प्रतिहारक m. (-कः) A Juggler.<BR> E. कन् added to प्रतिहार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारण|प्रतिहारणं
प्रतिहारण n. (-णं) Entrance, permission to enter a door. E.<BR>प्रति before, हृ to take, causal v. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारभूमि|प्रतिहारभूमिः
प्रतिहारभूमि f. (-मि) A threshold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहाररक्षी
प्रतिहाररक्षी f. (-क्षि) A female doorkeeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=483-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहास|प्रतिहासः
प्रतिहास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Returning a laugh, laughing with or at.<BR>2. A shrub, (Nerium odorum.)<BR> E. प्रति intensitive, हस् to<BR>smile, aff. घञ्, whence it is also प्रतीहास ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहित
प्रतिहित f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Fitted to.<BR>	 2. Placed on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहिंसा
प्रतिहिंसा f. (-सा) Retaliation, revenge.<BR> E. प्रति, and हिंसा injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक|प्रतीकः
प्रतीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Contrary, adverse.<BR>	 2. Inverted, reversed,<BR>against the natural order or state.<BR>	 3. Directed towards.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. A limb, a member.<BR>	 2. A part, a portion n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. the face.<BR>	 2.<BR>The front.<BR>	 3. An image.<BR>	 4. The first word of a verse or sentence. E.<BR>प्रति before, ई to go, ईकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रती
प्रती(ति)कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Revenge, retaliation.<BR>	 2. Remedying, obviating,<BR>correcting.<BR>	 3. Remedying, administering medicines.<BR> E. प्रति against,<BR>(re), and कार making, re-action, the is made long in conse-<BR>quence of the aff. being घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकाश|प्रतीकाशः
प्रतीकाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Like, resembling, (in composition.)<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Look, appearance.<BR>	 2. Reflection.<BR> E. प्रति before, काश् to shine, aff.<BR>घञ्; it is also written प्रतिकाश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षक
प्रतीक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Expecting.<BR>	 2. Looking at.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>ईक्ष् to see, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षण
प्रतीक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Looking to or at, considering, referring to.<BR>	 2. Re-<BR>specting.<BR>	 3. Expecting, waiting for.<BR> E. प्रति before, ईक्ष् to see,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षणीय
प्रतीक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be had in view, to be considered or re-<BR>garded.<BR> E. प्रति before, ईक्ष् to see, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षा
प्रतीक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Reference, regard to, consideration, looking to or<BR>at.<BR>	 2. Hope, expectation.<BR>	 3. Waiting for.<BR> E. प्रति before, ईक्ष् to see,<BR>अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षित
प्रतीक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Contemplated, considered, had regard to.<BR>2. Respected, honoured.<BR>	 3. Expected, looked for, hoped.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>before, ईक्ष् to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षिन्
प्रतीक्षिन् mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि) Expecting, looking or waiting for. E.<BR>प्रतीक्षा, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्ष्य|प्रतीक्ष्यः
प्रतीक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. To be considered, to be had regard to.<BR>2. To be expected. Ind. Having considered, having expected, &c.<BR>3. Venerable, respectable.<BR> E. प्रति before, ईक्ष् to see, aff. ण्यत् or ल्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीघात|प्रतीघातः
प्रतीघात m. (-तः) Warding off or returning as a blow.<BR>	 2. Preventing,<BR>prohibiting.<BR> E. प्रतिघात, and the इ made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीची
प्रतीची f. (-ची) The west quarter: see प्रत्यच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीचीन|प्रतीचीनं
प्रतीचीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. West, western, westerly.<BR>	 2. Future, Subse-<BR>quent.<BR> E. प्रतीची the west, and खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीच्छक|प्रतीच्छकः
प्रतीच्छक m. (-कः) A receiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीच्य|प्रतीच्यः
प्रतीच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) Western, west.<BR> E. प्रतीच for प्रत्यच् west, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीत|प्रतीतः
प्रतीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Famous, celebrated, renowned.<BR>	 2. Known by<BR>the name of, called.<BR>	 3. Glad, delighted, pleased.<BR>	 4. Respectful.<BR>5. Past, gone.<BR>	 6. Proved, established.<BR>	 7. Firmly determined.<BR>	 8.<BR>Learned.<BR>	 9. Believing in<BR> E. प्रति before, इ to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीति|प्रतीतिः
प्रतीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Knowledge, understanding.<BR>	 2. Fame, renown.<BR>	 3.<BR>Respect.<BR>	 4. Delight.<BR>	 5. Conviction.<BR> E. प्रति before, इ to go, aff.<BR>क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीत्त
प्रतीत्त f. (-त्ता) Adj. Given back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीन्धक|प्रतींधक|प्रतींधकः|प्रतीन्धकः
प्रतीन्धक m. (-कः) A name of the Videha country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीप|प्रतीपं|प्रतीपः
प्रतीप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Turned away, having the face averted.<BR>	 2. Back-<BR>wards, following an order or course the reverse of natural, against<BR>the grain or stream.<BR>	 3. Retrograde, coming back.<BR>	 4. Disobedient,<BR>refractory, perverse.<BR>	 5. Cross, contradictory.<BR>	 6. Disagreeable, dis-<BR>pleasing.<BR>	 m. (-पः) The father of SĀNTANU, and grandfather of<BR>BHĪṢMA.<BR>	 n. (-पं) Comparing Upamāna or a new object with Upa-<BR>meya or the established object, as with the moon, &c., inverse<BR>comparison. There are five forms of this figure according to<BR>some, and four according to others; some contend that it is not a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">Page484-b+ 60</a>]<BR>separate figure but a form of Upamā.<BR> E. प्रति before, अप् water,<BR>and the अ changed to इ by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपम्
प्रतीपम् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of “against” as in<BR>मा स्म प्रतीपं गमः; secondly “in an inverted order.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपग
प्रतीपग Adj. Going against, unfavourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपगमन
प्रतीपगमन (-नं) n. Retrograde motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपतरण
प्रतीपतरण n. (-णं) Sailing against the stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपदर्शिनी
प्रतीपदर्शिनी f. (-नी) A woman.<BR> E. प्रतीप turning the face away, and दर्शिनी looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपवचन
प्रतीपवचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Contradiction.<BR>	 2. A perverse or evasive answer, a<BR>speech to a third person without replying to a previous speaker.<BR>E. प्रतीप, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीमान
प्रतीमान n. (-नं) A measure of capacity.<BR> E. प्रति, and मा to measure,<BR>ल्युट् aff. and the vowel of the prep. made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीयमान
प्रतीयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being believed or trusted.<BR> E. प्रति before, इ<BR>to go, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीयिवस्
प्रतीयिवस् mfn. (-वान्-युसी-वस्) Coming back, returning.<BR> E. प्रति back, ईय् to go, क्कसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीर|प्रतीरं
प्रतीर n. (-रं) A shore or bank.<BR> E. प्र beyond, तीर shore, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवाप|प्रतीवापः
प्रतीवाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Calcining or fluxing metals.<BR>	 2. Throwing one sub-<BR>stance into another to alter its form or state.<BR>	 3. Adding any<BR>thing to a medicine during or after decoction.<BR>	 4. Mixing whey<BR>with milk.<BR>	 5. A public danger or calamity, as a plague, &c. E.<BR>प्रति before, वप् to spread, aff. घञ्, whence the vowel of the<BR>prefix is lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवेश|प्रतीवेशः
प्रतीवेश m. (-शः) A neighbouring residence, a neighbourhood: see प्रतिवेश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवेशिन
प्रतीवेशिन mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) A neighbour, living in the neighbourhood.<BR>E. प्रतिवेश a neighbourhood, and इनि aff; also प्रतिवेशिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहार|प्रतीहारः
प्रतीहार m. (रः)<BR>	 1. A door.<BR>	 2. A porter, a warder.<BR>	 3. An agreement<BR>for return of assistance, alliance, confederacy.<BR>	 f. (-री) A female<BR>doorkeeper; (though this word is a feminine in form, is not<BR>necessarily so in sense.)<BR> E. प्रति severally, mutually, हृ to convey,<BR>aff. घञ्; also प्रतिहार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहास|प्रतीहासः
प्रतीहास m. (-सः) A plant, (Nerium odorum.)<BR> E. प्रति before, हस् to<BR>smile, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुद|प्रतुदः
प्रतुद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A bird of game, a falcon, a hawk, or rather one that<BR>kills or strikes with his beak, including also the owl, parrot,<BR>crow, raven, peacock, &c.<BR>	 2. An instrument for pricking. E.<BR>प्र before, तुद् to torment, (with the beak,) and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुष्टि|प्रतुष्टिः
प्रतुष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Satisfaction, gratification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुष्टुषु
प्रतुष्टुषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु)<BR>	 1. Wishing to praise.<BR>	 2. Wishing to prepare or<BR>make ready.<BR> E. प्र before, ष्टु to praise, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतूणी
प्रतूणी f. (-णी) Pain shooting from the rectum along the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतूर्ण
प्रतूर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Quick, fleet.<BR> E. प्र before, त्वर् to make haste,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोद|प्रतोदः
प्रतोद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A long whip.<BR>	 2. A goad.<BR> E. प्र thoroughly, तुद् to tor-<BR>ment, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोली
प्रतोली f. (-ली) A high street, the principal road through a town or<BR>village.<BR> E. प्र before, तुल् to weigh, aff. अच् गौरा० ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोलीक
प्रतोलीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having a high street, (a town.)<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्त|प्रत्तं
प्रत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Given, presented.<BR>	 2. Given in marriage, either<BR>betrothed or married.<BR> E. प्र before, दा to give, aff. क्त, form special.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्तवत्
प्रत्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Giving, presenting.<BR> E. प्र before, दा to give,<BR>क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्न|प्रत्नः
प्रत्न mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं)<BR>	 1. Old, ancient.<BR>	 2. Traditional, customary.<BR> E. प्र for<BR>प्रगे here said to mean old, त्न aff. and गे rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक
प्रत्यक Ind.<BR>	 1. Subsequent, behind, following in time or place.<BR>	 2. In an<BR>opposite direction.<BR>	 3. Against.<BR>	 4. In the interior.<BR>	 5. Uniform,<BR>unmixed.<BR>	 6. Western.<BR>	 7. Formerly, in old days: see प्रत्यच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्पर्णी
प्रत्यक्पर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR> E. प्रत्यच् uniform,<BR>and पर्ण a leaf. “अपामार्गे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=484-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्पुष्पी
प्रत्यक्पुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR> E. प्रत्यच् uniform,<BR>पुष्प a flower. “अपामार्गे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्श्रेणी
प्रत्यक्श्रेणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Dantī.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Sal-<BR>vinia cucullata.)<BR> E. प्रत्यक् western, and श्रेणी line or row.<BR>“मूषिकपर्ण्याञ्च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्ष|प्रत्यक्षं
प्रत्यक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Perceptible, perceivable, present, cognizable<BR>by any of the organs of sense.<BR>	 2. Distinct, clear, evident.<BR>	 3. Direct,<BR>immediate.<BR>	 4. Corporeal.<BR>	 n. (-क्षं) Ocular evidence, apprehension by<BR>the senses, perception, (considered as a mode of proof. In Phil.) E.<BR>अक्ष an organ of sense with प्रति indicative prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षम्
प्रत्यक्षम् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of:--1. In the pre-<BR>sence of, before, 2. Publicly.<BR>	 3. Immediately, directly, personally:<BR>also similar words as प्रत्यक्षेण and प्रत्यक्षात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षज्ञान
प्रत्यक्षज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge obtained by perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षतस्
प्रत्यक्षतस् Ind. Evidently, perceptibly.<BR> E. प्रत्यक्ष, and तम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षदर्शन|प्रत्यक्षदर्शनं
प्रत्यक्षदर्शन m. (-नः) A witness, an eye-witness.<BR> E. प्रत्यक्ष what is present,<BR>and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षप्रमा
प्रत्यक्षप्रमा f. (-मा) Correct knowledge obtained through perception by<BR>the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षप्रमाण
प्रत्यक्षप्रमाण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Ocular proof, evidence of the senses.<BR>	 2. An organ<BR>or faculty of perception.<BR> E. प्रत्यक्ष and प्रमाण proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षफल
प्रत्यक्षफल Adj. Having visible consequences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षभूत
प्रत्यक्षभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Manifested, become visible.<BR> E. प्रत्यक्ष and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षभोग|प्रत्यक्षभोगः
प्रत्यक्षभोग m. (-गः) Enjoyment or use of any thing with the con-<BR>sciousness of the owner.<BR> E. प्रत्यक्ष, and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षवादिन्
प्रत्यक्षवादिन् m. (-दी) A Bauddha.<BR> E. प्रत्यक्ष, and वादिन् who declares;<BR>admitting of no other evidence than actual presence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षविहित
प्रत्यक्षविहित Adj. Expressly enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षिन्
प्रत्यक्षिन् mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि) Seeing, perceiving, conscious of what is<BR>perceptible.<BR> E. प्रत्यक्ष perceptible, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षीकरण
प्रत्यक्षीकरण n. (-णं) Making manifest or apparent.<BR> E. प्रत्यक्ष, करण mak-<BR>ing, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षीकृत
प्रत्यक्षीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Manifested, displayed, made present or<BR>visible.<BR> E. प्रत्यक्ष and कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्स्रोतस्
प्रत्यक्स्रोतस् Adj. Flowing towards the west.<BR>	 f. (-तः) An epithet of<BR>Narmadā, the river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यगक्ष
प्रत्यगक्ष n. (-क्षं) An inner organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यगात्मन्
प्रत्यगात्मन् m. (-त्मा) The individual soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यगाशापति|प्रत्यगाशापतिः
प्रत्यगाशापति m. (-तिः) A name of VARUṆA.<BR> E. प्रत्यक् west, आशा a quarter,<BR>पति regent or lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यगुदच्
प्रत्यगुदच् f. (-दङ्) The north-west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्र|प्रत्यग्रः
प्रत्यग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. New, fresh, recent.<BR>	 2. Pre-purified.<BR>	 3. Repea-<BR>ted.<BR> E. प्रति before, अग्र first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्रता
प्रत्यग्रता f. (-ता) Newness, freshness.<BR> E. तल् added to प्रत्यग्र; also with<BR>त्व, प्रत्यग्रत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्रथ|प्रत्यग्रथः
प्रत्यग्रथ m. (-थः) A country; also अहिच्छत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्रवयस्
प्रत्यग्रवयस् n. (-यः) Youth.<BR> E. प्रत्यग्र, and वयस् age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यङ्ग|प्रत्यंग|प्रत्यङ्गं
प्रत्यङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) An organ of perception.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-ङ्गं) On the body, or<BR>the limbs severally.<BR>	 n. Subst. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. A minor member of the<BR>body, as the chin, nose, ear, &c.<BR>	 2. A subdivision of science, &c.<BR>E. प्रति belonging to, अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यङ्गिराः
प्रत्यङ्गिराः f. (-रा) A form of DURGĀ, one of the goddesses of the<BR>Tantrīkas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यङ्मुख
प्रत्यङ्मुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Facing the west.<BR> E. प्रत्यञ्च, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यच्
प्रत्यच् or प्रत्यञ्च् mfn. (-प्रत्यङ्-प्रतीची or according to some प्रत्यञ्ची-प्रत्यक्)<BR>1. Behind or subsequent, following in time or place.<BR>	 2. Turned<BR>away.<BR>	 3. West, western.<BR>	 4. Uniform, unmixed.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>अञ्च् to go, aff. क्विप् or विच्; the neuter form is used as a particle:<BR>see प्रत्यक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यञ्च्|प्रत्यंच्
प्रत्यच् or प्रत्यञ्च् mfn. (-प्रत्यङ्-प्रतीची or according to some प्रत्यञ्ची-प्रत्यक्)<BR>1. Behind or subsequent, following in time or place.<BR>	 2. Turned<BR>away.<BR>	 3. West, western.<BR>	 4. Uniform, unmixed.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>अञ्च् to go, aff. क्विप् or विच्; the neuter form is used as a particle:<BR>see प्रत्यक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यदन
प्रत्यदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Eating.<BR>	 2. Food.<BR> E. प्रति before, अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यनन्तर|प्रत्यनंतर
प्रत्यनन्तर n. Adv. (-रं) Next in succession.<BR> E. प्रति, अनन्तर without an<BR>interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यनीक|प्रत्यनीकः
प्रत्यनीक m. (-कः) An enemy.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Injuring one who cannot retaliate.<BR>E. प्रति against, अनीक an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यन्त|प्रत्यंत|प्रत्यन्तः
प्रत्यन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्त) Bordering, skirting, contiguous.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः) The<BR>country of the Mlecchas or savages.<BR> E. प्रति about, अन्त the end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यन्तपर्व्वत|प्रत्यन्तपर्वत|प्रत्यंतपर्वत|प्रत्यन्तपर्व्वतः
प्रत्यन्तपर्व्वत m. (-तः) A small hill near a mountain.<BR> E. प्रत्यन्त skirting, and<BR>पर्व्वत a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञात
प्रत्यभिज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Recognised, known.<BR> E. प्रति, and अभि before,<BR>ज्ञा to know, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञान|प्रत्यभिज्ञानं
प्रत्यभिज्ञान n. (-नं) Recognition, knowing, recognising.<BR> E. प्रति and अभि<BR>before, ज्ञा to know, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिभूत
प्रत्यभिभूत f. (-ता) Overcome, conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभियुक्त
प्रत्यभियुक्त f. (-क्ता) Accused in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभियोग|प्रत्यभियोगः
प्रत्यभियोग m. (-गः) A counter plaint or charge, an accusation brought<BR>against the accuser or plaintiff.<BR> E. प्रति against, अभियोग accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिवाद|प्रत्यभिवादः
प्रत्यभिवाद m. (-दः) Returning a salute or obeisance, the benediction<BR>of a teacher.<BR> E. प्रति (re), अभिवाद salute; also प्रत्यभिवादन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यय|प्रत्ययः
प्रत्यय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Trust, faith, belief, confidence.<BR>	 2. Oath, ordeal.<BR>	 3.<BR>Cause, motive.<BR>	 4. Usage, custom, practice.<BR>	 5. Fame, celebrity.<BR>6. Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 7. Knewledge, apprehension.<BR>	 8. A<BR>termination or an affix to roots and words forming derivatives and<BR>inflections, (in Gram.)<BR>	 9. A dependent, a subject, 10. Instrument,<BR>means of agency, a helpmate or associate, applicable either<BR>to persons or things.<BR>	 11. A householder who keeps a sacred fire.<BR>12. Religious contemplation.<BR>	 13. A hole.<BR> E. प्रति again, against,<BR>to or towards, इण् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययकारिणी
प्रत्ययकारिणी f. (-णी) A seal, a signet.<BR> E. प्रत्यय confidence, and कारिणी causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययित|प्रत्ययितः
प्रत्ययित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Trusted, confidential.<BR> E. प्रत्यय confidence, and<BR>इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययिन्
प्रत्ययिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Trusting, believing, having faith in.<BR> E. प्रत्यय,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थ
प्रत्यर्थ n. (-र्थं)<BR>	 1. A reply, an answer, a counter-representation.<BR>	 2. Oppo-<BR>sition, hostility.<BR>	 f. (-र्था) Useful, expedient.<BR> E. प्रति successive order,<BR>and अर्थ representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थक|प्रत्यर्थकः
प्रत्यर्थक m. (-कः) An opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थिन्
प्रत्यर्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>	 1. Hostile, inimical.<BR>	 2. Opposing, contra-<BR>dicting, rejecting.<BR>	 m. (-र्थी)<BR>	 1. An enemy.<BR>	 2. (In law,) A defendant.<BR>E. प्रति again, against (re), अर्थ meaning, intention, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्पण|प्रत्यर्पणं
प्रत्यर्पण n. (-णं) The returning of a thing.<BR> E. प्रति back, अर्पण delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्पित|प्रत्यर्पितं
प्रत्यर्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Returned, restored, re-delivered.<BR> E. प्रति again,<BR>अर्पित delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवमर्श|प्रत्यवमर्शः
प्रत्यवमर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Counsel, advice, injunction.<BR>	 2. Profound contem-<BR>plation.<BR>	 3. A counter-conclusion.<BR> E. प्रति and अव before, मृश् to<BR>advise, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवमर्ष|प्रत्यवमर्षः
प्रत्यवमर्ष m. (-र्षः) Patience, constant in pursuit or exertion.<BR> E. प्रति, अव<BR>before, मृष् to bear, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवरोधन|प्रत्यवरोधनं
प्रत्यवरोधन n. (-नं) Obstruction, hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवसान|प्रत्यवसानं
प्रत्यवसान n. (-नं) Eating.<BR> E. प्रति and अव prefixed to षो to destroy, aff.<BR>ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवसित|प्रत्यवसितं
प्रत्यवसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eaten.<BR> E. प्रति, अव before, षो to destroy, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्कन्द|प्रत्यवस्कंद|प्रत्यवस्कंदः|प्रत्यवस्कन्दः
प्रत्यवस्कन्द m. (-न्दः) A special plea at law; admission of a fact, but quali-<BR>fying or explaining it so as not to allow it to be a matter of accu-<BR>sation.<BR> E. प्रति against, अव before, स्कदि to go, aff. घञ्; also with<BR>ल्युट् aff. प्रत्यवस्कन्दन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्थातृ
प्रत्यवस्थातृ m. (-ता) An enemy.<BR> E. प्रति and अव before, स्था to stay, to<BR>oppose or encounter and तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्थान|प्रत्यवस्थानं
प्रत्यवस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Former state or place, in status quo.<BR>	 2. Removal.<BR>3. Opposition, hostility.<BR> E. प्रति and अवस्थान situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवहार|प्रत्यवहारः
प्रत्यवहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Withdrawal.<BR>	 2. Universal destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=485-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवाय|प्रत्यवायः
प्रत्यवाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Sin.<BR>	 2. Disappearance, either of what exists or non-<BR>production of what does not exist.<BR>	 3. Reverse, contrary course or<BR>proceeding.<BR>	 4. Disappointment.<BR>	 5. Disarrangement.<BR> E. प्रति and<BR>अव before, इण् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवेक्षण|प्रत्यवेक्षणं
प्रत्यवेक्षण n. (-णं) Looking after, taking care of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यश्मन्
प्रत्यश्मन् n. (-श्म) Red chalk.<BR> E. प्रति like, अश्मन् a stone. “गैरिके” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यस्तमय|प्रत्यस्तमयः
प्रत्यस्तमय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The setting of the sun.<BR>	 2. End, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यहम्
प्रत्यहम् Ind.<BR>	 1. In the morning.<BR>	 2. Day by day, every day.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>implying succession, and अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याकार|प्रत्याकारः
प्रत्याकार m. (-रः) A scabbard, a sheath.<BR> E. प्रति like, आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याकलित
प्रत्याकलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Interposed.<BR>	 2. Introduced, as a step in<BR>legal process.<BR> E. प्रति and आङ् before, कल् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याक्षेपक
प्रत्याक्षेपक f. (-पिका) Deriding, treating scornfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्यात|प्रत्याख्यातः
प्रत्याख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Removed, set aside.<BR>	 2. Informed, apprised.<BR>3. Discouraged, prohibited, forbidden.<BR>	 4. Denied, refused.<BR>	 5.<BR>Celebrated, notorious.<BR> E. प्रति before, आख्यात said, declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्यान|प्रत्याख्यानं
प्रत्याख्यान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rejection, refutation, disallowance, disregard.<BR>	 2.<BR>Denial, refusal.<BR>	 3. Reproach.<BR> E. प्रति reverse, आङ् before, ख्या to<BR>say and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्येय
प्रत्याख्येय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be declined or refused.<BR>	 2. To be refuted,<BR>denied, &c.<BR> E. प्रति and आङ् before, ख्या to speak, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागत
प्रत्यागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Come back, returned.<BR>	 2. Arrived at.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>again, आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागम|प्रत्यागमः
प्रत्यागम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Return.<BR>	 2. Arrival.<BR> E. प्रति, and आगम coming; also<BR>प्रत्यागमन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागार
प्रत्यागार m. (-रः) Former place or state.<BR> E. प्रति, and आगार mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादान|प्रत्यादानं
प्रत्यादान n. (-नं) Resumption, receiving back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादिष्ट|प्रत्यादिष्टः
प्रत्यादिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Removed, set aside.<BR>	 2. Informed, apprised.<BR>3. Warned, cautioned.<BR>	 4. Declared, (as from heaven.)<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>आदिष्ट shown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादेश|प्रत्यादेशः
प्रत्यादेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Rejection, disallowance.<BR>	 2. Information, apprising,<BR>informing.<BR>	 3. Warning, caution.<BR>	 4. Refusal, denial.<BR>	 5. Putting to<BR>shame, obscuring.<BR>	 6. Heavenly annunciation or declaration.<BR> E. प्रति,<BR>आङ् before, दिश् to show, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यानयन|प्रत्यानयनं
प्रत्यानयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Bringing back, recovering.<BR> E. प्रति, आङ् before, णी to<BR>lead, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यानिनीषु
प्रत्यानिनीषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Desirous of bringing back.<BR> E. प्रति and आङ् be-<BR>fore, णी to bring, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यानीत
प्रत्यानीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Brought back.<BR> E. प्रति and आङ् before, णी to<BR>obtain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यापत्ति|प्रत्यापत्तिः
प्रत्यापत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Return.<BR>	 2. Indifference to wordly objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याम्नाय|प्रत्याम्नायः
प्रत्याम्नाय m. (-यः) The fifth member of a complete syllogism, (the repe-<BR>tition of the first statement).<BR> E. प्रतिरूपतया आम्नायते प्रति + आ + म्ना-<BR>कर्मणि घञ् । प्रतिनिधित्वेन विधीयमाने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याय|प्रत्यायः
प्रत्याय m. (-यः) A toll, a tax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायन|प्रत्यायनं
प्रत्यायन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Marrying.<BR>	 2. Setting.<BR> E. प्रति + आ + इ-णिच् “णौ गमिर<BR>बोधने” पातञ्जल उक्तेः न गमादेशः भावे ल्युट् । बोधने, विश्वासजनने च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यालीढ|प्रत्यालीढं
प्रत्यालीढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Eaten.<BR>	 n. (-ढं) A particular attitude in shoot-<BR>ing, the left foot advanced and right retracted.<BR> E. प्रति and आङ्<BR>before, लिह् to lick, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यावर्त्तन|प्रत्यावर्तन|प्रत्यावर्तनं
प्रत्यावर्त्तन n. (-नं) Returning, coming back.<BR> E. प्रति and आङ् before, वृत् to<BR>be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यावृत्त
प्रत्यावृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Returned, come back.<BR> E. प्रति and आङ् before,<BR>वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याशा
प्रत्याशा f. (-शा) Hope, expectation, desire.<BR> E. प्रति specific, and आशा hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याशिन्
प्रत्याशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Hoping, expecting.<BR> E. प्रत्याशा, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याश्वस्त
प्रत्याश्वस्त f. (-स्ता) Revived refreshed, consoled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याश्वास|प्रत्याश्वासः
प्रत्याश्वास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Respiration.<BR>	 2. Consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासङ्कलित|प्रत्यासंकलित
प्रत्यासङ्कलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Added to.<BR>	 2. Ascertained, determined. E.<BR>प्रति and आङ् before, सङ्कलित added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासत्ति|प्रत्यासत्तिः
प्रत्यासत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Close contact.<BR>	 2. An agony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासन्न|प्रत्यासन्नः
प्रत्यासन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Near, proximate, contiguous.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>आसन्न near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यास
प्रत्यास(सा)र m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The rear of an army.<BR>	 2. An array behind an<BR>array.<BR> E. प्रति and आङ् before, सृ to go, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासार|प्रत्यासारः
प्रत्यासार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The rear of an army.<BR>	 2. A form of array.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>and आङ् before, सृ to go, aff. घञ्; also प्रत्यासर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहत
प्रत्याहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Repelled, resisted, repulsed.<BR> E. प्रति, and आहत<BR>struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहरण|प्रत्याहरणं
प्रत्याहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Restraining the organs of sense.<BR>	 2. Taking back.<BR>3. Withholding.<BR> E. प्रति and आङ् before, हृ to take, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहरणीय
प्रत्याहरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be restrained or controlled.<BR>	 2. Resum-<BR>able, to be taken back.<BR>	 3. To be withheld, &c.<BR> E. प्रति and आङ्<BR>before, हृ to take, अनीयर् aff.; also प्रत्याहर्त्तव्य and प्रत्याहार्य्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहार|प्रत्याहारः
प्रत्याहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Abstraction, insensibility, restraining the organs so<BR>as to be indifferent to disagreeable or agreeable excitement, (in Yoga<BR>Phil.)<BR>	 2. Abridgement, compendium.<BR>	 3. (In gram. Combination<BR>of two or more letters of the alphabet to form a class of letters;<BR>the inclusion of a number of letters into one syllable effected<BR>by combining the first letter of a Sūtra with its final indicatory<BR>consonant:--as “अच्” or “हल्” in Pānini's gram.<BR>	 4. Substitution of<BR>one thing for another.<BR>	 5. Withholding.<BR>	 6. Taking back.<BR>	 7. March-<BR>ing back, retracting.<BR>	 8. The dissolution of the world.<BR> E. प्रति and<BR>आङ् before, हृ to seize or convey, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहृत
प्रत्याहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Withheld.<BR>	 2. Restrained.<BR>	 3. Resumed, &c.:<BR>E. प्रति and आङ् before, हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युक्ति|प्रत्युक्तिः
प्रत्युक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Answer, reply.<BR>	 2. Contradiction.<BR> E. प्रति again, वच्<BR>to speak, aff. क्तिन्, the semi-vowel changed to उ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युच्चार|प्रत्युच्चारः
प्रत्युच्चार m. (-रः) Repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युज्जीवन|प्रत्युज्जीवनं
प्रत्युज्जीवन n. (-नं) Revivifying, resuscitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत
प्रत्युत Ind. On the contrary, on the other hand, otherwise.<BR> E. प्रति and<BR>उत whether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्क्रम|प्रत्युत्क्रमः
प्रत्युत्क्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A subordinate act, or effort tending to a main<BR>object.<BR>	 2. First step or measure in any business.<BR>	 3. Declaration<BR>of war.<BR>	 4. Setting out to assail an enemy.<BR> E. प्रति and उत् before,<BR>क्रम् to go, aff. अच्; also प्रत्युत्क्रमण and प्रत्युत्क्रान्ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्क्रान्ति|प्रत्युत्क्रांति|प्रत्युत्क्रांतिः|प्रत्युत्क्रान्तिः
प्रत्युत्क्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः) A subordinate act, tending to a main object, &c.:<BR>see the last. E. As above, see प्रत्युत्क्रम aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्तर|प्रत्युत्तरं
प्रत्युत्तर n. (-रं) A rejoinder, a reply to an answer, an answer.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>again, उत्तर an answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्थान|प्रत्युत्थानं
प्रत्युत्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rising from a seat, as a mark of respect shown<BR>to a visitor.<BR>	 2. Making preparations for an encounter.<BR>	 3. Rising<BR>against.<BR> E. प्रति and उत् before, स्था to stay, aff. ल्युट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्थित
प्रत्युत्थित f. (-ता) Adj. Risen to meet or to encounter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्न|प्रत्युत्पन्नः
प्रत्युत्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Reproduced, regenerated.<BR>	 2. Prompt, ready.<BR>3. (In arithmetic,) Multiplied.<BR>	 n. (-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Multiplication.<BR>	 2. The<BR>product of a sum in multiplication.<BR> E. प्रति again, उत्पन्न produced,<BR>or प्रति and उत् before, पन्न made, done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्नजाति|प्रत्युत्पन्नजातिः
प्रत्युत्पन्नजाति f. (-तिः) (In arithmetic,) Assimilation of fractional increase.<BR>E. प्रत्युत्पन्न, and जाति reduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्नमति|प्रत्युत्पन्नमतिः
प्रत्युत्पन्नमति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>	 1. Confident, bold, arrogant.<BR>	 2. Sharp,<BR>subtle, quick.<BR>	 3. Endowed with presence of mind, ready-witted.<BR>E. प्रत्युत्पन्न prompt, and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गत
प्रत्युद्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Met.<BR>	 2. Risen, as from a seat to receive a<BR>visitor.<BR>	 3. Gone forth against.<BR> E. प्रति, उद्गत gone up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गम|प्रत्युद्गमः
प्रत्युद्गम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Rising, as from a seat.<BR>	 2. Going to meet a guest,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. Counterbalance.<BR> E. प्रति and उद् before, गम् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गमन|प्रत्युद्गमनं
प्रत्युद्गमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rising from a seat, as a mark of respect, &c.<BR>2. Going forth or out, going to meet any one, &c.<BR> E. प्रति and उत्<BR>before, गम् to go, aff. घञ्; also with ल्युट्, प्रत्युद्गमनं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गमनीय|प्रत्युद्गमनीयं
प्रत्युद्गमनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be placed near, upon or before.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be worshipped or reverenced.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A pair of bleached cloths,<BR>or the upper and lower garments, as worn at meals and sacrifices,<BR>&c.<BR> E. प्रति and उत् before, गम् to go, अनीयर् aff. of the future par-<BR>ticiple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्धरण|प्रत्युद्धरणं
प्रत्युद्धरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Recovering, re-obtaining.<BR>	 2. Rising up again. E.<BR>प्रति, उद् before, हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्धृत
प्रत्युद्धृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Recovered.<BR> E. प्रति and उद् before, हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्यम|प्रत्युद्यमः
प्रत्युद्यम m. (-मः) Counteracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्यात
प्रत्युद्यात f. (-ता) Adj.: see प्रत्युद्गत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपकार|प्रत्युपकारः
प्रत्युपकार m. (-रः) Requital or aid or assistance, mutual assistance. E.<BR>प्रति, and उपकार aid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपकारिन्
प्रत्युपकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Requiting a favour or kindness. E.<BR>प्रत्युपकार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपलब्ध
प्रत्युपलब्ध f. (-ब्धा) Recovered, gained back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपवेष
प्रत्युपवेष m. (-षः) Besetting any one in order to bring him to compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपस्थान|प्रत्युपस्थानं
प्रत्युपस्थान n. (-नं) Vicinity, neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युप्त
प्रत्युप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Set, inlaid, studded.<BR>	 2. Sown.<BR> E. प्रति before,<BR>वप् to sow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युव
प्रत्युव m. (-षः) The morning, dawn, daybreak. E. See प्रत्यूष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युषस्
प्रत्युषस् n. (-षः) Morning. E. See प्रत्यूषस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूष|प्रत्यूषं|प्रत्यूषः
प्रत्यूष mn. (-षः-षं)<BR>	 1. Morning.<BR>	 2. One of the demi-gods called VASUS.<BR>3. The sun.<BR> E. प्रति before, ऊष् to be sick, aff. क; also with उष्<BR>to burn, प्रत्युष; and with असि aff. प्रत्युषस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूषस्
प्रत्यूषस् n. (-षः) Morning, dawn.<BR> E. प्रति before, ऊष् to be sick, and असि<BR>aff.; also प्रत्युष and प्रत्युषस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूह|प्रत्यूहः
प्रत्यूह m. (-हः) Obstacle, impediment.<BR> E. प्रति before, ऊह् to infer, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्येक|प्रत्येकं
प्रत्येक n. Adv. (-कं) Singly, one by one, one at a time.<BR> E. प्रति, and<BR>एक one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्येतृ
प्रत्येतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Believing, trusting, having confidence.<BR> E. प्रति<BR>before, इ to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथ
प्रथ r. 1st. cl. (प्रथते)<BR>	 1. To be famous or renowned.<BR>	 2. To increase.<BR>3. To Spread abroad.<BR>	 4. To appear, to arise. भ्वा० आ० अक० सेट् । r.<BR>10th cl. (प्राथयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To throw or cast.<BR>	 2. To scatter, to spread.<BR>3. To celebrate. ख्यातौ अक० विक्षेपे सक० चुरा० उभ० सेट् घटा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथन|प्रथनं
प्रथन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Spreading, extension, scattering.<BR>	 2. Throwing, projec-<BR>ting.<BR>	 3. Celebrating.<BR>	 4. Showing, evincing.<BR>	 5. A place where any<BR>thing is spread.<BR> E. प्रथ् to cast, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथम|प्रथमः
प्रथम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. First, prior, initial.<BR>	 2. Chief, principal,<BR>incomparable.<BR>	 3. The “third person” (in gram.) according to<BR>European System. The nominative Plu. M. of this word is either<BR>प्रथमे or प्रथमा<BR> E. प्रथ् to be famous, अमच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमम्
प्रथमम् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of:--1. Firstly.<BR>	 2.<BR>Previously.<BR>	 3. Immediately.<BR>	 4. Before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमकल्प|प्रथमकल्पः
प्रथमकल्प m. (ल्पः) The best course to follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमकल्पित
प्रथमकल्पित f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. First in rank.<BR>	 2. Previously devised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमयौवन
प्रथमयौवन n. (-नं) The first period of youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमसाहस|प्रथमसाहसः
प्रथमसाहस m. (-सः) The first or lowest degree of fine or punishment.<BR>E. प्रथम, and साहस infliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथयत्|प्रथयन्त्
प्रथयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Displaying, making manifest, famous,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Seeing, beholding.<BR>	 3. Casting, throwing.<BR> E. प्रथ् to be famous,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथा
प्रथा f. (-था) Fame, celebrity.<BR> E. प्रथ् to be famous, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथित|प्रथितः
प्रथित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Famous, celebrated.<BR>	 2. Made known, declared.<BR>3. Increased, extended.<BR>	 4. Published announced.<BR>	 5. Shewn, mani-<BR>fested, evinced.<BR>	 6. Spread, scattered.<BR>	 7. Stretched.<BR>	 8. Cast, thro-<BR>wn.<BR>	 9. Intent upon, engaged in, occupied with, devoted to.<BR> E. प्रथा<BR>fame, aff. इतच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिति|प्रथितिः
प्रथिति f. (-तिः) Celebrity, notoriety.<BR> E. प्रथ् to be famous, ति Unādi aff.,<BR>and इट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिमन्
प्रथिमन् m. (-मा) Greatness, extension, magnitude.<BR> E. पृथु large, इमनिच्<BR>aff. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिमिन्
प्रथिमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Large, great, having size or magnitude. E.<BR>प्रथिमा magnitude, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिवि|प्रथिविः
प्रथिवि f. (-वि) The earth; also प्रथिवी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिष्ठ|प्रथिष्ठः
प्रथिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very large.<BR> E. पृथु large, इष्ठन् superl, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथीयस्
प्रथीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very large.<BR> E. पृथु large and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथु|प्रथुः
प्रथु Adj. Wide, wide-spread, m. (-थुः) Viṣṇu.<BR> E. प्रथ-उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथुक|प्रथुकः
प्रथुक m. (-कः) The young of any animal.<BR> E. प्रथ् to be famous, कुकन्<BR>aff. see पृथुक. According to Vāchaspatya:--Rice parched and<BR>flattened.<BR> E. प्रथ बा उक “चिपिटके” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद|प्रदः
प्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) A giver, giving bountiful.<BR>	 f. (-दा) A gift, a dona-<BR>tion.<BR> E. प्र before, दा to give, श aff. or अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिण|प्रदक्षिणं|प्रदक्षिणः
प्रदक्षिण mfn. subst. (-णः-णा-णं) Reverential salutation, by circumam-<BR>bulating a person or object, keeping the right side towards them.<BR>E. प्र before, दक्षिण the right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणम्
प्रदक्षिणम् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of,:--1. From left<BR>to right.<BR>	 2. Turning the right side towords.<BR>	 3. In a southern<BR>direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिणपट्टिका
प्रदक्षिणपट्टिका f. (-का) A courtyard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदग्ध
प्रदग्ध f. (-ग्धा) Burnt, consumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदत्त|प्रदत्तं
प्रदत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Given, bestowed, conferred.<BR> E. प्र before, दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर|प्रदरः
प्रदर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Splitting, rending, tearing.<BR>	 2. Fracturation, breaking.<BR>3. The dispersion of an army.<BR>	 4. A disease of women, (Mænorr-<BR>hagia.)<BR>	 5. An arrow.<BR> E. प्र intensitive, दृ to tear, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्प|प्रदर्पः
प्रदर्प m. (-र्पः) Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्श|प्रदर्शः
प्रदर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Look, appearance.<BR>	 2. Direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शक|प्रदर्शकः
प्रदर्शक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A teacher, an expounder.<BR>	 2. A prophet.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>दर्शक who shows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शन|प्रदर्शनं
प्रदर्शन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Shewing.<BR>	 2. Explaining generally, not exclusively.<BR>	 3.<BR>Explaining or specifying.<BR>	 4. An example.<BR>	 5. Prophesying.<BR>	 6.<BR>Look, aspect, appearance.<BR> E. प्र before, दृश् to see, causal v., ल्युट्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शित|प्रदर्शितः
प्रदर्शित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Mentioned, specified.<BR>	 2. Shewn.<BR>	 3. Prophesied.<BR>4. Taught.<BR> E. प्र before, दृश् to see, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदल|प्रदलः
प्रदल m. (-लः) An arrow.<BR> E. प्र before, दल् to tear, or the र of प्रदर<BR>changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदव|प्रदवः
प्रदव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Who or what annoys, distresses, &c.<BR>	 2. Burning,<BR>inflaming.<BR> E. दु to annoy, with प्र prefix, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदातृ
प्रदातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. A donor, who or what gives.<BR>	 2. One who<BR>gives a daughter in marriage.<BR>	 3. An epithet of Indra.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>दा to give, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदान|प्रदानं
प्रदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. Bestowing, granting.<BR>	 3. Instructing,<BR>teaching.<BR>	 4. Giving away in marriage.<BR>	 5. A goad.<BR> E. प्र before दा<BR>to give, or दो to cut, aff. ल्युट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदानक|प्रदानकं
प्रदानक n. (-कं) An offering, a donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदाय|प्रदायं
प्रदाय n. (-यं) A present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदि|प्रदिः
प्रदि m. (-दिः) A present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिग्ध|प्रदिग्धं
प्रदिग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं) Smeared, anointed.<BR>	 n. (-ग्धं) Fried<BR>ment.<BR>	 m. (-ग्धः) A kind of sauce or gravy.<BR> E. प्र before, दिग्ध<BR>smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिश्
प्रदिश् f. (-दिक्) Intermediate point of the compass, or half quarter,<BR>as north-east, south-west. &c.<BR>	 2. Direction, order, command.<BR> E. प्र<BR>implying division, and दिश् a point or quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिष्ट
प्रदिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Appointed, directed. E.<BR>	 2. Shown. प्र before,<BR>दिश् to show, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप|प्रदीपः
प्रदीप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A lamp.<BR>	 2. Elucidation, (at the end of titles of<BR>works.)<BR> E. प्र before, दीप् to shine, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपन|प्रदीपनः
प्रदीपन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Inflaming, illuminating.<BR>	 2. Stimulating,<BR>exciting, who or what does so.<BR>	 n. (-नं) The act of inflaming,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">Page488-a+ 60</a>]<BR>exciting, &c.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A sort of mineral poison, of a red colour,<BR>and caustic operation.<BR> E. प्र before, दीप् to inflame, aff. ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्त
प्रदीप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Kindled, illuminated.<BR>	 2. Shining, blazing,<BR>burning.<BR>	 3. Excited, stimulated, (as hunger).<BR> E. प्र before, दीप्<BR>to inflame, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदुष्ट
प्रदुष्ट f. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. Wicked, bad, Sinful.<BR>	 2. Wanton, licentious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदुह्
प्रदुह् mfn. (-धुक्) Who or what milks much or well.<BR> E. प्र before, दुह्<BR>to milk, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदूषित
प्रदूषित f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Spoiled, corrupted, vitiated.<BR>	 2. Polluted, defiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेय|प्रदेयः
प्रदेय n. (-यं) A gift.<BR> E. प्र before, देय to be given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेश|प्रदेशः
प्रदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A place in general, a country a district, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>foreign country, abroad.<BR>	 3. A short span, measured from the tip<BR>of the thumb to the end of the fore-finger.<BR>	 4. A wall.<BR>	 5. Decision,<BR>determination.<BR> E. प्र before, देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशन|प्रदेशनं
प्रदेशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A gift, a present, a bribe of offering, any thing given<BR>to the gods, to superiors, or friends, &c.<BR>	 2. Advice, instruction.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी) The fore-figner.<BR> E. प्र before, दिश् to show, aff. ल्युट्, fem. aff.<BR>ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशिनी
प्रदेशिनी f. (-नी) The fore-finger.<BR> E. प्र before, दिश् to show, aff. णिनि,<BR>fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेह|प्रदेहः
प्रदेह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Unguent, unction, a plaster.<BR>	 2. Applying a plaster.<BR>E. प्र before, दिह् to plaster, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोष|प्रदोषः
प्रदोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Evening, the first part of the night.<BR>	 2. Fault, offence.<BR>defect, transgression.<BR>	 3. A disordered condition.<BR> E. प्र implying<BR>commencement, &c. and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषतिमिर
प्रदोषतिमिर n. (-रं) The dusk of early night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोह|प्रदोहः
प्रदोह m. (-हः) Milking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्यु
प्रद्यु n. Adv. (-द्यु) Heavenly, holy, securing heaven.<BR> E. प्र before, द्यु for<BR>द्युस् heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युम्न|प्रद्युम्नः
प्रद्युम्न m. (-म्नः) KĀMA, the Hindu CUPID, reborn as the son of KṚṢṆA.<BR>by Rukmini. He was Stolen from the lying-in-chamber by Sam-<BR>bara when he was but six days old. Sambara cast him into the<BR>ocean when a large fish swallowed the child. The fish was caught<BR>by a fisherman and delivered to Sambara. When the fish was<BR>cut open his wife Māyābati found the beautiful boy alive and<BR>reared him up. When Pradyumna knew that Sambara had stolen<BR>him when a child he defied the demon to battle and killed him<BR>and went back to his father's house with Māyābati as his wife.<BR>E. प्र pre-eminent, द्युम्न power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युतित
प्रद्युतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Illuminated, irradiated.<BR> E. प्र before, द्यु to shine,<BR>क्त aff., and the vowel unchanged; also प्रद्योतित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योत|प्रद्योतः
प्रद्योत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A ray of light.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR>	 3. Lighting, illumin-<BR>ing.<BR>	 4. The name of a king of Ujjayinī but considered to be<BR>spurious by Mallinātha.<BR> E. प्र excess, and द्योत shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योतन|प्रद्योतनं|प्रद्योतनः
प्रद्योतन m. (-नः) The sun.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Blazing, shining, light.<BR> E. प्र excess,<BR>द्युत् to shine, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योतित
प्रद्योतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Illuminated, lighted.<BR> E. प्र. before, द्यु to shine,<BR>क्त aff; also प्रद्युतित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्राव|प्रद्रावः
प्रद्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Flight, retreat, running away.<BR>	 2. Going, going quick<BR>or well.<BR> E. प्र before, द्रु to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्राविन्
प्रद्राविन् mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि) Who retreats, flies, goes, &c.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>द्रु to go, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वार|प्रद्वारं
प्रद्वार n. (-रं) A place near a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्विष्
प्रद्विष् mfn. (-द्विट्) Who hates or dislikes, hostile, inimical.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>द्विष् to hate, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्विषत्
प्रद्विषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Hating, hostile, an enemy.<BR> E. प्र, and द्विषत a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वेष|प्रद्वेषः
प्रद्वेष m. (-षः) Dislike, aversion, hatred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वेष्टृ
प्रद्वेष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Who hates or dislikes.<BR> E. प्र before, द्विव् to hate, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध
प्रध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Who or what has or holds.<BR> E. प्र before, धा to have,<BR>श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधन|प्रधनं
प्रधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Tearing, rending, destroying.<BR>	 3. Spoil<BR>taken in battle.<BR> E. प्र before, धा to have, aff. क्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधमन|प्रधमनं
प्रधमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Blowing in or into.<BR>	 2. A sternutatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्ष|प्रधर्षः
प्रधर्ष m. (-र्षः) Assaulting, assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षित
प्रधर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Haughty, arrogant.<BR>	 2. Attacked.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>धृष् to be proud, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षितवत्
प्रधर्षितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Proud, arrogant.<BR> E. प्र before, धृष् to be<BR>proud, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधान|प्रधानं|प्रधानः
प्रधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Nature, the natural state of anything, or the cause of<BR>the material world.<BR>	 2. The SUPREME GOD.<BR>	 3. Intellect, understand-<BR>ing.<BR>	 4. Chief, principal, (in this sense, it is always neuter and<BR>confined to the singular number.)<BR>	 mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>	 1. The first com-<BR>panion of a king, his minister, his eunuch or confident, &c. a<BR>courtier, a noble, 2. An elephant-driver.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Prevalent, pre-<BR>dominant.<BR> E. प्र before, धा to have, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानतस्
प्रधानतस् Ind. According to eminence or superiority.<BR> E. प्रधान, and<BR>तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानता
प्रधानता f. (-ता) Excellence, superiority, supremacy.<BR> E. तल् added to<BR>प्रधान; also with त्व, प्रधानत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानधातु|प्रधानधातुः
प्रधानधातु m. (-तुः) Semen virile.<BR> E. प्रधान principal, and धातु radical part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानपुरुष|प्रधानपुरुषः
प्रधानपुरुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The most distinguished personage.<BR>	 2. An epithet<BR>of SĪVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानवृष्टि|प्रधानवृष्टिः
प्रधानवृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Heaviest rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानमन्त्रिन्|प्रधानमंत्रिन्
प्रधानमन्त्रिन् m. (-न्त्री) Prime minister.<BR> E. प्रधान, and मन्त्रिन् counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानाङ्ग|प्रधानांग
प्रधानाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) The chief member of the body, the chief person of a<BR>state, branch of a science, &c.<BR> E. प्रधान, and अङ्ग limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानामात्य|प्रधानामात्यः
प्रधानामात्य m. (-त्यः) Prime minister.<BR> E. प्रधान, and अमात्य minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानोत्तम
प्रधानोत्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Warlike, brave.<BR>	 2. Eminent, illustrious.<BR>E. प्रधान, and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधावन|प्रधावनः
प्रधावन m. (-नः) Air, wind.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Rubbing, rubbing off, washing off.<BR>E. प्र violently, धु to shake, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधि|प्रधिः
प्रधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. The periphery of a wheel.<BR>	 2. A well.<BR> E. प्र principal, धा<BR>to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधिमण्डल
प्रधिमण्डल n. (-लं) The circumference of a wheel.<BR> E. प्रधि, मण्डल a<BR>circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधी
प्रधी Adj. Pre-eminently intelligent.<BR>	 f. (-धी) Great intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधूपित
प्रधूपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Heated, burned.<BR>	 2. Lighted, inflamed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Afflicted.<BR>	 4. Excited.<BR>	 5. Perfumed, fumigated.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A woman<BR>in trouble or affliction.<BR>	 2. The quarter to which the sun is proceed-<BR>ing.<BR> E. प्र before, धूप् to heat, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधृष्ट
प्रधृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Proud, arrogant.<BR>	 2. Treated with contumely.<BR>E. प्र before, धृष् to be proud, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्यान|प्रध्यानं
प्रध्यान n. (-नं) Deep thought, reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंस|प्रध्वंसः
प्रध्वंस m. (-सः) Destruction, loss.<BR> E. प्र entirely, ध्वंस loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंसाभाव|प्रध्वंसाभावः
प्रध्वंसाभाव m. (-वः) Nonexistence on account of annihilation, non-exis-<BR>tence of anything which existed before, (in logic.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंसिन्
प्रध्वंसिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Destroying, annihilating.<BR> E. प्र before, ध्वंस्<BR>to destroy, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वनयत्
प्रध्वनयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Causing to sound.<BR> E. प्र before, ध्वन् to sound,<BR>causal v, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वस्त
प्रध्वस्त f. (-स्ता) Annihilated, destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्मा
प्रध्मा mfn. (-ध्माः-ध्माः-ध्म) Blowing violently.<BR> E. प्र before, ध्मा to blow, aff. विच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्रुह्
प्रध्रुह् mfn. (-क्)<BR>	 1. Injurious, doing wrong or violence to.<BR>	 2. Rebel-<BR>lious, refractory.<BR> E. प्र before, द्रुह् to seek to hurt, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनर्त्तित|प्रनर्तित
प्रनर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, agitated, set in motion.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>नृत् to dance, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनप्तृ
प्रनप्तृ m. (-तृः) A great grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनष्ट|प्रनष्टः
प्रनष्ट f. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. Lost.<BR>	 2. Disappeared, vanished.<BR>	 3. Perished, ruined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रना
प्रना(ण)ल mf. (-लः-ली) A water-course, a canal.<BR> E. प्र before, नल् to go,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनिधातन
प्रनिधातन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. प्र and नि before, हन् to kill or<BR>hurt, ल्युट् aff., and the radical letters changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनृत्त
प्रनृत्त f. (-त्ता) Dancing.<BR>	 n. (-त्तं) A dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपक्ष|प्रपक्षः
प्रपक्ष m. (-क्षः) The extremity of a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्च|प्रपंच|प्रपंचः|प्रपञ्चः
प्रपञ्च m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>	 1. Reverse, opposition, reversion or inversion.<BR>	 2. Extent,<BR>expanse.<BR>	 3. Heap, abundance, quantity.<BR>	 4. Delusion, deceit, trick<BR>or fraud.<BR>	 5. Joke, jest.<BR>	 6. Prolixity, copiousness, in style or com-<BR>position.<BR>	 7. Error, illusion, 8. The world, considered as the<BR>expansion of the primary germ and as the scene of manifold action.<BR>9. Elucidation, explanation.<BR>	 10. Phenomenon, appearance.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, षचि to spread, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चन|प्रपंचन|प्रपंचनं
प्रपञ्चन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Diffusion.<BR>	 2. Explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चबुद्धि|प्रपंचबुद्धि
प्रपञ्चबुद्धि Adj. Cunning, artful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चवचन|प्रपंचवचन
प्रपञ्चवचन n. (-नं) Prolix discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपञ्चित|प्रपंचित|प्रपञ्चितं
प्रपञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Expanded, diffused.<BR>	 2. Erring, mistaken.<BR>	 3.<BR>Tricked, deceived, beguiled.<BR>	 4. Declared fully, explained, treated<BR>at length.<BR> E. प्रपञ्च prolixity, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रप्रतन
प्रप्रतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Death dying.<BR>	 2. Destruction.<BR>	 3. Falling.<BR>	 4. Alighting.<BR>5. Flying forth.<BR>	 6. A precipice, a rock.<BR> E. प्र before, पत् to fall,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपतित
प्रपतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dead.<BR>	 2. Decayed.<BR>	 3. Fallen.<BR>	 4. Come down.<BR>E. प्र before, पत् to fall, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपथ|प्रपथः
प्रपथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Languid, enervated, relaxed.<BR> E. प्र before, पथ् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपद|प्रपदं
प्रपद n. (-दं) The point of the foot, the tip of the toes.<BR> E. प्र projecting<BR>and पद the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपदीन
प्रपदीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Relating to the top of the foot, extending to it,<BR>fitting it, &c.<BR> E. प्रपद, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपन्न|प्रपन्नः
प्रपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Taking refuge with.<BR>	 2. Reaching, arriving at.<BR>	 3.<BR>Seeking, adhering to.<BR>	 4. Effecting, producing.<BR>	 5. Promised, assent-<BR>ed to.<BR>	 6. Attained, obtained, possessed of.<BR>	 7. Poor.<BR>	 8. Distressed.<BR>E. प्र before, पद् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपन्नाड|प्रपन्नाडः
प्रपन्नाड m. (-डः) The chakramarda tree. “दाद्मर्द्दन इति भाषा” See प्रपुन्नाड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपर्ण
प्रपर्ण m. (-र्णः) A fallen leaf.<BR> E. प्र before, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायन|प्रपलायनं
प्रपलायन n. (-नं) Flight, running away.<BR> E. प्र before, पलायन flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायित
प्रपलायित mfn. (-तः-ता-त) Routed, defeated.<BR> E. प्र before, पलायित<BR>the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायिन्
प्रपलायिन् m. (-यी) A fugitive, one who deserts his cause.<BR> E. प्र before, पलायिन् who flies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपवण
प्रपवण n. (-णं) Purifying.<BR> E. प्र before, पु to purify, ल्युट् aff., the ण being<BR>optionally changed, whence also प्रपवन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपवणीय
प्रपवणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be purified or cleansed.<BR> E. प्र before, पु to<BR>purify, अनीयर् aff.; also प्रपवनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपश्यत्
प्रपश्यत् mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्)<BR>	 1. Foreseeing.<BR> E. प्र, and पश्यत् seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपा
प्रपा f. (-पा)<BR>	 1. A place where water is distributed.<BR>	 2. A supply of water,<BR>3. A Plan for watering cattle.<BR>	 4. A well, a cistern.<BR> E. प्र before, पा<BR>to drink, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाठक|प्रपाठकः
प्रपाठक m. (-कः) A chapter or subdivision of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाणि|प्रपाणिः
प्रपाणि m. (-णिः) The palm of the hand.<BR> E. प्र prostrate, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाणीय
प्रपाणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Drinkable.<BR> E. प्र before, पा to drink, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपात|प्रपातः
प्रपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A cliff, a precipice.<BR>	 2. A cascade or water fall.<BR>	 3. A<BR>bank, a shore.<BR>	 4. Facing an enemy.<BR>	 5. Going away, departure.<BR>	 6.<BR>Falling down, a fall.<BR>	 7. A sudden attack.<BR>	 8. Throwing oneself<BR>down from a rock.<BR>	 9. Emission, discharge.<BR> E. प्र before, पत् to des-<BR>cend, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाथ|प्रपाथः
प्रपाथ m. (-थः) A road,<BR> E. प्र before, पथ् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपादिक|प्रपादिकः
प्रपादिक m. (-कः) A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपानक|प्रपानकं
प्रपानक n. (-कं) A kind of drink or beverage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपायिन्
प्रपायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिणी-यि)<BR>	 1. Who or what drinks.<BR>	 2. Who or what<BR>protects.<BR> E. प्र before, पा to drink, &c. घिनुण् aff. and आय inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपावन|प्रपावनं
प्रपावन n. (-नं) A cool grove, a pleasure garden.<BR> E. प्रपा a place of refresh-<BR>ment, and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपितामह|प्रपितामहः
प्रपितामह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A paternal great grandfather.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 f. (-ही) A paternal great grandmother.<BR> E. प्र preceding,<BR>पितामह a grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपितृव्य|प्रपितृव्यः
प्रपितृव्य m. (-व्यः) A paternal grand uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपित्सु
प्रपित्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु) Wishing or intending to descend, alight, fall,<BR>&c.<BR> E. प्र before, पत् to go, desid, v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपीडन|प्रपीडनं
प्रपीडन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pressing, squeezing.<BR>	 2. An astringent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपीत
प्रपीत(न) f. (-ता or -ना) Adj. Swollen, extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुनाड|प्रपुनाडः
प्रपुनाड m. (-डः) A sort of Cassia, (C. tora,): see प्रपुन्नाड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्नड|प्रपुंनड|प्रपुन्नडः
प्रपुन्नड m. (-डः) Cassia tora: see प्रपुन्नाड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्ना
प्रपुन्ना f. (-न्ना) A sort of grass, (Hedysarum alhaji.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्नाड|प्रपुंनाड|प्रपुन्नाडः
प्रपुन्नाड(ट) m. (-डः or टः) A tree, (Cassia tora.)<BR> E. प्र excellently, पुमस्<BR>mankind, and णल् to smell, aff. अण्, the स of पुमस् is rejected,<BR>and the ल of the radical changed optionally to ड or ट; the anti-<BR>penultimate is occasionally short, and one of the conjunct न is<BR>sometimes rejected; whence the word is variously written, प्रपुन्नाल,<BR>or प्रपुन्नड, or प्रपुनाड, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्नाल|प्रपुंनाल|प्रपुन्नालः
प्रपुन्नाल m. (-लः) Cassia tora: see the last. “चाकुन्दा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरण|प्रपूरणं
प्रपूरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The drawing out of a bow string for the purpose of<BR>shooting.<BR>	 2. Inserting, injecting.<BR>	 3. Filling, filling up.<BR>	 4. Satisfy-<BR>ing, satiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरिका
प्रपूरिका f. (-का) A prickly nightshade, (Solanum Jacquini.) “कण्टकार्य्याम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपृष्ठ
प्रपृष्ठ f. (-ष्ठा) Adj. Having a prominent back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपौण्डरीक|प्रपौण्डरीकं|प्रपौण्डरीकः
प्रपौण्डरीक m. (-कः) A small herbaceous plant, used in medicine as<BR>a perfume, commonly Punderya; in medicine it forms the basis of<BR>applications to ulcers, and bad eyes.<BR> E. प्र excellent, पुण्डरीक the<BR>same, and अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपौत्र|प्रपौत्रः
प्रपौत्र m. (-त्रः) A great grandson.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A great grand-daughter.<BR> E. प्र<BR>preceding, पौत्र a son's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रप्यान
प्रप्यान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fat, bulky.<BR> E. प्र before, प्याय् to be fat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्त
प्रफुल्त f. (-ल्ता) See the next.<BR> E. प्र + फल्-क्त आदित्वात् इटोऽभावे अत इत्त्वम् ।<BR>प्र + फुल्ल-विकाशे अच् वा (लद्वययुतः) Mallināth reads प्रफुल्लम् and notices<BR>the variant of this word in his commentary on Raghubansha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्ल|प्रफुल्लः
प्रफुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>	 1. Blown, as flower.<BR>	 2. Smiling.<BR>	 3. Shining.<BR>	 4.<BR>Glad, pleased.<BR> E. प्र before, फुल्ल flowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्लनयन
प्रफुल्लनयन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having full or sparkling eyes.<BR> E. प्रफुल्ल, नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्लवदन
प्रफुल्लवदन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having a cheerful or smiling countenance,<BR>looking gay or happy.<BR> E. प्रफुल्ल, and वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबद्ध
प्रबद्ध Adj.<BR>	 f. (-द्धा)<BR>	 1. Bound, fastened.<BR>	 2. Suppressed, checked, stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबद्धृ
प्रबद्धृ m. (-द्धृः) An author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्ध|प्रबंध|प्रबंधः|प्रबन्धः
प्रबन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Continuous application or action, continuance, unin-<BR>terruptedness.<BR>	 2. A connected discussion.<BR>	 3. A tie, a bond.<BR>	 4. A<BR>literary composition, particularly a poetical one.<BR> E. प्र before, बधि<BR>to bind, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्धकल्पना|प्रबंधकल्पना
प्रबन्धकल्पना f. (-ना) A feigned story, a work of imagination, whether<BR>founded on fact or not.<BR> E. प्रबन्ध a connected narrative, and कल्पना a<BR>making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबन्धन|प्रबंधन|प्रबंधनं
प्रबन्धन n. (-नं) Bond, tie.<BR> E. प्र + बन्ध्-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबभ्र|प्रबभ्रः
प्रबभ्र m. (-भ्रः) An epithet of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रब
प्रब(व)र्ह f. (-र्हा) Adj. Most excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबल|प्रबलः
प्रबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Strong, powerful.<BR>	 2. Important.<BR>	 3. Violent.<BR>4. Dangerous.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A sprout, a shoot.<BR> E. प्र before, बल् to be<BR>strong, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रब
प्रब(व)ल्हिका f. (-काः) See प्रहेलिक्रा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाधन|प्रबाधनं
प्रबाधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Oppressing, tormenting.<BR>	 2. Refusing, denying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाधमान
प्रबाधमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Paining, afflicting, tormenting.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>बाध् to pain, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाल|प्रबालं|प्रबालः
प्रबाल mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. Coral.<BR>	 2. A shoot, a sprout, a new leaf.<BR>	 3. The<BR>neck of a lute, m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. An animal.<BR>	 2. A pupil.<BR> E. प्र before, बल<BR>to be strong, and aff. घञ्; also प्रबालक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालफल|प्रबालफलं
प्रबालफल n. (-लं) Red sandal wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालाश्मन्तक|प्रबालाश्मंतक|प्रबालाश्मन्तकः
प्रबालाश्मन्तक m. (-कः) The red Asmantaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालवत्|प्रबालवन्त्
प्रबालवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having new leaves or shoots.<BR> E. प्रबाल, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालिक|प्रबालिकः
प्रबालिक m. (-कः) “जीवशाके” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाहु|प्रबाहुः
प्रबाहु m. (-हुः) The forearm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाहुकम्
प्रबाहुकम् Ind.<BR>	 1. On high.<BR>	 2. At the same time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबुद्ध|प्रबुद्धः
प्रबुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Wise, learned.<BR>	 2. Blown, expanded.<BR>	 3. Wake-<BR>ned, awake, roused.<BR>	 4. Beginning to take effect.<BR> E. प्र before, बुध्<BR>to be wise, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोध|प्रबोधः
प्रबोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Vigilance, wakefulness, active or vigilant state of<BR>being.<BR>	 2. Intellect, understanding.<BR>	 3. Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>	 4.<BR>Sense, consciousness.<BR>	 5. Awaking either from ignorance or sleep.<BR>	 5.<BR>Blowing, (as of a flower.)<BR>	 6. Consolation.<BR>	 7. Reviving the frag-<BR>rance of a perfume.<BR> E. प्र before, बुध् to understand, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधन|प्रबोधनं
प्रबोधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Awaking, arousing, exciting, reviving.<BR>	 2. Instruc-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>	 4. Reviving the fragrance of a per-<BR>fume, which had lost its scent.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The lunation on which<BR>VIṢṆU is supposed to wake from his sleep, the eleventh of the<BR>light half of Kārtika; also प्रबोधिनी.<BR> E. प्र before, बुध् to know or<BR>understand, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधित
प्रबोधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Aroused, awakened.<BR>	 2. Instructed.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, बुध् to know, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधिता
प्रबोधिता f. (-ता) A species of the Atijagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभङ्ग|प्रभंगः|प्रभङ्गः
प्रभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Breaking down, destroying.<BR> E. प्र before, भञ्ज to break, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभञ्जन|प्रभंजन|प्रभंजनं|प्रभञ्जनः
प्रभञ्जन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Breaking, destroying.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Air or wind.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, भञ्ज् to break, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभद्र|प्रभद्रः
प्रभद्र m. (-द्रः) The Nimba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभव|प्रभवः
प्रभव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. Superior, powerful.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Generative cause, the basis or root of being or existence.<BR>	 2. The<BR>operative cause, or immediate origin of being, as the father or<BR>mother, &c.<BR>	 3. The place of receiving existence, or where an<BR>object is first perceived, as हिमवान् गङ्गाप्रभवः the Himavāna moun-<BR>tain, (is) the place where Gangā is first seen.<BR>	 4. Birth, production.<BR>5. The basis or origin of water. i. e. “Light.” 6. The name of a<BR>Muni.<BR>	 7. Strength, superiority, power.<BR>	 8. The Creator.<BR> E. प्र supe-<BR>riority or manifestation, and भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवन|प्रभवनं
प्रभवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Being born or produced.<BR>	 2. Ruling, presiding.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, भू to be, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभविष्णु|प्रभविष्णुः
प्रभविष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Mighty, potent.<BR>	 2. Born completely or<BR>well.<BR>	 3. An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR> E. प्र before, भू to be, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभविष्णुता
प्रभविष्णुता f. (-ता) Consequence, importance, power, authority, supre-<BR>macy.<BR> E. प्र before, भू to be, इष्णुच् aff. and तल् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभव्य
प्रभव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be born or produced.<BR>	 2. Fit for rule. E.<BR>प्र before, भू to be, aff. क्यप्; also प्रभवनीय and प्रभवितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभा
प्रभा f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. Light, radiance.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR>	 3. The city of<BR>KUVERA.<BR>	 4. One of the wives of the sun.<BR>	 5. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>6. A name of an Apsarā.<BR> E. प्र exceeding, भा to shine, affs. अङ्<BR>and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाकर|प्रभाकरः
प्रभाकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR>	 4. The ocean.<BR>	 5.<BR>An epithet of Śiva.<BR>	 6. Name of a learned author, the founder of<BR>that school of the Mimānsā philosophy which goes by his name.<BR>E. प्रभा light, and कर what makes. “कुशद्वीपस्थे वर्षभेदेः अष्टममन्वन्तरे च” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाकीट|प्रभाकीटः
प्रभाकीट m. (-टः) The fire-fly.<BR> E. प्रभा light, कीट insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाग|प्रभागः
प्रभाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Division.<BR>	 2. The fraction of a fraction, (in Math.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाज्
प्रभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Who or what shares or divides.<BR> E. प्र before, भज्<BR>to divide, and ण्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाञ्जन|प्रभाञ्जनः
प्रभाञ्जन m. (-नः) A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR> E. प्रभा light, beauty,<BR>अञ्ज् to go, aff. ल्युट् । “शोभाञ्जने” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभात|प्रभातं
प्रभात n. (-तं) Morning, dawn, daybreak.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Begun to become<BR>light.<BR> E. प्र before, भा to shine, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभातरल
प्रभातरल Adj. Tremulously radient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभान|प्रभानं
प्रभान n. (-नं) Light, radiance, shining.<BR> E. प्र before, भा to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभानीय
प्रभानीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be irradiated or lighted.<BR> E. प्र before, भि<BR>to shine, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभामण्डल|प्रभामंडल
प्रभामण्डल n. (-लं) A circle of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभालेपिन्
प्रभालेपिन् Adj. Covered with splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाव|प्रभावः
प्रभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Majesty, dignity, magnanimity, glory, high-spirit.<BR>2. Power, strength.<BR>	 3. Spirit.<BR>	 4. Tranquillizing, conciliation.<BR>	 5.<BR>Splendour, brilliance.<BR>	 6. Miraculous or superhuman power.<BR> E. प्र<BR>pre-eminence, भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावज|प्रभावजः
प्रभावज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Proceeding from conscious majesty or power.<BR>E. प्रभाव, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावत्|प्रभावन्त्
प्रभावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Luminous, radiant, splendid.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The<BR>mother of MALLI the 19th of the Jinas or Jaina saints.<BR>	 2. The<BR>lute of one of the demi-gods attendant on SĪVA or other principal<BR>deities.<BR>	 3. A form of poetical metre.<BR> E. प्रभा light or splendour,<BR>and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाषण|प्रभाषणं
प्रभाषण n. (-णं) Explanation, interpretation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभास|प्रभासः
प्रभास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A place of pilgrimage near DWĀRAKĀ in the<BR>west of India.<BR>	 2. One of the eight VASUS.<BR>	 3. One of the Gaṇād-<BR>hipas of the Jainas.<BR>	 4. Splendour, beauty.<BR> E. प्र before, भास् to<BR>shine, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभासन|प्रभासनं
प्रभासन n. (-नं) Illumining, brightening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिन्न|प्रभिन्नः
प्रभिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Well cut or detached.<BR>	 2. Severed, separated.<BR>3. Budded, opened, expanded.<BR>	 4. Altered, changed, deformed.<BR>	 5.<BR>Loosened.<BR>	 m. (-न्नः) A furious elephant, one in rut, or from whose<BR>temples the juice is exuding.<BR> E. प्र much, भिन्न broken, or seized<BR>with fury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिन्नाञ्जन|प्रभिन्नांजन
प्रभिन्नाञ्जन n. (-नं) A kind of collyrium mixed with oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभु|प्रभुः
प्रभु mfn. (-भुः-भ्वी-भु)<BR>	 1. Strong, able, (generally with an inf.)<BR>	 2. Always,<BR>eternal.<BR>	 3. A superior, an owner, a proprietor, a master or mistresss,<BR>&c.<BR>	 4. A match for, (with a dat.)<BR>	 m. (-भुः)<BR>	 1. A master, a lord.<BR>2. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. Quick silver.<BR>	 4. Sound.<BR> E. प्र pre-emi-<BR>nent, भू to be, aff. क्विप् and the final vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुता
प्रभुता f. (-ता) Greatness, power, supremacy, lordship or sovereignty.<BR>E. प्रभु master, aff. तल्; also with त्व aff. प्रभुत्व n. (-त्वं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुभक्त|प्रभुभक्तः
प्रभुभक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Faithful, devoted.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) A good horse. E.<BR>प्रभु a master and भक्त worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुभक्ति|प्रभुभक्तिः
प्रभुभक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Attachment to a lord, faithfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूत|प्रभूतं
प्रभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Much, abundant.<BR>	 2. Gone up or upwards.<BR>	 3.<BR>Been, become, produced.<BR>	 4. High, Lofty.<BR>	 5. Goverened, presided<BR>over.<BR>	 6. Mature, perfect.<BR> E. प्र principal, &c. भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतता
प्रभूतता f. (-ता) Abundance, plenty.<BR> E. तल् added to the last;<BR>also प्रभूतत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतवयस्
प्रभूतवयस् Adj. Advanced in years, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूति|प्रभूतिः
प्रभूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Source, origin.<BR>	 2. Power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूष्णु|प्रभूष्णुः
प्रभूष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Strong, able.<BR> E. प्र before, भू to be, aff. ष्णुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभृति|प्रभृतिः
प्रभृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Beginning, commencement, (in this sense the word gene-<BR>rally occurs as the last member of a Bahubrihi compound).<BR>	 2. Man-<BR>ner, kind.<BR>	 3. Etcetera, others, rest, remainder, (in composition;)<BR>as गर्म्मुत्प्रभृतयः तृणं the grass called Germut and other sorts. मुनयः<BR>सोमश्रवः प्रभृतयः the Munis, Somasravas, and the rest; ततः प्रभृति<BR>thence, after. Ind. Beginning with, from, since, (with an abl.)<BR>as “अद्य प्रभृति”.<BR> E. प्र before, भृ to nourish, aff. क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेद|प्रभेदः
प्रभेद m. (-दः) Kind, sort, difference.<BR>	 2. Splitting, opening.<BR>	 3. The<BR>flowing of ichor from the temples of an elephant.<BR> E. प्र before, भेद<BR>kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रश्यमान
प्रभ्रश्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Falling down, being broken off or down.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, भ्रंश् to break, pass. v., शानच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशथु|प्रभ्रंशथुः
प्रभ्रंशथु m. (-थुः) A particular disease of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्ट
प्रभ्रष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, dropping, fallen off.<BR>	 2. Broken.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं)<BR>A chaplet of flowers suspended from the lock on the head,: see<BR>the next.<BR> E. प्र before, भ्रंश् to fall, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्टक|प्रभ्रष्टकं
प्रभ्रष्टक n. (-कं) A chaplet of flowers suspended from the middle lock<BR>of hair.<BR> E. प्र before, भ्रंश् to fall or depend, aff. क्त and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमग्न
प्रमग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Immersed, drowned.<BR> E. प्र and मग्न plunged in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमङ्गन
प्रमङ्गन n. (-नं) Going, proceeding.<BR> E. प्र before, मगि to go, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमङ्गित
प्रमङ्गित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone, proceeded.<BR> E. प्र before, मगि to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमण
प्रमण(न)स् mfn. (णाः-णाः-णः) Joyful, cheerful.<BR> E. प्र implying pleasure,<BR>sure, मनस् the mind; also प्रमनस्; the ण being optionally changed<BR>to न ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत
प्रमत f. (-ता) Adj. Thought out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्त|प्रमत्तः
प्रमत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Careless, negligent, (usually with a loc).<BR>	 2.<BR>Blundering, a blunderer.<BR>	 3. Intoxicated.<BR>	 4. Insane.<BR>	 5. Swerving<BR>from, (with an abl. as in स्वाधिकारात्प्रमत्तः)<BR>	 6. Wanton, lascivious.<BR>E. प्र before, मत्त mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्तगीत
प्रमत्तगीत Adj. Sung carelessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्तचित्त
प्रमत्तचित्त Adj. Negligent, careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथ|प्रमथः
प्रमथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. An attendant on ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR>	 f. (-था)<BR>	 1. Yellow<BR>myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.) “हरितक्याम्”.<BR>	 2. Pain, affliction.<BR>E. प्र excess, मथि to churn, (the enemies of ŚIVA,) aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथन|प्रमथनं
प्रमथन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Paining, distressing.<BR>	 3. Agitat-<BR>ing, churning.<BR> E. प्र before, मथि to churn, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथाधिप|प्रमथाधिपः
प्रमथाधिप m. (-पः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. प्रमथ a follower of ŚIVA, and अधिप master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथालय|प्रमथालयः
प्रमथालय n. (-यं) Hell.<BR> E. प्रमथ pain, and आलय an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथित|प्रमथितं
प्रमथित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well-churned.<BR>	 2. Pained, distressed.<BR>	 3. Tram-<BR>pled down.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Butter-milk without water.<BR> E. प्र before, मथि to<BR>churn, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद|प्रमदः
प्रमद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Mad, intoxicated, figuratively with passion or<BR>literally with liquor.<BR>	 2. Violent.<BR>	 3. Careless.<BR>	 4. Impassioned.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-दः)<BR>	 1. Joy, pleasure, delight, rapture.<BR>	 2. Dhuturā, (D. metel.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-दा) A woman, a handsome woman.<BR> E. प्र before, मद् mad, drunk,<BR>aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदकानन|प्रमदकाननं
प्रमदकानन n. (-नं) A royal garden or pleasure ground for the wives of a<BR>king.<BR> E. प्रमद pleasure, and कानन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदन|प्रमदनं
प्रमदन n. (-नं) Amorous desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदवन|प्रमदवनं
प्रमदवन n. (-नं) A royal garden or pleasure ground attached to the<BR>Haram.<BR> E. प्रमद pleasure and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदा
प्रमदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. A young handsome woman.<BR>	 2. A woman in general.<BR>	 3.<BR>The sign VIRGO of the Zodiac.<BR> E. प्र + मद्-अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदाकानन|प्रमदाकाननं
प्रमदाकानन n. (-नं) A royal garden.<BR> E. प्रमदा a woman, and कानन a wood;<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदावन|प्रमदावनं
प्रमदावन n. (-नं) A royal garden or pleasure ground attached especially<BR>to the private apartments of the palace.<BR> E. प्रमदा a woman and वन<BR>a grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद्वर
प्रमद्वर f. (-रा) Adj. Careless, inattentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन
प्रमन(ण)स् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Happy, delighted.<BR> E. प्र implying pleasure, मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्यु
प्रमन्यु mfn. (-न्युः-न्युः-न्यु)<BR>	 1. Distressed, sorrowful.<BR>	 2. Enraged, incensed.<BR>E. प्र, and मन्यु grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमय|प्रमयः
प्रमय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Death.<BR>	 2. Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. प्र before, मी to injure, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमर्दन|प्रमर्दनं|प्रमर्दनः
प्रमर्दन n. (-नं) Crushing, destroying.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमा
प्रमा f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. True knowledge, or knowledge exempt from all error,<BR>(in logic.)<BR>	 2. Consciousness, perception.<BR> E. प्र before, मा to mete<BR>or measure, affs. अङ् and टाप्; that by which every object is<BR>measured or estimated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाण|प्रमाणं|प्रमाणः
प्रमाण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Cause, motive.<BR>	 2. Limit.<BR>	 3. Proof, testimony, authority.<BR>4. A scripture, a work of sacred authority.<BR>	 5. Measure, (whether<BR>of weight, length or capacity.)<BR>	 6. Magnitude, extent.<BR>	 7. Standard,<BR>authority.<BR>	 8. Correct knowledge, accurate perception, (in logic.)<BR>	 9.<BR>Unity.<BR>	 10. Quantity.<BR>	 11. A speaker of the truth.<BR>	 12. Always, eter-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">Page491-b+ 60</a>]<BR>nal.<BR>	 13. A title of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 14. Principal, capital.<BR> E. प्र before, मा to<BR>measure, aff. ल्युट्; that by which all is measured; this word is gener-<BR>ally restricted to the singular number, as वेदाः प्रमाणं the Vedas<BR>are the authority; it is also confined to the neuter gender, as पुत्त्रः<BR>प्रमाणं the boy is a witness; some exceptions occur however, as प्रमाणः<BR>पुरुषः, प्रमाणा स्त्री the man witness, the woman witness; and in the<BR>following rule, प्रत्यक्षानुमानोपमानशब्दाः प्रमाणानि perception, inference,<BR>comparison, and sound, are proofs. According to the Naiyāyikas<BR>अनुपलब्धि or non-perception and अर्थापत्ति or the inference from cir-<BR>cumstances of the Mimānsakas being exempted by them; the<BR>Sānkhys recognize प्रत्थक्ष, अनुमान and शब्द only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणज्ञ|प्रमाणज्ञः
प्रमाणज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. An epithet of Sīva.<BR>	 2. A logician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणतस्
प्रमाणतस् Ind.<BR>	 1. According to proof or authority.<BR>	 2. Agreeably to mea-<BR>sure, to weight, &c.<BR> E. प्रमाण, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणदृष्ट
प्रमाणदृष्ट Adj. Recognized by authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणशास्त्र
प्रमाणशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) Logic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणमूत्र
प्रमाणमूत्र n. (-त्रं) A measuring cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणपुरुषः|प्रमाणपुरुष
प्रमाणपुरुषः m. (-षः) An umpire, an arbitrator, a judge.<BR> E. प्रमाण, and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणयत्
प्रमाणयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Receiving, admitting, or obeying, &c. as<BR>authority.<BR> E. प्रमाण nominal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणान्तर|प्रमाणांतर
प्रमाणान्तर n. (-रं) Another means of proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणाभाव|प्रमाणाभावः
प्रमाणाभाव m. (-वः) Want or absence of proof or authority.<BR> E. प्रमाण,<BR>and अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणिक
प्रमाणिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Forming an authority.<BR>	 2. A measure of<BR>length considered from the elbow to the top of the middle<BR>finger.<BR>	 f. (-का) A species of the Anushtubh metre.<BR> E. प्रमाण and<BR>टन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणीकरण
प्रमाणीकरण n. (-णं) Establishing or admitting as authority or proof.<BR>E. प्रमाण, and करण making, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणीकृत
प्रमाणीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Admitted or established as proof or authority.<BR>E. प्रमाण, and कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणीभूत
प्रमाणीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Proving, establishing.<BR> E. प्रमाण, भूत become, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातामह|प्रमातामहः
प्रमातामह m. (-हः) A maternal great grandfather.<BR>	 f. (-ही) A maternal<BR>great grandmother.<BR> E. प्र before, मातामह a grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातृ
प्रमातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Proving, evidence, who or what is proof or authori-<BR>ty.<BR> E. प्र before, मा to measure, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथ|प्रमाथः
प्रमाथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Killing.<BR>	 2. Paining, afflicting, torturing.<BR>	 3. Violence.<BR>E. प्र before, मथि to churn, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथिन्
प्रमाथिन् mfn. (थी-थिनी-थि)<BR>	 1. Afflicting, inflicting pain or sorrow.<BR>	 2.<BR>Killing, destroying.<BR>	 3. Breaking, cutting.<BR>	 4. Striking down.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, मथि to churn, to grind, to pain, and घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाद|प्रमादः
प्रमाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Inadvertence, carelessness, error, inaccuracy, a<BR>blunder.<BR>	 3. Intoxication.<BR>	 4. Insanity.<BR> E. प्र before, मद् to be mad,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादवत्|प्रमादवन्त्
प्रमादवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Heedless, careless, incautious, inconsi-<BR>derate, unreflecting.<BR>	 2. Insane.<BR>	 3. Intoxicated.<BR> E. प्रमाद careless-<BR>ness, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिका
प्रमादिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An imprudent or careless woman.<BR>	 2. A deflowered<BR>girl.<BR> E. प्र before. मद् to be careless, ण्वुल् aff. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिन्
प्रमादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Careless, indifferent.<BR>	 2. Insane.<BR>	 3. In-<BR>toxicated.<BR> E. प्र before, मद् to be inebriate, and घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाद्य
प्रमाद्य n. (-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Carelessness.<BR>	 2. Insanity.<BR> E. प्र before, मद् to be mad,<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाद्यतस्
प्रमाद्यतस् Ind. From carelessness.<BR> E. प्रमाद्य, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापण|प्रमापणं
प्रमापण n. (-णं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. प्र before, मीञ् to hurt or kill, पुक्<BR>augment, from its taking the causal form, and ल्युट् aff.; the न of<BR>the affix also being unchanged, the word is written प्रमापन n. (-नं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापिन्
प्रमापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Killing, destroying.<BR> E. प्र before, मी to kill,<BR>causal v., णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमार्जन|प्रमार्जनं
प्रमार्जन n. (-नं) Rubbling off, wiping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमित|प्रमितः
प्रमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, understood.<BR>	 2. Established, proved.<BR>3. Measured.<BR>	 4. Limited, few.<BR> E. प्र before, मा to measure, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिताक्षरा
प्रमिताक्षरा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A species of Jagatī metre.<BR>	 2. The name of the<BR>commentary on Muhurta chintāmani.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिति|प्रमितिः
प्रमिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. True knowledge derived from senses, inference, an-<BR>alogy or information.<BR>	 2. Measuring.<BR> E. प्र before, मा to measure,<BR>(by which,) क्तिन् aff., and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीठ
प्रमीठ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Thick.<BR>	 2. Passed, passed as urine.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>मिह् to sprinkle, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीणत्
प्रमीणत् mfn. (-णन्-णन्ती-णत्)<BR>	 1. Overcoming, subduing.<BR>	 2. Injuring, kill-<BR>ing.<BR> E. प्र before, मी to hurt or kill, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीत|प्रमीतः
प्रमीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dead, deceased.<BR>	 2. An animal killed at a<BR>sacrifice.<BR> E. प्र before, मी to hurt or kill, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीति|प्रमीतिः
प्रमीति f. (-तिः) Death, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीला
प्रमीला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Lassitude, enervation, exhaustion from indolence or<BR>fatigue.<BR>	 2. The name of the sovereign of the kingdom of women.<BR>She was conquered by Arjūna and become his wife.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>मील् to twinkle, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीलित
प्रमीलित f. (-ता) With closed eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसुक्त
प्रसुक्त f. (-क्ता)<BR>	 1. Set free, liberated.<BR>	 2. Resigned, renounced.<BR>	 3. Cast, hurled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुक्तकण्ठम्|प्रमुक्तकंठम्
प्रमुक्तकण्ठम् Ind. Bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुख|प्रमुखं|प्रमुखः
प्रमुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>	 1. Chief, principal.<BR>	 2. Best, most excellent.<BR>	 3.<BR>First.<BR>	 m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A chief, a sage, any respectable man.<BR>	 2. A heap,<BR>a multitude.<BR>	 3. A tree used in dying, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>	 n. (-खं)<BR>1. Time being, the present.<BR>	 2. The mouth.<BR>	 3. Beginning of a chap-<BR>ter or section.<BR>	 f. (-खा) Facing.<BR> E. प्र before, मुख the face, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुखतस्
प्रमुखतस् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of:--“In the pre-<BR>sence of” “In front of”: also प्रमुखे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुखत्व
प्रमुखत्व n. (-त्वं) Superiority, pre-dominance.<BR> E. प्रमुख, and त्व aff.; also<BR>with तल् प्रमुखता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुग्ध
प्रमुग्ध f. (-ग्धा)<BR>	 1. Extremely charming.<BR>	 2. Unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुद्
प्रमुद् mfn. (-मुत्)<BR>	 1. Pleased, happy.<BR>	 2. Extreme joy.<BR> E. प्र before, मुद् to<BR>be pleased, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुदित|प्रमुदितः
प्रमुदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pleased, glad, content, happy.<BR> E. प्र excess, मुद् to be pleased, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुषिता
प्रमुषिता f. (-ता) A kind of riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमूढ
प्रमूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. A fool, foolish, stupid.<BR>	 2. Bewildered, deceived.<BR>E. प्र, and मूढ a fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमूढसंज्ञ
प्रमूढसंज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Bewildered, infatuated.<BR> E. प्रमूढ and संज्ञा sign of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृत
प्रमृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Covered, concealed, withdrawn or gone out of<BR>sight.<BR>	 2. Dead.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Tillage, cultivation.<BR> E. प्र before, मृ to die,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृष्ट
प्रमृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Polished, bright, clear.<BR>	 2. Rubbed.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>मृज् to clean, or मृष् to rub, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेदित
प्रमेदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Greasy, unctuous.<BR>	 2. Becoming or made unc-<BR>tuous.<BR> E. प्र before, मिद् to be unctuous, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेदितवत्
प्रमेदितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Being or made unctuous.<BR> E. प्र before, मिद्<BR>to be unctuous, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेय
प्रमेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Proveable, what may or ought to be proved.<BR>	 2.<BR>2. Measurable, finite.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. The thing to be proved.<BR>	 2. In logic,<BR>the second head, or topic including twelve objects, as the soul,<BR>body, &c. or the form and end of existence.<BR> E. प्र before, मा to<BR>measure, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेह|प्रमेहः
प्रमेह m. (-हः) Urinary affection, as change in the colour, quantity, or<BR>consistence of the urine; twenty-one varieties are enumerated,<BR>including diabetes, gonorrhœa, &c.<BR> E. प्र implying change, मिह् to<BR>pass urine, with घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोघ
प्रमोघ m. (-घः) Discharging, liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोचन|प्रमोचनं
प्रमोचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Liberating, setting free.<BR>	 2. Shedding, emitting.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, मुच् to liberate, ल्युट aff.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A sort of cucumber:<BR>see गवाक्षी.<BR> E. प्र before, मुच् to loose, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोद|प्रमोदः
प्रमोद m. (-दः) Pleasure, happiness, delight.<BR> E. प्र before, मुद् to be<BR>pleased, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदन|प्रमोदनं|प्रमोदनः
प्रमोदन n. (-नं) Gladdening, making glad.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An epithet of VIṢṆU<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदित|प्रमोदितः
प्रमोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Happy, delighted.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A name of KUVERA,<BR>E. प्रमोद happiness, इतच् aff.; or प्र before, मुद् to be happy, क्त aff.<BR>and the radical changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदिन्
प्रमोदिन् mfn. (-दि-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Happy, delighted.<BR>	 2. Delighting, making<BR>happy.<BR> E. प्रमोद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोह|प्रमोहः
प्रमोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Fascination.<BR>	 2. Fainting, insensibility.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>मुह् to be bewildered, घज् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोहित
प्रमोहित f. (-ता) Bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रम्लोचा
प्रम्लोचा f. (-चा) One of the Apsarās, or nymphs of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयच्छन्
प्रयच्छन् mfn. (-च्छन्-च्छती-च्छत्) Giving, presenting, bestowing.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, दा to give, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत|प्रयतः
प्रयत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well-governed, restrained, self-subdued.<BR>2. Careful, prudent.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A holy or pious person, one purified<BR>by austerity and mortification.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Pure.<BR>	 2. Submissive.<BR>	 3.<BR>Keeping the organs of sense under restraint.<BR> E. प्र intensely, यत् to<BR>to endeavour, aff. नङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतात्मन्
प्रयतात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Devout, pious of a holy spirit.<BR> E. प्रयत, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्न|प्रयत्नः
प्रयत्न n. (-त्नं)<BR>	 1. Continued or presevering effort, exertion.<BR>	 2. Act, action.<BR>3. (In logic,) Active effort of three kinds, engaging in any act,<BR>prosecuting it, and completing it.<BR>	 4. Caution, care.<BR>	 5. Articula-<BR>tion of sounds.<BR> E. प्र intensitive, यत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नतस्
प्रयत्नतस् Ind. Particularly, especially, with special effort, care or pains.<BR>E. प्रयत्न and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नवत्|प्रयत्नवन्त्
प्रयत्नवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Active, zealous, enterprising, assiduous,<BR>persevering.<BR> E. प्रयत्न effort, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्
प्रयस् mfn. (-याः-याः-यः) Valuable, precious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्त|प्रयस्तं
प्रयस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Seasoned, dressed with sauces and condiments.<BR>E. प्र before, यस् to take pains, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाग|प्रयागः
प्रयाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>	 2. A celebrated place of pilgrimage,<BR>the confluence of the Ganges and Jamunā, with the supposed sub-<BR>terraneous addition of the Saraswatī; the modern Allāhābād. The<BR>term in composition is applied of many places of reputed sanctity,<BR>situated at the confluence of two rivers, as Deva-Prayāga, Rudra-<BR>Prayāga, Karṇa-Prayaga, and Nanda-Prayāga, in the Himālayā<BR>mountains, which with Prayāga or Allāhābād, constitute the five<BR>principal places so termed.<BR>	 3. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 4. A horse.<BR> E. प्र<BR>principal, यज् to worship, and घञ् aff.; actual worship, or the<BR>place where worship is peculiarly efficacious; Allāhābād is one of<BR>the places where BRAHMĀ is supposed to have consummated ten<BR>Aśwamedhas or sacrifices of the horse, in commemoration of his<BR>recovery, of the four Vedas from ŚANKHĀSURA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयागभय|प्रयागभयः
प्रयागभय m. (-यः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. प्रयाग sacrifice, especially of<BR>the horse or Aśwamedha and भय fear; INDRA being dethroned<BR>by the performance of a hundred such sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाचन|प्रयाचनं
प्रयाचन n. (-नं) Begging, imploring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाज|प्रयाजः
प्रयाज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A principal ceremony or sacrifice.<BR>	 2. A part of a sac-<BR>rifice.<BR> E. प्र before, यज् to sacrifice, aff. घञ्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाण|प्रयाणं
प्रयाण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going, motion.<BR>	 2. Going forth or to a distance.<BR>	 3.<BR>Departure.<BR>	 4. Death.<BR>	 5. March of an assailing force, attack, in-<BR>vasion.<BR>	 5. Beginning, commencement.<BR>	 6. The back of a horse.<BR>	 7.<BR>The hind part of any animal.<BR> E. प्र before, या to go, aff. ल्युट्;<BR>also with कन् added, प्रयाणक n. (-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणकाल|प्रयाणकालः
प्रयाणकाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Time of departure.<BR>	 2. Death.<BR> E. प्रयाण and काल<BR>time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणभङ्ग|प्रयाणभंग|प्रयाणभङ्गः
प्रयाणभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A break in a journey, a halt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणार्ह
प्रयाणार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Worthy of death.<BR> E. प्रयाण, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयात|प्रयातः
प्रयात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone.<BR>	 2. Removed, gone away or to a distance.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">Page493-a+ 60</a>]<BR>3. Deceased.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A name of BHṚGU.<BR>	 2. A sleepy or lazy<BR>fellow.<BR>	 3. An invasion.<BR>	 4. A precipice.<BR> E. प्र before, यत् to endea-<BR>vour, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापण|प्रयापणं
प्रयापण n. (-ण)<BR>	 1. Sending, dispatching.<BR>	 2. Expelling, driving away. E.<BR>प्र before, या to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.; also न being unchanged,<BR>प्रयापन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापणीय
प्रयापणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be sent or sent away.<BR> E. प्र before, या to go,<BR>causal v., अनीयर् aff.; also प्रयापनीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापित
प्रयापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Driven or sent away, made to go or pass away.<BR>E. प्र before, या to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापिन्
प्रयापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Causing to go, who or what sends, or sends<BR>away, &c.<BR> E. प्र before, या to go, causal v., णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाप्यमाण
प्रयाप्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being sent or made to go, pass away, &c. E.<BR>प्र before, या to go, causal v., pass. v., शानच् aff.; also प्रयाप्यमान ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाम|प्रयामः
प्रयाम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Checking, restraining.<BR>	 2. Scarcity, dearth.<BR>	 3. Com-<BR>petition of buyers in consequence of scarcity.<BR>	 4. Length, either of<BR>space or time.<BR> E. प्र before, यम् to refrain, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाम्य
प्रयाम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) To be checked, controlled, &c.<BR> E. प्र before, यम्<BR>to check, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयास|प्रयासः
प्रयास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Trouble, labour, fatigue.<BR>	 2. Desire for or pursuit of<BR>any object.<BR> E. प्र before, यस् to make exertion, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयासभाज्
प्रयासभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Capable of exertion or fatigue, active, energetic.<BR>E. प्रयास, and भाज् sharing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयास्यत्
प्रयास्यत् mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्) Going, about to go or depart.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>या to go, शतृ aff. to the fut. tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्त|प्रयुक्तं
प्रयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Endowed with, possessing as an attribute, &c.<BR>2. Resulting from, consequential.<BR>	 3. Appointed, nominated.<BR>	 4.<BR>Associated or connected with.<BR>	 5. Applied, employed, (as a word.)<BR>	 6.<BR>Compact, closely united.<BR>	 7. Harnessed, yoked.<BR>	 8. Done, to or for.<BR>9. Abstracted, lost in meditation.<BR>	 10. Lent, (as money.)<BR>	 11. Asleep.<BR>n. (-क्तं) Cause.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to join, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्तसंस्कार
प्रयुक्तसंस्कार Adj. Refined, polished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्ति|प्रयुक्तिः
प्रयुक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Occasion, cause, main object or end.<BR>	 2. Use, employ-<BR>ment.<BR>	 3. Instigation.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to join and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुज्
प्रयुज् mfn. (-युक्) Who or what joins or is connected with, literally or<BR>figuratively, as a cause, motive, &c.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to join, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुज्य
प्रयुज्य Ind.<BR>	 1. Having acted or behaved to or towards.<BR>	 2. Having con-<BR>nected.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to join, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुज्यमान
प्रयुज्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being united or connected with.<BR>	 2. Being<BR>used, employed, applied, &c.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to join, pass. v.,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुञ्जान
प्रयुञ्जान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Adding, joining.<BR>	 2. Using, employing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Appointing, deputing.<BR>	 4. Performing, doing.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to<BR>join, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुत|प्रयुतं
प्रयुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Joined, combined, united.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Ten hundred<BR>thousand, a million.<BR> E. प्र before, यु to join, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुत्सु|प्रयुत्सुः
प्रयुत्सु m. (-त्सुः)<BR>	 1. A warrior.<BR>	 2. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 3. A name of the<BR>wind.<BR>	 4. A ram.<BR>	 5. An ascetic.<BR> E. प्र before, युद्ध to contend, in the<BR>desiderative form, with उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुद्ध|प्रयुद्धं
प्रयुद्ध n. (-द्धं) War, battle.<BR> E. प्र before, युद्ध the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुद्धार्थ|प्रयुद्धार्थः
प्रयुद्धार्थ m. (-र्थः) War, battle, going to war or battle.<BR> E. प्र initiatory, युद्ध<BR>war, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोक्तव्य
प्रयोक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Applicable, suitable, to be applied or employ-<BR>ed.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to unite, aff. तव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोक्तृ
प्रयोक्तृ f. (-क्त्री)<BR>	 1. One who uses or employs, (as a word.)<BR>	 2. One who ins-<BR>tigates.<BR>	 3. One who lends money on interest.<BR>	 4. One who repre-<BR>sents, (a drama.)<BR>	 5. One who shoots, (an arrow.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोग|प्रयोगः
प्रयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Occasion, cause, motive, object.<BR>	 2. Consequence,<BR>result.<BR>	 3. Affair, matter.<BR>	 4. Appointing, appointment.<BR>	 5. Appli-<BR>cation, use, employment.<BR>	 6. Ceremonial form, course of preceding.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">Page493-b+ 60</a>]<BR>7. Usage, practice, as in भूरिप्रयोग.<BR>	 8. Hurling, throwing, sending.<BR>	 9.<BR>Delivery, recitation.<BR>	 10. Exhibition of a dance, dancing.<BR>	 11. Prac-<BR>tice, performance, (opposed to theory.)<BR>	 12. Beginning, commence-<BR>ment.<BR>	 13. Consequence, result.<BR>	 14. Application of magic, magical<BR>rites.<BR>	 15. Subduing, fascinating.<BR>	 16. Device, contrivance.<BR>	 17.<BR>Example, comparision.<BR>	 18. Act, action.<BR>	 19. Dramatic action or<BR>performance.<BR>	 20. Principal, loan bearing interest.<BR>	 21. Lending<BR>money at interest.<BR>	 22. Profits of usury or trade.<BR>	 23. A horse.<BR>	 24.<BR>Text, authority.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to join, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगतस्
प्रयोगतस् Ind.<BR>	 1. According to or in consequence of.<BR>	 2. Actually, in ac-<BR>tion.<BR> E. तसि added to प्रयोग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगातिशय|प्रयोगातिशयः
प्रयोगातिशय m. (-यः) Bringing a character on the stage unexpectedly at<BR>the moment when his name is incidentally pronounced. The word<BR>is thus explained on Vāchaspatya:--<BR>“यदि प्रयोग एकस्मिन् प्रयोगोऽन्यः प्रयुज्यते ।<BR>तेन पात्र प्रवेशश्चेत् प्रयोगातिशयस्तदा ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगार्थ|प्रयोगार्थः
प्रयोगार्थ m. (-र्थः) Act, tending to a main object.<BR> E. प्रयोग aim or end,<BR>and अर्थ purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगिन्
प्रयोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Having some object in view, calculated for<BR>some particular purpose.<BR> E. प्रयोग object, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजक|प्रयोजकः
प्रयोजक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Who or what causes or induces any act.<BR>2. Who or what deputes or appoints.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A founder or ins-<BR>titutor of any ceremony.<BR>	 2. A law-giver, a legislator.<BR>	 3. An author.<BR>4. A money-lender.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to join, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजककत्तृत्व
प्रयोजककत्तृत्व n. (-त्वं) Acting as an instigator or promoter.<BR> E. प्रयोजक,<BR>and कत्तृत्व agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजन|प्रयोजनं
प्रयोजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Use, need, necessity, (with an inst.)<BR>	 2. Cause, occa-<BR>sion.<BR>	 3. Motive, origin.<BR>	 4. Purpose, object, intention, design.<BR>	 5.<BR>Profit, interest.<BR>	 6. Means of attaining.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to join,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजनवत्|प्रयोजनवन्त्
प्रयोजनवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Designing, purposing.<BR>	 2. Having a<BR>cause, caused, produced.<BR> E. प्रयोजन, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजयत्
प्रयोजयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Behaving to or towards, showing, dis-<BR>playing.<BR>	 2. Combining, &c.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to join, aff. शतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोज्यं|प्रयोज्य|प्रयोज्यः
प्रयोज्यं mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. To be set to work, to be appointed or direc-<BR>ted.<BR>	 2. To be used, practised, employed, &c.<BR>	 3. To be thrown.<BR>4. To be produced.<BR>	 n. (-ज्यं) Capital, principal.<BR>	 m. (-ज्यः) A servant,<BR>a slave.<BR> E. प्र before, युज् to join, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररुदित
प्ररुदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wept, weeping.<BR> E. प्र before, रुद् to weep, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररूढ|प्ररूढः
प्ररूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Rooted, fastened, growing or proceeding from<BR>a root.<BR>	 2. Grown, increased.<BR>	 3. Born, produced.<BR>	 m. (-ढः) The belly.<BR>E. प्र before, रुह् to grow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोचन
प्ररोचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Stimulating, exciting.<BR>	 2. Propitiating.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Praise<BR>of the author of a drama, &c., in the prelude, to secure the favour<BR>of the spectators.<BR> E. प्र before, रुच् to be light, causal v. णिच्-ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोह|प्ररोहः
प्ररोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A bud, a shoot.<BR>	 2. A shoot of light.<BR> E. प्र before, रुह्<BR>to grow, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोहिन्
प्ररोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Budding, sprouting.<BR> E. प्ररोह and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलपत्
प्रलपत् mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>	 1. Speaking, talking.<BR>	 2. Talking nonsense. E.<BR>प्र before, लप् to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलपित|प्रलपितः
प्रलपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Said, spoken, declared.<BR>	 2. Prating.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>लप् to speak, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलब्ध
प्रलब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Over-reached, cheated, deceived.<BR> E. प्र before, लभ् to gain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्ब|प्रलंब|प्रलम्बः
प्रलम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>	 1. Hanging down, depending from, pendulous.<BR>2. Slow, dilatory.<BR>	 m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. Depending, hanging on or from.<BR>	 2.<BR>The new shoot or bud of a creeping plant.<BR>	 3. A garland of flowers<BR>worn round the neck.<BR>	 4. A branch.<BR>	 5. The female breast.<BR>	 6. The<BR>name of a Daitya, killed by BALARĀMA.<BR>	 7. Head.<BR> E. प्र before, लवि<BR>to oppose, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बघ्न|प्रलंबघ्न|प्रलम्बघ्नः
प्रलम्बघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A name of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. प्रलम्ब a demon, killed by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">Page494-a+ 60</a>]<BR>BALADEVA, and घ्न who kills; also similar compounds, as<BR>प्रलम्बभित् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बभिद्
प्रलम्बभिद् m. (-भित्) BALADEVA, the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. प्रलम्ब, and<BR>भिद् who destroys: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बाण्ड|प्रलंबांड|प्रलम्बाण्डः
प्रलम्बाण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A man having large testicles.<BR> E. प्रलम्ब pendulous,<BR>and अण्ड testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्बित|प्रलंबित|प्रलम्बितः
प्रलम्बित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Suspended pendulous, hanging.<BR> E. प्रलम्ब hanging. इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलम्भ|प्रलंभ|प्रलंभः|प्रलम्भः
प्रलम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Obtaining, gaining.<BR>	 2. Fraud, cheating.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>लभि to get, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलय|प्रलयः
प्रलय m. (-यः) The end of a Kalpa, or destruction of the world.<BR>	 2.<BR>Death, dying, loss, destruction, dissolution, annihilation.<BR>	 3. Faint-<BR>ing, syncope, loss of sense or consciousness, considered as one of<BR>the thirty-three subordinate feelings, (in Rhetoric.)<BR>	 4. The mystic<BR>Syllable “Om.”<BR> E. प्र before, ली to destroy, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलयकाल|प्रलयकालः
प्रलयकाल m. (-लः) The time of universal destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलयदहन|प्रलयदहनः
प्रलयदहन m. (-नः) The fire at the dissolution of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलयपयोधि|प्रलयपयोधिः
प्रलयपयोधि m. (-धिः) The ocean at the dissolution of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रललाट
प्रललाट f. (-टा) Having a prominent forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलव|प्रलवः
प्रलव m. (-वः) A fragrant, a chip.<BR> E. प्र + लू-भावे अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलवित्र|प्रलवित्रं
प्रलवित्र n. (-त्रं) An instrument for cutting.<BR> E. प्र + लू-करणे इत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलाप|प्रलापः
प्रलाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Unmeaning or incoherent speech.<BR>	 2. Speaking.<BR>	 3.<BR>Discourse, conversation.<BR>	 4. Lamentation.<BR> E. प्र before, लप् to speak,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलापिन्
प्रलापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>	 1. Talking much, or unmeaningly, chatter-<BR>ing.<BR>	 2. Speaking to, conversing with.<BR> E. प्र before, लप् to<BR>speak, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलिप
प्रलिप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Who or what smears, plasters, &c.<BR> E. प्र before, लिप् to anoint, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलीन
प्रलीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Destroyed, annihilated.<BR>	 2. Unconscious, insen-<BR>sible.<BR>	 3. Melted.<BR> E. प्र before, ली to destroy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलीनता
प्रलीनता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Destruction, annihilation.<BR>	 2. The end of the universe.<BR>3. Unconsciousness, loss of sense.<BR> E. तल् added to the last;<BR>also with त्व प्रलीनत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलून
प्रलून f. (-ना) Cut off, cut asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेप|प्रलेपः
प्रलेप m. (-पः) An unguent, an ointment.<BR> E. प्र, लिप् to smear, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेपक|प्रलेपकः
प्रलेपक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what anoints, smears, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A plasterer.<BR>	 2. A slow fever.<BR> E. प्र before, लिप् to smear, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेह|प्रलेहः
प्रलेह m. (-हः) A kind of food. “कोर्मा”<BR> E. प्र + लिह्-कर्मणि-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोठन|प्रलोठनं
प्रलोठन n. (-नं) Rolling on the ground, heaving, tossing, (as of the<BR>ocean.)<BR> E. प्र before, लुठ् to roll, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोठित
प्रलोठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rolling, heaving, tossing.<BR> E. प्र before, लुठ् to roll, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोढ
प्रलोढ m. (-ढः)<BR>	 1. Cupidity, covetousness.<BR>	 2. Allurement, seduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोढन
प्रलोढन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Allurement.<BR>	 2. A lure, a bait.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभ|प्रलोभः
प्रलोभ m. (-भः) Desire, cupidity.<BR> E. प्र before, लुभ् to covet, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभन|प्रलोभनं
प्रलोभन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Allurement, inducement.<BR>	 2. Attraction, attracting,<BR>seducing.<BR> E. प्र before, लुभ् to desire, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभनी
प्रलोभनी f. (-नी) Sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोल
प्रलोल f. (-ला) Extremely agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवक
प्रवक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what goes.<BR> E. प्रु to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवक्तव्य
प्रवक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be expounded or explained.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>वच् to speak, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवक्तृ
प्रवक्तृ mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ) Who speaks or declares.<BR>	 m. (-क्ता) A teacher, an<BR>expounder, an orator.<BR> E. प्र before, वच् to speak, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवग|प्रवगः
प्रवग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. A monkey.<BR> E. प्रवग + लस्य रः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचन|प्रवचनं|प्रवचनः
प्रवचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A Veda, scripture.<BR>	 2. Excellent speech or language,<BR>eloquence.<BR>	 3. Teaching, expounding, exposition.<BR>	 4. Declaration. E.<BR>प्र principal, वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचनीय|प्रवचनीयः
प्रवचनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. A good speaker.<BR>	 2. To be well or elegantly<BR>spoken.<BR> E. प्र before, वच् to speak, aff. अनीयर् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचनपटु
प्रवचनपटु mfn. (-टुः-टुः-टु) Eloquent.<BR> E. प्रवचन and पटु skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्र
प्र(प्रा)वट m. (-टः) Wheat.<BR> E. प्र before, वट् to divide, aff. अट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव
प्रव(ब)ण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Declivity, declining, steep.<BR>	 2. Bent, bowed.<BR>3. Attached or adhering to, filled with, possessed of, endowed with.<BR>4. Inclined to, disposed to, tending to.<BR>	 5. Addicted to, devoted to<BR>6. Favourably disposed towords.<BR>	 7. Curved, crooked.<BR>	 8. Swift.<BR>	 9.<BR>Generous.<BR>	 10. Humble, modest.<BR>	 11. Wasted, decayed.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A<BR>place where four roads meet.<BR> E. प्र before, वन् to sound, &c.<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवत्स्यत्
प्रवत्स्यत् f. (ती or न्ती) About to go on a journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवत्स्यत्पतिका
प्रवत्स्यत्पतिका f. (-का) The wife of one who is about to go on a journey,<BR>regarded as one of the eight Nāyikās, (in belles lettres.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवदत्
प्रवदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>	 1. Speaking to or with, conversing, addressing.<BR>2. Speaking much or well.<BR>	 3. Arguing, a disputant.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>वद् to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवपण|प्रवपणं
प्रवपण n. (-णं) Sowing.<BR> E. प्र before, वप् to sow, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवयण|प्रवयणं
प्रवयण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A goad.<BR>	 2. The upper part of a piece of woven cloth.<BR>E. प्र before, अज् to go, वी substituted for the root, and aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवयस्
प्रवयस् m. (-याः) An old man.<BR> E. प्र past, and वयस् life or age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर|प्रवरं|प्रवरः
प्रवर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Best, most excellent.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A line of ancestors.<BR>2. An ancestor.<BR>	 3. Lineage.<BR>	 4. An exalted ancestor who contributes<BR>to the credit of a particular Gotra.<BR>	 5. A particular invocation ad-<BR>dressed to Agni by a Brāhmana at the consecration of his fire.<BR>	 6.<BR>A call, a summons.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Offspring, descendants.<BR>	 2. Family, race,<BR>kindred.<BR>	 3. A black sort of kidney bean, known as Aloe-wood.<BR>	 4.<BR>Covering, screening.<BR>	 5. A Muni, who contributes to the continua-<BR>tion of and credit of a particular caste or tribe of Brāhmans.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, वृ to chuse, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरललित
प्रवरललित n. (-तं) A species of the Ashti metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरवाहन
प्रवरवाहन m. (-नः) Du. An epithet of the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ग|प्रवर्गः
प्रवर्ग m. (-र्गः) Sacrificial fire.<BR> E. प्र before, वृज् to abandon, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ग्य|प्रवर्ग्यः
प्रवर्ग्य m. (-र्ग्यः) An officiating priest.<BR>	 n. (-र्ग्यं) A particular ceremony or<BR>sacrifice.<BR> E. प्रवर्ग, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्त्त|प्रवर्त|प्रवर्तः
प्रवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. Engaging in, undertaking.<BR>	 2. Excitement, stimulus.<BR>E. प्र before, वृत् to be, घञ् aff.: see प्रवर्त्तन and प्रवृत्ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्त्तक|प्रवर्तक|प्रवर्तकः|प्रवर्त्तकः
प्रवर्त्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Inciting, stimulating, inducing, who or what<BR>sets in action.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The original instigator of any act-<BR>the author, the principal.<BR>	 2. An arbiter, a judge.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The en-<BR>trance of the first person of the drama on the close of the intro-<BR>duction<BR> E. प्र before, वृत् to be, aff. णिच्-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्त्तन|प्रवर्तन|प्रवर्तनं|प्रवर्त्तनं
प्रवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Action, business, worldly interest or activity as op-<BR>posed to abstract contemplation.<BR>	 2. Fixing, establishing 3. Engag-<BR>ing, (in any work.)<BR>	 4. Beginning.<BR>	 5. Inciting, stimulating.<BR>	 6. Direct-<BR>ing, superintending.<BR>	 7. Informing 8. Revolving.<BR>	 9. Behaviour, con-<BR>duct, procedure.<BR>	 10. Happening, coming to pass.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Order,<BR>permission, the sense of the precative, or qualified imperative<BR>tense, stimulating to action.<BR> E. प्र before, वृत् to be, aff. युच् fem.<BR>aff. ठाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्त्तमान|प्रवर्तमान
प्रवर्त्तमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Engaging in, practising, doing.<BR>	 2. Being<BR>used or employed.<BR> E. प्र before, वृत् to be, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्त्तित|प्रवर्तित|प्रवर्त्तितः
प्रवर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Informed, apprized.<BR>	 2. Stimulated, excited,<BR>instigated.<BR>	 3. Revolving, going round.<BR>	 4. Made, rendered, caused.<BR>5. Made pure.<BR> E. प्र before, वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्द्धन
प्रवर्द्धन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) What causes to grow or increase.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Increase,<BR>augmenting.<BR> E. प्र before, वृध् to increase, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्षण|प्रवर्षणं
प्रवर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Raining.<BR>	 2. The first rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ह|प्रवर्हः
प्रवर्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Chief, principal, first.<BR> E. प्र before, वृह् to increase, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवलाकिन्
प्रवलाकिन् m. (-की)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. A peacock.<BR>	 3. One with a variegated<BR>girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवसत्
प्रवसत् mfn. (-सन्-सत्ती-सत्) Residing abroad.<BR> E. प्र before, वस् to dwell, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवसन|प्रवसनं
प्रवसन n. (-नं) Going abroad, sojourning in a foreign country.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, वस् to dwell, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह|प्रवहः
प्रवह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Going forth, or from a town.<BR>	 2. Streaming forth.<BR>	 3.<BR>One of the seven Vāyus, or courses of the wind which is said to<BR>cause the motion of the planets.<BR>	 4. Wind, air.<BR> E. प्र before, वह् to<BR>bear, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहण|प्रवहणं
प्रवहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A covered car, a litter or carriage for women.<BR>	 2. A ship.<BR>E. प्र forth, वह् to bear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहत्
प्रवहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>	 1. Bearing.<BR>	 2. Receiving, enjoying.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, वह् to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लि|प्रवह्लिः
प्रवह्लि f. (-ह्लिः-ह्ली) A riddle.<BR> E. प्र before, वल्ह् to speak, aff. इन्, and<BR>ङीप् optionally added: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लिका
प्रवह्लिका f. (-का) A riddle, an enigma, a conundrum or charade, &c. E.<BR>प्र before, वल्ह् to speak or tell, aff. क्वुन्; the conjunct consonants<BR>of the root are transposed,: also प्रवह्लि and प्रवह्ली, and with कन् add-<BR>ed to the latter, प्रवह्लीका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाच्
प्रवाच् mfn. (-वाक्) Eloquent oratorical, speaking, a speaker.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>वच् to speak, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाचक|प्रवाचकः
प्रवाचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Speaking well, eloquent.<BR> E. प्र before, वच् to speak, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाचन|प्रवाचनं
प्रवाचन n. (-नं) Proclamation, promulgation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाण|प्रवाणं
प्रवाण n. (-णं) The trimming of a piece of woven cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाणी
प्रवाणी f. (-णी) A weaver's shuttle.<BR> E. प्र before, वी to go, aff. ल्युट्<BR>fem. aff. ङीप्; also प्रवाणि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवात
प्रवात f. (-ता) Agitated by the wind.<BR>	 n. (-त)<BR>	 1. A current of air.<BR>	 2.<BR>Stormy weather.<BR>	 3. An airy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाद|प्रवादः
प्रवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Rumour, report.<BR>	 2. Discourse, conversation.<BR>3. Popular belief.<BR>	 4. A fable, a myth.<BR>	 5. Litigious language.<BR>	 6.<BR>Mutual defiance the conversation of antagonists prior to combat.<BR>E. प्र spreading, and वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवादिन्
प्रवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Who or what speaks, reports, &c.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>वद् to speak, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवापिन्
प्रवापिन् m. (-पी) A sower, one who sows seed.<BR> E. प्र before, वप् to sow, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवार|प्रवारः
प्रवार m. (-रः) Covering, clothing.<BR> E. प्र before, वृ to cover, aff. घञ्, also<BR>with अप् aff., and in other senses, प्रवर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवारण|प्रवारणं
प्रवारण m. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A desirable gift.<BR>	 2. Prohibition, objection, opposition.<BR>3. Priority of choice.<BR>	 4. Satisfying.<BR>	 5. A voluntary gift.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>वृ to chuse, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवास|प्रवासः
प्रवास m. (-सः) A temporary or foreign residence, a habitation away<BR>from home.<BR> E. प्र far or removed, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासत्
प्रवासत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्) Dwelling or being abroad or absent.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, वस् to dwell, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासन|प्रवासनं
प्रवासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Dwelling abroad, sojourning,<BR>lodging.<BR>	 3. Exile.<BR> E. प्र away, वस् to dwell, or divide, causal<BR>v., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासित
प्रवासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Expelled, expatriated.<BR> E. प्र before, वस् to dwell, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासिन्
प्रवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) A traveller, a sojourner, one living away<BR>from home.<BR> E. प्रवास a foreign or strange habitation, and इनि aff; or<BR>प्र before, वस् to dwell, and घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाह|प्रवाहः
प्रवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Stream, flow, continuous passage.<BR>	 2. Uninterrupted<BR>series, continuity.<BR>	 3. Moving onwards like a stream, course of<BR>events.<BR>	 4. Action, occupation, active life.<BR>	 5. A pond.<BR>	 6. A swift<BR>horse.<BR>	 f. (-ही) Sand.<BR> E. प्र continually, वह् to bear, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहक|प्रवाहकः
प्रवाहक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what bears or carries well.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>An imp, a goblin.<BR>	 f. (-हिका) Diarrhœa.<BR> E. प्र before, वह् to bear,<BR>aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहन|प्रवाहनं
प्रवाहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Driving forth.<BR>	 2. Evacuation by stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाही
प्रवाही f. (-ही) Sand.<BR> E. प्र + वह्-णिच् अच् गौरा० ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहुकम्
प्रवाहुकम् Ind.<BR>	 1. At the same time.<BR>	 2. Above, over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविकशत्
प्रविकशत् mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्) Expanding, opening, blossoming.<BR> E. प्र and<BR>वि before, कश् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविख्याति|प्रविख्यातिः
प्रविख्याति f. (-तिः) Celebrity, reputation.<BR> E. प्र वि prefixed to ख्या<BR>to say, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचय|प्रविचयः
प्रविचय m. (-यः) Examination, investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचार|प्रविचारः
प्रविचार m. (-रः) Discerning, discrimination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवितत
प्रवितत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Spread out, expanded.<BR>	 2. Dishevelled.<BR> E. प्र<BR>and वि before, तन् to spread, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविदारण|प्रविदारणं
प्रविदारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. War, battle, combat.<BR>	 2. Tearing, rending, breaking.<BR>3. Tumult, crowd, confusion.<BR>	 4. Bursting, budding.<BR> E. प्र and वि<BR>prefixed to दॄ to tear to pieces, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविदारित
प्रविदारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Torn, rent, severed.<BR>	 2. Opened, expanded.<BR>E. प्र and वि before, दॄ to tear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविद्ध
प्रविद्ध f. (-द्धा) Cast away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविद्रुत
प्रविद्रुत f. (-ता) Dispersed, scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभक्त
प्रविभक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Partitioned, divided, separated, shared.<BR> E. प्र<BR>and विभक्त divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभाग|प्रविभागः
प्रविभाग m. (-गः) Division, a part, distribution.<BR> E. प्र and विभान division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविर|प्रविरः
प्रविर m. (-रः) A yellow fragrant wood.<BR> E. प्र and वि before, रा to get<BR>or be, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविरल
प्रविरल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. A part, separate, isolated.<BR>	 2. Very few, rare.<BR> E. प्र, विरल distinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविलय|प्रविलयः
प्रविलय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Melting away.<BR>	 2. Complete dissolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविलुप्त
प्रविलुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Lost, removed, fallen or rubbed off.<BR> E. प्र and<BR>वि before, लुप् to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविवर
प्रविवर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Yellow Sandal.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Perforated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविवाद|प्रविवादः
प्रविवाद m. (-दः) Dispute, quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविविक्त
प्रविविक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Separated, detached.<BR>	 2. Solitary.<BR> E. प्र and विविक्त detached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविव्राजयिषु
प्रविव्राजयिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing or intending to banish.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>व्रज् to go, causal desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविश्लेष|प्रविश्लेषः
प्रविश्लेष m. (-षः) Separation, parting.<BR> E. प्र, वि negative prefix before,<BR>श्लिष् to unite, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविषण
प्रविषण mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं)<BR>	 1. Sad, spiritless.<BR>	 2. Dejected, separated.<BR> E. प्र<BR>much, विषण्ण dejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविषा
प्रविषा f. (-षा) A plant, commonly Ātāīch.<BR> E. प्र against, (anti), and विष poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविष्ट|प्रविष्टः
प्रविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Entered, gone in or into.<BR>	 2. Entered upon,<BR>(as an affair,) engaged in.<BR> E. प्र before, विष् to enter, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविष्टक|प्रविष्टकं
प्रविष्टक n. (-कं) Entrance on the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवि
प्रवि(स्त)लार m. (-रः) Expance, extent, compass, circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीण|प्रवीणः
प्रवीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Skilful, clever, conversant.<BR> E. प्र implying excell-<BR>ence, and वीणा a lute, or वीण् a nominal verb, to play on a lute,<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीणता
प्रवीणता f. (-ता) Proficiency, skill.<BR> E. प्रवीण, and तल् aff.; also with त्वं, प्रवीणत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीर|प्रवीरः
प्रवीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Best, most excellent.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A hero, a warrior.<BR>2. A chief, a person of rank or distinction.<BR>	 3. Strong, powerful.<BR>E. प्र pre-eminent, and वीर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृञ्जनीय
प्रवृञ्जनीय m. (-यः) A great hero.<BR> E. प्र + वृञ्ज्-अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्त|प्रवृत्तः
प्रवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Fixed, settled, determined, done.<BR>	 2. Engaged<BR>in, undertaking, occupied by.<BR>	 3. Begun, beginning.<BR>	 4. Doing,<BR>acting.<BR>	 5. Undisputed, (as dominion.)<BR>	 6. Round, globular.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः) A round ornament.<BR> E. प्र before, वृत् to be, aff. क्त; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तकर्म्मन्|प्रवृत्तकर्मन्
प्रवृत्तकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Any act the cause of being born again.<BR> E. प्रवृत्त, and<BR>कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तचक्रता
प्रवृत्तचक्रता f. (-ता) Absolute dominion.<BR> E. प्रवृत्त fixed, चक्र rule, and तल् abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्ति|प्रवृत्तिः
प्रवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Activity, occupation, active life, as opposed to contem-<BR>plative devotion; or it is defined to consist of the wish to do,<BR>knowledge of the means of success and accomplishing the desired<BR>object.<BR>	 2. Prosecution, perseverance.<BR>	 3. Addiction to, predilection<BR>for.<BR>	 4. Practice, conduct.<BR>	 5. Tidings, intelligence.<BR>	 6. Continuous<BR>flow, stream, current.<BR>	 7. Employment, occupation.<BR>	 8. Fate, Des-<BR>tiny.<BR>	 9. Signification, sense.<BR>	 10. Direct perception.<BR>	 11. Progress,<BR>advance.<BR>	 12. Rise, source, origin.<BR>	 13. Appearance, manifestation.<BR>14. The juice that exudes from the elephant's temples, when in rut.<BR>15. Oujein, or any holy place.<BR>	 16. (In arithmetic,) The multiplier.<BR>E. प्र before, वृत् to be or abide, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिज्ञ|प्रवृत्तिज्ञः
प्रवृत्तिज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) An emissary, an agent, a spy.<BR> E. प्रवृत्ति news, and ज्ञ<BR>who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिनिमित्त
प्रवृत्तिनिमित्त n. (-त्तं) Relation for the use of any work in a particular sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिमार्ग|प्रवृत्तिमार्गः
प्रवृत्तिमार्ग m. (-र्गः) Worldly life, attachment to the pleasures of the<BR>world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृद्ध|प्रवृद्धः
प्रवृद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Full grown.<BR>	 2. Expanded, diffused, spread<BR>abroad or dispersed.<BR>	 3. Swollen, (as a river.)<BR>	 4. Full, deep, (as a<BR>sigh.)<BR>	 5. Haughty, arrogant.<BR> E. प्र before, वृद्ध् to increase or grow,<BR>aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृद्धि|प्रवृद्धिः
प्रवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Increase, growth.<BR>	 2. Prosperity, preferment, promotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक|प्रवेकः
प्रवेक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Chief, head, principal.<BR> E. प्र before, विच् to dis-<BR>tinguish, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक्षण
प्रवेक्षण n. (-णं) Foreseeing.<BR> E. प्र and अव before, ईक्ष् to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक्षित
प्रवेक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Foreseen, anticipated.<BR> E. प्र and अव before, ईक्ष्<BR>to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक्ष्यत्
प्रवेक्ष्यत् mfn. (-क्ष्यन्-क्ष्यन्ती-क्ष्यत्) Foreseeing, anticipating.<BR> E. प्र and अव be-<BR>fore, ईक्ष् to see, शतृ aff., the first syllable made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेग|प्रवेगः
प्रवेग m. (-गः) Great speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेट|प्रवेटः
प्रवेट m. (-टः) Barley.<BR> E. प्र before, वी to sound, aff. ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणि|प्रवेणिः
प्रवेणि f. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. The hair twisted, and undecorated, as worn by wo-<BR>men in the absence of their husbands.<BR>	 2. An elephant's housings.<BR>3. The current of a river.<BR> E. प्र before, वेल् to go, aff. इण्; also with<BR>ङीप् added, प्रवेणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणी
प्रवेणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Un-ornamented hair.<BR>	 2. An elephant's housing, &c. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेतृ
प्रवेतृ m. (-र्त्ता) A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेदन|प्रवेदनं
प्रवेदन n. (-नं) Making known, announcing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपण
प्रवेपण n. (-णं) Shaking, agitation, tremulous motion.<BR> E. प्र before, वेपृ<BR>to tremble, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेरित
प्रवेरित f. (-ता) Cast hither and thither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेल|प्रवेलः
प्रवेल m. (-लः) The yellow variety of kidney bean.<BR> E. प्र before, वेल् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेश|प्रवेशः
प्रवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Intentness on an object, engaging closely in a pursuit<BR>or purpose.<BR>	 2. Entrance, penetration.<BR>	 3. A door.<BR>	 4. Entrance on<BR>the stage.<BR>	 5. Income, revenue.<BR> E. प्र before, विश् to enter, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशक|प्रवेशकः
प्रवेशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what enters.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An inferior<BR>actor who announces the entrance of the principal characters, or<BR>an interlude acted by inferior characters for the sake of making<BR>known to the audience events which are not represented on the<BR>stage and a knowledge of which is necessary for the understanding<BR>of what follows, provided that it can never occur in the begin-<BR>ning of the first act or at the end of the last.<BR>	 2. An entry.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, विश् to enter, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशन|प्रवेशनं
प्रवेशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The entrance to a house, the principal door or gate.<BR>	 2.<BR>Entering, penetrating.<BR>	 3. Introducing, leading into.<BR>	 4. Sexual in-<BR>tercourse.<BR> E. प्र before, विश् to enter, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशित
प्रवेशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Called or sent in 2. Introduced.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>विश् to enter, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेश्य
प्रवेश्य Ind. Having sent in, thrown into, &c.<BR> E. प्र before, विश् to enter,<BR>causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेश्य
प्रवेश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) To be entered, to be pervaded.<BR> E. प्र before, विश्<BR>to enter, यत् aff.; also प्रवेशनीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेष्ट|प्रवेष्टः
प्रवेष्ट m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. An arm.<BR>	 2. The fore-arm, or wrist.<BR>	 3. An elephant's<BR>gums.<BR>	 4. An elephants housings.<BR>	 5. The back of an elephant.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, वेष्ट् to encompass, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेष्टव्य
प्रवेष्टव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be entered, to be penetrated or pervaded. E.<BR>प्र before, विश् to enter, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्यक्त|प्रव्यक्तं
प्रव्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Evident, apparent, manifest.<BR> E. प्र and वि before,<BR>अञ्ज् to spread, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्यक्ति|प्रव्यक्तिः
प्रव्यक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Manifestation, appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्यथित
प्रव्यथित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Distressed, pained.<BR> E. प्र before व्यथ् to pain, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्यहार
प्रव्यहार m. (-रः) Prolongation of discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रजन|प्रव्रजनं
प्रव्रजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going abroad.<BR>	 2. Becoming a recluse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रजित|प्रव्रजितः
प्रव्रजित m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. An ascetic or mendicant.<BR>	 2. The pupil, or attendant<BR>of a Jaina or Bauddha mendicant.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A female devotee or<BR>ascetic.<BR>	 2. Spikenard, (Valeriana Jatamansi)<BR>	 3. A plant, commonly<BR>Muṇḍīrī, (Sphœranthus molis.)<BR>	 n. (-तं) The life of an ascetic. E.<BR>प्र before, व्रज् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्या
प्रव्रज्या f. (-ज्या)<BR>	 1. Roaming, travelling, wandering about, as a religious<BR>mendicant especially.<BR>	 2. Abandonment of the world.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>व्रज् to go, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्यावसित|प्रव्रज्यावसितः
प्रव्रज्यावसित m. (-तः) An ascetic, who has broken his observance. E.<BR>प्रव्रज्या, and अवसित finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रश्चन|प्रव्रश्चनः
प्रव्रश्चन m. (-नः) A knife for cutting fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्राज
प्रव्राज m. (-जः) An ascetic.<BR> E. प्र, व्रज् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्राजन|प्रव्राजनं
प्रव्राजन n. (-नं) Banishment.<BR> E. प्र before, व्रज् to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंशन
प्रशंशन n. (-नं) Praising, eulogising: see प्रशंसन.<BR> E. प्र before, शण्स to<BR>praise, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंशा
प्रशंशा f. (-शा) Praise, eulogium.<BR> E. प्र before, शण्स to praise, अङ् and<BR>टाप् affs.: see प्रशंसा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसन|प्रशंसनं
प्रशंसन n. (-णं) Praising, eulogising.<BR> E. प्र before, शण्स to praise, ल्युट् aff.; also प्रशंशन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसनीय
प्रशंसनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be praised, praise-worthy.<BR> E. प्र before, शण्स<BR>to praise, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसा
प्रशंसा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. Praise, applause, flattery, commendation.<BR>	 2. Fame, re-<BR>putation, glory.<BR>	 3. Description, as in अप्रस्तूतप्रशंसा<BR> E. प्र especially<BR>शण्स, to praise, affs. अङ् and टाप्; the root is also read शण्श, when<BR>this word and the analogous derivatives are read प्रशंशा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसित
प्रशंसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Praised, eulogised.<BR> E. प्रशंसा, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसितव्य
प्रशंसितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be praised, praise-worthy.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>शंस् to praise, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसोपमा
प्रशंसोपमा f. (-मा) A kind of Upamā according to Dandin, who thus<BR>defines and illustrates it:--<BR>ब्रह्यणोत्प्युद्भवः पद्मश्चन्द्रः शम्भुशिरोधृतः ।<BR>तौ तुलौ तन्मुखेनेति सा प्रशंसोपमोच्यते ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशत्वन्
प्रशत्वन् m. (-त्वा) The ocean f. (-री) A river.<BR> E. प्र before, शद् to go, and<BR>क्वनिप् Unādi aff, र inserted before ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशम|प्रशमः
प्रशम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Calmness, tranquillity, composure.<BR>	 2. Assuagement,<BR>appeasement.<BR>	 3. Abatement, extinction.<BR> E. प्र, शम् to pacify, अच् or<BR>घञ् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमन|प्रशमनं
प्रशमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Pacifying, tranquillising.<BR>	 3.<BR>Quiescence, reposing.<BR>	 4. Soothing, assuaging.<BR>	 5. Ouring, healing.<BR>6. Extinguishing.<BR>	 7. Bestowing fitly.<BR>	 8. Securing, guarding.<BR>	 9.<BR>Cessation, abatement.<BR> E. प्र before, शम् to pacify, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमित
प्रशमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Allayed, appeased, relived, tranquilised, &c.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, शम् to be calm, causal v., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमय्य
प्रशमय्य Ind. Having appeased.<BR> E. प्र before, शम् to be calm, causal v., ल्यट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशम्यमान
प्रशम्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Pacified, quieted, appeased, flattered.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, शम्, to be at rest, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्त|प्रशस्तं
प्रशस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Happy, well, right.<BR>	 2. Good, excellent, best.<BR>3. Praised, extolled.<BR> E. प्र before, शण्स to praise or commend,<BR>aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्ति|प्रशस्तिः
प्रशस्ति f. (-स्तिः)<BR>	 1. Excellence, eminence.<BR>	 2. Eulogy.<BR>	 3. A small poem<BR>written in praise of any one.<BR>	 4. Instruction.<BR> E. प्र before, शणस to<BR>praise, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्य|प्रशस्यः
प्रशस्य f. (-स्या) Praise-worthy, excellent.<BR> E. प्र + शण्स to praise, क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाख
प्रशाख f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. Having red branches.<BR>	 2. In the fifth stage of for-<BR>mation. (as an embryo.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाखिक
प्रशाखिक m. (-कः) A small branch or twig.<BR> E. प्र before, शाखा a branch,<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्त|प्रशांत|प्रशान्तः
प्रशान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्त)<BR>	 1. Calmed, clam, tranquillised.<BR>	 2. Ceased, dis-<BR>continued, (as active effort.)<BR>	 3. Ended.<BR>	 4. Relieved.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>शम् to be calm, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तचेष्ट|प्रशांतचेष्ट
प्रशान्तचेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Resting,<BR> E. प्रशान्त and चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तात्मन्|प्रशांतात्मन्
प्रशान्तात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Peaceful, calm, composed in mind. E.<BR>प्रशान्त and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्ति|प्रशांति|प्रशांतिः|प्रशान्तिः
प्रशान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Calm, quiet, tranquility, moral or physical.<BR>	 2.<BR>Quenching, extinguishing.<BR> E. प्र before, शम् to be calm, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशान्तोज
प्रशान्तोज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Weakened, prostrate in strength.<BR> E. प्रशान्त,<BR>and ओजस् strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाम्
प्रशाम् mfn. (-प्रशान्) Quiet, tranquil.<BR> E. प्र before, शम् to be tranquil,<BR>क्विप् aff., and the penultimate made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाम|प्रशामः
प्रशाम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Tranquillity, quiescence.<BR>	 2. Allaying, pacifying.<BR>	 3.<BR>Laying, suppressing.<BR> E. प्र before, शम् to be at rest, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासन|प्रशासनं
प्रशासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Governing, ruling.<BR>	 2. Enacting.<BR> E. प्र before, शास् to<BR>rule, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशास्तृ
प्रशास्तृ m. (-स्ता) A king.<BR> E. प्र + शास्-अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासित
प्रशासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Governed, ruled.<BR>	 2. Promulgated, enacted.<BR>E. प्र before, शास् to rule, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासितृ
प्रशासितृ m. (-ता) A ruler or governor.<BR> E. प्र before, शास् to<BR>govern, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिथिल
प्रशिथिल f. (-ला) Very loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिष्य|प्रशिष्यः
प्रशिष्य m. (-ष्यः) The disciple of disciple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशोष|प्रशोषः
प्रशोष m. (-षः) The becoming dry, aridity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्चोतन्
प्रश्चोतन् mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्) Sprinkling, scattering. प्र before, श्च्युत् to<BR>sprinkle, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्न|प्रश्नः
प्रश्न m. (-श्नः)<BR>	 1. A question, a demand, an inquiry, an interrogation.<BR>2. Judicial inquiry.<BR>	 3. The subject of a controversy, a contro-<BR>verted point.<BR>	 4. Inquiry into the future.<BR>	 5. Problem for calcula-<BR>tion.<BR>	 6. Section of a book.<BR>	 f. (-श्नी) An aquatic plant, (Pistia-<BR>stratiotes.) “पाना” इति भाषा ।<BR> E. प्रच्छ् to ask, aff. नङ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नदूती
प्रश्नदूती f. (-ती) A riddle, an enigma, an intricate or enigmatical ques-<BR>tion.<BR> E. प्रश्न a question, and दूती playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रथ|प्रश्रथः
प्रश्रथ m. (-थः) Laxity, relaxation, flaccidity,<BR> E. प्र before, श्रथ् to be<BR>loose, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रय|प्रश्रयः
प्रश्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Affection, affectionate regard or solicitation.<BR>	 2. Res-<BR>pect.<BR>	 3. Courtesy, civility.<BR> E. प्र before, श्रि to serve, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रवण
प्रश्रवण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A fountain, a cascade, a water-fall.<BR>	 2. Oozing, flowing.<BR>3. A range of mountains in the south, part of the western Ghats.<BR>E. प्र before, श्रु to ooze or drop, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रित|प्रश्रितः
प्रश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Modest, humble, well-behaved.<BR> E. प्र before, श्रि<BR>to serve, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रुत
प्रश्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Flowing, oozing, issuing.<BR> E. प्र before, श्रु to drop, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लथ|प्रश्लथः
प्रश्लथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Languid, flaccid, loose, relaxed, unnerved,<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, श्लथ् to be loose, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लिष्ट|प्रश्लिष्टः
प्रश्लिष्ट f. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. Entwined.<BR>	 2. Well-reasoned.<BR> E. प्र + श्लिष-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लेष|प्रश्लेषः
प्रश्लेष m. (-षः) Close, contact, pressing hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्वास|प्रश्वासः
प्रश्वास m. (-सः) Respiration.<BR> E. प्र + श्वस्-घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्टव्य
प्रष्टव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be asked.<BR> E. प्रच्छ् to ask, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्टृ
प्रष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Asking, demanding, an asker or questioner. E.<BR>प्रच्छ् to ask, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठ|प्रष्ठः
प्रष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. A leader, a conductor, one who goes first or be-<BR>fore.<BR>	 2. Prior, preceding.<BR>	 3. Chief, principal, best.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठी) The<BR>wife of a leader or chief.<BR> E. प्र pre-eminent, स्था to stay or<BR>be, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठवाह्
प्रष्ठवाह् m. (-वाट्-वाड्) A young bull or steer, training for the plough,<BR>&c.<BR> E. प्रष्ठ a leader, and वह् to bear, aff. ण्वि or विच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठौही
प्रष्ठौही f. (-ही) A cow pregnant with her first calf.<BR> E. प्रष्ठ here said to<BR>be the first birth, and वह् to bear, aff. ण्वि or विच्, fem. aff. ङीप्,<BR>and व is changed to ऊ, which with the preceding vowel becomes<BR>औ by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस
प्रस r. 1st cl. (प्रस्यते)<BR>	 1. To spread or diffuse.<BR>	 2. To bring forth young.<BR>सक० दिवा० आ० सेट् । मित् घटादि णिच् (प्रसयति-ते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसक्त|प्रसक्तं
प्रसक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Eternal, constant, continual.<BR>	 2. Opened, ex-<BR>panded.<BR>	 3. Obtained, gained, attained.<BR>	 4. Attached to, devoted<BR>to, (person or thing,) engaged in.<BR>	 5. United to, connected with,<BR>accompanying.<BR>	 6. Applied to, used, employed.<BR>	 7. Applicability,<BR>application.<BR>	 8. Conclusion, deduction.<BR>	 9. Topic of conversation.<BR>10. Energy, perseverance.<BR>	 n. adv. (-क्तं) Continually, incessantly,<BR>eternally.<BR> E. प्र before, सन्ज to unite or embrace, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसक्ति|प्रसक्तिः
प्रसक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Union, connection.<BR>	 2. Adherence or attachment to.<BR>3. Energy, perseverance.<BR>	 4. Acquiring.<BR>	 5. Inference, conclusion,<BR>deduction.<BR>	 6. A topic, or subject of conversation.<BR> E. प्र before, सन्ज<BR>to unite, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंख्या|प्रसङ्ख्या
प्रसंख्या f. (-ख्या)<BR>	 1. Total number.<BR>	 2. Reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंख्यान
प्रसंख्यान m. (-नः) Payment, liquidation.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Enumeration.<BR>	 2. Re-<BR>nown, reputation.<BR>	 3. Reflection, meditation.<BR> E. प्र + सम्-ख्या-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्ग|प्रसंग|प्रसंगः|प्रसङ्गः
प्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Introduction, insertion.<BR>	 2. Association, connexion.<BR>	 3.<BR>Addiction or attachment to 4. Connected language or style.<BR>5. Connected reasoning or argument.<BR>	 6. Double or conjoint re-<BR>sult, producing two effects, attaining two objects by one act.<BR>7. Revealing a secret.<BR>	 8. (In dramatic language.) A second or<BR>subsidiary incident or plot.<BR>	 9. Union, association, intercourse,<BR>(as in स्त्री प्रसङ्ग)<BR>	 10. Illicit intercourse.<BR>	 11. Topic of conversation.<BR>12. Occupation.<BR>	 13. Contingency, event, case.<BR>	 14. Mention of<BR>parents.<BR>	 15. Equal extent, inseparable connection, (in logic.)<BR>	 16. A<BR>conclusion, an inference.<BR>	 17. Time, opportunity, occasion.<BR> E. प्र<BR>preceding, सन्ज to join, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गनिवारण|प्रसंगनिवारण
प्रसङ्गनिवारण n. (-णं) Obviation of similar contingencies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गवशात्|प्रसंगवशात्
प्रसङ्गवशात् Ind. By the force of circumstances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसङ्गेन
प्रसङ्गेन Incidentally, by way of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसञ्जन|प्रसंजन|प्रसंजनं
प्रसञ्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Bringing into use, employing, applying, bringing to<BR>bear.<BR>	 2. Combining, connecting.<BR> E. प्र before, सन्ज to unite, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसत्ति|प्रसत्तिः
प्रसत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Purity, cleanness, brightness, transparency.<BR>	 2. Favour,<BR>graciousness, complacency.<BR> E. प्र before, सद् to go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसत्वन्
प्रसत्वन् m. (-त्वा)<BR>	 1. Virtue, piety.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ f. (-री) Acquisition, ac-<BR>complishment.<BR> E. प्र before, सद् to go, वनिप् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्न|प्रसन्नः
प्रसन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Clear, clean, bright, pellucid.<BR>	 2. Pleased, de-<BR>lighted.<BR>	 3. Complacent, gracious, favourable.<BR>	 f. (-न्ना)<BR>	 1. Propitiating,<BR>pleasing.<BR>	 2. Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>	 3. Open, clear, easily<BR>intelligible, (as the meaning of a passage.)<BR>	 4. True.<BR> E. प्र prin-<BR>cipally, &c. सद् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नता
प्रसन्नता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Brightness, pellucidness, clearness, purity.<BR>	 2. Favour,<BR>kindness, being pleased with.<BR> E. प्रसन्न clear, and तल् aff; also with<BR>त्व, प्रसन्नत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नमुख
प्रसन्नमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Agreeable-looking, smiling, looking pleased.<BR>E. प्रसन्न and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नात्मन्
प्रसन्नात्मन् Adj. Propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्नेरा
प्रसन्नेरा f. (-रा) Spirituous liquor.<BR> E. प्रसन्न clear, and ईरा wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसभ|प्रसभः
प्रसभ n. (-भं) Violently, forcibly.<BR>	 2. Much, exceedingly.<BR>E. प्र gone, passed, सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसभम्
प्रसभम् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of: 1. Exceedingly,<BR>much.<BR>	 2. Violently, forcibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसभहरण
प्रसभहरण n. (-णं) Carrying off by force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसमीक्षण|प्रसमीक्षणं
प्रसमीक्षण n. (-णं) Considering, deliberating, discussing.<BR> E. प्र, सम् before,<BR>ईक्ष् to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसमीक्षा
प्रसमीक्षा f. (-क्षा) Deliberation, judgment.<BR> E. प्र and सम् before, ईक्ष to<BR>see, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसमीक्ष्य
प्रसमीक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) To be weighed, considered, discussed, &c.<BR>Ind. Having considered.<BR> E. प्र and सम् before, ईक्ष् to see, यत् or<BR>ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसयन|प्रसयनं
प्रसयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Fastening, binding.<BR>	 2. A net.<BR> E. प्र + सि-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर|प्रसरः
प्रसर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Who or what proceeds projects, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">Page498-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Spreading, extending.<BR>	 2. Space, room.<BR>	 3. Occasion, opportunity.<BR>4. affectionate solicitation.<BR>	 5. Speed, velocity.<BR>	 6. Battle, war.<BR>	 7.<BR>Multitude, assemblage.<BR>	 8. An iron arrow.<BR>	 9. A projection, a pro-<BR>cess.<BR>	 10. Free course, unimpeded motion.<BR>	 11. Diffusion.<BR>	 12. A<BR>flow, a stream, a torrent, a flood.<BR> E. प्र before, सृ to go, aff. अप्<BR>or अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरण|प्रसरणं
प्रसरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going forth or round.<BR>	 2. Surrounding an enemy.<BR>	 3.<BR>Spreading over the country to forage.<BR>	 4. Amiability.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>सृ to go, aff. ल्युट्; also प्रसरणी and प्रसरणि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरणि|प्रसरणिः
प्रसरणि f. (-णिः or -णी) Surrounding an enemy.<BR> E. प्र before, सृ to go,<BR>aff. अनि, and ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरत्
प्रसरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>	 1. Expanding, spreading, bursting.<BR>	 2. Pro-<BR>ceeding, projecting.<BR> E. प्र before, सृ to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पक
प्रसर्पक m. (-कः) An uninvited guest, an intruder.<BR> E. प्र before, सृप् to<BR>go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पण|प्रसर्पणं
प्रसर्पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Spreading, stretching, expanding.<BR>	 2. Going, proceed-<BR>ing.<BR> E. प्र before, सृप् to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पत्
प्रसर्पत् mfn. (-र्पन्-र्पन्ती-र्पत्) Advancing, proceeding.<BR> E. प्र before, सृप् to<BR>go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस
प्रस(श)ल m. (-लः) The cold season, (हेमन्ते)<BR> E. प्र + शल्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसव|प्रसवः
प्रसव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Bringing forth, bearing, (as young.)<BR>	 2. Birth, pro-<BR>duction.<BR>	 3. Offspring, posterity.<BR>	 4. Fruit.<BR>	 5. A blossom, a flower.<BR>6. Source, origin.<BR> E. प्र before, सू to bear, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवक|प्रसवकः
प्रसवक m. (-कः) A tree commonly Piyal, (Buchanania latifolia)<BR> E. प्रसव<BR>a flower, aff. कन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवगृह
प्रसवगृह n. (-हं) A lying in-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवबन्धन|प्रसवबंधन|प्रसवबन्धनं
प्रसवबन्धन n. (-नं) The foot-stalk of a leaf or flower, the petiole or ped-<BR>uncle.<BR> E. प्रसव a flower, and बन्धन a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवत्
प्रसवत् mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्) Bearing.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती) A woman in labour.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, सू to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवन|प्रसवनं
प्रसवन n. (-नं) Bringing forth, fecundity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसववेदना
प्रसववेदना f. (-ना) The Pangs of child-birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवस्थली
प्रसवस्थली f. (-ली) A mother.<BR> E. प्रसव and स्थल place, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवितृ
प्रसवितृ m. (-ता) A father.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A mother.<BR> E. प्र before, सू to bear or<BR>have offspring, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसविन्
प्रसविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Having or bearing young.<BR> E. प्रसव, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसव्य|प्रसव्यं
प्रसव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Contrary, reverse, unfavourable, inverted, re-<BR>verted.<BR> E. प्र inclined towards, सव्य the left or wrong side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह|प्रसहः
प्रसह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A beast or bird of prey.<BR>	 2. Resistance, endurance.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-हा) Adj. Withstanding, bearing up.<BR> E. प्र before, सह् to be able,<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसहन|प्रसहनः
प्रसहन m. (-नः) A beast or bird of prey.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Embracing, an em-<BR>brace.<BR>	 2. Defeat.<BR>	 3. Bearing, enduring.<BR> E. प्र before, सह् to<BR>bear, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्य
प्रसह्य Ind.<BR>	 1. Forcibly, violently.<BR>	 2. Exceedingly.<BR> E. प्र excessively, सह्<BR>to be able, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्यचौर|प्रसह्यचौरः
प्रसह्यचौर m. (-रः) A robber, a plunderer.<BR> E. प्रसह्य violently, and चौर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसातिका
प्रसातिका f. (-का) A kind of rice. “अणुधान्ये” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाद|प्रसादः
प्रसाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Clearness, cleanness, transparency, brightness.<BR>	 2. Fa-<BR>vour, kindness, propitiousness, approbation.<BR>	 3. Well-being, wel-<BR>fare.<BR>	 4. Composure, calmness of mind.<BR>	 5. Poetry written in an<BR>elegant but an easy style.<BR>	 6. Perspicuity.<BR>	 7. Connection, associa-<BR>tion.<BR>	 8. Propitiatory offering.<BR>	 9. Good humour, good temper.<BR>	 10.<BR>Food that has been offered to an idol, or of which a spiritual<BR>teacher has partaken.<BR> E. प्र before, सद् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादक
प्रसादक f. (-दिका) Adj.<BR>	 1. Purifying, making pellucid.<BR>	 2. Gladdening,<BR>cheering.<BR>	 3. Courting favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादन|प्रसादनं|प्रसादनः
प्रसादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Boiled-rice.<BR>	 2. Cleaning, freeing from soil or impu-<BR>rities.<BR>	 3. Pleasing, gratifying.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Cheering, soothing.<BR>	 2.<BR>Purifying, rendering clear.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Service.<BR>	 2. Worship.<BR>	 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">Page498-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Purifying.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A Royal tent.<BR> E. प्र before, सद् to go, aff. ल्युट्<BR>fem. aff. टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादपराङ्मुख
प्रसादपराङ्मुख Adj. Not caring for any body's favour.<BR>	 2. Withdrawing<BR>favour from any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादयत्
प्रसादयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Pleasing, propitiating.<BR> E. प्र before, सद<BR>to go, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादस्थ
प्रसादस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Kind, propitious, happy.<BR> E. प्रसाद and<BR>स्थ who or what is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादित
प्रसादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pleased, propitiated.<BR>	 2. Worshipped.<BR>	 3.<BR>Purified, cleansed.<BR> E. प्र before, षद् to go, क्त aff. or प्र + साधि-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादोन्मुख
प्रसादोन्मुख Adj. Disposed to favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधक|प्रसाधकः
प्रसाधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Who or what accomplishes or perfects.<BR>	 2.<BR>Who or what cleanses or purifies.<BR>	 3. A valet-de-chamber.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>1. Wild-rice.<BR>	 2. A dresser, a female attendant, one who decorates<BR>or adorns.<BR> E. प्र before, साध् to accomplish, aff. ण्वुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधन|प्रसाधनं|प्रसाधनः
प्रसाधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Dress, decoration, embellishment.<BR>	 2. Accomplishing,<BR>effecting.<BR>	 3. Arranging.<BR>	 4. Means of decoration, things of orna-<BR>mentation.<BR>	 nf. (-नं-नी) A comb.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A drug, commonly called<BR>Siddhi.<BR> E. प्र before, साध् to accomplish, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनविधि|प्रसाधनविधिः
प्रसाधनविधि m. (-धिः) Decoration, embellishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनविशेष|प्रसाधनविशेषः
प्रसाधनविशेष m. (-षः) The highest decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधिका
प्रसाधिका f. (-का) A female attendant who dresses her mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधित|प्रसाधितः
प्रसाधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ornamented, decorated.<BR>	 2. Accomplished,<BR>completed, done.<BR> E. प्र before, साध् to finish, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाध्य
प्रसाध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Accomplishable, what may be done.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be done for, destroyed.<BR> E. प्र and साध् to accomplish, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसार|प्रसारः
प्रसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Going about, spreading, extending.<BR>	 2. Going to for-<BR>age, spreading over the country for grass and fuel.<BR> E. प्र afar, सृ<BR>to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारण|प्रसारणं
प्रसारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going about, spreading.<BR>	 2. Expanding, extending.<BR>3. Unfolding.<BR>	 4. Surrounding an enemy.<BR>	 5. The dispersion of an<BR>army by detachments for that purpose, or for collecting forage.<BR>6. The change of a semi-vowel into a vowel, (in Gram.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णी) A plant, (Pœderia fœtida.)<BR> E. प्र before, सृ to go, aff. णिच्<BR>ल्युट्; also प्रसरण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारित
प्रसारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stretched, expanded, extended.<BR>	 2. Laidont.<BR>E. प्र before, सृ to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारिन्
प्रसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Going along gently, gliding, flowing,<BR>creeping.<BR>	 2. Spreading, expanding.<BR>	 3. Spreading around or about.<BR>4. Expanded, unfolded.<BR>	 5. Surrounding an enemy.<BR> E. प्र before, सृ<BR>to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाह|प्रसाहः
प्रसाह m. (-हः) Overpowering, defeating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसित|प्रसितं
प्रसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Diligent, attentive, adhering to, or engaged<BR>in.<BR>	 2. Ingrossed by, devoted or attached to.<BR>	 3. Bound, fastened.<BR>4. Longing for, greatly desirous of, (with an inst. or loc.)<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Pus, matter.<BR> E. प्र before, षिञ् to bind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिति|प्रसितिः
प्रसिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Ligament, fetters, binding, tie.<BR>	 2. A net, a snare. E.<BR>प्र before, सिञ to bind, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्ध|प्रसिद्धः
प्रसिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Famous, celebrated.<BR>	 2. Adorned, ornamented.<BR>E. प्र before, सिद्ध accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्धि|प्रसिद्धिः
प्रसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Fame, celebrity, notoriety.<BR>	 2. Ornament, decoration.<BR>3. That which is notorious or known.<BR>	 4. Success, accomplishment.<BR>E. प्र before, सिध् to go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसीदिका
प्रसीदिका f. (-का) A small garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसुप्त
प्रसुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Sleeping, asleep, fast asleep.<BR> E. प्र, सुप्त slept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसुप्ति|प्रसुप्तिः
प्रसुप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Sleepiness.<BR>	 2. Paralysis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसू
प्रसू f. (-सूः)<BR>	 1. A mother.<BR>	 2. A mare.<BR>	 3. A spreading creeper.<BR>	 4. The<BR>plantain. Adj. Bringing forth, bearing.<BR> E. प्र before, सू to bear,<BR>aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूका
प्रसूका f. (-का) A mare.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूत|प्रसूतं|प्रसूतः
प्रसूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Born, engendered.<BR>	 2. Bearing, bringing forth,<BR>delivered.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A flower.<BR>	 2. Any productive source.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>A woman who has borne a child, or one who is recently delivered.<BR>E. प्र before, सू to bear, aff. क्त, fem. aff. टाप्; also प्रसूतिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूति|प्रसूतिः
प्रसूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Bringing forth, (as young.)<BR>	 2. Birth, production.<BR>	 3.<BR>Offspring, children, a son or daughter.<BR>	 4. A mother.<BR>	 5. A producer,<BR>a procreator.<BR>	 6. Calving or laying eggs.<BR> E. प्र before, सू to bear,<BR>aff. क्तिन् or क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिका
प्रसूतिका f. (-का) A woman who has had a child, or one who has been<BR>recently delivered.<BR> E. प्रसूता the same, pleonastic aff. कन्,<BR>fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिज|प्रसूतिजं
प्रसूतिज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Pain, affliction, mental or corporeal.<BR>	 2. Pain resulting<BR>as a necessary consequence of birth.<BR> E. प्रसूति birth, and ज pro-<BR>duced; attending man from birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिवायु|प्रसूतिवायुः
प्रसूतिवायु m. (-युः) Air produced in the womb during travail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसून|प्रसूनं
प्रसून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Born, produced.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A flower, a bud, a blos-<BR>som.<BR>	 2. Fruit.<BR> E. प्र before, सू to bear, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूनेषु|प्रसूनेषुः
प्रसूनेषु m. (-षुः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. प्रसून a flower, and इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृत|प्रसृतं|प्रसृतः
प्रसृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dispersed, extended, spread abroad.<BR>	 2. Stretched.<BR>3. Long, lengthened.<BR>	 4. Modest, humble.<BR>	 5. Swift, quick.<BR>	 6. Gone.<BR>7. Attached to, engaged in, occupied with.<BR>	 8. Appointed.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>The palm of the hand, hollowed as if to hold liquids.<BR>	 f. (-ता) The<BR>leg.<BR>	 mn. (-तः-तं) A measure of two Palās.<BR> E. प्र before, सृ to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृतज|प्रसृतजः
प्रसृतज m. (-जः) A son born in adultery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृति|प्रसृतिः
प्रसृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The palm of the hand stretched out and hollowed.<BR>2. A handful considered as a measure.<BR>	 3. Progress, advance.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, सृ to go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृष्ट
प्रसृष्ट f. (-ष्टा) Adj.<BR>	 1. Hurt, injured.<BR>	 2. Laid aside.<BR> E. प्र + सृज्-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृष्टा
प्रसृष्टा f. (-ष्टा) A finger stretched forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृमर
प्रसृमर f. (-रा) Adj. Dropping, distilling, flowing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेक|प्रसेकः
प्रसेक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>	 2. Dropping, oozing.<BR>	 3. Runn-<BR>ing or watering of the mouth and nose, emission, discharge.<BR>	 4.<BR>Vomiting.<BR> E. प्र before, सिच् to sprinkle, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेदिका
प्रसेदिका f. (-का) A small garden.<BR> E. प्र excellence, सद् to go, aff. ण्वुल्<BR>fem. aff. टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेदिवस्
प्रसेदिवस् mfn. (-वान् दुषी-वस्) Pleased, propitiated, favourable.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, षद् to go, क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेव|प्रसेवः
प्रसेव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Part of a lute: see the next.<BR>	 2. A sack.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>सिव् to tie or sew, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेवक|प्रसेवकः
प्रसेवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A part of a lute, a wooden vessel covered with<BR>leather, placed under the neck to render the sound deeper.<BR>	 2. A<BR>crooked piece of wood at the end of a lute.<BR>	 3. A leathern bottle,<BR>a bag for grain.<BR> E. प्र before, षेव् to serve, aff. क्वुन्; or प्र + सिव-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्दन|प्रस्कंदन|प्रस्कंदनं|प्रस्कन्दनं|प्रस्कन्दनः
प्रस्कन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Purging, diarrhœa.<BR>	 2. Springing across.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR> E. प्र before, स्कन्द् to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्दिका|प्रस्कंदिका
प्रस्कन्दिका f. (-का) Diarrhœa.<BR> E. प्र before, स्कन्द् to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्न|प्रस्कन्नः
प्रस्कन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, dropped.<BR>	 2. Defeated.<BR>	 m. (-न्नः) A<BR>sinner, an outcast, one who has violated the usages of his caste<BR>or order.<BR> E. प्र before, स्कन्द् to go, to drop, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कुन्द|प्रस्कुंद|प्रस्कुंदः|प्रस्कुन्दः
प्रस्कुन्द m. (-न्दः) An alter of a circular shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्खलन|प्रस्खलनं
प्रस्खलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Staggering.<BR>	 2. Tumbling.<BR>	 3. Falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तर|प्रस्तरः
प्रस्तर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A stone or rock.<BR>	 2. A jewel, a precious stone.<BR>	 3. A<BR>couch, made of flowers or grass.<BR>	 4. Any bed or couch.<BR>	 5. A flat, a<BR>level, a surface.<BR>	 6. A tabular form of representing the long and<BR>short vowels of poetical metre.<BR>	 7. Notation of music.<BR>	 8. A hand-<BR>ful or bundle of Kusa grass used at sacrifices.<BR> E. प्र before, स्तृ to<BR>spread, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तरण|प्रस्तरणं
प्रस्तरण mf. (-णः-णा)<BR>	 1. A bed, a couch.<BR>	 2. A seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तार|प्रस्तारः
प्रस्तार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A jungle, a thicket or wood, overgrown with grass.<BR>	 2.<BR>Covering, spreading.<BR>	 3. A bed made with blossoms, leaves, &c.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">Page499-b+ 60</a>]<BR>4. Any bed or couch.<BR>	 5. A flat surface, a plain.<BR>	 6. Representation<BR>of the long and short vowels of a metre and its possible varie-<BR>ties, (in prosody.)<BR> E. प्र before, स्तृ to spread, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्ताव|प्रस्तावः
प्रस्ताव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Opportunity, occasion, season.<BR>	 2. Occasional or intro-<BR>ductory eulogium.<BR>	 3. Subject matter of a composition.<BR>	 4. A chap-<BR>ter, a section.<BR>	 5. Beginning, commencement.<BR>	 6. Mention, allusion.<BR>E. प्र before, स्तु to praise, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावना
प्रस्तावना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Commencement, introduction.<BR>	 2. A dramatic prelude,<BR>an introductory dialogue, usually spoken by the manager and one<BR>of the actors.<BR>	 3. Praising, praise.<BR> E. प्र before, स्तु to praise, aff.<BR>ल्युट्; the commencement of books, &c. being usually the praise<BR>of gods or princes. It is thus defined by Bharata:--“नटी विदूषको<BR>वापि पारिपार्श्विक एव वा । सूत्रधारेण सहिताः संलापं यत्र कुर्वते । आमुखं नाम<BR>तज्ज्ञेयं सैव प्रस्तावना मता ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावयज्ञ|प्रस्तावयज्ञः
प्रस्तावयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A conversation to which each interlocutor contri-<BR>butes his share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावसदृश
प्रस्तावसदृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Suited to the occasion, appropriate, season-<BR>able.<BR> E. प्रस्ताव and सदृश like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावित
प्रस्तावित f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Begun, commenced.<BR>	 2. Mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तिर|प्रस्तिरः
प्रस्तिर m. (-रः) A bed or couch made of blossoms, flowers, leaves, &c.<BR>E. प्र before, स्तृ to spread, aff. अच् and इर substituted, for अर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तीत|प्रस्तीतः
प्रस्तीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Crowded, clustering.<BR>	 2. Sounded, making a<BR>noise.<BR> E. प्र before, स्त्यै to crowed, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तीम
प्रस्तीम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Crowded together, swarming, clustering.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sounded.<BR> E. प्र before, स्त्यै to crowed, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तुत|प्रस्तुतः
प्रस्तुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Said, revealed, propounded, declared.<BR>	 2.<BR>Ready, prepared.<BR>	 3. Praised, panegyrised.<BR>	 4. Accomplished, done.<BR>5. Happened, come to pass.<BR>	 6. Made or consisting of.<BR>	 7. Ap-<BR>proached, proximate.<BR>	 8. Done with effort or energy.<BR>	 9. Expected<BR>desired.<BR>	 10. Begun, commenced.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A subject under discuss-<BR>ion, a matter in hand, (in this sense the word is often used in<BR>the sense of Upameya in rhetorical works.)<BR> E. प्र before, स्तु to<BR>praise, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तुताङ्कुर|प्रस्तुतांकुर|प्रस्तुताङ्कुरः
प्रस्तुताङ्कुर m. (-रः) A figure of speech, (according to some writers,) con-<BR>sisting in the mention of any passing circumstance to indicate<BR>something in the hearer's mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तृत|प्रस्तृतः
प्रस्तृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Spread.<BR>	 2. Disappeared.<BR> E. प्र before, स्तृ to<BR>spread, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थ|प्रस्थः
प्रस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Expanding, spread.<BR>	 2. What stays well, firm,<BR>solid.<BR>	 3. Who goes on a journey or march, &c.<BR>	 m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>measure of quantity, four Kuḍavas, or forty-eight double-hand-<BR>fuls.<BR>	 2. Table land on the top of a mountain.<BR>	 3. A level expanse.<BR>4. A Prastha of any thing, or any thing measuring a Prastha. E.<BR>प्र before, स्था to stand, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थपुष्प|प्रस्थपुष्पः
प्रस्थपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A sort of Tulasi, or basil with small leaves.<BR> E. प्रस्थ the<BR>top of a mountain and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थान|प्रस्थानं
प्रस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going forth, preceeding, departing.<BR>	 2. March of an<BR>assailant.<BR>	 3. March.<BR>	 4. Method, system.<BR>	 5. Dying, death.<BR>	 6. An<BR>inferior kind of drama the personages of which are slaves and<BR>outcasted.<BR> E. प्र away, away from, स्था to stay, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थानविघ्न|प्रस्थानविघ्नः
प्रस्थानविघ्न n. (-घ्नं) Non-attendance at a festival, impeding its taking<BR>place, &c.<BR> E. प्रस्थान proceeding and विघ्न obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थानिक
प्रस्थानिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging or relating to departure.<BR> E. प्रस्थान,<BR>ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थापन|प्रस्थापनं
प्रस्थापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sending away.<BR>	 2. Appointment on an embassy.<BR>	 3.<BR>Proving, establishing.<BR>	 4. Carrying, carrying off cattle, &c.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, स्था to stay, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थापनीय
प्रस्थापनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be sent away.<BR>	 2. To be carried or<BR>driven off.<BR> E. प्र before, स्था to stay, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थापित|प्रस्थापितः
प्रस्थापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sent, dispatched.<BR>	 2. Sent away, dismissed.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">Page500-a+ 60</a>]<BR>3. Established, proved.<BR> E. प्र reverse, स्था to stay, in the causal form,<BR>aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थायिन्
प्रस्थायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Who or what goes, travels marches, &c.<BR>E. प्र before, स्था to stay, णिनि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थित
प्रस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone, departed, set forth, (on a journey, march<BR>&c.)<BR> E. प्र before, स्था to stay, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थिति|प्रस्थितिः
प्रस्थिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Going forth or away.<BR>	 2. Journey.<BR>	 3. March.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, स्था to stay, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्न|प्रस्नः
प्रस्न m. (-स्नः) A vessel for bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नव|प्रस्नवः
प्रस्नव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Flowing, pouring forth.<BR>	 2. A stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नुत
प्रस्नुत f. (-ता) Adj. Dropping, pouring forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नुतस्तनी
प्रस्नुतस्तनी f. (-नी) A woman whose breasts distil milk, (through excess of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नुषा
प्रस्नुषा f. (-षा) The wife of a grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्पन्दन|प्रस्पंदन|प्रस्पंदनं
प्रस्पन्दन n. (-नं) Palpitating, vibrating.<BR> E. प्र + स्पन्द्-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फुट|प्रस्फुटः
प्रस्फुट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Blown, expanded.<BR>	 2. Spread abroad, pub-<BR>lished.<BR>	 3. Evident, clear, manifest.<BR> E. प्र before, स्फुट् to blossom,<BR>क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फुरित
प्रस्फुरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Swollen.<BR>	 2. Budded.<BR>	 3. Quivering, tremb-<BR>ling.<BR> E. प्र before, स्फुर् to expand, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फोटन|प्रस्फोटनं
प्रस्फोटन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A winnowing basket.<BR>	 2. Striking, beating.<BR>	 3. Ex-<BR>panding, budding, opening, blowing.<BR>	 4. Winnowing corn.<BR>	 5. Ripen-<BR>ing, making manifest or apparent.<BR> E. प्र before, स्फुट् to blossom,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्मृति|प्रस्मृतिः
प्रस्मृति f. (-तिः) Forgetfulness, forgetting.<BR> E. प्र privative, स्मृति recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्यन्द|प्रस्यंद|प्रस्यंदः|प्रस्यन्दः
प्रस्यन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Trickling, forth.<BR>	 2. Any thing that exudes, gum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्यन्दन|प्रस्यंदन|प्रस्यंदनं
प्रस्यन्दन n. (-नं) Exuding, trickling forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रंसिन्
प्रस्रंसिन् f. (-नी) Adj. Miscarrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रव|प्रस्रवः
प्रस्रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Trickling forth, oozing out.<BR>	 2. A flow, a stream.<BR>	 3.<BR>Milk flowing from a breast or an udder.<BR>	 4. Urine.<BR>	 m. Plu. Falling<BR>tears: See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रवण|प्रस्रवणं|प्रस्रवणः
प्रस्रवण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A pool of water formed by dripping of springs in<BR>the mountains.<BR>	 2. Dripping or fall of water, cascade, cataract.<BR>	 3.<BR>Washing away of rocks, &c. by the dripping of water.<BR>	 4. Oozing,<BR>leaking, dripping.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Sweat, perspiration.<BR>	 2. Pissing,<BR>urining.<BR>	 3. Flowing of milk from a breast or an udder.<BR>	 4. A<BR>range of mountains in the peninsula; also Malayāvan.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, स्रु to drop, aff. ल्युट्; also प्रश्रवण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्राव|प्रस्रावः
प्रस्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Flowing, dropping.<BR>	 2. Urine.<BR> E. प्र forth, स्रु to ooze,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रुत
प्रस्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Oozed is used, dropped.<BR> E. प्र before, स्रु to drop, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्व
प्रस्व(स्वा)न m. (-नः) A loud noise.<BR> E. प्र before, स्वन् to sound, aff. अप् or<BR>घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वाप|प्रस्वापः
प्रस्वाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Sleep.<BR>	 2. A missile which brings on sleep.<BR>	 3. A dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वापन|प्रस्वापनं
प्रस्वापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Causing sleep, inducing sleep.<BR>	 2. A missile which<BR>sends the person attacked to sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्विन्न
प्रस्विन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Perspiring, covered with perspiration.<BR>	 2.<BR>Heated, sweated.<BR> E. प्र before, स्विद् to sweat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वेद|प्रस्वेदः
प्रस्वेद m. (-दः) Great or excessive perspiration.<BR> E. प्र intensitive,<BR>स्वेद sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वेदित
प्रस्वेदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Perspiring, sweating.<BR>	 2. Heated, sweated.<BR>	 3.<BR>Hot, causing perspiration.<BR> E. प्र before, ष्विद् to sweat, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वेदितवत्
प्रस्वेदितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत) Suffering or producing perspiration. E.<BR>प्र before, ष्विद् to sweat, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहणन|प्रहणनं
प्रहणन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहनेमि|प्रहनेमिः
प्रहनेमि m. (-मिः) The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहत|प्रहतं
प्रहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Struck, wounded, killed.<BR>	 2. Repelled, repulsed,<BR>overcome, defeated.<BR>	 3. Spread, expanded.<BR>	 4. Contiguous, bound-<BR>ing, limitative.<BR>	 5. Learned, accomplished.<BR>	 6. Beaten, frequented,<BR>(as a path).<BR>	 7. Beaten, (as a drum).<BR> E. प्र again and हत struck,<BR>injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर|प्रहरः
प्रहर m. (-रः) A watch, an 8th part of the day, or a division compri-<BR>sing about three hours.<BR> E. प्र before, ह to take, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरक|प्रहरकः
प्रहरक m. (-कः) A watch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरण|प्रहरणं
प्रहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A weapon.<BR>	 2. A covered car, a litter for women or any<BR>litter or small covered car for diversion.<BR>	 3. War, battle.<BR>	 4. Strik-<BR>ing, killing.<BR>	 5. Assailing, attacking.<BR>	 6. Removing, expelling.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, हृ to take, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरणकलिका
प्रहरणकलिका f. (-का) A species of the Sarkari metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरणीय|प्रहरणीयं
प्रहरणीय n. (-यं) A weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरिन्
प्रहरिन् m. (-री) A watchman, a bellman.<BR> E. प्रहर a watch, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरिष्यत्
प्रहरिष्यत् mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्) Taking, intending or wishing to take. E.<BR>प्र, हृ to take, with a future sense, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्त्तृ|प्रहर्तृ
प्रहर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>	 1. Striking, a striker, a combatant.<BR>	 2. Fighting.<BR>3. Shooting.<BR> E. प्र before, हृ to take, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्ष|प्रहर्षः
प्रहर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Delight, joy, rapture, exultation.<BR>	 2. Erection of the<BR>male organ.<BR> E. प्र before, हृष् to rejoice, णिच्-ल्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षण|प्रहर्षणं|प्रहर्षणः
प्रहर्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Happy, delighted.<BR>	 2. Delighting.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>The planet Mercury, or its ruler.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Turmeric.<BR>	 2. A form<BR>of metre.<BR> E. प्र before, हृ to rejoice, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षुल|प्रहर्षुलः
प्रहर्षुल m. (-लः) The planet mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षिणी
प्रहर्षिणी f. (-णी) A species of the Atijagati metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षित
प्रहर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Delighted, very happy.<BR> E. प्र before, हृष् to rejoice, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसत्|प्रहसन्त्
प्रहसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्) Laughing, laughing heartily.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती) Ara-<BR>bian jasmine.<BR> E. प्र before, हस् to smile, aff. शतृ, fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसन|प्रहसनं
प्रहसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Loud, violent or hearty laughter.<BR>	 2. Mirth, merri-<BR>ment.<BR>	 3. Sarcasm, satire, as a branch of rhetorical composition.<BR>	 4.<BR>Reproof, ridicule, irony.<BR>	 5. A farce, a comedy. It is thus defined<BR>in Sāhitya Darpana:--भाणवत् सन्धिसन्ध्यङ्गलास्याङ्गाङ्कैर्विनिर्मितम् । भवेत्<BR>प्रहसनं वृतं निन्द्यानां कविकल्पितम् ।<BR> E. प्र before, हस् to laugh,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसन्ती|प्रहसंती
प्रहसन्ती f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A kind of Jasmine.<BR>	 2. A large fire-pan.<BR> E. प्र + हस्-<BR>शतृ-ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसित
प्रहसित n. (-तं) Laughter, mirth.<BR> E. प्र and हस् to laugh, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहस्त|प्रहस्तः
प्रहस्त m. (-स्तः)<BR>	 1. The oped hand with the fingers extended.<BR>	 2. Name<BR>of one of the generals of Rāvana.<BR> E. प्र exchanging, हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहाण|प्रहाणं
प्रहाण n. (-णं) Abandoning, omitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहाणि|प्रहाणिः
प्रहाणि f. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. Abandoning.<BR>	 2. Want, deficiency.<BR> E. प्र + हा-णि-णत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहापण
प्रहापण n. (-णं) Driving away, forced abandonment or departure.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, हा to quit, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहार|प्रहारः
प्रहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Striking.<BR>	 2. Wounding, killing.<BR>	 3. A blow, a knock,<BR>a stroke.<BR>	 4. A cut, a thrust.<BR>	 5. A kick.<BR>	 6. Suiting, fitting.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, हृ to take, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारण|प्रहारणं
प्रहारण n. (-णं) A desirable gift.<BR> E. प्र before, हृ to take, aff. ल्युट्; also प्रवारण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारार्त्त|प्रहारार्त
प्रहारार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Bruised, wounded, hurt by a blow.<BR>	 n. (-र्त्त)<BR>Lasting and acute pain from a wound or maim.<BR> E. प्रहार striking,<BR>and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहास|प्रहासः
प्रहास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Loud laughter.<BR>	 2. Ridicule, derision.<BR>	 3. Irony.<BR>	 4.<BR>Blowing, (as a flower).<BR>	 5. Sīva.<BR>	 6. An actor, a dancer.<BR>	 7. A place<BR>of pilgrimage; also सोमतीर्थ.<BR> E. प्र before, हस् to laugh, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहासिन्
प्रहासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>	 1. Laughing aloud.<BR>	 3. Diverting or causing<BR>laughter.<BR>	 m. (-सी) A jester, a Buffoon, a clown.<BR> E. प्र before, हस् to<BR>laugh, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहि|प्रहिः
प्रहि m. (-हिः) A well.<BR> E. प्र before, हृ to take, unādi aff. इन्, and the<BR>final of the radical rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहित|प्रहितं
प्रहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sent, dispatched.<BR>	 2. Appointed, commissioned.<BR>3. Stretched out, extended.<BR>	 4. Placed.<BR>	 5. Discharged as an arrow<BR>from a bow.<BR>	 6. Learned.<BR>	 7. Suitable, appropriate.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Sauce,<BR>gravy, condiment.<BR> E. प्र before, हित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहीण|प्रहीणः
प्रहीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Left, abandoned.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Removal, loss, waste,<BR>destruction.<BR> E. प्र before, हा to quit, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहीणजीवित
प्रहीणजीवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dead, slain.<BR> E. प्रहीण and जीवित life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहुत|प्रहुतं|प्रहुतः
प्रहुत n. (-तं) Offering articles of food to spirits or goblins.<BR> E. प्र well, हु<BR>to offer in oblation, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृत
प्रहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seized.<BR>	 2. Struck, beaten, wounded.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Striking, killing.<BR>	 2. A stroke, a blow.<BR> E. प्र and हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्ट
प्रहृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Pleased, delighted.<BR>	 2. Bristling.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>हृष् to be pleased, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्टक|प्रहृष्टकः
प्रहृष्टक m. (-कः) A crow.<BR> E. प्र before, हृष्ट pleased, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेणक|प्रहेणकं
प्रहेणक n. (-कं) Victuals or sweetmeats, &c. distributed at festivals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलक|प्रहेलकं|प्रहेलकः
प्रहेलक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A riddle, an enigma, a puzzling question.<BR>	 2. A kind<BR>of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेला
प्रहेला f. (-ला) Playful dalliance, loose-behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलि|प्रहेलिः
प्रहेलि f. (-लिः) A poetic riddle.: See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलिका
प्रहेलिका f. (-का) An enigma, a riddle, a puzzling or enigmatical ques-<BR>tion.<BR> E. प्र before, हिल् to play and इन्-संज्ञायां कन् aff.<BR>It is thus defined in Vāchaspatya.<BR>“व्यक्तीकृत्य कमप्यर्थं स्वरूपार्थस्य गोपनात् ।<BR>यत्र बाह्यान्तरावर्थौ कथ्यते सा प्रहेलिका ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्राद|प्रह्रादः
प्रह्राद m. (-दः) A prince: see प्रह्लाद.<BR> E. ल changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लत्ति|प्रह्लत्तिः
प्रह्लत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Pleasure, happiness.<BR> E. प्र before, ह्लद् to be glad, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लन्न|प्रह्लन्नः
प्रह्लन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Pleased, happy, glad.<BR> E. प्र before, ह्लाद् to be<BR>happy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लन्नि|प्रह्लन्निः
प्रह्लन्नि f. (-न्निः) Pleasure, delight.<BR> E. प्र before, ह्लद् to be happy, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लाद|प्रह्लादः
प्रह्लाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Pleasure, joy, happiness.<BR>	 2. Sound, noise.<BR>	 3. The<BR>name of HIRAṆYĀKSHA'S PIOUS son and regent of one division<BR>of Pātāla.<BR> E. प्र before, ह्लाद gladness or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लादित
प्रह्लादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rejoiced, delighted.<BR> E. प्रह्लाद to be<BR>happy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्व|प्रह्वः
प्रह्व mfn. (-ह्वः-ह्वा-ह्वं)<BR>	 1. Bowed, bent, stooping.<BR>	 2. Intent upon, engaged<BR>in, engrossed by.<BR>	 3. Sloping, slanting, inclining.<BR>	 4. Submissive,<BR>humble.<BR> E. प्र before, ह्वेञ् to call, Unādi aff. वन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वलिका
प्रह्वलिका f. (-का) See प्रहेलिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वाञ्जलि|प्रह्वांजलि
प्रह्वाञ्जलि mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि) Stooping or bowing with the palm of the<BR>hands joined, and put to the forehead in taken of respect.<BR> E. प्रह्व,<BR>and अञ्जलि salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वाय|प्रह्वायः
प्रह्वाय m. (-यः) Calling, summoning, invocation.<BR> E. प्र before, ह्वे to call, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वीकृत
प्रह्वीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Conquered, won, subjected.<BR>	 2. Bent, bowed.<BR>E. प्रह्व, and कृत made, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रा
प्रा r. 2nd cl. (प्राति) To fill. अदा० पर० सक० अनिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांशु|प्रांशुः
प्रांशु mfn. (-शुः-शुः-शु)<BR>	 1. High, tall, lofty.<BR>	 2. A tall man, a man of<BR>great stature.<BR> E. प्र before, अंशु a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्
प्राक् Ind.<BR>	 1. Before, already, prior, preceding, in place or time.<BR>	 2. In<BR>front of.<BR>	 3. As for as, up to.<BR>	 4. Previously.<BR>	 5. East, eastern.<BR>	 6.<BR>Past, gone.<BR>	 7. First.<BR>	 8. Between, amongst, amidst.<BR>	 9. At dawn,<BR>early in the morning. E. See प्राच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकट्य|प्राकट्यं
प्राकट्य n. (-ठ्यं) Publicity, notoriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकरणिक
प्राकरणिक f. (-की) Belonging to the subject under discussion, relevant<BR>to the matter in hand; (the word is sometimes used in the sense<BR>of upameya in rhetorical works).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकर्षिक
प्राकर्षिक f. (-की) Deserving preference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकषिक|प्राकषिकः
प्राकषिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A catamite.<BR>	 2. A dancer, but especially one who<BR>employs or hires the wives of others.<BR>	 3. One who gets his livelihood<BR>by another man's wife.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् prefixed to कष् to go,<BR>Unādi aff. किकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाम्य|प्राकाम्यं
प्राकाम्य n. (-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Irresistible will or fiat, one of the ŚIVA'S eight<BR>attributes.<BR>	 2. Wilfulness, following or obeying one's own will or<BR>inclination.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before, कम् to desire, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकार|प्राकारः
प्राकार m. (-रः) An inclosure, a fence, a rampart, particularly a sur-<BR>rounding wall, &c. elevated on a mound of earth.<BR> E. प्र and आङ्<BR>implying initial, first, कृ to make, aff. घञ्; otherwise the prefix<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">Page501-b+ 60</a>]<BR>is considered as प्र only, the vowel being made long by the affix<BR>being घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकारीय
प्राकारीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Walled, enclosed by a wall.<BR>	 2. Of, belonging<BR>to, or fit for wall.<BR> E. प्राकार and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाश्य|प्राकाश्यं
प्राकाश्य n. (-श्यं)<BR>	 1. Publicity.<BR>	 2. Fame, renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृत|प्राकृतः
प्राकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Low, common, vulgar, thence especially appli-<BR>cable to a provincial and peculiar dialect of the Sanskrit language.<BR>2. Natural.<BR>	 3. Belonging to or derived from the philosophical Pra-<BR>kritī, illusory, material, &c.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A low man or one following<BR>a degraded profession.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Any dialect not Sanskrit, it is espe-<BR>cially spoken by the female characters and the inferior personages<BR>of plays,<BR> E. प्रकृति nature, and अण् aff., or प्र pre-eminently and<BR>अकृत not made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतज्वर|प्राकृतज्वरः
प्राकृतज्वर m. (-रः) Common or usual fever, occurring from the affections<BR>of the wind, bile, and phlegm severally, in as many seasons, or<BR>the rains, autumn and spring.<BR> E. प्राकृत and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतप्रलय|प्राकृतप्रलयः
प्राकृतप्रलय m. (-यः) The total dissolution of the world.<BR> E. प्राकृत material,<BR>and प्रलय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतमानुष|प्राकृतमानुषः
प्राकृतमानुष m. (-षः) A man in general.<BR> E. प्राकृत, and मानुष man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतमित्र|प्राकृतमित्रं
प्राकृतमित्र m. (-त्रः) A natural friend or ally; as applied to a sovereign,<BR>it means one whose states are removed by an intervening kingdom<BR>from those to which it should be friendly, the प्राकृतारि or natural<BR>enemy is the chief of the intervening state, and the प्राकृतोदासीनः<BR>or natural neutral is the outer one of the four.<BR> E. प्राकृत natural,<BR>and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतारि|प्राकृतारिः
प्राकृतारि m. (-रिः) A natural enemy or the sovereign of an adjacent country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतिक|प्राकृतिकः
प्राकृतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging or relating to Prakritī, nature<BR>or matter, material, natural, illusory, &c.<BR> E. प्रकृति, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्काल|प्राक्कालः
प्राक्काल n. (-लं) Former age or time.<BR> E. प्राच् and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्कालीन
प्राक्कालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Anterior, ancient, of a former time.<BR> E. प्राक्काल and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्कूल
प्राक्कूल m. (-लः) The tip of Kusa grass placed to the east.<BR> E. प्राक्<BR>and कूल point of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तन|प्राक्तनः
प्राक्तन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Old, ancient.<BR>	 2. Prior, anterior, preceding,<BR>former.<BR> E. प्राक् formerly, ठ्युल् aff. and तन् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तनकर्म्मन्|प्राक्तनकर्मन्
प्राक्तनकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Fate, destiny.<BR>	 2. Any act formerly done.<BR> E. प्राक्तन<BR>prior, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्फल|प्राक्फलः
प्राक्फल m. (-लः) The bread-fruit-tree.<BR> E. प्राक् before, (flower,) and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्फल्गुनी
प्राक्फल्गुनी f. (-नी) The eleventh of the lunar asterisms: see पूर्व्वफल्गुनी.<BR>E. प्राक् preceding, and फल्गुनी the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्फल्गुनीभव|प्राक्फल्गुनीभवः
प्राक्फल्गुनीभव m. (-वः) A name of VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. प्राक्फल्गुनी and भव<BR>born, when the moon was in that mansion; also similar com-<BR>pounds as प्राक्फाल्गुनीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्फाल्गुन|प्राक्फाल्गुनः
प्राक्फाल्गुन m. (-नः) VṚHASPATI.<BR> E. प्राक्फल्गुनी, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्शिरस
प्राक्शिरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Facing the east.<BR>	 2. Having the head to<BR>the east in burial.<BR> E. प्राच्, and शिरस् the head, मच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्सन्ध्या|प्राक्संध्या
प्राक्सन्ध्या f. (-न्ध्या) Dawn.<BR> E. प्राक् the first, सन्ध्या junction of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राखर्य्य|प्राखर्य|प्राखर्यं|प्राखर्य्यं
प्राखर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Sharpness.<BR>	 2. Pungency.<BR>	 3. Wickedness.<BR> E. प्रखर<BR>and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागग्र
प्रागग्र Adj. Having the point turned towards the east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागभाव|प्रागभावः
प्रागभाव m. (-वः) Antecedent privation, the nonexistence of any thing<BR>which may yet be. In law, the non-possession of property that<BR>may be possessed.<BR> E. प्राक् prior, अ negative and भाव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागल्भ्य|प्रागल्भ्यं
प्रागल्भ्य n. (-ल्भ्यं)<BR>	 1. Confidence, boldness, determination.<BR>	 2. Arrogance,<BR>effrontery.<BR>	 3. Importance, rank.<BR> E. प्रगल्भ confident, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागार|प्रागारः
प्रागार m. (-रः) A house, a building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागुदीची
प्रागुदीची f. (-ची) The north-east.<BR> E. प्राक् the east, and उदीची the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्गामिन्
प्राग्गामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Going before, a precursor.<BR> E. प्राच् and<BR>गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्ज्योतिष|प्राग्ज्योतिषः
प्राग्ज्योतिष m. (-षः) A country, Kāmarupa, part of Assām.<BR> E. प्राक् for-<BR>merly, ज्योतिष light; being the scene of BRAHMĀ'S penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्भार|प्राग्भारः
प्राग्भार m. (-रः) The top or peak of a mountain.<BR> E. प्राक् first, भार bur-<BR>then; also read प्राग्भाव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्भाव|प्राग्भावः
प्राग्भाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Prior existence.<BR>	 2. Superiority, excellence.<BR>	 3.<BR>The top of a mountain.<BR> E. प्राक् and भाव being or nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्भावतस्
प्राग्भावतस् Ind. From a prior state of being.<BR> E. प्राग्भाव, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्र|प्राग्रं
प्राग्र n. (-ग्रं) The highest point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्रसर
प्राग्रसर Adj. Foremost, first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्रहर|प्राग्रहरः
प्राग्रहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Chief, principal.<BR> E. प्र, and अग्र first, हर who surpasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्राट|प्राग्राटं|प्राग्राटः
प्राग्राट n. (-टं) Thin curds.<BR> E. प्र before, अग्र the top, and अट what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्र्य|प्राग्र्यं
प्राग्र्य mfn. (-ग्र्यः-ग्र्या-ग्र्यं) Chief, principal.<BR> E. प्र prefixed to अग्र्य chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्व्य
प्राग्व्य f. (-ग्व्या) Adj. Best, chief, most excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्वंश|प्राग्वंशः
प्राग्वंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The room opposite to that which contains the ma-<BR>terials for an oblation, and in which the family and friends of the<BR>sacrificer assemble.<BR>	 2. A former dynasty or race.<BR> E. प्राक् before,<BR>and वंश a race, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघात|प्राघातः
प्राघात m. (-तः) War, battle.<BR> E. प्र before, हन् to kill, aff. घञ्, and the<BR>vowel of the prefix optionally made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघार|प्राघारः
प्राघार m. (-रः) Dropping, oozing, trickling, aspersion, or pouring out<BR>of any oily substance.<BR> E. प्र before, घॄ to sprinkle or drop,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघुण|प्राघुणः
प्राघुण m. (-णः) A guest, a visitor, one demanding hospitality.<BR> E. प्र and<BR>आङ् before, घुण् to turn round, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघुण|प्राघुणः
प्राघुण(णि)क m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A guest.<BR> E. प्रघुण स्वार्थें ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघूर्णिक|प्राघूर्णिकः
प्राघूर्णिक m. (-कः) A guest.<BR> E. प्र before, घूर्ण going about, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राङ्ग|प्रांग|प्रांगं|प्राङ्गः
प्राङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A sort of small tabor or drum.<BR> E. प्र before, अञ्ज् to go or<BR>be, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राङ्गण|प्रांगण|प्रांगणं|प्राङ्गणं
प्राङ्गण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A sort of drum.<BR>	 2. A court, a yard.<BR>	 3. A hall, a floor.<BR>E. प्र before, अगि to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राङ्न्याय|प्राङ्न्यायः
प्राङ्न्याय m. (-यः) Plea of a former trial, special plea.<BR> E. प्राक् former, न्याय proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राङ्मुख
प्राङ्मुख mfn. (-खः-खा खी-खं) Facing the east.<BR> E. प्राञ्च, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्
प्राच् or प्राञ्च् mfn. (-प्राङ्-प्राची-प्राक्)<BR>	 1. East, eastern.<BR>	 2. Before, in front.<BR>3. Former, prior, first.<BR>	 4. At top, above.<BR>	 m. Plu.<BR>	 1. The people of<BR>the east.<BR>	 2. Grammarians of the eastern school.<BR>	 f. (-ची) The east.<BR>E. प्र before, अन्च to go, aff. क्विप् or ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्च्|प्रांच्
प्राच् or प्राञ्च् mfn. (-प्राङ्-प्राची-प्राक्)<BR>	 1. East, eastern.<BR>	 2. Before, in front.<BR>3. Former, prior, first.<BR>	 4. At top, above.<BR>	 m. Plu.<BR>	 1. The people of<BR>the east.<BR>	 2. Grammarians of the eastern school.<BR>	 f. (-ची) The east.<BR>E. प्र before, अन्च to go, aff. क्विप् or ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचार
प्राचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Contrary to rectitude, deviating from the ordi-<BR>nary institutions and observances.<BR> E. प्र reverse and आचार<BR>ordinance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचार्य्य|प्राचार्य|प्राचार्यः
प्राचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A scholar, a pupil.<BR> E. प्र meaning प्राप्त obtained and आचार्य्य a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचिका
प्राचिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A musquito.<BR>	 2. The female falcon.<BR> E. प्राचिनोति मधु<BR>प्र + आ + चि-ड स्वार्थेकापि अत इत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीन|प्राचीनः
प्राचीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. East, eastern.<BR>	 2. Former, prior, ancient, old.<BR>3. Placed towards the east.<BR>	 fn. (-ना-नं) A bound hedge, a fence, a<BR>wall.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>	 2. The ichneu-<BR>mon plant: see रास्ना.<BR> E. प्राक् the east, aff. ख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनतिलक|प्राचीनतिलकः
प्राचीनतिलक m. (-कः) The moon.<BR> E. प्राचीन eastern, and तिलक mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनपनस|प्राचीनपनसः
प्राचीनपनस m. (-सः) A tree, (Ægle marmelos.) “बिल्वे”<BR> E. प्राचीन eastern,<BR>and पनस the jack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनबर्हिस
प्राचीनबर्हिस m. (-र्हिः)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR> E. प्राचीन eastern,<BR>and वर्हिर्स् light; presiding over the eastern quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनामलक|प्राचीनामलकं
प्राचीनामलक m. (-कः) A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR> E. प्राचीन east-<BR>ern, आमलक myrobalan. “पानीयामलके” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनानीत
प्राचीनानीत n. (-तं) The sacrificial thread, worn over the right arm, and<BR>passing under the left, as at Shrāddhas.<BR> E. प्राचीन east, आनीत<BR>hung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीनावीतिन्
प्राचीनावीतिन् m. (-ती) A Brāhman wearing his cord over his right<BR>shoulder, as at Shrāddhas.<BR> E. प्राचीनावीत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीपति|प्राचीपतिः
प्राचीपति m. (-तिः) A name of Indra.<BR> E. प्राची the east, and पति master, regent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीर|प्राचीरं
प्राचीर n. (-रं) A bound hedge, a fence, a wall, an inclosure, a rampart.<BR>E. प्र and आङ् prefixed to चि to collect, aff. क्रन्, and the radical<BR>vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचेतस|प्राचेतसः
प्राचेतस m. (-सः) VĀLMĪKI, the author of the Rāmāyana.<BR>	 m. Plu. (-साः)<BR>The ten sons of Prachinavarhi.<BR> E. प्रचेतस् the father of the poet,<BR>and अण् aff.; it also occurs प्राचेतस् m. (-ताः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्य|प्राच्यः
प्राच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) Eastern, easterly.<BR>	 m. (-च्यः) The eastern country,<BR>the country south or east of the SARASWATĪ, which flows from the<BR>north-east to the south-west.<BR> E. प्राच् the east, aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्छ्|प्राछ्
प्राच्छ् m. (-प्राट्) An inquirer, a questioner.<BR> E. प्रच्छ् to ask, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजक|प्राजकः
प्राजक m. (-कः) A coachman, a driver.<BR> E. प्र before, अज् to go, causal<BR>form, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजन|प्राजनं|प्राजनः
प्राजन n. (-नं) A goad.<BR> E. प्र before, अज् to go, in the causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजापत्य|प्राजापत्यं|प्राजापत्यः
प्राजापत्य m. (-त्यः)<BR>	 1. A form of marriage, the gift of a girl, respectfully<BR>by her father to her lover.<BR>	 2. A name of Allāhābād or Prayāga.<BR>3. The first of the persons, called Vāsudevas, by the Jainas.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-त्यं)<BR>	 1. A sort of penance, eating once a day for three days in<BR>the morning, once in the night for three days subsisting, three<BR>days on food given as alms, and fasting three days more.<BR>	 2.<BR>A particular sacrifice performed before appointing a daughter to<BR>raise issue in default of male heirs.<BR>	 3. The asterism Rohīnī.<BR>	 f.<BR>(त्या) Giving away the whole of one's property before entering up-<BR>on the life of an ascetic or mendicant.<BR> E. प्रजापति BRAMHA,<BR>and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजितृ
प्राजितृ m. (-ता) A coachman, a charioteer.<BR> E. प्र before, अज् to go, causal, v., तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञ|प्राज्ञः
प्राज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Patient in investigation.<BR>	 2. Wise, clever, sen-<BR>sible.<BR>	 m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. A Pandit, a learned or wise man.<BR>	 2. A skilful or<BR>clever person.<BR>	 f. (-ज्ञा) Knowledge, understanding.<BR>	 f. (-ज्ञा-ज्ञी) A<BR>clever or intelligent woman.<BR>	 f. (-ज्ञी) The wife of a Pandit.<BR> E. प्र<BR>and आङ् before, ज्ञा to know, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञत्व
प्राज्ञत्व n. (-त्वं) Learning, wisdom.<BR> E. प्राज्ञ and त्व aff.; also with तल् प्राज्ञता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञमान|प्राज्ञमानः
प्राज्ञमान n. (-नं) Respect for learned men.<BR> E. प्राज्ञ, and मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञमानिन्
प्राज्ञमानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Respecting men of learning.<BR> E. प्राज्ञमान,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्य|प्राज्यं
प्राज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) Much, many.<BR> E. प्र before, अन्ज to pervade, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जल|प्रांजल|प्राञ्जलः
प्राञ्जल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Honest, upright, sincere.<BR> E. प्र before, अन्ज to<BR>go, aff. अलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राञ्जलि|प्रांजलि
प्राञ्जलि f. (-लिः) Putting the hands together to the forehead as a mark<BR>of respect.<BR> E. प्र and अञ्जलि the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राड्विवाक|प्राड्विवाकः
प्राड्विवाक m. (-कः) A judge, a magistrate.<BR> E. प्राट् who asks, and विवाक<BR>who decides or discriminates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राण|प्राणः
प्राण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Full, replete, filled.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Air inhaled, ins-<BR>piration, breath.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>	 3. Life, vitality.<BR>	 4. A vital organ<BR>or part.<BR>	 5. Strength, power.<BR>	 6. Myrrh.<BR>	 7. Poetical talent or ins-<BR>piration.<BR>	 8. A name of BRAMHĀ.<BR>	 9. A title of BRAMHĀ, the Su-<BR>preme spirit.<BR>	 10. An aspiration in the articulation of letters.<BR>	 m.<BR>plu. (-णाः) The five vital airs or modes of inspiration and expira-<BR>tion collectively.<BR> E. प्र before, अन् to breathe, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणक|प्राणकः
प्राणक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An animal or sentient being.<BR>	 2. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 3. A<BR>plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR> E. प्राण life, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणकर्म्मन्|प्राणकर्मन्
प्राणकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Vital action.<BR> E. प्राण and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणत्|प्राणन्त्
प्राणत् mfn. (-णन्-णन्ती-णत्) Living, breathing.<BR> E. प्राण nominal v., to<BR>live, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणत्यान
प्राणत्यान m. (-गः) Abandoning life, dying, suicide.<BR> E. प्राण and त्याग<BR>relinquishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणथ|प्राणथः
प्राणथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A strong or powerful man.<BR>	 3. A pro-<BR>genitor of mankind.<BR>	 4. A place of pilgrimage.<BR> E. प्र before, अन् to<BR>breathe or be strong, Unādi aff. अथ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणद|प्राणदं|प्राणदः
प्राणद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Who or what gives life.<BR>	 n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2.<BR>Blood.<BR> E. प्राण life and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणधारण
प्राणधारण n. (-णं) Sustenance, supporting life.<BR> E. प्राण and धारण upholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणन|प्राणनं|प्राणनः
प्राणन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Life, living.<BR>	 2. The throat.<BR> E. प्र before, अन् to live or<BR>breathe, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणनाथ|प्राणनाथः
प्राणनाथ m. (-थः) A husband.<BR> E. प्राण life and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणन्त|प्राणंत|प्राणंतः|प्राणन्तः
प्राणन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A sort of collyrium: see रसाञ्जन.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-न्ती)<BR>	 1. Sneezing.<BR>	 2. Hic-cough.<BR> E. प्र before, अन् to breathe, Unādi<BR>aff. झच्, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणपरिग्रह|प्राणपरिग्रहः
प्राणपरिग्रह m. (-हः) Life, existence.<BR> E. प्राण and परिग्रह possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणप्रद
प्राणप्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Saving life, when in imminent danger.<BR> E. प्राण<BR>and प्रद who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणप्रदा
प्राणप्रदा f. (-दा) A medicinal plant, commonly called Riddhi.<BR> E. प्राण<BR>life, प्रद what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणबाध
प्राणबाध m. (-धः) Extreme peril or distress, fear for life.<BR> E. प्राण, and बाध obstruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणभात्वत्
प्राणभात्वत् m. (-स्वान्) The ocean.<BR> E. प्राण life, भास्वत् the sun, the sun be-<BR>ing produced or rising from the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणभृत्
प्राणभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Living, sentient.<BR> E. प्राण, and भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणमय
प्राणमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Living, breathing, endowed with breath or life.<BR>E. प्राण and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणमयकोष|प्राणमयकोषः
प्राणमयकोष m. (-षः) One of the cases or investitures of the soul, the<BR>vital or organic case.<BR> E. प्राणमय and कोष a sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणयत्
प्राणयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Rescuing, restoring to life.<BR> E. प्राण, nom. v.<BR>caus. form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणयात्रा
प्राणयात्रा f. (-त्रा) Support of life, subsistence.<BR> E. प्राण, यात्रा proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणव्यय|प्राणव्ययः
प्राणव्यय m. (-यः) Death, expenditure of life.<BR> E. प्राण, and व्यय expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणसंयम|प्राणसंयमः
प्राणसंयम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A peculiar religious exercise: see “प्राणायाम ।” 2.<BR>Suspending the breath.<BR> E. प्राण breath, सम् before, यम् to res-<BR>train, aff. अञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणसद्मन्
प्राणसद्मन् n. (-द्म) The body.<BR> E. प्राण vital air and सद्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणसमा
प्राणसमा f. (-मा) A wife.<BR> E. प्राण life, समा equal to, same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणहर
प्राणहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Destructive, taking away life.<BR> E. प्राण and हर<BR>who or what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणहारक|प्राणहारकं
प्राणहारक n. (-कं) Aconite.<BR> E. प्राण and हारक what takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणहारिन्
प्राणहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Mortal, deadly.<BR> E. प्राण, and हारिन् what<BR>takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणाद
प्राणाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Fatal, deadly.<BR> E. प्राण and अद what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणाधिनाथ|प्राणाधिनाथः
प्राणाधिनाथ m. (-थः) A husband.<BR> E. प्राण life, अधि over, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणान्त|प्राणांत|प्राणान्तः
प्राणान्त n. (-न्तं) Death.<BR> E. प्राण and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणान्तिक|प्राणांतिक
प्राणान्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Fatal, destructive of life.<BR>	 2. Capital, (as<BR>punishment.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) Murder, assassination.<BR> E. प्राण and अन्तिक final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणापहारिन्
प्राणापहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Deadly, fatal.<BR> E. प्राण and अपहारिन्<BR>what takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणापान
प्राणापान m. Du. (-नौ)<BR>	 1. The Ashwinī kumāras.<BR>	 2. Two of the vital<BR>airs.<BR> E. प्राण and अपान the air expelled by the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणाबाध|प्राणाबाधः
प्राणाबाध n. (-धं) Any act injurious to life.<BR> E. प्राण and आङ् before,<BR>बाध् to pain, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणायाम|प्राणायामः
प्राणायाम m. (-मः) Breathing in a peculiar way through the nostrils,<BR>during the mental recitation of the names or attributes of some<BR>deity; it is differently performed. the Vaidikas or followers<BR>of the Veda close the right nostril first with the thumb, and in-<BR>hale breath through the left, then they close both nostrils, and<BR>finally open the right for exhalation; the followers of the Tantras<BR>close the left nostril first, and exhale also through it; these<BR>operations are severally called पूरक, कुम्भक and रेचक<BR> E. प्राण breath,<BR>आ before, यम् to restrain, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिनिषु
प्राणिनिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing for life.<BR> E. प्राण nom. v., desid, form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिद्यूत|प्राणिद्यूतं
प्राणिद्यूत n. (-तं) Cock-fighting, ram-fighting, setting animals to fight<BR>for wagers.<BR> E. प्राणि a living being and द्यूत gaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिन्
प्राणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि) Living, breathing.<BR>	 m. (-णी) An animal, a<BR>sentient or living being.<BR> E. प्राण vital air, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिपीडा
प्राणिपीडा f. (-डा) Cruelty to animals. प्राणिन् and पीडा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिमाता
प्राणिमाता f. (-ता) A mother.<BR> E. प्राणिन् and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिहिंसा
प्राणिहिंसा f. (-सा) Doing harm to any living creature.<BR> E. प्राणि, and<BR>हिंसा injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिहित
प्राणिहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Favourable or good for living beings.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>A shoe, a boot.<BR> E. प्राणि an animal, (man,) and हित suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणीत्य|प्राणीत्यं
प्राणीत्य n. (-त्य) Debt.<BR> E. प्राणीत taken, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणेश|प्राणेशः
प्राणेश m. (-शः) A husband.<BR>	 f. (-शा) A wife.<BR> E. प्राण life, ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राण्यङ्ग|प्राण्यंग
प्राण्यङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Any animal part or product, (as flesh, bone, milk,<BR>Ghee, &c.)<BR> E. प्राणिन्, and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातःकृत्य|प्रातःकृत्यं
प्रातःकृत्य n. (-त्यं) Morning duty or ceremonies, worship, ablution, puri-<BR>fication, &c.<BR> E. प्रातर्, and कृत्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातःसन्ध्या|प्रातःसंध्या
प्रातःसन्ध्या f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>	 1. Dawn.<BR>	 2. The morning-sacrifice.<BR> E. प्रातः and सन्ध्या part of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातःसमय|प्रातःसमयः
प्रातःसमय m. (-यः) Early morning, day-break.<BR> E. प्रातर and समय season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातःस्नान|प्रातःस्नानं
प्रातःस्नान n. (-नं) Morning ablution, bathing at sunrise.<BR> E. प्रावर् and<BR>लान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्
प्रातर् Ind. Morning, dawn.<BR> E. प्र initial, अत् to go, अरु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातराश|प्रातराशः
प्रातराश m. (-शः) The morning meal, breakfast.<BR> E. प्रातर morning, अश्<BR>to eat, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातराशित
प्रातराशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Breakfasted, having had the morning meal. E.<BR>प्रातर् and आशित eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्गेय|प्रातर्गेयः
प्रातर्गेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be sang or chanted in the morning.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>A minstrel a bard, but one who especially wakes the sovereign or<BR>prince by his morning chant.<BR> E. प्रातर् in the morning, गेय<BR>to be sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्भोक्तृ
प्रातर्भोक्तृ mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ) Who or what eats early.<BR>	 m. (-क्ता) A crow. E.<BR>प्रातर् morning, and भोक्तृ who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्भोजन|प्रातर्भोजनं
प्रातर्भोजन n. (-नं) Breakfast the, morning-meal.<BR> E. प्रातर् morning, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राति|प्रातिः
प्राति f. (-तिः) The span of the thumb and fore-finger.<BR>	 2. Filling 3. Gain-<BR>ing.<BR> E. प्र and भावे क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिका
प्रातिका f. (-का) The China-rose. “जवावृक्षे”<BR> E. प्र + अत-ण्वुल् टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिकूलिक
प्रातिकूलिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Opposed to, opposing.<BR> E. प्रतिकूल and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिकूल्य|प्रातिकूल्यं
प्रातिकूल्य n. (-ल्यं) I. Contrariety, contradiction, opposition.<BR> E. प्रतिकूल<BR>and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिजनीन
प्रातिजनीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fit for or suitable to dependants, family, &c.<BR>E. प्रतिजन, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिज्ञ|प्रातिज्ञं
प्रातिज्ञ n. (-ज्ञं) The topic under discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपक्ष
प्रातिपक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Hostile, belonging to an enemy.<BR>	 2. Ad-<BR>verse, contrary.<BR> E. प्रतिपक्ष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपथिक|प्रातिपथिकः
प्रातिपथिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Hostile, opposing.<BR> E. प्रतिपथ, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपदिक|प्रातिपदिकः
प्रातिपदिक n. (-कं) A crude noun, a noun before any of its inflections are<BR>formed with appropriate affixes.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Fire.<BR> E. प्र and अति before,<BR>पद an inflected word, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभ
प्रातिभ f. (-भी)<BR>	 1. Relating to divination.<BR>	 2. Relating to genius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभाव्य|प्रातिभाव्यं
प्रातिभाव्य n. (-व्यं) Security, the act of becoming bail or surety, or be-<BR>ing answerable for the appearance of the debtor, of his being<BR>trust-worthy, or for the payment of his debt is case of his falling<BR>to do it.<BR> E. प्रतिभू a security, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभासिक
प्रातिभासिक f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Existing only in appearance, (not real)<BR>	 2. Resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिलोम्य|प्रातिलोम्यं
प्रातिलोम्य n. (-म्यं) Inverted order.<BR> E. प्रतिलोम, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेश्य|प्रातिवेश्यः
प्रातिवेश्य m. (-श्यः) A next-door-neighbour.<BR> E. प्रतिवेश, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिशाख्य|प्रातिशाख्यं
प्रातिशाख्य n. (-ख्यं) A grammatical treatise teaching the phonetic<BR>changes that the words in any particular Vedic Shākhā undergo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिस्विक|प्रातिस्विकं
प्रातिस्विक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Own, peculiar, proper.<BR> E. प्रति to or towards,<BR>स्व own, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहर
प्रातिहर m. (-रः) A juggler.<BR> E. प्रतिहार the same, and अण् pleonastic:<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहारक|प्रातिहारकः
प्रातिहारक m. (-कः) A juggler.<BR> E. कन् added to प्रातिहार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहारिक|प्रातिहारिकः
प्रातिहारिक m. (-कः) A juggler, a conjuror.<BR> E. प्रतिहार disguise,<BR>trick, aff. ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीतिक
प्रातीतिक f. (-की) Mental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीप|प्रातीपः
प्रातीप m. (-पः) A name of ŚANTANU.<BR> E. प्रतीप the father of this prince<BR>and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीपिक
प्रातीपिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Reverse, contrary, retrograde.<BR> E. प्रतीप and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्थयिक
प्रात्थयिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Trusty, confidential, having faith in, m. (-कः)<BR>A surety.<BR> E. प्रत्यय and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथमकल्पिक|प्राथमकल्पिकः
प्राथमकल्पिक m. (-कः) A student, one who has just commenced the peru-<BR>sal of the Vedas.<BR> E. प्रथम first, कल्प beginning, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथमिक|प्राथमिकः
प्राथमिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) First, of the first, initial, initiative.<BR> E. प्रथम,<BR>and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथम्य|प्राथम्यं
प्राथम्य n. (-म्यं) Firstness, priority.<BR> E. प्रथम and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादक्षिण्य|प्रादक्षिण्यं
प्रादक्षिण्य n. (-ण्यं) Circumambulation.<BR> E. प्रदक्षिण and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुर्भाव|प्रादुर्भावः
प्रादुर्भाव m. (-वः) Appearance, manifestation.<BR> E. प्रादुस्, and भाव quality,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुष्कृत
प्रादुष्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Manifested, made apparent.<BR> E. प्रादुस् and<BR>कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुस्
प्रादुस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Evidently, apparently, manifestly.<BR>	 2. Visible, apparent.<BR>3. Name, appellation.<BR>	 4. Existence.<BR>	 5. Co-existence.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>अद् to go, or eat, Unādi aff. उसि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेश|प्रादेशः
प्रादेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The span of the thumb and fore-finger.<BR>	 2. Place, coun-<BR>try.<BR> E. प्र before, दिश् to show, aff. घञ्; whence the vowel of the<BR>prefix is optionally made long: see प्रदेश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशन|प्रादेशनं
प्रादेशन n. (-नं) Gift, donation.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before, दिश् to give, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशिक|प्रादेशिकः
प्रादेशिक f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Precedented.<BR>	 2. Limited, local.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The owner<BR>of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादोष|प्रादोषः
प्रादोष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Belonging, or relating to the evening.<BR> E. प्रदोष<BR>evening, aff. अण्; also with ठञ् aff. प्रादोषिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधनिक|प्राधनिकं
प्राधनिक n. (-कं) A destructive weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधानिक
प्राधानिक n. (-की) Most eminent.<BR>	 2. Derived from Pradhāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधान्य|प्राधान्यं
प्राधान्य n. (-न्यं) Supremacy, superiority.<BR> E. प्रधान chief, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधान्यतस्
प्राधान्यतस् Ind. Chiefly.<BR> E. प्राधान्य, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधीत
प्राधीत m. (-तः) A Brāhman who has finished his studies.<BR> E. प्र and अधीत read over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्ययन|प्राध्ययनं
प्राध्ययन n. (-नं) Reading, study,<BR> E. प्र before, अधि to read through,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्व|प्राध्वं|प्राध्वः
प्राध्व mfn. (-ध्वः-ध्वा-ध्वं)<BR>	 1. Distant, remote, long, as a road or journey.<BR>	 2.<BR>Bowed, bent.<BR>	 3. Binding, confining.<BR>	 m. (-ध्वः) A car, a carriage. E.<BR>प्र before, अध्वन् a road, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्वम्
प्राध्वम् Ind.<BR>	 1. In conformity, conformably.<BR>	 2. Crooked, crookedly, stoop-<BR>ing.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before, ध्वन् to sound, aff. डम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्त|प्रांत|प्रांतः|प्रान्तः
प्रान्त m. (-न्तः) Edge, margin, border, end.<BR> E. प्र before, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्ततस्|प्रांततस्
प्रान्ततस् Ind. Bordering, marginally, along or upon the extremity. E.<BR>प्रान्त the edge, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्तदुर्ग|प्रांतदुर्ग
प्रान्तदुर्ग m. (-र्गः) A suburb or collection of houses out of the walls of the<BR>town, a Pettāh, &c.<BR> E. प्रान्त skirting, दुर्ग the fort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्तर|प्रांतर|प्रांतरं|प्रान्तरं
प्रान्तर m. (-रः) A long and unshaded road, a lonesome or tiresome path.<BR>2. A forest.<BR>	 3. The hollow of a tree.<BR> E. प्र considerable, अन्तर space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रान्तरशून्य|प्रांतरशून्य|प्रान्तरशून्यः
प्रान्तरशून्य n. (-न्यं) A long and tiresome road.<BR> E. प्रान्तर spacious, and शून्य<BR>empty, void.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप
प्राप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Watery, abounding with water.<BR> E. प्र and अप water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापक|प्रापकः
प्रापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Procuring causing to obtain.<BR>	 2. Obtaining,<BR>who or what obtains.<BR> E. प्राप् to obtain, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापण|प्रापणं
प्रापण n. (-णं) Obtaining,<BR> E. प्र before, आप् to gain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापणिक|प्रापणिकः
प्रापणिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A trader, a dealer.<BR>	 2. A retail dealer.<BR> E. प्र and आङ्<BR>before, पण् to deal, to transact business, किकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापित
प्रापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Brought, placed.<BR>	 2. Procured.<BR> E. प्र before, आप्<BR>to gain, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्त|प्राप्तः
प्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Obtained, gained, received, procured.<BR>	 2. Fixed,<BR>placed.<BR>	 3. Proper, right.<BR> E. प्र before, आप् to gain, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तकाल|प्राप्तकालः
प्राप्तकाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Fated, destined, one whose fated time<BR>has come.<BR>	 2. Opportune, in season.<BR> E. प्राप्त and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तपञ्चत्व|प्राप्तपंचत्व|प्राप्तपञ्चत्वं
प्राप्तपञ्चत्व mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं) Dead, deceased.<BR> E. प्राप्त obtained, पञ्चत्व death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तबुद्धि
प्राप्तबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>	 1. Enlightened, instructed, intelligent.<BR>	 2.<BR>Recovering, becoming conscious, (after fainting.)<BR> E. प्राप्त and<BR>बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तभार|प्राप्तभारः
प्राप्तभार m. (-रः) A draft ox or beast of burthen.<BR> E. प्राप्त and भार load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तभाव|प्राप्तभावः
प्राप्तभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Wise.<BR>	 2. Handsome.<BR>	 3. Of a good disposi-<BR>tion.<BR>	 m. (-वः) A bullock.<BR> E. प्राप्त gained, भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तरूप|प्राप्तरूपः
प्राप्तरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Learned, wise.<BR>	 2. Handsome, pleasing.<BR> E. प्राप्त<BR>gained or proper, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तार्थ|प्राप्तार्थः
प्राप्तार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Successful, having gained an object.<BR> E. प्राप्त, and<BR>अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तापराध
प्राप्तापराध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Offending, being in fault.<BR> E. प्रात, and अपराध offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तावसर|प्राप्तावसरः
प्राप्तावसर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Opportune, seasonable, taking or finding<BR>occasion.<BR> E. प्राप्त and अवसर opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्ति|प्राप्तिः
प्राप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Gain, profit.<BR>	 2. Acquiring, getting, obtaining.<BR>	 2. Im-<BR>provement, success.<BR>	 4. Rise, ascent.<BR>	 5. Collection, assemblage,<BR>quantity.<BR>	 6. Happy denouement, successful termination of a plot.<BR>7. Guessing, discovering from a hint.<BR>	 8. One of the eight super-<BR>human faculties, the power of obtaining everything.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>आप् to get or obtain, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्य|प्राप्यं
प्राप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Attainable, obtainable,<BR> E. प्र before, आप् to attain,<BR>aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबल्य|प्राबल्यं
प्राबल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Power, vigour.<BR>	 2. Pre-dominance,<BR> E. प्रबल strong, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबोधिक|प्राबोधिकः
प्राबोधिक m. (-कः) Dawn, day-break.<BR> E. प्रबोध waking, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभव|प्राभवं
प्राभव n. (-वं) Superiority, pre-eminence.<BR> E. प्रभु a master, aff. ण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभबन्य
प्राभबन्य n. (-न्यं) Power, authority.<BR> E. प्रभवन being superior, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभृत|प्राभृतं
प्राभृत n. (-तं) A present, an offering to a deity or sovereign, or a gift<BR>to a friend, a bribe, the Nazur of Hindustan.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before,<BR>भृ to nourish, aff. क्त; also with कन् aff. प्राभृतक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाणिक|प्रामाणिकः
प्रामाणिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Exercising or proceeding from some evid-<BR>ence or authority, &c.<BR>	 2. Being of authority.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A presi-<BR>dent, the chief or head of a trade, &c.<BR>	 2. A learned man, one who<BR>supports his arguments by reference to book, &c.<BR> E. प्रमाण testi-<BR>mony, authority, aff, ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाण्य|प्रामाण्यं
प्रामाण्य n. (-ण्यं) Authority, proof.<BR> E. प्रमाण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाद्य|प्रामाद्यं|प्रामाद्यः
प्रामाद्य m. (-द्यः) A tree, (Justicia adhenatoda.)<BR>	 n. (-द्यं) Madness, frenzy,<BR>fury, intoxication.<BR> E. प्र before, मद् to delight, aff. ण्यत् and अच्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामीत्य|प्रामीत्यं
प्रामीत्य n. (-त्यं) Debt.<BR> E. प and आङ् before, मा to measure, क्यप् aff.,<BR>and तुक् aug.; also read प्राणीत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राय|प्रायः
प्राय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Like, resembling, (used in composition.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Exceeding, much.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Fasting to death, as a religious or<BR>penitentiary act, after abandoning all wordly goods and<BR>desires.<BR>	 2. Quantity, abundance.<BR>	 3. Death, dying.<BR>	 4. A state<BR>or condition of life, age, youth, &c.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Sin.<BR> E. प्र before, इन् to<BR>go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायण|प्रायणं
प्रायण n. (-णं) Death, voluntary death.<BR> E. प्र, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायशस्
प्रायशस् Ind. Usually, commonly, for the most part.<BR> E. प्राय, and<BR>शासि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायिक|प्रायिकं
प्रायिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Common, usual.<BR> E. प्राय, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्त|प्रायश्चित्तं
प्रायश्चित्त m. (-त्तः) Expiation, penance.<BR> E. प्राय sin, चित्त or चित्ति reflec-<BR>tion, and सुट् aug.; hence also प्रायश्चित्ति f. (-तिः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्तविधि
प्रायश्चित्तविधि f. (-धि) Rules for penance or expiation.<BR> E. प्रायश्चित्त,<BR>and विधि rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायस्
प्रायस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Frequently, generally, for the most part.<BR>	 2. Abundantly,<BR>largely.<BR> E. प्र before, इण् or अय् to go, aff. अमुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायुधेषिन्
प्रायुधेषिन् m. (-षी) A horse.<BR> E. प्र mostly, आयुध a weapon, इष् to wish,<BR>aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायोपवेशन
प्रायोपवेशन n. (-नं) Fasting to death.<BR> E. प्राय and उपवेशन sitting down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायोपवेशनिका
प्रायोपवेशनिका f. (-का) Sitting down to die by fasting.<BR> E. प्राय, उपवेश sitt-<BR>ing down, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारब्ध|प्रारब्धं
प्रारब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Begun, beginning.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before, रभ् to<BR>begin, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारब्धि|प्रारब्धिः
प्रारब्धि f. (-ब्धिः)<BR>	 1. Beginning, commencement.<BR>	 2. A rope or fastening<BR>for an elephant.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before, रभ् to commence, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारम्भ|प्रारंभ|प्रारंभः|प्रारम्भः
प्रारम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Beginning.<BR>	 2. An undertaking.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before,<BR>रभि to begin, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राराह
प्राराह m. (-हः) A shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्ण|प्रार्णं
प्रार्ण n. (-र्णं) A chief debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्वक
प्रार्वक mfn. (-कः-र्थिका-कं) Asking, an asker, a solicitor.<BR> E. प्र before, अर्थ<BR>to seek, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थन|प्रार्थनं
प्रार्थन nf. (-नं-ना) Asking, begging.<BR> E. ब before, अर्थ to ask, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थना
प्रार्थना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Desire.<BR>	 2. Solicitation.<BR>	 3. Prayer, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थनीय|प्रार्थनीयं
प्रार्थनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be asked or begged.<BR>	 n. (-यं) The third or<BR>Dwāpar age of the world.<BR> E. प्र before, अर्थ to ask, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थयितृ
प्रार्थयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) One who asks or solicits, a beggar, an inquirer,<BR>a solicitor.<BR> E. प्र before, अर्थ to seek, त्तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थित|प्रार्थितः
प्रार्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Asked, begged, solicited.<BR>	 2. Said, spoken.<BR>	 3.<BR>obstructed or opposed by an enemy.<BR>	 4. Killed, hurt.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>अर्थ to ask, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थितवत्
प्रार्थितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वनी-वत्) Asking, begging.<BR> E. प्र before, अर्थ to ask, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालम्ब|प्रालंब|प्रालम्बं|प्रालम्बः
प्रालम्ब n. (-म्बं) A garland hanging round the neck, and reaching to<BR>the breast.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before, लवि to hang or fall, aff. अच्;<BR>also with कन् added प्रालम्बक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालम्बिका|प्रालंबिका
प्रालम्बिका f. (-का) A garland, a golden necklace.<BR> E. प्रालम्ब a garland,<BR>&c. कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेय|प्रालेयं
प्रालेय n. (-यं) Frost.<BR> E. प्र before, लीच् to unite with, aff. अच्; प्रलय here<BR>said to mean a mountain, अण् aff. of derivation, and the penul-<BR>timate vowel changed to ए ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेयांशु|प्रालेयांशुः
प्रालेयांशु m. (-शुः) The moon. E. (प्रालेय) frost or cold, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावट|प्रावटः
प्रावट m. (-टः) Barley.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before, वट् to encompass, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावण|प्रावणं
प्रावण n. (-णं) A spade, a hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावर|प्रावरः
प्रावर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An inclosure, a fence, a hedge.<BR>	 2. An upper garment.<BR>E. प्र and आङ् before, वृ to surround, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावरण|प्रावरणं
प्रावरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. An upper or outer garment.<BR>	 2. Any covering,<BR> E. प्र<BR>and आङ् before, वृ to cover, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावार|प्रावारः
प्रावार m. (-रः) An upper or outer garment, a cloak, a mantle,<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, वृ with आङ् prefix, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावारकीट|प्रावारकीटः
प्रावारकीट m. (-टः) A body louse.<BR> E. प्रावार the outward garment, and कीट and insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावीण्य|प्रावीण्यं
प्रावीण्य m. (-ण्यं) Cleverness, skilfulness.<BR> E. प्रवीण and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावुर्वृषु
प्रावुर्वृषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to wear.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before, वृ to<BR>wear, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृत|प्रावृतं|प्रावृतः
प्रावृत mfn. subst. (-तः-ता-तं) A veil, a wrapper, a cloak or mantle. Adj.<BR>Covered, inclosed, encompassed,<BR> E. प्र before, वृ with आङ् prefix, to<BR>cover, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृति|प्रावृतिः
प्रावृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. An inclosure, a fence, a bound hedge.<BR>	 2. Spiritual<BR>darkness.<BR> E. प्र before, वृ with आङ् prefix, to inclose, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृष्
प्रावृष् f. (-वृट्) The rainy season, monsoon about July and August.<BR>E. प्र before, वृष् to sprinkle, aff. क्विप् and the vowel of the prefix<BR>made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषा
प्रावृषा f. (-षा) The season of the rain.<BR> E. प्रावृष् as above and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषायणी
प्रावृषायणी f. (-णी) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. प्रावृष् the rains,<BR>फक् aff.; growing in the rains. “आल्कुशी” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषिक|प्रावृषिकः
प्रावृषिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Produced, &c. in the rainy season m. (-कः) A<BR>peacock.<BR> E. प्रावृष् the rains. aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषिज|प्रावृषिजः
प्रावृषिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced in the rainy season.<BR> E. प्रावृष् in<BR>the 7th case, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषेण्य|प्रावृषेण्यः
प्रावृषेण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Produced in the rains.<BR>	 2. Much abundant.<BR>m. (-ण्यः)<BR>	 1. The Dhārā-Kadama tree, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>Kutaja tree.<BR> E. प्रावृष् the rains, and एण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेशन
प्रावेशन n. (-नं) A manufactory, a workshop.<BR>	 f. (-नी) To be done on<BR>entering.<BR> E. प्र before, आवेशन entering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशन|प्राशनं
प्राशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Feeding, causing to taste or eat.<BR>	 2. Tasting<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>अश् to eat, intransitive or causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशित|प्राशितं
प्राशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Eaten, devoured.<BR>	 2. Tasted, taken into the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">Page505-b+ 60</a>]<BR>mouth without reaching to the throat.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Oblation to deified<BR>progenitors.<BR> E. प्र before, अशित eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशिव
प्राशिव n. (-त्रं) Any edible article.<BR> E. प्र before, अश् to eat, इत्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्निक|प्राश्निकः
प्राश्निक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An assistant at a spectacle or assembly.<BR>	 2. An in-<BR>quirer, an asker.<BR> E. प्रश्न a question, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्य
प्राश्य Ind. Having tasted or sipped.<BR> E. प्र before, अश् to eat, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास|प्रासः
प्रास m. (-सः) A barbed dart.<BR> E. प्र before, अस् to throw, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासक्क
प्रासक्क m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A die, dice.<BR>	 2. A barbed missile.<BR> E. प्र before, अस् to<BR>throw, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्ग|प्रासंग|प्रासंगः|प्रासङ्गः
प्रासङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A yoke for cattle.<BR> E. प्र and आङ् before, सन्ज to join, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्गिक|प्रासंगिक
प्रासङ्गिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Proceeding from or belonging to any con-<BR>nexion or relation.<BR>	 2. Relevant, belonging to any topic.<BR>	 3. Inher-<BR>ent, innate.<BR>	 4. Inseparably connected with.<BR>	 5. Incidental, episodi-<BR>cal.<BR> E. प्रसङ्ग and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासङ्ग्य|प्रासंग्य|प्रासंग्यः|प्रासङ्ग्यः
प्रासङ्ग्य m. (-ङ्ग्यः) A beast of draught, an ox, yoked or in training E.<BR>प्रासङ्ग a yoke, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासाद|प्रासादः
प्रासाद m. (-दः) A temple a palace, a building consecrated to a deity,<BR>or inhabited by a prince.<BR> E. प्र before, सद् to go, aff. घञ्, and the<BR>vowel of the prefix lengthened, or आङ् prefixed to the verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादकुक्कुट|प्रासादकुक्कुटः
प्रासादकुक्कुट m. (-टः) A pigeon,<BR> E. प्रासाद a palace, and कुक्कुट a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासाद्रपृष्ठ
प्रासाद्रपृष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A terrace or balcony on the top of a large house. E.<BR>प्रासाद and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादशृङ्ग|प्रासादशृंग
प्रासादशृङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A turret, a spire on a palace or temple.<BR> E. प्रासाद, and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादीय
प्रासादीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of or belonging to a palace<BR> E. प्रासाद, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासिक|प्रासिकः
प्रासिक m. (-कः) A spearman, a lancer, a soldier armed with a dart or<BR>spear.<BR> E. प्रास a dart and ठक् affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्त
प्रास्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown, thrown of or away.<BR>	 2. Thrown into.<BR>	 3.<BR>Expelled, turned out, banished.<BR> E. प्र before, अस् to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्थिक|प्रास्थिकः
प्रास्थिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Brought for a Prastha, containing a Prastha,<BR>&c.<BR> E. प्रस्थ a certain measure, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह|प्राहः
प्राह m. (-हः) Instruction in the art of acting or dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्ण|प्राह्णः
प्राह्ण m. (-ह्णः) The forenoon<BR> E. प्र prior, अह्न the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णे
प्राह्णे Ind. In the morning, in the forenoon. E. The seventh case of the<BR>last word, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णेतन|प्राह्णेतनः
प्राह्णेतन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Belonging to the forenoon.<BR> E. प्राह्णे in the morning, aff. द्यु and तुक् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णेतमा
प्राह्णेतमा(रा)म् Ind. Early in the day, in the forenoon<BR> E. प्राह्ले with तमप्<BR>or तरप् aff. and आमु added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रिय|प्रियः
प्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Beloved, dear, desired.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A husband a<BR>lover.<BR>	 2. A sort of drug, commonly Riddhi 3. A sort of deer.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>1. A woman.<BR>	 2. A wife or mistress.<BR>	 3. Small cardamoms.<BR>	 4. News,<BR>information.<BR>	 5. Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 6. Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>	 7.<BR>A species of the Supratishthā metre.<BR> E. प्री to please, aff. क, and<BR>the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियक|प्रियकः
प्रियक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A kind of tree, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>	 2. A plant, com-<BR>monly Priyangu.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>	 4. A varie-<BR>gated or spotted deer.<BR>	 5. A bee.<BR>	 6. Saffron.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियकार
प्रियकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Kind, favourable, affectionate, doing good<BR>to, or treating kindly.<BR>	 2. Suiting, congenial.<BR> E. प्रिय, and कृ to do,<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियकृत्
प्रियकृत् mfn. (-कृत्त्) Kind, friendly, a friend, a benefactor.<BR> E. प्रिय, and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियङ्कर|प्रियंकर|प्रियङ्करः
प्रियङ्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Amiable, exciting or attracting regard.<BR>	 2. Act-<BR>ing kindly or affectionately to.<BR> E. प्रिय beloved, कृ to make, aff. खच्-<BR>मुम् aug.; also with अण् aff. प्रियकार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियङ्करण|प्रियंकरण
प्रियङ्करण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>	 1. Acceptable, grateful to.<BR>	 2. Acting kind-<BR>ly to, who or what does so.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Gratifying, treating kindly,<BR>(the act).<BR> E. प्रिय, कृ to do, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियङ्गु|प्रियंगु|प्रियंगुः|प्रियङ्गुः
प्रियङ्गु m. (-ङ्गुः)<BR>	 1. A medicinal plant, and perfume, commonly known<BR>by the name Priyangu, and described in some places as a fra-<BR>grant seed.<BR>	 2. Panick seed, (Panicum italicum.)<BR>	 3. Black mustard<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">Page506-a+ 60</a>]<BR>seed.<BR>	 4. Long pepper.<BR>	 5. A peculiar tree: see कटुकी.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Saffron.<BR>E. प्रिय desired, गम् to go, aff. डुन् and मुम् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=505-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियतम|प्रियतमः
प्रियतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Dearest, most beloved.<BR>	 m. (-मः) A tree, (Celosia<BR>cristata).<BR> E. प्रिय desirable, तमप् aff. “मयूरशिखावृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियतर|प्रियतरः
प्रियतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Dearer, more dear.<BR> E. प्रिय, तरप् comparative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियता
प्रियता f. (-ता) Love, affection.<BR> E. प्रिय beloved, तल् aff.; also with त्व aff.<BR>प्रियत्व n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियदर्शन|प्रियदर्शनः
प्रियदर्शन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Handsome, lovely, good-looking.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>parrot.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Mimusops kauki).<BR> E. प्रिय beloved, and दर्शन<BR>appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियप्राय|प्रियप्रायं
प्रियप्राय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Eloquent, well-spoken, of pleasing speech.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-यं) Eloquence in language.<BR> E. प्रिय desired, प्राय abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियप्रेप्सु|प्रियप्रेप्सुः
प्रियप्रेप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Lamenting the loss or absence of any beloved<BR>object, wishing or grieving for it.<BR> E. प्रिय beloved and प्रेप्सु desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियभाषण
प्रियभाषण n. (-णं) Speaking kindly.<BR> E. प्रिय and भाषण speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियमधु|प्रियमधुः
प्रियमधु m. (-धुः) BALARĀMA, the half-brother of KṚṢṆA<BR> E. प्रिय fond,<BR>मधु wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियमाण
प्रियमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Beloved, affectionate.<BR> E. प्रि to please, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंवद|प्रियंवदः
प्रियंवद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Sweet or pleasant speaking.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A sort of<BR>demi-god or Vidyādhara<BR> E. प्रिय kind, desired, वद् to speak, aff. खच्,<BR>मुम् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियम्भविष्णु|प्रियंभविष्णु
प्रियम्भविष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Become dear to, or beloved by.<BR> E. प्रिय, मू to<BR>be, खिष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियम्भविष्णुता
प्रियम्भविष्णुता f. (-ता) Amiability, becoming beloved by.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियम्भावुक|प्रियंभावुक
प्रियम्भावुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Become dear to, or beloved by.<BR> E. प्रिय, and भू<BR>to be, खुकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियम्भावुकता
प्रियम्भावुकता f. (-ता) Amiability, becoming beloved, the state or condi-<BR>tion.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियवर्णी
प्रियवर्णी f. (-र्णी) A creeping plant, (Echites frutescens.)<BR> E. प्रिय desired, घर्ण class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियवादिन्
प्रियवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Sweet or pleasant spoken, flattering, a flat-<BR>terer.<BR> E. प्रिय kind, वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियसख|प्रियसखः
प्रियसख m. (-खः) A tree, (Khayer, or Mimosa catechu.)<BR>	 f. (-खी) A female<BR>friend or companion, a confidant.<BR> E. प्रिय desired, सखि a friend,<BR>टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियसत्य|प्रियसत्यं
प्रियसत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Pleasant and true.<BR>	 n. (-त्यं) Eloquent or pleas-<BR>ing, as well as true, (discourse.)<BR> E. प्रिय loved, and सत्य true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियसन्देश|प्रियसंदेश|प्रियसंदेशः|प्रियसन्देशः
प्रियसन्देश m. (-शः) A tree bearing a fragrant flower, (Michelia cham-<BR>paca.)<BR> E. प्रिय a friend, and सन्देश intelligence “चम्पकवृक्षे”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियाख्य
प्रियाख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं) Announcing good tidings.<BR> E. प्रिय, and आख्य who says<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियाल|प्रियालः
प्रियाल m. (-लः) A tree, commonly Piyāsāl, (Buchanania latifolia, Rox-<BR>BUKGH'S catalogue, but the name is applied to different trees.) E.<BR>प्रि to satisfy, aff. कालन् and the radical vowel changed to रि;<BR>also with कन् added प्रियालक m. (-कः) and with the vowel protract<BR>ed. प्रीयाल m. (-लः) also-as derived from पीय a Sautra root, पीयाल.<BR>or पियाल &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियासु
प्रियासु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Fond of life.<BR> E. प्रिय, and असु breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियैषिन्
प्रियैषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Friendly, affectionate, wishing to please. E.<BR>प्रिय, and एषिन् seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियोदित|प्रियोदितं
प्रियोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well or kindly spoken, pleasingly uttered.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं) Kindly or gentle speech.<BR> E. प्रिय kind, &c. and उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्री
प्री (ङ) प्रीङ् r. 4th cl. (प्रीयते) (ञ) प्रीञ् r. 9th cl. (प्रीणाति प्रीणीते) and<BR>1st and 10th cls. (प्रियति-ते प्राययति-ते) or प्रीणयति 1. To please, to<BR>delight, to satisfy.<BR>	 2. To be pleased or satisfied.<BR>	 3. To desire<BR>or love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीण|प्रीणः
प्रीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Old ancient.<BR>	 2. Pleased, satisfied.<BR> E. प्री to please, aff. णिच्-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीणन|प्रीणनं
प्रीणन n. (-नं) Satisfaction, satisfying, satiety.<BR> E. प्री to please aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीणयित्वा
प्रीणयित्वा Ind. Having pleased or propitiated,<BR> E. प्री to please, क्ता aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीत|प्रीतः
प्रीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pleased, happy, glad.<BR>	 2. Pleased or satisfied<BR>with.<BR>	 3. Gracicus, kind, affectionate.<BR>	 4. Beloved, dear to.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Pleasure, delight.<BR> E. प्री to please, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतात्मन्
प्रीतात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Pleased, satisfied, content.<BR> E. प्रीत and आत्मन्<BR>self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीति|प्रीतिः
प्रीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Joy, pleasure, happiness.<BR>	 2. Love, affection, regard.<BR>3. The wife of KĀMA, or Cupid.<BR>	 4. The second of the twenty-seven<BR>astronomical Yogas.<BR> E. प्री to please, aff. क्तिच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिकर
प्रीतिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Pleasing, agreeable to.<BR> E. प्रीति and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिजुषा
प्रीतिजुषा f. (-षा) The wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR> E. प्रीति the wife of KĀMA,<BR>जुष् to serve, affs. क and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिद|प्रीतिदः
प्रीतिद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Affectionate, inspiring love or regard.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A<BR>jester, a buffoon.<BR> E. प्रीति affection, pleasure and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिदान
प्रीतिदान n. (-नं) A kind or friendly present.<BR> E. प्रीति affection, and दान<BR>giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिदाय|प्रीतिदायः
प्रीतिदाय n. (-यं) A gift or token of affection.<BR> E. प्रीति and दाय a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिपूर्व्वक
प्रीतिपूर्व्वक n. (-कं) Adv. Through favour or kindness.<BR> E. प्रीति and पूर्व्वक<BR>an antecedent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिमत्|प्रीतिमन्त्
प्रीतिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Kind, affectionate.<BR> E. प्रीति and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिमनस
प्रीतिमनस mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>	 1. Content, happy.<BR>	 2. Kind.<BR> E. प्रीति and<BR>मन्स् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिवचस्
प्रीतिवचस् n. (-चः) Gracious or kindly speech.<BR> E. प्रीति and वचस् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतु
प्रीतु m. (-तुः) A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीयमाण
प्रीयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being pleased or propitiated.<BR> E. प्री to please, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रु
प्रु (ङ) प्रुङ् r. 1st cl. (प्रवते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To jump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष
प्रुष r. 1st cl. (उ) प्रुषु (प्रोषति) To burn, to consume with fire. r. 9th cl.<BR>(पुष्णाति) To be unctuous or bland.<BR>	 2. To sprinkle.<BR>	 3. To fill.<BR>	 4. To<BR>set free.<BR>	 5. To be fond of or kind to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्ट|प्रुष्टः
प्रुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Burnt.<BR> E. प्रुष् to burn, aff. क्ता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्व|प्रुष्वः
प्रुष्व m. (-ष्वः)<BR>	 1. A season of the year, a period of two months.<BR>	 2. The<BR>sun.<BR>	 f. (-ष्वा) A drop of water.<BR> E. प्रुष् to burn, Unādi aff. क्कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षक|प्रेक्षकः
प्रेक्षक m. (-कः) A spectator, a beholder, one of an audience.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, ईक्ष् to see, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षण|प्रेक्षणं
प्रेक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The eye.<BR>	 2. Any public show or spectacle, a sight.<BR>	 2.<BR>A place where public exhibitions are held.<BR>	 nf. (-णं-णा) Seeing,<BR>viewing, looking at, regarding.<BR> E. प्र before, ईक्ष् to see, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणिक
प्रेक्षणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Looking, who looks at.<BR>	 f. (-का) A woman<BR>fond of seeing shows.<BR> E. प्रेक्षण seeing, ठक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणीय
प्रेक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Visible, apparent.<BR>	 2. Looking or appearing<BR>like.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Beautiful to the sight.<BR>	 2. To be seen.<BR>	 3. To be con-<BR>sidered as.<BR> E. प्र before, ईक्ष् to see, अनीयर् aff. also with कन् added,<BR>प्रेक्षणीयक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षमाण
प्रेक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Looking at or on, beholding, regarding.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, इक्ष् to see, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्ष्यमाण
प्रेक्ष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being seen or looked at.<BR> E. प्र before, ईक्ष् to see, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षा
प्रेक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Intellect, understanding.<BR>	 2. Dancing.<BR>	 3. Seeing, view-<BR>ing, observing.<BR>	 4. Seeing a play or entertainment of dancing, &c.<BR>5. The branch of a tree.<BR>	 6. Deliberation, reflection.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>ईक्ष् to see, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षित
प्रेक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Seen, behold, looked at.<BR>	 n. (-नं) A look.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore ईक्ष् to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खण|प्रेंखण
प्रेङ्खण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going, wandering.<BR>	 2. Entering.<BR>	 3. Swinging.<BR>	 4. A<BR>minor drama in one act.<BR> E. प्र before, इखि to go, aff. ल्युट्-णत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खत्
प्रेङ्खत् mfn. (-ङ्खन् ङ्खन्ती-ङ्खत्)<BR>	 1. Touching, being in contact with.<BR>	 2. Scat-<BR>tering, diffusing.<BR>	 3. Shaking, moving.<BR>	 4. Wandering, roving. E.<BR>प्र before, इखि to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खा|प्रेंखा
प्रेङ्खा f. (-ङ्खा)<BR>	 1. A swing, a sort of hammock or swinging cot, either for<BR>travelling or diversion.<BR>	 2. Wandering, roaming, travelling about.<BR>3. A horse's going or motion.<BR>	 4. Dancing.<BR> E. प्र before, इखि to go,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खित|प्रेंखित|प्रेङ्खितं
प्रेङ्खित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken, moving, set in motion, swung, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Joined to, being in contact with<BR> E. प्र before, इखि to go, aff. क्त or<BR>प्रेङ्खा a swing, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=506-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खोलिन
प्रेङ्खोलिन n. (-नं) A swing, a swinging cot or hammock.<BR> E. प्रङ्खोल to swing<BR>or shake, nominal verb, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेङ्खोलित|प्रेङ्खोलितं
प्रेङ्खोलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Agitated, shaken, swung, set in motion. E.<BR>प्रेङ्खोल nominal verb, to swing, aff क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत|प्रेतः
प्रेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dead, deceased.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A ghost, a goblin, a<BR>spirit, an evil being, especially animating the carcases of the<BR>dead.<BR>	 2. The spirit before obsequial rites are performed.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतकर्म्मन्|प्रेतकर्मन्
प्रेतकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Funeral or obsequial rites.<BR> E. प्रेत and कर्म्मन् act; also<BR>प्रेतकार्य्य, प्रेतक्रिया &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतकार्य्य|प्रेतकार्य|प्रेतकार्य्यं
प्रेतकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Obsequial ceremonies, any usages observed in honour<BR>of the dead.<BR> E. प्रेत dead, कार्य्य practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतकृत्य
प्रेतकृत्य nf. (-त्यं-त्या) Obsequial rites.<BR> E. प्रेत and कृत्य a ceremony; also प्रेतकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतगृह|प्रेतगृहं
प्रेतगृह n. (-हं) A cemetery, a burying-ground.<BR> E. प्रेत a spirit and गृहं<BR>abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतत्व
प्रेतत्व n. (-त्वं) The character or state of a departed spirit.<BR> E. प्रेत and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतधूम|प्रेतधूमः
प्रेतधूम n. (-मं) The smoke of a funeral pile.<BR> E. प्रेत and धूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतनदी
प्रेतनदी f. (-दी) The river of hell.<BR> E. प्रेत a goblin and नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतनर|प्रेतनरः
प्रेतनर m. (-रः) A ghost, a corpse.<BR> E. प्रेत and नर a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतनिर्हारक|प्रेतनिर्हारकः
प्रेतनिर्हारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A man-employed to carry forth dead bodies.<BR>2. A kinsman who does so.<BR> E. प्रेत and निर् out, हृ to take, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतपक्ष|प्रेतपक्षः
प्रेतपक्ष n. (-क्षं) The dark half of the month.<BR> E. प्रेत and पक्ष a fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतपटह|प्रेतपटहः
प्रेतपटह m. (-हः) A drum played at the death of a person.<BR> E. प्रेत dead,<BR>and पटह a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतपति|प्रेतपतिः
प्रेतपति m. (-तिः) YAMA, ruler of the dead.<BR> E. प्रेत dead and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतपात्र
प्रेतपात्र n. (-त्रं) A vessel used in obsequial presentations.<BR> E. प्रेत and पात्र<BR>a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतराज|प्रेतराजः
प्रेतराज m. (-जः) YAMA.<BR> E. प्रेत and राज king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतलोक|प्रेतलोकः
प्रेतलोक m. (-कः) The region of disembodied spirits, in which they re-<BR>main for one year, or until the obsequial rites are completed. E.<BR>प्रेत and लोक region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतवन|प्रेतवनं
प्रेतवन n. (-नं) A burying ground, a cemetery, a place where bodies are<BR>burnt or buried.<BR> E. प्रेत a spirit and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतवाहित|प्रेतवाहितः
प्रेतवाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Possessed by a devil or fiend.<BR> E. प्रेत a spirit<BR>and वाहित borne, actuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतशुद्धि|प्रेतशुद्धिः
प्रेतशुद्धि m. (-द्धिः) Purification after the death of a kinsman.<BR> E. प्रेत and शुद्धि purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतहार|प्रेतहारः
प्रेतहार m. (-रः) One who carries a corpse, a near kinsman.<BR> E. प्रेत and<BR>हार who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतान्न
प्रेतान्न n. (-न्नं) Food offered to the manes or distributed on a person's<BR>death.<BR> E. प्रेत and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतोद्देश|प्रेतोद्देशः
प्रेतोद्देश m. (-शः) An offering to the manes.<BR> E. प्रेत and उद्देश object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्य
प्रेत्य Ind.<BR>	 1. In the next world.<BR>	 2. Having died.<BR> E. प्रेत dead, and यत् aff.<BR>or प्र before, इ to go, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्वन्
प्रेत्वन् m. (-त्वा)<BR>	 1. Wind.<BR>	 2. INDRĀ.<BR> E. प्र + इ-क्वनिप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेप्सु
प्रेप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Desirous of obtaining.<BR> E. प्र before, अप् to ob-<BR>tain, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमन्
प्रेमन् mn. (-मा-म)<BR>	 1. Affection, kindness, tender regard.<BR>	 2. Pleasure,<BR>sport, pastime, joy.<BR>	 m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. Air.<BR> E. प्रे for प्रिय loved,<BR>इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमपर
प्रेमपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Affectionate, loving constant.<BR> E. प्रेम and पर attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमपातन|प्रेमपातनं
प्रेमपातन n. (-नं) Rheum, tears.<BR> E. प्रेम tenderness, पातन falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेयस्
प्रेयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Dearest, most beloved, very dear.<BR>	 f. (-सी) A<BR>wife, a mistress.<BR> E. प्रिय dear, and ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेयोपत्य|प्रेयोपत्यः
प्रेयोपत्य m. (-त्यः) A heron.<BR> E. प्रेयस् dear and अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरण|प्रेरणं
प्रेरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Sending, directing, 2. Ordering, commanding.<BR>	 3. Passion,<BR>operation of the organs of sense.<BR>	 4. The sense of the causal verb.<BR>E. प्र before, ईर to go, णिच्-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरित|प्रेरितः
प्रेरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sent, directed, dispatched.<BR>	 2. Ordered.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>A messenger.<BR> E. प्र before, ईर् to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्यभाव|प्रेत्यभावः
प्रेत्यभाव m. (-वः) Being born again after dying.<BR> E. प्रेत्य, भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्वन
प्रेत्वन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pervading, spreading.<BR>	 2. Satisfying.<BR> E. प्र before, इवि to<BR>pervade, &c. ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेर्त्वन्
प्रेर्त्वन् m. (-र्त्वा) The ocean.<BR>	 f. (-री) A river.<BR> E. प्र before, ईर to go, Unādi<BR>aff. क्वनिप् and तुट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष|प्रेषः
प्रेष (ऋ) प्रेषृ r. 1st. cl. (प्रेषति) To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष|प्रेषः
प्रेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Sending, directing, dispatching.<BR>	 2. Pain, affliction.<BR> E. प्र<BR>before, इष् to go or send, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषण|प्रेषणं
प्रेषण n. (-णं) Sending, dispatching.<BR> E. प्र before, इष् to go, aff. णिच्-युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषित|प्रेषितं
प्रेषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sent, directed.<BR> E. प्र before, इष् to go, aff. क्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषितवत्
प्रेषितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Sent, having sent.<BR> E. प्र before, ईष् to go,<BR>क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्ठ|प्रेष्ठः
प्रेष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Most or very dear.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>	 1. A wife.<BR>	 2. The leg.<BR>E. प्रिय dear, aff. इष्ठन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्य|प्रेष्यः
प्रेष्य m. (-ष्यः) A servant.<BR> E. प्र before, इष् to go, or प्रेष् to send, aff. ण्यत्; also प्रैष्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैष|प्रैषः
प्रैष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Sorrow, distress, affliction.<BR>	 2. Pain, suffering.<BR>	 3. Send-<BR>ing, directing.<BR>	 4. Phrenzy, intoxication, insanity.<BR> E. प्र before, इष्<BR>to go, aff. घञ् also प्रेष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैष्य|प्रैष्यः
प्रैष्य m. (-ष्यः) A servant, a slave.<BR>	 n. (-ष्यं) Service, servitude.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>इष् to go, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्त|प्रोक्तं
प्रोक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Said, declared.<BR> E. प्र before, वच् to speak, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्तवत्
प्रोक्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having or had said, was saying<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>वच् to speak, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षण|प्रोक्षणं
प्रोक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Killing animals in sacrifice, immolation of victims.<BR>2. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 3. Sprinkling with water, &c.<BR>	 4. A text to be<BR>repeated when animals are offered.<BR> E. प्र before, ऊक्ष् to sprinkle,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षणीपात्र
प्रोक्षणीपात्र n. (-त्रं) A vessel for sprinkling water, &c.<BR> E. प्रोक्षण, and पात्र a vessel, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षित|प्रोक्षितं
प्रोक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkled.<BR>	 2. Killed, slaughtered.<BR>	 3. Offered<BR>in sacrifice.<BR> E. प्र before, उक्ष् to sprinkle, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चण्ड|प्रोच्चंड
प्रोच्चण्ड f. (-ण्डा) Exceedingly terrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चैस्
प्रोच्चैस् Ind.<BR>	 1. In a very high degree.<BR>	 2. Very loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छलत्|प्रोच्छलन्त्
प्रोच्छलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्) Flowing, issuing, coming out, or up. E.<BR>प्र and उत् before, शल् to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छून
प्रोच्छून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Swollen.<BR> E. प्र and उच्छून swelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्जासन|प्रोज्जासनं
प्रोज्जासन n. (-नं) Killing, slaughter.<BR> E. प्र and उत् before, जस् to<BR>hurt or kill, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झन|प्रोज्झनं
प्रोज्झन n. (-नं) Leaving, quitting, letting go.<BR> E. प्र before, उज्झ, to<BR>leave, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झित|प्रोज्झितं
प्रोज्झित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abandoned, shunned, avoided.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>उज्झित left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोञ्छग
प्रोञ्छग n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Wiping away.<BR>	 2. Picking up.<BR> E. प्र + उञ्छ-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोण्ठ|प्रोंठः|प्रोण्ठः
प्रोण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A spitting-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत|प्रोतं
प्रोत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sewn or stitched.<BR>	 2. Tied, strung.<BR>	 3. Set, inlaid.<BR>	 4.<BR>Impaled.<BR>	 5. Joined, connected.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Cloth, clothes.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>वे to weave or sew, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोतोत्सादन|प्रोतोत्सादनं
प्रोतोत्सादन n. (-नं) A parasol, a Chātā, an umbrella.<BR> E. प्रीत cloth,<BR>उत् over, सादन a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्फल|प्रोत्फलः
प्रोत्फल m. (-लः) A sort of palm tree.<BR> E. प्र and उत् above, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्सादन
प्रोत्सादन n. (-नं) Contriving, device.<BR> E. प्र and उत् before, षद् to go, causal<BR>v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्सारण|प्रोत्सारणं
प्रोत्सारण n. (-णं) Clearing away, getting rid of, expelling.<BR> E. प्र and उत्<BR>before, सृ to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्सारित
प्रोत्सारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Relinquished, left, given up.<BR>	 2. Got rid of,<BR>ejected, expelled.<BR> E. प्र and उत् before, सृ to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साह|प्रोत्साहः
प्रोत्साह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 2. Stimulus, incitement.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साहक|प्रोत्साहकः
प्रोत्साहक m. (-कः) The instigator or adviser of any act, or in law, of any<BR>crime.<BR> E. प्रोत्साह with कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साहन|प्रोत्साहनं
प्रोत्साहन n. (-नं) Instigating, exciting, stimulating<BR> E. प्र and उत् before,<BR>सह् to bear, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=507-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साहित
प्रोत्साहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Incited, instigated, stimulated, encouraged. E.<BR>प्र and उत् before, सह् to bear, in the causal form, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथ|प्रोथः
प्रोथ (ऋ) प्रोथृ r. 1st. cl. (प्रोथति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be able, adequate or competent.<BR>2. To complete or ample.<BR>	 3. To destroy, to subdue or overpower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथ|प्रोथः
प्रोथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>	 1. Travelling, wayfaring, a traveller.<BR>	 2. Notorious,<BR>famous.<BR>	 3. Placed, fixed.<BR>	 mn. (-थः-थं)<BR>	 1. The nose of a horse or the<BR>tip of it.<BR>	 2. The snout of a hog.<BR>	 m. (-थं)<BR>	 1. The loins or hip.<BR>	 2.<BR>Old clothes.<BR>	 3. The embryo or fœtus.<BR>	 4. An excavation.<BR> E. प्रु to go,<BR>Unādi aff. थक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्घुष्ठ
प्रोद्घुष्ठ mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Resonant, sounding well.<BR>	 2. Making a loud<BR>noise.<BR> E. प्र and उद्घुष्ट sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्घोषण|प्रोद्घोषणं
प्रोद्घोषण n. (-णं) Sounding or crying aloud.<BR> E. प्र and उत् before, घुष् to<BR>cry, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्भिन्न
प्रोद्भिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Breaking forth, (as seeds, &c.)<BR> E. प्र and उद्भिन्न<BR>put forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोन्नत
प्रोन्नत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Towering, very lofty.<BR> E. प्र, and उन्नत high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोम्भन
प्रोम्भन n. (-नं) Filling.<BR> E. प्र before, उम्भ् to fill, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोम्भित
प्रोम्भित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Filled.<BR> E. प्र before, उम्भ् to fill, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोर्णुनविषु
प्रोर्णुनविषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to cover.<BR> E. प्र before, ऊर्णु to cover,<BR>desire. v., उ aff. and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोर्णुनूषु
प्रोर्णुनूषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to cover.<BR> E. प्र before, ऊर्णु to cover,<BR>desid. v., उ aff. and the augment इ omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लाघित
प्रोल्लाघित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Recovered from sickness, convalescent.<BR>	 2.<BR>Strong, robust.<BR> E. प्र and उत् before, लाघ् to be able, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लिखत्
प्रोल्लिखत् mfn. (-खन्-खन्ती-खत्) Marking, marking lines, scratches, &c. E.<BR>प्र, and उल्लिख to mark, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोल्लेखन|प्रोल्लेखनं
प्रोल्लेखन n. (-नं) Scratching, marking, drawing lines or marks.<BR> E. प्र<BR>and उत् before, लिख् to write, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष|प्रोषः
प्रोष m. (-षः) Burning.<BR> E. प्रुष् to burn, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषित|प्रोषितः
प्रोषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abroad, absent, away from home, sojourning in<BR>another country.<BR> E. प्र before, वस् to dwell, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषितभर्तृका|प्रोषितभर्त्तृका
प्रोषितभर्तृका f. (-का) A woman whose husband is absent.<BR> E. प्रोषित ab-<BR>road, भर्त्तृ a husband, aff. कन् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषितमरण
प्रोषितमरण n. (-णं) Dying in a foreign country.<BR> E. प्रोषित absent, and मरण dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोषितवत्
प्रोषितवत् mfn. (वान्-वती-वत्) Strange, a stranger, a sojourner.<BR> E. प्र be-<BR>fore, वस् to dwell, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रो
प्रो(प्रौ)ष्ठ mf. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी) A sort of carp, (Cyprinus Pausius, Ham.) “पुंँटिमाछ”<BR>m. (-ष्ठः) An ox.<BR>	 3. A bench, a stool.<BR> E. प्र before, उष् to burn, aff.<BR>थन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठपदा
प्रोष्ठपदा f. (-दा) One of the constellations, the twenty-sixth or twenty-<BR>seventh, containing stars in the wing of Pegasus see भाद्रपदा.<BR>E. प्रोष्ठ here said to mean an ox, and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रो
प्रो(प्रौ)ष्ठपाद mfn. (-दः-दी-दं) Born under the sign Proṣṭhapada.<BR> E. प्रोष्ठ-<BR>पद and अण् aff. in this sense; in any other, the form is प्रोष्ठपद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रो
प्रो(प्रौ)ह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Skilful, clever.<BR>	 2. Logical, reasoning, a rea-<BR>soner, a disputant.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. An elephant's foot.<BR>	 2. A joint, a<BR>knot.<BR>	 3. The ancle of an elephant.<BR> E. प्र before, वह् to bear, or ऊह्<BR>to reason, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोहणीय
प्रोहणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be reasoned or argued.<BR> E. प्र before, ऊह् to<BR>reason, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौ
प्रौ(प्रो)ढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Full-grown.<BR>	 2. Confident, bold, arrogant.<BR>	 3.<BR>Impudent.<BR>	 4. Full-grown, (as the moon.)<BR>	 5. Thick, heavy, (darkness,<BR>&c.)<BR>	 6. Forward, (as the hand to seize any thing.)<BR>	 7. Raised, lifted<BR>up.<BR>	 8. Controverted.<BR>	 9. Old.<BR>	 10. Married.<BR>	 f. (-ढा)<BR>	 1. A woman from<BR>thirty years of age to fifty-five.<BR>	 2. A description of the Nāyikā<BR>or mistress, a woman whose feelings are violent or impetuous, or<BR>one who is not in any awe of her lover or husband.<BR> E. प्र before,<BR>वह to bear, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौ
प्रौ(प्रो)ढपाद m. (-दः) One who sits with his feet upon a seat.<BR> E. प्रौढ raised<BR>and पाद the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौ
प्रौ(प्रो)ढि f. (-ढिः)<BR>	 1. Enterprise, zeal, confident or audacious exertion.<BR>2. Investigation, controversy, discussion.<BR> E. प्र before, वह् to bear,<BR>aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौण|प्रौणः
प्रौण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Clever, learned, skilful.<BR> E. प्र + ओणृ-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौर्णुवितृ
प्रौर्णुवितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Extending over, covering.<BR> E. प्र and ऊर्णु to<BR>cover, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौष्ठप्रद
प्रौष्ठप्रद m. (-दः) The month Bhādra, (August-September.)<BR>	 f. (-दौ) Full<BR>moon in Bhādra.<BR> E. प्रोष्ठपदा the sign, and अण् aff. when the moon<BR>is near the wing of Pegasus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्ष|प्लक्षः
प्लक्ष r. 1st cl. (प्लक्षति-ते) To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्ष|प्लक्षः
प्लक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. Waved-leaf fig-tree, (Ficus infectoria.)<BR>	 2. Another<BR>tree, (Hibiscus populneoides.)<BR>	 3. The holy fig, (Fious religiosa.)<BR>4. One of the seven Dwīpas or continents, into which the world is<BR>divided.<BR>	 5. A private or back-door.<BR> E. प्लष् to burn, Unādi aff. स,<BR>and अ substituted for the penultimate vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लव|प्लवं|प्लवः
प्लव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Who or what goes by leaps or jumps, leaping, just-<BR>ing, a tumbler.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Jumping, leaping, plunging, going by<BR>leaps or plunges.<BR>	 2. Swimming, floating, diving.<BR>	 3. A raft, a float.<BR>4. A frog.<BR>	 5. A monkey.<BR>	 6. A sheep.<BR>	 7. A diver, or bird so called,<BR>(Pelicanus fusicollis.)<BR>	 8. A sort of duck.<BR>	 9. A man of a low or de-<BR>graded tribe.<BR>	 10. Waved-leaf fig-tree, (Ficus infectoria.)<BR>	 11. The<BR>continuous protracted accent, the lengthened sound of vowels in<BR>poetry or the Vedas.<BR>	 12. Protracting a sentence through several<BR>stanzas.<BR>	 13. A declivity or shelving ground.<BR>	 14. A piece of water.<BR>15. A sort of basket or snare of basket-work for catching fish.<BR>	 16.<BR>An enemy.<BR>	 17. Sending, directing.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. A sort of grass, (Cy-<BR>perus rotundus.)<BR>	 2. Fragrant grass in general, or another sort E.<BR>प्लु to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवक|प्लवकः
प्लवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tumbler, a dancer, a man who walks on the edge<BR>of a sword, a rope-dancer, &c.<BR>	 2. An outcast.<BR>	 3. A frog.<BR> E. प्लव् a<BR>tumbler, &c. and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवग|प्लवगः
प्लवग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A monkey, an ape.<BR>	 2. A frog.<BR>	 3. The charioteer of the<BR>sun.<BR>	 4. A sort of bird, the diver.<BR>	 3. A frog.<BR> E. प्लव् leaping, and ग<BR>who goes, from गम् with ड aff. “शिरीषवृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवगति|प्लवगतिः
प्लवगति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A frog.<BR>	 2. Going by leaps and jumps.<BR> E. प्लव leaping, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवङ्ग|प्लवंग|प्लवंगः|प्लवङ्गः
प्लवङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A monkey.<BR>	 2. A deer.<BR> E. प्लव leaping, गम् to go, aff.<BR>खच् with the power of ड, whence the nasal is inserted, and final<BR>syllable rejected; also प्लव, प्लवग, and प्लवङ्गम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवङ्गम|प्लवंगम|प्लवंगमः|प्लवङ्गमः
प्लवङ्गम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A monkey, an ape.<BR>	 2. A frog.<BR> E. प्लव leaping, गम् to<BR>go, aff. खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवन|प्लवनः
प्लवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Jumping, leaping.<BR>	 2. A deluge, an inundation.<BR>	 3.<BR>Swimming, plunging into.<BR> E. प्लु to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवमान
प्लवमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Bounding, springing, leaping.<BR>	 2. Swimming.<BR>E. प्लु to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लवाका
प्लवाका f. (-का) A boat, a raft.<BR> E. प्लव् tossing, अक what goes, टाप् fem.<BR>aff.; also प्लविका, from प्लु with वुन् aff. and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लविक
प्लविक f. (-का) Taking over on a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाक्ष|प्लाक्षं
प्लाक्ष n. (-क्षं) The fruit of the Hibiscus populneoides.<BR> E. प्लक्ष्, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाव|प्लावः
प्लाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Submersion.<BR>	 2. Filling a vessel till it runs over.<BR>	 3.<BR>Jumping.<BR>	 4. Filtering.<BR> E. प्लु to go, causal v., घञ् aff.; also with<BR>ल्युट्, प्लावनं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाव्य
प्लाव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be jumped, leaped, &c.<BR>	 2. To be sumbmerged<BR>or inundated.<BR> E. प्लु to go, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लाविन्
प्लाविन् m. (-वी) A bird.<BR> E. प्लु to go, aff. घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लिह
प्लिह r. 1st cl. (प्लेहति) To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लिहन्
प्लिहन् m. (-हा) The spleen: see प्लीहन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लिहा
प्लिहा f. (-हा) The spleen: see प्लीहन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ली
प्ली r. 9th cl. (प्लीणाति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहघ्न|प्लीहघ्नः
प्लीहघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A medicinal plant, (Andersonia rohitaka, Rox.)<BR> E. प्लीह<BR>the spleen, (the disease, &c.) घ्न what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=508-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहन्
प्लीहन् m. (-हा) The spleen; the organ or the disease of it, as in Eng-<BR>lish; in the latter sense, however, it is equally applied to the<BR>enlargement of the mesenteric glands, &c.<BR> E. प्लिह् to increase,<BR>Unādi aff. कनिन्, and the vowel made long; otherwise being<BR>प्लिहन्; and with क and टाप् affs., and the vowel long or short प्लिहा<BR>or प्लीहा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहशत्रु|प्लीहशत्रुः
प्लीहशत्रु m. (-त्रुः) A medical plant, commonly Rohera or Rohinī, (An-<BR>dersonia rohitaka, Rox.)<BR> E. प्लीह for प्लोहन् the spleen, (the disease,)<BR>and शत्रु enemy; also प्लीहाशत्रु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लीहारि|प्लीहारिः
प्लीहारि m. (-रिः) The holy fig-tree, (Ficus religiosa,)<BR> E. प्लीहा the spleen,<BR>and अरि enemy. “अश्वत्थवृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लु
प्लु (ङ) प्लुङ् r. 1st cl. (प्लवते)<BR>	 1. To go, to approach.<BR>	 2. To go by leaps,<BR>to jump, &c.<BR>	 3. To be lengthened, (as a vowel.) With उत् pre-<BR>fixed, To leap up. With वि, To plunge in, to be submerged<BR>or inundated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुक्षि|प्लुक्षिः
प्लुक्षि m. (-क्षिः) Fire or its deity.<BR> E. प्लुष् to burn, Unādi aff. किस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुत|प्लुतं|प्लुतः
प्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Jumped, leaped, gone by leap or jump, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Thrown or tossed up.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Bounding, capering, one of a<BR>horse's paces.<BR>	 2. Leaping, jumping, tumbling.<BR>	 mn. (-तः-तं) The third<BR>sound given to vowels; the protracted or continuous sound, being<BR>three times the length of the short vowel, and occupying three<BR>moments in its utterance.<BR> E. प्लु to go by leaps, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुति|प्लुतिः
प्लुति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Over-flowing.<BR>	 2. Jumping.<BR>	 3. A particular pace of a<BR>horse.<BR>	 4. Protraction, (of a vowel.)<BR> E. प्लु, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष्
प्लुष् r. 1st cl. (उ) प्लुषु (प्लोषति) r. 4th cl. (ऌ) प्लुषॢ (प्लुष्यति) To burn. r. 9th<BR>cl. (प्लुष्णाति)<BR>	 1. To be unctuous.<BR>	 2. To sprinkle.<BR>	 3. To fill.<BR>	 4. To set<BR>free.<BR>	 5. To be fond of or kind to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष|प्लुषः
प्लुष m. (-षः) Burning, combustion.<BR> E. प्लुष् to burn, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुष्ट|प्लुष्टः
प्लुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Burnt.<BR> E. प्लुष् to burn, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लुस
प्लुस (इर) प्लुसिर r. 4th cl. (प्लुस्यति)<BR>	 1. To burn, 2. To share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लेव
प्लेव (ऋ) प्लेवृ r. 1st cl. (प्लेवते) To serve, to gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लो
प्लो(प्रो)ष m. (-षः) Burning, combustion.<BR> E. प्लुष् to burn, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सा
प्सा r. 2nd cl. (प्साति) To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सा
प्सा f. (प्सा) Eating.<BR> E. प्सा to eat, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सात|प्सातं
प्सात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eaten.<BR> E. प्सा to eat, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्सान|प्सानं
प्सान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Eating.<BR>	 2. Food<BR> E. प्सा to eat, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फ|फं|फः
फ The twenty-second consonant of the Nāgari Alphabet, the aspirate<BR>of the preceding letter, and expressed by Ph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फ|फं|फः
फ m. (-फः)<BR>	 1. Increasing, swelling, enlarging, expanding.<BR>	 2. Perform-<BR>ance of a mystical rite, by which KUVERA'S attendants are pro-<BR>pitiated.<BR>	 3. A high wind, a gale.<BR>	 4. Wind expelled in yawning.<BR>	 5.<BR>Fruitfulness, fertility.<BR>	 6. An augmentor or increaser.<BR>	 nf. (फं-फा)<BR>Unprofitable or idle speech.<BR>	 n. (-फं)<BR>	 1. Angry speech.<BR>	 2. Bursting<BR>with some little noise, as air bubbles, boiling water, &c.; bubbling,<BR>boiling.<BR>	 f. (-फा) Distress, anxiety.<BR> E. फल् to bear fruit, or स्फाय् to<BR>swell, aff. ड; in the latter case, the initial is rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फक्क|फक्कः
फक्क r. 1st cl. (फक्कति)<BR>	 1. To creep, to move slowly or sluggishly.<BR>	 2. To<BR>behave ill, to practise ill or improper conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फक्किका
फक्किका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A position, an assertion or argument, to be proved<BR>or maintained.<BR>	 2. Logical exposition or elucidation.<BR>	 3. A sophism.<BR>4. A trick.<BR>	 5. Illusion.<BR>	 6. Fraud.<BR> E. फक्क् to move slowly, aff.<BR>ण्वुल् टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फञ्जिका
फञ्जिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>	 2. A species of<BR>Hedysarum, (H. alhagi.)<BR> E. भञ्ज् to break, (disease,) aff. ण्वुल्, and<BR>the radical initial changed to फ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फञ्जिपुत्रिका
फञ्जिपुत्रिका f. (-का) A plant, (Talvinia cucullata.)<BR> E. फञ्जि as above, and<BR>पुत्रिका infant. “उन्दुरकानि” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फट|फटः
फट mfn. subst. (-टः-टा-टं) The expanded hood or neck of the Cobra<BR>de capello.<BR>	 mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>	 1. A tooth.<BR>	 2. A cheat.<BR> E. स्फुट् to burst or<BR>expand, aff. अच् fem. aff. टाप्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फट्
फट् Ind. Exclamation of no meaning, forming part of a Mantra or in-<BR>cantation.<BR> E. स्फुट् to burst, aff. क्विप्, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फडिङ्गा|फडिंगा
फडिङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) A cricket, a locust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण|फणः
फण r. 1st cl. (फणति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To produce easily or readily.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>unoily, Causal form, (फाणयति)<BR>	 1. To dilute.<BR>	 2. To shine. (फणयति)<BR>To cause to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण|फणः
फण mfn. Subst. (-णः-णा-णं) The expanded hood or neck of the Cobra<BR>de capello, &c.<BR> E. फण् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणकर|फणकरः
फणकर m. (-रः) A snake, especially the Cobra de capello, or COLUBER<BR>naja.<BR> E. फल् the hood, and कर who makes; also फणाकर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणधर|फणधरः
फणधर m. (-रः) A snake.<BR> E. फण the hood, and धर who has; also<BR>फणाधर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणभृत्
फणभृत् m. (-भृत्) A snake.<BR> E. फण a hood, and भृत् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणमणि|फणमणिः
फणमणि m. (-णिः) A jewel supposed to be in the head of a snake.<BR> E. फण<BR>and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणवत्|फणवन्त्
फणवत् m. (-वान्) A snake.<BR> E. फणा a hood, and मतुप् possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणाकर|फणाकरः
फणाकर m. (-रः) A snake: see फणकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणाधर|फणाधरः
फणाधर m. (-रः) A snake: see फणधर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणाभर|फणाभरः
फणाभर m. (-रः) A snake.<BR> E. फण the hood expanded, भृ to possess, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणावत्|फणावन्त्
फणावत् m. (-वान्) A snake: see फणवत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिकेशर|फणिकेशरः
फणिकेशर m. (-रः) A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR> E. फणिन् a snake and केशर<BR>filaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिखेल|फणिखेलः
फणिखेल m. (-लः) A quail.<BR> E. फणि a snake, and खेल who plays. “भारुइपाखि” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिज्झक|फणिज्झकः
फणिज्झक m. (-कः) A plant, also Marua.<BR>	 f. (-का) A plant, commonly<BR>Rāmadūti, apparently a sort of basil with small leaves.<BR> E. फणि for<BR>फणी a snake, and उज्झ to abandon, aff. वुन् deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणित|फणितः
फणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone.<BR>	 2. Diluted.<BR> E. फण् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणितल्पग|फणितल्पगः
फणितल्पग m. (-गः) VIṢṆU whose bed in the serpent Sesha.<BR> E. फणि a<BR>snake, तल्प a bed, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिन्
फणिन् m. (-णी) A snake.<BR> E. फण a hood, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिप्रिय|फणिप्रियः
फणिप्रिय m. (-यः) Air, wind.<BR> E. फणि for फणी a snake, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिफेण
फणिफेण m. (-णः) Opium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिभाष्य
फणिभाष्य n. (-ष्यं) The commentary of Patanjali on Pānini's Sutras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिभुज्
फणिभुज् m. (-भुक्)<BR>	 1. An epithet of Garuda.<BR>	 2. A Peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणिमुख
फणिमुख n. (-खं) An instrument for throwing earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फणीश्वर|फणीश्वरः
फणीश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The great serpent ANANTA.<BR>	 2. An epithet of Śeṣa.<BR>E. फणी a snake, and ईश्वर sovereign; also फणीन्द्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फण्ड|फंडः|फण्डः
फण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The belly.<BR> E. फण् to go, Unādi aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फत्कारिन्
फत्कारिन् m. (-री) A bird.<BR> E. फत् imitative sound, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फर|फरं
फर n. (-रं) A shield.<BR> E. र substituted for ल; see फल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फरुवक|फरुवकं
फरुवक n. (-कं) A betel-box.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फर्फर
फर्फर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) One moving quickly.<BR> E. स्फुर्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फर्फरीक|फर्फरीकः
फर्फरीक m. (-कः) The Palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-कं) Young shoot or branch.<BR>	 f. (-का) A shoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फरीक
फरीक m. (-कः) The palm of the hand with the fingers extended.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>Sweetness.<BR> E. स्फुर् to expand, Unādi aff. ईकन् and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्
फल् r. 1st cl. (फलति)<BR>	 1. To produce or bear fruit.<BR>	 2. To make fruitful,<BR>to fructify.<BR>	 3. To go. (ञि, आ) ञिफला r. 1st cl. (फलति) To divide, to<BR>cleave or split.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल|फलं|फलः
फल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The fruit of any plant, fruit in general.<BR>	 2. Fruit, (meta-<BR>phorically,) result, produce, consequence.<BR>	 3. Prosperity, flourish-<BR>ing, thriving.<BR>	 4. Gain, profit, acquisition.<BR>	 5. Recompense, reward.<BR>6. A shield.<BR>	 7. The blade of a sword or knife, the head of an ar-<BR>row, &c.<BR>	 8. A sort of fragrant berry and drug commonly Kākoli.<BR>9. A nutmeg.<BR>	 10. The three myrobalans collectively.<BR>	 11. The men-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">Page510-a+ 60</a>]<BR>strual discharge.<BR>	 12. Gift, giving.<BR>	 13. A ploughshare.<BR>	 14. The<BR>quotient of a sum, (in arithmetic.)<BR>	 15. The area of a circle, &c.<BR>16. An equation.<BR>	 17. (In astronomy,) The anomalistic equation of<BR>a planet.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A medicinal plant, commonly Priangu.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>A plant, (Echites anti-dysenterica, Rox.:) see कुटज.<BR> E. फल् to bear<BR>or produce fruit, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=509-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलक|फलकं|फलकः
फलक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A shield.<BR>	 2. A bench.<BR>	 3. A plank.<BR>	 4. A layer.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः)<BR>	 1. A bone, the os frontis, or bone of the forehead.<BR>	 2. A leaf<BR>or page for writing on.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) The<BR>buttocks.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding, or फल् to split or divide,<BR>aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकपाणि|फलकपाणिः
फलकपाणि m. (-णिः) A soldier armed with a shield.<BR> E. फलक and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकयन्त्र|फलकयंत्र
फलकयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) An astronomical instrument invented by Bhāskarā-<BR>chārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकामना
फलकामना f. (-ना) Desire of any consequence.<BR> E. फल, and कामना desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकिन्
फलकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Having or being armed with a shield, &c.<BR>m. (-की) A sort of fish commonly Phalūi.<BR> E. फलक as above and<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकृष्ण|फलकृष्णः
फलकृष्ण m. (-ष्णः) A small fruit, (Carissa carandas.)<BR> E. फल fruit and<BR>कृष्ण black. “पानिआमलके” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकेशर|फलकेशरः
फलकेशर m. (-रः) The cocoanut-tree.<BR> E. फल the fruit and केशर hair,<BR>covered with a fibrous coat-like hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलकोषक|फलकोषकः
फलकोषक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The cocoanut-tree.<BR>	 2. The testicle.<BR> E. फल fruit,<BR>कोष sheath, and कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलखण्डन
फलखण्डन n. (-नं) Disappointing.<BR> E. फल and खण्डन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलग्रहि|फलग्रहिः
फलग्रहि mfn. (-हिः-हिः-हि) Fruitful, bearing fruit in due season.<BR> E. फल<BR>fruit, ग्रह् to take, aff. इन्, also फलेग्रहि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलग्राहिन्
फलग्राहिन् m. (-ही) A tree.<BR> E. फल fruit, ग्रह् to take, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलचमस|फलचमसः
फलचमस m. (-सः) The bark of the Indian fig, ground and eaten with<BR>curds, by way of penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलत्
फलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्) Yielding fruit, profit, &c.<BR> E. फल् to bear fruit, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलत्रय|फलत्रयं
फलत्रय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Three sorts of fruit collectively, as the fruit of the<BR>vine, the Parush, and the Gmelina arborea.<BR>	 2. The three myrobal-<BR>ans.<BR> E. फल fruit and त्रय three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलत्रिक|फलत्रिकं
फलत्रिक n. (-कं) The three myrobalans collectively.<BR> E. फल fruit, and त्रिक<BR>threefold. “शुण्ठीपिप्पली मरिचरूपायाम् च” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलद|फलदः
फलद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Yielding or bearing fruit, result, &c.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A<BR>tree.<BR> E. फल fruit, and द what gives; also फलदातृ, फलदायिन् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलन|फलनं
फलन n. (-नं) Fructifying, bearing fruit, producing consequences. E.<BR>फल, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलनिवृत्ति|फलनिवृत्तिः
फलनिवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Cessation of consequences.<BR> E. फल and निवृत्ति stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलनिर्वृत्ति
फलनिर्वृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Final consequence or result.<BR> E. फल and निर्वृत्ति<BR>completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलनिष्पत्ति|फलनिष्पत्तिः
फलनिष्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Bearing fruit.<BR>	 2. Yielding profit or desired re-<BR>sults.<BR> E. फल and निष्पत्ति putting forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपाक|फलपाकः
फलपाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The ripening of fruit.<BR>	 2. The fulness of conse-<BR>quences.<BR>	 3. The Caronda.<BR> E. फल fruit and पाक ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपाकान्ता
फलपाकान्ता f. (-न्ता) An annual plant.<BR> E. फल fruit, पाक ripening or ripe-<BR>ness, and अन्त end; dying after bearing fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपातन
फलपातन n. (-नं) Knocking down or gathering fruit.<BR> E. फल and पातन felling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपुच्छ|फलपुच्छः
फलपुच्छ m. (-च्छः) A sort of esculent root or bulb.<BR> E. फल fruit and पुच्छ<BR>a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपूर|फलपूरः
फलपूर m. (-रः) Common citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR> E. फल fruit and पूर् to fill, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलपूरक|फलपूरकः
फलपूरक m. (-कः) Common citron.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलप्रद|फलप्रदः
फलप्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Yielding fruit, productive, yielding a reward,<BR>&c.<BR> E. फल and प्रद what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलप्रदान
फलप्रदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A ceremony at weddings.<BR>	 2. The giving of fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलप्रयुक्त
फलप्रयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Connected with or producing consequences,<BR>yielding fruit, &c.<BR> E. फल and प्रयुक्त applied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलप्राप्ति|फलप्राप्तिः
फलप्राप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Obtaining the desired result or fruit.<BR> E. फल and प्राप्ति acquiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलप्रिया
फलप्रिया f. (-या) Priyangu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलबन्धिन्|फलबंधिन्
फलबन्धिन् Adj. Forming or developing fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलभाज्
फलभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Having or receiving fruit, consequence, &c.<BR> E. फल<BR>and माज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलभूमि|फलभूमिः
फलभूमि f. (-मिः) Any region not included in the known continent, as<BR>heaven, hell, &c.<BR> E. फल fruit, (of actions,) and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलभोग|फलभोगः
फलभोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Receipt or enjoyment of consequences.<BR>	 2. Possess-<BR>ion of rent or profit, usufruct.<BR> E. फल and भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलभोगिन्
फलभोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Who receives the profits, consequences,<BR>&c.<BR> E. फल and भोगिन् who enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलमुख्या
फलमुख्या f. (-ख्या) Common carroway. “अजमोदा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलमुद्गरिका
फलमुद्गरिका f. (-का) A sort of date.<BR> E. फल fruit and मुद्गर a mallet, aff.<BR>कन् in the fem. form. “पिण्डीखेजुर” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलयोग|फलयोगः
फलयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The attainment of an object.<BR>	 2. Remuneration, wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलराजन्
फलराजन् m. (-जा) The water-melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलवत्|फलवन्त्
फलवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Bearing fruit.<BR>	 2. Yielding results or con-<BR>sequences.<BR> E. फल fruit and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलशाडव|फलशाडवः
फलशाडव m. (-वः) The promegranate.<BR> E. फल fruit, शाड् to extol, aff. अव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलशालिन्
फलशालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Bearing or yielding fruit.<BR> E. फल and<BR>शलिन् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलश्रेष्ठ|फलश्रेष्ठः
फलश्रेष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) The mango.<BR> E. फल fruit and श्रेष्ठ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलस|फलसः
फलस m. (-सः) The jack or bread-fruit.<BR> E. फल fruit, सह् to be able. aff.<BR>डः also read फलशः see पनस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलसम्पद्|फलसंपद्
फलसम्पद् f. (पद् or -पत्) Prosperity, success.<BR> E. फल and सम्पत् abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलसम्भव
फलसम्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced in or by fruit.<BR> E. फल and सम्भव born<BR>also फलसम्भू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलसाधन
फलसाधन n. (-नं) Means or instrument of success.<BR> E. फल and साधन means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलसिद्धि|फलसिद्धिः
फलसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Realising an object, reaping the fruit of any act.<BR>E. फल and सिद्धि perfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलहानि|फलहानिः
फलहानि f. (-निः) Loss of fruit or profit.<BR> E. फल and हानि abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलहारी
फलहारी f. (-री) An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलाकाङ्क्षा|फलाकांक्षा
फलाकाङ्क्षा f. (-ङ्क्षा) Hope or expectation of favourable consequences.<BR>E. फल and आकाङ्क्षा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलागम|फलागमः
फलागम m. (-मः) The fruit-season, autumn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलादन|फलादनः
फलादन m. (-नः) A parrot.<BR> E. फल fruit, अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलाध्यक्ष|फलाध्यक्षं|फलाध्यक्षः
फलाध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) A tree, commonly Khirani, (Mimusops Kauki.)<BR> E. फल<BR>fruit, अध्यक्ष superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलान्त|फलान्तः
फलान्त m. (-न्तः) A bamboo.<BR> E. फल fruit or blossom, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलानुबन्ध|फलानुबंध|फलानुबन्धः
फलानुबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Sequence of results.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलानुमेय
फलानुमेय Adj. Inferable from consequences of results.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलानुसरण
फलानुसरण n. (-णं) Rate or aggregate of profits.<BR> E. फल and अनुसरण<BR>conformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलापेक्षा
फलापेक्षा f. (-क्षा) Regard to or expectation of consequences.<BR> E. फल and<BR>अपेक्षा expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलापेत
फलापेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unproductive, unfertile.<BR> E. फल and अपेत de-<BR>prived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलाभोग
फलाभोग m. (-गः) Non-enjoyment of profits, &c.<BR> E. फल and अभोग non-use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलायोषित्
फलायोषित् f. (-त्) A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलाशन|फलाशनः
फलाशन m. (-नः) A parrot.<BR> E. फल fruit and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलाशिन्
फलाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Living on fruits.<BR> E. फल and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलासक्त
फलासक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Doing any thing for the sake of reward.<BR>2. Fond of or seeking to pluck fruit.<BR> E. फल and आसक्त attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलि|फलिः
फलि m. (-लिः) A kind of fish. “फलुइ” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलिग
फलिग m. (-गः) The cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलित|फलितं|फलितः
फलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fruitful, bearing fruit.<BR>	 2. Successful, yielding<BR>a result.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A tree.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A woman in her courses.<BR> E. फल<BR>fruit and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलिन्
फलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>	 1. Bearing fruit, fruitful.<BR>	 2. Productive of<BR>consequences.<BR>	 m. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A sort of fish, commonly Phalūi, (Mys-<BR>tus kapirat.)<BR>	 2. A tree, (especially in fruit.)<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A medicinal<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">Page511-a+ 60</a>]<BR>plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>	 2. A potherb, (Echites dichotoma.)<BR>3. A flower, (Celosia cristata.)<BR> E. फल fruit, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलूष|फलूषः
फलूष m. (-षः) A sort of creeper.<BR> E. फल fruit, and ऊषन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलेग्रहि|फलेग्रहिः
फलेग्रहि mfn. (-हिः-हिः-हि) Bearing fruit in season, fruitful.<BR> E. फल fruit,<BR>ग्रह् to take, aff. इन्; ए substituted irregularly for the final of फल;<BR>also फलग्रहि and फलेग्राहिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलेग्राहिन्
फलेग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Bearing fruit in due season. E. As above, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलेपुष्पा
फलेपुष्पा f. (-ष्पा) A kind of flower known as “द्रोणपुष्पी” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलेरुहा
फलेरुहा f. (-हा) The trumpet-flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.)<BR> E. फल<BR>fruit, in the seventh case, रुह् to grow, aff. क । “पाटलिवृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोच्चय|फलोच्चयः
फलोच्चय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Collecting of fruits.<BR>	 2. A collection of fruits.<BR> E. फल<BR>and उच्चय abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोत्तमा
फलोत्तमा f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A small sort of grape without stones.<BR>	 2. The three<BR>myrobalans collectively.<BR>	 3. The benefit arising from sacred study.<BR>E. फल fruit, उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोत्पति
फलोत्पति(त्ति) m. (-तिः or त्ति) The mango.<BR>	 f. (-त्तिः) Production of fruit.<BR>E. फल fruit, उत् over, पति ruler; or फलाय उत्पत्तिरस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोदय|फलोदयः
फलोदय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Gain, profit.<BR>	 2. Heaven, paradise.<BR>	 3. Joy, happiness.<BR>4. Consequence, result.<BR> E. फल fruit, gain, &c. उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोद्देश|फलोद्देशः
फलोद्देश m. (-शः) Regard to results.<BR> E. फल and उद्देश pointing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोनि
फलोनि m. (-निः) Pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फलोपेत
फलोपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having or yielding fruit, &c.<BR> E. फल and उपेत possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्क|फल्कः
फल्क m. (-ल्कः) An expanded or extended body.<BR> E. फल् to separate,<BR>Unādi aff. क । “विशोधिताङ्गे च” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गु|फल्गुः
फल्गु mfn. (-ल्गुः-ल्गुः-ल्गु)<BR>	 1. Pithless, sapless.<BR>	 2. Vain, unprofitable,<BR>unmeaning, useless.<BR>	 3. Weak, feeble.<BR>	 f. (-ल्गुः)<BR>	 1. The opposite<BR>leaved fig-tree, (F. oppositi-folia, Rox.)<BR>	 2. The name of a river<BR>which is said to run underneath Gya.<BR>	 3. Falsehood, false or lying<BR>speech.<BR>	 4. A red powder, usually of the root of wild ginger, col-<BR>oured with sappan wood, and thrown over one another by the<BR>Hindus, at the Holi festival.<BR>	 5. The spring season.<BR> E. फल् to bear<BR>fruit, Unādi aff. गुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुन|फल्गुनः
फल्गुन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of ARJUNA. The month Phālguna.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>The constellation Phalguni.<BR> E. फल् to bear fruit, Unādi aff. उनन्<BR>and गुक् aug.: see फाल्गुन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्गुनाल|फल्गुनालः
फल्गुनाल m. (-लः) The month Phālguna.<BR> E. फल्गु, and अल equal to, the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्य|फल्यं
फल्य n. (-ल्यं) A bud, a flower.<BR> E. फल fruit, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फल्लकिन्
फल्लकिन् m. (-की) A fish, caught in ponds, commonly Phalūi, (Mystus kapirat.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाट्
फाट् Ind. An interjection of calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाणि|फाणिः
फाणि f. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. Unrefined sugar, molasses.<BR>	 2. Flour or meal mixed<BR>with curds.<BR> E. स्फायी to swell, Unādi aff. नि, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाणित|फाणितं
फाणित n. (-तं) Raw sugar, the inspissated juice of the sugarcane.<BR> E. फण्<BR>to go, causal form, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाण्ट|फांट|फाण्टं|फाण्टः
फाण्ट mfn. (-ण्टः-ण्टा-ण्टं) Readily prepared, made by an extemporaneous<BR>easy process, (decoction, &c.)<BR>	 n. (-ण्टं)<BR>	 1. Diluted decoction, decoc-<BR>tion, easily prepared.<BR>	 2. The first particles of butter that are<BR>produced by churning.<BR> E. फण् to prepare easily, aff. क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल|फालं|फालः
फाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Made of cotton, (vesture.)<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>SĪVA.<BR>	 2. A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>	 3. A citron tree.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The<BR>share of a plough.<BR> E. फल् to divide, in the causal form. aff. घञ्<BR>or फल fruit and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फालकृष्ट|फालकृष्टः
फालकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Furrowed, ploughed.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) A ploughed-field.<BR>E. फाल and कृष्ट furrowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुन|फाल्गुनः
फाल्गुन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of ARJUNA.<BR>	 2. A sort of tree, (Pentaptera<BR>Arjuna.)<BR>	 3. A month, commonly called by the name Phālguna,<BR>(February-March.)<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Day of full moon on the month of<BR>Phālguṇa, on which Holi or great vernal festival of the Hindus is<BR>celebrated.<BR>	 2. A name common to the eleventh and twelfth lunar<BR>asterisms, distinguished by the epithets first and last, or पूर्व्व and<BR>उत्तरफाल्गुनीः see पूर्व्वफाल्गुनी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुनानुज|फाल्गुनानुजः
फाल्गुनानुज m. (-जः) Spring.<BR> E. फाल्गुन the month, अनु according, ज<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फाल्गुनिक|फाल्गुनिकः
फाल्गुनिक m. (-कः) The month Phālguna.<BR> E. फाल्गुनी day of full moon<BR>in this month, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फि|फिः
फि m. (फिः) Anger, passion.<BR> E. फल् to separate, aff. डि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फिङ्गक|फिंगकः|फिङ्गकः
फिङ्गक m. (-कः) The fork-tailed shrike.<BR> E. फिङ्ग imitative sound, कै to<BR>utter, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फिरङ्ग|फिरंग|फिरंगः|फिरङ्गः
फिरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The country of the Franks.<BR>	 2. A particular disease.<BR>It is a word of foreign origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुक|फुकः
फुक m. (-कः) A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुट|फुटः
फुट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Blown.<BR>	 2. Burst.<BR>	 3. The hood or expanded neck<BR>of a snake.<BR> E. स्फुट् to swell, aff. क, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फु|फुः
फु(फू)त् Ind.<BR>	 1. Expression of disregard or contempt, (Phoo, hoot.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Imitative sound, implying the bubbling or boiling of water, &c.<BR>or of blowing into any liquid.<BR> E. स्फुर् to swell, aff. क्विप्, स rejected,<BR>and तुक् added, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुत्कर|फुत्करः
फुत्कर m. (-रः) Fire.<BR> E. फुत् boiling and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुत्कार|फुत्कारः
फुत्कार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Arrogant, contemptuous, disdainful.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The sound of bubbling or breathing into, (as to cool it.)<BR> E. फुत्<BR>expression of contempt, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुत्कृत
फुत्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Blown up, (as a bubble.)<BR>	 2. Blown into,<BR>cooled by blowing into it.<BR> E. फुत् and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुप्फुस|फुप्फुसः
फुप्फुस m. (-सः) The lungs see पुप्फुस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ल|फुल्लः
फुल्ल r. 1st cl. (फुल्लति) To blow or blossom, to bud or flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ल|फुल्लः
फुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>	 1. Blown, opened, expanded, (as a flower.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Opened, (as the eyes with pleasure, &c.), smiling, gay.<BR> E. फुल्ल् to<BR>blow, aff. अच्; also फुल्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लदामन्
फुल्लदामन् n. (-म) A species of the Atidhriti metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लनयन|फुल्लनयनः
फुल्लनयन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Full or large-eyed.<BR>	 2. Smiling, looking hap-<BR>py.<BR> E. फुल्ल and नयन the eye; also similar compounds, as फुल्लनेत्र,<BR>फुल्लदृष्टि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लफाल|फुल्लफालः
फुल्लफाल m. (-लः) Winnowing corn.<BR> E. फुल्ल blown, and फाल for स्फाल् spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लरीक|फुल्लरीकः
फुल्लरीक m. (-कः) A serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्ललोचन|फुल्ललोचनः
फुल्ललोचन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Full-eyed.<BR>	 2. Looking pleased or happy.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-नं) A large full eye.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A species of the antelope.<BR> E. फुल्ल्<BR>full, expanded, and लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लवत्|फुल्लवन्त्
फुल्लवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Blossoming, blowing.<BR> E. फुल्ल् to blow, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लवदन
फुल्लवदन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Looking pleased or happy.<BR> E. फुल्ल् and वदन<BR>the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लि|फुल्लिः
फुल्लि f. (-ल्लिः) Blowing, blossoming.<BR> E. फुल्ल् to blow, aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फुल्लति
फुल्लति f. (-तिः) Flowering, blossoming.<BR> E. फुल्ल् to blow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फूत्
फूत् Ind. Imitative sound of bubbling, sobbing, &c.: see फुत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फूत्कार
फूत्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Bubbling.<BR>	 2. Sobbing.<BR>	 3. Blowing or breathing into<BR>any liquid.<BR> E. फूत् and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फूत्कृत
फूत्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bubbled, bubbling, made to sound so.<BR>	 2.<BR>Blown or breathed into, (a liquid.)<BR>	 3. Sounded, as in sobbing. E.<BR>फूत्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फे
फे(ण)न m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Froth, foam.<BR>	 2. Cuttle-fish-bone, supposed to be the<BR>indurated foam of the sea.<BR>	 3. Vapour.<BR> E. स्फायी to swell, नक् Unādi<BR>aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फे
फे(ण)नक m. (-कः) Cuttle-fish-bone.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Rice, ground and boiled<BR>with water.<BR>	 2. The soap berry.<BR> E. फेन froth, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनता
फेनता f. (-ता) Frothiness, vapour.<BR> E. तल् added to फेन; also with त्व, फेनत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनल|फेनलः
फेनल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Frothy, foamy.<BR> E. फेन froth, अलच् poss. aff.; also<BR>with इलच् similar aff. फेनिल, and with the usual possessive मतुप्,<BR>फेनवत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनवत्|फेनवन्त्
फेनवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Frothy, foaming, bubbling.<BR> E. फेन froth and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनवाहिन्
फेनवाहिन् m. (-ही) The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR> E. फेन foam, वह् to bear,<BR>aff. णिनि; INDRA having used the foam of the sea for his thunder-<BR>bolt, to kill the demon VRITRĀSURA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनाग्र|फेनाग्रं
फेनाग्र n. (-ग्रं) A bubble.<BR> E. फेन foam, and अग्र top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनायमान|फेनायमानः
फेनायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Foaming, frothing.<BR> E. फेन nom. verb to foam,<BR>शनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनाशनि|फेनाशनिः
फेनाशनि m. (-निः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. फेन foam and अशनि the thund-<BR>bolt: see फेनवाहिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनि
फेनि(णि)का f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Froth arising from treacle.<BR>	 2. A kind of sweet-<BR>meat called Patty. “खाजा” ।<BR> E. फेन foam, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनिल|फेनिलं|फेनिलः
फेनिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Frothy, foamy.<BR>	 m. (-लः) The soap plant, (Sapin-<BR>dus detergens, Rox.)<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The fruit of the jujube.<BR>	 2. The<BR>fruit of the Vangueria spinosa.<BR> E. फेन froth or foam, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेर|फेरः
फेर m. (-रः) A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरण्ड|फेरंड|फेरंडः|फेरण्डः
फेरण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A jackal.<BR> E. फे imitative sound, रम् to sport, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरव|फेरवः
फेरव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Fraudulent, crafty, a rogue or cheat.<BR>	 2. Mali-<BR>cious, noxious, injurious.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A jackal.<BR>	 2. A demon, a<BR>goblin.<BR> E. फे imitative sound, रु to utter, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरु|फेरुः
फेरु m. (-रुः) A jackal.<BR> E. फे imitative sound, रु to cry, aff. डु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेल|फेलं
फेल (ऋ) फेऌ r. 1st cl. (फेलति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेलक|फेलकः
फेलक m. (-कः) Orts, leavings of a meal, or droppings from the mouth.<BR>E. फेल् to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेला
फेला f. (-ला) Orts, leavings.<BR> E. फेल् to go, अच् aff. fem. aff. टाप्; also फेलक and फेलि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेलि|फेलिः
फेलि f. (-लिः or -ली) Orts, leavings.<BR> E. फेल् to go, इन् aff.; ङीप् optionally<BR>added; also with टाप् and कन् added, फेलिका f. (-का) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फ्वल
फ्वल r. 1st. cl. (फ्वलति) to live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब|बः
ब The twenty-third consonant of the Nāgari Alphābet, corresponding<BR>to the letter B, and often confounded with the analogous semi-<BR>vowel व or V, with which some grammarians consider it to be at<BR>all times optionally interchangeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब|बः
ब m. (बः)<BR>	 1. A name of VARUṆA.<BR>	 2. A water jar.<BR>	 3. Ocean.<BR>	 4. The<BR>vulva.<BR> E. बण् to sound, &c. aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहिष्ठ|बंहिष्ठः
बंहिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very much, excessively many.<BR> E. बहु much, इष्ठन्<BR>superlative aff. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहीयस्
बंहीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-य) Very many.<BR> E. बहु much, ईयमुन् superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बठ
बठ r. 1st cl. (बठति) To be large, powerful, or able: better also वठ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवा
बडवा f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A mare.<BR>	 2. A female slave.<BR>	 3. The nymph AŚHWINI,<BR>or the personified asterism which is designated by a horse's head.<BR>E. बल strength or force, and वा to go to, affs. क and टाप्, and ल<BR>change to ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवाकृ
बडवाकृ(हृ)त m. (-तः) The gallant of a female slave, and thence also a<BR>slave.<BR> E. बडवा and कृत or हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवाग्नि|बडवाग्निः
बडवाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Submarine fire: see the next.<BR> E. बडवा a mare, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवानल|बडवानलः
बडवानल m. (-लः) Submarine fire; in mythology, a being consisting<BR>of flame, but with the head of a mare, who sprang from the thighs<BR>of AURVA^1, and was received by the ocean.<BR> E. बडवा a mare, and<BR>अनल fire.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260525. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/236.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवामुख|बडवामुखः
बडवामुख m. (-खः) Submarine fire: see बडवानल.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The infernal<BR>regions.<BR> E. वडबा a mare, and मुख head, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडवासुत
बडवासुत m. dual. (-तौ) The two sons of AŚHWINĪ and the physicians of<BR>heaven.<BR> E. बडवा the nymph AŚHWINĪ and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बण|बणः
बण r. 1st cl. (बणति) To sound; better also वण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बण|बणः
बण m. (-णः) Sound, noise.<BR> E. बण् to sound, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिक्पथ
बणिक्पथ n. (-थं) Traffic, commerce.<BR> E. बनिज् and पथ् for पथिन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिक्पत्त्र
बणिक्पत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) The son of a merchant or a young merchant or<BR>trader.<BR>	 f. (-त्त्री) A young woman of the same tribe.<BR> E. बणिज् and पुत्त्र<BR>a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिग्बन्धु|बणिग्बन्धुः
बणिग्बन्धु m. (-न्धुः) The indigo plant, (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR> E. बणिज् a<BR>trader, and बन्धु the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिग्भाव|बणिग्भावः
बणिग्भाव n. (-वं) Traffic, trade, commerce.<BR> E. बणिज् a trader, and भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिग्वह|बणिग्वहः
बणिग्वह m. (-हः) A camel.<BR> E. बणिज् a trader, वह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिज्
बणिज् m. (-णिक्)<BR>	 1. A merchant, a trader.<BR>	 2. The sixth of the astro-<BR>nomical periods called Karanas, corresponding to the half of a<BR>lunar day.<BR>	 f. (-णिक्) Trade, traffic.<BR> E. पण् to transact business, इजि<BR>Unādi aff. and ब substituted for प; also बणिज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बणिज्य|बणिज्यं
बणिज्य nf. (-ज्यं-ज्या) Trade, traffic.<BR> E. बणिज् a trader, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद
बद r. 1st cl. (बदति) To be steady or firm. r. 1st and 10th cls. (बदति-ते<BR>बादयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To declare or communicate informa-<BR>tion; in these two senses, the root is more commonly and correct-<BR>ly written वद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदर|बदरं|बदरः
बदर mf. (-रः-री)<BR>	 1. The jujube, (Zizyphus jujuba or scandens.)<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>The seed of the cotton pod.<BR>	 f. (-रा-री) Cotton.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A plant,<BR>(Mimosa octandra.)<BR>	 2. A medicinal drug, commonly Varāhakrānti.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The fruit of the jujube.<BR>	 2. The berry or pod of the cot-<BR>ton.<BR> E. बद् to be firm, Unādi aff. अरच्; or if derived from वद् to<BR>give information; it is read by some authorities वदर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरप
बदरप (पा) चन n. (-नं) Name of a sacred bathing place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरामलक|बदरामलकं
बदरामलक m. (-कः) A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR> E. बदर the jujube,<BR>आमलक myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरि|बदरिः
बदरि m. (-रिः) The jujube: see बदर.<BR> E. बद्द् to be firm, aff. अरि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरिकाश्रम|बदरिकाश्रमः
बदरिकाश्रम m. (-मः) The hermitage at Badarikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरी
बदरी f. (-रीः)<BR>	 1. The jujube tree.<BR>	 2. A name of one of the sources of the<BR>Ganges and the hermitage of Nara and Nārāyana.<BR> E. बदर, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीच्छदा|बदरीछदा
बदरीच्छदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. A kind of perfume, apparently a dried shell fish.<BR>2. A tree, apparently a species of the zizyphus.<BR> E. बदर the juju-<BR>be, छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीपत्रक|बदरीपत्रकं
बदरीपत्रक n. (-कं) A sort of perfume, a leaf.<BR> E. बदरी the jujube, पत्र a<BR>leaf, and कन् aff. of comparison added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीफला
बदरीफला f. (-ला) A plant, commonly blue Śephālikā or nyctanthes.<BR>E. बदरी the jujube, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीशैल|बदरीशैलः
बदरीशैल n. (-लं) A part of the Himālaya range, and a celebrated place<BR>of pilgrimage; the Badrināth of modern travellers, or a town<BR>and temple on the west bank of the Alakānanda river, in the<BR>province of Srinagar.<BR> E. बदरी the jujube and शैल mountain; also<BR>बदरीवन n. (-नं) The wood of jujubes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्ध|बद्धं
बद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Bound, tied.<BR>	 2. Checked, suppressed.<BR>	 3. Fixed,<BR>firm.<BR>	 4. Withheld.<BR>	 5. Captured.<BR>	 6. Confined.<BR>	 7. United.<BR>	 8. Dis-<BR>played.<BR>	 9. Cherished.<BR> E. बन्ध् to bind, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धकक्ष
बद्धकक्ष Adj. Having the girdle girt up, prepared, ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धकोप
बद्धकोप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. One who governs or suppresses wrath.<BR>	 2.<BR>Smothering resentment.<BR> E. वद्ध and कोप passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धचित्त
बद्धचित्त Adj. Riveting the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धजिह्व
बद्धजिह्व Adj. Tongue-tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धमूल|बद्धमूलं
बद्धमूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Fast or firmly rooted.<BR> E. बद्ध, and मूल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धशिख|बद्धशिखः
बद्धशिख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Young, a pupil, a child, one whose hair has<BR>not been shaven.<BR>	 f. (-खा) A sort of pungent root, a kind of<BR>garlic.<BR> E. बद्ध tied, and शिखा a crest or lock of hair, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धाञ्जलि|बद्धांजलि
बद्धाञ्जलि mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि) Saluting respectfully, putting the hands<BR>joined to the forehead.<BR> E. बद्ध attached, अञ्जलि the palms joined and<BR>touching the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धानुशय
बद्धानुशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Of fixed intent.<BR>	 2. Taking aim.<BR> E. बद्ध, and अनुशय purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध
बध r. 1st cl. (वीभत्सते)<BR>	 1. To bind or tie.<BR>	 2. To hate, to despise, to loathe.<BR>3. To suffer change or affection of the mind. r. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>(बधति-बाधयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To tie, to bind.<BR>	 2. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध
बध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter, slaying, murder.<BR>	 2. A killer, a slau-<BR>ghter.<BR> E. बध् substituted for हन् to kill, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधक
बधक m. (-कः) A slaughterer, a killer.<BR> E. हन् changed to बध and कुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधकाङ्क्षिन्
बधकाङ्क्षिन् mfn. (-ङ्क्षी-ङ्क्षिणी-ङ्खि) Wishing death.<BR> E. बध and काङ्क्षिन् who<BR>wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधकाम्या
बधकाम्या f. (-म्या) Intent or desire to kill.<BR> E. बध and काम्या desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधजीविन्
बधजीविन् m. (-वी) A hunter, a fowler, a butcher. &c.<BR> E. बध killing, and<BR>जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधत्र
बधत्र n. (-त्रं) A weapon.<BR> E. बध् to kill, Unādi aff. अत्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधदण्ड
बधदण्ड n. (-ण्डं) Capital punishment.<BR> E. बध and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधस्थली
बधस्थली f. (-ली) A place of slaughter or execution.<BR> E. बध killing, स्थल<BR>ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधस्थान
बधस्थान n. (-नं) Place of slaughter or execution.<BR> E. बध killing, स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधाङ्गक
बधाङ्गक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Poison.<BR>	 2. Prison.<BR> E. बध killing, अङ्ग the body,<BR>aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधार्ह
बधार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Deserving death.<BR> E. बध and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिर|बधिरः
बधिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Deaf.<BR> E. बन्ध् to bind, (the hearing.) aff. किरच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधू
बधू f. (-धूः)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. A wife.<BR> E. बन्ध् to bind, aff. ऊ; it is more<BR>usually derived from वह् to bear, and is consequently written with<BR>the semi-vowel: see वधू &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधोदर्क
बधोदर्क mfn. (-र्कः-र्का-कं) Effecting or causing death,<BR> E. बध, and उदरक future result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधोद्यत
बधोद्यत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Murderous, felonious, an assassin, a murderer.<BR>E. बध killing, and उद्यत endeavouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधोपाय
बधोपाय m. (-यः) Instrument or means of putting to death.<BR> E. बध, and उपाय means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्य
बध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Deserving death.<BR>	 2. Condemned to death. E.<BR>बध् for हन् to kill, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्यता
बध्यता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Destruction.<BR>	 2. Fitness to be killed.<BR> E. बध्य, and तल् aff.;<BR>also with त्व, बध्यत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्यभूमि
बध्यभूमि f. (-मिः) Place of public execution.<BR> E. बध्य and भूमि site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्यस्थान
बध्यस्थान n. (-नं) Place of execution.<BR> E. बध्य, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धा
बद्धा Ind.<BR>	 1. Having tied or bound.<BR>	 2. Having killed.<BR> E. बन्ध् to tie, or<BR>बध् to kill, and क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्र|बध्रं
बध्र n. (-ध्रं) Lead.<BR>	 f. (-ध्री) A thong.<BR> E. वन्ध् to bind, aff. ष्ट्रन्; see वर्द्ध and वर्द्धी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्र्य
बध्र्य n. (-ध्र्यं) A shoe, a slipper.<BR> E. बन्ध् to bind or tie, ष्ट्रान् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन
बन (उ) (बनु) r. 8th cl. (बनुते) To ask or beg, preferably written वन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध|बंध|बंधः|बन्धः
बन्ध r. 9th. cl. (बध्नाति) r. 10th cl. (बन्धयति-ते) To bind or tie; with आङ्<BR>prefixed. To loosen, to let loose. With अनु, 1. To follow.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>affixed or attached to. With नि, to disunite. With सम्, to connect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध|बंध|बंधः|बन्धः
बन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. A pledge, a deposit.<BR>	 2. A binding, a tie or fetter, &c.<BR>3. Binding, tying.<BR>	 4. The body.<BR>	 5. Joining.<BR>	 6. Forming.<BR>	 7. A li-<BR>gature, a bandage.<BR>	 8. Connection, intercourse.<BR>	 9. Agreement,<BR>union.<BR>	 10. Result.<BR>	 11. Border, frame-work.<BR>	 12. The body.<BR>	 13.<BR>Manifestation, display.<BR>	 14. Bondage, (opposite to annihilation.)<BR>15. A posture.<BR>	 16. The different forms of sexual intercourse men-<BR>tioned in Kāma Shāstra.<BR>	 17. Feeling.<BR>	 18. Laying snares.<BR>	 19. A<BR>stanza which can be arranged in a particular shape, as “Padma<BR>bandha,” &c.<BR> E. बन्ध् to tie, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धक|बंधक|बन्धकं|बंधकः|बन्धकः
बन्धक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Exchanging, barter.<BR>	 2. A city.<BR>	 3. A binding, 4. Bind-<BR>ing, confinement.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A pledge.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>	 1. An unchaste wo-<BR>man, a harlot, a wanton.<BR>	 2. A barren woman.<BR>	 3. A she-elephant,<BR>E. बन्ध् to bind, ण्वुल् aff. fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धतन्त्र|बंधतंत्र
बन्धतन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A complete army, or one with its four divisions, of chari-<BR>ots, elephants, horse and foot.<BR> E. बन्ध् binding, तन्त्र an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धन|बंधन|बन्धनं
बन्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Binding, tying, confining.<BR>	 2. A rope for tying cattle.<BR>3. Killing.<BR>	 4. Hurting, injuring.<BR>	 mfn. Subst. (-नः-ना or -नी-नं) The<BR>implement of binding or tying, a rope, a chain, a bandage, a liga-<BR>ture, &c.<BR> E. बन्ध् to tie, aff. ल्युट् or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनग्रन्थि|बंधनग्रंथि|बन्धनग्रन्थिः
बन्धनग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः)<BR>	 1. A rope for tying cattle.<BR>	 2. The knot of a ligature.<BR>E. बन्धन tying, and ग्नन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनरज्जु
बन्धनरज्जु f. (-ज्जुः)<BR>	 1. A rope for tying cattle, &c.<BR>	 2. Any rope or string<BR>used for tying.<BR> E. बन्धन tying, रज्जु a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनवेश्मन्|बंधनवेश्मन्
बन्धनवेश्मन् n. (-श्म) A prison.<BR> E. बन्धन confinement, and वेश्मन् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनालय|बंधनालय|बन्धनालयः
बन्धनालय m. (-यः) A prison.<BR> E. बन्धन confinement and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धस्तम्भ|बंधस्तंभ|बन्धस्तम्भः
बन्धस्तम्भ m. (-म्भः) The post to which an elephant is tied.<BR> E. बन्ध् a bind-<BR>ing and स्तम्भ a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धित्र|बन्धित्रं|बंधित्रः|बन्धित्रः
बन्धित्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Love, desire.<BR>	 2. A leathern fan.<BR> E. बन्ध् to bind, इत्र<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धु|बंधु|बंधुः|बन्धुः
बन्धु m. (-न्धुः)<BR>	 1. A kinsman, a relation, but especially a distant or cog-<BR>nate kinsman, and subsequent in right of inheritance to the gen-<BR>tile or Sagotra; the Bandhu, is of three kinds; the kinsman of<BR>the person himself, of his father or his mother, as his father's<BR>brother's son, and his mother's sister's or brother's son; and the<BR>same reckoning upwards, as his father's father's sister's son, &c.<BR>2. A friend.<BR>	 3. A brother.<BR>	 4. A flower, (Pentapetes phœnicea.) E.<BR>बन्ध् to bind or connect, (in affection.) उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुक|बंधुक|बंधुकः|बन्धुकः
बन्धुक m. (-कः) A flower: see बन्धूक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुजन|बंधुजन|बन्धुजनः
बन्धुजन m. (-नः) A relation, a friend.<BR> E. बन्धु, and जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुजीव|बंधुजीव|बन्धुजीवः
बन्धुजीव m. (-वः) A flower, (Pentapetes Phœnicea.)<BR> E. बन्धु a friend, जीव्<BR>to live, aff. अच्; also कन् being added, बन्धुजीवक m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुता|बंधुता
बन्धुता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A multitude of relations.<BR>	 2. Relationship.<BR> E. बन्धु a<BR>kinsman, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुत्व|बंधुत्वं
बन्धुत्व n. (-त्वं) Relationship.<BR> E. बन्धु and त्व aff.; also with तल् बन्धुता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुदत्त|बंधुदत्त
बन्धुदत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Given by a kinsman.<BR>	 n. (-त्तं) One kind of fe-<BR>male property, that given to a girl at her marriage by her own<BR>relations.<BR> E. बन्धु and दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुर|बंधुर|बन्धुरं|बन्धुरः
बन्धुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Uneven, undulating, wavy, partially even and de-<BR>pressed.<BR>	 2. Bowed, bent.<BR>	 3. Pleasing, delightful, handsome, beauti-<BR>ful.<BR>	 4. Deaf.<BR>	 5. Injurious, mischievous.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A goose.<BR>	 2. A<BR>flower, (Pentapetes Phœnicea.)<BR>	 3. A drug, commonly Biranga.<BR>	 4. A<BR>bird.<BR>	 5. A crane.<BR>	 6. A drug, commonly Rishabha.<BR>	 7. The vulva.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A diadem, a crest.<BR>	 2. The dregs of oil, or oil-cake.<BR>	 3.<BR>A hole.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A whore, a prostitute.<BR>	 f. plu. (-राः) The meal of<BR>parched corn.<BR> E. बन्ध् to bind, उरच् Unādi aff.; also with ऊरच्<BR>aff. बन्धूर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुल|बंधुल|बन्धुलः
बन्धुल f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Bent, inclined.<BR>	 2. Attractive.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A bastard.<BR>2. An attendant in the chamber of a harlot.<BR>	 3. The Bandhuka<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुहीन|बंधुहीन
बन्धुहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Friendless, relationless.<BR> E. बन्धु and हीन devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूक|बंधूक|बंधूकः|बन्धूकः
बन्धूक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A shrub bearing a red flower, (Pentapetes Phœnicea,<BR>but also applied to the Ixora Bandhūca.)<BR>	 2. A tree, (Pentaptera.)<BR>3. A bastard.<BR> E. बन्ध् to bind, ऊक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूकपुष्प|बन्धूकपुष्पः
बन्धूकपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR> E. बन्धूक the Penta-<BR>petes or Ixora and पुष्प flower; having a similar flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूर|बंधूर|बन्धूरः
बन्धूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Wavy, undulating, uneven.<BR>	 2. Bowing, bent.<BR>3. Beautiful, handsome.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A hole, a chasm.<BR> E. बन्ध् to bind,<BR>Unādi aff. ऊरच्; also बन्धुर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूलि|बंधूलि|बंधूलिः|बन्धूलिः
बन्धूलि m. (-लिः) A flower, (Pentapetes, &c.): see बन्धूक.<BR> E. बन्ध् and ऊलिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्य|बंध्य|बन्ध्यः
बन्ध्य mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्या-न्ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Barren, unfruitful, not bearing fruit in due<BR>season.<BR>	 2. Detained, confined, under arrest.<BR>	 f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>	 1. A child-<BR>less woman.<BR>	 2. A barren cow.<BR>	 3. A perfume, commonly Bālā. E.<BR>बन्ध् to bind, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभूवस्
बभूवस् mfn. (-वान्-भूषी-वः) Been, become.<BR> E. भू to be, बसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्र
बभ्र r. 1st cl. (बभ्रति) To go; also वभ्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रवी
बभ्रवी f. (-वी) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. बभ्रु ŚIVA, and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रि|बभ्रिः
बभ्रि mfn. (-भ्रिः-भ्रिः-भ्रि) Who or what has, holds, possesses, &c.<BR> E. भृ to<BR>cherish, किन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बभ्रु|बभ्रुः
बभ्रु mfn. (-भ्रुः-भ्रुः or -भ्रूः-भ्रु)<BR>	 1. Large, great.<BR>	 2. Tawny, &c.<BR>	 3. Bald-<BR>headed through disease.<BR>	 m. (-भ्रुः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. SĪVA.<BR>3. AGNI or fire.<BR>	 4. A large ichneumon.<BR>	 5. The name of a<BR>Muni or holy sage.<BR>	 6. A rat.<BR>	 n. (-भ्रु)<BR>	 1. A tawny or brown<BR>colour.<BR>	 2. Any object of that colour.<BR> E. भृ to fill, aff. कु, and the<BR>initial repeated; or बभ्र, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बम्भर|बंभर|बंभरः|बम्भरः
बम्भर m. (-रः) A bee.<BR> E. बम्भ् imitative sound, रा to make, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बम्भराली|बंभराली
बम्भराली f. (-ली) A fly.<BR> E. बम्भ् imitative sound, रा to make, लच् aff.: also<BR>भम्भराली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर
बर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Best, excellent.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A boon, a blessing, &c.<BR>2. A Son-in-law.<BR>	 3. Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>	 4. A catamite.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-र) Saffron.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Asparagus racemosus.<BR>	 f. (-रा) The three my-<BR>robalans.<BR>	 n. or ind. (-रं) Slightly desired, preferable.<BR> E. बॄ, to<BR>select, &c. अच् aff.; the root is more usually written वॄ, and the<BR>derivative वर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्ब|बर्ब
बर्ब्ब (र्ब) r. 1st cl. (बर्ब्बति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्बट|बर्बट|बर्बटः|बर्ब्बटः
बर्ब्बट mf. (-टः-टी) A sort of bean, (Dolichos catjang.) “बरबटी” f. (-टी) A<BR>whore.<BR> E. बर्ब्ब् to go, अट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्बणा|बर्बणा
बर्ब्बणा f. (-णा) A blue fly.<BR> E. बर्ब्ब् to go, aff. युच् or ल्यु; or derived from<BR>बर् imitative sound, and बण् or वण् to sound, aff. अच्, बर्ब्बण or<BR>बर्ब्बण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ब्बर|बर्बर|बर्बरः
बर्ब्बर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A blockhead, a fool.<BR>	 2. A barbarian.<BR> E. बर्ब्ब् to go, अरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्बुर|बर्बुरः
बर्बुर n. (-रं) Water.<BR> E. बर्ब-उरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ह|बर्हं|बर्हः
बर्ह r. 1st cl. (बर्हते)<BR>	 1. To be pre-eminent or excellent; (also वर्ह, but less<BR>usually.<BR>	 2. To speak or tell.<BR>	 3. To kill or hurt.<BR>	 4. To cover.<BR>	 5. To<BR>remember.<BR>	 6. To spread.<BR>	 7. To give. (In these senses it is more<BR>usually वर्ह.) r. 10th cl. (-बर्हयति) To hurt or kill; also वर्ह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्ह|बर्हं|बर्हः
बर्ह mn. (-र्हः-र्हं)<BR>	 1. A peacock's tail.<BR>	 2. A leaf.<BR>	 3. Dependents, retinue.<BR>E. बर्ह to spread, &c. aff. अच्; this word and the corresponding<BR>forms are more usually derived from वृह् to increase, &c. and are<BR>written with the semi-vowel: see वर्ह, वर्हिस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल|बलं|बलः
बल r. 1st and 10th cls. (बलति बलयति)<BR>	 1. To live.<BR>	 2. To hoard<BR>grain.<BR>	 3. To prevent or obstruct wealth. r. 1st cl. (बलते)<BR>	 1. To kill<BR>2. To go. r. 10th cl. (बालयते) To explain. (बालयति) To support,<BR>nourish, rear, as a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल|बलं|बलः
बल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Strong, stout, robust, powerful.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. BALA-<BR>DEVA, the elder brother of KṚṢṆA, and the third of the three<BR>incarnations termed RAMĀS.<BR>	 2. A crow.<BR>	 3. A demon, slain by IN-<BR>DRA.<BR>	 4. The Varunā tree.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Strength, power.<BR>	 2. Bulkiness.<BR>3. Form, figure.<BR>	 4. An army, forces.<BR>	 5. Gum myrrh.<BR>	 6. Semen<BR>virile.<BR>	 7. The body.<BR>	 8. The leaf of a tree.<BR>	 9. Blood.<BR>	 10. Rigour,<BR>severity.<BR>	 f. (-ला) An aquatic plant, (Sida cordifolia.)<BR> E. बल् to live,<BR>aff. अच्; in some of the senses it may be derived from वल् to go or<BR>surround, and may then be written with the semi-vowel; see वल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलक्ष|बलक्षः
बलक्ष m. (-क्षः) White, (the colour, &c.)<BR> E. बल strength, and क्षै to waste,<BR>aff. क; this word is more properly written वलक्ष, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलज|बलजं
बलज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by or from strength or power.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>1. A field.<BR>	 2. A city-gate.<BR>	 3. Fruit.<BR>	 4. War.<BR>	 5. Pith, marrow.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-जा)<BR>	 1. A pretty or handsome woman.<BR>	 2. The earth.<BR>	 3. Arabian<BR>jasmine.<BR> E. बल strength, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलद|बलदः
बलद m. (-दः) An ox.<BR> E. बल, द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलद्विष्
बलद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. बल, and द्विष् a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलदेव|बलदेवः
बलदेव m. (-वः) BALADEVA, the elder brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>f. (-वा) A medicinal plant, commonly Trāyamāṇa.<BR> E. बल the same<BR>and देव divine, or बल strength, and देव who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलनिग्रह
बलनिग्रह m. (-हः) Weakening, reducing strength or power.<BR> E. बल, and<BR>निग्रह restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलप्रसू
बलप्रसू f. (-सूः) ROHINĪ, the mother of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. बल and प्रसू the<BR>mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभद्र|बलभद्रः
बलभद्र m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. BALADEVA.<BR>	 2. ANANTA, the great serpent, consi-<BR>dered as identified with the proceding, BALADEVA being re-<BR>garded by some authorities as an incarnation of ANANTA.<BR>	 3. A<BR>strong or robust man.<BR>	 4. A tree, commonly Lodh.<BR>	 f. (-द्रा)<BR>	 1. A<BR>young girl, a maiden.<BR>	 2. A drug, commonly Trāyamāṇa.<BR> E. बल<BR>strength, and भद्र auspicious, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभद्रिका
बलभद्रिका f. (-का) A medicinal plant, Trāyamāṇa.<BR> E. बलभद्र the<BR>same, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभिद्
बलभिद् mfn. (-भिद्) Breaking or routing an army.<BR>	 m. (-भिद्) INDRA. E.<BR>बल and भिद् who or what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलराम|बलरामः
बलराम m. (-मः) The demi-god named BALARĀMA, half brother to<BR>KṚṢṆA, and the third of the RĀMAS; according to some, the<BR>eighth Avatār of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. बल strength, रम् to sport, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलल|बललः
बलल m. (-लः) BALARĀMA: see the last.<BR> E. बल strength, aff. कलच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवत्|बलवन्त्
बलवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Strong, stout, lusty, powerful.<BR> E. बल<BR>strength, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवत्ता
बलवत्ता f. (-त्ता) Strength, power.<BR> E. बलवत्, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलबर्द्धन
बलबर्द्धन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Strengthe ning.<BR>	 2. Ennobling.<BR> E. बल, and<BR>वर्द्धन augmenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवर्द्धिन्
बलवर्द्धिन् mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि) Strengthening.<BR>	 f. (-र्द्धिनी) A plant: see<BR>जीवक.<BR> E. बल, and वर्द्धिन् what augments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलविन्यास|बलविन्यासः
बलविन्यास m. (-सः) Array of troops.<BR> E. बल forces and विन्यास disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवृत्रनिसूदन
बलवृत्रनिसूदन m. (-नः) INDRA.<BR> E. बल and वृत्र two demons, and निसूदन<BR>destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवृत्रहन्
बलवृत्रहन् m. (-हा) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. बलवृत्र as before, हन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलव्यसन
बलव्यसन n. (-नं) Defeat or rout of an army.<BR> E. बल, व्यसन calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलशालिता
बलशालिता f. (-ता) Pride of, or confidence in strength or prowess.<BR> E. बल-<BR>शालि, and तल् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलशालिन्
बलशालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Having strength, confident of strength, &c.<BR>E. बल, and शालिन् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलसूदन|बलसूदनः
बलसूदन m. (-नः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. बल the demon, and सूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलस्थिति|बलस्थितिः
बलस्थिति f. (-तिः) A royal residence, a royal camp or quarters.<BR> E. बल<BR>forces, स्थिति station.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलहन्
बलहन् m. (-हा) Phlegm, the phlegmatic humour.<BR> E. बल strength and हन् destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलहीन
बलहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Weak, infirm.<BR> E. बल and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलहीनता
बलहीनता f. (-ता) Exhaustion, weakness, prostration of strength, infirm-<BR>ity from fatigue or age, &c.<BR> E. बलहीन and तल् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाका
बलाका f. (-का) A sort of crane.<BR> E. बल strength, अक् to go, aff. अच्; it is<BR>preferably written वलाका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाञ्चिता|बलांचिता
बलाञ्चिता f. (-ता) A sort of Vina or lute, called also RĀMA'S lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाट|बलाटः
बलाट m. (-टः) A sort of bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR> E. बल strength, and<BR>अट what goes or grows. “मुग इति भाषा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलात्कार|बलात्कारः
बलात्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Violence, oppression, exaction.<BR>	 2. (In law.) The de-<BR>tention of the person of a debtor by his creditor, and the violent<BR>measures taken by the latter, (flogging, &c.) to recover his debt.<BR>E. बल strength, अत् to go, aff. क्विप्, बलात्, and कार making, doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलात्मिका
बलात्मिका f. (-का) A sort of sun-flower, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR> E. बल<BR>strength, आत्मन् self, aff. कन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाध्यक्ष|बलाध्यक्षः
बलाध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) Commander of an army, a general.<BR> E. बल and अध्यक्ष<BR>superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलान्वित
बलान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Strong, powerful.<BR>	 2. Leading an army. E.<BR>बल and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलानुज|बलानुजः
बलानुज m. (-जः) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. बल, BALARĀMA, and अनुज younger born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलापकर्षम्
बलापकर्षम् Ind. By force.<BR> E. बल and अपकर्ष removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाबल
बलाबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Strong and weak.<BR> E. बल, and अबल feeble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाय|बलायः
बलाय m. (-यः) A plant, (Capparis trifoliata.)<BR> E. बल strength, अय to<BR>go, aff. अच् । “वरुणवृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाराति|बलारातिः
बलाराति m. (-तिः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. बल a demon, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलालक|बलालकः
बलालक m. (-कः) The Caronda, (Carissa carandas,)<BR> E. बल strength, आङ्<BR>before, ला to get, aff. वुन् । “पानीयामलके” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलावलेप|बलावलेपः
बलावलेप m. (-पः) Pride of strength or prowess.<BR> E. बल, and अवलेप pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाश|बलाशः
बलाश m. (-शः) The phlegmatic humour.<BR> E. बल strength, अश् to eat or<BR>destroy, aff. अच्; also with कन् added बलाशक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलास|बलासः
बलास m. (-सः) The phlegmatic humour.<BR> E. बल life or strength, अस् to<BR>pervade, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलासम|बलासमः
बलासम m. (-मः) One of the Jaina saints.<BR> E. बल strength, असम unequalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाह|बलाहं|बलाहः
बलाह n. (-हं) Water.<BR> E. बल strength, आहा to quit, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाहक|बलाहकः
बलाहक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A mountain.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. One of the Nāgas or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">Page515-a+ 60</a>]<BR>infernal serpents.<BR>	 4. The name of a demon.<BR>	 5. A kind of crane.<BR>6. Name of one of the seven clouds which arise at the end of the<BR>world.<BR> E. बल strength, अ the negative prefix to हा to abandon,<BR>aff. क्वुन्, this word is differently derived also, and preferably<BR>written वलाहक, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलि|बलिः
बलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. Tax, royal revenue.<BR>	 2. An oblation, religious offering<BR>in general.<BR>	 3. The handle of a Chowrie or fly-flapper.<BR>	 4. Presenta-<BR>tion of food to all created beings, one of the five great sacraments<BR>of the Hindu religion: it consists in throwing a small parcel of<BR>the offering Ghee or rice, or the like, into the open air at the back<BR>of the house.<BR>	 5. The sacrifice of an animal, or raw flesh offered to<BR>the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 6. Fragments of food left at an oblation or a<BR>meal.<BR>	 7. An animal, or one which is fit for an oblation.<BR>	 8. Three-<BR>folds of skin at the end of the rectum.<BR>	 9. A king, and Daitya, also<BR>MAHĀBALI, the virtuous sovereign of Mahābalipur, tricked out<BR>of the dominion he had obtained over earth and heaven, by VISH-<BR>ṆU, in the Vāmana or dwarf Avatar, and left in consideration<BR>of his merits, the sovereignty of Pātāla, or the infernal regions.<BR>f. (-लिः-ली)<BR>	 1. A wrinkle, skin shrivelled by old age.<BR>	 2. The fold of<BR>skin in stout persons, especially females, upon the upper part of<BR>the belly, or between the ensiform cartilage and the navel.<BR>	 3.<BR>The ridge of a thatch.<BR> E. बल् to live, or बध् to hurt or kill, ध<BR>changed to ल, aff. इन् or इ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिक
बलिक m. (-कः) The edge of a thatch.<BR> E. बलि the ridge, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिकर
बलिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Offering sacrifices.<BR>	 2. Producing wrinkles. E.<BR>बलि before, क्त to make, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिकरम्भ|बलिकरम्भः
बलिकरम्भ m. (-म्भः) Sacrificial cake.<BR> E. बलि, and करम्भ a sort of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिकर्म्मन्|बलिकर्मन्
बलिकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Offering of oblation to all creatures.<BR> E. बलि, and<BR>कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिदान|बलिदानं
बलिदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Offering victims in sacrifice.<BR>	 2. Giving food to all be-<BR>ings.<BR> E. बलि, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिध्वंसिन्
बलिध्वंसिन् m. (-सी) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. बलि the king so named, and ध्वंसिन् injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिन्
बलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Strong, stout, robust.<BR>	 m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A camel.<BR>	 2.<BR>A buffalo.<BR>	 3. A bull.<BR>	 4. A hog.<BR>	 5. Phlegm.<BR>	 6. A name of BALA-<BR>RĀMA.<BR>	 7. A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR>	 8. A sort of jas-<BR>mine, (J. Pubescens.)<BR>	 f. (-नी) Sida cordifolia.<BR> E. बल strength,<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिन|बलिनः
बलिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shrivelled, wrinkled, flabby, flaccid.<BR> E. बलि<BR>wrinkled skin, aff. न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिनन्दन|बलिनंदन|बलिनन्दनः
बलिनन्दन m. (-नः) VĀNĀSUR, the son of BALI.<BR> E. बलि, and नन्दन the<BR>son; BALI had however four sons, to either of whom the epithet<BR>is applicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिन्दम|बलिंदम|बलिंदमः
बलिन्दम m. (-मः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. बलि, and दम् to humble, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिपुष्ट|बलिपुष्टः
बलिपुष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A crow.<BR> E. बलि fragments of food, and पुष्ट nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिप्रिय|बलिप्रियः
बलिप्रिय m. (-यः) The Lodh tree.<BR> E. बलि sacrifice, and प्रिय fond of;<BR>said to grow the quicker for being perfumed and illuminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिभ|बलिभः
बलिभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Shrivelled, withered, flaccid, wrinkled.<BR> E. बलि a<BR>wrinkle, भ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिभुज्
बलिभुज् m. (-भुक्)<BR>	 1. A crow.<BR>	 2. A sparrow.<BR>	 3. A crane.<BR> E. बलि the orts<BR>of a meal or sacrifice, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिमत्|बलिमन्त्
बलिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Wrinkled, shrivelled, flaccid.<BR> E. बलि a wrin-<BR>kle, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिमन्दिर|बलिमंदिर|बलिमन्दिरं
बलिमन्दिर n. (-रं) The infernal regions.<BR> E. बलि the Daitya, and मन्दिर abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिमुख|बलिमुखः
बलिमुख m. (-खः) A monkey.<BR> E. बलि a wrinkle, and मुख a face: also<BR>बलीमुख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिष्ठ|बलिष्ठः
बलिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very strong, more or most powerful.<BR> E. बल, and इष्ठन् super. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिष्णु|बलिष्णुः
बलिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Arrogant, disrespectful.<BR> E. बल् to be powerful,<BR>इष्णु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिसङ्ग
बलिसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The lash of a whip.<BR>	 2. A number of monkeys.<BR>	 3.<BR>The base of an ant-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिसद्मन्
बलिसद्मन् n. (द्म) The infernal regions.<BR> E. बलि the Daitya, sovereign of<BR>Pātāla, and सद्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिहन्
बलिहन् m. (-हा) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. बलि BALI, and हन् to injure, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीक|बलीकं|बलीकः
बलीक m. (-कः) The edge of a thatched roof.<BR> E. वृ to cover, इकन् aff.;<BR>see बलिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीन|बलीनः
बलीन m. (-नः) A scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीमुख|बलीमुखः
बलीमुख m. (-खः) A monkey.<BR> E. बली a wrinkle, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीयस्
बलीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very strong, exceedingly powerful.<BR> E. बल<BR>strong, ईयसुन् superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीयस्त्व
बलीयस्त्व n. (-स्त्वं) Superiority in strength.<BR> E. बलीयस् and त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलीवर्द्द|बलीवर्द|बलीवर्दः|बलीवर्द्दः
बलीवर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) A bull or ox.<BR> E. बल strength, and वर्द्ध increasing, ली<BR>substituted for ल, and द final for ध; also बरीवर्द्द and वलीवर्द्द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलूल|बलूलः
बलूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Strong.<BR> E. बल + सिध्मा० वालच्-ऊङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलोपविष्ट
बलोपविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Endowed with or possessed of strength. E.<BR>बल, and उपविष्ट entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलोपेत
बलोपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Possessed of strength.<BR> E. बल, and उपेत possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल्य|बल्यं|बल्यः
बल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Strong, vigorous.<BR>	 n. (-ल्यं) Semen virile.<BR>	 m. (-ल्यः)<BR>A Bauddha mendicant.<BR> E. बल strength, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल्लव|बल्लवः
बल्लव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A cowherd.<BR>	 2. A cook.<BR>	 3. The name assumed by Bhima<BR>when living in disguise at the palace of VIRĀTA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल्वज|बल्वजः
बल्वज mf. (-जः-जा) A kind of grass. “उलपे तृणभेदे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बष्क
बष्क(स्क)य(यि)णी(नी) f. (-णी or -नी) A cow bearing many calves: see वष्कयणी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बस्त|बस्तः
बस्त m. (-स्तः) A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह
बह (इ) बहि r. 1st cl. (बंहते) To grow or increase; also बहि, but upon<BR>inferior authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहल|बहलः
बहल f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Much.<BR>	 2. Dense.<BR>	 3. Hard.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A kind of sugarcane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहिस्
बहिस् Ind. Out of doors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहु
बहु mfn. (-हुः-हुः-ह्वी-हु)<BR>	 1. Much, many.<BR>	 2. Large, great.<BR> E. बहि to in-<BR>crease, Unādi aff. कु; it is less correctly derived from वह् to obtain<BR>and written वहु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुक|बहुकः
बहुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A crab.<BR>	 2. A gallinule.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Asclepias<BR>gigantea.)<BR>	 4. The digger of a tank, (जलखातके.)<BR> E. बहु much,<BR>कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुकण्टक|बहुकण्टकः
बहुकण्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A prickly plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>marshy date tree.<BR> E. बहु many, कण्ट a thorn, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुकर|बहुकरः
बहुकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. A sweeper.<BR>	 2. Industrious, labouring.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः) A camel.<BR>	 f. (-री) A broom.<BR> E. बहु much, कृ to do, अप् or अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुक्षम|बहुक्षमः
बहुक्षम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Patient, enduring.<BR>	 m. (-मः) A Jaina deified saint.<BR>E. बहु much, and क्षम् to bear, aff. ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुगन्ध|बहुगन्धं|बहुगन्धः
बहुगन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Smelling, strong-scented.<BR>	 m. (-न्धः) Olibanum.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-न्धा)<BR>	 1. Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 2. The bud of the Champaka.<BR> E. बहु<BR>much, गन्ध odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुगर्ह्यवाच्
बहुगर्ह्यवाच् mfn. (-वाक्) Talking much and blameably.<BR> E. बहु much,<BR>गर्ह्य reproachable, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुगुण
बहुगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Many times.<BR>	 2. Having many good qualities.<BR>E. बहु and गुण quality, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुग्रन्थि|बहुग्रन्थिः
बहुग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) Tamarisk, (Tamarix diœca.)<BR> E. बहु many and ग्रन्थि a<BR>knot or joint. “झाउवृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुग्रह
बहुग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) What takes or holds much.<BR> E. बहु, and ग्रह what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतन्त्रि|बहुतन्त्रिः
बहुतन्त्रि mfn. (-न्त्रिः-न्त्री-न्त्रि) Many-fibred, (applicable only to the body)<BR>E. बहु many, and तन्त्री a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतन्त्रीक|बहुतंत्रीक|बहुतन्त्रीकः
बहुतन्त्रीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Many-stringed, (a musical instrument, &c.) E.<BR>बह् many, तन्त्री a wire, and कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतर
बहुतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Much, many, most.<BR> E. तरप् aff. added to बहु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतस्
बहुतस् Ind. From or by much, or many.<BR> E. बहु much, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुतिथ|बहुतिथः
बहुतिथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Manieth, (the ordinary of many.)<BR> E. बहु many,<BR>much, इट् aff. and तिथुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्र
बहुत्र Ind. In many ways, or places, &c.<BR> E. बहु much, many, त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्व|बहुत्वं
बहुत्व n. (-त्वं) Plurality, multitude, muchness, abundance.<BR> E. बहु much,<BR>त्व aff. of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्वक्क|बहुत्वक्कः
बहुत्वक्क m. (-क्कः) The Bhurja-patra or Birch-tree.<BR> E. बहु much, त्वच् skin<BR>or bark, कन् aff.; having several layers of bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्वच्
बहुत्वच् m. (-त्वक्) The Bhurja-patra, or Birch tree.<BR> E. बहु much, and<BR>त्वच् bark: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुद
बहुद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Liberal, munificent.<BR> E. बहु, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदक्षिण
बहुदक्षिण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Accompanied with many presents, (a cere-<BR>mony.)<BR>	 2. Liberal, bountiful.<BR> E. बहु, and दक्षिणा a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदण्डिक|बहुदण्डिकः
बहुदण्डिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having many staff-bearers, &c.<BR> E. बहु many,<BR>दण्डिन् having a staff, कन् aff.; also in the masculine form बहु-<BR>दण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदुग्ध|बहुदुग्धः
बहुदुग्ध m. (-ग्धः) Wheat.<BR>	 f. (-ग्धा) A cow giving much milk.<BR> E. बहु<BR>much and दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदुग्धिका
बहुदुग्धिका f. (-का) A plant, yielding a caustic milky juice, (Euphor-<BR>bia, of various sorts.)<BR> E. बहु much. दुग्ध milk, कन् aff.; fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदृष्ट
बहुदृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Experienced.<BR> E. बहु, and दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुदोष
बहुदोष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Full of faults or defects, very wicked, very bad.<BR>E. बहु and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुधन
बहुधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wealthy, rich.<BR> E. वहु, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुधा
बहुधा Ind. In many ways. sorts, &c.<BR> E. बहु much, धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुधागत
बहुधागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dispersed, scattered.<BR> E. बहुधा, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुधार|बहुधारं
बहुधार m. (-रः) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. बहु many, धारा edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुनाद|बहुनादः
बहुनाद m. (-दः) The conch-shell.<BR> E. बहु much, नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपटु|बहुपटुः
बहुपटु mfn. (-टुः-ट्वी-टु) Very clever.<BR> E. बहु much, and पटु clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपत्र|बहुपत्रं|बहुपत्रः
बहुपत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री त्रं) Many-leaved.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः) An onion.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं) Talc.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-त्री) A drug, (Trigonella fœnugræcum.)<BR> E. बहु many, पत्र a leaf, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपर्णी
बहुपर्णी f. (र्णी) A medicinal plant, (Trigonella fœnugræcum.)<BR> E. बहु<BR>many, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपाद्
बहुपाद् m. (-पाद्) The Indian fig-tree.<BR> E. बहु many, पाद foot: also बहुपाद<BR>m. (-दः) Alluding to the branches, which grow down-wards and<BR>take root again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुपुत्त्र
बहुपुत्त्र mfn. (-त्त्रः-त्त्री-त्त्रं) Having many children.<BR>	 m. (-त्त्रः) A tree, (Echites<BR>scholaris.)<BR>	 f. (-त्त्री) A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR> E. बहु many,<BR>पुत्त्र a child or produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुप्रज|बहुप्रजः
बहुप्रज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Having a numerous progeny.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>hog.<BR>	 2. A sort of grass: see मुञ्ज.<BR> E. बहु many, प्रजा offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुप्रतिज्ञ|बहुप्रतिज्ञः
बहुप्रतिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Complicated, containing more than one<BR>circumstance.<BR>	 2. (In law.) Comprising many counts, (a plaint, &c.)<BR>E. बहु many, प्रतिज्ञा assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुप्रद|बहुप्रदः
बहुप्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Munificent, bountiful.<BR> E. बहु much, and प्रद who<BR>gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुप्रवाह
बहुप्रवाह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Flowing in many streams.<BR> E. बहु and प्रवाह course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुप्रसू
बहुप्रसू f. (-सूः) The mother of many children.<BR> E. बहु much, and प्रसू who<BR>bears offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुफल|बहुफलः
बहुफल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Fertile, fruitful.<BR>	 m. (-लः) The Kadamba tree,<BR>(Nauclea kadamba.)<BR>	 f. (-ली) The opposite-leaved fig-tree.<BR> E. बहु<BR>much, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुभाग्य
बहुभाग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Fortunate.<BR> E. बहु, and भाग्य fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुभुज्
बहुभुज् mfn. (-भुक) Voracious.<BR> E. वहु and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमत
बहुमत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Thought much of, respected, considered.<BR>	 2.<BR>Having many different opinions.<BR> E. बहु and मत minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमति|बहुमतिः
बहुमति f. (-तिः) Value, estimation, prizing or preferring.<BR> E. बहु, and<BR>मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमल|बहुमलः
बहुमल n. (-लं) Lead.<BR> E. बहु much, मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमार्ग|बहुमार्गं|बहुमार्गः
बहुमार्ग m. (-र्गः) A place where four roads meet.<BR> E. बहु many, मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमान|बहुमानः
बहुमान n. (-नं) Respect, reverence.<BR> E. बहु, and मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमूर्त्ति|बहुमूर्ति|बहुमूर्तिः|बहुमूर्त्तिः
बहुमूर्त्ति mfn. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्तिः-र्त्ति) Multiform.<BR>	 f. (-र्त्तिः) Wild-cotton.<BR> E. बहु<BR>many, मूर्त्ति form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमूर्द्धन्
बहुमूर्द्धन् mfn. (-र्द्धा-र्द्धा-र्द्ध) Many-headed.<BR>	 m. (-र्द्धा) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. बहु many,<BR>मूर्द्धन् a forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमूल|बहुमूलः
बहुमूल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Many-rooted, having many roots.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">Page516-b+ 60</a>]<BR>sort of reed or grass: see इक्कट and इत्कट.<BR> E. बहु many, and मूल a<BR>root; also with कुन् added, बहुमूलक m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुमूल्य|बहुमूल्यं
बहुमूल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Costly, precious.<BR> E. बहु much, and मूल price, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुरूप|बहुरूपः
बहुरूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Multiform.<BR>	 m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Resin.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR>4. Love, CUPID.<BR>	 5. A chameleon.<BR>	 6. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 7. Hair.<BR>	 8. One<BR>of the Jinas or Jaina saints.<BR> E. बहु many, रूप shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुरेखा
बहुरेखा m. plu. (-खाः) Wrinkles, furrows, marks of care or pain. E.<BR>बहु many, रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुरेतस्
बहुरेतस् m. (-ताः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. बहु much, and रेतस् seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुरोमन्
बहुरोमन् m. (-मा) A sheep.<BR> E. बहु much, and रोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुल|बहुलं|बहुलः
बहुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Much, many, 2. Black.<BR>	 3. Variously applicable,<BR>comprehensive, (a rule, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. AGNI or fire.<BR>	 2. The dark<BR>half of a month.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The sky.<BR>	 f. plu. (-लाः). The Pleiades.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला)<BR>	 1. Indigo.<BR>	 2. Cardamoms.<BR>	 3. A cow.<BR> E. बहु many, ला to get,<BR>aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुलत्व|बहुलत्वं
बहुलत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Abundance, muchness.<BR>	 2. Comprehensiveness, (of a<BR>rule.)<BR> E. त्व added to the last; also with तल् aff. बहुलता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुलीकरण|बहुलीकरणं
बहुलीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Multiplying, magnifying, making much.<BR>	 2. Win-<BR>nowing.<BR> E. बहुल and करण making, with च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुलीकृत|बहुलीकृतं
बहुलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Threshed and winnowed.<BR>	 2. Made manifold<BR>or much.<BR> E. बहुल much, कृत made, and च्वि substituted for the final<BR>of the former, by which the ई is inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुवचन
बहुवचन n. (-नं) The plural number. (in grammar.)<BR> E. बहु, and वचन<BR>saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुवार|बहुवारः
बहुवार m. (-रः) A fruit, (Cordia myxa.)<BR> E. बहु much, वॄ to nourish, aff.<BR>अण्; also with कन् added, बहुवारक m. (-कः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुविध|बहुविधः
बहुविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Various multiform, of many sorts or kinds. E.<BR>बहु many, and विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुविस्तीर्ण
बहुविस्तीर्ण mfn. (र्णः-र्णा-र्ण) Widely spread or diffused.<BR>	 f. (-र्णा) A shrub<BR>bearing a small red and black berry, (Abrus precatorious.)<BR> E. बहु<BR>much, विस्तीर्ण spreading. “कुंँच” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुवीज|बहुवीजं
बहुवीज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Having many or much seed.<BR>	 n. (-जं) The cus-<BR>tard-apple, (Annona squamosa.) “आता”<BR> E. बहु many, and वीज a<BR>seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुवीर्य्य|बहुवीर्य|बहुवीर्यः|बहुवीर्य्यः
बहुवीर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) Beleric myrobalan. (Terminalia belerica.)<BR> E. बहु much<BR>and वीर्य्य seed. “वहेडा”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुत्रीहि
बहुत्रीहि m. (-हिः) One of the forms of grammatical composition, the<BR>compounding two or more words to furnish an epithet or attri-<BR>butive, as बहुमाल or बहुमालक having many necklaces, from बहु, and<BR>माला a necklace.<BR> E. बहु many, and व्रीहि grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुशत्रु|बहुशत्रुः
बहुशत्रु mfn. (-त्रुः-त्रुः-त्रु) Having many enemies.<BR>	 m. (-त्रुः) A sparrow. E.<BR>बहु many, and शत्रु an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुशस्
बहुशस् Ind. Abundantly, plentifully.<BR> E. बहु much, many, शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुशाख
बहुशाख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Having many branches or ramifications.<BR> E. बहु,<BR>and शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुश्रुत
बहुश्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well-taught, learned.<BR>	 2. Acquainted with<BR>the Vedas.<BR> E. बहु, and श्रुत heard, or श्रुति Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुश्रेयस्
बहुश्रेयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Having many excellencies.<BR>	 2. Very<BR>excellent.<BR> E. बहु, and श्रेयस् best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुस्पृश्
बहुस्पृश् mfn. (-स्पृक्) Expanded, spread, diffused.<BR> E. बहु, and स्पृश् what<BR>touches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुसन्तति|बहुसंतति|बहुसंततिः|बहुसन्ततिः
बहुसन्तति m. (-तिः) A species of bamboo, (Bambusa spinosa.)<BR> E. बहु<BR>much, सन्तति spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुसुता
बहुसुता f. (-ता) A plant, (Asparagus.)<BR> E. वहु many, सुत a birth or shoot.<BR>“शतमूली” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुसू
बहुसू f. (-सूः)<BR>	 1. A sow 2. The mother of many children.<BR> E. बहु many,<BR>and सू bearing, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुसूति|बहुसूतिः
बहुसूति f. (-तिः) A cow bearing many calves.<BR> E. बहु many, सू to bear, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहुस्वन|बहुस्वनः
बहुस्वन m. (-नः) An owl.<BR> E. बहु much, स्वन noise or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बहूदक|बहूदकः
बहूदक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having much water.<BR> E. बहु and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्ल
बह्ल r. 1st cl. (बह्लते)<BR>	 1. To be pre-eminent or excellent, (also वह्ल,) but less<BR>usually.)<BR>	 2. To speak or tell.<BR>	 3. To kill or hurt.<BR>	 4. To cover, to<BR>spread.<BR>	 5. To give, (also वह्ल in these four senses, and more accu-<BR>rately.)<BR>	 6. To remember. r. 10th cl. (बह्लयति) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्वर्थ
बह्वर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Important, having much meaning.<BR>	 2. Having<BR>many objects.<BR> E. बहु, and अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्वपत्य|बह्वपत्यः
बह्वपत्य m. (-त्यः)<BR>	 1. A hog.<BR>	 2. A rat.<BR>	 f. (-त्या) A cow that has borne<BR>many calves.<BR> E. बहु many, अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्वाशिन्
बह्वाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Voracious, gluttonous.<BR> E. बहु much, आशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्वृच्
बह्वृच् f. (-ह्वृक्) The Rig-Veda.<BR> E. बहु many, ऋच् a hymn or prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बह्वृची
बह्वृची f. (-ची) The wife of a Brāhman conversant with the Rig-<BR>Veda.<BR> E. वहु many, ऋच् a prayer or incantation, aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बा
बा Ind.<BR>	 1. As, like.<BR>	 2. Or, either: see वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाड
बाड (ऋ) बाडृ r. 1st cl. (बाडते) To bathe, to dive and emerge. Vopadeva<BR>differs from other authorities in writing this with an initial व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडव|बाडवं|बाडवः
बाडव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Submarine fire.<BR>	 2. A Brāhman.<BR>	 n. (-वं) A stud, a col-<BR>lection of mares.<BR> E. वाडव a mare, and अण् aff. of derivation: see<BR>बडवानल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडवाग्नि|बाडवाग्निः
बाडवाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Hell.<BR> E. बडवाग्नि submarine fire, and अण् aff. of place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडवेय
बाडवेय m. du. (-यौ) The two sons of ĀSHWINĪ and physicians of Swar-<BR>ga.<BR> E. बडवा a mare, Sanjaya changed into a mare, and टक् aff. of<BR>descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडव्य|बाडव्यं
बाडव्य n. (-व्यं) A number of Brāhmans.<BR> E. बाडव a Brāhman, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाडीर|बाडीरः
बाडीर m. (-रः) A servant, a hired labourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाण|बाणः
बाण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. An arrow, a shaft.<BR>	 2. An aim.<BR>	 3. The udder of a cow.<BR>4. The feathered end of an arrow.<BR>	 5. A kind of creeper, (Blue<BR>Barleria.)<BR>	 6. A name of a demon, son of Virochan.<BR>	 7. The name<BR>of the celebrated poet, the author of Kādambari and Harsha-<BR>charita, &c.<BR>	 8. The number five.<BR> E. बण् or वण् to sound, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणगोचर|बाणगोचरः
बाणगोचर m. (-रः) The course of an arrow.<BR> E. बाण and गोचर object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणि|बाणिः
बाणि f. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. Speech.<BR>	 2. The goddess of speech, &c.: see वाणि.<BR> E. बण्<BR>or वण् to speak, in the causal form, aff. इ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणिज|बाणिजः
बाणिज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A merchant, a trader.<BR>	 2. Submarine fire.<BR> E. बणिज्, &c. aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणिजिक|बाणिजिकः
बाणिजिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Submarine fire.<BR>	 2. A trader, a merchant.<BR>	 3. A<BR>rogue, a cheat.<BR> E. बणिज् trade, aff. ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणिज्य|बाणिज्यं
बाणिज्य nf. (-ज्यं-ज्या) Trade, traffic, commerce.<BR> E. बणिज् a trader, with<BR>ष्यञ् aff.; or बाणिज् the same, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाणिनी
बाणिनी f. (-नी) An excellent woman.<BR>	 2. A shrewd woman.<BR>	 3. A dancing<BR>girl.<BR>	 4. A drunken woman.<BR> E. बण-णिनि-ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बा
बा(वा)दर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Made of cotton, mf. (-रः-रा) The cotton plant.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The jujube.<BR>	 2. Silk.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR>	 4. A garment made of<BR>cotton.<BR>	 5. A conch-shell that winds from left to right.<BR> E. वदर<BR>cotton, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बा
बा(वा)दरायण m. (-णः) An epithet of Vyāsa, as the author of the Ve-<BR>dānta Sūtra.<BR> E. बदर, फक् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बा
बा (वा) दरायणि m. (-णिः) An epithet of Sūka the son of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध|बाधः
बाध (ऋ) बाधृ r. 1st cl. (बाधते)<BR>	 1. To resist, to oppose.<BR>	 2. To annoy or<BR>afflict.<BR>	 3. To assault.<BR>	 4. To drive.<BR>	 5. To abolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध|बाधः
बाध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Opposing, hindering.<BR>	 2. Annoyance.<BR>	 3. Refutation<BR>arising from incompatibility or contradiction of assigned cause<BR>and effect, (in logic.)<BR>	 4. Danger.<BR> E. बाध् to oppose, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधक|बाधकः
बाधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What hinders, opposes, pains, &c.<BR>	 f. (-धिका)<BR>	 1.<BR>Tormenting.<BR>	 2. Annulling.<BR>	 3. Vexing.<BR> E. बाध् and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधन|बाधनं
बाधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pain.<BR>	 2. Impeding, opposing.<BR> E. बाध् to oppose, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधमान
बाधमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Painting, annoying.<BR> E. बाध् to annoy, and<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध्यमान
बाध्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being harassed or tormented.<BR> E. बाध् to annoy,<BR>pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधा
बाधा f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. Pain.<BR>	 2. Annoyance.<BR>	 3. Resistance.<BR>	 4. Injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधित|बाधितः
बाधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Obstructed, impeded.<BR>	 2. Pained, tormented.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">Page517-b+ 60</a>]<BR>3. Self-refuted, (in logic.), contradictory, incompatible.<BR> E. बाध् to<BR>oppose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धकिनेय|बांधकिनेय|बांधकिनेयः|बान्धकिनेयः
बान्धकिनेय m. (-यः) A bastard, the son of a disloyal wife.<BR> E. बन्धकी a<BR>wanton, aff. ढक्, and इनङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धव|बांधव|बांधवः|बान्धवः
बान्धव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A relation, a kinsman: see बन्धु.<BR>	 2. A friend.<BR> E. बन्धु a<BR>kinsman, अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धवाक्रोशिन्
बान्धवाक्रोशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Calling upon or bewailing a kinsman. E.<BR>बान्धव and आक्रोशिन् who calls aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्ब्बटीर|बार्बटीर|बार्बटीरः|बार्ब्बटीरः
बार्ब्बटीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Tin.<BR>	 2. A shoot of the mango.<BR>	 3. The stone of the<BR>mango fruit.<BR>	 4. The son of an unchaste woman, a bastard.<BR> E. बर्ब्बटी<BR>a whore, and र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाभ्रवी
बाभ्रवी f. (-वी) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. बभ्रु SĪVA, with अण् and ङीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्ह
बार्ह f. (-हीं) Made of the feathers of a peacock's tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्हस्पत|बार्हस्पतं
बार्हस्पत f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. Relating to Brihaspatī.<BR>	 2. Descended from him.<BR>	 3.<BR>Sacred to him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्हस्पत्य|बार्हस्पत्यः
बार्हस्पत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Relating to Brihaspatī.<BR>	 m. (-त्यः)<BR>	 1. A pupil<BR>of him.<BR>	 2. A materialist.<BR>	 n. (-त्यं) The constellation Pushyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाल|बालं|बालः
बाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Ignorant, unwise, uninstructed.<BR>	 2. Young, in-<BR>fantine, a child.<BR>	 mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>	 1. An infant, a child; it usually<BR>means the young child, under five years old, but is equally appli-<BR>cable till sixteen years of age.<BR>	 2. A colt.<BR>	 3. An elephant of five years<BR>old.<BR>	 4. An elephant's tail.<BR>	 5. A horse's tail.<BR>	 6. Any tail.<BR>	 7. Hair.<BR>8. A sort of fish, (Cyprinus Rohita, HAM.)<BR>	 mn. (-लः-लं) A perfume<BR>perhaps a sort of fragrant grass, (Andropogon schænanthus.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला)<BR>	 1. Small cardamoms.<BR>	 2. A woman, a female.<BR>	 3. Aloes.<BR>	 4. An-<BR>other plant, commonly Ākanādi.<BR>	 5. The cocoa-nut.<BR>	 6. Turmeric.<BR>7. A sort of jasmine.<BR>	 8. A flower, (Hibiscus tortuosus, Rox.)<BR>	 9.<BR>Pure, (applied specially to a female animal, as a heifer, &c. fit for<BR>an oblation.)<BR>	 f. (-ली) A sort of ear-ring.<BR> E. बल् to live, aff. घञ्, it<BR>sometimes occurs, but less accurately perhaps, with a palatial<BR>initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालक|बालकं|बालकः
बालक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A boy, an infant: see the last.<BR>	 2. A fool, a block-<BR>head.<BR>	 3. The tail of a horse or elephant.<BR>	 4. A finger-ring.<BR>	 5. A<BR>bracelet.<BR>	 6. A perfume; also द्रीवेर.<BR>	 f. (-लिका)<BR>	 1. A female infant.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sand.<BR>	 3. The knot or flower of an ear-ring.<BR>	 4. The rustling of<BR>leaves.<BR>	 5. Small cardamoms.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A sort of Hibiscus, (H. muta-<BR>bilis.)<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालकत्व
बालकत्व n. (-त्वं) Childheod, childishness.<BR> E. बालक, and त्व aff.: also with<BR>तल्, बालकता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालकीय
बालकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Childish, infantine.<BR> E. बालक, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालकृमि|बालकृमिः
बालकृमि m. (-मिः) A louse.<BR> E. बाल hair, and कृमि a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाल|बालं|बालः
बाल (लि) खिल्य m. (-ल्यः) A divine personage, of the size of the thumb,<BR>sixty thousand of whom were produced from the hair of BRAH-<BR>MĀ'S body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालगर्भिणी
बालगर्भिणी f. (-णी) A cow with calf for the first time.<BR> E. बाल young, गर्भिणी pregnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालचर्य्य|बालचर्य|बालचर्यः|बालचर्य्यः
बालचर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. बाल a child and चर्य्य usage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालतनय|बालतनयः
बालतनय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A young son.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR> E. बाल<BR>young or small, and तनय offspring, leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालतन्त्र|बालतंत्र|बालतन्त्रं
बालतन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) Midwifery, care of a lying-in woman and her child. E.<BR>बाल an infant, and तन्त्र rule, management.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालतृण|बालतृणं
बालतृण n. (-णं) Young grass.<BR> E. बाल young and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालदलक|बालदलकः
बालदलक m. (-कः) A tree, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR> E. बाल small, दल a leaf, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालधन
बालधन n. (-नं) The property of a minor or infant.<BR> E. बाल, धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालधि|बालधिः
बालधि m. (-धिः) A hairy tail, as a horse's &c.<BR> E. बाल hair, धा to have,<BR>aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालपत्र|बालपत्रः
बालपत्र m. (-त्रः) Khayer, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR> E. बाल young or small and<BR>पत्र a leaf; also with कन् added, बालपत्रक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालपाश्या
बालपाश्या f. (-श्या)<BR>	 1. An ornament of gold or silver, &c. worn between<BR>the hair divided on the forehead.<BR>	 2. A string of pearls binding<BR>the hair.<BR> E. बाल hair, पाश a tie or quantity and यत् aff. “सिंँती” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालपुष्पी
बालपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A sort of jasmine, (J. auriculatum.)<BR> E. बाल the hair<BR>and पुष्प flower; worn in the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालभद्रक|बालभद्रकः
बालभद्रक m. (-कः) A sort of mineral poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालभाव|बालभावः
बालभाव m. (-वः) Childhood.<BR> E. बाल and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालमूषिका
बालमूषिका f. (-का) A small rat or mouse.<BR> E. बाल small, मूषिका a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालयज्ञोपवीतक|बालयज्ञोपवीतकं
बालयज्ञोपवीतक n. (-कं) A sort of substitute for the sacrificial thread, a<BR>string or scarf as worn by children.<BR> E. बाल a child and यज्ञोपवीत<BR>the Brāhminical cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालराज|बालराजं
बालराज m. (-जः) Lapis lazuli.<BR> E. बाल young, and राज what shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालवत्स|बालवत्सः
बालवत्स m. (-त्सः) A pigeon, a dove.<BR> E. बाल a child, and वत्स dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालवायज|बालवायजं
बालवायज n. (-जं) Lapis lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालवासस्
बालवासस् m. (-साः) Woolen garments.<BR> E. बाल hair, (of cows, goats, &c.)<BR>and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालवाह्य|बालवाह्यः
बालवाह्य m. (-ह्यः) A wild goat.<BR> E. बाल hair, वह् to endeavour, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालव्यजन|बालव्यजनं
बालव्यजन n. (-नं) A Chowrie, a whisk, a fly-flapper.<BR> E. बाल hair and<BR>व्यजन a fan; it being made usually of the tail of the Yak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालव्रत|बालव्रतः
बालव्रत m. (-तः) A Bauddha saint; also named MANJUGHOSHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालसन्ध्याभ|बालसंध्याभ|बालसन्ध्याभः
बालसन्ध्याभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Of a purple colour.<BR>	 m. (-भः) Purple, the<BR>colour.<BR> E. वाल young, and सन्ध्या twilight, आङ् before, भा to shine,<BR>aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालहस्त|बालहस्तः
बालहस्त m. (-स्तः) The tail of a horse, or any hairy animal.<BR> E. बाल hair<BR>and हस्त the hand, to which organ it is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालाक्षी
बालाक्षी f. (-क्षी) A plant, commonly Keśapushpi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालातप|बालातपः
बालातप m. (-पः) The rays of the rising sun.<BR> E. बाल and आतप light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालापत्य
बालापत्य n. (-त्यं) Young offspring or progeny.<BR> E. बाल, अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालि|बालिः
बालि m. (-लिः) The celebrated monkey king, the son of INDRA, killed<BR>by RĀMA.<BR> E. बाल hair and इञ् aff.; being born from the hair of<BR>his mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिका
बालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A girl.<BR>	 2. A kind of ear-ring.<BR>	 3. Sand.<BR>	 4. The<BR>rustling of leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिन्
बालिन् m. (-ली) The monkey-son of INDRA.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The constellation<BR>AśHwini. E. See the last, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिश|बालिशं|बालिशः
बालिश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Young.<BR>	 2. Ignorant.<BR>	 3. Careless, heedless.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-शं) A pillow.<BR> E. बाड् to emerge, इन् aff., बाडि or बालि and शो to<BR>destroy, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिश्य|बालिश्यं
बालिश्य n. (-श्यं)<BR>	 1. Thoughtlessness, heedlessness.<BR>	 2. Youth.<BR>	 3. Folly.<BR>E. बालिश and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिसम्भव
बालिसम्भव m. (-वः) Name of celebrated monkey, the son of BĀLI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालिहन्तृ|बालिहंतृ
बालिहन्तृ m. (-न्ता) RĀMA.<BR> E. बालि the monkey, and हन्तृ killer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाली
बाली f. (-ली) A kind of ear-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालीश|बालीशः
बालीश m. (-शः) Pain in making water from gravel, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालु|बालुः
बालु m. (-लुः) A drug, commonly Elabāluka<BR> E. बल् to live, aff. उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुक|बालुकं|बालुकः
बालुक m. (-कः) A drug and perfume; also Elabāluka.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Sand,<BR>gravel.<BR>	 2. (also बालुकी) A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissi-<BR>mus.)<BR>	 3. Camphor.<BR>	 4. A sand-cloth.<BR> E. बल् to live, (by its means,)<BR>उकञ् aff. or बालु as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुकागड|बालुकागडः
बालुकागड m. (-डः) A sort of fish, (Cheilodipterus culius and butis,<BR>HAM.)<BR> E. बालुका sand and गड् to scatter, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुकात्मिका
बालुकात्मिका f. (-का) Sugar.<BR> E. बालुका sand, आत्मन् identity, कन् aff. in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुकाप्रभा
बालुकाप्रभा f. (-भा) One of the seven hells of the Jainas, the hell of sand.<BR>E. बालुका sand and प्रभा splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुङ्की|बालुंकी
बालुङ्की f. (-ङ्की) A sort of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.) Also<BR>बालुकी and बालुङ्गी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालुङ्गी|बालुंगी
बालुङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A sort of cucumber.: see the last; also with कन् add-<BR>ed बालुङ्गिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालूक|बालूकः
बालूक m. (-कः) A sort of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालेय|बालेयः
बालेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Soft.<BR>	 2. Fit or proper for a child.<BR>	 3. Fit or<BR>proper for a tax, a sacrifice, &c.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. An ass.<BR>	 2. A demon,<BR>a Daitya.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR> E. बलि a tax, a sacri-<BR>fice, or बाल a child and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालेयशाक|बालेयशाकः
बालेयशाक m. (-कः) A plant, Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR> E. बालेय an ass and<BR>शाक a potherb; also बालेय । “वामनहाटि” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालोपवीत|बालोपवीतं
बालोपवीत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The sacrificial thread, or a substitute for it as<BR>worn by children.<BR>	 2. A cloth covering the privities.<BR> E. वाल a child,<BR>उपवीत the thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाल्य|बाल्यं
बाल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Childhood.<BR>	 2. Immaturity of understanding.<BR>	 3. A state<BR>of waxing.<BR> E. बाल a child. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाल्हि|बाल्हिः
बाल्हि m. (-लहि) Name of the “Balkh” country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाष्प|बाष्पं|बाष्पः
बाष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. Vapour, steam.<BR>	 2. A tear, tears, rheum.<BR>	 3. Iron. E.<BR>बाध to oppose, Unādi aff. प. and ध changed to ष; according to<BR>other etymologies, this word is वाष्प, or बास्प and वास्प ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाह|बाहः
बाह (ऋ) बाहृ r. 1st cl. (बाहते)<BR>	 1. To resolve, to attempt perse-<BR>veringly or resolutely, to endeavour diligently; also वाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाह|बाहः
बाह mf. (-हः-हा)<BR>	 1. The arm.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR> E. बाह् to endeavour, aff.<BR>अच्; it is sometimes read वाह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहिक
बाहिक m. plu. (-कः) The people of Punjab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहु|बाहुः
बाहु m. (-हुः)<BR>	 1. The arm.<BR>	 2. The side of any angular geometrical fig-<BR>ure, the leg of a triangle, &c.<BR>	 3. A door-post.<BR> E. बाध् to oppose, कु<BR>Unādi aff. and ध changed to ह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुक|बाहुकः
बाहुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A servant, servile, dependent.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>name of NALA, after his change of form, by the bite of KARKO-<BR>TAKA Nāga.<BR>	 2. A monkey.<BR>	 f. (-का) The name of a river.<BR> E. बाहु an<BR>arm, कन् aff.; or कृ to do, with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुकुन्थ|बाहुकुंथ|बाहुकुन्थः
बाहुकुन्थ m. (-न्थः) A wing<BR> E. बाहु the arm, कुन्थ what adheres to, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुकुब्ज
बाहुकुब्ज mfn. (-ब्जः-ब्जा-ब्जं) Crooked-armed.<BR> E. बाहु an arm, and कुब्ज bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुज|बाहुजः
बाहुज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The Kṣatriya or warrior, born from the arms of<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A parrot.<BR>	 3. Sesamum growing wild or spontaneous-<BR>ly.<BR> E. बाहु the arm, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुत्राण|बाहुत्राणं
बाहुत्राण n. (-णं) Armour for the arms.<BR> E. बाहु the arm, and त्राण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुदन्तिन्|बाहुदंतिन्
बाहुदन्तिन् m. (-न्ती) INDRA.<BR> E. बह् many, (four.), दन्त a tooth, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुदा
बाहुदा f. (-दा) The name of a river, said to rise in the snowy chain of<BR>the Himālaya, and probably the modern Behut, the classical Hy-<BR>daspes.<BR> E. बाहु an arm, and दा bestower; alluding to a legend of a<BR>saint's recovering his lost arms, by bathing in this stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुप्रहरण|बाहुप्रहरणः
बाहुप्रहरण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) A striker, a boxer.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Boxing, wrestling.<BR>E. बाहु and प्रहरण striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुभूषा
बाहुभूषा f. (-षा) An armlet, an ornament worn round the upper arm. E.<BR>बाहु the arm, and भूषा an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुमय
बाहुमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made or done with the arms.<BR> E. बाहु, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुमूल|बाहुमूलं
बाहुमूल n. (-लं) The arm-pit.<BR> E. बाहु the arm, मूल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुयुद्ध|बाहुयुद्धं
बाहुयुद्ध n. (-द्धं) Close fight, personal struggle, boxing, wrestling.<BR> E. बाहु<BR>the arm and युद्ध fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुल|बाहुलं|बाहुलः
बाहुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Fire or its deity.<BR>	 2. The month Kārtika.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Mail worn on the arm.<BR>	 2. A term in grammar, implying various or<BR>irregular formation, or construction or such as is analogous to<BR>this word.<BR> E. बहुल fire, and अण् aff.; also with कन् added, बाहुलक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुलेय|बाहुलेयः
बाहुलेय m. (-यः) The deity KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. बहुला the Pleiades, consider-<BR>ed as nymphs, and nurses of this god; aff. of relation ढक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुल्य|बाहुल्यं
बाहुल्य n. (-ल्यं) Plenty, abundance, quantity.<BR> E. बहल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुवीर्य्य|बाहुवीर्य
बाहुवीर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Personal prowess.<BR> E. बाहु, and वीर्य्य heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहुसहस्रभृत्
बाहुसहस्रभृत् m. (-भृत्) A king killed by PARASURĀMA, also named<BR>KĀRTAVĪRJAYA.<BR> E. बाहु, an arm, सहस्र a thousand, भृत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाहू
बाहू(हा)बाहवि Ind. Arm to arm, hand to hand, (fighting, &c.)<BR> E. बाहु<BR>the arm, (repeated.) इच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिट्
बिट् r. 1st cl. (बेटति) To curse: Also विट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिडालक|बिडालकं|बिडालकः
बिडालक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cat.<BR>	 2. Application of ointment to the eye.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-कं) Yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिद्
बिद् (इ) बिदि r. 1st cl. (बिन्दति) To make or constitute a part; the root is<BR>obsolete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिदल|बिदलं
बिदल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A slip.<BR>	 2. A twig.<BR>	 3. A split bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिन्दु|बिंदु|बिंदुः|बिन्दुः
बिन्दु m. (-न्दु)<BR>	 1. A drop.<BR>	 2. a particle.<BR>	 3. A dot, a point.<BR>	 4. A cipher,<BR>(in math.)<BR> E. विदि उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिन्दुजाल|बिंदुजाल|बिन्दुजालं
बिन्दुजाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A collection of drops or particles.<BR>	 2. Red marks<BR>on the trunks of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्रक्षु|बिभ्रक्षुः
बिभ्रक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>	 1. Desirous to destroy or lose.<BR>	 2. Wishing to<BR>scorch, fry, parch.<BR>	 m. (-क्षुः) Fire.<BR> E. भ्रस्ज् to break, to fry, desid.<BR>v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्रज्जिषु|बिभ्रज्जिषुः
बिभ्रज्जिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to fry or scorch.<BR>	 m. (-षुः) Fire. E.<BR>भ्रस्ज् to fry, desid, v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्
बिल् r. 6th cl. (बिलति) r., 10th cl. (बेलयति-ते) To break, to tear or rend, to divide or detach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल|बिलं|बिलः
बिल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A hole.<BR>	 2. A pit.<BR>	 3. An outlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिलेशय|बिलेशयः
बिलेशय m. (यः)<BR>	 1. An animal that lives in holes.<BR>	 2. A snake.<BR>	 3. A<BR>hare.<BR>	 4. A rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्ल|बिल्लं
बिल्ल n. (-ल्लं)<BR>	 1. A basin for water round the root of a tree.<BR>	 2. Asafœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्व|बिल्वं|बिल्वः
बिल्व m. (-ल्वः) A species of tree.<BR>	 n. (-ल्वं)<BR>	 1. The fruit of this tree.<BR>	 2. A<BR>weight equal to one pala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिस्
बिस् (इर्) विसिर् r. 4th cl. (बिस्यति) To throw or cast, to send or direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिसिनी
बिसिनी f. (-नी) The lotus-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीज|बीजं|बीजः
बीज n. (-जं) See वीज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बीभत्स|बीभत्सः
बीभत्स mfn. Subst. (-त्सः-त्सा-त्सं)<BR>	 1. Disgust, abhorrence. Adj. Detesting,<BR>loathing, changed or averted in mind.<BR>	 2. Cruel, mischievous.<BR>	 3.<BR>Compassionate.<BR>	 4. Wicked.<BR>	 5. Envious.<BR> E. बध् to bind, to hate, &c.<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्क|बुक्कं|बुक्कः
बुक्क r. 1st and 10th cls. (बुक्कति बुक्कयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To bark.<BR>	 2. To speak. r.<BR>10th cl. To give pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्क|बुक्कं|बुक्कः
बुक्क Subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-क्कः-क्का-क्वी-क्वं)<BR>	 1. The heart.<BR>	 2. The chest.<BR>	 3. Blood.<BR>m. (-क्कः)<BR>	 1. A goat.<BR>	 2. Time.<BR> E. बुक्क to bark, &c., aff. अच्; also<BR>बुक्कन् mn. (-क्का-क्कं) and बूक्क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्कन|बुक्कनं
बुक्कन n. (-नं) Barking, (as of a dog.)<BR> E. बुक्क् to bark, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्काग्रमांस|बुक्काग्रमांसं
बुक्काग्रमांस n. (-सं) The heart.<BR> E. बुक्व् the heart, अग्र principal, मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुक्वार
बुक्वार m. (-रः) The roar or barking of a lion.<BR> E. बुक्क् to bark, आर aff.,<BR>the lion of Hindustan barks much like a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुड्
बुड् r. 6th cl. (बुडति)<BR>	 1. To leave, to abandon.<BR>	 2. To cover, to clothe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्
बुद् (उ, इर) उवुदिर् r. 1st cl. (बुदति-ते) To discern, to apprehend, to<BR>perceive, to understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध|बुद्धः
बुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Known, understood.<BR>	 m. (-द्धः)<BR>	 1. A generic name<BR>for a deified teacher of the Bauddha sect, amongst whom numer-<BR>ous Buddhas are reckoned; the name is especially applied to the<BR>9th incarnation of VIṢṆU and the apparent founder of the reli-<BR>gion of the Bauddhas; the term is often confounded but impro-<BR>perly, with a Jina: see जिन.<BR>	 2. A sage, a wise or learned man.<BR>E. बुध् to know, aff. क्तः see बुध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धद्रव्य|बुद्धद्रव्यं
बुद्धद्रव्य n. (-व्यं) Avarice, covetous accumulation.<BR> E. बुद्ध known, द्रव्य thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धि|बुद्धिः
बुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Understanding, intellect.<BR> E. बुध् to know, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिविनाश
बुद्धिविनाश m. (-शः) Loss or deficiency of understanding.<BR> E. बुद्धि and<BR>विनाश destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिजीविन्
बुद्धिजीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Rational, an intellectual being.<BR> E. बुद्धि and जीविन् alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिभृत्
बुद्धिभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Wise, intelligent.<BR> E. बुद्धि and भृत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिमत्|बुद्धिमन्त्
बुद्धिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Wise, learned.<BR>	 2. Famed, known.<BR>	 3.<BR>Humble, docile.<BR>	 m. (-मान्) A man.<BR> E. बुद्धि wisdom, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिसहाय|बुद्धिसहायः
बुद्धिसहाय m. (-यः) A counsellor, a minister.<BR> E. बुद्धि understanding and<BR>सहाय companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिहीन
बुद्धिहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Ignorant, silly, a fool.<BR> E. बुद्धि and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिहीनत्व
बुद्धिहीनत्व n. (-त्वं) Folly, ignorance.<BR> E. बुद्धिहीन and त्व aff.; also with<BR>तल्, बुद्धिहीनता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धीन्द्रिय|बुद्धींद्रिय|बुद्धीन्द्रियं
बुद्धीन्द्रिय n. (-यं) An organ of intellect, as the mind, eye, ear, nose,<BR>tongue, and skin.<BR> E. बुद्धि understanding and इन्द्रिय an organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धुद
बुद्धुद m. (-दः) A bubble.<BR> E. बुद् imitative sound, बुद् to perceive, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध्यवज्ञान
बुद्ध्यवज्ञान n. (-नं) Disregard of or contempt for one's understanding. E.<BR>बुद्धि, and अवज्ञान disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध्
बुध् (औ) औबुध r. 1st cl. (बोधति) r. 4th cl. (बुध्यते-ति) also (उ, इर) उबुधिर् r.<BR>1st cl. (बोधति-ते) To know, to understand. With प्रति, to look for,<BR>expect. With प्रति and वि, to wake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध|बुधः
बुध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. BUDDHA, the son of the moon and regent of the planet<BR>MERCURY, with whom he is identified.<BR>	 2. A wise or learned man, a<BR>sage.<BR>	 f. (-धा) Indian spikenard.<BR> E. बुध् to know or understand, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधजन|बुधजनः
बुधजन m. (-नः) A wise man.<BR> E. बुध्, and जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधतात|बुधतातः
बुधतात m. (-तः) The moon, the father of BUDDHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधवार|बुधवारः
बुधवार m. (-रः) Wednesday,<BR> E. बुध् MERCURY, and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधसुत|बुधसुतः
बुधसुत m. (-तः) PURŪRAVAS, the first king of the lunar dynasty.<BR> E. बुध्<BR>BUDDHA or MERCURY, and the son of SOMA, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधान|बुधानः
बुधान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A wise man, a sage.<BR>	 2. A holy teacher.<BR>	 3. One who<BR>speaks kindly.<BR>	 4. A worshipper or adorer of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. बुध् to<BR>know, आनच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधित|बुधितं
बुधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Known, understood.<BR> E. बुध् to know, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुधिल|बुधिलः
बुधिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Wise, learned.<BR> E. बुध् to know, Unādi aff. किलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध्न|बुध्नः
बुध्न m. (-ध्नः)<BR>	 1. The root of a tree.<BR>	 2. The bottom of a vessel.<BR>	 3. ŚIVA.<BR>E. बुध् to know, Unādi aff. नक्ः also ब्रध्न in the last sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुन्द्|बुंद्
बुन्द् (उ, इर्) उबुन्दिर् r. 1st cl. (बुन्दति-ते) To discern, to perceive, literally<BR>or figuratively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुन्ध्|बुंध्
बुन्ध् (उ, इर्) उबुधिर् r. 1st. cl. (बुन्धति-ते) To discern, to perceive: see बुन्द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुक्षा
बुभुक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Hunger.<BR>	 2. The desire of enjoyment.<BR> E. भुज् to eat,<BR>in the desid. form, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुक्षित|बुभुक्षितः
बुभुक्षित mfn. (तः-ता-तं) Hungry.<BR> E. बुभुक्षा hunger, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुक्षु
बुभुक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Wishing to eat.<BR> E. भुज् to eat, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुत्सा
बुभुत्सा f. (-त्सा) The wishing to know.<BR> E. बुध् to know, desid, v., अङ् and<BR>टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभुत्सु
बुभुत्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु) Wishing to know.<BR> E. बुध् to know, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभूषा
बुभूषा f. (-षा) Desire to be or become.<BR> E. भू to be, desid. v., affs. अङ्<BR>and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभूषु
बुभूषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to be or become.<BR> E. भू to be, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुभूर्षु
बुभूर्षु mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु)<BR>	 1. Wishing to fill.<BR>	 2. Desirous to nourish, &c. E.<BR>भृ to nourish, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुल्
बुल् r. 10th cl. (बोलयति-ते) To sink, to dive, to plunge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुलि|बुलिः
बुलि f. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. The vulva.<BR>	 2. Fear.<BR> E. बुल् to emerge, aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुष|बुषं
बुष n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Chaff.<BR>	 2. Water; also बुस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस्
बुस् r. 4th cl. (बुस्यति) To dismiss, to loose, to quit or leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस|बुसं
बुस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Chaff. rubbish, refuse.<BR>	 2. Wealth.<BR>	 3. Dry cow-dung.<BR>	 4.<BR>The thick part of sour curds.<BR>	 f. (-सा) A younger sister, (in<BR>theatrical language.)<BR> E. बुस् to abandon, aff. क; also बुष, स being<BR>changed to ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस्त|बुस्तं
बुस्त r. 10th cl. (बुस्तयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To regard, to respect.<BR>	 2. To disregard, to treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस्त|बुस्तं
बुस्त n. (-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Fried meat.<BR>	 2. The inner part of the jack fruit.<BR> E. बुस्त<BR>to disrespect, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बूक्क|बूक्कं
बूक्क mfn. (-क्कः-क्का-क्कं) The heart; also बुक्क; also with a final न्, बूक्कन् mfn.<BR>(-क्का-क्का-क्क) also बृक्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृक्क|बृक्कं
बृक्क mfn. (-क्कः-क्का-क्कं)<BR>	 1. The heart.<BR>	 2. The kidney. E. See the last, ऋ<BR>substituted for ऊ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृशी
बृशी (षी) f. (-शी or -षी) The seat of a holy sage: also बृसी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृह
बृह r. 1st cl. (बर्हति) To grow, to increase: see वृह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृहत्|बृहन्त्
बृहत् mfn. (-हन् हन्ती हत्) See वृहत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बॄ
बॄ r. 9th cl. (बॄणाति)<BR>	 1. To choose or select 2. To support or nourish;<BR>also in the first sense, वॄ more usually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोद्धव्य
बोद्धव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be informed, taught, waked, &c.<BR>	 2. Re-<BR>quiring to be taught or explained.<BR>	 3. Necessary to be understood.<BR>E. बुध् to know, causal v., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोध|बोधः
बोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Wisdom, intellect.<BR>	 2. A wakening, arousing.<BR> E. बुध् to<BR>understand, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधक|बोधकः
बोधक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A spy, an informer.<BR>	 2. A teacher.<BR> E. बुध् to under-<BR>stand, causal form, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधकर|बोधकरः
बोधकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who teaches, informs, awakes, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः) An<BR>awakener, a sort of minstrel who awakens the prince or chief in<BR>the morning, by music.<BR> E. बोध awakening, कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधन|बोधनं|बोधनः
बोधन nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>	 1. Knowledge.<BR>	 2. Teaching, informing.<BR>	 3. Awaking,<BR>arousing.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Burning incense.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The planet MERCURY.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी) Long-pepper.<BR> E. बुध् to know, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधनीय|बोधनीयः
बोधनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be explained or expounded, to be rendered<BR>intelligible.<BR> E. बुध् to know, in the causal form, aff. अनीयर् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधयत्
बोधयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Informing, apprising.<BR>	 2. Teaching.<BR>	 3.<BR>Arousing, waking.<BR> E. बुध् to know, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधि|बोधिः
बोधि mfn. (-धिः-धिः-धि) Wise, learned.<BR>	 m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. A branch of holy<BR>study; keeping the mind awake to the knowledge of the true GOD.<BR>2. Intellect, understanding.<BR>	 3. The holy fig-tree.<BR> E. बुध् to know,<BR>Unādi aff. इन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधितरु|बोधितरुः
बोधितरु m. (-रुः) The holy fig-tree.<BR> E. बोधि wisdom, and तरु the tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिद्रुम|बोधिद्रुमः
बोधिद्रुम m. (-मः) The holy fig-tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR> E. बोधि know-<BR>ledge, द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिसत्त्व|बोधिसत्त्वं|बोधिसत्त्वः
बोधिसत्त्व m. (-त्त्वः) A Buddha, or Bauddha saint.<BR> E. बोधि intellect, सत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोध्य
बोध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) To be informed, taught, waked, &c.<BR> E. बुध् to<BR>know, causal v., यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौद्ध|बौद्धं|बौद्धः
बौद्ध m. (-द्धः) A Bauddha, or follower of the religion of the Buddhas.<BR>E. बुद्ध a Buddha, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौध|बौधः
बौध m. (-धः) A name of PURŪRAVAS, the son of BUDDHA, and grandson<BR>of SOMA or the moon.<BR> E. बुध् MERCURY, and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्युष्
ब्युष् r. 4th cl. (ब्युष्यति) To burn. r. 10th cl. (ब्युषयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To divide.<BR>	 2.<BR>To offer in oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रण्
ब्रण् r. 1st cl. (ब्रणति) To sound; व्रण more properly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रतति|ब्रततिः
ब्रतति f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>	 1. A creeper.<BR>	 2. Expansion.<BR> E. प्र before, तन् to<BR>spread, aff. क्तिच्, and प changed to ब; also व्रतति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रध्न|ब्रध्नः
ब्रध्न m. (-ध्नः)<BR>	 1. The root of a tree.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. SĪVA.<BR>	 4. BRAHMĀ.<BR>5. A horse.<BR>	 6. The body.<BR>	 7. A day.<BR>	 8. The Arka plant.<BR>	 9. Bubo,<BR>(the disease.)<BR>	 10. Lead.<BR> E. बन्ध् to bind, aff. नक् and ब्रध substituted<BR>for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मकन्यका
ब्रह्मकन्यका f. (-का) The goddesss SARASWATĪ.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and कन्या<BR>the daughter; being born from the head of that deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मगिरि|ब्रह्मगिरिः
ब्रह्मगिरि m. (-रिः) A mountain.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and गिरि a hill; the hill of<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्यघातक
ब्रह्यघातक m. (-कः) The slayer of a Brāhman.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and घातक who<BR>kills; also ब्रह्मघातिन् m. (-ती) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मघातिनी
ब्रह्मघातिनी f. (-नी) A woman on the second day of the menses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मघ्न|ब्रह्मघ्नः
ब्रह्मघ्न m. (-घ्नः) The slayer of a Brāhman.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and घ्न who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्यचर्य्य
ब्रह्यचर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) The Brahmacharya or Brahmachārī, the religious<BR>student: see ब्रह्मचारिन् n. (-र्य्यं) The order or condition of the reli-<BR>gious student.<BR> E. ब्रह्म the Veda and चर्य्य observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मचर्य्यस्खलन|ब्रह्मचर्यस्खलन
ब्रह्मचर्य्यस्खलन n. (-नं) Incontinence.<BR> E. ब्रह्मचर्य्य and स्खखन deviating from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मचारिन्
ब्रह्मचारिन् m. (-री) The Brahmachārī or religious student; the young<BR>Brāhman, from the time of his investiture with the cord, to the<BR>period of his becoming a householder: it is also applied to a per-<BR>son, who continues with his spiritual teacher, through life, study-<BR>ing the Vedas and observing the duties of the student; it is<BR>also given as a title to Pandits learned in the Vedas; to a class of<BR>ascetics; by the Tantras, it is assigned to persons whose chief<BR>virtue is the observance of continence; and it is assumed by<BR>many religious vagabonds.<BR>	 f. (-रिणी A woman leading a life of con-<BR>tinence.<BR> E. ब्रह्म the Veda and चर् to go or follow, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मजन्मन्
ब्रह्मजन्मन् n. (-न्म) Second or spiritual birth, investiture.<BR> E. ब्रह्म the<BR>Vedas and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मजीविन्
ब्रह्मजीविन् m. (-वी) An impure Brāhman, one who converts his religious<BR>duties into a trade, and performs sacrifice, teaches the Veda, &c.<BR>for hire.<BR> E. ब्रह्मन् an officiating priest, and जीविन् who gets a living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मज्ञ|ब्रह्मज्ञः
ब्रह्मज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A sage, one who has spiritual wisdom.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and ज्ञ<BR>who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मज्ञान|ब्रह्मज्ञानं
ब्रह्मज्ञान n. (-नं) Spiritual wisdom.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मण्य|ब्रह्मण्यः
ब्रह्मण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Relating to or connected with BRAHMĀ or a<BR>Brāhman.<BR>	 m. (-ण्यः)<BR>	 1. The mulberry tree, (Morus Indica.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>planet SATURN.<BR> E. ब्रह्मन् and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मतत्त्व
ब्रह्मतत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) The true knowledge of Supreme Spirit.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and तत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मत्व|ब्रह्मत्वं
ब्रह्मत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Identification with BRAHMĀ or God.<BR>	 2. God-head. E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, त्व aff. of the abstract; also with तल् aff. ब्रह्मता, or<BR>with भूय added ब्रह्मभूय n. (-यं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मद|ब्रह्मदः
ब्रह्मद m. (-दः) A spiritual teacher.<BR> E. ब्रह्म the Veda or holy knowledge,<BR>and द who gives, also ब्रह्मदातृ, ब्रह्मदायिन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदण्ड|ब्रह्मदंड|ब्रह्मदण्डः
ब्रह्मदण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A plant. see ब्रह्मयष्टि.<BR>	 2. A curse, an anathema.<BR>3. The tribute paid to a Brāhmana in the shape of a fine.<BR> E. ब्रह्म a<BR>Brāhman and दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदत्त|ब्रह्मदत्तः
ब्रह्मदत्त m. (-त्तः) One of the sovereigns of the race of Ikshwāku<BR>enumerated by the Jains.<BR> E. ब्रह्म by or to BRAHMĀ, दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदर्भा
ब्रह्मदर्भा f. (-र्भा) A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen, Rox.)<BR> E. ब्रह्म and दर्भा<BR>sacrificial grass. “यमानिकायाम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदान
ब्रह्मदान n. (-नं) Instruction in the Vedas.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मदारु|ब्रह्मदारुः
ब्रह्मदारु m. (-रुं) The mulberry, (Morus Indica.)<BR> E. ब्रह्म and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मन्
ब्रह्मन् m. (-ह्मा)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ, the first deity of the Hindu triad, and the<BR>operative creator of the world.<BR>	 2. A Brāhman.<BR>	 3. The superin-<BR>tending or presiding priest at the sacrifice.<BR>	 4. One of the astrono-<BR>mical Yogas.<BR>	 5. One of the principal servants of the Jinas.<BR>	 n. (-ह्म)<BR>1. The divine cause and essence of the world, from which all<BR>created things are supposed to emanate and to which they return;<BR>the unknown God.<BR>	 2. The practice of austere devotion.<BR>	 3. The<BR>Vedas or scripture.<BR>	 4. Holy knowledge.<BR> E. वृह् to increase, (man-<BR>kind) aff. मनिन् and the initial letter changed to ब ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मनाभ|ब्रह्मनाभः
ब्रह्मनाभ m. (-भः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. ब्रह्मन् BRAHMĀ and नाभि the navel; BRAH-<BR>MĀ having arisen to create the world, in a lotus, which sprang<BR>from the navel of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मनिर्व्वाण|ब्रह्मनिर्वाण|ब्रह्मनिर्व्वाणं
ब्रह्मनिर्व्वाण n. (-णं) Absorption into or identification with the Supreme.<BR>E. ब्रह्म, and निर्व्वाण final absorption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मपद
ब्रह्मपद n. (-दं) The place or nature of spiritual being.<BR>	 2. The station or<BR>rank of a Brahman or of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. ब्रह्म, and पद to place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मपादप|ब्रह्मपादपः
ब्रह्मपादप m. (-पः) The Palāsh tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. ब्रह्म a Brāhman,<BR>and पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मपुत्त्र
ब्रह्मपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. A sort of poison.<BR>	 2. The Brahmaputra river, which<BR>rises in the Himālaya and with the Ganges falls into the Bay of<BR>Bengal.<BR>	 2. A place of pilgrimage, probably the source of the<BR>stream.<BR>	 f. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. The SARASWATĪ river.<BR>	 2. The goddess SARAS-<BR>WATĪ.<BR> E. ब्रह्मन् BRAHMĀ and पुत्त्र offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मपुरी
ब्रह्मपुरी f. (-री) The capital of BRAHMĀ on the mountain Kailasā. E.<BR>ब्रह्मन् and पुरी the city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मबन्धु|ब्रह्मबंधु|ब्रह्मबन्धुः
ब्रह्मबन्धु m. (-न्धुः)<BR>	 1. The epithet or appellative of a BRĀHMAN.<BR>	 2. A<BR>term of abuse.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ and बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मभूत
ब्रह्मभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Become one with the Supreme spirit.<BR> E. ब्रह्म<BR>and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मभूति|ब्रह्मभूतिः
ब्रह्मभूति f. (-तिः) Twilight.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ and भूति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मभूय|ब्रह्मभूयं
ब्रह्मभूय n. (-यं) Identification with BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, and भूय<BR>being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्ममय
ब्रह्ममय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Consisting of or identified with spirit.<BR>	 2. Belong-<BR>ing to or fit for a BRĀHMAN, &c.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्ममूर्द्धभृत्
ब्रह्ममूर्द्धभृत् m. (-भृत्) ŚIVA.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, मूर्द्धन् the forehead and भृत् who<BR>has: having in a dispute cut off one of BRAHMĀ'S heads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मयज्ञ|ब्रह्मयज्ञः
ब्रह्मयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) The study of the Vedas.<BR> E. ब्रह्म a Veda or the Supreme<BR>being, and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मयष्टि|ब्रह्मयष्टिः
ब्रह्मयष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen, Rox.)<BR> E. ब्रह्म a Brāhman<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">Page521-a+ 60</a>]<BR>and यष्टि a stick; also with कन् added in the fem. form, ब्रह्मयष्टिका,<BR>for with ङीप् added ब्रह्मयष्टी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मयोग|ब्रह्मयोगः
ब्रह्मयोग m. (-गः) Cultivation of spiritual knowledge.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and योग addition to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मयोनि|ब्रह्मयोनिः
ब्रह्मयोनि m. (-निः) A particular mountain. Adj. Sprung from BRAHMĀ.<BR>E. ब्रह्म and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मरन्ध्र|ब्रह्मरंध्र|ब्रह्मरन्ध्रं
ब्रह्मरन्ध्र n. (-न्ध्रं) An aperture in the crown of the head, through which<BR>the soul is supposed to escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मंराक्षस
ब्रह्मंराक्षस m. (-सः) A demon or fiend of the Brāhminical class.<BR> E. ब्रह्म<BR>and राक्षम a goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मरात्रि|ब्रह्मरात्रिः
ब्रह्मरात्रि m. (-त्रिः)<BR>	 1. A name of YĀJNYAVALKYA, a saint and legislator.<BR>E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, रा to give, ष्ट्रिन् aff.; conferring the knowledge of<BR>BRAHMĀ upon JANAKA in return for his bounty.<BR>	 2. A night of<BR>BRAHMĀ, equal to a thousand divine ages.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ and<BR>रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मरीति|ब्रह्मरीतिः
ब्रह्मरीति f. (-तिः) Brass.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and रीति calx.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मरेखा
ब्रह्मरेखा f. (-खा) The lines written by BRAHMĀ on the forehead of a<BR>man indicative of his lot in this world: also ब्रह्मलेखा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मर्षि|ब्रह्मर्षिः
ब्रह्मर्षि m. (-र्षिः) A divine saint, a Ṛṣi of a particular class, including<BR>VĀSISHṬHA, &c.<BR> E. ब्रह्म a Brāhman, and ऋषि a saint; the saints<BR>of this class are supposed to be of the Brāhminical order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मर्षिदेश|ब्रह्मर्षिदेशः
ब्रह्मर्षिदेश m. (-शः) A part of India, including the four countries of<BR>Kuru-kshetra, Matsya, Panchāla, and Surasena or Mathurā. E.<BR>ब्रह्मर्षि a Ṛṣi, देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मलोक|ब्रह्मलोकः
ब्रह्मलोक m. (-कः) A division of the universe, the supposed eternal resi-<BR>dence of the spirits of the pious.<BR> E. ब्रह्मन् BRAHMĀ and लोक a<BR>world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवद्य|ब्रह्मवद्यं
ब्रह्मवद्य n. (-द्यं) Knowledge or declaration of BRAHMĀ, the knowledge of<BR>the universal permeation of one spirit, as taught by the Vedānta<BR>system of philosophy. E. BRAHMĀ or the spiritual deity, वद् to<BR>speak or declare, aff. क्यप्, also with the aff. यत्, and the semi-vowel<BR>changed, ब्रह्मोद्य n. (-द्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्च्चस्|ब्रह्मवर्चस्
ब्रह्मवर्च्चस् n. (-र्च्चः) The power or sanctity of a Brāhman.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and वर्च्चस् splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्च्चस|ब्रह्मवर्चस|ब्रह्मवर्च्चसं
ब्रह्मवर्च्चस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Holiness, resulting from the study and observance<BR>of the Vedas.<BR>	 2. The sanctity or superhuman power of a Brāh-<BR>man.<BR> E. ब्रह्म the Velas, and वर्च्चस splendour, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्च्चस्विन्|ब्रह्मवर्चस्विन्
ब्रह्मवर्च्चस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>	 1. Endowed with sanctity, pure, pious.<BR>2. Having Brāhminical power or virtue.<BR> E. ब्रह्मवर्च्चस्, and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्त्त|ब्रह्मवर्त|ब्रह्मवर्तः|ब्रह्मवर्त्तः
ब्रह्मवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A district of western India; also ब्रह्मावर्त्त.<BR> E. ब्रह्म a<BR>Brāhman, and वृत् to abide, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवर्द्धन
ब्रह्मवर्द्धन n. (-नं) Copper.<BR> E. ब्रह्म a Brāhman, and वर्द्धन increasing, favour-<BR>ing; being highly proper for utensils of worship. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवाद|ब्रह्मवादः
ब्रह्मवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Citing the Vedas.<BR>	 2. Declaring or teaching spiritual<BR>knowledge.<BR> E. ब्रह्म scripture, and वाद speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवादिन्
ब्रह्मवादिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A follower of the Vedānta system of philosophy,<BR>one who maintains all things are spirit.<BR>	 2. A defender or ex-<BR>pounder of the Veda.<BR> E. ब्रह्म the Veda or BRAHMĀ, GOD, and वादिन्<BR>who recites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मविद्
ब्रह्मविद् m. (-वित् or -विद्) A sage, one who knows the nature of the<BR>Supreme Spirit.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मविद्या
ब्रह्मविद्या f. (-द्या) Knowledge of spirit.<BR> E. ब्रह्म, and विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मविन्दु|ब्रह्मविंदु|ब्रह्मविन्दुः
ब्रह्मविन्दु m. (-न्दुः) A drop of saliva sputtered out in reading the Vedas.<BR>E. ब्रह्म scripture, and विन्दु a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवृक्ष|ब्रह्मवृक्षः
ब्रह्मवृक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The Palāsh tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>	 2. The glomer-<BR>ulus fig-tree.<BR> E. ब्रह्म a BRAHMĀ and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवृन्दा
ब्रह्मवृन्दा f. (-न्द्रा) The capital of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. ब्रह्मन् and वृन्द heap, assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवेद|ब्रह्मवेदः
ब्रह्मवेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Knowledge of BRAHMĀ, monotheism.<BR>	 2. Knowledge<BR>of the Vedas.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ and वेद knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवेदि|ब्रह्मवेदिः
ब्रह्मवेदि f. (-दिः) A country. see ब्रह्मावर्त्त.<BR> E. ब्रह्म a Brāhman and बेदि a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवेदिन्
ब्रह्मवेदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Knowing or acquainted with the Vedas,<BR>with spiritual knowledge, &c.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मशल्य|ब्रह्मशल्यः
ब्रह्मशल्य m. (-ल्यः) A tree, (Mimosa Arabica.)<BR> E. ब्रह्म a Brāhman, and शल्य<BR>a stake. “वाव्ला” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मशासन|ब्रह्मशासनं
ब्रह्मशासन n. (-नं) An edict or grant, &c. addressed to Brāhmans.<BR> E. ब्रह्म<BR>a Brāhman and शासन governing or an edict, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसत्र
ब्रह्मसत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Study and teaching of the Vedas.<BR>	 2. The constant<BR>study of them.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and सत्र sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसर्प|ब्रह्मसर्पः
ब्रह्मसर्प m. (-र्पः) A sort of snake.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ and सर्प a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसम्भव|ब्रह्मसंभव|ब्रह्मसंभवः|ब्रह्मसम्भवः
ब्रह्मसम्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Born or produced from BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 m. (-वः) The<BR>second of the persons called VĀSUDEVA or KṚṢṆA by the Jains.<BR>E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ and सम्भव offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसायुज्य|ब्रह्मसायुज्यं
ब्रह्मसायुज्य n. (-ज्यं) Identification with BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ and<BR>सायुज्य intimate union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसार्ष्टिता
ब्रह्मसार्ष्टिता f. (-ता) Equality with BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and सार्ष्टिता sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसुवर्च्चला|ब्रह्मसुवर्चला
ब्रह्मसुवर्च्चला f. (-ला) A plant, an infusion of which is to be drank in ex-<BR>piation of having anything touched by a dog, cat, &c.<BR> E. ब्रह्म,<BR>and सुवर्च्चला linseed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसू
ब्रह्मसू m. (-सूः)<BR>	 1. ANIRUDDHA, the son of KĀMA.<BR>	 2. KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. ब्रह्म<BR>BRAHMĀ and सू the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसूत्र|ब्रह्मसूत्रं
ब्रह्मसूत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The sacrificial or Brāhminical thread.<BR>	 2. An aphor-<BR>ism of the Vedānta philosophy.<BR> E. ब्रह्म a Brāhman and सूत्र thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसूनु|ब्रह्मसूनुः
ब्रह्मसूनु m. (-नुः) A sovereign according to the Jains, of the race of Iksh-<BR>wāku.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ and सूनु son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मस्वरूप
ब्रह्मस्वरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Of the nature of spirit, of the same essence as<BR>the God-head.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and स्वरूप nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महत्या
ब्रह्महत्या f. (-त्या)<BR>	 1. Brāhminicide, killing a Brāhman.<BR>	 2. Any crime<BR>equally heinous.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and हत्या killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महन्
ब्रह्महन् m. (-हा) The murderer or slayer of a Brāhman.<BR> E. ब्रह्मन् and हन्<BR>who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महुत|ब्रह्महुतं
ब्रह्महुत n. (-तं) The performance of hospitality, &c., that one of the<BR>great sacraments which consists in the veneration of mankind. E.<BR>ब्रह्म a Brāhman हुत worshipped; being the most worthy of res-<BR>pect, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माक्षर
ब्रह्माक्षर m. (-रः) The sacred and mysterious name of the deity.<BR> E. ब्रह्म<BR>GOD, अक्षर a letter, the Omkāra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माग्रभू
ब्रह्माग्रभू m. (-भूः) A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माञ्जलि|ब्रह्मांजलि|ब्रह्माञ्जलिः
ब्रह्माञ्जलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. Joining both hands together, whilst reading the<BR>Vedas, either as an act of humility or to mark the accentuation<BR>of the Sāma-Veda.<BR>	 2. Paying obeisance to the spiritual preceptor<BR>at the beginning or end of a lecture.<BR> E. ब्रह्म the Vedas and अञ्चलि<BR>the hands joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माणी
ब्रह्माणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The female energy of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A sort of perfume,<BR>commonly Renukā.<BR>	 3. A kind of brass; “वेङापितल” ।<BR> E. ब्रह्मन्<BR>BRAHMĀ, fem. aff. ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माण्ड|ब्रह्मांड|ब्रह्माण्डं
ब्रह्माण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. The globe, the world.<BR>	 2. One of the Purānas.<BR> E. ब्रह्म<BR>BRAHMĀ and अण्ड an egg, to which it is compared; in creation<BR>there are said to have been innumerable Brahmāndas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माधिगमन
ब्रह्माधिगमन n. (-नं) Perusal of the Vedas.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and अघिगमन going<BR>through; also ब्रह्माधिगम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माधिगामिक
ब्रह्माधिगामिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or contributing to a course of<BR>sacred study.<BR> E. ब्रह्माधिगम and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माभ्यास|ब्रह्माभ्यासः
ब्रह्माभ्यास m. (-सः) Study or repetition of scripture.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and अभ्यास exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माम्भस्|ब्रह्मांभस्
ब्रह्माम्भस् n. (-म्भं) Cow's urine.<BR> E. ब्रह्मन् a Brāhman and अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मारण्य|ब्रह्मारण्यं
ब्रह्मारण्य n. (-ण्यं) A place where the Vedas are read and explained. E.<BR>ब्रह्म the Veda and अरण्य a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मावर्त्त|ब्रह्मावर्त|ब्रह्मावर्तः|ब्रह्मावर्त्तः
ब्रह्मावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) The country to the north-west of Delhi, lying<BR>between the rivers Saraswatī and Dṛṣadvatī.<BR> E. ब्रह्म a Brāh-<BR>man आवर्त्त abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मासन|ब्रह्मासनं
ब्रह्मासन n. (-नं) A posture suited to devout and religious meditation. E.<BR>ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ and आसन sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मास्त्र|ब्रह्मास्त्रं
ब्रह्मास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) The BRAHMĀ'S weapon, a fabulous weapon originally<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">Page522-a+ 60</a>]<BR>from BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. The imprecation of a Brāhman.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and अस्त्र<BR>a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=521-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माहूति
ब्रह्माहूति f. (-तिः) An oblation of ghee.<BR> E. ब्रह्म the Veda, and आहूति an offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मो
ब्रह्मो f. (-ह्मी)<BR>	 1. A sort of fish, commonly Pāncāl, (Macrognathus Pan-<BR>calus, HAM.)<BR>	 2. A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR> E. वृह् to grow or<BR>increase, affs. मनिन् and ङीप्; also ब्राह्मी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मोज्झता
ब्रह्मोज्झता f. (-ता) Neglecting or forgetting the Veda.<BR> E. ब्रह्म, उज्झता<BR>abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मोद्य|ब्रह्मोद्यं
ब्रह्मोद्य n. (-द्यं) Reciting or explaining the Vedas.<BR> E. ब्रह्म, वद् to speak, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मौदन|ब्रह्मौदनं|ब्रह्मौदनः
ब्रह्मौदन n. (-नं) Boiled-rice distributed to priests at a sacrifice.<BR> E. ब्रह्मन् a<BR>Brāhman and ओदन boiled-rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रा
ब्रा (व्रा) ह्म mfn. (ह्मः-ह्मी-ह्मं) Relating or belonging to BRAHMĀ, the Vedas,<BR>&c.<BR>	 n. (-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. The part of the hand under the root of the<BR>thumb.<BR>	 2. One of the eight forms of marriage, the presentation<BR>of the bride elegantly adorned, by the father to the bridegroom<BR>whom he has invited.<BR>	 3. The missile presided over by<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 m. (-ह्मः) NĀRADA the sage and son of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ह्मी) One of the eight divine mothers of created beings, or<BR>the personified energies of the gods; the Saktī or energy of<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. The goddess of speech, SARASWATĪ.<BR>	 3. The<BR>moon plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>	 4. A sort of potherb, (Ruta grave-<BR>olens.<BR>	 5. A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>	 6. A sort of fish.<BR>	 7.<BR>The asterism Rohini.<BR>	 8. A she-frog.<BR>	 9. A yellow-coloured ant.<BR>	 10.<BR>The wife of a Brāhman.<BR> E. ब्रह्म BRAHMĀ, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण|ब्राह्मणं|ब्राह्मणः
ब्राह्मण m. (-णः) A man of the first Hindu tribe, a Brāhman.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1.<BR>An assemblage of Brāhmans, a council, a conclave.<BR>	 2. A portion of<BR>the Vedas, that which comprises the precepts that inculcate reli-<BR>gious duties, the maxims which explain those precepts and the<BR>arguments which relate to theology; it is, however, now often<BR>blended with other portions.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The wife of a Brāhman,<BR>or a woman of the Brāhminical tribe.<BR>	 2. A kind of wasp.<BR>	 3. A<BR>small ant.<BR>	 4. a potherb, (Ruta graveolens.)<BR>	 5. A shrub, (Sipho-<BR>nanthus Indica.)<BR>	 5. A sort of grass, (Trigonella corniculata.) E.<BR>ब्रह्मन् the Veda, &c. अण् aff. and the final syllable of the ori-<BR>ginal word retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणचाण्डाल|ब्राह्मणचांडाल|ब्राह्मणचाण्डालः
ब्राह्मणचाण्डाल m. (-लः) An outcaste Brāhman, one who is attended by a<BR>wife of another caste or the son of a Śūdra by a Brāhman female.<BR>E. ब्राह्मण and चाण्डाल an outcaste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणजाति|ब्राह्मणजातिः
ब्राह्मणजाति f. (-तिः) The Brāhminical tribe or caste.<BR> E. ब्राह्मण and जाति tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणजातीय
ब्राह्मणजातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging to the Brāhminical race.<BR> E. ब्राह्मण<BR>and जातीय generic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणजीविका
ब्राह्मणजीविका f. (-का) The occupation or subsistence of a Brāhman. E.<BR>ब्राह्मण and जीविका livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणता
ब्राह्मणता f. (-ता) Brāhmanhood.<BR> E. ब्राह्मण and तल् aff.; also with त्व, ब्राह्मणत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणबध
ब्राह्मणबध m. (-धः) Brāhminicide.<BR> E. ब्राह्मण and बध killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणब्रुव|ब्राह्मणब्रुवः
ब्राह्मणब्रुव m. (-वः) A Brāhman by birth but not by attention to his du-<BR>ties; one who subsists by avocations properly limited to the<BR>other tribes.<BR> E. ब्राह्मण a Brāhman and ब्रुव who speaks, who calls<BR>himself, (improperly.) a Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणयष्टिका
ब्राह्मणयष्टिका f. (-का) A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR> E. ब्राह्मण a Brāh-<BR>man and यष्टि a staff, aff. कन् । “वामनहाटी” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणसंस्थ
ब्राह्मणसंस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Belonging to or abiding with a Brāhman.<BR>E. ब्राह्मण and संस्थ what stays with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणहित|ब्राह्मणहितः
ब्राह्मणहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Suitable to or fit for a Brāhman.<BR> E. ब्राह्मण and<BR>हित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणातिक्रम|ब्राह्मणातिक्रमः
ब्राह्मणातिक्रम m. (-मः) Disregarding or disrespecting Brāhmans.<BR> E. ब्राह्मण<BR>and अतिक्रम going over or beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणात्मक
ब्राह्मणात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Belonging to, or with one containing<BR>Brāhmans, the Brāhmana section of the Vedas, &c.<BR> E. ब्राह्मण and<BR>आत्मक own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणादर्शन
ब्राह्मणादर्शन n. (-नं) Absence of Brāhminical instruction or guidance. E.<BR>ब्राह्मण and अदर्शन not showing or teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्ति|ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्तिः
ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्ति f. (-त्तिः) The protection of a Brāhman. E.<BR>ब्राह्मण and अभ्युपपत्ति defence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणायण
ब्राह्मणायण m. (-णः) A Brāhman, sprung from a learned and holy proge-<BR>nitors.<BR> E. ब्राह्मण and फक् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणीगामिन्
ब्राह्मणीगामिन् m. (-मी) The gallant of a woman of the Brāhminical tribe<BR>or the wife of a Brāhman.<BR> E. ब्राह्मणी a female Brāhman. and गामिन्<BR>who goes to or with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण्य|ब्राह्मण्यः
ब्राह्मण्य m. (-ण्यः) The planet SATURN.<BR>	 n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. An assembly of Brāh-<BR>mans.<BR>	 2. The state, quality or business of a Brāhman, Brāhman-<BR>hood.<BR> E. ब्रह्मन् and यञ् aff.; or ब्राह्मन and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मदेया
ब्राह्मदेया f. (-या) A girl to be wedded by the Brāhma form.<BR> E. ब्राह्म and<BR>देय to be given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मपिङ्गा
ब्राह्मपिङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) Silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्ममुहूर्त्त|ब्राह्ममुहूर्त|ब्राह्ममुहूर्तः|ब्राह्ममुहूर्त्तः
ब्राह्ममुहूर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A particular period of the early part of the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्माहोरात्र|ब्राह्माहोरात्रः
ब्राह्माहोरात्र m. (-त्र) A day and night of BRAHMĀ, a period of two thou-<BR>sand ages of the gods or two Kalpas of mortals.<BR> E. ब्राह्मण relating<BR>to BRAHMĀ, अहन् a day and रात्रि a night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मिका
ब्राह्मिका f. (-का) A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR> E. ब्राह्मी and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मीपुत्त्र
ब्राह्मीपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) The son of a woman married according to the<BR>Brāhma form.<BR> E. ब्राह्मी and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म्य|ब्राह्म्यं
ब्राह्म्य n. (-ह्म्यं)<BR>	 1. The worship or veneration of Brāhmans, considered<BR>as one of the great sacraments.<BR>	 2. Astonishments.<BR> E. ब्रह्म and<BR>ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्महुत
ब्राह्महुत n. (-तं) Respect shown to guests, especially to Brāhmans, hos-<BR>pitality.<BR> E. ब्राह्म्य and हुत sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रुवत्
ब्रुवत् mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्) Speaking, saying.<BR> E. ब्रु to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रूवाण
ब्रूवाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Speaking, saying.<BR> E. ब्रू to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रू
ब्रू (ञ) ब्रूञ् r. 2nd cl. (ब्रवीति or आह) To speak or tell: आह is option-<BR>ally substituted for this root before the first five inflections of the<BR>present tense and वच in several other tenses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्लेष्क|ब्लेष्कं
ब्लेष्क n. (-ष्कं) A snare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ|भं|भः
भ The twenty-fourth consonant of the Nāgari alphabet and aspirate<BR>of the last letter, or Bh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ|भं|भः
भ n. (-भं)<BR>	 1. A star.<BR>	 2. An asterism.<BR>	 3. A planet.<BR>	 4. The number<BR>twenty-seven.<BR>	 m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A name of SUKRA, regent of the planet<BR>VENUS.<BR>	 2. A bee.<BR>	 2. Error, delusion.<BR>	 f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. Light, lustre,<BR>splendour.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR>	 f. (-मी) Fear.<BR> E. भा to shine, or भी to<BR>fear, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्किका
भक्किका f. (-का) A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्त|भक्तं|भक्तः
भक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Attached or attentive to, devoted to, engrossed<BR>by.<BR>	 2. Served, worshipped.<BR>	 3. Dressed, cooked.<BR>	 4. Distributed.<BR>5. Divided.<BR>	 6. Loyal.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Boiled-rice.<BR>	 2. Food.<BR>	 3. Any<BR>edible grain boiled with water.<BR>	 4. A share.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) A follower,<BR>a votary.<BR> E. भज् to serve, &c. aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तकर|भक्तकरः
भक्तकर m. (-रः) Factitious incense, incense prepared from various fra-<BR>grant resins and perfumes.<BR> E. भक्त dressed, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तकार|भक्तकारः
भक्तकार m. (-रः) A cook.<BR> E. भक्त boiled rice, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तछन्द|भक्तच्छन्द|भक्तच्छंद
भक्तछन्द n. (-न्दं) Appetite, wish for food.<BR> E. भक्त and छन्द will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तजा
भक्तजा f. (-जा) Nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तता
भक्तता f. (-ता) Devotedness, implied faith in and attachment to<BR> E. भक्त<BR>and तल् aff.; also with त्व, भक्तत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=522-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ततूर्य्य|भक्ततूर्य|भक्ततूर्य्यं
भक्ततूर्य्य n. (र्य्यं) Music played at the hour of eating, amongst princes<BR>and great men.<BR> E. भक्त rice or food. and तूर्य्यं a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तद
भक्तद m. (-दः) A supporter, a maintainer.<BR> E. भक्त and द who gives:<BR>also भक्तदायक, भक्तदायिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तदातृ
भक्तदातृ m. (-ता) A maintainer, a feeder.<BR> E. मक्त food and दातृ a donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तदास|भक्तदासः
भक्तदास m. (-सः) A slave, one maintained in consideration of service.<BR>E. भक्त food, दास a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ति|भक्तिः
भक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Service, worship.<BR>	 2. Faith, belief.<BR>	 3. Devotion or<BR>attachment to.<BR>	 4. Part, portion.<BR>	 5. Fracture, division.<BR>	 6. Meto-<BR>nymy.<BR> E. भज् to serve, or भञ्ज् to break, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिमत्|भक्तिमन्त्
भक्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Faithful, devoted to.<BR> E. भक्ति and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तियोग|भक्तियोगः
भक्तियोग m. (-गः) Devotion or worship. as shown by implicit faith in<BR>any divinity.<BR> E. भक्ति and योग devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिल|भक्तिलः
भक्तिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A good horse.<BR>	 2. A follower, a votary.<BR> E. भक्ति ser-<BR>vice, &c. ला to afford, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्
भक्ष् r. 1st and 10th cls. (-भक्षति भक्षयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To eat.<BR>	 2. To waste.<BR>	 3. To bite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षक|भक्षकः
भक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Gluttonous, voracious, gourmand.<BR>	 2. A feeder,<BR>an eater, who or what eats.<BR>	 f. (-क्षिका) A meal, a feed.<BR> E. भक्ष् to<BR>eat, aff. ण्वल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षकार|भक्षकारः
भक्षकार m. (-रः) A confectioner, a pastry cook.<BR> E. भक्ष् food, कार who<BR>prepares; also भक्षङ्कार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षण|भक्षणं
भक्षण n. (-णं) Eating.<BR> E. भक्ष् to eat, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षणीय|भक्षणीयं
भक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Eatable, to be eaten.<BR> E. भक्ष् and अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षमाण
भक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Eating.<BR> E. भक्ष to eat, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षयत्
भक्षयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Eaten.<BR> E. भक्ष् to eat, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षित|भक्षितं
भक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eaten.<BR> E. भक्ष् to eat, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षितव्य
भक्षितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be eaten, what may be eaten.<BR> E. भक्ष् to<BR>eat, तव्य aff.; also भक्षयितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्य|भक्ष्यं
भक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्य) Eatable.<BR>	 n. (-क्ष्यं) Food.<BR> E. भक्ष् to eat, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्यकार|भक्ष्यकारः
भक्ष्यकार m. (-रः) A baker.<BR> E. भक्ष्य eatable and कार who makes or pre-<BR>pares; also भक्ष्यंकार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्यमाण
भक्ष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) To be eaten.<BR> E. भक्ष् to eat, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग|भगं|भगः
भग n. (गं)<BR>	 1. Pudendum muliebre.<BR>	 2. Fortune, prosperity.<BR>	 3. Beauty,<BR>splendour.<BR>	 4. Excellence, greatness.<BR>	 5. Desire, wish, love.<BR>	 6.<BR>Strength, vigour.<BR>	 7. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 8. Fame, glory.<BR>	 9. Know-<BR>ledge.<BR>	 10. Absence of passion, the tranquillity of the religious<BR>man, who has divested himself of worldly excitability.<BR>	 11. Omni-<BR>potence, supreme or divine power.<BR>	 12. Virtue, moral merit.<BR>	 13.<BR>Final emancipation.<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. One of the twelve suns<BR>or Ādityas.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR>	 4. A form of ŚIVA.<BR> E. भज् to serve, &c.<BR>ग aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगण|भगणः
भगण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The whole multitude of stars.<BR>	 2. Revolution of the<BR>planets in the Zodiac.<BR>	 3. The Zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगदेवता
भगदेवता f. (-ता) Hymeneal divinity.<BR> E. भग and देवता divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगन्दर|भगंदर|भगंदरः|भगन्दरः
भगन्दर m. (-रः) Fistula in ano.<BR> E. भग the vulva, दृ to divide, aff. खश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवत्|भगवन्त्
भगवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Respectable, worshipful, adorable, and hence<BR>the common appellative of a prince or deity.<BR>	 m. (-वान्) One of the<BR>generic titles of a Jina or Jaina deified sage.<BR>	 f. (-वती)<BR>	 1. A name<BR>of GAURĪ.<BR>	 2. Any goddess.<BR> E. भग fortune, supremacy, &c., and<BR>मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगाङ्कुर|भगांकुर|भगाङ्कुरः
भगाङ्कुर m. (-रः) The clitoris.<BR> E. भग and अङ्कुर a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगाल|भगालं
भगाल m. (-लः) The human skull.<BR> E. भग ŚIVA, अल् to adorn, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगालिन्
भगालिन् m. (-लो) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. भगाल a skull, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगिन्
भगिन् f. (-नी) Adj.<BR>	 1. Prosperous, fortunate.<BR>	 2. Grand, splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगिनी
भगिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A sister.<BR>	 2. A lucky woman.<BR>	 3. A woman in general.<BR>E. भग prosperity, desire, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगीरथ|भगीरथः
भगीरथ m. (-थः) A king of the solar dynasty, whose austerities brought<BR>down GANGĀ, the river, from heaven to the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगोल|भगोलः
भगोल m. (-लः) The starry sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगोस्
भगोस् Ind. A particle used as a respectful term of address.<BR> E. भगवत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">Page523-b+ 60</a>]<BR>reverend and ओस् irregularly substituted for the three final<BR>letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्न|भग्नं
भग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Torn, broken.<BR>	 2. Overcome, defeated.<BR>	 3. Disre-<BR>garded, despised.<BR>	 4. Disappointed.<BR>	 5. Destroyed.<BR>	 6. Checked.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-ग्नं) Fracture of the leg.<BR> E. भञ्ज् to break, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नजानु
भग्नजानु mfn. (-नुः-नुः-नु) Having a broken leg.<BR> E. भग्न and जानु the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नपृष्ठ|भग्नपृष्ठः
भग्नपृष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Confronting, encountering, coming before or in<BR>front of.<BR> E. भग्न disregarded and पृष्ठ the back, heedless of what is<BR>behind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नप्रक्रम
भग्नप्रक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Disorder, confusion.<BR>	 2. Want of method or arrange-<BR>ment in composition.<BR> E. भग्न and प्रक्रम proceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नसन्धिक|भग्नसंधिक|भग्नसन्धिकं
भग्नसन्धिक n. (-कं) Butter milk.<BR> E. भग्न broken, सन्धि union, and कप् aff.;<BR>divided by churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नात्मन्
भग्नात्मन् m. (-त्मा) The moon.<BR> E. भग्न broken and आत्मन् the body; having<BR>been cut in two by the trident of ŚIVA, as a punishment for<BR>having violated the wife of VRIHASPATĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नाश|भग्नाशः
भग्नाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Disappointed.<BR> E. भग्न and आशा expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नी
भग्नी f. (-ग्नी) A sister.<BR> E. भञ्ज् to share, aff. क्त, fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नोद्यम
भग्नोद्यम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Labouring in vain.<BR>	 2. Baffled.<BR> E. भग्न, उद्यम effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्कारी|भंकारी
भङ्कारी f. (-री) A bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्क्तृ
भङ्क्तृ mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ) Breaking, a breaker, who or what breaks.<BR> E. भञ्ज् to break, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्ग|भंग|भंगः|भङ्गः
भङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Breaking, splitting.<BR>	 2. A chasm, a fissure, a division.<BR>3. Defeat, discomfiture.<BR>	 4. Disappointment.<BR>	 5. Fear.<BR>	 6. Dishonesty,<BR>fraud, circumvention, cheating.<BR>	 7. Going, motion.<BR>	 8. A wave.<BR>	 9. A<BR>water-course, a canal.<BR>	 10. Disease in general.<BR>	 11. A disease, (hemi-<BR>plegia, palsy.)<BR>	 12. Interruption of the voice.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>	 1. Hemp,<BR>(Cannabis sativa.)<BR>	 2. A plant, commonly Teori.<BR>	 3. A fibrous plant<BR>from which a sort of flax is obtained, (Crotolaria juncea.)<BR> E. भञ्ज्<BR>to break, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गभाज्
भङ्गभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Breaking, being broken.<BR> E. भङ्ग, and भाज् partaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गवासा|भंगवासा
भङ्गवासा f. (-सा) Tumeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गसार्थ|भंगसार्थ|भङ्गसार्थः
भङ्गसार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Crafty, fraudulent, dishonest.<BR> E. भङ्ग breaking,<BR>fraud, &c., स for सम् with, and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गान|भङ्गानः
भङ्गान m. (-नः) A sort of fish, (Cyprinus Banggana, HAM.)<BR> E. भङ्ग a<BR>wave, अन् to live, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गारी|भंगारी
भङ्गारी f. (-री) A bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गि|भंगि|भंगिः|भङ्गिः
भङ्गि f. (-ङ्गिः-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. Fracture, division, separation.<BR>	 2. Fraud, deception,<BR>trick, disguise.<BR>	 3. Irony.<BR>	 4. Wit, repartee.<BR>	 5. A wave.<BR>	 6. A<BR>crooked path.<BR>	 7. A step.<BR>	 8. Modesty.<BR>	 9. A current.<BR>	 10. Interval.<BR>11. Circumlocation.<BR> E. भञ्ज् to break, aff. इन्, ङीप् optionally<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गील|भंगील
भङ्गील n. (-लं) Defeat in the organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गुर|भंगुर|भङ्गुरः
भङ्गुर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Crooked, bent.<BR>	 2. Fraudulent, crafty, dishon-<BR>est.<BR>	 3. Perishable.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The bend or elbow of a river.<BR> E. भञ्ज्<BR>to break, aff. घुरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्ग्य|भंग्यं|भङ्ग्यं
भङ्ग्य n. (-ङ्ग्यं) A field of hemp.<BR> E. भङ्गा hemp, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भज
भज r. 1st cl. (औ) भजौ (भजति-ते) 1. To serve, to worship.<BR>	 2. To possess,<BR>to enjoy, (carnally.) r. 10th cl. (भजयति)<BR>	 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To dress or<BR>cook.<BR>	 3. To separate or divide: see भाज् (इ) भजि r. 10th cl. (भंज-<BR>यति)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To speak: with वि prefixed, to measure; with<BR>प्र and वि, to discriminate, to discuss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजत्
भजत् mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>	 1. Serving, waiting upon.<BR>	 2. Enjoying, (carnal-<BR>ly.)<BR>	 3. Dividing, sharing.<BR> E. भज् to serve, &c., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजन|भजनं
भजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Service, adoration.<BR>	 2. Possessing or enjoying carnally.<BR>3. Sharing.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The sound of the conch.<BR> E. भज् to serve,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजमान|भजमानः
भजमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Serving, waiting.<BR>	 2. Enjoying, possessing,<BR>(carnally.)<BR>	 3. Dividing, sharing.<BR>	 4. Right, fit, proper.<BR> E. भज् to<BR>serve, &c., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्ज्|भंज्
भञ्ज् (ओ, औ) ओभञ्जौ r. 7th cl. (भनक्ति) To break, to destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जक|भंजक|भञ्जकः
भञ्जक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what breaks, severes, divides, destroys,<BR>&c.<BR> E. भञ्ज् to break, ण्वुल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जत्
भञ्जत् mfn. (-ञ्जन्-ञ्जन्ती-ञ्जत) Breaking, destroying<BR> E. भञ्ज्, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जन|भंजन|भञ्जनं|भञ्जनः
भञ्जन nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>	 1. Breaking, destroying.<BR>	 2. Afflicting.<BR>	 3. Arresting.<BR>	 4.<BR>Causing violent pain.<BR>	 5. Routing.<BR>	 6. Removing.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Decay<BR>of teeth.<BR> E. भञ्ज to break, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जनक|भंजनक|भंजनकः|भञ्जनकः
भञ्जनक m. (-कः) A disease of the mouth, contortion of the lips, and<BR>decay of the teeth.<BR> E. भञ्जन, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जरु|भंजरु|भंजरुः|भञ्जरुः
भञ्जरु m. (-रुः) A tree growing near a temple.<BR> E. भञ्ज to break, उरु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्
भट् r. 1st. cl. (भटति)<BR>	 1. To hold or cherish.<BR>	 2. To hire or maintain.<BR>	 3.<BR>To speak. (इ) भटि r. 10th cl. (भंटयति) To deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट|भटः
भट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A mercenary.<BR>	 2. A warrior, a soldier, a combatant.<BR>3. A barbarian, or outcaste of a particular tribe.<BR>	 4. A goblin. E.<BR>भट् to maintain, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भटित्र|भटित्रं
भटित्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Rosted on a spit, (meat, &c.)<BR> E. भट to nourish, इत्र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्ट|भट्टः
भट्ट m. (-ट्टः)<BR>	 1. A philosopher, a learned man, especially one conver-<BR>sant with the philosophical systems.<BR>	 2. An enemy.<BR>	 3. Best excell-<BR>ent.<BR>	 4. Authority.<BR>	 5. A bard in general.<BR> E. भट-तन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टार|भट्टारः
भट्टार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Worshipful, reverend, entitled to homage or res-<BR>pect: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारक|भट्टारकः
भट्टारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Venerable, respectable, entitled to reverence<BR>or to homage.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः)<BR>	 1. A sage, a Muni or saint.<BR>	 2. A deity.<BR>	 3.<BR>(In theatrical language,) A king.<BR>	 4. The sun.<BR>	 5. A term especially<BR>applied to a Bauddha teacher.<BR> E. भट to nourish, aff. क्विप्, तृ to<BR>pass, aff. खुल् and त changed to ट; otherwise with टल् to be con-<BR>fused, the same aff., and ल changed to ष; a cherisher and punisher,<BR>a distributor of rewards and punishments; again, भट्ट said here to<BR>mean, authority ऋ to go to or obtain, अण् aff. कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारकवार|भट्टारकवारः
भट्टारकवार n. (-रं) Sunday<BR> E. भट्टारक and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टिनी
भट्टिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A queen, not crowned.<BR>	 2. The wife of a Brāhman.<BR>In plays the word is often used by maids-in-waiting in addressing<BR>a queen or princess.<BR> E. भट्ट authority: see etymology of the last<BR>word, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भड्
भड् (इ) भडि r. 1st cl. (भण्डते)<BR>	 1. To rally. to deride or treat with merri-<BR>ment.<BR>	 2. To jest, to joke.<BR>	 3. To speak.<BR>	 4. To upbraid, to reprove.<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (भण्डते भण्डयति-ते) To do an auspicious act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भडिल|भडिलः
भडिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A servant.<BR>	 2. A hero.<BR> E. भड् a Sautra root, to be<BR>happy, Unādi aff. इलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्
भण् r. 1st cl. (भणति) To sound, to utter articulate sound, to speak or<BR>say. With प्रति, to reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भणित|भणितं
भणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounded, spoken, uttered.<BR> E. भण to speak, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भणिति|भणितिः
भणिति f. (-तिः) Speech, speaking.<BR> E. भण् to speak, aff. क्तिन्, with the<BR>augment इट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्टाकी
भण्टाकी f. (-की) The egg plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR> E. भट् to<BR>nourish, aff. आक, and नुम् augment. “वेगुण” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्ड|भंड|भंडः|भण्डः
भण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A mime, a jester, a buffoon, an actor.<BR> E. भडि to deride, &c. aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डक|भंडक|भंडकः|भण्डकः
भण्डक m. (-कः) A wagtail.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डन|भंडन|भंडनं|भण्डनं
भण्डन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Armour, mail.<BR>	 2. War, battle.<BR>	 3. Evil, wickedness,<BR>mischief.<BR> E. भडि to blame, &c., aff. ल्युट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डहासिनी|भंडहासिनी
भण्डहासिनी f. (-बी) A whore, a harlot.<BR> E. भण्ड a jester, and हासिनी who delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डि|भंडि|भंडिः|भण्डिः
भण्डि f. (-ण्डिः-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A plant, from the wood of which a red dye is<BR>prepared; Bengal māddār, (Rubia manjith, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A wave. E.<BR>भडि to be auspicious, &c. aff. इन्; also with कन् added भण्डिका; also<BR>भण्डिरी and भण्डीरी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डिर|भण्डिरः
भण्डिर m. (-रः) A tree, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR>	 f. (-री) Māddār. E. See भण्डिल भण्डीरी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डिल|भंडिल|भण्डिलः
भण्डिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. A messenger, one sent or dispatched.<BR>	 2.<BR>Fortunate, happy, prosperous, auspicious.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A mess-<BR>enger.<BR>	 2. An artizan.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR> E. भडि to be<BR>happy, &c., Unādi aff. इलच्; also र being substituted for ल,<BR>भण्डिर, or the short vowel being lengthened, भण्डील ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डीरी
भण्डीरी f. (-री) The Bengal māddār tree: see भण्डि.<BR> E. भडि to be ans-<BR>picious, ईरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डील|भण्डीलः
भण्डील m. (-लः) The Sirisha tree: see भण्डिल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भण्डूक|भण्डूकः
भण्डूक m. (-कः) A flower, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. भडि to be auspicious, ऊकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्
भद् (इ) भदि r. 1st and 10th cls. (भन्दति-ते भन्दयति)<BR>	 1. To do an auspici-<BR>ous act.<BR>	 2. To be happy, well prosperous, &c.<BR>	 3. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भदन्त|भदंत|भदंतः|भदन्तः
भदन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Reverend, venerable, worshipped or adored.<BR>2. Brilliant, splendid.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A Saugata, a Bauddha, a<BR>heterodox or sceptical philosopher.<BR>	 2. A devotee, an ascetic.<BR>भदि to be happy or pleased, to shine, Unādi aff. झच्, and the<BR>nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भदाक|भदाकः
भदाक mn. (-कः-कं) Prosperous, fortunate, auspicious.<BR> E. भदि to be<BR>happy, Unādi aff. आकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्र|भद्रं|भद्रः
भद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Happy, prosperous, lucky, propitious.<BR>	 2. Best,<BR>excellent.<BR>	 3. Pure, pious, virtuous.<BR>	 n. Subst. (-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Prosperity,<BR>fortune, happiness. (Adv.) Happy, well, right.<BR>	 n. (-द्रं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR>	 3. Iron or steel.<BR>	 nf. (-द्रं-द्री)<BR>One of the astrological periods called Karanas, the seventh; also<BR>called Vishti, regarded as an unlucky period.<BR>	 m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. A name<BR>of SĪVA 2. A wagtail.<BR>	 3. A bull.<BR>	 4. A heap, a multitude.<BR>	 5. A<BR>description of elephant, one of four classes into which they are<BR>divided.<BR>	 6. Mount Meru.<BR>	 7. One of the nine persons termed<BR>Suklabalas by the Jainas.<BR>	 8. A title of reverential address.<BR>9. A hypocrite.<BR>	 f. (-द्रा)<BR>	 1. The Ganges of heaven.<BR>	 2. The<BR>ichneumon plant: see राम्ना 3. Indigo.<BR>	 4. Asclepias pseudosarsa.<BR>5. A shrub, (Pœderia fœtida.)<BR>	 6. A medicinal plant, commonly<BR>Kayaphal.<BR>	 7. A name of the second, seventh, and twelfth days<BR>of the lunar fortnight.<BR>	 8. A female Saktī or deity of the Jainas.<BR>9. One of the four divisions of the Ganges, according to the<BR>Purānas, that which flows to the northern Kuru.<BR>	 10. A tree, (Gme-<BR>lina arborea.)<BR>	 11. A cow.<BR>	 12. Turmeric.<BR>	 13. Dear.<BR>	 14. Hypocritical.<BR>15. Head, chief.<BR>	 16. A term of respect used in addressing ladies.<BR>E. भदि to happy, Unādi aff. रन् and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रक|भद्रकं|भद्रकः
भद्रक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, pleasing agreeable.<BR>	 2. Respectable,<BR>worthy, estimable.<BR>	 3. Lucky, fortunate.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A sort of grass,<BR>(Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR>	 m. (-कः) A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadāru.) E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकाली
भद्रकाली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. One the forms of the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A fragrant<BR>grass, (Cyperus pertenuis or rotundus.)<BR> E. भद्र SĪVA, कल् to ap-<BR>proximate, affs. घञ् and ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकुम्भ|भद्रकुंभ|भद्रकुम्भः
भद्रकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A golden jar filled with water from a holy place, or<BR>with the water of the Ganges and used especially at the consecra-<BR>tion of a king.<BR> E. भद्र auspicious and कुम्भ a water jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रगणित
भद्रगणित n. (-तं) The construction of magical diagrams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रगन्धिका
भद्रगन्धिका f. (-का) A creeping plant, (Asclepias pseudosarsa, the<BR>narrow-leaved variety.)<BR> E. भद्र auspicious and गन्ध smell, affs. कन्<BR>and टाप्; some copies read भद्रवल्लिका in place of this word. “मुस्तके”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रघट|भद्रघटः
भद्रघट m. (-टः) A vessel from which a lottery is drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रङ्कर|भद्रंकर|भद्रङ्करः
भद्रङ्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Auspicious, conferring happiness or prosperity. E.<BR>भद्र happy and कृ to make, aff. खश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रचूड|भद्रचूडः
भद्रचूड m. (-डः) A sort of Euphorbia, (E. tirucalli.)<BR> E. भद्र propitious<BR>and चूडा a crest. “लङ्कासिज्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रदारु
भद्रदारु m. (-रुः) A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadāru.)<BR> E. भद्र auspicious and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रदार्व्वादिक
भद्रदार्व्वादिक m. (-कः) A class of thirty-one medicinal plants and subs-<BR>tances.<BR> E. भद्रदारु the pine, आदि etcetera, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रनामन्
भद्रनामन् m. (-मा) The woodpecker.<BR> E. भद्र auspicious and नामन् a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रपदा
भद्रपदा f. (-दा) A name given to the 26th and 27th lunar asterisms:<BR>see भाद्रपदा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रपर्णा
भद्रपर्णा f. (-र्णा) A shrub, (Pœderia fœtida.)<BR> E. भद्र auspicious, पर्ण a leaf,<BR>and टाप् fem. aff. “गान्धाल” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रपर्णी
भद्रपर्णी f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>	 2. A shrub, (Pœderia<BR>fœtida.)<BR> E. भद्र lucky, पर्ण a leaf, and ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रपीट
भद्रपीट n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. A splendid seat, a throne.<BR>	 2. A king of winged-insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रबलन|भद्रबलनः
भद्रबलन m. (-नः) A name of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. भद्र conferring happiness<BR>and बल to be strong, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रब
भद्रब(व)ला f. (-ला) A shrub, (Pœderia fœtida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमल्लिका
भद्रमल्लिका f. (-का) A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis Madraspatanus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमुस्तक|भद्रमुस्तकः
भद्रमुस्तक m. (-कः) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus pertenuis.)<BR> E. भद्र lucky<BR>and मुस्तक Cyperus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमृग|भद्रमृगः
भद्रमृग m. (-गः) A particular kind of elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रयव|भद्रयवः
भद्रयव n. (-वं) The seed of the Echites or Wrightea antidysenterica. E.<BR>भद्र lucky, and यव seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्ररेणु|भद्ररेणुः
भद्ररेणु m. (-णुः) The elephant of INDRA.<BR> E. भद्र auspicious and रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रवती
भद्रवती f. (-ती) A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रवर्म्मन्|भद्रवर्मन्
भद्रवर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा) Double jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रबल्ली
भद्रबल्ली f. (-ल्ली)<BR>	 1. Arabian jasmine, (Jasminum zambac.)<BR>	 2. The large<BR>Bengal creeper, (Gærtnera, racemosa.)<BR> E. भद्र lucky, वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रश्रय|भद्रश्रयं
भद्रश्रय n. (-यं) Sandal.<BR> E. भद्र auspicious, श्रय for आश्रय asylum, place of<BR>growing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रश्री
भद्रश्री f. (-श्रीः) Sandal-wood.<BR> E. भद्र best, श्री excellence or beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रसोमा
भद्रसोमा f. (मा) A name of GANGĀ.<BR> E. भद्र SĪVA, स with or equal to, उमा<BR>the wife of ŚIVA; equally dear with UMĀ to that deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राकरण|भद्राकरणं
भद्राकरण n. (-णं) Shaving.<BR> E. भद्र auspicious, with डाट् aff., and कृ to do<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रात्मज|भद्रात्मजः
भद्रात्मज m. (-जः) A sword, a scimitar.<BR> E. भद्र iron, and आत्मज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रारक|भद्रारकः
भद्रारक m. (-कः) One of the eighteen minor Dwipas, or divisions of the<BR>world.<BR> E. भद्र prosperity, ऋ to go to, or attain, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रालपत्रिका
भद्रालपत्रिका f. (-का) A shrub, (Pœderia fœtida.)<BR> E. भद्र auspicious, अल्<BR>what is equal to, and पत्र a leaf, aff. कन् । “गान्धाल ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राली
भद्राली f. (-ली) A shrub, (Pœderia fœtida.)<BR> E. भद्रा the same plant, ला to<BR>go or be, affs. ड and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राश्व|भद्राश्वं|भद्राश्वः
भद्राश्व n. (-श्वं) One of the four Mahā Dwipas, into which the known<BR>world is divided, according to some systems; or according to<BR>another system, one of the nine Khandas, or smaller divisions<BR>of the continent; in either case it is the east division.<BR>	 m. (-श्वः)<BR>One of the nine sons of AGNIDHRA, whom the division of the earth<BR>called Bhadrāswa was assigned and from whom it was so named. E.<BR>भद्र auspicious, अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राश्रय|भद्राश्रयः
भद्राश्रय m. (-यः) Sandal-wood.<BR> E. भद्र auspicious and आश्रय abode, habitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भदासन
भदासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A throne.<BR>	 2. A peculiar posture, in which abstract<BR>meditation is performed by the devotee; the legs bent and crossed<BR>underneath, and turned so as to bring the ancles in contact with<BR>the perineum, whilst the soles of the feet are held close to the<BR>sides.<BR> E. भद्र auspicious or beautiful and आसन a seat or sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रिका
भद्रिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An amulet.<BR>	 2. Name of the second, seventh and<BR>twenty days of a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रोदनी
भद्रोदनी f. (-नी) A plant, (Sida cordifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दिल|भंदिल|भंदिलं|भन्दिलं
भन्दिल n. (-लं) Good, happiness, welfare, prosperity.<BR>	 2. Tremulous mo-<BR>tion.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A messenger.<BR> E. भदि to be auspicious, Unādi aff.<BR>इलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भपति|भपतिः
भपति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. भ a star, and पति chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भ|भंभ|भंभः|भम्भः
भम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Smoke.<BR>	 2. A fly.<BR> E. भम् imitative sound, भा to emit<BR>sound, to shine, &c. and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भरालिका|भंभरालिका
भम्भरालिका f. (-का) A gnat, a musquito.<BR> E. भम्भराली a fly and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भराली|भंभराली
भम्भराली f. (-ली) A fly, especially of a large sort.<BR> E. भम् imitative sound,<BR>repeated, रा to make, and लच् aff.; making a buzzing noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भम्भासार|भम्भासारः
भम्भासार m. (-रः) A sovereign of Magadha; also SRENIKA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भय|भयं|भयः
भय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Frightful, fearful, horrible, dreadful.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Fear, alarm, fright, dread.<BR>	 2. The flower of the Trapa bispinosa.<BR>m. (-यः) Sickness.<BR> E. भी to be afraid, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयकारक
भयकारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Terrifying, frightening.<BR> E. भय and कारक what<BR>causes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयङ्कर|भयंकर|भयङ्करं|भयंकरः
भयङ्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Fearful, formidable, frightful.<BR> E. भय fear, कृ to<BR>make, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयद
भयद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Fearful, terrifying.<BR> E. भय and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयदर्शिन्
भयदर्शिन् mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि) Fearful, frightful.<BR> E. भय, दर्शिन् appearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयदाय
भयदाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Terrific.<BR> E. भय and दाय what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयद्रुत|भयद्रुतः
भयद्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Routed, put to flight.<BR> E. भय fear, द्रुत flown, fled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयप्रतीकार|भयप्रतीकारः
भयप्रतीकार m. (-रः) Removal of fear.<BR> E. भय and प्रतीकार counteraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भतप्रद
भतप्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Causing or inspiring fear.<BR> E. भय and प्रद who or<BR>what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयप्रस्ताव|भयप्रस्तावः
भयप्रस्ताव m. (-वः) Season or occasion of alarm.<BR> E. भय, and प्रस्ताव occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयभ्रष्ट|भयभ्रष्टः
भयभ्रष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Put to flight.<BR> E. भय fear, भ्रष्ट fallen, gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयविधायिन्
भयविधायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Alarming, fearful.<BR> E. भय, and विधायिन्<BR>causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयविप्लुत
भयविप्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Panic-struc.<BR> E. भय and विप्लुत immersed in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयसंहृष्टरोमन्
भयसंहृष्टरोमन् mfn. (-मा-मा-मं) Horrified.<BR> E. भय, संहृष्टरोमन् having the<BR>hair erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयस्थान
भयस्थान n. (-नं) Seat or part exposed to peril or hurt.<BR> E. भय, and स्थान<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयहेतु|भयहेतुः
भयहेतु n. (-तुं) Cause of alarm.<BR> E. भय and हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयातुर
भयातुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Afraid.<BR> E. भय and आतुर affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयार्त्त|भयार्त
भयार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Frightened, afraid.<BR> E. भय and आर्त्त afficted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयानक|भयानकः
भयानक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Frightful, formidable, terrific.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Terror.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. RĀHU or the personified ascending node.<BR>	 2. A tiger.<BR>3. One of the nine sentiments in poetry, or the sentiment of terror,<BR>as excited by poetical or dramatic composition.<BR> E. भी to fear,<BR>आनक Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयापह|भयापहः
भयापह m. (-हः) A king, a sovereign.<BR> E. भय fear, अप् before, हा to quit,<BR>to oppose or remove from, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयावह|भयावहः
भयावह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Formidable, fearful.<BR> E. भय fear, वह् to bear, aff.<BR>अच् and आङ् prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयैकप्रवण
भयैकप्रवण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Engrossed by fear.<BR> E. भय, एक alone, प्रवण bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयोत्तर
भयोत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Attended with or succeeded by fear.<BR> E. भय and<BR>उत्तर subsequent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयोपशम
भयोपशम m. (-मः) Encouraging, allaying fear.<BR> E. भय and उपशम tranquillising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर|भरः
भर Adv.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Much, excessive. Noun.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A measure of<BR>weight, two thousand Palas.<BR>	 mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं) Who or what<BR>cherishes, upholds, supports, &c.<BR> E. भृ to cherish, अप् aff.; or<BR>with घञ् aff. भार, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरट|भरटः
भरट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A potter.<BR>	 2. A servant.<BR> E. भृ to cherish, Unādi aff. अटन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण|भरणं|भरणः
भरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Cherishing, maintaining, nourishing, supporting.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wages, hire.<BR>	 3. The constellation Bharaṇī.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The name of<BR>the second lunar asterism, containing three stars, (Musca,) and<BR>figured by the pudendum muliebre.<BR>	 2. A creeper, commonly Gho-<BR>shā.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरणीभू
भरणीभू m. (-भूः) The personified ascending node or Rāhu.<BR> E. भरणी the<BR>asterism personified as a nymph and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरणीय|भरणीयः
भरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fit or proper to be cherished or maintained,<BR>a dependent.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्ड|भरंड|भरंडः|भरण्डः
भरण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A master, an owner, a lord, a husband.<BR>	 2. A sover-<BR>eign, a king.<BR>	 3. A bull.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, Unādi aff. अण्डन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्य|भरण्यं
भरण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) To be cherished or protected.<BR>	 n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Wages,<BR>hire.<BR>	 2. Cherishing, maintaining.<BR>	 3. The asterism Bharaṇī.<BR>	 f. (-ण्या)<BR>A woman.<BR> E. भरण maintaining and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्यभुज्
भरण्यभुज् mfn. (-भुक्) A labourer, a hireling, one who works for hire. E.<BR>भरण्य wages or hire, भुज् to eat, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्याह्वा
भरण्याह्वा f. (-ह्वा) A plant, commonly Rāmadūti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ|भं|भः
भ (भु) रण्यु m. (-ण्युः)<BR>	 1. A master, a protector.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR>4. The fire.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, अन्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरत्|भरन्त्
भरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Upholding, supporting, having, cherishing. E.<BR>भृ to cherish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरत|भरतः
भरत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The younger brother of RĀMA.<BR>	 2. The son of DUSH-<BR>YANTA by SAKUNTALĀ.<BR>	 3. The name of a sage or Muni.<BR>	 4. The<BR>name of a celebrated writer on dramatic composition, of which he<BR>is also sometimes considered as the inventor; the term is also ap-<BR>plied to his work, which appears to have been a body of Sūtras,<BR>or rules relating to every branch of theatrical writing and exhi-<BR>bition; it is said to be lost, but is constantly quoted by the com-<BR>mentators on the Nātakas or Indian dramas.<BR>	 5. An actor, a<BR>dancer, a mime.<BR>	 6. A barbarian, a mountaineer, a savage.<BR>	 7. A<BR>weaver.<BR>	 8. A descendant of BHARATA.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, अतच्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरत्रपुत्त्रक
भरत्रपुत्त्रक m. (-कः) An actor, a mime.<BR> E. भरत the dramatic author, पुत्त्र a<BR>son and कन् aff. of comparision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतप्रसू
भरतप्रसू f. (-सूः) A name of KAIKEYĪ, wife of DASARATHA and mother<BR>of BHARATA.<BR> E. भरत as above and प्रसू parent; hence equally appli-<BR>cable to SAKUNTALĀ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतवर्ष|भरतवर्षः
भरतवर्ष n. (-र्षं) India.<BR> E. भरत the son of DUSHYANTA and वर्ष region; he<BR>is supposed to have been the first emperor or monarch of all<BR>India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरताग्रज|भरताग्रजः
भरताग्रज m. (-जः) A name of RĀMA.<BR> E. भरत and अग्रज elder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरथ|भरथः
भरथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A sovereign, a king.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. A deity presiding over<BR>one of the regions of the world.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, aff. अथ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरद्वाज|भरद्वाजः
भरद्वाज m. (जः)<BR>	 1. A sky lark.<BR>	 2. The name of a Muni.<BR>	 3. The son of<BR>VRIHASPATĪ.<BR> E. भरत् upholding and वाज a wing: also भारद्वाज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरद्वाजक|भरद्वाजकः
भरद्वाजक m. (-कः) A lark.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरित|भरितः
भरित mfn. (-तः-ता or -ती-तं)<BR>	 1. Green, of a green colour.<BR>	 2. Nourished.<BR>3. Filled.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, Unādi aff. इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरिमन्
भरिमन् m. (-मा) Nourishing, cherishing.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, aff. इमनिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरु|भरुः
भरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. Gold.<BR>	 4. A<BR>husband, a lord.<BR>	 5. The sea.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, Unādi aff. उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुज|भरुजः
भरुज m. (-जः) A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुटक|भरुटकं
भरुटक n. (-कं) Fried-meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरे
भरे Ind. War.<BR> E. भृ-उट-कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ग|भर्गः
भर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR>	 3. A name BRAHMĀ.<BR>4. Cooking, frying.<BR> E. भ्रस्ज् to fry, aff. ल्युट्; having scorched<BR>KĀMADEVA to ashes, with a look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ज्जन|भर्जन|भर्जनं
भर्ज्जन f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Frying.<BR>	 2. Annihilating.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The act of frying<BR>or roasting.<BR>	 2. A frying-pan.<BR> E. भ्रस्ज् to fry, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तव्य|भर्तव्य|भर्त्तव्यं
भर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be cherished or maintained.<BR> E. भृ to nourish,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृ|भर्तृ
भर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-त्त्री-र्त्तृ)<BR>	 1. A cherisher, a nourisher, a protector.<BR>	 2. A<BR>holder, a supporter.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>	 1. A husband.<BR>	 2. A lord, a master. E.<BR>भृ to nourish, &c. aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृघ्नी|भर्तृघ्नी
भर्त्तृघ्नी f. (-घ्नी) The murderess of her husband.<BR> E. भर्त्तृ, a husband, हन् to<BR>kill, aff. ङीष् and घ्न substituted for the radical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृता|भर्तृता
भर्त्तृता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Masterhood.<BR>	 2. Husbandship.<BR> E. तल् added to the<BR>last; also with त्व, भर्त्तृत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृताङ्गत|भर्तृताङ्गत
भर्त्तृताङ्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Subject, married.<BR> E. भर्त्तृतां 2nd case, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृदारक|भर्तृदारक|भर्तृदारकः|भर्त्तृदारकः
भर्त्तृदारक m. (-कः) A young prince, designated as successor, and<BR>associated to the empire, (in theatrical language.)<BR>	 f. (-रिका) (in<BR>theatrical language.) A princess.<BR> E. भर्त्तृ the master or monarch,<BR>and दारक the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्तृहरि|भर्तृहरि|भर्तृहरिः|भर्त्तृहरिः
भर्त्तृहरि m. (-रिः) The brother of VIKRAMĀDITYA, prince and poet.<BR>E. भर्त्तृ a prince and हरि VIṢṆU, a deity amongst kings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्रिम
भर्त्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Maintained, nourished, supported.<BR> E. भृ to<BR>nourish, क्ति aff. and मप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्स
भर्त्स r. 10th cl. (भर्त्सयति-ते) To reprove, to reproach, to abuse or menace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सन|भर्त्सनं
भर्त्सन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Threat, menace.<BR>	 2. Reproach, abuse, cursing, re-<BR>viling.<BR> E. भर्त्स् to abuse, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्भ
भर्भ r. 1st cl. (भर्भति) To injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्म्म|भर्म|भर्मं|भर्म्मं
भर्म्म n. (-र्म्मं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Hire, wages.<BR>	 3. The navel.<BR>	 4. A particular<BR>coin.<BR>	 5. Dhūturā.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, Unādi aff. मन्, whence it is<BR>properly भर्म्मन्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्म्मण्या|भर्मण्या
भर्म्मण्या f. (-ण्या) Wages, hire.<BR> E. भर्म्मन् hire, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्म्मन्|भर्मन्
भर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Wages, hire.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR>	 3. The navel.<BR>	 4. A coin, a<BR>piece of money.<BR>	 5. Support, maintenance.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, Unādi<BR>aff. मन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्व|भर्व्व
भर्व r. 1st cl. (भर्वति) To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्
भल् r. 1st and 10th cls. (भलते भालयते)<BR>	 1. To describe, to expound, to<BR>explain.<BR>	 2. To see. r. 1st cl.<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure.<BR>	 2. To give. r.<BR>10th cl. To throw up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भलता
भलता f. (-ता) A shrub, (Pœderia fœtida.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ल्
भल्ल् r. 1st cl. (भल्लते)<BR>	 1. To tell, to describe.<BR>	 2. To hurt, to injure, to<BR>wound or kill.<BR>	 3. To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ल|भल्लं|भल्लः
भल्ल m. (-ल्लः)<BR>	 1. A bear.<BR>	 2. An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR>	 mn. (-ल्लः-ल्लं) A kind of<BR>arrow.<BR>	 f. (-ल्ली)<BR>	 1. An arrow, with a crescent-shaped head.<BR>	 2. The<BR>marking-nut plant; also भल्लातकी.<BR> E. भल्ल् to hurt or kill, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लक|भल्लकः
भल्लक m. (-कः) A bear.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लपुच्छी
भल्लपुच्छी f. (-च्छी) A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR> E. भल्ल a bear,<BR>पुच्छ a tail; to which the flower is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लात|भल्लातः
भल्लात m. (-तः) Marking-nut plant. E. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लातक|भल्लातकः
भल्लातक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) The marking-nut plant, (Semicarpus anacardi-<BR>um.)<BR> E. भल्ल an arrow, अत् to resemble, aff. घञ् with कन् added;<BR>wounding like a weapon; also भल्लात, भल्ली, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लिका
भल्लिका f. (-का) Marking-nut.<BR> E. कन् added to भल्ली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लुक|भल्लुकः
भल्लुक m. (-कः) A bear.<BR> E. भल्ल् to hurt, aff. उक; also भल्लूक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लूक|भल्लूकः
भल्लूक m. (-कः) A bear.<BR> E. भल्ल् to injure, Unādi aff. ऊक; also भाल्लुक<BR>and भल्लुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव|भवं|भवः
भव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Being, existing, the self-support of something already<BR>produced.<BR>	 2. Birth.<BR>	 3. Origin, production.<BR>	 4. The place or means<BR>of being.<BR>	 5. The state of being.<BR>	 6. The being or becoming poss-<BR>essed of any thing, as family, cattle, &c.<BR>	 7. Welfare, prosperity.<BR>8. Obtaining, acquisition.<BR>	 9. Excellence, superiority.<BR>	 10. The<BR>world.<BR>	 11. A deity, a god.<BR>	 12. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 13. The world.<BR>14. Life.<BR>	 n. (-व) A fruit, the fruit of the Dillenia speciosa.<BR> E. भू<BR>to be, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवघस्मर|भवघस्मरः
भवघस्मर m. (-रः) A forest-conflagration.<BR> E. भव being, घस्मर voracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवत्|भवन्त्
भवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Thou; but used as a respectful term of ad-<BR>dress, as Sir or Lord, and governing the verb in the third person.<BR>E. भा to shine, डवतुप् Unādi aff.<BR>	 mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Present.<BR>	 2.<BR>Being, existing.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती) A poisoned arrow.<BR> E. भू to be, participial<BR>aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवदीय|भवदीयं
भवदीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Yours, your honour's.<BR> E. भवत् as above and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवद्भी
भवद्भी mfn. (-द्भी-द्भिः-द्भि) Afraid.<BR> E. भवत् being and भी fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन|भवनं|भवनः
भवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 2. A nature, a quality.<BR>	 3. The<BR>place of abiding or being, scite, field, spot, &c.<BR>	 4. Production. E.<BR>मू to be, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनाशिनी
भवनाशिनी f. (-नी) Sarayu the river, which runs from the Himālaya<BR>chain and falls into the Goggrah with which it is then confound-<BR>ed.<BR> E. भव being and नाशिनी destructress, giving eternal happiness,<BR>being a sacred stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनीय|भवनीयं
भवनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be or become, what is or ought to be.<BR> E. भू<BR>to be, अनीयर् aff. of the gerund.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनोदर
भवनोदर n. (-रं) The interior apartments.<BR> E. भवन and उदर belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्त|भवंत|भवंतः|भवन्तः
भवन्त m. (-न्तः) Time in general, or time present.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती) A virtuous<BR>wife.<BR> E. भू to be, Unādi aff. झच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्ति|भवंति|भवंतिः|भवन्तिः
भवन्ति m. (-न्तिः) Time being, the present.<BR> E. भू to be, Unādi aff. झिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभाज्
भवभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Living, sharing the world<BR> E. भव, and भाज who<BR>possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभूति|भवभूतिः
भवभूति m. (-तिः) The author of MĀLATI MĀDHAVA and other dramas.<BR>E. भव the world, भूति increase, in wisdom, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवरुद्
भवरुद् f. (-रुद्-रुत्) A drum played at funerals.<BR> E. भव being, रुद् to<BR>weep or wail, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भववीति|भववीतिः
भववीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Liberation from the world, cessation from worldly<BR>acts.<BR>	 2. End of the world.<BR> E. भव and वीति passing away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवात्मजा
भवात्मजा f. (-जा) The goddess MANASĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवादृश्
भवादृश् mfn. (-दृक) Like you, your like.<BR> E. भवत् you, दृश् to show, aff.<BR>क्विप्; also भवादृश, and भवादृक्ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवानी
भवानी f. (-नी) The goddess PĀRVATĪ or DURGĀ, in her pacific and<BR>amiable form.<BR> E. भव ŚIVA. fem. aff. ङीप्, and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवानीगुरु|भवानीगुरुः
भवानीगुरु m. (-रुः) The personified Himālaya mountain.<BR> E. भवानी the<BR>goddess, and गुरु here put for father; DURGĀ in this form being<BR>the daughter of the mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवाभाव
भवाभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Nonexistence of the world.<BR>	 2. A sage, one unaffec-<BR>ted by worldly infirmities.<BR> E. भब, and अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवाभिभाविन्
भवाभिभाविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Superior to or overcoming the world.<BR>E. भव and अभिभाविन् disgracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवायना
भवायना f. (-ना) The Ganges.<BR> E. भव the world, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविक|भविकं
भविक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Prosperous, happy, welfaring.<BR>	 2. Beneficial.<BR>n. (-कं) Prosperity, welfare.<BR> E. भव being, (for well-being,) and<BR>ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवित|भवितः
भवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Been, become.<BR> E. भव being, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितव्य|भवितव्यं
भवितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be or become, what is to be.<BR> E. भू to be,<BR>तव्य aff. of the gerund.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितव्यता
भवितव्यता f. (-ता) Fate, destiny.<BR> E. भवितव्य what is to be, तल् abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितृ
भवितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Actually being, or disposed to be.<BR>	 2. Well-be-<BR>ing, wel-faring.<BR> E. भू to be, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविन्
भविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Living, being, having life and sensation.<BR> E. भव being, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविन|भविनः
भविन m. (-नः) A poet, a versifier.<BR> E. भू to think, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविल|भविलः
भविल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Being, existing, what is or exists.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>catamite.<BR>	 2. A sensualist.<BR> E. भू to be, इलच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्णु|भविष्णुः
भविष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Actually being or disposed to be.<BR>	 2. Being<BR>well, existing happily, virtuously, &c.<BR> E. भू to be, इष्णुच् parti-<BR>cipial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्य|भविष्यः
भविष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Future, what will be. E. See भविष्यत्, the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यत्|भविष्यन्त्
भविष्यत् mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्) What is to be, what will be, future.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-ष्यत्) The future.<BR> E. भू to be, शतृ participial aff., स्य augment, इट्<BR>inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव्य|भव्यं|भव्यः
भव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Happy, auspicious, prosperous.<BR>	 2. Well,<BR>proper, fit, right.<BR>	 3. True.<BR>	 4. To be or become, what is to be.<BR>5. A being, what is or exists.<BR>	 m. (-व्यः) The Kāmaranga, a small<BR>fruit tree, (Averhoa carambola.)<BR>	 f. (-व्या)<BR>	 1. A name of UMĀ.<BR>	 2. A<BR>large sort of pepper.<BR>	 3. Existing.<BR>	 4. Beautiful.<BR>	 5. Happy.<BR>	 6.<BR>Calm.<BR>	 n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. A bone.<BR>	 2. Fruit, result.<BR>	 3. Being, existence.<BR>	 4.<BR>Welfare.<BR>	 mn. (-व्यः-व्यं) One division of the poetical Rasas or<BR>sentiments.<BR> E. भू to be, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भशिरा
भशिरा f. (-रा) A sort of beet, (Beta Bengalensis)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भष्
भष् r. 1st cl. (भषति)<BR>	 1. To bark or growl.<BR>	 2. To reproach, to speak<BR>malevolently, to rail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भष|भषः
भष m. (-षः) A dog.<BR>	 f. (-षी) A bitch.<BR> E. भष् to bark, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषक|भषकः
भषक m. (-कः) A dog.<BR> E. भष् to bark, क्कुन् aff.; it is sometimes written.<BR>भसक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषण|भषणं|भषणः
भषण m. (-णः) A dog.<BR>	 n. (-णं) The barking of a dog.<BR> E. भष् to bark, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भषत्
भषत् n. (-त्)<BR>	 1. The heart.<BR>	 2. Wood.<BR>	 3. The thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्
भस् r. 3d cl. (वभति)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To blame or abuse; this root is<BR>usually restricted to the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसद
भसद f. (-सद्)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Pudendum muliebre.<BR>	 3. The mons veneris.<BR>4. Time.<BR>	 5. A sort of duck.<BR>	 6. A float, a raft.<BR>	 7. Flesh.<BR>	 n. (-सत्)<BR>The hinder parts.<BR> E. भस् to shine, अदि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसन|भसनः
भसन m. (-नः) A large bee.<BR> E. भस् to sound, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसन्त|भसंत|भसंतः|भसन्तः
भसन्त m. (-न्तः) Time.<BR> E. भस् to shine, aff. झच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसित|भसितं
भसित n. (-तं) Ashes.<BR> E. भस् to shine, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसूचक|भसूचकः
भसूचक m. (-कः) An astronomer or astrologer.<BR> E. भ a star, मूचक an intelligencer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रका
भस्त्रका f. (-का) A bellows.<BR> E. कन् added to भस्त्रा; also भस्त्रिका and भस्त्रका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रा
भस्त्रा f. (-स्त्रा) A bellows, a large hide with valves and a clay nozzle,<BR>which is used for this purpose.<BR> E. भस् to shine, त्रन् Unādi aff.,<BR>fem. aff. टाप्; also with ङीष् aff. भस्त्री and with कन् in the fem.<BR>form being added भस्त्रका or भस्त्रिका optionally; and with the<BR>feminine termination retained also, भस्त्राका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्राका
भस्त्राका f. (का) A bellows: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्राफला
भस्त्राफला f. (-ला) क्षुपभेदे “टेपारि” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्रिक
भस्त्रिक mf. (-कः-की) A bellows-blower, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) An inflated skin on<BR>which rafts, &c. are floated.<BR>	 f. (-का) A bellows: see भस्त्र.<BR> E. भस्त्रन् a<BR>bellows, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्त्री
भस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) A bellows: see भस्त्रा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मक|भस्मकं
भस्मक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A disease of the eyes, thickening of the membranes,<BR>and indistinctness of vision.<BR>	 2. Morbid appetite from over-diges-<BR>tion, constant craving for food with general decay.<BR>	 3. An an-<BR>thelmintic plant, commonly Biranga.<BR>	 4. Gold or silver.<BR> E. भस्मन्<BR>ashes, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मकार|भस्मकारः
भस्मकार m. (-रः) A washerman.<BR> E. भस्मन् ashes, and कार agent; using<BR>the ashes of wood in place of soap or ley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मगन्धिका|भस्मगंधिका
भस्मगन्धिका f. (-का) A perfume, commonly Reṇukā.<BR> E. भस्मन् ashes, and<BR>गन्ध smell, aff. कन्, and टाप्; also भस्मगन्धिनी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मगर्भा
भस्मगर्भा f. (-र्भा)<BR>	 1. The Sisu tree, or a variety of it, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>2. A sort of perfume, commonly Reṇukā.<BR> E. भस्प्र ashes, and गर्भ<BR>place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मतूल|भस्मतूलं
भस्मतूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A number of villages.<BR>	 2. A shower of dust.<BR>	 3. Frost<BR>or snow.<BR> E. भस्म ashes, तूल् to weigh, and aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मन्
भस्मन् n. (-स्म)<BR>	 1. Ashes.<BR>	 2. Holy ashes.<BR> E. भस् to shine, Unādi aff. मनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मवेधक|भस्मवेधकः
भस्मवेधक m. (-कः) Camphor.<BR> E. भस्मन् ashes, and वेधक distresser;<BR>whiter than ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मसात्
भस्मसात् Ind. To the state of ashes, to ashes, as स भस्मसाच्चकारारीन् He<BR>reduced the enemies to ashes.<BR> E. भस्मन्, and साति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्माह्वय|भस्माह्वयः
भस्माह्वय m. (-यः) Camphor.<BR> E. भस्मन् ashes, आह्वय a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मीकरण|भस्मीकरणं
भस्मीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Reducing to ashes.<BR>	 2. Calcining.<BR> E. भस्म, and करण<BR>doing, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मीकृत
भस्मीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Reduced to ashes.<BR>	 2. Calcined, (as a metal.)<BR>E. भस्म, and कृत made, with च्वि aug.; also भस्मकृत and भस्मसात्कृत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भस्मीभूत
भस्मीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Reduced to ashes.<BR>	 2. Being mere ashes, i. E.<BR>being wholly worthless.<BR> E. भष्मन्, and भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भा
भा r. 2nd cl. (-भाति)<BR>	 1. To shine, to be luminous, splendid or beauti-<BR>ful.<BR>	 2. To be pleased.<BR>	 3. To be angry.<BR>	 4. To below.<BR>	 5. To be, to<BR>exist. With आङ् To flash. With प्र or वि To shine brightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भा
भा f. (भा)<BR>	 1. Light.<BR>	 2. Beauty.<BR>	 3. The shadow of a gnomon.<BR>	 m. (-भाः)<BR>The sun.<BR> E. भा to shine, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाकूट|भाकूटः
भाकूट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A mountain, apparently the part of the Himālaya,<BR>called Bhākur.<BR>	 2. A sort of fish. “भेट्की”.<BR> E. भा light, कूट a peak<BR>or quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाकोष|भाकोषः
भाकोष m. (-षः) The sun.<BR> E. भा light, कोष receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाक्त|भाक्तं
भाक्त m. (-क्तः)<BR>	 1. A follower, a dependent, one to whom food is regu-<BR>larly given.<BR>	 2. Grain, edible grain, as rice, &c.<BR>	 f. (-क्ती)<BR>	 1. Fit for<BR>food.<BR>	 2. Inferior, secondary.<BR>	 3. Confined to any science, (as a<BR>term).<BR>	 4. Dependant.<BR> E. भक्त food, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाक्तिक|भाक्तिकः
भाक्तिक m. (-कः) One who is fed by another, a dependent, a retainer.<BR> E. भक्त. food, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाक्ष
भाक्ष f. (-क्षी) Gluttonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग|भागः
भाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A portion, a share, a part.<BR>	 2. Fate, fortune, luck.<BR>	 3.<BR>A half-rupee.<BR>	 4. Part of any thing given as interest.<BR>	 5. A division<BR>of time, the thirtieth part of a Rasi or zodiacal sign.<BR>	 6. A degree,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">Page528-a+ 60</a>]<BR>the 360th part of the circumference of a great circle.<BR>	 7. A frac-<BR>tion.<BR>	 8. The quotient, (in math.)<BR>	 9. Place, spot.<BR>	 10. Room.<BR> E. भज्<BR>to share, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागक|भागकः
भागक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what divides.<BR>	 m. (-कः) (In arithmetic.),<BR>A divisor.<BR> E. भज्, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागजाति|भागजातिः
भागजाति f. (-तिः) Assimilation of fractions.<BR> E. भाग, and जाति species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागण|भागणः
भागण m. (-णः) The whole collection of stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागर्धय
भागर्धय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. An heir, a co-heir.<BR>	 2. Royal revenue.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Fate,<BR>destiny, luck.<BR>	 2. Good-luck.<BR>	 3. Property.<BR> E. भाग and धेय to be<BR>taken, or धेय aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागन|भागनं
भागन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The period, during which the sun passess through the<BR>twelve signs of the zodiac, thence by ellipsis, the zodiac.<BR>	 2. The<BR>circumference of a great circle.<BR> E. भाग् to divide, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागलक्षणा
भागलक्षणा f. (-णा) The secondary use of a word in which part of the<BR>primary meaning is retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागवत|भागवतं|भागवतः
भागवत f. (-ती) Adj.<BR>	 1. Relating to or worshipping of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>2. Holy, sacred.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A devotee of the said deity.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Name of one of the eighteen Purānas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागशस्
भागशस् Ind. According to a share or portion, in parts or portions. E.<BR>भाग and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागहर|भागहरः
भागहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Taking a part, sharing.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A co-heir.<BR>	 2.<BR>(In arithmetic,) Division.<BR> E. भाग and हर who or what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागार्थिन्
भागार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Desirous of a share.<BR> E. भाग and अर्थिन् who<BR>seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागानुबन्धजाति|भागानुबन्धजातिः
भागानुबन्धजाति f. (-तिः) Assimilation of fractional increase.<BR> E. भाग, अनुबन्ध<BR>accession, जाति kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागापवाहजाति|भागापवाहजातिः
भागापवाहजाति f. (-तिः) Assimilation of fractional decrease.<BR> E. भाग, अप-<BR>वाह taking away, जाति kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिक|भागिकं
भागिक mf. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Bearing interest, subject to a deduction for<BR>interest.<BR>	 2. Having a part.<BR>	 3. Relating to a part.<BR>	 4. Fractional. E.<BR>भाग a part and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिन्
भागिन् mfn. (गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>	 1. Who or what shares.<BR>	 2. Having parts, con-<BR>sisting of parts or shares.<BR>	 mf. (-गी-गिनी) A co-heir or co-heiress.<BR>E. भाग and घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागिनेय|भागिनेयः
भागिनेय m. (-यः) A sister's son.<BR> E. भगिनी a sister, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागीरथी
भागीरथी f. (-थी) The Ganges.<BR> E. भगीरथ a pious monarch, at whose in-<BR>tercesion the Ganges first descended from heaven, affs. अण्<BR>and ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भागरि
भागरि m. (-रिः) A celebrated grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाग्य|भाग्यं
भाग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>	 1. To be portioned or divided.<BR>	 2. Bearing<BR>interest, subject to a deduction of some part on that account.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-ग्यं) Destiny, fortune, good or ill-luck.<BR> E. भज् to divide, ण्यत् aff.;<BR>or भाग a part and यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्गक|भांगक|भांगकः|भाङ्गकः
भाङ्गक m. (-कः) A ragged cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाङ्गीन|भांगीन|भांगीनं|भाङ्गीनं
भाङ्गीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Bearing hemp, (a field, &c.)<BR> E. भङ्ग hemp and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज्
भाज् r. 10th cl. (भाजयति-ते) To divide, to separate; it is usually employ-<BR>ed with वि prefixed, especially in a legal sense, as to divide or<BR>portion an inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज्
भाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Who or what participates or possesses, used chiefly<BR>in composition, as धनभाज् rich, &c.<BR> E. भाज् to divide and क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजक्
भाजक् Ind. Swiftly, quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजक|भाजकः
भाजक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Dividing.<BR>	 2. A divisor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजन|भाजनं
भाजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Any vessel, as a pot or cup, a plate, &c.<BR>	 2. A clever,<BR>capable or fit person.<BR>	 3. Sharing, dividing.<BR>	 4. (In arithmetic,)<BR>Division.<BR>	 5. Representation.<BR>	 6. A measure equal to sixty-four<BR>Palas.<BR> E. भज् to serve or share, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजित|भाजितं
भाजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Divided, portioned.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A portion, a share.<BR>E. भाज् to divide, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाजी
भाजी f. (-जी) Rice, gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाज्य|भाज्यं
भाज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) Divisible, to be portioned or divided.<BR>	 n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">Page528-b+ 60</a>]<BR>(-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. A portion, a share, an inheritance.<BR>	 2. (In arithmetic.)<BR>The dividend.<BR> E. भाज् to divide, aff. यत्; or भज्-ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाटक|भाटकं|भाटकः
भाटक m. (-कः) Price, especially paid for the use of any thing or per-<BR>son; wages, hire.<BR> E. भट् to hire, or maintain, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाटि|भाटिः
भाटि f. (-टिः)<BR>	 1. Wages, hire, fee.<BR>	 2. The gettings of a prostitute. E.<BR>भट् to hire, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण|भाणः
भाण m. (-णः) A sort of dramatic entertainment, described as one, in<BR>which one only of the interlocutors appears on the scene; or as<BR>the narrative of some intrigue, told either by the hero or a third<BR>person.<BR> E. भण् to speak, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाणक|भाणकः
भाणक m. (-कः) A proclaimer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाणिका
भाणिका f. (-का) A comic drama in one act.<BR> E. भाण and कन् dimin. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्ड|भांड|भांडं|भाण्डं|भाण्डः
भाण्ड n. (-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Any vessel, a pot, a cup, a plate, &c.<BR>	 2. Any musi-<BR>cal instrument.<BR>	 3. Any implement or utensil.<BR>	 4. Capital, principal,<BR>5. An ornament in general.<BR>	 6. An ornament round a horse's neck<BR>and breast.<BR>	 7. The bed of a river, the space between its banks.<BR>	 8.<BR>Mimickry, buffoonery, the practice of the Bhānda or professional<BR>jester.<BR>	 9. A box, a case, &c.<BR>	 10. A tool.<BR>	 11. The stock of a shop-<BR>keeper, (hence any valued posses sion.)<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः) A tree, (Hibiscus<BR>propulneoides.)<BR>	 m. plu. Mercandise.<BR> E. भदि to be auspicious,<BR>aff. अच्; or भण् to sound, aff. ड, deriv. irr.; or भण्ड a jester and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डक|भांडक|भांडकं|भांडकः|भाण्डकः
भाण्डक m. (-कः) A cup, a plate, a vessel or utensil.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Goods, mer-<BR>chandize.<BR> E. भाण्ड and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डपुट|भांडपुट|भाण्डपुटः
भाण्डपुट m. (-टः) A barber.<BR> E. भाण्ड a vessel, पुट् to rub, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डपुष्प|भाण्डपुष्पः
भाण्डपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A sort of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डप्रतिभाण्डक|भांडप्रतिभांडक
भाण्डप्रतिभाण्डक m. (-कः) Rule of barter, (in arithmetic.)<BR> E. भाण्ड and<BR>प्रति for, again, भाण्डक goods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डभरक|भाण्डभरकः
भाण्डभरक m. (-कः) The contents of any vessel.<BR> E. भाण्ड, and भरक<BR>what fills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डवादन
भाण्डवादन n. (-नं) Playing on musical instruments.<BR> E. भाण्ड and वादन sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डागार|भांडागार|भाण्डागारः
भाण्डागार m. (-रः) A store-room, a place where household goods and<BR>utensils are kept.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A treasury.<BR> E. भाण्ड a vessel and आगार<BR>a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डार|भांडार|भांडारं
भाण्डार n. (-रं) A store-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डि|भांडि|भांडिः|भाण्डिः
भाण्डि f. (-ण्डिः) A razor-case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिक|भांडिक|भांडिकः|भाण्डिकः
भाण्डिक m. (-कः) A musician, one especially who is to waken the<BR>prince or chief in the morning by vocal or instrumental music. E.<BR>भाण्ड a vessel, (an instrument,) and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिन्
भाण्डिन् mfn. (-ण्डी-ण्डिनी-ण्डि) Having a vessel, utensil, &c.<BR> E. भाण्ड and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिवाह|भांडिवाह|भाण्डिवाहः
भाण्डिवाह m. (-हः) A barber.<BR> E. भाण्डि for भाण्ड having a basin and वाह<BR>who works or labours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डिल|भांडिल|भांडिलः|भाण्डिलः
भाण्डिल m. (-लः) A barber.<BR> E. भाण्ड a vessel and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाण्डीर|भांडीर|भांडीरः|भाण्डीरः
भाण्डीर m. (-रः) The Indian fig-tree.<BR> E. भाण्ड a vessel, ईर् to bring, aff. क;<BR>referable perhaps to the legend that describes the infant KṚṢṆA,<BR>taking his meals under a tree of this kind in the woods of Brin-<BR>dābana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भात्
भात् mfn. (-भान्-भान्ती or -भाती-भात्) Shining splendid.<BR> E. भा to shine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भात|भातं|भातः
भात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shone, bright, resplendent.<BR>	 m. (-तः) Morning,<BR>dawn.<BR> E. भा to shine, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाति|भातिः
भाति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Light, brightness.<BR>	 2. Perception, knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भातु|भातुः
भातु m. (-तुः) The sun.<BR> E. भा to shine, तुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्र|भाद्रः
भाद्र m. (-द्रः) The name of a month, (August-September,) when the<BR>moon is full near the wing of Pegasus.<BR> E. भद्र for भद्रपदा and अण्<BR>aff: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रपद|भाद्रपदः
भाद्रपद m. (-दः) The month Bhādra.<BR> E. भद्रपदा the asterism and अण् aff.<BR>f. (-दा) A name common to the twenty-sixth and twenty-seventh<BR>lunar asterisms, distinguished by the epithets prior and subsequent<BR>or पूर्व्व and उत्तरः see पूर्व्वभाद्रपदा, &c.<BR> E. भाद्र said to mean a cow, and<BR>पद foot, अण् added optionally; whence it it is often read भद्रपदा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रमातुर|भाद्रमातुरः
भाद्रमातुर m. (-रः) The son of a virtuous and loyal mother.<BR> E. भद्र aus-<BR>picious, मातृ a mother, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भान|भानं
भान n. (-नं) The act of growing visible.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR>	 3. Perception.<BR> E. भा, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानु|भानुः
भानु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Light.<BR>	 3. A ray of light.<BR>	 4. A master.<BR>	 5.<BR>A sovereign, a prince.<BR>	 6. The father of the fifteenth Jaina pontiff.<BR>7. Beauty.<BR>	 8. A day.<BR>	 9. An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-नुः) A handsome<BR>woman.<BR> E. भा to shine, Unādi aff. नु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुफला
भानुफला f. (-ला) The plantain, (Musa sapientum.)<BR> E. भानु the sun, फल<BR>the fruit; being offered in the worship of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुमत्|भानुमन्त्
भानुमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Luminous, splendid, resplendent.<BR>	 2.<BR>Beautiful, handsome.<BR>	 m. (-मान्) The sun.<BR> E. भानु light, मतुप्<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुवार|भानुवारः
भानुवार m. (-रः) Sunday.<BR> E. भानु the sun and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानेमि|भानेमिः
भानेमि m. (-मिः) The sun.<BR> E. भा light, नेमि circumference. “अर्कवृक्षेच ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाभ
भाभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Bright, (as a planet.)<BR> E. भ and आभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम्
भाम् r. 1st cl. (भामते) r. 10th cl. (भामयति) To be angry or wrathful, to<BR>be impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम|भामः
भाम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Passion, anger, wrath.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 4.<BR>A sister's husband.<BR>	 f. (-मा) A passionate woman.<BR> E. भा to shine,<BR>and मन् Unādi aff., or भाम् to be angry, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामक|भामकः
भामक m. (-कः) A sister's husband.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामिन्
भामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Angry, passionate.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A passionate wo-<BR>man.<BR> E. भाम passion, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार|भारः
भार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A weight of gold, equal to two thousand Palas.<BR>	 2. A<BR>yoke for carrying burden.<BR>	 3. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. A weight, a<BR>burthen.<BR>	 5. Excess.<BR>	 6. Labour, toil, trouble.<BR> E. भृ to nourish,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारत|भारतं|भारतः
भारत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Bhāratavarsha or India proper, so called from BHA-<BR>RATA, the son of DUSHYANTA, whose patrimony it was. (E. भरत the<BR>the prince and अण् aff.)<BR>	 2. The great sacred epic-poem of the Hin-<BR>dus. (E. भार weight, त aff., भारतः having been put by the Ṛṣis<BR>in a scale and weighed against the four Vedas which it was found<BR>to outweigh; thence its usual prefix of Mahā or great: a special<BR>grammatical rule, however, derived it from भरत the prince so<BR>named, because the war narrated in it occurred amongst his descen-<BR>dants.)<BR>	 m. (-तः) An actor, a mime.<BR>	 2. A name of fire.<BR>	 3. A descen-<BR>dant of BHARATA f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The goddess of speech.<BR>	 2. Speech.<BR>	 3. A<BR>quail.<BR>	 4. A branch of the dramatic art, dramatic recitation or de-<BR>clamation, the delivery of the dialogue that is composed in ela-<BR>borate Sanskrit stanzas.<BR> E. भरत the inventor of the Indian drama,<BR>aff. अण्; or the name of a sage, whose devotions brought the god-<BR>dess SARASWATĪ from heaven; or again, भॄ to nourish, aff. अतच्,<BR>fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारती
भारती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The goddess of speech.<BR>	 2. Speech, eloquence.<BR>	 3. A<BR>quail.<BR>	 4. A particular kind of style.<BR> E. भृ, अतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाज|भारद्वाजं|भारद्वाजः
भारद्वाज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A name of DROṆA, the military preceptor of the<BR>Kurus and Pāndus.<BR>	 2. One of the seven Ṛṣis.<BR>	 3. A name of the<BR>Muni AGASTYA.<BR>	 4. The son of VRIHASPATĪ.<BR>	 5. A sky-lark.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>A bone.<BR>	 f. (-जी) Wild-cotton.<BR> E. भरद्वाज a lark, and अण् pleonastic<BR>or derivative aff.; in the latter case it refers to a legend of the<BR>Ṛṣi BHARADWĀJA having been nursed by a lark, in consequence<BR>of being abandoned at his birth by his natural parents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारय|भारयः
भारय m. (-यः) A lark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारयष्टि|भारयष्टिः
भारयष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A pole or yoke for carrying burdens; a stick carried<BR>over the shoulder, with strings attached to either end of it, form-<BR>ing at their lower extremity a noose, in which the articles to be<BR>conveyed are suspended.<BR> E. भार a burthen and यष्टि a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारव|भारवं
भारव n. (-वं) A bow-string.<BR>	 f. (-वी) Holy-basil.<BR> E. भार a weight, बा to<BR>take. aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवत्|भारवन्त्
भारवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Loaded, burthened, bearing a burthen.<BR> E. भार and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाह|भारवाहः
भारवाह m. (-हः) A porter, a bearer of burthens.<BR> E. भार a burthen, वह्<BR>to bear, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाहन|भारवाहनः
भारवाहन m. (-नः) A beast of burthen, (as a camel, &c.)<BR>	 n. (-नं) A vehi-<BR>cle for burthens, a waggon.<BR> E. भार and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाहिक|भारवाहिकः
भारवाहिक mfn. (कः-की-कं) Carrying burthens.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A porter. E.<BR>भारवाह and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाहिन्
भारवाहिन् m. (-ही) A porter.<BR> E. भार and वाहिन् who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवि|भारविः
भारवि m. (-विः) The name of a poet, the author of the Kirātārjuniya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवृक्ष|भारवृक्षः
भारवृक्ष m. (-क्ष) A fragrant substance, commonly Kākshi, considered<BR>variously as a vegetable or mineral product.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारसह
भारसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Able to carry loads.<BR>	 2. Fit for the yoke. E.<BR>भार and सह what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारहर|भारहरः
भारहर m. (-रः) A porter.<BR> E. भार a burthen, and हर who takes, from हृ<BR>with ट aff.; also with अण् aff., भारहार and कन् added, भारहारक; or<BR>with घिनुण्, भारहारिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारहार|भारहारः
भारहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A porter.<BR>	 2. Carrying a load. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारहारिक
भारहारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bearing a load, relating or referring to it,<BR>&c.<BR> E. भारहार and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाराक्रान्त|भाराक्रांत
भाराक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Loaded, laden, bearing a burthen.<BR>	 f. (-न्ता) A<BR>species of the Atyshti metre.<BR> E. भार and आक्रान्त overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारि|भारिः
भारि m. (-रिः) A lion.<BR> E. भृ to threaten, aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिक|भारिकः
भारिक m. (-कः) A porter.<BR>	 f. (-का) Adj. Heavy.<BR> E. भार a burthen, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिन्
भारिन् m. (-री) A porter.<BR> E. भार a burthen and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारोद्धरण
भारोद्धरण n. (-णं) Taking up or bearing a burthen.<BR> E. भार and उद्धरण taking up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारोद्वहन
भारोद्वहन n. (-नं) Bearing a load.<BR> E. भार, and उद्वहन uplifting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गव|भार्गवः
भार्गव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A name of PARASURĀMA.<BR>	 2. A name of SUKRA re-<BR>gent of VENUS, and preceptor of the Titans or demons.<BR>	 3. An<BR>archer.<BR>	 4. An elephant.<BR>	 f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. The goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>	 2. The<BR>goddes LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 3. Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon, the Agrostis<BR>linearis of LINNÆUS; according to the Hindus, and black variety.)<BR>E. भृगु a Muni, the ancestor of PARASU RĀMA, &c. and अण् aff. of<BR>descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गवप्रिय|भार्गवप्रियः
भार्गवप्रिय m. (-यः) The diamond.<BR> E. भार्गव SUKRA, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गी
भार्गी f. (-र्गी) A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR> E. भर्ग BRAHMĀ, and अण्<BR>aff.; sacred to that deity. “वामनहाटि” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्द्वाजी
भार्द्वाजी f. (-जी) Wild-cotton. E. A various reading of भारद्वाजी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्य|भार्य|भार्यः
भार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्या|भार्या
भार्य्या f. (-र्य्या) A wife, espoused according to the ritual of the Vedas.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्याट|भार्याट|भार्य्याटः
भार्य्याट m. (-टः) A man who lets out his wife for prostitution.<BR> E. भार्य्या<BR>wife, अट् to go, aff. अच्; who lives by his wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्याटिक|भार्याटिक|भार्याटिकः|भार्य्याटिकः
भार्य्याटिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A henpecked-husband, one over-ruled by his<BR>wife.<BR>	 2. A kind of deer.<BR> E. भार्य्या a wife, अट् to go or be with,<BR>aff. अच्, भार्य्याट, and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्यातिक्रम
भार्य्यातिक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Adultery.<BR>	 2. Connubial intercourse.<BR> E. भार्य्या<BR>and अतिक्रम approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्यात्व|भार्यात्व
भार्य्यात्व n. (-त्वं) The condition or state of a wife.<BR> E. भार्य्या, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्यापति|भार्यापति
भार्य्यापति m. dual only. (-तौ) Husband and wife.<BR> E. भार्य्या wife, and पति<BR>a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्यारु|भार्यारु|भार्यारुः|भार्य्यारुः
भार्य्यारु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. The name of a mountain.<BR>	 2. A sort of deer.<BR>	 3.<BR>The father of a child by another man's wife.<BR> E. भार्य्या wife, ऋ to<BR>go to or with, उण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य्योढ|भार्योढ
भार्य्योढ m. (-ढः) Married.<BR> E. भार्य्या, and ऊढ married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल|भालं
भाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The forehead.<BR>	 2. Darkness.<BR> E. भल् to explain, and<BR>अञ् aff.; a man's fortunes being supposed to be legible on his<BR>forehead; or भा to shine, aff. लच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालदर्शन|भालदर्शनं|भालदर्शनः
भालदर्शन n. (-नं) Red lead.<BR> E. भाल, and दर्शन appearing; being used<BR>to stain the forehead with particular lines, and marks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालदृश्
भालदृश् m. (-दृक्) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. भाल and दृश् the eye, having the<BR>third eye in his forehead; also similar compounds, as भाललोचन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालाङ्क|भालांक|भालाङ्कः
भालाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A sort of fish, commonly the Rohita, (Cyprinus<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">Page530-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Rohita, HAM.)<BR>	 2. A saw.<BR>	 3. A sort of potherb.<BR>	 4. A man born with<BR>lucky lines on his forehead.<BR>	 5. A tortoise.<BR>	 6. A name of ŚIVA. E.<BR>भाल the forehead, and अङ्क a spot or mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालु|भालुः
भालु m. (-लुः) The sun.<BR> E. भॄ-ञुण् रस्य लः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्लुक|भाल्लुकः
भाल्लुक m. (-कः) A bear.<BR> E. भल्ल् to injure, aff. उकञ् or ऊकञ्, whence<BR>also भाल्लूक; and with उक aff. भल्लुक, भल्लूक, &c. q. v. also भालुक<BR>and भालूक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव|भावः
भाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. State or condition of being.<BR>	 2. Natural state of being,<BR>innate property, disposition, nature.<BR>	 3. Meaning, purpose, inten-<BR>tion.<BR>	 4. Mind, soul.<BR>	 5. State or affection of mind, emotion, pass-<BR>ion, sentiment, especially as an object of amatory and dramatic<BR>poetry; two kinds of Bhāvas are usually enumerated, the Sthayi<BR>and Vyābhichāri; the first of which comprehends eight varieties,<BR>and the second thirty-three; the list blends both feelings and<BR>effects, and sorrow, and sleep, and passion, and death, &c. are<BR>equally classed amongst the Bhāvas; dramatic writers add two<BR>other classes, the Vibhāvas or preceding states of mind, leading<BR>to a particular condition of mind or body, and Anubhāvas the<BR>external signs of any state of mind.<BR>	 6. Birth.<BR>	 7. Act, action.<BR>	 8.<BR>Movement, gesture.<BR>	 9. Wanton sport or pastime.<BR>	 10. Corporeal<BR>expression of amorous sentiments; or love, of which the origin and<BR>effects are ascribed to the organs of the body.<BR>	 11. Thing, subs-<BR>tance.<BR>	 12. A being, a living thing.<BR>	 13. The place of birth, or<BR>pudendum muliebre.<BR>	 14. Superhuman power.<BR>	 15. The abstract<BR>idea conveyed by any word.<BR>	 16. The simple idea derived from<BR>the root, as expressed in one class of derivatives, as a going, a<BR>doing, &c.<BR>	 17. Advice, instruction.<BR>	 18. A learned man, a pandit,<BR>(in theatrical language; but especially applied to the manager,<BR>or principal performer.)<BR>	 19. Venerable, respectable.<BR>	 20. The world,<BR>the universe.<BR>	 21. An organ of sense or passion.<BR> E. भू to be,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावक|भावकः
भावक m. (-कः) The external expression of amatory sentiments.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>Adj.<BR>	 1. Effecting.<BR>	 2. Promoting any one's welfare.<BR>	 3. Imagining.<BR>4. Having a poetical taste.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावज|भावजः
भावज m. (-जः) Love, KĀMA.<BR> E. भाव sentiment and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत|भावतः
भावत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Yours, your honour's.<BR> E. भवत् you, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत्क|भावत्कः
भावत्क mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं) Yours, (but used respectfully.) your honour's.<BR>E. भवत् you, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावन|भावनं|भावनः
भावन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Mental perception, recollection, the present con-<BR>sciousness of past ideas or perceptions.<BR>	 2. Imagination.<BR>	 3. Religi<BR>ous and abstract meditation.<BR>	 4. Looking about, (literally or figur-<BR>atively.) observing, investigating.<BR>	 5. Causing to be.<BR>	 6. Decorating<BR>any person or object with flowers, perfume, &c, scenting, anoint-<BR>ing.<BR>	 7. Steeping, infusion, especially repeatedly drying the article<BR>by day and keeping it moist at night.<BR>	 8. (In arithmetic,) Composi-<BR>tion.<BR>	 9. (In law,) Ascertainment, proof.<BR> E. भू to be, in the causal<BR>form, to bring present or into being, aff. णिच्-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावबोधक|भावबोधकः
भावबोधक m. (-कः) The sign or indication of any sentiment or passion.<BR>E. भाव sentiment, and बोधक what indicates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावयत्
भावयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Fancying, imagining, calling to mind.<BR> E. भू<BR>to be, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावशवलता
भावशवलता f. (-ता) Co existence of various emotions.<BR> E. भाव and शवलता variety of colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावशान्ति
भावशान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Allaying any transitory or incidental emotion.<BR> E. भाव<BR>and शान्ति quieting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसंशुद्धि
भावसंशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Purification of the natural condition or quality. E.<BR>भाव and संशुद्धि qualification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसन्धि|भावसंधि|भावसंधिः
भावसन्धि m. (-न्धिः) Co-existence of two emotions.<BR> E. भाव and सन्धि union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसमाहित
भावसमाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Of restrained purpose or thought, abstract-<BR>devout.<BR> E. भाव and समाहित collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाट|भावाटः
भावाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The external expression or indication of amatory<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">Page530-b+ 60</a>]<BR>feeling.<BR>	 2. A pious or holy man.<BR>	 3. An actor.<BR>	 4. A libidinous man.<BR>5. Dress, decoration.<BR> E. भाव the sentiment or disposition, अट् to<BR>go with, aff. अण् or अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावानुग
भावानुग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Natural, simple, not forced or assumed.<BR>	 f. (-गा)<BR>A shadow.<BR> E. भाव and अनुग according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाभास|भावाभासः
भावाभास m. (-सः) Simulation of feeling or emotion.<BR> E. भाव and आभास appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावार्थ|भावार्थः
भावार्थ m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. The simple inherent or abstract meaning of words.<BR>2. The obvious purport of a phrase or sentence.<BR> E. भाव and अर्थ<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाव
भावाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Tender, compassionate.<BR> E. भाव and अव what preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविक|भाविकः
भाविक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Natural, innate.<BR>	 2. Sentimental, relating<BR>to feeling, &c.<BR>	 3. Future.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A figure of rhetoric, describing<BR>the past or future as present.<BR> E. भाव and ठक् aff.; or भू to be, causal<BR>v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावित|भावितः
भावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Occupied with, pervaded by, having as an in-<BR>herent or pervading property.<BR>	 2. Animated, inspired.<BR>	 3. Imagined,<BR>conceived.<BR>	 4. Perfumed, scented.<BR>	 5. Mixed, (with any thing as an<BR>ingredient, as asafœtida or other fragrant substances in curry, &c.)<BR>6. Obtained, got.<BR>	 7. Promised, agreed, acknowledged.<BR>	 8. Steeped,<BR>infused, digested, &c.<BR>	 9. (In arithmetic,) Supposed, as the product<BR>of unknown quantities.<BR> E. भू to be, passive or causal v., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितवत्
भावितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Imagining, conceiving.<BR>	 2. Infusing, &c.<BR>E. भू to be, causal v., क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितात्मन्
भावितात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>	 1. Intent upon, engaged in.<BR>	 2. Meditative.<BR>3. One whose soul is purified by meditation on the universal soul.<BR>E. भावित pervaded, आत्मन् spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावित्र|भावित्रं
भावित्र n. (-त्रं) The three worlds; earth, heaven and hell collectively. E.<BR>भू to exist, णित्रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविन्
भाविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Future, what will be or what is about to be,<BR>proximately future.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A wanton woman.<BR> E. भू to be, Unādi<BR>aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावोदय
भावोदय m. (-यः) Accession or occurrence of emotions.<BR> E. भाव, उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुक|भावुकं|भावुकः
भावुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Happy, well, right.<BR>	 2. Actually being and dis-<BR>posed to be.<BR>	 3. (In composition with other nouns,) Becoming what<BR>it was not before, as हाढ्यंभावुक one who becomes rich.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Happiness, auspiciousness.<BR>	 2. Language full of passions.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>A sister's husband, (in theatrical language.)<BR> E. भू to be, aff.<BR>उकञ्; used in composition, the aff. is खुकञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव्य|भाव्यं
भाव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. What must, will, or ought to be.<BR>	 2. To be in-<BR>vestigated or determined.<BR> E. भू to be, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्
भाष् (ऋ) भाषृ r. 1st cl. (भाषते) To speak: with परि prefixed, to explain,<BR>to expound; with सम् to discourse, to converse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषण|भाषणं
भाषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Speaking, speech.<BR>	 2. Declaration of satisfaction at the<BR>end of a drama.<BR> E. भाष् to speak, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषत्
भाषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Speaking, saying.<BR> E. भाष and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषमाण
भाषमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Speaking, saying.<BR> E. भाष् to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषा
भाषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Speech.<BR>	 2. A language.<BR>	 3. Common or vernacular speech.<BR>4. A charge, (in law.)<BR>	 5. SARASWATĪ, the goddess of speech.<BR>6. One of the Rāginis.<BR> E. माष् to speak, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषापाद|भाषापादः
भाषापाद n. (-दं) The plaint, the charge, the first of the four divisions of<BR>a lawsuit.<BR> E. भाषा speech, averment, and पाद quarter, division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषासम|भाषासमः
भाषासम m. (-मः) A figure of rhetoric, arrangement of a sentence so<BR>that it is both Sanskrit and Prākrita.<BR> E. भाषा and सम same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषित|भाषितं
भाषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spoken, uttered, said.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Speech.<BR> E. भाष् to<BR>speak, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्य|भाष्यं
भाष्य mfn. (ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) To be said or spoken.<BR>	 n. (-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. A com-<BR>mentary, but particularly the explanation and application of a<BR>technical Sūtra or aphorism; hence applied to many of the anno-<BR>tations on the grammatical aphorisms of PĀṆINI, to comments<BR>on the Vedas, &c.<BR>	 2. A sort of building.<BR> E. भाष् to speak, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यकर|भाष्यकरः
भाष्यकर m. (-रः) A commentator or expounder of technical texts or<BR>aphorisms; commonly applied as an epithet of PĀTANJALĪ, the<BR>author of the Mahābhāshya or commentary on the annotations of<BR>KĀTYĀYANA. on PĀṆINI'S grammatical aphorisms.<BR> E. भाष्य as<BR>above, and कार who makes; also with कृत्, भाष्यकृत् the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यमाण
भाष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being spoken to or addressed.<BR> E. भाष् to speak,<BR>pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
भास् (ऋ) भासृ r. 1st cl (भासते) To shine. With प्र and नि prefixed, To<BR>appear to, to seem likely or probable to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम्
भाम् f. (-भाः)<BR>	 1. Light.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR>	 3. Wish, desire.<BR> E. भास् to shine, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास|भासः
भास mf. (-सः-सा) Light, lustre, shining.<BR>	 m. (सः)<BR>	 1. A vulture.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of bird described as a water-fowl.<BR>	 3. A cock.<BR>	 4. A station of<BR>cowherds.<BR>	 5. Fancy.<BR> E. भास् to shine, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासक|भासकः
भासक f. (-सिका)<BR>	 1. Illumining.<BR>	 2. Making evident.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Name of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासन्त|भासंत|भासन्तः
भासन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, handsome.<BR>	 2. Shining, splendid.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. A kind of water-fowl.<BR>	 mf.<BR>(-न्तः-न्ती) A star.<BR> E. भास् to shine, झच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासयत्
भासयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Shining, radiant.<BR> E. भास् to shine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासस्
भासस् n. (-सः) Light, lustre.<BR> E. भास् to shine, असिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासु|भासुः
भासु m. (-सुः) The sun.<BR> E. भास् to shine, Unādi aff. उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासुर|भासुरं|भासुरः
भासुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Shining, splendid.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A species of Costus,<BR>(C. speciosus.)<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Crystal.<BR>	 2. A hero.<BR> E. भास् to shine,<BR>घुरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्कर|भास्करं|भास्करः
भास्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Resplendent, shining.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>3. A hero.<BR>	 4. The name of a celebrated astronomer.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Gold.<BR>E. भा light, and कृ to make, अच् aff., and स inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करप्रिय|भास्करप्रियः
भास्करप्रिय n. (-यं) The ruby.<BR> E. भास्कर the sun, and प्रिय fond of. “पद्मराग”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्मन
भास्मन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Ashy, ashen, made or consisting of ashes. E.<BR>भस्मन् and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वत्|भास्वन्त्
भास्वत् mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्) Luminous, splendid, shining.<BR>	 m. (-स्वान्)<BR>	 1.<BR>The sun.<BR>	 2. Light.<BR>	 3. A hero.<BR>	 f. (-स्वती) The city of the sun.<BR> E. भास्<BR>light, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वर|भास्वरं|भास्वरः
भास्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Shining, radiant.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A day.<BR>n. (-रं) A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR> E. भास् to shine, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्ष्
भिक्ष् r. 1st cl. (भिक्षते)<BR>	 1. To beg.<BR>	 2. To obtain.<BR>	 3. To fail of obtaining.<BR>4. To solicit any thing through cupidity or covetousness.<BR>	 5. To be<BR>weary or distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षण|भिक्षणं
भिक्षण n. (-णं) Begging, asking alms.<BR> E. भिक्ष् to beg, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षमाण
भिक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Asking, begging.<BR> E. भिक्ष् to beg, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षा
भिक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Service.<BR>	 2. Hire, wages.<BR>	 3. Begging, asking.<BR>	 4. The<BR>thing obtained by begging, alms.<BR>	 5. A mouthful or handful of<BR>food, given as alms.<BR> E. भिक्ष् to beg or obtain by begging, अङ् and<BR>टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाक|भिक्षाकः
भिक्षाक mf. (-कः-की) A mendicant, a beggar.<BR> E. भिक्षा alms, and काकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाचर|भिक्षाचरः
भिक्षाचर mf. (-रः-री) A mendicant, a beggar.<BR> E. भिक्षा alms, चर् to go,<BR>aff. ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाटन|भिक्षाटनं|भिक्षाटनः
भिक्षाटन n. (-नं) Begging, mendicancy.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A mendicant.<BR> E. भिक्षा<BR>alms, and अटन going about for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षान्न
भिक्षान्न n. (-न्नं) Food obtained as alms.<BR> E. भिक्षा, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षापात्र
भिक्षापात्र n. (-त्रं) A beggar's bowl, a vessel for collecting alms.<BR> E. भिक्षा,<BR>and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाशित्व|भिक्षाशित्वं
भिक्षाशित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Profligacy, roguery.<BR>	 2. Mendicancy, subsisting<BR>on alms.<BR> E. भिक्षाशिन् a beggar, त्व abstract aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाशिन्
भिक्षाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>	 1. A beggar, a mendicant, subsisting on<BR>alms.<BR>	 2. Dishonest.<BR> E. भिक्षा alms, अश् to eat, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षार्ह
भिक्षार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Fit for a beggar.<BR> E. भिक्षा, and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षित
भिक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Begged, sought as alms.<BR> E. भिक्ष् to beg, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षु|भिक्षुः
भिक्षु m. (-क्षुः) The mendicant; the Hindu who has entered the fourth<BR>order and subsists wholly upon alms.<BR>	 2. The fourth order of the<BR>Hindus.<BR>	 3. A Bauddha mendicant.<BR> E. भिक्ष् to beg, aff. उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुक|भिक्षुकः
भिक्षुक mf. (-कः-की) A beggar.<BR> E. भिक्षु a beggar, कन् added; or भिक्ष-उक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुसंघाटी
भिक्षुसंघाटी f. (-टी) Old or ragged raiment, the garb of a beggar.<BR> E. भिक्षु<BR>a beggar, सम् with, घट् to endeavour, affs. अण् and ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षोत्कर
भिक्षोत्कर m. (-रः) Scattering alms.<BR> E. भिक्षा alms, उत् before, कॄ to scat-<BR>ter, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्त|भित्तं
भित्त n. (-त्तं)<BR>	 1. A part, a portion.<BR>	 2. A fragment, a bit.<BR>	 3. A wall, a<BR>partition.<BR> E. भिद् to divide, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्ति|भित्तिः
भित्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. A wall of earth or masonry.<BR>	 2. A thing broken or<BR>divided.<BR>	 3. A place, a part.<BR>	 4. Opportunity, occasion.<BR>	 5. An<BR>asylum.<BR>	 6. Breaking, tearing, dividing.<BR>	 7. A flaw, a defect.<BR>	 8. A<BR>rent, a fissure.<BR>	 9. A fragment, a bit, a broken piece or part.<BR>	 10. A<BR>mat.<BR> E. भिद् to divide, to break, to tear, &c. aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिका
भित्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A wall.<BR>	 2. A small house-lizard.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिचौर|भित्तिचौरः
भित्तिचौर m. (-रः) A housebreaker.<BR> E. भित्ति a wall and चौर a thief; the<BR>mud-wall of the Hindu cottages being easily and commonly cut<BR>through, for burglarious purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिपातन|भित्तिपातनः
भित्तिपातन n. (-नं) A rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्
भिद् (इर्) भिदिर् r. 7th cl. (-भिनत्ति-भिन्ते) To break, to break or tear to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्
भिद् mfn. (-भिद् or भित्) Who or what breaks, divides, severs, des-<BR>troys, &c.<BR>	 f. (भिद् or भित्)<BR>	 1. Kind, sort, difference.<BR>	 2. Breaking,<BR>dividing.<BR> E. भिद् to break, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदक|भिदकं|भिदकः
भिदक m. (-कः) A sword.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>	 2. A diamond.<BR>E. भिद् to break, aff. क्वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदा
भिदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. Tearing, rending.<BR>	 2. Coriander.<BR>	 3. Separation.<BR>	 4. Diff-<BR>erence.<BR>	 5. Kind, species.<BR> E. भिद् to divide, aff. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदि|भिदिः
भिदि m. (-दिः) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. भिद् to break, Unādi aff. कि; also भिदु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदिर|भिदिरं
भिदिर n. (-रं) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. भिद् to break or split, किरच्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदु|भिदुः
भिदु m. (-दुः) The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR> E. भिद् to split, Unādi aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदुर|भिदुरं|भिदुरः
भिदुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Brittle.<BR>	 2. Breaking.<BR>	 3. Mixed.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The<BR>thunderbolt.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The Plaksha-tree.<BR> E. भिद् to break, (the<BR>earth, the mountains, &c.) कुरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदेलिम
भिदेलिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) To be, or what may be broken.<BR> E. भिद् to<BR>break, केलिमर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्य|भिद्यः
भिद्य m. (-द्यः) A river, a male river.<BR> E. भिद् to break, (its banks,) क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्यमान
भिद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being divided, pierced, broken, &c.<BR>	 2. Being<BR>separated or distinguished.<BR> E. भिद् to break, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्र|भिद्रं|भिद्रः
भिद्र mn. (-द्रः-द्रं) The thunderbolt.<BR> E. भिद् to break, Unādi aff. रक्;<BR>also भिदु, भिदुर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दत्
भिन्दत् mfn. (-न्दन्-न्दन्ती-न्दत्) Breaking, destroying.<BR> E. भिद् to break, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्द
भिन्द(न्दि)पाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A short arrow thrown from the hand, or shot<BR>through a tube.<BR>	 2. A sling, a string-instrument for throwing<BR>stones.<BR> E. भिदि-इन् भिन्दि, पालि-अन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्न|भिन्नः
भिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Split, broken, torn, rent.<BR>	 2. Divided, dis-<BR>tinguished, other, different.<BR>	 3. Separated, detached.<BR>	 4. Blown,<BR>budded, opened.<BR>	 5. Neglected, deviated from.<BR>	 6. Loosened.<BR>	 7.<BR>Pounded 8. Deprived of.<BR>	 9. Furious, in rut, (as an elephant.)<BR>m. (-न्नः) A flaw in a jewel.<BR>	 n. (-न्नं)<BR>	 1. A bit, a portion.<BR>	 2. (In<BR>arithmetic,) A fraction.<BR> E. भिद् to break, to divide, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नक|भिन्नकः
भिन्नक m. (-कः) A heterodox sectary, a Bauddha, a seceder.<BR> E. भिन्न<BR>broken, separated, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नगात्रिका
भिन्नगात्रिका f. (-का) A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis utilatissimus.) E.<BR>भिन्न divided, गात्र the body, aff. of comparison कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नगुणन
भिन्नगुणन n. (-नं) Multiplication of fractions.<BR> E. भिन्न, and गुणन multiplying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नघन|भिन्नघनः
भिन्नघन n. (-नं) The cube of a fraction.<BR> E. भिन्न and घन a cube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नदेह
भिन्नदेह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Wounded.<BR> E. भिन्न and देह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्ननौक
भिन्ननौक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Wrecked.<BR> E. भिन्न and नौका a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नभागहर|भिन्नभागहरः
भिन्नभागहर m. (-रः) Division of fractions.<BR> E. भिन्न and भागहर division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नभाण्ड
भिन्नभाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A pot-sherd, a broken plate or vessel.<BR> E. भिन्न and<BR>भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नभिन्नात्मन्
भिन्नभिन्नात्मन् m. (-त्मा) Chick-pea, (Cicer arietinum,)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नमर्म्मन्|भिन्नमर्मन्
भिन्नमर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्म-र्म्म) Pierced in the joints, mortally wounded. E.<BR>भिन्न and मर्म्मन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवत्
भिन्नवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Divided, scattered.<BR> E. भिद् to break, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवर्ग|भिन्नवर्गः
भिन्नवर्ग m. (-र्गः) Square of a fraction.<BR> E. भिन्न and वर्ग a square.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवृत्ति
भिन्नवृत्ति mfn. (-त्ति-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>	 1. Neglecting the prescribed observances.<BR>2. Following an occupation not suited to birth or caste.<BR> E. भिन्न,<BR>and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नव्यवकलित
भिन्नव्यवकलित n. (-तं) Subtraction of fractions.<BR> E. भिन्न, व्यवकलित subtrac-<BR>tion; also भिन्नव्यवकलनं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नसङ्कलित|भिन्नसंकलित
भिन्नसङ्कलित n. (-तं) Addition of fractions.<BR> E. भिन्न, सङ्कलित addition;<BR>also भिन्नसङ्कलनं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नस्वर
भिन्नस्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Hesitating, (in speech.)<BR>	 2. Hoarse, discordant.<BR> E. भिन्न, स्वर a note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिया
भिया f. (-या) Fear.<BR> E. भी to fear, टाप् aff., and इयङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिल्
भिल् r. 10 cl. (भेलयति-ते) To divide or separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिल्ल्
भिल्ल् m. (-ल्लः) A barbarian of a particular tribe, perhaps the modern<BR>Bheel, a savage race dwelling especially along the course of the<BR>Narmadā, and subsisting chiefly by plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषग्जित|भिषग्जितं
भिषग्जित n. (-तं) A drug, a medicament.<BR> E. भिषज् a physician, and जित<BR>subdued, (by whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिषज्
भिषज् m. (-षक्) A Vaidya or physician.<BR> E. भी to fear, अजि Unādi aff.,<BR>and षुक् augment; or भिषज् a Kanḍwādi root, to overcome,<BR>(disease,) aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिस्मटा
भिस्मटा f. (-टा) Scorched-rice.<BR> E. भिस्मा boiled-rice, टीक् to go or re-<BR>semble, ड aff.; this word is variously read भिस्मिटा भिष्मिटा, भिष्मिष्टा,<BR>भिष्मिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिस्मा
भिस्मा f. (-स्मा) Boiled-rice.<BR> E. भिद to break, aff. क्विप्, सो to destroy, aff. क,<BR>and the द of भिद् changed irrly. to स; also read भिष्म; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भी
भी (ञि) ञिभी r. 3rd cl. (विभेति) To dread, to fear, to be afraid of: also,<BR>r. 1st and 10th cls. (भयति भाययति) but not always admitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भी
भी f. (-भीः) Fear, dread.<BR> E. भी to fear, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीत|भीतं
भीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Afraid, frightened, fearful, timid.<BR>	 2. Imperiled.<BR>n. (-तं) Fear, alarm, apprehension.<BR> E. भी to fear, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीतङ्कार|भीतंकार|भीतंकारं
भीतङ्कार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Fear-inspiring.<BR> E. भीत, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीतभीत
भीतभीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Much frightened.<BR> E. भीत afraid, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीतवत्
भीतवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वन्) Afraid.<BR> E. भी to fear, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीति|भीतिः
भीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Fear, apprehension.<BR>	 2. Trembling, shaking.<BR> E. भी to<BR>fear, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीम|भीमं|भीमः
भीम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Horrible, fearful, terrific.<BR>	 n. (-मं) Horror, terror.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. One of the five Pāndu princes.<BR>	 3.<BR>A kind of sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius.)<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>2. Whip.<BR>	 3. A sort of perfume: see रोचना.<BR> E. भी to fear, Unādi<BR>aff. मक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमकर्म्मन्|भीमकर्मन्
भीमकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Dreadful, destructive.<BR> E. भीम, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमदर्शन
भीमदर्शन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Frightful, hideous.<BR> E. भीम, दर्शन appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमनाद|भीमनादः
भीमनाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. A loud or fearful sound.<BR>	 3. Name of one<BR>of the seven clouds which spring up at the end of the world. E.<BR>भीम formidable, नाद voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमर|भीमरं|भीमरः
भीमर m. (-रः) War, battle.<BR> E. भीम fear, रा to give or get, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमरथी
भीमरथी f. (-थी)<BR>	 1. A particular night, supposed to be the ordinary pe-<BR>riod of human life; seventh night, in the seventh month, of the<BR>seventy-seventh year; a person after this period exempt from all<BR>religious or specific observances.<BR>	 2. The name of a river in the<BR>Himālaya mountains.<BR> E. भीम formidable, रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमविक्रम
भीमविक्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Tremendous in power or strength.<BR> E. भीम,<BR>and विक्रम prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमविक्रान्त|भीमविक्रांत|भीमविक्रान्तः
भीमविक्रान्त m. (-न्तः) A lion.<BR> E. भीम formidable, विक्रान्त power, valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमविग्रह
भीमविग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Gigantic, terrific in appearance.<BR> E. भीम, and<BR>विग्रह body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमवेग
भीमवेग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Terribly swift or rapid.<BR> E. भीम्, and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमशासन|भीमशासनः
भीमशासन m. (-नः) A name of YAMA.<BR> E. भीम formidable, शासन edict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीमसेन|भीमसेनः
भीमसेन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The third of the five Pāndu princes.<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>camphor.<BR> E. भीम formidable, and सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरु|भीरुः
भीरु mfn. (-रुः-रुः or -रुः-रु) Timid, fearful.<BR>	 f. (-रुः-रूः)<BR>	 1. A timid woman.<BR>2. A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>	 3. A sort of prickly night-<BR>shade.<BR>	 4. A jackal.<BR>	 5. A centipede.<BR>	 6. A tiger.<BR>	 7. A goat.<BR>	 n. (-रु)<BR>Silver.<BR> E. भी to fear, Unādi aff. क्रु; also र being changed to<BR>उ, भीलु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुक|भीरुकं|भीरुकः
भीरुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Timid, fearful, 2. Formidable.<BR>	 3. Shy.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-कं) A wood, a forest.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An owl.<BR>	 2. A bear.<BR> E. भी to fear,<BR>Unādi aff. क्रुकन्; also ल being substituted for र, भीलुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुचेतस्
भीरुचेतस् m. (-ताः) A deer.<BR> E. भीरु timid. चेतस् disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुता
भीरुता f. (-ता) Fear, timidity, fearfulness.<BR> E. तल् added to भीरु, also<BR>with त्व, भीरुत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुमय
भीरुमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Terrific, frightful.<BR> E. भीरु and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुरन्ध्र|भीरुरंध्र|भीरुरन्ध्रः
भीरुरन्ध्र m. (-न्ध्रः) An oven, a furnace.<BR> E. भीरु fearful and रन्ध्र a chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीरुहृदय|भीरुहृदयः
भीरुहृदय m. (-यः) A deer.<BR> E. भीरु timid, हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीलु|भीलुः
भीलु mfn. (-लुः-लुः or लूः-लु) Timid, fearful: see भीरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीलु|भीलुः
भीलु(लू)क mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Timid, fearful.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A bear: see भीरुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषण|भीषणः
भीषण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Horrible, terrific, formidable.<BR>	 2. Hard, harsh.<BR>3. Exciting the sentiment of horror, applied to poetical composi-<BR>tions.<BR>	 m. (-णः) The olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>	 2. A name<BR>of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. A pigeon.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Horror, terror the property that<BR>excites fear.<BR>	 2. The sentiment of horror as the object of poetical<BR>com position.<BR> E. भी to fear, in the causal form, aff. ल्युट् or युच्, and<BR>सुक् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषयमाण
भीषयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Terrifying, frightening.<BR> E. भी to fear, causal v., शानच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीषा
भीषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Terrifying, frightening, intimidation.<BR>	 2. Terror.<BR> E. भी<BR>to fear, causal v., अङ् and टाप् affs., and सुक् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्म|भीष्मं|भीष्मः
भीष्म mfn. (-ष्मः-ष्मा-ष्मं) Horrible, terrific, fearful.<BR>	 n. (-ष्मं) Horror, horri-<BR>bleness, the property of exciting fear or terror.<BR>	 m. (-ष्मः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The grand-uncle of the Pāndus.<BR>	 3. An imp, a<BR>goblin.<BR> E. भी to fear, मक् Unādi aff. and सुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मसू
भीष्मसू f. (-सूः) The Ganges.<BR> E. भीष्म the prince so named, and सू mother;<BR>being the mother of BHĪṢMA by ŚANTANU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्त|भुक्तं
भुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Eaten, eating, (either that which is eaten, or<BR>the person who has eaten.)<BR>	 2. Possessed, enjoyed.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं) Food.<BR>E. भुज् to eat, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तवत्|भुक्तवन्त्
भुक्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Having eaten.<BR>	 2. Having possessed. E.<BR>भुज् to eat, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तशेष|भुक्तशेषः
भुक्तशेष n. (-षं) Orts, leavings.<BR> E. भुक्त and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तसमुज्झित|भुक्तसमुज्झितं
भुक्तसमुज्झित n. (-तं) Orts, leavings, either after a meal or what has<BR>dropped from the mouth.<BR> E. भुक्त eaten, समुज्झित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्ति|भुक्तिः
भुक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Eating.<BR>	 2. Possession, fruition, usufruct.<BR>	 3. Food.<BR>	 4.<BR>The diurnal motion of a planet.<BR> E. भुज् to eat, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्त्वा
भुक्त्वा Ind. Having possessed, eaten, enjoyed, &c.<BR> E. भुज् to eat, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुग्न|भुग्नः
भुग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Crooked, curved.<BR>	 2. Bent, bowed. bending,<BR>stooping.<BR>	 3. Broken.<BR> E. भुज् to curve, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
भुज् r. 7th cl. (भुनक्ति भुंक्ते)<BR>	 1. To save, to cherish or protect.<BR>	 2. To eat.<BR>3. To enjoy, (carnally.)<BR>	 4. To suffer or endure. (ओ, औ) औभुजौ r.<BR>6th. cl. (भुजति) To bend, to make crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
भुज् Adj. (At the end of a compound.)<BR>	 1. Eating, enjoying, as in स्वधा-<BR>भुज्.<BR>	 2. Ruling, as in क्षितिभुज्.<BR>	 f. 1. Enjoyment.<BR>	 2. Profit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज|भुजः
भुज mf. (-जः-जा)<BR>	 1. The arm.<BR>	 2. The hand 3. The trunk of an ele-<BR>phant.<BR>	 4. The arm or leg of a geometrical figure, as a square or<BR>triangle.<BR>	 5. A bending, a curve.<BR> E. भुज् to bend, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजकोटर|भुजकोटरः
भुजकोटर m. (-रः) The armpit.<BR> E. भुज the arm, and कोटर a hollow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजग|भुजगः
भुजग m. (-गः) A snake.<BR> E. भुज् a curve, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजगदारण|भुजगदारणः
भुजगदारण m. (-णः) The bird of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. भुजग a snake, and दारण des-<BR>troyer; this word, and similar compounds, may be applied equally<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">Page533-a+ 60</a>]<BR>to any of the natural enemies of the serpent race, as the ardea, the<BR>peacock, the ichneumon, &c. ut infra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजगान्तक|भुजगांतक|भुजगान्तकः
भुजगान्तक m. (-क.) GARUḌA, the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. भुजग a snake, and<BR>अन्तक destroyer: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजगाभोजिन्
भजगाभोजिन् m. (-जी) A peacock.<BR> E. भुजग a snake, and आभोजिन् who eats: see भुजगदारण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजगातशन
भुजगातशन m. (-नः) GARUḌA.<BR> E. भुजग a snake, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्ग|भुजंग|भुजंगः|भुजङ्गः
भुजङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. A catamite, a lecher.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी) A female<BR>snake.<BR> E. भुज् a curve, गम् to go, खच् aff.; also भुजङ्गम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गघातिनी|भुजंगघातिनी
भुजङ्गघातिनी f. (-नी) A plant considered as an antidote, commonly Kan-<BR>kālika, and said to be a sort of mustard.<BR> E. भुजङ्ग a snake, घातिनी<BR>destructive. “सर्पाक्षीलतायास च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गप्रयात|भुजंगप्रयात|भुजङ्गप्रयातं
भुजङ्गप्रयात n. (-तं) A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गभुज्|भुजंगभुज्
भुजङ्गभुज् m. (-भुक्)<BR>	 1. The bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A peacock.<BR>E. भुजङ्ग a snake, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गभोजिन्|भुजंगभोजिन्
भुजङ्गभोजिन् m. (-जी) The large Indian serpent, (Boa constrictor.) E.<BR>भुजङ्ग a snake, and भोजिन् who eats; devouring the smaller races.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गम|भुजंगम|भुजंगमः|भुजङ्गमः
भुजङ्गम m. (-मः) A snake.<BR> E. भुज् bending, गम् to go, and खच् aff.; also<BR>भुजग and भुजङ्ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गविजृम्भित
भुजङ्गविजृम्भित n. (-तं) A species of the Utkritī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गशिशु|भुजंगशिशु|भुजङ्गशिशुः
भुजङ्गशिशु m. (-शुः) A species of the Vrihatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गसङ्गता|भुजंगसंगता
भुजङ्गसङ्गता f. (-ता) Another species of the Vrihatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गहन्|भुजंगहन्
भुजङ्गहन् m. (-हा) GARUḌA.<BR> E. भुजङ्ग a snake, and हन् who kills: see भुजगदारण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गाक्षी|भुजंगाक्षी
भुजङ्गाक्षी f. (-क्षी) A plant, (the ichneumon plant: see रास्वा.<BR> E. भुजङ्ग a<BR>snake, अक्ष to pervade, affs. अण् and ङीप्; otherwise भुजङ्ग and अक्ष्<BR>an eye; the flowers being compared to the eye of the snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजङ्गाख्य|भुजंगाख्य|भुजङ्गाख्यः
भुजङ्गाख्य m. (-ख्यः) A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR> E. भुजङ्ग a snake, and<BR>आख्या a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूजज्या
भूजज्या f. (-ज्या) The base sine, (in astronomy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजशिरस्
भुजशिरस् n. (-रः) The shoulder, the shoulder blade.<BR> E. भुज् the arm, शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजा
भुजा f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. The arm.<BR>	 2. The land.<BR>	 3. The coil of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजाकण्ट|भुजाकंट|भुजाकण्टः
भुजाकण्ट m. (-ण्ट) A finger-nail.<BR> E. भुजा the hand, and कण्ट a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजादल|भुजादलः
भुजादल m. (-लः) A hand.<BR> E. भुजा the arm, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजान्तर|भुजांतर|भुजान्तरं
भुजान्तर n. (-रं) The breast, the chest.<BR> E. भुज् the arm, and अन्तर inter-<BR>vening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजापीड|भुजापीडः
भुजापीड m. (-डः) Clasping or enfolding in the arms.<BR> E. भुज and आपीड pressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजामध्य|भुजामध्यः
भुजामध्य n. (-ध्यं) The elbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजि|भुजिः
भुजि m. (-जिः) Fire.<BR> E. भुज् to eat, इन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजिष्य|भुजिष्यः
भुजिष्य mf. (-ष्यः-ष्या) A servant, a slave.<BR>	 m. (-ष्यः)<BR>	 1. An independent<BR>man.<BR>	 2. A string worn round the wrist.<BR>	 3. A companion.<BR>	 4. A<BR>disease.<BR>	 f. (-ष्या)<BR>	 1. A harlot, a whore.<BR>	 2. A female slave.<BR> E. भुज्<BR>to be crooked, Unādi aff. किष्यन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्यमान
भुज्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being enjoyed or possessed.<BR>	 2. Being eaten.<BR>E. भुज् to enjoy, pass. v., शानथ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्यु|भुज्युः
भुज्यु m. (-ज्युः) Eating.<BR> E. भुज् to eat, युच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुञ्जान|भुञ्जानः
भुञ्जान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. An enjoyer, a possessor.<BR>	 2. Eating, feeding.<BR>E. भुज् to enjoy, aff. शानच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुड
भुड (इ) भुडि r. 1st. cl. (भुण्डते)<BR>	 1. To support, to maintain.<BR>	 2. To select.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुरिज
भुरिज f. (-रिक्) The earth.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, इजि Unādi aff, and उर subs-<BR>tituted for the radical vowel; also भूरिज् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवन|भुवनं
भुवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A world, (they are said to be either three or fourteen<BR>in number.)<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Heaven.<BR>	 4. Man, mankind.<BR>	 5. The<BR>number “fourteen.” 6. The earth.<BR> E. भू to be, क्युन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवन्यु|भुवन्युः
भुवन्यु m. (-न्युः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The Moon.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR>	 4. A Master or<BR>lord.<BR> E. भू to be, Unādi aff. कन्थुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवनत्रय
भुवनत्रय n. (-यं) The three worlds: heaven, atmosphere and earth.<BR> E. भुवन, त्रय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवर्लोक|भुवर्लोकः
भुवर्लोक m. (-कः) One of the divisions of the universe, the space<BR>between the earth and the sun, and the haunt of the Siddhas,<BR>Munis and other saintly beings.<BR> E. भुवस् heaven, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुवस्
भुवस् Ind. Heaven, æther, sky, or atmosphere.<BR> E. भू to be, Unādi aff.<BR>असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुविस्
भुविस् n. (-विः) The ocean.<BR> E. भू to be, Unādi aff. इसि and the radical<BR>vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भु
भु(श)शुण्डी f. (-ण्डी) A weapon, apparently a kind of fire arms or rocket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भू
भू r. 1st. cl. (भवति)<BR>	 1. To be, to become, to exist.<BR>	 2. To be born or<BR>produced. r. 10th cl. (भावयति)<BR>	 1. To mix.<BR>	 2. To think.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>clear or pure. r. 1st and 10th cls. (भवति-ते भावयति-ते) To obtain.<BR>The first form of this root takes most of the prefixes, and then<BR>possesses a great variety of applications. With अधि. To rule or pre-<BR>side over. With अनु.<BR>	 1. To feel, to apprehend or perceive.<BR>	 2. To<BR>do, to make.<BR>	 3. To enjoy.<BR>	 4. To investigate. With अभि.<BR>	 1. To over-<BR>come.<BR>	 2. To pain or afflict. With उत्, To be born or produced.<BR>With परा To be vanquished. With प्र, 1. To become manifest, to<BR>appear, to come into sight or existence.<BR>	 2. To be equal to in per-<BR>sonal conflict, to be a match for.<BR>	 3. To rule, to be supreme, to<BR>preside over.<BR>	 4. To be beyond or over.<BR>	 5. To proceed. With प्रति<BR>To be substitute for. With परि, 1. To disrespect.<BR>	 2. To surround.<BR>With वि, 1. To see.<BR>	 2. To uphold.<BR>	 3. To prove.<BR>	 4. To have majesty<BR>or power. With वि and अति, व्यतिभवते, To be mutually or recipro-<BR>cally. With सम्, 1. To be possible.<BR>	 2. To exist, to be born or pro-<BR>duced.<BR>	 3. To contain.<BR>	 4. To overcome.<BR>	 5. To be able or adequate.<BR>6. To associate, to collect, to mix or assemble.<BR>	 7. To nourish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भू
भू Adj. (At the end of a compound,)<BR>	 1. Becoming, springing from, as<BR>in गिरिभू, वित्तभू, &c.<BR>	 2. Being, existing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भू
भू f. (-भूः)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. Place, site, the place of being or abiding.<BR>	 3.<BR>Landed property.<BR>	 4. The base of a geometrical figure.<BR>	 5. Subject-<BR>matter, subject.<BR>	 6. The number “one.” 7. The first of the three<BR>mystical syllables uttered by a Brāhmana at the beginning of his<BR>daily prayers.<BR>	 8. Sacrificial-fire. Ind. (भू) The lowest of the seven<BR>hells.<BR> E. भू to be, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूक|भूकं|भूकः
भूक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A hole, a chasm.<BR>	 2. Time.<BR>	 3. Darkness.<BR>	 4. A<BR>spring.<BR> E. भू to be, Unādi aff. कक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकदम्ब|भूकदंब|भूकदम्बः
भूकदम्ब m. (-म्बः) A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR> E. भू the earth, and<BR>कदम्ब nauclea. “कोक्सिमा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकम्प|भूकंप|भूकम्पः
भूकम्प m. (-म्पः) An earthquake.<BR> E. भू the earth, and कम्प a trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकर्ण|भूकर्णः
भूकर्ण m. (-र्णः) (In astronomy,) The radius of the equator.<BR> E. भू, कर्ण a<BR>sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकल|भूकलः
भूकल m. (-लः) A restiff unmanageable horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकश्यप|भूकश्यपः
भूकश्यप m. (-पः) A name of VASUDEVA, the father of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. भू<BR>the earth, and कश्यप KAŚYAPA; being an incarnation of that<BR>personage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकाक|भूकाकः
भूकाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A small kind of heron.<BR>	 2. A kind of pigeon.<BR>	 3. The<BR>curlew.<BR> E. भू earth, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकेश|भूकेशः
भूकेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>Indian-fig.<BR>	 f. (-शा) A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>	 f. (-शी) A<BR>Rākshasi or female goblin.<BR> E. भू the earth, and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूक्षित्
भूक्षित् m. (-क्षित्-क्षिद्) A hog.<BR> E. भू the earth, क्षि to destroy, aff. छिप्<BR>तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूगर्भ|भूगर्भः
भूगर्भ m. (-र्भः) A name of BHAVABHŪTI, the author of the Mālati<BR>Mādhava, and other dramas.<BR> E. भू the earth, गर्म fœtus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूगर|भूगरं
भूगर n. (-रं) Poison.<BR> E. भू and गर poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूगोल|भूगोलः
भूगोल m. (-लः) The terrestrial globe, the earth.<BR> E. भू the earth, गोल<BR>a ball or globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूचक्र
भूचक्र n. (-क्रं) (In astronomy,) The equinoctial line.<BR> E. भू and चक्र a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूच्छाया|भूछाया
भूच्छाया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. The shadow of the earth, popularly called RĀhu.<BR>2. Darkness.<BR> E. भू the earth, and छाया shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूजन्तु|भूजंतु|भूजन्तुः
भूजन्तु m. (-न्तुः)<BR>	 1. An earth-worm.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR> E. भू and जन्तु a being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूजम्बू|भूजंबू
भूजम्बू f. (-म्बूः)<BR>	 1. Wheat.<BR>	 2. The fruit of the Vikankata, (Flacourtia<BR>sapida.)<BR> E. भू the earth, and जम्बू rose-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत|भूतं|भूतः
भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Been, become.<BR>	 2. Being, existing.<BR>	 3. Gone, past.<BR>4. (In composition,) Like, resembling.<BR>	 5. Obtained, got.<BR>	 6. Pro-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">Page534-a+ 60</a>]<BR>per, right.<BR>	 7. True.<BR>	 8. Known.<BR>	 9. Mixed.<BR>	 mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>	 1. A goblin, a<BR>ghost, a malignant spirit, haunting cemeteries, lurking in trees,<BR>animating carcases and deluding or devouring human beings.<BR>	 2. A<BR>living being.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A son, a child.<BR>	 2. A demi-god of a parti-<BR>cular class.<BR>	 3. The fourteenth day of the dark half of the lunar<BR>month.<BR>	 4. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 n. (-त)<BR>	 1. An element; five Bhūtas<BR>are enumerated: earth, fire, water, air and Ākās or æther.<BR>	 2.<BR>(In law,) Fact, matter of fact, the real state of the case, or what<BR>has actually been.<BR>	 3. The past.<BR>	 4. Welfare.<BR>	 5. The world.<BR>	 6. The<BR>number “five,” (in math.)<BR> E. भू to be, aff. क्त of the participle past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतकेश|भूतकेशः
भूतकेश f. (-शी) The white basil.<BR> E. भूत a spirit and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतक्रान्ति|भूतक्रांति|भूतक्रान्तिः
भूतक्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Possession by evil spirits.<BR> E. भूत a goblin, क्रान्घि going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतगण|भूतगणः
भूतगण m. (-णः) A class of spirits or goblins.<BR> E. भूत and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतगन्धा
भूतगन्धा f. (-न्धा) Mura, a sort of perfume.<BR> E. भूत a goblin, and गन्ध a per-<BR>fume; used perhaps in the ceremonies with which those beings<BR>are worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतग्राम|भूतग्रामः
भूतग्राम m. (-मः) Any aggregate of elementary matter, the body, the<BR>world.<BR> E. भूत and ग्राम a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतघ्न|भूतघ्नः
भूतघ्न m. (-घ्नः)<BR>	 1. A camel.<BR>	 2. Garlic.<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly<BR>Mundīrī.<BR>	 2. Holy basil.<BR> E. भूत a spirit, and घ्न what destroys or<BR>removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतचतुर्दशी|भूतचतुर्द्दशी
भूतचतुर्दशी f. (-शी) The fourteenth day of the second half of Kārtic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतजटा
भूतजटा f. (-टा) Indian spikenard, (Valeriana jatāmānsi.)<BR> E. भूत a gob-<BR>lin, and जटा clustered locks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतदया
भूतदया f. (-या) Compassion or tenderness to all creatures.<BR> E. भूत and दया clemency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतधात्री
भूतधात्री f. (-त्री) The earth.<BR> E. भूत a living being, and धात्री a nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनाथ|भूतनाथः
भूतनाथ m. (-थः) SĪVA.<BR> E. भूत a spirit of element, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनायिका
भूतनायिका f. (-का) DURGĀ.<BR> E. भूत a spirit, and नायिका leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनाशन|भूतनाशनं|भूतनाशनः
भूतनाशन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Marking-nut plant, (Semicarpus anacardium.)<BR>	 2.<BR>mustard.<BR>	 n. (-नं) The Elecarpus seed.<BR> E. भूत a goblin, and नाशन<BR>dispelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपुष्प|भूतपुष्पः
भूतपुष्प m. (-ष्प.) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. भूत a spirit, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपूर्णिमा
भूतपूर्णिमा f. (-मा) Day of full-moon in Āshwin.<BR> E. भूत a spirit, and<BR>पूर्णिमा full moon; the Bhūtas being worshipped in this day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपूर्व्वम्|भूतपूर्वम्
भूतपूर्व्वम् Ind. Formerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतबलि|भूतबलिः
भूतबलि f. (-लिः) Throwing the remnants of an offering on the ground<BR>for animals and outcaste, &c.<BR> E. भूत and बलि an offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभर्त्तृ|भूतभर्तृ
भूतभर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-त्त्री-र्त्तृ) Supporting the elements, living beings.<BR> E. भूत<BR>and भर्त्तृ who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभाव
भूतभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Elementary.<BR> E. भूत and भाव a nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभृत्
भूतभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Supporting the elements, living beings.<BR> E. भूत and<BR>भृत् sustaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतमात्र
भूतमात्र nf. (-त्रं-त्रा) The rudiment of an element.<BR> E. भूत and मात्र element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतयज्ञ|भूतयज्ञः
भूतयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. Offering viands, &c. to all created beings.<BR>	 2. Wor-<BR>shipping evil spirits.<BR> E. भूत and यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतल
भूतल n. (-लं) The earth, the surface of the earth.<BR> E. भू and तल् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवत्|भूतवन्त्
भूतवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Being, been.<BR> E. भू to be, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवास|भूतवासः
भूतवास m. (-सः) Beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica.)<BR> E. भूत a<BR>goblin, and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतविक्रिया
भूतविक्रिया f. (-या) Epilepsy, possession by evil spirits.<BR> E. भूत and विक्रिया change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतविद्या
भूतविद्या n. (-द्या) Demonology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवृक्ष|भूतवृक्षः
भूतवृक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>	 2. A species of Bignonia,<BR>(B. Indica.)<BR> E. भूत a goblin and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवेशी
भूतवेशी f. (-शी) A species of the Nibāri (Nyctanthes tristis,) with<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसञ्चार|भूतसंचार|भूतसंचारः|भूतसञ्चारः
भूतसञ्चार m. (-रः) Possession by evil spirits.<BR>	 f. (-री) Fire in a forest. E.<BR>(-रिणी ।)<BR>भूत a goblin, सम् with, चर् to go, aff. घञ्; also भूतसञ्चारिन् f.<BR>white flowers.<BR> E. भूत a goblin, विश् to pervade, अण् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसम्पृक्त
भूतसम्पृक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Combined with elementary matter.<BR> E. भूत<BR>and सम्पृक united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसम्प्लव|भूतसंप्लव|भूतसंप्लवः
भूतसम्प्लव m. (-वः) A deluge, a drowning of the world.<BR> E. भूत all beings,<BR>and सम्प्लब swimming, floating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसंसार|भूतसंसारः
भूतसंसार m. (-रः) The world of mortals.<BR> E. भूत a sentient being, and संसार world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसर्ग|भूतसर्गः
भूतसर्ग m. (-र्गः) Elementary nature.<BR> E. भूत and सर्ग nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतस्थ
भूतस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Residing or existing in the elements.<BR> E. भूत,<BR>and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतात्मन्
भूतात्मन् m. (-त्मा)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. A name of Śiva.<BR>	 4. War,<BR>conflict.<BR>	 5. The elementary or vital principle, or the proximate<BR>cause of life and action.<BR> E. भूत an element, आत्मन् self or soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतादि|भूतादिः
भूतादि m. (-दिः) God, the originator beings.<BR> E. भूत and आदि first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतारि|भूतारिः
भूतारि m. (-रिः) Asafœtida.<BR> E. भूत and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतार्त्त|भूतार्त|भूतार्त्तः
भूतार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-त्ता-र्त्तं) Possessed by an evil spirit.<BR> E. भूत a spirit, आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतावास|भूतावासः
भूतावास m. (-सः) The body.<BR> E. भूत and आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूताविष्ट|भूताविष्टः
भूताविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्ट) Occupied or possessed by a devil.<BR> E. भूत a<BR>spirit, आविष्ट entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतावेश|भूतावेशः
भूतावेश m. (-शः) Possession by a devil or evil spirit.<BR> E. भूत a goblin, and आवेश entrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूति|भूतिः
भूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Power, dignity.<BR>	 2. Superhuman power, as attributable<BR>to ŚIVA especially, and attainable by the practice of austere and<BR>magical rites.<BR>	 3. Prosperity, success.<BR>	 4. Production, birth.<BR>	 5.<BR>Ashes.<BR>	 6. Fried meat.<BR>	 7. The rut of elephants.<BR>	 8. State of being,<BR>&c.<BR>	 9. Wealth, riches, fortune.<BR>	 10. Welfare.<BR>	 11. Decoration of<BR>elephant, with coloured stripes.<BR> E. भू to be, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिक|भूतिकं|भूतिकः
भूतिक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A sort of gentian, (G. Cherayta.)<BR>	 2. A fragrant grass,<BR>(Andropogon schœnanthus.)<BR>	 3. Another kind of grass.<BR>	 4. A medi-<BR>cinal plant, commonly Kayaphal.<BR>	 5. Ligusticum ajwaen.<BR>	 6.<BR>Camphor.<BR>	 7. Sandal-wood.<BR> E. भूत being or spirit, &c. aff. ठक्; also<BR>भूतीक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकाम|भूतिकामः
भूतिकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Desirous of wealth, aggrandisement, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-मः)<BR>	 1. A king's counsellor, a minister of state.<BR>	 2. VRIHASPATĪ.<BR>E. भूति and काम who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकाल|भूतिकालः
भूतिकाल m. (-लः) A happy hour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकील|भूतिकीलः
भूतिकील m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A moat, a ditch.<BR>	 2. A celler, a place under<BR>ground for concealing wealth, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकृत्य
भूतिकृत्य n. (-त्यं) Any ceremony of a festive character, as a marriage,<BR>&c.<BR> E. भूति and कृत्य rite; also भूतिकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिगर्भ|भूतिगर्भः
भूतिगर्भ m. (-र्भः) BHAVABHŪTI, the dramatic poet.<BR> E. भूति superhuman<BR>power, and गर्भ embryo, being resuscitated by his contemporary,<BR>and rival KĀLIDĀNA, after having lost his life in an intrigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिज्य
भूतिज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) A worshipper of spirits.<BR> E. भूत, इज्या worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिनिधान|भूतिनिधानं
भूतिनिधान n. (-नं) The twenty-fourth lunar mansion, Dhaniṣṭhā. E.<BR>भूति prosperity, and निधानं receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतीक|भूतीकं
भूतीक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A sort of gentian.<BR>	 2. A kind of lovage, (Ligusticum<BR>ajwaen.)<BR>	 3. A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schœnanthus.)<BR>	 4. An-<BR>other sort of grass.<BR>	 5. Sandal wood.<BR>	 6. Camphor.<BR> E. भूत being, aff.<BR>ईकक् otherwise भूतिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतृण|भूतृणं|भूतृणः
भूतृण m. (-णः) A kind of fragrant grass, called “चिप्पगड्डि” by the<BR>Tailangeese.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेश|भूतेशः
भूतेश m. (-शः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. भूत an imp, ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतोपहत
भूतोपहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Possessed by an evil spirit.<BR> E. भूत and उपहत affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत्तम|भूत्तमं
भूत्तम n. (-मं) Gold.<BR> E. भू earth, उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत्वा
भूत्वा Ind. Having been or become.<BR> E. भू to be, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूदार|भूदारः
भूदार m. (-रः) A hog.<BR> E. भू earth, दृ to tear, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूदेव|भूदेवः
भूदेव m. (-वः) A Brāhman<BR> E. भू the earth, and देव a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूधन|भूधनः
भूधन m. (-नः) A king.<BR> E. भू the earth, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूधर|भूधरः
भूधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A mountain.<BR>	 2. A kind of chemical or medicinal ap-<BR>paratus; a sand bath in which a covered crucible is placed, and<BR>the fire is lighted above as well as below it.<BR>	 3. The number<BR>“seven.”<BR> E. भू earth, धृ to support, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूध्र|भूध्रः
भूध्र m. (-ध्रः) A mountain.<BR> E. भू the earth, धृ to hold, aff. अप्, and the<BR>vowel changed to its analogous semi-vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूनाग|भूनागः
भूनाग m. (-गः) An earth-worm.<BR> E. भू the earth, and नाग a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूनिम्ब|भूनिम्बः
भूनिम्ब m. (-म्बः) A species of gentian, commonly cheraytā, (Gentiana<BR>cheraytā, Rox.)<BR> E. भू the earth, and निम्ब the Nimba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेतृ
भूतेतृ m. (-ता) A king, a sovereign.<BR> E. भू the earth, and नेतृ a leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूप|भूपः
भूप m. (-पः) A sovereign, a prince, a king.<BR> E. भू the earth, पा to che-<BR>rish, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपति|भूपतिः
भूपति m. (-तिः) A king, a sovereign.<BR> E. भू the earth, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपद|भूपदः
भूपद m. (-दः) A tree.<BR>	 f. (-दी) Arabian jasmine, (Jasminum zambac.)<BR>E. भू the earth, and पद foot, root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपरिधि|भूपरिधिः
भूपरिधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. The equinoctial line.<BR>	 2. The circumference of the<BR>earth.<BR> E. भू and परिधि a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपाल|भूपालः
भूपाल m. (-लः) A king, a sovereign.<BR> E. भू the earth, and पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपुत्त्री
भूपुत्त्री f. (-त्त्री) SĪTĀ, the wife of RĀMA.<BR> E. भू the earth, and पुत्त्री a<BR>daughter; being turned up out of the soil by a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभुज्
भूभुज् m. (-भुक्) A king, a sovereign.<BR> E. भू the earth, भुज् to enjoy,<BR>aff. क्किप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभृत्
भूभृत् m. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. A king, a sovereign.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR> E. भू the earth, भृत् sustaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमण्डल|भूमंडल
भूमण्डल n. (-लं) The terrestrial globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमन्
भूमन् mfn. (-मा-मा-म) Much, many.<BR>	 2. Wealth.<BR>	 n. (-म)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>2. A piece of ground.<BR>	 3. A being.<BR> E. भू for बहु many, इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूनय
भूनय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of or consisting the earth.<BR>	 f. (-यी) A name<BR>of Chāyā or shadow personified, the wife of the sun.<BR> E. भू earth,<BR>and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमि|भूमिः
भूमि f. (-मिः-मी)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. Place, site in general.<BR>	 3. A dis-<BR>trict.<BR>	 4. Land, soil.<BR>	 5. A story, floor.<BR>	 6. A site, situation.<BR>	 7. Atti-<BR>tude, posture.<BR>	 8. A mask, a character, (in Dramaturgy.)<BR>	 9. Subject,<BR>object.<BR>	 10. The tongue 11. Abode.<BR>	 12. The base of any figure in<BR>geometry.<BR> E. भू to be and मि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिका
भूमिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Theatrical dress, the costume of any character, re-<BR>presented on the stage.<BR>	 2. Decorating images, temples, gateways,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. A board for writing.<BR>	 4. A preface, an introduction.<BR>	 5. A<BR>floor.<BR>	 6. A place.<BR>	 7. A step, a degree.<BR>	 8. Earth, soil.<BR> E. भूमि place<BR>of being, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिचम्पक|भूमिचम्पकः
भूमिचम्पक m. (-कः) A plant, (Kæmpferia rotunda.)<BR> E. भूमि earth, and चम्पक Michelia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिज|भूमिजं|भूमिजः
भूमिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born or produced of or on the earth.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>1. The planet MARS.<BR>	 2. Naraka the demon.<BR>	 3. A man.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>SĪTĀ, the wife of RĀMA.<BR> E. भूमि earth, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिजम्बु|भूमिजम्बुः
भूमिजम्बु f. (-म्बुः-म्बू) A tree, (Premna herbacea.)<BR> E. भूमि earth, and जम्बु<BR>Engenia: also with कन् added to either form, भूमिजम्बुका and<BR>भूमिजम्बूका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिजीविन्
भूमिजीविन् m. (-वी) The Vaiśya or Hindu of the third or agricultural<BR>and mercantile tribe.<BR> E. भूमि the earth, and जीविन् who gets a<BR>livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिदान
भूमिदान n. (-नं) Donation of landed property.<BR> E. भूमि and दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिदेव|भूमिदेवः
भूमिदेव m. (-वः) A Brāhman.<BR> E. भूमि the earth, and देव a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिधर|भूमिधरः
भूमिधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A mountain, (especially the Kulāchala which is<BR>supposed to exist in the seven divisions of the continent.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>number “seven.” 3. A king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिप|भूमिपः
भूमिप m. (-पः) A prince, a sovereign.<BR> E. भूमि the earth, and प who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिपक्ष|भूमिपक्षः
भूमिपक्ष m. (-क्षः) A horse of a good breed.<BR> E. भूमि the earth, and पक्ष<BR>part or side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिपति|भूमिपतिः
भूमिपति m. (-तिः) A king.<BR> E. भूमि and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिपतित्व
भूमिपतित्व n. (-त्वं) Princedom, sovereignty.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिपिशाच|भूमिपिशाचः
भूमिपिशाच m. (-चः) The palmyra tree, (Borassus flabelliformis.)<BR> E. भूमि<BR>earth, पिशाच goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिभृत्
भूमिभृत् m. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. A king.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR> E. भूमि and मृत् who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिमण्डा|भूमिमंडा
भूमिमण्डा f. (-ण्डा) Arabian jasmine, (Jasminum zambac.)<BR> E. भूमि the<BR>earth, मडि to ornament, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिरक्षक|भूमिरक्षकः
भूमिरक्षक m. (-कः) A horse of a good breed.<BR> E. भूमि the earth, रक्ष् to<BR>preserve, aff. वुन्; it is also written भूमिरक्ष and भूमिपक्ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिलाभ|भूमिलाभः
भूमिलाभ m. (-भः) Death, dying, (in figuratively.)<BR> E. भूमि earth, लाभ<BR>acquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिलेपन|भूमिलेपनं
भूमिलेपन n. (-नं) Cow-dung.<BR> E. भूमि earth and लेपन plastering; the clay<BR>floors of houses, temples, &c. being usually kneaded up with this<BR>article.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिवर्द्धन
भूमिवर्द्धन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Increasing or adding to the earth.<BR>	 mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>A corpse.<BR> E. भूमि the earth and वर्द्धन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिशय|भूमिशयः
भूमिशय mfn. (-यः-यी यं) Sleeping on the ground.<BR> E. भूमि and शी to sleep, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिष्ठ
भूमिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Standing or staying on the earth.<BR> E. भूमि and स्थ<BR>who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिसम्भव|भूमिसंभव|भूमिसंभवः
भूमिसम्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced in or of the earth.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The<BR>planet Mars.<BR>	 2. The demon Naraka.<BR>	 f. (-वा) ŚITĀ.<BR> E. भूमि the<BR>earth and सम्भव born: see भूपुत्त्री ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिस्नु|भूमिस्नुः
भूमिस्नु m. (-स्नुः) An earth-worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिस्पृश्
भूमिस्पृश् m. (-स्पृक्)<BR>	 1. A man, man, mankind.<BR>	 2. The Vaiśya or Hindu<BR>of the third tribe, the cultivator or trader.<BR>	 3. A thief, one who<BR>creeps along the ground to carry off his plunder.<BR>	 4. A blind man<BR>5. A cripple, a lame man.<BR> E. भूमि the earth, the ground, and स्पृश<BR>who touches, from स्पृश्, with क्किन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमीन्द्र|भूमींद्र|भूमीन्द्रः
भूमीन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A king, a sovereign.<BR> E. भूमि earth, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूम्यामलकी
भूम्यामलकी f. (-की) A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR> E. भूमि the earth,<BR>आमलकी a myrobalan; also भूम्यासनी f. (-नी ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूय|भूयं|भूयः
भूय n. (-यं) Abstract state, but used in composition, as ब्रह्मभूय the state<BR>of BRAHMĀ, or identification with BRAHMĀ, becoming of the<BR>same nature, &c.<BR> E. भू to be, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयशस्
भूयशस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Generally, as a rule 2. Very much.<BR>	 3. Again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयस्
भूयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Much, many.<BR>	 2. Abounding. Ind. Fre-<BR>quently, repeatedly, again.<BR>	 2. Exceeding, over, above.<BR>	 3. Further.<BR>E. बहु much, इयसुन् affix of the superlative, भू substituted for बहु,<BR>and the ई of the aff. rejected; also with इष्ठन् aff. भूयिष्ठ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयिष्ठ|भूयिष्ठं
भूयिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Many, very many, much, most: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरि|भूरिः
भूरि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>	 1. Much, many.<BR>	 2. Large, great. Ind. Much, ex-<BR>ceeding.<BR>	 m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. ŚIVA 4.<BR>Indra.<BR>	 n. (-रि) Gold.<BR> E. भू to be, क्रिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिगम|भूरिगमः
भूरिगम m. (-मः) An ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिज्
भूरिज् f. (-रिक्) The earth.<BR> E. भृ to support, इजि Unādi aff. and ऋ changed to ऊर् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिधामन्
भूरिधामन् mfn. (-मा-मा-म)<BR>	 1. Splendid, bright.<BR>	 2. Illustrious.<BR> E. भूरि, and<BR>धामन् Splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिपुष्पा
भूरिपुष्पा f. (-ष्पा) Fennel: see शतपुष्पा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिप्रयोग
भूरिप्रयोग Adj. In common use, (as a word.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिप्रेमन्
भूरिप्रेमन् m. (-मा) The ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिफेना
भूरिफेना f. (-ना) A plant, commonly Charmakasā.<BR> E. भूरि much, and फेन cuttle-fish-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिमाय|भूरिमायः
भूरिमाय m. (-यः) A jackal.<BR> E. भूरि much, माय deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिरस|भूरिरसः
भूरिरस m. (-सः) The sugarcane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिलाभ|भूरिलाभः
भूरिलाभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Very profitable or beneficial.<BR>	 n. (-भं) Great<BR>gain.<BR> E. भूरि and लाभ gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिशस्
भूरिशस् Ind. Manifold, many by many.<BR> E. भूरि many, शस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरुण्डी
भूरुण्डी f. (-ण्डी) A sort of sun-flower, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR> E. भू the<BR>earth, रुह् to grow; or रुद्ध् to oppose, क aff., deriv. irr. “हातिशुंँडा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरुह|भूरुहः
भूरुह m. (-हः) A tree.<BR> E. भू the earth, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्ज्ज|भूर्ज|भूर्जः
भूर्ज्ज m. (-र्ज्जः) The Bhurja-patra tree growing in the snowy<BR>mountains, a kind of birch; the bark is used for writing on, and<BR>very generally for hooka snakes.<BR> E. भू the earth, and ऊर्ज्ज् to be<BR>strong or hardy, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्ज्जकण्ठक|भूर्जकण्ठक
भूर्ज्जकण्ठक m. (-कः) A man of one of the inferior or mixed classes,<BR>sprung from an outcaste Brāhman by a woman of the same tribe.<BR>E. भूर्ज्ज the Bhurj, and कण्ठ the throat, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्ज्जपत्र|भूर्जपत्र|भूर्जपत्रः|भूर्ज्जपत्रः
भूर्ज्जपत्र m. (-त्रः) The Bhurja-patra: see भूर्ज्ज.<BR> E. भूर्ज्ज as above, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्णि|भूर्णिः
भूर्णि f. (-र्णिः)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. A desert, a country ill-supplied with<BR>water.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, Unādi aff. नि, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्लोक|भूर्लोकः
भूर्लोक m. (-कः) The earth, the habitation of mortals, the terrestrial<BR>globe.<BR> E. भूः the earth, and लोक the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूलता
भूलता f. (-ता) A worm, an earth-worm.<BR> E. भू the earth, लता a creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूशक्र|भूशक्रः
भूशक्र m. (-क्रः) A king.<BR> E. भू the earth, and शक्र INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूशुद्धि|भूशुद्धिः
भूशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Purifying the ground by sweeping, burning, &c.<BR> E. भू<BR>and शुद्धि Purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूश्रवस्
भूश्रवस् m. (-वाः) An ant or mole hill.<BR> E. भू the earth, and श्रु to exude, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्
भूष् r. 1st and 10th cls. (भूषति भूषयति-ते) To decorate, to adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषण|भूषणं|भूषणः
भूषण n. (-णं) Ornament, embellishment.<BR> E. भूष् to adorn, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषयितव्य
भूषयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be decorated or ornamented.<BR> E. भूष्, and<BR>तव्य aff.; also भूषणीय &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषा
भूषा f. (-षा) Adorning, decorating with trinkets, jewels, &c.<BR> E. भूष् to<BR>adorn, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषित|भूषितः
भूषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Adorned, decorated, dressed.<BR> E. भूष् to adorn, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्णु|भूष्णुः
भूष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Being, existing.<BR>	 2. Being well, faring well.<BR>E. भू to be, ग्ष्णु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूसुत|भूसुतः
भूसुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The planet MARS.<BR>	 2. The demon Naraka.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>SĪTĀ, the wife of RĀMA.<BR> E. भू the earth, and सुत the offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्तृण|भूस्तृणं|भूस्तृणः
भूस्तृण n. (-णं) A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schænanthus.)<BR> E. भू the<BR>earth, तृण् grass, and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्पृश्
भूस्पृश् m. (-स्पृक्) Man, a man, mankind.<BR> E. भू the earth, and स्पृश् who<BR>touches: see भूमिस्पृश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्वर्ग|भूस्वर्गः
भूस्वर्ग m. (-र्गः) The mountain Sumeru.<BR> E. भू, and स्वर्ग paradise; a heaven on earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्वामिन्
भूस्वामिन् m. (-मी) A landlord, a landholder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृ
भृ (ञ्) भृञ् r. 1st cl. (भरति-ते) (डु, ञ्) डुभृञ् r. 3rd cl. (विभर्त्ति विभृते)<BR>1. To nourish, to cherish, to foster, to maintain.<BR>	 2. To fill.<BR>	 3. To<BR>hold or support.<BR>	 4. To suffer.<BR>	 5. To confer. With सम्, 1. To col-<BR>lect.<BR>	 2. To prepare.<BR>	 3. To nourish.<BR>	 4. To produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुंस|भृकुंसः
भृकुंस m. (-सः) A mail actor or dancer in female apparel.<BR> E. भ्रु an eye-<BR>brow, कुसि to speak, aff. अच्, रु changed to ऋ; also with कन् added<BR>भृकुंसक, and र unchanged भ्रकुंस; also from कुशि, भृकुंश; &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुटि|भृकुटिः
भृकुटि f. (-टिः-टी) A frown, a contraction of the brows.<BR> E. भ्रु the eye-<BR>brow, कुट् to be or make crooked, aff. कि, and ङीप् optionally add-<BR>ed, भृ substituted for भ्र्; otherwise भ्रकुटि, भ्रुकुटी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृग्
भृग् Ind. An imitative word expressive of the crackling sound of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगु|भृगुः
भृगु m. (-गुः)<BR>	 1. The name of a celebrated Muni, and one of the<BR>ten Brahmādikas or Prājapatis, the sons of BRAHMĀ, and<BR>first created of beings.<BR>	 2. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. ŚUKRA, the regent<BR>of VENUS.<BR>	 4. A precipice.<BR>	 5. Table land, the level summit of a<BR>mountain.<BR>	 6. The Ṛṣi JAMADAGNI, the father of PARASURĀMA<BR>and grandson of the Muni BHRIGU.<BR> E. भ्रस्ज् to fry, (in religious<BR>fervour,) Unādi aff. कु; र is changed to ऋ, the स rejected, and<BR>the final ज becomes ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुपति|भृगुपतिः
भृगुपति m. (-तिः) The hero, and Avatār PARASURĀMA.<BR> E. भृगु implying<BR>the race of BHRIGU or JAMADAGNI, and पति master, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुवासर|भृगुवासरः
भृगुवासर m. (-रः) Friday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुसुत|भृगुसुतः
भृगुसुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. SUKRA or VENUS, the son the Muni BHRIGU, and<BR>the preceptor of the DAITYAS.<BR>	 2. The hero PARASURĀMA.<BR> E. भृगु<BR>the saint BHRIGU, or his descendant JAMADAGNI, and सुत the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगूणाम्पति|भृगूणांपति
भृगूणाम्पति m. (-तिः) The first of the three incarnations of VIṢṆU<BR>called RĀMAS; PARASURĀMA the son of JAMADAGNI.<BR> E. भृगु in<BR>the sixth case plural, and पति master, chief of the BHRIGUS or<BR>race of BHRIGU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्ग|भृंग|भृङ्गं|भृंगः|भृङ्गः
भृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A large black bee, the humble bee.<BR>	 2. A catamite, a<BR>libertine, a lecher.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Eclipta or Verbesina prostrata.)<BR>4. A wasp, either the common kind, or the Vespa solitaria.<BR>	 5.<BR>A golden vase.<BR>	 6. The fork-tailed shrike, (Lanius cærulescens.)<BR>	 7.<BR>A bird, apparently a sort of shrike different from the preceding.<BR>n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Woody cassia.<BR>	 2. Talc.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, गन् Unādi aff.,<BR>and कित्-नुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गक|भृंगकः|भृङ्गकः
भृङ्गक m. (-कः) A bird, a sort of shrike, (Lanius malabaricus.)<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गज|भृंगज|भृङ्गजं
भृङ्गज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Alœ-wood or Agallochum.<BR>	 2. Talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गपर्णिका|भृंगपर्णिका
भृङ्गपर्णिका f. (-का) Small or Gnzarāti cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गरजस्
भृङ्गरजस् m. (-जाः) Eclipta prostrata: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गराज|भृङ्गराजः
भृङ्गराज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A spreading shrub, (Eclipta or Verbesina pros-<BR>trata, or perhaps more properly, Verbesina scandens.)<BR>	 2. A sort<BR>of bird, apparently the variety of shrike termed Malabar, (Lanius<BR>malabaricus.)<BR>	 3. The humble bee.<BR>	 4. A particular sacrifice.<BR> E. भृङ्ग<BR>a bee, and राज् to shine, aff. अच्; or with रजस् dust, भृङ्गरजस् and<BR>with राजन् shining, ruling, भृङ्घराजन् m. (-जा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गरिट
भृङ्गरिट m. (-टः) One of ŚIVA'S doorkeepers.<BR> E. भृङ्ग a bee, रट् to speak<BR>or make a noise, to buzz, aff. अच्, and the penultimate changed<BR>to इ; also with इन् aff., and the penultimate long or short, the<BR>word is read भृङ्गरिटि, भृङ्गरीट, and भृङ्गरीटि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गरोल|भृंगरोल|भृङ्गरोलः
भृङ्गरोल m. (-लः) A wasp.<BR> E. भृङ्ग a bee, रु to cry, लच् aff. “भीम्रुल” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गवल्लभ|भृंगवल्लभ|भृङ्गवल्लभः
भृङ्गवल्लभ m. (-भः) A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गसोदर|भृङ्गसोदरः
भृङ्गसोदर m. (-रः) A plant, apparently a variety of Eclipta or Verbesina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गार|भृंगार|भृंगारं|भृङ्गारं|भृंगारः|भृङ्गारः
भृङ्गार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A golden vase, especially used at royal ceremonials.<BR>2. A shrub, (Eclipta prostrata, &c.: see भृङ्गराज)<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Cloves.<BR>2. Gold.<BR>	 f. (-री) A cricket.<BR> E. भृ to contain, (water, &c.) आरक्<BR>Unādi aff., and गुक् augment; or भृङ्ग a bee, and अरि an enemy,<BR>fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गारिका|भृंगारिका
भृङ्गारिका f. (-का) A cricket.<BR> E. भृङ्ग a bee, अरि an enemy, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गावली|भृंगावली
भृङ्गावली f. (-ली) A line or flight of bees.<BR> E. भृङ्ग, and आवली a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गिन्|भृंगिन्
भृङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. One of ŚIVA'S chamberlains.<BR>	 2. The Indian fig-tree.<BR>E. भृङ्ग a bee, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गीफल|भृङ्गीफलः
भृङ्गीफल m. (-लः) The hog-plum: see आसातक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृङ्गीश|भृङ्गीशः
भृङ्गीश m. (शः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. भृङ्गी the attendant of the deity, and ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृज्
भृज् (इ) भृजी r. 1st. cl. (भर्जते) To parch, to fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृज्जन|भृज्जनं|भृज्जनः
भृज्जन n. (-नं) A frying-pan.<BR> E. भ्रस्ज् to fry, Unādi aff. क्युन्, and the<BR>root changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत|भूतं|भूतः
भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Hired, paid, maintained.<BR>	 2. Cherished, suppor-<BR>ted.<BR>	 3. Filled.<BR>	 4. Having, being possessed of, or endowed with.<BR>5. Borne, carried.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A servant.<BR>	 2. A hired labourer. E.<BR>भृ to nourish, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतक|भृतकः
भृतक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A hired labourer.<BR>	 2. A servant.<BR> E. भृत hired, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतकाध्यापक|भृतकाध्यापकः
भृतकाध्यापक m. (-कः) A hired teacher, one who gives instructions for<BR>pay.<BR> E. भृतक, and अध्यापक a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतकाध्यापित|भृतकाध्यापितः
भृतकाध्यापित m. (-तः) A student who pays his teacher.<BR> E. भृतक, and अध्यापित instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतभूति
भृतभूति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>	 1. Prosperous, powerful, exalted.<BR>	 2. Smeared<BR>with ashes.<BR> E. भृत possessed, and भूति power, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतरन्ध्र
भृतरन्ध्र mfn. (-न्ध्रः-न्ध्रा-न्ध्रं) Filled up, (as a hole or depression.)<BR> E. भृत, रन्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृति|भृतिः
भृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Wages, hire.<BR>	 2. Capital, principal.<BR>	 3. Nourishment,<BR>maintenance.<BR>	 4. Supporting, support.<BR>	 5. Service for wages.<BR> E. भृ to<BR>nourish, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतिभुज्
भृतिभुज् m. (-भुक्) A hired labourer or servant.<BR> E. भृति hire, भुज् to eat, aff. क्किप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्य|भृत्यः
भृत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्य) To be nourished or maintained.<BR>	 m. (-त्यः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>dependent.<BR>	 2. A servant, a slave.<BR>	 3. A minister.<BR>	 f. (-त्या) Hire,<BR>wages.<BR> E. भृ to nourish, aff. क्यप्, with तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यत्व|भृत्यत्वं
भृत्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Servitude, service, dependence.<BR> E. त्व added to the last;<BR>also with तल्, भृत्यता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यध्यापन
भृत्यध्यापन n. (-नं) Teaching, (especially the Vedas,) for hire.<BR> E. भृति,<BR>and अध्यापन instructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यभरण
भृत्यभरण n. (-णं) Maintaining or cherishing, dependents, servants, &c.<BR>E. भृत्य, and भरण nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यभर्त्तृ|भृत्यभर्तृ
भृत्यभर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) A master of a family taking good care of his depen-<BR>dents.<BR> E. भृत्य, and भर्त्तृ who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यवात्सल्य
भृत्यवात्सल्य n. (-ल्यं) Kindness to dependents or servants.<BR> E. भृत्य, and<BR>वात्सल्य tenderness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यविनिवेश
भृत्यविनिवेश m. (-शः) Fixing or planting firmly.<BR> E. भृत्य, and विनिवेश<BR>placing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यवृत्ति|भृत्यवृत्तिः
भृत्यवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Maintenance of servants or dependents.<BR> E. भृत्य, and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यशालिन्
भृत्यशालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Having many servants.<BR> E. भृत्य, and<BR>शालिन् possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्या
भृत्या f. (-त्या)<BR>	 1. Rearing, nourishing.<BR>	 2. Maintenance.<BR>	 3. Service.<BR>	 4. Wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्रिम
भृत्रिम f. (-मा) Adj. Nourished.<BR> E. भृ क्त्रि-मप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृ
भृ (भ्र) मि m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. A whirlwind, a hurricane, a high wind.<BR>	 2. An<BR>eddy, a whirlpool.<BR> E. भ्रम् to turn round, इन् Unādi aff., and the<BR>semi-vowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृश्
भृश् (इर्, उ) भृशु r. 4th cl. (भृश्यति) To fall, to fall down, literally or<BR>figuratively, as from a height, from dignity or virtue, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृश|भृशं
भृश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Much, exceeding.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-शं) Much exceedingly.<BR>Ind. (भृशम्)<BR>	 1. Much.<BR>	 2. Eminently, superiorly, better.<BR>	 3. Repeated-<BR>ly.<BR>	 4. Beautifully.<BR> E. भृश् to fall, aff. कृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृशस्विद्
भृशस्विद् mfn. (-स्विद्) Perspiring violently.<BR> E. भृश and स्विद् to sweat, क्विन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्ट|भृष्टः
भृष्ट mfn. (ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Fried.<BR> E. भ्रस्ज् to fry, aff. क्त, the vowel substituted<BR>for the semi-vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्टान्न|भृष्टान्नं
भृष्टान्न n. (-न्नं) Rice boiled and then fried.<BR> E. भृष्ट fried, अन्न boiled-rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृष्टि|भृष्टिः
भृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Frying.<BR>	 2. An uninhabited or lonely garden, &c. E.<BR>भ्रस्ज् to fry, aff. क्तिन् the semi-vowel changed to ऋ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भॄ
भॄ r. 9th. cl. (भॄणाति)<BR>	 1. To blame or censure.<BR>	 2. To nourish, to<BR>maintain, to support.<BR>	 3. To hold.<BR>	 4. To fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेक|भेकः
भेक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A frog.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. A timid man.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>	 1. The<BR>female of the frog, or a small frog.<BR>	 2. A kind of creeper, (Hydro-<BR>cotyle Asiatica.)<BR> E. भी to fear, Unādi aff. कन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेकपर्णी
भेकपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A creeper, (Hydrocetyle Asiatica.)<BR> E. भेक frog, and<BR>पर्ण a leaf; resembling the animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेकभुज्
भेकभुज् m. (-भुक्) A serpent, a snake.<BR> E. भेक, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेकरव|भेकरवः
भेकरव m. (-वः) The croaking of frogs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेड|भेडः
भेड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A ram, a sheep.<BR>	 2. A raft, a float.<BR>	 3. The name of a<BR>saint.<BR>	 f. (-डी) An ewe.<BR> E. भिल् a Sautra root, to separate, aff. अच्,<BR>and ल changed to ड; also with कन् added, भेडक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेतव्य
भेतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be feared or apprehended.<BR> E. भी to fear,<BR>तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेत्तृ
भेत्तृ mfn. (-त्ता-त्त्री-त्तृ) Who or what divides, disunites, &c.<BR>	 m. (-त्ता)<BR>1. A divider or separator.<BR>	 2. A factious or seditious man, a traitor,<BR>or one who secretly corresponds with an enemy, &c.<BR> E. भिद् to di-<BR>vide, to sow dissension, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेद|भेदः
भेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Dividing, separating.<BR>	 2. Tearing, rending, breaking, &c.<BR>3. Distinction, kind, sort, species, difference.<BR>	 4. Disunion, disagree-<BR>ment.<BR>	 5. Sowing dissension, breaking the unanimity of confeder-<BR>ates, one of the means of success against an opponent.<BR>	 6. Chasm,<BR>cleft.<BR>	 7. Change.<BR>	 8. Hitting, (as a mark.)<BR>	 9. Disclosure.<BR>	 10.<BR>Dualism, (in phil.)<BR>	 11. Evacuation of the bowels, (in medicine.)<BR>E. भिद् to divide, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदक|भेदकः
भेदक mfn. (-कः-दिका-कं) A breaker, who or what breaks or divides.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) A mischief-maker.<BR>	 m. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. An adjective.<BR>	 2. Purgative.<BR>E. भिद् to break ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदकर
भेदकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Separating, disuniting.<BR>	 2. Causing dissen-<BR>sion.<BR> E. भेद and कर who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदन|भेदनं|भेदनः
भेदन n. (-नं) Dividing, separating, literally or figuratively, as tearing,<BR>breaking, specifying, discriminating, causing separation or dis-<BR>sension, &c.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A hog.<BR> E. भिद् to break, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदप्रत्यय|भेदप्रत्ययः
भेदप्रत्यय m. (-यः) Belief in the reality of the multiform appearances of<BR>the world, in opposition to the doctrine that every thing is GOD.<BR>E. भेद difference, प्रत्यय faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदित|भेदितः
भेदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Divided, separated, literally or figuratively. E.<BR>भिद् to break, aff. क्त; also भिन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदिन्
भेदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Who or what divides, &c. Having a dis-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">Page537-b+ 60</a>]<BR>tinction or division.<BR>	 m. (-दी) The ratan.<BR> E. भिद् to divide, घिनुण्<BR>aff. or भेद sort, &c. and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदिर|भेदिरं
भेदिर n. (-रं) See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेदुर|भेदुरं
भेदुर n. (-रं) The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR> E. भिद् to split, (rocks, &c.)<BR>उरच् aff.; also भिदुर and भेदिर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेद्य|भेद्यं
भेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. To be broken.<BR>	 2. To be divided, pierced, cut,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. To be disconcerted or deterred.<BR>	 4. To be set at variance or<BR>disunited.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं) A substantive.<BR> E. भिद् to break, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेन|भेनः
भेन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. भ a star, &c. इन a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरि|भेरिः
भेरि mf. (-रिः-री) A kettle-drum.<BR> E. भी to fear, to cause to fear, Unādi<BR>aff. क्रिन्; otherwise रन् aff., and ङीप् added; also भेर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरुण्ड|भेरुंड|भेरुण्डं|भेरुण्डः
भेरुण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Formidable, fearful.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा) One of the Yak-<BR>shinis, or female attendants on DURGĀ.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः) A particular<BR>deity; a form of ŚIVA, according to the Tantras.<BR>	 n. (-ण्डं) Con-<BR>ception, impregnation.<BR> E. भी to fear, deriv. irr.; it is sometimes<BR>read भरण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेरुण्डक|भेरुंडक|भेरुंडकः|भेरुण्डकः
भेरुण्डक m. (-कः) A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेल|भेलं|भेलः
भेल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Ignorant, unwise, foolish.<BR>	 2. Fearful, timid.<BR>	 3.<BR>Unsteady, (figuratively or literally.)<BR>	 4. Tall.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A raft, a<BR>float.<BR>	 2. The name of a Muni, the author of some medical works.<BR>E. भी to fear, Unādi aff. रन् and the final changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेलक|भेलकं|भेलकः
भेलक mn. (-कः-कं) A raft, a float,<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेष्
भेष् (ऋ) भेषृ r. 1st cl. (भेषति-ते)<BR>	 1. To fear or dread.<BR>	 2. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषज|भेषजं
भेषज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. A remedy, a drug, a medicament.<BR>	 2. A kind of fennel,<BR>(Nigella Indica.)<BR> E. भेष here interpreted disease, जि to conquer, aff.<BR>ड; or भिषज् a root of a particular class, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषजाङ्ग|भेषजांग|भेषजाङ्गं
भेषजाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) The vehicle or medium in which medicine is adminis-<BR>tered, as water gruel, &c.<BR> E. भेषज a drug, and अङ्ग a limb or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्ष|भैक्षं
भैक्ष n. (-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Alms, what is collected by begging.<BR>	 2. Begging, men-<BR>dicancy.<BR>	 f. (-क्षी) Subsisting on alms.<BR> E. भिक्षा alms, given and re-<BR>ceived, aff. अण्; alse भैक्ष्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षचरण
भैक्षचरण n. (-णं) Plying for alms, begging.<BR> E. भैक्ष and चरण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षचर्य्या|भैक्षचर्या
भैक्षचर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) Begging, collecting alms.<BR> E. भैक्ष, and चर्य्या practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षजीविका
भैक्षजीविका f. (-का) Living upon alms, begging, mendicancy.<BR> E. भैक्ष<BR>aggregate alms, जीविका livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षभुज्
भैक्षभुज् m. (-भुक्) A mendicant.<BR> E. भैक्ष alms, and भुज् who subsists;<BR>also भैक्षाशिन्, भिक्षाशिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षाशिन्
भैक्षाशिन् m. (-शी) A mendicant.<BR> E. भैक्ष, and आशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षाहार|भैक्षाहारः
भैक्षाहार m. (-रः) A mendicant, one living on charity.<BR> E. भैक्ष and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्ष्य|भैक्ष्यं
भैक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं) Mendicity, begging.<BR> E. भिक्षा, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमी
भैमी f. (-मी)<BR>	 1. A patronymic of Damayantī, wife of NALA.<BR>	 2. The<BR>eleventh, day of the bright half of Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरव|भैरवं|भैरवः
भैरव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Formidable, horrible, terrific.<BR>	 n. (-वं) Horror,<BR>the property of exciting terror.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA, but<BR>more especially an inferior manifestation or form of the deity,<BR>eight of which are called by the common name Bhairava, and<BR>are severally termed ASITĀNGA, RURU, CHANDA, KRODHA, UN-<BR>MATTA, KUPATI, BHISHANA, and SANHĀRA, all alluding to terrific<BR>properties of mind or body.<BR>	 2. The name of a river.<BR>	 3. A musical<BR>mode; that which is calculated to excite emotion of terror.<BR>	 f. (-वी)<BR>1. A name or form of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A young girl personating DURGĀ<BR>at the festival of that goddess.<BR>	 3. Name of a Rāgini.<BR> E. भीरु fear-<BR>ful, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरवकारक
भैरवकारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Formidable.<BR> E. भैरव, and कारक what causes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषज|भैषजं|भैषजः
भैषज m. (-जः) A sort of quail.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Medicament.<BR> E. भिषज a medica-<BR>ment, and अण् referential or pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषज्य|भैषज्यं
भैषज्य n. (-ज्यं) A drug, a medicament.<BR> E. भेषज, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भो
भो Ind. A vocative particle.<BR> E. भा to shine, डो aff., more commonly भोस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तव्य|भोक्तव्यं
भोक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be used or enjoyed.<BR>	 2. To be eaten. E.<BR>भुज् to eat, &c., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तृ
भोक्तृ mfn. (-क्ता-क्ती-क्तृ)<BR>	 1. Enjoying, an enjoyer.<BR>	 2. An eater.<BR>	 m. (-क्ता)<BR>	 1.<BR>A husband.<BR>	 2. A lover.<BR>	 3. A possessor.<BR>	 4. A king.<BR> E. भुज् to enjoy,<BR>&c., aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तृत्व|भोक्तृत्वं
भोक्तृत्व n. (-त्वं) Possession, enjoyment.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्ष्यमाण
भोक्ष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being about to eat.<BR> E. भुज् to eat, and शानच्<BR>aff., here of the future tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग|भोगः
भोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Pleasure, enjoyment.<BR>	 2. Wealth.<BR>	 3. Nourishing,<BR>cherishing.<BR>	 4. Eating.<BR>	 5. A snake's body.<BR>	 6. A snake's expanded<BR>hood.<BR>	 7. Hire.<BR>	 8. The hire of dancing girls or courtezans.<BR>	 9. A<BR>snake.<BR>	 10. An army in column.<BR>	 11. (In arithmetic,) The nu-<BR>merator of a fraction.<BR>	 12. Food.<BR>	 13. A repost.<BR>	 14. Food offered<BR>to an idol.<BR>	 15. Gain.<BR>	 16. Rule, government.<BR>	 17. Experiencing.<BR>18. Advantage.<BR>	 19. The use of a deposit.<BR> E. भुज् to eat, &c.<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगगुच्छ
भोगगुच्छ n. (-च्छं) Price paid to harlots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगगृह|भोगगृहं
भोगगृह m. (-हः) The inner or private apartment, the harem.<BR> E. भोग<BR>enjoyment, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगतृष्ण
भोगतृष्ण f. (-ष्णा) Thirst for worldly enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगदेह|भोगदेहः
भोगदेह m. (-हः) The body which a dead person carries with him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपति|भोगपतिः
भोगपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A viceroy, a governor.<BR>	 2. A person having poss-<BR>ession or usufruct.<BR> E. भोग enjoyment, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपाल|भोगपालः
भोगपाल m. (-लः) A groom.<BR> E. भोग pleasure, and पाल who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपिशाचिका
भोगपिशाचिका f. (-का) Hunger.<BR> E. भोग eating, पिशाचिका an imp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगभूमि|भोगभूमिः
भोगभूमि f. (-मिः) Svarga or paradise.<BR> E. भोग enjoyment, and भूमि soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगभृतक|भोगभृतकः
भोगभृतक m. (-कः) A servant or slave, who work for maintenance only.<BR>E. भोग enjoyment, and भृतक a hireling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगलाभ|भोगलाभः
भोगलाभ m. (-भः) Interest or profit made by the use of any thing<BR>pledged.<BR> E. भोग enjoyment, and लाभ gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगवत्|भोगवन्त्
भोगवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Enjoying having enjoyment.<BR>	 2. Delight-<BR>ful, pleasurable, yielding enjoyment.<BR>	 3. Having curves.<BR>	 m. (-वान्)<BR>1. A snake.<BR>	 2. Dancing, acting and singing together.<BR>	 3. A moun-<BR>tain.<BR>	 f. (-वती)<BR>	 1. The capital of the Nāgas, or serpent.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Ganges of the lower regions.<BR>	 3. The night of the second day of a<BR>lunar month.<BR> E. भोग enjoyment, aff. मतुप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगसद्मन्
भोगसद्मन् n. (-द्म) The inner apartment, the harem.<BR> E. भोग pleasure, सद्मन् a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगस्थान
भोगस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The body as the seat of sensual enjoyment.<BR>	 2. A<BR>harem, &c.<BR> E. भोग enjoyment and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगाधि|भोगाधिः
भोगाधि m. (-धिः) A pledge that may be used until it is redeemed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगार्ह
भोगार्ह n. (-र्हं) Wealth, property.<BR> E. भोग and अर्ह fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगावली
भोगावली f. (-ली) Praise, eulogium, the panegyric of professional<BR>encomiasts or bards.<BR> E. भोग enjoyment, आवली a row or range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगावास|भोगावासः
भोगावास m. (-सः) The harem, the inner or women's apartment.<BR> E. भोग<BR>enjoyment, आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिक|भोगिकः
भोगिक m. (-कः) A horse-keeper, a groom.<BR> E. भोग pleasure, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिकान्त|भोगिकांत|भोगिकान्तः
भोगिकान्त m. (-न्तः) Air, wind.<BR> E. भोगि a snake and कान्त friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिन्
भोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Enjoying, possessing, an enjoyer, &c.<BR>	 m. (-गी)<BR>1. A snake.<BR>	 2. A king, a prince.<BR>	 3. A barber.<BR>	 4. The head man<BR>of a village.<BR>	 5. A person who accumulates money for a particular<BR>expenditure.<BR>	 6. The constellation Aśleshā.<BR>	 f. (-गिनी)<BR>	 1. The capital<BR>of the Nāgas.<BR>	 2. A royal concubine.<BR>	 3. Having curves.<BR>	 4. Any<BR>woman of the Royal harem except the crowned queen.<BR> E. भोग<BR>enjoyment, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिवल्लभ|भोगिवल्लभं
भोगिवल्लभ n. (-भं) Sandal.<BR> E. भोगिन् a snake, वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगीन्द्र|भोगींद्र|भोगीन्द्रः
भोगीन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. The serpent ANANTA.<BR>	 2. The serpent VĀSUKĪ. E.<BR>भोगि a snake, इन्द्र a sovereign; also भोगीश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग्य|भोग्यं
भोग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) To be enjoyed.<BR>	 n. (-ग्यं)<BR>	 1. Wealth.<BR>	 2. Grain.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ग्या) A whore.<BR>	 m. (-ग्यः) A pledge that can be used until re-<BR>deemed.<BR> E. भुज् to enjoy, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज|भोजः
भोज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A country, Pātnā and Bhāgalpur.<BR>	 2. The name of a<BR>sovereign of Oujein, or MĀLAVA who is supposed to have flour-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">Page538-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ished about the end of the tenth century; he was a celebrated<BR>patron of learned men, and the nine gems or poets and philoso-<BR>phers, are often ascribed to his æra.<BR>	 3. A cowherd.<BR> E. भुज् to<BR>enjoy, aff. अच् and the final consonant unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजकट|भोजकटः
भोजकट m. (-टः) The country of Bhoja, the present Bhojpur, or the<BR>vicinity of Pātnā and Bhāgalpur.<BR> E. भोज the same, and कट् to go,<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजन|भोजनं|भोजनः
भोजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Food.<BR>	 2. Eating.<BR>	 3. Any object of enjoyment.<BR>	 4.<BR>Wealth.<BR> E. भुज् to eat, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनविशेष|भोजनविशेषः
भोजनविशेष m. (-षः) Choice food, a delicacy.<BR> E. भोजन, विशेष superior sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनव्यग्र
भोजनव्यग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं) Straitened for food.<BR> E. भोजन and ष्यग्र anxious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनाधिकार|भोजनाधिकारः
भोजनाधिकार m. (-रः) Commissariat, stewardship, charge of provender.<BR>E. भोजन, अधिकार superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनीय
भोजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be enjoyed.<BR>	 2. To be eaten.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Food.<BR>E. भुज् to enjoy, aff. अनीयर् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजयित्वा
भोजयित्वा Ind. Having fed.<BR> E. भुज् to eat, causal v., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजाधिप|भोजाधिपः
भोजाधिप m. (-पः) A name of KARṆA, the half brother of the Pāndus.<BR>E. भोज Bhāgalpur, and अधिप sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्य|भोज्यं
भोज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) To be eaten, edible.<BR>	 n. (-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. Food.<BR>	 2. A<BR>dainty.<BR>	 3. Enjoyment.<BR> E. भुज् to eat, ण्यत् aff. and the final<BR>unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्यसम्भव|भोज्यसंभव|भोज्यसंभवः|भोज्यसम्भवः
भोज्यसम्भव m. (-वः) Chyme, the primary juice of the body.<BR> E. भोज्य food, सम्भव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोट|भोटः
भोट m. (-टः) Tibet. “भोटान देशे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोटाङ्ग|भोटांग|भोटाङ्गः
भोटाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A country probably Bhutan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोभो
भोभो Ind. A particle of calling or addressing.<BR> E. भो as above, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोमीरा
भोमीरा f. (-रा) Coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोलि|भोलिः
भोलि m. (-लिः) A camel.<BR> E. भा to shine, उलिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोस्
भोस् Ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of calling or addressing.<BR>	 2. A particle of sor-<BR>row.<BR>	 3. An interrogative particle.<BR> E. भा to shine, aff ङोस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौत|भौतः
भौत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>	 1. Demoniacal, relating to spirits or goblins.<BR>	 2.<BR>Elemental.<BR>	 3. Relating to existing beings.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. An attendant<BR>upon idols.<BR>	 2. A worshipper of spirits and goblins.<BR>	 f. (-ती) Night.<BR>E. भूत a goblin, &c. aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीतिक
भीतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating or appertaining to evil spirits.<BR>	 2.<BR>Elemental.<BR>	 3. Existent.<BR>	 m. (-कः) ŚIVA.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A pearl.<BR> E. भूत a<BR>spirit, &c. ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौम|भौमः
भौम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Earthly, terrestrial, produced in or relating to<BR>the earth.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The planet MARS.<BR>	 2. Hell.<BR>	 3. Ambergris.<BR>4. Water.<BR>	 5. Life.<BR>	 f. (-मी) A name of ŚITĀ.<BR> E. भूमि the earth, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौम|भौमः
भौम (व) न m. (-नः) An epithet of Vishwakarman, the architect of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमरत्न|भौमरत्नं
भौमरत्न n. (-त्नं) Coral.<BR> E. भौम and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमिक|भौमिकः
भौमिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Earthly, terrestrial.<BR> E. भूमि and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौरिक|भौरिकः
भौरिक m. (-कः) The superintendent of gold, the treasurer.<BR> E. भूरि<BR>gold, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौवादिक
भौवादिक f. (-की) Belonging to the class of roots which begins with भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्यस्
भ्यस् r. 1st. cl. (भ्यसते) To fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंश्
भ्रंश् (उ) भ्रंशु r. 4th cl. (भ्रंश्यते) To fall down; also भ्रंस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंश|भ्रंशः
भ्रंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Falling, declining from a height, or from propriety.<BR>2. Falling from or off.<BR>	 3. Decay, ruin.<BR>	 4. Decline.<BR>	 5. Loss.<BR>	 6. Run-<BR>ning away.<BR> E. भ्रन्श् to fall, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंस्
भ्रंस् (उ) भ्रंसु r. 1st cl. (भ्रंसते) To fall down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रकुंस|भ्रकुंसः
भ्रकुंस m. (-सः) An actor wearing female apparel.<BR> E. भ्र for भ्रू the eye-<BR>brow, and कुशि or कुसि to speak, aff. अच्; hence also भ्रकुंश, भ्रूकुंस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रकुटि|भ्रकुटिः
भ्रकुटि f. (-टिः-टी) A frown.<BR> E. भ्र for भ्रू the eyebrow, कुट् to curve, aff.<BR>इन्; also भ्रुकुटि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रक्ष्
भ्रक्ष् r. 1st cl. (भ्रक्षति-ते) To eat; also म्लक्ष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रज्जन|भ्रज्जनं
भ्रज्जन n. (-नं) The act of frying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रण्
भ्रण् r. 1st. cl. (भ्रणति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रन्श्
भ्रन्श् r. 1st. cl. (भ्रंशति) To fall; also भ्रंश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=538-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रम्
भ्रम् (उ) भ्रमु r. 1st cl. (भ्रमति भ्रम्यति) r. 4th cl. (भ्राम्यति)<BR>	 1. To turn round,<BR>to move circularly.<BR>	 2. To be unsteady or unfixed.<BR>	 3. To roam, to<BR>wander; it is also figuratively applicable to mental unsteadiness,<BR>as to err, to wander, to be ignorant or mistaken, &c. With परि,<BR>To wander about. With वि, To play, to wanton. With सम्, 1. To<BR>hurry.<BR>	 2. To honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रम|भ्रमः
भ्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Whirling, going, round.<BR>	 2. Straying, roaming.<BR>	 3.<BR>Error, ignorance, mistake, misapprehension.<BR>	 4. A whirlpool, an<BR>eddy 5. A drain, a water-course.<BR>	 6. A lathe, a potter's wheel, &c.<BR>E. भ्रम् to go round, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमण|भ्रमणं
भ्रमण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Whirling, going round 2. Wandering, literally or<BR>figuratively.<BR>	 3. Erring.<BR>	 4. Giddiness.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A leech.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of game, performed by women for the amusement of a lover<BR>or husband.<BR> E. भ्रम् to go round, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमत्
भ्रमत् mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Going round, whirling, revolving.<BR>	 2. Rov-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Erring.<BR> E. भ्रम् to turn round, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमत्कुटी
भ्रमत्कुटी f. (-टी) An umbrella, a concave mat carried on the head for<BR>that purpose, &c.<BR> E. भ्रमत् and कुटी a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रसर
भ्रसर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) What whirls or goes round.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A large<BR>black bee.<BR>	 2. A lecher, a lover.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Vertigo, epilepsy.<BR> E. भ्रम्<BR>to go round, aff. करन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरक|भ्रमरकः
भ्रमरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Hair curled upon the forehead.<BR>	 2. A bee.<BR>	 3. A ball<BR>for playing with.<BR>	 4. A whirlpool.<BR> E. भ्रमर a bee, &c. कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरकीट|भ्रमरकीटः
भ्रमरकीट m. (-टः) A sort of wasp, that builds a solitary nest in the<BR>angles of walls, doors, &c. (Vespa solitaria.)<BR> E. भ्रमर a bee, and<BR>कीट an insect. “कुमीर पोका” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरप्रिय|भ्रमरप्रियः
भ्रमरप्रिय m. (-यः) The Dhārā-Kadamba tree.<BR> E. भ्रमर a bee, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरविलसिता
भ्रमरविलसिता f. (-ता) A species of the Trishtubh metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरालक|भ्रमरालकः
भ्रमरालक m. (-कः) Hair curled upon the forehead.<BR> E. भ्रमर a bee, and अलक a curl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमासक्त|भ्रमासक्तः
भ्रमासक्त m. (-क्तः) An armourer, a sword-cleaner, a knife-grinder. E.<BR>भ्रम a turning instrument, a grind-stone, and आसक्त diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमि|भ्रमिः
भ्रमि f. (-मि.)<BR>	 1. Whirling, going round.<BR>	 2. Error, blunder, mistake.<BR>	 3.<BR>A lathe, a potter's wheel.<BR>	 4. A whirlpool.<BR> E. भ्रम् to turn round,<BR>Unādi aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमिन्
भ्रमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिणी-मि) Whirling, going round, or about.<BR> E. भ्रम् to go<BR>round, aff. घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रश्
भ्रश् (उ) भ्रशु r. 4th cl. (भ्रश्यति) To fall down; also भृश and भ्रंश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रशिमन्
भ्रशिमन् m. (-मा) Vehimence.<BR> E. भृश्-इसनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्ट|भ्रष्टं
भ्रष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, lost.<BR>	 2. Vicious, depraved, fallen<BR>from virtue.<BR>	 3. Fried, parched.<BR> E. भ्रंश् to fall, or भ्रसज् to fry, क्त<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टराज्य
भ्रष्टराज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) Deposed, deprived of a kingdom.<BR> E. भ्रष्ट and राज्य principality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रस्ज्
भ्रस्ज् (औ) औभ्रस्जौ r. 6th cl. (भृज्जति-ते) To broil or fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राज्
भ्राज् (टु, ऋ) टुभ्राजृ r. 1st cl. (भ्राजते) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजक|भ्राजकं
भ्राजक n. (-कं) Bile, the bilious humour.<BR>	 f. (-जिका) Making bright. E.<BR>भ्राज् to shine, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजथु|भ्राजथुः
भ्राजथु f. (-थुः) Brilliance, splendour, beauty.<BR> E. भ्राज् to shine, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजथुमत्|भ्राजथुमन्त्
भ्राजथुमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Splendid.<BR>	 2. Beautiful.<BR> E. भ्राजथु and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिष्णु|भ्राजिष्णुः
भ्राजिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Elegant, splendid, radiant in ornament and<BR>vesture.<BR> E. भ्राज् to shine, aff. इष्णुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृ
भ्रातृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A brother, a uterine brother.<BR>	 2. A relative.<BR>	 3. A term<BR>of friendly address. Dual only, (-री) Brother and sister.<BR> E. भ्राज्<BR>to shine, Unādi aff. तृच्, and the radical final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृक|भ्रातृकः
भ्रातृक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Fraternal, brotherly, of or belonging to a<BR>brother.<BR> E. भ्रातृ a brother, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृज|भ्रातृजः
भ्रातृज m. (-जः) A brother's son.<BR> E. भ्रातृ a brother, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्रिजाया
भ्रात्रिजाया f. (-या) A sister-in-law, a brother's wife.<BR> E. भ्रातृ a brother,<BR>and जाया a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भातृद्वितीया
भातृद्वितीया f. (-या) The second day of the first-half of KĀRTIKA when<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">Page539-b+ 60</a>]<BR>sisters entertain their brothers in consequence of the Yamunā<BR>once having entertained her brother Yama on that day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृपत्री
भ्रातृपत्री f. (-त्री) A brother's wife.<BR> E. भ्रातृ, and पत्नी a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृभगिनी
भ्रातृभगिनी Dual only, (-न्यौ) A brother and sister.<BR> E. भ्रातृ a brother<BR>and भगिनी a sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृबल
भ्रातृबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Having a brother.<BR> E. भ्रातृ, वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृव्य|भ्रातृव्यः
भ्रातृव्य m. (-व्यः)<BR>	 1. A brother's son.<BR>	 2. An enemy.<BR> E. भ्रातृ a brother, व्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृश्वशुर|भ्रातृश्वशुरः
भ्रातृश्वशुर m. (-रः) A husband's elder brother.<BR> E. भ्रातृ a brother, and<BR>श्वशुर a father-in-law, (as it were.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्रीय|भ्रात्रीयः
भ्रात्रीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fraternal, belonging or relating to a brother.<BR>m. (-यः) A brother's son.<BR> E. भ्रातृ a brother, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्त|भ्रांत|भ्रान्तः
भ्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Whirled, revolved.<BR>	 2. Blundering, mistaken.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. An elephant in rut.<BR>	 2. The Dhuturā plant.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Moving about.<BR>	 2. Error.<BR> E. भ्रम् to revolve, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्ति|भ्रांति|भ्रांतिः|भ्रान्तिः
भ्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Error, mistake, ignorance.<BR>	 2. Going round, whirl-<BR>ing, revolving.<BR>	 3. Unsteadiness, locomotion.<BR>	 4. Going about, wan-<BR>dering.<BR>	 5. Confusion.<BR>	 6. Delusion.<BR>	 7. Doubt.<BR> E. भ्रम् to go round,<BR>aff. क्तिन्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तिमत्|भ्रांतिमत्|भ्रान्तिमन्त्
भ्रान्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Erring, mistaking.<BR>	 2. Wandering.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-मान्) A figure of speech (in rhetoric.)<BR> E. भ्रान्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तिहर|भ्रांतिहर|भ्रान्तिहरः
भ्रान्तिहर m. (-रः) A counsellor, a minister.<BR> E. भ्रान्ति error, and हर who<BR>repels or removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राम|भ्रामः
भ्राम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Wandering, roving.<BR>	 2. Error.<BR> E. भ्रम् to turn round, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामक|भ्रामकः
भ्रामक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A jackal.<BR>	 2. A cheat, a rogue.<BR>	 3. A sort of load-<BR>stone.<BR>	 4. The sun-flower.<BR> E. भ्रम् to turn round, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामयत्
भ्रामयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Whirling round.<BR>	 2. Bewildering.<BR> E. भ्रम्<BR>to wander or whirl, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामर|भ्रामरं|भ्रामरः
भ्रामर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Whirling, going round.<BR>	 2. A dance performed in a<BR>ring round-about.<BR>	 3. A village.<BR>	 4. Epilepsy, 5. A honey.<BR>	 6. A<BR>mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A sort of loadstone.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>1. A name of PĀRVATĪ from her having assumed the form of<BR>a bee, in order to contend with MAHĀSUR.<BR>	 2. Yogiṇī, or<BR>female attendant on DURGĀ.<BR> E. भ्रमर a bee, &c. aff. अण् or घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामरिन्
भ्रामरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Whirling, revolving.<BR>	 2. Epileptic, giddy.<BR>3. Made of honey or from a bee, &c.<BR> E. भ्रामर, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राग्यत्
भ्राग्यत् mfn. (-म्यन्-म्यती-म्यत्)<BR>	 1. Wandering about, roving, roaming.<BR>	 2.<BR>Erring, deviating.<BR> E. भ्रम् to wander, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राश्
भ्राश् (-टु, ऋ) टुभ्राशृ r. 1st cl. (भ्राशते भ्राश्यते) To shine. Also म्लाश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्र|भ्राष्ट्रं|भ्राष्ट्रः
भ्राष्ट्र mfn. (-ष्ट्रः-ष्ट्री-ष्ट्रं) Fried in a pan.<BR>	 mn. (-ष्ट्रः-ष्ट्रं) A frying-pan.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ष्ट्रः) Light.<BR> E. भ्रस्ज् to fry, Unādi aff. ष्ट्रन्; and in the attributive,<BR>अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रास्
भ्रास् r. 1st cl. (भ्रासते, भ्रास्यते) To shine, also म्लास् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्री
भ्री r. 9th cl. (भ्रीणाति भ्रिणीते)<BR>	 1. To fear.<BR>	 2. To help.<BR>	 3. To cherish, to<BR>maintain or support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुकुंस|भ्रुकुंसः
भ्रुकुंस m. (-सः) An actor in female apparel.<BR> E. भ्रु for भ्रू an eyebrow,<BR>कुसि or कुशि to shine or speak, aff. अच्; hence also भ्रूकुंस भ्रुकुंश, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुकुटि|भ्रुकुटिः
भ्रुकुटि f. (-टिः-टी) A frown.<BR> E. भ्रु for भ्रू an eyebrow, कुट् to make crook-<BR>ed, इन् aff.: see भ्रूकुटि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुड्
भ्रुड् r. 6th cl. (भ्रुडति)<BR>	 1. To cover.<BR>	 2. To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रू
भ्रू f. (-भ्रूः) An eyebrow.<BR> E. भ्रम् to round, Unādi aff. डु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूकुंस|भ्रूकुंसः
भ्रूकुंस m. (-सः) A male actor in female apparel.<BR> E. भ्रू the eyebrow,<BR>कुसि to speak or shine, aff. अच्; also from कुशि, भ्रूकुंश; this word<BR>is variously written भ्रुकुंश or भ्रुकुंस, भृकुंश or भृकुंस, and भ्रकुंश or<BR>भ्रकुंस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूकुटि|भ्रूकुटिः
भ्रूकुटि f. (-टिः-टी) A frown, a look of displeasure.<BR> E. भ्रू the brow, कुट् to<BR>be curved, aff. इन् and ङीप् optionally added; it is also written<BR>variously, like the last, and occurs भ्रुकुटि, भृकुटि, or भ्रकुटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूक्षेप|भ्रूक्षेपः
भ्रूक्षेप m. (-पः) A frown.<BR> E. भ्रू, and क्षेप throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूण्
भ्रूण् r. 10th cl. (भ्रूणयते)<BR>	 1. To hope, to trust.<BR>	 2. To confide, to be with-<BR>out doubt.<BR>	 3. To wish for, to desire.<BR>	 4. To fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=539-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूण|भ्रूणः
भ्रूण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The embryo or fœtus.<BR>	 2. A child.<BR> E. भ्रूण to hope, to<BR>fear, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूणघ्न
भ्रूणघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Producing or causing abortion, who or what<BR>does so.<BR> E. भ्रूण, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूणहत्या
भ्रूणहत्या f. (-त्या)<BR>	 1. Murder of the fœtus, procuring or causing abor-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. Any sin equally heinous.<BR> E. भ्रूण, and हत्या killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूणहन्
भ्रूणहन् mf. (-हा-घ्नी)<BR>	 1. One who occasions or procures abortion.<BR>	 2.<BR>The murderer of a Brāhman.<BR> E. भ्रूण the embryo, (or any thing<BR>of which the death is equally heinous.) and हन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूभङ्ग|भ्रूभंग|भ्रूभङ्गः
भ्रूभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A frown.<BR> E. भ्रू the brow, भङ्ग a breaking, bending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूविलास|भ्रूविलासः
भ्रूविलास m. (-सः) Playful motion of the eyebrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेज्
भ्रेज् (ऋ) भ्रेजृ r. 1st cl. (भ्रेजते) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेश्
भ्रेश् (ऋ) भ्रेशृ r. 1st cl. (भ्रेशति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To fall.<BR>	 3. To be angry.<BR>	 4. To fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेश
भ्रेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Going.<BR>	 2. Loss.<BR>	 3. Deviation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेष्
भ्रेष् (ऋ) भ्रेषृ r. 1st cl. (-भ्रेषति-ते) To go, to move, to fear: see भ्रेश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेष|भ्रेषः
भ्रेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Deviation from rectitude, declining or falling from<BR>virtue, &c.<BR>	 2. Going, proceeding.<BR>	 3. Loss.<BR> E. भ्रेष् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रेषण|भ्रेषणं
भ्रेषण n. (-णं) Going, moving.<BR> E. भ्रेष् to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लक्ष्
भ्लक्ष् r. 1st cl. (भ्लक्षति-ते) To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लाश्
भ्लाश् (टृ, ऋ) टुम्लाशृ r. 1st cl. (भ्लाश्यते भ्लाशते) To shine; sometimes भ्लास्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लेष्
भ्लेष् (ऋ) म्लेषृ r. 1st cl. (भ्लेषति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To fear: see भ्रेष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म|मः
म The twenty-fifth consonant of the Nāgari alphabet, corresponding<BR>to the letter M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म|मः
म m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. YAMA.<BR>	 5.<BR>Time, season.<BR>	 6. Poison, venom.<BR>	 7. A magical or mystical verse<BR>or formula.<BR>	 8. The moon.<BR>	 9. The abbreviated name of the fourth<BR>note of the gamut.<BR>	 f. (मा)<BR>	 1. A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. A mother.<BR>3. Measure.<BR>	 4. Light, lustre.<BR>	 5. Knowledge.<BR>	 6. Binding, tying.<BR>	 7.<BR>Death.<BR>	 8. A woman's waist.<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Good-fortune, auspicious-<BR>ness.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR> E. मा to measure, क aff.; or मन् to worship, &c.,<BR>aff. ड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्
मक् (इ) मकि r. 1st cl. (मङ्कते)<BR>	 1. To decorate, to grace or adorn.<BR>	 2. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकर|मकरः
मकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A marine monster, confounded usually with the<BR>crocodile and shark, but properly a fabulous animal: as a fish it<BR>might be conjectured to be the horned-shark, or the unicorn fish;<BR>but it is often drawn, as it in the pictured sign Capricornus of the<BR>zodiac, with the head and forelegs of an antelope, and the body<BR>and tail of a fish: it is the emblem of the god of love.<BR>	 2. One of<BR>the signs of zodiac, corresponding with the above, and like<BR>the Greek representation of that sign, being an animal in<BR>the foreparts, and ending in the tail of a fish. One of the nine<BR>treasures of KUVERA.<BR>	 3. A particular array of troops, in the form<BR>of a Makara.<BR>	 4. An ear-ring in that shape.<BR> E. म for मुख the mouth,<BR>कृ to scatter, aff. अच्; or माङ् prohibitive aff., कृ to do, अच् aff.,<BR>form irr.; grammarians however, sometimes consider this word<BR>as a primitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरकेतन|मकरकेतनः
मकरकेतन m. (-नः) KĀMA, the Hindu CUPID.<BR> E. मकर, a marine monster<BR>and केतन emblem; being painted on KĀMA'S banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरकेतु|मकरकेतुः
मकरकेतु m. (-तुः) KĀMA: see the preceding.<BR> E. मकर, and केतु an emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरध्वज|मकरध्वजः
मकरध्वज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. KĀMA: see the two last.<BR>	 2. A particular array of<BR>troops.<BR>	 3. A particular medical preparation.<BR> E. मकर Makara, and<BR>ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरन्द|मकरंदः|मकरन्दः
मकरन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. The nectar or honey of a flower.<BR>	 2. The Kokila<BR>or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 3. A bee.<BR>	 4. A fragrant kind of mango.<BR>	 5. A<BR>kind of jasmine, (Jasminum pubescens.)<BR>	 6. The filament of a lotus.<BR>E. मकर the emblem of KĀMA, and दो to destroy, i. e. to surpass,<BR>as an incentive to love, aff. क, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरन्दवती
मकरन्दवती f. (-ती) The trumpet flower, (Bignonia suave-olens.) E.<BR>मकरन्द honey, and मतुप् aff., fem. form. “पाटला वृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरसप्तमी
मकरसप्तमी f. (-मी) The seventh day in the first half of the month<BR>māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकराकर|मकराकरः
मकराकर m. (-रः) The ocean.<BR> E. मकर a marine monster, and आकर receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकराकार|मकराकारः
मकराकार m. (-रः) A plant, said to be a species of Karañja or Cæsal-<BR>pinia.<BR> E. मकर a fish, आकार form. “कांँटा करम्जा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकराङ्क|मकरांक|मकराङ्कः
मकराङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR> E. मकर a marine mons-<BR>ter. and अङ्क mark, emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरालय|मकरालयः
मकरालय m. (-यः) The ocean.<BR> E. मकर a sort of fish, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकराश्व|मकराश्वः
मकराश्व m. (-श्वः) VARUṆA.<BR> E. मकर a marine monster, and अश्व a horse;<BR>riding on the Makara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकरिन्
मकरिन् m. (-री) The ocean.<BR> E. मकर a marine monster, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुट|मकुटं
मकुट n. (-टं) A crest, a head-dress, a crown, a tiara.<BR> E. मकि to adorn,<BR>aff. उट form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुति|मकुतिः
मकुति f. (-तिः) An edict or order of the government, addressed to the<BR>Śūdra tribe, or to a Śūdra.<BR> E. मकि-उति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुर|मकुरः
मकुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A mirror.<BR>	 2. The stick of a potter's wheel.<BR>	 3. An un-<BR>blown flower.<BR>	 4. A tree with light yellow, and fragrant flowers,<BR>(Mimusops elengi.)<BR> E. मकि to adorn, उरच् Unādi aff. and deriv.<BR>irr.; also मुकुर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुल|मकुलः
मकुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. An opening bud.<BR>	 2. A kind of tree, (Mimusops elen-<BR>gi.)<BR> E. मकि to adorn, उलच् aff., deriv. irr. “वकुल वृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुष्टक|मकुष्टकः
मकुष्टक m. (-कः) A kind of kidney-bean, a wild variety, perhaps of the<BR>Phaseolus mungo.<BR> E. मकु irrly. derivd, from मक् to adorn, ष्टक् to<BR>impede, aff. अच्; also मकुष्ठक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुष्ठ|मकुष्ठः
मकुष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्टा-ष्ठं) Going lazily, slowly, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः) A sort of rice.<BR>E. मकि to adorn, aff. उ, deriv. irr. मकु, and स्था to stand, aff. क.<BR>also मुकुष्ठ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकुष्ठक|मकुष्ठकः
मकुष्ठक m. (-कः) A sort of kidney-bean.<BR> E. मकु ornament: (see the<BR>two last;) स्था to stay or be, aff. क्वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मकूलक|मकूलकः
मकूलक m. (-कः) A plant commonly Dantī.<BR> E. मकि to adorn, ऊलच् aff. and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्क्
मक्क् r.<BR>	 1. cl. (मक्कते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्कूल
मक्कूल n. (-लं) A mineral substance, considered variously to be chalk or<BR>benzoin.<BR> E. मक्क् to go, to be, aff. ऊलच् । “शिलाजतु” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्कोल|मक्कोलः
मक्कोल m. (-लः) Chalk: see the last.<BR> E. मक्क् to go, ओलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्ष्
मक्ष् r. 1st cl. (मक्षति)<BR>	 1. To fill.<BR>	 2. To be angry.<BR>	 3. To mix, to combine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्ष|मक्षः
मक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. Hypocrisy, slyness, concealment of one's own defects.<BR>2. Multitude.<BR> E. मक्ष् to fill. aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षिका
मक्षिका f. (-का) A fly.<BR> E. मक्ष् to be angry, Unādi aff. सिकन्; or मक्ष् the same, क्कुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मक्षीका
मक्षीका f. (-का) A fly. E. See the last, the pen. vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख|मखः
मख r. 1st cl. (मखति) also (इ) मखि (मङ्क्षति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मख|मखः
मख m. (-खः) Sacrifice, oblation.<BR> E. मख् to go, aff. घञ् or घ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखत्रातृ
मखत्रातृ m. (-ता) RĀMA, the son of DASARATHA, and second incarnation<BR>of VIṢṆU so named.<BR> E. मख sacrifice, and त्रातृ who preserves; his<BR>first exploit being the discomfiture of the Rākshasas, who dis-<BR>turbed the sacrifices of VISWĀMITRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखवह्नि|मखवह्निः
मखवह्नि m. (-ह्निः) Sacrificial-fire.<BR> E. मख sacrifice, and वह्नि fire; also<BR>similar compounds, as मखाग्नि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखानल|मखानलः
मखानल m. (-लः) Sacrificial-fire.<BR> E. मख and अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मखासुहृद्
मखासुहृद् m. (-द) ŚIVA.<BR> E. मख् sacrifice, here meaning the sacrifice<BR>offered by DAKṢA and असुहृद् unfriendly; having disturbed the<BR>ceremony, and slain the sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मग्
मग् (इ) मगि r. 1st cl. (मङ्गति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगध|मगधः
मगध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A country, South Behar.<BR>	 2. An inhabitant of that<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">Page541-a+ 60</a>]<BR>country.<BR>	 3. A bard, whose peculiar province is to sing the praises<BR>of a chief's ancestry in his presence, a family bard or minstrel.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-धा)<BR>	 1. Long pepper.<BR>	 2. The town of the Magadhas.<BR> E. मगध a<BR>Kandwādi verb, to ask, aff. अच्; or मगध the country, अण् aff.,<BR>with alteration of the vowel optional; hence also मागध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=540-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगधेश्वर|मगधेश्वरः
मगधेश्वर m. (-रः) A name of JARA SANDHA.<BR> E. मगध South Bihar, ईश्वर king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मग्न|मग्नः
मग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Plunged, dived, immersed.<BR>	 2. Sunk, drowned.<BR>	 3.<BR>Absorbed.<BR> E. मस्ज् to plunge into water, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघ्
मघ् (इ) मघि r. 1st cl. (मङ्घते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To begin moving.<BR>	 3.<BR>To begin.<BR>	 4. To move swiftly.<BR>	 5. To blame.<BR>	 6. To gamble.<BR>	 7. To<BR>cheat, to be addicted to dishonest practices. (मङ्घति) To decorate,<BR>to adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघ|मघः
मघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. One of the Dwīpas or divisions of the universe.<BR>	 2. A<BR>country, that of the modern Mugs, or Ārrākān.<BR>	 3. A drug.<BR>	 4.<BR>Pleasure, happiness.<BR>	 5. A kind of medicine.<BR>	 n. (-घं) A kind of<BR>flower.<BR>	 f. (-घा) The tenth lunar asterism, containing five stars<BR>figured by a house: it is sometimes considered to be confined to<BR>the plural number. (मघाः)<BR>	 f. (-घा-घी) A sort of grain.<BR> E. मह to wor-<BR>ship, aff. कन् and ह changed to घ; or मघि-अच् पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघवत्|मघवन्त्
मघवत् m. (-वान्) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. मघ happiness, (of paradise<BR>or Svarga,) मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघवन्
मघवन् m. (-वा)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. One of the twelve Chakravartis, or uni-<BR>versal monarchs of the Jainas.<BR>	 3. An epithet of Vyāsa 4. An owl.<BR>E. मह to sacrifice, कनिन् Unādi aff. and वुक् augment, form irr.;<BR>before the vowel affs. of the second case plural, and the last five<BR>cases, the व of this word is changed to उ, and thence becomes ओ<BR>as usual, as मघोनः, मघोना, मघोने, &c.; also with ङीष् aff. the fem.<BR>form is मघीनी f. (-नी) Sāchi, the wife of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघाभव|मघाभवः
मघाभव m. (-वः) The planet VENUS.<BR> E. मघा the asterism, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मघाभू
मघाभू m. (-भूः) SUKRA.<BR> E. मघा and भू born; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्किल|मंकिल|मंकिलः|मङ्किलः
मङ्किल m. (-लः) A fire in a forest.<BR> E. मकि to adorn, aff. इलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्कुर|मंकुर|मंकुरः|मङ्कुरः
मङ्कुर m. (-रः) A mirror.<BR> E. मकि to adorn, उरच् aff., and the nasal re-<BR>tained; also मकुर and मुकुर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्तृ
मङ्क्तृ mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>	 1. Bathing or drowning; any thing, or person.<BR>2. Cleaning any thing by immersion.<BR> E. मस्ज् to bathe, aff. तृच्,<BR>and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्षण|मंक्षण|मंक्षणं|मङ्क्षणं
मङ्क्षण n. (-णं) Cuisses or greaves, armour for the thighs or legs.<BR> E. मङ्क्ष-<BR>ल्युट् aff.; it is sometimes read मङ्क्षुण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्षु|मंक्षु
मङ्क्षु Ind.<BR>	 1. Quickly, Swiftly, instantly.<BR>	 2. Much, exceedingly.<BR> E. मस्ज्<BR>to purify, सु aff., and नुम् augment; also मङ्खु.<BR> E. मखि-उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्क्षुण|मंक्षुण|मङ्क्षुणं
मङ्क्षुण n. (-णं) Cuisses or greaves, armour for the thighs or legs;<BR>a sort of iron chain-work petticoat, coming down to the knees,<BR>is still worn in some parts of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्ख|मंख|मंखः|मङ्खः
मङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>	 1. A royal bard.<BR>	 2. A mendicant of a particular<BR>order.<BR> E. मखि to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्ग|मंग|मंगः|मङ्गः
मङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The head of a boat.<BR> E. मगि to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल|मंगल|मङ्गलं|मङ्गलः
मङ्गल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Lucky, fortunate, prosperous, faring well or<BR>happily.<BR>	 2. Brave.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Happiness, good-fortune.<BR>	 2. Preserving<BR>property, taking care of what has been gained.<BR>	 3. Prudence, care-<BR>fulness.<BR>	 3. A good woman.<BR>	 4. Festivity.<BR>	 5. Turmeric.<BR>	 6. An ancient<BR>custom.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The planet MARS.<BR>	 2. Burnt offering on various<BR>occasions of rejoicing.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A name of UMĀ, the wife of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A bent grass, (Panicum dactylon,) with white blossoms.<BR>3. A virtuous and obedient wife.<BR>	 4. The mother of the fifth Jina<BR>or Jaina teacher SUMATĪ.<BR>	 5. A species of Cæsalpinia.<BR> E. मगि to<BR>go, अलच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलच्छाय|मंगलच्छाय|मङ्गलच्छायः
मङ्गलच्छाय m. (-यः) Waved-leaf fig-tree, (Ficus infectoria.)<BR> E. मङ्गल pros-<BR>perous, lucky, and छाया shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलदेवता|मंगलदेवता
मङ्गलदेवता f. (-ता) A tutelary deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलपाठक|मंगलपाठक|मङ्गलपाठकः
मङ्गलपाठक m. (-कः) A bard, an encomiast.<BR> E. मङ्गल good fortune, and पाठक who reads or recites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलप्रतिसर|मंगलप्रतिसर|मङ्गलप्रतिसरः
मङ्गलप्रतिसर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An auspicious string worn by married women<BR>round the neck.<BR>	 2. The cord of an amulet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलप्रदा
मङ्गलप्रदा f. (-दा) Turmeric.<BR> E. मङ्गल auspiciousness, and प्रदा bestowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलाक्षत|मंगलाक्षत
मङ्गलाक्षत m. (-तः) Rice thrown by Brāhmans upon people in bestow-<BR>ing a blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलाचरण|मंगलाचरण
मङ्गलाचरण n. (-णं) An auspicious introduction in the shape of a prayer<BR>at the beginning of an undertaking or of any written work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गलाष्टक|मंगलाष्टक
मङ्गलाष्टक n. (-कं) A benedictory stanza repeated by priests for good<BR>luck on the bride and bridegroom at the time of wedding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल्य|मंगल्य|मङ्गल्यं|मङ्गल्यः
मङ्गल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Auspicious, propitious, conferring happi-<BR>ness, prosperity, &c.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, pleasing, agreeable.<BR>	 2. Pure,<BR>pious.<BR>	 m. (-ल्यः)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Trayamāna.<BR>	 2. The<BR>holy fig-tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>	 3. The Vilwa, (Ægle marme-<BR>los.)<BR>	 4. A sort of pulse, (Cicer lens.)<BR>	 5. The cocoanut-tree.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ल्या)<BR>	 1. A fragrant sort of Agallochum or aloe wood.<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of Mimosa, (M. Suma, Rox.)<BR>	 3. A herb, commonly<BR>Gojihvā, (Hieracium or according to Rox's Catalogue, a herb<BR>of the same class, Elephantopus scaber.)<BR>	 4. A sort of grass,<BR>(Andropogun aciculatum.)<BR>	 5. A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>6. A sort or perfume, commonly Rochanā.<BR>	 7. A kind of Orris root,<BR>(Acorus calamus.)<BR>	 n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Sour curds.<BR>	 2. Sandal.<BR>	 3. Red lead.<BR>4. Gold.<BR>	 5. Water brought from various sacred places for the<BR>coronation of a king.<BR> E. मङ्गल prosperous and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल्यक|मंगल्यक|मंगल्यकः|मङ्गल्यकः
मङ्गल्यक m. (-कः) Lentils, (Cicer lens.)<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गल्यनामधेया
मङ्गल्यनामधेया f. (-या) A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR> E. मङ्गल्य auspicious,<BR>नामधेया appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मङ्गिनी|मंगिनी
मङ्गिनी f. (-नी) A boat.<BR> E. मङ्ग the head of a boat, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मच्
मच् also (इ) मचि r. 1st cl. (मचते मञ्चते)<BR>	 1. To be vain or proud.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be wicked.<BR>	 3. To speak.<BR>	 4. To pound or grind. मचि r. 1st cl. (मञ्चते)<BR>1. To hold or have.<BR>	 2. To be high or tall.<BR>	 3. To revere, to adore,<BR>to worship.<BR>	 4. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मचर्च्चिका|मचर्चिका
मचर्च्चिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Excellence, happiness.<BR>	 2. (In apposition,) Best,<BR>excellent, (the gender is unchanged.)<BR> E. म ŚIVA, चर्च्च to worship,<BR>affs. ण्वुल् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मच्चित्त
मच्चित्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Who or what has the mind fixed on me, (God.)<BR>E. मत् me, चित्त mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मच्छ|मच्छः
मच्छ m. (-च्छः) A fish in general.<BR> E. मद् to delight, and श aff., form irr. see मत्स्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जकृत्
मज्जकृत् n. (-कृत्) A bone.<BR> E. मज्ज marrow and कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जत्
मज्जत् mfn. (-ज्जन्-ज्जन्ती-ज्जत्) Plunging in or into, being immersed, dip-<BR>ping, drowning.<BR> E. मस्ज् to be immersed, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जन्
मज्जन् m. (-ज्जा)<BR>	 1. The marrow of the bone and flesh.<BR>	 2. The pith or<BR>sap of trees, &c.<BR> E. सस्ज् to be immersed, (in the centre of the<BR>bones, &c.) and कनिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जन|मज्जनं|मज्जनः
मज्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Bathing, ablution.<BR>	 2. Immersion.<BR>	 3. Drowning.<BR>	 4.<BR>Marrow.<BR> E. मस्ज् to bathe, &c. aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जसमुद्भव|मज्जसमुद्भवं|मज्जसमुद्भवः
मज्जसमुद्भव n. (-वं) Semen Virile.<BR> E. मज्ज marrow, समुद्भव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जा
मज्जा f. (-ज्जा) Marrow, pith, sap.<BR> E. मज्जन् marrow and अच्-टाप् aff.:<BR>see मज्जन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जारजस्
मज्जारजस् n. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Hell.<BR>	 2. Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जारस|मज्जारसः
मज्जारस m. (-सः) Semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जासार|मज्जासारं|मज्जासारः
मज्जासार n. (-रं) Nutmeg. “जातीफले ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जिका
मज्जिका f. (-का) The female of the Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मज्जषा
मज्ज षा f. (-षा) A basket. E. See मञ्जूषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्च्|मंच्
मञ्च् (उ) मञ्चु r. 1st cl. (मञ्चति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्च|मंच|मंचः|मञ्चः
मञ्च m. (-ञ्चः)<BR>	 1. A bed, a bedstead 2. A platform, a scaffold.<BR>	 3. An ele-<BR>vated shed raised on bamboos in a cornfield, &c., where a watch-<BR>man is stationed to protect the corn from cattle, birds, wild<BR>beasts, &c.<BR>	 4. A sort of throne or chair of state, or the platform<BR>on which it is raised, the dais.<BR> E. मचि to be high or tall,<BR>aff. धञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=541-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्चक|मंचक|मंचकं|मञ्चकः
मञ्चक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A bed, a bedstead.<BR>	 2. A platform, a scaffold.<BR>	 3. A<BR>stand for holding fire.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्चकाश्रय|मंचकाश्रय|मञ्चकाश्रयः
मञ्चकाश्रय m. (-यः) A bug.<BR> E. मञ्चक a bed, and आश्रय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्चमण्डप|मञ्चमण्डपः
मञ्चमण्डप m. (-पः) A sort of temporary open shed, a platform erected<BR>for particular ceremonies, as marriages, &c.<BR> E. मञ्च a scaffold, and<BR>मण्डप a temporary hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्ज्|मंज्
मञ्ज् r. 10th cl. (मञ्जयति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To clean, to purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जर|मंजर|मंजरं|मञ्जरं
मञ्जर nf. (-रं-री)<BR>	 1. A pearl.<BR>	 2. A compound pedicle.<BR>	 3. A sort of plant,<BR>commonly Tilaka.<BR> E. मञ्जु beautiful, ऋ to go or be, aff. अप्, deriv.<BR>irr.; or मन्ज्-अरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरि|मंजरि|मंजरिः|मञ्जरिः
मञ्जरि f. (-रिः-री)<BR>	 1. A compound pedicle, a fruit or flower-stalk.<BR>	 2. A<BR>A large pearl.<BR>	 3. A plant, commonly Tilaka.<BR>	 4. A line.<BR>	 5. A<BR>creeper.<BR>	 6. The holy-basil.<BR>	 mf. (-रिः-री) A shoot, a sprout.<BR> E. मञ्जु<BR>beautiful, ऋ to go, or be, aff. इ, deriv. irr., ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरिचामर|मंजरिचामर
मञ्जरिचामर n. (-रं) A fan-like sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरित|मंजरित
मञ्जरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Mounted on a stalk, (a bud, &c.)<BR> E. मञ्जर and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जरिनम्र|मंजरिनम्र|मञ्जरिनम्रः
मञ्जरिनम्र m. (-म्रः) The Vetasa plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जा|मंजा
मञ्जा f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>	 1. A compound pedicle: see the last.<BR>	 2. A she-goat.<BR>	 3.<BR>A creeper.<BR> E. मजि to sound, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जि|मंजि|मंजिः|मञ्जिः
मञ्जि f. (-ञ्जिः-ञ्जी) A compound pedicle; also मञ्जरी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिका|मंजिका
मञ्जिका f. (-का) A harlot, a whore.<BR> E. मजि-ण्वुलु-टाप् अत इत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिफला|मंजिफला
मञ्जिफला f. (-ला) The plantain, (Musa sapientum.)<BR> E. मञ्जि a foot-stalk,<BR>and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिमन्|मंजिमन्
मञ्जिमन् n. (म) Beauty, elegance.<BR> E. मञ्जु handsome, इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिष्ठा|मंजिष्ठा
मञ्जिष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा) Bengal madder, a plant used in medicine, and in dy-<BR>ing, (Rubia Manjith, Rox.)<BR> E. मञ्जु beautiful, स्था to stay or be, क<BR>aff., deriv. irr.; or मञ्जि a compound pedicle, and स्थ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जिष्ठाराग|मंजिष्ठाराग|मञ्जिष्ठारागः
मञ्जिष्ठाराग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The dye of madder.<BR>	 2. An attachment as dura-<BR>ble as the colour of the Indian madder, permanent attachment,<BR>(figuratively.)<BR> E. मञ्जिष्ठा and राग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जीर|मंजीर|मंजीरं|मंजीरः|मञ्जीरः
मञ्जीर n. (-रं) An ornament for the feet or toes.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A post, round<BR>which passes the string that works the stick of a churn.<BR> E. मन्ज् to<BR>sound, aff. ईरन्; also with कन् added मञ्जीरक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जील|मंजील|मंजीलः|मञ्जीलः
मञ्जील m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A village, inhabited chiefly by washermen.<BR>	 2. An<BR>anklet.<BR> E. मञ्ज् to sound, ईरन् aff. and र changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जु|मंजु
मञ्जु mfn. (-ञ्जुः-ञ्जुः-ञ्जु) Beautiful, pleasing, agreeable.<BR> E. मन्ज् to clean,<BR>aff. उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुकेशिन्|मंजुकेशिन्
मञ्जुकेशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Beautiful-haired.<BR>	 m. (-शी) A name of<BR>KṚṢṆA, or VIṢṆU in that form.<BR> E. मञ्जु beautiful, केश hair,<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुगमना|मंजुगमना
मञ्जुगमना f. (-ना) A goose.<BR> E. मञ्जु beautiful, elegant, and गमन gait.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुगुञ्ज|मंजुगुंज|मञ्जुगुञ्जः
मञ्जुगुञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः) A charming murmur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुघोष|मञ्जुघोषः
मञ्जुघोष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Having a sweet voice or cry.<BR>	 m. (-षः) One of<BR>the Bauddha teachers.<BR>	 f. (-षा) One of the Apsarās or courtezans<BR>of Svarga.<BR> E. मञ्जु agreeable, and घोष sound, voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुनाशी|मंजुनाशी
मञ्जुनाशी f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. The wife of INDRA.<BR>	 3. A<BR>handsome woman.<BR> E. मञ्जु beautiful and नाश destruction; putting<BR>every other beauty to shame by their superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुपाठक|मंजुपाठक|मञ्जुपाठकः
मञ्जुपाठक m. (-कः) A parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुप्राण|मंजुप्राण|मञ्जुप्राणः
मञ्जुप्राण m. (-णः) A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. मञ्जु pleasing and प्राण life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुभद्र|मञ्जुभद्रः
मञ्जुभद्र m. (-द्रः) Bauddha; also called Manjughosha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुभाषिन्
मञ्जुभाषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Speaking sweetly or pleasantly.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1.<BR>A woman speaking kindly.<BR>	 2. A species of Atijagatī metre.<BR> E. मञ्जु<BR>and भाषिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुल|मंजुल|मञ्जुलं|मञ्जुलः
मञ्जुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Beautiful, agreeable, pleasing.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A galli-<BR>nule.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A natural water-course or channel, a spring, a<BR>well.<BR>	 2. An arbour, a bower.<BR>	 3. An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria<BR>octandra.)<BR> E. मञ्जु handsome, ला to be, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुवक्त्र|मंजुवक्त्र
मञ्जुवक्त्र mfn. (-क्त्रः-क्त्रा-क्त्रं) Lovely, handsome.<BR> E. मञ्जु beautiful, वक्त्र the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जुश्री
मञ्जुश्री m. (-श्रीः) A Bauddha saint: see मञ्जुघोष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मञ्जूषा|मंजूषा
मञ्जूषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. A basket, a large basket, 2. A stone.<BR>	 3. Bengal mād-<BR>der.<BR>	 4. The case in which the great bow that RĀMA broke, was<BR>kept.<BR> E. मन्ज् to make pure or clean by ablution, Unādi aff. ऊषन्,<BR>and the nasal augment; also with a short vowel मञ्जुषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मटती
मटती f. (-ती) Hail; also मटची ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मटस्फटि|मटस्फटिः
मटस्फटि m. (-टिः) Incipient pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मट्टक|मट्टकं
मट्टक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The ridge of a thatch.<BR>	 2. A sort of grain, (Eleusine corocana.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठ्
मठ् r. 1st cl. (मठति)<BR>	 1. To be confused or disturbed in mind.<BR>	 2. To<BR>dwell, to inhabit.<BR>	 3. To grind.<BR>	 4. To go. (इ) मठि r. 1st cl. (मण्ठते)<BR>1. To bewail, to regret, to remember with sorrow or regret.<BR>	 2.<BR>To long for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठ|मठं|मठः
मठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. A school, a college, the residence of young Brāhmans,<BR>prosecuting sacred studies.<BR>	 2. A building inhabited by asceties of<BR>the same order.<BR>	 3. A temple.<BR>	 4. A cart, a carriage, particularly<BR>drawn by oxen.<BR> E. मठ् to dwell, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठर|मठरः
मठर m. (-रः) The name of a Muni or saint.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Intoxicated.<BR> E. मत्<BR>to respect, Unādi aff. अरच्, and ठ substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मठी
मठी f. (-ठी) A cell.<BR>	 2. A cloister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मड्
मड् (इ) मडि r. 1st cl. (मण्डते)<BR>	 1. To divide, to separate.<BR>	 2. To clothe 3.<BR>To surround, to encompass. r. 1st and 10th cls. (मण्डति मण्डयति-ते)<BR>To adorn, to grace, to decorate. r. 10th cl. (मण्डयति-ते) To gladden,<BR>to rejoice, to make happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मडक|मडकः
मडक m. (-कः) A kind of grain, (Eleusine corocana.)<BR> E. मडि-क्वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मड्डु|मड्डुः
मड्डु m. (-ड्डुः) A sort of drum.<BR> E. मस्ज् to purify, aff. उन्, deriv. irr.;<BR>also with कन् added, मड्डुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण
मण r. 1st cl. (मणति) To sound, to sound inarticulately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणि|मणिः
मणि mf. (-णिः-णिः-णी)<BR>	 1. A gem, a jewel, a precious stone.<BR>	 2. Orna-<BR>ment in general.<BR>	 3. A load-stone, a magnet.<BR>	 4. Any thing excell-<BR>ent of its kind.<BR>	 5. A pearl.<BR>	 6. Fleshy processes pending from<BR>the neck of a goat.<BR>	 7. A small water-pot.<BR>	 8. The glans penis.<BR>9. The clitoris.<BR>	 10. The wrist.<BR>	 11. One of the Nāgas or serpent<BR>chiefs of Pātāla.<BR> E. मण् to sound, aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिक|मणिकं|मणिकः
मणिक n. (-कं) A small water-jar, a pitcher.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A jewel.<BR> E. मणि the same, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकण्ठ|मणिकण्ठः
मणिकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) The blue jay.<BR> E. मणि a jewel, and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकण्ठक|मणिकण्ठकः
मणिकण्ठक m. (-कः) A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकर्ण|मणिकर्णः
मणिकर्ण mfn. (र्णः-णा-र्णी-र्णं) Jewel-eared.<BR> E. मणि, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकर्णिका
मणिकर्णिका f. (-का) A holy pool at Benares, in which pilgrims are<BR>directed to bathe.<BR> E. माण, and कर्ण the ear, aff. कन्, fem. form;<BR>Devi having dropped one of her ear-rings at this place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकाच|मणिकाचः
मणिकाच m. (-चः) The feathered part of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकानन|मणिकाननं
मणिकानन n. (-नं) The neck or throat.<BR> E. मणि a jewel, and कानन a<BR>wood; abounding with such ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिकार|मणिकारः
मणिकार m. (-रः) A jeweller, a lapidary or worker in precious stones.<BR>E. मणि a gem, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिग्रीव|मणिग्रीवः
मणिग्रीव m. (-वः) One of KUVERA'S sons.<BR> E. मणि a gem, ग्रीवा the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिछिद्रा|मणिच्छिद्रा
मणिछिद्रा f. (-द्रा)<BR>	 1. Marrow.<BR>	 2. A sort of drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणित|मणितं
मणित n. (-तं) Low murmuring sound uttered at cohabitation.<BR> E. मण् to<BR>sound, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणितारक|मणितारकः
मणितारक m. (-कः) The Indian crane.<BR> E. मणि a jewel, तृ to pass over, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिद्वीप|मणिद्वीपः
मणिद्वीप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The crest or hood of the great serpent ANANTA.<BR>2. Name of an island in the ocean of nectar.<BR> E. मणि a jewel, and<BR>द्वीप a continent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिधनुष्
मणिधनुष् m. (-नुः) The rainbow.<BR> E. मणि a jewel, and धनुस् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिपुष्पक|मणिपुष्पकः
मणिपुष्पक m. (-कः) The conch-shell of Sahadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिपूर|मणिपूरं|मणिपूरः
मणिपूर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The navel.<BR>	 2. A sort of bodice worn by women, and<BR>often richly ornamented with.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The pit of the stomach, as<BR>one of the mystical Chakras of the body: see चक्र.<BR>	 2. Name of a<BR>town in Kalinga.<BR> E. मणि a jewel, and पूर filling, full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिबन्ध|मणिबंध|मणिबन्धः
मणिबन्ध m. (-न्धः) The wrist.<BR> E. मणि a jewel, and बन्ध binding; where<BR>bracelets of precious stones are bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=542-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिबन्धन|मणिबंधन
मणिबन्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. An ornament of pearls.<BR>	 2. That part of a ring<BR>where the jewels are set.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिभद्र|मणिभद्रः
मणिभद्र m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. One of the Jinas, or Jaina deified teachers.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of the king of the Yakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिभित्ति|मणिभित्तिः
मणिभित्ति f. (-त्तिः) The place of the great serpent, SESHA Nāga.<BR> E. मणि<BR>a jewel, and भित्ति a wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिभूमि|मणिभूमिः
मणिभूमि f. (-मिः) A jewel-mine, or a place where gems or precious<BR>stones are found.<BR> E. मणि a gem, and भूमि ground, also मणिभू<BR>f. (-भूः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमण्डप|मणिमण्डपः
मणिमण्डप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The capital of Sesha.<BR>	 2. The place of NAIRI-<BR>TA, regent of the S. W. quarter.<BR> E. मणि a jewel, and मण्डप a<BR>building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमत्|मणिमन्त्
मणिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Having jewels, possessed of or adorned<BR>with them.<BR>	 m. (-मान्) The sun.<BR> E. मणि, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमध्य
मणिमध्य n. (-ध्यं) A species of the Vrihatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमन्थ|मणिमन्थं
मणिमन्थ n. (-न्थं)<BR>	 1. A mountain or range where salt is found.<BR>	 2. Rock-<BR>salt.<BR> E. मणि a gem, and मन्थ what churns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिमाला
मणिमाला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A necklace, a zone, a fillet, &c. of precious stones.<BR>2. The circular impression left by a bite, (in amorous sports.)<BR>	 3.<BR>The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 4. Light, lustre.<BR>	 5. A species of the<BR>Jagatī metre.<BR> E. मणि a gem, and माला a necklace, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिरत्न
मणिरत्न n. (-त्नं) A precious gem.<BR> E. मणि, and रत्न a jewel, or the best of<BR>any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिव|मणिवः
मणिव m. (-वः) One of the Nāgas or serpents of Pātāla.<BR> E. मणि a gem, and व poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिवीज|मणिवीजः
मणिवीज m. (-जः) The pomegranate.<BR> E. मणि a gem, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिसर|मणिसरः
मणिसर n. (-रं) A string of gems, a necklace, &c.<BR> E. मणि, and सर<BR>what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिसोपान
मणिसोपान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A staff or stick set with jewels.<BR>	 2. A stair-case<BR>set with jewels.<BR> E. मणि a jewel, सोपान a ladder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणीचक्र
मणीचक्र n. (-क्रं) The moon-gem, probably a sort of crystal.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A king-fisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मणिवक
मणिवक n. (-कं) A flower.<BR> E. मण् to sound. deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्ड|मंडं|मण्डं|मंडः|मण्डः
मण्ड mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Scum, skimmings, froth, foam, barm, &c., the<BR>upper part of any infusion in a state of boiling or ferment.<BR>	 2.<BR>Pith, essence.<BR>	 3. The head.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. Ornament, decoration.<BR>	 2.<BR>The castor-oil tree. (Palma christi.)<BR>	 3. A sort of potherb.<BR>	 4. A<BR>frog.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा)<BR>	 1. Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>	 2. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>E. मडि to adorn, Unādi aff. ड; मन-ड तस्य-नेत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डन|मंडन|मण्डनं|मण्डनः
मण्डन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Adorning, dressing, decorating, fond of or put-<BR>ting on ornaments.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Ornament, decoration, jewels, trinkets,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Name of a philosopher, a contemporary and opponent<BR>of Sankarāchārjya.<BR> E. मडि to adorn, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डप|मंडपः|मण्डपः
मण्डप mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>	 1. A temporary building, an open shed or hall,<BR>adorned with flowers and erected on festival occasions, as in<BR>marriages, &c.<BR>	 2. An open temple or building consecrated to a<BR>deity.<BR>	 3. A bower.<BR>	 4. A pavilion.<BR> E. मण्ड ornament, and पा to<BR>preserve, aff. क; or मडि-कप्न् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डयन्त|मंडयंतः|मण्डयन्तः
मण्डयन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. An ornament, a decoration of trinkets, jewels, &c.<BR>2. An actor.<BR>	 3. Food.<BR>	 4. An assembly of women.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती) A wo-<BR>man, a wife.<BR> E. मडि to adorn, Unādi aff. झच्, fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डरी|मंडरी
मण्डरी f. (-री) The mole cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डल|मंडल|मण्डलं|मण्डलः
मण्डल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The<BR>sun's disk.<BR>	 2. An orb, a circumference in general, or the circle<BR>bounding the view, the visible horizon.<BR>	 3. (In astronomy,) A<BR>great circle, as नाडीमण्डलं the equator, क्रान्तिमण्डलं the ecliptic.<BR>	 4.<BR>A ball, a globe.<BR>	 5. A wheel.<BR>	 6. A province, a region, a district,<BR>extending twenty, or according to some authorities, forty Yojanas<BR>in every way.<BR>	 7. The country or empire, over which the twelve<BR>princes termed Chakravartis are supposed to have ruled; perhaps<BR>the peninsula of India, where the term Mandala or Mandel is of<BR>constant occurrence, to signify a province or district, as in Coro<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">Page543-b+ 60</a>]<BR>mandel, &c.<BR>	 8. Surrounding or contiguous countries.<BR>	 9. A sort of<BR>leprosy with circular spots.<BR>	 10. A heap, a quantity, a multitude<BR>or assemblage.<BR>	 11. An attitude in shooting, the fifth position,<BR>in which both knees are bent.<BR>	 12. The impression or scratch of a<BR>finger-nail.<BR>	 13. A sort of perfume, resembling in appearance a<BR>dried shell-fish.<BR>	 14. A sort of mystical diagram, used in summon-<BR>ing a divinity.<BR>	 15. A sweet-meat a sugar-ball.<BR>	 16. A form of<BR>array, an army drawn up in a circle.<BR>	 17. A division of the Rig-<BR>veda.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A kind of snake.<BR>	 2. A dog.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Bent grass.<BR>E. मडि to adorn, aff. कलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलक|मंडलकं|मण्डलकं|मण्डलकः
मण्डलक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. An orb or disk.<BR>	 2. A sort of leprosy, with large<BR>round spots.<BR>	 3. A mirror.<BR>	 4. A form of array, an army drawn up<BR>in a circle.<BR>	 5. A circular figure or diagram.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A dog.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलनृत्य|मण्डलनृत्यं
मण्डलनृत्य n. (-त्यं) Dancing in a ring, especially a dance imitative of<BR>one, said to have been danced by the Gopis round KṚṢṆA and<BR>his mistress RĀDHĀ.<BR> E. मण्डल a circle, and नृत्य dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलन्यास|मण्डलन्यासः
मण्डलन्यास m. (-सः) The drawing of a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलपुच्छक|मण्डलपुच्छकः
मण्डलपुच्छक m. (-कः) A kind of poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलाग्र|मण्डलाग्रः
मण्डलाग्र m. (-ग्रः) A sword, a scimitar.<BR> E. मण्डल a circle, अग्र a top or point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलाधीश|मण्डलाधीशः
मण्डलाधीश m. (-शः) An emperor, a king of kings.<BR> E. मण्डल an exten-<BR>sive district or empire, and अधीश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलायित|मंडलायित|मण्डलायितं
मण्डलायित n. (-तं) A ball, a globe.<BR> E. मण्डल a circle, क्यप् aff., क्त added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलिन्|मंडलिन्
मण्डलिन् mfn. (ली-लिनी-लि) Being in a circle, made up into a coil or<BR>ball.<BR>	 2. Surrounded by.<BR>	 m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A large species of snake.<BR>	 2. A<BR>cat.<BR>	 3. A Pole cat.<BR>	 4. A dog.<BR>	 5. The sun.<BR>	 6. The ruler or governor<BR>of a Mandal or district.<BR>	 7. The Indian fig-tree.<BR> E. मण्डल a circle,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलीकरण|मंडलीकरणं
मण्डलीकरण n. (-णं) Rounding, gathering in a ball or a circle, coiling,<BR>&c.<BR> E. मण्डल and करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलीकृत|मंडलीकृत
मण्डलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rounded, made round or globular, gathered<BR>in a ball or circle.<BR> E. मण्डल, and कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलेशः|मण्डलेश
मण्डलेशः m. (-शः) An emperor, a supreme monarch.<BR> E. मण्डल an empire,<BR>and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डलेश्वर|मण्डलेश्वरः
मण्डलेश्वर m. (-रः) A sovereign, a monarch.<BR> E. मण्डल a district, and ईश्चर<BR>a sovereign; the power of this prince is limited by AMARA, and<BR>the Mandaleswara is considered as an emperor or supreme prince,<BR>only when in addition to his territorial sway, he has performed<BR>the Rājasuya sacrifice, in which he has been attended by all his<BR>tributary or subject princes: other authorities confound the so-<BR>vereign of a Mandala, with the Chakravarti or emperor, and with<BR>the Samrāj or lord paramount, and others confine him to the<BR>government of a district of twenty or forty Yojanas in each<BR>direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डहारक|मण्डहारकः
मण्डहारक m. (-कः) A distiller of spirits.<BR> E. मण्ड froth, ferment, and हृ<BR>to take, aff. अण्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डा
मण्डा f. (-ण्डा)<BR>	 1. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 2. The myrobalan tree.<BR>	 3. Trigonella<BR>foenum graecum. “मेति”.<BR> E. मडि-अच्-टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डित|मंडित|मण्डितः
मण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ornamented, adorned.<BR>	 m. (-तः) One of the<BR>eleven persons called Gaṇadhipas by the Jainas.<BR> E. मडि to adorn,<BR>aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डूक|मंडूकः|मण्डूकः
मण्डूक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A frog.<BR>	 2. The name of a Muni.<BR>	 3. A flower, (Big-<BR>nonia Indica.)<BR>	 f. (-का-की) Madder, (Rubia Manjith.)<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>	 1.<BR>A female frog.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica, or Hydrocotyle<BR>Asiatica.)<BR>	 3. An unchaste or abandoned woman.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A kind<BR>of coitus.<BR> E. मडि to ornament, Unādi aff. ऊकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डूकपर्ण|मण्डूकपर्णः
मण्डूकपर्ण mf. (-र्णः-र्णी) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>	 f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. Bengal<BR>madder, (Rubia Manjith.)<BR>	 2. A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>	 3.<BR>A sort of creeper, (Hydrocotyle Asiatica.)<BR> E. मण्डूक a frog, and पर्ण<BR>a leaf, compared to the animal in shape or colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=543-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डुकयोग
मण्डुकयोग m. (-गः) A kind of meditation in which the meditator sits<BR>motionless like a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डुकानुवृत्ति
मण्डुकानुवृत्ति f. (-क्तिः) A frog-leap, hence skipping over any portion or<BR>omitting it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डूर|मंडूरं|मण्डूरं
मण्डूर mn. (-रः-रं) Rust of iron used as a medicine.<BR> E. मडि to adorn, ऊरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मण्डोदक|मण्डोदकं
मण्डोदक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Painting figures or flowers, on the walls or floors<BR>of an apartment, &c. on festival occasions, with a white pigment<BR>made from ground rice.<BR>	 2. Variegated colour.<BR>	 3. Mental excite-<BR>ment.<BR> E. मण्ड scum, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्
मत् Ind. Mine. E. Irregular substitute for मम, possessive case of अस्मद्,<BR>and is used in composition, as मत्पुत्त्र my son, मन्नाथ my lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत|मतं|मतः
मत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, understood.<BR>	 2. Admitted, believed, held<BR>or entertained, (as opinion, &c.)<BR>	 3. Respected, reverenced, mind-<BR>ed, regarded.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Purpose, intention, wish, mind, (as to<BR>have a mind to any thing.)<BR>	 2. Knowledge.<BR>	 3. Doctrine, tenet,<BR>belief, opinion.<BR>	 4. Counsel, advice.<BR>	 5. Design, aim.<BR>	 6. Approba-<BR>tion.<BR> E. मन् to mind, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतङ्ग|मतंग|मतंगः|मतङ्गः
मतङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The name of a Muni.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. An elephant. E.<BR>मद् to please, to be pleased, अङ्गच् Unādi aff., द changed to तः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतङ्गज|मतंगज|मतंगजः|मतङ्गजः
मतङ्गज m. (-ङ्गः) An elephant.<BR> E. मतङ्ग cloud, (in colour.) and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतल्लिका
मतल्लिका f. (-का) Excellence, happiness: (also attributively, but un-<BR>varying in gender,) excellent, best, happiest; It is used at the<BR>end of a compound only and there is no etymon of this word,<BR>according to the best authorities; Vāchaspatya defined it thus:<BR>सतिमलति भूषयति ण्वुल्-पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मति|मतिः
मति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Understanding, intellect.<BR>	 2. Wish, desire, inclination.<BR>3. Memory, recollection.<BR>	 4. Respect, reverence.<BR>	 5. A potherb. E.<BR>मन् to respect, &c. aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिप्रकर्ष|मतिप्रकर्षः
मतिप्रकर्ष m. (-र्षः) Cleverness, talent.<BR> E. मति, and प्रकर्ष superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिभ्रम|मतिभ्रमः
मतिभ्रम m. (-मः) Error, mistake.<BR> E. मति understanding, and भ्रम error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिभ्रान्ति|मतिभ्रांति|मतिभ्रान्तिः
मतिभ्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Error, mistake, misapprehension.<BR> E. मति mind,<BR>understanding, and भ्रान्ति error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिमत्|मतिमन्त्
मतिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Sensible, clever, intelligent.<BR> E. मति, and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिविभ्रम|मतिविभ्रमः
मतिविभ्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Error.<BR>	 2. Madness, lunacy.<BR> E. मति, and विभ्रम error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मतिहीन
मतिहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Stupid, ignorant.<BR> E. मति, and हीन devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्क|मत्कः
मत्क mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं) Mine, belonging to me, &c.<BR>	 m. (-त्कः) A bug:<BR>(see the next.)<BR> E. मत् for मम mine, and कन् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कुण|मत्कुणः
मत्कुण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A bug.<BR>	 2. A flea.<BR>	 3. An elephant without tusks.<BR>4. A beardless man.<BR>	 5. The cocoanut tree.<BR>	 6. A buffalo.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>Armour for the thighs or legs.<BR>	 f. (-णा) The pudendum muliebre,<BR>without hair on the pubis.<BR> E. मद् or मत् pleasure, क्वन् to sound,<BR>aff. अच्, the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कुणारि|मत्कुणारिः
मत्कुणारि m. (-रिः) Hemp, (Cannabis sativa.)<BR> E. मत्कुण a bug, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्त|मत्तः
मत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Pleased, glad, delighted.<BR>	 2. Intoxicated,<BR>(drunk with liquor.)<BR>	 3. Intoxicated, (with pride, passion, &c.)<BR>	 4.<BR>Furious, mad, insane.<BR>	 m. (-त्तः)<BR>	 1. A furious elephant, or one in<BR>rut.<BR>	 2. Buffalo.<BR>	 3. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 4. The thorn-<BR>apple, (Dhūturā.)<BR>	 f. (-त्ता)<BR>	 1. Vinous liquor.<BR>	 2. A species of the<BR>Panktī metre.<BR> E. मद् to rejoice, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तकाशिनी
मत्तकाशिनी f. (-नी) An excellent woman.<BR> E. मत्त intoxicated, and काश् to<BR>shine, aff. इनि; also from काष् or कास्, मत्तकाषिणी, and मत्तकासिनी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तकीश|मत्तकीशः
मत्तकीश m. (-शः) An elephant.<BR> E. मत्तक for मत्त furious, and ईश lord,<BR>the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तदन्तिन्|मत्तदंतिन्
मत्तदन्तिन् m. (-न्ती) A furious elephant.<BR> E. मत्त, and दन्तिन् an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तमयूर|मत्तमयूरः
मत्तमयूर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A species of the Atijagatī metre. E.<BR>सत्त, and मयूर a peacock, (by which.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तर|मत्तरः
मत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Better or more than mine.<BR> E. मत् for मम mine,<BR>and डतरच् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तवारण|मत्तवारणं|मत्तवारणः
मत्तवारण m. (-णः) A furious elephant, or one in rut.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A paint-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">Page544-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ed wooden turret or vārāndāh, on the top of a large building or<BR>palace.<BR>	 2. An enclosure of trees, &c. round the walls of a princely<BR>residence.<BR>	 3. Pounded betle-nut.<BR> E. मत्त wild, and वारण an ele-<BR>phant, or fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्ताक्रीड
मत्ताक्रीड n. (-डं) A species of the Vikritī metre.<BR> E. मत्त, आक्रीड playing,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तालम्ब|मत्तालम्बः
मत्तालम्ब m. (-म्बः) A fence or enclosure round the walls of a palace, either<BR>artificial as palisades, or natural as a grove of trees, &c.<BR> E. मत्त<BR>mad, wild, (enemies, &c.) आलम्ब delaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तेभगमना
मत्तेभगमना f. (-ना) A woman with a lounging or rolling walk.<BR> E. मत्त<BR>intoxicated, इभ an elephant, गमना who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्पर
मत्पर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Devoted to me, (God.)<BR> E. मत्, and पर attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्य|मत्यं
मत्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. The iron-bound handle of a sickle.<BR>	 2. The exercise or<BR>application of knowledge.<BR>	 3. The means of acquiring knowledge.<BR>E. मति knowledge, &c. aff. यत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्र्
मत्र् (इ,) मत्रि r. 1st and 10th cls. (मन्त्रति मन्त्रयति) To speak privately, to<BR>counsel or advise. With आङ्, To address or salute. With नि,<BR>To invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स|मत्सः
मत्स m. (-त्मः) A fish.<BR> E. मदि to be pleased, स aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सगण्ठ|मत्सगण्ठः
मत्सगण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) Fish-sauce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सर|मत्सरः
मत्सर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Envious.<BR>	 2. Niggardly, covetous.<BR>	 mf. (-रः-रा)<BR>1. Envy, impatience of another's success or prosperity.<BR>	 2. Pas-<BR>sion, anger.<BR>	 3. A gnat, a musquito.<BR>	 4. Greediness.<BR> E. मदि to re-<BR>joice, Unādi aff. सर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सरिन्
मत्सरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Wicked, depraved, bad.<BR>	 2. Envious.<BR> E. मत्सर envy, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्य|मत्स्यः
मत्स्य mf. (-त्स्य-त्सी) A fish in general.<BR>	 m. (-त्स्यः)<BR>	 1. A particular fish<BR>probably the Saphari, or fish in which VIṢṆU was incarnate in<BR>his Matsya Avatār.<BR>	 2. A name of VIṢṆU, from his incarnation as<BR>a fish.<BR>	 3. A country, enumerated amongst the midland divisions<BR>of India, (Diṇajpur and Rangpur.)<BR>	 4. One of the Purānas.<BR> E. मदि<BR>to be pleased, Unādi aff. स्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यकरण्डिका|मत्स्यकरंडिका
मत्स्यकरण्डिका f. (-का) A fish-basket.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, and करण्ड a basket,<BR>कन् added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यगन्ध
मत्स्यगन्ध f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Lāngaliya; (the common name<BR>is applied to the Nama zeylanica, and the commelina salicifolia.)<BR>2. Satyavatī, the mother of the sacred poet VYĀSA: see मत्स्योदरी.<BR>E. मत्स्य a fish, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यघात|मत्स्यघातः
मत्स्यघात m. (-तः) Catching fish.<BR> E. मत्स्य, and घात killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यजाल|मत्स्यजालं
मत्स्यजाल n. (-लं) A fishing-net.<BR> E. मत्स्य fish, and जाल net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यण्डी|मत्स्यंडी
मत्स्यण्डी f. (-ण्डी) Coarse or unrefined sugar, the juice of the sugar-cane,<BR>either after its first boiling, or after it is partially freed from im-<BR>purities by straining.<BR> E. मन्द slowly, स्यन्द् to trickle or ooze, अण्<BR>aff., fem. aff. ङीप्, deriv. irr.; also with कन् added, मत्स्यण्डिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यधानी
मत्स्यधानी f. (-नी) A fish basket, a small basket used by fishermen, to<BR>put the fish into when caught; it is also sometimes, but less<BR>accurately, applied to a kind of snare of reeds or grass, which is<BR>left in the water, and entangles the fish that swim with the curr-<BR>ent.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, धा to have or hold, aff. ल्युट्; also with आङ्<BR>prefixed, मत्स्याधानी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यनाशक|मत्स्यनाशकः
मत्स्यनाशक m. (-कः) An ospray.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, and नाशक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यनाशन|मत्स्यनाशनः
मत्स्यनाशन m. (-नः) An ospray.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, and नाशन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यपित्ता
मत्स्यपित्ता f. (-त्ता) A medicinal plant, commonly Katkī.<BR> E. मत्स्य a<BR>fish, and पित्त bile; being as bitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यबन्धिन्|मत्स्यबंधिन्
मत्स्यबन्धिन् m. (-न्धी) A fisherman.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A fish-basket.<BR> E. मस्य a fish,<BR>and बन्ध confining, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यरङ्ग|मत्स्यरंग|मत्स्यरङ्गः
मत्स्यरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A king-fisher.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, and रङ्ग inclination;<BR>also with कन् added, मत्स्यरङ्गक; it is read मत्स्यरङ्ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यराज|मत्स्यराजः
मत्स्यराज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The Rohtai, a sort of fish, (Cyprinus Rohita,<BR>HAM.)<BR>	 2. The country called Matsya.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, राज supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यवेधन|मत्स्यवेधनं
मत्स्यवेधन nf. (-नं-नी) A fish-hook.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A bird, the shag.<BR> E. मत्स्य a<BR>fish, विध् to pierce, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=544-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यसंचात
मत्स्यसंचात m. (-तः) A shoal of young or small fish.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, and<BR>संघात heap, quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यसन्तानिक|मत्स्यसंतानिक|मत्स्यसन्तानिकः
मत्स्यसन्तानिक m. (-कः) Fish baked in a crust of clay and straw, and<BR>eaten with condiments and oil.<BR> E. मत्स्य fish, सन्तान product,<BR>aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्याक्षी
मत्स्याक्षी f. (-श्ची) The moon-plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish,<BR>अक्ष an eye, aff. ङीष्; to which the flowers are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्याङ्गी
मत्स्याङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A plant, (Hingtsha pens, Rox.)<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, अङ्ग<BR>the body or form, aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्याद
मत्स्याद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Who or what feeds upon fish.<BR> E. मत्स्य, and अद who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यादनी
मत्स्यादनी f. (-नी) A name applied to several plants, as to Jussieua<BR>repens, Hingtsha repens, Nama zeylanica, &c.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, अदन<BR>eating, food, aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यावतार|मत्स्यावतारः
मत्स्यावतार m. (-रः) VIṢṆU in his first Avatāra; when the seventh<BR>Manu was reigning, the whole earth was destroyed by a flood and<BR>all living beings perished except the reigning Manu and the<BR>seven Ṛṣis who were saved by VIṢṆU in the form of a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्याशन|मत्स्याशनः
मत्स्याशन m. (-नः) The king-fisher.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, अशन eating. ‘माछराङ्गा’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्योदरी
मत्स्योदरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A name of SATYAVATĪ, the mother of VYĀSA.<BR>	 2.<BR>A place of pilgrimage, a particular pool at Benares held in re-<BR>verence by pilgrims to that sacred city.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, and उदर<BR>the belly; the mother of VYĀSA was found in the belly of a fish,<BR>and retaining a fishy-odour, was thence also called MATSYAGAN-<BR>DHĀ, till the scent was changed to that of a lotus by her para-<BR>mour the Muni PARĀSARA, the father of VYĀSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ
मथ (ए) मथे r. 1st cl. (मथति)<BR>	 1. The churn.<BR>	 2. To stir or agitate. (इ) मथि<BR>(मन्थति) 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To afflict.<BR>	 3. To suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथन|मथनं|मथनः
मथन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Churning.<BR>	 2. Rubbing.<BR>	 3. Injury.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A tree, the<BR>wood of which is used to produce fire by attrition, (Premna<BR>longifolia.)<BR> E. मथ् to churn, to stir or rub, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथनाचल|मथनाचलः
मथनाचल m. (-लः) The mountain Mandara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथित|मथितं
मथित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stirred, churned.<BR>	 2. Agitated, (mentally,) dis-<BR>tressed, anxious.<BR>	 3. Crushed, pinched.<BR>	 4. Dislocated.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Butter-milk, without any watery admixture.<BR> E. मथ् to churn,<BR>aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथिन्
मथिन् m. (-न्था)<BR>	 1. A churning-stick.<BR>	 2. The Penis.<BR>	 3. Wind.<BR>	 4. The<BR>thunderbolt.<BR> E. मथि to stir or agitate, aff. इन्, and the nasal<BR>rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथुरा
मथुरा f. (-रा) A town in the province of Āgrā, celebrated as the birth<BR>place, and early residence of KṚṢṆA, and still an object of<BR>pilgrimage amongst the Hindus.<BR> E. मथ् to stir, Unādi aff. उरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथुरेश|मथुरेशः
मथुरेश m. (-शः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. मथुरा a town, and ईश ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथूरा
मथूरा f. Mathurā.<BR> E. ऊरच् affixed to मथि, instead of उरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्
मद् r. 10th cl. (मादयते) (इ, इर्) मदि r. 1st cl. (मन्दते) and (ई, इर्) मदी r.<BR>4th cl. (माद्यति)<BR>	 1. To be glad, to be satisfied or content, to<BR>rejoice.<BR>	 2. To be proud. (इ) मदि r. 1st cl. (मन्दते)<BR>	 1. To praise.<BR>	 2.<BR>To sleep, to doze, to be lazy or sluggish.<BR>	 3. To be stupid, to be<BR>an idiot or fool.<BR>	 4. To be elegant.<BR>	 5. To go or approach. मद r.<BR>10th cl. (मादयते) To cause or justify satisfaction or contentment.<BR>मदी r. 1st cl. causal form. (मादयति)<BR>	 1. To delight, to make glad, to<BR>exhilarate.<BR>	 2. To madden or intoxicate, literally or figuratively.<BR>3. To be poor or distressed.<BR>	 4. To be proud. With नि prefixed,<BR>(निमादयति) To articulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्
मद् A form of the first personal pronoun in the singular number used<BR>at the beginning of compounds, as in मत्सादृश्य “my likeness.” &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद|मदः
मद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Joy, pleasure, delight.<BR>	 2. The juice that flows from an<BR>elephant's temples when in rut.<BR>	 3. Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>4. Inebriety, intoxication.<BR>	 5. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 6. Insanity, mad-<BR>ness.<BR>	 7. Semen virile.<BR>	 8. Musk.<BR>	 9. A male river.<BR>	 10. Ardent<BR>passion, desire.<BR>	 11. Love.<BR>	 12. Delight.<BR>	 13. Arrogance.<BR>	 14. Honey.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">Page545-b+ 60</a>]<BR>15. Any beautiful object.<BR>	 f. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A drinking vessel.<BR>	 2. An<BR>instrument for making furrows.<BR> E. मद् to be pleased, &c. aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकल|मदकलः
मदकल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Speaking inarticulately or like a drunken<BR>person.<BR>	 2. Uttering low sounds of love.<BR>	 3. Sweet and indistinct.<BR>m. (-लः) An elephant in rut.<BR> E. मद inebriety, &c., कल् to sound,<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकोहल|मदकोहलः
मदकोहल m. (-लः) A bull that has been liberated at some festival, and<BR>is allowed to wander about at will.<BR> E. मद pleasure, कुह् to<BR>sound, aff. अलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदगन्धा|मदगंधा
मदगन्धा f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 2. Hemp.<BR> E. मद intoxication, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदगमन|मदगमनः
मदगमन m. (-नः) A buffalo.<BR> E. मद pleasure, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदघ्नी
मदघ्नी f. (-घ्नी) A potherb, (Basella lucida, &c.)<BR> E. मद inebriety, घ्नी what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदच्युत
मदच्युत f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Gladdening.<BR>	 2. Wanton, drunk.<BR>	 m. (-तः) INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदन|मदनः
मदन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. KĀMADEVA, the Hindu CUPID.<BR>	 2. The season of<BR>spring.<BR>	 3. A plant commonly Mayanā, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>	 4.<BR>Thorn-apple, (Dhūtūra metel.)<BR>	 5. A bee.<BR>	 6. A sort of bean, (Pha-<BR>seolus radiatus.)<BR>	 7. Bee's wax.<BR>	 8. A tree, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>	 9. A<BR>kind of embrace.<BR>	 f. (-ना-नी)<BR>	 1. Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>	 2. De-<BR>lighting,<BR> E. मद् to exhilarate or rejoice, aff. ल्युट्, fem. aff. टाप्,<BR>or ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनकण्टक|मदनकंटक|मदनकण्टकः
मदनकण्टक m. (-कः) Horripilation caused by the feeling of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनकाकुरव|मदनकाकुरवः
मदनकाकुरव m. (-वः) A pigeon, a dove.<BR> E. मदन love, काकु change of<BR>voice, and रव who utters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनक्लिष्ट
मदनक्लिष्ट Adj. Afflicted by love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनगोपाल|मदनगोपालः
मदनगोपाल m. (-लः) KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनचतुर्दशी|मदनचतुर्द्दशी
मदनचतुर्दशी f. (-शी) The fourteenth day in the first half of Chaitra<BR>sacred to the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदननालिका
मदननालिका f. (-का) A faithless wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनपक्षिन्
मदनपक्षिन् f. (-क्षिणी) The Khanjana bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनपाठक|मदनपाठकः
मदनपाठक m. (-कः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. मदन spring, and<BR>पाठक reader; announcing the season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनवश
मदनवश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Subdued by love, in love.<BR> E. मदन, वश suddued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनमहोत्सव|मदनमहोत्सवः
मदनमहोत्सव m. (-वः) A festival held in honour of Kāmadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनललित
मदनललित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Sign or effect of love.<BR>	 2. A species of the Ashtī<BR>metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनलेख|मदनलेखः
मदनलेख m. (-खः) A love letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनशलाका
मदनशलाका f. (-क्य)<BR>	 1. A provocative medicine.<BR>	 2. The Mayanā, or more<BR>properly the Sārikā, a small bird.<BR>	 3. The female of the Kokila or<BR>Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. मदन love, &c., and शलाका the bird, or a dart, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनसारिका
मदनसारिका f. (-का) The Sārikā a small bird, (Turdus salica.) E.<BR>मदन love, and सारिका the Sālika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनाग्रक|मदनाग्रकः
मदनाग्रक m. (-कः) A kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनाङ्कुश|मदनांकुश|मदनाङ्कुशः
मदनाङ्कुश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Membrum virile.<BR>	 2. A nail-wound.<BR> E. मदन<BR>KĀMADEVA, and अङ्कुश a goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनातुर
मदनातुर m. (-रः) Enamoured, in love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनायुध|मदनायुधः
मदनायुध m. (-धः) Pudendum muliebre.<BR> E. मदन, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनालय|मदनालयः
मदनालय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A sovereign, a prince.<BR>	 2. A lotus.<BR>	 3. Pudendum<BR>muliebre.<BR> E. मदन pleasure, आलय receptacle, abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनावस्था
मदनावस्था f. (-स्था) Separation of lovers.<BR> E. मदन love, अव depreciative<BR>prefix, स्था to stay, affs. क, and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनी
मदनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 2. Musk.<BR>	 3. The Atimukta creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनीय
मदनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be enamoured.<BR>	 2. Causing or exciting<BR>passion.<BR> E. मद् to delight, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदनोत्सव|मदनोत्सवः
मदनोत्सव m. (-वः) The vernal festival of the Hindus, the Holī.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>A courtezan of heaven.<BR> E. मदन spring of love, and उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदप्रयोग|मदप्रयोगः
मदप्रयोग m. (-गः) The issue of the fluid from the forehead of an ele-<BR>phant when in rut.<BR> E. मद the fluid, and प्रयोग junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदभञ्जिनी
मदभञ्जिनी f. (-नी) A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR> E. मद inebriety, भञ्ज्<BR>breaking, इनि aff. “शतमूल्याम्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयन्तिका|मदयंतिका
मदयन्तिका f. (-का) Arabian jasmine.<BR> E. कन् added to the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=545-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयन्ती|मदयंती
मदयन्ती f. (-न्ती) Arabian jasmine.<BR> E. मद् to delight, झच् Unādi aff.,<BR>and ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदयित्नु|मदयित्नुः
मदयित्नु m. (-त्नुः)<BR>	 1. Love or CUPID.<BR>	 2. A distiller of spirituous liquor.<BR>3. A drunken man, a mad man.<BR>	 4. A cloud.<BR>	 n. (-त्नुं) Vinous or<BR>spirituous liquor.<BR> E. मद in the causal form, to intoxicate, &c.<BR>Unādi aff. इत्नुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदराग|मदरागः
मदराग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Love or KĀMA.<BR>	 2. A cock.<BR>	 3. A drunken man. E.<BR>मद passion or desire, and राग propensity, inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदविक्षिप्त|मदविक्षिप्तः
मदविक्षिप्त m. (-प्तः)<BR>	 1. A furious elephant, or one in rut.<BR>	 2. One dis-<BR>tracted by passion.<BR> E. मद the juice, and विक्षिप्त tossed, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदविह्वल
मदविह्वल m. (-लः) Mad with lust or pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदवृन्द|मदवृंद|मदवृन्दः
मदवृन्द m. (-न्दः) An elephant.<BR> E. मद the juice, and वृन्द a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदशौण्डक|मदशौंडक
मदशौण्डक n. (-कं) Nutmeg. “जातिफल” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदसार|मदसारः
मदसार m. (-रः) The cotton-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदस्थल|मदस्थलं
मदस्थल n. (-लं) A tavern, a dram-shop.<BR> E. मद intoxication and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदस्थान|मदस्थानं
मदस्थान n. (-नं) A place where liquor is sold, a tavern, a dram-shop. E.<BR>मद drunkenness, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाद्य
मदाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Intoxicated, drunk.<BR>	 m. (-द्यः) The palm-tree.<BR>f. (-द्या) A sort of Barleria, with red flowers.<BR> E. मद intoxication,<BR>आद्या fit or proper for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदातङ्क|मदातंक|मदातङ्कः
मदातङ्क m. (-ङ्क) Pain and sickness, consequent upon inebriety.<BR> E. मद, and आतङ्क fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदात्यय|मदात्ययः
मदात्यय m. (-यः) Disorder induced by drunkenness; headache, sick-<BR>ness, loss of appetite, &c.<BR> E. मद drunkenness, अत्यय consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदान्ध|मदांध
मदान्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Blind with pride or passion, arrogant, dis-<BR>solute, &c.<BR> E. मद, and अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाम्नात|मदाम्नातः
मदाम्नात m. (-तः) A drum carried on an elephant.<BR> E. मद pride, आम्नात<BR>minded, respected, from म्ना with आङ् prefix, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाम्बर|मदांबर|मदाम्बरः
मदाम्बर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. INDRA'S elephant.<BR>	 2. An elephant in rut.<BR> E. मद the<BR>frontal fluid, and अम्बर garment, housing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदार|मदारः
मदार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An elephant in rut.<BR>	 2. A rogue.<BR>	 3. A libertine, a<BR>lecher.<BR>	 4. An elephant in rut.<BR>	 5. A hog.<BR>	 6. The name of king.<BR>	 7.<BR>A sort of perfume, probably musk.<BR> E. मद् to be intoxicated,<BR>&c., Unādi aff. आरन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदार्म्मद|मदार्मद|मदार्मदः|मदार्म्मदः
मदार्म्मद m. (-दः) A sort of fish: see फलक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदालस
मदालस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Indolent, slothful, overcome with passion,<BR>pride or drunkenness.<BR> E. मद and अलस idle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदालापिन्
मदालापिन् m. (-पी) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. मद delight, आङ्<BR>before, लप् to speak, aff. णिनि; the song of this bird is constantly<BR>heard in the spring in most parts of Hindustan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदावस्था
मदावस्था f. (-स्था)<BR>	 1. Ruttishness.<BR>	 2. Wantonness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाह्व|मदाह्वः
मदाह्व m. (-ह्वः) Musk.<BR> E. मद musk, and आह्व name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदि|मदिः
मदि f. (-दिः) A kind of harrow.<BR> E. मृद-इन् पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिर|मदिरः
मदिर m. (-रः) A red species of Khayer, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1.<BR>Wine, spirits, spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>	 2. A wagtail.<BR>	 3. A spe-<BR>cies of the Akritī metre.<BR> E. मद् to be delighted, &c., Unādi aff.<BR>किरच्, fem. aff. टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिराक्षी
मदिराक्षी f. (-क्षी) A woman, a mistress, a wife.<BR> E. मदिरा wine, अक्षि the<BR>eye, अच् and ङीष् affs., whose eyes inebriate like wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिरागृह|मदिरागृहं
मदिरागृह n. (-हं) A tavern, a dram-shop.<BR> E. मदिरा wine and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिरासख|मदिरासखः
मदिरासख m. (-खः) The mango, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR> E. मदिरा wine or<BR>spirits, and सखि the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिरेक्षणा
मदिरेक्षणा f. (-णा) A fascinating woman.<BR> E. मदिरा, and ईक्षण the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदिष्ठा
मदिष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा) Vinous liquor.<BR> E. मद what delights or intoxicates, इष्ठन्<BR>superlative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदीय|मदीयं
मदीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Mine, my own.<BR> E. मत् for मम mine, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोत्कट|मदोत्कटः
मदोत्कट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Arrogant, haughty.<BR>	 2. Furious, mad.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-टः)<BR>	 1. An elephant in rut.<BR>	 2. A pigeon.<BR>	 3. A dove.<BR>	 f. (-टा) A<BR>spirituous liquor.<BR> E. मद and उत्कट who is furious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोदग्र
मदोदग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं) Haughty, arrogant.<BR>	 f. (-ग्रा) A woman in gene-<BR>ral.<BR> E. मद and उदग्र elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोद्धत|मदोद्धतः
मदोद्धत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Drunk, intoxicated.<BR>	 2. Arrogant, drunk<BR>with pride.<BR> E. मद drunkenness, उद्धत struck, overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोन्मत्त
मदोन्मत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Drunk or mad with pride, passion, &c. E.<BR>मद and उन्मत्त mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्गु|मद्गुः
मद्गु m. (-द्गुः)<BR>	 1. An aquatic bird, the shag.<BR>	 2. An outcaste, the son of<BR>a Brāhmana by a woman of the bard, or panegyrist class, whose<BR>employment is hunting wild beasts.<BR>	 3. A ship, a galley.<BR> E. मस्ज्<BR>to emerge, to dive, उ aff., deriv, irr.; or मद to be delighted, (in<BR>the water,) and गुक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्गुर|मद्गुरः
मद्गुर m. (-रः) A fish, (Macropteronatus Magur, Ham.)<BR> E. मद् to intoxi-<BR>cate, उरच् Unādi aff., and गुक् augment, form irr.; also with<BR>कन् added मद्गुरक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्गुरसी
मद्गुरसी f. (-सी) A sort of fish. “शृङ्गीमत्स्ये” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्य|मद्यं
मद्य n. (-द्यं) Wine, vinous or spirituous liquor.<BR>	 f. (-द्या)<BR>	 1. Intoxicating.<BR>2. Gladdening.<BR> E. मद to be intoxicated, (by it), aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यपङ्क|मद्यपङ्कः
मद्यपङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) Vinous liquor for distilling.<BR> E. मद्य wine, पङ्क mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यपाशन|मद्यपाशनं
मद्यपाशन n. (-नं) Eating a relish, or what excites thirst.<BR> E. मद्य wine, अश्<BR>to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यपीत
मद्यपीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Drunk, a drunkard.<BR> E. मद्य and पीत drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यपुष्पी
मद्यपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A plant, the blossoms of which are used in distilling:<BR>see मद्यवासिनी, &c.<BR> E. मद्य wine, पुष्प the flower. “धाइफुल् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यमण्ड|मद्यमंड|मद्यमण्डः
मद्यमण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Yeast, barm, froth.<BR> E. मद्य wine, मण्ड froth, scum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यवासिनी
मद्यवासिनी f. (-नी) The Dhātuki creeper, the blossoms of which are<BR>used in distilling, (Grislea tomentosa, or Lythrum fruticosum.)<BR>E. मद्य wine, वस् to dwell, aff. णिनि and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यवीज
मद्यवीज n. (-जं) A drug used to produce fermentation.<BR> E. मद्य wine,<BR>and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्यसन्धान|मद्यसंधान|मद्यसन्धानं
मद्यसन्धान n. (-नं) Distillation of spirits.<BR> E. मद्य vinous liquor, and सन्धान distilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्र|मद्रः
मद्र m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. Joy, delight.<BR>	 2. A country enumerated amongst those<BR>to the N. W. of Hindustan proper.<BR>	 3. A sovereign of that coun-<BR>try.<BR>	 f. (-द्रा) The name of a river.<BR> E. मदि to be delighted, Unādi<BR>aff. रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्रक|मद्रकः
मद्रक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Produced, &c. in the country of Madra.<BR> E. मद्र<BR>a country so named, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्रकार|मद्रकारः
मद्रकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Delighting, giving delight.<BR> E. मद्र delight, कृ to<BR>make, aff. अण्; also with खच् aff. मद्रङ्कर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्रसुता
मद्रसुता f. (-ता) The wife of Pāndu, mother of the two youngest<BR>Pāndu princes.<BR> E. मद्र a proper name, and सुता the daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्वन्
मद्वन् m. (-द्वा) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. मद् to be intoxicated, वनिप् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्वर्गीण|मद्वर्गीणः
मद्वर्गीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Connected with, or related to me.<BR> E. मत् mine,<BR>वर्ग a class or number, ख aff.; also with छ aff. मद्वर्ग्गीय; and with<BR>यत्, मद्वर्ग्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधव्य|मधव्यः
मधव्य m. (-व्यः) The lunar month Vaiśākha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधु|मधुः
मधु mfn. (-धुः-ध्वी-धु) Sweet, literally or figuratively.<BR>	 n. (-धु)<BR>	 1. Spirituous<BR>liquor, distilled from the blossoms of the Bassia latifolia, or accor-<BR>ding to some explanations wine, or spirit distilled from grapes.<BR>	 2.<BR>Honey.<BR>	 3. The nectar, or honey of flowers.<BR>	 4. Water.<BR>	 5. Milk.<BR>6. Sugar.<BR>	 7. Sweetness, in flavour, sound, or disposition.<BR>	 m. (-धुः)<BR>1. The month Chaitra, (March-April.)<BR>	 2. The season of spring.<BR>3. A tree, (Bassia latifoliā.)<BR>	 4. The name of Daitya or demon,<BR>slain by VIṢṆU.<BR>	 5. The Asoka tree, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>	 6. Liquo-<BR>rice.<BR>	 7. The name of a RĀKSHASA killed by SATRUGHNA.<BR>	 8. An<BR>epithet of king Kārtavirya.<BR>	 f. (-धुः) A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>E. मन् to mind or respect, Unādi aff. उ, and ध substituted for<BR>the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुक|मधुकं|मधुकः
मधुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Sweet, (in taste.)<BR>	 2. Sweet-speaking or<BR>sounding, mellifluous, melodious.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A bard, a pane-<BR>gyrist, one who recites the lineage and praises of sovereigns in<BR>their presence.<BR>	 2. A kind of bird.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>	 mn.<BR>(-कः-कं) Liquorice, &c.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Tin.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Menis-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">Page547-a+ 60</a>]<BR>permum glabrum.)<BR>	 2. The sweet lime.<BR>	 3. A kind of panic seed. E.<BR>मधु sweet, कै to sound, aff. ड; or मधु honey, कन् aff. of com-<BR>parison, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=546-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकण्ठ|मधुकंठ|मधुकण्ठः
मधुकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. मधु honey, (as sweet,) कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकर|मधुकरः
मधुकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bee.<BR>	 2. A lover.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>4. A fruit, the round sweet lime.<BR> E. मधु honey, and कर what<BR>makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकर्क्कटिका|मधुकर्कटिका
मधुकर्क्कटिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A sort of citron, the round sweet lime.<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of date.<BR> E. मधु honey and कर्क्कटी or कर्क्कटिका a cucumber;<BR>some authorities have मधुकुक्कुटिका in place of this word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकारिन्
मधुकारिन् m. (-री) A bee.<BR> E. मधु, and कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकुक्कुटी
मधुकुक्कुटी f. (-टी) A kind of citron tree: see मधुकर्क्कटिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकुल्या
मधुकुल्या f. (-ल्या) A stream of honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकृत्
मधुकृत् m. (-कृत्) A bee.<BR> E. मधु honey, and कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकेशट|मधुकेशटः
मधुकेशट m. (-टः) A bee.<BR> E. मधुके in honey, and शट् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकोष|मधुकोषः
मधुकोष m. (-षः) The honey-comb or bee-hive.<BR> E. मधु honey, कोष recep-<BR>tacle. Also मधुकोश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुक्रम|मधुक्रमः
मधुक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Tippling.<BR>	 2. The honey-comb.<BR> E. मधु wine or honey,<BR>and क्रम order, arrangement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुक्षीर|मधुक्षीरः
मधुक्षीर m. (-रः) The date tree.<BR> E. मधु honey, and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुगायन|मधुगायनः
मधुगायन m. (-नः) The Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुगुञ्जन|मधुगुञ्जनः
मधुगुञ्जन m. (-नः) A tree. (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुघोष|मधुघोषः
मधुघोष m. (-षः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. मधु sweet, and घोष voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुज|मधुजं
मधुज n. (-जं) Bee's wax.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. Clayed or candied<BR>sugar.<BR> E. मधु honey, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुजम्बीर|मधुजंबीर|मधुजम्बीरः
मधुजम्बीर m. (-रः) A kind of citron. “कमलालेवु ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुजित्
मधुजित् m. (-जित्) VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. मधु the demon so named, and जित् conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुतृण|मधुतृणं|मधुतृणः
मधुतृण n. (-णं) Sugar-cane.<BR> E. मधु sweet, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुत्रय|मधुत्रयं
मधुत्रय n. (-यं) The three sweet things, viz.:--Clarified butter, honey<BR>and sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुदीप|मधुदीपः
मधुदीप m. (-पः) KĀMA, the Hindu CUPID.<BR> E. मधु spring, and दीप inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुद्गत
मधुद्गत m. (-तः) The mango tree.<BR> E. मधु spring, and द्गत messenger;<BR>blossoming in spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुद्र|मधुद्रः
मधुद्र m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. A bee.<BR>	 2. A libertine.<BR> E. मधु honey, द्रु to take, क aff.,<BR>and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुद्रव|मधुद्रवः
मधुद्रव m. (-वः) A red variety of the Hyperanthera morunga.<BR> E. मधु<BR>honey, and द्रव dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुद्रुम|मधुद्रुमः
मधुद्रुम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A tree, from the blossoms of which a spirit is dis-<BR>tilled, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>	 2. The mango tree.<BR> E. मधु wine, द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुधातु|मधुधातुः
मधुधातु m. (-तुः) A sort of pyrites.<BR> E. मधु honey, (as yellow,) and धातु<BR>mineral, honey-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुधूलि|मधुधूलिः
मधुधूलि f. (-लिः) Molasses, sugar before it is quite purified.<BR> E. मधु<BR>honey, धूलि dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुनालिकेरक|मधुनालिकेरकः
मधुनालिकेरक m. (-कः) A sweet kind of cocoanut.<BR> E. मधु sweet, नालिकेरक cocoanut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुनेतृ
मधुनेतृ m. (-ता) A bee.<BR> E. मधु honey, नी to get, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुनोलीह
मधुनोलीह m. (-हः) A bee.<BR> E. मधुनः of honey, लेह who licks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुप|मधुपः
मधुप m. (-पः) A bee.<BR> E. मधु honey, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधपटल
मधपटल m. (-लः) A bee-hive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपर्क|मधुपर्कं|मधुपर्कः
मधुपर्क n. (-र्कं) A dish of curds, ghee and honey, to be offered to a<BR>respectable guest on his arrival.<BR> E. मधु honey, पृच् to sprinkle,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपर्णिका
मधुपर्णिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The indigo plant.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>3. Moon plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>	 4. A creeper of the Cryptogamia<BR>class, (Lycopodium imbricatum, Rox.)<BR>	 5. A shrub, (Menispermum.)<BR>E. मधु honey, पर्ण a leaf, aff. कन्, fem. form; also मधुपर्णी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपर्णी
मधुपर्णी f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. A sort of creeper, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>	 3. The indigo plant.<BR>	 4. The sweet lime.<BR>E. मधु honey, पर्ण the leaf, aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपायिन्
मधुपायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Living on honey.<BR>	 m. (-यी) A bee.<BR> E. मधु<BR>honey, पा to drink, णिनि aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपालिका
मधुपालिका f. (-का) A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR> E. मधु honey, पाल् to<BR>nourish, वन् aff., fem. form. “गाम्भार्य्याम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपुरी
मधुपुरी f. (-री) Mathurā, a city so called.<BR> E. मधु the Rākshasa killed<BR>by SATRUGHNA, and पुरी a city or capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुपुष्प|मधुपुष्पः
मधुपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>	 2. The Mimosa Sirisha.<BR>	 3.<BR>The Bakula tree, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR> E. मधु wine or honey, and<BR>पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुप्रमेह|मधुप्रमेहः
मधुप्रमेह m. (-हः) Name of a particular disease of the urinary system.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुप्राशन
मधुप्राशन n. (-नं) One of the sixteen purificatory rites, consisting in<BR>putting a little honey into the month of a new-born child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुप्रिय|मधुप्रियः
मधुप्रिय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (Ardisia solanacea.)<BR>	 2. A name of BALA-<BR>RĀMA.<BR> E. मधु wine, &c., and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुफल|मधुफलः
मधुफल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>	 2. A sweet kind<BR>of cocoanut.<BR> E. मधु honey, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुफलिका
मधुफलिका f. (-का) A kind of date.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुबहुला
मधुबहुला f. (-ला) The Mādhabi creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुबीज|मधुबीजः
मधुबीज m. (-जः) The Pomegranate tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुभिद्
मधुभिद् m. (-भिद् or -भित् A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR> E. मधु the<BR>Daitya; and भिद् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमक्षिका
मधुमक्षिका f. (-का) A bee.<BR> E. मधु honey, and मक्षिका a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमज्जन|मधुमज्जनः
मधुमज्जन m. (-नः) The Ākhotaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमत्|मधुमन्त्
मधुमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Sweet, honied.<BR>	 f. (-ती) A species of the<BR>Ushnih metre.<BR> E. भधु and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमथन|मधुमथनः
मधुमथन m. (-नः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. मधु the Daitya, and मथन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमय
मधुमय f. (-यः-यी-यं) Sweet, luscious.<BR> E. मधु, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमल्ली
मधुमल्ली f. (-ल्ली) Double jasmine.<BR> E. मधु, and मल्ली jasmine. “मालतीपुष्पे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमस्तक|मधुमस्तकं
मधुमस्तक n. (-कं) A sweetmeat made of flour, honey, oil and ghee.<BR> E. मधु<BR>honey, and मस्तक a head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमाधवी
मधुमाधवी f. (-वी) A kind of intoxicating drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमाध्वीक|मधुमाध्वीकं
मधुमाध्वीक n. (-कं) A spirit distilled from the flowers of the Bassia<BR>latifolia.<BR> E. मधु spirit, and माध्वीक the same prepared from honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमारक|मधुमारकः
मधुमारक m. (-कः) A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमूल|मधुमूलं
मधुमूल n. (-लं) An esculent root, a sort of yam.<BR> E. मधु spirit, and मूल root. “मौआलु ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुयष्टि|मधुयष्टिः
मधुयष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Sugar-cane.<BR> E. मधु honey, and यष्टि a cane or stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुयष्टिका
मधुयष्टिका f. (-का) Liquorice, (Glyeirrhiza glabra, or rather the Abrus<BR>precatorius, of which the root is similarly used.)<BR> E. मधु honey,<BR>यष्टि a stick, and कन् added; or without the aff. मधुयष्टी f. (-ष्टी).<BR>“यष्टिमधु ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुर|मधुरं|मधुरः
मधुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Sweet.<BR>	 2. Pleasing, agreeable, liked.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The sweet taste, sweetness.<BR>	 2. A drug, commonly Jivaka.<BR>	 3. Mo-<BR>lasses.<BR>	 4. The red sugar-cane.<BR>	 5. Rice.<BR>	 6. A kind of mango tree.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रं)<BR>	 1. Poison.<BR>	 2. Tin.<BR>	 3. Treacle, syrup.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A sort of fennel,<BR>(Anethum sowa or panmorium. Rox.)<BR>	 2. Anise, (Pimpinella<BR>anisum.)<BR>	 3. A plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>	 4. Liquorice.<BR>	 5. The<BR>sweet lime.<BR>	 6. Marrow.<BR>	 7. The city Mathurā.<BR>	 8. A Medicinal<BR>plant, commonly Kakkoli.<BR>	 9. Asparagus racemosus.<BR>	 10. Bengal<BR>beet.<BR> E. मधु honey, and रा to get or be, aff. क; to have the<BR>flavour of honey, to be as sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरक|मधुरकः
मधुरक m. (-कः) A medicinal plant, commonly Jivaka.<BR> E. मधुर the<BR>same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरकण्टक|मधुरकंटक|मधुरकण्टकः
मधुरकण्टक m. (-कः) A sort of fish.<BR> E. मधुर sweet, and कण्टक bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरजम्बीर|मधुरजम्बीरः
मधुरजम्बीर m. (-रः) The sweet lime.<BR> E. मधुर sweet, जम्बीर lime. “कम्लालेवु ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरत्वच|मधुरत्वचः
मधुरत्वच m. (-चः) A shrub, (Orislea tomentosa.)<BR> E. मधुर sweet, त्वच bark<BR>अच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरनिस्वना
मधुरनिस्वना f. (-ना) A woman with a sweet voice.<BR> E. मधुर sweet, निस्वन who sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरवीजपूर
मधुरवीजपूर m. (-रः) The sweet lime.<BR> E. मधुर sweet, वीजपूर a citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरस|मधुरसः
मधुरस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Sweetness, (in flavour.)<BR>	 2. Sweetness, (in speech.)<BR>	 3.<BR>The sugar-cane.<BR>	 4. The palm-tree.<BR>	 f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (San-<BR>seviera zeylanica.)<BR>	 2. A plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>	 3. Grapes.<BR> E. मधु<BR>wine or honey, and रस juice, flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=547-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुराचर
मधुराचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Sweet, mellifluous, mellow, melodious.<BR> E. मधुर,<BR>and अक्षर letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुराम्लक|मधुराम्लकः
मधुराम्लक m. (-कः) The hog-plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR> E. मधुर sweet, अम्ल sour, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरालापा
मधुरालापा f. (-पा) The talking-Mainā, (Turdus Sālika.)<BR> E. मधुर sweet,<BR>आलाप talking, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरिका
मधुरिका f. (-का) A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa, Rox.)<BR> E. मधुरा the<BR>same, कन् aff.; this name is applied also to the Anethum pan-<BR>morium, Rox. and the Bengali derivative Mouri is applied to<BR>common anise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरिपु|मधुरिपुः
मधुरिपु m. (-पुः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. मधु the demon, and रिपु foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरिमन्
मधुरिमन् m. (-मा) Sweetness, agreeableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरोदक|मधुरोदकः
मधुरोदक m. (-कः) The sea of a fresh or sweet water, surrounding<BR>Pushkara dwīpa, and being the outermost of seven seas.<BR> E. मधुर<BR>sweet, and उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुल|मधुलं
मधुल n. (-लं) Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR> E. मधु wine, ला to be or get, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुलिका
मधुलिका f. (-का) Black mustard. “राइसर्षपे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुलिह्
मधुलिह् m. (-लिड्-लिट्) A bee.<BR> E. मधु honey, लिह् to lick, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुलेह
मधुलेह m. (-हः) A bee.<BR> E. मधु and लेह what licks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुलेहिन्
मधुलेहिन् m. (-ही) A bee.<BR> E. मधु, honey, लिह् to lick, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुवन|मधुवनं|मधुवनः
मधुवन m. (-नः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Name of the<BR>forest inhabited by the demon Madhu in Muttra.<BR> E. मधु sweet,<BR>and वन who speaks or cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुवार|मधुवारः
मधुवार m. (-रः) Tippling, drinking frequently and repeatedly.<BR> E. मधु<BR>wine, वार quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुवीज|मधुवीजः
मधुवीज m. (-जः) The pomegranate.<BR> E. मधु sweet, वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुव्रत|मधुव्रतः
मधुव्रत m. (-तः) A bee.<BR> E. मधु honey, व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुशाख|मधुशाखः
मधुशाख m. (-खः) Bassia latifolia.<BR> E. मधु spirituous liquor, शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुशिग्रु|मधुशिग्रुः
मधुशिग्रु m. (-ग्रुः) A red variety of the Hyperanthera morunga.<BR> E. मधु<BR>sweet, and शिग्रु the same tree. “रक्तशोभाञ्जने ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुश्रेणी
मधुश्रेणी f. (-णी) A plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR> E. मधु honey, श्वेणी a<BR>line or row. “मूर्वायाम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुष्ठील|मधुष्ठीलः
मधुष्ठील m. (-लः) A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR> E. मधु spirit, ष्ठीव् to eject, aff.<BR>क, and ल substituted for the final. “मौल ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसख|मधुसखः
मधुसख m. (-खः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. मधु, spring, and सख for सखि friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसहाय|मधुसहायः
मधुसहाय m. (-यः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. मधु, spring, and सहाय friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसात्
मधुसात् Ind. As honey, sweet.<BR> E. मधु and साति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसाद्भूत
मधुसाद्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Become sweet. E. (मधुसात्, and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसारथि|मधुसारथिः
मधुसारथि m. (-थिः) KĀMA the Hindu CUPID.<BR> E. मधु the spring personi-<BR>fied, and सारथि a charioteer, having Vasanta or spring for his<BR>coachman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसिक्थक|मधुसिक्थकः
मधुसिक्थक m. (-कः) A sort of poison.<BR> E. मधु honey, and सिक्थक wax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसुहृद्
मधुसुहृद् m. (-हृद् or -हृत्) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. मधु spring, सुहृत् the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुसूदन|मधुसूदनः
मधुसूदन m. (-नः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Bengal beet.<BR> E. मधु the<BR>Daitya or honey, and सूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुस्थान
मधुस्थान n. (-नं) A bee-hive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुस्रवस्
मधुस्रवस् m. (-वाः) A tree, (Bassia latifolia).<BR> E. मधु spirituous liquor, स्नु<BR>to drop or distil, aff. अमुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुस्रवा
मधुस्रवा f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>	 2. Liquorice.<BR> E. मधु honey,<BR>स्नु to drop, affs. अप् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुस्वर|मधुस्वरः
मधुस्वर m. (-रः) The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. मधु sweet or spring,<BR>and स्वर note, song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुहन्
मधुहन् m. (-हा)<BR>	 1. A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. A particular bird of prey.<BR>3. A sooth-sayer.<BR> E. मधु the Daitya, and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुक|मधुकं|मधुकः
मधुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>	 2. A bee.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A flower<BR>of the Madhūka tree.<BR> E. मन् to respect, ऊक aff., and ध substi-<BR>tuted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूच्छिष्ट|मधूच्छिष्टं
मधूच्छिष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Bee's wax.<BR> E. मध्रु honey and उच्छिष्ट left, rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूपघ्न|मधूपघ्नं|मधूपघ्नः
मधूपघ्न n. (-घ्नं) The city Mathurā.<BR> E. मधु the demon, उपघ्न destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुल|मधुलं
मधुल m. (-लः) A sort of Bassia, described as growing in watery or<BR>mountainous situations.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Liquorice.<BR>	 2. The sweet lime.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">Page548-b+ 60</a>]<BR>3. The mango tree.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR> E. मधु<BR>honey or spirit, ला to be or get, aff. ड, and the उ of मधु irregular-<BR>ly long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूलक|मधूलकः
मधूलक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Sweet.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sort of Bassia, grow-<BR>ing in watery or mountainous sites.<BR>	 2. Sweetness.<BR>	 f. (-लिका) A<BR>plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्य|मध्यं|मध्यः
मध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Middle, intermediate.<BR>	 2. Right, proper, rea-<BR>sonable.<BR>	 3. Low, vile.<BR>	 4. Amongst, amidst.<BR>	 5. Mean, middle, (in<BR>astronomy,) as मध्यच्छाया middle or mean shadow.<BR>	 mn. (-ध्यः-ध्यं)<BR>	 1.<BR>The interior.<BR>	 2. Mean or common time in music.<BR>	 3. The middle, the<BR>centre.<BR>	 4. The waist.<BR>	 5. The belly, abdomen.<BR>	 6. Pause, internal.<BR>7. The middle term of a progression.<BR>	 f. (-ध्या)<BR>	 1. A young woman,<BR>a girl arrived at puberty.<BR>	 2. The middle-finger.<BR>	 3. A form of<BR>metre, a stanza of four lines containing three syllables in each.<BR>4. Of a middle size or quantity, moderate.<BR>	 5. Neutral.<BR>	 6. Just,<BR>reasonable.<BR>	 m. (-ध्यः) Cessation, rest, interval.<BR>	 n. (-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. A very<BR>large number, ten thousand billions.<BR>	 2. A horse's flank.<BR> E. मा<BR>beauty, या to have, अण् aff., deriv. irr., or properly सन्-यत् aff. and<BR>ध substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यकर्ण|मध्यकर्णः
मध्यकर्ण m. (-र्णः) A radius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यग
मध्यग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Who or what goes in the centre or betwixt,<BR>amongst, &c.<BR> E. मध्य and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यगन्ध|मध्यगंध|मध्यगन्धः
मध्यगन्ध m. (-न्धः) The mango tree.<BR> E. मध्य middle and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यग्रहण
मध्यग्रहण n. (-णं) The middle of an eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यचारिन्
मध्यचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Going amongst or amidst.<BR> E. मध्य and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यतस्
मध्यतस् Ind. From or in the middle, centrical, centrically.<BR> E. मध्य the<BR>middle, and तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यदिन
मध्यदिन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Noon, midday.<BR>	 2. The Bandhuka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यदीपक
मध्यदीपक n. (-कं) A species of the figure of speech called Dīpaka; in<BR>it the common term which throws light on the whole stanza is<BR>used in the middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यदेश|मध्यदेशः
मध्यदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The middle region; part of India, bounded by Ku-<BR>ruksketra on the north, Allāhābād on the south, the Himālaya<BR>mountains on the east, and the Vindhya mountains on the west;<BR>comprising therefore the modern provinces of Allāhābād, Agrā,<BR>Delhi, Oudh, &c.; the northern limit is elsewhere defined to<BR>be the disappearance of the Saraswatī.<BR>	 2. The middle part of<BR>any thing.<BR>	 3. The waist.<BR>	 4. The Belly.<BR>	 5. The meridian.<BR> E. मध्य<BR>middle, and देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यपदलोपिन्
मध्यपदलोपिन् m. (-पी) A compound word which omits the middle mem-<BR>ber in its composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यम|मध्यमं|मध्यमः
मध्यम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Middle, centrical, intervening, intermediate.<BR>2. Middle-born, neither the oldest nor youngest.<BR>	 3. Mean, (in<BR>astronomy,) as मध्यमगति mean motion, (of a planet.)<BR>	 mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>The waist, the middle of the body.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. One of the seven<BR>musical notes, the fourth note of the Hindu gamut.<BR>	 2. The middle<BR>country: see मध्यदेश । 3. A sort of deer.<BR>	 4. One of the Grāmas or<BR>musical scales of Hindus, corresponding apparently with the<BR>major made of European music.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A girl arrived at pu-<BR>berty, or in whom menstruation has commenced.<BR>	 2. The middle<BR>finger.<BR>	 3. A central blossom.<BR>	 4. The pericarp of a lotus.<BR>	 5. A<BR>woman in the middle of her youth considered as a character in<BR>poetic composition.<BR>	 6. A form of metre, a verse of four lines of<BR>three syllables each.<BR> E. मध्य middle, and म aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमपाण्डव|मध्यमपांडव|मध्यमपाण्डवः
मध्यमपाण्डव m. (-वः) ARJUNA, the third or middle of the PĀṆḌU prin-<BR>ces.<BR> E. मध्यम middle and पाण्डव, Pāndava or descendant of PĀNDU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमपुरुष|मध्यमपुरुषः
मध्यमपुरुष m. (-षः) The second person, (in gram.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमभृतक|मध्यमभृतकः
मध्यमभृतक m. (-कः) A husbandman.<BR> E. मध्यम middle, and भृतक a la-<BR>bourer; working partly for his own advantage, and partly for<BR>that of the landlord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=548-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमलोक|मध्यमलोकः
मध्यमलोक m. (-कः) The earth, the world of mortals.<BR> E. मध्यम middle,<BR>and लोक world; between heaven and hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमवयस्क
मध्यमवयस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) Middle-aged.<BR> E. मध्यम and वयस्क aged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमसंग्रह
मध्यमसंग्रह m. (-हः) Intriguing with another man's wife, the act of<BR>presenting flowers, perfumes, &c. to her, and conversing with her<BR>privately.<BR> E. मध्यम middle, संग्रह connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमसाहस|मध्यमसाहसं|मध्यमसाहसः
मध्यमसाहस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Punishment due to crimes of a middling degree.<BR>2. Injuring building, throwing down walls, &c.<BR> E. मध्यम middle,<BR>साहस violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमाहरण
मध्यमाहरण n. (-णं) The elimination of the middle term in an equation, (in algebra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमिका
मध्यमिका f. (-का) A girl arrived at puberty, one in whom menstrua-<BR>tion has commenced.<BR> E. मध्यमा, कन् added, in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमीय|मध्यमीयं
मध्यमीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Central, middle.<BR> E. मध्यम middle and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्ययव|मध्ययवः
मध्ययव m. (-वः) A weight of six white mustard seeds.<BR> E. मध्य middle,<BR>and यव barley-corn, the Yava being sometimes considered equal<BR>to eight seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यखत्र
मध्यखत्र m. (-त्रः) Midnight.<BR> E. मध्य middle, रात्र night, and the mascu-<BR>line form in the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यरेखा
मध्यरेखा f. (-खा) The first meridian, (in astronomy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यलोक|मध्यलोकः
मध्यलोक m. (-कः) The earth, the dwelling of mortals.<BR> E. मध्य middle,<BR>and लोक world; placed in the middle between heaven and hell;<BR>also with कन् added मध्यलोकक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यलोकेश|मध्यलोकेशः
मध्यलोकेश m. (-शः) A king, a sovereign.<BR> E. मध्यलोक the earth, and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यवत्तिन्
मध्यवत्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>	 1. Central, middle.<BR>	 2. Being amongst or<BR>amidst.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्ती) A mediator.<BR> E. मध्य and वर्त्तिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यवृत्त
मध्यवृत्त n. (-त्तं) The navel.<BR> E. मध्य the middle, and वृत्त abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यसूत्र
मध्यसूत्र n. (-त्रं) The central meridian, (in astronomy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थ|मध्यस्थः
मध्यस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Centrical, middle.<BR>	 2. Neutral.<BR>	 3. Mediat-<BR>ing.<BR>	 m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. A middle man, an umpire, an arbitrator, a<BR>mediator.<BR>	 2. An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR> E. मध्य middle, and स्थ what<BR>or who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थता
मध्यस्थता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Middle state or character.<BR>	 2. Indifference.<BR> E. मध्यस्थ<BR>middle, and तल् aff. of the abstract; also with त्व मध्यस्थत्व n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थल|मध्यस्थलं
मध्यस्थल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The waist.<BR>	 2. A middle place.<BR>	 3. The centre.<BR> E. मध्य<BR>middle, स्थल place or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थान
मध्यस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A Neutral soil.<BR>	 2. A middle place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्याह्न|मध्याह्नः
मध्याह्न m. (-ह्नः) Mid-day, noon.<BR> E. मध्य middle, अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वल|मध्वलः
मध्वल m. (-लः) Tippling, drinking, repeatedly.<BR> E. मधु wine, अल् to be<BR>equal to, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वापात
मध्वापात m. (-तः) Taste or touch of honey.<BR> E. मधु and आपात alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वालुक|मध्वालुकं
मध्वालुक n. (-कं) Sweet potato.<BR> E. मधु sweet, आलु and esculent root,<BR>कन् added. “मौआलु ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वासव|मध्वासवः
मध्वासव m. (-वः) A spirituous liquor, distilled from the blossoms of<BR>the Bassia latifolia.<BR> E. मधु the Bassia, and आसव spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वासवनिक|मध्वासवनिकः
मध्वासवनिक m. (-कः) A distiller.<BR> E. मध्वासव spirit, नी to go, aff. क, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्विजा
मध्विजा f. (-जा) Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्
मन् r. 4th cl. (मन्यते) (उ) मनु r. 8th cl. (मनुते)<BR>	 1. To know, to under-<BR>stand.<BR>	 2. To regard, to mind.<BR>	 3. To think, to conceive. r. 10th<BR>cl. (मानयते)<BR>	 1. To be dull or insensible.<BR>	 2. To be proud.<BR>	 3. To<BR>oppose, to stop. r. 1st and 10th cls. (मनति मानयति) To honour, to<BR>respect, to worship. With अनु prefixed, To assent to, to agree.<BR>With अभि. To desire. With अव, To disrespect. With सम To<BR>concur, to agree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन|मनः
मन n. (-नं) Indian spikenard.<BR> E. मन् to respect, aff. अच् । “जटामांस्याम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनआप|मनआपः
मनआप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Pleasing, agreeable, beautiful.<BR> E. मनस् the mind,<BR>आप् to go or attract, aff. अण्; the final consonant of the first<BR>word is rejected, and the vowels do not coalesce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःकृत
मनःकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Attended to, applying the mind.<BR> E. मनस् and<BR>कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःशिल|मनःशिलः
मनःशिल mf. (-लः-ला) Red arsenic.<BR> E. मन्स् the mind, शिला a stone;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">Page549-b+ 60</a>]<BR>mineral delightful to the mind or heart; also with the dental स,<BR>मनःसिल । “मन्छाल ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःसिल
मनःसिल mf. (-लः-ला) Red arsenic: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनन|मननं
मनन n. (-नं) Minding, understanding.<BR> E. मन् to know, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्
मनस् n. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The mind, considered as the seat of perception and<BR>passion, the heart.<BR>	 2. The intellect, the understanding.<BR>	 3. The con-<BR>necting link between the Indriyas and Buddhi, (in Nyāya Phil.)<BR>4. Thought, imagination, conception, fancy.<BR>	 5. Intention, de-<BR>sign, purpose, wish.<BR>	 6. Desire, affection.<BR>	 7. Disposition, temper.<BR>8. Energy, spirit.<BR>	 9. Conscience.<BR>	 10. Red arsenic.<BR>	 11. An epithet<BR>of the lake Mānasa.<BR> E. मन् to know, to understand, aff. असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसा
मनसा f. (-सा) The goddess of the serpent race, and the particular pro-<BR>tectress against their venom.<BR> E. मनस् the mind, aff. टाप्; the<BR>object of love, and devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसाज्ञायिन्
मनसाज्ञायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Knowing by the mind, perceiving in-<BR>tellectually.<BR> E. मनसा third case of मनस् and ज्ञायिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसादेवी
मनसादेवी f. (-वी) The goddess presiding over snakes: see the last. E.<BR>मनसा the same, and देवी goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसिज|मनसिजः
मनसिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Mental, intellectual.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A name of<BR>KĀMA or love.<BR> E. मनसि in the heart or mind, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसिशय|मनसिशयः
मनसिशय m. (-यः) KĀMA or love.<BR> E. मनसि in the heart or mind, and<BR>शय who reposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्क
मनस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) Mental.<BR> E. मनस् and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्कार|मनस्कारः
मनस्कार m. (-रः) The attention of the mind to its own sensations, con-<BR>sciousness of pleasure or pain.<BR> E. मनस् of the mind and कार opera-<BR>tion; the compound also occurs with the seventh case मनसिकार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्ताप|मनस्तापः
मनस्ताप m. (-पः) Mental distress.<BR> E. मनस् and त्राप sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्ताल|मनस्तालः
मनस्ताल m. (-लः) The lion of DURGĀ.<BR> E. मनस् the mind, तल् to depress, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्विता
मनस्विता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Hope, expectation, dependence.<BR>	 2. Intelligence. E.<BR>मनस्विन् and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्विन्
मनस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>	 1. Attentive, fixing the mind upon any<BR>thing.<BR>	 2. Intelligence, intellectual.<BR>	 f. (-स्विनी) A virtuous wife. E.<BR>मनस् the mind or heart, aff. विन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाक्
मनाक् Ind.<BR>	 1. A little.<BR>	 2. Tardily, slowly.<BR> E. मन् to know, आक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाका
मनाका f. (-का) A female elephant.<BR> E. मन् to mind, &c. Unādi aff. आक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाक्कर|मनाक्करं
मनाक्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Doing little, lazy, sluggish.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A sort of<BR>Agallochum.<BR> E. मनाक् a little, and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनायी
मनायी f. (-यी) The wife of MANU.<BR> E. मनु the saint, ङीष् aff., and उ<BR>changed to ऐ; otherwise मनावी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनित|मनितं
मनित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Known, understood.<BR> E. मन् to know, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीक|मनीकं
मनीक n. (-कं) Collyrium, powdered antimony or other substances,<BR>used as an application and ornament to the eye.<BR> E. मन् to know,<BR>to be agreeable, ईकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषा
मनीषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Intellect, understanding.<BR>	 2. Desire, wish.<BR> E. मनस्<BR>the mind, ईष् to go, aff. क, or ईष aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषिन्
मनीषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Intellectual, intelligent.<BR>	 m. (-षी) A Pandit,<BR>a learned Brāhman, a teacher.<BR> E. मनीषा understanding, इनि poss-<BR>essive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनु|मनुः
मनु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. MANU, the legislator and saint, the son of BRAHMĀ, or<BR>a personification of BRAHMĀ himself, the creator of the world<BR>and progenitor of mankind; the name is however a generic term.<BR>and in every Kalpa or interval from creation to creation, there<BR>are fourteen successive MANUS presiding over the universe for<BR>the period of a Manwantara, respectively; in the present crea-<BR>tion there have been the six following MANUS: MARĪCHĪ or<BR>SWAYAMBHUVA, the supposed revealer of the code of law possessed<BR>by the Hindus, SWĀROCHISHA, OUTTAMĪ, TĀMASA, RAIVATA, and<BR>CHĀKSHUSHA; the seventh or the present MANU is VAIVASWATA,<BR>and is regarded to be the founder of the solar race of kings;<BR>SĀBARNĪ, DAKṢA-SĀBARNĪ, BRAHMĀ-SĀBARNĪ, DHARMA-SĀ-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">Page550-a+ 60</a>]<BR>BARNĪ, RUDRASĀBARNĪ, DEVA-SĀBARNĪ, and INDRA-SĀVARNĪ,<BR>these seven Manus are to come in the present creation.<BR>	 2. A<BR>man in general.<BR>	 3. One of the Jaina saints.<BR>	 4. A Mantra, a<BR>mystical verse or formula.<BR>	 5. The number fourteen.<BR>	 f. (-नुः-नायी-<BR>नावी) The wife of a legislator or MANU.<BR> E. मन् to know or under-<BR>stand, (the Vedas or scripture especially,) and उ Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=549-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुज|मनुजः
मनुज m. (-जः) A man in general.<BR>	 f. (-जा) A woman.<BR> E. मनु the legis-<BR>lator and progenitor of mankind, and ज born, descended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुजेन्द्र
मनुजेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A king.<BR> E. मनुज and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुभू
मनुभू m. (-भूः) Man, a man, mankind.<BR> E. मनु the saint, and भू born: see मनुज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुराज्
मनुराज् m. (-राट्) KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR> E. मनु man, and राज् to<BR>shine, aff. क्किप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुषी
मनुषी f. (-षी) A woman, the wife or female of the man.<BR> E. मनुष्य a man, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्य|मनुष्यः
मनुष्य m. (-ष्यः) Man, a man, mankind.<BR> E. मनु the progenitor of man-<BR>kind, यत् aff. of descent, and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यत्व|मनुष्यत्वं
मनुष्यत्व n. (-त्वं) The state or condition of man, manhood, humanity.<BR>E. त्व added to मनुष्य; also with तल्, मनुष्यता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यधर्म्मन्|मनुष्यधर्मन्
मनुष्यधर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा) KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>	 n. (-र्म्म) The duty of<BR>man.<BR> E. मनुष्य man, and धर्म्मन् piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्ययज्ञ|मनुष्ययज्ञः
मनुष्ययज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) Hospitality, (one of the five daily acts of piety.) E.<BR>मनुष्य a man, and यज्ञ sacrifice, sacrament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यसभा
मनुष्यसभा f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. A multitude, a crowd, a meeting.<BR>	 2. A place of<BR>meeting or assembly.<BR> E. मनुष्य a man, mankind, and सभा assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगत
मनोगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Seated in the mind.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Thoughts, ideas,<BR>notions, feelings.<BR> E. मनस् and गत gone to or in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगवी
मनोगवी f. (-वी) Wish, desire.<BR> E. मनस् the mind, and गो a cow, &c. fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगुप्त
मनोगुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Thought or meditated on secretly.<BR>	 f. (-प्ता) Red<BR>arsenic.<BR> E. मनस् and गुप्त cherished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोग्रहण
मनोग्रहण n. (-णं) Captivating the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोज
मनोज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born or seated in the mind.<BR>	 m. (-जः) KĀMA.<BR>E. मनस् and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजन्मन्
मनोजन्मन् mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म) Born or seated in the mind.<BR>	 m. (-न्मा) KĀMA<BR>or CUPID.<BR> E. मनस् the heart or mind, and जन्मन् birth; also मनोज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजव|मनोजवः
मनोजव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Fatherly, parental.<BR>	 2. Quick in thought or<BR>apprehension.<BR>	 3. Swift, as thought.<BR>	 f. (-वा) A plant: see अग्निजिह्वा.<BR>n. (-वं) Quickness of thought or apprehension.<BR> E. मनस् the mind, जु<BR>to move, to pervade, aff. अच्; or मनस् compounded with जव speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजवस|मनोजवसः
मनोजवस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Fatherly.<BR> E. मनोज desire, love, वस् to abide,<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोज्ञ|मनोज्ञं|मनोज्ञः
मनोज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Beautiful, handsome, lovely, pleasing, agree-<BR>able.<BR>	 f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>	 1. Red arsenic.<BR>	 2. Intoxicating liquor.<BR>	 3. The daughter<BR>of a sovereign, a princess.<BR> E. मनस् the mind or heart, ज्ञा to know,<BR>to get, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोदण्ड|मनोदंड|मनोदण्डः
मनोदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Restraint or control over the mind.<BR> E. मनस् and दण्ड castigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीनीत
मनीनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Chosen, preferred.<BR> E. मनस् and नीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभव|मनोभवः
मनोभव m. (-वः) KĀMA or CUPID.<BR> E. मनस् the mind or heart, and<BR>भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभू
मनोभू m. (-भूः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. मनस् the heart, भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोमयकोश|मनोमयकोशः
मनोमयकोश m. (-शः) The second of the five sheaths in which the soul<BR>is encased, (in Vedanta Phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोयायिन्
मनोयायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Swift, quick, as thought.<BR> E. मनस्, and<BR>यायिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोयोनि|मनोयोनिः
मनोयोनि m. (-निः) The deity KĀMA.<BR> E. मनस the heart, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरथ|मनोरथः
मनोरथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2. A desired object.<BR>	 3. A wish ex-<BR>pressed indirectly, (in drama.)<BR> E. मनस् the heart, and रथ vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरम|मनोरमं
मनोरम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Beautiful, lovely, pleasing, f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A god-<BR>dess, peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>	 2. A species of the Panktī metre.<BR>3. A beautiful woman.<BR> E. मनस् the mind, रम् to delight, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोलौल्य
मनोलौल्य n. (-ल्यं) Fancy, caprice, whim.<BR> E. मनस्, लौल्य unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहत|मनोहतः
मनोहत mfn. (-तः-ता-त) Disappointed.<BR> E. मनस् the mind, हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहर|मनोहरं|मनोहरः
मनोहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Beautiful, lovely, pleasing.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Gold.<BR> E. मनस्<BR>the mind, हृ to take or steal, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहारिन्
मनोहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Beautiful, pleasing, agreeable, lovely. E.<BR>मनस् the mind, हृ to steal, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोह्वा
मनोह्वा f. (-ह्वा) Red-arsenic.<BR> E. मन्स् the mind, and ह्वेञ् to call, to<BR>arrest, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्ज्
मन्ज् r. 1st cl. (मञ्जति) To clean, to polish, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तव्य|मंतव्य|मन्तव्यं
मन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be reflected on, to be ascertained or fixed<BR>in the mind, to be discussed either mentally or with proper per-<BR>sons.<BR>	 2. To be thought, believed, conceived, &c.<BR> E. मन् to know,<BR>aff. तव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तु|मंतु|मंतुः|मन्तुः
मन्तु m. (-न्तुः)<BR>	 1. Fault, offence, transgression.<BR>	 2. A man, mankind.<BR>	 3.<BR>A king.<BR>	 f. (-न्तुः) Understanding, intellect.<BR> E. मन् to know, Unādi<BR>aff. तु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तृ|मंतृ
मन्तृ m. (-न्ता)<BR>	 1. A sage, one who is possessed of holy knowledge.<BR>	 2.<BR>An adviser, a counsellor.<BR> E. मन् to know, Unādi aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्र|मंत्र|मंत्रः|मन्त्रः
मन्त्र m. (-न्त्रः)<BR>	 1. A division of the Vedas; in the first or practical<BR>part or Kāndam, it includes prayers and hymns, addressed to<BR>particular deities, and used at peculiar sacrifices, &c.; in the<BR>Uttara Kāndam, it is applied to addresses to BRAHMĀ or God,<BR>and to didactic explanations of his nature and attributes, &c.<BR>2. A mystical verse or incantation, (in the Tantras.)<BR>	 3. A formula<BR>sacred to any individual deity, as Om Viṣṇave nama, Om Si-<BR>vāya nama, &c.<BR>	 4. Secret consultation, private advice.<BR> E. मत्रि to<BR>advise or consult privately, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकुशल|मंत्रकुशल
मन्त्रकुशल Adj. Skilled in giving advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकृत्|मंत्रकृत्
मन्त्रकृत् m. (-कृत्)<BR>	 1. A counsellor, a minister.<BR>	 2. One who recites a<BR>sacred text.<BR>	 3. A composer of Vedic hymns.<BR> E. मन्त्र advice, and<BR>कृत् who gives or makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकृत
मन्त्रकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Consecrated by the Mantra<BR> E. मन्त्र and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रगण्डक|मंत्रगंडक|मन्त्रगण्डकः
मन्त्रगण्डक m. (-कः) Knowledge, science.<BR> E. मन्त्र advice, गडि to be a part<BR>of, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रगुप्ति|मंत्रगुप्ति|मन्त्रगुप्तिः
मन्त्रगुप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Secret counsel.<BR> E. मन्त्र and गुप्ति concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रगूढ|मंत्रगूढ|मन्त्रगूढः
मन्त्रगूढ m. (-ढः) A spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR> E. मन्त्र advice, in-<BR>formation. गूढ secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रजिह्व|मंत्रजिह्व|मन्त्रजिह्वः
मन्त्रजिह्व m. (-ह्वः) A name of fire.<BR> E. मन्त्र prayer, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रज्ञ|मंत्रज्ञ|मन्त्रज्ञः
मन्त्रज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. A spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR>	 2. A counsellor,<BR>an adviser.<BR>	 3. A priest, a sacred teacher.<BR> E. मन्त्र advice, &c. and ज्ञ<BR>who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रण|मंत्रण|मंत्रणं|मन्त्रणं
मन्त्रण nf. (-णं-णा) Advising, counselling in private.<BR> E. मत्रि to counsel, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रतस्
मन्त्रतस् Ind.<BR>	 1. From, with or by, a Mantra or mystical prayer.<BR>	 2. Ad-<BR>visedly, deliberately.<BR> E. मन्त्र and तसि substituted for the termina-<BR>tion of the fourth or fifth cases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रद|मंत्रद|मन्त्रदः
मन्त्रद m. (-दः) A spiritual guide or teacher.<BR> E. मन्त्र initiatory text, and<BR>द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रदर्शिन्|मंत्रदर्शिन्
मन्त्रदर्शिन् m. (-र्शी) A Brāhman learned in the Vedas.<BR> E. मन्त्र and दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रदीधिति|मंत्रदीधिति|मन्त्रदीधितिः
मन्त्रदीधिति m. (-तिः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. मन्त्र holy prayer, and दीघिति lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रपूतात्मन्
मन्त्रपूतात्मन् m. (-त्मा) A name of GARUḌA.<BR> E. मन्त्र and पूतात्मन् pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रफल
मन्त्रफल n. (-ल) The object or effect of counsel.<BR> E. मन्त्र and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रभेद|मंत्रभेद|मन्त्रभेदः
मन्त्रभेद m. (-दः) Divulging or betraying counsel.<BR> E. मन्त्र, भेद breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रयत्
मन्त्रयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Counselling, consulting.<BR> E. मत्रि to advise,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रयन्त्र|मंत्रयंत्र
मन्त्रयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A mystical diagram with a Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रयोग|मंत्रयोग|मन्त्रयोगः
मन्त्रयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The employment of Mantras.<BR>	 2. Magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवत्|मंत्रवत्|मन्त्रवन्त्
मन्त्रवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Accompanied with holy texts, (a cere-<BR>mony.)<BR>	 2. Entitled to use the Vedas.<BR>	 3. Initiated.<BR>	 4. Having or<BR>hearing counsel.<BR> E. मन्त्र and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवित्
मन्त्रवित् m. (-विद्-वित्)<BR>	 1. A spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR>	 2. A<BR>counsellor.<BR>	 3. A priest.<BR>	 4. A Brāhman learned in the Vedas. E.<BR>मन्त्र secret counsel, &c. and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=550-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रस्पृश्
मन्त्रस्पृश् mfn. (-त्पृक्) Obtaining or effecting any thing by means of<BR>mystic formalæ or prayers.<BR> E. मन्त्र a prayer of the Vedas, &c.,<BR>and स्पृश् to touch, aff. क्विन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रित|मंत्रित|मन्त्रितः
मन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Advised, counselled, planned.<BR>	 2. Consecrated<BR>with Mantras.<BR> E. मत्रि to consult, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रित्व|मंत्रित्वं
मन्त्रित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Property or condition of a counsellor, counsel-<BR>lorship.<BR> E. मन्त्रिन्, and त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिन्|मंत्रिन्
मन्त्रिन् m. (-न्त्री) A counsellor or adviser, a king's counsellor, a minister.<BR>E. मत्रि to advise, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रोदक|मंत्रोदक
मन्त्रोदक n. (-कं) Water consecrated by Mantras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रोपष्टम्भ|मंत्रोपष्टंभ|मन्त्रोपष्टम्भः
मन्त्रोपष्टम्भ m. (-म्भः) Encouraged by advice or direction.<BR> E. मन्त्र and उपष्टम्भ stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थ्|मंथ्
मन्थ् r. 1st cl. (मन्थति)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To afflict.<BR>	 2. To suffer pain.<BR>r. 1st and 9th cls. (मन्थति मथ्नाति) To agitate, to stir, to churn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थ|मंथ|मंथः|मन्थः
मन्थ m. (-न्थः)<BR>	 1. A churning stick.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. A dish made of<BR>barley-meal with ghee and water, a sort of gruel or porridge.<BR>	 4.<BR>A disease of the eyes, cataract or opacity.<BR>	 5. Rheum, excretion of<BR>the eyes.<BR>	 6. Killing, destroying.<BR>	 7. Agitating, stirring, churning.<BR>8. A ray of light.<BR>	 9. An instrument for kindling fire by fric-<BR>tion.<BR> E. मन्थ् to churn, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थगुण|मंथगुण|मन्थगुणः
मन्थगुण m. (-णः) A churning-cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थज|मंथज|मन्थजं
मन्थज n. (-जं) Butter.<BR> E. मन्थ churning, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थदण्डक|मंथदंडक|मन्थदण्डकः
मन्थदण्डक m. (-कः) A churning-stick.<BR> E. मन्थ churning, and दण्डक a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थन|मंथन|मन्थनं|मंथनः|मन्थनः
मन्थन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Agitating, stirring, churning.<BR>	 2. Killing, injuring.<BR>	 3.<BR>Kindling fire by friction.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A churn.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A churning-<BR>stick.<BR> E. मन्थ् to agitate, &c. aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थनघटी|मंथनघटी
मन्थनघटी f. (-टी) A churn, a common earthen-pot used for the purpose.<BR>E. मन्थन churning, and घटी a small jar or pitcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थर|मंथर|मन्थरं|मन्थरः
मन्थर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Slow, lazy, tardy.<BR>	 2. Large, bulky.<BR>	 3. Curv-<BR>ed, bowed, crooked.<BR>	 4. Stupid, dull, a fool.<BR>	 5. Low, vile, little.<BR>	 6.<BR>Low, hollow, (as sound.)<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A soldier marching slowly.<BR>2. A spy, an informer.<BR>	 3. A treasury, a store, a repertory.<BR>	 4.<BR>Fruit.<BR>	 5. An obstacle, a hindrance.<BR>	 6. A churning-stick.<BR>	 7. Fresh<BR>butter.<BR>	 8. The month Vaiśākha.<BR>	 9. Passion, wrath.<BR>	 10. A deer.<BR>11. A fort, a strong-hold.<BR>	 12. The mountain Mandara.<BR>	 13. The<BR>hair of the head.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Safflower.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Name of the favourite<BR>female slave of KAIKEYĪ. the favourite wife of DAŚARATHA. E.<BR>मन्थ् to agitate, &c. aff. अरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थरु|मंथरु|मंथरुः|मन्थरुः
मन्थरु m. (-रुः) The wind from a Chowrie or whisk.<BR> E. मन्थ् to agitate, अरुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थशैल|मंथशैल|मन्थशैलः
मन्थशैल m. (-लः) The mountain Mandara.<BR> E. मन्थ a churning-stick, and<BR>शैल a mountain, being so employed in churning the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थान|मंथान|मंथानः|मन्थानः
मन्थान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A churning-stick.<BR>	 2. An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>(cassia fistula.)<BR> E. मन्थ् to agitate, आनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थिन्|मंथिन्
मन्थिन् mfn. (-न्थि-न्थिनी-न्थि)<BR>	 1. Agitating, churning.<BR>	 2. Paining, afflict-<BR>ing.<BR>	 m. (-न्थि) Semen virile.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A churning-vessel.<BR> E. मन्थ् to<BR>churn, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्थोदधि|मंथोदधि|मन्थोदधिः
मन्थोदधि m. (-धिः) Sea of milk.<BR> E. मन्थ churning, and उदधि a sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्द|मंद|मन्दः
मन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>	 1. Slow, tardy.<BR>	 2. Dull, stupid, heavy.<BR>	 3. Fool-<BR>ish, a fool.<BR>	 4. Unlucky.<BR>	 5. Sick, diseased.<BR>	 6. Little.<BR>	 7. Idle, lazy.<BR>8. Drunken, addicted to drunkenness.<BR>	 9. Vile, wicked.<BR>	 10. Self-<BR>willed.<BR>	 11. Cold, phlegmatic, apathetic.<BR>	 12. Low, (as a tone.)<BR>	 13.<BR>Withered, (as flowers.)<BR>	 m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. A name of SATURN.<BR>	 2. A sort<BR>of elephant.<BR>	 3. A name of YAMA.<BR>	 4. (In astronomy.) Anomaly.<BR>5. A destruction of the universe.<BR> E. मदि to be lazy, &c.<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दकान्त
मन्दकान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Dull, not bright.<BR> E. मन्द, and कान्त shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दकान्ति|मंदकांति|मन्दकान्तिः
मन्दकान्ति m. (-न्तिः) The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दग|मंदग|मन्दगः
मन्दग m. (-गः) The planet SATURN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दगत
मन्दगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Going slowly.<BR> E. मन्द, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दगति
मन्दगति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Slow moving.<BR>	 f. (-तिः) Going slowly.<BR> E. मन्द,<BR>and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दगमन
मन्दगमन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Who or what moves slowly.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Moving<BR>or going slowly.<BR> E. मन्द, and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दगामिन्|मंदगामिन्
मन्दगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Going slowly or gently.<BR>	 m. (-मी) A soldier<BR>marching slowly.<BR> E. मन्द, गम् to go, aff. घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दचेतस्|मंदचेतस्
मन्दचेतस् Adj.<BR>	 1. Silly.<BR>	 2. Absent-minded.<BR>	 3. Fainting away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दच्छाय|मंदच्छाय
मन्दच्छाय Adj. Lustreless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दजननी|मंदजननी
मन्दजननी f. (-नी) The wife of SŪRYA.<BR> E. मन्द SATURN, and जननी mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दट|मंदट|मंदटः|मन्दटः
मन्दट m. (-टः) The coral tree, (Erythrina fulgens.)<BR> E. मदि to please,<BR>aff. अटच् । “पारिभद्रवृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दन|मंदन|मंदनं|मन्दनं
मन्दन n. (-नं) Praise, eulogium.<BR> E. मदि to be pleased, (by) Unādi aff. क्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दफल
मन्दफल n. (-ल) (In astronomy.) The anomalistic equation of a planet.<BR>E. मन्द, and फल product.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दबुद्धि|मंदबुद्धि
मन्दबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Stupid, foolish.<BR> E. मन्द, बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दभाग्य|मंदभाग्य
मन्दभाग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Wretched, unhappy, unfortunate.<BR> E. मन्द,<BR>and भाग्य fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दमति|मंदमति
मन्दमति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Dull, stupid, slow of apprehension.<BR> E. मन्द, and मति intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दयमान
मन्दयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Slow, tardy.<BR> E. मदि to be slow, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दयन्ती
मन्दयन्ती f. (-न्ती) An epithet of DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दर|मंदर|मन्दरः
मन्दर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Large, bulky.<BR>	 2. Slow, sluggish, dull, lazy, &c.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The mountain Mandara, with which the ocean was<BR>churned by the Suras, and Asuras, after the deluge, for the purpose<BR>of recovering the sacred things lost in it during that period.<BR>	 2.<BR>The Mandāra tree, one of the five trees of paradise.<BR>	 3. Svarga or<BR>the paradise of the Hindus.<BR>	 4. A string of pearls, &c.<BR>	 5. A mirror.<BR>E. मदि to please, to be lazy, &c. अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दसान|मंदसानः|मन्दसानः
मन्दसान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>	 2. Life, living.<BR>	 3. Sleep,<BR>sleeping.<BR> E. मदि to be slow or sleepy, Unādi aff. असानच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दसानु|मन्दसानुः
मन्दसानु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. Sleep.<BR>	 2. Life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दस्मित|मंदस्मित
मन्दस्मित n. (-तं) A smile.<BR> E. मन्द slowly, gently, स्मित smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दहास्य|मंदहास्य
मन्दहास्य n. (-स्यं) A smile, a gentle laugh.<BR> E. मन्द slowly, gently, and<BR>हास्य laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाक|मंदाक|मन्दाकं|मंदाकः|मन्दाकः
मन्दाक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Praising, praise.<BR>	 2. A stream, a current.<BR> E. मन्द् to<BR>praise, आकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाकिनी|मंदाकिनी
मन्दाकिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The Ganges of heaven.<BR>	 2. A species of the Jagatī.<BR>metre.<BR> E. मन्द slowly, अक् to go, aff. णिनि, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाक्रान्ता
मन्दाक्रान्ता f. (-न्ता) A species of the Atyashtī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाक्ष|मंदाक्ष|मन्दाक्षं
मन्दाक्ष n. (-क्षं) Modesty, shame, bashfulness.<BR> E. मन्द slow, retiring, and<BR>अक्ष organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाग्नि|मंदाग्नि|मन्दाग्निः
मन्दाग्नि m. (-ग्नि) Weakness of digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दात्मन्|मंदात्मन्
मन्दात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Slow of apprehension, dull. मन्द and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दादर|मंदादर
मन्दादर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Disregarding, neglecting, disrespecting.<BR> E. मन्द<BR>and आदर respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दानिल|मंदानिल|मन्दानिलः
मन्दानिल m. (-लः) A gentle breeze, zephyr.<BR> E. मन्द, and अनिल wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दायमान
मन्दायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-न) Delaying, going tardly.<BR> E. मदि to be lazy,<BR>causal v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दार|मंदार|मंदारः|मन्दारः
मन्दार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. One of the five trees of Svarga.<BR>	 2. The coral tree,<BR>(Erythrina fulgens.)<BR>	 3. Swallow wort, (Asclepias gigantea.)<BR> E. मदि<BR>to delight, &c. aff. आरक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दासु|मंदासु
मन्दासु Adj. Having weak breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दास्य|मन्दास्यं
मन्दास्य n. (-स्यं) Shame, modesty.<BR> E. मन्द retiring, and आस्य face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिकुकुर|मन्दिकुकुरः
मन्दिकुकुर m. (-रः) A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिमन्|मंदिमन्
मन्दिमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Slowness.<BR>	 2. Stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिर|मंदिर|मंदिरं|मन्दिरं|मन्दिरः
मन्दिर nf. (-र-रा) A house.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A town.<BR>	 2. A temple.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The sea.<BR>	 2. The back of the knee, the ham.<BR>	 3. One of the Gan-<BR>dharbas.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A stable.<BR> E. मदि to sleep, &c. Unādi aff. किरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिरपशु|मंदिरपशु|मन्दिरपशुः
मन्दिरपशु m. (-शुः) A cat.<BR> E. मन्दिर a house, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दीभव
मन्दीभव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Tardiness.<BR>	 2. Stupidity.<BR> E. मन्द, and भू to be, अप् aff.,<BR>च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दीभूत
मन्दीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Being slow, dull, stupid, &c.<BR> E. मन्द, and भू to<BR>be, aff. क्त, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=551-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दुरज
मन्दुरज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born in a stable.<BR> E. मन्दुरा, and ज born, the<BR>final of the first rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दुरा|मंदुरा
मन्दुरा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A stable.<BR>	 2. A bed, a mat used as one.<BR> E. मदि to<BR>please, &c. Unādi aff. उरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोच्छ
मन्दोच्छ m. (-च्छः) The apsis of a planet's orbit.<BR> E. मन्द and उच्छ high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोदरी|मंदोदरी
मन्दोदरी f. (-री) A proper name, the wife of RĀVAṆA.<BR> E. मन्द slow,<BR>heavy, उदर the belly, aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोदरीश|मन्दोदरीशः
मन्दोदरीश m. (-शः) A name of RĀVAṆA.<BR> E. मन्दोदरी as above, and ईश<BR>lord or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोदरीसुत|मन्दोदरीसुतः
मन्दोदरीसुत m. (-तः) The son of RĀVAṆA.<BR> E. मन्दोदरी the wife of the king, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोष्ण|मंदोष्ण|मन्दोष्णं
मन्दोष्ण mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं) Temperate, tepid, moderately warm.<BR>	 n. (-ष्णं)<BR>Warmth, gentle heat.<BR> E. मन्द slack, and उष्ण hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्द्र|मंद्र|मन्द्रः
मन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. A base or low tone, such as the grumbling of clouds,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A sort of drum.<BR>	 3. A species of elephant.<BR>	 f. (-द्रा) Hollow,<BR>deep, rumbling.<BR> E. मदि to please, Unādi aff. रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथ|मन्मथः
मन्मथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A name of KĀMA, the god of love.<BR>	 2. Love, amor-<BR>ous passion or desire.<BR>	 3. The elephant or wood-apple.<BR> E. मत् the<BR>heart, मथ् to agitate, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथालय|मन्मथालयः
मन्मथालय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Pudendum muliebre.<BR>	 2. The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथिन्
मन्मथिन् mfn. (-थी-थिनी-थि) Amorous, impassioned, in love.<BR> E. मन्मथ, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मन|मन्मनः
मन्मन m. (-नः) Whispering, murmuring, low reiterated sound, especial-<BR>ly murmur libidinosum.<BR> E. मत् the heart or mind, मन् to express,<BR>aff. अच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मय
मन्मय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Full of me, like me, (God.)<BR> E. मत् and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्यमान
मन्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Thinking, considering.<BR>	 2. Respecting, atten-<BR>ding to.<BR>	 3. Praising.<BR> E. मन् to mind, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्या
मन्या f. (-न्या) The tendon forming the nape of the neck.<BR> E. मन् to mind,<BR>to admire, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्याका
मन्याका f. (-का) The tendon of the trapezium muscle forming the nape<BR>of the neck.<BR> E. मन्या the same, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्यु|मन्युः
मन्यु m. (-न्युः)<BR>	 1. Sorrow, grief.<BR>	 2. Distress, indigence.<BR>	 3. Anger, wrath.<BR>4. A sacrifice.<BR>	 5. Pride.<BR> E. मन् to know, Unādi aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्युमत्|मन्युमन्त्
मन्युमत् mfn. (-मन-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Sorrowful, distressed.<BR>	 2. Angry, wrathful.<BR>E. मन्यु, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्वन्तर|मन्वंतर|मन्वन्तरं
मन्वन्तर n. (-रं) The reign of a MANU, a period equal to seventy-one<BR>ages of the gods, or 306, 720,000 years of mortals, or with its<BR>Sandhi or interval of universal deluge, 308, 448, 000 years; four-<BR>teen Manwantaras constitute a Kalpa; the grand period of<BR>creation and destruction, or 4, 320,000,000 years; each Man-<BR>wantara is governed by its distinct MANU, and is provided with<BR>its own INDRA, and minor deities; according to Hindu cosmo-<BR>gony, there have been innumerable Manwantaras, since the first<BR>creation of the world.<BR> E. मनु MANU, and अन्तर period or interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्वान
मन्वान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Thinking, conceiving.<BR>	 2. Minding, regarding.<BR>E. म्ना to mind, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मपष्ट|मपष्टः
मपष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A sort of bean, (Phaseolus mungo;) also मपष्टक, and मपुष्टक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मपुष्टक|मपुष्टकः
मपुष्टक m. (-कः) A sort of bean, (Phaseolus mungo.) also मयूष्टक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मभ्र्
मभ्र् r. 1st cl. (मभ्रति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मम
मम Ind. The genitive singular of the first personal pronoun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममता
ममता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Pride, arrogance, self-sufficiency.<BR>	 2. The interest or<BR>affection entertained for other objects from considering them as<BR>belonging to or connected with one's self.<BR>	 3. Individuality.<BR> E. मम<BR>mine, the possessive case of अस्मद्, and तल् aff. of the abstract;<BR>also with त्व aff. ममत्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममतायुक्त|ममतायुक्तः
ममतायुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Selfish.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) A miser, a niggard.<BR> E. ममता<BR>selfishness, and युक्त affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसापताल
मसापताल m. (-लः) An object of sense.<BR> E. मव्य to bind, आलन् Unādi aff.,<BR>व rejected, and म substituted for व, and आपतुद् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मय्
मय् r. 1st cl. (मयते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मय|मयः
मय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A camel.<BR>	 2. A mule.<BR>	 3. A demon, and the carpenter<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">Page552-b+ 60</a>]<BR>or architect of the DAITYAS.<BR>	 4. Hurting, injuring.<BR>	 f. (-या) Adminis-<BR>tering remedies, the practice of physic.<BR>	 f. (-यी) Used as and<BR>affix in the sense of “consisting of” “Made of” Full of.<BR> E. मय्<BR>to go, or मि to scatter, or मी to hurt, affs. अच or खल् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयट|मयटः
मयट m. (-टः) A hut of grass or leaves.<BR> E. मय to go, अटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयु|मयुः
मयु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. A KINNARA or chorister of Svarga, 2. A deer.<BR> E. मि to<BR>scatter, (sweet sounds, &c.) Unādi aff. उ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयुराज|मयुराजः
मयुराज m. (-जः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. मयु KINNARA, and राज chief;<BR>having these beings attached especially to his court and capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयुष्टक|मयुष्टकः
मयुष्टक m. (-कः) A sort of bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR> E. मय् to go, aff.<BR>उ, मयु one who goes, ष्टक् to impede, aff. ड, मयुष्ट, and with the<BR>pleonastic addition, कन् मयुष्टक; also with अच् aff. after मय् to go,<BR>मयष्ट, and मयष्टक; and again with प substituted for म, मपष्ट, मपष्टक,<BR>मपुष्ट or मपुष्टक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूख|मयूखः
मयूख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. Light, lustre, brightness.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR>	 3.<BR>Flame.<BR>	 4. Beauty.<BR>	 5. The pin or gnomon of a sun-dial.<BR> E. मा to<BR>measure, (time, &c.,) ऊख Unādi aff., मय substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूर|मयूरः
मयूर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2. A flower, the coxcomb, (Celosia cristata.)<BR>3. A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A pea-hen.<BR>	 2. A<BR>potherb, (Basella rubra, &c.)<BR> E. मि to scatter, Unādi aff. ऊरन्; or<BR>मही the earth in the seventh case, मह्यां, रु to cry, ड aff. and the<BR>formation irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरक|मयूरकं|मयूरकः
मयूरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>	 2. A flower, (Celosia<BR>cristata.)<BR>	 3. A peacock.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Blue vitriol.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरग्रीवक|मयूरग्रीवकं
मयूरग्रीवक n. (-कं) Blue vitriol “तुंँते” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरचटक|मयूरचटकः
मयूरचटक m. (-कः) A house or dunghill cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरचूडा
मयूरचूडा f. (-डा) Coxcomb, (Celosia cristata.)<BR> E. मयूर a peacock. चूडा the comb or crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरपदक|मयूरपदकं
मयूरपदक n. (-कं) A sort of scratch with a finger-nail.<BR> E. मयूर a peacock,<BR>पद a foot, and कन् aff.; implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरारि|मयूरारिः
मयूरारि m. (-रिः) A chameleon, a lizard.<BR> E. मयूर a peacock. and अरि the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरक|मरकः
मरक m. (-कः) Epidemic or pestilential disease.<BR> E. मृ to die, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरकत|मरकतं
मरकत m. (-तः) An emerald.<BR> E. मरक epidemic disease, तॄ to cross or<BR>escape, aff. ड; it is also read मरकतक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरक्त|मरक्तं
मरक्त n. (-क्तं) An emerald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरण|मरणं
मरण n. (-णं) Death, dying.<BR> E. मृ to die, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरत|मरतः
मरत m. (-तः) Death, dying.<BR> E. मृ to die, अतच Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरन्द|मरंद|मरंदः|मरन्दः
मरन्द m. (-न्दः) The nectar or honey of a flower.<BR> E. मकरन्द, q. v. the<BR>second syllable being rejected; also with कन् added मरन्दक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरन्दीकस्
मरन्दीकस् n. (-कः) A flower.<BR> E. मरन्द nectar or honey, ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मराकाली
मराकाली f. (-ली) a plant, commonly Bichati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरार|मरारः
मरार m. (-रः) A granary, a place where grain, &c. is kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मराल|मरालः
मराल mfn. (-लः-ला-ली-लं) Soft, mild, bland.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A sort of goose<BR>with red legs and bill, or perhaps the Flamingo.<BR>	 2. Lamp-black,<BR>used as a collyrium.<BR>	 3. A duck.<BR>	 4. A horse.<BR>	 5. A cloud.<BR>	 6. A<BR>grove or garden of pomegranate trees.<BR>	 7. A rogue, a scoundrel.<BR>f. (-ला) Greasy, soft.<BR> E. मृ to die, aff. आलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरिच|मरिचं|मरिचः
मरिच n. (-चं) Pepper.<BR> E. मृ to die, (venom,) and इच् aff.; considered<BR>as an antidote; also मरीच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरिमन्
मरिमन् m. (-मा) Death, dying.<BR> E. मृ to die, मनिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीच|मरीचं|मरीचः
मरीच n. (-चं) Pepper, (Piper nigrum.)<BR> E. मृ to die, ईच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीचि|मरीचिः
मरीचि m. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. A saint, the son of BRAHMĀ, and one of the Pra-<BR>jāpatis, and Brahmādikas, or first created beings, and sovereigns<BR>of the world.<BR>	 2. A niggard, a miser.<BR>	 mf. (-चिः) A ray of light. E.<BR>मृ to perish, (darkness,) Unādi aff. ईचि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीचिका
मरीचिका f. (-का) The Mirage; vapour which in hot and sandy coun-<BR>tries especially appears at a distance like a sheet of water. E.<BR>मरीचि a ray of light, कन् aff., implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीचिमालिन्
मरीचिमालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Splendid, radiant.<BR>	 m. (-ली) The sun. E.<BR>मरीचि and मालिन् having a chaplet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=552-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरीमृज
मरीमृज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Who or what cleans or rubs repeatedly. E.<BR>मृज् to rub, reiter. v., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरु|मरुः
मरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A region or soil destitute of water, sands, a desert.<BR>	 2.<BR>A mountain.<BR>	 3. The province Mārwār, or in the plu. (-रुवः) The<BR>inhabitants.<BR> E. मृ to die, (where,) and Unādi aff. उ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुक|मरुकः
मरुक m. (-कः) A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुज|मरुजः
मरुज m. (-जः) A sort of perfume, commonly Nakhi.<BR> E. मरु a desert, ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुटा
मरुटा f. (-टा) A woman with a high forehead.<BR> E. मृ to perish, (of love<BR>for such a woman,) उटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुण्डा|मरुंडा
मरुण्डा f. (-ण्डा) A woman with a high forehead.<BR> E. मृ to die, उण्डच् aff.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्
मरुत् m. (-रुत्)<BR>	 1. Wind, air, or its deified personification.<BR>	 2. A deity,<BR>an immortal.<BR>	 n. (-रुत) A sort of perfume, commonly Granthipar-<BR>na.<BR>	 f. (-रुत्) A kind of grass, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR> E. मृ to die,<BR>Unādi aff. उति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत|मरुतः
मरुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A deity.<BR>	 3. A plant, commonly Ghan-<BR>tāpātali.<BR> E. अच् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्कर|मरुत्करः
मरुत्कर m. (-रः) A sort of bean, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR> E. मरुत् wind, (eruc-<BR>tation,) and कर making. “राजमाषे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्त|मरुत्तः
मरुत्त m. (-त्तः)<BR>	 1. Wind, a gale.<BR>	 2. The name of a king.<BR> E. मरुत्, and तप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्पथ|मरुत्पथः
मरुत्पथ m. (-थः) The atmosphere, sky, heaven.<BR> E. मरुत् the wind, and<BR>पथ road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्पाल|मरुत्पालः
मरुत्पाल m. (-लः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. मरुत् the wind, and पाल who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्पुत्त्र
मरुत्पुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) BHĪMASENA, the second of the PĀṆḌU princes. E.<BR>मरुत् the deity of the wind, and पुत्त्र son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्प्लव|मरुत्प्लवः
मरुत्प्लव m. (-वः) A lion.<BR> E. मरुत् wind, and प्लव who leaps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्फल|मरुत्फलं
मरुत्फल n. (-लं) Hail.<BR> E. मरुत् wind, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्वत्|मरुत्वन्त्
मरुत्वत् m. (-त्वान्)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. The monkey Hanumāna.<BR>	 3.<BR>A cloud.<BR> E. मरुत् wind, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुत्सख|मरुत्सखः
मरुत्सख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. The Chittraka-tree.<BR> E. मरुत् the<BR>wind, (the deity.) and सखि friend, aff. टच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुदान्दोल|मरुदांदोल|मरुदान्दोलः
मरुदान्दोल m. (-लः) A sort of fan made of deer's or buffalo's skin. E.<BR>मरुत् wind, आन्दोल agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्ध्वज|मरुद्ध्वजं
मरुद्ध्वज n. (-जं) Flocculent seeds wafted by the wind, the down of<BR>cotton floating in the air.<BR> E. मरुत् wind, ध्वज standard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्बद्ध|मरुद्बद्धः
मरुद्बद्ध m. (-द्धः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A sort of vessel used in sacrifices.<BR>	 3.<BR>A portion of the Sāma Veda.<BR> E. मरुत् the wind, बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्रथ|मरुद्रथः
मरुद्रथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. A car in which idols are carried.<BR> E. मरुत्<BR>the wind, and रथ a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्रुम|मरुद्रुमः
मरुद्रुम m. (-मः) A fœtid mimosa.<BR> E. मरु dry, द्रुम a tree. “विट्खदिरे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्वर्त्मन्
मरुद्वर्त्मन् n. (-र्त्म) The atmosphere, heaven, sky.<BR> E. मरुत् the wind, and<BR>वर्त्मन् road or path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्वाह|मरुद्वाहः
मरुद्वाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Smoke.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. Chittraka tree.<BR> E. मरुत् wind, वाह vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्विप|मरुद्विपः
मरुद्विप m. (-पः) A camel.<BR> E. मरु the desert, and द्विप the elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुद्वृता
मरुद्वृता f. (-ता) The Kāverī river in the peninsula.<BR> E. मरुत् the wind,<BR>and वृत covered, screened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुन्माला
मरुन्माला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A sort of grass, (Trigonella corniculata.) “पिडिङ्-<BR>शाक.<BR>	 2. Another plant, commonly Belsuṇṭh.<BR> E. मरुत् a deity, and<BR>माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुप्रिय|मरुप्रियः
मरुप्रिय m. (-यः) A camel.<BR> E. मरु a sandy soil, and प्रिय fond of; it also<BR>occurs मरुत्प्रिय m. (-यः) from मरुत् wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुभू
मरुभू m. (-भूः) The province of Mārwār, or plu. (-भुवः) The inhabitants<BR>of Mārwār.<BR> E. मरु sandy, and भू country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुल|मरुलः
मरुल m. (-लः) A sort of duck.<BR> E. मृ to die, उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुवक|मरुवकः
मरुवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A large thorny shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>species of basil (Ocymun.) described as having small leaves and<BR>red flowers.<BR>	 3. A variety of the citron or lime, said to be a thorny<BR>plant, and to bear a small fruit.<BR>	 4. A flower, (Artemisia vulgaris.)<BR>5. A tiger.<BR>	 6. The ascending node.<BR>	 7. A crane.<BR> E. मरु a sandy or<BR>dry soil, वा to grow or go, aff. क, and कन्, added; it sometimes<BR>occurs, मरूवक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरुस्थल
मरुस्थल nf. (-लं-ली) A desert, a dry and desert tract.<BR> E. मरु, स्थल a<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरूक|मरूकः
मरूक m. (-कः) A sort of deer.<BR> E. मृ to die, ऊकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरूद्भवा
मरूद्भवा f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A cucumber.<BR>	 2. Wild-cotton.<BR>	 3. A small species of<BR>the fœtid mimosa.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR> E. मरु dry<BR>soil, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरोलि|मरोलिः
मरोलि m. (-लिः) The Makara, a marine monster, apparently the<BR>Monodon or unicorn, and usually confounded with the crocodile<BR>or shark.<BR> E. मृ to die, (by it.) ओलच् aff.; also with कन् added<BR>मरोलिक m. (-कः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्क|मर्कः
मर्क m. (-र्कः)<BR>	 1. The air, the wind.<BR>	 2. The body.<BR>	 3. A monkey.<BR> E. मर्च<BR>to sound, or a Santra root, to move, Unādi aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कक|मर्ककः
मर्कक m. (-कः) A spider.<BR> E. मर्क going, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कट|मर्कटः
मर्कट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A monkey, or ape.<BR>	 2. A spider.<BR>	 3. The large crane,<BR>called in India the adjutant, (Ardea argala.)<BR>	 4. A mode of sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR>	 5. A kind of venom.<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. A variety of grey<BR>Bonduc, (Guilandina bonduccella.)<BR>	 2. Cowatch, (Carpopogon<BR>pruriens.)<BR>	 3. A small or female monkey.<BR> E. मर्क a Sautra root,<BR>to go, Unādi aff. अटन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटक|मर्कटकः
मर्कटक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A spider.<BR>	 2. An ape.<BR>	 3. A fruit.<BR>	 4. A demon.<BR>	 5. A<BR>kind of fish.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटपिप्पली
मर्कटपिप्पली f. (-ली) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR> E. मर्कट an ape,<BR>and पिप्पली long pepper. “अपामार्गे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटप्रिय|मर्कटप्रियः
मर्कटप्रिय m. (-यः) A tree, a kind, of Mimosa, (M. kauki.)<BR> E. मर्कट mon-<BR>key and प्रिय beloved. “खिरुइ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटवास|मर्कटवासः
मर्कटवास m. (-सः) A spider's web, a cobweb.<BR> E. मर्कट a spider, and वास<BR>abode; also with कन् added मर्कटवासक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटशीर्ष|मर्कटशीर्षं
मर्कटशीर्ष n. (-र्ष) Vermilion. “हिङ्गुले ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटास्य|मर्कटास्यं
मर्कटास्य n. (-स्यं) Copper.<BR> E. मर्कट a monkey, and आस्य face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्कटेन्दु|मर्कटेंदु|मर्कटेन्दुः
मर्कटेन्दु m. (-न्दुः) A sort of ebony, (Diospyros melanoxylon.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्करा
मर्करा f. (-रा) A cave, a hole, a chasm.<BR>	 2. A vessel.<BR>	 3. A barren or<BR>childless woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्च|मर्च्च
मर्च r. 4th and 10th cls. (मर्चति मर्चयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sound 2. To go.<BR>	 3. To take.<BR>	 4. To cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्ज्जू|मर्जू
मर्ज्जू f. (-र्ज्जूः) Cleaning, cleansing, purification.<BR>	 m. (-र्ज्जूः)<BR>	 1. A washer-<BR>man.<BR>	 2. A catamite.<BR> E. मृज् to cleanse, aff. ऊन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्त्त|मर्त|मर्तः|मर्त्तः
मर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. A man, a mortal.<BR>	 2. The world of mortals.<BR> E. मृ to<BR>die, तन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्त्तव्य|मर्तव्य
मर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Mortal, what must or should die.<BR> E. मृ to die, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्त्त्य
मर्त्त्य m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. A man, a mortal.<BR>	 2. The earth, the world, the habi-<BR>tation of mortals.<BR>	 f. (-र्त्त्या) A woman, a female.<BR>	 n. (-र्त्त्यं) The body.<BR>E. मर्त्त as above, यत् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्त्त्यमुख
मर्त्त्यमुख m. (-खः) A demi-god, attendant on KUVERA, a KINNARA, a<BR>Yakṣa, being the figure of an animal and the head of a man. E.<BR>मर्त्त्य a mortal, and मुख chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द|मर्दः
मर्द m. (-र्दः)<BR>	 1. A violent stroke.<BR>	 2. Grinding, crushing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द्दन|मर्दन|मर्द्दनं
मर्द्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rubbing, touching.<BR>	 2. Grinding, pounding, &c.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pressing.<BR>	 4. Devastating.<BR>	 5. Paining.<BR> E. मृद् to rub or grind, aff.<BR>ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द्दनीय|मर्दनीय
मर्द्दनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be rubbed or touched.<BR> E. मृद् to rub, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द्दयित्वा|मर्दयित्वा
मर्द्दयित्वा Ind. Having rubbed or touched.<BR> E. मृद् to rub, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द्दल|मर्दल|मर्दलः|मर्द्दलः
मर्द्दल m. (-लः) A sort of drum.<BR> E. मृद् to rub or strike, aff. अच्; मर्द्द<BR>striking, and ला to get, aff. क । “मांँदल ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्द्दित|मर्दित|मर्द्दितं
मर्द्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Strung, tied.<BR>	 2. Rubbed, ground, pounded.<BR>	 2.<BR>Obtained, got.<BR> E. मृद् to rub, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्ब|मर्ब्ब
मर्ब r. 1st cl. (मर्बति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मज्ञ|मर्मज्ञ|मर्मज्ञः|मर्म्मज्ञः
मर्म्मज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A learned and intelligent man or Brāhmana.<BR> E. मर्म्म se-<BR>cret meaning, (of the Shāstras.) and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मन्|मर्मन्
मर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. A joint, an articulation of the body.<BR>	 2. A vital mem-<BR>ber or organ.<BR>	 3. Secret meaning or purpose, a secret, any thing<BR>hidden or recondite.<BR> E. मृ to die, aff. मनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=553-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मभेदिन्|मर्मभेदिन्
मर्म्मभेदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Fatal.<BR>	 2. Penetrating, piercing.<BR>	 2. Pain-<BR>ful.<BR> E. मर्म्म and भेदिन् what cuts or breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मर|मर्मर|मर्मरः|मर्म्मरः
मर्म्मर m. (-रः) The rustling sound of cloth or dry leaves.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A<BR>sort of pine, (P. Devadāru.)<BR>	 2. Turmeric.<BR> E. मृ to die, अरन् aff.,<BR>and मुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मरीक|मर्मरीक|मर्मरीकः|मर्म्मरीकः
मर्म्मरीक m. (-कः) A pauper, a low or humble man.<BR> E. मृ to die, (with<BR>distress,) Unādi aff. ईकन् and the root reduplicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मविद्|मर्मविद्
मर्म्मविद् m. (-विद् or -वित्) A learned and intelligent man or Brāhmana.<BR>E. मर्म्म secret, meaning, (of the Shāstras.) and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मवेदिन्|मर्मवेदिन्
मर्म्मवेदिन् m. (-दी) An acute and intelligent man.<BR> E. मर्म्म secret, and<BR>वेदिन् who knows: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मस्पृश्|मर्मस्पृश्
मर्म्मस्पृश् mfn. (-स्पृक्) Sharp, corrosive, giving pain.<BR> E. मर्म्म a joint, and स्पृश् what touches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्माविद्
मर्म्माविद् mfn. (-विद् or -वित्) Piercing or affecting the joints, (pain,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. मर्म्म a joint, व्यध् to pierce or pain, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मावेदिन्
मर्म्मावेदिन् m. (-दी) An acute and intelligent man.<BR> E. मर्म्म secret, the<BR>semi-vowel and following vowel of the radical changed to इ, and<BR>the final vowel of the noun made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्म्मिक|मर्मिक|मर्म्मिकः
मर्म्मिक m. (-कः) An intelligent and penetrating man.<BR> E. मर्म्म a joint,<BR>and ठक् aff.: see मर्म्मविद् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्य्या|मर्या
मर्य्या f. (-य्या) A boundary, a limit.<BR> E. मृ-यत् Ind. Bounding, limitative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्य्यादा|मर्यादा
मर्य्यादा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. Continance in the right way, propriety of conduct,<BR>steadiness, rectitude.<BR>	 2. A boundary, a limit.<BR>	 3. An agreement.<BR>4. A bank, a shore.<BR> E. मर्य्या limitative, आदा to have or take, affs.<BR>अङ् and टाप्; or परि about, round, prefixed to आदा, अङ् aff. and<BR>म substituted for प ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्व|मर्व्व
मर्व r. 1st cl. (मर्वति)<BR>	 1. To fill.<BR>	 2. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्श|मर्शः
मर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Counsel, advice.<BR>	 2. A sternutatory.<BR> E. मृश् to counsel, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्शन|मर्शनं
मर्शन n. (-नं) Advising, counselling, deliberating.<BR>	 2. Examination, in-<BR>quiry.<BR>	 3. Rubbing, touching.<BR> E. मृश् to counsel, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्ष|मर्षः
मर्ष m. (-र्षः) Patience, endurance.<BR> E. मृष to bear with, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्षण|मर्षणं
मर्षण n. (-णं) Enduring, bearing, patience, resignation.<BR> E. मृष् to bear<BR>with, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्षित|मर्षितः
मर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Borne, endured.<BR>	 2. Patient, content.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Patience.<BR> E. मृष् to bear with, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मर्षितवत्
मर्षितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Patient, enduring.<BR> E. मृष् to bear, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्
मल् r. 1st cl. (मलते) r. 10th cl. (मलयति)<BR>	 1. To hold.<BR>	 2. To wear.<BR>	 3.<BR>To stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल|मलः
मल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Dirty.<BR>	 2. Miserly, niggardly.<BR>	 mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Excretion of the body, as serum, semen, blood, marrow, urine,<BR>fæces, ear-wax, nails, phlegm, tears, rheum, and sweat.<BR>	 2. Sin.<BR>	 3.<BR>dirt, filth.<BR>	 4. Dreg, sediment.<BR>	 5. Rust.<BR>	 6. Camphor.<BR>	 7. Cuttle-<BR>fish-bone.<BR>	 8. Tanned leather.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A particular base metal.<BR>f. (-ला) A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta:) see झटामला.<BR> E. मल्<BR>to hold or contain, (in the body.) अच aff.; or मृज् to cleanse,<BR>Unādi aff. कल, and the penultimate and final radical rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलज|मलजं
मलज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced from dregs or dirt, &c.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Pus,<BR>matter.<BR> E. मल as above, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलदूषित|मलदूषितं
मलदूषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Foul, dirty, filthy.<BR> E. मल dirt, दूषित faulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलद्रव|मलद्रवः
मलद्रव m. (-वः) Diarrhœa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलधात्री
मलधात्री f. (-त्री) A nurse who attends to the necessities of a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलन|मलनं|मलनः
मलन m. (-नः) A tent.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Rubbing, grinding, &c.<BR> E. मल् to hold,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलपङ्किन्
मलपङ्किन् mfn. (-ङ्की-ङ्किनी-ङ्कि) Filthy, covered with mud and dirt.<BR> E. मल and पङ्क mud, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलपू
मलपू f. (-पूः) The opposite-leaved fig tree, (Ficus oppositifolia, Rox.)<BR>E. मल sin, पू to purify, aff. क्विप्; it is also read with a final con-<BR>sonant, derived from पूर् to complete or fill, मलपूर् f. (-पूः) Also<BR>मलयू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलपृष्ठ
मलपृष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) The outer page of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलभुज्
मलभुज् m. (-भुक्) A crow.<BR> E. मल dirt, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलमल्लक|मलमल्लकः
मलमल्लक n. (-कं) A piece of cloth covering the privities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलमास|मलमासः
मलमास m. (-सः) An intercalary month, in which any performance of<BR>religious ceremonies is strictly prohibited in the Shāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलय|मलयः
मलय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A mountain or mountainous range, from which the<BR>best Sandal-wood is brought, answering to the western Ghats in<BR>the peninsula of India.<BR>	 2. The country that lies along the Malaya<BR>range, or the west coast of the peninsula, Malayālam or Mālābār.<BR>3. A garden.<BR>	 4. The garden of INDRA.<BR>	 5. One of the minor Dwi-<BR>pas or divisions of the world.<BR>	 f. (-या) A plant, commonly Teorī,<BR>(Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR> E. मल् to hold or contain, (Sandal-wood.)<BR>Unādi aff. कयन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयगन्धिनी
मलयगन्धिनी f. (-नी) One of DURGĀ'S female attendants.<BR> E. मलय the<BR>mountain, and गन्धिन् fragrant; also मलयवासिनी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयज|मलयजं|मलयजः
मलयज mn. (-जः-ज) Sandal-wood.<BR> E. मलय the mountain Malaya, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयाचल|मलयाचलः
मलयाचल m. (-लः) The mountain Malaya.<BR> E. मलय Malaya, and अचल a<BR>mountain; also similar compounds, as मलयाद्रि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयानिल|मलयानिलः
मलयानिल m. (-लः) The southerly wind that prevails in central India<BR>during the hot weather. The Malaya Zephyr charged with the<BR>sent of Sandal-wood or other herbs is a poetical common-place.<BR>E. मलय the Malaya mountain, over which the air is supposed to<BR>have blown, and अनिल wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलयू
मलयू f. (-यूः) The opposite-leaved fig tree.<BR> E. मल sin, यु to join, aff. क्विप्<BR>and the final made long; also with the final short मलयु, or de-<BR>rived from पूञ, मलपू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलवासस्
मलवासस् f. (-सा) A woman in her courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलवाहिन्
मलवाहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) What conveys or contains soil or filth.<BR>E. मल and वाहिन् bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलाकर्षिन्
मलाकर्षिन् m. (-र्षी) A sweeper, a cleaner.<BR> E. मल dirt, fæces, and कृष् to<BR>draw, with आङ् prefix, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलाका
मलाका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A female messenger.<BR>	 2. A lewd woman.<BR>	 3. A female<BR>elephant.<BR> E. मल, आक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलापकर्षण|मलापकर्षणं
मलापकर्षण n. (-णं) Purification, cleaning, cleansing.<BR> E. मल dirt, excrescence, अपकर्षण removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलावह|मलावहं
मलावह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Soiling, dirtying.<BR>	 2. Defiling, disgracing.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-हः) Acceptance of forbidden gifts.<BR> E. मल and आवह what brings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलाशय|मलाशयः
मलाशय m. (-यः) The belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलि|मलिः
मलि f. (-लिः) Having, possessing.<BR> E. मल् to hold, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिन|मलिनं
मलिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Dirty, filth, foul.<BR>	 2. Black.<BR>	 3. Vile, bad.<BR>	 4.<BR>Foul, (figuratively,) soiled with crime or vice, sinful, depraved.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Butter-milk.<BR>	 2. Fault, defect.<BR>	 3. Borax.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A woman<BR>during menstruation.<BR> E. मल dirt, इलन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनप्रभ
मलिनप्रभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Obscured, beclouded.<BR> E. मलिन and प्रभा light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनमुख|मलिनमुखः
मलिनमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-ख)<BR>	 1. Cruel, fierce savage.<BR>	 2. Vile, wicked.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-खः)<BR>	 1. AGNI or fire.<BR>	 2. A ghost, a goblin.<BR>	 3. The black-faced<BR>monkey.<BR>	 4. The Chittraka tree.<BR> E. मलिन black, and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनाम्बु|मलिनांबु
मलिनाम्बु m. (-म्बुः) Ink.<BR> E. मलिन dirty, and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनास्य|मलिनास्यः
मलिनास्य m. (-स्यः) A savage, a cruel or ferocious man.<BR> E. मलिन black,<BR>foul, (with fury,) and आस्य the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनित
मलिनित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Soiled, defiled.<BR>	 2. Corrupted, wicked. E.<BR>मलिन and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिनिमन्
मलिनिमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Impurity, sin.<BR>	 2. Darkness, blackness.<BR>	 3. Dirtiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिम्लुच|मलिम्लुचः
मलिम्लुच m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. A thief.<BR>	 2. Burning, blazing.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR>	 4. Air, wind.<BR>5. The intercalary lunar month, introduced every third year, in<BR>order to approximate the lunar, and solar modes of computation.<BR>6. A gnat, a musquito.<BR>	 7. Frost.<BR>	 8. A thief, a robber.<BR>	 9. A Brāh-<BR>mana who neglects the five daily acts of piety.<BR>	 10. A demon. E.<BR>मलि possession, and म्लुच् to steal, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलिष्ठ
मलिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Very foul or unclean.<BR>	 2. Very wicked.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>A woman during menstruation.<BR> E. मल unclean, इष्टन् aff. of the<BR>superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलीमस|मलीमसं|मलीमसः
मलीमस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Dirty, foul, unclean.<BR>	 2. Wicked.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>1. Iron.<BR>	 2. Green vitriol.<BR> E. मल dirt, इमसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=554-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलीयस्
मलीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Very dirty or impure.<BR>	 2. Very wicked.<BR>E. मल and ईयसुन् aff. of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलूक|मलूकः
मलूक m. (-कः) A kind of worm.<BR> E. मल dirt, ऊकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्ल्
मल्ल् r. 1st. cl. (मल्लते) To hold, to have.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्ल|मल्लः
मल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं)<BR>	 1. Strong, stout, athletic, robust.<BR>	 2. Best, excell-<BR>ent m. (-ल्लः)<BR>	 1. A wrestler, a boxer, by birth; the offspring of<BR>an outcaste Kṣatriya by a Kṣatriya female.<BR>	 2. A cup or vessel.<BR>3. The cheek and temples, the hemicranium.<BR>	 4. A kind of fish.<BR>5. The residue of an oblation.<BR>	 f. (-ल्ला)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. Arabian<BR>jasmine.<BR>	 3. Ornamenting the person with coloured unguents. E.<BR>मल्ल् to hold, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लक|मल्लकः
मल्लक mf. (-ल्लकः-ल्लिका) An oil-vessel, a vessel made of the shell of<BR>a cocoanut for holding oil, whether for culinary purposes<BR>or for burning as a lamp.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A tooth.<BR> E. मल्ल् to hold,<BR>aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लज|मल्लजं
मल्लज n. (-जं) Black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लतूर्य्य|मल्लतूर्य|मल्लतूर्य्यं
मल्लतूर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) A musical instrument, a drum or trumpet used at<BR>athletic contests.<BR> E. मल्ल wrestler, and तूर्य्य an instrument of music;<BR>it is also occurs गन्धतूर्य्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लनाग|मल्लनागः
मल्लनाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The elephant of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A name of the saint<BR>VĀTSYĀYANA.<BR>	 3. A letter-carrier.<BR>	 4. A work on amorous topics by<BR>VĀTSYĀYANA Muni.<BR> E. मल्ल strong, and नाग an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लभू
मल्लभू f. (-भूः) A palæstrum or arena, a place for athletic contests; it<BR>is also applied to the site of any conflict, as a field of battle, &c.<BR>E. मल्ल a wrestler, and भू earth, place; also मल्लभूमि f. (-मिः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लयात्रा
मल्लयात्रा f. (-त्रा) A match of wrestling or boxing.<BR> E. मल्ल a wrestler, and<BR>यात्रा a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लयुद्ध|मल्लयुद्धं
मल्लयुद्ध n. (-द्धं) Wrestling, boxing.<BR> E. मल्ल a wrestler, युद्ध contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लारी
मल्लारी f. (-री) One the of Rāginis or divisions of the musical mode<BR>Megha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लि|मल्लिः
मल्लि m. (-ल्लिः)<BR>	 1. Having, holding.<BR>	 2. One of the Jinas or Jaina saints,<BR>the 19th of the present era.<BR>	 f. (-ल्लिः-ल्ली) Arabian jasmine, (Jas-<BR>minum zambac.)<BR> E. मल्ल् to hold, Unādi aff. इन् and ङीष् optionally<BR>added for the fem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिक|मल्लिकः
मल्लिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A bird, said to be a sort of goose with brown legs<BR>and bill.<BR>	 2. A shuttle.<BR>	 3. The month Māgha.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Arabian<BR>jasmine, (Jasminum zambac.)<BR>	 2. A kind of fish.<BR>	 3. An earthen<BR>vessel for holding oil, &c.<BR>	 4. A goblet, a cup, a drinking vessel.<BR>5. A river.<BR> E. कन् added to मल्लि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिकाक्ष|मल्लिकाक्षः
मल्लिकाक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A horse marked with white about the eyes.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of goose with brown legs and bill.<BR> E. मल्लिका the jasmine and<BR>अक्ष the eye, being of like whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिकापुष्प|मल्लिकापुष्पः
मल्लिकापुष्प m. (-ष्पः) Arabian jasmine.<BR> E. मल्लिका the same, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिगन्धि|मल्लिगंधि
मल्लिगन्धि m. (-न्धिः) Aloe-wood.<BR> E. मल्लि jasmine, and गन्धि smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिनाथ|मल्लिनाथः
मल्लिनाथ m. (-थः) Name of a celebrated commentator who lived at the<BR>beginning of the fifth century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लिपत्र|मल्लिपत्रं
मल्लिपत्र n. (-त्रं) A mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मल्लु|मल्लुः
मल्लु m. (-ल्लुः) A bear.<BR> E. मल्ल् to hold, aff. उ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मव्
मव् r. 1st cl. (मवति) To bind, to tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मवित|मवितः
मवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Strung, tied.<BR> E. मू to bind, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मव्य्
मव्य् r. 1st cl. (मवति) To bind, to tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मश्
मश् r. 1st cl. (मशति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To be angry or irascible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मश|मशः
मश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Anger.<BR>	 2. Sounding.<BR>	 3. A musquito.<BR> E. मश to sound,<BR>&c., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशक|मशकः
मशक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A gnat, a musquito.<BR>	 2. A kind of cutaneous eruption<BR>the formation of small pustules or warts.<BR>	 3. A leather water-bag.<BR>E. मश् to be angry and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशकिन्
मशकिन् m. (-का) The glomerous fig-tree.<BR> E. मशक a gnat, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशच्छद|मशछद
मशच्छद m. (-दः) A sort of grass, (Andropogon serratus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशहरी
मशहरी f. (-री) Musquito curtains, bed-curtains of gauze, or of any<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">Page555-b+ 60</a>]<BR>thin substance, used to keep off musquitoes.<BR> E. मश् a musquito,<BR>हृ to take off, ट and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मशुन|मशुनः
मशुन m. (-नः) A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मष्
मष् r. 1st cl. (मषति) To injure, to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मषि|मषिः
मषि f. (-षिः-षी)<BR>	 1. Ink.<BR>	 2. The stalk of the Nyctanthes tristis.<BR> E. मष् to<BR>hurt, इन् aff.; also मशि or मसि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस|मसः
मस(इर्, ई)इर् मसी r. 4th cl. (मस्यति)<BR>	 1. To mete or measure by<BR>weight, bulk, length, &c.<BR>	 2. To change from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस|मसः
मस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Measure.<BR>	 2. Weight.<BR> E. मस् to measure, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसक|मसकः
मसक m. (-कः) A gnat.<BR> E. मष् to hurt, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसन|मसनं
मसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Hurting.<BR>	 2. Measuring.<BR>	 3. A medicinal fruit, (Serratula<BR>anthelmintica.)<BR> E. मष् to hurt, ल्यु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसार|मसारः
मसार m. (-रः) An emerald.<BR> E. मस weight, ऋ to go or get, aff. अण्; also<BR>with कन् added मसारक; in some places it seems to be confounded<BR>with another gem of a blue colour, perhaps the sapphire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसि|मसिः
मसि mf. (-सिः-सी)<BR>	 1. Ink.<BR>	 2. The stalk of the Nyctanthes tristis.<BR>	 3.<BR>Lamp-black.<BR>	 4. A black powder used as a collyrium.<BR> E. मस् to<BR>weigh, Unādi aff. इन्; it also occurs, मशि, मशी, मषि and मषी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिक|मसिकः
मसिक m. (-कः) A snake's hole.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Nyctanthes<BR>tristis.)<BR>	 2. Ink.<BR> E. मसि the stalk of the plant, &c., कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिकूपी
मसिकूपी f. (-पी) An inkstand.<BR> E. मसि ink, कूपी a little well; also with<BR>कन् added मसिकूपिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिधान|मसिधानं
मसिधान nf. (-नं-नी) An inkstand.<BR> E. ससि ink, and धान what holds or<BR>contains; also मशिधान, मषिधान, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिन|मसिनं
मसिन n. (-नं) Alliance by the right of presenting the funeral meat-<BR>balls to a deceased common progenitor.<BR> E. मस् to measure, (affi-<BR>nity,) Unādi aff. इनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिपण्य|मसिपण्यः
मसिपण्य m. (-ण्यः) A scribe, a clerk, an accountant.<BR> E. मसि ink, पण्य hireable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिपथ|मसिपथः
मसिपथ m. (-थः) A pen.<BR> E. मसि and पथ path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिप्रसू
मसिप्रसू f. (-सूः)<BR>	 1. An inkstand.<BR>	 2. A pen.<BR> E. मसि ink, प्रसू parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिमणि|मसिमणिः
मसिमणि f. (-णिः) An inkstand.<BR> E. मसि ink, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसिवर्द्धन
मसिवर्द्धन n. (-नं) Gum myrrh.<BR> E. ममि ink, वृद्ध् to increase, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसीजल|मसीजलं
मसीजल n. (-लं) Writing ink.<BR> E. मसी ink, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसीधानी
मसीधानी f. (-नी) An inkstand.<BR> E. मसी ink, धानी what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसीना
मसीना f. (-ना) Linseed, (Linum utilatissimum.)<BR> E. मस्-इनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसुर|मसुरः
मसुर mf. (-रः-रा) A sort of pulse or lentil, (Ervum hirsutum, or Cicer<BR>lens.)<BR>	 f. (-रा) A whore.<BR> E. मस् to weigh, Unādi aff. उरच्; more<BR>usually मसूर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसूर|मसूरः
मसूर mf. (-रः-रा) A sort of pulse or lentil, (Ervum hirsutum, and<BR>Cicer lens.)<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A whore.<BR>	 2. A lentil.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Small pox.<BR>2. A small round pillow.<BR> E. मस् to weigh, Unādi aff. ऊरच्, मसूर,<BR>the pulse; the other meanings refer to this, implying resem-<BR>blance to the pea in figure, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसूरक|मसूरकः
मसूरक m. (-कः) A small round pillow.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसूरविदला
मसूरविदला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A black variety of the plant, commonly called<BR>Teorī, (Convolvulous turpethum.)<BR>	 2. A twining shrub, (Echites<BR>frutescens.)<BR> E. मसूर pulse, विदल division; having a leaf like a<BR>split pea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसूरिका
मसूरिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A bawd, a procuress.<BR>	 2. Small pox.<BR>	 3. A musquito-<BR>curtain.<BR> E. मसूरा a whore, aff. कन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मसृण|मसृणं
मसृण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Smooth, soft, not hard, not rough.<BR>	 2. Bland,<BR>mild, unctuous.<BR>	 3. Sweet, soft.<BR>	 f. (-णा) Linseed.<BR> E. मस् to mea-<BR>sure or weigh, aff. ऋण, form irr.; or सम equally, smoothly,<BR>ऋण् to go or be, aff. क, and the initiatory letters irregularly<BR>transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्क्
मस्क् r. 1st cl. (मस्कति) To go, to move: sometimes read मष्क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्कर|मस्करः
मस्कर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bamboo.<BR>	 2. A hollow bamboo.<BR>	 3. Going, motion.<BR>4. Knowledge.<BR> E. मस्क् to go, aff. अरच्; or मकि to adorn, aff. अर,<BR>and the nasal rejected, with सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्करिन्
मस्करिन् m. (-री)<BR>	 1. The Brāhmana of the fourth and mendicant<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">Page556-a+ 60</a>]<BR>order 2. The moon.<BR> E. मस्कर a bamboo, (staff,) and इनि posses-<BR>sive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=555-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्ज्
मस्ज्(टु, ओ)टुमस्जो r. 6th cl. (मज्जति)<BR>	 1. To immerse, to sink or plunge<BR>in water.<BR>	 2. The purify by washing or bathing.<BR>	 3. To be dis-<BR>heartened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्त|मस्तं
मस्त n. (-स्तं) The head; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तक|मस्तकं|मस्तकः
मस्तक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. The head, the skull.<BR>	 2. The head or top of any<BR>thing.<BR> E. मस् to weigh, aff. क्त, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तकपिण्डक|मस्तकपिंडक|मस्तकपिण्डकः
मस्तकपिण्डक mn. (-कः-कं) A protuberance on the temples of an elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तकमूलक
मस्तकमूलक n. (-कं) The neck, the upper part of it supporting the head.<BR>E. मस्तक the head, मूल the root, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तकस्नेह|मस्तकस्नेहः
मस्तकस्नेह m. (-हः) The brain.<BR> E. मस्तक the head, and स्नेह marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तकाख्य|मस्तकाख्यः
मस्तकाख्य m. (-ख्यः) The top of a tree.<BR> E. मस्तक, आख्या appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तदारु|मस्तदारुः
मस्तदारु n. (-रुं) The Devadāru tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्ति|मस्तिः
मस्ति f. (-स्तिः) Weighing, measuring.<BR> E. मस् to weigh, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तिष्क|मस्तिष्कं
मस्तिष्क m. (-ष्कः) The brain.<BR> E. मस्-क्तिन् मस्तिं परिणति भेदं मुष्कति मुष्क गतौ<BR>अच् पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तिष्कत्वच्
मस्तिष्कत्वच् f. (-त्वक्) The membrance surrounding the brain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तु
मस्तु n. (-स्तुः)<BR>	 1. The watery part of curds, the whey.<BR>	 2. Sour cream. E.<BR>मस् to weigh, Unādi aff. तुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मस्तुलुङ्ग|मस्तुलुंग|मस्तुलुङ्गः
मस्तुलुङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The brain; it also occurs मस्तुलुङ्गक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मह्
मह् r. 1st and 10th cls. (महति महयति-ते) To revere, to worship, to<BR>adore. (इ)महि r. 1st cl. (मंहते) To grow or increase. r. 10th cl.<BR>(मंहयति)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मह|महं|महः
मह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A festival.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR>	 3. A buffalo.<BR>	 4. Sacrifice,<BR>oblation.<BR>	 f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. A cow.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioi-<BR>des.)<BR> E. मह् to worship, aff. घञ्: see महस and महि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महक|महकः
महक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An excellent man.<BR>	 2. A tortoise.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR> E. मह् to worship, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महक्क|महक्कः
महक्क m. (-क्कः) Diffusive fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महत्|महन्त्
महत् mfn. (-हान्-हती-हत्)<BR>	 1. Great, large, bulky.<BR>	 2. Much, many.<BR>	 3.<BR>Best, excellent, illustrious.<BR>	 4. Loud.<BR>	 5. Far advanced.<BR>	 6. Long.<BR>	 7.<BR>Intense.<BR>	 8. Important.<BR>	 9. Eminent, high.<BR>	 10. Dense, thick.<BR>	 11.<BR>Numerous.<BR>	 n. (-त्)<BR>	 1. Kingdom, dominion.<BR>	 2. The intellectual<BR>principle, the second principle in creation.<BR>	 3. Sacred knowledge.<BR>4. Infinity, greatness. Adv. Much, very, exceeding.<BR>	 f. (-ती) The<BR>Vinā or lute of NĀRADA, containing seven or one hundred<BR>strings.<BR>	 2. The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>	 m. (-हान्)<BR>	 1. The<BR>second of the twenty five principles of creation according to<BR>Sānkhya philosophy.<BR>	 2. A camel.<BR>	 3. An epithet of Rudra.<BR> E. मह् to<BR>worship, अति Unādi aff. In composition महा is generally substi-<BR>tuted, आ being inserted in place of the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महत्तर|महत्तरः
महत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Greater, more.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A man of the fourth<BR>or servile tribe, a Śūdra.<BR>	 2. The headman of a village.<BR>	 3. A<BR>courtier.<BR> E. महत् great, and तरप् aff. of comparison, perhaps in<BR>derision, or in comparison with the mixed tribes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महत्त्व|महत्त्वं
महत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) Greatness, either in bulk or rank.<BR> E. महत् great, त्व aff. of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महदाश्चर्य्य|महदाश्चर्य
महदाश्चर्य्य n. Adv. (-र्य्यं) Very surprising.<BR> E. महत् and आश्वर्य्य surprising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महदाश्रय|महदाश्रयः
महदाश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Dependent upon or attached to the great. E.<BR>महत् and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महद्विल
महद्विल n. (-लं) Æther, heaven, Akās.<BR> E. महत् great and विल a variety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महन्त|महंतः|महन्तः
महन्त m. (-न्तः) The head of a monastery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्लोक|महर्लोकः
महर्लोक m. (-कः) A division of the universe; a region said to be one<BR>Crore or Yojanas above the polar star, and to be the abode of<BR>those saints who survive a destruction of the world.<BR> E. महस् sa-<BR>crifice, लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्षि|महर्षिः
महर्षि m. (-र्षिः) A Ṛshi or saint of a particular order, including VYĀSA<BR>and others.<BR> E. मह for महत् great, and ऋषि saint: see राजर्षि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महल्लक|महल्लकः
महल्लक m. (-कः) An eunuch employed in a Hārem.<BR>	 2. A large<BR>house.<BR>	 f. (-ल्लिका) Feeble.<BR> E. महल्ल said to mean the inner apart-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">Page556-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ments, probably an Arabic word, and कन् added: otherwise with<BR>ठक् added महल्लिक m. (-कः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महस्
महस् n. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A festival, a sacred festival.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR>	 3.<BR>Greatness, vigour.<BR>	 4. Sacrifice, oblation.<BR> E. मह to worship, aff.<BR>असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महस|महसं
महस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Knowledge.<BR>	 2. Kind, sort, difference.<BR> E. मह् to worship, Unādi aff. असच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकच्छ|महाकच्छः
महाकच्छ m. (-च्छः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. The deity of the ocean VARUṆA.<BR>	 3.<BR>A mountain.<BR> E. महा great, and कच्छ a shore or bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकण्टकिनी
महाकण्टकिनी f. (-नी) The Indian prickly pear, (Cactus Indicus.)<BR> E. महा<BR>great, कण्टक a thorn, इनि and ङीष् affs. “फणिमन्सा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकन्द|महाकंद|महाकन्दः
महाकन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Garlic.<BR>	 2. A very large esculent root, a sort of<BR>yam.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR> E. महा great and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकपर्द|महाकपर्दः
महाकपर्द m. (-र्दः) A species of shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकपित्थ|महाकपित्थः
महाकपित्थ m. (-त्थः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>	 2. Red garlic.<BR> E. महा<BR>great, and कपित्थ wood-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकर
महाकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Large-handed, &c.<BR>	 2. Having a large<BR>revenue.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A large hand, rent, &c.<BR> E. महा, and कर a hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकर्णिकार|महाकर्णिकारः
महाकर्णिकार m. (-रः) A plant, (cassia fistula.) आरग्वधे “सोंँदाल्” इति भाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकला
महाकला f. (-ला) The night of the new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकवि|महाकविः
महाकवि m. (-विः)<BR>	 1. An epithet of Sūkra.<BR>	 2. A classical poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकाय|महाकायः
महाकाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Large, bulky, stout.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>NANDĪ, the doorkeeper and attendant of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR>E. महा large and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकाल|महाकालः
महाकाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A name or rather a form of ŚIVA, in his character<BR>of the destroying deity, being then represented of a black colour,<BR>and of aspect more or less terrific.<BR>	 2. A name of NANDĪ, ŚIVA'S<BR>porter and attendant.<BR>	 3. The mango tree.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. The wife of the<BR>preceding deity, and a terrific form of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A goddess pecu-<BR>liar to the Jainas.<BR>	 3. One of the Vidyā-devis of the same sect. E.<BR>महा great, excessively, काल black, or time; in one capacity that of<BR>जगद्भक्षकः the world-eater, ŚIVA or MAHĀKĀLA may be considered<BR>as a personification of time that destroys all things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकाव्य|महाकाव्यं
महाकाव्य n. (-व्यं) A regular and classical poem.<BR> E. महा great, and काव्य<BR>a poem; the title is applied especially to five works; the Kumāra<BR>Sambhava, and Raghu Vaṃśa of KALIDĀSA; the Kirātārjuniya<BR>of BHĀRABĪ; the Naisadha of SRIHARSHA, and the Sisupāla<BR>Badham of MĀGHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकुल|महाकुलः
महाकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Eminent by birth, of good family or extrac-<BR>tion.<BR> E. महा great, and कुल lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकुलीन|महाकुलीनः
महाकुलीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Of good family.<BR> E. महा great, and कुलीन of family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकूप|महाकूपः
महाकूप m. (-पः) A large or deep well.<BR> E. महा great, and कूप a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकूल|महाकूलः
महाकूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Of a good family. E. See महाकुल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकृच्छ्र
महाकृच्छ्र n. (-च्छ्रं) A great penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाक्षीर|महाक्षीरः
महाक्षीर m. (-रः) Sugar-cane.<BR> E. महा great, and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाग
महाग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Great, prosperous.<BR> E. महा and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महागद|महागदः
महागद m. (-दः) Fever.<BR> E. महा and गद sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महागन्ध|महागंध|महागन्धं|महागन्धः
महागन्ध m. (-न्धः) A sort of cane growing near water, (Calamus fasci-<BR>culatus, Rox.)<BR>	 f. (-न्धा) A name or form of DURGĀ.<BR>	 n. (-न्धं) Gum<BR>myrrh.<BR>	 2. A kind of Sandal-wood.<BR> E. महा great, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महागिरि|महागिरिः
महागिरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. Any large mountain.<BR>	 2. A sacred personage pe-<BR>culiar to the Jainas.<BR> E. महा great and गिरि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाग्रीव|महाग्रीवः
महाग्रीव m. (-वः) A camel.<BR> E. महा great, and ग्रीवा a neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाग्रीविन्
महाग्रीविन् m. (-वी) A camel.<BR> E. महा large, ग्रीवा neck, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाघास|महाघासः
महाघास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Abounding with grass or fodder.<BR> E. महा, घास grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाघूर्णा
महाघूर्णा f. (-र्णा) Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR> E. महा great, much, घूर्ण<BR>to roll, affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाघोर|महाघोरः
महाघोर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Very formidable, terrific, horrible.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A<BR>division of Tartarus or hell.<BR> E. महा great, much, and घोर terrific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाघोष|महाघोषं|महाघोषः
महाघोष m. (-षः) A great noise, a loud sound.<BR>	 n. (-षं) A market, a fair.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly called Karkatasringi or Crab's horn<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">Page557-a+ 60</a>]<BR>described as a climbing and milky plant, and supposed to be the<BR>Asclepias geminata.<BR>	 2. Gum olibanum tree.<BR> E. महा great, घोष<BR>sound, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=556-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाङ्ग|महांग|महाङ्गः
महाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Bulky, big, large-bodied.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A camel.<BR>2. A kind of rat.<BR>	 3. An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR> E. महा great, अङ्ग body.<BR>“गोक्षुरक्षुपे, रक्तचित्रकक्षुपे च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाचण्ड|महाचण्डः
महाचण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. One of YAMA'S attendants.<BR>	 2. A very violent or<BR>passionate man.<BR> E. महा great, much, चण्ड hot, passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाच्छाय|महाच्छायः|महाछाय
महाच्छाय m. (-यः) The Indian fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाज|महाजः
महाज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Illustrious, high-born.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A large goat.<BR>E. महा great, and अज a goat, or ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाजन|महाजनः
महाजन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A virtuous or illustrious man, a great man.<BR>	 2. A<BR>merchant, a trader.<BR>	 3. The mob.<BR> E. महा great, जन a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाजम्बू
महाजम्बू f. (-म्बूः) A plant, perhaps a kind of Eugenia.<BR> E. महा great,<BR>and जम्बू the rose-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाजातीय|महाजातीयः
महाजातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of an excellent sort or species.<BR> E. महा great,<BR>जातीय of a species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाजाली
महाजाली f. (-ली) A plant, a sort of Ghosa, with yellow flowers.<BR> E. महा great, जाल a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाज्वाल|महाज्वालः
महाज्वाल m. (-लः) Sacrificial fire.<BR>	 f. (-ला) One of the Vidyā-devīs or<BR>goddesses peculiar to the Jainas.<BR> E. महा great, ज्वाल flame, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातमप्रभा
महातमप्रभा f. (-भा) The lowermost division of Naraka or hell.<BR> E. महा<BR>great, तम darkness, and प्रभा flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातरु|महातरुः
महातरु m. (-रुः) A plant, (Euphorbia of various kinds.)<BR> E. महा large,<BR>and तरु a tree. “स्नुहीवृक्षे” “मन्सा गाछ” इति भाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातल|महातलं
महातल n. (-लं) The fifth in descent of the seven Pātālas or regions<BR>under the earth, inhabited by various races of evil beings, as the<BR>Nāgas, Asuras, Daityas, &c.<BR> E. महा great, and तल depth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातारा
महातारा f. (-रा) A goddess of the Bauddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातिक्त|महातिक्तः
महातिक्त mfn. (-क्त्रः-क्ता-क्तं) Very bitter.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) The large Nimba tree,<BR>(Melia sempervirens.)<BR>	 f. (-क्ता) A plant, commonly Ākanādi. E.<BR>महा much, and तिक्त bitter. यवतिक्तायांच “तित्पल्ता” इति भाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातीक्ष्ण
महातीक्ष्ण mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं) Very sharp, (as flavour,) or literally, (as a<BR>weapon,) or figuratively, (as perception, &c.)<BR>	 f. (-क्ष्णा) The mark-<BR>ing-nut plant.<BR> E. महा great or much, तीक्ष्ण sharp, acrid, acute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महातेजस्
महातेजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>	 1. Very bright.<BR>	 2. Very energetic or vigor-<BR>ous.<BR>	 m. (-जाः)<BR>	 1. A name of KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. AGNI, the deity of<BR>fire.<BR>	 3. A hero, a demi-god.<BR>	 n. (-क्ष्णं) Quicksilver.<BR> E. महा great,<BR>and तेजस् light or glory, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महात्मन्
महात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Liberal, lofty-minded, magnanimous.<BR> E. महा great, आत्मन् self, soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महादन्त|महादंत|महादन्तः
महादन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. An elephant with large tusks.<BR>	 2. An elephant's<BR>tusk.<BR> E. महा great, and दन्त tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महादश
महादश f. (-शां) The influence of a predominant planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महादारु
महादारु m. (-रुः) A sort of pine, (P. Devadāru.)<BR> E. महा large, and दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महादुन्दु
महादुन्दु m. (-न्दुः) A large military drum.<BR> E. महा great, दुन्दु a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महादेव|महादेवः
महादेव m. (-वः) ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-वी) DURGĀ the wife of ŚIVA.<BR> E. महा great,<BR>and देव god; the epithet Mahā compounded with a substantive<BR>forms many appellatives of these deities especially; thus ŚIVA<BR>is Mahākāla, Mahārūdra, Maheśwara, &c. and DURGĀ is named<BR>Mahāvidya, Mahāsmriti, Mahāmedha, Mahāmoha, &c. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाद्रुम|महाद्रुमः
महाद्रुम m. (-मः) The holy fig-tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR> E. महा great, and<BR>द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाधन|महाधनं
महाधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Rich, opulent.<BR>	 2. Costly, precious, valuable.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Any thing costly or precious.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR>	 3. Incense.<BR>	 4.<BR>Costly raiment.<BR>	 5. Agriculture.<BR> E. महा great, धन wealth or price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाधातु|महाधातुः
महाधातु m. (-तुः) Gold.<BR> E. महा great, chief, and धातु mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानट|महानटः
महानट m. (-टः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. महा great, and नट a dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानन्द|महानंद|महानन्दः
महानन्द m. (-न्दः) Eternal emancipation or beatitude.<BR>	 f. (-न्दा)<BR>	 1. Wine.<BR>2. Name of a particular river.<BR> E. महा great, आनन्द happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानरक|महानरकः
महानरक n. (-कं) One of the twenty-one hells or divisions of Tartarus.<BR>E. महा and नरक hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानल|महानलः
महानल m. (-लः) A kind of reed. “देवनले ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानवमी
महानवमी f. (-मी) The ninth day of the first half of Āshwina sacred to DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानस|महानसं|महानसः
महानस mn. (-सः-सं) A kitchen.<BR>	 n. (-सं) A heavy carriage.<BR> E. महा great,<BR>chief, अनस rice or food, टच् added; to which the food is conveyed<BR>to be dressed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानाद|महानादः
महानाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A large black rainy cloud.<BR>	 2. A loud sound.<BR>	 3.<BR>An elephant.<BR>	 4. A lion.<BR>	 5. The ear.<BR>	 6. A camel.<BR>	 7. A conch-shell.<BR>n. (-दं) A musical instrument.<BR> E. महा great and नाद noise or sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानिद्रा
महानिद्रा f. (-द्रा) Death, dying.<BR> E. महा great, निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानिम्ब|महानिम्बः
महानिम्ब m. (-म्बः) A large kind of Nimba tree, (Melia sempervirens.) E.<BR>महा great, and निम्ब the Nimba. “घोडानिम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानिशा
महानिशा f. (-शा) Midnight.<BR> E. महा great, and निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानीच|महानीचः
महानीच m. (-चः) A washerman.<BR> E. महा great, much, and नीच vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानील|महानीलः
महानील m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The emerald.<BR>	 2. One of the Nāgas.<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>(Verbesina scandens, Rox.)<BR> E. महा great, and नील blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानुभाव|महानुभावः
महानुभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Magnanimous, liberal.<BR>	 m. (-वः) A gentleman.<BR>E. महा great, अनुभाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानेमि|महानेमिः
महानेमि m. (-मिः) A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापक्ष|महापक्षः
महापक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A sort of duck.<BR>	 2. An epithet of GARUḌA.<BR>	 f. (-क्षी)<BR>An owl.<BR> E. महा large, and पक्ष a side, a wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापञ्चमूलक
महापञ्चमूलक n. (-कं) The great five roots; they are as follows:--<BR>“विल्वोऽग्निमन्थः श्योनाकः काश्मर्य्यः पाटलातथा ।<BR>सर्वैस्तु मिलितैरेतैः स्यान्महापञ्चमूलकम् ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापञ्चविष|महापंचविष|महापञ्चविषं
महापञ्चविष n. (-षं) The five great poisons; they are as follows:--<BR>“शृङ्गी च कालकूटश्च मुस्तको वत्सनाभकः ।<BR>शक्तुकश्चेति योगोऽयं महापञ्चविषाभिधः ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापत्र
महापत्र m. (-त्रः) A potherb. “मालाकन्दे” f. (-त्रा) A kind of Eugenia.<BR>“महाजम्बूवृक्षे” ।<BR> E. महा large, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापथ|महापथः
महापथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. The principal path or entrance to a town or house.<BR>&c., a main road, a highway.<BR>	 2. The end of life, the way of all<BR>flesh.<BR>	 3. Name of certain precipices from which people used to<BR>throw themselves to obtain entrance into heaven.<BR> E. महा chief,<BR>पथ road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापथगम|महापथगमः
महापथगम m. (-मः) Dying.<BR> E. महापथ the great way, (by which all mortals travel,) गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापद्म|महापद्मः
महापद्म m. (-द्मः)<BR>	 1. One of the principal Nāgas or serpents of Pātāla.<BR>2. One of KUVERA'S Nidhis or treasures.<BR>	 3. A large number, one<BR>hundred thousand millions.<BR>	 4. A Kinnara or attendant on KUVE-<BR>RA.<BR>	 n. (-द्मं) The large white lotus.<BR> E. महा great, and पद्म a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापातक|महापातकं
महापातक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A crime of the highest degree, as killing a Brāh-<BR>mana, stealing gold from a priest, drinking spirits, adultery with<BR>the wife of a spiritual teacher, and associating with persons who<BR>have committed these offences.<BR>	 2. Great crime in general.<BR> E. महा<BR>great, पातक offence: see पञ्चमहापातक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापातकिन्
महापातकिन् m. (-की) An offender in the highest degree: see the last.<BR>E. महापातक great sin, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापाप|महापापं
महापाप n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. A sin of the highest kind. see महापातक.<BR>	 2. Heinous<BR>crime, or sin in general.<BR> E. महा excessive, and पाप sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापासक|महापासकः
महापासक m. (-कः) A religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापुरुष|महापुरुषः
महापुरुष m. (-षः) A great man.<BR> E. महा and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापुरुषदन्ता
महापुरुषदन्ता f. (-न्ता) A plant, (Asparagus racemosa.) “शतमूल्याम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापुष्पा
महापुष्पा f. (-ष्पा) A flower, (Clitoria ternatea.) “अपराजितायाम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्रभ|महाप्रभः
महाप्रभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Very bright, splendid.<BR>	 m. (-भः) Lamp-light,<BR>the light of a lamp.<BR> E. महा much, प्रभा shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्रभु|महाप्रभुः
महाप्रभु m. (-भुः)<BR>	 1. A holy man, a saint.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR>	 3. INDRA.<BR>	 4. ŚIVA.<BR>E. महा chief, and प्रभु master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्रलय|महाप्रलयः
महाप्रलय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A destruction of the world, occuring after every<BR>period of 4,320,000,000 years.<BR>	 2. A total destruction of the uni-<BR>verse, happening after a period commensurate with the life of<BR>BRAHMĀ, or 100 years, each day of which is equal to the period<BR>first stated, and each night of which is of similar duration; at<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">Page558-a+ 60</a>]<BR>the expiration of this term, the seven Lokas, with the saints,<BR>gods, and BRAHMĀ himself, are annihilated.<BR> E. महा great, प्रलय<BR>destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=557-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाप्राण|महाप्राणः
महाप्राण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A raven.<BR>	 2. The aspirate utterance of the aspirated letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाफल|महाफलः
महाफल m. (-लः) A particular fruit-tree, (Agle marmelos.)<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A<BR>bitter gourd: see इन्द्रवारुणी.<BR>	 2. A kind of spear.<BR> E. महा and फल<BR>fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाफेणा
महाफेणा f. (-णा) Cuttle-fish-bone.<BR> E. महा great, and फेण froth, foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाबल|महाबलं|महाबलः
महाबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Strong, robust, powerful.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Air,<BR>wind.<BR>	 2. A Buddha or Bauddha deified saint.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Lead.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला) A sort of Sida with yellow flowers, (S. rhombifolia.)<BR> E. महा<BR>great or much, and बल strong, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाबाहु|महाबाहुः
महाबाहु mfn. (-हुः-हुः-हु) Having long arms.<BR> E. महा great, बाहु an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाबोधि|महाबोधिः
महाबोधि m. (-धिः) A Buddha, a deified teacher of the Bauddhas. E.<BR>महा great and बोधि a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाब्राह्मण|महाब्राह्मणः
महाब्राह्मण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A priest who officiates at funeral ceremonies.<BR>	 2.<BR>An eminent Brāhmana.<BR> E. महा great, and ब्राह्मण a Brāhmana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभद्रा
महाभद्रा f. (-द्रा) The Ganges.<BR> E. महा much, and भद्रा propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभाग
महाभाग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Virtuous in a high degree, pure, holy.<BR>	 2.<BR>Eminent, exalted.<BR> E. महा and भाग portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभागता
महाभागता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Possession of the cardinal virtues, clemency, &c.<BR>2. Exalted station or merit.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with<BR>त्व, महाभागत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभारत|महाभारतं
महाभारत n. (-तं) Name of the great epic which details the history of<BR>the sons of DHRITARĀSTRA and PĀNDU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभाष्य
महाभाष्य n. (-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. The commentary of Patanjalī on the Sutras of<BR>PĀNINĪ.<BR>	 2. Any great commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीत
महाभीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Very timid, pusillanimous, cowardly.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>A sort of sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.) “लज्जावती लता”<BR> E. महा<BR>much, and भीत frightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीम|महाभीमः
महाभीम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A name of SĀNTANU.<BR>	 2. One of ŚIVA'S chamber-<BR>lains.<BR> E. महा great or much, भीम formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीरु|महाभीरुः
महाभीरु m. (-रुः) A sort of beetle, found in cow-dung.<BR> E. महा much, भीरु fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभीष्म|महाभीष्मः
महाभीष्म m. (-ष्मः) A name of SĀNTANU, a sovereign, and the father of<BR>BHĪṢMA.<BR> E. महा much, and भीष्म formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभूत|महाभूतं|महाभूतः
महाभूत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A primary element; as air, fire, water, earth, and<BR>Ākās or æther.<BR>	 2. A great creature.<BR> E. महा principal, भूत<BR>element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामति|महामतिः
महामति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Magnanimous, high-minded.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) The<BR>planet Jupiter.<BR> E. महा, मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामद|महामदः
महामद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. An elephant in rut.<BR>	 2. Great pride or intoxication.<BR>E. महा great, and मद fury, or the fluid that issues from the ani-<BR>mal's temples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामनस्
महामनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Magnanimous, high-minded, liberal, muni-<BR>ficent.<BR> E. महा great, मनस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामन्त्रिन्|महामंत्रिन्
महामन्त्रिन् m. (-न्त्री) The prime minister.<BR> E. महा and मन्त्रिन् a counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामहिमन्
महामहिमन् mfn. (-मा-मा-म) Very great, high and mighty.<BR> E. महा, and<BR>महिमन् greatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामात्र|महामात्रः
महामात्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A king's minister or associate, any high officer in<BR>a kingdom: as a counsellor, a general, &c.<BR>	 2. An elephant-driver,<BR>a Māhut.<BR>	 3. Superintendent of the elephants.<BR>	 4. A man of wealth<BR>and consequence.<BR>	 f. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. The wife of a spiritual preceptor.<BR>	 2.<BR>The wife of an officer of state, &c.<BR> E. महा great, मात्र wealth or<BR>retinue, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामानसी
महामानसी f. (-सी) A goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामाया
महामाया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. Worldly illusion or unrea-<BR>lity; the divine power of illusion which makes the material uni-<BR>verse appear what we see it to be.<BR> E. महा great, माया illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामारी
महामारी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. Cholera.<BR> E. महा great, मारी<BR>destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामाष|महामाषः
महामाष m. (-षः) A kind of bean, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR> E. महा large, and<BR>माष the Phaseolus radiatus. “राजमाषे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामुख|महामुखः
महामुख m. (-खः) A crocodile, an alligator.<BR> E. महा large, and मुख the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामुनि|महामुनिः
महामुनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. A name of AGASTYA.<BR>	 2. A name of Bauddha or<BR>more properly, of any one of the sacred persons called by that<BR>name.<BR>	 3. The epithet of a warlike saint, celebrated in the Mahā-<BR>bhārata.<BR>	 4. Time.<BR>	 5. A name of VYĀSA.<BR>	 n. (-नि)<BR>	 1. Coriander.<BR>	 2.<BR>Any medicinal drug.<BR> E. महा great, and मुनि saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामूल|महामूलः
महामूल m. (-लः) A kind of onion. “राजपलाण्डौ” n. (-लं) A large radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामूल्य|महामूल्यं|महामूल्यः
महामूल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Costly, precious.<BR>	 m. (-ल्यः) A ruby.<BR> E. महा<BR>great, मूल्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामृग|महामृगः
महामृग m. (-गः) An elephant.<BR> E. महा great, मृग an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामृत्यु|महामृत्युः
महामृत्यु m. (-त्युः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. महा great, मृत्यु death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामेद|महामेदः
महामेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The coral tree, (Erythrina Indica.)<BR>	 2. A drug,<BR>classed amongst the principal drugs, and described as a tonic,<BR>and stimulant.<BR> E. महा much, and मेद marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामैत्र|महामैत्रः
महामैत्र m. (-त्रः) Buddha, the founder of the Bauddha sect, or a Baud-<BR>dha or form of him.<BR> E. महा great, मैत्र friendliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाम्ल|महाम्लं
महाम्ल mfn. (-म्लः-म्ला-म्लं) Very acid.<BR>	 n. (-म्लं) Acid seasoning.<BR> E. महा<BR>much, very, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायक्ष|महायक्षः
महायक्ष m. (-क्षः) A sort of demi-god, supposed to attend the Jinas or<BR>Jaina saints.<BR> E. महा great, and यक्ष a divine being, attending<BR>usually on KUVERA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायज्ञ|महायज्ञः
महायज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) An essential sacrifice, a sacrament of the Hindu<BR>religion; five acts are enumerated of this description, severally<BR>considered as due to the Vedas, to the gods, to man, to the manes,<BR>and to all created beings; they are respectively, study of scrip-<BR>ture, offering of sacrifice to the gods, hospitable treatment of<BR>guests, libation of water, &c. to deceased progenitors, and the<BR>casting of food on the ground or in water as an offering to the<BR>gods, to spirits, &c.<BR> E. महा great, यज्ञ sacrifice or act of wor-<BR>ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायन्त्र
महायन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) Any great mechanical work, as a lock, or dyke, &c.<BR>E. महा and यन्त्र mechanical contrivance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायमक
महायमक n. (-कं) A stanza wholly consisting of yamakas, (i. e.) having<BR>all the four pādas identical in sound though different in sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायशस्
महायशस् mfn. (-शाः-शाः-शः) Illustrious, celebrated.<BR>	 m. (-शाः) The fifth<BR>Jaina of the past era.<BR> E. महा great, यशस् fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायशस्क|महायशस्कः
महायशस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्क) Illustrious, celebrated.<BR> E. महा great, यशस्<BR>celebrity, कप added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायुग
महायुग m. (-गः) A great Yuga; the aggregate of the four ages, or a<BR>period of four millions, three hundred and twenty thousand years.<BR>E. महा great, and युग age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारजत|महारजतं
महारजत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. The thorn-apple.<BR> E. महा great, रजत silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारजन|महारजनं
महारजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Safflower.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR> E. महा great, रञ्ज् to colour, aff.<BR>क्युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारण्य|महारण्यं
महारण्य n. (-ण्यं) A large forest.<BR> E. महा great, अरण्य a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारथ|महारथः
महारथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2. A large car.<BR>	 3. A warrior fighting<BR>in a car, or any leader or warrior of note. It is thus defined in<BR>Vāchaspatya:--“एको दशसहस्राणि योधयेद् यस्तु धन्विनाम् ।<BR>शस्त्रशास्त्रप्रवीणश्च विज्ञेयः स महारथः ॥”<BR>E. महा great, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारस|महारसं|महारसः
महारस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The date tree, (Phœnix sylvestris.)<BR>	 2. A species of<BR>club rush, (Scirpus kysoor.)<BR>	 3. Any precious mineral.<BR>	 4. Quick-<BR>silver.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Gruel made from the fermentation of rice-water. E.<BR>महा great, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराज|महाराजः
महाराज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A sovereign, an emperor.<BR>	 2. A finger-nail.<BR>	 3. A<BR>Jaina deified teacher.<BR> E. महा great, राजन् a king, aff. टच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराजक|महाराजकः
महाराजक m. (-कः) A sort of demi-god: see महाराजिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराजचूत|महाराजचूतः
महाराजचूत m. (-तः) A kind of mango.<BR> E. महाराज sovereign, chief, and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">Page559-a+ 60</a>]<BR>चूत the mango; bearing a superior sort of fruit; also similar<BR>compounds: as महाराजाम्र, महाराजफल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=558-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराजाधिराज
महाराजाधिराज m. (-जः) A paramount sovereign, an emperor.<BR> E. महाराज,<BR>अधिराज chief sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराजिक|महाराजिकः
महाराजिक m. (-कः) A kind of demi-god, of which there is a class of<BR>220.<BR> E. महा great, राजि splendour, aff. कन्; or महाराज the epithet<BR>of their chief and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारात्र
महारात्र m. (-त्रः) Midnight.<BR> E. महा great, and रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाराष्ट्र|महाराष्ट्रः
महाराष्ट्र n. (-ष्ट्रं) A country in the west of India, that of the original<BR>Mahrāttas.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ट्री) A dialect, Mahrātta.<BR> E. महा and राष्ट्र kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारूप|महारूपः
महारूप m. (-पः) Resin.<BR> E. महा chief, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारूपक|महारूपकं
महारूपक m. (-कः) A drama, a play or dramatic poem.<BR> E. महा chief,<BR>रूपक rhetorical composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारौरव|महारौरवः
महारौरव m. (-वः) One of the divisions of Tartarus, a hell.<BR> E. महा<BR>great, रुरु a demon, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्घ|महार्घं|महार्घः
महार्घ mfn. (-र्घः-र्घा-र्घं) Costly, precious, of great price or value.<BR>	 m. (-र्घः)<BR>A sort of quail.<BR> E. महा great, अर्घ cost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्णव|महार्णवः
महार्णव m. (-वः) The ocean.<BR> E. महा great, अर्णव the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्थ
महार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Significant, meaning.<BR>	 2. Great, dignified.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-र्थः) A principal object.<BR> E. महा and अर्थ sense or object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्द्ध
महार्द्ध m. (-र्द्धः) A plant, commonly Mahā-Ādā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्ह|महार्हं
महार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>	 1. Costly, valuable.<BR>	 2. Very worthy.<BR> E. महा and<BR>अर्ह worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालक्ष्मी
महालक्ष्मी f. (-क्ष्मीः)<BR>	 1. SARASWATĪ the wife of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A young girl<BR>who personates DURGĀ at the festival of that goddess.<BR> E. महा<BR>great, and लक्ष्मी the goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालय|महालयः
महालय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. GOD, the supreme being.<BR>	 2. A place of pilgrimage.<BR>3. A tree, &c. sacred to a deity.<BR>	 4. The Loka or world of BRAHMĀ.<BR>5. A place of refuge, a sanctuary, an asylum.<BR>	 6. A temple.<BR> E. महा<BR>great, आलय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालोध
महालोध m. (-धः) A tree, the bark of which is used as an astringent,<BR>(Symplocos racemosa.)<BR> E. महा great, लोध the Lodh tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालोल|महालोलः
महालोल m. (-लः) A crow.<BR> E. महा great, लोल moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालोह|महालोहं
महालोह n. (-हं) The load-stone.<BR> E. महा great, chief, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावन|महावनं
महावन n. (-नं) A large forest.<BR> E. महा large, वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावप|महावपः
महावप m. (-पः) A plant and drug, commonly Mahāmeda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावरा
महावरा f. (-रा) Bent grass: see दूर्व्वा.<BR> E. महा great, वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावराह|महावराहः
महावराह m. (-हः) VIṢṆU in his boar-incarnation.<BR> E. महा, वराह a boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावर्त्तन|महावर्तन
महावर्त्तन n. (-नं) Large pay or allowance.<BR> E. महा and वर्त्तन maintaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावल्ली
महावल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A large and handsome creeping plant, (Gærtnera<BR>racemosa.)<BR> E. महा great, and वल्ली pedicle. “माधबीलतायाम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावस|महावसः
महावस m. (-सः) The Gangetic porpoise.<BR> E. महा large, वस who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावाक्य|महावाक्यं
महावाक्य n. (-क्यं)<BR>	 1. Any continuous composition, any literary work.<BR>2. A long sentence.<BR>	 3. A principal sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविदेहा
महाविदेहा f. (-हा) A certain condition of the mind, (in (Yoga Phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविद्या
महाविद्या f. (-द्या) The name of the following ten goddess:--<BR>“काली तारा महाविद्या षोडशी भुवनेश्वरी ।<BR>भैरवी छिन्नमस्ता च विद्या धूमावती तथा ।<BR>वगला सिद्धविद्या च मातङ्गी कमलात्मिका ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविभाषा
महाविभाषा f. (-षा) A rule containing a general alternative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाबिल
महाबिल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Sky, heaven, atmosphere.<BR>	 2. A water jar.<BR>	 3. The<BR>heart, the mind.<BR>	 4. A cave, a hole.<BR> E. महा great, and विल a chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविशिष्ट
महाविशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Endowed with great, or excellent qualities.<BR>E. महा great, विशिष्ठ endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविष|महाविषः
महाविष m. (-षः) A small venomous snake, supposed to be two-headed.<BR>E. महा great, and विष venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाविषुव|महाविषुवं
महाविषुव n. (-वं) The Sankrāntī or moment of the sun's entering<BR>ARIES; the vernal equinox, but varying several days from the<BR>European computation.<BR> E. महा great, and विषुव equinox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीचि|महावीचिः
महावीचि f. (-चिः) One of the divisions of Tartarus.<BR> E. महा, वीचि a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीज्य|महावीज्यं
महावीज्य n. (-ज्यं) The septum of the scrotum, and part of the peri-<BR>nœum.<BR> E. महा chief, वीज seed, यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीर|महावीरः
महावीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. GARUḌA the bird, and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A<BR>hero.<BR>	 3. A lion.<BR>	 4. A white horse.<BR>	 5. Sacrificial fire.<BR>	 6. INDRA'S<BR>thunderbolt.<BR>	 7. A bird, a sort of hawk.<BR>	 8. The Kokila or Indian<BR>cuckoo.<BR>	 9. The last and most celebrated Jina or Jaina teacher<BR>of the present who age, is supposed to have flourished in the<BR>province of Behar, in the sixth century before the Christian era.<BR>10. Sacrificial vessel.<BR>	 11. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 12. Agni or fire.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A<BR>sort of drug, commonly Kṣīrakākolī, and conceived to be the<BR>dried root of a species of lily.<BR> E. महा great, and बीर hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावीर्य्य|महावीर्य|महावीर्यः|महावीर्य्यः
महावीर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. A Jina or Jaina saint.<BR>	 2. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-र्य्या)<BR>	 1. A name of SANJNYĀ the wife of the sun.<BR>	 2. Wild-cotton.<BR>E. महा great, and वीर्य्य essence. “वाराहीकन्देच ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावृक्ष|महावृक्षः
महावृक्ष m. (-क्षः) Euphorbia, of several species: see स्नुही<BR> E. महा great, वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावृहती
महावृहती f. (-ती) The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR> E. महा great,<BR>वृहती the egg-plant. “महावार्त्ताक्याम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावेग|महावेगः
महावेग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A monkey.<BR>	 2. GARUḌA.<BR>	 3. Great volocity.<BR> E. महा great, वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाव्याधि|महाव्याधिः
महाव्याधि m. (-धिः) A virulent type of leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाव्याहृति|महाव्याहृतिः
महाव्याहृति f. (-तिः) The three mystical words, Bhūr, Bhuvah, and<BR>Swer, the essential part, with Om and Gāyatrī of the daily<BR>Brāhminical prayer.<BR> E. महा great, and व्याहृति a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाव्रतिन्
महाव्रतिन् m. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A devotee, an ascetic.<BR> E. महा<BR>great, and व्रत religious penance or observance, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाव्रीहि
महाव्रीहि m. (-हिः) A large kind of rice.<BR> E. महा large, and व्रीहि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशक्ति|महाशक्तिः
महाशक्ति m. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. KĀRTIKEYA, the martial deity of the Hindus.<BR>	 2.<BR>ŚIVA.<BR> E. महा great, शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशङ्ख|महाशंख|महाशङ्खः
महाशङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>	 1. A human bone.<BR>	 2. The forehead.<BR>	 3. A thousand<BR>millions.<BR>	 4. One of KUVERA'S Nidhis or treasures.<BR>	 5. A great<BR>conch-shell.<BR> E. महा great, शङ्ख a shell, a number, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशठ|महाशठः
महाशठ m. (-ठः) A kind of thorn-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशय|महाशयः
महाशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Magnanimous, liberal, munificent.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The ocean.<BR>	 2. A gentleman, sir.<BR> E. महा great, आशय purpose or<BR>an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशय्या
महाशय्या f. (-य्या) A throne, a regal seat.<BR> E. महा great, and शय्या bed or couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशल्क|महाशल्कः
महाशल्क m. (-ल्कः) A prawn or shrimp.<BR> E. महा large, शल्क a scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशाक|महाशाकं
महाशाक m. (-कः) A kind of potherb.<BR> E. महा large, शाक a potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशाल|महाशालः
महाशाल m. (-लः) A great house-holder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशालि|महाशालिः
महाशालि m. (-लिः) A fragrant sort of rice.<BR> E. महा large, chief, शालि rice<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशीता
महाशीता f. (-ता) A plant, (Asparagus racemosa.)<BR> E. महा, शीता cooling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशुक्ति|महाशुक्तिः
महाशुक्ति f. (-क्तिः) The pearl oyster.<BR> E. महा great, &c. शुक्ति oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशुक्ला
महाशुक्ला f. (-क्ला) The goddess SARASWATĪ.<BR> E. महा very, शुक्ल white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशुभ्र|महाशुभ्रं
महाशुभ्र n. (-भ्रं) Silver.<BR> E. महा much, and शुभ्र white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशूद्र|महाशूद्रः
महाशूद्र m. (-द्रः) The cowherd.<BR>	 f. (-द्री) The milk-woman, either the wife<BR>of a cowherd or a woman of that caste.<BR> E. महा great, शूद्र Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्मशान|महाश्मशानं
महाश्मशान n. (-नं) The holy city Benāres.<BR> E. महा great, and श्मशान<BR>cemetery; people going thither to die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्यामा
महाश्यामा f. (-मा) A creeper, (Echites frutescens.)<BR> E. महा large, श्याम<BR>black. “श्यामालतायाम्, कृष्णशिंशपावृक्षे च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्रमण|महाश्रमणः
महाश्रमण m. (-णः) A Jaina or Bauddha saint.<BR> E. महा much, and श्रमण<BR>labouring, (in devotion.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्री
महाश्री f. (-श्रीः)<BR>	 1. A goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>	 2. An epithet of<BR>LAKṢMĪ.<BR> E. महा great, and श्री prosperity or the goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्वेत
महाश्वेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Very white.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A name of SARASWATĪ.<BR>2. A white variety of the Convolvulus paniculatus.<BR>	 3. Clayed or<BR>candied sugar.<BR>	 4. A sort of Clitoria, (C. ternata, with white flow-<BR>ers.)<BR> E. महा much, and श्वेत white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासत्व
महासत्व mfn. (-त्वः-त्वा-त्वं) Good, virtuous, just.<BR> E. महा and सत्व purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासन्न|महासन्नः
महासन्न m. (-न्नः) A name of KUVERA; also महासत्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासर्ज|महासर्जः
महासर्ज m. (-र्जः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>	 2. The jack<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">Page560-a+ 60</a>]<BR>tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR> E. महा large, and सर्ज the Sāl<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=559-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासह|महासहः
महासह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Much-enduring.<BR>	 f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. A Plant, (Glycine<BR>debilis.)<BR>	 2. A flower, (Gomphræna globosa.)<BR>	 3. A medicinal<BR>plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR> E. महा great, सह् to bear, affs.<BR>अच् or अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासान्तपन|महासांतपन|महासान्तपनं|महासांतपनः
महासान्तपन n. (-नं) A sort of penance; subsisting for six successive<BR>days, respectively, on cow's urine, cowdung, milk, curds, Ghee, and<BR>water in which Kūsa grass has been boiled, and fasting on the<BR>seventh day: instead of one day some authorities assign a period<BR>of three days to each, considering the first as the common Sānta-<BR>pana penance; others omit the two last periods, making it last<BR>fifteen days.<BR> E. महा great, सान्तपन a penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासार|महासारः
महासार m. (-रः) A kind of Khadira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासाहस|महासाहसं
महासाहस n. (-सं) Excessive violence, brutal assault.<BR> E. महा great,<BR>साहस violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासाहसिक|महासाहसिकः
महासाहसिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A robber, a plunderer, one who carries off pro-<BR>perty openly and by force.<BR>	 2. An assaulter, a violator.<BR> E. महा-<BR>साहस violence, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासि|महासिः
महासि m. (-सिः) A large scymitar or sword.<BR> E. महा and असि a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासुख|महासुखं|महासुखः
महासुख m. (-खः) A Bauddha or Jaina saint.<BR>	 n. (-खं) Copulation. E.<BR>महा great, and सुख happiness, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासूक्ष्म
महासूक्ष्म mfn. (-क्ष्मः-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मं) Subtile, fine, minute.<BR>	 f. (-क्ष्मा) Sand.<BR> E. महा very, सूक्ष्म thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासूत|महासूतः
महासूत m. (-तः) A military drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासेन|महासेनः
महासेन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. KARTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. A general, the commander of a<BR>large force.<BR>	 3. The father of eighth Jina or Jaina saint of the<BR>present era.<BR> E. महा great, सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्कन्ध|महास्कंध|महास्कन्धः
महास्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) A camel.<BR> E. महा and स्कन्ध shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्थली
महास्थली f. (-ली) The earth.<BR> E. महा great, स्थली heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्वायु
महास्वायु m. (-युः) Any principal vessel of the body.<BR> E. महा large, स्नायु a<BR>tubular vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्वन|महास्वनः
महास्वन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Loud-sounding.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. An instrument of<BR>martial music, a kind of drum or trumpet.<BR>	 2. A loud sound. E.<BR>महा great, and स्वन sound or noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाहव|महाहवः
महाहव m. (-वः) A great battle or war.<BR> E. महा and आहव war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाहास|महाहासः
महाहास m. (-सः) A hoarse laugh.<BR> E. महा great, and हास laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाह्रस्वा
महाह्रस्वा f. (-स्वा) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.) “आल्कुशी ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महि|महिः
महि f. (-हिः) The earth.<BR> E. मह् to worship, aff. इन्; more commonly<BR>मही q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिका
महिका f. (-का) Frost, mist.<BR> E. मह् to worship, aff. क्वन्, fem. form; more commonly मिहिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महित|महितं
महित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Proper, right.<BR>	 2. Worshipped, reverenced,<BR>&c.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The trident of ŚIVA.<BR> E. मह् to worship, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिन|महिनं
महिन n. (-नं) Kingdom, sovereignty.<BR> E. मह् to worship or be worship-<BR>ped, Unādi aff. इनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिन्धक|महिंधकः
महिन्धक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A rat.<BR>	 2. An ichneumon.<BR>	 3. The string of a pole for carrying loads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिमन्
महिमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Greatness in general, literally, or figuratively.<BR>	 2.<BR>Magnitude as one of ŚIVA'S attributes, illimitability.<BR>	 3. Might,<BR>power, glory.<BR>	 4. High rank.<BR>	 5. The superhuman power of in-<BR>creasing in bulk at will, considered as one of the eight Siddhis.<BR>E. महत् great, इमनिच् aff. of the abstract property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिर|महिरः
महिर m. (-रः) The sun.<BR> E. मह् to be worshipped, aff. इरच् । “अर्कवृक्षे च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिला
महिला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A woman, a female.<BR>	 2. A woman literally or figura-<BR>tively intoxicated.<BR>	 3. A plant bearing a fragrant seed, commonly<BR>Priyangu.<BR>	 4. A perfume commonly Reṇukā.<BR> E. मह् to worship or<BR>be worshipped, Unādi aff. इलच्; also महला and महेला ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिलाह्वया
महिलाह्वया f. (-या) A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR> E. महिला a woman,<BR>and आह्वय appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिष|महिषः
महिष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A buffalo.<BR>	 2. The emblem of one of the Jaina saints.<BR>3. The emblem and vehicle of YAMA.<BR>	 4. The name of an Asura<BR>or demon slain by DURGĀ.<BR>	 f. (-षी)<BR>	 1. A female buffalo.<BR>	 2. The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">Page560-b+ 60</a>]<BR>wife of a king, but especially the one who has been consecrated or<BR>crowned, a queen.<BR>	 3. A drug.<BR> E. मह् to worship or be worshipped,<BR>Unādi aff. टिषच्, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिषध्वज|महिषध्वजः
महिषध्वज m. (-जः) YAMA, the sovereign of hell, and judge of the dead.<BR>E. महिष a buffalo, and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिषमर्द्दिनी|महिषमर्दिनी
महिषमर्द्दिनी f. (-नी) The goddess DURGĀ.<BR> E. महिष the ASURA so<BR>named, and मर्द्दिनी destructress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिषवाहन|महिषवाहनः
महिषवाहन m. (-नः) YAMA, the PLUTO of the Hindus.<BR> E. महिष a buffalo, वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महिषाक्ष|महिषाक्षः
महिषाक्ष m. (-क्षः) A plant, supposed to be the Bdellium tree.<BR> E. महिष<BR>a buffalo, and अक्ष eye. “गुग्गुलभेदे, भगन्दररोगे च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मही
मही f. (-ही)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. A river, the Mahī which rises in the pro-<BR>vince of Mālwā, and after pursuing a westerly course of about<BR>280 miles, falls into the upper part of the gulf of Cambay.<BR>	 3. A<BR>cow.<BR>	 4. A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR>	 5. The base of a plain<BR>figure, (in geometry.)<BR> E. मह् to worship or be worshipped, aff. इ,<BR>and ङीष् added; also without the addition महि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीक्षित्
महीक्षित् m. (-क्षित्) A king, a sovereign.<BR> E. मही the earth, and क्षि to<BR>rule, aff. क्किप् and तुक् final augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीज|महीजं|महीजः
महीज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The planet MARS.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Wet ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीतल
महीतल n. (-लं) The surface of the earth.<BR> E. मही and तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीधर|महीधरः
महीधर m. (-रः) A mountain.<BR> E. मही and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीध्र|महीध्रः
महीध्र m. (-ध्रः) A mountain.<BR> E. मही the earth, and धृ to uphold, aff.<BR>क, and the vowel changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीप|महीपः
महीप m. (-पः) A king.<BR> E. मही and प who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीपति|महीपतिः
महीपति m. (-तिः) A sovereign, a king.<BR> E. मही and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीपाल|महीपालः
महीपाल m. (-लः) A king.<BR> E. मही and पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीप्राचीर|महीप्राचीरं
महीप्राचीर n. (-रं) The ocean.<BR> E. मही the earth, and प्राचीर a boundary;<BR>being supposed to surround the earth completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीभर्त्तृ|महीभर्तृ
महीभर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) A king.<BR> E. मही, and भर्त्तृ who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीभुज्
महीभुज् m. (-भुक्) A king.<BR> E. मही and भुज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीमय|महीमयः
महीमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Earthen, made of earth or clay.<BR> E. मही earth, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीयस्
महीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Greatest, very great.<BR> E. महत् great, ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीय्यमान
महीय्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) To be worshipped, to be reverenced, to be<BR>treated with respect.<BR> E. मह् to worship, शानच् aff., यक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीरुह|महीरुहः
महीरुह m. (-हः) A tree.<BR> E. मही the earth, and रुह् to grow, aff. क; also<BR>with क्विप् aff. महीरुह् m. (-रुट् ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीलता
महीलता f. (-ता) An earth-worm.<BR> E. मही the earth, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महीसुत|महीसुतः
महीसुत m. (-तः) The regent of the planet MARS.<BR> E. मही the earth, and<BR>सुत son; said to have sprung from the soil, near Oujein, which<BR>was sprinkled with the perspiration from ŚIVA'S body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेच्छ|महेच्छः|महेछ
महेच्छ mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं) Liberal, magnanimous, high-minded.<BR> E. महा<BR>great, and इच्छा wise or design.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेन्द्र|महेंद्र|महेन्द्रः
महेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) INDRA, the ruler of Svarga.<BR>	 2. A range of mountains,<BR>one of the seven principal chains in Bhārata-Barsha or India, and<BR>apparently the northern part of the Ghāts of the peninsula. E.<BR>महा chief, great, इन्द्र the deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेन्द्रनगरी|महेंद्रनगरी
महेन्द्रनगरी f. (-री) Amarāvatī the city of the immortals, and capital of<BR>INDRA.<BR> E. महेन्द्र INDRA, and नगरी capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेन्द्राणी
महेन्द्राणी f. (-णी) The wife of INDRA.<BR> E. महा great, and इन्द्राणी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेरणा
महेरणा f. (-णा) The Olibanum tree, (Boswellia, thurifera.)<BR> E. महा great,<BR>ईरण diffusion; or मह sacrifice, ईर् to go to, to be used in, aff. ल्यु;<BR>also महेरुणा । “शल्लकीवृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेला
महेला f. (-ला) A woman.<BR> E. मह a festival, इला the earth or site; or मह्<BR>to worship, इलच् Unādi aff., and the vowel irregularly changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेलिका
महेलिका f. (-का) A woman.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेश|महेशः
महेश m. (-शः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. मह great, ईश lord or god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेशबन्धु|महेशबन्धुः
महेशबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A fruit tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR> E. महेश ŚIVA, and बन्धु friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेश्वर|महेश्वरः
महेश्वर m. (-रः) ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. DURGĀ the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Mixed or<BR>bell-metal.<BR>	 3. A flower, (Clitoria ternata.)<BR> E. महा great, and ईश्वर<BR>God, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=560-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेश्वरकरच्युता
महेश्वरकरच्युता f. (-ता) The Kharatoya river in the north of Bengal. E.<BR>महेश्वर ŚIVA, कर the hand and च्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेषु|महेषुः
महेषु f. (-षुः) A large arrow.<BR> E. महा and इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेष्वास|महेष्वासः
महेष्वास m. (-सः) A warrior, a champion, an archer.<BR> E. महेषु, and आस who shoots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोक्ष|महोक्षः
महोक्ष m. (-क्षः) A large bull or ox.<BR> E. महा large, उक्षन् an ox, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्का
महोत्का f. (-त्का) Lightning.<BR> E. महा great, (frequent.) उत्क opportunity,<BR>interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्पल|महोत्पलं|महोत्पलः
महोत्पल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A lotus, (Nymphæa nelumbo.)<BR>	 2. The Sārasa or<BR>Indian crane.<BR> E. महा large, chief, and उत्पल a water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्सव|महोत्सवः
महोत्सव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A great festival.<BR>	 2. KĀMA.<BR> E. महा, and उत्सव a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्साह|महोत्साहः
महोत्साह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Persevering, diligent, making strenuous and<BR>unremitting exertion.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A king, possessing all the ap-<BR>pendages and powers of monarchy.<BR>	 2. Diligence, effort, exertion.<BR>E. महा great, and उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदधि|महोदधिः
महोदधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. INDRA.<BR> E. महा great, उदधि the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदय|महोदयं|महोदयः
महोदय n. (-यं) Kanouj, the ancient city and district.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Final<BR>beatitude, emancipation from vitality and absorption into the<BR>divine essence.<BR>	 2. Prosperity, elevation, eminence.<BR>	 3. Pride.<BR>	 4.<BR>Abandoning, relinquishment.<BR>	 5. A master, a lord.<BR>	 6. Sour milk<BR>mixed with honey.<BR> E. महा great, उदय rising, splendour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदार
महोदार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Mighty, powerful.<BR> E. महा and उदार great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोद्यम|महोद्यमः
महोद्यम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Diligent, persevering, making strenuous and<BR>unremitting effort.<BR>	 m. (-मः) Great effort, energy, exertion.<BR> E. महा<BR>great, उद्यम effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोन्नत|महोन्नतः
महोन्नत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Very high.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The palmyra tree.<BR> E. महा and उन्नत high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोन्मद|महोन्मदः
महोन्मद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Intoxication, either literal or figurative, as with<BR>pride, passion, &c.<BR>	 2. A sort of fish, commonly Phalui.<BR> E. महा<BR>much, उन्मद intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोरग|महोरगं|महोरगः
महोरग n. (-गं) The root of a plant: see तगर.<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A sort of demi-<BR>god of the serpent genus, and forming one of the classes inhabit-<BR>ing Pātāla, &c.<BR>	 2. A large snake.<BR> E. महा great, and उरग a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौजस्
महौजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः) Very mighty or wonderful.<BR>	 m. (-जाः) A<BR>hero, a champion.<BR>	 n. (-जः) Great might or power.<BR> E. महा great,<BR>and ओजस् power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौजस
महौजस n. (-सं) The discus of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. टच् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौषध|महौषधं
महौषध n. (-धं)<BR>	 1. Garlic.<BR>	 2. A plant commonly Atāich, (Betula.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Long pepper.<BR>	 4. A panacea.<BR>	 nf. (-धं-धी) Dry ginger.<BR>	 f. (-धी) A po-<BR>therb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR> E. महा great and औषध a drug; this<BR>word is of course applicable to a great number of plants and<BR>substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौषधि|महौषधिः
महौषधि f. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. A sort of grass, commonly Durbā.<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.) “लज्जावती लता”<BR> E. महा large and<BR>औषधि a deciduous plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
मा r. 2nd. cl. (माति) r. 3rd cl. (मिमीते) r. 4th cl. (मायते)<BR>	 1. To mete, to<BR>measure.<BR>	 2. To be contained: with अनु prefixed, to infer, to con-<BR>clude; with उप, to resemble; with परि, to measure; with प्र,<BR>to be evidence or authority; with सम, to compare, to equalize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
मा Ind.<BR>	 1. A prohibitive and negative particle.<BR>	 2. A particle imply-<BR>ing doubt.<BR> E. मा to measure, aff. क्किप्; this particle is chiefly<BR>prefixed to verbs, in the imperative mood, as माकुरु do not do,<BR>(any act.) &c.; it is also read sometimes, माङ् the final being<BR>redundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मा
मा f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. A mother.<BR>	 3. A measure.<BR>	 4. An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांस|मांसं|मांसः
मांस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Flesh.<BR>	 2. The fleshy part of fruit.<BR>	 f. (-सी)<BR>	 1. Indian<BR>spikenard, (Valeriana Jatāmānsi.)<BR>	 2. A sort of drug, commonly<BR>Kākoli.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. A worm.<BR> E. सन् to mind, स Unādi<BR>aff., and the vowel made long by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसकाम|मांसकामः
मांसकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Fond of flesh.<BR> E. मांस, कम् to desire, ज aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसकारि
मांसकारि n. (-रिः) Blood.<BR> E. मांस flesh, कारि making, causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसज|मांसजं
मांसज n. (-जं) Marrow or serum of the flesh, adeps.<BR> E. मांस flesh, ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसतेजस्
मांसतेजस् n. (-जः) The marrow of the flesh, meaning probably adeps.<BR>E. मांस flesh, and तेजस् lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसदलन|मांसदलनः
मांसदलन m. (-नः) A plant, (Andersonia rohitaka.)<BR> E. मांस flesh and दलन dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसनिर्य्यास|मांसनिर्यास|मांसनिर्यासः
मांसनिर्य्यास m. (-सः) The hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसद्राविन्
मांसद्राविन् m. (-वी) A species of sorrel. “अम्लवेतसे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसपिटक|मांसपिटकः
मांसपिटक mn. (-कः-कं) A basket of flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसपित्त
मांसपित्त n. (-त्तं) A bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसपेशी
मांसपेशी f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A muscle.<BR>	 2. The fetus during its early formation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसभक्ष|मांसभक्षः
मांसभक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Eating flesh, carnivorous.<BR> E. मांस flesh, भक्ष<BR>eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसल|मांसलं|मांसलः
मांसल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Strong, stout, lusty.<BR> E. मांस flesh, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसविक्रय|मांसविक्रयः
मांसविक्रय m. (-यः) Selling flesh or meat.<BR> E. मांस and विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसविक्रयिन्
मांसविक्रयिन् m. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A vendor of the flesh or beasts or birds.<BR>	 2. A.<BR>term of reproach, designating a mean or vile person.<BR> E. मांस flesh<BR>विक्रयिन् who sells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसशील
मांसशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Fleshy.<BR> E. मांस flesh, &c. and शील possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांससार|मांससारः
मांससार m. (-रः) Adeps, fat, the serum, &c., of the flesh.<BR> E. मांस flesh,<BR>सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसस्नेह|मांसस्नेहः
मांसस्नेह m. (-हः) Adeps, the serum or marrow of the flesh.<BR> E. मांस flesh, स्नेह unguent<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसहासा
मांसहासा f. (-सा) Skin.<BR> E. मांस flesh, हास a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांसिक|मांसिकः
मांसिक m. (-कः) A vendor of flesh or meat, whether of beasts or of<BR>birds.<BR> E. मांस flesh, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकन्द|माकंद|माकंदः|माकन्दः
माकन्द m. (-न्दः) The mango.<BR>	 f. (-न्दी)<BR>	 1. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 2. Yellow<BR>sandal-wood.<BR>	 3. The name of a city.<BR> E. मा beauty, and कन्द root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकर
माकर f. (-री) Belonging to the sea-monster MAKARA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकरन्द|माकरंद
माकरन्द f. (-न्दी) Relating to the juice of flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माकलि|माकलिः
माकलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. The charioteer of INDRA.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्ष्
माक्ष् (इ) माक्षि r. 1st cl. (माङ्क्षति) To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षि
माक्षि (क्षी) क n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A mineral substance, of which two kinds are des-<BR>cribed; the स्वर्णमाक्षिक or gold Mākshika, of a bright yellow colour,<BR>apparently the common pyritic iron ore: and the रूप्यमाक्षिक or<BR>silver Mākshika, which answers in appearance to the Hepatic py-<BR>rites of iron; other names of these ores occur; as विट्माक्षिक and<BR>कांस्यमाक्षिक, or feculent Mākshika and mixed metal Mākshika<BR>they are however, perhaps rather synonymes of the gold and<BR>silver ore, respectively, than names of distinct species.<BR>	 2. Honey.<BR>E. मक्षिका a bee, अण् aff. of derivation; the name is applied to the<BR>ore, from its honey-like colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षिकज|माक्षिकजं
माक्षिकज n. (-जं) Bee's wax.<BR> E. माक्षिक honey, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षिकशर्करा
माक्षिकशर्करा f. (-रा) A kind of sugar, candied sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माक्षिकाश्रय|माक्षिकाश्रयं
माक्षिकाश्रय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Bee's wax.<BR>	 2. A honey-comb.<BR> E. माक्षिक honey, आश्रय receptacle.;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मागध|मागधः
मागध mfn. (-धः-धी-धं) Belonging to, or produced in the province of<BR>Magadha or south Behar.<BR>	 m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A bard, a minstrel, whose<BR>duty it is, to recite the praises of sovereigns, their genealogy, and<BR>the deeds of their ancestors, in their presence; and to attend on<BR>the march of an army, and animate the soldiers by martial songs:<BR>the minstrel forms a particular caste, said to spring from a<BR>Vaiśya father, and Kṣatriya mother; in mythology, they are<BR>said to have been created at once by the will of ŚIVA; under the<BR>name of Bhauts, they are still numerous in the west of Inda<BR>where they are a privileged tribe.<BR>	 2. Cumin-seed.<BR>	 m. Plu. (-धाः)<BR>The inhabitants or people of Magadha.<BR>	 f. (-धी)<BR>	 1. A kind of jas-<BR>mine. (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>	 2. Long-pepper, (Piper longum.)<BR>3. A sort of cardamoms grown in Guzerāt.<BR>	 4. Refined sugar.<BR>	 5. A<BR>dialect of Sanskrit: one of the principal forms of Prākrita, and<BR>nearly the same as that used in the sacred books of the Bauddhas<BR>and Jainas: in the drama it is the dialect of the attendants and<BR>companions of royal personages.<BR> E. मगध a Kandwādi verb, to ask,<BR>(reward,) aff. अण्; or मगध the country, and अण् derivative aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघ|माघः
माघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. One of the months of the Hindu year, (January-Fe-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">Page562-a+ 60</a>]<BR>bruary.)<BR>	 2. A poet, the author of the SIŚUPĀLA Vadha or as it<BR>is named after him the Māgha Kāvya, one of the great profane<BR>poems of Hindu literature.<BR>	 f. (-घी)<BR>	 1. A potherb, (Hingtsha re-<BR>pens.)<BR>	 2. The day of full-moon in the Month of Māgha.<BR> E. मघा<BR>the asterism, in which the moon is full in this month, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=561-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघमा
माघमा f. (-मा) A female crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माघ्य|माघ्यं
माघ्य n. (-घ्यं) Many-flowered jasmine, (jasminum multiflorum or pube-<BR>scens.) “कुन्दपुष्पे”<BR> E. माघ the month Māgha, ष्यञ् aff. of derivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गलिक|मांगलिक
माङ्गलिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Propitious, tending to good fortune, wishing<BR>for it, indicating or portending it, &c.<BR> E. मङ्गल and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माङ्गल्य|मांगल्य|माङ्गल्यं
माङ्गल्य n. (-ल्यं) Welfare, propitiousness.<BR> E. मङ्गल and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माच|माचः
माच m. (-चः) A road, a way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचल|माचलः
माचल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A robber, a bandit.<BR>	 2. An alligator, a crocodile.<BR>	 3.<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR> E. मा fortune, wealth, चल् to go, (by such means.)<BR>and टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचिका
माचिका f. (-का) A fly.<BR> E. मच्-स्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माचिर|माचिरं
माचिर Ind. Quickly, without delay.<BR> E. मा prohibitive, and चिर long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माजल|माजलः
माजल m. (-लः) A sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माञ्जिष्ठ|मांजिष्ठ|माञ्जिष्ठं
माञ्जिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्टी-ष्टं) Of a red colour.<BR>	 n. (-ष्ठं) Red, the colour. E.<BR>मञ्जिष्ठा Bengal madder, used as a red dye, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठ|माठः
माठ m. (-ठः) A road.<BR>	 f. (-ठी) An armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठ्य
माठ्य m. (-ठ्यः) A road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माठर|माठरः
माठर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. One of the sun's attendants.<BR>	 2. The poet VYĀSA.<BR>	 3.<BR>Name of a Muni.<BR>	 4. A distiller.<BR> E. मन् to reverence, अरन् Unādi<BR>aff., ठच् substituted for the radical final, and the vowel optionally<BR>long; also माठर्य्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माड्
माड्(ऋ)माडृ r. 1st cl. (माडति-ते) To measure, to weigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माड|माडः
माड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. Weight or quantity.<BR>	 2. A species of tree.<BR> E. माड् to<BR>weigh, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माडि|माडिः
माडि m. (-डिः) A palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माड्डुक|माड्डुकः
माड्डुक m. (-कः) A drummer, a player on a sort of drum called Maḍ-<BR>ḍaka or Maḍḍu. q. v.<BR> E. मड्डु and अण् aff.; also with ठक् aff.<BR>माड्डुकिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माढि|माढिः
माढि m. (-ढिः)<BR>	 1. The germ of leaves, the young leaf before it opens.<BR>2. Distress, affliction.<BR>	 3. Evidence or declaration of distress.<BR>	 4. A<BR>back or double tooth.<BR>	 5. The hem or border of a garment.<BR>	 6. Po-<BR>verty, indigence.<BR>	 7. Anger, passion.<BR> E. मह् to worship, aff. क्तिन्;<BR>the final becomes ढ, and the preceding vowel is made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण
माण(न)क m. (-कः) A small shrub, (Arum Indicum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणव|माणवः
माणव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A child.<BR>	 2. A man, (in a contemptuous sense,) a<BR>manikin.<BR>	 3. A pearl-necklace of sixteen or twenty strings.<BR> E. मनु<BR>a man, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणवक|माणवकः
माणवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A child, a boy not exceeding sixteen years of age,<BR>a manikin.<BR>	 2. A pupil, a scholar, a religious student.<BR>	 3. A man,<BR>an ignorant or ridiculous man, a childish man.<BR>	 4. A necklace of<BR>sixteen or twenty strings.<BR>	 5. A species of the Anushtubh me-<BR>tre.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणवीन|माणवीनं
माणवीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Boyish, childish, fit or suitable for a child. E.<BR>माणव as above, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणव्य|माणव्यं
माणव्य n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. A number of boys.<BR>	 2. Boyhood.<BR> E. माणव a boy, यत्<BR>aff. of property or multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिका
माणिका f. (-का) A weight of eight Palas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिक्य|माणिक्यं
माणिक्य n. (-क्यं) A ruby.<BR>	 f. (-क्या) A house-lizard.<BR> E. मणि a gem, कै to<BR>call, यत् or यञ् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिबन्ध|माणिबंध|माणिबंधं|माणिबन्धं
माणिबन्ध n. (-न्धं) Rock-salt.<BR> E. मणिबन्ध a mountain, अण् aff; found there.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माणिमन्थ|माणिमंथ|माणिमंथं|माणिमन्थं
माणिमन्थ n. (-न्थं) Rock-salt.<BR> E. मणिमन्थ a mountain, from which the<BR>salt is supposed to be produced, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माण्डलिक|मांडलिक|माण्डलिकः
माण्डलिक m. (-कः) The ruler of a province.<BR>	 f. (-की) Ruling a province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातङ्ग|मातंग|मातंगः|मातङ्गः
मातङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. A man of a degraded caste, a<BR>Caṇḍāla, and outcaste.<BR>	 3. A sort of divine being attendant on a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">Page562-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Jina.<BR>	 4. The sacred fig-tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>	 5. A mountaineer,<BR>a barbarian.<BR>	 6. Any thing the best of its kind, (at the end of a<BR>compound.)<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. The goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR>	 2. The wife<BR>of VASIṢṬHA.<BR> E. मतङ्ग a saint, an elephant, &c., and अण् aff. of<BR>descent or pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातरपितृ
मातरपितृ m. Du. (-तरौ) Parents, mother and father.<BR> E. मातृ mother, and पितृ father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातरिश्वन्
मातरिश्वन् m. (-श्वा) Air, wind.<BR> E. मातृ space in the seventh case, in the<BR>heavens, श्वि to increase, Unādi aff. मनिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातलि|मातलिः
मातलि m. (-लिः) The charioteer of INDRA.<BR> E. मातल, and इञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातली
मातली f. (-ली) One of DURGĀ'S female companions.<BR> E. माता from मातृ<BR>DURGĀ, and आली a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातापितृ
मातापितृ m. Du. (-तरौ) Mother and father.<BR> E. माता from मातृ a mother,<BR>and पितृ a father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातामह|मातामहः
मातामह m. (-हः) A maternal grandfather.<BR>	 f. (-ही) A maternal grand-<BR>mother.<BR> E. मातृ a mother, डामहच् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माति|मातिः
माति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Measure.<BR>	 2. Conception, idea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुल|मातुलः
मातुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A maternal uncle.<BR>	 2. Thorn-apple, (Dhuturā metal.)<BR>3. A sort of grain.<BR>	 4. A variegated snake.<BR>	 f. (-ला-ली or -लानी)<BR>	 1. The<BR>wife of a maternal uncle, &c.<BR>	 2. Hemp, (Cannabis sativa.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Common Bengal San, a sort of Crotolaria, (C. juncea.)<BR>	 f. (-लानी)<BR>Pulse of various kinds.<BR> E. मातृ a mother, and डुलच् aff., fem. aff.<BR>टाप् or ङीष् with आनुक् optionally inserted before the latter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलपुत्त्रक
मातुलपुत्त्रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The son of maternal uncle.<BR>	 2. The fruit of the<BR>Dhuturā.<BR> E. मातुल a maternal uncle, &c., and पुत्त्र son, with कन्<BR>pleonasm, or aff. of comparison; also similar compounds, as<BR>मातुलात्मज m. (-जः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलाहि|मातुलाहिः
मातुलाहि m. (-हिः) A variegated serpent.<BR> E. मातुल the same, and अहि snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलि
मातुलि m. (-लिः) INDRA'S charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलुङ्ग|मातुलुंग|मातुलुंगः|मातुलुङ्गः
मातुलुङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Common citron.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गा) The sweet lime. E. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलुङ्गक|मातुलुङ्गकः
मातुलुङ्गक m. (-कः) Common citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR> E. मा prohibitive<BR>prefix, तुला a balance, गम् to go, खच् aff.; with the power of डित्,<BR>and कन् added, not sold by weight; also without the additional<BR>prefix, मतुलुङ्ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृ
मातृ f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A mother.<BR>	 2. A divine mother, the personified energy<BR>of a deity or his wife; in a figurative sense, a mother to mortals;<BR>eight divine Mātṛs are enumerated, BRĀHMĪ, the Mātṛ of<BR>BRAHMĀ; MAHEŚWARĪ, the Mātṛ of ŚIVA; VAISHNAVĪ, of<BR>VIṢṆU; AINDRĪ, of INDRA; VĀRĀHĪ, of VIṢṆU, as the Varāha<BR>Avatār; KAUMĀRĪ, of KĀRTIKEYA; KAUVERĪ or CHĀMUNDĀ of<BR>KUVERA, and CHARCHIKĀ of ŚIVA, in one of his minor incarna-<BR>tions; another list calls them MAHEŚWARĪ, BRĀHMĪ, NĀRĀYANĪ,<BR>AINDRĪ, VARĀHĪ, KAUMĀRĪ, NARASĪNHĪ, and APARĀJITĀ, differ-<BR>ing from the preceding one in the two last names, the first one of<BR>which, is the energy of VIṢṆU in the Narasinha Avatār, and the<BR>latter a form of DURGĀ; another enumeration makes the Mātṛs<BR>sixteen, and another but seven.<BR>	 3. A cow.<BR>	 4. A female of the Brāh-<BR>mana tribe, or the wife of a Brāhman.<BR>	 5. The earth.<BR>	 6. A name of<BR>LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 7. A name of REVATĪ.<BR>	 8. Space, ether.<BR> E. मान to res-<BR>pect, Unādi aff. तृच्, and the final of the radical rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृक|मातृकः
मातृक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Maternal, belonging to a mother.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A<BR>maternal uncle.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A mother.<BR>	 2. A nurse.<BR>	 3. The alphabet<BR>employed in certain diagrams for magical purposes.<BR>	 4. A simple<BR>sound, a note, a vowel.<BR>	 5. A goddess.<BR>	 6. A grand-mother.<BR>	 7.<BR>Source, origin.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृकच्छिद|मातृकच्छिदः|मातृकछिद
मातृकच्छिद m. (-दः) PARASURĀMA.<BR> E. मातृ mother, क the head, and छिद्<BR>to cut, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृकेशट|मातृकेशटः
मातृकेशट m. (-टः) A mother's brother.<BR> E. मातृ a mother, and केशट a brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृगण|मातृगणः
मातृगण m. (-णः) The assemblage of divine mothers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृगन्धिनी|मातृगंधिनी
मातृगन्धिनी f. (-नी) An unnatural mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृगामिन्
मातृगामिन् m. (-मी) An incestuous son.<BR> E. मातृ, and गामिन् who goes to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=562-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृगोत्र
मातृगोत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Belonging to the mother's family.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं) The<BR>mother's family.<BR> E. मातृ, and गोत्र race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृघातुक|मातृघातुकः
मातृघातुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. A matricide.<BR> E. मातृ a mother, DITĪ<BR>the mother of the gods, and घातुक destroyer, injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृपक्ष|मातृपक्षः
मातृपक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Belonging or relating to the maternal line, or<BR>mother, &c.<BR> E. मातृ, and पक्ष side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृबन्धु|मातृबंधु|मातृबन्धुः
मातृबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) The cognate relation by the mother's side, as any<BR>of the maternal grandfather's or grandmother's sister's or brother's<BR>children.<BR> E. मातृ a mother, and बन्धु a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृभोगीण
मातृभोगीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Fit or proper to be possessed, &c. by the<BR>mother.<BR> E. मातृ, भोग enjoyment, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृमुख|मातृमुखः
मातृमुख m. (-खः) A blockhead, a fool.<BR> E. मातृ a mother, मुख principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृशासित|मातृशासितः
मातृशासित m. (-तः) A blockhead, a fool.<BR> E. मातृ a mother and शासित<BR>governed, mother-led.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृष्वसृ
मातृष्वसृ f. (-सा) A mother's sister.<BR> E. मातृ mother, and ष्वसृ a sister also, मातुःष्वसृ or मातुःस्वसृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृष्वसेय|मातृष्वसेयः
मातृष्वसेय m. (-यः) A mother's sister's son.<BR>	 f. (-यी) A mother's sister's<BR>daughter.<BR> E. मातृ a mother, ष्वसृ a sister, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृष्वस्रीय|मातृष्वस्रीयः
मातृष्वस्रीय m. (-यः) A mother's sister's son.<BR>	 f. (-या) A mother's sister's<BR>daughter.<BR> E. मातृष्यसृ a maternal aunt, and छन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृसिंही
मातृसिंही f. (-ही) A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda, and ganderussa.) “वासक वृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्र|मात्रं|मात्रः
मात्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The whole, the entire thing or class of things.<BR>	 2. (Adv.)<BR>Only, solely, (exclusive and identical, the very thing.)<BR>	 3. The<BR>primitive subtle or invisible type of visible elementary matter.<BR>	 4.<BR>A pleonastic addition to words.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. Requisite, material.<BR>	 2.<BR>Quantity, measure.<BR>	 3. A little.<BR>	 4. An ear-ring.<BR>	 5. Wealth, subs-<BR>tance.<BR>	 6. A short vowel.<BR>	 7. A moment.<BR>	 8. Quantity in metre or<BR>prosody, a syllabic foot.<BR>	 9. The upper or horizontal limb of the<BR>Nāgarī characters.<BR> E. मा to measure, Unādi aff. त्रन्, fem. aff. टाप्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्रक
मात्रक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Mere, only, solely.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सर
मात्सर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Envious, or impatient of another's prosperity<BR>E. मत्सर envy, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सर्य्य|मात्सर्य|मात्सर्यं|मात्सर्य्यं
मात्सर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Envy, malice.<BR> E. मत्सर envious, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्स्यिक|मात्स्यिकः
मात्स्यिक m. (-कः) A fisherman.<BR> E. मत्स्य a fish, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथ्
माथ् (इ) माथि r. 1st cl. (मान्थति) To hurt or kill, to afflict, to suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथ|माथः
माथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Churning, stirring.<BR>	 2. A road.<BR>	 3. Hurting, injuring,<BR>killing.<BR> E. माथ् to hurt, aff. अच्; or मथ् to agitate, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद|मादः
माद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Intoxication, literal or figurative.<BR>	 2. Pride.<BR>	 3. Joy,<BR>ecstasy.<BR> E. मद् to be delighted or inebriated, and aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादक|मादकः
मादक m. (-कः) A gallinule.<BR>	 f. (-दिका)<BR>	 1. Intoxicating.<BR>	 2. Gladdening.<BR>E. मद् to delight, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादन|मादनं|मादनः
मादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cloves.<BR>	 2. Delighting, inebriating.<BR>	 3. Exhilaration.<BR>	 4.<BR>Intoxication.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. KĀMA.<BR>	 2. The thorn apple.<BR> E. मद् to be<BR>pleased, in the causal form, to please, &c., aff. ल्युट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादृश्
मादृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Like me, resembling me.<BR> E. मा for अस्मद् I. दृश् to see,<BR>aff. क्विन्; also with कञ् or कस, aff. मादृश and मादृक्ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्री
माद्री f. (-द्री) The wife of PĀṆḌU, and mother of the youngest of the<BR>Pāṇḍava princes.<BR> E. मद्र a king, अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रीपति|माद्रीपतिः
माद्रीपति m. (-तिः) A name of PĀṆḌU.<BR> E. माद्री the wife of the sover-<BR>eign, पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रीपृथापति
माद्रीपृथापति m. (-तिः) A name of PĀṆḌU.<BR> E. माद्री, and पृथा his other wife, पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधव|माधवः
माधव mfn. (-वः-वी-व) Made of honey, &c.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A name of KṚṢṆA<BR>or VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. The month Vaisākha.<BR>	 3. Spring.<BR>	 4. An epi-<BR>thet of PARASURĀMA.<BR>	 5. INDRA.<BR>	 f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. Sugar, clayed or<BR>candied.<BR>	 2. A large creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>	 3. Spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>	 4. A bawd.<BR>	 5. A sort of dentifrice, commonly Misi.<BR>	 6.<BR>Sacred basil.<BR>	 7. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 n. (-वं) Sweetness.<BR> E. मधु<BR>honey, &c., and अण् aff. of derivation or reference; or मा-धव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवक|माधवकः
माधवक m. (-कः) A spirituous liquor, made from the blossoms of the<BR>Bassia latifolia.<BR>	 f. (-विका)<BR>	 1. A kind of creeper.<BR>	 2. A female atten-<BR>dant.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवीलता
माधवीलता f. (-ता) A large creeper bearing white fragrant flowers,<BR>(Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR> E. माधवी the same, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवेष्टा
माधवेष्टा f. (-ष्टा) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. माधव, and इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुकरी
माधुकरी f. (-री) The alms obtained from five places by the third<BR>class of religious mendicants, gathering alms from door to door<BR>as a bee gathers honey from flower to flower.<BR> E. मधुकर a<BR>bee, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुमत
माधुमत m. Plu. (-ताः) The people of Kāshmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुर|माधुरं
माधुर n. (-रं) Arabian jasmine or its flower.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Spirituous or<BR>vinous liquor.<BR>	 2. Sweetness of temper, amiableness.<BR> E. मधुर sweet,<BR>&c., affs. अण् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुर्य्य|माधुर्य|माधुर्यं|माधुर्य्यं
माधुर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Sweetness of flavour or disposition.<BR> E. मधुर sweet,<BR>literally or figuratively, aff. ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधूक
माधूक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Sweet-speaking or sounding.<BR>	 2. Made from<BR>the Bassia tree.<BR> E. मधूक and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्य
माध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) Middle, mid, (day.)<BR> E. मध्य and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यम|माध्यमं
माध्यम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Middle-born.<BR> E. मध्यम the same, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ|माध्यस्थं
माध्यस्थ n. (-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Middle state or condition.<BR>	 2. Indifference to earthly<BR>objects.<BR> E. मध्यस्थ and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ्य|माध्यस्थ्यं
माध्यस्थ्य n. (-स्थ्यं) Mediation, intercession.<BR> E. मध्यस्थ and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यक
माध्यक m. (-कः) Spirit distilled from the flowers of the Bassia.<BR> E. मधु<BR>Bassia, अण् aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वी
माध्वी f. (-ध्वी)<BR>	 1. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 2. A sort of fish.<BR> E. मधु sweet, q. v. अण् and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वीक|माध्वीकं
माध्वीक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Spirituous liquor, distilled from the blossoms of the<BR>Bassia latifolia.<BR>	 2. Wine, spirit distilled from grapes.<BR> E. माध्वी as<BR>above, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्
मान् r. 1st cl. (मीमांसते) To investigate, to seek or desire knowledge. r.<BR>1st and 10th cls. (मानति मानयति-ते) To respect, to revere, to wor-<BR>ship. With अप or अव prefixed, to treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान|मानं|मानः
मान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Measure in general, whether of weight, length, or capa-<BR>city.<BR>	 2. A measure, the fourth or eighth part of a Khāri.<BR>	 3. The<BR>computation of the duration of a year, solar, lunar, sydereal, &c.<BR>4. Proof, demonstration.<BR>	 5. Likeness.<BR>	 6. Dimension.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Arrogance, haughtiness, pride.<BR>	 2. Female arrogance or indigna-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Taking, seizing.<BR>	 4. A blockhead.<BR>	 5. An agent.<BR>	 6. A<BR>barbarian.<BR>	 7. Honour.<BR> E. मा to measure, ल्युट् aff.; or मन् to revere,<BR>(one's self,) aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानक|मानकं
मानक n. (-कं) A plant, of which the root is sometimes eaten, (Arum<BR>indicum.)<BR>	 f. (-निका)<BR>	 1. The fourth or eighth part of a Khāri.<BR>	 2.<BR>A kind of spirituous liquor.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानकलह|मानकलहः
मानकलह m. (-हः) A quarrel caused by jealousy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानकलि|मानकलिः
मानकलि f. (-लिः) Coolness, haughtiness, disdain.<BR> E. मान pride, and<BR>कलि quarrelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानग्रन्थि|मानग्रंथि|मानग्रन्थिः
मानग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः)<BR>	 1. Fault, transgression.<BR>	 2. Pride, self-conceit.<BR> E. मान<BR>pride, and ग्रन्थि a knot or joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानद|मानदः
मानद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Inspiring pride.<BR>	 2. Measuring.<BR> E. मान and द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानदण्ड|मानदंड|मानदण्डः
मानदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A measuring-rod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानधानिका
मानधानिका f. (-का) A cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानन|माननं
मानन nf. (-नं-ना) Honouring, paying respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माननीय|माननीयं
माननीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be respected or revered.<BR> E. मान to respect, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानरन्ध्रा|मानरंध्रा
मानरन्ध्रा f. (-न्ध्रा) A perforated copper vessel filled with water, to<BR>mark the time, &c.: see ताम्री.<BR> E. मान a measure, and रन्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव|मानवः
मानव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A man, man.<BR>	 2. A boy.<BR>	 f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. A<BR>goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>	 3. A daughter of the first MANU.<BR>n. (-वं) A particular fine.<BR> E. मनु the progenitor of mankind, and<BR>अण् patronymic aff.: see माणव and माणवक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवत्|मानवन्त्
मानवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Proud, haughty, high-spirited.<BR>	 f. (-वती) A<BR>woman angry from jealousy.<BR> E. मान and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवर्ज्जित|मानवर्जित|मानवर्जितः
मानवर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Humble, lowly.<BR> E. मान pride, and वर्ज्जित<BR>freed from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव्य|मानव्यं
मानव्य n. (-व्यं) A multitude of boys.<BR> E. माणव or मानव a boy, यत् aff. of<BR>multitude, more properly माणव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानस|मानसं|मानसः
मानस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Mental.<BR>	 n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. The mind, the seat or faculty<BR>of reason and feeling.<BR>	 2. The lake Mānus, or Mānasarovara in the<BR>Himālaya mountains.<BR>	 3. (In law,) Tacit or implied consent.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-सी)<BR>	 1. Mental, born from the mind.<BR>	 2. A kind of salt.<BR>	 3. A god-<BR>dess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR> E. मनस् the mind, aff. अण्; or मनस्<BR>BRAHMĀ, the supreme mind, अण् aff. of derivation, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसत्व
मानसत्व n. (-त्वं) Thoughtfulness.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसालय|मानसालयः
मानसालय m. (-यः) A gander or wild swan.<BR> E. मानस and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसूत्र|मानसूत्रं
मानसूत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A chain of gold or silver, worn as an ornament<BR>round the loins.<BR>	 2. A measuring-cord.<BR> E. मान pride and सूत्र thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसौकस्
मानसौकस् m. (-काः) The wild swan or goose.<BR> E. मानस् the lake Mānasa-<BR>rovara, and ओकस् dwelling; being supposed to migrate yearly<BR>from Hindusthan to the banks of the lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिता
मानिता f. (-ता) Pride, dignity.<BR> E. मानिन् and तल् aff.; also with त्व, मानित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिन्
मानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>	 1. Proud, arrogant, haughty.<BR>	 2. (In compo-<BR>sition,) Who thinks or fancies.<BR>	 f. (-निनी)<BR>	 1. A woman, especially<BR>one displeased and indignant towards her lover.<BR>	 2. A resolute<BR>woman.<BR>	 3. A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>	 4. A species of the<BR>Atisarkarī metre.<BR>	 m. (-नी) A lion.<BR> E. मान pride, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष|मानुषः
मानुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Human.<BR>	 m. (-षः) A man.<BR>	 f. (-षी)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2.<BR>A branch of medicine, the administering of drugs and herbs. E.<BR>मनुष a man, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्य|मानुष्यं
मानुष्य n. (-ष्यं) Manhood, manliness, humanity, the state or quality<BR>of man or mortal.<BR> E. मनुष a man, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्यक|मानुष्यकं
मानुष्यक n. (-कं) A multitude of men.<BR> E. मनुष्य a man, and वुञ् aff. of multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानोज्ञक|मानोज्ञकं
मानोज्ञक n. (-कं) Beauty, agreeableness, loveliness.<BR> E. मनोज्ञ agreeable,<BR>and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्त्रिक|मांत्रिक|मांत्रिकः|मान्त्रिकः
मान्त्रिक m. (-कः) One who is conversant with spells or incantations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्द्य|मांद्य|मांद्यं|मान्द्यं
मान्द्य n. (-न्द्यं)<BR>	 1. Sickness, indisposition.<BR>	 2. Sluggishness, torpor, apa-<BR>thy, stupidity, &c.<BR> E. मन्द slow, sluggish, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्धातृ|मांधातृ
मान्धातृ m. (-ता) A king fostered by INDRA.<BR> E. मां me, धातृ drinker;<BR>from धे to drink; having on one occasion sucked Amrita from the<BR>finger of INDRA, who then used the exclamation which afterwards<BR>was the name of the prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्य|मान्यः
मान्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Respectable.<BR> E. मन् to respect, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापत्य|मापत्यः
मापत्य m. (-त्यः) A name of KĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापन|मापनं|मापनः
मापन m. (-नः) A balance, a pair of scales.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Measure, measur-<BR>ing.<BR>	 2. Making, forming,<BR> E. मा to measure, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामक|मामकं|मामकः
मामक mfn. (-कः-मिका-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Mine.<BR>	 2. Selfish.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A miser, a<BR>niggard.<BR>	 2. A mother's brother.<BR> E. ममक mine, from मम the poss.<BR>case of अहम् I, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामकीन|मामकीनं
मामकीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Mine.<BR> E. मम mine, खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माय|मायः
माय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A mime, a juggler.<BR>	 2. An Asura or evil spirit.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>1. Fraud, trick, deceit, illusion.<BR>	 2. A female juggler.<BR>	 3. Under-<BR>standing, human intellect.<BR>	 4. Compassion.<BR>	 5. Wickedness, vil-<BR>lainy, villainous deception.<BR>	 6. A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 7. Trick in<BR>negotiation, political fraud, diplomacy.<BR>	 8. Philosophical illusion,<BR>idealism, unreality of all worldly existance; personified in mytho-<BR>logy as a female, the consort of BRAHMĀ or GOD, and the imme-<BR>diate and active cause of creation.<BR>	 9. The mother of BUDDHA.<BR>10. The Pradhāna of the Sānkhyas.<BR>	 11. Illusion which makes<BR>one see the supreme spirit and the universe to be two distinct<BR>realities, (in Vedānta Phil.)<BR> E. मा to measure, Unādi aff. यत्; the<BR>medium through which all things are seen, and by which they<BR>are estimated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाकार|मायाकारः
मायाकार m. (-रः) A juggler, a mime, an actor.<BR> E. माया trick or delu-<BR>sion, कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाकृत्
मायाकृत् m. (-कृत्) A juggler.<BR> E. माया trick, and कृत् who practises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाचण
मायाचण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Illusive, deceptive.<BR> E. माया and चणष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाजीविन्
मायाजीविन् m. (-वी) A conjurer, a juggler.<BR> E. माया trick, and जीविन् who<BR>lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाद|मायादः
मायाद m. (-दः) A crocodile, an alligator.<BR> E. माया illusion, and द who gives or makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायादेवीसुत|मायादेवीसुतः
मायादेवीसुत m. (-तः) BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha sect. E.<BR>मायादेवी the goddess MĀYĀ or illusion, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायापटु
मायापटु mfn. (-टुः-टुः-टु) Delusive, expert in deceiving.<BR> E. माया, and पटु clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाप्रयोग|मायाप्रयोगः
मायाप्रयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Application of tricks.<BR>	 2. Employment of magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायामय
मायामय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Illusive, deceptive.<BR> E. माया and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावचन
मायावचन n. (-नं) A deceptive speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावत्|मायावन्त्
मायावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Deceptive, illusory.<BR>	 m. (-वान्) A name of<BR>KANSA.<BR>	 f. (-वती) the wife of KĀMA.<BR> E. माया fraud, illusion, and<BR>मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावसिक|मायावसिकः
मायावसिक m. (-कः) A deceiver, a cheater, a liar.<BR> E. माया fraud, वस् to abide, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाविन्
मायाविन् m. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A juggler, a conjurer.<BR>	 2. A cat.<BR>	 3. A demon.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-वी) A gallnut.<BR> E. माया trick, and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायासुत|मायासुतः
मायासुत m. (-तः) BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR> E. माया<BR>the goddess so named, and सुत the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिक|मायिकं|मायिकः
मायिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Illusory, deceptive.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A juggler, a conju-<BR>rer.<BR> E. माया trick, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिन्
मायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Deceptive, illusory.<BR>	 m. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A conjurer, a<BR>juggler.<BR>	 2. A cheat, a deceiver.<BR>	 3. ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. AGNI.<BR>	 5. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 6.<BR>KĀMA or love.<BR> E. माया fraud, &c., and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायु|मायुः
मायु m. (-युः) Bile, the bilious humour.<BR> E. सि to scatter or diffuse,<BR>(through the body,) उण् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायुराज|मायुराजः
मायुराज m. (-जः) The son of KUVERA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूर|मायूरं
मायूर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Belonging to a peacock, made of its feathers, &c.<BR>n. (-रं) A flock of peacocks.<BR> E. मयूर a peacock, and अण् aff. of mul-<BR>titude, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरिक|मायूरिकः
मायूरिक m. (-कः) A hunter or killer of peacocks.<BR> E. मयूर a peacock, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार|मारः
मार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Death, dying.<BR>	 2. Killing, slaying, destroying.<BR>	 3. Ob-<BR>struction, opposition, impediment.<BR>	 4. Thorn-apple, (Dhuturā me-<BR>tal.)<BR>	 5. A name of KĀMA.<BR>	 6. Love, passion.<BR>	 7. The devil, the evil<BR>one, (in Buddhistic works.)<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A name of CHANDĪ, a<BR>form of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. Plague, pestilence, epidemic.<BR>	 3. Ruin.<BR> E. मृ<BR>to die, aff. घञ्; or in the causal form, with अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारक|मारकः
मारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Epidemic disease, plague.<BR>	 2. A falcon, a hawk.<BR>	 3.<BR>A slayer, a destroyer.<BR>	 4. The god of death.<BR> E. मृ to die, causal<BR>form, aff. वुन्, ण्वुल् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारकत
मारकत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Relating to an emerald, of the colour of an emerald, &c.<BR> E. मरकत, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारजातक|मारजातकः
मारजातक m. (-कः) A cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारजित्
मारजित् m. (-जित्) A BUDDHA.<BR> E. मार love and जित् who overcomes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारण|मारणं
मारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. A magical ceremony for the<BR>purpose of destroying an enemy.<BR>	 3. A kind of poison.<BR> E. मृ to die,<BR>causal form, to kill, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारात्मक
मारात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Murderous.<BR> E. मार and आत्मक disposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारि|मारिः
मारि f. (-रिः-री)<BR>	 1. Killing.<BR>	 2. Ruin.<BR>	 3. Plague, epidemic.<BR> E. मृ to die,<BR>causal form, इ aff.: see मार and मारी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिचिक|मारिचिकं
मारिचिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Peppered, seasoned with pepper.<BR> E. मरिच<BR>pepper, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारित|मारितः
मारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Killed, slain.<BR> E. मृ to die, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिव्यसनवारक|मारिव्यसनवारकः
मारिव्यसनवारक m. (-कः) The name of a royal saint.<BR> E. मारि plague, व्यसन<BR>calamity, वारक stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिष|मारिषः
मारिष m. (-षः) A venerable person, (in dramatic language, especially<BR>the title of the manager, or principal actor.)<BR>	 mf. (-षः-षी) A potherb,<BR>(Amaranthus oleraceus.)<BR>	 f. (-षी) The mother of the sage DAKṢA.<BR>E. मृष् to bear patiently, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीच|मारीचः
मारीच m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. The name of a Rākshasa, the son of Sunda and Tā-<BR>dakā. He allured RĀMA away in the form of a golden deer and<BR>thus assisted RĀVANA in his design of carrying off SITA.<BR>	 2. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">Page565-a+ 60</a>]<BR>military or royal elephant.<BR>	 3. A sort of berry, commonly Kak-<BR>koli.<BR>	 f. (-ची) A goddess, peculiar to the Bauddhas.<BR>	 n. (-चं) A<BR>collection of pepper plants.<BR> E. मरीच a saint, &c. aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुण्ड|मारुंड|मारुंडः|मारुण्डः
मारुण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A serpent's egg.<BR>	 2. A road.<BR>	 3. A place spread with<BR>cow-dung; some authorities have मारण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुत|मारुतः
मारुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. Vital air, one of the three humours<BR>of the body.<BR>	 3. A demi-god, of whom there is a class consist-<BR>ing of forty-nine.<BR>	 4. The trunk of an elephant.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Burnt-<BR>offering on conception.<BR>	 2. The constellation Svāti.<BR> E. मृ to die,<BR>(by excess of it,) उति aff., and the vowel made long; the demi-<BR>gods, called Marutas, are said to be the sons of Diti, formed<BR>of the divisions of the fœtus in utero, by the Bajra or thunder-<BR>bolt of INDRA, and to be named from that deity's addressing the<BR>fœtus he thus divided by मारोदीः weep not.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतव्रत|मारुतव्रतं
मारुतव्रत n. (-तं) One of the duties of a king, his universal presence<BR>by means of his emissaries.<BR> E. मारुत the wind, and व्रत observance,<BR>pervading all things like the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतात्मज|मारुतात्मजः
मारुतात्मज m. (-जः) HANUMĀNA the monkey-god.<BR> E. मारुत air, आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतापह|मारुतापहः
मारुतापह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Removing or opposing wind, windy humour,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-हः) A plant, (Capparis trifoliata.) “वरुणवृक्षे”.<BR> E. मारुत<BR>wind, or a disease of that humour, अपह removing, obviating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुताशन|मारुताशनः
मारुताशन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fasting, feeding on air.<BR> E. मारुत the wind,<BR>and अशन who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुति|मारुतिः
मारुति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A name of HANUMĀNA.<BR>	 2. The Pāṇḍava prince<BR>BHĪMA.<BR> E. मरुत wind, the deity, and इञ् patronymic aff.; the<BR>son of the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कटपिपीलिका
मार्कटपिपीलिका f. (-का) A small black ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्ड|मार्कंड|मार्कंडः|मार्कण्डः
मार्कण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A Muni, and narrator of one of the Purāṇas. E.<BR>मृकण्डु the father of the saint, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्डेय|मार्कंडेय|मार्कंडेयः|मार्कण्डेयः
मार्कण्डेय m. (-यः) MĀRKANDEYA a holy sage, the supposed author or<BR>narrator of one of the Purānas, named the Mārkandeya Purāṇa.<BR>E. मृकण्डु the father of the sage, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कव|मार्कवः
मार्कव m. (-वः) A spreading shrub: see भृङ्गराज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग्
मार्ग् r. 1st and 10th cls. (मार्गति मार्गयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To make or prepare.<BR>	 2.<BR>To go.<BR>	 3. To prepare the way, to make a road.<BR>	 4. To feather an<BR>arrow.<BR>	 5. To beg.<BR>	 6. To ask in marriage. (मार्गयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To seek.<BR>2. To go.<BR>	 3. To adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग|मार्गः
मार्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. A road, a path or way.<BR>	 2. Search, seeking, inquiry.<BR>	 3.<BR>The anus.<BR>	 4. Musk.<BR>	 5. A way, a means.<BR>	 6. The path of a planet.<BR>7. Mode, method, course, manner.<BR>	 8. Style, diction.<BR>	 9. The<BR>month in which the moon is full in the asterism Mrigaśirsha,<BR>(November-December.)<BR>	 10. The constellation Mrigaśirsha.<BR>	 11. (In<BR>geometry,) A section.<BR> E. मृग् to inquire, aff. अण्; or मृज् to clean,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गक|मार्गकः
मार्गक m. (-कः) The month Agrahāyaṇa, (November-December.)<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गण|मार्गणं|मार्गणः
मार्गण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Mendicant, asking, begging, a beggar.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>1. Asking, soliciting, begging.<BR>	 2. Research, inquiry.<BR>	 3. Affection,<BR>affectionate solicitation or inquiry.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. A<BR>suppliant, a solicitor.<BR>	 3. The number “five.”<BR> E. मार्ग् to ask, to<BR>seek, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गणक|मार्गणकः
मार्गणक m. (-कः) A suppliant, a beggar.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गतोरण
मार्गतोरण n. (-णं) An arch erected over a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गधेनु|मार्गधेनुः
मार्गधेनु m. (-नुः) A Yojana, a measure of distance equal to 4,000 fa-<BR>thoms or four Kos, above eight miles.<BR> E. मार्ग a road, धेनु a milch<BR>cow; also with कन् added, मार्गधेनुक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गव|मार्गवः
मार्गव m. (-वः) A man of a low caste, born of a Nishada by an Ayogava female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशिर|मार्गशिरः
मार्गशिर m. (-रः) The month Agrahāyaṇa, (November-December.) E.<BR>मृगशिरस् the asterism in which the moon is full, and अण् aff.;<BR>also from मृगशीर्ष with अण् aff. मार्गशीर्ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशीर्ष|मार्गशीर्षः
मार्गशीर्ष m. (-र्षः) The month Mārgaśirsha: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गिक|मार्गिकः
मार्गिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A deer-killer, a hunter.<BR>	 2. A traveller, a way-farer.<BR>E. मृग a deer, or मार्ग a road, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गित|मार्गितं
मार्गित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sought, inquired after, pursued.<BR> E. मार्ग् to seek for, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग्य|मार्ग्यं
मार्ग्य mfn. (-र्ग्यः-र्ग्या-र्ग्यं)<BR>	 1. To be cleaned or purified.<BR>	 2. To be sought.<BR>E. मृज् to cleanse, aff. ण्वत्; or मार्ग् to seek, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्
मार्ज् r. 1st cl. (मार्जयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज|मार्जः|मार्ज्ज|मार्ज्जः
मार्ज m. (-र्जः)<BR>	 1. Cleaning the body.<BR>	 2. A washerman.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR> E. मृज् to cleanse, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जन|मार्जनः|मार्ज्जन|मार्ज्जनं|मार्ज्जनः
मार्जन nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>	 1. Cleaning, cleansing, wiping.<BR>	 2. Cleaning the person,<BR>by wiping, bathing, or rubbing it with oil or fragrant unguents.<BR>m. (-नः) A tree, commonly Lodh.<BR>	 f. (-ना) The sound of a drum.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी)<BR>	 1. A brush, a broom.<BR>	 2. One of DURGĀ'S attendants.<BR> E. मृज्<BR>to clean, aff. युच् or ल्युट्; or मार्ज् to sound, with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जनीय|मार्जनीयः
मार्जनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be cleaned, to be cleansed or purified. E.<BR>मृज् to cleanse, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जार|मार्जारः|मार्ज्जार
मार्जार mf. (-रः-री)<BR>	 1. The common cat.<BR>	 2. The wild or pole-cat.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>1. A female cat.<BR>	 2. Musk.<BR> E. मृज् to cleanse, (its skin and face,)<BR>आरन् aff., and the vowel made long; also read मार्ज्जाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जारक|मार्जारक|मार्जारकः
मार्ज्जारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cat.<BR>	 2. A peacock.<BR> E. मार्जार a cat, and कन् aff.<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जारकण्ठ|मार्जारकण्ठ|मार्जारकंठ|मार्जारकण्ठः
मार्ज्जारकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A peacock, perhaps a wrong reading for the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जारकरण|मार्जारकरण
मार्ज्जारकरण n. (-णं) A particular mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जारकर्णिका|मार्जारकर्णिका
मार्ज्जारकर्णिका f. (-का) A goddess, a form of DURGĀ.<BR> E. मार्जार a cat, कर्ण<BR>the ear, कन् aff. fem. form; also मार्जारकर्णी having the ears of a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जारगन्धिका|मार्जारगन्धिका
मार्ज्जारगन्धिका f. (-का) A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus trilobus.) “मुद्नपर्ण्या”<BR>E. मार्जार a cat, गन्ध smell, कन् aff. of comparison: also मार्जारगन्धा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जारी|मार्जारी
मार्ज्जारी(ली)य mf. (-यः-या)<BR>	 1. A cat.<BR>	 2. A Śūdra: see मार्ज्जालीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जाल|मार्जाल|मार्जालः
मार्ज्जाल m. (-लः) A cat. E. See मार्जार, the final being changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जालीय|मार्जालीय|मार्जालीयः
मार्ज्जालीय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A cat.<BR>	 2. A Śūdra.<BR>	 3. Cleaning the body.<BR> E. मृज्<BR>to clean, and आलीयच् Unādi aff.; it is also written मार्जारीय, from<BR>the र and ल being interchanged; or as derived from मार्जार, with<BR>छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जित|मार्ज्जित
मार्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cleansed.<BR>	 2. Adorned.<BR>	 3. Swept, brushed.<BR>E. मार्ज् to clean, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्जिता|मार्जिता
मार्ज्जिता f. (-ता) Curds with honey and spices.<BR> E. मार्ज् to clean, aff. क्त, fem. aff. टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्तण्ड|मार्तण्ड|मार्तंड|मार्तंडः|मार्तण्डः|मार्त्तण्डः
मार्त्तण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A hog.<BR>	 3. The Arka plant.<BR>	 4. The<BR>number “twelve.”<BR> E. मृतण्ड the progenitor of the sun, aff. अण्;<BR>or मृते अण्डे भवः अण् शक०; also sometimes मार्त्ताण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्तिक|मार्तिक|मार्त्तिकः
मार्त्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Earthen, made of clay or earth.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The<BR>lid of a pot or pitcher.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A potsherd.<BR> E. मृत्तिका earth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्य
मार्त्य n. (-र्त्यं) Mortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्दङ्ग|मार्दङ्ग|मार्दंग|मार्दंगः|मार्दङ्गः|मार्द्दङ्गं
मार्द्दङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A town, a city.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) A drummer.<BR> E. मृदङ्ग a drum,<BR>(played in or by,) अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्दङ्गिक|मार्दङ्गिक|मार्दंगिक|मार्दंगिकः|मार्दङ्गिकः|मार्द्दङ्गिकः
मार्द्दङ्गिक m. (-कः) A drummer, a player on the drum.<BR> E. मृदङ्ग a drum, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्दव|मार्दव|मार्दवं|मार्द्दवं|मार्द्दवः
मार्द्दव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Softness.<BR>	 2. Gentleness, leniency.<BR> E. मृदु soft, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्धव
मार्द्धव m. (-वः) A man of low caste and occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्धीक
मार्द्धीक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Made of or from grapes.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Wine. E.<BR>मृद्धीका a grape, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष|मार्षः
मार्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. A venerable or respectable man, (in dramatic langu-<BR>age.)<BR>	 2. A potherb. “तण्डुलीयशाके”.<BR> E. मृष् to suffer, aff. अण्;<BR>also मारिष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष्टि|मार्ष्टिः
मार्ष्टि f. (-र्ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Cleaning the person, bathing, wiping, smearing it<BR>with unguents or oil.<BR>	 2. Cleaning, cleansing in general.<BR> E. मृज्<BR>to cleanse, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल|मालं|मालः
माल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A field.<BR>	 2. Rising round.<BR>	 3. Fraud, deceit.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>1. A man.<BR>	 2. A mountain, a barbarian, one of a particular<BR>tribe.<BR>	 3. A country, lying west and south-west of Bengal:<BR>Ramghur, &c., or according to WILFORD, Mālbhūm in Midnā-<BR>pur.<BR>	 4. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A line, a row.<BR>	 2. A gar<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">Page566-a+ 60</a>]<BR>land, a string or wreath of flowers.<BR>	 3. A chaplet of flowers.<BR>	 4.<BR>A string of beads, a rosary.<BR>	 5. (In rhetorical or poetical descrip-<BR>tion,) a series or string of epithets, smiles, &c.<BR> E. मा fortune, ला to<BR>get or be, affs. अङ् and टाप्; or मा to measure, Unādi aff. र, and<BR>र changed to ल; or मल-संज्ञायां कर्त्तरि घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=565-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालक|मालकं|मालकः
मालक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The Nimba tree, (Melia azadiracta.)<BR>	 2. A vessel<BR>made of cocoanut-shell.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-का) A garland.<BR> E. माला a garland, कन् aff. and the final of the<BR>fem. rejected; also in the fem. form, मालाका and मालिका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालचक्रक|मालचक्रकं
मालचक्रक n. (-कं) The hip-joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालती
मालती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. Great-flowered jasmine, (Jasminum grandiflorum.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A bud, a blossom.<BR>	 3. A young woman.<BR>	 4. Moon-light.<BR>	 5. Night.<BR>	 6.<BR>A particular river.<BR>	 7. A flower, (Bignonia suave olens.)<BR>	 8. A<BR>shrub, (Echites caryophyllata.)<BR>	 9. A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR>E. मा LAKṢMĪ, लत a Sautra root, to shake, affs. अच् and ङीप्; or<BR>मल् to hold, अतच् aff.; or माल VIṢṆU, अत् to go, (to be presented<BR>to,) affs. अण् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतीतीरज|मालतीतीरजः
मालतीतीरज m. (-जः) Borax.<BR> E. मालती the river, तीर the band, ज produced. “टङ्कणे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतीपत्रिका
मालतीपत्रिका f. (-का) The shell of a nut-meg. “जैत्री” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतीफल|मालतीफलं
मालतीफल n. (-लं) Nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालय|मालयः
मालय n. (-यं) Sandal, the unguent prepared from it.<BR> E. मलय the<BR>mountain whence the wood is brought, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालव|मालवः
मालव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The province of Mālwā.<BR>	 2. Name of a musical mode.<BR>m. plu. (-वाः) The people of that province; also with ञ्य pleo-<BR>nasm मालव्य, fem. मालवी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालविका
मालविका f. (-का) A plant of valuable purgative properties, commonly Teori: see त्रिवृत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालसी
मालसी f. (-सी) A plant, commonly Keśhapusta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाका
मालाका f. (-का) A garland, a wreath.<BR> E. माला the same, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाकार|मालाकारः
मालाकार m. (-रः) A flower-seller, a florist, a gardener.<BR> E. माला a gar-<BR>land, and कार who makes; also, मालाकृत्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालातृणक|मालातृणकं
मालातृणक m. (-कः) A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schœnanthus.) E.<BR>माला a wreath, तृण grass, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालादीपक
मालादीपक n. (-कं) In rhetoric, affinity of various objects, by a common<BR>property.<BR> E. माला, and दीपक illustrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाफल
मालाफल n. (-लं) The seed of the Eleocarpus, of which common ro-<BR>saries are made.<BR> E. माला a rosary, and फल fruit. “रुद्राक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिक|मालिकः
मालिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Relating to a garland, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A flo-<BR>rist, a flower-gatherer or seller.<BR>	 2. A sort of bird.<BR>	 3. A colorist,<BR>a painter.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Double jasmine, (Jasminum zambac, floribus<BR>multiplicatis.)<BR>	 2. A daughter.<BR>	 3. A necklace, any ornament of the<BR>neck.<BR>	 4. A garland of flowers, a wreath.<BR>	 5. The name of a river.<BR>6. A spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>	 7. Linseed, (Linum utilatissimum.)<BR>8. A palace.<BR>	 9. A row, a series.<BR> E. माला a garland, ठन् aff., or कन्<BR>added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्
मालिन् m. (-ली) A florist, a gatherer and vendor of flowers, a gardener.<BR>f. (-लिनी)<BR>	 1. A name of UMĀ or DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. The Ganges of heaven.<BR>3. The city Champā, the modern Bhāgalpur.<BR>	 4. A poetical stanza,<BR>consisting of alternate verses or hemistichs of eight and seven<BR>syllables; it is especially used to conclude a section or canto.<BR>	 5.<BR>The wife of a flower-gatherer, or a female vendor of garlands, &c.<BR>6. A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>	 7. A shrub, (Echites caryophy-<BR>llata.)<BR>	 8. A girl seventeen years old personating DURGĀ at the<BR>festival of that goddess.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Adj.<BR>	 1. Wearing a garland.<BR>	 2.<BR>Encircled by.<BR> E. माला a garland, इनि aff., fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्य|मालिन्यं
मालिन्य n. (-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Foulness, dirtiness, impurity.<BR>	 2. Blackness.<BR>	 3. Sinful-<BR>ness.<BR>	 4. Trouble, affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालु|मालुः
मालु m. (-लुः)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. A sort of creeper. “पात्लता”.<BR> E. मल् to<BR>hold, Unādi aff. उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालुधान|मालुधानः
मालुधान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A variegated snake.<BR>	 2. A kind of serpent. “मालुया-<BR>साप्” f. (-नी) A sort or creeper.<BR> E. मालु a creeper, धान having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालूर|मालूरः
मालूर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A fruit tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>	 2. The Kapittha tree.<BR>E. मा fortune, लू to cut, रक् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालेय|मालेयः
मालेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating to a garland, &c.<BR>	 f. (-या) Large carda-<BR>moms.<BR> E. माला, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्य|माल्यं
माल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Proper or fit for a garland, &c.<BR>	 n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>flower.<BR>	 2. A garland, a wreath.<BR>	 3. A chaplet, a garland for the<BR>forehead.<BR>	 f. (-ल्या) A sort of grass, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR> E. माला<BR>a garland, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यवत्|माल्यवन्त्
माल्यवत् m. (-वान्)<BR>	 1. A mountainous range, described as one of the<BR>smaller mountains of India proper; lying eastward of mount<BR>Meru.<BR>	 2. An epithet of the maternal grand uncle of RĀVANA.<BR>LANKĀ was originally built for him: but it was deserted by him<BR>and occupied by KUVERA. RĀVANA recovered it from the latter<BR>and Mālyabat returned with his relations to live with RĀVANA<BR>as his minister.<BR>	 f. (-वती) Name of a river.<BR> E. माल्य a wreath, and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्ल|माल्लः
माल्ल m. (-ल्लः) Name of a mixed tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्लवी
माल्लवी f. (-वी) A wrestling or boxing match.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माशब्दिक|माशब्दिकः
माशब्दिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Prohibitive, prohibiting, a prohibitor, a for-<BR>bidder.<BR> E. मा particle of negation or prohibition, शब्द a sound, a<BR>word, ठक् aff.; implying the person or thing whence it proceeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माष|माषः
माष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus radiatus.) “माषकडाइ”<BR>2. A jeweller's or goldsmith's weight, variously reckoned at five,<BR>eight, or ten, Rattis, or seeds of the Abrus precatorius; the<BR>weight in common use, is about seventeen grains troy.<BR>	 3. A<BR>blockhead, a fool.<BR>	 4. A cutaneous disease.<BR> E. मष् to hurt, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषक|माषकः
माषक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A weight of silver of two Rattis or about 4(1/2) grains.<BR>2. The same in gold.<BR>	 3. A Māsha: see the last.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषप
माषप(व)र्णी f. (-र्णी) A kind of leguminous shrub, (Glycine debilis.)<BR>“माषाणी”<BR> E. माष the kidney-bean, पर्ण a leaf, aff. ङीष्, resembling<BR>it in the leaf; also माषपर्णा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषवर्द्धक
माषवर्द्धक m. (-कः) A goldsmith, a jeweller.<BR> E. माष the weight so called, बृद्ध् to increase, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषशस्
माषशस् Ind. Māsha by Māsha, (given away, &c.)<BR> E. माष a particular<BR>weight, and शसि aff. of successive order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषाज्य
माषाज्य n. (-ज्यं) Beans cooked with ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषाद|माषादः
माषाद m. (-दः) A tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषाश|माषाशः
माषाश m. (-शः) A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषिक
माषिक f. (-की) Adj. Worth one Māsha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषीण|माषीणं
माषीण n. (-णं) A field of kidney-beans.<BR> E. माष as above, खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माष्य|माष्यं
माष्य n. (-ष्यं) A field of kidney-beans.<BR> E. माष as above, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्
मास् m. (-माः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A month.<BR> E. मा splendour, light, अस् to<BR>throw, क्विप् aff.; or सा to measure, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास|मासं|मासः
मास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A month, the twelfth part of the Hindu year; it is<BR>usually a lunar one, consisting of thirty Tithis, but it may be a<BR>Saura or solar month, being equal to the sun's passage through<BR>a sign of the zodiac; there is also a Savan month, consisting of<BR>thirty risings and settings of the sun; a Nākshatra month, or<BR>month regulated by the lunar asterisms, and a fifth description<BR>of month called Vārhaspatya, depending on the motions of the<BR>planet JUPITER; the lunar month also, being of two kinds, as<BR>reckoned from the new or from the full moon, completes six<BR>different modes of monthly computation.<BR>	 2. A jeweller's weight:<BR>see माष.<BR> E. मास् the moon, aff. अण्; or मस् to measure, (the year<BR>by it,) aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासजात
मासजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) A month old.<BR> E. मास, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासज्ञ|मासज्ञः
मासज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A gallinule.<BR> E. मास a month, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासन|मासनं
मासन n. (-नं) A medicinal seed, (Serratula anthelmintica.) “सोमराज ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासप्रमित|मासप्रमितः
मासप्रमित m. (-तः) New-moon.<BR> E. मास, and प्रमित measured, (by.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासमान|मासमानः
मासमान m. (-नः) A year.<BR> E. मास a month, and मान measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=566-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासर|मासरः
मासर m. (-रः) The scum of boiled-rice.<BR> E. मस् to measure, aff. अरन्,<BR>and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासवर्त्तिका|मासवर्तिका
मासवर्त्तिका f. (-का) A kind of bird.<BR> E. मास a month, वृत् to be, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासान्त|मासांत|मासान्तः
मासान्त m. (-न्तः) Day of new-moon.<BR> E. मास the month, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासिक|मासिकं|मासिकः
मासिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Monthly, relating or belonging to a month.<BR>2. Payable in a month, (a debt, &c.)<BR>	 3. Hired by the month, (a<BR>servant.)<BR>	 4. Lasting for a month.<BR>	 5. Happening or occurring at<BR>the end of a month, what will occur a month hence, &c.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>A particular Śrāddha, or obsequial sacrifice performed every<BR>day of new-moon, during the first year of the death of a man. E.<BR>मास a month, and ठक् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासीन
मासीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Of a month, a month old.<BR> E. मास, and खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासु
मासु (सू) री f. (-री) The beard.<BR> E. मस् to measure, aff. उरन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्म
मास्म Ind. A prohibitive particle.<BR> E. मा prohibitive, and स्म termination<BR>added; or मस्-णिच्-बा० मप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्य
मास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Of or lasting a month, a month old.<BR> E. मास, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माह्
माह् (उ, or ऋ) माहु or माहृ r. 1st cl. (माहति-ते) To mete, to measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहन|माहनः
माहन m. (-नः) A Brāhmana.<BR> E. मा prohibitive prefix, हन् to kill, aff.<BR>अच्, radical letters unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहा
माहा f. (-हा) A cow.<BR> E. मा prohibitive prefix, हन् to kill, affs. ड and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाकुल|माहाकुलः
माहाकुल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Of a respectable family.<BR> E. महाकुल of respect-<BR>able lineage, and अण् aff. of descent; also with खञ् aff., माहा-<BR>कुलीन, or with ख महाकुलीन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाजनिक
माहाजनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Fit for or suitable to great persons, &c.<BR>E. महाजन, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहात्मिक
माहात्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Glorious, majestic.<BR>	 2. Magnanimous.<BR>	 3.<BR>Of great sanctity or honour.<BR> E. महात्मन्, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहात्म्य|माहात्म्यं
माहात्म्य n. (-त्म्यं)<BR>	 1. Majesty, greatness, might.<BR>	 2. The peculiar efficacy<BR>or virtue of any divinity or sacred shrine, &c.<BR>	 3. A work, giving<BR>an account of the merits of any holy place or object.<BR> E. महात्मन्<BR>great, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहानाम्रिक
माहानाम्रिक m. (-कः) A Brāhmana versed in a peculiar portion of the<BR>Vedas.<BR> E. महानाम्नी a portion of the Vedas so called, and ठञ् aff.;<BR>also with the final dropped, माहानामिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाराजिक
माहाराजिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Imperial, royal, fit for a king, &c.<BR> E. महाराज, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिन|माहिनं
माहिन n. (-नं) Kingdom, dominion.<BR> E. महिन the same, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिर|माहिरः
माहिर m. (-रः) A same of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष
माहिष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Belonging to or derived from a buffalo, (flesh,<BR>milk. &c.)<BR> E. महिष, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिषक|माहिषकः
माहिषक m. (-कः) A buffalo-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिषिक|माहिषिकः
माहिषिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A buffalo-keeper.<BR>	 2. The paramour of an un-<BR>chaste women.<BR>	 3. One who lives by the prostitution of his wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष्य|माहिष्यः
माहिष्य m. (-ष्यः) A man of a mixed class, sprung from a Kṣatriya<BR>father and Vaiśya mother.<BR> E. महिष a buffalo, and यत् aff., with<BR>अण् added; attendance on cattle forming with the practice of as-<BR>tronomy and music, are the business of the Māhishya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेन्द्र|माहेंद्र|माहेन्द्रः
माहेन्द्र mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्रा-न्द्रं) Relating to or belonging to INDRA, fit or pro-<BR>per for, (as an oblation to him, &c.)<BR>	 f. (-न्द्री)<BR>	 1. The wife of INDRA.<BR>2. A cow.<BR>	 3. The east.<BR> E. महेन्द्र the deity, and अण् aff.; also with<BR>छ, माहेन्द्रिय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेय|माहेयः
माहेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Earthen, made of or from earth.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Coral.<BR>	 2. The planet Mars.<BR>	 f. (-यी) A cow.<BR> E. मही the earth,<BR>ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेश्वरी
माहेश्वरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. One of the divine mothers or<BR>energies of the gods, the Saktī of ŚIVA.<BR> E. महेश्वर ŚIVA, अण् and<BR>ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मि
मि(डुञ्)डुमिञ् r. 5th cl. (मिनोति मिनुते)<BR>	 1. To cast, to throw, to throw<BR>about, to scatter.<BR>	 2. To measure.<BR>	 3. To perceive. (This root is not<BR>used in classics.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिच्छ्|मिछ्
मिच्छ् r. 6th cl. (मिच्छति)<BR>	 1. To pain, to inflict pain or distress.<BR>	 2. To obstruct, to hinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित|मितः
मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Measured.<BR>	 2. Moderate, limited, few or little.<BR>3. Known, understood.<BR>	 4. Examined.<BR>	 5. Scattered, sprinkled. E.<BR>मा to mete, or मि to scatter, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितङ्गम|मितंगम|मितंगमः|मितङ्गमः
मितङ्गम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Going deliberately or slowly.<BR>	 m. (-मः) An<BR>elephant.<BR>	 f. (-मा) A she-elephant.<BR> E. मित measured, गम् to go,<BR>aff. खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितद्रु|मितद्रुः
मितद्रु m. (-द्रुः) The ocean.<BR> E. मित what is measured, (the earth,) द्रु to go, Unādi aff. कु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितभुज्
मितभुज् mfn. (-भुक्) Moderate, temperate.<BR> E. मित, भुज् who eats. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितम्पच|मितंपच|मितम्पचः
मितम्पच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>	 1. Miserly, niggardly, a niggard, a miser.<BR>	 2.<BR>Cooking little.<BR> E. मित measured, (food,) and पच who cooks, from<BR>पच् with खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितवाच्
मितवाच् mfn. (-वाक्) Prudent in speaking, of measured speech.<BR> E. मित, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितार्थ
मितार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Of certain or restricted meaning.<BR>	 m. (-र्थः) A<BR>cautious emissary.<BR> E. मित, and अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिताशन|मिताशनः
मिताशन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Abstemious, moderate in diet, eating little<BR>and sparingly.<BR> E. मित measured, and अशन who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिताक्षर
मिताक्षर Adj.<BR>	 1. Short, brief.<BR>	 2. Metrical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिति|मितिः
मिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Measuring, measure.<BR>	 2. Weighing, weight.<BR>	 3. Value.<BR>4. Knowledge.<BR>	 5. Proof, evidence.<BR> E. मा to measure, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्र|मित्त्रं|मित्रं|मित्रः
मित्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A friend.<BR>	 2. An ally; in this form it is always neuter;<BR>but it is convertible into an attributive, and is then of three<BR>genders, (मित्रः-मित्रा-मित्रं) Friendly, a friend.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>2. The name of a Vedic deity.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा) One of the wives of DASA-<BR>RAṬHA, the mother of SATRUGHNA.<BR> E. मिद् to be affectionate, aff.<BR>क्त; hence more properly मित्त्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रकार्य्य|मित्रकार्य
मित्रकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) A friendly deed, friendship.<BR> E. मित्र and कार्य्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रत्व|मित्रत्वं
मित्रत्व n. (-त्वं) Friendship, friendliness.<BR> E. मित्र with त्व aff.; also with<BR>तल्, मित्रता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रद्रुह्
मित्रद्रुह् m. (-द्रुक्) A false or treacherous friend.<BR> E. मित्र, and द्रुह् who injures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रद्विष्
मित्रद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) A treacherous friend.<BR> E. मित्र and द्विष् who hates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रभेद|मित्रभेदः
मित्रभेद m. (-दः) Breach of friendship.<BR> E. मित्र and भेद division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रयु|मित्रयुः
मित्रयु mfn. (-युः-युः-यु) Attractive, winning or acquiring friends.<BR>	 m. (-युः)<BR>1. A rememberer or retainer of traditions, a person acquainted<BR>with popular and unrecorded customs.<BR>	 2. A friend.<BR> E. मित्र a friend.<BR>या to obtain, aff. कु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रयुद्ध|मित्रयुद्धं
मित्रयुद्ध n. (-द्धं) The contest of friends, the conflict of allies.<BR> E. मित्र,<BR>and युद्ध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रलब्धि|मित्रलब्धिः
मित्रलब्धि f. (-ब्धिः) Acquirement of friendship.<BR> E. मित्र a friend, and लब्धि acquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रलाभ|मित्रलाभः
मित्रलाभ m. (-भः) Acquirement of a friend or friendship, forming friend-<BR>ship, &c.<BR> E. मित्र a friend, and लाभ gain, acquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रवत्सल|मित्रवत्सलः
मित्रवत्सल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Acquiring friendship, winning, captivating,<BR>engaging, etc.<BR> E. मित्र a friend, and वत्सल kind, affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रशीस्
मित्रशीस् m. (-शीः) A ruler over his friends or allies.<BR> E. मित्र, and शास्<BR>to govern, क्विप् aff., and ई substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रीयत्
मित्रीयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Becoming or acting as a friend, desiring<BR>friendship.<BR> E. मित्र nominal verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रोदय|मित्रोदयः
मित्रोदय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Sunrise.<BR>	 2. The prosperity of a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्
मिथ्(ऋ)मिथृ r. 1st cl. (मिथति-ते)<BR>	 1. To understand.<BR>	 2. To injure, to<BR>hurt.<BR>	 3. To unite, to pair.<BR>	 4. To wrangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथस्
मिथस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Mutually, reciprocally.<BR>	 2. Privately.<BR> E. मिथ् to pair, aff.<BR>असुन् and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथिला
मिथिला f. (-ला) A city, giving name also to a kingdom, lying north-<BR>east of Bengal, the modern Tirhut.<BR> E. मिथ् to be agitated, (ene-<BR>mies by that kingdom,) and ईलच् Uṇadi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुन|मिथुनं|मिथुनः
मिथुन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A couple, a pair, a brace, male and female.<BR>	 2. Copu-<BR>lation.<BR>	 3. Union, junction.<BR>	 4. Twins.<BR>	 5. A root compounded with<BR>a preposition, (in gram.)<BR>	 m. (-नः) The sign Gemini of the<BR>zodiac.<BR> E. मिथ् to unite, उनन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनीभाव|मिथुनीभावः
मिथुनीभाव m. (-वः) Amorous inclination.<BR> E. मिथुन, भाव property, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनेचर|मिथुनेचरः
मिथुनेचर m. (-रः) The ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=567-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्या
मिथ्या Ind.<BR>	 1. Falsely, untruly.<BR>	 2. In vain.<BR> E. मिथ् to injure, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याचरत्
मिथ्याचरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रन्) Acting or practising falsehood.<BR> E. मिथ्या<BR>and आचरत् observing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याचार|मिथ्याचारः
मिथ्याचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Acting, falsely.<BR> E. मिथ्या and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याज्ञान
मिथ्याज्ञान n. (-नं) Error, misapprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यादृष्टि|मिथ्यादृष्टिः
मिथ्यादृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Denial of future existence, atheism, heresy.<BR> E. मिथ्या<BR>falsely, and दृष्टि vision, knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याध्यवसिति|मिथ्याध्यवसितिः
मिथ्याध्यवसिति f. (-तिः) A figure of rhetoric, confirmation of one error<BR>or impossibility by another.<BR> E. मिथ्या falsehood, अध्यवसिति perse-<BR>verance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याप्रतिज्ञ
मिथ्याप्रतिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Treacherous, guilty of a breach of pro-<BR>mise.<BR> E. मिथ्या and प्रतिज्ञा promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याप्रसुप्त
मिथ्याप्रसुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Pretendedly asleep, but not so in reality. E.<BR>मिथ्या and प्रसुप्त asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याफल
मिथ्याफल n. (-लं) An imaginary advantage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याभियोग|मिथ्याभियोगः
मिथ्याभियोग m. (-गः) Groundless plaint or demand.<BR> E. मिथ्या falsely,<BR>अभियोग plaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याभिशंसन|मिथ्याभिशंसनं
मिथ्याभिशंसन n. (-नं) A false accusation.<BR> E. मिथ्या falsely, अभिशंसन accusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याभिशंसिन्
मिथ्याभिशंसिन् m. (-सी) A false or unjust accuser.<BR> E. मिथ्या falsely, अभि-<BR>शंसिन् who accuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यामति|मिथ्यामतिः
मिथ्यामति f. (-तिः) Error, ignorance, mistake.<BR> E. मिथ्या falsely, and मति understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावदत्
मिथ्यावदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्दी-दत्) Speaking, falsely.<BR> E. मिथ्या, वदत् speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावादिन्
मिथ्यावादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Lying, a liar.<BR> E. मिथ्या and वादिन् who<BR>speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्योत्तर|मिथ्योत्तरं
मिथ्योत्तर n. (-रं) A false or prevaricating reply.<BR> E. मिथ्या, उत्तर answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्योपचार|मिथ्योपचारः
मिथ्योपचार m. (-रः) Pretended friendly services.<BR> E. मिथ्या and उपचार<BR>assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिद्
मिद् r. 1st cl. (मेदति)<BR>	 1. To be proud.<BR>	 2. To be humble. r. 10th cl.<BR>(मेदयति-ते) (इ) मिदि r. 1st and 10th cls. (मिन्दति मिन्दयति) also (ञि, आ)<BR>ञिमिदा r. 1st cl. (मेदते) r. 4th cl. (मेद्यति)<BR>	 1. To be unctuous, to be<BR>oily or greasy.<BR>	 2. To liquefy, to melt.<BR>	 3. To annoint.<BR>	 4. To have<BR>affection or regard for.<BR>	 5. To be soft, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>(ऋ) मिदृ r. 1st cl. (मेदति-ते)<BR>	 1. To understand.<BR>	 2. To hurt, to<BR>injure.<BR>	 3. To unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिद्ध|मिद्धं
मिद्ध n. (-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Sloth, indolence.<BR>	 2. Sleepiness, torpor.<BR>	 3. Dulness,<BR>heaviness of spirits or intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्व्
मिन्व् r. 1st cl. (मिन्वति)<BR>	 1. To moisten.<BR>	 2. To revere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमङ्क्षा|मिमंक्षा
मिमङ्क्षा f. (-ङ्क्षा) Wishing to bathe or plunge into.<BR> E. मस्ज् to bathe,<BR>desid. v., अङ् and ठाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमङ्क्षु
मिमङ्क्षु mfn. (-ङ्क्षुः-ङ्क्षुः-ङ्क्षु) Wishing to bathe, to plunge into, to be<BR>immersed in.<BR> E. मस्ज् to bathe, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमन्थिषा
मिमन्थिषा f. (-षा) Desire or purpose to destroy.<BR> E. मथि to shake, desid.<BR>v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमन्थिषु
मिमन्थिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to destroy, shake, overturn, &c. E.<BR>मथ् to injure, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिल्
मिल् r. 6th cl. (मिलति or मिलति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be connected or united with,<BR>to mix, to associate.<BR>	 2. To clash.<BR>	 3. To happen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलन|मिलनं
मिलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Mixing with, being in contact with, associating with,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Encountering, meeting.<BR>	 3. Contact.<BR> E. मिल् to mix, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलित|मिलितः
मिलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Mixed, united, combined, or connected with,<BR>2. Found, met with, encountered.<BR> E. मिल् to mix, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिव
मिव (इ) मिवि r. 1st cl. (मिन्वति)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle or moisten.<BR>	 2. (According<BR>to some authorities,) To serve, to gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्
मिश् r. 1st cl. (मेशति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिशि|मिशिः
मिशि f. (-शिः-शी)<BR>	 1. A sort of fennel, (Anethum panmorium.)<BR>	 2. Indian<BR>spikenard.<BR>	 3. Common anise.<BR> E. मिश् to sound, कि aff. and ङीष्<BR>optionally added; also मिषि मिसि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्र्
मिश्र् r. 10th cl. (मिश्रयति-ते) To mix, to join, to blend, to combine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्र|मिश्रं|मिश्रः
मिश्र mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं) Mixed, mingled, blended.<BR>	 n. (-श्रं) Mixing, mix-<BR>ture.<BR>	 m. (-श्रः)<BR>	 1. An elephant, the fourth of the four classes in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">Page568-b+ 60</a>]<BR>which elephants are arranged.<BR>	 2. A respectable person; in which<BR>sense it is a common affix to proper names; or compounded with<BR>आर्य्य, as आर्य्यमिश्राः &c.<BR> E. मिश्र् to mix, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रक|मिश्रकं|मिश्रकः
मिश्रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An adulterator of commodities, &c.<BR>	 2. A mixer, a<BR>compounder.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A garden of the gods, a grove of paradise.<BR>2. A description of song or singing.<BR>	 3. A kind of salt.<BR> E. मिश्र<BR>mingled, (flowers, &c.) and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रकावण|मिश्रकावणं
मिश्रकावण n. (-णं) The grove of INDRA.<BR> E. मिश्रका for मिश्रक a divine<BR>garden, and वन a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रज|मिश्रजः
मिश्रज m. (-जः) A mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रण|मिश्रणं
मिश्रण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Mixing, uniting.<BR>	 2. (In arithmetic,) Addition.<BR> E. मिश्र to mix, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रवर्ण|मिश्रवर्णं
मिश्रवर्ण n. (-र्णं) A black kind of aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रित|मिश्रितं
मिश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Respected, respectable.<BR>	 2. Mixed, mingled.<BR>3. Added.<BR> E. मिश्र् to mix, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रेया
मिश्रेया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. A sort of fennel, (Anethum panmorium, Rox.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Another kind, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>	 3. Common anise, (Pimpinella<BR>anisum.)<BR> E. मिश्र mixture, इड् to go or get, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्
मिष् (उ) मिषु r. 1st cl. (मेषति) To sprinkle. r. 6th cl. (मिषति)<BR>	 1. To con-<BR>tend with, to emulate, to contest.<BR>	 2. To look at or on. With उद्<BR>1. To open the eyes.<BR>	 2. To blossom.<BR>	 3. To shine. With नि To shut<BR>the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष|मिषं|मिषः
मिष m. (-षः) Rivalry, emulation.<BR>	 n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Fraud, trick, decep-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. Envy.<BR> E. मिष् to vie, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिषि|मिषिः
मिषि f. (-षिः-षी)<BR>	 1. Spikenard, (Valeriana jatāmānsi.)<BR>	 2. A sort of fen-<BR>nel, (Anethum panmorium, &c.)<BR> E. मस् to measure, इन् and ङीष्<BR>affs., स changed to ष, and इ substituted for the radical vowel;<BR>also मिसि, मिशि, and with कन् added मिषिका, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्ट|मिष्टं|मिष्टः
मिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkled, wetted.<BR>	 2. Sweet, sugary.<BR>	 3. Dainty,<BR>savoury.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) A sweetmeat.<BR> E. मिष् to sprinkle, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्टकर्त्तृ|मिष्टकर्तृ
मिष्टकर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) A confectioner, a good cook.<BR> E. मिष्ट and कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्टान्न|मिष्टान्नं
मिष्टान्न n. (-न्नं) Sauce, gravy seasoning, a mixture of sugar and acids,<BR>&c. eaten with bread or rice.<BR> E. मिष्ट sprinkled, अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिसि|मिसिः
मिसि f. (-सिः-सी)<BR>	 1. A sort of fennel, (Anethum panmorium, Rox.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Another kind, (A. sowa.)<BR>	 3. Spikenard, (Valeriana jatāmānsi.)<BR>4. A sort of lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR>	 5. Common anise, (Pim-<BR>pinella an sum.)<BR> E. मस् to mete, aff. इन् and optionally ङीष्; the<BR>radical vowel changed to इ, deriv. irr.; also मिशि and मिषि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिस्र्
मिस्र् r. 10th cl. (मिस्रयति) To mix, to mingle or join.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिह्
मिह् (औ) मिहौ r. 1st cl. (मेहति)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle, to shed.<BR>	 2. To emit seminal water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिका
मिहिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Frost.<BR>	 2. Snow.<BR> E. मिह् to sprinkle, aff. क्वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिर|मिहिरः
मिहिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A sage.<BR>	 3. A cloud.<BR>	 4. Air, wind.<BR>	 5.<BR>The moon.<BR>	 6. An old man.<BR> E. मिह् to sprinkle or scatter, (radi-<BR>ance, &c.) Unādi aff. किरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिराण|मिहिराणः
मिहिराण m. (-णः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. मिहिर the sun, अन् to live, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मी
मी r. 1st and 10th cls. (मयति माययति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To<BR>know. (टु, ङ्) टुमीङ् r.<BR>	 4. cl. (मीयते) To part with life, to die. (ञ)<BR>मीञ् r. 9th cl. (मीनाति मीनीते)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR>	 2. To<BR>violate.<BR>	 3. To diminish.<BR>	 4. To go astray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढ|मीढं|मीढः
मीढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Passed as urine.<BR> E. मिह् to sprinkle, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढुष्टम|मीढुष्टमः
मीढुष्टम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीन|मीनः
मीन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A fish 2. The sign of the Zodiac Pisces.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU<BR>in his first incarnation.<BR> E. मी to hurt, Unādi aff. नक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनकेतन|मीनकेतनः
मीनकेतन m. (-नः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. मीन a fish, and केतन a symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनगोधिका
मीनगोधिका f. (-का) A pond, a pool.<BR> E. मीन a fish, and गोधिका a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनरङ्ग|मीनरंग|मीनरङ्गः
मीनरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A king-fisher.<BR> E. मीन fish, रञ्ज् to annoy, aff. अच्; it is<BR>also written but perhaps incorrectly मीनरङ्क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनर|मीनरः
मीनर m. (-रः) A marine monster, sometimes applied to the shark and<BR>alligator: see मकर.<BR> E. मीन a fish, रा to seize, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाक्षी
मीनाक्षी f. (-क्षी) The daughter of KUVERA.<BR> E. मीन a fish, and अक्षि the<BR>eye, टच् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=568-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाघातिन्
मीनाघातिन् m. (-ती)<BR>	 1. A crane.<BR>	 2. A fisherman.<BR> E. मीन fish and<BR>आघातिन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाण्ड|मीनांड
मीनाण्ड n. (-ण्डं) Fish-spawn, roe, milt.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डी) Clayed or candied<BR>sugar.<BR> E. मीन a fish, and अण्ड egg, spawn, ङीष् aff., to which the<BR>last is compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाम्रीण|मीनाम्रीणः
मीनाम्रीण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A wagtail.<BR>	 2. A sort of sauce, fish-sauce.<BR> E. मीन<BR>fish, आम्र the mango, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनालय|मीनालयः
मीनालय m. (-यः) The ocean.<BR> E. मीन a fish, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीम्
मीम् (ऋ) मीमृ r. 1st. cl. (मीमति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसक|मीमांसकः
मीमांसक m. (-कः) A Mīmānsaka, a follower of the Mīmānsā phi loso-<BR>phy.<BR>	 2. An examiner.<BR> E. मीमांसा the doctrine so termed, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसा
मीमांसा f. (-सा) One of the philosophical systems of the Hindus, or<BR>rather a two-fold system, the two parts of which form two of the<BR>six Darśhanas or schools of philosophy; the first part, the Pūrva<BR>Mīmānsā, or Mīmānś simply, originates with the Muni JAIMINĪ,<BR>and illustrates the Karma-kāṇḍa of the Vedas or the practical<BR>part, (the ritual,) of religion and devotion, including also moral<BR>and legal obligations. The second part, or Uttara Mīmāṃsā,<BR>ascribed to VYĀSA, is the same as the Vedānta, founded on<BR>the Jnāna-kāṇḍa, or theological portion of the Vedas, and<BR>treating of the spiritual worship of the Supreme Being or soul<BR>of the universe.<BR> E. मान् to seek knowledge, affs. अङ् and टाप्; the<BR>derivative takes the augment of the reduplicate form of the verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीर|मीरः
मीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A limit, a boundary.<BR> E. मी to scatter,<BR>रक् Unādi aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मील्
मील् r. 1st cl. (मीलति)<BR>	 1. To wink or twinkle, to close or contract<BR>the eyelids.<BR>	 2. To fade, to disappear: with उत् prefixed, to<BR>awake, and figuratively to expand, to bud, to blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलत्
मीलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्) Winking, twinkling, closing, (as the eyes.)<BR>E. मील् to wink, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलन|मीलनं
मीलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Twinkling, blinking, winking.<BR>	 2. Closing the eyes.<BR>	 3.<BR>The closing of a flower.<BR> E. मील् to twinkle, &c. aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलित|मीलितं
मीलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Twinkled.<BR>	 2. Unblown, partly opened, as a<BR>young bud, &c.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Indirect allusion or description, (in rhe-<BR>toric.)<BR> E. मील् to twinkle, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीव्
मीव् r. 1st cl. (मीवति)<BR>	 1. To be large or corpulent.<BR>	 2. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवन्
मीवन् m. (-वा) Air, wind.<BR> E. मी to move, वन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवर|मीवरः
मीवर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Mischievous, hurting, killing.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The leader<BR>of an army.<BR> E. मी to hurt or kill, ष्वरच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवा
मीवा f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. The worm of the intestines, Ascarides, &c.<BR>	 2. Air,<BR>wind.<BR> E. मी to hurt, Unādi aff. वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मु|मुः
मु m. (-मुः)<BR>	 1. Binding, confinement.<BR>	 2. Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>	 3. ŚIVA.<BR>4. Eternal beatitude or final emancipation.<BR>	 5. A funeral pile. E.<BR>मू to bind, aff. क्विप्; or मुच् to loosen, &c., aff. डु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकन्दक|मुकंदक|मुकंदकः|मुकन्दकः
मुकन्दक m. (-कः) The onion; also मुकुन्दक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकु|मुकुः
मुकु f. (-कुः) Freedom, liberation.<BR> E. मुच् to let loose, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुट|मुकुटं
मुकुट n. (-टं) A crest, a diadem, a tiara.<BR>	 f. (-टी) Snapping the fingers.<BR>E. मकि to adorn, aff. उट, and उ substituted for the radical vowel,<BR>form irr.; also मकुट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्द|मुकुंद|मुकुंदः|मुकुन्दः
मुकुन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. Gum olibanum.<BR>	 3. A preci-<BR>ous gem.<BR>	 4. Quicksilver.<BR>	 5. One of the nine treasures of KUVE-<BR>RA.<BR>	 6. A kind of drum.<BR> E. मुकु liberation, (from passion, &c.) in<BR>the second case मुकुं and दा to give, aff. क; or मुच् to liberate, or<BR>मुकु as before, उन्द to wet, to sprinkle, aff. अच्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्दक|मुकुंदकः|मुकुन्दकः
मुकुन्दक m. (-कः) An onion; also मुकन्दक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्दु|मुकुन्दुः
मुकुन्दु m. (-न्दुः) Gum olibanum; also मुकुन्द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुर|मुकुरः
मुकुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A mirror.<BR>	 2. The handle of a potter's lathe.<BR>	 3. A tree,<BR>(Mimusops elengi.)<BR>	 4. A bud.<BR>	 5. Arabian jasmine.<BR> E. मक् to adorn,<BR>उरच् Unādi aff., and उ optionally substituted for the radical<BR>vowel, deriv. irr.; also मकुर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुल|मुकुलं|मुकुलः
मुकुल mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. An opening bud.<BR>	 2. The body.<BR>	 3. The soul or<BR>spirit.<BR> E. मुच् to let loose, (the flower, &c.) उलच् aff., च changed<BR>to क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलित
मुकुलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Half-closed, (as a bud.)<BR>	 2. Half-shut, (as the<BR>eye,) blinking, winking.<BR> E. मुकुल, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलीकृत
मुकुलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Closed, shut, (as a bud.)<BR> E. मुकुल and कृत<BR>made, with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुष्टक|मुकुष्टकः
मुकुष्टक n. (-कं) A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus lobatus.) Also मकुष्टक, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकूलक|मुकूलकः
मुकूलक m. (-कः) A plant, commonly Dantī, (Croton polyandrum.) E.<BR>मकि to adorn, ऊलच् aff., कन् added, and उ substituted for the<BR>radical vowel, deriv. irr.; also मकूलक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्त|मुक्तः
मुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Released, liberated, loosed, let go.<BR>	 2. Liber-<BR>ated from corporeal existence, finally happy.<BR>	 3. Discharged, loosed,<BR>as a weapon; this may be in two ways, as पाणिमुक्त thrown with<BR>the hand, as a dart, etc., and यन्त्रमुक्त thrown from an instrument,<BR>as an arrow from a bow, etc.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं) The spirit released from<BR>mundane existence, and re-integrated with its divine original.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-क्ता)<BR>	 1. A pearl.<BR>	 2. A harlot.<BR> E. मुच् to set free, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तक|मुक्तकं
मुक्तक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Any missile weapon.<BR>	 2. A stanza or sentence com-<BR>pleting the sense of a passage.<BR>	 3. Simple prose.<BR> E. मुक्त loosed,<BR>let fly, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकच्छ|मुक्तकच्छः
मुक्तकच्छ m. (-च्छः) A Buddhist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकञ्चुक|मुक्तकंचुक|मुक्तकञ्चुकः
मुक्तकञ्चुक m. (-कः) A snake that has cast his slough.<BR> E. मुक्त let loose, कञ्चुक the slough of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकण्ठम्
मुक्तकण्ठम् Ind. Aloud, as shouting or crying.<BR> E. मुक्त and कण्ठ throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तचक्षुस्
मुक्तचक्षुस् m. (-क्षुः) A lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तसङ्ग|मुक्तसंग|मुक्तसंगः
मुक्तसङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Disinterested, free from worldly attachment<BR>or improper bias.<BR> E. मुक्त and सङ्ग attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तहस्त
मुक्तहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Parting with, giving away, liberal.<BR>	 2.<BR>Loosed, let go.<BR> E. मुक्त and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताकलाप|मुक्ताकलापः
मुक्ताकलाप m. (-पः) A pearl-necklace, a string of pearls.<BR> E. मुक्ता a pearl,<BR>and कलाप a sort of chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तागार|मुक्तागारं|मुक्तागारः
मुक्तागार n. (-रं) The pearl-oyster.<BR> E. मुक्त a pearl, and आगार abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताप्रलम्ब
मुक्ताप्रलम्ब m. (-म्बः) A pearl-necklace.<BR> E. मुक्ता a pearl, and प्रलम्ब string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताप्रसू
मुक्ताप्रसू f. (-सूः) The pearl-oyster.<BR> E. मुक्ता a pearl, and प्रसू mother, mo-<BR>ther of pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताफल|मुक्ताफलं
मुक्ताफल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Camphor.<BR>	 2. A pearl.<BR>	 3. A sort of fruit, the custard-<BR>apple. “नोयाड”<BR> E. मुक्ता a pearl, फल fruit, comparable to a pearl<BR>in whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तामुक्त|मुक्तामुक्तः
मुक्तामुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Loosed, and not loosed; applied especially<BR>to weapons which may be wielded or hurled, as a club, a javelin,<BR>etc.<BR> E. मुक्त loosed, अमुक्त not loosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तालता
मुक्तालता f. (-ता) A pearl-necklace.<BR> E. मुक्ता a pearl, and लता a creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तावली
मुक्तावली f. (-ली) A pearl-necklace.<BR> E. मुक्ता a pearl, आवली a line, a row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तास्फोट|मुक्तास्फोटः
मुक्तास्फोट mf. (-टः-टा) A pearl-oyster.<BR> E. मुक्ता, स्फुट to burst, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ति|मुक्तिः
मुक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Final beatitude, the delivery of the soul from the<BR>body and exemption from further transmigration; the re-absorp-<BR>tion of the emancipated spirit into its great primary source,<BR>identification with GOD.<BR>	 2. Liberation, setting or becoming free or<BR>loose.<BR> E. मुच् to let loose, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्त्वा
मुक्त्वा Ind. Having set free, loose, etc.<BR> E. मुच् to free, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख|मुखं|मुखः
मुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>	 1. First, initial.<BR>	 2. Chief, pre-eminent, principal.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. The mouth.<BR>	 2. The face.<BR>	 3. The entrance to a house.<BR>4. Commencement.<BR>	 5. A means, an expedient.<BR>	 6. Sound.<BR>	 7. The<BR>opening division of a drama, the first act, &c.<BR>	 8. The previous<BR>or preparatory incidents of a drama.<BR>	 9. A direction, a quarter.<BR>10. Opening, entrance.<BR>	 11. The head, the top, the tip.<BR>	 12. The<BR>edge of any sharp instrument.<BR>	 13. Utterance.<BR>	 14. Source, cause,<BR>occasion.<BR>	 15. The Vedas, scripture.<BR>	 m. (-खः) The beak of a bird.<BR>E. खन् to dig, Unādi aff. अच् with the power of ड, by which the<BR>final is rejected, मुट initial augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=569-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखकमल
मुखकमल n. (-लं) A lotus-like face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखखुर|मुखखुरः
मुखखुर m. (-रः) A tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखगन्धक|मुखगंधक|मुखगन्धकः
मुखगन्धक m. (-कः) An onion.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, and गन्धक scenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखघण्टा
मुखघण्टा f. (-ण्टा) Howling, uttering, a particular cry of grief, etc. E.<BR>मुख the mouth, and घण्टा a bell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखचपल
मुखचपल Adj. Talkative f. (-ला) A species of the Āryā metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखचीरी
मुखचीरी f. (-री) The tongue.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, and चीरी the cry or<BR>chirp of the cricket, or a cricket; also मुखचीरि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखज|मुखजः
मुखज mfn. (-जः-जा-ज) Derived or proceeding from the mouth, born<BR>in the mouth, etc.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A Brāhmana, (born from the mouth<BR>of BRAHMĀ.)<BR>	 2. A tooth.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखतस्
मुखतस् Ind. From the mouth.<BR> E. मुख, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखतीय|मुखतीयं
मुखतीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating or pertaining to the mouth.<BR> E. मुखतस्<BR>as above, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखदूषण|मुखदूषणः
मुखदूषण m. (-णः) The onion.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, and दूषण fouling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखधौता
मुखधौता f. (-ता) A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.) “वामनहाटि ।”<BR> E. मुख<BR>the mouth, धौत cleansed, (by it.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखनिरीक्षक|मुखनिरीक्षकः
मुखनिरीक्षक m. (-कः) An idler, a lazy man.<BR> E. मुख the face, निरीक्षक contemplating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखनिवासिनी
मुखनिवासिनी f. (-नी) The goddess SARASWATĪ.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, and<BR>निवासिनी abiding; as the goddess of speech, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखपट|मुखपटः
मुखपट m. (-टः) A veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखपिण्ड|मुखपिंड|मुखपिण्डः
मुखपिण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A mouthful of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखपूरण|मुखपूरणं
मुखपूरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A mouthful of water for rinsing the mouth.<BR>	 2. A<BR>mouthful.<BR>	 3. Filling the mouth.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, पूरण filling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखप्रिय|मुखप्रियः
मुखप्रिय m. (-यः) An orange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखबन्धन|मुखबंधन
मुखबन्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A preface.<BR>	 2. A lid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखभूषण|मुखभूषणं
मुखभूषण n. (-णं) Betel, the leaf of the piper-betel eaten with the Areca<BR>nut, catechu and caustic lime, &c.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, भूषण an<BR>ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखभेद|मुखभेदः
मुखभेद m. (-दः) Distortion of the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखम्प्रच
मुखम्प्रच m. (-चः) A beggar, a petitioner.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, पच who<BR>ripens, (his purpose,) from पच् with खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखयन्त्रण|मुखयंत्रण|मुखयन्त्रणं
मुखयन्त्रण n. (-णं) The bit of a bridle.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, यन्त्रण restraining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखर|मुखरः
मुखर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Foul-mouthed, speaking harshly or scurrilous-<BR>ly.<BR>	 2. Sounding, noisy.<BR>	 3. Speaking in ridicule of, rallying, mock-<BR>ing, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A ring-leader.<BR>	 2. A conch-shell.<BR>	 3. Leading,<BR>preceding.<BR>	 4. A crow.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, र aff., implying deprecia-<BR>tion, or रा to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखरिका
मुखरिका f. (-का) The bit of a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखरित
मुखरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounding, ringing, making a noise.<BR> E. मुखर and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखरीकरण
मुखरीकरण n. (-णं) Rallying, mocking.<BR> E. मुखर, करण making, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखलाङ्गल|मुखलांगल|मुखलाङ्गलः
मुखलाङ्गल m. (-लः) A hog.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, and लाङ्गल a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखलेप|मुखलेपः
मुखलेप m. (-पः) A disease of the phlegmatic humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखवल्लभ|मुखवल्लभः
मुखवल्लभ m. (-भः) A pomegranate tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखवाद्य|मुखवाद्यं
मुखवाद्य n. (-द्यं)<BR>	 1. A musical instrument played with the mouth, a<BR>jew's harp.<BR>	 2. Making a noise with the mouth by strinking it<BR>with the hand, playing on the mouth.<BR> E. मुख the mouth and वाद्य<BR>a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखवासन|मुखवासनः
मुखवासन m. (-नः) A perfume for the mouth, any drug, as camphor or<BR>orris-root so used, or a composition usually taken in the form of<BR>a pill.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, and वासन perfuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखविलुण्ठिका|मुखविलुंठिका
मुखविलुण्ठिका f. (-का) A she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखविष्ठा
मुखविष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा) A cockroach.<BR> E. मुख the mouth and विष्ठा fæces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखव्यादान|मुखव्यादानं
मुखव्यादान n. (-नं) Opening the mouth wide.<BR> E. मुख with वि and आङ्<BR>prefixed to दा to give, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखशफ|मुखशफः
मुखशफ mfn. (-फः-फा-फं) Foul-mouthed, scurrilous.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, शफ a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखशेष|मुखशेषः
मुखशेष m. (-षः) An epithet of RĀHU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखशोधन|मुखशोधनं|मुखशोधनः
मुखशोधन m. (-नः) Pungency, sharp or pungent flavour.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Clean-<BR>ing the mouth.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, शोधन cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखशोधिन्
मुखशोधिन् m. (-धी) The lime or citron.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, शोधिन् what cleanses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखष्ठील|मुखष्ठीलः
मुखष्ठील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Foul-mouthed, scurrilous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखसम्भव|मुखसंभव|मुखसंभवः|मुखसम्भवः
मुखसम्भव m. (-वः) A Brāhmana.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, (of BRAHMĀ,) सम्मव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखसुर|मुखसुरं
मुखसुर n. (-रं) The moisture of the lips.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, and सुरा<BR>spirituous liquor, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखस्राव|मुखस्रावः
मुखस्राव m. (-वः) Spittle, saliva.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, स्रु to drop, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखाग्नि|मुखाग्निः
मुखाग्नि m. (-ग्निः)<BR>	 1. The conflagration of a forest.<BR>	 2. A sort of goblin<BR>with a face of fire.<BR>	 3. Fire put into the mouth of the corpse at<BR>the time of lighting the funeral pile.<BR>	 4. A sacrificial or consecra-<BR>ted fire.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, face, or chief, principal, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखास्त्र|मुखास्त्रः
मुखास्त्र m. (-स्त्रः) A crab.<BR> E. मुख the mouth, and अस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुखोल्का
मुखोल्का f. (-ल्का) Fire in a forest.<BR> E. मुख face or mouth, उल्का flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख्य|मुख्यः
मुख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं)<BR>	 1. Chief, primary, principal.<BR>	 2. Relating to the<BR>face or mouth.<BR>	 n. (-ख्यं)<BR>	 1. A principal or essential rite or ordi-<BR>nance.<BR>	 2. Reading or teaching the Vedas.<BR>	 3. The month when<BR>reckoned from new moon to new moon.<BR>	 m. (-ख्यः) A leader. E.<BR>मुख chief, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख्यता
मुख्यता f. (-ता) Pre-eminence, being best or chief.<BR> E. मुख्य, तल् aff. also with त्व, मुख्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुख्यशस्
मुख्यशस् Ind. Principally, particularly.<BR> E. मुख्य and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुगूह|मुगूहः
मुगूह m. (-हः) A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुग्ध|मुग्धः
मुग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Lovely, beautiful.<BR>	 2. Stupid, ignorant, an<BR>idiot, a fool.<BR>	 3. Simple, silly.<BR>	 4. Infatuated.<BR>	 f. (-ग्धा) A young and<BR>lovely female.<BR> E. मुह् to be foolish, aff. क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुग्धता
मुग्धता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Loveliness.<BR>	 2. Ignorance, stupidity.<BR>	 3. Simplicity. E.<BR>मुग्ध and तल् added; also मुग्धत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुग्धा
मुग्धा f. (-ग्धा) A girl attractive by her artlessness, (in rhetoric.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुग्धानन
मुग्धानन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Lovely-faced.<BR> E. मुग्ध and आनन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुच्
मुच् (ऌ, औ) औ मुचॢ r. 6th cl. (मुञ्चति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be loose or free.<BR>	 2. To<BR>forsake or abandon. r. 10th cl. (मोचयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To let loose, to let go,<BR>to discharge as arrows, to part with, as wealth, &c.<BR>	 2. To gladden,<BR>to delight. r. 1st cl. (मोचते) To deceive, to cheat. (इ) मुचि (मुञ्चते)<BR>1. To be vain or proud.<BR>	 2. To be wicked.<BR>	 3. To speak.<BR>	 4. To grind<BR>or pound.<BR>	 5. To cheat, to deceive. With प्र To give much. With वि<BR>1. To obtain liberation.<BR>	 2. To give or bestow.<BR>	 3. To lose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचक|मुचकः
मुचक m. (-कः) Lac, the dye.<BR> E. मुच् to loosen, aff. क्कुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचिर|मुचिरः
मुचिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Munificent, generous, liberal in giving, a donor,<BR>a giver.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A deity.<BR>	 2. Wind.<BR>	 3. Virtue.<BR> E. मुच् to let<BR>loose, to part with wealth, and किरच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचु
मुचु(च)कुन्द m. (-न्दः) A tree, (Pterospermum salicifolium.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुचुटी
मुचुटी f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. Snapping the fingers.<BR>	 2. The fist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुज्
मुज् r. 1st cl. (मोजति मोजयति-ते) also (इ) मुजि (मुञ्जति मुञ्जयति-ते) 1. To<BR>sound.<BR>	 2. To cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्च्|मुंच्
मुञ्च् r. 1st cl. (मुञ्चति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्चक|मुञ्चकः
मुञ्चक m. (-कः) The testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्चत्
मुञ्चत् mfn. (-ञ्चन्-ञ्चन्ती-ञ्चत्)<BR>	 1. Letting go or loose.<BR>	 2. Shooting, discharging.<BR> E. मुच् to let go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्ज|मुंज|मुंजः|मुञ्जः
मुञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>	 1. A sort of grass, from the fibres of which a string is<BR>prepared, of which the triple thread worn by the Brāhmana as a<BR>girdle should be formed, (Saccharum munja, Rox.)<BR>	 2. The Brāh-<BR>minical girdle, or in common use, the sacred string or cord.<BR>	 3.<BR>An arrow.<BR> E. मुजि to sound, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जकेश|मुंजकेश|मुञ्जकेशः
मुञ्जकेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR> E. मुञ्ज a sort of grass, and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जकेशिन्|मुंजकेशिन्
मुञ्जकेशिन् m. (-शी) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. मुञ्ज the plant, केश hair, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जबन्धन|मुंजबंधन
मुञ्जबन्धन n. (-नं) Investiture with the girdle or with the Brāhminical<BR>cord.<BR> E. मुञ्ज and बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जर|मुंजर|मुंजरं|मुञ्जरं
मुञ्जर n. (-रं) The fibrous root of the lotus.<BR> E. मुञ्ज a sort of grass, रा to<BR>go or resemble, aff. क; or मुजि-अरन् । “शालुके ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुञ्जातक|मुञ्जातकः
मुञ्जातक m. (-कः) Munja grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुट्
मुट् r. 1st cl. (मोटति) 6th cl. (मुटति) and 10th cl. (मोटयति-ते); also (इ)<BR>मुटि r. 1st cl. (मुण्टति)<BR>	 1. To rub, to press, to grind or pound, to<BR>reduce to powder.<BR>	 2. To break down, to trample on. r. 6th cl.<BR>(मुटति) To reprove, to rebuke, to blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=570-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुठ्
मुठ् (इ) मुठि r. 1st cl. (मुण्ठते)<BR>	 1. To guard, to protect, to defend or<BR>cherish.<BR>	 2. To fly, to run away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुड्
मुड् r. 6th cl. (मुडति)<BR>	 1. To quit, to leave.<BR>	 2. To clothe or cover. (इ,)<BR>मुडि r. 1st cl. (मुण्डते)<BR>	 1. To be pure or clean.<BR>	 2. To cleanse.<BR>	 3. To<BR>sink, (as in water.)<BR>	 4. To sink, (in estimation.) to be despised<BR>or disregarded. (मुण्डति)<BR>	 1. To shave or cut.<BR>	 2. To grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्
मुण् r. 6th cl. (मुणति) To vow or promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्ड|मुंड|मुण्डं|मुण्डः
मुण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Shaved, bald, having no hair on the head.<BR>2. Low, mean.<BR>	 mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. The head.<BR>	 2. The forehead.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A bald pate.<BR>	 2. A barber.<BR>	 3. The name of a Daitya or<BR>Demon.<BR>	 4. RĀHU, the personified ascending node.<BR>	 5. The trunk<BR>of a lopped tree.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा) Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR> E. मुडि<BR>to shave or cut, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डक|मुंडक|मुण्डकं|मुंडकः|मुण्डकः
मुण्डक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A barber.<BR>	 2. The trunk of a tree stripped of its<BR>branches.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The head.<BR> E. मुडि to shave, aff. वुन्; or मुण्ड the<BR>head, कन् pleonasm; or मुडि-णिच् ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डचणक|मुण्डचणकः
मुण्डचणक m. (-कः) A kind of pulse. “कलाये ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डन|मुंडन|मुंडनं|मुण्डनं
मुण्डन n. (-नं) Shaving, shearing, cutting.<BR> E. मुडि to shave or cut, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डफल|मुंडफल|मुण्डफलः
मुण्डफल m. (-लः) The cocoanut-tree.<BR> E. मुण्ड the head, and फल fruit;<BR>the fruit being one step towards a human head, made by VIŚ-<BR>WĀMITRA, when he purposed establishing an opposition creation<BR>to that of BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डमण्डली
मुण्डमण्डली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A number of shaven heads.<BR>	 2. A mass of troops<BR>of an inferior description.<BR> E. मुण्ड and मण्डली a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डशालि|मुंडशालि|मुण्डशालिः
मुण्डशालि m. (-लिः) A kind of grain or rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डित|मुंडित|मुण्डितं
मुण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bald, shaven.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Iron.<BR> E. मुण्ड bald, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डितशिरस्
मुण्डितशिरस् mfn. (-राः-राः-रः) Bald-pated, shaven-headed.<BR> E. मुण्डित,<BR>शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डितिका
मुण्डितिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Muṇḍīrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डिन्|मुंडिन्
मुण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A barber.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR> E. मुण्ड shaving, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डीरिका
मुण्डीरिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Muṇḍīrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुण्डीरी
मुण्डीरी f. (-री) A plant, described as a creeper, bearing a red and<BR>yellow flower, commonly called by the same name, Muṇḍīrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुत्य|मुत्यं
मुत्य n. (-त्यं) A pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुथ्
मुथ् (इ) मुथि r. 1st cl. (मुन्थति)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्
मुद् r. 1st cl. (मोदते) To rejoice, to be glad. r. 10th cl. (मोदयति-ते)<BR>1. To mix, to blend, to unite.<BR>	 2. To clean, to wipe off. With अनु To<BR>allow, to permit, to approve. With आ 1. To be glad.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्
मुद् f. (-मुद्-मुत्)<BR>	 1. Pleasure, delight, joy.<BR>	 2. Intoxication, phrensy.<BR>	 3.<BR>A wife.<BR> E. मुद् to be pleased, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदा
मुदा f. (-दा) Happiness, joy.<BR> E. मुद् to be happy, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदान्वित
मुदान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pleased, happy.<BR> E. मुदा and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदित|मुदितः
मुदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pleased, delighted.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Pleasure, happiness.<BR>E. मुद् to rejoice, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदिर|मुदिरः
मुदिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A lover, a libertine.<BR>	 3. A frog.<BR> E. मुद् to<BR>be pleased, Unādi aff. किरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुदी
मुदी f. (-दी) Moonlight.<BR> E. मुद् to please, affs. क and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्ग|मुद्गः
मुद्ग m. (-द्गः)<BR>	 1. A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>	 2. A cover,<BR>as a lid or cloth.<BR>	 3. A kind of sea-bird.<BR> E. मुदि to please, Unādi<BR>aff. गक् नेट् । “मुग् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गपर्णी
मुद्गपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR> E. मुद्ग P.<BR>mungo, पर्ण a leaf, ङीष् aff. “मुगानी ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गभुज्
मुद्गभुज् m. (-भुक्) A horse.<BR> E. मुङ्ग kidney-bean, भुज् who eats: also<BR>मुद्गभोजिन् m. (-जी) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गर|मुद्गरं|मुद्गरः
मुद्गर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A mallet, a mace, a weapon formed like a carpenter's<BR>hammer.<BR>	 2. A staff, armed with iron, and larger at the lower ex-<BR>tremity, used for breaking clods of earth, &c.<BR>	 3. A carpenter's<BR>hammer.<BR>	 4. A sort of flower, said to be a kind of jasmine, perhaps<BR>jasminum zambac, (the wild variety.)<BR> E. मुद् pleasure, ग to swal-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">Page571-b+ 60</a>]<BR>low or destroy, aff. अच्; also with र changed to ल, मुद्गल “कर्मार<BR>वृक्षे च; काम्राङ्गा इति भाषा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गष्ट|मुद्गष्टः
मुद्गष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus lobatus.)<BR> E. मुद्ग P.<BR>mungo, स्था to stay, to resemble, aff. क; also with कन् added<BR>मुद्गष्टक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रण|मुद्रणं
मुद्रण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Sealing.<BR>	 2. Closing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रा
मुद्रा f. (-द्रा)<BR>	 1. A seal, a signet.<BR>	 2. A seal-ring.<BR>	 3. The mark of a seal<BR>or similar impression, a stamp, a print, &c.<BR>	 4. A coin.<BR>	 5. A medal.<BR>6. A sign, a token.<BR>	 7. A mystery.<BR>	 8. A mode of intertwining the<BR>fingers during religious worship.<BR> E. मुद् to please, (by it,) Unādi<BR>aff. रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्राङ्कित|मुद्राङ्कितः
मुद्राङ्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stamped, sealed.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A mint.<BR> E. मुद्रा a seal,<BR>अङ्कित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रिका
मुद्रिका f. (-का) A sealed or signed paper.<BR> E. मुद्रा a seal, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रित|मुद्रितं
मुद्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sealed.<BR>	 2. Marked, struck, stamped.<BR>	 3. Con-<BR>tracted, closed, sealed up.<BR>	 4. Unblown, (as a flower.)<BR> E. मुद्रा a seal,<BR>इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुधा
मुधा Ind. In vain, uselessly, unprofitably, idly.<BR> E. मुह् to be foolish, aff. का; ह changed to ध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनि|मुनिः
मुनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. A holy sage, a pious and learned person, endowed<BR>with more or less of a divine nature, or having attained it<BR>by rigid abstraction and mortification; the title is applied to the<BR>Ṛṣis, the Brahmadikās, and to a great number of persons dis-<BR>tinguished for their writings, considered as inspired, as PĀṆINI,<BR>VYĀSA, &c.<BR>	 2. An ascetic, a devotee.<BR>	 3. An Arhat or Jaina deified<BR>teacher.<BR>	 4. The saint AGASTYA.<BR>	 5. The Palāśh tree, (Butea<BR>frondosa.)<BR>	 6. Another tree, (Buchanania latifolia.)<BR> E. मन् to be<BR>revered, Unādi aff. इन्, and उ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिच्छद|मुनिच्छदः
मुनिच्छद m. (-दः) सप्तच्छदे. “छातिम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिद्रुम|मुनिद्रुमः
मुनिद्रुम m. (-मः) A tree, (Æschynomene grandiflora.)<BR> E. मुनि the saint<BR>AGASTYA, and द्रुम a tree. “श्योनाक वृक्षे, वकवृक्षे च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपित्तल|मुनिपित्तलं
मुनिपित्तल n. (-लं) Copper.<BR> E. मुनि a devotee, and पित्तल brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपुङ्गव|मुनिपुंगव|मुनिपुङ्गवः
मुनिपुङ्गव m. (-वः) A pre-eminent sage.<BR> E. मुनि a sage, and पुङ्गव, (in com-<BR>position) pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपुत्त्रक
मुनिपुत्त्रक m. (-कः) A wagtail.<BR> E. मुनि a sage, पुत्त्र a child, and कन् aff. of<BR>comparison. “दमन वृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपूग|मुनिपूगः
मुनिपूग m. (-गः) A kind of Areca, (A. triandra, or gracilis, Rox.)<BR> E. मुनि and पूग Areca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिभेषज|मुनिभेषजं
मुनिभेषज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Fasting.<BR>	 2. The fruit of the yellow myrobalan.<BR>	 3.<BR>The saint AGASTYA.<BR> E. मुनि a sage, भेषज a drug or medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिसुव्रत|मुनिसुव्रतः
मुनिसुव्रत m. (-तः) The twentieth Jaina pontiff of the present era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिस्थान|मुनिस्थानं
मुनिस्थान n. (-नं) A hermitage, the abode or retirement of holy sages.<BR>E. मुनि an ascetic, and स्थान a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनीन्द्र|मुनींद्र|मुनीन्द्रः
मुनीन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. A superior Muni or sage.<BR>	 2. A Buddha, a Bauddha<BR>sage or teacher.<BR> E. मुनि a sage, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुन्थ्
मुन्थ् r. 1st cl. (मन्थति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुन्यन्न
मुन्यन्न n. (-न्नं) Wild grain, roots, fruit, &c.<BR> E. मुनि a hermit, अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षा
मुमुक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Desire of liberation.<BR>	 2. Desire of final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षु|मुमुक्षुः
मुमुक्षु m. (-क्षुः)<BR>	 1. A sage, abstracted from all human passion and feel-<BR>ing, and preparing himself for eternal emancipation.<BR>	 2. Any one<BR>anxious for liberation, especially from mundane existence.<BR> E. मुच्<BR>to liberate, in the desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुचान|मुमुचानः
मुमुचान m. (-नः) A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुषिषु|मुमुषिषुः
मुमुषिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to steal.<BR> E. मुष् to steal, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुषिषुवत्
मुमुषिषुवत् Ind. Like a thief.<BR> E. मुमु, षिषुवति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमूर्षा
मुमूर्षा f. (-र्षा) Wish to die, impatience of life.<BR> E. मृ to die, desid v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमूर्षु|मुमूर्षुः
मुमूर्षु m. (-र्षुः) A man at the point of the death, a dying-man.<BR> E. मृ to<BR>die, desiderative or expectative form, and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्
मुर् r. 6th cl. (मुरति) To encircle, to entwine, to bind together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्
मुर् f. (-मूः) Fainting.<BR> E. मुर्च्छ् to faint, aff. क्किप्, the छ rejected<BR>after र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर|मुरं|मुरः
मुर m. (-रः) The name of a DAITYA killed by VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">Page572-a+ 60</a>]<BR>table perfume.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Surrounding, encircling.<BR> E. मुर to encircle,<BR>aff. क, or अङ् and टाप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=571-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरज|मुरजः
मुरज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A small drum, a tabor.<BR>	 2. A stanza the letters of<BR>which can be arranged in the form of a drum.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. The wife<BR>of KUVERA.<BR>	 2. A large drum.<BR> E. मुर encircling, with wood, &c.<BR>ज born, made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरजफल|मुरजफलः
मुरजफल m. (-लः) The jack-fruit tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरण्ड|मुरण्डः
मुरण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A country on the north west of Hindusthan, called<BR>also Lampaka, and now Lamgan.<BR>	 m. Plu (-ण्डाः) The inhabitants<BR>of Lamgan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरद|मुरदः
मुरद m. (-दः) The conch of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. मुर a demon, दो to cut, (to alarm,) aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरन्दला|मुरंदला
मुरन्दला f. (-ला) The Narmadā river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरमण्ड
मुरमण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Pimples on the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुररिपु|मुररिपुः
मुररिपु m. (-पुः) A name of KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR> E. मुर the demon,<BR>रिपु enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरला
मुरला f. (-ला) The Narmadā river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरलि
मुरलि f. (-ली) A flute, a pipe.<BR> E. मुर surrounding, ला to get or have, affs. क and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरलीधर|मुरलीधरः
मुरलीधर m. (-रः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. मुरली a flute, धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरहन्
मुरहन् m. (-हा) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. मुर the demon, हन् slayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरारि|मुरारिः
मुरारि m. (-रिः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. मुर the demon, अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्च्छ्
मुर्च्छ् (आ,) मुर्च्छा r. 1st cl. (मूर्च्छति)<BR>	 1. To be faint, to lose conscious-<BR>ness or perception.<BR>	 2. To increase, to grow.<BR>	 3. To settle in a solid<BR>form, to become dense.<BR>	 4. To prevail against.<BR>	 5. To be frequent.<BR>6. To sound loudly. With सम् To be intense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्भिणी
मुर्भिणी f. (-णी) A small fireplace or fire-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्मुर|मुर्मुरः
मुर्मुर m. (रः)<BR>	 1. A name of KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>	 2. A fire of chaff.<BR>	 3.<BR>One of the horses of the sun.<BR> E. मुर-क पृषो० द्वित्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्व्
मुर्व् (ई) मुर्व्वी r. 1st cl. (मुर्वति) To bind, to tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुल्
मुल् r. 10th cl. (मोलयति-ते) To plant: more usually मूल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुशटी
मुशटी f. (-टी) A kind of panick-seed, (Panicum italicum,) described as<BR>a white variety.<BR> E. मुष् -अटच् गौरा ङीष् पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुश
मुश(स)ली f. (-ली) A small house-lizard: see मुषली; also with कन् added<BR>मुशलिका f. (-का) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्
मुष् r. 1st cl. (मोषति) To injure, to kill. r. 9th cl. (मुष्णाति)<BR>	 1. To steal,<BR>to rub, to plunder.<BR>	 2. To captivate.<BR>	 3. To surpass. r. 4th cl.<BR>(मुष्यति)<BR>	 1. To cut, to divide, to break.<BR>	 2. To steal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषक|मुषकः
मुषक m. (-कः) A rat: see मूषक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषल|मुषलः
मुषल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A club, a mace.<BR>	 2. A pestle for cleaning rice.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>1. A house-lizard.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Curculigo orchioides:) see मुशली,<BR>मुसल, and मुसली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषलामुषलि
मुषलामुषलि Ind. Club to club, (fighting, &c.)<BR> E. मुषल repeated, इच्<BR>added; also मुसलामुसली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुल्य
मुल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Meriting or pounding to death: see मुसल्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषा
मुषा f. (-षा) A crucible.<BR> E. मुष् to steal, affs. अङ् and टाप्; also मूषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुषित|मुषितं
मुषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stolen, robbed.<BR> E. मुष् to steal, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्क|मुष्कः
मुष्क m. (-ष्कः)<BR>	 1. The scrotum.<BR>	 2. The testicle.<BR>	 3. A heap, a quantity.<BR>4. A thief.<BR>	 5. A stout man.<BR>	 6. A plant, commonly Ghaṇtāpārali.<BR>E. मुष् to steal, (semen, &c.) कक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कक|मुष्ककः
मुष्कक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Ghaṇtāpārali.<BR> E. मुष्क a thief,<BR>(of disease,) कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कद्वय
मुष्कद्वय n. (-यं) The testicles.<BR> E. मुष्क and द्वय pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कर|मुष्करः
मुष्कर m. (-रः) A man with large testicles.<BR> E. मुष्क testicle, and रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्कशून्य|मुष्कशून्यः
मुष्कशून्य m. (-न्यः) An eunuch, a guard of the women's apartments. E.<BR>मुष्क testicle, and शून्य wanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्ट
मुष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Theft, robbery.<BR> E. मुष् to steal, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टि|मुष्टिः
मुष्टि mf. (-ष्टिः-ष्टी)<BR>	 1. The fist, the closed hand.<BR>	 2. The hilt or handle of<BR>a sword, etc.<BR>	 3. A handful or Pala, the initiatory measure in the<BR>tables of the measures of grain.<BR>	 4. The penis.<BR>	 5. Filching, steal-<BR>ing.<BR> E. मुष् to steal or take, aff. क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिक|मुष्टिकः
मुष्टिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A goldsmith.<BR>	 2. A particular position of the hands.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">Page572-b+ 60</a>]<BR>3. Name of a demon killed by BALADEVA.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A pugilistic<BR>encounter.<BR> E. मुष्टि stealing and कृ to make, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिकान्तक|मुष्टिकांतक|मुष्टिकान्तकः
मुष्टिकान्तक m. (-कः) A name of BALADEVA the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिद्यूत|मुष्टिद्यूतं
मुष्टिद्यूत n. (-तं) A kind of game, odd or even.<BR> E. मुष्टि the fist, द्यूत<BR>gaming. “पुरमुट् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिन्धम|मुष्टिंधम
मुष्टिन्धम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Who blows in or on his closed fist.<BR> E. मुष्टि,<BR>and ध्मा to breathe, aff. खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिन्धय|मुष्टिंधय|मुष्टिंधयः|मुष्टिन्धयः
मुष्टिन्धय m. (-यः) A child.<BR> E. मुष्टि the fist, धे to drink or suck, aff. खश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिपात|मुष्टिपातः
मुष्टिपात m. (-तः) Pummelling, boxing.<BR> E. मुष्टि, पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिबन्ध|मुष्टिबंध|मुष्टिबन्धः
मुष्टिबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Clenching the fist.<BR> E. मुष्टि the fist, बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिसंग्राहपीडित
मुष्टिसंग्राहपीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Squeezed, pressed, griped.<BR> E. मुष्टि, संग्राह<BR>taking, पीडित squeezed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्टिमुष्टि
मुष्टिमुष्टि Ind. Fist to fist, (fighting,) fisticuffs.<BR> E. मुष्टि repeated in this<BR>sense, and the final made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्णत्
मुष्णत् mfn. (-ष्णन्-ष्णन्ती-ष्णत्)<BR>	 1. Stealing, robbing.<BR>	 2. Depriving of.<BR>	 3.<BR>Obscuring, eclipsing.<BR> E. मुष् to steal, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्
मुस् (इर) मुसिर r. 4th cl. (मुस्यति) To divide, to cut or break to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसल|मुसलं|मुसलः
मुसल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A pestle, a wooden pestle used for cleaning rice.<BR>	 2. A<BR>club.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Curculigo orchioides.)<BR>	 2. A house-<BR>lizard.<BR> E. मुस् to break, aff. कलच्; it is also read with its com-<BR>pounds and derivatives मुषल, मुषली, and sometimes मुशल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसलिन्
मुसलिन् m. (-ली) A name of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. मुसल a pestle, or pestle-like<BR>club, used by him as a weapon, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसल्य|मुसल्यः
मुसल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Deserving death by pounding with a pestle.<BR>E. मुसल a pestle, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्त्
मुस्त् r. 10th cl. (मुस्तयति-ते) To accumulate, to collect, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्त|मुस्तं|मुस्तः
मुस्त mf. (-स्तः-स्ता) A sort of grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. मुस्त to<BR>accumulate, aff. अच् “मुथा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तक|मुस्तकः
मुस्तक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>	 2. A sort<BR>of poison.<BR> E. मुस्त to accumulate, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्ताद|मुस्तादः
मुस्ताद m. (-दः) A hog.<BR> E. म्रस्ता Cyperus, and अद who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तु|मुस्तुः
मुस्तु m. (-स्तुः) The fist.<BR> E. मुस् to break, तुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्र|मुस्रं
मुस्र n. (-स्रं)<BR>	 1. A pestle.<BR>	 2. A tear.<BR> E. मुस् to divide, Unādi aff. रच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुह्
मुह् (ऊ) मुहू r. 4th cl. (मुह्यति) To be foolish, to be incapable of dis-<BR>crimination or judgment, to be bereft of sense or wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहिर|मुहिरः
मुहिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Love, desire, KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 2. A fool, a blockhead. E.<BR>मुह् to grow foolish, Unādi aff. किरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहुर्भाषा
मुहुर्भाषा f. (-षा) Tautology, repetition.<BR> E. मुहुस् repeatedly, भाषा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहुस्
मुहुस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Repeatedly, reiteratedly, again and again.<BR>	 2. For a<BR>moment.<BR> E. मुह् to be foolish, Unādi aff. उसिक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहूर्त्त|मुहूर्त|मुहूर्तं|मुहूर्तः|मुहूर्त्तः
मुहूर्त्त mn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्तं) Adivision of time, the thirtieth part of a day and<BR>night, or an hour of forty-eight minutes.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्तः) An astrologer.<BR>E. हुर्च्छ to be crooked or fraudulent, क्त aff., form irr., and मुक्<BR>initiatory augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहेर|मुहेरः
मुहेर m. (-रः) A fool, a blockhead, an ignoramus.<BR> E. मुह् to be foolish, एरक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मू
मू r. 1st cl. (मवते) To bind, to tie, to make fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मू
मू f. (-मूः) Binding, tying.<BR> E. मू to tie, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूक|मूकः
मूक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Dumb.<BR>	 2. Poor, wretched.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A fish.<BR>2. A demon.<BR>	 3. A pauper.<BR> E. मू imitative sound, and कै to utter,<BR>aff. क; or मू to bind, कक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूकिमन्
मूकिमन् m. (-मा) Silence, dumbness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढ|मूढः
मूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Foolish, ignorant.<BR>	 2. Cold, apathetic, stupid.<BR>3. Perplexed, in doubt.<BR>	 4. Deceived, erring.<BR>	 m. (-ढः)<BR>	 1. An idiot,<BR>a fool.<BR>	 2. A sluggard.<BR> E. मुह् to be foolish, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढगर्भ|मूढगर्भः
मूढगर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. A bad presentation of the child at birth, causing<BR>difficult delivery.<BR>	 2. A dead fœtus.<BR> E. मूढ, and गर्भ the fœtus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढग्राह|मूढग्राहः
मूढग्राह m. (-हः) Infatuation.<BR> E. मूढ, and ग्राह seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढचेतस्
मूढचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ता-तः) Insane, bewildered.<BR> E. मूढ, and चेतस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढता
मूढता f. (-ता) Folly, silliness, ignorance.<BR> E. मूढ, and तल् aff.; also मूढत्वं<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढात्मन्
मूढात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Foolish, a fool.<BR> E. मूढ, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=572-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत|मूतः
मूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bound, tied.<BR>	 2. Confined.<BR> E. मू to bind, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्र्
मूत्र् r. 10th cl. (मूत्रयति-ते) To urine, to make water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्र|मूत्रं
मूत्र n. (-त्रं) Urine, piss.<BR> E. मूत्र to piss, घञ् aff.; or मुच् to loose, Unādi<BR>aff. त्रन्, and ऊ substituted for the vowel; or मूत्र-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रकृच्छ्र|मूत्रकृच्छ्रं
मूत्रकृच्छ्र n. (-च्छ्रं)<BR>	 1. Strangury.<BR>	 2. Urinary affection in general, as<BR>gravel, &c.<BR> E. मूत्र urine, कृच्छ्र pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रग्रन्थि|मूत्रग्रन्थिः
मूत्रग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) Obstruction at the neck of the bladder.<BR> E. मूत्र, ग्रन्थि,<BR>knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रदोष|मूत्रदोषः
मूत्रदोष m. (-षः) Gonorrhœa, considered as an urinary complaint.<BR> E. मूत्र urine, दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रपतन|मूत्रपतनः
मूत्रपतन m. (-नः) A civet cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रपुट|मूत्रपुटं
मूत्रपुट n. (-टं) The lower belly.<BR> E. मूत्र urine, and पुट to be shallow, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रमार्ग|मूत्रमार्गः
मूत्रमार्ग m. (-र्गः) The urethra.<BR> E. मूत्र, मार्ग passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रल|मूत्रलं
मूत्रल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Diuretic.<BR>	 mf. (-लः-ला) A cucumber.<BR> E. मूत्र urine, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रशुक्र
मूत्रशुक्र n. (-क्रं) Milky urine, depositing a thick white sediment.<BR> E. मूत्र,<BR>and शुक्र, semen, which is supposed to give the colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रसङ्ग|मूत्रसंग|मूत्रसंगः
मूत्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Urinary obstruction.<BR> E. मूत्र, and सङ्ग being with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्राघात|मूत्राघातः
मूत्राघात m. (-तः) Suppression of urine.<BR> E. मूत्र, and आघात impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रातीत
मूत्रातीत m. (-तः) Difficult or slow passage of urine.<BR> E. मूत्र, अतीत passed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्राशय|मूत्राशयः
मूत्राशय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The bladder.<BR>	 2. The lower belly, the pubic region.<BR>E. मूत्र urine, and आशय place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रित|मूत्रितः
मूत्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pissed, voided as urine.<BR> E. मूत्र to urine, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रोत्सङ्ग|मूत्रोत्संग
मूत्रोत्सङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Obstructed or tardy flow of urine, discharge of it<BR>mixed with blood, &c.<BR> E. मूत्र and उत्सङ्ग adhesion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ख|मूर्खः
मूर्ख mfn. (-र्खः-र्खा-र्खं) Foolish, ignorant, stupid, idiotic.<BR>	 m. (-र्खः) A sort<BR>of bean, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR> E. मूर्ख substituted for मुह् to be fool-<BR>ish, aff. अच्; or मुर् substituted for the root, with ख Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खभ्रातृक|मूर्खभ्रातृकः
मूर्खभ्रातृक m. (-कः) The brother of a fool.<BR> E. मूर्ख a fool, भ्रातृ a brother,<BR>कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छत्
मूर्च्छत् mfn. (-र्च्छन्-र्च्छन्ती-र्च्छत्) Fainting, swooning,<BR> E. मूर्च्छ् to faint, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छन
मूर्च्छन nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>	 1. Fainting syncope, swooning, meeting.<BR>	 2. Vehe-<BR>mence growth, increase.<BR>	 3. Causing insensibility, (applied to one of<BR>the five arrows of KĀMA.)<BR>	 4. Calcining quicksilver with sulphur,<BR>&c.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. The rise and fall of sounds in music.<BR>	 2. Modula-<BR>tion, melody.<BR> E. मूर्च्छ् to faint, to become insensible, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छा
मूर्च्छा f. (-र्च्छा)<BR>	 1. Fainting, loss of consciousness or sense.<BR>	 2. Delusion.<BR>3. A particular process in calcining metals.<BR> E. मूर्च्छा to be faint,<BR>affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छाल
मूर्च्छाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Fainted, fainting, insensible.<BR> E. मूर्च्छा fainting, (the act,) लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छावत्
मूर्च्छावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Faint.<BR> E. मूर्च्छा, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूच्छित
मूच्छित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fainting, fainted, insensible.<BR>	 2. Stupid, igno-<BR>rant.<BR>	 3. Tall, lofty.<BR>	 4. Grown, increased, augmented.<BR>	 5. Intensi-<BR>fied.<BR>	 6. Filled with.<BR>	 7. Calcined.<BR> E. मूर्च्छ् to be faint, to grow or<BR>increase, &c., aff. क्त; or मूर्च्छा as above, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ण|मूर्णः
मूर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Bound, tied,<BR> E. मूर्व्व् to bind, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त्त|मूर्त|मूर्त्तः
मूर्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Fainting, fainted, losing sense or conscious-<BR>ness.<BR>	 2. Solid, material, endowed with form or shape.<BR>	 3. Embo-<BR>died, corporeal.<BR>	 4. Hard.<BR>	 5. Stupid.<BR> E. मुर्च्छ् to lose consciousness,<BR>aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त्ति|मूर्ति|मूर्तिः|मूर्त्तिः
मूर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Matter, substance, solidity.<BR>	 2. The body.<BR>	 3. Figure,<BR>form, body in general, or any definite shape or image.<BR>	 4. Manifes-<BR>tation.<BR>	 5. Beauty.<BR>	 6. Hardness.<BR> E. मूर्च्छ् to faint, to become insen-<BR>sible, aff. क्तिन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त्तिमत्|मूर्तिमत्|मूर्तिमन्त्
मूर्त्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Material, substantial, having shape or<BR>substance.<BR>	 2. Incarnate, embodied.<BR>	 n. (-मत्) The body.<BR> E. मूर्त्ति<BR>shape, &c. मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्ध
मूर्द्ध(र्ध्व)क m. (-कः) The man of the second or military class.<BR> E. मूर्द्ध the<BR>head, and कन् aff.; also मूर्धक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धकर्णी
मूर्द्धकर्णी f. (-र्णी) An umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धकर्प्परी
मूर्द्धकर्प्परी f. (-री) An umbrella, or inverted basket carried on the head<BR>for the same purpose.<BR> E. मूर्द्ध the head, कर्प्पर a sort of pan, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धखोल
मूर्द्धखोल n. (-लं) A sort of umbrella: see the last.<BR> E. मूर्द्ध the head, खोल<BR>or खोलक a helmet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धज
मूर्द्धज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Hair, the hair of the head.<BR>	 2. The name.<BR> E. मूर्द्ध the<BR>head, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धज्योतिस्
मूर्द्धज्योतिस् n. (-तिः) A hole in the crown of the head from which the<BR>soul is supposed to escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धन्
मूर्द्धन् m. (-र्द्धा)<BR>	 1. The head.<BR>	 2. The Forehead.<BR>	 3. Top.<BR>	 4. Front, 5. The<BR>head, the chief.<BR> E. मूह् to be foolish, Unādi aff. कनिन्, form<BR>irr.; or मुर्व्व् to bind, the same aff., धञ् augment; also read मूर्धन्<BR>and मूर्ध्वन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्ध्वन्य
मूर्द्ध्वन्य f. (-न्या)<BR>	 1. Being in or on the head.<BR>	 2. Pre-eminent, excellent.<BR>3. Cerebral, (applied to the following letters, viz:--ऋ, ॠ, ट, ठ,<BR>ड, ढ, ण, र and ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धपुष्प
मूर्द्धपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A tree, commonly Sirisha, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR> E. मूर्द्ध the head, पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धरस
मूर्द्धरस m. (-सः) The scum of boiled rice, &c.<BR> E. मूर्द्ध head, top, रस<BR>juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धवेष्टन
मूर्द्धवेष्टन n. (-नं) A turban, a fillet, a diadem, &c.<BR> E. मूर्द्ध the head, वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्द्धाभिषिक्त
मूर्द्धाभिषिक्त m. (-क्तः)<BR>	 1. A man of the second or military class, the<BR>Kṣatriya or soldier.<BR>	 2. A king, a prince.<BR>	 3. A chief minister, a<BR>counsellor of state.<BR>	 4. The name of a mixed class, sprung from a<BR>Brāhmana, and female of the second or Kṣatriya tribe; the prin-<BR>cipal of the mixed races, and soldier by profession.<BR> E. मूर्द्ध the<BR>head, and अभिषिक्त sprinkled, anointed; kings being consecrated<BR>by having poured on their heads, while seated on a throne pre-<BR>pared for the purpose, water from some sacred stream, mixed<BR>with honey, clarified butter, and spirituous liquor, as well as two<BR>sorts of grass and the sprouts of corn: the term applies to the<BR>Kṣatriya as identified with the king, the duties of royalty,<BR>belonging especially to the military caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ध्वन्
मूर्ध्वन् m. (-र्द्धा)<BR>	 1. The head.<BR>	 2. The base, (in geometry.)<BR> E. मूर्व्वा to bind,<BR>Unādi aff. कनिन् and ध्वङ् substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्व्वा|मूर्वा
मूर्व्वा f. (-र्व्वा-र्व्वी) A sort of creeper, from the fibres of which bow-<BR>strings are made, (Sanseviera zeylanica;) they should also form<BR>the girdle worn by the Kṣatriya class.<BR> E. मुर्व्व् to bind, affs. अङ्<BR>and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्
मूल् r. 1st cl. (मूलति-ते)<BR>	 1. To stand, to be rooted or firm.<BR>	 2. To accu-<BR>mulate. r. 10th cl. (मूलयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To plant or transplant.<BR>	 2. To<BR>grow as a plant, to sprout, to shoot or germinate. With उद्<BR>prefixed, to root up or out, to eradicate, to exterminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल|मूलं|मूलः
मूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A root, the root of a tree, &c.<BR>	 2. Origin, commencement.<BR>3. Capital, principal.<BR>	 4. Near, proximate.<BR>	 5. Own, peculiar, pro-<BR>per.<BR>	 6. The root of the Arum campanulatum.<BR>	 7. The original text<BR>of any work, as opposed to the Tīkā or comment.<BR>	 8. The root<BR>or bottom of any thing.<BR>	 9. The end of any thing by which it is<BR>joined to something else.<BR>	 10. Authority, source, origin.<BR>	 11.<BR>Vicinity.<BR>	 12. Basis, foundation.<BR>	 13. A hereditary servant.<BR>	 14.<BR>Capital, stock.<BR>	 15. Square root, (in math.)<BR>	 16. A king's own<BR>territory.<BR>	 17. A thicket.<BR>	 18. A vender who is not a true owner.<BR>mn. (-लः-लं) The nineteenth lunar asterism, containing eleven<BR>stars, which appear to be the same as those in the SCORPION'S<BR>tail.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A small house-lizard.<BR> E. मूल् to stand, to be rooted or<BR>firm, aff. क; or मू to bind, Unādi aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलक|मूलकं|मूलकः
मूलक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. The radish, (Raphanus sativus.)<BR>	 2. A large sort<BR>of yam.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A sort of poison.<BR> E. मूल a root, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकपण|मूलकपणः
मूलकपण m. (-णः) A handful of radishes, &c. for sale.<BR> E. मूलक, and पण<BR>measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकपोतिका
मूलकपोतिका f. (-का) A radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकमूला
मूलकमूला f. (-ला) A plant, commonly Kṣīrakākoli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकर्म्मन्|मूलकर्मन्
मूलकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Magic.<BR> E. मूल original, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकारिका
मूलकारिका f. (-का) A fire place.<BR> E. मूल primary, (work,) कारिक an agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=573-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकृच्छ्र|मूलकृच्छ्रः
मूलकृच्छ्र n. (-च्छ्रं) A sort of penance, subsisting for a given time on the<BR>roots of plants only.<BR> E. मूल a root, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकेशर|मूलकेशरः
मूलकेशर m. (-रः) A citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलखानक|मूलखानकः
मूलखानक m. (-कः) A digger for roots.<BR> E. मूल, and खानक a digger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलगुण|मूलगुणः
मूलगुण m. (-णः) The coefficient of a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलज|मूलजं|मूलजः
मूलज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born from a root, &c.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A plant growing<BR>from a root, as lotus, &c.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Green ginger.<BR> E. मूल a root, and<BR>ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलदेव|मूलदेवः
मूलदेव m. (-वः) A name of KAṂSA, the uncle of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. मूल origi-<BR>nal, and देव a deity; the incarnation of a demi-god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलद्रव्य|मूलद्रव्यं
मूलद्रव्य n. (-व्यं) Capital, principal, stock.<BR> E. मूल capital, द्रव्य substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलधन|मूलधनं
मूलधन n. (-नं) Capital, principal, stock.<BR> E. मूल capital, धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलधातु|मूलधातुः
मूलधातु m. (-तुः) Lymph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलपर्णी
मूलपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Hydrocotyle asiatica.) “मण्डुकपर्ण्याम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलपुरुष|मूलपुरुषः
मूलपुरुष m. (-षः) The male representative of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलप्रकृति|मूलप्रकृतिः
मूलप्रकृति f. (-तिः) The Pradhāna of the Sānkhyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलभद्र|मूलभद्रः
मूलभद्र m. (-द्रः) A name of KAṂSA, the uncle of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. मूल<BR>origin, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलभृत्य|मूलभृत्यः
मूलभृत्य m. (-त्यः) An old or hereditary servant.<BR> E. मूल, भृत्य dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलविभुज|मूलविभुजः
मूलविभुज m. (-जः) A car, a carriage a chariot.<BR> E. मूल the root, (the<BR>axle,) and विभुज what bends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलशाकट|मूलशाकटः
मूलशाकट mfn. (-टः-टी-टं) Fit or cultivated for esculent roots, (as the<BR>arum, the radish and others, a field, &c.)<BR> E. मूल a root, and शाकट<BR>aff.; also with शाकिन aff., मूलशाकिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलस्थान
मूलस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Ether, heaven, space or atmosphere.<BR>	 2. God.<BR>3. Base, foundation.<BR>	 f. (-नी) GAURĪ.<BR> E. मूल primary origin, &c.,<BR>and स्थान place, abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूला
मूला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The name of a plant. “शतमूल्याम्” 2. The asterism MŪLA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलाधार|मूलाधारः
मूलाधार n. (-रं) The navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिक|मूलिकः
मूलिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Radical, (literal or figurative,) primary, prin-<BR>cipal.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A devotee, living on roots.<BR> E. मूल a root, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिन्
मूलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Having a root, stock, origin, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ली)<BR>A tree.<BR> E. मूल a root, aff. इनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलेर|मूलेरः
मूलेर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Indian spikenard.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR> E. मूल to be rooted, Unādi aff. एरक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्य|मूल्यं
मूल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. To be eradicated, to be pulled or plucked up<BR>by the root.<BR>	 2. To be bent from the root, &c.<BR>	 3. To be bought,<BR>purchasable.<BR>	 4. To be bought for a fair or just price.<BR>	 n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Price, worth.<BR>	 2. Wages, hire.<BR>	 3. An article purchased.<BR>	 4. Gain.<BR>5. Capital, principal.<BR> E. मूल principal, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष्
मूष् r. 1st cl. (मूषति) To steal, to rob or plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष|मूषः
मूष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं)<BR>	 1. A rat, a mouse.<BR>	 2. A crucible.<BR>	 3. An air-hole,<BR>a window.<BR>	 f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. A sort of grass, (Andropogon serratum.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A female rat.<BR> E. मूष् to steal, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषक|मूषकः
मूषक mf. (-कः-षका or षिका)<BR>	 1. A mouse, a rat.<BR>	 2. A thief.<BR> E. कन् or नक् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषकाराति|मूषकारातिः
मूषकाराति m. (-तिः) A cat.<BR> E. मूषक a rat, and अराति enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषण|मूषणं
मूषण n. (-णं) Stealing, pilfering.<BR> E. मूष् to steal, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषत्
मूषत् mfn. (-षन्-षन्ती-षत्) Stealing, plundering.<BR> E. मूष, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषाकर्णी
मूषाकर्णी f. (-र्णी) An aquatic plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR> E. मूषा a rat,<BR>कर्ण the ear; to which the leaf of the plant is compared, fem. aff.<BR>ङीष्; also मूषिकपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषातुत्थ|मूषातुत्थं
मूषातुत्थ n. (-त्थं) Blue vitriol.<BR> E. मूषा a crucible. तुत्थ sulphate of copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिक|मूषिकः
मूषिक mf. (-कः-का) A rat, a mouse.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree, commonly<BR>Sirisha, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR>	 2. A thief, a plunderer.<BR>	 3. A country,<BR>the part of the Mālābār coast between Quilon and Cape Comorin.<BR>f. (-का) A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>	 2. A crucible.<BR> E. मूष् to<BR>steal, Unādi aff. किनन् and the vowel made long; also मूषिका, मूषा,<BR>and मूषी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकपर्णी|मूषिकपर्ण्णी
मूषिकपर्णी f. (-र्णी) An aquatic plant of the cryptogamia class, (Sal-<BR>vinia cucullata.)<BR> E. मूषिक a rat, (ears, understood,) and पर्णी a leaf,<BR>aff. ङीष्; having a leaf compared to a mouse's ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकाङ्क|मूषिकांक|मूषिकाङ्कः
मूषिकाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. मूषिक a rat, अङ्क a mark or<BR>emblem; being usually painted riding on a rat or attended<BR>by one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकाञ्चन|मूषिकांचन|मूषिकाञ्चनः
मूषिकाञ्चन m. (-नः) A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. मूषिक a rat, and अञ्चन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकार|मूषिकारः
मूषिकार m. (-रः) A male mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकाराति|मूषिकारातिः
मूषिकाराति m. (-तिः) A cat.<BR> E. मूषिक, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकाह्वय|मूषिकाह्वयः
मूषिकाह्वय m. (-यः) A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR> E. मूषिक a rat, and<BR>आह्वय appellation; also मूषिकाह्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषित
मूषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stolen.<BR> E. मूष and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिपर्णिका
मूषिपर्णिका f. (-का) A plant; see the last.<BR> E. मूषि for मूषी, and कन् added to पर्णी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषीक|मूषीकः
मूषीक mf. (-कः-का) A rat, a mouse.<BR> E. मूष् to steal, कीकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष्यायण|मूष्यायणः
मूष्यायण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Born of unknown parents, of concealed birth<BR>or origin.<BR> E. अमूष्यायण the son of some body, and the initiatory<BR>vowel rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृ
मृ (मृ) r. 6th cl. (म्रियते) To die. With अनु, to die after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृकण्डक|मृकण्डकः
मृकण्डक m. (-कः) The name of a saint; also called MĀRKAṆḌEYA. E.<BR>मृकण्ड the name of his father, and वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृकण्डु|मृकण्डुः
मृकण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) The saint MĀRKAṆḌEYA.<BR> E. मृकण्डु his father, अण्<BR>aff.; but the word unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृक्ष्
मृक्ष् r. 1st cl. (मृक्षति) To accumulate, to collect, to fill. r. 10th cl.<BR>(मृक्षयति)<BR>	 1. To mix, to mingle, to blend or combine.<BR>	 2. To speak<BR>incorrectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग्
मृग् r. 4th cl. (मृग्यति) r. 10th cl. (मृगयते)<BR>	 1. To seek, or pursue, to<BR>hunt, to chase.<BR>	 2. To investigate.<BR>	 3. To beg any thing from<BR>any body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग|मृगः
मृग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A deer, an antelope.<BR>	 2. An animal in general.<BR>	 3. Re-<BR>search, inquiry, investigation.<BR>	 4. Asking, soliciting, begging.<BR>	 5.<BR>A kind of elephant, one with white marks on his forehead.<BR>	 6. The<BR>fifth lunar constellation, more usually Mṛgaśiras: see मृगशिरस्.<BR>	 7.<BR>The month in which the moon is full in the constellation Mṛgas-<BR>īras.<BR>	 8. A particular sacrifice.<BR>	 9. Musk.<BR>	 10. Hunting, chase.<BR>	 11.<BR>One of the four classes into which men are divided, (in erotic<BR>works.)<BR>	 12. The spots of the moon represented as an antelope.<BR>f. (-गी)<BR>	 1. A description of woman, perhaps the same as the<BR>one termed चित्रिणी, the corresponding female to the male<BR>called मृग.<BR>	 2. A female deer, a doe.<BR>	 3. A species of the Madhya<BR>metre.<BR>	 4. Epilepsy.<BR> E. मृग् to search, to chase, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगक्षीर|मृगक्षीरं
मृगक्षीर n. (-रं) Doe's milk.<BR> E. मृग for मृगी a female deer, and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगगामिनी
मृगगामिनी f. (-नी) A kind of medical plant, “विडङ्गायाम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगचैटक
मृगचैटक m. (-कः) A wild or pole-cat. “खटाश् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगजल
मृगजल n. (-लं) Mirage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगजलस्नान
मृगजलस्नान n. (-नं) Bathing in the waters of a mirage, (i. e.) an impossibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगजालिका
मृगजालिका f. (-का) A net for confining deer.<BR> E. मृग a deer, जालिका a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगजीवन|मृगजीवनः
मृगजीवन m. (-नः) A hunter.<BR> E. मृग a deer, जीवन living, subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगण
मृगण nf. (-णं-णा) Search, inquiry, research.<BR> E. मृग् to search for or<BR>after, affs. युच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृष्
मृगतृष् f. (-तृट्) Vapour floating over sands or deserts, and appearing<BR>at a distance like water.<BR> E. मृग a deer, तृष् to thirst, aff. क्विप्; deer<BR>being deceived by it; also with अङ् and टाप् aff, मृगतृषा, and with<BR>तृष्णा thirst, मृगतृष्णा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृषा
मृगतृषा f. (-षा) Mirage: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृष्णा
मृगतृष्णा f. (-ष्णा) Sultry vapour, mirage: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगतृष्णिका
मृगतृष्णिका f. (-का) Sultry vapour.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगदंशक|मृगदंशकः
मृगदंशक m. (-कः) A dog.<BR> E. मृग deer, and दंशक who bites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगदृश्
मृगदृश् f. (-दृक्) A deer-eyed woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगद्युत्
मृगद्युत् m. (-द्युत्) A hunter.<BR> E. मृग, द्यु to go, क्विप् aff., तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगद्यू
मृगद्यू m. (-द्यूः) A hunter.<BR> E. मृग and दिव् to play, क्विप् aff., and the<BR>semi-vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगद्विष्
मृगद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) A lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगधर|मृगधरः
मृगधर m. (-रः) The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगधूर्त्तक|मृगधूर्तक|मृगधूर्तकः|मृगधूर्त्तकः
मृगधूर्त्तक m. (-कः) A jackal.<BR> E. मृग a deer, and धूर्त्तक a cheat; preying<BR>upon them only in consequence of his luring them into his reach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगनाभि|मृगनाभिः
मृगनाभि m. (-भिः) Musk.<BR> E. मृग a deer, (the musk-deer,) and नाभि the<BR>navel; the musk being formed in a bag attached to the belly of<BR>the animal about the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगनाभिज
मृगनाभिज nf. (-जं-जा) Musk.<BR> E. मृग a deer, नाभि the navel, ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगनेत्र
मृगनेत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Possessing or relating to the constellation<BR>Mṛgasīrsha.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A woman with beautiful eyes, or eyes like a<BR>deer.<BR> E. मृग the asterism, णी to get, तृच् aff., and अप् added; or मृग<BR>a deer, and नेत्र the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगपातो
मृगपातो m. (-तिः) A lion.<BR> E. मृग an animal or a deer, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगपद
मृगपद n. (-दं) A deer's foot.<BR> E. मृग, and पद for पाद foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगपालिका
मृगपालिका f. (-का) The musk-deer.<BR> E. मृग a deer, पाल् to nourish, वुन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगपिप्लु|मृगपिप्लुः
मृगपिप्लु m. (-प्लुः) The moon.<BR> E. मृग a deer, and पिप्लु a mark or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगधाजीव
मृगधाजीव m. (-वः) A hunter, a deer-killer.<BR> E. मृग a deer, वध killing,<BR>and आजीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगबन्धिनी|मृगबंधिनी
मृगबन्धिनी f. (-नी) A net for confining deer.<BR> E. मृग a deer, and बन्धिनी confinement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगभोजनी
मृगभोजनी f. (-नी) Bitter apple or Colocynth.<BR> E. मृग, and भोजन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगमद|मृगमदः
मृगमद m. (-दः) Musk.<BR> E. मृग a deer, and मद passion, or fluid that dis-<BR>tils from the elephant's temples when in rut, and to which this<BR>secretion is considered analogous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगमदवासा
मृगमदवासा f. (-सा) A musk-bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगमन्द्र|मृगमंद्र|मृगमन्द्रः
मृगमन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) Name of a particular class of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगमातृका
मृगमातृका f. (-का) A female antelope.<BR> E. मृग, मातृ mother, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगमान
मृगमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Seeking, pursuing, hunting.<BR> E. मृग् to seek,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगमुख|मृगमुखः
मृगमुख m. (-खः) The sign Capricornus of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगया
मृगया f. (-या) Chase, hunting.<BR> E. मृग् to search or seek, यत् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगयु|मृगयुः
मृगयु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A jackal.<BR>	 3. A hunter.<BR> E. मृग a deer, या<BR>to go, कु Unādi aff., form irr; or मृग्-यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगराज्
मृगराज् m. (-राट्)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. The sign Leo of the zodiac.<BR>	 3. A tiger.<BR>4. The moon.<BR> E. मृग an animal, and राज् who rules over: also<BR>with a final vowel सृगराज m. (-जः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगरिपु|मृगरिपुः
मृगरिपु m. (-पुः) A lion.<BR> E. मृग an animal, and रिपु the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगरोमज|मृगरोमजं
मृगरोमज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Woollen, (cloth, &c.)<BR> E. मृष an animal, रोम<BR>hair, and ज produced, made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगलाञ्छन|मृगलांछन|मृगलाञ्छनः
मृगलाञ्छन m. (-नः) The moon.<BR> E. मृङ्ग a deer, लाञ्छन symbol, sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगलेखा
मृगलेखा f. (-खा) The deer-like streak on the disc of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगवाहन|मृगवाहनः
मृगवाहन m. (-नः) Air, wind.<BR> E. मृग a deer, and वाहन vehicle. “स्वातिनक्षत्रे च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगव्य|मृगव्यं
मृगव्य n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Chase, hunting.<BR>	 2. The butt or mark in archery. E.<BR>मृग a deer, व्यथ् to destroy, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगव्याध|मृगव्याधः
मृगव्याध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A hunter.<BR>	 2. The dog-star.<BR>	 3. ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगशार
मृगशार m. (-रः) A fawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगशिरस्
मृगशिरस् n. (-रः) The fifth lunar mansion, containing three stars, one<BR>of which is ORIONIS, and figured by an antelope's head, whence<BR>its name.<BR> E. मृग a deer, and शिरस् the head; also मृगशिरा f. (-रा) or<BR>मृगशिरस् m. (-रः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगशीर्ष|मृगशीर्षं|मृगशीर्षः
मृगशीर्ष m. (-र्षः) The constellation Mrīgaśiras: see the last.<BR> E. मृग a<BR>deer, and शीर्ष the head; also f. (-र्षा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाक्षी
मृगाक्षी f. (-क्षी)<BR>	 1. Bitter-apple, (Cucumis coloquintida.)<BR>	 2. A woman<BR>with eyes like a deer's.<BR> E. मृग a deer, अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाङ्क|मृगांक|मृगाङ्कः
मृगाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>	 3. Camphor.<BR> E. मृग a deer,<BR>and अङ्क a symbol, or अकि to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाजिन
मृगाजिन n. (-नं) A deer-skin.<BR> E. मृग, and अजिन a skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाजीव|मृगाजीवः
मृगाजीव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A hyena.<BR>	 2. A hunter.<BR> E. मृग a deer, and आजीव<BR>who lives by or preys upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाण्डजा|मृगांडजा
मृगाण्डजा f. (-जा) Musk.<BR> E. मृग a deer, अण्ड testicle, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाद्
मृगाद् m. (-द or -त्) A tiger.<BR> E. मृग a deer, अद् to eat, aff. क्विन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगादन|मृगादनः
मृगादन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A hyena.<BR>	 2. A leopard.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Colocynth, (Cucumis<BR>coloquintida.) “इन्द्रवारुणी”<BR> E. मृग a deer, and अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगान्तक|मृगांतक|मृगान्तकः
मृगान्तक m. (-कः) The Chitā or hunting leopard.<BR> E. मृग a deer, अन्तक<BR>destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाराति|मृगारातिः
मृगाराति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A dog.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR> E. मृग a deer, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगारि|मृगारिः
मृगारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. A tiger.<BR>	 3. A dog, a hound.<BR> E. मृग a<BR>deer, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगाविध्
मृगाविध् m. (-विद्) A hunter, a deer-killer.<BR> E. मृग a deer, व्यध् to des-<BR>troy, with अङ् prefix, and क्किप् aff., and the semi-vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगास्य|मृगास्यः
मृगास्य m. (-स्यः) The sign Capricornus of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगित|मृगितः
मृगित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sought, pursued.<BR> E. मृग् to chase, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगेन्द्र|मृगेंद्र|मृगेन्द्रः
मृगेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A lion.<BR> E. मृग an animal, इन्द्र lord, master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगेन्द्रचटक|मृगेंद्रचटक|मृगेन्द्रचटकः
मृगेन्द्रचटक m. (-कः) A hawk, a falcon.<BR> E. मृगेन्द्र a lion, चटक a sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगेन्द्रमुख
मृगेन्द्रमुख n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. The lion's mouth.<BR>	 2. A species of the Atijagatī<BR>metre.<BR> E. मृगेन्द्र, and मुख mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगैर्व्वारु|मृगैर्वारु
मृगै(गे)र्व्वारु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A white deer.<BR>	 2. Colocynth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग्य|मृग्यः
मृग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) To be sought or inquired for.<BR> E. मृग् to search,<BR>क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग्यमान
मृग्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being sought or inquired after.<BR> E. मृग् to search, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृच्चय|मृच्चयः
मृच्चय m. (-यः) A heap of earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृच्छकटिका
मृच्छकटिका f. (-का) A small cart of clay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज्
मृज् (ऊ) मृजू r. 2nd cl. (मार्ष्टि) r. 1st and 10th cls. (मार्जति मार्जयति-ते)<BR>	 1.<BR>To clean, to cleanse.<BR>	 2. To be clean or pure.<BR>	 3. To ornament.<BR>	 4.<BR>To sound.<BR>	 5. To sharpen. With अप or प्र prefixed, 1. To sweep, to<BR>sweep away.<BR>	 2. To clean. With सम 1. To clean.<BR>	 2. To stroke.<BR>	 3.<BR>To filter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज|मृजः
मृज m. (-जः) A musical instrument, probably a sort of tabor or drum.<BR>f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. Cleaning the body, by washing, anointing, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Purification, ablution.<BR>	 3. Complexion.<BR> E. मृज् to cleanse, to sound<BR>aff. क, or अङ्, and टाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृजान्वय
मृजान्वय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Clean, cleansed.<BR> E. मृजा, and अन्वय order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृजित
मृजित f. (-ता) Adj. Wiped away, removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृज्य|मृज्यं
मृज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) To be cleaned or purified.<BR> E. मृज् to cleanse,<BR>क्यप् aff.; also मार्ग्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृड्
मृड् r. 6th cl. (मृडति) r. 9th cl. (मृड्णाति)<BR>	 1. To delight, to make<BR>happy.<BR>	 2. To rejoice, to be happy or delighted. r. 9th cl. (Accord-<BR>ing to some authorities,) To grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृड|मृडः
मृड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The fire that completes an obla-<BR>tion.<BR>	 f. [डा or -डा(दा)नी] DURGĀ, the wife of ŚIVA.<BR> E. मृड् to be<BR>pleased or delighted, aff. क, fem. aff. ङीष्, with आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडङ्कण|मृडङ्कणः
मृडङ्कण m. (-णः) A child, a pupil.<BR> E. मृड् to be pleased, Unādi aff.<BR>कङ्कण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृडीक|मृडीकः
मृडीक m. (-कः) A deer.<BR> E. मृड् to delight, Unādi aff. कीकन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृण्
मृण् r. 6th cl. (मृणति)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure.<BR>	 2. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणाल|मृणालं|मृणालः
मृणाल mn. (-लः-लं) The film or fibres attached to the stalk of a lotus.<BR>n. (-लं) The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>“वीरणमूले”.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A small fibre in the stalk of the water-lily. E.<BR>मृण् to hurt, Unādi aff. कालन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणालिका
मृणालिका f. (-का) A lotus-stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृणालिन्
मृणालिन् m. (-ली) A lotus.<BR>	 f. (-लिनी)<BR>	 1. An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>2. A place abounding with lotuses.<BR>	 3. A lotus plant.<BR> E. मृणाल a<BR>fibre, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृण्मय
मृण्मय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of earth or clay, (as porcelain, &c.)<BR> E. मृत, मयट् aff.; also मृन्मय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत|मृतं
मृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dead, expired, extinct, defunct.<BR>	 2. Calcined,<BR>reduced, (metals.)<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Solicited alms.<BR>	 2. Death.<BR> E. मृ to die,<BR>aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतक|मृतकं|मृतकः
मृतक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A dead body, a corpse.<BR>	 2. Impurity contracted by the<BR>death of a near relation.<BR> E. मृत् dead, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतकल्प|मृतकल्पः
मृतकल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) Insensible, fained.<BR> E. मृत, कल्प aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतकान्तक|मृतकांतक|मृतकान्तकः
मृतकान्तक m. (-कः) A jackal.<BR> E. मृत dead, and कान्तक fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतगृह
मृतगृह n. (-हं) A grave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतण्ड|मृतंडः|मृतण्डः
मृतण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=575-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतपा
मृतपा m. (-पाः) A man of the lowest caste, who for a subsistence coll-<BR>ects dead men's clothes; conveys dead bodies to the river side to<BR>be burnt; executes criminals, &c.<BR> E. मृत, and पा who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतमत्त|मृतमत्तः
मृतमत्त m. (-त्तः) A jackal.<BR> E. मृत a corpse, and मत्त fond of, mad for;<BR>also with कन् added मृतमत्तक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतवत्सा
मृतवत्सा f. (-त्सा) A woman or female animal, whose offspring never live long.<BR> E. मृत, वत्स young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतशङ्का
मृतशङ्का f. (-ङ्का) The fear entertained of a person's being dead.<BR> E. मृत,<BR>शङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतसञ्जीवनी|मृतसंजीवनी
मृतसञ्जीवनी f. (-नी) A Mantra for reviving the dead.<BR> E. मृत, सञ्जीवनी reviving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतस्नात|मृतस्नातः
मृतस्नात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bathed after mourning.<BR>	 2. Dying immediate-<BR>ly after ablution.<BR> E. मृत dead, स्नात bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतस्नान|मृतस्नानं
मृतस्नान n. (-नं) Funeral ablution, bathing after mourning.<BR> E. मृत dead,<BR>and स्नान bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतस्वमोक्तृ
मृतस्वमोक्तृ m. (-क्ता) The name of a royal saint.<BR> E. मृत death, स्व his own, and मोक्तृ liberator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृताण्ड|मृतांड|मृताण्डः
मृताण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The sun.<BR> E. मृत dead, and अण्ड egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतामद|मृतामदं|मृतामदः
मृतामद n. (-दं) Blue vitriol.<BR> E. मृत् earth, मद् to please, आङ् prefix, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतालक|मृतालकं
मृतालक n. (-कं) A fragrant sort of earth.<BR> E. मृत earth, अल् to adorn,<BR>causal, form, aff. अण्, and कन् added; also मृत्तालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृताशौच
मृताशौच n. (-चं) Impurity contracted through the death of a near relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृति|मृतिः
मृति f. (-तिः) Death, dying.<BR> E. मृ to die, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृतोद्भव|मृतोद्भवः
मृतोद्भव m. (-वः) The ocean.<BR> E. मृत dead, destroyed, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्कण|मृत्कणः
मृत्कण m. (-णः) A small lump of earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्कर|मृत्करः
मृत्कर m. (-रः) A potter.<BR> E. मृत earth, and कर who works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्कांस्य|मृत्कांस्यं
मृत्कांस्य n. (-स्यं) An earthen vessel, a mug, a pitcher.<BR> E. मृत् earth, and<BR>कांस्य a goblet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्किरा
मृत्किरा f. (-रा) An earth-worm.<BR> E. मृत् earth, and किर a hog, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्खलिनी
मृत्खलिनी f. (-नी) A plant, commonly Charmakasā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्ताल|मृत्तालं
मृत्ताल n. (-लं) A sort of fragrant earth; also called Surat earth.<BR> E. मृत्<BR>earth, ताल site; place of abiding; also with कन् added, मृत्तालक n.<BR>(-कं) and with a single consonant, मृतालक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्तिका
मृत्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Earth, clay, soil.<BR>	 2. A fragrant earth.<BR> E. मृत् earth<BR>and तिकन् pleonastic addition, fem. aff. टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्फली
मृत्फली f. (-ली) A sort of Costus. “कुड”<BR> E. मृत् earth, फल a fruit, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्यु|मृत्युः
मृत्यु mfn. Subst. (-त्युः-त्युः-त्यु) Death, dying.<BR>	 m. (-त्युः) YAMA, the judge<BR>of the dead.<BR> E. मृ to die, Unādi aff. त्युक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युञ्जय|मृत्युंजय|मृत्युंजयः|मृत्युञ्जयः
मृत्युञ्जय m. (-यः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. मृत्यु death, and जय conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युतूर्य्य|मृत्युतूर्य
मृत्युतूर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) The drum beaten at funerals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युनाशक|मृत्युनाशकः
मृत्युनाशक m. (-कः) Quicksilver.<BR> E. मृत्यु death, नाशक destroyer, remover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युपुष्प|मृत्युपुष्पः
मृत्युपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) Sugar-cane.<BR> E. मृत्यु death, पुष्प flower; dying after<BR>flowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युफल|मृत्युफलः
मृत्युफल n. (-लं) A sort of fruit considered as poisonous.<BR>	 f. (-ला or -ली)<BR>The plantain.<BR> E. मृत्यु death, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युभङ्गुरक|मृत्युभङ्गुरकः
मृत्युभङ्गुरक m. (-क्षः) A drum beat on funeral occasions.<BR> E. मृत्यु death,<BR>भङ्गुर crooked, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युभृत्य|मृत्युभृत्यः
मृत्युभृत्य m. (-त्यः) Sickness, malady, disease.<BR> E. मृत्यु death, भृत्य servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युवञ्चन|मृत्युवंचन|मृत्युवञ्चनः
मृत्युवञ्चन m. (-नं)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A raven or a kind of crow, the carrion<BR>crow.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR> E. मृत्यु death or decay, and<BR>वञ्चन deceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युवीज|मृत्युवीजः
मृत्युवीज m. (-जः) The bamboo.<BR> E. मृत्यु death, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्युसूति|मृत्युसूतिः
मृत्युसूति f. (-तिः) A female crab.<BR> E. मृत्य death, and सूति bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्सा
मृत्सा f. (-त्सा)<BR>	 1. Good or rich soil.<BR>	 2. A fragrant earth.<BR> E. मृत् earth, स<BR>aff. of superior quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्स्ना
मृत्स्ना f. (-त्स्ना)<BR>	 1. Good soil.<BR>	 2. A fragrant sort of earth.<BR> E. मृत् earth, स्न aff. of excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृत्स्नाभाण्डक|मृत्स्नाभाण्डकः
मृत्स्नाभाण्डक n. (-कं) A pitcher, an earthen vessel for carrying water. E.<BR>मृत्स्ना earth, भाण्डक vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्
मृद् r. 9th cl. (मृद्नाति)<BR>	 1. To grind, to powder, to reduce to dust or<BR>powder.<BR>	 2. To trample on, to tread under foot.<BR>	 3. To squeeze.<BR>	 4.<BR>To wipe away.<BR>	 5. To overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्
मृद् f. (मृद् or मृत्)<BR>	 1. Earth, soil, clay.<BR>	 2. A fragrant earth.<BR> E. मृद् to trample on, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदङ्कुर|मृदंकुरः|मृदङ्कुरः
मृदङ्कुर m. (-रः) The green pigeon, (Columba hariala, BUCH.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदङ्ग|मृदंग|मृदंगः|मृदङ्गः
मृदङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A tabour, a small drum.<BR>	 2. A double drum.<BR>	 3. A<BR>sound, a noise.<BR>	 4. A bamboo-cane.<BR> E. मृद् to be trampled on, to be<BR>beat, Unādi aff. अङ्गच्; also with कन् added मृदङ्गक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदङ्गफल|मृदंगफल|मृदङ्गफलः
मृदङ्गफल m. (-लः) The jack tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR> E. मृदङ्ग a<BR>drum, and फल a fruit; perhaps alluding to its size and shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदर
मृदर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Sportive, sporting.<BR>	 2. Passing quickly away,<BR>transient.<BR> E. मृ to die, दर Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदा
मृदा f. (-दा) Earth, clay, soil.<BR> E. मृद् to trample on, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदाकर|मृदाकरः
मृदाकर m. (-रः) The thunderbolt.<BR> E. मृदा earth, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदित|मृदितः
मृदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rubbed, ground.<BR>	 2. Trodden or trampled on.<BR>3. Pressed.<BR> E. मृद् to reduce to powder, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदिनी
मृदिनी f. (-नी) Good soil or earth.<BR> E. मृद् earth, इनि aff., fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदु|मृदुः
मृदु mfn. (-दुः-द्वी-दु)<BR>	 1. Soft.<BR>	 2. Blunt, not sharp.<BR>	 3. Gentle, mild.<BR>	 4.<BR>Slow, weak.<BR>	 f. (-द्वी) The brown grape.<BR>	 m. (-दुः) The planet Saturn.<BR>E. मृद् to rub, aff. कु, and the semi-vowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुकृष्णायस|मृदुकृष्णायसं
मृदुकृष्णायस n. (-सं) Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुकोष्ठ
मृदुकोष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A man of lax bowels, one easily affected by medicine.<BR>E. मृदु, and कोष्ठ intestinal canal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुगमना
मृदुगमना f. (-ना) A goose, a swan.<BR> E. मृदु soft, गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुचर्म्मिन्|मृदुचर्मिन्
मृदुचर्म्मिन् m. (-र्म्मी) The Bhurja-patra-tree.<BR> E. मृदु soft, चर्म्म skin or bark इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुच्छद|मृदुच्छदः
मृदुच्छद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The Bhurja-patra or brich tree.<BR>	 2. A kind of Pīlu,<BR>or tree growing in the hills.<BR> E. मृदु soft, and च्छद covering or bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुता
मृदुता f. (-ता) Softness.<BR> E. तल् added to मृदु; also with त्व, मृदुत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुत्वच|मृदुत्वचः
मृदुत्वच m. (-चः) The Bhurjapatra or brich tree, the bark of which<BR>peels off, and is used in making Hooka-snakes, &c.<BR> E. मृदु soft,<BR>and त्वच skin; also with a final consonant, मृदुत्वच् m. (-त्यक्) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुन्नक|मृदुन्नकं
मृदुन्नक n. (-कं) Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुपर्व्वन्|मृदुपर्वन्
मृदुपर्व्वन् n. (-र्व्व) A cane or ratan; also मृदुपर्वक m. (-कः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुपाणि
मृदुपाणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) Having a soft and delicate hand.<BR> E. मृदु and<BR>पाणि hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुपुष्प|मृदुपुष्पः
मृदुपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) The Sirisha tree, (Mimosa sirisha.)<BR> E. मृदु soft, पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुरोमवत्|मृदुरोमवन्त्
मृदुरोमवत् m. (-वान्) A hare.<BR> E. मृदु soft, रोमन् hair, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुल|मृदुलं
मृदुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Soft.<BR>	 2. Mild, gentle.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of aloe-wood.<BR> E. मृदु soft, and कुलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुलोमक|मृदुलोमकः
मृदुलोमक m. (-कः) A hare.<BR> E. मृदु soft, लोम hair, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदुवात
मृदुवात m. (-तः) A gentle breeze, zephyr.<BR> E. मृदु soft, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृदूत्पल|मृदूत्पलं
मृदूत्पल n. (-लं) The blue lotus, (Nymphæa cærulea.)<BR> E. मृदु, उत्पल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्भाण्ड|मृद्भांड
मृद्भाण्ड m. (-ण्डं) An earthen vessel.<BR> E. मृत् and भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्वङ्ग|मृद्वंग|मृद्वङ्गं
मृद्वङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Of soft or tender frame or body.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी) A<BR>delicate woman.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं) Tin.<BR> E. मृदु soft, अङ्ग body, substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृद्वीका
मृद्वीका f. (-का) A grape.<BR> E. मृद् to hurt, कीकन् aff. and उक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृध्
मृध् (उ) मृधु r. 1st. cl. [मर्द्ध(र्ध)ति-ते] 1. To be moist or wet.<BR>	 2. To hurt or<BR>kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृध|मृधं
मृध n. (-धं) War, battle.<BR> E. मृध् to hurt, or kill, aff. ध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृन्मरु|मृन्मरुः
मृन्मरु m. (-रुः) A stone, a rock.<BR> E. मृद् earth and मरु dry as a desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृल्लोष्ट|मृल्लोष्टः
मृल्लोष्ट n. (-ष्टं) A clod of earth or clay.<BR> E. मृत् and लोष्ट a lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृश्
मृश् (औ) मृशौ r. 6th cl. (मृशति)<BR>	 1. To touch.<BR>	 2. To see, to perceive.<BR>	 3.<BR>To consult, to consider, to deliberate. With परा, to counsel, to<BR>advise. With वि, 1. To consider, to discuss.<BR>	 2. To touch.<BR>	 3. To<BR>observe.<BR>	 4. To examine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्
मृष् r. 1st and 10th cls. (मर्षति-ते मर्षयति-ते) and 4th cl. (मृष्यति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>bear, to suffer, to endure patiently.<BR>	 2. To permit.<BR>	 3. To pardon.<BR>(उ) मृषु r. 1st cl. (मर्षति-ते) To sprinkle. With आङ्, To be angry.<BR>With वि, To be distressed, to bear hardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषा
मृषा Ind.<BR>	 1. Falsely.<BR>	 2. Uselessly, in vain.<BR> E. मृष् to bear, with का, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषाध्यायिन्
मृषाध्यायिन् m. (-यी) A species of crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषार्थक|मृषार्थकं
मृषार्थक n. (-कं) An impossibility, an absurdity, (in speech or composi-<BR>tion;) the sense of which is evidently false, as कूर्म्मलोमतनुत्राणः, शश-<BR>शृङ्गधनुर्धरः, his armour is of tortoise wool, and his bow the horn<BR>of a hare.<BR> E. मृषा falsely, अर्थ meaning, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=576-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषालक|मृषालकः
मृषालक m. (-कः) The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषावाद|मृषावादः
मृषावाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Irony, ironical praise.<BR>	 2. Falsehood.<BR>	 3. Flattery. E.<BR>मृषा falsely, वाद speech, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषावादिन्
मृषावादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Speaking falsely, lying, a liar.<BR>	 m. (-दी)<BR>A false accuser, one who brings forward an unjust or unfounded<BR>accusation.<BR> E. मृषा falsely, and वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषोद्य|मृषोद्यं|मृषोद्यः
मृषोद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Speaking falsely, lying, a liar, a flatterer.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-द्यं) Falsehood.<BR> E. मृष् falsely, वद् to speak, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्ट|मृष्टं|मृष्टः
मृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Cleaned, cleansed.<BR>	 2. Touched, rubbed.<BR>	 3. Sprin-<BR>kled.<BR>	 4. Cooked.<BR>	 5. Considered, deliberated.<BR>	 6. Agreeable.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-ष्टं) Pepper.<BR> E. मृज् to clean, or मृष् to rub, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टि|मृष्टिः
मृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Touching, contact.<BR>	 2. Cleaning.<BR>	 3. Sprinkling.<BR>	 4.<BR>Preparing the food for a meal.<BR> E. मृज् to clean, or मृष् to sprin-<BR>kle, &c., क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टेरुक|मृष्टेरुकः
मृष्टेरुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A liberal man, a donor, a benefactor.<BR>	 2. A chur-<BR>lish or inhospitable man.<BR>	 3. An eater of sweetmeats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मॄ
मॄ r. 9th cl. (मृणाति) To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मे
मे r. 1st cl. (मयते)<BR>	 1. To barter or exchange.<BR>	 2. To return, to restore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेक|मेकः
मेक m. (-कः) A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकल|मेकलः
मेकल mf. (-लः-ला)<BR>	 1. Name of a certain part of Vindhya mountain.<BR>	 2. A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकलकन्यका
मेकलकन्यका f. (-का) The Narmadā river.<BR> E. मेकल or मेखल the name of<BR>a Ṛṣi the supposed father, or of a mountain, the source of the<BR>stream, and कन्यका daughter; hence also मेखककन्यका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकलाद्रिजा
मेकलाद्रिजा f. (-जा) The Narmadā river.<BR> E. मेकलाद्रि the Mekala moun-<BR>tain, part of the Vindhya range, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखला
मेखला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A woman's girdle or zone.<BR>	 2. A sword-knot, a string<BR>or chain fastened to the hilt, and in fighting bound round the<BR>wrist to secure the weapon.<BR>	 3. A sword-belt.<BR>	 4. The slope of<BR>a mountain.<BR>	 5. The Narmadā river.<BR>	 6. The sacrificial string<BR>of a Brāhmana when made of deer-skin.<BR>	 7. A sort of figure,<BR>made on the four sides of the hole in which sacrificial fire is<BR>offered.<BR>	 8. A triple zone or string worn round the loins by the<BR>three first classes; the girdle of the Brāhmana should be of the<BR>fibres of the Munja or of Kuśa grass, that of the Kṣatriya of<BR>a Mūrvā, and that of the Vaiśya of a thread of the Śaṇa, &c.<BR>9. The girth of a horse.<BR>	 10. The hips.<BR> E. मि to scatter, खलच् aff.,<BR>deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलापद
मेखलापद n. (-दं) The hip and loins.<BR> E. मेखला a zone, and पद place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलिन्
मेखलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Wearing a girdle.<BR>	 m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A youth of<BR>the Brāhmana tribe, who previous to his marriage wears a girdle<BR>suited to his caste.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR> E. मेखला, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघ|मेघः
मेघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>	 3.<BR>A demon, a goblin.<BR>	 4. A mass, a multitude.<BR>	 n. (-घं) Talc.<BR> E. मिह् to<BR>sprinkle, aff. अच्, and the final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघकफ|मेघकफः
मेघकफ m. (-फः) Hail.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and कफ phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघकाल|मेघकालः
मेघकाल m. (-लः) The rains, the rainy season.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघगर्ज्जन|मेघगर्जन
मेघगर्ज्जन fn. (-ना-नं) Thunder.<BR> E. मेघ, गर्ज्जन noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघङ्कर|मेघंकर
मेघङ्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Cloud-producing, (rainy season.)<BR> E. मेघ, कृ to make, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघचिन्तक|मेघचिंतक|मेघचिन्तकः
मेघचिन्तक m. (-कः) The Chātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucus.)<BR> E. मेघ a<BR>cloud, चिन्तक who think of; being supposed to drink no water<BR>but rain, and therefore naturally anxious for cloudy and rainy<BR>weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघज|मेघजं|मेघजः
मेघज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Cloud-born, produced in or from the clouds.<BR>m. (-जः) A large pearl.<BR> E. मेघ, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघजाल|मेघजालं
मेघजाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Talc.<BR>	 2. A mass of clouds.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and जाल a<BR>net; some copies read मेधनाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघजीवक|मेघजीवकः
मेघजीवक(न) m. (-कः or नः) The Chātaka.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, जीवक living,<BR>or जीवन life: see मेघचिन्तक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघज्योतिस्
मेघज्योतिस् m. (-तिः) A flash of lightning or the fire of it.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, ज्योतिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघडम्बर|मेघडंबर|मेघडम्बरः
मेघडम्बर m. (-रः) Thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघतिमिर|मेघतिमिरं
मेघतिमिर n. (-रं) Cloudiness, cloudy or rainy weather.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud,<BR>तिमिर darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघदीप|मेघदीपः
मेघदीप m. (-पः) Lightning.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and दीप inflamer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघद्वार
मेघद्वार n. (-रं) Sky, heaven, ether.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and द्वार the gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनाद|मेघनादः
मेघनाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The son of RĀVAṆA.<BR>	 2. A name of VARUṆA, the<BR>deity of water.<BR>	 3. The noise or grumbling of clouds.<BR>	 4. The Palā-<BR>śha tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>	 5. A sort of amaranth, (Amaranthus<BR>Polygamus.)<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and नाद sound or noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनादजित्
मेघनादजित् m. (-जित्) LAKSHMAṆA, the favourite brother and com-<BR>panion of RĀMA.<BR> E. मेघनाद the son of RĀVANA, जित् conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनादानुलासिन्
मेघनादानुलासिन् m. (-सी) A peacock.<BR> E. मेघनाद the muttering of clouds,<BR>अनुलस to be delighted by, णिनि aff.; pairing in the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनामन्
मेघनामन् m. (-मा) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. मेघ a cloud,<BR>and नामन् appellation, or it may apply to every term for a cloud,<BR>being a synonym of the grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघनिर्घोष|मेघनिर्घोषः
मेघनिर्घोष m. (-षः) The muttering or grumbling of clouds, low or dis-<BR>tant thunder.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and निर्घोष sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघपुष्प|मेघपुष्पं|मेघपुष्पः
मेघपुष्प n. (-ष्पं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. River-water.<BR>	 3. Hail.<BR>	 m. (-ष्पः) One of<BR>VIṢṆU'S horses.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघप्रसव|मेघप्रसवः
मेघप्रसव m. (-वः) Water.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and प्रसव a parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघभूति|मेघभूतिः
मेघभूति m. (-तिः) The thunderbolt.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and भूति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघमाला
मेघमाला f. (-ला) A gathering or succession of clouds.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud,<BR>माला a necklace or garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघयोनि|मेघयोनिः
मेघयोनि m. (-निः) Smoke, fog.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, योनि place of birth or production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघराग|मेघरागः
मेघराग m. (-गः) One of the six modes of music.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, राग<BR>mode; being supposed capable of bringing down rain from<BR>heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवर्णा|मेघवर्ण्णा
मेघवर्णा f. (-र्णा) The indigo-plant.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and वर्णा colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवर्त्मन्
मेघवर्त्मन् n. (-र्त्म) Sky, atmosphere.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and वर्त्मन् road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवह्नि|मेघवह्निः
मेघवह्नि m. (-ह्निः) The fire of lightning.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, वह्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवाहन|मेघवाहनः
मेघवाहन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, वाहन<BR>vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघविस्फुर्ज्जित
मेघविस्फुर्ज्जित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Thunder.<BR>	 2. A species of the Atidhritī metre.<BR>E. मेघ, and विस्फुर्ज्जित bursting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघवेश्मन्
मेघवेश्मन् n. (-श्म) Sky, atmosphere.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and वेश्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघसार|मेघसारः
मेघसार m. (-रः) A kind of camphor. “चीनकर्पूरे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघसुहृद्
मेघसुहृद् m. (-हृद्) A peacock.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and सुहृद् a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघस्तनित
मेघस्तनित n. (-तं) Thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघाख्य|मेघाख्यं
मेघाख्य n. (-ख्यं) Talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघागम|मेघागमः
मेघागम m. (-मः) The rains, the rainy season.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and आगम arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघाटोप|मेघाटोपः
मेघाटोप m. (-पः) A dense cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघानन्दिन्|मेघानंदिन्
मेघानन्दिन् m. (-न्दी) A peacock.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, and आनन्दिन् delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघान्त|मेघांत|मेघान्तः
मेघान्त m. (-न्तः) The autumn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघारि|मेघारिः
मेघारि m. (-रिः) Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघास्थि
मेघास्थि n. (-स्थि) Hail.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघास्पद|मेघास्पदं
मेघास्पद n. (-दं) Heaven, ether, sky, atmosphere.<BR> E. मेघ a cloud, आस्पद place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघोदर|मेघोदरः
मेघोदर m. (-रः) The father of the fifth Jina or Jaina saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेचक|मेचकं|मेचकः
मेचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Black, dark, of a dark, or black colour.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. Black or dark-blue, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. The eye of a peacock's tail.<BR>3. A cloud.<BR>	 4. Smoke.<BR>	 5. A nipple.<BR>	 6. A plant, (Hyperanthera<BR>morunga.)<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं) Darkness.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Sulphuret of antimony.<BR>E. मच् to mix, Unādi aff. वुन्, and the vowel changed to ए ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेचकापगा
मेचकापगा f. (-गा) The Yamunā river.<BR> E. मेचक dark, and अपगा the river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेट्
मेट् (ऋ) मेटृ r. 1st. cl. (मेटति) To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेटुला
मेटुला f. (-ला) A tree, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>	 2. The emblic myrobalan-<BR>tree.<BR> E. मेट् to be mad, उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेठ|मेठः
मेठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. An elephant-keeper or feeder.<BR>	 2. A ram; also मेण्ठ and मेण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेड्
मेड् (ऋ) मेडृ r. 1st cl. (मेडति) To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेढ्र|मेढ्रः
मेढ्र m. (-ढ्रः)<BR>	 1. The penis.<BR>	 2. A ram.<BR> E. मिह् to urine, ष्ट्रन् aff.; also with कन्, मेढ्रक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेढ्रचर्मन्
मेढ्रचर्मन् n. (-र्म) The prepuce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=577-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेढ्रशृङ्गी
मेढ्रशृङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A milky plant, the fruit of which is crooked, and<BR>therefore compared to a ram's horn, (Asclepias geminata.) E.<BR>मेढ्र a ram, शृङ्गी a horn, ङीप् aff. “गाडरशिङा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ठ|मेंठ|मेंठः|मेण्ठः
मेण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) An elephant-keeper: also read मेठ as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ड|मेंड|मेंडः|मेण्डः
मेण्ड m. (-ण्डः) An elephant-keeper or feeder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेण्ढ|मेंढ|मेंढः|मेण्ढः
मेण्ढ m. (-ण्ढः) A ram.<BR> E. मिह् to urine, घञ् aff., नुम् inserted and the<BR>final changed; also with कन् added मेण्ढक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेथ्
मेथ् (ऋ) मेथृ r. 1st cl. (मेथति-ते)<BR>	 1. To understand to comprehend.<BR>	 2.<BR>To hurt, to injure.<BR>	 3. To kill.<BR>	 4. To associate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेथि|मेथिः
मेथि m. (-थिः)<BR>	 1. A pillar in the centre of a threshing floor, round which<BR>the cattle turn to tread out the corn.<BR>	 2. A prop for supporting<BR>the shafts of a carriage.<BR>	 f. (-थी) A sort of grass, (Trigonella<BR>fœnugræcum.)<BR> E. मथ् to understand, &c. इन् aff., fem. aff. ङीष्;<BR>also with कन् added in the fem. form मेथिका; also मेधि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेद्
मेद् (ऋ) मेदृ r. 1st cl. (मेदति-ते)<BR>	 1. To understand.<BR>	 2. To kill or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेद|मेदः
मेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Adeps, fat, the supposed proper seat of which is the<BR>abdomen.<BR>	 2. One of the outcast tribes.<BR>	 f. (-दा) A drug, described<BR>as a sort of root resembling ginger, brought from the Morung<BR>district; it is one of the eight principal medicaments, and is said<BR>to be of cooling and emollient properties, and of particular use in<BR>fever and consumption.<BR> E. मिद to be greasy or unctuous, aff. घञ्;<BR>also मेदस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदक|मेदकः
मेदक m. (-कः) Vinous liquor for distilling.<BR> E. मिद् to be unctuous, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदस्
मेदस् n. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Marrow; applicable not merely to the marrow of<BR>the bones, but more properly, to the serous or adipose secretion<BR>that spreads amongst the muscular fibres, and which is consi-<BR>dered as performing the same functions to the flesh that the<BR>marrow of the bones performs to them: in Hindu physiology its<BR>proper seat is said to be the abdomen.<BR>	 2. Morbid or unnatural<BR>corpulency.<BR> E. मिद् to be unctuous, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदस्कृत्
मेदस्कृत् n. (-स्कृत्) Flesh.<BR> E. मेदस् adeps, and कृत् made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदस्विन्
मेदस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>	 1. Robust, stout, strong.<BR>	 2. Fat, corpulent.<BR>E. मेदस् and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदिनी
मेदिनी f. (-नी) The earth.<BR> E. मेदस् adeps, इनि and ङीप् affs.; being<BR>made, according to the legend, of the adeps of two demons slain<BR>by BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदिनीद्रव|मेदिनीद्रवः
मेदिनीद्रव m. (-वः) Dust.<BR> E. मेदिनी the earth, and द्रु to get, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदुर|मेदुरः
मेदुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Smooth, soft, bland, unctuous, saponaceous, &c.<BR>E. मिद् to be unctuous, घुरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोग्रन्थि|मेदोग्रंथि|मेदोग्रन्थिः
मेदोग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) A fatty tumor.<BR> E. मेदस्, and ग्रन्थि knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोज|मेदोजं
मेदोज n. (-जं) A bone.<BR> E. मेदस् marrow, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोधरा
मेदोधरा f. (-रा) A membrane in the abdomen, containing the fat,<BR>the omentum.<BR> E. मेदस्, धरा what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोर्व्वुद
मेदोऽर्व्वुद n. (-दं) Fatty tumours unattended with pain.<BR> E. मेदस्, अर्व्वुद a tumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोवह
मेदोवह n. (-हं) A vessel carrying fat, a lymphatic.<BR> E. मेदस्, and वह what<BR>bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेदोवृद्धि|मेदोवृद्धिः
मेदोवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Corpulence.<BR>	 2. Enlargement of the scrotum.<BR> E. मेदस् वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेद्य
मेद्य f. (-द्या)<BR>	 1. Fat 2. Thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध्
मेध् (ऋ) मेधृ r. 1st cl. (मेधति-ते)<BR>	 1. To understand, to comprehend.<BR>	 2.<BR>To associate.<BR>	 3. To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध|मेधः
मेध m. (-धः) Sacrifice, offering oblation.<BR>	 f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. Apprehension, con-<BR>ception, understanding.<BR>	 2. Retentiveness.<BR> E. मेध् to associate,<BR>aff. अप् or अङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधाजित्
मेधाजित् m. (-जित्) The name of a saint and grammarian; also KĀTYĀ-<BR>YANA.<BR> E. मेधा apprehension, and जित् victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधारुद्र|मेधारुद्रः
मेधारुद्र m. (-द्रः) The poet KĀLIDĀSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधाविन्
मेधाविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Intelligent, comprehending, ready compre-<BR>hension or conception.<BR>	 m. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A parrot.<BR>	 2. A learned man, a<BR>sage.<BR>	 3. Intoxicating beverage.<BR>	 4. The inspired writer Vyāri.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी) The wife of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. मेधा apprehension, विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधि|मेधिः
मेधि m. (-धिः) A post fixed in the centre of a threshing floor or barn<BR>to which the cattle are attached, as they turn round it to tread<BR>out the corn.<BR> E. मेध to associate or connect, (the oxen, &c.) इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेधिर|मेधिरः
मेधिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Intelligent, possessing a ready and just appre-<BR>hension.<BR> E. मेधा apprehension, इरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेध्य|मेध्यं|मेध्यः
मेध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Pure, purified.<BR>	 2. Fit for a sacrifice or obla-<BR>tion.<BR>	 f. (-ध्या) A kind of orris root, described as the red sort.<BR>	 3. A<BR>sort of pigment: see रोचना.<BR>	 m. (-ध्यः)<BR>	 1. Khayer, (Mimosa cate-<BR>chu.)<BR>	 2. Barley.<BR>	 3. A goat.<BR> E. मेध् to associate, aff. ण्यत्; or मेध a<BR>sacrifice, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनका
मेनका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. One of the courtezans of Svarga.<BR>	 2. Name of the wife<BR>of Himālaya.<BR> E. मे to me, का any one, न not, (equal or com-<BR>parable.); or मि-नक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनकात्मजा
मेनकात्मजा f. (-जा) DURGĀ or PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. मेनका the wife of the perso-<BR>nified mountain, and आत्मजा daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनकाप्राणेश|मेनकाप्राणेशः
मेनकाप्राणेश m. (-शः) The personified Himālaya mountain.<BR> E. मेनका, प्राणेश husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनजा
मेनजा f. (-जा) PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. मेना, the mother of the goddess, जा born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेना
मेना f. (-ना) The wife of Himālaya: see मेनका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनाद|मेनादः
मेनाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A cat.<BR>	 2. A goat.<BR>	 3. A peacock.<BR> E. मे imitative cry,<BR>mew, नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेनाधव|मेनाधवः
मेनाधव m. (-वः) Himālaya the personified mountain and father of<BR>DURGĀ as PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. मेना the wife of the mountain, and धव<BR>husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेन्धी|मेंधी
मेन्धी f. (-न्धी) A plant, from the leaves of which a reddish dye is pre-<BR>pared, with which the palms of the hands, tips of the fingers,<BR>soles of the feet, and fingernails are stained, (Lawsonia inermis;)<BR>also मेन्धिका । मा लक्ष्मीः इध्यते यया इन्ध् घञ् गौरा० ङीष् “मेइदी ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेप्
मेप् (ऋ) मेपृ r. 1st cl. (मेपते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेब्
मेब् (ऋ) मेबृ r. 1st cl. (मेबते) To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेय
मेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Measurable, what is to be measured.<BR> E. मा to measure, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरक|मेरकः
मेरक m. (-कः) An Asura and foe to VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरु|मेरुः
मेरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. The sacred mountain Meru, in the centre of the seven<BR>continents, compared to the cup or seed-vessel of the lotus, the<BR>leaves of which are formed by the different Dwipas: its height<BR>is said by the Hindus to be 84,000 Yojanas, sixteen thousand<BR>of which are below the surface of the earth: the shape is various-<BR>ly described, as square, conical, columnar, spherical, or spiral;<BR>and the four faces of it are of various colours, or white towards<BR>the east, yellow to the south, black to the west, and red towards<BR>the north: the river Ganges falls from heaven on its summit,<BR>and flows thence to the surrounding worlds in four streams; the<BR>southern branch is the Ganges of India, the northern running into<BR>Tartary is the Bhadrasomā, the eastern is the Sitā, and the wes-<BR>tern the Chacshu or Oxus: on the summit of Meru BRAHMĀ re-<BR>sides attended and worshipped by the Ṛṣis, Gandharbas, &c.;<BR>the regents of the points of the compass occupy the correspond-<BR>ing faces of the mountain, the whole of which consists of gold and<BR>gems: considered in any but a fabulous light, mount Meru<BR>appears to mean the high land of Tartary, immediately to the<BR>north of the Himālaya mountains.<BR>	 2. The central bead in a rosary.<BR>3. The middle gem in a necklace.<BR> E. मि to scatter, (radiance,)<BR>Unādi aff. रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरुक|मेरुकः
मेरुक m. (-कः) Fragrant resin, incense.<BR> E. मेरु mount Meru, कन् aff. “यक्षधूपे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेरुयन्त्र
मेरुयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A spindle.<BR> E. मेरु and यन्त्र implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेल|मेलः
मेल mf. (-लः-ला) Meeting, union, assemblage; in the modern dialects,<BR>applied to a large concourse of people collected at stated periods<BR>for religious or commercial purposes, as at Haridwār, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>1. Ink.<BR>	 2. Antimony or any collyrium.<BR>	 3. Union, intercourse.<BR>	 4. A<BR>company, a society.<BR>	 5. The indigo-plant.<BR>	 6. A musical scale. E.<BR>मिल to mix, to meet, aff. घञ्; also with ल्युट् aff. मेलन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=578-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलक|मेलकः
मेलक m. (-कः) Meeting, union, assemblage.<BR> E. मेल the same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलन|मेलनं
मेलन n. (-नं) Meeting assembling.<BR>	 2. Encounter.<BR>	 3. Associating with.<BR>4. Mixing with 5. Adding to.<BR> E. मिल to mix, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलयत्
मेलयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Mixing, adding, or causing to be mixed<BR>with, or added to.<BR> E. मिल् to mix, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलानन्द|मेलानंद|मेलानन्दः
मेलानन्द mf. (-न्दः-न्दा) An inkstand.<BR> E. मेला ink, आनन्द delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलान्धु|मेलान्धुः
मेलान्धु f. (-न्धुः) An inkstand.<BR> E. मेला ink, अन्धु a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेलाम्बु|मेलांबु|मेलाम्बुः
मेलाम्बु m. (-म्बुः) An inkstand.<BR> E. मेला ink, अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेव्
मेव् (ऋ) मेवृ r. 1st cl. (मेवते) To serve, to gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेष|मेषः
मेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A ram.<BR>	 2. The sign Aries.<BR>	 3. A kind of drug.<BR>	 f. (-षा)<BR>A sort of small cardamom, brought from Guzerāt.<BR>	 f. (-षी) An<BR>ewe.<BR> E. मिष् to contend with, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषविषाणिका
मेषविषाणिका f. (-का) A plant: see मेढ्रशृङ्गी.<BR> E. मेष a ram, विषाण a horn, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषशृङ्ग|मेषशृङ्गः
मेषशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A sort of poison.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी) A kind of creeping plant,<BR>(Asclepias geminata, &c.;) see मेढ्रशृङ्गी.<BR> E. मेष a ram, शृङ्ग horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषाक्षिकुसुम|मेषाक्षिकुसुमः
मेषाक्षिकुसुम m. (-मः) A sort of Cassia, (C. tora.)<BR> E. मेष a ram, अक्षि the<BR>eye, and कुसुम a flower; which is compared to a sheep's eye; also<BR>analogous terms as मेषलोचन, &c.; it is also read मेषाख्य and<BR>मेषाह्व, &c., as being named from the Mesa or ram. “चक्रमर्दे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषाण्ड|मेषांड|मेषाण्डः
मेषाण्ड m. (-ण्डः) INDRA.<BR> E. मेष a ram, and अण्ड the testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषालु|मेषालुः
मेषालु m. (-लुः) A sort of shrub, commonly Ververa or Barbari,<BR>(Ocimum pilosum.)<BR> E. मेष a ram, and आलु esculent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेषिका
मेषिका f. (-का) An ewe.<BR> E. मेषी an ewe, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेह|मेहः
मेह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Urinary disease, especially inflammatory affection of<BR>the urethra, including gonorrhœa, &c.<BR>	 2. A ram.<BR>	 3. A goat.<BR>	 4.<BR>Urine, piss.<BR> E. मिह् to pass as urine, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहत्
मेहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्) Urining, passing urine.<BR> E. मिह् to urine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहन|मेहनं|मेहनः
मेहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Membrum virile.<BR>	 2. Urine, piss.<BR>	 3. Passing urine,<BR>pissing.<BR> E. मिह् to urine, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेहिन्
मेहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>	 1. Urining.<BR>	 2. Suffering from urinary affec-<BR>tions.<BR> E. मेह, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्र|मैत्रं|मैत्रः
मैत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) Of or belonging to a friend, friendly, amicable.<BR>m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A Brāhmana.<BR>	 2. A mixed caste.<BR>	 3. The anus.<BR>	 nf.<BR>(-त्रं-त्री)<BR>	 1. Friendship.<BR>	 2. Evacuation of excrement.<BR>	 3. Union.<BR>	 4. A<BR>name of the seventeenth lunar asterism, (see the next.)<BR> E. मित्र a<BR>friend, or the sun and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रभ|मैत्रभं
मैत्रभ n. (-भं) The seventeenth lunar asterism; also ANURĀDHĀ.<BR> E. मित्र<BR>the deity, presiding over the asterism, अण् aff. of relation, मैत्र be-<BR>longing to Mitra, and भ an asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेत्रावरुण
मेत्रावरुण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A name of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>	 2. VĀLMĪKI.<BR>	 3.<BR>One of the officiating priests at a sacrifice.<BR> E. मित्र the sun, वरुण<BR>the deity of water, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रावरुणि|मैत्रावरुणिः
मैत्रावरुणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A name of AGASTYA.<BR>	 2. VĀLMĪKI.<BR>	 3. VAŚISTHA.<BR>E. मित्रवरुण a sage, the father of this saint, and इञ् aff.; or मित्र<BR>the sun, and वरुण VARUṆA, alluding to a legend of the birth of<BR>the saint from a contest between these deities, for the posses-<BR>sion of URVASĪ, one of the courtezans of INDRA'S heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रीवल
मैत्रीवल m. (-लः) A Buddha or Bauddha deified saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रेय|मैत्रेयः
मैत्रेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Of or relating to a friend.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A man of<BR>a mixed caste, the son of a Vaideha by an Ayogava mother: his<BR>business is to announce the hours in verse.<BR>	 2. The seventh Bud-<BR>dha, or one still to come.<BR>	 3. The name of a saint or Muni, the<BR>disciple of PARĀSARA, to whom the Viṣṇu Purāna is narra-<BR>ted.<BR> E. मित्र a proper name, or मित्र a friend, and ढक् aff. of descent<BR>or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रेयक|मैत्रेयकः
मैत्रेयक m. (-कः) A crier or chanter of the hours: see the last.<BR> E. मैत्रेय, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्रेयिका
मैत्रेयिका f. (-का) The contest of friends or allies.<BR> E. मैत्रेय relating to<BR>friends, वुञ् aff. of animosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैत्र्य|मैत्र्यं
मैत्र्य nf. (-त्र्यं-त्री) Friendship.<BR> E. मित्र friend, ष्यञ् aff. of property, fem.<BR>aff. ङीष्, and the semi-vowel of the aff. rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथिल|मैथिलः
मैथिल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Belonging to, born in, &c. Mithilā.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A<BR>name of ŚITĀ.<BR> E. मिथिला, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुन|मैथुनं
मैथुन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Copulation.<BR>	 2. Union, association.<BR>	 3. Marriage.<BR> E. मिथुन a couple, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुनज्वर|मैथुनज्वरः
मैथुनज्वर m. (-रः) The excitement of sexual passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैथुनिका
मैथुनिका f. (-का) Union by marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैधावक|मैधावकं
मैधावक n. (-कं) Wisdom, prudence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनाक|मैनाकः
मैनाक m. (-कः) A mountain, or rock in the sea between the southern<BR>end of the Peninsula, and Lankā.<BR> E. मेनका the wife of Himālaya,<BR>अण् aff. of descent, being in mythology her son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनाकस्वसृ
मैनाकस्वसृ f. (-सा) The goddess DURGĀ as PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. मैनाक, स्वसृ sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनाद
मैनाद m. (-दः) A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैनिक|मैनिकः
मैनिक m. (-कः) A fisherman.<BR> E. मीन a fish, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैन्द|मैंद|मैंदः|मैन्दः
मैन्द m. (-न्दः) The name of a demon killed by KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैन्दहन्|मैंदहन्
मैन्दहन् m. (-हा) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. मैन्द as above, and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैरेय|मैरेयं|मैरेयः
मैरेय n. (-यं) A sort of spirituous liquor, prepared from the blossoms<BR>of the Lythrum fruticosum, with sugar, &c.<BR> E. मिरा said to be<BR>the name of a country or drug, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मैलिन्द|मैलिंद|मैलिंदः|मैलिन्दः
मैलिन्द m. (-न्दः) A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक|मोकं
मोक n. (-कं) The cast-off skin of an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्तव्य
मोक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be loosed or let go, to be liberated. E.<BR>मुच् to let go, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्ष्
मोक्ष् r. 1st and 10th cls. (मोक्षति मोक्षयति-ते) To let go, to release, to dis-<BR>charge, to send, to cast or throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्ष|मोक्षः
मोक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. Final and eternal happiness, the liberation of the soul<BR>from the body, and its exemption from further transmigration.<BR>2. Death.<BR>	 3. Libertion, freedom.<BR>	 4. Loosening, untying.<BR>	 5. End of<BR>an eclipse.<BR>	 6. Scattering.<BR>	 7. Shooting.<BR>	 8. A plant commonly<BR>Ghaṇtāpārali.<BR>	 9. Acquittance of an obligation, as by a son<BR>to his father.<BR> E. मोक्ष् to let loose or free, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षक|मोक्षकः
मोक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what sets at liberty.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A deli-<BR>verer, a liberator.<BR> E. मोक्ष्, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षण|मोक्षणं
मोक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Letting go or free, liberating.<BR>	 2. Squandering.<BR>	 3.<BR>Giving up.<BR>	 4. Causing to flow.<BR> E. मोक्ष् to let go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षणीय
मोक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be, or what may be liberated.<BR> E. मोक्ष, अनी-<BR>यर् aff.; also मोक्ष्य, and मोक्षितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षित
मोक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Let go, liberated.<BR> E. मोक्ष, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोक्षोपाय|मोक्षोपायः
मोक्षोपाय m. (-यः) A sage, a devotee.<BR> E. मोक्ष emancipation, उपाय means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघ|मोघं|मोघः
मोघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं)<BR>	 1. Vain, useless, fruitless.<BR>	 2. Left, abandoned.<BR>3. Idle.<BR>	 f. (-घा) Trumpet-flower, (Bignonia suave olens.)<BR>	 m. (-घः) A<BR>fence, a hedge.<BR> E. मुह् to be foolish, aff. अच् and the final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघकर्म्मन्|मोघकर्मन्
मोघकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Following vain practices, observing useless<BR>ceremonies.<BR> E. मोघ, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघज्ञान
मोघज्ञान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Cultivating vain knowledge or any but re-<BR>ligious wisdom.<BR> E. मोघ, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघपुष्पा
मोघपुष्पा f. (-ष्पा) A barren woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघाश
मोघाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Indulging vain hopes.<BR> E. मीघ, and आशा hope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोघोली
मोघोली m. (-ली) A fence, a hedge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोच|मोचं|मोचः
मोच m. (-चः) A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>	 f. (-चा)<BR>	 1. The silk-<BR>cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>	 2. The plantain, (Musa<BR>sapientum.)<BR>	 3. The indigo-plant.<BR>	 n. (-चं) A plantain, (the fruit.) E.<BR>मुच् to loose, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचक|मोचकः
मोचक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>	 2. The silk-cotton<BR>tree.<BR>	 3. The plantain tree.<BR>	 4. A plant, commonly Ghantāpāralī.<BR>5. A devotee, one who has divested himself of worldly passion and<BR>desire.<BR>	 6. A liberator.<BR> E. मुच् to be let loose, aff. ण्वुल्; or causal<BR>form, aff. अच्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचन|मोचनं
मोचन n. (-नं) Liberating, setting free.<BR> E. मुच् to be free, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचनीय
मोचनीय mfn. (-यः-या-य)<BR>	 1. To be liberated or let loose.<BR>	 2. To be resign-<BR>ed or given up.<BR> E. मुच् to be loose, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचरस|मोचरसः
मोचरस m. (-सः) The gum of the silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. मोच the Bombax,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">Page580-a+ 60</a>]<BR>and रस juice; also similar compounds, as मोचनिर्य्यास, मोचसार,<BR>मोचस्राव, and मोचस्रुत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=579-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचाट|मोचाटः
मोचाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A kind of pungent seed, (Nigella Indica.) “कृष्णजीरके”<BR>2. Sandal.<BR>	 3. The heart of the plantain tree.<BR>	 4. A plantain,<BR>(the fruit.)<BR> E. मोच a plantain, &c. अट् to go, (to be used with, to<BR>resemble, &c.) aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोचिनी
मोचिनी f. (-नी) A prickly-nightshade. “कण्टकार्य्याम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोच्य
मोच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्य)<BR>	 1. To be let loose.<BR>	 2. To be given up.<BR> E. मुच् to be free, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोटक|मोटकं|मोटकः
मोटक mn. (-कः-कं) A pill.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Two broken blades of kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोटकी
मोटकी f. (-की) One of the Rāginīs or female personification of the<BR>musical modes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोटन|मोटनं|मोटनः
मोटन m. (-नः) Air, wind.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Rubbing, grinding, pressing.<BR> E. मुट् to rub, &c. aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोटनक|मोटनकं
मोटनक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Destruction.<BR>	 2. A species of the Anuṣṭubh metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोट्टायित|मोट्टायितं
मोट्टायित n. (-तं) One of the ten Bhāvas, or properties of women, the<BR>silent expression of returned affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोण|मोणः
मोण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Dried fruit.<BR>	 2. A sort of water-fly, the crocodile-fly.<BR>3. A basket for carrying snakes in.<BR> E. मुण् to vow, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोद|मोदः
मोद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Joy, delight, happiness.<BR>	 2. Fragrance.<BR> E. मुद् to rejoice,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदक|मोदकः
मोदक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Delighting, rejoicing, causing happiness or de-<BR>light.<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं) A sort of sweetmeat.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A mixed caste.<BR>E. मुद् to be glad, in the causal form, to make glad, and ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदयत्
मोदयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Delighting, pleasing.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. Arabian<BR>jasmine.<BR>	 2. A wild sort of lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR> E. मुद् to<BR>be pleased, causal form, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदित|मोदितः
मोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pleased, delighted.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Pleasure, delight.<BR>E. मुद् to rejoice, aff. क्त, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदिनी
मोदिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Jasmine.<BR>	 2. Musk.<BR>	 3. Spiritious liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरट|मोरटं|मोरटः
मोरट n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. Root of sugar cane.<BR>	 2. The blossom of the Alan-<BR>gium hexapetalum.<BR>	 3. Milk of seven days standing, or when it<BR>has lost its milky nature.<BR>	 f. (-टा) A sort of creeper, (Sanseviera<BR>zeylanica.)<BR> E. मुर् to surround, aff. अटन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोष|मोषः
मोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A robber.<BR>	 2. Plundering.<BR>	 3. Stolen property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषक|मोषकः
मोषक m. (-कः) A thief.<BR> E. मुष् to steal, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषण|मोषणं
मोषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Stealing.<BR>	 2. Killing.<BR>	 3. Cutting.<BR> E. मुष्, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषयित्नु|मोषयित्नुः
मोषयित्नु m. (-त्नुः)<BR>	 1. Brāhmana.<BR>	 2. The kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषा
मोषा f. (-षा) Stealing, theft.<BR> E. मुष् to steal, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोह|मोहं|मोहः
मोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Fainting, loss of consciousness or sense.<BR>	 2. Ignorance,<BR>folly, foolishness; it is applied especially to that spiritual igno-<BR>rance which leads men to believe in the reality of worldly objects,<BR>and to addict themselves to mundane or sensual enjoyment.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pain, affliction.<BR>	 4. Error, mistake.<BR>	 5. Bewilderment, distraction.<BR>E. मुह् to be ignorant or foolish, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहकलिल
मोहकलिल n. (-लं) The snare of illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहन|मोहनं|मोहनः
मोहन mfn. (-नः-ना or -नी-नं) Fascinating, stupefying, depriving of<BR>sense or understanding.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Copulation.<BR>	 2. One of the<BR>arrows of KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 3. Temptation, seduction, the overpower-<BR>ing of reason and reflection by worldly or sensual allurements.<BR>4. A charm employed to bewilder an enemy.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The thorn-<BR>apple, (Dhuturā.)<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A sort of grass, (Trigonella cornicu-<BR>lata.)<BR>	 2. A kind of jasmine, commonly the Tripura or Tipperāh<BR>jasmine.<BR> E. मुह् to be foolish, causal form, aff. युच् or ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनक|मोहनकः
मोहनक m. (-कः) The month of chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनास्त्र
मोहनास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) A weapon which fascinates the person against whom<BR>it is directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहित
मोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Puzzled, perplexed.<BR>	 2. Beguiled, deceived. E.<BR>मुह् to be foolish, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहिन्
मोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Illusive, fallacious, beguiling.<BR> E. मोह, and<BR>इनि aff.; or मुह् to be foolish causal v., घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहिनी
मोहिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A kind of jasmine, commonly Tripuramāli.<BR>	 2.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">Page580-b+ 60</a>]<BR>VIṢṆU in the form of a fascinating woman.<BR>	 3. A name of an<BR>APSARĀ.<BR> E. मोह folly, इनि aff., and fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौकुलि|मौकुलिः
मौकुलि m. (-लिः) A crow, some books have मीकलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिक|मौक्तिकं
मौक्तिक n. (-कं) A pearl.<BR> E. मुक्ता a pearl, ठक् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकगुम्फिका|मौक्तिकगुंफिका
मौक्तिकगुम्फिका f. (-का) A woman who prepares strings of pearls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकप्रसवा
मौक्तिकप्रसवा f. (-वा) The pearl-oyster.<BR> E. मौक्तिक, and प्रसवा a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकशुक्ति|मौक्तिकशुक्तिः
मौक्तिकशुक्ति f. (-क्तिः) A pearl-oyster.<BR> E. मौक्तिक, a pearl शुक्ति an oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्य|मौक्यं
मौक्य n. (-क्यं) Dumbness.<BR> E. मूक. and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौखर्य्य|मौखर्य|मौखर्यं|मौखर्य्यं
मौखर्य्य nf. (-र्य्यं-र्य्यी) Scurrility, defamation.<BR> E. मुखर foul-mouthed, ष्यञ् aff., fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौख्य|मौख्यं
मौख्य n. (-ख्यं) Pre-eminence, precedence.<BR> E. मुख chief, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौग्ध
मौग्ध n. (-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Simplicity, silliness.<BR>	 2. Ignorance.<BR>	 3. A feminine pro-<BR>perty, asking a lover to tell what is already known.<BR> E. मुग्ध, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौच|मौचं
मौच n. (-चं) The fruit of the banana tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जी|मौंजी
मौञ्जी f. (-ञ्जी) The girdle of a Brāhmana made of three strings of<BR>Munja grass.<BR> E. मुञ्जा, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्चिबन्धन
मौञ्चिबन्धन n. (-नं) Investiture with the distinguishing cord.<BR> E. मौञ्जि the<BR>girdle, and बन्धन binding; both being assumed at the same time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौढ्य|मौढ्यं
मौढ्य n. (-ढ्यं) Ignorance, folly, especially spiritual folly: see मोह. E.<BR>मूढ fool, ष्यञ् aff. of property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौण्ड्य|मौंड्यं
मौण्ड्य n. (-ण्ड्यं) Baldness, natural or artificial.<BR> E. मुण्ड, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौत्र|मौत्रं
मौत्र n. (-त्रं) A quantity of urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौदकिक|मौदकिकः
मौदकिक m. (-कः) A confectioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गलि|मौद्गलिः
मौद्गलि m. (-लिः) A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गीन|मौद्गीनं
मौद्गीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fit for or bearing, &c. kidney-beans.<BR> E. मुद्ग<BR>kidney-bean, and खञ् aff.; also with अण् aff. मौद्ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौन|मौनं
मौन n. (-नं) Silence, taciturnity.<BR> E. मुनि a sage, (who practises,) अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनव्रत
मौनव्रत n. (-तं) A vow of silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनिन्
मौनिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि) Silent, taciturn.<BR>	 m. (-नी) An ascetic, a hermit,<BR>a religious sage, one who has overcome his passions and retired<BR>from the world.<BR> E. मौन silence, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौरजिक|मौरजिकः
मौरजिक m. (-कः) A player on a drum.<BR> E. मुरज a drum, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्ख्य|मौर्ख्यं
मौर्ख्य n. (-र्ख्यं) Stupidity, folly, fatuity.<BR> E. मूर्ख a fool, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्व्वी|मौर्वी
मौर्व्वी f. (-र्व्वी) A bow-string.<BR> E. मूर्व्वा the plant, from the fibres of<BR>which bow-strings are made, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौल|मौलः
मौल mfn. (-लः-ला-ली-लं)<BR>	 1. Radical, proceeding from a root or origin.<BR>	 2.<BR>Of pure blood, descended from a respectable and primitive family<BR>without any improper intermixture.<BR> E. मूल a root, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलि|मौलिः
मौलि mf. (-लिः-लिः or ली)<BR>	 1. A lock of hair on the crown of the head.<BR>2. Hair ornamented and braided round the head.<BR>	 3. A diadem, a<BR>tiara.<BR>	 4. The head.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The earth.<BR> E. मूल the root or base, aff.<BR>इञ्; or मूल a name, and इञ् aff of descent; or मू to bind, लि<BR>aff., and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौष्टा
मौष्टा m. (-ष्टा) Boxing, sparring, playing at fisticuffs.<BR> E. मुष्टि the fist, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौष्टिक|मौष्टिकः
मौष्टिक m. (-कः) A rogue, a swindler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौसल|मौसलः
मौसल f. (-ली) Adj. Formed like a club.<BR>	 2. Fought with clubs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौहूर्त्त|मौहूर्त|मौहूर्तः|मौहूर्त्तः
मौहूर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) An astrologer.<BR> E. मुहूर्त्त an hour, and अण् aff.; also<BR>with ठक् aff. मौहूर्त्तिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्ना
म्ना r. 1st cl. (मनति) To fix in the memory by frequent practice or<BR>repetition, to study, to acquire by study, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्नात
म्नात f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Learnt.<BR>	 2. Repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्ष्
म्रक्ष् r. 1st cl. (म्रक्षति)<BR>	 1. To accumulate.<BR>	 2. To smear, to anoint. r. 10th<BR>cl. (म्रक्षयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To mix.<BR>	 2. To combine 3. To speak incorrectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्ष|म्रक्षः
म्रक्ष m. (-क्षः) Slyness, hypocrisy, concealment of one's vice or defects.<BR>E. म्रक्ष् to anoint, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्षण|म्रक्षणं
म्रक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Oil.<BR>	 2. Smearing the body with fragrant oils or un-<BR>guents.<BR>	 3. Heaping up.<BR> E. म्रक्ष् to smear or anoint, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रच्
म्रच् r. 1st. cl. (म्रचति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रद्
म्रद् r. 1st cl. (म्रदते)<BR>	 1. To grind, to pound, to reduce to powder or<BR>dust.<BR>	 2. To tread or trample on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिमन्
म्रदिमन् m. (-मा) Softness.<BR> E. मृदु soft, and इमलिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=580-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिमान्वित
म्रदिमान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Soft.<BR>	 2. Kind.<BR> E. म्रदिमन्, अन्वित endowed<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिष्ठ|म्रदिष्ठः
म्रदिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very soft, exceedingly soft, softest.<BR> E. मृद् soft,<BR>and इष्ठन् aff. of the superlative, ऋ changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदीयस्
म्रदीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Softer, milder.<BR> E. मृदु soft, and ईयसुन aff.<BR>of the comparative, and the vowel changed to the semi-vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रियमाण
म्रियमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Dying.<BR> E. मृ to die, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रुच्
म्रुच् (उ) म्रुचु r. 1st cl. (म्रोचति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रुञ्च्|म्रुंच्
म्रुञ्च् (उ) म्रुञ्चु r. 1st cl. (म्रुञ्चति) To go, to move; also read म्रुनच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रेट्
म्रेट् (ऋ) म्रेटृ r. 1st cl. (म्रेटति) To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रेड्
म्रेड् (ऋ) म्रेडृ r. 1st cl. (म्रेडति) To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लक्ष्
म्लक्ष् r. 10th cl. (म्लक्षयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To mix, to unite.<BR>	 2. To speak incorrectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लात
म्लात f. (-ता) Adj. Faded, withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लान|म्लानं
म्लान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Foul, dirty.<BR>	 2. Languid, weary.<BR>	 3. Faded,<BR>withered.<BR>	 4. Melancholy.<BR> E. म्लै to be languid, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानि|म्लानिः
म्लानि f. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Weariness, languor.<BR>	 2. Foulness, filth.<BR>	 3. Fading,<BR>decay.<BR>	 4. Sadness.<BR> E. म्लै to be languid, &c., aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लास्नु
म्लास्नु f. (-स्नु)<BR>	 1. Growing languid.<BR>	 2. Growing thin.<BR>	 3. Growing withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लिष्ट|म्लिष्टं|म्लिष्टः
म्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Indistinct, (as speech.)<BR>	 2. Languid.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं)<BR>Indistinct speech.<BR> E. म्लेच्छ् to speak indistinctly, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुक्त
म्लुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Mixed, intermixed, inlaid, set.<BR> E. म्लुच् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुच्
म्लुच्(उ)म्लुचु r. 1st cl. (म्लोचति) To go, to move. With अभि and नि pre-<BR>fixed.<BR>	 1. To go down.<BR>	 2. To set as the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुञ्च्|म्लुंच्
म्लुञ्च् (उ) म्लुञ्चु r. 1st cl. (म्लुञ्चति) To go, to move; also read म्लुन्च् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छ्|म्लेछ्
म्लेच्छ् r. 1st and 10th cls. (म्लेच्छति म्लेच्छयति-ते) To speak inarticulately<BR>or incorrectly, to use a provincial or barbarous dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छ|म्लेच्छं|म्लेच्छः|म्लेछ
म्लेच्छ m. (-च्छः)<BR>	 1. The generic term for a barbarian or foreigner; that<BR>is, for one speaking any language but Sanskrit, and not subject<BR>to the usual Hindu institutions.<BR>	 2. A sinner, a criminal.<BR>	 3. Indis-<BR>tinct or barbarous speech.<BR> E. म्लेच्छ् to speak inarticulately, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छकन्द|म्लेच्छकंद|म्लेच्छकन्दः
म्लेच्छकन्द m. (-न्दः) Garlic.<BR> E. म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and कण्ड root. “लशुने ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छजाति|म्लेच्छजातिः
म्लेच्छजाति m. (-तिः) A Mleccha or barbarian or a man of an outcast<BR>race. The tribes enumerated under this head by MANU, but who<BR>are by him said to be properly, degraded Kṣatriyas, appear to be<BR>chiefly the inhabitants of the countries bordering immediately<BR>upon India, both to the north and south: as far as modern re-<BR>search and similarity of appellation may be trusted, the tribes of<BR>Mlecchas are as follows: the Pauṇḍrakas, (the people of pro-<BR>vinces bordering on Bengal and Bihar, and to the south of the<BR>Ganges,) Oḍras, (Urīyās,) Drāviras, (people of the southern part<BR>of the Coromandel coast,) Cāmbojas, (Arachosians,) Yavanas,<BR>(Greeks or Bactrians,) Śakas, (the people of the Sacha region or<BR>Sakai,) Pāravas, (Paropamisans,) Pahlavas, (the ancient Persians,)<BR>Chīnas, (Chinese,) Kirātas, (generally mountaineers, here per-<BR>haps especially the inhabitants of the Himālaya or Imaus,) Dera-<BR>das, (Daradæ,) and Khasas, (Scuthi or Chasas.)<BR>	 n. (-च्छं) Copper. E.<BR>म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and जाति tribe, class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छदेश|म्लेच्छदेशः
म्लेच्छदेश m. (-शः) The countries bordering on India, or those inhabi-<BR>ted by people of a different faith and language; defined to be any,<BR>where the black antelope is not found.<BR> E. म्लेच्छ् a barbarian, an<BR>outcast, देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छभोजन|म्लेच्छभोजनं|म्लेच्छभोजनः
म्लेच्छभोजन m. (-नः) Wheat.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Half-ripe barley.<BR> E. म्लेच्छ an outcast, भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छमण्डल|म्लेच्छमंडल|म्लेच्छमण्डलं
म्लेच्छमण्डल n. (-लं) The country of the Mlecchas or barbarians. E.<BR>म्लेच्छ, मण्डल region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छमुख|म्लेच्छमुखं
म्लेच्छमुख n. (-खः) Copper.<BR> E. म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and मुख countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छवाच्
म्लेच्छवाच् mfn. (-वाक्) Speaking a barbarous dialect.<BR> E. म्लेच्छ, वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छाश|म्लेच्छाशः
म्लेच्छाश m. (-शः) Wheat.<BR> E. म्लेच्छ a barbarian, अश् to eat, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छास्य|म्लेच्छास्यं
म्लेच्छास्य n. (-स्यं) Copper.<BR> E. म्लेच्छ a barbarian, and आस्व face, which<BR>would seem to allude to the fair complexion of the Greek or Maha-<BR>mmedan invaders of Hindusthan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छित|म्लेच्छितं
म्लेच्छित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spoken incorrectly or barbarously.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Foreign or barbarous language.<BR>	 2. Ungrammatical speech.<BR> E. म्लेच्छ्<BR>a barbarian, इतच् aff.; or म्लेच्छ् to speak inaccurately, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेट्
म्लेट् (ऋ) म्लेटृ r. 1st. cl. (म्लेटति) To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेड्
म्लेड् (ऋ) म्लेडृ r. 1st. cl. (म्लेडति) To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेव्
म्लेव् (ऋ,) म्लेवृ r. 1st cl. (म्लेवते) To serve, to gratify by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लै
म्लै r. 1st. cl. (म्लायति)<BR>	 1. To be faint or languid, to yawn with languor<BR>or fatigue.<BR>	 2. To fade, to decay.<BR>	 3. To become thin. With परि, 1.<BR>To be dejected.<BR>	 2. To wither. With प्र, 1. To fade.<BR>	 2. To be dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

य|यं|यः
य The twenty-six consonant of the Nāgari alphabet, or semi-vowel Y;<BR>in Bengal, it is usually pronounced J.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

य|यं|यः
य mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Who goes, a goer, a mover.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2.<BR>Union, Joining.<BR>	 3. Fame, celebrity.<BR>	 4. Barley.<BR>	 5. Light, lustre.<BR>6. Abandoning.<BR>	 7. YAMA.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Pudendum muliebre.<BR>	 2. Going,<BR>proceeding.<BR>	 3. A car, a carriage.<BR>	 4. Prohibiting, restraining, check-<BR>ing.<BR>	 5. Religious meditation.<BR>	 6. Getting, obtaining.<BR> E. यज् to wor-<BR>ship, or यम् to check, &c., aff. ड; or या-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक|यकः
यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Which, (of many.)<BR> E. यद् which, and अकच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृत्
यकृत् m. (-कृत्) The liver.<BR> E. य union, (of the parts of the body,) कृ to<BR>make, aff. क्विप् and तुक् augment. यकन् is optionally substituted<BR>for this word in some of the declensions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृदात्मिका
यकृदात्मिका f. (-का) A cock-roach.<BR> E. यकृत् the liver, आत्मन् self, कन् aff.,<BR>fem. form; like it in colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृद्वैरी
यकृद्वैरी f. (-री) A plant, a sort of tree, (Andersonia rohitaka.)<BR> E. यकृत् liver, वैर inimical to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्
यक्ष् r. 10th cl (यक्षयते) To worship, to honour or adore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष|यक्षः
यक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A demi-god, attendant especially on KUVERA, and em-<BR>ployed in the care of his gardens and treasures.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>KUVERA.<BR>	 3. The residence of INDRA.<BR>	 f. (-क्षी) The wife of<BR>KUVERA.<BR> E. यक्ष् to worship, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षकर्द्दम|यक्षकर्दम|यक्षकर्दमः|यक्षकर्द्दमः
यक्षकर्द्दम m. (-मः) Perfumed paste, used especially for anointing the<BR>body, and consisting of camphor, agallochum, musk and<BR>Kakkola; or the three first, with saffron and Sandal in equal<BR>proportions.<BR> E. यक्ष the demi-god, and कर्द्दम clay; a perfume of<BR>which these beings are supposed to be fond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षग्रह|यक्षग्रहः
यक्षग्रह m. (-हः) The being possessed by an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षतरु|यक्षतरुः
यक्षतरु m. (-रुः) The Indian fig-tree. “वटवृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षधूप|यक्षधूपः
यक्षधूप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Resin in general.<BR>	 2. Turpentine, the resinous exuda-<BR>tion of the pine.<BR> E. यक्ष the demi-god, धूप perfume or incense,<BR>अण् aff. “सर्ज्जरसे” धुना इति माषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षरस|यक्षरसः
यक्षरस m. (-सः) Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR> E. यक्ष the demi-god, रस taste, fondness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराज्
यक्षराज् m. (-राट्) KUVERA, the deity of wealth, and lord of the demi-<BR>gods called Yakṣas.<BR>	 2. A palæstrum, a place prepared for wrest-<BR>ling or boxing.<BR> E. यक्ष a Yakṣa, and राज who rules or shines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराज|यक्षराजः
यक्षराज m. (-जः) KUVERA: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराट्पुरी
यक्षराट्पुरी f. (-री) Alakā, the capital of KUVERA, supposed to be seated<BR>on mount Kailāsa.<BR> E. यक्षराज, पुरी city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षरात्रि|यक्षरात्रिः
यक्षरात्रि f. (-त्रिः) The night of the day of full moon in the month<BR>of Kārtika: see दीपाली.<BR> E. यक्ष the demi-god, रात्रि night; these<BR>spirits being supposed to be then abroad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षवित्त|यक्षवित्तः
यक्षवित्त Adj. One who stores up wealth but never uses it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षामलक|यक्षामलकं
यक्षामलक m. (-कः) A tree, described as a sort of date.<BR> E. यक्ष a Yakṣa,<BR>आमलक myrobalan. “पिण्डीखेजुर ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=581-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षावास|यक्षावासः
यक्षावास m. (-सः) The Indian fig-tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR> E. यक्ष a demi-god,<BR>आवास abode. “वटवृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षिणी
यक्षिणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. The wife of KUVERA.<BR>	 2. The wife of a Yakṣa.<BR>	 3.<BR>A sort of female fiend, attached to the service of DURGĀ, and<BR>frequently maintaining, like a sylph or fairy, an intercourse with<BR>mortals.<BR> E. यक्षिन् a name of KUVERA, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षेन्द्र|यक्षेन्द्रः
यक्षेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A name of KUVERA.<BR> E. यक्ष, and इन्द्र lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षेश
यक्षेश m. (-शः) KUVERA.<BR> E. यक्ष, and ईश lord; also यक्षेश्वर and the like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षोडुम्बुरक
यक्षोडुम्बुरक n. (-कं) The fruit of the Ficus religiosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मघ्नी
यक्ष्मघ्नी f. (-घ्नी) The raisin, dried-grape.<BR> E. यक्ष्म consumption, घ्न destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मन्
यक्ष्मन् m. (-क्ष्मा) Pulmonary consumption.<BR> E. यक्ष् to worship, and मनिन्<BR>Unādi aff.; also with मन् aff., यक्ष्म m. (-क्ष्मः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मिन्
यक्ष्मिन् f. (-क्ष्मिणी) One who suffers from consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्यमाण
यक्ष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Proposing or wishing to worship.<BR> E. यक्ष् to<BR>worship, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यङ्न्त
यङ्न्त m. (-न्तः) The frequentative deponent verb, (in gram.)<BR> E. यङ्, अन्त termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यङ्लुगन्त
यङ्लुगन्त m. (-न्तः) The frequentative active verb.<BR> E. यङ्, लुक् dropped,<BR>and अन्त termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्
यज् r. 1st. cl. (यजति-ते)<BR>	 1. To worship a deity.<BR>	 2. To associate with.<BR>	 3. To present or endow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्
यजत् mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्) Sacrificing, worshipping. E.<BR> E. यज् to wor-<BR>ship, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत|यजतः
यजत m. (-तः) The officiating priest at a sacrifice.<BR> E. यज् to worship, अतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजति|यजतिः
यजति m. (-तिः) A term for those sacrifices to which the verb यजति is<BR>applied, as distinguished from those rites to which the verb जुहोति<BR>applies. Sarvajnya-Nārāyana renders जुहोति by उपविष्टहोम and<BR>यजति by तिष्ठद्धोम्<BR> E. यज-अतिच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्र|यजत्रः
यजत्र m. (-त्रः) A Brāhamana who has maintained his consecrated fire.<BR>E. यज् to sacrifice, अत्रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजन|यजनं
यजन n. (-नं) Offering sacrifices, performing worship.<BR> E. यज् to worship, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजन्त|यजन्तः
यजन्त m. (-न्तः) A sacrificer, a worshipper.<BR> E. यज् to sacrifice, aff. झच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजमान|यजमानः
यजमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Worshipping.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. An employer of priests<BR>at sacrifice, the person who institutes its performance, and pays<BR>the expence of it.<BR>	 2. A patron, a host.<BR> E. यज् to worship, शानच्<BR>aff. of the present participle, with मक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजाक|यजाकः
यजाक m. (-कः) A donor, a benefactor, a liberal giver of presents, &c.<BR>E. यज् to present, Unādi aff. आकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजि|यजिः
यजि m. (-जिः) A sacrificer, one who institutes or performs a sacrifice.<BR>E. यज् to sacrifice, aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुर्वेद|यजुर्वेदः|यजुर्व्वेदः
यजुर्वेद n. (-दं) The Yajur-Veda: see the next.<BR> E. यजुस्, वेद a Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुस्
यजुस् n. (-जुः) The Yajur or Yajush, one of the four Vedas; it is di-<BR>vided into two principal portions, the white and black, or Vāja-<BR>saneyi and Taittirīya, the former of which is attributed to the<BR>saint YĀJNAWALKYA, to whom it was revealed by the sun, in<BR>the form of a horse; and the latter to TAITTIRI, to whom it<BR>was communicated by YĀSKA, the first pupil of its original<BR>author, the sage VAIŚAMPĀYANA: according to the Purāṇas<BR>the Taittirīya portion was named from Tittiri a partridge;<BR>the disciples of VAIŚAMPĀYANA being changed into those birds,<BR>to pick up the texts of the Veda as they were disgorged in a<BR>tangible shape by YĀJNAWALKYA, at the command of VAIŚAM-<BR>PĀYANA: both portions of this Veda are very full on the sub-<BR>ject of religious rites, and the prayers peculiar to it, are chiefly<BR>in measured and poetical prose.<BR> E. यज् to worship, Unādi aff. उसि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञ|यज्ञः
यज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A sacrifice, a ceremony in which oblations are presented.<BR>E. यज् to worship, aff. नङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकर्म्मन्|यज्ञकर्मन्
यज्ञकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Any sacrificial act of ceremony.<BR> E. यज्ञ, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकल्प
यज्ञकल्प Adj. Of the nature of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकीलक|यज्ञकीलकः
यज्ञकीलक m. (-कः) The post to which the victim is fastened at a sacri-<BR>fice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकुण्ड|यज्ञकुंड
यज्ञकुण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A hole in the ground built for receiving the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकृत्
यज्ञकृत् m. (-कृत्) A sacrificer, a worshipper, or priest conducting a<BR>sacrifice.<BR> E. यज्ञ sacrifice, कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञक्रतु|यज्ञक्रतुः
यज्ञक्रतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. A complete rite.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञद्रुह्
यज्ञद्रुह् m. (-ध्रुक्) A Rākshasa, an imp.<BR> E. यज्ञ, द्रुह् to wrong, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपशु|यज्ञपशुः
यज्ञपशु m. (-शुः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. Any animal offered in sacrifice.<BR> E. यज्ञ a<BR>sacrifice, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपात्र
यज्ञपात्र n. (-त्रं) A sacrificial vessel.<BR> E. यज्ञ, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपुरुष|यज्ञपुरुषः
यज्ञपुरुष m. (-षः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. यज्ञ sacrifice, पुरुष man or male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञभाजन|यज्ञभाजनं
यज्ञभाजन n. (-नं) A sacrificial vessel.<BR> E. यज्ञ sacrifice, and भाजन vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञभूमि|यज्ञभूमिः
यज्ञभूमि f. (-मिः) Place prepared for a sacrifice, or where it is offered.<BR>E. यज्ञ, and भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञवराह|यज्ञवराहः
यज्ञवराह m. (-हः) VIṢṆU in his boar-incarnation.<BR> E. यज्ञ, and वराह the boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञवल्लि|यज्ञवल्लिः
यज्ञवल्लि f. (-ल्लिः-ल्ली) The Soma plant; also यज्ञश्रेष्ठा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञवाट|यज्ञवाटः
यज्ञवाट m. (-टः) A place prepared and enclosed for a sacrifice.<BR> E. यज्ञ a<BR>sacrifice, वाट inclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञवृक्ष|यज्ञवृक्षः
यज्ञवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The Indian fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञवेदि|यज्ञवेदिः
यज्ञवेदि f. (-दिः or दी) A sacrificial altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञशरण
यज्ञशरण n. (-णं) A building or a temporary structure under which a sacrifice is performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञशिष्ट
यज्ञशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) What is left from a sacrifice or oblation. E.<BR>यज्ञ, शिष्ट remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञशेष|यज्ञशेषः
यज्ञशेष m. (-षः) The relics of a sacrifice or oblation.<BR> E. यज्ञ, शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसदस्
यज्ञसदस् n. (-दः) An assembly of people at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसार|यज्ञसारः
यज्ञसार m. (-रः) The glomerous fig-tree, (Ficus glomerata, Rox.) E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, सार essence. “यज्ञोडुम्बर वृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसिद्धि|यज्ञसिद्धिः
यज्ञसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Performance of sacrifice.<BR>	 2. Obtaining the objects<BR>of a sacrifice.<BR> E. यज्ञ, and सिद्धि accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञसूत्र|यज्ञसूत्रं
यज्ञसूत्र n. (-त्रं) The characteristic thread, worn by the three principal<BR>classes of Hindus.<BR> E. यज्ञ sacrifice, and सूत्र thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञस्थान|यज्ञस्थानं
यज्ञस्थान n. (-नं) A place of sacrifice.<BR> E. यज्ञ and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञाङ्ग|यज्ञांग|यज्ञाङ्गः
यज्ञाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The glomerous fig, (Ficus glomerata, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>	 3. A part of any sacrificial cere-<BR>mony.<BR> E. यज्ञ a sacrifice, अङ्ग a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञान्त|यज्ञान्तः
यज्ञान्त m. (-न्तः) A supplementary sacrifice.<BR> E. यज्ञ the principal, अन्त end, finish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञारि|यज्ञारिः
यज्ञारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A demon, a goblin.<BR> E. यज्ञ a<BR>sacrifice, अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञिक|यज्ञिकः
यज्ञिक m. (-कः) The Palāsh tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. यज्ञ, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञिय|यज्ञियं|यज्ञियः
यज्ञिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Proper for or suitable to a sacrifice.<BR>	 2. Pious.<BR>3. Sacred.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The third Yuga or Dwāpara age.<BR>	 2. A god,<BR>a deity.<BR> E. यज्ञ sacrifice, and घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञियदेश|यज्ञियदेशः
यज्ञियदेश f. (-शः) The country of Hindus; those districts in which the<BR>ritual and institutes of the Hindu system are enforced; properly<BR>the country in which the black deer or antelope is native. E.<BR>यज्ञिय sacrificial, and देश a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञियशाला
यज्ञियशाला f. (-ला) A temple, a shrine, a place of sacrifice.<BR> E. यज्ञिय to be<BR>sacrificed, (where,) शाला hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञीयब्रह्मपादप|यज्ञीयब्रह्मपादपः
यज्ञीयब्रह्मपादप m. (-पः) The Vikantaka tree. “वंँइचि ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोडुम्बर|यज्ञोडुम्बरः
यज्ञोडुम्बर m. (-रः) The glomerous fig-tree, (Ficus glomerata, Rox.) E.<BR>यज्ञ sacrifice, उडुम्बर the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपकरण
यज्ञोपकरण n. (-णं) Any utensil or implement necessary for a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपवीत|यज्ञोपवीतं
यज्ञोपवीत n. (-तं) The sacrificial cord, originally worn by the three<BR>principal casts of Hindus: at present from the loss of the pure<BR>Kṣatriya and Vaiśya casts in Bengal, confined to the Brāh-<BR>minical order.<BR> E. यज्ञ sacrifice, उपवीत thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपवीतिन्
यज्ञोपवीतिन् m. (-ती) A Brāhmana, &c. invested with the sacred thread.<BR>E. यज्ञोपवीत, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्यु|यज्युः
यज्यु m. (-ज्युः) A Brāhmana, conversant with the Yajur-Veda.<BR> E. यज्<BR>to worship, Unādi aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्वन्
यज्वन् m. (-ज्वा)<BR>	 1. A sacrificer in due form, or agreeably to the ritual<BR>of the Vedas.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-ज्वरी) Sacrificing, worshipping. E.<BR>यज् to worship, वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=582-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्वनापति
यज्वनापति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. यज्वन् a sacrificer in the sixth case<BR>plural, पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्|यन्त्
यत् (ई) यती r. 1st cl. (यतते) To resolve or determine in consequence<BR>of a wish or desire, to apply or endeavour strenuously, to energize,<BR>to persevere. r. 10 cl. (यातयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To distress or afflict.<BR>	 2. To<BR>beat.<BR>	 3. To order.<BR>	 4. To collect, to assemble.<BR>	 5. To work, to make<BR>or manufacture.<BR>	 6. To prevent, to remove.<BR>	 7. To return, to give<BR>back, to requite.<BR>	 8. To barter or exchange.<BR>	 9. To purify.<BR>	 10. To<BR>encourage. With निर or वि prefixed, To chastise, to punish, to<BR>inflict pain. With निस् or प्रति, 1. To restore.<BR>	 2. To requite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्|यन्त्
यत् Ind. Because as, since, wherefore, correlative of तत् thence, there-<BR>fore, &c.<BR> E. यत् to check, to restrain, क्विप् and तुक् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत|यतः
यत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Governed, controlled.<BR>	 2. Limited, restrained.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं) The stirring of an elephant by means of the rider's feet. E.<BR>यम् to check, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतचित्त
यतचित्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Resigned, subdued, one of well-governed<BR>thoughts or feelings.<BR> E. यत and चित्त the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतचित्तात्मन्
यतचित्तात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Having power over the soul and spirit,<BR>of subdued mind.<BR> E. यतचित्त, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतत्
यतत् mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्) Striving, making effort.<BR> E. यत् to make effort, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतन|यतनं
यतन n. (-नं) Making effort or exertion.<BR> E. यत् to make effort, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतनीय
यतनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be exerted, or persevered, to be made as an<BR>effort.<BR> E. यत् to make effort, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतम|यतमः
यतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Which, (of many.)<BR> E. यद् which, डतमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतमान
यतमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Making effort, striving, struggling, persevering.<BR>E. यत् to strive, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतमैथुन
यतमैथुन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Disinclined to sexual intercourse, abstaining<BR>from it.<BR> E. यत, and मैथुन coition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतर|यतरः
यतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रत्) Which, (of two), whether.<BR> E. यद् which, डतरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतव्रत
यतव्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Firm to an engagement or vow.<BR> E. यत, व्रत a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतस्
यतस् Ind. Because, as, since, whence: see यत्<BR> E. यद् which, what, and<BR>तसिल् substituted for the termination of the 5th case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतस्ततस्
यतस्ततस् Ind.<BR>	 1. From any place whatsoever.<BR>	 2. From any person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतात्मत्
यतात्मत् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Of subdued or well-governed spirit.<BR> E. यत,<BR>आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतात्मवत्|यतात्मवन्त्
यतात्मवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Self-subdued, having the mind and all its<BR>powers in subjection.<BR> E. यतात्म, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यताहार
यताहार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Temperate, abstemious.<BR> E. यत, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यति|यतिः
यति Pron. How many, as many, (declined only in the plural, nomi-<BR>native and accusative यति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यति|यतिः
यति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A sage, whose passions are completely under subjec-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. A religious mendicant, especially one of the Jaina sect.<BR>	 3.<BR>Stopping, ceasing, rest, term.<BR>	 4. Restraining, controlling, cheek-<BR>ing.<BR>	 f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A pause in poetry or metre, a stop, a rest.<BR>	 2. Uni-<BR>on, joining.<BR>	 3. Restraint, check.<BR>	 4. Guidance.<BR> E. यत् endeavour,<BR>&c., aff. इन्; or यम् to restrain, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतित
यतित f. (-ता) Adj. Attempted, striven after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतिन्
यतिन् m. (-ती) A sage with subdued passions.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A widow.<BR> E. यत<BR>restraining, from यम् with क्त aff. and इनि added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतिपात्र
यतिपात्र n. (-त्रं) A vessel for collecting alms, made of wood, or a hol-<BR>low bamboo, an earthen bowl, or a gourd.<BR> E. यति and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतिमैथुन|यतिमैथुनं
यतिमैथुन n. (-नं) The copulation or cohabitation of holy personages. E.<BR>यति as above, and मैथुन coition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतु
यतु(तू)का f. (-का) A plant, Chakāwat commonly. “वेतोशाक ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतीन्द्रय
यतीन्द्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Chaste, pure, of subdued passions.<BR> E. यत, इन्द्रिय<BR>an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतेन्द्रिय|यतेंद्रिय
यतेन्द्रिय Adj.<BR>	 m. (-यः) Of subdued passions, pious, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यतोयतस्
यतोयतस् Ind.<BR>	 1. From whatever place.<BR>	 2. Wherever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्कर
यत्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Doing what.<BR> E. यत् and कृ to do, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्त
यत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Striven, resolved, exerted.<BR> E. यत् to resolve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्न|यत्नः
यत्न m. (-त्नः) Effort, exertion, perseverance, energy.<BR> E. यत् to endea-<BR>vour strenuously or continuously, aff. नङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्नतस्
यत्नतस् Ind. Vigorously, strenuously.<BR> E. यत्न and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्नवत्|यत्नवन्त्
यत्नवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Persevering, diligent, making effort or exer-<BR>tion.<BR> E. यत्न effort, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्य
यत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) To be exerted or made as an effort.<BR> E. यत् to exert, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्र
यत्र Ind.<BR>	 1. Where, in what place.<BR>	 2. When.<BR>	 3. Because, since, as<BR>that.<BR> E. यद् what, and त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यत्र्
यत्र् (इ) यत्रि r. 1st and 10th cls. (यन्त्रति-ते यन्त्रयति-ते) To confine, to res-<BR>train, to subdue or regulate: the root may also be written यन्त्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथा
यथा Ind. As, according to; correlative to तथा so: it is also commonly<BR>used in composition to form adverbs; as यथाकालं seasonably, यथा-<BR>क्रमं regularly, यथान्यायं fitly, suitably, यथाशास्त्रं according to scrip-<BR>ture, &c.<BR> E. यद् what, थाल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथांशतस्
यथांशतस् Ind. Proportionably, in due proportion.<BR> E. यथा as, according to, अंश part, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकथा
यथाकथा Ind. As much as, tantum quantum; it is especially used as<BR>a term of disrespect.<BR> E. यथा as, and कथा how.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकथाच
यथाकथाच Ind. Rarely, unfrequently, seldomer than proper.<BR> E. यथा as<BR>much, कथा how much, with च the particle aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकर्त्तव्य|यथाकर्तव्य
यथाकर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) What is right or proper to be done.<BR> E. यथा<BR>कर्त्तव्य to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकर्म
यथाकर्म Ind. According to action, duties or circumstances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकल्प
यथाकल्प Adv.<BR>	 n. (-ल्पं) As designed.<BR> E. यथा and कल्प making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकाम
यथाकाम Adv.<BR>	 n. (-म) At pleasure, as you please.<BR> E. यथा, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकामिन्
यथाकामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Wilful, independent, uncontrolled, follow-<BR>ing one's own inclinations.<BR> E. यथा as, according to, काम desire,<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकालम्
यथाकालम् Ind. At the right moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाकृत
यथाकृत Adj. As agreed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाक्रम|यथाक्रमं
यथाक्रम Adv.<BR>	 n. (-मं) In order, orderly, successively, methodically. E.<BR>यथा agreeably to, क्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाक्षमम्
यथाक्षमम् Ind. According to ability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथागत
यथागत Adv.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Applied to a person's being sent away or returning<BR>as he came.<BR> E. यथा and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाजात|यथाजातः
यथाजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Foolish, stupid, a fool, a natural.<BR>	 2. Bar-<BR>barous, outcast.<BR> E. यथा as, जात born, as simple as at birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाज्ञानम्
यथाज्ञानम् Ind. To the best of one's knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथातथ|यथातथं
यथातथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Right, true Ind. or adv.<BR>	 n. (-थं)<BR>	 1. Properly,<BR>suitably.<BR>	 2. Precisely, exactly. Noun. (-थः) Narrative of events,<BR>history.<BR> E. यथा as, and तथा so, with the termination of the neuter<BR>gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथातथा
यथातथा Adv. In any way, any how.<BR> E. यथा and तथा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथापूर्व्व|यथापूर्व|यथापूर्व्वं
यथापूर्व्व n. Adv. (-र्व्वं)<BR>	 1. In order or succession.<BR>	 2. Formerly, pre-<BR>cedingly, in prior time or place.<BR> E. यथा as, पूर्व्व formerly, before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाप्राणम्
यथाप्राणम् Ind. With all one's might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाभागम्
यथाभागम् Ind.<BR>	 1. According to share.<BR>	 2. Each in his respective place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाभिमतम्
यथाभिमतम् Ind. According to one's wish or purpose.<BR> E. यथा, and<BR>अभिमत purposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाभूतम्
यथाभूतम् Ind. According to truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथामुखीन|यथामुखीनः
यथामुखीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Like, resembling, showing, similarly or<BR>reflecting.<BR>	 2. Looking strait at, (with a genitive.)<BR> E. यथा as, मुख<BR>the countenance, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथायथम्
यथायथम् Ind.<BR>	 1. As, thereto, appertaining.<BR>	 2. Rightly.<BR> E. यथा repeated,<BR>with the termination of the neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्थ|यथार्थं
यथार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Right, proper.<BR>	 2. According to the sense.<BR>	 n.<BR>Adv. or ind. (-र्थं) Properly, suitably.<BR> E. यथा as, अर्थ property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्थता
यथार्थता f. (-ता) Rectitude, propriety; fitness.<BR> E. तल् added to the<BR>last; also with त्व, यथार्थत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्ह|यथार्हं
यथार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Proper, suitable, appropriate.<BR>	 n. adv. or ind. (-र्हं)<BR>Properly, suitably.<BR> E. यथा as, अर्ह properly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=583-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्हतस्
यथार्हतस् Adv. Properly, fitly.<BR> E. यथार्ह and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथार्हवर्ण|यथार्हवर्णः
यथार्हवर्ण m. (-र्णः) A spy, a secret emissary.<BR> E. यथार्ह properly, suitably,<BR>वर्ण form, colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावकाश
यथावकाश Adv.<BR>	 n. or ind. (-शं)<BR>	 1. According to opportunity.<BR>	 2. In the<BR>proper place.<BR> E. यथा, and अवकाश season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावत्
यथावत् Ind.<BR>	 1. Truly, exactly, as it was, according to law or usage.<BR>	 2.<BR>accordingly, conformably.<BR> E. यथा and वत्रि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावसर
यथावसर Adv.<BR>	 n. or ind. (-रं) According to opportunity.<BR> E. यथा and<BR>अवसर opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाविधि
यथाविधि Ind. or n. adv. According to rule.<BR> E. यथा, and विधि precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथावृत्त
यथावृत्त Adv. (-त्तं) Circumstantially, relating a thing as it happened.<BR>E. यथा, and वृत्त being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाशक्ति
यथाशक्ति Adv. Extent of capability, as much as possible.<BR> E. यथा as<BR>much as, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथाशास्त्र|यथाशास्त्रं
यथाशास्त्र Adv.<BR>	 n. (-स्त्रं) According to the Shāstras, agreeably to scrip-<BR>ture.<BR> E. यथा agreeably to, शास्त्र the Shāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथासुख
यथासुख Adv.<BR>	 n. (-खं) Happily,<BR> E. यथा, and सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथास्थित|यथास्थितं
यथास्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Right, proper, fit, true.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Circums-<BR>tantially, or all that happened or existed.<BR> E. यथा as, and स्थित<BR>fixed, established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथास्वम्
यथास्वम् Ind. As, according or appertaining to, properly, peculiarly. E.<BR>यथा as, and स्व own, peculiar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथेप्सित|यथेप्सितं
यथेप्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wished, desired. Adv.<BR>	 n. or ind. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Wil-<BR>lingly, voluntarily.<BR>	 2. Wilfully, independently.<BR> E. यथा as, इप्सित<BR>(participle past, desiderative form of आप् to obtain,) desired,<BR>wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथेष्ट|यथेष्टं
यथेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Wished, desired Adv.<BR>	 n. or ind. (-ष्टं) According to will or inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथेष्टचारिन्
यथेष्टचारिन् m. (-री) A bird.<BR> E. यथा as, इष्ट wished, चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथोचित|यथोचितं
यथोचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Right, proper. Adv.<BR>	 n. or ind. (-तं) Properly,<BR>suitably.<BR> E. यथा, and उचित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यथोदित|यथोदितं
यथोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) As said or explained.<BR> E. यथा as, उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्
यद् mfn. Relative pronoun. (-यः-या-यत्) Who, which, what.<BR> E. यज् to<BR>worship, Unādi aff. अदि, with the power of डित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदा
यदा Ind. When, at what time.<BR> E. यद् what, दाच् aff., the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदि
यदि Ind. If.; particle of suspicion or doubt.<BR> E. यत् to make effort, इञ्<BR>aff., and the radical final changed to द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदु|यदुः
यदु m. (-दुः)<BR>	 1. The name of a king, the ancestor of KṚṢṆA, and the<BR>eldest son of YAYĀTĪ and DEVAYĀNĪ, the sixth monarch of the<BR>lunar dynasty.<BR>	 2. A country on the west of the Jamunā river about<BR>Mathurā and Brindābana, over which YADU ruled, and named<BR>after him: according to some authorities, however, the kingdom<BR>of YADU, is the Dakshin or Peninsula of India.<BR>	 m. Plu. (-वाः)<BR>I. The Yādavas, the people of YADU.<BR>	 2. Descendants of king<BR>YADU: more usually however यादवाः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदुनाथ|यदुनाथः
यदुनाथ m. (-थः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. यदु the son of YAYĀTI, here<BR>put for his race, नाथ lord, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदृच्छा
यदृच्छा f. (-च्छा)<BR>	 1. Wilfulness, independence, following one's own fan-<BR>cies.<BR>	 2. (In grammar,) A noun which is neither a generic nor speci-<BR>fic term, or noun of agency; one either not derived from au-<BR>thority, or not possessing meaning.<BR> E. यत् what, which, ऋच्छ् to<BR>go, affs. अ and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यदृच्छाभिज्ञ|यदृच्छाभिज्ञः
यदृच्छाभिज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A voluntary or self-offered witness.<BR> E. यदृच्छा, and अभिज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्यपि
यद्यपि Adv. Although.<BR> E. यदि, and अपि certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यद्वत्
यद्वत् Ind. As, in what manner, correlative to तद्वत्.<BR> E. यद्, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्तृ|यंतृ
यन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) A check, a restraint, any person or thing that<BR>restrains, &c.<BR>	 m. (-न्ता)<BR>	 1. A charioteer.<BR>	 2. An elephant-driver.<BR>E. यम् to restrain, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्र्|यंत्र्
यन्त्र् r. 1st and 10 cls. (यन्त्रति-ते यन्त्रयति-ते) To restrain: see यत्रि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्र|यंत्र|यंत्रं|यन्त्रं
यन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A machine in general, any implement or apparatus.<BR>	 2.<BR>A diagram of a mystical nature, or astrological character.<BR>	 3. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">Page584-b+ 60</a>]<BR>sort of vessel.<BR>	 4. Restraining, checking, controlling.<BR>	 5. A fetter, a<BR>cord.<BR>	 6. A lock, a bolt.<BR> E. यम् to check, Unādi aff. त्र; or यत्रि-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रक|यंत्रक|यन्त्रकं|यंत्रकः|यन्त्रकः
यन्त्रक m. (-कः) One acquainted with machinery.<BR>	 f. (-का) A wife's<BR>younger sister.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A turner's lathe.<BR>	 2. A bandage, (in<BR>medicine.)<BR> E. यन्त्र a machine or restraining, &c., कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रगृह|यंत्रगृह|यन्त्रगृहं
यन्त्रगृह n. (-हं)<BR>	 1. An oil-mill.<BR>	 2. A manufactory.<BR> E. यन्त्र machine, the<BR>apparatus used for grinding substances yielding oil, गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रगोल|यन्त्रगोलः
यन्त्रगोल m. (-लः) Common-pea.<BR> E. यन्त्र a machine, and गोल round. “मटर ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रण|यंत्रण|यंत्रणं|यन्त्रणं
यन्त्रण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Pain, anguish, affliction.<BR>	 2. Binding, confining.<BR>	 3.<BR>Checking, controlling, especially the passions.<BR>	 4. Guarding, pro-<BR>tecting.<BR> E. यत्रि to restrain, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रणी
यन्त्रणी f. (-णी) A wife's younger sister; also यन्त्रिणी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रपेषणी
यन्त्रपेषणी f. (-णी) A handmill.<BR> E. यन्त्र a machine, पेषणी a stone for grinding on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रित|यंत्रित|यन्त्रितः
यन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bound, tied, chained, fettered.<BR>	 2. Checked,<BR>restrained.<BR> E. यन्त्र restraining, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रितकथ
यन्त्रितकथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Restrained in speech, constrained to be silent.<BR>E. यन्त्रित, कथा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यन्त्रिन्|यंत्रिन्
यन्त्रिन् m. (-न्त्री)<BR>	 1. A horse furnished with harness or trappings.<BR>	 2. A<BR>tormenter.<BR>	 3. One having an amulet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम्
यम् (औ) यमौ r. 1st cl (यमति) To copulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम्
यम् r. 1st cl. (औ, उ) औयमु (यच्छ्वति) To stop, to cease, to refrain. With<BR>नि prefixed, 1. To remove, to dispel.<BR>	 2. To observe as a vow or<BR>religious rite.<BR>	 3. To regulate, to restrain. With उत्, 1. To rise, to<BR>mount on.<BR>	 2. To make effort or exertion.<BR>	 3. To lift up, to raise.<BR>With वि and आङ्, To exercise. With सम् and नि, To restrain. In<BR>some senses it takes the deponent form, as with आङ् prefix,<BR>(आयच्छते) To put forth, to use or employ any part of one's own body<BR>as the hand, &c. (आयच्छति)<BR>	 1. To size.<BR>	 2. To go to, to proceed to,<BR>With सम्, (संयच्छते) To heap together any thing that is one's own.<BR>(संयच्छति) To associate with. With उप, (उपयच्छते) 1. To marry.<BR>	 2.<BR>To agree or accede to.<BR>	 3. To master by learning. r. 10th cl.<BR>(यमयति-ते यामयति)<BR>	 1. To feed, to give food to.<BR>	 2. To restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम|यमः
यम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Twin, fellow, one of the pair or brace.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Restraining, controlling.<BR>	 2. Forbearance, refraining.<BR>	 3. Cessa-<BR>tion, stop, conclusion, finish.<BR>	 4. Religious restraint or obli-<BR>gation, considered the first of the eight steps of Yoga.<BR>	 5.<BR>Penance, purification, the performance of those acts which re-<BR>move impurity of any kind.<BR>	 6. Any of the five acts or virtues,<BR>which constitute pure characters, as refraining from violence or<BR>injury, patience, sincerity, obedience to a spiritual teacher, and<BR>the observance of all purificatory ceremonies.<BR>	 7. A festival.<BR>	 8. A<BR>crow.<BR>	 9. A name of the planet SATURN.<BR>	 10. YAMA, the deity of<BR>Naraka or hell, where his capital is placed, in which he sits in<BR>judgment on the dead, and distributes rewards and punishments,<BR>sending the good to Svarga, and the wicked to the division of<BR>Naraka or Tartarus appropriated to their crimes: he corresponds<BR>with the Grecian god PLUTO, and the judge of hell MINOS, and in<BR>Hindu mythology often identified with Death and Time: he is<BR>the son of SŪRYA, or the sun, and brother of the personified YA-<BR>MUNĀ or Jamunā river.<BR>	 n. (-म) A brace, a couple, a pair.<BR>	 f. (-मी)<BR>The Yamunā river.<BR> E. यम् to restrain, &c., aff. अच्, घञ् or अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमक|यमकं|यमकः
यमक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Twin, fellow, one of a pair or twins.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A religious obligation or observance.<BR>	 2. A twin.<BR>	 3. Restraint,<BR>check.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A species of alliteration, the repetition of<BR>similar words or syllables either in a similar or a dis-similar<BR>sense in various parts of a stanza, beginning, middle, or end of<BR>each hemistich, pervading the whole verse: ten varieties are<BR>enumerated.<BR>	 2. A couple of like articles; (in medicine,) serum<BR>and marrow; oil and ghee, (in diet,) &c.<BR>	 3. A double bandage. E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=584-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमकालिन्दी
यमकालिन्दी f. (-न्दी) SANJNYĀ, the wife of the sun.<BR> E. यम YAMA, and<BR>कालिन्दी the Yamunā river; their mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमकिङ्कर|यमकिङ्करः
यमकिङ्कर m. (-रः) A messenger of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमकीट|यमकीटः
यमकीट m. (-टः) An earth worm.<BR> E. यम YAMA, and कीट a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमज|यमजः
यमज Adj. Twin-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

य|यं|यः
य(ज)मदग्रि m. (-ग्निः)<BR>	 1. The saint JAMADAGNI, the father of the first RĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमदूत|यमदूतः
यमदूत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. An infernal spirit, the messenger or minister of<BR>YAMA, employed to bring the souls of the dead to YAMA'S judg-<BR>ment seat, and thence conduct them to their final destination.<BR>2. A crow.<BR> E. यप्त YAMA, and दूत a messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमदूतक|यमदूतकः
यमदूतक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A crow.<BR>	 2. A messenger or minister of YAMA.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-तिका) The tamarisk tree.<BR> E. कन् aff. to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमदेवता
यमदेवता nf. (-तं-ता) The lunar asterism Bharanī.<BR> E. यम YAMA. देवता<BR>deity, the deity or regent of this constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमद्वितीया
यमद्वितीया f. (-या) The second day in the bright-half of KĀRTIKA when<BR>sisters entertain their brothers: see भ्रातृद्वितीया ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमन|यमनं|यमनः
यमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Binding, confining.<BR>	 2. Term, cessation, rest.<BR>	 3. Con-<BR>trolling, restraining.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A name of YAMA.<BR> E. यम् to restrain,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यम|यमः
यम(व)निका f. (-का) A screen of cloth surrounding a tent.<BR> E. यम् to<BR>stop or check, aff. ल्युट्, कन् added, fem. form; also जवनिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमप्रिय|यमप्रियः
यमप्रिय m. (-यः) Indian fig-tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR> E. यम YAMA, प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमभगिनी
यमभगिनी f. (-नी) The YAMUNĀ river.<BR> E. यम YAMA, भगिनी sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमयातना
यमयातना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. The torture inflicted after death by YAMA.<BR>	 2. An<BR>extreme torture, (figuratively.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमरय
यमरय m. (-थः) A buffalo.<BR> E. यम YAMA, and रय a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमराज्
यमराज् m. (-राट्) YAMA, the Indian PLUTO.<BR> E. यम YAMA, and राज् a<BR>ruler; also with a final vowel यमराज m. (-जः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमल|यमलं|यमलः
यमल n. (-लं) A pair, a brace, a couple.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A sort of dress, a<BR>bodice and petticoat.<BR>	 2. A pair.<BR>	 f. (-ला) Violent hic cough.<BR> E. यम्<BR>to refrain, to cease, aff. कलच्; or यमं योगं लाति ला-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमलार्जुनहन्
यमलार्जुनहन् m. (-हा) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. यमलार्जुन a tree so named in the<BR>forest of Brindāvana, हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमवाहन|यमवाहनः
यमवाहन m. (-नः) A buffalo.<BR> E. यम YAMA, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमव्रत|यमव्रतं
यमव्रत n. (-तं) One of the duties of royalty, punishing offences<BR>without regard to persons, or without partiality or prejudice. E.<BR>यम the judge of Tartarus, and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमसभ
यमसभ n. (-भं) The court or tribunal of Yama.<BR> E. यम, सभा assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमसभनीय
यमसभनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging to the court of Yama.<BR> E. यमसभ, छ<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमसाकृत
यमसाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made over to, devoted to, or sent to YAMA. E.<BR>यम with साति aff., and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमसूर्य्य|यमसूर्य
यमसूर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) A building with two halls, one with a western and the<BR>other with a northern aspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमस्वसृ
यमस्वसृ f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. The YAMUNĀ river.<BR>	 2. A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. यम YAMA, स्वसृ the sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमानी
यमानी f. (-नी) A sort of lovage, (Ligusticum ajwaen, Rox.)<BR> E. यम्<BR>to check, (indigestion,) आङ् before, नी to obtain, affs. अण् and<BR>ङीष्; with ण्वुल् aff. यमानिका; it is incorrectly read यवानी, and<BR>यवानिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमान्तक|यमान्तकः
यमान्तक m. (-कः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. यम YAMA, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमिन्
यमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Who or what restrains, checks, &c.<BR>	 m. (-मी) A<BR>sage, who has subdued his sense.<BR> E. यम restraint, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुना
यमुना f. (-ना) The YAMUNĀ or Jamunā river, which rises on the south<BR>side of the Himālaya range, at a short distance to the north-west<BR>of the source of the Ganges, and which after a course of about<BR>378 miles falls into that river immediately below Allāhābād;<BR>in mythology, the personified river is considered as the daughter<BR>of SŪRYA, and sister of YAMA.<BR> E. यम् to stop, (at the Ganges,)<BR>and उनन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुनाजनक|यमुनाजनकः
यमुनाजनक m. (-कः) SŪRYA, or the sun.<BR> E. यमुना the river, जनक father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुनाभिद्
यमुनाभिद् m. (-भिद् or भित्) BALADEVA, the brother of KṚṢṆA. E.<BR>यमुना the Yamunā, and भिद् divider; having divided the river<BR>into two parts with his ploughshare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमुनाभ्रातृ
यमुनाभ्रातृ m. (-ता) A name of YAMA.<BR> E. यमुना the Yamunā, भ्रातृ brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यमेरुका
यमेरुका f. (-का) A Gong, a metal plate, or a large drum used to strike<BR>the hours or watches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययाति|ययातिः
ययाति m. (-तिः) A monarch of India the fifth of the lunar race and son<BR>of NAHUSA. At first he married Devajāni, the only child of SŪKRA,<BR>the preceptor of the demons and subsequently ŚARMISHṬHĀ the<BR>daughter of VRISHAPARVAN, who was ordered by her father to attend<BR>on Devajāni as a servant, as a punishment for her throwing her in<BR>a well. For his marrying and making love to ŚARMISHṬHĀ Yajāti<BR>became old and infirm before his time through the curse of SUKRA,<BR>but having appeased his father-in-law obtained permission to<BR>transfer his decrepitude to any one who would consent to take it.<BR>Out of his five sons PURU complied with his father's wishes. The<BR>King being endowed with renovated youth, passed his time in<BR>the enjoyment of pleasures for a full thousand years, and after<BR>which he restored his youth to PURU and resuming his own de-<BR>crepitude departed to the wood of penance.<BR> E. यस्य वायोरिव याति-<BR>सर्वत्र रथगतिरस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययि|ययिः
ययि m. (-यिः or यी)<BR>	 1. A road.<BR>	 2. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. A horse.<BR> E. या to go, Unādi aff. इ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ययु|ययुः
ययु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. A horse fit for the Aśwamedha sacrifice.<BR>	 2. Any horse.<BR>E. या to go, Unādi aff. कु, the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यर्हि
यर्हि Adv. While, wherefore, when.<BR>	 3. Because. It is the proper cor-<BR>relative of तर्हि but is rarely used in classics.<BR> E. यद्, and र्हिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव|यवः
यव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Barley, (Hordeum hexastichon.)<BR>	 2. The measure of a<BR>barley-corn, considered as equal to six mustard seeds.<BR>	 3. A mea-<BR>sure of length equal to one-eighth of an Angūla.<BR>	 4. A natural<BR>line across the thumb at the second joint, when it may be com-<BR>pared to a grain of barley, and supposed to indicate good fortune.<BR>5. Speed, velocity.<BR>	 6. A double convex lens.<BR> E. यु to join, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक|यवकः
यवक m. (-कः) Barley.<BR> E. यव barley, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक्य|यवक्यं
यवक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं) Fit for or producing barley, a field, &c.<BR> E. यवक barley, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक्षार|यवक्षारः
यवक्षार m. (-रः) Salt-petre, nitre, nitrate of potash.<BR> E. यव barley क्षार<BR>ashes or salt; being prepared, according to some of the com-<BR>mentators, accurately enough, from burnt barley, the potash<BR>being thus procured; according to others it is so termed, from<BR>the crystals being supposed to resemble the spike of the plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवक्षोद|यवक्षोदः
यवक्षोद m. (-दः) Barley meals.<BR> E. यव barley, and क्षोद meal or powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवगण्ड|यवगण्डः
यवगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A kind of eruption on the face.<BR> E. यव for युव youth,<BR>and गण्ड affecting the cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवज|यवजः
यवज m. (-जः) Nitre.<BR> E. यव barley, and ज born: see यवक्षार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवन|यवनः
यवन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A Country; probably Bactria, or it may be extended<BR>from that colony to Ionia, (to which word it bears some resem-<BR>blance,) or still further to Greece: by late Hindu writers, it is<BR>most commonly applied to Arabia.<BR>	 2. A Yavana, apparently ori-<BR>ginally a Greek, but since applied to both the Mohammedan and<BR>European invaders of India, and often used as a general term for<BR>any foreign or barbarous race.<BR>	 3. Speed, velocity.<BR>	 4. A swift horse.<BR>5. Wheat.<BR>	 6. A carrot.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The wife of a Yavana.<BR> E. यु to mix,<BR>aff. युच्; or जु to be swift, and the consonant changed to its ana-<BR>logous semi-vowel; or योनि the womb, (of the cow of VAŚISH-<BR>ṬHA,) and अण् aff.; being born for the purpose of opposing the<BR>armies of VIŚWĀMITRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनप्रिय|यवनप्रियं
यवनप्रिय n. (-यं) Black pepper.<BR> E. यवन a Yavana, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनाचार्य्य|यवनाचार्य|यवनाचार्यः|यवनाचार्य्यः
यवनाचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) An astronomical writer, frequently quoted by Varā-<BR>ha-mihira, and other ancient Hindu astronomers: perhaps<BR>PTOLEMY, or the Greek astronomers collectively.<BR> E. यवन a<BR>Yavana, and आचार्य्य a holy teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=585-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनारि|यवनारिः
यवनारि m. (-रिः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. यवन a Yavana, अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनाल|यवनालः
यवनाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A sort of grass, very generally cultivated, and the<BR>grain extensively eaten, (Andropogon or Holcus bicolor.) “देधान”<BR>2. Barley straw.<BR> E. यव barley, नाल culm or stalk; also यावनाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनालज|यवनालजः
यवनालज m. (-जः) Nitre.<BR> E. यवनाल barly straw, ज produced: see यवक्षार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनिका
यवनिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An outer tent, a screen of cloth surrounding a tent<BR>or tents.<BR>	 2. A YAVANA woman. E. See जवनिका, ज being changed to य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवनेष्ट|यवनेष्टं|यवनेष्टः
यवनेष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Lead.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. Garlic.<BR>	 2. A sort of onion.<BR>	 3. The<BR>Nimba-tree.<BR> E. यवन a Yavana, इष्ट wished, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवप्रख्या
यवप्रख्या f. (-ख्या) A small hard indolent tumour like a barley-corn. E.<BR>यव, and प्रख्या appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवफल|यवफलः
यवफल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A bamboo.<BR>	 2. Indian spikenard.<BR>	 3. A medicinal plant.<BR>(Wrightea anti-dysenterica.)<BR>	 4. An onion.<BR> E. यव barley, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवमध्य|यवमध्यं|यवमध्यः
यवमध्य n. (-ध्यं) A form of penance, diminishing the food daily during<BR>the fortnight, fasting on the new-moon, and gradually aug-<BR>menting the food till the full-moon.<BR>	 f. (-ध्या) A form of metre, a<BR>triplet, the divisions of which are of unequal length, the middle<BR>line having one syllable more than the first or last.<BR> E. यव barley,<BR>मध्य centrical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवमय|यवमयः
यवमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of, or from barley.<BR> E. यव barley, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवलास|यवलासः
यवलास m. (-सः) Nitre, salt-petre.<BR> E. यव barley, and लस् to like, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवशूक|यवशूकः
यवशूक m. (-कः) Nitre, salt-petre.<BR> E. यव barley, शूक the beard of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवस|यवसं
यवस m. (-सः) Meadow or pasturage.<BR> E. यु to mix, असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवसुर|यवसुरं
यवसुर n. (-रं) Spirituous or fermented liquor distilled from barley,<BR>malt-liquor, beer.<BR> E. यव barley, सुरा wine, ष aff. in the neuter<BR>gender; also यवसुरा the second member being unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवागू
यवागू f. (-गूः) Sour gruel, prepared by the spontaneous fermentation<BR>of water in which rice, &c. has been boiled.<BR> E. यु to mix, आगूच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवाग्रज|यवाग्रजः
यवाग्रज m. (-जः) Salt-petre.<BR> E. यव barley, अग्र the top or ear, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवान|यवानः
यवान mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Swift, fleet.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Ligusticum<BR>ajwaen.)<BR>	 2. Bad barley.<BR> E. यव speed, नी to possess, prefix अञ्, and<BR>aff. ड; also with कन् added, fem. form यवानिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवास|यवासः
यवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (Hedysarum alhagi.) “दुरालभा ।” 2. A kind<BR>of Khayer.<BR> E. यु to mix, Unādi aff. आस; with कन् added, यवासक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यविष्ठ|यविष्ठः
यविष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Youngest, very young.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः) A younger bro-<BR>ther.<BR> E. युवन् young, इष्ठन् aff. of the superlative; also with कन्<BR>added, यविष्ठक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यविष्ठवत्|यविष्ठवन्त्
यविष्ठवत् Adv. Like a youth.<BR> E. यविष्ठ, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यवीयस्
यवीयस् m. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Youngest, very young.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A younger<BR>brother.<BR>	 2. A Śūdra.<BR> E. युवन् young, ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यव्य|यव्यं|यव्यः
यव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Fit for barley, sown with barley, &c.<BR>	 m. (-व्यः) A<BR>month.<BR> E. यव barley and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशःपटह|यशःपटहः
यशःपटह m. (-हः) A drum, a double drum.<BR> E. यशस् fame, पटह a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशःशेष|यशःशेषः
यशःशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Dead, (i. e.) having left nothing but glory.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-षः) Death, dying.<BR> E. यशस् fame, शेष end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशद|यशदं
यशद n. (-दं) Zink. (Zinkum.) “दला”<BR> E. य wind, शद to decay, (by which,) aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्
यशस् n. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Glory, fame, celebrity, reputation.<BR>	 2. Splendour, lus-<BR>tre.<BR>	 3. Praise, eulogium.<BR> E. अश् to pervade, to spread abroad, aff.<BR>असुन्, and युट् substituted for the initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्कर|यशस्करः
यशस्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Rendering famous, conferring celebrity. E.<BR>यशस fame, कृ to make, aff. टच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्काम
यशस्काम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Ambitious, desirous of fame or glory.<BR> E. यशस्,<BR>and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्काम्यत्
यशस्काम्यत् mfn. (-म्यन्-म्यती-म्यत्) Desiring fame or glory.<BR> E. यशस्, काम्यत् desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्काय
यशस्काय m. (-यः) Body in the form of fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्वत्|यशस्वन्त्
यशस्वत् mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्) Famous, celebrated.<BR> E. यशस् fame, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्विन्
यशस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि) Famed, renowned, celebrated.<BR>	 f. (-स्विनी)<BR>Wild-cotton.<BR> E. यशस् fame, विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशस्य
यशस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Conferring fame.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Celtis orienta-<BR>lis.) “जीवन्ती वृक्षे ।”<BR> E. यशस् and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशोघ्न
यशोघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Destroying fame, rendering infamous.<BR> E. यशस्,<BR>घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशोद|यशोदः
यशोद m. (-दः) Quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यशोधन
यशोधन Adj. Rich in fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टि|यष्टिः
यष्टि mf. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः or ष्टी)<BR>	 1. A staff, a stick.<BR>	 2. A staff armed with iron,<BR>&c. used as a weapon, a club, a mace.<BR>	 3. A necklace.<BR>	 4. Any<BR>creeping plant.<BR>	 5. Liquorice.<BR>	 6. A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>7. A string, a thread, especially as strung with pearls, &c.<BR>	 8. A<BR>thread in general.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. A flag-staff.<BR>	 2. The arm, and fore-<BR>arm.<BR>	 3. A pillar.<BR>	 4. A support.<BR>	 5. A stalk.<BR>	 6. A branch.<BR> E. यक्ष to<BR>worship, aff. क्तिन्; the क of the compound final rejected; Vāchas-<BR>patya defines it thus:--यज् क्तिन् नि० न सम्प्रसारणम् । This word<BR>implies “thinness” “slenderness” &c. when used at the end of<BR>compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टि|यष्टिः
यष्टि(ष्टी)क m. (-कः) A bird, the lapwing. “तितिरपाखी” f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A pearl-<BR>necklace, especially of but one string.<BR>	 2. A pond, a pool.<BR>	 3.<BR>Liquorice 4. A club, a staff, a bludgeon.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टिग्रह|यष्टिग्रहः
यष्टिग्रह m. (-हः) A club-bearer, one carrying a staff or stick.<BR> E. यष्टि a<BR>stick, and ग्रह् to take, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टिमधु
यष्टिमधु n. (-धु) Liquorice, or the root of the Abrus precatorius.<BR>E. यष्टि a stick, and मधु honey; also with कन् added, fem. form<BR>यष्टिमधुका; and with the final of the first word long<BR>यष्टीमधु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यष्टृ
यष्टृ m. (-ष्टा) A sacrificer, one who employs priests for a sacrifice. E.<BR>यज् to worship, aff. तृच्, and ज changed to ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस्
यस् (इर्, उ) इर् यसु r. 1st and 10th cls. (यसति यस्यति)<BR>	 1. To endeavour, to<BR>persevere, to make strenuous and presevering exertion.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>afflicted. With आङ् prefixed, To labour. With निर्, To exude. r.<BR>10th cl. (यासयति-ते) With आ, To torment, to trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस्य
यस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) To be done with energy or perseverance.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be killed or put to death.<BR> E. यस् to strive, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यस्यत्व
यस्यत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Death, being killed.<BR>	 2. Effort, energy.<BR> E. त्व added to<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यह्व|यह्वः
यह्व m. (-ह्वः) A sacrificer, an institutor of sacrifices.<BR> E. या to go, वन्<BR>Unādi aff., and हुक् augment, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

या
या r. 2nd cl. (याति)<BR>	 1. To go, to go to.<BR>	 2. To obtain, to get.<BR>	 3. To<BR>invade.<BR>	 4. To withdraw.<BR>	 5. To elapse, (as time.)<BR>	 6. To come to<BR>pass, to become.<BR>	 7. To have carnal intercourse with.<BR>	 8. To re-<BR>quest.<BR>	 9. To attempt.<BR>	 10. To discover. With अनु, prefixed, To<BR>follow. With अभि, To approach. to reach. With आङ्, To come,<BR>to arrive. With उप, To give way, to yield. With निर्, 1. To go<BR>out or forth.<BR>	 2. To go readily or quickly. With प्र, To go to.<BR>With प्रति, To go to or towards. With प्रति and उत्, To meet, to<BR>advance to. With सम् and अभि, To approach. With सम् and आङ्,<BR>To arrive. With अति, 1. To transgress.<BR>	 2. To surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याग|यागः
याग m. (-गः) A sacrifice, any ceremony in which offerings and obla-<BR>tions are presented.<BR> E. यज् to worship, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्
याच् (टु, ऋ) टुयाचृ r. 1st cl. (याचति-ते)<BR>	 1. To ask or beg, to solicit, to re-<BR>quest.<BR>	 2. To offer, to tender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचक|याचकः
याचक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Beggar, mendicant, asking, one who asks, or<BR>solicits.<BR> E. याच् to ask, aff. ण्वुल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचनक|याचनकः
याचनक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Beggar, mendicant.<BR> E. याचन an asker, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचना
याचना f. (-ना) Asking, begging.<BR> E. याच् to ask, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचमान|याचमानः
याचमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Asking, soliciting.<BR> E. याच् to ask, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचनीय
याचनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be asked, &c.<BR> E. याच् to ask, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचित|याचितं
याचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Asked, begged, solicited.<BR> E. याच् to ask, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याचितक|याचितकं
याचितक n. (-कं) A thing borrowed for use.<BR> E. याचित asked, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्य|याच्यं
याच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) To be asked, begged, &c.<BR> E. याच् to ask, ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याच्यमान
याच्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being asked.<BR> E. याच् to ask, pass. v., शानचे aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=586-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञा
याज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) Asking, begging.<BR> E. याच् to ask, नङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज|याजः
याज m. (-जः) Boiled-rice, or generally food.<BR> E. यज् to present, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजक|याजकः
याजक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An officiating priest, a Brāhamana who conducts<BR>any part of a sacrifice.<BR>	 2. A royal elephant.<BR>	 3. A furious elephant.<BR>E. यज् to worship, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजन|याजनं
याजन n. (-नं) Conducting a sacrifice or causing its performance.<BR> E. यज्<BR>to worship, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजि|याजिः
याजि m. (-जिः) A sacrificer, an institutor of sacrificial ceremonies. E.<BR>यज् to sacrifice, Unādi aff. इञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजिन्
याजिन् m. (-जी) Sacrificing, one who officiates at a sacrifice.<BR> E. यज् to sacrifice, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याजुष|याजुषं|याजुषः
याजुष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Belonging to or relating to the Yajur-Veda. E.<BR>यजुर् or यजुस् the Veda, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञदत्ति
याज्ञदत्ति m. (-त्तिः) KUVERA.<BR> E. यज्ञदत्त a proper name, इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञवल्क्य|याज्ञवल्क्यः
याज्ञवल्क्य m. (-ल्क्यः) A celebrated saint and legislator; the supposed<BR>author of a celebrated code of laws, and the first reputed teacher<BR>of the white portion of the Yayar-Veda revealed to him by the<BR>sun.<BR> E. यज्ञवल्क the father of the saint, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञसेनी
याज्ञसेनी f. (-नी) A name of DRAUPADĪ, the wife of the Pāṇḍavas. E.<BR>यज्ञसेन the father of the princess, अण् patronymic aff., fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिक|याज्ञिकः
याज्ञिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sacrificer, an institutor of a sacrifice.<BR>	 2. An<BR>officiating priest at a sacrifical ceremony.<BR>	 3. Kuśa or sacrificial<BR>grass.<BR> E. यज्ञ sacrifice, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिक्य|याज्ञिक्यं
याज्ञिक्य n. (-क्यं) Sacrifice, sacrificial ceremonies.<BR> E. याज्ञिक a sacrificer, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्ञिय|याज्ञियः
याज्ञिय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Fit for sacrifice.<BR> E. यज्ञिय, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याज्य|याज्यं|याज्यः
याज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) To be offered or sacrificed.<BR>	 m. (-ज्यः) A sacri-<BR>ficer, the person for whom it is performed.<BR>	 n. (-ज्यं) Property or<BR>presents derived from officiating at sacrifices.<BR> E. यज् to worship,<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्
यात् Ind. An interjection. I. Of pleasure.<BR>	 2. Of alarm.<BR>	 3. Of restlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्
यात् m. (-यान्-यान्ती-यात्) Going.<BR> E. या to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात|यातं|यातः
यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone, went.<BR>	 2. Obtained, got.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Driving<BR>or guiding an elephant with a goad.<BR>	 2. Going, motion.<BR>	 3. The<BR>pastime.<BR> E. यत् to endeavour, or या to go, aff. श ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातन|यातनं
यातन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Requital, recompense.<BR>	 2. Revenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातना
यातना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Pain, agony, sharp or acute pain.<BR>	 2. Pain or punish-<BR>ment inflicted by YAMA or his ministers, the pains of hell.<BR> E. यत्<BR>to inflict pain, aff. युच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातयाम|यातयामं
यातयाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Old.<BR>	 2. Used, impaired.<BR>	 3. Rejected, abando-<BR>ned.<BR>	 4. Raw, half-ripe or dressed.<BR>	 5. Aged, exhausted.<BR> E. यात<BR>gone or got, याम forbearance, relinquishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातव्य
यातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be gone.<BR>	 2. To be gone against, to be<BR>attacked or invaded.<BR> E. या to go, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातु|यातुः
यातु mfn. (-तुः-तुः-तु) A goer, one who goes or moves.<BR>	 m. (-तुः) A demon,<BR>a goblin, an imp or evil spirit.<BR>	 m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. A traveller, a<BR>wayfarer.<BR>	 3. Wind.<BR> E. या to go, तु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातुधान|यातुधानः
यातुधान m. (-नः) A goblin, an evil spirit.<BR> E. यातु the same, धा to have, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यातृ
यातृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A charioteer, a driver.<BR>	 2. A husband's brother's wife.<BR>E. यत् to endeavour assiduously, Unādi aff. ऋत्, and the radical<BR>vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्य|यात्यं|यात्यः
यात्य m. (-त्यः) An infernal or condemned spirit.<BR> E. यत् to endeavour,<BR>causal form, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रा
यात्रा f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. Going moving, proceeding, marching travelling.<BR>	 2.<BR>Passing away time.<BR>	 3. Practice, usage, custom.<BR>	 4. A holy festival,<BR>but especially the procession of idols, &c. which usually forms<BR>part of the ceremonies on such an occasion.<BR>	 5. An expedient, a<BR>means.<BR>	 6. The march of an assailing force.<BR>	 7. Going to pilgrimage.<BR>8. A sort of dramatic entertainment.<BR>	 9. Intercourse.<BR>	 10. Way,<BR>means.<BR>	 11. A vehicle in general.<BR> E. या to go, Unādi aff. ष्ट्रन्<BR>or त्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्राकरण
यात्राकरण n. (-णं) Setting forth on a journey, &c.<BR> E. यात्रा, करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्राप्रसङ्ग|यात्राप्रसंगः
यात्राप्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Performing a pilgrimage.<BR> E. यात्रा, प्रसङ्ग engaging in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रिक|यात्रिकः
यात्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating to a march, &c.<BR>	 2. Customary,<BR>usual.<BR>	 3. Requisite for the support of life.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A pilgrim.<BR>2. A traveller.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Provision, supplies, conveyance, &c., for a<BR>march.<BR> E. यात्रा and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यात्रोत्सव|यात्रोत्सवः
यात्रोत्सव m. (-वः) A public festival.<BR> E. यात्रा procession, उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथातथ्य|याथातथ्यं
याथातथ्य n. (-थ्यं) Rectitude, truth, propriety.<BR> E. यथातथा, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथार्थिक
याथार्थिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Just, true.<BR> E. यथार्थ, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याथार्थ्य|याथार्थ्यं
याथार्थ्य n. (-र्थ्यं) Application, use, accomplishment, attainment of an<BR>object.<BR> E. यथार्थ, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादईश|यादईशः
यादईश m. (-शः) The ocean.<BR> E. यादस् an aquatic animal, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादःपति|यादःपतिः
यादःपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. VARUṆA, regent of water.<BR> E. यादस्<BR>a fish, &c., and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादव|यादवः
यादव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. KṚṢṆA, as descended from the family of Yadu.<BR>	 2.<BR>A Yādava, or descendant of Yadu.<BR>	 f. (-वी) A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-वं) Stock of cattle.<BR> E. यदु a proper name, अण् aff. of descent, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादस्
यादस् n. (-दः) Any aquatic or amphibious animal.<BR> E. या to go, (with<BR>speed,) असुन् aff., and दुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादसांनाथ
यादसांनाथ m. (-थः) VARUṆA, the deity of water.<BR> E. यादस् an aquatic<BR>animal, in the sixth case plural, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादसाम्पति|यादसांपति|यादसांपतिः
यादसाम्पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. VARUṆA.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR> E. यादसाम्, पति lord: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादृच्छिक|यादृच्छिकः
यादृच्छिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Independent, following one's own will.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) A ministering priest who does as he pleases.<BR> E. यदृच्छा, ठञ्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादृश्
यादृश् mfn. (-दृक्) As like, how like, which like.<BR> E. यद् what, दृश् to see,<BR>क्किन् aff., form irr.; also with खञ् aff. यादृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) and<BR>with क्स added यादृक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यादोनिवासस्
यादोनिवासस् n. (-सः) Water.<BR> E. यादज् an aquatic animal, निवासस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यान|यानं|यानः
यान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Any vehicle or form of conveyance, as a carriage, a litter,<BR>a horse, an elephant, &c.<BR>	 2. Going, marching, proceeding.<BR>	 3. In-<BR>vading, marching against an enemy.<BR> E. या to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यानपात्र|यानपात्रं
यानपात्र n. (-त्रं) A vessel, a ship, a boat.<BR> E. यान going, (by water,)<BR>and पात्र a cup or vessel; also with कन् added यानपात्रक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यानमुख|यानमुखं
यानमुख n. (-खं) The forepart of a carriage, the pole or part where the<BR>yoke is fixed<BR> E. यान a vehicle, and मुख face or front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यानस्वामिन्
यानस्वामिन् m. (-मी) The owner of a vehicle.<BR> E. यान and स्वामिन् master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापन|यापनं
यापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Spending or passing away time.<BR>	 2. Abinding, staying,<BR>being.<BR>	 3. Rejection, ejection, expelling, expulsion.<BR>	 4. Allaying, al-<BR>leviating, (as pain or sickness.)<BR> E. या to go, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यापनीय
यापनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be passed or spent as time.<BR>	 2. To be al-<BR>layed or relieved though not cured, (disease or a sick person.) E.<BR>या to go, causal. v. अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याप्ता
याप्ता f. (-प्ता) Twisted or matted hair.<BR> E. या to, in the causal form, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याप्य|याप्यः
याप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>	 1. Low, vile, contemptible.<BR>	 2. To be passed or<BR>spent, (as time, &c.)<BR>	 3. (In medicine,) To be alleviated or relieved<BR>though not cured, (disease.)<BR> E. या to go, causal form, aff. णिच्-ण्यत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याप्ययान|याप्ययानं
याप्ययान n. (-नं) A litter, a palanquin.<BR> E. याप्य vile, and यान a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम|यामः
याम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Relating to YAMA, done by him, ordered by him,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The eighth part of a day, a watch of three hours.<BR>	 2.<BR>Forbearance.<BR>	 3. Cessation, term.<BR> E. या to go, (through the day,)<BR>मन् Unādi aff.; or यम् to restrain, aff. घञ्; or यम्, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामघोष|यामघोषः
यामघोष m. (-षः) A cock.<BR>	 f. (-षा) A clock, a metal plate to which the<BR>hours are struck, or a drum used for similar purpose.<BR> E. याम a<BR>watch, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामनाली
यामनाली f. (-ली) A metal plate on which the hours are struck, or a<BR>drum used for that purpose.<BR> E. याम a watch, नाली the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामनेमि|यामनेमिः
यामनेमि m. (-मिः) A name of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामयम|यामयमः
यामयम m. (-मः) A regular occupation for every hour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामल|यामलं
यामल n. (-लं) A pair, a couple, a brace.<BR> E. यमल, अण् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामवती
यामवती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. Turmeric.<BR> E. याम a watch, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=587-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामवृत्ति|यामवृत्तिः
यामवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) The being on watch or guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामातृ
यामातृ m. (-ता) A daughter's husband.<BR> E. य substituted for ज; see जामातृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामि|यामिः
यामि f. (-मिः-मी)<BR>	 1. A sister.<BR>	 2. A virtuous woman.<BR>	 3. Night.<BR>	 4. The<BR>south.<BR>	 5. Relating to YAMA.<BR>	 6. A daughter, or daughter-in-law,<BR>newly married.<BR> E. या to go, मि aff.; or य substituted for जः see<BR>जामि; or यम YAMA, इन् aff. of reference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिका
यामिका f. (-का) Night.<BR> E. याम a watch, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिनी
यामिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Night 2. Turmeric.<BR> E. याम a watch, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामिनीपति|यामिनीपतिः
यामिनीपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. यामिनी night, पति<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामीर|यामीरः
यामीर m. (-रः) The moon.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Night.<BR> E. यामी night, रा to have or be, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामुन|यामुनं
यामुन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Relating to the Yamunā river.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Antimony,<BR>or rather the sulphuret of antimony, generally used as an appli-<BR>cation to darken the eyelashes, and strengthen the eyes.<BR> E. यमुना<BR>the Jamunā river, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामुनेष्ठक
यामुनेष्ठक n. (-कं) Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यामेय|यामेयः
यामेय m. (-यः) A sister's son.<BR> E. यामि a sister, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम्य|याम्यः
याम्य m. (-म्यः)<BR>	 1. Sandal.<BR>	 2. The saint AGASTYA.<BR>	 f. (-म्या)<BR>	 1. The south.<BR>2. The lunar asterism, Bharaṇi.<BR>	 3. Night.<BR> E. यम YAMA, ण्यत् aff.;<BR>being sacred to or governed by that deity, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम्यायन|याम्यायनं
याम्यायन n. (-नं) The sun's course, south of the line, the winter sols-<BR>tice.<BR> E. याम्य the south, अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याम्योत्तर
याम्योत्तर Adj. Going from south to north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायजूक|यायजूकः
यायजूक m. (-कः) The performer of frequent sacrifices.<BR> E. यज् to sacrifice.<BR>aff. ऊक, the root repeated, and the first vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायावर|यायावरः
यायावर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Going repeatedly.<BR>	 2. Wandering, vagrant.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः)<BR>	 1. A horse fit for the Aśwamedha sacrifice.<BR>	 2. The saint<BR>JARATKĀRU.<BR>	 3. A Brāhmana who has preserved his household-<BR>fire.<BR>	 4. A vagrant.<BR> E. या to go, in the reiterative form, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यायिन्
यायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Going, who or what goes.<BR> E. या to go, णिनि<BR>aff., युक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याव|यावः
याव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Relating to barley.<BR>	 m. (-वः) Lac, the red animal-<BR>dye.<BR> E. यु to join, aff. अण्; the nest yielding a sort of resinous<BR>substance used as sealing-wax: or यत barley, to which the grains<BR>of the dye are compared, and अप्-अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावक|यावकं|यावकः
यावक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Half-ripe barley.<BR>	 2. Awnless barley 3. A sort of kid-<BR>ney-bean, (Phaseolus)<BR>	 4. A kind of pulse, (Dolichos biflorus.)<BR>	 5.<BR>A kind of pulse said to be peculiar to Cashmir.<BR>	 6. Lac.<BR> E. यु to<BR>mix, aff. वुन्, and अण् added; or याव as above, pleonastic aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावच्छक्य
यावच्छक्य Adv. (-क्यं) To the utmost of one's power.<BR> E. यावत् and शक्य able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावज्जीव|यावज्जीवं
यावज्जीव Adv. (-वं) For life, as long as life.<BR> E. यावत् until, जीव life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावत्|यावन्त्
यावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) As much, how much, such. Ind.<BR>	 1. As much<BR>as.<BR>	 2. As many as.<BR>	 3. As long as.<BR>	 4. As far as, until, unto.<BR>	 5.<BR>When, (i. e. as much, applied to time.); the correlative of<BR>तावत्.<BR> E. यत् what or which, डवतुप् aff. and आ substituted for the<BR>pronominal final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावतिथ|यावतिथः
यावतिथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) That which is as far as, or as much as, &c. the<BR>ordinal of the particle यावत्<BR> E. यावत् as much as. &c. and तिथक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावत्तावत्
यावत्तावत् Ind.<BR>	 1. As much as, quantum-tantum.<BR>	 2. (In algebra,) The<BR>relation of the unknown number and its co-efficient.<BR> E. यावत्, तावत्<BR>so much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावन|यावनः
यावन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Belonging or relating to a Yavana, Ionian,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Incense.<BR> E. यवन the country of the Yavanas, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावनाल|यावनालः
यावनाल m. (-लः) A kind of grain, (Zea mays.) “जनार”.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Sugar<BR>prepared from Zea mays.<BR> E. यवनाल, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावशूक|यावशूकः
यावशूक m. (-कः) Nitre, salt-petre.<BR> E. यव barley, शूक the spike, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यावस|यावसः
यावस m. (-सः) A quantity or heap of grass.<BR> E. यु to mix, Unādi aff.<BR>असच् with the effect of णित्, which makes the vowel long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याव्य|याव्यं
याव्य mfn. (-व्या-व्या-व्यं) To be mixed or joined, miscible.<BR> E. यु to join or<BR>mix, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याशोधरेय|याशोधरेयः
याशोधरेय m. (-यः) The son of ŚĀKYAMUNI, the probable founder of the<BR>Bauddha sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

याष्टीक|याष्टीकः
याष्टीक m. (-कः) A warrior armed with a club.<BR> E. यष्टि a stick, a club,<BR>ठक् aff., and both vowels made long; or यष्टिः-ईकक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यास|यासः
यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Hedysarum alhagi) “दुरालभायाम्”.<BR>	 2. Effort.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-सा) A sort of bird, the Sālika.<BR> E. यस् to endeavour, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यास्क|यास्कः
यास्क m. (-स्कः) Name of the author of NIRUKTA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यास्यत्
यास्यत् mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यती-स्यत्) Going, who or what will be going.<BR> E. या to<BR>go, शतृ aff. with the future tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियक्षमान
यियक्षमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Purposing or wishing to worship.<BR> E. यज् to<BR>worship, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियक्षु
यियक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Desirous of sacrificing.<BR> E. यज् to worship, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियविषा
यियविषा f. (-षा) Wish to mix, blend, &c.<BR> E. यु to mix, desid. v., अङ् and<BR>टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यियविषु
यियविषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to mix or blend.<BR> E. यु to mix, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यु
यु r. 2nd cl. (यौति)<BR>	 1. To mix, to join, to blend.<BR>	 2. To separate or not<BR>mix. r. 10th cl. (यावयते) To censure, to blame, to disrespect, to<BR>despise. (ञ) युञ् r. 9th cl. (युनाति युनीते) To bind, to tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्
युक् Ind. Badly, ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्त|युक्तं|युक्तः
युक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Joined, combined, united, identified.<BR>	 2. Right,<BR>fit, proper.<BR>	 3. Proved, concluded by inference or argument.<BR>	 4. Mo-<BR>derate, limited.<BR>	 5. Possessing, endowed with, as virtues, qualities,<BR>&c.<BR>	 6. Intent on, attached to, as a study or pursuit.<BR>	 7. Employed or<BR>engaged in business, &c.<BR>	 8. Occupied in performance of the reli-<BR>gious exercise called Yoga.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) The sage who has acquired the<BR>command of his feelings and passions, and who performs the cus-<BR>tomary devotional offices without any regard to their result.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-क्तं)<BR>	 1. A measure of four cubits.<BR>	 2. A team, a yoke.<BR>	 f. (-क्ता) A<BR>plant, commonly Elāni.<BR> E. युज् to join or mix, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तरसा
युक्तरसा f. (-सा) A plant, commonly Elāni, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR> E. युक्त<BR>mixed, joined, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तायस्
युक्तायस् n. (-यः) A sort of wooden spade or shovel.<BR> E. युक्त bound, joined, अयस् iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्ति|युक्तिः
युक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Union, connection, joining.<BR>	 2. Propriety, fitness.<BR>	 3.<BR>Usage, custom, traditionary and unwritten law.<BR>	 4. Inference, de-<BR>duction from circumstance or argument, the reason of a thing or<BR>argument.<BR>	 5. Insertion of circumstances in written evidence,<BR>specification in writting of place, time, &c., considered as one of the<BR>means of verifying such evidence.<BR>	 6. A figure of rhetoric, emble-<BR>matic or mystical expression of purpose, so as to conceal it form<BR>all but its immediate object.<BR>	 7. Supplying an ellipsis.<BR>	 8. Connec-<BR>tion of dramatic events, the production of one incident by ano-<BR>ther.<BR>	 9. Alloying of metals.<BR> E. युज् to join, &c., aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तिकर
युक्तिकर Adj.<BR>	 1. Suitable.<BR>	 2. Proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युक्तियुक्त
युक्तियुक्त Adj.<BR>	 1. Expert.<BR>	 2. Suitable, fit.<BR>	 3. Proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्
युग् (इ) युगि r. 1st cl. (युङ्गति) To except, to abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग|युगं|युगः
युग n. (-गं)<BR>	 1. A pair, a couple, a brace.<BR>	 2. An age, as the Śatya or<BR>Krita, Tretā, Dwāpara, and Kali.<BR>	 3. A lustre, or period of five<BR>years.<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A yoke.<BR>	 2. A measure of four cubits.<BR>	 3. An ex-<BR>pression for the numbers “four and “twelve”.<BR>	 4. Life, birth.<BR>	 5. A<BR>drug, commonly Riddhi.<BR> E. युज् to join, aff. अच, the final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगकीलक|युगकीलकः
युगकीलक m. (-कः) The pin of a yoke.<BR> E. युग a yoke, कील a pin, कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगक्षय|युगक्षयः
युगक्षय m. (-यः) Destruction of the world.<BR> E. युग and क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगन्धर|युगंधर|युगंधरं|युगंधरः|युगन्धरः
युगन्धर mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. The pole of a carriage, or wood to which the<BR>yoke is fixed.<BR>	 2. The name of a mountain.<BR> E. युग a yoke, धृ to hold<BR>or support, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपत्
युगपत् Ind.<BR>	 1. At one time, at once.<BR>	 2. Together, conjointly.<BR> E. यु to join, गपतक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगप
युगप(पा)त्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A sort of ebony.<BR>	 2. The Ashmantā a tree.<BR>	 3.<BR>The Lodh or Lodhra tree, (symplocos racemosa.): see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपत्रक|युगपत्रकः
युगपत्रक m. (-कः) Mountain-ebony, (Bauhinia variegata.) “रक्त्रकाञ्चनार-<BR>वृक्षे”.<BR>	 f. (-त्रिका)<BR>	 1. The Sishu-tree, (Dalbergia Sishu.) “शिंशपावृक्षे.”<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">Page589-a+ 60</a>]<BR>2. The Sarsapa-tree, (sinapis dichotoma.)<BR> E. युग a pair, पत्र a leaf,<BR>aff. कन्, double-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=588-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगपार्श्वग|युगपार्श्वगः
युगपार्श्वग m. (-गः) A young ox in training.<BR> E. युग a yoke, पार्श्व a side,<BR>and ग who goes, or with कन् aff. युगपार्श्वक m. (-कः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगल|युगलं
युगल n. (-लं) A pair, a brace, a couple.<BR> E. युग a pair, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगलक|युगलकं
युगलक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A hair.<BR>	 2. Two verses forming one sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगांशक|युगांशकः
युगांशक m. (-कः) A year.<BR> E. युग an age, and अंशक a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगान्त|युगांत|युगान्तः
युगान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A destruction of the universe.<BR>	 2. The end of an age.<BR>3. Mid-day, noon.<BR>	 4. The end of a yoke.<BR> E. युग an age, either ge-<BR>nerally or individually, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युगान्तबन्धु
युगान्तबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A real friend, a friend in need.<BR> E. युगान्त, बन्धु a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्म|युग्मं
युग्म n. (-ग्मं)<BR>	 1. A pair, a couple, a brace.<BR>	 2. A twin.<BR>	 3. Mixing, unit-<BR>ing.<BR>	 4. A couple of verses.<BR>	 5. The sign Gemini of the Zodiac.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ग्मा) Even.<BR> E. युज् to join, Unādi aff. मक्, the final changed to ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मक
युग्मक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A couple.<BR>	 2. A couple of verses connected by the con-<BR>struction of the sentence, the sense being completed only by the<BR>two together.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मपत्र|युग्मपत्रः
युग्मपत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Alstonia scholaris. Syn. Echites scholaris.)<BR>2. The Sishu-tree.<BR>	 3. The Rakta-Kānchana tree, (Bauhinia varie-<BR>gata.)<BR>	 4. The Bhūrja-patra tree.<BR> E. युग्म a couple, and पत्र a leaf,<BR>doble-leaved: see युगपत्रक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मपत्रिका
युग्मपत्रिका f. (-का) A timber-tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.): see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्मफलोत्तम
युग्मफलोत्तम m. (-मः) A plant, (Asclepias rosea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युग्य|युग्यं|युग्यः
युग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Fit or proper to be yoked or harnessed.<BR>	 n. (-ग्यं)<BR>Any vehicle or conveyance.<BR>	 m. (-ग्यः) An animal yoked, a carriage-<BR>horse.<BR> E. युज् to join, aff. यत् or क्यप्; जस्य ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युच्छ्|युछ्
युच्छ् r. 1st cl. (युच्छति) To be inattentive or negligent, to err or mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज् (औ) युजी r. 4th cl. (युज्यते)<BR>	 1. To confine the thoughts, to keep the<BR>mind fixed in abstract meditation.<BR>	 2. To be fit.<BR>	 3. To be right. r.<BR>1st and 10th cls. (योजति योजयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To bind, to tie, to connect.<BR>2. To yoke.<BR>	 3. To instigate.<BR>	 4. To oblige.<BR>	 5. To put to. With नि,<BR>To yoke. With सम, To unite. (योजयते) To blame. (औ इर्,) औ युजिर्<BR>r. 7th cl. (युनक्ति युङ्क्ते)<BR>	 1. To join, to mix, to unite, &c.<BR>	 2. To apply,<BR>to use.<BR>	 3. To prepare, to make ready.<BR>	 4. To meditate.<BR>	 5. To grant to<BR>endow.<BR>	 6. To design, to intend, &c. With अनु prefixed, 1. To ask,<BR>to inquire.<BR>	 2. To reprove. With अभि, 1. To utter, to speak.<BR>	 2. To<BR>accuse.<BR>	 3. To claim. With उत्, 1. To make effort.<BR>	 2. To prepare.<BR>With उप, 1. To seize, to take, to lay hold of.<BR>	 2. To eat.<BR>	 3. To use.<BR>With नि, 1. To order, to appoint, (with a loc.)<BR>	 2. To join. With प्र<BR>1. To be fit or due.<BR>	 2. To attach or apply to.<BR>	 3. To lend money.<BR>4. To make effort.<BR>	 5. To combine or connect.<BR>	 6. To give.<BR>	 7. To<BR>move.<BR>	 8. To perform on the stage. With वि, 1. To separate, to<BR>sunder.<BR>	 2. To send.<BR>	 3. To leave, to abandon. With वि and नि, 1.<BR>To appoint or employ.<BR>	 2. To expend.<BR>	 3. To send.<BR>	 4. To involve<BR>in or force upon. With वि and प्र, To separate, to part, to divide.<BR>With सम्, To unite, to combine. With सम् and आङ्, To think<BR>profoundly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युज्
युज् n. (युक्) A pair, a couple.<BR>	 m. (-युक्-युग्) A sage, one who devotes<BR>his time to abstract contemplation. Dual. (-जौ) The twin-sons of<BR>AŚHWINĪ, and physicians of Svarga.<BR>	 m. (-युङ्) A joiner, one who<BR>joins, or unites.<BR>	 f. (-युक्) A measure of three hundred poles.<BR> E. युज्<BR>to join to meditate, &c., aff. क्विप्; also युजिर् the same, with the<BR>same aff., when न is inserted after the vowel, before the first<BR>five affixes in the masculine and feminine genders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युञ्जत्
युञ्जत् mfn. (-ञ्जन्-ञ्जन्ती-ञ्जत्)<BR>	 1. Uniting, Joining.<BR>	 2. Uniting spiritually,<BR>practising devotion.<BR> E. युज् to join, &c., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युञ्जान|युंजान|युञ्जानः
युञ्जान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Uniting, combining, joining with.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>charioteer.<BR>	 2. A Brāhmana engaged in the religious exercise called<BR>Yoga.<BR> E. युज् to join, &c., aff. शानच् and नुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत्
युत् (ऋ) युतृ r. 1st cl. (योतते) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत्
युत् Ind. Badly, ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युत|युतं|युतः
युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Joined, combined, connected, identified.<BR>	 2. Atta-<BR>ched to, engaged in or by.<BR>	 3. Endowed with, possessed of.<BR>	 4. Sepa-<BR>rated.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A measure of four cubits.<BR> E. यु to join, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युतक|युतकं
युतक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Joined, combined.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>2. A pair, a brace.<BR>	 3. Nuptial presents.<BR>	 4. The end of a cloth worn<BR>by women.<BR>	 5. A garment worn by women; it is applied, both<BR>to the petti-coat and the upper wrapper or cloth.<BR>	 6. The<BR>ends of a cloth.<BR>	 7. The edge of a winnowing basket.<BR>	 8. Asylum.<BR>9. Forbearance, cessation.<BR>	 10. Alliance, acquaintance, forming an<BR>alliance, friendship.<BR> E. युत joined, &c., कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युति|युतिः
युति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Joining, uniting.<BR>	 2. Obtaining possession of.<BR>	 3. A con-<BR>junction, (in astro.)<BR>	 4. (In arith.) Addition.<BR> E. यु to join, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्ध|युद्धं
युद्ध n. (-द्धं)<BR>	 1. War, battle, contest.<BR>	 2. Conflict of the planets, (in as-<BR>tronomy.)<BR> E. युध् to fight, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्धरङ्ग|युद्धरंग|युद्धरङ्गः
युद्धरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. A battle-arena.<BR> E. युद्ध war, and रङ्ग delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्धवीर|युद्धवीरः
युद्धवीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A warrior.<BR>	 2. A warlike hero in a poem.<BR>	 3. The<BR>sentiment of heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्धसार|युद्धसारः
युद्धसार m. (-रः) A horse.<BR> E. युद्ध war, सृ to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युद्धोन्मत्त
युद्धोन्मत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Fierce or frantic in battle.<BR> E. युद्ध, उन्मत्त frantic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्
युध् (औ) औयुध् r. 4th cl. (युध्यते) To fight, to contend in battle, to slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्
युध् f. (युत् or युद्) War, battle.<BR> E. युध् to fight, aff. क्विप् or टाप् also युध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधान|युधानः
युधान m. (-नः) A man of the second or military order, a warrior.<BR> E. युध्<BR>to fight, Unādi aff. आनच्, and the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युधिष्ठिर|युधिष्ठिरः
युधिष्ठिर m. (-रः) The elder of the five Pāṇḍava princes, and leader in the<BR>great war, between them and the Kurus, in the beginning of the<BR>fourth age; the nominal son of PĀṆḌU whom he succeeded in<BR>the sovereignty of India, but according to the legend, begotten on<BR>Kunti by the deity YAMA.<BR> E. युधि in war or battle, and ष्ठिर for<BR>स्थिर firm; it is also sometimes read युद्धस्थिर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्म|युध्मः
युध्म m. (-ध्मः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. A bow.<BR>	 3. An arrow.<BR>	 4. A warrior, a<BR>combatant.<BR> E. युध् to fight, मक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युध्यमान
युध्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fighting, warring.<BR> E. युध् to fight, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युप्
युप् (इर्) युपीर r. 4th cl. (युप्यति) To confuse, to perplex.<BR>	 2. To trouble.<BR>3. To efface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयु|युयुः
युयु m. (-युः) A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुक्खुर|युयुक्खुरः
युयुक्खुर m. (-रः) A hyena.<BR> E. युयुक् joined, खुर a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुक्षमान
युयुक्षमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Wishing to join or unite.<BR>	 2. Devout, wish-<BR>ing to effect spiritual union with the divine essence.<BR> E. युज् to<BR>be devout or to join, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सा
युयुत्सा f. (-त्सा) Wish or purpose to fight, enmity, pugnacity.<BR> E. युध् to<BR>fight, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सारहित
युयुत्सारहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cowardly, having no intention to fight.<BR> E. युयुत्सा, रहित void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुत्सु|युयुत्सुः
युयुत्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु) Wishing or ready to make war or fight, pug-<BR>nacious, hostile, ambitious.<BR>	 m. (-त्सुः) A combatant.<BR> E. युध् to make<BR>war, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युयुधान|युयुधानः
युयुधान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A proper name, one of the chiefs of the Pāṇḍus.<BR>	 2.<BR>A warrior.<BR> E. युध् to fight, in the reduplicate form, कानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवखलति
युवखलति mfn. (-तिः-तिः or ती-ति) Bald in youth.<BR> E. युवन् and खलति bald;<BR>also युवाखलति, and fem. युवतिःखलति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवगण्ड|युवगण्डः
युवगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Eruptions on the face peculiar to youth.<BR> E. युव a<BR>young person, from युवन्, and गण्ड what affects the cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवजरत्|युवजरन्त्
युवजरत् mfn. (-रन्-रती-रत्) Being old as it were in youth, old-fashioned,<BR>or prematurely infirm.<BR> E. युवन्, and जरत् old; also युवाजरत् and in<BR>the fem. युवतिःजरती ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवजानि|युवजानिः
युवजानि m. (-निः) Having a young wife.<BR> E. युव, and जानि wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवति|युवतिः
युवति f. (-तिः or ती) A young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवन्
युवन् mfn. (युवा युवतिः or -ती or यूनी-युव)<BR>	 1. Young.<BR>	 2. Best, excellent.<BR>	 3.<BR>Endowed with native or natural strength.<BR>	 m. (Nom. -युवा-वानी-वानः<BR>acc. plu. युनः)<BR>	 1. A younger descendant, the elder being alive.<BR>	 m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">Page590-a+ 60</a>]<BR>(-वा) A young man or one of the virile age, or from sixteen to<BR>seventy.<BR>	 f. (-तिः-ती or यूनी) A young woman, one from sixteen to<BR>thirty.<BR>	 f. (-तिः) Turmeric.<BR> E. यु to mix or associate, Unādi aff.<BR>क्वनिन्, the fem. form takes ति, and optionally adds ङीष् in one<BR>form, with which affix the semi-vowel व is changed to its con-<BR>gener उ, and the two short vowels coalesce into one long one,<BR>making यूनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=589-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवनाश्वज|युवनाश्वजः
युवनाश्वज m. (-जः) A name of MĀNDHĀTṚ, an early sovereign of the<BR>Solar dynasty.<BR> E. युवनाश्व his father, who appears as the eighth<BR>monarch of the Solar line, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवपलित
युवपलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Grey-haired in youth.<BR> E. युवन्, and पलित grey-<BR>haired; also युवापलित, and fem. युवतिःपलिता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवराज|युवराजः
युवराज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A young prince, especially the heir apparent, asso-<BR>ciated to the throne.<BR>	 2. One of the Jaina pontiffs.<BR> E. युव young,<BR>राजन् a prince, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युवराज्य
युवराज्य n. (-ज्यं) The dignity of heir apparent and associate in the<BR>throne.<BR> E. युवराज, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्मद्
युष्मद् 2nd personal pronoun.<BR>	 mfn. (-त्वं) Thou.<BR> E. युष a Sautra root, to<BR>serve, to worship, Unādi aff. मदिक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

युष्मद्वाच्य
युष्मद्वाच्य n. (-च्यं) (In gram.) The second person.<BR> E. युष्मद्, and बाच्य to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यू
यू f. (-यूः) The water in which pulse, &c. has been boiled, pease-soup,<BR>&c.<BR> E. यु to mix, aff. क्किप्, and vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूक|यूकः
यूक mf. (-कः-का) A louse.<BR> E. यु to mix, (with the hair,) Unādi aff.<BR>कन्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूति|यूतिः
यूति f. (-तिः) Joining, mixing.<BR> E. यु to join, aff. क्तिच्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथ|यूथं
यूथ n. (-थं) A multitude of birds or beasts, a herd, a flock.<BR>	 f. (-थी) A<BR>kind of jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR> E. यु to mix, थक् Unādi<BR>aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथनाथ|यूथनाथः
यूथनाथ m. (-थः) A large elephant, the leader of a wild herd.<BR> E. यूथ a<BR>multitude, (of elephants,) and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथप|यूथपः
यूथप m. (-पः) The leader of a wild herd of elephants.<BR> E. यूथ a herd,<BR>and प who protects: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथभ्रष्ट|यूथभ्रष्टः
यूथभ्रष्ट m. (-ष्टः) An elephant turned out or driven from a herd.<BR> E. यूथ a herd, भ्रष्ट expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथशस्
यूथशस् Adv. Gregariously, in flocks.<BR> E. यूथ and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूथिका
यूथिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A sort of jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>	 2. Globe<BR>amaranth.<BR> E. यूथी the jasmine, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूनि|यूनिः
यूनि f. (-निः) Joining, union, junction.<BR> E. यु to join or mix, aff. क्तिन्, न<BR>substituted for the final, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूप|यूपः
यूप mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>	 1. A sacrificial post, a pillar usually made of bamboos,<BR>or the wood of the Khadira, to which the victim at a sacrifice is<BR>bound.<BR>	 2. A trophy, a column erected in honour of a victory. E.<BR>यु to bind, (the victim,) प Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपकटक|यूपकटकः
यूपकटक m. (-कः) A wooden ring on the top of a sacrificial post, or<BR>according to some authorities, an iron ring at its base.<BR> E. यूप the<BR>post, and कटक a ring, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपकर्ण|यूपकर्णः
यूपकर्ण m. (-र्णः) A part of a sacrificial post sprinkled with ghee.<BR> E. यूप the post, कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपद्रु|यूपद्रुः
यूपद्रु m. (-द्रुः) The Khayar, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR> E. यूप a sacrificial post,<BR>and द्रु a tree; the wood of this tree being especially fit for the<BR>sacrificial post; also यूपद्रुम m. (-मः) । “रक्तखदिरे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपलक्ष्य|यूपलक्ष्यः
यूपलक्ष्य m. (-क्ष्यः) A bird.<BR> E. यूप a sacrificial post, put for any post, and<BR>लक्ष्य an aim; a sort of net being made about a post, on which<BR>birds may alight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपाग्र|यूपाग्रं
यूपाग्र m. (-ग्रः) The top of the sacrificial post.<BR> E. यूप as above, अग्र top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूपोच्छ्रय
यूपोच्छ्रय m. (-यः) The ceremony of erecting the sacrificial post.<BR> E. यूप a<BR>sacrificial post, and उच्छ्रय elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूष्
यूष् r. 1st cl. (यूषति) To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यूष|यूषं|यूषः
यूष mn. (-षः-षं) Pease-soup, pease-porridge, the water in which pulse<BR>of various kinds has been boiled.<BR>	 m. (-षः) The mulberry tree, (Mo-<BR>rus Indica;) also पूष.<BR> E. यूष् to hurt, क aff.; यूषन् is optionally subs-<BR>tituted for this word is some cases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येन
येन Ind. (Inst. sing of यत्, used as an adverb.)<BR>	 1. By which means,<BR>wherefore, whereby.<BR>	 2. As, so that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

येष
येष (ऋ) येषृ r. 1st cl. (येषते) To resolve, to endeavour diligently, to persevere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्तव्य
योक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be joined or united.<BR>	 2. To be performed<BR>(as devotion.)<BR>	 3. To be united spiritually.<BR> E. युज् to join, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योक्त्र|योक्त्रं
योक्त्र m. (-क्त्रं) The tie of the yoke of a plough or carriage.<BR> E. युज् to<BR>join, Unādi aff., त्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग|योगः
योग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Junction, joining, union.<BR>	 2. Combination, association,<BR>meeting, conflux.<BR>	 3. Religious and abstract meditation.<BR>	 4. Keep-<BR>ing the body in a fixed posture.<BR>	 5. Devotion, spiritual worship of<BR>GOD, or union with the Supreme Being by means of abstract<BR>contemplation; this does not necessarily imply an abandonment<BR>of the world or relinquishment of the usual observances of re-<BR>ligion, but it involves internal indifference to objects of pleasure<BR>and pain, and utter disregard of the consequences or fruit of<BR>ceremonial rites.<BR>	 6. The particular practice of the preceding sort<BR>of devotion, or the exercise of that abstraction by which union<BR>with God is supposed to be obtained; in the Gītā it is described<BR>as sitting on Kuśa grass, with the body firm, the eyes fixed on<BR>the tip of the nose, and the mind intent on the Deity; in the Tan-<BR>tras a fanciful operation is prescribed, by which the vital spirit sea-<BR>ted in the lower part of the body, and the etherial spirit placed in<BR>the head, are supposed to be brought into combination in the<BR>brain, when the devotee becomes united with BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 7. The sys-<BR>tem of philosophy which treats of the union of the soul with BRAH-<BR>MĀ or GOD; it is the same as the Patanjalī doctrine, and consti-<BR>tutes one of the six Darshanas or philosophical schools of the<BR>Hindus.<BR>	 8. Magic, or the acquisition of supernatural powers by the<BR>mystical and magical worship of ŚIVA and DURGĀ especially.<BR>	 9.<BR>Consequence, result, the main end or object of any thing or act.<BR>10. Connection of one thing with another, as of cause with effect,<BR>predicate with subject, quality with substance, &c.<BR>	 11. Acquisi-<BR>tion of something not possessed before, accession of property or<BR>wealth; in grammar this application is assigned to any unusual<BR>construction of words or compounds, unauthorised by rule, but<BR>sanctioned by the authority that employs them.<BR>	 12. A rule, an<BR>aphorism.<BR>	 13. Propriety, fitness.<BR>	 14. Side, part, cause or argument<BR>to be maintained or defended.<BR>	 15. Thing, substance.<BR>	 16. Wealth.<BR>17. A drug, a medicament, especially a compound of various, in-<BR>gredients.<BR>	 18. Fraud, trick.<BR>	 19. A logician.<BR>	 20. A spy, an informer.<BR>21. A violator of truth or confidence.<BR>	 22. A conveyance, a carriage,<BR>a boat, &c.<BR>	 23. A means, an expedient.<BR>	 24. Armour.<BR>	 25. Putting<BR>on armour.<BR>	 26. Lucky conjuncture.<BR>	 27. (In arithmetic,) Addition.<BR>28. (In astronomy,) The leading or principal star of a lunar man-<BR>sion.<BR>	 29. The twenty-seventh part of 3600 of a great circle measur-<BR>ed on the plane of the ecliptic, and used in calculating the longitu-<BR>des of the sun and moon; each Yoga has a distinct name; as-<BR>trologers also enumerate twenty-eight Yogas differently named<BR>from the foregoing, and corresponding with the twenty-eight Nak-<BR>shatras, or the divisions of the moon's path, but varying accor-<BR>ding to the day of the week.<BR>	 30. A period, or the time during<BR>which the sum of the motions of the sun and moon amount to one<BR>Nakshatra, the mean duration of which is 23hs. 474 4444.<BR> E. युज्<BR>to join literally or figuratively, (as with GOD,) aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगक्षेम|योगक्षेमं|योगक्षेमः
योगक्षेम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Charge of property, keeping of cattle, &c. for an-<BR>other.<BR>	 2. Insurance or charge for secure conveyance of goods, and<BR>the profit on their sale.<BR>	 3. Profit, gain, keeping the old and mak-<BR>ing fresh gains.<BR>	 4. Such articles as are not divisible amongst<BR>coheirs.<BR>	 5. Welfare, well-being.<BR>	 6. National prosperity, the good<BR>government of a state, or the means of maintaining it; as the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">Page591-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Rājā, minister, priest, &c. forming the administration.<BR> E. योग<BR>profit, क्षेम safety or preservation; or योग association, क्षेम patience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=590-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगक्षेमकर
योगक्षेमकर m. (-रः) A keeper, one who takes charge of property, &c. E.<BR>योगक्षेम, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगचर|योगचरः
योगचर m. (-रः) A name of HANUMĀNA.<BR> E. योग possession of superhu-<BR>man powers, चर going, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगचूर्ण
योगचूर्ण mn. (-र्णः-र्णं) Magical powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगतस्
योगतस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Suitably, properly.<BR>	 2. Seasonably, in due season.<BR>	 3.<BR>Through devotion, magic, &c.<BR>	 4. Conjointly.<BR> E. योग, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगतारा
योगतारा f. (-रा) The chief star in a constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगदान|योगदानं
योगदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A fraudulent gift.<BR>	 2. Communicating the Yoga doc-<BR>trine.<BR> E. योग, दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगनाविक|योगनाविकः
योगनाविक m. (-कः) A sort of fish, (Silurus ascita.) “गर्गाटमत्मे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगनिद्रा
योगनिद्रा f. (-द्रा)<BR>	 1. The sleep of VIṢṆU during the deluge.<BR>	 2. A state<BR>of half contemplation and half sleep.<BR>	 3. A goddess, a form of<BR>DURGĀ or VIṢṆU'S sleep personified.<BR> E. योग mystery, निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगपट्ट|योगपट्टं
योगपट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A cloth drawn round the lower extremities of the asce-<BR>tic as he squats to perform religious abstraction.<BR> E. योग a religious<BR>exercise, पट्ट cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगमाया
योगमाया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. The personified power of god in the creation of the world.<BR>	 2. DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगरङ्ग|योगरंग|योगरङ्गः
योगरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The orange, (Citrus aurantium.) “कम्लालेवु” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगरूढ|योगरूढः
योगरूढ m. (-ढः) A word which retains only a part of its etymological<BR>meaning; for instance, the word जलज may etymologically mean<BR>any thing produced in water, such as, fish, shell, &c., but its<BR>meaning are restricted to lotus only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगरोचना
योगरोचना f. (-ना) A magical ointment having the power of making<BR>one invisible or invulnerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगवल
योगवल n. (-लं) The power of devotion or magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगवर्त्तिका|योगवर्तिका
योगवर्त्तिका f. (-का) A magical lamp, a magical lantern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगवाहिन्
योगवाहिन् m. (-ही) A menstruum or medium for mixing medicines, as<BR>honey, &c.<BR> E. योग, वाहिन् conveyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगवाही
योगवाही f. (-ही)<BR>	 1. Alkali.<BR>	 2. Quicksilver.<BR> E. योग joining of metals, वाह effecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगविक्रय|योगविक्रयः
योगविक्रय m. (-यः) Fraudulent sale.<BR> E. योग, and विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगविद्
योगविद् m. (-वित्)<BR>	 1. A follower of the Yoga doctrines.<BR>	 2. A practiser<BR>of devotional exercises.<BR>	 3. A magician.<BR>	 4. A compounder of medi-<BR>cines.<BR> E. योग and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगविभाग|योगविभागः
योगविभाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Separation of that which is usually combined.<BR>	 2.<BR>The separation of the words of a Sūtra or text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगसमाधि|योगसमाधिः
योगसमाधि m. (-धिः) The absorption of the soul in profound meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगसार|योगसारः
योगसार m. (-रः) A panacea, a universal remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगसेवा
योगसेवा f. (-वा) Practising religious abstraction.<BR> E. योग, सेवा observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगाङ्ग|योगांग
योगाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A means of attaining Yoga; There are eight such<BR>means; viz:--यम, नियम, आसन, प्राणायाम्, प्रत्याहार, धारणा, ध्यान and<BR>ममाधि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगाचार|योगाचारः
योगाचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The observance of Yoga.<BR>	 2. A follower of that Bu-<BR>ddhist sect which maintains the external existence of intelligence<BR>alone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगाधमन|योगाधमनं
योगाधमन n. (-नं) A fraudulent pledge.<BR> E. योग fraud, and आधमन a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगारूढ|योगारूढः
योगारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Engaged in devotional exercises.<BR> E. योग, and<BR>आरूढ mounted on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगासन|योगासनं
योगासन n. (-नं) A religious posture, the position in which the devotee<BR>sits to perform the religious exercise called Yoga.<BR> E. योग as above,<BR>and आसन a seat or sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगिन्
योगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>	 1. Who or what joins, or effects junction or<BR>connection, &c.<BR>	 2. Possessed of superhuman powers.<BR>	 m. (-गी)<BR>	 1.<BR>A devotee, an ascetic in general.<BR>	 2. The religious or devout man,<BR>who performs worldly actions and ceremonies without regard to<BR>their results, and keeps his mind fixed upon BRAHMĀ or GOD<BR>alone.<BR>	 3. The performer of the particular act of meditation<BR>called Yoga.<BR>	 4. A magician, a conjuror, one supposed to have<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">Page591-b+ 60</a>]<BR>obtained supernatural powers.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Name of the eight female<BR>fiend or spirit attendant on, and created by DURGĀ;<BR> E. योग as<BR>above, इनि aff.; or युज् to join, aff. घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगिनिद्रा
योगिनिद्रा f. (-द्रा) Light sleep, wakefulness.<BR> E. योगिन् a saint, निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगेश|योगेशः
योगेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The city of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. The saint and legislator<BR>YĀGNYAWALKYA.<BR>	 3. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. Any principal Muni or<BR>Yogi.<BR> E. योग a Yogi or religious personage, &c., ईश lord or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगेश्वर|योगेश्वरः
योगेश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A principal sage or ascetic.<BR>	 2. A magician, one who<BR>has superhuman faculties.<BR>	 3. A deity, the object of devout con-<BR>templation.<BR> E. योग and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योगेष्ट|योगेष्टं
योगेष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Lead.<BR> E. योग affinity, (of metals or amalgamation,) इष्ट desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग्य|योग्यं|योग्यः
योग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>	 1. Clever, skilful.<BR>	 2. Fit or proper for a Yoga,<BR>or for religious meditation.<BR>	 3. Powerful, able.<BR>	 4. Fit, proper,<BR>suitable.<BR>	 n. (-ग्यं)<BR>	 1. A drug, commonly Ṛddhi.<BR>	 2. A cake.<BR>	 3.<BR>A vehicle or conveyance.<BR>	 4. Sandal.<BR>	 m. (-ग्यः) A calculator of<BR>expedients.<BR>	 f. (-ग्या)<BR>	 1. Military exercise.<BR>	 2. Medical practice. E.<BR>युज् to join or mix, aff. ण्यत्; or योग union, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योग्यता
योग्यता f. (-ता) Fitness, suitableness, propriety.<BR> E. योग्य, तल् aff.; also<BR>with त्व, योग्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजन|योजनं
योजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. GOD, the SUPREME BEING, the soul of the world.<BR>	 2. A<BR>measure of distance equal to four Krosas, which at 8000 cubits<BR>or 4000 yards to the Krosa or Kos, will be exactly nine miles;<BR>other computations make the Yojana but about five miles, or<BR>even no more than four miles and a half.<BR>	 3. Joining, union,<BR>junction, yoking.<BR>	 4. Application, preparation.<BR>	 5. Construction,<BR>putting together of the sense of a passage.<BR>	 6. Instigation, excit-<BR>ing.<BR>	 7. Concentration of the mind.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Union, connection.<BR>2. Grammatical construction.<BR> E. युज् to join, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजनगन्धा
योजनगन्धा f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. Musk.<BR>	 2. A name of SĪTĀ.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>SATYAVATĪ, the mother of the sage and poet VYĀSA.<BR> E. योजन a<BR>Yojana, and गन्ध smell; whose odour is perceptible miles off; also<BR>with कन् added, fem. form, योजनगन्धिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजनपर्णी
योजनपर्णी f. (-र्णी) Bengal madder.<BR> E. योजन joining, पर्ण leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजनवल्ली
योजनवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.) “मञ्जिष्ठायाम्.”<BR> E. योजन<BR>joining, वल्ली pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजनीय
योजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be joined.<BR>	 2. To be added.<BR> E. युज् to join, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजयितृ
योजयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Joining, combining, who or what unites. E.<BR>युज् to join, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योजित|योजितं
योजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Mixed, joined.<BR> E. युज् to join, aff. क्त; more usually युक्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योतु|योतुः
योतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. Measure in general.<BR>	 2. Cleaning, purifying.<BR>	 3. A clean-<BR>ser, a purifier.<BR> E. यु to mix, or not to mix, and तुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योत्र|योत्रं
योत्र n. (-त्रं) The tie that fastens the yoke of a plough to the neck of<BR>the ox.<BR> E. यु to join, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योत्स्यमान
योत्स्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) About to fight, ready to fight.<BR> E. युध् to fight,<BR>desid. v., future tense, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योद्धव्य
योद्धव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be fought, what must or ought to be fought.<BR>E. युध् to fight, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योद्धृ
योद्धृ m. (-द्धा) A warrior, a combatant.<BR> E. युध् to fight, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योध|योधः
योध m. (-धः) A warrior, a soldier, a combatant.<BR> E. युध् to fight, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधमुख्य|योधमुख्यः
योधमुख्य m. (-ख्यः) A leader, a chief warrior.<BR> E. योध and मुख्य chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधयत्
योधयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Fighting, warring.<BR> E. युध् to fight, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधवीर
योधवीर m. (-रः) A hero, a warrior.<BR> E. योध, and वीर a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधसंराव|योधसंरावः
योधसंराव m. (-वः) Mutual defiance, challenging or braving each other.<BR>E. योध a warrior, संराव cry or shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधहर
योधहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Carrying soldiers fit for war, (horses.)<BR> E. योध, हर what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधिन्
योधिन् m. (-धी) A warrior.<BR> E. युध् to fight, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योधेय|योधेयः
योधेय m. (-यः) A warrior.<BR> E. युध् war, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनल|योनलः
योनल m. (-लः) A sort of grain, (Andropogon or Holcus sorghum.) “दे-<BR>धान”.<BR> E. यव barley, नल culm or stalk, the व of the first word cha-<BR>nged to उ, and उ with the inherent vowel of य changed to ओ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=591-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनि|योनिः
योनि mfn. (-निः-निः or -नी)<BR>	 1. The vulva.<BR>	 2. A mine.<BR>	 3. Cause, origin.<BR>4. Water.<BR>	 5. Place or site of birth or production in general.<BR>	 6. A<BR>repository, a seat.<BR>	 7. Home, abode, nest.<BR>	 8. A form of existence,<BR>race, birth, as in “देवयोनि,” &c.<BR> E. यु to join or mix, Unādi aff. नि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिज|योनिजं
योनिज Adj. Born of the womb, viviparous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिदेवता
योनिदेवता f. (-ता) The 11th Nakshatra or lunar asterism; also Pūrva-<BR>phālguni.<BR> E. योनि the vulva, and देवता presiding deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिनासा
योनिनासा f. (-सा) The upper part of the vulva or the union of the labiæ.<BR>E. योनि the womb, and नासा the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिभ्रंश|योनिभ्रंशः
योनिभ्रंश m. (-शः) Fall of the womb, Prolapsus uteri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिरञ्जन|योनिरंजन
योनिरञ्जन n. (-नं) The menstrual excretion.<BR> E. योनि pudendum, रञ्जन colouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिलिङ्ग|योनिलिंग
योनिलिङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) The clitoris.<BR> E. योनि the pudendum, लिङ्ग the penis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिसंवृत्ति|योनिसंवृत्तिः
योनिसंवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Contraction or closure of the vagina.<BR> E. योनि and<BR>संवृत्ति contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योनिसङ्कर|योनिसंकर|योनिसंकरः
योनिसङ्कर m. (-रः) Fault or blemish of birth on the mother's side, as<BR>from inferiority of caste, &c.<BR> E. योनि, and सङ्कर mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योन्यर्शस्
योन्यर्शस् n. (-र्शः) An affection of the vulva, Menorrhagia, or prolapsus<BR>uteri.<BR> E. योनि the vulva, and अर्शस् piles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योपन|योपनं
योपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Effacing.<BR>	 2. Anything used for effacing.<BR>	 3. Destroying, oppressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषा
योषा f. (-षा) A young women.<BR> E. युष् to serve, sautra root, casual form,<BR>affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषित्
योषित् f. (-षित्) A woman in general.<BR> E. युष् Sautra root, to serve, to<BR>worship, to hurt, इति Unādi aff.; also with टाप् added योषिता f.<BR>(-ता) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

योषित्कृत
योषित्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done by a woman, contracted by her, &c.<BR> E. योषिन् कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौक्तिक|यौक्तिकः
यौक्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Connective, binding.<BR>	 2. Inferrible, deducible.<BR>3. Customary, usual.<BR>	 4. Right, proper.<BR>	 5. Founded on reasoning,<BR>logical.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A minister or associate to one's pleasure or<BR>amusement.<BR> E. युक्ति union, association, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगक|यौगकः
यौगक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to the religious practice, &c. called<BR>Yoga.<BR> E. योग, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगपद
यौगपद n. (-दं) Simultaneousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौगिक|यौगिकः
यौगिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Customary, usual, common.<BR>	 2. Relating to<BR>the Yoga, &c.<BR>	 3. Proper, regular, (as the sense of words, depen-<BR>ing upon their derivation or construction.)<BR> E. योग and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौजनशतिक|यौजनशतिकः
यौजनशतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Proceeding or extending a hundred Yoja-<BR>nas.<BR> E. योजन a measure so named, शत a hundred, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौजनिक|यौजनिकः
यौजनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Extending, &c. a Yojana.<BR> E. योजन्, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौट्
यौट् (ऋ) यौटृ r. 1st cl. (यौटति) To bind, to tie, to fasten; also यौडृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौतक|यौतकं
यौतक n. (-कं) A nuptial gift, presents made to a bride, at her marri-<BR>age, by her father or friends; some consider it also implying a<BR>gift to the bridegroom.<BR> E. युतक the same, pleonastic aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौतव|यौतवं
यौतव n. (-वं) Measure in general.<BR> E. योतु the same, अण् aff.; some<BR>authorities read यौवत and पौतव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौधेय|यौधेयः
यौधेय m. (-यः) A warrior.<BR> E. योधेय the same, and अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौन|यौनं
यौन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Relating to the womb or place of origin, uterine:<BR>2. Connected by female alliance, marriage, &c.<BR> E. योनि and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवत|यौवतं
यौवत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Measure in general.<BR>	 2. An assemblage of young wo-<BR>men.<BR>	 3. The state of being a youthful woman.<BR> E. यु to mix, deriv.<BR>irr.; or युवती a young woman, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवन|यौवनं
यौवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Youth, manhood, prime of life, puberty.<BR>	 2. An assem-<BR>blage of young women.<BR> E. युवन् young, अण् aff.; with कन् यौवनक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनकण्टक|यौवनकण्टकं|यौवनकण्टकः
यौवनकण्टक m. (-कः) Pimples on the face, especially in young persons.<BR>E. यौवन youth, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनदर्प|यौवनदर्पः
यौवनदर्प m. (-र्पः) Pride of youth, rashness, conceit.<BR> E. यौवन, दर्प pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनदशा
यौवनदशा f. (-शा) The period of youth.<BR> E. यौवन, दशा state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनपिडका
यौवनपिडका f. (-का) Blotches on the face in youth.<BR> E. यौवन, पिडका pimples, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनलक्षण|यौवनलक्षणं
यौवनलक्षण n. (-ण)<BR>	 1. The bosom, the female breast.<BR>	 2. Beauty, hand-<BR>someness, charm, loveliness.<BR>	 3. Characteristic of youth.<BR> E. यौवन<BR>youth, लक्षण mark or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनवत्|यौवनवन्त्
यौवनवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Youthful.<BR> E. यौवन, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवनाश्व|यौवनाश्वः
यौवनाश्व m. (-श्वः) A name of MĀNDHĀTṚ, one of the kings of the solar<BR>dynasty.<BR> E. युवनाश्व a proper name, and अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौवराज्य|यौवराज्यं
यौवराज्य n. (-ज्यं) The office of YUVARĀJA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौष्माक|यौष्माकं
यौष्माक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Yours, belonging to you.<BR> E. युष्माक for युष्मद you, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यौष्माकीन|यौष्माकीनं
यौष्माकीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Yours, thine.<BR> E. युष्माक for युष्मद् thou, स्वञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

र|रं|रः
र The twenty-seventh consonant of the Nāgari Alphabet, correspond-<BR>ing to the letter R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

र|रं|रः
र m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Fire or Agni.<BR>	 2. Heat, warmth.<BR>	 3. Burning, scorching.<BR>	 4.<BR>Love, desire.<BR>	 5. Speed.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Giving.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR>	 f. (-री) Going,<BR>moving.<BR> E. रा to give, or रम् to play, &c., aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंह|रंहः
रंह r. 1st and 10th cl. (रंहति रंहयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To hasten, to move with<BR>speed.<BR>	 2. To urge on, to cause to move or flow.<BR>	 3. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहति|रंहतिः
रंहति f. (-तिः) Speed, velocity, in general, or the speed of a chariot.<BR>E. रम् to sport, क्तिन् aff., हुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रंहस्
रंहस् n. (-हः) Speed, velocity.<BR> E. रम् to sport, Unādi aff. असुब्, हुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्
रक् r. 10th cl. (राकयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To taste.<BR>	 2. To obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक|रकः
रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The sum gem.<BR>	 2. Crystal.<BR>	 3. A hard shower.<BR> E. रक् to get, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्त|रक्तं|रक्तः
रक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Dyed, tinged, coloured, stained.<BR>	 2. Red, of a<BR>red colour.<BR>	 3. Fond of, attached to, affected with love or interest<BR>towards any object.<BR>	 4. Pure, purified.<BR>	 5. Sporting, engaging in<BR>play or pastime.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः) Red, the colour.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Blood.<BR>	 2.<BR>Saffron.<BR>	 3. Copper.<BR>	 4. Minium.<BR>	 5. Vermilion.<BR>	 6. The fruit of the<BR>Flacourtia cataphracta.<BR>	 f. (-क्ता)<BR>	 1. Passionate, attached.<BR>	 2.<BR>Pleasant, charming.<BR>	 3. The Gūnjā plant, (Abrus precatorious.)<BR>	 4.<BR>Lac.<BR>	 5. Bengal madder.<BR> E. रञ्ज् to colour or dye, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तक|रक्तकः
रक्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant bearing a red blossom, (Pentapetes phœnicea;)<BR>it is also applied to the Ixora bandhuca.)<BR>	 2. Globe amaranth,<BR>(Gomphræna globosa, the red variety.)<BR>	 3. Red garments or cloth.<BR>4. A man affected with passion or fondness.<BR>	 5. A gambler, a<BR>player.<BR>	 6. Safflower.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Red.<BR>	 2. Fond of.<BR>	 3. Pleasing.<BR>	 4.<BR>Bloody.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकण्ठ|रक्तकंठ
रक्तकण्ठ mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं)<BR>	 1. Sweet-voiced.<BR>	 2. The Indian cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकन्द|रक्तकंद|रक्तकन्दः
रक्तकन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Coral.<BR>	 2. A sort of onion.<BR>	 3. A kind of yam, (Dios-<BR>corea purpurea.)<BR> E. रक्त red, and कन्द a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकन्दल|रक्तकंदल|रक्तकन्दलः
रक्तकन्दल m. (-लः) Coral.<BR> E. रक्त red, कन्द a root, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकमल|रक्तकमलं
रक्तकमल n. (-लं) The red lotus.<BR> E. रक्त red, and कमल the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकाञ्चन|रक्तकाञ्चनः
रक्तकाञ्चन m. (-नः) Mountain-ebony. (Bauhinia variegata, or B. Pur-<BR>purea.)<BR> E. रक्त red, काञ्चन the tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकुमुद|रक्तकुमुदं
रक्तकुमुद n. (-दं) The red lotus, (Nymphæa rubra, Rox.)<BR> E. रक्त red, कुमुद the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकैरव|रक्तकैरवं|रक्तकैरवः
रक्तकैरव n. (-वं) The red lotus.<BR> E. रक्त, and कैरव a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तकोकनद|रक्तकोकनदं|रक्तकोकनदः
रक्तकोकनद n. (-दं) The red lotus.<BR> E. रक्त and कोकनद a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तगुल्म|रक्तगुल्मः
रक्तगुल्म m. (-ल्मः)<BR>	 1. A disease, a hard lump in the abdomen of the<BR>female after conception, perhaps scirrhus of the ovarium.<BR>	 2. A clot<BR>of blood.<BR> E. रक्त and गुल्म cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तघ्न|रक्तघ्नः
रक्तघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A small tree, (Andersonia rohitaka.)<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी) A kind of<BR>grass, a variety of the Durbā grass.<BR> E. रक्त blood, घ्न removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तचन्दन|रक्तचंदन|रक्तचन्दनं
रक्तचन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Red wood, either red Sandal or sappan wood. (Ptro-<BR>carpus Santalinus.)<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR> E. रक्त red and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तचित्रक|रक्तचित्रकः
रक्तचित्रक m. (-कः) A tree, (Plumbago rosea or coccinea. Syn. P.<BR>Rosea.) “रक्तचिता”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तचूर्ण|रक्तचूर्णं
रक्तचूर्ण n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Red lead.<BR>	 2. Any red powder.<BR> E. रक्त, चूर्ण powder, dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=592-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तछर्दि|रक्तच्छर्दि|रक्तच्छर्दिः
रक्तछर्दि f. (-र्दिः) Vomiting blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तजन्तुक|रक्तजन्तुकः
रक्तजन्तुक m. (-कः) An earth-worm.<BR> E. रक्त red, जन्तु an insect, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तजिह्व|रक्तजिह्वः
रक्तजिह्व m. (-ह्वः) A lion.<BR> E. रक्त red, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तझावुक
रक्तझावुक m. (-कः) A tree, (Tamarix dioica.) “लाल् झाउ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ततुण्ड|रक्ततुंड|रक्ततुण्डः
रक्ततुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A parrot.<BR> E. रक्त red, तुण्ड a beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तत्व
रक्तत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Redness.<BR>	 2. Passion, affection.<BR> E. त्व added to रक्त; also with तल्, रक्तता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तदन्ती
रक्तदन्ती f. (-न्ती) A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. रक्त red, दन्त a tooth, aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तदृश्
रक्तदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Red-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-दृक) A pigeon.<BR> E. रक्त red, दृश् eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तधातु|रक्तधातुः
रक्तधातु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. Red chalk or red orpiment. “गैरिके.” 2. Copper. E.<BR>रक्त, धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तनयन
रक्तनयन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Red-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The Greek partridge, “चकोरे”<BR>(Perdix rufa.)<BR> E. रक्त red, and नयन the eye, red-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तनासिक|रक्तनासिकः
रक्तनासिक m. (-कः) An owl.<BR> E. रक्त red, नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तप|रक्तपः
रक्तप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Who or what drinks blood.<BR>	 m. (-पः) An imp, a<BR>goblin.<BR>	 f. (-पा)<BR>	 1. A leech.<BR>	 2. A female goblin.<BR> E. रक्त blood, and प<BR>what drinks, from पा with क aff., and टाप् for the feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपक्ष|रक्तपक्षः
रक्तपक्ष m. (-क्षः) GARUḌA.<BR> E. रक्त red, and पक्ष wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपदी
रक्तपदी f. (-दी) A plant, considered as a sort of sensitive plant, or a<BR>species of Lycopodium.<BR> E. रक्त red, पद foot or root, aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपल्लव|रक्तपल्लवः
रक्तपल्लव m. (-वः) The Āsoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपा
रक्तपा f. (-पा) A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपात|रक्तपातः
रक्तपात m. (-तः) Spilling of blood.<BR> E. रक्त, and पात causing to fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपाता
रक्तपाता f. (-ता) A leech.<BR> E. रक्त blood, पात nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपाद|रक्तपादः
रक्तपाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Red-footed.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A parrot.<BR>	 2. A war-<BR>chariot.<BR> E. रक्त red, पाद foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपायिन्
रक्तपायिन् m. (-यी) A bug.<BR>	 f. (-यिनी) A leech.<BR> E. रक्त, पायिन् what drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपारद|रक्तपारदं|रक्तपारदः
रक्तपारद n. (-दं) Native vermilion, cinnabar.<BR> E. रक्त, पारद quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपिण्ड|रक्तपिंड|रक्तपिण्डं
रक्तपिण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. The China-rose, (Hibiscus, rosa sinensis.) “जवाफुल्”.<BR>2. A climbing plant, (Ventilago madraspatana.)<BR>	 3. A spontaneous<BR>discharge of blood from the nose and mouth.<BR>	 4. A red pimple or<BR>boil.<BR> E. रक्त red, and पिण्ड lump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपित्त|रक्तपित्तं
रक्तपित्त m. (-त्तः) Plethora, spontaneous hæmorrhages from the mouth,<BR>nose, rectum and cuticle, accompanied with fever and headache,<BR>vomiting, purging, &c.<BR> E. रक्त red, and पित्त bile, the bile being of<BR>that colour; or रक्त blood and पित्त bile, it being supposed to be<BR>an affection of both fluids or humours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपित्तहा
रक्तपित्तहा f. (-हा) A variety of bent grass, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR> E. रक्त<BR>पित्त the disease, and हा what removes. “गेंँटेदूर्व्वा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपुष्प|रक्तपुष्पः
रक्तपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. Nerium odorum, the red variety.<BR>	 2. A small tree,<BR>(Andersonia rohitaca, Rox.)<BR>	 mf. (-ष्पः-ष्पा) The silk-cotton tree,<BR>(Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी)<BR>	 1. The trumpet-flower, (Bigno-<BR>nia suave-olens)<BR>	 2. Bryony, (Bryonia grandis.)<BR> E. रक्त red, and पुष्प<BR>flower, when it may be applied to any plant bearing red blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपुष्पक|रक्तपुष्पकः
रक्तपुष्पक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The Palāsh tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>	 2. A small tree,<BR>(Andersonia rohitaca, Rox.)<BR>	 3. A red flower, (Ixora bandhuka, or<BR>Pentapetes phœnicea.)<BR>	 4. The silk-cotton tree.<BR>	 5. The coral tree.<BR>6. A tree from which a red dye is prepared, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR>f. (-ष्पिका) A sort of sensitive plant or species of Lycopodium. E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तपोस्त
रक्तपोस्त m. (-स्तः) Red-poppy, (Papaver Rhoeas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तप्रमेह|रक्तप्रमेहः
रक्तप्रमेह m. (-हः) The passing of blood in the urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तफल|रक्तफलः
रक्तफल m. (-लः) The Indian fig-tree.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A cucurbitaceous plant,<BR>(Momordica monadelpha.) “तेलाकुचा”.<BR> E. रक्त red, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तफेनज|रक्तफेनजः
रक्तफेनज m. (-जः) A part of the body, apparently intending the lungs.<BR>“फुस्फुसे”.<BR> E. रक्त blood, फेन froth or phlegm, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तबालुक
रक्तबालुक n. (-कं) Red lead.<BR> E. रक्त red, बालुका sand. “सिन्दुरे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तमञ्जर|रक्तमञ्जरः
रक्तमञ्जर m. (-रः) A plant, (Barringtonia acutangula.) “निवुल वृक्षे.” E.<BR>रक्त red, मञ्जरी a pedicle aff. टच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तमण्डल
रक्तमण्डल n. (-लं) The red lotus.<BR> E. रक्त red, and मण्डल a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तमय
रक्तमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Bloody, full or consisting of blood.<BR> E. रक्त and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तमोक्षण|रक्तमोक्षणं
रक्तमोक्षण n. (-णं) Bleeding, letting blood.<BR> E. रक्त, मोक्षण loosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तयष्टि|रक्तयष्टिः
रक्तयष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR> E. रक्त, यष्टि a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तरेणु|रक्तरेणुः
रक्तरेणु m. (-णुः)<BR>	 1. Red lead.<BR>	 2. The blossom of the Palāsh, (Butea<BR>frondosa.)<BR>	 3. A sort of cloth.<BR>	 4. An angry man.<BR> E. रक्त red, and रेणु<BR>dust; also with कन् added in the second meaning रक्तरेणुका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तलोचन|रक्तलोचनः
रक्तलोचन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Red-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A pigeon.<BR> E. रक्त, लोचन eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवटी
रक्तवटी f. (-टी) Small-pox.<BR> E. रक्त red, and वटी a pustule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवरटी
रक्तवरटी f. (-टी) Small-pox.<BR> E. रक्त red, वरटी a pustule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवर्ग|रक्तवर्गः
रक्तवर्ग m. (-र्ग)<BR>	 1. Lac.<BR>	 2. The Pomegranate tree.<BR>	 3. Safflower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवर्ण|रक्तवर्णः
रक्तवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Red, of a red colour.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. An earth-worm.<BR>“केल्लुइ”.<BR>	 2. Red, (the colour.)<BR>	 n. (-र्णं) Gold.<BR> E. रक्त red, वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवर्द्धन
रक्तवर्द्धन m. (-नं) The egg-plant, (Solanum molongena.)<BR> E. रक्त blood, and<BR>वर्द्धन increasing. “वार्त्ताकौ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवसन|रक्तवसनः
रक्तवसन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dressed in red.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The mendicant, or<BR>Brāhmana of the fourth order, especially as occasionally clad in<BR>red garments.<BR> E. रक्त red, वसन vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवाहिन्
रक्तवाहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Conveying blood, (as an artery.)<BR> E. रक्त, and<BR>वाहिन् what bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तविद्रधि|रक्तविद्रधिः
रक्तविद्रधि m. (-धिः) A sore or ulcer from a vitiated state of blood.<BR> E. रक्त, and विद्रघि a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तविन्दु
रक्तविन्दु m. (-न्दुः)<BR>	 1. A red spot forming a flaw in a gem.<BR>	 2. A drop of<BR>blood.<BR> E. रक्त red, and विन्दु a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवीज|रक्तवीजः
रक्तवीज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The pomegranate.<BR>	 2. The name of a demon killed<BR>by DURGĀ.<BR> E. रक्त red, and वीज the seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तवृन्ता
रक्तवृन्ता f. (-न्ता) A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis.) “शेफालिकायाम्”.<BR> E. रक्त red, वृन्त a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तशालि|रक्तशालिः
रक्तशालि m. (-लिः) A red variety of rice, (Oriza sativa.)<BR> E. रक्त, शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तशासन|रक्तशासनं
रक्तशासन n. (-नं) Red lead.<BR> E. रक्त red, शासन an edict; from the docu-<BR>ment perhaps being sealed or signed with a preparation of this<BR>substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तशीर्षक|रक्तशीर्षकः
रक्तशीर्षक m. (-कः) A kind of heron. “सारसपक्षिणि ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तशृङ्गिक|रक्तशृङ्गिकं
रक्तशृङ्गिक m. (-कः) A kind of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसङ्कोच|रक्तसंकोचः
रक्तसङ्कोच n. (-चं) Safflower.<BR> E. रक्त red, (a dye,) सङ्कोच a contracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसङ्कोचक|रक्तसंकोचक
रक्तसङ्कोचक n. (-कं) The blue lotus.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसंज्ञ
रक्तसंज्ञ n. (-ज्ञं) Saffron.<BR> E. रक्त red or blood, and संज्ञा appellation; also<BR>similar compounds, as रक्तनामन्, रक्तनामक, &c. “कुङ्कुमे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसन्ध्यक|रक्तसन्ध्यकं
रक्तसन्ध्यक n. (-कं) The red lotus, (Nymphæa rubra.)<BR> E. रक्त red, सन्ध्या<BR>twilight, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसरोरुह|रक्तसरोरुहं
रक्तसरोरुह n. (-हं) The red lotus.<BR> E. रक्त, सरोरुह a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसर्षप|रक्तसर्षपः
रक्तसर्षप m. (-पः) Mustard, (Brassica nigra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तसौगन्धिक|रक्तसौगन्धिकं
रक्तसौगन्धिक m. (-कः) The red lotus. “रक्तकम्बल”.<BR> E. रक्त blood, &c., सौगन्धिक a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तस्राव|रक्तस्रावः
रक्तस्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Venesection, bleeding.<BR>	 2. A kind of dock or sorrel.<BR>E. रक्त and स्राव causing to flow; also रक्तस्रावणं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तहंसा
रक्तहंसा f. (-सा) One of the Rāginis or female personifications of the musical modes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तहीन
रक्तहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Bloodless, cold-blooded.<BR> E. रक्त, हीन devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताक्त|रक्ताक्तं
रक्ताक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkled with blood.<BR>	 2. Dyed red.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं)<BR>Red wood, (Pterocarpus santolinus; applied also to the Cæsalpi-<BR>nia sappan.)<BR> E. रक्त, and आक्त sprinkled, spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताक्ष|रक्ताक्षः
रक्ताक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्ष) Red-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A buffalo.<BR>	 2. A pigeon.<BR>3. The Greek partridge, (Perdix rufa.) “चकोरे.” 4. A tyrant, a<BR>savage, a barbarous or cruel man.<BR>	 5. The Indian crane.<BR> E. रक्त<BR>red, अक्षि the eye, aff. ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताङ्ग|रक्तांग|रक्ताङ्गं|रक्ताङ्गः
रक्ताङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The planet MARS.<BR>	 2. A plant, (a species of Crinum.)<BR>3. A bug.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Coral.<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी) A plant, (Celtis<BR>orientalis.)<BR> E. रक्त red and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तातिसार|रक्तातिसारः
रक्तातिसार m. (-रः) Dysentery.<BR> E. रक्त, and अतिसार diarrhœa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताधार|रक्ताधारः
रक्ताधार m. (-रः) The skin.<BR> E. रक्त blood, आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताधिमन्थ|रक्ताधिमन्थः
रक्ताधिमन्थ m. (-न्थः) Inflammation of the eyes, ophthalmia with spongi-<BR>ness of the vessels so as to discharge blood on being touched. E.<BR>रक्त, and अघिमन्थ ophthalmia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताभ
रक्ताभ Adj. Red-looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताभिष्यन्द
रक्ताभिष्यन्द m. (-न्दः) Redness or the vessels of the eye with flow of tears.<BR> E. रक्त, अभिष्यन्दं flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=593-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताम्बर|रक्तांबर|रक्ताम्बरं|रक्ताम्बरः
रक्ताम्बर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Dressed in red.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Any vagrant devotee,<BR>wearing red garments.<BR> E. रक्त red, अम्बर vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताम्लान|रक्ताम्लानः
रक्ताम्लान m. (-नः) Globe amaranth, the red variety.<BR> E. रक्त red, अम्लान amaranth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तार्ब्बुद|रक्तार्बुद|रक्तार्बुदः
रक्तार्ब्बुद m. (-दः) A bloody tumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तालु|रक्तालुः
रक्तालु m. (-लुः) Common yam, (Dioscorea Sativa.)<BR> E. रक्त red, आलु yam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तावसेचन
रक्तावसेचन n. (-नं) Letting blood, bleeding.<BR> E. रक्त, अवसेचन sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ताशय|रक्ताशयः
रक्ताशय m. (-यः) Viscus in which the blood is contained or secreted,<BR>viz.:--the heart, the liver, and the spleen.<BR> E. रक्त, आशय receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ति|रक्तिः
रक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Affection, attachment.<BR>	 2. Addiction to.<BR>	 3. Charming-<BR>ness.<BR> E. रञ्ज् to be affected, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तिका
रक्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Abrus precatorious.)<BR>	 2. The seed of the<BR>Abrus precatorious used as a weight, or a fictitious weight deno-<BR>minated from the seeds originally so used; the seed weighs about<BR>one and five-sixteenth troy grains, the artificial Ratti or Raktikā<BR>should be double that weight, but in common use it averages<BR>nearly two grains and a quarter.<BR> E. रक्त red, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तिमन्
रक्तिमन् m. (-मा) Redness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तेक्षण
रक्तेक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Red-eyed, having the eyes inflamed or blood-<BR>shot.<BR> E. रक्त, and ईक्षण the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तोत्पल|रक्तोत्पलं|रक्तोत्पलः
रक्तोत्पल n. (-लं) The red lotus, (Nymphæa rubra.)<BR> E. रक्त red, उत्पल lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तोत्पलाभ|रक्तोत्पलाभः
रक्तोत्पलाभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Red.<BR>	 m. (-भः) Redness, red, the colour. E.<BR>रक्तोत्पल the red lotus, आभ resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्तोपल|रक्तोपलं
रक्तोपल n. (-लं) Indurated ochre, or clay iron stone.<BR> E. रक्त red, उपल a<BR>stone, hence applied to red ochre, red orpiment, red chalk, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्
रक्ष् r. 1st cl. (रक्षति)<BR>	 1. To guard.<BR>	 2. To protect, to cherish, to pre-<BR>serve. With परि, To save from ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष|रक्षः
रक्ष mf. (-क्षः-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Preserving, protecting.<BR>	 2. Lac.<BR>	 f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Ashes.<BR>	 2.<BR>A tutelary deity.<BR>	 f. (-क्षिका-क्षी) A sort of bracelet, a twist of<BR>thread or tinsel, with a small packet containing a few carmina-<BR>tive seeds, bound round the wrist at particular periods, especially<BR>at the day of full-moon in Srāvana.<BR> E. रक्ष् to preserve, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षःसभ|रक्षःसभं
रक्षःसभ n. (-भं) A multitude or assemblage of goblins.<BR> E. रक्षस् a demon,<BR>सभा assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षक|रक्षकः
रक्षक mfn. (-कः-क्षिका-कं) Who or what protects, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A guar-<BR>dian, a protector.<BR>	 2. A watch, a guard.<BR> E. रक्ष to preserve, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षण|रक्षणं|रक्षणः
रक्षण n. (-णं) Preserving, defending.<BR>	 f. (-णी) Rein, bridle.<BR> E. रक्ष to pre-<BR>serve, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षणि|रक्षणिः
रक्षणि f. (-णिः or णी) A medicinal plant, “त्रायमाणलतायाम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षणीय
रक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be guarded, preserved, protected, &c.<BR> E. रक्ष्<BR>to preserve, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षणीरक|रक्षणीरकः
रक्षणीरक m. (-कः) Urinary affection, as gonorrhœa, &c.; elsewhere read रक्षणारक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षत्
रक्षत् mfn. (-क्षन्-क्षन्ती-क्षत्) Preserving, guarding, protecting.<BR> E. रक्ष् to<BR>preserve, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षस्
रक्षस् n. (-क्षः) Rākshas, an evil spirit, apparently distinguishable into<BR>three classes; one sort of Rākshas is of a domi-celestial nature<BR>and is ranked with the attendants on KUVERA; another corres-<BR>ponds to a goblin, an imp, or ogre, haunting cemeteries, animat-<BR>ing dead bodies, disturbing sacrifices, and ensnaring and devour-<BR>ing human beings; the third kind approaches more to the nature<BR>of the Titan, or relentless, and powerful enemy of the gods.<BR> E. रक्ष्<BR>to preserve, (KUVERA'S treasure, &c.) असुन् aff.; also राक्षस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षस्पाश
रक्षस्पाश m. (-शः) A contemptible Rākshas.<BR> E. रक्षस्, and पाश aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षागृह
रक्षागृह n. (-हं) A lying-in-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षाधिकृत|रक्षाधिकृतः
रक्षाधिकृत m. (-तः) A governor, a magistrate.<BR> E. रक्षा, अघिकृत set over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षापत्र|रक्षापत्रः
रक्षापत्र m. (-त्रः) A sort of birch-tree. “श्वेतसर्षपे च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षापेक्षक|रक्षापेक्षकः
रक्षापेक्षक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A doorkeeper or porter.<BR>	 2. A guard of the<BR>women's apartments.<BR>	 3. A catamite.<BR>	 4. An actor, a mine.<BR> E. रक्ष्<BR>preserving, अप् before, ईक्ष् to see, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षाप्रदीप|रक्षाप्रदीपः
रक्षाप्रदीप m. (-पः) A light kept burning for protection against the evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षामणि|रक्षामणिः
रक्षामणि m. (-णिः) An ornament or jewel worn as a preservative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षित|रक्षितं
रक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Preserved, protected, defended.<BR>	 2. Kept,<BR>detained.<BR> E. रक्ष् to preserve, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षितव्य
रक्षितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be guarded, protected, &c.<BR> E. रक्ष् to preserve, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षितृ
रक्षितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what protects, defends, &c., a protector,<BR>a guard.<BR> E. रक्ष् to preserve, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षिन्
रक्षिन् mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि) Who or what preserves, &c.<BR> E. रक्ष् to pre-<BR>serve, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षिवर्ग|रक्षिवर्गः
रक्षिवर्ग m. (-र्गः) A guard, a sentinel.<BR> E. रक्षि from रक्षिन् a preserver, वर्ग class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षोगण
रक्षोगण m. (-णः) A class or troop of evil spirits.<BR> E. रक्षस्, गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षोघ्न|रक्षोघ्नं|रक्षोघ्नः
रक्षोघ्न m. (-घ्नः) Marking-nut plant.<BR>	 n. (-घ्न)<BR>	 1. Sour gruel made from<BR>the fermentation of rice-water.<BR>	 2. Asafœtida.<BR> E. रक्षस् a goblin,<BR>and घ्न destroying, repelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्षोजननी
रक्षोजननी f. (-नी) Night.<BR> E. रक्षस् a spirit, जननी mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्ण|रक्ष्णः
रक्ष्ण m. (-क्ष्णः) Preserving, guarding, protection.<BR> E. रक्ष् to preserve,<BR>aff. नङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्य
रक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) To be guarded, protected, &c.<BR> E. रक्ष् to preserve, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रक्ष्यमाण
रक्ष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Preserved.<BR> E. रक्ष् to preserve, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रख्
रख् r. 1st cl. (रखति) also (इ) रखि r. 1st cl. (रङ्खति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रग्
रग् r. 1st cl. (ए) रगे (रगति) To suspect, to doubt, to fear. r. 10th cl.<BR>(रागयति)<BR>	 1. To taste.<BR>	 2. To obtain. (इ) रगि r. 1st cl. (रङ्गति) To go,<BR>to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघ्
रघ् (इ) रघि r. 1st cl. (रङ्घते) To go, to move. r. 10th cl. (रङ्घयति-ते) To<BR>shine; also without the indicatory letter. r. 10th cl. (रापयति) To<BR>taste. KĀLIDĀSA derives रघु from this root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघु|रघुः
रघु m. (-घुः)<BR>	 1. The name of a sovereign of Oudh, the great grand-father<BR>of RĀMACHANDRA.<BR>	 2. The family or descendants of RAGHU.<BR> E. लघि<BR>to shine, कु Unādi aff., ल changed to र, nasal augment rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुकार|रघुकारः
रघुकार m. (-रः) The poet KĀLIDĀSA.<BR> E. रघु the race of RAGHU, which<BR>forms the subject of a poem by this writer, and कार author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुनन्दन|रघुनन्दनः
रघुनन्दन m. (-नः) RĀMA, the second incarnation of VIṢṆU, under<BR>that appellation.<BR> E. रघु the king RAGHU, नन्दन a son or descendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुनाथ|रघुनाथः
रघुनाथ m. (-थः) A name of RĀMA.<BR> E. रघु the race of RAGHU, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुवंश|रघुवंशः
रघुवंश m. (-शः) The race or family of RAGHU; hence also the name of<BR>a poem by KĀLIDĀSA, which treats of the ancestors of RĀMA,<BR>from DILĪPA to that prince, and his descendants to AGNIVARṆA;<BR>nearly one half relates to the history of RAGHU and as much to<BR>that of RĀMA, the remainder is occupied with the remaining<BR>princes.<BR> E. रघु as above, and वंश race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघुवर|रघुवरः
रघुवर m. (-रः) RĀMA.<BR> E. रघु the race of RAGHU, and वर eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रघूद्वह|रघूद्वहः
रघूद्वह m. (-हः) RĀMA.<BR> E. रघु the race of RAGHU, and उद्वह pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्क|रंक|रङ्कः
रङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं)<BR>	 1. Niggardly, avaricious, a miser.<BR>	 2. Slow, dull.<BR>3. Hungry.<BR> E. रकि to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्कु|रंकु|रंकुः|रङ्कुः
रङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः) A sort of deer, (the spotted axis.)<BR> E. रम् to sport, aff. कु, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्ग|रंग|रङ्गं|रंगः|रङ्गः
रङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Paint, colour, tint, dye.<BR>	 2. Dancing, acting, singing,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. A field of battle.<BR>	 4. The place where acting, &c. is exhibi-<BR>ted, a stage.<BR>	 5. A place answering to an amphi-theatre.<BR>	 6. An<BR>assembly.<BR>	 7. The nasal modification of a vowel.<BR>	 8. Borax.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Tin.<BR> E. रगि to go, aff. अच्; or रञ्ज् to colour, aff. घञ्, the final<BR>changed, and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गचर|रंगचर|रङ्गचरः
रङ्गचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An actor.<BR>	 2. A gladiator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गज|रंगज|रङ्गजं
रङ्गज n. (-जं) Red lead.<BR> E. रङ्ग colour, ज produced. “सिन्दुरे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गजीवक|रंगजीवक|रङ्गजीवकः
रङ्गजीवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An actor, a dancer, a mine.<BR>	 2. A painter.<BR> E. रङ्ग a<BR>stage or colour, &c., and जीवक who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गदेवता|रंगदेवता
रङ्गदेवता f. (-ता) The goddess supposed to preside over sports and diversions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गद्वार|रंगद्वार
रङ्गद्वार n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A stage-door.<BR>	 2. The prologue of a play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गभूति|रंगभूति|रङ्गभूतिः
रङ्गभूति m. (-तिः) The day of full-moon in the month Āshwin, (Septem-<BR>ber-October,) on the night of which LAKṢMĪ descended, promising<BR>wealth to all who were awake.<BR> E. रङ्ग dancing and singing,<BR>भूति being, the night being spent in playing ancient chess, in<BR>Nāutches, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=594-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गभूमि|रंगभूमि|रङ्गभूमिः
रङ्गभूमि f. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. A field.<BR>	 2. A stage, a theatre, a place where danc-<BR>ing is exhibited, or the Indian dramas where represented.<BR> E. रङ्ग<BR>dancing, &c., and भूमि ground, spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गमल्ली
रङ्गमल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A lute.<BR> E. रङ्ग् singing, &c., मल्ल् to hold, affs. अच् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गमातृ|रंगमातृ
रङ्गमातृ f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A bawd.<BR>	 2. Lac, the animal-dye.<BR> E. रङ्ग passion or<BR>colour, &c., and मातृ parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गमातृका
रङ्गमातृका f. (-का) Lac, or the insect which forms the red dye.<BR> E. रङ्ग<BR>colour, मातृ parent, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गलासिनी
रङ्गलासिनी f. (-नी) A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis.) “शेफालिकायाम्”. E.<BR>रङ्ग colour, (of the stalk,) लस् to shine, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गवाट|रंगवाट|रङ्गवाटः
रङ्गवाट m. (-टः) A place enclosed for contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गवीज
रङ्गवीज n. (-जं) Silver.<BR> E. रङ्ग tin, वीज seed or essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गशाला|रंगशाला
रङ्गशाला f. (-ला) A hall for public exhibitions, as Nāutches, plays, &c.,<BR>a ball-room, a theatre.<BR> E. रङ्ग acting, &c., and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गाजीव|रंगाजीव|रङ्गाजीवः
रङ्गाजीव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A painter.<BR>	 2. An actor, a dancer.<BR> E. रङ्ग colour, &c.,<BR>आजीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गावतरण|रंगावतरण
रङ्गावतरण n. (-णं) Acting, playing, exhibiting in public.<BR> E. रङ्ग, अवतरण alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गावतारक|रङ्गावतारकः
रङ्गावतारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An actor, a buffoon.<BR>	 2. A boxer.<BR>	 3. A bard or<BR>panegyrist.<BR> E. रङ्ग acting, dancing, अव depreciative prefix, तॄ to pass,<BR>वुन् aff.; also with णिनि aff., रङ्गावतारिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्गिन्|रंगिन्
रङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिणी-ङ्गि)<BR>	 1. Colouring, dying.<BR>	 2. Impassioned, having<BR>propensity or passion.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>“शतमूल्याम्”.<BR> E. रङ्ग colour, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रङ्घस्|रंघस्
रङ्घस् n. (-ङ्घः) Speed, volocity: see रंहस्; ह being changed to घ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रच्
रच् r. 10th cl. (रचयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To make mechanically, to work, to manu-<BR>facture.<BR>	 2. To write, to compose.<BR>	 3. To decorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचक
रचक m. (-कः) A maker, a composer.<BR> E. रच् to make, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचना
रचना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Orderly and becoming arrangement or disposition in<BR>general.<BR>	 2. Decoration or dressing of hair.<BR>	 3. Stringing flowers,<BR>&c., weaving wreaths, chaplets, or similar decorations.<BR>	 4. Military<BR>array, arrangement of troops.<BR>	 5. Literary composition, whether in<BR>verse or prose.<BR>	 6. Suspending garlands, &c. at the doors of a<BR>house or building on festival occasions.<BR>	 7. Making or preparing<BR>any thing.<BR> E. रच् to make, to manufacture, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रचित|रचितः
रचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made, manufactured.<BR>	 2. Written, composed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Strung.<BR> E. रच् to make, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज|रजं|रजः
रज mn. (-जः-जं)<BR>	 1. Dust.<BR>	 2. The pollen of flowers.<BR>	 3. The menstrual<BR>excretion.<BR>	 4. The second property of humanity, the quality of<BR>passion.<BR> E. रन्ज् to colour, &c., aff. अच्, and the nasal rejected;<BR>this word more commonly occurs रजस्, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजःशय|रजःशयः
रजःशय m. (-यः) A dog.<BR> E. रजस् dust, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजःसारथि|रजःसारथिः
रजःसारथि m. (-थिः) Air, wind.<BR> E. रजस् dust, and सारथि charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजक|रजकः
रजक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A washerman.<BR>	 2. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 f. (-की) A washer-<BR>man's wife or a washer-woman.<BR> E. रञ्ज् to colour, (clothes,) ष्वुन् or<BR>क्कुन् aff.; or रण्ज्-ण्वुल् न लोपः in the latter case the fem. is रजिका a<BR>washer-woman, and रजकी a washer-woman's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजत|रजतं
रजत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) White.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A pearl-necklace.<BR>	 2. Silver.<BR>	 3.<BR>Gold.<BR>	 4. Elephant's teeth, ivory.<BR>	 5. The name of a lake.<BR>	 6. The<BR>name of a mountain, perhaps Kailāsa; see रजताद्रि.<BR>	 7. White,<BR>(the colour.)<BR>	 8. Blood.<BR>	 9. An asterism, a constellation.<BR>	 10. An ele-<BR>phant.<BR> E. रञ्ज् to colour, &c., अतच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजतद्युति|रजतद्युतिः
रजतद्युति m. (-तिः) The monkey HANUMĀNA.<BR> E. रजत silver, द्युति lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजतप्रस्थ|रजतप्रस्थः
रजतप्रस्थ m. (-स्थः) Mount Kailāsa, the residence of KUVERA and his<BR>attendant demi-gods.<BR> E. रजत white, (or silver,) and प्रस्थ table-land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजताद्रि|रजताद्रिः
रजताद्रि m. (-द्रिः) Mount Kailāsa,: see the last.<BR> E. रजत, अद्रि mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजन|रजनं|रजनः
रजन n. (-नं) Colouring, dyeing.<BR> E. रञ्ज् to colour, Unādi aff. युक् or क्युन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनि|रजनिः
रजनि f. (-निः-नी)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. The indigo-plant.<BR>	 3. Turmeric.<BR>	 4. Lac. E.<BR>रञ्ज् to colour, अनि Unādi aff., and ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनिकर|रजनिकरः
रजनिकर m. (-रः) The moon.<BR> E. रजनि, and कर who makes; also रजनीकर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनिंमन्य
रजनिंमन्य Adj. A cloudy day, (looking like a night.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीगन्ध
रजनीगन्ध m. (-न्धः) The tuberose, (Polianthes tuberosa.)<BR> E. रजनी night,<BR>and गन्ध smell, emitting a powerful smell after sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीचर|रजनीचरः
रजनीचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A Rākshasa a fiend, a goblin, a ghost.<BR>	 2. A watch-<BR>man.<BR>	 3. A thief.<BR> E. रजनी night, चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीजल|रजनीजलं
रजनीजल n. (-लं) Frost, hoar-frost, dew.<BR> E. रजनी night, जल water, fall-<BR>ing at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीमुख|रजनीमुखं
रजनीमुख n. (-खं) Evening, beginning of the night.<BR> E. रजनी, मुख commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजनीहासा
रजनीहासा f. (-सा) A flower, (Nyctanthes arbor tristis.) “शेफालिकायाम्”.<BR>E. रजनी night, हास a smile; the flowers blossoming at night,<BR>and diffusing a powerful scent after sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्
रजस् n. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The second of the three primary qualities of nature<BR>the quality or property of passion: that which produces sensual<BR>desire, worldly coveting, pride, and falsehood, and is the cause of<BR>pain.<BR>	 2. Dust.<BR>	 3. The dust or pollen of a flower.<BR>	 4. Any particle of<BR>matter.<BR>	 5. The menstrual evacuation.<BR>	 6. Cultivated fields.<BR>	 7. A<BR>mole in a sun-beam.<BR> E. रञ्ज् to colour, to be attached to, Unādi<BR>aff. असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजसानु|रजसानुः
रजसानु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. The heart or mind.<BR> E. रञ्ज् to colour, to<BR>feel affection for, सानु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्तमस्क
रजस्तमस्क Adj. Being under the influence of Rajas and Tamas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्तोक|रजस्तोकः
रजस्तोक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. Avarice.<BR>	 2. The child of passion, (a term ap-<BR>plied to a person to mark his insignificance.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजस्वल|रजस्वलः
रजस्वल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A buffalo.<BR>	 2. Quicksilver.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A woman during<BR>menstruation.<BR>	 2. A girl, one above ten years of age.<BR>	 3. Dusty.<BR>	 4.<BR>Full of passion.<BR> E. रजस् dust, &c., and वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजित
रजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Affected, moved, attracted, or excited by.<BR> E. रञ्ज्<BR>to effect, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजोगुण|रजोगुणः
रजोगुण m. (-णः) The second condition of humanity: see रजस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजोदर्शन
रजोदर्शन n. (-नं) The first appearance of the menses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजोबन्ध|रजोबंध|रजोबन्धः
रजोबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Suppression of menstruation.<BR> E. रजस्, and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजोबल|रजोबलं
रजोबल n. (-लं) Darkness.<BR> E. रजस् dust, बल heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजोरस|रजोरसं|रजोरसः
रजोरस n. (-सं) Darkness.<BR> E. रजस् dust, and रस essence, or perhaps this<BR>and the preceding should be the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रजोहर|रजोहरः
रजोहर m. (-रः) A washerman.<BR> E. रजस् dust, dirt, and हर who removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्जु|रज्जुः
रज्जु m. (-ज्जुः)<BR>	 1. A rope, a cord, a tie, a string.<BR>	 2. A lock of braided<BR>hair.<BR>	 3. A sinew proceeding from the vertebral column.<BR> E. सृज् to<BR>create, &c., Unādi aff. उ, and the radical स rejected, the vowel<BR>changed to its semi-vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रज्जुदालक|रज्जुदालकः
रज्जुदालक m. (-कः) Wild-fowl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्ज्|रंज्
रञ्ज् (औ) औरञ्ज् r. 1st cl. (रजति-ते) r. 4th cl. (रज्यति-ते) To dye, to tinge,<BR>to give tint or colour to any thing. r. 1st cl. (रजति) To be attached<BR>to, or intent on, to have one's affections or passions engaged by<BR>and object. With अनु prefixed.<BR>	 1. To be fond of or attached to,<BR>(with a loc.)<BR>	 2. To redden. With अप and वि, To averse, to dislike.<BR>With उप, 1. To be eclipsed.<BR>	 2. To suffer calamity. Caus. (रञ्जयति-ते)<BR>1. To colour, to redden.<BR>	 2. To please.<BR>	 3. To conciliate. (रजयति)<BR>To hunt deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जक|रंजक|रञ्जकं|रञ्जकः
रञ्जक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. What incites or affects.<BR>	 2. What colours, &c.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Colouring, dyeing.<BR>	 2. A colorist, a painter.<BR>	 3. A dyer.<BR>4. A stimulus, an inciter of affection, &c.<BR>	 5. Biliary humour on<BR>which vision depends.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Vermilion.<BR>	 2. The mendhi-plant,<BR>(Lawsonia inermis.)<BR> E. रञ्ज् to colour, वुन् aff. “भल्लातके, काम्पिल्ल वृक्षे च.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जन|रंजन|रञ्जनं|रञ्जनः
रञ्जन mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>	 1. Colouring, dyeing, painting, &c.<BR>	 2. Affecting the<BR>heart, exciting passion, &c.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Red Sandal or Sappan wood.<BR>“वकम्काठ”.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The Indigo plant, (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Bengal madder.<BR>	 3. Another plant, commonly Sundarochani, (a<BR>species of Crinum.) “कमलागुंँडि इति भाषा ।” 4. A flower, (Nyctan-<BR>thes tristis.)<BR> E. रञ्ज् to colour, aff. युच् or ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रञ्जित|रंजित
रञ्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Moved or affected.<BR>	 2. Coloured, dyed, tinted.<BR>E. रञ्ज् to colour, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=595-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रट्
रट् r. 1st and 10th cl. (रटति रटयति)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To shout aloud.<BR>	 3.<BR>To roar. With आ, to call to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटत्
रटत् mfn. (-टन्-टन्ती-टत्) Speaking.<BR> E. रट् to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटन|रटनं
रटन n. (-नं) Speaking, shouting.<BR> E. रट्, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटन्ती|रटंती
रटन्ती f. (-न्ती) The fourteenth of the dark-half of Māgha when bathing<BR>is enjoined.<BR> E. रट् to speak, झश् aff., the waters speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रटित|रटितं
रटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spoken, said.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The roaring of flame.<BR> E. रट्<BR>to speak, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रठ्
रठ् r. 1st cl. (रठति) To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्
रण् r. 1st cl. (रणति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण|रणं|रणः
रण mn. (-णः-णं) War, battle.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Sound, noise.<BR>	 2. The quill or<BR>bow of a lute, &c.<BR>	 3. Going, moving.<BR> E. रण् to sound, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणकामिन्
रणकामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Desirous of war, wishing to fight.<BR> E. रण,<BR>कामिन् who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणत्
रणत् mfn. (-णन्-णन्ती-णत्)<BR>	 1. Warring, fighting.<BR>	 2. Going.<BR>	 3. Sounding.<BR> E. रण् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणत्कार|रणत्कारः
रणत्कार m. (-रः) A rutting sound, humming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणतूर्य्य|रणतूर्य|रणतूर्य्यं
रणतूर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) A military drum.<BR> E. रण war, तूर्य्य a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणधुरा
रणधुरा f. (-रा) The front or van of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणपण्डित|रणपण्डितः
रणपण्डित m. (-तः) A warrior.<BR> E. रण, and पण्डित learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणप्रिय|रणप्रियं|रणप्रियः
रणप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Warlike.<BR>	 n. (-यं) The root of a fragrant grass,<BR>(Andropogon muricatum.)<BR> E. रण, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणमत्त|रणमत्तः
रणमत्त m. (-त्तः) An elephant.<BR> E. रण war, मत्त mad, wild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणमुष्टि|रणमुष्टिः
रणमुष्टि m. (-ष्टिः) A shrub: see विषमुष्टि, “कुचिला ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणरङ्क|रणरंक|रणरङ्कः
रणरङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) The part of an elephant's face between his tusks.<BR> E. रण, रङ्क slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणरङ्ग|रणरंग|रणरङ्गः
रणरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A battle-field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणरण|रणरणं|रणरणः
रणरण n. (-णं) Regret, anxiety, anxious regret, sorrow, of which the<BR>object is lost or absent.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A musquito, a gnat.<BR> E. रण war,<BR>and noise, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणरणक|रणरणकः
रणरणक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Anxiety, regret: see the last.<BR>	 2. Love, desire.<BR>	 3.<BR>KĀMA.<BR> E. रण् to sound, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणसङ्कुल|रणसंकुल|रणसङ्कुलं
रणसङ्कुल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Mixed or tumultuary combat.<BR>	 2. A melee.<BR> E. रण, सङ्कुल a mingling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणस्तम्भ|रणस्तंभ|रणस्तम्भः
रणस्तम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. A trophy, a pillar, a monument of war.<BR>	 2. A coun-<BR>try, “Chitore.”<BR> E. रण, स्तम्भ a pillar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणाङ्गण|रणांगण
रणाङ्गण n. (-णं) A field of battle.<BR> E. रण, and अङ्गण a court-yard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणाजिर
रणाजिर n. (-रं) A field of battle.<BR> E. रण, and अजिर a court.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणाभियोग|रणाभियोगः
रणाभियोग m. (-गः) Engaging in battle.<BR> E. रण, and अभियोग encounter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणित|रणितं
रणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sounded.<BR>	 2. Warred.<BR> E. रण to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रणोत्साह|रणोत्साहः
रणोत्साह m. (-हः) Prowess in battle.<BR> E. रण, and उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्ड|रंड|रण्डः
रण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A man who dies without male issue.<BR>	 2. A barren tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्डक|रंडकः|रण्डकः
रण्डक m. (-कः) A barren tree.<BR> E. रण्डा a widow, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रण्डा
रण्डा f. (-ण्डा)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.) “मूषिकपर्ण्याम्.” 2. A<BR>widow.<BR>	 3. A term of abuse in addressing woman.<BR> E. रम् to sport, ड<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत|रतं
रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Occupied or engaged by, actively intent on.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>1. Copulation, sexual union.<BR>	 2. Pleasure.<BR>	 3. A privity, a private<BR>part.<BR> E. रम् to sport, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतकील|रतकीलः
रतकील m. (-लः) A dog.<BR> E. रत copulation, and कील a pin, fastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतकूजित|रतकूजितं
रतकूजित n. (-तं) Lascivious murmur.<BR> E. रत copulation, कूजित murmur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतगुरु|रतगुरुः
रतगुरु m. (-रुः) A husband.<BR> E. रत copulation, and गुरु teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतज्वर|रतज्वरः
रतज्वर m. (-रः) A crow.<BR> E. रत coition, ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रततालिन्
रततालिन् m. (-ली) A libertine, a lecher, a whore-monger.<BR> E. रत copula-<BR>tion, तल to complete, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतताली
रतताली f. (-ली) A bawd, a procuress.<BR> E. रत copulation, तल् to complete<BR>or effect, and अण् aff., fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतनारीच|रतनारीचः
रतनारीच m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. A dog.<BR>	 2. KĀMA or love.<BR>	 3. Sonitus in coitu.<BR>	 4. A<BR>libertine, a lecher.<BR> E. रत coition, नारी a female, चि to collect, or चर्<BR>to go, aff. क or ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतनिधि|रतनिधिः
रतनिधि m. (-धिः) A wagtail.<BR> E. रत copulation, निधि a treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतर्द्धिक
रतर्द्धिक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A day.<BR>	 2. Bathing for pleasure.<BR>	 3. The aggregate<BR>of four auspicious object.<BR> E. रत copulation, अधि increase, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतव्रण|रतव्रणः
रतव्रण m. (-णः) A dog.<BR> E. रत copulation, and व्रण a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतशायिन्
रतशायिन् m. (-यी) A dog.<BR> E. रत copulation, and शायिन् who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतहिण्डक|रतहिण्डकः
रतहिण्डक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A libertine, a lecher.<BR>	 2. A ravisher, one who<BR>carries off and violates a woman.<BR> E. रत coition, हिडि to go, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतान्दुक|रतान्दुकः
रतान्दुक m. (-कः) A dog.<BR> E. रत copulation, and अन्दुक a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतान्ध्री
रतान्ध्री f. (-न्ध्री) Fog, mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतामर्द्ध
रतामर्द्ध m. (-र्द्ध्वः) A dog.<BR> E. रत coition, आङ् before, मृध् to rub, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतायनी
रतायनी f. (-नी) A whore, a harlot.<BR> E. रत copulation, अयन a going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतार्थिन्
रतार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Libidinous, lascivious.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A libidinous<BR>woman, a wanton, a harlot.<BR> E. रत copulation, अर्थ seeking soliciting,<BR>इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रति|रतिः
रति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Passion, desire.<BR>	 2. Coition, copulation 3. A privity, a<BR>private part.<BR>	 4. The wife of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. रम् to sport, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिकुहर|रतिकुहरं
रतिकुहर n. (-रं) Pudendum muliebre.<BR> E. रति copulation, कुहर a cavity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिक्रिया
रतिक्रिया f. (-या) Copulation.<BR> E. रति the same, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिगृह|रतिगृहं
रतिगृह n. (-हं)<BR>	 1. A pleasure house.<BR>	 2. A brothel.<BR>	 3. The vagina. E.<BR>रति, and गृह abode, place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतितस्कर|रतितस्करः
रतितस्कर m. (-रः) A Ravisher, a seducer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिपति|रतिपतिः
रतिपति m. (-तिः) The deity of love, KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. रति the wife of the<BR>god, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिप्रिय|रतिप्रियः
रतिप्रिय m. (-यः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. रति the wife of the deity, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिमदा
रतिमदा f. (-दा) A courtezan of INDRA'S heaven.<BR> E. रति copulation, मम् to<BR>delight, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिमन्दिर|रतिमंदिर|रतिमन्दिरं
रतिमन्दिर n. (-रं) Pudendum muliebre.<BR> E. रति copulation, and मन्दिर abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिरमण|रतिरमणः
रतिरमण m. (-णः) KĀMADEVA, the god of love.<BR> E. रति the goddess, so<BR>named, and रमण husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिलक्ष|रतिलक्षं
रतिलक्ष n. (-क्षं) Copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतिसत्वरा
रतिसत्वरा f. (-रा) A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.) “पिडिंशाक्”<BR> E. रति<BR>copulation, सत्वर quick; perhaps considered as on aphrodisiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतू
रतू f. (-तूः) The Ganges of heaven.<BR>	 2. An honest woman, one who<BR>speaks the truth.<BR> E. ऋत a Sautra root, कू Unādi aff., अम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रतोद्वह|रतोद्वहः
रतोद्वह m. (-हः) The Kokila.<BR> E. रत copulation, उद्वह exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्न|रत्नं
रत्न n. (-त्नं)<BR>	 1. A jewel, a gem.<BR>	 2. Any thing the best of its kind, or<BR>figuratively, the jewel of the species.<BR> E. रम् to sport, Unādi aff.<BR>न, and त substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नकन्दल|रत्नकंदल|रत्नकन्दलः
रत्नकन्दल m. (-लः) Coral. “प्रवाले”.<BR> E. रत्न a jewel, and कन्दल a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नकूट|रत्नकूटः
रत्नकूट m. (-टः) A mountain in the Dakshin.<BR> E. रत्न a jewel, कूट a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नगर्भ|रत्नगर्भः
रत्नगर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. The god of wealth, KUVERA.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR>	 f. (-र्भा)<BR>The earth.<BR> E. रत्न a jewel, and गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नप्रभा
रत्नप्रभा f. (-भा) The first of the seven hells or purgatories, according to<BR>the Jainas.<BR> E. रत्न a jewel, and प्रभा splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नमय
रत्नमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Gemmed, full or made of gems.<BR> E. रत्न, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नमुख्य|रत्नमुख्यं
रत्नमुख्य n. (-ख्यं) The diamond.<BR> E. रत्न a jewel, and मुख्य chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नराज्
रत्नराज् m. (-राट्) A ruby. “माणिक्ये ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नवत्|रत्नवन्त्
रत्नवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having gems.<BR>	 f. (-ती) The earth.<BR> E. रत्न a jewel, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नवर्षुक|रत्नवर्षुकं
रत्नवर्षुक n. (-कं) The carriage of KUVERA.<BR> E. रत्न, वर्षुक showering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नवृक्ष
रत्नवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) Coral.<BR> E. रत्न a jewel, and वृक्ष tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नसानु|रत्नसानुः
रत्नसानु m. (-नुः) The mountain Meru.<BR> E. रत्न a jewel, सानु ridge of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नसू
रत्नसू f. (-सूः) The earth.<BR> E. रत्न a jewel, and सू a mother; also रत्नसूति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नसूति|रत्नसूतिः
रत्नसूति f. (-तिः) The earth: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नाकर|रत्नाकरः
रत्नाकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A jewel mine.<BR> E. रत्न jewel, आकर mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नाङ्क|रत्नाङ्कः
रत्नाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) The car of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. रत्न a jewel, and अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नावलि
रत्नावलि f. (-लिः) A necklace of gems.<BR> E. रत्न, आवलि a row; also रत्नावली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नि|रत्निः
रत्नि mf. (-त्निः-त्नी)<BR>	 1. A sort of cubit, measured from the elbow to the<BR>end of the closed fist; it is also computed at tweenty-one<BR>breadths of the middle of the thumb.<BR>	 2. The closed hand, the fist.<BR>E. ऋ to go, कत्निच् aff., the vowel changed to the semi-vowel, other-<BR>wise अरत्नि, and as derived from मृ to go, सरत्नि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्यङ्ग|रत्यंग|रत्यङ्गं
रत्यङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) The male or female organ.<BR> E. रति copulation, अङ्ग member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथ|रथः
रथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A car, a war-chariot.<BR>	 2. A car, a carriage in general,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">Page597-a+ 60</a>]<BR>any vehicle or mode of conveyance.<BR>	 3. A limb, a member.<BR>	 4. The<BR>body.<BR>	 5. A foot.<BR>	 6. A sort of cane, (Calamus rotang.)<BR> E. रम् to<BR>sport, Unādi aff. क्थन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकट्या
रथकट्या f. (ठ्या) A multitude of cars.<BR> E. रथ a car, and कठ्यच् aff. of multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकर|रथकरः
रथकर m. (-रः) A carpenter.<BR> E. रथ a car, and कर who makes; also<BR>रथकार and रथकृत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकल्पक|रथकल्पकः
रथकल्पक m. (-कः) An officer who has charge of a king's chariots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकार|रथकारः
रथकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A carpenter.<BR>	 2. A man sprung from the male of<BR>the Māhisya, and woman of the Kereṇ or writer caste; by pro-<BR>fession, a maker of cars, a coach-maker.<BR> E. रथ, कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकुटुम्बिन्|रथकुटुंबिन्
रथकुटुम्बिन् m. (-म्बी) A charioteer.<BR> E. रथ a car, कुटुम्बिन् who takes care<BR>of as a part of his family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथकूबर
रथकूबर mn. (-रः-रं) The polar shaft of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथगर्भक|रथगर्भकः
रथगर्भक m. (-कः) A car or litter borne on men's shoulders.<BR> E. रथ, गर्भ an embryo, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथगुप्ति|रथगुप्तिः
रथगुप्ति f. (-प्तिः) A piece of wood, or an iron net-work, encompassing<BR>a war-chariot, to secure it form being injured by weapons or col-<BR>lision.<BR> E. रथ car, गुप्ति screening, preserving; also रथगोपन n. (-नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथचरण|रथचरणः
रथचरण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The ruddy-goose.<BR>	 2. A chariot-wheel.<BR> E. रथ a car,<BR>and चरण the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथद्रु|रथद्रुः
रथद्रु m. (-द्रुः) A timber tree, (Dalbergia ougeiniensis.)<BR> E. रथ a car, द्रु<BR>the tree, the wood being used for wheels, &c.; also रथद्रुम m. (-मः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथन्तर|रथंतर|रथन्तरः
रथन्तर n. (-रं) The Sāma-Veda.<BR> E. रथ (as by) a car, तॄ to pass, (the<BR>world,) खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथपर्य्याय|रथपर्याय|रथपर्य्यायः
रथपर्य्याय m. (-यः) A sort of cane, the ratan.<BR> E. रघ a car, पर्य्याय order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथपाद|रथपादः
रथपाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A wheel.<BR>	 2. The ruddy-goose.<BR> E. रथ, पाद the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथप्सा
रथप्सा f. (-प्सा) The name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथयात्रा
रथयात्रा f. (-त्रा) A festival at which the chariots of the gods go in<BR>procession: in Bengal and Orissa it is applied to the procession of<BR>KRĪṢNĀ, as JAGANNĀTH, on the second of light fortnight of<BR>Āsāra.<BR> E. रथ, and यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथवाहक
रथवाहक m. (-कः) A charioteer.<BR> E. रथ and वाहक what conveys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथशक्ति|रथशक्तिः
रथशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) The staff which supports the banner of a war chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथाङ्ग|रथांग|रथाङ्गं|रथाङ्गः
रथाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. A wheel.<BR>	 2. Any part of a carriage.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) The<BR>ruddy-goose, (Anas casarca.)<BR> E. रथ a car, अङ्ग a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथाङ्गपाणि|रथाङ्गपाणिः
रथाङ्गपाणि m. (-णिः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. रथाङ्ग a wheel, (the discus<BR>with which one of his hands is armed,) and पाणि the hand; also<BR>रधाङ्गिन् and the like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथाभ्र|रथाभ्रः
रथाभ्र m. (-भ्रः) A sort of cane, (Calamus rotang.) “वेतसवृक्षे”.<BR> E. रथ, अभ्र a cloud or water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथाभ्रपुष्प|रथाभ्रपुष्पः
रथाभ्रपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A sort of reed: see the last.<BR> E. रथाभ्र the same, and<BR>पुष्प a flower; also रथ, रथाभ्र, and अभ्रपुष्प ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथारूढ
रथारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Mounted on or ridding in a car.<BR> E. रथ, आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथारोहण
रथारोहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Riding in a car.<BR>	 2. Fighting in a war-chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथारोहिन्
रथारोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Riding in a car.<BR>	 m. (-ही) A warrior who<BR>fights in a car.<BR> E. रथ a car, and आरोहिन् who mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथार्भक
रथार्भक m. (-कः) A small car.<BR> E. रथ, and अर्भक small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथावरोहण
रथावरोहण n. (-णं) Alighting for a car.<BR> E. रथ, and अवरोहण descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथावरोहिन्
रथावरोहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Descending from a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिक|रथिकः
रथिक m. (-कः) The owner of a car, or one who rides in it.<BR> E. रथ, ष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिन्
रथिन् m. (-थी)<BR>	 1. A warrior who fights in a car.<BR>	 2. The owner of or<BR>rider in a car.<BR> E. रथ, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिन|रथिनः
रथिन m. (-नः) The master of a car.<BR> E. रथ, and इन a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथिर|रथिरः
रथिर m. (-रः) The owner of or rider in a car.<BR> E. रथ, and इरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथोपस्थ|रथोपस्थः
रथोपस्थ m. (-स्थः) The charioteer's seat for driving.<BR> E. रथ, उप near, स्थ<BR>what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रथ्य|रथ्यः
रथ्य m. (-थ्यः) A car or carriage-horse.<BR>	 f. (-थ्या)<BR>	 1. A multitude of cars.<BR>2. A high street.<BR>	 3. A main or carriage-road.<BR>	 4. A place where<BR>several roads meet.<BR>	 n. (-थ्यं) A wheel.<BR> E. रथ a car, य or यत् affixes<BR>of multitude or fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्
रद् r. 1st cl. (रदति)<BR>	 1. To divide, to split, to ear or break.<BR>	 2. To dig,<BR>to delve, to root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद|रदः
रद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A tooth.<BR>	 2. Splitting, dividing.<BR> E. रद् to divide, aff.<BR>अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदच्छद|रदच्छदः|रदछद
रदच्छद m. (-दः) A lip.<BR> E. रद a tooth, and च्छद covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदन|रदनः
रदन m. (-नः) A tooth.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Tearing, rending.<BR> E. रद् to divide, aff. ल्युट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदनच्छद|रदनच्छदः|रदनछद
रदनच्छद m. (-दः) A lip.<BR> E. रदन a tooth, and च्छद covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रदिन्
रदिन् m. (-दी) An elephant.<BR> E. रद a tooth, tusk, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्ध
रद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Hurt, injured.<BR> E. रध् to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रद्धृ
रद्धृ mfn. (-द्धा-द्ध्री-द्धृ) Injurious, hurtful, who or what hurts.<BR> E. रध् to hurt, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रध्
रध् (ऌ, उ) ॡरधु r. 4th cl. (रध्यति)<BR>	 1. To finish, to complete, to accom-<BR>plish.<BR>	 2. To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR>	 3. To be right or correct.<BR>4. To cook or mature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रधित
रधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hurt, injured.<BR> E. रध् to hurt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रधितृ
रधितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Injurious, hurtful.<BR> E. रध् to hurt, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ति
रन्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Pleasure, sport.<BR>	 2. Cessation, stop.<BR> E. रम् to sport, क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तिदेव|रंतिदेव|रंतिदेवः|रन्तिदेवः
रन्तिदेव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A king of lunar dynasty;<BR>also called ŚASIDEVA.<BR>	 3. A dog.<BR> E. रन्ति sport, देव deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्तु|रंतुः|रन्तुः
रन्तु f. (-न्तुः)<BR>	 1. A road.<BR>	 2. A river.<BR> E. रम् to sport, aff. तु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धक
रन्धक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Injurious, hurtful.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A cook.<BR> E. रध् to hurt, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्धन|रंधन|रंधनं|रन्धनं
रन्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The act of destroying.<BR>	 2. Of cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ध्र|रंध्र|रंध्रं
रन्ध्र n. (-न्ध्रं)<BR>	 1. A hole, a fissure, a cavity, a chasm.<BR>	 2. A fault, a de-<BR>fect.<BR> E. रम् to sport, aff. क्विप्, धृ to have or hold, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ध्रबभ्रु|रंध्रबभ्रु|रन्ध्रबभ्रुः
रन्ध्रबभ्रु m. (-भ्रुः) A rat.<BR> E. रन्ध्र a hole, and बभ्रु an ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रन्ध्रवंश|रंध्रवंश|रन्ध्रवंशः
रन्ध्रवंश m. (-शः) Small sort of hollow bamboo. “तल्ता वांँश ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रप्
रप् r. 1st cl. (रपति) To speak, to say or tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रफ्
रफ् (इ) रफि r. 1st cl. (रफति रम्फति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रब्
रब् (इ) रबि r. 1st cl. (रम्बति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रब्ध
रब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Begun.<BR> E. रभ् to begin, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रब्धृ
रब्धृ mfn. (-ब्धा-ब्ध्री-ब्धृ) Beginning, who or what begins.<BR> E. रभ् to begin, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभ्
रभ् (औ) औ रभ r. 1st cl. (रभते) or more usually (आरभते) To begin, to<BR>make a beginning, to begin willingly, &c.<BR>	 2. To be pleased with.<BR>(इ) रभि r. 1st cl. (रंभते) To sound. With परि prefixed, To embrace.<BR>With सम, 1. To be enraged.<BR>	 2. To be agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रभस|रभसः
रभस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Speed, velocity.<BR>	 2. Joy, delight.<BR>	 3. Consideration of<BR>causes and events, or the past and future.<BR>	 4. Regret, sorrow for<BR>something lost or absent.<BR>	 5. Rashness, Precipitation.<BR>	 6. Passion,<BR>rage.<BR>	 f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. Violent, fierce, wild.<BR>	 2. Eager, strong, powerful.<BR>E. रभ् to begin, असच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्
रम् (औ, उ) औरमु r. 1st. cl. (रमते)<BR>	 1. To sport or play.<BR>	 2. To rest, to<BR>stay.<BR>	 3. To be pleased.<BR>	 4. To have sexual intercourse with. With<BR>अभि, To be delighted. With some prefixes this root forms an active<BR>verb, as with आङ्, उप and वि; आरमति to rest, to repose, &c.;<BR>with उप the form is optional, if the sense is intransitive, as<BR>(उपरमति or ते)<BR>	 1. To stop or cease.<BR>	 2. To desist from.<BR>	 3. To die.<BR>Caus. (रमयति-ते) To amuse, to please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम|रमः
रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Dear, beloved.<BR>	 2. Pleasing, delighting, charming.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A husband, a lover.<BR>	 2. KĀMA.<BR>	 3. A red variety of the<BR>Aśoka tree, (Jonesia asoca.)<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. A<BR>wife, a mistress.<BR> E. रम् to sport, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमक|रमकः
रमक m. (-कः) A lover, a gallant.<BR> E. रम् to sport, क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमठ|रमठं
रमठ n. (-ठं) Asafœtida. “हिङ्गुनि”.<BR> E. रम् to sport, अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमठध्वनि|रमठध्वनिः
रमठध्वनि m. (-निः) Asafœtida. रमठ इतिशब्देन ध्यन्यते ध्वन-इन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमण|रमणं|रमणः
रमण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Causing pleasure, pleasing, charming, delightful.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Sporting, playing.<BR>	 2. Dalliance, amorous sport.<BR>	 3. Coi-<BR>tion, copulation.<BR>	 4. The mons veneris.<BR>	 5. A sort of cucumber.<BR>	 6.<BR>The hip and the loins.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A name of KĀMA. or love.<BR>	 2.<BR>A husband.<BR>	 3. A lover, a gallant.<BR>	 4. An ass.<BR>	 5. A testicle.<BR>f. (णा or णी)<BR>	 1. A woman, or an agreeable woman, a wife, a<BR>mistress, &c.<BR>	 2. A kind of metre, having eleven syllables in the<BR>first and third, and twelve in the second and fourth Pādas of every<BR>stanza.<BR> E. रम् to sport, युच् or ल्य ट aff., fem. aff., टाप् or ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणीय|रमणीयं
रमणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Beautiful, pleasing.<BR> E. रम् to please, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमणीयता
रमणीयता f. (-ता) Agreeableness, pleasantness.<BR> E. तल् added to the<BR>preceding; also with त्व, रमणीयत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमण्य|रमण्यं
रमण्य n. (-ण्यं) Sport, pleasure, wanton sport or dalliance.<BR> E. रम् to sport, अन्य Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमत्
रमत् mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्) Playing, sporting.<BR> E. रम् to play, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमति|रमतिः
रमति m. (-तिः) A lover, a gallant.<BR>	 2. Paradise, heaven.<BR>	 3. A crow.<BR>	 4.<BR>Time.<BR>	 5. Love or the deity KĀMA.<BR> E. रम् to sport or stop, &c.<BR>Unādi aff. अतिच्; the final of the radical retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रममान
रममान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Sporting, playing,<BR> E. रम् to please, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमापति|रमापतिः
रमापति m. (-तिः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. रमा LAKṢMĪ, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमाप्रिय|रमाप्रियं|रमाप्रियः
रमाप्रिय n. (-यं) The lotus.<BR> E. रमा LAKṢMĪ, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रमावेष्ट|रमावेष्टः
रमावेष्ट m. (-ष्टः) Turpentine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भ|रंभः|रम्भः
रम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. A bamboo.<BR>	 2. The name of a monkey.<BR>	 f. (-म्भा)<BR>	 1. A<BR>plantain.<BR>	 2. One of the Apsarās or courtezans of Svarga, and wife<BR>of NALA-KŪBARA.<BR>	 3. A harlot, a whore.<BR>	 4. A name of GAURĪ.<BR>	 5.<BR>Lowing, as of a cow.<BR> E. रमि to sound, to begin, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भक
रम्भक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Beginning, who or what begins.<BR>	 2. Sounding.<BR>E. रभि to sound, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भित
रम्भित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounded.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Lowing, (of kine.)<BR> E. रभि to<BR>sound, &c., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्भोरु
रम्भोरु f. (-रुः or रूः) Having thighs as full and round as a plantain tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्य|रम्यः
रम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Pleasing, delightful, agreeable, charming.<BR>	 2.<BR>Handsome.<BR>	 m. (-म्यः) The champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 f. (-म्या)<BR>1. Night.<BR>	 2. The name of a river.<BR>	 n. (-म्यं)<BR>	 1. The root of a species<BR>of cucumber.<BR>	 2. Semen virile.<BR> E. रम् to sport, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्यक|रम्यकं
रम्यक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. One of the minor Dwīpas or divisions of the world,<BR>lying to the north of Ilāvṛta; also रमणक, and रमण्यक.<BR>	 2. The<BR>root of the Paṭola.<BR> E. रम्य agreeable, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्यता
रम्यता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Agreeableness, pleasantness.<BR>	 2. Gracefulness, beauty.<BR>E. रम्य and तल् aff.; also with त्व, रम्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रम्र|रम्रः
रम्र m. (-म्रः)<BR>	 1. Purple, the colour of the dawn.<BR>	 2. Beauty, splendor.<BR>E. रम् to please, aff. रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रय्
रय् r. 1st cl. (रयते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रय|रयः
रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Speed, velocity.<BR>	 2. The stream or current of a river.<BR>	 3.<BR>Violence, ardour, zeal.<BR> E. रय् to go, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयि
रयि n. (-यि)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Wealth.<BR> E. रय् to go, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रयिष्ठ|रयिष्ठः
रयिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Fleetest, very fleet.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. KUVERA.<BR>	 2. Fire<BR>or AGNI.<BR>	 3. BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. रय speed, quick, (used attributively,) and<BR>इष्ठन् aff. of the superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रल्लक|रल्लकः
रल्लक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A blanket.<BR>	 2. An eyelash.<BR>	 4. A sort of deer.<BR> E. रम् to<BR>please, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् with the final dropped रत् comfort, plea-<BR>sure, ला to give, aff. क्विप्, रल्ल and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रव्
रव् (इ) रवि r. 1st cl. (रम्वते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रव|रवः
रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Sound in general, cry, noise, singing of birds, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>thunder.<BR>	 3. A roar.<BR> E. रु to cry out, &c. aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवण|रवणं|रवणः
रवण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Sounding, sonorous.<BR>	 2. Hot, warm, sharp.<BR>	 3.<BR>Unsteady, fickle or shaking.<BR>	 4. Jesting, a jester.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>camel.<BR>	 2. The Kokila.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Bell-metal or brass.<BR>	 2. Sounding.<BR>E. रु to sound, Unādi aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवथ|रवथः
रवथ m. (-थः) The Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. रु to cry, &c. Unadī aff. अथन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रवि|रविः
रवि m. (-विः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The right canal for the passage of the<BR>vital air.<BR> E. रु to sound, passive form, to be praised or glorified,<BR>Unādi aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविकान्त|रविकांत|रविकान्तः
रविकान्त m. (-न्तः) The sun-stone, a sort of crystal. “सूर्य्यकान्तमणौ”<BR> E. रवि<BR>the sun, कान्त in this compound, a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविनन्दन|रविनन्दनः
रविनन्दन m. (-नः) The monkey chief SUGRĪVA.<BR> E. रवि the sun, नन्दन a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविनाथ|रविनाथं
रविनाथ n. (-थं) A lotus.<BR>	 m. (-थः) A flower, (Pentapetes phœnicea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविन्द
रविन्द n. (-न्दं) Lotus.<BR> E. रवि the sun, and दा to give, aff. खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविप्रिय|रविप्रियं|रविप्रियः
रविप्रिय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Copper.<BR>	 2. The red-lotus.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A plant, (Arto-<BR>carpus lacucha.)<BR> E. रवि the sun, प्रिय beloved. रक्तकरवीरे, अर्कवृक्षे च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविमण्डल
रविमण्डल n. (-लं) The disc of the sun.<BR> E. रवि, and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविमार्ग
रविमार्ग m. (-र्गः) The sun's path.<BR> E. रवि, मार्ग road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविमार्गभङ्ग
रविमार्गभङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Very high, stopping the course of the sun.<BR>E. रविमार्ग, भङ्ग what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविरत्न
रविरत्न n. (-त्नं) The ruby. “माणिक्ये ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविलोह|रविलोहं
रविलोह n. (-हं) Copper.<BR> E. रवि the sun, and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविवार|रविवारः
रविवार m. (-रः) Sunday.<BR> E. रवि, and वार a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविसंक्रान्ति
रविसंक्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः) The sun's entrance into a sign of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रविसंज्ञक
रविसंज्ञक n. (-कः) Copper.<BR> E. रवि the sun, and संज्ञक appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रशना
रशना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A tongue.<BR>	 2. A woman's girdle or zone. E. See रसन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रश्मि|रश्मिः
रश्मि m. (-श्मिः)<BR>	 1. A ray of light.<BR>	 2. A rein, a bridle.<BR>	 3. An eyelash.<BR>E. अश् to pervade, Unādi aff. मि, रश substituted for the radical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रश्मिजाल
रश्मिजाल n. (-लं) A blaze or stream of light.<BR> E. रश्मि, and जाल heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्
रस् r. 1st cl. (रसति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To roar, to cry. r. 10th cl. (रसयति<BR>ते)<BR>	 1. To taste, to relish.<BR>	 2. To love, to regard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस|रसं|रसः
रस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Flavour, taste, viz:--sweet, salt, pungent, bitter, sour,<BR>and astringent.<BR>	 2. Taste, sentiment, emotion, as an object of poe-<BR>try or composition; eight sentiments are usually enumerated, viz:--<BR>Sringāra or love, Hāsya or mirth, Karuṇa or tenderness, Raudra<BR>or anger, Bīra or heroism, Bhayānaka or terror, Bibhatsa or<BR>disgust, and Adbhuta or surprise; Śānta, tranquility or content<BR>or Bātsalya, paternal tenderness, is sometimes considered as the<BR>ninth.<BR>	 3. Affection of the mind, passion.<BR>	 4. Juice, exudation, a<BR>fluid, a liquid, or liquified substance.<BR>	 5. Poison.<BR>	 6. Semen virile.<BR>7. Water.<BR>	 8. The primary or essential juice or fluid of the body,<BR>whence blood, serum, sweat, &c. are supposed to be engendered;<BR>it corresponds best with chyle, but is probably of a fanciful<BR>nature.<BR>	 9. Gum myrrh.<BR>	 10. Quicksilver, from its being a semi-fluid<BR>metal, and according to certain alchemical notions possessed of<BR>supernatural power over the juices of the body, &c.<BR>	 11. A mineral<BR>or a metallic salt, as sulphur, borax, talc, blue or green vitriol,<BR>&c.; they are however usually called Upa or inferior Rasas.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-सा)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. The tongue.<BR>	 3. A plant, commonly Ākanādi.<BR>(Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>	 4. A sort of grain, (Panicum italicum.)<BR>5. The frankincense-tree, (Boswellia thurifera)<BR>	 6. The grape.<BR>	 7. A<BR>medical drug, commonly Kākoli.<BR> E. रस् to taste, to love, aff. अच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसक|रसकः
रसक m. (-कः) Stewed or boiled meat.<BR> E. रस juice, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसकर्प्पूर|रसकर्पूर|रसकर्पूरं
रसकर्प्पूर n. (-रं) A white sublimate or a muriate of mercury, made in<BR>close vessels with sulphur, mercury, and common salt; the cryst-<BR>als formed in the first operation are sublimed a second time,<BR>which seems to be the only essential difference between this and<BR>the preparations called Rasapushpa; ut infra.<BR> E. रस mercury, and<BR>कर्प्पूर camphor; from its white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसकला
रसकला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A low sweet sound.<BR>	 2. Singing upon intoxication. E.<BR>रस taste or vinous juice, and कला a note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसकेसर
रसकेसर n. (-रं) Camphor.<BR> E. रस juice, केसर a filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसगन्ध|रसगन्धं|रसगन्धः
रसगन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Gum myrrh.<BR>	 2. Sulphur.<BR> E. रस exudation, गन्ध fra-<BR>grance; with कन् added, रसगन्धक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसगर्भ|रसगर्भं
रसगर्भ n. (-र्भं)<BR>	 1. A mineral preparation used as a stibium.<BR>	 2. Vermi-<BR>lion.<BR> E. रस quicksilver, and गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसघ्न|रसघ्नः
रसघ्न m. (-घ्नः) Borax.<BR> E. रस mercury, घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसज|रसजं|रसजः
रसज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born or produced by or in passion flavour, fluids,<BR>&c.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Blood.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Any insect engendered by the<BR>acetous fermentation of liquids.<BR>	 2. Molasses, treacle.<BR> E. रस juice,<BR>the primary juice or chyle, &c., and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसज्ञ|रसज्ञः
रसज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Discriminating or acquainted with tastes, sen-<BR>timents, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. A poet, a writer who understands the<BR>different Rasas or sentiments to be described.<BR>	 2. An alchemist,<BR>one who has obtained a command over the magical properties of<BR>mercury.<BR>	 3. A physician, a medical preparer and administerer<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">Page599-a+ 60</a>]<BR>of mercurial and chemical compounds.<BR>	 f. (-ज्ञा) The tongue.<BR> E. रस<BR>as above, and ज्ञ who or what knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसज्ञता
रसज्ञता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Poetical skill or taste.<BR>	 2. Knowledge of flavours.<BR>	 3.<BR>Alchemy.<BR> E. रसज्ञ and तल् aff.; also with त्व, रसज्ञत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसज्येष्ठ|रसज्येष्ठः
रसज्येष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. The sweet flavour or taste, sweetness.<BR>	 2. The senti-<BR>ment of love.<BR> E. रस taste or sentiment, and ज्येष्ठ eldest, best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसत्
रसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Speaking, sounding.<BR>	 2. Tasting, having<BR>flavour.<BR> E. रस् to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसतेजस्
रसतेजस् n. (-जः) The blood.<BR> E. रस chyle, and तेजस् light, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसधातु|रसधातुः
रसधातु n. (-तु) Quicksilver.<BR> E. रस fluid, and धातु metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसन|रसनं|रसनः
रसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Tasting, taste.<BR>	 2. Sound, noise.<BR>	 3. Thunder.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>1. The tongue.<BR>	 2. A rope.<BR>	 3. A bridle.<BR>	 4. A plant, commonly<BR>Rāsnā.<BR>	 5. A woman's girdle, a sort of chain worn round the<BR>loins.<BR>	 6. A plant, (Pæderia fœtida.)<BR> E. रस् to sound or taste, aff.<BR>युच्; or अश् to eat, युच् Unādi aff., and रश substituted; also रशना ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनाथ|रसनाथः
रसनाथ m. (-थः) Quicksilver.<BR> E. रस juice, fluid, and नाथ chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनायक|रसनायकः
रसनायक m. (-कः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. रस mercury, नायक leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनारद|रसनारदः
रसनारद m. (-दः) A bird.<BR> E. रसना the tongue, रद a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनालिह्
रसनालिह् m. (-लिट्) A dog.<BR> E. रसना the tongue, लिह् to lick, aff. क्किप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनिवृत्ति|रसनिवृत्तिः
रसनिवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Loss of taste, flavour, &c.<BR> E. रस, and निवृत्ति cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनेत्रिका
रसनेत्रिका f. (-का) Red arsenic.<BR> E. रस, नेतृ eye, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसपुष्प
रसपुष्प n. (-ष्प) A preparation of mercury, a kind of muriate formed by<BR>subliming. in close vessels, a mixture of sulphur, mercury, and<BR>common salt.<BR> E. रस mercury, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसफल|रसफलः
रसफल m. (-लः) The cocoanut tree.<BR> E. रस water or juice, and फल the<BR>fruit, the nut containing a saccharine fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसभङ्ग|रसभंग|रसभङ्गः
रसभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Interruption or destruction of passion or sentiment,<BR>&c.<BR> E. रस, भङ्ग a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसभव|रसभवं
रसभव n. (-वं) The blood.<BR> E. रस chyle, and भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसभस्मन्
रसभस्मन् n. (-स्म) Calx or oxid of mercury.<BR> E. रस, and भस्मन् ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसयित्वा
रसयित्वा Ind. Having tasted.<BR> E. रस् to taste, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसराज|रसराजः
रसराज m. (-जः) Quicksilver.<BR> E. रस a mineral, राज sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसवत्|रसवन्त्
रसवत् Ind. Including a secondary or subsidiary feeling or passion. E.<BR>रस, वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसवत्|रसवन्त्
रसवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Juicy.<BR>	 2. Well-flavoured.<BR>	 3. Tasteful,<BR>applied to a composition, &c.<BR>	 4. Spirited, witty.<BR>	 f. (-ती) A kitchen.<BR>E. रस juice, flavour, &c., मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसविक्रय|रसविक्रयः
रसविक्रय m. (-यः) Selling juices or liquors, as the juice of the sugar-<BR>cane, or wine, &c.<BR> E. रस juice, and विक्रय sale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसशोधन|रसशोधनं|रसशोधनः
रसशोधन m. (-नं) Borax.<BR> E. रस a metal, &c., and शोधन purifying; being<BR>used as a flux in refining and melting metals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिद्ध
रससिद्ध m. (-द्धः) An alchemist, an adept: see the next.<BR> E. रस mercury,<BR>सिद्ध accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिद्धि|रससिद्धिः
रससिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) The knowledge of alchemy, the possession of peculiar<BR>familiarity with mercury, obtained by the performance of chemi-<BR>cal operations conjoined with certain mystical and magical rites,<BR>and the securing thence to the adept, of happiness, health, and<BR>wealth, the power of transmuting metals, and the art of pro-<BR>longing life.<BR> E. रस mercury, and सिद्धि accomplishment, especially<BR>of some supernatural object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिन्दूर|रससिन्दूरं
रससिन्दूर n. (-रं) A sort of factitious cinnabar, made with zinc, mer-<BR>cury, blue vitriol, and nitre, fused together; the compound is<BR>used as an escharotic.<BR> E. रस mercury and सिन्दूर minium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसस्थान|रसस्थानं
रसस्थान n. (-नं) Cinnabar or vermilion.<BR> E. रस mercury and स्थान abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाखन|रसाखनः
रसाखन m. (-नः) A cock.<BR> E. रसा the earth, and खन who digs or picks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाञ्जन|रसाञ्जनं
रसाञ्जन n. (-नं) A sort of collyrium, prepared either with the calx of<BR>brass, or with the Amomum anthorrhiza.<BR> E. रस juice, &c., अञ्जन<BR>collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसातल|रसातलं
रसातल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Pātāla; the seven infernal regions under the earth,<BR>and the residence of the Nāgas, Asuras, Daityas, and other races<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">Page599-b+ 60</a>]<BR>of monstrous and demoniacal beings, under the various govern-<BR>ments of Sesha, Bali, and other chiefs; this is not to be confound-<BR>ed with Naraka or Tartarus, the proper hell or abode of guilty<BR>mortals after death.<BR>	 2. The lowest of the seven divisions of Pātāla.<BR>E. रसा the earth, and तल below, underneath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसादान|रसादानं
रसादान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sucking, suction.<BR>	 2. Drying, drying up, absorbing.<BR>E. रस water, or juice, &c., आदान taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाधार|रसाधारः
रसाधार m. (-रः) The sun.<BR> E. रस water, आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसान्तर
रसान्तर n. (-रं) Change or diversion of passion or sentiment.<BR> E. रस and अन्तर different.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाभास|रसाभासः
रसाभास m. (-सः) Concealment of sentiment, attributing evident emo-<BR>tions to some cause different from the real one.<BR> E. रस sentiment,<BR>आभास unreal exposition or display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाभिनिवेश|रसाभिनिवेशः
रसाभिनिवेश m. (-शः) Accession of sentiment or passion.<BR> E. रस, अभिनिवेश intentness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाम्ल|रसाम्लं|रसाम्लः
रसाम्ल m. (-म्लः) Sour sauce.<BR>	 n. (-म्लं) The hog-plum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसायक|रसायकः
रसायक m. (-कः) A sort of grass, (Saccharum munja.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसायन|रसायनं|रसायनः
रसायन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Alchemy, chemistry.<BR>	 2. The employment of mercury<BR>in medicine.<BR>	 3. A medicine preventing old age, and prolonging<BR>life, the Elixir Vitæ of the alchemists.<BR>	 4. Poison.<BR>	 5. Butter-milk.<BR>m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. GARUDĀ.<BR>	 2. An anthelmintic drug commonly Biranga,<BR>(Embelia ribes.)<BR>	 2. An alchemist.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A vessel conveying nu-<BR>trition, a lacteal, an absorbent.<BR> E. रस juice, quicksilver, &c., अयन<BR>a road, a going, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसायनफला
रसायनफला f. (-ला) Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.) “हरीतकी<BR>वृक्षे”.<BR> E. रसायन juice, abiding, फला fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाल|रसालं|रसालः
रसाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The sugar-cane.<BR>	 2. The mango-tree, (Mangifera In-<BR>dica.)<BR>	 3. The jack-tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR>	 4. The Olibanum<BR>tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>	 5. Wheat.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Frankincense.<BR>	 2.<BR>Gum myrrh.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The tongue.<BR>	 2. Bent grass, (Panicum dac-<BR>tylon.)<BR>	 3. A flower, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>	 4. A grape.<BR>	 5.<BR>Curds mixed up with sugar and spices.<BR> E. रस juice, आङ् before,<BR>ला to yield, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालसा
रसालसा f. (-सा) A tubular vessel of the body, a nerve, a tendon, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालिहा
रसालिहा f. (-हा) A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia.) “चाकुलिया ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसास्वाद|रसास्वादः
रसास्वाद m. (-दः) The sense of poetical beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसास्वादिन्
रसास्वादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Tasting, relishing.<BR>	 2. Sensitive, having<BR>taste.<BR>	 m. (-दी) A bee.<BR> E. रस flavour, and आस्वादिन् who tastes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाह्व|रसाह्वः
रसाह्व n. (-ह्वं) Turpentine, resin.<BR> E. रस juice and आह्व appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिक|रसिकः
रसिक mfn. (-कः-का-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Flavoured, having taste or flavour.<BR>	 2.<BR>Tasteful, as a composition, &c.<BR>	 3. Having a taste for poetry, &c.<BR>4. Sentimental.<BR>	 5. Impassioned.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. An ele-<BR>phant.<BR>	 3. A libertine.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Curds mixed with sugar and spice.<BR>2. Molasses, the juice of the sugar-cane.<BR>	 3. The tongue.<BR>	 4. A wo-<BR>man's zone or girdle.<BR> E. रस flavour, sentiment, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसित|रसितं
रसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gilded, plated, washed or spread with gold,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Sounded.<BR>	 3. Having taste, flavour, or sentiment.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>1. The rattling of thunder.<BR>	 2. Voice, sound in general.<BR>	 3. Wine.<BR>E. रस् to sound, aff. क्त; or रस fluid, (metal, &c.,) इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसितवत्
रसितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Tasting, having tested or having a taste<BR>for.<BR>	 2. Sounding.<BR> E. रस to have flavour, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिताशिन्
रसिताशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>	 1. Eating or seizing with a noise or roar.<BR>2. Drinking wine.<BR> E. रसित आशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसितृ
रसितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Sounding, making a noise.<BR>	 2. Tasting, relish-<BR>ing.<BR> E. रस् to sound, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिन्
रसिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>	 1. Tasting.<BR>	 2. Impassioned.<BR>	 3. Humerous.<BR> E. रस, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसुन|रसुनः
रसुन m. (-नः) Garlic. E. See लसुन, र being changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसेन्द्र|रसेंद्र|रसेन्द्रः
रसेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. Quicksilver.<BR>	 2. The philosopher's stone, the touch of<BR>which turns iron to gold.<BR> E. रस a mineral and इन्द्र best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसोत्पत्ति|रसोत्पत्तिः
रसोत्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Production of taste or flavour.<BR>	 2. Development<BR>of passion or sentiment.<BR>	 3. Generation of the vital fluids.<BR> E. रस,<BR>and उत्पत्ति production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसीन
रसीन m. (-नः) A kind of garlic, (Allium ascalonicum.)<BR> E. रस flavour<BR>taste, ऊन to be less or deficient, aff. अच्; being supposed to con-<BR>tain in the leaves, stalk, root, &c., every flavour except sourness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसोपल|रसोपलं
रसोपल n. (-लं) A pearl.<BR> E. रस water, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्व
रस्व n. (-स्वं) Thing, substance.<BR> E. रस juice, &c., and नक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्य|रस्यं
रस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Juicy.<BR>	 n. (-स्यं) Blood.<BR> E. रस chyle, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रह्
रह् r. 1st cl. (रहति) r. 10th cl. (रहयति-ते) To quit, to leave, to forego,<BR>to lose or abandon. With वि, To be separate or away from, (इ) रहि<BR>r. 1st cl. (रंहति) To go, to move with speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रह|रहः
रह m. (-हः) Solitariness, privacy.<BR> E. रह् to be private, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहण|रहणं
रहण n. (-णं) Quitting, leaving.<BR> E. रह् to leave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहत्
रहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्) Leaving, abandoning.<BR> E. रह् to leave, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्
रहस् n. Subst. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Solitariness, privacy.<BR>	 2. Copulation.<BR>	 3. A pri-<BR>vity.<BR>	 4. A religious or mystic truth. Ind. or an adv. (-हः) Solitary,<BR>private, in private, secretly, privily.<BR> E. रह् to abandon, (society,<BR>&c.) and असुन् aff.; or रम् to sport or play, with the same aff., and<BR>अह substituted for the radical final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस
रहस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. Heaven.<BR> E. रह् to leave, असच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्य|रहस्यं
रहस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Private, secret, either fit to be concealed or<BR>occuring in secret.<BR>	 n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. A secret, a mystery, anything hid-<BR>den, recondite or mysterious.<BR>	 2. Any esoteric teaching.<BR>	 f. (-स्या)<BR>	 1.<BR>Clandestine.<BR>	 2. Mysterious.<BR>	 3. The name of a river, perhaps the<BR>Saraswatī, from its being supposed to flow in an unknown chan-<BR>nel.<BR> E. रहस् secret, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहाट|रहाटः
रहाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A minister.<BR>	 2. A ghost.<BR>	 3. Spring.<BR> E. रह् privately, अट् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहित|रहितं
रहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Left, quitted, abandoned.<BR>	 2. Free from, devoid<BR>of.<BR> E. रह् to leave, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहीभूत
रहीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Alone, solitary, in private.<BR> E. रह and भूत been, with च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रा
रा r. 2nd. cl. (राति)<BR>	 1. To get, to gain, to receive.<BR>	 2. To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राका
राका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Full-moon, or the day of full-moon.<BR>	 2. A girl in whom<BR>menstruation has commenced.<BR>	 3. Scab, itch.<BR>	 4. The name of a<BR>river.<BR> E. रा to give, (good fortune,) क Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षस|राक्षसः
राक्षस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Infernal, demoniacal.<BR>	 m. (-सः) An evil spirit, a<BR>demon, a vampire, a fiend, but who appears to be of various des-<BR>criptions, and is either a powerful Titan or enemy of the gods in<BR>a superhuman or incarnate form, as RĀVAṆA and others; an at-<BR>tendant on KUVERA, and guardian of his treasures; or a mischie-<BR>vous and cruel goblin or ogre, haunting cemeteries, animating<BR>dead bodies, and devouring human beings.<BR>	 f. (-सी)<BR>	 1. A female<BR>fiend, the female of the preceding.<BR>	 2. A large tooth, a tusk.<BR>	 3. A<BR>sort of perfume, commonly Chor.<BR>	 n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. A form of marriage,<BR>the violent seizure and rape of a girl after the repulse or des-<BR>truction of her relatives.<BR>	 2. Surgery, cure by the knife of cautery.<BR>E. रक्ष् to preserve, to be preserved, (from whom,) aff. असुन्, and<BR>अण् pleonasm added; or रक्षस् a demon, and अण् aff. of reference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षसेन्द्र|राक्षसेन्द्रः
राक्षसेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. RĀVAṆA.<BR>	 2. KUVERA.<BR> E. राक्षस a demon, इन्द्र lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षा
राक्षा f. (-क्षा) Lac, the red animal dye.<BR> E. रक्ष् to preserve, (colour,) अ<BR>aff.; the vowel made long; perhaps an incorrect form of लाक्षा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राख्
राख् (ऋ) राखृ r. 1st cl. (राखति)<BR>	 1. To be dry or arid.<BR>	 2. To adorn.<BR>	 3.<BR>To suffice, to be able or competent.<BR>	 4. To impede or prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राग|रागः
राग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Colour, hue, tint. dye.<BR>	 2. Affection, prepossession,<BR>love, desire.<BR>	 3. Mental affection in general, as sorrow, joy, &c.<BR>4. Envy, impatience of another's success.<BR>	 5. A mode of music;<BR>of which six are enumerated, viz.:--Bhairava, Kausika, Srīrāga,<BR>Hindola, Dipaka, and Megha; they are personified in poe-<BR>try and mythology.<BR>	 6. A king, a sovereign.<BR>	 7. The Raja Gūna,<BR>the property or quality of passion.<BR>	 8. Greediness, cupidity.<BR>	 9.<BR>Colouring, painting, dying.<BR>	 f. (-गी) A sort of grain, commonly<BR>Raggy, much cultivated in the south of India, (Eleusine corocana,<BR>or Cynosurus corocanus.)<BR> E. रञ्ज् to colour, &c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागचूर्ण|रागचूर्णः
रागचूर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. A name of KĀMA.<BR>	 2. A tree, yielding an astringent<BR>resin or extract, the wood of which is used in dying, (Acacia ca-<BR>techu.)<BR>	 3. Red lead.<BR>	 4. The red powder thrown over one another<BR>by the Hindus, at the vernal festival named Holi.<BR> E. राग passion<BR>or colour, and चूर्ण powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागच्छन्न|रागच्छन्नः|रागछन्न
रागच्छन्न m. (-न्नः) KĀMA.<BR> E. राग and च्छन्न covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागद|रागदः
रागद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Colouring.<BR>	 2. Inspiring passion.<BR>	 f. (-दा) Crys-<BR>tal.<BR> E. राग colour, दा to give, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागबन्ध|रागबन्धः
रागबन्ध m. (-न्धः) The manifestation of musical harmony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागयुज्
रागयुज् m. (-युट्) A ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागरज्जु|रागरज्जुः
रागरज्जु m. (-ज्जुः) The deity of love, KĀMA.<BR> E. राग passion, रज्जु a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागलता
रागलता f. (-ता) The wife of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. राग, लता a creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागवत्|रागवन्त्
रागवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Coloured.<BR>	 2. Impassioned.<BR> E. राग, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागवृन्त|रागवृन्तः
रागवृन्त m. (-न्तः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. राग passion, वृन्त the stalk of a<BR>flower, the support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागषाढव
रागषाढव m. (-वः) A sweetmeat of unripe mangoes dressed with treacle and oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागसूत्र|रागसूत्रं
रागसूत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The string of a balance.<BR>	 2. A string or thread of<BR>silk.<BR>	 3. Any coloured thread or string.<BR> E. राग colour, सूत्र a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागान्वित
रागान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Affected dy passion.<BR>	 2. Coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागार्ह
रागार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं)<BR>	 1. One who excites hopes and disappoints them.<BR>2. Who or what is an object of affection.<BR> E. राग, अर्ह fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागाशनि|रागाशनिः
रागाशनि m. (-निः) A Jaina saint.<BR> E. राग, अश् to throw, (away,) अनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिन्
रागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि)<BR>	 1. Passionate, impassioned.<BR>	 2. Colouring,<BR>painting.<BR>	 3. Coloured, dyed.<BR>	 m. (-गी)<BR>	 1. A dyer, a painter.<BR>	 2. A<BR>libertine, a lover.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A shrewd and intriguing woman.<BR>	 2.<BR>A modification of a musical mode of which five are assigned to<BR>each mode; in mythology, personified as a female, and the wife of<BR>the Rāga.<BR> E. राग passion, इनि aff., or रञ्ज् to colour, &c., घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघ्
राघ् (ऋ,) राघृ r. 1st cl. (राघते) To be able or equal to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघव|राघवः
राघव m. (वः)<BR>	 1. A name of RĀMACHANDRA.<BR>	 2. A sort of fish.<BR> E. रघु<BR>the ancestor of the demi-god, and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कल|रांकलः|राङ्कलः
राङ्कल m. (-लः) A thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कव|रांकव|राङ्कवं
राङ्कव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Woolen, made of the hair of a sort of deer or any<BR>other animal.<BR>	 n. (-वं) A woolen garment. made of the deer's hair,<BR>a blanket.<BR> E. रङ्कु a kind of deer, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्
राज् (ऋ,) राजृ r. 1st cl. (राजति-ते or irregularly रेजते) To shine: With<BR>निर् prefixed, To overcome, to subdue. Caus. (राजयति-ते) With निस्<BR>1. To adorn, to illuminate.<BR>	 2. To wave light before an idol or a<BR>king, (as an act of worship.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्
राज् m. (-राट्) A king, a monarch or prince.<BR> E. राज् to shine, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजक|राजकं|राजकः
राजक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Ruling, a ruler.<BR>	 2. Splendid, irradiating,<BR>bright in itself, and the cause of brilliancy in others.<BR>	 n. (-कं) An<BR>assemblage of princes.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A petty prince.<BR> E. राजन् a prince,<BR>and वुञ् aff. of multitude; or राज् to shine, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकर|राजकरः
राजकर n. (-रं) Tax or toll imposed by the king.<BR> E. राज and कर tribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकदम्ब|राजकदम्बः
राजकदम्ब m. (-म्बः) A sort of Kadamba.<BR> E. राज royal, कदम्ब Nauclea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकशेरु|राजकशेरुः
राजकशेरु m. (-रुः) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR> E. राज, कशेरु cyperus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकार्य्य|राजकार्य
राजकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Royal duties, state affairs.<BR> E. राज, and कार्य्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकीय|राजकीयः
राजकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Royal, kingly<BR> E. राजन् a king, क substituted<BR>for the final, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकुल
राजकुल n. (-लं) A royal race.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A prince, a king.<BR> E. राज and कुल family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकुष्माण्ड|राजकुष्माण्डः
राजकुष्माण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR> E. राज royal,<BR>and कुष्माण्ड a gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकृत्वन्
राजकृत्वन् m. (-त्वा) A king-maker, one who raises him to the throne,<BR>&c.<BR> E. राजन्, and कृ to make, क्वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजगामिन्
राजगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Going to the prince or ruler, devolving or<BR>falling to the king, (as property, &c. to which there are no heirs.)<BR>E. राज the king, गामिन् what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजगुरु|राजगुरुः
राजगुरु m. (-रुः) The king's spiritual preceptor.<BR> E. राज a king, and<BR>गुरु preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजग्रीव|राजग्रीवः
राजग्रीव m. (-वः) A sort of flat fresh water-fish, commonly Phalūi. E.<BR>राज shining, ग्रीव the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजघ|राजघः
राजघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं) Sharp, hot.<BR>	 m. (-घः) A king-killer, a slayer of<BR>sovereigns, a regicide.<BR> E. राज a king, and घ for घ्न, who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजचिह्नक|राजचिह्नकं
राजचिह्नक n. (-कं) The male or female organs of generation.<BR> E. राज chief,<BR>चिह्न mark, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजजक्ष्मन्
राजजक्ष्मन् m. (-क्ष्मा) Pulmonary consumption.<BR> E. राज royal, principal,<BR>and जक्ष्मम् for यक्ष्मन् consumption; also राजयक्ष्मन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजजम्बू
राजजम्बू f. (-म्बूः)<BR>	 1. A large kind of eugenia or rose-apple. “वड जाम इति<BR>भाषा” 2. A sort of date.<BR> E. राज royal, and जम्बू Eugenia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजत|राजतं
राजत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Silver, made of silver, &c.<BR> E. रजत silver, अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतान्वित
राजतान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Plated, inlaid.<BR> E. राजत, अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजताल|राजतालः
राजताल m. (-लः) The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel.)<BR> E. राज, ताल palm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतिमिष
राजतिमिष m. (-षः) A cucumber.<BR> E. राज royal, and तिमिष a kind of<BR>gourd; it is also read राजतेमिष । “तरमुज्”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतेजस्
राजतेजस् n. (-जः) Majesty, kingly dignity.<BR> E. राज, and तेजस् splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजत्व|राजत्वं
राजत्व n. (-त्वं) Sovereignty, royalty.<BR> E. राज a king, त्व aff. of the<BR>abstract; also with तल्, राजता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदण्ड|राजदण्डः
राजदण्ड n. (-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Punishment ordered by the king.<BR>	 2. A baton, a<BR>sceptre.<BR> E. राज, दण्ड a staff, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदन्त|राजदन्तः
राजदन्त m. (-न्तः) An upper and fore-tooth, applied to the two middle<BR>ones.<BR> E. राज royal, दन्त tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदर्शन
राजदर्शन n. (-नं) A levee, and audience.<BR> E. राज, and दर्शन seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदेशीय|राजदेशीयः
राजदेशीय m. (-यः) A petty prince or chief, one something less than a<BR>king.<BR> E. राज a king, and देशीयर् aff., implying something less or<BR>defective, or with देश्य aff. of the same power, राजदेश्य m. (-श्यः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजद्रोह|राजद्रोहः
राजद्रोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Oppression.<BR>	 2. Rebellion.<BR> E. राज, द्रोह violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजद्रोहिन्
राजद्रोहिन् m. (-ही) A rebel, a traitor.<BR> E. राजद्रोह, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजद्वार
राजद्वार n. (-रं) The gate of the palace.<BR> E. राज for राजा king, द्वार gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधन
राजधन n. (-नं) Royal revenue or right to property.<BR> E. राज, धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधर्म्म|राजधर्म|राजधर्मः|राजधर्म्मः
राजधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>	 1. Royal duty.<BR>	 2. The duty of the military tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधर्म्मविद्|राजधर्मविद्
राजधर्म्मविद् m. (-वित्) A statesman, one who knows the duties of royal-<BR>ty.<BR> E. राज, धर्म्म duty, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधान
राजधान nf. (-नं-नी) A royal city, a capital, a metropolis.<BR> E. राज a king,<BR>धान holding, containing; also with कन् added in the n. or f. (राज-<BR>धानक-राजधानिका) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधान्य|राजधान्यं
राजधान्य n. (-न्यं) A sort of grain, (Panicum frumentaceum, Rox.) E.<BR>राज royal, धान्य grain. “राजभोग हैमन्तिक धान्य भेदः ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजधुरा
राजधुरा f. (-रा) Royal state or function, government.<BR> E. राज, धुरा a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्
राजन् m. (-जा)<BR>	 1. A king, a prince, a sovereign.<BR>	 2. A soldier by birth,<BR>a man of the regal and military tribe.<BR>	 3. A master.<BR>	 4. The moon.<BR>5. A Yakṣa.<BR>	 6. INDRA.<BR>	 7. (In com.) Royal, denoting eminence<BR>or excellence.<BR>	 f. (-ज्ञी)<BR>	 1. A queen, the wife of a king.<BR>	 2. The wife<BR>of the sun.<BR>	 3. Deep coloured brass, consisting of three parts of<BR>copper to one of zinc or tin.<BR> E. राज् to shine, Unādi aff. कनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजनय|राजनयः
राजनय m. (-यः) Polity.<BR> E. राज, नय conduct; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजनीति|राजनीतिः
राजनीति f. (-तिः) Regal polity, statesmanship, civil and military<BR>government.<BR> E. राज, and नीति polity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजनील|राजनीलं
राजनील n. (-लं) The emerald.<BR> E. राज royal, and नील blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्य|राजन्यः
राजन्य m. (-न्यः)<BR>	 1. A Kṣatriya, a man of the military or regal tribe.<BR>	 2.<BR>A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Mimusops kauki, Rox.) “क्षीरिणी<BR>गाछ.”<BR> E. राज् to shine, अन्य Unādi aff.; or राजन् a king, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्यक|राजन्यकं
राजन्यक n. (-कं) A number of Kṣatriyas or men of the military tribe.<BR>E. राजन्य a soldier, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्वत्|राजन्वन्त्
राजन्वत् mfn. (-न्वान्-न्वती-न्वत्) Possessing or governed by a just and<BR>active monarch, (a country, &c.)<BR> E. राजन् a king, (or by distinction<BR>a good king,) and मतुप् poss. aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपटोल|राजपटोलः
राजपटोल m. (-लः) A kind of cucumber, (Trichosanthes diœca.)<BR> E. राज<BR>royal, and पटोल the same; also with कन् added, राजपटोलक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपट्ट|राजपट्टः
राजपट्ट m. (-ट्टः)<BR>	 1. A gem, said to be an inferior kind of diamond<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">Page601-b+ 60</a>]<BR>brought from BIRĀTA DEŚA, a country in the north-west of<BR>India.<BR>	 2. A tiara or royal fillet.<BR> E. राज a king, and पट्ठ a bandage,<BR>worn in the tiara or diadem of a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपत्नी
राजपत्नी f. (-त्नी) A queen.<BR> E. राज, and पत्नी wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपुत्त्र
राजपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. The planet MERCURY.<BR>	 2. A Kṣatriya or man of<BR>the military tribe.<BR>	 3. A soldier by profession but one of a mixed<BR>birth or fabulous origin.<BR>	 4. The son of a king, a prince.<BR>	 f. (-त्त्री)<BR>	 1.<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 2. A bitter gourd.<BR>	 3. The musk-shrew.<BR>	 4. A kind<BR>of brass or bell-metal.<BR>	 5. A princess.<BR>	 6. A woman of the Rājput<BR>tribe.<BR> E. राज a king or the moon, and पुत्त्र a son, a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपुत्त्रिका
राजपुत्त्रिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A kind of bird. “शरालपाखी”.<BR>	 2. A king's daughter.<BR>E. राज a king, पुत्त्र a child, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपुरुष|राजपुरुषः
राजपुरुष m. (-षः) A guard, a watchman, a constable, &c.<BR> E. राज and पुरुष a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजपुष्प|राजपुष्पः
राजपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A plant, (Mesua ferrea.) “नागेश्वर गाछ” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजफणिञ्झक
राजफणिञ्झक m. (-कः) The orange-tree.<BR> E. राज royal, फणिञ्झक a<BR>sort of lime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजफल|राजफलं
राजफल n. (-लं) A cucumber, (Trichosanthes diœca.)<BR> E. राज royal, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजबदर|राजबदरं|राजबदरः
राजबदर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A plant, (a sort of Justicia.)<BR>	 2. Salt.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The<BR>jujube.<BR> E. राज royal, and बदर the jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभट्टिका
राजभट्टिका f. (-का) A water-fowl. “हापुत्रीपक्षिणि ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभद्रक|राजभद्रकः
राजभद्रक n. (-कं) A sort of costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR> E. राज royal, भद्रक auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभाज्
राजभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Belonging to or claimed by the king.<BR> E. राज, and<BR>भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभूय|राजभूयं
राजभूय n. (-यं) Royalty, sovereignty.<BR> E. राज a king, and भूय condition of being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभृत्य|राजभृत्यः
राजभृत्य m. (-त्यः) A courtier, a servant of the king, any public officer.<BR>E. राज, and भृत्य a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभोग्य|राजभोग्यं
राजभोग्य m. (-ग्यः) A tree, (Chironjia sapida, or Buchanania latifolia,<BR>Rox.) “पियालवृक्षे” n. (-ग्यं) Mace.<BR> E. राज royal, and भोग्य enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजभौत|राजभौतः
राजभौत m. (-तः) A king's fool or jester.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमण्डुक
राजमण्डुक m. (-कः) A large kind of frog.<BR> E. राज a king, मण्डुक a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमल्ल|राजमल्लः
राजमल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A king's wrestler.<BR> E. राज a king, मल्ल a wrestler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमार्ग|राजमार्गः
राजमार्ग m. (-र्गः) A royal road, one passable for horses and elephants,<BR>and forty cubits broad.<BR> E. राज a king, and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमाष|राजमाषः
राजमाष m. (-षः) A kind of bean, (Dolichos Catjang or sinensis.) “वरवटी”<BR>E. राज् royal, and माष a sort of kidney-bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमुद्ग|राजमुद्गः
राजमुद्ग m. (-द्गः) A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus.)<BR> E. राज royal, and<BR>मुद्ग P. mungo. “मकुष्ठके, मुग् इति भाषा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयक्ष्मन्
राजयक्ष्मन् m. (-क्ष्मा) Pulmonary consumption.<BR> E. राज chief, यक्ष्मन् phthisis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयुध्वन्
राजयुध्वन् m. (-ध्वा) An enemy, a rebel, one making war against a prince.<BR>E. राज, युध् to make war, क्वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयोग|राजयोगः
राजयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The configuration of planets at the birth of a man<BR>indicating his future king-ship.<BR>	 2. An easy mode of abstract medi-<BR>tation, as distinguished from the rigorous one called Hatayoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयोग्य|राजयोग्यः
राजयोग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Proper or suitable for a sovereign, princely,<BR>royal.<BR> E. राज a king, and योग्य what is fit for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजरङ्ग|राजरंग|राजरङ्गं
राजरङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Silver.<BR> E. राज royal, and रङ्ग tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजराज|राजराजः
राजराज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A name of KUVERA.<BR>	 2. An emperor, an universal<BR>monarch, or king of kings.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR> E. राज a king, (of a king<BR>or kings,) or a Yakṣa, and राज sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजरीति|राजरीतिः
राजरीति f. (-तिः) Bell-metal. “वेङा पितल ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजर्षि|राजर्षिः
राजर्षि m. (-र्षिः) A kind of saint; that holy and superhuman personage<BR>which a king or man of the military class may become by the<BR>practice of religious austerities; seven classes of Ṛṣis are enu-<BR>merated, the DeVARSHI, BRAHMARSHI, MAHARSHI, PARAMARSHI,<BR>RAJARSHI, KĀṆḌARSHI, and ŚRUTARSHI: the order is variously<BR>given, but the RĀJARSHI is inferior to the four preceding ones,<BR>and the two last mean the inspired saints and supposed authors of<BR>the scriptures.<BR> E. राज king, and ऋषि a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलक्षण
राजलक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Royal insignia.<BR>	 2. Any natural mark indicating<BR>future Kingship, or Hindu royalty.<BR> E. राज, and लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलक्ष्मन्
राजलक्ष्मन् m. (-क्ष्मा) A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR> E. राज royal, लक्ष्मन् a mark<BR>or symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलक्ष्मी
राजलक्ष्मी f. (-क्ष्मी) The prosperity of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलेख|राजलेखः
राजलेख m. (-खः) A royal letter or order.<BR> E. राज, and लेख a writing; also राजलेख्यं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवंश्य|राजवंश्यः
राजवंश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Of royal parentage or descent.<BR> E. राज royal,<BR>वंश family, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवत्|राजवन्त्
राजवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Governed by a just and able monarch,<BR>(a country, &c.)<BR>	 2. Royal, kingly.<BR> E. राज a king, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवर्त्मन्
राजवर्त्मन् n. (-र्त्म) A royal or main road.<BR> E. राज a king, and वर्त्मन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवला
राजवला f. (-ला) A plant, (Pæderia fœtida.)<BR> E. राज a king, and वल sur-<BR>rounding. “गन्धभादुलिया” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवल्ली
राजवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A small gourd, (Momordica charantia.) “कारवेल्लके” E.<BR>राज royal, वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवसति|राजवसतिः
राजवसति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A throne.<BR>	 2. A palace.<BR> E. राज, and वसति abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवाह|राजवाहः
राजवाह m. (-हः) A horse.<BR> E. राज a king, and वाह a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवाह्य|राजवाह्यः
राजवाह्य m. (-ह्यः) A royal elephant.<BR> E. राज a king, and वाह्य a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवि|राजविः
राजवि m. (-विः) The blue-jay.<BR> E. राज, and वि a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजविद्या
राजविद्या f. (-द्या) Kingcraft, state policy, statesmanship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजविहार|राजविहारः
राजविहार m. (-रः) A royal convent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवीजिन्
राजवीजिन् mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि) Springing from a royal race.<BR> E. राज a<BR>king, वीज seed, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवृक्ष|राजवृक्षः
राजवृक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The Piyāla tree, (Buchanania latifolia.)<BR>	 2. A sort<BR>of tree, (Cassia fistula.) “सोन्दाल”.<BR>	 3. Euphorbia of various kinds. E.<BR>राज royal, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशण|राजशणः
राजशण m. (-णः) A plant, from the fibres of which a coarse cordage and<BR>canvas are prepared, (Corchorus capsularis or olitorius.)<BR> E. राज<BR>royal, and शण Crotolaria. “पाट गाछ” इति भाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशय्या
राजशय्या f. (-य्या) A royal seat or throne.<BR> E. राज a king, and शय्या a bed or couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशासन
राजशासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A royal edict.<BR>	 2. A royal badge.<BR> E. राज and शासन<BR>an edict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशुक|राजशुकः
राजशुक m. (-कः) A sort of parrot, (Psittacus Lori.) “मयनापाखी”.<BR> E. राज royal, and शुक a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशृङ्ग|राजशृंग|राजशृङ्गं|राजशृङ्गः
राजशृङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) The royal Chātta or umbrella.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) A sort of<BR>sheat fish, (Silurus batachus.) “मागुरमाछ”.<BR> E. राज royal, शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस|राजसः
राजस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Relating to, or derived, &c. from the quality of<BR>Rajas or passion.<BR>	 f. (-सी)<BR>	 1. The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. The state of<BR>being in this world or the next, in which the Raja Guṇa or quality<BR>of passion predominates: it is divided into three classes: the first<BR>class comprises the Gandharbas, Yakṣas, Guhyakas, &c.; the<BR>second king and heroes, and the third, boxers, wrestlers, gamb-<BR>lers, tipplers, actors, &c.<BR> E. रजस् the quality of passion, अण् and<BR>ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसत्ता
राजसत्ता f. (-त्ता) Majesty, royal dignity.<BR> E. राज, and सत्ता existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसदन|राजसदनं
राजसदन n. (-नं) A palace.<BR> E. राज a king, and सदन a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसफर|राजसफरः
राजसफर m. (-रः) The Iliśa or Hilsā fish, (Clupanodon Ilisha, HAM.) E.<BR>राज king, and सफर another sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसभा
राजसभा f. (-भा) A royal assembly or court.<BR> E. राज a king, सभा assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसर्प|राजसर्पः
राजसर्प m. (-र्पः) A large kind of snake, (Boa.)<BR> E. राज, and सर्प a snake;<BR>the king of snakes. “राजसाप” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसर्षप|राजसर्षपः
राजसर्षप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Mustard, (Sinapis dichotoma, or S. ramosa, Rox.)<BR>2. A mustard seed, as a measure of weight.<BR> E. राज royal, सर्षप<BR>mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसायुज्य|राजसायुज्यं
राजसायुज्य n. (-ज्यं) Royalty, sovereignty.<BR> E. राज a king, सायुज्य state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसारस|राजसारसः
राजसारस m. (-सः) A peacock.<BR> E. राज royal, and सारस the Indian crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसिंह
राजसिंह m. (-हः) A great king.<BR> E. राज, and सिंह a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसूय|राजसूयः
राजसूय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A sacrifice performed only by an universal monarch,<BR>attended by his tributary princes; as in the case of YUDHIṢṬHIRA,<BR>and others.<BR>	 2. A lotus.<BR>	 3. A mountain.<BR>	 4. A sort of rice.<BR> E. राज a<BR>king, (by him,) and षू to be produced, to be effected, aff. क्यप्; or<BR>राज the moon, for the moon-plant of which the acid-juice is drank<BR>at the ceremony, and सु to bring forth, the same aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसूयक
राजसूयक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to a royal sacrifice.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसूययाजिन्
राजसूययाजिन् m. (-जी) A priest officiating at the royal sacrifice. E.<BR>राजसूय, and याजिन् who sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसेवक
राजसेवक m. (-कः) A courtier, a royal attendant.<BR> E. राज, and सेवक a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्कन्ध|राजस्कन्धः
राजस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) A horse.<BR> E. राज a king, and स्कन्ध the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्व|राजस्वं
राजस्व n. (-स्वं) Royal revenue, impost, duty, tax.<BR> E. राज, and स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहंस|राजहंसः
राजहंस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A white goose with red legs and bill, or more proper-<BR>ly perhaps the flamingo.<BR>	 2. A drake.<BR>	 3. An excellent king.<BR> E. राज,<BR>and हंस a goose, the king-goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहर्षण|राजहर्षणं
राजहर्षण n. (-णं) A city, a town.<BR> E. राज a king, and हर्षण delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहस्तिन्
राजहस्तिन् m. (-स्ती) A royal elephant.<BR> E. राज, and हस्तिन् an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहासक|राजहासकः
राजहासक m. (-कः) A sort of large fish, (Cyprinus niloticus.) “कात्लामाछ”<BR>E. राज a king, हासक diverting, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाज्ञा
राजाज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) A royal edict or command.<BR> E. राज and आज्ञा order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजातन|राजातनः
राजातन m. (-नः) A tree, (Buchanania latifolia.) “पीतशालवृक्षे”.<BR> E. राज a<BR>king, and आङ् before, तन् to stretch, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजादन|राजादनं|राजादनः
राजादन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Bachanania latifolia.)<BR>	 2. Another tree,<BR>(Mimusops kauki.) “क्षीरिणीवृक्षे”.<BR>	 3. The Kinśuka, (Butea frondosa.)<BR>E. राज a king, अदन eating; also राजातन, and राजादनफल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाधिराज|राजाधिराजः
राजाधिराज m. (-जः) A paramount sovereign.<BR> E. राजा, अधिराज superior prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजान्न|राजान्नं
राजान्न m. (-न्नः) A sort of rice, of a superior quality, said to grow in<BR>the Āndhra country.<BR> E. राज, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाम्र|राजाम्रः
राजाम्र m. (-म्रः) A superior sort of mango.<BR> E. राज royal, अम्र mango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाम्ल|राजाम्लः
राजाम्ल m. (-म्लः) A kind of dock or sorrel: see अम्लवेतस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजार्क|राजार्कः
राजार्क m. (-र्कः) Gigantic swallow wort, (Asclepias gigantea, with white<BR>flowers.)<BR> E. राज royal, and अर्क swallow wort. “श्वेतआकन्दे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजार्ह|राजार्हं
राजार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Royal, noble, fit or proper for a king.<BR>	 n. (-र्हं)<BR>Aloe-wood, (Amyris agallochum, Rox.) “अगुरुकाष्ठे”.<BR> E. राज a sover-<BR>eign, and अर्ह proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजालुक|राजालुकः
राजालुक m. (-कः) An esculent root, a sort of yam. “रशुने”.<BR> E. राज royal,<BR>आलु a yam, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजावर्त्त|राजावर्त|राजावर्तः|राजावर्त्तः
राजावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A gem, described as an inferior kind of diamond,<BR>brought from the country Birāta.<BR> E. राज a king, आवर्त्त a turning;<BR>it is considered as a lucky possession for princes, though not es-<BR>teemed as an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजावलि|राजावलिः
राजावलि f. (-लिः-ली) A line of kings, a royal dynasty or genealogy. E.<BR>राज and आवली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाहि|राजाहिः
राजाहि m. (-हिः) A sort of snake said to be two-headed.<BR> E. राज royal, अहि a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजि|राजिः
राजि f. (-जिः-जी)<BR>	 1. A row, a line.<BR>	 2. An unbroken row, a continuous<BR>line.<BR>	 3. A small vessel of the body.<BR> E. राज् to shine, इन् Unādi aff.,<BR>ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिका
राजिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Black mustard, (Sinapis racemosa, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A field.<BR>3. A line, a row, a range.<BR>	 4. A continuous or unbroken line. E.<BR>राज to shine, क्वुन् aff., fem. form; or राजि as above, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजित
राजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Adorned, embellished.<BR>	 2. Illuminated, irradia-<BR>ted.<BR> E. राज to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिल|राजिलः
राजिल m. (-लः) A sort of snake, (Amphisbæna.) “ढोंडासाप”.<BR> E. राजि a line, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीव|राजीवं|राजीवः
राजीव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Attending on or living about a prince.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A large fish, (Cyprinus niloticus, BUCH.)<BR>	 2. A kind of deer.<BR>	 3. An<BR>elephant.<BR>	 n. (-वं) A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum.)<BR> E. राजी a line,<BR>a row, व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेन्द्र|राजेंद्र|राजेन्द्रः
राजेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) An emperor.<BR> E. राज, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेभ
राजेभ m. (-भः) A state elephant.<BR> E. राज, and इभ an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेय
राजेय m. (-यः) A kind of cucumber: see पटोल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्ञी
राज्ञी f. (-ज्ञी) A queen. नील्यां, कांस्ये, जातीपुष्यवृक्षे, पित्तलेच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्य|राज्यं
राज्य n. (-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. A government, a country, a principality, a kingdom.<BR>2. Administration or exercise of sovereignty or government. E.<BR>राज for राजन् a prince, and यत् or यक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यच्युत
राज्यच्युत m. (-तः) A prince who has lost his kingdom.<BR> E. राज्य, and च्युत fallen from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यच्युति
राज्यच्युति f. (-तिः) Deposal, loss of sovereignty.<BR> E. राज्य, and च्युति falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यतन्त्र|राज्यतंत्र
राज्यतन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) Science of government, system of administration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यधुरा
राज्यधुरा f. (-रा) Administration, burden or yoke of government. E.<BR>राज्य, धुरा burthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभङ्ग|राज्यभंग|राज्यभङ्गः
राज्यभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Subversion of sovereignty.<BR> E. राज्य and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभाज्
राज्यभाज् m. (-भाक्) A king.<BR> E. राज्य, and भाज् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभ्रंश|राज्यभ्रंशः
राज्यभ्रंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Deposal or loss of a kingdom.<BR> E. राज्य and भ्रंश falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभ्रष्ट
राज्यभ्रष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A deposed sovereign.<BR> E. राज्य, भ्रष्ट fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यरक्षा
राज्यरक्षा f. (-क्षा) Protection or defence of a kingdom.<BR> E. राज्य, रक्षा preservation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यलोभ|राज्यलोभः
राज्यलोभ m. (-भः) Ambition.<BR> E. राज्य and लोभ desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्याङ्ग|राज्यांग|राज्याङ्गं
राज्याङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A requisite of regal administration; variously enu-<BR>merated, as seven, eight, or nine, viz.:--first, the monarch;<BR>second, the prime minister; third, a friend or ally; fourth, trea-<BR>sure; fifth territory; sixth a strong-hold; and seventh, an army;<BR>the eighth is the population or companies of citizens, and the<BR>ninth the Purohita or spiritual adviser.<BR> E. राज्य royalty, and अङ्ग<BR>limb or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्याधिकार|राज्याधिकारः
राज्याधिकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Government of a kingdom.<BR>	 2. Right or title<BR>to a sovereignty.<BR> E. राज्य and अधिकार superintendance, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्याभिषेक|राज्याभिषेकः
राज्याभिषेक m. (-कः) Inauguration of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राटि|राटिः
राटि f. (-टिः) War, battle.<BR> E. रट् to speak, to sound, aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राढा
राढा f. (-ढा)<BR>	 1. Beauty, splendour, light, lustre.<BR>	 2. A country or dis-<BR>trict, part of Bengal to the west of the Hugli-river.<BR> E. रह to quit,<BR>aff. घञ्, and ह changed to ढ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राण|राणं
राण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A leaf.<BR>	 2. A peacock's tail.<BR> E. रण् to sound, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रक|रात्रकं|रात्रकः
रात्रक n. (-कं) A period of five nights collectively.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A man who<BR>takes up his abode in a harlot's house for one year.<BR> E. रात्रि night,<BR>and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रि|रात्रिः
रात्रि f. (-त्रिः-त्री) Night, the darkness of night.<BR> E. रा to give, (pleasure or<BR>rest,) त्रिप् Unādi aff., ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिकर|रात्रिकरः
रात्रिकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिचर|रात्रिचरः
रात्रिचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Going or moving at night.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A goblin, a<BR>fiend, a ghost or evil spirit.<BR>	 2. A thief, a robber.<BR>	 3. A guard, a<BR>patrole.<BR> E. रात्रि night, (by night,) and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिचर्या
रात्रिचर्या f. (-र्या)<BR>	 1. Night-roving.<BR>	 2. A nightly act or ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिज
रात्रिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Nocturnal, born or produced at night.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>A star, a constellation.<BR> E. रात्रि night, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजल|रात्रिजलं
रात्रिजल n. (-लं) Dew, mist, fog.<BR> E. रात्रि night, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजागर|रात्रिजागरः
रात्रिजागर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Keeping watch at night, sitting up at night.<BR>m. (-रः) A dog.<BR> E. रात्रि night, and जागर who wakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजागरण
रात्रिजागरण n. (-णं) Sitting up all night.<BR> E. रात्रि, and जागरण waking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजागरद|रात्रिजागरदः
रात्रिजागरद m. (-दः) A musquito, a gnat.<BR> E. रात्रिजागर waking by night,<BR>and द who gives or makes, from दा to give, or from दो to cut, who<BR>stings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिञ्चर|रात्रिंचर|रात्रिञ्चरः
रात्रिञ्चर m. (-रः) A ghost, a goblin.<BR> E. रात्रि night, चर् to go, ट aff., मुम् aug.; also रात्रिचर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रितरा
रात्रितरा f. (-रा) The dead of night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिपुष्प|रात्रिपुष्पं
रात्रिपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) A lotus-flower opening at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिमट|रात्रिमटः
रात्रिमट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A ghost, a goblin.<BR>	 2. A thief.<BR>	 3. A guard.<BR>	 4. A<BR>night-walker.<BR> E. रात्रि night, अट् to go, aff. अच्, and मुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिमणि|रात्रिमणिः
रात्रिमणि m. (-णिः) The moon.<BR> E. रात्रि night, मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिम्मन्य|रात्रिंमन्य
रात्रिम्मन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Thinking it night.<BR> E. रात्रि, मन्य who believes, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रियोग|रात्रियोगः
रात्रियोग m. (-गः) Coming on of night.<BR> E. रात्रि, and योग joining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिराग|रात्रिरागः
रात्रिराग m. (-गः) Darkness, obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिवासस्
रात्रिवासस् n. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Night-dress.<BR>	 2. Darkness.<BR> E. रात्रि night, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिविगम|रात्रिविगमः
रात्रिविगम m. (-मः) Dawn, day-light.<BR> E. रात्रि night, विगम stop, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिविश्लेषगामिन्
रात्रिविश्लेषगामिन् m. (-मी) The ruddy-goose.<BR> E. रात्रि night, विश्लेष separa-<BR>tion, and गामिन् who goes: these birds being supposed to pass the<BR>night apart. “चक्रवाकपक्षिणि” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिवेद|रात्रिवेदः
रात्रिवेद m. (-दः) A cock.<BR> E. रात्रि night, वेद who knows, its measure or duration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिवेदिन्
रात्रिवेदिन् m. (-दी) A cock.<BR> E. रात्रि night, वेदिन् who knows: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिहास|रात्रिहासः
रात्रिहास m. (-सः) The white lotus.<BR> E. रात्रि night, and हास what smiles,<BR>blossoming at night. “श्वेतोत्पले” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिहिण्डक|रात्रिहिण्डकः
रात्रिहिण्डक m. (-कः) A guard of the interior or women's apartments.<BR> E. रात्रि, हिडि to go, क्कुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र्यट|रात्र्यटः
रात्र्यट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. An imp, a goblin.<BR>	 2. A ghost.<BR>	 3. A thief.<BR>	 4. A night-<BR>walker.<BR> E. रात्रि, अट् to go, aff. अच्; also with nasal inserted, रात्रिमट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र्यन्ध|रात्र्यंध|रात्र्यन्धः
रात्र्यन्ध Adj. Night-blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्ध|राद्धं
राद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Cooked, dressed.<BR>	 2. Perfected, as a religious<BR>vow; observed, as a fast, &c.<BR>	 3. Perfect, in mysterious or magical<BR>power, adept, initiated.<BR>	 4. Perfect in general, accomplished,<BR>mature, &c.<BR>	 5. Successful, fortunate.<BR>	 6. Propitiated, conciliated.<BR>E. राध् to accomplish or be accomplished, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धान्त|राद्धांत|राद्धान्तः
राद्धान्त m. (-न्तः) Demonstrated truth, proved and established fact or<BR>conclusion, a dogma.<BR> E. राद्ध established, अन्त end, result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धि|राद्धिः
राद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Accomplishment. Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध्
राध्(औ)औराध r. 4th cl. (राध्यति)<BR>	 1. To be favourable or merciful.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be ready, to be successful.<BR>	 3. To kill. With अनु or आ, To propitiate,<BR>to adore. With अप, (usually used with a loc., but sometimes with<BR>a gen.)<BR>	 1. To offend, to miss, to err.<BR>	 2. To injure. With वि, To<BR>injure, to offend, to hurt. Caus. (रोधयति-ते) With आ, 1. To<BR>please.<BR>	 2. To serve. r. 5th cl. (राध्नोति)<BR>	 1. To bring anything to<BR>fulness or completion, to finish, to effect, to accomplish, to<BR>complete.<BR>	 2. To attain completion, to succeed, to be finished or<BR>accomplished.<BR>	 3. To destroy. With अप prefixed, To offend, to be in<BR>fault. With आङ्, To worship, to propitiate by worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध|राधः
राध m. (-धः) The month Vaiśākha, (April-May.)<BR>	 f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. The<BR>asterism, in which the moon is full in the month Vaiśākha; the<BR>sixteenth of the Nakshatras, containing four stars in the shape of<BR>a festoon.<BR>	 2. A celebrated Gopi, the favourite mistress of KṚṢṆA,<BR>during his residence in Brindāvana amongst the cow-<BR>herds.<BR>	 3. Name of the foster mother of KARṆA.<BR>	 4. Prosperity.<BR>	 5.<BR>Lightning.<BR>	 6. An attitude in shooting, standing with the feet a<BR>span apart.<BR>	 7. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 8. A flower, (Clitoria ternata.)<BR>E. राध् to accomplish, aff. अच्, fem. aff. टाप्; or राधा the asterism,<BR>अण् aff. of reference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधन|राधनं
राधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Completing, accomplishing, succeeding, effecting.<BR>	 2.<BR>Obtaining, acquisition.<BR>	 3. Pleasure, satisfaction.<BR>	 4. The means or<BR>instrument of accomplishing any thing.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Speech, speaking.<BR>E. राध् to accomplish, aff. ल्युट् or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधरङ्क|राधरङ्कः
राधरङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A plough.<BR>	 2. Thin-rain.<BR>	 3. Hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधाकान्त|राधाकान्तः
राधाकान्त m. (-न्तः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. राधा, and कान्त beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधातनय|राधातनयः
राधातनय m. (-यः) KARṆA.<BR> E. राधा, and तनय son; see राधासुत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधानाथ
राधानाथ m. (-थः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. राधा, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधापुत्त्र
राधापुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) KARṆA.<BR> E. राधा, and पुत्त्र son: see राधासुत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधाभेदिन्
राधाभेदिन् m. (-दी) A name of ARJUNA.<BR> E. राधा the mistress of KṚṢṆA,<BR>and भेदिन् dividing; having prevailed on KṚṢṆA to abandon her.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधावल्लभ
राधावल्लभ m. (-भः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. राधा, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधावेधिन्
राधावेधिन् m. (-धी) ARJUNA.<BR> E. राधा the mistress of KṚṢṆA, and वेधिन्<BR>who hurts or wounds: see राधाभेदिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधासुत|राधासुतः
राधासुत m. (-तः) KARṆA.<BR> E. राधा the name of the wife of the charioteer<BR>of DHRITARĀSHTRA, (by whom the prince, after exposure by his<BR>own mother KUNTĪ, was found and fostered,) and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधेय|राधेयः
राधेय m. (-यः) A name of KARṆA.<BR> E. राधा a proper name, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राप्य|राप्यः
राप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be said or spoken.<BR> E. रप् to speak, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम|रामं|रामः
राम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Black.<BR>	 2. White.<BR>	 3. Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>1. A name common to three incarnations of VIṢṆU, viz:-firstly,<BR>PARAŚURĀMA, the son of the Muni JAMADAGNI, born at the com-<BR>mencement of the second or TRETA YUGA, for the purpose of<BR>punishing the tyrannical kings of the Kṣatriya race. Secondly,<BR>RĀMACHANDRA, the son of DAŚARATHA, king of Oudh, born at<BR>the close of the second age, to destroy the demons who infested<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">Page604-a+ 60</a>]<BR>the earth, and especially RĀVAṆA the Daitya-sovereign of Ceylon.<BR>Thirdly, BALARĀMA, (the elder and half-brother of KṚṢṆA,)<BR>the son of BĀSUDEVA by ROHINI, born at the end of the DWĀPARA<BR>or third age.<BR>	 2. A name of VARUṆA, regent of the waters.<BR>	 3. A<BR>horse.<BR>	 4. A sort of deer.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A woman, a female, a plea-<BR>sing or beautiful female.<BR>	 2. Asafœtida.<BR>	 3. A river.<BR>	 4. Vermilion.<BR>n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>	 2. A sort of Costus,<BR>(C. speciosus.)<BR> E. रम् to sport, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकरी
रामकरी f. (-री) One of the Rāgīnis, or female personifications of the<BR>musical modes.<BR> E. राम delighting, करी who makes; also रामकली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकर्पूर
रामकर्पूर m. (-रः) A fragrant sort of grass.<BR> E. राम pleasant, and कर्पूर<BR>(smelling like,) camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासकली
रासकली f. (-ली) A Rāgīni.<BR> E. राम pleasant, कला sound or note, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामगिरि|रामगिरिः
रामगिरि m. (-रिः) The name of a mountain, variously applied, but espe-<BR>cially assigned to a mountain called COMPTEH or CHITRAKŪṬA in<BR>BUNDELKHUND, and to another near NĀGPORE, called now RĀMTEK.<BR>E. राम the hero RĀMA, and गिरि a mountain; being one of his<BR>halting places in his progress from Oudh to the Peninsula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामचन्द्र|रामचंद्र|रामचन्द्रः
रामचन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) The hero RĀMACHANDRA, the son of DASARATHA. E.<BR>राम and चन्द्र the moon, the moon-like RĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामजननी
रामजननी m. (-नी) The mother of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. राम and जननी mother,<BR>hence it is equally applicable to RENUKĀ, the mother of<BR>PARAŚURĀMA, and to KAUŚALYA, the mother of RĀMACHANDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामठ|रामठं|रामठः
रामठ n. (-ठं) Asafœtida.<BR> E. रम् to please, अठ Unādi aff., and the radi-<BR>cal vowel lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामणीयक|रामणीयकं
रामणीयक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Beautiful, pleasing.<BR> E. रमणीय the same, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामदूत|रामदूतः
रामदूत m. (-तः) The monkey HANUMĀNA, the friend and messenger of<BR>RAMĀ.<BR>	 f. (-तिः-ती) A shrub, apparently a variety of basil with<BR>small leaves. “नाग्दोना”.<BR> E. राम RĀMA, and दूत a messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामनवमी
रामनवमी f. (-मी) The ninth day in the light-half of Chaitra, the anni-<BR>versary of the birth of RĀMACHANDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामपूग|रामपूगः
रामपूग m. (-गः) A small species of the areca or betel-nut tree, (Areca<BR>triandra, Rox.)<BR> E. राम RĀMA, पूग areca.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामभद्र|रामभद्रः
रामभद्र m. (-द्रः) The hero RĀMACHANDRA.<BR> E. राम the same, and भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामवीणा
रामवीणा f. (-णा) A sort of Vina or lute.<BR> E. राम RĀMA and वीणा a lute;<BR>it may be also ironically applicable to the horn blown by BALA-<BR>RĀMA, and called still the RĀMASINHĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामशर|रामशरः
रामशर m. (-रः) A variety of the Saccharum Sara, a sort of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामसख|रामसखः
रामसख m. (-खः) The monkey-king SUGRĪVA.<BR> E. राम RĀMA, and सख<BR>friend; RĀMA having restored him to his throne, whence he had<BR>been driven by his elder brother BĀLI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामसेतु|रामसेतुः
रामसेतु m. (-तुः) A bridge of sand, now a chain of islands, between the<BR>Indian Peninsula and Ceylon, popularly known by “Adam's bridge”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामायण|रामायणं
रामायण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The first epic poem of the Hindus, written by the<BR>poet VĀLMIKI, recording the adventures of RĀMA, the son of DAŚA<BR>RATHA, sovereign of Oudh.<BR>	 2. A name of several poems on the<BR>life and adventures of RĀMA.<BR> E. राम the prince, and अयन abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामानुज|रामानुजः
रामानुज m. (-जः) Name of the founder of a Vedāntic sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामिल|रामिलः
रामिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>	 2. A lover, a husband.<BR> E. राम<BR>pleasing, agreeable, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम्भ|रांभ|रांभः|राम्भः
राम्भ m. (-म्भः) The bamboo staff of a religious student.<BR> E. रम्भा a bamboo, aff. अञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायण|रायणं
रायण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Pain.<BR>	 2. Sounding, crying.<BR> E. रै to sound, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायभाटी
रायभाटी f. (-टी) The current or flow of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रारस्यमान
रारस्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Crying aloud and repeatedly.<BR> E. रस to cry, reit. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राल|रालः
राल m. (-लः) Resin, the resinous and fragrant exudation of the Shorea<BR>robusta. “धुना”.<BR> E. रा to give or get, aff. अलच्; also अराल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राव|रावः
राव m. (-वः) Sound, noise.<BR> E. रु to cry or sound, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावण|रावणः
रावण m. (-णः) The Daitya-sovereign of Lankā or Ceylon, killed by<BR>RĀMACHANDRA.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Noise, tumult.<BR> E. रु to cry, (in the causal<BR>form,) aff. ल्युट; afflicting mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणारि|रावणारिः
रावणारि m. (-रिः) The hero RĀMA.<BR> E. रावण, अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणि|रावणिः
रावणि m. (-णिः) The eldest son of RĀVAṆA.<BR> E. रावण, इञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राश्
राश्(ऋ)राशृ r. 1st and 4th cl. (राशते राश्यते) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशि|राशिः
राशि m. (-शिः)<BR>	 1. A heap, a quantity.<BR>	 2. A sign of the zodiac.<BR>	 3. Arith-<BR>metical or algebraic quantity.<BR>	 4. A part and its divisor or nu-<BR>merator and denominator.<BR>	 5. A congeries of number or quantity.<BR>E. अश् to pervade, इण् Unādi aff., and रुट् initial augment; or<BR>रश् to sound, with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिगत
राशिगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Heaped, accumulated.<BR>	 2. Computed, sum-<BR>med either by arithmetic or algebra.<BR> E. राशि, and गत gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिचक्र|राशिचक्रं
राशिचक्र n. (-क्रं) The zodiac.<BR> E. राशि, a sign, and चक्र a wheel or circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशित्रय
राशित्रय n. (-यं) The rule of three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिभाग|राशिभागः
राशिभाग m. (-गः) A fraction.<BR> E. राशि, भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिभोग|राशिभोगः
राशिभोग m. (-गः) Passage of a planet through a sign of the zodiac. E.<BR>राशि, भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीकरण
राशीकरण n. (-णं) Heaping, piling, gathering.<BR> E. राशि, करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीकृत
राशीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Heaped, piled, &c.<BR> E. राशि, कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीभूत
राशीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Heaped, piled.<BR> E. राशि, and भूत become, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्र|राष्ट्रं|राष्ट्रः
राष्ट्र mn. (-ष्ट्रः-ष्ट्रं)<BR>	 1. An inhabited country or realm, a region.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>public calamity, as plague, famine, &c.<BR> E. राज् to shine or govern,<BR>aff. ष्ट्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रनिवासिन्
राष्ट्रनिवासिन् m. (-सी) An inhabitant of any civilized country.<BR> E. राष्ट्र a<BR>district, निवासिन् a dweller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिक|राष्ट्रिकः
राष्ट्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Bolonging to or inhabiting a country.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>A prickly sort of night-shade, (Solanum jacquini.) “कण्टकारी”.<BR> E. राष्ट्र<BR>a country, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिय|राष्ट्रियः
राष्ट्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of or belonging to a kingdom, produced or born<BR>in it, &c.<BR> E. राष्ट्र a region, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रीय|राष्ट्रीयः
राष्ट्रीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging or relating to a region or realm.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-यः) A king's brother-in-law, (in theatrical language.)<BR> E. राष्ट्र a<BR>region, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्
रास्(ऋ)रासृ r. 1st cl. (रासते) To sound, to cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास|रासः
रास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Confused noise, uproar, hubbub.<BR>	 2. Sound in general.<BR>	 3.<BR>Speech, discourse.<BR>	 4. A chain.<BR>	 5. A festival amongst the cowherds,<BR>including songs and dances, especially the circular dance as per-<BR>formed by KṚṢṆA and the Gopis or cowherdesses.<BR>	 6. A game<BR>played by children.<BR> E. रास् to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासक|रासकं
रासक n. (-कं) A kind of minor drama in one act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभ|रासभः
रासभ m. (-भः) An ass.<BR>	 f. (-भी) The she-ass.<BR> E. रास् to sound, अभच Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभधूसर
रासभधूसर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Grey or light-brown, ass-grey.<BR> E. रासभ,<BR>धूसर grey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभवन्दिनी
रासभवन्दिनी f. (-नी) Arabian jasmine.<BR> E. रासभ an ass, वदि to praise, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासयात्रा
रासयात्रा f. (-त्रा) A festival held in honour of KṚṢṆA on the full-<BR>moon of Kārtika.<BR> E. रास, and यात्रा festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासेरस|रासेरसः
रासेरस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. An assembly, a company, a party.<BR>	 2. A game or<BR>festival peculiar to the cowherds: see रास.<BR>	 3. Love, desire, the<BR>passion or sentiment.<BR>	 4. Alchemy: see रससिद्धि.<BR>	 5. The sixth night<BR>after delivery, on which the family and friends sit up all night.<BR>6. Sport, mirth, pastime.<BR>	 7. Any festival or holiday.<BR> E. रास noise,<BR>&c., and रस flavour, taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्ना
रास्ना f. (-स्ना)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>	 2. Another plant, (the ser-<BR>pent ophioxylon.)<BR>	 3. A sort of perfume.<BR> E. रस् to sound, नक् Unādi<BR>aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहित्य|राहित्यं
राहित्य n. (-त्यं) The being without anything, destitution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहु|राहुः
राहु m. (-हुः) The ascending node; in mythology, the son of VIPRACHITTI<BR>by SINHIKĀ, a Daitya, with the tail of a dragon, whose head was<BR>severed from his body by VIṢṆU, on the information of the sun<BR>and the moon who caught him in the act of drinking Amrita which<BR>was being served to gods, but being immortal by tasting it, his<BR>head and tail retained their separate existence, and being transferred<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">Page605-a+ 60</a>]<BR>to the stellar sphere, became the authors of eclipses; the first<BR>especially, by endeavouring at various times to swallow the sun<BR>and the moon to wreak his vengeance.<BR> E. रह् to abandon, (the<BR>planets which it has vainly attempted to devour,) aff. उण्, and the<BR>vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुग्रस्त
राहुग्रस्त m. (-स्तः) Eclipsed, (as the sun or moon.)<BR> E. राहु, and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुग्रास|राहुग्रासः
राहुग्रास m. (-सः) Immersion of a planet in an eclipse.<BR> E. राहु, and ग्रास<BR>mouthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुग्राह|राहुग्राहः
राहुग्राह m. (-हः) An eclipse of the sun or moon.<BR> E. राहु the dragon's head, ग्राह seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुभेदिन्
राहुभेदिन् m. (-दी) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. राहु the Daitya, भेदिन् the divider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुमूर्द्धभिद्
राहुमूर्द्धभिद् m. (-भित्) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. राहु the Daitya, मूर्द्ध the head, and भिद्<BR>who divides, who decapitates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुलसू
राहुलसू m. (-सूः) A name of the legislator Buddha or Sākyasingha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुसंस्पर्श|राहुसंस्पर्शः
राहुसंस्पर्श m. (-र्शः) An eclipse.<BR> E. राहु the dragon's head, and संस्पर्श<BR>seizure, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुसूतक
राहुसूतक n. (-कं) The birth of RĀHU. i. e. an eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुहन्
राहुहन् m. (-हा) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. राहु the Daitya, हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहूच्छिष्ट|राहूच्छिष्टः
राहूच्छिष्ट m. (-ष्टः) Garlic.<BR> E. राहु the demon, उच्छिष्ट vomited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहूत्सृष्ट|राहूत्सृष्टः
राहूत्सृष्ट m. (-ष्टः) Garlic.<BR> E. राहु the Daitya, उत्सृष्ट created. “रशोने” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रि
रि r. 5th cl. (रिणोति) To hurt or injure. r. 6th cl. (रियति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रि
रि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. The tone of voice by which the note Rishabha is uttered.<BR>2. Dancing, tumbling.<BR>	 3. Waste, loss.<BR>	 f. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2.<BR>Light, lustre.<BR> E. रा to give, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक
रिक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The heart, the mind.<BR>	 2. Law, litigation.<BR> E. रिच् to divide, &c., aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्त|रिक्तं
रिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Empty, void.<BR>	 2. Poor, indigent.<BR>	 3. Unloaded,<BR>unburthened.<BR>	 4. Purged.<BR>	 5. Divided.<BR>	 6. Abandoned.<BR>	 7. Joined.<BR>n. (-क्तं)<BR>	 1. A wood, a forest.<BR>	 2. A vacuity, a vacuum.<BR>	 f. (-क्ता) The<BR>fourth, ninth, or fourteenth days of the lunar fortnight.<BR> E. रिच्<BR>to void by stool, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तक|रिक्तकं
रिक्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Void, empty.<BR>	 2. Unladen, unburthened. E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तता
रिक्तता f. (-ता) Vacuity, void, space.<BR> E. रिक्त, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, रिक्तत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तभाण्ड
रिक्तभाण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Having no vessels or effects.<BR>	 n. (-ण्डं) An<BR>empty vessel.<BR> E. रिक्त, and भाण्ड vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्तहस्त
रिक्तहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Empty-handed.<BR> E. रिक्त, हस्त hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थ|रिक्थं
रिक्थ n. (-क्थं) Substance, property, wealth.<BR>	 2. Property left at death.<BR>3. Gold.<BR> E. रिच् to separate, Unādi aff. थक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थहारिन्
रिक्थहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Taking or inheriting property.<BR>	 m. (-री)<BR>1. An heir, one who succeeds to the property of the deceased, and<BR>gives the funeral cake.<BR>	 2. A maternal uncle.<BR>	 3. The seed of the<BR>Indian fig.<BR> E. रिक्थ wealth, and हारिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्थिन्
रिक्थिन् mfn. (-क्थी-क्थिनी-क्थि) Wealthy, possessing property.<BR>	 m. (-क्थी)<BR>A successor or an heir.<BR> E. रिक्थ wealth, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिक्षा
रिक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. A nit.<BR>	 2. A mole in a sun-beam. E. See लिक्षा, ल being changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिख्
रिख् r. 1st cl. (रिखति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिख्
रिख्(इ)रिखि r. 1st cl. (रिङ्खति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move slowly.<BR>	 2. To creep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिग्
रिग्(इ)रिगि r. 1st cl. (रिङ्गति)<BR>	 1. To go slowly.<BR>	 2. To crawl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्ख|रिङ्खः
रिङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>	 1. Disappointing, deceiving.<BR>	 2. A horse's hoof.<BR>	 3. One of<BR>a horse's paces.<BR>	 4. Dancing.<BR>	 5. Sliding.<BR> E. रिखि to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्खण|रिंखण|रिंखणं|रिङ्खणं
रिङ्खण n. (-णं) Slipping, sliding, stumbling, tumbling; or figuratively,<BR>deviating from rectitude or virtue.<BR> E. रिखि to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिङ्गण|रिंगण|रिंगणं|रिङ्गणं
रिङ्गण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Creeping, (as a child on all fours.)<BR>	 2. Tumbling, slip-<BR>ping, sliding.<BR>	 3. Deviating from rectitude, sliding from virtue. E.<BR>रिगि to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिच्
रिच् r. 1st and 10th cls. (रेचति-रेचयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To join, to unite.<BR>	 2. To divide,<BR>to scatter or separate.<BR>	 3. To purge. With आ, To cause to dance,<BR>to move, to contract. (औ, इर) औरिचिर r. 7th cl. (रिणक्ति-रिङ्क्ते) To<BR>purge, to evacuate fæces frequently. With अति prefixed, to exceed,<BR>to be more than enough. With वि, To purge. With उद्, To overflow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिज्
रिज् r. 1st cl. (रेजते) To fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिटि|रिटिः
रिटि f. (-टिः)<BR>	 1. The crackling or roaring of flame.<BR>	 2. A musical<BR>instrument.<BR>	 3. Black-salt.<BR>	 m. (-टिः) Name of an attendant of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपु|रिपुः
रिपु m. (-पुः) An enemy.<BR> E. रप् to speak, to abuse, aff. उन्, and इ substi-<BR>tuted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपुघातिन्
रिपुघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Killing a foe.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A shrub, (Abrus<BR>precatorius.)<BR> E. रिपु an enemy, घातिन् destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपुञ्जय|रिपुंजय
रिपुञ्जय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Victorious.<BR>	 m. (-यः) Name of a king.<BR> E. रिपु, जि<BR>to conquer, खच् aff., मुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिपुता
रिपुता f. (-ता) Hostility, enmity.<BR> E. रिपु and तल् aff.; also with त्व रिपुत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिप्र|रिप्रः
रिप्र mfn. (-प्रः-प्रा-प्रं) Vile, bad, wicked.<BR> E. री to hurt, Unādi aff. र, the<BR>vowel made short, and पुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिफ्
रिफ् r. 6th cl. (रिफति)<BR>	 1. To speak, to say or tell.<BR>	 2. To fight.<BR>	 3. To<BR>blame.<BR>	 4. To hurt or injure.<BR>	 5. To give.<BR>	 6. To praise, to flatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिम्फ्|रिंफ्
रिम्फ् r. 6th cl. (रिम्फति) To hurt, to injure, to kill; also read रिन्फ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिम्फ|रिंफ
रिम्फ n. (-म्फं) The zodiac.<BR> E. रिम्फ् to hurt, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरंसा
रिरंसा f. (-सा) Wish to sport.<BR> E. रम् to play, desid. v., अङ् and टाप affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरंसु
रिरंसु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Desirous to sport.<BR> E. रम् to sport, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिरी
रिरी f. (-री) Pale-brass, prince's metal, &c.<BR> E. री to go, क्रिन् aff., ङीप्<BR>added. “पित्तले ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिव्
रिव्(इ)रिवि r. 6th cl. (रिण्वति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिश्
रिश् r. 6th cl. (रिशति) To hurt, to injure, to kill or attempt to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिश्य|रिश्यः
रिश्य m. (-श्यः) A deer.<BR> E. रिश् to hurt, aff. क्यप्; also रिष्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्
रिष् r. 1st cl. (रेषति) r. 4th cl. (रिष्यति) To hurt, to kill, or attempt to<BR>kill. r. 6th cl. (रिष्णाति) To separate, to depart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिषि|रिषिः
रिषि m. (-षिः) A saint.<BR> E. रि substituted for ऋ; see ऋषि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्ट|रिष्टं|रिष्टः
रिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Hurt, injured.<BR>	 2. Unlucky.<BR>	 3. Lucky.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं)<BR>1. Happiness, prosperity.<BR>	 2. Good-luck, fortune.<BR>	 3. Bad-luck, ill-<BR>fortune.<BR>	 4. Destruction, loss, privation.<BR>	 5. Mischief, harm.<BR>	 6. Sin.<BR>m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. A sword.<BR>	 2. The soap-nut-tree.<BR>	 3. A demon, destroyed by<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR> E. रिष् to hurt or injure, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्टक|रिष्टकः
रिष्टक m. (-कः) The soap-berry plant, (Sapindus of several species.) E.<BR>रिष्ट the same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्टि|रिष्टिः
रिष्टि m. (-ष्टिः) A sword.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टिः) Prosperity, good fortune.<BR> E. रिष् to hurt, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्य|रिष्यः
रिष्य m. (-ष्यः) A deer.<BR> E. रिष् to hurt, to be hurt, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिष्व|रिष्वः
रिष्व mfn. (-ष्वः-ष्वा-ष्वं) Mischievous, injurious.<BR> E. रिष् to hurt, Unādi aff.<BR>वन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रिह्
रिह् r. 1st cl. (रेहति) To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

री
री r. 9th cl. (रिणाति)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure.<BR>	 2. To go, to move.<BR>	 3. To<BR>howl, as a wild beast. (ङ्) रीङ् r. 4th cl. (रीयते)<BR>	 1. To distil, to ooze,<BR>to drop.<BR>	 2. To fall, to alight. r. 2nd cl. (रेति) To bear or conceive,<BR>(as a child.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीज्या
रीज्या f. (-ज्या)<BR>	 1. Reproach, censure.<BR>	 2. Shame, modesty.<BR> E. ह्री to be ashamed, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीठा
रीठा f. (-ठा) The Soap-nut tree. “रीठाकरञ्जवृक्षे”ः see रिष्टक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीढक|रीढकः
रीढक m. (-कः) The back-bone.<BR> E. रिह् to hurt, aff. क्त, and the vowel made<BR>long, रीढ, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीढा
रीढा f. (-ढा) Disrespect, irreverence, disregard.<BR> E. रिह् to kill, &c., aff.<BR>क्त, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीण|रीणं
रीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Oozing, dripping, leaking, distilling.<BR> E. री to leak, to run out, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीति|रीतिः
रीति f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>	 1. Usage, custom, practice, local or traditionary ob-<BR>servance.<BR>	 2. Oozing, leaking, distilling.<BR>	 3. Brass, pale-brass, or<BR>prince's metal.<BR>	 4. Rust of iron.<BR>	 5. Calx of brass.<BR>	 6. Scoria of any<BR>metal, or the oxide formed on the surface of metals by their ex-<BR>posure to heat and air.<BR>	 7. Boundary, limit.<BR>	 8. Going, motion.<BR>	 9.<BR>Natural property or disposition.<BR>	 10. A stream, a river.<BR>	 11. Style,<BR>diction; they are:--वैदर्भी, गौडी, पाञ्चाली and लाटिका or मागधी ।<BR>E. री to go, to run out, &c. aff. क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीतिका
रीतिका f. (-का) Clax of brass.<BR> E. रीति brass, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीतिपुष्प|रीतिपुष्पं
रीतिपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) Calx of brass.<BR> E. रीति brass, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रीव्
रीव् r. 1st. cl. (रीवति-ते)<BR>	 1. To take.<BR>	 2. To screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रु|रुः
रु(टु,)टुरु r. 2nd cl. (रौति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To make a particular sort of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">Page606-a+ 60</a>]<BR>sound. (ङ्) रुङ् r. 1st. cl. (रवते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To hurt, to<BR>injure or kill.<BR>	 3. To speak.<BR>	 4. To be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रु|रुः
रु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Noise, sound.<BR>	 f. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. Fear, alarm.<BR>	 2.<BR>Cutting, dividing.<BR> E. रु to sound, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक|रुकः
रुक m. (-कः) A liberal man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्प्रतिक्रिया
रुक्प्रतिक्रिया f. (-या) The practice of physic, curing, remedying.<BR> E. रुक्<BR>from रुच् disease, प्रतिक्रिया resisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्म|रुक्मं|रुक्मः
रुक्म n. (-क्मं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Iron.<BR>	 f. (-क्मा) Bright.<BR> E. रुच् to shine, Unādi aff. मक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मकारक|रुक्मकारकः
रुक्मकारक m. (-कः) A gold-smith.<BR> E. रुक्म gold, and कारक a worker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मवत्|रुक्मवन्त्
रुक्मवत् mfn. (-वात्-वती-वत्) Golden.<BR>	 f. (-वती) A species of the Panktī<BR>metre.<BR> E. रुक्म, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिदर्प|रुक्मिदर्पः
रुक्मिदर्प m. (-र्पः) A name of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. रुक्मिन् a king, and दर्प pride;<BR>proud of overcoming him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिदारिन्
रुक्मिदारिन् m. (-री) BALARĀMA.<BR> E. रुक्मिन् a prince, and दारिन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिन्
रुक्मिन् m. (-क्मी) The name of a prince slain by BALARĀMA.<BR>	 f. (-क्मिणी)<BR>1. The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. A name of the daughter of king<BR>BHĪMAKA. She was betrothed to Sīśupāla, but she had enter-<BR>tained a passion for KṚṢṆA and sent to invite him to marry her<BR>off. KṚṢṆA made her his own by the Rākshasa ritual. PRA-<BR>DYUMNA was her son.<BR> E. रुक्म gold, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्मिभिद्
रुक्मिभिद् m. (-भित्) BALARĀMA.<BR> E. रुक्मि a prince, the elder brother of<BR>RUKMINĪ, and भिद् breaker, conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्सद्मन्
रुक्सद्मन् n. (-द्म) Excrement, fæces.<BR> E. रुज् disease, सद्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुक्ष|रुक्षः
रुक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Harsh, unkind.<BR>	 2. Rough, hard.<BR>	 3. Rough to the<BR>taste or feeling harsh.<BR>	 4. Rugged, uneven.<BR>	 5. Dry, arid.<BR> E. रुह् to<BR>grow, Unādi aff. क्स; it is more properly written रूक्ष, as derived from<BR>रूक्ष् to be rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुग्न|रुग्नः
रुग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Bent, crooked, curved.<BR>	 2. Broken.<BR>	 3. Impaired,<BR>injured.<BR>	 4. Diseased, sick, infirm.<BR> E. रुज् to be disordered, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुग्नता
रुग्नता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 2. Crookedness.<BR> E. रुग्न, and तल् aff.;<BR>also with त्व, रुग्नत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच्
रुच् r. 1st cl. (रोचते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To please, to be pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच्
रुच् f. (-रुक्)<BR>	 1. Light, lustre, splendour.<BR>	 2. Beauty, loveliness.<BR>	 3. Light-<BR>ning.<BR>	 4. Wish, desire.<BR>	 5. The chattering of the parrot or Mainā.<BR>6. The Rig-Veda.<BR> E. रुच् to shine, aff. क्विप्; also with टाप् added रुचा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचक|रुचकं|रुचकः
रुचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Agreeable, pleasing.<BR>	 2. Sharp, acrid.<BR>	 3. Tonic,<BR>stomachic.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR>	 2. A pigeon.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-कं)<BR>	 1. Salt.<BR>	 2. Natron, alkali.<BR>	 3. Borax.<BR>	 4. A garland, a chaplet.<BR>5. A curl on a horse's neck.<BR>	 6. The woody Cassia.<BR>	 7. Any auspicious<BR>or fortunate object.<BR>	 8. A perfume, commonly Rochanā.<BR>	 9. An<BR>anthelmintic medicine, commonly Biranga, (Embelia ribes.)<BR>	 10. A<BR>sort of temple.<BR>	 11. A stomachic.<BR>	 12. An ornament of the neck<BR>or breast.<BR>	 13. A tooth.<BR> E. रुच् to shine, &c., in the causal form,<BR>क्वुन् aff.; the embellisher, the polisher, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचि|रुचिः
रुचि f. (-चिः-ची)<BR>	 1. Light, lustre.<BR>	 2. Beauty, appearance, colour.<BR>	 3.<BR>Passion.<BR>	 4. Wish, desire.<BR>	 5. A ray of light.<BR>	 6. Intent application<BR>to any object or undertaking.<BR>	 7. Hunger, appetite.<BR>	 8. Taste, senti-<BR>ment.<BR> E. रुच् to shine, कि or ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिकर
रुचिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Beautifying.<BR>	 2. Sharpening, as the appetite,<BR>&c.<BR> E. रुचि, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचित|रुचितं
रुचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sweet.<BR>	 2. Sharpened, (as the appetite.)<BR>	 3. Diges-<BR>ted.<BR>	 4. Bright, brightened.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 5. A species of the Atijagatī<BR>metre.<BR> E. रुच् to please, Unādi aff. कितच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिर|रुचिरं
रुचिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, charming, pleasing.<BR>	 2. Sweet, dainty.<BR>3. Stomachic, restorative.<BR>	 4. Bright.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Saffron.<BR>	 2. Cloves.<BR>f. (-रा) A kind of yellow pigment.<BR> E. रुच् to please, Unādi aff. किरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिरमुद्
रुचिरमुद् mfn. (-द्) Affording great pleasure.<BR> E. रुचिर, मुद् what delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिरानन
रुचिरानन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Handsome, beautiful.<BR> E. रुचिर, and आनन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिरापाङ्गी
रुचिरापाङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A beautiful and charming woman.<BR> E. रुचिर, and अपाङ्ग<BR>corner of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुचिष्य|रुचिष्यं
रुचिष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Sweet.<BR>	 2. Stomachic.<BR> E. रुच् to be agreeable,<BR>Unādi aff. किष्यन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुच्य|रुच्यं|रुच्यः
रुच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>	 2. Stomachic, tonic.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-च्यः) A husband, a lover.<BR>	 n. (-च्यं) A digestive, a tonic.<BR> E. रुच् to<BR>please, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुज्
रुज्(औ, ओ)औरुजो r. 6th cl. (रुजति)<BR>	 1. To afflict, to disorder, to afflict<BR>with pain or disease.<BR>	 2. To bend or break. r. 10th cl. (रोजयति-ते)<BR>To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुज्
रुज् f. (-रुक्)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 2. Fracture.<BR>	 3. Effort.<BR> E. रुज् to be or<BR>make sick, aff. क्विप्; also with टाप् added रुजा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजत्
रुजत् mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>	 1. Breaking.<BR>	 2. Giving pain, making ill or<BR>sick.<BR>	 3. Being sick.<BR> E. रुज् to afflict, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजा
रुजा f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 2. Overthrow, destruction.<BR>	 3. Toil,<BR>fatigue.<BR>	 4. An ewe.<BR> E. रुज् to be or make sick, affs. क and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजाकर|रुजाकरं|रुजाकरः
रुजाकर mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं) Sickening, making sick or ill.<BR>	 m. (-रः) One<BR>of the Bhāvas or sentiments, the sickness induced by passion<BR>or love.<BR>	 n. (-रं) An acid fruit, (the fruit of the Averrhoa carambola.)<BR>“कामराङ्गा”.<BR> E. रुजा sickness, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजाप्रतिक्रिया
रुजाप्रतिक्रिया f. (-या) Practice of medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुजासद्मन्
रुजासद्मन् n. (-द्म) Excrement, feces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुट्
रुट् r. 1st cl. (रोटते)<BR>	 1. To resist or oppose.<BR>	 2. To strive again.<BR>	 3. To<BR>tumble or roll for passion. r. 10th cl. (रोटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be angry.<BR>	 2.<BR>To shine. (इ) रुटि r. 1st cl. (रुण्टति) To steal, to rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुठ्
रुठ् r. 1st cl. (रोठति) To strike, to fell, to knock down, to overturn.<BR>(रोठते) To resist, to oppose. (इ) रुठि r. 1st cl. (रुण्ठति)<BR>	 1. To go, to<BR>move.<BR>	 2. To steal.<BR>	 3. To be idle.<BR>	 4. To be lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुणस्वरा
रुणस्वरा f. (-रा) A cow easily milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्ड|रुंड|रुण्डः
रुण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A headless body, retaining life and mixing in combat.<BR>“कवन्धे”.<BR>	 2. A trunk.<BR> E. रुडि for रुटि or रुठि to take or steal, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुण्डिका|रुंडिका
रुण्डिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The threshold of a door.<BR>	 2. A field of battle.<BR>	 3. A<BR>female messenger or go-between.<BR>	 4. Superhuman power.<BR> E. रुण्ड as<BR>above, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुत|रुतं
रुत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The cry of birds, &c.<BR>	 2. The humming of bees.<BR>	 3. Any<BR>cry or noise.<BR> E. रु to sound, to make a particular sound, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुतज्ञ|रुतज्ञः
रुतज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) An augur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुतव्याज|रुतव्याजः
रुतव्याज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Mimicry.<BR>	 2. Simulated cry or sound.<BR> E. रुत and व्याज disguise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुतायत
रुतायत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rendered vocal by the cry of birds, &c.<BR> E. रुत<BR>cry, used as a verb, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्
रुद् (इर) रुदिर r. 2nd cl. (रोदिति)<BR>	 1. To weep.<BR>	 2. To call or address<BR>weeping. With उप and आङ्, To weep for another, to sympathize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्
रुद् f. (-रुत्)<BR>	 1. Grief.<BR>	 2. Pain, affliction.<BR>	 3. Disease.<BR>	 4. Sound, noise.<BR>	 5.<BR>Cry, wail, lamentation.<BR> E. रुद् to weep, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदत्
रुदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती or दती-दत्) Weeping, wailing.<BR> E. रुद् to weep, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदथ|रुदथः
रुदथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A dog.<BR>	 2. A pupil, a scholar.<BR> E. रुद् to weep, अथन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदन|रुदनं
रुदन n. (-नं) Weeping crying, lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुदित|रुदितं
रुदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Crying, weeping, wept, (by whom.)<BR>	 n. (-तं) Weep-<BR>ing.<BR> E. रुद to weep, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्ध|रुद्धं
रुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Surrounded, begirt, as with a fence or river,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Secured, protected from access.<BR>	 3. Obstructed, stopped,<BR>shut up.<BR>	 4. Opposed, impeded.<BR>	 5. Besieged, invested, blockaded.<BR>f. (-द्धा) A siege.<BR> E. रुध् to close, &c. aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्यमान
रुद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being weeping or wailing.<BR> E. रुद् to weep, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्र|रुद्रः
रुद्र m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. A name or form of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A demi-god, an inferior<BR>manifestation of ŚIVA, or according to one legend, a being, born<BR>from the forehead of BRAHMĀ: the RUDRAS are eleven in number,<BR>and are severally named, AJAIKAPADA, AHIVRADHNA, VIRŪPĀK-<BR>SHA, SUREŚHWARA, JAYANTA, BAHURŪPA, TRYAMBAKA, APARĀ-<BR>JITA, BAIBASWATA, SAVITRA and HARA.<BR>	 f. (-द्री) A sort of lute or<BR>guitar.<BR>	 f. (-द्राणी) A name of PĀRVATĪ, wife of RUDRA.<BR> E. रुद् to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">Page607-a+ 60</a>]<BR>weep, रक् Unādi aff., and the vowel unchanged; the name is given<BR>to ŚIVA, because according to his own declaration, he disperses the<BR>tears of mortals: to the demi-gods, because they wept at their<BR>birth. or because they made the enemies of the gods weep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रज|रुद्रजः
रुद्रज n. (-जं) Quicksilver.<BR> E. रुद्र ŚIVA, and ज born, being supposed to<BR>be the semen of the deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रपत्नी
रुद्रपत्नी f. (-त्नी)<BR>	 1. Linseed, (Linum.)<BR>	 2. The goddess DURGĀ.<BR> E. रुद्र ŚIVA, पत्नी wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रप्रिया
रुद्रप्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. रुद्र ŚIVA, &c., and प्रिया the beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रबलि
रुद्रबलि m. (-लिः) Oblations of meat, &c., presented to the RUDRAS. E.<BR>रुद्र a RUDRA, and बलि sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रभू
रुद्रभू f. (-भूः) A cemetery.<BR> E. रुद्र ŚIVA, and भू site or haunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रसू
रुद्रसू f. (-सूः) The mother of eleven children.<BR> E. रुद्र a RUDRA, of whom<BR>there are eleven, and सू mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्राक्रीड|रुद्राक्रीडः
रुद्राक्रीड m. (-डः) A cemetery, a place where dead bodies are burnt or<BR>buried.<BR> E. रुद्र ŚIVA, and आक्रीड place of sport; being supposed to<BR>dance and sport in such places at evening twilight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्राक्ष|रुद्राक्षं|रुद्राक्षः
रुद्राक्ष m. (-क्षः) A tree, (Eleocarpus ganitrus, Rox.)<BR>	 n. (-क्षं) The berry<BR>of the Eleocarpus, of which rosaries are usually made.<BR> E. रुद्र ŚIVA,<BR>and अक्ष from अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्राणी
रुद्राणी f. (-णी) The goddess DURGĀ, as the wife of RUDĀ or ŚIVA. E.<BR>रुद्र ŚIVA, ङीष् aff., आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रारि|रुद्रारिः
रुद्रारि m. (-रिः) KĀMA, the deity of love.<BR> E. रुद्र ŚIVA, and अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुद्रावास|रुद्रावासः
रुद्रावास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Benares.<BR>	 2. Mount Kailāsa.<BR>	 3. Cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुध्
रुध् r. 4th cl. (With अनु prefixed,) (अनुरुध्यते)<BR>	 1. To desire, to wish for,<BR>to love.<BR>	 2. To be kind to.<BR>	 3. To consent, to concur.<BR>	 4. To lament,<BR>or be sorry for. With अव, To implant, to infix. With उप, 1. To<BR>confine.<BR>	 2. To block up.<BR>	 3. To Molest. With नि, To stop. With वि,<BR>To quarrel with, to oppose. With सम, 1. To obstruct, to check.<BR>2. To fetter. (ञि, औ, इर्) ञिऔरुधिर् r. 7th cl. (रुणद्ध्वि रुन्धे)<BR>	 1. To<BR>impede, to oppose, to obstruct, to block or confine.<BR>	 2. To invest, to<BR>blockade, to besiege.<BR>	 3. To cover.<BR>	 4. To harass. With अभि<BR>and सम् prefixed, To prevent. With अव, To guard. With उप, To<BR>blockade. With प्रति or वि, To oppose. With सम् and नि, To<BR>shut up, to surround or blockade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुधिर|रुधिरं|रुधिरः
रुधिर m. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Blood.<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The planet MARS.<BR> E. रुध् to obstruct, किरच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुधिरपायिन्
रुधिरपायिन् m. (-यी) A Rākshasa, a demon.<BR> E. रुधिर, पायिन् who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुध्वा
रुध्वा Ind. Having stopped, checked, &c.<BR> E. रुध् to hinder, क्त्वाच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुन्धत्
रुन्धत् mfn. (-न्धन्-न्धन्ती-न्धत्)<BR>	 1. Hindering, opposing, stopping.<BR>	 2. Re-<BR>sisting, refusing.<BR> E. रुध् to hinder, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुप्
रुप् r. 4th cl. (रुप्यति) To confound, to perplex, to confuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुभेटि
रुभेटि f. (-टिः) Fog, vapour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुमा
रुमा f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. The wife of the monkey-chief SUGRĪVA.<BR>	 2. The dis-<BR>trict or more properly the salt mines of Sambhar, a town in Ajmere,<BR>twenty miles west of Jayanagar.<BR> E. रु to weep, मक् Unādi aff., with<BR>टाप् fem. aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुम्र|रुम्रः
रुम्र m. (-म्रः) ARUṆA, or the dawn.<BR> E. रम् to sport, Unādi aff. रक्, and रु<BR>substituted for the initial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरु|रुरुः
रुरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A sort of deer.<BR>	 2. A Daitya flayed by ŚIVA.<BR> E. रु to weep, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुत्सु
रुरुत्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु)<BR>	 1. Wishing to oppose or obstruct.<BR>	 2. Wishing<BR>to bind or tie up, (as the hair.)<BR> E. रुध् to oppose, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुरुदिषु
रुरुदिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing or purposing to wail or weep, ready<BR>to cry.<BR> E. रुद् to weep, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवत्
रुवत् mfn. (-वन्-वन्ती-वत्) Crying, calling, howling.<BR> E. रु to cry, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवथु
रुवथु m. (-थुः)<BR>	 1. Sound, noise.<BR>	 2. A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुवु|रुवुः
रुवु m. (-वुः) The castor-oil tree, (Ricinus communis.)<BR> E. रु, उकक् aff.; or<BR>रु to weep, कु aff., and the final vowel changed to उव; also with<BR>कन् added रुवुक and with the first or second vowel made long,<BR>रूवुक and रुवूक; also as differently derived, उरुवूक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुश्
रुश् r. 6th cl. (रुशति) To hurt or kill. (इ) रुशि r. 10th cl. (रुंशयति) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुशत्|रुशन्त्
रुशत् mfn. (-शन्-शती or शन्ती-शत्)<BR>	 1. Maledictory, imprecative.<BR>	 2. Cursing<BR>imprecating.<BR> E. रुश् to seek, to injure, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्
रुष् r. 1st cl. (रोषति) r. 4th cl. (रुष्यति-ते)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure, to kill or<BR>attempt to kill.<BR>	 2. To vex. (इर्) रुषिर् r. 4th and 10th cls. (रुष्यति-ते<BR>रोषयति-ते) To be angry to be passionate or wrathful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्
रुष् f. (-रुट्) Anger, wrath, passion.<BR> E. रुष् to be angry, aff. क्विप्; also<BR>with टाप् added, रुषा f. (-षा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुषित|रुषितः
रुषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Enraged, angry.<BR> E. रुष् to be angry, aff. क्त with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्ट|रुष्टः
रुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Angry, enraged.<BR> E. रुष् to be angry, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुष्टि|रुष्टिः
रुष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Wrath, rage, anger.<BR> E. रुष् to be angry, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह्
रुह् (ञि, औ) ञिऔरुह r. 1st cl. (रोहति)<BR>	 1. To grow from seed, to grow,<BR>as tree, &c.<BR>	 2. To be produced or become manifest.<BR>	 3. To be born<BR>With अधि prefixed. To go up or over, to ascend. With अधि, and<BR>आङ्, To ascend. With अव, To descend. With आङ्, 1. To mount,<BR>to ride on.<BR>	 2. To rise, to ascend. With प्र, To grow, to shoot forth<BR>as a branch or shoot taking fresh root. The senses of this root<BR>with or without a preposition are variously modified according<BR>to the noun, with which it is joined; but all of them express the<BR>notion of “motion upwards” either literal or metaphorical. Caus.<BR>(रोहयति-ते, रोपयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To elevate.<BR>	 2. To plant, to put in.<BR>	 3. To<BR>entrust. With आ, 1. To ascribe.<BR>	 2. To enter. With वि, To heal,<BR>(as a wound.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह|रुहः
रुह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Growing, springing up.<BR>	 2. Mounted, ascended.<BR> E. रुह् to grow, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुहक|रुहकं
रुहक n. (-कं) A hole, a vacuity, a cave, a chasm.<BR> E. रुह् to go or mount,<BR>(insects, &c.,) क्कुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुहा
रुहा f. (-हा) Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR> E. रुह् to grow, affs. क and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रुह्वन्
रुह्वन् m. (-ह्वा) A tree.<BR> E. रुक्ष् to grow, Unādi aff. क्वनिप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्ष्
रूक्ष् r. 10th cl. (रूक्षयति-त) To be harsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्ष|रूक्षं|रूक्षः
रूक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Harsh, rough, not smooth or soft.<BR>	 2. Rough to<BR>the taste, astringent, austere, not bland or sapid.<BR>	 3. Rugged,<BR>uneven.<BR>	 4. Harsh, unkind, unfriendly.<BR>	 5. Dry.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः) A tree in<BR>general.<BR> E. रूक्ष् to be harsh or rough, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्षण|रूक्षणं
रूक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The act of making dry or thin.<BR>	 2. Treatment for reducing fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूक्षता
रूक्षता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Roughness.<BR>	 2. Harshness.<BR> E. रूक्ष and तल् aff.; also<BR>with त्व, रूक्षत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढ|रूढं|रूढः
रूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. Famous, notorious.<BR>	 3. Certain,<BR>ascertained.<BR>	 4. Budded, blown.<BR>	 5. Much, exceeding.<BR>	 6. Increased,<BR>grown.<BR>	 7. Traditional, conventional or known, applied especially<BR>to words of foreign or unknown origin, but of which the employ-<BR>ment and application are familiar.<BR> E. रुह् to be born, &c., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढि|रूढिः
रूढि f. (-ढिः)<BR>	 1. Birth, production.<BR>	 2. Growing, growth.<BR>	 3. Fame, noto-<BR>riety.<BR>	 4. Traditional or customary meaning of words, as opposed to<BR>their etymological signification; it is especially applied to words of<BR>foreign or uncertain origin, and incapable of etymological analy-<BR>sis.<BR> E. रुह् to grow, &c., aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूढिशब्द|रूढिशब्दः
रूढिशब्द m. (-ब्दः) A word used in a peculiar but familiar sense.<BR> E. रूढि, and शब्द noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्
रूप् r. 10th cl. (रूपयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To form, to express form, to represent shape,<BR>either to the eye or the understanding.<BR>	 2. To represent in gesture,<BR>to act, to feign. With नि prefixed.<BR>	 1. To discuss, to investigate.<BR>2. To explain, to describe, to declare, to expound.<BR>	 3. To represent.<BR>4. To look out.<BR>	 5. To Consider.<BR>	 6. To appoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप|रूपं
रूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Like, resembling, (in composition, as पितृरूपः पुत्त्रः a<BR>son like his father.)<BR>	 n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. Natural property or disposition,<BR>nature.<BR>	 2. Beauty.<BR>	 3. Form, figure.<BR>	 4. Appearance, semblance.<BR>	 5.<BR>Cattle in general, flocks and herds, &c.<BR>	 6. A verse.<BR>	 7. Declension,<BR>conjugation, the inflection of nouns or verbs.<BR>	 8. A play, a drama-<BR>tic poem.<BR>	 9. Acquiring familiarity with any book or authority<BR>by frequent perusal, learning by heart or rote.<BR>	 10. An image, a fi-<BR>gure, a reflection or resemblance of any real object.<BR>	 11. Colour,<BR>form, any object of vision.<BR>	 12. (In arithmetic,) Discrete or distinct<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">Page608-a+ 60</a>]<BR>quantity, an entire number.<BR>	 13. Known quantity, whence the first<BR>syllable Rū is used in algebra to express the same.<BR> E. रूप् to ex-<BR>press form, aff. क; or रु to sound, Unādi aff. प, and the radical<BR>vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपक|रूपकं|रूपकः
रूपक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A drama, a dramatic poem.<BR>	 2. Shape, form, figure.<BR>3. A figure of rhetoric in general.<BR>	 4. A particular class of rhetorical<BR>or poetical figures, including various modes of poetical description,<BR>or the illustration and exhibition of visible things and persons.<BR>	 5.<BR>Identification of the objects of a comparison; their being not<BR>only like, but the very same.<BR>	 6. Symptom of disease.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A<BR>coin.<BR>	 f. (-पिका) Swallow wort.<BR> E. रूप form, figure, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपण|रूपणं
रूपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Metaphorical description.<BR>	 2. Investigation, proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपतत्त्व|रूपतत्त्वं
रूपतत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) Natural or inherent disposition or property, nature. E.<BR>रूप form, and तत्त्व truth, essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपधृत्
रूपधृत् mfn. (-धृत्) Having the form, resembling, like.<BR> E. रूप, and धृ to<BR>have, क्किप् aff., and तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपनाशन|रूपनाशनः
रूपनाशन m. (-नः) An owl.<BR> E. रूप् form, नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपभृत्
रूपभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Having form or beauty.<BR> E. रूप, भृ to possess, aff. क्विप्, तुक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपयत्
रूपयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Describing, representing.<BR> E. रूप् to form, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपलावण्य
रूपलावण्य n. (-ण्यं) Elegance, loveliness.<BR> E. रूप, and लावण्य beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपवत्|रूपवन्त्
रूपवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Having shape or colour, &c.<BR>	 2. Well-<BR>shaped, beautiful, handsome.<BR> E. रूप form, &c., and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपविपर्यय|रूपविपर्ययः
रूपविपर्यय m. (-यः) Morbid change of bodily form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपसम्पद्|रूपसंपद्
रूपसम्पद् f. (-त् or द्) Beauty.<BR> E. रूप, and सम्पद् fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपाजीवा
रूपाजीवा f. (-वा) A whore, a harlot.<BR> E. रूप beauty, आजीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपाधिबोध|रूपाधिबोधः
रूपाधिबोध m. (-धः) The perception, evidence, or influence of the<BR>senses, i. e. of colour, flavour, odour, contact and sound.<BR> E. रूप<BR>and अधिबोध perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपास्त्र|रूपास्त्रः
रूपास्त्र m. (-स्त्रः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. रूप beauty, and अस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूपिन्
रूपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, having a handsome form or shape.<BR>2. Having form or shape.<BR> E. रूप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्य|रूप्यं
रूप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 n. (-प्यं)<BR>	 1. Silver.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wrought silver.<BR>	 3. Wrought gold.<BR> E. रूप form, colour, &c., and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूप्याध्यक्ष|रूप्याध्यक्षः
रूप्याध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) The master of the mint, the superintendent of the<BR>silver, or silver coinage.<BR> E. रूप्य silver, अध्यक्ष superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूवुक|रूवुकः
रूवुक m. (-कः) The castor-oil tree, (Ricinus communis:) see रुवु; also<BR>रूवूक, and रुवुक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूष्
रूष् r. 1st cl. (रूषति)<BR>	 1. To decorate, to adorn.<BR>	 2. To smear, to cover<BR>with dust. r. 10th cl. (रूपयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To tremble.<BR>	 2. To burst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूषक|रूषकः
रूषक m. (-कः) A plant, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR> E. रूष् to adorn, aff. क्वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रूषित|रूषितं
रूषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pounded, reduced to dust or powder.<BR>	 2.<BR>Covered, spread over, coated, inlaid.<BR>	 3. Adorned, decorated.<BR>	 4.<BR>Made rough or rugged.<BR> E. रूष् to adorn, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रे
रे A vocative particle, but expressive of contempt or disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक्
रेक् (ऋ,) रेकृ r. 1st cl. (रेकते)<BR>	 1. To suspect or think probable.<BR>	 2. To<BR>excite or entertain doubt: in the last case with आङ् usually<BR>prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेक|रेकः
रेक mf. (-कः-का)<BR>	 1. Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>	 2. Fear, apprehension.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः)<BR>	 1. Looseness, purging.<BR>	 2. An outcaste, a low man.<BR>	 3. A frog.<BR>E. रेक् to suspect, to fear, aff. अच्, or रिच् to purge, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेकणस्
रेकणस् n. (-णः) Gold.<BR> E. रिच् to divide, Unādi aff. असुन्, नुट् augment,<BR>and च changed to क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेखा
रेखा f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A line, a continuous line.<BR>	 2. Deceit, fraud.<BR>	 3. A little.<BR>4. Fulness, satisfaction.<BR>	 5. A small portion, a jot.<BR>	 6. Drawing,<BR>delineating.<BR>	 7. The prime meridian drawn from Ceylon to Meru<BR>through Ujjayini. E. See लेखा, the initial being changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेखांश|रेखांशः
रेखांश m. (-शः) A degree of longitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेखागणित|रेखागणितः
रेखागणित n. (-तं) Geometry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेखान्तर
रेखान्तर n. (-रं) Distance east or west from the first meridian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचक|रेचकं|रेचकः
रेचक mfn. (-कः-चिका-कं)<BR>	 1. Purgative, aperient.<BR>	 2. Emptying the lungs,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">Page608-b+ 60</a>]<BR>emitting the breath.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cathartic, a purgative.<BR>	 2. Nitre,<BR>salt-petre.<BR>	 3. The purging-nut plant, (Croton tiglium.)<BR>	 4. Exhala-<BR>tion through one of the nostrils, (opposed to पूरक.)<BR>	 5. A syringe.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-कं) A purge.<BR> E. रिच् to evacuate by stool, causal form, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचन|रेचनं
रेचन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Purging, looseness.<BR>	 2. Emitting breath.<BR>	 3. Evacua-<BR>tion.<BR>	 f. (-ना-नी) A drug, commonly Śuṇḍārochanī.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>plant, Teorī, (Convolvulus turpethum,) the white sort.<BR>	 2. Another<BR>plant, commonly Dantī, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR> E. रिच् to purge,<BR>aff. ल्युट् or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेचित
रेचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Left void or empty, freed from, cleared.<BR>	 2.<BR>Purged.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A horse's gallop.<BR> E. रिच् to purge, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेज्
रेज् (ऋ,) रेजृ r. 1st. cl. (रेजते) To shine: this root is not universally admitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेज्
रेज् m. (रेट्) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. रेज् to shine, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेट्
रेट् (ऋ,) रेदृ r. 1st cl. (रेटति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणु|रेणुः
रेणु mf. (-णुः-णुः)<BR>	 1. Dust.<BR>	 2. The pollen of flowers.<BR>	 m. (-णुः) A medi-<BR>cinal plant, commonly Khet-Pāprā.<BR> E. रि to hurt, Unādi aff. नु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुका
रेणुका f. (-का) A sort of perfume and medicine, of a bitter and slightly<BR>pungent taste and greyish colour; it is procured in grains about<BR>the size of those of pepper.<BR>	 2. The wife of the saint JAMADAGNI<BR>and mother of PARAŚURĀMA; once she saw the Gandharba-king<BR>CHITTRARATHA sporting with his queen and felt envious of their<BR>felicity. Defiled by unworthy thoughts she returned disquieted to<BR>her home. JAMADAGNI seeing her fallen from sanctity, was enraged<BR>and ordered his sons to cut off her head; and one of them PARA-<BR>SŪRĀMA with explicit obedience to his father's command beheaded<BR>her; but her husband was so much pleased with the dutifulness<BR>of his son that he restored her to life at the request of his son<BR>PARASŪRĀMA.<BR>	 3. A sort of pulse, (Ervum or Cicer lens.)<BR> E. रेणु<BR>sand, dust, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुकासुत|रेणुकासुतः
रेणुकासुत m. (-तः) PARAŚURĀMA.<BR> E. रेणुका the mother of the hero, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुरूषित|रेणुरूषितः
रेणुरूषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dusty, covered over with dust.<BR>	 m. (-तः) An<BR>ass.<BR> E. रेणु dust, and रूषित made rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुवास|रेणुवासः
रेणुवास m. (-सः) A bee.<BR> E. रेणु dust, (the pollen of flower,) and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेणुसार|रेणुसारः
रेणुसार m. (-रः) Camphor.<BR> E. रेणु dust, and सार essence; also with कन्<BR>added रेणुसारक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतजा
रेतजा f. (-जा) Sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतन|रेतनं
रेतन n. (-नं) Semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेतस्
रेतस् n. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The seminal fluid.<BR>	 2. Quicksilver.<BR> E. री to ooze, Unādi aff. असुन्, तुट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेत्य|रेत्यं
रेत्य n. (-त्यं) Calx of brass.<BR> E. री to go, यत् aff., and तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेत्र|रेत्रं
रेत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Semen virile.<BR>	 2. Quicksilver.<BR>	 3. Nectar or ambrosia.<BR>	 4.<BR>Perfumed or aromatic powder, pulvilio.<BR> E. री to flow, ष्ट्रन् aff. तुट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेप्
रेप् (ऋ) रेपृ r. 1st cl. (रेपते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेप|रेपः
रेप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Low, vile, inferior, contemptible.<BR>	 2. Cruel, sav-<BR>age.<BR> E. रि to injure, प aff; or रेप, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेपस्
रेपस् mfn. (-पाः-पाः-पः)<BR>	 1. Low, vile, contemptible.<BR>	 2. Cruel, savage.<BR>	 3.<BR>Miserly, niggardly, a miser.<BR>	 4. Wicked, abandoned.<BR> E. रप् to speak,<BR>to revile, Unādi aff. असुन्, and ए substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेफ|रेफः
रेफ mfn. (-फः-फा-फ)<BR>	 1. Low, vile, contemptible, wicked.<BR>	 2. Defamed,<BR>reviled.<BR>	 m. (-फः)<BR>	 1. The letter “R”.<BR>	 2. Passion, affection of the mind.<BR>3. A grating sound.<BR> E. र the letter R, with inherent short vowel,<BR>and इफ aff.; or रिफ् to defame, to reproach, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेफस्
रेफस् mfn. (-फाः-फाः-फः)<BR>	 1. Low, vile, contemptible.<BR>	 2. Wicked, aban-<BR>doned.<BR>	 3. Miserly, a niggard.<BR>	 4. Cruel, savage.<BR> E. रिफ् to reproach,<BR>aff. असुन्ः also रेफ, रेपस्, and रेप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेब्
रेब्(ऋ)रेबृ r. 1st cl. (रेबते) To go, to move: see रेव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभ्
रेभ् (ऋ) रेभृ r. 1st cl. (रेभते) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेभण|रेभणं
रेभण n. (-णं) The lowing of kine.<BR> E. रेभ् to sound, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेरिहाण|रेरिहाणः
रेरिहाण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. An Asūra; an evil spirit.<BR>	 3. A chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेव्
रेव् (ऋ) रेवृ r. 1st. cl. (रेवते)<BR>	 1. To go by leaps or jumps, to leap, to<BR>jump.<BR>	 2. To go, to move.<BR>	 3. To flow as a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवट|रेवटं|रेवटः
रेवट n. (-टं) A conch shell with sinistral convolutions, or the spiral lines<BR>turning from the right to the left.<BR>	 m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. Oil of the Morunga<BR>tree.<BR>	 2. A plantain, the fruit.<BR>	 3. A hog.<BR>	 4. Dust.<BR>	 5. A whirl-wind.<BR>6. A conjuror, a juggler, a snake-dancer.<BR> E. रेव् to go, अटन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवत|रेवतः
रेवत m. (-तः) A prince, the father of the wife of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. रेव-अतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवती
रेवती f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The wife of BALARĀMA, the half-brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2.<BR>The last of the Nakshatras or lunar asterisms, containing thirty-<BR>two stars, figured by a tabor; one of the stars is the piscium.<BR>	 3.<BR>One of the MĀTRIS or energies of the gods.<BR>	 4. A cow.<BR> E. रेवत the<BR>name of a king, the father of BALARĀMA'S wife, and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवतीभव|रेवतीभवः
रेवतीभव m. (-वः) The planet SATURN.<BR> E. रेवती the nymph or asterism<BR>personified, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवतीरमण|रेवतीरमणः
रेवतीरमण m. (-णः) BALARĀMA.<BR> E. रेवती the wife of BALARĀMA, and रमण husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवतीश|रेवतीशः
रेवतीश m. (-शः) BALARĀMA.<BR> E. रेवती the wife of this demi-god, ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवन्त|रेवन्तः
रेवन्त m. (-न्तः) The fifth MANU of the present Kalpa; also called<BR>RAIVATA.<BR> E. रेव, झच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवन्तमनुसू
रेवन्तमनुसू f. (-सूः) SANJNYĀ, wife of the sun.<BR> E. रेवन्त, मनु the MANU, and सू mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेवा
रेवा f. (-बा)<BR>	 1. The Narbadda, or Narmadā river, which rises in the<BR>mountain Āmrakūṭa, or Amarkantak, in the province of Gond-<BR>wāna and runs nearly due west about 750 miles, when it falls into<BR>the sea below Baroach.<BR>	 2. RATĪ, the wife of KĀMA.<BR>	 3. The indigo-<BR>plant.<BR> E. रेव् to flow, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्
रेष् (ऋ) रेषृ r. 1st cl. (रेषते)<BR>	 1. To utter an inarticulate sound.<BR>	 2. To<BR>neigh.<BR>	 3. To howl.<BR>	 4. To roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्
रेष् mfn. (रेट्) Who or what neighs, howls, &c.<BR> E. रेष् to neigh, विच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेषण|रेषणं
रेषण n. (-णं) Howling, roaring.<BR> E. रेष् to sound inarticulately, aff. ल्युट्;<BR>also with अङ् and टाप् aff., रेषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेषित
रेषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounded, made as a noise.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Neighing,<BR>roaring.<BR> E. रेष् to sound, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रेष्टृ
रेष्टृ m. (-ष्टा) An injurer.<BR> E. रिष् to hurt, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रै
रै r. 1st cl. (रायति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रै
रै m. (-राः)<BR>	 1. Wealth property, substance.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR>	 3. Sound, noise.<BR> E. रा to give, aff. डै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैत्य
रैत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्यी-त्यं) Brazen, made of brass.<BR> E. रीति, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवत|रैवतः
रैवत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A mountain, the eastern part of the Vindhya range,<BR>or that part in which the Revā rises.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>3. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. A Daitya or demon.<BR>	 5. The fifth MANU of<BR>the present Kalpa.<BR> E. रेवा the Revā river, aff. अञ् and त added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रैवतक|रैवतकं|रैवतकः
रैवतक m. (-कः) The mountain Raivata.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding;<BR>also with ठक् added to रेवत, रैवतिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोक|रोकं|रोकः
रोक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A hole, a chasm, a vacuity.<BR>	 2. A boat.<BR>	 3. Moving,<BR>shaking.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Buying with ready money.<BR>	 2. Light.<BR> E. रुच् to<BR>shine, aff. घञ्; or रु-कन् तस्य-नेत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोग|रोगः
रोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease in general, or a disease.<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR> E. रुज् to be or make sick, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगग्रस्त
रोगग्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Sick, diseased.<BR> E. रोग, and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगघ्न|रोगघ्नं
रोगघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Curative, medical.<BR> E. रोग, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगभू
रोगभू f. (-भूः) The body.<BR> E. रोग disease and भू the soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगराज|रोगराजः
रोगराज m. (-जः) Consumption.<BR> E. रोग disease, and राज principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगलक्षण|रोगलक्षणं
रोगलक्षण n. (-ण) The symptoms or sign of a disease or of its progress.<BR>E. रोग a disease, and लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगशान्तक|रोगशान्तकः
रोगशान्तक m. (-कः) A physician.<BR> E. रोग disease, and शान्तक alleviator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगशान्ति|रोगशान्तिः
रोगशान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Cure or alleviation of disease.<BR> E. रोग, and शान्ति<BR>appeasing; also रोगशमः and the like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगशिला
रोगशिला f. (-ला) Red arsenic. “मनछाल्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगशिल्पिन्
रोगशिल्पिन् m. (-ल्पी) A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. रोग disease, and शिल्पिन् an artisan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगह|रोगहं
रोगह n. (-ह) A drug, a medicament.<BR> E. रोग, हा to abandon, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगहन्
रोगहन् m. (-हा) A physician.<BR> E. रोग, and हन् to destroy, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगहर
रोगहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Curative, medicinal.<BR> E. रोग, and हर what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगहारिन्
रोगहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Curative, medicinal.<BR>	 m. (-री) A physician.<BR>E. रोग disease, हृ to remove, to take away, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगान्तक|रोगान्तकः
रोगान्तक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Curative, medicinal.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A physician. E.<BR>रोग, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगान्वित
रोगान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sick, diseased.<BR> E. रोग, अन्वित having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगार्त्त|रोगार्त
रोगार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Suffering pain or sickness.<BR> E. रोग, आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगिता
रोगिता f. (-ता) Sickness, disease.<BR> E. रोगिन्, तल् aff.; also with त्व, रोगित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगिन्
रोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Diseased, ill, sick, affected with sickness or<BR>disease.<BR> E. रोग disease, and इनि aff.; or रुज-घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगिवल्लभ|रोगिवल्लभं
रोगिवल्लभ n. (-भं) A drug, a medicament.<BR> E. रोगि a sick man, वल्लभ the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोगोपशम|रोगोपशमः
रोगोपशम m. (-मः) Cure or alleviation of disease.<BR> E. रोग, उपशम allaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोग्य|रोग्यं
रोग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>	 1. Counter-indieated, regimen, &c., what is<BR>improper to be taken in any disease or with the medicines<BR>administered.<BR>	 2. Related to or connected with disease.<BR> E. रोग<BR>sickness, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचक|रोचकः
रोचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What pleases, brightens, strengthens, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः)<BR>	 1. Hunger, appetite.<BR>	 2. The plantain.<BR>	 3. A sort of onion.<BR>4. A stomachic, a carminative, any medicine, fruit or fossil, sup-<BR>posed to strengthen the tone of the stomach and restore lost<BR>appetite.<BR>	 5. A relish.<BR>	 6. A worker in glass or artificial ornaments.<BR>E. रुच् to shine, &c., and ण्वुल्, aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचन|रोचनः
रोचन mfn. (-नः-ना or -नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Splendid, beautiful.<BR>	 2. Irradiating,<BR>illumining, beautifying.<BR>	 3. Gratifying, pleasing.<BR>	 4. Whetting,<BR>sharpening, (the appetite.)<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A species of the silk-cotton<BR>tree.<BR>	 2. The onion.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Andersonia Rohitaka.)<BR>	 4. The Cassia<BR>fistula.<BR>	 5. The pomegranate.<BR>	 6. The citron.<BR>	 7. A stomachic, a<BR>carminative.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A yellow pigment, commonly Gorochanā<BR>and supposed to be the concrete bile of the cow; or according to<BR>some authorities, to be found in the head of the animal, used as a<BR>medicine, a dye and perfume.<BR>	 2. The manna of bamboos.<BR>	 3. An<BR>excellent woman.<BR>	 4. A red lotus.<BR>	 f. (-ना-नी)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly<BR>Guṇdārochanī, a sort of Crimum.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A variety of Teorī,<BR>(Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>	 2. Red arsenic.<BR>	 fn. (-ना-नं) The bright<BR>sky, the firmament.<BR> E. रुच् to shine, ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचनिका
रोचनिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Gūndārochanī.<BR>	 2. The manna<BR>of a bamboo.<BR> E. कन् added to रोचनी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचमान|रोचमानः
रोचमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Splendid, shining.<BR>	 2. Pleasing, gratifying.<BR>m. (-नः) A tuft or curl of hair round the neck of a horse or on the<BR>lower part of it.<BR> E. रुच् to shine, aff. शानच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचिष्णु|रोचिष्णुः
रोचिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Elegantly dressed or ornamented.<BR>	 2. Splen-<BR>did, brilliant.<BR>	 3. Giving an appetite.<BR> E. रुच् to shine, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोचिस्
रोचिस् n. (-चिः) Light, splendour, flame.<BR> E. रुच् to shine, इसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोची
रोची f. (-ची) A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.) “हिञ्चेशाक”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोच्य|रोच्यं
रोच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्य) To be illuminated, &c.<BR> E. रुच् to shine, aff. ण्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोड्
रोड् (ऋ) रोडृ r. 1st cl. (रोडति)<BR>	 1. To be mad.<BR>	 2. To disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदन|रोदनं
रोदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Weeping, crying.<BR>	 2. A tear, tears.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A plant,<BR>(Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR> E. रुद् to weep, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदस्
रोदस् n. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Heaven.<BR>	 2. Earth. Dual. (-सी) Heaven and earth.<BR> E. रुद्<BR>to weep, aff. असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोदसी
रोदसी f. (-सी)<BR>	 1. Heaven, paradise.<BR>	 2. Earth.<BR>	 f. Dual. (-स्यी) Heaven and<BR>earth.<BR> E. ङीप् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध|रोधः
रोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A bank, a shore.<BR>	 2. Confining, siege, &c.<BR> E. रुध् to obstruct, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधन|रोधनः
रोधन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Impeding, that which impedes or obstructs, an<BR>obstacle, a hinderer or hindrance.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The planet MERCURY.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Impeding, obstructing.<BR>	 2. Besieging, blockading.<BR> E. रुध्<BR>to obstruct, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधवक्रा
रोधवक्रा f. (-क्रा) A river.<BR> E. रोध a bank, and वक्र the course of a stream, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधवप्र
रोधवप्र m. (-प्रः) A rapid river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधस्
रोधस् n. (-धः) A bank, a shore, a dam.<BR> E. रुध् to obstruct, and असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोधोवक्रा
रोधोवक्रा f. (-क्रा) A river.<BR> E. रोधस् a bank, and वक्र winding course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध्र|रोध्रं|रोध्रः
रोध्र m. (-ध्रः) A tree, commonly Lodh.<BR>	 n. (-ध्रं)<BR>	 1. Offence, transgress-<BR>ion.<BR>	 2. Sin.<BR> E. रुध् to obstruct, and रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोध्रपुष्प|रोध्रपुष्पः
रोध्रपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A tree, (Bassia latifolia.) “मधूकवृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोप|रोपः
रोप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. Confusing, disturbing, (the ideas.)<BR>	 3. The<BR>act of raising or planting.<BR>	 n. (-पं) A hole, a vacuity, a chasm. E.<BR>रुप् to disturb, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपक|रोपकः
रोपक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what plants, raises, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A<BR>weight of metal or a coin, the seventieth part of a Suvarṇa.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>A healing application.<BR> E. रुह् to rise, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपण|रोपणं|रोपणः
रोपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Placing in or upon.<BR>	 2. Planting.<BR>	 3. Raising.<BR>	 4. A dis-<BR>turbing or bewildering of the mind, a confusing or confusion of<BR>ideas.<BR>	 5. Cicatrizing, healing.<BR>	 6. A healing application to sores or<BR>wounds.<BR>	 7. A kind of collyrium.<BR>	 m. (-णः) Quicksilver.<BR> E. रुह् to<BR>ascend, causal v., or रुप् to bewilder, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोपित
रोपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Placed in or upon.<BR>	 2. Planted.<BR>	 3. Raised,<BR>elevated.<BR>	 4. Bewildered, perplexed.<BR> E. रुह् to rise, causal v., or रुप्<BR>to bewilder, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोम|रोमं|रोमः
रोम n. (-मं) Water.<BR>	 m. (-मः) A hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमक|रोमकं|रोमकः
रोमक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The city of Rome.<BR>	 2. A Roman.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Loadstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमकर्णक|रोमकर्णकः
रोमकर्णक m. (-कः) A hare.<BR> E. रोम hair, and कर्ण the ear, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमकसिद्धान्त|रोमकसिद्धान्तः
रोमकसिद्धान्त m. (-न्तः) One of the five chief systems of Astronomy, the<BR>one of which was probably received from the Romans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमकूप|रोमकूपः
रोमकूप m. (-पः) A pore of the skin.<BR> E. रोम hair, and कूप a well, a pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमकेशर|रोमकेशरं
रोमकेशर n. (-रं) A Chowri.<BR> E. रोम hair of an animal, (especially of<BR>the Yak,) and केशर a filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमगुच्छ|रोमगुच्छः
रोमगुच्छ n. (-च्छं) A Chowri, a sort of whisk.<BR> E. रोम hair, (see the last<BR>word,) गुच्छ a cluster; also with कन् added, रोमगुच्छक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्
रोमन् n. (-म) The hair of the body.<BR> E. रु to make, Unādi aff. मनिन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमन्थ|रोमंथः|रोमन्थः
रोमन्थ n. (-न्थं)<BR>	 1. Ruminating, chewing the cud, or also eating, without<BR>chewing what has been once swallowed and again brought into<BR>the mouth.<BR>	 2. Frequent repetition.<BR> E. रोग disease, and मन्थ् to<BR>destroy or remove, aff. अच्, deriv. irr.; this habit in animals being<BR>indispensable to digestion and health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमपुलक|रोमपुलकः
रोमपुलक m. (-कः) Bristling of the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमबद्ध
रोमबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Made of or fastened with the hair of animals,<BR> E. रोम, बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमभूमि|रोमभूमिः
रोमभूमि f. (-मिः) The skin.<BR> E. रोम the hair, and भूमि soil, site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमरन्ध्र
रोमरन्ध्र n. (-न्ध्रं) A pore of the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमलता
रोमलता f. (-ता) A line of hair extending to the navel.<BR> E. रोम hair, लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमवत्|रोमवन्त्
रोमवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Hairy, woolly.<BR> E. रोम hair of the body, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमविकार|रोमविकारः
रोमविकार m. (-रः) Horripilation.<BR> E. रोम the hair, विकार change of state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमविक्रया
रोमविक्रया f. (-या) Horripilation.<BR> E. रोम the hair, and विक्रिया change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमविध्वंश
रोमविध्वंश m. (-शः) A body louse.<BR> E. रोम, and विध्वंश loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमश|रोमशः
रोमश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Hairy, woolly.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A ram, a sheep.<BR>	 2.<BR>A hog, a boar.<BR> E. रोमन् hair, and श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमहर्ष|रोमहर्षः
रोमहर्ष m. (-र्षः) Horripilation.<BR> E. रोम the hair of the body, and हर्ष pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमहर्षण|रोमहर्षणं|रोमहर्षणः
रोमहर्षण n. (-णं) Horripilation, erection or rigidity of the hair of the<BR>body, conceived to be occasioned by and to express exquisite<BR>delight.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. SŪTA, the pupil of VYĀSA, and supposed<BR>narrator of the events recorded in the Purāṇas.<BR>	 2. Beleric myro-<BR>balan.<BR> E. रोम the hair, and हर्षण delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमाञ्च|रोमांच|रोमाञ्चः
रोमाञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) Horripilation, rigidity and erection of the hair of the<BR>body.<BR> E. रोम the hair, अञ्च् to worship, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमाञ्चित|रोमांचित|रोमाञ्चितः
रोमाञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having the hair of the body erect, considered<BR>as a proof of exquisite pleasure; enraptured, delighted.<BR> E. रोमाञ्च<BR>horripilation, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमाली
रोमाली f. (-ली) A line of hair, extending across the navel.<BR> E. रोमन् hair, आली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमावलि|रोमावलिः
रोमावलि f. (-लिः-ली) A line of hair across the middle of the belly or<BR>navel.<BR> E. रोम and आवली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमोद्गम|रोमोद्गमः
रोमोद्गम m. (-मः) Horripilation.<BR> E. रोम hair, उद्गम rising; also रोमोद्ग m. (-द्गः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोमोद्भेद|रोमोद्भेदः
रोमोद्भेद m. (-दः) Horripilation.<BR> E. रोम hair of the body, and उद्भेद<BR>breaking forth, protrusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुदा
रोरुदा f. (-दा) Violent weeping.<BR> E. रुद् to weep, frequent. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुदावत्|रोरुदावन्त्
रोरुदावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Weeping or wailing violently.<BR> E. रोरुदा,<BR>and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोरुद्यमान
रोरुद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Crying bitterly.<BR> E. रुद् to weep, frequent. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोल|रोलः
रोल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>	 2. Moist ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोलम्ब|रोलंबः|रोलम्बः
रोलम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं) Distrustful, unbelieving.<BR>	 m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. A bee,<BR>2. Dry or arid soil.<BR> E. रोड् to be mad, अम्बच् aff., ड changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोशंसा
रोशंसा f. (-सा) Wish, desire; (this word is used in Prākrita.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोष|रोषः
रोष m. (-षः) Anger, wrath.<BR> E. रुष् to be angry, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोषण|रोषणः
रोषण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Angry, passionate.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Quicksilver.<BR>	 2. A<BR>touchstone.<BR>	 3. Arid or desert soil.<BR> E. रुष् to be angry, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोषवाहण
रोषवाहण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Angry, feeling and displaying wrath. E.<BR>रोष, and वह् to bear, causal v., युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोष्टृ
रोष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Violent, wrathful, angry.<BR> E. रुष् to be angry, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोह|रोहः
रोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A bud, a blossom.<BR>	 2. Mounting, ascending.<BR>	 3. The<BR>rising of a number from a smaller to a higher denomination.<BR>	 4.<BR>Growth.<BR> E. रुह् to grow, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहक|रोहकः
रोहक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A rider, riding, mounted, one who rides on<BR>any animal or is carried in any vehicle.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sort of gob-<BR>lin.<BR>	 2. Rising, growing, mounting.<BR> E. रुह् to rise, aff. वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहग
रोहग m. (-गः) The name of a mountain, known by Adam's peak in<BR>Ceylon.<BR> E. रोह rising, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहण|रोहणं|रोहणः
रोहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Semen virile.<BR>	 2. Rising in or on, mounting, ascending.<BR>3. Growing, as a plant.<BR>	 4. Healing of a wound.<BR>	 5. A particular<BR>mountain: see the last.<BR> E. रुह् to grow, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहणद्रुम|रोहणद्रुमः
रोहणद्रुम m. (-मः) The sandal-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहन्त|रोहंतः|रोहन्तः
रोहन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A kind of tree.<BR>	 2. Any tree.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती) A sort of creeper.<BR>E. रुह to grow, Unādi aff. झच्, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहि|रोहिः
रोहि m. (-हिः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. A seed.<BR>	 3. A pious or religious man, one<BR>observing a vow, &c.<BR>	 4. A kind of deer. “वनरोह इति भाषा ।”<BR> E. रुह्<BR>to grow, Unādi aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिण|रोहिणं|रोहिणः
रोहिण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The Indian-fig tree.<BR>	 2. A fragrant grass.<BR>	 n. (-णं) A<BR>part of the fore-noon, extending to mid-day, in which Shrāddhas<BR>are especially to be observed.<BR> E. रुह् to grow, Unādi aff. इनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणिका
रोहिणिका f. (-का) A woman red with anger, &c., or with red pigments.<BR>E. रोहिणी fem. form of रोहित red, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणीपति|रोहिणीपतिः
रोहिणीपति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. रोहिणी the nymph, (see रोहिन्,) पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणीवल्लभ|रोहिणीवल्लभः
रोहिणीवल्लभ m. (-भः) The moon.<BR> E. रोहिणी the nymph, वल्लभ the lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिणीश|रोहिणीशः
रोहिणीश m. (-शः) The moon.<BR> E. रोहिणी the nymph, ईश lord or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहित्
रोहित् m. (-हित्) The sun.<BR>	 f. (-हित्)<BR>	 1. A deer, a doe.<BR>	 2. A sort of cree-<BR>per.<BR> E. रुह् to go or grow, Unādi aff. इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहित|रोहितं|रोहितः
रोहित mfn. (-रोहितः रोहिता or रोहिणी रोहितं) Red, of a red colour.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>1. Red, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. The Rohi-fish, (Cyprinus Rohita, HAM.)<BR>3. A kind of deer.<BR>	 4. A tree, (Andersonia Rohitaka, Rox.)<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>1. INDRA'S bow unbent and invisible to mortals.<BR>	 2. Safflower,<BR>(Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>	 3. Blood.<BR> E. रुह् to grow or go, Unādi aff.<BR>इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितक|रोहितकः
रोहितक m. (-कः) A tree, (Andersonia Rohitaka, Rox.)<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितश्व
रोहितश्व m. (-श्वः)<BR>	 1. A name of Agni.<BR>	 2. The son of HARIŚCHANDRA. E.<BR>रोहित् a deer, or red, and अश्व a horse; also from रोहित sometimes<BR>read रोहिताश्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितिका
रोहितिका f. (-का) A woman whose face is stained with red pigments,<BR>or who is red with rage, &c.<BR> E. रोहित red, fem. form, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहितेय|रोहितेयः
रोहितेय m. (-यः) A tree, (Andersonia Rohitaka.) “रोहितक वृक्षे”.<BR> E. रोहित<BR>the same. ढक् pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिन्
रोहिन् m. (-ही)<BR>	 1. The Indian-fig tree.<BR>	 2. The holy-fig tree.<BR>	 3. The<BR>Andersonia Rohitaka.<BR>	 f. (-हिणिः-हिणी)<BR>	 1. The fourth lunar asterism,<BR>figured by a wheeled carriage, and containing five stars, probably;<BR>in mythology, the asterism is personified as one of the daughters<BR>of Daksha, and wives of the moon.<BR>	 2. The mother of BALARĀMA.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णी)<BR>	 1. One of the VIDYĀDEVIS of the Jainas.<BR>	 2. A cow.<BR>	 3. Inflam-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">Page611-a+ 56</a>]<BR>matory affection of the throat.<BR>	 4. Lightning.<BR>	 5. The name of a<BR>medicinal plant.<BR>	 6. The moon-plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>	 7.<BR>A woman stained with red pigments, or red with passion, &c.<BR>	 8.<BR>Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>	 9. Bengal madder.<BR>	 10.<BR>A girl nine years old.<BR> E. रुह् to grow, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रोहिष|रोहिषः
रोहिष n. (-षं) A sort of grass.<BR>	 m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The Rohi, a kind of fish.<BR>	 2.<BR>A deer said to resemble an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौक्ष्य|रौक्ष्यं
रौक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Roughness, ruggedness.<BR>	 2. Harshness, unkindness.<BR> E. रुक्ष hard, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौचनिक
रौचनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Dyed or coloured with Rochanā of a yellow-<BR>ish or orange tint.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The tartar of the teeth.<BR> E. रोचना a pig-<BR>ment, and अण् or ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौच्य|रौच्यः
रौच्य m. (-च्यः)<BR>	 1. An ascetic with a staff of Bilwa-wood.<BR>	 2. The thirteenth Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौट्
रौट्(ऋ)रौटृ, r. 1st cl. (रौटति) To treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौड्
रौड्(ऋ)रौडृ r. 1st cl. (रौडति) To treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्र|रौद्रं|रौद्रः
रौद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा or द्री-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Formidable, fearful, terrific 2. Sharp, acute.<BR>3. Relating or belonging to RŪDRA or ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. Violent, wrathful,<BR>irascible.<BR>	 mn. (-द्रः-द्रं) Wrath rage, (the sentiment as an object of<BR>poetical description.)<BR>	 n. (-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Heat, warmth.<BR>	 2. Wrath.<BR>	 3.<BR>YAMA.<BR>	 f. (-द्री) GAURI, the wife of ŚIVA.<BR> E. रुद्र ŚIVA, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्रता
रौद्रता f. (-ता) Fierceness, formidableness.<BR> E. रौद्र, तल् aff.; with त्व, रौद्रत्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौद्रदर्शन
रौद्रदर्शन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Formidable, terrific.<BR> E. रौद्र, दर्शन appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौप्य|रौप्यं
रौप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्यी-प्यं) Silver, of silver.<BR>	 n. (-प्यं) Silver.<BR> E. रूप्य the same,<BR>अण् pleonasm or aff. of relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौम|रौमं
रौम n. (-मं) A sort of salt; see the next.<BR> E. रुम the place where it is found, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौमक|रौमकं
रौमक n. (-कं) A kind of salt, according to some authorities, brought<BR>from a mountain in AJMERE, but in fact produced from a salt lake<BR>near the town of SĀMBHAR, about twenty miles west of JAYANA-<BR>GAR.<BR> E. रुम the district of RUMA or SĀMBHAR, aff. अण्, and कन्<BR>added; also रौम and रौमलवण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौमलवण|रौमलवणं
रौमलवण n. (-णं) Sāmbher-salt; see the last.<BR> E. रौम as above, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौरव|रौरवः
रौरव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Formidable, horrible, terrific.<BR>	 2. Dishonest,<BR>fraudulent.<BR>	 3. Unsteady, slipping.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. One of the divisions<BR>of Naraka or Tartarus.<BR>	 2. A savage, a monster.<BR> E. रुद् to weep,<BR>deriv. irr.; or रुरु said to mean a living being, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिण|रौहिणं|रौहिणः
रौहिण m. (-णः) Sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिणेय|रौहिणेयं|रौहिणेयः
रौहिणेय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>	 2. The planet MERCURY.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-यं) An emerald.<BR>	 mf. (-यः-यी)<BR>	 1. A calf.<BR>	 2. The planet SATURN. E.<BR>रोहिणी the nymph, &c., ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रौहिष|रौहिषं|रौहिषः
रौहिष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A sort of deer.<BR>	 2. The Rohi-fish.<BR>	 n. (-षं) A kind of<BR>grass.<BR> E. रुह् to grow, Unādi aff., ठिषच्, the vowel changed to औ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल|लं|लः
ल The twenty-eighth consonant of the Nāgari alphabet, the letter L.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल|लं|लः
ल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. Cutting.<BR>	 3. A short syllable, (in prosody.)<BR>4. PĀṆINI'S technical term for all the tenses and modes, (in gram.)<BR>f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Giving.<BR>	 2. Receiving, taking.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Embracing,<BR>adhering or clinging to.<BR>	 2. Liquifying, melting.<BR> E. ला to give or<BR>take, &c., aff. क or ड, fem. aff. टाप् or ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्
लक् r. 10th cl. (लाकयति ते)<BR>	 1. To taste.<BR>	 2. To obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक|लकः
लक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The forehead.<BR>	 2. The ear or spike of wild-rice.<BR> E. लक्<BR>to taste, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लकच|लकचः
लकच m. (-चः) A tree; see the next.<BR> E. लक् बा० अचन् । “डहुवृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लकुच|लकुचः
लकुच m. (-चः) A species of the bread-fruit tree, (Artocarpus Lacucha,<BR>Rox.)<BR> E. लक् to taste, उचन् aff.; also अ substituted for उ, लकच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लकुट|लकुटः
लकुट m. (-टः) A club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्तक|लक्तकः
लक्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Old and tattered cloth, a rag or rags.<BR>	 2. Lac, the dye.<BR>“आल्ता” ।<BR> E. लक् to obtain, aff. क्त, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्तकर्म्मन्|लक्तकर्मन्
लक्तकर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा) A tree used in dyeing, a red variety of the Lodh-<BR>tree.<BR> E. लक्त for रक्त coloured and कर्म्मन् office, act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्तिका
लक्तिका f. (-का) A lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्
लक्ष् r. 1st cl. (लक्षते) To perceive, to see. r. 10th cl. (लक्षयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>see, to look at, to notice or inspect.<BR>	 2. To mark, to mark<BR>any mark on.<BR>	 3. To define, to discriminate. With उप prefixed,<BR>To remark. With सम्, To know, to understand. With वि, 1. To ob-<BR>serve.<BR>	 2. To become confused.<BR>	 3. To distinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष|लक्षं
लक्ष nf. (-क्ष-क्षा) A Lac, one hundred thousand.<BR>	 n. (-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Fraud, dis-<BR>guise.<BR>	 2. A mark or butt.<BR> E. लक्ष् to mark, or see, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षक|लक्षकं
लक्षक f. (-का) Expressing secondarily, indicating indirectly.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>One hundred thousand.<BR> E. लक्ष, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षण|लक्षणं|लक्षणः
लक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A mark, a spot.<BR>	 2. A name, an appellation.<BR>	 3. Sight,<BR>seeing.<BR>	 4. An indication, a predicate, any thing by which an<BR>object is designated or distinguished.<BR>	 5. A symptom or any indi-<BR>cation of actual disease.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The younger brother of RĀMA.<BR>2. The Indian crane.<BR>	 f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. The female of the Indian crane.<BR>	 2.<BR>A goose.<BR>	 3. An ellipsis, a word, &c. understood, though not insert-<BR>ed.<BR>	 4. The force or application of a word or phrase.<BR> E. लक्ष् to see,<BR>to mark, aff. ल्युट्; or लक्ष् as before, Unādi aff. न and अट् augment;<BR>also with मुट् augment, लक्ष्मण, which in the masc. and fem. forms<BR>is the more usual reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षण्य|लक्षण्यः
लक्षण्य f. (-ण्या)<BR>	 1. Defined.<BR>	 2. Marked.<BR>	 3. Aimed at.<BR>	 4. Indicated.<BR>	 5. Seen.<BR>	 6. Examined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्षित|लक्षितः
लक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seen.<BR>	 2. Marked.<BR> E. लक्ष् to mark, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मण|लक्ष्मणं|लक्ष्मणः
लक्ष्मण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Prosperous fortunate.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The son of<BR>DAŚARATHA by SUMITRĀ, the half-brother and faithful compani-<BR>on of RĀMACHANDRA.<BR>	 2. The Sāras or Indian crane.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>mark, a spot or sign.<BR>	 2. A name, an appellation.<BR>	 f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. The<BR>female of the Sāras.<BR>	 2. A kind of drug.<BR> E. लक्ष् to mark or see,<BR>Unādi aff. न, and मुट् augment. also with अट् augment, लक्षण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मणप्रसू
लक्ष्मणप्रसू f. (-सूः) SUMITRĀ, one of DAŚARAT'HA'S four wives, the mother<BR>of LAKSHMAṆA.<BR> E. लक्ष्मण, प्रसू the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मन्
लक्ष्मन् n. (-क्ष्म)<BR>	 1. A mark, a spot, &c.<BR>	 2. Chief, principal.<BR>	 3. Definition.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The Sārasa bird.<BR>	 2. LAKSHMANA, the son of DAŚA-<BR>RATHA.<BR> E. लक्ष् to mark, &c., मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मी
लक्ष्मी f. (-क्ष्मी)<BR>	 1. LAKṢMĪ, one of the three principal female deities of<BR>the Hindus, the wife of VIṢṆU, and goddess of wealth and pros-<BR>perity.<BR>	 2. Fortune, success, prosperity.<BR>	 3. SĪTĀ, the wife of RĀMA.<BR>4. Beauty, splendour.<BR>	 5. The name of a medicinal root, common-<BR>ly Briddhi.<BR>	 6. Another root, termed Riddhi.<BR>	 7. A plant: see<BR>प्रियङ्गु.<BR>	 8. The wife of a hero.<BR>	 9. Turmeric.<BR>	 10. A pearl.<BR>	 11. Royal<BR>power.<BR> E. लक्ष् to see, &c., Unādi aff. ई, and मुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीगृह|लक्ष्मीगृहं
लक्ष्मीगृह n. (-हं) The red lotus.<BR> E. लक्ष्मी the goddess, and गृह abode,<BR>appearing at the creation, floating over the water on the expand-<BR>ed petals of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीपति|लक्ष्मीपतिः
लक्ष्मीपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A king, a sovereign prince.<BR>	 3. The<BR>clove-tree. “लवङ्गवृक्षे”.<BR>	 4. The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel.)<BR> E. लक्ष्मी<BR>the goddess of prosperity and पति master, husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीपुत्त्र
लक्ष्मीपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. KĀMADEVA, the god of love.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR>	 3. Either<BR>of the sons of RAMA and SĪTĀ.<BR> E. लक्ष्मी the goddess, or SĪTĀ,<BR>(she being LAKṢMĪ incarnate,) and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीपुष्प|लक्ष्मीपुष्पः
लक्ष्मीपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) Ruby.<BR> E. लक्ष्मी the goddess of fortune, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीफल|लक्ष्मीफलः
लक्ष्मीफल m. (-लः) A fruit tree, (Ægle marmelos.) “विल्ववृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीमत्
लक्ष्मीमत् m. (-मान्) The bread-fruit tree, (Artocarpus integrifolia.) E.<BR>लक्ष्मी prosperity, मतुप् aff., and the म unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीवत्|लक्ष्मीवन्त्
लक्ष्मीवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Prosperous, fortunate, wealthy, thriving.<BR>2. Beautiful.<BR>	 m. (-वान्) Jack-fruit tree.<BR> E. लक्ष्मी prosperity, मतुप्<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीश|लक्ष्मीशः
लक्ष्मीश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. The mango-tree.<BR>	 3. A prosperous man. E.<BR>लक्ष्मी the goddess of fortune, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्मीसहज|लक्ष्मीसहजः
लक्ष्मीसहज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR>	 3. Uccaishrabā, the<BR>horse of Indra.<BR> E. लक्ष्मी the goddess, सह with, ज born; rising as<BR>well as LAKṢMĪ from the ocean, at the time it was churned by<BR>the Gods and Asuras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्य|लक्ष्यं|लक्ष्यः
लक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. To be seen or noted.<BR>	 2. To be defined or<BR>described.<BR>	 3. To have attributes or predicates attached.<BR>	 n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1.<BR>A mark, a butt.<BR>	 2. A mark, a sign.<BR>	 3. Fraud, disguise.<BR>	 4. A Lac,<BR>a hundred thousand.<BR>	 5. A secondary meaning.<BR>	 6. The thing de-<BR>fined.<BR> E. लक्ष् to see, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्यक्रम
लक्ष्यक्रम Adj. Having the order perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्यभेद|लक्ष्यभेदः
लक्ष्यभेद m. (-दः) The cleaving of a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लक्ष्यसुप्त
लक्ष्यसुप्त Adj. Pretending to be asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लख्
लख् r. 1st cl. (लखति) (इ) लखि (लङ्खति) To go, to move, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्
लग् (ए) लगे r. 1st cl. (लङ्गति) To be with or near, to touch, to be in<BR>contact or union with. With वि and अव, To adhere to. (इ) लगि r.<BR>1st cl. (लङ्गति)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To go limpingly, to be lame.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लगयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To taste.<BR>	 2. To obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगड|लगडं
लगड mfn. (-डः-डा-डं) Beautiful, handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगित|लगितं
लगित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Obtained, gained.<BR>	 2. Connected with, attached<BR>to.<BR> E. लग् to be in contact with, aff. क्त, and इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगुड|लगुडः
लगुड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A staff, a stick.<BR>	 2. An iron club, or one bound with<BR>iron.<BR> E. लग् to go, aff. डुलच्, ल changed to ड; also लगुर and लगुल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगुर|लगुरः
लगुर m. (-रः) A club, a stick. E. See the last; ड changed to ल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लगुरहस्त
लगुरहस्त m. (-स्तः) A man armed with a stick, a mace or staff-bearer. E.<BR>लगुर, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्न|लग्नं|लग्नः
लग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Attached to, intent on.<BR>	 2. Ashamed.<BR>	 3. Joined<BR>to, connected with.<BR>	 n. (-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. The rising of a sign, its appearance<BR>above the horizon; the oblique ascension, or the divisions of the<BR>equator, which rise in succession with each sign in an oblique<BR>sphere; also defined as the arc of the equator, which passes the<BR>meridian in the same time with each sign of the ecliptic; in<BR>popular acceptation it is the moment of the sun's entrance into a<BR>zodiacal sign.<BR>	 2. An auspicious moment, the time for action.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ग्नः)<BR>	 1. A bard, a panegyrist.<BR>	 2. An elephant in rut.<BR> E. लग् to be<BR>with or near, or लस्ज् to be ashamed, aff. क्त, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्नक|लग्नकः
लग्नक m. (-कः) A security, a surety.<BR> E. लग्न engaged or associated, (in<BR>the business,) aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्नकाल|लग्नकालः
लग्नकाल m. (-लः) The time fixed upon by astrologers as favourable for any undertaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्नभुज|लग्नभुजः
लग्नभुज m. (-जः) Ascensional difference.<BR> E. लग्न and भुज arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लग्निका
लग्निका f. (-का) A girl ten years old, one before menstruation.<BR> E. लस्ज्<BR>to be ashamed, aff. कन्, fem. form; also नग्निका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघ्
लघ् r. 10th cl. (लाघयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To taste.<BR>	 2. To obtain. (इ) लघि r. 1st cl.<BR>(लङ्घते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To go beyond the limit.<BR>	 3. To fast,<BR>to abstain from food. (लङ्घति)<BR>	 1. To dry, to dry up.<BR>	 2. To dimi-<BR>nish, to lessen.<BR>	 3. To sorrow. r. 10th cl. (लङ्घयति-ते) To speak. With<BR>उत् or वि prefixed, To go beyond or over, to cross, to pass, to leap<BR>or spring over; also morally, to exceed, to transgress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघट्
लघट् m. (-ट्) Air, wind.<BR> E. लघि to go, अटि Unādi aff., nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघटि|लघटिः
लघटि m. (-टिः) Air, wind.<BR> E. लघि to go, Unādi aff. हटिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघिमन्
लघिमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Lightness, absence of weight.<BR>	 2. The power of<BR>assuming excessive lightness at will, considered as one of the<BR>eight supernatural faculties.<BR>	 3. Diminutiveness.<BR>	 4. Insignifi-<BR>cance.<BR> E. लघु light, aff. इमनिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघिष्ट
लघिष्ट mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Lightest, very light.<BR>	 2. Very small, least. E.<BR>लघ light, इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघीयस्
लघीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Lightest, most or very light.<BR> E. लघु light,<BR>and ईयसुन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघु|लघुः
लघु mfn. (-घुः-घुः or घ्वी-घु)<BR>	 1. Light, not heavy.<BR>	 2. Swift, quick.<BR>	 3. Sapless,<BR>pithless.<BR>	 4. Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>	 5. Small, little.<BR>	 6. Light, vain,<BR>frivolous.<BR>	 7. Insignificant, mean, low.<BR>	 8. Weak, feeble.<BR>	 9. Clean,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">Page612-b+ 60</a>]<BR>pure.<BR>	 10. Short, (as a vowel.)<BR>	 11. Easy.<BR>	 12. Soft.<BR>	 13. Young.<BR>14. Pure.<BR>	 15. Brief.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-घु) Quickly, swiftly. Subst. (-घु)<BR>1. A black kind of Aloe-wood or Agallochum.<BR>	 2. The root of<BR>the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>	 f. (-घुः) A plant, (Trigonella corni-<BR>culata.)<BR>	 f. (-घ्वी)<BR>	 1. A slight or delicate woman.<BR>	 2. A small light<BR>carriage.<BR> E. लघि to go, Unādi aff. कु, and the nasal not inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुकाय|लघुकायः
लघुकाय m. (-यः) A goat.<BR> E. लघु small, and काय a body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुखट्विका
लघुखट्विका f. (-का) A small bedstead.<BR> E. लघु small, खट्विका a bedstead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुगर्ग|लघुगर्गः
लघुगर्ग m. (-र्गः) A kind of fish, probably a variety of the Pimelodus.<BR>E. लघु small, and गर्ग for गर्गर a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुचेतस्
लघुचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः) Low-minded, frivolous.<BR> E. लघु and चेतस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुजङ्गल|लघुजंगल|लघुजङ्गलः
लघुजङ्गल m. (-लः) A sort of quail.<BR> E. लघु light, जङ्गल flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुता
लघुता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Lightness.<BR>	 2. Meanness, insignificance.<BR> E. तल् added to<BR>लघु; also with त्व, लघुत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुदुन्दुभि|लघुदुन्दुभिः
लघुदुन्दुभि m. (-भिः) A small kettle-drum.<BR> E. लघु light, small, and दुन्दुभि a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुपत्रक|लघुपत्रकः
लघुपत्रक m. (-कः) A plant, commonly Guṇdārochani, (Crinum.) E.<BR>लघु light, small, and पत्रक a leaf. “कमलागुडि ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुप्रयत्न
लघुप्रयत्न mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं) Indolent, impotent.<BR> E. लघु and प्रयत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुमांस|लघुमांसः
लघुमांस m. (-सः) The Francoline partridge.<BR> E. लघु light, (of digestion,)<BR>and मांस flesh. “तितिरपाखी ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुमित्त्र
लघुमित्त्र n. (-त्त्रं) A friend or ally of little power or value.<BR> E. लघु and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुमूल
लघुमूल n. (-लं) In algebra, the least root with reference to the additive<BR>quantities.<BR> E. लघु, मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुलय|लघुलयं
लघुलय n. (-यं) The root of a fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>E. लघु light, लय contexture, (in Tatties, &c.); or लघु and लय, both<BR>meaning the same root. “वेणार मूल ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुवासस्
लघुवासस् mfn. (-साः-साः-सः)<BR>	 1. Thinly or lightly dressed.<BR>	 2. Wearing<BR>clean or pure clothing.<BR> E. लघु, वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुविक्रम
लघुविक्रम Adj. Having a quick step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुवृत्ति
लघुवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति)<BR>	 1. Low, vile.<BR>	 2. Ill-done, mismanaged.<BR>	 3.<BR>Frivolous.<BR> E. लघु, वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुवृत्तिता
लघुवृत्तिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Insignificance, meanness.<BR>	 2. Mismanagement, bad<BR>conduct.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघुहस्त|लघुहस्तः
लघुहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Ready or light-handed.<BR>	 m. (-स्तः) A good archer.<BR> E. लघु, हस्त hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघूकरण
लघूकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Reducing in weight or consequence.<BR>	 2. Thinking<BR>little of, contemning.<BR> E. लघु, and करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघूकृत
लघूकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made light, reduced in weight.<BR>	 2. Reduced<BR>in consequence, made insignificant.<BR>	 3. Thought lightly of.<BR> E. लघु,<BR>कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघ्वाशिन्
लघ्वाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Eating little, moderate.<BR> E. लघु, and अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघ्वाहार
लघ्वाहार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Temperate, abstemious.<BR> E. लघु and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लघ्वी
लघ्वी f. (-घ्वी)<BR>	 1. A delicate woman.<BR>	 2. A light carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्का|लंका
लङ्का f. (-ङ्का)<BR>	 1. The capital of RĀVAṆA in Ceylon; the name is ex-<BR>tended also to the island, which according to the notions of the<BR>Hindus, is much more considerable in size, and lies further from<BR>the continent than in reality; it is described as being equal to<BR>one-twelvth of the equatorial circumference of the earth, and is<BR>one of the places lying under the first meridian, whence the<BR>longitude is computed; it is thus placed in the Eastern ocean,<BR>South of Ceylon, and according to WILFORD is the peninsula of<BR>Malacca: according to some Hindu accounts also, it is distinct<BR>from Ceylon, from which island Lankā is said to be just visible.<BR>2. A goddess or evil spirit, one of the Śākinīs, perhaps the same<BR>as the tutelary deity of the city of Lankā.<BR>	 3. An unchaste woman.<BR>4. A branch.<BR>	 5. A kind of grain.<BR> E. लक् to obtain, (happiness, in<BR>which,) aff. अच्, and नुम् irr. augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कादाहिन्|लंकादाहिन्
लङ्कादाहिन् m. (-ही) The monkey HANUMĀNA.<BR> E. लङ्का the city, and<BR>दाहिन् burner; having set fire to the city with his burning tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कापति|लंकापति|लङ्कापतिः
लङ्कापति m. (-तिः) RĀVAṆA, the Daitya-sovereign of Ceylon.<BR> E. लङ्का<BR>the city, and पति master, ruler; also लङ्काधिपति &c.,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=612-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कायिका
लङ्कायिका f. (-का) A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR> E. लक् to taste,<BR>root of the 10th cl., aff. ण्वुल्, fem. form, नुम् augment; also य being<BR>changed to प, लङ्कापिका, and by a different derivation लङ्कोपिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कास्थायिन्
लङ्कास्थायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Residing or being in Lankā.<BR>	 m. (-यी) A<BR>plant, (Euphorbia Tirucalli.) “लङ्कासिज”.<BR> E. लङ्का Lankā or Ceylon,<BR>and स्थायिन् what abides or grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्केश|लंकेश|लङ्केशः
लङ्केश m. (-शः) The Daitya king RĀVAṆA.<BR> E. लङ्का the city Lankā, ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्कोपिका
लङ्कोपिका f. (-का) A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR> E. लङ्का<BR>Lankā or Ceylon. वप् to sow or be sown, aff. क्वुन्, fem. form, and<BR>the semi-vowel changed to its congener. “पिडिं शाक” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्खनी|लंखनी
लङ्खनी f. (-नी) The bit of a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्ग|लंग|लंगः|लङ्गः
लङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Union, association, proximate connection.<BR>	 2. A lecher,<BR>a catamite.<BR>	 3. Limping, lameness.<BR> E. लगि to be near or with, &c.,<BR>aff. अच्; also with कन् added लङ्गक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गल|लंगल|लंगलं
लङ्गल n. (-लं) A plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्गूल|लंगूल|लंगूलं|लङ्गूलं
लङ्गूल n. (-लं) The tail of an animal.<BR> E. लगि to go, ऊलच् aff., more commonly लाङ्गूल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घन|लंघन|लंघनं|लङ्घनं
लङ्घन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Fasting, abstinence.<BR>	 2. Going, proceeding.<BR>	 3. Leaping,<BR>springing, going by leaps or jumps.<BR>	 4. Jumping over or beyond.<BR>5. Exceeding, transgressing, disregarding propriety, going be-<BR>yond proper bounds.<BR>	 6. Storming a fort, entering by escalade, &c.<BR>7. Capturing a fort in any way.<BR>	 8. One of a horse's paces, cur-<BR>vetting, bounding.<BR>	 9. Injury.<BR> E. लघि to go, to fast, &c. aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घनीय|लंघनीय
लङ्घनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be passed.<BR>	 2. Transgressible.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>fasted.<BR> E. लघि to go, अनीयर् aff.; also लङ्घ्य and लङ्घितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लङ्घित|लंघित
लङ्घित f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Leaped over.<BR>	 2. Traversed.<BR>	 3. Violated.<BR>	 4. Insulted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लछ्|लच्छ्
लछ् r. 1st cl. (लच्छति) To mark; also लच्छ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्
लज् r. 1st cl. (लजते) also (इ) लजि (लञ्जति) 1. To fry.<BR>	 2. To affront, to in-<BR>sult.<BR>	 3. To blame. (ओ, ई) ओलजी r. 6th cl. (लजति-ते) To be ashamed,<BR>to be modest or bashful. r. 10th cl. (लजयति-ते) To shine. (लाजयति-ते)<BR>To hide, to cover, to screen or clothe: also (लजति) or (इ) लजि<BR>(लञ्जयति) 1. To be manifest or apparent.<BR>	 2. To shine. (इ) लजि<BR>(लञ्जयति-ते) 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To dwell.<BR>	 3. To injure.<BR>	 4. To be strong.<BR>5. To censure.<BR>	 6. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लजकारिका
लजकारिका f. (-का) The sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR> E. लज for<BR>लज्जा shame, कारिका making, showing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जका
लज्जका f. (-का) The wild cotton-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जत्
लज्जत् mfn. (-ज्जन्-ज्जन्ती-ज्जत्) Being ashamed, blushing, shrinking. E.<BR>लस्ज् to be ashamed, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जमान
लज्जमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being ashamed.<BR> E. लस्ज् to be ashamed, aff. शानच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जा
लज्जा f. (-ज्जा) Shame, modesty, bashfulness.<BR> E. लस्ज् to be modest, affs.<BR>अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जाकर
लज्जाकर mfn. (-रः-री or रा-रं) Shameful, causing shame.<BR> E. लज्जा, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जाकारिन्
लज्जाकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Causing or occasioning shame.<BR> E. लज्जा<BR>and कारिन् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जान्वित
लज्जान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ashamed, bashful.<BR> E. लज्जा, अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जारहित
लज्जारहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shameless, immodest.<BR> E. लज्जा, रहित void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जालु|लज्जालुः
लज्जालु m. (-लुः) A sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR> E. लज्जा, आलुक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जावत्|लज्जावन्त्
लज्जावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Modest, bashful.<BR> E. लज्जा, shame, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जाशील|लज्जाशीलः
लज्जाशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Bashful, modest.<BR> E. लज्जा, शील possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जाहीन
लज्जाहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shameless, impudent.<BR> E. लज्जा and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्जित|लज्जितः
लज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ashamed, modest.<BR> E. लज्जा modesty, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लज्ज्या
लज्ज्या f. (-ज्ज्या) Modesty, bashfulness.<BR> E. लस्ज् to be ashamed, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्ज्|लंज्
लञ्ज् r. 10th cl. (लञ्जयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be manifest.<BR>	 2. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्ज|लंज|लंजः|लञ्जः
लञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>	 1. A foot.<BR>	 2. The end of the lower garment tucked into<BR>the waist band.<BR>	 3. A tail.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>	 1. An adulteress.<BR>	 2. Sleep.<BR>	 3.<BR>LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 4. A current.<BR> E. लजि to be strong, &c., or लञ्ज् aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लञ्जिका|लंजिका
लञ्जिका f. (-का) A harlot, a whore.<BR> E. लजि to censure, aff. क्वुन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्
लट् r. 1st cl. (लटति)<BR>	 1. To be a child, to talk or be like one.<BR>	 2. To<BR>speak a little.<BR>	 3. To cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट|लटः
लट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A blockhead, a fool, one speaking ignorantly or fool-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">Page613-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ishly.<BR>	 2. Fault, defect.<BR>	 3. A thief.<BR> E. लट् to be or talk as a child,<BR>&c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लटक|लटकः
लटक m. (-कः) A vile or contemptible man.<BR> E. लट् to talk as a child, वुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लटभ
लटभ f. (-भा) Adj. Handsome, attractive. This word has Prākrita origin<BR>and is not used in classical Sanskrit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्ट|लट्टः
लट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A vile or bad man, a wretch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लट्व|लट्वः
लट्व m. (-ट्वः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. A division of music.<BR>	 3. A low and wild<BR>tribe, a tribe of mountaineers.<BR>	 4. A dancing boy.<BR>	 f. (-ट्वा)<BR>	 1. A bird<BR>said to be a kind of sparrow.<BR>	 2. A fruit, a variety of the Karañja.<BR>3. A bad or unchaste woman.<BR>	 4. Curls on the forehead or hanging<BR>down on the face.<BR>	 5. Safflower.<BR>	 6. A sweetmeat.<BR>	 7. A kind of<BR>musical instrument.<BR> E. लट् to be like a child, Unādi aff. क्वन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्
लड् r. 1st and 10th cls. (लडति लडयति)<BR>	 1. To frolic, to sport or dally.<BR>2. To loll, (the tongue.)<BR>	 3. To use the tongue.<BR>	 4. To stir with the<BR>tongue.<BR>	 5. To stir, to agitate.<BR>	 6. To pain. r. 10th cl. (लाडयति-ते)<BR>	 1.<BR>To nurse, to foster, to attend closely.<BR>	 2. To shake.<BR>	 3. To feel de-<BR>sire.<BR>	 4. To spread. (औ, इ) औलडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (लण्डति लण्ड-<BR>यति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. The toss or throw up.<BR>	 3. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लडह|लडहः
लडह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Beautiful, pleasing, charming, (used in Prākrita.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्ड|लड्डः
लड्ड m. (-ड्डः) A wretch, a villain, a low or bad man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लड्डुक|लड्डुकः
लड्डुक n. (-कं) A class of sweetmeats, or a sweetmeat, a sort of ball<BR>made with flour fried with oil or ghee, and mixed with sugar and<BR>spices, and distinguished into different kinds, according to some<BR>slight varieties in its less essential ingredients; also read लड्डक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लण्ड|लंड|लंडं|लण्डं
लण्ड n. (-ण्डं) Excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लण्ड्र|लंड्र|लंड्रः|लण्ड्रः
लण्ड्र m. (-ण्ड्रः) London.<BR> E. लडि, रन् aff. According to others it is deri-<BR>ved from the French Londres.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लता
लता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A creeper, a creeping or winding plant in general;<BR>(this word is often employed as the last member of compounds to<BR>indicate “thinness” or “tenderness.”)<BR>	 2. A branch.<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>commonly Priyangū.<BR>	 4. A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corni-<BR>culata.)<BR>	 5. Heart-pea, (Cardiospermum haliacacabum.)<BR>	 6. The large<BR>Bengal creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>	 7. A sort of grass, (Panicum<BR>dactylon.)<BR>	 8. A vegetable and medicinal substance, commonly<BR>Latākastūrī or the musk-creeper, said to grow in the Dakshin.<BR>9. Thread.<BR>	 10. A whip.<BR>	 11. A string of pearls.<BR> E. लत a Sautra root,<BR>to hurt, to enfold, &c. affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताकसूरिका
लताकसूरिका f. (-का) A medicinal plant, commonly Latākastūrī. E.<BR>लता a creeper, and कसूरिका musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताजिह्व|लताजिह्वः
लताजिह्व m. (-ह्वः) A snake.<BR> E. लता a creeper, and जिह्वा the tongue,<BR>which becomes masc. in the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतातरु|लतातरुः
लतातरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. The orange tree.<BR>	 2. The palm tree.<BR>	 3. The Sāl tree.<BR>E. लता a creeper, and तरु a tree: fit for creepers to cling to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताद्रुम|लताद्रुमः
लताद्रुम m. (-मः) A timber tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR> E. लता, द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतान्त|लतांत
लतान्त n. (-न्तं) A flower.<BR> E. लता a creeper, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतापनस|लतापनसः
लतापनस m. (-सः) The water-melon. “तरमुज”.<BR> E. लता a creeper, पनस the<BR>jack, to the fruit of which the melon may be compared in size.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताप्रतानिनी
लताप्रतानिनी f. (-नी) A spreading creeper.<BR> E. लता a creeper, and प्रता-<BR>निनी spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताभवन
लताभवन n. (-नं) An arbour, a bower.<BR> E. लता, भवन house; also लतामण्डप, लतागृह &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामणि|लतामणिः
लतामणि m. (-णिः) Coral.<BR> E. लता a creeper, and मणि a jewel. “प्रवाले” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामरुत्
लतामरुत् f. (-रुत्) A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.) “पिडिं” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामाधवी
लतामाधवी f. (-वी) The Mādhavī creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR> E. लता<BR>a creeper in general, माधवी the particular one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतामृग|लतामृगः
लतामृग m. (-गः) An ape or monkey.<BR> E. लता and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतायष्टि|लतायष्टिः
लतायष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR> E. लता a creeper,<BR>यष्टि a stick or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतायावक|लतायावकं
लतायावक n. (-कं) Coral.<BR> E. लता a creeper, यावक barley or similar grain; of similar shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतारसन|लतारसनः
लतारसन m. (-नः) A snake.<BR> E. लता a creeper, and रसना the tongue, but<BR>made masc. in the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतार्क|लतार्कः
लतार्क m. (-र्कः) A green onion.<BR> E. लता a creeper, अर्क to heat, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतालक|लतालकः
लतालक m. (-कः) An elephant.<BR> E. लता a creeper, and अलक a curl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतावेष्टन
लतावेष्टन n. (-नं) Embracing, an embrace.<BR> E. लता, वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतावेष्टितक|लतावेष्टितकं
लतावेष्टितक n. (-कं) An embrace, embracing.<BR> E. लता a creeper, (like it,)<BR>वेष्टित a surrounding or enfolding, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लताशङ्ख|लताशङ्खः
लताशङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः) The Sāl tree, (Shorea robusta.) This word is else-<BR>where read लताशङ्कु or लतातरु and शङ्कुतरु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लतिका
लतिका f. (-का) A twining plant.<BR> E. लता the same, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लत्तिका
लत्तिका f. (-का) A lizard.<BR> E. लत a Sautra root, to hurt, तिकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लप्
लप् (ऋ) लपृ r. 1st cl. (लपति) To speak, to utter. With अनु prefixed.<BR>	 1.<BR>To talk like, to mimic.<BR>	 2. To repeat. With अप, To deny. With<BR>आङ्, To address, to speak to. With प्र, To talk incoherently.<BR>With प्रति, To gain, to get. With वि, To lament, to bewail. With<BR>वि and प्र, To contradict, to dispute. With सम्, 1. To converse, to<BR>discourse.<BR>	 2. To be cunning or crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लपन|लपनं
लपन n. (-नं) The mouth.<BR>	 2. Talking.<BR> E. लप् to speak, ल्युट् aff. of the<BR>instrument or act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लपित|लपितं
लपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spoken, said.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Voice or speech.<BR> E. लप् to speak, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्
लब् (इ) लबि r. 1st cl. (लम्बते)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To fall or tumble, to be<BR>prostrate. With अव prefixed, 1. To hold, to support.<BR>	 2. To hang<BR>from or on, to depend from.<BR>	 3. To rest upon.<BR>	 4. To hang with<BR>head downwards. With आङ्, To trust in, to depend on. With<BR>वि, 1. To hang from.<BR>	 2. To decline, to set.<BR>	 3. To stay, to remain.<BR>4. To delay, to detain. With उद्, To stand erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्ध|लब्धः
लब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Gained, acquired, obtained, received.<BR>	 f. (-ब्धा) A<BR>woman whose husband or lover is faithless.<BR> E. लभ् to get, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धचेतस्
लब्धचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः) Recovered, restored to one's senses, come<BR>to a right mind.<BR> E. लब्ध, and चेतस् intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धजन्मन्
लब्धजन्मन् mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म) Born.<BR> E. लब्ध, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धधन
लब्धधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wealthy.<BR> E. लब्ध, धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धप्रशमन
लब्धप्रशमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Securing what has been obtained.<BR>	 2. Bestowing on proper person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धलक्ष्य
लब्धलक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. One who has hit the mark.<BR>	 2. Skilled in<BR>the use of missiles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धवर्ण|लब्धवर्णः
लब्धवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Sage, learned, a Pandit.<BR> E. लब्ध got, वर्ण praise, celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धविद्य
लब्धविद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Learned.<BR> E. लब्ध and विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धसंज्ञ
लब्धसंज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Revived, recovered from fainting.<BR> E. लब्ध, संज्ञा<BR>consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धान्तर|लब्धांतर
लब्धान्तर Adj.<BR>	 1. One who has found an opportunity.<BR>	 2. One who has got admission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धावकाश
लब्धावकाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Having found an opportunity or interval.<BR>E. लब्ध, अवकाश opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्धि|लब्धिः
लब्धि f. (-ब्धिः)<BR>	 1. Acquisition.<BR>	 2. Gain, profit, advantage.<BR>	 3. The quotient, (in math.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्ध्रिम
लब्ध्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Obtained.<BR> E. लभ् to gain, क्त्रिमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लब्ध्वा
लब्ध्वा Ind. Having gained or got.<BR> E. लभ् to get, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभ्
लभ् (डु, अष्) डुलभष् r. 1st cl. (लभते)<BR>	 1. To obtain, to get or gain.<BR>	 2. To<BR>find.<BR>	 3. To be able, to be permitted.<BR>	 4. To recover.<BR>	 5. To know.<BR>With आ, 1. To touch.<BR>	 2. To offer as a sacrifice.<BR>	 3. To attain.<BR>With उप, 1. To attain.<BR>	 2. To perceive, to see. With उप and आ<BR>prefixed, 1. To blame.<BR>	 2. To learn. With प्रति, To gain or regain.<BR>With वि and प्र, 1. To cheat.<BR>	 2. To insult.<BR>	 3. To recover. With सम,<BR>To obtain. Caus. (लम्भयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To receive.<BR>	 3. To dis-<BR>cover.<BR>	 4. To cause to take.<BR>	 5. To cause to suffer. Desid. (लिप्सते) To<BR>long for. (इ) लभि r. 1st cl. (लम्भते)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To injure.<BR>	 3. To<BR>revile.<BR>	 4. To gain. With उप prefixed, 1. To apprehend, to under-<BR>stand.<BR>	 2. To delay. With उप and आङ्, To revile, to abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभन|लभनं
लभन n. (-नं) The act of obtaining or conceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभस|लभसः
लभस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Wealth.<BR>	 2. A solicitor, one who asks or solicits.<BR>n. (-सं) A horse's foot-rope.<BR> E. लभ् to get, Unādi aff. असच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लभ्य|लभ्यं
लभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>	 1. Attainable, procurable.<BR>	 2. Fit, right, pro-<BR>per.<BR> E. लभ् to get, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लमक|लमकः
लमक m. (-कः) A lover, a gallant.<BR> E. रम् to sport, Unādi aff. वुन्, and र changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पट|लंपट|लम्पटः
लम्पट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A lecher, a libertine, a whore-monger, a gallant.<BR>2. The Bakula tree.<BR>	 f. (-टा) Greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पटता
लम्पटता f. (-ता) Libertinism, dissoluteness.<BR> E. लम्पट and तल् aff.; also with त्व लम्पटत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पाक|लंपाक|लम्पाकः
लम्पाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A country, the district of Lamghan in Cābul.<BR>	 2.<BR>A libertine, a lecher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्पापटह|लम्पापटहः
लम्पापटह m. (-हः) A kettle-drum, a state-drum, the Nākarā of the Mussulmāns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्फ|लंफ|लंफः|लम्फः
लम्फ m. (-म्फः) A leap, a jump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्ब|लंब|लम्बः
लम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>	 1. Spacious, capacious.<BR>	 2. Great, large, broad,<BR>long, expanded either in breadth or length, or both.<BR>	 3. Pendu-<BR>lous, depending.<BR>	 m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. A bribe, a present.<BR>	 2. Moving a man<BR>at a sort of backgammon or draughts.<BR>	 3. A perpendicular, (in geo-<BR>metry.)<BR>	 4. (In astronomy,) The arc between the pole and zenith of<BR>any place.<BR>	 f. (-म्बा)<BR>	 1. A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. A name of GAURĪ<BR>or DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. A bitter gourd.<BR> E. लबि to fall, to sound, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बक|लंबक|लंबकः|लम्बकः
लम्बक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A section, a chapter.<BR>	 2. A perpendicular, (in geometry.)<BR>3. The complement of latitude.<BR> E. लबि to fall, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बकर्ण|लंबकर्ण|लम्बकर्णः
लम्बकर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. A goat.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR>	 3. A goblin or Rākshasa.<BR>4. A tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>	 5. A hare.<BR>	 6. An ass.<BR>	 7. A<BR>name of GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. लम्ब large or pendulous, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बज्या
लम्बज्या f. (-ज्या) Sine or cosine of the latitude.<BR> E. लम्ब, and ज्या sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बन|लंबन|लम्बनं|लंबनः|लम्बनः
लम्बन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Depending, descending, falling.<BR>	 2. A long necklace,<BR>one which depends from the neck to the navel.<BR>	 3. Parallax in<BR>longitude, (of the moon.)<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Phlegm, the phlegmatic humour.<BR>2. An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR> E. लबि to fall, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बमान|लम्बमानं
लम्बमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Depending, descending, hanging or falling,<BR>going down.<BR>	 2. Being large or bulky.<BR> E. लबि to fall, &c., and शानच्<BR>aff., मुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बिका|लंबिका
लम्बिका f. (-का) The uvula or soft palate.<BR> E. लबि to hang down, aff. क्कुन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बित|लंबित|लम्बितः
लम्बित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Suspended, depending, falling or hanging<BR>down.<BR>	 2. Gone down.<BR>	 3. Resting on.<BR> E. लबि to fall down, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बुषा|लंबुषा
लम्बुषा f. (-षा) A necklace or seven strings.<BR> E. लबि to depend, उषच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बोदर|लंबोदर|लम्बोदरः
लम्बोदर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>	 2. A glutton.<BR> E. लम्ब large,<BR>and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्बौष्ठ|लंबौष्ठ|लम्बौष्ठः
लम्बौष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A camel.<BR> E. लम्ब large, ओष्ठ a lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भ|लंभ|लंभः|लम्भः
लम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Acquirement.<BR>	 2. Gain.<BR>	 3. Recovery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भन|लंभन|लंभनं|लम्भनं
लम्भन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Abuse, reviling.<BR>	 2. Gaining, getting.<BR> E. लभि to sound,<BR>&c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भयत्
लम्भयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Causing to get, procuring, producing. E.<BR>लभ् to get, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भा
लम्भा f. (-म्भा) A sort of chain enclosure or fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लम्भित|लंभित
लम्भित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Caused to get, given to, procured for.<BR>	 2. Ap-<BR>plied to, employed.<BR>	 3. Spoken to, addressed.<BR>	 4. Heightened, im-<BR>proved, rendered more perfect or intense.<BR>	 5. Cherished.<BR>	 6. Gained.<BR>7. Abused.<BR> E. लभ् to gain, causal form, or लभि to revile, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लय्
लय् r. 1st cl. (लयते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लय|लयः
लय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Equal time in music and dancing.<BR>	 2. Adherence, union.<BR>3. Fusion, solution, absorption.<BR>	 4. Concentration, exclusive devo-<BR>tion.<BR>	 5. Rest, repose.<BR>	 6. Mental inactivity.<BR>	 7. An embrace.<BR>	 8. Des-<BR>truction.<BR>	 9. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 10. Sport, pastime.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. The<BR>root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>	 2. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 3. Fusi-<BR>on, melting.<BR> E. ली adhere to, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लयन|लयनं
लयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Adhering, clinging.<BR>	 2. Rest, repose.<BR>	 3. A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लयपुत्त्री
लयपुत्त्री f. (-त्त्री) An actress, a female dancer.<BR> E. लय equal time in music,<BR>पुत्त्री daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लयालम्ब|लयालम्बः
लयालम्ब m. (-म्बः) An actor, a dancer, a mime.<BR> E. लय equal time, &c.,<BR>and आलम्ब who moves to; it also occurs लयारम्भ and लयालम्भ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लर्व्व्|लर्व्
लर्व्व् r. 1st cl. (लर्व्वति) To go, to move; also लर्व् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल्
लल् r. 1st cl. (ललति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sport, to dally.<BR>	 2. To loll, as the tongue,<BR>&c.: see लड, of which it is considered as a various reading only.<BR>r. 10th cl. (लालयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To desire, to wish for, to seek to obtain.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">Page615-a+ 60</a>]<BR>2. To sport, to wanton.<BR>	 3. To lay.<BR>	 4. To fondle. (ललयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>desire.<BR>	 2. To loll the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लल
लल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Sporting, frolicking.<BR>	 2. Lolling, wagging.<BR>	 3.<BR>Wishing, desirous.<BR> E. लड् or लल् to sport, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललजिह्व
ललजिह्व mfn. (-ह्वः-ह्वा-ह्वं) Fierce, savage, (as a beast of prey, &c.)<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ह्वः)<BR>	 1. A camel.<BR>	 2. A dog.<BR> E. लल lapping, licking, जिह्व the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललत्
ललत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>	 1. Shaking, tremulous.<BR>	 2. Licking, lapping,<BR>stirring or touching with the tongue, lolling the tongue, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wantoning, dallying.<BR> E. लड् to loll, to frolick, &c., participial<BR>aff. शतृ, and ड changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललदम्बु|ललदम्बुः
ललदम्बु m. (-म्बुः) A flower, (Nerium odorum.)<BR> E. लल trembling, अम्बु water. “लिम्पाके च ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललन|ललनं|ललनः
ललन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Pleasure, sport, pastime.<BR>	 2. Lolling the tongue.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-नः) The Sāl tree.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A woman in general.<BR>	 2. A wanton<BR>woman.<BR>	 3. The tongue.<BR> E. लड् to frolic, &c., aff. ल्युट्, ड changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललनिका
ललनिका f. (-का) A little woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललन्तिका|ललंतिका
ललन्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A necklace hanging as low as the navel.<BR>	 2. A<BR>lizard.<BR> E. ललत् sporting, lolling, &c. fem. form, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाक|ललाकः
ललाक m. (-कः) The penis.<BR> E. लड् to frolic, aff. आकन, ड changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाट|ललाटं
ललाट n. (-टं) The forehead.<BR> E. लल wish or dalliance, from लड् with अच्<BR>aff., अट् to go or be, aff. अण्; also with कन् added ललाटक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटतट
ललाटतट n. (-टं) The slope of the forehead.<BR> E. ललाट, and तट a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटन्तप|ललाटंतप|ललाटंतपः|ललाटन्तपः
ललाटन्तप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Burning the forehead, (as the sun.)<BR>	 m. (-पः)<BR>The sun.<BR> E. ललाट the forehead, तप् to scorch or inflame, aff. खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटपट्ट|ललाटपट्टः
ललाटपट्ट n. (-ट्टं)<BR>	 1. A tiara, a fillet.<BR>	 2. The flat surface of the fore-<BR>head.<BR> E. ललाट, and पट्ट a cloth or any flat surface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटफलक
ललाटफलक n. (-कं) The open forehead.<BR> E. ललाट, and फलक a plank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटरे
ललाटरे(ले)खा f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A line on the forehead, supposed to indicate<BR>long life.<BR>	 2. A wrinkled or corrugated brow.<BR>	 3. A coloured<BR>sectarial mark on the forehead.<BR> E. ललाट the forehead, रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटिका
ललाटिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An ornament worn on the forehead, a jewel or star<BR>suspended there, or a kind of tiara bound over it.<BR>	 2. A mark made<BR>with sandal, &c., on the forehead.<BR> E. ललाट and कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाटूल
ललाटूल f. (-ला) Adj. Having a handsome forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललाम|ललामं|ललामः
ललाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Beautiful, agreeable, charming, (in this sense<BR>some authorities confine it to the neuter gender, and to its use<BR>compounded with another word.)<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. A mark or sign.<BR>	 2. A<BR>banner, a flag, a symbol or ensign.<BR>	 3. A mark on the forehead.<BR>	 4.<BR>A horn.<BR>	 5. A tail.<BR>	 6. Majesty, dignity.<BR>	 7. Chief, principal.<BR>	 8. A<BR>horse.<BR>	 9. An ornament.<BR>	 10. A horse's ornament.<BR>	 11. A coloured<BR>mark on the forehead of a horse or bull, &c.<BR>	 12. A mane.<BR>	 13. A<BR>line, a row.<BR>	 f. (-मी)<BR>	 1. Charming.<BR>	 2. An ornament worn on the<BR>ear.<BR> E. लल् to play, &c., aff. अच्, अम् to go, to contribute to or<BR>occasion, aff. अण्; also with कनिन् aff. ललामन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललामक|ललामकं
ललामक n. (-कं) A chaplet of flowers falling over the forehead.<BR> E. ललाम<BR>a mark on the forehead, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललामन्
ललामन् n. (-म)<BR>	 1. A mark or sign, &c.: see ललाम 2. A species of stanza<BR>having ten syllables in the first two Pādas, eleven in the third,<BR>and thirteen in the fourth.<BR>	 3. An ornament, a decoration.<BR>	 4. A<BR>banner, a flag.<BR>	 5. A sectarial mark.<BR>	 6. A tail.<BR>	 7. Anything the<BR>best of its kind: see ललाम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललित|ललितं|ललितः
ललित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wished, desired.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, lovely.<BR>	 3. Wan-<BR>ton, dallying.<BR>	 4. Shaken, trembling, tremulous.<BR>	 5. Graceful.<BR>	 6. Gay,<BR>cheerful, careless.<BR>	 7. Slow, gentle.<BR>	 8. Destroyed.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>branch of feminine action, arising from the passion or sentiment of<BR>love, and expressive of satisfaction and triumph; softness and<BR>delicacy of gesture or motion, putting on appropriate ornaments,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Love of pleasure and gaiety.<BR>	 3. Sport, dalliance.<BR>	 4. Beauty,<BR>charm.<BR>	 5. Simplicity, innocence.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Musk.<BR>	 2. A woman<BR>in general.<BR>	 3. A wanton.<BR> E. लड् to frolic, &c., or लल् to desire,<BR>aff. क्त; in the first case, ड changed to ख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललितपद
ललितपद Adj. Elegantly composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललितप्रहार|ललितप्रहारः
ललितप्रहार m. (-रः) A gentle blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललितार्थ
ललितार्थ n. (-र्थं) Having an amorous meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ललितासप्तमी
ललितासप्तमी f. (-मी) The seventh day of the first-half of Bhādrapada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लव|लवं|लवः
लव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Cutting.<BR>	 2. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 3. Reaping.<BR>	 4. Small,<BR>little; (according to some authorities, this when used attributively<BR>changes its gender, making लवः-लवा-लवं; according to others it<BR>is invariably masc.)<BR>	 5. Smallness, littleness.<BR>	 6. A minute division<BR>of time, the sixtieth part of the twinkling of an eye.<BR>	 7. A larger<BR>division of time, two Kāṣṭhas or 36 twinkling of the eye, or<BR>about (1/2) a second.<BR>	 8. One of the twin sons of RĀMACHANDRA, by<BR>ŚITĀ, born after she had been abandoned by her husband and<BR>brought up at the hermitage of VĀLMĪKI 9. A kind of quail.<BR>	 10.<BR>Hair, wool, &c.; that which is cut or shorn from domestic ani-<BR>mals.<BR>	 11. (In arithmetic,) The numerator of a fraction.<BR>	 12. A de-<BR>gree, (in astronomy.)<BR>	 13. Sport.<BR>	 14. Plucking, mowing.<BR>	 15. A sec-<BR>tion, a fragment.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. The nutmeg.<BR>	 2. Cloves.<BR> E. लू to cut,<BR>aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवक|लवकः
लवक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what cuts, reaps, &c.<BR> E. लू to cut, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवङ्ग|लवंग|लवङ्गं|लवंगः|लवङ्गः
लवङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The clove tree, (Myristica caryophyllata.)<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>Cloves.<BR> E. लू to cut, Unādi aff. अङ्गच्; also with कन् added, लवङ्गक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवण|लवणं|लवणः
लवण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Salt, saline.<BR>	 2. Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>1. Sea-salt.<BR>	 2. Rock or fossile salt.<BR>	 3. Factitious salt, or salt<BR>obtained by boiling clay found near the sea-shore, or any earth<BR>impregnated with saline particles.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The saline or salt<BR>taste, saltness.<BR>	 2. The sea of salt-water.<BR>	 4. The name of a Rākshasa<BR>mentioned in the Rāmāyana.<BR>	 f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Saline, briny.<BR>	 2. Light,<BR>lustre, beauty.<BR>	 3. A small river in Tirhut.<BR> E. लू to cut, (rawness,<BR>or to assist digestion,) aff. ल्युट्, and the final letter made nasal<BR>by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणखानि|लवणखानिः
लवणखानि m. (-निः) A salt mine in general, or the district of Sāmbhar<BR>in Ajmere, celebrated for its fossile salt.<BR> E. लवण salt, खानि a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणसमुद्र|लवणसमुद्रः
लवणसमुद्र m. (-द्रः) The sea of salt-water.<BR> E. लवण, समुद्र ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणाकर|लवणाकरः
लवणाकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A salt mine.<BR>	 2. A mine of beauty.<BR> E. लवण, आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणिमन्
लवणिमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Saltness.<BR>	 2. Beauty, loveliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणोत्तम|लवणोत्तमं
लवणोत्तम n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Nitre.<BR>	 2. Rock or river salt.<BR> E. लवण salt, उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवणोद|लवणोदः
लवणोद m. (-दः) The sea of salt-water.<BR>	 n. (-दं) Brine.<BR> E. लवण, उद water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवन|लवनं
लवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Reaping.<BR>	 2. Cutting.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A coarse kind of custard-<BR>apple, (Annona reticulata.) “लोणा आता ।”<BR> E. लू to cut, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवम्
लवम् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of “a little.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवली
लवली f. (-ली) A kind of tree, (Averrhoa acida.) “नोयाड गाछ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवशस्
लवशस् Ind. Piece meal, in pieces.<BR> E. लव a bit, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवाक|लवाकः
लवाक m. (-कः) A sickle or reaping-hook.<BR> E. लू to cut, Unādi aff. आकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवाणक|लवाणकः
लवाणक n. (-कं) A sickle, a reaping-hook.<BR> E. लू to cut, आणक Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवि|लविः
लवि mfn. (-विः-विः-वि) Cutting, edged, sharp, (as an instrument, &c.)<BR>E. लू to cut, Unādi aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवित्र|लवित्रं
लवित्र n. (-त्रं) A sickle, a small reaping-hook.<BR> E. लू to cut, aff. इत्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लवेप्सु
लवेप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Wishing to cut or reap.<BR> E. लव and ईप्सु desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लव्य
लव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be cut.<BR> E. लू to cut, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लश्
लश् r. 10th cl. (लाशयति-ते) To be skilful or clever, to do any thing skil-<BR>fully and scientifically. (This root is sometimes written लष् or लस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लशुन|लशुनं|लशुनः
लशुन n. (-नं) Garlic.<BR> E. अश् to eat, Unādi aff. उनन्, and लश substitu-<BR>ted for the root; also with the vowel of the aff, long, लशून n. (-नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लशुनीय
लशुनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Garlicky.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Cat's-eye.<BR> E. लशुन and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लष्
लष् r. 1st and 4th cls. (लषति-ते or लष्यति-ते) To desire, to like, to love.<BR>(अभि is usually prefixed.) r. 10th cl. (लाषयति-ते) To be skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लष्व|लष्वः
लष्व m. (-ष्वः) A dancer, an actor.<BR> E. लष् to be skilled in any art, (as<BR>dancing, &c.) and वन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्
लस् r. 1st cl. (लसति)<BR>	 1. To embrace.<BR>	 2. To sport or play.<BR>	 3. To glitter.<BR>4. To arise. With उद्, 1. To glitter.<BR>	 2. To appear.<BR>	 3. To blow, to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">Page616-a+ 60</a>]<BR>open. With परि, To appear gaudy. With वि, To sound, to echo. r.<BR>10th cl. (लासयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be skilful, to do any thing skilfully or<BR>scientifically.<BR>	 2. To work. With उत् prefixed, 1. To shine, to be<BR>brilliant or splendid.<BR>	 2. To be happy or delighted. With वि, To<BR>gambol, to sport, especially amorously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसत्
लसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Sporting, playing.<BR>	 2. Shining.<BR>	 3. Glancing,<BR>(as rays of light.)<BR> E. लस् to sport, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसा
लसा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. Turmeric.<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR> E. लस् to sport, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसिका
लसिका f. (-का) Saliva, spittle.<BR> E. रस् to taste, &c., aff. वुन्, र changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसित
लसित f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Sported.<BR>	 2. Arose, appeared.<BR>	 3. Moved about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लसीका
लसीका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Spittle.<BR>	 2. Pus, matter.<BR>	 3. Lymph.<BR>	 4. The juice of<BR>the sugarcane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्ज्
लस्ज् (ओ, ई) ओलस्जी r. 6th cl. (लज्जते)<BR>	 1. To be modest or ashamed.<BR>	 2. To blush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्त|लस्तः
लस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Grasped, embraced.<BR>	 2. Skilled, skilful.<BR>	 m. (-स्तः)<BR>The middle of a bow.<BR> E. लस् to embrace, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्तक|लस्तकः
लस्तक m. (-कः) The middle of a bow.<BR> E. लस्त grasped, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लस्तकिन्
लस्तकिन् m. (-की) A bow.<BR> E. लस्तक the middle of a bow, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लहरि|लहरिः
लहरि f. (-रिः-री) A large wave or surf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ला
ला r. 2nd cl. (लाति)<BR>	 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To get, to receive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाकुटिक|लाकुटिकः
लाकुटिक m. (-कः) Armed with a club: see लागुडिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षकी
लाक्षकी f. (-की) A name of Śitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षणिक|लाक्षणिकः
लाक्षणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Secondary, inferior, subordinate.<BR>	 2. In-<BR>dicatory, characteristic.<BR>	 3. Technical.<BR>	 4. Acquainted with signs.<BR>m. (-कः) A technical term, a word implying a definition.<BR> E. क्षणण<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षण्य
लाक्षण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) Indicative, symptomatic, relating to a mark<BR>or sign, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ण्या) One who can interpret signs.<BR> E. लक्षण, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षा
लाक्षा f. (-क्षा) Lac, a red dye, or an insect which is analogous to the<BR>cochineal insect, and like it forms when died and prepared, a dye<BR>of a red colour; the nest is formed of a resinous substance<BR>which is used as sealing wax, and as an article of decoration by<BR>women, and is usually termed Shel lac.<BR> E. लक्ष् to mark or stain,<BR>aff. अ, and अण् added, the vowel made long; or लक्ष a hundred<BR>thousand, अण् aff.; made by a multitude of the insects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षातरु|लाक्षातरुः
लाक्षातरु m. (-रुः) The Palāsh-tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. लाक्षा lac, and<BR>तरु a tree; the insect being especially found in this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षाप्रसादन|लाक्षाप्रसादनः
लाक्षाप्रसादन m. (-नः) The red Lodh, a tree from the bark of which an<BR>astringent infusion is prepared, which is used to fix colour in<BR>dyeing.<BR> E. लाक्षा lac, प्रसादन cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षावृक्ष|लाक्षावृक्षः
लाक्षावृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The Butea frondosa.<BR> E. लाक्षा the lac, and वृक्ष a tree: see लाक्षातरु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाक्षिक
लाक्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Made of lac, &c.<BR>	 2. Relating to a large<BR>number or a lakh.<BR> E. लाक्षा, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाख्
लाख् (ऋ) लाखृ r. 1st cl. (लाखति)<BR>	 1. To be dry or arid.<BR>	 2. To adorn.<BR>	 3.<BR>To be able or competent to.<BR>	 4. To give.<BR>	 5. To refuse or prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लागुडिक
लागुडिक f. (-की) Adj. Armed with a club.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A sentinel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाघ्
लाघ् (ऋ) लाघृ r. 1st cl. (लाघते) To be able, equal or competent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाघव|लाघवं
लाघव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Health.<BR>	 2. Lightness, delicacy, minuteness.<BR>	 3. Mean-<BR>ness, insignificance.<BR>	 4. Frivolity.<BR>	 5. Speed.<BR>	 6. Activity.<BR>	 7. Small-<BR>ness.<BR>	 8. Ease.<BR>	 9. Brevity.<BR>	 10. Contempt.<BR> E. लघु light, &c. and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गल|लांगल|लांगलं|लाङ्गलं|लाङ्गलः
लाङ्गल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A plough.<BR>	 2. The penis.<BR>	 3. The palm tree.<BR>	 4. A sort of<BR>flower.<BR>	 5. The main beam of a house.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. An aquatic shrub,<BR>(Jussiaea repens.)<BR>	 2. A creeping shrub, (Commelina salicifolia.)<BR>3. Another creeper, (Nama repens.)<BR>	 4. A plant, (Gloriosa superba.)<BR>E. लगि to go, to limp, &c., Unādi aff. कलच्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलग्रह|लांगलग्रह|लाङ्गलग्रहः
लाङ्गलग्रह m. (-हः) A ploughman.<BR> E. लाङ्गल a plough, and ग्रह who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलग्रहण
लाङ्गलग्रहण n. (-णं) Guiding the plough, ploughing.<BR> E. लाङ्गल, ग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलदण्ड|लांगलदंड|लाङ्गलदण्डः
लाङ्गलदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The pole or shaft of a plough.<BR> E. लाङ्गल, दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलध्वज|लांगलध्वज|लाङ्गलध्वजः
लाङ्गलध्वज m. (-जः) An epithet of BALARĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलपद्धति|लांगलपद्धति|लाङ्गलपद्धतिः
लाङ्गलपद्धति f. (-तिः) A furrow.<BR> E. लाङ्गल a plough, and पद्धति a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलफाल|लांगलफाल|लाङ्गलफालः
लाङ्गलफाल mn. (-लः-लं) A ploughshare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलिक|लांगलिक|लाङ्गलिकः
लाङ्गलिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to a plough.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>One of the thirty-four species of the fixed, or mineral and vegetable<BR>poisons.<BR>	 f. (-का-की) A small creeper, commonly called Lāngalī,<BR>(Gloriosa superba, or Commelina salicifolia.)<BR> E. लाङ्गली a name of<BR>several plants, aff. कन्, fem. form; or लाङ्गल and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलिन्|लांगलिन्
लाङ्गलिन् m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A name of BALARĀMA.<BR>	 2. The cocoanut-tree.<BR>	 3. A<BR>snake.<BR> E. लाङ्गल a plough, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गलीषा
लाङ्गलीषा f. (-षा) The pole of a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गुल|लांगुल|लांगुलं|लाङ्गुलं
लाङ्गुल n. (-लं) A horse's tail.<BR> E. लगि to go, aff. उलव्: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गूल|लांगूल|लांगूलं|लाङ्गूलं
लाङ्गूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A hairy tail, (as a horse's, &c.)<BR>	 2. The penis.<BR>	 3. A<BR>granary, a basket or shed for holding corn or grain.<BR> E. लगि to go,<BR>Unādi aff. उलच्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाङ्गूलिन्|लांगूलिन्
लाङ्गूलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Tailed.<BR>	 m. (-ली) A monkey.<BR> E. लाङ्गूल a tail, aff इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाच्छ्
लाच्छ् (इ) लाच्छि r. 1st cl. (लाञ्छति)<BR>	 1. To mark.<BR>	 2. To decorate; also लाछ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाज्
लाज् r. 1st cl. (लाजति) (इ) लाजि (लाञ्जति) 1. To blame.<BR>	 2. To fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाज|लाजं|लाजः
लाज m. (-जः) Grain, wetted or sprinkled.<BR>	 n. (-जं) The root of the<BR>Andropogon muricatum.<BR>	 f. (-जा) or masc. plu. (-जाः) Fried grain.<BR>E. लाज् to fry, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाञ्छन|लांछन|लांछनं|लाञ्छनं|लाञ्छनः
लाञ्छन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A name, an appellation.<BR>	 2. A mark or sign.<BR>	 3. A<BR>stain, a mark of ignominy.<BR>	 4. A land-mark.<BR>	 5. The spots on the<BR>disc of the moon.<BR> E. लाञ्छि to mark, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाञ्छित|लांछित
लाञ्छित f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Marked, distinguished.<BR>	 2. Named.<BR>	 3. Furnished with.<BR>	 4. Decorated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाट|लाटः
लाट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Old or worn, spoiled, shabby, (as clothes, orna-<BR>ments, &c.)<BR>	 2. Childish.<BR>	 m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 2. Fault, defect.<BR>3. Idle or inebriate language.<BR>	 4. Repetition of words in the same<BR>sense, but in a different application.<BR>	 5. The name of a country, the<BR>upper part of the Dakshin, Lār or Larice.<BR> E. लट् to be childish,<BR>aff. अण् or घञ्; or लाट a Kāndwādi root, to live, aff. अच्, ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाटानुप्रास|लाटानुप्रासः
लाटानुप्रास m. (-सः) A figure of rhetoric; repetition of a word in the same<BR>sense, but with a different application.<BR> E. लाट, अनुप्रास alliteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाटी
लाटी f. (टी or टिका)<BR>	 1. A particular style of composition.<BR>	 2. Name of a<BR>Prākrita dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाड्
लाड् r. 10th cl. (लाडयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To throw, to toss.<BR>	 2. To fondle, to caress.<BR>	 3. To blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाण्ठनी|लांठनी
लाण्ठनी f. (-नी) An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लात
लात f. (-ता) Taken, received.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाप|लापः
लाप m. (-पः) Speaking, talking, prating.<BR> E. लप् to speak, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाप्य|लाप्यं
लाप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be said or spoken.<BR> E. लप् to speak, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाब|लाबः
लाब m. (-बः) A sort of quail; also with कन् added, लाबक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभ्
लाभ् r. 10th cl. (लाभयति) To throw, to send or direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभ|लाभः
लाभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. Profit.<BR>	 2. Gain, in general, acquirement, acquisition.<BR>	 3.<BR>Interest.<BR>	 4. Conquest.<BR>	 5. Perception.<BR> E. लभ् to get or gain, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभकृत्
लाभकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Gaining, making profit.<BR> E. लाभ, कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभलिप्सु
लाभलिप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Covetous, grasping, desirous of gain or<BR>profit.<BR> E. लाभ, and लिप्सु desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाभालाभ
लाभालाभ m. (-भः) Profit and loss.<BR> E. लाभ, and अलाभ not gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लामज्जक|लामज्जकं
लामज्जक n. (-कं) The root of the Andropogon muricatum, a fragrant<BR>grass.<BR> E. ला what takes or removes, (heat, &c.), मज्जा the pith, and<BR>कप् added. “वेणार मूल” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालन|लालनं|लालनः
लालन n. (-नं) Wheedling, coaxing.<BR> E. लल् to sport, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालप्यमान
लालप्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Bewailing or supplicating much.<BR> E. लप् to<BR>speak, freq. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालष्यमान
लालष्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wishing to enjoy.<BR> E. लष् to desire, freq. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालस|लालसः
लालस f. (-सा) Adj.<BR>	 1. Ardently desirous of.<BR>	 2. Devoted to, finding<BR>pleasure in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालसा
लालसा mf. (-सः-सा)<BR>	 1. Ardent desire.<BR>	 2. Regret, sorrow, missing, wish-<BR>ing for any person or object absent.<BR>	 3. Soliciting, asking.<BR>	 4. The<BR>longing of pregnant women.<BR>	 5. Wanton sport, dalliance.<BR> E. लल् to<BR>desire, to wish for, असण् Unādi aff.; or लष् to wish, or लस् to<BR>sport, affs. घञ् and टाप्, and the root reiterated, deriv. irr. Vā-<BR>chaspatya defines it thus:--लस स्पृहायां यङ् लुक् भावे अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालसोक
लालसोक n. (-कं) Sauce, gravy.<BR> E. लालसा desire, ईकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाला
लाला f. (-ला) Saliva, spittle.<BR> E. लल् to wish, णिच्-अच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाटिक|लालाटिकः
लालाटिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating to the forehead, worn on it, be-<BR>longing to it, &c.<BR>	 2. Contemplating the forehead, looking at it, &c.<BR>3. Low, vile.<BR>	 4. Relating to fate or destiny.<BR>	 mf. (-कः-की)<BR>	 1. An<BR>attentive servant, one who watches a master's countenance, and<BR>learns by it what is necessary to be done.<BR>	 2. An idler, one who<BR>is unable to work, and is a burden to his patron.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A par-<BR>ticular mode of embracing.<BR> E. ललाट the forehead, aff. ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालामेह|लालामेहः
लालामेह m. (-हः) Passing mucous urine.<BR> E. लाला, and मेह urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालाविष|लालाविषः
लालाविष m. (-षः) An insect, whose spittle is venomous or acrid, as a<BR>spider, &c.<BR> E. लाला saliva, विष venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालास्राव|लालास्रावः
लालास्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A spider.<BR>	 2. A flow of saliva.<BR> E. लाला saliva, स्रु to distil, aff. णिच् अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालिक|लालिकः
लालिक m. (-कः) A buffalo.<BR>	 f. (-का) A jesting or evasive reply, equivo-<BR>que.<BR> E. लाला saliva, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालित
लालित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Loved, desired.<BR>	 2. Cherished, treated tenderly.<BR>3. Coaxed, wheedled, seduced.<BR> E. लल् to desire, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालितक|लालितकः
लालितक m. (-कः) A fondling, a pet, a little favourite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालित्य|लालित्यं
लालित्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Beauty, loveliness.<BR>	 2. Gaiety.<BR>	 3. Amorous gestures.<BR>4. Gracefulness, &c.<BR> E. ललित, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालिन्
लालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Wheedling, coaxing, fondling.<BR>	 m. (-ली) A<BR>seducer.<BR>	 f. (-लिनी) A wanton.<BR> E. लल् to sport, causal v., घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लालुका
लालुका f. (-का) A sort of necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाव|लावः
लाव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Cutting down.<BR>	 2. Killing.<BR>	 3. Plucking, gather-<BR>ing.<BR>	 mf. (-वः-वा) A sort of quail, (Perdix chinensis.)<BR> E. लू to cut, to<BR>eat, (corn), causal form, aff. घञ्; also with कन् added, लावक m. (-कः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावक|लावकः
लावक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cutter, a divider.<BR>	 2. A quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण|लावणं
लावण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>	 1. Salted, dressed or cooked with salt.<BR>	 2. Salt,<BR>belonging or relating to it, &c.<BR> E. लवण salt, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावणिक|लावणिकं|लावणिकः
लावणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Salted, cooked or dressed with salt.<BR>	 2.<BR>Relating to salt, &c.<BR>	 3. Lovely, beautiful.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A vender of salt.<BR>n. (-कं) A vessel holding salt, a salt-cellar.<BR> E. लवण salt, aff. ठण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण्य|लावण्यं
लावण्य n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Saltness, the taste or property of salt.<BR>	 2. Beauty,<BR>loveliness.<BR> E. लवण salt, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण्यश्री
लावण्यश्री f. (-श्रीः) Great beauty.<BR> E. लावण्य, and श्री wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावण्यार्जित|लावण्यार्जितं
लावण्यार्जित n. (-तं) Property belonging to a woman, consisting of that<BR>which has been presented to her at her marriage as a token of<BR>respect, as a mark of kindness, or by her father or mother-in-law.<BR>E. लावण्य loveliness, and अर्जित acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाविक|लाविकः
लाविक m. (-कः) A buffalo.<BR> E. लव cutting, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लावु|लावुः
लावु f. (-वुः-वूः) A pumpkin gourd, (Cucurbita lagenaria.)<BR> E. लू to cut,<BR>to destroy, (disease,) aff. उण्; also with कन् added लावुका, and<BR>with अ or आङ् prefixed, अलावु आलावु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाव्य
लाव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be cut, to be cut off or drown.<BR> E. लू to cut, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाषुक
लाषुक f. (-का or की) Adj. Covetous, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास|लासः
लास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Dancing in general.<BR>	 2. Dancing, as practised by wo-<BR>men: see लास्य.<BR>	 3. Pulse that has been steeped or slightly boiled,<BR>pea-water, &c. not thickened to the consistency of Yūsha or pease-<BR>soup.<BR>	 4. Dalliance, wanton sport, &c.<BR> E. लस् to sport, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लासक|लासकं|लासकः
लासक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A dancer, an actor, a mime.<BR>	 2. A peacock.<BR>	 3. Em-<BR>bracing, enfolding, surrounding.<BR>	 4. One who sports or gambols.<BR>n. (-कं) A turret, a room on the top of a building.<BR>	 f. (लासिका or<BR>लासकी)<BR>	 1. A female dancer, a Nāutch-girl.<BR>	 2. A wanton, a harlot.<BR>E. लस् to embrace, to be skilful, (in the art of dancing,) aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्फोटनी
लास्फोटनी f. (-नी) A gimlet, an auger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्य|लास्यं|लास्यः
लास्य n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Dancing in general.<BR>	 2. Symphony, or union of song,<BR>dance, and instrumental music.<BR>	 3. A mode of dance in which<BR>the emotions of love are represented mimically, the Nāutch<BR>of India, or dance practised by women chiefly, and confined to<BR>attitude and gesticulation, with a shuffling motion of the feet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">Page617-b+ 60</a>]<BR>seldom lifted from the ground; this style is said to have been<BR>invented by PĀRVATĪ, and communicated by her to the daughter<BR>of VĀṆASURA, by whom her female friends and companions were<BR>instructed in it; as a species, it is opposed to the TĀNDAVA, the<BR>most boisterous dance of ŚIVA, and his followers or men.<BR>	 4. A<BR>part or embellishment of dramatic composition, the occasional<BR>introduction of music and singing; also abrupt transition from<BR>Prākrita to Sanskrit and from Sanskrit to Prākrita, &c.<BR>	 m. (-स्यः)<BR>A dancer.<BR>	 f. (-स्या) A female dancer.<BR> E. लस् to be skilled in the art<BR>of dancing, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्यक|लास्यकं
लास्यक n. (-कं) Dancing in general, or a particular style of dancing.<BR> E. लास्य, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लास्याङ्ग
लास्याङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A part of a drama, of the Lāsya order: see लास्य. E.<BR>लास्य and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लि|लिः
लि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. Weariness.<BR>	 2. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 3. End, term.<BR>	 4. Equality,<BR>sameness.<BR>	 5. A bracelet.<BR> E. ला to take, or ली to melt, &c., aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिकुच|लिकुचं|लिकुचः
लिकुच m. (-चः) A sort of bread-fruit tree, (Artocarpus lacucha.) E.<BR>लकुच q. v., and इ substituted for the first vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिक्का
लिक्का f. (-क्का) A nit, a young louse. E. It is a various reading of लिक्षा. “निकि” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिक्षा
लिक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. A nit, a young louse, or the egg of a louse.<BR>	 2. A<BR>poppy seed considered as a measure of weight, or one sixth of a<BR>mustard seed.<BR> E. लक्ष् to mark, aff. घञ्, इ substituted for the radical<BR>vowel and the deriv. irr.: also क्क being substituted for the final<BR>लिक्का, and with कन् added, fem. form, लिक्षिका; again with ई<BR>substituted for the radical vowel लीक्षा, &c.; also read लिख्या ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिक्षिका
लिक्षिका f. (-का) A nit. “केशकीटभेदे, निकि इति भाषाः see लिक्का ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख्
लिख् r. 6th cl. (लिखति)<BR>	 1. To write.<BR>	 2. To scratch, to scrape, to tear<BR>up.<BR>	 3. To draw a line, to make a mark, &c.<BR>	 4. To draw, to sketch,<BR>to portray, to paint.<BR>	 5. To touch.<BR>	 6. To make smooth.<BR>	 7. To unite<BR>sexually with female. With आ, 1. To scratch.<BR>	 2. To write.<BR>	 3. To<BR>paint. With उद्, 1. To scrape.<BR>	 2. To carve.<BR>	 3. To polish. With प्रति,<BR>To write in return, to reply. With वि, 1. To scratch.<BR>	 2. To write.<BR>3. To paint, to draw, to delineate.<BR>	 4. To implant, to infix. r. 1st cl.<BR>(लेखति) (इ) लिखि r. 1st cl. (लिङ्खति.) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख|लिखः
लिख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. Writing.<BR>	 2. A writer.<BR> E. लिख् to write, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखत्
लिखत् mfn. (-खन्-खन्ती or खती-खत्)<BR>	 1. Writing.<BR>	 2. Painting, delineating.<BR>3. Scratching, making streaks or lines.<BR> E. लिख् to write, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखन|लिखनं
लिखन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Scripture, writing.<BR>	 2. A writing, a written document.<BR>3. Scratching.<BR>	 4. Writing, inscribing.<BR>	 5. Scarifying.<BR> E. लिख् to<BR>write, aff. ल्युट्; and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखित|लिखितं|लिखितः
लिखित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Written.<BR>	 2. Drawn, delineated, painted:<BR>(painting being considered a sort of writing.)<BR>	 3. Drawn as lines,<BR>scratched.<BR>	 4. Sacrified.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Scripture, writing.<BR>	 2. A writing,<BR>a manuscript, a written book or paper.<BR> E. लिख् to write, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिखित्वा
लिखित्वा Ind. Having written, delineated, &c.<BR> E. लिख् to write, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिख्या
लिख्या f. (-ख्या) A poppy seed, considered as a minute measure of<BR>weight, variously estimated at four or eight Traśarenus or motes,<BR>or the sixth part of a mustard seed, &c.<BR> E. लिख् to write, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिग्
लिग्(इ)लिगि r. 1st cl. (लिङ्गति) To go, to move. r. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>(लिङ्गति लिङ्गयति-ते) To paint, to variegate. With आङ् To embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिगु|लिगुः
लिगु n. (-गु)<BR>	 1. The heart, the mind.<BR>	 m. (-गुः)<BR>	 1. A fool, a blockhead.<BR>2. A deer.<BR>	 3. Part of the earth.<BR> E. लग् to be near or with, Unādi<BR>aff. कु, and इ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्ग|लिंग|लिंगं|लिङ्गं
लिङ्ग n. (-ङ्कं)<BR>	 1. A mark, a spot, a stain, a sign, a token, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>badge or mark assumed with a view to deceive.<BR>	 3. A sign of sex,<BR>the penis.<BR>	 4. The phallus, or ŚIVA under that emblem.<BR>	 5. In-<BR>ference, probable conclusion.<BR>	 6. The premises leading to a con-<BR>clusion.<BR>	 7. Nature or Prakritī, according to the Sānkhya<BR>philosophy, which considers this as the active power in creation.<BR>8. Gender, (as पुंलिङ्गः the masculine gender, &c.)<BR>	 9. The order of<BR>the religious student.<BR>	 10. Symptom or mark of disease.<BR>	 11. The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">Page618-a+ 60</a>]<BR>predicate of a proposition.<BR>	 12. Evidence.<BR> E. लिगि to go, &c., aff.<BR>अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गक|लिंगक|लिंगकः|लिङ्गकः
लिङ्गक m. (-कः) The elephant or wood-apple, (Feronia elephantium,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. लिङ्ग the penis, and कन् aff. “कयेतवेल् इति भाषा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गन|लिंगन|लिंगनं
लिङ्गन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Licking.<BR>	 2. Embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गनाश|लिंगनाश|लिङ्गनाशः
लिङ्गनाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Loss of any characteristic mark, &c.<BR>	 2. Loss of<BR>vision from cataract, &c., considered to be discoloration of the<BR>pupil, either red, white, or yellow.<BR>	 3. Loss of the penis.<BR> E. लिङ्ग<BR>mark, (of the eye &c.), नाश destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गपरामर्श|लिंगपरामर्श|लिङ्गपरामर्शः
लिङ्गपरामर्श m. (-र्शः) The consideration of a sign or Hetu, (in logic).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गवर्द्धन
लिङ्गवर्द्धन m. (-नः) The elephant or wood-apple, (Feronia elephantium.)<BR>E. लिङ्ग the penis, and वर्द्ध्वन increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गवर्द्धिनी
लिङ्गवर्द्धिनी f. (-नी) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.) “अपामार्ग वृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गविपर्यय|लिंगविपर्यय|लिङ्गविपर्ययः
लिङ्गविपर्यय m. (-यः) Change of gender, (in grammar.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गवृत्ति|लिंगवृत्ति|लिङ्गवृत्तिः
लिङ्गवृत्ति m. (-त्तिः) A religious hypocrite, one who assumes the dress,<BR>&c., of an ascetic in order to get a livelihood.<BR> E. लिङ्ग a mark,<BR>external show or sign, (as the clotted hair, &c.) and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गशरीर|लिंगशरीर
लिङ्गशरीर n. (-रं) One of the five sheaths that enclose the soul, (in Ve-<BR>dānta philosophy.) Also लिङ्गदेह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गस्थ|लिङ्गस्थः
लिङ्गस्थ m. (-स्थः) A religious student.<BR> E. लिङ्ग and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गानुशासन|लिंगानुशासन
लिङ्गानुशासन n. (-नं) The laws of Grammatical gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गार्च्चन|लिङ्गार्चन|लिंगार्चन
लिङ्गार्च्चन n. (-नं) Worship of the Linga or phallus.<BR> E. लिङ्ग, and अर्च्चन worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गालिका
लिङ्गालिका f. (-का) A small mouse or shrew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गिन्|लिंगिन्
लिङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>	 1. Having marks, &c.<BR>	 2. Indicated,<BR>characterized.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. A hypocrite, a pre-<BR>tended devotee.<BR>	 3. An ascetic.<BR>	 4. A religious student.<BR>	 5. A wor-<BR>shipper of ŚIVA in the phallic type.<BR>	 6. The subject of a preposi-<BR>tion, (in logic.)<BR> E. लिङ्ग a mark, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिङ्गिवेष|लिङ्गिवेषः
लिङ्गिवेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The dress or the insignia of religious student, the<BR>skin, staff, bowl, &c.<BR>	 2. The dress or appearance of a follower of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR> E. लिङ्गिन्, and वेष attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्
लिप् (ञि, औ) ञि औलिप r. 6th cl. (लिम्पति-ते)<BR>	 1. To increase or add to.<BR>	 2.<BR>To anoint, to smear, to plaster.<BR>	 3. To cover.<BR>	 4. To kindle, to inflame.<BR>5. To stain, to pollute. With अनु, 1. To besmear, to anoint.<BR>	 2. To<BR>cover, to envelop. With अव, To anoint. With आ, 1. To besmear.<BR>2. To contaminate. With वि, To besmear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप|लिपः
लिप m. (-पः) Smearing, plastering.<BR> E. लिप् to smear, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपि|लिपिः
लिपि f. (-पिः-पी)<BR>	 1. Writing in general, handwriting.<BR>	 2. A writing, a<BR>written paper or book, &c.<BR>	 3. Painting, drawing.<BR>	 4. Smearing.<BR>5. Alphabet.<BR>	 6. A document.<BR> E. लिप् to spread, (ink, &c.) Unādi aff.<BR>इक् with ङीप् optionally added, the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिकर|लिपिकरः
लिपिकर m. (-रः) A scribe, &c. see लिपिकार.<BR> E. लिपि, कर who executes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिका
लिपिका f. (-का) Writing, a writing.<BR> E. लिपि writing, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिकार|लिपिकारः
लिपिकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A scribe, a writer.<BR>	 2. An engraver.<BR>	 3. A plaster-<BR>er, a white-washer.<BR> E. लिपि writing, and कार who makes, from<BR>कृ to make, and अण् aff; also with ट aff. लिपिकर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिज्ञ
लिपिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञ) One who can write.<BR> E. लिपि, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिपिसज्जा
लिपिसज्जा f. (-ज्जा) Implements or materials for writing.<BR> E. लिपि, and<BR>सज्जा preparation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्त|लिप्तं
लिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Smeared, anointed, plastered, spread.<BR>	 2. Eaten.<BR>3. Envenomed, spread or touched with any poisonous substance.<BR>	 4.<BR>Embraced, united, connected with, &c.<BR>	 5. Defiled or contaminated<BR>by.<BR>	 6. Stained, soiled.<BR> E. लिप् to smear, aff. क्त; or in the last sense<BR>ली to cling to, Unādi aff. त, with पुट् augment, and the radical<BR>vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्तक|लिप्तकः
लिप्तक m. (-कः) A poisoned arrow.<BR> E. लिप्त poisoned, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्तवत्
लिप्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Anointed, plastered.<BR>	 2. Touched.<BR>	 3.<BR>Vitiated, defiled.<BR> E. लिप् to smear, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्तहस्त
लिप्तहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Having the hands stained or smeared.<BR> E. लिप्त, हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सा
लिप्सा f. (-प्सा) Wish, desire, (in general.)<BR>	 2. Desire of obtaining. E.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">Page618-b+ 60</a>]<BR>लिप्स the desiderative form of to लभ् get, (to wish to get,) सन्<BR>affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सित
लिप्सित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Coveted, desired.<BR> E. लिप्स् to wish, to obtain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिप्सु|लिप्सुः
लिप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Desirous, desiring, wishing, cupidinous. E.<BR>लिप्स् desiderative of लभ्, (see the last,) and उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्प|लिंप|लिंपः|लिम्पः
लिम्प m. (-म्पः) Smearing, anointing, plastering.<BR> E. लिप् to smear<BR>(taking in its derivative forms the nasal augment,) and श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्पट|लिंपट|लिम्पटः
लिम्पट m. (-टः) A lecher, a whore-monger.<BR>	 f. (-टा) Libidinous, lust-<BR>ful.<BR> E. लिपि to smear with unguents, अटच् aff.; also लम्पट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिम्पाक|लिंपाक|लिम्पाकं|लिंपाकः|लिम्पाकः
लिम्पाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The lime tree, (Citrus acida.) “पातिलेबुर गाछ ।”<BR>2. An ass.<BR> E. लिपि to smear, aff. काकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिवि|लिविः
लिवि f. (-विः-वी) Writing, hand-writing, or a writing, a manuscript. E.<BR>लिप् to smear, (with ink,) Unādi aff. इक्, with the vowel unchan-<BR>ged, and व substituted for प ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिविकर|लिविकरः
लिविकर m. (-रः) A scribe, a writer.<BR> E. लिवि writing, कर who executes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिविङ्कर|लिविंकर|लिविङ्करः
लिविङ्कर m. (-रः) A writer, a scribe.<BR> E. लिवि writing, कृ to practise, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिश्
लिश्(औ)लिशौ r. 4th cl. (लिश्यते) To lessen or become less. r. 6th cl.<BR>(लिशति) To go, to move, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिष्ट
लिष्ट f. (-ष्टा) Lessened, decreased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिष्व|लिष्वः
लिष्व m. (-ष्वः) A dancer, an actor.<BR> E. लष् to be skilled, (in dancing,)<BR>Unādi aff. क्वन्, and इ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लिह्
लिह् r. 2nd cl. (लेढि लीढे Desid, लिलिक्षति-ते) To taste, to taste with<BR>tongue, to lick, to sip. With अव, To chew, to lick. With आ, 1. To<BR>lick.<BR>	 2. To pierce.<BR>	 3. To wound. With उद्, To polish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ली
ली r. 1st cl. (लयति) To melt, to liquefy. r. 4th cl. (लीयते)<BR>	 1. To stick<BR>together.<BR>	 2. To lurk in, to hide in.<BR>	 3. To be dissolved.<BR>	 4. To be<BR>sticky.<BR>	 5. To be devoted to.<BR>	 6. To vanish, to disappear. With अभि,<BR>To cover, to spread over. With आ, 1. To cover, to besmear.<BR>	 2. To<BR>lurk or hide in. With नि, 1. To lie down, to alight.<BR>	 2. To conceal<BR>oneself, (with an abl.)<BR>	 3. To perish. With प्र, 1. To be absorbed<BR>in.<BR>	 2. To vanish. With वि, 1. To cleave to.<BR>	 2. To settle on.<BR>	 3. To<BR>melt away.<BR>	 4. To disappear, to perish. With सम, 1. To cling to.<BR>2. To lie down.<BR>	 3. To be concealed.<BR>	 4. To melt away. r. 9th cl.<BR>(लिनाति)<BR>	 1. To join, to adhere or cling to, to be in union or connec-<BR>tion with.<BR>	 2. To obtain.<BR>	 3. To melt.<BR>	 4. To be absorbed. With<BR>वि, To melt away. r. 10th cl. (लयति लाययति-ते लापयति-ते लालयति-ते<BR>लीनयति-ते) To melt, to liquefy, to fuse or dissolve. With आङ्, To<BR>waste away. With प्र and वि, To acquire or gain. According to Pā-<BR>ninī the form लापयते is used in the sense of “To obtain honour.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ली
ली f. (-लीः) Embracing.<BR> E. ली to embrace, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीक्का
लीक्का f. (-क्का) A nit: see लिक्का ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीक्षा
लीक्षा f. (-क्षा) A nit: see लिक्षा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीढ|लीढः
लीढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Eaten.<BR>	 2. Licked.<BR> E. लिह् to lick or taste, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीढमुक्त
लीढमुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Rejected after being tasted.<BR> E. लीढ, मुक्त let go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीन|लीनः
लीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Embraced, clung or adhered to.<BR>	 2. Melted, dis-<BR>solved.<BR>	 3. Dissolved with softness, overcome with passion.<BR>	 4. Dif-<BR>fused.<BR>	 5. Effaced, wiped away, vanished.<BR>	 6. Staying, being situated.<BR>7. Left, departed.<BR>	 8. Lurking, hiding.<BR>	 9. Resting on.<BR>	 10. Absorped,<BR>swallowed up.<BR>	 11. Devoted to.<BR> E. ली to be in contact, &c., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीला
लीला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A branch of feminine action, proceeding from love;<BR>or the imitation of a lover's manner, speech, gait, &c. by his mis-<BR>tress, to pass the time in his absence.<BR>	 2. Play, sport, pastime in<BR>general.<BR>	 3. Amorous or wanton sport.<BR>	 4. Fecility in doing anything.<BR>5. Mien, manner.<BR>	 6. Grace, charm.<BR>	 7. Pretence, disguise, sham.<BR>	 8.<BR>A species of the Dandaka metre.<BR> E. ली to embrace, क्विप् aff., and<BR>ला to get or give, affs. क and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलाकलह|लीलाकलहः
लीलाकलह m. (-हः) A sham quarrel of a coquette with her lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलाखेल
लीलाखेल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Playful.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A species of the Atiśārkarī<BR>metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलाङ्ग|लीलांग
लीलाङ्ग Adj. Having graceful limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलाब्ज
लीलाब्ज n. (-ब्जं) A lotus flower held in the hand as a plaything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलायित|लीलायितं
लीलायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done or written sportively, or in the way<BR>of sport or pleasure.<BR> E. लीला used as a verb, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलावतार|लीलावतारः
लीलावतार m. (-रः) The descent of VIṢṆU on the earth for amusement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलावती
लीलावती f. (-ती) A wanton or sportful woman.<BR> E. लीला, and मतुप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलोद्यान|लीलोद्यानं
लीलोद्यान n. (-न) A pleasure ground.<BR> E. लीला sport, उद्यान a garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लु
लु m. (-लुः) Cutting, lopping, shearing, reaping, &c.<BR> E. लू to cut, aff.<BR>क्विप्, and the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुक्
लुक् Ind. A technical term in Pānini's grammar employed to express<BR>the disappearance of affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुच्
लुच्(इ)लुचि r. 1st cl. (लुञ्चति)<BR>	 1. To cut.<BR>	 2. To pare or peel.<BR>	 3. To tear off, to pluck out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुच्
लुच् f. (-लुक्) Cutting off, dropping, rejecting.<BR> E. लुच् to cut, क्किप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुज्
लुज्(इ)लुजि r. 10th cl. (लुञ्जयति)<BR>	 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To injure.<BR>	 3. To be strong.<BR>4. To dwell.<BR>	 5. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुञ्चित|लुंचित
लुञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cut.<BR>	 2. Peeled.<BR> E. लुच् to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुट्
लुट्(ऌ)लुटॢ r. 1st cl. (लोटति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To resist.<BR>	 3. To suffer<BR>pain. r. 4th cl. (लुट्यति)<BR>	 1. To stir, to agitate.<BR>	 2. To be joined or<BR>connected with.<BR>	 3. To roll upon the ground.<BR>	 4. To rob. r. 1st cl.<BR>(लोटति)<BR>	 1. To resist or oppose.<BR>	 2. To strike again.<BR>	 3. To shine. r.<BR>6th cl. (लुटति) To embrace. r. 10th cl. (लोटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2.<BR>To shine, (इ) लुटि r. 1st and 10th cls. (लुण्टति लुण्टयति)<BR>	 1. To steal,<BR>to rob or plunder.<BR>	 2. To disregard, to disobey or disrespect.<BR>	 3. To<BR>be lame.<BR>	 4. To be idle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुट्यत्
लुट्यत् mfn. (-ठ्यन्-ठ्यन्ती-ठ्यत्) Rolling about, (in pain or grief.)<BR> E. ल्युट to roll about, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठ्
लुठ् r. 1st cl. (लोठति) To knock down. (लोठते)<BR>	 1. To resist or oppose.<BR>2. To suffer pain.<BR>	 3. To roll on the ground. r. 6th cl. (लुठति)<BR>	 1. To<BR>be connected or in contact with, to rest in or on.<BR>	 2. To roll. r. 1st<BR>and 6th cl. (लोठते लुठति)<BR>	 1. To roll on the ground.<BR>	 2. To flow,<BR>to trickle. r. 10th cl. (लोठयति-ते) To rob. (इ) लुठि r. 1st cl. (लुण्ठति)<BR>1. To be lazy.<BR>	 2. To repel, to resist, or oppose.<BR>	 3. To go, to move.<BR>4. To steal.<BR>	 5. To be lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठत्
लुठत् mfn. (-ठन्-ठन्ती-ठत्)<BR>	 1. Rolling on the ground, falling down.<BR>	 2.<BR>Flowing, trickling.<BR> E. लुठ् to roll, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठन|लुठनं
लुठन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A horse's rolling himself on the ground.<BR>	 2. Rolling on<BR>the ground with sorrow or vexation, &c.<BR>	 3. Wallowing.<BR> E. लुट् or<BR>ल्युठ् to cast one's self on the ground, aff. क्युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुठित|लुठितः
लुठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rolling on the ground, (as a horse, &c.)<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तः) A horse's rolling himself on the ground. &c.<BR> E. लुठ् to roll<BR>on the ground, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुड्
लुड् r. 1st cl. (लोडति) To agitate, to stir, to churn. r. 1st and 6th cls.<BR>(लोडति लुडति)<BR>	 1. To be in connection or contact with anything,<BR>to join, to adhere to, to rest in or on, &c.<BR>	 2. To embrace. r. 6th<BR>cl. (लुडति) To cover, to conceal.<BR>	 2. To adhere. (इ) लुडि r. 10th cl.<BR>(लुण्डयति)<BR>	 1. To be agitated.<BR>	 2. To plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्टक|लुण्टकः
लुण्टक m. (-कः) A sort of potherb, (Chironia centauroides, &c.)<BR> E. लुटि<BR>to be prostrate, &c., aff. क्वुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्टा|लुंटा
लुण्टा f. (-ण्टा)<BR>	 1. A horse's rolling himself on the ground.<BR>	 2. Stealing.<BR>E. लुटि or लुठि to roll on the ground, or to rob, affs. अङ् and टाप्;<BR>also लुण्ठा and लुण्ठि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्टाक|लुंटाक|लुण्टाकः
लुण्टाक m. (-कः) A robber, a thief.<BR>	 f. (की) Stealing.<BR> E. लुटि to rob, काकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठत्
लुण्ठत् mfn. (-ण्ठन्-ण्ठन्ती-ण्ठत्) Rolling on the ground.<BR> E. लुठि to roll, &c.,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठन|लुंठन|लुंठनं|लुण्ठनं
लुण्ठन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rolling on the ground.<BR>	 2. Robbing, plundering.<BR> E. लुठि<BR>to roll on the ground, or to rob, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठा|लुंठा
लुण्ठा f. (-ण्ठा)<BR>	 1. Stealing.<BR>	 2. A horse's rolling on the ground: see the<BR>last, and लुण्ठा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठाक|लुंठाक|लुंठाकः|लुण्ठाकः
लुण्ठाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A crow.<BR>	 2. A robber.<BR> E. लुठि to roll, or to rob, काकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्ठी|लुंठी
लुण्ठी f. (-ण्ठी)<BR>	 1. Plundering.<BR>	 2. A horse's rolling himself on the ground.<BR>E. लुठि to roll on the ground, or to rob, affs. अच् and ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्डिका|लुंडिका
लुण्डिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A round mass.<BR>	 2. Fitting conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुण्डी|लुंडी
लुण्डी f. (-ण्डी) Observing the rules of princely conduct, acting and<BR>judging rightly.<BR> E. लुडि to be agitated, &c., affs. अच् and ङीप्;<BR>also with कन् added, fem. form लुण्डिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुथ्
लुथ्(इ)लुथि r. 1st cl. (लुन्थति)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR>2. To afflict.<BR>	 3. To suffer pain or affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्
लुप् r. 4th cl. (लुप्यति)<BR>	 1. To disturb, to bewilder, to perplex, and con-<BR>found the understanding.<BR>	 2. To vanish. (ॡ, औ, ऋ) औलुऌ r. 6th<BR>cl. (लुम्पति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cut, to divide, to cut off or down.<BR>	 2. To rob.<BR>3. To seize.<BR>	 4. To suppress. With वि, 1. To break off.<BR>	 2. To carry<BR>away.<BR>	 3. To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्त|लुप्तं
लुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Gone, lost, disappeared.<BR>	 2. (In grammar,) Cut<BR>off., rejected.<BR>	 n. (-प्तं) Booty, plunder.<BR> E. लुप् to rob, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्तता
लुप्तता f. (-ता) Disappearance, nonexistence.<BR> E. लुप्त, and तल् aff.; also<BR>with त्व, लुप्तत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्तपिण्डोदकक्रिय
लुप्तपिण्डोदकक्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Deprived of funeral rites.<BR> E. लुप्त,<BR>पिण्डोदक cake and water, क्रिया rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुप्तोपमा
लुप्तोपमा f. (-मा) An imperfect comparison in which one or more of the<BR>four requisites are not expressed.<BR> E. लुप्त, and उपमा simile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्
लुब्(इ)लुबि r. 1st and 10th cls. (लुम्बति लुम्बयति-ते) To hurt, to pain, to<BR>afflict or torment. r. 10th cl. (लुम्बयति) To disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्ध|लुब्धः
लुब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Covetous, greedy, desirous, cupidinous.<BR>	 m. (-ब्धः)<BR>1. A hunter.<BR>	 2. A lecher, a libertine.<BR> E. लुभ् to desire, to wish for<BR>vehemently, to covet, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुब्धक|लुब्धकः
लुब्धक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A hunter.<BR>	 2. A libertine, a rake, a whore-monger.<BR>	 3.<BR>A covetous or greedy man.<BR>	 4. The star Sirius.<BR>	 5. A tiger.<BR> E. लुब्ध<BR>desirous, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुभ्
लुभ् r. 4th cl. (लुभ्यति) To desire, to covet. r. 6th cl. (लुभति)<BR>	 1. To be-<BR>wilder, to perplex or delude.<BR>	 2. To desire eagerly.<BR>	 3. To allure.<BR>With प्र or सम्, To attract or allure. Caus. (लोभयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To excite<BR>desire.<BR>	 2. To attract.<BR>	 3. To excite lust.<BR>	 4. To disturb. With वि, 1.<BR>To attract.<BR>	 2. To divert, to amuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुभित|लुभितः
लुभित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Perplexed, deluded, fascinated.<BR> E. लुभ् to fascinate, aff., क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुल्
लुल् r. 1st cl. (लोलति)<BR>	 1. To stir or agitate, to make tremulous.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be attached to or connected with, to join.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुलाप|लुलापः
लुलाप m. (-पः) A buffalo.<BR> E. लुल् to agitate, aff. क, stirring, shaking,<BR>(in the mud,) आप् to get or obtain, aff. अण्; it is also read लुलाय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुलित|लुलितः
लुलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken, trembling, tremulous, agitated, stirred.<BR>2. Heaving, panting.<BR>	 3. Agreeable, pleasing, beautiful, elegant.<BR>	 4.<BR>Injured, destroyed.<BR>	 5. Coming in contact.<BR> E. लुल् to agitate, aff. क्तं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुष्
लुष् r. 1st and 10th cls. (लोषति लोषयति)<BR>	 1. To rob, to steal.<BR>	 2. To hurt,<BR>to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुषभ|लुषभः
लुषभ m. (-भः) An elephant in rut.<BR> E. रुष् to be enraged, Unādi aff.<BR>अभच्, with लुष् substituted for the root, and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लुह्
लुह् r. 1st cl. (लोहति) To covet, to wish for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लू
लू r. 6th cl. (लुनाति लुनीते)<BR>	 1. To cut.<BR>	 2. To sever. With आ, To pluck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूता
लूता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A spider.<BR>	 2. An ant.<BR>	 3. Local inflammation produced<BR>by the urine of a spider.<BR> E. लू to cut, तक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूतिका
लूतिका f. (-का) A spider.<BR> E. लूता a spider, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लून|लूनः
लून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Cut.<BR>	 2. Wounded.<BR>	 3. Cut off.<BR>	 4. Plucked.<BR>	 5.<BR>Bitten, nibbled.<BR> E. लू to cut, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूनक|लूनकः
लूनक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An animal.<BR>	 2. Sort, species, difference.<BR>	 3. A wound,<BR>a division, what is cut or broken.<BR> E. लून to cut, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूनि|लूनिः
लूनि f. (-निः) Cutting, reaping.<BR> E. लू to cut, aff. क्तिन्, and न substituted<BR>for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूम|लूमं
लूम n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. A tail.<BR>	 2. A hairy tail, as a horse's, a monkey's, &c.<BR> E. लू to cut, aff. मक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूमविष|लूमविषः
लूमविष m. (-षः) Any animal that stings with its tail, as a scorpion,<BR>&c.<BR> E. लूम a tail, and विष venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लूष्
लूष् r. 1st cl. (लूषति) To adorn, to decorate. r. 10th cl. (लूषयति-ते)<BR>	 1.<BR>To hurt, to injure.<BR>	 2. To steal, to rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लृञ्च्
लृञ्च् r. 1st cl. (लृञ्चति) To put away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख|लेखः
लेख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A letter, an epistle.<BR>	 2. A god, a deity.<BR>	 f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A<BR>line, a mark or row, &c.<BR>	 2. Writing, hand-writing.<BR>	 3. Delineation,<BR>painting.<BR>	 4. A likeness, an impression.<BR>	 5. Hem, border.<BR>	 6. The<BR>moon's crescent.<BR> E. लिख् to write, aff. घञ्; it is applied to the<BR>second sense, because the figures of the gods are written or deli-<BR>neated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखक|लेखकः
लेखक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A writer, a scribe, a clerk, a copyist, &c.<BR>	 2. A painter.<BR> E. लिख to write, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखन|लेखनं|लेखनः
लेखन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Writing, scripture.<BR>	 2. The bark of the Bhurja-tree,<BR>which is used for writing on in Nepāland Upper Hindusthan.<BR>	 3.<BR>Vomiting.<BR>	 4. The leaf of the palm tree.<BR>	 5. Scraping or cleaning the<BR>tongue.<BR>	 6. Scarifying, scratching.<BR>	 7. Reducing corpulency, thinning.<BR>m. (-नः) A sort of grass or reed, of which pens are made, (Sac-<BR>charum spontaneum.)<BR>	 f. (-नी) A pen, a style.<BR> E. लिख् to write, aff.<BR>of the act or instrument ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनवस्ति|लेखनवस्तिः
लेखनवस्ति f. (-स्तिः) Use of enemas to reduce corpulency.<BR> E. लेखन, and वस्ति a glyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनिक|लेखनिकः
लेखनिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A letter-carrier, an express, a postman.<BR>	 2. One<BR>who signs a paper by proxy, who makes his mark, from inability<BR>to write, &c.<BR> E. लेखन writing, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख|लेखः
लेख(खि)नी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A pen, a writing-reed.<BR>	 2. A spoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखनीय|लेखनीयः
लेखनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be written.<BR>	 n. (-यं) An accusation or defence<BR>in law, which are required to be given in writing.<BR> E. लिख् to<BR>write, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखर्षभ|लेखर्षभः
लेखर्षभ m. (-भः) INDRA.<BR> E. लेख a deity, and ऋषभ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखहार|लेखहारः
लेखहार m. (-रः) A letter-carrier.<BR> E. लेख a letter, हृ to convey, aff. अण्;<BR>also with कन् added लेखहारक, or with णिनि, लेखहारिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेखित|लेखितं
लेखित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Written.<BR> E. लिख् to write, क्त aff., and the<BR>vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्य|लेख्यं
लेख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं) To be written.<BR>	 2. To be scarified.<BR>	 n. (-ख्यं)<BR>1. A letter, an epistle.<BR>	 2. A manuscript.<BR>	 3. A drawing, a delinea-<BR>tion.<BR>	 4. A written accusation or defence.<BR> E. लिख् to write, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यक
लेख्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Written, in writing, epistolary.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यकृत
लेख्यकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done in writing, contracted, executed.<BR> E. लेख्य and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यचूर्णिका
लेख्यचूर्णिका f. (-का) A painted brush, a pencil.<BR> E. लेख्य a delineation,<BR>चूर्ण् to pound or grind, affs. वुन् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यपत्र|लेख्यपत्रः
लेख्यपत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A leaf or sheet of anything for writing.<BR>	 2. A<BR>written paper, a writing, a letter.<BR> E. लेख्य, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यपत्रक
लेख्यपत्रक m. (-कः) The palm tree.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A leaf of the palm or any<BR>other substance used for writing on.<BR> E. लेख्य writing, पत्र a leaf,<BR>कन् aff.; books in south of India, &c., being made of the leaves<BR>of the palmyra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यप्रसङ्ग|लेख्यप्रसंगः
लेख्यप्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Written contract, record, or document.<BR> E. लेख्य, प्रसङ्ग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यस्थान|लेख्यस्थानं
लेख्यस्थान n. (-नं) An office, a counting-house, &c.<BR> E. लेख्य writing or<BR>what is to be written, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेख्यारूढ
लेख्यारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Recorded, committed to writing.<BR> E. लेख्य, आरूढ mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेण्ड|लेंड|लेंडं|लेण्डं
लेण्ड n. (-ण्डं) Excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेत|लेतं|लेतः
लेत mn. (-तः-तं) Tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्
लेप्(ऋ)लेपृ r. 1st cl. (लेपते) To go, to approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप|लेपः
लेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Plastering, smearing.<BR>	 2. Food.<BR>	 3. Mortar, plaster,<BR>Chunam.<BR>	 4. Stain, spot, smearing.<BR>	 5. The wipings of the hand<BR>which has offered funeral oblations to three ancestors, and which<BR>are considered as an oblation to ancestors in the 4th, 5th, and 6th<BR>degrees.<BR>	 6. Pollution, impurity.<BR>	 7. Sin.<BR> E. लिप् or लेप् to smear,<BR>&c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपक|लेपकः
लेपक m. (-कः) A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR> E. लिप् to smear, (Chunam,) ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपन|लेपनं|लेपनः
लेपन m. (-नः) Incense.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Smearing, plastering, anointing.<BR>	 2.<BR>An ointment.<BR>	 3. Flesh.<BR> E. लिप् to smear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपभागिन्
लेपभागिन् m. (-गी) An ancestor in the 4th, 5th, and 6th degrees. E.<BR>लेप, भागिन् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपभुज
लेपभुज m. (-भुक्) A paternal ancestor of the 4th, 5th, or 6th degree.<BR> E. लेप, भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेपिन्
लेपिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Who or what smears, plasters, anoints, &c.<BR>m. (-पी) A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR> E. लेप् to plaster, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्य|लेप्यं
लेप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be spread, as unguent or plaster, to be<BR>anointed or plastered.<BR>	 n. (-प्यं)<BR>	 1. Plastering, spreading or smearing<BR>ointment, mortar, &c.<BR>	 2. Making models, moulding.<BR> E. लिप् to<BR>plaster, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्यकृत्
लेप्यकृत् m. (-कृत्) A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR> E. लेप्य plastering, कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्यमयी
लेप्यमयी f. (-यी) A doll, a puppet.<BR> E. लेप्य plastering, मयट् aff., made of<BR>wood with a coat of plaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेप्यस्त्री
लेप्यस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) A woman, perfumed with fragrant unguents.<BR> E. लेप्य plastering, स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलायमाना
लेलायमाना f. (-ना) One of the seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिह|लेलिहः
लेलिह m. (-हः) A worm breeding in the stomach.<BR> E. लिह् to lick, root redup क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेलिहान|लेलिहानः
लेलिहान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Who or what licks.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A snake.<BR> E. लिह् to lick, aff. शानच्, root redup. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेश|लेशः
लेश Adj. Masc. only. (-शः) Small, little. Subst.<BR>	 1. Smallness, littleness.<BR>2. A little.<BR>	 3. A particular measure of time equal to two Kalās.<BR>4. Name of a figure of speech, (in rhetoric.)<BR> E. लिश् to be small,<BR>aff. घञ्. Some authorities vary the gender of the attribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेशोक्त
लेशोक्त Adj. Hinted at, insinuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेश्या
लेश्या f. (-श्या) Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेष्टु|लेष्टुः
लेष्टु m. (-ष्टुः) A clod of earth.<BR> E. लिश् to become less or small, तुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेष्टुघ्न|लेष्टुघ्नः
लेष्टुघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A harrow.<BR> E. लेष्टु a clod of earth, and घ्न destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेष्टुभेदन|लेष्टुभेदनः
लेष्टुभेदन m. (-नः) A harrow.<BR> E. लेष्टु a clod of earth, and भेदन breaking;<BR>also लेष्टुभेदिन् and लोष्टभेदन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेसिक|लेसिकः
लेसिक m. (-कः) The rider on an elephant, who sits on the animal's loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेह|लेहः
लेह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Food.<BR>	 2. Licking, tasting.<BR> E. लिह् to taste, aff. घञ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहन|लेहनं
लेहन n. (-नं) Licking, tasting with the tongue.<BR> E. लिह् to taste, to<BR>lick, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहिन्
लेहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Who or what licks, laps, tastes, &c.<BR> E. लिह् to lick, aff. घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेहिन|लेहिनः
लेहिन m. (-नः) Borax.<BR> E. लिह् to lick, aff. इनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लेह्य|लेह्यं
लेह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be licked.<BR>	 n. (-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. The food or beverage<BR>of the gods, nectar, ambrosia.<BR>	 2. Syrup, electuary.<BR> E. लिह् to<BR>taste, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैङ्गिक|लैंगिक|लैङ्गिकः
लैङ्गिक f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Depending on a mark, &c.<BR>	 2. Inferred.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A statuary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लैण्
लैण्(ऋ)लैणृ r. 1st cl. (लैनति)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To command or<BR>direct an act.<BR>	 3. To touch or embrace.<BR>	 4. To pound or grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोक्
लोक्(ऋ)लोकृ r. 1st cl. (लोकते) To see. With अव, To see, to perceive.<BR>With आ, To view. r. 10th cl. (लोकयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To shine.<BR>3. To know.<BR>	 4. To look. With अव, 1. To see.<BR>	 2. To learn.<BR>	 3.<BR>To look after. With आ, 1. To see.<BR>	 2. To know.<BR>	 3. To regard as.<BR>With वि, 1. To perceive.<BR>	 2. To search.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोक|लोकः
लोक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Man, mankind.<BR>	 2. A world, a division of the universe;<BR>in general three Lokas are enumerated; viz:--heaven, hell, and<BR>earth: another classification enumerates seven, exclusive of the<BR>infernal regions; viz:--Bhūr-loka the earth, Bhūvar-loka the<BR>space between the earth and the sun, the region of the Munis,<BR>Siddhas, &c.; Swar-loka the heaven of INDRA, between the sun<BR>and the polar star; Mahar-loka the usual abode of BHRIGU, and<BR>others saints, who are supposed to be co-existent with BRAHMĀ:<BR>during the conflagration of these lower worlds, the saints ascend<BR>to the next, or Jana-loka, which is described as the abode of BRAH-<BR>MĀ'S sons, SANAKA, SĀNANDA, SANĀTANA, and SANATKUMĀRA;<BR>above this, is the fifth world or the Tapo-loka, where the deities called<BR>Vairāgis reside; the seventh world, Satya-loka or Brahma-loka,<BR>is the abode of BRAHMĀ, and translation to this world exempts<BR>beings from further birth: the three first worlds are destroyed at<BR>the end of each Kalpa or day of BRAHMĀ; the three last at the<BR>end of his life, or of 100 of his years; the fourth Loka is equally<BR>permanent, but is uninhabitable from heat, at the time the three<BR>first are burning: another enumeration calls these seven worlds,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">Page621-a+ 60</a>]<BR>earth, sky, heaven, middle region, place of births, mansion of the<BR>blest, and abode of truth, placing the sons of BRAHMĀ in the<BR>sixth division, and stating the fifth or Jana-loka to be that,<BR>where animals destroyed in the general conflagration are born<BR>again. The seven lower regions descending from the earth one<BR>below the other are:--ATALA, BITALA, SŪTALA, RASĀTALA,<BR>TALĀTALA, MAHĀTALA, PĀTĀLA, respectively.<BR>	 3. The human race.<BR>4. The earth.<BR>	 5. The subjects.<BR>	 6. A class, a community.<BR>	 7. A<BR>region.<BR>	 8. The number “seven.” 9. Common life, or usage, (oppo-<BR>rite to Shāstra and Veda respectively.)<BR>	 10. Sight, seeing.<BR>	 11. An<BR>element, a primary or radical part of being.<BR> E. लोक् to see, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककृत्
लोककृत् m. (-कृत्) The Creator, BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. लोक and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकगाथा
लोकगाथा f. (-था) A song current among people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकचक्षुस्
लोकचक्षुस् m. (-क्षुः) The sun.<BR> E. लोक the world, चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकचरित्र
लोकचरित्र n. (-त्रं) The ways of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकजित्
लोकजित् m. (-जित्)<BR>	 1. A conqueror of the world.<BR>	 2. A sage.<BR>	 3. A Bud-<BR>dha or Bauddha deified teacher.<BR> E. लोक the world, and जित्<BR>who conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकज्ञ
लोकज्ञ Adj. Conversant with the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकतत्व
लोकतत्व n. (-त्वं) Knowledge of mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकतुषार|लोकतुषारः
लोकतुषार m. (-रः) Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकत्रय
लोकत्रय n. (-यं-यी) The three worlds, heaven, earth, and hell.<BR> E. लोक, and त्रय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकद्वार
लोकद्वार n. (-रं) The gate of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकधातु|लोकधातुः
लोकधातु m. (-तुः) A continent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकनाथ|लोकनाथः
लोकनाथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A sovereign of the universe.<BR>	 2. One of the Jaina<BR>or Bauddhha saints.<BR> E. लोक the world, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकनीय
लोकनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Visible, to be seen.<BR> E. लोक् to see, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपाल|लोकपालः
लोकपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A king, a sovereign.<BR>	 2. A divinity who protects<BR>the regions, or the sun, moon, fire, wind, INDRA, YAMA, VARUṆA,<BR>and KUVERA.<BR> E. लोक the world, पाल a cherisher; also लोकपालक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकप्रकाशन|लोकप्रकाशनः
लोकप्रकाशन m. (-नः) The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकप्रवाद|लोकप्रवादः
लोकप्रवाद m. (-दः) Common or current report or saying.<BR> E. लोक, and<BR>प्रवाद report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकप्रसिद्ध
लोकप्रसिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Notorious, well-known.<BR> E. लोक, प्रसिद्ध celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकबान्धव|लोकबांधव|लोकबान्धवः
लोकबान्धव m. (-वः) The sun.<BR> E. लोक the world, and बान्धव the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकमर्य्यादा|लोकमर्यादा
लोकमर्य्यादा f. (-दा) Established custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकमातृ
लोकमातृ f. (-ता) LAKṢMĪ, the wife of VIṢṆU, and goddess of wealth<BR>and fortune.<BR> E. लोक the world, and मातृ the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकयात्रा
लोकयात्रा f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. Worldly affairs, civil conduct, usage, practice.<BR>	 2.<BR>Resort of men, traffic, intercourse.<BR> E. लोक, यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकरञ्जन|लोकरंजन
लोकरञ्जन n. (-नं) Popularity, gaining public confidence.<BR> E. लोक, रञ्जन pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकरव|लोकरवः
लोकरव m. (-वः) Popular report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकलोचन|लोकलोचनं
लोकलोचन m. (-नः) The sun.<BR> E. लोक the world, and लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवाद|लोकवादः
लोकवाद m. (-दः) Rumour, popular report.<BR> E. लोक, वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवाह्य
लोकवाह्य m. (-ह्यः) An outcaste, one who observes no sort of institutes,<BR>and feeds on the flesh of horses and kine.<BR> E. लोक mankind, वाह्य<BR>for वहिर् without, excluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविक्रुष्ट
लोकविक्रुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Censured or condemned by the world.<BR> E. लोक, विक्रुष्ट censured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविधि|लोकविधिः
लोकविधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Mode of proceeding prevalent in the world.<BR>	 2.<BR>The creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविश्रुत
लोकविश्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, famous.<BR>	 2. Current.<BR> E. लोक and विश्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविश्रुति|लोकविश्रुतिः
लोकविश्रुति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Unfounded rumour or report.<BR>	 2. Fame, notoriety.<BR>E. लोक the world, विश्रुति rumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवृत्त
लोकवृत्त n. (-त्तं) Worldly or idle conversation and intercourse.<BR> E. लोक, वृत्त practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकातिग
लोकातिग Adj. Extraordinary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकातिशय
लोकातिशय Adj. Superior to the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकात्मन्
लोकात्मन् m. (-त्मा) The universal spirit.<BR> E. लोक, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकानुराग|लोकानुरागः
लोकानुराग m. (-गः) Philanthrophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकान्तर|लोकांतर
लोकान्तर n. (-रं) Another world.<BR> E. लोक, and अन्तर other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकान्तरगत
लोकान्तरगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dead.<BR> E. लोकान्तर, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकान्तरप्राप्त
लोकान्तरप्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Dead.<BR> E. लोकान्तर, and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकापवाद|लोकापवादः
लोकापवाद m. (-दः) Popular accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकाभ्युदय|लोकाभ्युदयः
लोकाभ्युदय m. (-यः) Public welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायत|लोकायतं|लोकायतः
लोकायत n. (-तं) The system of atheistical philosophy taught by<BR>Chārvāka.<BR> E. लोक the world, आङ् before, यति to strive, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायतिक|लोकायतिकः
लोकायतिक m. (-कः) A follower of the Chārvāka doctrine, an atheist,<BR>an unbeliever.<BR> E. लोकायत as above, and ठक् aff. with the vowel<BR>unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकालोक|लोकालोकः
लोकालोक m. (-कः) A mountainous belt, surrounding the outermost of<BR>the seven seas and bounding the world.<BR>	 m. DU. The visible and<BR>unvisible world.<BR> E. लोक seeing, आलोक not seeing; causing light<BR>and darkness, as interposed between the Dwīpas and the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकित
लोकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Seen, beheld.<BR> E. लोक् to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकेश|लोकेशः
लोकेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A king, an emperor.<BR>	 3. A Jaina deified<BR>sage.<BR>	 4. Quicksilver.<BR> E. लोक the world, and ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकेश्वर|लोकेश्वरः
लोकेश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR>	 3. A Jaina deified sage.<BR> E. लोक<BR>the world, and ईश्वर sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकेश्वरात्मजा
लोकेश्वरात्मजा f. (-जा) A female deity peculiar to the Jainas.<BR> E. लोकेश्वर a<BR>Jaina sage, and आत्मजा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोच्
लोच्(ऋ)लोचृ r. 1st cl. (लोचते) To see, to perceive, to view or inspect. r.<BR>10th cl. (लोचयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To shine. With आङ्, To<BR>consider. Caus. (लोचयति-ते) To cause to see. With आ, 1. To know.<BR>2. To see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोच|लोचं
लोच n. (-चं) Tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचक|लोचकः
लोचक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A ball or lump of flesh or meat.<BR>	 2. The pupil of the<BR>eye.<BR>	 3. Stibium or lamp-black, &c. so used.<BR>	 4. An ornament, worn<BR>by women on the forehead.<BR>	 5. Blue or black vesture.<BR>	 6. An ear-<BR>ring.<BR>	 7. The plantain tree.<BR>	 8. A bow-string.<BR>	 9. A wrinkled or con-<BR>tracted eyebrow.<BR>	 10. Folly, stupidity.<BR>	 11. The rejected slough of<BR>the snake.<BR>	 12. The slough of a tree.<BR>	 13. Wrinkled skin.<BR> E. लोच् to<BR>see, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचन|लोचनं
लोचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The eye.<BR>	 2. Seeing, looking.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A goddess of<BR>the Jainas.<BR> E. लोच् to see, ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचनमार्ग|लोचनमार्गः
लोचनमार्ग m. (-र्गः) The range of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचनहिता
लोचनहिता f. (-ता) Blue vitriol. “तुंँत इति भाषा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचनामय|लोचनामयः
लोचनामय m. (-यः) Diseased affection of the eye, Ophthalmia, &c. E.<BR>लोचन eye, आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचमर्कट|लोचमर्कटः
लोचमर्कट m. (-टः) A flower, (Celosia cristata.) “रुद्रजटा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोचमस्तक|लोचमस्तकः
लोचमस्तक m. (-कः) A flower, (Celosia cristata.)<BR> E. लोच sight, seeing, मस्तक head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोट्
लोट् (ऋ) लोटृ r. 1st cl. (लोटति) To be mad or foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोटन|लोटनं
लोटन n. (-नं) Tumbling, rolling.<BR> E. लुट् to roll, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोठ|लोठः
लोठ m. (-ठः) Rolling on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोड्
लोड् (ऋ) लोडृ r. 1st cl. (लोडति) To mad, to be frantic or foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोडन|लोडनं
लोडन n. (-नं) Disturbing, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोणार|लोणारं|लोणारः
लोणार m. (-रः) A kind of salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोत|लोतं|लोतः
लोत mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>	 1. Plunder, booty, stolen goods.<BR>	 2. A tear, tears.<BR>	 3.<BR>A mark, a spot, a sign.<BR> E. लू to cut, Undādi aff. तन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोत्र|लोत्रं
लोत्र n. (-त्रं) Plunder, booty, stolen goods.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. Tears.<BR>	 2. A<BR>mark, a token.<BR> E. लू to cut, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोध|लोधः
लोध m. (-धः) A sort of tree with white or red flowers.: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोध्र|लोध्रः
लोध्र m. (-ध्रः) A tree, the bark of which is used in dyeing, (Sym-<BR>plocos racemosa.)<BR> E. रुध् to hinder, aff. रन्, and ल substituted for र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप|लोपः
लोप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Rejection, cutting off in general, especially used as a<BR>grammatical term for dropping letters, syllables, &c.<BR>	 2. Dis-<BR>appearance, destruction.<BR>	 3. Erasure.<BR>	 4. Annulling, cancelling. E.<BR>लुप् to cut, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपन|लोपनं
लोपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Violation.<BR>	 2. Omission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपा
लोपा f. (-पा) The wife of the Muni AGASTYA.<BR> E. लुप् to disturb, affs.<BR>अच् and टाप्ः see लोपामुद्रा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपाक|लोपाकः
लोपाक m. (-कः) A jackal.<BR> E. लुप् to cut, आकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपापक|लोपापकः
लोपापक m. (-कः) A jackal.<BR>	 f. (-पिका) A fox.<BR> E. लोप rejection, (offal,)<BR>आप् to take, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपामुद्रा
लोपामुद्रा f. (-द्रा) The wife of the saint AGASTYA and daughter of the<BR>king of Vidarbha. It was for her that the saint went out to<BR>acquire riches and destroyed VĀTĀPI and ILVALA in the attempt.<BR>E. लोप losing, (reputation,) अमुद्रा sad, not happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपामुद्रापति|लोपामुद्रापतिः
लोपामुद्रापति m. (-तिः) The Muni AGASTYA.<BR> E. लोपामुद्रा as above, पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोपाशक|लोपाशकः
लोपाशक m. (-कः) A jackal.<BR>	 f. (-शिका)<BR>	 1. A female jackal.<BR>	 2. A fox.<BR>E. लोप rejection, अश् to eat, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप्य
लोप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be rejected, erased, lost, &c.<BR> E. लुप् to cut off, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोप्त्र|लोप्त्रं
लोप्त्र nf. (-प्त्रं-प्त्री) Plunder, booty.<BR> E. लुप् to cut off, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभ|लोभः
लोभ m. (-भः) Covetousness, cupidity, intense or greedy desire.<BR> E. लुभ्<BR>to desire or covet, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभन
लोभन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Allurement, temptation.<BR>	 2. Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभमोहित
लोभमोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Beguiled or overcome by cupidity.<BR> E. लोभ, मोहित beguiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभविरह|लोभविरहः
लोभविरह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Free from cupidity.<BR> E. लोभ, विरह separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभाकृष्ट
लोभाकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Tempted or attracted by greediness or desire.<BR>E. लोभ, आकृष्ट drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभिन्
लोभिन् mfn. (-भी-भिनी-भि) Desirous, cupidinous, covetous, greedy. E.<BR>लोभ desire, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोभ्य|लोभ्यः
लोभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं) Desirable.<BR>	 m. (-भ्यः) A sort of bean, (Phaseolus<BR>mungo.)<BR>	 n. (-भ्यं) A tail.<BR> E. लुभ् to covet or desire, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोम|लोमं|लोमः
लोम m. (-मः) A tail, a hairy tail.<BR> E. लू to cut, aff. मन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमकर्ण|लोमकर्णः
लोमकर्ण m. (-र्णः) A hare.<BR> E. लोम hair, कर्ण an ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमकिन्
लोमकिन् m. (-की) A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमकीट|लोमकीटः
लोमकीट m. (-टः) A louse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमकूप|लोमकूपः
लोमकूप m. (-पः) A pore of the skin.<BR> E. लोम, and कूप a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमघ्न|लोमघ्नं
लोमघ्न n. (-घ्नं) Falling of the hair, morbid baldness.<BR> E. लोम hair of the<BR>body, applied here to the hair of the head, and घ्न destroying. “टाक”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमन्
लोमन् n. (-म) The hair of the body.<BR> E. रू to sound, मनिन् Unādi aff.,<BR>र changed to ल; or लू to cut, मनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमपाद|लोमपादः
लोमपाद m. (-दः) The name of a king of Anga, the eastern division of Bengal, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमपादपुरी
लोमपादपुरी f. (-री) Champā, the capital of Lomapāda, the modern<BR>Bhāgalpur, and its vicinity.<BR> E. लोमपाद a king, and पुरी the city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोममणि|लोममणिः
लोममणि m. (-णिः) An amulet made of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमविष|लोमविषः
लोमविष m. (-षः) An animal, whose hair is supposed to be poisonous,<BR>as a tiger, &c.<BR> E. लोम hair, and विष poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमश|लोमशः
लोमश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Hairy, covered with or made of hair.<BR>	 2. Wool-<BR>len.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A ram.<BR>	 2. The name of a Ṛṣi celebrated in the<BR>Mahābhārata.<BR>	 f. (-शा)<BR>	 1. A fox.<BR>	 2. A sort of Bonduc.<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>(Leea hirta.)<BR>	 4. Indian spikenard, (Valerianā jatāmānsi.)<BR>	 5.<BR>Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>	 6. A medicinal plant, commonly<BR>Mahā-meda.<BR>	 7. Sida cordifolia.<BR>	 8. A female demi-divine being,<BR>an attendant on DURGĀ, one of the Sākinīs.<BR>	 9. Green vitriol.<BR>	 10.<BR>Orris root.<BR>	 11. An ape.<BR> E. लोम hair, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमशपर्णिनी
लोमशपर्णिनी f. (-नी) A plant, (Glycine debilis.)<BR> E. लोमश hairy, पर्ण a leaf, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमशमार्जार|लोमशमार्जारः|लोमशमार्ज्जारः
लोमशमार्जार m. (-रः) The pole-cat.<BR> E. लोमश hairy, and मार्जार a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमसंहर्षण
लोमसंहर्षण Adj. Causing horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमसार|लोमसारः
लोमसार m. (-रः) The emerald.<BR> E. लोम hair, and सार strength, essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमहर्षण|लोमहर्षणं|लोमहर्षणः
लोमहर्षण n. (-णं) Horripilation, erection of the hair of the body.<BR> E. लोम,<BR>हर्षण rejoicing, supposed to be an indication of great pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमहृत्
लोमहृत् mfn. (-हृत्) Depilatory.<BR>	 m. (-हृत्) Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. लोम hair,<BR>and हृत् removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमाञ्च|लोमांच|लोमाञ्चः
लोमाञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) Horripilation: see रोमाञ्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमालिका
लोमालिका f. (-का) A fox.<BR> E. लोम hair, आलो a line, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमावली
लोमावली f. (-ली) The line of hair from the breast to the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोमाश|लोमाशः
लोमाश m. (-शः) A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोल|लोलः
लोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Shaking, tremulous.<BR>	 2. Rolling, tossing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Agitated, alarmed.<BR>	 4. Fickle, unsteady.<BR>	 5. Desiring, wishing, cup-<BR>idinous.<BR>	 6. Greedy.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The tongue.<BR>	 2. The goddess<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">Page622-b+ 60</a>]<BR>LAKṢMĪ, or the goddess of wealth and fortune.<BR>	 3. A species of<BR>the Sarkarī metre.<BR>	 4. Lightning.<BR> E. लोड् to be frantic, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलजिह्व
लोलजिह्व mfn. (-ह्वः-ह्वा-ह्वं) Greedy, insatiable.<BR> E. लोल, जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलमान
लोलमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Rolling, tossing, rolling on the ground.<BR> E. लोड्<BR>to be frantic, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलाक्षि
लोलाक्षि mfn. (-क्षिः-क्षिः or क्षी-क्षि) Having a rolling eye.<BR> E. लोल, and अक्षि<BR>the eye; also लोलचक्षुस्, लोलनयन, लोललोचन, लोलनेत्र, and the like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलिका
लोलिका f. (-का) A sort of dock or sorrel, (Rumex vesicarius.) “पातिहांँस”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलित|लोलितः
लोलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, tremulous, trembling.<BR> E. लुल् to agitate,<BR>aff. क्त, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुप|लोलुपः
लोलुप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Very desirous or covetous, wishing, longing for,<BR>greedy, insatiable.<BR> E. लुप् to desire, aff. अच्, and the intensitive form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुभ|लोलुभः
लोलुभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Very cupidinous, excessively desirous, very<BR>covetous or greedy.<BR> E. लुभ् to desire or covet, aff. अच्, int. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलुव
लोलुव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Cutting much or often.<BR> E. लू to cut, freq. v., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलूया
लोलूया f. (-या) Determination to cut.<BR> E. लू to cut, intensitive v., अङ्<BR>and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलूयावत्
लोलूयावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Resolved to cut or cut off.<BR> E. लोलूया, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्ट्
लोष्ट् r. 1st cl. (लोष्टते) To heap, to assemble, to collect into a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्ट|लोष्टं|लोष्टः
लोष्ट mn. (-ष्टः-ष्टं) A lump of earth.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) Rust of iron or iron<BR>filings.<BR> E. लोष्ट् to heap, aff. अच्; or लू to cut, Unādi aff. क्त, with<BR>change of the radical vowel, सुट् aug.; also with कन् added लोष्टक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टघ्न|लोष्टघ्नः
लोष्टघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A harrow.<BR> E. लोष्ट a clod, and घ्न destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टभेदन|लोष्टभेदनः
लोष्टभेदन m. (-नः) A harrow.<BR> E. लोष्ट a clod, and भेदन what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टमय
लोष्टमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of a clod or of earth.<BR> E. लोष्ट and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टमर्द्दिन्|लोष्टमर्दिन्
लोष्टमर्द्दिन् mfn. (-र्द्दी-र्द्दिनी-र्द्दि) Who or what breaks clods of earth. E.<BR>लोष्ट, and मर्द्दिन् who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोष्टु|लोष्टुः
लोष्टु m. (-ष्टुः) A lump of earth.<BR> E. लोष्ट् to heap, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोह|लोहं|लोहः
लोह mn. (-हः-हं)<BR>	 1. Iron, either crude or wrought.<BR>	 2. Steel.<BR>	 3. Any<BR>metal.<BR>	 4. A weapon.<BR>	 5. Aloe-wood or Agallochum.<BR>	 6. Blood.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-हः) A red coloured goat.<BR>	 f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. Red, reddish.<BR>	 2. Made of cop-<BR>per or iron.<BR> E. लू to cut, aff. ह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहकण्टक|लोहकण्टकः
लोहकण्टक m. (-कः) A thorny shrub.<BR> E. लोह iron, कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहकान्त|लोहकांत|लोहकान्तं|लोहकान्तः
लोहकान्त n. (-न्तं) The load-stone.<BR> E. लोह iron, कान्त in this compound a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहकार|लोहकारः
लोहकार m. (-रः) A blacksmith, an ironsmith.<BR> E. लोह iron, कार who<BR>works in; also with कन् added लोहकारक m. (-कः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहकिट्ट|लोहकिट्टं
लोहकिट्ट n. (-ट्टं) Rust of iron, or iron filings.<BR> E. लोह, किट्ट soil or sediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहचूर्ण|लोहचूर्णं
लोहचूर्ण n. (-र्णं) Iron filings.<BR> E. लोह, चूर्ण powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहज|लोहजं
लोहज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Bell-metal.<BR>	 2. Rust of iron, or iron filings.<BR> E. लोह, ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहजाल
लोहजाल n. (-लं) A coat of mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहजित्
लोहजित् m. (-जित्) The diamond.<BR> E. लोह iron, and जित् conquering, (in hardness.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहदारक|लोहदारकः
लोहदारक n. (-कं) A hell.<BR> E. लोह and दारक what tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहद्राविन्
लोहद्राविन् m. (-वी) Borax.<BR> E. लोह metal, and द्राविन् what fuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहनाल|लोहनालः
लोहनाल m. (-लः) An iron arrow.<BR> E. लोह iron, and नाल a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहपृष्ठ|लोहपृष्ठः
लोहपृष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A heron.<BR> E. लोह iron, पृष्ठ the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहप्रतिमा
लोहप्रतिमा f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. An image of iron.<BR>	 2. An anvil.<BR> E. लोह iron, प्रतिमा an image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहबन्ध|लोहबंध
लोहबन्ध m. (-न्धः) An iron fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहमय|लोहमयं
लोहमय mfn. (-यः-यो-यं) Made of iron.<BR> E. लोह iron, aff. मयट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहमारक|लोहमारकः
लोहमारक m. (-कः) A plant (Achyrantnes triandra, Rox.) “शालिञ्चशाके”<BR>E. लोह iron, मारक destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहमुक्तिका
लोहमुक्तिका f. (-का) A red pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहराजक
लोहराजक n. (-कं) Silver.<BR> E. लोह metal, राज shining, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहल|लोहलः
लोहल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Lisping, speaking inarticulately.<BR>	 2. Iron,<BR>irony.<BR>	 m. (-लः) The principal ring of a chain.<BR> E. लोह iron, ला to<BR>get or be, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहवर|लोहवरं
लोहवर n. (-रं) Gold.<BR> E. लोह a metal, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहवर्म्मन्|लोहवर्मन्
लोहवर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Mail, armour.<BR> E. लोह, and वर्म्मन् armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहशङ्कु|लोहशंकु|लोहशङ्कुः
लोहशङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>	 1. A hell.<BR>	 2. An iron pike.<BR> E. लोह, शङ्कु a pike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहश्लेषण|लोहश्लेषणः
लोहश्लेषण m. (-णः) Borax.<BR> E. लोह metal, श्लिष् to embrace, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहाभिसा
लोहाभिसा(हा)र m. (-रः) Lustration of arms, ceremonies performed on the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">Page623-a+ 60</a>]<BR>ninth of the light-half of the month Ashwin; formerly a celebration<BR>observed by princes before opening a campaign, but now confined<BR>to the domestic decoration and worship of the soldier's weapon.<BR>E. लोह a weapon, अभि about, सृ to go, or हृ to take, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहाभिहार|लोहाभिहारः
लोहाभिहार m. (-रः) Lustration of arms.<BR> E. लोह, a weapon, अभि about,<BR>हृ to take, aff. घञ्; also लोहाभिसार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहामिष|लोहामिषः
लोहामिष n. (-षं) The flesh of a goat with red hair.<BR> E. लोह, आमिष flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिका
लोहिका f. (-का) A sort of large shallow bowl, sometimes of iron, but<BR>usually of wood and bound with iron, for the purpose of washing<BR>rice, &c.<BR> E. लोह iron, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहित|लोहितं|लोहितः
लोहित mfn. (-तः-ता or नी-तं)<BR>	 1. Red, of a red colour.<BR>	 2. Made of copper.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Red, the colour.<BR>	 2. The planet MARS.<BR>	 3. One of the male<BR>rivers.<BR>	 4. The Rohi-fish, (Cyprinus Rohita, HAM.)<BR>	 5. A sort of deer.<BR>6. A snake.<BR>	 7. A deity, a demi-god.<BR>	 8. A sort of bean, (Ervum<BR>hirsutum.)<BR>	 9. A form of array.<BR>	 10. A tree, (Andersonia Rohitaka.)<BR>n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Blood.<BR>	 2. A red kind of Agallochum.<BR>	 3. Saffron.<BR>	 4.<BR>Red sanders.<BR>	 5. War, battle.<BR>	 6. Copper.<BR>	 7. An imperfect form of<BR>a rainbow.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A woman red with anger or with colour,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A sort of creeper, (Lycopodium imbricatum.)<BR> E. रुह् to<BR>grow, इतच् Unādi aff., and र changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितक|लोहितकं|लोहितकः
लोहितक mfn. (-कः-तिका or निका-कं) Red.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A ruby.<BR>	 2. The<BR>planet MARS.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Calx of brass.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितग्रीव|लोहितग्रीवः
लोहितग्रीव m. (-वः) An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितचन्दन|लोहितचंदन|लोहितचन्दनं
लोहितचन्दन n. (-नं) Saffron.<BR> E. लोहित red, and चन्दन sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोलितपुष्पक
लोलितपुष्पक m. (-कः) The pomegranate tree. “दाडिम वृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितमृत्तिका
लोहितमृत्तिका f. (-का) Red chalk.<BR> E. लोहित red, and मृत्तिका soil, earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितशतपत्र
लोहितशतपत्र n. (-त्रं) A red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिताक्ष|लोहिताक्षः
लोहिताक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Red-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2.<BR>The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 3. A kind of snake.<BR> E. लोहित red,<BR>and अक्ष for अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिताङ्ग|लोहितांग|लोहिताङ्गः
लोहिताङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The planet MARS.<BR> E. लोहित, अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितानन|लोहिताननः
लोहितानन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Red-faced.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An ichneumon.<BR> E. लोहित<BR>red, आनन the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहितायस्
लोहितायस् n. (-यः) Copper.<BR> E. लोहित red, and अयस् iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहिनी
लोहिनी f. (-नी) A woman red with anger, or painted red. E. See<BR>लोहित, the fem. aff. being ङीप्, and the penultimate consonant<BR>changed to न ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोहोत्तम|लोहोत्तमं
लोहोत्तम n. (-मं) Gold.<BR> E. लोह a metal, and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकायतिक|लौकायतिकः
लौकायतिक m. (-कः) An atheist, a materialist, a Bauddha.<BR> E. लोकायत<BR>a particular heterodox doctrine, and ठक् aff.; also लोकायतिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकिक|लौकिकः
लौकिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Mundane, worldly, human, what prevails<BR>amongst or is familiar to mankind.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Common, vulgar.<BR>2. Secular, temporal.<BR>	 3. Customary.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Any usage or general<BR>custom.<BR> E. लोक mankind, the world, and ठण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौकिकता
लौकिकता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Worldliness.<BR>	 2. Worldly currency custom. E.<BR>तल् added to the last; also लौकिकत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौक्य
लौक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>	 1. Mundane, human.<BR>	 2. Common.<BR> E. लोक and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौड्
लौड् r. 1st cl. (लौडति) To be mad or foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौल्य|लौल्यं
लौल्य n. (-ल्य)<BR>	 1. Fickleness, inconstancy.<BR>	 2. Eagerness, passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौह|लौहः
लौह mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>	 1. Iron, made of iron, copper, &c.<BR>	 2. Red, copper-<BR>coloured.<BR>	 m. (-हः) Iron.<BR>	 f. (-ही) An iron vessel, a pot.<BR> E. लौह iron,<BR>and अण् deriv. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहबन्ध|लौहबंध|लौहबन्धः
लौहबन्ध n. (-न्धं) An iron chain or fetters.<BR> E. लौह and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहभाण्ड|लौहभांड|लौहभाण्डः
लौहभाण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A pestle and mortar, usually of metal.<BR> E. लौह and<BR>भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहभू
लौहभू f. (-भूः) A sort of iron vessel, a boiler, a caldron.<BR> E. लौह iron, भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहात्मन्
लौहात्मन् f. (-त्मा) A sort of iron boiler, a kettle, &c.<BR> E. लौह made of<BR>iron, and आत्मन् substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहिक
लौहिक m. (-कः) The trident of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहित|लौहितः
लौहित m. (-तः) The trident of ŚIVA.<BR> E. लोहित and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहितीक|लौहितीकः
लौहितीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Redish, like or resembling red, &c.<BR> E. लोहित<BR>red, and ईकक aff., implying similarity in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लौहित्य|लौहित्यं|लौहित्यः
लौहित्य nf. (-त्य-ती) Redness.<BR>	 m. (-त्यः)<BR>	 1. A male river.<BR>	 2. The ocean. E.<BR>लोहित as above, ष्यञ् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल्पी
ल्पी r. 9th cl. (ल्पिनाति) To unite, to join, to be connected or attached<BR>to: it is also read ल्यी-ह्ली-ल्वी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ल्वी
ल्वी r. 9th cl. (ल्विनाति or ल्वीनाति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move or approach.<BR>	 2. To<BR>join or be connected with, to mix with, to unite.<BR>	 3. To obtain:<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व|वं|वः
व The twenty-ninth consonant of the Nagari alphabet, or more pro-<BR>perly the semi vowel V; it is often confounded with the labial<BR>consonant or ब, with which it is also optionally interchangeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व|वं|वः
व m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. The arm.<BR>	 3. A name of VARUṆA.<BR>	 4. Ad-<BR>dressing.<BR>	 5. Auspiciousness.<BR>	 6. Strong, powerful.<BR>	 7. A dwelling.<BR>8. The residence of VARUṆA.<BR>	 9. The ocean.<BR>	 10. Water.<BR>	 11.<BR>Shaving.<BR>	 12. Like, as, (rarely used.)<BR>	 13. An epithet of RĀHU.<BR>	 14.<BR>A tiger.<BR>	 15. Cloth.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. Going.<BR>	 2. Hurting, injury.<BR>	 3. An<BR>arrow.<BR>	 4. Weaving.<BR>	 5. A weaver.<BR>	 n. (-वं) A sort of incantation or<BR>Mantra, of which the object is the deity VARUṆA.<BR> E. वा to go, to<BR>injure, &c., aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंश|वंशः
वंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Race, lineage, family.<BR>	 2. Assemblage, multitude.<BR>	 3. A<BR>bamboo, (Bambusa arundinacea.)<BR>	 4. The back-bone, the spine.<BR>5. A staff.<BR>	 6. A joint.<BR>	 7. The Sāl tree.<BR>	 8. A sort of sugar-<BR>cane.<BR>	 9. A particular measure of length equal to ten hastas.<BR>mf. (-शः-शी)<BR>	 1. A pipe, a fife, a flute.<BR>	 2. Bamboo-manna.<BR> E. वंश् to<BR>shine, घ aff., and नुम् augment; or वन् to sound, to serve, aff. श ।<BR>According the Vāchaspatya:--वमति उद्गिरात वम-श तस्य नेत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशक|वंशकं|वंशकः
वंशक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A small fish, (Cynoglossus lingua, HAM.)<BR>	 2. A large<BR>kind of sugar-cane. “शामशाडा ।” nf. (शकं-शिका) Aloe-wood.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>A kind of pipe or flute.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशकठिन|वंशकठिनः
वंशकठिन m. (-नः) A thicket of bamboos.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशकफ|वंशकफं
वंशकफ n. (-फं) Flocks of cotton or cottony pods floating in the air. E.<BR>वंश a bamboo, and कफ phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशकर|वंशकरः
वंशकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Making or perpetuating a family.<BR> E. वंश, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशकीर्त्ति|वंशकीर्ति
वंशकीर्त्ति mfn. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्तिः-र्त्ति) Famous, celebrated.<BR> E. वंश, कीर्त्ति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशक्षय|वंशक्षयः
वंशक्षय m. (-यः) Decay of a family.<BR> E. वंश, and क्षय decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशक्षीरी
वंशक्षीरी f. (-री) The manna of the bamboo.<BR> E. वंश the bamboo, and क्षीर<BR>milk; being of a milky colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशचरित्र
वंशचरित्र n. (-त्रं) A genealogical table or list, the history of a race or<BR>dynasty, &c.<BR> E. वंश, and चरित्र an account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशचिन्तक|वंशचिंतक|वंशचिन्तकः
वंशचिन्तक m. (-कः) A genealogist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशज|वंशजः
वंशज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Sprung from a good family.<BR>	 2. Produced by<BR>the bamboo.<BR>	 nf. (-ज-जा) Bamboo-manna.<BR> E. वश a bamboo, or<BR>lineage, &c., and ज born, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशधर|वंशधरः
वंशधर mfn. (-रः-रा-र)<BR>	 1. Who or what supports a family.<BR>	 2. Carrying<BR>or holding a bamboo, &c.<BR> E. वंश, and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशनालिका
वंशनालिका f. (-का) A pipe, a reed or flute.<BR> E. वंश a bamboo, नाल a tube,<BR>कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशनेत्र|वंशनेत्रं
वंशनेत्र n. (-त्रं) The root of sugarcane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशपत्रक|वंशपत्रकं|वंशपत्रकः
वंशपत्रक n. (-कं) Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A sort of fish, (Cynoglossus<BR>lingua, HAM.)<BR> E. वंश a bamboo, and पत्र a leaf, the shape of the fish<BR>resembling to that of the leaf of the bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशपत्रपतित|वंशपत्रपतितं
वंशपत्रपतित n. (-तं) A species of the Atyashtī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशपरम्परा|वंशपरंपरा
वंशपरम्परा f. (-रा) Family, lineage, descent.<BR> E. वंश, and परम्पर successive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशपूरक|वंशपूरकं
वंशपूरक n. (-कं) The root of a sugarcane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशभोज्य
वंशभोज्य n. (-ज्यं) Hereditary estate.<BR> E. वंश, and भोज्य to be possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=623-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवंरोचना
शवंरोचना f. (-ना) An earthy concretion of a milk-white colour, formed<BR>in the hollow of the bamboo, an known by the name of bamboo-<BR>manna.<BR> E. वंश the bamboo, रुच् to shine, aff. युच्; also र being<BR>changed to ल, वंशलोचना ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशलोचना
वंशलोचना f. (-ना) The manna of the bamboo: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशवर्द्धन
वंशवर्द्धन n. (-नं) Increasing or exalting a family.<BR> E. वंश, वर्द्धन augmenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशवितति|वंशविततिः
वंशवितति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A clump of bamboos.<BR>	 2. A Family, descent. E.<BR>वंश a bamboo or lineage, and वितति extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशविशुद्ध
वंशविशुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Of a goad family.<BR>	 2. Of a good bamboo,<BR>(made, constructed.)<BR> E. वंश, and विशुद्ध pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशवृद्धि
वंशवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Prosperity of a family.<BR> E. वंश and वृद्धि, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशशर्करा
वंशशर्करा f. (-रा) The bamboo-manna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशशलाका
वंशशलाका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The bamboo pipe that forms the body of the Vinā<BR>or lute.<BR>	 2. Any small bamboo pin or stake, as the bar of a cage,<BR>&c.<BR> E. वंश a bamboo and शलाका a pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशसमाचार
वंशसमाचार m. (-रः) Family usage.<BR> E. वंश and समाचार practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशस्थविल|वंशस्थविलं
वंशस्थविल n. (-लं) A species of the Jagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशस्थिति|वंशस्थितिः
वंशस्थिति f. (-तिः) The perpetuation of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशहीन
वंशहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having no kindred or family.<BR> E. वंश and हीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशाग्र|वंशाग्रं
वंशाग्र n. (-ग्रं) The shoot of a bamboo.<BR> E. वंश and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशाङ्कुर|वंशांकुर|वंशाङ्कुरः
वंशाङ्कुर m. (-रः) The shoot of a bamboo.<BR> E. वंश, and अङ्कुर a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशानुचरित|वंशानुचरितं
वंशानुचरित n. (-तं) A pedigree, a genealogical list, or history.<BR> E. वंश a<BR>family, अनु implying succession, and चरित proceeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशावली
वंशावली f. (-ली) A pedigree, a genealogy.<BR> E. वंश, and आवली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशिक|वंशिकं
वंशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging or relating to a family or bamboo,<BR>&c.<BR>	 nf. (-कं-का)<BR>	 1. Aloe-wood.<BR>	 2. A Kind of flute.<BR> E. वंश, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशी
वंशी f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A flute, a pipe.<BR>	 2. An artery.<BR>	 3. Bamboo-manna.<BR>	 4.<BR>A particular weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंशीधर|वंशीधरः
वंशीधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A piper.<BR>	 2. A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. वंशी, धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंश्य|वंश्यः
वंश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>	 1. Of a good family.<BR>	 2. Of the same family.<BR>	 3.<BR>Relating to the back-bone.<BR>	 m. (-श्यः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A pupil, a scho-<BR>lar.<BR>	 3. A kinsman, from seven generations above and seven below.<BR>4. A bone in the leg or arm.<BR> E. वंश a family, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंहिष्ठ
वंहिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Most, very much or great.<BR> E. वंह substituted<BR>for वृन्दारक great, and इष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंहीयस्
वंहीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very much or very large.<BR> E. वंह for वृन्दारक, ईयसुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्
वक्(इ)वकि r. 1st cl. (वङ्कते)<BR>	 1. To be crooked, (literally or figuratively,)<BR>to be curved or bent, to be depraved or wicked.<BR>	 2. To bend, to<BR>make crooked.<BR>	 3. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक
वक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A crane, (Ardea nivea.)<BR>	 2. A tree, (Sesbana gran-<BR>diflora.)<BR>	 3. KUVERA.<BR>	 4. The name of a demon.<BR>	 5. A small appara-<BR>tus for calcining or subliming metals or minerals consisting of<BR>two crucibles, one inverted over the other, luted together and<BR>placed over a fire.<BR> E. वच् to speak, or वकि to be crooked, aff. घञ्<BR>or अच्; in the latter case the nasal augment is not inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकचिञ्चिका
वकचिञ्चिका f. (-का) A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकजित्
वकजित् m. (-जित्) A name of BHĪMA.<BR> E. वक a demon, and जित् the conqueror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकधूप|वकधूपः
वकधूप m. (-पः) Compound perfume: see वृकघूप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकनिसूदन|वकनिसूदनः
वकनिसूदन m. (-नः) BHĪMA.<BR> E. वक the demon, and निसूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकपुष्प|वकपुष्पः
वकपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A tree, (Æschynomene grandiflora.)<BR> E. वक curving,<BR>from वकि to be crooked, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकवृत्ति|वकवृत्तिः
वकवृत्ति m. (-त्तिः) A false or hypocritical devotee: see वकव्रतिन्<BR> E. वक, वृत्ति livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकवैरिन्
वकवैरिन् m. (-री) BHĪMA.<BR> E. वक the demon, and वैरिन् a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकव्रतिन्
वकव्रतिन् m. (-ती) A false devotee, a religious hypocrite, or one who as-<BR>sumes the appearance of devotion or meditation, for interested pur-<BR>poses.<BR> E. वक a crane, व्रत observance, and इनि aff.; compared to<BR>the crane, who stands by a pool demure and sly, and apparently<BR>absorbed in contemplation, till be sees a fish on which to dart;<BR>also with ठक् aff. वकव्रतिक, and derived from वक, and चर who<BR>goes, वकचर; or वकव्रतचर m. (-रः) &c.: see वैडालव्रतिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकाची
वकाची f. (-ची) A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकुल|वकुलः
वकुल m. (-लः) A plant, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR>	 f. (-ली) A sort of drug,<BR>commonly Kākoli.<BR> E. वक् to be crooked, aff. उलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकेरुका
वकेरुका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A small crane.<BR>	 2. The branch of a tree bent by the<BR>wind.<BR> E. वक a crane, or वक् to be crooked, ईर् to go or be, aff.<BR>उकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वकोट
वकोट n. (-टः) A crane.<BR> E. वक् to be crooked, ओटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्क्
वक्क् r. 1st cl. (वक्कते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तव्य|वक्तव्यः
वक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Fit or proper to be said or spoken, to be<BR>spoken or uttered.<BR>	 2. To be spoken about or against.<BR>	 3. Vile, bad,<BR>reprehensible.<BR>	 4. Subject, dependent.<BR>	 5. Low, base.<BR>	 n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>rule, a dictum, a sentence.<BR>	 2. Speech.<BR>	 3. Reproach.<BR> E. वच् to<BR>speak, and तव्य aff., of the future participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तव्यता
वक्तव्यता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Blame, reprehension.<BR>	 2. The nature or property of<BR>what is to be said, or the occasion for it.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तुकाम
वक्तुकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Desirous of speaking.<BR> E. वक्तु for वक्तुम् to<BR>speak, काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्तृ
वक्तृ mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ)<BR>	 1. Speaking, a speaker.<BR>	 2. Loquacious, talkative.<BR>3. Speaking well or sensibly, eloquent.<BR>	 4. Wise, learned.<BR>	 5. Speak-<BR>ing truly or truth, honest, sincere.<BR>	 m. (-क्ता)<BR>	 1. An expounder, a<BR>teacher.<BR>	 2. An orator, a speaker.<BR> E. वच् to speak, तृच् participial aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्र|वक्त्रं
वक्त्र m. (-क्त्रः) A hog.<BR>	 n. (-क्त्रं)<BR>	 1. The mouth or face.<BR>	 2. A sort of gar-<BR>ment.<BR>	 3. Metre, verse, especially of the Vedas.<BR>	 4. A plant: see<BR>तगरमूल.<BR>	 5. The sprout of a jug.<BR> E. वच् to speak, Unādi aff. ष्ट्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रखुर|वक्त्रखुरः
वक्त्रखुर m. (-रः) A tooth.<BR> E. वक्त्र the mouth, and खुर a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रज|वक्त्रजः
वक्त्रज m. (-जः) A Brāhman.<BR> E. वक्त्र the mouth, (of BRAHMĀ,) ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रताल|वक्त्रतालं
वक्त्रताल mn. (-लः-लं) A musical instrument, played on with the mouth.<BR>E. वक्त्र the mouth, ताल tune; it may also signify, making a noise<BR>with the mouth, by striking it with the hand at the moment of<BR>uttering sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रतुण्ड|वक्त्रतुण्डः
वक्त्रतुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A name of GANESA.<BR> E. वक्त्र and तुण्ड beak or nose,<BR>having the proboscis of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रपट्ट|वक्त्रपट्टः
वक्त्रपट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A bag containing corn tied round a horse's head. E.<BR>वक्त्र the mouth, पट्ट a cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रभेदिन्
वक्त्रभेदिन् m. (-दी) Pungency, pungent or acrid flavour.<BR> E. वक्त्र mouth, भेदिन् what cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्ररन्ध्र|वक्त्ररंध्र
वक्त्ररन्ध्र n. (-न्ध्रं) The aperture of the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रवास|वक्त्रवासः
वक्त्रवास m. (-सः) An orange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रशोधिन्
वक्त्रशोधिन् m. (-धी) The citron tree.<BR> E. वक्त्र, शोधिन् what cleanses; also वक्त्रशोधन m. (-नः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्त्रासव|वक्त्रासवः
वक्त्रासव m. (-वः) Saliva.<BR> E. वक्त्र the mouth, and आसव wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्र|वक्रं|वक्रः
वक्र mfn. (-क्रः-क्रा-क्रं)<BR>	 1. Crooked, curved, bowed or bent.<BR>	 2. Cruel,<BR>malignant.<BR>	 3. Dishonest, fraudulent.<BR>	 4. Indirect, evasive.<BR>	 5. Long,<BR>(in prosody.)<BR>	 n. (-क्रं)<BR>	 1. The winding course of a river or waterfall,<BR>the arm or bend of a stream.<BR>	 2. The retrograde motion of a pla-<BR>net.<BR>	 3. A species of the Anuṣṭubh metre.<BR>	 m. (-क्रः)<BR>	 1. A name<BR>of SATURN.<BR>	 2. The planet MARS.<BR>	 3. RUDRA or ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. The demon<BR>TRIPURĀ.<BR> E. वकि to go crookedly, रक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रकण्ट|वक्रकंट|वक्रकण्टः
वक्रकण्ट m. (-ण्टः)<BR>	 1. The jujube tree.<BR>	 2. The khadira tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रखङ्क
वक्रखङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A sabre or scimitar.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, and खङ्क a sword;<BR>also with कन् added, वक्रखङ्कक m. (-कः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रगामिन्
वक्रगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिणी-मि)<BR>	 1. Who or what goes tortuously.<BR>	 2.<BR>Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR> E. वक्र and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रग्रीव|वक्रग्रीवः
वक्रग्रीव m. (-वः) A camel.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, ग्रीवा the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रचञ्चु|वक्रचंचु|वक्रचञ्चुः
वक्रचञ्चु m. (-ञ्चुः) A parrot.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, and चञ्चु the beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रता
वक्रता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Crookedness.<BR>	 2. Wickedness.<BR>	 3. Craft, cunning.<BR>	 4.<BR>Evasive or indirect speech.<BR> E. वक्र, तल् added; also with त्व वक्तत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रतुण्ड|वक्रतुंड|वक्रतुण्डः
वक्रतुण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. An epithet of GANESA.<BR>	 2. A parrot.<BR> E. वक्र, तुण्ड a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रदंष्ट्र|वक्रदंष्ट्रः
वक्रदंष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A boar.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, and दंष्ट्र a tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रदृष्टि
वक्रदृष्टि Adj.<BR>	 1. Envious.<BR>	 2. Having an evil eye.<BR>	 3. Squinting.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>An oblique look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रनक्र|वक्रनक्रः
वक्रनक्र m. (-क्रः)<BR>	 1. A low or depraved man.<BR>	 2. A parrot.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, नक्र the nose, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=624-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रनासिक|वक्रनासिकः
वक्रनासिक m. (-कः) An owl.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, and नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रपुच्छ|वक्रपुच्छः
वक्रपुच्छ m. (-च्छः) A dog.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, and पुच्छ a tail; also वक्रपुच्छिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रपुष्प|वक्रपुष्पः
वक्रपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) The Sesbana grandiflora.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, पुष्प the flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रबालधि|वक्रबालधिः
वक्रबालधि m. (-धिः) A dog.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, बालधि a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रभणित|वक्रभणितं
वक्रभणित n. (-तं) Indirect speech, equivoque, evasion.<BR> E. वक्र crooked,<BR>भणित spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रम|वक्रमः
वक्रम m. (-मः) Flight, retreat.<BR> E. अव reverse, क्रम् to go, aff. अच्, and the initial rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रवक्त्र|वक्रवक्त्रः
वक्रवक्त्र m. (-क्त्रः) A hog.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, and वक्त्र a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्राग्र|वक्राग्रं
वक्राग्र n. (-ग्रं) A plant, commonly Bentua.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्राङ्ग|वक्रांग|वक्राङ्गः
वक्राङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A goose.<BR>	 2. The ruddy goose.<BR>	 3. A snake.<BR> E. वक्र bending, अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रि|वक्रिः
वक्रि mfn. (-क्रिः-क्रिः-क्रि) Speaking falsely, uttering untruths, prevarica-<BR>ting, lying.<BR> E. वक्र to be crooked, (metaphorically,) क्रिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रिन्
वक्रिन् mfn. (-क्री-क्रिणी-क्रि)<BR>	 1. Crooked.<BR>	 2. Dishonest, fraudulent.<BR>	 m. (-क्री)<BR>A Jaina or Bauddha.<BR> E. वक्र crooked, fraudulent, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रिम
वक्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Bent, curved.<BR> E. वकि to go crookedly, क्रिमच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रिमन्
वक्रिमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Crookedness, curvature.<BR>	 2. Craftiness, cunning.<BR>	 3.<BR>Indirectness.<BR> E. वक्र, and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रीकरण
वक्रीकरण n. (-णं) Curving, bending, distorting.<BR> E. वक्र, and करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रीकृत
वक्रीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bent, made crooked.<BR> E. वक्र, and कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रीभाव|वक्रीभावः
वक्रीभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Curvature, curve.<BR>	 2. Fraudulent or dishonest dis-<BR>position.<BR> E. वक्री, भाव property, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रीभूत
वक्रीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bent, crooked.<BR>	 2. Dishonest.<BR> E. वक्र, भूत become, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रोक्ति|वक्रोक्तिः
वक्रोक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Equivoque, evasion, pun, the covert expression of<BR>something else than the words used naturally imply, either from<BR>the manner in which they are uttered, or some other sense of<BR>which they are susceptible.<BR>	 2. Hint, insinuation.<BR>	 3. Sarcasm. It<BR>is thus defined in Sāhityadarpana:--<BR>“अन्यस्यान्यार्थकं वाक्यमन्यथायोजयेद्यदि ।<BR>अन्यः श्लेषेण काक्वा वा सा वक्रोक्तिस्ततो द्विधा ॥”<BR>E. वक्र crooked, dishonest, and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्रोष्ठिका
वक्रोष्ठिका f. (-का) A gentle smile, one in which the teeth are not shown.<BR>E. वक्र crooked, ओष्ठ the lip, and कन् aff., fem. form; also वक्रोष्टिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्ष्
वक्ष् r. 1st cl. (वक्षति) To be angry.<BR>	 2. To accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षण|वक्षणं
वक्षण n. (-णं) The breast: see वक्षस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षस्
वक्षस् n. (-क्षः) The breast, the bosom, the chest.<BR>	 m. (-क्षाः) An ox, (con-<BR>fined to the Vedas.)<BR> E. वच् to speak, or वक्ष् to accumulate, aff. असुन्<BR>in the first case सुट् is inserted; again वह् to bear, असुन् aff., सुट्<BR>augment, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षःसम्मर्द्दिनी|वक्षःसम्मर्दिनी
वक्षःसम्मर्द्दिनी f. (-नी) Wife of the bosom.<BR> E. वक्षस् and सम्मर्द्दिनी who rubs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षः|वक्ष
वक्षः(क्ष)स्थल n. (-लं) The breast, the heart.<BR> E. वक्षस् and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षोज|वक्षोजं|वक्षोजः
वक्षोज n. (-जं) The female breast.<BR> E. वक्षस् the breast or chest, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्षोरुह|वक्षोरुहः
वक्षोरुह m. (-हः) The female breast.<BR> E. वक्षस् the chest, रुह what rises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वक्ष्यमाण|वक्ष्यमाणः
वक्ष्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being to be said or described.<BR> E. वच् to say,<BR>desid. pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वख्
वख् r. 1st cl. (वखति) (इ) वखि (वङ्खति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वग्
वग्(इ)वगि r. 1st cl. (वङ्गति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To go lamely, to limp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वगाह|वगाहः
वगाह m. (-हः) Bathing, ablution.<BR> E. अव before, गाह् to agitate, aff. अच्,<BR>and the initial rejected; also अवगाह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वग्नु|वग्नुः
वग्नु m. (-ग्नुः) A speaker.<BR> E. वच् to speak, नु Unādi aff., and च changed to ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वघ्
वघ्(इ)वघि r. 1st cl. (वङ्घते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To blame or censure.<BR>	 3. To be-<BR>gin.<BR>	 4. To begin moving.<BR>	 5. To move swiftly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क|वंक|वंकः|वङ्कः
वङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. The bend or elbow of a river, the winding course of a<BR>stream.<BR>	 2. Crookedness.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्का) The pummel of a saddle.<BR> E. वकि<BR>to curve or bend, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्किल|वंकिल|वंकिलः|वङ्किलः
वङ्किल m. (-लः) A thorn.<BR> E. वङ्क crookedness, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्य|वङ्क्यः
वङ्क्य mfn. (-ङ्क्यः-ङ्क्या-ङ्क्यं) Crooked, curved.<BR> E. वञ्च् to go, ण्यत् aff., च<BR>changed to क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्रि|वंक्रि|वंक्रिः|वङ्क्रिः
वङ्क्रि f. (-ङ्क्रिः) A rib.<BR>	 mn. (-ङ्क्रिः-ङ्क्रिं)<BR>	 1. The wood of a thatch.<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of musical instrument.<BR> E. वकि to be crooked, रि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्षण|वंक्षणं|वङ्क्षणः
वङ्क्षण n. (-णं) The groin, the public and iliac regions.<BR> E. वाञ्छि to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">Page625-b+ 60</a>]<BR>desire, ल्युट् aff., and the form irr.; or वक्ष् to accumulate, ल्युट् aff.<BR>and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्क्षु|वंक्षु|वंक्षुः|वङ्क्षुः
वङ्क्षु f. (-ङ्क्षुः) A small arm or branch of the Ganges.<BR> E. वङ्क्ष् to accumulate, aff. उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्ग|वंग|वङ्गं|वङ्गः
वङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Lead.<BR>	 2. Tin.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Bengal, or the eastern parts of<BR>the modern province.<BR>	 2. Cotton.<BR>	 3. The egg-plant, (Solanum<BR>melongena.)<BR> E. वगि to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गज|वंगज|वङ्गजं
वङ्गज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Brass.<BR>	 2. Red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गजीवन|वंगजीवन
वङ्गजीवन n. (-नं) Silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गन|वङ्गनः
वङ्गन m. (-नः) The egg-plant. “वेगुण गाछ ।”<BR> E. वगि to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गशुल्वज|वंगशुल्वज|वङ्गशुल्वजं
वङ्गशुल्वज n. (-जं) Brass.<BR> E. वङ्ग tin, शुल्व copper, and ज produced; an<BR>alloy of tin and copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गसेन|वङ्गसेनः
वङ्गसेन m. (-नः) The Sesbana grandiflora. “वक्फुलेर गाछ ।”<BR> E. वङ्ग Bengal,<BR>सि to sew, aff. ल्युट्; also with कन् added, वङ्गसेनक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गारि|वंगारि|वङ्गारिः
वङ्गारि m. (-रिः) Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. वङ्ग lead, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वङ्गुला
वङ्गुला f. (-ला) A mode of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच्
वच्(औ)औवच r. 1st cl. (वचति) r. 2nd cl. (वक्ति) and 10th cl. (वाचयति-ते)<BR>	 1.<BR>To speak, to tell.<BR>	 2. To inform.<BR>	 3. To read, to expound.<BR>	 4. To<BR>name: (the second cl. is the most usual form of the root, in which<BR>its inflections however are very irregular.) With प्र, 1. To begin<BR>to speak.<BR>	 2. To call.<BR>	 3. To announce. With प्रति, To answer. With<BR>अनु, To recite. With निस्, To explain etymologically.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वच|वचः
वच m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. A parrot.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 f. (-चा)<BR>	 1. Orris root, (Acorus<BR>calamus; also Zinziber Zedoaria.)<BR>	 2. The Sārikā, (Turdus Salica.)<BR>E. वच् to speak, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचक्नु|वचक्नुः
वचक्नु mfn. (-क्नुः-क्नुः-क्नु) Talkative, loquacious, eloquent.<BR>	 m. (-क्नुः) A<BR>Brāhmana.<BR> E. वच् to speak, Unādi aff. अक्नुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचन|वचनं
वचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Speech, speaking.<BR>	 2. A sentence, a text, a dictum, an<BR>aphorism, a rule.<BR>	 3. Recitation.<BR>	 4. Advice.<BR>	 5. Order, command.<BR>6. Dry-ginger.<BR>	 7. The pronunciation of a letter, (in gram.)<BR>	 8. The<BR>meaning of a word.<BR>	 9. Number, (in gram.)<BR> E. वच् to speak, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनकर|वचनकरः
वचनकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Obedient.<BR>	 2. Speaking.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The<BR>author or enunciator of a precept.<BR> E. वचन, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनक्रम|वचनक्रमः
वचनक्रम m. (-मः) Discourse, order of words.<BR> E. वचन, and क्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनग्राहिन्
वचनग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Compliant, conformable, submissive,<BR>humble.<BR> E. वचन speech, ग्राहिन् taking, obeying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनविरुद्ध
वचनविरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Contrary to a text or precept.<BR> E. वचन, विरुद्ध्व opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनविरोध|वचनविरोधः
वचनविरोध m. (-धः) Incongruity, contradiction, inconsistency of texts.<BR>E. वचन, विरोध opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनव्यक्ति|वचनव्यक्तिः
वचनव्यक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Distinctness or perspicuity of a text.<BR> E. वचन, and व्यक्ति plainness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनीय|वचनीयः
वचनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be spoken or said.<BR>	 2. Censurable, to be<BR>noticed or reproved.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Censure.<BR> E. वच् to speak. अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनीयता
वचनीयता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Rumour, report, especially ill report, detraction,<BR>scandal.<BR>	 2. Blame, reprehension.<BR> E. वचनीय to be censured, तल् aff.;<BR>also with त्व, aff., वचनीयत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनमात्र
वचनमात्र n. (-त्रं) Mere words, assertion unsupported by facts.<BR> E. वचन, मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनशत
वचनशत n. (-तं) Repeated speech or declaration.<BR> E. वचन, शत a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचनेस्थित|वचनेस्थितः
वचनेस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Compliant, conformable, obedient.<BR> E. वचने in<BR>the word, and स्थित who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचर|वचरः
वचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A cock.<BR>	 2. A rogue, a cheat.<BR> E. वच् to speak, अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचलु|वचलुः
वचलु m. (-लुः) Offence, fault.<BR> E. वच् to speak. अलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्
वचस् n. (-चः)<BR>	 1. Speech, voice.<BR>	 2. Words.<BR>	 3. A sentence.<BR>	 4. Advice.<BR>	 5.<BR>Command.<BR>	 6. Number, (in gram.)<BR> E. वच् to speak, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वचस्कर|वचस्करः
वचस्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Obedient, compliant.<BR> E. वचस्, and कर who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्
वज् r. 1st cl. (वजति) To go. r. 10th cl. (वाजयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To<BR>make.<BR>	 3. To prepare the way.<BR>	 4. To trim or feather an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्र|वज्रं|वज्रः
वज्र mfn. (-ज्रः-ज्रा-ज्रं)<BR>	 1. Hard, impenetrable, adamantine.<BR>	 2. Cross, fork-<BR>ed.<BR>	 mn. (-ज्रः-ज्रं)<BR>	 1. A thunderbolt in general, or the thunderbolt<BR>of INDRA, which is said to have formed out of the bones of the<BR>sage Dadhīchī, (in Hindu mytho.)<BR>	 2. The diamond, (the gem being<BR>considered analogous in hardness to the thunderbolt, or in fact<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">Page626-a+ 60</a>]<BR>to be the same substance.)<BR>	 3. A diagram, the figure of which<BR>is supposed to be that of the thunderbolt.<BR>	 4. A child or pupil.<BR>5. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 6. Sour gruel.<BR>	 7. The blossom of the se-<BR>samum.<BR>	 8. Harsh language.<BR>	 m. (-ज्रः)<BR>	 1. One of the astronomi-<BR>cal Yogas.<BR>	 2. Kuśa grass.<BR>	 3. A form of military array.<BR>	 n. (-ज्रं)<BR>1. Steel.<BR>	 2. A kind of talc.<BR>	 3. Severe language.<BR>	 4. A child.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ज्रा-ज्री) A species of Euphorbia f. (-ज्रा)<BR>	 1. A plant: see गुडुची.<BR>	 2.<BR>A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR> E. वज् to go, रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=625-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रक|वज्रकं
वज्रक n. (-कं) A sort of salt, an impure carbonate of soda.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रकङ्कट|वज्रकंकट|वज्रकङ्कटः
वज्रकङ्कट m. (-टः) Hanumāna, the monkey demigod.<BR> E. वज्र the<BR>thunderbolt, (as hard,) and कङ्कट armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रकण्टक|वज्रकण्टकः
वज्रकण्टक m. (-कः) Euphorbia.<BR> E. वज्र a thunderbolt, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रकपालिन्
वज्रकपालिन् m. (-ली) One of the Bauddha saints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रक्षार|वज्रक्षारं
वज्रक्षार n. (-रं) An alkaline earth, an impure carbonate of soda.<BR> E. वज्र<BR>diamond, क्षार alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रचर्मन्
वज्रचर्मन् m. (-र्मा) A rhinoceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रजित्
वज्रजित् m. (-जित्) A name of GARUDĀ.<BR> E. वज्र bolt, जित् who conquers;<BR>being invulnerable to repeated shocks of INDRA'S bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रज्वाला
वज्रज्वाला f. (-ला) A clap of thunder.<BR> E. वज्र the bolt, and ज्वाला flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रटीक|वज्रटीकः
वज्रटीक m. (-कः) A Jaina deified saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रतुण्ड|वज्रतुंड|वज्रतुण्डः
वज्रतुण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. The deity GANESA.<BR>	 2. GARUDĀ, the bird and<BR>vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A vulture.<BR>	 4. A gnat, a musquito.<BR> E. वज्र<BR>the thunderbolt, and तुण्ड face or beak, (as hard.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रदन्त|वज्रदंत|वज्रदन्तः
वज्रदन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A hog.<BR>	 2. A rat.<BR> E. वज्र a thunderbolt, (as hard,) दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रदशन|वज्रदशनः
वज्रदशन m. (-नः) A rat.<BR> E. वज्र and दशन a tooth; see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रद्रु|वज्रद्रुः
वज्रद्रु m. (-द्रुः) Euphorbia of various species.<BR> E. वज्र thunderbolt, (as<BR>hard,) and द्रु a tree; also वज्रद्रुम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रद्रुम|वज्रद्रुमः
वज्रद्रुम m. (-मः) Euphorbia: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रधर|वज्रधरः
वज्रधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. INDRA, as the JUPITER Tonans of the Hindus.<BR>2. A Bauddha saint.<BR> E. वज्र the thunderbolt, धर who has or holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रनाभ|वज्रनाभः
वज्रनाभ m. (-भः) The discus of KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रनिर्घोष|वज्रनिर्घोषः
वज्रनिर्घोष m. (-षः) A clap of thunder.<BR> E. वज्र the bolt, and निर्घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रनिष्पेष|वज्रनिष्पेषः
वज्रनिष्पेष m. (-षः) A clap of thunder.<BR> E. वज्र the bolt, and निष्पेष here<BR>meaning the sound produced by friction or concussion, from निर्<BR>forth, पिष् to grind, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रपाणि|वज्रपाणिः
वज्रपाणि m. (-णिः) INDRA.<BR> E. वज्र the bolt, पाणि the hand: see वज्रधर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रपात|वज्रपातः
वज्रपात m. (-तः) A thunderbolt, a stoke of lightning.<BR> E. वज्र, पात fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रपुष्प|वज्रपुष्पं
वज्रपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) The blossom of the sesamum. “तिलपुष्पे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रबध
वज्रबध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Death by lightning.<BR>	 2. Cross multiplication.<BR> E. वज्र,<BR>and बध killing, or multiplying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रमय
वज्रमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Hard, adamantine.<BR>	 2. Hard-hearted.<BR> E. वज्र, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्ररद|वज्ररदः
वज्ररद m. (-दः) A hog.<BR> E. वज्र a thunderbolt, (as hard,) and रद a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रलप
वज्रलप m. (-पः) A kind of hard cement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रलोहक|वज्रलोहकः
वज्रलोहक m. (-कः) A loadstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रवराही
वज्रवराही f. (-ही) A female personification of Māyā or unreality,<BR>amongst the Bauddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रवल्ली
वज्रवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A species of sun-flower, (Heliotropium.)<BR> E. वज्र the<BR>thunderbolt, वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रशृङ्खला
वज्रशृङ्खला f. (-ला) A female deification peculiar to the Jainas, and one<BR>of their sixteen Vidyā-Devis.<BR> E. वज्र a diamond, and शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रसार
वज्रसार Adj. Of the nature of a diamond, (as hard.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रसूर्य्य|वज्रसूर्य|वज्रसूर्य्यः
वज्रसूर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A Jaina saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राङ्ग|वज्रांग|वज्राङ्गः
वज्राङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A snake.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी) A sort of grain, (Coix barbata.) “गवेधु”.<BR>the thunderbolt, (as hard,) अङ्ग body or substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राघात|वज्राघातः
वज्राघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A thunderbolt or stroke.<BR>	 2. A sudden calamity. E.<BR>वज्र, आघात blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राभ|वज्राभः
वज्राभ m. (-भः) Precious opal.<BR> E. वज्र the diamond, (in hardness perhaps,) आभ resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राभ्यास|वज्राभ्यासः
वज्राभ्यास m. (-सः) Cross multiplication.<BR> E. वज्र, and अभ्यास practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्राशनि|वज्राशनिः
वज्राशनि m. (-निः) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वज्रिन्
वज्रिन् m. (-ज्री)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. A Jaina deified saint.<BR>	 3. A buffalo.<BR>	 4. An<BR>owl.<BR> E. वज्र the thunderbolt, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्च्|वंच्
वञ्च्(उ)वञ्चु r. 1st cl. (वञ्चति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To go secretly. r. 1st and<BR>10th cls. (वञ्चते वञ्चयते) To delude, to cheat, to trick or deceive.<BR>Caus. (वञ्चयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shun, to evade.<BR>	 2. To beguile, to defraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चक|वंचक|वञ्चकः
वञ्चक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Fraudulent, crafty.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A jackal 2. A<BR>tame or house ichneumon.<BR>	 3. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 4. A low or vile<BR>man.<BR>	 5. A musk-rat.<BR>	 f. (-चिका) Cheating.<BR> E. वञ्च् to cheat, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चति|वंचति|वंचतिः|वञ्चतिः
वञ्चति m. (-तिः) Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चथ|वंचथ|वंचथः|वञ्चथः
वञ्चथ m. (-थः) A rogue, a knave, a cheat.<BR> E. वञ्च् to cheat, Unādi aff. अथ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चन|वंचन|वंचनं|वञ्चनं
वञ्चन n. (-नं) Cheating, fraud.<BR> E. वञ्च् to cheat, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चनीय
वञ्चनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be cheated.<BR> E. वञ्च to cheat, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चयित्वा
वञ्चयित्वा Ind. Having cheated.<BR> E. वञ्च् to cheat, क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चित|वंचित|वञ्चितः
वञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Tricked, deceived.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A kind of riddle. E.<BR>वञ्च् to cheat, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्चुक|वंचुक|वञ्चुकः
वञ्चुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Crafty, fraudulent.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A jackal.<BR> E. वञ्च् to<BR>cheat, aff. उकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्च्य|वञ्च्यं
वञ्च्य mfn. (-ञ्च्य-ञ्च्या-ञ्च्यं)<BR>	 1. To be gone.<BR>	 2. To be cheated.<BR> E. वञ्च् to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्जुल|वंजुल|वञ्जुलः
वञ्जुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Dalbergia Ougeinensis.)<BR>	 2. Another<BR>tree, (Jonesia Asoca.)<BR>	 3. Common cane, (Calamus rotang.)<BR>	 4. A<BR>flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR>	 5. A sort of bird.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A cow that<BR>yields abundance of milk.<BR> E. वञ्च to go, aff. उलच्, च changed to ज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वञ्जुलप्रिय|वंजुलप्रिय|वञ्जुलप्रियः
वञ्जुलप्रिय m. (-यः) The ratan, (Calamus rotang.) “वेतसे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट्
वट् r. 1st and 10th cls. (वटति वटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To surround or encompass.<BR>	 2.<BR>To tie or string, to connect.<BR>	 3. To partition, to divide. r. 1st cl.<BR>causal form (वटयति) To speak. (इ) वटि r. 4th and 10th cls. (वण्टति<BR>वण्टयति) To partition, to separate or divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वट|वटः
वट Subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-टः-टी-टं) A string, a rope, a tie.<BR>	 m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The large<BR>Indian fig-tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>	 2. A round figure, a circle, a<BR>cipher, a ball or globe.<BR>	 3. Pulse ground and fried with oil or<BR>butter.<BR>	 4. A small shell, a cowrie.<BR>	 5. Equality in shape or dimen-<BR>sion.<BR> E. वट् to surround, to tie, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटक|वटकः
वटक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Pulse ground and fried in oil or butter.<BR>	 2. A weight<BR>of eight Māshās.<BR>	 f. (-टिका) A pill.<BR> E. वट् to surround, aff. क्वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटपत्रा
वटपत्रा f. (-त्रा) A plant, from the fibrous leaves of which bow-strings,<BR>&c., are made, (Aletris hyacinthoides: Sanseviera zeylanica, Rox.'s<BR>Cata.)<BR> E. वट a string, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटर|वटरः
वटर mfn. (-रः-रा-र)<BR>	 1. Wicked, villainous.<BR>	 2. Slippery, unsteady.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः)<BR>	 1. A cock.<BR>	 2. A thief.<BR>	 3. A cloth worn round the head, a<BR>turban.<BR>	 4. A mat.<BR>	 5. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>	 6. A churning<BR>stick.<BR> E. वट् to surround, अरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटवासिन्
वटवासिन् mf. (-सा-सिनी) A sort of demigod, male and female; a YAKSHA<BR>or YAKSHINĪ, KUVERA'S special attendants.<BR> E. वट the Indian-fig in<BR>which these spirits are supposed to be fond of abiding, वास abode,<BR>and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटाकर|वटाकरः
वटाकर m. (-रः) A cord, a rope, a string.<BR> E. वट surrounding, आकर<BR>what makes, from कृ to make, with आङ् prefix, and टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटावीक|वटावीकः
वटावीक m. (-कः) A notorious thief, a dacoit, a robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटि|वटिः
वटि m. (-टिः) A sort of tick or body louse.<BR> E. वट् to surround, aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटिक|वटिकः
वटिक m. (-कः) A pawn at chess.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A pill.<BR>	 2. A chessman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटिन्
वटिन् mfn. (-टी-टिनी-टि)<BR>	 1. Stringed, having a string.<BR>	 2. Circular, glo-<BR>bular.<BR> E. वट, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटु|वटुः
वटु m. (-टुः)<BR>	 1. The Brahmachāri or religious student, after his investi-<BR>ture with the sacred thread.<BR>	 2. A lad, a youth in general.<BR>	 3. A<BR>flower, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. वट् to surround, (with the string, &c.)<BR>or to speak, उ Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटुक|वटुकः
वटुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A lad, a young man in general, or one fit to receive<BR>the sacrificial thread.<BR>	 2. A religious student.<BR>	 3. A stupid fellow,<BR>a blockhead.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वटूकरण
वटूकरण n. (-णं) Investiture with the sacred and characteristic thread.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">Page627-a+ 60</a>]<BR>E. वटु a lad after investiture. कृ to make, aff. ल्युट्, and the vowel of<BR>वटु made long or technically, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=626-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वठ्
वठ् r. 1st cl. (वठति) To be large, powerful or able; also वठ(इ)वठि<BR>(वण्ठते) To move alone or unaccompanied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वठर|वठरः
वठर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Vile, wicked, abandoned.<BR>	 2. Stupid, slow, dull.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A blockhead, a fool.<BR>	 2. A physician.<BR>	 3. A waterpot. E.<BR>वच् to speak, अरच् aff., and च changed to ठ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वड्
वड्(इ)वडि r. 1st cl. (वण्डते)<BR>	 1. To partition, to share or divide.<BR>	 2. To<BR>surround or encompass.<BR>	 3. To cover: in the first sense it is some-<BR>times read as a root of the 10th cl. (वण्डयति-ते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडभि|वडभिः
वडभि f. (-भिः or भी)<BR>	 1. The wooden frame of a thatch.<BR>	 2. A temporary<BR>building or awning on the top of a palace, or a room or turret so<BR>situated.<BR> E. वल् to cover, अभच् aff., इन् added, and again optionally<BR>ङीष्, ल changed to ड; otherwise वलभि and वलभी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडा
वडा f. (-डा) Pulse ground and fried with oil or butter.<BR> E. वल् to cover,<BR>अच् and टाप् affs., and ल changed to its congener ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वडिश
वडिश nf. (-शं-शा or शी)<BR>	 1. A fish-hook.<BR>	 2. A bait.<BR> E. वटिन् having a<BR>string, शी to destroy, ड aff.; the radical ट changed to ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वड्र|वड्रं
वड्र mfn. (-ड्रः-ड्रा-ड्रं) Large, great.<BR> E. वल् to cover, रक् aff., ल changed to ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्
वण्(ऋ)वणृ r. 1st cl. (वणति) To sound; also वन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ट्|वंट्
वण्ट् r. 10th cl. (वण्टयति-ते) To partition, to separate or divide; also वटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ट|वंट|वण्टः
वण्ट m. (-ण्टः)<BR>	 1. A part, a portion.<BR>	 2. A man unmarried.<BR>	 3. The handle<BR>of a sickle.<BR> E. वटि to divide, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टक|वंटक|वंटकः|वण्टकः
वण्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A part, a portion, a share.<BR>	 2. A distributer.<BR>	 3. Dis-<BR>tributing.<BR> E. वटि to divide, घञ्, and कन् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टन|वंटन|वंटनं
वण्टन n. (-नं) Portioning, dividing.<BR> E. वटि to divide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टनीय
वण्टनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Divisible, to be divided.<BR> E. वटि to divide,<BR>अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्टाल|वंटाल|वंटालः|वण्टालः
वण्टाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A contest of heroes.<BR>	 2. A boat.<BR>	 3. A shovel, a hoe: also वण्डाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठ|वंठ|वण्ठः
वण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>	 1. An unmarried man.<BR>	 2. A dwarf.<BR>	 3. A javelin.<BR>	 f. (-ण्ठा)<BR>1. Dwarfish.<BR>	 2. Unmarried.<BR> E. वठि to go alone, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ठर|वंठर|वंठरः|वण्ठरः
वण्ठर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The new shoot of the Tāl or palm tree.<BR>	 2. The sheath<BR>that envelopes the young bamboo.<BR>	 3. A rope for tying a goat, &c.<BR>4. A female breast.<BR>	 5. A dog's tail.<BR>	 6. A dog.<BR>	 7. A cloud.<BR> E. वठि<BR>to go alone, aff. अरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्ड|वंड|वण्डः
वण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Maimed, defective, crippled, but especially<BR>in the hands.<BR>	 2. Unmarried.<BR>	 3. Impotent, emasculated.<BR>	 m. (-ण्डः)<BR>1. A man who is circumcised or has no prepuce.<BR>	 2. An ox without<BR>his tail.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा) An unchaste woman.<BR> E. वण् to sound, &c., aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्डर|वंडर|वंडरः|वण्डरः
वण्डर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A niggard, a miser.<BR>	 2. An eunuch or attendant on<BR>the woman's apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वण्डाल|वंडाल|वंडालः|वण्डालः
वण्डाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A description of conflict, the contest of heroes.<BR>	 2.<BR>A boat.<BR>	 3. A spade, a hoe.<BR> E. वडि to divide, आलच् aff.; also वण्टाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्
वत् Ind. As, like, similar: this is more generally considered as an<BR>affix to words, termed technically वति, as ब्राह्मणवत् like a Brāh<BR>man, &c.<BR>	 f. (-वती) An affix added to nouns to form possessive<BR>adjectives, as लक्ष्मीवत्; also added to past passive participles to<BR>form past active participles, as कृतवत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत
वत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Uttered, sounded, spoken.<BR>	 2. Asked, begged.<BR>Ind.<BR>	 1. A particle analogous to ah, oh, &c. expressing sorrow.<BR>	 2.<BR>Compassion.<BR>	 3. Pleasure.<BR>	 4. Oh, ho, a vocative particle.<BR> E. वन् to<BR>ask or beg, &c. aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतंस|वतंसः
वतंस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. An ear-ring.<BR>	 2. A crest.<BR> E. अव before, तसि to adorn,<BR>and अच् aff., the initial rejected; also अवतंस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतण्ड|वतण्डः
वतण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The name of a Muni.<BR> E. अव before, तडि to beat, aff. अच्, अ rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वतोका
वतोका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A cow miscarrying from accident.<BR>	 2. A barren wo-<BR>man.<BR> E. अव before, तोक offspring, and अ rejected; also अवतोका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्स|वत्सं|वत्सः
वत्स n. (-त्सं) The breast, the chest.<BR>	 m. (-त्सः)<BR>	 1. A calf.<BR>	 2. A year.<BR>	 mf.<BR>(-त्सः-त्सा) A term of endearment, used to children, scholars, &c. E.<BR>वद् to speak, to speak kindly to, or वस् to love, Unādi aff. स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सक|वत्सकं|वत्सकः
वत्सक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A calf.<BR>	 2. A child.<BR>	 3. A medicinal plant, (Wrightea<BR>antidysenterica.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) Black sulphate of iron.<BR> E. वत्स and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सकाम
वत्सकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Fond of or anxious about a child.<BR>	 f. (-मा) A<BR>cow anxious after her calf, a mother anxious after her child, &c.<BR>E. वत्स a calf, &c. and काम् to desire, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सगुरु
वत्सगुरु m. (-रुः) A master.<BR> E. वत्म, and गुरु teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सतर|वत्सतरः
वत्सतर m. (-रः) A steer.<BR>	 f. (-रिः or री) A heifer.<BR> E. वत्स a calf, and तरप्<BR>aff. of excess; more than a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सतन्त्री
वत्सतन्त्री f. (-न्त्री) The rope that ties a calf.<BR> E. वत्स, and तन्त्री a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सनाभ|वत्सनाभः
वत्सनाभ m. (-भः) An active poison; also called Mītha Zeher, the root<BR>of the Aconite ferox brought from Nepāl.<BR> E. वत्स a calf, and नभ्<BR>to injure, अण् aff.; the root is sometimes compared to the nipple<BR>of a cow, whence perhaps this etymology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सपत्तन|वत्सपत्तनं
वत्सपत्तन n. (-नं) The name of a city in the north of India; one place<BR>to which it is applied is now a village in the district of Gorakhpur<BR>E. वत्स a calf, and पत्तन a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सर|वत्सरः
वत्सर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A year.<BR>	 2. An epithet of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. वस् to abide, सरन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सरान्तक|वत्सरांतक|वत्सरान्तकः
वत्सरान्तक m. (-कः) The month Phālguṇa.<BR> E. वत्सर, and अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सल|वत्सलः
वत्सल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Afflctionate, kind.<BR>	 n. (-लं) Affection, fondness.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला) A cow anxious for her calf.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A fire fed with grass.<BR>E. वत्स a child, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सलता
वत्सलता f. (-ता) Tenderness, affection.<BR> E. वत्सल, तल् aff.; also with त्व, वत्सलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्साक्षी
वत्साक्षी f. (-क्षी) A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis madraspatanus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सादन|वत्सादनः
वत्सादन m. (-नः) A wolf.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.) E.<BR>वत्स a calf, अदन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सिमन्
वत्सिमन् m. (-मा) Youth, childhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वत्सीय|वत्सीयः
वत्सीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Proper or fit for a calf.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A cowherd. E.<BR>वत्स a calf, &c., and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद्
वद् r. 1st and 10th cl. (वदति-ते वदयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To inform, to speak to or<BR>tell, to declare.<BR>	 2. To speak articulately.<BR>	 3. To abide.<BR>	 4. To shine.<BR>5. To be an authority on.<BR>	 6. To toil. With अनु, (अनुवदते) 1. To<BR>speak similarly or subsequently.<BR>	 2. To resound.<BR>	 3. To confirm, to<BR>ratify.<BR>	 4. To imitate in loud and distinct voice. With अप prefixed,<BR>(अपवदति-ते) To reprove, to censure. With, अभि, To salute respect-<BR>fully or by name. With उप, (उपवदते) 1. To explain.<BR>	 2. To flatter,<BR>to cajole.<BR>	 3. To conciliate, to persuade. With निर्, To speak out<BR>or plainly. With परि, (परिवदति) To speak against. With प्र, 1. To<BR>rumour, to slander.<BR>	 2. To call.<BR>	 3. To consider. With प्रति, (प्रति-<BR>वदति) To reply to or answer. With वि, (विवदते) 1. To dispute.<BR>	 2.<BR>To litigate. With वि and प्र, (विप्रवदति or -ते) To wrangle or dispute<BR>together. With वि, and प्र, To break a promise. With सम and प्र,<BR>(संप्रवदते) To speak articulately in concert; (संप्रवदति) To utter<BR>or articulate sounds together. With सम, 1. To converse.<BR>	 2. To<BR>speak to.<BR>	 3. To call, to name.<BR>	 4. To coincide, to resemble, (with<BR>an inst.) Caus. (वादयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cause to utter.<BR>	 2. To play on an<BR>instrument. With अभि, To salute. With वि, and सम्, To make<BR>inconsistent. With सम्, To consult, (with an inst.) (इ) वदि (वन्दते)<BR>1. To salute with reverence or respect.<BR>	 2. To praise, to eulogize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद|वदः
वद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Speaking, able to speak, speaking well or sensibly.<BR>E. वद् to speak, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदत्
वदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्) Speaking, saying.<BR> E. वद् to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन|वदनं
वदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The mouth, the face.<BR>	 2. The front.<BR>	 3. Look, appearance.<BR>4. The summit or apex of a triangle.<BR> E. वद् to speak, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदनसरोज
वदनसरोज n. (-जं) The face of a mistress.<BR> E. वदन, and सरोज a lotus;<BR>also similar compounds, and वदनाम्बुरुह वदनारविन्द, वदनकमल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदनासव|वदनासवः
वदनासव m. (-वः) Saliva, the moisture of the lips.<BR> E. वदन the mouth,<BR>आसव spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदनेन्दु
वदनेन्दु m. (-न्दुः) The face.<BR> E. वदन, इन्दु the moon; also similar com-<BR>pounds, as वदनचन्द्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=627-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन्ति|वदन्तिः
वदन्ति f. (-न्तिः-न्ती) Speech, discourse, talk.<BR> E. वद् to say or speak, झिच्<BR>Unādi aff., ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदन्य|वदन्यः
वदन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Munificent, bountiful.<BR> E. वद् to speak, aff. अन्य; also वदान्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदमान
वदमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Saying, calling.<BR>	 2. Glorifying, boasting. E.<BR>वद् to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदरिक
वदरिक m. (-कः) The jujube: see बदरि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदान्य|वदान्यः
वदान्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Liberal, munificent.<BR>	 2. Speaking kindly or<BR>agreeably.<BR>	 3. Eloquent.<BR> E. वद् to speak, अन्य Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदाल|वदालः
वदाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A sheat-fish, (Silurus Boalis, HAM.)<BR>	 2. A whirl-pool.<BR>E. वद् to speak, aff. आलच्, also with कन् added, वदालक m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदावद|वदावदः
वदावद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Speaking, a speaker, able to speak, able to speak<BR>well, eloquent.<BR> E. वद् to speak, aff. अच्, the root repeated, and आ<BR>inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वदि
वदि Ind. In the dark half of, (any month.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वद्य
वद्य f. (-द्या) Adj.<BR>	 1. Unblamable.<BR>	 2. The second or dark, (fortnight of<BR>a lunar month.)<BR>	 n. (-द्यं) Speech, speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधु|वधुः
वधु f. (-धुः)<BR>	 1. A son's wife.<BR>	 2. A wife in general. वह् to bear, उ aff.; more commonly वधू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधुका
वधुका f. (-का) A wife.<BR> E. वधु for वधू, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधुटी
वधुटी f. (-टी) A daughter-in-law: see वधूटी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधू
वधू f. (-धूः)<BR>	 1. Woman in general, a female.<BR>	 2. A wife.<BR>	 3. A young<BR>wife, one recently married, a bride.<BR>	 4. A son's wife.<BR>	 5. A sort of<BR>bulbous root, (Curcuma reclinata.)<BR>	 6. A gramineous plant,<BR>(Trigonella corniculata:) see पृक्का 7. A plant, (Echites frute-<BR>scens.)<BR> E. वह् to bear, उ aff., and ह changed to ध; also derived<BR>from बध् to bind, in which case it is written बधू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूजन|वधूजनः
वधूजन m. (-नः) A woman.<BR> E. वधू a female, and जन person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूटी
वधूटी f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. A son's wife.<BR>	 2. A young woman living in her father's<BR>house, whether married or unmarried.<BR> E. वधू wife, टी aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूवस्त्र
वधूवस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) Bridal apparel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधूशयन
वधूशयन n. (-नं) A lattice, a loophole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्
वन् r. 1st and 10th cls. (वनति वानयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To serve, to<BR>honour.<BR>	 3. To help.<BR>	 4. To be distressed. (उ) वनु r. 1st and 10th<BR>cls. (वनति वानयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To act, to transact business.<BR>	 2. To injure;<BR>r. 8th cl. (वनुते) To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन|वनं
वन nf. (-नं-नी) A forest, a wood, a grove.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. A resi-<BR>dence, a dwelling or abode.<BR>	 3. A house.<BR>	 4. Timber.<BR>	 5. A cascade<BR>or fountain.<BR> E. वन् to sound, to serve, to seek, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनकचु
वनकचु m. (-चुः) A species of Arum, (A. calocasia.)<BR> E. वन, and कचु the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनकणा
वनकणा f. (-णा) Wild pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनकरिन्
वनकरिन् m. (-री) A wild elephant.<BR> E. वन, and करिन् an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनकार्प्पासी|वनकार्पासी
वनकार्प्पासी f. (-सी) Wild cotton, or a plant resembling it, (Hibiscus<BR>vitifolius.)<BR> E. वन a wood, and कार्प्पासी cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनकुक्कुट|वनकुक्कुटः
वनकुक्कुट m. (-टः) Wild fowl.<BR> E. वन and कुक्कुट a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनगज
वनगज m. (-जः) A wild elephant.<BR> E. वन, and गज an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनगहन
वनगहन n. (-नं) A thicket.<BR> E. वन, and गहन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनगुप्त|वनगुप्तः
वनगुप्त m. (-प्तः) A spy, an emissary.<BR> E. वन a wood, and गुप्त concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनगो
वनगो f. (-गौः) The Gāyal, (Bos Gavæus.)<BR> E. वन wood, and गो a cow;<BR>also वनगव m. (-वः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनगोचर|वनगोचरः
वनगोचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Frequenting forests.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A hunter, a<BR>forester.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A forest.<BR> E. वन, and गोचर an object, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनचन्दन|वनचंदन|वनचन्दनं
वनचन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Aloe-wood or Agallochum.<BR>	 2. A sort of pine, (Pinus<BR>Devadāru.)<BR> E. वन a wood, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनचर|वनचरः
वनचर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A forester, a woodman.<BR>	 2. A wild animal.<BR>	 3. The<BR>fabulous animal called Sārabha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनचारिन्
वनचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Forest, forester, savage.<BR> E. वन, and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनच्छेद
वनच्छेद m. (-दः) Cutting timber.<BR> E. वन, and छेद who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनछाग|वनच्छाग|वनच्छागः
वनछाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A wild goat.<BR>	 2. A hog.<BR> E. वन a wood, and छाग a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनछिद्|वनच्छिद्
वनछिद् m. (-द्) A wood-cutter.<BR> E. वन, and छिद् who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनज|वनजं|वनजः
वनज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Wild, forest, born or produced in a wood.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>A lotus.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>	 2. An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">Page628-b+ 60</a>]<BR>elephant.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. A sort of pulse, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>wild cotton tree.<BR>	 3. Wild ginger.<BR> E. वन wood, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनजीविन्
वनजीविन् m. (-वी) A woodman, a forester.<BR> E. वन, and जीविन् who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनतिक्त|वनतिक्तः
वनतिक्त m. (-क्तः) A sort of myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>	 f. (-क्ता)<BR>A plant, commonly Ākanādi, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR> E. वन<BR>wood, तिक्त bitter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनतिक्तिका
वनतिक्तिका f. (-का) A climbing plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR> E. कन्<BR>in the fem. form added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनद|वनदः
वनद m. (-दः) A cloud.<BR> E. वन water, and द what yield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनदीप|वनदीपः
वनदीप m. (-पः) The Champaka, (Michelia Champaca.)<BR> E. वन a wood,<BR>and दीप a lamp or illuminator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनधारा
वनधारा f. (-रा) An avenue of trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनधेनु|वनधेनुः
वनधेनु f. (-नुः) The female of the Bos Gavæus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनपल्लव|वनपल्लवः
वनपल्लव m. (-वः) A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga, &c.)<BR> E. वन a wood,<BR>पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनपांशुल|वनपांशुलः
वनपांशुल m. (-लः) A hunter, a deer-killer.<BR> E. वन a wood, पांशुल a low man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनपादप
वनपादप m. (-पः) A forest tree.<BR> E. वन, पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनपूरक|वनपूरकः
वनपूरक m. (-कः) The wild citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनप्रवेश|वनप्रवेशः
वनप्रवेश m. (-शः) Entering a forest, commencing to live as a hermit.<BR> E. वन, प्रवेश entry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनप्रस्थ|वनप्रस्थः
वनप्रस्थ n. (-स्थं) A wood situated on table land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनप्रिय|वनप्रियं|वनप्रियः
वनप्रिय m. (-यः) The Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. वन a wood, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनभुज्
वनभुज् m. (-भुक्) A medicinal root, commonly Rishabha.<BR> E. वन a wood,<BR>भुज् to eat, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमल्ली
वनमल्ली f. (-ल्ली) Wild jasmine.<BR> E. वन a wood, मल्ली jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमाक्षिका
वनमाक्षिका f. (-का) A gad-fly.<BR> E. वन a wood, and माक्षिका fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमाला
वनमाला f. (-ला) The chaplet or garland worn by KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. वन a<BR>wood, and माला necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमालिन्
वनमालिन् m. (-ली) KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Dvārakā the capital of KṚṢṆA.<BR>2. A female energy of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. वनमाला as above, इनि, ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमुच्
वनमुच् m. (-मुक्) a cloud.<BR> E. वन water, and मुच् to let loose, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमुद्ग|वनमुद्गः
वनमुद्ग m. (-द्गः) A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR> E. वन a<BR>wood, मुद्ग kidney-bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनमूत|वनमूतः
वनमूत m. (-तः) A cloud.<BR> E. वन water, and मूत sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनर|वनरः
वनर m. (-रः) A monkey.<BR> E. वन a wood, रम् to play, aff. ड; also वानर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनराज|वनराजः
वनराज m. (-जः) A lion.<BR> E. वन a wood, and राजन् a sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनराजि|वनराजिः
वनराजि mfn. (-जिः-जिः or जी-जि) Embellishing or beautifying a forest.<BR>E. वन, राजृ to shine, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनलक्ष्मी
वनलक्ष्मी f. (-क्ष्मी)<BR>	 1. The plantain.<BR>	 2. The beauty of a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवर्त्तिन्|वनवर्तिन्
वनवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) Residing in the woods.<BR> E. वन, वर्त्तिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवह्नि|वनवह्निः
वनवह्नि m. (-ह्निः) A forest-conflagration.<BR> E. वन a forest, and वह्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवास|वनवासः
वनवास m. (-सः) Living in the woods, as a hermit, &c.<BR> E. वन, वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवासन|वनवासनः
वनवासन m. (-नः) A civet or pole cat.<BR> E. वन a wood, वस् to dwell, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनवासिन्
वनवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Wild, forest, who or what dwells in woods.<BR>m. (-सी)<BR>	 1. An anchoret, a hermit.<BR>	 2. A forester.<BR> E. वन forest, वास<BR>abode, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनविडाल
वनविडाल m. (-लः) A sort of wild cat, (Felis caracal.)<BR> E. वन, and विडाल a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनव्रीहि|वनव्रीहिः
वनव्रीहि m. (-हिः) Rice growing wild in pools or swamps, and consi-<BR>dered by botanists, as the parent stock of all the varieties cul-<BR>tivated in India.<BR> E. वन wood or water, and व्रीहि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनशृङ्गाट|वनशृङ्गाटः
वनशृङ्गाट m. (-टः) A plant, (Ruellia longifolia:) see गोक्षर.<BR> E. वन a wood,<BR>and शृङ्गाट the same plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनशोभन|वनशोभनं
वनशोभन n. (-नं) A lotus.<BR> E. वन water, शोभन adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनश्वन्
वनश्वन् m. (-श्वा)<BR>	 1. A jackal.<BR>	 2. A tiger.<BR>	 3. A civet or pole cat.<BR> E. वन a<BR>wood, श्वन् a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनसङ्कट|वनसंकट|वनसङ्कटः
वनसङ्कट m. (-टः) A sort of pulse, (Ervum hirsutum.)<BR> E. वन a wood,<BR>सङ्कट what contracts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनसमूह|वनसमूहः
वनसमूह m. (-हः) A multitude of groves or forests.<BR> E. वन, and समूह a<BR>collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनसरोजिनी
वनसरोजिनी f. (-नी) The wild cotton plant.<BR> E. वन wild, सरोजिनी Hibiscus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्थ|वनस्थः
वनस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Wild, savage, forest or grove-abiding, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">Page629-a+ 60</a>]<BR>(-स्थः)<BR>	 1. A deer.<BR>	 2. A hermit.<BR>	 f. (-स्था) The holy-fig tree.<BR> E. वन (in)<BR>a wood, and स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=628-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्थली
वनस्थली f. (-ली) Forest-ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्थायिन्
वनस्थायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Being or abiding in a wood.<BR>	 m. (-यी) A<BR>hermit, an anchoret.<BR> E. वन, स्थायिन् who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्थित
वनस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Situated or being in a forest.<BR> E. वन, स्थित what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्पति|वनस्पतिः
वनस्पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A tree that bears fruit but no apparent blossoms,<BR>as several species of the fig, the jack, &c.<BR>	 2. A tree in general.<BR>3. An ascetic.<BR> E. वन forest, and पति lord, सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्रज्
वनस्रज् f. (स्रक् or स्रग्) A garland of forest flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनहास|वनहासः
वनहास m. (-सः) A sort of tall grass, (Saccharum spontaneum.)<BR> E. वन<BR>wood, and हास a smile, from हस् to laugh, with घञ् aff.; also<BR>with कन् added, वनहासक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाकम्प
वनाकम्प m. (-म्पः) Shaking of the trees of wood by the wind.<BR> E. वन, आकम्प trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाखु|वनाखुः
वनाखु m. (-खुः) A hare.<BR> E. वन a wood, and आखु a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाखुक|वनाखुकः
वनाखुक m. (-कः) A sort of bean, (Phaseolus Mungo.)<BR> E. अव-नख-उकञ् अवाल्लोपः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाज|वनाजः
वनाज m. (-जः) A wild goat.<BR> E. वन a wood, and अज a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाटु|वनाटुः
वनाटु m. (-टुः)<BR>	 1. The anus.<BR>	 2. A blue fly.<BR> E. वन a thicket, अट् to go, उन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनान्त|वनांत|वनान्तः
वनान्त n. (-न्तं) The skirts of a wood.<BR> E. वन, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनापगा
वनापगा f. (-गा) A forest stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाभिलाव
वनाभिलाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Wood-destroying.<BR> E. वन, अभिलाव destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनामल|वनामलः
वनामल m. (-लः) A fruit, (Carissa carondas.)<BR> E. वन wood, and आमल for<BR>आमलक myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनायु|वनायुः
वनायु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. A country distinguished for its breed of horses, (i. e.)<BR>ARABIA. also वानायु.<BR>	 2. An antelope.<BR> E. वन, आयुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनायुज|वनायुजः
वनायुज m. (-जः) A horse of the Vanāyu breed.<BR> E. वनायु a country, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनारिष्टा
वनारिष्टा f. (-ष्टा) Wild turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनार्च्चक|वनार्चक|वनार्चकः|वनार्च्चकः
वनार्च्चक m. (-कः) A flower-gatherer.<BR> E. वन a wood, अर्च्च् to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनालक्त
वनालक्त n. (-क्तं) Red earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनालिका
वनालिका f. (-का) A sun-flower, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR> E. वन a wood,<BR>अल् to adorn, aff. वन् and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाश्रय|वनाश्रयः
वनाश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Forest, forester, who or what is in a forest.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-यः)<BR>	 1. A raven, or perhaps more properly a sort of crow.<BR>	 2.<BR>Dwelling in a forest.<BR> E. वन a wood, आश्रय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाश्रित
वनाश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Leading the life of a hermit, &c.<BR> E. वन, आश्रित repaired to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाहिर|वनाहिरः
वनाहिर m. (-रः) A hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनि|वनिः
वनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Fire or its deity.<BR>	 2. Wish, desire.<BR> E. वन् to worship,<BR>Unādi aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिका
वनिका f. (-का) A woody place, a grove.<BR> E. वनी, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनित|वनितः
वनित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Solicited, begged.<BR>	 2. Served.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A wo-<BR>man in general.<BR>	 2. A beloved woman, a wife, a mistress.<BR> E. वन्<BR>to ask, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिताविलास|वनिताविलासः
वनिताविलास m. (-सः) The wanton sport of woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिन्
वनिन् m. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. A Brāhman in the third stage of his life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिष्ठु|वनिष्ठुः
वनिष्ठु m. (-ष्ठुः) The entrails of an animal offered in sacrifice.<BR> E. वन् to<BR>worship, इष्ठुच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिष्णु
वनिष्णु Adj. Begging, soliciting.<BR> E. वन, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीक|वनीकः
वनीक m. (-कः) A beggar; also वनीयक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीयक|वनीयकः
वनीयक m. (-कः) A beggar, a mendicant.<BR> E. वन् to ask, इन् aff., क्यच्<BR>and वुन् added; also य being changed to प, वनीपक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेक्षुद्रा
वनेक्षुद्रा f. (-द्रा) A tree, commonly Karañja.<BR> E. वने in a wood, क्षुद्रा small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेचर|वनेचरः
वनेचर mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं) Who or what inhabits in a wood, forest,<BR>&c, a forester.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A forester, one of a savage tribe in-<BR>habiting woods, a sylvan, a satyr.<BR>	 2. An imp, &c.<BR> E. वने in a forest,<BR>चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेचराग्र्य
वनेचराग्र्य m. (-ग्र्यः) An ascetic, an anchorite.<BR> E. वनेचर and अग्र्य a chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेशय
वनेशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Living in the woods.<BR> E. वने, शी to sleep, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनैकदेश
वनैकदेश m. (-शः) A part of a thicket.<BR> E. वन, and एकदेश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनोत्साह|वनोत्साहः
वनोत्साह m. (-हः) A rhinoceros.<BR> E. वन a wood, and उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनोद्देश
वनोद्देश m. (-शः) A part of a thicket.<BR> E. वन, and उद्देश direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनोद्भव
वनोद्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced in a forest.<BR>	 f. (-वा) Wild cotton.<BR> E. वन a<BR>wood, उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीकस्
वनीकस् m. (-काः)<BR>	 1. A forester.<BR>	 2. A monkey, an ape.<BR>	 3. An ascetic. E.<BR>वन wood, ओकस् dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दका
वन्दका f. (-का) A parasite plant.<BR> E. वन्दा the same, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दथ|वंदथ|वंदथः|वन्दथः
वन्दथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A panegyrist, a eulogist, a bard.<BR>	 2. One deserving<BR>praise or eulogium.<BR> E. वन्द् to praise, Unādi aff. अथ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दन|वंदन|वंदनं|वन्दनं
वन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The face or mouth.<BR>	 2. Obeisance to a Brāhmana or<BR>superior by touching the feet, &c.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Reverence, worship,<BR>adoring.<BR>	 2. Begging, soliciting, asking.<BR>	 3. A drug for reviving the<BR>dead.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Praise, praising, especially the gods or great men.<BR>E. वदि to praise, aff. ल्युट् or युच्, fem. aff. ङीष् or टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनमाला|वंदनमाला
वन्दनमाला f. (-ला) The ornamented arch of a gate-way.<BR> E. वन्दन praising,<BR>माला a garland; being hung with flowers on festival occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनमालिका|वंदनमालिका
वन्दनमालिका f. (-का) The ornamented arch of a gate way.<BR> E. वन्दन<BR>praising, माला a garland, कन् aff. in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनीय|वंदनीय|वन्दनीयः
वन्दनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Praise-worthy, to be eulogised.<BR>	 f. (-या) A yellow<BR>substance used as a pigment, said in the Tantras to be procured<BR>from the head of a cow: see रोचना.<BR> E. वदि to praise, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दा|वंदा
वन्दा f. (-न्दा)<BR>	 1. A parasite plant, (Epidendrum tessellatum, &c.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Any parasite plant.<BR>	 3. A female beggar.<BR> E. वदि to praise, affs.<BR>अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दाका
वन्दाका f. (-का) A parasite plant.<BR> E. वदि, आकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दार|वन्दारः
वन्दार m. (-रः) A parasite plant.<BR> E. वन्दा the same, ऋ to go, or be, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दारु|वंदारु|वन्दारुः
वन्दारु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु)<BR>	 1. Civil, complementary, polite.<BR>	 2. Praising,<BR>celebrating.<BR>	 m. (-रुः) A panegyrist, a bard.<BR> E. वदि to praise, आरु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दि|वन्दिः
वन्दि f. (-न्दिः or न्दी)<BR>	 1. A captive, a prisoner, man or beast confined.<BR>	 2.<BR>A ladder or stairs.<BR> E. वदि to praise, aff., इन्, ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिग्राह|वन्दिग्राहः
वन्दिग्राह m. (-हः) A housebreaker, especially one who breaks into the<BR>place in which the sacred fire is preserved, into an armoury, or a<BR>temple.<BR> E. वन्दि captive, (what is confined or shut up,) ग्राह who<BR>seizes; also वन्दिचौर &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिचौर|वन्दिचौरः
वन्दिचौर m. (-रः) A thief, a housebreaker.<BR> E. वन्दि, and चौर thief: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिन्|वंदिन्
वन्दिन् m. (-न्दी)<BR>	 1. A panegyrist, a bard, a herald, a servant whose<BR>duty it is to proclaim the titles of a great man as he passes along;<BR>or a poet, who sings the praises of a prince in his presence, or<BR>accompanies an army, to chant martial songs: considered as<BR>one of a distinct tribe, he is the son of a Kṣatriya by a Śūdra<BR>female.<BR>	 2. A flatterer.<BR>	 3. A prisoner.<BR> E. वदि to praise, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिपाठ|वन्दिपाठः
वन्दिपाठ m. (-ठः) A complementary stanza, a panegyric, a eulogium,<BR>often improvisatore, recited by a bard.<BR> E. वन्दि a bard, पाठ reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दीकार|वन्दीकारः
वन्दीकार m. (-रः) A thief, a housebreaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्य|वंद्य
वन्द्य mfn. (-न्द्यः-न्द्या-न्द्यं) To be praised, commendable, laudable.<BR>	 f. (-न्द्या)<BR>A parasite plant.<BR> E. वदि to praise, यत् aff., or यक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्र|वंद्र|वन्द्रं|वंद्रः|वन्द्रः
वन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A worshipper.<BR>	 n. (-न्द्रं) Prosperity.<BR> E. वन्द् to praise, aff. रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्य|वन्यं|वन्यः
वन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Forest, savage, wild, produced in a wood, &c.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-न्या)<BR>	 1. A multitude of groves.<BR>	 2. A quantity of water, a flood,<BR>a deluge.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR> E. वन् a wood, &c., यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्न|वन्नः
वन्न m. (-न्नः) A co-partner, a co-heir, &c.<BR> E. वत् to ask, रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्
वप्(ड)डुवप r. 1st cl. (वपति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sow seed.<BR>	 2. To procreate.<BR>	 3. To<BR>shave.<BR>	 4. To weave. With आ, To scatter. With नि, 1. To scatter<BR>seed.<BR>	 2. To make offerings to the MANES.<BR>	 3. To kill. With निस्, 1.<BR>To scatter.<BR>	 2. To perform.<BR>	 3. To offer.<BR>	 4. To present libations to<BR>the MANES. With प्रति, 1. To sow.<BR>	 2. To pierce, to fix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप|वपः
वप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Shaving.<BR>	 2. Sowing seed.<BR>	 3. Weaving.<BR>	 f. (-पा)<BR>	 1. The<BR>mucous or glutinous secretion of the flesh or bones; according to<BR>some, also the marrow of the bones.<BR>	 2. Any hole or cavity.<BR> E. वप्<BR>to sow seed, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपन|वपनं
वपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sowing seed.<BR>	 2. Shaving.<BR>	 3. Semen virile.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>barber's shop.<BR>	 2. A weaver's workshop.<BR> E. वप् to shave, &c. aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=629-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपाकृत्
वपाकृत् m. (-कृत्) Marrow.<BR> E. वपा, कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपिल|वपिलः
वपिल m. (-लः) A father.<BR> E. वप् to sow seed, (figuratively,) इलच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुन|वपुनः
वपुन m. (-नः) A deity.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Knowledge.<BR> E. वप् to sow, उनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुर्धर
वपुर्धर Adj.<BR>	 1. Embodied.<BR>	 2. Beautiful, handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष्टमा
वपुष्टमा f. (-मा) A plant, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष्मत्|वपुष्मन्त्
वपुष्मत् mfn. (-ष्मान्-ष्मन्ती-ष्मत्) Having a body, corporeal, incarnate.<BR> E. वपुस्, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुस्
वपुस् n. (-पुः)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. A handsome form or figure.<BR>	 3. Beauty,<BR>beautiful appearance.<BR> E. वप् to sow, Unādi aff. उसि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुस्रव
वपुस्रव m. (-वः) A humour of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्तव्य
वप्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be sown.<BR>	 2. To be given, conferred,<BR>implanted, &c.<BR>	 3. To be emitted seminally, to be impregnated or<BR>begotten.<BR> E. वप् to sow, तव्य aff.; also वपनीय &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्तृ
वप्तृ mfn. (-प्ता-प्त्री-प्तृ) A sower, a planter, &c.<BR>	 m. (-प्ता)<BR>	 1. A father, a pro-<BR>genitor.<BR>	 2. A poet.<BR>	 3. A sage.<BR> E. वप् to sow, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्र|वप्रं|वप्रः
वप्र mn. (-प्रः-प्रं)<BR>	 1. A field.<BR>	 2. A rampart, a mud-wall, earth taken<BR>from the ditch of a town and raised as a wall or buttress, or as<BR>the foundation of a wall of masonry, &c.<BR>	 3. The foundation of<BR>any building.<BR>	 4. The gate of a fortified city.<BR>	 5. A shore or bank.<BR>6. Dust, earth.<BR>	 7. A mound, a hillock.<BR>	 8. The slope of a hill.<BR>	 9. A<BR>summit, a peak.<BR>	 10. A ditch.<BR>	 11. A field.<BR>	 12. The butting of an<BR>elephant or bull.<BR>	 m. (-प्रः) A father.<BR>	 n. (-प्रं) Lead.<BR>	 f. (-प्री) A<BR>hillock, an ant-hill.<BR> E. वप् to sow, रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रक्रीडा
वप्रक्रीडा f. (-डा) Butting, as of an elephant or bull, &c., against a bank.<BR>E. वप्र a mound, and क्रीडा sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रानत
वप्रानत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bowed or stooping to butt at a wall or bank.<BR> E. वप्र, आनत bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रान्तर
वप्रान्तर Ind. In or between banks, mounds, &c.<BR> E. वप्र, अन्तर् within.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्राभिघात|वप्राभिघातः
वप्राभिघात m. (-तः) Butting at a bank or mound.<BR> E. वप्र, अभिघात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्राम्भस्
वप्राम्भस् n. (-म्भः) The water near or along the bank.<BR> E. वप्र, अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रि|वप्रिः
वप्रि m. (-प्रिः)<BR>	 1. A field.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR> E. वप् to sow, Unādi aff. रि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वभ्र्
वभ्र् r. 1st cl. (वभ्रति) To go; also बभ्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्
वम्(टु, उ)टुवमु r. 1st cl. (वमति) To vomit, to eject from the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम|वमः
वम mf. (-मः-मी) Vomiting.<BR> E. वम् to vomit, aff. अच्; also वमन and वमि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमथु|वमथुः
वमथु m. (-थुः)<BR>	 1. Vomiting, ejecting any thing from the mouth.<BR>	 2.<BR>Water ejected from an elephant's trunk.<BR> E. वम् to vomit, aff. अथुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमन|वमनं|वमनः
वमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Vomiting, ejecting any thing from the mouth.<BR>	 2.<BR>Causing vomiting, an emetic.<BR>	 3. Pain.<BR>	 4. Offering oblations to<BR>fire.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Hemp.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A leech.<BR> E. वम् to vomit, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमनीया
वमनीया f. (-या) A fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमि|वमिः
वमि m. (-मिः or मी)<BR>	 1. Vomiting, sickness.<BR>	 2. An emetic.<BR>	 m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of fire.<BR>	 2. A rogue, a cheat.<BR> E. वम् to vomit, aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमित|वमितः
वमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sickened, made to vomit.<BR> E. वम् to be sick,<BR>causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमित्वा
वमित्वा Ind. Having vomited or been sick.<BR> E. वम् to be sick, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमिन्
वमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Vomiting, sick.<BR> E. वम् to vomit, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्भारव|वंभारव|वंभारवः|वम्भारवः
वम्भारव m. (-वः) The lowing of a cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्री
वम्री f. (-म्री) A small ant burrowing in trees; also वम्रा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्रीकूट|वम्रीकूटः
वम्रीकूट n. (-टं) An ant-hill, a hillock.<BR> E. वम्री a sort of ant, कूट a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वय्
वय् r. 1st cl. (वयते) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयन|वयनं
वयन n. (-नं) Weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्
वयस् n. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. Age, time of life.<BR>	 3. Youth.<BR> E. वय् to go,<BR>असुन् aff.; or वी as substituted for अज् to go, with the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्क
वयस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) Relating to age, aged.<BR> E. वयस् and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःस्थ|वयःस्थः
वयःस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Middle-aged, young, &c.: see वयस्थ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्थ|वयस्थः
वयस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Young, in the prime of life.<BR>	 2. Mature, mid-<BR>dle-aged, past childhood, or from sixteen to seventy.<BR>	 m. (-स्थः) A<BR>friend, an associate, a contemporary.<BR>	 f. (-स्था)<BR>	 1. The moon-plant,<BR>(Asclepias acida.)<BR>	 2. Emblic myrobalan, (Phyllanthus emblica.)<BR>3. Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>	 4. Small cardamoms.<BR>5. A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>	 6. A medicinal root, com-<BR>monly Kākoli.<BR>	 7. A woman's female friend or companion, a con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">Page630-b+ 60</a>]<BR>fidante.<BR>	 8. The silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. वयस् life, स्था to be or stay, aff.<BR>क, fem. aff. टाप्, the final of the former changed to Visarga, and<BR>that optionally rejected; hence also वयःस्थ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्य|वयस्यः
वयस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Aged, relating to age.<BR>	 m. (-स्यः) A friend, a co-<BR>temporary, an associate or companion.<BR>	 f. (-स्या) A woman's female<BR>friend or confidante.<BR> E. वयस् life, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयुन|वयुनं|वयुनः
वयुन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>	 2. A temple. (in this sense it is<BR>masc. according to some.)<BR> E. वी substituted for अज् to go, उनन्<BR>Unādi aff.; or वय्-उनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोगत
वयोगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Aged, very old.<BR> E. वयस् and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोधस्
वयोधस् m. (-धाः) A young or middle-aged man.<BR> E. वयस् youth or man-<BR>hood, धा to have, Unādi aff. असि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोधिक
वयोधिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Very old.<BR> E. वयस् and अधिक exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्
वर् r. 10th cl. (वरयति-ते) To desire, to obtain, to covet or ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर|वरं|वरः
वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Best, excellent.<BR>	 2. Eldest.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A boon, a<BR>blessing, especially in the gift of a Brāhmana or deity.<BR>	 2. Enga-<BR>ging, selecting, appointing.<BR>	 3. Requesting, soliciting, especially<BR>prevailing on a person by entreaty to undertake any business.<BR>	 4.<BR>Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>	 5. A husband, a bridegroom.<BR>	 6. A<BR>son-in-law.<BR>	 7. A catamite.<BR>	 8. A drug: see गुग्गुल.<BR>	 9. Wish, desire.<BR>10. A sparrow.<BR>	 n. Adv. (वरं) or Ind. (वरम्) Better, preferable,<BR>it would be better if.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Saffron.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. The three myro-<BR>balans.<BR>	 2. A sort of perfume, commonly Renukā.<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>(Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>	 4. Turmeric.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Asparagus<BR>racemosus.<BR>	 2. A name of CHHĀYĀ, wife of the sun.<BR> E. वृ to<BR>select, to cover, &c., aff. अप् or अच्; it is also derived from<BR>बृ, and is then written with an initial consonant: see बर; also<BR>वर् to desire, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरक|वरकं|वरकः
वरक n. (-कं) The cover or awning of a boat.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A wild kidney-<BR>bean.<BR>	 2. A request.<BR>	 3. A towel, a wiper.<BR>	 4. A cloak.<BR> E. वृ to cover,<BR>aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरक्रतु|वरक्रतुः
वरक्रतु m. (-तुः) INDRA.<BR> E. वर best, क्रतु sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरचन्दन|वरचंदन|वरचन्दनं
वरचन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A dark sort of Sandal or Agallochum.<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>pine, (Pinus Devadāru.)<BR> E. वर best, चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरट|वरटं|वरटः
वरट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A gander.<BR>	 2. A man of a barbarous or foreign race.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-टं) Many flowered jasmine.<BR>	 f. (-टा-टी)<BR>	 1. A goose.<BR>	 2. A wasp, &c.<BR>E. वृ to choose, aff., अटन्; fem. aff. टाप् or ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण|वरणं|वरणः
वरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Appointing, selecting, choosing.<BR>	 2. Surrounding, in-<BR>closing.<BR>	 3. Screening, covering.<BR>	 4. Nourishing, supporting.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-णः)<BR>	 1. An outer building, an enclosure, a wall of masonry, &c.<BR>raised on a mound of earth.<BR>	 2. A causeway, a bridge.<BR>	 3. A camel.<BR>4. A tree, (Capparis trifoliata.)<BR>	 5. Any tree.<BR>	 f. (-णा) A rivulet,<BR>running past the north of Benāres, into the Ganges, now called<BR>the Barunā.<BR> E. वृ to choose or appoint, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणमाला
वरणमाला f. (-ला) The garland placed by the bride on the head of the bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणसी
वरणसी f. (-सी) The city Benares, more usually वाराणसी.<BR> E. वरणा a rivu-<BR>let as above, and असि another rivulet, running on the south of<BR>the city; deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणीय
वरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be applied to or solicited for a boon, &c.<BR>2. To be selected.<BR> E. वर् to ask as a boon, or वृ to choose, अनीयर्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्ड|वरंड|वरंडः|वरण्डः
वरण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A portico.<BR>	 2. Pimples on the face.<BR>	 3. A multitude.<BR>4. A heap of grass.<BR>	 5. The string of a fish-hook.<BR>	 6. A packet, a<BR>package.<BR>	 7. A long rod according to some; a projecting wall ac-<BR>cording to others.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा)<BR>	 1. A small bird, (Turdus.)<BR>	 2. A dagger.<BR>3. The wick of a lamp.<BR> E. वृञ् to cover, &c., Unādi aff. अण्डच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डक|वरंडक|वरण्डकः
वरण्डक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Fearful, terrified.<BR>	 2. Large, great.<BR>	 3. Miser-<BR>ly, a miser.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A Howdāh, a chair or canopy on the back<BR>of an elephant.<BR>	 2. A wall.<BR>	 3. Eruption or pimples on the face.<BR>	 4.<BR>A ball, a globe.<BR>	 5. A mound of earth.<BR> E. वरण्ड as above, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=630-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डालु|वरंडालुः|वरण्डालुः
वरण्डालु m. (-लुः) The castor oil tree, (Ricinus communis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरतनु|वरतनुः
वरतनु f. (-नुः) An elegant woman.<BR> E. वर and तनु body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्करी
वरत्करी f. (-री) A sort of perfume, commonly Renukā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्रा
वरत्रा f. (-त्रा)<BR>	 1. An elephant's or horse's leather girth.<BR>	 2. A thong, a<BR>a strip of leather.<BR> E. वृञ् to cover or surround, Unādi aff. अत्रच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्वच|वरत्वचः
वरत्वच m. (-चः) The Nimba-tree, (Melia azadiracta.)<BR> E. वर best, and<BR>त्वच् skin, the final vowel added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरद|वरदः
वरद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Granting a prayer, conferring a boon.<BR>	 2. Pro-<BR>pitious, favourable.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A benefactor.<BR>	 2. Fire for burnt-<BR>offerings of a propitiatory character.<BR>	 f. (-दा) A girl, a virgin. E.<BR>वर a blessing, &c., द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरदान
वरदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Granting a boon.<BR>	 2. A place of pilgrimage.<BR> E. वर blessing, दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरपर्णाख्य|वरपर्णाख्यः
वरपर्णाख्य m. (-ख्यः) A sort of perfume, commonly Renukā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरप्रद
वरप्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Conferring a boon.<BR>	 f. (-दा) The wife of the saint<BR>AGASTYA.<BR> E. वर a boon, and प्रद who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरप्रदान
वरप्रदान n. (-नं) Conferring a boon.<BR> E. वर and प्रदान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरप्रस्थान
वरप्रस्थान n. (-नं) The setting out of a bridegroom towards the house of<BR>the bride for the celebration of marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरफल|वरफलः
वरफल m. (-लः) The cocoa-nut tree.<BR> E. वर best and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरम्
वरम् Ind. Better, sooner, rather, preferable: see वर ।<BR> E. वृ-अमु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरमुखी
वरमुखी f. (-खी) Renukā, a sort of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरम्बरा
वरम्बरा f. (-रा) The nux vomica plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरयितृ
वरयितृ m. (-ता) A husband.<BR> E. वर to choose, in the causal form, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वररुचि|वररुचिः
वररुचि m. (-चिः) A poet and philosopher, one of the ornaments of the<BR>court of Bhoja, or one of the nine gems usually ascribed to<BR>VIKRAMĀDITYA'S court.<BR> E. वर pre-eminent, रुचि light or renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरल|वरलः
वरल mf. (-लः-ला or ली) A wasp.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A goose.<BR> E. वर and ला to take<BR>aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरलब्ध|वरलब्धः
वरलब्ध m. (-ब्धः) The Champaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवत्सला
वरवत्सला f. (-ला) The wife of a father-in-law.<BR> E. वर a bridegroom, वत्सल affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवर्णिनी
वरवर्णिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. An excellent woman.<BR>	 2. A virtuous woman.<BR>	 3. A<BR>woman in general.<BR>	 4. Turmeric.<BR>	 5. Lāc.<BR>	 6. A brownish yellow<BR>pigment; also रोचना and गोरोचना.<BR>	 7. A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR>8. A name of GAURĪ.<BR>	 9. SARASWATĪ.<BR>	 10. LAKṢMĪ.<BR> E. वर best,<BR>वर्ण class or colour, aff. इनि and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवारण
वरवारण m. (-णः) A fine elephant.<BR> E. वर, and वारण an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवाह्लीक|वरवाह्लीकं
वरवाह्लीक n. (-कं) Saffron.<BR> E. वर, and वाह्लीक the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवृद्ध|वरवृद्धः
वरवृद्ध m. (-द्धः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. वर better, and वृद्ध old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराक|वराकः
वराक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Low, vile, impure.<BR>	 2. Poor, pitiable.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. War.<BR> E. वृ to cover, &c., षाकन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्ग|वरांग|वराङ्गं|वराङ्गः
वराङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. The head.<BR>	 2. The privity, a private part, male or female.<BR>3. Cassia bark.<BR>	 4. An elegant form or body.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) An ele-<BR>phant.<BR> E. वर best, excellent, अङ्ग body or member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गक|वराङ्गकं
वराङ्गक m. (-कः) Woody Cassia.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गना|वरांगना
वराङ्गना f. (-ना) A lovely woman.<BR> E. वर best, अङ्गना a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गरूपोपेत|वराङ्गरूपोपेतः
वराङ्गरूपोपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Handsome and well-shaped.<BR> E. वराङ्ग excell-<BR>ent body, रूप form, and उपेत invested, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराजीविन्
वराजीविन् m. (-वी) An astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराट|वराटः
वराट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A cord, a rope.<BR>	 2. A Cowri: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटक|वराटकः
वराटक mfn. Subst. (-टकः-टिका-टकं)<BR>	 1. A rope, a cord, a string.<BR>	 2. The<BR>small shell, called a Cowri, and used as a coin.<BR>	 3. The seed-<BR>vessel of the lotus.<BR>	 f. (-टिका) The Nāgeshwara plant.<BR> E. वृञ् to sur-<BR>round, aff. अटच्, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटकरजस्
वराटकरजस् m. (-जाः) A plant, commonly Nāgeshwara, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराण|वराणः
वराण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Capparis trifoliata.)<BR> E. वर best,<BR>and णी to obtain, with आङ् prefix, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराणसी
वराणसी f. (-सी) Benāres.<BR> E. वर best, अनस् water, ङीप् aff., i. e. the<BR>Ganges, on whose bank the city is situated; also वाराणसी and<BR>वरणसी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरादन|वरादनं
वरादन n. (-नं) A sort of Mimusops, (M. Kauki, Rox.)<BR> E. वर best, अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराम्र|वराम्रः
वराम्र m. (-म्रः) An acid fruit, (Carissa Carondas.)<BR> E. वर best, अम्र acid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारक|वरारकं
वरारक n. (-कं) The diamond.<BR> E. वर best, ऋ to go or be, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारोह|वरारोहः
वरारोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. An elephant driver.<BR>	 2. Mounting, riding.<BR>	 3. A rider<BR>on an elephant or horse.<BR>	 f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. A handsome or elegant woman.<BR>2. The hip or flank.<BR> E. वर excellent, आरोह mounting, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालक|वरालकः
वरालक m. (-कः) The Caronda fruit, (Carissa Carondas.)<BR> E. वर best,<BR>अल् to be equal to, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालि|वरालिः
वरालि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. A division of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालिका
वरालिका f. (-का) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. वर best, supreme, आलि a female<BR>friend, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराशि|वराशिः
वराशि m. (-शिः) Coarse cloth.<BR> E. वर covering, अश् to pervade, aff. इन्; also वरासि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरासन|वरासनं|वरासनः
वरासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The seat of honour.<BR>	 2. An excellent seat.<BR>	 3. A cis-<BR>tern, a reservoir.<BR>	 4. The China rose.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A whoremonger.<BR>2. A doorkeeper.<BR> E. वर best, &c., आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरासि|वरासिः
वरासि m. (-सिः)<BR>	 1. Coarse cloth.<BR>	 2. A swordsman.<BR>	 f. (-सी) Dirty<BR>clothes.<BR> E. वर covering, अस् to be, affs. इन् and ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराह|वराहः
वराह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A hog.<BR>	 2. A name of VIṢṆU in the third Avatār or<BR>descent, in which be assumed the shape of a boar.<BR>	 3. A bull.<BR>	 4.<BR>A ram.<BR>	 5. A cloud.<BR>	 6. A crocodile.<BR>	 7. An array of troops in the<BR>form of a hog.<BR>	 8. A mountain.<BR>	 9. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>	 10.<BR>A particular measure.<BR>	 11. One of the eighteen smaller Dwīpas<BR>or divisions of the universe.<BR> E. वर best, हन् to injure, with आङ्<BR>prefix, and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहकर्णिका
वराहकर्णिका f. (-का) A kind of missile weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहकान्ता
वराहकान्ता f. (-न्ता) A sort of yam.<BR> E. वराह a hog, and कान्ता beloved; also वराही ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहकालिन्
वराहकालिन् m. (-ली) A flower,: see सूर्य्यमणि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहक्रान्ता
वराहक्रान्ता f. (-न्ता) A plant, a sort of sensitive plant according to some<BR>authorities, but to others, a kind of moss, (Licopodium imbrica-<BR>tum, Rox.:) it is also considered sometimes, but erroneously, as<BR>synonimous with वराही Dioscorea.<BR> E. वराह a hog, and क्रान्त passing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहनामिन्
वराहनामिन् m. (-मा) An esculent root: see वाराही.<BR> E. वराह a hog, and<BR>नामन् a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिमन्
वरिमन् m. (-मा) Excellence, pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवसित|वरिवसितः
वरिवसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Served, honoured, adored, as a deity or spiri-<BR>tual teacher.<BR> E. वरिवस्या service, इतच् aff., and य optionally rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्या
वरिवस्या f. (-स्या) Service, honour, especially such devoted obedience<BR>as a pupil pays his spiritual preceptor.<BR> E. वरिवस indeclinable, here<BR>said to imply veneration, and क्याच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्यित|वरिवस्यितः
वरिवस्यित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Served, adored.<BR> E. वरिवस्या as above, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिशी
वरिशी f. (-शी) A fish-hook. E. See वडिशी, ड and र being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष|वरिषं
वरिष n. (-षं) A year.<BR>	 m. plu. (-षाः) The rains or rainy season.<BR> E. वृष् to<BR>sprinkle, aff. इषन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिषाप्रिय|वरिषाप्रियः
वरिषाप्रिय m. (-यः) The Chātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR> E. वरिषा the<BR>rainy season, प्रिय fond of; supposed to drink rain water only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष्ठ|वरिष्ठं|वरिष्ठः
वरिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Largest, greatest, most large.<BR>	 2. Heaviest,<BR>mightiest.<BR>	 3. Best, dearest, most preferable or beloved.<BR>	 n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Copper.<BR>	 2. Pepper.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. The Francoline partridge.<BR>	 2. The<BR>orange tree.<BR> E. वर् substituted for उरु large, or वर best, इष्ठन् aff.<BR>of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीयस्
वरीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Very large, largest, most large.<BR>	 2. Best,<BR>most preferable or excellent.<BR>	 3. Extremely young, tender, infan-<BR>tine.<BR>	 m. (-यान्) The eighteenth of the astronomical periods called<BR>Yogas.<BR> E. वर best, or substituted for उरु large, and ईयसुन् aff. of<BR>the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीवर्द्द|वरीवर्द|वरीवर्दः|वरीवर्द्दः
वरीवर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः) An ox or bull. E. See बलीवर्द्द, ब and ल being changed<BR>to व and र; also वलीवर्द्द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीषु|वरीषुः
वरीषु m. (-षुः) KĀMA or CUPID.<BR> E. वृ to choose, ईषुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुण|वरुणः
वरुण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. VARUṆA, the deity of the water and regent of the<BR>west.<BR>	 2. Water or the ocean.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Tapia cratœva, or Cap-<BR>paris trifoliata.)<BR>	 4. A name of the sun, or rather of one of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">Page632-a+ 60</a>]<BR>twelve forms of that luminary, or Ādityas.<BR> E. वृ to enclose, (the<BR>earth,) or वृ to select or prefer, being chosen by the gods for his<BR>office, and उनन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=631-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणात्मजा
वरुणात्मजा f. (-जा) Spirituous liquor.<BR> E. वरुण VARUṆA, or the ocean<BR>personified, आत्मजा daughter; being amongst the precious thing<BR>produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणानी
वरुणानी f. (-नी) The wife of VARUṆA.<BR> E. वरुण, with ङीप् aff. and आनुक्<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुत्र|वरुत्रं
वरुत्र n. (-त्रं) An upper and outer garment.<BR> E. वृ to cover, उत्र Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथ|वरूथं|वरूथः
वरूथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A sort of wooden fender or ledge round a carriage, as<BR>a defence from the effects of collision.<BR>	 2. The Kokila.<BR>	 3. Time.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-थं)<BR>	 1. Armour, mail.<BR>	 2. Leather, skin.<BR>	 3. A shield.<BR>	 4. A multi-<BR>tude, an assemblage.<BR>	 5. A house or dwelling.<BR> E. वृ to surround,<BR>Unādi aff. ऊथन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथिन्
वरूथिन् m. (-थी)<BR>	 1. A guard, a defender.<BR>	 2. A car.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. An army.<BR>2. Wearing an armour.<BR>	 3. Furnished with a protecting plank.<BR>	 4.<BR>Protecting.<BR> E. वरूथ part of a car, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण
वरेण m. (-णः) A wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण्य|वरेण्यं|वरेण्यः
वरेण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Chief, principal, pre-eminent.<BR>	 2. Desirable,<BR>eligible.<BR>	 n. (-ण्य) Saffron.<BR> E. वृ to select, Unādi aff. एण्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेन्द्र|वरेन्द्रः
वरेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. A chief, a sovereign.<BR>	 2. INDRA.<BR>	 f. (-न्द्री) Ancient<BR>Gaur, the capital and district so named.<BR> E. वर best, इन्द्र chief, and<BR>with ङीप् aff.; the favourite country of the deity, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेश्वर|वरेश्वरः
वरेश्वर m. (-रः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. वर best, principal, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोट|वरोटं|वरोटः
वरोट m. (-टः) A plant, commonly Marubaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोरु|वरोरुः
वरोरु f. (-रुः) A beautiful woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोल|वरोलः
वरोल mf. (-लः-ली) A wasp.<BR> E. वृ to cover, ओलच् aff., fem. aff. ङीप्; the<BR>fem. form may also mean, a smaller kind of wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कर|वर्करः
वर्कर mf. (-रः-री) Any young animal.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A lamb.<BR>	 2. A goat.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pleasure, pastime, sport, mirth, festivity.<BR> E. वृक् to take, aff. अरन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कराट|वर्कराटः
वर्कराट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A side-glance, a wink, a leer.<BR>	 2. The rays of the<BR>meridian sun.<BR>	 mn. (-टः-टं) The marks of a lover's fingernails on<BR>the bosom of a woman.<BR> E. वर्कर a young animal, अट् to be or re-<BR>semble, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कुट|वर्कुटः
वर्कुट m. (-टः) A pin, a bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ग|वर्गः|वर्ग्ग
वर्ग m. (-र्गः) A class, a tribe, a multitude of similar things, whether<BR>animate or inanimate; as Ka-varga, the class of guttural letters;<BR>Tri-varga, a class of three objects, (as love, duty, and wealth);<BR>the Śudra-varga, the Śudra tribe.<BR>	 2. A chapter, a book, a section.<BR>3. A square number, (in arithmetic.)<BR>	 4. Strength.<BR> E. वृज् to quit,<BR>to except, (any thing else), aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गघन|वर्गघनः
वर्गघन n. (-नं) The square of a cube.<BR> E. वर्ग and घन a cube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गमूल|वर्गमूलं
वर्गमूल n. (-लं) A square root.<BR> E. वर्ग and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गान्त्य|वर्गांत्य
वर्गान्त्य m. (-न्त्यः) A nasal, the last consonant in each of the first five<BR>classes of consonants being a nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गीय|वर्गीयः
वर्गीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Belonging to a class, a tribe, &c.<BR> E. वर्ग and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्घ्
वर्घ् r. 1st cl. (वर्घति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्च्|वर्च्
वर्च्च् r. 1st cl. (वर्च्चते) To shine. r. 10th cl. (वर्च्चयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cut.<BR>	 2. To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्चटी|वर्चटी
वर्च्चटी f. (-टी)<BR>	 1. A kind of rice.<BR>	 2. A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्चस्|वर्चस्
वर्च्चस् n. (-र्च्चः)<BR>	 1. Form, figure, shape.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR>	 3. Vigour,<BR>power.<BR>	 4. Ordure, fæces.<BR>	 m. (-र्च्चाः) The son of CHANDRA.<BR> E. वर्च्च् to<BR>shine, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्चस्क|वर्चस्क|वर्चस्कः|वर्च्चस्कः
वर्च्चस्क mn. (-स्कः-स्कं)<BR>	 1. Brightness.<BR>	 2. Fæces, excrement.<BR> E. वर्च्च् to<BR>shine, असुन् aff. and कन् depreciative aff. added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्चस्विन्|वर्चस्विन्
वर्च्चस्विन् mfn. (-स्वी-स्विनी-स्वि)<BR>	 1. Bright, glorious.<BR>	 2. Vigourous, active.<BR>E. वर्च्चस, विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्ज|वर्ज|वर्जं|वर्जः
वर्ज्ज mfn. (-र्ज्जः-र्ज्जा-र्ज्जं)<BR>	 1. Free from, devoid of.<BR>	 2. Excepted.<BR>	 m. (-र्ज्जः)<BR>1. Leaving, abandoning.<BR>	 2. Excepting.<BR> E. वृज् to abandon, aff.<BR>अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जक|वर्जक
वर्ज्जक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what leaves, shuns, excepts, &c.<BR> E. वृज् to quit, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जन|वर्जन|वर्जनं|वर्ज्जनं
वर्ज्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Quitting, abandonment, shunning, avoiding.<BR>	 2. In-<BR>jury, hurting.<BR>	 3. Killing.<BR> E. वृज् to abandon, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जनीय|वर्जनीय|वर्ज्जनीयं
वर्ज्जनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Improper, censurable, wicked, proper to<BR>be avoided.<BR>	 2. Irregular, to be excepted.<BR> E. वृज् to quit, अनीयर्<BR>aff. of the future participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जम्|वर्जम्
वर्ज्जम् Ind. Excluding, (at the end of compound.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जयित्वा|वर्जयित्वा
वर्ज्जयित्वा Ind.<BR>	 1. Having shunned or avoided.<BR>	 2. Having omitted, ex-<BR>cepting, leaving out.<BR> E. वृज् to quit, aff. क्त्वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्जित|वर्जित|वर्ज्जितः
वर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Abandoned, avoided.<BR>	 2. Given.<BR>	 3. Excluded,<BR>excepted.<BR> E. वृज् to quit, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्ज्य
वर्ज्ज्य mfn. (-र्ज्ज्यः-र्ज्ज्या-र्ज्ज्यं)<BR>	 1. To be shunned.<BR>	 2. To be excepted, ex-<BR>cluded, left out.<BR>	 n. (-र्ज्ज्यं) A point in each lunar mansion during<BR>the passage of the moon, in which no business should be begun.<BR>E. वृज् to quit, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण्
वर्ण् r. 10th cl. (वर्णयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To colour, to paint, to die.<BR>	 2. To send or<BR>cast, to direct, to order.<BR>	 3. To praise, to extol, to proclaim qua-<BR>lities.<BR>	 4. To describe.<BR>	 5. To spread or extend.<BR>	 6. To grind or<BR>pound.<BR>	 7. To make exertions.<BR>	 8. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण|वर्णं|वर्णः|वर्ण्ण
वर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. A tribe, a class, a caste, an order.<BR>	 2. Colour, hue,<BR>tint.<BR>	 3. Coloured cloth thrown over the back of an elephant, an<BR>elephant's housings.<BR>	 4. Quality, property.<BR>	 5. Fame, celebrity.<BR>	 6.<BR>Praise.<BR>	 7. Gold.<BR>	 8. Religious observance.<BR>	 9. The order or arrange-<BR>ment of a song or poem.<BR>	 10. A musical mode.<BR>	 11. Staining the<BR>body with coloured unguents.<BR>	 12. Beauty, lustre.<BR>	 13. Theatrical<BR>dress or embellishment.<BR>	 14. A cloak.<BR>	 mn. (-र्णः-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Perfume for<BR>the person.<BR>	 2. A letter of the alphabet.<BR>	 3. Form, figure.<BR>	 4. Sort,<BR>kind.<BR>	 5. Touch, the purity of gold, as ascertained by its streak<BR>on the touch-stone.<BR>	 6. In arithmetic, a co-efficient.<BR>	 n. (-र्णं) Saffron.<BR>f. (-र्णा) A leguminous shrub, (Cytisus cajan.)<BR> E. वर्ण् to paint, &c.,<BR>aff. अच् or घञ्; or वृ to cover or screen, Unādi aff. नक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णक|वर्णकं|वर्णकः|वर्ण्णक
वर्णक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. Perfume for the person, especially pounded or<BR>ground.<BR>	 2. The dress of an actor.<BR>	 3. Sandal.<BR>	 mf. (-कः-का) A paint,<BR>a pigment, as indigo, orpiment, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A panegyrist, a<BR>bard, a poetical encomiast, by tribe and profession.<BR>	 2. A circle,<BR>an orb.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Touch, standard, fineness or purity of gold.<BR>	 2.<BR>A mantle.<BR>	 3. A mask.<BR>	 4. A paint.<BR> E. वर्ण् to colour, &c., ण्वुल् aff.;<BR>or वर्ण as above, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णकवि|वर्णकविः
वर्णकवि m. (-विः) The son of KUVERA.<BR> E. वर्ण praise, and कवि a bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णकूपिका|वर्ण्णकूपिका
वर्णकूपिका f. (-का) An ink-stand.<BR> E. वर्ण a letter, and कूप a well, कन् aff.<BR>of comparison, in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णक्रम|वर्णक्रमः
वर्णक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Order of caste or tribe.<BR>	 2. Alphabetical arrangement,<BR>the alphabet.<BR> E. वर्ण and क्रम course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णगत
वर्णगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Coloured.<BR>	 2. Described.<BR>	 3. Algebraic.<BR> E. वर्ण, गत gone to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णचारक|वर्णचारकः|वर्ण्णचारक
वर्णचारक m. (-कः) A painter.<BR> E. वर्ण colour, चर् to go, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णज्येष्ठ|वर्णज्येष्ठः|वर्ण्णज्येष्ठ
वर्णज्येष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A Brāhmana.<BR> E. वर्ण caste, ज्येष्ठ elder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णतस्
वर्णतस् Ind. By or with colour, &c.<BR> E. वर्ण colour, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णतूलि|वर्णतूलिः|वर्ण्णतूलि
वर्णतूलि mf. (-लिः-ली) A pen.<BR> E. वर्ण a letter, and तूलि a brush; also<BR>with कन् added वर्णतूलिका f. (-का) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णद|वर्णदं|वर्ण्णद
वर्णद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Dying, colouring.<BR>	 2. Giving tribe, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-दः) Aloe-wood or Agallochum.<BR> E. वर्ण, द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णदातृ
वर्णदातृ m. (-ता) Turmeric.<BR> E. वर्ण, दातृ what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णदूत|वर्णदूतः|वर्ण्णदूत
वर्णदूत m. (-तः) A letter, an epistle.<BR> E. वर्ण a letter of the alphabet, &c.,<BR>दूत messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णदूषक
वर्णदूषक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Disturbing or violating the distinctions of<BR>caste.<BR> E. वर्ण, and दूषक what violates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णधर्म्म|वर्णधर्म|वर्णधर्मः|वर्णधर्म्मः
वर्णधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) The particular occupation or duty of each caste or<BR>tribe.<BR> E. वर्ण a tribe, धर्म्म virtue, moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णन|वर्णनं
वर्णन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Describing, expatiating, explaining, pointing out qua-<BR>lities or excellencies, &c.<BR>	 2. Colouring, painting, writing.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>Praise, panegyric,<BR> E. वर्ण् to colour, युच् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=632-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णनीय
वर्णनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be desired, delineated, praised, &c.<BR> E. वर्ण्<BR>to colour, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णपत्र
वर्णपत्र m. (-त्रः) A pallet, a leaf, &c., on which a painter mixes his<BR>colours.<BR> E. वर्ण a colour, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णपुष्प
वर्णपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) The flower of the globe-amaranth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णप्रसादन|वर्णप्रसादनं
वर्णप्रसादन n. (-नं) Aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णमातृ
वर्णमातृ f. (-ता) A pen.<BR> E. वर्ण a letter, and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णमातृका
वर्णमातृका f. (-का) SARASWATĪ, the goddess of speech and eloquence.<BR>E. वर्ण a letter, and मातृका divine parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णमाला
वर्णमाला f. (-ला) The alphabet.<BR> E. वर्ण a letter, माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णरेखा
वर्णरेखा f. (-खा) A white aluminous fossile often confounded with chalk,<BR>of which it is considered a species.<BR> E. वर्ण colour, रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णलेखा
वर्णलेखा f. (-खा) Chalk.<BR> E. वर्ण colour, लेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णवत्|वर्णवन्त्
वर्णवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having tribe, colour, &c.<BR>	 f. (-वती) Turmeric.<BR>E. वर्ण colour, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णविलासिनी
वर्णविलासिनी f. (-नी) Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णविलोडक|वर्णविलोडकः
वर्णविलोडक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plagiarist.<BR>	 2. A housebreaker.<BR> E. वर्ण praise,<BR>and वि before, लोड् to be mad, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णवृत्त
वर्णवृत्त n. (-त्तं) A metre regulated by the number of syllables, (opposite<BR>to मात्रावृत्त.)<BR> E. वर्ण, and वृत्त metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णश्रेष्ठ|वर्णश्रेष्ठः
वर्णश्रेष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Of a good tribe, caste, kind, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः) A<BR>Brāhman.<BR> E. वर्ण, श्रेष्ठ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसंहार|वर्णसंहारः
वर्णसंहार m. (-रः) An assemblage or mixture of the four tribes.<BR> E. वर्ण, संहार assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसङ्कर|वर्णसंकर|वर्णसंकरः|वर्णसङ्करः
वर्णसङ्कर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Mixture or confusion of castes.<BR>	 2. A man or tribe<BR>of mixed origin, or from a father and mother of different castes.<BR>E. वर्ण and सम + कृ-अप् सङ्कर mixture. वर्णतः सङ्करः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसङ्घाट|वर्णसंघाट
वर्णसङ्घाट m. (-टः) An alphabet or assemblage of letters.<BR> E. वर्ण, हन् to<BR>kill, with सम् prefixed, and घञ् aff., and घट substituted for the<BR>radical letter; also with घत, वर्णसङ्घात ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसङ्घात|वर्णसंघात|वर्णसंघातः
वर्णसङ्घात m. (-तः) The alphabet: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णसि|वर्णसिः
वर्णसि m. (-सिः) Water.<BR> E. वृ to surround, असि Unādi aff., and नुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णहीन
वर्णहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Outcaste.<BR> E. वर्ण and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाङ्का|वर्णांका
वर्णाङ्का f. (-ङ्का) A pen.<BR> E. वर्ण a letter, अकि to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाट|वर्णाटः
वर्णाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A singer.<BR>	 2. A painter.<BR>	 3. An actor, a mime.<BR>	 4. One<BR>who lives by his wife.<BR> E. वर्ण colour, &c., अट् to go or be, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णात्मन्
वर्णात्मन् m. (-त्मा) A word.<BR> E. वर्ण a letter, and आत्मन् the soul or essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णापसद|वर्णापसदः
वर्णापसद m. (-दः) An outcaste.<BR> E. वर्ण, अपसद who is or goes out from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णापेत
वर्णापेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Degraded, outcaste.<BR> E. वर्ण and अपेत devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाश्रम
वर्णाश्रम n. (-मं) The class and state of a person.<BR> E. वर्ण and आश्रम order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णाश्रमघर्म्म
वर्णाश्रमघर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) The duties of tribe and order.<BR> E. वर्णाश्रम, धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णि|वर्णिः
वर्णि n. (-र्णि) Gold.<BR> E. वर्ण् to colour, &c., Unādi aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिक|वर्णिकः
वर्णिक m. (-कः) A writer, a scribe, a secretary, &c.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A pen.<BR>2. Ink.<BR>	 3. A paint.<BR>	 4. A mask, a character.<BR> E. वर्ण a letter, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णित|वर्णितः
वर्णित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Praised, eulogised, extolled.<BR>	 2. Described, ex-<BR>plained.<BR>	 3. Painted.<BR> E. वर्ण् to praise, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णितवत्
वर्णितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Relating, describing, was relating or rela-<BR>ted, &c.<BR> E. वर्ण् to describe, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिन्
वर्णिन् mfn. (-र्णी-र्णिनी-र्णि) Belonging to a caste or tribe, of that caste,<BR>of that colour, &c.<BR>	 m. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. A painter.<BR>	 2. A scribe, a writer.<BR>3. A religious student.<BR>	 4. A man of either of the four regular<BR>castes.<BR>	 f. (-र्णिनी)<BR>	 1. A woman, a wife.<BR>	 2. Turmeric.<BR> E. वर्ण colour,<BR>&c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिबध
वर्णिबध m. (-धः) Killing or occasioning the death of a man of either of<BR>four castes.<BR> E. वर्णिन् and बध killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णिलिङ्गिन्|वर्णिलिंगिन्
वर्णिलिङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी) An ascetic, or one wearing the marks of a reli-<BR>gious student.<BR> E. वर्णिन्, लिङ्गिन् having a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णु|वर्णुः
वर्णु m. (-र्णुः)<BR>	 1. The name of a river and district.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. वृ<BR>to surround, Unādi aff. णु; or वर्ण-उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णोपेत
वर्णोपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having caste, tribe, &c.<BR> E. वर्ण, उपेत possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्त|वर्त|वर्तः
वर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) Living, livelihood, (generally at the end of a compound.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तक|वर्तक|वर्तकः|वर्त्तकं|वर्त्तकः
वर्त्तक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who is or abides, exists, lives, &c.<BR>	 mf. (-कः-का<BR>or की)<BR>	 1. A sort of quail, (Perdix olivacea.)<BR>	 2. A horse's hoof.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-कं) A sort of mixed or bell-metal, commonly Vidari.<BR> E. वृत् to be,<BR>ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तजन्मन्|वर्तजन्मन्
वर्त्तजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) A cloud.<BR> E. वृत् to be, aff. घञ्, वर्त्त abiding, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तन|वर्तन|वर्तनः|वर्त्तनं|वर्त्तनः
वर्त्तन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fixed, stationary, stable.<BR>	 nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>	 1. Staying,<BR>abiding, being, the property of a fixed presence.<BR>	 2. A road, a<BR>way.<BR>	 3. A ball at one end of a spindle to assist its rotatory mo-<BR>tion.<BR>	 4. Grinding.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Livelihood, subsistence.<BR>	 2. Occupa-<BR>tion, profession.<BR>	 3. Salary, hire, wages.<BR>	 4. A ball of cotton from<BR>which the threads are spun.<BR>	 5. A ball, a globe.<BR>	 6. Appointing.<BR>	 7.<BR>Turning.<BR>	 8. Abode, residence.<BR>	 9. Conduct.<BR>	 10. Commerce, traffic.<BR>m. (-नः) A dwarf.<BR> E. वृत् to be, to be fixed, &c., aff. ल्युट् or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तनदान|वर्तनदान
वर्त्तनदान n. (-नं) Gift of a situation, of wages or means of subsistence.<BR>E. वर्त्तन and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तनविनियोग|वर्तनविनियोग|वर्तनविनियोगः
वर्त्तनविनियोग m. (-गः) Appointment or assignment of salary, wages,<BR>&c.<BR> E. वर्त्तन, विनियोग appointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तनाभाव|वर्तनाभाव
वर्त्तनाभाव m. (-वः) Destitution, want of means of subsistence.<BR> E. वर्त्तन, अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तनि|वर्तनि|वर्तनिः|वर्त्तनिः
वर्त्तनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. The eastern country, or eastern India.<BR>	 2. A hymn,<BR>a panegyric.<BR>	 f. (-निः) A road.<BR> E. वृत् to be, Unādi aff. अनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तनीय|वर्तनीय
वर्त्तनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be lived, or dwelt in.<BR>	 2. What may be.<BR>E. वृत् to be, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तमान|वर्तमान|वर्तमानः|वर्त्तमानः
वर्त्तमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being, existing, living, being present.<BR>	 2.<BR>Dwelling or abiding in.<BR>	 3. Revolving.<BR>	 n. (-नं) (In grammar,) The<BR>present tense.<BR> E. वृत् to be, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तमानता|वर्तमानता
वर्त्तमानता f. (-ता) Being, being present, the property of time present.<BR>E. तल् added to the last: also with त्व aff. वर्त्तमानत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तयत्|वर्तयत्
वर्त्तयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Living, subsisting.<BR>	 2. Dwelling.<BR> E. वृत् to be, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तरूक|वर्तरूक|वर्तरूकः|वर्त्तरूकः
वर्त्तरूक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A river so named.<BR>	 2. A puddle, a pool of water.<BR>	 3.<BR>A crow's nest.<BR>	 4. A doorkeeper, a chamberlain; it is also written<BR>वर्त्तरूढ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्ति|वर्ति|वर्तिः|वर्त्तिः
वर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्ती)<BR>	 1. Perfume for the person.<BR>	 2. The wick of a lamp.<BR>3. A lamp.<BR>	 4. A tent, a bougie.<BR>	 5. A collyrium prepared from<BR>various substances and dried in a lozenge form; it is applied<BR>grinding with water or milk.<BR>	 6. A line, a ruled line.<BR>	 7. The ends<BR>of a cloth.<BR>	 8. The projecting threads of woven cloth.<BR>	 9. A protu-<BR>berance round a vessel.<BR>	 10. A surgical instrument.<BR> E. वृत् to be,<BR>Unādi aff. इन्, ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तिका|वर्तिका
वर्त्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A quail.<BR>	 2. The wick of a lamp.<BR>	 3. A paint.<BR>	 4. A<BR>paint-brush.<BR> E. वृत् to be, aff. ण्वुल्, fem. aff. टाप्; or वृत् the same,<BR>तिकन् Unādi aff.; also वर्त्तक, वर्त्तका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तित|वर्तित
वर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Caused as made to be or exist.<BR> E. वृत् to be, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तितव्य|वर्तितव्य
वर्त्तितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be lived.<BR>	 2. To be dwelt, remained, or<BR>continued.<BR>	 3. To be practised in.<BR>	 4. What may be, possible, pro-<BR>bable.<BR> E. वृत् to be, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तिन्|वर्तिन्
वर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति)<BR>	 1. Abiding, fixed, stationary.<BR>	 2. Being.<BR>3. Turning.<BR>	 4. Practising, (generally at the end of compounds.)<BR>E. वृत् to go, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्ति|वर्ति|वर्तिः|वर्त्तिः
वर्त्ति(र्त्ती)र m. (-रः) A kind of quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तिष्णु|वर्तिष्णु|वर्त्तिष्णुः
वर्त्तिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Staying, abiding, being stationary or fixed.<BR>2. Facing, (an enemy,) standing firm in battle.<BR>	 3. A circle.<BR> E. वृत्<BR>to be, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्तुल|वर्तुल|वर्तुलः|वर्त्तुलं|वर्त्तुलः
वर्त्तुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Round, circular, globular, spherical.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>1. A pea.<BR>	 2. A ball.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A ball of clay at the end of a spindle<BR>to assist its rotation.<BR> E. वृत् to be, उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मन्
वर्त्मन् n. (-र्त्म)<BR>	 1. A road.<BR>	 2. Custom, usage.<BR>	 3. Mode, manner, fashion.<BR>4. An edge, a border.<BR>	 5. An eyelid.<BR> E. वृत् to be, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मनि|वर्त्मनिः
वर्त्मनि f. (-निः or नी) A road, a way.<BR> E. वृत् to be, अनि Unādi aff. मुट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्मावबन्ध
वर्त्मावबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Rigidity of the eyelids, so that they can not shut. E.<BR>वर्त्म and अवबन्ध contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्त्स्यत्|वर्त्स्यन्त्
वर्त्स्यत् mfn. (-र्त्स्यन्-र्त्स्यन्ती-र्त्स्यत्) Purposing to augment.<BR> E. वृध् to aug-<BR>ment, शतृ aff. with the future form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्ध्
वर्द्ध् r. 10th cl. (वर्द्धयति-ते) The same as वर्ध् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्ध
वर्द्ध m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly BĀMANHĀTI.<BR>	 2. Increase, augmen-<BR>tation.<BR>	 3. Cutting.<BR>	 n. (-र्द्धं)<BR>	 1. Red lead.<BR>	 2. Lead.<BR> E. वृध् to grow or<BR>increase aff. घञ्; or वर्ध् to divide, aff. अच्; also written वर्ध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धक
वर्द्धक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Increasing, causing to grow or increase.<BR>	 2. Divi-<BR>ding.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly BĀMANHĀTI.<BR>	 2. A carpenter.<BR>E. वृध् to grow, or वर्द्ध् to divide, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्ध्वकि
वर्द्ध्वकि m. (-किः) A carpenter.<BR> E. वर्द्ध् to cut, अच् aff., कष् to injure, इ aff. form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धकिन्
वर्द्धकिन् m. (-की) A carpenter.<BR> E. वर्द्धक cutting, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धन
वर्द्धन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Growing, thriving.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Increasing, growing,<BR>thriving.<BR>	 2. Augmenting, causing to increase.<BR>	 3. Cutting, divi-<BR>ding.<BR>	 4. Animation.<BR>	 5. Educating, rearing.<BR>	 6. Elevation.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>1. A small water-jar.<BR>	 2. A brush, a broom.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A granter<BR>of prosperity.<BR>	 2. A tooth growing over another.<BR>	 3. An epithet of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR> E. वृध् to increase, or वर्ध् to cut, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धमान
वर्द्धमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Prosperous, thriving.<BR>	 2. Increasing, growing.<BR>3. A house having no entrance on the south-side.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>1. The castor-oil tree.<BR>	 2. A lid, a cover, especially a shallow<BR>earthen platter or saucer, used also as a top to water-jars, &c.<BR>3. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. A sort of riddle or charade.<BR>	 5. The last<BR>and most celebrated of the twenty-four Jinas or Jaina teachers<BR>of the present æra.<BR>	 6. A mystical figure or diagram.<BR>	 7. A district<BR>and city, Burdwān.<BR> E. वृध् to increase, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धमानक
वर्द्धमानक m. (-कः) A lid, a cover.<BR> E. वर्द्धमान as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धापन
वर्द्धापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cutting, dividing.<BR>	 2. The ceremony of cutting the<BR>umbilical cord.<BR>	 3. A festival when good wishes and congratula-<BR>tory expressions are offered.<BR> E. वर्द्ध् to cut, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धिन्
वर्द्धिन् mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि) Increasing, thriving.<BR> E. वृध् to increase, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धित
वर्द्धित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Grown, expanded, increased, thriven.<BR>	 2. Full,<BR>filled.<BR>	 3. Cut, divided.<BR> E. वृध् to increase, or वर्द्ध् to cut, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्धिष्णु
वर्द्धिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Increasing, growing, thriving.<BR>	 2. Enlar-<BR>ging, expanding.<BR> E. वृध् to increase, aff. इष्णुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्द्ध्र
वर्द्ध्र nf. (-र्द्ध्रं-र्द्ध्री) A leathern thong or girth for securing a saddle.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-र्द्ध्रं)<BR>	 1. Leather.<BR>	 2. Lead.<BR> E. वृध् to increase, Unādi aff. ष्ट्रन्; also<BR>written वर्ध्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध्
वर्ध् r. 10th cl. (वर्धयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cut or pierce, to divide.<BR>	 2. To fill; also वर्द्ध् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ध|वर्द्धं|वर्द्धः|वर्धः
वर्ध m. (-र्धः)<BR>	 1. Increase, augmentation.<BR>	 2. Cutting: see वर्द्ध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्पस्
वर्पस् n. (-र्पः) Form, figure.<BR> E. वृ to choose, aff. असुन्, पुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्फ्
वर्फ् r. 1st cl. (वर्फति)<BR>	 1. To move, to go.<BR>	 2. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्म्मकषा|वर्मकषा
वर्म्मकषा f. (-षा) A plant; also Charmakashā or Charmaghās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्म्मन्|वर्मन्
वर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Armour, mail.<BR>	 2. Bark, rind.<BR> E. वृ to cover, aff. मनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्म्महर|वर्महर
वर्म्महर m. (-रः) One who takes arms or who spoils another of them.<BR>Adj. Old enough to wear armour.<BR> E. वर्म्म, हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्म्मित|वर्मित|वर्म्मितः
वर्म्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Armed, accoutred.<BR> E. वर्म्म mail, इतच् aff.; or वर्मणिच्-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्य्य|वर्य|वर्यः|वर्य्यं|वर्य्यः
वर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Chief, principal.<BR>	 2. To be applied to for aid<BR>or a boon, &c.<BR>	 2. To be chosen or selected.<BR>	 3. To be yielded to, or<BR>indulged.<BR>	 m. (-र्य्यः) KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 f. (-र्य्या) A girl choosing her own<BR>husband.<BR> E. बर् to ask as a boon, or वृ to choose, यत् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वट|वर्वट
वर्व्वट mf. (-टः-टी) A sort of bean, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वणा|वर्वणा
वर्व्वणा f. (-णा) A blue fly.<BR> E. वर् imitative sound, and वण् or बण् to<BR>utter, aff. अच्; also वर्ब्बणा and बर्ब्बणा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वर|वर्वर|वर्वरः|वर्व्वरं|वर्व्वरः
वर्व्वर mfn. Subst. (-रः-रा or री-रं) A sort of basil, (Ocymum pilosum,<BR>Rox.)<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A low man one of a degraded tribe or occupa-<BR>tion, an out-caste, a barbarian.<BR>	 2. A region, a country, the coun-<BR>try inhabited by barbarians.<BR>	 3. Woolly or curly hair, as the hair of<BR>an African.<BR>	 4. A shrub, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR>	 5. A sort of<BR>worm.<BR>	 6. The noise or clash or weapons.<BR>	 7. A mode of dancing.<BR>f. (-रा-री)<BR>	 1. A sort of potherb.<BR>	 2. A small bee.<BR>	 3. The Baya or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">Page634-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Indian grossbeak, (Loxia philippensis.)<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Vermilion.<BR>	 2.<BR>Gum myrrh.<BR>	 3. A sort of Sandal wood.<BR> E. वृ to choose, Unādi aff.<BR>अरच् or the same root, with अच् aff., in the reiterative form; it is<BR>also derived from बर्ब् to go, and is variously written बर्ब्बर, बर्ब्बर्,<BR>बर्ब्बर and वर्व्वर &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वरीक|वर्वरीक|वर्वरीकः|वर्व्वरीकः
वर्व्वरीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Curly or woolly hair.<BR>	 2. A shrub, commonly BĀ-<BR>MANHĀTI.<BR>	 3. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. A sort of basil.<BR> E. वृ to select,<BR>Unādi aff. ईकन् and the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वरोत्थ
वर्व्वरोत्थ n. (-त्थं) White Sandal.<BR> E. वर्व्वर the country of barbarians, उत्थ what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वा|वर्वा
वर्व्वा f. (-र्व्वा) A sort of basil, (Ocymum pilosum, Rox.) “वावुइ तुलसी ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्व्वि|वर्वि|वर्विः|वर्व्विः
वर्व्वि m. (-र्व्विः) A glutton.<BR> E. वृ to choose, Unādi aff. विन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष|वर्षं|वर्षः
वर्ष r. 1st cl. (वर्षति) To be wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष|वर्षं|वर्षः
वर्ष mn. (-र्षः-र्षं)<BR>	 1. Rain, raining.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling, effusion.<BR>	 3. Seminal<BR>effusion.<BR>	 4. A year.<BR>	 5. A Varṣa, or division of the known con-<BR>tinent; nine such are reckoned; viz:--KURU, HIRANMAYA,<BR>RAMYAKA, ILĀVRITA, HARI, KETUMĀLĀ, BHADRĀŚHWA, KIN-<BR>NARA, and BHĀRATA.<BR>	 5. JAMBU-DWIPA, or India.<BR>	 6. A cloud.<BR>	 m.<BR>plu. (-र्षाः) The rains or rainy season, containing two months,<BR>according to the Hindu classification of the seasons, which<BR>some systems consider to be Śrāvaṇa and Bhādra, and<BR>others, Bhādra and Āśhwin; the duration of the monsoon is<BR>however longer, being reckoned from A sārha to Kārtika, or<BR>from the middle of June to the beginning of October.<BR>	 f. Sing. (-र्षा)<BR>A sort of gramineous plant: see पृक्का.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle, aff. अच्<BR>or घञ्; or वॄ to screen, &c., Unādi aff. स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षकर|वर्षकरः
वर्षकर mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं) Making or producing rain.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A cloud.<BR>f. (-री) A cricket.<BR> E. वर्ष rain, कृ to make or mark, ट aff.; the<BR>cricket chirping especially in wet weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षकोष|वर्षकोषः
वर्षकोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. An astrologer.<BR>	 2. A month.<BR> E. वर्ष a year, and कोष<BR>a vocabulary, &c.; also वर्षकोश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षज|वर्षजं
वर्षज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born or produced in the rains or rainy season.<BR>E. वर्ष the rains, and ज born; also वर्षेज ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षण|वर्षणं
वर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Raining, rain.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling.<BR>	 3. Bestowing.<BR> E. वृष् to<BR>sprinkle, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षणि|वर्षणिः
वर्षणि f. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. Abiding, staying.<BR>	 2. Act, action.<BR>	 3. Raining.<BR>	 4. A<BR>sacrificial act.<BR> E. वर्ष् to sprinkle, अनि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षत्|वर्षन्त्
वर्षत् mfn. (-र्षन्-र्षन्ती-र्षत्) Raining, showering, sprinkling.<BR> E. वृष् to rain, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षधर|वर्षधरः
वर्षधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An eunuch or attendant on the women's apartments.<BR>2. A cloud.<BR> E. वर्ष rain and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षधर्ष
वर्षधर्ष m. (-र्षः) An eunuch or attendant on the women's apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षपर्व्वत|वर्षपर्वत|वर्षपर्वतः|वर्षपर्व्वतः
वर्षपर्व्वत m. (-तः) A mountainous range, supposed to separate the<BR>various Varṣas or divisions of the globe from each other: six<BR>ranges are enumerated from south to north; viz.:--HIMAVĀN,<BR>HEMAKŪTA, NISĀDHA, NĪLA, ŚWETA, and SRINGĪ or ŚRINGA-<BR>VĀNA; MERU constitutes the seventh; some authorities places<BR>CHAITRA and KARNĪ instead of NĪLA and ŚWETA.<BR> E. वर्ष as<BR>above, पर्व्वत a mountain; also similar compounds, as वर्षगिरि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षपाकिन्
वर्षपाकिन् m. (-की) The hog plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR> E. वर्ष rain,<BR>पाकिन् ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षप्रिय|वर्षप्रियः
वर्षप्रिय m. (-यः) The Chātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR> E. वर्ष rain, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षवर|वर्षवरः
वर्षवर m. (-रः) A eunuch, a castrated attendant, one employed in the<BR>women's apartments.<BR> E. वर्ष seminal sprinkling, वृ to refrain from,<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षवृद्धि|वर्षवृद्धिः
वर्षवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Birth-day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षशत
वर्षशत n. (-तं) A century.<BR> E. वर्ष and शत a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षसहस्र
वर्षसहस्र n. (-स्रं) A thousand years.<BR> E. वर्ष, सहस्र a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षांश|वर्षांशः
वर्षांश m. (-शः) A month.<BR> E. वर्ष a year, अंश a part; also with कन् added वर्षांशक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाकाल|वर्षाकालः
वर्षाकाल n. (-लं) The rainy season.<BR> E. वर्षा and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाकालीन
वर्षाकालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Belonging to or produced in the rainy sea-<BR>son.<BR> E. वर्षाकाल and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाङ्ग|वर्षांग|वर्षाङ्गः
वर्षाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A month.<BR> E. वर्ष a year, and अङ्ग a limb or member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाघोष|वर्षाघोषः
वर्षाघोष m. (-षः) A frog.<BR> E. वर्षा and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाप्रभञ्जन|वर्षाप्रभञ्जनः
वर्षाप्रभञ्जन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Rain-scattering.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A high wind, a<BR>gale.<BR> E. वर्षा, प्रभञ्जन scattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाभू
वर्षाभू m. (-भूः) A frog.<BR>	 f. (-भ्वी)<BR>	 1. Hog-weed.<BR>	 2. An earth-worm, (Iulus.)<BR>3. A she-frog or any small frog.<BR> E. वर्षा the rains, भू to be, aff. क्किप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षामद|वर्षामदः
वर्षामद m. (-दः) A peacock.<BR> E. वर्ष the rains, आमद who rejoices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षाम्भःपारणाव्रत
वर्षाम्भःपारणाव्रत m. (-तः) A Chātaka.<BR> E. वर्षाम्भस् rain-water, पारणा atten-<BR>tion, and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षायुत
वर्षायुत n. (-तं) Ten thousand years.<BR> E. वर्ष and अयुत ten thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षारात्र|वर्षारात्रः
वर्षारात्र m. (-त्रः) A rainy night, the rainy season.<BR> E. वर्षा and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षार्च्चिस्|वर्षार्चिस्
वर्षार्च्चिस् m. (-र्च्चिः) The planet MARS.<BR> E. वर्षा the rains, अर्च्चिस् light,<BR>visible in the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षालङ्कायिका
वर्षालङ्कायिका f. (-का) A plant: see पृक्का.<BR> E. वर्ष and लङ्कायिक synonimous; conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षावसान|वर्षावसानः
वर्षावसान m. (-नः) The autumnal season.<BR> E. वर्षा the rains, अवसान end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिक
वर्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Raining, rainy, relating or belonging to the<BR>rains.<BR>	 2. Shedding, showering, pouring down.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Aloe-wood<BR>or Agallochum.<BR> E. वर्ष and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिन्
वर्षिन् mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>	 1. Raining.<BR>	 2. Sprinkling.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षिष्ठ|वर्षिष्ठः
वर्षिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Oldest, very old.<BR>	 2. Strongest.<BR> E. वर्ष substitu-<BR>ted for वृद्ध old, and इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षीयस्
वर्षीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Very aged, or old.<BR>	 2. Stronger.<BR> E. वर्ष subs-<BR>tituted for वृद्ध old, and ईयसुन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षुक|वर्षुकः
वर्षुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Rainy, watery.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle, and उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षुकाब्द|वर्षुकाब्दः
वर्षुकाब्द m. (-ब्दः) A rainy cloud.<BR> E. वर्षुक rainy, अब्द a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षेज|वर्षेजः
वर्षेज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born or produced in the rains.<BR> E. वर्षे in the rains, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षैक
वर्षैक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Yearly, annual.<BR> E. वर्षे and एक one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्षोपल|वर्षोपलः
वर्षोपल m. (-लः) Hail.<BR> E. वर्ष rain, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्म|वर्ष्मं
वर्ष्म n. (-र्ष्मं) The body: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्मन्
वर्ष्मन् n. (-र्ष्म)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. Measure.<BR>	 3. Height, elevation.<BR>	 4. A<BR>handsome form.<BR>	 5. A stone.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle, aff. मनिन्; also<BR>with a final vowel वर्ष्म ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ष्य
वर्ष्य mfn. (-र्ष्यः-र्ष्या-र्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. To be rained or showered.<BR>	 2. To be sprink-<BR>led.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ह्
वर्ह् r. 1st cl. (वर्हते)<BR>	 1. To cover.<BR>	 2. To give.<BR>	 3. To be excellent or<BR>pre-eminent: in this sense it is more properly बर्ह् r. 10th<BR>cl. (वर्हयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To kill or hurt.<BR>	 3. To speak: see बर्ह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ह|वर्हं
वर्ह n. (-र्हं)<BR>	 1. A peacock's tail.<BR>	 2. A leaf.<BR>	 3. A sort of perfume, com-<BR>monly Granthiparṇa.<BR>	 4. Train, retinue.<BR> E. वृह् to increase, aff.<BR>अच्; or वर्ह् or बर्ह् to cover, aff. अच्; in the latter case it is<BR>written बर्ह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हण|वर्हणं
वर्हण n. (-णं) A leaf.<BR> E. वृह् to grow, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हभार
वर्हभार m. (-रः) A tuft or peacock's feathers at the shaft of a lance or<BR>handle of a club.<BR> E. वर्ह and भार load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिःपुष्प|वर्हिःपुष्पं
वर्हिःपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) Granthiparṇa, a sort of vegetable perfume.<BR> E. वर्हिस्<BR>Kuśa-grass, पुष्प a flower, having a similar blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिःशुष्मन्
वर्हिःशुष्मन् m. (-ष्मा) A name of fire.<BR> E. वर्हिस् Kuśa-grass, शुष् to dry, aff. मनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिःष्ठ|वर्हिःष्ठं
वर्हिःष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) A perfume, commonly Bālā.<BR> E. वर्हिस् Kuśa grass, and<BR>स्था to be, aff. क, growing in the same places: the Visarga of वर्हिस्<BR>optionally retained; hence also वर्हिष्ठ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिकुसुम|वर्हिकुसुमं
वर्हि(-र्हिः)कुसुम n. (-मं) Granthiparna, also वर्हिपुष्प ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिर्ज्योतिस्
वर्हिर्ज्योतिस् m. (-तिः) A name of fire.<BR> E. वर्हिस् Kuśa-grass, ज्योतिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिण|वर्हिणः
वर्हिण m. (-णः) A peacock.<BR> E. वर्ह a peacock's tail, and इनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिणवाहन|वर्हिणवाहनः
वर्हिणवाहन m. (-नः) The deity Kārtikeya.<BR> E. वर्हिण a peacock, and वाहन<BR>a vehicle; mounted on that bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिध्वजा
वर्हिध्वजा f. (-जा) A name of the goddess CHANDĪ. वर्हि for वर्ही a pea-<BR>cock, and ध्वज an emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिन्
वर्हिन् m. (-र्ही) A peacock.<BR> E. वर्ह a peacock's tail, इनि possessive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिपुष्प|वर्हिपुष्पं
वर्हिपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A vegetable perfume, commonly Granthiparṇa.<BR> E. वर्हि<BR>a peacock, and पुष्प flower; also वर्हिःपुष्प ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिमुख
वर्हिमुख m. (-खः) A deity, a divinity.<BR> E. वर्हिस् fire, and मुख mouth;<BR>most offerings passing through fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिश्शुष्मन्
वर्हिश्शुष्मन् m. (-ष्मा) Fire.<BR> E. वर्हिस् an oblation, शुष्मन् who dries up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिषद्
वर्हिषद् m. (-षत् or -षद्) A Pitṛ or progenitor of a particular class. E.<BR>वर्हिष् Kuśa grass, अद् to eat, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिष्केश|वर्हिष्केशः
वर्हिष्केश m. (-शः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. वर्हिस् light, and केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिष्ठ|वर्हिष्ठं
वर्हिष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. A perfume, commonly Bālā, perhaps a species of<BR>Andropogon.<BR>	 2. The resin of the Pinus longifolia.<BR> E. वर्हिस् Kuśa-<BR>grass, स्था to stay, aff. क; the final of वर्हिस् changed to Visarga,<BR>and optionally rejected: see वर्हिःष्ठ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिष्मत्
वर्हिष्मत् mfn. (-ष्मन्-ष्मन्ती-ष्मत्)<BR>	 1. Having Kuśa or sacrificial grass.<BR>	 2.<BR>Having fire or light, blazing, shining.<BR> E. वर्हिस् and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्हिस्
वर्हिस् m. (-र्हिः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre, splendour.<BR>	 mn. (-र्हिः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Sacrificial grass, (Poa cynosuroides.)<BR>	 2. Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>	 3.<BR>Granthiparṇa, a vegetable perfume.<BR> E. वृह् to increase, aff. इसि; or<BR>वर्ह् or बर्ह् to excel, &c., with the same aff., in the latter case<BR>this word and its corresponding ones are written with an initial<BR>consonant बर्हिस्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्
वल् r. 1st cl. (वलते)<BR>	 1. To cover.<BR>	 2. To move.<BR>	 3. To surround or en-<BR>close.<BR>	 4. To go, to hasten.<BR>	 5. To be attached to.<BR>	 6. To grow, to<BR>increase. With वि, To move to and fro. r. 10th cl. (वालयति-ते) To<BR>cherish or maintain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल|वलं|वलः
वल n. (-लं) An army, forces.<BR> E. वल् to surround, aff. कः see बल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलक्ष|वलक्षः
वलक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) White.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः) White, the colour.<BR> E. वल to go,<BR>aff. क्विप्; वल् going, अक्ष् to pervade, aff. अच्; also बलक्ष, and अवलक्ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलक्षगु
वलक्षगु m. (-गुः) The moon.<BR> E. वलक्ष white, गौ a ray of light; the final<BR>vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलग्न|वलग्नं|वलग्नः
वलग्न mn. (-ग्नः-ग्नं) The middle, the waist: also अवलग्न ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलन|वलनं
वलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Turning, moving.<BR>	 2. Deflection, (in astronomy.)<BR> E. वल, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलभि|वलभिः
वलभि mf. (-भिः-भी)<BR>	 1. The wooden frame of a thatch.<BR>	 2. A turret or<BR>temporary building on the roof of a house.<BR> E. वल् to cover, अभस्<BR>aff., इन् and ङीष् added; also वडभि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलम्ब|वलंब|वलम्बः
वलम्ब m. (-म्बः) A perpendicular.<BR> E. अव, and लवि to depend, घञ् aff., the<BR>initial rejected; also अवलम्ब ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलय|वलयं|वलयः
वलय mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>	 1. A bracelet, an armlet.<BR>	 2. The zone of a married<BR>woman.<BR>	 3. Circle, circumference, boundary.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Sore-<BR>throat, inflammation of the larynx, &c.<BR>	 2. A boundary, an inclo-<BR>sure, a fence.<BR> E. वल् to surround, अयन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलयित|वलयितं
वलयित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Surrounded, encircled, enclosed, encompassed.<BR>E. वलय an inclosure. aff. इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलाक|वलाकः
वलाक mf. (-कः-का) A small kind of crane.<BR> E. वल् to surround, aff. आकन्; also बलाका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलासक|वलासकः
वलासक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 2. A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलाहक|वलाहकः
वलाहक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. A Daitya, a demon.<BR>	 4.<BR>One of the Nāgas.<BR>	 5. One of the horses of KṚṢṆA'S car. E.<BR>वलाका a crane, हा to go, aff. क्कुन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलि|वलिः
वलि f. (-लिः or ली)<BR>	 1. A line or streak made with fragrant unguents<BR>on the person.<BR>	 2. Natural line or folds of skin, a wrinkle m. (-लिः)<BR>Offerings to the spirits of air.<BR> E. वल् to surround, aff. इन्: see बलि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलि|वलिः
वलि(ली)क mn. (-कः-कं) The edge of a thatch.<BR> E. वल् to surround, Unādi<BR>aff. इकक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिक्रिया
वलिक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Making lines on the person.<BR>	 2. Making offerings to<BR>all beings.<BR> E. वलि, क्रिया act: see बलि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलित|वलितः
वलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Moved, constrained.<BR>	 2. Surrounded.<BR>	 3. Wrink-<BR>led.<BR> E. वल् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिर|वलिरः
वलिर f. (-रा) Squint-eyed.<BR> E. वल, इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलिश|वलिशं
वलिश nf. (-शं-शिः or शी) A fish-hook.<BR> E. वटिन् a bait, शो to destroy, aff.<BR>ड, ट changed to ड, and ड again interchangeable with ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलूक|वलूकं|वलूकः
वलूक n. (-कं) The root of the lotus.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A bird.<BR> E. वल् to surround,<BR>Unādi aff. ऊक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलूल|वलूलः
वलूल f. (-ला) Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्क्
वल्क् r. 10th cl. (वल्कयति-ते) To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्क|वल्कं|वल्कः
वल्क n. (-ल्कं)<BR>	 1. The bark of a tree.<BR>	 2. The scales of a fish.<BR>	 3. A gar-<BR>ment in general.<BR> E. वल् to surround, कक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्कल|वल्कलं|वल्कलः
वल्कल mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. The bark of a tree.<BR>	 2. A garment made of bark.<BR>3. A garment in general.<BR> E. वल् to surround, कलन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्कवत्|वल्कवन्त्
वल्कवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having scales or bark, wearing a dress made<BR>of the bark of trees, &c.<BR>	 m. (-वान्) A fish.<BR> E. वल्क a scale, &c., मतुप्<BR>possess. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्किल|वल्किलः
वल्किल m. (-लः) A thorn.<BR> E. वल्क bark, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्कुत|वल्कुतं
वल्कुत n. (-तं) Bark, rind.<BR> E. वल् to surround, कुतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ग्
वल्ग् r. 1st cl. (वल्गति)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To go by leaps, to jump.<BR>3. To be pleased or delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गत्
वल्गत् mfn. (-ल्गन्-ल्गन्ती-ल्गत्)<BR>	 1. Going.<BR>	 2. Jumping.<BR> E. वल्ग् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गा
वल्गा f. (-ल्गा) A bridle, a rein.<BR> E. वल्ग् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गित|वल्गितं
वल्गित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Leaped, jumped, gone by bounds or leaps.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>1. Running.<BR>	 2. A horse's gallop.<BR> E. वल्ग् to go by jumps, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गु|वल्गुः
वल्गु mfn. (-ल्गुः-ल्गुः-ल्गु)<BR>	 1. Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 2. Sweet.<BR>	 m. (-ल्गुः)<BR>A goat.<BR> E. वल् to surround, Unādi aff. उ, and गुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुक|वल्गुकं
वल्गुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Sandal.<BR>	 2. A<BR>wood.<BR>	 3. Price.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुपत्र|वल्गुपत्रः
वल्गुपत्र m. (-त्रः) A wild sort of pulse: see वनमुद्ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुला
वल्गुला f. (-ला or ली) A sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गुलिका
वल्गुलिका f. (-का) A cockroach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्गूयत्
वल्गूयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Become handsome or beautiful.<BR> E. वल्गु used as a verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्भ्
वल्भ् r. 1st cl. (वल्भते) To eat, to devour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्भन|वल्भनं
वल्भन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Eating.<BR>	 2. Food.<BR> E. वल्भ् to eat, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्भित
वल्भित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eaten.<BR> E. वल्भ् to eat, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्मिक|वल्मिकः
वल्मिक m. (-कः) An ant-hill; also वल्मीक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्मिकि|वल्मिकिः
वल्मिकि m. (-किः) An ant-hill; also वल्मीकि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्मीक|वल्मीकं|वल्मीकः
वल्मीक mn. (-कः-कं) A hillock, ground thrown up by moles, &c., but<BR>especially the large accumulations of soil, sometimes made by the<BR>white ant.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The poet VĀLMĪKI.<BR>	 2. Elephantiasis, or<BR>swellings of the neck, chest, hands and feet, which break and<BR>discharge ichor in many places.<BR> E. वल् to cover, or बल् to live,<BR>ईक Unādi aff., and मुट् augment; in the latter case this word<BR>and the corresponding ones are written बल्मीक, &c.; also वल्मिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्मीकूट|वल्मीकूटं
वल्मीकूट n. (-टं) An ant-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्युल्
वल्युल् and वल्यूल् r. 10th cl. (व[ल्यु]ल्यूलयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cut.<BR>	 2. To purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ल्
वल्ल् r. 1st cl. (वल्लते)<BR>	 1. To cover, to conceal.<BR>	 2. To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ल|वल्लः
वल्ल m. (-ल्लः)<BR>	 1. Winnowing corn.<BR>	 2. A Masha of silver.<BR>	 3. A weight of<BR>three Rattis.<BR>	 4. Prohibiting, prohibition.<BR>	 5. Covering.<BR> E. वल्ल् to<BR>move, &c., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लकी
वल्लकी f. (-की) The Vinā, or Indian lute.<BR> E. वल्ल् to cover, aff. क्वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभ|वल्लभः
वल्लभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. Beloved, desired, dear.<BR>	 2. Supreme, superin-<BR>tending.<BR>	 m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A lover, a husband, a friend.<BR>	 2. A horse with<BR>good marks.<BR>	 3. A superintendent, an overseer.<BR>	 4. The chief<BR>herdsman.<BR>	 f. (-भा) A mistress, a wife.<BR> E. वल्ल् to cover, अभच् Unādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभपालक|वल्लभपालकः
वल्लभपालक m. (-कः) A groom, a horse-keeper.<BR> E. वल्लभ a good horse, पालक who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभाचार्य्य|वल्लभाचार्य|वल्लभाचार्यः
वल्लभाचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) Name of the founder of a Vaishnaba sect; he<BR>is also a commentator of the Vedānta-sutra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभायित|वल्लभायितं
वल्लभायित n. (-तं) A mode of coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लर|वल्लरं
वल्लर n. (-रं) Aloe-wood.<BR>	 2. A bower.<BR>	 3. A branching foot-stalk.<BR> E. वल्ल्-अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लरि|वल्लरिः
वल्लरि f. (-रिः or री)<BR>	 1. A compound pedicle.<BR>	 2. A creeping or twining<BR>plant.<BR> E. वल्ल् to cover, अरन् aff, ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लव|वल्लवः
वल्लव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A cook.<BR>	 2. A herdsman.<BR>	 3. A name of BHĪMASENA.<BR>f. (-वी) A cowherdess.<BR> E. वल्ल covering, and व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लि|वल्लिः
वल्लि f. (-ल्लिः or ल्ली)<BR>	 1. A creeper, a climbing or creeping plant.<BR>	 f. (-ल्लिः)<BR>The earth.<BR>	 f. (-ल्ली) A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen.)<BR> E. वल्ल् to cover,<BR>इन् aff., and ङीप् occasionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लीज|वल्लीजं
वल्लीज n. (-जं) Pepper.<BR> E. वल्ली a creeper, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लुर|वल्लुरं
वल्लुर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. An arbour, a bower, a place over-grown with creeping<BR>plants.<BR>	 2. An uncultivated field or place overrun with wild grass.<BR>3. A sand, a desert, a place destitute of water.<BR>	 4. A field.<BR>	 5. A<BR>compound pedicle.<BR>	 6. A solitude, a wild.<BR>	 7. A thicket, a wood.<BR>8. Dried flesh.<BR> E. वल्ल् to cover, उरन् aff.; also वल्लूर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लूर|वल्लूरं|वल्लूरः
वल्लूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Dried flesh.<BR>	 2. Hog's flesh, the flesh of the wild<BR>hog.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. An uncultivated field, or one over run with grass.<BR>2. A thicket.<BR>	 3. A desert.<BR> E. वल्ल् to cover, ऊरन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ल्या
वल्ल्या f. (-ल्ल्या) Emblic myrobalan.<BR> E. वल्ल् to cover, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्वज|वल्वजः
वल्वज m. (-जः) A sort of coarse grass, (Eleusine Indica.)<BR> E. वलते भुवं<BR>वेष्टयति वल्-क्विप् तादृशः सन् वजति गच्छति वज्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ह्
वल्ह् r. 1st cl. (वल्ह्ते)<BR>	 1. To kill or hurt.<BR>	 2. To cover.<BR>	 3. To give.<BR>	 4.<BR>To be pre-eminent; in which sense it is more properly बल्ह्<BR>r. 10th cl. (वल्ह्यति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्
वश् r. 2nd cl. (वष्टि)<BR>	 1. To desire, to will, to wish.<BR>	 2. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश|वशं|वशः
वश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Humbled, subdued, tamed, over-powered.<BR>	 2.<BR>Enthralled, subdued by charms and incantations, fascinated,<BR>charmed, enchanted.<BR>	 mn. (-शः-शं) Wish, desire.<BR>	 n. (-शं)<BR>	 1. Autho-<BR>rity, supremacy, mastership.<BR>	 2. Subjection, submission, the state<BR>of being completely tamed and over-powered.<BR>	 3. Birth.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>The residence of harlots.<BR>	 f. (-शा)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. A wife.<BR>	 3. A<BR>daughter.<BR>	 4. A barren cow.<BR>	 5. A barren woman.<BR>	 6. A female ele-<BR>phant.<BR>	 7. A husband's sister.<BR> E. वश् to desire, aff. अप् or अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशका
वशका f. (-का) An obedient and docile wife.<BR> E. वश् subject, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशक्रिया
वशक्रिया f. (-या) Subduing or over-powering by drugs, gems, charms,<BR>or incantations.<BR>	 2. The drugs, &c. so used.<BR> E. वश subjection, क्रिया<BR>business or agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशग
वशग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Obedient, subject.<BR>	 f. (-गा) An obedient wife. E.<BR>वश subject, and ग who goes or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशङ्गत|वशंगत
वशङ्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Subject, obedient.<BR> E. वश and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशम्बद
वशम्बद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Submissive, acknowledging obedience or sub-<BR>jection.<BR> E. वश subjection, बद् to speak, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशवर्त्तिन्|वशवर्तिन्
वशवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) Obsequious, acting under subjection, or<BR>according to the pleasure of another.<BR> E. वश and वर्त्तिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशाकु
वशाकु m. (-कुः) A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशाढ्यक|वशाढ्यकः
वशाढ्यक m. (-कः) A porpoise, the Gangetic porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशात्
वशात् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of “through the power or influence of.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशानुग
वशानुग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Obedient, submissive.<BR>	 m. (-गः) A servant. E.<BR>वश, अनुग who pursues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशापायिन्
वशापायिन् m. (-यी) A dog.<BR> E. वशा subjection, पा to preserve, इनि aff., युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशि|वशिः
वशि m. (-शिः) Subjugating, fascinating, bewitching, holding others in<BR>magical or mysterious submission to one's will.<BR> E. वश् to desire,<BR>(supremacy,) इन् affix; also with तल् and त्व affs. वशिता and वशित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिक|वशिकः
वशिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Void, empty.<BR>	 f. (-का) Aloe-wood.<BR> E. वश् to<BR>desire, इन् aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिता
वशिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Fascinating, bewitching.<BR>	 2. Subjection, holding in<BR>order or subjugation; also वशित्वं.<BR> E. वशिन् and तल् or त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिन्
वशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>	 1. Subdued, subjugated, in subjection.<BR>	 2.<BR>Powerful.<BR>	 m. (-शी) A sage with subdued passions.<BR>	 f. (-शिनी)<BR>	 1. The<BR>Śhamī tree, (Mimosa Sama, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A parasite plant.<BR> E. वश, इनि<BR>and ङीप् affixes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिर|वशिरं|वशिरः
वशिर n. (-रं) Sea-salt.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of long pepper: see वशीर.<BR>	 3. Orris root.<BR> E. वश् to desire, इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिष्ठ|वशिष्ठः
वशिष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) VASHISṬHA, a Ṛṣi or divine sage of the first order,<BR>he is also a Brahmādika, a Prajāpati, and one of the seven<BR>stars of Ursa Major.<BR> E. अव before, शास् to govern, to instruct, (the<BR>other saints,) aff. क्त; the first vowel of the prefix rejected: also<BR>written वशिष्ट and वसिष्ट । अतिशयेन वशी इष्ठन् इनेर्लुक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीकरण|वशीकरणं
वशीकरण n. (-ण)<BR>	 1. Subduing or overcoming by drugs, charms, &c.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">Page637-a+ 60</a>]<BR>enchanting, charming.<BR>	 2. Subduing in general.<BR> E. वश subduing,<BR>and करण making, च्वि augment, leaving ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीकृत
वशीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bewitched, fascinated, subjected to another's<BR>will.<BR> E. वशी and कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीभूत|वशीभूतः
वशीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Subjugated, subject to another's will.<BR> E. वशी and<BR>भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीर|वशीरः
वशीर m. (-रः) A pungent fruit resembling pepper, (Pothos officinalis:)<BR>also वशिर ।<BR> E. वश, ईरन् aff. “गजपिप्पल्याम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्य|वश्यं|वश्यः
वश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं)<BR>	 1. Docile, tame, humble, governable.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>tamed or humbled.<BR>	 m. (-श्यः) A dependent, a slave, f. (-श्या) A do-<BR>cile and obedient wife.<BR>	 n. (-श्यं) Cloves.<BR> E. वश subjection, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्यका
वश्यका f. (-का) An obedient wife.<BR> E. वश्या and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्यता
वश्यता f. (-ता) Humility, subjugation, disposition to, or fitness for sub-<BR>jection.<BR> E. वश्य and तल् aff.; also with त्व, वश्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्यात्मन्
वश्यात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Of subdued mind.<BR> E. वशी and आत्मन् spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्
वष् r. 1st cl. (वषति) To kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्
वषट् Ind. An exclamation used on making an oblation to a deity with<BR>fire, (used with a dat.)<BR> E. वह् to bear or convey, aff. डषट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्कर्त्तृ|वषट्कर्तृ
वषट्कर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) The priest who pours the oiled butter into the fire<BR>at a sacrifice with the exclamation वषट्.<BR> E. वषट् an exclamation,<BR>&c., and कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्कार|वषट्कारः
वषट्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The formula वषट्.<BR>	 2. An oblation made with the<BR>exclamation वषट्.<BR> E. वषट् the exclamation used on this occasion,<BR>and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषटकृत
वषटकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Offered or sacrificed with fire with the formula<BR>वषट्.<BR> E. वषट् as above, कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्क्
वष्क् r. 1st cl. (वष्कते) r. 10th cl. (वष्कयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To see.<BR>	 2. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्कय|वष्कयः
वष्कय m. (-यः) A one year old calf.<BR> E. वष्क् to go, अयन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्कयणी
वष्कयणी f. (-णी) A cow bearing many calves.<BR> E. वष्कय a calf, नी to have,<BR>affs. ड and ङीष्; also वष्कय, with इनि and ङीप् affs., वष्कयिणी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्
वस्(औ)औवस r. 1st cl. (वसति) To dwell or inhabit. r. 2nd cl. (वस्ते) To<BR>cover with dress, to wear as clothes. r. 10th cl. (वसयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To per-<BR>fume.<BR>	 2. To dwell. (वासयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be affectionate, to love.<BR>	 2. To<BR>cut or divide.<BR>	 3. To kill.<BR>	 4. To accept. (इर, उ) इरवसु r. 4th cl.<BR>(वस्यति) To be straight, to be unbending; literally or figuratively.<BR>With अधि prefixed, To sit upon, to occupy. With उप, To fast.<BR>With नि, 1. To dwell in or inhabit.<BR>	 2. To dress. With प्र, To<BR>dwell abroad. With सम्, To cohabit. Caus. (वासयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cause<BR>to live or dwell.<BR>	 2. To put on, to dress. With निस्, To drive away,<BR>to expel, to banish. With प्र, To exile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसत्
वसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती or सती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Dwelling, inhabiting.<BR>	 2. Wearing,<BR>(as clothes.)<BR> E. वस् to dwell, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसति|वसतिः
वसति f. (-तिः or ती)<BR>	 1. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 2. Abiding, abode, resi-<BR>dence.<BR>	 3. Night.<BR> E. वस् to dwell, अति Unādi aff., ङीष् optionally<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन|वसनं
वसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cloth or clothes.<BR>	 2. Covering, clothing.<BR>	 3. A dwelling,<BR>a house.<BR>	 4. An ornament worn by women round the loins.<BR>	 5.<BR>Dwelling, residing.<BR> E. वस् to be clothed, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसनसद्मन्
वसनसद्मन् n. (-द्म) A tent.<BR> E. वसन and सद्मन् a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्त|वसंत|वसंतः|वसन्तः
वसन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Vasanta, the season of spring, comprising the month<BR>of Chaitra and Vaisākha, or its deified personification, which is<BR>considered to be a companion of KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 2. Dysentery,<BR>diarrhœa.<BR>	 3. Small-pox.<BR> E. वस् to dwell, Unādi aff. झच्, as<BR>applied to the season, when love is especially present on earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तकाल|वसंतकाल|वसन्तकालः
वसन्तकाल m. (-लः) The vernal season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तकुसुम|वसन्तकुसुमः
वसन्तकुसुम m. (-मः) A tree, (Cordia myxa and latifolia.)<BR> E. वसन्त spring,<BR>कुसुम a flower; blossoming in the spring. “वसन्तफुलेर गाछ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तघोषिन्|वसंतघोषिन्
वसन्तघोषिन् m. (-षी) The Indian cuckoo or Kokila.<BR> E. वसन्त spring,<BR>घोषिन् who sings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तज
वसन्तज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced in the spring.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. A festival in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">Page637-b+ 60</a>]<BR>honour of KĀMADEVA, held in the month of Chaitra.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Mādhabi creeper.<BR> E. वसन्त, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तदूत|वसंतदूत|वसन्तदूतः
वसन्तदूत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 2. The month Chai-<BR>tra, (March-April.)<BR>	 3. The mango tree.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. The trumpet<BR>flower.<BR>	 2. A large and beautiful creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.) E.<BR>वसन्त spring, and दूत the messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तद्रु|वसंतद्रु|वसन्तद्रुः
वसन्तद्रु m. (-द्रुः) The mango tree, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR> E. वसन्त spring,<BR>and द्रु a tree, or वसन्तद्रुम; the mango blossoms in March or April,<BR>and is then an object of great beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तपञ्चमी|वसंतपंचमी
वसन्तपञ्चमी f. (-मी) The fifth day of the light-half of Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तसख|वसंतसख|वसन्तसखः
वसन्तसख m. (-खः) KĀMADEVA or CUPID.<BR> E. वसन्त spring, सखि the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तोत्सव|वसंतोत्सव|वसन्तोत्सवः
वसन्तोत्सव n. (-वं) The celebration of the return of spring, formerly held<BR>on the full-moon of Chaitra, but now on the full-moon of Phāl-<BR>guṇa, being identified with the Dola-yātra or Holi.<BR> E. वसन्त and<BR>उत्सव a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसा
वसा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. The serum or marrow of the flesh, considered by some<BR>authorities as distinct from the marrow of the bones, though<BR>regarded by others as the same substance.<BR>	 2. Adeps, fat, suet. E.<BR>वस् to divide, (in the body,) अङ् and टाप् affs.; or वस्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसाढ्य|वसाढ्यः
वसाढ्य m. (-ढ्यः) The Gangetic porpoise, (Delphinus Gangeticus;) also<BR>वसाढ्यक and वशाढ्यक, the last perhaps incorrectly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसान
वसान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wearing, putting on, (as clothes.)<BR> E. वस् to<BR>clothe, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसापायिन्
वसापायिन् m. (-यी) A dog.<BR> E. वसा and पायिन् who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसार
वसार n. (-रं) Wish, purpose, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसि|वसिः
वसि m. (-सिः)<BR>	 1. Dwelling, abode.<BR>	 2. A dwelling.<BR>	 3. Clothes.<BR> E. वस् to dwell, Unādi aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसित
वसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stored, (as grain.)<BR>	 2. Dwelling, inhabiting.<BR>3. Put on, worn.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Abiding, residence.<BR>	 f. (-ता) The power of<BR>subduing all things: see वशिता.<BR> E. वस् to dwell, &c., क्त aff.; or<BR>वशिता as above, and श changed to स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसितृ
वसितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what wears.<BR> E. वस् to put on, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसित्वा
वसित्वा Ind. Having put on, (as clothes,) wearing.<BR> E. वस् to wear, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिर|वसिरं
वसिर n. (-रं) Sea-salt.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A pungent fruit, considered as a sort of<BR>pepper, (Pothos officinalis.)<BR> E. वस् to abide, (in the sea,) इरन् aff.;<BR>also, as derived from वश् to desire, वशिर &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिष्ठ|वसिष्ठः
वसिष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A celebrated Muni.<BR> E. वस् to abide, (in the practice of<BR>religious austerities,) aff. णिनि, वसिन्, superlative aff. इष्टन् added;<BR>pre-eminent amongst the ascetics; also वशिष्ठ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसु|वसुः
वसु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>	 1. Sweet, sweet-flavoured.<BR>	 2. Dry, dried.<BR>	 n. (-सु)<BR>	 1.<BR>Wealth, thing, substance.<BR>	 2. A gem, a jewel.<BR>	 3. A medicinal root,<BR>commonly Vriddhi.<BR>	 4. Water.<BR>	 5. Gold.<BR>	 6. A yellow kind of kidney-<BR>bean.<BR>	 7. A sort of salt.<BR>	 8. The number eight, i. e. the eight<BR>Vasus.<BR>	 m. (-सुः)<BR>	 1. A kind of demi-god, of whom eight are enumer-<BR>ated, viz.:--DHARA, DHRUVA, SOMA or the moon, ĀPA, ANILA<BR>or wind, ANALA or fire, PRABHĀSA and PRATYUSA.<BR>	 2. A name<BR>of ĀGNI or fire.<BR>	 3. A ray of light.<BR>	 4. The tie of a yoke.<BR>	 5. A tree,<BR>(Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR>	 6. The name of a king.<BR>	 7. A name of<BR>KUVERA.<BR>	 8. A tree in general.<BR>	 9. A lake, a pool.<BR>	 10. A rein, a<BR>halter.<BR>	 11. A plant, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>	 12. ŚIVA.<BR>	 13. The sun.<BR>14. A kind of fish.<BR> E. वस् to abide or dwell, Unādi aff. उ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसु|वसुः
वसु(सू)क n. (-कं) A fossil-salt, brought from a district in Ajmere,<BR>Sambhar-salt.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (Gigantic Asclepias.)<BR>	 2. A tree,<BR>(Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding; or वसु<BR>wealth, कै to sound, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुकीट|वसुकीटः
वसुकीट m. (-टः) A supplicant, a beggar, a petitioner.<BR> E. वसु wealth, कीट a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदा
वसुदा f. (-दा) The earth.<BR> E. वसु wealth, and दा who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेव|वसुदेवः
वसुदेव m. (-वः) BASUDEVA, the father of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. वसु a deity, the in-<BR>carnation of one of the Vasus, or वसु wealth, दिव् to shine, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेवता
वसुदेवता f. (-ता) The constellation Dhanisṭhā.<BR> E. वसु the Vasus, and<BR>देवता divinity; presiding over the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेवभू
वसुदेवभू m. (-भूः) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. वसुदेव and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेव्या
वसुदेव्या f. (-व्या)<BR>	 1. The asterism Dhanisṭhā.<BR>	 2. The ninth day of the fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधर्म्मिका|वसुधर्मिका
वसुधर्म्मिका f. (-का) Crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधा
वसुधा f. (-धा) The earth.<BR> E. वसु wealth, धा to have or contain, affs. क and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधाधर
वसुधाधर m. (-रः) A mountain.<BR> E. वसुधा and धर what holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधाधिप
वसुधाधिप m. (-पः) A king.<BR> E. वसुधा and अधिप sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधानगर
वसुधानगर n. (-रं) The capital of VARUṆA in the western ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुधारा
वसुधारा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A female Śaktī peculiar to the Jainas.<BR>	 2. The capital<BR>of KUVERA.<BR> E. वसु wealth, धृ to have, affs. घञ् and टाप्; some<BR>authorities read वसुभारा for KUVERA'S capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुन्धरा|वसुंधरा
वसुन्धरा f. (-रा) The earth.<BR> E. वसु wealth, धृ to have, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुप्राण|वसुप्राणः
वसुप्राण m. (-णः) Fire or its deity, AGNI.<BR> E. वसु a Vasu, प्राण life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुमत्|वसुमन्त्
वसुमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Wealthy, rich.<BR>	 f. (-ती) The earth.<BR> E. वसु<BR>wealth, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुरेतस्
वसुरेतस् m. (-ताः) Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुरोचिस्
वसुरोचिस् n. (-चिः) A religious ceremony in which the demi-gods called<BR>Vasus especially are worshipped.<BR> E. वसु, रुच् to shine, इसि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुल|वसुलः
वसुल m. (-लः) A deity, a divinity.<BR> E. वसु wealth, ला to have, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुश्रेष्ठ|वसुश्रेष्ठं
वसुश्रेष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Wrought gold.<BR>	 2. Silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुषेण|वसुषेणः
वसुषेण m. (-णः) A name of KARṆA, the illegitimate brother of the<BR>PĀṆḌU princes.<BR> E. वसु wealth, सेना an army; surrounded by<BR>hosts of beggars for his wealth, of which he was liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुस्थली
वसुस्थली f. (-ली) The city of KUVERA.<BR> E. वसु wealth, स्थल place or site,<BR>aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुहट्ट|वसुहट्टः
वसुहट्ट m. (-ट्टः) The Vaka-puspa, (Sesbana grandiflora;) also वसुहट्टक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसूक|वसूकं|वसूकः
वसूक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Sambhar-salt.<BR>	 2. The Sesbana grandiflora. E. See वसुक<BR>the उ of वसुक is here optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसूरा
वसूरा f. (-रा) A whore, a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्क्
वस्क् r. 1st cl. (वस्कते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्क|वस्कः
वस्क m. (-स्कः)<BR>	 1. Application, perseverance.<BR>	 2. Going, motion.<BR> E. वस्क्<BR>to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्कय|वस्कयः
वस्कय m. (-यः) A calf of one year, a yearling.<BR> E. वस्क् to go, अयन् aff.; also वष्कय &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्कयणी
वस्कयणी f. (-णी) A cow bearing many calves.<BR> E. वस्कय a calf, णी to have,<BR>affs. ड and ङीप्; also वष्कयणी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्कराटिका
वस्कराटिका f. (-का) A scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्
वस्त् r. 10th cl. (वस्तयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To go or move.<BR>	 3. To ask, to beg, to solicit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त|वस्तं|वस्तः
वस्त m. (-स्तः) A goat.<BR>	 n. (-स्तं) A house.<BR> E. वस्त् to kill, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तक|वस्तकं
वस्तक n. (-कं) A factitious salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तमोदा
वस्तमोदा f. (-दा) A plant, (Ligusticum ajwaen:) see अजमोदा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तव्य
वस्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be dwelt in, or inhabited, resided,<BR>remained at, &c.<BR> E. वस् to dwell, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तान्त्री
वस्तान्त्री f. (-न्त्री)<BR>	 1. Benzoin or storax.<BR>	 2. A plant, commonly Ajā-shringī.<BR>E. वस्त a goat, and अन्त्र entrail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्ति|वस्तिः
वस्ति mf. (-स्तिः)<BR>	 1. The lower belly, hypogastric or pubic region.<BR>	 2.<BR>The bladder.<BR>	 3. A clyster-syringe, or bag made of bladder or gut,<BR>with a wooden or metallic nozzle.<BR>	 4. Abiding, dwelling, staying.<BR>plu. only (-स्तयः) The ends of a cloth.<BR> E. वस् to wear, Unādi aff.<BR>ति; or वस् to abide, क्तिन् aff.; or वस्ते आवृणोति मूत्रम् वस्-तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तिकर्म्माढ्य|वस्तिकर्माढ्य|वस्तिकर्माढ्यः|वस्तिकर्म्माढ्यः
वस्तिकर्म्माढ्य m. (-ढ्यः) The soap-berry, (Sapindus detergens.)<BR> E. वस्ति the<BR>ends of cloth, कर्म्म business, and आढ्य rich in; used in washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तिमल|वस्तिमलं
वस्तिमल n. (-लं) Urine, piss.<BR> E. वस्ति the belly, and मल excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तिशिरस्
वस्तिशिरस् n. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The neck of the bladder.<BR>	 2. The pipe of the clys-<BR>ter-bag.<BR> E. वस्ति and शिरस् head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तिशोधन
वस्तिशोधन n. (-नं) A diuretic.<BR> E. वस्ति and शोधन cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तु
वस्तु n. (-स्तु)<BR>	 1. Thing, matter, substance.<BR>	 2. Natural disposition, es-<BR>sential property, nature, essence.<BR>	 3. The pith or substance of any<BR>thing.<BR>	 4. The main plot or subject of a poem or play.<BR>	 5. The rear.<BR>E. वस् to abide, Unādi aff. तुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तुक|वस्तुकं
वस्तुक n. (-कं) A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR> E. वस् to abide, (in<BR>the ground,) उकञ् aff., and तुट् augment; also वास्तुक, वास्तूक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तुतस्
वस्तुतस् Ind. In fact, really, essentially, substantially.<BR> E. वस्तु, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तुमात्र
वस्तुमात्र n. (-त्रं) Outline of any subject, skeleton of a discourse.<BR> E. वस्तु<BR>and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तुहानि
वस्तुहानि f. (-निः) Loss of substance or property.<BR> E. वस्तु and हानि abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्तूत्थापन
वस्तूत्थापन n. (-नं) Producing any change or incident in a play by magic.<BR>E. वस्तु and उत्थापन raising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्वन्तर
वस्त्वन्तर n. (-रं) Another thing or subject.<BR> E. वस्तु and अन्तर other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्वभाव|वस्त्वभावः
वस्त्वभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Insubstantial existence.<BR>	 2. Loss or destruction of<BR>property.<BR> E. वस्तु and अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्य|वस्त्यं
वस्त्य n. (-स्त्यं) A house.<BR> E. वस् to abide, ति aff. and यत् added; this word<BR>has many etymologies; it is also read पस्त्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्र|वस्त्रं
वस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>	 1. Cloth, clothes, raiment.<BR>	 2. Covering, a cover.<BR> E. वस्<BR>to wear, (as clothes,) ष्ट्रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रकुट्टिम|वस्त्रकुट्टिमं
वस्त्रकुट्टिम n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. A tent.<BR>	 2. An umbrella. वस्त्र cloth, and कुट्टिम a hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रगृह|वस्त्रगृहं
वस्त्रगृह n. (-हं) A tent.<BR> E. वस्त्र cloth, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रग्रन्थि|वस्त्रग्रंथि|वस्त्रग्रन्थिः
वस्त्रग्रन्थि m. (-न्थिः) The string or twist by which the lower garments<BR>are fastened above the hips.<BR> E. वस्त्र cloth, and ग्रन्थि knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रनिर्णेजक|वस्त्रनिर्णेजकः
वस्त्रनिर्णेजक m. (-कः) A washerman.<BR> E. वस्त्र, निर्णेजक who washes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रपुत्त्रिका
वस्त्रपुत्त्रिका f. (-का) A doll, a puppet.<BR> E. वस्त्र cloth, पुत्त्री infant, (as it<BR>were,) कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रभेदक|वस्त्रभेदकः
वस्त्रभेदक m. (-कः) A tailor.<BR> E. वस्त्र cloth, clothes, भेदक who pierces or cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रभेदिन्
वस्त्रभेदिन् m. (-दी) A tailor.<BR> E. वस्त्र cloth, add भेदिन् who pierces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रयुग्म
वस्त्रयुग्म n. (-ग्मं) A pair of clothes.<BR> E. वस्त्र and युग्म a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रयोनि|वस्त्रयोनिः
वस्त्रयोनि f. (-निः) The basis or material of cloth, as cotton, silk, wool,<BR>&c.<BR> E. वस्त्र cloth, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्ररञ्जन|वस्त्ररंजन|वस्त्ररञ्जनः
वस्त्ररञ्जन m. (-नः) Safflower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्राञ्चल|वस्त्रांचल|वस्त्राञ्चलः
वस्त्राञ्चल n. (-लं) The end or hem of a garment.<BR> E. वस्त्र, अञ्चल the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्त्रापहारक
वस्त्रापहारक m. (-कः) A stealer of clothes.<BR> E. वस्त्र and अपहारक who<BR>carries off; also वस्त्रापहारिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्न|वस्नं|वस्नः
वस्न m. (-स्नः) Price.<BR>	 n. (-स्नं)<BR>	 1. Wages, hire.<BR>	 2. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 3.<BR>Wealth.<BR>	 4. Death.<BR>	 5. Abiding, dwelling.<BR>	 6. Thing, substance.<BR>7. Skin.<BR>	 9. Health.<BR> E. वस् to dwell, Unādi aff. मन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्नन|वस्ननं
वस्नन n. (-नं) An ornament for a woman's loins, a zone, a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्नसा
वस्नसा f. (-सा) A tendon, a nerve, a fibre, described as a hollow tube<BR>resembling a string, attached to the bones, and supposed to be<BR>for the passage of the vital air.<BR> E. वस्न skin, सो to destroy, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्निक
वस्निक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Hireling, mercenary.<BR>	 2. Purchasable.<BR>	 3. Re-<BR>lating to hire, wages, price, &c.<BR> E. वस्न hire, &c., and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्वौकसारा
वस्वौकसारा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. The capital of INDRA.<BR>	 2. ALAKĀ, the residence of<BR>KUVERA.<BR>	 3. A lake attached to ALAKĀ or AMARĀVATĪ, and<BR>belonging to either deity.<BR> E. वसु the Vasus, ओकस् a residence, रा<BR>to contain, with आङ् prefixed, and क and टाप् affs., the favourite<BR>haunts of these demi-gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्
वह् r. 1st cl. (वहति) To bear, to carry, to convey or transport. (वहते) To<BR>flow, (as a stream.) Desid. (विवक्षति-ते) [This is one of those roots which<BR>take two accusatives.] 1. To transport.<BR>	 2. To move on.<BR>	 3. To flow.<BR>4. To blow.<BR>	 5. To marry.<BR>	 6. To be responsible for.<BR>	 7. To waft, to<BR>propel.<BR>	 8. To bear the load of.<BR>	 9. To possess. With अति, To pass,<BR>(as time.) With अप, 1. To carry off.<BR>	 2. To deduct. With आ, 1.<BR>To cause to bring about.<BR>	 2. To flow.<BR>	 3. To have, to possess. With<BR>उद्, 1. To raise, to elevate, to bear up.<BR>	 2. To marry.<BR>	 3. To bear<BR>the burden of.<BR>	 4. To wear.<BR>	 5. To have. With उप, To commence.<BR>With नि, To support. With निस्, To be finished. With परि, To<BR>overflow. With प्र, 1. To draw, to carry.<BR>	 2. To blow.<BR>	 3. To flow.<BR>4. To waft, (as scent.)<BR>	 5. To bear the burden of. With वि, To<BR>marry. With सम, 1. To bear along.<BR>	 2. To take a wife.<BR>	 3. To press<BR>together.<BR>	 4. To display. Caus. (वाहयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cause to draw or<BR>carry.<BR>	 2. To traverse, to go over. With अति, To lead, (as life.)<BR>With आ, To invoke. With निस्, To perform, to manage, to com-<BR>plete. With सम्, To press together, to rub. (इ) वहि r. 10th cl.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">Page639-a+ 60</a>]<BR>(वंहयति-ते) To shine. r. 1st cl. (वंहते) To grow or increase; this<BR>last root is more properly बहि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह|वहः
वह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Bearing, conveying.<BR>	 2. Any vehicle or means of con-<BR>veyance, as a horse, a car, &c.<BR>	 3. The shoulder of an ox.<BR>	 4. Air,<BR>wind.<BR>	 5. A road, a way.<BR>	 6. Any male river.<BR>	 7. A measure of four<BR>Droṇas.<BR>	 f. (-हा) A river in general.<BR> E. वह् to bear, aff. घ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहंलिह
वहंलिह m. (-हः) An ox.<BR> E. वह the shoulder, लिह् to lick, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहत्
वहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>	 1. Bearing, conveying.<BR>	 2. Assuming, taking.<BR>3. Wearing.<BR>	 4. Having, possessing.<BR> E. वह् to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहत|वहतः
वहत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. An ox.<BR>	 2. A traveller.<BR> E. वह to bear, Unādi aff. अतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहति|वहतिः
वहति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. An ox.<BR>	 2. A friend, a counsellor.<BR>	 3. Air, wind.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ती) A river.<BR> E. वह् to bear, अति Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहतु|वहतुः
वहतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. An ox.<BR>	 2. A traveller.<BR> E. वह् to bear, Unādi aff. अतु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहन|वहनं
वहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Bearing, conveying.<BR>	 2. Flowing, (as a stream.)<BR>	 3. Any<BR>vehicle.<BR>	 4. A raft, a float.<BR> E. वह् to bear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहनीय
वहनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be carried or borne.<BR> E. वह् to bear, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहन्त|वहंत|वहंतः|वहन्तः
वहन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. An infant.<BR> E. वह् to bear, Unādi aff. झच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहमान
वहमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Bearing, conveying.<BR>	 2. Having, possessing.<BR>3. Flowing.<BR> E. वह् to bear, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहल|वहलः
वहल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Hard, firm, compact.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A raft, a float.<BR> E. वह् to bear, aff. अलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहलचक्षुस्
वहलचक्षुस् m. (-क्षुः) A climbing and milky plant, (Asclepias geminata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिःकुटीचर|वहिःकुटीचरः
वहिःकुटीचर m. (-रः) A crab.<BR> E. वहिस् externally, कुटी crookedly, चर<BR>what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिःस्थ
वहिःस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) External, outer.<BR> E. वहिर् and स्था to stay, ड<BR>aff.; also वहिःस्थित, वहिःस्थायिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहित|वहितः
वहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, celebrated.<BR>	 2. Borne, conveyed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Obtained.<BR> E. वह् to bear, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहित्र|वहित्रं
वहित्र n. (-त्रं) A raft, a float, a boat, a vessel.<BR> E. वह् to bear, Unādi<BR>aff. इत्र; also with कन् added, वहित्रक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिन्
वहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Bearing, conveying.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A boat, a vessel.<BR>E. वस् to bear, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिरङ्ग
वहिरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. An outer or external part, limb, member, property,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A stranger, an indifferent person.<BR> E. वहिर् and अङ्ग a limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिरिन्द्रिय
वहिरिन्द्रिय n. (-यं) An organ of sense or perception, an organ of action,<BR>as the eye, hand, &c.<BR> E. वहिर् and इन्द्रिय organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्गत
वहिर्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone out or forth.<BR> E. वहिर् and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्गमन
वहिर्गमन n. (-नं) Going forth or out.<BR> E. वहिर् and गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्देश|वहिर्द्देश
वहिर्देश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A foreign country.<BR>	 2. A place without a town or<BR>village.<BR> E. वहिर् and देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्द्वार|वहिर्द्वारं
वहिर्द्वार n. (-रं) An outer gate.<BR> E. वहिर् for वहिस् outer, and द्वार door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्द्वारप्रकोष्ठक|वहिर्द्वारप्रकोष्ठकः
वहिर्द्वारप्रकोष्ठक n. (-कं) A portico, a covered terrace before the door of<BR>a house.<BR> E. वहिर्द्वार an outer door, प्रकोष्ठ an elbow, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्भव
वहिर्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced externally.<BR> E. वहिस् outwardly, भव<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्भूत|वहिर्भूतः
वहिर्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Being out or without, excluded.<BR> E. वहिस्, भूत being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्म्मुख|वहिर्मुख|वहिर्मुखः
वहिर्म्मुख m. (-खः) A deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिर्लम्ब
वहिर्लम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं) Obtuse angular.<BR> E. वहिस् and लम्ब a perpendicular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिश्चर|वहिश्चरः
वहिश्चर m. (-रः) A crab.<BR> E. वहिस् externally, and चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिष्क
वहिष्क f. (-ष्का) External, outer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिष्करण
वहिष्करण n. (-णं) Expelling, excluding.<BR> E. वहिस् out, and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिष्कृत
वहिष्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Expelled, excluded.<BR> E. वहिस् and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहिस्
वहिस् Ind. Out, outwards, external.<BR> E. वह् to bear, aff. इसुन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वहीरु
वहीरु m. (-रुः) A tendon, a nerve, a muscle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्नि|वह्निः
वह्नि m. (-ह्निः)<BR>	 1. Fire, or its deity Agni.<BR>	 2. Lead-wort, (Plumbago zey-<BR>lanica.)<BR>	 3. Marking-nut plant.<BR>	 4. Appetite, digestion, the meta-<BR>phorical fire of the stomach.<BR> E. वह to bear, (the oblations pre-<BR>sented to the gods,) and नि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निकर
वह्निकर mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं)<BR>	 1. Making fire, lighting.<BR>	 2. Stomachic,<BR>giving appetite.<BR>	 f. (-री) A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR> E. वह्नि fire,<BR>(appetite,) कृ to make, aff. अच् or ट, and टाप् or ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निगन्ध|वह्निगंध|वह्निगन्धः
वह्निगन्ध m. (-न्धः) Incense or resin<BR> E. वह्नि fire, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निगर्भ|वह्निगर्भः
वह्निगर्भ m. (-र्भः) A bamboo.<BR>	 f. (-र्भा) A sort of Mimosa, (M. Suma. Rox.)<BR>E. वह्नि fire, and गर्भ embryo; taking or producing fire by friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निदीपक|वह्निदीपकः
वह्निदीपक m. (-कः) Safflower.<BR> E. वह्नि fire, and दीपक what shines like or<BR>resembles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निनामन्
वह्निनामन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Marking-nut plant.<BR>	 2. Lead-wort.<BR> E. वह्नि fire, and<BR>नामन् appellation; the synonyms of fire being equally applicable<BR>to those plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निभोग्य|वह्निभोग्यं
वह्निभोग्य n. (-ग्यं) Ghee or clarified butter.<BR> E. वह्नि fire, भोग्य to be consumed or enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निमन्थ|वह्निमन्थः
वह्निमन्थ m. (-न्थः) A tree, the wood of which is used to procure fire by<BR>attrition, (Premna spinosa.)<BR> E. वह्नि fire, and मन्थ churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निमारक|वह्निमारकं
वह्निमारक n. (-कं) Water.<BR> E. वह्नि fire, and मारक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निमित्र|वह्निमित्रः
वह्निमित्र m. (-त्रः) Air, wind.<BR> E. वह्नि fire, and मित्र the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निरेतस्
वह्निरेतस् m. (-ताः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. वह्नि fire, रेतस् semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निलोह
वह्निलोह n. (-हं) Copper.<BR> E. वह्नि and लोह iron; also with कन् added वह्निलोहक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निवधू
वह्निवधू f. (-धूः) The wife of AGNI or fire.<BR> E. वह्नि and वधू the wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निवर्ण|वह्निवर्णं
वह्निवर्ण n. (-र्णं) The red water-lily.<BR> E. वह्नि fire, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निवल्लभ|वह्निवल्लभः
वह्निवल्लभ m. (-भः) Resin.<BR> E. वह्नि fire, and वल्लभ friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निवीज
वह्निवीज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. The common lime.<BR>	 3. A particle, to be<BR>repeated as the peculiar prayer of fire in the Tantra system:<BR>the syllable “रं”.<BR> E. वह्नि fire, वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निशिख|वह्निशिखं
वह्निशिख n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. Safflower, (Carthamus tinctorius.)<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-खा) A potherb, (Echites dichotoma.)<BR> E. वह्नि fire, and शिखा crest;<BR>also अग्निशिखा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निशिखर|वह्निशिखरः
वह्निशिखर m. (-रः) A flower, coxcomb, (Celosia cristata.)<BR> E. वह्नि fire, and शिखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्निसख|वह्निसखः
वह्निसख m. (-खः) The wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वह्य|वह्यं
वह्य n. (-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. A vehicle, a conveyance of any sort.<BR>	 2. A cart.<BR>	 f. (-ह्या)<BR>The wife of a Muni or saint.<BR> E. वह् to bear, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
वा r. 2nd cl. (वाति)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To blow, (as the wind.) With<BR>निर् prefixed, 1. To blow out, to extinguish.<BR>	 2. To cool.<BR>	 3.<BR>To hurt, to injure. Caus. (वापयति-ते) To cause to blow; also<BR>(वाजयति-ते) To shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
वा Ind. A particle of,:--1. Comparison, (as, like, so;)<BR>	 2. Alternative or-<BR>option, (or, either, else, sometimes.)<BR>	 3. Doubt and consideration,<BR>(or, whether.)<BR>	 4. Exception, (only, no other;)<BR>	 5. Asseveration or<BR>confirmation, (indeed, even, very.)<BR>	 6. A conjunction, (and,<BR>as well, also.)<BR>	 7. An expletive.<BR> E. वा to go, aff. क्विप्, the व is some-<BR>times changed to ब, and the word is read बा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांश|वांशः
वांश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Bamboo, of or belonging to, made from a bamboo,<BR>&c.<BR>	 f. (-शी) The manna of the bamboo.<BR> E. वंश a bamboo, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांशिक|वांशिकः
वांशिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A flute-player, a piper, a fifer.<BR>	 2. A bamboo-cutter,<BR>&c.<BR> E. वश a pipe, aff. ठक् or ठन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाःकिटि|वाःकिटिः
वाःकिटि m. (-टिः) A porpoise.<BR> E. वार् water, and किटि a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाःपुष्प
वाःपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) Cloves.<BR> E. वार् water, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाःसदन|वाःसदनं
वाःसदन n. (-नं) A large water-jar.<BR> E. वार् water, सदन abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक|वाकं|वाकः
वाक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging or relating to a crane.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A flight<BR>of cranes.<BR> E. वक, and अण्, अञ् or घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकुची
वाकुची f. (-ची) A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR> E. वा wind, and कुच्<BR>to contract, क aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्वलह
वाक्वलह n. (-हं) Quarrel, dispute.<BR> E. वाच् and कलह disturbance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्कीर|वाक्कीरः
वाक्कीर m. (-रः) A wife's brother.<BR> E. वाच् a speech, a phrase, and कीर<BR>parrot: having giving rise to a proverb; as a cock parrot is, so<BR>is the hen; i. e. of the same breed and disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्चपल
वाक्चपल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Frivolous, inconsistent, (in speech.)<BR> E. वाक्,<BR>चपल changeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्चापल्य
वाक्चापल्य n. (-ल्यं) Gossiping, chattering idle or improper talk.<BR> E. वाक्<BR>speech, चापल्य unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्छल|वाक्छलं
वाक्छल n. (-लं) Prevarication, equivocation.<BR> E. वाक् speech, छल disguise, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्छलान्वित
वाक्छलान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Equivocating, evasive.<BR> E. वाक्छल, and अन्वित<BR>possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पटु
वाक्पटु mfn. (-टुः-टुः-टु) Eloquent, able in speech.<BR> E. वाक्, and पटु skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पटुता
वाक्पटुता f. (-ता) Eloquence.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; with त्व, वाक्पटुत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पति|वाक्पतिः
वाक्पति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Eloquent.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) A name of VRIHASPATĪ.<BR>E. वाक् speech, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकपथ
वाकपथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Suitable or seasonable for discourse.<BR> E. वाक्, and पथ path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पारुष्य|वाक्पारुष्यं
वाक्पारुष्य n. (-ष्यं) Abuse, scurrility, defamation, wordy violence or<BR>assault.<BR> E. वाक् speech, पारुष्य violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्य|वाक्यं
वाक्य n. (-क्यं)<BR>	 1. A sentence.<BR>	 2. A rule or aphorism.<BR>	 3. Speech.<BR>	 4. (In<BR>astronomy,) The solar process for all astronomical computations.<BR>E. वच् to speak, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यखण्डन|वाक्यखंडन
वाक्यखण्डन n. (-नं) Refuting or criticising an assertion.<BR> E. वाक्य and खण्डन breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यप्रबन्ध|वाक्यप्रबंध|वाक्यप्रबन्धः
वाक्यप्रबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Connected composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यप्रयोग|वाक्यप्रयोगः
वाक्यप्रयोग m. (-गः) Employment or application of speech or language.<BR>E. वाक्य, प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यविन्यास|वाक्यविन्यासः
वाक्यविन्यास m. (-सः) Syntax, order, or arrangement of a sentence. E.<BR>वाक्य, विन्यास disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यविशारद
वाक्यविशारद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Eloquent.<BR> E. वाक्य and विशारद skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यशेष|वाक्यशेषः
वाक्यशेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The remainder of a speech.<BR>	 2. An ellipsis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यस्थ
वाक्यस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Contained in a sentence.<BR>	 2. Obedient, atten-<BR>tive.<BR> E. वाक्य and स्थ what stays; also वाक्यस्थित &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्ष्
वाक्ष्(इ)वाक्षि r. 10th cl. (वाङ्क्षति) To desire, to wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागपहारक|वागपहारकः
वागपहारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A stealer of books.<BR>	 2. A reader of prohibited<BR>works or passages.<BR> E. वाक् speech, अपहारक seizer, stealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागर|वागरः
वागर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A sage, a holy man, one desirous of final emancipa-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. A scholar, a Paṇḍit, a learned Brāhman.<BR>	 3. A hero, a<BR>brave man one who is intrepid or fearless.<BR>	 4. Certainty, ascer-<BR>tainment.<BR>	 5. A whet-stone.<BR>	 6. An obstacle, an impediment, or<BR>cause of obstruction.<BR>	 7. Submarine fire.<BR>	 8. A wolf.<BR> E. वाक् speech,<BR>ऋ to go, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागसि|वागसिः
वागसि f. (-सिः) Sharp or piercing speech.<BR> E. वाच्, असि a sword, piercing men's thoughts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागा
वागा f. (-गा) A bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागारु|वागारुः
वागारु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु) Breaking promise or faith, disappointing, a<BR>disappointer or deceiver.<BR> E. वाक् speech, ऋ to go, उण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागीश|वागीशः
वागीश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Eloquent, well spoken.<BR>	 m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. An author,<BR>an orator, a poet, &c.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. वाक् speech, ईश master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागीश्वर|वागीश्वरः
वागीश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An orator, a learned man.<BR>	 2. A Bauddha deified<BR>sage; also MANJUGHOSHA.<BR>	 3. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 f. (-री) SARASWATĪ. E.<BR>वाक् speech, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुजी
वागुजी f. (-जी) A plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR> E. वाच् speech, गुज्<BR>to sound inarticulately, aff. क, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुण|वागुणः
वागुण m. (-णः) An acid fruit, (Averrhoa carambola.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरा
वागुरा f. (-रा) A net, a snare, a noose.<BR> E. वा to hurt, उरच् Unādi aff., गन् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरावृत्ति|वागुरावृत्तिः
वागुरावृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Livelihood obtained by catching wild animals. E.<BR>वागुरा a snare, वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरिक|वागुरिकः
वागुरिक m. (-कः) A hunter, a deer-catcher.<BR> E. वागुरा a net, aff. ठक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागृषभ|वागृषभः
वागृषभ m. (-भः) A learned or eloquent man.<BR> E. वाच्, and ऋषभ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागृषभत्व
वागृषभत्व n. (-त्वं) Eloquence, learning, erudition.<BR> E. वागृषभ, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुद|वाग्गुदः
वाग्गुद m. (-दः) A sort of bird.<BR> E. वाक् speech, गुद् to sport, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुलि|वाग्गुलिः
वाग्गुलि m. (-लिः) The betel-bearer, an officer or servant whose business<BR>it is to have the box of Pān ready for his prince or master.<BR> E. वाक्<BR>speech, (command,) गुर् to obey, कि aff., and र changed to ल; or गृ<BR>to swallow, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुलिक|वाग्गुलिकः
वाग्गुलिक m. (-कः) A betel-bearer.<BR> E. ठक् pleonasm added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्डम्बर|वाग्डंबर|वाग्डम्बरः
वाग्डम्बर m. (-रः) Graceful or eloquent language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दण्ड|वाग्दंड|वाग्दण्डः
वाग्दण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. Reproof, reprimand.<BR>	 2. Restraint or control of<BR>speech.<BR> E. वाक् and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दत्त
वाग्दत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Promised.<BR>	 f. (-त्ता) A virgin betrothed.<BR> E. वाच्, दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दरिद्र|वाग्दरिद्रः
वाग्दरिद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं) Of few words, speaking little and humbly or<BR>guardedly.<BR> E. वाक speech, दरिद्र poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दल|वाग्दलं
वाग्दल n. (-लं) A lip.<BR> E. वाक् speech, दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दुष्ट|वाग्दुष्टः
वाग्दुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Abusive, ill-spoken, speaking ill, either morally<BR>or grammatically.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः) A Brāhman who has past the proper<BR>time of life, without receiving the initiatory Mantra, the investi-<BR>ture of the thread, &c.<BR> E. वाक् speech, दुष्ट bad, faulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्देवता
वाग्देवता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. VRIHASPATĪ.<BR>	 2. An eloquent man or writer.<BR> E. वाच्<BR>देवता divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्देवी
वाग्देवी f. (-वी) A name of SARASWATĪ.<BR> E. वाक् speech, and देवी goddess, the goddess of eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दोष|वाग्दोषः
वाग्दोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Speaking ill, defamation, abuse.<BR>	 2. Ungrammatical<BR>speech.<BR>	 3. Uttering a disagreeable sound.<BR> E. वाक् and दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्मात्र
वाग्मात्र n. (-त्रं) Mere speech, words alone.<BR> E. वाच् and मात्र only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्वन्धन
वाग्वन्धन n. (-नं) Stopping any one's speech.<BR> E. वाक्, वन्धन obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्मिन्
वाग्मिन् mfn. (-ग्मी-ग्मिनी-ग्मि)<BR>	 1. Loquacious, talkative, speaking much.<BR>2. Speaking well, eloquent.<BR>	 m. (-ग्मी) A name of VRIHASPATĪ. E.<BR>वाच् speech, ग्मिनि aff.; hence also वागिमन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्मूल
वाग्मूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Having root or origin in speech.<BR> E. वाच् and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्य|वाग्यः
वाग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं)<BR>	 1. Speaking little, and cautiously or humbly.<BR>	 2.<BR>Speaking truly.<BR>	 m. (-ग्यः)<BR>	 1. Humility, self-disparagement.<BR>	 2.<BR>Doubt, alternative.<BR> E. वाच् speech, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्यत|वाग्यतः
वाग्यत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reserved in speech, taciturn, silent.<BR> E. वाक्, यत् restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्यतस्
वाग्यतस् Ind. Silently.<BR> E. वाग्य speaking little, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्याम|वाग्यामः
वाग्याम m. (-मः) A dumb man, one silent from necessity.<BR> E. वाच् speech,<BR>यम् to restrain, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विनिःसृत
वाग्विनिःसृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Emitted or put forth by speech.<BR> E. वाच् and विनिःसृत issued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विलास|वाग्विलासः
वाग्विलास m. (-सः) Graceful or elegant speech.<BR> E. वाक् and विलास sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्व्यापार|वाग्व्यापारः
वाग्व्यापार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Manner, style or habit of speaking.<BR>	 2. Customary<BR>phraseology.<BR> E. वाक् and व्यापार usual practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्क|वांक|वांकः|वाङ्कः
वाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) The ocean, the sea.<BR> E. वङ्क a bend or creek, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मय|वाङ्मयं
वाङ्मय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Eloquent, rhetorical.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Eloquence.<BR>2. Rhetorical composition, rhetoric, belles lettres.<BR>	 f. (-यी) SARAS-<BR>WATĪ.<BR> E. वाक् speech, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मुख|वाङ्मुखं
वाङ्मुख m. (-खः) The opening of a speech, an exordium.<BR> E. वाच् speech, मुख beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्
वाच् f. (-वाक्)<BR>	 1. Speech.<BR>	 2. Speaking.<BR>	 3. SARASWATĪ, the goddess of<BR>speech.<BR>	 4. A phrase, a proverb or adage.<BR>	 5. An assertion, an<BR>assurance.<BR> E. वच् speak, aff. क्विप, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच|वाचं|वाचः
वाच m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. A plant: see मदन । 2. A kind of fish. “वाचा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचयम
वाचयम m. (-मः) A holy sage, practising rigid taciturnity, devoid of<BR>passions, and unmoved by pain or pleasure.<BR> E. वाच् speech, यम्<BR>to restrain, aff. खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचक|वाचकः
वाचक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Declaratory, explaining, speaking.<BR>	 2. Verbal,<BR>expressed by words.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A word, a significant sound.<BR>	 2.<BR>A speaker.<BR>	 3. A reader.<BR>	 4. A messenger.<BR> E. वच् to speak, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचकता
वाचकता f. (-ता) Expressiveness, significance.<BR> E. वाचक and तल् aff.;<BR>also with त्व, वाचकत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचकपद
वाचकपद n. (-दं) A clear and explicit term.<BR> E. वाचक and पद a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचन|वाचनं
वाचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Reading, reciting.<BR>	 2. Proclamation, declaration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचनक|वाचनकं
वाचनक n. (-कं) A riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचनीक
वाचनीक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Verbal.<BR>	 2. Textual.<BR> E. वचन and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचसाम्पति|वाचसांपति|वाचसाम्पतिः
वाचसाम्पति f. (-तिः) VRIHASPATĪ, regent of the planet JUPITER, and<BR>preceptor of the gods.<BR> E. वाच् speech, in the second case plural<BR>and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचस्पति|वाचस्पतिः
वाचस्पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. VRIHASPATĪ: see the last.<BR>	 2. A title of the great<BR>scholar Professor TĀRĀ-NĀTHA TARKA-BĀCHASPATĪ, son of the<BR>illustrious Pandit KĀLI-DĀSA SĀRBABHOUMA and grandson of the<BR>Venerable Pandit RĀM-RĀM TARKASIDDHĀNTA, the commentator<BR>of the six different schools of Hindu philosophy: (Vide Mr.<BR>ADAM'S report on the researches of the Pandits of Bengal.)<BR>He was born at KĀLNĀ, situated on the bank of the river<BR>BHĀGIRATHĪ, in the District of BURDWĀN in the year 1806<BR>A. D. and died at the sacred city of BENARES in 1885, at the<BR>ripe age of eighty, where he retired for abstract meditation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">Page641-a+ 60</a>]<BR>and contemplation of the Supreme Spirit. He is the commentator<BR>“of SĀNKHYA-TATWA-KOUMUDĪ,” of BĀCHASPATĪ MISHRA,<BR>“SIDDHĀNTA-KOUMUDĪ,” the most authoritative grammar of<BR>PĀNINĪ methodised by BHATTOJI-DIKSHITA, and several Sanskrit<BR>dramas; he is also the author of “SHABDĀRTHARATNA”, a useful<BR>work on the philosophy of grammar, “SIDDHĀNTABINDUSĀRA,” &c.;<BR>he is also the compiler of “ĀSHUBODH,” the well known Sanskrit<BR>grammar, “DHĀTURUPA,” the easy treatise on the paradigm of<BR>Sanskrit conjugations, both meant for beginners, “VĀCHASPATYA,”<BR>the first voluminous Sanskrit dictionary with derivations in al-<BR>phabetical order and “SHABDASTOMA-MAHĀNIDHĪ”, the most useful<BR>handy Sanskrit dictionary, and other works in almost all the bran-<BR>ches of Sanskrit language too numerous to mention, all of which he<BR>wrote single-handed.<BR> E. वाच् speech, in the sixth case, पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचस्पत्य|वाचस्पत्यं
वाचस्पत्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. The great encyclopædic Sanskrit lexicon by Prof.<BR>TĀRĀNĀTHA TARKAVĀCHASPATĪ, the most profoundest gram-<BR>marian and philosopher of the nineteenth century: see the last.<BR>	 2.<BR>Eloquence, an eloquent speech, a harangue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचा
वाचा f. (-चा)<BR>	 1. Speech.<BR>	 2. A text, an aphorism.<BR>	 3. The tongue.<BR>	 4. An<BR>oath.<BR> E. वाच् as above, टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचाट|वाचाटः
वाचाट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Talkative, talking much and idly or blamably.<BR>E. वाच् speech and आटच् aff. भत्वात् न कः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचाल|वाचालः
वाचाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Talkative, chattering, gabbling, talking much<BR>and idly or blamably.<BR> E. वाच् speech, and आलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिक|वाचिकं|वाचिकः
वाचिक mfn. (-कः-का or की-कं) Verbal.<BR>	 n. (-कं) News, tidings, intelli-<BR>gence.<BR> E. वाच् speech, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिकपत्रक
वाचिकपत्रक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A letter, a despatch.<BR>	 2. A newspaper, a gazette.<BR> E. वाचिक news, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिकहारक|वाचिकहारकः
वाचिकहारक n. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A letter, an epistle.<BR>	 2. A messenger, a courier.<BR>E. वाचिक news, हृ to convey, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचोयुक्ति|वाचोयुक्तिः
वाचोयुक्ति mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति) Speaking much or well.<BR> E. वाच speech, in<BR>the sixth case, and युक्ति joining, fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचोयुक्तिपटु|वाचोयुक्तिपटुः
वाचोयुक्तिपटु mfn. (-टुः-टुः or -ट्वी-टु) Eloquent, speaking much or well. E.<BR>वाचोयुक्ति as above, and पटु skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्छ्|वाछ्
वाच्छ्(इ)वाच्छि r. 1st cl. (-वाञ्छति) To wish or desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्य|वाच्यं
वाच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>	 1. Vile, bad.<BR>	 2. Vile, contemptible, low, out-<BR>cast.<BR>	 3. Fit or proper to be spoken or said.<BR>	 4. Attributive adjec-<BR>tive, to be predicated of any thing.<BR>	 5. Declinable as an adjective,<BR>taking the three genders.<BR>	 6. Expressed, (as the meaning of a<BR>word.)<BR>	 n. (-च्यं) Blame, reviling.<BR>	 2. A predicate, that which may<BR>be said of anything.<BR>	 3. (In grammar.) The voice or mode of a<BR>verb; as, कर्त्तृवाच्यं the active voice, कर्म्मणिवाच्यं the passive voice.<BR>	 4.<BR>The expressed or conventional meaning of word, (opposed to<BR>लक्ष्य and व्यङ्ग्य ।)<BR> E. वच् to speak, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यचित्र
वाच्यचित्र n. (-त्रं) One of the two kinds of the third or lowest division<BR>of poetry consisting in a striking idea or conceit expressed in<BR>words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यता
वाच्यता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Infamy, ill repute.<BR>	 2. Blame, reproach.<BR>	 3. The qua-<BR>lity of that which may be said of any thing.<BR>	 4. Conjugation. E.<BR>तल् added to the preceding; also with त्व, वाच्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाज|वाजं|वाजः
वाज mn. (-जः-जं) A wing.<BR>	 m. (-जः) The feather of an arrow.<BR>	 2. Speed.<BR>3. Sound.<BR>	 4. A Muni.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>	 2.<BR>Water.<BR>	 3. A Mantra or prayer which concludes a sacrifice.<BR>	 4.<BR>Rice offered at a Śrāddha or obsequial ceremony.<BR>	 5. Rice in<BR>general.<BR>	 6. The acidulous mixture of ground meal and water left<BR>to ferment.<BR> E. वज् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजपेय|वाजपेयं|वाजपेयः
वाजपेय mn. (-यः-यं) A particular sacrifice.<BR> E. वाज the acetous fermen-<BR>tation of meal and water, and पेय to be drank, (by the gods.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजभोजिन्
वाजभोजिन् m. (-जी) A particular sacrifice: see the last.<BR> E. वाज sour<BR>gruel, भुज् to eat, aff. णिनि, and the radical vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजसनेयिन्
वाजसनेयिन् m. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A name of YĀJNYAVALKA, the founder of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">Page641-b+ 60</a>]<BR>white YAJURVEDA.<BR>	 2. A member of the sect of the VĀJASANEYINS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिगन्ध|वाजिगन्धः
वाजिगन्ध m. (-न्धः) The name of a plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR> E. वाजिन्<BR>a horse, and गन्ध smell; also वाजिगन्धक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिता
वाजिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The condition of having wings.<BR>	 2. The nature of a<BR>horse.<BR> E. वाजिन् a horse, &c., तल् aff.; also with त्व, वाजित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिदन्त|वाजिदन्तः
वाजिदन्त m. (-न्तः) A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda.)<BR> E. वाजि a horse, दन्त a<BR>tooth, to which the flower is compared; with कन् added वाजिदन्तक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिन्
वाजिन् m. (-जी)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. A bird.<BR>	 4. A plant<BR>(Justicia adhenatoda.)<BR>	 f. (-जिनी) A mare.<BR> E. वाज speed or a feather,<BR>&c., and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिन|वाजिनं
वाजिन n. (-नं) Curd of two milk whey, or the whey from which the<BR>curds have been separated.<BR> E. वज् to prepare, aff. इनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिपृष्ठ|वाजिपृष्ठः
वाजिपृष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) Globe amaranth.<BR> E. वाजि a horse, and पृष्ठ back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिभूमि|वाजिभूमिः
वाजिभूमि f. (-मिः) Place where horses are bred.<BR> E. वाजिन्, भूमि place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिशाला
वाजिशाला nf. (-लं-ला) A stable.<BR> E. वाजि a horse, शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजीकर
वाजीकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Aphrodisiac.<BR> E. वाजिन् a horse, कर what makes, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजीकरण|वाजीकरणं
वाजीकरण n. (-णं) Stimulus or excitement of amorous desires by<BR>aphrodisiacs, &c.<BR> E. वाजि a horse, करण making, and च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छत्
वाञ्छत् mfn. (-ञ्छन्-ञ्छन्ती-ञ्छत्) Wishing, desiring.<BR> E. वाछि to wish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छन|वांछन|वांछनं
वाञ्छन n. (-नं) Desiring, wishing.<BR> E. वाछि to desire, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छनीय
वाञ्छनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Desirable, to be wished for.<BR> E. वाछि to wish,<BR>and अनीयर् aff.; also वाञ्छितव्य and वाञ्छ्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छा|वांछा
वाञ्छा f. (-ञ्छा) Wish, desire.<BR> E. वाच्छि to wish, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छित|वांछित|वाञ्छितं
वाञ्छित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wished, desired.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Wish.<BR> E. वाच्छि to wish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छिन्|वांछिन्
वाञ्छिन् mfn. (-ञ्छी-ञ्छिनी-ञ्छि) Wishing, desirous.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्छिनी) A libidi-<BR>nous woman, a wanton.<BR> E. वाञ्छा desire, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्
वाट् Ind. An exclamation on making an offering of boiled butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट|वाटं|वाटः
वाट mfn. Adj. (-टः-टी-टं) Made of the Indian fig-tree, of its wood, &c.<BR>Subst. (-टः-टी-टं)<BR>	 1. An enclosure, a piece of enclosed ground, whe-<BR>ther a simple enclosure, as a courtyard, or one for trees and<BR>plants, as an orchard, a garden, a plantation, &c.<BR>	 2. A road.<BR>	 3.<BR>A mud wall, a bound hedge or any enclosure of a town or village,<BR>&c.<BR>	 4. A sort of grain, (Panicum spicatum.)<BR>	 5. The groin.<BR>	 f. (-टी)<BR>1. The site of a house or building.<BR>	 2. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 3. A<BR>plant: see वाट्यालक<BR> E. वट् to surround, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटधान|वाटधानः
वाटधान m. (-नः) The descendant of an outcast Brāhman by a Brāh-<BR>man female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटशृङ्खला
वाटशृङ्खला f. (-ला) A sort of chain enclosure or fence.<BR> E. वाट an enclosure, शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटिका
वाटिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The site of a house.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Sida cordifolia.)<BR>3. A garden, an orchard.<BR> E. कन् added to वाटी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटीदीर्घ|वाटीदीर्घः
वाटीदीर्घ m. (-र्घः) A sort of grass, commonly Itcada.<BR> E. वाटी an enclo-<BR>sure, दीर्घ long. “इत्कटक्षुपे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्टक|वाट्टकं
वाट्टक n. (-कं) Fried barley; also read वाट्यक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाठ्य
वाठ्य mfn. (-ट्यः-ट्या-ट्यं) Belonging to a house or garden, &c.<BR> E. वाटी, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्यपुष्प
वाट्यपुष्प n. (-ष्पं)<BR>	 1. Sandal.<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी) A plant, (Sida cordifo-<BR>lia.)<BR> E. वाट्य belonging to a house or garden, पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्या
वाट्या f. (-ट्या) A plant, (Sida cordifolia.)<BR> E. वाटी a garden, यत्, and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्याल|वाट्यालः
वाट्याल mf. (-लः-ला) A herbaceous shrub, (Sida cordifolia:) see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्यालक|वाट्यालकः
वाट्यालक m. (-कः) A plant, commonly Beriyālā, (Sida cordifolia.) E.<BR>वाटी a garden, in the sixth case, अल् to adorn, with अण् aff., and<BR>कन् added, the ornament of a garden. “वेलेडा इति भाषा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाड्
वाड्(ऋ)वाडृ r. 1st cl. (वाडते) To bathe, to dive and emerge: the best<BR>authorities read this बाडृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवेय|वाडवेयः
वाडवेय m. (-यः) A bull.<BR>	 m. DU. The two son's of Ashwinī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडव्य|वाडव्यं
वाडव्य n. (-व्यं) A multitude of Brāhmans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाढ
वाढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Much, abundant, exceeding.<BR>	 2. Hard, firm.<BR>Adv.<BR>	 n. or Ind. (-ढं)<BR>	 1. Much, excessive, excessively.<BR>	 2. Very well,<BR>well, (assent, promise.)<BR>	 3. A particle signifying conclusion, de-<BR>duction.<BR> E. वह् to take, to bear, aff. क्त; form. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाढविक्रम
वाढविक्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Powerful, very strong, mighty.<BR> E. वाढ, विक्रम prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाण|वाणः
वाण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. A name of fire.<BR>	 3. The name of a sover-<BR>eign considered also as an Asura or infernal being, the son o t<BR>BALI, father. of UṢĀ, destroyed by VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. The udder of a<BR>cow.<BR>	 5. Alone, solitary.<BR>	 6. A pipe, a fife, a flute.<BR>	 mf. (-णः-णा)<BR>	 1.<BR>Blue Barleria.<BR>	 2. The root or feathered part of an arrow.<BR> E. वण् or<BR>बण् to sound or go, aff. घञ्; whence this word and other deriva-<BR>tives are sometimes also written with an initial ब ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणदण्ड|वाणदण्डः
वाणदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A weaver's loom.<BR> E. वाण an arrow, दण्ड stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणनिकृत
वाणनिकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pierced, wounded by an arrow.<BR> E. वाण, निकृत hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणपाणि
वाणपाणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) Armed with arrows.<BR> E. वाण, पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणपुर|वाणपुरं
वाणपुर n. (-रं) The capital of VĀṆA Rājā.<BR> E. वाण and पुर city; also<BR>with the final consonant बाणपुर् f. (-पूः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणमोक्षण
वाणमोक्षण n. (-णं) Shooting an arrow.<BR> E. वाण and मोक्षण letting fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणवार|वाणवारः
वाणवार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Armour.<BR>	 2. A breastplate, a cuirass.<BR> E. वाण an<BR>arrow, वृ to cover or screen, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणसुता
वाणसुता f. (-ता) UṢĀ, the daughter of VĀṆA, and wife of ANIRUDDHA.<BR> E. वाण, सुता daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणहन्
वाणहन् m. (-हा) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. वाण VĀṆA Rājā and हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणारि|वाणारिः
वाणारि m. (-रिः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. वाण the demon, and अरि enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणाश्रय|वाणाश्रयः
वाणाश्रय m. (-यः) A bow.<BR> E. वाण an arrow, and आश्रय receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणासन|वाणासनं
वाणासन n. (-नं) A bow.<BR> E. वाण an arrow, असन throwing, or आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणि|वाणिः
वाणि f. (-णिः or णी)<BR>	 1. Weaving.<BR>	 2. A weaver's loom.<BR>	 3. A species of<BR>the Ashtī metre.<BR> E. वण् to sound, aff. इनि; ङीप् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिज्य|वाणिज्यं
वाणिज्य n. (-ज्यं) Traffic, trade: see बाणिज्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिन्
वाणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि)<BR>	 1. Having an arrow.<BR>	 2. Speaking.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1.<BR>A sharp or clever woman, an intriguing woman.<BR>	 2. An actress, a<BR>Naūtch girl.<BR>	 3. A furious woman, one literally or figuratively<BR>intoxicated.<BR> E. वाण an arrow, or वाणि speech, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणी
वाणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. SARASWATĪ, the goddess of speech.<BR>	 2. Speech, sound.<BR>3. Voice, (as दैववाणी).<BR>	 4. Eloquence.<BR>	 5. Praise.<BR>	 6. A literary pro-<BR>duction.<BR> E. वण् to sound, aff. इञ् and ङीप् or ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात|वातः
वात r. 10th cl. (वातयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To serve.<BR>	 3. To be happy.<BR>	 4. To<BR>give pleasure in travelling.<BR>	 5. To blow gently, to fan or ventilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्
वात् mfn. (-वान्-वाती or वान्ती-वात्) Going, moving.<BR> E. वा to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात|वातः
वात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. Rheumatism, gout, inflammation of the<BR>joints.<BR>	 3. Air, wind, as one of the three humours of the body.<BR>	 4.<BR>The deity that presides over wind.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Blown.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wished for, solicited.<BR> E. वा to go, Unādi aff. तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातक|वातकः
वातक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A paramour.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.) E.<BR>वात wind, कृ to make, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकर्मन्|वातकर्म्मन्
वातकर्मन् n. (-र्म) Breaking wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकिन्
वातकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Rheumatic, gouty.<BR> E. वात inflammation of<BR>the joints, and इनि aff., कुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकुण्डलिका|वातकुंडलिका
वातकुण्डलिका f. (-का) Scanty and painful flow of urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकुम्भ|वातकुंभ|वातकुम्भः
वातकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) The part of an elephant's forehead below the frontal<BR>sinuses.<BR> E. वात wind and कुम्भ a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकेतु|वातकेतुः
वातकेतु m. (-तुः) Dust.<BR> E. वात wind, and केतु a symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकेलि|वातकेलिः
वातकेलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. Speaking in murmurs, especially amorous con-<BR>verse.<BR>	 2. The marks of finger-nails on the lover's person.<BR> E. वात<BR>wind, केलि playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातगामिन्
वातगामिन् m. (-मी) A bird.<BR> E. वात wind, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातगुल्म|वातगुल्मः
वातगुल्म m. (-ल्मः)<BR>	 1. A gale, a high wind.<BR>	 2. Acute gout or rheuma-<BR>tism.<BR>	 3. Any disease arising from the morbid affection of the<BR>windy humour, such as, madness, the glandular enlargement of<BR>the mesenteric gland, in the abdomen, so as to be perceived ex-<BR>ternally, &c. according to our Hindu system of pathology.<BR> E. वात<BR>wind, गुल्म a cluster, a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातग्रस्त
वातग्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Epileptic.<BR>	 2. Rheumatic.<BR> E. वात and ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातघ्न
वातघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Removing disorders from wind.<BR> E. वात and घ्न<BR>who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातज
वातज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by or arising from wind.<BR> E. वात, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातज्वर|वातज्वरः
वातज्वर m. (-रः) Fever arising from vitiated wind.<BR> E. वात and ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाततूल|वाततूलं
वाततूल n. (-लं) Cottony flocks or seeds floating in the air.<BR> E. वात, तुला cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातथुडा
वातथुडा f. (-डा)<BR>	 1. A gale, a high wind.<BR>	 2. Acute gout or rheumatism.<BR>3. A handsome woman.<BR>	 4. A disease, a sort of small pox.<BR> E. वात<BR>wind, हुड् to reap, aff. क, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातध्वज|वातध्वजः
वातध्वज m. (-जः) A cloud.<BR> E. वात wind, and ध्वज banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातपित्त
वातपित्त n. (-त्तं) Rheumatism attended with fever.<BR> E. वात, पित्त bile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातपुत्त्र
वातपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. A name of BHĪMA.<BR>	 2. The monkey HANUMĀNA.<BR>	 3.<BR>A cheat, a swindler.<BR> E. वात the wind, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातपोथ|वातपोथः
वातपोथ m. (-थः) The Palāsha tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. वात rheuma-<BR>tism, पुथ् to hurt, aff. अण्; also वातपोथक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातप्रमी
वातप्रमी m. (-मीः) A swift antelope.<BR> E. वात the wind, प्र before, मा to<BR>measure, to surpass or outgo, Unādi aff. ईप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातफुल्ल
वातफुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं) Inflated, puffed up with wind.<BR> E. वात, फुल्ल blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातफुल्लान्त्र|वातफुल्लान्त्रं
वातफुल्लान्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) Colic, flatulence, borborygmi.<BR> E. वात wind, and फुल्ल<BR>swoln, अन्त्र the intestines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातमज|वातमजः
वातमज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Going in or against the wind.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A<BR>swift antelope.<BR> E. वात wind, अज् to go, aff. खश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातमण्डली|वातमंडली
वातमण्डली f. (-ली) A whirl-wind.<BR> E. वात wind, मण्डल a region, aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातमृग|वातमृगः
वातमृग m. (-गः) A swift antelope.<BR> E. वात wind, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरहस्
वातरहस् mfn. (-हाः-हाः-हः) Swift, (as the wind.)<BR> E. वात, रंहस् speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातर
वातर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Windy, stormy.<BR>	 2. Swift, (as the wind.)<BR> E. वात<BR>and रा to get, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरक्त|वातरक्तं
वातरक्त n. (-क्तं) Acute gout or rheumatism.<BR> E. वात wind, and रक्त blood;<BR>ascribed to a vitiated state of the blood and the aerial humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरक्तघ्न|वातरक्तघ्नः
वातरक्तघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A plant, commonly Kukurmurā.<BR> E. वातरक्त gout, and<BR>घ्न destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरक्तारि|वातरक्तारिः
वातरक्तारि m. (-रिः) A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR> E. वातरक्त acute gout, अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरङ्ग|वातरंग|वातरङ्गः
वातरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The holy fig-tree. वातस्येव सततं रङ्गश्चलनमस्य; also वादरङ्ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरथ|वातरथः
वातरथ m. (-थः) A cloud.<BR> E. वात the wind, and रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरायण|वातरायणः
वातरायण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. An arrow's flight, the discharge of<BR>an arrow, a bow shot.<BR>	 3. A saw.<BR>	 4. The peak of a mountain.<BR>	 5.<BR>A mad man, one wild or intoxicated, either literally or figura-<BR>tively.<BR>	 6. An idler, one who lives to no purpose.<BR>	 7. The Saral, a<BR>sort of pine tree.<BR> E. वातर and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरूष|वातरूषः
वातरूष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A gale, a breeze.<BR>	 2. The rainbow.<BR>	 5. A bribe.<BR> E. वात<BR>wind, रूष् to rage, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरोग|वातरोगः
वातरोग n. (-गं) Rheumatism, gout.<BR> E. वात wind, and रोग disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातरोगिन्
वातरोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Rheumatic, afflicted with gout or rheu-<BR>matism, especially of the acute kind.<BR> E. वातरोग acute rheumatism,<BR>&c., aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातर्द्धि
वातर्द्धि m. (-र्द्धिः)<BR>	 1. A sort of cup or vessel made of wood, with an<BR>iron foot or stand.<BR>	 2. A mace, a club or stick bound with iron.<BR>3. Excess of wind.<BR> E. वात wind, ऋद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातल|वातलः
वातल mfn. (-लः-ला or ली-लं)<BR>	 1. Windy, stormy.<BR>	 2. Flatulent.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>1. A sort of pulse, (Cicer arietinum.)<BR>	 2. Wind.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A morbid<BR>state of the uterus.<BR> E. वात wind, ला to get, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातलमण्डली
वातलमण्डली f. (-ली) A whirl-wind.<BR> E. वातल windy, मण्डल a region, aff.<BR>ङीप्; also वातमण्डली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातवत्|वातवन्त्
वातवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Windy, gusty.<BR> E. वात and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातवलासक
वातवलासक m. (-कः) Nervous or low fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातवस्ति|वातवस्तिः
वातवस्ति f. (-स्तिः) Suppression of urine.<BR> E. वात and वस्ति the bladder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातवृद्धि|वातवृद्धिः
वातवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Swelled testicle.<BR> E. वात, वृद्धि increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातवैरिन्
वातवैरिन् m. (-री) The castor-oil tree, &c.: see वातारि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातव्याधि|वातव्याधिः
वातव्याधि f. (-धिः) Any morbid affection attributed to disorder of the<BR>wind.<BR> E. वात and व्याधि disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातशीर्ष|वातशीर्षं
वातशीर्ष n. (-र्षं) The lower belly.<BR> E. वात wind, शीर्ष the head or source.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातशूल
वातशूल n. (-लं) Colic with flatulence.<BR> E. वात and शूल colic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातशोणित|वातशोणितं
वातशोणित n. (-तं) Acute gout or rheumatism.<BR> E. वात wind, शोणित blood;<BR>ascribed to a vitiated state of these two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=642-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातसह|वातसहः
वातसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Gouty, rheumatic.<BR> E. वात the disease, सह bear-<BR>ing, suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातसारथि|वातसारथिः
वातसारथि m. (-थिः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. वात wind, and सारथि charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातस्कन्ध|वातस्कन्धः
वातस्कन्ध n. (-न्धं) The portion of the atmosphere where the wind blows.<BR>E. वात wind, स्कन्ध part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताट|वाताटः
वाताट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A horse of the sun.<BR>	 2. An antelope.<BR> E. वात the wind, and अट who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताण्ड|वातांड|वाताण्डः
वाताण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A disease of the testicles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातातिसार|वातातिसारः
वातातिसार m. (-रः) Dysentery produced by some disorder in the wind of the stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताद|वातादः
वाताद m. (-दः) The almond, (Prunus amygdalus. Syn. Amygdalus<BR>cummunis. Terminalia catappa.)<BR> E. वात windy humour, अद् to des-<BR>troy, aff. घञ्; also वाताम । “वादाम् इति भाषा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातानुलोमन
वातानुलोमन n. (-नं) Forcing the wind in downwards, as in inflating the lungs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातापि|वातापिः
वातापि m. (-पिः) The name of an Asura devoured by AGASTYA.<BR> E. वात<BR>wind, पा to drink, aff. कि, and आङ् prefixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातापिद्विष्
वातापिद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) The Muni AGASTYA.<BR> E. वातापि and द्विष् who hates;<BR>also similar names, as वातापिसूदन, वातापिहन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातामोदा
वातामोदा f. (-दा) Musk.<BR> E. वात the wind, आमोदा a diffusive fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताय
वाताय n. (-यं) A leaf.<BR> E. वात wind, अय् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातायन|वातायनं|वातायनः
वातायन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A window, an eyelet or loophole.<BR>	 2. A porch, a<BR>portico, a covered shed, a pavilion.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A horse.<BR> E. वात the<BR>wind, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातायु|वातायुः
वातायु m. (-युः) An antelope, a deer.<BR> E. वात wind, (like,) अय् to go, aff. उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातारि|वातारिः
वातारि f. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. The castor-oil tree.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Asparagus racemo-<BR>sus.)<BR> E. वात rheumatism, अरि hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताली
वाताली f. (-ली) A whirl-wind, a gale.<BR> E. वात wind, आली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताश्व|वाताश्वः
वाताश्व m. (-श्वः) A swift horse, or one of a good breed.<BR> E. वात the wind,<BR>and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातासह|वातासहः
वातासह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Rheumatic, gouty.<BR> E. वात rheumatism, आसह who bears or suffers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताहत
वाताहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stirred or shaken by the wind.<BR>	 2. Affected<BR>by rheumatism.<BR> E. वात and आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताहति|वाताहतिः
वाताहति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The action of the wind.<BR>	 2. The occurance of<BR>arthritic pains.<BR> E. वात and आहति striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाति|वातिः
वाति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. Air, wind.<BR> E. वा to go, Unādi aff. क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातिक|वातिकः
वातिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Windy, stormy.<BR>	 2. Rheumatic.<BR>	 3. Produced<BR>by or proceeding from wind, (disease, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-कः) Fever or<BR>inflammation ascribed to a vitiated state of the aerial humour. E.<BR>वात wind, &c., ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातिग|वातिगः
वातिग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Acquainted with or working in minerals or<BR>fossils, &c.<BR>	 m. (-गः) The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR> E. वाति<BR>wind, ग who counts, from गण with ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातिङ्गण|वातिंगण|वातिङ्गणः
वातिङ्गण m. (-णः) The egg-plant.<BR> E. वाति wind, गण् to count, aff. खच्,<BR>curing rheumatism, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातीय|वातीयं
वातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Windy, relating or belonging to wind, &c.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-यं) Sour rice-gruel.<BR> E. वात the wind, छ aff.; acidulated by air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातुल|वातुलः
वातुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Gouty, rheumatic.<BR>	 2. Mad, crazy.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>A whirlwind, a gale.<BR> E. वात wind, &c., and उलच् aff.; more com-<BR>monly वातूल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातुलि|वातुलिः
वातुलि f. (-लिः) A large bat, commonly the flying fox.<BR> E. वात wind, उलि aff., form irr. “वादुड ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातूल|वातूलः
वातूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Gouty, rheumatic.<BR>	 2. Mad, insane, inebriate.<BR>m. (-लः) A whirlwind, a gale, a hurricane.<BR> E. वात wind, ऊलच् aff.;<BR>also वातुल; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातृ
वातृ m. (-ता) Air, wind.<BR> E. वा to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्या
वात्या f. (-त्या) A gale, a whirlwind, a hurricane.<BR> E. वात wind, यत् implying quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सक|वात्सकं
वात्सक n. (-कं) A herd of calves.<BR> E. वत्स a calf, बुञ् aff. of number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सल्य|वात्सल्यं|वात्सल्यः
वात्सल्य n. (-ल्यं) Tenderness, affection, fondness.<BR> E. वत्सल affectionate,<BR>ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्सीपुत्त्र
वात्सीपुत्त्र m. (-त्तः) A barber.<BR> E. वात्सी a girl born of a Śūdra woman by a Brāhman, and पुत्त्र son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्स्यायन|वात्स्यायनः
वात्स्यायन m. (-नः) The name of a Muni.<BR> E. वात्स्य the father of the sage,<BR>and फक् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद|वादः
वाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Demonstrated conclusion, reply, result.<BR>	 2. Discourse,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">Page643-b+ 60</a>]<BR>discussion, defined as the speech of one desirous to know the<BR>truth.<BR>	 3. A plaint, an accusation.<BR>	 4. Sound, sounding.<BR>	 5. Rumour,<BR>report.<BR> E. वद् to speak, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादकर
वादकर mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं) Causing or making a dispute.<BR> E. वाद, कर<BR>what makes; also वादकृत् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादग्रस्त
वादग्रस्त Adj. In dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादचञ्चु|वादचंचु
वादचञ्चु Adj. Clever in repartee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादन|वादनं|वादनः
वादन n. (-नं) Sound, sounding, (as musical instruments.)<BR> E. वद् to sound,<BR>causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादयत्
वादयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Sounding, playing, (as on a musical instru-<BR>ment.)<BR> E. वद् to speak, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादयुद्ध
वादयुद्ध n. (-द्धं) Controversy, dispute.<BR> E. वाद, and युद्ध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादर|वादरं|वादरः
वादर f. (-री) Made of cotton.<BR>	 n. (-र) Cotton cloth.<BR> E. वदर cotton, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादरङ्ग|वादरंग|वादरंगः|वादरङ्गः
वादरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The religious fig-tree: see वातरङ्ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादरत
वादरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Adhering to or following a doctrine.<BR>	 2.<BR>Addicted to controversy, disputations.<BR> E. वाद, and रत fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादरा
वादरा f. (-रा) The cotton-shrub. “कापास तूला ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादरायण|वादरायणः
वादरायण m. (-णः) A name of VYĀSA, the compiler of the Vedas, and<BR>reputed author of the Purāṇas, &c.<BR> E. वादर a place of pilgrimage<BR>अयन going, aff. अण्; also written with an initial ब, बादरायण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादल|वादलं|वादलः
वादल n. (-लं) Liquorice, or the root of the Abrus precatorius, which is<BR>used for it.<BR> E. वा for वात wind, दल् to disperse, aff. अच्; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादवादिन्
वादवादिन् m. (-दी) A Jaina.<BR> E. वाद result, truth, वादिन् who declares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादसाधन
वादसाधन n. (-नं) Argument, maintaining a controversy.<BR> E. वाद and<BR>साधन instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादानुवाद
वादानुवाद m. (-दः) Attack and rejoinder, plaint and reply.<BR> E. वाद, अनुवाद<BR>subsequent dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादान्य|वादान्यः
वादान्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Munificent, liberal, &c.<BR> E. वदान्य, and अण् pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादाल|वादालः
वादाल m. (-लः) A sheat-fish.<BR> E. वदाल the same, अण् pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादि|वादिः
वादि mfn. (-दिः-दिः-दि) Wise, learned, skilful, sage.<BR> E. वद् to speak,<BR>(wisely, &c.,) इन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादित
वादित f. (-ता) Played, sounded.<BR>	 2. Made to speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादित्र|वादित्रं
वादित्र n. (-त्रं) A musical instrument.<BR> E. वद् to sound, Unādi aff. णित्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादिन्
वादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Speaking, discoursing.<BR>	 2. Asserting, de-<BR>claring.<BR>	 m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A sage, an expounder of the law and the Shās-<BR>tras.<BR>	 2. A plaintiff, an accuser.<BR>	 3. Leading or key note, (in music.)<BR>4. A disputant.<BR>	 5. A speaker.<BR> E. वद् to speak, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादिराज्
वादिराज् m. (-राट्) A Bauddha sage; also MANJUGHOSA.<BR> E. वादि a sage,<BR>राज् chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वादिश|वादिशः
वादिश m. (-शः) A learned and virtuous man, a sage, a seer.<BR> E. वादि<BR>truth or true conclusion, इशच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद्य|वाद्यं|वाद्यः
वाद्य n. (-द्यं) Any musical instrument.<BR> E. वद् to sound, aff. ण्यत्; to be sounded or played.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद्यकर|वाद्यकरः
वाद्यकर m. (-रः) A musician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद्यनिर्घोष
वाद्यनिर्घोष m. (-षः) The sound of musical instruments.<BR> E. वाद्य a musical<BR>instrument, and निर्घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाद्यभाण्ड|वाद्यभांड|वाद्यभाण्डं
वाद्यभाण्ड n. (-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. A multitude of musical instruments, a band.<BR>	 2.<BR>Any musical instrument.<BR> E. वाद्य a musical instrument, and भाण्ड<BR>assemblage or vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाध्
वाध्(ऋ)वाधृ r. 1st cl. (वाधते) To distress, to give pain: more correctly बाध् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाध|वाधः
वाध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Pain.<BR>	 2. Annoyance: see बाध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधुक्य|वाधुक्यं
वाधुक्य n. (-क्यं) Marriage.<BR> E. वधुका a wife, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाधू
वाधू f. (-धूः) A vessel, a boat, a raft.<BR> E. वह् to bear, aff. ऊण्; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ध्रीणस|वार्द्ध्रीणसः|वार्ध्रीणसः
वार्ध्रीणस m. (-सः) A rhinoceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान|वानं|वानः
वान mfn. Subst. (-नः-ना-नं) Dry fruit. Adj. Dry, dried.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Living.<BR>2. Going, moving.<BR>	 3. A mat of straw.<BR>	 4. A heavy sea, the rolling<BR>of water from wind, &c.; hence the high tide in the Indian rivers,<BR>commonly called the Bore.<BR>	 5. A hole in the wall of a house.<BR>	 6.<BR>A perfume, a fragrance.<BR>	 7. Weaving.<BR>	 8. Blowing.<BR>	 mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>Relating to a wood, a house, &c.: see वन.<BR>	 n. (-नं) A number<BR>or multitude of woods.<BR> E. वै to dry or wither, aff. क्त, form irr.:<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">Page644-a+ 60</a>]<BR>in other of its applications, वन् to sound, aff. घञ्; or वन a wood,<BR>water, a house, &c., and अण् referential aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=643-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानप्रस्थ|वानप्रस्थः
वानप्रस्थ m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. The Brāhmana of the third order, who has passed<BR>through the conditions of student and householder, and has left<BR>his house and family for lonely meditation in woods and wilds;<BR>the hermit, the anchoret.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Bassia latifolia.)<BR>	 3. The<BR>Palāsha-tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. वन a wood, अण् aff., वान a soli-<BR>tude in the woods, &c., प्रस्थ who goes forth to, from स्था to stay,<BR>with प्र prefix, and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानर|वानरः
वानर mf. (-रः-री) An ape, a monkey.<BR>	 f. (-री) Cowach, (Carpopogon<BR>pruriens.)<BR> E. वान what relates to a wood, रा to get, aff. क, a Sylvan;<BR>or वा implying resemblance, and नर a man; or वन a wood, रस् to<BR>play, aff. ड, वनर, and अण् pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानरप्रिय|वानरप्रियः
वानरप्रिय m. (-यः) A tree, (Mimusops kauki, Rox.)<BR> E. वानर a monkey, प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानराघात|वानराघातः
वानराघात m. (-तः) A tree, commonly Lodh, (Symplocos racemosa.) E.<BR>वानर a monkey, आघात struck, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानरेन्द्र|वानरेंद्र|वानरेन्द्रः
वानरेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः)<BR>	 1. The monkey-chief SUGRĪVA.<BR>	 2. HANUMĀNA.<BR> E. वानर, इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानल|वानलः
वानल m. (-लः) A kind of holy basil, distinguished as the black species<BR>of Tulasī, (Ocymum sanctum.) “काल वावुइ तुलसी ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानस्पत्य|वानस्पत्यः
वानस्पत्य m. (-त्यः) A tree bearing fruits from blossoms, as the mango,<BR>eugenia, &c.<BR> E. वनस्पति a tree, bearing fruits without blossoms,<BR>and ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानायु|वानायुः
वानायु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. A country to the north-west of India; see वनायु । 2. An antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानायुज|वानायुजः
वानायुज m. (-जः) A Vānāyu horse, considered as one of a particularly<BR>good breed.<BR> E. वनायु and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीर|वानीरः
वानीर m. (-रः) A sort of cane or ratan, (Calamus rotang.)<BR> E. वन water,<BR>ईरन् aff., and the first vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानेय|वानेयं
वानेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Relating or belonging to water, &c.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A<BR>fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. वन water, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्त|वांत|वान्तः
वान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Vomited, ejected from the mouth.<BR> E. वम् to<BR>vomit, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्ताद|वांताद|वान्तादः
वान्ताद m. (-दः) A dog.<BR> E. वान्त what is ejected from the mouth, and अद<BR>who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्ति|वांति|वान्तिः
वान्ति m. (-न्तिः) Vomiting, ejecting from the mouth.<BR> E. वम् to vomit, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्तिकृत्
वान्तिकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Emetic.<BR>	 m. (-कृत्) A thorny plant, (Vangueria spi-<BR>nosa.)<BR> E. वान्ति vomiting, and कृत् what makes; an emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्तिद
वान्तिद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Emetic.<BR>	 f. (-दा) A medicinal plant, commonly<BR>Katukī, (Wrightea antidysenterica; and Colotropis gigantea,<BR>BROWN.)<BR> E. वान्ति vomiting, and द what produces; an emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्या
वान्या f. (-न्या) A multitude of groves or thickets.<BR> E. वन a wood, यञ् aff.<BR>of multitude; also with यत् aff. वन्या ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाप|वापः
वाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Shaving.<BR>	 2. Sowing seed.<BR>	 3. Weaving.<BR> E. वप् to sow<BR>seed, &c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाप|वापः
वाप(य)दण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A weaver's loom.<BR> E. वाप or वाय weaving, दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापि|वापिः
वापि f. (-पिः or पी) A large oblong pond, a pool, a lake.<BR> E. वाप् to sow<BR>seed, (of the lotus, &c.) Unādi aff. इञ् and ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापित|वापितं
वापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sown as seed.<BR>	 2. Shaven.<BR> E. वाप shaving, &c.,<BR>इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापीह|वापीहः
वापीह m. (-हः) The Chātaka, a bird, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR> E. वापी<BR>a pool, हा to abandon, aff. क; drinking rain water only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाप्य|वाप्यं
वाप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be sown, what may or ought to be sown.<BR>m. (-प्यः) A sort of costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR> E. वप् to sow, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाम|वामं|वामः
वाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Left, not right.<BR>	 2. Reverse, contrary, inverted.<BR>3. Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>	 4. Vile, base, wicked.<BR>	 5. Short.<BR>	 6. Crooked.<BR>m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>	 3. An udder,<BR>a breast.<BR>	 4. A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR>	 5. An animal, a<BR>sentient being.<BR>	 6. A snake.<BR>	 n. (-मं) Wealth, possessions.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>1. A woman.<BR>	 2. Gourī.<BR>	 3. LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 4. SARASWATĪ.<BR>	 f. (-मी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>mare.<BR>	 2. A she-ass.<BR>	 3. A young female elephant.<BR>	 4. The female of<BR>the jackal.<BR> E. वा to go, Unādi aff. मन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामता
वामता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Perverseness, contrariety.<BR>	 2. Craftiness, wickedness.<BR>3. Loveliness.<BR> E. तल् added to वाम; also with त्व, वामत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामदेव|वामदेवः
वामदेव m. (-वः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. वाम contrary, (to human institu-<BR>tions,) देव who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामन|वामनः
वामन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Short, dwarfish, a dwarf.<BR>	 2. Depressed, pressed<BR>flat or down.<BR>	 3. Low, vile, base.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU in his charac-<BR>ter of the dwarf, in which he appeared on his fifth descent from<BR>heaven, to prevent BALĪ from obtaining dominion of the three<BR>worlds.<BR>	 2. The elephant that supports the south quarter.<BR>	 3. A<BR>tree, (Alangium hexapetalum.)<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A female dwarf.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of woman; also वामनिका । 3. A disease of the vagina.<BR>	 4. A<BR>mare.<BR> E. वम् to eject from the mouth, and ल्यु or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनीकृत
वामनीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shortened, flattened.<BR> E. वामन, कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामलूर|वामलूरः
वामलूर m. (-रः) An ant or mole hill, especially the hillocks of ground<BR>thrown up by the white ant.<BR> E. वाम inverted, reversed, लू to cut,<BR>aff. रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामलोचन
वामलोचन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fine-eyed.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A handsome woman.<BR> E. वाम beautiful, लोचन eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामशील|वामशीलः
वामशील m. (-लः) An epithet of KĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामाक्षी
वामाक्षी f. (-क्षी) A handsome woman.<BR> E. वाम beautiful, and अक्षि an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामाचार|वामाचारः
वामाचार m. (-रः) The doctrine of the Tantras according to one system.<BR>E. वाम left, and आचार institute; the left hand ritual, the use of<BR>flesh, spirits, &c., forming part of the Vāmācāra ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामाचारिन्
वामाचारिन् m. (-री) A follower of the left hand portion of the Tantras.<BR>E. वामाचार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामापीडन|वामापीडनः
वामापीडन m. (-नः) A tree, (Salvadora Persica, &c.:) see पीलु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामावर्त्त|वामावर्त|वामावर्तः
वामावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A conch-shell with the spiral turn running from<BR>right to left.<BR> E. वाम, and आवर्त्त a turn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामिल|वामिलः
वामिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Proud, haughty, intolerant.<BR>	 2. Handsome,<BR>beautiful.<BR>	 3. Deceitful.<BR> E. वम् to eject from the mouth, (the faults<BR>of others,) aff. इलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाय|वायः
वाय m. (-यः) Weaving.<BR> E. वे to weave, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायक|वायकः
वायक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A number, a multitude, a heap.<BR>	 2. A weaver.<BR> E. वय्<BR>to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाय|वायः
वाय(प)दण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A weaver's loom.<BR> E. वाय or वाप weaving, दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायन|वायनं
वायन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sweetmeats or cakes, forming a light refreshment,<BR>which is not supposed to be any breach of a religious fast.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sweetmeats or cakes, part of an offering to a deity, or prepared<BR>on particular occasions, as marriages, &c., and sent as presents<BR>to friends and acquaintances.<BR> E. वा to go, ल्युट् aff.; also with कन्<BR>added वायनक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव
वायव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Windy, relating or belonging to wind.<BR>	 f. (-वी) The<BR>north-west quarter or region of the wind.<BR> E. वायु air, wind, and अण्<BR>aff., fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव्य|वायव्यं
वायव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Relating to the wind, sacred to the deity of<BR>the wind, &c.<BR> E. वायु wind, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायस|वायसः
वायस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A crow.<BR>	 2. Agallochum, (Amyris Agallocha.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Turpentine.<BR>	 f. (-सी)<BR>	 1. A species of fig, (Ficus oppositifolia, Rox.)<BR>4. A vegetable, (Solanum Indicum.)<BR> E. वय् to go, Uṇādi aff. असच्,<BR>and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायसाराति|वायसारातिः
वायसाराति m. (-तिः) An owl.<BR> E. वायस a crow, and आराति an enemy;<BR>also similar compounds, as वायसारि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायसेक्षु|वायसेक्षुः
वायसेक्षु m. (-क्षुः) A sort of long grass, “काशतृणे ।” (Saccharum spon-<BR>taneum.)<BR> E. वायस a crow, and इक्षु the sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायसोली
वायसोली f. (-ली) A medicinal root, commonly Kākoli.<BR> E. वायस a crow, उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायु|वायुः
वायु m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind, or its personified deification.<BR>	 2. The air of<BR>the body, of which five are enumerated, viz. PRĀṆA, SAMĀNA,<BR>APĀNA, UDĀNA, and VYĀNA.<BR>	 3. Morbid affection of the windy<BR>humour.<BR> E. वा to go, उण् Unādi aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुकेतु|वायुकेतुः
वायुकेतु m. (-तुः) Dust.<BR> E. वायु wind, and केतु a symbol, a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुकोण|वायुकोणः
वायुकोण m. (-णः) The north west.<BR> E. वायु, and कोण corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुगण्ड|वायुगंड|वायुगण्डः
वायुगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Flatulence, indigestion.<BR> E. वायु wind, गडि to be a part<BR>of, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुगति
वायुगति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Quick, swift, as the wind.<BR> E. वायु, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुगुल्म|वायुगुल्मः
वायुगुल्म m. (-ल्मः)<BR>	 1. A whirlpool, an eddy.<BR>	 2. A whirlwind, a hurricane.<BR>E. वायु, गुल्म a cluster: see वातगुल्म ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुग्रस्त
वायुग्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Affected by wind, flatulent, epileptic.<BR> E. वायु, अस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुघ्न
वायुघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Destroying or curing windy disorders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुजात|वायुजातः
वायुजात m. (-तः) HANUMĀNA.<BR> E. वायु, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुदारु|वायुदारुः
वायुदारु m. (-रुः) A cloud.<BR> E. वायु wind, दृ to scatter, aff. उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुनिघ्न
वायुनिघ्न Adj. Mad, frantic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुनिवृत्ति|वायुनिवृत्तिः
वायुनिवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Calm, lull.<BR>	 2. Cure of windy disorders.<BR> E. वायु, निवृत्ति stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुपुत्त्र
वायुपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) A name of BHIMA.<BR>	 2. A name of HANUMĀNA.<BR> E. वायु the<BR>god of wind, and पुत्त्र a son; also similar compounds, as वायुतनय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुफल|वायुफलं
वायुफल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The rainbow.<BR>	 2. Hail.<BR> E. वायु wind, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुभक्ष|वायुभक्षः
वायुभक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Eating air, fasting.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2.<BR>An ascetic who lives on air.<BR> E. वायु wind, and भक्ष who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुभक्षण|वायुभक्षणः
वायुभक्षण n. (-णं) Fasting, living on air.<BR> E. वायु and भक्षण eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुभूत
वायुभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Becoming as the wind, going every where at<BR>will.<BR> E. वायु and भूत become.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुरोषा
वायुरोषा f. (-षा) Night.<BR> E. वायु wind, रुष् to rage, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुवर्त्मन्
वायुवर्त्मन् m. (-र्त्मा) The atmosphere, sky, heaven.<BR> E. वायु, वर्त्मन् path or road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुवाह|वायुवाहः
वायुवाह m. (-हः) Smoke, vapour.<BR> E. वायु the wind, and वाह vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुवाहिनी
वायुवाहिनी f. (-नी) A vessel of the body, supposed, as the arteries were<BR>once imagined, to convey the aerial humour.<BR> E. वायु, वाहिनी bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुवेगसम
वायुवेगसम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Swift as the wind.<BR> E. वायु, वेग speed, सम equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुष|वायुषः
वायुष m. (-षः) A sort of fish. “काल्वोस् माछ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुसख|वायुसखः
वायुसख m. (-खः) Fire.<BR> E. वायु wind, सखि friend, aff. टच्; also without<BR>the aff. वायुसखि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुसम
वायुसम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Like wind, unsubstantial.<BR>	 2. Swift.<BR> E. वायु, सम same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुसम्भव
वायुसम्भव m. (-वः) HANUMĀNA.<BR> E. वायु, सम्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाय्वास्पद|वाय्वास्पदं
वाय्वास्पद n. (-दं) Ether, atmosphere.<BR> E. वायु wind, आस्पद place, site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्
वार् n. (-वाः) Water.<BR> E. वृ to surround, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार|वारं|वारः
वार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A multitude, a quantity, a flock or herd, a heap.<BR>	 2.<BR>Occasion, opportunity.<BR>	 3. A day of the week.<BR>	 4. A moment.<BR>	 5. A<BR>name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 6. A door-way, a gate.<BR>	 7. Achyranthes aspera.<BR>	 8.<BR>A cover.<BR>	 9. A turn.<BR>	 10. The opposite bank of a river.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>vessel for holding spirituous liquor.<BR>	 2. Bile.<BR>	 2. Water. Adv. A<BR>time, as वारं बारं many a time, repeatedly, often: see वारम्बारं.<BR>E. वृ to cover, to choose, &c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारक|वारकं|वारकः
वारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Opposing, obstructing, an obstacle or agent of<BR>resistance.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A horse's paces.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The<BR>seat of pain.<BR>	 2. A sort of fragrant grass: see वाल.<BR> E. वृ to choose,<BR>&c., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारकिन्
वारकिन् m. (-की)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. Aihorse with good marks.<BR>	 3. An ene-<BR>my.<BR>	 4. An ascetic, one living upon leaves, &c.<BR> E. वारक an obstacle,<BR>&c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारकीर|वारकीरः
वारकीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A wife's brother.<BR>	 2. Submarine fire.<BR>	 3. A louse.<BR>	 4. A<BR>small comb.<BR>	 5. A horse of high spirit, a war-horse, a charger.<BR>	 6. A<BR>bearer of burthens, a porter.<BR> E. वार an obstacle, कॄ to scatter,<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारङ्क|वारंक|वारंकः|वारङ्कः
वारङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A bird in general.<BR> E. वार् water, अकि to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारङ्ग|वारंग|वारंगः|वारङ्गः
वारङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The handle of a sword or knife, &c.<BR> E. वृ to select, aff.<BR>अङ्गच्, and the radical vowel changed to the Vriddhi form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारट|वारटं
वारट n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. A field.<BR>	 2. A number of fields.<BR>	 f. (-टा) A goose; also<BR>वरटा.<BR> E. वार् water, अट् to go, aff. अच्; or वृ-अटच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारण|वारणं|वारणः
वारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Resistance, opposition, prohibition, obstacle or impe-<BR>diment.<BR>	 2. Defence, protecting, guarding.<BR>	 3. Warding off a blow,<BR>guarding, warding.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Armour, a cuirass or mail for the<BR>body.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR> E. वॄ to cover or screen, to defend, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणबुषा
वारणबुषा f. (-षा) The plantain or banana, (Musa sapientum.)<BR> E. वारण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">Page645-b+ 60</a>]<BR>an elephant, बुष् or बुस् to cast off, aff. क; hence it is written also<BR>वारणबुसा; also वार्बुषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणवल्लभा
वारणवल्लभा f. (-भा) The plantain tree.<BR> E. वारण an elephant, वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारत्र|वारत्रं
वारत्र n. (-त्रं) Leather fit for or made into thongs.<BR> E. वरत्रा, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारनारी
वारनारी f. (-री) A harlot.<BR> E. वार and नारी a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारबधू
वारबधू f. (-धूः) The chief of a set of harlots.<BR> E. वार a number, and बधू wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारबुषा
वारबुषा f. (-षा) A Banāna; also वारबूषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारमुख्या
वारमुख्या f. (-ख्या) The head of a set of harlots.<BR> E. वार a troop, मुख्या<BR>a chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारम्बारम्
वारम्बारम् Ind. Repeatedly, again and again.<BR> E. वार a day, a time, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारला
वारला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A wasp.<BR>	 2. A goose.<BR> E. वार a flock, a flight, ला to get,<BR>and क and टाप् affs.; also बरला &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारवाण|वारवाणः
वारवाण mn. (-णः-णं) Armour for the body or breast, an iron cuirass, or<BR>a thick quilted jacket worn for the same purpose.<BR> E. वार opposing,<BR>वाण an arrow; also वाणवार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारवाणि|वारवाणिः
वारवाणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A player on the flute.<BR>	 2. A singer, a musician.<BR>	 3.<BR>A judge.<BR>	 4. A year.<BR>	 f. (-णिः or णी)<BR>	 1. The chief of a set of harlots.<BR>2. A whore.<BR> E. वार् a multitude, वाणी speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारविलासिनी
वारविलासिनी f. (-नी) A harlot, a whore.<BR> E. वार a multitude, विलासिनी a wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारवृषा
वारवृषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Grain.<BR>	 2. Plantain.<BR> E. वारं जलसङ्घं वर्षत्यत्र वृष्-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारवेला
वारवेला f. (-ला) A portion of the day in which any act religious or<BR>secular is suspended.<BR> E. वार and वेला time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारसुन्दरी|वारसुंदरी
वारसुन्दरी f. (-री) A whore, a prostitute.<BR> E. वार the multitude, सुन्दरी a beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारसेवा
वारसेवा f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A set of courtezans.<BR>	 2. Prostitution, harlotry.<BR> E. वार<BR>the multitude, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारस्त्री
वारस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) A whore.<BR> E. वार the many, स्त्री a woman, a common woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारांनिधि
वारांनिधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. वारां of water, and निधि receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराङ्गना|वारांगना
वाराङ्गना f. (-ना) A harlot.<BR> E. वार and अङ्गना a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराणसी
वाराणसी f. (-सी) The holy city Benares.<BR> E. वर best, अनस् water, affs.<BR>अण् and ङीष् i. e. the Ganges on which it stands; also वराणसी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराणसेय|वाराणसेयः
वाराणसेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Produced at or born in Benares,<BR> E. वाराणसी<BR>the city, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारासन|वारासनं
वारासन n. (-नं) A large water-jar, a cistern, a reservoir.<BR> E. वार् water, आसन place of abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराह|वाराहः
वाराह mfn. (-हः-ही-हं) Relating to a boar, belonging to, derived from,<BR>&c.<BR>	 f. (-ही)<BR>	 1. An esculent root, a Yam, (Dioscorea.)<BR>	 2. One of<BR>the divine mothers.<BR>	 3. A measure.<BR>	 4. The earth.<BR>	 5. A sow. E.<BR>वराह a hog or VIṢṆU in that form, &c., अण् aff. and ङीप्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारि|वारिः
वारि n. (-रि)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. A vegetable perfume, commonly Bālā.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-रिः)<BR>	 1. A name of SARASWATĪ; the goddess of speech.<BR>	 2. The place<BR>where an elephant is tied or fastened.<BR>	 3. A captive, a prisoner.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-रिः or री)<BR>	 1. A water-pot, whether large or small, pitcher, a jar.<BR>	 2.<BR>The rope that fastens an elephant.<BR>	 3. A hole or trap for catching<BR>elephant.<BR> E. वृञ् to surround, Unādi aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिकण्टक|वारिकण्टकः
वारिकण्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>	 2. Another<BR>plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR> E. वारि water, and कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिकर्णिका
वारिकर्णिका f. (-का) A plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. वारि water, and कर्णिका<BR>here meaning leaf or leaf-let.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिकर्पूर|वारिकर्पूरः
वारिकर्पूर m. (-रः) The Iliśa-fish, (Cluponodon Ilisha, HAM.)<BR> E. वारि<BR>water, and कर्पूर camphor, to which it is compared in colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिकुब्ज|वारिकुब्जः
वारिकुब्ज m. (-ब्जः) An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR> E. वारि water,<BR>कुब्ज Achyranthes; also with कन् added, वारिकुब्जक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिक्रिमि|वारिक्रिमिः
वारिक्रिमि m. (-मिः) A leech.<BR> E. वारि water, and क्रिमि a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिचत्वर|वारिचत्वरः
वारिचत्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR>	 2. A piece<BR>of water.<BR> E. वारि water, चत्वर expanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिचर|वारिचरः
वारिचर mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं) Aquatic, living or moving in water.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः) A fish.<BR> E. वारि water, चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिचामर|वारिचामरं
वारिचामर n. (-रं) A sort of weed, (Vallisneria.)<BR> E. वारि water, and चामर Chowri or brush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिज|वारिजं|वारिजः
वारिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Aquatic, born or produced in or by water.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-जः)<BR>	 1. A conch-shell.<BR>	 2. Any bivalve-shell.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>2. A kind of salt.<BR>	 3. Cloves.<BR> E. वारि water, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारित
वारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hindered, prevented, impeded.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Warded<BR>off.<BR>	 2. Obstructed.<BR>	 3. Protected.<BR> E. वॄ to cover, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारितस्कर|वारितस्करः
वारितस्कर m. (-रः) A cloud.<BR> E. वारि water, तस्कर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारित्रा
वारित्रा f. (-त्रा) A sort of umbrella, or portable shed of leaves, carried<BR>on the head as one.<BR> E. वारि water, त्रा to preserve, affs. क and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिद|वारिदं|वारिदः
वारिद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) What yields water.<BR>	 m. (-दः) A cloud.<BR>	 n. (-दं) A<BR>sort of vegetable perfume: see वाल.<BR> E. वारि water, द what yields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिद्र|वारिद्रः
वारिद्र m. (-द्रः) The Chātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR> E. वारि water,<BR>दृ to take, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिधारा
वारिधारा f. (-रा) A shower of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिधि|वारिधिः
वारिधि m. (-धिः) The sea.<BR> E. वारि water, धा to contain, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिनाथ|वारिनाथः
वारिनाथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. The deity VARUṆA.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR>	 3. A cloud.<BR>	 4.<BR>The habitation of the Nāgas, or serpent race.<BR> E. वारि, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिनिधि|वारिनिधिः
वारिनिधि m. (-धिः) The sea, the ocean.<BR> E. वारि water, निधि a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिपथिक|वारिपथिकः
वारिपथिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Proceeding or conveyed by water.<BR> E. वारि<BR>water, पथिन् a road, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिपर्णी
वारिपर्णी f. (-र्णी) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. वारि water, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिप्रवाह|वारिप्रवाहः
वारिप्रवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A cascade, a water-fall.<BR>	 2. A current or flow of<BR>water.<BR> E. वारि water, and प्रवाह a fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिप्रश्नी
वारिप्रश्नी f. (-श्नी) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. वारि water, प्रश्नी the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिबदरा
वारिबदरा f. (-रा) A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR> E. वारि, बदर jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिबालक|वारिबालकं
वारिबालक n. (-कं) A perfume: see वाल.<BR> E. वारि water, वाल a perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिमसि|वारिमसिः
वारिमसि m. (-सिः) A cloud.<BR> E. वारि water, मसि ink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिमुच्
वारिमुच् m. (-मुक्) A cloud.<BR> E. वारि water, मुच् what emits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिमूली
वारिमूली f. (-ली) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. वारि water, मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारियन्त्र|वारियंत्र
वारियन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A wheel for raising water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिर
वारिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Giving or shedding water.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A cloud.<BR> E. वारि, रा to give, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिरथ|वारिरथः
वारिरथ m. (-थः) A raft, a float.<BR> E. वारि water, रथ a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिरारव
वारिरारव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Sounding like clouds or thunder.<BR> E. वारिर, आरव sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिराशि|वारिराशिः
वारिराशि m. (-शिः) The ocean.<BR> E. वारि water, राशि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिरुह|वारिरुहं
वारिरुह n. (-हं) The lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिलोमन्
वारिलोमन् m. (-मा) A name of VARUṆA.<BR> E. वारि water, लोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिवदन|वारिवदनं
वारिवदन m. (-नः) A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR> E. वारि water, वदन<BR>countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिवास|वारिवासः
वारिवास m. (-सः) A distiller or dealer in spirituous liquors.<BR> E. वारि, वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिवाह|वारिवाहः
वारिवाह m. (-हः) A cloud.<BR> E. वारि water, वाह what bears; also वारिवाहन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिवाहन|वारिवाहनः
वारिवाहन m. (-नः) A cloud.<BR> E. वारि water, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिश|वारिशः
वारिश m. (-शः) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. वारि water, शो to sleep, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारिसम्भव|वारिसम्भवं|वारिसंभवः|वारिसम्भवः
वारिसम्भव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Cloves.<BR>	 2. A kind of antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारीट|वारीटः
वारीट m. (-टः) An elephant.<BR> E. वारि the trap for an elephant, अट् to<BR>go, aff. अच्, form. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारीश|वारीशः
वारीश m. (-शः) The ocean.<BR> E. वार् water, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारु|वारुः
वारु m. (-रुः) A war-elephant carrying a standard.<BR> E. वृ to cover, aff. उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुठ|वारुठः
वारुठ m. (-ठः) A bier, the bed on which the corpse is carried.<BR> E. वृ to<BR>cover, aff. उठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुण|वारुणं|वारुणः
वारुण n. (-णं) Water.<BR>	 m. (-णः) Name of one of the nine divisions of<BR>BHĀRATA-VARSHA.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Belonging or sacred to VARUṆA.<BR>	 2.<BR>Given by VARUṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुणि|वारुणिः
वारुणि m. (-णिः) The saint AGASTYA.<BR> E. वरुण VARUṆA, इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुणी
वारुणी f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Any spirituous liquor, or more properly, a particular<BR>kind prepared from hogweed, ground with the juice of the date<BR>or palm, and then distilled.<BR>	 2. The west, the region of VARUṆA.<BR>3. The 25th lunar asterism, of which VARUṆA is the ruling deity.<BR>4. A species of Durbā-grass.<BR> E. वरुण the deity, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुणीवल्लभ|वारुणीवल्लभः
वारुणीवल्लभ m. (-भः) VARUṆA.<BR> E. वारुणी the asterism, वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुण्ड|वारुंड|वारुंडः|वारुण्डः
वारुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The chief of the serpent race.<BR>	 mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. The<BR>rheum of the eyes.<BR>	 2. The wax of the ear.<BR>	 3. A vessel for baling<BR>water out of a boat.<BR> E. वॄ to screen, aff. उण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारेण
वारेण Ind. Frequently, repeatedly.<BR> E. वार a time, in the third case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारेन्द्री|वारेंद्री
वारेन्द्री f. (-न्द्री) Part of Bengal and Behar, or a tract of inundation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">Page646-b+ 60</a>]<BR>north of the Ganges, and part of the present Zilā of Rājshāhī. E.<BR>वरेन्द्र a king, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्क्ष
वार्क्ष mfn. (-र्क्षः-र्क्षी-र्क्षं) Made of or derived from a tree.<BR>	 n. (-र्क्षं) A forest.<BR>f. (-र्क्षी) The name of a female mentioned in the Mahābhārat, a<BR>sort of Dryad.<BR> E. वृक्ष् a tree, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्क्ष्य|वार्क्ष्यं
वार्क्ष्य mfn. (-र्क्ष्यः-र्क्ष्यी-र्क्ष्यं) Made of or with trees.<BR>	 n. (-र्क्ष्यं) A stockade.<BR> E. वृक्ष, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्च|वार्च्चः
वार्च mfn. (-र्चः-र्चा-र्चं) Any aquatic animal.<BR> E. वारि चरति चर-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्णिक|वार्णिकः
वार्णिक m. (-कः) A scribe, a writer.<BR> E. वर्ण a letter, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्त|वार्त|वार्त्तं|वार्त्तः
वार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Well, healthy.<BR>	 2. Following any business or<BR>profession.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्तः) Health.<BR>	 n. (-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Chaff.<BR>	 2. Skill.<BR>	 3.<BR>Health, welfare.<BR>	 f. (-र्त्ता)<BR>	 1. Tidings, news, intelligence.<BR>	 2.<BR>Rumour, report.<BR>	 3. Livelihood, business, profession.<BR>	 4. Agriculture<BR>or trade, the proper occupation of the Vaiśyas.<BR>	 5. Abiding, stay-<BR>ing, being.<BR>	 6. Unsubstantial, light.<BR>	 7. Healthy.<BR>	 8. The egg-plant.<BR>E. वृत्ति being, &c., aff. अण् or ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्ताक|वार्ताक|वार्ताकः|वार्त्ताकः
वार्त्ताक m. (-कः) The egg-plant: see वार्त्ताकु, the उ being changed to अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्ताकर्म्मन्|वार्ताकर्मन्
वार्त्ताकर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्म) The peculiar occupation of the third or Vaiśya-class,<BR>agriculture, trade, &c.<BR> E. वार्त्ता, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्ताकि|वार्ताकि|वार्ताकिः
वार्त्ताकि f. (-किः or की) The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR> E. वृत् to<BR>be, काकिन् aff.; ङीप् or इन् fem. aff., form irr.; also वार्त्ताकु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्ताकिन्|वार्ताकिन्
वार्त्ताकिन् m. (-की) The egg-plant; also वार्त्ताकि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्ताकु|वार्ताकु|वार्ताकुः|वार्त्ताकुः
वार्त्ताकु m. (-कुः) The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR> E. वृत् to be, काकु<BR>Unādi aff., and the vowel made long by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तयन
वार्त्तयन m. (-नः) A spy, an emissary, an agent, an ambassador, an<BR>intelligencer, a news-monger.<BR> E. वार्त्ता news, अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तारम्भ
वार्त्तारम्भ m. (-म्भः) Commercial enterprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तावह|वार्तावह|वार्त्तावहः
वार्त्तावह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A chandler.<BR>	 2. A messenger.<BR> E. वार्त्ता news, वह् to bear, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तावृत्ति
वार्त्तावृत्ति m. (-त्तिः) A householder.<BR> E. वार्त्ता news, and वृत्ति business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्तिक|वार्तिक|वार्त्तिकं|वार्त्तिकः
वार्त्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating to news, bringing or conveying in-<BR>telligence, &c.<BR>	 2. Commentatory, explanatory, belonging to a<BR>comment or gloss, (as a rule, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An intelligencer, an<BR>informer, an agent or envoy.<BR>	 2. A man of third or mercantile<BR>tribe.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A gloss, a commentary, especially a supplementary<BR>explanation added to a grammatical or philosophical aphorism,<BR>and its immediate elucidation, supplying or illustrating both text<BR>and comment; it is defined to be, the exposition of the meaning,<BR>of that which is said, of that which is left unsaid, and of that<BR>which is ill or imperfectly said.<BR>	 f. (-का) A kind of quail.<BR> E. वृत्ति<BR>news, &c., or a comment, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्त्त्रघ्न
वार्त्त्रघ्न m. (-घ्नः) An epithet of ARJUNA.<BR> E. वृत्त्रघ्न INDRA, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्दर|वार्दर|वार्द्दरं
वार्द्दर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Silk.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. The seed of the Abrus precatorius.<BR>4. A conch-shell.<BR>	 5. A sort of curl on the right side of a horse's<BR>neck, considered as an auspicious mark.<BR>	 6. Speech.<BR> E. वार् water,<BR>दृ to divide, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्दल|वार्दल|वार्दलः|वार्द्दलं|वार्द्दलः
वार्द्दल n. (-लं) A rainy day, bad weather, &c.<BR>	 m. (-लः) An inkstand. E.<BR>वार् water, and द what gives, वार्द a cloud, ला to take, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धक
वार्द्धक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A number of old men.<BR>	 2. Old age.<BR>	 3. The infirmity,<BR>&c. of old age.<BR> E. वृद्ध old, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धक्य
वार्द्धक्य n. (-क्यं) Old age.<BR> E. वृद्ध old, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्ध्वि
वार्द्ध्वि m. (-र्द्धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. वार् water, धा to have, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषि
वार्द्धुषि m. (-षिः) An usurer.<BR> E. वृद्धि interest or increase, वृधुषि substituted,<BR>aff. ठक्, and the क rejected; also वार्द्धुषिक; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषिक
वार्द्धुषिक m. (-कः) An usurer: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुषिन्
वार्द्धुषिन् m. (-षी) An usurer.<BR> E. वृधुषि substituted for वृद्धि, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्धुष्य
वार्द्धुष्य n. (-ष्यं) Usurious loan, usury, interest.<BR> E. वृद्धि increase, aff. ष्यञ्,<BR>form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्ध्र
वार्द्ध्र nf. (-र्द्ध्रं-र्द्ध्री) A leather thong.<BR> E. वृद्ध् to increase, to lengthen, aff. ष्ट्र, अञ् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्द्ध्रीणस्
वार्द्ध्रीणस् m. (-सः) An old white goat with long ears.<BR> E. वार्द्ध्री a leather<BR>thong, and नस for नासिका a nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्भट|वार्भटः
वार्भट m. (-टः) An alligator.<BR> E. वार् water, भट् to maintain, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्म्मण|वार्मण|वार्मणं|वार्म्मणं
वार्म्मण n. (-णं) A number of coats of mail.<BR> E. वर्म्मण् armour, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्म्मिण|वार्मिण|वार्म्मिणं
वार्म्मिण n. (-णं) A number of men in armour.<BR> E. वर्म्मिन् a man in armour,<BR>and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्म्मुच्|वार्मुच्
वार्म्मुच् m. (-र्म्मुक्) A cloud.<BR> E. वार् water, मुच् to let loose, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य|वार्यं|वार्यः|वार्य्य|वार्य्यं
वार्य n. (-र्यं) A boon, a blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य्य|वार्य|वार्यं|वार्यः|वार्य्यं
वार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. To be selected or appointed.<BR>	 2. To be impe-<BR>ded, checked, stopped, &c.<BR> E. वृङ् to choose, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य्यमाण|वार्यमाण
वार्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being prevented, impeded, prohibited, &c. E.<BR>वृ to select, passive v., शानच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य्युद्भव|वार्युद्भव|वार्य्युद्भवं
वार्य्युद्भव n. (-वं) A lotus.<BR> E. वारि water, उद्भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्य्योकस्|वार्योकस्
वार्य्योकस् m. (-काः) A leech.<BR> E. वारि, and ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्राशि
वार्राशि m. (-शिः) The ocean.<BR> E. वार and राशि quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्व्वट|वार्वट|वार्वटः|वार्व्वटः
वार्व्वट m. (-टः) A boat, a vessel.<BR> E. वार् water, वट् to surround, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्वणा|वार्व्वणा
वार्वणा f. (-णा) A kind of blue fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ष
वार्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षी-र्षं) Belonging to a year, to the rains, &c.<BR> E. वर्ष, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षिक|वार्षिकं|वार्षिकः
वार्षिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Yearly, annual, or belonging to a year.<BR>	 2.<BR>Growing, &c. in the rainy season, or fit for or suited to it, &c.<BR>	 3.<BR>Lasting for one year.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A drug, commonly Trāyamānā. E.<BR>वर्ष rains, or a year, and ठक् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षिला
वार्षिला f. (-ला) Hail.<BR> E. वार्ष belonging to rain, from वर्ष with अण् aff., इलच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्षुक|वार्षुकः
वार्षुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Sprinkling, wetting, that which sprinkles, &c.<BR>E. वृष् to sprinkle, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हत|वार्हतं
वार्हत n. (-तं) The fruit of the solanum jacquini.<BR> E. वृहति the plant, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हद्रथ|वार्हद्रथः
वार्हद्रथ m. (-थः) A name of JARĀSANDHA.<BR> E. वृहद्रथ the father of this<BR>prince, and अण् patronymic; also with इञ् aff. वार्हद्रथि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हस्पत
वार्हस्पत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Sacred to VRIHASPATĪ.<BR> E. वृहस्पति and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्हस्पत्य
वार्हस्पत्य n. (-त्यं) Ethics, morality.<BR> E. वृहस्पति the supposed original au-<BR>thor of this science, and ण्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वालक|वालकः
वालक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A bracelet.<BR>	 2. A finger-ring.<BR> E. वल् to surround, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्क|वाल्कं
वाल्क mfn. (-ल्कः-ल्की-ल्कं) Made of the bark of trees.<BR> E. वल्क bark, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्कल|वाल्कलं
वाल्कल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Made of bark.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>A dress made of the bark of trees worn by ascetics.<BR> E. वल्कल bark,<BR>and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्मिकि|वाल्मिकिः
वाल्मिकि m. (-किः) The author of the Rāmāyaṇa; also वाल्मीकि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्मीक|वाल्मीकः
वाल्मीक m. (-कः) VĀLMĪKA or VĀLMĪKI, the first poet and the famous<BR>author of the Rāmāyaṇa. Though a Brāhmana by birth he led<BR>a depraved life and was a notorious cut-throat, but was reclaimed<BR>by Nārada. One day while he was engaged in his devotions, he<BR>saw a fowler in the act of shooting at a pair of curlews and a<BR>curse fell from his mouth in the shape of a regular stanza. The<BR>sage discovered that it was a new mode of composition and by<BR>the advice of BRAHMĀ he composed the Rāmāyaṇa in that style.<BR>SITĀ when repudiated by her husband, took refuge with this<BR>sage who brought up her twin sons.<BR> E. वल्मीक an ant-hill, aff. अण्,<BR>or with इञ् aff. वाल्मीकि; so immersed in abstraction as to be<BR>overrun with ant's nests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाल्लभ्य|वाल्लभ्यं
वाल्लभ्य n. (-भ्यं) The being beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावदूक|वावदूकः
वावदूक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Talking much, gabbling, prattling.<BR> E. वद् to<BR>speak, Unādi aff. ऊक, the root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावदूकता
वावदूकता f. (-ता) Garrulity, loquaciousness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last;<BR>also with त्व, वावदूकत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावय|वावयः
वावय m. (-यः) A sort of Basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावहि
वावहि mfn. (-हिः-हिः-हि) Who or what bears or carries much.<BR> E. वह् to bear, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावुट|वावुटः
वावुट m. (-टः) A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृत्
वावृत्(उ)वावृतु r. 4th cl. (वावृत्यते)<BR>	 1. To choose or select.<BR>	 2. To serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृत्त|वावृत्तः
वावृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Chosen, appointed.<BR> E. वृत् to be, aff. क्त, and the<BR>root reiterated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वावृत्यमान
वावृत्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Choosing, preferring.<BR> E. वावृत to choose, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाश्
वाश्(ऋ)वाशृ r. 4th cl. (वाश्यते)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To cry as a bird.<BR>	 3.<BR>To call.<BR>	 4. To howl, to growl, to roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशत्
वाशत् mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्)<BR>	 1. Crying or singing like a bird.<BR>	 2. Growling,<BR>roaring.<BR> E. वाश् to cry, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशन|वाशनं
वाशन n. (-नं) The cry or song of birds, bees, and the like.<BR> E. वाश् to<BR>sound as a bird, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशा
वाशा f. (-शा) A plant, (Justicia ganderussa:) see वास and वासक; also<BR>with कन् added वाशिका । “वाकस गाछ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशि|वाशिः
वाशि m. (-शिः) Fire.<BR> E. वाश् to sound, Unādi aff. इञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशित|वाशितं|वाशितः
वाशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Perfumed, scented.<BR>	 2. Sung, called, cried.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं) The cry of birds or animals.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. A female-<BR>elephant.<BR> E. वाष् to call, or वास् to perfume, aff. क्त, and ष or स<BR>changed to श ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशिष्ठ|वाशिष्ठः
वाशिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं) Relating to the sage VASIṢṬHA.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठी) The<BR>Goomti river, which rising in the Kumaun hills, pursues a<BR>winding and south-easterly course, and passing Lucknow and<BR>Jonpur falls into the Ganges, below Benares.<BR> E. वशिष्ठ the saint,<BR>अण् aff., derived from him; also read वासिष्ठ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाशुरा
वाशुरा f. (-रा) Night.<BR> E. वाश् to sound, Unādi aff. उरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाश्र|वाश्रं|वाश्रः
वाश्र m. (-श्रः) A day.<BR>	 n. (-श्रं)<BR>	 1. An edifice, a dwelling, a building.<BR>	 2.<BR>A place where four roads meet.<BR> E. वाश् to sound, Unādi aff. रक्;<BR>also read वास्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्कल|वाष्कलः
वाष्कल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Large, great.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्प|वाष्पं|वाष्पः
वाष्प(स्प) m. (-ष्पः or स्पः)<BR>	 1. Vapour, hot mist, steam, &c.<BR>	 2. A tear.<BR>	 3.<BR>Iron.<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी) A drug.<BR> E. वा to go, or वै to dry, aff. प, form irr.,<BR>also बाष्प, as derived from बाध् to oppose, and ध changed to ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पका
वाष्पका f. (-का) A drug, commonly Hingupatri.<BR> E. कन् added to वाष्प<BR>vapour; also वाष्पिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पाकल
वाष्पाकल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Uttered or articulated with tears.<BR> E. वाष्प, and आकल what sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पाकुल
वाष्पाकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Interrupted by tears.<BR> E. वाष्प, आकुल perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पिका
वाष्पिका f. (-का) A drug, commonly Hingupatri.<BR> E. वाष्प a tear, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाष्पोद्भव
वाष्पोद्भव m. (-वः) Starting of tears.<BR> E. वाष्प and उद्भव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्
वास् r. 10th cl. (वासयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To introduce another quality, but espe-<BR>cially fragrant odors, to perfume, to incense, to fumigate, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>To steal, to infuse.<BR>	 3. To season, to spice. (ऋ) वासृ r. 4th cl. (वास्यते)<BR>To sound, especially as a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास|वासः
वास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A house, a habitation.<BR>	 2. Site, situation, abode or<BR>place of staying or abiding.<BR>	 3. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 4. Perfuming.<BR>	 mf.<BR>(-सः-सा) A plant, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR> E. वस् to dwell, &c., aff.<BR>घञ्; or वास् to fumigate, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासःकुटी
वासःकुटी f. (-टी) A tent.<BR> E. वासस् cloth, and कुटी a hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासक|वासकः
वासक mf. (-कः-सका or सिका)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Perfuming.<BR> E. वास् to perfume, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासकसज्जा
वासकसज्जा f. (-ज्जा) A woman dressed with all her ornaments, and hav-<BR>ing her apartments, &c. decorated to receive her lover.<BR> E. वास clo-<BR>thes, कन् pleonasm, and सज्जा accoutrements; also with कन् added,<BR>वासकसज्जिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासकर्णी
वासकर्णी f. (-र्णी) A hall, where public exhibition, as Nāutches, &c.<BR>are held.<BR> E. वास a house, कर्ण the ear, aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासगृह|वासगृहं
वासगृह n. (-हं) The inner part of a house, an inner or sleeping room,<BR>a bed-chamber.<BR> E. वास abiding, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासत|वासतः
वासत m. (-तः) An ass.<BR> E. वास, अतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासताम्बूल|वासतांबूल
वासताम्बूल n. (-लं) Betel with other fragrant substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासतेय
वासतेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Habitable, fit or proper to be dwelt in.<BR>	 f. (-यी)<BR>Night.<BR> E. वसति abode, or night, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन|वासनं
वासन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fit for clothes or dwelling, &c.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Perfu-<BR>ming, fumigating or perfuming with fragrant vapour, or with in-<BR>cense, &c.<BR>	 2. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 3. Abiding, abode.<BR>	 4. A particular<BR>posture in which abstract meditation is performed; it is also a<BR>posture conceived to be peculiarly proper in princes and chiefs,<BR>and is then described as sitting with the knees bent and the feet<BR>turned backwards.<BR>	 5. Knowledge.<BR>	 6. A water-jar.<BR>	 7. A box, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">Page648-a+ 60</a>]<BR>basket, a vessel, &c.<BR>	 8. An envelope.<BR>	 9. Any receptacle.<BR>	 10. Steep-<BR>ing, infusing.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. The knowledge of anything derived from<BR>memory, the present consciousness of past perceptions.<BR>	 2. Fancy,<BR>imagination.<BR>	 3. Trust, confidence.<BR>	 4. Ignorance.<BR>	 5. Wish, desire.<BR>E. वस् to dwell, &c., aff. युच्; or वसन clothes, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासनस्थ
वासनस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Packed, folded, enveloped.<BR> E. वासन a box,<BR>&c., and स्थ what stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्त|वासंत|वासन्तः
वासन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Placed, situated.<BR>	 2. Vernal, relating to the<BR>season of spring, suitable to it, produced in it, &c.<BR>	 3. Young, in<BR>the spring of life.<BR>	 4. Diligent in the performance of religious cere-<BR>monies.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A camel.<BR>	 2. The Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 3. Any young<BR>animal, or a young elephant.<BR>	 4. A catamite.<BR>	 5. The southern wind,<BR>zephyr.<BR>	 6. A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>	 7. The<BR>black kind of Moong or bean.<BR>	 8. A plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A large creeper, (Gærtnera racemosa.)<BR>	 2. A species of<BR>jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>	 3. Long pepper.<BR>	 4. Trumpet-<BR>flower.<BR>	 5. A festival in honour of KĀMADEVA, held in the month<BR>of Chaitra.<BR>	 6. A species of the Sarkarī metre.<BR> E. वस् to dwell,<BR>aff. झच्, and the vowel made long; or वसन्त spring, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्तक|वासन्तकं
वासन्तक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Sown or growing in spring.<BR>	 2. Suitable to<BR>the spring season.<BR>	 3. Relating or belonging to it, vernal.<BR> E. वसन्त<BR>spring, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासन्तिक|वासंतिक|वासन्तिकः
वासन्तिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An actor, a dancer.<BR>	 2. The buffoon in a drama.<BR>f. (-की) Vernal.<BR> E. वसन्त spring, aff. ठक्; the spring being the<BR>festival season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासयोग|वासयोगः
वासयोग m. (-गः) Fragrant powder sprinkled on the clothes, especially<BR>the red powder scattered about at the Holī festival.<BR> E. वास per-<BR>fume, and योग joining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासर|वासरं|वासरः
वासर mn. (-रः-रं) A day.<BR>	 m. (-रः) One of the Nāgas or serpents.<BR> E. वस्<BR>to abide, in the causal form, Unādi aff. अरन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासरसङ्ग|वासरसंग|वासरसङ्गः
वासरसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. The morning.<BR> E. वासर, सङ्ग connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासव|वासवः
वासव m. (-वः) INDRA.<BR>	 f. (-वी) The mother of VYĀSA.<BR> E. वसु a VASU,<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासवि|वासविः
वासवि m. (-विः) An epithet of ARJUNA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासस्
वासस् n. (-सः) Cloth, clothes.<BR> E. वस् to cover or clothe, aff. असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाससज्जा
वाससज्जा f. (-ज्जा) A woman drest in all her ornaments to receive her<BR>lover.<BR> E. वास clothes, सज्ज armed, accoutred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासागार|वासागारं|वासागारः
वासागार n. (-रं) The inner or sleeping apartment.<BR> E. वास abiding, आगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासि|वासिः
वासि mf. (-सिः-सी) A small hatchet or chopper, an adze.<BR>	 m. (-सिः)<BR>Abiding.<BR> E. वस् to abide, Unādi aff. इञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिका
वासिका f. (-का) A plant, (Justicia:) see वासक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासित|वासितं|वासितः
वासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Perfumed, scented.<BR>	 2. Clothed, dressed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Famous, celebrated.<BR>	 4. Steeped, infused.<BR>	 5. Spiced, seasoned, (sau-<BR>ces, &c.)<BR>	 6. Peopled, populous, flourishing, (a country.)<BR>	 7. Having,<BR>possessing.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The cry of birds.<BR>	 2. Knowledge in general,<BR>but especially that derived from memory.<BR>	 3. Sound.<BR>	 4. Rendering<BR>a country populous and flourishing, causing it to be inhabited.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ता)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. A female-elephant.<BR> E. वस् to dwell, or clothes,<BR>cansal form, or वास् to call, (as a bird,) aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिन्
वासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Abiding, staying.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A white sort of<BR>Jhiṇṭī. (Barleria.)<BR> E. वस् to dwell, घिनुण् aff.; or वास-इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिष्ट|वासिष्टं
वासिष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासिष्ठ|वासिष्ठं|वासिष्ठः
वासिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं) Explained or composed by the sage VAAISHṬHA,<BR>a part of the Vedas or a particular prayer, &c.<BR> E. वसिष्ठ, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासु|वासुः
वासु m. (-सुः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. The soul, or the Supreme Being<BR>considered as the soul of the universe.<BR> E. वस् to abide, (eternally,)<BR>उण् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुकि|वासुकिः
वासुकि m. (-किः) The serpent VĀSUKI, sovereign of the snakes and<BR>worn by ŚIVA on his person.<BR> E. वसु a jewel, क the head, or वसुक<BR>here said to be a name of KAŚYAPA, aff. of descent इञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुकेय|वासुकेयः
वासुकेय m. (-यः) The serpent VĀSUKI. E. See the last, aff. ढक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुकेयस्वसृ
वासुकेयस्वसृ f. (-सा) A name of MANASĀ, the wife of JARATKĀRU, and<BR>goddess presiding over snakes.<BR> E. वामुकेय VĀSUKI, स्वसृ a sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुदेव|वासुदेवः
वासुदेव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. A descendent of Vasudeva, the general<BR>appellation of a class of persons peculiar to the Jainas.<BR> E. वसुदेव<BR>the father of the deity, and अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुपूज्य|वासुपूज्यः
वासुपूज्य m. (-ज्यः) The twelfth Jina or Jaina teacher of the present æra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुभद्र|वासुभद्रः
वासुभद्र m. (-द्रः) A name of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. वासु the soul, भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासुरा
वासुरा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. The earth.<BR>	 3. A woman.<BR>	 4. A female ele-<BR>phant.<BR> E. वास् to perfume, or वस् to abide, causal form, aff. उरन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासू
वासू f. (-सूः) A young girl, a wench (in theatrical language.)<BR> E. वस् to<BR>abide, in the causal form, (to take to dwell with one,) aff. ऊ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासोद
वासोद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Who or what gives clothes.<BR> E. वासस्, द what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासोयुग
वासोयुग n. (-गं) A suit of clothes.<BR> E. वासस्, युग a pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वासौकस्
वासौकस् n. (-कः) The inner or private apartments.<BR> E. वास dwelling,<BR>ओकस् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्त
वास्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ती-स्तं) Made or derived from a goat.<BR> E. वस्त and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तव|वास्तवं
वास्तव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Determined, demonstrated, fixed, substantia-<BR>ted.<BR>	 2. Real, substantial.<BR>	 n. (-वं) An appointment, anything fixed.<BR>f. (-वा) Dawn.<BR> E. वस्तु thing, substance, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तविक|वास्तविकं|वास्तविकः
वास्तविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Real, material, substantial, genuine.<BR>	 2.<BR>Determinate.<BR> E. वस्तु and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तवोषा
वास्तवोषा f. (-षा) Night.<BR> E. वास्तव an appointment, and ऊषा a libidinous<BR>woman: the season in which she makes an assignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तव्य|वास्तव्यः
वास्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be abided or dwelt in, to be fixed as a<BR>habitation.<BR>	 2. To be taken care of, (as a dependent.)<BR>	 m. (-व्यः) A<BR>kinsman, a dependent.<BR> E. वस् to dwell, causal form, aff. of the<BR>future participle तव्यर् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तु
वास्तु mn. (-स्तुः-स्तु)<BR>	 1. The site of a habitation.<BR>	 2. A house, a habitation.<BR>E. वस् to dwell, Unādi aff. तुन्, and the radical vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तुक|वास्तुकं
वास्तुक n. (-कं) A potherb: see वास्तूक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तुयाग|वास्तुयागः
वास्तुयाग m. (-गः) A religious rite performed on laying the foundation of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तुसंशमन
वास्तुसंशमन n. (-नं) A ceremony or sacrifice performed on entering a<BR>new habitation.<BR> E. वास्तु, संशमन consecration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तुसंशमनीय
वास्तुसंशमनीय n. (-यं) A ceremony performed on entering a new man-<BR>sion.<BR> E. छ added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तूक|वास्तूकं
वास्तूक n. (-कं) A potherb, (Chenopodium album, and other edible spe-<BR>cies.)<BR> E. वास्तु the site of a house, ठक् aff., and form irr. (growing<BR>there;) also with the vowel unaltered वास्तुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तेय|वास्तेयं
वास्तेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Abdominal, relating or belonging to the belly.<BR>2. Fit to be inhabited.<BR> E. वस्ति and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्तोष्पति|वास्तोष्पतिः
वास्तोष्पति m. (-तिः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. वास्तु the site of a dwelling, in<BR>the sixth case, पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्त्र|वास्त्रः
वास्त्र mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं) Cloth, made of or covered with cloth, &c.<BR> E. वस्त्र<BR>cloth, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्प|वास्पः
वास्प m. (-स्पः)<BR>	 1. Vapour.<BR>	 2. Tears; more correctly वाष्प, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्पविक्लव
वास्पविक्लव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Weeping, bursting into tears.<BR> E. वास्प, विक्लव distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वास्पाविलेक्षण
वास्पाविलेक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Suffused with tears, weeping.<BR> E. वास्प, and<BR>आविल turbid, ईक्षण the sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्
वाह्(ऋ)वाहृ r. 1st cl. (वाहते) To endeavour; the root is preferably read बाहृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह|वाहः
वाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. A measure of capacity containing ten<BR>Kumbhas, or nearly equal to the weight of an English wey or a<BR>ton in freight.<BR>	 3. A bull.<BR>	 4. Air, wind.<BR>	 5. The arm.<BR>	 6. A buffalo.<BR>	 7.<BR>A vehicle, a carriage or conveyance of any kind.<BR>	 8. A bearer, a<BR>porter, a carrier of burthens, &c.<BR>	 9. Carrying, bearing.<BR> E. वह् to<BR>bear, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहक|वाहकः
वाहक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A horseman.<BR>	 2. A porter, a carrier.<BR> E. वह् to bear, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहद्विषत्|वाहद्विषन्त्
वाहद्विषत् m. (-षन्) A buffalo.<BR> E. वाह a horse, and द्विषत् inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहन|वाहनं
वाहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A vehicle, a conveyance of any kind, as a horse, an ele-<BR>phant, a carriage.<BR>	 2. Carrying, conveying, &c.<BR>	 3. Making effort or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">Page649-a+ 60</a>]<BR>exertion.<BR> E. वह् to bear, causal form, or वाह् to endeavour, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहभ्रंश्
वाहभ्रंश् mfn. (-भ्रट्) Falling from a vehicle.<BR> E. वाह, भ्रश् to fall, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहयत्
वाहयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Employing, making use of.<BR> E. वह् to bear,<BR>causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहश्रेष्ठ|वाहश्रेष्ठः
वाहश्रेष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहस|वाहसः
वाहस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A large snake, (Boa constrictor)<BR>	 2. A water-course.<BR>3. A potherb, (Marsilia dentata.)<BR> E. वह् to bear, causal form, aff. असच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिक|वाहिकः
वाहिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A large drum.<BR>	 2. A car, &c., drawn by oxen.<BR> E. वह्<BR>to bear, इक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहित|वाहितं
वाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Exerted, endeavoured.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A heavy burden.<BR> E. वाह to endeavour, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहित्थ|वाहित्थं
वाहित्थ n. (-त्थं) The part of an elephant's forehead below the frontal<BR>globes.<BR> E. वाहिन्, स्था to stay, aff. क, and स changed to त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिन्
वाहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि) Bearing, carrying.<BR>	 m. (-ही) A chariot.<BR> E. वह<BR>to bear, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिनी
वाहिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. An army.<BR>	 2. A body of forces consisting of 81 ele-<BR>phants, 81 cars, 243 horse, 405 foot, a cohort, a battalion.<BR>	 3. A<BR>river.<BR> E. वाह a vehicle, &c., aff. इनि; fem. aff. ङीप् comprising the<BR>conveyances of cars, horse, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिनीनिवेश|वाहिनीनिवेशः
वाहिनीनिवेश m. (-शः) A camp.<BR> E. वाहिनी, and निवेश encampment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहिनीपति|वाहिनीपतिः
वाहिनीपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A general, a commanding officer.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR>E. वाहिनी an army or river, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहीक|वाहीकः
वाहीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Of burthen, bearing burthens.<BR>	 2. Outer, ex-<BR>ternal.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The name of a country, part of the Punjāb. E.<BR>वाह bearing, or वहिर् external, aff. ईकक् or ईकन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
वा(बा)ह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. To be carried or borne.<BR>	 2. Outer, external.<BR>n. (-ह्यं) A carriage, a vehicle.<BR>	 m. (-ह्यः) A beast of burthen, an ox,<BR>a horse, &c.<BR> E. वह् to bear, aff. ण्यत्, or वहिर् external, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्यतस्
वाह्यतस् Ind. Externally, solitarily.<BR> E. तसि added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्यमान
वाह्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being carried or conveyed.<BR>	 2. Being induced,<BR>urged, incited, &c.<BR> E. वह् to bear, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लि|वाह्लिः
वाह्लि f. (-ह्लिः) A country: see वाह्लीक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लिक|वाह्लिकं|वाह्लिकः
वाह्लिक m. (-कः) Bālkh: see बाह्लीक.<BR> E. वह-लिण् स्वार्थे क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लिज|वाह्लिजः
वाह्लिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born in Vahli or Vahlika country.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A<BR>Turki-horse.<BR> E. वाह्लि and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लीक|वाह्लीकं|वाह्लीकः
वाह्लीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A country lying north-west of Āfganisthān, Bālkh.<BR>2. A horse from Bālkh, considered as one of a good breed.<BR>	 3.<BR>One of the principal Gandharbas or choristers of heaven.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>1. Saffron.<BR>	 2. Asafœtida.<BR> E. वह्ल् to be pre-eminent, इकन् or ईकन्<BR>aff., वह्लिक or वह्लीक; again, अण् pleonastic or derivative added,<BR>वाह्लिक or वाह्लीक; the conjunct letters of the root being trans-<BR>posed; saffron, &c. are supplied still to India, especially from<BR>Kāshmir, Khorāsān, and the countries in that direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वि|विः
वि mf. (-विः-वी)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. The eye.<BR>	 3. Heaven.<BR>	 4. The region of the<BR>wind.<BR>	 5. A horse. Ind. A particle and prefix, implying:--1. Certain-<BR>ty, ascertainment, as विवेक्तुं to determine, to judge.<BR>	 2. Separation,<BR>disjunction, as वियोक्तुं to disjoin.<BR>	 3. Aversion, repugnance, as विरोद्धुं<BR>to oppose.<BR>	 4. Impatience, intolerance, as विमृष्टुं to be impatient.<BR>	 5.<BR>Variety, difference, विशेष्टुं to distinguish.<BR>	 6. Cause, motive, विधातुं<BR>to prescribe or order.<BR>	 7. Motion, progress, विचरितुं to go.<BR>	 8. Pri-<BR>vation, विणीतुं to take away. It generally corresponds to the Eng-<BR>lish adjuncts, a, ex, de, dis, in, un, &c. and is frequently an<BR>expletive.<BR> E. वा to go, Unādi aff. इन् with the effect of डित् or ड,<BR>which ejects the final syllable; or वा-कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंश|विंशः
विंश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Twentieth.<BR> E. विंशति twenty, and डट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशक|विंशकः
विंशक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Twenty, collectively, or an aggregate of twenty.<BR>E. विंशति, and ड्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशति|विंशतिः
विंशति Always f. sing. (-तिः) Twenty, a score. du. (-ती) Two twenties. plu. (-तयः) Many twenties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशतिक|विंशतिकः
विंशतिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Worth twenty, produced from or bought<BR>with twenty, &c.<BR> E. विंशति twenty, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशतितम|विंशतितमः
विंशतितम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Twentieth.<BR> E. विंशति, तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशतीश|विंशतीशः
विंशतीश m. (-शः) A governor of twenty villages.<BR> E. विंशति, ईश sovereign;<BR>also विंशतीशिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंशिन्
विंशिन् m. (-शी) Twenty, (collectively,) a score.<BR> E. विंशति, and डिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक|विकं
विक n. (-कं) The milk of a prolific cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकङ्कट|विकंकट|विकंकटः|विकङ्कटः
विकङ्कट m. (-टः) A plant, (Ruellia longifolia, &c.:) see गोक्षुर.<BR> E. वि apart, ककि to go, aff. अटन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकङ्कत|विकंकत|विकंकतः|विकङ्कतः
विकङ्कत m. (-तः) A small tree.<BR> E. वि apart, ककि to go or grow, अतच्<BR>aff.; or वि a bird, ककि, &c. as before; on which the birds roost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकच|विकचः
विकच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं)<BR>	 1. Blown, opened, expanded, (as a flower, &c.)<BR>2. Bald, having little or no hair on the head.<BR>	 m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>Bauddha mendicant.<BR>	 2. The planet KETU, or the personified<BR>descending node.<BR> E. वि apart, separate, कच् to go, aff. अच्; or वि<BR>privative, and कच hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकट|विकटः
विकट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Large, great, broad.<BR>	 2. Formidable, frightful,<BR>hideous, horrible.<BR>	 3. Large-toothed.<BR>	 4. Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>	 5.<BR>Changed in form or appearance.<BR>	 6. Obscure, obsolete.<BR>	 n. (-टं) A<BR>boil, a tumour.<BR>	 f. (-टा) A female divinity peculiar to the<BR>Bauddhas.<BR> E. वि implying separation or expansion, कट् to go<BR>or be, aff. अच्, or with कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकण्टक|विकण्टकः
विकण्टक m. (-कः) A herbaceous plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR> E. वि ex-<BR>panding, कण्ट a thorn, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थन|विकत्थनं
विकत्थन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Speaking idly.<BR>	 2. Praising ironically.<BR>	 3.<BR>Vaunting, boastful.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Irony, ironical or unmerited praise.<BR>2. Praise in general.<BR>	 3. Assigning anything to an unreal origin.<BR>4. Boasting.<BR>	 5. Repeating, proclaiming.<BR> E. वि implying difference<BR>or extension, and कत्थन praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थनीय
विकत्थनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be praised, commendable.<BR>	 2. Ridiculous,<BR>to be praised ironically.<BR> E. वि before, कत्थ् to praise, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्था
विकत्था f. (-त्था)<BR>	 1. Praise.<BR>	 2. Irony, ironical praise.<BR>	 3. Boasting.<BR>	 4.<BR>Repeating, proclaiming.<BR> E. वि, कत्थ् to praise, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थिन्
विकत्थिन् mfn. (-त्थी-त्थिनी-त्थि) Who or what boasts, praises, proclaims,<BR>&c.: see विकत्थन.<BR> E. वि, कत्थ् to boast, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकम्प|विकंप
विकम्प mfn. (-म्पः-म्पा-म्पं)<BR>	 1. Trembling.<BR>	 2. Heaving.<BR>	 3. Unsteady, not<BR>firm or continued.<BR>	 4. Shrinking from.<BR> E. वि, and कम्प trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकम्पित|विकंपित|विकम्पितः
विकम्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Trembling, tremulous, agitated.<BR>	 2. Palpi-<BR>tating, heaving.<BR>	 3. Broken, interrupted, unsteady.<BR>	 4. Shrinking<BR>from.<BR> E. वि before, कपि to tremble, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर|विकरः
विकर m. (-रः) Sickness, disease.<BR> E. वि implying difference, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकरण|विकरणः
विकरण m. (-णः) The inserted conjugational affix, (in gram.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकराल|विकरालः
विकराल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Formidable, frightful.<BR> E. वि intensitive, कराल frightful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्ण|विकर्णः
विकर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Ear-less.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) One of the KURŪ princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्णिक|विकर्णिकः
विकर्णिक m. (-कः) Sāraswata, a district in the north-west of Hindusthān,<BR>generally considered as part of the Punjāb, though sometimes<BR>confounded with Kāshmir.<BR> E. वि privative, and कर्ण KARṆA, aff.<BR>ठक्; the region from which KARṆA was proscribed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्त्तन|विकर्तन|विकर्तनः|विकर्त्तनः
विकर्त्तन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A son who has usurped his father's<BR>kingdom.<BR>	 3. The Arka plant.<BR> E. वि before, कृत् to cut, aff. ल्युट्;<BR>having been shorn of some of his beams, by VIŚHWAKARMAN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्म्मकृत्|विकर्मकृत्
विकर्म्मकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Acting illegally, one who does forbidden acts.<BR>	 2.<BR>Busy in various ways.<BR> E. विकर्म्म and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्म्मक्रिया|विकर्मक्रिया
विकर्म्मक्रिया f. (-या) Illegal or immoral act.<BR> E. विकर्म्म, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्म्मन्|विकर्मन्
विकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Various business or duty.<BR>	 2. Prohibited or unlaw-<BR>ful act.<BR>	 3. Fraud.<BR> E. वि and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्म्मस्थ|विकर्मस्थ|विकर्म्मस्थः
विकर्म्मस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Doing what is illegal or immoral, en-<BR>gaged in prohibited acts.<BR>	 2. Engaged in various business.<BR> E. विकर्म्म<BR>and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्म्मिक|विकर्मिक|विकर्मिकः
विकर्म्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Doing forbidden acts.<BR>	 2. Transacting<BR>various affairs.<BR>	 m. (-कः) Clerk or superintendent of markets or<BR>fairs.<BR> E. वि implying variety, कर्म्म business, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्ष|विकर्षः
विकर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Pulling, pulling apart or out.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR> E. वि<BR>separate, कृष् to attract, अच् or घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=649-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्षण|विकर्षणं|विकर्षणः
विकर्षण n. (-णं) Pulling, drawing, dragging.<BR>	 m. (-णः) One of the five<BR>arrows of KĀMA.<BR> E. वि before, कृष् to attract, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल|विकलः
विकल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Confused, confounded, agitated.<BR>	 2. Defective,<BR>imperfect.<BR>	 3. Decayed, impaired, withered, waned.<BR>	 f. (-ला or ली) A<BR>woman in whom menstruation has ceased.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The one-six-<BR>teenth of a Kalā, the second of a degree.<BR> E. वि privative, and कला<BR>a digit of the moon, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलपाणिक|विकलपाणिकः
विकलपाणिक m. (-कः) A cripple with a crooked or withered arm. E.<BR>विकल defective, पाणि the hand, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलाङ्ग|विकलांग|विकलाङ्गः
विकलाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Deformed, crippled, maimed.<BR> E. विकल defective, अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलीकरण|विकलीकरणं
विकलीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Spoiling, breaking, maiming.<BR>	 2. Confusing,<BR>agitating.<BR> E. विकल, and करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलीकृत
विकलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Broken, injured, impaired.<BR>	 2. Sick, lame,<BR>maimed.<BR>	 2. Confused, distressed.<BR> E. विकल and कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलीभूत
विकलीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Agitated, distressed.<BR>	 2. Maimed, defective.<BR>E. विकल and भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकलेन्द्रिय|विकलेंद्रिय
विकलेन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Having any of the organs of sense impaired<BR>or defective.<BR> E. विकल, and इन्द्रिय an organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्प|विकल्पः
विकल्प m. (-ल्पः)<BR>	 1. Error, ignorance, mistake.<BR>	 2. Alternative, option.<BR>	 3.<BR>Doubt, indecision.<BR>	 4. (In rhetoric,) Antithesis of opposites.<BR>	 5. (In<BR>grammar, &c.,) Admission of more than one form or rule.<BR>	 6.<BR>Device.<BR> E. वि distinction, and कल्प making, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पन|विकल्पनं
विकल्पन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Admitting of uncertainty.<BR>	 2. Indecision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पयत्
विकल्पयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Doubting, deliberating, weighing, alter-<BR>natives.<BR> E. वि before, कृप् to be able, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पित
विकल्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made or acknowledged as optional.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore, कृत् to be able, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्मष
विकल्मष f. (-षा) Sinless, guiltless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकश्व
विकश्व(स्व)र mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Opening, expanding.<BR> E. वि separately, कष् to go, वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकषा
विकषा f. (-षा) Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR> E. वि before, कष् to<BR>injure, अच् aff.; also विकसा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकष्वर
विकष्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Opening, expanding.<BR> E. वि before, कष् to go,<BR>aff. वरच्; also विकस्वर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकस|विकसः
विकस m. (-सः) The moon.<BR>	 f. (-सा) Bengal madder.<BR> E. वि before, कस् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकसत्
विकसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Opening, expanding.<BR>	 2. Budding, blow-<BR>ing.<BR> E. वि before, कस् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकसित|विकसितं
विकसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Blown, as a flower, budded, opened, expanded.<BR>E. वि apart, कस् to go, aff. क्त; also विकशित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकस्वर|विकस्वरः
विकस्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Opening, expanding.<BR> E. वि apart, कस् to go, aff.<BR>वरच्; also derived from कश् or कष्, विकश्वर, and विकष्वर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकार|विकारः
विकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Change of form or nature, alteration or deviation<BR>from the natural state.<BR>	 2. Sickness, disease, change from the state<BR>of health.<BR>	 3. Passion, feeling, emotion, transition from the natural<BR>or quiescent condition of the soul.<BR>	 4. Anything evolved from a<BR>previous source, (in Sānkhya Philosophy.)<BR> E. वि implying<BR>alteration, कृ to make, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारित
विकारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Changed, converted, made to undergo a<BR>changing.<BR>	 2. Rendered unfavourable or unfriendly.<BR> E. वि before, कृ<BR>to make, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारिन्
विकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Producing a change.<BR>	 2. Undergoing a<BR>change.<BR> E. वि before, कृ to make, णिनि aff.; or विकार, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाल|विकालः
विकाल m. (-लः) Twilight, the close of day.<BR> E. वि implying prohibition,<BR>(of peculiar ceremonies,) and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकालक|विकालकः
विकालक m. (-कः) Evening, twilight.<BR>	 f. (-लिका) A perforated copper-<BR>vessel, which is placed in a pan of water, and being filled at the<BR>expiration of a certain period, defines that period: a sort of Clep-<BR>sydra, or water-clock. “तांँवी”.<BR> E. वि before, काल time, and कन्<BR>added; or वि before, कल् to go, aff. क्कुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाश|विकाशः
विकाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Solitude, loneliness, privacy.<BR>	 2. Display, manifes-<BR>tation, open or splendid appearance.<BR>	 3. Opening, expanding.<BR>	 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">Page650-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Budding, blowing, (as a flower.)<BR>	 5. Pleasure, enjoyment.<BR>	 6. Ether,<BR>heaven.<BR>	 7. An open course.<BR>	 8. An oblique course.<BR>	 9. Retreat.<BR>	 10.<BR>Eagerness.<BR> E. वि before, काश to shine, aff. घञ्; the vowel of the<BR>prefix is more usually made long: see वीकाश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशता
विकाशता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Appearance, display.<BR>	 2. Loneliness.<BR>	 3. Expansion.<BR>E. विकाश shining, aff. तल्; also with त्व, विकाशत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशन|विकाशनं
विकाशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Expansion, extent.<BR>	 2. Manifestation.<BR>	 3. Blowing,<BR>(of a flower.)<BR> E. विकाश and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशभृत्
विकाशभृत् mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. Expanding, being full.<BR>	 2. Blown, budded. E.<BR>विकाश, भृत् who or what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशिन्
विकाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Expanding, spreading, opening.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, कश् to go, aff. घिनुण्; or काश, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाषिन्
विकाषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Expanding, &c.<BR> E. वि before, कष् to go, aff. घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकासिन्
विकासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Expanding, opening, budding, blowing.<BR>E. वि before, कस् to go, aff. घिनुण्; also with कश् or कष् the same,<BR>विकाशिन् and विकाषिन् as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिर|विकिरः
विकिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bird in general.<BR>	 2. A well.<BR>	 3. A fallen fragment,<BR>a scattered portion.<BR>	 4. Scattering.<BR>	 5. A tree.<BR> E. वि apart, &c., कॄ<BR>to scatter, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिरण|विकिरणं|विकिरणः
विकिरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Scattering, spreading about or abroad.<BR>	 2. Killing.<BR>3. Knowledge.<BR>	 m. (-णः) Gigantic swallow wort, (Asclepias gigan-<BR>tea.)<BR> E. वि before, कॄ to scatter, aff. यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिरत्
विकिरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Throwing, scattering, sprinkling.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore, कृ to scatter, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्ण|विकीर्णः
विकीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Scattered, extended, diffused.<BR>	 2. Cele-<BR>brated, famous.<BR> E. वि implying extension, कृ to scatter, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्य्य|विकीर्य
विकीर्य्य Ind. Having or being scattered.<BR> E. वि, कृ to scatter, aff. ल्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्य्यमाण|विकीर्यमाण
विकीर्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being tossed, agitated, scattered, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, कृ to scatter, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुर्व्वाण|विकुर्वाण|विकुर्व्वाणः
विकुर्व्वाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Joyful, cheerful, happy.<BR>	 2. Undergoing or<BR>making a change of form, &c.<BR> E. वि before, कृ to do, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुस्र|विकुस्रः
विकुस्र m. (-स्रः) The moon.<BR> E. वि before, कस् to shine, रक् Unādi aff.,<BR>and उ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूजन|विकूजनं
विकूजन n. (-नं) Cooing, humming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूणन|विकूणनं
विकूणन n. (-नं) A side-glance, a leer, a wink.<BR> E. वि before, कूण् to con-<BR>tract or close, (the eyes,) aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूणिका
विकूणिका f. (-का) The nose.<BR> E. वि before, कूण् to sound, aff. ण्वुल्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृत|विकृतं
विकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Entertaining the feeling of disgust, averse,<BR>estranged.<BR>	 2. Sick, diseased.<BR>	 3. Altered, changed, either in<BR>form or feeling.<BR>	 4. Imperfect, unfinished, incomplete.<BR>	 5. Over-<BR>come by feeling or passion.<BR>	 6. Strange, extraordinary.<BR>	 7. Loath-<BR>some, hideous.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Disgust, aversion.<BR>	 2. Sickness.<BR>	 3. Change.<BR>E. वि implying reverse, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृतवदन
विकृतवदन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having the face distorted.<BR> E. विकृत, वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृताकार
विकृताकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Changed in aspect, form, or appearance. E.<BR>विकृत and आकार form; also विकृताकृति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृताङ्ग
विकृताङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Distorted, deformed.<BR> E. विकृत, अङ्ग the limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृति|विकृतिः
विकृति f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>	 1. Change of any kind, as of purpose, mind, form,<BR>nature, &c., either permanent or temporary.<BR>	 2. Sickness, disease,<BR>change from the natural or healthy state.<BR>	 3. Fear, apprehension.<BR>4. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 5. A species of metre: the stanza consists of<BR>four lines of two syllables each, variously arranged.<BR> E. वि implying<BR>alteration or reverse, कृ to make, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृष्ट|विकृष्टः
विकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Pulled, drawn, (as a bow-string.)<BR>	 2. Attract-<BR>ed.<BR>	 3. Dragged, drawn. in general.<BR>	 4. Extended, protracted.<BR>	 5.<BR>Sounded, making a noise.<BR> E. वि before, कृष् to draw, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकेश
विकेश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Bald.<BR>	 f. (-शी)<BR>	 1. A small braid or tress of hair,<BR>first tied up severally, and then collected into the Venī or larger<BR>braid.<BR>	 2. A woman without hair.<BR>	 3. A woman with loose hair. E.<BR>वि severally or privative, केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=650-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकेशिका
विकेशिका f. (-का) A pledget, a piece of rag smeared with ghee or other<BR>substances and applied as a dressing to a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकोष|विकोषः
विकोष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Uncovered, denuded, unsheathed.<BR> E. वि pri-<BR>vative, and कोष a sheath, a cover; also विकोश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकौतुक
विकौतुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Incurious, indifferent.<BR> E. वि, कौतुक curious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्क|विक्कः
विक्क m. (-क्कः) A young elephant.<BR> E. विक imitative sound, कै to utter,<BR>aff. ड । विक्कणति वि + क्कण-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रम|विक्रमः
विक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Heroism, prowess, heroic valour.<BR>	 2. Great power or<BR>strength.<BR>	 3. Walking, going, proceeding.<BR>	 4. Overpowering, over-<BR>coming.<BR>	 5. Strength in general.<BR>	 6. A step, a stride, (as in<BR>त्रिविक्रम ।)<BR>	 7. The name of a sovereign of Ougein: see विक्रमादित्य.<BR>E. वि before, क्रम् to go, to move, to walk, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमण|विक्रमणं
विक्रमण n. (-णं) The stride of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रममाण
विक्रममाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Going, proceeding.<BR>	 2. Overpowering.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, क्रम् to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमादित्य|विक्रमादित्यः
विक्रमादित्य m. (-त्यः) The name of a celebrated prince, the sovereign of<BR>Ougein, and reputed founder of an æra still in use amongst the<BR>Hindus, commencing 56 years before the Christian æra; there<BR>are however many princes of this name, and it has been applied<BR>to BHOJA-Rāja, to SĀLIVĀHANA, and PRITHVĪ Rāja, as well as<BR>to five or six others; the name also occurs variously written, as<BR>VIKRAMĀDITYA, VIKRAMASENA, VIKRAMASINHA, VIKRAMĀRKA,<BR>&c.<BR> E. विक्रम power, and आदित्य the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमार्क|विक्रमार्कः
विक्रमार्क m. (-र्कः) A name of the sovereign VIKRAMĀDITYA: see the<BR>last.<BR> E. विक्रम heroism, अर्क the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमार्ज्जित|विक्रमार्जित
विक्रमार्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Conquered, acquired by valour.<BR> E. विक्रम and अर्ज्जित gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमिन्
विक्रमिन् m. (-मी)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. A hero.<BR> E. विक्रम strength, valour, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रय|विक्रयं|विक्रयः
विक्रय m. (-यः) Sale, selling, vending.<BR> E. वि before, क्री to buy, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयानुशय|विक्रयानुशयः
विक्रयानुशय m. (-यः) Rescission of sale.<BR> E. विक्रय, अनुशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयण|विक्रयणं
विक्रयण n. (-णं) Selling, vending.<BR> E. वि reverse, क्री to buy, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयिक|विक्रयिकः
विक्रयिक m. (-कः) A vender, a dealer, a salesman.<BR> E. विक्रय sale, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयिन्
विक्रयिन् m. (-यी) A seller, a vender.<BR> E. विक्रय sale, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रस्र|विक्रस्रः
विक्रस्र m. (-स्रः) The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्त|विक्रांत|विक्रान्तं|विक्रान्तः
विक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Valiant, mighty.<BR>	 2. Overcoming victorious.<BR>m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A hero, a warrior.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Valour.<BR>	 2. A<BR>step, a stride.<BR> E. वि before, क्रम् to go, aff. क्त, in an active sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्ति|विक्रांति|विक्रांतिः|विक्रान्तिः
विक्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. A horse's canter or gallop.<BR>	 2. Prowess, heroic<BR>strength and valour.<BR>	 3. Great power or strength.<BR>	 4. Striding. E.<BR>वि before, क्रम् to go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्तृ|विक्रांतृ
विक्रान्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ)<BR>	 1. Valiant.<BR>	 2. Victorious.<BR>	 m. (-न्ता) A hero, a<BR>victor.<BR> E. वि before, क्रम् to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रायक|विक्रायकः
विक्रायक m. (-कः) A vender, a seller.<BR> E. वि before, कृ to buy, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रिया
विक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Change of mind, form, purpose, condition, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Emotion, perturbation, passion.<BR>	 3. Anger, dis-satisfaction.<BR>	 4.<BR>Contraction.<BR>	 5. Vitiation, intermixture.<BR> E. वि implying reverse,<BR>and क्रिया action: see विकार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रीत|विक्रीतः
विक्रीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sold.<BR> E. वि before, क्री to buy, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रीय
विक्रीय Ind. Having sold.<BR> E. वि before, कृ to buy, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रुष्ट|विक्रुष्टं
विक्रुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Harsh, rugged or unkind, (as speech.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Called out, exclaimed.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. A cry of alarm or for help.<BR>	 2.<BR>Abuse.<BR> E. वि before, क्रुश् to call, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रेतृ
विक्रेतृ m. (-ता) A vender, a seller.<BR> E. वि before, क्री to buy, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रेय|विक्रेयं
विक्रेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Vendible, saleable.<BR> E. वि before, क्री to buy, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रोशन|विक्रोशनं
विक्रोशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Abusing, reviling.<BR>	 2. Calling out.<BR> E. वि before, क्रुश्<BR>to curse, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रोष्टृ
विक्रोष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>	 1. Who reviles, abuses, speaks harshly, &c.<BR>2. Who calls or cries out.<BR> E. वि before, क्रुश् to cry, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लव|विक्लवः
विक्लव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Overcome with fear or agitation, confused, con-<BR>founded, lost, bewildered.<BR> E. वि before, क्लु to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लवता
विक्लवता f. (-ता) Timidity, fear.<BR> E. विक्लव, तल् aff.; also with त्व, विक्लवत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लिन्न|विक्लिन्नः
विक्लिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Old.<BR>	 2. Withered, shrivelled, decayed.<BR>	 3. Wet,<BR>moist.<BR> E. वि before, क्लिद् to moisten, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लिष्ट
विक्लिष्ट f. (-ष्टा) Afflicted, distressed, injured.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) A fault in pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षण
विक्षण Adv.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Momentarily, for a moment.<BR> E. वि, क्षण a moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षत|विक्षतः
विक्षत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Struck, hurt, wounded.<BR> E. वि before, क्षत torn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षाव|विक्षावः
विक्षाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Cough.<BR>	 2. Sound.<BR> E. वि before, क्षु to sound, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षिपत्
विक्षिपत् mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>	 1. Throwing, tossing.<BR>	 2. Agitating.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, क्षिप् to throw, and शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षिप्त|विक्षिप्तः
विक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Scattered, dispersed.<BR>	 2. Thrown, cast.<BR>	 3.<BR>Agitated, bewildered, perplexed.<BR>	 4. Sent, dispatched.<BR>	 5. Refuted,<BR>falsified.<BR> E. वि severally, क्षिप्त thrown or sent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षीण
विक्षीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Wasted, destroyed.<BR> E. वि before, क्षै to decay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षीणक|विक्षीणकः
विक्षीणक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The chief of a class of demigods, enumerated<BR>amongst those attached to ŚIVA, and the ministers of destruction<BR>amongst men by plague, pestilence, &c.<BR>	 2. A meeting or assembly<BR>of the gods.<BR>	 3. A place prohibited to eaters of meat.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>क्षीण wasted, (by whom,) and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षीर|विक्षीरः
विक्षीर m. (-रः) The Arka plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेप|विक्षेपः
विक्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Casting, or throwing away.<BR>	 2. Sending, dispatching.<BR>3. Confusion, perplexity, fear proceeding from ignorance or<BR>error.<BR>	 4. Looking about vaguely or wildly, as of a woman for her<BR>absent lover.<BR>	 5. Refuting an argument, establishing its falsehood.<BR>6. Celestial latitude.<BR> E. वि before, क्षिप् to throw, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेपण|विक्षेपणं
विक्षेपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Scattering, dispersing.<BR>	 2. Sending, dispatching.<BR>	 3.<BR>Throwing.<BR>	 4. Confusion.<BR> E. वि before, क्षिप् to throw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेपध्रुव|विक्षेपध्रुवः
विक्षेपध्रुव m. (-वः) (In astronomy), The greatest inclination of a planet's<BR>orbit.<BR> E. विक्षेप, ध्रुव an arc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षोभ|विक्षोभः
विक्षोभ n. (-भं)<BR>	 1. Agitating, shaking.<BR>	 2. Conflict, struggle.<BR>	 3. Fearing.<BR>E. वि before, क्षुभ् to stir, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख|विखः
विख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Noseless; also विखु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखण्डित|विखंडित
विखण्डित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Broken, divided.<BR>	 2. Refuted.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>खण्डित the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखासा
विखासा f. (-सा) The tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखु|विखुः
विखु mfn. (-खुः-खुः-खुः) Noseless; also बिखु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखुर|विखुरः
विखुर m. (-रः) A goblin, a demon, a Rākshasa.<BR>	 2. A thief.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>खुर् to cut, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्य|विख्यः
विख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं) Noseless.<BR> E. वि privative prefix, and ख्य substi-<BR>tuted, for नस or नासिका; also other as arbitrary terms, or विख,<BR>विग्र, बिग्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्यात|विख्यातः
विख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, famous.<BR>	 2. Avowed, confessed.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, ख्या to say or tell, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्याति|विख्यातिः
विख्याति f. (-तिः) Fame, celebrity.<BR> E. वि before, ख्या to say, or tell, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्यापन|विख्यापनं
विख्यापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Confessing, acknowledging, avowing, declaring.<BR>	 2.<BR>Explaining, expounding.<BR> E. वि, ख्या to say, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्र|विख्रः
विख्र mfn. (-ख्रः-ख्रा-ख्रं) Noseless; also विख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्रु|विख्रुः
विख्रु mfn. (-ख्रुः-ख्रुः-ख्रु) Noseless; also विख and विखु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगणन|विगणनं
विगणन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Reckoning, computing.<BR>	 2. Considering, deliberating.<BR>3. Discharge of a debt.<BR> E. वि before, गणन counting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगणय्य
विगणय्य Ind.<BR>	 1. Having deliberated or weighed.<BR>	 2. Having reckoned.<BR>E. वि before, गण् to number, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगणित
विगणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Reckoned, calculated.<BR>	 2. Weighed, consi-<BR>dered.<BR>	 3. Discharged, (as a debt.)<BR> E. वि before, गण् to count, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगत|विगतः
विगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone, departed, disappeared.<BR>	 2. Separated,<BR>severed, parted.<BR>	 3. Freed or exempt from.<BR>	 4. Lost.<BR>	 5. Gloomy,<BR>dark, obscured.<BR>	 6. Dead.<BR> E. वि implying disunion, (of light, &c.)<BR>गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतकल्मष
विगतकल्मष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. Pure, righteous.<BR>	 2. Unsoiled.<BR> E. विगत and कल्मष sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतज्वर
विगतज्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Exempted from decay.<BR>	 2. Cured of fever. E.<BR>विगत and ज्वरा decay, or ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतराग
विगतराग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Devoid of passion or affection.<BR> E. विगतं and राग passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=651-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतश्रीक|विगतश्रीकः
विगतश्रीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unfortunate, unprosperous.<BR> E. विगत gone, श्री<BR>prosperity, कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतस्पृह
विगतस्पृह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Indifferent, devoid of wish or desire.<BR> E. विगत, स्पृहा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतार्त्तवा|विगतार्तवा
विगतार्त्तवा f. (-वा) A woman past child-bearing.<BR> E. विगत gone, आर्त्तव the<BR>menstrual excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगम|विगमः
विगम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Separation, parting.<BR>	 2. Destruction, death.<BR>	 3. Relin-<BR>quishment.<BR> E. वि apart, and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर|विगरः
विगर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An abstemious man, one who feeds on wind.<BR>	 2. A<BR>naked man.<BR>	 3. A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हण|विगर्हणं
विगर्हण nf. (-णं-णा) Abuse, abusing, censure, reproach.<BR> E. वि before, गर्ह<BR>to abuse, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हणीय
विगर्हणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Bad, wicked, reprehensible.<BR> E. वि before, गर्ह् to abuse, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हित|विगर्हितः
विगर्हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Abused, reviled.<BR>	 2. Low, vile.<BR>	 3. Bad, wicked.<BR>4. Condemned, reprobated.<BR> E. वि before, गर्ह् to abuse, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्ह्य
विगर्ह्य mfn. (र्ह्यः-र्ह्या-र्ह्यं) Blamable, reprehensible. Ind. Having blamed<BR>or reviled.<BR> E. वि before, गर्ह् to abuse, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्ह्यकथा
विगर्ह्यकथा f. (-था) Scandal, abuse.<BR> E. विगर्ह्य and कथा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगलत्
विगलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>	 1. Oozing, dropping, flowing.<BR>	 2. Fading,<BR>dispersing, weakening, (as emotion, &c.)<BR> E. वि before, गल् to ooze,<BR>शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगलित|विगलितः
विगलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, dropped, oozed, flowing.<BR>	 2. Removed,<BR>gone.<BR>	 3. Dissipated, dispersed.<BR>	 4. Decayed, impaired.<BR>	 5. Slackened,<BR>united, (as a knot.)<BR>	 6. Loose, disordered, (as dress.)<BR>	 7. Dissolved.<BR>E. वि before, गल् to ooze, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगलितकेश
विगलितकेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Having the hair dishevelled.<BR> E. विगलित, केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाढ|विगाढः
विगाढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Immersed, plunged, bathing.<BR>	 2. Much, excess-<BR>ive, deep.<BR>	 3. Flowing copiously.<BR> E. वि, गाह् to bathe, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगान|विगानं
विगान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Ill-report, detraction, scandal.<BR>	 2. Censure, reproach.<BR>E. वि depreciative prefix, गै to sing or sound, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाह|विगाहः
विगाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Bathing.<BR>	 2. Plunging into, literally or figuratively,<BR>(as water, a crowd, &c.) वि before, गाह् to bathe, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाहमान|विगाहमानः
विगाहमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Beholding, perceiving.<BR>	 2. Knowing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Bathing.<BR>	 4. Going, proceeding.<BR> E. वि, गाह् to agitate, aff. शानच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाह्य
विगाह्य Ind. Having bathed or plunged in.<BR> E. वि, गाह् to agitate, ल्यप aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगीत
विगीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Contradicted, contradictory, inconsistent.<BR>	 2.<BR>Abused, censured, reproached.<BR>	 3. Sung or said in various ways.<BR>4. Sung ill.<BR> E. वि, and गीत sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगीति|विगीतिः
विगीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Reproach, censure, abuse.<BR>	 2. Contradiction.<BR>	 3. Sing-<BR>ing in various styles.<BR>	 4. Singing ill.<BR> E. वि, and गीति singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगुण|विगुणः
विगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Void of all qualities.<BR>	 2. Bad, worthless,<BR>having no merit.<BR>	 3. Having no string.<BR> E. वि, and गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगूढ|विगूढः
विगूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Concealed, hidden.<BR>	 2. Blamed, reproached,<BR>censured.<BR> E. वि before, गुह् to conceal, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगृहोत
विगृहोत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Opposed, obstructed, prevented.<BR>	 2. Encoun-<BR>tered, (as in fight.)<BR>	 3. Seized.<BR>	 4. Separated, dissolved, (as a com-<BR>pound.)<BR> E. वि before, ग्रह् to seize, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगृह्य
विगृह्य ind. Having warred or contended with.<BR> E. वि before, ग्रह् to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगृह्यमाण
विगृह्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being warred upon or contended with. E.<BR>वि before, ग्रह् to take, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्र|विग्रः
विग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं) Noseless.<BR> E. वि privative prefix, and ग्र substituted for नासिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रह|विग्रहः
विग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. Extension, expansion, diffusion.<BR>	 3. A<BR>portion, a part.<BR>	 4. Shape, form, figure.<BR>	 5. (A grammatical term,)<BR>The proper application or sense of a compound word, resolution,<BR>analysis, separation.<BR>	 mn. (-हः-हं)<BR>	 1. War, battle, hostility, (consi-<BR>dered as one of the six modes of foreign policy.)<BR>	 2. Quarrel.<BR>	 3. Dis-<BR>favour.<BR>	 4. Opposition, encounter.<BR> E. वि various, (happiness, &c.) ग्रह्<BR>to take, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रहावर|विग्रहावरं
विग्रहावर n. (-रं) The back.<BR> E. विग्रह the body, अवर the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्राह्य
विग्राह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be warred or contended with.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>ग्रह् to take, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघटन|विघटनं
विघटन n. (-नं) Ruin, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघटिका
विघटिका f. (-का) Sixtieth part of a Gharī, equal to 24 seconds.<BR> E. वि,<BR>घटिका a Gharī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघटित
विघटित f. (-ता) Divided, separated.<BR> E. वि + घट-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्टन|विघट्टनं
विघट्टन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Rubbing, friction.<BR>	 2. Striking, asunder.<BR>	 3. Opening,<BR>undoing, untying.<BR>	 4. Offending.<BR> E. वि, घट्ट् to rub, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्टित|विघट्टितं
विघट्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rubbed, touched.<BR>	 2. Offended.<BR>	 3. Struck.<BR>	 4.<BR>Untied, undone.<BR> E. वि before, घट्ट् to rub, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघन|विघनः
विघन m. (-नः) A mallet, a hammer, an implement for striking.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, हन् to strike, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघस|विघसं|विघसः
विघस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The residue of food offered to the gods, to the manes,<BR>to a venerable guest, &c.<BR>	 2. Food in general.<BR>	 n. (-सं) Bee's-wax. E.<BR>वि before, अद to eat, aff. अप् or घञ्, घस substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघसाश|विघसाशः
विघसाश m. (-शः) One who eats the remains of an offering.<BR> E. विघस, आश<BR>eating; also विघसाशिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघात|विघातः
विघात mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>	 1. Impediment, obstacle.<BR>	 2. Prohibition or preven-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Opposition.<BR>	 4. Destruction.<BR>	 5. A blow.<BR>	 6. Killing.<BR>	 7.<BR>Abandoning.<BR> E. वि before, हन् to kill or hurt, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघातसिद्धि|विघातसिद्धिः
विघातसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Removing obstacles or impediments.<BR> E. विघात and<BR>सिद्धि attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघातिन्
विघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>	 1. Opposing, impeding, preventing.<BR>	 2. Re-<BR>moving, destroying.<BR>	 2. Wounding, killing.<BR> E. वि before, हन् to<BR>hurt or strike, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघुष्ट
विघुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Cried, proclaimed.<BR> E. वि before, घुष्ट cried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघुष्य
विघुष्य Ind. Having proclaimed.<BR> E. वि before, घुष् to cry, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघूर्णित
विघूर्णित f. (-ता) Rolling, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघोषण
विघोषण n. (-णं) Proclamation, crying.<BR> E. वि before, घुष् to cry aloud, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्न|विघ्नः
विघ्न m. (-घ्नः)<BR>	 1. Obstacle, impediment.<BR>	 2. Difficulty, trouble.<BR>	 3. The<BR>caronda, (Carissa Carondas.)<BR> E. वि before, हन् to be injured, (by<BR>it,) and क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नकर
विघ्नकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Opposing, impeding, obstructing.<BR> E. विघ्न and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नकारिन्
विघ्नकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Impeding, obstructing.<BR>	 2. Fearful, for-<BR>midable, terrible.<BR> E. विघ्न an obstacle, and कारिन् causing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्ननाशक|विघ्ननाशकः
विघ्ननाशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what removes difficulties, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. विघ्न, नाशक who or what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्ननाशन|विघ्ननाशनः
विघ्ननाशन n. (-नं) Removing obstacles.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A name of GAṆEŚA. E.<BR>विघ्न an obstacle, and नाशन removing; the deity being supposed<BR>capable of either causing or removing difficulties and impedi-<BR>ments, and being therefore especially worshipped at the com-<BR>mencement of any undertaking; also other similar compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नराज|विघ्नराजः
विघ्नराज m. (-जः) GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. विघ्न an obstacle, राज ruler: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नलेश
विघ्नलेश m. (-शः) Slight obstacle or impediment.<BR> E. विघ्न, लेश a little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नविनायक|विघ्नविनायकः
विघ्नविनायक m. (-कः) GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. विघ्न an obstacle, विनायक remover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नसिद्धि|विघ्नसिद्धिः
विघ्नसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Removal of obstacles.<BR> E. विघ्न, सिद्धि accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नहारिन्
विघ्नहारिन् m. (-री) GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. विघ्न, हारिन् who removes: see विघ्ननाशन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नित|विघ्नितः
विघ्नित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stopped, prevented, impeded.<BR> E. विघ्न, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नेश|विघ्नेशः
विघ्नेश m. (-शः) GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. विघ्न an obstacle, ईश lord: see विघ्ननाशन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विङ्ख|विंख|विंखः|विङ्खः
विङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः) A horse's hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्
विच्(औइर्)औ विचिर् r. 7th cl. (विनक्ति विंक्ते)<BR>	 1. To differ, to be sepa-<BR>rate or distinct.<BR>	 2. To divide, to separate, especially in judgment.<BR>to discriminate, to judge. With वि, 1. To divide.<BR>	 2. To discrimi-<BR>nate.<BR>	 3. To describe.<BR>	 4. To tear up, to remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचकिल|विचकिलः
विचकिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A kind of jasmine.<BR>	 2. A flower, commonly Dona,<BR>(Artemisia:) see दमन.<BR>	 3. A shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR> E. वि<BR>before, चक् to be satisfied, इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचक्षण|विचक्षणः
विचक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Clever, able, wise, sensible.<BR>	 2. Proficient,<BR>skilful.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A learned Brāhman or Paṇḍit, a holy teacher. E.<BR>वि before, चक्ष् to speak, (sensibly,) and युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचक्षुम्
विचक्षुम् mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु)<BR>	 1. Blind.<BR>	 2. Sad, perplexed.<BR> E. वि privative, चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचय|विचयः
विचय m. (-यः) Search, research.<BR> E. वि before, चि to collect, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=652-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचयन|विचयनं
विचयन n. (-नं) Search, research, &c.<BR> E. वि before, चि to collect, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचरत्|विचरन्त्
विचरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Wandering, roaming, going about.<BR> E. वि<BR>variously, चर् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचर्च्चिका|विचर्चिका
विचर्च्चिका f. (-का) Herpes, itch, scab.<BR> E. वि before, चर्च्च् to speak or tell, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचर्चित
विचर्चित f. (-ता) Anointed, smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचल|विचलः
विचल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Unsteady, unfixed, moving, going.<BR>	 2. Con-<BR>ceited.<BR> E. वि before, चल् to move, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचलत्
विचलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्) Moving, going, shaking, waving.<BR> E. वि before, चल् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचलन|विचलनं
विचलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Fickleness, unsteadiness.<BR>	 2. Self-praise, conceit.<BR>	 3.<BR>Deviating from.<BR> E. वि before, चल् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचलित|विचलितः
विचलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone, departed.<BR>	 2. Deviated from.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, चल् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचार|विचारः
विचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The exercise of judgment or reason on a present<BR>object, investigation, consideration, deliberation.<BR>	 2. Dispute, dis-<BR>cussion.<BR>	 3. Selection.<BR>	 4. Doubt, hesitation.<BR>	 5. Prudence.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore, चर् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारक|विचारकः
विचारक m. (-कः) An investigator a judge.<BR> E. वि before, चर् to go, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारकता
विचारकता f. (-ता) Investigation, discussion.<BR> E. तल् added to the last;<BR>also with त्व, विचारकत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारकर्त्तृ|विचारकर्तृ
विचारकर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) A judge, an investigator.<BR> E. विचार, कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारण|विचारणं
विचारण nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>	 1. Deliberation, investigation, the exercise of judg-<BR>ment, or decision after due examination or discussion.<BR>	 2. Doubt,<BR>hesitation.<BR>	 f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. The Mimānsa system of philosophy.<BR>	 2.<BR>Doubt.<BR>	 3. Examination, &c.<BR> E. वि, चर् to go, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारणीय|विचारणीयं
विचारणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be discussed or investigated.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>चर् to go, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारभू
विचारभू f. (-भूः)<BR>	 1. The judgment seat of Yama, the judge of the dead.<BR>2. Any meeting for literary or judicial investigation.<BR> E. विचार<BR>discussion or judgment, and भू place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारस्थल
विचारस्थल n. (-लं) A logical disputation.<BR>	 2. A tribunal.<BR> E. विचार, स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारित|विचारितः
विचारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Judged, discussed.<BR>	 2. Determined, decided.<BR>3. Examined.<BR> E. विचार discussion, aff. इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारिन्
विचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Judging.<BR> E. वि before, चर् to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचार्य्य|विचार्य|विचार्य्यं
विचार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be discussed, weighed, deliberated. Ind.<BR>Having deliberated.<BR> E. वि before, चर् to go, causal v., ण्यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचार्य्यमाण|विचार्यमाण
विचार्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being investigated or discussed.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, चर् to go, passive v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचाल|विचालं|विचालः
विचाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Intervening, intermediate.<BR> E. वि disjunctive pre-<BR>fix, चल् to go, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचि|विचिः
विचि f. (-चिः-ची) A wave.<BR> E. वि before, चि to collect, क्विप् aff.; or विच्-इक्; also वीची ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिकित्सा
विचिकित्सा f. (-त्सा)<BR>	 1. Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>	 2. Error, mistake.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, कित् to doubt, in the reduplicate form, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित
विचित f. (-ता) Searched through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्र|विचित्रं|विचित्रः
विचित्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Variegated, spotted.<BR>	 2. Painted, coloured.<BR>	 3.<BR>Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 4. Wonderful, surprising.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Varie-<BR>gated, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. Surprise.<BR>	 3. Speech implying apparently<BR>the reverse of the object intended.<BR> E. वि before, चित्र variegated, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रक|विचित्रकः
विचित्रक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Wonderful, surprising.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Astonishment,<BR>wonder.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The birch-tree.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रचीनांशुक
विचित्रचीनांशुक n. (-कं) Watered China-silk.<BR> E. विचित्र, चीनांशुक China-cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रता
विचित्रता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Wonder, wonderfulness.<BR>	 2. Being variegated, va-<BR>riety of colour or tint, &c.<BR> E. विचित्र, तल् aff.; also with त्व, विचित्रत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रदेह|विचित्रदेहः
विचित्रदेह mfn. (-हः-ही-हं)<BR>	 1. Having the body painted, &c.<BR>	 2. Elegant.<BR>m. (-हः) A cloud.<BR> E. विचित्र spotted, variegated, (with different<BR>tints,) and देह the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रवीर्य्य|विचित्रवीर्य|विचित्रवीर्यः|विचित्रवीर्य्यः
विचित्रवीर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A sovereign, the 22nd monarch of the lunar<BR>dynasty in the third age, the son of ŚĀNTANU and husband of<BR>PĀNDU'S mother.<BR> E. विचित्र wonderful, वीर्य्य power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रवीर्य्यसू|विचित्रवीर्यसू
विचित्रवीर्य्यसू f. (-सूः) The mother of VICHITRAVĪRYA by ŚĀNTANU; also<BR>of VYĀSA by PARĀŚARA.<BR> E. विचित्रवीर्य्य as above, and सू the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्राङ्ग|विचित्रांग|विचित्राङ्गः
विचित्राङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Elegant, well-formed, handsome.<BR>	 2. Hav-<BR>ing the body of various colours.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2. A tiger.<BR>E. विचित्र variegated or beautiful, अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रित|विचित्रितः
विचित्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wonderful.<BR>	 2. Painted, variegated.<BR> E. विचित्र, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्त्य
विचिन्त्य Ind. Having reflected.<BR> E. वि before, चित् to think, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्त्यमान
विचिन्त्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being to be thought or considered.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore, चिति to think, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्वत्
विचिन्वत् mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्) Thinking, considering.<BR> E. वि before, चि to collect, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्वत्क|विचिन्वत्कः
विचिन्वत्क m. (-त्कः)<BR>	 1. A hero.<BR>	 2. Discrimination, judging.<BR>	 3. Search. E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्वान
विचिन्वान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Thinking, considering, &c.<BR> E. वि before, चि to collect, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचीर्ण
विचीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Entered.<BR>	 2. Occupied or inhabited by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेतन
विचेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Unconscious, senseless, lifeless.<BR> E. वि priv., चेतना sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेतस्
विचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः)<BR>	 1. Sad, perplexed, unhappy.<BR>	 2. Ignorant,<BR>stupid.<BR> E. वि implying privation, चेतस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेष्टित|विचेष्टितः
विचेष्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Investigated, ascertained, inquired into or<BR>looked after.<BR>	 2. Struggled.<BR>	 3. Inconsiderate, ill-judged.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Evil or malicious act.<BR>	 2. Exertion, effort.<BR>	 3. Machination.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore, चेष्टित sought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छ्|विछ्
विच्छ् r. 6th cl. (विच्छायति-ते or विच्छति) To go or approach, (the form<BR>when it takes the augment आय) is rarely used.) r. 10th cl. (विच्छयति-<BR>ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छन्द|विच्छंद|विच्छंदः|विच्छन्दः|विछन्द
विच्छन्द m. (-न्दः) A building of several stories, and surrounded by a<BR>portico, or having a portico to the east and west only; a palace,<BR>a temple.<BR> E. वि before, छन्द wish, will; also with कन् added विच्छन्दक;<BR>and when derived from छृदि to be splendid, with वुन् aff. विच्छर्दक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छर्द्दक|विच्छर्दक|विच्छर्दकः|विच्छर्द्दकः|विछर्द्दक
विच्छर्द्दक m. (-कः) A large and handsome building, the temple of a<BR>god, or the palace of a prince: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छर्द्दन|विच्छर्दन|विच्छर्दनं|विछर्द्दन
विच्छर्द्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Disregarding.<BR>	 2. Wasting.<BR>	 3. Being sick.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, छृदि to vomit, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छर्द्दित|विच्छर्दित|विछर्द्दित
विच्छर्द्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Disregarded, neglected.<BR>	 2. Diminished,<BR>impaired.<BR>	 3. Vomited.<BR> E. वि before, छृद् to vomit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छाय|विच्छायं|विच्छायः|विछाय
विच्छाय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. The shadow of a flock of birds.<BR>	 2. A gem.<BR> E. वि a bird,<BR>छाय a shadow, which in this sort of compound becomes neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छित्ति|विच्छित्तिः
विच्छित्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Cutting, cutting off, excision.<BR>	 2. Dividing, frac-<BR>ture.<BR>	 3. Separation or absence.<BR>	 4. Loss, disappearance, destruc-<BR>tion.<BR>	 5. Cæsura, pause in a verse.<BR>	 6. The boundary or limits of a<BR>house, &c.<BR>	 7. A property of the Nāyīkā or mistress, carelessness<BR>or irregularity in dress and decoration through flurry and agita-<BR>tion.<BR>	 7. Colouring the body with coloured unguents.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>छिद् to cut, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिन्न|विच्छिन्नः
विच्छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्नी-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Cut, separated, severed.<BR>	 2. Absent or sepa-<BR>rated from.<BR>	 3. Divided, parted, portioned.<BR>	 4. Shared, divided<BR>equally.<BR>	 5. Crooked, curved.<BR>	 6. Scattered, dispersed.<BR>	 7. Hidden<BR>or cut off from view, intercepted.<BR>	 8. Broken.<BR>	 9. Ceased, ended.<BR>	 10.<BR>Smeared with unguents.<BR> E. वि apart, छिद् to cut, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छुरित|विछुरित
विच्छुरित f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Coated, covered.<BR>	 2. Inlaid.<BR>	 3. Anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेद|विच्छेदः
विच्छेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Separation, disjunction, removal.<BR>	 2. Prohibition.<BR>prevention.<BR>	 3. Dividing, cutting.<BR>	 4. The division of a book, a sec-<BR>tion.<BR>	 5. Space, interval.<BR>	 6. Dissension, difference.<BR>	 7. Interruption.<BR>8. Termination.<BR>	 9. Removal.<BR> E. वि before, छिद् to cut, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदक
विच्छेदक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What separates, divides, cuts, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>A sector, a cutter.<BR> E. वि before, छिद् to cut, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदन|विच्छेदनं
विच्छेदन n. (-नं) Separating, severing, dividing.<BR> E. वि before, छिद् to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदनीय
विच्छेदनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Divisible, to be divided or separated.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, छिद् to cut, aff. अनीयर् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्युत|विच्युतः
विच्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown or supplied off.<BR>	 2. Fallen or devia-<BR>ted from.<BR>	 3. Neglecting.<BR>	 4. Sloughed.<BR> E. वि before, च्युत fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्युति|विच्युतिः
विच्युति f. (-तिः or ती)<BR>	 1. Decay, decline.<BR>	 2. Separation.<BR>	 3. Failure, mis-<BR>carriage.<BR>	 4. Deviation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=653-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्
विज्(औ इर)औविजिर r. 3rd cl. (वेवेक्ति, वेविक्ते)<BR>	 1. To be distinct or separate,<BR>to differ.<BR>	 2. To separate or divide, especially by reason; to judge,<BR>to distinguish, to discriminate. (ओ, ई,) ओविजी r. 6th cl. (विजते, or<BR>usually with उद् prefixed उद्विजते) also r. 7th cl. (विनक्ति)<BR>	 1. To fear,<BR>to be afraid.<BR>	 2. To tremble with fear.<BR>	 3. To shake or tremble.<BR>	 4.<BR>To be agitated or distressed. With उद्, 1. To fear.<BR>	 2. To be dis-<BR>gusted.<BR>	 3. To be sorry.<BR>	 4. To frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन|विजनः
विजन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Private, lonely, solitary.<BR> E. वि privative, and जन man, people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजनन|विजननं
विजनन n. (-नं) Birth, bearing, delivery.<BR> E. वि, जन् to be born, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजनित
विजनित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Born, begotten.<BR> E. वि, जन् to be born, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन्मन्
विजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) A man born from a degraded Vaiśya.<BR> E. वि, जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजपिल|विजपिलं
विजपिल n. (-लं) Mud.<BR> E. विज + क पिल-क कर्म० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजय|विजयः
विजय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Victory, triumph, conquest.<BR>	 2. A name of ARJUNA.<BR>3. A divine car or chariot of the gods.<BR>	 4. The father of the<BR>twenty-first Jina.<BR>	 5. One of the persons named ŚUKLA BĀLAS by<BR>the Jainas.<BR>	 6. The god of Hades, YAMA.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>	 1. An epithet of<BR>the goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. One of the female friends or attendants of<BR>DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. One of the wives of YAMA.<BR>	 4. Hemp, (Cannabis sativa,)<BR>or the tops of the plant used as a narcotic.<BR>	 5. Yellow myrobalan,<BR>(Terminalia chebula.)<BR>	 6. Orris root.<BR>	 7. A peculiar lunar day; the<BR>third, eighth, or thirteenth of a fortnight; it is also applied to<BR>the tenth day of the light-half of the month Āshwin, (Sept-Oct.)<BR>on which the image of DURGĀ, set up during the great festival in<BR>honour of her, is cast into the water.<BR> E. वि before, जि to conquer,<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयकुञ्जर|विजयकुंजर|विजयकुञ्जरः
विजयकुञ्जर m. (-रः) A royal or war-elephant.<BR> E. विजय victory, कुञ्जर an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयच्छन्द|विजयच्छन्दः|विजयछन्द
विजयच्छन्द m. (-न्दः) A kind of necklace, one of 504 rows or strings. E.<BR>विजय triumph, &c. and छन्द covering, from छदि, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयनन्दन|विजयनन्दनः
विजयनन्दन m. (-नः) A sovereign of the race of IKSHWĀKU.<BR> E. विजय<BR>victory or a proper name, and नन्दन the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयमर्द्दल|विजयमर्दल|विजयमर्दलः|विजयमर्द्दलः
विजयमर्द्दल m. (-लः) A large military drum.<BR> E. विजय victory, मर्द्दल a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयमान
विजयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Victorious, triumphant.<BR> E. वि before, जि to<BR>conquer, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयसिद्धि|विजयसिद्धिः
विजयसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Success, victory.<BR> E. विजय, सिद्धि accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयासप्तमी
विजयासप्तमी f. (-मी) The seventh day of the light-half of a month fall-<BR>ing on a Sunday.<BR> E. विजया victory, सप्तमी the seventh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयिन्
विजयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Victorious, triumphant, conquering, a con-<BR>queror.<BR> E. विजय and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयिन|विजयिनं
विजयिन n. (-नं) Sauce mixed with the water of boiled-rice; also विजिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजर|विजरः
विजर n. (-रं) A stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल|विजलं
विजल n. (-लं) Sauce, &c. mixed with rice-water or gruel.<BR> E. विज् to<BR>shake, aff. कलच्; also विजिल, विज्जन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल्प|विजल्पः
विजल्प m. (-ल्पः)<BR>	 1. Talk, speech.<BR>	 2. A malicious speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजात|विजातः
विजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Born severally.<BR>	 2. Base-born, of mixed origin.<BR>3. Transformed.<BR>	 f. (-ता) The mother of children, a matron.<BR> E. वि<BR>severally, जात born, (from whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजाति|विजातिः
विजाति f. (-तिः) A different species or tribe.<BR> E. वि and जाति sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजातीय|विजातीयः
विजातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Of a different caste.<BR>	 2. Of mixed origin.<BR>	 3.<BR>Dissimilar, of a different sort or nature.<BR> E. वि, जाती caste, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजानत्
विजानत् mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्)<BR>	 1. Possessing various or extended know-<BR>ledge.<BR>	 2. Knowing, understanding<BR> E. वि, ज्ञा to know, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीष|विजिगीषः
विजिगीष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Desirous of victory, emulative, anxious to<BR>overcome or conquer, &c.<BR> E. वि before, जि to conquer, in the<BR>desiderative form, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषा
विजिगीषा f. (-षा) Competition, emulation, wish to surpass, or subdue.<BR>E. जि to conquer, with वि prefixed, desid. v., अङ्, and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषु|विजिगीषुः
विजिगीषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Desirous to conquer or overcome.<BR>	 m. (-षुः)<BR>	 1.<BR>A warrior.<BR>	 2. An invader, an antagonist.<BR>	 3. A disputant.<BR>	 4.<BR>An opponent in general, &c.<BR> E. वि before, जि to conquer,<BR>desiderative form, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिग्राहयिषु
विजिग्राहयिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to excite to war.<BR> E. वि before, ग्रह्<BR>to take, desid of the causal v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिघृक्षु
विजिघृक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Determined or wishing to encounter, oppose,<BR>fight with, overcome, &c.<BR> E. वि before, ग्रह to take, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजित|विजितः
विजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Defeated, conquered.<BR> E. वि before, जित conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितवत्|विजितवन्त्
विजितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Victorious, conquering.<BR> E. वि before, जि to<BR>conquer, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितव्य
विजितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be apprehended or feared.<BR> E. विज् to fear, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितात्मन्
विजितात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Self-subdued.<BR> E. विजित and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिति|विजितिः
विजिति f. (-तिः or ती) Victory, conquest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितृ
विजितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what separates, divides, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ता)<BR>1. A judge, a discriminator, a distinguisher.<BR>	 2. A partner or co-<BR>heir.<BR> E. विज् to separate, &c., aff. तृच् and इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितेन्द्रिय|विजितेंद्रिय
विजितेन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of subdued organs or passions.<BR> E. विजित and<BR>इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजित्य
विजित्य Ind. Having conquered.<BR> E. वि before, जि to conquer, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिन|विजिनं|विजिनः
विजिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Mixed with rice-gruel, &c. (sauce or condiments.)<BR>E. विज् to shake, aff. इनच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिल|विजिलं|विजिलः
विजिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Mixed with rice-water or gruel, (sauce or condi-<BR>ments, &c.)<BR> E. विज् to shake, aff. इलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिविल|विजिविलं
विजिविल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Mixed with rice-water, sauces, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिहीर्षा
विजिहीर्षा f. (-र्षा) Wish or intention to take pleasure or sport.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, हृ to take, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिहीर्षु
विजिहीर्षु mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु) Wishing or speaking for sport or amusement.<BR>E. वि before, हृ to take, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिह्म|विजिह्मः
विजिह्म mfn. (-ह्मः-ह्मा-ह्मं)<BR>	 1. Curved, bent.<BR>	 2. Awry, crooked in mind or<BR>purpose, dishonest, depraved.<BR> E. वि privative, and जिह्म straight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिह्मता
विजिह्मता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Crookedness.<BR>	 2. Craftiness.<BR> E. विजिह्म and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजुल|विजुलः
विजुल m. (-लः) The silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. विज-उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भण|विजृंभण|विजृंभणं|विजृम्भणं
विजृम्भण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Pastime, sport, especially amorous.<BR>	 2. Budding,<BR>blossoming, expanding.<BR>	 3. Yawning, gaping.<BR>	 4. Exhibiting, dis-<BR>playing.<BR> E. वि before, जृभि to yawn, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भित|विजृंभित|विजृम्भितं|विजृम्भितः
विजृम्भित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Blossomed, expanded, opened, unfolded.<BR>	 2.<BR>Yawning, gaping.<BR>	 3. Sported, wantoned.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>2. Pastime, sport.<BR> E. वि before, जृभि to yawn or open, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजेतृ
विजेतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Victorious, a victor.<BR> E. वि, जि to conquer, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जन|विज्जनं
विज्जन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Mixed with rice-water or gruel, (sauce, gravy,<BR>&c.): see विजिल; it is also occurs विज्जल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जल|विज्जलं
विज्जल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Mixed with rice-water, &c.: see विजिल.<BR>	 n. (-लं) An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जुल|विज्जुलं
विज्जुल n. (-लं) Cinnamon.<BR> E. विज-उलच् aff. “दारुचिनि ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञ|विज्ञः
विज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Skilful, able, clever, conversant.<BR>	 2. Wise,<BR>learned.<BR> E. वि implying separation, discrimination, ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञता
विज्ञता f. (-ता) Wisdom, learning.<BR> E. तल् added to the preceding; also<BR>with त्व, विज्ञत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञप्त
विज्ञप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Stated, reported, represented.<BR> E. वि, ज्ञा to know, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञप्ति|विज्ञप्तिः
विज्ञप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Information, representation, respectful communica-<BR>tion or information, or opinion on any subject.<BR>	 2. An announce-<BR>ment.<BR> E. वि before, ज्ञा to know, causal form, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञबुद्धि|विज्ञबुद्धिः
विज्ञबुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Indian spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञात|विज्ञातः
विज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Celebrated, famous, known.<BR>	 2. Known, under-<BR>stood.<BR> E. वि before, ज्ञा to know, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञान|विज्ञानं
विज्ञान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Knowledge, science, learning, worldly knowledge or<BR>wisdom, that which comprehends any subject, except an under-<BR>standing of the true nature of GOD or BRAHMĀ, acquirable by<BR>abstract meditation and the study of the Vedas; it is also des-<BR>cribed as conversancy with the arts of painting, &c., and with<BR>books, as the Smṛti-Shāstras or works on law, and other bran-<BR>ches of science or literature.<BR>	 2. Business, employment.<BR>	 3. Music.<BR>E. वि implying variety, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानपाद|विज्ञानपादः
विज्ञानपाद m. (-दः) An epithet of VYĀSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=654-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानमातृक|विज्ञानमातृकः
विज्ञानमातृक m. (-कः) A name of BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha<BR>religion.<BR> E. विज्ञान knowledge, मातृक parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानिक|विज्ञानिकः
विज्ञानिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Clever, skilful, conversant; also वैज्ञानिक.<BR>E. विज्ञान, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापक|विज्ञापकः
विज्ञापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what makes known.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An<BR>informant.<BR>	 2. An instructor.<BR> E. वि, ज्ञा to know, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापन|विज्ञापनं
विज्ञापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Teaching, instruction, communication of knowledge<BR>not religious, &c.<BR>	 2. Representing, informing.<BR> E. वि before, ज्ञा<BR>to know, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापनीय
विज्ञापनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be made known, represented, taught, &c.<BR>E. वि before, ज्ञा to know, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापित
विज्ञापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Apprised, informed.<BR>	 2. Instructed.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore, ज्ञा to know, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञाय
विज्ञाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Cognizable, comprehensible, what is to be or<BR>may be known or understood.<BR> E. वि implying discrimination, ज्ञा<BR>to know, यत् participle aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्वर
विज्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Exempt from decay.<BR>	 2. Free from fever.<BR> E. वि,<BR>ज्वरा decay, or ज्वर fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विझर्झर
विझर्झर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Harsh, disagreeable, (as sound.)<BR> E. वि before, झर्झर clanging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विञ्जामर|विंजामर|विंजामरं|विञ्जामरं
विञ्जामर n. (-रं) The white of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विञ्जोली|विंजोली
विञ्जोली f. (-ली) A line, a row, a range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्
विट् r. 1st cl. (वेटति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To curse. (इ) विटि r. 10th cl.<BR>(विण्टयति-ते) To decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट|विटः
विट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A catamite, a pathic.<BR>	 2. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 3. An<BR>attendant on a dissolute character or courtezan, he is represented<BR>as on familiar terms with his associate and accomplished in the<BR>arts of singing and poetry.<BR>	 4. A paramour, a gallant.<BR>	 5. A<BR>mountain.<BR>	 6. The Khayer-tree, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>	 7. A medi-<BR>cinal salt: see विड्लवण.<BR>	 8. A rat.<BR>	 9. The orange tree.<BR>	 10. A<BR>branch and its shoot.<BR> E. विट् to sound, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटङ्क|विटंक|विटंकः|विटङ्कः
विटङ्क mn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्कं)<BR>	 1. A dove-cot, an aviary.<BR>	 2. The highest point. E.<BR>वि variously, टकि to bind, aff. अच्; also with कन् added विटङ्कक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटप|विटपः
विटप mn. (-पः-पं)<BR>	 1. The branch of a tree or creeper with its new<BR>sprout or shoot.<BR>	 2. A new shoot.<BR>	 3. A branch.<BR>	 4. Expansion,<BR>spreading.<BR>	 5. A clump, a cluster.<BR>	 6. A bush.<BR>	 7. The perinæum or<BR>septum of the scrotum.<BR>	 m. (-पः) The keeper of pathics.<BR> E. विट a<BR>branch, &c., and पा to cherish, aff. क; or विट् to sound, Unādi<BR>aff. अप, with the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटपिन्
विटपिन् m. (-पी)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. The large Indian fig-tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>E. विटप a branch or shoot, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटमाक्षिक|विटमाक्षिकः
विटमाक्षिक m. (-कः) A kind of mineral: see माक्षिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटलवण|विटलवणं
विटलवण n. (-णं) A medicinal salt. see विट; also विट्लवण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटि|विटिः
विटि f. (-टिः or टी) Yellow saunders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्कारिका
विट्कारिका f. (-का) A kind of bird, probably a variety of the Turdus<BR>Salica of Buchannan.)<BR> E. विट् from विट् fæces, कारिका working.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्खदिर|विट्खदिरः
विट्खदिर m. (-रः) A fetid Mimosa.<BR> E. विट् fæces, खदिर Mimosa catechu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्चर|विट्चरः
विट्चर m. (-रः) The tame or village hog.<BR> E. विट् filth, &c. चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्पण्य
विट्पण्य n. (-ण्यं) Goods, merchandise.<BR> E. विट् a Vaiśya, पण्य wares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्पति|विट्पतिः
विट्पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A son-in-law, a daughter's husband.<BR>	 2. A head<BR>merchant.<BR> E. विश् a Vaiśya, &c., and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्लवण
विट्लवण n. (-णं) A fetid salt: see विड.<BR> E. विट् ordure, लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्सङ्ग|विट्संग|विट्संगः
विट्सङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Constipation.<BR> E. विट् and सङ्ग aggregate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्सारिका
विट्सारिका f. (-का) A bird, a sort of thrush; a variety of the bird,<BR>usually though inaccurately called Maina in Bengal.<BR> E. विट् fæces,<BR>सारिका the same bird, or another species of the same. “गुयेसालिक ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विठङ्क|विठंक
विठङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Bad, vile, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्
विड् r. 1st cl. (वेडति)<BR>	 1. To divide, to break.<BR>	 2. To curse, to revile.<BR>	 3. To cry out against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्
विड् f. (-विड्) A bit, a fragment.<BR> E. विड् to break, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड|विडं|विडः
विड n. (-डं)<BR>	 1. Factitious salt, or salt procured by boiling soil found<BR>near the sea-shore, or any earth impregnated with saline particles.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">Page655-b+ 60</a>]<BR>2. A particular fetid kind of salt, used as a tonic aperient, com-<BR>monly called black salt or Vit-lavaṇ, prepared by fusing fossile-<BR>salt with a small portion of Emblic myrobalans; the produce is<BR>muriate of soda with small quantities of muriate of lime, sulphur<BR>and oxid of iron.<BR>	 3. A part, a fracture, a bit.<BR> E. विड् to divide,<BR>aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडगन्ध
विडगन्ध n. (-न्धं) The medicinal salt called Vit-lavaṇ: see the last. E.<BR>विड salt, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडङ्ग|विडंग|विडङ्गं|विडङ्गः
विडङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Clever, able, skilful, conversant.<BR>	 mn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गं)<BR>A vegetable and medicinal substance, considered of great efficacy<BR>as a vermifuge.<BR> E. विड् to break, to curse, Unādi aff. अङ्गच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्ब|विडंब|विडंबः|विडम्बः
विडम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. Imitation.<BR>	 2. Distressing, afflicting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बन|विडंबन|विडंबनं|विडम्बनं
विडम्बन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Afflicting, distressing.<BR>	 2. Vexation, mortification.<BR>3. Frustrating, rendering vain.<BR>	 4. Imitation, copying, especially<BR>assuming a similar appearance or dress, disguise, masquerade.<BR>5. Deception, fraud.<BR>	 6. Ridiculousness.<BR>	 7. The supernatural<BR>assumption of a borrowed form, transformation.<BR> E. वि before, डवि<BR>to heap, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बनीय
विडम्बनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be distressed or annoyed.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>assumed as a disguise.<BR> E. वि before, डवि to heap, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बयत्
विडम्बयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Assuming, putting on, (as a borrowed<BR>dress or appearance.<BR>	 2. Imitating.<BR> E. वि before, डवि to heap, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बित|विडंबित|विडम्बितः
विडम्बित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Low, poor, abject, distressed.<BR>	 2. Vexed,<BR>mortified.<BR>	 3. Assumed, put on, (as a borrowed form, &c.) simu-<BR>lated, transformed.<BR>	 4. Copied, imitated.<BR>	 5. Ridiculed, derided.<BR>	 6.<BR>Deceived.<BR> E. वि before, डिवि to heap, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडारक|विडारकः
विडारक m. (-कः) A cat. E. See the next, the ल being changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडाल|विडालः
विडाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. cat.<BR>	 2. The eyeball.<BR> E. विड् to divide, to tear, (rats,)<BR>Unādi aff. कालन्; also with कन् added, विडालक, and ल being<BR>changed to र, विडारक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडालक|विडालकं|विडालकः
विडालक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Application of oint-<BR>ment to the external part of the eye, especially to the eyelids, of<BR>which the lashes have fallen off or been ulcerated.<BR>	 2. A cat.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडालपद|विडालपदः
विडालपद m. (-दः) A measure of weight, the same as the Karṣa or<BR>weight of sixteen Māshas.<BR> E. विडाल a cat, पद the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडीन|विडीनं
विडीन n. (-नं) One of the different modes of flight attributed to birds,<BR>imitative flight.<BR> E. वि severally, and डीन flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडुल|विडुलः
विडुल m. (-लः) A sort of cane, (Calamus rotang.)<BR> E. विड-कुलन् । “वेतस वृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडूरज|विडूरजं
विडूरज n. (-जं) The Lapis Lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडोजस्
विडोजस् m. (-जाः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. विड् a fragment; (splitting<BR>mountains, &c. with his thunderbolt,) or विट् from विश् a Vaiśya,<BR>(here meaning a subject or man in general,) and ओजस् strength,<BR>splendour; also विडौजस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडग्रह
विडग्रह m. (-हः) Constipation.<BR> E. विट् and ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्ज|विड्जः
विड्ज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced from ordure.<BR>	 n. (-जं) A fungus.<BR> E. विट्, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्भव
विड्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Born or produced from ordure.<BR> E. विट्, भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्भुज्
विड्भुज् mfn. (-भुक्) Feeding on ordure.<BR> E. विष् and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्लवण|विड्लवणं
विड्लवण n. (-णं) A medicinal salt, commonly black salt, Vitlaban: see<BR>विड.<BR> E. विड् to divide, aff. क्विप्, and लवण salt; also विट्लवण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्वराह|विड्वराहः
विड्वराह m. (-हः) A village or tame hog.<BR> E. विट् fæces, वराह a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितंस|वितंसः
वितंस m. (-सः) A cage, a net, a chain or any apparatus for confining<BR>beasts or birds.<BR> E. वि before, तसि to adorn, aff. अच्; also वीतंस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितण्ड|वितंडः|वितण्डः
वितण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A sort of lock or bolt with three divisions or wards.<BR>2. An elephant.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा)<BR>	 1. Controversy, argument, the subversion<BR>of another's opinion or interpretation and establishment of one's<BR>own.<BR>	 2. Criticism.<BR>	 3. An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR>	 4. Ben-<BR>zoin or styrax.<BR>	 5. The Oleander plant, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>	 6. A<BR>ladle, a spoon.<BR> E. वि before, तडि to beat, affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितत|विततं
वितत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stretched, spread, expanded.<BR>	 2. Pervaded,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">Page656-a+ 60</a>]<BR>diffused.<BR>	 3. Lengthened.<BR>	 4. Large, broad.<BR>	 5. Covered.<BR>	 6. Performed.<BR>n. (-तं) Any stringed instrument.<BR> E. वि before, तत stretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=655-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितति|विततिः
वितति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Spreading, expansion.<BR>	 2. Quantity, collection.<BR>	 3. A<BR>clump, a cluster, (of trees.)<BR> E. वि before, तन् to stretch, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विततीकरण
विततीकरण n. (-णं) Spreading, stretching.<BR> E. वितत, करण making, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विततीकृत
विततीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stretched, spread, expanded.<BR> E. वितत the same,<BR>कृत made, and च्वि augment, leaving ई ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितत्य
वितत्य Ind. Having spread.<BR> E. वि before, तन् to spread, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथ|वितथं
वितथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) False, untrue, vain, futile.<BR> E. वि implying re-<BR>verse, तथ्य true, अच् aff., and the semivowel rejected; or वि be-<BR>fore, तम् to desire, वथन् aff., and म rejected; also वितथ्य f. (-थ्या)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितद्रु|वितद्रुः
वितद्रु f. (-द्रुः) A name of a river, said to be situated in the Punjāb. E.<BR>वि before, तम् to desire, aff. रु and दङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितनु|वितनुः
वितनु mfn. (-नुः-न्वी-नु) Thin, graceful, delicate.<BR> E. वि and तनु the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्तु|वितंतुः|वितन्तुः
वितन्तु m. (-न्तुः) A good horse.<BR>	 f. (-न्तुः) A widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्वत्
वितन्वत् mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्) Spreading, stretching, expanding.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, तन् to stretch, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितमस्
वितमस् mfn. (-माः-माः-मः)<BR>	 1. Light, free from darkness.<BR>	 2. Exempt<BR>from the quality of ignorance.<BR> E. वि privative, तमस darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितरण|वितरणं
वितरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. Abandoning, quitting.<BR>	 2. Passing,<BR>crossing.<BR> E. वि implying privation, &c., and तॄ to cross, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्क|वितर्कः
वितर्क m. (-र्कः)<BR>	 1. Reasoning, discussion.<BR>	 2. Doubt, deliberation.<BR>	 3. A<BR>teacher, an instructor in divine knowledge.<BR>	 4. Consideration of<BR>probabilities, mental anticipation of alternatives, conjecture. E.<BR>वि implying discrimination, &c., तर्क् to reason, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्कण|वितर्कणं
वितर्कण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Reasoning, discussion, whether mental or contro-<BR>versial, argument, reflection.<BR>	 2. Apprehension, doubt.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>तर्क् to reason, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्क्य
वितर्क्य Ind. Having deliberated, considered, &c.<BR>	 mfn. (र्क्यः-र्क्या-र्क्यं) Doubt-<BR>ful, questionable.<BR> E. वि before, तर्क् to reason, ल्यप् or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्दि|वितर्दिः|वितर्द्दिः
वितर्दि f. (र्दिः or र्दी)<BR>	 1. A quadrangular building, or sort of covered<BR>terrace of wood in the centre of the court-yard of a temple or<BR>palace.<BR>	 2. A quadrangular resting place made of wood, a seat, a<BR>bench.<BR>	 3. A place in a court-yard for sitting in or standing under.<BR>4. A floor on four posts in the midst of a quadrangular house.<BR>5. A temporary stage or shed in the middle of a court-yard, for<BR>performing sacrifices, representing plays, &c.<BR>	 6. A terrace furnished<BR>with pillars, a vārāndāh, a balcony.<BR>	 7. A covered temporary terrace<BR>on which idols are sometimes placed and worshipped.<BR> E. वि pri-<BR>vative, तर्द् to injure, aff. इन्; also ङीष् optionally added, and<BR>with कन् added in the fem. form वितर्दिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितल|वितलं
वितल n. (-लं) One of the seven divisions of Pātāla, the second in<BR>descent below the earth.<BR> E. वि before, तल् to be low, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्ता
वितस्ता f. (-स्ता) Name of a river in the Punjāb, known to the Greeks<BR>as the Hydaspes and now called the Jhelum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्ति|वितस्तिः
वितस्ति f. (-स्तिः) A long span measured by the extended thumb and<BR>little finger, considered equal to twelve fingers.<BR> E. वि apart, तस्<BR>to throw, Unādi aff. क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितान|वितानं|वितानः
वितान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Empty, pithless, sapless.<BR>	 2. Empty, vacant.<BR>3. Dull, stupid.<BR>	 4. Wicked, abandoned.<BR>	 mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>	 1. Spreading,<BR>expansion.<BR>	 2. An awning, a canopy.<BR>	 3. Sacrifice, offering, oblation.<BR>4. The sacrificial hearth or hole in which the sacred fires are<BR>kept.<BR>	 5. A heap, a quantity.<BR>	 6. Season, opportunity.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>form of the Anuṣṭubh metre or verse of four lines of eight<BR>syllables each; each line of the stanza named Vitāna consists of<BR>two Iambics, one Trochee, and one Spondee.<BR>	 3. Leisure, rest,<BR>interval of occupation.<BR> E. वि before, तन् to spread, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानक|वितानकं|वितानकः
वितानक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. An awning, a canopy, especially a cloth spread<BR>over a large open hall or court, or any open space in which dancing<BR>singing, &c. are exhibited, at solemn or religious festivals.<BR>	 2. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">Page656-b+ 60</a>]<BR>heap, a quantity.<BR>	 3. An expanse.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानीकरण
वितानीकरण n. (-णं) Covering, overspreading, (as a canopy.)<BR> E. वितान,<BR>करण making, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानीकृत
वितानीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spread or extended over, (as a canopy.)<BR> E. वितान, कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितायमान
वितायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being overspread, covered, shaded, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, तन् to stretch, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितिष्ठमान
वितिष्ठमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Staying, being.<BR>	 2. Fixed, stationary.<BR>	 3.<BR>Permanent.<BR> E. वि before, स्था to stay, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितीर्ण
वितीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Crossed over, overpassed.<BR>	 2. Subdued, over-<BR>come.<BR>	 3. Effaced, rubbed out.<BR>	 4. Conferred, bestowed.<BR>	 5. Afforded,<BR>yielded.<BR>	 6. Conveyed.<BR> E. वि before, तॄ to cross, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्न|वितुन्नं
वितुन्न n. (-न्नं)<BR>	 1. A potherb, (Marsilia quadrifolia.)<BR>	 2. An aquatic plant<BR>(Vallisneria octandra.)<BR> E. वि privative, तुन्न pained; allaying pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्नक|वितुन्नकं|वितुन्नकः
वितुन्नक m. (-कः) A plant, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Corian-<BR>der seed.<BR>	 2. Blue vitriol.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुष्ट
वितुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Displeased, dissatisfied.<BR> E. वि priv., तुष्ट pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृष्ण
वितृष्ण mfn. (-ष्णः-ष्णा-ष्णं) Content, satisfied, free from any desire.<BR> E. वि<BR>priv., तृष्णा thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृष्णता
वितृष्णता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Satiety, satisfaction.<BR>	 2. Content.<BR> E. वि priv., तृष्णता cupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त|वित्तं|वित्तः
वित्त r. 10th cl. (वित्तयति-ते) To quit, to abandon, especially by giving<BR>away, to give alms; according to some, also (वित्तापयति-ते) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त|वित्तं|वित्तः
वित्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Judged, investigated, examined, discussed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Known, famous.<BR>	 3. Gained, acquired.<BR>	 n. (-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Wealth, property,<BR>thing, substance.<BR>	 2. Power.<BR> E. विद् to know, to discuss, to acquire,<BR>aff. क्त, form irr.; वित्त्यते त्यज्यते वित्त-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तद|वित्तदः
वित्तद m. (-दः) A benefactor, one who gives away property.<BR> E. वित्त wealth, द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तवत्|वित्तवन्त्
वित्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Rich, wealthy.<BR> E. वित्त and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तहीन
वित्तहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Poor, indigent.<BR> E. वित्त and हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्ति|वित्तिः
वित्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Discussion, discrimination, judgment, investigation.<BR>2. Knowledge.<BR>	 3. Gain, acquisition.<BR>	 4. Livelihood.<BR> E. विद् to know,<BR>&c., aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तेहा
वित्तेहा f. (-हा) Cupidity, avarice.<BR> E. वित्त, ईहा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रस्त|वित्रस्तः
वित्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ती-स्तं) Frightened, alarmed, afraid.<BR> E. वि before, त्रस to fear, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रास|वित्रासः
वित्रास m. (-सः) Fear, alarm.<BR> E. वि before, त्रास fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्सन|वित्सनः
वित्सन m. (-नः) An ox, a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथ्
विथ्(ऋ)विथृ r. 1st cl. (वेथते) To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथुर|विथुरः
विथुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A thief.<BR>	 2. An imp, a demon.<BR> E. व्यथ् to fear, Unādi<BR>aff. उरच्, the semivowel changed to इ, and that unaltered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथ्या
विथ्या f. (-थ्या) A plant, commonly Gojihwā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्
विद् r. 2nd cl. (वेत्ति वेद)<BR>	 1. To know.<BR>	 2. To look upon, to take for, to<BR>consider. With नि prefixed, To be sad or depressed. With सम्,<BR>(संवित्ते) To meditate, to know, to gain holy knowledge by abstract.<BR>meditation. r. 4th cl. (विद्यते) To be, to exist, to be present, to exist<BR>actually. r. 7th cl. (विन्ते)<BR>	 1. To consider, to reason.<BR>	 2. To under-<BR>stand.<BR>	 3. To regard, to take for.<BR>	 4. To discuss. r. 10th cl. (वेदयते)<BR>1. To be sensible.<BR>	 2. To know.<BR>	 3. To declare, to describe or<BR>explain; (in this sense नि is usually prefixed.)<BR>	 4. To dwell, to<BR>inhabit.<BR>	 5. To be fixed or steady.<BR>	 6. To suffer pain. With नि, or वि<BR>and नि prefixed, To deliver, to impart or communicate. With प्रति,<BR>To deliver, to give, (औ ऌ) औ विदॢ r. 6th cl. (विन्दति-ते)<BR>	 1. To gain,<BR>to get, to acquire or possess.<BR>	 2. To find.<BR>	 3. To experience.<BR>	 4. To<BR>marry. With अनु, To feel. With परि, To marry first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्
विद् m. (-वित्)<BR>	 1. Who or what knows.<BR>	 2. A learned man.<BR>	 3. The planet<BR>mercury.<BR>	 f. (-वित्) Knowledge, understanding.<BR> E. विद् to know, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदंश|विदंशः
विदंश m. (-शः) Pungent food that excites thirst.<BR> E. वि + दन्श्-घञ् aff.<BR>“चाट्नि ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्ध|विदग्धः
विदग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Clever, shrewd, knowing.<BR>	 2. Sharp, witty.<BR>3. Intriguing.<BR>	 4. Undigested.<BR>	 5. Burnt.<BR>	 m. (-ग्धः)<BR>	 1. A libertine, a<BR>lecher, an intriguer.<BR>	 2. A learned or clever man, a scholar, a Pan-<BR>dit f. (-ग्धा) A sharp knowing woman.<BR> E. वि before, दह् to burn, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=656-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धता
विदग्धता f. (-ता) Sharpness, shrewdness, cleverness, wit.<BR> E. तल् aff. of the<BR>abstract, added to the last; also with the aff. त्व, विदग्धत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदत्
विदत् mfn. (-दन्-दती-दत्) Wise, intelligent, learned, knowing.<BR> E. विद् to<BR>know, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदथ|विदथः
विदथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A wise or learned man, a sage, a scholar.<BR>	 2. A saint,<BR>a devotee.<BR> E. विद् to know, Unādi aff. कथच् and the radical vowel<BR>unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदधत्
विदधत् mfn. (-धन्-धती-धत्) Having, wearing, assuming.<BR> E. वि before, धा to have, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर|विदरं|विदरः
विदर m. (-रः) Tearing, rending.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The Indian prickly-pear,<BR>(Cactus Indicus.) “फणिमनसा”.<BR> E. वि before, दृ to tear, aff. अप् or अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भ|विदर्भः
विदर्भ mf. (-र्भः-र्भा) A district and city to the south-west of Bengal,<BR>the modern Bada-Nāgpur or Berār proper.<BR>	 m. (-र्भः) Any dry or<BR>desert soil.<BR> E. वि privative, and दर्भ the sacred grass; not growing<BR>in that country in consequence of the curse of a saint, whose son<BR>had died of a wound from a blade of the grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भजा
विदर्भजा f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. The wife of the saint AGASTYA.<BR>	 2. DAMAYANTĪ the<BR>wife of NALA, and heroine of the Naishada or poem so called.<BR>	 3.<BR>RUKMINĪ, the wife of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. विदर्भ the country, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदल|विदलं|विदलः
विदल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Opened, expanded, blown, (as a flower, &c.)<BR>2. Rent, split.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A shallow basket made of split bamboos,<BR>a vessel of wicker work.<BR>	 2. Split peas.<BR>	 3. Pomegranate bark.<BR>	 4.<BR>The cuttings or chips of any substance, that which has been pared<BR>or split.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Dividing, separating.<BR>	 2. A cake.<BR>	 3. Mountain-<BR>ebony, (Bauhinia variegata, &c.)<BR> E. वि before, दल tearing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलन|विदलनं
विदलन n. (-नं) Rending asunder, cutting, splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलित
विदलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rent, torn, split.<BR>	 2. Blown, expanded, (as a<BR>flower.)<BR> E. वि before, दल् to tear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलीकरण
विदलीकरण n. (-णं) Rending, dividing.<BR> E. विदल, and करण making, with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलीकृत
विदलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Divided, separated.<BR>	 2. Cut, split, torn, bro<BR>ken.<BR> E. विदल dividing, कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदश्यमान
विदश्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being bitten.<BR> E. वि before, दशि to bite, pass.<BR>v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदा
विदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. Knowledge.<BR>	 2. Intellect, understanding.<BR> E. विद् to know, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदार|विदारः
विदार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Tearing, rending.<BR>	 2. War, battle.<BR>	 3. An inundation,<BR>an overflow, the rising of a river or pond above its banks.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>1. A plant, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>	 2. A climbing plant,<BR>(Ipomœa paniculata.)<BR>	 3. Bubo, swelling in the groin, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, दॄ to tear, to divide, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारक|विदारकं|विदारकः
विदारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A divider, a render or tearer.<BR>	 2. A tree or rock in<BR>the middle of a stream, dividing its course.<BR>	 3. A hole or pit for<BR>water sunk in the bed of a dry river, &c.<BR>	 f. (-रिका)<BR>	 1. A plant,<BR>(Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>	 2. A bubo.<BR> E. वि before, दृ to divide, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारण|विदारणं|विदारणः
विदारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Tearing, breaking, splitting, severing, dividing.<BR>	 2.<BR>Paining, afflicting.<BR>	 3. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 mf. (-णः-णा) War, battle.<BR>m. (-णः) A tree, (Pterospermum acerifolium.)<BR> E. वि before, दृ to<BR>tear, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारयत्
विदारयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Tearing, rending, dividing.<BR> E. वि before, दॄ to tear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारित
विदारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Torn, split, broken.<BR> E. वि before, दृ to tear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारीगन्धा
विदारीगन्धा f. (-न्धा) A plant, (Hedysarum gangeticum.) “शालपाणि ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारु|विदारुः
विदारु m. (-रुः) A lizard.<BR> E. वि before, दृ to tear, उन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदार्य्य|विदार्य
विदार्य्य Ind. Having torn or rent.<BR> E. वि, दृ to tear, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदाह|विदाहः
विदाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Heat, burning.<BR>	 2. Pungency.<BR> E. वि before, दह् to burn, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदाहिन्
विदाहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>	 1. Burning, hot.<BR>	 2. Pungent, acrid.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, दह् to burn, aff. घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिक्चङ्ग|विदिक्चङ्गः
विदिक्चङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A sort of bird.<BR> E. विदिश् a point of the compass, चङ्ग handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदित|विदितं|विदितः
विदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Known, understood.<BR>	 2. Promised, agreed,<BR>assented.<BR>	 3. Represented, submitted, solicited.<BR>	 4. Apprised, in-<BR>formed, who or what knows.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A sage, a learned man.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं) Information, representation.<BR> E. विद् to know, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदित्वा
विदित्वा Ind. Having known or promised.<BR> E. विद to know, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिश|विदिशः
विदिश f. (-दिक्) An intermediate point of the compass.<BR> E. वि implying<BR>separation, and दिश् a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिशा
विदिशा f. (-शा) Name of a river in Mālava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदीर्ण|विदीर्णः
विदीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Torn, split, burst or broken.<BR>	 2. Expanded,<BR>opened.<BR> E. वि before, दृ to tear, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदीर्य्यमाण|विदीर्यमाण
विदीर्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being torn, split, broken, cut, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, दृ to rend, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदु|विदुः
विदु m. (-दुः)<BR>	 1. The hollow between the frontal globes of an elephant.<BR>2. The hippopotamus.<BR> E. विद् to know, (the goad,) aff. कु; with कू विदू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुर|विदुरः
विदुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Wise, knowing, intelligent.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A liber-<BR>tine, an intriguer.<BR>	 2. A learned or clever man.<BR>	 3. The younger bro-<BR>ther and counsellor of DHRITARĀSHTRA.<BR> E. विद् to know, कुरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुल|विदुलः
विदुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A sort of reed, (Calamus rotang;) also the same grow-<BR>ing in water, (C. fasciculatus.)<BR>	 2. Gum-myrrh.<BR> E. विद् to know, aff. कुलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदून
विदून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Agitated, distressed.<BR> E. वि, दु to distress, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूर|विदूरः
विदूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Very far or remote.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Name of a mountain<BR>whence the Lapis Lazuli is brought.<BR> E. वि intervening, दूर distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूरग|विदूरगः
विदूरग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Spreading, going far or wide.<BR> E. वि before, दूर<BR>far, remote, and ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूरज|विदूरजं
विदूरज n. (-जं) The Lapis Lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूराद्रि|विदूराद्रिः
विदूराद्रि m. (-द्रिः) The name of a mountain.<BR> E. विदूर remote, and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूषक|विदूषकः
विदूषक mfn. (-कः-षिका-कं)<BR>	 1. Facetious, witty, a wag, a jester.<BR>	 2. Cen-<BR>sorious, detracting, a detractor or abuser of other people.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. An actor, especially an interlocutor with the audience between<BR>the acts or scenes, a jester, a buffoon.<BR>	 2. (In dramatic language,)<BR>The humble and jocose companion of the principal character.<BR>	 3.<BR>A catamite.<BR>	 f. (-की) Corrupting, contaminating.<BR> E. वि before, दूष्<BR>to be or make bad, aff. क्वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूषण|विदूषणं
विदूषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Censuring, reviling, abuse, satire.<BR>	 2. Corruption. E.<BR>वि before, दूष् to make bad or faulty, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेश|विदेशः
विदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A foreign country, abroad.<BR>	 2. Any place away from<BR>home.<BR> E. वि variety, देश place or country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशगत
विदेशगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone abroad.<BR> E. विदेश and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशगमन
विदेशगमन n. (-नं) Travelling, going abroad.<BR> E. विदेश, गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशज
विदेशज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Foreign, exotic.<BR> E. विदेश, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशस्थ
विदेशस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Who or what remains abroad.<BR> E. विदेश, स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशिन्
विदेशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Foreign, foreigner, exotic.<BR> E. विदेश, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेह|विदेहः
विदेह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Incorporeal, without body.<BR>	 m. (-हः) A sovereign<BR>of the family of JANAKA, king of Mithilā.<BR>	 f. (-हा) A district in<BR>the province of Behār, the same as the ancient Mithilā, or the<BR>modern Tirhut.<BR> E. वि privative, and देह the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्ध|विद्धः
विद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Pierced, perforated.<BR>	 2. Thrown, cast, directed,<BR>sent.<BR>	 3. Like, resembling.<BR>	 4. Opposed, impeded.<BR>	 5. Beaten, whip-<BR>ped.<BR>	 m. (-द्धः) A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>	 n. (-द्धं) A wound.<BR> E. विध्<BR>to pierce, or व्यध् to beat, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्धकर्ण|विद्धकर्णः
विद्धकर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Having the ears pierced or slit.<BR>	 mf. (-र्णः-र्णा or<BR>-र्णी) A plant, commonly Ākanādi, (Cissampelos hexandra, Rox.)<BR>E. विद्ध pierced, and कर्ण the ear; also in the latter sense, with<BR>कन् added विद्धकर्णिका; also अविद्धकर्ण, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यमान|विद्यमानः
विद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being present or in existence.<BR>	 2. Actual,<BR>real, in possession, (as property.)<BR> E. विद् to be, 4th cl. and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्या
विद्या f. (-द्या)<BR>	 1. Knowledge, learning, science, whether sacred or profane,<BR>though more especially the former: it is sometimes classed into<BR>fourteen divisions; viz:--the four Vedas; the six Angas, or gram-<BR>mar, astronomy, &c.; the Purāṇas as the eleventh class; and<BR>the Mimānsā or theology, Nyāya or logic, and Dharma or law,<BR>as the remaining three.<BR>	 2. The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. A tree, (Premna<BR>spinosa.)<BR>	 4. A magical pill or bolus, by putting which into the<BR>mouth a person has the power of ascending to heaven.<BR>	 5. Spell,<BR>incantation.<BR> E. विद् to know, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=657-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याकर|विद्याकरः
विद्याकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Giving wisdom or science.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A learned<BR>man.<BR> E. विद्या, कर what makes, or आकर a mine: see विद्याधर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यागम|विद्यागमः
विद्यागम m. (-मः) Acquirement of knowledge.<BR> E. विद्या, आगम coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याचण|विद्याचणः
विद्याचण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Famous for learning or knowledge.<BR> E. विद्या<BR>knowledge, and चणप् aff. in this particular meaning; also विद्याचन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याचुञ्चु|विद्याचुञ्चुः
विद्याचुञ्चु mfn. (-ञ्चुः-ञ्चुः-ञ्चु) Famous for knowledge.<BR> E. विद्या knowledge,<BR>and चुञ्चुप् aff. implying celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यादल|विद्यादलः
विद्यादल m. (-लः) The Bhurja-patra tree.<BR> E. विद्या, दल a leaf: being used for writing on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यादान|विद्यादानं
विद्यादान n. (-नं) Giving knowledge or science.<BR> E. विद्या, दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यादेवी
विद्यादेवी f. (-वी) A female divinity, one of a class of sixteen peculiar<BR>apparently to the mythological system of the Jainas.<BR> E. विद्या<BR>science, देवी a goddess; a goddess of learning or science, a muse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याधन|विद्याधनं
विद्याधन n. (-नं) Property acquired by science, as by instruction, &c.<BR>E. विद्या knowledge, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याधर|विद्याधरः
विद्याधर m. (-रः) A demigod of a particular order or class, a spirit of<BR>the air.<BR> E. विद्या a magical pill, as above, and धर who has or holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यानुपालन
विद्यानुपालन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Patronising learning.<BR>	 2. Studying, acquiring<BR>learning.<BR> E. विद्या and अनुपालन encouraging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यानुपालिन्
विद्यानुपालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Studied, acquiring or having acquired<BR>learning.<BR> E. विद्या and अनुपालिन् who prosecutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यानुसेवन
विद्यानुसेवन n. (-नं) Cultivating science or learning.<BR> E. विद्या, अनुसेवन pursuing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यानुसेविन्
विद्यानुसेविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Cultivating learning, engaged in study.<BR>E. विद्या and अनुसेविन् addicted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याप्राप्ति|विद्याप्राप्तिः
विद्याप्राप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Acquirement of knowledge.<BR>	 2. Acquisition made<BR>by or through learning.<BR> E. विद्या and प्राप्ति gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याभ्यास|विद्याभ्यासः
विद्याभ्यास m. (-सः) Study, diligent application.<BR> E. विद्या, अभ्यास exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यार्ज्जन|विद्यार्जन
विद्यार्ज्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Acquiring knowledge.<BR>	 2. Acquiring anything by<BR>knowledge, as by teaching, &c.<BR> E. विद्या, अर्ज्जन gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यार्ज्जित|विद्यार्जित
विद्यार्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gained by or through knowledge.<BR> E. विद्या,<BR>अर्ज्जित obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यार्थ|विद्यार्थः
विद्यार्थ m. (-र्थः) Seeking for knowledge.<BR> E. विद्या and अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यार्थिन्
विद्यार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Seeking for knowledge.<BR>	 m. (-र्थी) A pupil,<BR>a student.<BR> E. विद्यार्थ and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यालब्ध
विद्यालब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Gained by or through learning.<BR> E. विद्या, लब्ध gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यालय|विद्यालयः
विद्यालय m. (-यः) A school, a college.<BR> E. विद्या and आलय a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यालाभ|विद्यालाभः
विद्यालाभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. Acquisition of learning.<BR>	 2. Acquirement by or<BR>through learning.<BR> E. विद्या and लाभ gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यावत्|विद्यावन्त्
विद्यावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Learned, possessed of learning or science.<BR>E. विद्या learning, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याविशिष्ट
विद्याविशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Possessed of learning or science.<BR> E. विद्या,<BR>विशिष्ट endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याविहीन
विद्याविहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Ignorant, uninstructed.<BR> E. विद्या, विहीन deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याव्रतस्नातक|विद्याव्रतस्नातकः
विद्याव्रतस्नातक m. (-कः) The Brāhmana who has finished his studies and<BR>period of studentship.<BR> E. विद्या, व्रत a religious obligation, स्नातक a<BR>householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यास्नातक|विद्यास्नातकः
विद्यास्नातक m. (-कः) The student who has finished his religious studies.<BR> E. विद्या, स्नातक a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्याहीन
विद्याहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Ignorant, uninstructed.<BR> E. विद्या, हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्
विद्युत् f. (-द्युत्)<BR>	 1. Lightning.<BR>	 2. A thunderbolt.<BR> E. वि intensitive or<BR>privative, and द्युत light, lustre, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्प्रिय|विद्युत्प्रियं
विद्युत्प्रिय n. (-यं) Bell-metal.<BR> E. विद्युत् lightning, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्वत्|विद्युत्वन्त्
विद्युत्वत् mfn. (-त्वन्-त्वती-त्वत्) Having or containing lightning, electri-<BR>cal, (a cloud, &c.)<BR> E. विद्युत् lightning and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युलता
विद्युलता f. (-ता) Zigzag lightning.<BR> E. विद्युत् and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यातन
विद्यातन f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Illuminating.<BR>	 2. Illustrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्योतमान
विद्योतमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Shining, blazing.<BR> E. वि before, द्युत् to shine, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्योपार्ज्जन|विद्योपार्जन
विद्योपार्ज्जन n. (-नं) Acquisition of knowledge.<BR> E. विद्या, उपार्ज्जन collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्योपार्ज्जित|विद्योपार्जित
विद्योपार्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Acquired by or through learning, &c. E.<BR>विद्या and उपार्ज्जित obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्र|विद्रं|विद्रः
विद्र n. (-द्रं)<BR>	 1. A hole, a chasm.<BR>	 2. Piercing, perforating.<BR> E. विध् to<BR>pierce, aff., रक् form irr.; or वि before, द्रा to sleep, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रधि|विद्रधिः
विद्रधि m. (-धिः) Phlegmonoid inflammation; especially deep-seated,<BR>or internal abscess.<BR> E. विद्र piercing, धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रधिनाशन|विद्रधिनाशनः
विद्रधिनाशन m. (-नः) A tree, (Hyperanthera Morunga.)<BR> E. विद्रधि bile or<BR>abscess, नाशन destroying, discussing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रव|विद्रवः
विद्रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Flight, escape, retreat.<BR>	 2. Fear, agitation, panic.<BR>	 3.<BR>Intellect, understanding.<BR>	 4. Censure, abuse, reproach.<BR>	 5. Lique-<BR>faction.<BR>	 6. Flowing out, oozing.<BR> E. वि before, द्रु to fly, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्राण
विद्राण f. (-णा) Awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्राव|विद्रावः
विद्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Flight, retreat, running away.<BR>	 2. Liquefaction.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, द्रु to go, causal v., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावक
विद्रावक mfn. (-कः-विका-कं)<BR>	 1. Liquefying, causing to flow or melt.<BR>	 2.<BR>Driving away.<BR> E. वि before, द्रु to flow, &c., causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावण|विद्रावणं
विद्रावण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Causing to flow or melt, fusing.<BR>	 2. Driving away,<BR>chasing, defeating.<BR> E. वि before, द्रु to run, &c., causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावित|विद्रावितं
विद्रावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Liquefied, fused.<BR>	 2. Driven away, put to<BR>flight.<BR> E. वि before, द्रु to flow, &c., causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रुत|विद्रुतः
विद्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Liquid, liquefied, fluid as an oily or metallic<BR>substance upon being heated.<BR>	 2. Flown, fled.<BR>	 3. Running, going<BR>fast.<BR>	 4. Agitated, alarmed.<BR> E. वि before, द्रु to ooze, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रुम|विद्रुमः
विद्रुम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Coral.<BR>	 2. A tree bearing precious gems.<BR>	 3. A young<BR>sprout or shoot.<BR> E. वि implying species, द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रुमलता
विद्रुमलता f. (-ता) A sort of vegetable perfume.<BR> E. विद्रुम coral, लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वत्कल्प|विद्वत्कल्पः
विद्वत्कल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं) Less learned, a little learned.<BR> E. विद्वस् learned<BR>and कल्पप् aff. of diminution or inferiority; also with the similar<BR>affs. देशीयर् and देश्य, विद्वद्देशीय and विद्वद्देश्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वस्
विद्वस् mfn. (-द्वान्-दुषी-द्वत्)<BR>	 1. Intelligent, wise.<BR>	 2. Learned.<BR>	 m. (-द्वान्)<BR>A sage, a seer, one who knows the true nature of the soul and of<BR>GOD.<BR> E. विद् to know, क्वसु aff. in lieu of शतृ, the usual affix of the<BR>present participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष्
विद्विष् mfn. (-द्विट्) An enemy.<BR> E. वि before, द्विष् to hate, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष|विद्विषः
विद्विष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Hating, adverse, inimical.<BR>	 m. (-षः) An enemy. E.<BR>वि before, द्विष् to hate, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष्ट
विद्विष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Hated, disliked.<BR> E. वि before, द्विष् to hate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेष|विद्वेषः
विद्वेष m. (-षः) Enmity, hatred.<BR> E. वि before, द्विष् to hate, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषण|विद्वेषणं|विद्वेषणः
विद्वेषण m. (-णः) A hater.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Causing hatred or enmity. E.<BR>वि + द्विष्-ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषणी
विद्वेषणी f. (-णी) A woman of a resentful temperament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषिन्
विद्वेषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Inimical, hostile, hating.<BR>	 m. (-षी) An enemy.<BR>E. विद्वेष enmity, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेष्टृ
विद्वेष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Who or what hates, adverse, inimical.<BR> E. विद्विष् to hate, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्
विध् r. 6th cl. (विधति)<BR>	 1. To administer, to govern, to rule or command.<BR>2. To pierce, to perforate.<BR>	 3. To divide.<BR>	 4. To honour or worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध|विधः
विध mf. (-धः-धा)<BR>	 1. Form, formula, rule.<BR>	 2. Manner, kind, sort.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fodder, the food of horses, elephants, &c.<BR>	 4. Prosperity, thriving.<BR>5. Hire, wages.<BR>	 6. Act, action.<BR>	 7. Piercing.<BR> E. वि before, धा to<BR>have, aff. क or अङ्, and fem. aff. टाप्; or विध् to rule, &c., aff. क<BR>or अच्; the masculine form, though it does occur, is not common,<BR>except in composition, when the word is used attributively, as<BR>द्विविध of two sorts.<BR>	 mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवन|विधवनं
विधवन n. (-नं) Shaking, trembling.<BR> E. वि before, धू to shake, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवा
विधवा f. (-वा) A widow.<BR> E. वि privative, धव a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवागामिन्
विधवागामिन् m. (-मी) One who has intercourse with a widow.<BR> E. विधवा<BR>and गामिन् who approaches, (carnally.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवावेदन
विधवावेदन n. (-नं) Marrying a widow.<BR> E. विधवा, आवेदन marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधव्य|विधव्यं
विधव्य n. (-व्यं) Trembling, tremor.<BR> E. वि before, धू to shake, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधस्
विधस् m. (-धाः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. वि severally or every kind, धा to have,<BR>Unādi aff. असुन्, and the radical vowel dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातव्य
विधातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be done or performed.<BR>	 2. To be done<BR>according to rule, to be observed as a rite or ceremony.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>ruled or regulated.<BR> E. वि before, धा to have, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=658-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातृ
विधातृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. Love or KĀMA.<BR>	 3. Fate.<BR> E. वि severally,<BR>धा to have or contain, (all things,) aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातृभू
विधातृभू m. (-भूः) NĀRADA, the Muni and son of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. विधातृ<BR>BRAHMĀ, भू offspring, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधात्रायुस्
विधात्रायुस् m. (-युः)<BR>	 1. The sun-flower.<BR>	 2. Sun-shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधात्री
विधात्री f. (-त्री) Long-pepper.<BR> E. वि before, धा to have, तृच् aff., fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधान|विधानं
विधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Act, action, general or particular, though more<BR>especially the performance of such acts or rites as are prescribed<BR>in the sacred books of the Hindus.<BR>	 2. Rule, precept, ordinance,<BR>injunction.<BR>	 3. An elephant's fodder.<BR>	 4. Form, mode, manner.<BR>	 5.<BR>Sending, ordering.<BR>	 6. Means, expedient.<BR>	 7. Wealth.<BR>	 8. Wor-<BR>ship.<BR>	 9. Active enmity or act of hostility.<BR>	 10. Gaining, getting,<BR>taking.<BR>	 11. Conflict or contrast of opposite feelings.<BR>	 12. (In gram-<BR>mar.) Affixing, prefixing, taking as an affix, &c.<BR>	 13. Pain, sorrow,<BR>distress.<BR>	 14. Arranging, disposing.<BR>	 15. Creating, forming.<BR>	 16.<BR>Doing, performing, using.<BR>	 17. Enjoying, prescribing.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>धा to have, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानक|विधानकं
विधानक n. (-कं) Pain.<BR> E. वि before, धा to have, ल्युट् aff. कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानग|विधानगः
विधानग m. (-गः) A Paṇḍit, a wise or learned man or teacher.<BR> E. विधान<BR>action, the performance of those acts prescribed by the Shāśtras,<BR>and ग who goes or performs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानज्ञ|विधानज्ञः
विधानज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A Paṇḍit, &c.: see the last.<BR> E. विधान, ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधाय
विधाय Ind. Having taken, assumed, put on, placed, &c.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>धा to have, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायक|विधायकः
विधायक mfn. (-कः-यिका-कं) Consigning, delivering, one who entrusts or<BR>deposits anything, or causes it to be fixed or secure.<BR>	 2. Arrang-<BR>ing, disposing.<BR>	 3. Doing, performing.<BR>	 4. Enjoining.<BR> E. वि before, धा<BR>to have, (causal form,) aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायकत्व
विधायकत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Consignment or delivery of anything, making<BR>anything firm or secure.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायिन्
विधायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Causing, occasioning, making.<BR>	 2. Pla-<BR>cing, fixing, securing.<BR>	 3. Delivering, entrusting.<BR>	 4. Establishing<BR>as a rule or law.<BR> E. वि before, धा to have, causal form, aff. घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधाव्य|विधाव्यं
विधाव्य n. (-व्यं) Shaking, agitation.<BR> E. वि before, धू to shake, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधास्यत्
विधास्यत् mfn. (-स्यन्-स्यन्ती-स्यत्)<BR>	 1. Purposing or willing to do, make,<BR>cause, &c.<BR>	 2. Intending to direct, enjoin, prescribe, &c. वि before,<BR>धा to have, शतृ aff., in the future tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधि|विधिः
विधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. A sacred precept, an act or rite prescribed by the<BR>Vedas, for effecting certain consequences.<BR>	 2. Rule, form, formula.<BR>3. Fate, luck, destiny.<BR>	 4. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 5. Time.<BR>	 6. Order, injunction,<BR>command.<BR>	 7. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 8. Act, action, general or parti-<BR>cular.<BR>	 9. A text, a sentence in some authority of law or religion,<BR>prescribing any particular act or observance.<BR>	 10. Kind, sort,<BR>manner.<BR>	 11. Fodder, food for elephants or horses.<BR>	 12. A sacred<BR>work, a Shāśtra, scripture, the law, (by metonymy.)<BR>	 13. Creation.<BR>14. A physician.<BR> E. वि before, घा to have; or विध् to rule, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिघ्न
विधिघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Who or what deviates from, disregards, or dis-<BR>turbs rules or modes of proceeding.<BR> E. विधि, घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिज्ञ|विधिज्ञः
विधिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Who or what knows the prescribed mode,<BR>form, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ज्ञः) A Brāhmana who knows the ritual.<BR> E. विधि<BR>and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधितस्
विधितस् Ind. According to rule.<BR> E. विधि and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सा
विधित्सा f. (-त्सा) Wish to do or make, design, purpose, desire.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, धा to have, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सु
विधित्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सु-त्सु) Wishing to make, produce, &c.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>धा to have, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिदर्शिन्
विधिदर्शिन् m. (-र्शी) A priest whose business at a sacrifice is to see that<BR>every thing is done according to the prescribed rules, and to<BR>correct any deviation from them.<BR> E. विधि a sacred precept, and<BR>दर्शिन् who sees; also विधिदर्शक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिदेशक|विधिदेशकः
विधिदेशक m. (-कः) A priest who corrects errors at a sacrifice: see the<BR>last.<BR> E. विधि the proper form, and देशक who shows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिपूर्ब्बक
विधिपूर्ब्बक n. (-कं) Adv. After or according to rule.<BR> E. विधि, पूर्ब्बक prior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिप्रयोग|विधिप्रयोगः
विधिप्रयोग m. (-गः) Acting upon or in conformity to a rule, &c.<BR> E. विधि<BR>and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिप्रसङ्ग
विधिप्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Application of or acting upon a rule.<BR> E. विधि, प्रसङ्ग association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधियज्ञ|विधियज्ञः
विधियज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A ceremonial act of worship.<BR> E. विधि, यज्ञ sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधियोग|विधियोगः
विधियोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The occurence of predoomed events.<BR>	 2. Combina-<BR>tion for any act or rite.<BR> E. विधि and योग union, accession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिवत्
विधिवत् Ind. Agreeable to rule, conformably to established ordinances.<BR>E. विधि a precept, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिहीन
विधिहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Unauthorised, irregular.<BR> E. विधि and हीन abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधीयमान
विधीयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being defined, enjoined, directed, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, धा to have, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधु|विधुः
विधु m. (-धुः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. Camphor.<BR>	 4. A name of<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 5. A Rākshasa, a goblin.<BR>	 6. An expiatory oblation. E.<BR>व्यध् to pain or hurt, Unādi, aff. कु, and the semivowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुक्षय|विधुक्षयः
विधुक्षय m. (-यः) The wane of the moon.<BR> E. विधु and क्षय decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुत|विधुतः
विधुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Left, abandoned, relinquished.<BR>	 2. Shaken,<BR>trembling.<BR> E. वि before, धु to tremble, aff. क्तः see विधूत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुति|विधुतिः
विधुति f. (तिः) Shaking, trembling.<BR> E. वि before, धु to agitate, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुनन|विधुननं
विधुनन n. (-नं) Tremor, trembling.<BR> E. वि before, धू in the 10th cl., to<BR>shake, aff. ल्युट्, and the vowel short, or वि + धु-णिच्-नुकच्; also<BR>विधूनन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुन्तुद|विधुंतुद|विधुंतुदः|विधुन्तुदः
विधुन्तुद m. (-दः) RĀHU, the personified ascending node.<BR> E. विधु the<BR>moon, तुद् to torment, aff. खश् or क, and the nasal inserted, the<BR>cause of the moon's eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुन्वत्
विधुन्वत् mfn. (-न्वन्-न्वती-न्वत्) Shaking, tossing.<BR> E. वि before, धु to agitate, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुपिञ्जर|विधुपिंजर
विधुपिञ्जर m. (-रः) A cimeter, a sabre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुप्रिया
विधुप्रिया f. (-या) A lunar mansion; in mythology, personified as a<BR>nymph, the daughter of DAKṢA, and wife of CHANDRA or the<BR>moon.<BR> E. विधु the moon, and प्रिया the beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुर|विधुरं|विधुरः
विधुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Agitated, distressed, overcome with anxiety,<BR>distress, &c.<BR>	 2. Bewildered, confused, (with fear, liquor, &c.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Separate, absent from a mistress or lover.<BR>	 4. Destitute of, free<BR>from.<BR>	 5. Hostile, adverse.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A widower.<BR>	 n. (-र)<BR>	 1. Separa-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. Agitation of mind from terror or distress, &c.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>Curds mixed up with sugar and spices.<BR> E. वि before, धुर a load, &c.,<BR>aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुवन|विधुवनं
विधुवन n. (-नं) Trembling, tremor.<BR> E. वि before, धु to agitate, ल्युट् aff. and उवङ् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूत|विधूतं
विधूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken.<BR>	 2. Trembling, tremulous.<BR>	 3. Unsteady.<BR>4. Abandoned.<BR>	 5. Tossed, waving.<BR> E. वि before, धू to agitate, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूति|विधूतिः
विधूति f. (-तिः) Shaking, agitation, tremor.<BR> E. वि, धू to shake, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूनन|विधूननं
विधूनन n. (-नं) Shaking, trembling.<BR> E. वि before, धू agitate, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूनित|विधूनितं
विधूनित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken, literally or figuratively, agitated,<BR>alarmed.<BR>	 2. Harassed, annoyed.<BR> E. वि before, धू to shake, 10th cl.,<BR>aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूय
विधूय Ind. Having shaken, shaking, trembling.<BR> E. वि before, धू to shake, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूयमान
विधूयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being shaken, shaking, waving, agitated. E.<BR>वि before, धू to shake, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृत|विधृतं
विधृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seized, held.<BR>	 2. Withheld, restrained.<BR>	 3. Hav-<BR>ing, possessing, assumed, taken.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Disregard of an injunc-<BR>tion or desire.<BR>	 2. Dissatisfaction.<BR> E. वि before, धृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेय|विधेयः
विधेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Compliant, tractable, governable.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>done, what is or ought to be practised.<BR>	 3. Proper to be enjoined as<BR>a rule or law.<BR>	 4. To be predicated.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A servant.<BR>	 n. (-य) The<BR>predicate of a sentence.<BR> E. वि before, धा to have, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयता
विधेयता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Necessary or proper act or conduct.<BR>	 2. Docility,<BR>submission.<BR>	 3. Fitness or enactment as a rule or law.<BR> E. तल् added<BR>to the last; also with त्व, विधेयत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=659-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयपद
विधेयपद n. (-दं) An affair to be done, an object to be accomplished. E.<BR>विधेय, पद place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयमार्ग
विधेयमार्ग n. (-र्गं) Attempting or seeking to do any necessary act.<BR> E. विधेय, मार्ग seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयाविमर्श|विधेयाविमर्शः
विधेयाविमर्श m. (-र्शः) Imperfect or inadequate expression of the predi-<BR>cate, giving a subordinate position to the predicate, (considered<BR>as a fault of composition.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्यत्|विध्यन्त्
विध्यत् mfn. (-ध्यन्-ध्यन्ती-ध्यत्) Piercing, striking, killing.<BR> E. व्यध् to pierce, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्यमान
विध्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being pierced, struck, wounded, &c.<BR> E. व्यध् to<BR>pierce, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंस|विध्वंसः
विध्वंस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Aversion, disrespect, enmity, dislike.<BR>	 2. Offence,<BR>insult.<BR>	 2. Destruction.<BR> E. वि before, ध्वंस् to fall, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंसिन्
विध्वंसिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>	 1. Hostile, adverse.<BR>	 2. Destroying.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, ध्वंस् to fall, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वस्त
विध्वस्त f. (-स्ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Ruined, destroyed.<BR>	 2. Obscured, darkened.<BR>	 3. Tossed up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनत|विनतः
विनत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bent, bowed, stooping.<BR>	 2. Crooked, curved.<BR>	 3.<BR>Humble, modest.<BR>	 4. Sunk down, depressed.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The wife of<BR>KAŚYAPA, and mother of ARUṆA and GARUḌA.<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>basket.<BR> E. वि before, नम् to bow, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनतासूनु|विनतासूनुः
विनतासूनु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. ARUṆA, the charioteer of the sun.<BR>	 2. GARUḌA, the<BR>younger brother of ARUṆA.<BR> E. विनता the mother of these two, सूनु<BR>the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनति|विनतिः
विनति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Bowing, bending.<BR>	 2. Humility, modesty.<BR> E. वि before, नम् to bow, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनद|विनदः
विनद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Sound, noise.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR> E. वि, नद्<BR>to sound, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनद्य
विनद्य Ind. Having sounded, sounding.<BR> E. वि, नद् to sound, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनमन|विनमनं
विनमन n. (-नं) Bending, bowing.<BR> E. वि before, नम् to bend, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनमित
विनमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bowed down, declined.<BR> E. वि and नमित bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्र
विनम्र mfn. (-म्रः-म्रा-म्रं)<BR>	 1. Bent, bowed.<BR>	 2. Humble, modest.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>नम्र bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्रक|विनम्रकं
विनम्रक n. (-कं) The flower of the TAGARA tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनय|विनयः
विनय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Modesty, affability, humility, mildness.<BR>	 2. Reverence,<BR>obeisance.<BR>	 3. Decorum, decency, propriety of conduct or beha-<BR>viour.<BR>	 4. Training, discipline.<BR>	 5. Subduing the senses.<BR>	 6. A man<BR>of subdued senses.<BR>	 7. A merchant.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Secret.<BR>	 2. Cast,<BR>thrown.<BR>	 3. A plant. (Sida cordifolia, &c.)<BR> E. वि before, नी to obtain<BR>or guide, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयग्राहिन्
विनयग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Compliant, tractable, humble, govern-<BR>able.<BR> E. विनय humility, and ग्राहिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयन|विनयनं
विनयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Removing.<BR>	 2. Education, instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयप्रमाथिन्
विनयप्रमाथिन् mfn. (-थी-थिनी-थि) Behaving ill or improperly.<BR> E. विनय,<BR>प्रमाथिन् vexing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयभाज्
विनयभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Modest, well-behaved.<BR> E. विनय, भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयवाच्
विनयवाच् mfn. (-वाक्) Speaking humbly or modestly.<BR>	 f. (-वाक्) Modest<BR>speech.<BR> E. विनय, and वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयस्य
विनयस्य mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Compliant, tractable, governable.<BR> E. विनय<BR>humility, स्थ who stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनर्द्दत्|विनर्दत्
विनर्द्दत् mfn. (-र्द्दन्-र्द्दन्ती-र्द्दत्) Sounding, making a noise.<BR> E. वि, नद्द् to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनशन|विनशनं|विनशनः
विनशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Destroying, destruction.<BR>	 2. A country, north-west of<BR>Delhī, Kurukshetra, the vicinity of the modern Pāniput.<BR> E. वि<BR>before नश् to destroy, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विणश्यत्
विणश्यत् mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्) Perishing, decaying, perishable.<BR> E. वि, नश् to perish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनश्वर
विनश्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Perishable.<BR> E. वि before, नश् to perish, क्वरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनष्ट|विनष्टः
विनष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Lost, destroyed ruined, perished.<BR>	 2. Corrup-<BR>ted.<BR>	 3. Disappeared.<BR> E. वि, नष्ट the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनष्टि|विनष्टिः
विनष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Disappearance, destruction.<BR> E. वि before, नश् to finish, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनस|विनसः
विनस mfn. (-सः-सा or सी-सं) Noseless.<BR> E. वि priv., नस् for नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विना
विना Ind. Without, except.<BR> E. वि privative, ना aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाकृत|विनाकृतं
विनाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abandoned, left, relinquished.<BR> E. विना except, कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाडिका
विनाडिका f. (-का) The 60th part of an Indian hour.<BR> E. वि, and नाडिका<BR>a Nārī, or hour of twenty-four minutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाथ
विनाथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Deserted, unprotected, unowned.<BR> E. वि priv.,<BR>नाथ a lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनायक|विनायकः
विनायक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A Buddha, a Bauddha, deified teacher.<BR>	 2. GAṆE-<BR>ŚA.<BR>	 3. GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. A Guru, or<BR>spiritual preceptor.<BR>	 5. An obstacle, an impediment or difficulty.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-यिका) The wife of GARUḌA.<BR> E. वि before, नी to conduct, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाश|विनाशः
विनाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Disappearance, destruction, loss, annihilation, ruin,<BR>decay.<BR>	 2. Removal.<BR> E. वि before, नश् to perish, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशक|विनाशकः
विनाशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Destroying, a destroyer.<BR> E. वि before, नश् to<BR>perish, causal form, aff. वुञ् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशधर्मिन्
विनाशधर्मिन् m. (-र्मी)<BR>	 1. Subject to decay, transient.<BR>	 2. Having the<BR>property of killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशयत्
विनाशयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Destroying.<BR> E. वि before, नश् to perish, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशित
विनाशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Destroyed.<BR> E. वि, नश् to perish, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशिन्
विनाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि)<BR>	 1. Destroyer, destructive.<BR>	 2. Perishing,<BR>being destroyed.<BR>	 3. Undergoing change or transformation.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, नश् to perish, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशोन्मुख|विनाशोन्मुखं
विनाशोन्मुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>	 1. Ripe, mature.<BR>	 2. About to perish. E.<BR>विनाश perishing, उन्मुख in the presence of; verging to rottenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनासक|विनासकः
विनासक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Noseless.<BR> E. वि privative, नासिका the nose, or<BR>नासा with कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाह|विनाहः
विनाह m. (-हः) The top or cover for the mouth of a well.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>नह् to bind or tie, aff. घञ्; also वीनाह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिःसरण
विनिःसरण n. (-णं) Going forth or out.<BR> E. वि and निर्, before सृ to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिःसृत
विनिःसृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone forth or out.<BR> E. वि and निर्, before सृत<BR>gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षिप्त|विनिक्षिप्तः
विनिक्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Tossed, thrown, sent.<BR> E. वि and नि, before क्षिप्त thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षेप|विनिक्षेपः
विनिक्षेप m. (-पः) Tossing, throwing, sending.<BR> E. वि and नि, before क्षिप्<BR>to throw, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिग्रह|विनिग्रहः
विनिग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Restraining, subduing.<BR>	 2. Mutual opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिघ्नत्
विनिघ्नत् mfn. (-घ्नन्-घ्नती-घ्नत्) Killing.<BR> E. वि before, हन् to kill, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिद्र|विनिद्रः
विनिद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Blown, budded.<BR>	 2. Awake, awakened, sleep-<BR>less.<BR> E. वि privative, निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिद्रत्व|विनिद्रत्वं
विनिद्रत्व n. (-त्वं) Vigilance, wakefulness, waking.<BR> E. विनिद्र sleepless, त्व<BR>aff.; also with तल्, विनिद्रता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिधाय
विनिधाय Ind. Having taken or placed.<BR> E. वि and नि, before धा to have, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपात|विनिपातः
विनिपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Falling, falling down, (literally or figuratively, as<BR>from a height, or from dignity, virtue, &c.)<BR>	 2. Calamity, unavoid-<BR>able evil, the infliction of the gods or of fate.<BR>	 3. Disrespect.<BR>	 4.<BR>Pain, distress.<BR>	 5. Death, destruction.<BR> E. वि and नि, prefixed to पत्<BR>to fall, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपातशंसिन्
विनिपातशंसिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Portentous, announcing misfortune or<BR>destruction.<BR> E. विनिपात, शंसिन् what proclaims.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपातित
विनिपातित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Killed, destroyed.<BR>	 2. Thrown down.<BR> E. वि<BR>and नि, before पत् to fall, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपात्य
विनिपात्य Ind. Having killed.<BR> E. वि and नि, before पत् to fall, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिमय|विनिमयः
विनिमय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Barter, exchange.<BR>	 2. A pledge, a deposit or secu-<BR>rity.<BR> E. वि and नि, prefixed to मी to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिमेष|विनिमेषः
विनिमेष m. (-षः) Twinkling of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियत
विनियत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Regulated, restrained.<BR> E. वि and नि, before यम् to restrain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियम|विनियमः
विनियम m. (-मः) Restraint, government.<BR> E. वि and नि, before यम् to res-<BR>train, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियम्य
विनियम्य Ind. Having restrained, checked.<BR> E. वि and नि, before यम् to restrain, aff. ल्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियुक्त
विनियुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Separated, sundered or detached from,<BR>absent, parted.<BR>	 2. Appointed, attached to.<BR>	 3. Parted with for a<BR>specific purpose.<BR>	 4. Applied to, employed in.<BR>	 5. Enjoined, com-<BR>manded.<BR> E. वि and नि, before युज् to join, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियोक्तव्य
विनियोक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be employed in, applied to, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>and नि, before युज् to join, तव्यर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियोग|विनियोगः
विनियोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Giving or parting with anything for a considera-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">Page661-a+ 60</a>]<BR>tion, or in expectation of some advantage.<BR>	 2. Abandoning, leav-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Separation or detachment from.<BR>	 4. Impediment.<BR>	 5. Ap-<BR>pointment to any office, &c.<BR>	 6. Application to or employment<BR>in.<BR> E. वि and नि, before युज् to join, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=660-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियोजित|विनियोजितः
विनियोजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Appointed, appropriated, applied, (as to<BR>any particular duty or purpose, &c.)<BR>	 2. Attached or joined to.<BR>	 3.<BR>Deputed, appointed.<BR>	 4. Employed.<BR> E. वि and नि, before युज् to join,<BR>aff. क्त, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्गत
विनिर्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone out or from.<BR> E. वि and निर्, before गम् to<BR>go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्गम|विनिर्गमः
विनिर्गम m. (-मः) Going forth or out.<BR> E. वि and निर्, before गम् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्जय|विनिर्जयः
विनिर्जय m. (-यः) Victory, conquest.<BR> E. वि and निर्, before जि to conquer,<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्ज्जित|विनिर्जित
विनिर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Conquered, overcome.<BR> E. वि and निर्, before<BR>जि to conquer, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्णय|विनिर्णयः
विनिर्णय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 2. A settled rule.<BR> E. वि, निर्णय the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्णीत
विनिर्णीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Certain, determined, ascertained.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>निर्णीत the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्द्धूत
विनिर्द्धूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Scattered, dissipated, dispersed.<BR> E. वि, निर्द्धूत shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्धूय
विनिर्धूय Ind. Having dispersed, scattered, thrown off, &c.<BR> E. वि and निर्,<BR>before धू to agitate, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्बन्ध|विनिर्बंध|विनिर्बंधः|विनिर्बन्धः
विनिर्बन्ध m. (-न्धः) Persistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मुक्त
विनिर्मुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Liberated, let loose or free.<BR>	 2. Exempt,<BR>free from.<BR> E. वि and निर्, before मुच् to loose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्य्यत्|विनिर्यत्
विनिर्य्यत् mfn. (र्य्यन्-र्य्यन्ती-र्य्यत्) Going out or forth, issuing.<BR> E. वि and निर्,<BR>before या to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्वृत्त|विनिर्वृत्तः
विनिर्वृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Excited, occasioned, produced, occurring.<BR>2. Completed, finished.<BR> E. वि and निर् privative or intensitive pre-<BR>fixes, वृत् to be, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवारित
विनिवारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Kept off, resisted, prevented.<BR>	 2. Screened,<BR>covered, kept out of view.<BR> E. वि and नि, before वॄ to chuse, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्त|विनिवृत्तः
विनिवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Stopped, ceased, ended, refrained, resting or<BR>desisting, &c.<BR> E. वि and नि privatives, वृत् to be, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्ति|विनिवृत्तिः
विनिवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Stop, term, cessation.<BR> E. वि and नि, before वृत् to be,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवेश|विनिवेशः
विनिवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Entrance.<BR>	 2. Impression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चय|विनिश्चयः
विनिश्चय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Certainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 2. Resolntion, decision.<BR>E. वि and निश्चय certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चल
विनिश्चल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Firm, steady, immovable.<BR> E. वि, निश्चल steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चित
विनिश्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Certain, determined, ascertained.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>निश्चित the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्वसत्
विनिश्वसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Sighing.<BR>	 2. Breathing hard.<BR> E. वि and<BR>नि, before श्वस् to breathe, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्वास|विनिश्वासः
विनिश्वास m. (-सः) Strong expiration, sighing, a sigh, breathing hard.<BR>E. वि and नि, before श्वस् to breathe, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पेष|विनिष्पेषः
विनिष्पेष m. (-षः) Grinding, bruising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहत|विनिहतः
विनिहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Struck, wounded.<BR>	 2. Overcome.<BR>	 3. Killed.<BR>m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A portent, a comet, a meteor.<BR>	 2. A great or un-<BR>avoidable calamity; the infliction of fate or heaven.<BR> E. वि and नि<BR>intensitive prefixes, हत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिह्नुत
विनिह्नुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Hidden, concealed.<BR> E. वि, निह्नुत the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीत|विनीतः
विनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Modest, humble, unassuming, unpretending.<BR>2. Compliant, governable, tractable.<BR>	 3. Placid, meek, virtuous,<BR>gentle, having the passions restrained, and the senses under sub-<BR>jection.<BR>	 4. Well-behaved, decent, decorous.<BR>	 5. Taken away.<BR>	 6.<BR>Trained, (as a horse or ox, &c.)<BR>	 7. Thrown, sent, dismissed.<BR>	 8.<BR>Lovely, handsome.<BR>	 9. Led, conveyed.<BR>	 10. Chastised, punished.<BR>	 11.<BR>Plain, neat, (in dress, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A horse trained for the<BR>manege.<BR>	 2. A merchant, a trader.<BR> E. वि before, नी to guide, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतक|विनीतकं
विनीतक mn. (-कः-कं) A mediate conveyance, as a bearer carrying a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">Page661-b+ 60</a>]<BR>litter, or a horse dragging a carriage.<BR> E. वि implying sort or kind,<BR>and नी to take, aff. क्त, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतात्मन्
विनीतात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>	 1. Well-behaved.<BR>	 2. Humble, lowly. E.<BR>विनीत, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीय|विनीयः
विनीय Ind. Having taken.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Sediment, dregs.<BR>	 2. Sin.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, नी to take, aff. क्यप् or ल्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनुद्यमान
विनुद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being sent, ordered, dispatched, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, नुद to send, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेतृ
विनेतृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A guide, an instructor, a teacher.<BR>	 2. A king, a ruler.<BR>3. A chastiser.<BR> E. वि before, नी to conduct, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेय|विनेयः
विनेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be taken, to be taken away or separated,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. To be governed or directed, docile, governable.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>नी to take or obtain, &c., aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेश्यत्
विनेश्यत् mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्) Wishing or intending to take, to deprive<BR>of, &c.<BR> E. वि before, नी to take, शतृ aff. with a future sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोक्ति|विनोक्तिः
विनोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) The rhetorical use of the word, ‘without’ as, का निशा<BR>शशिना विना? What is the night without the moon.<BR> E. विना, उक्ति<BR>saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोद|विनोदः
विनोद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Eagerness, vehemence.<BR>	 2. Play, sport, pastime.<BR>	 3.<BR>Dismissing, abandoning.<BR>	 4. Diversion, interest, interesting pursuit<BR>or occupation.<BR>	 5. Pleasure, gratification.<BR>	 6. Driving away, re-<BR>moving.<BR> E. वि before, नुद् to order, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदित
विनोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dismissed, dissipated, sent or driven away.<BR>2. Allayed, soothed.<BR>	 3. Delighted, made happy.<BR> E. वि before, नुद्<BR>to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्द|विन्दः
विन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Who or what finds, gets, gains, &c.<BR> E. विद् to gain, श aff., नुन् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दु|विंदु|विन्दुः
विन्दु mfn. (-न्दुः-न्दुः-न्दु)<BR>	 1. Intelligent, knowing.<BR>	 2. Liberal, munificent.<BR>m. (-न्दुः)<BR>	 1. A drop of water or any liquid.<BR>	 2. A spot, a dot, a<BR>mark.<BR>	 3. The bite or mark of a tooth.<BR>	 4. The part of the forehead<BR>between the eyebrows.<BR>	 5. A mark or spot of coloured paint on<BR>an elephant's face or trunk.<BR>	 6. The dot over a letter representing<BR>the nasal termination.<BR>	 7. A secondary but connecting incident<BR>in a drama.<BR> E. विद to know, to be, to be a part of, Unādi aff. उ,<BR>and the nasal augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुचित्रक|विन्दुचित्रकः
विन्दुचित्रक m. (-कः) The spotted deer.<BR> E. विन्दु a spot, चित्रक variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुजाल|विन्दुजालं
विन्दुजाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Coloured marks or spots on an elephant's face and<BR>trunk, &c.<BR>	 2. A collection of particles or drops.<BR> E. विन्दु a spot,<BR>and जाल multitude; also with कन् added विन्दुजालक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुतन्त्र|विन्दुतन्त्रः
विन्दुतन्त्र m. (-न्त्रः) A die, a dice.<BR> E. विन्दु dot, and तन्त्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुरेखक|विन्दुरेखकः
विन्दुरेखक m. (-कः) A kind of bird.<BR> E. विन्दु a spot, रेखा a line, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्धपत्र
विन्धपत्र m. (-त्रः) Bel-Suṇṭh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्य|विंध्यः|विन्ध्यः
विन्ध्य m. (-न्ध्यः)<BR>	 1. The Vindhya mountain, or the mountainous range<BR>which runs across India from the Province of Behār, nearly to<BR>Guzerāt, and properly divides Hindusthān from the Dakshin.<BR>	 2.<BR>A hunter.<BR>	 f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>	 1. A fruit, (Annona reticulata.)<BR>	 2. Small car-<BR>damoms.<BR> E. वि implying opposition, ध्यै to think, and क aff., form<BR>irr., the mountain is supposed to obstruct the course of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यकूट|विन्ध्यकूटः
विन्ध्यकूट m. (-टः) The saint AGASTYA.<BR> E. विन्ध्य the mountain, and कूट् to<BR>give pain, aff. क, or with युच् aff. विन्ध्यकूटन; Vindhya the personi-<BR>fied mountain, having once prostrated himself before AGASTYA<BR>his spiritual guide, was ordered by the saint to remain in that<BR>posture, as a punishment for the presumption, which had in-<BR>duced him to attempt rivalling the heighth of Meru and Himā-<BR>laya. The legend appears to originate in the little elevation of the<BR>Vindhya-chain compared with its extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यवासिन्
विन्ध्यवासिन् m. (-सी) The saint and grammarian VYĀRI.<BR>	 f. (-सिनी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A village and temple sacred to DURGĀ under<BR>the forms of Yoga-Māyā, and Bhoga-Māyā and a place of<BR>great resort amongst the Hindus, situated about three miles from<BR>MIRZĀPUR on the Ganges.<BR> E. विन्ध्य the mountain, वासिन् who dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=661-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यस्थ|विन्ध्यस्थः
विन्ध्यस्थ m. (-स्थः) The name of a Muni; also VYĀRI, a saint, and ins-<BR>pired grammarian.<BR> E. विन्ध्य the mountain, and स्थ abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्याचल
विन्ध्याचल m. (-लः) The Vindhya-range or mountains.<BR> E. विन्ध्य and अचल<BR>a mountain; also विन्ध्यपर्व्वत, and विन्ध्यशैल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्याटवी
विन्ध्याटवी f. (-वी) The great Vindhya forest, which appears to have<BR>spread at one time from near MATHURĀ to the Narmadā.<BR> E. विन्ध्य<BR>and अटवी a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यावलीपुत्त्र
विन्ध्यावलीपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) A name of the Demon Vāṇa.<BR> E. विन्ध्यावली the<BR>mother of the demon, and पुत्त्र son; also विन्ध्यावलीसुत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्न|विन्नः
विन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Judged, discussed.<BR>	 2. Gained, obtained.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fixed, placed.<BR>	 4. Known.<BR>	 5. Married. &c.<BR> E. विद् to know, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्नक|विन्नकः
विन्नक m. (-कः) An epithet of the saint AGASTYA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्त|विन्यस्तः
विन्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Placed, deposited, fixed.<BR>	 2. Delivered.<BR>	 3.<BR>Offered, presented.<BR> E. वि and नि, before अस् to be or throw, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्याक|विन्याकः
विन्याक m. (-कः) A tree, (Echites scholaris.) “छातियान् इति भाषा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यास|विन्यासः
विन्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Assemblage, collection, collecting or depositing<BR>anything.<BR>	 2. Site, place, receptacle, that in or on which anything<BR>is placed or deposited.<BR>	 3. Orderly arrangement or disposition.<BR>	 4.<BR>Entrusting, depositing.<BR>	 5. A deposit.<BR> E. वि and नि, prefixed to अस्<BR>to take, to throw or place, &c. aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्
विप् r. 10th cl. (वेपयति-ते) To throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्व
विपक्व f. (-क्वा)<BR>	 1. Ripened.<BR>	 2. Cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्त्रिम
विपक्त्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Matured, ripened.<BR>	 2. Fulfilled, come to pass,<BR>as the consequence of former actions.<BR> E. वि and पच् to cook, क्त्रि<BR>aff., and मपच् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्ष|विपक्षः
विपक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Opposed or adverse to, contrary, inimical.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-क्षः)<BR>	 1. An enemy, an adversary.<BR>	 2. A disputant, an opponent.<BR>3. Exception, (in grammar, &c.)<BR>	 4. (In logic.) An argument or<BR>syllogism in which the proposition to be maintained is wanting.<BR>E. वि implying opposite, contrary, and पक्ष part or side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षतस्
विपक्षतस् Ind. Hostilely, inimically.<BR> E. विपक्ष and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षता
विपक्षता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Hostility, enmity, opposition.<BR>	 3. Controversy, con-<BR>tradiction in argument.<BR> E. तल् added to विपक्ष; also with त्व,<BR>विपक्षत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षपात
विपक्षपात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Indifferent, impartial.<BR> E. वि priv., पक्षपात an adherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपञ्चिका|विपंचिका
विपञ्चिका f. (-का) A lute.<BR> E. कन् fem. form, added to the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपञ्ची|विपंची
विपञ्ची f. (-ञ्ची)<BR>	 1. A lute.<BR>	 2. Play, sport, pastime.<BR> E. वि before, पचि to<BR>extend, (causal form,) to diffuse sounds, aff. अच्, fem. aff. ङीष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपण|विपणः
विपण m. (-णः) Sale, contract of sale.<BR> E. वि before, पण् to be of price,<BR>aff. घञ् or घ; also with ल्युट्, विपणन n. (-नं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणि|विपणिः
विपणि mf. (-णिः-णी)<BR>	 1. A place where things are sold, a shop, stall.<BR>2. Trade, traffic.<BR>	 3. A fair, a market place.<BR>	 4. The street of a<BR>market.<BR>	 5. An article or commodity for sale.<BR> E. वि before, पण् to<BR>transact business, aff. इन्, and fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणिन्
विपणिन् m. (-णी) A dealer, a trafficker, a shop-keeper or merchant. E.<BR>विपण sale, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्काल|विपत्कालः
विपत्काल n. (-लं) Time of calamity or misfortune, adversity.<BR> E. विपद्, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्ति|विपत्तिः
विपत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Adversity, calamity, misfortune.<BR>	 2. Pain, agony.<BR>	 3.<BR>Death, dying.<BR>	 m. (-त्तिः) A distinguished foot-soldier.<BR> E. वि im-<BR>plying reverse, पद् to go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्तियुक्त
विपत्तियुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Unfortunate.<BR> E. विपत्ति, युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्तिरहित
विपत्तिरहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Prosperous, happy.<BR> E. विपत्ति and रहित free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्सागर|विपत्सागरः
विपत्सागर m. (-रः) Heavy calamity.<BR> E. विपद् and सागर ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपथ|विपथः
विपथ mn. (-थः-थं) A bad road, a wrong way, (either lit or fig.)<BR> E. वि<BR>depreciative prefix, and पथ for पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्
विपद् f. (-पत् or पद्)<BR>	 1. Calamity, adversity, misfortune.<BR>	 2. Death.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, पद् to go, क्विप् aff.; also with टाप् added, विपदा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपदा
विपदा f. (दा) Adversity. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपदुद्धार|विपदुद्धारः
विपदुद्धार m. (-रः) Extrication from misfortune.<BR> E. विपत्, उद्धार lifting<BR>up; also विपदुद्धरणं, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्ग्रस्त
विपद्ग्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Overtaken by or involved in calamity. E.<BR>विपद् and ग्रन्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्युक्त
विपद्युक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Unhappy, unfortunate.<BR> E. विपद्, युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्रहित
विपद्रहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Prosperous.<BR> E. विपद् and रहित left by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्न|विपन्नः
विपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Unfortunate, declined, fallen into adversity<BR>or misfortune.<BR>	 2. Lost, destroyed, annihilated.<BR>	 3. Dead, defunct.<BR>4. Disabled.<BR>	 m. (-न्नः) A snake.<BR> E. वि implying reverse, and पद् to<BR>go, aff. क्त; also with कन् added विपन्नक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणाम|विपरिणामः
विपरिणाम m. (-मः) Change of state or form.<BR> E. वि and परि, before णम्<BR>to bow, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणामिन्
विपरिणामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Undergoing or producing change of<BR>state or form.<BR> E. वि and परि, before णम् to bow, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्त्तन|विपरिवर्तन|विपरिवर्तनं
विपरिवर्त्तन n. (-नं) Turning back or away from.<BR> E. वि and परिवर्त्तन turn-<BR>ing round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्त्तित|विपरिवर्तित
विपरिवर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Turned back or away from, reverted, aver-<BR>ted.<BR> E. वि and परि, before वृत् to turn, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीत|विपरीतः
विपरीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Reverse, inverse, opposite, contrary.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wrong, incorrect.<BR>	 3. Crossed.<BR>	 4. Disagreeable, inauspicious.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ता) A lewd woman, a dishonest wife.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A particular mode<BR>of coitus.<BR> E. वि and परि implying contrariety or adverse, before<BR>इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतकारिन्
विपरीतकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Perverse, contradictory, acting con-<BR>trary or another's wishes.<BR> E. विपरीत and कारिन् who does; also<BR>विपरीतकर, विपरीतकर्त्तृ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतगति
विपरीतगति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Going backwards or reversely.<BR>	 f. (-तिः)<BR>Inverse or reverse motion.<BR> E. विपरीत and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतता
विपरीतता f. (-ता) Contrariety, reverse or opposite state or condition.<BR>E. विपरीत and तल् aff.; also with त्व, विपरीतत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतरत
विपरीतरत n. (-तं) Inverted sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्णक|विपर्णकः
विपर्णक m. (-कः) The Palāsha tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. वि separate,<BR>पर्ण a leaf, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्य्यय|विपर्यय|विपर्ययः|विपर्य्ययः
विपर्य्यय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Contrariety, opposition.<BR>	 2. Reverse in general, and<BR>thence applied to that of which reverse is predicated, as misery,<BR>calamity, (the reverse of fortune;) error, misapprehension, (the<BR>reverse of reason or truth;) inverted order or succession, (the<BR>reverse that which is usual or prescribed,) &c.<BR>	 3. Destruction,<BR>annihilation.<BR>	 4. Perverseness of disposition.<BR>	 5. Change of purpose<BR>or conduct.<BR>	 6. Enmity, hostility.<BR>	 7. Absence, nonexistence.<BR>	 8.<BR>Exchange, barter.<BR> E. वि and परि implying reverse, and इण् to go,<BR>aff. अच्; also with घञ् aff. विपर्य्याय m. (-यः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्य्यस्त|विपर्यस्त
विपर्य्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Opposite, contrary, reverse.<BR>	 2. Conceived<BR>to be real, (what is not so.)<BR> E. वि and परि, before अस् to be or to<BR>throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्य्याय|विपर्याय|विपर्यायः|विपर्य्यायः
विपर्य्याय m. (-यः) Contrariety, &c.: see विपर्य्यय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्य्यास|विपर्यास|विपर्यासः|विपर्य्यासः
विपर्य्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Contrariety, opposition.<BR>	 2. Reverse.<BR>	 3. Investing<BR>imaginary things with real attributes, imagining what is unreal<BR>or false to be real or true.<BR> E. वि and परि, before अस् to be, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपल|विपलं
विपल n. (-लं) A moment, an instant, either a Pala or second, or (1/6)th<BR>of it; a simple breathing or one-tenth of the latter.<BR> E. वि and पल<BR>a second.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलायन|विपलायनं
विपलायन n. (-नं) Flying, running away.<BR> E. वि and पलायन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलायित
विपलायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Put to flight, run away.<BR> E. वि before, पलायित<BR>the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपव्य|विपव्यं
विपव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be cleansed or purified.<BR> E. वि before, पूञ् to purify, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्चित्
विपश्चित् m. (-श्चित) A Paṇḍit, a learned Brāhman, a teacher.<BR> E. वि and<BR>प, before चि to collect, affs. क्विप् and तुक् aug.; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्य
विपश्य n. (-श्यं) Knowledge.<BR> E. वि variously, पश्य seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्यिन्
विपश्यिन् m. (-श्यी) A Bauddha saint, the first of the seven principal<BR>Bauddhas.<BR> E. विपश्य and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाक|विपाकः
विपाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Cooking, dressing.<BR>	 2. Ripening, maturing.<BR>	 3. Fla-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">Page663-a+ 60</a>]<BR>vour, taste.<BR>	 4. Unexpected or improbable result.<BR>	 5. Poverty, dis-<BR>tress.<BR>	 6. Change of form or state.<BR>	 7. The consequences of actions,<BR>either in this or in a former birth; the operation or time in ma-<BR>turing their results.<BR>	 8. Assimilation of food, its conversion into<BR>a state differing from its original one, digestion.<BR> E. वि before, पच्<BR>to ripen, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=662-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाटन|विपाटनं
विपाटन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Splitting, tearing up.<BR>	 2. Spoliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाठ|विपाठः
विपाठ m. (-ठः) A kind of large arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाण्डुर
विपाण्डुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Pale, pallid, white.<BR> E. वि पाण्डुर pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादन|विपादनं
विपादन n. (-नं) Destroying, killing.<BR> E. वि before, पद् to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादनीय
विपादनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be killed, fit or proper to be destroyed.<BR>E. वि before, पद् to go, causal v., अनीयर् aff.; also विपाद्य and<BR>विपादयितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादिका
विपादिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A kibe, a sore or blister on the foot.<BR>	 2. A riddle,<BR>an enigma.<BR> E. वि before, पद् to go, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादित
विपादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Killed, destroyed.<BR> E. वि before, पद् to go,<BR>causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाल
विपाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Unattended, unguarded.<BR> E. वि priv., पल a keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाश्
विपाश् f. (-पाट्) The Vipās or Vipāsā river. E. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाश
विपाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Unnoosed, unfettered, freed from a noose or<BR>tie.<BR>	 f. (-शा)<BR>	 1. The Vipāsā or the Beyāh river in the Punjāb. E.<BR>वि privative, and पाश or पाशा a noose, from पश् to bind, causal<BR>form, with अच् and टाप् or क्विप् aff.; hence also विपाश्; the name<BR>applies to the river as having destroyed the cord which the Muni<BR>VAAISHṬHA had tied round his neck, when about to hang himself<BR>through grief for the death of his sons slain by VISWĀMITRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपिन|विपिनं
विपिन n. (-नं) A wood, a forest.<BR> E. वेप् to shake, Unādi aff. इनन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुल|विपुलः
विपुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Large, great.<BR>	 2. Broad.<BR>	 3. Deep, profound.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः)<BR>	 1. The mountain MERU, or rather the western branch of it.<BR>2. The Himālaya mountain.<BR>	 3. A respectable man.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The<BR>earth.<BR>	 2. A form of the Āryā metre in which the line is irregular-<BR>ly divided by the Cæsura or pause: three species of this form are<BR>reckoned; the Ādi-vipulā with the pause in the first line, Antya-<BR>vipulā in the second, and Ubhaya-vipulā in both lines.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore, पुल् to be large or lofty, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलक
विपुलक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Free from horripilation.<BR> E. वि privative and<BR>पुलक erection of the hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलजघना
विपुलजघना f. (-ना) A woman with large hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलता
विपुलता f. (-ता) Magnitude, extent.<BR> E. विपुल and तल् aff.; also with त्व, विपुलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलमति
विपुलमति Adj. Endowed with great power of understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलरस|विपुलरसः
विपुलरस m. (-सः) The sugar-cane.<BR> E. विपुल much, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलेक्षण
विपुलेक्षण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Large-eyed.<BR> E. विपुल and ईक्षण sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपूय|विपूयः
विपूय m. (-यः) The Munja grass, (Saccharum Munja.)<BR> E. वि before, पुञ्<BR>to cleanse, aff. क्यप्; that which is to be cleaned before making<BR>into ropes, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्र|विप्रः
विप्र m. (-प्रः)<BR>	 1. A Brāhman.<BR>	 2. The Aśwattha tree.<BR>	 3. (In prosody,) A<BR>foot of four short syllables.<BR> E. वि before, प्रा a Sautra root, to fill<BR>or complete, (the essential observances,) and क aff.; or वप् to<BR>shave, Unādi aff. रन्, and इ substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकर्ष|विप्रकर्षः
विप्रकर्ष m. (-र्षः) Distance.<BR> E. वि + प्र, कृष् to attract, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकार|विप्रकारः
विप्रकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Injury, contumely, abuse.<BR>	 2. Wickedness.<BR>	 3. Oppo-<BR>sition, counteraction.<BR>	 4. Retaliation.<BR> E. वि and प्र depreciative pre-<BR>fixes, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकारिन्
विप्रकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Opposed to, treating with contempt.<BR>	 2.<BR>Retaliating.<BR> E. वि and प्र, before कृ to do, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकीर्ण
विप्रकीर्ण f. (-र्णा) Adj.<BR>	 1. Scattered, dispersed.<BR>	 2. Loose, dishevelled.<BR>3. Broad, expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृत|विप्रकृतः
विप्रकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Reviled, abused, treated with contempt.<BR>	 2.<BR>Opposed, counteracted.<BR>	 3. Injured, offended.<BR>	 4. Retaliated, requit-<BR>ed.<BR> E. वि and प्र, before कृत made; made little or nothing of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृति|विप्रकृतिः
विप्रकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Abuse, injury, contumely.<BR>	 2. Retaliation, retort. E.<BR>वि and प्र implying depreciation or mutuality, and कृति action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्ट|विप्रकृष्टः
विप्रकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Remote, distant.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. Drawn away,<BR>removed.<BR>	 2. Protracted, lengthened.<BR> E. वि and प्र, before कृष् to<BR>attract, aff. क्त; also with कन् added, विप्रकृष्टक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिकार|विप्रतिकारः
विप्रतिकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Contradiction, counteraction, opposition.<BR>	 2.<BR>Reverse.<BR>	 3. Retaliation.<BR> E. वि and प्रति, before कृ to do, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिकृत
विप्रतिकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Opposed, counteracted.<BR>	 2. Requited.<BR> E. वि<BR>and प्रति, before कृ to do, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपत्ति|विप्रतिपत्तिः
विप्रतिपत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Perplexity, confusion.<BR>	 2. Various acquirement.<BR>	 3.<BR>Mutual connexion with or relation to.<BR>	 4. Conversancy.<BR>	 5. Con-<BR>tradiction, difference, discrepancy.<BR>	 6. Contest, dispute.<BR>	 7. Oppo-<BR>sition of interests.<BR> E. वि privative, or implying variety, and प्रति-<BR>पत्ति knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपद्य
विप्रतिपद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. To be opposed, contradicted, contested.<BR>2. To be acquired.<BR> E. वि and प्रति, before पद् to go, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपद्यमान
विप्रतिपद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being disputed or contested.<BR>	 2. Being<BR>in course of acquirement.<BR> E. वि and प्रति, before पद् to go, pass. v.,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपन्न
विप्रतिपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Bewildered, perplexed, confused, uncer-<BR>tain.<BR>	 2. Conversant or acquainted with in various ways, severally<BR>or mutually.<BR>	 3. Connected with.<BR>	 4. Contested, disputed.<BR>	 5. Con-<BR>tradicted.<BR>	 6. Opposed, (as interests.)<BR> E. वि and प्रतिपन्न ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिषेध|विप्रतिषेधः
विप्रतिषेध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. The conflict of two courses of equal importance.<BR>2. The conflict of two rules by which two different operations can<BR>be undertaken, (in gram.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिसार|विप्रतिसारः
विप्रतिसार m. (-रः) Repentance: see विप्रतीसार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिसिद्ध
विप्रतिसिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Contradicted, opposed.<BR>	 3. Prohibited, for-<BR>bidden.<BR> E. वि and प्रति implying opposition, सिद्ध proved, perfected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतीसार|विप्रतीसारः
विप्रतीसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Repentance.<BR>	 2. Evil, wickedness, evil action.<BR>	 3.<BR>Hate, enmity.<BR>	 4. Rage, wrath.<BR> E. वि implying reverse, प्रति to or<BR>towards, सृ to go, घञ् aff.; the इ of प्रति optionally long;<BR>otherwise विप्रतिसार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदह|विप्रदहः
विप्रदह m. (-हः) Dried fruit or roots, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदुष्ट
विप्रदुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Spoiled, vitiated, defiled.<BR>	 2. Bad corrupt. E.<BR>वि and प्र, before दुष्ट the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदुष्टभाव
विप्रदुष्टभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Bad, vicious, sensual, corrupt.<BR> E. विप्रदुष्ट and<BR>भाव disposition or nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमुक्त
विप्रमुक्त f. (-क्ता)<BR>	 1. Set free, liberated.<BR>	 2. Shot, discharged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमोच्य
विप्रमोच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) To be liberated or freed from.<BR> E. वि and प्र,<BR>before मुच् to loose, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयाण|विप्रयाणं
विप्रयाण n. (-णं) Flight, retreat.<BR> E. वि and प्र, before या to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयुक्त|विप्रयुक्तः
विप्रयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Separated, disjoined, sundered, away or<BR>absent from.<BR>	 2. Released from.<BR>	 3. Deprived of.<BR> E. वि implying<BR>separation, प्रयुक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयोग|विप्रयोगः
विप्रयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Separation, absence, especially the separation of<BR>lovers.<BR>	 2. Disunion, disjunction.<BR>	 3. Quarrel, disagreement.<BR>	 4. De-<BR>serving.<BR> E. वि before, प्रयोग union, contiguity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलब्ध|विप्रलब्धः
विप्रलब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Tricked, cheated, deceived.<BR>	 2. Disappoint-<BR>ed.<BR>	 f. (-ब्धी) A mistress whose lover is not true to his appointment,<BR>(considered as a character in drama.)<BR> E. वि and प्र, before लब्ध gained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भ|विप्रलंभ|विप्रलंभः|विप्रलम्भः
विप्रलम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Tricking, deceiving, disappointing, deceiving by a<BR>false affirmation or by not keeping a promise.<BR>	 2. Separation, es-<BR>pecially of lovers.<BR>	 3. Disunion, disjunction.<BR>	 4. Quarrel, disagree-<BR>ment.<BR>	 5. The sentiment of love in separation, (opposite to सम्भोग.)<BR>E. वि and प्र implying reverse, लभि to get or gain, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलय|विप्रलयः
विप्रलय m. (-यः) Annihilation, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलाप|विप्रलापः
विप्रलाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Quarrel, wrangling, mutual contradiction.<BR>	 2. Idle<BR>or unmeaning discourse, nonsense.<BR>	 3. Infraction of a promise. E.<BR>वि and प्र implying contradiction or reciprocity, and लाप talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=663-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुप्त
विप्रलुप्त f. (-प्ता)<BR>	 1. Snatched away.<BR>	 2. Disturbed, interrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुम्पक
विप्रलुम्पक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Rapacious, exacting, avaricious.<BR> E. वि and प्र,<BR>before लुपि to cut, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवास|विप्रवासः
विप्रवास m. (-सः) Residence in a foreign country.<BR> E. वि and प्र implying<BR>separation, वस् to abide, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवासन|विप्रवासनं
विप्रवासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Residence abroad.<BR>	 2. Banishment.<BR> E. वि and प्र, before<BR>वस् to dwell, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रश्निका
विप्रश्निका f. (-का) A female fortuneteller.<BR> E. वि variously, पृच् to ask,<BR>aff. इञ्, with नङ् augment, and ठन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रसात्
विप्रसात् Ind. As, like as, one with, a Brāhmaṇa.<BR> E. विप्र, and साति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रस्व
विप्रस्व n. (-स्वं) The property of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR> E. विप्र, and स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रहीण
विप्रहीण f. (-णा) Deprived of, destitute of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रापवाद
विप्रापवाद m. (-दः) Abuse of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR> E. विप्र, and अपवाद reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रिय|विप्रियः
विप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Disliked, unbeloved, disagreeable.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>Offence, transgression.<BR> E. वि privative, and प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रुष्
विप्रुष् f. (-प्रुट्)<BR>	 1. A drop of water, &c.<BR>	 2. A spot, a mark, a dot.<BR> E. वि<BR>privative, प्रुष् to burn, aff. क्विप्; also विप्लुष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोषित|विप्रोषितः
विप्रोषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Absent, away from.<BR>	 2. Banished.<BR> E. वि and<BR>प्र, before वस् to dwell, aff. क्त, the semi-vowel changed to उ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोषितभर्त्तृका|विप्रोषितभर्तृका
विप्रोषितभर्त्तृका f. (-का) A woman whose husband or lover is absent. E.<BR>विप्रोषित absent, भर्त्तृ a husband, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोष्य
विप्रोष्य Ind. Having been absent, returning, coming home.<BR> E. वि and<BR>प्र, before वस् to dwell, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लव|विप्लवः
विप्लव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Tumult, confusion, trouble.<BR>	 2. Evil, calamity.<BR>	 3. Ra-<BR>pine, extortion.<BR>	 4. Sin, wickedness.<BR>	 5. Predatory or irregular<BR>warfare.<BR>	 6. Affray, scuffle.<BR>	 7. Terrifying an enemy by shouts and<BR>gestures.<BR>	 8. Confusion, perplexity, (of thought or speech.)<BR>	 9.<BR>Floating about.<BR>	 10. The rust, (of a mirror.)<BR>	 11. Loss, destruction.<BR>E. वि before, प्लु to go, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लाव|विप्लावः
विप्लाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Deluging, inundating.<BR>	 2. Devastating.<BR>	 3. Causing<BR>tumult or public disturbance.<BR>	 4. A horse's canter or gallop.<BR> E. वि,<BR>and प्लु to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लाव्य
विप्लाव्य Ind.<BR>	 1. Having cast away, defiled, contaminated.<BR>	 2. Having<BR>taught at improper seasons.<BR>	 3. Having caused to be deluged,<BR>devastated, &c.<BR> E. वि before, प्लु to go, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुत|विप्लुतः
विप्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Depraved, wicked, addicted to evil practices,<BR>as gaming, whoring, &c.<BR>	 2. Committing any crime.<BR>	 3. Contrary,<BR>adverse, averse.<BR>	 4. Inundated, immersed.<BR>	 5. Devastated, ravaged.<BR>6. Disturbed, confounded.<BR>	 7. Ruined, disgraced.<BR>	 8. Disappeared.<BR>9. Disfigured, obscured.<BR> E. वि before, प्लु to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुष्
विप्लुष् f. (प्लुट्)<BR>	 1. A drop of any fluid.<BR>	 2. A spot, a dot.<BR> E. वि before, प्लुष्<BR>to burn, aff. क्विप्; also विप्रुष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्सा
विप्सा f. (-प्सा) Repetition, succession: see वीप्सा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफल|विफलं
विफल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Vain, idle, unmeaning, fruitless, useless.<BR> E. वि<BR>privative, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलता
विफलता f. (-ता) Unprofitableness, fruitlessness.<BR> E. विफल, and तल् added; also विफलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीकरण
विफलीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Frustrating, foiling, defeating.<BR>	 2. Doing any<BR>thing in vain.<BR> E. विफल, and करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीकृत
विफलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rendered vain, frustrated.<BR>	 2. Done in vain.<BR>E. विफल, and कृत done, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीभविष्णु
विफलीभविष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Become unprofitable.<BR> E. विफल, and भविष्णु<BR>become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीभविष्णुता
विफलीभविष्णुता f. (-ता) Unprofitableness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also<BR>विफलीभविष्णुत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीभूत
विफलीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Become useless.<BR> E. विफल and भूत become, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबन्ध|विबंध|विबंधः|विबन्धः
विबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Ischury or constipation.<BR> E. वि before, बन्ध् to bind, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबाधा
विबाधा f. (-धा) Pain, agony, anguish.<BR> E. वि various, बाधा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुद्ध
विबुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Awake, aroused.<BR>	 2. Unconscious.<BR>	 3. Blossomed,<BR>expanded.<BR>	 4. Clever, skilful.<BR> E. वि, and बुद्ध wakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुध|विबुधः
विबुध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A god, an immortal.<BR>	 2. A Paṇḍit, a learned man,<BR>a teacher.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR> E. वि variously, बुध् to know, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोध|विबोधः
विबोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Inattention, absence.<BR>	 2. Intelligence.<BR>	 3. Awaking.<BR>	 4.<BR>Discovering any circumstance.<BR>	 5. Becoming conscious, (considered<BR>as one of the thirty-three subordinate feelings in rhetoric.)<BR> E. वि<BR>privative or intensitive, and बोध understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोधित
विबोधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Awakened.<BR>	 2. Instructed.<BR> E. वि before, बुध्<BR>to know, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्त|विभक्तः
विभक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Divided, portioned, partitioned.<BR>	 2. Separa-<BR>ted, parted.<BR>	 3. Dividing, sharing, a partner.<BR>	 4. Distinct.<BR>	 5. Dif-<BR>ferent, multifarious.<BR>	 6. Retired, isolated.<BR>	 7. Symmetrical.<BR>	 8. Orna-<BR>mental.<BR> E. वि severally, भज् to divide, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्तज|विभक्तजः
विभक्तज m. (-जः) A son born after partition of the family property be-<BR>tween his parents and brethren.<BR> E. विभक्त divided, (being or having<BR>been,) and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्ति|विभक्तिः
विभक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Part, portion, inheritance or share of inheritance,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A division, a partition.<BR>	 3. Inflexion of nouns, declension.<BR>E. वि before, भज to divide, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभङ्ग|विभंग|विभंगः|विभङ्गः
विभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Breaking, fracture.<BR>	 2. Division.<BR>	 3. Bending, contracting, (especially of the eyebrows.)<BR>4. Expression or play of<BR>features.<BR>	 5. Obstruction, stoppage.<BR> E. वि, भजि to break, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभजनीय|विभजनीयं
विभजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be portioned or partitioned.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>भज् to divide, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्य
विभज्य Ind. Having divided, portioned, &c.<BR> E. वि before, भज् to divide, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्यमान
विभज्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Divisible, portionable, to be or being divided<BR>or parted.<BR> E. वि before, भज् to divide, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभव|विभवः
विभव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Substance, thing, property, wealth.<BR>	 2. Emancipation<BR>from existence.<BR>	 3. Supreme or superhuman power.<BR>	 4. Magnani-<BR>mity, lofty-mindedness.<BR> E. वि implying variety, privation, &c., and<BR>भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभा
विभा f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. A ray of light.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR>	 3. Beauty.<BR> E. वि va-<BR>riously, भा to shine, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाकर|विभाकरः
विभाकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR> E. विभा light, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाग|विभागः
विभाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Part, portion, share.<BR>	 2. The share or portion of an<BR>inheritance.<BR>	 3. Partition of inheritance.<BR>	 4. (In arithmetic.) The<BR>numerator of a fraction.<BR>	 5. Separation, disjunction, (considered<BR>as a Guṇa in Nyāya Phil.<BR> E. वि implying variously, भाग a portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागकल्पना
विभागकल्पना f. (-ना) Apportioning or allotment of shares or portions.<BR>E. विभाग a division, and कल्पना a making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागतस्
विभागतस् Ind. Proportionately, according to a part or share.<BR> E. विभाग,<BR>and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागधर्म|विभागधर्मः
विभागधर्म m. (-र्मः) The law of inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागपत्रिका
विभागपत्रिका f. (-का) A deed of partition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागभाक्
विभागभाक् m. (-भाक्) One who shares in a portion of property already<BR>distributed, applied especially to a son by a father and mother of<BR>the same tribe, born subsequent to a distribution of property<BR>amongst his parents and brethren, in which case he inherits the<BR>portion allotted or reserved to the parents.<BR> E. विभाग a portion, and<BR>भाक् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागशस्
विभागशस् Ind. Proportionately, according to a part or share.<BR> E. विभाग, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाजन|विभाजनं
विभाजन n. (-नं) Distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाज्य|विभाज्यं
विभाज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) Divisible, portionable, what may be divided<BR>or apportioned.<BR> E. वि severally, भज् to divide, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभात्
विभात् mfn. (-भान्-भान्ती or भाती-भात्) Shining, splendid.<BR> E. वि before, भा<BR>to shine, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभात|विभातं
विभात n. (-तं) Dawn, day-break.<BR> E. वि before, भा to shine, aff. क्त; also विभातक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाव|विभावः
विभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A friend or acquaintance.<BR>	 2. One of the Bhāyas or<BR>classes of properties into which the objects of poetical composi-<BR>tion are divided; the causative or exciting property, as dress,<BR>perfumes, &c. of amorous desire; extravagant gesture of mirth;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">Page665-a+ 60</a>]<BR>distress or pain of tenderness; arms and tumult of wrath or<BR>heroism, &c.<BR> E. वि various, and भाव property, disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=664-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावक
विभावक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Discussing, showing, illustrating.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>भू to think, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावन|विभावनं
विभावन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Discussion, examination, discrimination.<BR>	 2. Per-<BR>ceiving, seeing, distinguishing.<BR>	 3. Conceiving, imagination.<BR>	 4.<BR>Ascertaining or judging of facts.<BR>	 5. Describing effects not arising.<BR>from the usual causes, (in rhetoric.)<BR> E. वि before, भू in the 10th cl.<BR>to think, &c., aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावनीय
विभावनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Distinguishable, ascertainable, to be judged<BR>or determined.<BR> E. वि and भू to think, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावरी
विभावरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. Turmeric.<BR>	 3. A bawd.<BR>	 4. A harlot.<BR>	 5. The<BR>shreds of a garment torn in a scuffle.<BR> E. वि before, भा to shine,<BR>(with stars,) क्वनिप् aff., fem. aff. ङीष्, and रच् substituted for the<BR>final; also विभाव amorous excitement, रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावस्
विभावस् m. (-वान्) The sun.<BR> E. विभा and क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावसु|विभावसुः
विभावसु m. (-सुः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR>	 4. A sort of neck-<BR>lace or garland.<BR> E. विभा light, वसु being, substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावित|विभावितः
विभावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seen, perceived, marked.<BR>	 2. Judged, discri-<BR>minated.<BR>	 3. Conceived, imagined.<BR>	 4. Known, understood.<BR>	 5.<BR>Proved, established.<BR> E. वि before, भू in the 10th cl. to know or<BR>perceive, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावितत्व
विभावितत्व n. (-त्वं) The state of being perceived or judged.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाव्य
विभाव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be seen or observed, remarkable, distin-<BR>guishable.<BR>	 2. To be conceived or imagined.<BR> E. वि before, भू to be,<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाषा
विभाषा f. or Ind. (-षा) Alternative, either of two ways.<BR> E. वि alternative,<BR>and भाषा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभासा
विभासा f. (-सा) Light, shining.<BR> E. वि before, भास् to be luminous, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभासित
विभासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Lighted, shining.<BR> E. वि, भास् to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभित्सु
विभित्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु) Wishing or purposing to hit or pierce.<BR> E. वि<BR>before भिद् to break, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिद्यमान
विभिद्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being wounded, pierced, broken.<BR>	 2. Being<BR>divided or scattered.<BR> E. वि before भिद् to break, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिन्न|विभिन्नः
विभिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Pierced, wounded.<BR>	 2. Broken.<BR>	 3. Scattered,<BR>dispersed.<BR>	 4. Mixed, intermixed, mingling.<BR>	 5. Various, different.<BR>6. Disappointed.<BR>	 7. Bewildered, perplexed.<BR> E. वि before भिद् to<BR>break, &c., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिन्नता
विभिन्नता f. (-ता) The state of being broken, scattered, &c.<BR> E. तल् added<BR>to the last; also with त्व, विभिन्नत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीत|विभीतं|विभीतः
विभीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fearless.<BR> E. वि priv., भीत afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतक|विभीतकं|विभीतकः
विभीतक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Beleric myrobalan, (Terminalia belerica.) E.<BR>विभीत fearless, कन् aff. “वहेडा इति भाषा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषण|विभीषणः
विभीषण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Fearful, formidable, terrific, horrible.<BR>	 nf.<BR>(-णं-णा) The property of exciting fear.<BR>	 m. (-णः) The brother of<BR>RĀVANA.<BR> E. वि, भी to fear, युच् aff. षुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषिका
विभीषिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Terror.<BR>	 2. A means of terrifying.<BR> E. वि + भी-णिच्-सुक्-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभु|विभुः
विभु mfn. (-भुः-भुः or भ्वी-भु)<BR>	 1. Omnipresent, all-pervading.<BR>	 2. Always,<BR>eternal.<BR>	 3. Firm, solid, hard.<BR>	 4. Powerful.<BR>	 m. (-भुः)<BR>	 1. A master,<BR>an owner.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 4. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 5. A servant.<BR>	 6.<BR>Æther.<BR>	 7. Space.<BR>	 8. Time.<BR>	 9. The soul.<BR> E. वि before भू to be,<BR>aff. डु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभुग्न
विभुग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Bent, bowed, crooked.<BR> E. वि before भुज् to bend, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभुता
विभुता f. (-ता) Power, supremacy.<BR> E. विभु, तल् aff. also with त्व, विभुत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूति|विभूतिः
विभूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Superhuman power, consisting of eight faculties<BR>especially attributed to ŚIVA, and supposed to be attainable by<BR>human beings, through a course of austere worship, attended<BR>with magical rites, in honor of that deity and his spouse DURGĀ:<BR>the eight properties thus supposed to be assumable at will are:-<BR>अणिमा extreme minuteness or invisibility; लघिमा extreme light-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">Page665-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ness or incorporeality; प्राप्ति attaining or reaching any thing, as<BR>illustrated by the power of touching the moon with the tip of the<BR>finger; प्राकाम्यं the fulfilment of every wish; महिमा illimitable<BR>bulk; ईशिता supreme dominion over animate or inanimate na-<BR>ture; वशिता the power of enchanting or changing the course of<BR>nature, and कामावशायिता the accomplishment of every promise or<BR>engagement.<BR>	 2. Power, dignity, dominion.<BR>	 3. Ashes of cow-dung,<BR>&c. with which ŚIVA is said to have smeared his body, and<BR>thence used in imitation of him by devotees.<BR>	 4. Prosperity.<BR>	 5.<BR>Wealth.<BR> E. वि implying change of form, &c., भू to be, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूतिमत्|विभूतिमन्त्
विभूतिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Superhuman.<BR>	 2. Smeared with ashes.<BR>E. विभूति and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषण|विभूषणं
विभूषण n. (-णं) Ornament, decoration.<BR> E. वि implying variety, and भूषण adorning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषा
विभूषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Lustre, splendour, beauty.<BR>	 2. Ornament, decoration.<BR>E. वि before भूष् to adorn, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषित|विभूषितः
विभूषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Adorned, decorated.<BR> E. वि variously, भूष् to<BR>adorn, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभृत|विभृतः
विभृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Held, retained.<BR>	 2. Upheld, supported.<BR> E. वि, भृत supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेद|विभेदः
विभेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Dividing, breaking.<BR>	 2. Wounding, piercing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Variety, distinction.<BR>	 4. Bewildering, perplexing.<BR>	 5. A division or<BR>separation.<BR>	 6. Enmity, opposition.<BR>	 7. Contradiction.<BR> E. वि before<BR>भिद् to break, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेदन
विभेदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Breaking, dividing.<BR>	 2. Separating, literally or figur-<BR>atively, as setting at variance.<BR> E. वि before भिद् to divide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंश|विभ्रंशः
विभ्रंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Falling away.<BR>	 2. Decay, ruin.<BR>	 3. A precipice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रत्
विभ्रत् mfn. (-भ्रन्-भ्रती-भ्रत्) Having, possessing.<BR> E. वि, भृ to support, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रम|विभ्रमः
विभ्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. One of the classes of feminine actions proceeding<BR>from the passion of love, flurry, confusion.<BR>	 2. Error, mistake<BR>blunder.<BR>	 3. Hurry, flurry.<BR>	 4. Doubt, apprehension.<BR>	 5. Beauty.<BR>	 6.<BR>Whirling, going round.<BR>	 7. Wandering.<BR>	 8. Whim, caprice.<BR>	 9.<BR>Amorous gesture.<BR>	 f. (-मा) Old age.<BR> E. वि before भ्रम् to err, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रष्ट
विभ्रष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Lost, gone.<BR>	 2. Broken off or from, fallen,<BR>separated.<BR> E. वि before भ्रस्ज् to be broken, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राज्
विभ्राज् mfn. (-भ्राड् or भ्राट्)<BR>	 1. Elegant, richly dressed or decorated.<BR>	 2.<BR>Splendid, luminous, shining.<BR> E. वि before भ्राज् to shine, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राजमान
विभ्राजमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Resplendent, glittering.<BR> E. वि, भ्राज् to shine,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राण
विभ्राण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Having, possessing.<BR> E. वि before भृ to have, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्त|विभ्रांत|विभ्रान्तः
विभ्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Hurried, flurried, erring, &c., through preci-<BR>pitation.<BR> E. वि before भ्रम् to err, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्तशील|विभ्रांतशील|विभ्रान्तशीलः
विभ्रान्तशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Mad, drunk, intoxicated or insane.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>1. A monkey.<BR>	 2. The disk of the sun or moon.<BR> E. विभ्रान्त wander-<BR>ing, and शील disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्ति|विभ्रांति|विभ्रांतिः|विभ्रान्तिः
विभ्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Error, confusion.<BR>	 2. Hurry, flurry, precipitation.<BR>3. Whirling, going round.<BR> E. वि before भ्रम् to err, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत|विमतः
विमत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Disliking, averse or hostile to.<BR>	 2. Disagreeing,<BR>of a different opinion.<BR>	 m. (-तः) An enemy.<BR> E. वि adverse, and मत<BR>disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमति|विमतिः
विमति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Dislike, aversion.<BR>	 2. Difference of opinion, dissent.<BR>3. Stupidity.<BR> E. वि and मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत्सर
विमत्सर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Unenvious, unambitious.<BR> E. वि priv., मत्सर envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमद
विमद f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. Free from intoxication.<BR>	 2. Joyless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्
विमनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः)<BR>	 1. Sad, perplexed, disordered, heart-broken.<BR>2. Changed in mind or feeling.<BR>	 3. Averse, disliking, displeased.<BR>4. Absent-minded, thinking of something else.<BR> E. वि privative and<BR>मनस् the mind; having no mind or heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्क|विमनस्कः
विमनस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) Sad, bewildered, heart-broken, &c.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनीकृत
विमनीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Altered in mind or feeling.<BR>	 2. Sad, sorrow-<BR>ful.<BR>	 3. Displeased, offended.<BR> E. विमनस् and कृत made with च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=665-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनीभूत
विमनीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Changed in mind or feeling, &c.: see the last.<BR>E. विमनस् and भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमन्यु
विमन्यु Adj.<BR>	 1. Free from anger.<BR>	 2. Free from grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमय|विमयः
विमय m. (-यः) Barter, exchange.<BR> E. वि before मि to scatter, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द्द|विमर्द|विमर्दः|विमर्द्दः
विमर्द्द m. (-र्द्दः)<BR>	 1. Rubbing, friction.<BR>	 2. The trituration of perfumes.<BR>3. Touch, contact.<BR>	 4. Destroying, killing.<BR>	 5. Crushing, bruising.<BR>6. Rubbing the body with unguents.<BR>	 7. Conjunction of the sun<BR>and moon.<BR>	 8. War.<BR>	 9. A plant, (Cassia esculenta.)<BR> E. वि before<BR>मृद् to grind, aff. अच्, कन् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द्दन|विमर्दन|विमर्दनं|विमर्द्दनं
विमर्द्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rubbing, pounding, grinding.<BR>	 2. Killing, destroying.<BR>3. The trituration of perfumes.<BR>	 4. Conjunction of the sun and<BR>moon, or eclipse.<BR> E. वि before मृद् to rub, &c. aff. ल्युट्; also विम-<BR>र्द्दक m. (-कः) and विमर्द्दना f. (-ना) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द्दार्द्ध|विमर्दार्ध
विमर्द्दार्द्ध n. (-र्द्धं) (In astronomy,) The time from the apparent conjunc-<BR>tion to the end of an eclipse.<BR> E. विमर्द्द, and अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्द्दोत्थ|विमर्दोत्थ|विमर्द्दोत्थः
विमर्द्दोत्थ m. (-त्थः) A pleasing scent.<BR> E. विमर्द्द rubbing, and उत्थ what rises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्श|विमर्शः
विमर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Discussion, investigation, reasoning, examination by<BR>reason.<BR>	 2. A conflicting judgment.<BR>	 3. The impression on the<BR>mind of past good or evil actions.<BR> E. वि implying discrimination,<BR>मृश् to perceive, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शन|विमर्शनं
विमर्शन n. (-नं) Investigating, discussing.<BR> E. वि, मृश् to judge, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शिन्
विमर्शिन् mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि) Thinking, deliberating.<BR> E. विमर्श, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्ष|विमर्षः
विमर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Irritation, impatience.<BR>	 2. Displeasure, dissatisfaction.<BR>3. Interruption of the prosperous course of a dramatic story, (one<BR>of the five Sandhis in a drama,) reverse.<BR> E. वि before मृष् to en-<BR>dure, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्षिन्
विमर्षिन् mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि)<BR>	 1. Impatient, intolerant.<BR>	 2. Averse, disliking.<BR> E. विमर्ष and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमल|विमलं|विमलः
विमल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Clean, pure, (either literally, as clothes, &c.<BR>or figuratively, as the heart or mind.)<BR>	 2. Beautiful.<BR>	 3. White.<BR>	 4.<BR>Transparent.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Charmaghās.<BR>	 2. A sort<BR>of soil.<BR>	 m. (-लः) An Arhat or Jaina deified sage.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Silver-<BR>gilt.<BR>	 2. Talc.<BR> E. वि privative, मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलमणि|विमलमणिः
विमलमणि m. (-णिः) Crystal.<BR> E. विमल clean, clear, मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलात्मक|विमलात्मकः
विमलात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Clean, pure.<BR> E. विमल clean, आत्मन् nature,<BR>aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलात्मन्
विमलात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Pure, undefiled.<BR> E. विमल, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलाद्रि|विमलाद्रिः
विमलाद्रि m. (-द्रिः) A particular mountain.<BR> E. विमल clean, or crystal,<BR>and अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलार्थक|विमलार्थकः
विमलार्थक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Clear, clean, pure.<BR> E. विमल clean, अर्थ pur-<BR>pose, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमस्तकित
विमस्तकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Beheaded, decapitated.<BR> E. वि priv., मस्त the head, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमांस|विमांसं|विमांसः
विमांस mn. (-सः-सं) Unclean meat, as the flesh of dogs, &c.<BR> E. वि depre-<BR>ciative prefix, and मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमातृ
विमातृ f. (-ता) A step-mother, a father's wife.<BR> E. वि different, मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमातृज|विमातृजः
विमातृज m. (-जः) A step-mother's son.<BR> E. विमातृ, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमान|विमानं|विमानः
विमान mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>	 1. A car or chariot of the gods, sometimes serving<BR>as a seat or throne, and at others carrying them through the skies<BR>self-directed and self-moving; hence it also applies to the sky.<BR>2. Any car or vehicle.<BR>	 3. A horse.<BR>	 4. A palace, the palace of an<BR>emperor, or supreme monarch.<BR>	 5. A seven-storied palace.<BR>	 6.<BR>Disrespect, dishonour.<BR>	 7. Measure.<BR> E. वि before मन् to under-<BR>stand, with घञ् aff.; or मा to measure, aff. ल्युट्; to वि priv.,<BR>मान honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानना
विमानना f. (-ना) Dishonour, disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानित
विमानित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dishonoured.<BR> E. विमान, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्ग|विमार्गः
विमार्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. A broom, a brush.<BR>	 2. A bad road.<BR>	 3. A wrong road,<BR>literally or figuratively, evil conduct.<BR> E. वि before मृज् to clean,<BR>aff. घञ्; or वि privative, and मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गण|विमार्गणं
विमार्गण n. (-णं) Searching, seeking.<BR> E. वि before मृग् to search, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिश्र
विमिश्र f. (-श्रा) Mixed together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्त|विमुक्तः
विमुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Loosed, liberated.<BR>	 2. Hurled, thrown.<BR>	 3.<BR>Quitted, abandoned.<BR>	 4. Issued or let loose from, given vent to. E.<BR>वि before मुक्त the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्ति|विमुक्तिः
विमुक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Liberation, especially final emancipation from<BR>future existence.<BR>	 2. Separation, parting.<BR> E. वि, मुक्ति the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुख|विमुखः
विमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>	 1. Averted, having the face cast down or<BR>turned away.<BR>	 2. Opposed, averse, disinclined.<BR>	 3. Void of.<BR> E. वि<BR>reverse, and मुख the countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखता
विमुखता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Disappearance, departure.<BR>	 2. Turning away.<BR>	 3. Oppo-<BR>sition.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, विमुखत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखिता
विमुखिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Turning away from, enmity.<BR>	 2. Departure.<BR>	 3. Oppo-<BR>sition.<BR> E. विमुखिन्, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, विमुखित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखिन्
विमुखिन् mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि)<BR>	 1. Averted, turned away.<BR>	 2. Hostile,<BR>averse to or from.<BR> E. विमुख, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखीकरण
विमुखीकरण n. (-णं) Turning away from, leaving.<BR> E. विमुख, करण doing, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुखीकृत
विमुखीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Turned away from, averted, departed. E.<BR>विमुख, कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुग्ध
विमुग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं) Bewildered, absorbed.<BR> E. वि, मुह् to be bewildered, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुच्यमान
विमुच्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being let loose or liberated, in the act of<BR>spreading abroad.<BR> E. वि before मुच् to be loosed, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुद्र|विमुद्रः
विमुद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Blown, budded, opened as a bud or flower.<BR>	 2.<BR>Unsealed, unclosed.<BR> E. वि privative, मुद्रा a seal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढ|विमूढः
विमूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Bewildered, discomposed.<BR>	 2. Foolish.<BR>	 3. Be-<BR>guiled, led astray, seduced, tempted.<BR> E. वि, मुह् to be foolish, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढसंज्ञ
विमूढसंज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Senseless, unconscious.<BR> E. विमूढ, संज्ञा sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढात्मन्
विमूढात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Beguiled, foolish.<BR> E. विमूढ, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृदित
विमृदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rubbed.<BR>	 2. Ground, pounded.<BR> E. वि, मृद् to<BR>rub, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृश्य
विमृश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) To be discussed or reflected upon. Ind. Hav-<BR>ing considered.<BR> E. वि, मृश् to reflect, युच् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृश्यकारिन्
विमृश्यकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Acting after due deliberation.<BR> E. विमृश्य<BR>and कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृष्ट
विमृष्ट f. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. Rubbed of, cleansed.<BR>	 2. Considered, reflected upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्ष|विमोक्षः
विमोक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. Liberation, freedom, being or letting loose.<BR>	 2. Dis-<BR>charging, shooting.<BR>	 3. Final emancipation.<BR> E. वि before मोक्ष the<BR>same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षण|विमोक्षणं
विमोक्षण nf. (-णं-णा) Quitting, abandoning, resigning.<BR> E. वि before मोक्षण the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोचन|विमोचनं
विमोचन n. (-नं) Liberating, unyoking.<BR> E. वि, मुच् to set free, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोचित
विमोचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Liberated, set free.<BR> E. वि before मुच् to liberate,<BR>causal v., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहन|विमोहनं|विमोहनः
विमोहन mfn. (-नः-ना or -नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Fascinating, seducing, bewitching,<BR>tempting, (the instrument or agent.)<BR>	 2. Name of a division of<BR>hell.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Seducing, tempting, confounding the mind and<BR>exciting the passions, (the act.)<BR> E. वि before मुह् to be foolish, in<BR>the causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहित|विमोहितः
विमोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fascinated, beguiled.<BR> E. वि before मुह् to be<BR>foolish, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्ब|विंब|विंबं|विम्बं|विंबः|विम्बः
विम्ब mn. (-म्बः-म्बं)<BR>	 1. The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>	 2. An image, a<BR>picture, a shadow, a reflected or represented form.<BR>	 3. The gourd of<BR>the Momordica monadelpha.<BR>	 nf. (-म्बं-म्बा or -म्बी) A cucurbitaceous<BR>plant with red fruit, (Momordica monadelpha.)<BR> E. वि to go, to<BR>shine, बन् Unādi aff., मुम् aug.; the radical vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बक|विंबक|विम्बकं
विम्बक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The disk of the sun or moon.<BR>	 2. The gourd of the<BR>Momordica monadelpha or the plant itself. “तेलाकुचा.”<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बजा
विम्बजा f. (-जा) Momordica monadelpha or the gourd.<BR> E. विम्ब the plant and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बट|विंबट|विंबटः|विम्बटः
विम्बट m. (-टः) The mustard plant, (Sinapis dichotoma, Rox.)<BR> E. विम्ब<BR>as above, अट् to go or grow, (like,) aff. अच् deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बागत
विम्बागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reflected.<BR> E. विम्ब and आगत arrived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बिका|विंबिका
विम्बिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A cucurbitaceous plant bearing a bright red gourd,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">Page667-a+ 60</a>]<BR>(Momordica monadelpha.)<BR>	 2. The disk of the sun or moon.<BR> E. कन्<BR>in the fem. form, added to विम्ब as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=666-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बित|विंबित
विम्बित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pictured, imaged, reflected.<BR> E. विम्ब, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बु|विंबु|विंबुः|विम्बुः
विम्बु m. (-म्बुः) The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बोष्ठ|विम्बोष्ठः
विम्बोष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं) Red-lipped, having lips like the Vimba fruit.<BR>E. विम्ब as above, and ओष्ठ the lip; also विम्बौष्ठ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लान
विम्लान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Fresh, pure, free from soil or decay.<BR>	 2. Re-<BR>freshed.<BR> E. वि priv., म्लान decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लापन|विम्लापनं
विम्लापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cleaning, wiping.<BR>	 2. Refreshing, reviving.<BR> E. वि priv.,<BR>म्ले to decay, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियच्चारिन्
वियच्चारिन् m. (-री) A kite.<BR> E. वियत् the sky, and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियत्|वियन्त्
वियत् n. (-यत्) Sky, heaven, æther, atmosphere.<BR> E. वि privative, यम् to<BR>refrain or cause, aff. क्विप् and तुक् final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियति|वियतिः
वियति m. (-तिः) A bird.<BR> E. वि, यत् to endeavour, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियद्गङ्गा|वियद्गंगा
वियद्गङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) The Ganges or river of heaven.<BR> E. वियत् heaven, गङ्गा the river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियद्गति
वियद्गति f. (-तिः) Moving in the air.<BR> E. वियत्, गति motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियद्भूति|वियद्भूतिः
वियद्भूति f. (-तिः) Darkness.<BR> E. वियत् the sky, and भूति superhuman power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियन्मणि|वियन्मणिः
वियन्मणि m. (-णिः) The sun.<BR> E. वियत् the sky, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियम|वियमः
वियम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Forbearance, restraint.<BR>	 2. Rest, cessation, stop.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pain or distress of various kinds.<BR> E. वि before यम् to check or res-<BR>train, aff. अप्; also वियाम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियात|वियातः
वियात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shameless, impudent, ill-behaved.<BR>	 2. Bold.<BR>E. वि implying prevention, and यात wished; wishing for what<BR>is prohibited or improper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियाम|वियामः
वियाम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Forbearance, restraint.<BR>	 2. Rest, stop, cessation.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pain or distress of various kinds.<BR> E. वि, यम् to restrain, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुक्त|वियुक्तः
वियुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Separated, sundered.<BR> E. वि priv., युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुत
वियुत f. (-ता) Separated from, deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोग|वियोगः
वियोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Absence, separation, especially of lovers.<BR>	 2. Disunion,<BR>disjunction.<BR>	 3. Loss, absence.<BR> E. वि privative, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगभाज्
वियोगभाज् mfn. (-भाक) Suffering separation.<BR> E. वियोग separation, भज्<BR>to serve, to be subject to, causal form, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगिन्
वियोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Separated, absent, remote, apart.<BR>	 m. (-गी)<BR>The ruddy goose.<BR> E. वि, युज् to join, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगिनी
वियोगिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A woman separated from her lover.<BR>	 2. Name of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोजित|वियोजितः
वियोजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Separated, disjoined, disunited.<BR>	 2. Parted<BR>from, deprived of.<BR> E. वि privative, योजित joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोनि|वियोनिः
वियोनि f. (नि or नी)<BR>	 1. Manifold birth.<BR>	 2. An ignominious birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्त|विरक्तः
विरक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Averse, indifferent, free from inclination or<BR>affection.<BR>	 2. Stoical, void of attachment to worldly objects.<BR>	 3.<BR>Impassioned, interested, feeling passion or regard for any person<BR>or any thing.<BR>	 4. Discoloured.<BR> E. वि privative or pleonastic, before<BR>रञ्ज् to feel passion, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्तभाव
विरक्तभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Disinclined to, disliking.<BR> E. विरक्त, भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्ति|विरक्तिः
विरक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Aversion, disinclination.<BR>	 2. Absence of affection. E.<BR>वि before रञ्ज् to affect, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचत्
विरचत् mfn. (-चन्-चन्ती-चत्) Making, composing, fabricating, embellish-<BR>ing, &c.<BR> E. वि before रच् to make, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचन|विरचनं
विरचन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Making, arranging.<BR>	 2. Composing, Embellishing.<BR>4. Embellishment, any artificial and ornamental fabric or contri-<BR>vance.<BR> E. वि before रच to make, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचित|विरचितः
विरचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made, prepared, effected.<BR>	 2. Written, com-<BR>posed.<BR>	 3. Trimmed, ornamented.<BR>	 4. Contrived, constructed,<BR>arranged.<BR>	 5. Put on, worn.<BR>	 6. Set, inlaid.<BR> E. वि pleonasm, and रच्<BR>to be made, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरच्य
विरच्य Ind. Having made.<BR> E. वि, रच् to make, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरज|विरजः
विरज m. (-जः) VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-जा) Free from dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्
विरजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>	 1. Free from dust.<BR>	 2. Free from passion.<BR>f. (-जाः) A woman who has ceased to menstruate.<BR> E. वि privative,<BR>रजस् the menses, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्तमस्
विरजस्तमस् m. (-माः) A virtuous man, one free from the two properties<BR>of ignorance and passion.<BR> E. वि privative, रजस् the quality of pass-<BR>ion, and तमस् that of ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजा
विरजा f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly कपित्थानी 2. A sort of grass, commonly Durbā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजीकृत
विरजीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Freed from passion.<BR>	 2. Clean, freed from<BR>dust, &c.<BR> E. वि priv., रजस् passion, &c., कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजीभूत
विरजीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Free from passion, pure, holy.<BR>	 2. Clean,<BR>clear.<BR> E. वि priv., रजस् passion, भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरञ्च|विरंच|विरंचः|विरञ्चः
विरञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. वि before रच् to create, aff. अच् and नुम्<BR>augment; more properly विरिञ्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरट|विरटः
विरट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The name of a king.<BR>	 2. The shoulder.<BR>	 3. A black<BR>kind of Agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरण|विरणं
विरण n. (-णं) A fragrant grass, (Andropogon schœnanthum.) E. See<BR>वीरण । “वेणार मूल ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरत|विरतः
विरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stopped, ceased, rested.<BR> E. वि before रम् to stop or rest, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरति|विरतिः
विरति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Stop, cessation, term, rest.<BR>	 2. End, term.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore रम् to play, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरम|विरमः
विरम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Cessation, stop.<BR>	 2. Sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरमत्
विरमत् mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Resting, stopping.<BR>	 2. Sporting.<BR> E. वि, रम् to sport, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरल|विरलं|विरलः
विरल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Fine, delicate, thin, (but with interstices.)<BR>2. Loose, relaxed.<BR>	 3. Apart, wide, separated by an interval.<BR>	 4.<BR>Remote, rare, occurring at distant or repeated intervals of time.<BR>n. (-लं) Sour curds.<BR> E. वि apart, रा to go or be, aff. कलन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलम्
विरलम् Ind. It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of “rarely,”<BR>“unfrequently.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलजानुक
विरलजानुक m. (-कः) A man with bandy legs.<BR> E. विरल wide, जानु the knee, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलद्रवा
विरलद्रवा f. (-वा) Gruel made of rice or other grain, with the addition<BR>of Ghee, &c.<BR> E. विरल apart, द्रु to ooze, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरस|विरसः
विरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Insipid.<BR>	 2. Painful.<BR>	 m. (-सः) Pain.<BR> E. वि, रस flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरह|विरहः
विरह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Separation, parting, absence, especially the separa-<BR>tion of lovers.<BR>	 2. Forbearance, cessation, relinquishment.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore रह् to abandon, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहज्वर|विरहज्वरः
विरहज्वर m. (-रः) The anguish of separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहय्य
विरहय्य Ind. Having abandoned.<BR> E. वि before, रह् to quit, causal form, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहानल|विरहानलः
विरहानल m. (-लः) The fire of separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहार्त्त|विरहार्त
विरहार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Pained by the absence of a lover.<BR> E. विरह, आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहित|विरहितः
विरहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Left, abandoned, deserted, relinquished.<BR>	 2.<BR>Void of, exempt, or free from.<BR> E. वि before रह् to abandon, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहिन्
विरहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Separate, sundered, absent or apart from.<BR>f. (-हिणी)<BR>	 1. Wages, hire.<BR>	 2. A woman absent from her husband<BR>or lover.<BR> E. विरह absence, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहोत्कण्ठ|विरहोत्कंठ
विरहोत्कण्ठ Adj. Pining away in absence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहोत्कण्ठिता|विरहोत्कंठिता
विरहोत्कण्ठिता f. (-ता) A woman whose lover or husband is absent. E.<BR>विरह separation, उत्कण्ठित afficted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराग|विरागः
विराग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The absence of desire or passion, indifference, philoso-<BR>phy, the disregard of all sensual enjoyment either in this world<BR>or the next.<BR>	 2. Change of colour.<BR>	 3. Dissatisfaction.<BR> E. वि priva-<BR>tive, and राग passion, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरागार्ह|विरागार्हः
विरागार्ह mfn. (-र्हः-र्हा-र्हं) Void of passion or desire.<BR> E. विराग the absence<BR>of desire, and अह worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरागिन्
विरागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Void of passion or desire.<BR> E. विराग and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज|विराजः
विराज m. (-राट्)<BR>	 1. A man of the regal or military class.<BR>	 2. Splendour,<BR>beauty.<BR>	 3. The body.<BR>	 4. The first progeny of BRAHMĀ, who<BR>having divided himself into male and female, produced from the<BR>female, VIRĀJ; VIRĀJ then by himself produced the first Manu<BR>or SWAYAMBHŪVA who was the progenitor of the Prajāpatis, and<BR>the secondary framer of the visible world: in other places VIRĀJ<BR>is the same as BRAHMĀ, and assumer of the androgynous form<BR>in his own person.<BR> E. वि severally or separately, &c., राज् to shine,<BR>aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=667-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजत्
विराजत् mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्) Shining, splendid, handsome.<BR> E. वि and<BR>राज् to shine, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजमान|विराजमानः
विराजमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Splendid, brilliant, handsome.<BR> E. वि before राज् to shine, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजित|विराजितः
विराजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Illuminated, irradiated, splendid.<BR>	 2. Ma-<BR>nifested, made visible.<BR> E. वि before राज् to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराट|विराटः
विराट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A country, one of the midland division of India, pro-<BR>bably Berār.<BR>	 2. A sovereign.<BR> E. वि before रट् to sound, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराटक|विराटकः
विराटक m. (-कः) An inferior kind of diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराटज|विराटजः
विराटज m. (-जः) An inferior sort of diamond, said to be found in the<BR>country Virāṭa.<BR> E. विराट the country, ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराणिन्
विराणिन् m. (-णी) An elephant.<BR> E. वि before रण battle, aff. अण् and इनि added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराद्ध
विराद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Treated with disrespect, reviled, abused.<BR>	 2.<BR>Opposed.<BR>	 3. Offended.<BR> E. वि before राध् to accomplish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराद्धृ
विराद्धृ mfn. (-द्धा-द्ध्री-द्धृ)<BR>	 1. Thwarting, opposing.<BR>	 2. Offending, injuring.<BR>3. Abusive, calumnious.<BR> E. वि before राध् to accomplish, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराध|विराधः
विराध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Opposition, prevention.<BR>	 2. Vexation, annoyance. E.<BR>वि before राध् to accomplish, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराधन|विराधनं
विराधन n. (-नं) Pain, agony, anguish.<BR> E. वि, राध to accomplish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराध्यत्
विराध्यत् mfn. (-ध्यन्-ध्यन्ती-ध्यत्)<BR>	 1. Opposing, thwarting.<BR>	 2. Offending,<BR>annoying, injuring.<BR> E. वि before राध् to accomplish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराम|विरामः
विराम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. End, conclusion, cessation, term.<BR>	 2. Rest, cessation<BR>from labour.<BR>	 3. Stop, pause of the voice.<BR>	 4. Interval between<BR>words or sentences.<BR> E. वि before रम् to stop, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराल|विरालः
विराल m. (-लः) A cat.<BR> E. विडाल as above, and ड changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराव|विरावः
विराव m. (-वः) Sound, noise.<BR> E. वि before रु to make a noise, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराविन्
विराविन् mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि) Shouting, roaring, crying, &c.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>broom.<BR>	 2. The name of a river.<BR>	 3. Weeping, crying.<BR> E. विराव noise,<BR>इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिक्त|विरिक्तः
विरिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Purged.<BR> E. वि before रिच् to void by stool, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्च|विरिंच|विरिंचः|विरिञ्चः
विरिञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) BRAHMĀ: see विरिञ्चि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्जन
विरिञ्जन m. (-नः) BRAHMĀ. see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्चि|विरिंचि|विरिंचिः|विरिञ्चिः
विरिञ्चि m. (-ञ्चिः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. ŚIVA.<BR> E. वि implying vari-<BR>ous kind, (of beings,) रच् to make or create, इन् aff., the radical<BR>vowel changed to इ and नुम् augment; also with अच् aff. विरिञ्च,<BR>and with युच्, विरिञ्चन; some authorities omit the change of the<BR>radical vowel, and write विरञ्च and विरञ्चि, but these seem to be<BR>less accurate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिब्ध|विरिब्धः
विरिब्ध m. (-ब्धः) A note, a tone.<BR> E. वि before रेभ् to sound, क्त aff., इट् aug.; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुग्न
विरुग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Broken, bent.<BR>	 2. Blunted.<BR>	 3. Destroyed.<BR> E. वि<BR>before रुज् to be sick, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुत
विरुत f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Screamed.<BR>	 2. Resounding.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Singing, chirp-<BR>ing.<BR>	 2. Din, noise, clamour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद|विरुदं|विरुदः
विरुद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Crying.<BR>	 2. Proclaiming.<BR> E. वि, रुद् to cry, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्ध|विरुद्धः
विरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Opposed, hindered.<BR>	 2. Reverse, contrary, oppo-<BR>site.<BR>	 3. Inconsistent, (in argument,) incongruous, a non sequitur.<BR>4. Opposed in quality. as sweet with sour, &c.<BR>	 5. Disagreeing<BR>with each other, (as articles of medicine or food.)<BR>	 6. Hostile, ad-<BR>verse.<BR>	 7. Excluded, disqualified.<BR>	 8. Surrounded, blockaded.<BR>	 9.<BR>Proving the reverse, as a Hetu, (in logic.)<BR> E. वि before रुध् to<BR>stop, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धता
विरुद्धता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Opposition, contrariety.<BR>	 2. Incongruity.<BR>	 3. Enmity. E.<BR>तल् added to विरुद्ध; also with त्व, विरुद्धत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धभुज्
विरुद्धभुज् mfn. (-भुक) Eating incompatible things.<BR> E. विरुद्ध and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धभोजन
विरुद्धभोजन n. (-नं) Incompatible food.<BR> E. विरुद्ध and भोजन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धान्न
विरुद्धान्न n. (-न्नं) Incompatible food.<BR> E. विरुद्ध and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुक्षण
विरुक्षण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Astringent, drying.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Censure, blame,<BR>reviling, abuse.<BR>	 2. Oath, imprecation.<BR>	 3. Contracting, roughening,<BR>acting as an astringent.<BR> E. वि before रूक्ष् to be rough, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूढ|विरूढः
विरूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Budded, blossomed.<BR>	 2. Born.<BR>	 3. Ascended,<BR>mounted.<BR> E. वि before रुह् to grow, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूप|विरूपं|विरूपः
विरूप mfn. (-पः-पा or -पी-पं)<BR>	 1. Deformed, monstrous.<BR>	 2. Unusual in<BR>form or nature, unnatural.<BR>	 n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. Irregular or monstrous<BR>shape.<BR>	 2. Difference of nature or character.<BR>	 f. (-पा) The wife of<BR>YAMA.<BR> E. वि implying variety, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपक|विरूपकः
विरूपक mfn. (-कः-पिका-कं)<BR>	 1. Frightful, hideous.<BR>	 2. Deformed, mis-<BR>shapen.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपकरण
विरूपकरण n. (-णं) Disfiguring.<BR> E. विरूप and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपाक्ष|विरूपाक्षः
विरूपाक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. One of the Rudras.<BR> E. वि implying reverse,<BR>रूप form, and अक्ष the eye; having three eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेक|विरेकः
विरेक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Purging, evacuation by stool.<BR>	 2. A purgative.<BR> E. वि<BR>before रिच् to purge, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेचन|विरेचनं|विरेचनः
विरेचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Purging, evacuation by stool.<BR>	 2. A purgative.<BR> E. वि<BR>before रिच् to purge, aff. णिच्-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेचित
विरेचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Purged, evacuated.<BR> E. वि before रिच् to purge, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेच्य
विरेच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) To be purged.<BR> E. वि, रिच् to purge, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेफ|विरेफः
विरेफ m. (-फः)<BR>	 1. A river in general.<BR>	 2. The absence of the letter र.<BR>E. वि privative, रेफ letter रु, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेभित|विरेभितः
विरेभित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounded, uttered.<BR> E. वि before रेभ् to sound, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोक|विरोकं|विरोकः
विरोक n. (-कं) A hole, a chasm.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A ray of light.<BR> E. वि before<BR>रुच् to shine, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचन|विरोचनः
विरोचन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR>	 4. The son of the<BR>sovereign PRAHLĀDA.<BR> E. वि before रुच् to shine, causal form, aff.<BR>ल्युट् or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचनसुत|विरोचनसुतः
विरोचनसुत m. (-तः) BALI, the sovereign of Mahābalipur.<BR> E. विरोचन the<BR>son of PRAHLĀDA, सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचिष्णु
विरोचिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु)<BR>	 1. Shining.<BR>	 2. Illuminating.<BR> E. वि, रुच् to be light, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोध|विरोधः
विरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Enmity, animosity.<BR>	 2. Restraint, check, control,<BR>confinement.<BR>	 3. Opposition, contradiction.<BR>	 4. Preventing, hin-<BR>drance.<BR>	 5. War.<BR>	 6. Calamity, misfortune.<BR>	 7. Surrounding, invest-<BR>ing, siege, blockade.<BR>	 8. Impediment to a successful progress of<BR>the story, (in a play.)<BR>	 9. Antithesis, contrast.<BR>	 10. Opposition of<BR>qualities, (in articles of food or medicine, &c.)<BR>	 11. Inconsistency,<BR>(in argument.)<BR>	 f. (-धी) Fixed rule, ordinance, institute.<BR> E. वि<BR>before रुध् to stop, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधन|विरोधनं
विरोधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Opposition, resistance, contradiction.<BR>	 2. Hindering,<BR>obstructing, preventing.<BR>	 3. Incongruity, inconsistency.<BR>	 4. Taunt-<BR>ing, provoking.<BR>	 5. Encountering or defying peril.<BR>	 6. Investing,<BR>blockading.<BR> E. वि before रुध् to stop, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधाभास
विरोधाभास m. (-सः) A rhetorical inconsistency which is apparent and<BR>can be explained away; it consists in describing things as exist-<BR>ing together though in the nature of things they ought not so<BR>to exist.<BR> E. विरोधः इवा भासते आ + भास्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधिकृत्
विरोधिकृत् m. (-कृत्) The forty-fifth year of the Indian cycle.<BR> E. विरोधि<BR>opposition, कृत् making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधिन्
विरोधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>	 1. Inimical, adverse, hostile.<BR>	 2. Opposing,<BR>preventing.<BR>	 3. Obstructive.<BR>	 4. Exclusive, disqualifying.<BR>	 5. Con-<BR>tradictory, inconsistent.<BR>	 6. Quarrelsome, contentious.<BR>	 7. Of oppo-<BR>site and incompatible quality, (food, medicine, &c.)<BR>	 8. Besieging,<BR>blockading.<BR>	 m. (-धी)<BR>	 1. An enemy, an opponent.<BR>	 2. The twenty-<BR>fourth year of the cycle.<BR> E. वि रुध् to oppose, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधोक्ति|विरोधोक्तिः
विरोधोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Quarrel, dispute, mutual contradiction.<BR> E. विरोध्<BR>contradiction and उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोप
विरोप(ह)ण n. (-णं) Healing, (as a wound.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोहित
विरोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Left, destitute, forsaken.<BR> E. वि, रुह् to ascend, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्
विल् r. 6th cl. (विलति)<BR>	 1. To wear, to put on, to clothe or cover.<BR>	 2. To<BR>break or divide. r. 10th cl. (वेलयति-ते) To throw, to cast, to direct<BR>or send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल|विलं|विलः
विल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A hole, a chasm, a vacuity.<BR>	 2. A cave, a cavern.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः)<BR>	 1. One of INDRA'S horses.<BR>	 2. A sort of reed or cane, (Cala-<BR>mus rotang.)<BR> E. विल् to divide, &c., aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=668-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्ष|विलक्षः
विलक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Astonished, surprised.<BR>	 2. Abashed, ashamed.<BR>3. Markless, having no mark or aim.<BR>	 4. Contraindicated, having<BR>a character or mark contrary to what is usual or natural.<BR>	 5. Hav-<BR>ing no characteristic mark or property.<BR>	 6. Bewildered.<BR>	 7. Extra-<BR>ordinary.<BR> E. वि before लक्ष् to see, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षण|विलक्षणं|विलक्षणः
विलक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Other, different.<BR>	 2. Strange.<BR>	 3. Having no<BR>distinguishing marks.<BR>	 4. Having inauspicious marks.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1.<BR>State or condition for which no cause can be assigned, vain and<BR>causeless state.<BR>	 2. Seeing, observing.<BR> E. वि privative or negative,<BR>and लक्षण a mark or sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षत्व
विलक्षत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Shame.<BR>	 2. Surprise.<BR>	 3. Absence of mark or aim.<BR>4. Absence of distinguishing property.<BR> E. त्व added to विलक्ष; also<BR>with तल् aff. विलक्षता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षित
विलक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seen, observed.<BR>	 2. Affected without a cause.<BR>3. Undiscriminated, unmarked.<BR>	 4. Distingnished.<BR>	 5. Perplexed,<BR>embarrassed.<BR> E. वि inten. or priv., and लक्षित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलग्न|विलग्नं
विलग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Joined or attached to, fixed on or connected<BR>with.<BR>	 2. Posted.<BR>	 3. Slender, thin.<BR>	 n. (-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. The waist, the middle.<BR>2. The rising of a constellation.<BR> E. वि, लग् to be connected<BR>with, क्त aff., form irr.; or विशेषेण लग्नं लस्ज्-क्त तस्य नः जस्य गः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घन|विलंघन|विलंघनं
विलङ्घन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Overstepping, transgressing.<BR>	 2. Offence, injury. E.<BR>वि before लघि to leap over, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घनीय
विलङ्घनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be transgressed or overstepped.<BR> E. वि<BR>before लघि to leap over, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घित|विलंघित
विलङ्घित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Transgressed, overstepped.<BR>	 2. Traversed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Surpassed.<BR> E. वि before लघि to leap over, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्ज|विलज्जः
विलज्ज mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं) Shameless, impudent, unabashed.<BR> E. वि<BR>priv. लज्जा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्जमान
विलज्जमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Modest.<BR> E. वि before लस्ज् to be modest, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपत्
विलपत् mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्)<BR>	 1. Speaking, talking.<BR>	 2. Prating, talking idly<BR>or wildly.<BR> E. वि before लप् to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपन|विलपनं
विलपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The dirt or sediment of any oily substance, as of<BR>clarified butter, &c.<BR>	 2. Talking, chattering, talking idly or wildly.<BR>3. Lamenting, wailing.<BR> E. वि before लप् to speak, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपित|विलपितं
विलपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Said.<BR>	 2. Chattered.<BR>	 3. Lamented, spoken in<BR>grief, spoken idly.<BR> E. वि before लप् to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्ब|विलंब|विलंबः|विलम्बः
विलम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. Falling or hanging down, pendulousness.<BR>	 2. Slow-<BR>ness, tardiness, delay.<BR> E. वि before लबि to go, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बन|विलंबन|विलंबनं|विलम्बनं
विलम्बन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Delaying, retarding, procrastination.<BR>	 2. Hanging on<BR>or from, depending.<BR> E. वि before लबि to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बमान
विलम्बमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Suspended on, hanging on or from.<BR> E. वि<BR>before लबि to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बिका|विलंबिका
विलम्बिका f. (-का) Constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बित|विलंबित|विलम्बितं
विलम्बित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Falling, pendulous, hanging or falling down.<BR>2. Slow, tardy, retarded.<BR>	 3. Closely connected with.<BR>	 4. Slow,<BR>(as time in music,) adagio.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Delay.<BR> E. विलम्ब delay, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बिन्|विलंबिन्
विलम्बिन् mfn. (-म्बी-म्बिनी-म्बि)<BR>	 1. Delaying, retarding.<BR>	 2. Pendulous,<BR>depending, hanging on or from.<BR>	 m. (-म्बी) The thirty-second year<BR>of the Indian cycle.<BR> E. विलम्ब slowness, delay, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्भ|विलंभ|विलंभः|विलम्भः
विलम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation, giving.<BR>	 2. Liberality.<BR> E. वि reverse,<BR>लभि to get or gain, aff. अच्; or वि + लभ्-घञ् मुम् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलय|विलयः
विलय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Destruction of the world.<BR>	 2. Destruction in general.<BR>3. Liquefaction.<BR> E. वि before ली to liquefy, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलयन|विलयनं
विलयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Destroying.<BR>	 2. Corroding, eating away.<BR>	 3. Liquefying.<BR>4. Removing, taking away.<BR>	 5. Attenuating, (as the fluids of the<BR>body.)<BR>	 6. An attenuant.<BR>	 7. An escharotic.<BR> E. वि, ली to melt, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलला
विलला f. (-ला) A sort of Sida, (S. cordifolia, &c.) “श्वेतबलायाम्”<BR> E. वि<BR>before लल् to shake, affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलवासिन्
विलवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Living in a hole, burrowing.<BR>	 m. (-सी) A<BR>snake.<BR> E. विल a hole, and वासिन् who inhabits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलशय|विलशयः
विलशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Living or burrowing in holes.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A snake.<BR>E. विल a hole, शी to sleep, aff. श ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसत्|विलसन्त्
विलसत् mfn. (-सन्-सती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Shining, beautiful, splendid.<BR>	 2. Sportive,<BR>wanton.<BR> E. वि before लस् to shine, &c., aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसन|विलसनं
विलसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sporting, dallying.<BR>	 2. Flashing, gleaming.<BR> E. वि<BR>before लस् to shine, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसित
विलसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sportive, wanton.<BR>	 2. Glittering, shining.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं)<BR>	 1. Wanton pastime or gestures.<BR>	 2. A gleam, a flash.<BR>	 3. Mani-<BR>festation.<BR> E. वि before लस् to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलाप|विलापः
विलाप m. (-पः) Lamentation, the language of grief and distress.<BR> E. वि<BR>before लप् to speak, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलाल|विलालः
विलाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. An instrument, a machine.<BR>	 2. A cat.<BR> E. वि before<BR>लल् to desire, &c., aff. घञ्; or विडाल as above, and ड changed to<BR>its congener ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलास|विलासः
विलास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. One kind of feminine action, considered as proceed-<BR>ing from and indicative of amorous sentiments; change of place,<BR>posture, gait or look, on the approach of the lover, as hiding at his<BR>approach, assuming a look of displeasure, &c.<BR>	 2. Sport, pastime,<BR>play, especially amorous pastime, dalliance, wantonness.<BR>	 3. Grace,<BR>elegance.<BR>	 4. Ease, facility.<BR> E. वि before लस् to desire, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासकानन
विलासकानन n. (-नं) A pleasure ground.<BR> E. विलास sport, कानन a grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासन|विलासनं
विलासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sport.<BR>	 2. Dalliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासमन्दिर|विलासमन्दिरं
विलासमन्दिर n. (-रं) A pleasure house, a summer house, &c.<BR> E. विलास<BR>sport, and मन्दिर a building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासवत्|विलासवन्त्
विलासवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Sportive, dallying, wanton.<BR> E. विलास, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासविभवानस|विलासविभवानसः
विलासविभवानस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Greedy, covetous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिका
विलासिका f. (-का) A drama in one act on any light subject or adven-<BR>ture. वि, लस् to shine, ण्वुल् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिन्
विलासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Wanton, sportive, dallying.<BR>	 m. (-सी)<BR>	 1.<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR>	 4. A sensualist, an enjoyer.<BR>	 5. A<BR>snake.<BR>	 6. ŚIVA.<BR>	 7. KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 8. KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>	 f. (-सिनी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>woman.<BR>	 2. A whore, a harlot.<BR> E. विलास pastime, &c., aff. इनि; or<BR>वि, लस् to shine, घिनुण् aff.; also read विलाषिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिखन|विलिखनं
विलिखन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Scratching.<BR>	 2. Writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिप्त
विलिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Anointed, plastered, smeared.<BR> E. वि before लिप<BR>to smear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलीन|विलीनः
विलीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Liquid, liquefied, semifluid, as melted oil or<BR>butter, &c.<BR>	 2. Disappeared, perished, removed from sight, either<BR>temporarily or permanently.<BR>	 3. Imagined, formed or infused, as<BR>in the mind.<BR>	 4. Contiguous to, in contact with, united or blend-<BR>ed with.<BR>	 5. Immersed in.<BR> E. वि before ली to melt, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुण्ठन|विलुंठन|विलुंठनं
विलुण्ठन n. (-नं) Robbing, plundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुप्त
विलुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Seized, taken.<BR>	 2. Cut off.<BR>	 3. Lost.<BR>	 4. Impaired,<BR>mutilated.<BR> E. वि before लुप् to cut off, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुभित
विलुभित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bewildered, disturbed, agitated.<BR>	 2. Shaken,<BR>(by the wind.)<BR> E. वि before लुभ् to beguile, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुम्पक|विलुंपक|विलुंपकः|विलुम्पकः
विलुम्पक m. (-कः) A thief, a robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुलित
विलुलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Tremulous, shaking, waving.<BR>	 2. Disordered,<BR>disarranged.<BR> E. वि before लुल् to agitate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलून
विलून f. (-ना) Cut off, cut asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेखन|विलेखनं
विलेखन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Digging, delving, rooting up.<BR>	 2. Dividing, splitting.<BR>3. Making marks or furrows.<BR> E. वि before लिख् to write, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेप|विलेपः
विलेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Ointment, unguent, especially fragrant unguent of<BR>Sandal, Agallochum, &c.<BR>	 2. Mortar, plaster.<BR>	 3. Anointing, plas-<BR>tering.<BR>	 f. (-पी) Rice-gruel.<BR> E. वि, लिप् to anoint or smear, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपन|विलेपनं
विलेपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Perfume of the person, unguent or oil of Sandal,<BR>saffron, camphor, bdellium, &c.<BR>	 2. Smearing the body with fra-<BR>grant oils, &c.<BR>	 2. Plastering.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A woman adorned with<BR>perfumes, &c.<BR>	 2. Rice-gruel.<BR> E. वि before लिप् to smear, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपिका
विलेपिका f. (-का) Rice-gruel; also विलेपी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=669-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेप्य|विलेप्यः
विलेप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) To be spread or plastered.<BR>	 m. (-प्यः) Rice-gruel.<BR>E. वि before लिप् to smear, aff. ण्यत् or यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेवासिन्
विलेवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Living or burrowing in holes.<BR>	 m. (-सी) A<BR>snake.<BR> E. विल 7th case, वासिन् who dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेशय|विलेशयः
विलेशय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. A rat.<BR>	 3. A hare.<BR>	 4. Any animal living<BR>or burrowing in holes.<BR> E. विल a hole, in the seventh case, and शय<BR>who sleeps or dwells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोक|विलोकः
विलोक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Solitary, lonely.<BR> E. वि priv., लोक a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकन|विलोकनं
विलोकन nf. (-नं-ना) Sight, seeing.<BR> E. वि before लोकृ to see, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकनीय
विलोकनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Agreeable, beautiful, fit to be seen or looked<BR>at.<BR> E. वि before लोकृ to see, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकनीयता
विलोकनीयता f. (-ता) Loveliness, beauty.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकयत्|विलोकयन्त्
विलोकयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Seeing, looking at.<BR> E. वि, लोकृ to see, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकित|विलोकितं
विलोकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seen, beheld.<BR>	 2. Examined.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A look,<BR>a glance.<BR> E. वि before लोकृ to see, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचन|विलोचनं
विलोचन n. (-नं) The eye.<BR> E. वि before लोच् to see, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचनपात|विलोचनपातः
विलोचनपात m. (-तः) A glance, a look.<BR> E. विलोचन and पात alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचनाम्बु|विलोचनांबु
विलोचनाम्बु n. (-म्बु) Tears.<BR> E. विलोचन and अम्बु water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोटक|विलोटकः
विलोटक m. (-कः) A sort of fish, (Clupea cultrata.)<BR> E. वि before लुट् to<BR>roll on the ground, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडन|विलोडनं
विलोडन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Agitating, shaking, churning.<BR>	 2. Rolling or tossing.<BR> E. वि, लुड् to agitate, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडित|विलोडितं
विलोडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Agitated, churned, shaken.<BR>	 2. Rolling or<BR>tumbling on the ground.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Butter-milk.<BR> E. वि before लोड् to<BR>be tremulous, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोप|विलोपः
विलोप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Seizing, taking away.<BR>	 2. Loss, disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोपन|विलोपनं
विलोपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Destruction.<BR>	 2. Deluding.<BR> E. वि before लुप् to cut,<BR>causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ|विलोभः
विलोभ m. (-भः) Attraction, delusion, seduction.<BR> E. वि before लुभ् to delude, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभन|विलोभनं
विलोभन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Allurement, attraction, temptation, seduction.<BR>	 2.<BR>Beguiling, perplexing.<BR>	 3. Praise, commendation, especially by<BR>contrast with inferiority.<BR> E. वि before लुभ् to delude, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभित
विलोभित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Allured, beguiled.<BR>	 2. Deceived.<BR>	 3. Praised.<BR>E. वि before लुभ् to delude, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ्य
विलोभ्य Ind. Having beguiled, fascinated, &c.<BR> E. वि before लुभ् to delude, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभ्यमान
विलोभ्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being fascinated, overcome, beguiled, &c.<BR>E. वि before लुभ् to beguile, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोम|विलोमं|विलोमः
विलोम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Reverse, opposite, contrary, backward, against<BR>the hair.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Reverse, opposite course or order, &c.<BR>2. A snake.<BR>	 3. VARUṆA, regent of the waters.<BR>	 4. A dog.<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>A water-wheel, or machine for raising water.<BR>	 f. (-मी) Emblic<BR>myrobalan.<BR> E. वि implying difference, &c., and लोम the hair of the<BR>body; also with कन् added विलोमक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमक्रिया
विलोमक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Doing any thing backwards or in reverse order.<BR>2. (In arithmetic,) Rule of Inversion.<BR> E. विलोन and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमज
विलोमज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born of a father of an inferior caste and<BR>mother of a superior.<BR> E. विलोम inverse order, and ज born; also<BR>विलोमजात, विलमोत्पन्न, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमजिह्व|विलोमजिह्वः
विलोमजिह्व m. (-ह्वः) An elephant.<BR> E. विलोम reverse, जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमत्रैराशिक
विलोमत्रैराशिक n. (-कं) Rule of Three Inverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमवर्ण|विलोमवर्णः
विलोमवर्ण m. (-र्णः) A man of mixed or inferior birth.<BR> E. विलोम contrary<BR>to the proper order, (of marriage, &c.) and वर्ण a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमविधि|विलोमविधिः
विलोमविधि f. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Inverted or reversed ceremony.<BR>	 2. (In arith-<BR>metic,) Rule of Inversion.<BR> E. विलोम and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोल|विलोलः
विलोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Shaking, trembling, tremulous.<BR>	 2. Fickle,<BR>unsteady.<BR>	 3. Rolling, (as the eyes.)<BR>	 4. Tossing, waving.<BR> E. वि before<BR>लुल् to agitate, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोलता
विलोलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Tremulousness.<BR>	 2. Unsteadiness.<BR>	 3. Rolling, (of<BR>the eyes.)<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, विलोलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोलन|विलोलनं
विलोलन n. (-नं) Shaking, stirring, agitating.<BR> E. वि before लुल् to agitate,<BR>causal v., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोलित
विलोलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, agitated, tossed.<BR> E. वि before लुल् to<BR>agitate, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलौकस्
विलौकस् m. (-काः) Any animal living in holes, a reptile.<BR> E. विल and ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्ल|विल्लं
विल्ल n. (-ल्लं)<BR>	 1. A pit, a hole.<BR>	 2. Asafœtida.<BR> E. विल a hole, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्लमूला
विल्लमूला f. (-ला) A sort of yam: see वाराही ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्व|विल्वं|विल्वः
विल्व m. (-ल्वः) A fruit tree, commonly named Bel, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>n. (-ल्वं)<BR>	 1. The fruit of the Bel.<BR>	 2. A measure, the same as the<BR>Pala.<BR> E. विल् to divide, Unādi aff. वन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षा
विवक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2. The wish to speak.<BR>	 3. Meaning, sense.<BR>E. वच् to speak, in the desiderative form, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षित|विवक्षितः
विवक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wished, desired.<BR>	 2. Purposed, intended.<BR>	 3.<BR>Literal, not figurative, (a word or phrase.)<BR>	 4. Intended to be<BR>spoken or said.<BR>	 5. Favourite.<BR>	 n. (-तं) An object desired.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>Purpose, wish, what one wishes to declare or speak.<BR> E. वच् to<BR>speak, desiderative form, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षु
विवक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Wishing to speak.<BR> E. वच् to speak, desid. v., उ<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवञ्चिषु|विवंचिषु
विवञ्चिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Crafty, deceitful.<BR> E. वि, वञ्च् to trick, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवत्सा
विवत्सा f. (-त्सा) A cow whose calf is dead.<BR> E. वि priv., वत्स a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवदत्
विवदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>	 1. Disputing, contending.<BR>	 2. Litigating. E.<BR>वि variously, वद् to speak, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवदमान|विवदमानः
विवदमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Disagreeing, contending, maintaining diff-<BR>erent arguments.<BR>	 2. Litigating.<BR> E. वि before वद् to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवध|विवधः
विवध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A road, a highway.<BR>	 2. A yoke for carrying burdens.<BR>3. A load.<BR>	 4. Storing grain or hay, &c.<BR>	 5. An ewer, a pitcher. E.<BR>वि before वध् to strike, aff. घञ्; also वीवध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवधिक|विवधिकः
विवधिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A chandler, a peddler.<BR>	 2. A load-carrier.<BR> E. विवध<BR>storing grain, ठन् aff. and the vowel unchanged; also वैवधिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवन्दिषु
विवन्दिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Desirous or wishing to praise.<BR> E. वदि to praise,<BR>desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर|विवरं|विवरः
विवर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A hole, a chasm, a vacuity.<BR>	 2. Fault, defect.<BR>	 3. Sepa-<BR>ration, disjunction.<BR>	 4. A solitary place.<BR>	 5. The number “nine.”<BR>E. वि before वृञ् to choose, to cover, &c., and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरण|विवरणं
विवरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Explanation, exposition, gloss, comment.<BR>	 2. Inter-<BR>pretation, translation.<BR>	 3. Uncovering, exposing, laying bare or<BR>open.<BR>	 4. Detailing, describing.<BR> E. वि before वृ to select, (the mean-<BR>ing,) aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरनालिका
विवरनालिका f. (-का) A pipe, a fife, a flute.<BR> E. विवर a hole, a perfora-<BR>tion, नाल a pipe, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरिषु
विवरिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to make manifest or declare.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore वृ to choose, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ज्जन|विवर्जन|विवर्जनं
विवर्ज्जन n. (-नं) Abandoning, leaving, shunning.<BR> E. वि before वृज् to leave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ज्जनीय|विवर्जनीय
विवर्ज्जनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be avoided, shunned, quitted, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>before वृज् to abandon, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ज्जयत्|विवर्जयत्
विवर्ज्जयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Avoiding, leaving.<BR> E. वि before वृज् to quit, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ज्जित|विवर्जित
विवर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Left, abandoned, avoided, shunned.<BR>	 2. De-<BR>prived of.<BR>	 3. Given.<BR> E. वि before वृज् to leave, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ण|विवर्णः
विवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Low, vile.<BR>	 2. Bad coloured.<BR>	 3. Wanting<BR>colour.<BR>	 4. Changing colour.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) A man of a low caste, one of<BR>degrading occupation, an outcaste.<BR> E. वि privative and वर्ण caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्णवदन
विवर्णवदन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Pale-faced.<BR> E. विवर्ण colourless, वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त्त|विवर्त|विवर्तः|विवर्त्तः
विवर्त्त m. (-त्तः)<BR>	 1. Assemblage, collection, heap or multitude.<BR>	 2. Dan-<BR>cing.<BR>	 3. Going or turning round, revolving, returning.<BR>	 4. Human<BR>error, worldly ignorance, the confounding of truth and falsehood,<BR>or the mistaking or unreal objects and conceiving them to be<BR>what they are not, as mirage for water, a rope for a snake, &c.<BR>5. Modification, various or altered state or condition.<BR> E. वि before<BR>वृत् to be, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त्तन|विवर्तन|विवर्तनं|विवर्त्तनं
विवर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going round, circumambulating, an alter, &c.<BR>	 2. Re-<BR>volving, turning round.<BR>	 3. Whirling, causing to go round.<BR>	 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">Page671-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Returning.<BR>	 5. Passing through in succession, as various lives,<BR>various hells, &c.<BR>	 6. Being, abiding.<BR>	 7. Reverential salutation. E.<BR>वि before वृत् to be, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=670-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त्तमान|विवर्तमान
विवर्त्तमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Turning back or round, recoiling, revolving,<BR>returning, &c.<BR> E. वि before वृत् to be, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त्तवाद|विवर्तवाद|विवर्तवादः
विवर्त्तवाद m. (-दः) The Vedāntic doctrine that regards Brahman as the<BR>only entity and the world to be illusory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्त्तित|विवर्तित
विवर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Revolved, returned.<BR>	 2. Whirled round.<BR>	 3.<BR>Turned back or away.<BR> E. वि before वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्द्धन
विवर्द्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Increase.<BR>	 2. Aggrandizement.<BR>	 3. Cutting, dividing.<BR>E. वि before वृध् to increase, to cut, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्द्धित
विवर्द्धित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Increased, enlarged.<BR>	 2. Furthered, advanced.<BR>3. Gratified.<BR>	 4. Cut, divided.<BR> E. वि, वृध् to increase, to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवश|विवशः
विवश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Subject, subjected.<BR>	 2. Independent.<BR>	 3. Appre-<BR>hensive of death, unwilling though about to die.<BR>	 4. Desirous of<BR>death, sedate at that period, or having the soul free from worldly<BR>cares and fears.<BR>	 5. Uncontrolled, unrestrained, unsubdued.<BR>	 6.<BR>Fainted, unconscious.<BR> E. वि before वश् to wish, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्त्र
विवस्त्र mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं) Unclothed, naked.<BR> E. वि priv., वस्त्र clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्वत्|विवस्वन्त्
विवस्वत् m. (-स्वान्)<BR>	 1. A god.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. ARUṆA, the charioteer of<BR>the sun.<BR>	 4. The seventh or present MANU; also VAIVASWATA.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ती) The city of the sun.<BR> E. वि implying variety, वस् to cover or<BR>hide, aff. क्विप्; विवस् here said therefore to imply various covering,<BR>as a garment of light, i. e. the rays of the sun, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवह|विवहः
विवह m. (-हः) One of the seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाक|विवाकः
विवाक m. (-कः) A judge.<BR> E. वि + वच्-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवात्
विवात् mfn. (-वान्-वान्ती or वाती-वात्) Blowing gently.<BR> E. वि before वा to blow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाद|विवादः
विवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Contest, contention.<BR>	 2. Contest at law, a legal dis-<BR>pute, litigation, a lawsuit.<BR> E. वि before वद् to speak, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादानुगत|विवादानुगतः
विवादानुगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Disputed, litigated.<BR> E. विवाद a lawsuit, अनु<BR>according to, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादार्थिन्
विवादार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-थिनी-र्थि) Seeking for a dispute or quarrel.<BR>	 m. (-र्थी)<BR>A litigant, a prosecutor, a plaintiff.<BR> E. विवाद and अर्थिन् who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादास्पदीभूत
विवादास्पदीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Litigated, contested at law.<BR> E. विवाद and<BR>आस्पद place, भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादिन्
विवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Disputing, contending, a litigant.<BR> E. विवाद and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवार|विवारः
विवार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Dilatation, expansion.<BR>	 2. Open or expanded state of<BR>the organs of speech for the articulation of vowels or sibilants. E.<BR>वि before वृ to cover, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवास|विवासः
विवास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Without clothes, naked.<BR>	 m. (-सः) Banishment.<BR>E. वि priv., and वास vesture or abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासकरण
विवासकरण n. (-णं) Banishing, transporting.<BR> E. विवास and करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासन|विवासनं
विवासन n. (-नं) Exile, banishment.<BR> E. वि away, वासन abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासित
विवासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Banished, expelled.<BR> E. वि वस् to dwell, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवास्य
विवास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) To be expelled or transported.<BR> E. वि away, वस्<BR>to dwell, causal v., यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाह|विवाहः
विवाह m. (-हः) Marriage; eight recognized forms of marriage are enu-<BR>merated by Hindu law-givers, viz:--<BR>“ब्राह्मो दैवस्तथैवार्षः प्राजापत्यस्तथासुरः ।<BR>गान्धर्वो राक्षसश्चैव पैशाचश्चाष्टमोऽधमः ॥”<BR>E. वि mutually, वह् to take, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहित|विवाहितः
विवाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Married.<BR> E. वि before वह् to bear, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाह्य|विवाह्यः
विवाह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Marriageable, to be married.<BR>	 m. (-ह्यः) A<BR>son-in-law, a bridegroom.<BR> E. विवाह marriage, यत् aff.; or वि + वह्-ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्त|विविक्तं
विविक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Lonely, solitary, desert.<BR>	 2. Pure, faultless.<BR>3. Separated, distinguished, disjoined, detached.<BR>	 4. Discrimina-<BR>tive, judicious, a judge.<BR>	 5. Discriminated, judged.<BR>	 6. Profound,<BR>(as judgment or thought.)<BR>	 7. Intent on.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Loneliness.<BR>	 2.<BR>A solitary place.<BR>	 f. (-क्ता) A woman disliked by her husband. E.<BR>वि before विच् to be or make separate, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्तभाव
विविक्तभाव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Intent upon any object.<BR> E. विविक्त and भव<BR>disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्तसेविन्
विविक्तसेविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Solitary, retired, recluse, seeking or affect-<BR>ing solitude.<BR> E. विविक्त, सेविन् who serves or pursues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्षत्
विविक्षत् mfn. (-क्षन्-क्षती-क्षत्) Wishing to enter.<BR> E. विश् to enter, desid. v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्षा
विविक्षा f. (-क्षा) Wish or purpose to enter.<BR> E. विश् to enter, desid. v., अङ्<BR>and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्षु
विविक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Wishing or intending to enter.<BR> E. विश् to enter, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविग्न
विविग्न f. (-ग्ना)<BR>	 1. Very agitated.<BR>	 2. Very angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविच्य
विविच्य Ind. Having considered, discussed, judged.<BR> E. विच् to judge,<BR>with वि prefixed, and ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविदिवस्
विविदिवस् mfn. (-वान्-द्युषी-वस्) Obtaining.<BR> E. विद् to know, वसु aff., with इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविद्वस्
विविद्वस् mfn. (-द्वान्-दुषी-द्वस्) Knowing, wise.<BR> E. विद् to know, वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविध|विविधं
विविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Various, multiform, of many sorts.<BR> E. वि, विधि sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविशिवस्
विविशिवस् mfn. (-वान्-श्युषी-वस्) Entering.<BR> E. विश् to enter, root rep.,<BR>वुसु aff., इट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविश्वस्
विविश्वस् mfn. (-श्वान्-शुषी-श्वस्) Entering, who or what enters.<BR> E. विश् to enter, वसु aff., root rep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवीत|विवीतः
विवीत m. (-तः) An inclosed spot of ground, abounding in grass, wood,<BR>&c., a preserved pasture, a paddock, &c.<BR> E. वि privative, वीत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवीतभर्त्तृ|विवीतभर्तृ
विवीतभर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) The superintendent or owner of a preserved pas-<BR>ture.<BR> E. विवीत a paddock, &c., and भर्त्तृ a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृक्त
विवृक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Abandoned, left.<BR>	 f. (-क्ता) A woman disliked or<BR>deserted by her husband.<BR> E. वि before वृज् to abandon, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत|विवृतं
विवृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Expanded, extended, extensive, large.<BR>	 2.<BR>Evident, displayed, made manifest.<BR>	 3. Exposed, discovered.<BR>	 4.<BR>Opened.<BR>	 5. Explained, interpreted, expounded.<BR>	 6. Open, (as the<BR>organs of speech for the articulation of vowels and sibilants.)<BR>	 7.<BR>Proclaimed, divulged.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A disease, an ulcer attended with<BR>much pain and heat.<BR> E. वि before वृ to be, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृताक्ष|विवृताक्षः
विवृताक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Large-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः) A cock.<BR> E. विवृत large,<BR>अक्षि the eye, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृति|विवृतिः
विवृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Explanation, exposition, gloss, comment, interpre-<BR>tation.<BR>	 2. Making clear or manifest.<BR>	 3. Discovery, exposure.<BR>	 4.<BR>Expansion.<BR>	 5. Display.<BR> E. वि before वृ to choose, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्त|विवृत्तं
विवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Turned or twisted round, whirling, revolving,<BR>rolling.<BR> E. वि before वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्ति|विवृत्तिः
विवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Whirling, turning round.<BR>	 2. A hiatus, (in gram.) E.<BR>वि, वृत् to be, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्सत्
विवृत्सत् mfn. (-त्सन्-त्सन्ती-त्सत्) Wishing to be.<BR> E. वि, वृत् to be, desid. v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्सितृ
विवृत्सितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what wishes to be.<BR> E. वृत् to be, desid.<BR>v., तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्ध
विवृद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Augmented, increased.<BR>	 2. Abundant.<BR>	 3.<BR>Grown up.<BR> E. वि and वृद्ध the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्धि|विवृद्धिः
विवृद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Growth, increase, augmentation.<BR>	 2. Prosperity.<BR> E. वि, वृद्धि the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक|विवेकः
विवेक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Discrimination, judgment, the faculty of distin-<BR>guishing things by their properties, and classing them according<BR>to their real not apparent nature; in the Vedānta system, it<BR>is applied to the power of separating BRAHMĀ or invisible spirit,<BR>from the ostensible world, truth from untruth, or reality from<BR>illusion.<BR>	 2. Discussion, investigation.<BR>	 3. A reservoir, a basin, a<BR>bath.<BR> E. वि severally, विच् to judge, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकता
विवेकता f. (-ता) Judgment, discrimination, the faculty or property of<BR>judgment.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, विवेकत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकदृश्वत्व
विवेकदृश्वत्व n. (-त्वं) Discrimination, discernment.<BR> E. विवेकदृश्वन्, and त्व<BR>aff.; or with तल्, विवेकदृश्वता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकदृश्वन्
विवेकदृश्वन् m. (-श्वा) A wise or discerning man.<BR> E. विवेक, दृश्वन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकिता
विवेकिता f. (-ता) Discussion, discrimination, discriminativeness. E.<BR>विवेकी discriminative, and तल् aff.; also विवेकित्व n. (-त्वं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकिन्
विवेकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Judicious, discriminative.<BR>	 m. (-की) A sage,<BR>a philosopher, a judge.<BR> E. वि before विच् to judge, धिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक्तव्य
विवेक्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be discussed or judged.<BR> E. वि before विच्<BR>to judge, तव्य aff.; also विवेच्य and विवेचनीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक्तृ
विवेक्तृ m. (-क्ता)<BR>	 1. A judge.<BR>	 2. A philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचन|विवेचनं
विवेचन n. (-नं) Discrimination, judgment, distinguishing truth from<BR>falsehood.<BR> E. वि before विच् to judge, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचनीय|विवेचनीयः
विवेचनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be judged or discussed.<BR> E. वि, विच् to judge,<BR>अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवोढृ
विवोढृ m. (-ढा) A husband, a bridegroom, a lover.<BR> E. वि before वह् to obtain, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विव्रुवत्
विव्रुवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Silent, refraining from or refusing to speak.<BR>E. वि privative, व्रुवत् speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विव्वोक|विव्वोकः
विव्वोक m. (-कः) Affectation of difference, one of the branches of<BR>amorous dalliance, or feminine actions, tending to excite love or<BR>desire.<BR> E. वि before वा to go, aff. कु; विवु said here to mean a<BR>particular gait, and ओक house, place, site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
विश् r. 6th cl. (विशति)<BR>	 1. To enter, to pervade.<BR>	 2. To fall to the lot of.<BR>3. To settle down on. With आङ् or प्र prefixed, 1. To go in, to<BR>enter.<BR>	 2. To occupy, to engross. With उप, 1. To sit, to sit down.<BR>2. To approach. With नि, 1. To dwell, to abide.<BR>	 2. To place or<BR>station.<BR>	 3. To sit down.<BR>	 4. To enter.<BR>	 5. To be intent on.<BR>	 6. To<BR>marry. With नि or अभि and नि, 1. To rest, to halt, to sit down,<BR>especially before or in presence of.<BR>	 2. To conceal. With निर्, To<BR>go out or forth. With परि, To place before, to present. With सम्,<BR>1. To lie down, to repose.<BR>	 2. To enter.<BR>	 3. To have sexual inter-<BR>course. With सम् and नि, To be near, to be close to or in the<BR>neighbourhood. With सम् and आङ्, To introduce. With अनु, To<BR>enter after some one. With निस्, 1. To enjoy.<BR>	 2. To embellish,<BR>Caus. (वेशयति-ते) With नि, 1. To apply, to bend, (the mind.)<BR>	 2. To<BR>draw, to portray.<BR>	 3. To place.<BR>	 4. To enter on, to commit. With<BR>प्र, To usher. With विनि, To fix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
विश् m. (-विट्)<BR>	 1. A man of the mercantile tribe.<BR>	 2. A man in<BR>general.<BR>	 f. (-विट्)<BR>	 1. Entrance.<BR>	 2. A daughter.<BR>	 3. Feces, ordure.<BR>	 4.<BR>People, subjects.<BR> E. विश् to enter, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश|विशं
विश n. (-शं) The film or fibres of the stalk of the water-lily.<BR> E. विश् to enter, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्क|विशंक|विशङ्कः
विशङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Fearless, undaunted.<BR> E. वि and शङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कट|विशंकट|विशङ्कटः
विशङ्कट mfn. (-टः-टा or टी-टं)<BR>	 1. Great, large.<BR>	 2. Strong, vehement. E.<BR>वि the particle, शङ्कटच् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कमान
विशङ्कमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fearing, apprehending.<BR> E. वि, शकि to doubt, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशत्
विशत् mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्) Entering.<BR> E. विश् to enter. शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशद|विशदः
विशद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Of a white colour.<BR>	 2. Clear, pure, pellucid.<BR>	 3.<BR>Evident, apparent, manifest.<BR>	 4. Beautiful.<BR>	 5. At ease.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>White, the colour.<BR> E. वि, शद् to wither or perish, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशय|विशयः
विशय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Doubt.<BR>	 2. Refuge, asylum.<BR> E. वि, शी to sleep, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशयिन्
विशयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Dubious, uncertain.<BR>	 2. Doubting. E.<BR>विशय doubt, इनि aff.; or वि before शी to sleep, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशर|विशरः
विशर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaying, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Bursting.<BR> E. वि before<BR>शृ to injure to kill, aff. अच्; also with ल्युट् aff. विशरण n. (-णं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्य|विशल्यः
विशल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Free from thorns or spikes.<BR>	 2. Free from<BR>care or pain.<BR>	 f. (-ल्या)<BR>	 1. A twining shrub, (Menispermum cordi-<BR>folium.)<BR>	 2. A sort of potherb, (the kind not ascertained.)<BR>	 3. A<BR>plant, commonly Dantī, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR>	 4. Another plant,<BR>commonly Teori, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR>	 5. A sort of fruit,<BR>Lāngaliya.<BR> E. वि privative, and शल्य a stalk or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्यकृत्
विशल्यकृत् m. (-कृत) A plant, (Echites dichotoma, Rox.) “हापरमाली ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसन|विशसनं|विशसनः
विशसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaying, slaughter, Dissecting, cutting.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-नः) A sabre, a crooked sword.<BR> E. वि before शस् to hurt, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसित|विशसितः
विशसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Hurt, killed.<BR>	 2. Cut, dissected.<BR>	 3. Well-<BR>mannered.<BR> E. वि before शस् to injure, aff. क्त, इट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसितृ
विशसितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Killing.<BR>	 2. Dissecting.<BR> E. वि, शस् to kill, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त|विशस्तः
विशस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Praised, celebrated.<BR>	 2. Arrogant, ill-man-<BR>nered, rude.<BR>	 3. Cut up.<BR> E. वि before शस् to praise, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त्र
विशस्त्र mfn. (-स्त्रः-स्त्रा-स्त्रं) Disarmed, unarmed.<BR> E. वि and शस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्तृ
विशस्तृ m. (-स्ता) A chandāla.<BR> E. वि + शस्-तृच् न इट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाकर|विशाकरः
विशाकर m. (-रः) A plant, (Euphorbia of various kinds.) “लङ्कासिज् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाख|विशाखः
विशाख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Branchless.<BR>	 m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. An<BR>attitude in shooting, standing with the feet a span apart.<BR>	 3. A<BR>solicitor, a petitioner, a beggar.<BR>	 4. A spindle.<BR>	 f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. The six-<BR>teenth lunar asterism, figured by a festoon, and containing four,<BR>or according to some, two stars.<BR>	 2. A cucurbitaceous plant, (Mo-<BR>mordica charantia.)<BR> E. वि without, शाख a branch; or विशाखा the<BR>asterism, (by which personified the god was cherished,) अण् aff.,<BR>and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखज|विशाखजः
विशाखज m. (-जः) The orange, (Citrus aurantium.)<BR> E. विशाख the aster-<BR>ism, and ञन् to be born, aff. ड; coming into season, when the<BR>sun is in this asterism, or about the end of October.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखल|विशाखलं
विशाखल n. (-लं) An attitude in shooting.<BR> E. विशाखा, लच् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाय|विशायः
विशाय m. (-यः) Sleeping and watching alternately, the rest taken in<BR>rotation by soldiers on watch.<BR> E. वि intervening, शी to sleep,<BR>aff. घञ् or पर्य्याये णच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारण|विशारणं
विशारण n. (-णं) Killing, slaying, slaughter.<BR> E. वि before शॄ to injure, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारद|विशारदः
विशारद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Learned, wise.<BR>	 2. Confident, bold, pre-<BR>suming.<BR>	 3. Famous, celebrated.<BR> E. विशाल great, extensive, (fame,<BR>&c.) and दा to give, aff. क, the ल changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाल|विशालः
विशाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Great, large.<BR>	 2. Broad.<BR>	 3. Great, eminent,<BR>illustrious.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A sort of deer.<BR>	 2. A sort of bird.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1.<BR>The city Ougein.<BR>	 2. Bitter apple, (Cucumis colocynthis.)<BR>	 3. Name<BR>of a river.<BR> E. वि particle, and शालच् aff.; or विश् to enter, Unādi<BR>aff. कालन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालकुल
विशालकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Well-born.<BR>	 n. (-लं) An illustrious family.<BR> E. विशाल, कुल race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालता
विशालता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Width, breadth.<BR>	 2. Magnitude, bulk.<BR>	 3. Eminence,<BR>distinction.<BR> E. विशाल large, तल् aff. of the abstract; also विशालत्व<BR>n. (-त्वं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालत्वच्
विशालत्वच् m. (-त्वक्) A tree, (Echites scholaris.) “सप्तच्छदवृक्षे”<BR> E. विशाल large, त्वच् skin or bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालाक्ष|विशालाक्षः
विशालाक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Having large or beautiful eyes.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1.<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. GARUḌA.<BR>	 f. (-क्षी) PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. विशाल large, and अक्षि the<BR>eye, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिख|विशिखः
विशिख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. An iron crow.<BR>	 3. A kind of reed.<BR>f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A spade, a hoe.<BR>	 2. A highway, a broad or carriage<BR>road.<BR>	 3. A very minute arrow, a sort of needle or spindle.<BR>	 4.<BR>A barber's wife.<BR>	 5. A sick room, or the dwelling of the sick. E.<BR>वि implying possessed of, &c., and शिखा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिञ्जान
विशिञ्जान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sounding.<BR> E. वि before शिजि to sound, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशित
विशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sharpened.<BR> E. वि before शि to sharpen, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिप|विशिपं
विशिप n. (-पं) A palace, a temple.<BR> E. विश् to enter, अप् Unādi aff., and<BR>इ substituted for the pen. vowel; or विश्-इपक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्ट|विशिष्टः
विशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Endowed with, possessed of, having inherent<BR>or attached to.<BR>	 2. Excellent, superior, distinguished.<BR>	 3. Especial,<BR>peculiar.<BR>	 4. Having distinctive and exclusive properties.<BR> E. वि<BR>before शिष् to tell qualities, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्टता
विशिष्टता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Excellence, distinction.<BR>	 2. Individuality, having<BR>distinguishing or characteristic qualities.<BR>	 3. Peculiarity, as of duty<BR>&c.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also विशिष्टत्व n. (-त्वं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्ण|विशीर्णः
विशीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Dry, dried up, withered, decayed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Wasted, impaired.<BR>	 3. Shattered.<BR>	 4. Shrunk, shrivelled.<BR> E. वि be-<BR>fore शॄ to injure, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्य्य|विशीर्य
विशीर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To crumble or fall to ruin, likely or fit to.<BR> E. वि, शॄ to injure, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्य्यमाण|विशीर्यमाण
विशीर्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being wasted or destroyed, decaying,<BR>perishing.<BR> E. वि before, शॄ to injure, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशील
विशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Ill-behaved, indecorous, immoral.<BR> E. वि priv.,<BR>शील behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्ध|विशुद्धं
विशुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Pure, purified, clean, cleansed, free from vice<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">Page673-a+ 60</a>]<BR>or fault.<BR>	 2. Pious, virtuous.<BR>	 3. Humble, modest, compliant.<BR>	 4.<BR>Corrected.<BR> E. वि intensitive prefix, शुध् to be pure or clean, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धि|विशुद्धिः
विशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Purity, purification.<BR>	 2. Equality, similarity.<BR>	 3. Re-<BR>moval of doubt.<BR>	 4. Correctness.<BR>	 5. In Algebra, a subtractive<BR>quantity.<BR> E. वि before शुद्धि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धिभाज्
विशुद्धिभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Pure, free from soil or vice.<BR> E. विशुद्धि, and भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशूल
विशूल f. (-ला) Without a spear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशृङ्खल|विशृंखल|विशृङ्खलः
विशृङ्खल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Unchecked, unrestrained, unfettered, (liter-<BR>ally or figuratively.)<BR>	 2. Dissolute.<BR> E. वि privative, शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष|विशेषः
विशेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Sort, kind, manner.<BR>	 2. Difference, individual or<BR>specific identity and consequent distinction from every other<BR>individual or species.<BR>	 3. (In logic,) The peculiar attribute, (predi-<BR>cabile proprium,) the cause of preception or conclusion.<BR>	 4.<BR>Excellence, superiority.<BR>	 5. A limb, a member.<BR>	 6. A mark on the<BR>forehead with Sandal.<BR>	 7. A figure of rhetoric, distinguished as of<BR>three kinds all implying variety of means or effect.<BR>	 8. A change<BR>for the better, a favourable turn, (as in sickness.)<BR>	 9. Name of the<BR>mundane egg.<BR>	 10. Individuality, considered as one of the seven<BR>Padārthas in Vaiśeshika Phil.<BR>	 11. A word which limits the<BR>meaning of another word.<BR> E. वि discriminative prefix, शिष् to<BR>attribute or distinguish by attributes, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषक|विशेषकः
विशेषक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Discriminative, distinguishing, attributive,<BR>characteristic.<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A mark on the forehead made with<BR>Sandal, &c. and worn either as an ornament or sectarial distinc-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. An attribute, a predicate.<BR>	 3. An arrangement of poetical<BR>composition.<BR> E. वि before, शिष् to attribute or distinguish, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषकाम
विशेषकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Amorous, desirous.<BR> E. विशेष, काम who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषगुण|विशेषगुणः
विशेषगुण m. (-णः) An object of a single and distinct kind as the soul,<BR>mind, time, place, and the atoms of earth, water, light and air.<BR>E. विशेष and गुण property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषज्ञ
विशेषज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Wise, intelligent.<BR> E. विशेष, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषण|विशेषणं
विशेषण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Discriminative, attributive.<BR>	 2. Distinctive, (as<BR>a property, &c.)<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Distinguishing, discriminating.<BR>	 2.<BR>An epithet, an attributive, an adjective, (opposed to विशेष्य.)<BR> E. वि<BR>before शिष् to distinguish by attributes, aff. ल्युट् or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषणीय
विशेषणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be discriminated or distinguished, what<BR>may or ought to be marked as distinct.<BR> E. वि before शिष् to dis-<BR>tinguish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषतस्
विशेषतस् Ind. Especially, particularly, specifically.<BR> E. विशेष and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषधर्म्म|विशेषधर्म|विशेषधर्मः
विशेषधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Peculiar or different duty.<BR> E. विशेष, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषभावना
विशेषभावना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Reflecting on or perceiving differences.<BR>	 2. (In<BR>algebra,) Composition by the difference of the products.<BR> E. विशेष,<BR>and भावना considering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषलक्षण
विशेषलक्षण n. (-णं) Specific or characteristic mark or sign.<BR> E. विशेष, and लक्षण mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषवचन
विशेषवचन n. (-नं) Special or different text.<BR> E. विशेष and वचन a text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषविद्वस्
विशेषविद्वस् m. (-द्वान्) A philosopher.<BR> E. विशेष excellence, विद्वान् learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषविधि|विशेषविधिः
विशेषविधि f. (-धिः) Special rule or observance.<BR> E. विशेष, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषित|विशेषितं
विशेषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Divided, distinguished, separated.<BR>	 2. Predica-<BR>ted, attributed, having as an attribute or being distinguished by<BR>it.<BR>	 3. Excellent, superior.<BR> E. विशेष sort, kind, &c., इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषोक्ति|विशेषोक्तिः
विशेषोक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. A figure of rhetoric, coupling cause with effect, so<BR>as to explain any peculiar manner or condition.<BR>	 2. Panegyric,<BR>recapitulation of merits.<BR> E. विशेष sort, kind, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष्य|विशेष्यः
विशेष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. To be distinguished or discriminated.<BR>	 2.<BR>Distinguishing, to be discriminated by.<BR>	 3. Principal, primary, chief.<BR>m. (-ष्यः) A name, a substantive.<BR>	 n. (-ष्यं) The object of a pre-<BR>dicate.<BR> E. वि before शिष् to distinguish by its attributes, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोक|विशोकः
विशोक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Without grief, happy.<BR> E. वि priv., शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधन|विशोधनं
विशोधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cleaning, purifying, freeing from soil, defect or sin.<BR>2. Expiation.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Nāgadanti.<BR>	 2. The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">Page673-b+ 60</a>]<BR>capital of BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. वि before शुध् to be pure, causal v.,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधनीय
विशोधनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be cleaned or purified, to be freed from<BR>soil, fault, &c.<BR> E. वि before शुध् to be pure, causal v., अनीयर् aff.;<BR>also विशोधितव्य and विशोध्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधित
विशोधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Purified, cleansed, freed from soil, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>before शुध् to be pure, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधित्व
विशोधित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Cleaning, purifying.<BR>	 2. Clearing, freeing from<BR>obstructions.<BR> E. विशोधिन् and त्व aff.; also with तल् विशोधिता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधिन्
विशोधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि)<BR>	 1. Cleaning, purifying.<BR>	 2. Clearing.<BR> E. वि<BR>before, शुध् to be pure, causal v., णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोध्य
विशोध्य n. (-ध्यं) A debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोषण|विशोषणं
विशोषण n. (-णं) Drying, desiccating.<BR> E. वि before शुष् to be dry, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोषित
विशोषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dried, dried up.<BR> E. वि before शुष् to be dry,<BR>causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्न|विश्नः
विश्न m. (-श्नः) Lustre, shining.<BR> E. विच्छ् or विश् to shine, नङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रणन|विश्रणनं
विश्रणन n. (-नं) Gift, giving, donation.<BR> E. वि before श्रण् to give, ल्युट्<BR>aff.; also विश्राणन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्ध|विश्रब्धः
विश्रब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Trusted, confident in, confided to.<BR>	 2. Patient,<BR>tranquil.<BR>	 3. Low-minded, not lofty, not magnanimous.<BR>	 4. Ex-<BR>cessive, exceeding, much.<BR>	 5. Firm, steady.<BR>	 6. Rested, reposed. E.<BR>वि before श्रम् to be weary or श्रम्भ् to trust, &c. aff. क्तः see विस्रब्ध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्धम्
विश्रब्धम् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of “confidingly”<BR>“without fear.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्धता
विश्रब्धता f. (-ता) Trust-worthiness.<BR> E. विश्रब्ध, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम|विश्रमः
विश्रम m. (-मः) Rest, repose, cessation from fatigue or work.<BR> E. वि pri-<BR>vative, श्रम् to be weary, aff. अच्; also with घञ्, विश्राम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रमित
विश्रमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Wearied, exhausted.<BR> E. विश्रम, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भ|विश्रंभ|विश्रंभः|विश्रम्भः
विश्रम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Trust, confidence.<BR>	 2. Affection, affectionate inquiry.<BR>3. Festive or sportive noise or tumult, amorous quarrel.<BR>	 4. Rest,<BR>repose.<BR>	 5. Killing.<BR> E. वि before श्रम्भ् to trust, aff. घञ्, and the<BR>initial optionally changed; also विस्रम्भ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्य
विश्रम्य Ind. Having rested.<BR> E. वि before, श्रम् to be weary, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रय|विश्रयः
विश्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Abode, asylum.<BR>	 2. Dependence upon.<BR> E. वि, श्री to<BR>serve, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रयिन्
विश्रयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिणी-यि)<BR>	 1. Living or dwelling in.<BR>	 2. Serving,<BR>depending on.<BR> E. वि before श्री to serve, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राणन|विश्राणनं
विश्राणन n. (-नं) Gift, giving donation.<BR> E. वि before श्रण् to give, r. 10th<BR>cl., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राणित
विश्राणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bestowed, given away.<BR> E. वि before श्रण् to<BR>give, r. 10th cl., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रान्त|विश्रांत|विश्रान्तः
विश्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Rested, reposed.<BR>	 2. Ceasing, desisting from.<BR>3. Calm, composed.<BR> E. वि before श्रान्त the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रान्ति|विश्रांति|विश्रांतिः|विश्रान्तिः
विश्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Rest, repose, cessation from toil or occupation.<BR> E. वि<BR>before श्रम् to be weary, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राम|विश्रामः
विश्राम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Rest, repose.<BR>	 2. Pause, stop, cessation.<BR>	 3. Tranquility,<BR>composure.<BR> E. वि before श्रम् to be weary, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राव|विश्रावः
विश्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Fame, celebrity.<BR>	 2. Flowing, dropping.<BR> E. वि before<BR>श्रु to hear or drop, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रावण
विश्रावण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Causing to flow or drop.<BR>	 2. Bleeding.<BR>	 3. Apprising,<BR>causing to hear.<BR> E. वि before श्रु to ooze, &c., causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुत|विश्रुतः
विश्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Famous, celebrated, renowned.<BR>	 2. Known.<BR>3. Pleased, happy.<BR>	 4. Dropped, flowing.<BR> E. वि before श्रुत heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुति|विश्रुतिः
विश्रुति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Celebrity, fame, notoriety.<BR>	 2. Oozing, flowing.<BR> E. वि<BR>before श्रु to hear, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लथ
विश्लथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Languid, relaxed, untied.<BR> E. वि before श्लथ loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लथाङ्ग
विश्लथाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Weak, relaxed.<BR> E. विश्लथ, अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लिष्ट
विश्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Separated, disunited.<BR> E. वि, श्लिष् to unite, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेष|विश्लेषः
विश्लेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Separation, distance, especially of lovers, or husband<BR>and wife.<BR>	 2. Disunion, disjunction, separation in general.<BR>	 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">Page674-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Absence, bereavement.<BR>	 4. A chasm.<BR>	 5. (In arithmetic,) The<BR>converse of addition.<BR> E. वि before श्लिष् to unite, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषजाति|विश्लेषजातिः
विश्लेषजाति f. (-तिः) (In arithmetic,) The assimilation of difference, the<BR>reduction of fractional difference.<BR> E. विश्लेष, and जाति kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषित
विश्लेषित f. (-ता) Disunited, severed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्व|विश्वं|विश्वः
विश्व mfn. (-श्वः-श्वा-श्वं) All, entire, whole, universal.<BR>	 n. (-श्वं) The world,<BR>the universe.<BR>	 m. Plu. (-श्वः) A deity of a particular class in which<BR>ten are enumerated; their names are VASU, SATYA, KRATU, DAKṢA,<BR>KĀLA, KĀMA, DHRITI, KURU, PURURAVAS, MĀDRAVAS: they are<BR>worshipped particularly at the funeral obsequies in honour of<BR>deceased progenitors in general, and receive an oblation of clarified<BR>butter at the daily and domestic Śrāddha.<BR>	 nf. (-श्वं-श्वा) Dry ginger.<BR>f. (-श्वा) A tree, the bark of which is said to be used in dyeing red,<BR>commonly Atis, (Betula.)<BR> E. विश् to enter, to pervade, Unādi aff. व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकद्रु|विश्वकद्रुः
विश्वकद्रु mfn. (-द्रुः-द्रुः-द्रु) Wicked, vile.<BR>	 m. (-द्रुः)<BR>	 1. A dog trained for the<BR>chase.<BR>	 2. Sound, noise.<BR> E. विश्व all, कन् pleonasm, द्रु to run, to pur-<BR>sue, aff. डु; or विश्व with कदि to cry or call, aff. डु and र augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकर्म्मन्|विश्वकर्मन्
विश्वकर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The son of BRAHMĀ, and artist of<BR>the gods.<BR>	 3. A saint.<BR> E. विश्व universal, कर्म्म work, act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकर्म्मसुता|विश्वकर्मसुता
विश्वकर्म्मसुता f. (-ता) SAṂJÑĀ, one of the wives of the sun.<BR> E. विश्वकर्म्मन्<BR>the artist of the gods, and सुता the daughter; also विश्वकर्म्मजा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वका
विश्वका f. (-का) A sort of gull, (Larus ridibundus.) “गाङ्गचिल् इति भाषा ।”<BR>E. विश्व all, कै to cry, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकृत्
विश्वकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Who or what makes all.<BR>	 m. (-कृत्)<BR>	 1. The creator,<BR>the maker of all things.<BR>	 2. The carpenter or architect, and artist<BR>of the gods.<BR> E. विश्व all and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकेतु|विश्वकेतुः
विश्वकेतु m. (-तुः) ANIRUDDHA, an incarnation of KĀMA, as the son<BR>of PRADYUMNA.<BR> E. विश्व universe, केतु a banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वकसेन
विश्वकसेन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A particular form of that deity, to<BR>whom the fragments of a sacrifice to VIṢṆU are offered.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>A plant, commonly priyangu.<BR> E. विश्वक् every way, and सेना an<BR>army; more properly विष्वक्सेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वगन्ध|विश्वगंध|विश्वगन्धं|विश्वगन्धः
विश्वगन्ध m. (-न्धः) An onion.<BR>	 n. (-न्धं) Myrrh.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा) The earth.<BR> E. विश्व<BR>all, universal, and गन्ध fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वगायत्
विश्वगायत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Spreading or going in every direction. E.<BR>विश्वक, आयत् going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वगोप्तृ
विश्वगोप्तृ m. (-प्ता)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. INDRA.<BR> E. विश्व all, गोप्तृ preserver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वङ्कर|विश्वंकर|विश्वंकरः|विश्वङ्करः
विश्वङ्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) All-creating, making all.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The eye.<BR> E. विश्व<BR>all, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजन
विश्वजन n. (-नं) All men, mankind.<BR> E. विश्व, जन people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजनीन
विश्वजनीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Good for or suitable to all men.<BR> E. विश्वजन, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजनीय
विश्वजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Suitable or relating to all men.<BR> E. विश्व all,<BR>जन mankind, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजन्य
विश्वजन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Fit or good for all men.<BR> E. विश्वजन, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वजित्
विश्वजित् mfn. (-जित्) All-subduing.<BR>	 m. (-जित्)<BR>	 1. A particular ceremony<BR>or sacrifice.<BR>	 2. The cord of noose of VARUṆA.<BR> E. विश्व all, and<BR>जित् what subdues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वञ्च्
विश्वञ्च् mfn. (-श्वङ्-शुची-श्वक्) Going every where. Ind. Adv. or n. (-श्वक्)<BR>Every where, universally.<BR> E. विश्व all, अञ्च् to go, aff. क्विप्; it is<BR>more usually written both in simple and compound forms विष्वञ्च्,<BR>from a different etymology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वतस्
विश्वतस् Ind. Every where, all around, universally.<BR> E. विश्व all, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वतोमुख
विश्वतोमुख Adj. Facing all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वथा
विश्वथा Ind. Every where.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वदेव|विश्वदेवः
विश्वदेव m. (-वः) A Viśvadeva, a deity of a particular class: see विश्व.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-वा) A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR> E. विश्व all, दिव् to<BR>sport, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वद्र्यञ्च्
विश्वद्र्यञ्च् mfn. (-द्र्यङ्-द्रीची-द्र्यक्) Moving every where, or universally.<BR>E. विश्वक every where, अद्रि substituted for the final, अञ्च् to go, aff.<BR>क्विप्; also विष्वद्र्यञ्च् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वधारिन्
विश्वधारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) All-sustaining.<BR>	 m. (-री) A deity.<BR>	 f. (-रिणी)<BR>The earth.<BR> E. विश्व all, and धारिन् upholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वनाथ|विश्वनाथः
विश्वनाथ m. (-थः) A name of Śiva, especially as the object of peculiar<BR>adoration at Benares.<BR> E. विश्व the universe, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वपा
विश्वपा m. (-पाः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR>	 4. The protector of<BR>all.<BR> E. विश्व, and पा who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वपावनी
विश्वपावनी f. (-नी) Holy basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वप्सन्
विश्वप्सन् m. (-प्सा)<BR>	 1. Fire, or the deity of fire.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. The<BR>sun.<BR>	 4. A god.<BR>	 5. The earth.<BR> E. विश्व all, प्सा to eat, Unādi aff. कनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वबोध|विश्वबोधः
विश्वबोध m. (-धः) A Buddha or Bauddha deified saint.<BR> E. विश्व all, and<BR>बोध who explains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वभुज्
विश्वभुज् mfn. (-भुक्)<BR>	 1. Enjoying or possessing all things.<BR>	 2. Eating all<BR>things.<BR> E. विश्व, and भुज् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वभू
विश्वभू m. (-भूः) The third of the seven Buddhas, according to some<BR>systems.<BR> E. विश्व all, and भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वभेषज|विश्वभेषजं|विश्वभेषजः
विश्वभेषज n. (-जं) Dry ginger.<BR> E. विश्व all, (diseases,) भेषज a medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वभोजन
विश्वभोजन n. (-नं) Eating all sorts of food.<BR> E. विश्व, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वभोजस्
विश्वभोजस् m. (-जाः) One who enjoys all things.<BR> E. विश्व all, भुज् to enjoy,<BR>Unādi aff. असि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वमदा
विश्वमदा f. (-दा) One of the seven tongues of fire.<BR> E. विश्व all, मद् to in-<BR>toxicate, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वम्मर
विश्वम्मर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) All-sustaining.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. INDRA.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-रा) The earth.<BR> E. विश्व all, (things,) भृ to support or nourish, अच्<BR>aff., मुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वम्भराधिप
विश्वम्भराधिप m. (-पः) A king.<BR> E. विश्वम्भरा the earth, and अधिप ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वयु|विश्वयुः
विश्वयु m. (-युः) Air, wind.<BR> E. विश्व all, यु to join, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वराज्
विश्वराज् m. (-राट् or राड्) A universal sovereign.<BR> E. विश्व all, राज् who rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वरूप|विश्वरूपः
विश्वरूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Taking all forms, existing in all forms,<BR>universal, omnipresent.<BR>	 m. (-पः) VIṢṆU.<BR>	 n. (-पं) Agallochum. E.<BR>विश्व all, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वरेतस्
विश्वरेतस् m. (-ताः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. विश्व all, रेतस् seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वरोचन|विश्वरोचनः
विश्वरोचन m. (-नः) An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR> E. विश्व all, रोचन digestive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वविधायिन्
विश्वविधायिन् m. (-यी) A deity, a creator.<BR> E. विश्व, विधायिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्ववेदस्
विश्ववेदस् m. (-दाः)<BR>	 1. A sage, a saint, one who knows all things.<BR>	 2. An<BR>epithet of AGNI.<BR> E. विश्व all, विदि to know, aff. असि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वव्यापक
विश्वव्यापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) All-pervading, every where diffused.<BR> E. विश्व,<BR>and व्यापक what pervades.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वव्यापिन्
विश्वव्यापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) All-diffused or pervading.<BR> E. विश्व, and व्यापिन् what spreads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वव्याप्ति
विश्वव्याप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Universal diffusion or permeation.<BR> E. विश्व, and व्याप्ति<BR>spreading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसन
विश्वसन n. (-नं) Trusting, confiding in.<BR> E. वि before श्वस् to breathe, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसनीय
विश्वसनीय f. (-या) Capable of inspiring confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसह
विश्वसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) All-enduring.<BR>	 f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. The earth.<BR>	 2. One of<BR>the seven tongues of fire.<BR> E. विश्व all, सह् to bear, affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसारक|विश्वसारकं
विश्वसारक n. (-कं) The prickly pear, (Cactus Indicus, Rox.) “फणिमन्सा.”<BR>E. विश्व all, सार essence, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसित|विश्वसितः
विश्वसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Trusted, believed or confided in.<BR> E. वि before<BR>श्वस् to breathe, aff. क्त, with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसृज्
विश्वसृज् m. (-सृक्, सृग्, सृट् or सृड्) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. विश्व all, (the universe,)<BR>सृज् to create, aff. क्विन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वस्त|विश्वस्तः
विश्वस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Trusted, confided in, faithful.<BR>	 f. (-स्ता) A<BR>widow.<BR> E. वि implying kind or sort, or in the fem. form, privation,<BR>and श्वस् to live or breathe, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वस्रष्टृ
विश्वस्रष्टृ m. (-ष्टा) The creator of all.<BR> E. विश्व, स्रष्टृ creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वाची
विश्वाची f. (-ची) One of the Apsarās or courtezans of Svarga.<BR> E. विश्वमञ्चति अन्च्-क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वात्मन्
विश्वात्मन् m. (-त्मा) BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 n. (-त्म) The soul of the world, the univer-<BR>sal spirit, GOD.<BR> E. विश्व all, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वाधायस्
विश्वाधायस् m. (-याः) A deity, a god.<BR> E. विश्व all, आङ् before धा to hold or<BR>support, असि aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वामित्र|विश्वामित्रः
विश्वामित्र m. (-त्रः) A Muni, the son of GĀDHĪ, originally of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">Page675-a+ 60</a>]<BR>military order, but who became by long and painful austerities a<BR>Brahmarshi, in which character he appears in the RĀMĀYAṆA,<BR>as the early preceptor and counsellor of RĀMA.<BR> E. विश्व all, मित्र<BR>the friend, and the vowel of the prefix made long in this sense;<BR>if attributively used, the compound is विश्वमित्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वामित्रप्रिय|विश्वामित्रप्रियः
विश्वामित्रप्रिय m. (-यः) The cocoanut tree.<BR> E. विश्वामित्र the saint VIŚWĀ-<BR>MITRA, and प्रिय beloved, having been created by the saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वावसु|विश्वावसुः
विश्वावसु m. (-सुः) One of the Gandharbas or celestial singers.<BR>	 f. (-सुः) A<BR>particular night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वास|विश्वासः
विश्वास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Trust, faith, confidence.<BR>	 2. A confidential commu-<BR>nication.<BR> E. वि before श्वस् to breathe or live, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासकारण
विश्वासकारण n. (-णं) Cause or motive of trust.<BR> E. विश्वास, कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासकृत्
विश्वासकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Inspiring confidence or faith.<BR> E. विश्वास, and कृत्<BR>who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासघात|विश्वासघातः
विश्वासघात m. (-तः) Violation of trust, treachery.<BR> E. विश्वास, and घात destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासघातक|विश्वासघातकः
विश्वासघातक m. (-कः) A traitor, one who betrays confidence.<BR> E. विश्वास,<BR>and घातक who destroys; also विश्वासघातिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासपात्र
विश्वासपात्र n. (-त्रं) A confidential agent, one worthy to be trusted. E.<BR>विश्वास, and पात्र person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासप्रतिपन्न
विश्वासप्रतिपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Confiding, trusting.<BR> E. विश्वास, and प्रतिपन्न possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासप्रद
विश्वासप्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Inspiring confidence.<BR> E. विश्वास, प्रद who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासभङ्ग|विश्वासभङ्गः
विश्वासभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Breach of faith, violation of confidence.<BR> E. विश्वास,<BR>and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासभूमि|विश्वासभूमिः
विश्वासभूमि f. (-मिः) An object of trust, a person worthy of confidence.<BR>E. विश्वास, and भूमि place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासस्थान
विश्वासस्थान n. (-नं) An object or person of trust or confidence.<BR> E. विश्वास, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासित
विश्वासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inspired with confidence.<BR> E. वि before श्वस् to<BR>breathe, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासिन्
विश्वासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>	 1. Trusting, confiding in.<BR>	 2. Honest, trusty.<BR>E. विश्वास, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वास्य
विश्वास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>	 1. To be trusted or depended on, to be<BR>believed.<BR>	 2. To be encouraged or inspired with confidence. Ind.<BR>Having encouraged or inspired with confidence.<BR> E. वि before श्वस्<BR>to breathe, ण्यत् aff; or causal v., and यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वास्यता
विश्वास्यता f. (-ता) Trust-worthiness.<BR> E. विश्वास्य, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वेदेवृ
विश्वेदेवृ m. (-वा) The clitoris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वेश|विश्वेशः
विश्वेश m. (-शः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. विश्व all, ईश lord: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वेश्वर|विश्वेश्वरः
विश्वेश्वर m. (-रः) ŚIVA, under a form or appellation in which espe-<BR>cially he is worshipped at Benares, where a celebrated temple is<BR>appropriated to him in the character of lord or god of the uni-<BR>verse.<BR> E. विश्व the universe, and ईश्वर god; also similar compounds,<BR>as विश्वेश, विश्वनाथ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
विष् r. 6th cl. (विषति) To pervade. (औ) औविष r. 9th cl. (विष्णाति) To<BR>have no occasion or use for, to separate or withdraw from, to<BR>disjoin. (उ) विषु r. 1st cl. (वेषति) To sprinkle. (औ इर ऌ) औ इर विषॢ<BR>r. 3rd cl. (वेवेष्टि-वेविष्टे)<BR>	 1. To pervade, to spread or extend through<BR>nature, &c.<BR>	 2. To go to, to go against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
विष् f. (-विट्)<BR>	 1. Fæces, ordure.<BR>	 2. Diffusion, spreading.<BR>	 3. A virgin.<BR>E. विष् to pervade, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष|विषं|विषः
विष mn. (-षः-षं) Poison, venom.<BR>	 n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. The fibres attached<BR>to the stalk of the lotus.<BR>	 3. Gum-myrrh.<BR>	 4. A vegetable poison,<BR>(Aconitum ferox.)<BR>	 f. (-षा) A tree, the bark of which is used in dye-<BR>ing of a red colour.<BR> E. विष् to pervade, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषकृमिन्याय
विषकृमिन्याय m. (-यः) The maxim of a worm in poison. It denotes a<BR>state of things which, though fatal to others, is not so to those<BR>who are born therein or naturalized thereto.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषक्त
विषक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Clinging or adhering to closely.<BR>	 2. In contact<BR>with.<BR> E. वि before षञ्ज् to embrace, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषघा
विषघा f. (घा) A twining shrub, (Menispermum cordifolium.)<BR> E. विष<BR>poison, हन् to destroy, aff. ड, घ substituted for the final. “गुडूच्याम्”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषघातिन्
विषघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Antidotic, an antidote.<BR>	 m. (-ती) A tree,<BR>(Mimosa sirisa.)<BR> E. विष poison, and घातिन् removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषघ्न|विषघ्नः
विषघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Antidotic, an antidote.<BR>	 m. (-घ्नः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Mimosa<BR>sirisa.)<BR>	 2. A plant, (Hedysarum alhaji.)<BR>	 3. Beleric myrobalan.<BR>(Terminalia belerica.)<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी)<BR>	 1. A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR>2. A plant, commonly Bichati.<BR>	 3. Turmeric.<BR>	 4. Bitter apple or<BR>colocynth.<BR> E. विष poison, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषजुष्ट
विषजुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Poisoned, suffering from poison.<BR>	 2. Poison-<BR>ous.<BR> E. विष, and जुष्ट united with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषज्वर|विषज्वरः
विषज्वर m. (-रः) A buffalo.<BR> E. विषमिव प्राणहन्ता ज्वरो यस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषणि
विषणि m. (-णिः) A sort of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्ड|विषंड|विषंडं|विषण्डं
विषण्ड n. (-ण्डं) The fibres of the stalk of the water-lily. “मृणाले ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्ण|विषण्णः
विषण्ण mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं) Dejected, desponding, spiritless, disinclined to<BR>exertion.<BR> E. वि before सद् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्णता
विषण्णता f. (-ता) Dejection, lassitude, want of energy or spirit, espe-<BR>cially as one of the effects of unsuccessful love.<BR> E. विषण्ण relaxed,<BR>तल् aff. of the abstract; also with त्व विषण्णत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्णवदन
विषण्णवदन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Looking sad or dejected.<BR> E. विषण्ण, and वदन<BR>face: also विषण्णमुख, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषतुल्य
विषतुल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं) Fatal, deadly.<BR> E. विष, and तुल्य equal to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषत्वर
विषत्वर m. (-रः) A buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषद|विषदं|विषदः
विषद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Yielding or giving poison.<BR>	 2. Shedding water.<BR>m. (-दः) A cloud.<BR>	 n. (-दं) Green vitriol.<BR> E. विष poison or water, and<BR>दा to give, aff. क; or वि + षद्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषदंष्ट्रा
विषदंष्ट्रा f. (-ष्ट्रा) A medicinal plant and antidote, commonly Sarpa-<BR>kankāli.<BR> E. विष venom, दंष्ट्र a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषदन्तक|विषदंतक|विषदन्तकः
विषदन्तक m. (-कः) A snake.<BR> E. विष poison, दन्त tooth, and कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषदर्शनमृत्युक|विषदर्शनमृत्युकः
विषदर्शनमृत्युक m. (-कः) The Chakora bird.<BR> E. विष poison, (perhaps put<BR>for the snake,) दर्शन seeing, मृत्युक who dies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषधर|विषधरः
विषधर mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं) Venomous, poisonous.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A snake.<BR>E. विष poison, धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषधर्म्मा|विषधर्मा
विषधर्म्मा f. (-र्म्मा) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.) “आल्कुशी ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषधात्री
विषधात्री f. (-त्री) The wife of JARATKĀRU, and goddess presiding over<BR>snakes.<BR> E. विष venom, धात्री a nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषनाशन|विषनाशनः
विषनाशन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Mimosa sirisa.)<BR>	 2. An antidote.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>Removing or curing poison.<BR> E. विष poison, and नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषनाशिन्
विषनाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Antidote.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A plant: see विषदंष्ट्रा. E.<BR>विष venom, नाशिन् destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषनुद्
विषनुद् m. (-नुत्) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.) “श्योनाकवृक्षे”.<BR> E. विष poison,<BR>नुद् to eject, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषपुष्प|विषपुष्पं|विषपुष्पः
विषपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>	 n. (-ष्पं) The blue lotus.<BR>E. विष poison, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषपुष्पक|विषपुष्पकः
विषपुष्पक m. (-कः) Sickness or disease induced by eating poisonous<BR>flowers.<BR> E. विष poison, पुष्प a flower; or विषपुष्प the Vangueria, &c.,<BR>कन् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषप्रयोग|विषप्रयोगः
विषप्रयोग m. (-गः) Employing or administering poison.<BR> E. विष and प्रयोग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषभक्षण
विषभक्षण n. (-णं) Taking poison.<BR> E. विष, and भक्षण feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषभिषज्
विषभिषज् m. (-षक्) A dealer in antidotes, a snake-catcher, or one who<BR>pretends to cure the bite of a snake.<BR> E. विष poison, भिषज् a doctor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषभुजङ्ग|विषभुजंग|विषभुजङ्गः
विषभुजङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A poisonous snake.<BR> E. विष poison, and भुजङ्ग a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषभृत्
विषभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Venomous, poisonous.<BR>	 m. (-भृत्) A snake.<BR> E. विष, and<BR>भृत् who or what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषम|विषमं|विषमः
विषम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Difficult, (of access,) rough, uneven.<BR>	 2. Diffi-<BR>cult, &c., (of comprehending,) as a book.<BR>	 3. Painful, difficult,<BR>troublesome. (in general.)<BR>	 4. Odd, (in numbers.)<BR>	 5. Unparalleled,<BR>unequalled.<BR>	 6. Wicked, dishonest.<BR>	 7. Fearful, frightful, awful.<BR>8. Irregular, unequal.<BR>	 9. Adverse, unpropitious.<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Difficulty, pain.<BR>	 2. Unevenness, inequality.<BR>	 3. Oddness, (in<BR>numeration.)<BR>	 4. An inaccessible place, a thicket, a precipice.<BR>	 5.<BR>(In rhetoric.) Description of unusual or incompatible cause and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">Page676-a+ 60</a>]<BR>effect.<BR> E. वि privative or contra-indicative, before सम even, smooth,<BR>equal, &c. and स after the इ of the prefix, changed to ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमकर्ण|विषमकर्णः
विषमकर्ण m. (-र्णः) The hypothenuse of a right-angled triangle, formed<BR>between the gnomon and the two sides of the shadow. विषम, and<BR>कर्ण hypothenuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमकर्म्मन्|विषमकर्मन्
विषमकर्म्मन् n. (र्म्म)<BR>	 1. An odd or unparalleled act.<BR>	 2. (In arithmetic,)<BR>The finding of quantities from their difference or that of their<BR>squares.<BR> E. विषम and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमखात
विषमखात n. (-तं) An irregular excavation or one with unequal sides. E.<BR>विषम and खात excavation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमचतुरस्र|विषमचतुरस्रः
विषमचतुरस्र n. (-स्रं) An unequal four-sided figure, a trapezium.<BR> E. विषम, चतुरस्र four-angled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमच्छद|विषमच्छदः|विषमछद
विषमच्छद m. (-दः) A plant, (Echites scholaris.)<BR> E. विषम odd, and छद<BR>a leaf; having seven leaves on a stalk. “सप्तच्छद वृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमच्छाया|विषमछाया
विषमच्छाया f. (-या) The shadow of the gnomon at noon when the sun<BR>is in the equinoxes.<BR> E. विषम oblique, and छाया shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमज्वर|विषमज्वरः
विषमज्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A violent fever.<BR>	 2. Irregularly remittent fever. E.<BR>विषम and ज्वर a fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमत्रिभुज|विषमत्रिभुजः
विषमत्रिभुज m. (-जः) A scalene triangle.<BR> E. विषम unequal, त्रिभुज triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमनयन|विषमनयनः
विषमनयन m. (-नः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. विषम odd, नयन an eye; having a third<BR>eye in his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमन्त्र|विषमंत्र|विषमन्त्रः
विषमन्त्र m. (-न्त्रः) A snake-catcher, one who by pretended charms, &c.<BR>attracts snakes and cures the bite.<BR>	 n. (-न्त्रं) A charm for curing<BR>snake bites.<BR> E. विष poison, मन्त्र a charm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषममय|विषममयं
विषममय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Resulting from or produced by inequality.<BR> E. विषम, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमरूप्य|विषमरूप्यं
विषमरूप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Resulting from or produced by unequal<BR>quantities or qualities.<BR> E. विषम uneven, and रूप्य aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमविभाग|विषमविभागः
विषमविभाग m. (-गः) Unequal division of property amongst co-heirs. E.<BR>विषम uneven, विभाग portion of inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमशायिन्
विषमशायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Sleeping irregularly.<BR> E. विषम and शायिन् who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमशिष्ट|विषमशिष्टः
विषमशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Unjust, unfair, (division)<BR> E. विषम, शिष्ट left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशमशील
विशमशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Uneven.<BR>	 2. Uneasy.<BR> E. विषम, शील having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमसाहस
विषमसाहस n. (-सं) Temcrity, daring.<BR> E. विषम and साहस violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमस्थ|विषमस्थः
विषमस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Standing unevenly.<BR>	 2. Inaccessible, safely<BR>posted.<BR>	 3. Being in difficulty, &c.<BR> E. विषम uneven, स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमाक्ष|विषमाक्षः
विषमाक्ष m. (-क्षः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. विषम odd, अक्षि the eye, aff. टच्; having a<BR>third eye, or one in his forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमायुध|विषमायुधः
विषमायुध m. (-धः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. विषम odd, आयुध a weapon; armed<BR>with five arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमाशन
विषमाशन n. (-नं) Eating irregularly, either as to quantity or time.<BR> E. विषम and अशन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमाशय
विषमाशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Crafty, dishonest.<BR> E. विषम and आशय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमित
विषमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made or become uneven, irregular, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Made difficult.<BR> E. विषम and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमीय|विषमीयं
विषमीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Produced or resulting from inequalities. E.<BR>विषम uneven, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमुष्टि|विषमुष्टिः
विषमुष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A kind of shrub of medicinal properties, commonly<BR>termed Bishdori or Kadhsinh.<BR> E. विष poison, मुष्टि a handful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमृत्यु|विषमृत्युः
विषमृत्यु m. (-त्युः) The Chakora bird.<BR> E. विष poison, and मृत्यु death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमेक्षण|विषमेक्षणः
विषमेक्षण m. (-णः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. विषम odd, (three,) ईक्षण eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमेषु|विषमेषुः
विषमेषु m. (-षुः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. विषम odd, (five,) इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषय|विषयः
विषय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Any object of sense, any thing perceivable by the<BR>senses, as colour, form, flavour, odour and sound; they are five<BR>for the five Indriyas, viz:--शब्द for the ear, स्पर्श for the skin, रूप<BR>for the eye, रस for the tongue, गन्ध for the nose.<BR>	 2. An object in<BR>general, as of affection or desire, &c.<BR>	 3. Worldly object or<BR>pursuit, affair, business, transaction, &c.<BR>	 4. A country, whether<BR>inhabited or uninhabited.<BR>	 5. Refuge, asylum.<BR>	 6. Department,<BR>sphere, element, home, province, that which is peculiarly known<BR>or frequented, as a particular study by its professors, a particular<BR>town by its townsfolk, water by fish, air by birds, &c.<BR>	 7. A collec-<BR>tion of villages.<BR>	 8. Any thing indigenous or peculiar to a province,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">Page676-b+ 60</a>]<BR>&c.<BR>	 9. A religious obligation or observance.<BR>	 10. Semen virile.<BR>	 11.<BR>A lover, a husband.<BR>	 12. Sensual enjoyment, sensuality.<BR>	 13. Sub-<BR>ject, topic, subject-matter.<BR>	 14. The subject of an Adhikaraṇa, (in<BR>Phil.)<BR>	 15. A thing aimed at.<BR>	 16. Scope, range, compass, reach.<BR>17. A realm, a kingdom, a domain.<BR> E. वि before षि to bind, aff.<BR>अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयक
विषयक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Relating to, concerning, (any object.)<BR> E. विषय and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयकत्व
विषयकत्व n. (-त्वं) State of an affair, circumstance or thing.<BR> E. त्व added<BR>to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयकर्म्मन्|विषयकर्मन्
विषयकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Worldly concern or act.<BR> E. विषय, कर्म्म act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयकाम
विषयकाम m. (-मः) Desire of worldly goods or pleasures.<BR> E. विषय, काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयग्राम|विषयग्रामः
विषयग्राम m. (-मः) The aggregate of the objects of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयवासिन्
विषयवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Engaged in the affairs of life<BR> E. विषय<BR>and वासिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयात्मक
विषयात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Identical with or affecting sensual or<BR>worldly objects.<BR> E. विषय and आत्मक own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयाभिरति|विषयाभिरतिः
विषयाभिरति f. (-तिः) Attachment to the objects of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयायिन्
विषयायिन् m. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A king.<BR>	 2. An organ of sense.<BR>	 3. KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 4.<BR>An epicurean, a sensualist, one heedful of objects of sense or<BR>attentive to worldly objects.<BR>	 5. A materialist, one who disbelieves<BR>the existence of that which is not cognizable by the senses. E.<BR>विषय an object of sense, अय् to go, to follow, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयासक्त
विषयासक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Attached to objects of sense, devoted to<BR>the world.<BR> E. विषय and आसक्त attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयिन्
विषयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिणी-यि)<BR>	 1. Attached to objects of sense, carnal, sen-<BR>sual.<BR>	 2. Conversant with or interested in worldly occupations or<BR>enjoyments.<BR>	 n. (-यि) An organ of sense.<BR>	 m. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A king.<BR>	 2.<BR>The deity KĀMA.<BR>	 3. A sensualist.<BR>	 4. A materialist, one who<BR>denies the existence of any thing which is not an object of sense.<BR>5. A man of business.<BR> E. विषय an organ of sense, aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयोपसेवा
विषयोपसेवा f. (-वा) Sensuality.<BR> E. विषय and उपसेवा addiction to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषल|विषलं|विषलः
विषल m. (-लः) Poison, venom.<BR> E. विष poison, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषविद्या
विषविद्या f. (-द्या) The administration of antidotes, the cure of poisons<BR>by drugs or charms.<BR> E. विष poison, विद्या science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषविधान
विषविधान n. (-नं) Administering poison judicially, or by way of ordeal.<BR>E. विष, विधान rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषवेग|विषवेगः
विषवेग m. (-गः) Absorption of venom, as shown by some bodily effects<BR>or changes.<BR> E. विष poison, and वेग natural excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषवैद्य|विषवैद्यः
विषवैद्य m. (-द्यः) A dealer in antidotes, one professing by charms, &c.<BR>to cure the bite of a snake.<BR> E. विष poison, and वैद्य physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषशालूक|विषशालूकः
विषशालूक m. (-कः) The root of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषशूक|विषशूकः
विषशूक m. (-कः) A wasp.<BR> E. विष venom, and शूक a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषशृङ्गिन्|विषशृंगिन्
विषशृङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी) A wasp.<BR> E. विष poison, शृङ्ग a horn, and इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषसूचक|विषसूचकः
विषसूचक m. (-कः) The Greek partridge, (Perdix rufa.) “चकोर खगे” E.<BR>विष poison, and सूचक informer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषसृक्कन्
विषसृक्कन् m. (-क्का) A wasp.<BR> E. विष poison, सृक्कन् the corner of the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषहर|विषहरः
विषहर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) An antidote, removing venom.<BR>	 f. (-रा or री) The<BR>goddess of the serpent race, the sister of VĀSUKI, and wife of<BR>JARATKĀRU.<BR> E. विष venom, हृ to take, aff. अप् or टच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषहृदय
विषहृदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Malicious, malignant, cherishing hatred or<BR>hostility.<BR> E. विष, and हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषह्य
विषह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. To be borne or endured.<BR>	 2. Possible to be<BR>determined. Ind. Having borne.<BR> E. वि, षह् to bear, aff. यत् or ल्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषा
विषा Ind. Apotte noun. Intellect, understanding.<BR>	 f. (-षा) Ordure, feces.<BR>E. षो to destroy, (ignorance,) with वि prefixed, and ओ Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाङ्कुर|विषांकुर|विषाङ्कुरः
विषाङ्कुर m. (-रः) A spear, a dart.<BR> E. विष poison, अङ्कुर a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाण|विषाणं|विषाणः
विषाण Subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>	 1. The horn of an animal.<BR>	 2. The tusks<BR>of an elephant.<BR>	 3. The tusk or fang of the boar.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A plant,<BR>the fruit of which is compared to the horn of a ram, &c. com-<BR>monly Mesa Sringī.<BR>	 2. A medicinal root: see क्षीरकाकोली.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">Page677-a+ 60</a>]<BR>A sort of Costus, (C. speciosus.)<BR> E. वि before अस् to be, चानश् aff.;<BR>the initial of the radical rejected, and स changed to ष; otherwise,<BR>वि before षण् to serve, aff. घञ्; or विष वा-कानच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणिका
विषाणिका f. (-का) A sort of plant, commonly Mesha Shringī.<BR> E. विषाणी<BR>as above, and कन् pleonasm; fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणिन्
विषाणिन् m. (-णी)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. A bull.<BR>	 3. Any animal with<BR>horns.<BR>	 f. (-णिनी) Having tusks or horns.<BR> E. विषाण a horn, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाद|विषादः
विषाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Lassitude, dejection, lowness of spirits, want of<BR>energy, especially as the result of unrequited love.<BR>	 2. Distress,<BR>affliction.<BR>	 2. Disappointment.<BR> E. वि before षद् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषादिन्
विषादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Dejected, disconsolate.<BR> E. विषाद, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषानन|विषाननः
विषानन m. (-नः) A snake.<BR> E. विष poison, and आनन the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषान्तक|विषांतक|विषान्तकः
विषान्तक m. (-कः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. विष poison, अन्तक destroyer; having swallow-<BR>ed the poison that was produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषापह|विषापहः
विषापह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Antidotic, an antidote.<BR>	 f. (-हा) A kind of birth-<BR>wort, (Aristolochia Indica.)<BR> E. विष poison, and अपह removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषायुध|विषायुधः
विषायुध m. (-धः) A snake.<BR> E. विष poison, and आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषार|विषारः
विषार m. (-रः) A snake.<BR> E. विष poison, ऋ to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषालु
विषालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Venomous, poisonous.<BR> E. विष, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषास्य|विषास्यः
विषास्य m. (-स्यः) A snake.<BR>	 f. (-स्या) Marking-nut plant, (Semicarpus<BR>anacardium.)<BR> E. विष poison, and आस्य face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषीदत्
विषीदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्) Sorrowing, despairing.<BR> E. वि before षद् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषु
विषु Ind.<BR>	 1. Many, various.<BR>	 2. Equally, same, like.<BR> E. विष, कु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुण|विषुणः
विषुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Having or possessing various or uniform<BR>motion or extension.<BR> E. विष्वञ्च् going every where, न poss. aff.,<BR>and the final consonant of the primitive rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुप|विषुपं
विषुप n. (-पं) The equinox: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुव|विषुवं
विषुव n. (-वं) The first point of ARIES or LIBRA into which the sun<BR>enters at the vernal or autumnal equinox.<BR> E. विषु equally, (the<BR>night and day,) and व or प aff.; also विषुप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवच्छाया|विषुवछाया
विषुवच्छाया f. (-या) The shadow of the gnomon at noon when the sun<BR>is in the equinoctial points.<BR> E. विषुव and छाया shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवत्|विषुवन्त्
विषुवत् n. (-वत्) The equinoctial point.<BR> E. विषु equally, (long, the day<BR>and night,) and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवदिन
विषुवदिन n. (-नं) The day of the equinox.<BR> E. विषुव and दिन day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवरेखा
विषुवरेखा f. (-खा) The equinoctial line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवसङ्क्रान्ति|विषुवसंक्रान्ति|विषुवसंक्रांति|विषुवसंक्रान्तिः
विषुवसङ्क्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः) The passage of the sun to the next sign at the<BR>equinoxes.<BR> E. विषुव, and सङ्क्रान्ति sun's entrance into a sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्क्
विष्क् r. 10th cl. (विष्कयति-ते) To see, to perceive. (विष्कयते) To injure or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्तृ
विष्कन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Going, going in various directions, dispersing.<BR>E. वि before स्कदि to go, तृन् aff.; also विस्कन्तृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्द|विष्कंद|विष्कंदः|विष्कन्दः
विष्कन्द m. (-न्दः) Going, dispersing.<BR> E. वि before स्कदि to go, अच् aff.; also विस्कन्द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्न
विष्कन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Gone.<BR>	 2. Gone in various directions, dis-<BR>persed.<BR> E. वि before स्कन्द् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भ|विष्कंभ|विष्कंभः|विष्कम्भः
विष्कम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. The first of the twenty-seven astronomical periods,<BR>called Yogās or Yoga star of the first lunar mansion.<BR>	 2. Obstacle,<BR>hindrance, impediment, resistance.<BR>	 3. Spreading, extension.<BR>	 4.<BR>Act, doing any thing.<BR>	 5. A posture of the devotees called Yogīs.<BR>6. One of the performers at a dramatic entertainment, either an<BR>actor who in the intervals of the scenes explains to the audience<BR>the progress of the story, or one or two of the personages of the<BR>drama, who do the same in a soliloquy or dialogue.<BR>	 7. A tree.<BR>	 8.<BR>The bolt or bar of a door.<BR>	 9. A post, the roof-tree of a house.<BR>	 10.<BR>The diameter of a circle.<BR> E. वि before ष्कभि to stop or hinder, aff.<BR>घञ्; or वि + स्कन्भ्-अच्; also with कन् added, विष्कम्भक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भक|विष्कंभक
विष्कम्भक m. (-कः) A Yoga, &c.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भिन्|विष्कंभिन्
विष्कम्भिन् mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि) Obstructive, impeding.<BR>	 m. (-म्भी) The<BR>bolt or bar of a door.<BR> E. विष्कम्भ obstruction, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्किर|विष्किरः
विष्किर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bird in general.<BR>	 2. Pulling or tearing to pieces.<BR>	 3.<BR>A cock.<BR> E. वि before कॄ to scatter, and क aff., with सुट् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ट|विष्टः
विष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Entered, penetrated, pervaded.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा) Fæces. E.<BR>विष् to pervade, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टप|विष्टपं|विष्टपः
विष्टप mn. (-पः-पं) A world.<BR> E. विश् to enter, (into which,) कपन् aff., तुट् aug.; also विष्टभ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टभ
विष्टभ n. (-भं) A world.<BR> E. विश् to pervade, अभच् aff., the vowel unchan-<BR>ged; deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टब्ध
विष्टब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Hindered, obstructed.<BR>	 2. Stayed, fixed, firm,<BR>well-supported.<BR>	 3. Placed in or upon.<BR>	 4. Paralysed, made stiff or<BR>motionless.<BR> E. वि before स्तभि to stop, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भ|विष्टंभ|विष्टंभः|विष्टम्भः
विष्टम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Impediment, hindrance, obstacle.<BR>	 2. Stopping, stay-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Placing in or upon.<BR>	 4. A disease, obstruction of urine or<BR>fæces, ischury, constipation.<BR>	 5. Paralysis, loss of motion.<BR> E. वि<BR>before स्तभि to stop or hinder, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भिन्|विष्टंभिन्
विष्टम्भिन् mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>	 1. Stopping, impeding, what hinders or<BR>obstructs.<BR>	 2. Checking, (as perspiration,) chilling.<BR>	 3. Making<BR>motionless.<BR> E. वि before स्तभि to stop, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टर|विष्टरः
विष्टर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. A handful of Kuśa or sacred grass.<BR>	 3. A<BR>seat, a stool, a chair, a couch, &c.<BR>	 4. The seat of the Brāhman,<BR>either real or in effigy, as presiding at a sacrifice.<BR>	 5. A bed.<BR>	 6. A<BR>seat made of twenty-five straws of Kuśa grass tied up in a sheaf.<BR>E. वि before स्तृ to spread, aff. अप् and स changed to ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टरश्रवस्
विष्टरश्रवस् m. (-वाः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. विष्टर a tree, श्रु to hear, aff. असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टरस्थ
विष्टरस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Sitting on a seat, or reclining on a bed of<BR>leaves.<BR> E. विष्टर and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टार|विष्टारः
विष्टार m. (-रः) A form of metre, a species of the order termed Panktī,<BR>consisting of a verse of four lines, the first and last of which<BR>consist of eight syllables each, and the second and third of twelve<BR>each.<BR> E. वि before स्तृ to spread, aff. घञ्, and स changed to ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टि|विष्टिः
विष्टि mfn. (-ष्टिः-ष्टिः-ष्टि) Working, labouring, a workman.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Unpaid labour, working without wages.<BR>	 2. Occupation, act, action.<BR>3. Hire, wages.<BR>	 4. The seventh of the variable Karaṇas, or astro-<BR>logical periods so termed, each answering to half a lunar day.<BR>	 5.<BR>Sending, dispatching.<BR>	 6. Consigning to torture, casting into hell,<BR>&c.<BR> E. विश् to enter, (into pain by it,) and क्तिन् or क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठल|विष्ठलं
विष्ठल n. (-लं) A place situated remote or apart.<BR> E. वि implying apart,<BR>स्थल a place, and स changed to ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठा
विष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>	 1. Fæces, ordure, excrement.<BR>	 2. The belly.<BR> E. वि before<BR>स्था to stay, (in the intestines,) affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णु|विष्णुः
विष्णु m. (-ष्णुः) VIṢṆU, one of the three principal Hindu deities, and<BR>the preserver of the world: during the periods of temporary anni-<BR>hilation, he is supposed to sleep on the waters floating on the<BR>serpent Śeṣa: BRAHMĀ is fabled to have sprung from a lotus,<BR>which originally grew from the navel of VIṢṆU, and the holy<BR>river Ganges is said to spring from his foot: the different<BR>Avatārs are considered as emanations of this deity, and in<BR>KṚṢṆA, he is supposed to have been really and wholly<BR>incarnate: LAKṢMĪ is his wife, and he is usually represented as a<BR>mild and benevolent deity.<BR>	 2. AGNI or fire.<BR>	 3. One of the demigods<BR>called Vasus.<BR>	 4. A pure or pious man.<BR>	 5. The name of an ancient<BR>law-giver.<BR> E. विश् to enter or pervade, (the universe,) नुक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुक्रान्ता
विष्णुक्रान्ता f. (-न्ता) A flower, (Clitorea ternatea.)<BR> E. विष्णु VIṢṆU, and<BR>क्रान्त overcome. “अपराजिता ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुगुप्त|विष्णुगुप्तः
विष्णुगुप्त m. (-प्तः) The saint KAUṆḌILYA.<BR> E. विष्णु, गुप्त hidden, having<BR>been concealed by VIṢṆU when pursued by ŚIVA, whom he had<BR>incensed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुगृह|विष्णुगृहं
विष्णुगृह n. (-हं) The name of a city or country; also Stambapurī.<BR> E. विष्णु, गृह residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुदैवत्या
विष्णुदैवत्या f. (-त्या) The eleventh and twelfth lunar day of each fort-<BR>night.<BR> E. विष्णु VIṢṆU, and दैवत्य divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुपद|विष्णुपदं
विष्णुपद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. The sky, heaven, atmosphere.<BR>	 2. The sea of milk.<BR>	 3.<BR>A lotus.<BR>	 f. (-दी)<BR>	 1. The Ganges.<BR>	 2. One of the twelve Sankrāntis<BR>or periods, at which the sun enters a sign of the zodiac, especially<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">Page678-a+ 60</a>]<BR>the first sign after the equinox.<BR> E. विष्णु, and पद abode, or foot;<BR>where VIṢṆU resides or rests, or proceeding from his foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=677-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुप्रीति|विष्णुप्रीतिः
विष्णुप्रीति f. (-तिः) Land granted rent-free to a BRĀHMANA for the main-<BR>tenance of VIṢṆU'S worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुरथ|विष्णुरथः
विष्णुरथ m. (-थः) Garuḍa, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. विष्णु,<BR>and रथ car or conveyance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुलिङ्गी
विष्णुलिङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A quail.<BR> E. विष्णु VIṢṆU, and लिङ्ग a mark, ङीप् diminutive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुवल्लभ
विष्णुवल्लभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Beloved by VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. A plant,<BR>(Echites caryophyllata.)<BR>	 2. A small fragrant shrub, (Ocymum<BR>sanctum.)<BR>	 3. LAKṢMĪ.<BR> E. विष्णु VIṢṆU, वल्लभ the beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुवाहन|विष्णुवाहनं|विष्णुवाहनः
विष्णुवाहन m. (-नः) Garuḍa the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्पन्द|विष्पंद|विष्पंदः|विष्पन्दः
विष्पन्द m. (-न्दः) Throbbing, beating.<BR> E. वि before स्पन्दि to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्फार|विष्फारः
विष्फार m. (-रः) The twang of a bow.<BR> E. वि before स्फर् or स्फुर् to expand,<BR>aff. घञ्; in the latter, आ is substituted for the vowel, and स is<BR>changed to ष; also विस्फार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्य|विष्यः
विष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं) Deserving death by poison.<BR> E. विष venom, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्यन्द|विष्यंदः|विष्यन्दः
विष्यन्द m. (-न्दः) Flowing, issuing, trickling.<BR> E. वि before ष्यदि to go,<BR>शानच् aff.; also read विस्यन्द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्यन्दमान
विष्यन्दमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Flowing, trickling.<BR> E. वि before ष्यदि to go,<BR>शानच् aff.; also read विस्यन्दमान ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्व|विष्वः
विष्व mfn. (-ष्वः-ष्वा-ष्वं) Injurious, mischievous.<BR> E. विष् to pervade, Unādi aff. व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वक्
विष्वक् Ind. Every way, all around: see विष्वच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वक्सेन|विष्वक्सेनः
विष्वक्सेन m. (-नः) VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A plant, commonly Priyangu. E.<BR>विष्वक् every where, सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वक्सेनप्रिया
विष्वक्सेनप्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. A sort of yam, (Dioscorea.)<BR>	 2. LAKṢMĪ. E.<BR>विष्वक्सेन VIṢṆU, and प्रिया beloved by, sacred to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वग्गत
विष्वग्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone all about, spread, extended.<BR> E. विष्वक्, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वग्गति
विष्वग्गति f. (-तिः) Going all about.<BR> E. विष्वक्, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वच्
विष्वच् or विष्वञ्च् mfn. (-ष्वङ्-षूची-ष्वक्)<BR>	 1. Going every where, all-<BR>pervading.<BR>	 2. Separating into parts, different.<BR>	 n. (-ष्वक्) The<BR>equinox.<BR> E. विषु variously, (in various directions,) or equally, अञ्च्<BR>to go, क्विन् aff.; it is also written, but less accurately विश्वच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वञ्च्|विष्वंच्
विष्वच् or विष्वञ्च् mfn. (-ष्वङ्-षूची-ष्वक्)<BR>	 1. Going every where, all-<BR>pervading.<BR>	 2. Separating into parts, different.<BR>	 n. (-ष्वक्) The<BR>equinox.<BR> E. विषु variously, (in various directions,) or equally, अञ्च्<BR>to go, क्विन् aff.; it is also written, but less accurately विश्वच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वणन|विष्वणनं
विष्वणन n. (-नं) Food, eating.<BR> E. वि before स्वन् to sound, (with the lips,<BR>to smack the lips,) and ल्युट् aff. “षत्वणत्वे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वद्र्यच्
विष्वद्र्यच् or द्र्यञ्च् mfn. (-द्र्यङ्-द्रीची-द्र्यक्) Going every where.<BR> E. विष्वच्<BR>every where, with अद्री augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वद्र्यञ्च्|विष्वद्र्यंच्
मूलद्रव्य n. (-व्यं) Capital, principal, stock.<BR> E. मूल capital, द्रव्य substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=574-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्वाण|विष्वाणः
विष्वाण m. (-णः) Eating, food.<BR> E. वि, स्वन् to sound, aff. घञ् । “षत्वणत्वे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंज्ञ
विसंज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Lifeless, bereft of sense.<BR> E. वि priv., संज्ञा sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंयुक्त
विसंयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Separated.<BR>	 2. Omitting.<BR> E. वि, संयुक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंयोग|विसंयोगः
विसंयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Separation.<BR>	 2. Omission.<BR> E. वि priv., संयोग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंवाद|विसंवादः
विसंवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Disappointing, deceiving, falsifying one's word,<BR>deceiving by a false affirmation or not keeping a promise.<BR>	 2. Con-<BR>tradiction, disagreement.<BR> E. वि implying reverse, संवाद agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंवादिन्
विसंवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Cunning, crafty, fraudulent.<BR>	 2. Dis-<BR>puting.<BR> E. विसंवाद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसंष्ठुल
विसंष्ठुल f. (-ला) Unsteady, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्
विस् r. 4th cl. (विस्यति)<BR>	 1. To throw, to send.<BR>	 2. To put forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस|विसं
विस n. (-सं) The film or fibres of the stalk of the water-lily.<BR> E. विस् to<BR>send, to put forth, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसकण्ठिका
विसकण्ठिका f. (-का) A small crane.<BR> E. विस the fibres of the lotus-stalk,<BR>aff. अच्, कण्ठ the throat, कन् aff., fem. form, implying comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसङ्कट|विसंकट|विसंकटः|विसङ्कटः
विसङ्कट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. The Ingudi tree.<BR> E. वि and सम before कट्<BR>to encompass, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसङ्गत|विसंगत
विसङ्गत f. (-ता) Inconsistent, not in harmony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसच्छेद|विसछेद
विसच्छेद m. (-दः) A part of the fibres of the lotus.<BR> E. विस, छेद section.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसज|विसजं
विसज n. (-जं) A lotus.<BR> E. विस the fibres of the stalk, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसनाभि|विसनाभिः
विसनाभि m. (-भिः) A quantity of lotuses.<BR> E. विस, नाभि navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसनासिका
विसनासिका f. (-का) A sort of crane.<BR> E. विस, नासिका the nose or beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसपुष्प
विसपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) A lotus.<BR> E. विस the stalk, and पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसप्रसून|विसप्रसूनं
विसप्रसून n. (-नं) A lotus, (Nelumbium speciosum.)<BR> E. विस, प्रसून a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर|विसरः
विसर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A multitude, an assemblage, a flock, a herd, a crowd,<BR>2. Spreading, going forth or abroad.<BR> E. वि before सृ to go, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्ग|विसर्गः
विसर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. Abandoning, relinquishment, getting rid of or free<BR>from any thing.<BR>	 2. Departure, going away.<BR>	 3. Separation.<BR>	 4. Gift,<BR>donation.<BR>	 5. Final emancipation or beatitude, exemption from<BR>worldly existence.<BR>	 6. Evacuation of excrement, voiding by stool,<BR>&c.<BR>	 7. The soft aspirate or Visarga, marked by two perpendicular<BR>dots, (ः), and as the substitute for the letters स or र, the termination<BR>of various inflections both of nouns and verbs.<BR>	 8. A division of the<BR>sun's course, the southern course.<BR>	 9. Light, splendour.<BR> E. वि before<BR>सृज् to let go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्जन|विसर्जनं|विसर्ज्जनं
विसर्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. Quitting, relinquishing.<BR>	 3. Send-<BR>ing, dispatching.<BR>	 4. Dismissing, sending away.<BR>	 5. Throwing the<BR>image, &c. into holy water, as the concluding rite of the festival<BR>of a deity.<BR> E. वि before सृज् to let go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्ज्जनीय|विसर्जनीय|विसर्जनीयः
विसर्ज्जनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be left, abandoned, given away, &c. (pro-<BR>per or fit to.)<BR> E. वि, सृज् to leave, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्ज्जित|विसर्जित
विसर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Abandoned, left.<BR>	 2. Given, given away.<BR>	 3.<BR>Dismissed.<BR> E. वि before सृज् to let go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वि|विः
वि(वी)सर्प m. (-र्पः)<BR>	 1. Spreading.<BR>	 2. Going.<BR>	 3. Going variously.<BR>	 4. Fly-<BR>ing, gliding.<BR>	 5. Unwished consequence of any act.<BR>	 6. Erysipelatous<BR>inflammation.<BR> E. वि before सृप् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पघ्न
विसर्पघ्न n. (-घ्नं) Bee's wax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पण|विसर्पणं
विसर्पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Spreading, extending.<BR>	 2. Going gently.<BR>	 3. Flying. E.<BR>वि before सृप् to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पत्
विसर्पत् mfn. (-र्पन्-र्पन्ती-र्पत्)<BR>	 1. Going, going along.<BR>	 2. Flying gently. E.<BR>वि before सृप् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसर्पिन्
विसर्पिन् mfn. (-र्पी-र्पिणी-र्पि) Spreading over or along, gliding, going<BR>gently.<BR> E. वि before, सृप् to go, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसल|विसलं
विसल n. (-लं) A shoot, a sprout.<BR> E. वि variously, सल् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसार|विसारः
विसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A fish.<BR>	 2. Going smoothly, creeping, gliding.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>Wood, timber.<BR>	 f. (-री) The region of the winds.<BR> E. वि before सृ to<BR>go, and घञ् or ण aff.; or वि priv., and सार pith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसारित|विसारितः
विसारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Effected, performed.<BR>	 2. Set on foot, occa-<BR>sioned.<BR> E. वि before सृ to go, causal form, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसारिन्
विसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Flowing, gliding, creeping.<BR>	 2. Spreading,<BR>diffusing.<BR>	 m. (-री) A fish.<BR> E. विसार going smoothly, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसिनी
विसिनी f. (-नी) An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR> E. विस the fibres of<BR>the lotus, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूचिका
विसूचिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Spasmodic cholera.<BR>	 2. Symptom of a disease.<BR> E. वि,<BR>सूच् to apprise, ण्वुल् aff.; or विशिष्टा सूचीव इवार्थे कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूरण|विसूरणं
विसूरण nf. (-णं-णा) Sorrow, distress.<BR> E. वि, सूर् to hurt, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसूरित|विसूरितं
विसूरित n. (-तं) Repentance.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A fever.<BR> E. वि before सूर् to hurt, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृजत्
विसृजत् mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्)<BR>	 1. Abandoning, leaving.<BR>	 2. Giving, giving<BR>away.<BR> E. वि before सृज् to let go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृज्य
विसृज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) To be left or abandoned. Ind. Having dis-<BR>missed, left, got rid of, &c.<BR> E. वि before सृज् to let go, यत् or ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृत|विसृतं
विसृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Spread, extended, expanded.<BR>	 2. Uttered. E.<BR>वि before सृ to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृत्वर|विसृत्वरः
विसृत्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Going smoothly, gliding, creeping, flowing. E.<BR>वि before सृ to go, क्वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृमर|विसृमरः
विसृमर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Creeping, flowing, gliding.<BR> E. वि before सृ to go, क्मरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृष्ट|विसृष्टः
विसृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Expelled, cast off or out.<BR>	 2. Abandoned,<BR>relinquished, god rid of.<BR>	 3. Given away.<BR>	 4. Dismissed.<BR>	 5. Shed.<BR>	 6.<BR>Emitted, emanated.<BR> E. वि before सृज् to let go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विसृष्टि|विसृष्टिः
विसृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Leaving, quitting.<BR>	 2. Giving.<BR>	 3. Dismissing.<BR> E. वि<BR>away, सृज् to leave, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्कन्तृ
विस्कन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Going, going away, dispersing.<BR> E. वि before<BR>स्कदि to go, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्कन्द
विस्कन्द m. (-न्दः) Going, dispersing.<BR> E. वि before स्कदि to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्त|विस्तः
विस्त mn. (-स्तः-स्तं) A weight of gold, a Karṣa of sixteen Māshas,<BR>about half an ounce troy.<BR> E. विस् to convey, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तर|विस्तरः
विस्तर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Spreading, expansion.<BR>	 2. Prolixity, minute detail.<BR>	 3.<BR>Affection or affectionate solicitation.<BR>	 4. Number, assemblage.<BR>	 5.<BR>Abundance, quantity.<BR>	 6. A seat, a stool.<BR>	 7. A bed, a layer.<BR> E. वि<BR>before स्तृ to spread over or cover, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तरशस्
विस्तरशस् Ind. Fully, at length.<BR> E. विस्तर, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तार|विस्तारः
विस्तार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Spreading, extension, diffusion.<BR>	 2. Vastness, expanse.<BR>3. Breadth, amplitude.<BR>	 4. Amplification.<BR>	 5. Diameter of a circle.<BR>6. The branch of a tree with its new shoots.<BR>	 7. A shrub.<BR> E. वि<BR>before स्तृ to cover, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तीर्ण|विस्तीर्णः
विस्तीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Large, roomy, great.<BR>	 2. Spread, expanded.<BR>	 3.<BR>Broad.<BR> E. वि before स्तृ to cover or spread, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तीर्णता
विस्तीर्णता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Diffusion, extension.<BR>	 2. Vastness.<BR> E. विस्तीर्ण, तल्<BR>aff.; also with त्व, विस्तीर्णत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तीर्णपर्ण|विस्तीर्णपर्णं
विस्तीर्णपर्ण n. (-र्णं) A sort of esculent root, (Arum Indicum.)<BR> E. विस्तीर्ण large, पर्ण leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तृत|विस्तृतः
विस्तृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Spread, diffused, extended.<BR>	 2. Broad, ex-<BR>panded.<BR>	 3. Ample.<BR>	 4. Diffused.<BR> E. वि before स्तृ to spread, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्तृति|विस्तृतिः
विस्तृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Spreading, expansion.<BR>	 2. The diameter of a circle.<BR>	 3.<BR>Breadth, width.<BR> E. वि, स्तृ to spread, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पर्द्धमान
विस्पर्द्धमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Emulating, envying.<BR> E. वि, स्पर्द्ध् to envy, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्पष्ट|विस्पष्टः
विस्पष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Apparent, manifest, open, clear.<BR>	 2. Plain,<BR>intelligible.<BR> E. वि before स्पष्ट apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फार|विस्फारः
विस्फार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The twang of a bow, string.<BR>	 2. Trembling, agita-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Vibrating.<BR> E. वि before स्फर् to shake, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फारित|विस्फारितः
विस्फारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken, trembling, tremulous.<BR>	 2. Evident,<BR>apparent.<BR>	 3. Twanged or drawn as a bow-string.<BR>	 4. Made to<BR>vibrate.<BR>	 5. Displayed.<BR> E. वि before स्फर् to tremble, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फार्य्यमाण|विस्फार्यमाण
विस्फार्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Being made open or manifest.<BR>	 2. Being<BR>drawn or twanged as a bow-string.<BR> E. वि before स्फर् to tremble,<BR>pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुरत्
विस्फुरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Swelling, enlarging.<BR> E. वि before स्फुर् to swell, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुरित|विस्फुरितः
विस्फुरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken, tremulous.<BR>	 2. Swollen, enlarged. E.<BR>वि before स्फुर् to tremble, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुलत्
विस्फुलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्)<BR>	 1. Going briskly or merrily.<BR>	 2. Shaking,<BR>trembling.<BR>	 3. Appearing.<BR> E. वि before, स्फुल् to shake, &c., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फुलिङ्ग|विस्फुलिंग|विस्फुलिंगः|विस्फुलिङ्गः
विस्फुलिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A sort of poison.<BR>	 2. A spark of fire.<BR> E. वि, स्फु<BR>imitative sound, लिङ्ग to go, aff. अच्; or वि + स्फुर्-डु तादृशं लिङ्गमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फूर्जथु|विस्फूर्जथुः
विस्फूर्जथु m. (-थुः)<BR>	 1. A clap of thunder.<BR>	 2. Roaring, rumbling.<BR> E. वि,<BR>स्फूर्ज्ज् to thunder, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्फोट|विस्फोटः
विस्फोट mf. (-टः-टा)<BR>	 1. Boil, pustule.<BR>	 2. Small-pox.<BR> E. वि before, स्फुट् to<BR>hurt or break, aff. घञ् or णिच्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मय|विस्मयः
विस्मय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Wonder, surprise, astonishment, (wonder or admira-<BR>tion considered as the feeling giving rise to the Adbhuta Senti-<BR>ment.)<BR>	 2. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 3. Doubt, uncertainty.<BR> E. वि before,<BR>स्मि to smile, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयाकुल
विस्मयाकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Bewildered, astounded.<BR> E. विस्मय and आकुल perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयान्वित|विस्मयान्वितः
विस्मयान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Astonished.<BR> E. विस्मय, अन्वित affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मयिन्
विस्मयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Astonished, surprised.<BR> E. विस्मय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मरण|विस्मरणं
विस्मरण n. (-णं) Forgetting, oblivion.<BR> E. वि, स्मृ to remember, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मरणीय
विस्मरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be forgotten.<BR> E. वि priv., स्मृ to remember,<BR>अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मर्य्य|विस्मर्य
विस्मर्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be forgotten.<BR> E. वि before स्मृ to remember, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मापन|विस्मापनः
विस्मापन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Deceit, illusion.<BR>	 2. A magical or enchanted city,<BR>one that appears and disappears unexpectedly, or in unexpected<BR>situations, a city of the Gandharbas.<BR>	 3. KĀMA or CUPID.<BR>	 4. As-<BR>tonishing, surprising, causing wonder or surprise.<BR> E. वि, स्मि to<BR>smile, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मित|विस्मितः
विस्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Astonished, surprised.<BR>	 2. Proud.<BR> E. वि, स्मि to smile, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मृत|विस्मृतः
विस्मृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Forgotten.<BR> E. वि privative, स्मृत remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मृति|विस्मृतिः
विस्मृति f. (-तिः) Forgetting, forgetfulness.<BR> E. वि priv., स्मृति recollect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्मेर
विस्मेर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Astonished, surprised.<BR> E. वि, स्मि to smile, र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्यन्द
विस्यन्द m. (-न्दः) Flowing, trickling.<BR> E. वि before, ष्यदि to flow, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्र|विस्रं
विस्र n. (-स्रं) A smell like that of raw meat.<BR> E. विस् to send, aff. रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रंस|विस्रंसः
विस्रंस mf. (-सः-सा)<BR>	 1. Relaxation, laxness.<BR>	 2. Debility, decay.<BR> E. वि, स्रंस्<BR>to fall, अङ् and टाप् affs., or घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रंसन
विस्रंसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Loosening, unfastening, untying.<BR>	 2. Falling.<BR>	 3.<BR>Flowing, dropping.<BR>	 4. A laxative, an aperient.<BR> E. वि separate, स्रस्<BR>to fall, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रगन्धि|विस्रगंधि|विस्रगन्धिः
विस्रगन्धि m. (-न्धिः) Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. विस्र the smell of raw meat, and गन्धि smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रता
विस्रता f. (-ता) Rawness of smell.<BR> E. तल् added to विस्र as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रब्ध|विस्रब्धः
विस्रब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Trusted, confided in.<BR>	 2. Placid, tamed,<BR>humble.<BR>	 3. Steady, diligent.<BR> E. वि before स्रंभ् to trust, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रम्भ|विस्रंभ|विस्रम्भः
विस्रम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Trust, confidence.<BR>	 2. Affection, regard, affectionate<BR>solicitation.<BR>	 3. Acquaintance.<BR>	 4. Killing.<BR> E. वि, स्रंभ् to trust, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रम्भिन्
विस्रम्भिन् mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि) Trusting.<BR> E. वि, स्रंभ् to trust, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रसा
विस्रसा f. (-सा) Decrepitude, the infirmity of old age.<BR> E. वि before स्रंस्<BR>to fall, affs. अङ् and टाप् and the radical nasal dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रस्त
विस्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Loosened, detached, fallen.<BR> E. वि, स्रंस् to fall, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्राव|विस्रावः
विस्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Flowing, dropping.<BR>	 2. The water of boiled-rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रावण|विस्रावणं
विस्रावण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Causing to flow.<BR>	 2. Bleeding.<BR>	 3. Distilling.<BR>	 4. A<BR>spirit distilled from molasses.<BR> E. वि, स्रु to drop, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रावित
विस्रावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bled.<BR>	 2. Caused to flow.<BR> E. वि, स्रु to flow,<BR>causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्राव्य
विस्राव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be bled, requiring bleeding.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>made to flow.<BR> E. वि, स्रु to ooze, causal v., यत् aff; also विस्रावितव्य<BR>and विस्रावणीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्रुत|विस्रुतः
विस्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spread, stretched.<BR>	 2. Dropped, flowing.<BR> E. वि<BR>apart, स्रु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्वर|विस्वरः
विस्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Discordant, unharmonious.<BR> E. वि deprec., स्वर sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विस्वाद
विस्वाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Insipid, flavourless.<BR> E. वि priv., स्वाद flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहग|विहगः
विहग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. An arrow.<BR>	 4. The sun.<BR>	 5. The<BR>moon.<BR>	 6. A planet.<BR> E. विह for विहायस् in the sky, and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहङ्ग|विहंग|विहंगः|विहङ्गः
विहङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Going swiftly, flying.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. A<BR>cloud.<BR>	 3. An arrow.<BR>	 4. The moon.<BR>	 5. The sun.<BR> E. विह for विहायस् in<BR>the air, and ग who goes: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहङ्गम|विहंगम|विहंगमः|विहङ्गमः
विहङ्गम m. (-मः) A bird.<BR>	 f. (-मा) A pole or yoke for carrying burdens.<BR>E. विह for विहायस् in the air, गम् to go, aff. खच्, whence the nasal<BR>is inserted; also with the final rejected, विहङ्ग &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहङ्गराज|विहंगराज|विहंगराजः|विहङ्गराजः
विहङ्गराज m. (-जः) GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहङ्गिका|विहंगिका
विहङ्गिका f. (-का) A sort of pole or yoke for carrying burdens. E.<BR>विहङ्ग a bird, and कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहत|विहतः
विहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Opposed, impeded, resisted.<BR>	 2. Hurt, killed.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-तः) A Bauddha or Jaina temple.<BR> E. वि, हन् to hurt or kill, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहति|विहतिः
विहति f. (-तिः) Striking, killing.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) A friend or companion.<BR> E. वि<BR>हन् to strike, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहनन|विहननं
विहनन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Opposition, obstruction, impediment.<BR>	 2. Injury,<BR>hurting.<BR>	 3. Killing.<BR>	 4. A bow for cleaning cotton.<BR> E. वि before हन्<BR>to kill or hurt, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर|विहरः
विहर m. (-रः) Separation, disunion, absence.<BR> E. वि before हृ to convey, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहरण|विहरणं
विहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking, taking off or away.<BR>	 2. Going about for<BR>pleasure or exercise.<BR> E. वि, हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहरणीय
विहरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be taken away.<BR>	 2. To be rambled or sport-<BR>ed.<BR> E. वि before हृ to take, अनीयर aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर्त्तृ|विहर्तृ
विहर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>	 1. A robber.<BR>	 2. A roamer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसन|विहसनं
विहसन n. (-नं) Laughing gently, smiling.<BR> E. वि, हस् to laugh, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसित|विहसितं
विहसित n. (-तं) A gentle laugh, a smile.<BR> E. वि, हस् to laugh, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहस्त|विहस्तः
विहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Confounded, perplexed, bewildered.<BR>	 2. Wise,<BR>learned.<BR> E. वि without, हस्त a hand; helpless, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहा
विहा Ind. Aptote noun. Heaven, paradise.<BR> E. वि, हा to abandon, Unādi aff. आ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहापित|विहापितं
विहापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Given.<BR>	 2. Extorted.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Gift, donation.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">Page680-a+ 60</a>]<BR>E. वि before हा to abandon, causal form, aff. क्त; giving being<BR>considered as the abandonment of the thing given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=679-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहाय|विहायः
विहाय Ind. Having left or abandoned.<BR> E. वि before हा to quit, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायत
विहायत n. (-तं) Gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायस्
विहायस् mn. (-याः-यः) The sky or atmosphere.<BR>	 m. (-याः) A bird.<BR> E. वि<BR>before हय् to go, causal form, aff. असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायस|विहायसं|विहायसः
विहायस mn. (-सः-सं) Heaven, sky, atmosphere.<BR>	 m. (-सः) A bird.<BR> E. अच् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायसा
विहायसा Ind. Heaven, sky, atmosphere. E. The third case of विहायस्<BR>used as an aptote noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहार|विहारः
विहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Walking for pleasure or amusement.<BR>	 2. Wandering,<BR>roaming, going about.<BR>	 3. A Bauddha or Jaina convent.<BR>	 4. A<BR>temple.<BR>	 5. Taking away, removing.<BR>	 6. Play, sport, pastime.<BR>	 7. A<BR>pleasure-ground.<BR>	 8. A palace.<BR>	 9. The shoulder.<BR>	 10. A sort of<BR>bird.<BR> E. वि before हृ to take, aff. घञ्; also वीहार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारिन्
विहारिन् mfn. (-री-रीणी-रि) Taking pleasure or relaxation.<BR> E. विहार<BR>sport, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहास|विहासः
विहास m. (-सः) A gentle laugh or smile.<BR> E. वि and हास laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहित|विहितः
विहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Placed, deposited.<BR>	 2. Improper, unsuitable,<BR>unfit.<BR>	 3. Done, acted, made.<BR>	 4. Appointed, fixed.<BR>	 5. Constructed,<BR>framed.<BR>	 6. Distributed, apportioned.<BR>	 7. Furnished with.<BR>	 8.<BR>Proper to be done.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A command.<BR> E. वि, धा to have, aff.<BR>क्त; or वि priv., हित applicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहिवत्
विहिवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Doing, performing, making.<BR> E. वि, धा to have, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहितागस्
विहितागस् mfn. (-गाः-गाः-गः) Faulty, offending, wicked.<BR> E. विहित done,<BR>आगस् sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहिताञ्जलि
विहिताञ्जलि mfn. (-लिः-लिः-लि) Making a respectful obeisance.<BR> E. विहित, अञ्जलि salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहिति|विहितिः
विहिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Action, performance.<BR>	 2. Arrangement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहित्रिम
विहित्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Done according to rule.<BR> E. वि, धा to have,<BR>क्ति aff., मप् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहीन|विहीनः
विहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Abandoned, left, deserted.<BR>	 2. Deprived of.<BR>	 3.<BR>Low, inferior.<BR> E. वि before हा to abandon, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृत|विहृतं
विहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sported, played.<BR>	 2. Expanded.<BR>	 n. (-तं) One of<BR>the ten feminine acts or properties indicating love, hesitation,<BR>reluctance, (in a female,) to avow her feelings to her lover.<BR> E. वि<BR>before हृ to take, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृति|विहृतिः
विहृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Opening, expansion.<BR>	 2. Sport, pastime.<BR>	 3. Taking<BR>away.<BR> E. वि apart, हृ to convey, aff. क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहत्य
विहत्य Ind.<BR>	 1. Having sported.<BR>	 2. Having or being spread.<BR> E. वि, हृ to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठ|विहेठः
विहेठ m. (-ठः) Hurting, injury.<BR> E. वि before हेठ् to annoy, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठक|विहेठकः
विहेठक m. (-कः) An injurer, a reviler, one who inflicts pain or injury<BR>on another.<BR> E. वि, हेठ् to annoy, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठन|विहेठनं
विहेठन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Injury, hurting, wounding, killing.<BR>	 2. Rubbing,<BR>grinding.<BR>	 3. Afflicting distressing.<BR>	 4. Pain, sorrow, affliction. E.<BR>वि before हेठ् to annoy or hurt, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वल|विह्वलः
विह्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Agitated, alarmed, overcome with fear or<BR>agitation, beside one's self, unable to restrain one's self.<BR>	 2. Dis-<BR>tressed, afflicted.<BR>	 3. Fused, liquid.<BR>	 4. Desponding.<BR> E. वि before ह्वल्<BR>to shake, aff., अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वलता
विह्वलता f. (-ता) Agitation, anxiety.<BR> E. विह्वल and तल् aff.; also with त्व, विह्वलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
वी r. 2nd cl. (वेति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To pervade.<BR>	 3. To conceive,<BR>to be impregnated.<BR>	 4. To desire.<BR>	 5. To throw or send.<BR>	 6. To eat.<BR>7. To be beautiful. With सम् prefixed, To invest, to inclose, to<BR>cover or wrap round or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
वी m. (-वीः)<BR>	 1. Going, moving.<BR>	 2. Covering.<BR> E. वी to go, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक|वीकः
वीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR>	 3. The mind.<BR> E. अज् to go, वि<BR>substituted for the root, कन् Unādi aff., the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
वी(वि)काश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Solitude, privacy.<BR>	 2. Display, manifestation. E.<BR>वि, काश् to shine, aff. अच्; the vowel of the prefix made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष|वीक्षं|वीक्षः
वीक्ष mf. (-क्षः-क्षा) Sight, seeing.<BR>	 n. (-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Surprise, astonishment.<BR>	 2.<BR>A visible object.<BR> E. वि before ईक्ष् to see, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षण|वीक्षणं
वीक्षण nf. (-णं-णा) Sight, seeing.<BR> E. वि before ईक्ष् to see, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षणीय
वीक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Visible, perceptible.<BR> E. वि, ईक्ष् to see, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षमाण
वीक्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-ण) Seeing, looking at.<BR> E. वि, ईक्ष् to see, शानच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षापन्न|वीक्षापन्नः
वीक्षापन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Astonished, surprised.<BR> E. वीक्ष sight, आपन्न disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षित|वीक्षितं|वीक्षितः
वीक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Seen, beheld.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A look, a glance.<BR> E. वि,<BR>ईक्ष् to see, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष्य|वीक्ष्यं|वीक्ष्यः
वीक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Visible, perceptible.<BR>	 2. Astonishing, won-<BR>derful. Ind. Having seen.<BR>	 n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Wonder, surprise.<BR>	 2. A visi-<BR>ble object.<BR>	 m. (-क्ष्यः)<BR>	 1. A dancer, an actor.<BR>	 2. A horse.<BR> E. वि<BR>before ईक्ष् to see, aff. यत् or ल्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीङ्खा|वींखा
वीङ्खा f. (-ङ्खा)<BR>	 1. Going, moving, locomotion, progress, proceeding.<BR>	 2.<BR>Dancing.<BR>	 3. A particular mode of moving.<BR>	 4. Cowach, (Carpopo-<BR>gon pruriens.)<BR>	 5. One of a horse's paces.<BR> E. वि, इखि to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचयन|विचयनं
विचयन n. (-नं) Research, enquiry.<BR> E. वि before चि to collect, ल्युट् aff.,<BR>and the vowel of the prefix made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचि|वीचिः
वीचि mf. (-चिः-चिः or ची)<BR>	 1. A wave.<BR>	 2. A small or rippling wave.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pleasure, delight, happiness.<BR>	 4. Leisure, interval, rest.<BR>	 5. A ray<BR>of light.<BR>	 6. Small, little.<BR>	 7. Thoughtlessness.<BR> E. वेञ् to weave,<BR>Unādi aff. ईचि, and the radical vowel rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचिमालिन्
वीचिमालिन् m. (-ली) The ocean.<BR> E. वीचि a wave, माला a necklace, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्
वीज् r. 10th cl. (वीजयति-ते) To fan, to cool by fanning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज|वीजं
वीज n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Seed, (of plants, &c.)<BR>	 2. Cause, origin in general.<BR>	 3.<BR>Semen virile.<BR>	 4. Receptacle, place of deposit or preparation.<BR>	 5.<BR>Truth, divine truth, as the seed or cause of being.<BR>	 6. Marrow.<BR>	 7.<BR>Algebra, analysis.<BR>	 8. The mystical letter or syllable which forms<BR>the essential part of the Mantra of any deity.<BR>	 9. The origin of the<BR>business of a drama.<BR> E. वि variously, जन् be born or produced,<BR>(from it,) aff. ड, and the vowel made long; or व्येञ् to cover, aff.<BR>क्विप्, वी covering, जन् to be born, aff. ड; or वि implying possession,<BR>ई LAKṢMĪ or prosperity, जन् to be produced, (by it,) with the<BR>same affix: there are other derivations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजक|वीजकः
वीजक m. (-कः) The common citron, (Citrus medica.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) Seed. E.<BR>वीज seed, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजकोश|वीजकोशः
वीजकोश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The seed-vessel of the lotus.<BR>	 2. Any seed-vessel.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-शी) A Pod, a legume.<BR> E. विज seed, and कोश or कोष receptacle;<BR>whence also वीजकोष m. (-षः) वीजकोषी f. (-षी) &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजगणित
वीजगणित n. (-तं) Algebra.<BR> E. वीज, and गणित calculation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजगुप्ति|वीजगुप्तिः
वीजगुप्ति f. (-प्तिः) A legume, a pod.<BR> E. वीज seed, गुप्ति concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजतस्
वीजतस् Ind. From or according to the seed.<BR> E. वीज, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजन|वीजनं|वीजनः
वीजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A fan.<BR>	 2. Fanning.<BR>	 3. Thing, substance.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>sort of pheasant.<BR>	 2. The ruddy goose.<BR> E. वीज, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजपुष्प|वीजपुष्पं
वीजपुष्प n. (-ष्पं)<BR>	 1. Common citron.<BR>	 2. A thorny plant, (Vangueria<BR>spinosa.)<BR> E. वीज a seed, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजपुष्पिका
वीजपुष्पिका f. (-का) A sort of grain, (Andropogon or Holcus sorghum.)<BR>E. वीज a seed, पुष्प a flower, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजपूर|वीजपूरः
वीजपूर m. (-रः) Common citron or a variety, (Citrus medica.)<BR> E. वीज a<BR>seed, and पूर what is full of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजपूर्ण|वीजपूर्णः
वीजपूर्ण m. (-र्णः) Common citron, or according to some authorities, a<BR>large kind of lime.<BR> E. वीज seed, and पूर्ण filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजप्रद
वीजप्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Sowing seed, &c.<BR>	 m. (-दः) Generating, or a<BR>generator.<BR> E. वीज, and प्रद what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजप्ररोह
वीजप्ररोह m. (-हः) Growing from seed.<BR> E. वीज, and प्ररोह growing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजमातृका
वीजमातृका f. (-का) The pericarp or seed-vessel of the lotus.<BR> E. वीज seed,<BR>and मातृका parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजरुह|वीजरुहः
वीजरुह mfn. (-हः-हा-र्हं) Growing from seed.<BR>	 m. (-हः) Grain, corn. E.<BR>वीज seed, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजवत्|वीजवन्त्
वीजवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Who or what has seed.<BR> E. वीज, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजवर
वीजवर m. (-रः) Kidney-bean, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR> E. वीज seed, and वर<BR>what screens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=680-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजसू
वीजसू f. (-सूः) The earth.<BR> E. वीज seed, and सू parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजा
वीजा Ind. By or with seed, sowing with seed.<BR> E. वीज, and डाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजाकृत|वीजाकृतं
वीजाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ploughed or harrowed after sowing, (a field,<BR>&c.)<BR> E. वीज a seed, and कृत made, with डाच् added to the first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजित
वीजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sown with, having for seed.<BR>	 2. Fanned, cooled<BR>by the wind proceeding from a fan.<BR> E. वीज, इतच् aff.; or वीज् to<BR>fan, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजिन्
वीजिन् mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि) Having seed, origin, &c.<BR>	 m. (-जी) A father,<BR>a progenitor.<BR> E. वीज semen, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजोत्कृष्ट
वीजोत्कृष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Good seed.<BR> E. वीज, and उत्कृष्ट excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजोदक|वीजोदकं
वीजोदक n. (-कं) Hail.<BR> E. वीज origin or original, उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्य|वीज्यः
वीज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. Sprung from a respectable family.<BR>	 2. Sprung<BR>from seed.<BR> E. वीज seed or origin, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्यमान
वीज्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fanned.<BR> E. वीज् to fan, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीटा
वीटा f. (-टा) A small piece of wood struck with a stick in kind of<BR>game played by boys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीटिका
वीटिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The betel-plant, (Piper betel.)<BR>	 2. The preparation<BR>of the Areca nut with spices and chunam, and enveloped in the<BR>leaf of the Piper betel, Betel, Pāun.<BR>	 3. A tye, a fastening.<BR> E. वि,<BR>इट् to go, aff. क्वुन्, fem. form; also with इन् or ङीप् aff. वीटि or वीटी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणा
वीणा f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. The Vīṇā, or Indian lute, a fretted instrument of the<BR>guitar kind, usually having seven wires or strings, and a large<BR>gourd at each end of the finger board; the extent of the instru-<BR>ment is two octaves: it is supposed to be the invention of<BR>NĀRADA, the son of BRAHMĀ, and has many varieties, enumer-<BR>ated according to the number of strings, &c.<BR>	 2. Lightning.<BR> E. वी<BR>to go, &c., Unādi aff. न, form irr.; or अज्-नक् वीभावः पृषो०<BR>णत्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणादण्ड|वीणादंड|वीणादण्डः
वीणादण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The neck of a Vina.<BR> E. वीणा a lute, दण्ड a stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणानुबन्ध|वीणानुबन्धः
वीणानुबन्ध m. (-न्धः) The tie of a lute or lower part of the tail piece,<BR>where the wires are fixed.<BR> E. वीणा the lute, अनुबन्ध appendage, tie,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणावाद|वीणावादः
वीणावाद m. (-दः) A player on the Vīṇā, a lutanist.<BR> E. वीणा a lute, and<BR>वाद who causes to speak or sound; also with कन् added, वीणावादक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणास्य|वीणास्यः
वीणास्य m. (-स्यः) NĀRADA, the son of BRAHMĀ, and inventor of the<BR>Vīṇā or lute.<BR> E. वीणा, and आस्य the countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीत|वीतं|वीतः
वीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone, departed.<BR>	 2. Exempt or freed from.<BR>	 3.<BR>Loosed, let go, unbound.<BR>	 4. Tranquil, quiet, tame.<BR>	 5. Excepted.<BR>	 6.<BR>Approved, liked, accepted.<BR>	 7. Unfit for war.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A horse<BR>or elephant, untrained to or unfit for war.<BR>	 2. Goading an ele-<BR>phant.<BR> E. वी to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतंस|वीतंसः
वीतंस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A cage, a chain or net, &c. for confining birds or<BR>beasts.<BR>	 2. An enclosure for tranquillising or taming them, an<BR>aviary, a menagerie.<BR>	 3. A place for keeping game, a preserve.<BR> E. वि<BR>before तसि to adorn, aff. घञ्; the vowel of the prefix made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतकल्मष
वीतकल्मष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Free from sin or soil.<BR> E. वीत, and कल्मष sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतकाम
वीतकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Free from desire.<BR> E. वीत, काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतदम्भ|वीतदम्भः
वीतदम्भ mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं) Humble, lowly.<BR> E. वीत gone, दम्भ pride, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतन|वीतनः
वीतन m. DU. (-नी) The sides of cartilages of the larynx.<BR> E. वि + तन्-अच्-<BR>पृषो० दीर्घ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतभय|वीतभयः
वीतभय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fearless, undaunted.<BR> E. वीत and भय fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतराग|वीतरागः
वीतराग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Exempt from passions or affections.<BR>	 2.<BR>Bleached, colourless.<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Any sage with subdued passions.<BR>2. A Bauddha deified sage.<BR> E. वीत gone, and राग passions, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतविरुद्धबुद्धि
वीतविरुद्धबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Peaceable, without hostile intentions. E.<BR>वीत, विरुद्ध opposed, and बुद्धि fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतशङ्क
वीतशङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Fearless.<BR> E. वीत, and शङ्क fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतशोक|वीतशोकः
वीतशोक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Free from care or sorrow.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The Aśoka<BR>tree, (Jonesia Aśoka.)<BR> E. वीत gone, and शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतस्पृह
वीतस्पृह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Free from desire.<BR> E. वीत, and स्पृहा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीति|वीतिः
वीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Going, moving, motion.<BR>	 2. Eating.<BR>	 3. Engendering,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">Page681-b+ 60</a>]<BR>producing.<BR>	 4. Cleaning, cleansing.<BR>	 5. Light, lustre.<BR>	 6. Enjoyment.<BR>m. (-तिः) A horse.<BR> E. वी to go, क्तिन् or क्तिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतिहोत्र|वीतिहोत्रः
वीतिहोत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. AGNI.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. वीति a horse, होत्र clarified<BR>butter, the usual offering or oblation with fire; also वीतिहात्रक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतोत्तर
वीतोत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Unable or disinclined to reply, having no<BR>answer.<BR> E. वीत, and उत्तर answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथि|वीथिः
वीथि f. (-थिः or थी)<BR>	 1. A road.<BR>	 2. A row, a line.<BR>	 3. A terrace in front of<BR>a house.<BR>	 4. A stall, a shop.<BR>	 5. A sort of drama, in one act, and by<BR>one or by two performers, the dramatic narration of an amatory<BR>story or intrigue.<BR> E. विथ् to ask or beg, aff. इन्, and the vowel made<BR>long; also ङीष् optionally added, with कन् aff., fem. form, वीथिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथ्यङ्ग|वीथ्यङ्गः
वीथ्यङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Dialogue, &c., suited to, and constituting the dramatic<BR>entertainment called Vithi, though employed in other kinds, as<BR>quibble, equivoque, jest, abuse, and the like.<BR> E. वीथि, अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीध्र|वीध्रं|वीध्रः
वीध्र mfn. (-ध्रः-ध्रा-ध्रं) Clean, clear, pure.<BR>	 n. (-ध्रं)<BR>	 1. The sky.<BR>	 2. Wind.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fire.<BR> E. वि, इन्ध् to shine, Unādi aff. रक्, the first consonant<BR>rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीनाह|वीनाहः
वीनाह m. (-हः) The top or cover of a well.<BR> E. वि before नह् to bind, aff.<BR>घञ्; also विनाह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीपा
वीपा f. (-पा) Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीप्सा
वीप्सा f. (-प्सा)<BR>	 1. Several or successive order, the arrangement of things<BR>or properties each by each, or in succession. as वृक्षं वृक्षं सिञ्चति, he<BR>waters tree after tree.<BR>	 2. Pervasion.<BR> E. वि before अप् to go, or get,<BR>desiderative form, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीबुकोश|वीबुकोशः
वीबुकोश m. (-शः) A Chowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीभ्
वीभ्(ऋ)वीभृ r. 1st. cl. (वीभते) To boast; also read चीभृ q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्
वीर् r. 10th cl. (वीरयति-ते) To be powerful or valiant, to make heroic<BR>or irresistible effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर|वीरं|वीरः
वीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Excellent, eminent, (used chiefly in composition.)<BR>2. Heroic.<BR>	 3. Powerful, mighty.<BR>	 4. Strong, robust.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>hero, a warrior, a champion.<BR>	 2. Heroism, the heroic Rasa or feeling,<BR>as an object of poetical description especially; It is fourfold;<BR>viz:--दानवीर, धर्मवीर, दयावीर and युद्घवीर । 3. The last Jina or<BR>Jaina pontiff of the present æra.<BR>	 4. An actor, a mime.<BR>	 5. A<BR>flower, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>	 6. Fire.<BR>	 7. Sacrificial fire.<BR>	 8. An epithet<BR>of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 9. A son.<BR>	 10. A husband.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A matron, a wife<BR>and mother.<BR>	 2. A sort of perfume, commonly Murā.<BR>	 3. A<BR>medicinal root, commonly Kṣira-kākolī.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Flacourtia<BR>cataphracta.)<BR>	 5. A drug (Elabāluka.)<BR>	 6. Plantain tree.<BR>	 7. A sort<BR>of Asclepias, (A rosea.)<BR>	 8. Opposite-leaved fig tree.<BR>	 9. A sort of<BR>Convolvulus, (C. paniculatus, the white and dark kind.)<BR>	 10. A<BR>small tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>	 11. Spirituous liquor or a particular<BR>kind of it.<BR>	 12. The aloe.<BR>	 13. A plant, commonly Atis.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>reed, (Arundo tibialis.)<BR>	 2. The root of the ginger plant.<BR>	 3.<BR>Pepper.<BR>	 4. Rice-gruel.<BR>	 5. The root of the Costus speciosus.<BR>	 6. The<BR>root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR> E. अज् to go, and वी substi-<BR>tuted for the root, रक् Unādi aff.; or वीर् to be powerful, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरकीट|वीरकीटः
वीरकीट m. (-टः) A contemptible warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरजयन्तिका|वीरजयंतिका
वीरजयन्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A war-dance, a dance performed by soldiers<BR>after a victory or on going to battle.<BR>	 2. War, battle.<BR> E. वीर a hero,<BR>जि to conquer, झच् aff., fem. form, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरण|वीरणं
वीरण n. (-णं) A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1.<BR>A side glance.<BR>	 2. A deep place.<BR> E. वि a bird, ईर् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरतर|वीरतरं|वीरतरः
वीरतर n. (-र)<BR>	 1. A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. A great hero.<BR> E. वीर powerful, तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरतरु|वीरतरुः
वीरतरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A large tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A shrub,<BR>(Barleria longifolia, Rox.)<BR> E. वीर a hero, and तरु the tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरत्रा
वीरत्रा f. (-ता) Heroism.<BR> E. तल् added to वीर; also with त्व aff. वीरत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरधन्वन्
वीरधन्वन् m. (-न्वा) KĀMA or CUPID.<BR> E. वीर a hero, and धन्वन् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरन्धर|वीरंधर|वीरंधरः
वीरन्धर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2. Fighting with wild beasts.<BR>	 3. A lea-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">Page682-a+ 60</a>]<BR>ther cuirass or jacket.<BR>	 4. The name of a river.<BR> E. वीर a hero, धृ to<BR>hold, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=681-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरपत्नी
वीरपत्नी f. (-त्नी) The wife of a hero.<BR> E. वीर a hero, and पत्नी the wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरपाण
वीरपाण n. (-णं) The drink of warriors, taken during the battle for re-<BR>freshment, or before it, to elevate courage.<BR> E. वीर a hero, and पान<BR>drink; the न is optionally changed whence it also occurs वीरपान ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरभद्र|वीरभद्रः
वीरभद्र m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. A horse fit for the Aśwamedha sacrifice.<BR>	 2. A<BR>distinguished hero.<BR>	 3. A fragrant grass, “वीरण” 4. One of ŚIVA'S<BR>attendants.<BR>	 5. One of the RŪDRAS.<BR> E. वीर a hero, भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरभद्रक|वीरभद्रकं
वीरभद्रक n. (-कं) A fragrant grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरभार्य्या|वीरभार्या
वीरभार्य्या f. (-र्य्या) The wife of a hero.<BR> E. वीर a hero, and भाय्या a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरमातृ
वीरमातृ f. (-ता) The mother of a hero.<BR> E. वीर and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरमुद्रिका
वीरमुद्रिका f. (-का) An ornament or ring worn on the middle toe. E.<BR>वीर a hero, मुद्रा a seal, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीररेणु|वीररेणुः
वीररेणु m. (-णुः) A name of BHIMASENA.<BR> E. वीर a hero, and रेणु dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवत्|वीरवन्त्
वीरवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having a champion or hero.<BR>	 f. (-ती) A<BR>woman whose husband and sons are living.<BR> E. वीर, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवत्सा
वीरवत्सा f. (-त्सा) The mother of a hero.<BR> E. वीर, वत्स a child, (of whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरविप्लावक|वीरविप्लावकः
वीरविप्लावक m. (-कः) A Brāhmana who performs his oblations with<BR>money, procured from the lower or Śūdra tribe.<BR> E. वीर sacrificial<BR>fire, वि before प्लु to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवृक्ष|वीरवृक्षः
वीरवृक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The marking-nut plant, (Semicarpus anacardium.)<BR>2. A large tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna.)<BR>	 3. A sort of grain, (Andro-<BR>pogon or Holcus sorghum.)<BR> E. वीर strong, वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसू
वीरसू f. (-सूः)<BR>	 1. The mother of a hero.<BR>	 2. The mother of a male child.<BR>E. वीर a hero, and सू mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसेन|वीरसेनं|वीरसेनः
वीरसेन m. (-नः) The father of NALA Rājā.<BR> E. वीर a hero, सेना a host.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसेनज|वीरसेनजः
वीरसेनज m. (-जः) NALA, a prince and hero of several celebrated poems<BR>as the Naishadha, Nalodaya, &c.<BR> E. वीरसेन, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसैन्य
वीरसैन्य n. (-न्यं) Garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरस्कन्ध|वीरस्कंध|वीरस्कन्धः
वीरस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) A buffalo.<BR> E. वीर powerful स्कन्ध the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरहन्
वीरहन् m. (-हा) A Brāhman, who has suffered the sacred domestic<BR>fire to become extinct, either from carelessness, impiety, or<BR>absence.<BR> E. वीर sacrificial fire, and हन् who destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीराशंसन|वीराशंसनं
वीराशंसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The post of danger, the place in battle which is<BR>most perilous and exposed.<BR>	 2. Keeping watch.<BR>	 3. A forlorn hope.<BR>E. वीर a hero, आङ् before शसि to wish, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरासन|वीरासनं
वीरासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sleeping out in the open air, a bivouac.<BR>	 2. A field<BR>of battle.<BR>	 3. A kneeling posture.<BR> E. वीर and आसन sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरुध्
वीरुध् f. (-रुद् or रुत्)<BR>	 1. A creeper or spreading creeper.<BR>	 2. A branch<BR>and shoot.<BR>	 3. A plant which grows after cutting.<BR>	 4. A bower. E.<BR>वि before रुध् to impede, aff. क्विप्, and the vowel of the prefix<BR>made long; also टाप् being added, वीरुधा f. (-धा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरेश्वर|वीरेश्वरः
वीरेश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. VĪRABHADRA, one of ŚIVA'S attendants.<BR>	 2. A<BR>great hero.<BR> E. वीर a hero, and ईश्वर lord or chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरोञ्झ
वीरोञ्झ m. (-ञ्झः) A Brāhman, who omits burnt offerings or<BR>neglects his sacrificial fire.<BR> E. वीर fire, उज्झ to abandon, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरोपजीविक|वीरोपजीविकः
वीरोपजीविक m. (-कः) A Brāhman, who claims alms or presents, on<BR>the merit of having preserved his sacrificial fire.<BR> E. वीर sacrificial<BR>fire and उपजीविक living by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्य|वीर्य|वीर्यं|वीर्य्यं
वीर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Strength, vigour, power.<BR>	 2. Dignity, consequence.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fortitude, firmness.<BR>	 4. Semen virile.<BR>	 5. Splendour, lustre.<BR>	 6.<BR>Heroism, valour.<BR>	 7. Seed, (of plants, &c.)<BR>	 8. Efficacy.<BR> E. वीर a<BR>hero, and यत् aff.; or वीर् to be strong, and अच् and यत् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यवत्|वीर्यवत्|वीर्यवन्त्
वीर्य्यवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Strong, stout, robust.<BR>	 2. Overcoming,<BR>victorious.<BR>	 3. Efficacious.<BR> E. वीर्य्य strength, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यविरहित|वीर्यविरहित
वीर्य्यविरहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Devoid of prowess or vigour, &c.<BR> E. वीर्य्य,<BR>विरहित deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यविशिष्ट|वीर्यविशिष्ट
वीर्य्यविशिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Possessed of courage, vigour, &c.<BR> E. वीर्य्य,<BR>विशिष्ट endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यहानि|वीर्यहानि
वीर्य्यहानि f. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Loss of vigour or courage.<BR>	 2. Impotence.<BR> E. वीर्य्य,<BR>हानि loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यहीन|वीर्यहीन
वीर्य्यहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Seedless.<BR>	 2. Cowardly.<BR> E. वीर्य्य, हीन void of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यावदान|वीर्यावदान
वीर्य्यावदान n. (-नं) Effecting any thing by prowess.<BR> E. वीर्य्य, अवदान end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्य्यावधूत|वीर्यावधूत
वीर्य्यावधूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Overcome or surpassed in prowess.<BR> E. वीर्य्य,<BR>and अवधूत shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीवध|वीवधः
वीवध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A yoke for carrying burdens.<BR>	 2. A burden.<BR>	 3.<BR>Storing or heaping corn.<BR>	 4. A pitcher.<BR>	 5. A road: see विवध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीवधिक|वीवधिकः
वीवधिक mf. (-कः-की)<BR>	 1. A chandler.<BR>	 2. A man or woman carrying a<BR>load by means of a pole.<BR> E. वीवध, ठन् aff., the first vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
वी(वि)हार m. (-रः) A holy place, a temple, a sanctuary, but especially a<BR>Jaina or Bauddha convent.<BR> E. वि, हृ to convey, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुग्
वुग्(इ)वुगि r. 1st cl. (वुङ्गति) To except, to leave, to abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुट्
वुट् r. 10th cl. (वुण्टयति-ते) To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुध्
वुध्(इ)वुधि r. 10th cl. (वुन्धयति-ते) To injure, to hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुवूर्षु
वुवूर्षु Adj. Desirous of choosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुस्
वुस् r. 4th cl. (वुस्यति) To throw or cast off; also बुस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वूर्ण
वूर्ण f. (-र्णा) Adj. Chosen, selected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वूष्
वूष् r. 10th cl. (वूषयति-ते) To kill, to hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृ
वृ(ङ,)वृङ् r. 9th cl. (वृणाति, वृणीते) To serve, to do homage or worship,<BR>to conciliate by service or adoration. (ञ) वृञ् r. 1st cl. (वरति-ते) r.<BR>5th cl. (वृणोति वृणुते) r. 10th cl. (वारयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To choose, to select,<BR>to prepare.<BR>	 2. To appoint, to invite.<BR>	 3. To screen, to invest, to<BR>cover. With अप prefixed, To convey, to screen, to shield or<BR>defend. With आङ्, To inclose, to cover, to surround. With नि or<BR>निर्, To cease, to refrain from, to finish or end. With परि, 1. To<BR>surround.<BR>	 2. To depend upon. With वि, To become evident or<BR>apparent, to open or appear. With सम्, To conceal. With सम् and<BR>आङ्, To wrap up, to involve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहण|वृंहणः
वृंहण mfn. (-णः-णा or णी-णं) Nourishing, fattening, nutritious.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>A kind of sweetmeat made of sugar, milk, spices, &c., fried in<BR>Ghee, and powdered with coarse sugar or treacle.<BR> E. वृहि to<BR>increase, and ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहणीय
वृंहणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be nourished, what ought to or may be.<BR> E. वृहि to grow, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंहित|वृंहितं
वृंहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Grown, increased.<BR>	 2. Cherished, nourished.<BR>n. (-त) The roar of elephants.<BR> E. वृहि to grow or increase, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्
वृक् r. 1st. cl. (वर्कते) To take or accept, to seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक|वृकः
वृक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A wolf.<BR>	 2. A crow.<BR>	 3. The Vaka-pushpa tree, (Ses-<BR>bana grandiflora.)<BR>	 4. A jackal.<BR>	 5. A hyena.<BR>	 6. A rat, a mouse.<BR>7. A Kṣatriya.<BR>	 8. Name of a demon.<BR>	 9. Name of a fire in the<BR>stomach.<BR>	 10. Turpentine.<BR>	 11. Compounded perfume.<BR>	 f. (-का) A<BR>plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR> E. वृक् to take, aff. क; or वृ to hide<BR>or screen, Unādi aff. कक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकदंश|वृकदंशः
वृकदंश m. (-शः) A dog.<BR> E. वृक a wolf, and दंश who bites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकधूप|वृकधूपः
वृकधूप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Compounded perfume.<BR>	 2. Turpentine.<BR> E. वृक the<BR>same meanings, and धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकाराति|वृकारातिः
वृकाराति m. (-तिः) A dog.<BR> E. वृक a wolf, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकारि|वृकारिः
वृकारि m. (-रिः) A dog.<BR> E. वृक a wolf, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृकोदर|वृकोदरः
वृकोदर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. Name of BHĪMA.<BR> E. वृक a<BR>wolf, or the name of a fire in the stomach, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्क|वृक्कः
वृक्क mf. (-क्कः-क्का)<BR>	 1. The heart.<BR>	 2. A kidney, (In this sense in the dual.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ण|वृक्णं
वृक्ण mfn. (-क्णः-क्णा-क्णं) Cut, divided, broken.<BR> E. व्रश्च् to cut, aff. क्त,<BR>form irr.; also read वक्न ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्णवत्
वृक्णवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Cutting, severing.<BR> E. व्रश्च् to cut, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्त
वृक्त f. (-क्ता) Cleaned, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ष्
वृक्ष् r. 1st cl. (वृक्षते)<BR>	 1. To appoint.<BR>	 2. To cover.<BR>	 3. To take or accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्ष|वृक्षः
वृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A tree in general.<BR> E. वृक्ष् to cover, (to shade,) aff. घञ्; or<BR>व्रश्च् to cut and क्स Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षक|वृक्षकः
वृक्षक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A small tree, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>	 2. Any<BR>tree.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=682-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षकुक्कुट|वृक्षकुक्कुटः
वृक्षकुक्कुट m. (-टः) A wild cock.<BR> E. वृक्ष and कुक्कुट a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षखण्ड|वृक्षखंड
वृक्षखण्ड n. (-ण्ड) A grove.<BR> E. वृक्ष and खण्ड a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षचर|वृक्षचरः
वृक्षचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Going or living in trees.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A monkey. E.<BR>वृक्ष a tree or any other synonym, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षच्छाया|वृक्षछाया
वृक्षच्छाया f. (-या) The shade of a single tree.<BR>	 n. (-यं) The shade of many<BR>trees or a grove.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, and च्छाया shade; in the second<BR>sense, it takes the neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षतल
वृक्षतल n. (-लं) The foot of a tree or ground about it.<BR> E. वृक्ष, तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षधूप|वृक्षधूपः
वृक्षधूप m. (-पः) Turpentine.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, and धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षनाथ|वृक्षनाथः
वृक्षनाथ m. (-थः) The Indian-fig tree.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षनिर्य्यास|वृक्षनिर्यास|वृक्षनिर्यासः
वृक्षनिर्य्यास m. (-सः) Gum, resin.<BR> E. वृक्ष and निर्य्यास exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षनिवास
वृक्षनिवास m. (-सः) Dwelling or living in a tree.<BR> E. वृक्ष, निवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षपाक|वृक्षपाकः
वृक्षपाक m. (-कः) The Indian-fig tree.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, and पाक what<BR>ripens or perfects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षभवन|वृक्षभवनं
वृक्षभवन n. (-नं) A hollow in a tree.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, and भवन dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षभिद्
वृक्षभिद् f. (-भिद् or भित्) An axe.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, भिद् breaking, cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षभेदिन्
वृक्षभेदिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A carpenter's chisel.<BR>	 2. A hatchet.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree,<BR>and भेदिन् what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षमय
वृक्षमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) A bounding with trees.<BR> E. वृक्ष and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षमर्कटिका
वृक्षमर्कटिका f. (-का) A squirrel.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, मर्कट a monkey, कन् aff.<BR>of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षमृद्भू
वृक्षमृद्भू m. (-द्भूः) A sort of cane or reed, (Calamus fascicularis.)<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, मृद् earth, भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षरुह
वृक्षरुह mf. (-हः-हा) A parasite plant, (Cymbidum tessalloides, &c.) E.<BR>वृक्ष, and रुह growing, having its roots attached to the trunk or<BR>branches of another plant or tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षरोपण
वृक्षरोपण n. (-णं) Planting trees.<BR> E. वृक्ष, and रोपण planting; also वृक्षारोपण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षवाटिका
वृक्षवाटिका f. (-का) A garden, a grove, one belonging to the residence of<BR>a minister of state, a courtezan, &c.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, and वाटिका or<BR>वाटी an enclosure; hence also वृक्षवाटी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षश|वृक्षशः
वृक्षश m. (-शः) A lizard, a chamæleon.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, शी to sleep, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षशायिका
वृक्षशायिका f. (-का) A squirrel.<BR> E. वुक्ष, शी to sleep, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षस्य
वृक्षस्य mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) What is or stays in or on a tree.<BR> E. वृक्ष, and<BR>स्थ who or what stays; also वृक्षस्थायिन्, वृक्षस्थित; &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षाग्र
वृक्षाग्र n. (-ग्रं) The top of a tree.<BR> E. वृक्ष, and अग्र top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षाङ्घ्रि|वृक्षाङ्घ्रिः
वृक्षाङ्घ्रि m. (-ङ्घ्रिः) The root of a tree.<BR> E. वृक्ष, and अङ्घ्रि foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षादन|वृक्षादनः
वृक्षादन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A carpenter's chisel or adze.<BR>	 2. A hatchet, a<BR>chopper.<BR>	 3. The Indian-fig tree.<BR>	 4. The Piyāl tree, (Buchanania<BR>latifolia.)<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A parasite plant, (Epidendron.)<BR>	 2. A shrub,<BR>(Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, अदन eating or food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षादिरुहक|वृक्षादिरुहकं
वृक्षादिरुहक n. (-कं) Embracing.<BR> E. वृक्षादि trees, &c., रुह ascended, and<BR>कन् aff. of comparison; entwining as a creeper round a tree, &c.;<BR>also derived from रुह् with क्त aff., वृक्षादिरूढ n. (-ढं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षाम्ल|वृक्षाम्लं|वृक्षाम्लः
वृक्षाम्ल m. (-म्लः) The hog-plum, (Spondias mangifera.)<BR>	 n. (-म्लं) Acid<BR>seasoning, or the fruit of the tamarind so used.<BR> E. वृक्ष, अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षारोपक|वृक्षारोपकः
वृक्षारोपक m. (-कः) A planter of a tree.<BR> E. वृक्ष and आरोपक who plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षारोपण
वृक्षारोपण n. (-णं) Planting tress.<BR> E. वृक्ष, and आरोपण planting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षालय|वृक्षालयः
वृक्षालय m. (-यः) A bird in general.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षावास|वृक्षावासः
वृक्षावास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. An ascetic, one who lives in the hollows of trees.<BR>	 2.<BR>A bird.<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षोत्थ
वृक्षोत्थ mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं) Growing on or borne by a tree.<BR> E. वृक्ष, उत्थ what rises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्षोत्पल|वृक्षोत्पलः
वृक्षोत्पल m. (-लः) A large handsome tree, commonly Kaniyar or KAR-<BR>NIKĀR, (Pterospermum acerifolium.)<BR> E. वृक्ष a tree, उत्पल a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृच्
वृच्(ई)वृवी r. 7th cl. (वृणक्ति)<BR>	 1. To cover.<BR>	 2. To quit, to abandon, to<BR>shun or avoid.<BR>	 3. To choose, to take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृज्
वृज्(ई)वृजी r. 1st cl. (वर्जति) r. 2nd cl. (वृङ्क्ते) r. 7th cl. (वृणक्ति)<BR>	 1. To<BR>choose.<BR>	 2. To lose, to avoid.<BR>	 3. To purify.<BR>	 4. To cover. With अप,<BR>To relinquish. r. 10th cl. (वर्ज्जयति-ते) To quit, to shun, to avoid,<BR>to except, to abandon. With आ, To bend, to incline.<BR>	 2. To offer.<BR>With वि, 1. To avoid.<BR>	 2. To be destitute of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजन|वृजनं|वृजनः
वृजन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Crooked.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sin.<BR>	 2. Sky, atmosphere.<BR>	 3. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">Page683-b+ 60</a>]<BR>field cleared for pasture.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Hair.<BR> E. वृज् to quit, &c.,<BR>Unādi aff. क्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजि|वृजिः
वृजि f. (-जिः) A country, probably that to the west of Delhi and<BR>Āgrā, or the modern Bruj.<BR> E. वृज् to quit, aff कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजिक
वृजिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of the district of Vrij or Bruj, (as a dialect, a<BR>native. &c.)<BR> E. वृजि as above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृजिन|वृजिनं|वृजिनः
वृजिन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Crooked, bent, curved.<BR>	 2. Wicked.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Sin, vice, wickedness.<BR>	 2. Red leather.<BR>	 3. Distress, affliction.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-नः) Hair.<BR> E. वृज् to cover, Unādi aff. इनच्, the vowel un-<BR>changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृण्
वृण् r. 6th cl. (वृणति) To please, to gratify. (उ) (वृणु) r. 8th cl. (वृणोति,<BR>वृणुते) To eat, to consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृण्वत्
वृण्वत् mfn. (-ण्वन्-ण्वन्ती-ण्वत्) Choosing, electing, preferring, (especially<BR>as a husband or wife.)<BR> E. वृ to choose, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृण्वाण
वृण्वाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Choosing.<BR> E. वृ to choose, शानच् aff.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्
वृत्(उ)वृतु r. 1st cl. (वर्त्तते) To be, to exist, to stay, to stand, to be fixed<BR>or stable. r. 4th cl. (वृत्यते)<BR>	 1. To choose, to select or appoint.<BR>	 2. To<BR>serve.<BR>	 3. To divide. r. 10th cl. (वर्त्तयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To speak.<BR>With अति prefixed, 1. To surpass or overcome.<BR>	 2. To pass over or<BR>beyond.<BR>	 3. To transgress. With अनु, 1. To follow, to imitate.<BR>	 2. To<BR>proceed. With अप, To turn back or round. With आङ्, 1. To turn<BR>round, to revolve.<BR>	 2. To do repeatedly. With नि, To make artifi-<BR>cially. With नि or निर्, To stop, to cease, to complete or terminate.<BR>With परि, 1. To surround.<BR>	 2. To exchange.<BR>	 3. To excel, to be pre-<BR>eminent.<BR>	 4. To advance.<BR>	 5. To retreat or return.<BR>	 6. To turn round.<BR>With प्र, To engage in any active pursuit. With प्रति and नि,<BR>To go away, to depart. With वि, 1. To roll, to whirl, to turn<BR>round.<BR>	 2. To revolve. With वि and नि, To return. With वि and परि,<BR>To revolve, (in the mind.) With सम् and अभि, To leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत|वृतः
वृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Chosen, selected, preferred.<BR>	 2. Agreed or<BR>assented to.<BR>	 3. Served.<BR>	 4. Covered, screened, defended.<BR>	 5. Affected<BR>by.<BR>	 6. Vitiated, spoiled.<BR>	 7. Hired.<BR> E. वृ to prefer, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृति|वृतिः
वृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Selecting, choosing, preferring, appointing.<BR>	 2. Solici-<BR>ting, asking, requesting.<BR>	 3. Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>	 4. An<BR>enclosure, a place enclosed for particular cultivation, and<BR>especially that of the Piper betel, which in many parts of India is<BR>surrounded and screened by mats.<BR>	 5. Hiding, secreting.<BR>	 6. A<BR>request.<BR> E. वृ to choose, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृतिङ्कर|वृतिंकर|वृतिंकरः|वृतिङ्करः
वृतिङ्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A plant,<BR>(Flacourtia sapida, Rox.)<BR> E. वृति surrounding, कृ to make, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त|वृत्तं|वृत्तः
वृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Chosen, selected, appointed.<BR>	 2. Done, perform-<BR>ed, engaged in or undertaken.<BR>	 3. Past, gone, been.<BR>	 4. Over, finish-<BR>ed.<BR>	 5. Dead, deceased.<BR>	 6. Read, studied, read through.<BR>	 7. Covered.<BR>8. Round.<BR>	 9. Firm, hard.<BR>	 10. Unobstructed, unimpaired.<BR>	 11. Fa-<BR>mons, celebrated.<BR>	 12. Turned.<BR>	 13. Been, existed.<BR>	 n. (-त्तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Verse, metre.<BR>	 2. Conduct, observance of enjoined practice in<BR>private or social life.<BR>	 3. Practice, profession, means of gaining<BR>a subsistence.<BR>	 4. Procedure, event, occurrence.<BR>	 5. A circle.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-त्तः) A tortoise.<BR> E. वृत् to be, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तकर्कटी
वृत्तकर्कटी f. (-टी) The water-melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तखण्ड|वृत्तखण्डः
वृत्तखण्ड n. (-ण्डं) Sector or segment of a circle.<BR> E. वृत्त, and खण्ड part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तगन्धि|वृत्तगंधि
वृत्तगन्धि n. (-न्धिः) Name given to a particular kind of prose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तचूड
वृत्तचूड Adj. Whose tonsure has been performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तज्ञ
वृत्तज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Who or what knows men's actions.<BR> E. वृत्त, ज्ञ<BR>who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्ततस्
वृत्ततस् Ind. In or relating to observance or duty, by caste or duty,<BR>not implying agency; as वृत्ततः पापं “by or according to caste, a<BR>sin.”<BR> E. तसि substituted for the termination of the third case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तपुष्प|वृत्तपुष्पः
वृत्तपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea cadamba.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>Shirisa tree.<BR>	 3. A cane.<BR> E. वृत्त round, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=683-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तफल|वृत्तफलं|वृत्तफलः
वृत्तफल n. (-लं) Black pepper.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The pomegranate.<BR>	 2. The<BR>jujube.<BR> E. वृत्त round, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तवत्|वृत्तवन्त्
वृत्तवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Discharging the duties of caste or calling,<BR>correct, well-conducted.<BR> E. वृत्त and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तसम्पन्न|वृत्तसंपन्न
वृत्तसम्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Well-behaved or conducted, behaving with<BR>propriety.<BR> E. वृत्त duty, and सम्पन्न perfect in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रसादिन्
वृत्रसादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Worthless, mean, vile.<BR> E. वृत्त, षद् to go, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तस्थ|वृत्तस्थः
वृत्तस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Discharging the duties of caste or calling. E.<BR>वृत्त established practice, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्ताध्ययनर्द्धि
वृत्ताध्ययनर्द्धि f. (-र्द्धिः) Holiness, sanctity, resulting from observance of<BR>the rules of life and study of scripture.<BR> E. वृत्त conduct, अध्ययन<BR>study, and ऋद्धि prosperity, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तानुवर्त्तिन्|वृत्तानुवर्तिन्
वृत्तानुवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) Obedient, conforming to rule.<BR> E. वृत्त,<BR>अनु according to, वत्तिन् abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तानुसार|वृत्तानुसारः
वृत्तानुसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Conforming to prescribed practice.<BR>	 2. Conformity<BR>to metre.<BR> E. वृत्त, अनुसार following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तानुसारिन्
वृत्तानुसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Conforming to established rule or prac-<BR>tice, doing what is enjoined or proper.<BR> E. वृत्तानुसार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तान्त|वृत्तांत|वृत्तान्तः
वृत्तान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Tidings, rumour, intelligence.<BR>	 2. Sort, kind, differ-<BR>ence.<BR>	 3. Mode, manner.<BR>	 4. Whole.<BR>	 5. Interval, rest, leisure, oppor-<BR>tunity.<BR>	 6. Topic, subject.<BR>	 7. A tale, a story.<BR>	 8. Event.<BR>	 9. Property,<BR>nature.<BR>	 10. Alone, solitary.<BR> E. वृत्त observance, &c., and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्ति|वृत्तिः
वृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Livelihood, profession, means of acquiring subsistence.<BR>2. Style or character of dramatic representation, or composition,<BR>considered to be of four sorts, viz:--Kaūsīkī, which exhibits love<BR>or passion; Bhāratī, which appears to implies declamation es-<BR>pecially; Sātwatī, of which the subject is virtue and heroism,<BR>and Ārbhattī, which treats of magic, delusion, wrath and<BR>battle.<BR>	 3. Style in general.<BR>	 4. Gloss, comment, explanation, expo-<BR>sition.<BR>	 5. Being, abiding, staying.<BR>	 6. Seizing, stopping, withhold-<BR>ing, restraining.<BR>	 7. Circumference of a wheel or circle.<BR>	 8. State,<BR>condition.<BR>	 9. Behaviour, action, course of action, conduct.<BR>	 10.<BR>Action, engagement, operation.<BR>	 11. Respectful treatment.<BR>	 12.<BR>Wages, hire.<BR>	 13. Revolving, turning round.<BR>	 14. A complex forma-<BR>tion, (in gram.)<BR>	 15. The connotative power of a word; (these are<BR>three, viz:--अभिधा, लक्षणा and व्यंजना ।)<BR> E. वृत् to be, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिकर्षित
वृत्तिकर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Attracted by or impelled to for the sake of<BR>subsistence.<BR> E. वृत्ति and कर्षित attracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिता
वृत्तिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. State of existence.<BR>	 2. Profession, subsistence.<BR> E. वृत्ति<BR>and तल् aff.; also with त्व, वृत्तित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिदान
वृत्तिदान n. (-नं) Giving maintenance, &c.<BR> E. वृत्ति and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिमत्|वृत्तिमन्त्
वृत्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Abiding, stationary.<BR> E. वृत्ति and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिवैकल्य
वृत्तिवैकल्य n. (-ल्यं) Want of livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिस्थ|वृत्तिस्थः
वृत्तिस्थ Adj.<BR>	 1. Being in employment.<BR>	 2. Of good behaviour.<BR>	 m. (-स्थः) A lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तिहेतु|वृत्तिहेतुः
वृत्तिहेतु f. (-तुः) Cause or means of subsistence.<BR> E. वृत्ति and हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्तौजस्
वृत्तौजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः) Mighty, irresistible.<BR> E. वृत्त, ओजस् strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त्य
वृत्त्य mfn. (-त्त्यः-त्त्या-त्त्यं)<BR>	 1. To be chosen, preferable, eligible.<BR>	 2. Excell-<BR>ent, eminent.<BR>	 3. To be abided or stayed.<BR> E. वृत् to select, aff. क्यप्;<BR>or वृञ् with the same aff. and तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त्यर्थम्
वृत्त्यर्थम् Ind. For the sake of subsistence.<BR> E. वृत्ति, अर्थम् for the sake of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त्यनुप्रास|वृत्त्यनुप्रासः
वृत्त्यनुप्रास m. (-सः) Alliteration suited to any style or expression. E.<BR>वृत्ति and अनुप्रास alliteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्त्युपाय|वृत्त्युपायः
वृत्त्युपाय m. (-यः) Means of subsistence.<BR> E. वृत्ति and उपाय means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्र|वृत्रः
वृत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. An enemy.<BR>	 2. Darkness.<BR>	 3. A demon slain by INDRA.<BR>4. A cloud.<BR>	 5. A name of INDRA.<BR>	 6. The name of a mountain.<BR>	 7.<BR>Sound, noise.<BR> E. वृत् to be or abide, Unādi aff. रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रद्विष्
वृत्रद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) INDRA.<BR> E. वृत्र the demon, and द्विष् the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रभोजन|वृत्रभोजनः
वृत्रभोजन m. (-नः) A kind of potherb, described by some as a sort of<BR>cucumber.<BR> E. वृत्र INDRA, and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रहन्
वृत्रहन् m. (-हा) INDRA.<BR> E. वृत्र demon, and हन् slayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत्रारि|वृत्रारिः
वृत्रारि m. (-रिः) INDRA.<BR> E. वृत्र demon, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथा
वृथा Ind.<BR>	 1. Uselessly, fruitlessly.<BR>	 2. Wrongly, incorrectly.<BR>	 3. In vain,<BR>(in composition with nouns.)<BR>	 4. Compounded with articles of food,<BR>it implies they are hot.<BR> E. वृ to choose, &c., aff. थाक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथाकथा
वृथाकथा f. (-था) Idle talk.<BR> E. वृथा and कथा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथाघात
वृथाघात m. (-तः) Striking or killing any being unnecessarily.<BR> E. वृथा and<BR>आघात a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथाट्या
वृथाट्या f. (-ट्या) Going about or travelling for pleasure.<BR> E. वृथा and अट्या roaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथादान|वृथादानं
वृथादान n. (-नं) Unprofitable donation, gift to encomiasts, harlots,<BR>wrestlers, money lost at play, &c.<BR> E. वृथा vain, and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथापशुघ्न
वृथापशुघ्न m. (-घ्नः) The slayer of an animal except for sacrifice.<BR> E. वृथा<BR>and पशु an animal, घ्न who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथामांस|वृथामांसं
वृथामांस n. (-सं) Flesh not intended to be offered to the gods or manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथालम्भ|वृथालम्भः
वृथालम्भ m. (-म्भः) Cutting or plucking unnecessarily.<BR> E. वृथा and लभि to<BR>get, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथोत्पन्न
वृथोत्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Born or produced in vain.<BR> E. वृथा and उत्पन्न produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्ध|वृद्धं|वृद्धः
वृद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Old, aged, ancient.<BR>	 2. Full-grown, large,<BR>expanded to the proper size.<BR>	 3. Wise, learned.<BR>	 4. Heaped, accumu-<BR>lated.<BR>	 5. Increased, augmented.<BR>	 m. (-द्धः)<BR>	 1. An old man, or one<BR>past seventy.<BR>	 2. A sage, a saint.<BR>	 3. A male descendant.<BR>	 f. (-द्धा)<BR>	 1.<BR>An old woman, either one past child-bearing, or one with grey<BR>hair.<BR>	 2. A female descendant.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं) Benzoin, (Styrax benzoin.)<BR>E. वृध् to increase or grow, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धकाक|वृद्धकाकः
वृद्धकाक m. (-कः) A sort of crow or raven.<BR> E. वृद्ध old or large, and काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धत्व|वृद्धत्वं
वृद्धत्व n. (-त्वं) Old age.<BR> E. वृद्ध old, त्व aff. of the abstracts; also वृद्धता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धदारक|वृद्धदारकः
वृद्धदारक m. (-कः) A climbing plant, (Lettsomia nervosa.)<BR> E. वृद्ध old,<BR>and दारक tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धनाभि|वृद्धनाभिः
वृद्धनाभि mfn. (-भिः-भिः or भी-भि) Pot-bellied, corpulent.<BR> E. वृद्ध large, नाभि the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धप्रपितामह|वृद्धप्रपितामहः
वृद्धप्रपितामह m. (-हः) A paternal great greatgrandfather.<BR>	 f. (-ही) A<BR>paternal great greatgrandmother.<BR> E. वृद्ध old, प्रपितामह great-<BR>grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धप्रमातामह|वृद्धप्रमातामहः
वृद्धप्रमातामह m. (-हः) A maternal great great-grandfather.<BR>	 f. (-ही) A<BR>maternal great great-grandmother.<BR> E. वृद्ध and प्रमातामह maternal<BR>greatgrandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धभाव|वृद्धभावः
वृद्धभाव m. (-वः) Old age.<BR> E. वृद्ध and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धराज|वृद्धराजः
वृद्धराज m. (-जः) A kind of dock or sorrel: see अम्लवेतस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धवाहन|वृद्धवाहनः
वृद्धवाहन m. (-नः) The mango tree.<BR> E. वृद्ध large, वाहन vehicle or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धविभीतक|वृद्धविभीतकः
वृद्धविभीतक m. (-कः) Hog-plum, (Spondias mangifera.) “आम्डा.”<BR> E. वृद्ध<BR>old or large, विभीतक myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धश्रवस्
वृद्धश्रवस् m. (-वाः) INDRA.<BR> E. वृद्ध aged, and श्रवस् hearing; who listens<BR>to the old or wise; or वृद्ध large, and श्रवस् the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धसंघ
वृद्धसंघ m. (-घः) An assembly of old men, a council or meeting of elders.<BR>E. वृद्ध an elder, and संघ assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धसूत्रक|वृद्धसूत्रकं
वृद्धसूत्रक n. (-कं) Flocculent seeds flying in the air.<BR> E. वृद्ध old, सूत्र thread, aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धसेवा
वृद्धसेवा f. (-वा) Reverence for old age.<BR> E. वृद्ध, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धाङ्गुलि|वृद्धांगुलि|वृद्धाङ्गुलिः
वृद्धाङ्गुलि f. (-लिः) The thumb.<BR> E. वृद्ध large, and अङ्गुलि a finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धाङ्गुष्ठ|वृद्धांगुष्ठ
वृद्धाङ्गुष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. The thumb.<BR>	 2. The great toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धाचार|वृद्धाचारः
वृद्धाचार m. (-रः) Ancient custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धारण्य
वृद्धारण्य m. (-ण्यः) A place where the Purāṇas, and other sacred works<BR>are read and expounded.<BR> E. वृद्ध a Pandit, a scholar, अरण्य a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धावस्था
वृद्धावस्था f. (-स्था) The condition or period of old age.<BR> E. वृद्ध, अवस्था state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धाश्रम
वृद्धाश्रम m. (-मः) Roaming, travelling, wandering about.<BR> E. वृद्ध, and<BR>आश्रम order or state of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धि|वृद्धिः
वृद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Increase, augmentation in general, as in bulk, conse-<BR>quence, wealth, &c.<BR>	 2. The third of the three conditions or objects<BR>of regal power, extension of power or revenue, or any indication<BR>of progression.<BR>	 3. Rise, ascending, mounting.<BR>	 4. Prosperity, suc-<BR>cess.<BR>	 5. One of the eight principal drugs or medical roots, des-<BR>cribed as mild and cooling, sweet and bitter, &c., as a remedy for<BR>phlegm, leprosy and worms.<BR>	 6. The eleventh of the astronomical<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">Page685-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Yogas, or Yoga star of the 11th lunar mansion.<BR>	 7. A particular<BR>period or division of time.<BR>	 8. The increase of the digits of the sun<BR>or moon.<BR>	 9. Enlargement of the scrotum, either from swelled tes-<BR>ticle or hydrocele or other morbid affections.<BR>	 10. Interest, usury,<BR>especially returning the principal, (as in the case of seed corn<BR>lent,) with a proportionate increment.<BR>	 11. Happiness, pleasure.<BR>12. A heap, a quantity, assemblage, multitude.<BR>	 13. Wealth, pro-<BR>perty.<BR>	 14. Cutting off, abscission.<BR>	 15. (In law,) Forfeiture, deduc-<BR>tion.<BR>	 16. Profit, gain.<BR>	 17. The lengthening of a vowel, the subs-<BR>titution of आ, ऐ, औ, आर् and आल् for अ, इ, उ, ऋ and ऌ (short<BR>or long; in gram.)<BR> E. वृध् to increase, aff. कि, or क्तिन् or क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=684-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिकर
वृद्धिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Yielding or causing increase, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिका
वृद्धिका f. (-का) A sort of drug: see वृद्धि.<BR> E. कन् added to वृद्धि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिजीविका
वृद्धिजीविका f. (-का) The profession of usury.<BR> E. वृद्धि, जीविका livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिपत्र
वृद्धिपत्र n. (-त्रं) A kind of razor or lancet.<BR> E. वृद्धि, and पत्र blade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिमत्|वृद्धिमन्त्
वृद्धिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Augmented, increased.<BR>	 2. Rich.<BR>	 3. Pros-<BR>perous.<BR> E. वृद्धि, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धिश्राद्ध|वृद्धिश्राद्धं
वृद्धिश्राद्ध n. (-द्धं) A Śrāddha or sacrifice to progenitors on any pros-<BR>perous occasion, as the birth of a son, &c.<BR> E. वृद्धि, and श्राद्ध cere-<BR>mony so termed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्धोक्ष|वृद्धोक्षः
वृद्धोक्ष m. (-क्षः) An old bull.<BR> E. वृद्ध old, and उक्ष a bull or ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृद्ध्याजीव|वृद्ध्याजीवः
वृद्ध्याजीव m. (-वः) A usurer.<BR> E. वृद्धि usury, and आजीव who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध्
वृध्(उ)वृधु r. 1st cl. (वर्द्धते)<BR>	 1. To increase or grow.<BR>	 2. The continue,<BR>to last.<BR>	 3. To become joyful, to have cause for congratulation.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वर्द्धयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To shine.<BR>	 2. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृधसान|वृधसानः
वृधसान m. (-नः) A man.<BR> E. वृध् to grow, &c. aff. असानच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृथसानु
वृथसानु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A man.<BR>	 2. A leaf.<BR>	 3. Act, action.<BR> E. वृध् to increase, असानु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध्न
वृध्न m. (-ध्नः) Bubo in the groin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृध्य|वृध्यं
वृध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) To be increased or augmented.<BR> E. वृध् to grow, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्त|वृंत|वृंतं|वृन्तं
वृन्त n. (-न्तं)<BR>	 1. The footstalk of a leaf or fruit.<BR>	 2. The nipple.<BR>	 3. The<BR>stand of a water-jar.<BR> E. वृञ् to choose, क्त aff., and नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्ताक|वृंताक|वृंताकः|वृन्ताकः
वृन्ताक mf. (-कः-की) The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR> E. वृन्त foot-<BR>stalk, अक् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्तिता
वृन्तिता f. (-ता) A medicinal plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR> E. वृन्त a<BR>stalk, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्द|वृंद|वृन्दं|वृन्दः
वृन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) All, many.<BR>	 n. (-न्दं) A heap, a multitude, a quan-<BR>tity, an aggregation.<BR>	 f. (-न्दा) Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.) E.<BR>वृण् to please, or वृत् to be, &c., aff. दन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दार|वृंदार|वृन्दारः
वृन्दार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, handsome, pleasing.<BR>	 2. Eminent,<BR>reputable.<BR> E. वृन्द a quantity, and आरक aff., implying pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दारक|वृंदारक|वृन्दारकः
वृन्दारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Handsome, agreeable, pleasing.<BR>	 2. Best,<BR>excellent, chief.<BR>	 3. Much, great.<BR>	 4. Reputable, respectable,<BR>eminent.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A deity, an immortal.<BR>	 2. A chief, the head or<BR>leader of a crowd or herd, &c., (at the end of a compound.)<BR> E. वृन्द<BR>a heap, and आरकन् aff., implying pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दिष्ठ|वृंदिष्ठ|वृन्दिष्ठः
वृन्दिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very beautiful or charming, very excellent or<BR>elevated, very reputable or venerable.<BR> E. वृन्दारक chief, excellent,<BR>वृन्द substituted, and इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. super.; also with ईयसुन्<BR>the same, वृन्दीयस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृन्दीयस्|वृंदीयस्
वृन्दीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Very eminent or excellent. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्
वृश् r. 4th cl. (वृश्यति) To choose, to prefer, to select.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश|वृशः
वृश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A rat.<BR>	 2. A flower, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR>	 f. (-शा) A<BR>drug.<BR>	 n. (-शं) Ginger.<BR> E. वृ to choose, शक् Uṇādi aff.: see वृष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्चिक|वृश्चिकः
वृश्चिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A scorpion.<BR>	 2. The sign Scorpio of the zodiac.<BR>	 3.<BR>A hairy caterpillar.<BR>	 4. A crab.<BR>	 5. A sort of beetle found in cow-<BR>dung.<BR>	 6. A centipede.<BR>	 7. A thorny shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>8. The month when the sun is in Scorpio.<BR>	 f. (-का) A potherb.<BR>(Basella.)<BR> E. व्रश्च् to cut, Unādi aff. किकन्, and the semi-vowel<BR>changed to the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्चिकप्रिया
वृश्चिकप्रिया f. (-या) A potherb, (Basella rubra and lucida.)<BR> E. वृश्चिक a scorpion, प्रिय found of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृश्चिकाली
वृश्चिकाली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A line of scorpions.<BR>	 2. A shrub, (Tragia involucra-<BR>ta.)<BR> E. वृश्चिक a scorpion, and आली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्
वृष्(उ)वृषु r. 1st cl. (वर्षति)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle.<BR>	 2. To rain.<BR>	 3. To hurt or kill.<BR>4. To weary.<BR>	 5. To give.<BR>	 6. To be capable of generating.<BR>	 7. To<BR>have supreme power. With अभि, 1. To shower.<BR>	 2. To bestow.<BR>With प्र, To rain. r. 10th cl. (वर्षयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To conceive, to be<BR>impregnated.<BR>	 2. To possess supreme or super-natural power.<BR>	 3. To<BR>be powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष|वृषं|वृषः
वृष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A bull.<BR>	 2. The sign Taurus of the zodiac.<BR>	 3. Virtue,<BR>moral merit.<BR>	 4. Virtue personified, as a bull or the bull of ŚIVA.<BR>5. A man of a lecherous disposition, one of the four descriptions<BR>into which men are divided in erotic works.<BR>	 6. A rat.<BR>	 7. A drug,<BR>commonly Rishabha.<BR>	 8. A plant, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR>	 9. (In<BR>composition,) Excellent, pre-eminent.<BR>	 10. A name of KARṆA.<BR>	 11.<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 12. An enemy, an adversary.<BR>	 13. Particular ground,<BR>judged proper for the foundation of a house.<BR>	 14. Love or KĀMA.<BR>15. A strong or athletic man.<BR>	 n. (-षं) A peacock's plumage or tail.<BR>f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR>	 2. Cowach, (Carpopogon<BR>pruriens.)<BR>	 f. (-षी) The seat of the religious student or one used<BR>by ascetics, formed of Kusa grass.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle, aff. क<BR>or अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषकर्णी
वृषकर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant. “सुदर्शना लतायाम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषण|वृषणः
वृषण m. (-णः) The scrotum, the bag which contains the testicles. E.<BR>वृष् to sprinkle, (seminal fluid,) aff. क्यु or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषणकच्छू
वृषणकच्छू f. (-च्छूः) Ulceration of the scrotum.<BR> E. वृषण and कच्छू a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषणश्व|वृषणश्वः
वृषणश्व m. (-श्वः) The horse of INDRA.<BR> E. वृषण INDRA, and अश्व the horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषण्वसु
वृषण्वसु n. (-सु) The horse, &c. of INDRA.<BR> E. वृषन् INDRA, and वसु wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषदशक
वृषदशक m. (-कः) A cat.<BR> E. वृष a rat, and दशक devourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषध्वज|वृषध्वजः
वृषध्वज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. GAṆEŚA.<BR>	 3. A virtuous man.<BR> E. वृष a bull,<BR>a rat, or virtue, and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषन्
वृषन् m. (-षा)<BR>	 1. INDRA, as god of the firmament.<BR>	 2. KARṆA, the hero.<BR>3. Pain, sorrow.<BR>	 4. Insensibility from extreme pain.<BR>	 5. A bull.<BR>	 6.<BR>A horse.<BR>	 7. The sign Taurus of the zodiac.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle,<BR>Unādi aff. कनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषनाशन|वृषनाशनः
वृषनाशन m. (-नः) A medicinal plant, commonly Viranga, (Embelia<BR>ribes.)<BR> E. वृष a bull, नाशन destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषपति|वृषपतिः
वृषपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A bull set at liberty.<BR> E. वृष a bull, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषपर्णी
वृषपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR> E. वृष a rat, पर्ण a leaf;<BR>fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषपर्व्वन्|वृषपर्वन्
वृषपर्व्वन् m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Name of a demon.<BR>	 3. A wasp.<BR>	 4. A sort<BR>of grass, (Scripus kysoor.)<BR> E. वृष a bull, &c., पर्व्वन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभ|वृषभः
वृषभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A bull.<BR>	 2. (In composition,) Pre-eminent, excellent.<BR>	 3.<BR>The orifice of the ear.<BR>	 4. An elephant's ear.<BR>	 5. A drug; also<BR>Rishabha, described as a root resembling the horn of a bull, brou-<BR>ght from the Himālaya mountains, of cooling and tonic properties,<BR>and serviceable in catarrh and consumption.<BR>	 6. The first of the<BR>Jaina pontiffs of the present era.<BR>	 7. Any male animal.<BR>	 f. (-भी)<BR>	 1.<BR>A widow.<BR>	 2. Cowach.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle, Unādi aff. अभच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभगति|वृषभगतिः
वृषभगति m. (-तिः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. वृषभ a bull, and गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभध्वज|वृषभध्वजः
वृषभध्वज m. (-जः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. वृषभ a bull, and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभासा
वृषभासा f. (-सा) The capital of INDRA, and the immortals.<BR> E. वृष the bull<BR>of ŚIVA, भास् splendour, and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषय|वृषयः
वृषय m. (-यः) An asylum, a place of refuge or shelter.<BR> E. वृ to screen,<BR>Unādi aff. कयन्, and षुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषल|वृषलः
वृषल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. A Śudra, or man of the servile tribe.<BR>	 3.<BR>The sovereign CHANDRAGUPTA.<BR>	 4. Garlic.<BR>	 5. A sinner, a reprobate,<BR>a wicked or unrighteous man.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A girl twelve years old,<BR>in whom menstruation has commenced, and who is unmarried.<BR>2. A barren woman.<BR>	 3. A woman during menstruation.<BR>	 4. The<BR>mother of a still-born child.<BR>	 5. A woman of a low caste.<BR> E. वृष a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">Page686-a+ 60</a>]<BR>bull, or virtue, &c., and ल to take, aff. क; or वृष् to sprinkle, कलच्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=685-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलक|वृषलकः
वृषलक m. (-कः) A contemptible Śudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलत्व
वृषलत्व n. (-त्वं) The condition or state of a Śudra.<BR> E. त्व added to वृषल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलात्मज|वृषलात्मजः
वृषलात्मज m. (-जः) The son of a reprobate.<BR> E. वृषल a wicked man, आत्मज<BR>son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलीसेवन
वृषलीसेवन n. (-नं) Intercourse with a Śudra female.<BR> E. वृषली, सेवन frequenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलोचन|वृषलोचनः
वृषलोचन m. (-नः) A rat.<BR> E. वृष a bull, and लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषवाहन|वृषवाहनः
वृषवाहन m. (-नः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. वृष a bull, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषशत्रु|वृषशत्रुः
वृषशत्रु m. (-त्रुः) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. वृष KARṆA, and शत्रु the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषसृक्की
वृषसृक्की f. (-क्की) A wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषस्पन्ती
वृषस्पन्ती f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A lascivious woman.<BR>	 2. A cow in heat.<BR> E. वृष a man<BR>of a particular class, or a bull, forming with the increments सुक्,<BR>and क्यच् a nominal verb, implying desire of such a man, &c.,<BR>participal aff. of the present tense शतृ, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाकपायी
वृषाकपायी f. (-यी)<BR>	 1. The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. GAURĪ.<BR>	 3. SWĀHĀ, the<BR>wife of AGNI.<BR>	 4. ŚACHĪ, the wife of INDRA.<BR>	 5. A shrub, (Asparagus<BR>racemosus.)<BR>	 6. A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR> E. वृषाकपि VIṢṆU, &c.,<BR>ङीष् aff., and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाकपि|वृषाकपिः
वृषाकपि m. (-पिः)<BR>	 1. KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. AGNI, or fire.<BR>4. INDRA.<BR> E. वृष virtue, अ not, कपि to shake or agitate, इ aff., and<BR>the radical augment rejected; or वृषा INDRA, अकपि untrembling,<BR>as before; or वृष virtue, or वृषा INDRA, and कपि an ape, being the<BR>ape as it were of the greater gods: other etymologies occur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाङ्क|वृषांक|वृषाङ्कः
वृषाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A pious man.<BR>	 3. Marking-nut plant.<BR>	 4.<BR>An eunuch, one employed in the zenana.<BR> E. वृष the bull of the<BR>deity, or virtue, and अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाङ्कज|वृषांकज|वृषाङ्कजः
वृषाङ्कज m. (-जः) A very small drum, held in one hand, and played by<BR>means of a string attached to it.<BR> E. वृषाङ्क ŚIVA, ज born, made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाञ्चन|वृषांचन|वृषाञ्चनः
वृषाञ्चन m. (-नः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. वृष a bull, and अञ्चन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाणक|वृषाणकः
वृषाणक m. (-कः) A form of ŚIVA.<BR> E. वृष a bull, अन् to be, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषान्तक|वृषान्तकः
वृषान्तक m. (-कः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. वृष virtue, अन्त end, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषायण|वृषायणः
वृषायण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A sparrow.<BR>	 2. An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाहार|वृषाहारः
वृषाहार m. (-रः) A cat.<BR> E. वृष a rat, and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषिन्
वृषिन् m. (-षी) A peacock.<BR> E. वृष his plumage, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृ
वृ(वृ)षी f. (-षिः or षी) The seat or cushion of an ascetic; also वृसी. E.<BR>वृष, कि or ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषोत्सर्ग|वृषोत्सर्गः
वृषोत्सर्ग m. (-र्गः) Setting a bull at liberty on occasion of a sacrifice or<BR>obsequial oblation.<BR> E. वृष, and उत्सर्ग letting loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्ट
वृष्ट f. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. Rained.<BR>	 2. Showering, pouring down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टि|वृष्टिः
वृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Rain.<BR>	 2. A shower in general.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिकर
वृष्टिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Raining, sprinkling.<BR> E. वृष्टि, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिकाल|वृष्टिकालः
वृष्टिकाल m. (-लः) The rainy season.<BR> E. वृष्टि, काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिघ्नी
वृष्टिघ्नी f. (-घ्नी) Guzeratty cardamoms.<BR> E. वृष्टि rain, घ्न destructive, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिजीवन|वृष्टिजीवनः
वृष्टिजीवन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Nourished or watered by rain, (as a country.)<BR>E. वृष्टि rain, जीवन living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिभू
वृष्टिभू m. (-भूः) A frog.<BR> E. वृष्टि rain, and भू being, or being born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिमत्|वृष्टिमन्त्
वृष्टिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Rainy, full of rain.<BR>	 m. (-मान्) A cloud. E.<BR>वृष्टि, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्णि|वृष्णिः
वृष्णि mfn. (-ष्णिः-ष्णिः-ष्णि)<BR>	 1. Heretical, heterodox.<BR>	 2. Angry, passionate.<BR>m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A ram.<BR>	 2. One of the descendants of YADU.<BR>	 3.<BR>VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 4. A heretic, a sectary.<BR>	 5. A ray of light.<BR>6. INDRA.<BR>	 7. AGNI.<BR>	 8. Air or wind.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle, Unādi aff.<BR>नि, and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्य|वृष्यं|वृष्यः
वृष्य mfn. (-ष्यः-ष्या-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Errhine, aphrodisiac, provocative, (food or<BR>medicine.)<BR>	 2. Provocative of sexual vigour.<BR>	 3. To be sprinkled or<BR>aspersed.<BR>	 m. (-ष्यः) Kidney-bean, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्या)<BR>A drug, commonly Riddhi.<BR> E. वृष् to sprinkle, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्यगन्धा
वृष्यगन्धा f. (-न्धा) A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृह्
वृह् r. 1st cl. (वर्हति) also (इ)वृहि(वृंहति) 1. To grow or increase.<BR>	 2. (In<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">Page686-b+ 60</a>]<BR>the second form only,) To roar, as a wild beast. (वृंहते) To grow,<BR>&c. r. 1st and 10th cls. (वृंहति वृंहयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To<BR>shine. (ऊ) वृहू r. 6th cl. (वृहति) To make any effort or exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहच्चित्त|वृहच्चित्तः
वृहच्चित्त m. (-त्तः) A citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहच्छरीर
वृहच्छरीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Large-bodied, gigantic.<BR> E. वृहत्, and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहच्छल्क|वृहच्छल्कः
वृहच्छल्क m. (-ल्कः) A prawn.<BR> E. वृहत् great, and शल्क scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहज्जन
वृहज्जन m. (-नः) A great or illustrious man.<BR> E. वृहत्, and जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहढक्का
वृहढक्का f. (-क्का) A large drum.<BR> E. वृहत् large, ढक्का a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्|वृहन्त्
वृहत् mfn. (-हन्-हती-हत्)<BR>	 1. Great, large.<BR>	 2. Great, much.<BR>	 f. (-हती)<BR>	 1.<BR>A small kind of egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>prickly nightshade, (Solanum hirsutum.)<BR>	 3. A large lute.<BR>	 4. A<BR>form of metre, the stanza of which consists of thirty-six syllables.<BR>5. A mantle, a wrapper.<BR>	 6. A reservoir, a place containing water.<BR>7. Speech.<BR> E. वृह् to grow or increase, Unādi aff. अति, with the<BR>effect of the participial aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहतिका
वृहतिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An upper garment, a mantle, a wrapper.<BR>	 2. A small<BR>sort of egg-plant.<BR> E. वृहती as above, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहतीपति|वृहतीपतिः
वृहतीपति m. (-तिः) VRIHASPATĪ, the preceptor of the gods.<BR> E. वृहती<BR>speech, eloquence, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्क|वृहत्कः
वृहत्क mfn. (-त्कः-त्का-त्कं) Large, great.<BR> E. वृहत् the same, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्कन्द|वृहत्कन्दः
वृहत्कन्द m. (-न्दः) A bulbous root, considered in some place as a large<BR>kind of onion, in others as a sort of garlic.<BR> E. वृहत् large, कन्द a<BR>root. “गृञ्जने ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्काय
वृहत्काय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Large-bodied, bulky, gigantic.<BR> E. वृहत्, काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्कालशाक|वृहत्कालशाकः
वृहत्कालशाक m. (-कः) A shrub, (Cassia purpurea, or a large variety of<BR>it.) “वडकालकासुन्दे.”<BR> E. वृहत् large, and कालशाक the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्काश|वृहत्काशः
वृहत्काश n. (-शं) A large kind of the grass Kāsa, (Saccharum spon-<BR>taneum.) “खागडा.”<BR> E. वृहत् large, काश the grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्कुक्षि|वृहत्कुक्षिः
वृहत्कुक्षि mfn. (-क्षिः-क्षिः or क्षी-क्षि) Corpulent, large or pot-bellied.<BR> E. वृहत्,<BR>कुक्षि the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्तृण|वृहत्तृणः
वृहत्तृण m. (-णः) The bamboo.<BR> E. वृहत् large, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्त्वच्
वृहत्त्वच् m. (-त्त्वक्) A plant, (Echites scholaris.) “छातियान्.”<BR> E. वृहत्, त्त्वच्<BR>skin or bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्पाटलि|वृहत्पाटलिः
वृहत्पाटलि f. (-लिः) Thorn-apple, (Dhutura metel.)<BR> E. वृहत् large, पाटलि the Bignonia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्पाद|वृहत्पादः
वृहत्पाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Large-footed.<BR>	 m. (-दः) The Indian-fig tree. E.<BR>वृहत्, पाद foot or root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहत्पुष्प
वृहत्पुष्प mfn. (-ष्पः-ष्पा-ष्पं) Having large flowers.<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी) Crotolaria of<BR>various species.<BR> E. वृहत् large, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहदङ्ग|वृहदङ्गः
वृहदङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Large-bodied, bulky.<BR>	 2. Large-limbed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Having many parts.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) A large elephant, such a one as is<BR>usually the leader of a wild herd.<BR> E. वृहत् large, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहदम्ल|वृहदम्लः
वृहदम्ल m. (-म्लः) A fruit tree, (Averrhoa carambola.) “कामराङ्गा”<BR> E. वृहत्,<BR>much, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहदसृङ्मति
वृहदसृङ्मति m. (-तिः) An evil spirit, a goblin.<BR> E. वृहत् large, असृक् blood,<BR>मति inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्गुह
वृहद्गुह m. (-हः) A country, described as lying behind the Vindhya<BR>mountains, near the province of Malwa, and perhaps comprising<BR>Bundelkhund, or the adjoining district.<BR> E. वृहत् large, गुह a house;<BR>also वृहद्गुह from गुह a cave, the country being mountainous, and<BR>the people probably having been Troglodytes or dwellers in caves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्गोल|वृहद्गोलं
वृहद्गोल n. (-लं) A water-melon. “तरमुज्”.<BR> E. वृहत्, गोल a ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहदद्युति
वृहदद्युति f. (-तिः) Radiance, splendour, a great light.<BR> E. वृहत्, द्युति<BR>light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्धल|वृहद्धलं
वृहद्धल n. (-लं) The furrow made by a plough.<BR> E. वृहत् large, हल a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्भट्टारिका
वृहद्भट्टारिका f. (-का) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. वृहत्, भट्टारिका princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्भानु|वृहद्भानुः
वृहद्भानु m. (-नुः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. वृहत् large, many, भानु a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्रथ|वृहद्रथः
वृहद्रथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. A sacrificial vessel.<BR>	 3. A particular Man-<BR>tra.<BR>	 4. A division of the Sāma Veda.<BR>	 f. (-थी) The name of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्रावी
वृहद्रावी f. (-वी) A small owl.<BR> E. वृहत् great, much, राव cry, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्वात|वृहद्वातः
वृहद्वात m. (-तः) A grain, generally eaten by the natives of India,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">Page687-a+ 60</a>]<BR>(Andropogon sorghum.) “देधान.”<BR> E. वृहत् much, and वात wind,<BR>supposed to generate this humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=686-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहद्वीज|वृहद्वीजः
वृहद्वीज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Having much or large seed.<BR>	 m. (-जः) The hog-<BR>plum, (Spendias mangifera.) “आम्रातके.”<BR> E. वृहत् large, वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहन्नल|वृहन्नलः
वृहन्नल m. (-लः) A large sort of reed, (Arundo gigantea.)<BR>	 f. (-ला) The<BR>name assumed by ARJUNA when residing at the palace of<BR>VĪRĀTA.<BR>	 3. The arm.<BR> E. वृह large, नल a reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहन्निवेश
वृहन्निवेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Large, bulky, protuberant.<BR> E. वृहत् and निवेश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहस्पति|वृहस्पतिः
वृहस्पति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The regent of the planet JUPITER, identified astro-<BR>nomically with the plant: in Mythology, he is the son of ĀNGI-<BR>RAS, and preceptor of the gods.<BR>	 2. The name of a saint and law-<BR>giver.<BR> E. वृहत् great, illustrious, (as the deities,) and पति master or<BR>Guru, सुट् augment, and the final of the first member rejected; it<BR>also occasionally occurs वृहत्तांपति; or वृहत्याः वाचः पतिः पृषो० नि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहस्पतिचक्र|वृहस्पतिचक्रं
वृहस्पतिचक्र n. (-क्रं) The cycle of 60 years.<BR> E. वृहस्पति, and चक्र a cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वॄ
वॄ r. 9th cl. (वृणाति)<BR>	 1. To choose.<BR>	 2. To support or nourish, (in this<BR>sense it is more usually written with the labial initial.) (ञ) वृञ् r.<BR>9th cl. (वृणाति, वृणीते)<BR>	 1. To choose, to elect or select.<BR>	 2. To cover,<BR>to screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वे
वे r. 1st cl. (वयति वयते) To weave. Caus. (वाययति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sew.<BR>	 2. To<BR>make, to compose. With प्र, 1. To set, to fix.<BR>	 2. To tie, to fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेकट|वेकटः
वेकट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A youth, an adolescent.<BR>	 2. A sort of fish, (perhaps<BR>the common Bhetkī.)<BR>	 3. A jeweller.<BR>	 4. An actor, a buffoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेग|वेगः
वेग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Speed, dispatch, velocity.<BR>	 2. Impetus, momentum.<BR>	 3.<BR>Stream, current.<BR>	 4. Sudden impulse, transition of mind, as from<BR>passion to apathy, &c.<BR>	 5. Determination, promptitude, energy,<BR>that effect of mind which is considered as the source of action.<BR>	 6.<BR>Pleasure, delight.<BR>	 7. Love, the sentiment or passion.<BR>	 8. External<BR>indication of any internal effect, proceeding from passion, medi-<BR>cine, poison, &c, as convulsion, horripilation, sweat, &c.<BR>	 9.<BR>Expulsion or evacuation of the natural excretions.<BR>	 10. Semen virile.<BR>11. The flight of an arrow.<BR>	 12. The fruit of a kind of mango. E.<BR>विज् to tremble, &c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगतस्
वेगतस् Ind. Quickly, speedily.<BR> E. वेग, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगनाशन|वेगनाशनः
वेगनाशन m. (-नः) Phlegm, the phlegmatic humour.<BR> E. वेग activity or<BR>speed, and नाशन injuring, inducing corpulency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगरोध|वेगरोधः
वेगरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Check, remora.<BR>	 2. Obstruction of the natural excre-<BR>tions.<BR> E. वेग, and रोध hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगवत्|वेगवन्त्
वेगवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Quick, expeditious.<BR>	 2. Agitated.<BR> E. वेग, and<BR>मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगवत्तर
वेगवत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Very quick.<BR>	 f. (-री) A species of metre, having<BR>nine syllables for the first and third pādas, and eleven for the se-<BR>cond and fourth.<BR> E. वेगवत्, and तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगवत्तम
वेगवत्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Very quick or swift.<BR> E. वेगवत्, and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगविधारण
वेगविधारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Stopping, retarding.<BR>	 2. Constipation, &c.<BR> E. वेग,<BR>and विधारण withholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगसर|वेगसरः
वेगसर m. (-रः) A mule.<BR> E. वेग speed, सर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगाघात|वेगाघातः
वेगाघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Stop, check.<BR>	 2. Obstruction of the natural excre-<BR>tions.<BR> E. वेग, and आघात resistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगानिल|वेगानिलः
वेगानिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Breeze caused by velocity.<BR>	 2. Violent gust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगित|वेगितः
वेगित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Quickened, expedited.<BR> E. वीज् to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगिता
वेगिता f. (-ता) Speed, quickness.<BR> E. तल् added to the next; also वेगित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगिन्
वेगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Swift, fleet, rapid.<BR>	 m. (-गी)<BR>	 1. A courier, an<BR>express.<BR>	 2. A hawk.<BR>	 f. (-गिनी) A river.<BR> E. वेग, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेचा
वेचा f. (-चा) Hire, wages.<BR> E. विच् to distinguish, aff. अच् or अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेजानी
वेजानी f. (-नी) A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.) “सोमराज्याम्”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेटा
वेटा f. (-टा) The abode of the Vaiśya tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेडा
वेडा f. (-डा) A boat.<BR> E. विड् to curse, aff. अच्, and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेण्
वेण्(ऋ)वेणृ r. 1st cl. (वेणति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To know.<BR>	 3. To<BR>reflect or remember.<BR>	 4. To discern.<BR>	 5. To hold or take a musical<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">Page687-b+ 60</a>]<BR>instrument.<BR>	 6. To play on an instrument.<BR>	 7. To take. The root is<BR>also read वेन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेण|वेणः
वेण m. (-णः) A musician, one by birth the son of a woman of the<BR>Ambaṣṭha and man of the Vaideha caste.<BR> E. वेण् to play on a<BR>musical instrument, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणि|वेणिः
वेणि f. (-णिः-णी) Unornamented and braided hair; the hair as worn<BR>especially by widows and woman whose husbands are absent,<BR>when it is simply collected from the forehead and temples as well<BR>as the back of the head, and twisted together into a single braid,<BR>which is when suffered to fall like a tail down the back, no sort of<BR>ornament being worn on the head; the term is also applied gene-<BR>rally to any braid of hair, or to a braid of the long hair, of which<BR>many are made, and the whole are then twisted together, and<BR>worn as a sort of rose or flower at the back of the head.<BR>	 f. (-णिः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Assemblage of water, as the conflux of rivers, &c., in that case it<BR>rather implies their parallel course, ending in a common point of<BR>union; as at Allāhābād, where the GANGĀ, YAMUNĀ, and as is<BR>supposed, the SARASWATĪ, all coming from the north, unite; this<BR>and other similar places, thence receive the name of Trivenī.<BR>	 2.<BR>Weaving.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Stream, current.<BR>	 2. A ewe.<BR>	 3. A sort of<BR>grass, (Andropogon serratum.)<BR> E. वी to go, Unādi aff. नि, and<BR>in some cases ङीप् added; or वेण-इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिका
वेणिका f. (-का) Braided hair.<BR> E. वेणी as above, कन् fem. form, added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिवेधनी
वेणिवेधनी f. (-नी) A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणीर|वेणीरः
वेणीर m. (-रः) The soap-berry, (Sapindus detergens.)<BR> E. वेण-इरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणु|वेणुः
वेणु m. (-णुः)<BR>	 1. A bamboo.<BR>	 2. A flute.<BR>	 3. A king so named.<BR> E. वी substi-<BR>tuted for अज् to go, aff. नु, or वन् to sound, कु aff.; or वेण्-उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुक|वेणुकं|वेणुकः
वेणुक n. (-कं) A pike used for driving an elephant.<BR> E. वेणु a bamboo,<BR>and कन् aff.; having a bamboo shaft or handle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुकर्क्कर|वेणुकर्कर|वेणुकर्करः
वेणुकर्क्कर m. (-रः) A thorny plant, commonly Karir or Karabira.<BR> E. वेणु<BR>a bamboo, कर्क्वर hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुध्म|वेणुध्मः
वेणुध्म m. (-ध्मः) A player on a fife or flute.<BR> E. वेणु a bamboo, ध्मा to blow, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुनिस्रुति|वेणुनिस्रुतिः
वेणुनिस्रुति m. (-तिः) The sugar-cane.<BR> E. वेणु a bamboo, निस्रुति oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुपत्री
वेणुपत्री f. (-त्री) A plant, one synonym of which, Hingupatri, appears<BR>to relate to the Asafœtida or some similar plant, whilst the cor-<BR>responding compound Bānspatra both in Hindi and Bengali,<BR>is applied to a species of Amaranthus, (A lanceifolius, Rox., or<BR>or A. atro-purpureus, Rox.)<BR> E. वेणु a bamboo, and पत्र a leaf, fem.<BR>aff. ङीष्, having long slender leaves, like those of the bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुवाद|वेणुवादः
वेणुवाद m. (-दः) A player on a flute.<BR> E. वेणु a flute, &c. वाद who sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतन|वेतनं
वेतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Hire, wages.<BR>	 2. Livelihood, subsistence.<BR>	 2. Silver. E.<BR>वी to go, तनन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतनदान
वेतनदान n. (-नं) Hiring, paying wages.<BR> E. वेतन and दान giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतनादान
वेतनादान n. (-नं) Non-payment of wages.<BR> E. वेतन and अदान not giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतस|वेतसः
वेतस mf. (-सः-सी)<BR>	 1. The ratan, (Calamus rotang.)<BR>	 2. The citron. E.<BR>वेञ् to sew or weave, Unādi aff. असच्, तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतसपत्र
वेतसपत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The leaf of the ratan.<BR>	 2. A lancet.<BR> E. वेतस, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेतस्वत्|वेतस्वन्त्
वेतस्वत् mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्) Reedy, abounding in reeds or canes, (a<BR>place or soil, &c.)<BR> E. वेतस् a cane, डवतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेताल|वेतालः
वेताल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A spirit, a goblin, especially one haunting cemeter-<BR>ies and animating dead bodies.<BR>	 2. A doorkeeper.<BR> E. व in the<BR>seventh case वे in air, and ताल habitation, fixation, from तल् to<BR>fix, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्तृ
वेत्तृ mfn. (-त्ता-त्ती-त्तृ)<BR>	 1. Knowing, understanding, acquainted with.<BR>	 2.<BR>Who obtains or acquires.<BR>	 m. (-त्ता)<BR>	 1. A sage, one who knows the<BR>nature of the soul and GOD.<BR>	 2. A husband, an espouser.<BR> E. विद् to<BR>know, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्र|वेत्रः
वेत्र m. (-त्रः) A reed, a cane, the ratan.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं) A stick, a staff.<BR> E. वी to go, Unādi aff. त्रल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रकीय|वेत्रकीयः
वेत्रकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Abounding with reeds or canes.<BR> E. वेत्र a cane,<BR>छ aff., and कुकक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=687-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रधर|वेत्रधरः
वेत्रधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A doorkeeper, a warder.<BR>	 2. A staff bearer, a mace-<BR>bearer.<BR> E. वेत्र a staff, and धर having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रधारक|वेत्रधारकः
वेत्रधारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A doorkeeper, a warder, a porter.<BR>	 2. A mace-<BR>bearer.<BR> E. वेत्र a stick, and धारक having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रवती
वेत्रवती f. (-ती) The Retwa river, which rises in the province of Malwa,<BR>and following a north-easterly direction for about 340 miles, falls<BR>into the Jumna below Calpi.<BR> E. वेत्र a ratan, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रासन|वेत्रासनं
वेत्रासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A small cot or oblong low couch of basket work;<BR>when furnished with bamboo sticks and a pole, it forms the com-<BR>mon Duli or litter.<BR>	 2. A cane-seat.<BR> E. वेत्र a cane, आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेत्रिन्
वेत्रिन् m. (-त्री) A porter, a doorkeeper.<BR> E. वेत्र a stick, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेथ्
वेथ्(ऋ)वेथृ r. 1st cl. (वेथते) To ask or beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद|वेदः
वेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A Veda, the generic term for the sacred writings or<BR>scripture of the Hindus; supposed to have been revealed by<BR>BRAHMĀ, and after being preserved by tradition for a consider-<BR>able period, to have been arranged in the present from by VYĀSA;<BR>the principle Vedas are three in number, the RICH, YAJUS, and<BR>SĀMA, to which a fourth, the ATHARVA, is usually added, and the<BR>ITIHĀSA and PURĀNAS, or ancient history and mythology, are<BR>sometimes considered as a fifth. The Vedas are regarded as a<BR>direct revelation from the deity and are called Śhruti, (what is<BR>heard,) to distinguish them from Smritī or sacred lore of human<BR>origin; the several sages to whom verses or hymns of the Vedas<BR>are ascribed are regarded as seers. (द्रष्टारः) and not as composers,<BR>(स्रष्टारः)<BR>	 2. Metre.<BR>	 3. Gloss, comment, explanation.<BR>	 4. Knowledge.<BR>5. VIṢṆU.<BR> E. विद् to know, (duty and religion from it,) aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदकौलेयक|वेदकौलेयकः
वेदकौलेयक m. (-कः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. वेद the Vedas, and कुल race, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदगर्भ|वेदगर्भः
वेदगर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A Brāhman.<BR> E. वेद the Vedas, and<BR>गर्भ embryo or womb, figuratively for origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदगुप्ति|वेदगुप्तिः
वेदगुप्ति f. (-प्तिः) The preservation of the Vedas by the Brāhmanical<BR>tribe.<BR> E. वेद a Veda, and गुप्ति concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदज्ञ|वेदज्ञः
वेदज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A Brāhman skilled in the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदण्ड|वेदंड|वेदंडः|वेदण्डः
वेदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदतत्त्व
वेदतत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) The true doctrine or substance of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद and तत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदत्रय
वेदत्रय nf. (-यं-यी) The three first Vedas.<BR> E. वेद and त्रय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदन|वेदनं
वेदन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Sensation, perception, knowledge conveyed by the<BR>senses.<BR>	 2. Pain, smart, agony.<BR>	 3. Knowledge.<BR>	 4. The ceremony of<BR>holding the ends of a mantle, to be observed by a Śudra female,<BR>on her marriage with a man of either of the first three classes.<BR>5. Presenting, delivering.<BR>	 6. Acquisition, wealth.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The true<BR>skin or cutis.<BR> E. विद् to know, &c., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनाद
वेदनाद m. (-दः) Sound of chanting or repeating the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, and<BR>नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनिन्दक|वेदनिंदक|वेदनिन्दकः
वेदनिन्दक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An atheist, a disbeliever.<BR>	 2. A Jaina or Bauddha,<BR>or any seceder from the belief of the divine origin and character<BR>of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद scripture, निन्दक defaming, disrespecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनिन्दा|वेदनिंदा
वेदनिन्दा f. (-न्दा) Reviling the Vedas, heresy.<BR> E. वेद, निन्दा blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनीय
वेदनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be known or perceived.<BR>	 2. To be, or to be<BR>made known.<BR> E. विद् to know, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदपारग|वेदपारगः
वेदपारग m. (-गः) A Brāhman skilled in the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, पारग who crosses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदपुण्य
वेदपुण्य n. (-ण्यं) The sanctity of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, and पुण्य holiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदमातृ
वेदमातृ f. (-ता) The mystical prayer or Gāyatrī, personified as the<BR>mother or source of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदमुख्या
वेदमुख्या f. (-ख्या) A sort of insect, the winged-bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदय
वेदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Who or what knows or obtains.<BR> E. विद् to know, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदरक्षण
वेदरक्षण n. (-णं) The conservation of the Vedas, as a duty of the Brāh-<BR>manical order.<BR> E. वेद a Veda, and रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवचन
वेदवचन n. (-नं) A text of the Veda.<BR> E. वेद, and वचन dictum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवाक्य
वेदवाक्य n. (-क्यं) Text of the Veda.<BR> E. वेद, and वाक्य sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवास|वेदवासः
वेदवास m. (-सः) A Brāhman.<BR> E. वेद a Veda, and वास above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदविद्
वेदविद् m. (-विद or वित्) A Brāhman versed in the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद the<BR>Vedas, विद् to know, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदविद्वस्
वेदविद्वस् m. (-द्वान्) A Brāhman learned in the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, विद्वस् a learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदविहित
वेदविहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taught or declared in the Vedas, scriptural.<BR>E. वेद and विहित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवृत्त
वेदवृत्त n. (-त्तं) The doctrine of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, and वृत्त done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदव्यास|वेदव्यासः
वेदव्यास m. (-सः) The Muni VYĀSA.<BR> E. वेद the Vedas, वि and आङ् sever-<BR>ally, before अस् to throw or place, aff. घञ्, the compiler and<BR>arranger of the Vedas; he first collected and arranged the Hindu<BR>scriptures into the four parts, in which they at present exist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदशब्द
वेदशब्द m. (-ब्दः) A word or term in the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, and शब्द a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदशास्त्र
वेदशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) The Vedas or any part of them.<BR> E. वेद, and शास्त्र an<BR>inspired writing, a scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसंहिता
वेदसंहिता f. (-ता) A collection of the formulæ of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, and संहिता a compendium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदस्
वेदस् m. (-दाः) The Vedas collectively.<BR> E. विद् to know, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसन्न्यास|वेदसंन्यास|वेदसंन्यासः
वेदसन्न्यास m. (-सः) Discontinuing the ritual of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, and<BR>सन्न्यास relinquishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसन्न्यासिक|वेदसंन्यासिक
वेदसन्न्यासिक m. (-कः) The religious ascetic or member of the fourth<BR>order, who discontinues the ritual of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, सन्न्यास,<BR>and ठक् aff.; also with इनि, वेदसन्न्यासिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसम्मत|वेदसंमत
वेदसम्मत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Conformable to the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, and सम्मत concurrent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाङ्ग|वेदांग|वेदाङ्गं
वेदाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A sacred science, considered as subordinate to, and in<BR>some sense, a part of the Vedas: six sciences come under this<BR>denomination; ŚIKSHĀ, or the science of pronunciation and articu-<BR>lation; KALPA, the detail of religious ceremonies; VYĀKARAṆA, or<BR>grammar; CHHANDAS, prosody; JYOTISH, or astronomy; and NI-<BR>RUKTĪ, or the explanation of the difficult or obscure words and<BR>phrases that occur in the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद the Vedas, अङ्ग a member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदादिवर्ण
वेदादिवर्ण n. (-र्णं) The mystical name of GOD.<BR> E. वेद the Vedas, आदि first,<BR>and वर्ण letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाधिगम|वेदाधिगमः
वेदाधिगम m. (-मः) Perusal or study of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, अधिगम going over or through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाध्ययन
वेदाध्ययन n. (-नं) Study of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, and अध्ययन reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाध्ययिन्
वेदाध्ययिन् m. (-यी) A student of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद, and अध्ययिन् who reads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाध्यापक|वेदाध्यापकः
वेदाध्यापक m. (-कः) A teacher of the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद and अध्यापक teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाध्यापन
वेदाध्यापन n. (-नं) Teaching the Vedas.<BR> E. वेद and अध्यापन teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्त|वेदांत|वेदान्तः
वेदान्त m. (-न्तः) The theological part of the Vedas; considered collec-<BR>tively it is contained in the many numerous passages or chapters<BR>of the Vedas termed Upanishads, which inculcate an abstract<BR>and speculative monotheistical worship, and these have been fur-<BR>ther explained and illustrated by later writers: the founder of<BR>the school is VYĀSA, and subsequently ŚANKARĀCHĀRYA is its<BR>most eminent teacher.<BR> E. वेद the Vedas, and अन्त end, sum, scope<BR>or substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तग|वेदांतग
वेदान्तग m. (-गः) A Vedāntī.<BR> E. वेदान्त, and ग who goes over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तज्ञ|वेदांतज्ञ
वेदान्तज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A Vedāntī.<BR> E. वेदान्त, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तिन्|वेदांतिन्
वेदान्तिन् m. (-न्ती) A Vedāntī, a follower of the Vedānta philosophy.<BR>E. वेदान्त the theism of the Vedas, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तोपगत
वेदान्तोपगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Derived from or produced by the Vedānta.<BR>E. वेदान्त and उपगत derived from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाभ्यास|वेदाभ्यासः
वेदाभ्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The repetition of the mystical syllable Om.<BR>	 2.<BR>Study of scripture.<BR> E. वेद the Vedas, and अभ्यास exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदार|वेदारः
वेदार m. (-रः) A chameleon, a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदि|वेदिः
वेदि f. (-दिः-दी)<BR>	 1. Ground for placing the vessels used at an oblation,<BR>or for binding the victim, or lighting the sacrificial fire; it is<BR>more or less raised and of various shapes; an alter, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>quadrangular spot in the court-yard of a temple or palace, usually<BR>furnished with a raised floor or seat, and covered with a roof<BR>supported by pillars: see वितर्द्दि.<BR>	 3. A seal-ring.<BR>	 m. (-दिः) A<BR>Pandit, a teacher.<BR>	 f. (-दिः) A name of SARASWATĪ.<BR> E. विद् to know,<BR>&c., Unādi aff. इन्, and ङीष् optionally added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिका
वेदिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A quadrangular open shed in the middle of a court-<BR>yard, erected for various purposes: see वितर्द्दि.<BR>	 2. Ground<BR>prepared for sacrificial ceremonies, a rude kind of altar.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिजा
वेदिजा f. (-जा) DRAUPADĪ.<BR> E. वेदि an alter, and ज born; born from sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदित|वेदितः
वेदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Set forth, represented, made known.<BR> E. विद् to<BR>know, causal from, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदितव्य|वेदितव्यं
वेदितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be known or ascertained.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>made known, to be explained or expounded.<BR> E. विद् to know,<BR>causal form, aff. तव्यर् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदितृ
वेदितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Wise, learned.<BR> E. विद् to know, तृच् aff., with<BR>the augment इट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदित्व
वेदित्व n. (-त्वं) Knowledge, experience.<BR> E. वेदिन् who knows, त्व aff.; also with तल्, वेदिता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिन्
वेदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Who or what knows.<BR>	 m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A Pandit, a<BR>learned Brāhman, a teacher.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 n. (-दि) A plant, (Ciss-<BR>ampelos hexandra.)<BR> E. विद् to know, aff. णिनि or घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदीश|वेदीशः
वेदीश m. (-शः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. वेदी SARASWATĪ, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोक्त|वेदोक्तः
वेदोक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Scriptural, taught or declared in the Vedas.<BR>E. वेद the Vedas, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोदय|वेदोदयः
वेदोदय m. (-यः) ŚURYA, or the sun.<BR> E. वेद the Veda, (the Sāma Veda,)<BR>and उदयं rise, origin; being said to have proceeded from the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोदित|वेदोदितः
वेदोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taught in the Vedas, scriptural.<BR> E. वेद the<BR>Vedas, and उदित spoken, from वद् to speak, with क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोपकरण
वेदोपकरण n. (-णं) A subordinate branch of the study of the Vedas: see<BR>वेदाङ्ग.<BR> E. वेद्, and उपकरण implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद्य|वेद्यं
वेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. To be known or ascertained.<BR>	 2. To be explained<BR>or taught.<BR>	 3. To be married.<BR> E. विद् to know, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेध|वेधः
वेध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Perforation, piercing.<BR>	 2. Wounding.<BR>	 3. A particular<BR>division of time.<BR>	 4. Depth, (in measurement.)<BR> E. व्यध् to pierce, aff.<BR>अच्; or विध्-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधक|वेधकं|वेधकः
वेधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Sharp, piercing, a piercer or perforator.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. Name of a division of hell.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Grain, rice.<BR>in the ear.<BR> E. व्यध् to pierce, aff. वुन्; or विध्-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधन|वेधनं
वेधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Piercing, perforation.<BR>	 2. Depth, (in measurement.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Excavation.<BR>	 4. Wounding.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. An instrument for piercing<BR>an elephant's ear.<BR>	 2. A small gimblet or perforating instrument<BR>used to pierce gems, shells, &c.<BR>	 2. An augre, a gimblet, &c., or<BR>any similar instrument.<BR> E. व्यध् to pierce, ल्युट् aff.; or विध्-ल्युट्-ङीप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधनिका
वेधनिका f. (-का) A small-pointed perforating instrument, used espe-<BR>cially to make holes in jewels, pearls, shells, &c., an augre, an<BR>awl, a gimblet, &c.<BR> E. कन् added to वेधन as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधमुख्यक|वेधमुख्यकः
वेधमुख्यक m. (-कः) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR> E. वेध piercing, (fig-<BR>uratively for pervading as by its odour,) मुख्य principal, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधस्
वेधस् m. (-धाः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A wise or learned man.<BR>	 4.<BR>The sun.<BR>	 5. ŚIVA.<BR>	 6. A kind of Arka-plant.<BR> E. वि before धा to<BR>have, Unādi aff. असि, and वेध substituted for the root and prefix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधस|वेधसं
वेधस n. (-सं) The root of the thumb, considered as sacred to BRAHMĀ.<BR>E. वेधस् BRAHMĀ, अण् added, the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधित|वेधितः
वेधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pierced, perforated.<BR> E. व्यध् to pierce, aff. क्त; or<BR>वेधो जातोऽस्य तार० इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधिन्
वेधिन् mfn. (-धी-धिनी-धि) Piercing, perforating.<BR>	 f. (-धिनी) A leech.<BR> E. व्यध् piercing, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेध्य|वेध्यं
वेध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) To be pierced or perforated.<BR>	 n. (-ध्यं) A mark, a<BR>butt.<BR> E. व्यध् to pierce, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन्
वेन् r. 1st cl. (वेनति-ते) To go, &c.: see वेण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन|वेनः
वेन m. (-नः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. वी substituted for अज् to go, Unādi aff. न ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन्ना
वेन्ना f. (-न्ना) The name of a river.<BR> E. वन् to sound, Unādi aff. न, and<BR>इ with the usual change, substituted for the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेप्
वेप्(टु ऋ)टुवेपृ r. 1st cl. (वेपते) To shake or tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपथु|वेपथुः
वेपथु m. (-थुः) Trembling, tremor.<BR> E. वेप् to tremble, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपन|वेपनं
वेपन n. (-नं) Tremor, trembling.<BR> E. वेप् to tremble, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपमान
वेपमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Trembling, shaking.<BR> E. वेप् to tremble, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपस्
वेपस् n. (-पः) Trembling.<BR> E. वेप् to tremble, aff. असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेम|वेमः
वेम m. (-मः) A loom.<BR> E. वेञ् to weave, aff. मन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेमन्
वेमन् mn. (-मा-म) A loom.<BR> E. वेञ् to weave, मनिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेर|वेरं|वेरः
वेर mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. The egg-plant.<BR>	 3. Saffron.<BR> E. वी to go, रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेरक|वेरकं|वेरकः
वेरक n. (-कं) Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेरट|वेरटः
वेरट m. (-टः) A low man, one of mixed or inferior caste.<BR>	 n. (-टं) The fruit of the Jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्
वेल्(ऋ)वेऌ r. 1st cl. (वेलति)<BR>	 1. To go or move.<BR>	 2. To shake, to tremble.<BR>r. 10th cl. (वेलयति-ते) To count or declare the time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल|वेलं|वेलः
वेल n. (-लं) A garden.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. Tide, flow, current.<BR>	 3. Boun-<BR>dary, limit.<BR>	 4. The sea-shore.<BR>	 5. Easy or sudden death.<BR>	 6. Sickness,<BR>disease.<BR>	 7. The food of ŚIVA.<BR>	 8. Speech.<BR>	 9. Leisure, interval.<BR>10. Season, opportunity.<BR>	 11. The wife of Budha.<BR>	 12. The gums. E.<BR>वेल् to go, aff. अच् and टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेलाकुल
वेलाकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Agitated by the tide.<BR> E. वेला, आकुल perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेलाकूल|वेलाकूलं
वेलाकूल n. (-लं) Tamlūk, the district or kingdom as it formerly existed,<BR>the southern part of the present HŪGLI district, forming the west<BR>bank of the Hūgli river, at its union with the sea: a village called<BR>Beercool, derived from this word probably, is still found in the<BR>maps, near the sea shore immediately south of the boundary of<BR>the Hūgli district.<BR> E. वेला tide, and कूल bank or shore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेलामूल
वेलामूल n. (-लं) The sea-shore.<BR> E. वेला, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेलायाम्
वेलायाम् Ind.<BR>	 1. On the sea-shore, coast-wise, &c.<BR>	 2. Seasonably, oppor-<BR>tunely.<BR> E. वेला a shore, &c., in the seventh case, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्ल्
वेल्ल् r. 1st cl. (वेल्लति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To tremble or shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्ल|वेल्लं|वेल्लः
वेल्ल m. (-ल्लः) Going, moving, shaking.<BR>	 mn. (-ल्लः-ल्लं) A plant, the seed<BR>of which is used as a vermifuge.<BR> E. वेल्ल् to shake, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लज|वेल्लजं
वेल्लज n. (-जं) Black pepper, (Piper nigrum.)<BR> E. वेल्ल shaking, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लन|वेल्लनं
वेल्लन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rolling on the ground, (as a horse.)<BR>	 2. A sort of roll-<BR>ing pin with which cakes, &c. are prepared.<BR>	 3. Shaking.<BR>	 4. Going.<BR>E. वेल्ल् to shake, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लहल|वेल्लहलः
वेल्लहल m. (-लः) A libertine, a debauchee.<BR> E. वेल्लं ह्वलयति-ह्वल्-अच्-पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लि|वेल्लिः
वेल्लि f. (-ल्लिः or ल्ली) A creeping plant.<BR> E. वेल्ल् to shake, aff. इन् or ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लिका
वेल्लिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Bel-Sunṭh.<BR>	 2. A potherb, “इन्दूपोदक्यां” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेल्लित|वेल्लितं|वेल्लितः
वेल्लित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken, trembling, tremulous.<BR>	 2. Crooked.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं)<BR>	 1. Going, moving.<BR>	 2. Shaking.<BR> E. वेल्ल् to shake, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेवी
वेवी r. 2nd cl. (वेवीते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To pervade.<BR>	 3. To conceive or become<BR>pregnant.<BR>	 4. To desire.<BR>	 5. To throw or send.<BR>	 6. To eat; also वी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश|वेशः
वेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Dress, decoration.<BR>	 2. Disguise, masquerade.<BR>	 3. The<BR>abode of harlots.<BR>	 4. Any house.<BR>	 5. Entrance, ingress.<BR> E. विश् to<BR>enter, (liter. or fig., as to enter or occupy the mind,) aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशक|वेशकः
वेशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what enters.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A house.<BR>	 f. (-शिका)<BR>Entrance, ingress.<BR> E. विश् to enter, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशदान|वेशदानः
वेशदान m. (-नः) The sun-flower.<BR> E. वेश ornament, दान gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशधारिन्
वेशधारिन् m. (-री) A hypocrite, a false devotee.<BR> E. वेश disguise, धारिन् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशन|वेशनं
वेशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. Entering.<BR> E. विश् to enter, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशनारी
वेशनारी f. (-री) A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशन्त|वेशंत|वेशंतः|वेशन्तः
वेशन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A basin, a small pond.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR> E. विश् to enter, झच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशभृत्
वेशभृत् mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. Dressed, adorned.<BR>	 2. Disguised.<BR> E. वेश, भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशर|वेशरः
वेशर m. (-रः) A mule; also वेसर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश|वेशः
वेश(स)वार m. (-रः) A condiment, as pepper, cloves, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशिन्
वेशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Assuming a particular dress or form.<BR> E. वेश, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मन्
वेश्मन् n. (-श्म) A house.<BR> E. विश् to enter, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मनकुल|वेश्मनकुलः
वेश्मनकुल m. (-लः) The musk shrew or rat.<BR> E. वेश्म a house, नकुल an ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मभू
वेश्मभू f. (-भूः) The site of a habitation.<BR> E. वेश्म a house, and भू ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्मस्थूणा
वेश्मस्थूणा f. (-णा) The main post of a house.<BR> E. वेश्म, स्थूणा a pillar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्यं|वेश्य
वेश्यं n. (-श्यं) The habitation of harlots.<BR>	 f. (-श्या)<BR>	 1. A harlot, a pros-<BR>titute, a whore.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR> E. विश् to<BR>enter, ण्यत् aff.; or वेश ornament, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्यागण|वेश्यागणः
वेश्यागण m. (-णः) A company of harlots.<BR> E. वेश्या, गण a number, a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्याचार्य्य|वेश्याचार्य|वेश्याचार्यः|वेश्याचार्य्यः
वेश्याचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. A catamite.<BR>	 2. The master or keeper of dancing<BR>girls, prostitutes, &c.<BR> E. वेश्या a whore, आचार्य्य spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्याजनसमाश्रय|वेश्याजनसमाश्रयः
वेश्याजनसमाश्रय m. (-यः) The habitation of harlots, a brothel.<BR> E. वेश्या a<BR>whore, जन people, सम् collective particle, and आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्यावार
वेश्यावार m. (-रः) A number or company of harlots.<BR> E. वेश्या, and वार<BR>assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्याश्रय|वेश्याश्रयः
वेश्याश्रय m. (-यः) A brothel, the habitation of harlots.<BR> E. वेश्या a whore, आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेश्वर|वेश्वरः
वेश्वर m. (-रः) A mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष|वेषः
वेष m. (-षः) Ornament, dress, decoration.<BR> E. विष् to invest, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेषण|वेषणं|वेषणः
वेषण m. (-णः) A shrub, (Cassia sophora.)<BR>	 f. (-णा) A plant, (Flacourtia<BR>cataphracta.)<BR>	 n. (-णं) Entrance, ingress, possession, occupation. E.<BR>विष् to enter, &c., aff. युच् or ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेषवार|वेषवारः
वेषवार m. (-रः) A condiment; also वेसवार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्ट|वेष्टः
वेष्ट r. 1st cl. (वेष्टते)<BR>	 1. To surround, to enclose, to encompass or circle.<BR>2. To dress. With आ, To fold, to from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्ट|वेष्टः
वेष्ट m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. A fence, an enclosure.<BR>	 2. Surrounding, enclosing.<BR>	 3.<BR>A turban.<BR>	 4. Exudation, gum, resin, in general.<BR>	 5. Turpentine. E.<BR>वेष्ट् to surround, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टक|वेष्टकं|वेष्टकः
वेष्टक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Surrounding, a surrounder, that which encom-<BR>passes or encloses.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A turban.<BR>	 2. Exudation, resin gum,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. Turpentine.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A wall, a fence.<BR>	 2. A pumpkin-<BR>gourd.<BR> E. वेष्ट, with कन् added; or वेष्ट् to surround, aff. वुन् or ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टन|वेष्टनं
वेष्टन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>	 2. A wall, an enclosure, a<BR>fence.<BR>	 3. A turban.<BR>	 4. A diadem, a tiara.<BR>	 5. The outer ear, or the<BR>meatus auditorious and the concha.<BR>	 6. A bandage.<BR>	 7. A girdle.<BR>8. An attitude in dancing, a particular disposition of the hands;<BR>also a crossing of the feet.<BR>	 9. Bdellium.<BR> E. वेष्ट्, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टनक|वेष्टनकः
वेष्टनक m. (-कः) A mode of coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टनीय
वेष्टनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be surrounded or encompassed.<BR> E. वेष्ट् to<BR>surround, अनीयर् aff.; also वेष्टितव्य and वेष्ट्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टयित्वा
वेष्टयित्वा Ind. Having bound round or encompassed.<BR> E. वेष्ट् to sur-<BR>round, causal v., क्त्वाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टवंश|वेष्टवंशः
वेष्टवंश m. (-शः) A sort of bamboo, (Bambusa spinosa.)<BR> E. वेष्ट surrounding, वंश a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्टित|वेष्टितं|वेष्टितः
वेष्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Surrounded, encompassed, enclosed.<BR>	 2. Stop-<BR>ped, secured from access.<BR>	 3. Bound round, enveloped, wrapped<BR>up.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Encompassing, encircling.<BR>	 2. One of the gestures or<BR>attitudes of dancing, particular motion of the fingers or a crossing<BR>of the feet.<BR> E. वेष्ट surrounding, इतच् aff.; or वेष्ट् the verb, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेष्य|वेष्यः
वेष्य m. (-ष्यः) Water.<BR> E. विष् to pervade, Unādi aff. य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेस्
वेस्(ऋ)वेसृ r. 1st cl. (वेसति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेसन|वेसनं
वेसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Chick-pea, &c. ground and reduced to powder.<BR>	 2. Going.<BR> E. वेस्-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेसर|वेसरः
वेसर m. (-रः) A mule.<BR> E. वेस-अरन्; also वेशर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेसवार|वेसवारः
वेसवार m. (-रः) A condiment, as ground coriander, mustard, pepper,<BR>spice, &c.<BR> E. विस् to send, aff. घञ्, वेस despatching, वॄ to choose,<BR>aff. अच्; also वेशवार and वेषवार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेह्
वेह्(ऋ)वेहृ r. 1st cl. (वेहते) To resolve or endeavour diligently. Also वेह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेहत्
वेहत् f. (-हत्) A cow miscarrying from taking the bull unseasonably.<BR>E. वि before हन् to kill, (the embryo,) Unādi aff. अति; the radical<BR>final rejected, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेह्ल
वेह्ल r. 1st cl. (वेह्लति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To tremble; also वेल् and वेल्ल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वै
वै(ओ)ओवै r. 1st cl. (वायति)<BR>	 1. To dry, to become dried or withered.<BR>2. To be languid or weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वै
वै Ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of affirmation, (so, indeed.)<BR>	 2. An expletive.<BR>	 3.<BR>A vocative particle.<BR> E. वा to go, aff. डै ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैंशतिक|वैंशतिकः
वैंशतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Purchased with twenty,<BR> E. विंशतिक relating to twenty, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकक्ष|वैकक्षं
वैकक्ष n. (-क्षं)<BR>	 1. A garland worn over one shoulder and under the<BR>other, like the sacrificial thread.<BR>	 2. An upper garment, a wrapper,<BR>a mantle.<BR> E. वि implying “possessed of” or “belonging to,” कक्ष्<BR>the flank. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकक्षक|वैकक्षकं
वैकक्षक n. (-कं) A garland or string of flowers worn as a scarf or like<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">Page690-b+ 60</a>]<BR>the sacrificial cord, over the left shoulder and under the right<BR>arm, hanging down below the hip.<BR> E. कन् added to the last; also<BR>as de rived from वि and कक्ष with ठक् aff. वैकक्षिक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकङ्कत|वैकङ्कतः
वैकङ्कत m. (-तः) A plant, (Flacourtia sapida.)<BR> E. अण् pleo. added to विकङ्कत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकटिक|वैकटिकः
वैकटिक m. (-कः) A jeweller.<BR> E. विकट difficult, (occupation,) ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकर्त्तन|वैकर्तन|वैकर्तनः
वैकर्त्तन m. (-नः) An epithet of KARṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्प|वैकल्पं
वैकल्प n. (-ल्पं)<BR>	 1. Optionality.<BR>	 2. Uncertainty, indecision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्पिक|वैकल्पिकः
वैकल्पिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Doubtful, indeterminate.<BR>	 2. Alternative,<BR>optional.<BR> E. विकल्प and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकल्य|वैकल्यं
वैकल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Lameness, mutilation.<BR>	 2. Deficiency, defect, mutilation.<BR>3. Nonexistence.<BR>	 4. Incompetency, insufficiency.<BR>	 5. Agitation,<BR>flurry.<BR> E. विकल defective, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकारिक|वैकारिकः
वैकारिक f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Relating to change or modification.<BR>	 2. Modified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकाल|वैकालः
वैकाल m. (-लः) Evening, afternoon.<BR> E. वि gone, काल time, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकालिक
वैकालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Occuring in or belonging to the afternoon.<BR>E. विकाल and ठक् aff.; also with खञ्, वैकालीन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकुण्ठ|वैकुंठ|वैकुंठः|वैकुण्ठः
वैकुण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. INDRA.<BR>	 n. (-ण्ठं)<BR>	 1. The para-<BR>dise or world of Vaikuṇṭha or VIṢṆU; its site is variously des-<BR>cribed, either as in the northern ocean, or on the eastern peak of<BR>mount Meru.<BR>	 2. Talc.<BR> E. विकुण्ठा the wife of ŚUBHRA, and mother<BR>of VIṢṆU, in one form, अण् patronymic aff.: other etymologies<BR>occur, as वि privative, &c. and कुण्ठ said to mean destruction, he<BR>who is indestructible; or वि before the same, explained knowledge<BR>or abode, being omniscient or omnipresent, &c.; again वि various,<BR>and कुण्ठ illusion, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृत|वैकृतं|वैकृतः
वैकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Changed, in mind or form.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Aversion,<BR>disgust.<BR>	 2. Change in mind or from.<BR>	 3. An event foreboding evil.<BR>f. (-ती) Hideous, loathsome.<BR> E. विकृत the same, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृतापह
वैकृतापह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Removing or preventing change.<BR> E. वैकृत, अपह<BR>what takes away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृतिक
वैकृतिक f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Changed, modified.<BR>	 2. Belonging to a VIKRITI, (in Śankhya Phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैकृत्य|वैकृत्यं
वैकृत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Changed, in form or mind.<BR>	 n. (-त्यं) Aversion,<BR>disgust.<BR>	 2. Change, alteration.<BR> E. विकृत the same, ष्यञ् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैक्रान्त|वैक्रांत|वैक्रांतं|वैक्रान्तं
वैक्रान्त n. (-न्तं) A kind of gem, said to resemble a diamond, and to be<BR>of similar properties; it is also considered to be a burnt diamond,<BR>and to be the common load-stone or magnet.<BR> E. विक्रान्त a warrior,<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैक्लव्य|वैक्लव्यं
वैक्लव्य n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Confusion, commotion.<BR>	 2. Affiction, grief.<BR> E. विक्लव confused, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैखरी
वैखरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Articulate utterance.<BR>	 2. Speech in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैखानस|वैखानसः
वैखानस m. (-सः) A man of the third religious order, a hermit, an<BR>anchoret.<BR>	 f. (-सी) A vessel used for frying meal to be offered in<BR>sacrifice.<BR>	 f. (-सी) Relating to hermits.<BR> E. वि before खन् to dig,<BR>ड-अन् असुन् कर्म० स्वार्थे अण्, subsisting on roots, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैगुण्य|वैगुण्यं
वैगुण्य n. (-ण्य)<BR>	 1. Absence of attributes or qualities.<BR>	 2. Contrariety of<BR>properties or qualities.<BR>	 3. Inferiority, badness, vileness.<BR>	 4. Fault,<BR>defect.<BR> E. विगुण void of properties or merit, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचक्षण्य|वैचक्षण्यं
वैचक्षण्य n. (-ण्य) Skill, cleverness, proficiency.<BR> E. विचक्षण clever, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचित्य
वैचित्य n. (-त्यं) Confusion of ideas, distraction, grief.<BR> E. विचित्ति wander-<BR>ing, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैचित्र्य|वैचित्र्यं
वैचित्र्य n. (-त्र्यं)<BR>	 1. Variety.<BR>	 2. Surprise.<BR>	 3. Manifoldness.<BR> E. विचित्र astonishing, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजनन|वैजननं|वैजननः
वैजनन n. (-नं) The last month of uterine gestation.<BR> E. वि before जन् to<BR>be born, aff. ल्युट्, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयन्त|वैजयंत|वैजयंतः|वैजयन्तः
वैजयन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. The place of INDRA.<BR>	 2. The banner or emblem of<BR>INDRA.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A flag, a banner, an ensign.<BR>	 2. A small tree,<BR>(Sesbana Ægyptiaca.)<BR>	 3. Another tree, (Premna spinosa, &c.)<BR>	 4.<BR>A kind of garland.<BR>	 5. A necklace.<BR>	 6. The necklace of VIṢṆU. E.<BR>वि before जि to conquer, झञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयन्तिक|वैजयंतिक|वैजयंतिकः|वैजयन्तिकः
वैजयन्तिक m. (-कः) A flag-bearer.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Sesbana Ægyp-<BR>tiaca.)<BR>	 2. A flag, a banner.<BR>	 3. A kind of necklace.<BR> E. वैजयन्ती a<BR>flag, with ठक् aff or कन् pleonasm, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजयि|वैजयिः
वैजयि m. (-यिः) The third Chakravartī or emperor according to the<BR>Jainas.<BR> E. विजया a proper name, and इञ् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजात्य|वैजात्यं
वैजात्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Difference or deviation from ordinary character or<BR>conduct.<BR>	 2. Exclusion from caste.<BR>	 3. Difference of caste or species.<BR>4. Looseness, wantonness.<BR> E. वि before जाति species, &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैजिक|वैजिकं|वैजिकः
वैजिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Seminal, relating to seed or origin.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Cause, origin, motive.<BR>	 2. Oil prepared from the Śigru or Morunga.<BR>3. The spiritual cause of existence, soul, spirit.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A young<BR>shoot.<BR> E. वीज seed, ठञ् or ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैज्ञानिक|वैज्ञानिकः
वैज्ञानिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Skilful, clever, proficient.<BR> E. विज्ञान knowledge, &c., aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैडालव्रतिक|वैडालव्रतिकः
वैडालव्रतिक m. (-कः) A hypocrite, a religious impostor, one who under<BR>the appearance of piety and virtue is covetous, malicious, and<BR>cruel.<BR> E. विडाल a cat, व्रत observance, and ठन् aff.; acting like a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैण|वैणः
वैण m. (-णः) A cutter of bamboos, a worker in bamboo-work.<BR> E. वेणु a<BR>bamboo, अण् aff., and the primitive final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणव|वैणवं|वैणवः
वैणव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Produced by or made of a bamboo.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>bamboo staff.<BR>	 2. A worker in bamboo or wicker-work.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>Bamboo-seed.<BR>	 f. (-वी) Bamboo-manna.<BR> E. वेणु a bamboo, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणविक|वैणविकः
वैणविक m. (-कः) A player on a flute.<BR> E. वेणु a pipe, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणिक|वैणिकः
वैणिक m. (-कः) A lutanist, a player on a Vinā.<BR> E. वीणा the Vinā, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणुक|वैणुकं|वैणुकः
वैणुक n. (-कं) A goad or bamboo-pike headed with iron, used to drive an<BR>elephant.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A player on a pipe or flute.<BR> E. वेणु a flute, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैणुकेय
वैणुकेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Relating or belonging to a bamboo, &c.<BR> E. वेणु a<BR>bamboo, and छण् aff., with कुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैण्य|वैण्यः
वैण्य m. (-ण्यः) A name of PṚTHU, the fifth sovereign of the solar race.<BR>E. वेण the father of this monarch, and यञ् aff.; also read वैन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतंसिक|वैतंसिकः
वैतंसिक m. (-कः) A vendor of the flesh or meat, either of beasts or birds<BR>E. वीतंस a snare or net, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतण्डिक|वैतंडिक|वैतंडिकः|वैतण्डिकः
वैतण्डिक m. (-कः) A disputatious man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतनिक|वैतनिकः
वैतनिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A hireling, a hired labourer.<BR>	 2. A stipendiary.<BR> E. वेतन wages, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतरणि|वैतरणिः
वैतरणि f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>	 1. The river of hell.<BR>	 2. Name of a river in the<BR>KALINGAS.<BR>	 3. The mother of the Rākshasas.<BR> E. वि various, तरण<BR>crossing, aff. इञ् or अण्, and ङीष् aff.; or वि prohibitive, तरणी<BR>crossing; or वितरण giving, (liberality in life securing a passage;)<BR>or वि priv., तरणी a boat, passed without a boat; the aff. is same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतस|वैतसः
वैतस m. (-सः) A sort of cane, (Calamus fasciculatus.)<BR>	 f. (-सी)<BR>	 1. Per-<BR>taining to the cane.<BR>	 2. Humble yielding.<BR> E. वेतस, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतान
वैतान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sacrificial, (as fire.)<BR>	 n. (-नं) Oblation with fire. E.<BR>वितान the hole in the hearth in which sacred fire is kept, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतानिक|वैतानिकः
वैतानिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Sacrificial, sacred, (as fire.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) Burnt-<BR>offering, especially of clarified butter, as presented daily by the<BR>Brāhmans.<BR> E. वितान the hearth, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतानोपासना
वैतानोपासना f. (-ना) The regular presentation of burnt-offering morning<BR>and evening.<BR> E. वैतान sacrificial, (fire,) and उपासना service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतालिक|वैतालिकः
वैतालिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A bard whose duty it is to awaken a chief or<BR>prince at dawn with music and song.<BR>	 2. A singer out of tune.<BR>	 3.<BR>One who has a demon for a familiar, the servant of a Vetāla.<BR> E. वि<BR>privative, &c., ताल tune, अण् aff., and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैतालीय
वैतालीय m. (-यः) A kind of metre, or tetrastich, the first and third<BR>lines of which contain the time of fourteen short syllables, and<BR>the second and fourth of sixteen; it admits of some varieties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैत्रक|वैत्रकः
वैत्रक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Cany, reedy, relating to a cane, &c.<BR> E. वेत्र cane,<BR>छण् aff. with कुक् aug.; the final of the aff. rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैत्रकीय|वैत्रकीयः
वैत्रकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating to a stick or cane.<BR> E. वेत्र a stick, छण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद|वैदः
वैद mfn. (-दः-दी-दं) Relating to or connected with a wise man, learned,<BR>knowing.<BR> E. विद् who knows. अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदग्ध|वैदग्धं
वैदग्ध n. (-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Cleverness, skill, dexterity.<BR>	 2. Acuteness, sharpness.<BR>3. Craft, cunning.<BR> E. विदग्ध clever, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदग्व्य
वैदग्व्य nf. (-ग्ध्य-ग्धी)<BR>	 1. Cunning, craft.<BR>	 2. Cleverness, dexterity, skill.<BR>2. Knowingness, sharpness, wit.<BR> E. विदग्ध clever, sharp, aff. ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदर्भ|वैदर्भं|वैदर्भः
वैदर्भ n. (-र्भं) Crafty or indirect speech.<BR>	 m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. The sovereign of<BR>VIDARBHA, the father of DAMAYANTĪ, &c.<BR>	 2. Gum-boil, f. (-र्भी)<BR>1. The law of VIDARBHA, as one by which cousins german were<BR>allowed to intermarry in that country, &c.<BR>	 2. The wife of<BR>AGASTYA.<BR>	 3. DAMAYANTĪ, the wife of NALA.<BR>	 4. RUKMINĪ; one of<BR>KṚṢṆA'S wives.<BR>	 3. A particular style of composition.<BR> E. विदर्भ<BR>the country so named. and अण् aff. of derivation or production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदल|वैदलं|वैदलः
वैदल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Wicker, of cane, wicker or basket work.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>1. A shallow cup or saucer made of clay usually, though some-<BR>times of metal, and sometimes of wood or wicker.<BR>	 2. Any seat<BR>or vessel of basket or wicker-work.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A flat unleavened<BR>cake, made of flour, &c., with cumin or coriander seeds, and<BR>fried in Ghee.<BR>	 2. Any leguminous vegetable or grain, as peas,<BR>beans, &c.<BR> E. वि before दल् to divide, aff. अच्, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदिक|वैदिकः
वैदिक mfn. (-कः-की or का-कं) Scriptural, derived from or conformable<BR>to the Vedas.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A Brāhman well-versed in the Vedas. E.<BR>वेद, and ठञ् or जिठ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदिकत्व
वैदिकत्व n. (-त्वं) Scriptural character or origin.<BR> E. वैदिक relating to the<BR>Vedas, and त्व aff. of the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदिकपाश|वैदिकपाशः
वैदिकपाश m. (-शः) One who possesses only a smattering knowledge of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदुषी
वैदुषी f. (-षी) Learning, wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदुष्य|वैदुष्यं
वैदुष्य nf. (-ष्यं-षी) Learning, sapience.<BR> E. विद्वस् a learned man, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदूर्य्य|वैदूर्य|वैदूर्य्यं
वैदूर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) A gem of a dark colour, the lapis lazuli.<BR> E. विदूर said to<BR>be the name of a mountain where the stone is found, or a city<BR>where it is polished, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेशिक|वैदेशिकः
वैदेशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Foreign, stranger.<BR> E. विदेश, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेश्य|वैदेश्यं
वैदेश्य n. (-श्य) Foreignness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेह|वैदेहः
वैदेह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A trader by caste or profession.<BR>	 2. An attendant on<BR>the women's apartments: see the next.<BR>	 f. (-ही)<BR>	 1. ŚITĀ, the<BR>daughter of JANAKA.<BR>	 2. Long-pepper.<BR>	 3. The wife of a trader or<BR>woman of the Vaideha caste.<BR>	 4. A sort of pigment, commonly<BR>Rochanā.<BR> E. विदेह the country, अण् aff. of origin or production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैदेहक|वैदेहकः
वैदेहक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A trader by profession.<BR>	 2. A man of a mixed caste,<BR>the offspring of a Vaiśya father and Brāhman mother, whose<BR>business is attendance in the women's apartments.<BR> E. विदेह the<BR>country, वुञ्. aff.; or वि various, दिह् to collect, (goods, &c.,) aff. ण्वुल्<BR>and अण् added; or विदेह a king, the supposed author of rules for<BR>merchants, वुञ् aff., or with अण् aff. and ठक् added वैदेहिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्य|वैद्यः
वैद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्यी-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Medical, practising or relating to medicine.<BR>	 2.<BR>Relating or conformable to the Vedas.<BR>	 m. (-द्यः)<BR>	 1. A physician.<BR>	 2.<BR>A tree, (Justicia ganderussa, &c.)<BR>	 3. A learned man.<BR>	 4. A follower<BR>of the Vedas, or one well in them.<BR>	 5. A man of a mixed class,<BR>the offspring of a Brāhmana by a Vaiśya woman.<BR>	 f. (-द्या) A<BR>drug, commonly KĀKOLĪ.<BR> E. वेद the medical or Āyur-Vedas or<BR>the Vedas in general, and यञ् or ष्यञ् aff.; or विद्याऽस्त्यस्य अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यक|वैद्यकं|वैद्यकः
वैद्यक m. (-कः) A physician.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The science of medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यक्रिया
वैद्यक्रिया f. (-या) The practice of medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यनाथ|वैद्यनाथः
वैद्यनाथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. DHANWANTARĪ.<BR> E. वैद्य a physician, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यबन्धु|वैद्यबन्धुः
वैद्यबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) Cassia fistula.<BR> E. वेद्य a physician, बन्धु the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यमातृ
वैद्यमातृ f. (-ता) A plant, (Justicia ganderussa.) “वासके”.<BR> E. वैद्य a physi-<BR>cian, and मातृ mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्यसिंही
वैद्यसिही f. (-ही) A plant, (Justicia ganderussa.)<BR> E. वैद्य medical, सिंह pre-eminent, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैद्युत
वैद्युत f. (-ती) Proceeding from lightning, electric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैध|वैधः
वैध mfn. (-धः-धी-धं) According to rule, preceptive, ritual.<BR> E. विधि, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधर्म्म्य
वैधर्म्म्य n. (-र्म्म्यं)<BR>	 1. Irreligion, injustice, impropriety.<BR>	 2. Difference of<BR>duty or obligation.<BR>	 3. Difference of characteristic qualities.<BR> E. वि<BR>before धर्म्म virtue, &c. ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधवेय|वैधवेयः
वैधवेय m. (-यः) The son of a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वधव्य
वधव्य n. (-व्यं) Widowhood.<BR> E. विधवा, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधात्र|वैधात्रः
वैधात्र m. (-त्रः) SANATKUMĀRA, the son of BRAHMĀ, and eldest of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">Page692-a+ 60</a>]<BR>progenitors of mankind.<BR> E. विधातृ BRAHMĀ, and अण् aff. of descent;<BR>it is applicable also to the other three sons of the same deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधिक
वैधिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Ritual, according to rule, &c.<BR> E. विधि, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधुर्य्य|वैधुर्य|वैधुर्यं
वैधुर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Agitation, tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैधेय|वैधेयः
वैधेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Foolish, ignorant, an idiot, a fool.<BR>	 2. Pres-<BR>cribed.<BR> E. विधेय performance of religious ceremonials, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैध्यत|वैध्यतः
वैध्यत m. (-तः) YAMA'S porter or chamberlain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैध्रातक
वैध्रातक n. (-कं) A vessel for holding or pouring ghee, used at sacrifices with fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनतेय|वैनतेयः
वैनतेय m. (-यः) GARUḌA or ARUṆA.<BR> E. विनता their mother, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनयिक|वैनयिकः
वैनयिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Ralating to morals or behaviour.<BR>	 2. Enfor-<BR>cing proper conduct.<BR>	 3. Magisterial.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A chariot used<BR>formerly in battle, a war-carriage.<BR> E. विनय, and ठक् aff.; or in the<BR>latter sense, वि before णी to get, अण् aff., and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनायिक|वैनायिकः
वैनायिक m. (-कः) A Bauddha, a follower of Buddha or a doctrine<BR>of that sect.<BR> E. विनायक a Buddha or teacher of this sect, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनाशिक|वैनाशिकं|वैनाशिकः
वैनाशिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A dependent, a subject, a slave.<BR>	 2. A spider.<BR>	 3.<BR>An astrologer.<BR> E. विनाश loss, destruction, aff. ठक् or ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैनीतक|वैनीतकः
वैनीतक mn. (-कः-क)<BR>	 1. A mediate conveyance, as a proter carrying a<BR>letter, a horse dragging a chariot, &c.<BR> E. वि variously, णी to take,<BR>aff. क्त, with कन् and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैपरीत्य|वैपरीत्यं
वैपरीत्य n. (-त्यं) Contrariety, opposition, reverse.<BR> E. विपरीत contrary, aff. ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैपुल्य|वैपुल्यं
वैपुल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Abundance, plenty.<BR>	 2. Largeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैफल्य|वैफल्यं
वैफल्य n. (-ल्यं) Fruitlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैबोधिक|वैबोधिकः
वैबोधिक m. (-कः) A watchman, a bell-man, one who announces the<BR>hours.<BR> E. विबोध awakening, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभव|वैभवं
वैभव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Grandour, wealth.<BR>	 2. Power.<BR> E. विभव and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभाजित्र|वैभाजित्रं
वैभाजित्र n. (-त्रं) Apportioning, dividing.<BR> E. विभाजयितृ one who makes a<BR>division or causes it to be made, अञ् aff.; the semi-vowel rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभाषिक
वैभाषिक f. (-की) Optional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभ्र|वैभ्रं
वैभ्र n. (-भ्रं) The heaven of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. वि variously, भ्राज् to shine, ड aff., अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैभ्राज|वैभ्राजं
वैभ्राज n. (-जं) A garden of the gods, a celestial grove or garden.<BR> E. वि<BR>variously, भ्राज् to shine, aff. अच् and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमत्य|वैमत्यं
वैमत्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Dissension.<BR>	 2. Dislike, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमनस्य|वैमनस्यं
वैमनस्य n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Mental distraction.<BR>	 2. Sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमात्र|वैमात्रः
वैमात्र m. (-त्रः) A step-mother's son.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा-त्री) A step-mother's daughter.<BR>E. वि different, मातृ a mother, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमात्रेय|वैमात्रेयः
वैमात्रेय m. (-यः) A step-mother's son.<BR>	 f. (-यी) A half-sister, or one by<BR>a different mother.<BR> E. विमातृ, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमानिक|वैमानिकः
वैमानिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to a heavenly car, borne in one, &c.<BR> E. विमान, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमुक्त|वैमुक्तं|वैमुक्तः
वैमुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Liberated, emancipated, being at liberty or<BR>loose.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं) Liberation.<BR> E. विमुक्त free, loose, अण् aff., implying<BR>property or possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमुख्य|वैमुख्यं
वैमुख्य n. (-ख्यं)<BR>	 1. Turning away the face.<BR>	 2. Flight, retreat.<BR> E. विमुख, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैमेय|वैमेयः
वैमेय m. (-यः) Barter, exchange.<BR> E. वि, मेङ् to barter, यत् aff., अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयग्र|वैयग्रं
वैयग्र n. (-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. Perplexity.<BR>	 2. Exclusive attention to any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयधिकरण्य|वैयधिकरण्यं
वैयधिकरण्य n. (-ण्यं) The having different substrata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयर्थ्य|वैयर्थ्यं
वैयर्थ्य n. (-र्थ्यं) Unprofitableness, uselessness.<BR> E. व्यर्थ useless, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाकरण|वैयाकरणः
वैयाकरण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Grammatical, relating to grammar.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>A grammarian.<BR> E. व्याकरण grammar, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाकरणपाश|वैयाकरणपाशः
वैयाकरणपाश m. (-शः) A bad grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाघ्र|वैयाघ्रः
वैयाघ्र mfn. (-घ्रः-घ्री-घ्रं) Covered with a tiger-skin, (a car, &c.)<BR> E. व्याघ्र a tiger, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयात्य|वैयात्यं
वैयात्य n. (-त्यं) Immodesty, boldness.<BR> E. वियात and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयासकि|वैयासकिः
वैयासकि m. (-किः) A son of VYĀSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयुष्ट|वैयुष्टः
वैयुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टी-ष्टं) Early, betimes, occurring or performed in the<BR>morning.<BR> E. व्यष्ट morning, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैर|वैरं
वैर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Enmity, hostility.<BR>	 2. Heroism, prowess.<BR> E. वीर a warrior,<BR>aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरकर|वैरकरः
वैरकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Causing or occasioning enmity, mischief-making.<BR>E. वैर and कर who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरकार|वैरकारः
वैरकार m. (-रः) An enemy.<BR> E. वैर and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरक्त्य|वैरक्त्यं
वैरक्त्य n. (-क्त्यं)<BR>	 1. Aversion, displeasure, dislike.<BR>	 2. Absence of worldly<BR>attachment.<BR> E. विरक्त and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरङ्गिक|वैरंगिकः|वैरङ्गिकः
वैरङ्गिक m. (-कः) An ascetic, a devotee, one who has subdued passion<BR>or desire.<BR> E. वि privative, रङ्ग passion, aff. ठक् or ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरनिर्य्यातन|वैरनिर्यातन|वैरनिर्यातनं
वैरनिर्य्यातन n. (-नं) Revenge, retaliation, requital of an injury.<BR> E. वैर<BR>enmity, निर्य्यातन donation, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरप्रतिक्रिया
वैरप्रतिक्रिया f. (-या) Revenge.<BR> E. वैर enmity, प्रतिक्रिया return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरल्य|वैरल्यं
वैरल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Scarceness, rareness.<BR>	 2. Looseness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरशुद्धि|वैरशुद्धिः
वैरशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Revenge, retaliation, requital.<BR> E. वैर enmity, शुद्धि purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराग|वैरागं
वैराग n. (-गं) Absence of worldly passion or desire.<BR> E. वि privative, राग<BR>passion, अण् aff.; with ष्यञ् aff. वैराग्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरागिक|वैरागिकः
वैरागिक m. (-कः) An ascetic, one with subdued passions.<BR> E. वि priv. राग passion, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरागिन्
वैरागिन् m. (-गी) An ascetic, a devotee, one who has subdued his world-<BR>ly desires: at present the term in common use is applied to a<BR>particular class of religious mendicants.<BR> E. वैराग absence of<BR>passion, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराग्य|वैराग्यं
वैराग्य n. (-ग्यं) Subjection of the appetite and passions, absence of<BR>worldly desires.<BR> E. विराग and ष्यञ् aff.: see वैराग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराट|वैराटः
वैराट m. (-टः) An earth-worm.<BR> E. वि before राज् to shine, aff. क्विप्, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराठ्या
वैराठ्या f. (-ट्या) One of the sixteen goddesses of the Bauddhas, termed<BR>Vidyā-devis or goddesses of learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरानुबन्ध|वैरानुबंध|वैरानुबन्धः
वैरानुबन्ध m. (-न्धः) Commencement of hostilities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरानुवन्धिन्
वैरानुवन्धिन् m. (-न्धी)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. The solar ray which is charged<BR>with heat.<BR> E. वैर heroism or strength, अनुवन्धिन् connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरायमाण
वैरायमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Hostile, inimical, an enemy.<BR> E. वैर enmity,<BR>used as a verb, with क्यङ् and शानच् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरारोह
वैरारोह m. (-हः) Desperate or arduous combat.<BR> E. वैर enmity, &c. आरोह ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरिता
वैरिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Enmity.<BR>	 2. Heroism.<BR> E. वैरिन् and तल् aff.; also<BR>with त्व, वैरित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरिन्
वैरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Hostile.<BR>	 m. (-री)<BR>	 1. An enemy.<BR>	 2. A hero.<BR> E. वैर enmity, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरूप्य|वैरूप्यं
वैरूप्य n. (-प्यं)<BR>	 1. Deformity.<BR>	 2. Difference of form, &c.<BR> E. विरूप, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचन|वैरोचनः
वैरोचन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The third of the Buddhas, called Dhyāni Bud-<BR>dhas.<BR>	 2. BALĪ, the sovereign so named.<BR>	 3. The son of AGNI.<BR>	 4.<BR>The son of ŚURYA, or the sun.<BR>	 5. A Siddha, a sort of demi-god or<BR>deified mortal.<BR> E. विरोचन the sun, &c. and aff. of descent अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचननिकेतन|वैरोचननिकेतनं
वैरोचननिकेतन n. (-नं) Pātāla the intermediate region between the earth<BR>and Tartarus or Naraka, over part of which BALĪ presides. E.<BR>वैरोचन the prince BALĪ, and निकेतन abode; the sovereign of this<BR>name being an incarnate Daitya or hereditary foe of the gods, and<BR>being invested with a sovereignty in the lower regions after his<BR>humiliation by VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचनि|वैरोचनिः
वैरोचनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. A BUDDHA.<BR>	 2. BALĪ.<BR>	 3. The son of ŚURYA.<BR> E. विरोचन, इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचि|वैरोचिः
वैरोचि m. (-चिः) The demon or Daitya VĀṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोद्धार|वैरोद्धारः
वैरोद्धार n. (-रं) Revenge, retaliation.<BR> E. वैर enmity, and उद्धार a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलक्षण्य|वैलक्षण्यं
वैलक्षण्य n. (-ण्यं) Difference, contrariety.<BR> E. विलक्षण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलक्ष्य|वैलक्ष्यं
वैलक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Contrariety, reverse, inversion.<BR>	 2. Contrary course<BR>or conduct to that which is usual or natural.<BR>	 3. Absence of any<BR>characteristic.<BR>	 4. Shame.<BR>	 5. Sorrow.<BR> E. विलक्ष, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलोम्य|वैलोम्यं
वैलोम्य n. (-म्यं) Opposition, contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैल्व|वैल्वं
वैल्व mfn. (-ल्वः-ल्वी-ल्वं) Relating or belonging to the Vilwa-tree.<BR>	 n. (-ल्वं)<BR>The fruit of the Vilwa, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR> E. विल्व the tree, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैल्वमय
वैल्वमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of the Vilwa, of the wood, &c. of that<BR>tree.<BR> E. वैल्व relating to the Bel, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैव
वैव(ब)धिक m. (-कः) A chandler, a vender of grain, oil, ghee, fruit, sweet-<BR>meats, &c.<BR> E. विवध storing grain, &c., aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्ण्य|वैवर्ण्यं
वैवर्ण्य n. (-र्ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Change of colour or complexion.<BR>	 2. Change of colour<BR>in general.<BR>	 3. Deviation or secession from tribe or caste, &c.<BR>	 4.<BR>Heterogeneousness, difference.<BR> E. वि privative or contra-indicative,<BR>and वर्ण colour, tribe, &c., aff. ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवस्वत|वैवस्वतः
वैवस्वत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. YAMA.<BR>	 2. One of the RUDRAS.<BR>	 3. The seventh MANU<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">Page693-a+ 60</a>]<BR>or the MANU of the present period.<BR>	 4. The planet Saturn.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं) The present age, presided over by the seventh MANU. E.<BR>विवस्वत् the sun, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाहिक|वैवाहिकः
वैवाहिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Nuptial, matrimonial, relating to marriage.<BR>mn. (-कः-कं) A marriage.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The bride or bridegroom's<BR>father-in-law.<BR> E. विवाह marriage, ठक् aff. of reference or relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशद्य|वैशद्यं
वैशद्य n. (-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Whiteness.<BR>	 2. Cleanness, purity, (literally or<BR>figuratively.)<BR>	 3. Composure.<BR> E. विशद white, &c., ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशम्पायन|वैशंपायन|वैशंपायनः|वैशम्पायनः
वैशम्पायन m. (-नः) A sage, the original teacher of the Yajur-Veda, and<BR>narrator of the Mahābhārata to JANAMBJAYA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस|वैशसं
वैशस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Hindrance, impediment.<BR>	 2. Slaughter.<BR> E. विशसस्य भावः स्वार्थे वा अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस्त्र|वैशस्त्रं
वैशस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>	 1. Government, sway, rule.<BR>	 2. The state of being dis-<BR>armed or defenceless.<BR> E. विशस्तृ ruling, अञ् aff., and the pen. vowel<BR>changed; or वि private, शस्त्र a weapon, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशाख|वैशाखं|वैशाखः
वैशाख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. The month in which the moon is full near the south-<BR>ern scale, (April-May,) the first month in the Hindu calendar.<BR>	 2.<BR>A churning-stick.<BR>	 n. (-खं) A particular attitude in shooting,<BR>standing with the feet a span apart.<BR>	 f. (-खी) The day of full-moon<BR>in the month of Vaiśākha.<BR> E. विशाखा the constellation in which<BR>the moon is full in this month, अण् aff.; or विशाखा said to mean<BR>here, pervading, revolving, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिक|वैशिकः
वैशिक n. (-कं) Harlotry, allurement of harlots.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A man who<BR>associates with courtezans.<BR> E. वेश्या, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिष्ट्य|वैशिष्ट्यं
वैशिष्ट्य n. (-ष्ट्यं)<BR>	 1. Endowment with some distinguishing attributes.<BR>2. Distinction, peculiarity.<BR>	 3. Excellence.<BR> E. विशिष्ट, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेषिक|वैशेषिकः
वैशेषिक m. (-कः) A follower of the Vaiśeshika doctrine.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The<BR>Vaiśeshika doctrine, or branch of the Nyāya or logical school of<BR>philosophy, instituted by KANĀDA. It differs from GAUTAMA'S<BR>system in recognizing only seven categories instead of sixteen. E.<BR>विशेष difference, (from the original Nyāya of GAUTAMA,) ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेष्य|वैशेष्यं
वैशेष्य n. (-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Specific or generic distinction.<BR>	 2. Superiority, pre-<BR>eminence.<BR> E. विशेष, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्य|वैश्यः
वैश्य m. (-श्यः) The Vaiśya or man of the third or agricultural and<BR>mercantile tribe.<BR>	 f. (-श्या) A woman of the Vaiśya caste.<BR> E. विश् to<BR>enter, (fields, &c.) क्विप् aff., यञ् pleonasm added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्यक्रिया
वैश्यक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Trade, agriculture.<BR> E. वैश्य, क्रिया act, business; also वैश्यकर्म्म, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्यवृत्ति
वैश्यवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Agriculture or trade.<BR> E. वैश्य, and वृत्ति subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवण|वैश्रवणः
वैश्रवण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. KUVERA, the god of wealth.<BR>	 2. RĀVAṆA.<BR> E. विश्रवस्<BR>their father, aff. अण्, and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणालय|वैश्रवणालयः
वैश्रवणालय m. (-यः) The Indian-fig tree.<BR> E. वैश्रवण KUVERA, आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणावास|वैश्रवणावासः
वैश्रवणावास m. (-सः) The Indian-fig tree.<BR> E. वैश्रवण KUVERA, आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणोदय|वैश्रवणोदयः
वैश्रवणोदय m. (-यः) The Indian-fig tree.<BR> E. वैश्रवण, उदय prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेव|वैश्वदेवः
वैश्वदेव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Sacred or dedicated to the Viśwadevas,<BR>offered to them, relating to them, &c.<BR>	 2. Relating to all divinities.<BR>n. (-वं) Offering to all the divinities.<BR>	 f. (-वी) Species of the Panktī<BR>metre.<BR> E. विश्वदेव, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेवकर्म्मन्|वैश्वदेवकर्मन्
वैश्वदेवकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Oblation of offering to the deities collectively. E.<BR>वैश्वदेव, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेवहोम
वैश्वदेवहोम n. (-मं) Oblation to the Viśwadevas.<BR> E. वैश्वदेव, and होम burnt-offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वानर|वैश्वानरः
वैश्वानर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Relating to, fit for, &c., all men.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. AGNI<BR>or fire.<BR>	 2. The digestive fire.<BR>	 3. The supreme being.<BR>	 f. (-री) A parti-<BR>cular sacrifice to be performed at the beginning of every year. E.<BR>विश्वानर a Muni, or विश्व all, नर mankind, अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वासिक
वैश्वासिक f. (-की) Trust-worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वी
वैश्वी f. (-श्वी) The second of the constellations called ĀSHĀDHĀ, and<BR>twenty-first of the whole.<BR> E. विश्व Viśwadeva, अण् and ङीष् affs.;<BR>those deities presiding over the asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषम्य|वैषम्यं
वैषम्य n. (-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Inequality, unevenness.<BR>	 2. Solitariness, singleness.<BR>	 3.<BR>Difficulty.<BR>	 4. Injustice.<BR> E. विषम odd, uneven, &c., aff. ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषयिक|वैषयिकः
वैषयिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sensualist, one addicted to the pleasures of sense.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">Page693-b+ 60</a>]<BR>2. One occupied with worldly objects or interests.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Re-<BR>lating to any object.<BR>	 2. Relating to an object of sense.<BR> E. विषय an<BR>object of sense, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्टुत|वैष्टुतं
वैष्टुत n. (-तं) The ashes of a burnt-offering.<BR> E. वि before स्तु to praise,<BR>aff. क्त and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्ट्र|वैष्ट्रं|वैष्ट्रः
वैष्ट्र n. (-ष्ट्रं)<BR>	 1. A world.<BR>	 2. Air.<BR>	 3. Heaven.<BR> E. विष् to extend, ष्ट्रन् Uṇadi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्णव|वैष्णवं|वैष्णवः
वैष्णव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Relating or belonging to VIṢṆU.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>follower of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. One of the modern Hindu sects, (the<BR>VAISHNABAS, the ŚAIVAS and the ŚĀKTAS are the three important<BR>modern Hindu sects.)<BR>	 f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. One of the Mātṛs, the personified<BR>energy or Śaktī of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. A flower,<BR>(Clitoria ternatea.)<BR>	 4. Sacred basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>	 n. (-वं) The<BR>ashes of a burnt offering.<BR> E. विष्णु VIṢṆU, अण् aff., fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैसारिण|वैसारिणः
वैसारिण m. (-णः) A fish.<BR> E. वि before सृ to go, णिनि aff., and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैसूचन|वैसूचनं
वैसूचन n. (-नं) A man's assuming female attire, (in the drama.)<BR> E. वि<BR>before सूच् to make known, क्युच् aff., and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहायस|वैहायसं
वैहायस f. (-सी) Being in the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहार्य्य|वैहार्य|वैहार्य्यः
वैहार्य्य f. (-र्य्या) One on whom jokes are to be practised; (as to the<BR>brother of a wife.)<BR> E. विहार joke, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहासिक|वैहासिकः
वैहासिक m. (-कः) A comic actor, a buffoon.<BR> E. वि, हास laughter, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोटा
वोटा f. (-टा) A female servant or slave.<BR> E. पुट् to contract, aff. अच्, and<BR>व being substituted for प; perhaps more correctly बोटा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोड्र|वोड्रः
वोड्र m. (-ड्रः)<BR>	 1. A large snake, (Borā or Boa Constrictor.)<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>fish.<BR>	 f. (-ड्री) The fourth part of a Paṇa.<BR> E. वा-बा० उड्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढव्य|वोढव्यः
वोढव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्यी-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be borne or carried.<BR>	 2. Able to bear or<BR>carry.<BR> E. वह् to bear, तव्यर् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढु|वोढुः
वोढु m. (-ढुः) The son of a woman living in her father's house, and<BR>whose husband is absent.<BR> E. वह् to bear, उ aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढृ
वोढृ m. (-ढा)<BR>	 1. A bridegroom.<BR>	 2. A porter, a bearer.<BR>	 3. A charioteer.<BR>4. A bull.<BR>	 5. A guide, a leader.<BR>	 6. A son.<BR>	 7. A draught horse.<BR> E. वह्<BR>to bear, aff. तृच्, ह changed to ढ, ओ substituted for the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोण्ट|वोंट|वोंटः|वोण्टः
वोण्ट m. (-ण्टः) A stalk, a stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोद|वोदः
वोद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Wet, moist, damp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोदाल|वोदालः
वोदाल m. (-लः) A sheat-fish, (Silurus Boalis, HAM.) “वोयाल माच् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोर
वोर m. (-रः) A sort of pulse, (Dolichos catjang.) E. Apparently not a<BR>Sanskrit word, though occurring in regular compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरक|वोरकः
वोरक m. (-कः) A scribe, a writer. E. See वोलक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरट|वोरटः
वोरट m. (-टः) A sort of jasmine. “कुन्दपुष्पे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरपट्टी
वोरपट्टी f. (-ट्टी) A sort of mat or mattress for sleeping on.<BR> E. वोर<BR>Dolichos catjang, पट्टी coarse cloth; perhaps made of the straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरव|वोरवः
वोरव m. (-वः) A kind of rice, which is cut in March or April. “वोरोधान्”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरुखान|वोरुखानः
वोरुखान m. (-नः) A horse, described as of a white and red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोल|वोलं|वोलः
वोल m. (-लः) Gum-myrrh.<BR> E. वा to go, to smell, उलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोलक|वोलकः
वोलक m. (-कः) A scribe.<BR>	 f. (-लिका) A sort of cake or pudding made<BR>with flour and sugar.<BR> E. वा to go, and उलच् aff., and कन् added;<BR>also ल being changed to र, वोरक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोल्लाह|वोल्लाहः
वोल्लाह m. (-हः) A horse, with white mane and tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोहित्थ|वोहित्थं|वोहित्थः
वोहित्थ n. (-त्थं) A vessel, a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वौषट्
वौषट् Ind. An exclamation used on offering an oblation to the gods or<BR>manes.<BR> E. वह् to bear, (what is borne by this,) and डौषट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंशक|व्यंशकः
व्यंशक m. (-कः) A mountain.<BR> E. वि various, अंश part, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंशुक|व्यंशुकः
व्यंशुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Undressed, naked.<BR> E. वि priv., अंशुक a garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसक|व्यंसकः
व्यंसक m. (-कः) A cheat, a juggler.<BR> E. वि before अंस् to divide, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसन|व्यंसनं
व्यंसन n. (-नं) Cheating, tricking.<BR> E. वि, अंस् to divide, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसनीय
व्यंसनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be deceived or cheated.<BR> E. वि before अंस<BR>to divide, अनीयर् aff.; also व्यंसितव्य and व्यंस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसित
व्यसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Deceived, tricked, cheated.<BR> E. वि, अंस् to divide, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्त|व्यक्तः
व्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Wise, learned.<BR>	 2. Evident, manifest, apparent,<BR>absolutely and specifically known or understood.<BR>	 2. Individual,<BR>specific.<BR> E. वि before अञ्ज् to make clear, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तत्व
व्यक्तत्व n. (-त्वं) Distinctness, manifestation.<BR> E. त्व added to the last; also<BR>व्यक्तता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तदृष्टार्थ|व्यक्तदृष्टार्थः
व्यक्तदृष्टार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Perceiving, understanding, present, an eye-<BR>witness.<BR> E. व्यक्त evident, दृष्ट seen, अर्थ meaning or object, (by whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तराशि|व्यक्तराशिः
व्यक्तराशि f. (-शिः) Known or absolute quantity.<BR> E. व्यक्त, राशि quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तलक्ष्मन्
व्यक्तलक्ष्मन् mfn. (-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मा-क्ष्म) Evident by certain signs or marks, manifest-<BR>ed, characterised.<BR> E. व्यक्त, and लक्ष्मन् a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्ति|व्यक्तिः
व्यक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Individuality, specific appearance or being.<BR>	 2.<BR>Appearance, manifestation.<BR>	 3. Case, inflexion, or the proper form<BR>of any inflected word.<BR> E. वि before अञ्ज् to make clear, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तिता
व्यक्तिता f. (-ता) Individuality.<BR> E. तल् added to व्यक्ति; also with त्व व्यक्तित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तीकरण
व्यक्तीकरण n. (-णं) Making distinct or manifest.<BR> E. व्यक्ति, करण making च्वि<BR>aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तीकृत
व्यक्तीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made clear or manifest.<BR> E. व्यक्ति, कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तीभूत
व्यक्तीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Distinct, clear.<BR> E. व्यक्ति, भूत become, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तोदित
व्यक्तोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Manifested, displayed.<BR> E. व्यक्त, उदित risen or<BR>said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यग्र|व्यग्रः
व्यग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं)<BR>	 1. Bewildered, perplexed, distracted.<BR>	 2. Alarmed,<BR>agitated, frightened.<BR>	 3. Engaged in, zealous, eager.<BR> E. वि before<BR>अग्र chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यग्रता
व्यग्रता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Perplexity, anxiety.<BR>	 2. Zeal.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; with त्व, व्यग्रत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्ग|व्यंग|व्यङ्गः
व्यङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Deformed, lame.<BR>	 2. Bodiless.<BR>	 3. Ill-arranged.<BR>m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A frog.<BR>	 2. A cripple.<BR>	 3. Discoloration of the face, dark<BR>spots on the cheek.<BR> E. वि depreciative, &c., अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्गार
व्यङ्गार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having no fire alight.<BR> E. वि priv., अङ्गार hot coals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्गुल|व्यंगुल|व्यंगुलं
व्यङ्गुल n. (-लं) The 60th part of a digit or Angula.<BR> E. वि, अङ्गुल a digit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यङ्ग्य|व्यंग्य|व्यङ्ग्यः
व्यङ्ग्य m. (-ङ्ग्यः)<BR>	 1. Figurative or poetical speech, elliptical language or<BR>that which conveys something more than the simple meaning of<BR>the words.<BR>	 2. Sarcasm, the covert but intelligible expression of<BR>suspicion or contempt.<BR> E. वि before अञ्ज् to make clear or manifest,<BR>aff. ण्यत्, or घञ् aff. and यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यच्
व्यच् r. 6th cl. (विचति) To cheat, to trick, to defraud or deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यज|व्यजः
व्यज m. (-जः) A fan.<BR> E. वि before अज् to go, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यजन|व्यजनं
व्यजन n. (-नं) A fan.<BR> E. वि before अज् to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जक|व्यंजक|व्यञ्जकः
व्यञ्जक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. External indication of passion or feeling.<BR>	 2. A sign,<BR>a mark, a symbol.<BR>	 3. Figurative or elliptical expression.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्जिका)<BR>1. Showing, making clear.<BR>	 2. Suggesting a meaning, as applied<BR>to a word or sense, (opposed to वाचक and लाक्षणिक ।)<BR> E. वि before<BR>अञ्ज् to manifest, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जकत्व
व्यञ्जकत्व n. (-त्वं) The nature or existence of figurative or poetical<BR>expression.<BR> E. व्यञ्जक, and त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जन|व्यंजन|व्यंजनं|व्यञ्जनं
व्यञ्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A mark, a spot, a sign, a token.<BR>	 2. Paraphernalia,<BR>insignia.<BR>	 3. The beard.<BR>	 4. A privy, part, either male er female.<BR>	 5.<BR>Sauce, condiment.<BR>	 6. A consonant.<BR>	 7. Making clear.<BR>	 8. A sign of<BR>puberty.<BR>	 9. A limb, a member.<BR>	 nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Figurative express-<BR>ion.<BR>	 2. Irony, sarcasm.<BR> E. वि before अञ्ज् to make clear, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जनावृत्ति|व्यञ्जनावृत्तिः
व्यञ्जनावृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Rhetorical or elliptical style.<BR> E. व्यञ्जना, and वृत्ति style.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जयत्
व्यञ्जयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Making visible.<BR> E. वि, अञ्ज् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जित|व्यंजित
व्यञ्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Distinguished, characterised.<BR>	 2. Manifested,<BR>visible.<BR>	 3. Suggested.<BR> E. वि before अञ्ज् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यञ्जिजिषु
व्यञ्जिजिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing or trying to expose, detect, make<BR>manifest, &c.<BR> E. वि before अञ्ज् to go, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यडम्बक|व्यडंबक|व्यडंबकः|व्यडम्बकः
व्यडम्बक m. (-कं) The castor-oil plant, (Ricinus communis.)<BR> E. वि before<BR>अड् to strive, aff. अच्, व्यड here said to mean excretion, अवि to go,<BR>to cause, ण्वुल् aff., form irr; also with युच् aff. व्यडम्बन m. (-नः) and<BR>by another reading, व्यडम्बर; other etymologies are given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकर|व्यतिकरः
व्यतिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Reciprocal, acting on or with one another.<BR>	 2.<BR>Pervading, who or what spreads through or over.<BR>	 3. Contiguous<BR>to, in contact with (-रः)<BR>	 1. Misfortune, calamity.<BR>	 2. Reciprocity,<BR>reciprocal action or relation 3. Reverse.<BR>	 4. Contact, contiguity.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">Page694-b+ 60</a>]<BR>5. Opportunity.<BR>	 6. An occurrence, an incident.<BR>	 7. Mixing<BR>together.<BR> E. वि and अति before कृ to make, to do, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकीर्ण
व्यतिकीर्ण f. (-र्णा) Mixed together, blended together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रम|व्यतिक्रमः
व्यतिक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Inverted or retrograde order, inversion, reverse.<BR>	 2.<BR>Contrariety, opposition in general; as the contrary of what is<BR>right or wrong, crime, vice: the contrary of prosperity, adversity,<BR>misfortune, &c.<BR>	 3. Retraction, non-performance, (as of contracts.)<BR>4. Passing over or beyond.<BR> E. वि and अति before क्रम् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रान्त|व्यतिक्रांत
व्यतिक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Reversed, inverted.<BR>	 2. Retracted.<BR>	 3. Passed<BR>over.<BR>	 4. Violated.<BR> E. वि and अति before क्रम् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरिक्त|व्यतिरिक्तः
व्यतिरिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Different, distinct.<BR>	 2. Excepted.<BR>	 3. With-<BR>drawn.<BR>	 4. Surpassing.<BR> E. वि and अति before रिच् to unite, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेक|व्यतिरेकः
व्यतिरेक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Difference, separateness.<BR>	 2. A figure in rhetoric,<BR>the dissimilitude of things compared in some respects to each<BR>other.<BR>	 3. Exception, exclusion.<BR>	 4. Excelling.<BR>	 5. Contrast.<BR>	 6. A<BR>logical discontinuance, opposed to अन्वय, (In Nyāya Phil.)<BR> E. वि<BR>and अति before रिच् to unite, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेकव्याप्ति
व्यतिरेकव्याप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Comprehensive argument derived from negatives<BR>or nonexistence.<BR> E. व्यतिरेक, and व्याप्ति pervading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेकिन्
व्यतिरेकिन् mfn. (-की-किणी-कि)<BR>	 1. Different, reverse.<BR>	 2. Excepting, dis-<BR>tinguishing.<BR>	 3. Implying negation or nonexistence.<BR>	 4. Excelling.<BR>E. व्यतिरेक, and इनि or घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेक्युदाहरण
व्यतिरेक्युदाहरण n. (-णं) Illustration by contrast or negatives.<BR> E. व्यतिरेकिन् उदाहरण example.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषक्त
व्यतिषक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Mutually connected, joined, related, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>and अति before षञ्ज् to embrace, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषङ्ग|व्यतिषंग|व्यतिषंगः|व्यतिषङ्गः
व्यतिषङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Mutual or reciprocal junction or relation.<BR>	 2.<BR>Fastening, tying together.<BR>	 3. Union.<BR>	 5. Intermixture.<BR> E. वि and<BR>अति before षञ्ज् to embrace, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषङ्गवत्
व्यतिषङ्गवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Connected, united, mixed.<BR> E. व्यतिषङ्ग, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यति
व्यति(ती)हार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Barter, exchange.<BR>	 2. Exchange of blows or<BR>abuse.<BR>	 3. Reciprocity.<BR> E. वि and अति before हृ to take, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीत|व्यतीतः
व्यतीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Past, gone.<BR>	 2. Departed from.<BR>	 3. Disregarded.<BR>E. वि before अतीत the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीपात|व्यतीपातः
व्यतीपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Great and portentous calamity, or a portent, indi-<BR>cating or occasioning it and therefore identified with it, as a comet,<BR>an earthquake, &c.<BR>	 2. Disrespect, contempt.<BR>	 3. The seventeenth of<BR>the astrological Yogas.<BR>	 4. Day of new-moon when it falls on a<BR>Sunday, and the moon is in certain mansions, Shrāvaṇa, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>and अति before पत् to fall, &c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीहार|व्यतीहारः
व्यतीहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Barter, exchange.<BR>	 2. Exchange of blows or abuse.<BR>E. वि, and अति implying reciprocity, हृ to take, aff. घञ्, and इ<BR>optionally made long: see व्यतिहार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यय|व्यत्ययः
व्यत्यय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Contrariety, opposition, reverse.<BR>	 2. Inverted or retro-<BR>grade order.<BR>	 3. Interchange.<BR> E. वि + अति before इण् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यस्त
व्यत्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Reversed, inverted, contrary, opposite.<BR> E. वि<BR>and अति before अस् to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यास|व्यत्यासः
व्यत्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Contrariety, opposition, reverse.<BR>	 2. Inverted or<BR>retrograde order.<BR>	 3. Reversed position.<BR> E. वि and आत् before<BR>अस् to throw or send, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथ्
व्यथ् r. 1st cl. (व्यथते)<BR>	 1. To fear.<BR>	 2. To be disquieted or unhappy.<BR>	 3. To<BR>be sorry or vexed.<BR>	 4. To suffer pain.<BR>	 5. To become dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथक|व्यथकः
व्यथक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Inflicting pain, torturing, painful.<BR>	 2. Dis-<BR>tressing, afflicting.<BR> E. व्यथ् to give pain, क्कुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथन|व्यथनं
व्यथन n. (-नं) Giving pain, paining.<BR> E. व्यथ् to pain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथनीय
व्यथनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be put to pain, what may be or ought to be<BR>pained.<BR> E. व्यथ्, and अनीयर् aff.; also व्यथ्य and व्यथितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथयत्
व्यथयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Paining, distressing.<BR> E. व्यथ् to pain, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथा
व्यथा f. (-था)<BR>	 1. Pain.<BR>	 2. Distress.<BR>	 3. Alarm, fear.<BR>	 4. Perturbation. E.<BR>व्यथ् to fear, to suffer pain, &c., affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथाकर
व्यथाकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Painful, excruciating.<BR> E. व्यथा, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=694-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथारहित
व्यथारहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Free from pain.<BR> E. व्यथा, and रहित quitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथित|व्यथितः
व्यथित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pained, tortured.<BR>	 2. Distressed, afflicted.<BR>	 3.<BR>Disturbed, troubled.<BR>	 4. Alarmed, frightened.<BR> E. व्यथा pain, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथ्यमान
व्यथ्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being agitated, distressed, pained, &c.<BR> E. व्यथ्<BR>to suffer pain, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्
व्यध्(औ)औव्यध r. 4th cl. (विध्यति) To beat, to strike, to pierce, to tear,<BR>to hurt or wound. With अनु, 1. To wound.<BR>	 2. To intertwine. With<BR>अप, 1. To cast away.<BR>	 2. To pierce. With आ, To throw, to pierce.<BR>With परि, To wound, to pierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध|व्यधः
व्यध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Perforating, piercing.<BR>	 2. Striking, smiting.<BR> E. व्यध् to<BR>strike, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यधन
व्यधन n. (-नं) Piercing, perforating.<BR> E. व्यध् to pierce, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यधिकरण|व्यधिकरणं
व्यधिकरण n. (-णं) The subsisting in different substrata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यधित
व्यधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made, done, caused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्य|व्यध्यः
व्यध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं) To be pierced or wounded.<BR>	 m. (-ध्यः) A butt, a<BR>mark to shoot at.<BR> E. व्यध् to pierce, aff. थत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्व|व्यध्वः
व्यध्व m. (-ध्वः) A bad road.<BR> E. वि depreciative, अध्वन् a road, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यनुनाद|व्यनुनादः
व्यनुनाद m. (-दः) Reverberation, loud and extending sound or noise. E.<BR>वि and अनु before नद् to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यनुनादयत्
व्यनुनादयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Causing to reverberate, filling with<BR>sound or noise.<BR> E. वि and अनु before नद् to sound, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यप्
व्यप् r. 10th cl. (व्यपयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To diminish, to decay.<BR>	 2. To throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपकृष्ट
व्यपकृष्ट f. (-ष्टा) Taken off, removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगत
व्यपगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone away.<BR> E. वि and अप before गम् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगम|व्यपगमः
व्यपगम m. (-मः) Going away, departure.<BR> E. वि and अप before गम् to go,<BR>अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपत्रपमाण
व्यपत्रपमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Ashamed.<BR> E. वि and अपत्रप to be shameless, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदिष्ट
व्यपदिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Named.<BR>	 2. Informed.<BR>	 3. Tricked.<BR>	 4. Pleaded<BR>in excuse.<BR>	 4. Shown.<BR> E. वि and अप before दिश् to show, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदेश|व्यपदेशः
व्यपदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Dishonesty, fraud, craft.<BR>	 2. Stratagem, device.<BR>3. Name, appellation.<BR>	 4. Information, notice, apprising.<BR>	 5. Hint.<BR>6. Excuse, pretext.<BR>	 7. Family, race.<BR>	 8. Fame, repute.<BR>	 9. Naming.<BR>E. वि and अप before दिश् to show, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदेष्टृ
व्यपदेष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ)<BR>	 1. Deceiving, a cheat.<BR>	 2. One who shows, names,<BR>&c.<BR> E. वि and अप before दिश् to show, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपनीत
व्यपनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taken away, removed.<BR> E. वि and अप before नीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरोपण|व्यपरोपणं
व्यपरोपण n. (-णं) Extirpating, expelling.<BR> E. वि and अप before रुह् to<BR>grow, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरोपित
व्यपरोपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Extirpated, eradicated, expelled.<BR> E. वि and अप<BR>before रुह् to grow, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाकृति|व्यपाकृतिः
व्यपाकृति f. (-तिः) Repelling, denial.<BR> E. वि and अप implying opposition,<BR>and आङ् before कृ to make, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रय|व्यपाश्रयः
व्यपाश्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Taking refuge with, lying upon, trusting to.<BR>	 2.<BR>Expectation.<BR> E. वि, अप and आङ् before श्री to serve, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रित
व्यपाश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having taken refuge with, relying upon, who<BR>or what does so.<BR> E. वि, अप and आङ् before श्री to serve, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रित्य
व्यपाश्रित्य Ind. Having sought or taken refuge with.<BR> E. वि, अप and आङ्<BR>before श्री to serve, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्ष
व्यपेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Expectant, waiting, attentive.<BR> E. वि and अप<BR>before ईक्ष् to see, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षण|व्यपेक्षणं
व्यपेक्षण n. (-णं) Expecting, looking for.<BR> E. वि and अप before ईक्ष् to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षणीय
व्यपेक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be expected or looked for.<BR> E. वि and अप<BR>before ईक्ष् to see, अनीयर् aff.; also व्यपेक्ष्य and व्यपेक्षितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षा
व्यपेक्षा f. (-क्षा) Expectation, especially if reciprocal.<BR>	 2. Mutual connec-<BR>tion or relation.<BR>	 3. Application, use.<BR>	 4. (In grammar,) The mutual<BR>application of two rules.<BR> E. वि severally, अपेक्षा looking to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षित
व्यपेक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Looked to reciprocally.<BR>	 2. Mutually related.<BR>3. Employed, applied.<BR> E. वि and अपेक्षित expected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेत
व्यपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone, passed away, got rid of.<BR>	 2. Opposed,<BR>contrary.<BR>	 3. Severed.<BR> E. वि and अप before इ to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोढ
व्यपोढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Opposite, contrary, reverse.<BR>	 2. Driven off or<BR>away.<BR>	 3. Exhibited.<BR> E. वि and अप before वह् to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोह|व्यपोहः
व्यपोह m. (-हः) Driving away, Keeping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोह्य
व्यपोह्य Ind.<BR>	 1. Having driven away, got rid of.<BR>	 2. Having passed<BR>through a place.<BR> E. वि and अप before वह् to convey, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचार|व्यभिचारः
व्यभिचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Following improper courses, doing what is prohi-<BR>bited or wicked.<BR>	 2. Erring, straying, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Wandering from an argument, a fallacious Hetu, one without<BR>the Sādhya, (in logic.)<BR>	 4. Infidelity of a husband or wife.<BR> E. वि<BR>and अभि before चर् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचारिन्
व्यभिचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Following or doing improper.<BR>	 2. Going<BR>astray, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>	 n. (-रि) A property, or class of<BR>properties into which feelings and emotions, as objects of poeti-<BR>cal description are classed; or the transitory feeling, (op. to<BR>स्थायिन्) which does not pervade a composition but, if properly<BR>developed at any stage, strengthens the prevailing sentiment.<BR>the BHĀVAS called VYABHICHĀRIS are thirty-two in number,<BR>to which two others are sometimes added, making thirty-<BR>four, viz:--1. NIRVEDA, humility, self-abasement; 2. GLĀNI,<BR>weakness, exhaustion; 3. ŚANKĀ, apprehension; 4. ASŪĀ,<BR>calumny; 5. MADA, inebriety; 6. ŚHRAMA, fatigue; 7. ĀLASYA,<BR>indolence; 8. DAINYA, indigence, distress.<BR>	 6. CHINTĀ, secret desire;<BR>contemplation of the object beloved; 10. MOHA, loss of sense or<BR>presence of mind from fear, anxiety, &c.; 11. SMRITĪ, recollection<BR>but especially the recollection of an absent or faithless lover exci-<BR>ted by present objects; 12. DHRITĪ, the enjoyment or consciousness<BR>of amatory woe, resignation or abandonment to despair, &c.; 13.<BR>VṚDA, shame; 14. CHAPALATĀ, fickleness, unsteadiness, want of<BR>firmness and steadiness; 15. HARSA, delight; 16. ĀBEGA, hurry,<BR>flurried haste; 17. JARATĀ, ignorance, imbecility; 18. GARBA,<BR>pride, arrogance; 19. BISHĀDA, want of energy or spirits, depress-<BR>ion of mind; 20. AUTSUKYA, regret, painful remembrance of some<BR>object lost or absent; 21. NIDRĀ, sluggishness, sleepiness; 22.<BR>APASMĀRA, epilepsy; 23. ŚUPTA, sleep; 24. BIBODHA, waking; 25.<BR>AMARSHA, wrathful impatience; 26. AVAHITTHĀ, dissimulation; 27.<BR>UGRATĀ, passion, rage; 28. MATI, intelligence, knowledge; 29.<BR>UPĀLAMBHA, reviling; 30. BYĀDHI, sickness, disease; 31. UNMĀDA,<BR>madness, delirium; 32. MARAṆA, death; the other two are, 33.<BR>TRĀSA, fear; 34. BITARKA, doubt, deliberation.<BR>	 f. (-रिणी) A wanton<BR>woman, an unchaste wife.<BR> E. वि and अभि before चर् to go, aff. णिनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभ्र
व्यभ्र mfn. (-भ्रः-भ्रा-भ्रं) Uncloud.<BR> E. वि priv., अभ्र a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यय्
व्यय् r. 1st. cl. (व्ययति-ते) To go, to move. r. 10th cl. (व्यययति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>lessen, to diminish.<BR>	 2. To send. r. 1st and 10th cls. (व्ययते व्यययति-<BR>ते)<BR>	 1. To expend, to disburse, to abandon wealth, to give away<BR>money, &c.<BR>	 2. To move, &c. (व्याययति-ते) To drive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यय|व्ययं|व्ययः
व्यय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Expenditure, spending.<BR>	 2. Destruction, disappearance.<BR>3. Misfortune, downfall, decline.<BR>	 4. Obstacle.<BR>	 5. Loss, waste.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-या) Mutable, liable to decay.<BR> E. व्यय् to expend, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययन|व्ययनं
व्ययन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Spending.<BR>	 2. Destroying.<BR> E. व्यय, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययमान
व्ययमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Spending, expending.<BR> E. व्यय् to spend, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययित|व्ययितः
व्ययित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Expended, spent.<BR>	 2. Gone, dissipated, dis-<BR>persed.<BR>	 3. Declined, fallen into decay.<BR> E. व्यय् to expend, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययिन्
व्ययिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Spending.<BR>	 2. Declining, falling into cala-<BR>mity.<BR>	 3. Wasting, decaying.<BR> E. व्यय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययीकरण
व्ययीकरण n. (-णं) Expending, wasting.<BR> E. व्यय, करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययीकृत
व्ययीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Expended, wasted.<BR> E. व्यय, कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययीभूत
व्ययीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spent, wasted.<BR> E. व्यय, भूत been, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्ण|व्यर्ण्ण
व्यर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Asked.<BR>	 2. Gone.<BR> E. अर्द्द to ask, with वि prefix,<BR>and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थ|व्यर्थं
व्यर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Useless, unprofitable.<BR>	 2. Unmeaning.<BR> E. वि, priv. अर्थ meaning, object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=695-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थक
व्यर्थक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Vain, useless.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थकता
व्यर्थकता f. (-ता) Unprofitableness, uselessness.<BR> E. व्यर्थक, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थता
व्यर्थता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Unprofitableness, uselessness.<BR>	 2. Absence of meaning,<BR>nonsense.<BR> E. तल added to व्यर्थ; also with त्व, व्यर्थत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यलीक|व्यलीकं|व्यलीकः
व्यलीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Disagreeable, displeasing, offensive.<BR>	 2. Im-<BR>proper, unfit to be done.<BR>	 3. Painful.<BR>	 4. Strange.<BR>	 5. False.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>1. Pain, torture.<BR>	 2. Fault, transgression.<BR>	 3. Any thing displeasing.<BR>4. Any improper act.<BR>	 5. Reverse.<BR>	 6. Cheating, tricking.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>A catamite.<BR> E. वि and अल् to be able or to adorn, aff. ईकक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यलीकता
व्यलीकता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Impropriety.<BR>	 2. Disagreeableness.<BR> E. तल् added to<BR>the last; also with त्व, व्यलीकत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवकलन|व्यवकलनं
व्यवकलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Subtraction, (in math.)<BR>	 2. Separation.<BR> E. वि and अव<BR>before कल् to reckon, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवकलित|व्यवकलितः
व्यवकलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Subtracted, deducted.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Subtraction. E.<BR>वि and अव before कल् to count, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवक्रोशन|व्यवक्रोशनं
व्यवक्रोशन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Wrangling, altercation, mutual abuse.<BR>	 2. Abuse,<BR>reviling.<BR> E. वि and अव before क्रुश् to call, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छिन्न|व्यवच्छिन्नं|व्यवछिन्न
व्यवच्छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Different, separate, divided.<BR>	 2. Distin-<BR>guished, discriminated.<BR>	 3. Cut in pieces.<BR>	 4. Interrupted.<BR> E. वि<BR>and अव before छिद् to cut, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छेद|व्यवच्छेदः|व्यवछेद
व्यवच्छेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Dividing, separating.<BR>	 2. A division.<BR>	 3. Discrimina-<BR>tion.<BR>	 4. Contrast, distinction.<BR>	 5. Letting fly an arrow, shooting,<BR>darting.<BR>	 6. Cutting in pieces.<BR> E. वि and अव before छिद् to cut, aff.<BR>घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवतिष्ठमान
व्यवतिष्ठमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Arranged, placed.<BR> E. वि and अव before स्था to<BR>stay, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधा
व्यवधा f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. A covering, a screen, any thing which holds or con-<BR>ceals from sight.<BR>	 2. The state of being covered, concealment, dis-<BR>appearance.<BR> E. वि and अव before धा to have, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधान|व्यवधानं
व्यवधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Covering, disappearance, either the thing which con-<BR>ceals, or the state of being concealed from sight.<BR>	 2. Intervening,<BR>intervention, space.<BR>	 3. The intervention of a letter, (in grammar.)<BR>E. वि and अव before धा to have, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधायक|व्यवधायकः
व्यवधायक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Concealing, screening, hiding.<BR>	 2. Interven-<BR>ing, intermediate, separating.<BR> E. वि अव before धा to have, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधि|व्यवधिः
व्यवधि m. (-धिः) Covering, or a covering: see व्यवधान.<BR> E. वि and अव<BR>before धा to have, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसाय|व्यवसायः
व्यवसाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Effort, exertion, persevering or industrious effort,<BR>perseverance, industry.<BR>	 2. Following any business or profession.<BR>	 3.<BR>Plan, device, trick.<BR>	 4. Resolve, determination.<BR>	 5. Boasting.<BR>	 6.<BR>Action.<BR>	 7. Conduct.<BR> E. वि and अव before षो to destroy, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसायात्मक
व्यवसायात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Laborious, relating to exertion.<BR> E. व्यवसाय,<BR>आत्मन् self, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसायिन्
व्यवसायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Active, energetic, persevering, resolute.<BR>2. Engaged in business.<BR> E. व्यवसाय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसित|व्यवसितः
व्यवसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Tricked, cheated.<BR>	 2. Energetic, taking pains,<BR>making effort or exertion.<BR>	 3. Resolved, determined.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Cer-<BR>tainty, ascertainment.<BR> E. वि and अव before षो to destroy. aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्था
व्यवस्था f. (-स्था)<BR>	 1. Separating, placing remote or apart.<BR>	 2. Placing or<BR>staying in or on.<BR>	 3. A decree, a written declaration of the law;<BR>applied in practice to the written extracts from the codes of law,<BR>stated as the opinions of the Hindu law officers attached to the<BR>court of justice.<BR>	 4. An engagement, an agreement, a contract.<BR>	 5.<BR>Fixity.<BR> E. वि and अव before स्था to stay or be, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थातिक्रम|व्यवस्थातिक्रमः
व्यवस्थातिक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Breaking an agreement or contract.<BR>	 2. Disre-<BR>garding the law.<BR> E. व्यवस्था and अतिक्रम transgressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थातिवर्त्तन|व्यवस्थातिवर्तन
व्यवस्थातिवर्त्तन n. (-नं) Breaking an agreement or contract.<BR> E. व्यवस्था and<BR>अतिवर्त्तन transgressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थातिवर्त्तिन्|व्यवस्थातिवर्तिन्
व्यवस्थातिवर्त्तिन् m. (-र्त्ती) One who does not keep an engagement, &c.<BR>E. व्यवस्था, and अतिवर्त्तिन् going from or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थान|व्यवस्थानं|व्यवस्थानः
व्यवस्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Steadiness.<BR>	 2. Regular arrangement, determination.<BR>3. Rule, decision.<BR>	 4. Firmness, perseverance.<BR> E. वि + अव + स्था-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापक
व्यवस्थापक f. (-पिका)<BR>	 1. Settling, deciding.<BR>	 2. Supervising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापन|व्यवस्थापनं
व्यवस्थापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Declaring, deciding, laying down as law.<BR>	 2. Fix-<BR>ing, determining.<BR>	 3. Appointing.<BR>	 4. Placing apart.<BR>	 5. Placing.<BR>	 6.<BR>Arranging.<BR> E. वि and अव before स्था to stay, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापित
व्यवस्थापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Declared, determined.<BR>	 2. Caused to be<BR>placed.<BR> E. वि and अव before स्था to stay, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थित|व्यवस्थितः
व्यवस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Separated, distant.<BR>	 2. Extracted.<BR>	 3. Invari-<BR>able, constant.<BR>	 4. Appointed.<BR>	 5. Declared, decreed.<BR>	 6. Staying or<BR>fixed in or on.<BR>	 7. Adjusted.<BR> E. वि and अव before स्था to be, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थिति|व्यवस्थितिः
व्यवस्थिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Constancy, perseverance.<BR>	 2. Determining, appoint-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Extracting.<BR> E. वि and अव before स्था to stay, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहर्त्तव्य|व्यवहर्तव्य
व्यवहर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be litigated or decided judicially.<BR>	 2.<BR>To be done or transacted.<BR> E. वि and अव before हृ to take, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहर्त्तृ|व्यवहर्तृ
व्यवहर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ) Transacting business, engaged in affairs.<BR>2. Observing or following established usages.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>	 1. A judge,<BR>an umpire, one conducting a judicial procedure.<BR>	 2. A litigant, a<BR>plaintiff, one instituting a dispute at law.<BR>	 3. Partaker, associate.<BR>E. वि and अव before हृ to take, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहार|व्यवहारः
व्यवहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The practice of the courts, or civil and criminal<BR>law, judicial procedure, administrative justice, as the examina-<BR>tion of evidence, &c.<BR>	 2. Title of jurisprudence, any act cognizable<BR>in courts of justice.<BR>	 3. Contest at law, lawsuit, litigation.<BR>	 4.<BR>Usage, custom.<BR>	 5. Conduct.<BR>	 6. Profession, business.<BR>	 7. Steadiness,<BR>property, adherence to law and custom.<BR>	 8. A contract.<BR>	 9. A sort<BR>of tree.<BR>	 10. Mathematical or arithmetical determination or<BR>ascertainment.<BR> E. वि, and अव implying dissension, and हृ to take,<BR>aff. घञ्, the term being explained to mean especially, a dispute<BR>between two parties, or the counter statements of plaintiff and<BR>defendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारज्ञ|व्यवहारज्ञः
व्यवहारज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. A person who has passed his minority, a young<BR>man of age, or one who has passed his sixteenth year, at which<BR>period he can assert his own rights in a court of law.<BR>	 2. One ac-<BR>quainted with legal procedure.<BR> E. व्यवहार a lawsuit, ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारदर्शन|व्यवहारदर्शनं
व्यवहारदर्शन n. (-नं) Judicial investigation, trial.<BR> E. व्यवहार legal proceed-<BR>ing, and दर्शन seeing, inspecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारपद|व्यवहारपदं
व्यवहारपद n. (-दं) A title of jurisprudence, any act cognizable in a court<BR>of law: see व्यवहारविषय.<BR> E. व्यवहार and पद object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारपाद|व्यवहारपादः
व्यवहारपाद m. (-दः) A division of legal proceeding, one of the four parts<BR>which are necessary to conduct a regular suit, or the plaint, the<BR>defence, the proof and the decision.<BR> E. व्यवहार a lawsuit, पाद a<BR>quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारप्राप्त
व्यवहारप्राप्त m. (-प्तः) A youth who has come of age.<BR> E. व्यवहार, प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारमातृका
व्यवहारमातृका f. (-का) Legal procedure or process in general, simple<BR>judicature, law as in all ordinary cases administered.<BR> E. व्यवहार<BR>legal contest, मातृका mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारमार्ग|व्यवहारमार्गः
व्यवहारमार्ग m. (-र्गः) A title of jurisprudence: see व्यवहारविषय.<BR> E. व्यवहार, मार्ग road or path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारविधि|व्यवहारविधिः
व्यवहारविधि m. (-धिः) Law, the law, the precepts or code by which<BR>judicature is to be regulated and decisions to be made.<BR> E. व्यवहार<BR>legal process, and विधि a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारविषय|व्यवहारविषयः
व्यवहारविषय mn. (-यः-यं) A title of jurisprudence, an act which may<BR>become the object of dispute amongst men, and should therefore be<BR>regulated by law; according to MANU, there are eighteen heads,<BR>but these are the principal only, and many things not comprised<BR>under them may still be actionable; the eighteen are:--1. ऋणादानं<BR>debt; 2. निक्षेपः deposit; 3. अस्वामिविक्रयः sale without ownership;<BR>4. सम्भूयसमुत्थानं concerns amongst partners; 5. दत्तस्यानपकर्म्म subtrac-<BR>tion of what has been given; 6. वेतनादानं non-payment of wages;<BR>7. सम्बिद्व्यतिक्रमः non-performance of agreement; 8. क्रयविक्रयानुशयः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">Page697-a+ 60</a>]<BR>rescission of sale and purchase; 9. स्वामिपालयोर्विवादः disputes<BR>between master and servant; 10. सीमाविवादः disputes about bound-<BR>aries; 11. वाक्पारुष्यं defamation, abuse; 12. दण्डपारुष्यं assault; 13.<BR>स्तेयं theft, larceny; 14. साहसं robbery, and other violence; 15.<BR>स्त्रीसंग्रहणं adultery; 16. स्त्रीपुंधर्म्मः duties of man and wife; 17. विभागः<BR>portioning of property, inheritance; 18. द्यूतं gambling of any kind<BR>as fighting animals, laying wagers, &c.<BR> E. व्यवहार legal process,<BR>and विषय object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=696-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारस्थान|व्यवहारस्थानं
व्यवहारस्थान n. (-नं) A title of jurisprudence: see व्यवहारविषय.<BR> E. व्यवहार legal procedure, स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहाराङ्ग|व्यवहारांग
व्यवहाराङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) The body of civil and criminal law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहाराभिशस्त्र
व्यवहाराभिशस्त्र mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Prosecuted, accused, proceeded against<BR>legally.<BR> E. व्यवहार and अभिशस्त accused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारायोग्य|व्यवहारायोग्यः
व्यवहारायोग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Unfitted or unsuited to legal proceedings.<BR>m. (-ग्यः)<BR>	 1. A minor.<BR>	 2. One incompetent to conduct business. E.<BR>व्यवहार and अयोग्य unfit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिक|व्यवहारिकः
व्यवहारिक mfn. (-कः-का or की-कं)<BR>	 1. Customary, usual.<BR>	 2. Engaged in<BR>customary duty or avocation.<BR>	 3. Connected with or relating to<BR>legal process.<BR>	 4. Litigant, being party to a suit.<BR> E. व्यवहार, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिका
व्यवहारिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Usage, custom.<BR>	 2. A brush, a broom.<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>commonly called Ingudī.<BR> E. कन् added to व्यवहार, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिन्
व्यवहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Litigant, litigating, engaged in a law-<BR>suit.<BR>	 2. Relating to legal process.<BR>	 3. Customary, usual.<BR>	 4. Follow-<BR>ing one's ordinary affairs or avocation.<BR> E. व्यवहार and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहार्य्य|व्यवहार्य|व्यवहार्य्यः
व्यवहार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. To be observed or practised, as a duty<BR>or avocation, customary, usual.<BR>	 2. Actionable, subject to legal pro-<BR>cess.<BR> E. वि and अव before हृ to take or convey, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहास
व्यवहास m. (-सः) Mutual laughter.<BR> E. वि and अव before हस् to laugh, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहित|व्यवहितः
व्यवहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Placed or situated contiguously to, attached or<BR>adhering to, &c.<BR>	 2. Intervening, separating.<BR>	 3. Covered, con-<BR>cealed.<BR>	 4. Excelled, surpassed, put to shame.<BR>	 5. Done, acted,<BR>performed.<BR>	 6. Not immediately connected.<BR>	 7. Obstructed.<BR>	 8. Omit-<BR>ted, passed over.<BR> E. वि and अव before धा to have or hold, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहृति|व्यवहृतिः
व्यवहृति f. (-तिः) Practice, performance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवाय|व्यवायं|व्यवायः
व्यवाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Copulation.<BR>	 2. Covering, disappearance.<BR>	 3. Purity.<BR>	 4.<BR>Interval, space.<BR>	 5. Separation, decomposition.<BR>	 6. Obstacle.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>Light, lustre.<BR> E. वि and अव before इण् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवायिन्
व्यवायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Lecherous.<BR>	 2. Pervading, diffusive.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-यी)<BR>	 1. A lecher, a libertine.<BR>	 2. A drug, an aphrodisiac.<BR>	 3. Any<BR>article that produces general excitement, as wine, poison, &c. E.<BR>व्यवाय copulation, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवेत
व्यवेत f. (-ता) Separated, decomposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यश्नुवान
व्यश्नुवान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Occupying, pervading.<BR> E. वि before अश् to pervade, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यष्टि
व्यष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Singleness.<BR>	 2. Distributive pervasion.<BR>	 3. A whole<BR>viewed as consisting of many separate objects, (as opposed to<BR>समष्टि,) (in Vedānta phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसन|व्यसनं
व्यसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Calamity, misfortune.<BR>	 2. Fate.<BR>	 3. Fault, vice, crime,<BR>frailty, arising from desire, or from anger; ten vices or faults are<BR>enumerated under the first head; viz:--hunting, gambling, sleeping<BR>in the day, calumny, whoring, dancing, singing, playing, idle roam-<BR>ing, and drinking; the second comprehends eight; viz:--depravi-<BR>ty, violence, injury, envy, malice, fraud, abuse, and assault.<BR>	 4. Sin.<BR>5. Fated consequence.<BR>	 6. Evil-destiny, ill-luck.<BR>	 7. Fruitless effort.<BR>8. Incompetence, inability.<BR>	 9. Intent, application or attachment to<BR>an object.<BR>	 10. Falling, (as opposed to उदय.)<BR>	 11. Air, wind.<BR>	 12.<BR>Individuality.<BR>	 13. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 14. Violation, infraction.<BR>	 15.<BR>Punishment.<BR> E. वि before अस् to throw, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनप्रहारिन्
व्यसनप्रहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Troublesome, giving trouble or pain. E.<BR>व्यसन and प्रहारिन् taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनात्त
व्यसनात्त, mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Afflicted, suffering pain or calamity.<BR> E. व्यसन<BR>misfortune, and आर्त्त affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनिता
व्यसनिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Wickedness.<BR>	 2. Calamity.<BR> E. व्यसनिन्, तल् aff.; also<BR>with त्व, व्यसनित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनिन्
व्यसनिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>	 1. Addicted to evil practices, as to gaming,<BR>drinking, wenching, &c.<BR>	 2. Excessively attached to any object.<BR>	 3.<BR>Calamitous, unfortunate.<BR> E. व्यसन vice, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनीय
व्यसनीय m. (-यः) A profligate, a debauchee.<BR> E. व्यसन and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसु
व्यसु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु) Inanimate, lifeless.<BR> E. वि priv., असु breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्त|व्यस्तः
व्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Confounded, confused, bewildered.<BR>	 2. Per-<BR>vaded, penetrated, spread.<BR>	 3. Present and essential, or inherent in<BR>all the parts of any thing, in opposition to the Samasta, or that<BR>which pervades the whole together.<BR>	 4. Reverse, inverse.<BR>	 5. Oppo-<BR>site.<BR>	 6. Opposed to, set or struck against.<BR>	 7. Tossed, thrown up<BR>or about.<BR>	 8. Reversed, inverted.<BR>	 9. Different, manifold.<BR>	 10. Divi-<BR>ded, severed.<BR>	 11. Simple, uncompounded.<BR> E. वि severally, &c.,<BR>अस् to be or pervade, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्तता
व्यस्तता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Agitation, bewilderment.<BR>	 2. Severalty, individuality.<BR>2. Inherence.<BR> E. व्यस्त, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, व्यस्तत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्तपद|व्यस्तपदं
व्यस्तपद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Perplexed and indistinct statement, want of preci-<BR>sion in an accusation or defence, (in law.)<BR>	 2. (In grammar,) A simple<BR>or uncompounded word.<BR> E. व्यस्त perplexed, पद a sentence, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्तविधि|व्यस्तविधिः
व्यस्तविधि f. (-धिः) Inversion, rule for inversion.<BR> E. व्यस्त, and विधि rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्तार|व्यस्तारं|व्यस्तारः
व्यस्तार n. (-रं) The issue of the fluid from the temples of the elephant.<BR>E. व्यस्त pervaded, ऋ to go, aff. ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यह्न
व्यह्न mfn. (-ह्नः-ह्ना-ह्नं) Done or produced, &c. in two days.<BR> E. वि sever-<BR>ally, and अह्न for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकरण|व्याकरणं
व्याकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The science of grammar, considered as one of the<BR>six Vedāṇgas.<BR>	 2. Explaining, expounding.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before<BR>कृ to make or do, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकार|व्याकारः
व्याकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Change of form.<BR>	 2. Deformity.<BR> E. वि and आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकीर्ण
व्याकीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Scattered, tossed, or thrown about or away. E.<BR>वि and आङ् before कॄ to scatter, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुल|व्याकुलः
व्याकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Confounded, bewildered, perplexed, overcome<BR>with fear, &c.<BR>	 2. Busily engaged in.<BR> E. वि before आकुल the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलता
व्याकुलता f. (-ता) Perplexity, agitation, alarm.<BR> E. तल् added to the last;<BR>also with त्व, व्याकुलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलमनस्
व्याकुलमनस् mfn. (-नाः-नाः-नः) Agitated, flurried, bewildered.<BR> E. व्याकुल, मनस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलित
व्याकुलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Agitated, flurried, perplexed.<BR> E. व्याकुल, इतच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकूति|व्याकूतिः
व्याकूति f. (-तिः) Fraud, deception, disguise.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before कू to sound, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृत
व्याकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Expounded, explained, made clear.<BR>	 2. Trans-<BR>formed, changed.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before कृ to make, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृति|व्याकृतिः
व्याकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Explaining, making clear.<BR>	 2. Grammar.<BR>	 3. Change<BR>of form.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before कृ to make, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकोश|व्याकोशः
व्याकोश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Budded, blown.<BR> E. वि and आङ् implying<BR>separation, and कोश or कोष a sheath; also व्याकोष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकोष|व्याकोषः
व्याकोष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Budded, blown, (as a flower.) E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्षेप|व्याक्षेपः
व्याक्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Tossing about.<BR>	 2. Delay, hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्या
व्याख्या f. (-ख्या)<BR>	 1. Exposition, explanation, gloss, comment.<BR>	 2.<BR>Communication.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before ख्या to relate, aff. अच् or<BR>अङ् and टाप् affs.; also with ल्युट् aff. व्याख्यान n. (-नं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यागम्य|व्याख्यागम्यं
व्याख्यागम्य n. (-म्यं) Indistinct averment, proceeding from grammatical<BR>inaccuracy or faulty construction.<BR> E. व्याख्या an explanation, and<BR>आगम्य to be attained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यात|व्याख्यातः
व्याख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Spoken, said.<BR>	 2. Conquered, overcome.<BR>	 3.<BR>Explained, expounded.<BR>	 4. Related, narrated, told.<BR> E. वि and<BR>आङ् before ख्या to say, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यान|व्याख्यानं
व्याख्यान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Narration, speech.<BR>	 2. Explanation, interpretation,<BR>exposition.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before ख्या to say, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्येय
व्याख्येय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be explained or described.<BR> E. वि and आङ्<BR>before ख्या to say, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=697-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघट्टन|व्याघट्टनं
व्याघट्टन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rubbing, friction.<BR>	 2. Churning.<BR> E. वि and आङ्<BR>before घट्ट् to use effort, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघट्टित
व्याघट्टित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Rubbed, rubbed together.<BR>	 2. Stirred,<BR>churned.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before घट्ट् to use effort, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघात|व्याघातः
व्याघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Obstacle, impediment.<BR>	 2. Striking, beating.<BR>	 3. Des-<BR>troying, destruction.<BR>	 4. Contradiction.<BR>	 5. The thirteenth of the<BR>astronomical Yogas.<BR>	 6. A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>	 7. A rhetorical<BR>figure, the production of two different effects from a similar cause<BR>or by similar agency.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before हन् to strike, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघातक
व्याघातक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what opposes, resists, &c.<BR> E. वि and<BR>आङ् before हन् to strike, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघातिन्
व्याघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Who or what opposes, resists, beats, &c.<BR>E. वि and आङ् before हन् to strike, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघारित
व्याघारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sprinkled, lubricated, (as with oil or ghee.)<BR>E. वि and आङ् before घॄ to sprinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्र|व्याघ्रः
व्याघ्र m. (-घ्रः)<BR>	 1. A tiger.<BR>	 2. (In composition,) Best, pre-eminent, (at<BR>the end of a compound.)<BR>	 3. A variety of the castor-oil plant,<BR>(the red variety.)<BR>	 4. A tree, (Galedupa arborea.)<BR>	 f. (-घ्री) A prickly<BR>sort of nightshade, (Solanum jacquini.)<BR> E. वि and आङ् before घ्रा<BR>to smell, Unādi aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रचर्म्मन्|व्याघ्रचर्मन्
व्याघ्रचर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) A tiger's skin.<BR> E. व्याघ्र and चर्म्मन् skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रदल|व्याघ्रदलः
व्याघ्रदल m. (-लः) A red variety of the castor-oil tree.<BR> E. व्याघ्रस्तत्पाद इव दलमस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रनख|व्याघ्रनखं|व्याघ्रनखः
व्याघ्रनख nf. (-खं-खी)<BR>	 1. A tiger's claw.<BR>	 2. A sort of perfume.<BR>	 n. (-खं)<BR>	 1.<BR>A kind of root.<BR>	 2. A scratch or impression of the finger-nails. E.<BR>व्याघ्र a tiger, and नख a nail, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रनखक|व्याघ्रनखकं
व्याघ्रनखक n. (-कं) A scratch, the impression of a finger-nail.<BR> E. व्याघ्र a<BR>tiger, and नख a nail, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रनायक|व्याघ्रनायकः
व्याघ्रनायक m. (-कः) A jackal.<BR> E. व्याघ्र a tiger, and नायक leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रपाद|व्याघ्रपादः
व्याघ्रपाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Flacourtia sapida, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A saint and<BR>law-giver, so named from having feet like those of a tiger.<BR> E. व्याघ्र<BR>a tiger, and पाद the foot of paw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रपुच्छ|व्याघ्रपुच्छः
व्याघ्रपुच्छ m. (-च्छः) The castor-oil tree, (Palma Christi, or Ricinus<BR>communis.)<BR> E. व्याघ्र a tiger, and पुच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्राट|व्याघ्राटः
व्याघ्राट m. (-टः) A sky-lark.<BR> E. व्याघ्र a tiger, and अट what goes, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रास्य|व्याघ्रास्यः
व्याघ्रास्य m. (-स्यः) A cat.<BR> E. व्याघ्र a tiger, and आस्य the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याज|व्याजः
व्याज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Deceit, fraud, craft, cunning.<BR>	 2. Disguise, either of<BR>purpose or person.<BR>	 3. Wickedness.<BR> E. वि before अज् to go, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याजनिन्दा
व्याजनिन्दा f. (-न्दा) Apparent censure, but covert praise, a figure of<BR>rhetoric.<BR> E. व्याज disguise, and निन्दा censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याजसुप्त
व्याजसुप्त Adj. A feigning sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याजस्तुति|व्याजस्तुतिः
व्याजस्तुति f. (-तिः) Praise or censure, conveyed in language that<BR>expresses the contrary, affected reproach or ironical commenda-<BR>tion.<BR> E. व्याज disguise, and स्तुति praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याजोक्ति|व्याजोक्तिः
व्याजोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Covert expression of any thing so as to mislead<BR>others from its real cause.<BR> E. व्याज craft or disguise, उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याड|व्याडः
व्याड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. A carnivorous animal or beast of prey.<BR>3. INDRA.<BR>	 4. A villain, a rogue.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before अड् to<BR>make effort, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याडि|व्याडिः
व्याडि m. (-डिः) The name of a celebrated grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यात्त|व्यात्तं
व्यात्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Vast, expanded.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before अत् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यात्युक्षी
व्यात्युक्षी f. (-क्षी) Bathing for amusement, sporting in water.<BR> E. वि and<BR>अति before उक्ष् to sprinkle, aff. णच् and अण् and ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादान|व्यादानं
व्यादान n. (-नं) Opening, setting open or ajar.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before दा<BR>to give, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादिश|व्यादिशः
व्यादिश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A director, a commander.<BR> E. वि + आ + दिश्-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याध|व्याधं|व्याधः
व्याध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. A hunter, one who lives by killing deer, &c.<BR>	 2. A<BR>low or wicked man.<BR> E. व्यध् to pierce, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधभीत|व्याधभीतः
व्याधभीत m. (-तः) A deer.<BR> E. व्याध a hunter, भीत afraid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधाम|व्याधामः
व्याधाम m. (-मः) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before धा to have,<BR>मन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधाव|व्याधावः
व्याधाव m. (-वः) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before धू to trem-<BR>ble, causal form, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधि|व्याधिः
व्याधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease in general, (op. to आधि or “mental<BR>distress.”)<BR>	 2. Leprosy.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before धा to have, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिकर
व्याधिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Causing sickness.<BR> E. व्याधि and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिधात
व्याधिधात m. (-तः) A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. व्याधि disease, हन् to destroy,<BR>aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिघ्न|व्याधिघ्नः
व्याधिघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Causing or removing disease.<BR> E. व्याधि and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधित|व्याधितः
व्याधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sick, ill, disease.<BR> E. व्याधि sickness, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधियुक्त
व्याधियुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Sick, diseased.<BR> E. व्यावि, युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिरहित
व्याधिरहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Free from disease, convalescent.<BR> E. व्याधि, रहित left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधुत|व्याधुतः
व्याधुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shaken, shaking, trembling, tremulous.<BR> E. वि,<BR>आङ् before धु to shake, aff. क्त; also from धू with क्त, व्याधूत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याध्युपशम
व्याध्युपशम m. (-मः) Allaying or curing disease.<BR> E. व्याधि, उपशम allaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यान|व्यानः
व्यान m. (-नः) One of the five vital airs, that which is diffused through-<BR>out the body.<BR> E. वि before अन् to breathe, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यानक
व्यानक n. (-कं) A mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापक|व्यापकः
व्यापक mfn. (-कः-पिका-कं)<BR>	 1. Diffusive, comprehensive, spreading or<BR>extending widely.<BR>	 2. (In law,) Comprehending all the points of an<BR>argument, pervading the whole plea.<BR>	 3. (In logic,) Embracing the<BR>whole of an argument or objection.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Essential and inherent<BR>property.<BR> E. वि before आप् to pervade, ण्वुल् aff., implying the agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापकत्व
व्यापकत्व n. (-त्वं) Diffusion, pervasion.<BR> E. त्व added to the last; also<BR>with तल्, व्यापकता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापत्ति|व्यापत्तिः
व्यापत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Misfortune, ruin.<BR>	 2. Substitution of one thing for another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापद्
व्यापद् f. (-पद्)<BR>	 1. Death, decease.<BR>	 2. Calamity.<BR>	 3. Derangement.<BR>	 4.<BR>Disease.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before पद् to go, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापद
व्यापद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Ruin.<BR>	 2. Evil design, malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापन|व्यापनं
व्यापन n. (-नं) Spreading through or throughout, pervading, penetra-<BR>ting.<BR> E. वि before आप् to obtain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापन्न|व्यापन्नः
व्यापन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Dead, deceased, expired.<BR>	 2. Hurt, injured,<BR>killed.<BR>	 3. Deranged, disordered.<BR>	 4. Vitiated, diseased.<BR>	 5. Fallen<BR>into misfortune.<BR>	 6. Substituted.<BR> E. वि, आङ् before पद् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापाद|व्यापादः
व्यापाद m. (-दः) Evil-design, malice, prepense, the wish or project to<BR>injure another person.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before पद् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादन|व्यापादनं
व्यापादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaying.<BR>	 2. Wishing or seeking to injure<BR>any one, ill-will, malice, evil design.<BR>	 3. Ruin.<BR> E. वि and आङ्<BR>before पद् to go, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादयितव्य
व्यापादयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be killed, what may or ought to be<BR>put to death.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before पद् to go, causal v., तव्य aff.;<BR>also व्यापादनीय and व्यापाद्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादित|व्यापादितः
व्यापादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Hurt, injured.<BR>	 2. Slain, killed.<BR> E. वि and<BR>आङ् before पद् to go, causal form, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादितवत्
व्यापादितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having killed, killing.<BR> E. वि and आङ्<BR>before पद् to go, causal v., क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापार|व्यापारः
व्यापार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Occupation, business, trade.<BR>	 2. Exercise, practice.<BR>3. Effort.<BR>	 4. Meddling.<BR> E. वि, आङ् before पृ to be busy, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारयत्
व्यापारयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Setting to work, employing.<BR> E. वि and<BR>आङ् before पृ to be busy, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारित
व्यापारित f. (-ता) Set to work, employed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारिन्
व्यापारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Motor, the cause or agent of motion<BR>or occupation.<BR>	 2. Busy, occupied.<BR>	 3. Exercising, practising.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-री) A dealer.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before पृ to be busy, causal form, aff.<BR>णिनि; or व्यापार business, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापिन्
व्यापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि)<BR>	 1. Diffusive, comprehensive.<BR>	 2. All-pervading.<BR>3. Covering.<BR>	 m. (-पी) The pervading property or power, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>and आप् to pervade, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापृत|व्यापृतः
व्यापृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Engaged, busy.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A minister, a member<BR>of royal government.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before पृ to be busy, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापृति|व्यापृतिः
व्यापृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Occupation.<BR>	 2. Effort.<BR>	 3. Action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्त|व्याप्तं
व्याप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Pervaded, occupied or penetrated by thorough-<BR>ly and essentially, (as the universe by spirit, &c.)<BR>	 2. Celebrated,<BR>famous.<BR>	 3. Filled, full of.<BR>	 4. Placed, fixed.<BR>	 5. Obtained, possessed.<BR>6. Encircled, encompassed, surrounded.<BR>	 7. Open, apart, out-<BR>spread.<BR>	 8. Included.<BR>	 9. Invariably accompanied, (in logic.)<BR> E. वि<BR>before आप् to pervade, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्ति|व्याप्तिः
व्याप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Pervading, inherence, the inherent and essential<BR>presence of any one, (thing or property,) in another, as of oil in the<BR>sesamum seed, heat in fire, or the Deity in the universe, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Getting, obtaining, gain.<BR>	 3. Universal permeation, omnipresence,<BR>as one of ŚIVA'S superhuman properties.<BR>	 4. An universal rule.<BR>	 5.<BR>Fulness.<BR> E. वि and आप् to pervade, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्तिग्रह|व्याप्तिग्रहः
व्याप्तिग्रह m. (-हः) Induction of universal concomitance, (in logic.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्तिज्ञान
व्याप्तिज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge of the existence of a substance from<BR>observation of the presence of its inherent properties.<BR> E. व्याप्ति, and<BR>ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्तिमत्|व्याप्तिमन्त्
व्याप्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Diffusive, pervading.<BR> E. व्याप्ति and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्तिलक्षण
व्याप्तिलक्षण n. (-णं) Sign or proof of the existence or nonexistence of an<BR>inherent property or attribute.<BR> E. व्याप्ति, and लक्षण indication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्य|व्याप्यं|व्याप्यः
व्याप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं)<BR>	 1. Permeable, penetrable.<BR>	 2. Capable of contain-<BR>ing any inherent property.<BR>	 n. (-प्यं)<BR>	 1. An instrument or agent.<BR>	 2.<BR>The thing or substance which may be the site or subject of attri-<BR>butes or inherent properties.<BR>	 3. The subject of an inference, as<BR>fire inferred from the presence of smoke, &c.<BR>	 4. A drug, (Costus<BR>speciosus.)<BR> E. वि before आप् to pervade, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्यत्व|व्याप्यत्वं
व्याप्यत्व n. (-त्वं) Capacity of being penetrated or essentially effected by.<BR> E. व्याप्य, त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्यत्वासिद्धि|व्याप्यत्वासिद्धिः
व्याप्यत्वासिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) (In logic,) Imperfect conclusion, one not compre-<BR>hending all the points of the argument.<BR> E. व्याप्यत्व, असिद्धि non-con-<BR>clusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभ्युक्षी
व्याभ्युक्षी f. (-क्षी) Gamboling in water, bathing for pleasure.<BR> E. वि, आङ्<BR>and अभि before उक्ष् to sprinkle, affs. अच् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याम|व्यामः
व्याम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A fathom, or the space between the tips of the<BR>fingers of either hand when the arms are extended.<BR>	 2. Disregard.<BR>3. Smoke.<BR> E. वि before अम् to go, with आङ् prefix and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामन|व्यामनं
व्यामन n. (-नं) Disregard, disrespect.<BR> E. वि before अम् to go, with आङ्<BR>prefixed, and ल्युट् aff.; or वि priv., म्ला to mind, आङ् prefix, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामर्ष|व्यामर्षः
व्यामर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Rubbing out, erasure.<BR>	 2. Impatience.<BR> E. वि and आङ्<BR>before मृष् to rub, &c. घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामिल्य
व्यामिल्य Ind. Having closed and opened, having twinkled, &c.<BR> E. वि<BR>and आङ् before मिल् to twinkle, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामिश्र|व्यामिश्रं
व्यामिश्र mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं) Mixed, blended, mingled.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before मिश्र mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामृष्ट
व्यामृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Rubbed, rubbed out, effaced.<BR> E. वि and आङ्<BR>before मृष् to rub, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामोह|व्यामोहः
व्यामोह m. (-हः) Embarrassment, bewilderment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायच्छमान|व्यायछमान
व्यायच्छमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Quarrelling.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before इण् to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायत|व्यायतं
व्यायत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Busy, occupied.<BR>	 2. Long.<BR>	 3. Hard, firm.<BR>	 4.<BR>Much, excessive.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before यम् to stop, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायाम|व्यायामः
व्यायाम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Fatigue, labour.<BR>	 2. A fathom, measured by the dis-<BR>tance to which both arms extended reach.<BR>	 3. Gymnastics, athletic<BR>exercise, as playing with heavy clubs, yielding a bow with a<BR>chain in place of a string, alternate rising and falling at full<BR>length on the ground, &c.<BR>	 4. Manhood, manliness.<BR>	 5. A difficulty.<BR>6. A difficult or impassable defile, &c.<BR>	 7. Business, occupation. E.<BR>वि and आङ् before यम् to refrain, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायामशील
व्यायामशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Active, robust, athletic, taking exercise. E.<BR>व्यायाम, शील practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायामिन्
व्यायामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Taking exercise, undergoing fatigue,<BR>active, athletic.<BR> E. व्यायाम and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायाम्य
व्यायाम्य Ind. Having exercised, practised as gymnastics, &c. disci-<BR>plined as troops.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before यम् to restrain, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायोग|व्यायोगः
व्यायोग m. (-गः) A kind of dramatic exhibition or composition in one<BR>act, the subject of which is some contest or war of a heroic kind,<BR>and of which woman is not the cause.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before युज् to<BR>unite, aff. घञ्; in which the valiant are associated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याल|व्यालः
व्याल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Wicked, villainous, bad.<BR>	 2. Cruel, fierce.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. A beast of prey.<BR>	 3. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 4. A<BR>vicious elephant.<BR>	 5. A king.<BR>	 6. A species of the Dandaka metre.<BR>E. वि and आङ् before अल् to adorn, aff. अच्; or अड् to make effort,<BR>aff. घञ् and ड changed to ल; hence also व्याड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालक|व्यालकः
व्यालक m. (-कः) A vicious elephant.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालग्राह|व्यालग्राहः
व्यालग्राह m. (-हः) A snake-catcher.<BR> E. व्याल a snake, ग्रह् to seize, aff. अण्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालग्राहिन्
व्यालग्राहिन् m. (-ही) A snake-catcher, one who lives by catching and<BR>exhibiting snakes.<BR> E. व्याल a snake, and ग्राहिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालतम
व्यालतम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Very injurious, cruel or fierce.<BR> E. व्याल, तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालमृग|व्यालमृगः
व्यालमृग m. (-गः) A flerce or wild stag.<BR> E. व्याल and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालम्ब|व्यालंब|व्यालंबः|व्यालम्बः
व्यालम्ब m. (-म्बः) The red variety of the castor-oil plant. वि + आ + लवि-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालायुध|व्यालायुधं|व्यालायुधः
व्यालायुध n. (-धं) A sort of perfume; see नखी.<BR> E. व्याल a beast of prey<BR>(a tiger,) आयुध a weapon, compared to the claw of the animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालिखत्
व्यालिखत् mfn. (-खन्-खन्ती-खत्)<BR>	 1. Drawing lines, delineating, scratch-<BR>ing, piercing.<BR>	 2. Extending to, in contact with.<BR> E. वि and आङ्<BR>before लिख् to write, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालीन
व्यालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Thick, clustering.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before ली to waste, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालोल
व्यालोल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Tremulous, shaking, waving.<BR> E. वि and आङ्<BR>before लोल् to shake, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावकलन|व्यावकलनं
व्यावकलन n. (-नं) Subtraction, (in arithmetic.)<BR> E. वि with आङ् and अव<BR>before कल् to count, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावकलित
व्यावकलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Subtracted.<BR> E. वि with आङ् and अव before कल् to count, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावक्रोशी
व्यावक्रोशी f. (-शी) Mutual imprecation.<BR> E. वि with आङ् and अव before<BR>क्रुश् to cry out, aff. णच्, अण and ङीप् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावभाषी
व्यावभाषी f. (-षी) Mutual abuse or imprecation.<BR> E. वि implying recipro-<BR>city, and अव depreciation, भाष् to speak, affs. णच् and ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्त्त|व्यावर्त|व्यावर्तः|व्यावर्त्तः
व्यावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. Going round, revolving.<BR>	 2. Encompassing.<BR>	 3. Choos-<BR>ing, appointing.<BR>	 4. Ruptured navel, (umbilical hernia.)<BR> E. वि and<BR>आङ् before वृत् to be, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्त्तक|व्यावर्तक
व्यावर्त्तक f. (-र्त्तिका)<BR>	 1. Excluding, separating from.<BR>	 2. Turning away from.<BR>	 3. Surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्त्तन|व्यावर्तन|व्यावर्तनं
व्यावर्त्तन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rolling round, revolving.<BR>	 2. A volute, a fold, a<BR>band.<BR>	 3. Encompassing.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before वृत् to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहारिक|व्यावहारिकः
व्यावहारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Usual, customary.<BR>	 2. Juridical, judicial,<BR>legal, relative or referring to judicial procedure.<BR>	 3. Relating to<BR>business.<BR>	 4. Relating to the worldly life of illusion, (in Vedānta<BR>phil.)<BR>	 m. (-कः) A counseller, a minister.<BR> E. व्यवहार litigation, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहारी
व्यावहारी f. (-री) Mutual seizing.<BR> E. वि + अव + हृ-णच् स्वार्थे अण्-ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहासी
व्यावहासी f. (-सी) Mutual or reciprocal laughter.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before<BR>हस् to laugh, aff. णच्, अण् and ङीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याविध
व्याविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Of various kinds or sorts.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before विध sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत
व्यावृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Covered, screened.<BR>	 2. Removed, excepted. E.<BR>वि and आङ् before वृ to choose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृति|व्यावृतिः
व्यावृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Exception, exclusion.<BR>	 2. Covering, screening.<BR> E. वि<BR>and आङ् before वृ to choose, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्त|व्यावृत्तः
व्यावृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Chosen, appointed.<BR>	 2. Encompassed,<BR>surrounded.<BR>	 3. Fenced, screened.<BR>	 4. Removed, uncovered.<BR>	 5.<BR>Excepted, excluded.<BR>	 6. Praised, hymned.<BR>	 7. Rolled backwards.<BR>	 8.<BR>Revolved.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before वृत् to be, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्ति|व्यावृत्तिः
व्यावृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Praise, eulogium.<BR>	 2. Rejection, exception, exclu-<BR>sion.<BR>	 3. Choice, selection.<BR>	 4. Screening, surrounding.<BR>	 5. Rolling<BR>back.<BR>	 6. Turning away.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before वृत् to be, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यास|व्यासः
व्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A celebrated saint and author, the supposed original<BR>compiler of the Vedas and Purāṇas; also the founder of the<BR>Vedānta philosophy.<BR>	 2. Diffusion, extension.<BR>	 3. Detail, distinc-<BR>tion, severalty.<BR>	 4. A measure.<BR>	 5. The diameter of a circle.<BR>	 6. A<BR>fault in pronunciation.<BR>	 7. Arrangement, compilation.<BR>	 8. The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">Page700-a+ 60</a>]<BR>analysis of a compound word.<BR>	 9. A public reader of the Purāṇas.<BR>E. वि and आङ् before अस् to pervade, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासक्त|व्यासक्तः
व्यासक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Bewildered.<BR>	 2. Connected with, attached or<BR>devoted to.<BR>	 3. Detached, separated.<BR> E. वि before आसक्त attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासङ्ग|व्यासंग|व्यासंगः|व्यासङ्गः
व्यासङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Confusion, perplexity.<BR>	 2. Separation, detachment.<BR>3. Attachment, addiction.<BR>	 4. Assiduous application.<BR>	 5. Diligent<BR>study.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before षञ्ज् to embrace, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासिद्ध|व्यासिद्धः
व्यासिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Prohibited, forbidden.<BR>	 2. Contraband, not<BR>allowed to be sold but to particular persons or in certain places.<BR>E. वि privative, and आसिद्ध perfected, accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहत|व्याहतः
व्याहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Confused, alarmed.<BR>	 2. Repelled, repulsed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Driving out, expelled.<BR>	 4. Disappointed.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before हन्<BR>to strike, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहरण|व्याहरणं
व्याहरण n. (-णं) Utterance, pronunciation.<BR>	 2. Narration, speech.<BR> E. वि<BR>and आङ् before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहरत्
व्याहरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Speaking, uttering, pronouncing.<BR> E. वि and<BR>आङ् before हृ to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहार|व्याहारः
व्याहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Voice, speech.<BR>	 2. A word, an articulate sound.<BR>	 3.<BR>Jest, joke, humorous speech.<BR> E. वि, आङ् before हृ to take, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृत
व्याहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uttered, said.<BR> E. वि, आङ् before हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृति|व्याहृतिः
व्याहृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Voice, speech.<BR>	 2. A word, an articulate sound.<BR>	 3. A<BR>mystical word or sound, as Om, Bhūr, Bhuvah, Swer, &c., which<BR>are the Mahā-Vyāhritis, and commence the daily prayers of the<BR>Brāhman.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before हृ to take, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृत्य
व्याहृत्य Ind. Having said or uttered.<BR> E. वि and आङ् before हृ to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छेद|व्युच्छेदः
व्युच्छेद m. (-दः) Cutting off, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत|व्युतः
व्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sewn, woven.<BR> E. वि before उत woven; also व्यूत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युति|व्युतिः
व्युति f. (-तिः) Sewing, weaving.<BR> E. वि before ऊय् to weave, aff. क्तिन्, form<BR>irr.; also व्यूति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रम|व्युत्क्रमं|व्युत्क्रमः
व्युत्क्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Inverted order, irregular arrangement.<BR>	 2. Trans-<BR>gression.<BR> E. वि and उद् before क्रम order, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रान्ता|व्युत्क्रांता
व्युत्क्रान्ता f. (-न्ता)<BR>	 1. Overstepped.<BR>	 2. Departed, left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्थान|व्युत्थानं
व्युत्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Independence, following one's own inclination.<BR>	 2.<BR>Opposition, contradiction, doing that which is prohibited.<BR>	 3.<BR>Obstruction, prohibition, hindering or opposing any one.<BR>	 4.<BR>Contempt.<BR>	 5. Completion of religious contemplation, the end of a<BR>period of abstraction.<BR> E. वि, उद् before स्था to stay or be, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पत्ति|व्युत्पत्तिः
व्युत्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Science, learning, conversancy with or proficiency<BR>in literature or science.<BR>	 2. Origin.<BR>	 3. Formation of words,<BR>derivation, etymology.<BR> E. वि and उद before पद् to go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पन्न|व्युत्पन्नः
व्युत्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Learned, studied, conversant or proficient in<BR>literature.<BR>	 2. Completed, finished.<BR>	 3. Derived, formed as a deri-<BR>vative word, (as opposed to a primitive word.)<BR>	 4. Generated,<BR>begotten.<BR> E. वि and उद् before पद् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदस्त
व्युदस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Put off, thrown aside, (especially as feeling or<BR>affection,) rejected.<BR> E. वि and उद् before अस् to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदस्य
व्युदस्य Ind. Having thrown off or put away, (as desire, feeling &c.) E.<BR>वि and उद् before अस् to throw, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदास|व्युदासः
व्युदास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Indifference to, disregard for.<BR>	 2. Making ill or<BR>unprofitable use of any thing, throwing away.<BR>	 3. Prohibition. E.<BR>वि and उद् before अस् to throw, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपदेश|व्युपदेशः
व्युपदेश m. (-शः) Pretext, deception, plausible but false council.<BR> E. वि priv., उपदेश advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपरम|व्युपरमः
व्युपरम m. (-मः) Stop, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपशम|व्युपशमः
व्युपशम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Inquietude.<BR>	 2. Cessation.<BR>	 3. Non-cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्
व्युष् r. 10th cl. (व्युषयति-ते) To abandon, to reject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्ट|व्युष्टं|व्युष्टः
व्युष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Burnt.<BR>	 2. Dawned, become daylight or dawn.<BR>3. Become clear.<BR>	 4. Dwelt.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Dawn, break of day.<BR>	 2. Day.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fruit, consequence.<BR> E. वि before वस् to abide, aff. क्त, and व changed<BR>to उ; or वि before उष् to burn, क्त aff. वा० इडभावः; or as derived<BR>from व्युष् to burn, &c., when it is more properly read व्युष्ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्टि|व्युष्टिः
व्युष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Fruit, consequence.<BR>	 2. Increase, prosperity.<BR>	 3. Praise.<BR>E. वि and वस् to abide, aff. क्तिन् and व changed to उ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युस्
व्युस्(इर)व्युसिर r. 4th cl. (व्युस्यति) To leave, to abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढ|व्यूढः
व्यूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Arranged, arrayed, placed in order or array.<BR>	 2.<BR>Compact, firm, well-knit.<BR>	 3. Large, great.<BR>	 4. Disarranged.<BR>	 5.<BR>Married.<BR> E. वि before वह् to bear, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढकङ्कट|व्यूढकंकट|व्यूढकङ्कटः
व्यूढकङ्कट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Armed, mailed.<BR> E. व्यूढ arranged, कङ्कट mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढोरस्क
व्यूढोरस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) Broad-chested.<BR> E. व्यूढ, उरस् breast, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढि|व्यूढिः
व्यूढि f. (-ढिः) Array, orderly arrangement or disposition.<BR> E. वि before<BR>वह् to bear, or ऊह् to reason, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूत|व्यूतं
व्यूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Woven.<BR> E. वि before ऊत the same; or वि + वे-क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूति|व्यूतिः
व्यूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Weaving.<BR>	 2. The wages of weaving.<BR> E. वि before वेञ्<BR>to weave, aff. क्तिन् and व changed to ऊ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूह|व्यूहः
व्यूह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Military array, the arrangement of troops in various<BR>positions; as दण्डव्यूहः the array in line, भोगव्यूहः in column, मण्डल-<BR>व्यूहः in circle, असंहतव्यूहः in mixed order; also various fanciful<BR>forms, as the शकटः or car-shape, मकरः or marine monster-like,<BR>पताका flag-shape, &c.<BR>	 2. A flock, a multitude.<BR>	 3. Logic, reasoning.<BR>4. Making, manufacture.<BR>	 5. The body.<BR>	 6. Formation, structure.<BR>	 7.<BR>A squadron.<BR> E. वि before ऊह् to reason, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहन|व्यूहनं
व्यूहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Arrying, array.<BR>	 2. Structure of the body, disposition<BR>of the members of the body.<BR> E. वि before ऊह् to reason, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहपार्ष्णि|व्यूहपार्ष्णिः
व्यूहपार्ष्णि m. (-र्ष्णिः) The rear of an army.<BR> E. व्यूह array, and पार्ष्णि the<BR>heel or back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहभङ्ग|व्यूहभङ्गः
व्यूहभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Throwing into disorder, breaking an array.<BR> E. व्यूहभङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहभेद|व्यूहभेदः
व्यूहभेद m. (-दः) Piercing or breaking an array.<BR> E. व्यूह, भेद breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यृद्धि|व्यृद्धिः
व्यृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Non-prosperity, ill-luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ये
व्ये(ञ)व्येञ् r. 1st cl. (व्ययति-ते)<BR>	 1. To cover.<BR>	 2. To sew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यो
व्यो Ind.<BR>	 1. Iron.<BR>	 2. Seed.<BR> E. व्ये-डो ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योकार|व्योकारः
व्योकार m. (-रः) A blacksmith.<BR> E. व्यो an imitative sound, or iron, कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमकेश|व्योमकेशः
व्योमकेश m. (-शः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. व्योम heaven, and केश hair; also with इनि poss.<BR>aff. added व्योमकेशिन् m. (-शी) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमचारिन्
व्योमचारिन् m. (-री)<BR>	 1. A God.<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR>	 3. A saint.<BR>	 4. A heavenly<BR>body.<BR> E. व्योम heaven, and चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमचारिपुर|व्योमचारिपुरं
व्योमचारिपुर n. (-रं) The city of HARIŚCHANDRA, suspended midway<BR>between heaven and earth.<BR> E. व्योम heaven, चारि going, पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमधूम|व्योमधूमः
व्योमधूम m. (-मः) A cloud.<BR> E. व्योम heaven and धूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमन्
व्योमन् n. (-म)<BR>	 1. Sky, heaven, atmosphere.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. A temple,<BR>sacred to the sun, or place where he is especially worshipped.<BR>	 4.<BR>Talc.<BR> E. व्येञ् to cover, Unādi aff. मनिन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमनासिका
व्योमनासिका f. (-का) A sort of quail.<BR> E. व्योम heaven, नासिका the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योममञ्जर|व्योममंजर|व्योममञ्जरं
व्योममञ्जर n. (-रं) A flag, a banner.<BR> E. व्योम the sky, and मञ्जर a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योममण्डल|व्योममंडल|व्योममण्डलं
व्योममण्डल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A flag.<BR>	 2. The horizon.<BR> E. व्योम sky, मण्डल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योममाय
व्योममाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Measuring the sky, high as the heavens. E.<BR>व्योम and माय what measures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योममुद्गर|व्योममुद्गरः
व्योममुद्गर m. (-रः) A gust of wind.<BR> E. व्योम the sky, and मुद्गर a club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमयान|व्योमयानं
व्योमयान n. (-नं) A carriage of the gods.<BR> E. व्योम the sky, यान a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमविस्तृत
व्योमविस्तृत n. (-तं) The expanse or firmament.<BR> E. व्योम and विस्तृत spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमसद्
व्योमसद् m. (-सद्) A spirit of heaven, a divinity.<BR> E. व्योम, सद who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमस्थली
व्योमस्थली f. (-ली) The earth.<BR> E. व्योम the sky, and स्थली base or site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमस्पृश्
व्योमस्पृश् mfn. (-स्पृक्) Sky-touching, lofty.<BR> E. व्योम, स्पृश् what touches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमाभ|व्योमाभः
व्योमाभ m. (-भः) A Jaina deified saint.<BR> E. व्योम sky, and आभ shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योष|व्योषं
व्योष n. (-षं) The aggregate of three spices, or black-pepper, long-<BR>pepper, and dry ginger.<BR> E. वि variously, उष् to burn, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्
व्रज् r. 1st cl. (व्रजति)<BR>	 1. To go, to travel.<BR>	 2. To pass away, (as time.)<BR>With अनु, 1. To follow.<BR>	 2. To perform. With परि prefixed, To<BR>wander about, as a mendicant. With प्र, 1. To go into exile.<BR>	 2.<BR>To enter on the fourth stage of life. With प्रति, To go to or<BR>towards. r. 10th cl. (व्राजयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To prepare, to perfect.<BR>	 2. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज|व्रजं|व्रजः
व्रज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A cow-pen, a station of cowherds.<BR>	 2. A road.<BR>	 3. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">Page701-a+ 60</a>]<BR>flock, a herd, a multitude.<BR>	 4. The district about Āgrā and Mathurā,<BR>the scene of KṚṢṆA'S juvenile adventures.<BR>	 5. An abode.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>Wandering, roaming.<BR> E. व्रज् to go, aff. घञर्ये-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजत्
व्रजत् mfn. (-जन्-जन्ती-जत्) Going, roaming.<BR> E. व्रज् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजन|व्रजनं
व्रजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going, roaming.<BR>	 2. Exile.<BR> E. व्रज् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजभू
व्रजभू m. (-भूः) A tree, (Nauclea cordifolia.)<BR> E. व्रज a cow-pen, भू being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजाङ्गना|व्रजांगना
व्रजाङ्गना f. (-ना) A woman of Vraja, a cowherdess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजाजिर
व्रजाजिर n. (-रं) A cow-yard, a cattle-fold or pen.<BR> E. व्रज, अजिर a yard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजित
व्रजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone, going.<BR>	 n. (-त) Roaming.<BR> E. व्रज् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्या
व्रज्या f. (-ज्या)<BR>	 1. Wandering about, either as an act of religious austeri-<BR>ty or in quest of alms.<BR>	 2. March of an assailant, attack, invasion.<BR>3. March in general.<BR>	 4. A class, a flock, a tribe.<BR>	 5. A theatre. E.<BR>व्रज् to go, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्यावत्|व्रज्यावन्त्
व्रज्यावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Wandering, roaming.<BR>	 2. Going gracefully.<BR> E. व्रज्या, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण्
व्रण् r. 1st cl. (व्रणति) To sound. r. 10th cl. (व्रणयति-ते) To wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण|व्रणं|व्रणः
व्रण mn. (-णः-णं) A tumor, a boil, an ulcer, a wound.<BR> E. व्रण् to wound,<BR>an abscess, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणकृत्
व्रणकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Making a sore, wounding, ulcerating, corroding, &c.<BR>m. (-कृत्) Marking-nut plant, (Semicarpus anacardium.)<BR> E. व्रण a<BR>sore, कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणद्विष्
व्रणद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR> E. व्रण a sore, द्विष्<BR>hostile to, healing, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणधूपन
व्रणधूपन n. (-नं) Fumigating a sore.<BR> E. व्रण, धूपन burning incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणवस्तु
व्रणवस्तु m. (-स्तुः) Part liable to ulcerate, as skin, flesh, &c.<BR> E. व्रण, वस्तु<BR>substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणविरोपण
व्रणविरोपण Adj. Healing a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणवेदना
व्रणवेदना f. (-ना) Pain of a wound or sore.<BR> E. व्रण and वेदना pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणशोधन
व्रणशोधन n. (-नं) Cleaning or cicatrising a sore.<BR> E. व्रण, शोधन cleaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणह|व्रणहः
व्रणह m. (-हः) The castor-oil tree.<BR>	 f. (-हा) A sort of creeper, (Menis-<BR>permum glabrum.)<BR> E. व्रण a sore, and हन् to destroy, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणाश
व्रणाश m. (-शः) Gum-myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणिन्
व्रणिन् mfn. (-णी-णिनी-णि) Having a boil, a sore or wound.<BR> E. व्रण, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रत|व्रतं|व्रतः
व्रत mn. (-तः-तं)<BR>	 1. Any meritorious act of devotion, the voluntary or<BR>vowed observance, or imposition of any penance, austerity, or<BR>privation, as fasting, continence, exposure to heat and cold, &c.<BR>2. Eating.<BR>	 3. Design, plan.<BR>	 4. Vow, resolution.<BR>	 5. Course of con-<BR>duct.<BR> E. वृ to choose, aff. अतच्, र substituted for the vowel; or<BR>व्रज् to go, (to heaven by it,) घ aff. and ज changed to त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतति|व्रततिः
व्रतति f. (-तिः or ती)<BR>	 1. Expansion, spreading.<BR>	 2. A creeper.<BR> E. वृत् to<BR>abide, अति aff.; the vowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतपारणा
व्रतपारणा f. (-णा) Conclusion of a fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतभङ्ग|व्रतभंग|व्रतभङ्गः
व्रतभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Breach of a religious vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतभिक्षा
व्रतभिक्षा f. (-क्षा) Solicting alms, as one of the ceremonies accom-<BR>panying investiture with the sacred thread.<BR> E. व्रत the observance<BR>of investiture, भिक्षा begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतलापन
व्रतलापन n. (-नं) Violating a religious vow or obligation.<BR> E. व्रत and लापन cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतसंग्रह
व्रतसंग्रह m. (-हः) Engaging in any act of devotion, taking on one's self<BR>some voluntary religious obligation.<BR> E. व्रत a vow, सग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतस्वातक
व्रतस्वातक m. (-कः) The Brāhman who has completed his term of<BR>studentship.<BR> E. व्रत and स्वातक a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रताचरण
व्रताचरण n. (-णं) Observing a religious obligation, especially continence,<BR>as the duty of the student.<BR> E. व्रत and आचरण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतादेश|व्रतादेशः
व्रतादेश m. (-शः) Investiture of a youth of either of the first three classes<BR>with the characteristic cord.<BR> E. व्रत observance, आदेश pointing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतिन्
व्रतिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति) Engaged in or observing a religious vow or<BR>obligation.<BR>	 m. (-ती)<BR>	 1. An employer of priests.<BR>	 2. An ascetic, a<BR>devotee, one engaged in the observance of a vow or penance.<BR>	 3.<BR>The religious student.<BR> E. व्रत a vow, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतीपवास
व्रतीपवास m. (-सः) Fasting, a fast, (as a religious penance or obliga-<BR>tion.)<BR> E. व्रत, उपवास fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रध्न
व्रध्न m. (-ध्नः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The root of a tree.<BR>	 3. A day.<BR>	 4. Lead.<BR>	 5.<BR>Arka-plant.<BR>	 6. ŚIVA.<BR>	 7. BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्च्
व्रश्च्(ओ, उ)ओद्रश्चु r. 6th cl. (वृश्चति) To cut, to tear, to wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्चन|व्रश्चनं|व्रश्चनः
व्रश्चन m. (-नः) A small saw or chisel.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Cutting.<BR> E. व्रश्च to cut, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राजि|व्राजिः
व्राजि f. (-जिः) A gale of wind.<BR> E. व्रज् to go, इञ् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात|व्रातः
व्रात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A multitude, an assemblage.<BR>	 2. The descendant of an<BR>outcaste Brāhman, &c.<BR>	 3. The company and attendants at a<BR>marriage feast.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Manual or bodily labour.<BR>	 2. Day-labour,<BR>employment of a precarious kind.<BR>	 3. Casual employment.<BR> E. वृ to<BR>choose, aff. अतच् and the vowel made long; or व्रत a religious<BR>observance, or व्रात्य an outcaste, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातीन|व्रातीनः
व्रातीन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A cooly, a hired porter or labourer.<BR>	 2. One who has<BR>no fixed or stated employment.<BR> E. व्रात bodily labour and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्य|व्रात्यः
व्रात्य m. (-त्यः)<BR>	 1. A Brāhman, or man of the three first classes, in<BR>whose youth the customary observances have been omitted, and<BR>who has not received his investiture with the sacred thread.<BR>	 2. A<BR>low person.<BR>	 f. (-त्या) A female of a fallen Brāhman.<BR> E. व्रात, य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्वता
व्रात्वता f. (-ता) The condition of one who has lost caste by neglect of the<BR>initiatory observances.<BR> E. व्रात्य and तल् aff.; also with त्व, व्रात्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यस्तोम|व्रात्यस्तोमः
व्रात्यस्तोम m. (-मः) A particular sacrifice performed to recover the rights<BR>forfeited by an improper delay of the ceremony of investiture. E.<BR>व्रात्य one not invested, &c., स्तोम a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्री
व्री r. 4th cl. (व्रीयते) To go. r. 9th cl. (व्रिणाति or व्रीणाति) To choose or select.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड्
व्रीड् r. 4th cl. (व्रीड्यते)<BR>	 1. To be modest, to be bashful or ashamed.<BR>2. To throw, to direct or send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड|व्रीडः
व्रीड mf. (-डः-डा) Shame, bashfulness.<BR> E. व्रीड् to be ashamed, aff. अच्; fem. aff. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडन|व्रीडनं
व्रीडन n. (-नं) Bashfulness, modesty.<BR> E. व्रीड् to be ashamed, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडानत
व्रीडानत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ashamed, hanging down the head with shame.<BR>E. व्रीडा, and आनत bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडान्वित
व्रीडान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Modest.<BR> E. व्रीडा, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडित
व्रीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ashamed, modest.<BR> E. व्रीड्, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीस्
व्रीस् r. 1st and 10th cls. (व्रीसति व्रासयति-ते) To hurt or injure, to kill or wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहि|व्रीहिः
व्रीहि m. (-हिः)<BR>	 1. Rice of various kinds: eight principal sorts are enu-<BR>merated by native authorities, but the varieties are more numer-<BR>ous.<BR>	 2. Rice ripening in the rainy season.<BR> E. व्री to choose, हि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिक|व्रीहिकः
व्रीहिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having or bearing rice.<BR> E. व्रीहि rice, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिकाञ्चन|व्रीहिकाञ्चनः
व्रीहिकाञ्चन m. (-नः) A sort of pulse, (Ervum lens or hirsutum, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिन्
व्रीहिन् mfn. (-हि-हिणी-हि) Having rice, (a field, &c.)<BR> E. व्रीहि rice, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिभेद|व्रीहिभेदः
व्रीहिभेद m. (-दः) A sort of grain, (Panicum miliaceum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिमय|व्रीहिमयः
व्रीहिमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made or consisting of rice.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A rice-cake<BR>offered with ghee as an oblation.<BR> E. व्रीहि rice, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिराजिक
व्रीहिराजिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Panic-seed, (Panicum italicum.)<BR>	 2. Another<BR>species, (Panicum miliaceum.)<BR> E. व्रीहि rice, राजिक shining,<BR>excelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीह्यगार|व्रीह्यगारं
व्रीह्यगार n. (-रं) A granary, a shed where rice or other grain is stored.<BR> E. व्रीहि, अगार a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रुड्
व्रुड् r. 6th cl. (व्रुडति)<BR>	 1. To cover.<BR>	 2. To heap.<BR>	 3. To sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रूस्
व्रूस् r. 1st and 10th cls. (व्रूसति व्रूसयति-ते) To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैह|व्रैहः
व्रैह mfn. (-हः-ही-हं) Made of or with rice.<BR> E. व्रीहि rice, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैहेय|व्रैहेयः
व्रैहेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Fit for or sown with rice, (a field, &c.)<BR> E. व्रीहि<BR>rice, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ली
व्ली r. 9th cl. (व्लिनाति or व्लीनाति)<BR>	 1. To choose or select.<BR>	 2. To hold, to maintain.<BR>	 3. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्लेक्ष्
व्लेक्ष् r. 10th cl. (व्लेक्षयति-ते) To see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श|शं|शः
श The thirtieth consonant of the Nāgarī alphabet and first of the<BR>three sibilants; it is termed the palatal sibilant, and corresponds<BR>to “Sh” pronounced softly, as in Shun; in the Roman character<BR>it is distinguished by an accent, as Ś.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=701-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श|शं|शः
श m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A weapon.<BR>	 3. A cutter, a destroyer.<BR>n. Adv. (-शं) or Ind. (शं or शम्) Happy, happily, auspiciously.<BR>E. शी to sleep or शी to pare, &c., aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंयु|शंयुः
शंयु mfn. (-युः-युः-युं) Happy, prosperous, fortunate.<BR>	 m. (-युः) A sort of<BR>snake.<BR> E. शम् happily, and युस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंय्य
शंय्य mfn. (-य्यः-य्या-य्यं) Happy, fortunate.<BR>	 f. (-य्या) Knowledge, under-<BR>standing.<BR> E. शम् happily, and यस् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंव|शंवः
शंव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Fortunate, prosperous.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The thunder-<BR>bolt of INDRA.<BR>	 2. The iron head of a pestle.<BR> E. श good fortune,<BR>and व poss. aff.; also as differently derived, read शम्ब and सम्ब &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंवर|शंवरं
शंवर n. (-रं) Water.<BR> E. शं happily, वृ to choose or cover, aff. अच् or अरप्;<BR>more usually read शम्बर. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्
शंस्(उ)शंसु r. 1st cl. (शसति)<BR>	 1. To praise.<BR>	 2. To hurt.<BR>	 3. To wish.<BR>	 4.<BR>To calumniate.<BR>	 5. To suggest.<BR>	 6. To report, to relate, (with a dat.<BR>or gen. of the person communicated to.) With अभि prefixed, To<BR>accuse wrongfully. With आङ्, 1. To hope.<BR>	 2. To speak.<BR>	 3. To<BR>wish. With प्र, To praise, to flatter; this root and its derivatives<BR>are sometimes read with the palatal sibilant final or शंश, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसन|शंसनं
शंसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The act of reciting.<BR>	 2. Praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसा
शंसा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. Narrating.<BR>	 2. Wish, desire.<BR>	 3. Praise, flattery, eulo-<BR>gium.<BR> E. शंस् to praise, &c., affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसित|शंसितः
शंसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Established, ascertained.<BR>	 2. Calumniated,<BR>falsely accused.<BR>	 3. Said, declared.<BR>	 4. Praised, celebrated.<BR>	 5.<BR>Wished, desired.<BR> E. शंस् to wish, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसिन्
शंसिन् f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Saying, indicating.<BR>	 2. Praising, (used at the end of a compound.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्तृ
शंस्तृ m. (-स्ता) An encomiast, a panegyrist, a flatterer.<BR> E. शंस् to praise,<BR>तृन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्थ|शंस्थः
शंस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Happy, prosperous, well-faring.<BR> E. शं happily,<BR>स्था to stay or be, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्य|शंस्यः
शंस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Desirable, to be wished.<BR>	 2. Meritorious, to<BR>be praised.<BR> E. शस् to praise, &c., aff. ण्यत् or क्यप्; also शस्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्
शक् r. 4th cl. (शक्यति-ते) (इर ऌ) इरशकॢ r. 5th cl. (शक्नोति)<BR>	 1. To bear<BR>patiently, to endure, to be patient.<BR>	 2. To be able to effect, to be<BR>competent.<BR>	 3. To be powerful, (generally with an inf.) (इ) शकि r.<BR>1st cl. (शङ्कते)<BR>	 1. To think probable, to suspect.<BR>	 2. To fear, to<BR>apprehend. With आङ्, To dread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक|शकः
शक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sovereign, and prince who gives his name to an era,<BR>especially applied to SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>	 2. A particular caste, the<BR>followers or descendants of ŚAKA or SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>	 3. A country.<BR>m. plu. (-काः)<BR>	 1. The inhabitants, the Sacæ, the Scythians.<BR>	 2. An<BR>era: see शाक.<BR> E. शक् to be able, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकट|शकटं|शकटः
शकट mfn. Subst. (-टः-टी-टं) A cart.<BR>	 m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A Daitya slain by<BR>KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. A cart-load.<BR>	 3. A form of military array resembling<BR>a wedge.<BR>	 4. A measure of capacity equal to two thousand Paṇas.<BR>E. शक् to be able, अटन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटविल|शकटविलः
शकटविल m. (-लः) A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटहन्
शकटहन् m. (-हा) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. शकट the demon so named, and हन् des-<BR>troyer; also similar compounds, as शकटारि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटाल
शकटाल m. (-लः) The minister of NANDA: also read SAKATĀRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटाह्वा
शकटाह्वा f. (-ह्वा) The fourth lunar asterism, called Rohinī, the stars of<BR>which are represented as a cart.<BR> E. शकट a cart, आह्व appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटिका
शकटिका f. (-का) A small cart, a toy-cart.<BR> E. कन् added to शकटी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकन्
शकन् n. (-का) Animal-dung; this word has no forms for the first five<BR>cases; according to some this is not a separate word but a substi-<BR>tute for शकृत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकल|शकलं|शकलः
शकल mn. (-लः-लं) A part, a portion, a piece.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Skin.<BR>	 2. Bark.<BR>3. A kind of (black) pigment or die.<BR>	 4. The scales of a fish.<BR> E. शक्<BR>to be able, कलच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलित
शकलित f. (-ता) Reduced to fragments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलिन्
शकलिन् m. (-ली) A fish.<BR> E. शकल skin or scales, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलीकरण
शकलीकरण n. (-णं) Parting, dividing, cutting or breaking in pieces. E.<BR>शकल, करण making, with च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलीकृत
शकलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Parted, cut in pieces, wounded,<BR> E. शकल, कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकव
शकव m. (-वः) A goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकशकायत्
शकशकायत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Rustling, making a noise, (as the leaves<BR>of a tree in the wind.)<BR> E. शकत् imitative sound, nominal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकान्तक|शकांतक|शकान्तकः
शकान्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The prince VIKPAMĀDITYA.<BR>	 2. The name of SĀLI-<BR>VĀHANA.<BR> E. शक an era or a Scythian, अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकाब्द|शकाब्दः
शकाब्द n. (-ब्दं)<BR>	 1. A year of the Saka era, or era of SĀLIVĀHANA. E.<BR>शक, अब्द a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकार|शकारः
शकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A silly brother-in-law of a Rājā.<BR>	 2. The brother of a king's concubine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकरि
शकरि m. (-रिः) VIKRAMĀDITYA, the celebrated sovereign of Oujein. E.<BR>शक a Saca or Scythian, अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन|शकुनं|शकुनः
शकुन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A bird in general.<BR>	 2. A kind of bird, either the<BR>Indian vulture or the common kite, (Falco cheela;) it is also<BR>applied to the pondicherry eagle, (Falco ponticeriana.)<BR>	 3. A sort<BR>of hymn or song, sung at festivals to solicit or secure lucky<BR>events.<BR>	 n. (-न) Any lucky or inauspicious object or omen.<BR> E. शक्<BR>to be able, उनन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनज्ञा
शकुनज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) A small house-lizard.<BR> E. शकुन a bird, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनज्ञान
शकुनज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge of omens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनि|शकुनिः
शकुनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. The maternal uncle of the Kaurava<BR>princes, and counsellor or DURYODHANA.<BR>	 3. One of the astrono-<BR>mical periods called Karaṇas.<BR>	 4. The Indian kite or eagle, (Falco<BR>cheela.)<BR>	 f. (-नी) A hen-sparrow.<BR> E. शक् to be able, उनि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनिप्रपा
शकुनिप्रपा f. (-पा) A trough or little well for watering birds.<BR> E. शकुनि a<BR>bird, प्र before पा to drink, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनिवाद|शकुनिवादः
शकुनिवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The sound of a bird.<BR>	 2. The crowing of a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनीश्वर|शकुनीश्वरः
शकुनीश्वर m. (-रः) A name of GARUḌA.<BR> E. शकुनि a bird, and ईश्वर chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्त|शकुंत|शकुंतः|शकुन्तः
शकुन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. A kind of bird, the Indian vulture.<BR>	 3.<BR>Another sort of bird, described as of aquatic habits, perhaps a kind<BR>of maritime or fishing-falcon.<BR>	 4. A sort of insect.<BR>	 5. The blue-jay.<BR>E. शक् to be able, उन्त Unādi aff.; also शकुन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तक|शकुंतक|शकुंतकः|शकुन्तकः
शकुन्तक m. (-कः) A bird.<BR>	 f. (-न्तिका)<BR>	 1. A kind of bird.<BR>	 2. A locust. E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तला|शकुंतला
शकुन्तला f. (-ला) The daughter of MENAKĀ, the courtezan of Svarga, by<BR>the sage VISHWĀMITRA, brought up by KANWA the hermit, and<BR>afterwards married to DUSHYANTA, by whom she became the mother<BR>of BHARATA, the sovereign of all India.<BR> E. शकुन्त a bird, ला to get,<BR>affs. क and टाप्, being born in a solitary forest, and protected by<BR>the birds till found by KANWA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तलात्मज|शकुन्तलात्मजः
शकुन्तलात्मज m. (-जः) BHARATA, the sovereign of India.<BR> E. शकुन्तला as above, आत्मज the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्ति|शकुंति|शकुंतिः|शकुन्तिः
शकुन्ति m. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. A bird in general.<BR>	 2. A kind of bird: see शकुन्त, &c.<BR>E. शक् to be able, Unādi aff. उन्ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तिका|शकुंतिका
शकुन्तिका f. (-का) A locust, a cricket.<BR> E. शकुन्त a bird, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुल|शकुलः
शकुल mf. (-लः-ली) A kind of fish. “शील”.<BR> E. शक् to be able, aff. उलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुलगण्ड|शकुलगण्डः
शकुलगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A kind of fish. “शालमाछ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुलाक्षक|शकुलाक्षकः
शकुलाक्षक m. (-कः) Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon,) with white bloss-<BR>oms.<BR> E. शकुल a kind of fish, अक्षि the eye, अच् substituted for the<BR>final vowel; the blossoms being compared to the eye of a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुलादनी
शकुलादनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A medicinal plant, commonly Kaṭuki, (Wrightea<BR>antidysenterica.)<BR>	 2. A creeping plant, (Jussieua repens.)<BR>	 3. A<BR>drug, commonly Kāyaphal.<BR>	 4. An earth-worm.<BR> E. शकुल a fish, अद्<BR>to eat, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुलार्भक|शकुलार्भकः
शकुलार्भक m. (-कः) A sort of fish. “गडुइ माछ ।”<BR> E. शकुल a fish, अर्भक a<BR>young one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृत्
शकृत् n. (-कृत्) Fæces, excrement.<BR> E. शक् to be able, (to expel,) Unādi aff. ऋतन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृत्करि|शकृत्करिः
शकृत्करि mf. (-रिः-री) A calf.<BR> E. शकृत् ordure. कृ to make, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृत्कार|शकृत्कारः
शकृत्कार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Making ordure or fæces.<BR> E. शकृत् ordure, and<BR>कार who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=702-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृद्द्वार|शकृद्द्वारं
शकृद्द्वार n. (-रं) The anus.<BR> E. शकृत् fæces, and द्वार passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्कर|शक्करः
शक्कर m. (-रः) A bull.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A river.<BR>	 2. A zone, a girdle.<BR>	 3. A form<BR>of metre, a stanza of four lines of fourteen syllables each.<BR>	 4. A<BR>woman of an impure caste; it is also read शक्वर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्करि|शक्करिः
शक्करि m. (-रिः) A bull: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्त|शक्तः
शक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Able, capable, strong, powerful.<BR>	 2. Speaking<BR>civilly, able to please by the manner of speaking.<BR>	 3. Diligent,<BR>attentive, intent.<BR>	 4. Opulent, rich.<BR>	 5. Significant, expressive, (as<BR>a word.)<BR> E. शक् to be able, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तता
शक्तता f. (-ता) Ability, power.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व शक्तत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ति|शक्तिः
शक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Power, regal power as resulting from “प्रभुशक्ति” or “प्रभाव-<BR>शक्ति” majesty, “उत्साहशक्ति” energy, perseverance, “मन्त्रशक्ति” the power<BR>of god counsel: see शक्तित्रय.<BR>	 2. Power, strength, prowess.<BR>	 3. An iron<BR>spear or dart.<BR>	 4. The energy or active power of a deity, per-<BR>sonified as his wife, as GAURĪ of ŚIVA, LAKṢMĪ of VIṢṆU, &c.<BR>5. The female organ as the counterpart of the phallic personifica-<BR>tion of ŚIVA, and worshipped either literally or figuratively by a<BR>sect of Hindus, thence termed ŚĀKTAS.<BR>	 6. Allaying or appeasing<BR>opposition.<BR>	 7. Force or signification of words, (op. to लक्षणा and<BR>व्यञ्जना.)<BR>	 8. The relation of a word to the thing designated by it,<BR>(in Nyāya Phil.)<BR>	 9. Poetic genius.<BR>	 10. The inherent power of a<BR>cause to produce its effects, (in Nyāya Phil.)<BR> E. शक् to be able,<BR>aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिग्रह|शक्तिग्रहः
शक्तिग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 3. A spearman,<BR>a lancer.<BR>	 4. Apprehending the meaning or acceptation of a word.<BR>E. शक्ति a spear, and ग्रह who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तितस्
शक्तितस् Ind. According to power or ability.<BR> E. शक्ति and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तित्रय
शक्तित्रय n. (-यं) The three ingredients of regal power; or king, minister,<BR>and vigour.<BR> E. शक्ति, and त्रय triad: see शक्ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिधर|शक्तिधरः
शक्तिधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A name of KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. A spearman, a lancer.<BR>Adj. Developed, powerful<BR> E. शक्ति a spear, धर the holder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिपर्ण|शक्तिपर्णः
शक्तिपर्ण m. (-र्णः) A tree, (Echites scholaris)<BR> E. शक्ति strength, (giving<BR>it,) पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिपाणि|शक्तिपाणिः
शक्तिपाणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. A spearman.<BR> E. शक्ति a spear, पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिभृत्
शक्तिभृत् m. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. KĀRTIKEYA: see the last.<BR>	 2. A soldier armed with<BR>a spear.<BR> E. शक्ति a spear, and भृत् who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिमत्|शक्तिमन्त्
शक्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Powerful, mighty.<BR> E. शक्ति, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिवैकल्य
शक्तिवैकल्य n. (-ल्यं) Inability, deficiency of power or strength.<BR> E. शक्ति,<BR>वैकल्य imperfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिहीन
शक्तिहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Powerless, impotent.<BR> E. शक्ति, हीन abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिहेतिक|शक्तिहेतिकः
शक्तिहेतिक m. (-कः) A spearman, a lancer, a soldier armed with an iron<BR>lance.<BR> E. शक्ति a spear, हेति a weapon, and कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तु|शक्तुः
शक्तु mn. (-क्तुः-क्तु) According to some authorities only.<BR>	 m. plu. (शक्तवः) The<BR>powder or flour of barley and other grain, first fried and then<BR>ground.<BR> E. शच् to go, &c., तुन् aff.; also read सक्तु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तुफला
शक्तुफला f. (-ला) The Śami tree, (Mimosa suma, Rox.)<BR> E. शक्त farina,<BR>and फल fruit; also शक्तुफली, and सक्तुफला ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्त्यपेक्ष
शक्त्यपेक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Being according to, or having reference to,<BR>ability, power, &c.<BR> E. शक्ति and अपेक्षा regard to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्न|शक्नः
शक्न mfn. (-क्नः-क्ना-क्नं) Speaking civilly or pleasingly: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्नु|शक्नुः
शक्नु mfn. (-क्नुः-क्नुः-क्नु) Speaking civilly or kindly.<BR> E. शक् to be able, (to<BR>please by speaking,) aff. नु; also with क्ल aff. शक्ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्मन्
शक्मन् m. (-क्मा) Power, strength.<BR> E. शक् to be able, मनिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्य|शक्यः
शक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं)<BR>	 1. Possible, practicable to be effected or done,<BR>(generally with an inf.)<BR>	 2. Fit to be effected or accomplished.<BR>	 3.<BR>Directly expressed, (as the meaning of a word.)<BR> E. शक् to be<BR>able, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्यता
शक्यता f. (-ता) Possibility.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, शक्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्यप्रतीकार
शक्यप्रतीकार m. (-रः) A possible remedy or counteragent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्र|शक्रः
शक्र m. (-क्रः)<BR>	 1. INDRA, the chief of the inferior gods, and ruler of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">Page703-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Svarga or paradise.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR>	 3. A<BR>tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>	 4. An owl.<BR>	 5. The number “fourteen”<BR>E. शक् to possess power, Unādi aff. रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रक्रीडाचल|शक्रक्रीडाचलः
शक्रक्रीडाचल m. (-लः) Mount Meru.<BR> E. शक INDRA, क्रीडा sport, pleasure, अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रगोप|शक्रगोपः
शक्रगोप m. (-पः) An insect of a red colour, “इन्द्रगोप”, (Coccinella or<BR>ladybird of various species.)<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, गो light, &c., पा to<BR>preserve, aff. क; or शक्रं शक्रधनुर्गापायति समवर्णत्वात् गुप-अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रज|शक्रजः
शक्रज m. (-जः) A crow<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रजात|शक्रजातः
शक्रजात m. (-तः) A crow.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रजित्
शक्रजित् m. (-जित्) MEGHANĀDA, the son of RĀVAṆA.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, जित् victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रधनुस्
शक्रधनुस् n. (-नुः) The bow of INDRA, the rain bow.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, and<BR>धनुस् the bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रध्वज|शक्रध्वजः
शक्रध्वज n. (-जं) A pole or flag set up in honour of INDRA.<BR> E. शक्र and ध्वज a flag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रनन्दन|शक्रनंदन|शक्रनन्दनः
शक्रनन्दन m. (-नः) ARJUNA.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, नन्दन a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रपादप|शक्रपादपः
शक्रपादप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A sort of pine, (P. devadaru, Rox.)<BR>	 2. The Kutaja-<BR>tree.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, पादप a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रपुष्पी
शक्रपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A sort of potherb; also Viśalyā.<BR> E. शक्र the pentaptera<BR>arjuna, and पुष्प a flower; having similar flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रभवन|शक्रभवनं
शक्रभवन n. (-नं) Sky, heaven.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, भवन abode; being the god<BR>of the firmament: it also occurs शक्रभुवन, from भुवन a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रभिद्
शक्रभिद् m. (-भिद्) The son of RĀVAṆA.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, भिद् defeater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रभूभवा
शक्रभूभवा f. (-वा) Colocynth, (Cucumis coloquintida.) “इन्द्रवारुण्याम् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रमूर्द्धन्
शक्रमूर्द्धन् m. (-र्द्धा) An ant-hill, a hillock.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, मूर्द्धन् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रवाहन|शक्रवाहनः
शक्रवाहन m. (-नः) A cloud.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रशरासन|शक्रशरासनं
शक्रशरासन n. (-नं) The rain-bow.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, शरासन a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रशाला
शक्रशाला f. (-ला) A place prepared for sacrifices to be offered in.<BR> E. शक्र<BR>INDRA, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रशिरस्
शक्रशिरस् n. (-रः) An ant-hill.<BR> E. शक्र, शिरस the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रसारथि|शक्रसारथिः
शक्रसारथि m. (-थिः) MĀTULI, the charioteer of INDRA.<BR> E. शक्र, सारथि a coachman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रसुत|शक्रसुतः
शक्रसुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The monkey king BĀLĪ.<BR>	 2. ARJUNA.<BR>	 3. JAYANTA.<BR>E. शक्र INDRA, सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रसुधा
शक्रसुधा f. (-धा) The resin of the Boswellia thurifera, or gum olibanum.<BR> E. शक्र, सुधा ambrosia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रसृष्टा
शक्रसृष्टा f. (-ष्टा) Yellow myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR> E. शक्र INDRA,<BR>सृष्ट created; springing originally, it is said, from the ground on<BR>which INDRA spilt a drop of nectar as he was drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्राख्य|शक्राख्यः
शक्राख्य m. (-ख्यः) An owl.<BR> E. “शक्रस्येवाख्या यस्य ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्राणी
शक्राणी f. (-णी) ŚACHĪ, the wife of INDRA.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA, ङीष् aff. आनुक् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्राशन|शक्राशनं|शक्राशनः
शक्राशन m. (-नः) A medicinal plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR> E. शक्र<BR>INDRA, अशन food: created by him; springing from the drops of<BR>Amrita which fell on the ground from the bodies of the monkies<BR>slain in the war with RĀVAṆA, and who were restored to life by<BR>INDRA by a shower of Amrita, or the liquor of immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रि|शक्रिः
शक्रि m. (-क्रिः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. Thunderbolt.<BR>	 3. An elephant.<BR> E. शक्-क्रिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रोत्सव|शक्रोत्सवः
शक्रोत्सव m. (-वः) A festival held in honour of INDRA on the twelfth<BR>day of the bright-half of the month Bhādrapada.<BR> E. शक्र INDRA,<BR>and उत्सव a festival; also शक्रोत्थान ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्ल|शक्लः
शक्ल mfn. (-क्लः-क्ला-क्लं) Speaking civilly or kindly.<BR> E. शक् to be able, (to<BR>delight simply by speaking,) क्ल Unādi affix; also शक्र and शक्रु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वन्
शक्वन् m. (-क्वा) An elephant.<BR> E. शक् to be powerful, and वनिप् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वर|शक्वरः
शक्वर m. (-रः) A bull, an ox.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A finger.<BR>	 2. A river.<BR>	 3. A zone,<BR>a girdle.<BR>	 4. A form of metre, a stanza of four lines of fourteen<BR>syllables each, and comprising many varieties according to the<BR>different Pādas of which the lines are composed.<BR> E. शक् to be able<BR>or strong, क्वरप् aff., or वनिप् aff. with र augment, and the final<BR>rejected: the feminine form is also derived from शक्वन् with ङीप्<BR>affix, and र augment, and the word is also read शक्कर and शक्करी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्क|शंक|शंकः|शङ्कः
शङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A draft-ox.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्का)<BR>	 1. Fear, terror, apprehension.<BR>	 2.<BR>Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>	 3. An objection started in disputation.<BR>	 4.<BR>Suspicion, expectation.<BR>	 5. Belief, understanding, impression.<BR>	 6. A<BR>species of the Dandaka metre.<BR> E. शकि to fear, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=703-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कनीय|शंकनीय
शङ्कनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Doubtful, questionable, to be doubted or<BR>apprehended.<BR> E. शकि to fear or doubt, अनीयर् aff.; also शङ्कितव्य,<BR>and शङ्क्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कर|शंकर|शंकरः|शङ्करः
शङ्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Auspicious, propitious, conferring happiness or<BR>good fortune.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The name of a celebrated<BR>teacher of the Vedānta philosophy.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. PĀRVATĪ, the<BR>wife of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The Śamī-tree.<BR>	 3. Bengal madder.<BR> E. शं good<BR>fortune, कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्करप्रिय|शंकरप्रिय|शंकरप्रियः|शङ्करप्रियः
शङ्करप्रिय m. (-यः) The francoline partridge.<BR> E. शङ्कर ŚIVA, प्रिय dear, beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्करावास|शंकरावासः|शङ्करावासः
शङ्करावास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. KAILĀSA, the abode of ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A kind of cam-<BR>phor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कान्वित
शङ्कान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Apprehensive, doubtful, afraid.<BR> E. शङ्का, अन्वित<BR>possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कामियोग
शङ्कामियोग m. (-गः) Accusation or charge on suspicion.<BR> E. शङ्का, अभियोग charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कामय
शङ्कामय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Fearful, afraid.<BR> E. शङ्का and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कास्पद
शङ्कास्पद n. (-दं) Cause or matter of doubt or apprehension.<BR> E. शङ्का and<BR>आस्पद site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्काहीन
शङ्काहीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Free from doubt or apprehension.<BR> E. शङ्का, and हीन free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कित|शंकित|शङ्कितः
शङ्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Alarmed, frightened.<BR>	 2. Weak, unsteady.<BR>	 3.<BR>Doubtful, uncertain.<BR> E. शङ्का fear, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कितवणक
शङ्कितवणक m. (-कः) A thief.<BR> E. शङ्कित frightened, वर्ण a caste, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कु|शंकु|शंकुः|शङ्कुः
शङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः)<BR>	 1. The trunk of a lopped tree.<BR>	 2. A javelin, a spear.<BR>	 3. A<BR>pin, a stake, a pale.<BR>	 4. The gnomon of a dial, usually twelve fingers<BR>long.<BR>	 5. A long thin column in front of a pagoda.<BR>	 6. The penis.<BR>7. A number.<BR>	 8. The small fibres of a leaf.<BR>	 9. The scate fish, (Raia<BR>Sankur, HAM.)<BR>	 10. A sort of perfume, commonly Nakhi.<BR>	 11. A<BR>goose.<BR>	 12. An ant-hill.<BR>	 13. A goblin, a demon.<BR>	 14. A Gandharba<BR>attached to ŚIVA.<BR>	 15. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 16. KĀMA.<BR>	 17. Sin.<BR>	 18.<BR>Fear, terror.<BR>	 19. The pointed head of an arrow, a shaft.<BR>	 20. A<BR>measuring rod.<BR>	 21. A large number “ten billions.” 22. Poison.<BR>	 23.<BR>Sine of altitude, (in astro.)<BR> E. शकि to doubt or apprehend, aff. उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुकर्ण|शंकुकर्ण|शङ्कुकर्णः
शङ्कुकर्ण m. (-र्णः) An ass.<BR> E. शङ्कु a javelin, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुचि|शंकुचिः|शङ्कुचिः
शङ्कुचि m. (-चिः) A scate-fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुतरु|शंकुतरु|शङ्कुतरुः
शङ्कुतरु m. (-रुः) The Śal tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR> E. शङ्कु a stake, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कर|शंकर|शंकरः|शङ्करः
शङ्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Formidable, fearful, frightful.<BR> E. शङ्कु fear, रा to<BR>give or cause, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुला|शंकुला
शङ्कुला f. (-ला) A pair of nippers, used to cut the betel-nut into small pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कुवृक्ष|शंकुवृक्ष|शङ्कुवृक्षः
शङ्कुवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The Śal tree.<BR> E. शङ्कु a pin or stake, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कोच|शंकोचः|शङ्कोचः
शङ्कोच m. (-चः) A scate-fish.<BR> E. शकि-उच्; also शङ्कु, शङ्कुचि and शङ्कीचि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्क्य
शङ्क्य mfn. (-ङ्क्यः-ङ्क्या-ङ्क्यं) To be feared or doubted.<BR> E. शकि to fear, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्ख|शंख|शंखं|शंखः|शङ्खः
शङ्ख mn. (-ङ्खः-ङ्खं) The conch-shell used by the Hindus, in two ways<BR>especially; offering libations with it, or when perforated at one<BR>end blowing it as a horn at sacrifices: frequent mention of it<BR>occurs in the battle pieces of the poets, each hero being provided<BR>with a conch as his horn.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्खः)<BR>	 1. One of KUVERA'S trea-<BR>sures.<BR>	 2. The temple or temporal bone, sometimes comprising<BR>the frontal bone also.<BR>	 3. A perfume, commonly Nakhi, appa-<BR>rently a dried shell-fish.<BR>	 4. A military drum.<BR>	 5. One of the<BR>eight chiefs of the Nāgas or serpents of Pātāla described as of<BR>a yellow colour.<BR>	 6. An elephant's cheek.<BR>	 7. A large number, “a<BR>hundred billions.” 8. The name of a saint and legislator.<BR>	 9. A<BR>poet, one of the nine gems, &c.<BR> E. शम् to pacify, &c., Unādi aff. ख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खक|शंखक|शंखकं|शङ्खकं|शंखकः|शङ्खकः
शङ्खक n. (-कं) A bracelet, (often made of the conch-shell.)<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>1. The conch-shell.<BR>	 2. Pain and heat with a puffiness in the tem-<BR>ples and forehead.<BR>	 3. The temples.<BR> E. कन् or वुन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खकार|शंखकार|शङ्खकारः
शङ्खकार m. (-रः) A worker in shells.<BR> E. शङ्ख a coach, and कार maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खचरी|शंखचरी
शङ्खचरी f. (-री) Sandal marks on the forehead.<BR> E. शङ्ख the forehead, and<BR>चर् to go, affs. टच् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खचर्च्ची|शङ्खचर्ची
शङ्खचर्च्ची f. (-र्च्ची) Sandal marks made across the forehead.<BR> E. शङ्ख the<BR>forehead, चर्च् to anoint, affs. अच् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खज|शङ्खजः
शङ्खज m. (-जः) A large pearl, of the shape of a pigeon's egg.<BR> E. शङ्ख a<BR>shell, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खध्म|शंखध्म|शङ्खध्मः
शङ्खध्म m. (-ध्मः) A shell-blower.<BR> E. शङ्ख a conch, and ध्म who blows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खनख|शंखनख|शंखनखः|शङ्खनखः
शङ्खनख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A small shell.<BR>	 2. A perfume, commonly नखी.<BR> E. शङ्ख<BR>a conch, नख the nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खपाल|शंखपाल|शङ्खपालः
शङ्खपाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A Nāga or serpent of Pātāla.<BR> E. शङ्ख a conch, &c., पाल who nourishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खपुष्पी
शङ्खपुष्पी f. (-ष्पी) A sort of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR> E. शङ्ख conch,<BR>पुष्प a flower, ङीप् aff., implying resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खप्रस्थ|शङ्खप्रस्थः
शङ्खप्रस्थ m. (-स्थः) Spots in the moon.<BR> E. शङ्ख a shell, and प्रस्थ pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खभृत्|शंखभृत्
शङ्खभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Having a conch or shell.<BR>	 m. (-भृत्) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. शङ्ख<BR>a conch, and भृत् who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खमुख|शंखमुख|शङ्खमुखः
शङ्खमुख m. (-खः) An alligator.<BR> E. शङ्ख a conch, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खिका
शङ्खिका f. (-का) A kind of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR> E. शङ्ख a<BR>shell, कन् or ठन् implying resemblance, fem. form. “चोरकाचका ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खिन्|शंखिन्
शङ्खिन् mfn. (-ङ्खी-ङ्खिनी-ङ्खि) Possessing or having a conch or shell, &c.<BR>m. (-ङ्खी)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. The ocean.<BR>	 3. A shell-blower.<BR>	 4. A worker<BR>in shells.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A sort of grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>	 3. A description of woman,<BR>one of the four classes into which females are divided in erotic<BR>writings; the Śankhinī is described as tall, with long hair,<BR>neither stout nor thin, of irascible disposition and strong<BR>passions.<BR>	 4. A goddess or Śaktī worshipped by the Bauddhas.<BR>	 5.<BR>A female spirit or goblin.<BR> E. शङ्ख a shell, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्खिनीवास|शङ्खिनीवासः
शङ्खिनीवास m. (-सः) A small tree, (Trophis aspera.) “श्याओडागाछ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शच्
शच् r. 1st cl. (शचते) To speak articulately, to say or tell. (इ) शचि r.<BR>1st cl. (शञ्चते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शचि|शचिः
शचि f. (-चिः or -ची)<BR>	 1. The wife of INDRA.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Asparagus race-<BR>mosus.)<BR>	 3. The astronomical Karaṇa or period or Viṣṭi.<BR> E. शच्<BR>to speak articulately, aff. इन्, ङीष् optionally added; also सचि,<BR>and सची ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शचीपति|शचीपतिः
शचीपति m. (-तिः) INDRA.<BR> E. शची the wife of the deity, पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट्
शट् r. 1st cl. (शटति)<BR>	 1. To be diseased or sick.<BR>	 2. To divide, to pierce<BR>or separate.<BR>	 3. To go.<BR>	 4. To be low-spirited, to be weary or<BR>dejected. r. 10th cl. (शाटयते) To flatter, to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट|शटः
शट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Sour, astringent, acid.<BR> E. शट् to pain, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शटा
शटा f. (-टा) An ascetic's clotted hair.<BR>	 2. A mane: see सटा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शटी
शटी f. (-टिः or टी) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumoot,) otherwise considered<BR>as a synonym of the Ambahaldi, or Carcumt Āmhaldī, the mango-<BR>smelling ginger, so termed because the fresh root possesses the<BR>smell of a green mango.<BR> E. शट् to divide, (remove disease,) aff. इन्<BR>and ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
शठ् r. 1st cl. (शठति)<BR>	 1. To cheat, to defraud or deceive.<BR>	 2. To kill or<BR>hurt.<BR>	 3. To suffer pain. r. 10th cl. (शाठयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To finish.<BR>	 2. To<BR>leave unfinished.<BR>	 3. To go or move. (शठयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak ill.<BR>	 2. To<BR>speak well.<BR>	 3. To abstain from speaking.<BR>	 4. To deceive. (शाठयते)<BR>To flatter, to coax, to praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ|शठं|शठः
शठ mfn. (-ठः-ठा-ठं) Wicked, depraved, perverse, dishonest.<BR>	 m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1.<BR>An umpire, a mediator, an arbitrator.<BR>	 2. A rogue, a knave.<BR>	 3. A<BR>blockhead, a fool.<BR>	 4. An idler.<BR>	 5. A false husband or lover, one<BR>who pretends affection to one female whilst his heart is fixed on<BR>another.<BR>	 6. Thorn apple, (Dhatura metel.)<BR>	 n. (-ठं)<BR>	 1. A sort of root,<BR>commonly Tagara.<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR>	 3. Iron.<BR> E. शठ् to be wicked, aff.<BR>अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठता
शठता f. (-ता) Wickedness, depravity.<BR> E. शठ wicked, तल् aff.; also शठत्व n. (-त्वं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शड्
शड्(इ)शडि r. 1st cl. (शण्डति)<BR>	 1. To disease or disorder.<BR>	 2. To hurt or<BR>wound.<BR>	 3. To collect, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्
शण् r. 1st cl. (शणति)<BR>	 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण|शणं|शणः
शण n. (-ण)<BR>	 1. Hemp, (Cannabis sativa)<BR>	 2. Bengal Saṇ, a plant from<BR>which a kind of hemp is prepared, (Crotolaria juncea and other<BR>kinds.)<BR>	 3. An arrow.<BR> E. शण् to give, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=704-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणतन्तु
शणतन्तु f. (-न्तुः) The thread or string made of the flax of the Crotolaria<BR>juncea.<BR> E. शण and तन्तु string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणतान्तव
शणतान्तव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Made of Saṇ string.<BR> E. शणतन्तु and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणपर्णी
शणपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR> E. शण Saṇ, and पर्ण a<BR>leaf; having similar leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणपुष्पिका
शणपुष्पिका f. (-का) Crotolaria of several species.<BR> E. शण the Saṇ, पुष्प a<BR>flower, aff. ङीष् and कन् added, fem. form, implying resemblance;<BR>also शणपुष्पी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणसूत्र|शणसूत्रं
शणसूत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The fibre or flax of the Saṇ plant, or string made<BR>from it.<BR>	 2. A net made of hemp or of Saṇ, or the thread of the<BR>Crotolaria juncea.<BR>	 3. Cordage, twine.<BR> E. शण hemp, &c., सूत्र a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणालु
शणालु m. (-लुः) A plant, (Cassia fistula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणीर|शणीरं
शणीर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A rock or small island in the midst of the river SONA.<BR>2. An insular spot inclosed by the branches of the SARAJU, where<BR>it falls into the Ganges above CHUPRĀH, at BHRIGURĀŚHRAMA or<BR>BAGERESSAN; called also, the bank of the DARDARĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ड|शंड|शण्डं|शंडः|शण्डः
शण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A bull set at liberty.<BR>	 2. An eunuch.<BR>	 n. (-ण्डं) A multi-<BR>tude of lotus flowers.<BR> E. शण् or षण् to give, aff. ड, hence also षण्ड,<BR>and differently derived, शण्ठ, षण्ड the more usual form; or शडि-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्डता
शण्डता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The state of a bull let loose or at liberty.<BR>	 2. Emascu-<BR>lation.<BR> E. शण्ड a bull set at liberty, &c. तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्डिल|शण्डिलः
शण्डिल m. (-लः) The name of a Muni, and ancestor of a particular<BR>family of Brāhmans.<BR> E. शण्ड an eunuch, and इलच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्ढ|शंढ|शंढः|शण्ढः
शण्ढ m. (-ण्ढः)<BR>	 1. An eunuch.<BR>	 2. An eunuch or emasculated attendant,<BR>as employed in a Harem or seraglio.<BR>	 3. An impotent man.<BR>	 4. A<BR>bull set at liberty.<BR>	 5. A mad man or a drunken man.<BR> E. शम् to bear<BR>or endure, Unādi aff. ढ; also षण्ढ and शण्ड, &c.; or शण-ढ तस्य नेत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत|शतं
शत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A hundred.<BR>	 2. Any large number.<BR> E. शो-डतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतक|शतकः
शतक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A hundred.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A century, a cento, a<BR>collection of one hundred stanzas, &c.<BR> E. शत a hundred, लन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतकीर्त्ति|शतकीर्ति|शतकीर्त्तिः
शतकीर्त्ति m. (-र्त्तिः) A Jina or Jaina pontiff of the last age.<BR> E. शत a<BR>hundred, and कीर्त्ति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतकुम्भ|शतकुंभ|शतकुम्भः
शतकुम्भ n. (-म्भं) Gold.<BR>	 m. (-म्भः) The name of a mountain.<BR>	 f. (-म्भा) A<BR>plant, (Phyalis flexuosa.)<BR> E. शत a hundred, and कुम्भ a water-jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतकोटि|शतकोटिः
शतकोटि m. (-टिः) INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>	 f. (-टिः) A hundred crores.<BR> E. शत<BR>a hundred, कोटि edge or a crore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतक्रतु|शतक्रतुः
शतक्रतु m. (-तुः) INDRA.<BR> E. शत a hundred, क्रतु sacrifice; a hundred<BR>AŚHWA-MEDHAS or sacrifices of an unbroken horse, elevating the<BR>sacrificer to the place and title of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतखण्ड|शतखंड|शतखण्डं
शतखण्ड n. (-ण्डं) Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतगु
शतगु mfn. (-गुः-गुः-गु) Possessed of a hundred cows, with as many, &c.<BR>E. शत, गु for गो a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतगुण
शतगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) A hundred times, a hundred-fold.<BR> E. शत, गुण a<BR>time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतघ्नी
शतघ्नी f. (-घ्नी)<BR>	 1. A weapon; it is generally supposed to be a sort of<BR>firearms, or the ancient Indian rocket, but it is also described as<BR>a stone set round with iron spikes.<BR>	 2. A female scorpion.<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>(Galedupa arborea.)<BR>	 4. A disease of the throat, apparently enlarge-<BR>ment of the tonsils.<BR> E. शत a hundred, हन् to kill, affs. अण् and<BR>ङीष् and the radical letters changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतच्छद|शतच्छदः
शतच्छद m. (-दः) The woodpecker.<BR> E. शत a hundred, च्छद a feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शततम|शततमः
शततम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Hundredth.<BR> E. शत a hundred, तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शततारा
शततारा f. (-रा) The constellation ŚATABHISHĀ, q. v.<BR> E. शत a hundred or<BR>many, and तारा a star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतद्रु|शतद्रुः
शतद्रु f. (-द्रुः) The river SUTLEJ, which rises in the Himālaya mountains<BR>in the vicinity, it is supposed, of the RĀVAṆA-HRADA, and run-<BR>ning to the S. W. unites in the PUNJĀB with the BEYĀH or<BR>VIPĀŚĀ, when it forms the HYPHASIS of the Greeks, and falls in to<BR>the INDUS below MOOLTĀN.<BR> E. शत a hundred, (fold, or in a hundred<BR>branches,) द्रु to flow, Unādi aff. कु; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतद्वार
शतद्वार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Hundred-gated, having a hundred or a number<BR>of doors or outlets.<BR> E. शत and द्वार a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधा
शतधा f. (-धा) Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon.) Ind.<BR>	 1. In a hundred<BR>ways, a hundred-fold.<BR>	 2. In a hundred parts.<BR> E. शत a hundred,<BR>(blossoms,) धा to have, क and टाप् affs.; or शत the same, धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधामन्
शतधामन् m. (-मा) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. शत्र a hundred, (i. e. many,) धामन् body;<BR>being multiplied in as many shapes as the creation exhibits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधार|शतधारं
शतधार mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Flowing in many streams.<BR>	 2. Having many<BR>edges.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The thunderbolt.<BR> E. शत, धारा an edge, टच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधृति|शतधृतिः
शतधृति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. INDRA.<BR>	 3. Heaven.<BR> E. शत, धृति sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपत्र|शतपत्रं|शतपत्रः
शतपत्र n. (-त्रं) A lotus in general, (Nelumbium speciosum or Nymphæa<BR>nelumbo.)<BR>	 m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2. The Sāras or Indian crane.<BR>	 3.<BR>A woodpecker.<BR>	 4. A parrot, the king-parrot or Loory.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा) A<BR>woman.<BR> E. शत a hundred, पत्र a leaf or feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपत्रक|शतपत्रकः
शतपत्रक m. (-कः) The woodpecker.<BR> E. कन् added to the last, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपथिक|शतपथिकः
शतपथिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Following a variety of paths or doctrines.<BR>E. शत a hundred, पथिन् a road and figurly. a doctrine, aff. षिकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपदी
शतपदी f. (-दी) A centipede, julus.<BR> E. शत a hundred, पद a foot, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपद्म|शतपद्मं
शतपद्म n. (-द्मं) The white lotus.<BR> E. शत hundred, (leaves), and पद्म a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपर्व्वन्|शतपर्वन्
शतपर्व्वन् m. (-र्व्वा) A bamboo.<BR> E. शत a hundred or many, पर्व्वन् a joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपर्व्वा|शतपर्वा
शतपर्व्वा f. (-र्व्वा)<BR>	 1. Bent grass, (Panicum dactylon.)<BR>	 2. Orris root.<BR>	 3.<BR>The wife of ŚUKRA.<BR>	 4. Day of full-moon in the month of Āshwin.<BR>E. शत a hundred, पर्व्वन् a joint or period, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपर्व्विका|शतपर्विका
शतपर्व्विका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Bent grass or Dūrbā.<BR>	 2. Orris root.<BR>	 3. Barley. E.<BR>कन् fem. form, added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपर्व्वेश|शतपर्वेश|शतपर्व्वेशः
शतपर्व्वेश m. (-शः) The planet VENUS or its regent.<BR> E. शतपर्व्वा the wife<BR>of ŚUKRA, ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपाद्
शतपाद् f. (-पाद् or -पात्) A centipede.<BR> E. शत a hundred, पाद् a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपादिका
शतपादिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A medicinal root, commonly Kākoli.<BR>	 2. A cen-<BR>tipede.<BR> E. शत a hundred, पाद a foot or root, कप् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपुष्प|शतपुष्पः
शतपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) The poet BHĀRAVI, the author of the KIRĀTĀRJU-<BR>NIYAM.<BR>	 f. (-ष्पा) A sort of dill or fennel, (Anethum sowa.) “सुलफा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपुष्पिका
शतपुष्पिका f. (-का) Anethum sowa.<BR> E. कन् fem. form, added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोन|शतपोनः
शतपोन m. (-नः) A sieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोनक|शतपोनकः
शतपोनक m. (-कः) Fistula in ano with many external openings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोरक
शतपोरक m. (-कः) A kind of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतप्रास|शतप्रासः
शतप्रास m. (-सः) A flower, (Nerium odorum. )<BR> E. शत a hundred, प्रास a<BR>dart, to which the leaves are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतभिषज्
शतभिषज् f. (-षक्) One of the lunar asterisms: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतभिषा
शतभिषा f. (-षा) The twenty-fifth of the Nakshatras or lunar mansions,<BR>containing 100 stars, one of which is Aquarii.<BR> E. शत a hundred,<BR>भिषज् to cure, aff. ड; requiring many physicians; as the Hindus<BR>say DHANWANTARI himself can not cure any person affected with<BR>disease, whilst the moon is in this asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतभीरु|शतभीरुः
शतभीरु f. (-रुः) Arabian jasmine, (J. zambac. )<BR> E. शत a hundred, (dangers,) भीरु timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमख|शतमखः
शतमख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. An owl.<BR> E. शत, मख a sacrifice: the per-<BR>formance of a hundred Aśhwa-medhas obtaining this situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमन्यु|शतमन्युः
शतमन्यु m. (-न्युः) INDRA.<BR> E. शत a hundred, मन्यु a sacrifice: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमान|शतमानः
शतमान mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>	 1. A pala of silver.<BR>	 2. An Āḍhaka or measure so<BR>termed.<BR> E. शत a hundred, मान measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमारिन्
शतमारिन् m. (-री) A man who has killed a hundred others.<BR> E. शत, मारिन् a killer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमार्ज|शतमार्जः
शतमार्ज m. (-र्जः) An armourer, a cutler.<BR> E. शत a hundred, (many weapons,)<BR>and मार्ज who cleans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमुख
शतमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं)<BR>	 1. Having a hundred mouths.<BR>	 2. Having a<BR>hundred openings.<BR>	 f. (-खी) A brush or broom.<BR> E. शत, मुख mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतमूली
शतमूली f. (-ली) A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR> E. शत a hundred or<BR>many, मूल a root, fem. aff. ङीष्; also with कन् added शतमूलिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतयष्टिक|शतयष्टिकः
शतयष्टिक m. (-कः) A necklace of 100 strings.<BR> E. शत a hundred, यष्टि a<BR>string, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=705-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतरूपा
शतरूपा f. (-पा)<BR>	 1. Name of the wife of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. An epithet of<BR>SĀVITRI, the daughter of BRAHMĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतलक्ष
शतलक्ष n. (-क्षं) A hundred Lākhs, ten millions.<BR> E. शत, लक्ष a hundred thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतलम्पक
शतलम्पक m. (-कः) A name of poet BHĀRAVI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतवर्ष
शतवर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं) Of a hundred years.<BR>	 n. (-र्षं) A century.<BR> E. शत, वर्ष a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतवीर्य्या|शतवीर्या
शतवीर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) White Dūrbā grass, (Panicum dactylon with white<BR>blossoms)<BR> E. शत a hundred, वीर्य्य seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतवेधिन्
शतवेधिन् m. (-धी) A sort of dock or sorrel, (Oxalis monadelpha or<BR>Rumex vesicarius.)<BR> E. शत a hundred, व्यध् to pierce, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतशस्
शतशस् Ind. By hundreds, a hundred-fold.<BR> E. शत, and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतशाख
शतशाख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>	 1. Having many branches.<BR>	 2. Multiform,<BR>various.<BR> E. शत, and शाखा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसहस्र|शतसहस्रं
शतसहस्र n. (-स्रं) A hundred thousand.<BR> E. शत, and सहस्र a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसहस्रशस
शतसहस्रशस Ind. By myriads.<BR> E. शस् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतसाहस्र
शतसाहस्र mfn. (-स्रः-स्री-स्रं) Having a hundred thousand, bought with,<BR>consisting of, &c.<BR> E. शतसहस्र, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतह्रदा
शतह्रदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. Lightning.<BR>	 2. The thunderbolt.<BR> E. शत a hundred, ह्रद<BR>a ray of light, or ह्राद sound; the vowel made short; also शतह्रादा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शताक्ष
शताक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Hundred-eyed.<BR>	 f. (-क्षी)<BR>	 1. Nigth.<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>	 3. The goddess PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. शत a hun-<BR>dred, अक्ष for अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शताङ्ग|शतांग|शताङ्गः
शताङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A car, a chariot.<BR> E. शत a hundred, and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतानक|शतानकं
शतानक n. (-कं) A place where dead bodies are burnt or buried, a burial<BR>ground, a cemetery.<BR> E. शत a hundred, आनक a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतानन्द|शतानंद|शतानन्दः
शतानन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 3. The car of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. The Muni GAUTAMA, the founder of the logical school<BR>of philosophy.<BR>	 5. The eldest son of GAUTAMA (according to the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa,) and Purohit or religious adviser of JANAKA of MITHILĀ.<BR>E. शत hundred or many, and आनन्द who delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतानीक|शतानीकः
शतानीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An old man.<BR>	 2. The name of a sovereign, the son<BR>and successor of JANAMEJAYA.<BR>	 3. The name of a saint, the pupil<BR>of VYĀSA.<BR> E. शत a hundred, आङ् before नी to obtain, कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतायुस्
शतायुस् m. (-युः) A man of hundred years old.<BR> E. शत, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतार|शतारं
शतार n. (-रं) The thunderbolt.<BR> E. शत a hundred, ऋ to go, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतारुस्
शतारुस् nf. (-रुः-रुषी) A leprous disease of the skin.<BR> E. शत hundred or<BR>many, and अरुस् a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतार्णा
शतार्णा f. (-र्णा) A plant, (Anethum sowa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतावरी
शतावरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (Asparagus recemosus.)<BR>	 2. The wife of<BR>INDRA.<BR> E. शत a hundred, (roots,) आङ् before वृ to choose, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतावर्त्त|शतावर्त|शतावर्तः|शतावर्त्तः
शतावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. शत a hundred, आवर्त्त revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतावर्त्तिन्|शतावर्तिन्
शतावर्त्तिन् m. (-र्त्ती) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. शत a hundred, आवर्त्त revolving, (appear-<BR>ances, or in the mind of his worshippers,) इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शताह्व
शताह्व f. (-ह्वा-ह्वी) A sort of dill or fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR> E. शत a hun-<BR>dred, and आह्वा name, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतिक|शतिकः
शतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Indicative of a hundred, (as a sign or omen.)<BR>2. Doing or effecting any thing with a hundred.<BR>	 3. Bearing tax or<BR>interest per hundred.<BR>	 4. Brought with a hundred.<BR>	 5. Changed with<BR>or for a hundred, &c.<BR>	 6. Relating or belonging to a hundred. E.<BR>शत a hundred, ठक्, ठञ् or ठन् aff.; also with यत् aff. शत्य in the same<BR>acceptations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतिन्
शतिन् m. (-ती) The owner of a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतेर|शतेरः
शतेर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An enemy.<BR>	 2. Injury, detriment, hurt.<BR> E. शद् to decay,<BR>to go, Unādi aff. एरक्, द changed to त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतेश|शतेशः
शतेश m. (-शः) The ruler or head-man of a hundred, (villages.)<BR> E. शत, ईश sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्त्रि
शत्त्रि m. (-त्त्रिः) An elephant.<BR> E. शद् to go, त्त्रिप् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्य|शत्यः
शत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Bought with a hundred, &c.: see शतिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रु|शत्रुः
शत्रु m. (-त्रुः)<BR>	 1. An enemy, a foe, an adversary.<BR>	 2. A destroyer.<BR>	 3. A<BR>political enemy, a neighbouring prince as being one with whom<BR>disputes are likely to occur.<BR> E. शद् to go, Unādi aff. त्रुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुकक्ष
शत्रुकक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The side of an enemy.<BR>	 2. An antagonist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुघात
शत्रुघात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Who beats or kills an enemy.<BR> E. शत्रु, घात who<BR>kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुघ्न|शत्रुघ्नः
शत्रुघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Killing a foe.<BR>	 m. (-घ्नः) The second brother of<BR>RĀMACHANDRA, the son of DASARATHA by SUMITRĀ, and uterine<BR>brother of LAKSHMAṆA. He slew RĀVAṆA, the demon and colo-<BR>nized MATHURĀ.<BR> E. शत्रु an enemy, and घ्न destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुघ्नजननी
शत्रुघ्नजननी f. (-नी) SUMITRĀ, the mother of LAKSHMAṆA, and ŚATRU-<BR>GHNA.<BR> E. शत्रुघ्न ŚATRUGHNA, and जननी the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुञ्जय|शत्रुंजय|शत्रुंजयः|शत्रुञ्जयः
शत्रुञ्जय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Subduing an enemy.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The mountain<BR>Vimala, or Girnār, or a mountainous range in Guzerāt.<BR>	 2. An<BR>elephant.<BR> E. शत्रु a foe, जि to conquer, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुता
शत्रुता f. (-ता) Hostility, enmity.<BR> E. तल् added to शत्रु: with त्व, शत्रुत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुनिकाय
शत्रुनिकाय m. (-यः) A number of enemies.<BR> E. शत्रु, निकाय a quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुनिलय
शत्रुनिलय m. (-यः) The dwelling of a foe.<BR> E. शत्रु and निलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुन्तप|शत्रुंतप|शत्रुन्तपः
शत्रुन्तप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Subduing enemies.<BR> E. शत्रु, तप् to harass, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुपक्ष|शत्रुपक्षः
शत्रुपक्ष m. (-क्षः) An antagonist, an enemy.<BR> E. शत्रु and पक्ष side or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुमर्द्दन|शत्रुमर्दन|शत्रुमर्दनः|शत्रुमर्द्दनः
शत्रुमर्द्दन m. (-नः) ŚATRUGHNA, the brother of RĀMA.<BR> E. शत्रु a foe, मर्द्दन<BR>destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुसह
शत्रुसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Bearing or patient with an enemy.<BR> E. शत्रु, सह् to bear, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्वरी
शत्वरी f. (-री) Night.<BR> E. शद् to go, क्वरप् aff.; fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्
शद्(औ, ऌ,)औ शदऌ r. 1st cl. (शीयते)<BR>	 1. To perish gradually, to wither<BR>or decay.<BR>	 2. To fall.<BR>	 3. To throw down.<BR>	 4. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद|शदः
शद m. (-दः) A vegetable, any edible vegetable product, as fruits, roots,<BR>&c.<BR> E. शद् to wither, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रि|शद्रिः
शद्रि m. (-द्रिः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR>	 3. ARJUNA.<BR>	 f. (-द्रिः)<BR>	 1. Light-<BR>ning.<BR>	 2. Clayed or candied sugar.<BR> E. शद् to go, क्रि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रु|शद्रुः
शद्रु mfn. (-द्रुः-द्रुः-द्रु)<BR>	 1. Wasting, decaying, falling, perishing.<BR>	 2. Going,<BR>moving.<BR> E. शद् to go, क्रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनकावलि|शनकावलिः
शनकावलि f. (-लिः or ली) A shrub, (Pothos officinalis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनकैस्
शनकैस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Slowly.<BR>	 2. Mildly.<BR>	 3. Gradually.<BR>	 4. Successively: the same as शनैस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनपर्णी
शनपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A medicinal plant, (Wrightea antidysenterica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनि|शनिः
शनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. The planet SATURN; he is the son of the Sun and<BR>represented as of a black colour or dressed in dark clothes.<BR>	 2.<BR>Saturday.<BR> E. शण् to give, aff. इन्; or शो-अनि-किच्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिज
शनिज n. (-जं) Black pepper.<BR> E. शनि SATURN, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिप्रदोष|शनिप्रदोषः
शनिप्रदोष m. (-षः) Worship of ŚIVA on the thirteenth day of a lunar<BR>fortnight when it falls on a Saturday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिप्रसू
शनिप्रसू f. (-सूः) CHHĀYĀ, the wife of the Sun.<BR> E. शनि SATURN, प्रसू the mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिप्रिय|शनिप्रियं
शनिप्रिय n. (-यं) The emerald or sapphire.<BR> E. शनि SATURN, प्रिय dear to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिवार|शनिवारः
शनिवार m. (-रः) Saturday.<BR> E. शनि the planet, and वार in this and simi-<BR>lar compounds, a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनैश्चर|शनैश्चरः
शनैश्चर m. (-रः) The planet SATURN or its mythological personification.<BR>Adj. Moving slowly.<BR> E. शनैस् slowly, and चर who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनैस्
शनैस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Slowly, tardily.<BR>	 2. Independently, at will.<BR>	 3. Softly.<BR>	 4.<BR>Little by little.<BR>	 5. In order.<BR> E. शण् to give, to produce,) aff. ऐस<BR>and the consonant changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् r. 1st cl. (शपति-ते) r. 4th cl. (शप्यति-ते)<BR>	 1. To revile, to wish evi-<BR>imprecations on, to curse.<BR>	 2. To take an oath, to swear; in this<BR>sense शप् sometimes governs a cognate accusative; but gener-<BR>ally it takes the accusative of the person to whom a promise is<BR>made, and the instrumental of the object by which it is made;<BR>when used intransitively it governs the dative of the object or<BR>person, by which the oath is taken.<BR>	 3. To blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् Ind. A particle and prefix of assent or acceptance, as शप्करोति he accepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप|शपः
शप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. An oath.<BR>	 2. An imprecation, a curse, cursing.<BR>	 3. A<BR>corpse; also शव.<BR> E. शप् to curse, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपत्र
शपत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. An imprecation.<BR>	 2. An oath.<BR>	 3. Abusive language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपथ|शपथः
शपथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. An oath, asseveration by oath or ordeal.<BR>	 2. An impre-<BR>cation.<BR>	 3. Cursing, wishing ill to.<BR> E. शप् to swear, Unādi aff. अथन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपन|शपनं
शपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. An oath, confirmation of the truth by oath or ordeal.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">Page707-a+ 60</a>]<BR>2. Abuse, imprecation, cursing, malediction.<BR> E. शप् to curse,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=706-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपमान
शपमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Reviling.<BR>	 2. Swearing.<BR> E. शप् to curse, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्त|शप्तः
शप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Cursed.<BR>	 2. Sworn.<BR>	 3. Abused.<BR>	 m. (-प्तः) A sort<BR>of grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR> E. शप् to curse, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफ|शफं|शफः
शफ mn. (-फः-फं)<BR>	 1. A hoof in general.<BR>	 2. The root of a tree.<BR>	 3. The hoof<BR>of a horse.<BR> E. शम् to be tranquil, aff. अच्, the final changed to फ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफर|शफरः
शफर mf. (-रः-री) A small fish, (Cyprinus Sophore, HAM.)<BR> E. शफ a hoof,<BR>रा to give, (to resemble,) aff. क । “पुंँटीमाछ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफराधिप|शफराधिपः
शफराधिप m. (-पः) The Ilisha fish, (Ilisha clupanodon.)<BR> E. शफर a carp, अधिप chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबल|शबलः
शबल f. (-ला or ली) A spotted cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्द|शब्दः
शब्द r. 10th cl. (शब्दयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sound, to make or utter sound.<BR>	 2. To<BR>call out to, to speak; with the prefixes प्र, प्रति, or वि, as well as<BR>uncompounded, this root means also:--1. To promise.<BR>	 2. To make<BR>clear or manifest, to explain.<BR>	 3. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्द|शब्दः
शब्द m. (-ब्दः)<BR>	 1. Sound in general, (considered as the property of<BR>Ākāsha.)<BR>	 2. A sound, a word.<BR>	 3. A declinable word, as noun,<BR>pronoun, &c., (in gram.)<BR>	 4. The sound of a musical instrument.<BR>	 5.<BR>Verbal authority, (considered as a “proof” by the Naiyāyikas.) E.<BR>शब्द् to sound, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दकार|शब्दकारः
शब्दकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Sounding, sonorous.<BR> E. शब्द sound, &c., कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दकोष
शब्दकोष m. (-षः) A lexicon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दगत
शब्दगत Adj. Being or residing in word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दग्रह|शब्दग्रहः
शब्दग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The ear.<BR>	 2. Receiving or catching sound.<BR>	 3. A fabu-<BR>lous arrow.<BR> E. शब्द sound, ग्रह what receives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दचातुर्य्य|शब्दचातुर्य
शब्दचातुर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Cleverness of diction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दचित्र
शब्दचित्र n. (-त्रं) One of the two divisions of the last division of poetry;<BR>in it the charm consists in the fanciful use of words giving plea-<BR>sure to the ear by mere sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दचोर|शब्दचोरः
शब्दचोर m. (-रः) A plagiary.<BR> E. शब्द, and चोर a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दतन्मात्र
शब्दतन्मात्र n. (-त्रं) The subtile element of sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दन|शब्दनः
शब्दन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sounding, sonorous.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sounding, uttering<BR>sounds.<BR>	 2. Sound.<BR>	 3. Calling out.<BR> E. शब्द् to sound, aff. ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दपति|शब्दपतिः
शब्दपति m. (-तिः) A nominal lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दबोध|शब्दबोधः
शब्दबोध m. (-धः) Knowledge derived from verbal testimony, (in phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दब्रह्मन्
शब्दब्रह्मन् n. (-ह्म) Inspired writ, the Vedas as uncreated and identifi-<BR>able with the Supreme Spirit.<BR> E. शब्द, and ब्रह्मन् the supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दभेदिन्
शब्दभेदिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A name of ARJUNA.<BR>	 2. The anus.<BR>	 3. A kind of<BR>arrow.<BR> E. शब्द sound, noise, and भेदिन् breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दयोनि|शब्दयोनिः
शब्दयोनि f. (-निः) A root, a radical word.<BR> E. शब्द, योनि place of origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दवृत्ति|शब्दवृत्तिः
शब्दवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Function of a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दवेधिन्
शब्दवेधिन् m. (-धी)<BR>	 1. ARJUNA.<BR>	 2. A kind of arrow. Adj. Hitting an<BR>invisible mark by the clue of mere sound.<BR> E. शब्द sound, and वेधिन्<BR>piercing; terrifying his enemies by his shouts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशक्ति|शब्दशक्तिः
शब्दशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Force or signification of words.<BR> E. शब्द, शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशासन
शब्दशासन n. (-नं) The rules of grammar.<BR> E. शब्द, and शासन regulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशास्त्र
शब्दशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) Philology, grammar, &c.<BR> E. शब्द, शास्त्र a science, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दश्लेष|शब्दश्लेषः
शब्दश्लेष m. (-षः) A play upon words, a verbal equivoque, a pun, (it<BR>differs from अर्थश्लेष in that the figure vanishes if the words on<BR>which it depends are substituted by others of the same meaning.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दसंग्रह
शब्दसंग्रह m. (-हः) A vocabulary, a lexicon.<BR> E. शब्द, and संग्रह collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दादि
शब्दादि m. (-दिः) The objects of sense, viz:--sound, form, scent, juice,<BR>contact; or what affords matter for the exercise of hearing, seeing,<BR>smelling, tasting and touching.<BR> E. शब्द, and आदि other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दाधिष्ठान|शब्दाधिष्ठानं
शब्दाधिष्ठान n. (-नं) The ear.<BR> E. शब्द sound, अधिष्ठान receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दानुरूप
शब्दानुरूप n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. Conformity or proportion to the sound.<BR>	 2. Imita-<BR>tion of sound.<BR> E. शब्द, अनुरूप conformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दानुशासन
शब्दानुशासन n. (-नं) The acceptation or sense of words.<BR> E. शब्द, अनुशासन government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दायमान
शब्दायमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sounding.<BR> E. शब्द sound, nominal verb,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दार्थ|शब्दार्थः
शब्दार्थ m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. The sense or meaning of words.<BR>	 2. Words and sense.<BR>E. शब्द, अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दालङ्कार|शब्दालंकार|शब्दालंकारः
शब्दालङ्कार m. (-रः) Rhetorical use of words; verbal figure, as alliter-<BR>ation, &c.<BR> E. शब्द and अलङ्कार ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दित
शब्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sounded.<BR>	 2. Uttered, articulated.<BR>	 3. Explained,<BR>made public or manifest.<BR>	 4. Converted into a noun, &c.<BR> E. शब्द् to<BR>sound. क्त aff.; or शब्द, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
शम्(इर् उ)इरश्मु r. 4th cl. (शाम्यति)<BR>	 1. To be pacified, to be calmed or<BR>appeased.<BR>	 2. To pacify, to calm.<BR>	 3. To be tranquil, to have the<BR>passions tamed and quiescent. r. 10th cl. (शामयते) To look, to look<BR>at or inspect. (शमयति-ते) To allay, to appease. (शामयति) To display.<BR>With उप prefixed, To tranquillize, to allay, to tame. With नि, 1.<BR>To hear.<BR>	 2. To observe, to perceive.<BR>	 3. To restrain or prevent. With<BR>प्र, 1. To destroy.<BR>	 2. To be very tranquil.<BR>	 3. To be soothed.<BR>	 4. To<BR>cease.<BR>	 5. To fade away. With सम्, To be extinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
शम् Ind. A particle meaning “welfare, prosperity, blessing, health,”<BR>(with a dat. or gen.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम|शमः
शम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Quiet of mind, stoicism, indifference, the absence of<BR>passion, as one of the qualities of the Vedāntī or follower of the<BR>Vedānta doctrine; it is defined to be the exclusion of every idea<BR>not derived from the precepts of that philosophy, and is so far<BR>synonymous with abstract meditation on BRAHMĀ, or God.<BR>	 2.<BR>Quiet, tranquillity, rest, calm, (in general.)<BR>	 3. Final happiness,<BR>emancipation from human existence.<BR>	 4. Cure, convalescence,<BR>alleviation of pain or disease.<BR>	 5. Abuse, imprecation, malediction.<BR>6. The hand.<BR> E. शम् to be pacified or calm, aff. घञ्, and the vowel<BR>not made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमक|शमकः
शमक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Pacifier, pacificator, tranquillizing.<BR> E. शम् to be<BR>tranquil, ण्वुल् aff. of attributive agency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमथ|शमथः
शमथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Quiet, tranquillity: (see the last)<BR>	 2. A counsellor,<BR>a minister.<BR> E. शम् to be calm, Unādi aff. अथच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमन|शमनं|शमनः
शमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing animals for sacrifice, immolation.<BR>	 2. Mental<BR>tranquillity, calmness, indifference.<BR>	 3. Abuse, malediction.<BR>	 4.<BR>Hurt, injury.<BR>	 5. Chewing, swallowing.<BR>	 6. The act of appeasing,<BR>soothing, consoling.<BR>	 7. Cessation, end, destruction.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1.<BR>YAMA, the ruler of Tartarus.<BR>	 2. An antelope.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Night. E.<BR>शम् to be tranquil, aff. ल्युट् or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनस्वसृ
शमनस्वसृ f. (-सा) YAMUNĀ, the personified river.<BR> E. शमन YAMA and<BR>स्वसृ the sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनीषद|शमनीषदः
शमनीषद m. (-दः) A Rākshasa, an evil spirit, a goblin.<BR> E. शमन night, षद who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमयत्
शमयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Appeasing, allaying.<BR>	 2. Terminating,<BR>stopping.<BR> E. शम् to pacify, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमल|शमलं
शमल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Fæces, ordure.<BR>	 2. Sin, impurity.<BR> E. शम् to be quiet, Unādi aff. कलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमान्तक|शमांतक|शमान्तकः
शमान्तक m. (-कः) The deity KĀMA or love, (personified.)<BR> E. शम mental<BR>or devotional tranquillity, अन्तक destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमि|शमिः
शमि f. (-मिः or मी) A legume or pod.<BR>	 f. (-मी)<BR>	 1. The Sami tree, (Acacia<BR>suma, Rox.)<BR>	 2. A shrub, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR> E. शम् to<BR>pacify, (sickness,) aff. इन्, ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमित|शमितः
शमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pacified, appeased.<BR>	 2. Quiet, tranquil, calm.<BR>3. Alleviated, relieved.<BR>	 4. Tempered, moderated.<BR>	 5. Relaxed,<BR>intermitted.<BR> E. शम् to be pacified or calm, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिन्
शमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Pacific, tranquillized.<BR> E. शम् to be tranquil, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिर|शमिरः
शमिर m. (-रः) A variety of the Śami tree.<BR> E. शमी the Śami tree, रा to<BR>get, (to resemble,) aff. क, and the vowel made short; also शमीर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिरोह|शमिरोहः
शमिरोह m. (-हः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. शमि for शमी the Śami tree, रोह who ascends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीगर्भ|शमीगर्भः
शमीगर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. A man of the sacerdotal class, a Brāhman.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of AGNI or fire.<BR> E. शमी the mimosa, (the wood of which is<BR>essential for certain sacrifice, &c.) and गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीधान्य|शमीधान्यं
शमीधान्य n. (-न्यं) Pulse, grain which grows in legumes or pods.<BR> E. शमी<BR>a legume, and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=707-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीपत्री
शमीपत्री f. (-त्री) A sort of sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR> E. शमी<BR>Acacia Suma, and पत्र the leaf; having a similar leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीर|शमीरः
शमीर m. (-रः) A small variety of the Mimosa Suma.<BR> E. शमी the Śami<BR>tree, and र aff. of diminution; also sometimes read शमिर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्पा|शंपा
शम्पा f. (-म्पा) Lightning.<BR> E. शम् happiness, पा to drink, क and टाप् affs.;<BR>destroying pleasure by its awful appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्पाक|शंपाक|शम्पाकः
शम्पाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A kind of Cassia, (C. fistula.)<BR>	 2. Bringing to matu-<BR>rity or ripeness, cooking, maturing.<BR>	 3. The lac pigment.<BR> E. शम्<BR>pleasure and पाक what matures; also सम्पाक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्ब्|शंब्
शम्ब् r. 1st cl. (शम्बति) To go. r. 10th cl. (शम्बयति-ते) To accumulate, to<BR>collect or heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्ब|शंब|शम्बः
शम्ब mfn. (-म्बः-म्बा-म्बं)<BR>	 1. Happy, fortunate.<BR>	 2. Poor, indigent.<BR>	 m. (-म्बः)<BR>1. INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>	 2. The iron head of a pestle.<BR>	 3. An iron<BR>chain worn round the loins.<BR>	 4. The second ploughing of a field.<BR>E. शम् happiness, and ब possessive aff.; or शम्ब् to accumulate, aff.<BR>अच्; it is also read सव, शंव, and सम्ब ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बर|शंबर|शम्बरं|शम्बरः
शम्बर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. A religious observance.<BR>	 3. Wealth.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>1. A Daitya.<BR>	 2. A sort of deer.<BR>	 3. A mountain.<BR>	 4. A fish in gener-<BR>al.<BR>	 5. War.<BR>	 6. Best, excellent.<BR>	 7. A Bauddha.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A drug<BR>or medicinal plant, (Anthericum tuberosum.)<BR>	 2. A female juggler.<BR>E. शम्ब् to accumulate, अरन् aff.; or श happiness, वृ to choose,<BR>aff. अप्; also read शंवर and सम्बर or संवर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बरसूदन|शंबरसूदन|शम्बरसूदनः
शम्बरसूदन m. (-नः) A name of PRADYUMNA.<BR> E. शम्बर the Daitya, सूदन destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बरारि|शंबरारि|शम्बरारिः
शम्बरारि m. (-रिः) PRADYUMNA.<BR> E. शम्बर the Daitya, अरि the foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बल|शंबल|शंबलं|शंबलः|शम्बलः
शम्बल mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. Provender for a journey, stock for travelling<BR>expenses.<BR>	 2. A bank, a shore.<BR>	 3. Envy, impatience or dislike of<BR>another's success.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A procuress, a bawd.<BR> E. शम्ब् to go, to<BR>collect, कलच् aff.; also शवल, and सम्बल or संवल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बाकृत|शम्बाकृतं
शम्बाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Twice-ploughed, (a field.)<BR> E. शम्ब a second<BR>ploughing, कृत made, and डाच् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बु|शंबु|शंबुः|शम्बुः
शम्बु m. (-म्बुः) A bivalve-shell. E. See शम्बूक below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बुक|शंबुक|शंबुकः|शम्बुकः
शम्बुक m. (-कः) A bivalve-shell: see शम्बूक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बुक्क|शंबुक्क|शंबुक्कः|शम्बुक्कः
शम्बुक्क m. (-क्कः) A bivalve-shell: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बूक|शंबूक|शंबूकः|शम्बूकः
शम्बूक mf. (-कः-का) A bivalve-shell.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A conch-shell.<BR>	 2. A<BR>snail.<BR>	 3. A Śūdra, who had become a devotee in the time of<BR>RĀMACHANDRA, and was slain by him.<BR>	 4. The edge of the frontal<BR>protuberance of the elephant.<BR>	 5. The name of a Daitya.<BR> E. शम् to<BR>be tranquil, ऊकन् aff. and वुक् augment; also with the vowel short,<BR>शम्बुक, and the final consonant then rejected, शम्बु; it is also<BR>read, शम्बुक्क and with the first vowel long, शाम्बूक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भ|शंभ|शंभः|शम्भः
शम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>	 2. The iron bound head of a<BR>club or pestle.<BR>	 3. A happy man.<BR> E. शम् particle of auspiciousness,<BR>भा to shine, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भली|शंभली
शम्भली f. (-ली) A bawd, a procuress.<BR> E. शम् pleasure, भल् to describe, अच् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भु|शंभु|शंभुः|शम्भुः
शम्भु m. (-म्भुः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. A Jaina sanctified teacher.<BR>4. A Siddha, a demi-divine being.<BR>	 5. A sage, a venerable man.<BR>	 6.<BR>A kind of Asclepias.<BR> E. शम् auspicious particle, भू to be, डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भुतनय|शंभुतनय|शंभुतनयः|शम्भुतनयः
शम्भुतनय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. KĀRTTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. GAṆEŚA.<BR> E. शम्भु ŚIVA, तनय son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भुनन्दन|शंभुनंदन|शंभुनन्दन|शंभुनन्दनः|शम्भुनन्दनः
शम्भुनन्दन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>	 2. A name of KARTIKEYA.<BR>E. शम्भु ŚIVA, नन्दन son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भुप्रिया|शंभुप्रिया
शम्भुप्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 2. An epithet of DURGĀ. E.<BR>शम्भु ŚIVA, प्रिया beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्या
शम्या f. (-म्या)<BR>	 1. The pin of a yoke.<BR>	 2. A sacrificial vessel.<BR>	 3. A stick,<BR>a staff.<BR> E. शम् to be kept quiet, यत् aff., fem. aff. टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्यापात|शम्यापातः
शम्यापात m. (-तः) The cast of a stick.<BR> E. शम्या and पात alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय|शयः
शय mfn. (-यः-या or यी-यं) Asleep, sleeping.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A hand.<BR>	 2. A<BR>snake, (Boa constrictor.)<BR>	 3. Sleep, sleeping.<BR>	 4. A bed, a couch.<BR>	 5.<BR>Abuse, imprecation.<BR> E. शी to sleep, aff. घ, टच् or अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयण्ड|शयंड|शयण्डः
शयण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डी-ण्डं) Asleep, sleeping,<BR> E. शी to sleep, अण्डच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयथ|शयथः
शयथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Asleep, sleeping.<BR>	 m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Death, dying.<BR>	 2. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">Page708-b+ 60</a>]<BR>sort of snake, the Boa.<BR>	 3. A boar.<BR>	 4. A fish.<BR> E. शी to sleep, अथच्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयन|शयनं
शयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sleep.<BR>	 2. A bed, a couch.<BR>	 3. Copulation.<BR> E. शी to sleep, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनगृह
शयनगृह n. (-हं) A bed-chamber.<BR> E. शयन and गृह house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनागार|शयनागारः
शयनागार m. (-रः) A bed chamber.<BR> E. शयन and आगार house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनीय|शयनीयं
शयनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fit for or suitable to sleep, to be slept on, &c.<BR>n. (-यं) A bed, a couch.<BR> E. शी to sleep, अनीयर् aff. of the future<BR>participle; also with कन् added शयनीयक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनैकादशी
शयनैकादशी f. (-शी) The eleventh day of the light-half of Āshādha, on<BR>which VIṢṆU'S sleep commences.<BR> E. शयन, एकादशी 11th lunation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयान|शयानः
शयान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sleeping, asleep.<BR> E. शी to sleep, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयानक|शयानकः
शयानक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. A lizard.<BR> E. शी to sleep, आनक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयालु|शयालुः
शयालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Sleepy, slothful, sluggish.<BR>	 m. (-लुः)<BR>	 1. A kind of<BR>snake, the Boa.<BR>	 2. A dog.<BR>	 3. A jackal.<BR> E. शी to sleep, आलुच् aff,<BR>implying disposition or habit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयित|शयितः
शयित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Asleep.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A plant, (Cordia myxa.)<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Sleep, sleeping.<BR> E. शी to sleep, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयितवत्
शयितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Sleeping, asleep.<BR> E. शीङ् to sleep, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयित्वा
शयित्वा Ind. Having slept.<BR> E. शी to sleep, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयु|शयुः
शयु m. (-युः) A large snake, (Boa.)<BR> E. शी to sleep, उ Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयुन|शयुनः
शयुन m. (-नः) A large kind of snake, (Boa.)<BR> E. शीङ् to sleep, Unādi aff. उनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय्या
शय्या f. (-य्या)<BR>	 1. A bed, a couch, a sopha.<BR>	 2. Tying in knots, stringing.<BR>E. शी to sleep, क्यप् aff., and अयङ् substituted for the vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर|शरं|शरः
शर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A sort of reed or grass, (Saccharum sara.)<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>3. The upper part or cream of slightly curdled milk.<BR>	 4. Mischief,<BR>injury, hurt.<BR>	 5. The number “five.” n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Versed<BR>sine of an arc.<BR> E. शॄ to hurt, aff. अप् or अच्; also सर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरकाण्ड|शरकांड|शरकाण्डः
शरकाण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. The stem of the Saccharum.<BR>	 2. The shaft of an<BR>arrow.<BR> E. शर, काण्ड stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरच्चन्द्र|शरच्चंद्र|शरच्चन्द्रः
शरच्चन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) The autumnal moon.<BR> E. शरद्, चन्द्र moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरज|शरजं|शरजः
शरज n. (-जं) Butter made from milk one day old.<BR> E. शर cream, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरजन्मन्
शरजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) A name of KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. शर a sort of grass, and<BR>जन्मन् birth: having been brought up in thickets of that grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरट|शरटः
शरट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A lizard, a chamæleon.<BR>	 2. Safflower, the plant.<BR> E. शॄ<BR>to hurt, अटन् aff.; also सरट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण|शरणं
शरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. A preserver, a protector, what or who<BR>protects or preserves.<BR>	 3. Preservation, protection, defence.<BR>	 4.<BR>Killing, slaying.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A plant, (Celtis.)<BR> E. शॄ to injure, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणागत|शरणागतः
शरणागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Refuge, appellant, one who comes for protec-<BR>tion or refuge.<BR> E. शरण protection, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणापन्न
शरणापन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Taken refuge.<BR> E. शरण and आपन्न obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणार्थिन्
शरणार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Unfortunate, wretched, involved in cala-<BR>mity or ruin, and dependent on others for protection or aid. E.<BR>शरण protection, and अर्थिन् soliciting, requiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणार्पक|शरणार्पकः
शरणार्पक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Unfortunate, calamitous, distressed, ruined:<BR>(see the last.)<BR> E. शरण protection, अर्पक who causes to be afforded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणि|शरणिः
शरणि mf. (-णिः-णी) A road, a path, a way.<BR> E. शॄ to hurt, अनि aff.; more<BR>usually सरणि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणैषिन्
शरणैषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Seeking for an asylum or protection.<BR> E. शरण, एषिन् who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्ड|शरंड|शरंडः|शरण्डः
शरण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A bird in general.<BR>	 2. A lizard, a chamæleon.<BR>	 3. A<BR>kind of ornament.<BR>	 4. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 5. A libertine, a lecher.<BR>E. शॄ to injure, (fruit, &c.) अण्डच् Unādi aff.; also सरण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्य|शरण्यः
शरण्य mfn. (-ण्यः-ण्या-ण्यं) To be protected or aided, poor, miserable,<BR>helpless.<BR>	 n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. A protection, a protector, that which or who<BR>affords refuge and defence.<BR>	 2. A house.<BR>	 3. Protection, defence.<BR>	 4.<BR>Injury, hurt.<BR> E. शृ to hurt, Unādi aff. अन्य; or शरण protection,<BR>and यत् aff. of fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्यु|शरण्युः
शरण्यु m. (-ण्युः)<BR>	 1. A plough.<BR>	 2. Wind, air.<BR>	 3. A protector, a defender.<BR>4. A cloud.<BR> E. शृ to injure, अन्यु aff.; also सरण्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरत्कामिन्
शरत्कामिन् m. (-मी) A dog.<BR> E. शरद् autumn, and कामिन् uxorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=708-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरत्काल|शरत्कालः
शरत्काल n. (-लं) The autumnal season.<BR> E. शरद् and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरत्कालीन
शरत्कालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Autumnal.<BR> E. शरत्काल and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरत्पर्व्वन्|शरत्पर्वन्
शरत्पर्व्वन् n. (-र्व्व) A festival, on the full-moon of Āshwin, (September-<BR>October:) see कोजागर.<BR> E. शरद् autumn, and पर्व्वन् a holy day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरद्
शरद् f. (-रत् or रद्)<BR>	 1. The season of autumn or the sultry season;<BR>the two months succeeding the rains; according to the VAIDIKAS,<BR>comprising the months BHĀDRA and ĀSHWIN, and according to<BR>the PAURĀNIKAS, ĀSHWIN and KĀRTIKA, fluctuating thus from<BR>AUGUST to NOVEMBER.<BR>	 2. A year.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, अदि Unādi<BR>aff.; also with टाप् added शरदा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरदा
शरदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. A year.<BR>	 2. The sultry season. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरदिज|शरदिजं
शरदिज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Autumnal, produced in Śarat or the season of<BR>autumn.<BR> E. शरद् as above in the 7th case, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरधि|शरधिः
शरधि m. (-धिः) A quiver.<BR> E. शर an arrow, धा to have or contain, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरन्मुख
शरन्मुख n. (-खं) Commencement of the autumn.<BR> E. शरद्, मुख beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरपात|शरपातः
शरपात m. (-तः) An arrow's fall or flight.<BR> E. शर and पात alighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरपातस्थान
शरपातस्थान n. (-नं) A bowshot, an arrow's flight.<BR> E. शरपात, स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरपुङ्खा|शरपुंखा
शरपुङ्खा f. (-ङ्खा) The feathered end of an arrow.<BR> E. शर an arrow, and<BR>पुङ्ख the feathered part of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरफल
शरफल n. (-लं) The blade or barb of an arrow.<BR> E. शर, and फल blade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरभ|शरभः
शरभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A fabulous animal, supposed to have eight legs, and<BR>to inhabit particularly the snowy mountains.<BR>	 2. A young elephant.<BR>3. A monkey in RĀMA'S army.<BR>	 4. A camel.<BR>	 5. A grasshopper.<BR>	 6.<BR>A locust.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, Unādi aff. अभच्; or शर an arrow, भा to<BR>shine, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरभू
शरभू m. (-भूः) KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. शर the grass, भू born; being reared in this grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरमय|शरमयं
शरमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of or consisting of Śara grass, &c.<BR> E. शर<BR>the grass, and मयट् aff., implying in this and other compounds<BR>change of form for any purpose except food or clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरमल्ल|शरमल्लः
शरमल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A small bird, considered as a variety of the Sālica or<BR>Mainā, (Turdus gosalica, RUCH, Mss.)<BR> E. शर the Śara grass, and<BR>मल्ल to hold or occupy, aff. अङ्; some authorities have शरमन्द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरयु|शरयुः
शरयु f. (-युः-यूः) The Sarajū-river; it is preferably, and more usually<BR>written सरयु, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरल|शरलः
शरल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Upright, honest.<BR>	 2. Crooked, fraudulent.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः) A tree, a sort of pine.<BR> E. सृ to go, अलच् aff., and स changed<BR>to श; whence the word is preferably read सरल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरलक|शरलकं
शरलक n. (-कं) Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरलता
शरलता f. (-ता) Uprightness, sincerity.<BR> E. तल् added to शरल; with त्व,<BR>शरलत्वं; also read सरलता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरव
शरव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A lid, a cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवणोद्भव|शरवणोद्भवः
शरवणोद्भव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. शर saccharum, वन a thicket or<BR>jungle, and उद्भव born: see शरजन्मन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवर्ष|शरवर्षः
शरवर्ष m. (-र्षः) A flight or shower of arrows.<BR> E. शर, वर्ष rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवर्षिन्
शरवर्षिन् mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि) Raining or shooting arrows.<BR> E. शर, वर्षिन् showering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवाणि|शरवाणिः
शरवाणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. The head of an arrow.<BR>	 2. A foot-soldier, an archer.<BR>3. A maker of arrows.<BR> E. शर an arrow, वण् to sound, aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरवृष्टि|शरवृष्टिः
शरवृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A heavy fall or shower of arrows.<BR> E. शर and वृष्टि rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरव्य|शरव्यं
शरव्य n. (-व्यं) A mark, a butt.<BR> E. शरु a weapon, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरसन्धान
शरसन्धान n. (-नं) Taking aim with an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराघात|शराघातः
शराघात m. (-तः) Shooting, (with a bow.)<BR> E. शर an arrow, आघात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराटि|शराटिः
शराटि f. (-टिः) A sort of bird, (Turdus ginginianus.)<BR> E. शर water or<BR>mischief, अट् to go, aff. इन्; or from अत् to go, शराति; and other-<BR>wise derived also शराडि and शरालि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराडि|शराडिः
शराडि f. (-डिः) A bird: see शरालि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराति|शरातिः
शराति f. (-तिः) A bird: see शराटि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराभ्यास|शराभ्यासः
शराभ्यास m. (-सः) Archery, practice with the bow and arrow.<BR> E. शर an arrow, अभ्यास exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारि|शरारिः
शरारि f. (-रिः) A sort of bird, commonly the Āli or Sarāli, (Turdus<BR>ginginianus.)<BR> E. शर water or mischief, ऋ to go, aff. इ; also ल<BR>being substituted, शरालि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारीमुखी
शरारीमुखी f. (-खी) Scissars.<BR> E. शरारी, मुख mouth or beak, ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारु|शरारुः
शरारु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु) Mischievous, noxious, hurtful.<BR> E. शृ to hurt, आरु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारोप|शरारोपः
शरारोप m. (-पः) A bow.<BR> E. शर an arrow, आरोप a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरालि|शरालिः
शरालि f. (-लिः or ली) Sarāli, a kind of bird, (Turdus ginginianus.)<BR> E. शर<BR>an arrow, अल् to be equal to, (in speed,) aff. इन्, and ङीष् optionally<BR>added; also शरारि, शराडि, शराटि, &c., and with कन् added, fem.<BR>form शरालिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराव|शरावं|शरावः
शराव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A lid, a cover.<BR>	 2. A shallow earthen cup or dish.<BR>	 3.<BR>A platter.<BR>	 4. A measure equal to two Kudavas.<BR> E. शर mischief,<BR>(from it,) अव् to preserve, aff. अण् or अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरावती
शरावती f. (-ती) A river so named.<BR> E. शर a sort of grass, मतुप् aff., fem.<BR>form, and the final of the first word made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराश्रय|शराश्रयः
शराश्रय m. (-यः) A quiver.<BR> E. शर an arrow, आश्रय receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरासन|शरासनं
शरासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A bow.<BR>	 2. Shooting arrows.<BR> E. शर, अस् to throw, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराहत
शराहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Struck by an arrow.<BR> E. शर, and आहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरिमन्
शरिमन् m. (-मा) Bearing, bringing forth.<BR> E. शॄ to hurt, इमनिच् Unādi<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीर|शरीरं
शरीर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. The body of any inanimate object.<BR>	 3. A<BR>dead body.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, to be injured, Unādi aff. ईरन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरक|शरीरकं|शरीरकः
शरीरक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A small or delicate body.<BR>	 2. The body.<BR> E. शरीर, and<BR>कन् diminutive, or pleonastic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरकर्षण
शरीरकर्षण n. (-णं) Emaciating or afflicting the body.<BR> E. शरीर and कर्षण attracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरज|शरीरजः
शरीरज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born or produced by the body, &c.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>1. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 2. The deity KĀMA or love.<BR>	 3. A son.<BR> E. शरीर<BR>the body, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरजन्मन्
शरीरजन्मन् mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म) Born or produced of or from the body.<BR> E. शरीर, जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरदण्ड|शरीरदंड|शरीरदण्डः
शरीरदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Corporal punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरपतन
शरीरपतन n. (-नं) Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरपाक|शरीरपाकः
शरीरपाक m. (-कः) Decay, emaciation.<BR> E. शरीर, and पाक a ripening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरबद्ध
शरीरबद्ध Adj. Invested with a body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरबन्धक|शरीरबंधक|शरीरबन्धकः
शरीरबन्धक m. (-कः) A hostage.<BR> E. शरीर, बन्धक a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरभाज्
शरीरभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Embodied, corporeal, having body.<BR> E. शरीर, भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरयष्टि|शरीरयष्टिः
शरीरयष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A slender body or figure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरयात्रा
शरीरयात्रा f. (-त्रा) Subsistence, support.<BR> E. शरीर, and यात्रा going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरयोग
शरीरयोग m. (-गः) Bodily union.<BR> E. शरीर, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरविमोक्षण
शरीरविमोक्षण n. (-णं) Liberation of the soul from the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरशुश्रूषा
शरीरशुश्रूषा f. (-षा) Personal attendance.<BR> E. शरीर and शुश्रूषा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरशोषण
शरीरशोषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Drying up, withering.<BR>	 2. Emaciating the body.<BR>E. शरीर, and शोषण drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरसंस्कार|शरीरसंस्कारः
शरीरसंस्कार m. (-रः) Purification of the body by various ceremonies at<BR>conception, birth, initiation, death, &c.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Decoration or<BR>adorning the person.<BR> E. शरीर and संस्कार making perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरावरण|शरीरावरणं
शरीरावरण n. (-णं) The skin.<BR> E. शरीर the body and आवरण enclosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरिन्
शरीरिन् mfn. (-रि-रिणी-रि) Embodied, corporeal, having body.<BR>	 m. (-री)<BR>An animal or sentiment being.<BR>	 n. (-रि) Life or soul connected<BR>with the body, or incorporate.<BR> E. शरीर the body and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरु|शरुः
शरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. Passion, anger.<BR>	 2. The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR>	 3. An<BR>arrow.<BR>	 4. Any weapon.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, Unādi aff. उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरेष्ट|शरेष्टः
शरेष्ट m. (-ष्टः) The mango-tree.<BR> E. शर an arrow and इष्ट desired; the<BR>blossoms of the mango being amongst those which tip the darts<BR>of CUPID.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करा
शर्करा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A potsherd, the fragrant of a broken pot.<BR>	 2. A stony<BR>nodule, or gravel.<BR>	 3. A soil or spot abounding in stony or gritty<BR>fragments.<BR>	 4. Clayed or candid sugar.<BR>	 5. A part, a piece.<BR>	 6.<BR>Gravel, (the disease.)<BR> E. शॄ to injure, Unādi aff. करन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्कराप्रभा
शर्कराप्रभा f. (-भा) The hell of gravel according to the Jainas, the<BR>second division of Tartarus.<BR> E. शर्करा gravel, प्रभा illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करावत्|शर्करावन्त्
शर्करावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Gritty, gravelly, full of stony particles. E.<BR>शर्करा gravel and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करिक|शर्करिकः
शर्करिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Stony, gravelly.<BR> E. शर्करा gravel, &c., ठज् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=709-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करिल|शर्करिलः
शर्करिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Abounding in stony or gravelly particles,<BR>(a spot, a place.)<BR> E. शर्करा gravel and इलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करी
शर्करी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A river.<BR>	 2. A girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्ध्
शर्ध् r. 1st cl. (शर्धति) To wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्द्ध
शर्द्ध mn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धं) Farting, a fart.<BR>	 m. (-र्द्धः)<BR>	 1. Strength.<BR>	 2. Multitude.<BR> E. शृध् to fart, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्द्धञ्जह
शर्द्धञ्जह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Causing flatulence.<BR>	 m. (-हः) Any leguminous<BR>grain or pulse, as beans, &c.<BR> E. शर्द्ध farting and हा to let go or loose,<BR>aff. खश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्ब्ब्|शर्ब्
शर्ब्ब् r. 1st cl. (शर्ब्बति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To hurt, to injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्म्मद|शर्मद|शर्मदः
शर्म्मद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Conferring prosperity, making happy, propitious.<BR>E. शर्म्मन् and द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्म्मन्|शर्मन्
शर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Happy, glad.<BR>	 n. (-र्म्म) Happiness, pleasure.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-र्म्मा) A name or appellation common to and proper for Brāhmans.<BR>E. शॄ to injure or destroy, (ill fortune,) मनिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्म्मवत्|शर्मवत्|शर्मवन्त्
शर्म्मवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Lucky, auspicious.<BR> E. शर्म्मन् and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्म्मर|शर्मर|शर्मरः|शर्म्मरः
शर्म्मर m. (-रः) A sort of garment or cloth.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A species of Curcuma,<BR>(C. zanthorhizon.)<BR> E. शर्म्म pleasure, रा to give, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्य्या|शर्या
शर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) Night.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्व्|शर्व्
शर्व्व् r. 1st cl. (शर्व्वति) To hurt, to injure or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्व|शर्व|शर्वः|शर्व्वः
शर्व्व m. (-र्व्वः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. शर्व्व् to injure, Unādi aff. अच्; also सर्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्वर|शर्वर|शर्वरः|शर्व्वरं
शर्व्वर m. (-रः) KĀMA.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Darkness.<BR> E. शर्व्व्, अरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्वरी|शर्वरी
शर्व्वरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Night.<BR>	 2. A woman.<BR>	 3. Turmeric.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, अरन्<BR>Unādi aff.; or शॄ-वनिप् ङीप् वनो र च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्वरीक|शर्वरीक
शर्व्वरीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A low or vile man, a rogue, a wretch.<BR>	 2. A cruel<BR>or mischievous man.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, ईकन् Unādi aff., रक् augment<BR>and the root repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्वला|शर्वला
शर्व्वला f. (-ला or ली) An iron crow.<BR> E. शर्व् to injure, कलच् aff.; also सर्व्वला ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्व्वाणी|शर्वाणी
शर्व्वाणी f. (-णी) A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. शर्व्व ŚIVA, ङीष् aff., and आनुक्<BR>augment; the wife of SARVA; also सर्व्वाणी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्
शल् r. 1st cl. (शलते)<BR>	 1. To move, to shake, to tremble or stir.<BR>	 2. To<BR>cover. (शलति) To go, to move to or towards. r. 10th cl. (शालयति-ते)<BR>To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल|शलं|शलः
शल mn. (-लः-लं) The quill of a porcupine.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A name of<BR>BHRINGI, ŚIVA'S attendant.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. A kind of field.<BR>	 4. A<BR>dart, a spear.<BR>	 5. A stake.<BR>	 6. A camel.<BR> E. शल् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलक|शलकः
शलक m. (-कः) A spider.<BR> E. शल् to go, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलङ्ग|शलंग|शलंगः|शलङ्गः
शलङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A king.<BR>	 2. A sort of salt.<BR> E. शल् to go, Unādi aff. अङ्गच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलभ|शलभः
शलभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A grass-hopper.<BR>	 2. A locust.<BR> E. शल् to go, अभच् Unādi<BR>aff.: see शरभ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलल|शललं
शलल nf. (-लं-ली) The quill of a porcupine.<BR> E. शल् to go, to project, aff. कलच्, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाका
शलाका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A javelin, a dart.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. A porcupine.<BR>	 4.<BR>The rib of an umbrella, the bar of a cage, &c., or any such small<BR>stake, rod, peg, or pin; it is applied also in common use, to a<BR>thin slip of bamboo, serving when tipped with sulphur for a match;<BR>to a round pointed piece of wood or bamboo serving as a toothpick;<BR>to a similar piece employed as a tent or probe, or to a larger one<BR>used as a ruler, &c.<BR>	 5. A bone.<BR>	 6. An oblong quadrangular piece<BR>of ivory or bone used in playing a particular game, a domino.<BR>	 7.<BR>A fibrous stick used as a brush or pencil.<BR>	 8. A thorny shrub,<BR>(Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>	 9. The Sārikā, (Turdus Gosalica, BUCH.)<BR>10. A shoot, a sprout.<BR> E. शल् to go, Unādi aff. आकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाकापरि
शलाकापरि Ind. Beat at a game played with pieces of stick.<BR> E. शलाका a<BR>match, &c., परि implying in this and similar compounds, reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाकापुरुष
शलाकापुरुष m. plu. (-षाः) Sixty-three persons considered by the Jainas<BR>as sacred and divine, viz.:--the 24 Jinas, 12 Chakravartties, 9<BR>Vāsudevas, 9 Baladevas, and 9 Prati vāsudevas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाट|शलाटः
शलाट m. (-टः) A cart-load, considered as twenty times one hundred<BR>Palas.<BR> E. शृ to injure, aff. आटन् and the र changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाटु|शलाटुः
शलाटु mfn. (-टुः-टुः-टु) Unripe, moist, (as fruit)<BR>	 m. (-टुः) A kind of<BR>root.<BR> E. शल् to go, आटु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलाभोलि|शलाभोलिः
शलाभोलि m. (-लिः) A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलालु|शलालुः
शलालु n. (-लुः) A sort of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शलालुक|शलालुकः
शलालुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Purchased with or procured for the substance<BR>termed Śalālu.<BR> E. शलालु as above, and ष्ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्क|शल्कं
शल्क n. (-ल्कं)<BR>	 1. A part, a portion.<BR>	 2. Bark, rind.<BR>	 3. The scale of a<BR>fish.<BR> E. शल् to go, Unādi aff. कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्कल|शल्कलं
शल्कल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The scale of a fish.<BR>	 2. Bark, rind.<BR> E. शल् to go, कलन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्कलिन्
शल्कलिन् m. (-ली) A fish.<BR> E. शल्कल and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्किन्
शल्किन् m. (-ल्की) A fish.<BR> E. शल्क a scale and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्भ्
शल्भ् r. 1st cl. (शल्भते)<BR>	 1. To praise, to flatter or coax.<BR>	 2. To stalk, to boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्मलि|शल्मलिः
शल्मलि mf. (-लिः-ली) The silk-cotton tree: see शाल्मलि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्य|शल्यं|शल्यः
शल्य mn. (-ल्यः-ल्यं) A dart, a javelin.<BR>	 n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. A bamboo rod or stake.<BR>2. Any stake or thorn.<BR>	 3. An arrow.<BR>	 4. An iron crow.<BR>	 5. Sin,<BR>crime.<BR>	 6. Difficulty, embarrassment, distress.<BR>	 7. An arrow,<BR>a thorn, or other extraneous substance which has lodged in the<BR>body, a dart, (lit.); but (fig.) any tormenting and heart-<BR>rending sorrow.<BR>	 8. Abuse, defamation.<BR>	 9. Poison.<BR>	 10. A bone.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ल्यः)<BR>	 1. A thorny shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>	 2. A porcupine.<BR>3. A hedgehog.<BR>	 4. A peg, a pin, &c.<BR>	 5. A boundary.<BR>	 6. Extrac-<BR>tion of splinters, (in surgery.)<BR>	 7. A king, the maternal uncle of<BR>YUDHISṬHIRA.<BR> E. शल् to go, aff. यत् or य Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यक|शल्यकः
शल्यक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A stake, a thorn.<BR>	 2. A dart, a pike.<BR>	 3. A porcupine.<BR>4. A hedgehog.<BR>	 5. A thorny shrub, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR> E. शल्य as<BR>above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यकण्ठ|शल्यकंठ|शल्यकण्ठः
शल्यकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A porcupine.<BR> E. शल्य a stake, and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यक्रिया
शल्यक्रिया f. (-या) The extraction of extraneous substances lodged in the<BR>body.<BR> E. शल्य, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यवत्|शल्यवन्त्
शल्यवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वन्)<BR>	 1. Shooting arrows.<BR>	 2. Set with stakes.<BR>	 3.<BR>Harassed with difficulties, &c.<BR> E. शल्य and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यवारङ्ग
शल्यवारङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) The part by which an arrow or the like lodged in the<BR>body is to be laid hold of for its extraction.<BR> E. शल्य, and वारङ्ग the<BR>place of seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यशास्त्र
शल्यशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) That part of Surgery which treats of the extraction<BR>of extraneous substances lodged in the body.<BR> E. शल्य, शास्त्र science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यारि|शल्यारिः
शल्यारि m. (-रिः) YUDHISṬHIRA.<BR> E. शल्य the prince, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्योद्धार|शल्योद्धारः
शल्योद्धार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Extraction of foreign substances from the body.<BR>2. Cleansing or purifying a new house.<BR> E. शल्य, उद्धार taking away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्ल्
शल्ल् r. 1st cl. (शल्लति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्ल|शल्लं|शल्लः
शल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A frog.<BR>	 n. (-ल्लं) Bark, rind.<BR> E. शल् to go, लच् aff.; or शल्ल-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्लक|शल्लकं|शल्लकः
शल्लक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) Bark, rind.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-की)<BR>	 1. A porcupine.<BR>	 2. The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thuri-<BR>fera.)<BR> E. शल् to go, aff. क्वुन्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्लकीद्रव|शल्लकीद्रवः
शल्लकीद्रव m. (-वः) Incense, Olibanum.<BR> E. शल्लकी the Boswellia thurifera, द्रव exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्व|शल्वः
शल्व m. (-ल्वः) A country so named in the north of India.<BR> E. शल् to go,<BR>व aff.; more usually शाल्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शव्
शव् r. 1st cl. (शवति)<BR>	 1. To go or approach.<BR>	 2. To change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शव|शवं|शवः
शव mn. (-वः-वं) A dead body, a corpse.<BR>	 n. (-वं) Water.<BR> E. शव् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवकाम्य|शवकाम्यः
शवकाम्य m. (-म्यः) A dog.<BR> E. शव a corpse, and काम्य desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवदाह|शवदाहः
शवदाह m. (-हः) Burning a corpse.<BR> E. शव, दाह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवदाहिन्
शवदाहिन् m. (-ही) A person who burns a corpse.<BR> E. शव, दाहिन् who burns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवयान|शवयानं
शवयान n. (-नं) The litter or bed on which a dead body is carried to be<BR>burnt.<BR> E. शव a corpse, and यान a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवर|शवरः
शवर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A barbarian, one inhabiting the mountainous districts<BR>of India, and wearing the feathers of the peacock, &c. as decora-<BR>tions.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. The hand.<BR>	 5. Name of a<BR>learned writer on Mimānsā Darshan.<BR> E. शव a corpse, रा to take,<BR>affs. क and टाप्: or शव्-अरन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवराल
शवराल m. (-लः) A sort of Lodh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवरालय|शवरालयः
शवरालय m. (-यः) The abode of an outcaste or low tribe.<BR> E. शवर a ber-<BR>barian, आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=710-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवरावास|शवरावासः
शवरावास m. (-सः) The abode of an outcaste or barbarous tribe.<BR> E. शवर<BR>a barbarian, आवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवल|शवलः
शवल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Variegated, of a variegated colour.<BR>	 2. Imita-<BR>tive.<BR>	 3. Articulate.<BR>	 4. Divided into various parts.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A varie-<BR>gated colour.<BR>	 f. (-ला-ली)<BR>	 1. A brindled cow.<BR>	 2. The cow of plenty,<BR>KĀMADHENU.<BR>	 n. (-ल)<BR>	 1. Water 2. A religious observance peculiar<BR>to the Bauddhas.<BR> E. शव् to alter, कलन् aff, and प changed to व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवलता
शवलता f. (-ता) Variegation, variety of colour.<BR> E. शवल and तल् aff.; also<BR>with त्व, शवलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवलीकृत
शवलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Variegated.<BR> E. शवल, कृत made. च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवसाधन
शवसाधन n. (-नं) A mystical and magical ceremony performed with a<BR>dead body.<BR> E. शव, and साधन implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवसान|शवसानः
शवसान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A traveller, (in the dialect of the Vedas.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>road.<BR>	 n. (-नं) A cemetery.<BR> E. शव् to go, with आनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्
शश् r. 1st cl. (शशति) To jump, to leap, to move by springing or leaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश|शशः
शश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A hare or rabbit.<BR>	 2. The Lodh-tree, (Symplocos race-<BR>mosa.)<BR>	 3. Gum myrrh.<BR>	 4. A man of mild and virtuous character,<BR>but uxorious and woman-led, one of the four characters in which<BR>men are classed by erotic writers.<BR>	 5. The spots on the moon, sup-<BR>posed to resemble the figure of a hare.<BR> E. शश् to go by leaps or<BR>jumps, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशक|शशकः
शशक m. (-कः) A hare.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशत्
शशत् mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्) Leaping, jumping.<BR> E. शश् to leap, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशधर|शशधरः
शशधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. शश a hare, and धर<BR>having; either as an emblem on his banners, or fancifully, as<BR>the spots on the moon's face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशप्लुतक|शशप्लुतकं
शशप्लुतक n. (-कं) A mark or scratch of the finger-nail.<BR> E. शश a hare, प्लुतक jumping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशबिन्दु|शशबिंदु|शशबिन्दुः
शशबिन्दु m. (-न्दुः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. A sovereign.<BR>	 3. The<BR>moon.<BR> E. शश a hare, and बिन्दु a spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशभृत्
शशभृत् m. (-भृत्) The moon.<BR> E. शश a hare, भृत् who cherishes: see<BR>शशधर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशमात्र
शशमात्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) As large as or of the size of a hare.<BR> E. शश, मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशलाञ्छन|शशलांछन|शशलाञ्छनः
शशलाञ्छन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. शश, लाञ्छन mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशलोमन्
शशलोमन् n. (-म) The skin of the hare or rabbit.<BR> E. शश a hare or rabbit,<BR>लोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशविषाण
शशविषाण n. (-णं) The horn of a hare; any thing improbable or extra-<BR>ordinary.<BR> E. शश, विषाण a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशस्थली
शशस्थली f. (-ली) The Doab, the country between the Ganges and<BR>Jamunā rivers.<BR> E. शश a hare, स्थल place, site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशाङ्क|शशांक|शशाङ्कः
शशाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. शश a hare, अङ्क a mark or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशाङ्कलेखा|शशांकलेखा
शशाङ्कलेखा f. (-खा) A digit of the moon.<BR> E. शशाङ्क, लेखा streak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशादन|शशादनः
शशादन m. (-नः) A hawk or falcon.<BR> E. शश a hare or rabbit, अदन what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिकान्त|शशिकांत|शशिकान्तं|शशिकान्तः
शशिकान्त m. (-न्तः) The moon-gem.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं) A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिग्रह|शशिग्रहः
शशिग्रह m. (-हः) An eclipse of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिज|शशिजः
शशिज m. (-जः) An epithet of BUDHA or MERCURY.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिदेव|शशिदेवः
शशिदेव m. (-वः) A sovereign, named also रन्तिदेव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिन्
शशिन् m. (-शी)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. The emblem of one of the Jinas.<BR>	 3.<BR>Camphor.<BR> E. शश a hare, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिपाद
शशिपाद m. (-दः) A moon-beam.<BR> E. शशि, and पाद a ray; also similar<BR>compounds, as शशिकर, शशिकिरण, शशिमयूख and शशिरश्मि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिप्रभ|शशिप्रभं
शशिप्रभ n. (-भं) The white esculent water-lily.<BR>	 f. (-भा) Moon-light. E.<BR>शशि the moon, प्रभ shining, (blossoming,) or प्रभा lustre, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिलेखा
शशिलेखा f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A digit of the moon.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Menispermum<BR>glabrum.)<BR>	 3. A metre, a variety of the line of the Atijagatī stanza<BR>of thirteen syllables, or of the Atisaccarī of fifteen syllables. E.<BR>शशि the moon, and लेखा a line or mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिवदना
शशिवदना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A woman with a face like the moon.<BR>	 2. A species of<BR>the Gāyatri metre.<BR> E. शशि, वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिशेखर|शशिशेखरः
शशिशेखर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. One of the Jaina pontiffs.<BR> E. शशि the moon, शेखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशीश|शशीशः
शशीश m. (-शः) A name of ŚIVA.<BR> E. शशि, ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशोर्ण|शशोर्णं|शशोर्ण्ण
शशोर्ण n. (-र्णं) The hair of the hare or rabbit.<BR> E. शश a hare, &c., ऊर्णा<BR>wool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्वत्|शश्वन्त्
शश्वत् Ind.<BR>	 1. Again and again, frequently, repeatedly, perpetually.<BR>	 2.<BR>Together with<BR> E. शश् to go by jumps, वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्
शष् r. 1st cl. (शषति) To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्कुल|शष्कुलः
शष्कुल m. (-लः) A plant, (Galedupa arborea, Rox)<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. The outer<BR>ear or opening of the external auditory passage.<BR>	 2. Rice or barley<BR>water, &c.<BR>	 3. A sort of pie.<BR>	 4. A kind of baked cake.<BR> E. शष्-कुलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्प|शष्पं|शष्पः
शष्प n. (-ष्पं) Young grass.<BR>	 m. (-ष्पः) Loss of intellect or confidence.<BR> E. शस्<BR>to hurt, Unādi aff. प, and स changed to ष; also शस्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्
शस्(इ) and the preposition आङ् usually prefixed आशसि r. 1st cl.<BR>(आशंसते)<BR>	 1. To bless, to wish good to, to confer a benediction.<BR>	 2.<BR>To wish, to desire.<BR>	 3. To speak. (उ) शसु r. 1st cl. (शसति) To hurt,<BR>to injure, to wound or kill. With अभि, To intreat. With वि, To<BR>kill. r. 2nd cl. शस्ति To dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शसन|शसनं
शसन n. (-नं) Immolation, offering an animal in sacrifice.<BR> E. शस् to hurt,<BR>aff. ल्युट्; also शमन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त|शस्तं|शस्तः
शस्त(इ)शस्ति r. 2nd cl. (शंस्ति) To sleep, (peculiar to the Vedas.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त|शस्तं|शस्तः
शस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Happy, well, right.<BR>	 2. Praised, eulogised.<BR>	 3.<BR>Best, excellent.<BR>	 4. Injured.<BR>	 n. (-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Happiness, excellence.<BR>	 2.<BR>The body.<BR>	 3. A finger-protector.<BR> E. शस् to bless, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तक|शस्तकं
शस्तक n. (-कं) A defence for the finger of an archer.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तकेशक|शस्तकेशकः
शस्तकेशक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Having much or beautiful hair.<BR> E. शस्त<BR>excellent, केश hair, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्र|शस्त्रं|शस्त्रः
शस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A weapon in general.<BR>	 2. Iron.<BR>	 3. Steel.<BR>	 4. An instru-<BR>ment.<BR>	 5. A hymn of praise.<BR>	 m. (-स्त्रः) A sword, a scymitar.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-स्त्री) A knife.<BR> E. शस् to hurt, aff. ष्ट्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रक|शस्त्रकं
शस्त्रक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Iron.<BR>	 2. Steel.<BR> E. शस्त्र a weapon, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रकार|शस्त्रकारः
शस्त्रकार m. (-रः) An armourer.<BR> E. शस्त्र, and कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रग्रह|शस्त्रग्रहः
शस्त्रग्रह m. (-हः) Taking arms.<BR> E. शस्त्र and ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रग्राहिन्
शस्त्रग्राहिन् m. (-ही) A man armed.<BR> E. शस्त्र, ग्राहिन् who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रघुष्टकर
शस्त्रघुष्टकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Clanging.<BR> E. शस्त्र, घुष्ट sounded, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रजाल
शस्त्रजाल n. (-लं) A quantity of weapons.<BR> E. शस्त्र, जाल a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रजीविन्
शस्त्रजीविन् m. (-वी) A soldier by profession.<BR> E. शस्त्र a weapon, जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रत्याग
शस्त्रत्याग m. (-गः) Throwing away a weapon.<BR> E. शस्त्र, त्याग abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रदेवता
शस्त्रदेवता f. (-ता) A deified weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रधर|शस्त्रधरः
शस्त्रधर m. (-रः) An armed man or soldier.<BR> E. शस्त्र, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रपाणि|शस्त्रपाणिः
शस्त्रपाणि mfn. (-णिः-णिः-णि) A warrior armed, having weapons in the<BR>hand.<BR> E. शस्त्र, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रपात
शस्त्रपात m. (-तः) The stroke of a weapon.<BR> E. शस्त्र, and पात falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रपूत
शस्त्रपूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Purified by arms, absolved from guilt by dying<BR>in the field of battle.<BR> E. शस्त्र, and पूत purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रप्रहरण
शस्त्रप्रहरण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Taking arms.<BR> E. शस्त्र, प्रहरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रभृत्
शस्त्रभृत् m. (-भृत्) An armed man, a soldier.<BR> E. शस्त्र a weapon, भृत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रमार्ज्ज|शस्त्रमार्ज|शस्त्रमार्जः
शस्त्रमार्ज्ज m. (-र्ज्जः) An armourer.<BR> E. शस्त्र a weapon, and मार्ज्ज cleaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रवृत्ति|शस्त्रवृत्तिः
शस्त्रवृत्ति m. (-त्तिः) A soldier, a man at arms.<BR> E. शस्त्र, and वृत्ति profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रसंहति|शस्त्रसंहतिः
शस्त्रसंहति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A quantity or number of weapons.<BR>	 2. An arsenal,<BR>an armoury.<BR> E. शस्त्र, and संहति assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रसमूह
शस्त्रसमूह n. (-ह)<BR>	 1. A quantity or number of weapons.<BR>	 2. An arsenal,<BR>an armoury.<BR> E. शस्त्र, and समूह a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रहत|शस्त्रहतः
शस्त्रहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Struck or killed by a weapon.<BR> E. शस्त्र, हत hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रहस्त|शस्त्रहस्तः
शस्त्रहस्त m. (-स्तः) A man carrying arms.<BR> E. शस्त्र a weapon, हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्राजीव|शस्त्राजीवः
शस्त्राजीव m. (-वः) A soldier.<BR> E. शस्त्र a weapon, आजीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्राभ्यास|शस्त्राभ्यासः
शस्त्राभ्यास m. (-सः) Military exercise or practice.<BR> E. शस्त्र a weapon, and<BR>अभ्यास practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रायस|शस्त्रायसं
शस्त्रायस n. (-सं) Steel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रास्त्र
शस्त्रास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) Use of weapons.<BR> E. शस्त्र, अस्त्र a weapon, or means of offence or defence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्
शस्त्रास्त्रभृत् m. (-भृत्) A soldier, a warrior.<BR> E. शस्त्रास्त्र, भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्त्व
शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) The military profession, the use of arms. E.<BR>शस्त्रास्त्रभृत्, त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=711-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रिन्
शस्त्रिन् mfn. (-स्त्री-स्त्रिणी-स्त्रि) Armed, having weapons.<BR> E. शस्त्र, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रोत्थापन
शस्त्रोत्थापन n. (-नं) Raising a weapon, (as to strike.)<BR> E. शस्त्र, उत्थापन<BR>taking up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रोद्यम|शस्त्रोद्यमः
शस्त्रोद्यम m. (-मः) Lifting up a weapon, (as to strike.)<BR> E. शस्त्र, and उद्यन lifting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रोपजीविन्
शस्त्रोपजीविन् m. (-वी) A soldier, a man at arms.<BR> E. शस्त्र, उपजीविन् living by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्प|शस्पं|शस्पः
शस्प n. (-स्पं)<BR>	 1. Young grass.<BR>	 2. Loss of confidence or understanding.<BR>E. शस् to injury, प aff., and the sibilant unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्य|शस्यं
शस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Excellent, best.<BR>	 2. To be hurt or injured.<BR>	 3.<BR>Desirable, to be wished.<BR>	 n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Fruit.<BR>	 2. Corn, grain in<BR>general.<BR>	 3. Good quantity, merit.<BR>	 4. Grass.<BR> E. शस् to hurt, aff.<BR>यत्; or शसि to wish, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यक्षेत्र
शस्यक्षेत्र n. (-त्रं) A corn-field.<BR> E. शस्य, and क्षेत्र a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यध्वंसिन्
शस्यध्वंसिन् m. (-सी) A timber tree, commonly Toon, (Cedrela tunna.)<BR>“तुंँद् गाछ ।”<BR> E. शस्य fruit, and ध्वंसिन् injurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यभक्षक
शस्यभक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Graminivorous.<BR> E. शस्य, and भक्षक what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यभक्षण
शस्यभक्षण n. (-णं) Feeding upon grain.<BR> E. शस्य, भक्षण eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यमञ्जरी|शस्यमंजरी
शस्यमञ्जरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. The ear or spike of corn.<BR>	 2. The fruit-stalk. E.<BR>शस्य and सञ्जरी pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यरक्षक
शस्यरक्षक m. (-कं) A watchman over a field of corn.<BR> E. शस्य, रक्षक who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यशूक|शस्यशूकं
शस्यशूक n. (-कं) The beard of corn.<BR> E. शस्य corn, शूक beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यसम्बर|शस्यसंबर|शस्यसम्बरः
शस्यसम्बर m. (-रः) The Sāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR> E. शस्य fruit, सम्बर<BR>surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यारु|शस्यारुः
शस्यारु m. (-रुः) A small variety of the Mimosa suma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांशप|शांशपः
शांशप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Made of Śisu wood, &c.<BR> E. शिंशपा the Śisu, अण्<BR>aff., and आङ् substituted for the first vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक|शाकं|शाकः
शाक mn. (-कः-कं) A pot-herb in general, any leaf, flower, fruit, stalk,<BR>root, &c., used as a vegetable.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. One of the seven Dvīpas<BR>or divisions of the world; the sixth, surrounded by the sea of<BR>milk or white sea.<BR>	 2. Power, strength.<BR>	 3. The Sirisha-tree, (Acacia<BR>sirisa.)<BR>	 4. The Teak-tree, (Tectona grandis.)<BR>	 5. An era, a period<BR>usually commencing with some celebrated prince, as YUDISHṬHIRA<BR>VIKRAMĀDITYA, ŚĀLIVĀHANA, &c., thence denominated SĀKE-<BR>ŚWARAS, &c.; the term in ordinary use is applied especially to the<BR>era of SĀLIVĀHANA, commencing 76 or 78 years after the<BR>Christian era.<BR> E. शक् to be able, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकचुक्रिका
शाकचुक्रिका f. (-का) The tamarind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकट|शाकटं|शाकटः
शाकट mfn. (-टः-टी-टं) Relating to a cart, (a cart-load, a cart-horse, &c.)<BR>m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A draught-ox.<BR>	 2. The Sleshmāntaka-tree.<BR> E. शकट a<BR>cart, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटायन|शाकटायनः
शाकटायन m. (-नः) Name of a philologist and grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटिक|शाकटिकः
शाकटिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Going in or on a cart.<BR> E. शकट a cart, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटीन|शाकटीनः
शाकटीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Belonging or relating to a cart.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A cart-<BR>load as a measure of weight or value.<BR> E. शकट a cart, खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकतरु|शाकतरुः
शाकतरु m. (-रुः) A plant, (Capparis trifoliata.) “सेगुण ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकपण|शाकपणः
शाकपण m. (-णः) A handful or similar quantity, as a measure of<BR>potherbs.<BR> E. शाक, and पण price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकबालेय
शाकबालेय m. (-यः) A plant, commonly Bāmanhāti; also बालेयशाक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकबिल्व
शाकबिल्व m. (-ल्वः) The egg-plant, (Solanum melongena.)<BR> E. शाक a<BR>potherb, बिल्व the Bel fruit; also with कन् added शाकबिल्वक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकम्भरी|शाकंभरी
शाकम्भरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A city, supposed to be the modern<BR>Sāmbher.<BR> E. शक a potherb, भृ to nourish, aff. खच्, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकम्भरीय|शाकंभरीय|शाकम्भरीयं
शाकम्भरीय n. (-यं) A fossile-salt brought from a lake in the vicinity of<BR>Sāmbher, a town in Ajmere.<BR> E. शाकम्भरी the city, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकरी
शाकरी f. (-री) One of the dialects of dramatic Prakrit, that spoken by<BR>the Sakāra.<BR> E. शकार, अण् and ङीष् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलिक|शाकलिकः
शाकलिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Having a piece or part.<BR> E. शकल a part, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकल्य|शाकल्यः
शाकल्य m. (-ल्यः) Name of an ancient grammarian who preceded PĀṆINI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकवीर|शाकवीरः
शाकवीर m. (-रः) A potherb, (Chenopodium album.)<BR> E. शक a potherb,<BR>and वीर eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकवृक्ष|शाकवृक्षः
शाकवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The Teak-tree.<BR> E. शाक the same, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकशाकट|शाकशाकटं
शाकशाकट n. (-टं) A field of vegetables, a kitchen garden.<BR> E. शाक a<BR>potherb, and शाकटच् aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकशाकिन|शाकशाकिनं
शाकशाकिन n. (-नं) A field cultivated for esculent plants, a field of vege-<BR>tables, a kitchen-garden.<BR> E. शाक a vegetable, and शाकिन aff. in<BR>this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकश्रेष्ठ|शाकश्रेष्ठः
शाकश्रेष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A potherb, (Chenopodium album.<BR> E. शाक a potherb, and श्रेष्ठ best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकाख्य|शाकाख्यं|शाकाख्यः
शाकाख्य m. (-ख्यः) The Teak-tree.<BR>	 n. (-ख्यं) A vegetable.<BR> E. शाक the<BR>same, आख्या appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकाङ्ग|शाकांग|शाकाङ्गं
शाकाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Pepper.<BR> E. शाक a potherb, and अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकिनी
शाकिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A female divinity of an inferior character, attendant<BR>especially on ŚIVA and DURGĀ.<BR>	 2. A field of vegetables.<BR> E. शाक,<BR>इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुण|शाकुणः
शाकुण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Repentant, regretting.<BR> E. शक-वा० उणन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन|शाकुनः
शाकुन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Of or relating to birds.<BR>	 2. Ominous, portentous.<BR>E. शकुन, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुनिक|शाकुनिकः
शाकुनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of or relating to birds, omens, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>A fowler, a bird-catcher.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Interpretation of omens, dreams,<BR>&c.<BR> E. शकुन a bird, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुनेय|शाकुनेयः
शाकुनेय m. (-यः) A small owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन्तलेय|शाकुंतलेयः|शाकुन्तलेयः
शाकुन्तलेय m. (-यः) BHARATA, the sovereign of India.<BR> E. शकुन्तला the<BR>nymph, and ढक् aff; being the son of ŚAKUNTALĀ and DUSHYANTA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुलिक|शाकुलिकः
शाकुलिक m. (-कः) A fisherman.<BR> E. शकुल a fish, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्कर|शाक्करः
शाक्कर m. (-रः) An ox.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A form of metre.<BR> E. शक्कर, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्त|शाक्तः
शाक्त m. (-क्तः) A worshipper of the female principle.<BR> E. शक्ति the divine<BR>energy in its feminine personification, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्तीक|शाक्तीकः
शाक्तीक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Speared, spearing, relating to or done with a<BR>spear.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A spearman, a lancer.<BR> E. शक्ति a spear, aff. ईकक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्त्य|शाक्त्यः
शाक्त्य m. (-क्त्यः) A worshipper of the female principle or Śakti.<BR> E. शक्ति<BR>the personified energy of a divinity, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्य|शाक्यः
शाक्य m. (-क्यः)<BR>	 1. BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha religion.<BR>	 2.<BR>The name of a tribe.<BR> E. शक् to be able, and ण्यत्, घञ् or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यमुनि|शाक्यमुनिः
शाक्यमुनि m. (-निः) A name of BUDDHA, the real or supposed founder<BR>of the Bauddha religion.<BR> E. शक्य said to be the name of a family<BR>or tribe, originating with one of the race of Ikswāku, condemned<BR>to take up his abode in a forest of Sāka trees, and मुनि a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यसिंह|शाक्यसिंहः
शाक्यसिंह m. (-हः) A name of BUDDHA.<BR> E. शाक्य the name of his tribe,<BR>and सिंह chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्री
शाक्री f. (-क्री) An epithet of ŚACHĪ, the wife of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्वर|शाक्वरः
शाक्वर m. (-रः) An ox.<BR> E. शक्-ष्वरप् स्वार्थे अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख|शाखः
शाख(ऋ)शाखृ r. 1st cl. (शाखति) To pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख|शाखः
शाख m. (-खः) A plant, (Galedupa arborea.)<BR>	 f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A branch, the<BR>branch of a tree.<BR>	 2. A branch or sub-division of the Vedas, consis-<BR>ting of the several Sanhitās or collections of prayers in each Veda,<BR>as received in different schools, modified more or less either in the<BR>arrangement of the whole text, or in particular portions of it.<BR>	 3.<BR>An arm.<BR>	 4. A sect, a faction, a party.<BR>	 5. Any sub-division.<BR>	 6. Any<BR>part of an animal not endowed with sensibility, as a horn, &c. E.<BR>शाख् to pervade, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाचन्द्रन्याय|शाखाचंद्रन्याय|शाखाचन्द्रन्यायः
शाखाचन्द्रन्याय m. (-यः) The maxim of the moon and a bough; it is<BR>adduced in illustration when an object has its position assigned to<BR>it from the appearance of contiguity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखानगर|शाखानगरं
शाखानगर n. (-रं) A suburb.<BR> E. शाखा a branch or sub-division, नगर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखापित्त|शाखापित्तः
शाखापित्त m. (-त्तः) Inflammation of the extremities of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखापुर|शाखापुरं
शाखापुर n. (-रं) A suburb.<BR> E. शाखा a branch, पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाभेद|शाखाभेदः
शाखाभेद m. (-दः) Difference of school or doctrine.<BR> E. शाखा, भेद difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखामृग|शाखामृगः
शाखामृग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A monkey, an ape.<BR>	 2. A squirrel.<BR> E. शाखा the<BR>branch of a tree, मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखारण्ड|शाखारंड|शाखारण्डः
शाखारण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A Brāhman who has changed his Śākhā or pecu-<BR>liar school of the Vedas for another.<BR> E. शाखा a branch of the<BR>Vedas, रम् to sport, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=712-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखारथ्या
शाखारथ्या f. (-थ्या) A branch-road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाल|शाखालः
शाखाल m. (-लः) A sort of cane: see वानीर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाशिफा
शाखाशिफा f. (-फा) A root proceeding from a branch, as in the Indian fig,<BR>the branches of which shoot downwards to the ground and take<BR>fresh root there.<BR> E. शाखा a branch, and शिफा a fibrous root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखिन्
शाखिन् mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि) Branched, branching, having branches.<BR>(literally or figuratively.)<BR>	 m. (-खी)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. Veda.<BR>	 3. A follower<BR>of any vedic school.<BR>	 4. An inhabitant of the northern districts<BR>bordering on India, a Turk or Tartar.<BR>	 5. The name of a king. E.<BR>शाखा a branch, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखोट|शाखोटः
शाखोट m. (-टः) A small tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR> E. शाख्, ओटन् aff.; also<BR>with कन् added शाखोटक m. (-कः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख्य|शाख्यः
शाख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्या-ख्यं) Branching, ramifying.<BR> E. शाखा a branch,<BR>(literally or figuratively,) and य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्कर|शांकर|शाङ्करं|शांकरः|शाङ्करः
शाङ्कर m. (-रः) A bull.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A form of metre.<BR> E. शङ्कर ŚIVA, and अण् aff.; also read शाक्कर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्करि|शांकरि|शांकरिः|शाङ्करिः
शाङ्करि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. GAṆEŚA.<BR>	 3. Fire.<BR>	 4. A Muni. E.<BR>शङ्कर ŚIVA, and इञ patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्कुची
शाङ्कुची f. (-ची) The scate fish; also शंकुची, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्क
शाङ्क n. (-ङ्कं) The sound of the conch-shell.<BR> E. शङ्कं the shell, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्किक
शाङ्किक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Made from, relating to, &c. the Śankha or<BR>conch.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A shell-cutter, a worker in shells.<BR>	 2. A player<BR>on the Śankha, a shell-blower.<BR> E. शङ्क the conch-shell, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्गुष्ठा
शाङ्गुष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा) A shrub, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाट|शाटः
शाट m. (-टः) A garment in general.<BR> E. शट्-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटक|शाटकं|शाटकः
शाटक mn. (-कः-कं) A petticoat.<BR> E. शट् to go, (round the limbs,) ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटी
शाटी mf. (-टः-टी) A petticoat.<BR> E. शट् to praise or flatter, to go, &c.<BR>aff. ण, fem. aff ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाठ्य|शाठ्यं
शाठ्य n. (-ठ्यं) Wickedness, villainy.<BR> E. शठ् wicked, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाड्
शाड्(ऋ)शाडृ r. 1st cl. (शाडते)<BR>	 1. To flatter, to praise, to coax.<BR>	 2. To<BR>boast.<BR>	 3. To float or swim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाड्वल|शाड्वलः
शाड्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Abounding in fresh grass, green, verdant. E.<BR>शाद young grass, ड्वलच् aff., and the final changed, also शाद्वल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण|शाणं|शाणः
शाण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Made of or from Bengal flax or Śaṇ.<BR>	 mf. (-णः-णी)<BR>1. A touchstone.<BR>	 2. A whet or grindstone.<BR>	 3. A weight of four<BR>Māshas.<BR>	 4. A saw.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Coarse cloth, sack-cloth, canvas.<BR>	 2.<BR>A hempen garment.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Ragged or torn raiment.<BR>	 2. A new<BR>unseamed and single-breadth of cloth, given to the religious<BR>student at his investiture for his upper garment.<BR>	 3. A ragged<BR>garment given to the Jaina ascetic at his initiation.<BR>	 4. A small<BR>tent or screen, used especially as a retiring room for actors and<BR>tumblers, &c.<BR>	 5. Gesture, gesticulation, making sings with the<BR>hands or eyes, &c.<BR>	 6. A saw.<BR>	 7. A touchstone.<BR>	 8. A whetstone.<BR>E. शण् to give, aff. घञ्; or शो to sharpen, and ण aff.; or शण<BR>Śaṇ, and अण् aff. of derivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणाजीव|शाणाजीवः
शाणाजीव m. (-वः) An armourer.<BR> E. शाण a whetstone, आजीव who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणि|शाणिः
शाणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A plant from the fibres of which a coarse cloth is<BR>prepared, (Corchorus olitorius.)<BR>	 2. A touchstone.<BR> E. शण Bengal<BR>Śaṇ, and इण् or ईञ् aff. implying descent or resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणित|शाणितः
शाणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Whetted, sharpened.<BR> E. शण् to give, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिल्य|शांडिल्य|शांडिल्यः|शाण्डिल्यः
शाण्डिल्य m. (-ल्यः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>	 2. A Muni from whom<BR>one of the three principal families of the Kanouj or Kānyacubja<BR>Brāhmans is said to be descended.<BR>	 3. A form of AGNI or fire. E.<BR>शण्डिल a saint, यञ् aff. of descent, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात|शातं|शातः
शात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Happy, well, prosperous.<BR>	 2. Feeble, thin.<BR>	 3.<BR>Sharpened, whetted, sharp.<BR>	 4. Handsome, bright.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Joy,<BR>pleasure, happiness.<BR> E. शो to reduce or diminish, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकुम्भ|शातकुंभ|शातकुंभं|शातकुम्भं|शातकुम्भः
शातकुम्भ n. (-म्भं) Gold.<BR>	 m. (-म्भः) A plant, (Nerium odorum.)<BR> E. शतकुम्भ<BR>said to be the name of a mountain, अण् aff. implying production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकौम्भ|शातकौंभ|शातकौंभं|शातकौम्भं
शातकौम्भ n. (-म्भं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. The Dhuturā plant.<BR> E. अण् pleonasm, added<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातन|शातनं
शातन n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Withering, decaying, becoming thin or small.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sharpening.<BR> E. शो to wither, णिच् तङ् च, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातपत्रकी
शातपत्रकी f. (-की) Moonlight.<BR> E. शतपत्र a lotus, कन् added, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातमन्यव
शातमन्यव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Relating to INDRA.<BR> E. शतमन्यु, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातमान|शातमानं
शातमान mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Bought with the measure of one hundred.<BR> E. शत<BR>a hundred, मान measure, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातशिख
शातशिख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Sharp-pointed, (as the nails, &c.)<BR> E. शात, and शिखा crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातोदरी
शातोदरी f. (-री) A woman with a small belly or waist.<BR> E. शात, and<BR>उदर the belly, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रव|शात्रवं|शात्रवः
शात्रव m. (-वः) An enemy.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Enmity, hostility.<BR>	 2. A multitude<BR>of enemies.<BR>	 f. (-वी) Hostile.<BR> E. शत्रु an enemy, and अण् pleonasm, or<BR>aff. of quality or number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रवीय
शात्रवीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Hostile, inimical, belonging or relating to an enemy.<BR> E. शात्रव, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद|शादः
शाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Mud.<BR>	 2. Young grass.<BR> E. शद्-घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शादहरित|शादहरितः
शादहरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Green or fresh with young grass.<BR> E. शाद<BR>young grass, हरित green.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद्वल|शाद्वलः
शाद्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Abounding in fresh or green grass.<BR> E. शाद young grass, ड्वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्
शान् r. 1st cl. desiderative form (शीशांसति-ते) To whet, to sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान|शानः
शान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A touchstone.<BR>	 2. A grindstone.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A sort of<BR>cucumber.<BR> E. शो to make small or sharpen, aff. ल्युट्; also शाण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानपाद|शानपादः
शानपाद m. (-दः) A stone for grinding sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त|शांत|शान्तं|शान्तः
शान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Calm, tranquil, pacified.<BR>	 2. Allayed, alleviated.<BR>3. Meek, humble.<BR>	 4. Purified, cleansed, freed from, (as soil.)<BR>	 5.<BR>Stilled, hushed, (as wind, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. An ascetic, one whose<BR>passions are subdued and who is engrossed by meditating on the<BR>deity.<BR>	 2. One of the Rasas or conditions of feeling, delineated in<BR>poetry or the drama, tranquillity or tranquil devotion, quietism,<BR>the assiduous exercise of meditation, &c. and indifference to all<BR>objects of pleasure or pain.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं) Appeasing, pacifying. Ind.<BR>(शान्तम्) A prohibitive particle or interjection, implying negation,<BR>aversion, disgust, (fie! for shame! Heaven forbid!)<BR> E. शम् to be<BR>appeased, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तचेतस्|शांतचेतस्
शान्तचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः) Composed, calm, unanxious.<BR> E. शान्त, and चेतस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तता
शान्तता f. (-ता) Quietness, calmness, meekness.<BR> E. शान्त, तल् aff.; also<BR>with त्व, शान्तत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तनव|शांतनव|शांतनवः|शान्तनवः
शान्तनव m. (-वः) BHĪṢMA, the reputed great uncle of the Pāndavas. E.<BR>शान्तनु a prince, and अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तनु|शांतनु|शान्तनुः
शान्तनु m. (-नुः) The 21st sovereign of the lunar dynasty in the third<BR>age, the father of BHĪṢMA by Gangā, or the Ganges personified.<BR>E. शं good fortune, (personified,) तनु the body, and the first vowel<BR>made long by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तमल
शान्तमल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Exempt from soil, literally or figuratively.<BR> E. शान्त cleansed, and मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तरय
शान्तरय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Slackened in speed.<BR> E. शान्त, रय rapidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तरस|शांतरस|शान्तरसः
शान्तरस m. (-सः) The sentiment of quietism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तविवाद
शान्तविवाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Reconciled, appeased.<BR> E. शान्त, and विवाद dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तात्मन्
शान्तात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Calm, composed, of resigned or composed<BR>spirit.<BR> E. शान्त, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तार्च्चिस्|शान्तार्चिस्
शान्तार्च्चिस् mfn. (-र्च्चिः-र्च्चिः-र्च्चि) Extinguished, put or gone out.<BR> E. शान्त, अर्च्चिस् flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्ति|शांति|शांतिः|शान्तिः
शान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. Quiet, tranquillity, stoicism, the absence of passion,<BR>and indifference to objects of pleasure or pain; it is especially<BR>applied to the tranquillity of devotion, or quietism, by which the<BR>mind is wholly fixed on the subject of its meditation or worship,<BR>and is utterly disregardless of external impressions.<BR>	 2. Good-<BR>fortune, auspiciousness, felicity.<BR>	 3. Rest, repose.<BR>	 4. Expiatory or<BR>propitiatory rites to avert any evil.<BR>	 5. Preliminary ceremonies to<BR>avert inauspicious accidents at any religious celebration.<BR>	 6.<BR>Remission, alleviation.<BR>	 m. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. The sixteenth Jina or Jaina<BR>deified sage of the present, era.<BR>	 2. One of the Jaina emperors of<BR>the universe.<BR> E. शम् to be appeased, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिक|शांतिक
शान्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Propitiatory, expiatory.<BR>	 2. Producing ease<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">Page714-a+ 60</a>]<BR>or quiet, &c.<BR>	 3. Relating to quiet, &c.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Ceremonies for the<BR>removal of calamities.<BR> E. शान्ति, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=713-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिकर
शान्तिकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Tranquillising, calming, appeasing, &c.<BR> E. शान्ति<BR>and कर who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिकर्त्तृ|शान्तिकर्तृ
शान्तिकर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ) Conferring tranquillity, calming, appeasing.<BR>m. (-र्त्ता) Any divinity who averts evil.<BR> E. शान्ति, कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिकाम|शान्तिकामः
शान्तिकाम m. (-मः) Desire of tranquillity and exemption from calamity.<BR>E. शान्ति peace, and काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिगृह|शांतिगृह|शान्तिगृहं
शान्तिगृह n. (-ह) A private apartment near the place of sacrifice.<BR> E. शान्ति<BR>devotion, गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिद
शान्तिद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Tranquillising, calming, allaying.<BR> E. शान्ति, द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिहोम|शांतिहोम|शान्तिहोमः
शान्तिहोम m. (-मः) Burnt offerings, to prevent threatening or possible<BR>evils.<BR> E. शान्ति, and हाम burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्युद|शांत्युद
शान्त्युद n. (-दं) Water offered at sacrifices for propitiation.<BR> E. शान्ति,<BR>and उद water; also शान्त्युदकं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्युदकुम्भ
शान्त्युदकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A vessel holding lustral water.<BR> E. शान्त्युद, and कुम्भ a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्व|शान्त्वं
शान्त्व r. 10th cl. (शान्त्वयति) To console, to comfort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्व|शान्त्वं
शान्त्व n. (-न्त्वं)<BR>	 1. Conciliation.<BR>	 2. Comforting, consoling.<BR> E. शम् to<BR>appease or allay, (opposition,) deriv. irr.; or शान्त्व to console, aff.<BR>अच्; also सान्त्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्वति|शान्त्वतिः
शान्त्वति f. (-तिः) A plant, (Siphonanthus indica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाप|शापः
शाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Oath, affirmation by oath or ordeal.<BR>	 2. Curse, impreca-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Abuse.<BR> E. शप् to swear, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापग्रस्त
शापग्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Having incurred or suffering under a curse.<BR>E. शाप, ग्रस्त seized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापज
शापज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Arising from a curse, being the effect of one.<BR> E. शाप, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापठिक|शापठिकः
शापठिक m. (-कः) A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापमुक्त
शापमुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Freed from a curse.<BR> E. शाप, and मुक्त released.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापान्त|शापांत|शापान्तः
शापान्त n. (-न्तं) The end of a curse or period of an imprecation.<BR> E. शाप,<BR>and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापास्त्र|शापास्त्रः
शापास्त्र m. (-स्त्रः) A Muni, a saint.<BR> E. शाप a curse, and अस्त्र a weapon; a<BR>curse denounced by such a personage, being formidable even to<BR>the deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापित
शापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sworn, made to take an oath.<BR> E. शप् to swear, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापोद्धार|शापोद्धारः
शापोद्धार m. (-रः) Deliverance from a curse or its effects.<BR> E. शाप, and<BR>उद्धार extricating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाफरिक|शाफरिकः
शाफरिक m. (-कः) A fisherman.<BR> E. शफर a kind of fish, put for any, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्द|शाब्दः
शाब्द mfn. (-ब्दः-ब्दी-ब्दं)<BR>	 1. Sonorous, sounding.<BR>	 2. Nominal, (as inflec-<BR>tion.)<BR>	 f. (-ब्दी)<BR>	 1. SARASWATĪ, goddess of speech and eloquence.<BR>	 2.<BR>Relating to or derived from a word.<BR>	 3. Relating to sound, (as<BR>opposed to आर्थ.)<BR> E. शब्द sound or a word, and अण् attributive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दिक|शाब्दिकः
शाब्दिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to sounds or words.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A profi-<BR>cient in the senses and forms of nouns or words.<BR> E. शब्द a sound,<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामन्
शामन् n. (-मं) Conciliation, appeasing, reconciling.<BR> E. शम् to appease,<BR>aff. मनिन्, and the vowel made long; also शामन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामन|शामनं|शामनः
शामन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Tranquillity, peace.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An<BR>epithet of YAMA.<BR> E. शम् to be pacified, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामित्र|शामित्रं
शामित्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Sacrificing.<BR>	 2. Tying up cattle for sacrifice.<BR>	 3. A<BR>sacrificial vessel.<BR> E. शम् to appease, इत्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामीन|शामीनं
शामीन n. (-नं) Ashes f. (-नी) A Sacrificial spoon.<BR> E. शम् ईनञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बरी|शांबरी
शाम्बरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A female-juggler.<BR>	 2. Jugglery, sorcery.<BR> E. शम्बर a<BR>demon, अण् added, and ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बविक|शांबविक|शांबविकः|शाम्बविकः
शाम्बविक m. (-कः) A worker in shells.<BR> E. शम्बु a shell, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बुक|शांबुक|शांबुकः|शाम्बुकः
शाम्बुक m. (-कः) A bivalve-shell.<BR> E. अण् pleonasm added to शम्बु; also<BR>read शाम्बूक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भव|शांभव|शाम्भवं|शाम्भवः
शाम्भव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A sort of poison.<BR>	 2. A worshipper of ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. The<BR>son of ŚAMBHU or ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. Camphor.<BR>	 n. (-वं) The Devadāru tree.<BR>f. (-वी) PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. शम्भु a name of ŚIVA, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायक|शायकः
शायक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. A sword.<BR> E. शी to destroy, ण्वुल् aff.; also सायक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायिका
शायिका f. (-का) Sleeping.<BR> E. शी to sleep, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायिन्
शायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Lying down.<BR> E. शी to sleep, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार|शारं|शारः
शार r. 10th cl. (शारयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be weak.<BR>	 2. To weaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार|शारं|शारः
शार mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Variegated, (in colour.)<BR>	 2. Yellow.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A piece or man at chess, backgammon, &c.<BR>	 3. Hur-<BR>ting, injuring.<BR>	 4. A mixture of blue and yellow, a green.<BR>	 5.<BR>Spotting, variegating.<BR>	 f. (-री) Kuśa grass.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारङ्ग|शारंग|शारंगः|शारङ्गः
शारङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Of a variegated colour.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The Chātaka,<BR>(Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>	 2. A deer.<BR>	 3. An elephant.<BR>	 4. A bee.<BR>	 5.<BR>A peacock.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी) A musical instrument, a stringed instrument<BR>played with a bow, a sort of fiddle.<BR> E. शार injured or variegated,<BR>गम् to go or get, aff. खच्; more usually, सारङ्ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारता
शारता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Variegated of colour.<BR>	 2. Yellowness.<BR> E. तल added to शार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद|शारदं|शारदः
शारद mfn. (-दः-दी-दं)<BR>	 1. Modest, diffident.<BR>	 2. New.<BR>	 3. Produced in the<BR>sultry season.<BR>	 4. Autumnal.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A year.<BR>	 2. Grain or rice<BR>ripening in the sultry season.<BR>	 3. A sort of kidney-bean, yellow<BR>Mūng.<BR>	 4. Autumnal sickness.<BR>	 5. Sunshine, (in autumn.)<BR>	 f. (-दा)<BR>1. A name of SARASWATĪ.<BR>	 2. A title of DurGĀ.<BR>	 3. A musical<BR>instrument, a sort of lute or guitar.<BR>	 f. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Jussieua,<BR>repens.)<BR>	 2. A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>	 3. Day of full-moon in the<BR>month of Kārtika, (October-November.)<BR>	 n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. The white<BR>lotus.<BR>	 2. Corn, grain.<BR> E. शरद् the autumn, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदिक|शारदिकं|शारदिकः
शारदिक n. (-कं) A particular obsequial ceremony, an annual or<BR>autumnal Śrāddha.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Autumnal sickness.<BR>	 2. Heat or<BR>sunshine in autumn.<BR> E. शारद autumn, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदिन्
शारदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Autumnal.<BR> E. शारद, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदीय
शारदीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Autumnal.<BR> E. शारद, and छण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारि|शारिः
शारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A piece or man at chess, draughts Chauper, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>An elephant's housings or armour.<BR>	 3. Fraud, trick.<BR>	 mf. (-रिः-री) A<BR>bird: see the next.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, Unādi aff. इञ् or ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिका
शारिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A bird, the proper or hill Mainā, (Gracula religiosa;)<BR>it is also applied to the small bird usually called Mainā in Bengal,<BR>(Turdus salica, BUCH.) of which several varieties are distinguished<BR>by the Hindus.<BR>	 2. A bow or stick that may be used for playing<BR>the Vīṇa or any stringed instrument.<BR>	 3. A man at chess.<BR> E. शॄ<BR>to injure, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारित
शारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Variegated, coloured.<BR> E. शार, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिफल|शारिफलं
शारिफल n. (-लं) A chequered cloth or table for playing draughts, &c. E.<BR>शारि a piece, फल fruit; also with कन् added शारिफलक mn. (-कः-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिवा
शारिवा f. (-वा) A plant: as synonimous with Śhyāmā, (Echites frutes-<BR>cens,) but more usually considered synonimous with Ananta-mūla<BR>(Asclepias pseudosarsa,) the broad-leaved variety, the root of<BR>which has been used as a substitute for Sarsaparilla, &c.<BR> E. शारि<BR>injuring, from शॄ with इञ् aff., and वन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिशृङ्खला
शारिशृङ्खला f. (-ला) A sort of die or dice, used for playing with.<BR> E. शारि<BR>a man or piece, and शृङ्खला a chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीर|शारीरं|शारीरः
शारीर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Corporeal, bodily, belonging to or produced<BR>from the body.<BR>	 2. Spiritual in connection with the body, incorpo-<BR>rate.<BR>	 3. A bull.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The soul or spirit whilst incorporate.<BR>	 2.<BR>A drug.<BR>	 3. Excrement, excretion.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Personal chastisement,<BR>corporeal punishment.<BR> E. शरीर the body, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरक|शारीरकं
शारीरक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Corporeal, relating to what is corporeal.<BR>2. Incorporate.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरिक|शारीरिकः
शारीरिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to the body, corporeal.<BR>	 2. Contained<BR>in the body, incorporate.<BR> E. शरीर, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारुक|शारुकः
शारुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Mischievous, noxious, injurious.<BR> E. शॄ to hurt, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्क|शार्कः
शार्क m. (-र्कः) Clayed or candied sugar.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कक|शार्ककः
शार्कक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The broth of milk, syllabub, cream.<BR>	 2. A ball of<BR>meat, &c.<BR>	 3. Clayed or candied sugar.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कर|शार्करः
शार्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Stony, gravelly.<BR>	 2. Sugary.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">Page715-a+ 60</a>]<BR>froth or skim of milk.<BR>	 2. Cream.<BR>	 3. A gravelly place.<BR> E. शर्करा<BR>sugar, gravel, &c., aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=714-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्करक|शार्करकः
शार्करक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Gravelly, stony, &c.<BR> E. शार्कर the same, and<BR>कक् added; also from शर्कर with ठक् aff. शार्करिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्करीय|शार्करीयः
शार्करीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Stony, gravelly, &c.<BR> E. शर्करा gravel, &c., and<BR>छ attributive aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्ग|शार्ंग|शार्ङ्गं|शार्ङ्गः
शार्ङ्ग mfn. (-र्ङ्गः-र्ङ्गी-र्ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Horny, made of horn, &c.<BR>	 2. Holding a<BR>bow.<BR>	 n. (-र्ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. A bow in general.<BR>	 2. The bow of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. शृङ्ग<BR>a horn, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ङ्गिन्|शार्ंगिन्
शार्ङ्गिन् m. (-र्ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A bowyer, an archer.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR> E. शार्ङ्ग a bow, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूल|शार्दूलः|शार्द्दूलः
शार्दूल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A tiger.<BR>	 2. Another animal.<BR>	 3. A Rākshasa.<BR>	 4. A sort<BR>of bird.<BR>	 5. (In composition,) Pre-eminent, excellent.<BR>	 6. A form<BR>of metre, a variety of the class Dhritī, or stanza of four lines of<BR>18 syllables each; also of the class Atidhritī, in which there are<BR>19 syllables in the line.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, दूलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूलललित|शार्द्दूलललितं
शार्दूलललित m. (-तः) A species of the Dhritī metre, of 4 lines of 18<BR>syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूलवाहन|शार्द्दूलवाहनः
शार्दूलवाहन m. (-नः) A Jaina teacher.<BR> E. शार्दूल a tiger, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूलविक्रीडित|शार्द्दूलविक्रीडितं
शार्दूलविक्रीडित m. (-तः) A form of metre, a variety of the class<BR>Atidhritī, or stanza of 4 lines of 19 syllables each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्वर|शार्व्वरं
शार्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Murderous, mischievous.<BR>	 2. Nocturnal.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रं) Darkness, gloom.<BR>	 f. (-री) Night.<BR> E. शर्वरी night, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्
शाल्(ऋ)शाऌ r. 1st cl. (शालते)<BR>	 1. To flatter, to praise.<BR>	 2. To boast.<BR>	 3.<BR>To tell.<BR>	 4. To be endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल|शालः
शाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A kind of fish, (Ophiocephalus wrahl, HAM.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>celebrated sovereign SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>	 3. The name of a river.<BR>	 4.<BR>The name of a tree.<BR>	 5. A tree in general.<BR>	 6. An enclosure, a<BR>fence.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. A hall.<BR>	 3. A large branch of a tree.<BR>E. शल् to go, घञ् aff.; or शाल् to praise, aff. अच्; in several of<BR>the meanings it is also written साल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालग्राम|शालग्रामः
शालग्राम m. (-मः) A particular sacred stone typical of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालङ्कायन|शालङ्कायनः
शालङ्कायन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The name of a saint.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA'S attendant NANDĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालङ्कायनजीवसू
शालङ्कायनजीवसू f. (-सूः) The mother of VYĀSA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शा
शा(सा)लज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A kind of fish, the Śāl or Sol, (Ophiocephalus<BR>wrahl HAM.)<BR>	 2. Exudation of the Śāla-tree. “धुना ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालनिर्य्यास|शालनिर्यास|शालनिर्यासः
शालनिर्य्यास m. (-सः) Resin, the resinous exudation of the Śāl or Sho-<BR>rea robusta.<BR> E. शाल the Śāl tree, and निर्य्यास exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालपर्णी
शालपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR> E. शाल the Śāl,<BR>and पर्ण a leaf, aff. ङीष्, having similar leaves; also सालपर्णी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालभञ्जिका|शालभंजिका
शालभञ्जिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A doll, a puppet.<BR>	 2. A whore, a harlot.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालभञ्जी|शालभंजी
शालभञ्जी f. (-ञ्जी) A doll, a puppet.<BR> E. शाल Śāl wood, भञ्ज् to rub, (to<BR>plane, &c., in order to make dolls,) affs. अच् and ङीष्; also with<BR>कन् added शालभञ्जिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालव|शालवः
शालव m. (-वः) The Lodh tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालवेष्ट|शालवेष्टः
शालवेष्ट m. (-ष्टः) Resin, the resin of the Śāl tree, used as incense, &c.<BR>E. शाल the Śāl tree, and वेष्ट exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालसार|शालसारः
शालसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. Asafœtida; also सालसार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाकिन्
शालाकिन् m. (-की)<BR>	 1. A surgeon.<BR>	 2. A barber.<BR>	 3. A spearman, &c. E.<BR>शलाका a probe, a dart, &c., अण् aff. of reference, and इनि poss. aff.<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाङ्की
शालाङ्की m. (-ङ्की) A doll, a puppet.<BR> E. शाला a hall, अकि to go, affs. अच् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाजिर|शालाजिरः
शालाजिर mn. (-रः-रं) A hollow earthen cup or saucer.<BR> E. शाला a house,<BR>जॄ to become old, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाञ्चि|शालाञ्चिः
शालाञ्चि f. (-ञ्चिः) A creeping plant, the leaves of which are used as a<BR>vegetable, (Achyranthes triandra.)<BR> E. शाला a house, अञ्च् to go, aff.<BR>इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालानी
शालानी f. (-नी) A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR> E. शाल the ŚĀL<BR>tree, आङ् before नी to get, (to resemble in the leaf,) aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालामृग|शालामृगः
शालामृग m. (-गः) A jackal.<BR> E. शाला a house, and मृग a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालार|शालारं
शालार n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A ladder, a flight of stairs or steps.<BR>	 2. A bird-cage.<BR>	 3.<BR>The claw of an elephant.<BR> E. शाला a house, ऋ to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालावृक|शालावृकः
शालावृक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A monkey.<BR>	 2. A dog.<BR>	 3. A jackal.<BR>	 4. A deer.<BR>	 5. A<BR>cat.<BR>	 6. A wolf.<BR> E. शाला a house, वृक a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालि|शालिः
शालि n. (-लि)<BR>	 1. Rice in general, but especially in two classes; one<BR>like white rice growing in deep water, and the other a red sort,<BR>requiring only a moist soil; there are a great many varieties of<BR>this grain.<BR>	 3. The civet or pole cat.<BR> E. शाड् to float or swim, aff.<BR>इन्, and ड changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिक|शालिकः
शालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to a hall, to the ŚĀL tree,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A weaver.<BR>	 2. A village of artificers.<BR>	 3. A toll, a tax.<BR>f. (-का) A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR> E. शाल the ŚĀL tree,<BR>कन् fem. form, aff. of comparison; or शाला a hall, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिञ्च|शालिञ्चः
शालिञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) A creeper, the leaf of which is used as a vegetable,<BR>(Achyranthes triandra, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिता
शालिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Possessing, having.<BR>	 2. Confidence in, relying upon. E.<BR>शालिन् and तल् aff.; with त्व, शालित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिन्
शालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>	 1. Belonging to a house, domestic, &c.<BR>2. A mistress of the house.<BR>	 3. Name of a metre.<BR>	 4. Possessing,<BR>having.<BR>	 5. Shining or resplendent with, (in the latter two senses<BR>when at the end of a compound.)<BR> E. शाल a house, and इनि<BR>aff.; in the fourth form it is the same as शील; the इ being chang-<BR>ed to आ when used in composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिनीकरण|शालिनीकरणं
शालिनीकरण n. (-णं) Abuse, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिपिष्ट|शालिपिष्टं
शालिपिष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Crystal.<BR> E. शालि rice, and पिष्ट ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिवाहन|शालिवाहनः
शालिवाहन m. (-नः) A sovereign of India, whose capital was Pratish-<BR>thāna in the Dakshin, and institutor of the era now called Śaka,<BR>beginning 76 or 78 years after CHRIST.<BR> E. शालि from शाल the ŚĀL<BR>tree, or a proper name, that of a Yakṣa transformed to a lion,<BR>on which the prince rode when an infant, and वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिहोत्र|शालिहोत्रः
शालिहोत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. Name of a writer on veterinary<BR>science.<BR> E. शालि rice, corn, and होत्र an oblation; also with इनि<BR>added शालिहोत्रिन् m. (-त्री) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीन|शालीनः
शालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Ashamed, bashful.<BR>	 2. Like, resembling.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-नः) An opulent house-holder, one who devotes his attention to<BR>worldly affairs.<BR> E. शाला a house, ख aff, (fit or worthy to enter it.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनत्व|शालीनत्वं
शालीनत्व n. (-त्वं) Modesty.<BR> E. त्व added to the last; also with तल्,<BR>शालीनता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनत्वविवर्ज्जित
शालीनत्वविवर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Immodest.<BR> E. शालीनत्व, विवर्ज्जित devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालु|शालुः
शालु m. (-लुः)<BR>	 1. An astringent substance.<BR>	 2. A sort of perfume, com-<BR>monly called Chor.<BR>	 3. A frog.<BR>	 n. (-लु) The root of the water-lily. E.<BR>शॄ to hurt, उ aff., and र changed to ल; or शाल्-उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुक|शालुकं|शालुकः
शालुक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Nutmeg.<BR>	 2. The root of a lotus: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूक|शालूकं|शालूकः
शालूक n. (-कं) The esculent root of the different kinds of Nymphæa or<BR>water-lily.<BR> E. शल् to go, to shake, Unādi aff. ऊकञ्; also with a<BR>short vowel शालुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूर|शालूरः
शालूर m. (-रः) A frog.<BR> E. शल् to go, ऊरच् aff. and the radical vowel made long; also शालुर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालेय|शालेयं|शालेयः
शालेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Fit for rice, (a field, &c.)<BR>	 m. (-यः) A sort of<BR>fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR> E. शालि rice, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालोत्तरीय|शालोत्तरीयः
शालोत्तरीय m. (-यः) A name of PĀṆINI, the inspired grammarian. E.<BR>शाला a house, the house of his preceptor, उत्तरीय latter, last;<BR>having been expelled for stupidity, and acquiring his subse-<BR>quent science by his worship of ŚIVA; according to others, he is<BR>supposed to be a native of SĀLOTTARA. The word is sometimes<BR>spelt शालातुरीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मल|शाल्मलः
शाल्मल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The silk-cotton tree.<BR>	 2. One of the Dwipas or divi-<BR>sions of the continent.<BR>	 3. The gum of the silk-cotton tree. E. See<BR>the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलि|शाल्मलिः
शाल्मलि mf. (-लिः-ली)<BR>	 1. The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR>2. One of the seven Dwipas, or islands or great divisions of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">Page716-a+ 60</a>]<BR>known continent; denominated from the tree first mentioned, said<BR>to grow there: it is surrounded by the sea of Ghee or clarified<BR>butter.<BR> E. शल् to go, causal form, क्विप् aff., शाल् exuding, emitting,<BR>मल् to hold, aff. इन् and ङीष् optionally added; also with अच् aff.<BR>शाल्मल, and with the first vowel short, शल्मलि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=715-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिन्
शाल्मलिन् m. (-ली) GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-लिनी)<BR>The silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलीवेष्ट|शाल्मलीवेष्टः
शाल्मलीवेष्ट m. (-ष्टः) The gum of the silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. शाल्मली the tree.<BR>and वेष्ट exudation; also with कन् added शाल्मलीवेष्टक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्व|शाल्वः
शाल्व m. Plu. (-ल्वाः) The inhabitants of one of the central divisions of<BR>India.<BR> E. शाल्-व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाव|शावः
शाव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Tawny, (of that colour.)<BR>	 2. Relating to the<BR>purification of defilement from the contact or consanguinity of a<BR>corpse, &c.<BR>	 3. Relating to a dead body.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Tawny, (the<BR>colour.)<BR>	 2. The young of any animal: see the next.<BR> E. शव a dead<BR>body, and अण् aff.; or शव् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावक|शावकः
शावक m. (-कः) The young of any animal.<BR> E. शाव, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावर|शावरः
शावर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Low, vile.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Fault, offence.<BR>	 2. Sin, wicked-<BR>ness.<BR>	 3. The Lodh-tree, (Symplocos racemosus.)<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Cowach,<BR>(Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR>	 2. A sort of Prākrit, that spoken by<BR>barbarians.<BR> E. शवर a man of low or degraded caste, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावरभेदाख्य
शावरभेदाख्य n. (-ख्यं) Copper.<BR> E. शावर relating to a low race, भेद class,<BR>and आख्य appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावाशौच
शावाशौच n. (-चं) Impurity from the demise of a relation.<BR> E. शाव, and अशौच impurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वत|शाश्वतं|शाश्वतः
शाश्वत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Eternal, perpetual.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A name of VYĀSA<BR>2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Heaven, ether.<BR>	 f. (-ती) The<BR>earth.<BR> E. शश्वत् perpetually, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वतिक
शाश्वतिक f. (-की) Eternal, permanent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुल
शाष्कुल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं) Eating flesh or fish.<BR> E. शुष्कुली flesh, अण् aff., form irr.: see शौष्कुल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुलिक|शाष्कुलिकं
शाष्कुलिक n. (-क) A multitude of pies.<BR> E. शष्कुली a sort of pie, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्
शास्(उ)शासु r. 2nd cl. (शास्ति)<BR>	 1. To instruct, to inform.<BR>	 2. To order,<BR>to direct, to enact.<BR>	 3. To rule, to govern.<BR>	 4. To correct, to punish.<BR>5. To advise. (शास्ते)<BR>	 1. To wish or desire: with आङ् prefixed,<BR>r. 1st cl. (आशासते) r. 2nd cl. (आशास्ते) To wish well to, to bless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासन|शासनं
शासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. An order, an edict, a command.<BR>	 2. A royal grant of<BR>land or of privileges, a charter, &c. usually inscribed on stone or<BR>copper.<BR>	 3. A writing, a deed, a written contract or agreement.<BR>	 4.<BR>A Shāstra or scripture.<BR>	 5. Devotion, or devotional tranquillity, the<BR>government of the passions.<BR>	 6. Governing, ruling, government. E.<BR>शास् to order, to direct, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनपत्र
शासनपत्र n. (-त्रं) A plate of copper, a stone or sheet of paper, &c., on<BR>which an edict or grant is inscribed.<BR> E. शासन, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनहर|शासनहरः
शासनहर m. (-रः) A royal messenger, one bearing an edict or grant. E.<BR>शासन an edict, and हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनीय
शासनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be governed or directed.<BR> E. शास् to rule,<BR>अनीयर् aff; also शासितव्य and शास्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासित|शासितः
शासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Governed, ruled.<BR> E. शास् to rule, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासितृ
शासितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Ordering, commanding, a governor or com-<BR>mander.<BR> E. शास् to order, तृच् aff. with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्ति|शास्तिः
शास्ति f. (-स्तिः)<BR>	 1. A command, an order.<BR>	 2. Governing, ruling, order-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. A sceptre.<BR>	 4. Correctre, punishment.<BR> E. शास् to govern,<BR>aff. क्तिन् or ति Uṇādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्तृ
शास्तृ mfn. (-स्ता-स्त्री-स्तृ)<BR>	 1. A ruler, one who rules or governs.<BR>	 2. A<BR>teacher, teaching, instructing.<BR>	 m. (-स्ता) A Buddha or Jina, or the<BR>deified teacher of one or both those sects.<BR> E. शास् to govern, &c.<BR>aff. तृच्, and the augment omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्र|शास्त्रं
शास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>	 1. An order or command.<BR>	 2. Scripture, science, insti-<BR>tutes of religion, law or letters, especially considered as of divine<BR>origin or authority: when used singly, it implies works of literature<BR>or science in general, and it is therefore customarily connected with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">Page716-b+ 60</a>]<BR>some other word to limit its application, as the Vedānta Śhās-<BR>tras, or treatises of philosophical theology; the Dharma-Śhāstras,<BR>books of law, &c.; it is also applied to less important branches of<BR>knowledge, as the Kāvya-Śhāstras, or poetical works; Shilpa-<BR>Śhāstras, works on the mechanical arts; and Kāma-Śhāstras, or<BR>erotic compositions; in the singular number it is also used com-<BR>prehensively to signify the body of all that has been written on<BR>the subject, as Dharma-Śhāstras, the institutes or code of law;<BR>Kāvya-Śhāstra, poetry; Alankāra-Śhāstra, rhetoric, &c.<BR>	 3. A<BR>book in general.<BR> E. शास् to govern or teach, aff. ष्ट्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रकृत्
शास्त्रकृत् m. (-कृत्)<BR>	 1. A Ṛṣi, a holy personage of divine character.<BR>	 2.<BR>An author in general.<BR> E. शास्त्र a Śhāstra or scripture, &c., and कृत्<BR>the author; the principal compositions in Hindu religion, law,<BR>and literature, being attributed to sanctified and superhuman<BR>personages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रगण्ड|शास्त्रगंड|शास्त्रगण्डः
शास्त्रगण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A general and superficial scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रचक्षुस्
शास्त्रचक्षुस् n. (-क्षुः) Grammar.<BR> E. शास्त्र science, and चक्षुस् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञ|शास्त्रज्ञः
शास्त्रज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Acquainted with the Śhāstras, skilled in the<BR>knowledge of law and religion especially.<BR> E. शास्त्र a sacred work<BR>and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञता
शास्त्रज्ञता f. (-ता) Knowledge of the Śhāstras.<BR> E. शास्त्रज्ञ and तल् aff.; also त्व with शास्त्रज्ञत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञान
शास्त्रज्ञान n. (-नं) Knowledge derived from the study of sacred works.<BR>E. शास्त्र, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रतत्त्व
शास्त्रतत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) The truth or true knowledge taught in sacred works.<BR>E. शास्त्र and तत्त्व truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रतत्त्वज्ञ|शास्त्रतत्त्वज्ञः
शास्त्रतत्त्वज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Understanding the works of sacred science.<BR>m. (-ज्ञः) An astrologer, an astronomer.<BR> E. शास्त्र sacred or astrono-<BR>mical science, तत्त्व the truth, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रतस्
शास्त्रतस् Ind. After or according to the Śhāstras.<BR> E. शास्त्र, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रदाशन्
शास्त्रदाशन् mfn. (-र्शा-र्शिनी-र्शि) Skilled in sacred science.<BR> E. शास्त्र Śhās-<BR>tra, and दशिन् who inspects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रनिन्दा
शास्त्रनिन्दा f. (-न्दा) Reviling or denying the authority of sacred works.<BR>E. शास्त्र, and निन्दा reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रप्रसङ्ग|शास्त्रप्रसंगः
शास्त्रप्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The subject of the Śhāstra.<BR>	 2. Discussing works<BR>of sacred literature.<BR> E. शास्त्र, प्रसङ्ग attaching to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रवत्|शास्त्रवन्त्
शास्त्रवत् Ind. Conformably or according to written authority.<BR> E. शास्त्र, वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रवत्|शास्त्रवन्त्
शास्त्रवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having or following sacred institutes, &c.<BR>E. शास्त्र, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविद्
शास्त्रविद् mfn. (-विद्) Understanding or conversant with the scrip-<BR>tures, skilled in sacred science.<BR> E. शास्त्र a Śhāstra, विद् who<BR>knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविधान
शास्त्रविधान n. (-नं) Sacred ritual, ceremonial precept.<BR> E. शास्त्र, and विधान<BR>direction; also शास्त्रविधि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविप्रतिषिद्ध|शास्त्रविप्रतिषिद्धः
शास्त्रविप्रतिषिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Contrary to law or religion, illegal,<BR>forbidden.<BR> E. शास्त्र a Śhāstra, and विप्रतिषिद्ध prohibited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविप्रतिषेध|शास्त्रविप्रतिषेधः
शास्त्रविप्रतिषेध n. (-धं) Any act contrary to the legal and religious<BR>institutes of the Hindus.<BR> E. शास्त्र an institute, and वि and प्रति<BR>contra-indicative prefixes before षिद्ध् to accomplish, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविरुद्ध
शास्त्रविरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Contrary to law or religion.<BR> E. शास्त्र and<BR>विरुद्ध opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविरोध|शास्त्रविरोधः
शास्त्रविरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Opposition or deviation from sacred authority.<BR>2. Contradiction or incompatibility of different systems.<BR> E. शास्त्र,<BR>and विरोध contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रशिल्पिन्
शास्त्रशिल्पिन् plu.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The people of Kāshmir.<BR> E. शास्त्र a treatise, and शिल्पिन् an artificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रसिद्ध
शास्त्रसिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Established or proved by sacred institutes or<BR>divine works.<BR> E. शास्त्र, and सिद्ध established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्राचरण|शास्त्राचरणः
शास्त्राचरण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Versed in the scriptures, well read in the works<BR>of sacred science, a Paṇḍit.<BR>	 2. A follower of the Vedas, one<BR>whose conduct is regulated by their precepts.<BR> E. शास्त्र a sacred<BR>treatise, and आचरण who goes through or studies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=716-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रातिक्रम|शास्त्रातिक्रमः
शास्त्रातिक्रम m. (-मः) Behaving ill or immorally, transgressing, acting<BR>contrary to the Śhāstras.<BR> E. शास्त्र and अतिक्रम surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानुष्ठान
शास्त्रानुष्ठान n. (-नं) Following the Śhāstras, conforming to the law or<BR>ritual, &c.<BR> E. शास्त्र, and अनुष्ठान conforming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानुष्ठित
शास्त्रानुष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Who or what obeys or follows sacred<BR>institutes, &c.<BR>	 2. Established or authorised by the Śhāstras. E.<BR>शास्त्र, and अनुष्ठित following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानुसार|शास्त्रानुसारः
शास्त्रानुसार m. (-रः) Conformity to sacred ordinances.<BR> E. शास्त्र, अनुसार following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्राभिज्ञ
शास्त्राभिज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Learned, versed in the Śhāstras.<BR> E. शास्त्र, and<BR>अभिज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रिन्
शास्त्रिन् m. (-स्त्री) A Paṇḍit, a teacher of holy science, or one skilled<BR>in it.<BR> E. शास्त्र as above, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रीय
शास्त्रीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Scriptural, authorised by or conformable to<BR>sacred institutes.<BR> E. शास्त्र, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रोक्त
शास्त्रोक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Said or declared in a work of sacred authority.<BR> E. शास्त्र, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्य|शास्यः
शास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>	 1. To be regulated or ordained, to be enforced,<BR>to be provided for by any act of government or judicature.<BR>	 2.<BR>To be advised.<BR>	 3. Punishable, deserving punishment.<BR> E. शास् to<BR>govern, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि(ञ)शिञ् r. 5th cl. (शिनोति शिनुते)<BR>	 1. To make thin or small.<BR>	 2. To<BR>whet, to sharpen.<BR>	 3. To excite.<BR>	 4. To be attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि m. (-शिः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. Auspiciousness, good fortune.<BR>	 3. Peace, com-<BR>posure, calm.<BR> E. शि to whet, or शो to destroy, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंशपा
शिंशपा f. (-पा)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Dalbergia Sisu.)<BR>	 2. The Asoka tree.<BR> E. शीघ्र<BR>quick, or शीर्ष the head or top; पा to cherish, or पत् to fall, &c., aff.<BR>क or ड, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्कु|शिक्कुः
शिक्कु mfn. (-क्कुः-क्कुः-क्कु) Idle, lazy, following no business or profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्थ|शिक्थं
शिक्थ n. (-क्थं) Bee's wax; also शिक्थकं and सिक्थकं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्य|शिक्यं
शिक्य nf. (-क्यं-क्या)<BR>	 1. The string or loop suspended from either end of a<BR>pole or yoke to receive the burthen.<BR>	 2. The burthen so carried.<BR>	 3.<BR>The strings of a balance.<BR> E. श्रंस् to fall, Unādi aff. यत्; शि substi-<BR>tuted for the root, and कुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्याधार
शिक्याधार m. (-रः) The hook or eye at each end of a pole or beam, to<BR>which the strings of a yoke or balance are fastened.<BR> E. शिक्या as<BR>above, and आधार receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्यित|शिक्यितं
शिक्यित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Suspended or carried in a sort of loop.<BR> E. शिक्य a loop, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्
शिक्ष् r. 1st cl. (शिक्षते) To learn, to acquire science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षक|शिक्षकः
शिक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) A learner, a teacher.<BR> E. शिक्ष् to learn, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षण|शिक्षणं
शिक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Learning.<BR>	 2. Teaching, instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षणीय
शिक्षणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be taught or learnt.<BR> E. शिक्ष् to learn, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षा
शिक्षा f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. One of the six Vedāṇgas or sciences attached to the<BR>Vedas: the proper pronunciation of the vocal sounds which<BR>occur in them, as explained by PĀṆINI.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Bignonia<BR>Indica.)<BR>	 3. Learning, study, the acquisition of knowledge.<BR>	 4.<BR>Modesty, humility.<BR> E. शिक्ष् to learn, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाकर|शिक्षाकरः
शिक्षाकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. VYĀSA.<BR>	 2. An instructor.<BR> E. शिक्षा the science of<BR>pronunciation, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षानर|शिक्षानरः
शिक्षानर m. (-रः) An epithet of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाशक्ति|शिक्षाशक्तिः
शिक्षाशक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Dexterity, skill.<BR> E. शिक्षा discipline, and शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षित|शिक्षितः
शिक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Skilful, clever, conversant.<BR>	 2. Modest,<BR>diffident.<BR>	 3. Disciplined, exercised.<BR>	 4. Tame, trained, (as an<BR>animal.)<BR>	 5. Docile.<BR>	 6. Studied, learned.<BR> E. शिक्षा studying, इतच् aff.;<BR>or शिक्ष् to study, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षितव्य
शिक्षितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be taught or learnt.<BR> E. शिक्ष् to learn, and तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षिताक्षर|शिक्षिताक्षरः
शिक्षिताक्षर m. (-रः) A pupil, a scholar.<BR> E. शिक्षित study, (by whom,) and<BR>अक्षर a letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्य
शिक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. To be taught, teachable.<BR> E. शिक्ष् to learn, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्यमाण
शिक्ष्यमाण m. (-णः) A pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिख्
शिख्(इ) r. 1st cl. (शिङ्खति) To go, to move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्ड|शिखंड|शिखंडः|शिखण्डः
शिखण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. The tail of a peacock.<BR>	 2. Locks of hair left on the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">Page717-b+ 60</a>]<BR>crown or the sides of the head, at the period of tonsure in chil-<BR>dren: see the next.<BR> E. शिखिन् a peacock or any crested object, अम्<BR>to be or belong to, ड aff. and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डक|शिखंडक|शिखंडकः|शिखण्डकः
शिखण्डक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Locks of hair left at the time of tonsure; three or<BR>five locks left in children in general, or especially those of the<BR>military class, in which latter case, the hair is left in a semicir-<BR>cular patch on each side of the head, covering rather more than<BR>the temporal bones, and following much the same outline: see<BR>काकपक्ष.<BR>	 2. The crest or lock of hair left on the crown of the head.<BR>3. A peacock's tail.<BR> E. शिखा a crest, अण्ड an egg, and कन् pleonasm,<BR>or aff. of comparison; also शिखाण्डक and शिखण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिक|शिखंडिक|शिखंडिकः|शिखण्डिकः
शिखण्डिक m. (-कः) A cock.<BR>	 f. (-का) A lock of hair on the crown of the<BR>head.<BR> E. शिखण्ड a crest, &c. aff. ठक् or कन् in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिन्|शिखंडिन्
शिखण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2. A peacock's tail.<BR>	 3. A cock.<BR>	 4. An<BR>arrow.<BR>	 5. A Ṛṣi, either of the seven represented by the stars of the<BR>greater bear: see चित्रशिखण्डिन् । 6. The son of DRUPADA, by metamor-<BR>phosis: see below.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A kind of jasmine, (J. auriculatum.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A shrub, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR>	 3. The daughter of DRUPADA, after-<BR>wards changed to a male.<BR>	 4. A peahen.<BR> E. शिखण्ड a crest, इनि<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखर|शिखरं|शिखरः
शिखर mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. The peak or summit of a mountain.<BR>	 2. The top of<BR>a tree.<BR>	 3. Point, end, top in general.<BR>	 4. Horripilation.<BR>	 5. The<BR>armpit.<BR>	 6. A piece of a ruby or a gem, described as of the colour<BR>of the ripe pomegranate seed or a bright red.<BR>	 7. The bud of the<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 8. The edge or point of a sword.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A<BR>plant, from the fibres of which bow-strings were made, (Sanse-<BR>viera zeylanica.)<BR> E. शिखा a crest, and रच् poss. aff., and the vowel<BR>made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरवासिनी
शिखरवासिनी f. (-नी) DURGĀ.<BR> E. शिखर the peak, (of the Himālaya,) and वासिनी abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरिन्
शिखरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Crested, peaked, pointed.<BR>	 m. (-री)<BR>	 1. A<BR>mountain.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR>	 4. A strong-<BR>hold, a hill-fort.<BR>	 5. The lapwing.<BR>	 f. (-रिणी)<BR>	 1. A form of metre,<BR>a species of the class Atyashtī metre or verse of four lines of<BR>17 syllables each.<BR>	 2. A dish of curds and sugar with spices.<BR>	 3. An<BR>excellent woman.<BR>	 4. Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 5. A line of hair extending<BR>across the navel.<BR> E. शिखर a point or peak, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखलोहित|शिखलोहितः
शिखलोहित m. (-तः) A plant, commonly Kukurmurā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखा
शिखा f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. Point, top in general.<BR>	 2. A crest.<BR>	 3. A peacock's crest.<BR>4. A lock of hair on the crown of the head.<BR>	 5. Flame.<BR>	 6. A radi-<BR>cating branch.<BR>	 7. Any branch.<BR>	 8. A plant, commonly Lāngaliyā.<BR>9. Chief, principal.<BR>	 10. Fever, proceeding from libidinous excite-<BR>ment or love.<BR>	 11. A ray of light.<BR>	 12. The end of a garment.<BR>	 13. A<BR>fibrous root.<BR>	 14. The forepart of the foot.<BR> E. शीङ् to sleep, Unādi<BR>aff. ख, and the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखाण्डक|शिखाण्डकः
शिखाण्डक m. (-कः) Hair left on each side of the head: see शिखण्डक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखातरु|शिखातरुः
शिखातरु m. (-रुः) A candle-stick or lamp-stand.<BR> E. शिखा flame, तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखाधर|शिखाधरः
शिखाधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Crested, pointed.<BR>	 2. Having a top-knot.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2. A jaina deified saint.<BR> E. शिखा a crest, and<BR>धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखाधरज
शिखाधरज n. (-जं) A peacock's feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखाधार|शिखाधारः
शिखाधार m. (-रः) A peacock.<BR> E. शिखा a crest, and धार who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखामूल|शिखामूलं
शिखामूल n. (-लं) A carrot, a turnip, or any root with a tuft of leaves<BR>growing from it.<BR> E. शिखा a crest, and मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखालु|शिखालुः
शिखालु m. (-लुः) A peacock's crest.<BR> E. शिखा, आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावत्|शिखावन्त्
शिखावत् m. (-वान्)<BR>	 1. A name of AGNI or fire.<BR>	 2. The personified<BR>descending node.<BR>	 3. A lamp.<BR>	 f. (-वती) A plant, (Sansevier a<BR>zeylanica.)<BR> E. शिखा a crest, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावर|शिखावरः
शिखावर m. (-रः) The jack-fruit tree (Artocarpus integrifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावल|शिखावलः
शिखावल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Crested, pointed.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A peacock.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>A flower, (Celosia cristata.)<BR> E. शिखा a crest, and वलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=717-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावृक्ष|शिखावृक्षः
शिखावृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The stand of a lamp.<BR> E. शिखा a flame, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावृद्धि|शिखावृद्धिः
शिखावृद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Usurious interest payable daily.<BR> E. शिखा a tuft of<BR>hair, and वृद्धि interest; growing constantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिकण्ठ|शिखिकंठ|शिखिकण्ठं
शिखिकण्ठ n. (-ण्ठं) Blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिग्रीव|शिखिग्रीवं
शिखिग्रीव n. (-वं) Blue vitriol.<BR> E. शिखि for शिखिन् a peacock, ग्रीवा the<BR>neck, अच् added; being of the same colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिध्वज|शिखिध्वजः
शिखिध्वज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Smoke.<BR>	 2. The deity KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. शिखि a<BR>peacock or fire, and ध्वज an emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिन्
शिखिन् mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि)<BR>	 1. Crested.<BR>	 2. Having a lock of hair on the<BR>top of the head.<BR>	 3. Proud.<BR>	 m. (-खी)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. A peacock.<BR>	 3. A<BR>bull.<BR>	 4. An arrow.<BR>	 5. A tree.<BR>	 6. A cock.<BR>	 7. KETU, the personified<BR>descending node.<BR>	 8. A horse.<BR>	 9. A mountain.<BR>	 10. A Brāhman.<BR>	 11.<BR>A lamp.<BR>	 12. A religious mendicant.<BR> E. शिखा a crest, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिपुच्छ|शिखिपुच्छं
शिखिपुच्छ n. (-च्छं) A peacock's tail.<BR> E. शिखि a peacock, and पुच्छ a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिमण्डल|शिखिमण्डलः
शिखिमण्डल m. (-लः) A tree, (Tapia cratæva.)<BR> E. शिखि a peacock, and<BR>मण्डल district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखियुप
शिखियुप m. (-पः) An antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिवर्द्धक
शिखिवर्द्धक m. (-कः) A pumpkin-gourd.<BR> E. शिखि a peacock, and वर्द्धक increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिवाहन|शिखिवाहनः
शिखिवाहन m. (-नः) KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. शिखि a peacock, and वाहन a vehi-<BR>cle, the deity being mounted on this bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिशिखा
शिखिशिखा f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. Flame.<BR>	 2. A peacock's crest.<BR> E. शिखिन्, and शिखा a crest, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिशेखर
शिखिशेखर n. (-रं) A peacock's crest.<BR> E. शिखिन्, and शेखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रु|शिग्रुः
शिग्रु m. (-ग्रुः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Morunga guilandina and hyperanthera.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A pot-herb in general.<BR> E. शि to sharpen, रुक् aff., and गुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रुज|शिग्रुजं
शिग्रुज n. (-जं) The seed of the Morunga.<BR> E. शिग्रु, ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रुमूल
शिग्रुमूल n. (-लं) The pungent root of the Morunga.<BR> E. शिग्रु, मूल the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रुवीज
शिग्रुवीज n. (-जं) The seed of the Morunga.<BR> E. शिग्रु, and वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिघ्
शिघ्(इ)शिघि r. 1st cl. (शिङ्घति) To smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घाण|शिंघाण|शिङ्घाणं|शिंघाणः|शिङ्घाणः
शिङ्घाण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Any glass-vessel.<BR>	 2. The mucus of the nose.<BR>	 3. Rust<BR>of iron.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Phlegm.<BR>	 2. Froth, foam.<BR> E. शिघि to smell,<BR>आणच् Unādi affix, and the final optionally rejected; also शिङ्घाणक<BR>and सिङ्घाणक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घाणक|शिंघाणक|शिंघाणकं|शिंघाणकः|शिङ्घाणकः
शिङ्घाणक m. (-कः) Phlegm.<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं) The mucus of the nose.<BR> E. शिघि to smell, aff. आणच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिङ्घित|शिंघित|शिङ्घितं
शिङ्घित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Smelled.<BR> E. शिघि to smell, aff. क्त्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिच्
शिच् f. (-शिक्) The string of a pole for carrying burdens.<BR> E. श्रंस् to fall,<BR>deriv. irr.: see शिक्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिज्
शिज्(इ)शिजि r. 2nd cl. (शिङ्क्ते) r. 10th cl. (शिञ्जयति ते)<BR>	 1. To make an<BR>inarticulate sound.<BR>	 2. To tinkle, to jingle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्ज|शिंज|शिंजः|शिञ्जः
शिञ्ज mf. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा) The tinkling sound of silver and other metallic orna-<BR>ments worn round the waist, arm, or ankle, &c.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्जा)<BR>	 1. A bow-<BR>string.<BR>	 2. Jingle of ornaments.<BR> E. शिजि to make an inarticulate<BR>sound, affs. अङ् and टाप्: also शिञ्जिनी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जञ्जिका|शिंजंजिका
शिञ्जञ्जिका f. (-का) A chain worn round the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जित|शिंजित|शिञ्जितं
शिञ्जित n. (-तं) The tinkling of metallic ornaments worn as rings,<BR>chains, &c.<BR> E. शिञ्जा inarticulate sound, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिञ्जिन्
शिञ्जिन् mfn. (-ञ्जी-ञ्जिनी-ञ्जि) Tinkling, making a tinkling.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्जिनी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>bow-string.<BR>	 2. Metallic rings worn round the toes, an ornament of<BR>the feet.<BR> E. शिञ्जा a tinkling, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिट्
शिट् r. 1st cl. (शेटति) To disregard, to treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शित|शितं
शित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Thin, emaciated, wasted, declined.<BR>	 2. Weak,<BR>feeble.<BR>	 3. Sharpened, whetted.<BR> E. शि to sharpen, or शो to pare or<BR>whet, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितता
शितता f. (-ता) Sharpness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, शितत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितद्रु|शितद्रुः
शितद्रु f. (-द्रुः) The Śatadru or the river Sutlej.<BR> E. शित weakened, द्रु<BR>to flow, aff. कुः see शतद्रु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितधार
शितधार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Sharp-edged.<BR> E. शित, and धारा an edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितशूक|शितशूकः
शितशूक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Barley.<BR>	 2. Wheat.<BR> E. शित sharpened, शूक the beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिताग्र|शिताग्रः
शिताग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं) Sharp-pointed.<BR>	 m. (-ग्रः) A thorn.<BR> E. शित, अग्रं<BR>point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितास्त्रभृत्
शितास्त्रभृत् m. (-भृत्) Armed with sharp weapons.<BR> E. शित, अस्त्र a weapon, भृत् who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिति|शितिः
शिति mfn. (-तिः-ती-ति)<BR>	 1. Black.<BR>	 2. White.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) The Bhurja-patra or<BR>birch tree.<BR> E. शि to sharpen, क्तिन् or क्तिच् aff.; or शत् to go, Unādi<BR>aff. इन्, and इ substituded for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिकण्ठ|शितिकंठ|शितिकण्ठः
शितिकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A gallinule.<BR>	 3. A peacock.<BR> E. शिति black,<BR>and कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिचार|शितिचारः
शितिचार m. (-रः) A potherb, (apparently Marsilea dentata, Rox.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिच्छद|शितिच्छदः|शितिछद
शितिच्छद m. (-दः) A goose.<BR> E. शिति white, छद a feather; also सितच्छद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिपक्ष|शितिपक्षः
शितिपक्ष m. (-क्षः) A goose.<BR> E. शिति white, पक्ष a wing; also सितपक्ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिरत्न
शितिरत्न n. (-त्नं) A sapphire.<BR> E. शिति, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिसारक|शितिसारकः
शितिसारक m. (-कः) A sort of ebony, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR> E. शिति<BR>black, and सार essence, resin, कप् added; yielding a strong black<BR>resin that is used for calking boats, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितेषु
शितेषु m. (-षुः) A sharp arrow.<BR> E. शित, and इषु an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिल|शिथिलं
शिथिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Loose, lax, flaccid, flabby.<BR>	 2. Languid, inert,<BR>feeble.<BR>	 3. Ineffective, unenergetic.<BR>	 4. Relaxed, slackened.<BR>	 5. Not<BR>rigidly observed.<BR>	 6. Loosely retained or possessed.<BR>	 7. Abandoned,<BR>got rid of, shaken off.<BR> E. श्लथ् to be lax or loose, Unādi aff. किलच्;<BR>the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलता
शिथिलता f. (-ता) Relaxation, looseness, being unfastened, &c.<BR> E. शिथिल,<BR>and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शिथिलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलबल
शिथिलबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Weakened, relaxed.<BR> E. शिथिल, बल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलवसु
शिथिलवसु mfn. (-सुः-सुः-सु)<BR>	 1. Reduced in wealth.<BR>	 2. Shining with dimi-<BR>nished rays.<BR> E. शिथिल, and वसु wealth, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलशक्ति
शिथिलशक्ति mfn. (-क्तिः-क्तिः-क्ति) Impaired in strength or power.<BR> E. शिथिल, शक्ति power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलित
शिथिलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Let go, loosed, released.<BR>	 2. Relaxed,<BR>loosened.<BR> E. शिथिल, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलीकरण
शिथिलीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Loosening, unfastening.<BR>	 2. Impairing, weaken-<BR>ing, reducing.<BR> E. शिथिल, and करण doing, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलीकृत
शिथिलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unbound, unfastened, slackened.<BR>	 2.<BR>Reduced, impaired, weakened.<BR>	 3. Let loose.<BR> E. शिथिल, कृत made,<BR>च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिनि|शिनिः
शिनि m. (-निः) A proper name, a chief of the Kṣatriya tribe.<BR> E. शि to<BR>make thin or small, Unādi aff. निक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिनेर्नप्तृ
शिनेर्नप्तृ m. (-प्ता) A name of SĀTYAKI, one of the chiefs of the Pāṇ-<BR>ḍus.<BR> E. शिनि a proper name, and नप्तृ grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपविष्ट|शिपविष्टः
शिपविष्ट m. (-ष्टः) Bald, &c.: see शिपिविष्ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपि|शिपिः
शिपि m. (-पिः) A ray of light.<BR>	 f. (-पिः) Skin, leather.<BR>	 n. (-पि) Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपिविष्ट|शिपिविष्टः
शिपिविष्ट m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. A bald man.<BR>	 2. A man naturally void of prepuce.<BR>3. ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 5. A leper.<BR> E. शिपि a ray of light, and विष्ट<BR>entered; also शिपविष्ट and शिविपिष्ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिप्र|शिप्रः
शिप्र m. (-प्रः) Name of a lake on the Himālaya.<BR>	 f. (-प्रा) Name of a river<BR>which flows by Ujjayini.<BR> E. शि-रक् पुक् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफा
शिफा f. (-फा)<BR>	 1. A fibrous root.<BR>	 2. Spikenard, (Valeriana jatamansi.)<BR>3. A river.<BR>	 4. A mother.<BR>	 5. Turmeric.<BR>	 6. The root of a water-lily.<BR>7. A lash with a whip.<BR> E. शी to sleep, फक् aff., and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफाकन्द|शिफाकन्दः
शिफाकन्द mn. (-न्दः-न्दं) The root of a water-lily.<BR> E. शिफा a fibrous root,<BR>कन्द a root; also शिफाक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफाधर|शिफाधरः
शिफाधर m. (-रः) A branch.<BR> E. शिफा a fibrous root, धर what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफारुह|शिफारुहः
शिफारुह m. (-हः) The Indian-fig tree.<BR> E. शिफा a fibrous root, रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्ब|शिंबः|शिम्बः
शिम्ब m. (-म्बः) A sort of large shrub, (Cassia alata.)<BR>	 f. (-म्बा) A legume,<BR>a pod;<BR> E. शम् बा० डम्बच्ः also सिम्बा and शिम्बि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बि|शिम्बिः
शिम्बि f. (-म्बिः-म्बी)<BR>	 1. A legume, a pod.<BR>	 2. A kind of grass.<BR> E. शम्-बि०<BR>नि० वा ङीप्; also शिम्बा, and सिम्बा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बिक|शिम्बिकः
शिम्बिक m. (-कः) A sort of kidney-bean, (Phaseolus max.)<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A<BR>legume, a pod.<BR>	 2. A kind of kidney-bean.<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>last; also शिम्बा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बिपर्णी
शिम्बिपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A sort of bean, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR> E. शिम्बि a pod,<BR>and पर्ण leaf, aff. ङीष्; also with कन् added, fem. form शिम्बिपर्णिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिर|शिरं|शिरः
शिर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The head.<BR>	 2. The root of the pepper plant.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Any<BR>vessel of the body, really or supposed to be, of a tubular form, as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">Page719-a+ 60</a>]<BR>a nerve, a tendon, a gut, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bed.<BR>	 2. A large serpent.<BR>E. शॄ to injure, क aff.: see शिरस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःकपालिन्
शिरःकपालिन् m. (-ली) A devotee carrying a human skull as his emblem.<BR>E. शिरस् the head, कपाल the skull, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःपीडा
शिरःपीडा f. (-डा) Pain of the head, head-ache.<BR> E. शिरस्, and पीडा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःप्रावरण
शिरःप्रावरण n. (-णं) A head-dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःफल|शिरःफलः
शिरःफल m. (-लः) The cocoa-nut tree.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःस्रात
शिरःस्रात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having the head bathed.<BR> E. शिरस्, स्रात bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरज|शिरजः
शिरज m. (-जः) The hair of the head.<BR> E. शिर the head, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्
शिरस् n. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The head.<BR>	 2. The skull.<BR>	 3. The top of a tree.<BR>	 4. A<BR>summit, a peak.<BR>	 5. The van of an army.<BR>	 6. Chief, principal,<BR>head.<BR> E. श्रि to honour, in the passive form, to be honoured, (by<BR>the other members,) असुन् Unādi aff., and the form irr.; or शॄ-<BR>असुन् नि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरसिज|शिरसिजः
शिरसिज m. (-जः) The hair of the head.<BR> E. शिरसि seventh case, in the head, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरसिरुह्
शिरसिरुह् m. (-रुट्) The hair of the head.<BR> E. शिरसि on the head, रुह्<BR>what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्क|शिरस्कं
शिरस्क n. (-स्कं)<BR>	 1. A helmet.<BR>	 2. A turban, a hat or cap.<BR>	 f. (-स्का) A<BR>litter, a palanquin.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, and कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्तस्
शिरस्तस् Ind. From the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्तापिन्
शिरस्तापिन् m. (-पी) An elephant.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, तप् to inflame, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्त्र|शिरस्त्रं
शिरस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A helmet.<BR>	 2. A cap, a turban, &c.<BR> E. शिरस् the head,<BR>त्रै to protect, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्त्राण|शिरस्त्राणं
शिरस्त्राण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A helmet.<BR>	 2. A cap, a turban, &c.<BR> E. शिरस् the<BR>head, त्राण the instrument of defence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्य|शिरस्यः
शिरस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Of or on the head.<BR>	 m. (-स्यः) Clean unentangled<BR>hair.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्स्थ
शिरस्स्थ mfn. (-स्स्थः-स्स्था-स्स्थं) At or on the head, at the top, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-स्स्थः) A chief, a leader.<BR> E. शिरस् head, chief, स्था to stay or be,<BR>aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरापत्र|शिरापत्रः
शिरापत्र m. (-त्रः) The elephant or wood apple, (Feronia elephantium.)<BR>E. शिरा a vein, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिराल|शिरालं
शिराल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Veiny, sinewy, tendinous, skinny, showing the<BR>tendons or veins.<BR>	 n. (-लं) An acid fruit, (Averrhoa carambola.) E.<BR>शिरा a vein, लच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरालक|शिरालकः
शिरालक m. (-कः) A plant, (Cissus quadrangularis.)<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरावृत्त|शिरावृत्तं
शिरावृत्त n. (-त्तं) Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरि|शिरिः
शिरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A sword.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. A murderer, a killer.<BR>	 4. A<BR>locust.<BR> E. शॄ to injure or kill, Unādi aff. इ, and the radical vowel<BR>changed to इर् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरीष|शिरीषः
शिरीष m. (-षः) A kind of tree, (Acacia sirisa.)<BR> E. शॄ to injure, Unādi<BR>aff. ईषन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोगृह|शिरोगृहं
शिरोगृह n. (-हं) A room on the top of the house, a turret.<BR> E. शिरस् top, and गृह house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोग्रह|शिरोग्रहः
शिरोग्रह m. (-हः) Affection of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोग्रीव|शिरोग्रीवं
शिरोग्रीव n. (-वं) The head and neck.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, ग्रीव the neck, the compound neuter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोधरा
शिरोधरा f. (-रा) The neck.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, and धर what upholds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोधि|शिरोधिः
शिरोधि f. (-धिः) The neck.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, धा to hold, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोभूषण
शिरोभूषण n. (-णं) An ornament for the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोमणि|शिरोमणिः
शिरोमणि mf. (-णिः-णी)<BR>	 1. A gem worn in a crest, or on the top of the<BR>head.<BR>	 2. A title of respect conferred on learned men.<BR> E. शिरस्<BR>the head, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोमर्म्मन्|शिरोमर्मन्
शिरोमर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा) A hog.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, मर्म्मन् vitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोमालिन्
शिरोमालिन् m. (-ली) An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरत्न|शिरोरत्नं
शिरोरत्न n. (-त्नं) A gem worn in the crest.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, रत्न a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरुजा
शिरोरुजा f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Echites scholaris.)<BR>	 2. Pain or diseased<BR>affection of the head.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, and रुजा sickness; a<BR>remedy being prepared from the leaves of the plant for head-ache.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरुह्
शिरोरुह् m. (-रुट्) Hair.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, रुह् to grow, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरुह|शिरोरुहः
शिरोरुह m. (-हः) The hair of the head.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, रुह् to grow,<BR>क aff.; also शिरोरुह् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोरोग|शिरोरोगः
शिरोरोग m. (-गः) Disease of the head.<BR> E. शिरस्, रोग sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोर्त्ति|शिरोर्ति|शिरोर्त्तिः
शिरोर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः) Pain of the head, head-ache, &c.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, आर्त्ति pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोवर्त्तिन्|शिरोवर्तिन्
शिरोवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) At the head or top, &c.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्ती) A<BR>chief; one at the head of affairs or of an army.<BR> E. शिरस्, and<BR>वर्त्तिन् staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोवल्ली
शिरोवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) The crest or comb of the peacock.<BR> E. शिरस् the head,<BR>and वल्ली a creeper; it is also read शिरोबन्दि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोवृत्त|शिरोवृत्तं
शिरोवृत्त n. (-त्तं) Pepper.<BR> E. शिरस् the head or top, and वृत्त surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोवेष्ट|शिरोवेष्टः
शिरोवेष्ट m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. A turban.<BR>	 2. A cap.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, and वेष्ट what<BR>surrounds; also शिरोवेष्टन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोवेष्टन|शिरोवेष्टनं
शिरोवेष्टन n. (-नं) A turban.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, and वेष्टन enfolding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोस्थि
शिरोस्थि n. (-स्थिः) A skull.<BR> E. शिरस् the head, and अस्थि a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्
शिल् r. 6th cl. (शिलति) To glean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल|शिलं|शिलः
शिल n. (-लं) Gleaning ears of corn.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A stone, a rock.<BR>	 2.<BR>Arsenic.<BR>	 3. A flat stone on which condiments, &c. are ground with<BR>a muller.<BR>	 f. (-ला-ली)<BR>	 1. The timber of a door-frame.<BR>	 2. A transverse<BR>beam or a beam or stone placed across the top of a post or pillar.<BR>3. Camphor.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A small earth-worm.<BR>	 2. A dart, a spike.<BR>E. शिल् to glean, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाकर्णी
शिलाकर्णी f. (-र्णी) The Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाकुट्टक|शिलाकुट्टकः
शिलाकुट्टक m. (-कः) A stone-cutter's chisel.<BR> E. शिला a stone, कुट्ट् to cut, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाकुसुम
शिलाकुसुम n. (-मं) Storax: see शिलाज ।<BR> E. शिला, कुसुम flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाघन
शिलाघन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Firm or hard as a stone or rock.<BR> E. शिला, घन thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाज|शिलाजं
शिलाज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced in a mountain or rock, fossile,<BR>mineral.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1. Storaz or Benzoin, the resins of the Styrax<BR>benzoinum or S. officinale, which are usually confounded by<BR>the Hindus.<BR>	 2. Iron.<BR> E. शिला a rock, and ज born; the balsams<BR>being supposed to be fossile productions, and to exude from<BR>the soil of mountainous places; being confounded with bitumen<BR>or petroleum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाजतु
शिलाजतु n. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. Bitumen.<BR>	 2. Red chalk.<BR> E. शिला a stone, and जतु lac;<BR>it is supposed to ooze from the stones of mountains in the hot<BR>weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाजित्
शिलाजित् f. (-जित्) Bitumen.<BR> E. शिला a stone, and जित् what conquers or excels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाटक|शिलाटकः
शिलाटक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A room on the top of a house.<BR>	 2. A hole.<BR>	 3. A<BR>fence, an enclosure.<BR> E. शिला a stone, अट् to go, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलातल
शिलातल n. (-लं) The surface of a rock or stone.<BR> E. शिला, तल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलात्मज|शिलात्मजं
शिलात्मज n. (-जं) Iron.<BR> E. शिला a stone, आत्मन् self, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलात्मिका
शिलात्मिका f. (-का) A crucible.<BR> E. शिला a stone, आत्मन् substance, कन्<BR>aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलादद्रु|शिलादद्रुः
शिलादद्रु m. (-द्रुः) Bitumen.<BR> E. शिला a stone, and दद्रु herpes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाधातु|शिलाधातुः
शिलाधातु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. Chalk.<BR>	 2. Red chalk.<BR>	 3. A white fossile subs-<BR>tance; an aluminous earth of a white colour, and thence consider-<BR>ed to be a sort of chalk.<BR> E. शिला a stone or rock, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलापट्ट|शिलापट्टः
शिलापट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A flat stone for grinding condiments, &c.<BR> E. शिला a<BR>stone, and पट्ट a flat surface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलापुत्त्र
शिलापुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) A muller or roller for grinding condiments, &c. on<BR>a flat stone.<BR> E. शिला a flat stone, and पुत्त्र child; also शिलापुत्त्रक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलापुष्प|शिलापुष्पं
शिलापुष्प n. (-ष्पं) Storax or Benzoin.<BR> E. शिला a rock, पुष्प flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाफलक
शिलाफलक n. (-कं) A layer or table of rock or stone.<BR> E. शिला, फलक<BR>a plank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाभव|शिलाभवं
शिलाभव n. (-वं) Storax or Benzion.<BR> E. शिला a rock, and भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाभेद|शिलाभेदः
शिलाभेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Plectranthes scutellaroides.)<BR>	 2. A stone-<BR>cutter's chisel.<BR> E. शिला a stone, and भेद what breaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलामय
शिलामय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Made of stone.<BR> E. शिला, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलारस|शिलारसः
शिलारस m. (-सः) Incense, Benjamin or Olibanum.<BR> E. शिला a stone, रस, juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाबल्का
शिलाबल्का f. (-ल्का) A medicinal substance said to be of cooling and<BR>lithonthriptic properties, commonly termed Silabāk; a sort of<BR>lichen or moss.<BR> E. शिला a stone or rock, and वल्क bark; also<BR>termed शिलावल्कल, शिलात्वच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलावृष्टि|शिलावृष्टिः
शिलावृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Hail.<BR> E. शिला, and वृष्टि rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलावेश्मन्
शिलावेश्मन् n. (-श्मं) A rocky recess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलाव्याधि|शिलाव्याधिः
शिलाव्याधि m. (-धिः) Bitumen.<BR> E. शिला a rock or stone, व्याधि sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलासन|शिलासनं
शिलासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Benzoin or Storax.<BR>	 2. A stone bench or seat.<BR> E. शिला<BR>a stone or rock, and असन abiding or आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलासार|शिलासारं
शिलासार n. (-रं) Iron.<BR> E. शिला a stone, and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलि|शिलिः
शिलि f. (-लिः-ली)<BR>	 1. The lower timber of a door.<BR>	 2. A female frog.<BR>3. An arrow.<BR>	 4. A kind of earth-worm.<BR>	 m. (-लिः) The Bhurja-<BR>patra or birch-tree.<BR> E. शिल् to glean, कि aff.: see शिल, शिला, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलिन्द|शिलिंद|शिलिंदः|शिलिन्दः
शिलिन्द m. (-न्दः) A kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीन्ध्र|शिलींध्र|शिलीन्ध्रं|शिलींध्रः|शिलीन्ध्रः
शिलीन्ध्र n. (-न्ध्रं)<BR>	 1. The flower of the plantain tree.<BR>	 2. Hail.<BR>	 3. A<BR>mushroom.<BR>	 m. (-न्ध्रः)<BR>	 1. A sort of tree.<BR>	 2. A kind of fish;<BR>also चित्रफलक.<BR>	 f. (-न्ध्री)<BR>	 1. Earth, clay.<BR>	 2. A small earth-worm.<BR>	 3.<BR>A sort of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीन्ध्रक|शिलींध्रक|शिलीन्ध्रकं
शिलीन्ध्रक n. (-कं) A mushroom, one growing out of cowdung, a<BR>fungus.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीपद|शिलीपदः
शिलीपद m. (-दः) Enlarged or Tropical leg; also श्लीपद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलीमुख|शिलीमुखः
शिलीमुख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A bee.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. A fool, a block-head.<BR>	 4.<BR>War.<BR> E. शिली a dart, (a sting,) and मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलेय|शिलेयं
शिलेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Like a stone or rock, as hard, &c.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>Storax.<BR> E. शिला a rock; ढक् aff. and the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोच्चय|शिलोच्चयः
शिलोच्चय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A mountain.<BR>	 2. A high mountain.<BR> E. शिला a stone<BR>or rock, उत् up, चि to collect, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोञ्छ|शिलोञ्छः
शिलोञ्छ m. (-ञ्छः)<BR>	 1. Following more than one occupation.<BR>	 2. Gleaning.<BR>E. शिला gleaning, उञ्छ् to gather or glean, aff. अच्; gleaning a<BR>subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोञ्छवृत्ति
शिलोञ्छवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Livelihood gained by gleaning.<BR>	 2. Extraordinary<BR>occupation.<BR> E. शिलोञ्छ, and वृत्ति subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोत्थ|शिलोत्थं
शिलोत्थ mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं) Growing from or upon rock or stone.<BR>	 n. (-त्थं)<BR>Benzoin or Storax.<BR> E. शिला a stone, and उत्थ what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलोद्भव|शिलोद्भवं
शिलोद्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced from stone or rock.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. A<BR>superior sort of Sandal-wood, either the white or brass-coloured<BR>sort.<BR>	 2. Storax or Benzoin.<BR> E. शिला a stone or rock, उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलौकस्
शिलौकस् m. (-काः) GARUḌA.<BR> E. शिला a rock, and ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्प|शिल्पं
शिल्प n. (-ल्पं)<BR>	 1. An art, any manual or mechanical art, (sixty-four<BR>such arts are enumerated.)<BR>	 2. Skill, ingenuity.<BR>	 3. A ceremonial<BR>act.<BR>	 4. A sort of spoon or ladle, used at sacrifices to throw the<BR>Ghee or butter into the fire.<BR> E. शिल् to be clever or skilled, पक्<BR>Unādi aff., and the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पक|शिल्पकं
शिल्पक n. (-कं) A sort of drama: one exhibiting magical and mystical<BR>rites,<BR> E. शिल्प manual art, and कन् aff.; also read शिल्पिकं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पकर्म्मन्|शिल्पकर्मन्
शिल्पकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Manual labour, handicraft.<BR> E. शिल्प, and कर्म्मन् act;<BR>also शिल्पक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पकार|शिल्पकारः
शिल्पकार m. (-रः) An artisan, a mechanic.<BR> E. शिल्प a handicraft, कार who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पविद्या
शिल्पविद्या f. (-द्या) Art, mechanical or manual skill.<BR> E. शिल्प, and विद्या<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पशाल
शिल्पशाल nf. (-लं-ला) A work-shop, a manufactory.<BR> E. शिल्प art, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिक
शिल्पिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Manual, mechanic.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Handicraft.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of drama: see शिल्पक.<BR> E. शिल्प, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिन्
शिल्पिन् mfn. (-ल्पी-ल्पिनी-ल्पि)<BR>	 1. An artist, an artificer or artisan.<BR>	 2.<BR>Belonging or relating to a mechanical profession or art.<BR>	 f. (-ल्पि नी)<BR>A drug or herb, a kind of grass said to the known by the name of<BR>Lahānasipi, and described as sweet and cooling, and bearing<BR>seeds of tonic, and restorative properties; also शिल्पिका, &c.<BR> E. शिल्प<BR>art, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिशाल
शिल्पिशाल nf. (-लं-ला) A work-shop, a manufactory.<BR> E. शिल्पि an artisan, and शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिशास्त्र
शिल्पिशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) A treatise or set of treatises on works of art. E.<BR>शिल्पि an artist, and शास्त्र book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिव|शिवं|शिवः
शिव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Prosperous, happy.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The deity ŚIVA,<BR>the most formidable of the Hindu triad, the destroyer of creation:<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">Page720-b+ 60</a>]<BR>the adoration of which he is the object, is of a more gloomy nature<BR>in general than that of the rest, and he is the particular god of<BR>the Tāntrikas or followers of the books called Tantras.<BR>	 2. Final<BR>emancipation from existence, eternal happiness.<BR>	 3. A pillar or<BR>post to which cattle are tied.<BR>	 4. An auspicious planetary conjunc-<BR>tion.<BR>	 5. Scripture, the Vedas.<BR>	 6. A drug, commonly Elabālukā.<BR>7. A perfume, Puṇḍarīya.<BR>	 8. Bdellium.<BR>	 9. One of the astronomi-<BR>cal periods termed Yogas.<BR>	 10. Quicksilver.<BR>	 11. The penis.<BR>	 12. The<BR>phallic emblem of ŚIVA.<BR>	 13. A god.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Happiness, pleasure.<BR>2. Auspiciousness, well-being.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR>	 4. Sea or fossile salt.<BR>	 5.<BR>Borax.<BR>	 6. Rock-salt.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. The goddess DURGĀ, the wife of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. The Śami tree, (Mimosa suma, Rox.)<BR>	 3. Yellow myro-<BR>balan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR>	 4. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 5. A jackal.<BR>6. The mother of the twenty-second Jina.<BR>	 7. Final emancipation.<BR>8. A kind of yellow pigment.<BR>	 9. The Durbā-grass.<BR> E. शी to sleep<BR>Unādi aff. वन्, on or in whom or which, the universe reposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवक|शिवकः
शिवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A post to which cows or calves are tied.<BR>	 2. A post<BR>for cattle to rub against.<BR> E. शिव the same, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवकर|शिवकरः
शिवकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Propitious, auspicious, making happy.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>A Jina of the last age.<BR> E. शिव good fortune, and कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवकीर्त्तन|शिवकीर्तन|शिवकीर्तनः|शिवकीर्त्तनः
शिवकीर्त्तन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. An attendant on ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. KṚṢṆA or VIṢṆU.<BR>n. (-नं) Praising or hymning ŚIVA.<BR> E. शिव ŚIVA, कीर्त्तन celebrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवगति|शिवगतिः
शिवगति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>	 1. Happy, prosperous.<BR>	 2. Worshipping ŚIVA.<BR>m. (-तिः) One of the Jinas of the past age.<BR> E. शिव auspiciousness.<BR>गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवघर्म्मज|शिवघर्मज|शिवघर्मजः|शिवघर्म्मजः
शिवघर्म्मज m. (-जः) The planet MARS.<BR> E. शिव ŚIVA, घर्म्म perspiration, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवङ्कर|शिवंकर|शिवङ्करः
शिवङ्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Propitious, auspicious, conferring happiness or<BR>good fortune.<BR> E. शिव good fortune, कृ to make, aff. खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवचतुर्दशी
शिवचतुर्दशी f. (-शी) A festival held in honour of ŚIVA, on the fourteenth<BR>of the dark-half of Māgha.<BR> E. शिव, चतुर्दशी fourteenth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवज्ञ
शिवज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Knowing what is good or propitious.<BR>	 2.<BR>Worshipping ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-ज्ञा) A female devotee of the Saiva sect. E.<BR>शिव ŚIVA, and ज्ञा to know, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवताति|शिवतातिः
शिवताति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Propitious, conferring happiness or fortune.<BR>E. शिव happiness, तातिल् aff.; also शिवतातिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवदत्त|शिवदत्तं
शिवदत्त n. (-त्तं) The discus of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. शिव ŚIVA, and दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवदारु
शिवदारु m. (-रुः) The Devadāru tree, (Pinus Deodar.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवदूतिका
शिवदूतिका f. (-का) One of the Mātṛs or divine mothers.<BR> E. शिवदूति<BR>DURGĀ, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवदूती
शिवदूती f. (-ती) DURGĀ.<BR> E. शिव ŚIVA, and दूती, from दूत a messenger, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवधातु|शिवधातुः
शिवधातु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. The milk stone, opal or chalcedony.<BR>	 2. Quick-silver.<BR>E. शिव ŚIVA, धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवपुरी
शिवपुरी f. (-री) The holy city Benares.<BR> E. शिव, and पुरी the city; being sacred to ŚIVA especially.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवप्रिय|शिवप्रियं|शिवप्रियः
शिवप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Dear to or esteemed by ŚIVA.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>Sesbana grandiflora.<BR>	 2. Crystal.<BR>	 f. (-या) The goddess DURGĀ.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-यं) The seeds of the Eleocarpus.<BR> E. शिव, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवमल्ली
शिवमल्ली f. (-ल्ली) The Sesbana grandiflora.<BR> E. शिव, and मल्ली jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवरस|शिवरसः
शिवरस m. (-सः) The water of boiled-rice or pulse three days old, and<BR>undergoing spontaneous fermentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवरात्रि|शिवरात्रिः
शिवरात्रि f. (-त्रिः) A celebrated festival held in honour of ŚIVA on the<BR>fourteenth of the moon's wane or dark-fortnight in Māgha. E.<BR>शिव, and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवलिङ्ग|शिवलिंग|शिवलिङ्गं
शिवलिङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) ŚIVA in the form of a phallus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिववल्लभ|शिववल्लभः
शिववल्लभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Loved or esteemed by ŚIVA.<BR>	 m. (-भः)<BR>1. The mango tree.<BR>	 2. Gigantic swallow-wort.<BR>	 f. (-भा) The goddess<BR>PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. शिव ŚIVA, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिववाहन|शिववाहनः
शिववाहन m. (-नः) A bull.<BR> E. शिव the deity, वाहन vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिववीज|शिववीजं
शिववीज n. (-जं) Quicksilver.<BR> E. शिव ŚIVA, and वीज semen; its supposed origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवशेखर|शिवशेखरः
शिवशेखर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The Sesbana grandiflora.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. शिव<BR>ŚIVA, and शेखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवाक्ष|शिवाक्षं
शिवाक्ष n. (-क्षं) The seed of the Eleocarpus.<BR> E. शिव ŚIVA, and अक्ष from<BR>अक्षि the eye. “रुद्राक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवानी
शिवानी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A flower, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR>	 2. A name of DURGĀ. E.<BR>शिव the deity, ङीष् aff., and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवाप्रिय|शिवाप्रियः
शिवाप्रिय m. (-यः) A goat.<BR> E. शिवा DURGĀ, and प्रिय beloved by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवाराति|शिवारातिः
शिवाराति m. (-तिः) A dog.<BR> E. शिवा a jackal, and अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवालय|शिवालयं|शिवालयः
शिवालय m. (-यः) Red Tulaśi or basil.<BR>	 n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. A cemetery or place<BR>where dead bodies are burnt or buried.<BR>	 2. Any temple dedicated<BR>to ŚIVA.<BR> E. शिव ŚIVA, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवालु|शिवालुः
शिवालु m. (-लुः) A jackal. शिवायालति अल-उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवास्मृति|शिवास्मृतिः
शिवास्मृति f. (-तिः) A plant, (Celtis orientalis.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवि|शिविः
शिवि m. (-विः)<BR>	 1. A beast of prey.<BR>	 2. The Bhurja-patra or birch-tree.<BR>	 3. A king so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविका
शिविका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A palanquin, a litter.<BR> E. शिव nominal verb, to give<BR>pleasure or ease, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविपिष्ट|शिविपिष्टः
शिविपिष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A name of ŚIVA: see शिपिविष्ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविर|शिविरं
शिविर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A camp.<BR>	 2. A royal camp or residence.<BR>	 3. A guard or<BR>defence for the soldiers.<BR>	 4. A sort of grain.<BR> E. शी to sleep or rest,<BR>किरक् Unādi aff. and वुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवीरथ|शिवीरथः
शिवीरथ m. (-थः) A palanquin, a litter.<BR> E. शिवी for शिविका the same, रथ a conveyance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशयिषा
शिशयिषा f. (-षा) Drowsiness, sleepiness, wish to sleep.<BR> E. शी to sleep,<BR>desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशयिषु
शिशयिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Sleepy, drowsy.<BR> E. शी to sleep, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशिर|शिशिरः
शिशिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Cold, frigid, chilly, freezing.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Frost.<BR>	 mn.<BR>(-रः-रं) The cold season, comprising two months from about the<BR>middle of January to that of March.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Coolness.<BR>	 2. Dew,<BR>hoar-frost.<BR>	 3. The cool season.<BR> E. शश् to go, (the sun, north of the<BR>equator,) किरच् Unādi aff. and the radical vowel changed to इ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशिरकाल|शिशिरकालः
शिशिरकाल n. (-लं) The dewy season: see the last.<BR> E. शिशिर, काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशु|शिशुः
शिशु m. (-शुः)<BR>	 1. The young of man or any animal, a child, a calf,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. A pupil, a scholar.<BR>	 3. A boy under eight years of age.<BR>4. A lad or boy not more than sixteen.<BR> E. शो to destroy, Unādi<BR>aff. उ, and the root repeated, with इ substituted for the semivowel<BR>to which the radical vowel is changed in its inflections.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुक|शिशुकः
शिशुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A porpoise.<BR>	 2. Another fish, resembling a porpoise.<BR>3. A child, a young animal.<BR>	 4. A tree.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुक्रन्द|शिशुक्रंद|शिशुक्रन्दः
शिशुक्रन्द m. (-न्दः) The weeping of an infant or child.<BR> E. शिशु a child,<BR>and क्रन्द weeping; also शिशुक्रन्दन n. (-नं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुक्रन्दनीय
शिशुक्रन्दनीय m. (-यः) A book or work treating of infantine or juvenile<BR>grievances.<BR> E. शिशुक्रन्द as above, and छ aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुगन्धा|शिशुगंधा
शिशुगन्धा f. (-न्धा) Double jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुत्व|शिशुत्वं
शिशुत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Boyhood, pupilage, the period before sixteen.<BR>	 2.<BR>Childhood, the period up to eight years of age.<BR> E. शिशु a child, त्व<BR>abstract aff.; also with तल् aff. शिशुता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुपाल|शिशुपालः
शिशुपाल m. (-लः) The sovereign of a country in the central part of<BR>India or Cedi, opposed to KṚṢṆA and slain by him: his death<BR>forms the subject of one of the Hindu epic poems, thence named<BR>Śiśupāla-Badha, by MĀGHA.<BR> E. शिशु a child, पाल who cherishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुपालक|शिशुपालकः
शिशुपालक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A king: see the last.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Nauclea cordi-<BR>folia.)<BR> E. शिशु child, पाल who or what pleases or cherishes, aff कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुपालहन्
शिशुपालहन् m. (-हा) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. शिशुपाल the king, हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुमार|शिशुमारः
शिशुमार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The Gangetic porpoise, (Delphinus gangeticus.)<BR>	 2.<BR>The heavenly porpoise, or collection of the stars and planets.<BR>	 3.<BR>A name or form of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. शिशु child, and मार what kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुवाहक|शिशुवाहकः
शिशुवाहक m. (-कः) A wild goat.<BR> E. शिशु a child, वह् to bear, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुवाह्यक|शिशुवाह्यकः
शिशुवाह्यक m. (-कः) A wild goat.<BR> E. शिशु a child, वह् to bear, ण्यत् aff.,<BR>and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्न|शिश्नं|शिश्नः
शिश्न m. (-श्नः) The penis.<BR> E. शश् to move, aff. नक्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्विदान|शिश्विदानः
शिश्विदान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Innocent, virtuous.<BR>	 2. Guilty, sinful, wicked.<BR>E. श्वित् to be white, (pure or virtuous,) आनच् Unādi aff., त<BR>changed to द, and the reduplicate form of the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्
शिष् r. 1st cl. (शेषति) To hurt, to injure or kill. r. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>(शेषति शेषयति-ते) To leave a residue, not to use the whole.<BR>(Usually with वि prefixed.) To excel. (ॡ and with वि prefixed.)<BR>विशिषॢ r. 7th cl. (विशिनष्टि) To assign attributes or qualities to,<BR>to distinguish, to individualize, to specify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्ट|शिष्टः
शिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Obedient, docile.<BR>	 2. Ordered, commanded,<BR>disciplined, trained.<BR>	 3. Chief, principal, eminent, select.<BR>	 4. Left,<BR>remaining.<BR>	 5. Wise.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. A courtier, a counsellor.<BR>	 2. A<BR>chief.<BR> E. शास् to order, aff. क्त, form irr.; or शिष् to leave, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टता
शिष्टता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Good behaviour, urbanity, civility.<BR>	 2. Docility.<BR>	 3. The<BR>property of being left or remaining.<BR> E. शिष्ट, and तल् aff.; also with<BR>त्व, शिष्टत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टसभा
शिष्टसभा f. (-भा) A council of state, an assembly of chief officers.<BR> E. शिष्ट,<BR>सभा an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टसभाचार
शिष्टसभाचार m. (-रः) History or tradition of eminent persons.<BR> E. शिष्ट, सभाचार account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टाचार|शिष्टाचारः
शिष्टाचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Well-behaved.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Good-manners, proper<BR>behaviour.<BR> E. शिष्ट, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टि|शिष्टिः
शिष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. An order or command.<BR>	 2. Ruling, commanding.<BR>	 3.<BR>Correcting, keeping in order.<BR>	 4. Personal correction or chastise-<BR>ment.<BR> E. शास् to order, aff. क्तिन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्ट्वा
शिष्ट्वा Ind.<BR>	 1. Having confessed publicly, or proclaimed.<BR>	 2. Having<BR>governed, regulated, trained.<BR> E. शास् to rule, or शिष् to hurt, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्य|शिष्यः
शिष्य m. (-ष्यः)<BR>	 1. A pupil, a scholar.<BR>	 2. Passion, anger.<BR>	 3. Violence. E.<BR>शास् to order, aff. क्यप्; the vowel changed to इ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्यशिष्टि|शिष्यशिष्टिः
शिष्यशिष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Chastisement or correction of a pupil.<BR> E. शिष्य, शिष्टि correction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिह्ल|शिह्लः
शिह्ल m. (-ह्लः) Incense, benjamin or olibanum.<BR> E. ष्णिह् to melt, लक्<BR>aff., deriv. irr.; more usually सिह्ल; also with कन् added शिह्लक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शी
शी(ङ)शीङ् r. 2nd cl. (शेते) To sleep. With अति prefixed, 1. To sleep<BR>longer than.<BR>	 2. To to be profuse or copious, to be much or<BR>more, to exceed. With अधि, 1. To lie down on.<BR>	 2. To abide, to<BR>be. With सम्, To doubt. With उप, To lie near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शी
शी m. (-शीः)<BR>	 1. Sleep, repose.<BR>	 2. Devotion, tranquillity, indifference to<BR>every thing but the object of worship.<BR> E. शी to sleep, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीक्
शीक् r. 1st cl. (ऋ) शीकृ (शीकते) 1. To wet, to moisten, to sprinkle.<BR>	 2.<BR>To move gently. r. 1st and 10th cls. (शीकति शीकयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>endure patiently, to be patient.<BR>	 2. To touch.<BR>	 3. To wet, to<BR>moisten.<BR>	 4. To be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीकर|शीकरं|शीकरः
शीकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Thin rain, or rain driven by wind.<BR>	 2. A drop of<BR>water.<BR>	 n. (-रं) A sort of pine or its resin.<BR> E. शीक् to sprinkle, aff.<BR>अरन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीकरोघ
शीकरोघ mfn. (-घः-घा-घं) Abounding with mist, spray or thin rain.<BR> E. शीकर, ओघ a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्र|शीघ्रं
शीघ्र mfn. (-घ्रः-घ्रा-घ्रं) Quick, speedy.<BR>	 m. (-घ्रः) (In astronomy,) Parallax.<BR>n. Adv. (-घ्रं) Quickly, swiftly.<BR> E. शिघ् to smell, रक् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रग|शीघ्रगः
शीघ्रग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Going quick.<BR> E. शीघ्र and ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रगामिन्
शीघ्रगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Going quick or expeditiously.<BR> E. शीघ्र<BR>quickly, and गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रचेतन|शीघ्रचेतनः
शीघ्रचेतन m. (-नः) A dog.<BR> E. शीघ्र quickly, चेतन thinking, knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रजन्मन्
शीघ्रजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) A plant, (Cæsalpinia bonduccella.)<BR> E. शीघ्र quick,<BR>जन्मन् birth. “कांँटा करम्चा ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रता
शीघ्रता f. (-ता) Quickness, speed.<BR> E. शीघ्र, तल् aff.; also with त्व, शीघ्रत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रवेधिन
शीघ्रवेधिन m. (-धी) A good archer, a good shot.<BR> E. शीघ्र quick, and वेधिन्<BR>who pierces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रायमाण
शीघ्रायमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Becoming quick or expeditious.<BR> E. शीघ्र<BR>nominal verb, to be quick, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रिय|शीघ्रियः
शीघ्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Quick, fleet.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3.<BR>The fighting of cats.<BR> E. शीघ्र quick, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्र्य|शीघ्र्यं
शीघ्र्य m. (-घ्य्रः)<BR>	 1. The fighting of cats.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्
शीत् Ind. A sound made to express any sudden thrill, (especially<BR>applied to the sound made during sexual enjoyment.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत|शीतं|शीतः
शीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cold, chilly, frigid.<BR>	 2. Idle, lazy.<BR>	 3. Cold, dull,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">Page722-a+ 60</a>]<BR>apathetic, stupid.<BR>	 4. Decocted, boiled.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Cold, coldness.<BR>	 2.<BR>Water.<BR>	 3. Cold weather or the six months of the rainy, dewy and<BR>cold seasons.<BR>	 4. Cinnamon.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A small tree, (Cordia myxa.)<BR>2. A kind of ratan, (Calamus fasciculatus.)<BR>	 3. A plant, (Marsilea<BR>quadrifolia.)<BR>	 4. The Nimba-tree.<BR>	 5. Camphor.<BR>	 6. The cold season.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The wife of RĀMA.<BR>	 2. A furrow.<BR> E. श्यै to go, aff. क्त; the<BR>fem. form more usually occurs सीता, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=721-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतक|शीतकः
शीतक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Cold weather or the cold season, winter.<BR>	 2. A lazy<BR>man, one who is dilatory or dull.<BR>	 3. One devoid of care or anxiety,<BR>a happy man.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Marsilea dentata.)<BR>	 5. A scorpion. E.<BR>कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतकाल|शीतकालः
शीतकाल n. (-लं) Cold weather, winter.<BR> E. शीत, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतकालीन
शीतकालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Produced in winter.<BR> E. शीतकाल, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतकृच्छ्र|शीतकृच्छ्रः
शीतकृच्छ्र m. (-च्छ्रः) A religious penance, drinking cold water three days,<BR>cold milk three days, cold Ghee three days, and fasting three. E.<BR>शीत cold, and कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतकुम्भ|शीतकुम्भः
शीतकुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A flower, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>	 f. (-म्भा) An aquatic plant.<BR>E. शीत cold, कुम्भ a water-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतक्षार|शीतक्षारं|शीतक्षारः
शीतक्षार n. (-रं) Refined Borax.<BR> E. शीत cold, क्षार nitre. “श्वेतटङ्कणे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतगन्ध|शीतगंध|शीतगन्धं|शीतगन्धः
शीतगन्ध n. (-न्धं) White Sandal.<BR> E. शीत cold, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतगु|शीतगुः
शीतगु m. (-गुः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. शीत cold, and गु neut.<BR>form of गो a ray of light, here forming a masc. compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतचम्पक|शीतचंपक|शीतचम्पकः
शीतचम्पक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A lamp.<BR>	 2. Pleasing, satisfying.<BR>	 3. A mirror. E.<BR>शीत cold, cool, and चम्पक a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतता
शीतता f. (-ता) Cold, coldness.<BR> E. शीत and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शीतत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतदीधिति|शीतदीधितिः
शीतदीधिति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपर्णी
शीतपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Cleome pentaphylla.)<BR> E. शीत cool, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपल्लव
शीतपल्लव m. (-वः) A plant, (Ardisea solanacea.)<BR> E. शीत cool, पल्लव a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपाकिनी
शीतपाकिनी f. (-नी) A medicinal root, commonly Kākoli.<BR> E. शीत the<BR>cold, (in a cold climate,) पाक ripening, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपाकी
शीतपाकी f. (-की)<BR>	 1. A medicinal root, commonly Kākoli.<BR>	 2. A plant,<BR>(Sida cordifolia.)<BR> E. शीत cold, (in cold weather, &c.) पाक a ripening,<BR>ङीप् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपुष्प|शीतपुष्पः
शीतपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) The Sirisha tree.<BR>	 n. (-ष्पं) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus<BR>rotundus.)<BR> E. शीत cold, (in the cold weather, &c.) and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतपुष्पक|शीतपुष्पकं|शीतपुष्पकः
शीतपुष्पक n. (-कं) Storax or Benzoin.<BR> E. शीत cold, (in the snowy<BR>mountains,) पुष्प a flower, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतप्रभ|शीतप्रभः
शीतप्रभ m. (-भः) Camphor.<BR> E. शीत cool, and प्रभ shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतभानु|शीतभानुः
शीतभानु m. (-नुः) The moon.<BR> E. शीत cool, भानु the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतभीरु|शीतभीरुः
शीतभीरु f. (-रुः) Arabian jasmine, (Jasminum zambac.)<BR> E. शीत the cold, भीरु afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतभोजिन्
शीतभोजिन् mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि) Eating cold viands.<BR> E. शीत, भुज् to eat,<BR>णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतमयूख|शीतमयूखः
शीतमयूख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. शीत cool, मयूख a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतमरीचि|शीतमरीचिः
शीतमरीचि m. (-चिः) The moon.<BR> E. शीत cool, मरीचि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतमूलक|शीतमूलकं
शीतमूलक n. (-कं) The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR> E. शीत cool, मूलक a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतरम्य|शीतरम्यः
शीतरम्य m. (-म्यः) A lamp.<BR> E. शीत cool, and रम्य agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतरुच्
शीतरुच् m. (-रुक्) The moon.<BR> E. शीत, and रुच् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतल|शीतलं|शीतलः
शीतल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Cold, chilly, frigid.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Green vitriol.<BR>	 2.<BR>Storax.<BR>	 3. Sandal.<BR>	 4. White Sandal.<BR>	 5. A lotus.<BR>	 6. A pearl.<BR>	 7.<BR>Cold, coldness.<BR>	 8. The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>1. A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR>	 2. A Jina or Jaina teacher,<BR>the 10th of the twenty-four Tirthakārs.<BR>	 3. A religious ceremony<BR>observed upon the sun's entering Aries.<BR>	 4. The moon.<BR>	 5. A small<BR>tree, (Cordia myxa.)<BR>	 6. The Champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 7.<BR>A sort of camphor.<BR>	 8. Turpentine.<BR>	 f. (-ला-ली)<BR>	 1. A plant, perhaps<BR>intending the Phrynium dichotymum, from the split stems of<BR>which a smooth, cool mat is made, thence termed Sitala-pāti.<BR>	 2.<BR>Small-pox.<BR>	 3. The goddess presiding over or inflicting small-pox.<BR>E. शीत cool, लच् poss. aff., or ला to give or get, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलता
शीतलता f. (-ता) Coldness, coolness.<BR> E. शीतल, तल् aff.; also with त्व, शीतलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलप्रद|शीतलप्रदः
शीतलप्रद m. (-दः) Sandal.<BR> E. शीतल cold, and प्रद who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलवात|शीतलवातः
शीतलवात m. (-तः) A cool wind.<BR> E. शीतल, and वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलवातक|शीतलवातकः
शीतलवातक m. (-कः) A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR> E. शीतल cool, वात<BR>wind, कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलषष्ठी
शीतलषष्ठी f. (-ष्ठी) The sixth of the light-half of Māgha, when only cold<BR>food is eaten.<BR> E. शीतल, and षष्ठी sixth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतशिव|शीतशिवं|शीतशिवः
शीतशिव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. A sort of resin, (Storax benzoin.)<BR>	 2. Rock salt.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-वः)<BR>	 1. A kind of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>	 2. The Śami-tree,<BR>(Mimosa suma, Rox.)<BR> E. शीत cool, and शिव auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतशूक|शीतशूकः
शीतशूक m. (-कः) Barley.<BR> E. शीत cold, and शूक an awn or beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतसह|शीतसहः
शीतसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Bearing or enduring cold.<BR>	 m. (-हः) A Pilu, or<BR>tree so named, growing in the Himālaya mountains.<BR> E. शीत cold,<BR>and सह enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतहर
शीतहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Removing cold.<BR> E. शीत, and हर what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतांशु|शीतांशुः
शीतांशु m. (-शुः)<BR>	 1. Camphor.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. शीत cold, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीताकुल
शीताकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Benumbed, frozen.<BR> E. शीत, आकुल perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीताद|शीतादः
शीताद m. (-दः) Scorbutic affection of the gums.<BR> E. शीत, अद what eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीताद्रि|शीताद्रिः
शीताद्रि m. (-द्रिः) The snowy mountain.<BR> E. शीत cold, अद्रि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतार्त्त|शीतार्त|शीतार्त्तः
शीतार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Cold, chilled, shivering, suffering or shrinking<BR>from cold.<BR> E. शीत cold, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतालु|शीतालुः
शीतालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Cold, shivering, shrinking from cold.<BR> E. शीत<BR>cold, आलुच् aff., here implying aversion or impatience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीताश्मन्
शीताश्मन् m. (-श्मा) The moon-gem, crystal.<BR> E. शीत cold, अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतोभाव
शीतोभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Final emancipation.<BR>	 2. Coolness, composure.<BR>	 3.<BR>Cold, coldness.<BR> E. शीत cold, भाव nature, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतोत्तम|शीतोत्तमं
शीतोत्तम n. (-मं) Water.<BR> E. शीत cold, उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्य|शीत्यं
शीत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Ploughed, tilled: more usually सीत्य.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>cooled or chilled.<BR> E. शीत cold, or शीता a furrow, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्कार|शीत्कारः
शीत्कार m. (-रः) Uttering a sound expressive of pleasurable sensations.<BR>E. शीत् imitative sound, and कार making: also with कृत made,<BR>uttered, शीत्कृत n. (-तं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधु|शीधुः
शीधु mn. (-धुः-धु) Rum, distilled from molasses.<BR> E. शी to sleep, or rest, Unādi aff. धुक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधुगन्ध|शीधुगंध|शीधुगन्धः
शीधुगन्ध m. (-न्धः) A plant, (Mimusops elengi.)<BR> E. शीधु Rum, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधुप|शीधुपः
शीधुप mf. (-पः-पी) A drinker of spirits, a dram-drinker.<BR> E. शीधु spirits,<BR>and पा to drink, aff. टक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीन|शीनं|शीनः
शीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Thick, congealed, (as oil or butter.)<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>fool, a blockhead.<BR>	 2. A large snake.<BR> E. श्यै to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीफालिका
शीफालिका f. (-का) A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis:) see शेफालिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभ्
शीभ्(ऋ)शीभृ r. 10th cl. (शीभते)<BR>	 1. To flatter.<BR>	 2. To boast.<BR>	 3. To say.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभव|शीभवः
शीभव m. (-वः) Thin rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभ्य|शीभ्यः
शीभ्य m. (-भ्यः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A bull.<BR> E. शीभ् to praise, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीयमान
शीयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Going away, dissipating, dispersing, departing.<BR>E. शद् to go, शानच् aff.; शीय substituted for the radical letters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर|शीरः
शीर m. (-रः) A large snake, (Boa constrictor.)<BR>	 2. A plough.<BR> E. शी<BR>to sleep, रक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्ण|शीर्णं
शीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Thin, small, slender.<BR>	 2. Wasted, withered,<BR>decayed.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णता
शीर्णता f. (-ता) Emaciation, withering.<BR> E. शीर्ण, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, शीर्णत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णनाला
शीर्णनाला f. (-ला) A plant, (Hemionites cordifolia.)<BR> E. शीर्ण shrivelled<BR>or slender, नाल stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णपत्र|शीर्णपत्रः
शीर्णपत्र m. (-त्रः) A tree, (Pterospermum acerifolium.)<BR> E. शीर्ण withered,<BR>पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णपाद|शीर्णपादः
शीर्णपाद m. (-दः) An epithet of the planet Saturn.<BR> E. शीर्ण shrivelled, पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णपुष्पिका
शीर्णपुष्पिका f. (-का) A kind of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR> E. शीर्ण shrunk,<BR>पुष्प a flower, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णवृन्त|शीर्णवृंत|शीर्णवृन्तं|शीर्णवृन्तः
शीर्णवृन्त n. (-न्तं) A water-melon.<BR> E. शीर्ण slender, and वृन्त foot-stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णाङ्घ्रि|शीर्णांघ्रि|शीर्णाङ्घ्रिः
शीर्णाङ्घ्रि m. (-ङ्घ्रिः) YAMA, judge of the dead.<BR> E. शीर्ण shrivelled, अङ्घ्रि a<BR>foot: being shrunk up in consequence of a curse of his mother's.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्व्वि|शीर्वि|शीर्व्विः
शीर्व्वि mfn. (-र्व्विः-र्व्विः-र्व्वि) Mischievous, malignant, hurtful, savage. E.<BR>शॄ to injure, क्विन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्ष|शीर्षं
शीर्ष n. (-र्षं) The head. E. See शिरस् for which it is substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षक|शीर्षकं|शीर्षकः
शीर्षक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A helmet.<BR>	 2. The skull.<BR>	 3. The head.<BR>	 4. Judgment,<BR>award, sentence, the fruit or result of judicial investigation.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) Rāhu, the personified ascending node.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षकस्थ
शीर्षकस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Staying in or on the head.<BR>	 2. Abiding<BR>by an award, agreeing to submit to the penalty imposed by it. E.<BR>शीर्षक, and स्थ who stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षघातिन्
शीर्षघातिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>	 1. Beheading, decapitating.<BR>	 2. Striking<BR>or injuring the head.<BR> E. शीर्ष the head, हन् to strike, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षच्छेद|शीर्षच्छेदः|शीर्षछेद
शीर्षच्छेद m. (-दः) Decapitating.<BR> E. शीर्ष, च्छेद cutting; also शीर्षच्छेदन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षच्छेदक|शीर्षछेदक
शीर्षच्छेदक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Meriting decapitation.<BR> E. शीर्ष the head,<BR>च्छेद cutting, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षच्छेदिन्|शीर्षछेदिन्
शीर्षच्छेदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Who or what decapitates.<BR> E. शीर्ष, च्छेदिन्<BR>who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षच्छेद्य|शीर्षच्छेद्यः|शीर्षछेद्य
शीर्षच्छेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Meriting death by decapitation.<BR> E. शीर्ष the<BR>head, च्छेद्य to be cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षण्य|शीर्षण्यः
शीर्षण्य n. (-ण्यं) A helmet.<BR>	 m. (-ण्यः) Clean and unentangled hair. E.<BR>शीर्षन् substituted for शिरस्, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षरक्ष|शीर्षरक्षं
शीर्षरक्ष n. (-क्षं) A helmet.<BR> E. शीर्ष the head, and रक्ष preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील्
शील् r. 1st cl. (शीलति)<BR>	 1. To meditate, to consider, to reflect profoundly<BR>and abstractedly.<BR>	 2. To worship, to adore. r. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>(शीलति शीलयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To practise, to exercise, (as the memory,<BR>&c.)<BR>	 2. To repeat.<BR>	 3. To honour.<BR>	 4. To visit, to go to. r. 10th cl.<BR>(शीलयति)<BR>	 1. To wear.<BR>	 2. To have or be endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील|शीलः
शील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Possessed of, endowed with, practising, versed<BR>in, &c.)<BR>	 2. Behaviour, conduct.<BR>	 3. Well-behaved, well-disposed.<BR>mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. Nature, quality.<BR>	 2. Disposition, inclination.<BR>	 3.<BR>Good conduct or disposition, steady and uniform observance of<BR>law and morals.<BR>	 4. Beauty.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A large snake.<BR> E. शील् to me-<BR>ditate, to learn, &c., aff. अच्; or शी to sleep, and लक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलत्व
शीलत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Disposition, quality.<BR>	 2. Conversancy.<BR> E. शील, and त्व<BR>added; also with तल्, शीलता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलन|शीलनं
शीलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Careful study of the Śhāstras or sacred writings.<BR>	 2.<BR>Serving, honouring.<BR>	 3. Putting on.<BR> E. शील् to meditate, &c., aff.<BR>ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवत्|शीलवन्त्
शीलवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Of a good or amiable disposition.<BR> E. शील good conduct, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवृत्त
शीलवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Noral, steady and uniform in good behaviour.<BR>E. शील, वृत्त practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलसम्पन्न
शीलसम्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Well-conducted, of proper conduct or dispo-<BR>sition.<BR> E. शील, and सम्पन्न abounding with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलित|शीलितं
शीलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Skilled, learned, conversant, exercised.<BR>	 2.<BR>Having, endowed with.<BR>	 3. Made or consisting of.<BR>	 4. Visited. E.<BR>शील् to learn, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीवन्
शीवन् m. (-वा) A large snake, the Boa.<BR> E. शी to sleep, क्वनिप् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीवल|शीवलं
शीवल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR>	 2. Benzoin or Storax.<BR>E. शी to sleep, (on the water,) वलच् aff., and the vowel unchanged;<BR>also शीवाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंशुमार|शुंशुमारः
शुंशुमार m. (-रः) A porpoise; more usually शिशुमार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शु
शु Ind.<BR>	 1. Handsomely, brilliantly, elegantly.<BR>	 2. Well, right.<BR> E. शुभ्<BR>to be splendid, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्
शुक् r. 1st. cl. (शोकति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक|शुकं|शुकः
शुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A parrot.<BR>	 2. The son of VYĀSA, the author or narra-<BR>tor of the Bhāgavat.<BR>	 3. The minister of RĀVAṆA.<BR>	 4. The Sirisha<BR>tree.<BR>	 5. A plant, commonly Seyāla kāntā.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A drug<BR>and perfume, commonly Ganthiala.<BR>	 2. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 3. The ends<BR>or hem of a cloth.<BR>	 4. A turban, a helmet.<BR>	 5. A plant, (Bignonia<BR>Indica.)<BR> E. शुभ् to shine, कक् Unādi aff., and the radical final<BR>rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकच्छद|शुकच्छदं|शुकछद
शुकच्छद n. (-दं) A fragrant root, of which various kinds are said to be<BR>known.<BR> E. शुक a parrot, and च्छद a cover or wing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकजिह्वा
शुकजिह्वा f. (-ह्वा) A plant, commonly Sūyā-Thontee or parrot's beak.<BR>E. शुक a parrot, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकतरु|शुकतरुः
शुकतरु m. (-रुः) The Sirīṣa, (Acacia Sirisha.)<BR> E. शुक the same, and तरु tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकदेव|शुकदेवः
शुकदेव m. (-वः) The son of VYĀSA: see शुक,<BR> E. शुक, and देव divine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकद्रुम|शुकद्रुमः
शुकद्रुम m. (-मः) The Sirīṣa tree: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकनामा
शुकनामा f. (-मा) A plant; see शुकजिह्वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकनास|शुकनासः
शुकनास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>	 2. Another tree,<BR>(Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR> E. शुक, and नास the nose, the flowers being<BR>compared to a parrot's beak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकपितामह
शुकपितामह m. (-हः) The sage PARĀŚARA, the father of VYĀSA, and<BR>grandfather of ŚUKA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकपुच्छ|शुकपुच्छः
शुकपुच्छ m. (-च्छः) Sulphur.<BR> E. शुक a parrot, पुच्छ the tail; of similar colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकपुच्छक|शुकपुच्छकं
शुकपुच्छक n. (-कं) A perfume and medicinal root, commonly Gānthiāla.<BR>E. शुक a parrot, पुच्छ the tail, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकप्रिया
शुकप्रिया f. (-या) The rose-apple, (Eugenia jambu.)<BR> E. शुक a parrot, प्रिया beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकम्
शुकम् Ind. Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकवर्ह|शुकवर्हं
शुकवर्ह n. (-र्हं) Gānthiālā, a perfume.<BR> E. शुक a parrot, वर्ह a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकवल्लभ|शुकवल्लभः
शुकवल्लभ m. (-भः) The pomegranate.<BR> E. शुक a parrot, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकवाह|शुकवाहः
शुकवाह m. (-हः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. शुक a parrot, and वाह who is borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकादन|शुकादनः
शुकादन m. (-नः) The pomegranate.<BR> E. शुक a parrot, अदन eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकानना
शुकानना f. (-ना) A plant, commonly Sūyā-Thontee.<BR> E. शुक a parrot,<BR>आनन the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्त|शुक्तं
शुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Sour, acid.<BR>	 2. Pure, clean.<BR>	 3. Harsh, hard.<BR>	 4.<BR>Lovely.<BR>	 5. United, joined.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Flesh.<BR>	 2. Sour-gruel.<BR>	 3.<BR>Vinegar, acid, or an acid preparation made from roots or fruits,<BR>by steeping them in oil and salt, drying them, and then leaving<BR>them in water, where they undergo the acetous fermentation: the<BR>fluid produce is used as vinegar.<BR>	 4. Crabbed or harsh speech.<BR>	 5.<BR>A hymn of the Vedas.<BR>	 f. (-क्ता) A sort of sorrel.<BR> E. शुच् to be pure,<BR>&c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्ति|शुक्तिः
शुक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. A pearl-oyster.<BR>	 2. A conch.<BR>	 3. A small shell.<BR>	 4. A<BR>cockle.<BR>	 5. A sort of perfume, in appearance a dried shell-fish.<BR>	 6.<BR>A portion of the skull used as a cup, &c.<BR>	 7. A curl or feather on<BR>a horse's neck or breast.<BR>	 8. A weight of two Karṣas or half a<BR>Pala.<BR>	 9. A disease of the cornea, formation of specks on it.<BR> E. शुच्<BR>to sorrow, &c., aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिका
शुक्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A pearl-oyster.<BR>	 2. A sort of dock or sorrel.<BR> E. शुक्ति<BR>as above, or शुक्त sour, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिज|शुक्तिजं
शुक्तिज n. (-जं) A pearl.<BR> E. शुक्ति the oyster, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिपुट
शुक्तिपुट n. (-टं) The pearl oyster-shell.<BR> E. शुक्ति, पुट a bag or sheathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिपेशी
शुक्तिपेशी f. (-शी) The envelope of the pearl or pearl-oyster-shell.<BR> E. शुक्ति,<BR>and पेशी a covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिबधू
शुक्तिबधू f. (-धूः) Mother of pearl or the pearl oyster.<BR> E. शुक्ति, and बधू<BR>wife or female; in which the pearl, it is supposed, is bred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिमत्|शुक्तिमन्त्
शुक्तिमत् m. (-मान्) One of the seven principal mountains or mountainous<BR>ranges of India.<BR> E. शुक्ति a pearl-oyster, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिवीज
शुक्तिवीज n. (-जं) A pearl.<BR> E. शुक्ति the oyster, and वीज a seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिस्पर्श|शुक्तिस्पर्शः
शुक्तिस्पर्श m. (-र्शः) Dusky spots on a pearl, causing it to be of little<BR>value.<BR> E. शुक्ति a pearl, and स्पर्श contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्र|शुक्रं|शुक्रः
शुक्र m. (-क्रः)<BR>	 1. The planet VENUS or its regent, the son of BHRIGU,<BR>and preceptor of the Daityas or Titans.<BR>	 2. A name of fire.<BR>	 3. The<BR>month Jyeṣṭha, (April-May.)<BR>	 n. (-क्रं)<BR>	 1. Semen virile.<BR>	 2. The<BR>essence of anything.<BR>	 3. A morbid affection of the iris, change of<BR>colour, ulceration, &c. accompanied by imperfect vision.<BR> E. शुच् to<BR>grieve, &c., Unādi aff. रक्, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रकर|शुक्रकरः
शुक्रकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Producing semen, spermatic.<BR>	 m. (-रः) The marrow<BR>of the bones.<BR> E. शुक्र seed, and कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रभुज्
शुक्रभुज् m. (-भुक्) A peacock.<BR> E. शुक्र semen, भुज् to eat, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रभू
शुक्रभू f. (-भूः) The marrow of the bones.<BR> E. शुक्र semen, भू being, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रल
शुक्रल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Spermatic, augmenting the seminal secretion.<BR>	 f.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">Page724-a+ 60</a>]<BR>(-ला) A fragrant grass, considered by some as a sort of Cyperus,<BR>and by others, Zedoary.<BR> E. शुक्र semen, and लच् aff., or ला to get<BR>or give, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रवार|शुक्रवारः
शुक्रवार m. (-रः) Friday.<BR> E. शुक्र ŚUKRA, the regent of VENUS, or the planet, वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रशिष्य|शुक्रशिष्यः
शुक्रशिष्य m. (-ष्यः) A demon, a Titau, a powerful being opposed to the<BR>gods.<BR> E. शुक्र the teacher of this race, and शिष्य a pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रिय|शुक्रियः
शुक्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Sacred to ŚUKRA, &c.<BR> E. शुक्र as above, घन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्राचार्य्य|शुक्राचार्य
शुक्राचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) The regent of VENUS.<BR> E. शुक्र, and आचार्य्य teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्ल|शुक्लं|शुक्लः
शुक्ल mfn. (-क्लः-क्ला-क्लं) White, of a white colour.<BR>	 m. (-क्लः)<BR>	 1. White, (the<BR>colour.)<BR>	 2. The light-half of a lunar month: see शुक्लपक्ष.<BR>	 3. One of<BR>the astronomical Yogas.<BR>	 n. (-क्लं)<BR>	 1. Silver.<BR>	 2. Fresh butter.<BR>	 3. A<BR>disease of the cornea, opacity, albugo.<BR>	 4. Sour gruel.<BR>	 f. (-क्ला)<BR>	 1.<BR>A name of SARASWATI.<BR>	 2. Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>	 3. A woman<BR>with white complexion.<BR> E. शुच् to be pure, &c., Unādi aff. रन्, and<BR>र changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लक|शुक्लकः
शुक्लक f. (-का) White.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The white colour.<BR>	 2. The light-half of a lunar month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लकण्ठक|शुक्लकंठक|शुक्लकण्ठकः
शुक्लकण्ठक m. (-कः) A kind of gallinule or water-hen.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, कण्ठ<BR>the throat, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लकर्म्मन्|शुक्लकर्मन्
शुक्लकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Innocent, virtuous.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, pure, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लत्व|शुक्लत्वं
शुक्लत्व n. (-त्वं) Whiteness.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, त्व aff.; also with तल् aff. शुक्लता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लदुग्ध|शुक्लदुग्धः
शुक्लदुग्ध m. (-ग्धः) An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR> E. शुक्ल white,<BR>दुग्ध milk. “शृङ्गाटके ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लधातु|शुक्लधातुः
शुक्लधातु m. (-तुः) Chalk.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लपक्ष|शुक्लपक्षः
शुक्लपक्ष m. (-क्षः) The light-half of a month, the fifteen days of the<BR>moon's increase, or from new to full-moon.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, पक्ष part<BR>or fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लपुष्प|शुक्लपुष्पः
शुक्लपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. The white variety of Amaranth, (Gomphrœna<BR>globosa.)<BR>	 2. A species of jasmine, (Jasminum pubescens.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पा)<BR>1. A shrub, (Phrynium dichotomum.)<BR>	 2. A sort of sun-flower. E.<BR>शुक्ल white, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लपृष्ठक|शुक्लपृष्ठकः
शुक्लपृष्ठक m. (-कः) A small tree, (Vitex nigundo.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लबल|शुक्लबलः
शुक्लबल m. (-लः) A name common to nine persons peculiar to the<BR>Jainas.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, and बल a BALADEVA; there being nine white<BR>BALADEVAS, corresponding to the nine KṚṢṆAS, or black<BR>VĀSUDEVAS, according to the notions of this sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लमण्डल|शुक्लमण्डलं
शुक्लमण्डल n. (-लं) The white of the eye, the cornea.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, मण्डल<BR>a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लवर्ग|शुक्लवर्गः
शुक्लवर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. A class of white objects, or the conch, pearl-oyster<BR>and cowrie, &c.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लवायस|शुक्लवायसः
शुक्लवायस m. (-सः) A crane.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, and वायस a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लाङ्ग|शुक्लांग|शुक्लाङ्गः
शुक्लाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Having a white body or limbs.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) A pea-<BR>cock.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लापाङ्ग|शुक्लापांग|शुक्लापाङ्गः
शुक्लापाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A peacock.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, अपाङ्ग the corner of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लाम्ल|शुक्लाम्लं
शुक्लाम्ल n. (-म्लं) A kind of sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लिमन्
शुक्लिमन् m. (-मा) Whiteness.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लीकरण
शुक्लीकरण n. (-णं) Whitening, making white.<BR> E. शुक्ल, करण making, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लीकृत
शुक्लीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made white, whitened.<BR> E. शुक्ल, कृत made, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लोपला
शुक्लोपला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>	 2. Any white stone.<BR> E. शुक्ल<BR>white, and उपला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्षि|शुक्षिः
शुक्षि m. (-क्षिः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. Light.<BR> E. शुष् to dry up, Unādi aff. क्सि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुङ्ग|शुंग|शुंगः|शुङ्गः
शुङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The Indian-fig tree, (Ficus Indica.)<BR>	 2. The hog-plum,<BR>(Spondias mangifera.)<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>	 1. The sheath or calyx of a young<BR>bud.<BR>	 2. The waved-leaf fig.<BR>	 3. The awn of barley, &c.<BR> E. शम् to<BR>rest or pacify, aff. गच्; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुङ्गिन्|शुंगिन्
शुङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी) The Indian-fig tree.<BR> E. शुङ्ग the calyx of the bud, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
शुच् r. 1st cl. (शोचति) To regret, to grieve for. (ई, इर) ईशूचिर r. 4th cl.<BR>(शुच्यति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be wet.<BR>	 2. To be clean or pure.<BR>	 3. To stink, to be<BR>fetid.<BR>	 4. To wound.<BR>	 5. To regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
शुच् f. (-शुक्)<BR>	 1. Sorrow, grief, distress, regret.<BR>	 2. Calamity, affliction. E.<BR>शुच् to regret, aff. क्विप्; also with टाप् added, शुचा f. (-चा) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचा
शुचा f. (-चा) Sorrow, distress: see शुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचि|शुचिः
शुचि mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि)<BR>	 1. White.<BR>	 2. Clean, cleansed, purified.<BR>	 3. Pure,<BR>pious, exempt from passion or vice.<BR>	 4. Correct, free from fault<BR>or error.<BR>	 m. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. White, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. Purification by<BR>ablution, &c.<BR>	 3. Judicial acquittal.<BR>	 4. Mental purity, virtue,<BR>goodness.<BR>	 5. Accuracy, correctness.<BR>	 6. The condition of the reli-<BR>gious student.<BR>	 7. A faithful and tried minister or friend.<BR>	 8. The<BR>month Āshādha, (June-July.)<BR>	 9. The month Jyeṣṭha, (May-<BR>June.)<BR>	 10. The hot season.<BR>	 11. The passion or sentiment of love.<BR>12. ŚIVA.<BR>	 13. The sun.<BR>	 14. The moon.<BR>	 15. The planet VENUS, or<BR>its ruler.<BR>	 16. A name of fire.<BR>	 17. A Brāhman.<BR>	 18. Oblation to fire<BR>at the first feeding of an infant.<BR> E. शुच् to purify, Unādi aff. इन्,<BR>and the vowel unchanged; or शुच्-कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचित
शुचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sad, lamenting.<BR>	 2. Pure, clean, cleansed. E.<BR>शुच् to grieve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिता
शुचिता f. (-ता) Purity, cleanness.<BR> E. शुचि, तल् aff.; also with त्व, शुचित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिप्रणी
शुचिप्रणी f. (-णी) Sipping water, rinsing the mouth, &c.<BR> E. शुचि purifi-<BR>cation, and प्रणी effecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिमणि|शुचिमणिः
शुचिमणि m. (-णिः) Crystal.<BR> E. शुचि white, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिरोचिस्
शुचिरोचिस् m. (-चीः) The moon.<BR> E. शुचि white, and रोचिस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिव्रत
शुचिव्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pious, virtuous.<BR> E. शुचि, and व्रत observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिस्मित
शुचिस्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Smiled, smiling sweetly, accompanied with a<BR>sweet smile.<BR> E. शुचि white, (from the teeth being shown,) and स्मित<BR>smiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्य
शुच्य(इ)शुच्यी r. 1st cl. (शुच्यति)<BR>	 1. To bathe.<BR>	 2. To distil.<BR>	 3. To press<BR>or squeeze out.<BR>	 4. To churn.<BR>	 5. To pain or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीर|शुटीरः
शुटीर m. (-रः) A hero.<BR> E. शौटीर-पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीरता
शुटीरता f. (-ता) Valour, heroism.<BR> E. शौटीर a hero, तल् aff., and the diph-<BR>thong changed to the short vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीर्य्य|शुटीर्य|शुटीर्यं|शुटीर्य्यं
शुटीर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Heroism, prowess.<BR> E. शौटीर a hero, यत् aff.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुठ्
शुठ् r. 1st cl. (शोठति)<BR>	 1. To be impeded.<BR>	 2. To be lame.<BR>	 3. To resist.<BR>r. 10th cl. (शोठयति-ते) To be idle, to be lazy; also (इ) शुठि r. 1st<BR>and 10th cls. (शुण्ठति-शुण्ठयति-ते) To purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण
शुण r. 6th cl. (शुणति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठि|शुंठि|शुंठिः|शुण्ठिः
शुण्ठि f. (-ण्ठिः-ण्ठी) Dry ginger.<BR> E. शुठि to be stopped, (by it, phlegm,)<BR>aff. अच्, and fem. aff. ङीप्, or in one case इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठ्य|शुंठ्य
शुण्ठ्य n. (-ण्ठ्यं) Dry ginger.<BR> E. शुठि to be stopped, (disease by it,) and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ड|शुंड|शुंडः|शुण्डः
शुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The exudation from an elephant's temples.<BR>	 f. (-ण्डा)<BR>	 1. A<BR>tavern.<BR>	 2. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 3. A liquor-shop.<BR>	 4. An animal called<BR>the water-elephant, the hippopotamus perhaps.<BR>	 5. An elephant's<BR>proboscis or trunk.<BR>	 6. The stalk of the lotus.<BR>	 7. A whore.<BR>	 8. A<BR>bawd.<BR> E. शुण् to go, aff. ड, fem. aff. टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डक|शुंडक|शुंडकः|शुण्डकः
शुण्डक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A distiller.<BR>	 2. A military flute or fife.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डापान|शुंडापान|शुण्डापानं
शुण्डापान n. (-नं) A place where spirits are sold, a tavern, a dram-shop.<BR>E. शुण्डा spirits, and पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डार|शुंडार|शुंडारः|शुण्डारः
शुण्डार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A distiller, a vintner.<BR>	 2. An elephant's proboscis.<BR> E. शुण्डा spirits, र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डाल|शुंडाल|शुंडालः|शुण्डालः
शुण्डाल m. (-लः) An elephant.<BR> E. शुण्डा his trunk, लच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डिका|शुंडिका
शुण्डिका f. (-कां) The soft palate.<BR> E. शुण्डा an elephant's proboscis, कन्<BR>fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डिन्|शुंडिन्
शुण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1. A distiller, a preparer and vender of spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR> E. शुण्डा spirits, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्रि|शुतुद्रिः
शुतुद्रि f. (-द्रिः) The river Śatadru or Sutlej: see शतद्रु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्रु|शुतुद्रुः
शुतुद्रु f. (-द्रुः-द्रूः) The river Śatadru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्ध|शुद्धं|शुद्धः
शुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Pure, purified, clean, cleansed.<BR>	 2. Faultless,<BR>correct.<BR>	 3. Alone, only, mere, simple.<BR>	 4. White.<BR>	 5. Whetted,<BR>sharp, (as an arrow.)<BR>	 6. Authorised, admitted.<BR>	 7. Innocent.<BR>	 8.<BR>Acquitted.<BR>	 9. Bright.<BR>	 10. Honest, chaste.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Pure spirit.<BR>	 2.<BR>Rock-salt.<BR>	 3. Black pepper.<BR> E. शुध् to be or make pure, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धकोटि|शुद्धकोटिः
शुद्धकोटि f. (-टिः) One of the sides of a right-angled triangle.<BR> E. शुद्ध,<BR>and कोटि flank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धजङ्घ|शुद्धजंघ|शुद्धजङ्घः
शुद्धजङ्घ m. (-ङ्घः) An ass.<BR> E. शुद्ध clean, pure, and जङ्घा the thigh or leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धत्व
शुद्धत्व n. (-त्वं) Purity, cleanness, freedom from soil or defect.<BR> E. त्व added<BR>to शुद्ध; also with तल्, शुद्धता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धदत्|शुद्धदन्त्
शुद्धदत् mfn. (-दन् दन्ती-दत्) White-toothed, having handsome teeth.<BR> E. शुद्ध, दत् for दन्त tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धधी
शुद्धधी mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि) Of pure understanding.<BR> E. शुद्ध, धी intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धबध
शुद्धबध m. (-धः) Simple putting to death, i. e. in any ordinary way. E.<BR>शुद्ध, and बध putting to death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धमति|शुद्धमतिः
शुद्धमति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>	 1. Of pure or sincere purposes, honest, free<BR>from guile.<BR>	 2. Intelligent.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) One of the Jaina pontiffs of<BR>the last age.<BR> E. शुद्ध pure, मति understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धवर्ण
शुद्धवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Of a good colour, caste, &c.<BR>	 2. Well-lettered.<BR>E. शुद्ध, वर्ण colour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धवल्लिका
शुद्धवल्लिका f. (-का) A plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR> E. शुद्ध pure, वल्ली<BR>pedicle, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धवासस्
शुद्धवासस् mfn. (-साः-साः-सः) Clean, having clean vesture.<BR> E. शुद्ध, वासस् clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धानुमान
शुद्धानुमान n. (-नं) A figure of rhetoric.<BR> E. शुद्ध correct, अनुमान inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धान्त|शुद्धांत|शुद्धान्तः
शुद्धान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A seraglio, a Harem.<BR>	 2. The private or women's<BR>apartments in the palace of a prince.<BR>	 f. (-न्ता) The king's wife or<BR>concubine.<BR> E. शुद्ध pure, and अन्त end, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धान्तपालक|शुद्धांतपालक|शुद्धान्तपालकः
शुद्धान्तपालक m. (-कः) A eunuch or an attendant on the women's apart-<BR>ments.<BR> E. शुद्धान्त the Harem, and पालक a guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धान्तयुज्
शुद्धान्तयुज् f. (-युक्) Change of mode or key in music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धापह्नुति|शुद्धापह्नुतिः
शुद्धापह्नुति f. (-तिः) A figure of rhetoric.<BR> E. शुद्ध correct, अपह्नुति concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धि|शुद्धिः
शुद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Cleaning, cleansing.<BR>	 2. Purity, purification.<BR>	 3. Correc-<BR>tion, correctness.<BR>	 4. Innocence established by ordeal or trial,<BR>acquittal.<BR>	 5. Paying off arrears.<BR>	 6. Subtraction.<BR>	 7. Brightness.<BR>	 8.<BR>An expiation.<BR>	 9. DURGĀ.<BR> E. शुध् to be or make pure, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धिभृत्
शुद्धिभृत् mfn. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. Clean, clear, free from soil.<BR>	 2. Pure, virtuous. E.<BR>शुद्धि, भृत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धोदन
शुद्धोदन m. (-नः) King of KAPILA and father of SĀKYA.<BR> E. शुद्ध, ओदन rice, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धोदनसुत|शुद्धोदनसुतः
शुद्धोदनसुत m. (-तः) SĀKYA, the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR> E. शुद्धोदन<BR>the father of this personage, and सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुध्
शुध्(ओ, ऌ)ओशुधॢ r. 4th cl. (शुध्यति)<BR>	 1. To be or become pure or puri-<BR>fied.<BR>	 2. To be made clear, to have doubts removed. With परि, वि,<BR>or सम्, To be purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्
शुन् r. 6th cl. (शुनति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन|शुनः
शुन m. (-नः) A dog.<BR> E. शुण् to go, क aff.: see शुनि, श्वन्, &c.; also with कन् added शुनक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनाशोर
शुनाशोर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. An owl.<BR> E. सु good, venerable, नासीर van<BR>of his army; the स in each case changed; also शुनासीर, and more<BR>correctly, सुनासीर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनि|शुनिः
शुनि m. (-निः) A dog.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A bitch.<BR> E. शुण् to go, इक aff.; or श्वन्<BR>with ङीष् aff., and the semi-vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनिन्धय|शुनिंधय
शुनिन्धय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Suckled by a bitch.<BR> E. शुनी, धे to suck, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनीर|शुनीरः
शुनीर m. (-रः) A number of female dogs.<BR> E. शुनी, र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्ध्|शुंध्
शुन्ध् r. 1st and 10th cls. (शुन्धति-ते शुन्धयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be or become pure.<BR>2. To cleanse, to purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्ध्यु|शुंध्युः|शुन्ध्युः
शुन्ध्यु m. (-न्ध्युः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR> E. शुधि to purify, चुश् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्य|शुन्यं
शुन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Empty, void.<BR>	 n. (-न्यं)<BR>	 1. A number of dogs.<BR>	 2. A<BR>cipher.<BR> E. श्वन् a dog, and वत् aff., the vowel substituted for the<BR>semi-vowel; more commonly शून्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्
शुभ् r. 1st cl. (शोभते)<BR>	 1. To look beautiful.<BR>	 2. To appear to advantage.<BR>3. To shine. r. 6th cl. (शुम्भति)<BR>	 1. To hurt or injure, to kill.<BR>	 2. To<BR>look beautiful.<BR>	 3. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ|शुभं|शुभः
शुभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. Happy, well, right, fortunate, auspicious.<BR>	 2.<BR>Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 3. Splendid, shining.<BR>	 4. Eminent, distin-<BR>guished.<BR>	 5. Learned, versed in the Vedas, &c.<BR>	 n. (-भं)<BR>	 1. Good,<BR>good fortune, auspiciousness, happiness.<BR>	 2. An ornament.<BR>	 3. A<BR>particular fragrant wood.<BR>	 m. (-भः) One of the astrological Yogas.<BR>f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. An assemblage of the gods.<BR>	 2. A female friend and<BR>companion of the goddess UMĀ.<BR>	 3. Bamboo-manna.<BR>	 4. Bent<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">Page725-b+ 60</a>]<BR>grass.<BR>	 5. The Śami tree.<BR>	 6. A yellow pigment: see गोरोचना.<BR>	 7.<BR>Light, lustre.<BR>	 8. Beauty.<BR>	 9. Desire.<BR> E. शुभ् to shine, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंयु|शुभंयुः
शुभंयु mfn. (-युः-युः-यु) Happy, fortunate, prosperous.<BR> E. शुभं happy, युस्<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभकर
शुभकर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Propitious, producing good, &c.<BR> E. शुभ, and<BR>कर what makes: also शुभङ्कर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभकर्म्मन्|शुभकर्मन्
शुभकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Pious or virtuous act.<BR>	 2. Reputable occupation or<BR>employment.<BR> E. शुभ, and कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभग
शुभग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Elegant, graceful.<BR>	 2. Fortunate, propitious.<BR>E. शुभ, and गम् to go or obtain, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभगन्धक|शुभगंधक|शुभगन्धकं
शुभगन्धक n. (-कं) Gum-myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभङ्कर|शुभंकर|शुभङ्करः
शुभङ्कर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Propitious, auspicious, conferring happiness or<BR>fortune.<BR>	 f. (-री) PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. शुभ happiness, कृ to make, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभद|शुभदः
शुभद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Propitious, auspicious.<BR> E. शुभ, द who or what gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभदन्ती|शुभदंती
शुभदन्ती f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. The female elephant of the N. W. quarter.<BR>	 2. A<BR>woman with good teeth.<BR> E. शुभ handsome, दन्त tooth, ङीप् aff.; else-<BR>where read शुभ्रदन्ती ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभफल
शुभफल n. (-लं) Happy result or consequence.<BR> E. शुभ, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभलग्न|शुभलग्नः
शुभलग्न m. (-ग्नः) An auspicious moment.<BR> E. शुभ, and लग्न rise of a planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभवासन|शुभवासनः
शुभवासन m. (-नः) Perfume for the mouth.<BR> E. शुभ, वासन perfuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभशील
शुभशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Of a good disposition.<BR> E. शुभ, शील disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभस्थली
शुभस्थली f. (-ली) A room or hall in which sacrifices are offered.<BR> E. शुभ<BR>auspicious, and स्थल place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाङ्ग
शुभाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Handsome, elegant.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. The wife of<BR>KĀMA.<BR>	 2. The wife of KUVERA.<BR>	 3. A handsome woman.<BR> E. शुभ<BR>handsome, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाचार
शुभाचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Virtuous.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A female attendant on UMĀ.<BR> E. शुभ, आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाञ्जन|शुभाञ्जनः
शुभाञ्जन m. (-नः) A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga:) see शोभाञ्जन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभानन
शुभानन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Handsome, good-looking.<BR>	 f. (-ना) A handsome<BR>woman.<BR> E. शुभ, and आनन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभान्वित|शुभान्वितः
शुभान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Happy, prosperous, fortunate.<BR> E. शुभ good<BR>fortune, and अन्वित endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभापाङ्गा|शुभापांगा
शुभापाङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) A beautiful woman.<BR> E. शुभ, and अपाङ्ग the corner of<BR>the eye, for the eye or face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाशुभ
शुभाशुभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Prosperous and unfortunate, good and evil.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-भं) Good and ill-fortune.<BR> E. शुभ, अशुभ unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभेतर
शुभेतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Unlucky, inauspicious.<BR>	 2. Evil, bad.<BR> E. शुभ, इतर other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्र|शुभ्रं|शुभ्रः
शुभ्र mfn. (-भ्रः-भ्रा-भ्रं)<BR>	 1. White.<BR>	 2. Shining.<BR>	 m. (-भ्रः)<BR>	 1. White, (the<BR>colour.)<BR>	 2. Sandal.<BR>	 n. (-भ्रं)<BR>	 1. Talc.<BR>	 2. Silver.<BR>	 3. Green vitriol.<BR>	 4.<BR>Rock-salt.<BR>	 5. Sandal.<BR>	 f. (-भ्रा)<BR>	 1. The Ganges.<BR>	 2. Crystal.<BR>	 3.<BR>Bamboo-manna.<BR> E. शुभ् to shine, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रकृत्
शुभ्रकृत् m. (-कृत्) The thirty-sixth year of the Indian cycle.<BR> E. शुभ्र<BR>white, कृत् making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रदन्ती
शुभ्रदन्ती f. (-न्ती) The female elephant of the north-west quarter.<BR> E. शुभ्र white, दन्त a tusk, ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्ररश्मि|शुभ्ररश्मिः
शुभ्ररश्मि m. (-श्मिः) The moon.<BR> E. शुभ्र white, and रश्मि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रांशु|शुभ्रांशुः
शुभ्रांशु m. (-शुः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. शुभ्र white, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रि|शुभ्रिः
शुभ्रि m. (-भ्रिः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. शुभ् to be propitious, क्रिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भ्|शुंभ्
शुम्भ् r. 6th cl. (शुम्भति)<BR>	 1. To shine, to be splendid or beautiful.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be handsome.<BR>	 3. To hurt or injure.<BR>	 4. To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भ|शुंभ|शुंभः|शुम्भः
शुम्भ m. (-म्भः) An Asura or demon slain by DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भघातिनी|शुंभघातिनी
शुम्भघातिनी f. (-नी) DURGĀ.<BR> E. शुम्भ the Asura, and घातिनी destructress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भपुर|शुम्भपुरं
शुम्भपुर nf. (-रं-री) A city and district, perhaps the modern Sambhalpūr,<BR>in the district of Gondwāna.<BR> E. शुम्भ the Asura, and पुर city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भमर्द्दिनी|शुम्भमर्दिनी|शुंभमर्दिनी
शुम्भमर्द्दिनी f. (-नी) DURGĀ.<BR> E. शुम्भ the Asura, and मर्द्दिनी destructress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुर्
शुर्(ई)शुरी r. 4th cl. (शूर्य्यते)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to kill.<BR>	 2. To make firm.<BR>	 3.<BR>To be stupid or insensible; also शूर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुर
शुर m. (-रः) A lion.<BR> E. शुर् to injure, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्क्
शुल्क् r. 10th cl. (शुल्कयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To gain or acquire.<BR>	 3. To<BR>create.<BR>	 4. To abandon, to leave or forsake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्क|शुल्कं|शुल्कः
शुल्क mn. (-ल्कः-ल्कं)<BR>	 1. Toll, duty, customs or taxes.<BR>	 2. The present<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">Page726-a+ 60</a>]<BR>made by the bridegroom to the bride, at the time of bringing her<BR>home to his family; a marriage settlement or dower.<BR>	 3. Money<BR>given to the parents of the bride.<BR>	 4. Money given at the purchase<BR>of any thing to ratify the bargain.<BR>	 5. The profits of household<BR>labour, employment of domestic utensils, care of milch-cattle,<BR>preservation of ornaments, superintendance of servants, &c., when<BR>considered as the perquisite of the wife and her own legal property.<BR>E. शुल्क् to quit, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=725-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्कस्थान
शुल्कस्थान n. (-नं) Any object of taxation or duty.<BR> E. शुल्क, स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्कहानि
शुल्कहानि f. (-निः) Loss or forfeiture of wages, dower, &c.<BR> E. शुल्क,<BR>हानि privation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्ल|शुल्लं
शुल्ल n. (-ल्लं)<BR>	 1. A cord, a rope or string.<BR>	 2. Copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्व्
शुल्व् r. 10th cl. (शुल्वयति ते)<BR>	 1. To measure.<BR>	 2. To create.<BR>	 3. To give.<BR>	 4. To dismiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्व|शुल्वं
शुल्व Subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-ल्वः-ल्वा or ल्वी-ल्वं) A rope, a cord, a string.<BR>	 n. (-ल्वं)<BR>1. Copper.<BR>	 2. A sacrificial observance.<BR>	 3. An institute, a law.<BR>4. A place near water.<BR>	 5. A rope.<BR> E. शुल्व् to measure, aff. अच्; or<BR>शुध् to be pure, &c., Unādi aff. वन्, and ध changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्वज
शुल्वज n. (-जं) Brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्वारि|शुल्वारिः
शुल्वारि m. (-रिः) Sulphur.<BR> E. शुल्व copper, and अरि a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुशुमा
शुशुमा f. (-मा) The wife of ŚUKRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रवस्
शुश्रवस् mfn. (-वान्-श्रुषी-वः) Heard, having heard.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, aff. क्वसु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूष
शुश्रूष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Obedient, serving, attending.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, desid.<BR>v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषक|शुश्रूषकः
शुश्रूषक m. (-कः) A servant, comprehending five descriptions of per-<BR>sons, a pupil, a religious pupil or the member of a religious com-<BR>munity, under a common head, a hired servant, an officer or<BR>deputy, and a slave.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, desid. v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषण|शुश्रूषणं
शुश्रूषण n. (-णं) Service, serving.<BR>	 f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Desire to hear.<BR>	 2. Obedience.<BR>3. Service, attendance.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, desiderative form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषा
शुश्रूषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Service, serving of five kinds: see शुश्रूषक.<BR>	 2. Saying,<BR>speaking, telling.<BR>	 3. Wishing to hear.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, desiderative<BR>form, अच aff., fem. aff. ठाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषापर
शुश्रूषापर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Diligent or attentive in service.<BR> E. शुश्रूषा, and<BR>पर intent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्
शुष्(औ, ॡ)औशुषॣ r. 4th cl. (शुष्यति)<BR>	 1. To dry.<BR>	 2. To be withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष|शुषः
शुष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Drying.<BR>	 2. A hole in the ground.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषि|शुषिः
शुषि f. (-षिः-षी)<BR>	 1. A hole, a chasm.<BR>	 2. Drying.<BR>	 3. The hollow or<BR>groove in the fang of a snake.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिर|शुषिरं|शुषिरः
शुषिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Perforated, bored, pierced, full of holes or spaces.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A hole, a vacuity, a chasm.<BR>	 2. A wind-instrument.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-रः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. A rat.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. A sort of perfume, commonly<BR>Nali.<BR>	 2. A river in general.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, Unādi aff. किरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिल|शुषिलः
शुषिल m. (-लः) Air wind.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, किरच् aff., and the semi-vowel<BR>changed to ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्क|शुष्कः
शुष्क mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं)<BR>	 1. Dry, dried.<BR>	 2. Groundless, causeless.<BR>	 3. Unpro-<BR>ductive, unprofitable.<BR>	 4. Emaciated, withered.<BR>	 5. Feigned.<BR>	 6.<BR>Offensive.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, aff. क्त, or Unādi aff. कक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कता
शुष्कता f. (-ता) Dryness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, शुष्कत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कमांस|शुष्कमांसं
शुष्कमांस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Dry flesh.<BR>	 2. Dried meat.<BR> E. शुष्क dry, मांस flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कल|शुष्कलं|शुष्कलः
शुष्कल mfn. subst. (-लः-ला or ली-लं) Dry flesh. Adj. Eating fish and flesh.<BR>E. शुष् to dry, कलच् Unādi aff.; or शुष्क, and ला to take, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कवैर
शुष्कवैर n. (-रं) Groundless enmity.<BR> E. शुष्क, and वैर enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कव्रण|शुष्कव्रणः
शुष्कव्रण m. (-णः) A scar, a cicatrised sore.<BR> E. शुष्क dry, व्रण a sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्काङ्ग|शुष्काङ्गः
शुष्काङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Emaciated, withered.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी) A lizard, a<BR>chameleon.<BR> E. शुष्क dry, अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कान्न
शुष्कान्न n. (-न्नं) Rice in the husk.<BR> E. शुष्क, and अन्न rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कार्द्र|शुष्कार्द्रं
शुष्कार्द्र n. (-र्द्रं) Dry ginger.<BR> E. शुष्क dry, and आर्द्र ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्ण|शुष्णः
शुष्ण m. (-ष्णः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, न Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्म|शुष्मं|शुष्मः
शुष्म m. (-ष्मः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. Air, wind.<BR>	 4. A bird.<BR>	 n. (-ष्मं)<BR>1. Light, lustre.<BR>	 2. Strength, prowess.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, मन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्मन्
शुष्मन् m. (-ष्मा) Fire.<BR>	 n. (-ष्म)<BR>	 1. Light, lustre.<BR>	 2. Strength, prowess. E.<BR>शुष् to dry, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्यत्
शुष्यत् mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्) Drying.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूक|शूकं|शूकः
शूक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. The awn of barley, &c.<BR>	 2. A bristle, a spiculæ.<BR>	 3.<BR>Compassion, clemency, tenderness.<BR>	 4. Top, point.<BR>	 5. A kind of<BR>poisonous insect.<BR>	 f. (-का) Cowach.<BR> E. शो to make sharp or thin,<BR>ऊक aff., deriv. irr.; or श्वि-कक्-सम्प्र० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकक|शूककः
शूकक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Barley, or bearded kind of wheat resembling it.<BR>	 2. The<BR>sentiment of compassion or tenderness.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूककीट|शूककीटः
शूककीट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A caterpillar.<BR>	 2. A worm that eats holes in clothes.<BR>E. शूक a bristle, (the hairs on the insect,) and कीट a worm; also<BR>with कन् added शूककीटक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकतृण|शूकतृणं
शूकतृण n. (-णं) A kind of grass.<BR> E. शूक an awn, तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकधान्य|शूकधान्यं
शूकधान्य n. (-न्यं) Awned or bearded grain, as barley, &c.<BR> E. शूक an awn,<BR>धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकपिण्डि|शूकपिंडि|शूकपिण्डिः
शूकपिण्डि f. (-ण्डिः-ण्डी) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. शूक an awn, पिण्डि a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकर|शूकरः
शूकर m. (-रः) A hog.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A kind of moss, (Lycopodium inbrica-<BR>tum.)<BR>	 2. A sow.<BR> E. शूक an awn, (a bristle,) र aff.; or शू imitative<BR>sound, कृ to make, with अच् and ठाप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकराक्रान्ता
शूकराक्रान्ता f. (-न्ता) A kind of moss, &c.: see the last; also वराहक्रान्ता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकल|शूकलः
शूकल m. (-लः) A restive horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकवत्|शूकवन्त्
शूकवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Awned, bearded.<BR>	 f. (-ती) Cowach.<BR> E. शूक an awn, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकशिम्बा|शूकशिंबा
शूकशिम्बा f. (-म्बा) Cowach.<BR> E. शूक an awn, and शिम्बा a pod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकशिम्बि|शूकशिम्बिः
शूकशिम्बि f. (-म्बिः-म्बी) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. शूक an awn,<BR>and शिम्बि a pod; also with कन् added शूकशिम्बिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकापूट्ट|शूकापूट्टः
शूकापूट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A gem, perhaps amber.<BR> E. शूक an awn, आङ् before पट्ट्<BR>to become small, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकिन्
शूकिन् mfn. (-की-किनी-कि) Awned, bearded, (as grain.)<BR> E. शूक, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकुल
शूकुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A fish in general.<BR>	 2. A kind of fish.<BR>	 3. A fragrant<BR>grass, (Cyperus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूक्ष्म|शूक्ष्मं|शूक्ष्मः
शूक्ष्म mfn. (-क्ष्मः-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मं) Minute, small, fine, subtile.<BR>	 m. (-क्ष्मः)<BR>	 1. Fraud,<BR>dishonesty.<BR>	 2. Universal spirit.<BR> E. स substituted for श in the more<BR>correct form सूक्ष्म, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्र|शूद्रः
शूद्र m. (-द्रः) A man of the fourth or servile tribe, said to have sprung<BR>from the feet of BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 f. (-द्रा) A woman of the Śūdra tribe.<BR>f. (-द्री or द्राणी) The wife of Śūdra.<BR> E. शुच् to purify or cleanse,<BR>Uṇadi aff. रक्, the vowel made long, and च changed to द ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रता
शूद्रता f. (-ता) The nature or condition of a Śūdra.<BR> E. शूद्र and तल् aff.;<BR>also with त्व, शूद्रत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रधर्म्म|शूद्रधर्म|शूद्रधर्म्मः
शूद्रधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) The duty of the Śūdra tribe, the service of the other<BR>three.<BR> E. शूद्र a Śūdra, and धर्म्म moral merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रप्रेष्य|शूद्रप्रेष्यः
शूद्रप्रेष्य m. (-ष्यः) A man of the three first classes, who has become a<BR>servant to one of the fourth.<BR> E. शूद्र a Śūdra. and प्रेष्य a slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रभिक्षित
शूद्रभिक्षित n. (-तं) Alms begged or received from a Śūdra.<BR> E. शूद्र, and<BR>भिक्षित begged as alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रभूयिष्ठ
शूद्रभूयिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Abounding with Śūdra.<BR> E. शूद्र, भूयिष्ठ many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रयाजक|शूद्रयाजकः
शूद्रयाजक m. (-कः) A priest who conducts sacrifices for Śūdras.<BR> E. शूद्र,<BR>and याजक sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रराज्य
शूद्रराज्य n. (-ज्यं) A country of which a Śūdra is king.<BR> E. शूद्र, and राज्य<BR>kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रवृत्ति|शूद्रवृत्तिः
शूद्रवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) The duty or occupation of a Śūdra.<BR> E. शूद्र, and वृत्ति employment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रशासन|शूद्रशासनं
शूद्रशासन n. (-नं) An edict or grant, &c., addressed to persons of the<BR>servile caste.<BR> E. शूद्र a Śūdra, शासन edict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रापरिणयन
शूद्रापरिणयन n. (-नं) Marrying a Śūdra female.<BR> E. शूद्रा, परिणयन marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रापुत्त्र
शूद्रापुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) The son of any man by a Śūdra woman.<BR> E. शूद्रा, and<BR>पुत्त्र son; also शूद्रासुतः, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्राभार्य्य|शूद्राभार्य|शूद्राभार्यः|शूद्राभार्य्यः
शूद्राभार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) The husband of a Śūdra woman.<BR> E. शूद्रा Śūdrawoman, and भार्य्या a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रार्त्ता|शूद्रार्ता
शूद्रार्त्ता f. (-र्त्ता) A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR> E. शूद्र a Śūdra, and आर्त्त<BR>pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रावेदन
शूद्रावेदन n. (-नं) Marrying a woman of the fourth class.<BR> E. शूद्रा, and आवेदन marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रावेदिन्
शूद्रावेदिन् m. (-दी) A man of the three first classes, who has a Śūdra<BR>wife.<BR> E. शूद्रा, and आवेदिन् who marries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून|शूनः
शून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Swelled, increased, grown.<BR>	 2. Morbidly swollen.<BR>f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A shambles, a slaughter-house.<BR>	 2. The soft palate.<BR>	 3. A<BR>piece of house-hold furniture which destroys animal life. viz:--<BR>“पञ्च शुना गृहस्थस्य चुल्लीपेषण्युपस्करः ।<BR>कण्डनीचोदकुम्भश्च बध्यते यास्तुवाहयन् ॥”<BR>E. श्वि to increase, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूनावत्
शूनावत् m. (-वान्) A butcher, one who keeps a place where animals are<BR>killed for sale.<BR> E. शूना a shambles, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्य|शून्यं|शून्यः
शून्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Empty, void.<BR>	 2. Lonely, desert.<BR>	 3. Vacant.<BR>	 4.<BR>Devoid of.<BR>	 5. Indifferent.<BR>	 6. Guileless.<BR>	 7. Absent-minded.<BR>	 8. Non-<BR>sensical.<BR>	 9. Naked, bare.<BR>	 n. (-न्यं)<BR>	 1. Heaven, sky, æther.<BR>	 2. A<BR>dot, a spot.<BR>	 3. A cipher.<BR>	 4. A vacuum.<BR>	 5. Non-entity.<BR>	 f. (-न्या)<BR>	 1. A<BR>hollow reed.<BR>	 2. The prickly-pear.<BR>	 3. A barren woman.<BR> E. शुन a dog,<BR>यत aff. of fitness, and the vowel substituted for the semi-vowel,<BR>and made optionally long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यगेह
शून्यगेह n. (-हं) An empty or deserted house.<BR> E. शून्य, and गेह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यत्व
शून्यत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Vacuity, emptiness.<BR>	 2. Unreality, the false or<BR>illusory nature of all existence.<BR> E. त्व added to शून्य; with तल्, शून्यता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यमध्य|शून्यमध्यः
शून्यमध्य m. (-ध्यः) A hollow reed.<BR> E. शून्य empty, and मध्य the middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यमुख
शून्यमुख Adj. Pale-faced, having a dejected countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यवादिन्
शून्यवादिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A Bauddha.<BR>	 2. An atheist.<BR> E. शून्य vacuum, and<BR>वादिन् declaring; denying the existence of any thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यस्थान
शून्यस्थान n. (-नं) An empty place.<BR> E. शून्य, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्यहस्त
शून्यहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Empty-handed.<BR> E. शून्य, हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूयमान
शूयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Swelling, enlarging, expanding.<BR> E. श्वि to swell, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर|शूरः
शूर r. 10th cl. (शूरयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be valiant or powerful, to act the hero.<BR>2. To make great effort or exertion. (ई) शूरी r. 4th cl. (शूर्य्यते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To be stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर|शूरः
शूर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A hero.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. A lion.<BR>	 4. A boar.<BR>	 5. The grand-<BR>father of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 6. The Śal tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>Brave, mighty.<BR> E. शु to bear, Sautra root, Unādi aff. क्रन्, and<BR>the vowel made long; or शूर् to be brave, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरकीट|शूरकीटः
शूरकीट m. (-टः) A contemptible warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरण|शूरणः
शूरण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. An esculent root, (Arum campanulatum, Rox.) “ओल.”<BR>2. A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. शूरी to hurt, (some diseases,)<BR>aff. युच्; or शूर्-ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरणोद्भुज|शूरणोद्भुजः
शूरणोद्भुज m. (-जः) A kind of bird.<BR> E. शूरण the Arum, and उद् before भुज् to eat, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरता
शूरता f. (-ता) Heroism, prowess.<BR> E. तल् added to शूर; also with त्व, शूरत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरदेव|शूरदेवः
शूरदेव m. (-वः) The second Jaina of the future era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरमान
शूरमान n. (-नं) Vaunting, pride of prowess.<BR> E. शूर, and मान pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरमानिन्
शूरमानिन् m. (-नी) A boaster, one who thinks himself a hero.<BR> E. शूर,<BR>मन् to think, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरम्मन्य|शूरंमन्य
शूरम्मन्य m. (-न्यः) A boaster, one who thinks himself a hero.<BR> E. शूर, मन् to think, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरसेन|शूरसेनः
शूरसेन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The country about Mathurā.<BR>	 2. The name of a<BR>prince.<BR> E. शूर a hero, सेना an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्
शूर्प् r. 10th cl. (शूर्पयति-ते) To mete or measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्प|शूर्प|शूर्पं|शूर्पः
शूर्प्प mn. (-र्प्पः-र्प्पं)<BR>	 1. A winnowing basket.<BR>	 2. A measure of two<BR>Dronās.<BR>	 f. (-र्प्पी)<BR>	 1. A small kind of winnowing basket, a toy for<BR>children.<BR>	 2. The sister of RĀVAṆA: see शूर्प्पनखा.<BR> E. शॄ to injure,<BR>Unādi aff. प, and ऊ substituted for the vowel; or शूर्प्-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पक|शूर्पक|शूर्पकः
शूर्प्पक m. (-कः) A demon, the enemy of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. शूर्प्प् to<BR>measure, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पकर्ण|शूर्पकर्ण|शूर्पकर्णः
शूर्प्पकर्ण m. (-र्णः) An elephant.<BR> E. शूर्प्प a winnowing basket, कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पकाराति|शूर्पकाराति|शूर्पकारातिः
शूर्प्पकाराति m. (-तिः) KĀMA or CUPID.<BR> E. शूर्प्पक a demon, and अराति an<BR>enemy; also शूर्प्पकारि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पणखा|शूर्पणखा
शूर्प्पणखा f. (-खा) The sister of the Daitya RĀVAṆA.<BR> E. शूर्प्प a winnow-<BR>ing basket, and नख a fingernail, (having them as large,) fem. aff.<BR>टाप् or ङीप्, whence also शूर्प्पणखी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पनिष्पाव|शूर्पनिष्पाव
शूर्प्पनिष्पाव m. (-वः) A measure (a basket) of winnowed corn.<BR> E. शूर्प्प,<BR>निष्पाव winnowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पपर्णी|शूर्पपर्णी
शूर्प्पपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A sort of bean, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पवात|शूर्पवात|शूर्पवातः
शूर्प्पवात m. (-तः) The air as agitated by the shaking of the winnowing<BR>basket.<BR> E. शूर्प्प a basket, वात wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्पश्रुति|शूर्पश्रुति|शूर्पश्रुतिः
शूर्प्पश्रुति f. (-तिः) An elephant.<BR> E. शूर्प्प winnowing basket, श्रुति an ear; as large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्म्म|शूर्म|शूर्मः|शूर्म्मः
शूर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) An iron image, &c., also सूर्म्मः see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्म्मि|शूर्मि|शूर्मिः|शूर्म्मिः
शूर्म्मि mf. (-र्म्मिः-र्म्मी)<BR>	 1. An iron image.<BR>	 2. An anvil.<BR> E. शु for शोभा beauty,<BR>and ऊर्म्मि a wave or line, ङीष् optionally added; deriv. irr.; also<BR>with इ rejected, and कन् added, fem. form शूर्म्मिका; again, as<BR>differently read, सूर्म्मि, स्युर्म्मि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल्
शूल् r. 1st cl. (शूलति)<BR>	 1. To disorder, to distemper or disease.<BR>	 2. To<BR>make a loud noise.<BR>	 3. To impale, to transfix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल|शूलं|शूलः
शूल mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. Sharp pain in general, or especially in the belly,<BR>as colic, &c., or in the joints, from rheumatism or gout.<BR>	 2. A<BR>weapon, a pike, a dart.<BR>	 3. An iron pin or spit.<BR>	 4. A banner, an<BR>ensign.<BR>	 5. An astrological Yoga, that of the 9th lunar mansion.<BR>6. Death, dying.<BR>	 7. A stake for impaling criminals.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A<BR>whore.<BR>	 2. An instrument used for putting criminals to death, a<BR>stake for impaling them.<BR> E. शूल् to disease, &c., aff. अच् or क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलक|शूलकः
शूलक m. (-कः) A restive horse.<BR> E. शूल् to distress, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलघातन|शूलघातनं
शूलघातन n. (-नं) Iron rust or filings.<BR> E. शूल pain, घातन what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलघ्न|शूलघ्नः
शूलघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Removing or allaying sharp pain, sedative,<BR>anodyne.<BR> E. शूल, and घ्न what destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलधन्वन्
शूलधन्वन् m. (-न्वा) ŚIVA.<BR> E. शूल a pike or the three-pronged one, the<BR>trident of this deity, धन्वन् a bow, put for a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलधर|शूलधरः
शूलधर m. (-रः) ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-रा) DURGĀ.<BR> E. शूल a pike or trident, धर who holds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलधृष्
शूलधृष् f. (-धृक्) DURGĀ.<BR> E. शूल a trident, and धृष् to be bold, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलनाशन|शूलनाशनं
शूलनाशन n. (-नं) White Sachal-salt.<BR> E. शूल colic, and नाशन removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलशत्रु|शूलशत्रुः
शूलशत्रु m. (-त्रुः) The castor-oil plant, (Ricinus communis.)<BR> E. शूल<BR>colic, शत्रु hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलहस्त|शूलहस्तः
शूलहस्त m. (-स्तः) One armed with a lance or pike.<BR> E. शूल, हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलहृत्
शूलहृत् m. (-हृत्) Asafœtida.<BR> E. शूल colic, and हृत् removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलाकृत|शूलाकृतं
शूलाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Roasted on a spit, (meat.)<BR> E. शूल a spit, and<BR>कृत made, with डाच् augment; spitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलाग्र
शूलाग्र n. (-ग्रं) The point of a pike, stake, &c.<BR> E. शूल, and अग्र end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिक|शूलिकं|शूलिकः
शूलिक n. (-कं) Roast meat.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A hare.<BR> E. शूल a spit, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिन्
शूलिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि)<BR>	 1. Suffering sharp pain, having the colic, &c.<BR>2. Armed with a spear.<BR>	 m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. MAHĀDEVA.<BR>	 2. A spearman.<BR>	 3.<BR>A stake-bearer.<BR>	 4. A hare.<BR> E. शूल a trident, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिन|शूलिनः
शूलिन m. (-नः) The Indian-fig tree.<BR> E. शूल a stake, इनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलोत्खा
शूलोत्खा f. (-त्खा) A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.) “सोमराज्यां ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल्य|शूल्यं
शूल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Roasted, (on a spit.)<BR>	 2. Deserving impale-<BR>ment.<BR>	 n. (-ल्यं) Roasted meat.<BR> E. शूल a spit, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूष्
शूष् r. 1st. cl. (शूषति)<BR>	 1. To bring forth, to propagate.<BR>	 2. To beget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृकाल|शृकालः
शृकाल m. (-लः) A jackal: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगाल|शृगालः
शृगाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A shakal or jackal.<BR>	 2. A coward, a poltroon.<BR>	 3. A<BR>rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 4. An ill-natured or harsh-speaking man.<BR>	 5. A<BR>demon so named.<BR>	 6. KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Flight, retreat.<BR>	 2. A fox.<BR>3. A she-jackal.<BR> E. सृज् to create or abandon, (deceit, &c.) कालन्<BR>aff.; or शृङ्ग a horn, अ negative prefix, ला to possess, aff. क, deriv.<BR>irr.; also सृगाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालकण्टक|शृगालकण्टकः
शृगालकण्टक m. (-कः) A plant, commonly. Seyāla-kāṇṭā or jackal's<BR>thorn, (Zizyphus scandens.)<BR> E. शृगाल, कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालकोलि|शृगालकोलिः
शृगालकोलि m. (-लिः) A sort of jujube.<BR> E. शृगाल a jackal, कोलि the jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालजम्बू|शृगालजंबू
शृगालजम्बू f. (-म्बूः)<BR>	 1. A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis madraspatanus.)<BR>2. The fruit of the jujube.<BR> E. शृगाल a jackal, जम्बू rose-apple. “गोमुक् ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालिका
शृगालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The female jackal.<BR>	 2. A fox.<BR>	 3. Running away,<BR>flight, retreat.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Convolvulus paniculatus.)<BR> E. शृगाली as<BR>above, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खल|शृंखल|शृंखलं|शृंखलः|शृङ्खलः
शृङ्खल Subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. A belt or chain worn round a man's<BR>body.<BR>	 2. A chain for confining an elephant.<BR>	 3. A chain, a fetter<BR>in general.<BR> E. शृङ्ग a horn, here said to mean a link, and खल् to<BR>collect, aff. अच्; or शिञ्जा the tinkling of a chain, and स्खल् to go,<BR>aff. अच्, deriv irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खलक|शृंखलक|शृंखलकः|शृङ्खलकः
शृङ्खलक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A young camel with wooden rings or clogs on his<BR>feet.<BR>	 2. A chain.<BR> E. शृङ्खल a chain, and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खलता
शृङ्खलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Connexion, concatenation.<BR>	 2. Restraint.<BR> E. तल् added<BR>to शृङ्खल; also with त्व, शृङ्खलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्खलित|शृंखलित|शृङ्खलितः
शृङ्खलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bound, chained, fettered, captive.<BR> E. शृङ्खला a chain, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्ग|शृंग|शृंगं|शृङ्गं|शृङ्गः
शृङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. A horn.<BR>	 2. A mark, a sign.<BR>	 3. The top of a mountain.<BR>4. The summit of a building.<BR>	 5. Any point or projection.<BR>	 6. A<BR>horn of the moon.<BR>	 7. A horn used as a wind-instrument.<BR>	 8. Sover-<BR>eignty, mastership.<BR>	 9. Dignity, elevation.<BR>	 10. A fountain, an<BR>artificial one or jet d'eau.<BR>	 11. A lotus.<BR>	 12. Very sharp.<BR>	 13. Minutely<BR>fine.<BR>	 14. Excess of love.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A medicinal root, commonly<BR>Jivaka.<BR>	 2. A Muni so named.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. A fish, (Silurus<BR>Singio, HAM.)<BR>	 3. A plant (Betula.)<BR>	 4. Rishabha, a medicinal root,<BR>sharped like a bull's horn.<BR>	 5. Another plant, a kind of Rhus,<BR>with an excrescence or gall in the bark, compared to a crab's<BR>horn.<BR> E. शॄ to injure, Unādi aff. गन्, and the vowel made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गक|शृंगक|शृंगकं|शृंगकः|शृङ्गकः
शृङ्गक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A horn.<BR>	 2. Any pointed object.<BR>	 3. A horn of the<BR>moon.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A medicinal root, commonly Jivaka.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गज|शृंगज|शृङ्गजं|शृङ्गजः
शृङ्गज m. (-जः) An arrow.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गला
शृङ्गला f. (-ला) A plant, a kind of Rhus, having an excrescence in the<BR>bark formed by an insect, which is compared in shape to the horn<BR>of a goat or a crab.<BR> E. शृङ्ग a horn, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गवेर|शृंगवेर
शृङ्गवेर n. (-रं) Ginger.<BR> E. शृङ्ग a horn, and वेर body or shape; also with कन् added शृङ्गवेरक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गाट|शृंगाट|शृङ्गाटं|शृंगाटः|शृङ्गाटः
शृङ्गाट n. (-टं) A place where four roads meet.<BR>	 m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. An aquatic<BR>plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>	 2. A shrub, (Ruellia or Barleria longifo-<BR>lia.)<BR> E. शृङ्ग a horn, अट् to go or be, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गाटक|शृंगाटक|शृङ्गाटकं|शृंगाटकः|शृङ्गाटकः
शृङ्गाटक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A place where four roads meet.<BR>	 2. An aquatic plant,<BR>(Trapa bispinosa.)<BR>	 3. A door.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A collection or mountain<BR>of three peaks.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गान्तर|शृंगांतर
शृङ्गान्तर n. (-रं) The interval between the horns of an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गार|शृंगार|शृङ्गारं|शृंगारः|शृङ्गारः
शृङ्गार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Love, the passion or sentiment as an object of poeti-<BR>cal description or dramatic representation.<BR>	 2. Copulation, coition.<BR>3. Marks made with red-lead on an elephant's head and trunk by<BR>way of ornament.<BR>	 4. A dress suitable for amorous purposes.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रं)<BR>	 1. Cloves.<BR>	 2. Red-lead.<BR>	 3. Fragrant powder for the dress or<BR>person.<BR>	 4. Ginger.<BR>	 5. Agallochum.<BR> E. शृङ्ग eminence, dignity, ऋ<BR>to go to or obtain, and अण् aff.; being the chief of the poetical<BR>Rasas; or शॄ to hurt, आरन् Unādi aff., with नुम् and गुक् augments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारक|शृङ्गारकं|शृंगारकः|शृङ्गारकः
शृङ्गारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Horned, having a horn or crest.<BR> E. शृङ्ग, आरकन्<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारभूषण|शृंगारभूषण|शृङ्गारभूषणं
शृङ्गारभूषण n. (-णं) Red-lead.<BR> E. शृङ्गार love, भूषण adorning. “सिन्दुरे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारयोनि|शृंगारयोनि|शृङ्गारयोनिः
शृङ्गारयोनि m. (-निः) The deity of love.<BR> E. शृङ्गार the passion, योनि origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारवेश|शृंगारवेश|शृङ्गारवेशः
शृङ्गारवेश m. (-शः) A dress suitable for amorous purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारसहाय|शृंगारसहाय|शृङ्गारसहायः
शृङ्गारसहाय m. (-यः) An assistant in love affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारित|शृंगारित
शृङ्गारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Stained with red-lead, reddened.<BR>	 2. Deco-<BR>rated.<BR>	 3. Affected with passion.<BR> E. शृङ्गार, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारिन्|शृंगारिन्
शृङ्गारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Feeling or relating to the passion of<BR>love.<BR>	 2. Stained with red-lead.<BR>	 m. (-री)<BR>	 1. An empassioned lover.<BR>2. Dress, decoration.<BR>	 3. An elephant.<BR>	 4. A ruby.<BR>	 5. The betel-nut<BR>tree, (Areca faufel.)<BR> E. शृङ्गार love, इनि aff. of relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गि|शृंगि|शृंगिः|शृङ्गिः
शृङ्गि f. (-ङ्गिः or -ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A sort of sheat-fish, (Silurus Singio, HAM.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>kind of poison.<BR>	 mn. (-ङ्गिः-ङ्गि) Gold for ornaments: see शृङ्ग, शृङ्गी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिक|शृंगिक|शृंगिकं|शृङ्गिकं
शृङ्गिक n. (-कं) A sort of poison.<BR>	 f. (-का) A plant, (Betula.)<BR> E. शृङ्क a fish,<BR>&c., ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिकनक
शृङ्गिकनक n. (-कं) Gold for ornaments.<BR> E. शृङ्गि the same, and कनक gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिण|शृंगिण|शृंगिणः|शृङ्गिणः
शृङ्गिण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Horned.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A ram.<BR> E. शृङ्ग a horn, इनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिन्|शृंगिन्
शृङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिणी-ङ्गि)<BR>	 1. Horned.<BR>	 2. Crested, peaked.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1.<BR>An elephant.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. A tree.<BR>	 4. An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR>5. Name of an attendant of ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गिणी)<BR>	 1. A cow.<BR>	 2.<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 3. Heart-pea.<BR>	 4. Katuki, a medicinal plant. E.<BR>शृङ्ग a horn, &c., इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृणि|शृणिः
शृणि f. (-णिः) The hook for goading an elephant.<BR> E. शृ to injure, नि<BR>aff., and the radical vowel made short; also सृणि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृण्वत्
शृण्वत् mfn. (-ण्वन्-ण्वन्ती-ण्वत्) Hearing.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृत|शृतं
शृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Boiled, (water, milk or Ghee.)<BR> E. श्रा to boil, aff. क्त,<BR>form irr.; or शृ-क्त; as applied to any other substances, the form<BR>is श्राण or श्रपित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृध्
शृध्(उ)शृधु r. 1st. cl. (शर्द्धते) To fart. (शर्द्धति-ते) To cut. r. 10th cl.<BR>(शर्द्धयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To insult, to ridicule.<BR>	 2. To take, to seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृधु|शृधुः
शृधु f. (-धुः)<BR>	 1. The anus.<BR>	 2. Intellect.<BR> E. शृध् to fart, &c., Unādi aff.<BR>कू; also read शृधू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शॄ
शॄ r. 9th cl. (शृणाति) To hurt, to wound or kill. With वि prefixed,<BR>pass. v. (विशीर्य्यते) To be injured or impaired, to waste or decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखर|शेखरं|शेखरः
शेखर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A garland of flowers worn on the crown of the head.<BR>2. A crest.<BR>	 3. The burden of a song.<BR>	 4. Anything the best of its<BR>kind, (when used at the end of a compound.)<BR>	 f. (-री) A parasite<BR>plant.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The root of the Hyperanthera morunga.<BR>	 2.<BR>Cloves.<BR> E. शिखि to go, अरन् aff.; the nasal omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखरित
शेखरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Crested, tufted, peaked.<BR> E. शेखर, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेणवी
शेणवी f. (-वी) Understanding, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेणा
शेणा f. (-णा) Understanding, mind, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेप|शेपः
शेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. The penis.<BR>	 2. A testicle.<BR> E. शी to sleep, पन् aff.: see<BR>शेफस्; also read शेपस् n. (-पः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेपाल|शेपालः
शेपाल m. (-लः) Vallisneria: see शैवाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफ|शेफः
शेफ m. (-फः) The penis.<BR> E. शी to sleep, फन् aff.: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफस्
शेफस् n. (-फः) The penis.<BR> E. शी to sleep, (semine effuso,) असुन् aff., and<BR>फुट् augment; also with पुट् augment, शेपस्, and with a final<BR>vowel, शेफ or शेप; again, व being substituted for प, शेव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफालि|शेफालिः
शेफालि f. (-लिः-ली) A plant: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफालिका
शेफालिका f. (-का) A flower, (Nyctanthes arbor-tristis.)<BR> E. शेफा sleeping,<BR>from शी with फ aff., अलि a bee, fem. aff. ङीष्, कप् added;<BR>also शेफालि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेमुषी
शेमुषी f. (-षी) Understanding, intellect.<BR> E. शे derived from शीङ् to<BR>sleep, with the aff. विच्, implying ignorance or delusion and मुष् to<BR>steal, to take away, affs. क and ङीष्; or शम् to pacify, (the senses,)<BR>क्कसु participial aff., fem. form, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेल्
शेल्(ऋ)शेऌ r. 1st cl. (शेलति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To shake, to<BR>tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेलु|शेलुः
शेलु m. (-लुः) A small tree, (Cordia myxa.)<BR> E. शिल् to glean, उन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेव|शेवः
शेव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The penis.<BR>	 2. A snake.<BR>	 3. Heighth, elevation.<BR>	 4. Happi-<BR>ness.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. The penis.<BR>	 2. Happiness. Ind. (-वम्) Hail, homage,<BR>a term of exclamation or salutation addressed to the deities. E.<BR>शीङ् to sleep, Unādi aff. वन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवधि|शेवधिः
शेवधि m. (-धिः) A treasure as belonging to KUVERA, a Nidhi or<BR>substance of extraordinary rarity and value, possessed only by<BR>the god of wealth.<BR> E. शेव happiness, धा to have, कि aff.; or शे in<BR>future, अवधि boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवल|शेवलं
शेवल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra:) see the<BR>next.<BR>	 2. The green moss-like substance that grows on the<BR>surface of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवलिनी
शेवलिनी f. (-नी) A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवाल|शेवालं
शेवाल n. (-लं) An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.)<BR> E. शी to sleep,<BR>(on the water,) वालन् Unādi aff.; also व being changed to प, शेपाल,<BR>and the pen. vowel shortened, शेवल; also शैवल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेश्यित
शेश्यित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fast asleep, sleeping much.<BR> E. शी to sleep,<BR>intens. v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेश्यितवत्
शेश्यितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Sleeping much or soundly.<BR> E. शी to sleep, intens. v., क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेश्वीयमान
शेश्वीयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Enlarging, expanding.<BR> E. श्वि to increase,<BR>intens. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेष|शेषं|शेषः
शेष n. (-षं) Remainder, leavings, rest, balance, what is left, omitted<BR>or rejected.<BR>	 m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. The king of the serpent race, as a large<BR>thousand-headed snake, at once the couch and canopy of VIṢṆU,<BR>and the upholder of the world, which rests on one of his heads.<BR>2. A name of BALADEVA.<BR>	 3. Killing, destroying, finishing.<BR>	 4.<BR>Result, end, conclusion.<BR>	 f. (-षा) Flowers and other things that<BR>have been offered to an idol and are then distributed amongst the<BR>worshippers and attendants.<BR> E. शिष् to specify, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषकाल|शेषकालः
शेषकाल n. (-लं) The last term, the time of death.<BR> E. शेष and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषभाग|शेषभागः
शेषभाग m. (-गः) The last or remaining part.<BR> E. शेष and भाग portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषभुज्
शेषभुज् mfn. (-भुक्) Who eats the leavings of others.<BR> E. शेष, भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषभोजन
शेषभोजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Eating the rest of the food after feeding the family,<BR>guests, &c.<BR>	 2. Eating the leavings of a meal.<BR> E. शेष and भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषरक्षण
शेषरक्षण n. (-णं) Taking care that an undertaking is brought to a<BR>conclusion.<BR> E. शेष and रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषरात्रि|शेषरात्रिः
शेषरात्रि f. (-त्रिः) The last watch of the night.<BR> E. शेष the remainder, and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषशयन|शेषशयनः
शेषशयन m. (-नः) An epithet of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषान्न
शेषान्न n. (-न्नं) Leavings of a meal, &c.<BR> E. शेष, अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषावस्था
शेषावस्था f. (-स्था) The last state or condition of life.<BR> E. शेष and अवस्था state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शै
शै r. 1st cl. (शायते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्ष|शैक्षः
शैक्ष m. (-क्षः) A young Brāhman in his novitiate, one who has begun<BR>to read the Vedas.<BR> E. शिक्षा the pronunciation of the language of<BR>the Vedas, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्ष्य|शैक्ष्यं
शैक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं) Learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैख|शैखः
शैख m. (-खः) The offspring of an outcaste Brāhman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैखरिक|शैखरिकः
शैखरिक m. (-कः) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR> E. शेखर a crest or top,<BR>ठक् aff.; also with ढक् aff. शैखरेय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैघ्र्य|शैघ्र्यं
शैघ्र्य n. (-घ्य्रं) Quickness, rapidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैत्य|शैत्यं
शैत्य n. (-त्यं) Cold, coldness.<BR> E. शीत cold, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैथिल्य|शैथिल्यं
शैथिल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Looseness, laxity.<BR>	 2. Flaccidity.<BR>	 3. Slackness,<BR>remission.<BR>	 4. Relaxation of rule or connexion.<BR> E. शिथिल, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैनेय|शैनेयः
शैनेय m. (-यः) SĀTYAKI, the charioteer of KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैरीयक|शैरीयकः
शैरीयक m. (-कः) A shrub, (Barleria cristata;) also शैरेयक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैल|शैलं|शैलः
शैल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>	 1. Mountainous, mountaineer, &c.<BR>	 2. Stony, rocky.<BR>m. (-लः) A mountain.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Bitumen.<BR>	 2. Storax.<BR>	 3. A sort of<BR>collyrium: see रसाञ्जन.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A concise interpretation of a<BR>grammatical aphorism.<BR>	 2. A mode of interpretation.<BR>	 3. Course,<BR>conduct.<BR> E. शिला a rock, a stone, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलक|शैलकं
शैलक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Storax or Benzoin.<BR>	 2. Bitumen.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलकटक|शैलकटकः
शैलकटक m. (-कः) The brow or slope of a mountain.<BR> E. शैल, कटक flank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलज|शैलजं
शैलज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced in or on mountains, rocks, &c.<BR>	 n. (-जं)<BR>	 1.<BR>A fragrant resinous substance, (Storax or Benzoin.)<BR>	 2. Bitumen.<BR>E. शैल a mountain, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलजन|शैलजनः
शैलजन m. (-नः) A mountaineer.<BR> E. शैल, and जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलधन्वन्
शैलधन्वन् m. (-न्वा) ŚIVA.<BR> E. शैल a mountain, and धन्वन् a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलधर|शैलधरः
शैलधर m. (-रः) KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. शैल a mountain, and धर who upholds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलनिर्य्यास|शैलनिर्यास|शैलनिर्यासः|शैलनिर्य्यासं
शैलनिर्य्यास m. (-सः) Storax, Benzoin.<BR> E. शैल a rock, निर्य्यास exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलपति|शैलपतिः
शैलपति m. (-तिः) The Himālaya.<BR> E. शैल, and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलभित्ति|शैलभित्तिः
शैलभित्ति f. (-त्तिः) A stone-cutter's chisel or axe, an instrument for<BR>cutting stones.<BR> E. शैल a mountain, भिद् to divide, aff. क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलमय
शैलमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Rocky.<BR> E. शैल, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलरन्ध्र|शैलरंध्र
शैलरन्ध्र n. (-न्ध्रं) A cavern, a cave.<BR> E. शैल, रन्ध्र a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलशिखर
शैलशिखर n. (-रं) The crest or peak of a mountain.<BR> E. शैल, शिखर a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलशिविर|शैलशिविरं
शैलशिविर n. (-रं) The ocean.<BR> E. शैल a rock, and शिविर a camp or place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलशृङ्ग
शैलशृङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) The peak of a mountain.<BR> E. शैल, and शृङ्ग a horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलसार
शैलसार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Hard, firm, as a rock.<BR> E. शैल and सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलाग्र|शैलाग्रं
शैलाग्र n. (-ग्रं) The peak of a mountain.<BR> E. शैल a mountain, and अग्र top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलाट|शैलाटः
शैलाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. A mountaineer, a savage, a barbarian.<BR>	 3.<BR>An attendant on an idol.<BR>	 4. Crystal.<BR> E. शैल a mountain, and अट्<BR>to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलालिन्
शैलालिन् m. (-ली) An actor, a dancer.<BR> E. शिलालिन् a Muni, said to have<BR>been the author of the principles of acting, &c., अण् aff., शैलाल<BR>his institutes, and इनि aff. of profession or practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलिक्य|शैलिक्यः
शैलिक्य m. (-क्यः) An impostor, a pretended devotee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूष|शैलूषः
शैलूष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. An actor, a dancer, a tumbler, &c.<BR>	 2. A rogue, a<BR>cheat.<BR>	 3. The master of the band, or one who beats time.<BR>	 4. The<BR>Bel-tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR> E. शिलूष one of the early teachers of<BR>the arts of acting, &c., अण् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूषिक|शैलूषिकः
शैलूषिक m. (-कः) One who follows the profession of an actor.<BR> E. शैलूष, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलेय|शैलेयं|शैलेयः
शैलेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Produced in the mountains, &c., mountain-<BR>ous, mountaineer.<BR>	 2. Mountain-like.<BR>	 n. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A fragrant resin,<BR>(Stcrax or Benzoin.)<BR>	 2. A vegetable perfume, commonly Murā.<BR>3. Rock-salt.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A bee.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR>	 f. (-यी) A name of<BR>PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. शिला a mountain, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलोपशल्य
शैलोपशल्य n. (-ल्यं) The skirts of a mountain or low-land at its base.<BR>E. शैल and उपशल्य neighbouring space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैल्य|शैल्यं
शैल्य nf. (-ल्यं-ल्यी) Hardness, stoniness.<BR> E. शिला a stone, a rock, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैव|शैवं|शैवः
शैव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Relating or appertaining to the god ŚIVA.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-वः) A worshipper of ŚIVA.<BR>	 n. (-वं) An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria<BR>octandra.)<BR> E. शिव the deity, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवल|शैवलं|शैवलः
शैवल m. (-लः) An aquatic plant, moss.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A drug, commonly<BR>termed Padma-kāth.<BR> E. शी to sleep, (on the water,) वलञ् aff.;<BR>also शैवाल शेवाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवलिनी
शैवलिनी f. (-नी) A river in general.<BR> E. शैवल Vallisneria, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवाल|शैवालं
शैवाल m. (-लः) An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.)<BR> E. शी to sleep,<BR>(on the water,) वालञ् aff., शेवाल and अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैव्य|शैव्यः
शैव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्यी-व्यं) Relating to ŚIVA, &c.<BR>	 m. (-व्यः)<BR>	 1. One of the<BR>four horses of KṚṢṆA'S car.<BR>	 2. A horse in general.<BR>	 3. A king<BR>and champion in the Pāṇḍava's army.<BR> E. शिव, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशव|शैशवं
शैशव n. (-वं) Childhood, pupilage, the period under sixteen.<BR> E. शिशु a<BR>child, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशिर|शैशिरः
शैशिर f. (-री) Adj. Relating of the dewy-season.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A species of<BR>chātaka bird.<BR> E. शिशिर, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैष्योपाध्यायिका
शैष्योपाध्यायिका f. (-का) Instruction of youth, tuition.<BR> E. शिष्य a pupil,<BR>उपाध्याय a preceptor, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शो
शो r. 4th cl. (श्यति)<BR>	 1. To reduce or make small, to pare.<BR>	 2. To whet or sharpen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोक|शोकः
शोक m. (-कः) Sorrow, grief.<BR> E. शुच् to regret, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकचर्चा|शोकचर्च्चा
शोकचर्चा f. (-र्चा) Indulgence in sorrow.<BR> E. शोक, and चर्चा search.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकच्छिद्|शोकछिद्
शोकच्छिद् mfn. (-च्छिद्) Consoling, allaying, removing sorrow.<BR> E. शोक,<BR>and च्छिद् what cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकनिहत
शोकनिहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Afflicted, overcome with grief.<BR> E. शोक, and<BR>निहत struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकभङ्ग
शोकभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Dissipating or removing sorrow.<BR> E. शोक, and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकमूर्च्छित
शोकमूर्च्छित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Involved in distress, swooning with grief. E.<BR>शोक, and मूर्च्छित fained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकस्थान
शोकस्थान n. (-नं) Site, circumstance, or occasion of sorrow.<BR> E. शोक, and<BR>स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकाकुल
शोकाकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Overcome with sorrow.<BR> E. शोक, and आकुल bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकाग्नि|शोकाग्निः
शोकाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Deep distress, violent grief.<BR> E. शोक and अग्नि fire;<BR>also similar compounds, as शोकानल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकाग्निसन्तप्त|शोकाग्निसंतप्त
शोकाग्निसन्तप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Distressed.<BR> E. शोकाग्नि, and सन्तप्त inflamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकापनुद
शोकापनुद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Alleviating, consoling.<BR>	 2. Being consoled.<BR>E. शोक, and अपनुद what drives away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकापनोद|शोकापनोदः
शोकापनोद m. (-दः) A teacher of holy wisdom, a philosopher.<BR> E. शोक<BR>worldly care, अप away, नुद् to send, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकापहर्त्तृ|शोकापहर्तृ
शोकापहर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्ती-र्त्तृ) Allaying or dissipating grief.<BR> E. शोक, and<BR>अपहर्त्तृ what drives away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकारि|शोकारिः
शोकारि m. (-रिः) The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea Kadamba.)<BR> E. शोक<BR>sorrow, अरि hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकार्त्त|शोकार्त
शोकार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Pained, afflicted by sorrow.<BR> E. शोक, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकोद्भव
शोकोद्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Born or produced from or caused by grief. E.<BR>शोक, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचन|शोचनं
शोचन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sorrowing, sorrowful.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Sorrow, grief, grie-<BR>ving.<BR> E. शुच् to grieve, aff. युच् or ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचनीय
शोचनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be grieved or lamented.<BR> E. शुच् to be sad, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचित
शोचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sorrowful, afflicted.<BR> E. शुचि to grieve, causal v.,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचितव्य
शोचितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be grieved for, lamentable.<BR> E. शुच् to grieve, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचित्वा
शोचित्वा Ind. Grieving or having grieved for.<BR> E. शुचि to lament, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचिष्केश|शोचिष्केशः
शोचिष्केश m. (-शः) Fire or its deity.<BR> E. शोचिस् light, and केश hair,<BR>having locks of flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचिस्
शोचिस् n. (-चिः) Light, lustre, radiance, flame.<BR> E. शुच् to be or make pure, Unādi aff. इसि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोच्य
शोच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं)<BR>	 1. To be lamented or bewailed.<BR>	 2. To be clean-<BR>sed or purified.<BR>	 3. Low, vile.<BR> E. शुच् to grieve, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोच्यक
शोच्यक m. (-कः) A low man.<BR> E. शोच्य to be purified, (from,) कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोठ|शोठः
शोठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. A fool, a blockhead.<BR>	 2. A sluggard.<BR>	 3. A rogue, a<BR>cheat.<BR>	 4. A low man, one of a degraded tribe or business.<BR>	 5. A<BR>villain, a criminal, a sinner.<BR>	 f. (-ठा)<BR>	 1. Foolish.<BR>	 2. Wicked.<BR>	 3.<BR>Lazy, idle.<BR> E. शुठ् to be prevented or stopped, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोण्
शोण्(ऋ)शोणृ r. 1st cl. (शोणति)<BR>	 1. To be red.<BR>	 2. To move or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोण|शोणं|शोणः
शोण mfn. (-णः-णा or णी-णं)<BR>	 1. Crimson, of a crimson colour.<BR>	 2. Red in<BR>the face, from passion, &c.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Crimson, the colour of the<BR>red lotus.<BR>	 2. A horse of a reddish or bright chesnut colour.<BR>	 3. The<BR>Śona river, which rises in the table land of Amerakantāk and<BR>running first northerly and then easterly for 500 miles, falls into<BR>the Ganges above Pātnā.<BR>	 4. A flower, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR>	 5. Fire<BR>or its deity.<BR>	 6. An ocean.<BR>	 7. A red sort of sugar-cane.<BR>	 8. The<BR>planet Mars.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Red-lead.<BR>	 2. Blood.<BR> E. शोण् to be red, aff.<BR>अच्, fem. aff. टाप् or ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणक|शोणकः
शोणक m. (-कः) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणरत्न|शोणरत्नं
शोणरत्न n. (-त्नं) A ruby.<BR> E. शोण deep red, and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणाक|शोणाकः
शोणाक m. (-कः) A tree, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. शोण red, अक् to go or be, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणाम्बु|शोणांबु|शोणाम्बुः
शोणाम्बु m. (-म्बुः) Name of a cloud which would rise at the destruction<BR>of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणित|शोणितं
शोणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Red, crimson, purple.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Blood.<BR>	 2. Saff-<BR>ron.<BR> E. शोण redness, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणितप
शोणितप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Who or what drinks blood.<BR> E. शोणित and पा to drink, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणितपुर|शोणितपुरं
शोणितपुर n. (-रं) The city of Vānāsura.<BR> E. शोणित red, and पुर city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणिताह्वय|शोणिताह्वयं
शोणिताह्वय n. (-यं) Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणितोक्षित
शोणितोक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stained or sprinkled with blood.<BR> E. शोणित, and उक्षित moistened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणितोपल|शोणितोपलः
शोणितोपल n. (-लं) A ruby.<BR> E. शोणित red, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणिमन्
शोणिमन् m. (-मा) Redness.<BR> E. शोण् and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथ|शोथः
शोथ m. (-थः) Swelling, intumescence.<BR> E. शु to go, (to grow,) Unādi aff.<BR>थन्; also with कन् added, शोथक m. (-कः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथघ्न|शोथघ्नः
शोथघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Discutient, removing swellings.<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी) Hogweed,<BR>(Boerhavia diffusa.)<BR> E. शोथ swelling, घ्न removing, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथजित्
शोथजित् mfn. (-जित्) Discutient.<BR>	 f. (-जित्) Hogweed: see the last. E.<BR>शोथ swelling, and जित् overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथरोग|शोथरोगः
शोथरोग m. (-गः) Dropsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथहृत्
शोथहृत् mfn. (-हृत्) Discutient, removing swelling.<BR>	 m. (-हृत्) Marking-<BR>nut plant.<BR> E. शोथ swelling. and हृत् removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोध|शोधः
शोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Purification.<BR>	 2. Correction.<BR>	 3. Retalition.<BR>	 4. Acquittance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधक|शोधकः
शोधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what cleans, purifies, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>refiner.<BR>	 2. (In arithmetic,) The subtrahend.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A kind of<BR>earth.<BR> E. शुध् to be pure, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधन|शोधनं|शोधनः
शोधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Cleaning, purifying &c., that which cleanses,<BR>refines, &c.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cleaning, cleansing, purifying.<BR>	 2. Correcting,<BR>freeing from faults or errors.<BR>	 3. Correcting, as a writing.<BR>	 4. Subtrac-<BR>tion, (in arithmetic.)<BR>	 5. The refining of metals.<BR>	 6. A sort of refining,<BR>practised for chemical or medical purposes: exposing the metals to<BR>heat, and then sprinkling them with the urine of cows, &c.<BR>	 7. Pay-<BR>ment, acquittance.<BR>	 8. Feces, ordure.<BR>	 9. Green vitriol.<BR>	 10. Deter-<BR>mination.<BR>	 11. Punishment.<BR>	 12. Expiation.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The lime.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी) A broom.<BR> E. शुध् to be make pure, aff. ल्युट् or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधनीय|शोधनीयः
शोधनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be corrected.<BR>	 2. To be cleansed or purified.<BR>3. To be refined.<BR>	 4. To be subtracted.<BR>	 5. To be liquidated, (as a<BR>debt,) due.<BR> E. शुध् to purify, aff. अनीयर्; also शोध्य and शोधितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधयित्वा
शोधयित्वा Ind.<BR>	 1. Having paid or discharged.<BR>	 2. Having cleared, &c. E.<BR>शुध् to be pure, causal v., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधित|शोधितं
शोधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cleaned, cleansed.<BR>	 2. Strained.<BR>	 3. Corrected.<BR>4. Refined.<BR>	 5. Purified.<BR>	 6. Discharged, liquidated, (as a debt.) E.<BR>शुध् to clean, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोध्य|शोध्यः
शोध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. To be purified, cleaned, refined, &c.<BR>	 2. Payable,<BR>due.<BR>	 3. To be subtracted.<BR>	 m. (-ध्यः) An accused person, one to be<BR>justified or tried.<BR>	 n. (-ध्यं) A constant number to be subtracted in<BR>some astronomical computation.<BR> E. शुध् to be pure, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोफ|शोफः
शोफ m. (-फः) Intumescence, swelling.<BR> E. शु to go, aff. फन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभ
शोभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. Handsome.<BR>	 2. Bright.<BR>	 f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. Light, lustre,<BR>radiance, splendour.<BR>	 2. Beauty.<BR>	 3. Distinguished merit.<BR>	 4. A species<BR>of the Kriti-metre.<BR> E. शुभ् to shine, aff. अच्, fem. aff. टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभकृत्
शोभकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Beautifying.<BR>	 m. (-कृत्)<BR>	 1. The thirty-sixth year of<BR>the Hindu cycle.<BR>	 2. Marking-nut plant.<BR> E. शोभ handsome, and कृत्<BR>what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभन|शोभनं|शोभनः
शोभन mfn. (-नः-ना or नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, handsome.<BR>	 2. Shining, splendid.<BR>3. Richly dressed or ornamented.<BR>	 4. Propitious, auspicious.<BR>	 5. Virtu-<BR>ous, moral, decorous, good.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The fifth Yoga.<BR>	 2. A planet.<BR>3. Burnt-offering for auspicious results.<BR>	 4. A name of ŚIVA.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-नं)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. Shining, being splendid or handsome.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>1. A virtuous or beautiful woman.<BR>	 2. Turmeric.<BR>	 3. A kind of Pig-<BR>ment, commonly called Gorochanā.<BR> E. शुभ् to shine, aff. ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभनक|शोभनकः
शोभनक m. (-कः) A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR> E. कन् added to the<BR>preceding. “शजिना गाछ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभनाचरित
शोभनाचरित n. (-तं) Virtuous practice.<BR> E. शोभन, and आचरित done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभमान
शोभमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fair, splendid, shining.<BR> E. शुभ् to shine, &c.,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभा
शोभा f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. Light, lustre.<BR>	 2. Beauty, grace, loveliness.<BR>	 3. Grandeur.<BR>4. Turmeric.<BR>	 5. The Pigment called “गोरोचना.”<BR> E. शुभ्, अ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभाञ्जन|शोभांजन|शोभाञ्जनः
शोभाञ्जन m. (-नः) A tree, commonly Sajina or Sahajnā, (Hyperanthera<BR>morunga;) the legumes, blossoms, and leaves are esculent, and<BR>the root of the young tree is used as a substitute for horse-radish:<BR>in medicine the root is used as a rubefacient externally, as a<BR>stimulant internally, and the expressed oil of the seeds is employed<BR>to relieve arthritic pains, &c.<BR> E. शोभा beauty, अञ्ज् to pervade or<BR>anoint, and ल्युट् or युच् aff.; also शौभाञ्जन and सोभाञ्जन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभित
शोभित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Beautified, decorated.<BR> E. शुभ् to shine, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोलि
शोलि f. (-लिः or -ली) Wild turmeric.<BR> E. शूल-अच् पृषो० ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोशुच्यमान
शोशुच्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Sorrowing or grieving deeply.<BR> E. शुच् to be<BR>sorrowful, intens. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोष|शोषः
शोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Pulmonary consumption.<BR>	 2. Drying up, dryness.<BR>	 3.<BR>Intumescence, swelling.<BR>	 4. Emaciation, withering.<BR> E. शुष् to dry,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषण|शोषणं|शोषणः
शोषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Suction, sucking.<BR>	 2. Drying up.<BR>	 3. Exhaustion.<BR>	 4.<BR>Dry-ginger.<BR>	 m. (-णः) One of the arrows of KĀMADEVA, or CUPID.<BR>f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Drying up.<BR>	 2. Causing to wither.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषयित्वा
शोषयित्वा Ind. Having dried up.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, causal v., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषित|शोषितः
शोषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dried, dried up, desiccated.<BR> E. शुष् to dry, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोस्
शोस् Ind. A particle of reproach or contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक|शौकं
शौक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A flock of parrots.<BR>	 2. Sorrowfulness.<BR> E. शुक a parrot,<BR>अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्त|शौक्तं
शौक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ती-क्तं) Acid, acetic.<BR> E. शुक्त vinegar, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तिक
शौक्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Acid, acetic.<BR>	 2. Relating to a pearl, &c. E.<BR>शुक्त or शुक्ति, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तेय|शौक्तेयं
शौक्तेय n. (-यं) A pearl.<BR> E. शुक्ति a pearl-oyster, ढक् aff.; also from शुक्तिका<BR>with the same, शौक्तिकेय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्लिकेय|शौक्लिकेयः
शौक्लिकेय m. (-यः) A sort of poison.<BR> E. शुक्लिक a country, ढक् aff.:<BR>according to some it is the venom of a snake of the Amphisbœna<BR>kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्ल्य|शौक्ल्यं
शौक्ल्य n. (-क्ल्यं) Whiteness, clearness.<BR> E. शुक्ल white, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौच|शौचं
शौच n. (-चं)<BR>	 1. Purification by ablution, &c. from personal defilement.<BR>2. Purification at given periods from defilement caused by the<BR>death of a relation, &c.<BR>	 3. The state or property of freedom from<BR>defilement, purity, cleanness.<BR> E. शुचि purity, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचकल्प
शौचकल्प m. (-ल्पः) A purificatory rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचकूप|शौचकूपः
शौचकूप m. (-पः) A privy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचविधि
शौचविधि f. (-धिः) The rules of purification after defilement by the<BR>death of a relation, &c.<BR> E. शौच. and विधि precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचाचार|शौचाचारः
शौचाचार m. (-रः) A rule of purification, the mode in which the person<BR>is to be cleansed by ablution, &c., after voiding any excrement or<BR>contracting any impurity.<BR> E. शौच purification, and आचार rule, rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचेय|शौचेयः
शौचेय m. (-यः) A washerman.<BR> E. शुचि cleaning, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचेप्सु
शौचेप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Wishing or intending to be purified.<BR> E. शीच, इप्सु desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौट्
शौट्(ऋ)शौटृ r. 1st cl. (शौटति) To be proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौटीर|शौटीरः
शौटीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Proud, haughty.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A hero.<BR>	 2. An ascetic,<BR>one who abandons the world.<BR>	 3. A proud or haughty man, but of<BR>low tribe or occupation, an upstart.<BR> E. शौट् to be proud, and इरन्<BR>Unādi aff.; also as derived from शौड the same, शौडीर; also the<BR>short vowel being substituted for the diphthong, शुटीर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौटीर्य्य|शौटीर्य|शौटीर्यं|शौटीर्य्यं
शौटीर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Heroism, prowess.<BR>	 2. Pride, arrogance.<BR> E. शौटीर a<BR>hero, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौड्
शौड्(ऋ)शौडृ r. 1st cl. (शौडति) To be proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्ड|शौंड|शौण्डः
शौण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डी-ण्डं)<BR>	 1. Drunk, intoxicated.<BR>	 2. Fond of, addicted<BR>to, (as liquor.)<BR>	 3. Skilful, (with a loc.) as in अक्षशौण्ड । f. (-ण्डी)<BR>	 1.<BR>Long-pepper.<BR>	 2. Another sort, (Piper chavya.)<BR> E. शुण्डा spirituous<BR>liquor, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डय्य
शौण्डय्य n. (-र्य्यं) Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डिक|शौंडिक|शौंडिकः|शौण्डिकः
शौण्डिक m. (-कः) A distiller and vender of spirituous liquors.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>A female keeper of a tavern or dram-shop.<BR> E. शुण्डा spirits, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डिकेय|शौंडिकेय|शौंडिकेयः|शौण्डिकेयः
शौण्डिकेय m. (-यः) A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौण्डिर
शौण्डिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Proud, haughty.<BR>	 2. Elevated, looking<BR>upwards; more properly शौडीर, and शौठीर as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौद्धोदनि|शौद्धोदनिः
शौद्धोदनि m. (-निः) BUDDHA, the founder of the Bauddha sect.<BR> E. शुद्धो-<BR>दन a prince of the family of IKSHWĀKU, and इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौद्र|शौद्रः
शौद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्री-द्रं) Śūdra, servile, relating or belonging to the last<BR>class.<BR>	 m. (-द्रः) The son of a man of either of the first three classes<BR>by a Śūdra woman, the last of the twelve sons acknowledged in<BR>the ancient Hindu law.<BR> E. शूद्र a Śūdra, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौधिका
शौधिका f. (-का) A white variety of panic-seed.<BR> E. शोधः शोधन मलविरेकस्तस्मै हितः ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौन|शौनं
शौन n. (-नं) Meat kept at a slaughter-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनक|शौनकः
शौनक m. (-कः) The name of an inspired legislator older than MANU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनिक|शौनिकः
शौनिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A butcher, a poulterer, a vender of the flesh of<BR>beasts or birds.<BR>	 2. Chase, hunting.<BR> E. शूना a slaughter-house, ठञ्<BR>or ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभ|शौभं|शौभः
शौभ n. (-भं) The city of HARISCHANDRA, suspended in the air.<BR>	 m. (-भः)<BR>1. A god, a divinity.<BR>	 2. The betel-nut tree.<BR> E. शुभ, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभनेय|शौभनेयः
शौभनेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Sprung from a handsome mother.<BR>	 2. Relating<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">Page731-b+ 60</a>]<BR>to anything handsome or brilliant.<BR> E. शोभना a handsome woman,<BR>aff. ढक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभाञ्जन|शौभांजन|शौभांजनः|शौभाञ्जनः
शौभाञ्जन m. (-नः) The Sajinā-tree.<BR> E. अण् pleonasm, added to शोभाञ्जन q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभिक|शौभिकः
शौभिक m. (-कः) A juggler, a conjurer.<BR> E. शौभं व्योमपुरं शिल्पमस्य ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौरि|शौरिः
शौरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. The planet<BR>SATURN.<BR> E. शूर a proper name or a hero, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्प्प|शौर्प|शौर्पः
शौर्प्प mfn. (-र्प्पः-र्प्पी-र्प्पं) Measured by winnowing basket, &c.<BR> E. शूर्प्प a<BR>basket, अण् aff; also with ठक् aff. शौर्प्पिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्य्य|शौर्य|शौर्यं|शौर्य्यं
शौर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Valour, heroism, prowess.<BR>	 2. The heroic drama; or<BR>that which treats of war, magic, &c.<BR>	 3. Representation of super-<BR>natural events on the stage.<BR> E. शूर a hero, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्य्योपार्ज्जित|शौर्योपार्जित
शौर्य्योपार्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Acquired by valour.<BR> E. शौर्य्य, and उपार्ज्जित acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्क|शौल्कं|शौल्कः
शौल्क mfn. (-ल्कः-ल्की-ल्कं) Relating to customs or duties, levied as a tax,<BR>&c.<BR>	 m. (-ल्कः) A superintendent of tolls or customs, a custom-<BR>house officer.<BR> E. शुल्क a toll or tax, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्किक|शौल्किकः
शौल्किक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to a tax, a toll, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>Superintendent of tolls or customs.<BR> E. शुल्क a toll, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्विक|शौल्विकः
शौल्विक m. (-कः) A copper-smith.<BR> E. शुल्व copper, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौव|शौवं
शौव f. (-वी) Relating to dogs, canine.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. A number of dogs.<BR>2. The nature of a dog.<BR> E. शुनः सङ्कोचः श्वन् + अण् टिलोपः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवन|शौवनं
शौवन f. (-नी) Canine.<BR>	 n. (-नं) The progeny of a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवस्तिक|शौवस्तिकं
शौवस्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of or belonging to tomorrow.<BR> E. श्वस्तन् of<BR>tomorrow, ठक् added, with तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवस्तिकत्व
शौवस्तिकत्व n. (-त्वं) Ephemeralness, duration for a day.<BR> E. शौवस्तिक, and<BR>त्व added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवापद|शौवापदं
शौवापद mfn. (-दः-दी-दं) Relating to a beast of prey, savage, wild,<BR>ferocious, &c.<BR> E. श्वापद a beast of prey, अण् aff., and औ augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौष्कल|शौष्कलः
शौष्कल mfn. (-लः-ली-लं)<BR>	 1. Eating fish and flesh.<BR>	 2. A vender of flesh.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-लं) The price of dried-meat.<BR> E. शुष्कली dried flesh, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चुत्
श्चुत्(इर्)श्चुतिर r. 1st cl. (श्चोतति)<BR>	 1. To ooze, to drop or distil.<BR>	 2. To<BR>sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चोत|श्चोतः
श्चोत m. (-तः) Sprinkling, aspersion.<BR> E. श्चुत् to sprinkle, aff. घञ्; also श्च्योत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्युत्
श्च्युत्(इर्)श्च्युतिर् r. 1st cl. (श्च्योतति)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle.<BR>	 2. To ooze, to drop<BR>or distil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्युतित
श्च्युतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dropping, flowing.<BR>	 2. Shed, sprinkled, issued,<BR>oozed.<BR> E. श्च्युत् to sprinkle, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्योत|श्च्योतः
श्च्योत m. (-तः) Sprinkling, pouring forth, aspersion.<BR> E. श्च्युत् to sprinkle, aff. घञ्; also श्चोत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्योतत्
श्च्योतत् mfn. (-तन्-तन्ती-तत्)<BR>	 1. Oozing, flowing, trickling.<BR>	 2. Shedding. E.<BR>श्च्युत् to ooze, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मन्
श्मन् Aptote noun.<BR>	 1. The face, the mouth.<BR>	 2. Corpse.<BR> E. शेते शी-मनिन् डिच्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशान|श्मशानं
श्मशान n. (-नं) A cemetery, a place where dead bodies are burnt or<BR>buried.<BR> E. श्म substituted for शव a corpse, and शान for शयन place<BR>of repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशानवासिन्
श्मशानवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) A ghost, a goblin, a spirit, male or<BR>female, abiding in cemeteries, &c.<BR> E. श्मशान a cemetery, and वासिन्<BR>who abides; also श्मशाननिवासिन्, श्मशानवर्त्तिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशानवेश्मन्
श्मशानवेश्मन् m. (-श्मा)<BR>	 1. MAHĀDEVA.<BR>	 2. A ghost.<BR> E. श्मशान a cemetery,<BR>and वेश्मन् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशानवैराग्य
श्मशानवैराग्य n. (-ग्यं) Momentary abandonment of worldly attachments<BR>such as is caused by the sight of a cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रु
श्मश्रु n. (-श्रु) The beard.<BR> E. श्मन् for मुख the face, श्रि to serve, Unādi<BR>aff. डन्, form irr.; or श्म पुंमुखं श्रूयते लक्ष्यतेऽनेन श्रु-डु; also श्मश्रुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रुमुखी
श्मश्रुमुखी f. (-खी) A woman with a beard.<BR> E. श्मश्रु a beard, and मुख the<BR>face, ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रुल
श्मश्रुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Bearded, having a beard.<BR> E. श्मश्रु, and लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रुवर्द्धक
श्मश्रुवर्द्धक m. (-कः) A barber.<BR> E. श्मश्रु, and वर्द्धक who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रूयमाण
श्मश्रूयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being as if bearded, having something like<BR>a beard.<BR> E. श्मश्र used as a verb, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मील
श्मील r. 1st cl. (श्मीलति)<BR>	 1. To wink, to contract the eyelids.<BR>	 2. To twinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मीलन|श्मीलनं
श्मीलन n. (-नं) Winking, twinkling.<BR> E. श्मील, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मीलित|श्मीलितं
श्मीलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Winked, blinked.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A wink, winking. E.<BR>श्मील् to wink, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यान|श्यानः
श्यान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Viscous, thick, adhesive, as clarified butter,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Congealed.<BR>	 3. Gone.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Smoke.<BR> E. श्यै to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याम|श्यामः
श्याम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Black or dark-blue.<BR>	 2. Green.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>sacred-fig-tree at Prayāga or Āllāhābād.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. The<BR>Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 4. A potherb, (Convolvulus argenteus.)<BR>5. Black, (the colour.)<BR>	 6. Green, (the colour.)<BR>	 7. Thorn-apple,<BR>(Datura metel.)<BR>	 mf. (-मः-मा) A sort of grain, (Panicum frumen-<BR>taceum.)<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Black-pepper.<BR>	 2. Sea salt.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A woman,<BR>described as one who has not borne children; also described as a<BR>female of slender make; or one from eight to sixteen; or one<BR>who resembles in darkness of complexion, the blossom of the<BR>Priyanga, or its stalk, in shape.<BR>	 2. Night.<BR>	 3. Shade, shadow.<BR>	 4.<BR>The Jumnā river.<BR>	 5. A form of DURGĀ.<BR>	 6. A plant, commonly<BR>Priyangu.<BR>	 7. A sort of convolvulus, (C. turpethum,) with black<BR>flowers.<BR>	 8. A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>	 9. Indigo.<BR>10. A twining shrub, (Ichnocarpus frutescens.)<BR>	 11. Turmeric.<BR>	 12.<BR>Holy-basil.<BR>	 13. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>	 14. A shrub, (Abrus<BR>precatorius.)<BR>	 15. A small singing bird with black plumage, com-<BR>monly Shyāmā, (Turdus macrourus.)<BR>	 16. A cow.<BR> E. श्यै to go,<BR>Unādi aff. मक् or मन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामक|श्यामकं|श्यामकः
श्यामक m. (-कः) A sort of grain, (Panicum frumentaceum, &c.)<BR> E. श्यामा<BR>the same, कन् added, m. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामकण्ठ|श्यामकंठ|श्यामकण्ठः
श्यामकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. A small kind of bird. E.<BR>श्याम black or blue, कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामकर्ण|श्यामकर्णः
श्यामकर्ण m. (-र्णः) A horse suitable for a horse-sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामत्व
श्यामत्व n. (-त्वं) Blackness.<BR> E. त्व added to श्याम; also with तल्, श्यामता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामपत्र|श्यामपत्रः
श्यामपत्र m. (-त्रः) The Tamāla-tree, (Xanthocymus pictorius.)<BR> E. श्याम<BR>black, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामभास्
श्यामभास् mfn. (-भाः-भाः-भः) Black as jet, of a glossy black hue.<BR> E. श्याम and भास् shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामल|श्यामलः
श्यामल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Of a black or dark-blue colour.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Black, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. Black-pepper.<BR>	 3. The religious-fig-tree.<BR>	 4.<BR>A large bee.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A name of PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. श्याम black, ला to<BR>have, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामलता
श्यामलता f. (-ता) A climbing plant, (Ichnocarpus frutescens.)<BR> E. श्याम and लता a creeper<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामाक|श्यामाकः
श्यामाक m. (-कः) A kind of grain generally eaten by the Hindus, (Pa-<BR>nicum frumentaceum; also P. colonum.)<BR> E. श्यामा the same, कन्<BR>added and the final retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामाङ्ग|श्यामांग|श्यामाङ्गः
श्यामाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Black-bodied, black.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) The planet<BR>MERCURY or its ruler.<BR> E. श्याम black, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामापूजा
श्यामापूजा f. (-जा) Worship of SYĀMĀ or DURGĀ on the new-moon of<BR>Kārtika.<BR> E. श्यामा and पूजा worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामिका
श्यामिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Blackness.<BR>	 2. Impurity, alloy.<BR> E. श्याम, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामित
श्यामित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Blackened, turned or become black.<BR> E. श्याम<BR>and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याल|श्यालः
श्याल m. (-लः) A wife's brother.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A wife's sister.<BR> E. श्यै to go, aff. कालन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यालक|श्यालकः
श्यालक m. (-कः) A wife's brother.<BR>	 f. (-लिका or लकी) A wife's sister. E.<BR>कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याव|श्यावः
श्याव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Of a brown colour.<BR>	 m. (-वः) Brown, (the colour.)<BR> E. श्यै to go, वन् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यावतैल|श्यावतैलः
श्यावतैल m. (-लः) The mango-tree.<BR> E. श्याव brown, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यावदत्|श्यावदन्त्
श्यावदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्) Dark or black toothed, (naturally so.) E.<BR>श्याव dark or brown, दत् for दन्त a tooth; also श्यावदन्त, श्यावदन्तक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येत|श्येतः
श्येत mfn. (-तः-ता or ती-तं) White, of a white colour.<BR>	 m. (-तः) White,<BR>(the colour.)<BR> E. श्यै to go, Unādi aff. इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येतकोलक|श्येतकोलकः
श्येतकोलक m. (-कः) A sort of fish, (Cyprinus saphore, Ham.) “पुंँटिमाछ ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येन|श्येनः
श्येन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A hawk, a falcon.<BR>	 2. White, (the colour.)<BR>	 3. White-<BR>ness, paleness.<BR>	 4. Violence, desperation.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The female<BR>hawk.<BR>	 2. A species of the Triṣṭubh-metre.<BR> E. श्यै to go, इनन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनकरण
श्येनकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Acting rashly or desperately.<BR>	 2. Burning on a<BR>separate funeral pile.<BR> E. श्येन and करण acting; also श्येनकरणिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनचित्
श्येनचित् m. (-चित्)<BR>	 1. A hawk-feeder or keeper.<BR>	 2. A receptacle shaped<BR>like a hawk for a sacrificial-fire.<BR> E. श्येन a hawk, and चित् what<BR>collects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनजीविन्
श्येनजीविन् m. (-वी) One who sells hawks or lives by training them.<BR> E. श्येन and जीविन् living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनोपदेश
श्येनोपदेश m. (-शः) Recommendation or injunction to women, to burn<BR>on a separate funeral pile.<BR> E. श्येन violence, and उपदेश advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यै
श्यै r. 1st cl. (श्यायते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To wither.<BR>	 3. To coagulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यैनम्पाता|श्यैनंपाता
श्यैनम्पाता f. (-ता) Hawking, hunting.<BR> E. श्येन a hawk, पात falling, अण्<BR>aff., with नुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्योणा
श्योणा(ना)क m. (-कः) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. श्यै to go डुणाक aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रक्
श्रक्(इ)श्रकि r. 1st cl. (श्रङ्कति) To go, to creep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रग्
श्रग्(इ)श्रगि r. 1st cl. (श्रङ्गति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रण्
श्रण् r. 1st and 10th cls. (श्रणति, श्राणयति-ते) Usually with वि prefixed,<BR>(विश्राणयति) To give, to present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रत्
श्रत् Ind. A particle and prefix implying belief or reverence.<BR> E. श्रो-डति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथ्
श्रथ् r. 1st and 10th cls. (श्रथति, श्राथयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR>2. To let loose or discharge, to set free, to liberate.<BR>	 3. To bind<BR>or tie. r. 10th cl. (श्राथयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To apply diligently, to endeavour<BR>sedulously.<BR>	 2. To delight frequently.<BR>	 3. To march. r. 10th cl.<BR>(श्रथयति-ते) To be weak or infirm. (इ) श्रथि r. 1st cl. (श्रन्थते)<BR>	 1. To be<BR>loose or lax, to be slack or flaccid.<BR>	 2. To let loose, to loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथन|श्रथनं
श्रथन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Tying, stringing.<BR>	 2. Loosening, untying.<BR>	 3. Killing.<BR>	 4.<BR>Effort.<BR> E. श्रथ् to tie, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्दधत्
श्रद्दधत् mfn. (-धन्-धन्ती-धत्) Believing, having faith.<BR> E. श्रत् and दधत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्दधान|श्रद्दधानः
श्रद्दधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Trusting, believing.<BR>	 2. Venerating, respecting.<BR>E. श्रत् particle of faith or respect, धा to have, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्ध
श्रद्ध nf. (-द्धं-द्धा)<BR>	 1. Respect, reverence.<BR>	 2. Wish, desire.<BR>	 3. Faith, belief,<BR>confidence.<BR>	 4. Purity.<BR>	 5. Composure of mind.<BR>	 6. Belief in divine<BR>revelation.<BR> E. श्रत् a particle implying belief, &c., धा to hold or have,<BR>affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धाकृत
श्रद्धाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done with faith.<BR> E. श्रद्धा and कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धाजाड्य
श्रद्धाजाड्य n. (-ड्यं) Obstinate adherence to one's faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धान्वित
श्रद्धान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Believing, faithful.<BR> E. श्रद्धा and अन्वित endowed<BR>with; also श्रद्धासमन्वित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धामय
श्रद्धामय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Believing, full of faith.<BR> E. श्रद्धा and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धायुक्त
श्रद्धायुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Having faith, believing.<BR> E. श्रद्धा, युक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धारहित
श्रद्धारहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Distrusting, unbelieving.<BR> E. श्रद्धा and रहित<BR>abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धालु|श्रद्धालुः
श्रद्धालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>	 1. Faithful, believing.<BR>	 2. Wishing, desirous.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-लुः) A pregnant woman longing for anything.<BR> E. श्रद्धा faith,<BR>आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धावत्|श्रद्धावन्त्
श्रद्धावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Believing, trusting, having faith.<BR> E. श्रद्धा,<BR>and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थ्|श्रंथ्
श्रन्थ् r. 9th cl. (श्रथ्नाति)<BR>	 1. To set free, to let loose, to liberate.<BR>	 2. To<BR>gladden, to delight frequently.<BR>	 3. To string, to tie together. r.<BR>1st and 10th cls. (श्रन्थति श्रन्थयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To arrange, to place in order.<BR>2. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थ|श्रंथ|श्रंथः|श्रन्थः
श्रन्थ m. (-न्थः)<BR>	 1. Loosening, liberating.<BR>	 2. Looseness, flaccidity.<BR>	 3. Ty-<BR>ing, binding, stringing.<BR>	 4. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. श्रन्थ् to tie, &c.,<BR>aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थन|श्रंथन|श्रंथनं|श्रन्थनं
श्रन्थन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Stringing flowers, &c.<BR>	 2. Killing, destroying.<BR>	 2. Ty-<BR>ing, binding.<BR>	 4. Loosening, untying.<BR> E. श्रन्थ् to tie or untie, aff.<BR>युच् or ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थित|श्रंथित|श्रन्थितः
श्रन्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Strung, connected, bound together.<BR>	 2. Over-<BR>come, surpassed, over-powered.<BR>	 3. Hurt, injured.<BR>	 4. Loosed, let<BR>loose.<BR> E. श्रन्थ् to tie, or श्रथि to hurt, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपण|श्रपणं|श्रपणः
श्रपण n. (-णं) Boiling in a pot.<BR> E. श्रै to boil, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपयित्वा
श्रपयित्वा Ind. Having boiled or dressed.<BR> E. श्रै to cook, causal v., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपित|श्रपितं
श्रपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Boiled, (anything except water, milk or Ghee.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ता) Rice-gruel.<BR> E. श्रै to cook or boil, causal v., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्
श्रम्(ञि इर्, उ)श्रमु r. 4th cl. (श्राम्यति)<BR>	 1. To perform acts of austere devo-<BR>tion, to undergo mortification or penance.<BR>	 2. To be wearied or fati-<BR>gued.<BR>	 3. To be distressed.<BR>	 4. To exert oneself. With परि, To be<BR>fatigued. With वि, 1. To take rest.<BR>	 2. To cease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम|श्रमः
श्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Military exercise.<BR>	 2. Weariness, fatigue.<BR>	 3. Labour, exer-<BR>tion, toil.<BR>	 4. Penance, mortification of the body.<BR>	 5. Hard study.<BR>6. Distress.<BR> E. श्रम् to be wearied, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमजल
श्रमजल n. (-लं) Perspiration from exertion or fatigue.<BR> E. श्रम, जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमण|श्रमणः
श्रमण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Following a low or degraded business or pro-<BR>fession.<BR>	 2. Base, vile, bad.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A religious character, an<BR>ascetic, a Yatī, one devoted to meditation for the purpose of ob-<BR>taining final emancipation from existence, probably the Sarmanes<BR>of the Greek writers.<BR>	 2. A beggar, the religious mendicant.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णा or णी)<BR>	 1. Indian spikenard, (Valeriana Jatamansi.)<BR>	 2. Bengal<BR>madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>	 3. A handsome woman.<BR>	 4. A woman<BR>of low caste or business.<BR>	 5. A female mendicant.<BR> E. श्रम् to be<BR>wearied, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमसिद्ध
श्रमसिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Accomplished by labour or exertion.<BR> E. श्रम and<BR>सिद्ध accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमार्त्त|श्रमार्त
श्रमार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Exhausted, overcome with fatigue.<BR> E. श्रम and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमिन्
श्रमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि)<BR>	 1. Wearying, tiring, undergoing or incurring<BR>weariness or fatigue.<BR>	 2. Laborious, diligent.<BR> E. श्रम् to be weary,<BR>aff. इनि or घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्भ्|श्रंभ्
श्रम्भ्(उ)श्रम्भु r. 1st cl. (श्रम्भते) To be careless or inattentive, to err, to<BR>neglect, to mistake. With वि, To confide in, to put faith in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रय|श्रयः
श्रय m. (-यः) Asylum, refuge, protection.<BR> E. श्रि to serve, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयण|श्रयणं
श्रयण n. (-णं) Asylum, refuge, shelter, protection.<BR> E. श्रि to serve, aff.<BR>ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयणीय
श्रयणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be defended or sheltered.<BR> E. श्रि to serve, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रव|श्रवः
श्रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The ear.<BR>	 2. Oozing, dripping.<BR>	 3. The hypotenuse of a<BR>triangle.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, &c., aff. अप्; also श्रवण, स्रव, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवण|श्रवणं|श्रवणः
श्रवण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Produced in or under the sign ŚRAVAṆĀ.<BR>	 mn.<BR>(-णः-णं)<BR>	 1. The ear.<BR>	 2. Hearing.<BR>	 3. The hypotenuse of a triangle.<BR>n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Service.<BR>	 2. Dripping, oozing.<BR>	 mf. (-णः-णा) The twenty-<BR>third of the lunar asterisms, represented by three footsteps, and<BR>containing three stars or Acquilæ.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The act of hearing.<BR>2. Studying.<BR>	 3. Fame, glory.<BR>	 4. Wealth.<BR>	 5. That which is heard,<BR>i. e. The Veda.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, &c., aff. ल्युट् or युच्; or श्रवणा the<BR>asterism, अण् aff. of derivation, and the effect rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणगोचर|श्रवणगोचरः
श्रवणगोचर m. (-रः) Ear-shot. Adj. Within the range of hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणपथ|श्रवणपथः
श्रवणपथ m. (-थः) The ear.<BR> E. श्रवण, and पथ for पथिन् path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणाधिकारिन्
श्रवणाधिकारिन् m. (-री) A speaker, an addresser.<BR> E. श्रवण, and अधिकारिन्<BR>connected with or acting on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणेन्द्रिय|श्रवणेंद्रिय
श्रवणेन्द्रिय n. (-यं) The organ of hearing, the ear.<BR> E. श्रवण, इन्द्रिय organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणोदर
श्रवणोदर n. (-रं) The hollow of the outer ear.<BR> E. श्रवण, उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्
श्रवस् n. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The ear.<BR>	 2. Fame, glory.<BR>	 3. Wealth.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, aff.<BR>असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्य|श्रवस्यं
श्रवस्य n. (-स्यं) Fame, glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवाप्य|श्रवाप्यः
श्रवाप्य m. (-प्यः) An animal fit or proper for sacrifice.<BR> E. श्रु to drip,<BR>(Ghee,) आप्य Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रविष्ठ
श्रविष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Produced in or under the sign ŚRAVISHṬHĀ.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ष्ठा) The twenty-fourth lunar asterism, also called DHANISHṬHĀ,<BR>corresponding to the DOLPHIN,<BR> E. श्रव an ear, मतुप् poss. aff., इष्ठन्<BR>aff. of the superlative, and the possessive rejected; the attribu-<BR>tive is formed by the aff. अण् and that again or its effect option-<BR>ally rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रविष्ठाज|श्रविष्ठाजः
श्रविष्ठाज m. (-जः) The planet MERCURY.<BR> E. श्रविष्ठा the asterism, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रा
श्रा r. 2nd cl. (श्राति)<BR>	 1. To boil, to cook, to mature, to ripen, &c.<BR>	 2. To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">Page733-b+ 60</a>]<BR>sweat. Causal from, (श्रपयति ते) To render mature or ripe by cook-<BR>ing, &c. (श्रापयति) To heat, to cause to sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राण|श्राणं
श्राण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Boiled, dressed, (anything except butter,<BR>milk or water.)<BR>	 2. Moist, wet.<BR>	 f. (-णा) Rice-Gruel.<BR> E. श्रै to cook,<BR>aff. क्त, form irr.; or properly श्रा, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्ध|श्राद्धं
श्राद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Faithful, believing.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं) A funeral ceremony<BR>observed at various fixed periods and for different purposes, con-<BR>sisting of offerings with water and fire to the gods and manes,<BR>and gifts and food to the relations present and assisting Brāh-<BR>mans; it is especially performed for a present recently deceased,<BR>or for three paternal ancestors or for all ancestors collectively,<BR>and is supposed necessary to secure the ascent and residence of<BR>the souls of the deceased in a world appropriated to the manes,<BR>The following distributions of this ceremony are specified: the<BR>पार्व्वणं in honour of three ancestors, एकोद्दिष्टं of one, नित्यं regular,<BR>नैमित्तिकं occasionally, काम्यं for the attainment of some particular<BR>object, आह्निकं daily, वृद्धिः for the obtaining of increase of pros-<BR>perity, and सपिण्डनं in which the balls of meat offered to the<BR>deceased individually and collectively are blended together.<BR>There are many other kinds: those for a person recently decea-<BR>sed are one on the day after mourning expires, and twelve others<BR>in twelve successive months; one at the end of the third fort-<BR>night, one in the sixth month, and one in the twelfth, concluding<BR>with a Sapiṇḍaṇa, on the anniversary of the person's death; in<BR>general they are all performed in the course of the two or three<BR>first days, and the Śrāddha for the deceased is only annually<BR>repeated. There is also a short of Śrāddha performed daily<BR>during the days of mourning, usually ten, on which a funeral cake<BR>is presented, increasing one or more each day till ten cakes are<BR>offered.<BR> E. श्रद्धा faith, अण् or ण aff. of possession or relation, as the<BR>abandonment or presentation of meat, &c., through faith of<BR>its efficacy, in behalf of the souls of the deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धकर
श्राद्धकर m. (-रः) The offerer or an obsequial oblation.<BR> E. श्राद्ध, कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धकर्म्मन्|श्राद्धकर्मन्
श्राद्धकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्मं) The rite or ceremony of funeral oblation.<BR> E. श्राद्ध,<BR>and कर्म्मन् act; also श्राद्धक्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धकृत्
श्राद्धकृत् m. (-कृत्) The celebrator of an obsequial rite. श्राद्ध, कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धद|श्राद्धदः
श्राद्धद m. (-दः) The offerer of an obsequial rite.<BR> E. श्राद्ध, द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धदिन|श्राद्धदिनः
श्राद्धदिन mn. (-नः-नं) The anniversary of the death of a relative to<BR>whom a Śrāddha is offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धदेव|श्राद्धदेवः
श्राद्धदेव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. YAMA.<BR>	 2. A god presiding our funeral rites.<BR>	 3. A<BR>VIŚHWADEVA.<BR> E. श्राद्ध the funeral ceremony called Śrāddha,<BR>and देव deity; as judge and monarch of the dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धदेवता
श्राद्धदेवता f. (-ता) A divinity presiding over obsequial rites, a Pitṛ or<BR>progenitor, or YAMA.<BR> E. श्राद्ध, and देवता divinity: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धभुज्
श्राद्धभुज् mfn. (-भुक्) Eating or partaking of the food prepared at a<BR>Śrāddha or obsequial rite.<BR> E. श्राद्ध भुज्, who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धशिष्ट
श्राद्धशिष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Food that has been presented to the manes.<BR> E. श्राद्ध, शिष्ट left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिक|श्राद्धिकः
श्राद्धिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. The object, receiver, or enjoyer of an obse-<BR>quial oblation.<BR>	 2. Anything relating to a Śrāddha.<BR> E. श्राद्ध as<BR>above, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिन्
श्राद्धिन् mfn. (-द्धी-द्धिनी-द्धि) The object or receiver of a funeral oblation.<BR> E. श्राद्ध, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्त|श्रांत|श्रान्तः
श्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Wearied, fatigued.<BR>	 2. Calmed, tranquil.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>An ascetic, one with subdued passions.<BR> E. श्रम् to be weary, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्तसंवाहन|श्रान्तसंवाहनं
श्रान्तसंवाहन n. (-नं) Affording rest or relief to the weary, giving them<BR>seats, beds, &c.<BR> E. श्रान्त wearied, संवाहन relieving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्ति|श्रांति|श्रांतिः|श्रान्तिः
श्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः) Weariness, exhaustion.<BR> E. श्रम् to be weary, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राम|श्रामः
श्राम r. 10th cl. (श्रामयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To call, to summon, to invite.<BR>	 2. To<BR>counsel, to advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राम|श्रामः
श्राम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A month.<BR>	 2. A temporary shed, or platform and<BR>canopy.<BR>	 3. Time.<BR> E. श्रम् to be weary, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रामणेर|श्रामणेरः
श्रामणेर m. (-रः) A follower or disciple and servant of the principal<BR>Jainas or Jinas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राय|श्रायः
श्राय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Sacred or belonging to the goddess SHRĪ.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>Refuge, reliance, shelter or protection.<BR> E. श्रि to serve, aff. अण्, or<BR>in the attributive form, श्री the goddess, घञ् aff., and इ substituted<BR>for the primitive vowel changed to अय, and अ made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रायस|श्रायसः
श्रायस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Produced in or on the best, &c.<BR> E. श्रयस् the best<BR>अण् aff., and the form changed by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राव|श्रावः
श्राव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Oozing, dropping, flowing.<BR>	 2. Hearing, listening.<BR> E. श्रु<BR>to ooze, &c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावक|श्रावकः
श्रावक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The lay votary of a Buddha or Jina.<BR>	 2. A crow.<BR>	 3.<BR>A hearer.<BR>	 4. A pupil.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, causal form, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावण|श्रावणः
श्रावण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>	 1. Produced in or under the asterism Śrāvaṇā.<BR>2. Relating to the ear or hearing.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. The month Śrāvaṇā<BR>or Śrāvaṇ, (July-August.)<BR>	 2. A heretic, an impostor.<BR>	 3. Name<BR>of a Vaiśya devotee killed by DAŚARATHA through mistake, and<BR>for which he was cursed by Śhrāvana's old parents, to die of<BR>a broken heart at the separation of his sons.<BR>	 n. (-ण) Causing to<BR>be heard.<BR>	 f. (-णा) A plant, commonly Katuki.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. Day of<BR>full-moon in the month Śrāvaṇa.<BR>	 2. A religious rite performed<BR>in this day.<BR> E. श्रवणा the asterism, &c., aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणिक|श्रावणिकः
श्रावणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating to or produced in the month Śhrāva-<BR>ṇa.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The month Śrāvaṇa.<BR> E. श्रवणा the asterism in<BR>which the moon is full this month, and ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणीय
श्रावणीय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) To be declared or pronounced, to be made to<BR>be heard.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, causal v., अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावन्ती
श्रावन्ती f. (-न्ती) A city, also Darmapattan.<BR> E. श्रु to ooze, causal form<BR>झच् aff.; also read श्रावस्ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावयितव्य
श्रावयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be declared, to be made to be heard.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, causal v., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावष्ठीय
श्रावष्ठीय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Produced in or under the asterism ŚRAVISH-<BR>ṬHĀ, relating to it, &c.<BR> E. श्रविष्ठा, and छण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावित
श्रावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Spoken or read, caused to be heard.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राव्य
श्राव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be heard.<BR>	 1. To be read or related, to be<BR>caused to be heard.<BR>	 f. (-व्या) Plain, audible.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, ण्यत् aff.,<BR>or causal v., and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रि
श्रि r. 1st cl. (श्रयति-ते) To serve. With आङ् prefixed, 1. To seek<BR>asylum, to depend upon, to have recourse to.<BR>	 2. To be near to.<BR>	 3.<BR>To use, to employ.<BR>	 4. To choose.<BR>	 5. To enter.<BR>	 6. To inhabit. With<BR>अप and आङ्, To quit, to forsake. With उत् or सम्, To be high or<BR>elevated. With वि, अप, and आङ्, 1. To fall, to prostrate, to wor-<BR>ship.<BR>	 2. To expect, to rely upon, to trust to. With सम, 1. To<BR>attain.<BR>	 2. To see.<BR>	 3. To depend upon.<BR>	 4. To have recourse to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रित|श्रितः
श्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Cherished, protected, refuged.<BR>	 2. Served,<BR>honoured, worshipped.<BR>	 3. Joined with, contiguous to, connected<BR>with.<BR>	 4. Covered, overspread.<BR>	 5. Having, possessing.<BR>	 6. Auxiliary,<BR>subservient.<BR>	 7. Collected.<BR> E. श्रि to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रितवत्
श्रितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Served, honoured.<BR>	 2. Taking refuge with.<BR>E. श्रि to serve, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिति|श्रितिः
श्रिति f. (-तिः) Approach, recourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिमन्य
श्रिमन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Haughty, confident in wealth, beauty, &c. E.<BR>श्री, and मन्य who thinks, the vowel of the first made short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिष्
श्रिष्(उ)श्रिषु r. 1st cl. (श्रेषति) To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री r. 9th cl. (श्रीणाति श्रीणीते) To cook, to dress, to boil. r. 1st and<BR>10th cls. (श्रयति-ते श्राययति-ते) To satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री f. (-श्रीः)<BR>	 1. Fortune, prosperity, success, thriving.<BR>	 2. Wealth.<BR>	 3.<BR>Beauty, splendour, lustre.<BR>	 4. Appearance.<BR>	 5. Light.<BR>	 6. Any virtue<BR>or excellence.<BR>	 7. The three objects of life collectively, or love<BR>“काम,” duty “धर्म्म,” and wealth “अर्थ”.<BR>	 8. Dress, decoration.<BR>	 9.<BR>State, paraphernalia.<BR>	 10. Majesty, royalty.<BR>	 11. Superhuman<BR>power.<BR>	 12. Intellect, understanding.<BR>	 13. Elevation, consequence.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">Page734-b+ 60</a>]<BR>14. Fame, glory.<BR>	 15. The goddess LAKṢMĪ, the wife of VIṢṆU,<BR>and deity of plenty and prosperity.<BR>	 16. A name of SARASWATĪ.<BR>17. The mother of KUNTHU, the seventeenth Jina of the pre-<BR>sent age.<BR>	 18. The Sarala tree, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>	 19. The Bilwa<BR>tree.<BR>	 20. A lotus.<BR>	 21. Cloves.<BR>	 22. A prefix to the names of deities,<BR>forming a kind of invocation at the beginning of a letter, &c.,<BR>and often used repeatedly, as Śhrī Śhrī DURGĀ; also a prefix<BR>of respect to proper names of persons, as Śhrī JAYADEVA; also<BR>of works, as Śhrī Bhāgavat; this use of it is elliptical; the poss-<BR>essive aff. मतुप् or adj. युक्त joined, &c. being understood, and the<BR>sense will then be, the splendid, the illustrious, the famous,<BR>&c.<BR> E. श्रि to serve, (i. e. whom the world worships,) क्विप् aff.<BR>and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकण्ठ|श्रीकंठ|श्रीकण्ठः
श्रीकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A country N. W. of Delhi, or about<BR>Thāneshwar.<BR>	 3. BHAVABHŪTĪ, the author of the Mālati-Mādhava,<BR>a celebrated drama.<BR> E. श्री prosperity or eloquence, कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकण्ठपदलाञ्छन|श्रीकण्ठपदलाञ्छनः
श्रीकण्ठपदलाञ्छन m. (-नः) BHAVABHŪTĪ, the poet.<BR> E. श्रीकण्ठ and पद the<BR>the name of title, लाञ्छन a mark; he who is known by the title<BR>of Śhrī-kaṇṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकण्ठसख|श्रीकंठसख|श्रीकण्ठसखः
श्रीकण्ठसख m. (-खः) KUVERA.<BR> E. श्रीकण्ठ ŚIVA, and सखि the friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकर|श्रीकरं|श्रीकरः
श्रीकर mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं) Giving fortune or prosperity.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The red lotus.<BR> E. श्री fortune, and कर who makes or<BR>confers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकरण|श्रीकरणं
श्रीकरण m. (-णः) A pen.<BR> E. श्री the word Śhrī, करण implement of making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकान्त|श्रीकांत|श्रीकान्तः
श्रीकान्त m. (-न्तः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. श्री the goddess, and कान्त husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीकारिन्
श्रीकारिन् mf. (-री) An antelope.<BR> E. श्री increasing, (nourishment, &c.) कृ<BR>to make, aff. णिनि; the flesh being considered as highly digestible<BR>and nutritive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीखण्ड|श्रीखंड|श्रीखण्डः
श्रीखण्ड mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं) Sandal-wood.<BR> E. श्री fortune, and खण्ड part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीगदित
श्रीगदित n. (-तं) One of the minor dramatic compositions, a piece in<BR>one act dedicated chiefly to the goddess of prosperity.<BR> E. श्री and<BR>गदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीगर्भ|श्रीगर्भः
श्रीगर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A sword.<BR> E. श्री fortune, and गर्भ womb or origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीग्रह|श्रीग्रहः
श्रीग्रह m. (-हः) A trough for watering birds.<BR> E. श्री wealth, ग्रह taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीघन|श्रीघनं|श्रीघनः
श्रीघन n. (-नं) Sour curds.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A Buddha or Bauddha saint.<BR> E. श्री<BR>prosperity, and घन a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीचक्र|श्रीचक्रं
श्रीचक्र n. (-क्रं)<BR>	 1. A magical diagram.<BR>	 2. An astrological division of the<BR>body, the uterine or pubic region.<BR>	 3. A wheel of INDRA'S car.<BR>4. The circle of the globe or earth.<BR> E. श्री prosperity, &c., चक्र a<BR>wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीज|श्रीजः
श्रीज m. (-जः) The deity of love.<BR> E. श्री LAKṢMĪ, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीद|श्रीदः
श्रीद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Conferring wealth, prosperity, &c.<BR>	 m. (-दः) KUVERA,<BR>the god or riches.<BR> E. श्री wealth, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीधर|श्रीधरः
श्रीधर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A Jina of the past period.<BR> E. श्री the<BR>goddess, fortune, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीनन्दन|श्रीनंदन|श्रीनन्दनः
श्रीनन्दन m. (-नः) The deity of love, KĀMA.<BR> E. श्री LAKṢMĪ, नन्दन the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीनिकेतन|श्रीनिकेतनः
श्रीनिकेतन m. (-नः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. श्री the goddess, and निकेतन abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीनिवास|श्रीनिवासः
श्रीनिवास m. (-सः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. श्री the goddess, and निवास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपति|श्रीपतिः
श्रीपति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A king, a prince.<BR> E. श्री the goddess of<BR>fortune or rank, and पति husband or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपथ|श्रीपथः
श्रीपथ m. (-थः) A highway, a royal road.<BR> E. श्री royal paraphernalia, पथ<BR>for पथिन् road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपर्ण|श्रीपर्णं
श्रीपर्ण n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. A tree, the wood of which is used to pro-<BR>cure fire by attrition, (Premna spinosa.)<BR>	 f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. A shrub,<BR>(Gmelina arborea.)<BR>	 2. A medicinal plant, commonly Kāyaphal.<BR>3. The silk-cotton tree.<BR>	 4. An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.) E.<BR>श्री beauty or the goddess, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपर्णिका
श्रीपर्णिका f. (-का) A medicinal shrub, commonly Kāyaphal.<BR> E. कन्<BR>added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपिष्ट|श्रीपिष्टः
श्रीपिष्ट m. (-ष्टः) Turpentine.<BR> E. श्री the Śarala or pine, and पिष्ट pounded ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=734-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपुत्त्र
श्रीपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. KĀMA.<BR> E. श्री fortune, or the goddess,<BR>पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीपुष्प|श्रीपुष्पं
श्रीपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) Cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीफल|श्रीफलः
श्रीफल m. (-लः) A fruit tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>	 f. (-ला or ली)<BR>	 1. The<BR>indigo-plant, (Indigofera tinctoria.)<BR>	 2. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>The Bel-fruit.<BR> E. श्री beauty or the goddess, (to whom it may be<BR>offered,) फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीभद्र
श्रीभद्र m. (-द्रः) A fragrant grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR> E. श्री LAKṢMĪ, भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीभ्रातृ
श्रीभ्रातृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. श्री the goddess, भ्रातृ<BR>brother; being recovered as well a LAKṢMĪ, at the churning of<BR>the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीमत्|श्रीमन्त्
श्रीमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Wealthy, opulent.<BR>	 2. Pleasing, beautiful.<BR>3. Prosperous, fortunate, thriving.<BR>	 4. Famous, illustrious.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-मान्)<BR>	 1. A tree, commonly Tila or Tilaka.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. KUVERA,<BR>the god of wealth.<BR>	 4. ŚIVA.<BR>	 5. A title applied to any venerable<BR>person.<BR> E. श्री beauty, &c., मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीमस्तक|श्रीमस्तकः
श्रीमस्तक m. (-कः) Garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीमुख|श्रीमुखः
श्रीमुख m. (-खः) The seventh year of the Indian cycle.<BR> E. श्री prosperity, मुख chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीयुक्त|श्रीयुक्तः
श्रीयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Famous, illustrious.<BR>	 2. Fortunate, wealthy.<BR>E. श्री prosperity, and युक्त joined with, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीयुत|श्रीयुतः
श्रीयुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Famous, illustrious.<BR>	 2. Fortunate, wealthy. E.<BR>श्री fortune, युत joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीरस|श्रीरसः
श्रीरस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Turpentine.<BR>	 2. Resin.<BR> E. श्री the Sārala tree or pine, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीराग|श्रीरागः
श्रीराग m. (-गः) One of the Rāgas or personified musical modes.<BR> E. श्री<BR>illustrious, राग the mode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीराम|श्रीरामः
श्रीराम m. (-मः) RĀMACHANDRA.<BR> E. श्री celebrated, and राम Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रील|श्रीलः
श्रील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Fortunate, prosperous.<BR>	 2. Rich, wealthy.<BR>	 3.<BR>Beautiful.<BR>	 4. Famous.<BR> E. श्री fortune, लच् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्स|श्रीवत्सः
श्रीवत्स m. (-त्सः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A particular mark, usually said to be a<BR>curl of hair, on the breast of VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 3. A hole in a<BR>wall made for felonious purposes.<BR>	 4. The emblem of the tenth<BR>Jina, or the mark above ascribed to VIṢṆU or KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. श्री<BR>LAKṢMĪ, and वत्स dear to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्सकिन्
श्रीवत्सकिन् m. (-की) A horse having a curl of hair on his breast. E.<BR>श्रीवत्स the mark of VIṢṆU, कन् aff. of comparison, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्सभृत्
श्रीवत्सभृत् m. (-भृत्) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. श्रीवत्स the mark so termed, भृत् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्सलाञ्छन|श्रीवत्सलांछन|श्रीवत्सलाञ्छनः
श्रीवत्सलाञ्छन m. (-नः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. श्रीवत्स the figure so named, लाञ्छन sign,<BR>mark, (whose.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्साङ्क|श्रीवत्साङ्कः
श्रीवत्साङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) VIṢṆU: see the last.<BR> E. श्रीवत्स and अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवराह|श्रीवराहः
श्रीवराह m. (-हः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. श्री illustrious, वराह the Boar-Avatār.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवास|श्रीवासः
श्रीवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Turpentine.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A lotus.<BR>	 4. ŚIVA.<BR> E. श्री<BR>the Śarala or pine, or LAKṢMĪ, &c.; and वास abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवासस्
श्रीवासस् n. (-सः) Turpentine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवृक्ष|श्रीवृक्षः
श्रीवृक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. The holy-fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR>	 2. The Bilwa-<BR>tree.<BR>	 3. The Aśwattha-tree.<BR> E. श्री auspicious, वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवृक्षक|श्रीवृक्षकः
श्रीवृक्षक m. (-कः) A curl or lock of hair on the chest of a horse: a<BR>various reading perhaps for श्रीवत्सकः see श्रीवत्सकिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवेष्ट|श्रीवेष्टः
श्रीवेष्ट m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. Turpentine.<BR>	 2. Resin.<BR> E. श्री the Śarala or pine tree, वेष्ट extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीश|श्रीशः
श्रीश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. RĀMACHANDRA.<BR> E. श्री the goddess<BR>LAKṢMĪ, also incarnate in SĪTĀ, and ईश husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीसंज्ञ
श्रीसंज्ञ n. (-ज्ञं) Cloves.<BR> E. श्री LAKṢMĪ, and संज्ञा appellation, the names<BR>of the goddess being all applied to the spice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीसहोदर|श्रीसहोदरः
श्रीसहोदर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. The horse of INDRA.<BR>	 3. Camphor. E.<BR>श्री the goddess, and सहोदर uterine brother; being reproduced<BR>with her and other objects, at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीहस्तिनी
श्रीहस्तिनी f. (-नी) The sun-flower, (Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR> E. श्री<BR>LAKṢMĪ, हस्त the hand, इनि and ङीष् affs.; held in the hand of the<BR>goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रु
श्रु r. 1st cl. form irr. (शृणोति) To hear: form reg. (श्रवति) To go, to<BR>move, especially as a fluid, to drop, to ooze, to flow. r. 5th cl.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">Page735-b+ 60</a>]<BR>(pp. श्रुत, pres. शृणोति, pass. श्रूयते)<BR>	 1. To hear.<BR>	 2. To obey. With प्रति<BR>or सम् prefixed, To promise, to assent or agree to. With वि, To be<BR>famous. With अनु, To hear. With अभि, To listen. With आङ्, To<BR>promise, (with the dat. of the person to whom the promise is made.)<BR>With उप, To hear, to learn from. With सम, (Atm.; when used<BR>intransitively.) To hear, to listen to. Caus. (श्रावयति-ते) To recite<BR>to, to communicate. Desid. (शुश्रूषते)<BR>	 1. To desire to hear.<BR>	 2. To<BR>obey.<BR>	 3. To wait upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुग्वारु|श्रुग्वारुः
श्रुग्वारु m. (-रुः) A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुघ्निका
श्रुघ्निका f. (-का) Natron, alkali. “सर्जिकाक्षारे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत|श्रुतं|श्रुतः
श्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Heard.<BR>	 2. Understood.<BR>	 3. Well-known.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Sacred science, holy writ, &c.<BR>	 2. The object of hearing, that<BR>which is heard.<BR>	 3. Learning in general.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतकीर्त्ति|श्रुतकीर्ति|श्रुतकीर्त्तिः
श्रुतकीर्त्ति mfn. (-र्त्तिः-र्त्तिः-र्त्ति) Famous, celebrated.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. A divine<BR>sage.<BR>	 2. A generous man, a benefactor, a donor.<BR>	 f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>river.<BR>	 2. The wife of BHARATA.<BR> E. श्रुत heard, कीर्त्ति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतदेवी
श्रुतदेवी f. (-वी) SARASWATĪ.<BR> E. श्रुत that which is heard, (science, &c.)<BR>and देवी presiding deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतधर|श्रुतधरः
श्रुतधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Recollecting, remembering what has been<BR>heard.<BR>	 2. Having or observing the Vedas.<BR> E. श्रुत, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतर्षि|श्रुतर्षिः
श्रुतर्षि m. (-र्षिः) A Ṛṣi of a particular order; one by whom holy writ<BR>has been heard, not taught; as the author of the Suśruta, a<BR>medical work, the son of VIŚVĀMITRA, &c.<BR> E. श्रुत heard, and<BR>ऋषि a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतवत्|श्रुतवन्त्
श्रुतवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Hearing, having heard.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतश्रवोनुज|श्रुतश्रवोनुजः
श्रुतश्रवोनुज m. (-जः) The planet ŚHANI or SATURN.<BR> E. श्रुतश्रवस् one of the<BR>other sons of SŪRYA, and अनुज younger born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतादान|श्रुतादानं
श्रुतादान n. (-नं) Citing the Vedas.<BR> E. श्रुत holy writ, आदान referring to, taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुताध्ययनसम्पन्न|श्रुताध्ययनसम्पन्नः
श्रुताध्ययनसम्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Well read in sacred science, conversant<BR>with the Vedas, and the branches of knowledge or philosophy,<BR>dependent on them.<BR> E. श्रुत heard, (knowledge of grammar, &c., that<BR>has been taught viva voce,) अध्ययन perusal, (of the Vedas,) सम्पन्न<BR>accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतान्वित|श्रुतान्वितः
श्रुतान्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Acquainted with or conforming to the Vedas.<BR>E. श्रुत, and अन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुति|श्रुतिः
श्रुति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The Vedas, severally or collectively, scripture, holy<BR>writ.<BR>	 2. An ear.<BR>	 3. Hearing.<BR>	 4. Intelligence, news, rumour, re-<BR>port.<BR>	 5. (In music,) A division of the octave, a quarter tone or<BR>interval, of which twenty-two are enumerated; four constituting<BR>a major tone, three a minor, and two a semitone: the Śhrutis are<BR>personified as nymphs.<BR>	 6. A sound in general.<BR>	 7. The constellation<BR>Śravaṇā.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिकट|श्रुतिकटः
श्रुतिकट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. Penance, expiation.<BR>	 2. A snake.<BR> E. श्रुति the Vedas,<BR>organ ear, &c., and कट् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिकटु|श्रुतिकटुः
श्रुतिकटु m. (-टुः) A Harsh sound, (regarded as a fault in rhetoric.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिकथित|श्रुतिकथितः
श्रुतिकथित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taught or prescribed by the Vedas.<BR> E. श्रुति<BR>as above, and कथित said, declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिचोदन|श्रुतिचोदनः
श्रुतिचोदन n. (-नं) Holy precept or injunction, the doctrine of the<BR>Vedas.<BR> E. श्रुति, and चोदन saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिजीविका
श्रुतिजीविका f. (-का) Law, the code of laws.<BR> E. श्रुति the Vedas, and<BR>जीविका living; existing to scripture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतितत्पर|श्रुतितत्परः
श्रुतितत्पर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Hearing, having ears.<BR>	 2. Studying the Vedas.<BR>E. श्रुति hearing, or the Vedas, and तत्पर attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिद्वैध
श्रुतिद्वैध n. (-धं) Disagreement or contradiction of any two passages in<BR>the Vedas, or of two Vedas.<BR> E. श्रुति, and द्वैध difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिधर|श्रुतिधरः
श्रुतिधर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Having, being versed in, or observing the<BR>Vedas.<BR>	 2. Hearing.<BR> E. श्रुति, and धर who or what has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिन्
श्रुतिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>	 1. Hearing.<BR>	 2. Observing, obeying.<BR>	 3. Having<BR>or following the Vedas.<BR> E. श्रुत, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिनिदर्शन
श्रुतिनिदर्शन n. (-नं) The evidence of revelation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=735-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिमूल
श्रुतिमूल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The root of the ear.<BR>	 2. The text of the Vedas. E.<BR>श्रुति, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिमण्डल
श्रुतिमण्डल n. (-लं) The outer ear.<BR> E. श्रुति, and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिवर्ज्जित|श्रुतिवर्जित|श्रुतिवर्ज्जितः
श्रुतिवर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Deaf.<BR>	 2. Ignorant or unread in the Vedas.<BR>E. श्रुति hearing, or the Vedas, and वर्ज्जित abandoned, lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिविषय|श्रुतिविषयः
श्रुतिविषय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. An object or doctrine of the Vedas.<BR>	 2. Sound,<BR>the object of the sense of hearing.<BR>	 3. The reach of the ear.<BR>	 4. The<BR>ear.<BR> E. श्रुति, and विषय an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिवेध|श्रुतिवेधः
श्रुतिवेध m. (-धः) The boring of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिस्मृतिविहित
श्रुतिस्मृतिविहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Scriptural, declared by the Vedas and the<BR>law.<BR> E. श्रुति, and स्मृति, and विहित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्यनुप्रास|श्रुत्यनुप्रासः
श्रुत्यनुप्रास m. (-सः) Alliteration.<BR> E. श्रुति hearing, and अनुप्रास similarity of sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्युक्त
श्रुत्युक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Said or enjoined by the Vedas.<BR> E. श्रुति, and उक्त<BR>said; also श्रुत्युदित, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्वा
श्रुत्वा Ind. Having heard.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुव|श्रुवः
श्रुव m. (-वः) Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>	 nf. (-वं-वा) A sort of ladle used for<BR>pouring Ghee or oiled butter at a sacrifice.<BR> E. श्रु to ooze or leak,<BR>aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रूयमाण
श्रूयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Hearing, being hearing.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, pass. v.,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेढी
श्रेढी f. (-ढी) A progression, (in math.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेढीफल
श्रेढीफल n. (-लं) The sum of a progression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणि|श्रेणिः
श्रेणि mf. (-णिः-णिः or -णी)<BR>	 1. A line, a row, a range.<BR>	 2. A multitude.<BR>	 3.<BR>A company of artizans following the same business.<BR>	 4. A corpo-<BR>ration, a company of traders or those dealing in the same articles.<BR>5. A bucket, a baling vessel.<BR> E. श्रि to serve, नि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणिक|श्रेणिकः
श्रेणिक m. (-कः) The name of one of the kings of Magadha, contemporary<BR>with and patron of SĀKYA-SINHA., f. (-का) A tent.<BR> E. श्रेणि a line, &c.,<BR>कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणिधर्म
श्रेणिधर्म m. Plu. The customs of trades or guilds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणिभूत
श्रेणिभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made or become a heap.<BR>	 2. Arranged, set in<BR>rows.<BR> E. श्रेणि a range, भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेधी
श्रेधी f. (-धी)<BR>	 1. A set or succession of substances.<BR>	 2. (In arithmetic,)<BR>Progression. E. A various reading of श्रेष्ठी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्
श्रेयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः) Best, excellent, most excellent. Ind. Well, most<BR>excellent.<BR>	 n. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Virtue, moral merit.<BR>	 2. Final happiness.<BR>	 3.<BR>Good fortune, auspiciousness, prosperity.<BR>	 m. (-यान्) The 11th Jina<BR>or Jaina pontiff.<BR>	 f. (-यसी)<BR>	 1. A plant resembling pepper, (Pothos<BR>officinalis.)<BR>	 2. A shrub, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>	 3. Yellow myro-<BR>balan.<BR> E. श्र substituted for प्रशस्त good, and ईयसुन् aff. of the irr.<BR>superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्कर
श्रेयस्कर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Conferring, or the means of future felicity.<BR>2. Propitious.<BR>	 3. Making better or superior.<BR> E. श्रेयस् and कर who or<BR>what does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्काम
श्रेयस्काम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Desiring final felicity, &c.<BR> E. श्रेयस्, काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्त्व
श्रेयस्त्व n. (-स्त्वं)<BR>	 1. Superiority, betterness.<BR>	 2. Final felicity, &c.<BR> E. श्रेयस्<BR>and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयांश
श्रेयांश m. (-शः) The eleventh Jina or Jaina pontiff of the present era; also श्रेयांस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयोर्थिन्
श्रेयोर्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Desirous of good, ambitious.<BR> E. श्रेयस्, and<BR>अर्थिन् who asks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठ|श्रेष्ठं|श्रेष्ठः
श्रेष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Best, excellent, most excellent, pre-eminent.<BR>	 2.<BR>Oldest, senior.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठः)<BR>	 1. KUVERA.<BR>	 2. A king.<BR>	 3. A Brāhman.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-ष्ठं) Cow's milk.<BR> E. श्र for प्रशस्त best, इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठकाष्ठ|श्रेष्ठकाष्ठः
श्रेष्ठकाष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) The main pillar of a house.<BR> E. श्रेष्ठ best, and काष्ठ timber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठवाच्
श्रेष्ठवाच् f. (-वाक्) Adj. Eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठता
श्रेष्ठता f. (-ता) Superiority, betterness, excellence.<BR> E. श्रेष्ठ, and तल् aff.;<BR>also with त्व, श्रेष्ठत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठाश्रम|श्रेष्ठाश्रमः
श्रेष्ठाश्रम m. (-मः) The best order of life, viz. that of a householder.<BR> E. श्रेष्ठ<BR>best, आश्रम order or state; the householder being considered the<BR>best of the four orders, as it supports the other three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठिन्
श्रेष्ठिन् mfn. (-ष्ठी-ष्ठिनी-ष्ठि) Best, chief.<BR>	 m. (-ष्ठी)<BR>	 1. An artist eminent by<BR>birth.<BR>	 2. The head or chief of a body of persons following the same<BR>trade or occupation, a president, a foreman.<BR> E. श्रेष्ठ excellence, इनि<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रै
श्रै r. 1st cl (श्रायति)<BR>	 1. To boil, to cook.<BR>	 2. To melt, to liquefy.<BR>	 3. To sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रैष्ठ्य|श्रैष्ठ्यं
श्रैष्ठ्य n. (-ष्ठ्यं) Superiority, betterness, preference.<BR> E. श्रेष्ठ, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोण्
श्रोण्(ऋ)श्रोणृ r. 1st cl. (श्रोणति) To accumulate, to heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोण|श्रोणः
श्रोण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Dressed, cooked, matured.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A cripple.<BR>f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. The constellation Śravaṇā.<BR>	 2. Rice-gruel.<BR> E. श्रोण् to<BR>heap together, aff. अच्; or शॄ to injure, Unādi aff. न ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणि|श्रोणिः
श्रोणि f. (-णिः or णी)<BR>	 1. The hip and loins.<BR>	 2. A road, a way.<BR> E. श्रोण् to<BR>heap, aff. इन्; or श्रु to hear, Unādi aff. नि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणितट|श्रोणितटः
श्रोणितट m. (-टः) The slope of the hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणिफलक|श्रोणिफलकं
श्रोणिफलक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The hip and loins, or the hip only.<BR>	 2. The hip-<BR>bone, the os ilium.<BR> E. श्रोणि the same, and फल fruit, कन् aff. of<BR>comparison, or फलक a plank; also श्रोणिफल n. (-लं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणिविम्ब
श्रोणिविम्ब n. (-म्बं) A string worn round the loins, a waist band.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतस्
श्रोतस् n. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The ear.<BR>	 2. The current of a stream.<BR>	 3. An organ of<BR>sense.<BR>	 4. The trunk of an elephant.<BR> E. श्रु to hear or to leak, aff.<BR>असुन्, and तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतव्य|श्रोतव्यं
श्रोतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be heard, or listened to.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, तव्य<BR>aff. of the future participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतृ
श्रोतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Hearing, a hearer, who hears.<BR> E. श्रु to hear. तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्र|श्रोत्रं
श्रोत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The ear.<BR>	 2. The veda.<BR> E. श्रु to hear, Unādi aff. ष्ट्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रसुख
श्रोत्रसुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Melodious, musical, sounding agreeably. E.<BR>श्रोत्र, and सुख pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रादि
श्रोत्रादि Ind. The five senses.<BR> E. श्रोत्र and आदि etcetera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रिय|श्रोत्रियः
श्रोत्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Modest, docile, well-behaved.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>Brāhman versed in the study of the Vedas.<BR>	 2. A Brāhman follow-<BR>ing a particular branch or school of the Vedas.<BR> E. श्रोत्र considered<BR>as substituted for छन्दस् the metre of the Vedas, and खन् aff.; or<BR>श्रोत्र the ear, said also to mean the Vedas, and घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रियता
श्रोत्रियता f. (-ता) Conversancy with the Vedas, the duty of a Brāhman.<BR>E. श्रोत्रिय a priest acquainted with the Vedas, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रियस्व
श्रोत्रियस्व n. (-स्वं) The property of a learned Brāhman.<BR> E. श्रोत्रिय, स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत|श्रोतः
श्रोत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Relating or belonging to the Vedas, to the ear,<BR>hearing, &c.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Preservation of the sacred fire.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>observance ordained by the Vedas.<BR>	 3. The three sacred fires<BR>collectively, viz. गार्हपत्य, आवहनीय and दक्षिण.<BR>	 f. (-ती) Comparison<BR>expressed by a particle, so, as, like, &c.<BR> E. श्रुति the Vedas, and<BR>अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौतसूत्र
श्रौतसूत्र n. (-त्रं) Name of a class of Sūtra writings based on the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौतस्मार्त्तक्रिया|श्रौतस्मार्तक्रिया
श्रौतस्मार्त्तक्रिया f. (-या) Acts conformable to law and religion.<BR> E. श्रौत and<BR>स्मार्त्त, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौतस्मार्त्तधर्म्म|श्रौतस्मार्तधर्म
श्रौतस्मार्त्तधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Duty enjoined by the Vedas and laws.<BR> E. श्रौत and स्मार्त्त, and धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौत्र|श्रौत्रं
श्रौत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Conversancy with Vedas.<BR>	 2. The ear.<BR> E. श्रोत्र the ear,<BR>or श्रोत्रिय a Brāhmana studied in scripture, अण् aff.; in the second<BR>case the last syllable rejected as well as the pen. vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौषट्
श्रौषट् Ind. An exclamation used in making an offering with fire to the<BR>gods or manes<BR> E. श्रु to hear, (the prayer being heard in consequence,)<BR>and डौषट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्र्याह्व|श्र्याह्वं
श्र्याह्व n. (-ह्वं) The lotus.<BR> E. श्रौ LAKṢMĪ, and आह्वा appellation, the god-<BR>dess appearing in the first instance from within the flower, and<BR>thence deriving many of her names.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्
श्लक्(इ)श्लकि r. 1st cl. (श्लङ्कते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्ण|श्लक्ष्णं
श्लक्ष्ण mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)<BR>	 1. Small, fine, minute.<BR>	 2. Gentle, mild, amiable.<BR>3. Honest, sincere.<BR>	 4. Plain, even, smooth.<BR> E. श्लिष् to embrace, क्स्न<BR>aff., the short vowel substituted for the penultimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णक|श्लक्ष्णकं
श्लक्ष्णक n. (-कं) The areca-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लग्
श्लग्(इ)श्लगि r. 1st cl. (श्लङ्गति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ्
श्लथ् r. 10th cl. (श्लथयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be weak, to be relaxed, loose, flaccid.<BR>2. To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ
श्लथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं)<BR>	 1. Loose, flaccid, relaxed.<BR>	 2. Dishevelled,<BR>(hair).<BR>	 3. Untied, unfastened.<BR> E. श्लथ् to be relaxed, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाख्
श्लाख्(ऋ)श्लाखृ r. 1st cl. (श्लाखति) To pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्
श्लाघ्(ऋ)श्लाघृ r. 1st cl. (श्लाघते)<BR>	 1. To praise, to eulogise.<BR>	 2. To flatter, to<BR>coax, to wheedle, (with a dat.)<BR>	 3. To boast, (with an inst.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघा
श्लाघा f. (-घा)<BR>	 1. Praise, flattery, eulogium.<BR>	 2. Service, obedience.<BR>	 3.<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>	 4. Self-praise.<BR> E. श्लाघ् to praise, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघित
श्लाघित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Praised, commended.<BR> E. श्लाघ् to praise, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्य|श्लाघ्यः
श्लाघ्य mfn. (-घ्यः-घ्या-घ्यं) Venerable, respectable, praise-worthy, entitled<BR>to praise or veneration.<BR> E. श्लाघा praise, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिकु|श्लिकुः
श्लिकु m. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. A servant, a slave.<BR>	 2. A blackguard.<BR>	 3. A lecher,<BR>libertine or debauchee.<BR>	 n. (-कु) Astronomy, or astrology.<BR> E. श्लिष् to<BR>embrace, Unādi aff. कु and क substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिक्यु|श्लिक्युः
श्लिक्यु m. (-क्युः)<BR>	 1. A servant.<BR>	 2. A libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्
श्लिष्(ञि औऌ)श्लिषॢ r. 4th cl. (श्लिष्यति) r. 1st cl. (श्लेषति)<BR>	 1. To embrace.<BR>2. To adhere or cling to.<BR>	 3. To unite, to join or connect. With<BR>उप and आ, To embrace. With वि, 1. To burst.<BR>	 2. To be separated.<BR>With सम्, To cling to. r. 10th cl. (श्लेषयति-ते) To connect. (उ) श्लिषु r.<BR>1st cl. (श्लेषति) To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिषा
श्लिषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. Embracing, an embrace.<BR>	 2. Clinging.<BR> E. श्लिष् to embrace, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्ट|श्लिष्टः
श्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Embraced.<BR>	 2. Touched by, clung or adhered<BR>to.<BR>	 3. Leaving on.<BR>	 4. Susceptible of a double interpretation, (in<BR>rhetoric.)<BR> E. श्लिष् to embrace, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्टि|श्लिष्टिः
श्लिष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Adherence.<BR>	 2. Embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्यत्
श्लिष्यत् mfn. (-ष्यन्-ष्यन्ती-ष्यत्) Embracing, clinging, adhering to, being in<BR>close contact with.<BR> E. श्लिष् to embrace, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपद|श्लीपदं
श्लीपद n. (-दं) Morbid enlargement of the legs, elephantiasis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदप्रभव|श्लीपदप्रभवः
श्लीपदप्रभव m. (-वः) The mango-tree.<BR> E. श्लीपद swelled leg, and प्रभव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदापह|श्लीपदापहः
श्लीपदापह m. (-हः) A plant, (Nageia putranjiva.)<BR> E. श्लीपद, अपह removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लील|श्लीलः
श्लील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Prosperous, fortunate, affluent, happy.<BR> E. श्ली good<BR>fortune, लच् poss. aff., and र changed to ल: see श्रील ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष|श्लेषः
श्लेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Union, junction, the proximity of contact.<BR>	 2. Associa-<BR>tion, society, presence.<BR>	 3. Embracing, an embrace.<BR>	 4. Adhering or<BR>clinging to, &c.<BR>	 5. A figure of rhetoric, choice or connection of<BR>words so as to admit of a double interpretation, a species of paron-<BR>omasia or pun.<BR> E. श्लिष् to embrace, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मक|श्लेष्मकः
श्लेष्मक m. (-कः) Phlegm, the watery or phlegmatic humour.<BR> E. श्लेष्मन् the<BR>same, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मघ्न
श्लेष्मघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्ना-घ्नं) Removing phlegm.<BR>	 f. (-घ्ना or घ्नी)<BR>	 1. Arabian<BR>jasmine.<BR>	 2. A flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR>	 f. (-घ्नी) Hogweed.<BR>E. श्लेष्म phlegm, and घ्न removing, fem. aff. टाप् or ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मज
श्लेष्मज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced or proceeding from phlegm.<BR> E. श्लेष्मन्, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मण|श्लेष्मणः
श्लेष्मण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Phlegmatic.<BR>	 f. (-णा) A plant, (Justicia adhena-<BR>toda, &c.)<BR> E. श्लेष्मन् the humor, and न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मन्
श्लेष्मन् m. (-ष्मा) The phlegmatic humour, one of the three principal<BR>humours or fluids of the body.<BR> E. श्लिष् to embrace or adhere to, (the<BR>body,) aff. मनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मल|श्लेष्मलः
श्लेष्मल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Phlegmatic, abounding or affected with<BR>phlegm, &c.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A plant, (Cordia latifolia.)<BR> E. श्लेष्म phlegm,<BR>लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मह|श्लेष्महः
श्लेष्मह m. (-हः) A medicinal plant, commonly Kāyaphal.<BR> E. श्लेष्म phlegm, ह destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मात|श्लेष्मातः
श्लेष्मात m. (-तः) A small tree, (Cordia latifolia.)<BR> E. श्लेष्मन् phlegm,<BR>अत् to go, (to remove,) aff. अच्; also with कन् added श्लेष्मातक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लैष्मिक
श्लैष्मिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Allaying or exciting, phlegm, phlegmatic. E.<BR>श्लेष्मन् phelgm, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक्
श्लोक्(ऋ)श्लोकृ r. 1st. cl. (श्लोकते)<BR>	 1. To put together, to compose, as<BR>verses.<BR>	 2. To heap together.<BR>	 3. To acquire.<BR>	 4. To relinquish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक|श्लोकः
श्लोक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A verse, a stanza.<BR>	 2. A stanza written in Anush-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">Page737-b+ 60</a>]<BR>ṭubh metre.<BR>	 3. Praising, praise.<BR>	 4. An object of praise.<BR>	 5. A pro-<BR>verb, a saying.<BR>	 6. Fame, celebrity.<BR> E. श्लोक् to compose, (as verses,)<BR>aff. अच्; according to the Rāmāyaṇa, irrly. derived from शोक<BR>sorrow: the first verse ever composed, having been the involun-<BR>tary expression of VĀLMĪKI'S grief at beholding a bird killed<BR>by a fowler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोकत्व
श्लोकत्व n. (-त्वं) Versification.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोण्
श्लोण्(ऋ)श्लोणृ r. 1st cl. (श्लोणति) To heap together, to collect or assemble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वःश्रेयस|श्वःश्रेयसं
श्वःश्रेयस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Happy, prosperous.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-सं) Happy,<BR>well, right. Subst.<BR>	 1. Happiness, prosperity.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ, the<BR>Supreme Being.<BR> E. श्वस् particle, implying happiness, श्रेयस best,<BR>excellent, and a final अच् or vowel added to the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वक्
श्वक्(इ)श्वकि r. 1st cl. (श्वङ्कते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वक्रीडिन्
श्वक्रीडिन् m. (-डी) A dog-feeder or trainer.<BR> E. श्व and क्रीडिन् who plays with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वग्
श्वग्(इ)श्वगि r. 1st cl. (शङ्कति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वगण|श्वगणः
श्वगण m. (-णः) A pack or number of dogs.<BR> E. श्व a dog, and गण a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वगणिक|श्वगणिकः
श्वगणिक m. (-कः) A hunter.<BR>	 mf. (-कः-का)<BR>	 1. A dog-feeder.<BR>	 2. One<BR>carried by dogs.<BR> E. श्व a dog, गण a number, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वच्
श्वच् r. 1st cl. (श्वचते) (इ) श्वचि (श्वञ्चते) 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To be opened, to be split.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वज्
श्वज् r. 1st cl. (श्वजते) also (इ) श्वजि (श्वञ्जते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वठ्
श्वठ् r. 10th cl. (श्वठयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To adorn, to accom-<BR>plish. (श्वाठयति-ते) (इ) श्वठि (श्वण्ठयति-ते) 1. To finish.<BR>	 2. To leave defec-<BR>tive or unfinished.<BR>	 3. To go, to move.<BR>	 4. To Speak ill. (श्वठयति)<BR>	 1. To<BR>speak amiss.<BR>	 2. To speak well.<BR>	 3. To abstain from speaking: see शठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वदंष्ट्रा
श्वदंष्ट्रा f. (-ष्ट्रा)<BR>	 1. A dog's tooth.<BR>	 2. A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.) E.<BR>श्व for श्वन् a dog, दंष्ट्वा a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वधूर्त्त|श्वधूर्त|श्वधूर्तः|श्वधूर्त्तः
श्वधूर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A jackal.<BR> E. श्वन् a dog, and धूर्त्त a cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वन्
श्वन् m. (-श्वा-श्वानौ-श्वानः) Accu. plu. (-शुनः) A dog.<BR>	 f. (-शुनी) A bitch.<BR> E. श्वि<BR>to increase, Unādi aff. कनिन्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वनर|श्वनरः
श्वनर m. (-रः) A currish fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वनिश|श्वनिशं
श्वनिश nf. (-शं-शा) A night on which dogs bark and howl.<BR> E. श्व for श्वन् a dog, निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपच|श्वपचः
श्वपच mf. (-चः-चा)<BR>	 1. A man or woman of a low and degraded caste.<BR>	 2.<BR>A dog-feeder or keeper.<BR> E. श्वन् a dog, पच् to cook, (for his food,) or<BR>to cherish as his property, and अच् aff.; also with क्विप् aff. श्वपच् m.<BR>(-पक्) and with घञ् aff. श्वपाक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपद
श्वपद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. A dog's foot.<BR>	 2. A mark like one, to be branded on the<BR>forehead of a thief.<BR> E. श्व, and पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपाक|श्वपाकः
श्वपाक m. (-कः) A man of a degraded and outcaste tribe, the son of an<BR>Ugra woman by a Kṣattṛ male, and classed with the Caṇḍāla,<BR>with whom he is ordered to live out of the town, to feed from<BR>broken vessels, and wear the clothes of the dead; to possess no<BR>other property than asses and dogs, and to be excluded from<BR>all intercourse with other tribes; he can only be employed<BR>as public executioner, or to carry out the bodies of those who die<BR>without kindred.<BR> E. श्व a dog, पच् to cook, (to feed on or to cherish,)<BR>aff. घञ्ः see श्वपच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वफल|श्वफलः
श्वफल n. (-लं) The lime or citron.<BR> E. श्व for श्वन् a dog, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभीरु|श्वभीरुः
श्वभीरु m. (-रुः) A jackal.<BR> E. श्वन् a dog, and भीरु afraid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभ्र्
श्वभ्र् r. 10th cl. (श्वभ्रयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To live in misery or distress.<BR>	 2. To go,<BR>to move.<BR>	 3. To make a hole, to pierce or perforate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभ्र|श्वभ्रं
श्वभ्र n. (-भ्रं) A hole, a gap, a chasm.<BR> E. श्वभ्र् to pierce, aff. अच्; or श्व a<BR>dog, भृ to cherish, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयथु|श्वयथुः
श्वयथु m. (-थुः) Swelling, intumescence.<BR> E. श्वि to swell, aff. अथुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयीचि|श्वयीचिः
श्वयीचि f. (-चिः or ची) Sickness, disease.<BR> E. श्वि to increase, Unādi aff.<BR>ईचि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वर्त्त्|श्वर्त्
श्वर्त्त् r. 10th cl. (श्वर्त्तयति)<BR>	 1. To live in misery or distress.<BR>	 2. To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्
श्वल् r. 1st cl. (श्वलति) To run, to go quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्क्
श्वल्क् r. 10th cl. (श्वल्कयति-ते) To speak, to narrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्ल्
श्वल्ल् r. 1st cl. (श्वल्लति) To run, to go fast or quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्ववत्|श्ववन्त्
श्ववत् Ind. Like a dog, cur-like.<BR> E. श्व, वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्ववत्|श्ववन्त्
श्ववत् m. (-वान्) A dog-feeder or trainer.<BR> E. श्व, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्ववृत्ति|श्ववृत्तिः
श्ववृत्ति m. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. The life of a dog.<BR>	 2. Service, servitude.<BR> E. श्व a dog, वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वव्याघ्र|श्वव्याघ्रः
श्वव्याघ्र m. (-घ्रः) The hunting-leopard, Chitā.<BR> E. श्व a dog, व्याघ्र a tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुर|श्वशुरः
श्वशुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A father-in-law, a wife's or husband's father.<BR>	 2. A<BR>venerable man, one to be treated as a father-in-law.<BR>	 m. Du. (-री)<BR>A father and mother-in-law.<BR> E. शु a particle, implying respect, अश्<BR>to pervade, Unādi aff. उरच्; also with कन् added श्वशुरक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुर्य्य|श्वशुर्य|श्वशुर्यः|श्वशुर्य्यः
श्वशुर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. A brother-in-law, a wife's or husband's brother.<BR>	 2. A<BR>husband's younger brother.<BR> E. श्वशुर a father-in-law, and यत् patro-<BR>nymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वश्रू
श्वश्रू f. (-श्रूः) A mother-in-law.<BR> E. श्वशुर a father-in-law, the उ and अ<BR>rejected, र conjoined with श, and ऊङ् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वश्रूश्वशुर
श्वश्रूश्वशुर m. Du. (-रौ) Mother and father-in-law.<BR> E. श्वश्रू, श्वशुर conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्
श्वस् r. 2nd cl. (श्वसिति)<BR>	 1. To breathe.<BR>	 2. To live.<BR>	 3. To sigh.<BR>	 4. To hiss,<BR>to snort. With आङ् prefixed, 1. To recover, to revive, to console.<BR>2. To take courage.<BR>	 3. To sigh. With उत्, 1. To open, to expand.<BR>2. To console.<BR>	 3. To upheave.<BR>	 4. To breathe.<BR>	 5. To sigh. With निर्, 1.<BR>To breathe out, to expire.<BR>	 2. To sigh. With वि, 1. To have trust or<BR>faith in, (generally with a loc.)<BR>	 2. To be fearless. With सम्, To<BR>calm oneself, to take heart. Caus. (श्वासयति-ते) With आ, To com-<BR>fort, to console. With वि, To inspire confidence, to cause to<BR>confide. With सम्, To cheer up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्
श्वस् Ind.<BR>	 1. To-morrow; (at the beginning of compounds it has the<BR>sense of “future.)” 2. A particle, implying auspiciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसत्
श्वसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती or सती-सत्) Breathing, sighing.<BR> E. श्वस्, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसन|श्वसनं|श्वसनः
श्वसन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A thorny plant, (Vangueria spinosa.)<BR>	 n.<BR>(-नं)<BR>	 1. Breathing, breath.<BR>	 2. Sighing.<BR> E. श्वस् to breathe, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसनाशन|श्वसनाशनः
श्वसनाशन m. (-नः) A snake.<BR> E. श्वसन breathing, अशन food; eating air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसनेश्वर|श्वसनेश्वरः
श्वसनेश्वर m. (-रः) A tree, (Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR> E. श्वसन, ईश्वर sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसनोत्सुक|श्वसनोत्सुकः
श्वसनोत्सुक m. (-कः) A snake.<BR> E. श्वसन breathing, and उत्सुक delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसित|श्वसितं
श्वसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sighed, breathed, sighing, breathing.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Breathing, breath.<BR>	 2. Sighing, a sigh.<BR> E. श्वस् to breathe, उनन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसुन|श्वसुनः
श्वसुन m. (-नः) A plant, (Conyza lacera, &c.)<BR> E. श्व a dog, and सुत a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्तन|श्वस्तनं
श्वस्तन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Future, what will be tomorrow, &c.<BR> E. श्वस्<BR>tomorrow, ठ्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्त्य|श्वस्त्यं
श्वस्त्य mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं) To-morrow's, what will be tomorrow.<BR> E. श्वस् tomorrow, त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्पृष्ट
श्वस्पृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Touched by a dog, defiled.<BR> E. श्व, स्पृष्ट touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वागणिक|श्वागणिकः
श्वागणिक m. (-कः) A hunter.<BR>	 mf. (-कः-की)<BR>	 1. A dog-keeper, one who<BR>lives by feeding or keeping dogs.<BR>	 2. One who rides or is drawn by<BR>dogs.<BR> E. श्वगण a number of dogs, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वादन्त|श्वादंत|श्वादंतः|श्वादन्तः
श्वादन्त m. (-न्तः) A dog's tooth.<BR> E. श्वन् a dog, दन्त a tooth, and the vowel<BR>termination of the first word made long in this similar compounds,<BR>as श्वाकर्ण, श्वापुच्छ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वान|श्वानः
श्वान m. (-नः) A dog.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A bitch. E. A various reading of श्वन् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वाननिद्रा
श्वाननिद्रा f. (-द्रा) A light slumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वानवैखरी
श्वानवैखरी f. (-री) A term for angry snarling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वापद|श्वापदः
श्वापद mfn. (-दः-दी-दं) Ferocious, savage, relating or belonging to a<BR>beast of prey.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A beast of prey in general.<BR>	 2. A tiger.<BR>E. श्वन् a dog, आपद् to resemble, aff. अच्; or श्वपद with अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वाविध्
श्वाविध् m. (-विद् or -वित्) A porcupine. “शजारु”<BR> E. श्वन् a dog, आङ् before<BR>व्यध् to pierce, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वाश्व|श्वाश्वः
श्वाश्व m. (-श्वः) BHAIRAVA, or ŚIVA, in a terrific form.<BR> E. श्व a dog, and<BR>अश्व a horse; being usually represented mounted on a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वास|श्वासः
श्वास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Breath, breathing.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>	 3. Sighing, a sigh. E.<BR>श्वस् to breathe, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासकास|श्वासकासः
श्वासकास m. (-सः) Asthma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासप्रश्वासधारण|श्वासप्रश्वासधारणं
श्वासप्रश्वासधारण n. (-णं) Breathing through the nostrils for a few seconds<BR>as a religious exercise: see प्राणायाम.<BR> E. श्वास inspiration, प्रश्वास<BR>expiration, and धारण holding or checking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासहेति|श्वासहेतिः
श्वासहेति f. (-तिः) Sleep, sleepiness.<BR> E. श्वास breathing or sighing, हेति a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासारि|श्वासारिः
श्वासारि m. (-रिः) A plant, commonly Bāmana-hāti.<BR> E. श्वास breath, अरि<BR>hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासिन्
श्वासिन् m. (-सी)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A living creature.<BR> E. श्वास breath, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वि
श्वि (इर टु and ओ) टुओश्वि r. 1st cl. (श्वयति)<BR>	 1. To move, to go, or go to.<BR>2. To grow, to increase.<BR>	 3. To swell. With उद्, To swell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्
श्वित्(आ)श्विता r. 1st cl. (श्वेतते) To be white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्विति|श्वितिः
श्विति f. (-तिः) Whiteness.<BR> E. श्वित् to be white, कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्र|श्वित्रं
श्वित्र n. (-त्रं) Whiteness of the skin, vitiligo.<BR> E. श्वित् to be white, Unādi aff. रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्रघ्नी
श्वित्रघ्नी f. (-घ्नी) A plant, (Tragia involucrata.)<BR> E. श्वित्र vitiligo, घ्न destroy-<BR>ing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वित्रिन्
श्वित्रिन् mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि) Affected with vitiligo or whiteness of the skin.<BR> E. श्वित्र, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्विद्
श्विद्(इ)श्विदि r. 1st cl. (श्विन्दति) To be white, to become or continue so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वृ
श्वृ r. 9th cl. (श्वृणाति) To hurt, to injure, to wound or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेत|श्वेतं|श्वेतः
श्वेत mfn. (-तः-ता or नी-तं) White.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. White, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. The<BR>planet VENUS, or its regent ŚUKRA.<BR>	 3. The sixth range of moun-<BR>tains, dividing the known continent, the white mountains separa-<BR>ting the Varṣas of Hiranmaya and Romanaka.<BR>	 4. One of the<BR>minor Dwipas or divisions of the world; in fable the White<BR>Island, identified geographically by WILFORD, with Britain.<BR>	 5.<BR>A white cloud.<BR>	 6. Cummin-seed.<BR>	 7. A conch.<BR>	 mf. (-तः-ता) A small<BR>white shell used as a coin, a Cowrie.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Silver.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A<BR>grass, (Andropogon aciculatum.)<BR>	 2. A plant, Kāṣṭha-Pātala.<BR>3. A flower, (Clitoria ternatea.)<BR>	 4. Hogweed.<BR>	 5. Bent grass with<BR>white blossoms.<BR>	 6. Bamboo-manna.<BR>	 7. Crystal.<BR>	 8. Clayed or can-<BR>died sugar.<BR>	 9. A cowrie.<BR> E. श्वित् to be white, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतक|श्वेतकं|श्वेतकः
श्वेतक m. (-कः) A Cowri.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Silver.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतकुञ्जर|श्वेतकुंजर|श्वेतकुञ्जरः
श्वेतकुञ्जर m. (-रः) INDRA'S elephant.<BR> E. श्वेत white, and कुञ्जर an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतकेतु|श्वेतकेतुः
