श्वेतहय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A white horse.<BR>	 2. The horse of INDRA.<BR>	 3. A name of<BR>ARJUNA.<BR> E. श्वेत white, and हय a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतहस्तिन्
श्वेतहस्तिन् m. (-स्ती)<BR>	 1. A white elephant.<BR>	 2. The elephant of INDRA. E.<BR>श्वेत white, and हस्तिन् an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतार्क|श्वेतार्कः
श्वेतार्क m. (-र्कः) Gigantic swallow-wort, (Asclepias gigantea,) with<BR>white flowers.<BR> E. श्वेत white, and अर्क the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतोदर|श्वेतोदरः
श्वेतोदर m. (-रः) KUVERA.<BR> E. श्वेत white, and उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेतौही
श्वेतौही f. (-ही) An epithet of ŚACHI, the wife of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेत्र|श्वेत्रं
श्वेत्र n. (-त्रं) White leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वेनी
श्वेनी f. (-नी) One of the fem. form of श्वेतः see श्वेत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैत्य|श्वैत्यं
श्वैत्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Whiteness.<BR>	 2. Vitiligo.<BR> E. श्वित or श्वेत, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वैत्र|श्वैत्रं
श्वैत्र n. (-त्रं) Vitiligo.<BR> E. श्वेत to be white, रन् aff.; also श्वैत्र्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वोभूत
श्वोभूत Adj. Being tomorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वोवसीयस|श्वोवसीयसं
श्वोवसीयस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Auspicious, fortunate.<BR>	 n. (-सं) good fortune.<BR>E. श्वस् and वस both particles implying auspiciousness, ईयसुन् affixed<BR>to the latter, and a final vowel added to the compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष|षः
ष The thirty-first consonant of the Nāgari alphabet, and second<BR>sibilant, corresponding to Sh, pronounced in some schools Kh:<BR>this letter is usually the first element of the roots, the derivatives<BR>of which commence with स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष|षः
ष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Best, excellent.<BR>	 m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A learned man, a teacher.<BR>2. A nipple.<BR>	 3. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 4. Rest, remainder.<BR>	 5. Loss of<BR>knowledge, previously acquired.<BR>	 6. Eternal happiness, final eman-<BR>cipation.<BR>	 7. Heaven, paradise.<BR>	 8. Sleep.<BR>	 9. End, term.<BR>	 10. Hair.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">Page739-b+ 60</a>]<BR>n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. The embryo.<BR>	 2. Patience, endurance.<BR> E. षो to destroy,<BR>&c., aff. कं or ड and the consonant unchanged, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षग्
षग्(ए)षगे r. 1st cl. (सगति) To cover: also written सग् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षघ्
षघ्(ए)षघे r. 5th cl. (सघ्नोति) To hurt or kill: also सघ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षच्
षच् r. 1st cl. (सचते)<BR>	 1. To wet, to moisten, to sprinkle.<BR>	 2. To serve, to<BR>gratify by service. (सचति)<BR>	 1. To be connected.<BR>	 2. To understand<BR>thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षञ्च्
षञ्च् r. 1st cl. (सञ्चति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षञ्ज्
षञ्ज् r. 1st cl. (सजति) To embrace, to cling or adhere to, to be in con-<BR>tact or connexion with. With अव prefixed, To hang down from,<BR>to be suspended. With वि and आङ्, To struggle together. With<BR>आङ्, To be attached or devoted to. (उ) षञ्जु r. 2st cl. (सञ्जति-ते)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्
षट् r. 1st cl. (षटति) To be a part or portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्क|षट्कः
षट्क mfn. (-ट्कः-ट्का-ट्कं)<BR>	 1. Six.<BR>	 2. Having six-fold, &c.<BR>	 n. (-ट्कं)<BR>An aggregate of six.<BR> E. षष् six, and कन् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कर्ण|षट्कर्णः
षट्कर्ण m. (-र्णः) A sort of lute. Adj. Heard by six ears, i. e. by three<BR>persons.<BR> E. षष् six, and कर्ण an ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कर्म्मन्|षट्कर्मन्
षट्कर्म्मन् m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>	 1. A Brāhman.<BR>	 2. An adept, (in the Tantras, &c.)<BR>	 n.<BR>(-र्म्म or pl. -र्म्माणि)<BR>	 1. The six acts proper for a Brāhman, (collective-<BR>ly,) or teaching the Vedas, holy study, offering sacrifices, conduct-<BR>ing them for others, giving, and accepting gifts.<BR>	 2. Six acts allow-<BR>able to a Brāhman for subsistence, or gleaning, accepting gifts, ask-<BR>ing alms, agriculture, trade, and tending cattle, or according to<BR>some lending money at interest.<BR>	 3. The six acts taught in the<BR>Tantras, or killing, infatuating, enthralling, expelling, exciting<BR>animosity, and the stopping or privation of any faculty.<BR> E. षष् six,<BR>कर्म्मन् act or duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कोण|षट्कोणं
षट्कोण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A hexagon, a six-angled figure.<BR>	 2. The thunderbolt<BR>of INDRA.<BR> E. षष् six, कोण a corner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्चक्र|षट्चक्रं
षट्चक्र n. (-क्रं) The six mystical circles of the body, (in Tantra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्चरण|षट्चरणः
षट्चरण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A bee, 2. A louse.<BR>	 3. A locust.<BR> E. षट् six, चरण a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्ट्
षट्ट् r. 10th cl. (सट्टयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To injure, to hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To give.<BR>	 3.<BR>To be strong.<BR>	 4. To dwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्त्रिंशत्
षट्त्रिंशत् f. (-शत्)<BR>	 1. Thirty-six.<BR>	 2. A work on law.<BR> E. षष् six, and त्रिंशत् thirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पद|षट्पदः
षट्पद m. (-दः) A bee.<BR>	 mf. (-दः-दी) A louse.<BR>	 f. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A louse.<BR>	 2. A<BR>female bee.<BR>	 3. A stanza consisting of six lines.<BR> E. षष् six, पद<BR>a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पदप्रिय|षट्पदप्रियः
षट्पदप्रिय m. (-यः) The Nāgeshwar, (Mesue ferrea.)<BR> E. षट्पद a bee, and<BR>प्रिय beloved by; equally applicable therefore to the lotus, jas-<BR>mine, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पदातिथि|षट्पदातिथिः
षट्पदातिथि m. (-थिः)<BR>	 1. The mango-tree.<BR>	 2. The Champaka.<BR> E. षट्पद a bee, अतिथि a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्प्रज्ञ|षट्प्रज्ञः
षट्प्रज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. A sage, one acquainted with the four objects of human<BR>existence, or virtue, wealth, desire, and final happiness, and with<BR>the nature of the world, and of divine truth.<BR>	 2. A catamite. E.<BR>षष् six, and प्रज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडक्षीण|षडक्षीणः
षडक्षीण m. (-णः) A fish.<BR> E. षष् six, and अक्षि the eye, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडङ्ग|षडङ्गं|षडङ्गः
षडङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Having six limbs or members.<BR>	 2. Having six<BR>parts, six ingredients, &c.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Six parts of the body collec-<BR>tively; as the two arms, two legs, and the head and waist.<BR>	 2.<BR>The six supplementary parts of the Vedas or grammar, prosody,<BR>astronomy, pronunciation, the meaning of unusual terms, and the<BR>ritual of the Hindu religion.<BR> E. षष् six, and अङ्ग a limb or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडङ्गजित्
षडङ्गजित् m. (-जित्) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. षडङ्ग the six members, जित् who subdues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडङ्गपानीय
षडङ्गपानीय n. (-यं) An infusion or decoction of six drugs.<BR> E. षडङ्ग, and<BR>पानीय drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडङ्घ्रि|षडंघ्रि|षडङ्घ्रिः
षडङ्घ्रि m. (-ङ्घ्रिः) A bee.<BR> E. षष् six, and अङ्घ्रि a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडभिज्ञ|षडभिज्ञः
षडभिज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A Buddha or Bauddha deified sage.<BR> E. षष् six,<BR>(branches of learning or piety,) and अभिज्ञ understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडानन|षडाननः
षडानन m. (-नः) KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. षष् six, and आनन a face; having six<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">Page740-a+ 60</a>]<BR>faces, four directed to the four cardinal points, and two to the<BR>zenith and nadir, according to some accounts, though not gener-<BR>ally so represented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडूषण|षडूषणं
षडूषण n. (-णं) Six spices collectively, or long-pepper, black-pepper,<BR>dried ginger, the root of long-pepper, the fruit of the plumbago,<BR>and of the Piper chavya.<BR> E. षष् six, and ऊषण a spice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडृतु|षडृतुः
षडृतु m. Plur. (-तवः) The six seasons; also personified as divinities. E.<BR>षष्, and ऋतु a season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षङ्गव
षङ्गव n. (-वं) A yoke of six oxen or six oxen collectively.<BR> E. षष् six, गो an ox, अच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्गुण
षड्गुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Six-fold, six times.<BR>	 n. (-णं) An assemblage,<BR>of six qualities or properties.<BR>	 mf. (-णः-णा) The six acts of a king<BR>in his military character, viz. “सन्धि” alliance, “विग्रह” war, “यान”<BR>march, “स्थान” halt, “आसन” strategem, and “द्वैधीभाव” aid of other<BR>kings.<BR> E. षष् and गुण a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्ग्रन्थ|षड्ग्रन्थः
षड्ग्रन्थ n. (-न्थः) A variety of the Cæsalpinia bonducella.<BR>	 f. (-न्था) Orris<BR>root, (Acorus calamus.)<BR> E. षष् six, ग्रन्थि a knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्ग्रन्थिका|षड्ग्रंथिका
षड्ग्रन्थिका f. (-का) Zedoara, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR> E. षड्ग्रन्थ as above, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्ज|षड्जः
षड्ज m. (-ड्जः) The first of the seven primary notes in music.<BR> E. षष्<BR>six, ज born: supposed to require for its articulation the employ-<BR>ment of the tongue, teeth, palate, nose, throat, and chest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्दर्शन|षड्दर्शनः
षड्दर्शन n. (-नं) The six systems of philosophy taken together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्धा
षड्धा Ind. In six ways.<BR> E. षष् six, and धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भाग|षड्भागः
षड्भाग m. (-गः) A sixth, a sixth part.<BR> E. षष्, and भाग share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भागभाज्
षड्भागभाज् mfn. (-भाक्) Entitled to a sixth.<BR> E. षड्भाग, भाज् who shares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भुज|षड्भुजः
षड्भुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Six armed, six-sided.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A hexagon.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-जा) The water-melon. “खरमुज.”<BR> E. षष् six, भुज an arm or<BR>branch, &c., aff. टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्रस|षड्रसः
षड्रस n. (-सं) The six flavours collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्रेखा
षड्रेखा f. (-खा) A water-melon.<BR> E. षष् six, and रेखा a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्वर्ग|षड्वर्गः
षड्वर्ग m. (-र्गः) A class or aggregate of six, as of six defects or enemies<BR>of humanity taken together. viz:--“काम” desire, “क्रोध” wrath,<BR>“लोभ” covetousness, “मोह” bewilderment, “मद” pride, and<BR>“मात्मर्य्य” envy.<BR> E. षष् six, and वर्ग a class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्वर्गवश्य
षड्वर्गवश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) Subject to the six vices.<BR> E. षड्वर्ग, वश्य to be subjected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्विध|षड्विधं
षड्विध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) In six ways, of six kinds.<BR> E. षष्, and विध kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्विन्दु
षड्विन्दु m. (-न्दुः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. षष् six, and विन्दु a drop or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्
षण्(उ)षणु r. 8th cl. (सनोति सनुते)<BR>	 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To serve or honour;<BR>also written षन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्ड|षंड|षंडः|षण्डः
षण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A bull at liberty.<BR>	 2. A eunuch.<BR>	 3. A multitude, a<BR>heap.<BR>	 mn. (-ण्डः-ण्डं) A quantity of lotuses.<BR> E. षण् to give, ड<BR>Unādi aff.; also शण्ड, षण्ढ, and शण्ढ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्डाली|षंडाली
षण्डाली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A measure of oil, the vessel holding a Chatāk.<BR>	 2.<BR>A wanton woman.<BR>	 3. A pond, a pool.<BR> E. षण्ड a bull, a eunuch, &c.,<BR>and अल् to be able, affs. अच् and ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्ढ|षंढ|षंढः|षण्ढः
षण्ढ m. (-ण्ढः) A eunuch: see षण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मास|षण्मासः
षण्मास m. (-सः) A half year, six months.<BR> E. षष्, and मास a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मास्य|षण्मास्यः
षण्मास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Six month old, of six months standing, &c.<BR>E. षण्मास and यत् aff.; also षाण्मास्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मुख|षण्मुखः
षण्मुख m. (-खः) KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 f. (-खा) A water-melon.<BR> E. षष् six, मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षत्वणत्व
षत्वणत्व n. (-त्वं) The substitution of the letters ष or ण for स and न in<BR>grammatical derivatives,<BR> E. ष and ण the letters, with the abstract<BR>affix attached to each respectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षद्
षद्(औ ऌ)औषदॢ r. 1st and 6th cls. (सीदति)<BR>	 1. To wither, to wane, to<BR>perish gradually.<BR>	 2. To be low-spirited, to despond, to be wearied or<BR>distressed, to lack energy.<BR>	 3. To break or destroy.<BR>	 4. To go or move.<BR>With आङ् prefixed, आषदॢ r. 1st and 10th cls. (आसादति आसादयति-ते)<BR>1. To go.<BR>	 2. To assail, to encounter. With अव prefixed, 1. To be<BR>exhausted or languid.<BR>	 2. To finish. With आङ्, 1. To obtain, to<BR>attain, to reach or arrive at.<BR>	 2. To attack. With उत्, 1. To ascend.<BR>2. To destroy. With उप, 1. To approach.<BR>	 2. To worship. With नि,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">Page740-b+ 60</a>]<BR>1. To sit in or on.<BR>	 2. To stand.<BR>	 3. To protect. With प्र, 1. To be<BR>propitious to, to favour or be pleased with.<BR>	 2. To please or pro-<BR>pitiate.<BR>	 3. To purify.<BR>	 4. To smile. With वि, To be languid or sorrow-<BR>ful. With सम्, 1. To attain.<BR>	 2. To be in company or society with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षध्
षध् r. 5th cl. (सध्नोति) To wish to hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षन्
षन्(उ)षनु r. 8th cl. (सनोति सनुते) To give; also षण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षप्
षप् r. 1st. cl. (सपति)<BR>	 1. To be connected.<BR>	 2. To understand thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षम्
षम् r. 1st cl. (समति)<BR>	 1. To be unconfused.<BR>	 2. To be confused. r. 10th cl.<BR>(समयति-ते) To perplex or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षम्ब्
षम्ब् r. 1st cl. (सम्बति) To go, to move. r. 10th cl. (सम्बयति-ते) To unite,<BR>to join, to collect or assemble together; also read सम्ब् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षर्ज्ज्
षर्ज्ज् r. 1st cl. (सर्ज्जति) To earn, to acquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षर्ध्
षर्ध् r. 1st cl. (-सर्द्धति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षर्व|षर्व्व
षर्व r. 1st cl. (सर्वति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To injure, to hurt; also read सर्व् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षर्षपी
षर्षपी f. (-पी) A small bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षल्
षल् r. 1st cl. (सलति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्
षष् mfn. Plu. only (षट् or षड्) Six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टि|षष्टिः
षष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Sixty.<BR> E. षष् six, डटि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिक|षष्टिकः
षष्टिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Bought with sixty.<BR>	 mf. (-कः-का) A kind of rice<BR>of quick growth.<BR> E. षष् six, (days,) ठन् aff.; or षष्टि sixty, and कन्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिक्य|षष्टिक्यं
षष्टिक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं) Fit for rice of quick growth, (a field, &c.)<BR> E. षष्टिक, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टितम|षष्टितमः
षष्टितम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Sixtieth.<BR> E. षष्टि sixty, and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिधा
षष्टिधा Ind. In sixty ways.<BR> E. षष्टि sixty, and धा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिमत्त|षष्टिमत्तः
षष्टिमत्त m. (-त्तः) An elephant who has reached the age of sixty<BR>and is in rut.<BR> E. षष्टि sixty, मत्त furious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टियोजनी
षष्टियोजनी f. (-नी) A journey or extent of sixty YOJANAS.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिहायन|षष्टिहायनः
षष्टिहायन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. An elephant sixty years old.<BR>	 2. A kind of rice. E.<BR>षष्टि, हायन a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठ|षष्ठः
षष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं) Sixth.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ठी)<BR>	 1. DURGĀ as one of the sixteen<BR>divine mothers.<BR>	 2. The sixth day of the lunar fortnight.<BR>	 3. The<BR>sixth or genetive case, (in gram.)<BR> E. षष् six, डति aff., थुक् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठक|षष्ठकः
षष्ठक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Sixth.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठांश|षष्ठांशः
षष्ठांश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The sixth part of agricultural produce taken by the<BR>sovereign from the subject in the shape of a land-tax.<BR>	 2. A sixth<BR>part in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठान्न
षष्ठान्न n. (-न्नं) A sixth meal.<BR> E. षष्ठ, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठान्नकाल
षष्ठान्नकाल n. (-लं) The taking of food once in three days, as an act of<BR>penance.<BR> E. षष्ठान्न, and काल time; also with कन् added, षष्ठान्नकालकं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठान्नकालता
षष्ठान्नकालता f. (-ता) Eating once in three days, on the evening of the<BR>third day.<BR> E. षष्ठान्नकाल, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठिन्
षष्ठिन् mfn. (-ष्ठी-ष्ठिनी-ष्ठि) Being or having the sixth, (year, &c.)<BR> E. षष्ठ,<BR>इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठीतत्पुरुष|षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः
षष्ठीतत्पुरुष m. (-षः) The Tatpurusha compound of which the first<BR>member, (generally) takes a genetive case in dissolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठीपूजा
षष्ठीपूजा f. (-जा) The worship of the goddess DURGĀ, as one of the<BR>sixteen divine mothers, on the sixth day after the delivery of a<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षस्
षस् r. 2nd cl. (सस्ति) To sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षस्ज्
षस्ज् r. 1st cl. (सज्जति) To move, to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षस्त्
षस्त्(इ)षस्ति r. 2nd cl. (संस्ते) To dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षह्
षह् r. 1st cl. (सहते) r. 4th cl. (सह्मति) r. 10th cl. (साहयति-ते)<BR>1. To bear, to endure, to suffer or support, to forbear, to have<BR>patience.<BR>	 2. To be content or satisfied.<BR>	 3. To be able. With उत्<BR>prefixed, 1. To make effort or exertion, to persevere, to energize.<BR>2. To be happy or delighted. With प्र, To be violent. With वि, To<BR>determine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षहसानु|षहसानुः
षहसानु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2. A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाट्
षाट् Ind. An interjection of calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाट्कौशिक
षाट्कौशिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Enveloped in six sheathes.<BR> E. षट्, कोश a sheath, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाडव|षाडवः
षाडव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Sentiment, passion.<BR>	 2. Singing, music.<BR>	 3. A Rāga in<BR>which six of the seven primary notes are used, (in music.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाड्गुण्य|षाड्गुण्यं
षाड्गुण्य n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. An aggregate of six properties or qualities.<BR>	 2. The<BR>six acts of royal military policy.<BR>	 3. Multiplication of anything<BR>by six.<BR> E. षड्गुण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाण्मातुर|षाण्मातुरः
षाण्मातुर m. (-रः) KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. षष् six, and मातृ a mother, अण् aff.;<BR>having been brought up by the six Kirtikās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाण्मासिक
षाण्मासिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of or relating to six months, half yearly,<BR>&c.<BR> E. षण्मास, and ढञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षात्वणत्विक|षात्वणत्विकः
षात्वणत्विक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relative to the substitution of ष or ण for स<BR>and न, (as a rule, &c.)<BR> E. ठक् added to षत्वणत्व as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाध्
षाध्(उ)साधु r. 4th cl. (साध्यति) r. 5th cl. (साध्नोति)<BR>	 1. To effect, to accom-<BR>plish or complete.<BR>	 2. To succeed; also साध् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षान्त्व्
षान्त्व् r. 10th cl. (सान्त्वयति-ते) To console, to comfort; also सान्त्व् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाष्ठ|षाष्ठः
षाष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठी-ष्ठं) Sixth.<BR> E. षष्ठ the same, and अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षि
षि(ञ)षिञ् r. 5th cl. (सिनोति सिनुते) r. 9th cl. (सिनाति सिनीते) To tie, to<BR>bind. With अधि and अव prefixed, To accomplish. With वि and अव,<BR>To transact as business. With वि, To be an object or purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिच्
षिच्(औ)षिचौ r. 6th cl. (सिञ्चति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle.<BR>	 2. To moisten, to<BR>water, (as plants.)<BR>	 3. To pour out.<BR>	 4. To pour in. With अभि<BR>prefixed, 1. To anoint, to initiate.<BR>	 2. To sprinkle. With उद्, 1.<BR>To sprinkle.<BR>	 2. To make proud. With नि, 1. To pour.<BR>	 2. To im-<BR>pregnate. With परि, To pour round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिट्
षिट् r. 1st cl. (सेटति) To disregard, to contemn, to despise, to treat with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिड्ग|षिड्गः
षिड्ग m. (-ड्गः)<BR>	 1. A catamite.<BR>	 2. A libertine, a lecher.<BR>	 3. A gallant.<BR>E. षिट् to despise, Unādi aff. गन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिध्
षिध् r. 1st cl. (सेधति) To go. (ऊ) षिधू r. 1st cl. (सेधति)<BR>	 1. To command,<BR>to order.<BR>	 2. To ordain, especially with respect to holy observances.<BR>3. To do an auspicious act, or one indicating good fortune.<BR>4. To drive off.<BR>	 5. To restrain.<BR>	 6. To interdict.<BR>	 7. To instruct.<BR>With अप, To remove. With नि, 1. To remove.<BR>	 2. To prohibit.<BR>3. To ward off. With प्रति, To prevent. With विप्रति, To contradict.<BR>(उ) षिधु r. 4th cl. (सिध्यति)<BR>	 1. To succeed, to effect fully or com-<BR>pletely.<BR>	 2. To complete a series of mystical observances by<BR>which supernatural powers are attained, to be an adept, to<BR>be initiated.<BR>	 3. To be perfect, to be finished or accomplished.<BR>4. To be right or correct. With नि or प्रति prefixed, (निषेधति<BR>प्रतिषेधति) To prevent, to prohibit. With प्र, To be celebrated or<BR>notorious. With सम् 1. To be accomplished.<BR>	 2. To be made per-<BR>fect.<BR>	 3. To attain beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिभ्
षिभ्(उ)षिभु r. 1st cl. (सेभति)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To speak.<BR>	 3. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिम्
षिम्(उ)षिमु r. 1st cl. (सेमति) To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिम्भ्
षिम्भ्(उ)शिम्भु r. 1st cl. (सिम्भति)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To speak.<BR>	 3. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिल्
षिल् r. 6th cl. (सिलति) To glean: more usually सिल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिव्
षिव्(उ)षिवु r. 4th cl. (सीव्यति)<BR>	 1. To sew, to stitch.<BR>	 2. To sow, as seed.<BR>3. To join. With अनु, To string together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षु|षुः
षु r. 1st. cl. (सवति-ते) To go. (सवति)<BR>	 1. To bring forth. To possess<BR>power. r. 2nd cl. (सौति)<BR>	 1. To bear, to bring forth.<BR>	 2. To possess<BR>power or supremacy. (ञ) षुञ् r. 5th cl. (सुनोति सुनुते)<BR>	 1. To bathe,<BR>(preparatory to a sacrifice)<BR>	 2. To distil, to extract a spirit.<BR>	 3. To<BR>churn, to stir or agitate.<BR>	 4. To pain. With अभि, 1. To sprinkle.<BR>2. To bathe.<BR>	 3. To extract juice.<BR>	 4. To mix. With प्र, To bear or<BR>bring forth. With उद्, To agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षु|षुः
षु m. (-षुः) Parturition, delivery.<BR> E. सु-बा० डु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुट्ट
षुट्ट r. 10th cl. (सुट्टयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To disregard, to despise.<BR>	 2. To be small or<BR>shallow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुभ्
षुभ् r. 1st cl. (सोभति) r. 6th cl. (सुभति)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To shine.<BR>	 3. To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुम्भ्
षुम्भ् r. 1st and 6th cls. (सुम्भति)<BR>	 1. To speak.<BR>	 2. To shine.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>beautiful.<BR>	 4. To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुर्
षुर् r. 6th cl. (सुरति)<BR>	 1. To possess supreme or superhuman power.<BR>	 2. To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुह्
षुह् r. 4th cl. (सुह्यति)<BR>	 1. To bear, to endure.<BR>	 2. To be content or<BR>satisfied.<BR>	 3. To be able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षू
षू(ङ)षूङ् r. 2nd cl. (सूते) r. 4th cl. (सूयते)<BR>	 1. To bear a child, to bring<BR>forth.<BR>	 2. To produce in general. r. 6th cl. (सुवति)<BR>	 1. To direct, to<BR>send, to throw or cast.<BR>	 2. To incite, impel.<BR>	 3. To discharge.<BR>	 4.<BR>To remit, (as debt.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षू
षू f. (-षूः) Birth, delivery, child-bearing.<BR> E. षू to bring forth, aff. क्विप्<BR>and the consonant unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षूद्
षूद् r. 1st cl. (सूदते) To prevent, (सूदति) To kill. r. 10th cl. (सूदयति-ते)<BR>1. To leak, to drop, to flow, to distil.<BR>	 2. To deposit, to place.<BR>3. To hurt, to wound, to kill or attempt to kill.<BR>	 4. To promise.<BR>5. To urge on.<BR>	 6. To cook. With अभि or नि, To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षूर्
षूर्(ई)षूरी r. 4th cl. (सूर्य्यते)<BR>	 1. To be stopped or fixed.<BR>	 2. To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षूर्क्ष्
षूर्क्ष् r. 1st cl. (सूर्क्षति)<BR>	 1. To respect, to regard, to treat with reverence<BR>or respect.<BR>	 2. To disregard, to disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षूर्क्ष्य
षूर्क्ष्य r. 1st cl. (सूर्क्ष्यति)<BR>	 1. To envy, to be impatient of another's rise.<BR>2. To be intolerent or impatient of another's faults.<BR>	 3. To dis-<BR>regard or contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षूष्
षूष् r. 1st cl. (सूषति) To bring forth, to bear; also सूष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षृभ्
षृभ्(उ)षृभु r. 1st cl. (सर्भति) To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षृम्भ्
षृम्भ्(उ)षृम्भु r. 1st cl. (सृम्भति) To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षेक्
षेक्(ऋ)षेकृ r. 1st cl. (सेकते) To go, to move; preferably सेक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षेल्
षेल्(ऋ)षेऌ r. 1st cl. (सेलति) To go, to move; also शेल्, and सेल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षेव्
षेव्(ऋ)षेवृ r. 1st cl. (सेवति-ते)<BR>	 1. To serve, to gratify by service.<BR>	 2. To<BR>rely or depend on.<BR>	 3. To worship.<BR>	 4. To follow, to practise, to be<BR>addicted to.<BR>	 5. To enjoy, (sexually.)<BR>	 6. To dwell in.<BR>	 7. To watch<BR>over. With आ, 1. To enjoy.<BR>	 2. To practise. With उप, 1. To<BR>practise.<BR>	 2. To perform.<BR>	 3. To enjoy.<BR>	 4. To serve. With नि, 1. To<BR>pursue.<BR>	 2. To employ.<BR>	 3. To enjoy.<BR>	 4. To inhabit.<BR>	 5. To observe.<BR>6. To attend. With परि, To take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षै
षै r. 1st cl. (सायति) To waste, to wane or decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षो
षो r. 4th cl. (स्यति)<BR>	 1. To destroy, to put an end to.<BR>	 2. To be destroy-<BR>ed, to perish.<BR>	 3. To finish. With अव, To fail.<BR>	 2. To complete.<BR>With अधि and अव, 1. To practise.<BR>	 2. To be able.<BR>	 3. To determine.<BR>4. To reflect. With परि and अव, 1. To endeavour.<BR>	 2. To com-<BR>plete, to conclude.<BR>	 3. To resolve.<BR>	 4. To be lost.<BR>	 5. To be reduced<BR>to. With वि and अव, 1. To determine upon, to accept.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>convinced.<BR>	 3. To endeavour, to strive.<BR>	 4. To effectuate.<BR>	 5. To<BR>desire.<BR>	 6. To believe. With सम् and वि, To decree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडत्|षोडन्त्
षोडत् m. (-डन्) A young ox, or one with six teeth.<BR> E. षष् six, and<BR>दत् for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडश|षोडशः
षोडश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Sixteenth.<BR> E. षोडशन् sixteen, डट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशक
षोडशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Sixteen, (collectively.)<BR> E. षोडश, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशन्
षोडशन् mfn. Plu. only. (-श) Sixteen.<BR> E. षष् six, and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशभुजा
षोडशभुजा f. (-जा) A form of DURGĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशमातृका
षोडशमातृका fem. plu.<BR>	 f. (-का) The sixteen divine mothers; they are:--<BR>गौरी पद्मा शची मेधा सावित्री विजया जया ।<BR>देवसेना स्वधा स्वाहा मातरो लोकमातरः ।<BR>शान्तिः पुष्टिर्धृतिस्तुष्टिः कुलदेवात्मदेवता ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशर्त्तुनिशा|षोडशर्तुनिशा
षोडशर्त्तुनिशा f. (-षा) Any one of sixteen nights from the commence-<BR>ment of menstruation.<BR> E. षोडश, and ऋतु menses, निशा night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशांश
षोडशांश m. (-शः) A sixteenth.<BR> E. षोडश and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशांशु|षोडशांशुः
षोडशांशु m. (-शुः) The planet VENUS.<BR> E. षोडश sixteen, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशाङ्घ्रि|षोडशांघ्रि|षोडशाङ्घ्रिः
षोडशाङ्घ्रि m. (-ङ्घ्रिः) A crab.<BR> E. षोडश sixteen, and अङ्घ्रि a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशार्च्चिस्|षोडशार्चिस्
षोडशार्च्चिस् m. (-र्च्चिः) The planet VENUS.<BR> E. षोडश sixteen, अर्च्चिस् a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशावर्त्त|षोडशावर्त|षोडशावर्तः|षोडशावर्त्तः
षोडशावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A conch-shell.<BR> E. षोडश sixteen, आवर्त्त a twist or<BR>spire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशिक
षोडशिक f. (-की) Adj. Sixteen-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशोपचार|षोडशोपचारः
षोडशोपचार m. plu. (-रः) The sixteen ways of doing homage; they<BR>are:--“आसनं स्वागतं पाद्यमर्घमाचमनीयकम् ।<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">Page742-a+ 60</a>]<BR>मधुपर्काचमस्नानं वसनाभरणानि च ।<BR>गन्धपुष्पे धूपदीपौ नैवेद्यं वन्दनं तथा ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोढा
षोढा Ind. In six ways.<BR> E. षष् six, उ substituted for the final, धाच् aff.,<BR>and ध changed to ढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोढामुख|षोढामुखः
षोढामुख m. (-खः) Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टक्
ष्टक् r. 1st. cl. (स्तकति)<BR>	 1. To resist or oppose.<BR>	 2. To strike against; also स्तक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टग्
ष्टग्(ए)ष्टगे r. 1st. cl. (स्तगति) To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टन्
ष्टन् r. 1st. cl. (स्तनति) r. 10th cl. (स्तनयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To groan,<BR>to sigh.<BR>	 3. To thunder. With नि, 1. To sigh.<BR>	 2. To bewail;<BR>also स्तन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टभ्
ष्टभ्(इ)ष्टभि r. 1st cl. (स्तम्भते)<BR>	 1. To stop or hinder, to oppose, to impede,<BR>to resist or prevent.<BR>	 2. To be stupid or dull, to be inanimate<BR>or insensible.<BR>	 3. To be fixed as a post.<BR>	 4. To be astounded or<BR>stupefied.<BR>	 5. To be paralysed; also स्तभ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टम्
ष्टम् r. 1st. cl. (स्तमति)<BR>	 1. To be confused.<BR>	 2. To be clear or unconfused.<BR>r. 10th cl. (स्तमयति-ते) To confuse or annoy; also स्तम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टिध्
ष्टिध् r. 5th cl. (स्तिध्नुते) To assail, to assault, to attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टिप्
ष्टिप्(ऋ)ष्टिपृ r. 1st cl. (स्तेपते)<BR>	 1. To ooze, to drop, to distil.<BR>	 2. To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टिम्
ष्टिम् r. 4th cl. (स्तिम्यति) To be wet or moist, to reek, to steam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टीम्
ष्टीम् r. 4th cl. (स्तीम्यति) To be wet or moist, to reek, to steam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टु
ष्टु(ञ)ष्टुञ् r. 2nd cl. (स्तौति or स्तुते स्तवीति or स्तवीते)<BR>	 1. To praise, to<BR>eulogise.<BR>	 2. To extol, to celebrate.<BR>	 3. To hymn, to worship with<BR>praises. With सम्, 1. To praise.<BR>	 2. To be familiar with; also स्तु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टुच्
ष्टुच् r. 1st cl. (स्तोचते) To be clear, to be bright, to be pellucid.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be propitious or pleased; also स्तुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टुप्
ष्टुप् r. 10th. cl. (स्तोपयति-ते) To heap up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टुभ्
ष्टुभ्(उ)ष्टुभु r. 1st cl. (स्तोभते)<BR>	 1. To stop, to hinder.<BR>	 2. To be stupid<BR>or dull. (स्तोभति)<BR>	 1. To praise.<BR>	 2. To celebrate; also स्तुभ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टूप्
ष्टूप्(इ)ष्टूपि r. 4th cl. (स्तूप्यति) r. 10th cl. (स्तूपयति-ते) To heap together,<BR>to pile up, to collect into a heap.<BR>	 2. To erect; also स्तूप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टृक्ष्
ष्टृक्ष् r. 1st cl. (स्तृक्षति) To go, to move; also स्तृक्ष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टृह्
ष्टृह्(उ)ष्टृहु r. 6th cl. (स्तृहति) To hurt or kill; also स्तृह् and ष्टॄह् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टॄह्
ष्टॄह्(ऊ)ष्टॄहू r. 6th cl. (स्तॄहति) To hurt or kill; also ष्टृह् and स्तॄह् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टेप्
ष्टेप्(ऋ)ष्टेपृ r. 1st cl. (स्तेपते)<BR>	 1. To leak, to flow, to distil or drop.<BR>	 2.<BR>To sprinkle. r. 10th cl. (स्तोपयति-ते) To send; also स्तेप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्टै
ष्टै r. 1st cl. (स्तायति)<BR>	 1. To surround, to encompass.<BR>	 2. To put on, to<BR>adorn; also स्तै ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ट्युम|ष्ट्युमः
ष्ट्युम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ट्यै
ष्ट्यै r. 1st cl. (स्त्यायति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To crowd or swarm.<BR>	 3. To<BR>envelope.<BR>	 4. To spread about; also स्त्यै ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठग्
ष्ठग्(ए)ष्ठगे r. 1st cl. (स्थगति) To cover; also स्थग् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठल्
ष्ठल् r. 1st cl. (स्थलति)<BR>	 1. To stand.<BR>	 2. To be firm; also स्थल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठस्
ष्ठस्(उ)ष्ठसु r. 4th cl. (स्थम्यति) To dwell in, to inhabit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठा
ष्ठा r. 1st cl. (तिष्ठति) To stand, to stop, to be still, to refrain from<BR>moving.<BR>	 2. To abide, to stay, to be.<BR>	 3. To remain.<BR>	 4. To be<BR>at hand.<BR>	 5. To stand by.<BR>	 6. To rest on.<BR>	 7. To be in any situa-<BR>tion.<BR>	 8. To perform. (तिष्ठते)<BR>	 1. To apply or refer to, as an umpire<BR>or judge.<BR>	 2. To indicate or reveal one's thoughts to another.<BR>	 3. To<BR>stand as a prostitute, to give oneself up to sexual embrace, to offer<BR>oneself to. With अधि prefixed, (अधितिष्ठति)<BR>	 1. To excel, to sur-<BR>pass, to overcome.<BR>	 2. To sit or stand upon or over.<BR>	 3. To be placed<BR>or preside over. With अनु, (अनुतिष्ठति) 1. To practise as a duty, to<BR>obey or follow as a law.<BR>	 2. To apply or adhere to. With अव,<BR>(अवतिष्ठति-ते) 1. To stay or stand.<BR>	 2. To attend upon. With आङ्,<BR>(आतिष्ठते) 1. To affirm or assert.<BR>	 2. To apply. (आतिष्ठति)<BR>	 1. To<BR>ascend, to mount.<BR>	 2. To promise or engage. With उत्, (उत्तिष्ठते) 1.<BR>To seek for, to endeavour, to obtain; (उत्तिष्ठति) To get up, to rise<BR>as from a seat, &c. With उप, (उपतिष्ठति-ते) 1. To propitiate, (as a<BR>deity.)<BR>	 2. To praise or hymn, to worship, to adore.<BR>	 3. To embrace.<BR>4. To treat in a friendly manner, to form a friendship or con-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">Page742-b+ 56</a>]<BR>nection with.<BR>	 5. To pass or lie along or near to, that is, as a path<BR>or road.<BR>	 6. To arrive at or near. (उपतिष्ठते) To hope to gain or<BR>acquire. With नि, (नितिष्ठते) To be established. With परि and अव,<BR>(पर्य्यवतिष्ठते) To be stationary or immovable. With प्र, (प्रतिष्ठते) To<BR>set off, to go forth, to depart.<BR>	 2. To go to. With प्र and उत्,<BR>(प्रोत्तिष्ठति) To get up, to rise. With प्रति, (प्रतितिष्ठति) To be erected<BR>for holy purposes, to be sacred or consecrated. With वि, (वितिष्ठते)<BR>1. To stand apart, to be separated.<BR>	 2. To stay or be. With वि and<BR>अव, (व्यवतिष्ठते) To decree, to pronounce. With सम्, (सन्तिष्ठते) 1. To be<BR>well.<BR>	 2. To be close to or together.<BR>	 3. To be of the same inclina-<BR>tions or opinions, to conform, to agree.<BR>	 4. To be completed or fini-<BR>shed. With सम् and आङ्, (समातिष्ठते) To perform, to be engaged in.<BR>With सम् and उत्, (समुत्तिष्ठति) To rise or get up. With सम् and प्र, To<BR>go forth or on a journey. With प्र in the causal, (प्रस्थापयति-ते) To send.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठिव्
ष्ठिव्(उ)ष्ठिवु r. 1st cl. (ष्ठीवति) r. 4th cl. (ष्ठीव्यति) To eject from the<BR>mouth, to spit, to sputter, (the radical sibilant is unchanged in<BR>this root;) also ष्ठीव् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठीव्
ष्ठीव्(उ)ष्ठीवु r. 1st cl. (ष्ठीवति) r. 4th cl. (ष्ठीव्यति)<BR>	 1. To spit or eject<BR>from the mouth.<BR>	 2. To sputter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठीवन|ष्ठीवनं
ष्ठीवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Spitting, ejecting saliva.<BR>	 2. Saliva, spittle.<BR> E. ष्ठीव् and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठीवित्वा
ष्ठीवित्वा Ind. Having spitten.<BR> E. ष्ठीव् to spit, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठेवन|ष्ठेवनं
ष्ठेवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The act of spitting.<BR>	 2. Spittle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठ्युत
ष्ठ्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ejected as saliva, spit.<BR> E. ष्ठीव् to spit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णस्
ष्णस्(उ)ष्णसु r. 4th cl. (स्नस्यति) To eject from the mouth, to spit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णा
ष्णा r. 2nd cl. (स्नाति) To bathe, to purify by ablution. With अप, To<BR>bathe after mourning. With नि, To be skilled in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णिह्
ष्णिह् (ऌ ऊ) r. 4th cl. (स्निह्यति)<BR>	 1. To bear affection to, to love, to<BR>regard, to be kind to or pleased with.<BR>	 2. To be sticky.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>kind to; (this root and all its derivatives govern the loc. of<BR>the person or thing for whom or which affection is or felt. r. 10th<BR>cl. (स्नेहयति-ते) To be unctuous, to be bland or greasy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णु
ष्णु r. 2nd cl. (-स्नौति) To distil, to drop, to ooze or leak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णुच्
ष्णुच् r. 1st cl. (स्नोचते) To be clear or pellucid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णुस्
ष्णुस्(उ)ष्णुसु r. 4th cl. (स्नुस्यति)<BR>	 1. To eat.<BR>	 2. To take.<BR>	 3. To disappear.<BR>4. To eject from the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णुह्
ष्णुह् (ऌ ऊ) r. 4th cl. (स्नुह्यति) To be sick, to retch, to throw up, to vomit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्णै
ष्णै r. 1st cl. (स्नायति) To surround, to encompass, to dress, to envelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्मि
ष्मि r. 1st cl. (स्मयते) To smile. r. 10th cl. (स्माययति-ते) To disrespect. With<BR>वि prefixed, To surprise or astonish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वक्क्
ष्वक्क् r. 1st cl. (ष्वक्कते) To go, to move; the radical sibilant is unchang-<BR>ed by special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वञ्ज्
ष्वञ्ज् r. 1st cl. (स्वजते) To embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वद्
ष्वद् r. 1st cl. (स्वदते) r. 10th cl. (स्वादयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To taste.<BR>	 2. To be pleas-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. To cover; also स्वाद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वप्
ष्वप्(ञि औ)ञिष्वपौ r. 2nd cl. (स्वपिति) To sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वर्त्त
ष्वर्त्त r. 10th cl. (स्वर्त्तयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To be wretched or<BR>distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वष्क्
ष्वष्क् r. 1st cl. (ष्वष्कते) To go, to move: the radical sibilant is unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्विद्
ष्विद्(ञि आ)ञिष्विदा r. 1st cl. (स्वेदते) r. 4th cl. (स्विद्यति)<BR>	 1. To perspire,<BR>to sweat.<BR>	 2. To be greasy or unctuous.<BR>	 3. To be fascinated, to be<BR>tempted or deluded.<BR>	 4. To quit, to yield.<BR>	 5. To release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स|सं|सः
स The thirty-second consonant of the Nāgarī Alphabet, correspon-<BR>ding to S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स|सं|सः
स m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. Air, wind.<BR>	 5. The abbre-<BR>viated name of the musical note षड्ज.<BR>	 6. A bird.<BR>	 7. He, the nominative<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">Page743-a+ 60</a>]<BR>case masc. of तद् the third personal pronoun: before many letters<BR>the Visarga is rejected.<BR>	 f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. She,<BR>the nominative case fem. of तद्.<BR>	 n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Knowledge.<BR>	 2. Medita-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. A carriage-road.<BR>	 4. A fence. Ind.<BR>	 1. (In composition,)<BR>With, together with; being substituted for सम्. or सह.<BR>	 2. Like,<BR>similar, as in “सधर्म” which means having similar duties.<BR>	 3. Same,<BR>identical, as in “सोदर”; combined with nouns it forms adjectives<BR>and adverbs; as सकोपः angry, सकोपम् angrily; सगर्व्वः proud,<BR>सगर्व्वम् haughtily; सविनयः modest, well-behaved, सविनयम् respect-<BR>fully; ससम्भ्रमः flurried, ससम्भ्रमम् flurriedly, सानन्दः joyful, सानन्दम्<BR>joyfully, &c.<BR> E. षो to go, &c., aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सं|स|सः
सं Ind. (In composition,) With, together with, &c.; being the optional<BR>form of writing सम् before a consonant: before consonants of the<BR>first five classes, the Anuswāra may be again changed to the<BR>nasal of the class to which the letter it preceds belongs, as सं for<BR>सम् and कल्प make सङ्कल्प, &c.: before the semi-vowels, the sibilants,<BR>and ह, it preferably remains unaltered; this practice however is<BR>very arbitrary in this respect and the change is expressed or not,<BR>in all manuscripts according to the pleasure of the writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षेप|सङ्क्षेप|संक्षेपः
संक्षेप m. (-पः) Abridgment: see सङ्क्षेप ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञ
संज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Knock-kneed.<BR>	 n. (-ज्ञं) A yellow fragrant wood.<BR>f. (-ज्ञा)<BR>	 1. Name, appellation.<BR>	 2. Thought, mind, intellect.<BR>	 3. Con-<BR>sciousness.<BR>	 4. Gesture, sign, gesticulation.<BR>	 5. The sacred verse<BR>or Gāyatri of the Vedas.<BR>	 6. One of the wives of the sun, and<BR>daughter of VISHWAKARMAN.<BR>	 7. (In grammar,) The technical<BR>name of any affix, &c.<BR> E. सम् before ज्ञा to know, affs. अङ् and<BR>टाप्; that by which anything is known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञप्ति
संज्ञप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaying.<BR>	 2. Apprising, informing.<BR> E. सम् be-<BR>fore ज्ञा to know, also, to slay, (causal form,) aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञाधिकार
संज्ञाधिकार m. (-रः) A heading rule which gives a peculiar names to<BR>the rules which fall under it and influences them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञापन
संज्ञापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, slaughter.<BR>	 2. Apprising, informing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Teaching.<BR> E. सम् before ज्ञा to know, also, to slay, (causal form,)<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञावत्
संज्ञावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Recovered after insensibility, become<BR>sensible, revived.<BR>	 2. Having a name or denomination.<BR> E. संज्ञा sign,<BR>name, &c., मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञाविषय
संज्ञाविषय m. (-यः) An epithet or attributive.<BR> E. संज्ञा and विषय object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञासुत
संज्ञासुत m. (-तः) An epithet of SATURN.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्ञित
सज्ञित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Called, denominated.<BR> E. संज्ञा, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संज्ञु
संज्ञु mfn. (-ज्ञुः-ज्ञुः-ज्ञु) Knock-kneed.<BR> E. सम् together ज्ञु for जानु the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संय|संयः
संय m. (-यः) The skeleton.<BR> E. सम् together, यम् to restrain, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयत्|संयन्त्
संयत् mf. (-यत्) War, battle.<BR> E. सम् before यम् to restrain, aff. क्विप्, तुक्<BR>added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयत|संयतः
संयत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Checked, restrained, constrained, suppressed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Bound, confined, fettered, imprisoned.<BR> E. सम् before यम् to res-<BR>train, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयतात्मन्
संयतात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Self-subdued, of well regulated spirit.<BR> E. संयत, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयतेन्द्रिय
संयतेन्द्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of subdued or controlled passions and<BR>desires.<BR> E. संयत, and इन्द्रिय an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयद्वर|संयद्वरः
संयद्वर m. (-रः) A king, a prince.<BR> E. सम् before यम् to restrain, क्वरप्<BR>Unādi aff.; or संयत् war, वर chief; also संयत्वर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयन्तृ|संयंतृ
संयन्तृ mfn. (-न्ता-न्त्री-न्तृ) Constraining, constrainer.<BR> E. सम् before यम् to<BR>restrain, aff. तृच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयम|संयमः
संयम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Restraint, forbearance.<BR>	 2. Humanity, avoiding the<BR>infliction of pain on others.<BR> E. सम् before यम् to restrain, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमत्
संयमत् mfn. (-मन्-मन्ती-मत्) Curbing, restraining, subduing, who or<BR>what does so.<BR> E. सम् before यम् to restrain, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमन|संयमनं|संयमनः
संयमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Restraining, checking.<BR>	 2. Forbearance, self-denial or<BR>control.<BR>	 3. Binding, confinement.<BR>	 4. Holding, detaining.<BR>	 5. A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">Page743-b+ 60</a>]<BR>religious vow or obligation.<BR>	 6. A cluster of four houses.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>1. A ruler.<BR>	 2. YAMA.<BR>	 f. (-नी) The capital of YAMA.<BR> E. सम् imply-<BR>ing completeness, or entirely, and यम् to restrain, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमित|संयमितः
संयमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Checked, controlled, restrained.<BR>	 2. Bound,<BR>confined, held, detained.<BR> E. सम् before यम् to check, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमिन्
संयमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Who or what checks, restrains, curbs, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-मी) A saint, a sage, one who subdues or controls his passions.<BR>E. संयम restraint, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयात्रा
संयात्रा f. (-त्रा) Travelling into another island or continent, voyaging,<BR>travelling by water.<BR> E. सम् before या to go, त्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयान|संयानं|संयानः
संयान m. (-नः) A mould.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Accompanying, going together.<BR>	 2.<BR>Carrying out a dead body.<BR> E. सम् together, या to go or get, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयाम|संयामः
संयाम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Forbearance, check, control, restraint.<BR>	 2. Humanity,<BR>abstaining from giving pain to others.<BR> E. सम् before यम् to res-<BR>train, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयामवत्|संयामवन्त्
संयामवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Forbearing.<BR> E. संयाम, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयाव|संयावः
संयाव m. (-वः) A sort of roll, or a thin cake of unleavened bread, fried<BR>with Ghee, pounded and again made up into an oblong form with<BR>fresh bread, sugar, and spices, and again fried with Ghee.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, यु to mix, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुक्त|संयुक्तः
संयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Joined with, connected, attached.<BR>	 2. Mixed,<BR>blended.<BR>	 3. Endowed with, possessed of.<BR>	 4. Accompanied or<BR>attended by.<BR>	 5. Consisting of, (with an inst.)<BR>	 6. Relating to.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, युज् to join, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुग|संयुगः
संयुग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Union, mixture.<BR> E. सम् before युज् to join, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुज्
संयुज् mfn. (-युक्)<BR>	 1. Possessed of or endowed with good qualities.<BR>2. Connected or associated with.<BR>	 3. Joined, united.<BR> E. सम् before<BR>युज् to join, aff. क्विन्, and the consonant unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुत|संयुतः
संयुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Connected, joined, mixed, blended, attached to.<BR>2. Furnished with.<BR> E. सम् together, यु to join, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुयुषु
संयुयुषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to mix, join, unite, to bring together<BR>in any way.<BR> E. सम् before यु to join, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोग|संयोगः
संयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Intimate union or association.<BR>	 2. Living with, being<BR>in company with.<BR>	 3. Adherence, junction.<BR>	 4. The conjunction of<BR>two heavenly bodies, (in astro.)<BR>	 5. (In grammar,) A conjunct<BR>consonant.<BR> E. सम् before युज् to join, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोगविरुद्ध|संयोगविरुद्धं
संयोगविरुद्ध n. (-द्धं) Any eatables which cause disease by being mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोगित|संयोगितः
संयोगित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Joined, connected.<BR> E. संयोग union, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोजन|संयोजनं
संयोजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Copulation, coition.<BR>	 2. Conjunction.<BR> E. सम् with युज्<BR>to join, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोजित|संयोजितः
संयोजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Joined, attached, annexed.<BR> E. सम् together, युज् to join, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्त
संरक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Inflamed, angry.<BR>	 2. Empassioned.<BR>	 3.<BR>Coloured red.<BR>	 4. Charmed.<BR>	 5. Beautiful.<BR> E. सम् before रञ्ज् to be<BR>affected, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्ष|संरक्षः
संरक्ष m. (-क्षः) Care, preservation, protection.<BR> E. सम्, रक्ष preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्षण|संरक्षणं
संरक्षण n. (-णं) Taking care of, protecting, preserving.<BR> E. सम् before रक्ष्<BR>to preserve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्षित
संरक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taken care of, preserved, protected.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before रक्ष् to preserve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्ष्य
संरक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) Fit, proper, or necessary to be taken care of,<BR>guarded, preserved, &c.<BR> E. सम् before रक्ष् to preserve, यत् aff.; also<BR>संरक्षणीय and संरक्षितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरब्ध
संरब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Incensed, angry.<BR>	 2. Agitated.<BR>	 3. Overwhel-<BR>med.<BR> E. सम् before रभि to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरम्भ
सरम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Wrath, rage.<BR>	 2. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 3. Flurry, agita-<BR>tion.<BR>	 4. Swelling with heat and redness.<BR>	 5. Turbulence.<BR>	 6. Begin-<BR>ning.<BR> E. सम् before रभि to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भपरुष
संरम्भपरुष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Exceedingly harsh, rough, or scurrilous.<BR> E. संरम्भ, परुष harsh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भरस
संरम्भरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Angry, resentful.<BR> E. संरम्भ, and रस taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भवेग|संरंभवेग|संरम्भवेगः
संरम्भवेग m. (-गः) The violence of wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भिव
संरम्भिव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Wrath.<BR>	 2. Pride.<BR>	 3. Agitation.<BR> E. संरम्भिन्, and त्व aff.;<BR>also with तल्, संरम्भिता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरम्भिन्|संरंभिन्
संरम्भिन् mfn. (-म्भी-म्भिनी-म्भि)<BR>	 1. Proud.<BR>	 2. Angry.<BR>	 3. Flurried.<BR> E. संरम्भ, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराग|संरागः
संराग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Anger.<BR>	 2. Affection.<BR>	 3. Colouring.<BR> E. सम्, रञ्ज् to be<BR>affected, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराधन|संराधनं
संराधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Propitiating, pleasing by worship.<BR>	 2. Accomplishing.<BR>3. Deep meditation.<BR> E. सम्, before राध् to accomplish, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराधित
संराधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Propitiated, pleased.<BR> E. सम् before राध् to<BR>accomplish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराव|संरावः
संराव m. (-वः) Sound, noise, uproar.<BR> E. सम् before रु to sound, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराविन्
संराविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Roaring, shouting, making a noise or uproar.<BR>E. सम् before रु to sound, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरुग्ण
संरुग्ण f. (-ग्णा) Shattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरुद्ध
संरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Checked, stopped, impeded, curbed, opposed.<BR>2. Concealed.<BR>	 3. Refused.<BR> E. सम् before रुध् to obstruct, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरूढ|संरूढः
संरूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Confident, audacious, presuming.<BR>	 2. Budded,<BR>blossomed.<BR>	 3. Grown together.<BR>	 4. Healed.<BR>	 5. Sprouted.<BR>	 6. Burst-<BR>forth.<BR>	 7. Taking firm root.<BR> E. सम् before रुह् to grow, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरोध|संरोधः
संरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Hindering, stopping. opposing, preventing.<BR>	 2. Im-<BR>pediment, obstruction.<BR>	 3. Bond, fetter.<BR>	 4. Crub, check.<BR>	 5. Throw-<BR>ing, sending.<BR>	 6. Siege.<BR> E. सम् before रुध् to obstruct, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलक्षण|संलक्षणं
संलक्षण n. (-णं) Distinguishing, characterising.<BR> E. सम् before लक्ष् to mark,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलक्षित
संलक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Marked, distinguished.<BR> E. सम् before लक्ष् to<BR>mark, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलक्ष्य
संलक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं) To be marked with or by.<BR> E. सम् before लक्ष् to mark, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलग्न|संलग्नः
संलग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Joined, united, adherent.<BR>	 2. Come to blows. E.<BR>सम्, लग्न attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलज्जमान
संलज्जमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Ashamed.<BR> E. सम्, लस्ज् to be ashamed, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलय|संलयः
संलय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Sleep, sleepiness.<BR>	 2. Melting away.<BR>	 3. Universal des-<BR>truction.<BR> E. सम् before ली to join, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संललित
संललित f. (-ता) Caressed, fondled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलाप|संलापः
संलाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Conversation, discourse.<BR>	 2. In the drama, high dis-<BR>course, dialogue of profound or occult meaning.<BR>	 3. Secret con-<BR>versation.<BR> E. सम् with, together with, लप् to speak, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलापक|संलापकः
संलापक n. (-कं) A species of minor drama, a controversial drama. E.<BR>संलाप, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलापित
संलापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Discoursing, conversing.<BR> E. संलाप, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलापिन्
संलापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिनी-पि) Discoursing, who or what discourses. E.<BR>संलाप, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलीढ
संलीढ f. (-ढा) Licked up, enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलीन
संलीन f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Clung to.<BR>	 2. Hidden.<BR>	 3. Contracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलीनमानस
संलीनमानस Adj. Drooping or depressed in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवंहयत्
संवंहयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Increasing.<BR> E. सम्, वहि to grow, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवत्|संवन्त्
संवत् Ind.<BR>	 1. A year.<BR>	 2. A year of Vikramāditya's era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवत्सर|संवत्सरः
संवत्सर m. (-रः) A year.<BR> E. सम् with, completely, वत्सर a year; or सम्<BR>with वस् to abide, सरन् Unādi aff., and त substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवद्
संवद् Ind.<BR>	 1. A year.<BR>	 2. A year of VIKRAMĀDITYA'S era.<BR> E. सम् before वद्<BR>to speak, aff. विच्; or सम् before वय् to go, क्विप् aff., य rejected, and<BR>तुक् final augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवदन|संवदनं
संवदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Communication of tidings or intelligence.<BR>	 2. Sight,<BR>seeing.<BR>	 nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Subduing by charms, over-powering any thing<BR>or person by magical compounds, or drugs, or mystical gems, &c.<BR>2. A charm, an amulet, the article by which the above is effected.<BR>E. सम् with वद् to speak, युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवनन|संवननं
संवनन nf. (-नं-ना) Subduing by magical drugs or charms: see the last.<BR>E. सम् before वन् to ask, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर|संवरं|संवरः
संवर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Self-control.<BR>	 3. Concealment.<BR>	 4. A particular<BR>religious observance with Buddhists.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The name of a<BR>demon.<BR>	 2. Collection, comprehension.<BR>	 3. Contraction, compression.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">Page744-b+ 60</a>]<BR>4. A mound a bridge, &c.<BR>	 5. Concealing.<BR>	 6. A kind of deer. E.<BR>सम् before वृ to choose, aff. अप्; more usually derived from शम्ब् or<BR>षम्ब् to collect, and then written शम्बर or षम्बर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबर्जन
संबर्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The act of appropriating to oneself.<BR>	 2. Consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त्त|संवर्त|संवर्तः|संवर्त्तः
संवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. Destruction of the universe.<BR>	 2. Beleric myrobalan.<BR>3. The name of a Muni.<BR>	 4. A cloud of a particular class.<BR>	 5. Being,<BR>becoming.<BR>	 6. Turning towards.<BR>	 7. Collection.<BR>	 8. A year.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before वृत् to be, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त्तक|संवर्तक|संवर्तकः|संवर्त्तकः
संवर्त्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. BALADEVA.<BR>	 2. The plough of BALADEVA.<BR>	 3. Sub-<BR>marine fire.<BR>	 4. The fire that is to destroy the world at the period<BR>of universal dissolution.<BR>	 5. A cloud of a particular class.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before वृत् to be or abide, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त्तकिन्|संवर्तकिन्
संवर्त्तकिन् m. (-की) BALADEVA, the elder brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. संवर्त्तक<BR>his plough, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त्ति|संवर्ति|संवर्तिः|संवर्त्तिः
संवर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः) The new leaf of a water-lily.<BR> E. सम् before वृत् to be, aff. इनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्त्तिका|संवर्तिका
संवर्त्तिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The new leaf of a water-lily.<BR>	 2. The petal near the<BR>filament.<BR>	 3. The flame of a lamp.<BR> E. सम् near, (the stalk,) वृत् to<BR>be, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्द्धक
संवर्द्धक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Augmenting, prospering, an augmentor,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Hospitable.<BR> E. सम् before वृद्ध् to increase, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्द्धन
संवर्द्धन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Augmenting, increasing.<BR>	 2. Prospering, thriving.<BR>	 3.<BR>Bringing up, cherishing.<BR> E. सम् before वृद्ध् to increase or prosper,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्द्धित
संवर्द्धित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cherished, protected, brought up, patronised,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सम् before वृद्ध् to increase, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्म्मित|संवर्मित
संवर्म्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fully armed.<BR> E. सम्, and वर्म्म armour, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवलित|संवलितः
संवलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Mixed, mingled.<BR>	 2. Encompassed, surround-<BR>ed.<BR>	 3. Having, possessed of.<BR>	 4. United.<BR>	 5. Broken, diversified.<BR>E. सम् together, वल् to surround, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवल्गित
संवल्गित f. (-ता) Over-run.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवसथ|संवसथः
संवसथ m. (-थः) A village.<BR> E. सम् before वस् to abide, अथच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवह|संवहः
संवह m. (-हः) Name of the third of the seven courses of wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाटिका
संवाटिका f. (-का) An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवात्
संवात् mfn. (-वान्-वाती or वान्ती वात्) Blowing, breathing, (as wind.)<BR> E. सम्<BR>before वा to blow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाद|संवादः
संवाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Communication of intelligence, information, news.<BR>	 2.<BR>Assent, concurrence.<BR>	 3. Conformity, correspondence, sameness.<BR>4. Conversation, dialogue.<BR>	 5. Discussion.<BR> E. सम् with वद् to<BR>speak, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवादिन्
संवादिन् f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Corresponding, similar.<BR>	 2. Speaking, Conversing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवार|संवारः
संवार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Contraction, diminution.<BR>	 2. Compression of the lips,<BR>&c. in pronunciation.<BR>	 3. Protection.<BR>	 4. Covering, closing up.<BR>E. सम् before वृ to choose, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवास|संवासः
संवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 2. An open space, either within<BR>or without a town, for the meeting and diversion of the townsmen.<BR>3. Company, society.<BR>	 4. Domestic intercourse.<BR> E. सम् with, वास an<BR>abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाह|संवाहः
संवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. An attendant employed to rub and knead the body.<BR>	 2.<BR>Rubbing the body.<BR>	 3. Pressing together.<BR>	 4. Bearing or carrying<BR>along.<BR> E. सम् before वाह् to exert one's self and अच् aff; or when<BR>the action is implied, वह् to obtain or bear, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहक|संवाहकः
संवाहक m. (-कः) An attendant rubbing and kneading the limbs.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before वह् to obtain, (pleasure or ease,) causal form, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहन|संवाहनं
संवाहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rubbing the person, kneading the limbs.<BR>	 2. Bearing,<BR>carrying.<BR> E. सम् before वह् to obtain or bear, (causal form,)<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहित
संवाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Rubbed, kneaded, (as the limbs.)<BR> E. सम् before<BR>वह् to bear, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाह्य
संवाह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. To be rubbed or kneaded.<BR>	 2. To be borne.<BR> E. सम् before वह् to bear, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविक्त|संविक्तं
संविक्त n. (-क्तं) That which is separated or individualized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविग्न
संविग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Agitated, flurried, alarmed.<BR> E. सम् before विज्<BR>to fear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविग्नमानस
संविग्नमानस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Distracted.<BR> E. संविग्न, and मानस the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविज्ञात
संविज्ञात f. (-ता) Universally known, generally allowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवित्ति|संवित्तिः
संवित्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Understanding, intellect.<BR>	 2. Perception.<BR>	 3. Accom-<BR>modation, reconciliation.<BR>	 4. Recognition, recollection of a thing<BR>or person previously known.<BR> E. सम् before विद् to know, aff. क्तिन्:<BR>see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविद्
संविद् f. (-वित् or विद्)<BR>	 1. Intellect, understanding.<BR>	 2. Promise, assent.<BR>3. Contract, engagement, agreement, covenant.<BR>	 4. Knowledge.<BR>	 5.<BR>A watch-word, a cry of battle.<BR>	 6. War, battle.<BR>	 7. Name, appella-<BR>tion.<BR>	 8. Sign, signal.<BR>	 9. Institute, prescribed custom or observa-<BR>tion.<BR>	 10. Pleasing, delighting.<BR>	 11. Sympathy.<BR>	 12. Conversation.<BR>13. Meditation.<BR>	 14. Hemp.<BR> E. सम् with, together with, विद् to<BR>know, &c., aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविदा
संविदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. Agreement, promise.<BR>	 2. Hemp.<BR> E. सम् + विद्-क्विप् टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविदित|संविदितः
संविदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Promised, agreed.<BR>	 2. Known, understood.<BR>3. Explored.<BR>	 4. Admonished, advised.<BR> E. सम् before विद् to know,<BR>aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविद्व्यतिक्रम|संविद्व्यतिक्रमः
संविद्व्यतिक्रम m. (-मः) Non-performance of agreements.<BR> E. संविद्, व्यतिक्रम departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधा
संविधा f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. Plan.<BR>	 2. Mode of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधान|संविधानं
संविधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Mode, rite.<BR>	 2. An expedient.<BR>	 3. Performance.<BR>	 4. Dis-<BR>position.<BR> E. सम्, वि before धा to have, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधानक|संविधानकं
संविधानक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Strange or unusual occurrence.<BR>	 2. The plot of a<BR>drama.<BR> E. संविधान, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविभक्त
संविभक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Parted, divided.<BR> E. सम्, वि before भज् to divide, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविभाग|संविभागः
संविभाग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Part, portion, share.<BR>	 2. Distributing, apportioning.<BR>E. सम्, and वि before भज् to divide, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविषा
संविषा f. (-षा) A plant, (Betula.)<BR> E. सम् intensitive, विष poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविष्ट
संविष्ट f. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. Clothed, dressed.<BR>	 2. Lying down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवीक्षण|संवीक्षणं
संवीक्षण n. (-णं) Search, inquiry, looking for or after anything.<BR> E. सम्<BR>and वि intensitives, ईक्ष् to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवीत|संवीतं
संवीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Surrounded, enclosed, encompassed.<BR>	 2. Cover-<BR>ed, clothed.<BR>	 3. Well-adorned.<BR>	 4. Overwhelmed.<BR>	 5. Shut in.<BR> E. सम्<BR>completely, व्येञ् to surround, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवुवूर्षु
संवुवूर्षु mfn. (-र्षुः-र्षुः-र्षु) Wishing to conceal, disguise, hide, cover, &c. E.<BR>सम् before वृ to screen, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृक्त
संवृक्त f. (-क्ता) Consumed, devoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत|संवृतः
संवृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Covered.<BR>	 2. Closed.<BR>	 3. Contracted, compress-<BR>ed, (as the lips, &c in pronunciation.)<BR>	 4. Retired, secluded.<BR>	 5.<BR>Sequestered.<BR>	 6. Filled with.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A secret place.<BR>	 2. A parti-<BR>cular mode of pronunciation.<BR> E. सम् before वृ to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृताकार
संवृताकार Adj. One who suppresses all outward manifestation of feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृति|संवृतिः
संवृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Covering up.<BR>	 2. Concealment, suppression.<BR>	 3. Secret<BR>purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्त|संवृत्तः
संवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Covered, concealed, hidden.<BR>	 2. Furnished<BR>with, filled with, possessed of.<BR>	 3. Being, become.<BR>	 4. Past, gone.<BR>m. (-त्तः) VARUṆA, deity of the ocean.<BR> E. सम् with, वृत् to be, &c.,<BR>aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्ति|संवृत्तिः
संवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Hiding, concealing.<BR>	 2. Covering.<BR>	 3. Possession,<BR>endowment.<BR>	 4. Accomplishment.<BR>	 5. Secret purpose.<BR> E. सम् with, वृत्<BR>to screen or cover, &c., aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृद्ध
संवृद्ध f. (-द्धा)<BR>	 1. Full-grown.<BR>	 2. Blooming, flourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेम
संवेम m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Hurry, flurry, haste proceeding from fear, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Haste, speed.<BR>	 3. Vehemence, impetuosity.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, विज्<BR>to be agitated, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेद|संवेदः
संवेद m. (-दः) Perception, consciousness.<BR> E. सम्, with विद् to know, aff. घञ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेदन|संवेदनं
संवेदन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. The act of perceiving.<BR>	 2. Sensation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेश|संवेशः
संवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Sleep, sleeping.<BR>	 2. Dreaming, a dream.<BR>	 3. Copulation.<BR>4. A stool, a chair, a seat.<BR> E. सम् before विश् to enter, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेशन|संवेशनं
संवेशन n. (-नं) Copulation, coition.<BR> E. सम् before विश् to enter, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यान|संव्यानं
संव्यान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. An upper-garment.<BR>	 2. Cloth, clothes, vesture.<BR>	 3.<BR>Covering.<BR> E. सम् completely, ष्येञ् to cover, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यूढ
संव्यूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Mixed, united.<BR> E. सम्, and वि before ऊह् to<BR>reason, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यूह|संव्यूहः
संव्यूह m. (-हः) Combination, mixture, union.<BR> E. सम्, and वि before ऊह् to reason, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशकला
संशकला Aptote. Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशप्तक|संशप्तकः
संशप्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A picked man or soldier, one of a select band sworn<BR>never to recede, and stationed to prevent the flight of the rest, a<BR>brother in arms.<BR>	 2. A conspirator bound by oath to kill another.<BR>E. सम् with, together, शप्त sworn, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशय|संशयः
संशय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>	 2. Logical indecision.<BR>	 3. Diffi-<BR>culty, risk.<BR>	 4. Possibility. सम् before शी to sleep, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयस्थ
संशयस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Doubtful, uncertain.<BR> E. संशय, and स्थ who or<BR>what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयात्मन्
संशयात्मन् m. (-त्मा) A sceptic.<BR> E. संशय, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयान|संशयानः
संशयान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dubious, uncertain.<BR> E. सम् before शीङ् to sleep, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयापन्न
संशयापन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Affected with doubt, hesitating, dubious.<BR>2. Doubtful, uncertain.<BR> E. संशय, and आपन्न having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयापन्नमानस|संशयापन्नमानसः
संशयापन्नमानस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Irresolute, dubious, uncertain.<BR> E. संशय<BR>doubt, आपन्न affected, and मानस the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयालु|संशयालुः
संशयालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Dubious, doubting, sceptic.<BR> E. संशय, आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयितृ
संशयितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Dubious, sceptical, a sceptic.<BR> E. सम् before शीङ्<BR>to sleep, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशय्य
संशय्य Ind. Having doubted or deliberated, being in doubt.<BR> E. सम् before शी to sleep, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशरण|संशरणं
संशरण n. (-णं) Commencement of a combat, charge, attack, &c.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, शॄ to injure, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशित|संशितं
संशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Certain, certified, ascertained, established.<BR>	 2.<BR>Completed, effected, finished.<BR>	 3. Completing, effecting, diligent<BR>and attentive in accomplishing.<BR> E. सम् before शो to destroy, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशितव्रत
संशितव्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Faithful to a vow or obligation.<BR> E. संशित<BR>completing, व्रत a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशितात्मन्
संशितात्मन् Adj. One whose mind is thoroughly matured or disciplined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशिश्रीषु
संशिश्रीषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to adhere to or depend upon, to serve,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सम् before श्रि to serve, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुद्ध
संशुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Pure, purified.<BR>	 2. Clean.<BR>	 3. Refined.<BR>	 4. Dis-<BR>charged, acquitted, (as a debt.)<BR>	 5. Acquitted, (of a crime.)<BR> E. सम्,<BR>and शुद्ध pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुद्धि|संशुद्धिः
संशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Cleaning the body.<BR>	 2. Purification in general.<BR>	 3.<BR>Correction.<BR>	 4. Acquittal of debt, &c.<BR>	 5. Acquittance of charge or<BR>crime.<BR> E. सम् completely, शुद्धि purification, cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुष्क|संशुष्कं
संशुष्क mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं) Dry, dried.<BR> E. सम् before शुष्क dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोधन|संशोधनं
संशोधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Cleaning, cleansing, purifying the body by ablutions,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Correcting.<BR>	 3. Refining.<BR>	 4. Discharging, paying.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before शोधन purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोध्य
संशोध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. To be rectified or purified.<BR>	 2. To be paid<BR>or acquitted, (as a debt, &c.)<BR> E. सम्, शुध् to be pure, यत् aff.;<BR>also संशोधनीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्चत्
संश्चत् n. (-श्चत्) Deceit, trick, illusion, juggling.<BR> E. सम् before चि to<BR>collect, Unādi aff. अति and सुट् augment; also संश्वत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्यान|संश्यानः
संश्यान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Contracted, rolled up, gathered up, shrunk,<BR>frozen, collapsed.<BR> E. सम् together, श्यै to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रय|संश्रयः
संश्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Protection, refuge, asylum.<BR>	 2. Seeking the alliance of<BR>a powerful prince, as a safety against actual or future enemies,<BR>(one of the six Guṇas in polities.)<BR>	 3. Pertaining to, (when used at<BR>the end of a compound.)<BR> E. सम् intensitive, श्रि to serve, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रव|संश्रवः
संश्रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Promise, assent, agreement.<BR>	 2. Hearing attentively.<BR>E. सम्, and श्रु to hear, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रवण|संश्रवणं
संश्रवण n. (-णं) The ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्राव
संश्राव m. (-वः) Sprinkling, aspersion, pouring out.<BR> E. सम्, श्रु to ooze, causal v., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रित|संश्रितः
संश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Protected, supported.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A servant, a<BR>follower, a dependent.<BR> E. सम् before श्रि to serve, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रुत|संश्रुतः
संश्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Promised, agreed, assented.<BR>	 2. Well-heard.<BR>E. सम् before श्रु to hear, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लिष्ट|संश्लिष्टः
संश्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Close together, adjoining, touching.<BR>	 2.<BR>Bound, united.<BR>	 3. Embraced.<BR>	 4. Endowed with.<BR> E. सम् before श्लिष्ट<BR>united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेष|संश्लेषः
संश्लेष n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. Embrace, embracing.<BR>	 2. Union, connection, junction,<BR>contact, association.<BR> E. सम् with श्लिष् to unite, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेषणा
संश्लेषणा f. (-णा) Means of binding together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्वत्
संश्वत् n. (-श्वत्) Fraud, trick, cheating, deception.<BR> E. सम् before श्वि to<BR>increase, aff. अति; deriv. irr.; also संश्चत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्त|संसक्तः
संसक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Near, adjoining, contiguous.<BR>	 2. Possessing,<BR>endowed with, affected by.<BR>	 3. Connected or acquainted with.<BR>	 4.<BR>Attached to, intent on.<BR>	 5. Tied or attached.<BR>	 6. Mixed, confused.<BR>E. सम् before षञ्ज् to embrace, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्तयुग
संसक्तयुग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Harnessed, yoked.<BR> E. संसक्त, and युग a yoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्ति|संसक्तिः
संसक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Proximity, contact.<BR>	 2. Union, junction.<BR>	 3. Acquain-<BR>tance, intimacy, connection with.<BR>	 4. Devotion or addiction to.<BR>	 5.<BR>Tying, fastening.<BR> E. सम् before षञ्ज् to embrace or adhere to, aff.<BR>क्तिच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसज्जमान
संसज्जमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Prepared, ready.<BR> E. सम्, षस्ज to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसद्
संसद् f. (-सत् or सद्)<BR>	 1. An assembly, a meeting.<BR>	 2. A court of justice. E.<BR>सम् before षद् to go, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसरण|संसरणं
संसरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going, proceeding in general.<BR>	 2. Going well or un-<BR>obstructedly.<BR>	 3. The unresisted march of troops.<BR>	 4. The beginning<BR>of war or battle.<BR>	 5. A high-way, the principal road through a<BR>village or town.<BR>	 6. The world.<BR>	 7. Birth, the production of living<BR>beings.<BR>	 8. A resting place for passengers near the gates of a city.<BR>E. सम् together, &c., सृ to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्ग|संसर्गः
संसर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. Union, proximity, approximation, contact.<BR>	 2. Ac-<BR>quaintance, familiarity, intercourse.<BR>	 3. Co-existence, (in logic.)<BR>	 4.<BR>Sensual attachment.<BR> E. सम् with, सृज् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गदोष|संसर्गदोषः
संसर्गदोष m. (-षः) The fault or evil consequences arising from the<BR>society of bad people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गाभाव|संसर्गाभावः
संसर्गाभाव m. (-वः) Logical nonexistence or annihilation; of three kinds,<BR>prior, incidental, and final, or absence of birth or production,<BR>destruction of present being, and necessary end or cessation of ex-<BR>istence.<BR> E. संसर्ग union, and अभाव non existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गित्व
संसर्गित्व n. (-त्वं) Familiarity, fellowship.<BR> E. संसर्गिन्, and त्व added; also<BR>with तल्, संसर्गिता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गिन्
संसर्गिन् mfn. (-र्गी-र्गिणी-र्गि)<BR>	 1. Familiar, keeping company, acquainted,<BR>an acquaintance.<BR>	 2. United or mixed with, in contact with, &c. E.<BR>सम् before सृज् to go, aff. घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्ज्जन|संसर्जन|संसर्जनं
संसर्ज्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Abandoning, leaving.<BR>	 2. Voiding.<BR> E. सम् before सृज् to quit, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्प|संसर्पः
संसर्प m. (-र्पः)<BR>	 1. An equable or gentle motion, as the creeping of a<BR>snake, the gliding of a stream, &c.<BR>	 2. The intercalary month<BR>occurring in a year in which there falls a Kṣaya-māsa.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before सृप् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्पण|संसर्पणं
संसर्पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The act of creeping along.<BR>	 2. An unexpected attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्पिन्
संसर्पिन् mfn. (-र्पी-र्पिणी-र्पि) Flowing, gliding.<BR> E. सम् intensitive prefix,<BR>सृप् to go, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसाद|संसादः
संसाद m. (-दः) An assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसार|संसारः
संसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The world, the habitation of mortals.<BR>	 2. Mundane ex-<BR>istence.<BR>	 3. A succession of births or existences.<BR>	 4. Transmigration,<BR>metempsychosis.<BR>	 5. Wordly illusion.<BR>	 6. Secular life.<BR>	 7. Course,<BR>passage.<BR> E. सम् together, (mankind,) सृ to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारगुरु|संसारगुरुः
संसारगुरु m. (-रुः) KĀMA or love.<BR> E. संसार the world, गुरु the spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारमार्ग|संसारमार्गः
संसारमार्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. The vulva.<BR>	 2. Mundane existence.<BR> E. संसार the<BR>world, (or mankind,) मार्ग a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारिन्
संसारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Worldly, mundane.<BR>	 m. (-री) An animal or<BR>sentient being.<BR> E. संसार the world, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिद्ध
संसिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Perfected, fully done or accomplished.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before सिद्ध effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिद्धि|संसिद्धिः
संसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Nature, disposition, the natural state or quality.<BR>	 2.<BR>Perfection, completion, accomplishment.<BR>	 3. Final emancipation.<BR>	 4.<BR>A passionate or intoxicated woman.<BR> E. सम् before सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिसृक्षु
संसिसृक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Wishing to unite.<BR> E. सम् before सृज् to create,<BR>desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिस्मयिषमाण
संसिस्मयिषमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Wishing or purposing to ridicule, laugh<BR>at, &c.<BR> E. सम् before स्मि to smile, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसूचन|संसूचनं
संसूचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Telling, informing.<BR>	 2. Reproaching, scolding.<BR>	 3.<BR>Hinting.<BR>	 4. The act of showing plainly or proving.<BR> E. सम् before<BR>षूच् to inform, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसूचित
संसूचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Informed, apprised, told.<BR>	 2. Reproved, scolded.<BR>E. सम् before षूच् to inform, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृति|संसृतिः
संसृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The world.<BR>	 2. Flow, stream, current.<BR>	 3. Transmigra-<BR>tion.<BR> E. सम् and सृ to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्ट|संसृष्टः
संसृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. United, joined, connected.<BR>	 2. Mixed.<BR>	 3. Re-<BR>united, rejoined.<BR>	 4. Connected as partners or co-partners.<BR>	 5. Clean-<BR>dressed, clad in clean garments.<BR>	 6. Involved in 7. Composed.<BR>	 8.<BR>Created.<BR> E. सम् before सृज् to leave or make, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टत्व|संसृष्टत्वं
संसृष्टत्व n. (-त्वं) Union, association.<BR>	 2. Re-union.<BR>	 3. (In law,) The<BR>voluntary co-residence or re-union of father and son, or of brothers<BR>with each other, after partition of property.<BR> E. संसृष्ट associated,<BR>aff. त्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टरूप
संसृष्टरूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Mixed, adulterated.<BR> E. संसृष्ट, and रूप nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टि|संसृष्टिः
संसृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Uniting, combining.<BR>	 2. Collecting, assembling.<BR>	 3.<BR>Living together in one family.<BR>	 4. (In rhetoric,) The use of a<BR>number of figures in one passage.<BR> E. सम्, सृज् to make, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टिन्
संसृष्टिन् m. (-ष्टी) A co-parcener, a brother, whether of whole or half<BR>blood, who after the partition of the family-property continues or<BR>returns to reside with his father, his paternal uncle, or his other<BR>brothers.<BR> E. संसृष्ट united or re-united, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेवन
संसेवन n. (-नं) Wating on, serving.<BR> E. सम् before सेव् to serve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेवित
संसेवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Waited on, served, attended.<BR> E. सम् before सेव्<BR>to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कर्त्तृ|संस्कर्तृ
संस्कर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ) Who or what polishes, completes, initiates, &c.<BR>E. सम् before कृ to make, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कार|संस्कारः
संस्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Completing, accomplishing, finishing, perfecting.<BR>	 2.<BR>Apprehension, conception.<BR>	 3. The power of memory, the faculty<BR>of recollection.<BR>	 4. Faculty in general, one of the twenty-four<BR>qualities enumerated by logicians.<BR>	 5. An essential and purificatory<BR>rite or ceremony amongst the Hindus; as those of the three first<BR>classes, commencing with conception and ending with marriage;<BR>or गर्भाधानं sacrifice on conception; पुंसवनं on vitality in the fœtus;<BR>सीमन्तोन्नयनं in the fourth, sixth, or eight month; जातकर्म्म giving the<BR>infant clarified butter out of a golden spoon to taste, before divi-<BR>ding the navel string; नामकरणं naming the child on the tenth,<BR>eleventh, twelfth, or hundred and first day: निष्क्रमणं carrying<BR>him out to see the moon on the third lunar day of the third light<BR>fortnight, or to see the sun in the third or fourth month; अन्नप्राशनं<BR>feeding him with rice in the sixth or eighth month, or when he has<BR>cut teeth; चूडाकार्य्यं tonsure in the second or third year; उपनयनं<BR>investiture with the string in the fifth, eight, or sixteenth year;<BR>विवाहः or marriage is the tenth and last Sanskāra.<BR>	 5. Embellish-<BR>ment, decoration, elegance.<BR>	 6. Purity, perfection.<BR>	 7. Preparing as<BR>an article of medicine or food, cooking, dressing, compounding,<BR>&c.<BR>	 8. Purification, consecration.<BR>	 9. Impression, form, mould. E.<BR>सम् implying perfection, कृ to make, अण् aff. and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कारजं|संस्कारज|संस्कारजः
संस्कारजं mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced from a purificatory ceremony, &c.<BR>E. संस्कार as above, with the power of the fifth case, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कारवर्जित|संस्कारवर्ज्जितः
संस्कारवर्जित m. (-तः) A Brāhman, &c., who has not received the usual<BR>initiatory ceremonies.<BR> E. संस्कारं purificatory rite and वर्जित deprived<BR>of; also संस्काररहित, संस्कारहीन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कारहीन|संस्कारहीनः
संस्कारहीन m. (-नः) A man of the three first classes, who has not been<BR>invested with the mystic thread, and who has not received the<BR>other ceremonies necessary to purification.<BR> E. संस्कार a rite, &c.,<BR>हीन lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृत|संस्कृतं|संस्कृतः
संस्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wrought, made, artificially produced.<BR>	 2. Ex-<BR>cellent, best.<BR>	 3. Decorated, ornamented.<BR>	 4. Cooked, dressed.<BR>5. Clean, cleansed.<BR>	 6. Purified.<BR>	 7. Finished, perfect, completed.<BR>8. Consecrated.<BR>	 9. Initiated.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A word regularly formed, a<BR>regular derivative.<BR>	 2. A learned man.<BR>	 3. A man of the three first<BR>classes who have received all the purificatory rites.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Language formed by perfect grammatical rules, the classical and<BR>sacred language of the Hindus.<BR>	 2. Offering oblation.<BR> E. सम् imply-<BR>ing completion or perfection, कृत made, and सुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृतात्मन्
संस्कृतात्मन् m. (-त्मा)<BR>	 1. A man who has undergone the initiatory rites.<BR>2. A sage.<BR> E. संस्कृत, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृतोक्ति|संस्कृतोक्तिः
संस्कृतोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Classical or polished language.<BR> E. संस्कृत, उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कत्यं
संस्कत्यं Ind. Having perfected, polished, adorned, &c.<BR> E. सम् before कृ<BR>to do, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृत्रिम
संस्कृत्रिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Perfected, polished.<BR>	 2. Fabricated, made.<BR>E. सम् before कृ to make, त्रि aff. and मन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्क्रिया
संस्क्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Funeral ceremonies, as burning the dead body, &c.<BR>2. Any purificatory rite: see संस्कार.<BR> E. सम् before क्रिया act,<BR>action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तब्ध
संस्तब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Made firm, rigid, &c.<BR>	 2. Confirmed, corro-<BR>borated.<BR>	 3. Stopped, stayed.<BR> E. सम् before स्तभि to stop, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तभ्यं|संस्तभ्य
संस्तभ्यं Ind.<BR>	 1. Having made firm, stable, rigid, &c.<BR>	 2. Having confirm-<BR>ed or established.<BR> E. सम् before स्तभि to stop, aff. ल्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भ|संस्तंभ|संस्तंभः|संस्तम्भः
संस्तम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Fixing, making firm, (as a post.)<BR>	 2. Confirming,<BR>establishing.<BR>	 3. Paralysis, muscular rigidity.<BR>	 4. Stop, stay.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before स्तभि to stop, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तम्भनीय
संस्तम्भनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be made firm.<BR>	 2. To be stopped.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before स्तभि to stop, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तर|संस्तरः
संस्तर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A bed, a couch.<BR>	 2. A bed made of leaves, &c.<BR>	 3.<BR>Sacrifice.<BR> E. सम् before स्तृ to spread, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तव|संस्तवः
संस्तव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Acquaintance, intimacy.<BR>	 2. Praise.<BR> E. सम् together, ष्टु to praise, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तवान|संस्तवानः
संस्तवान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Eloquent, talking fluently and well.<BR> E. सम् before<BR>ष्टु to praise, आनच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्ताव|संस्तावः
संस्ताव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The place occupied at a sacrifice by the Brāhmans<BR>reciting hymns and prayers.<BR>	 2. Celebrating or hymning in chorus,<BR>the repetition of the verses of the Vedas by a number of Brāh-<BR>mans.<BR> E. सम् together, (in chorus,) ष्टु to praise, (the gods,) घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तुत|संस्तुतः
संस्तुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Intimated, acquainted.<BR>	 2. Praised, hymned,<BR>eulogised.<BR>	 3. Agreeing together.<BR> E. सम् before ष्टु to praise, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तुति|संस्तुतिः
संस्तुति f. (-तिः) Praise, celebration.<BR> E. सम् before ष्टु to praise, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्त्याय|संस्त्यायः
संस्त्याय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Assemblage, collection, heap or number.<BR>	 2. Viciniay,<BR>proximity.<BR>	 3. Spreading, expansion, diffusion.<BR>	 4. A house.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before ष्ट्ये to crowd, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थ|संस्थः
संस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Staying, stopping, fixed, stationary.<BR>	 2. Stay-<BR>ing with, associated, domesticated.<BR>	 m. (-स्थः)<BR>	 1. A spy, a secret<BR>emissary.<BR>	 2. A countryman, a neighbour, a person of the same<BR>country, &c.<BR>	 3. A dweller, an inhabitant.<BR>	 f. (-स्था)<BR>	 1. Continuance<BR>in the right way, correct conduct.<BR>	 2. State or condition of being,<BR>time of life, &c.<BR>	 3. Occupation, business, profession.<BR>	 4. Stop,<BR>stay.<BR>	 5. End, completion.<BR>	 6. Manifestation, appearance.<BR>	 7. Resem-<BR>blance, likeness.<BR>	 8. A sort of sacrifice.<BR>	 9. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 10.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">Page747-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Death, dying.<BR>	 11. Form.<BR>	 12. An assembly.<BR>	 13. A royal ordinance.<BR>E. सम् implying completeness, association, &c., and ष्ठा to stay,<BR>affs. क or अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थान|संस्थानं
संस्थान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Like, resembling.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Form, figure, shape.<BR>2. Death, dying.<BR>	 3. Fabrication, construction.<BR>	 4. A place where<BR>four roads meet.<BR>	 5. Any place.<BR>	 6. A mark, a spot, a sign.<BR>	 7. A<BR>heap, a quantity.<BR>	 8. Primary formation, the aggregation of the<BR>primitive atoms.<BR>	 9. A vicinity, a neighbourhood, a common place<BR>of abode.<BR>	 10. Configuration.<BR>	 11. Position, (in Vedānta philoso-<BR>phy.)<BR> E. सम् before ष्ठा to stay or stand, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापन|संस्थापनं
संस्थापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Placing, fixing.<BR>	 2. Establishing.<BR>	 3. Collecting.<BR>	 4.<BR>Restraining.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Restraining, bringing back.<BR> E. सम् before ष्ठा<BR>to stay, causal v. aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापित
संस्थापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Placed, fixed, deposited.<BR>	 2. Established.<BR>	 3.<BR>Accumulated.<BR>	 4. Controled, restrained.<BR> E. सम् before ष्ठा to stay,<BR>causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थाप्य
संस्थाप्य Ind. Having placed.<BR> E. सम् before ष्ठा to stay, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थित|संस्थितः
संस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dead, deceased.<BR>	 2. Ended, finished.<BR>	 3. Es-<BR>tablished, fixed.<BR>	 4. Staying, stationary.<BR>	 5. Residing, being in or<BR>at.<BR>	 6. Heaped, collected.<BR>	 7. Placed in or on.<BR>	 8. Near or contiguous<BR>to.<BR>	 9. Like, resembling.<BR> E. सम् before ष्ठा to stay, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थिति|संस्थितिः
संस्थिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Death, dying.<BR>	 2. Abode, abiding, being or being<BR>stationary.<BR>	 3. Abiding, being or residing with.<BR>	 4. Duration, con-<BR>tinuance.<BR>	 5. State or condition, (of life.)<BR>	 6. Contiguity, connection.<BR>7. Heap, accumulation.<BR>	 8. Restraint.<BR> E. सम् before स्थिति staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पर्श|संस्पर्शः
संस्पर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Touching, contact, laying hold of.<BR>	 2. Perception,<BR>sense.<BR>	 f. (-र्शा) A fragrant plant, commonly Chakawat.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before स्पृश् to touch, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पर्शज
संस्पर्शज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born or produced by sense, by contact, &c.<BR> E. संस्पर्श, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पृष्ट
संस्पृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Touched.<BR> E. सम् before स्पृश् to touch, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फाल|संस्फालः
संस्फाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A ram.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR> E. सम् before स्फल् to shake, aff.,<BR>घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फुट|संस्फुटः
संस्फुट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Blossomed, blown,<BR> E. सम् before स्फुट् to blow, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फेट|संस्फेटः
संस्फेट m. (-टः) War, battle.<BR> E. सम् before स्फुट् to disrespect, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फोट|संस्फोटः
संस्फोट m. (-टः) War, battle.<BR> E. सम् before स्फुट् to hurt or kill, aff. घञ्;<BR>or with इ aff. संस्फोटि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मरण|संस्मरणं
संस्मरण n. (-णं) Remembering, calling to mind.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, and स्मरण remembering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृत
संस्मृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Remembered, called to mind.<BR> E. सम् and स्मृ to<BR>remember, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृति|संस्मृतिः
संस्मृति f. (-तिः) Recollection, remembrance.<BR> E. सम् before स्मृ to remember, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्राव|संस्रावः
संस्राव m. (-वः) Flowing, oozing.<BR> E. स्रु to go, with सम् prefix and ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहत|संहतः
संहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Strong-knit, well-limbed.<BR>	 2. Compact, close.<BR>3. Joined, attached or approximated to.<BR>	 4. Closed, shut.<BR>	 5. Col-<BR>lected, assembled.<BR>	 6. Struck, hurt, wounded, killed.<BR>	 7. Acting or<BR>making effort together, combining, combined.<BR>	 8. Closely allied.<BR>E. सम् with, together with, हन् to hurt or strike, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतजानुक|संहतजानुकः
संहतजानुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Knock-kneed.<BR> E. संहत approximated, close,<BR>and जानु the knee, कन् aff.; also without the aff. संहतजानु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहततल
संहततल m. (-लः) The two hands open, and the palms brought toge-<BR>ther.<BR> E. संहत closed, ला to get or be, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतता
संहतता f. (-ता) Close approximation or contact, &c.: see the next.<BR> E. संहत, तल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतत्व|संहतत्वं
संहतत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Compactness.<BR>	 2. Combination, &c.<BR>	 3. Approximation,<BR>contact.<BR>	 4. Union, agreement.<BR> E. संहत and त्व aff.; also with तल्,<BR>संहतता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतभ्रू
संहतभ्रू Adj. Knitting the brows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतस्तनी
संहतस्तनी f. (-नी) A woman with contiguous breasts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहति|संहतिः
संहति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Assemblage, collection, heap, number, host, multi-<BR>tude, &c.<BR>	 2. Combination, joint effort.<BR>	 3. Union, junction.<BR>	 4.<BR>Compactness.<BR>	 5. Strength.<BR>	 6. The body.<BR>	 7. Agreement.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, हन् to strike or hurt, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहनन|संहननं
संहनन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The body.<BR>	 2. Rubbing the limbs.<BR> E. सम् before हन् to<BR>strike or hurt, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहरण|संहरणं
संहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Collecting, accumulating.<BR>	 2. Restraining, checking.<BR>3. Taking, seizing.<BR>	 4. Destroying.<BR> E. सम् before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्ष|संहर्षः
संहर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. Pleasure, joy.<BR>	 3. Erection of the hair<BR>of the body, either from pleasure, or disease.<BR>	 4. Envy, emula-<BR>tion.<BR>	 5. Trituration, rubbing, grinding.<BR> E. सम् before हृष् to be<BR>pleased, or घृष् to rub, &c., aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्षयोगिन्
संहर्षयोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Joyful, delighted.<BR> E. संहर्ष, योगिन् who joins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहवन|संहवनं
संहवन n. (-नं) A group of four houses.<BR> E. सम् together हु to sacrifice,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहात|संहातः
संहात m. (-तः) One of the twenty-one hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहार|संहारः
संहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Destruction, loss.<BR>	 2. The destruction of the world.<BR>3. A division of Tartarus.<BR>	 4. Abridgment, abbreviation.<BR>	 5. Col-<BR>lection, assemblage.<BR>	 6. Restraining, suppressing.<BR>	 7. Practice.<BR>	 8.<BR>A fault in pronunciation.<BR>	 9. Close, end, conclusion.<BR>	 10. A charm<BR>or spell for restraining a magical weapon.<BR> E. सम् together, हृ to<BR>take, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहित|संहितः
संहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Attached, joined.<BR>	 2. Collected, assem-<BR>bled.<BR>	 3. Placed, fixed.<BR>	 4. Provided, furnished, equipped.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>1. An arrangement of the text of the Vedas into short sentences,<BR>regulated when the style is verse by the species of verse, and<BR>when prose by the subject, and denominated after the person or<BR>persons by whom the arrangement was originally made: it is also<BR>sometimes considered as synonymous with a Sākhā, a branch or<BR>or school of the Vedas of which sixteen are reckoned to the<BR>Rig-Veda, one hundred and one to the Yajush, one thousand in<BR>the Sāma, and nine in the Atharvan.<BR>	 2. A compendium, a collec-<BR>tion more or less compressed of laws, legends, &c.<BR>	 3. (In gram-<BR>mar,) Proximity of two letters without an intermediate pause,<BR>Sandhi or junction, though usually considered rather as the state<BR>preparatory to the actual junction than the junction itself.<BR>	 4. A<BR>compilation, a code, a digest.<BR> E. सम् before धा to have, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहूति|संहूतिः
संहूति f. (-तिः) Clamour, shout, tumultuous exclamation.<BR> E. सम् toge-<BR>ther, हूति calling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृत|संहृतः
संहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seized, laid hold of.<BR>	 2. Scattered, thrown.<BR>3. Destroyed.<BR>	 4. Compressed, contracted, abridged.<BR>	 5. With-<BR>drawn.<BR>	 6. Curbed, restrained.<BR> E. सम् before हृ to take, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृति|संहृतिः
संहृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Destruction, loss, disappearance.<BR>	 2. Contraction,<BR>abridgment.<BR>	 3. Taking, seizure.<BR>	 4. Connection.<BR> E. सम् before हृ to<BR>take, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृत्य
संहृत्य Ind. Having contracted or reduced in bulk.<BR>	 2. Having abridged,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सम्, हृ to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृष्ट
संहृष्ट f. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. Thrilled with joy.<BR>	 2. Bristling.<BR>	 3. Fired with emulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्राद|संह्रादः
संह्राद m. (-दः) Sound, noise.<BR> E. सम् before ह्रद् to sound, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्रादिन्
संह्रादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Sounding, making a noise.<BR> E. सम् before ह्रद्<BR>to sound, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्रीण
संह्रीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Bashful, modest, ashamed.<BR> E. सम्, and ह्री to be ashamed, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक|सकः
सक m. (-कः) He, that man.<BR> E. स he, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकट|सकटः
सकट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं) Bad, vile.<BR>	 m. (-टः) A small tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>E. स with, कट bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकटान्न|सकटान्नं
सकटान्न n. (-न्नं) Impure food.<BR> E. सकट, and अन्न boiled-rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकण्टक|सकंटक|सकण्टकः
सकण्टक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Thorny, prickly.<BR>	 2. Troublesome, perilous.<BR>m. (-कः) An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria.)<BR> E. स for सम् like or with,<BR>कण्टक a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर
सकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Bearing or returning tax or toll.<BR>	 2. Having<BR>rays, &c.<BR> E. स with, कर tax, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकरुण|सकरुणः
सकरुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Tender, compassionate.<BR> E. स with, करुण compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकण
सकण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Having ears.<BR>	 2. Hearing, listening.<BR> E. स for<BR>सह with, कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्म्मन्|सकर्मन्
सकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Performing any act or rite.<BR>	 2. Following<BR>similar business.<BR> E. स with or same, कर्म्म act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्म्मक|सकर्मक|सकर्म्मकः
सकर्म्मक m. (-कः) (In grammar,) The transitive verb.<BR> E. स with, कर्म्म act, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकल|सकलं
सकल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) All, whole, entire.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Together with<BR>a part.<BR>	 2. Entire.<BR>	 3. With all the digits, full, (as the moon.)<BR>	 4.<BR>Having a soft or low sound.<BR> E. स with, कला a part, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाकौल
सकाकौल m. (-लः) One of the twenty-one hells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाम|सकामः
सकाम f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Full of love.<BR>	 2. Lustful.<BR>	 3. One who has obtained his wish, satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकामम्
सकामम् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of:--1. With plea-<BR>sure.<BR>	 2. Contentedly.<BR>	 3. Assuredly.<BR>	 4. Indeed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकारण
सकारण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Having a cause, originating from a cause. E.<BR>स with, कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाल
सकाल n. Adv. (-लं) Betimes, early in the morning.<BR> E. स with, काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाश|सकाशः
सकाश f. (-शा) Having visibility.<BR>	 m. (-शः) Presence, nearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुक्षि
सकुक्षि Adj. Having the same womb, uterine, (as a brother.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुल|सकुलः
सकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Belonging to a noble family.<BR>	 2. Belonging<BR>the same family.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A Kinsman.<BR>	 2. A sort of fish; also<BR>शकुल.<BR> E. स with, कुल a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुल्य|सकुल्यः
सकुल्य m. (-ल्यः)<BR>	 1. A kinsman, one of the same family name and com-<BR>mon origin: see सगोत्र.<BR>	 2. A distant kinsman or relation; one who<BR>shares a divided oblation, as the grandson's grandson or other<BR>descendants as far as three degrees from him, or the offspring of<BR>the grandfather's grandfather or other remoter ancestor.<BR> E. स<BR>same, कुल्य of family: some authorities extend the name of<BR>Sakulya to the tenth descendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृत्
सकृत् m. (-कृत्) Fæces, ordure: more usually, शकृत्. Ind.<BR>	 1. Once.<BR>2. With, together with.<BR>	 3. Always.<BR>	 4. Formerly.<BR> E. सकृत् substi-<BR>tuted for एक one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृतगर्भा
सकृतगर्भा f. (-र्भा) A mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृत्प्रज|सकृत्प्रजः
सकृत्प्रज m. (-जः) A crow.<BR> E. सकृत् once, व्रज progeny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकोप
सकोप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Angry, displeased.<BR> E. स with, कोप wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्त|सक्तः
सक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Attached, joined, in contact with.<BR>	 2. Diligent,<BR>attentive, intent.<BR>	 3. Devoted or addicted to.<BR> E. षञ्ज् to embrace<BR>or adhere to, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्ति|सक्तिः
सक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Contact, union, junction, cohesion.<BR>	 2. Devotion or<BR>addiction to.<BR> E. षञ्ज् to embrace or adhere to, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तु|सक्तुः
सक्तु m. Plu. (-क्तुः) The flour fried and then ground.<BR> E. षच् to moisten,<BR>Unādi aff. तुन्; also read शक्तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तुक|सक्तुकः
सक्तुक m. (-कः) A species of poison.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तुफला
सक्तुफला f. (-ला) The Śami tree, (Mimosa suma, Rox.)<BR> E. सक्तु barley-<BR>meal, and फल fruit; of a similar white colour; also सक्तुफली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्थि
सक्थि n. (-क्थि)<BR>	 1. The thigh.<BR>	 2. Part of the frame of a cart.<BR>	 3. A bone.<BR>In compound सक्थि is changed to सक्थ after उत्तर, पूर्व, मृग, or a<BR>word denoting an object with which it is compared.<BR> E. षञ्ज् to<BR>unite, Unādi aff. क्थिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्षण
सक्षण f. (-णा) Having leisure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखि
सखि m. (सखा)<BR>	 1. A friend.<BR>	 2. An associate, a companion.<BR>	 f. (-खी) A<BR>woman's female friend or companion, a confidante, &c.<BR> E. स for<BR>समान all, (the world,) ख्या to celebrate, aff. इन्, and ङीष् fem. aff.;<BR>the masc. noun is irregularly inflected. At the end of compounds<BR>सखि is changed to सख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखित्व|सखित्वं
सखित्व n. (-त्वं) Friendship.<BR> E. सखि a friend, and त्व aff.; also सखिता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखीजन
सखीजन n. (-नं) A female friend or confidante.<BR> E. सखी, जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सख्य|सख्यं|सख्यः
सख्य n. (-ख्यं)<BR>	 1. Friendship.<BR>	 2. Equality.<BR>	 m. (-ख्यः) A friend.<BR> E. सखि a<BR>friend, यत् aff. of the property or pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सग्
सग्(ए)सगे r. 1st cl. (सगति) To cover; also षग् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगन्ध|सगंध|सगन्धः
सगन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>	 1. Fragant, odoriferous.<BR>	 2. Proud.<BR>	 m. (-न्धः) A<BR>relation, a co-heir.<BR> E. स for सम् same, like, and गन्ध connection;<BR>or स with, गन्ध smell, scent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर|सगरः
सगर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Poisonous.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A sovereign of Ayodhyā,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">Page749-a+ 60</a>]<BR>the father of ASAMANJA by KEŚINĪ, and sixty-thousand sons by<BR>SUMATI: the latter being turned into a heap of ashes by the<BR>sage KAPILA. GARUḌA instructed the king to perform their funer-<BR>al ceremonies with the waters of Gangā, to be brought from<BR>heaven for that purpose; this was finally accomplished by the<BR>devotion of BHAGĪRATHA, the great-grandson of ASAMANJA, who<BR>having led the river to the sea, denominated it Sāgara, in honour<BR>of his ancestor.<BR> E. स for सह with गर poison; being born together<BR>with a poison given to his mother by the other wife of his father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्भ|सगर्भः
सगर्भ m. (-र्भः) A brother by the same father and mother.<BR> E. स for<BR>समान the same, and गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्भ्य|सगर्भ्यः
सगर्भ्य m. (-र्भ्यः) A brother of whole blood, one by the same father<BR>and mother.<BR> E. स for समान same, गर्भ embryo, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्व्व|सगर्व
सगर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं)<BR>	 1. Proud.<BR>	 2. Flated.<BR> E. स with, गर्व्व pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगुण
सगुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Having or endowed with properties, qualities,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Worldly.<BR>	 3. Having a string, (as a bow.)<BR> E. स with, गुण a<BR>quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगोत्र|सगोत्रं|सगोत्रः
सगोत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Being of one family, of kin, related.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः)<BR>1. A distant kinsman.<BR>	 2. A kinsman of the same family-name,<BR>or one sprung from a common ancestor; one connected by funer-<BR>al oblations of food and water.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं) A family, a race or lineage.<BR>E. स for समान like, common, and गोत्र family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सग्धि|सग्धिः
सग्धि f. (-ग्धिः) Eating together.<BR> E. स for सम् with, अद् to eat, क्तिच् aff.;<BR>घस् is substituted for the root, the स rejected, घ changed to ग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सघ्
सघ् r. 5th cl. (सघ्नोति) To hurt, to kill; also षघ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घट
सङ्घट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Narrow, contracted.<BR>	 2. Crowded.<BR>	 3. Impass-<BR>able, impervious.<BR>	 n. (-टं)<BR>	 1. Difficulty, trouble.<BR>	 2. A defile, a pass.<BR>E. सम् before कटच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कटाक्ष|संकटाक्ष|सङ्कटाक्षः
सङ्कटाक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Winking, leering.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः) A tree, (Grislea<BR>tomentosa.)<BR> E. सङ्कट contracted, अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कथा|संकथा
सङ्कथा f. (-था) Conversation, discourse, talking together.<BR> E. सम् toge-<BR>ther, कथा speech; also सङ्कथन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कर|संकर|संकरः|सङ्करः
सङ्कर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Mixing, blending, confounding.<BR>	 2. A mixed caste or<BR>race, one proceeding from the promiscuous intercourse of the<BR>four tribes in the first instance, and again from their commerce<BR>with the descendants of such a connection, or the indiscriminate<BR>cohabitation of those descendants amongst one another; most<BR>Hindus of the present age are of one of the many branches of<BR>this race, the highest of which is impure and inferior to the<BR>Śūdra: under this term two kinds of men are included according<BR>to the Rāmāyana; the one denominated योनिसङ्कर, mixed or<BR>degraded by birth and the other आचारसङ्कर degraded by conduct.<BR>3. The mixing together of two or more dependent figures of speech<BR>in the same passage.<BR>	 4. Dust, sweepings.<BR>	 5. The crackling of<BR>flame.<BR>	 f. (-री) A new bride.<BR> E. सम् before कॄ to scatter, or कृ to<BR>make, aff. अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्करीकरण|संकरीकरण|सङ्करीकरणं
सङ्करीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Reducing to the state of the mixed or outcaste<BR>tribes, causing loss of caste.<BR>	 2. Blending, mixing.<BR>	 3. Confusion,<BR>either in kind, number, arrangement.<BR> E. सङ्कर a mixed-race, च्वि<BR>augment, करण doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्करीकृत
सङ्करीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Blended, mixed, confused.<BR>	 2. Outcaste.<BR> E. सङ्कर, and कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कर्षण|संकर्षण|संकर्षणं|सङ्कर्षणं|संकर्षणः|सङ्कर्षणः
सङ्कर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Attracting, drawing.<BR>	 2. Ploughing, making<BR>furrows, &c.<BR>	 m. (-णः) BALADEVA.<BR> E. सम् before कृष् to plough, &c.,<BR>aff. युच् or ल्युट्. As applied to the demi-god it refers to his re-<BR>moval in embryo from the womb of DEVAKĪ to that of ROHIṆĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल|संकल|संकलः|सङ्कलः
सङ्कल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. Collection, quantity.<BR>	 2. Addition.<BR> E. सम् together,<BR>कल् to number, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कलन|संकलन|संकलनं|सङ्कलनं
सङ्कलन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Contact, junction.<BR>	 2. Blending, clinging, twin-<BR>ing, intermixture.<BR>	 3. Heaping as corn, &c.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Addition, (in<BR>arithmetic.)<BR> E. सम् with or like, कल् to number, aff. युच् or ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कला|संकला
सङ्कला Aptote. Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कलित|संकलित|सङ्कलितः
सङ्कलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Heaped, piled, arranged.<BR>	 2. Brought in con-<BR>tact, blended, intermixed.<BR>	 3. Laid hold of.<BR>	 4. Added.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Addition, (in arithmetic.)<BR> E. सम् before कल् to number, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्प|संकल्प|संकल्पः|सङ्कल्पः
सङ्कल्प m. (-ल्पः)<BR>	 1. Volition, will, resolve, mental determination.<BR>	 2. A<BR>solemn vow or declaration of purpose.<BR>	 3. Expectation of desired<BR>consequences from any voluntary act.<BR> E. सम् before कृप् to be able,<BR>aff. घञ्, and the र changed to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पज|संकल्पज|संकल्पजः
सङ्कल्पज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Born of or proceeding from the hope or<BR>expectation of advantage.<BR>	 m. (-जः) KĀMA or love.<BR> E. सङ्कल्प, and ज<BR>born; also सङ्कल्पजन्मन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पजन्मन्|संकल्पजन्मन्
सङ्कल्पजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. सङ्कल्प volition, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पभव|संकल्पभव|सङ्कल्पभवः
सङ्कल्पभव m. (-वः) KĀMA.<BR> E. सङ्कल्प will, भव born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पयोनि|संकल्पयोनि|सङ्कल्पयोनिः
सङ्कल्पयोनि m. (-निः) KĀMA, the deity of love.<BR> E. सङ्कल्प will, योनि place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्परूप|संकल्परूप
सङ्कल्परूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Of the nature of or conformable to the<BR>will or purpose.<BR> E. सङ्कल्प, and रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पसम्भव|संकल्पसम्भव|संकल्पसंभव
सङ्कल्पसम्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Produced from or arising out of the hope or<BR>desire of advantage.<BR>	 m. (-वः) Love or KĀMA.<BR> E. सङ्कल्प, सम्भव birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पात्मक|संकल्पात्मक
सङ्कल्पात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Willing, resolving, referring to volition. E.<BR>सङ्कल्प, आत्मक one with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कल्पित|संकल्पित
सङ्कल्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Proposed, sought as the result of any act. E.<BR>सङ्कल्प, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कसूक
सङ्कसूक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Unsteady, fickle, changeable.<BR>	 2. Uncertain,<BR>doubtful.<BR>	 3. Weak, feeble.<BR>	 4. Bad, wicked.<BR> E. सम् before कस्<BR>to go, Unādi aff. ऊकन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कार|संकार|संकारः|सङ्कारः
सङ्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Dust, sweepings.<BR>	 2. The crackling of flame.<BR>	 f. (-री) A<BR>girl recently deflowered, a new bride, &c.<BR> E. सम्, कृ to make, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्काश|संकाश|संकाशः|सङ्काशः
सङ्काश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Like, similar, (in composition.)<BR>	 2. Near.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-शः) Appearance, presence.<BR> E. सम् before काश् to shine, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्किल|संकिल|संकिलः|सङ्किलः
सङ्किल m. (-लः) A burning torch, a fire-brand.<BR> E. सम् before किल् to be<BR>white, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कीर्ण|संकीर्ण|सङ्कीर्णं|संकीर्णः|सङ्कीर्णः
सङ्कीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Crowded, confused.<BR>	 2. Miscellaneous.<BR>	 3. Im-<BR>pure.<BR>	 4. Mixed.<BR>	 5. Of mixed and consequently impure origin or<BR>caste.<BR>	 6. Contracted, narrow.<BR>	 7. Spread, diffused.<BR>	 8. Scattered.<BR>	 9.<BR>Indistinct, confused, (as a writing.)<BR>	 m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. A man of a mixed<BR>caste.<BR>	 2. A mixed mode or note, (in music.)<BR>	 3. An elephant in<BR>rut.<BR>	 n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. An enemy.<BR>	 2. A difficulty.<BR> E. सम् before कॄ to<BR>scatter, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कीर्णचारिन्|संकीर्णचारिन्
सङ्कीर्णचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Wandering about, going in to all sorts<BR>of places.<BR> E. सङ्कीर्ण, चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कीर्णयोनि|संकीर्णयोनि
सङ्कीर्णयोनि mfn. (-निः-निः-नि)<BR>	 1. Of mixed or impure origin.<BR>	 2. Of a<BR>mongrel breed, (as a mule.)<BR> E. सङ्कीर्ण, योनि place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कीर्त्तन|सङ्कीर्तन|संकीर्तनं|सङ्कीर्त्तनं
सङ्कीर्त्तन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Celebrating, praising, honour, glorification.<BR>	 2.<BR>Singing the praise of a deity.<BR> E. सम् before कॄत् to praise, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कीर्त्तित|सङ्कीर्तित|संकीर्तित|सङ्कीर्त्तितः
सङ्कीर्त्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Praise, renowned, celebrated.<BR> E. सम् intensitive,<BR>कॄत् to praise, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कु
सङ्कु m. (-ङ्कुः) A hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कुचित|संकुचित|सङ्कुचितं
सङ्कुचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Unblown, unopened.<BR>	 2. Closed, shut.<BR>	 3.<BR>Narrowed, contracted.<BR> E. सम् before कुच् to contract, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कुल|संकुल|सङ्कुलं
सङ्कुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Crowded, confused, filled with so as to be im-<BR>pervious.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Inconsistent and contradictory speech.<BR>	 2. War.<BR>3. A crowd, a mob.<BR>	 4. A flock, a flight.<BR> E. सम् together, कुल् to<BR>accumulate, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कृति|संकृति
सङ्कृति f. (-तिः) A from of metre, a stanza of four lines, of 24 syllables<BR>each.<BR> E. सम् complete, कृति a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्केत|संकेत|संकेतः|सङ्केतः
सङ्केत r. 10th cl. (सङ्केतयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To call or invite.<BR>	 2. To counsel or advise.<BR>3. To fix or appoint a time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्केत|संकेत|संकेतः|सङ्केतः
सङ्केत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Engagement, agreement, appointment, convention.<BR>	 2.<BR>Condition, provision, the circumstances under which any thing is<BR>necessarily or naturally effected.<BR>	 3. Sign, gesture, gesticulation.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">Page750-a+ 60</a>]<BR>4. A short explanatory rule, (in gram.)<BR>	 n. (-तं) Rendezvous. E.<BR>सङ्केत to appoint a time, &c., aff. अच्; or सम + कित-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्केतक|संकेतकः
सङ्केतक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Rendezvous.<BR>	 2. Convention.<BR>	 3. Appointment.<BR>	 4. A<BR>lover or mistress who meets by assignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्केतस्थान|संकेतस्थान
सङ्केतस्थान n. (-नं) Place of assignation.<BR> E. सङ्केत, and स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कोच|संकोच|सङ्कोचं|संकोचः|सङ्कोचः
सङ्कोच m. (-चः)<BR>	 1. Shutting, closing, contracting, contraction.<BR>	 2. Bind-<BR>ing, tying.<BR>	 3. Abridgment, diminution.<BR>	 4. Terror, fear.<BR>	 5. A sort<BR>of fish, a scate, (Raia Sancura, HAM.)<BR>	 n. (-चं) Saffron.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before कुच् to contract, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्कोचन|संकोचन|संकोचनं
सङ्कोचन n. (-नं) Astringing, causing to shrink or close.<BR> E. सम्, कुच् to<BR>contract, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रन्दन|संक्रन्दन|संक्रंदन|संक्रंदनः|संक्रन्दनः|सङ्क्रन्दनः
सङ्क्रन्दन m. (-नः) INDRA.<BR> E. सम् before क्रदि to cry out, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संङ्क्रम
संङ्क्रम mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>	 1. Difficult progress, clambering up rocks, fording<BR>torrents, making way through almost impervious or inaccessible<BR>passes, &c.<BR>	 2. The means of effecting such a passage, a causeway<BR>a bridge, &c.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Going, moving, travelling.<BR>	 2. The pass-<BR>age of a planetary body through the zodiac.<BR>	 3. Passage from one<BR>point to another, traversing, transit, transition.<BR>	 4. Concurrence. E.<BR>सम् before क्रम् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संङ्क्रमण
संङ्क्रमण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going from or to, passage, transition.<BR>	 2. Going with,<BR>concurrence.<BR>	 3. The sun's passage from one sign of the zodiac to<BR>another.<BR>	 4. The first day of the summer solstice.<BR>	 5. A certain<BR>class of problems, (in algebra.)<BR> E. सम्, and क्रम् to go, ल्युट् aff.:<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रमितृ|संक्रमितृ
सङ्क्रमितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who goes or proceeds, who or what passes<BR>from one to another.<BR> E. सम्, क्रम् to go, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रान्त|संक्रांत|संक्रान्त|सङ्क्रान्तः
सङ्क्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Passed, gone from one to another, trans-<BR>ferred, &c.<BR>	 2. Entered, (into a new sign.)<BR>	 3. Depicted, imaged,<BR>reflected.<BR> E. सम् before क्रम् to go, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रान्ति|संक्रान्ति|संक्रांति|संक्रांतिः|संक्रान्तिः|सङ्क्रान्तिः
सङ्क्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. The actual passage of the sun or other planetary<BR>bodies from one sign of the zodiac into another.<BR>	 2. Passage in<BR>general, proceeding from one time or condition or life to another,<BR>from one place to another, &c.<BR>	 3. Going, proceeding in general.<BR>	 4.<BR>Meeting together, union.<BR>	 5. Transference, imparting.<BR>	 6. The<BR>power of teaching or transference.<BR>	 7. Imitation, reflection.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before क्रम् to go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्राम|संक्राम|संक्रामः|सङ्क्रामः
सङ्क्राम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Difficult progress or passage over steep rocks,<BR>through narrow defiles, &c.<BR>	 2. A bridge of ropes, &c: see सङ्क्रम. E.<BR>सम् before क्रम् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रीडण
सङ्क्रीडण n. (-णं) Sporting, playing.<BR> E. सम् before क्रीड् to play, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रीडमाण
सङ्क्रीडमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Sporting, playing.<BR> E. सम् before क्रीड् to<BR>play, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्रुद्ध|संक्रुद्ध
सङ्क्रुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Violent, enraged.<BR> E. सम्, and क्रुद्ध angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्लेद|संक्लेद|संक्लेदः|सङ्क्लेदः
सङ्क्लेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The fluid secretion which is supposed to form<BR>upon conception, and to be the rudiment of the fœtus.<BR>	 2. Mois-<BR>ture, wet, damp.<BR> E. सम् together, and क्लेद moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षय|संक्षय|संक्षयः
सङ्क्षय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The destruction of the world.<BR>	 2. Loss, destruction<BR>in general.<BR>	 3. End.<BR> E. सम् completely, क्षि to perish, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षिप्त|संक्षिप्त|संक्षिप्तः
सङ्क्षिप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Abridged, abbreviated, concise, compressed.<BR>2. Small, compact.<BR>	 3. Thrown.<BR>	 4. Sent.<BR>	 5. Taken from or away,<BR>seized.<BR> E. सम् before क्षिप् to throw or send, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षिप्ति|संक्षिप्ति|संक्षिप्तिः
सङ्क्षिप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Abridgment.<BR>	 2. Throwing.<BR>	 3. Sending.<BR>	 4. Ambuscade.<BR>5. Transition from one feeling to another.<BR> E. सम्, क्षिप् to throw,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षीयमाण
सङ्क्षीयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Perishing being destroyed.<BR> E. सम् before क्षि to waste, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षेप|संक्षेप|संक्षेपः
सङ्क्षेप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Abridgment, abbreviation, conciseness, compression.<BR>2. Sending.<BR>	 3. Throwing.<BR>	 4. Taking away.<BR>	 5. Assisting in another's<BR>duty.<BR> E. सम् before क्षिप to throw or send aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षेपण|संक्षेपण|संक्षेपणं
सङ्क्षेपण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Abridgment, brevity.<BR>	 2. Sending.<BR>	 3. Throwing.<BR>	 4.<BR>Taking away.<BR> E. सम् before क्षिप् to throw or send, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्षोभ|संक्षोभ|संक्षोभः
सङ्क्षोभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. Overturning, upsetting.<BR>	 2. Shaking, trembling, agita-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Pride, arrogance.<BR> E. सम् before क्षुभ् to tremble, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्क्ष्णुवान
सङ्क्ष्णुवान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Whetting, sharpening.<BR>	 2. Inflaming, exci-<BR>ting.<BR> E. सम् before क्ष्णु to sharpen, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्य|संख्य|संख्यं|सङ्ख्यं
सङ्ख्य n. (-ङ्ख्यं) War, battle.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्ख्या)<BR>	 1. Number in general, or a number,<BR>a numeral.<BR>	 2. Deliberation, reasoning, reflection.<BR>	 3. Intellect, un-<BR>derstanding.<BR>	 4. Manner.<BR>	 5. Enumeration.<BR> E. सम् before ख्या substi-<BR>tuted for चक्ष् to speak well, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यता|संख्यता
सङ्ख्यता f. (-ता) Number, numeration, counting.<BR> E. तल् added to the last;<BR>also with त्व, सङ्ख्यत्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यात|संख्यात|सङ्ख्यातं
सङ्ख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Numbered, counted, reckoned.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A num-<BR>ber.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A kind of riddle or enigma.<BR> E. सम् before ख्या to tell,<BR>aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यान|संख्यान|संख्यानं|सङ्ख्यानं
सङ्ख्यान n. (-नं) Numbering, numeration, reckoning.<BR> E. सम् before ख्या to tell, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्यावत्|संख्यावत्|संख्यावन्त्
सङ्ख्यावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Having or being possessed of number,<BR>numbered.<BR>	 2. Intelligent, discriminating.<BR>	 m. (-वान्) A learned<BR>Brāhman, a Paṇḍit.<BR> E. सङ्ख्या number, &c., मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ख्येय|संख्येय|सङ्ख्येयं
सङ्ख्येय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Numerable, to be counted or numbered.<BR> E. सङ्ख्या<BR>a number, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग|संग|संगः|सङ्गः
सङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. Meeting, encountering.<BR>	 2. Association, intercourse,<BR>friendship.<BR>	 3. Joining, uniting.<BR>	 4. Desire, wish, cupidity.<BR>	 5. Addic-<BR>tion or devotion to.<BR>	 6. Confluence of rivers.<BR>	 7. Contact, touch.<BR>	 8.<BR>Worldly attachment.<BR> E. सम् together, गम् to go, aff. ड; or षञ्ज् to<BR>embrace, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गणिका|संगणिका
सङ्गणिका f. (-का) Incomparable or unequalled discourse.<BR> E. सम् before<BR>गण् to count, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गत|संगत|सङ्गतं
सङ्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Apposite, proper, (as speech.)<BR>	 2. Mixed, united.<BR>3. Met, encountered.<BR>	 4. Collected, accumulated.<BR>	 5. In conjunction,<BR>(of planets.)<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Convened, met.<BR>	 2. Joined.<BR>	 3. United in<BR>wedlock.<BR>	 4. Adapted.<BR>	 5. Contracted, shrunk up n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Friend-<BR>ship, acquaintance.<BR>	 2. Union, meeting.<BR>	 3. Alliance.<BR>	 4. A consist-<BR>ant speech.<BR> E. सम्, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गति|संगति|संगतिः|सङ्गतिः
सङ्गति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Meeting, union, mixture.<BR>	 2. Knowledge.<BR>	 3. Associa-<BR>tion, intercourse.<BR>	 4. Frequenting, going to.<BR>	 5. Accidental meeting.<BR>6. Relation, applicability, connection.<BR>	 7. Questioning for con-<BR>tinued or further information.<BR> E. सम् together, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गम|संगम|संगमः|सङ्गमः
सङ्गम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Meeting, union, mixture, junction, the encounter of<BR>persons, the association of friends or lovers, the confluence of<BR>rivers, the fitness or adaptation of two things to each other, &c.<BR>2. (In astronomy,) Planetary conjunction.<BR>	 3. Touch, contact.<BR>	 4.<BR>society, company.<BR>	 5. Sexual intercourse.<BR>	 6. Fitness, adaptation. E.<BR>सम् together, like, suitably, गम going: see also सङ्ग, सङ्गत, सङ्गति, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गर|संगर|सङ्गरं|संगरः|सङ्गरः
सङ्गर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Misfortune, calamity.<BR>	 3. Promise,<BR>assent, agreement.<BR>	 4. A bargain, a transaction of sale.<BR>	 5. Poison.<BR>6. Knowledge.<BR>	 7. Acceptance.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The fruit of the Śami tree.<BR>E. सम् before गॄ to swallow, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गरहित
सङ्गरहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Indifferent, stoical, free from attachment.<BR> E. सङ्ग, रहित free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गव|संगव|संगवः|सङ्गवः
सङ्गव m. (-वः) A name of the three MUHŪRTAS after early dawn, (form-<BR>ing the second watch of the day.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गवर्ज्जित|सङ्गवर्जित
सङ्गवर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Free from worldly attachments or affections.<BR> E. सङ्ग, वर्ज्जित abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गविच्युति
सङ्गविच्युति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Separation from, or dissolution of worldly affec-<BR>tion.<BR>	 2. Disunion.<BR> E. सङ्ग, and विच्युति separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गिन्|संगिन्
सङ्गिन् mfn. (-ङ्गी-ङ्गिनी-ङ्गि)<BR>	 1. Uniting with, going to or with, attached.<BR>2. Devoted or addicted to, intent on.<BR>	 3. Libidinous, lustful,<BR>desirous.<BR> E. सङ्ग union, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गिरमाण
सङ्गिरमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Promising.<BR> E. सम् before गॄ to speak, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गीत|संगीत|सङ्गीतं
सङ्गीत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The exhibition of song, dancing, and music, as a<BR>public entertainment.<BR>	 2. The art or science of singing accom-<BR>panied by music and dancing.<BR>	 3. Chorus.<BR>	 f. (-ता) Sung in chorus<BR>or harmony.<BR> E. सम् together, and गीत sung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गीतक|संगीतकं
सङ्गीतक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Concert, symphony.<BR>	 2. A public entertainment con-<BR>sisting of songs, dancing and music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गीतार्थ|संगीतार्थः
सङ्गीतार्थ m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. The apparatus or materials for a concert.<BR>	 2. The<BR>subject of a musical performance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गीति|संगीति|संगीतिः|सङ्गीतिः
सङ्गीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Conversation, discourse.<BR>	 2. The science of music and<BR>dancing.<BR>	 3. Concert, harmony.<BR> E. सम् together, गा or गै to sing,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गीर्ण|संगीर्ण|सङ्गीर्णं
सङ्गीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Promised, agreed.<BR> E. सम् before गॄ to speak, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गुप्त|संगुप्त|सङ्गुप्तः
सङ्गुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Hidden, concealed.<BR>	 m. (-प्तः) A Buddha or Bauddha<BR>saint.<BR> E. सम् before गुप्त hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गूढ|संगूढ|सङ्गूढः
सङ्गूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Heaped, piled, arranged.<BR>	 2. United, joined,<BR>brought in contact.<BR>	 3. Contracted, abridged.<BR> E. सम् before गुह् to<BR>hide, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गृहीत|संगृहीत
सङ्गृहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken, accepted, seized.<BR>	 2. Assented to.<BR>E. सम् before ग्रह् to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्गोपन|संगोपन|सङ्गोपनं
सङ्गोपन n. (-नं) Hiding, concealment.<BR> E. सम् before गुप् to hide, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्रह|संग्रह|संग्रहः|सङ्ग्रहः
सङ्ग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A compilation and abridgment.<BR>	 2. A catalogue. a<BR>list or summary.<BR>	 3. Quantity, collection.<BR>	 4. Restraining, confin-<BR>ing.<BR>	 5. Taking, seizing.<BR>	 6. Propitiating, pleasing, attaching.<BR>	 7.<BR>Protecting, guarding.<BR>	 8. A place where anything is kept.<BR>	 9. As-<BR>sent, promise.<BR>	 10. Elevation, loftiness.<BR>	 11. Velocity.<BR>	 12. Clenching<BR>the fist.<BR>	 13. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 14. Reception, admission.<BR>	 15. Con-<BR>junction, conglomeration.<BR>	 16. Agglomeration.<BR>	 17. Sum, amount.<BR>18. Mention.<BR>	 19. Accumulation, hoarding up.<BR>	 20. An epithet of<BR>ŚIVA.<BR> E. सम् before ग्रह् to take, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्रहण|संग्रहण|संग्रहणं
सङ्ग्रहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking, accepting, seizing.<BR>	 2. Sexual intercourse.<BR>	 3.<BR>Hope.<BR>	 4. Collecting.<BR>	 5. Compiling.<BR>	 6. Encasing.<BR>	 7. Adultery.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णी) Diarrhœa, dysentery.<BR> E. सम् before ग्रह् to take, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्राम|संग्राम|संग्रामः|सङ्ग्रामः
सङ्ग्राम r. 10th cl. (सङ्ग्रामयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To fight.<BR>	 2. To make war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्राम|संग्राम|संग्रामः|सङ्ग्रामः
सङ्ग्राम m. (-मः) War, battle.<BR> E. सङ्ग्राम to fight, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्रामपटह|संग्रामपटह|संग्रामपटहः|सङ्ग्रामपटहः
सङ्ग्रामपटह m. (-हः) A large military drum.<BR> E. संग्राम war, पटह a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्ग्राह|संग्राह|संग्राहः|सङ्ग्राहः
सङ्ग्राह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Laying hold of forcibly, seizing, griping.<BR>	 2. The fist.<BR>3. Clenching the fist.<BR>	 4. The gripe of a shield.<BR> E. सम् before ग्रह्<BR>to seize, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घ|संघ|संघः|सङ्घः
सङ्घ n. (-ङ्घं)<BR>	 1. Flock, multitude, number, a collection of living beings<BR>either of the same or different species.<BR>	 2. A heap, a quantity in<BR>general.<BR>	 3. A number of people living together.<BR> E. सम् before हन्<BR>to kill or hurt, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घचारिन्|संघचारिन्
सङ्घचारिन् m. (-री) A fish in general.<BR> E. सङ्घ a shoal, चर् to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घजीविन्|संघजीविन्
सङ्घजीविन् m. (-वी) A hired porter or labourer, a colly.<BR> E. सङ्घ a crowd,<BR>and जीविन् who lives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घट्ट|संघट्ट|संघट्टः|सङ्घट्टः
सङ्घट्ट m. (-ट्टः)<BR>	 1. Clash, shock, collision.<BR>	 2. Friction, rubbing together.<BR>3. Meeting, encounter.<BR>	 4. Embracing.<BR>	 f. (-ट्टा) A large creeper.<BR>E. सम् before घट्ट् to go, affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घट्टन|संघट्टन|संघट्टनं|सङ्घट्टनं
सङ्घट्टन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Meeting, encountering, occurrence.<BR>	 2. Union, junc-<BR>tion, contact, cohesion.<BR>	 3. Close contact, cleaving or adhering to,<BR>the intertwining of wrestlers, the embraces of lovers, &c.<BR>	 4. Fric-<BR>tion, rubbing together.<BR> E. सम् before घट्ट् to move, aff. ल्युट् or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घर्ष|संघर्ष|संघर्षः|सङ्घर्षः
सङ्घर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Envy, emulation, rivalry, vieing or contending for<BR>superiority.<BR>	 2. Trituration, rubbing, grinding.<BR>	 3. Collision.<BR>	 4.<BR>Going gently, gliding, flowing.<BR> E. सम् before घृष् to rub, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घशस्|संघशस्
सङ्घशस् Ind. Collectively, altogether, in flocks.<BR> E. सङ्घ and शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घाटिका|संघाटिका
सङ्घाटिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A bawd, a procuress.<BR>	 2. A pair, a couple.<BR>	 3. Smell.<BR>4. An aquatic plant, (Trapa bispinosa.)<BR> E. सम् before घट् to unite,<BR>aff. ण्वुल्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घात|संघात|संघातः|सङ्घातः
सङ्घात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Assemblage, multitude, heap, quantity.<BR>	 2. Associa-<BR>tion, combination.<BR>	 3. Composition of words, formation of com-<BR>pound terms.<BR>	 4. Killing, striking, hurting.<BR>	 5. Phlegm.<BR>	 6. A<BR>particular mode of walking in dramatic representation.<BR>	 7. A<BR>division of Tartarus.<BR> E. सम् before हन् to strike or kill, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घातवत्|संघातवत्|संघातवन्त्
सङ्घातवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having or connected with many, a heap,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सङ्घात and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सङ्घुष्ट|संघुष्ट|सङ्घुष्टं|संघुष्टः
सङ्घुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Resonant, resounding.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः) Sound, cry,<BR>noise.<BR> E. सम् before धुष् to sound, aff. क्त; also optionally with the<BR>augment इट्, सङ्घुषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचकितम्
सचकितम् Ind. Alarmingly, timorously, in a startled manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचराचर
सचराचर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) All whether animate or inanimate.<BR> E. स with<BR>चर moving, अचर stationary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचि|सचिः
सचि m. (-चिः)<BR>	 1. Friendship, intimacy, connection.<BR>	 2. A friend.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-चिः or ची) The wife of INDRA.<BR> E. षच to be connected, aff. इन्<BR>and ङीष् optionally added; also शचि and शची ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचिल्लक|सचिल्लकः
सचिल्लक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Blear-eyed.<BR> E. स for सह with, चिल्ल a bad eye, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचिव|सचिवः
सचिव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A friend, a companion, an associate.<BR>	 2. A minister,<BR>a counsellor.<BR> E. सचि friendship, वा to go or get, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेतन
सचेतन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Rational.<BR>	 2. Conscious, sensible.<BR> E. स with,<BR>चेतन intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेतस्
सचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः) Conscious, reflective, understanding.<BR> E. स with, चेतस् mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेल
सचेल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Clothed, dressed.<BR> E. स with, चेल clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचेष्ट|सचेष्टः
सचेष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Active, making effort.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः) The mango-<BR>tree, (Mangifera Indica.)<BR> E. स with, चेष्टा effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चरित
सच्चरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Honest, upright.<BR>	 2. Virtuous.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Good<BR>conduct.<BR> E. सत् good, चरित conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चारा
सच्चारा f. (-रा) Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चिदंश
सच्चिदंश m. (-शः) Intellect, intellectual part or portion.<BR> E. सत् being,<BR>चित् intellect, and अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चिदात्मन्
सच्चिदात्मन् m. (-त्मा) The soul which consists of entity and thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चिदानन्द|सच्चिदानंद|सच्चिदानन्दः
सच्चिदानन्द n. (-न्दं)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ, or the Supreme Spirit.<BR>	 2. Entity,<BR>knowledge and joy.<BR> E. सत् being present, चित् intellect, and आनन्द<BR>happiness; the external source of wisdom and happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्छूद्र
सच्छूद्र m. (-द्रः) A Śūdra, who has gone through the same ceremonies<BR>as the other classes, which though not directed by and indeed<BR>contrary to law, is in some places customary.<BR> E. सत् pure, and शूद्र<BR>a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजन|सजनः
सजन f. (-ना) Having men or living beings.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजम्बाल|सजंबाल|सजम्बालः
सजम्बाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Muddy, clayed.<BR> E. स for सह with, जम्बाल mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजल
सजल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Watery, wet,<BR> E. स with, जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजाति|सजातिः
सजाति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>	 1. Of the same sort or species, of the same<BR>tribe, &c.<BR>	 2. Like, similar.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) The son of a man and woman<BR>of the same caste.<BR> E. स for समान same, and जाति species.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजातीय|सजातीयः
सजातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Descended from parents of the same tribe or<BR>caste.<BR>	 2. Of the same tribe.<BR>	 3. Of the same species.<BR>	 4. Like,<BR>similar.<BR> E. स for समान same, जाति sort, kind, and च्छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सजुष्
सजुष् mfn. (-जूः-जूः-जुः) Associated, an associate or companion.<BR>	 2. Lov-<BR>ing, attached.<BR>	 m. (nom. सजूः, सजुषी, सजुषः) A companion. Ind. (-जूः)<BR>With, together with.<BR> E. स with जुष् to please, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्ज|सज्जः
सज्ज mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं)<BR>	 1. Armed, accoutred.<BR>	 2. Fortified.<BR>	 3. Prepared,<BR>got ready.<BR>	 4. Ornamented, decorated.<BR>	 5. Covered, clothed.<BR>	 f. (-ज्जा)<BR>1. Dress, decoration.<BR>	 2. Armour, mail.<BR> E. षस्ज् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जन|सज्जनं|सज्जनः
सज्जन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Of good family, well-born.<BR>	 2. Respectable,<BR>reputable.<BR>	 3. Good, virtuous.<BR>	 4. Arming, putting on armour.<BR>	 5.<BR>Dressing, preparing.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A guard, a sentry, a picquet.<BR>	 2. A<BR>ferry, a Ghāt.<BR>	 3. Fastening.<BR>	 4. Preparing.<BR>	 5. Dressing.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1.<BR>Caparisoning an elephant.<BR>	 2. Dress, decoration.<BR>	 3. Arming,<BR>accoutring.<BR> E. षसज् to go, aff. युच्; or सत् excellence, जन a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जमान
सज्जमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Arming.<BR>	 2. Dressing.<BR>	 3. Getting ready, pre-<BR>paring.<BR>	 4. Hesitating, (in speech.)<BR> E. षस्ज् to go, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जित|सज्जितः
सज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Armed, accoutred.<BR>	 2. Dressed, decorated,<BR>ornamented.<BR>	 3. Prepared, made.<BR> E. सज्जा armour, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जीकरण
सज्जीकरण n. (-णं) Arming, arraying, preparing, decorating.<BR> E. सज्ज<BR>armed, and करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जीकृत
सज्जीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Armed, accoutred, prepared, decorated.<BR> E. सज्ज<BR>and कृत made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जीभूत
सज्जीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Armed, prepared, decorated.<BR> E. सज्ज, भूत become, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्य
सज्य mfn. (-ज्यः-ज्या-ज्यं) Strung, (as a bow,) having a bow-string.<BR> E. स<BR>with, ज्या a bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्वर
सज्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Heat, fever.<BR>	 2. Wrath, indignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्च|संच|संचः|सञ्चः
सञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) A collection of leaves for writing.<BR> E. सम् + चि-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चकित|संचकित
सञ्चकित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Afraid, timid.<BR> E. सम्, and चकित timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चत्|संचत्
सञ्चत् n. (-ञ्चत्) Cheating, juggling.<BR> E. सम् together, चि to collect, अति<BR>Unādi aff. and the radical vowel rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चय|संचय|संचयः|सञ्चयः
सञ्चय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Heap, quantity, number, multitude.<BR>	 2. Gathering. E.<BR>सम् together, चि to collect, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चयन|संचयन|संचयनं|सञ्चयनं
सञ्चयन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Collecting, gathering.<BR>	 2. Collecting the ashes or bones<BR>of a body which has been burnt.<BR> E. सम् together, चि to collect,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चयिन्|संचयिन्
सञ्चयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Who or what collects.<BR> E. सम्, चि to collect, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चर|संचर|संचरः|सञ्चरः
सञ्चर m. (-रः) A defile, any narrow or difficult pass, a road along the<BR>edge of a mountain, or a bridge over a mountain-stream, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Difficult passage, travelling along almost impracticable routes.<BR>	 3.<BR>A road, a way.<BR>	 4. The body.<BR>	 5. Killing.<BR>	 6. The passage of a<BR>planet from one sign of the zodiac to another.<BR> E. सम् before चर्<BR>to go, aff. घञ्; also सञ्चार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चरण|संचरणं
सञ्चरण n. (-णं) Going, motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चलन|संचलन|संचलनं|सञ्चलनं
सञ्चलन nf. (-नं-ना) Trembling, shaking.<BR> E. सम् before चल् to go, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चान|संचानः|सञ्चानः
सञ्चान m. (-नः) A bird, a hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चाय्य|संचाय्य|संचाय्यः|सञ्चाय्यः
सञ्चाय्य m. (-य्यः) A particular sacrifice, at which the juice of the acid<BR>Asclepias is drank.<BR> E. सम् together, चि to collect, participial aff.<BR>ण्यत्, form irr., आय being substituted for the regular change: see<BR>सञ्चेय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चार|संचार|संचारः|सञ्चारः
सञ्चार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Difficult progress.<BR>	 2. Difficulty, distress.<BR>	 3. Leading,<BR>guiding.<BR>	 4. Inciting.<BR>	 5. Impelling, setting in motion.<BR>	 6. Conta-<BR>gion, communication or transmission of disease.<BR>	 7. Course, transi-<BR>tion.<BR>	 8. A gem supposed to be found in the head of a serpent.<BR>9. A way, a pass.<BR> E. सम् before चर् to go, aff. घञ्: see सञ्चर; or सम्<BR>and चर् to go, causal v., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारक|संचारक|संचारकः
सञ्चारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A leader, a guide.<BR>	 2. An instigator.<BR>	 3. An orator.<BR>E. सम्, चर् to go, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारजीविन्|संचारजीविन्
सञ्चारजीविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Indigent, distressed, calamitous in want<BR>of aid or protection.<BR> E. सञ्चार difficulty, and जीविन् living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारण|संचारण|संचारणं
सञ्चारण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Leading, guiding.<BR>	 2. Impelling, instigating.<BR>	 3.<BR>Moving, setting in motion.<BR> E. सम् before चर् to go, causal v.,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारिका|संचारिका
सञ्चारिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A female messenger or go-between.<BR>	 2. A bawd.<BR>	 3.<BR>A brace, a pair.<BR>	 4. Smell.<BR> E. सम् before चर् to go, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारित|संचारित
सञ्चारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Led, guided.<BR>	 2. Driven, impelled.<BR>	 3. Set in<BR>motion, moved.<BR>	 4. Communicated, (as disease.)<BR> E. सम् before चर् to<BR>go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चारिन्|संचारिन्
सञ्चारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Fickle, changeable, not permanent.<BR>	 2.<BR>Moving, going.<BR>	 3. Difficult, inaccessible.<BR>	 4. Moving, putting in<BR>motion.<BR>	 5. Transmitted, hereditary, (as disease.)<BR>	 6. Contagious.<BR>m. (-री)<BR>	 1. Incense.<BR>	 2. A division of the Bhāvas, the same as the<BR>व्यभिचारिन्, q. v. or the reverse of the स्थायिन् or fixed and steady<BR>sentiments.<BR>	 3. An evanescent feeling which strengthens the per-<BR>vading sentiments.<BR>	 4. Air, wind.<BR> E. सम् before चर् to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चित|संचित
सञ्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Assembled, accumulated, collected, gathered.<BR>2. Enumerated.<BR>	 3. Full of, provided with.<BR>	 4. Obstructed.<BR>	 5.<BR>Dense, thick, (as a wood.)<BR> E. सम्, चि to collect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चिति|संचिति|संचितिः
सञ्चिति f. (-तिः) A collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चित्रा|संचित्रा
सञ्चित्रा f. (-त्रा) A plant, (Salvainia cucullata.)<BR> E. सम् completely, चित्र<BR>variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चिन्तन|संचिन्तन|संचिंतनं
सञ्चिन्तन n. (-नं) Considering, reflecting.<BR> E. सम् before चि to think,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चिन्तित|संचिंतित|संचिन्तित
सञ्चिन्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Deliberated, weighed.<BR> E. सम्, चिति to think, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चिन्त्य|संचिन्त्य
सञ्चिन्त्य Ind. Having considered, reflected, thoughtful.<BR> E. सम्, चिति to<BR>think, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चूर्णन|संचूर्णन|संचूर्णनं
सञ्चूर्णन n. (-नं) Breaking to pieces, reducing to powder.<BR> E. सम्, चूर्ण to grind, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चूर्णित|संचूर्णित
सञ्चूर्णित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cut or broken to pieces, pulverised, com-<BR>minuted.<BR> E. सम् before चूर्ण to pound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चेय|संचेय|सञ्चेयं
सञ्चेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be collected or accumulated.<BR> E. सम्, चि to gather, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्चोदित|संचोदित
सञ्चोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ordered, commanded.<BR> E. सम्, and चोदित ordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छन्न|संछन्न
सञ्छन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Covered.<BR> E. सम् completely, and छन्न covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्छिन्न|संछिन्न
सञ्छिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Cut, cut off.<BR>	 2. Dissipated, removed.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before छिद् to cut, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्|संज्
सञ्ज् r. 1st cl. (सञ्जति) To go or move: see षञ्ज् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज|संज|संजः|सञ्जः
सञ्ज m. (-ञ्जः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-ञ्जा) A she-goat.<BR> E. सम् uniform-<BR>ly, all (mankind), जन् to be born, (or created by whom,) and ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जनन|संजनन
सञ्जनन n. (-नं) Begetting, causing, producing.<BR> E. सम् before जन् to be<BR>born, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जनयत्
सञ्जनयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Begetting, producing, causing.<BR> E. सम् before<BR>जन् to be born, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जल्प|संजल्प|संजल्पः
सञ्जल्प m. (-ल्पः)<BR>	 1. Conversation.<BR>	 2. Uproar, confusion, confused talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जवन|संजवन|संजवनं|सञ्जवनं
सञ्जवन n. (-नं) A group of four houses joined together in a qua-<BR>drangle.<BR> E. सम् together, जु to go, aff. युच्; also सञ्जीवन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जात|संजात
सञ्जात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. Become.<BR> E. सम् and जात<BR>born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जानान|संजानान
सञ्जानान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Knowing, observing.<BR>	 2. Watching, who or<BR>what keeps watch.<BR> E. सम् before ज्ञा to know, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जीवन|संजीवन|संजीवनं|सञ्जीवनं
सञ्जीवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Animating, bringing to life.<BR>	 2. A cluster of four<BR>houses.<BR>	 3. One of the twenty-one hells.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A kind of elixir.<BR>E. सम् together, जीव् to live, ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जुघुक्षा|संजुघुक्षा
सञ्जुघुक्षा f. (-क्षा) Wish or attempt to preserve.<BR> E. सम् before गुह् to hide,<BR>desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्जुघुक्षु|संजुघुक्षु
सञ्जुघुक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Wishing to preserve, hide, conceal, &c.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before गुह् to hide, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्वर|संज्वर|संज्वरः|सञ्ज्वरः
सञ्ज्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Heat, the heat of fire, burning, scorching, burn.<BR>	 2.<BR>Fever.<BR> E. सम् before ज्वर् to burn, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्वरातुर|संज्वरातुर
सञ्ज्वरातुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Overcome by or affected with fever, fevered,<BR>feverish.<BR> E. सञ्ज्वर, and आतुर distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सञ्ज्वारिन्|संज्वारिन्
सञ्ज्वारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Affected with fever, fevered, diseased. E.<BR>सम् before ज्वर् to be feverish, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्
सट् r. 1st cl. (सटति) To form a part. r. 10th cl. (साटयति-ते) To show, to manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट|सटं
सट mfn. Subst. (-टः-टा-टं) An ascetic's clotted hair, or the hair<BR>collected into a loose braid and twisted forwards upon the fore-<BR>head.<BR>	 2. A mane.<BR>	 3. A crest.<BR>	 4. Bristles of a boar.<BR> E. षट् to be a<BR>part of, and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटाङ्क|सटांक|सटाङ्कः
सटाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A lion.<BR> E. सटा mane, and अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटि|सटिः
सटि f. (-टिः or -टी) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet,) but applied also to<BR>the Curcuma amda: see सटि.<BR> E. षट् to be a part of, इन् aff. and<BR>ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटीक
सटीक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Accompanied or explained by a commentary.<BR>E. स with, टीका a comment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्ट्
सट्ट् r. 10th cl. (सट्टयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To be strong.<BR>	 3. To give.<BR>	 4. To dwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्टक|सट्टकं
सट्टक n. (-कं) A sort of minor drama in Prākrit only.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्वा
सट्वा f. (-ट्वा)<BR>	 1. A kind of bird.<BR>	 2. A musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सठ्
सठ् r. 10th cl. (साठयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To finish, to complete.<BR>	 2. To leave un-<BR>finished.<BR>	 3. To go, to move.<BR>	 4. To adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सणसूत्र|सणसूत्रं
सणसूत्र n. (-त्रं) Packthread, hempen cord or thread. E. See शणसूत्र,<BR>the sibilants being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सण्ड|संड|सण्डः
सण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A eunuch: see षण्ड, and शण्ड, &c., the sibilants being interchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सण्डिश|संडिश|संडिशः|सण्डिशः
सण्डिश m. (-शः) A pair of tongs. “सांँडासि ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सण्डीन|संडीन|संडीनं|सण्डीनं
सण्डीन n. (-नं) One of the modes of flight attributed to birds,<BR>perching, alighting.<BR> E. सम् before डी to fly, aff. क्त, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्|सन्त्|संत्
सत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>	 1. True.<BR>	 2. Good, virtuous.<BR>	 3. Being, existing.<BR>	 4.<BR>Excellent, best.<BR>	 5. Venerable, respectable.<BR>	 6. Wise, learned.<BR>	 7.<BR>Firm, steady.<BR>	 8. Right, proper.<BR>	 f. (-सती)<BR>	 1. A virtuous wife; in<BR>ordinary use applied especially to the wife, who burns herself<BR>with her husband's corpse.<BR>	 2. The goddess UMĀ.<BR>	 3. A fragrant<BR>earth, commonly Surat-earth.<BR>	 4. A species of the Pratishthā<BR>metre.<BR>	 n. (सत्)<BR>	 1. The true GOD, the always present and all-pervad-<BR>ing spirit.<BR>	 2. That which really is, entity, existence, essence.<BR>	 3.<BR>Truth, reality.<BR>	 4. That which is good.<BR>	 m. (-सन्) A virtuous man.<BR>Ind. (-सत्) In composition, a particle of reverence or respect,<BR>implying, good, fit, &c.; as सत्क्रिया virtue, doing what is right,<BR>&c.<BR> E. अस् to be, aff. of the participle of the present tense शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतत|सततं
सतत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eternal, continual.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-तं) Eternally,<BR>continually.<BR> E. सम् before तन् to spread, aff. क्त, and the म rejected<BR>optionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतत्त्व|सतत्त्वं
सतत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं) Natural property, nature.<BR> E. स for समान universal, तत्त्व nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतानन्द|सतानन्दः
सतानन्द m. (-न्दः) The sage GAUTAMA, the author of the Nyāya or<BR>logical philosophy.<BR> E. सत् the good, and आनन्द who delights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सति|सतिः
सति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. End, destruction.<BR>	 2. Gift, giving, donation.<BR> E. षण् to<BR>give or षो to destroy, क्तिन् aff.; also साति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीत्व|सतीत्वं
सतीत्व n. (-त्वं) Virtuousness or purity in a wife.<BR> E. सतीः see सत्, and त्व<BR>aff.; also with तल्, सतीता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीन|सतीनः
सतीन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Pease, or a particular kind of pulse.<BR>	 2. A bamboo. E.<BR>सति, from सत् being life, इन् master; with कन् added सतीनक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीनक|सतीनकः
सतीनक m. (-कः) Pease; also सितीनक, and सतीलक, &c.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीर्थ|सतीर्थः
सतीर्थ m. (-र्थः) A fellow student, the pupil of the same spiritual<BR>preceptor.<BR> E. स for सह same, तीर्थ a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीर्थ्य|सतीर्थ्यः
सतीर्थ्य m. (-र्थ्यः) A fellow student: see the last.<BR> E. स for सह the same, तीर्थ्य a teacher, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतील|सतीलः
सतील m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A bamboo.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>	 mf. (-लः-ला) Pease, pulse, or<BR>a particular kind, called Teorā.<BR> E. सती, लक्ष् to make, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीलक|सतीलकः
सतीलक m. (-कः) Pulse in general, or a particular sort.<BR> E. सतील wind,<BR>कै to utter, aff. ड; also सितीलक, सतीनक, सातीलक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतृष्
सतृष् mfn. (-तृट्)<BR>	 1. Thirsty, greedy, cupidinous.<BR>	 2. Thursty, (literally.)<BR>E. स for सहित with, तृष् thirst, literally or figuratively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतेर|सतेरः
सतेर m. (-रः) Husk, chaff.<BR> E. सन, एर aff; the न is changed to त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कदम्ब|सत्कदम्बः
सत्कदम्ब m. (-म्बः) A tree, (Nauclea cordifolia.)<BR> E. सत् good, कदम्ब the<BR>Cadamba-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कर्म्मन्|सत्कर्मन्
सत्कर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. A good act, piety, virtue.<BR>	 2. Hospitality.<BR>	 3. Funeral<BR>obsequies.<BR>	 4. Expiation.<BR> E. सत् and कर्म्मन् act; also सत्क्रिया, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्काञ्चनार|सत्काञ्चनारः
सत्काञ्चनार m. (-रः) A sort of ebony: see रक्तकाञ्चन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्काण्ड|सत्कांड|सत्काण्डः
सत्काण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A hawk, a kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कार|सत्कारः
सत्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Reverence, respect.<BR>	 2. Hospitable treatment or<BR>reception.<BR>	 3. Care.<BR>	 4. A meal.<BR>	 5. A festival.<BR> E. सत्, कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कृत|सत्कृतः
सत्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Worshipped, adored.<BR>	 2. Respected, revered.<BR>3. Welcomed, saluted.<BR>	 4. Entertained, treated with hospitality.<BR>5. Done rightly or properly.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Hospitality.<BR>	 2. Respect.<BR>	 3.<BR>Virtue.<BR>	 m. (-तः) Śiva.<BR> E. सत् excellent, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कृतिः|सत्कृति
सत्कृतिः f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Doing good, acting properly, virtue, morality, &c.<BR>2. Treating with respect.<BR> E. सत् good, and कृति act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कृत्य
सत्कृत्य Ind. Having treated with respect, &c.<BR> E. सत्, कृत्य having made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्क्रिया
सत्क्रिया f. (-या) Funeral or obsequial ceremonies.<BR>	 2. Any purificatory<BR>ceremony.<BR>	 3. Doing good, charity, virtue, &c.<BR>	 4. Worship,<BR>homage.<BR>	 5. Respectful treatment.<BR>	 6. Salutation, welcome, courtesy.<BR>7. Hospitality.<BR> E. सत् good, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्तम|सत्तमः
सत्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Best, excellent.<BR>	 2. Very venerable or respect-<BR>able.<BR>	 3. Most virtuous.<BR> E. सत् good, and तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ता
सत्ता f. (-त्ता)<BR>	 1. Being, existence.<BR>	 2. Goodness, excellence.<BR>	 3. Reality. E.<BR>सत् being, तल् aff. of the abstract; also सत्त्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्र
सत्त्र n. (-त्त्रं)<BR>	 1. Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>	 2. A long sacrificial session lasting<BR>from 13 to 100 days.<BR>	 3. Good conduct.<BR>	 4. Liberality, munificence.<BR>5. Covering, clothing, concealing.<BR>	 6. Fraud, roguery, cheating.<BR>	 7. A<BR>wood, a forest.<BR>	 8. Wealth.<BR>	 9. A house.<BR>	 10. A tank, a pond.<BR>	 m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>SATRĀJIT the father of SATYABHĀMĀ.<BR> E. सद् to go, Unādi aff. त्रन्<BR>or ष्ट्र; in writting, one त may be omitted, and it occurs, सत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रशाला
सत्त्रशाला f. (-ला) An apartment in which Brāhmans or mendicants, &c.<BR>are presented with food and gifts.<BR> E. सत्र giving, and शाला a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रा
सत्त्रा Ind. With, together with.<BR> E. स for सह with, त्रा to preserve, aff.<BR>क्विप्; also written, सत्रा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रि
सत्त्रि m. (-त्त्रिः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR>	 3. A victor, a conqueror.<BR>E. षद् to go, or waste, to destroy, &c., Unādi aff. त्रि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रिन्
सत्त्रिन् m. (-त्त्री)<BR>	 1. A liberal house-keeper, one constantly performing<BR>sacrifice and distributing alms.<BR>	 2. An ambassador, an agent<BR>residing in a foreign country.<BR>	 3. A priest superintending or per-<BR>forming a sacrifice.<BR> E. सत्त्र munificence, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्व|सत्त्वं|सत्त्वः
सत्त्व n. (-त्त्वं)<BR>	 1. One of the three Guṇas or properties of man and<BR>nature; the quality of excellence or goodness: that which<BR>enlightens, constitutes knowledge, and is the cause of truth, and<BR>the predominance of which renders the person, in whom it resides,<BR>virtuous, gentle, devout, charitable, chaste, honest, &c., and the<BR>thing, pure, mild, &c.<BR>	 2. Substance, thing, either elementary<BR>substance, as, earth, air fire, &c., or anything of which some<BR>property may be predicated.<BR>	 3. Mind, intellect.<BR>	 4. Nature,<BR>natural, property or disposition.<BR>	 5. Vigour, power.<BR>	 6. Strength.<BR>7. Self-possession or command.<BR>	 8. Breath.<BR>	 9. Being, existence.<BR>	 10.<BR>Essence, substance.<BR>	 11. Wealth.<BR>	 12. Certainty.<BR>	 13. Life, the<BR>principle of being.<BR>	 14. A substantive, noun.<BR>	 15. A demon, a<BR>goblin.<BR>	 mn. (-त्त्वः-त्त्वं)<BR>	 1. An animal, a being.<BR>	 2. An embryo.<BR> E. षद् to<BR>perish, aff. त्वत्; or सत् being, good, excellent, &c., त्व aff. of the<BR>abstract: one त being rejected also, it is read सत्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वगुण|सत्त्वगुणः
सत्त्वगुण m. (-णः) The property of goodness: see the last.<BR> E. सत्त्व, गुण attribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वता
सत्त्वता f. (-ता) Purity, goodness, the existence of the Satwa-Guṇa, or<BR>property of truth and virtue, &c.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वमेजय
सत्त्वमेजय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Frightening animals, making them tremble.<BR>E. सत्त्व, and एज् to shake, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्ववत्|सत्त्ववन्त्
सत्त्ववत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Pure, virtuous, endowed with the quality<BR>of goodness.<BR>	 2. Natural.<BR>	 3. Existent, &c.<BR> E. सत्त्व and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वविहित
सत्त्वविहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Done spontaneously or naturally.<BR>	 2.<BR>Virtuous, upright.<BR> E. सत्त्व, and विहित effected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसंप्लव|सत्त्वसम्प्लव|सत्त्वसंप्लवः
सत्त्वसंप्लव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Universal destruction.<BR>	 2. Loss of vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसंशुद्धि|सत्त्वसंशुद्धिः
सत्त्वसंशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Purity of nature or disposition.<BR> E. सत्त्व, संशुद्धि purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसम्पन्न|सत्त्वसंपन्न|सत्त्वसम्पन्नः
सत्त्वसम्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Equable, even-minded, neither elated by<BR>prosperity nor depressed by misfortune.<BR>	 2. Good, excellent.<BR> E. सत्त्व<BR>the good quality, and सम्पन्न endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसार|सत्त्वसारः
सत्त्वसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Essence of strength.<BR>	 2. A most powerful person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वस्थ|सत्त्वस्थः
सत्त्वस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Excellent, holy, pure.<BR>	 2. Being or existing<BR>in the nature of things.<BR>	 3. Animate, inherent in animals.<BR> E. सत्त्व,<BR>स्थ what stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वानुरूप
सत्त्वानुरूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) According to nature or natural quality.<BR> E. सत्त्व, अनुरूप conformable to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वोत्साह|सत्त्वोत्साहः
सत्त्वोत्साह m. (-हः) Natural energy or perseverance.<BR> E. सत्त्व, उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पत्र|सत्पत्रं
सत्पत्र n. (-त्रं) The new leaf of a water-lily.<BR> E. सत् good, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पथ|सत्पथः
सत्पथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A good road.<BR>	 2. Correct or virtuous conduct, doc-<BR>trine, &c.<BR> E. सत् good, पथ a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्परिग्रह|सत्परिग्रहः
सत्परिग्रह m. (-हः) Acceptance of gifts from proper persons.<BR> E. सत्, and<BR>परिग्रह acceptance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पशु|सत्पशुः
सत्पशु m. (-शुः) An animal fit for a sacrifice, a victim.<BR> E. सत् good, and पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पात्र
सत्पात्र n. (-त्रं) A worthy or virtuous person.<BR> E. सत्, and पात्र a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पात्रवर्ष
सत्पात्रवर्ष m. (-र्षः) Judicious liberality bestowing favours on the worthy.<BR>E. सत्पात्र, वर्ष raining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पुत्त्र
सत्पुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. The father of a son.<BR>	 2. A virtuous son.<BR>	 3. A son<BR>who performs all the prescribed rites in honour of his ancestors.<BR>E. सत् being or good, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्परुष
सत्परुष m. (-षः) A worthy or spirited man.<BR> E. सत् and पुरुष a male.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्प्रतिपक्ष|सत्प्रतिपक्षः
सत्प्रतिपक्ष m. (-क्षः) Contrariety of doctrine or argument, knowledge of<BR>the opposite arguments proving the existence or nonexistence of<BR>a thing; viz:--sound is eternal because it is audible; on the<BR>other hand sound is non-eternal because it is a product, (in<BR>logic.)<BR> E. सत् being, प्रतिपक्ष opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्फल|सत्फलः
सत्फल m. (-लः) The pomegranate.<BR> E. सत् good, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्य|सत्यं|सत्यः
सत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं)<BR>	 1. True.<BR>	 2. Sincere, honest, speaking the truth.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Truth.<BR>	 2. An oath.<BR>	 3. The first Yuga or age, the golden<BR>age, comprising one million seven hundred and twety-eight thou-<BR>sand years.<BR>	 4. Demonstrated conclusion.<BR>	 m. (-त्यः)<BR>	 1. RĀMA-<BR>CHANDRA.<BR>	 2. The uppermost of the seven Lokas or worlds, the<BR>abode of BRAHMĀ, and heaven of truth.<BR>	 f. (-त्या)<BR>	 1. SĪTĀ, the wife<BR>of RĀMA.<BR>	 2. The mother of VYĀSA.<BR>	 3. DRAUPADĪ.<BR>	 4. DURGĀ.<BR>	 5.<BR>SATYABHĀMĀ.<BR>	 6. Speaking the truth, sincerity, veracity. Ind.<BR>(सत्यम्) Indeed, verily, a particle of interrogation and assevera-<BR>tion.<BR> E. सत् being, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यक|सत्यकं
सत्यक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) True, veracious.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Ratification of a bargain.<BR>E. सत्य as above, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यङ्कार|सत्यंकार|सत्यंकारः|सत्यङ्कारः
सत्यङ्कार m. (-रः) Ratification of a bargain.<BR> E. सत्य truth, कार making,<BR>confirming, मुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यङ्कारकृत|सत्यंकारकृत|सत्यङ्कारकृतः
सत्यङ्कारकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Given or deposited in order to bind or ratify<BR>a bargain.<BR> E. सत्यङ्कार as above, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यता
सत्यता f. (-ता) Truth, trueness.<BR> E. तल् added to सत्य; also with त्व, सत्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यधन
सत्यधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Virtuous, sincere, upright.<BR> E. सत्य, धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यभामा
सत्यभामा f. (-मा) One of KṚṢṆA'S wives and daughter of SATRĀJIT.<BR>E. सत्य true, भाम beautiful, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यभारत|सत्यभारतः
सत्यभारत m. (-तः) VYĀSA, the poet.<BR> E. सत्य true, भारत the Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ययुग|सत्ययुगं
सत्ययुग n. (-गं) The first of the four Yugas or ages, the period of genera<BR>virtue and purity, or golden age, comprising a term of 1,728,000<BR>years.<BR> E. सत्य truth, युग age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ययौवन|सत्ययौवनः
सत्ययौवन m. (-नः) A Vidyādhara or demi-god so named.<BR> E. सत्य truth, यौवन youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यरत|सत्यरतः
सत्यरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Honest, sincere.<BR>	 m. (-तः) VYĀSA.<BR> E. सत्य the<BR>truth, and रत devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवक्तृ
सत्यवक्तृ mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ) A speaker of truth.<BR> E. सत्य, वक्तृ who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवचन
सत्यवचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Speaking truth.<BR>	 2. Acknowledging or admitting<BR>truth.<BR> E. सत्य, and वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवचस्
सत्यवचस् mfn. (-चाः-चाः-चः) Speaking truth, veracious.<BR>	 m. (-चाः) A Ṛṣi,<BR>a saint, a seer.<BR>	 n. (-चः) Truth.<BR> E. सत्य truth, वचस् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवत्|सत्यवन्त्
सत्यवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) True, possessing or practising truth.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-वान्) The name of a king.<BR>	 f. (-वती)<BR>	 1. The mother of a VYĀSA,<BR>and wife of PARĀŚARA.<BR>	 2. The wife of NĀRADA.<BR>	 3. The wife of<BR>RISHIKA, a saint.<BR> E. सत्य truth, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवतीसुत|सत्यवतीसुतः
सत्यवतीसुत m. (-तः) The poet VYĀSA.<BR> E. सत्यवती his mother's name, सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवद्य
सत्यवद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) True-speaking, veracious.<BR>	 m. (-द्यः) Truth. E.<BR>सत्य, and वद् to speak, with क्यप् or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवाच्
सत्यवाच् mfn. (-वाक्) Speaking truth, veracious, sincere.<BR>	 m. (-वाक्)<BR>	 1.<BR>A crow.<BR>	 2. A Ṛṣi, a saint.<BR> E. सत्य true, वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवादित्व
सत्यवादित्व n. (-त्वं) Speaking truth.<BR> E. सत्यवादिन्, त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवादिन्
सत्यवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Speaking truth.<BR> E. सत्य truth, वादिन् who speaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवृत्त|सत्यवृत्तः
सत्यवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Practising or speaking the truth.<BR> E. सत्य truth,<BR>and वृत्त chosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यव्रत|सत्यव्रतः
सत्यव्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Practising or adhering to the truth, veracious,<BR>honest, sincere.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A king, the 25th of the solar dynasty in<BR>the second age.<BR> E. सत्य the truth, व्रत religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसङ्काश|सत्यसंकाश|सत्यसङ्काशः
सत्यसङ्काश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Likely, probable, possible, like the truth. E.<BR>सत्य truth, सङ्काश like; also, similar compounds, as सत्यसन्निभ, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसङ्गर|सत्यसंगर|सत्यसंगरः|सत्यसङ्गरः
सत्यसङ्गर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) True, veracious.<BR>	 m. (-रः) KUVERA, the god of<BR>wealth.<BR> E. सत्य the truth, सम् with गॄ to swallow, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसन्ध|सत्यसंध|सत्यसंधः|सत्यसन्धः
सत्यसन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Veracious, adhering to or observing the truth.<BR>m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. RĀMA.<BR>	 2. BHARATA, the younger brother of RĀMA.<BR>	 3.<BR>The prince JANAMEJAYA.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा) DRAUPADĪ, the wife of PĀṆḌU<BR>princes.<BR> E. सत्य truth, सम् before धा to have or hold, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसाक्षिन्
सत्यसाक्षिन् m. (-क्षी) An unexceptionable witness.<BR> E. सत्य, साक्षिन् a<BR>witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याकृति|सत्याकृतिः
सत्याकृति f. (-तिः) Ratification of a bargain.<BR> E. सत्य truth, आङ् before कृ<BR>to make, to confirm, aff. क्तिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याग्नि|सत्याग्निः
सत्याग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A name of the saint AGASTYA.<BR> E. सत्य the truth, and अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यात्मन्
सत्यात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्मं) True.<BR>	 m. (-त्मा) A virtuous and upright man.<BR>E. सत्य, and आत्मन् Soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यानुरक्त
सत्यानुरक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Upright, true.<BR> E. सत्य, and अनुरक्त attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यानृत|सत्यानृतं
सत्यानृत n. (-तं) Commerce, trade, traffic.<BR> E. सत्य truth, and अनृत false-<BR>hood, a mixed practice of truth and lies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यापन|सत्यापनं
सत्यापन nf. (-नं-ना) Ratification of a bargain.<BR> E. सत्य nominal verb, to<BR>speak or observe the truth, causal form, सत्याप, and ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्योत्कर्ष|सत्योत्कर्षः
सत्योत्कर्ष m. (-र्षः) Eminence or excellence in truth.<BR> E. सत्य, and उत्कर्ष<BR>excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्योद्य
सत्योद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Speaking the truth.<BR> E. सत्य the truth, उद्य to be said or uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र|सत्त्रं|सत्रं
सत्र r. 10th cl. (सत्रयते)<BR>	 1. To act liberally.<BR>	 2. To be connected.<BR>	 3. To<BR>spread or extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र|सत्त्रं|सत्रं
सत्र n. (-त्रं) Sacrifice, &c.: see सत्त्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रप
सत्रप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Ashamed, modest.<BR> E. स with, त्रपा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रिजातक|सत्रिजातकं
सत्रिजातक n. (-कं) Meat which has been once fried with spices, &c., then<BR>soaked and dried, and again dressed with Ghee and condiments.<BR>E. स for सह with, त्रि three, जातक species of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्व
सत्व n. (-त्वं) The quality of excellence or goodness, &c.: see सत्त्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वर|सत्वरं
सत्वर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Quick, expeditious.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-रं) Quickly, swiftly.<BR>E. स for सह with, त्वरा dispatch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वरता
सत्वरता f. (-ता) Quickness, speed.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with<BR>त्व, सत्वरत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्संसर्ग|सत्संसर्गः
सत्संसर्ग m. (-र्गः) Association with the good or respectable.<BR> E. सत्, संसर्ग connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सङ्ग|सत्संग|सत्संगः
सत्सङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Association with the good.<BR> E. सत्, and सङ्ग association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सन्निधान|सत्संनिधान
सत्सन्निधान n. (-नं) Association or intercourse with the wise and good. E.<BR>सत्, and सन्निधान propinquity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्समागम|सत्समागमः
सत्समागम m. (-मः) Association with the good.<BR> E. सत्, समागम encounter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सहाय|सत्सहायः
सत्सहाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Having a friend.<BR>	 2. Having virtuous friends.<BR>E. सत् being, or good, &c. सहाय a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सार|सत्सारः
सत्सार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A painter.<BR>	 2. A poet. Adj. Having good essence. E.<BR>सत् excellence, सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सथूत्कार|सथूत्कारः
सथूत्कार n. (-रं) Sputtering in speech.<BR> E. स for सहित with, थूत imitative<BR>sound, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदंशक|सदंशकः
सदंशक m. (-कः) A crab.<BR> E. स with, दंशक a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदंशवदन|सदंशवदनः
सदंशवदन m. (-नः) A heron.<BR> E. स with, दंश a tooth or beak, वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद|सदः
सद m. (-दः) The fruit of trees.<BR> E. षद् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदञ्जन|सदञ्जनं
सदञ्जन n. (-नं) Calx of brass.<BR> E. सत good, excellence, अञ्जन stibium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदन|सदनं
सदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Perishing, decaying.<BR>	 4. Exhaus-<BR>tion.<BR>	 5. A sacrificial hall.<BR> E. षद् to go or perish, aff. युच् or ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदय
सदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Benevolent, compassionate.<BR> E. स with, दया<BR>clemency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदर
सदर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Fearful, afraid.<BR> E. स with, दर fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदस्
सदस् fn. (-दाः-दः)<BR>	 1. An assembly, a meeting.<BR>	 2. Seat, residence.<BR> E. षद्<BR>to go, (to which,) Unādi aff. असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदसत्|सदसन्त्
सदसत् mfn. (-सन्-सती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Existent and nonexistent.<BR>	 2. True and<BR>false.<BR>	 3. Perceptible and non-perceptible.<BR>	 4. Real and unreal.<BR>	 5.<BR>Good and bad.<BR>	 6. Virtuous and wicked.<BR>	 n. Du.<BR>	 1. Entity and non-<BR>entity.<BR>	 2. Good and evil.<BR> E. सत्, असत untrue, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदसदात्मक
सदसदात्मक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Being both real and unreal, existent and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">Page755-a+ 60</a>]<BR>nonexistent, substantial though imperceptible.<BR> E. सदसत् and<BR>आत्मक self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदसद्विवेक
सदसद्विवेक m. (-कः) Discrimination between true and false, &c. E.<BR>सदसत्, विवेक judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदसद्व्यक्तिहेतु
सदसद्व्यक्तिहेतु m. (-तुः) The cause of discrimination between what is good and bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदस्य|सदस्यः
सदस्य m. (-स्यः)<BR>	 1. An assistant or by-stander at a sacrifice, &c., one<BR>whose business it is to notice and correct mistakes.<BR>	 2. Any per-<BR>son present at an assembly, a spectator, an assessor, a member,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सदस् an assembly, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदा
सदा Ind. Always, ever, at all times.<BR> E. स for सर्व्व all, दाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदागति|सदागतिः
सदागति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>	 3. Final happiness, eman-<BR>cipation from life.<BR>	 4. The Supreme Spirit.<BR> E. सदा, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाचार|सदाचारः
सदाचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The traditionary observances of the Hindu castes, as<BR>preserved in the land lying between the Sarasvatī and Drishad-<BR>wati rivers.<BR>	 2. Virtuous conduct.<BR> E. सत् pure, virtuous, and आचार<BR>observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदातन|सदातनः
सदातन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Eternal.<BR>	 m. (-नः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सदा always, ठ्युल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदातोया
सदातोया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Mimosa octandra.)<BR>	 2. An overflowing<BR>river.<BR> E. सदा always, तोय water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदात्मन्
सदात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Good, virtuous.<BR> E. सत्, and आत्मत् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदादान|सदादानः
सदादान n. (-नं) Liberality, munificence.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The elephant of<BR>INDRA.<BR>	 2. A name of GAṆEŚA.<BR>	 3. An elephant in rut.<BR> E. सदा<BR>always, दान giving, or the ichor that exudes from the elephant's<BR>temples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानन्द|सदानंद|सदानन्दः
सदानन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Always happy.<BR>	 m. (-न्दः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. सदा, आनन्द happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानर्त्त|सदानर्त|सदानर्तः|सदानर्त्तः
सदानर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A wagtail.<BR> E. सदा always, नर्त्त a dancer. “खञ्जने ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानीरवहा
सदानीरवहा f. (-हा) A small river in the north of Bengal.<BR> E. सदा always,<BR>नीर water, वह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानीरा
सदानीरा f. (-रां) The Karatoya, a small river in the north of Bengal.<BR> E. सदा always, नीर water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदापुष्प|सदापुष्पः
सदापुष्प m. (-ष्पः) The cocoanut.<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी) A shrub, gigantic swallow-wort<BR>(the white variety.)<BR> E. सदा always, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाफल|सदाफलः
सदाफल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The cocoanut tree.<BR>	 2. The glomerous-fig tree.<BR>	 3.<BR>The Bel, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR> E. सदा always, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाभव्य
सदाभव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Attentive, present.<BR> E. सदा always, भव्य being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाभद्रा
सदाभद्रा f. (-द्रा) A shrub, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR> E. सदा always, भद्र<BR>auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदायोगिन्
सदायोगिन् m. (-गी) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सदा always, योग union by meditation, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाशिव|सदाशिवः
सदाशिव m. (-वः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. सदा always, शिव auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाश्रित
सदाश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Attached or belonging to the virtuous, pure,<BR>good, lovely, &c.<BR>	 2. Always connected with or dependent on. E.<BR>सत् good, &c., or सदा always, and आश्रित connected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदुत्तर
सदुत्तर n. (-रं) A proper or good reply.<BR> E. सत्, and उत्तर answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृक्ष|सदृक्षः
सदृक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Like, similar.<BR>	 2. Conformable, fit, proper.<BR>	 3.<BR>Worthy, becoming.<BR> E. स for सम् same, दृश् to see, क्स aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृश्
सदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Like, similar.<BR> E. स for सम same, दृश् to see, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृश|सदृशः
सदृश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं)<BR>	 1. Like, resembling, similar.<BR>	 2. Fit, proper,<BR>right.<BR> E. स for सम the same, दृश् to see, aff. ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृशता
सदृशता f. (-ता) Likeness, sameness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, सदृशत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदेश|सदेशः
सदेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. Of the same country or<BR>place.<BR>	 3. Having a country.<BR> E. स for समान the same, देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्गति|सद्गतिः
सद्गति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Felicity or fortune.<BR>	 2. Good conduct.<BR> E. सत्, गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्गुण|सद्गुणः
सद्गुण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Good, pure, virtuous.<BR>	 2. Excellent, eminent.<BR>E. सत्, गुण quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्धेतु|सद्धेतुः
सद्धेतु m. (-तुः) (In logic,) The co-existence of cause and effect.<BR> E. सत् being, हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्भाव|सद्भावः
सद्भाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A pure or holy disposition or nature.<BR>	 2. A good<BR>temper.<BR>	 3. Amiability, kindly feeling.<BR>	 4. The quality or nature of<BR>being, entity.<BR>	 5. The property of goodness.<BR> E. सत्, and भाव quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्भूत|सद्भूतः
सद्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) True.<BR> E. सत् true, and भूत been.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्मन्
सद्मन् n. (-द्म)<BR>	 1. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. An altar.<BR>	 4. A<BR>temple.<BR> E. षद् to go, aff. मनिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्मचिति
सद्मचिति f. (-तिः) A number of houses.<BR> E. सद्म, and चिति an assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःकृत|सद्यःकृतं
सद्यःकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done promptly or quickly.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A name, an<BR>appellation.<BR> E. सद्यस् instantly, कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःशीथा
सद्यःशीथा f. (-था) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. सद्यस् instantly,<BR>शोथा a swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्
सद्यस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Instantly, momentarily, at the moment, in an instant.<BR>2. To day.<BR> E. स for सम् the same, and द्यस् for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्क|सद्यस्कः
सद्यस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) New, recent.<BR> E. सद्यस् in the moment, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्काल
सद्यस्काल m. (-लः) Present time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्युवती
सद्युवती f. (-ती) A virtuous maiden.<BR> E. सत्, and युवती a young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्योजात|सद्योजातः
सद्योजात m. (-तः) A calf.<BR> E. सद्यस् in a moment, and जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्योभाविन्
सद्योभाविन् m. (-वी) A calf.<BR> E. सद्यस् in a moment, भाविन् being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्रु
सद्रु mfn. (-द्रुः-द्रुः-द्रु)<BR>	 1. Resting, staying.<BR>	 2. Going.<BR> E. सद् to go or sit, रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वंश
सद्वंश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Of high birth, of a good race.<BR> E. सत्, वंश a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वसथ|सद्वसथः
सद्वसथ m. (-थः) A village.<BR> E. सत् good, वस् to abide, अथच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वृत्त|सद्वृत्तं
सद्वृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Amiable, well-behaved.<BR>	 2. Moral, virtuous.<BR>	 3.<BR>Well-rounded, handsomely orbicular.<BR>	 n. (-त्तं) Amiableness, good<BR>or amiable disposition.<BR> E. सत good, and वृत्त selected, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधन
सधन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Wealthy, rich.<BR> E. स with, धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्म्मन्|सधर्मन्
सधर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Like, equal, resembling.<BR>	 2. Of the same<BR>sect or caste, performing like duties.<BR>	 3. Of the same or similar<BR>properties.<BR> E. स for समान same, धर्म्म merit, practice, and अनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्म्मचारिणी|सधर्मचारिणी
सधर्म्मचारिणी f. (-णी) A wife, one married with religious rites.<BR> E. स with,<BR>(her husband,) धर्म्म duty, चारिणी who proceeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्म्मिन्|सधर्मिन्
सधर्म्मिन् mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि) Observing the same customs or laws.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-र्म्मिणी) A wife wedded according to the ritual of the Vedas.<BR> E. स<BR>same or with, धर्म्म virtue or duty, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधवा
सधवा f. (-वा) Wife, whose husband is living.<BR> E. स for सह with, धव a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधि|सधिः
सधि m. (-धिः) A name of AGNI or fire.<BR> E. स with, धा to have, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधिस्
सधिस् m. (-धिः) An ox, a bull.<BR> E. षह् to bear, Uṇadi aff. इसि, and ह<BR>changed to ध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्र्यञ्च्|सध्र्यंच्
सध्र्यञ्च् mfn. (-ध्राङ्-ध्रीची-ध्राक्) Accompanying, going with, a companion.<BR>f. (-ध्रीची) A woman's female friend, a confidante.<BR> E. सध्रि substi-<BR>tuted for सह with, अञ्च् to go, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन|सनः
सन mf. (-नः-नी) The flapping of an elephant's ears.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A plant,<BR>commonly Ghantāpārali.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी)<BR>	 1. GAURĪ.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR> E. षन् to give, or serve, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनक|सनकः
सनक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. One of the companions of VIṢṆU, or four sons of<BR>BRAHMĀ, inhabiting the Janaloka.<BR>	 2. Name of an inspired<BR>legislator.<BR> E. षन् to serve, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्
सनत् m. (-नत्) BRAHMĀ. Ind. Always, perpetually.<BR> E. सन् to serve or give, aff. अति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्कुमार|सनत्कुमारः
सनत्कुमार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. One of the four sons of BRAHMĀ, and eldest of<BR>the progenitors of mankind.<BR>	 2. One of the twelve emperors of<BR>India according to the Jainas.<BR> E. सनत् always, कुमार a youth: i. e.<BR>continent; retaining the purity of that age, or being devoid of<BR>human passion; otherwise, सनत् BRAHMĀ, and कुसार son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनन्द|सनन्दः
सनन्द m. (-न्दः) One of the four sons of BRAHMĀ, inhabiting the<BR>Janaloka.<BR> E. स with, नन्द pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनपर्णी
सनपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Marsilea quadrifolia.)<BR> E. सन the Asana or<BR>pentaptera, पर्ण a leaf; more usually असनपर्णी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनस्
सनस् n. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Excrement, ordure.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA'S trident.<BR>	 3. Crystal. E.<BR>षन् to give, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनसूत्र|सनसूत्रं
सनसूत्र n. (-त्रं) Packthread, or a net made of it. E. See शणसूत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सना
सना Ind. Always, eternally, perpetually.<BR> E. षन् to serve, आच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनातन|सनातनः
सनातन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Eternal, continual, perpetual.<BR>	 2. Firm, fixed,<BR>permanent.<BR>	 3. Primeval.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. BRAHMĀ.<BR>4. A guest of the Manes, or one who is to be fed whenever he<BR>chooses to attend the obsequial ceremonies or Śhrāddhas.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>1. The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 3. SARASVATĪ.<BR>E. सना always, and द्यु or द्युत् aff.; or सदा ठ्युल् तुट् च नि० दस्य नः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनात्र्
सनात्र् Ind. Always, perpetually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाथ
सनाथ f. (-था) A woman whose husband is living.<BR> E. स for सह with, नाथ husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभि|सनाभिः
सनाभि mfn. (-भिः-भिः-भि)<BR>	 1. Like, resembling.<BR>	 2. Affectionate.<BR>	 m. (-भिः)<BR>1. A kinsman, one of the same family name: it is considered also<BR>the same as the Sapiṇḍa or gentile, a relation as far as the<BR>seventh degree, and qualified to offer the funeral cake.<BR>	 2. A<BR>uterine brother.<BR> E. स with or same, नाभि navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभ्य|सनाभ्यः
सनाभ्य m. (-भ्यः) A relation as far as the seventh degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनामक|सनामकः
सनामक m. (-कः) The Morunga tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनि|सनिः
सनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Service, worship.<BR>	 2. Giving, donation.<BR>	 mf. (-निः-नी)<BR>Request, solicitation, respectful solicitation as addressed to a<BR>spiritual preceptor, &c.<BR>	 2. Quarter, region, point of the compass.<BR>E. षन् to honour, to give, इनि Unādi aff. ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्ठीव|सनिष्ठीवं
सनिष्ठीव n. (-वं) Sputtered speech, utterance interrupted by saliva. E.<BR>स for सह with, निर् before ष्ठीव् to eject saliva, घञ् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्ठेव|सनिष्ठेवं
सनिष्ठेव n. (-वं) Speech uttered with emission of saliva or sputtered. E.<BR>स with, नि before ष्ठीव् to spit, aff. घञ्; also सनिष्ठीव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनीड|सनीडः
सनीड mfn. (-डः-डा-डं) Near, proximate.<BR> E. स for समान same, नीड nest or abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनुतर
सनुतर Ind. Concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त|संत|संतः|सन्तः
सन्त m. (-न्तः) The hands opened and joined.<BR> E. सन बा० त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तक्षण|संतक्षणं
सन्तक्षण n. (-णं) Sarcastic language, scoff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तत|संतत|सन्ततं
सन्तत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Eternal, continual.<BR>	 2. Spread, extended.<BR>	 3.<BR>Continuous.<BR>	 4. Much, many.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-तं) Eternally.<BR> E. सम् before<BR>तन् to spread, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ततम्
सन्ततम् It is used as an indeclinable in the sense of “constinually,” “constantly,” &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तताभ्यास|संतताभ्यास|सन्तताभ्यासः
सन्तताभ्यास m. (-सः) The regular study and perusal of the Vedas.<BR> E. सन्तत<BR>constant, continual, अभ्यास exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तति|संतति|संततिः|सन्ततिः
सन्तति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Race, lineage.<BR>	 2. A son, a daughter, offspring,<BR>progeny.<BR>	 3. Descent, succession.<BR>	 4. A continuous line, a row, a<BR>range.<BR>	 5. Extent, expanse, spreading, stretching.<BR>	 6. Heap, multi-<BR>tude.<BR> E. सम् with, equally, तन् to spread, aff. क्तिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तपन|संतपन|संतपनं
सन्तपन n. (-नं) Inflaming, torturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तप्त|संतप्त|सन्तप्तः
सन्तप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Suffering pain or distress, distressed, afflicted,<BR>wretched.<BR>	 2. Suffering from extreme heat.<BR>	 3. Burnt, scorched.<BR>	 4.<BR>Inflamed with passion, &c.<BR> E. सम् before तप् to heat, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तमस्|संतमस्
सन्तमस् n. (-मः) Great or universal darkness.<BR> E. सम् completely, तमस्<BR>gloom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तमस|संतमस|सन्तमसं
सन्तमस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Darkened, clouded.<BR> E. सम्, and तमस् darkness, अच् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तर्ज्जन|सन्तर्जन|संतर्जन|संतर्जनं
सन्तर्ज्जन n. (-नं) Abusing, reproving, scolding.<BR> E. सम् before तर्ज्ज् to<BR>abuse, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तर्ज्जित|सन्तर्जित|संतर्जित
सन्तर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Abused, scolded, reproved.<BR> E. सम् before तर्ज्ज् to abuse, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तर्पण|संतर्पण|संतर्पणं|सन्तर्पणं
सन्तर्पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Satisfying, satiating, gratifying.<BR>	 2. Anything giving<BR>delight.<BR> E. सम् before तृप् to be satisfied, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तर्पित|संतर्पित
सन्तर्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Satisfied, satiated.<BR> E. सम् before तृप् to be satis-<BR>fied, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तान|संतान|संतानं|संतानः|सन्तानः
सन्तान m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Family, race, lineage.<BR>	 2. Offspring, progeny, a son<BR>or daughter.<BR>	 3. One of the five trees of heaven.<BR>	 4. Spreading,<BR>expansion.<BR>	 5. Continuous line.<BR> E. सम् before तन् to spread, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तानक|संतानक|संतानकः
सन्तानक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) What spreads, scatters, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) One of<BR>the five trees of heaven.<BR>	 f. (-निका)<BR>	 1. Cream, the coagulum of<BR>milk, &c.<BR>	 2. A cobweb.<BR>	 3. The blade of a knife or sword.<BR>	 4.<BR>Froth, foam.<BR> E. सम् before तन् to spread, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तानसन्धि|संतानसंधि|संतानसंधिः
सन्तानसन्धि f. (-न्धिः) Peace cemented by family alliance.<BR> E. सन्तान, सन्धि peace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ताप|संताप|संतापः|सन्तापः
सन्ताप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Heat, burning heat.<BR>	 2. Affliction, pain, distress.<BR>	 3.<BR>Passion.<BR>	 4. Repentance.<BR>	 5. Penance.<BR> E. सम्, तप् to heat, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तापन|संतापन|संतापनः|सन्तापनः
सन्तापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Burning, scorching.<BR>	 2. Paining, affliction.<BR>	 3. Exciting<BR>passion.<BR>	 m. (-नः) One of the arrows of KĀMADEVA or love.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before तप् to heat, causal form, युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तापहर|संतापहर
सन्तापहर mfn. (-रः-रा or री-रं)<BR>	 1. Cooling.<BR>	 2. Consolatory, consoling. E.<BR>सन्ताप, and हर what removes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तापित|संतापित|सन्तापितः
सन्तापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pained, distressed, afflicted.<BR>	 2. Suffering<BR>from heat.<BR>	 3. Inflamed with passion.<BR> E. सम् before तप् to burn,<BR>causal v., aff. क्त, and इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ताप्य|संताप्य
सन्ताप्य Ind. Having caused to be heated.<BR> E. सम्, तप् to be hot, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ति|संति|संतिः|सन्तिः
सन्ति f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. End, destruction.<BR>	 2. Gift, giving.<BR> E. षण् to give, क्तिच्<BR>aff.; also सति and साति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तुष्ट|संतुष्ट|सन्तुष्टः
सन्तुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Delighted, pleased.<BR> E. सम् intensitive prefix, तुष्ठ pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तोष|संतोष|संतोषः|सन्तोषः
सन्तोष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Joy, pleasure, delight, satisfaction, happiness.<BR>	 2.<BR>Thumb and fore-finger.<BR> E. सम् intensitive prefix, तुष् to be pleased,<BR>aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तोषण|संतोषण|संतोषणं
सन्तोषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Pleasing, propitiating.<BR>	 2. Comforting.<BR> E. सम् before<BR>तुष् to be pleased, causal. v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तोषित|संतोषित
सन्तोषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Consoled, comforted.<BR>	 2. Gratified.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before तुष् to be pleased, causal, v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तोष्ठव्य
सन्तोष्ठव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be pleased, comforted, gratified, &c. E.<BR>सम्, तुष् to be pleased, causal v., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्तोष्य|संतोष्य
सन्तोष्य Ind. Having pleased or gratified.<BR> E. सम् before तुष् to be pleased, causal v., ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्यक्त|संत्यक्त
सन्त्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Left, abandoned.<BR> E. सम्, and व्यज् to leave, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्यजन|संत्यजन|संत्यजनं
सन्त्यजन n. (-नं) Leaving, abandoning.<BR> E. सम्, त्यज् to leave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्रस्त|संत्रस्त
सन्त्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Frightened, alarmed.<BR> E. सम्, त्रस् to fear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्त्रास|संत्रास|संत्रासः
सन्त्रास m. (-सः) Fear, alarm.<BR> E. सम् before, त्रस् to fear, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दंश|संदंश|संदंशः|सन्दंशः
सन्दंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A pair of tongs or nippers.<BR>	 2. The great compress-<BR>ion of the teeth in the pronunciation of vowels.<BR> E. सम् with, दंश<BR>biting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दंशक|संदंशक|संदंशकः
सन्दंशक n. (-कं) A pair of tongs.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A pair of nippers, or small<BR>shears or tongs.<BR>	 2. A vice.<BR> E. सम् before दंश् to bite or nip, aff.<BR>क्वुन्, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दधान
सन्दधान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Having, possessing.<BR>	 2. Being at peace with,<BR>making peace.<BR>	 3. Fixing or placing in or on.<BR> E. सम् before धा to<BR>have, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्भ|संदर्भ|संदर्भः|सन्दर्भः
सन्दर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. Weaving garlands, collecting flowers into a wreath<BR>or chaplet, &c.<BR>	 2. Stringing, collecting, arranging.<BR>	 3. Uniting,<BR>mixture.<BR>	 4. Regular connection.<BR>	 5. Composition.<BR>	 6. Construction.<BR>E. सम् with, together, दृभि to collect, aff. अच्; or सम् + दृभ्-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्शन|संदर्शन|संदर्शनं|सन्दर्शनं
सन्दर्शन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Looking, seeing.<BR>	 2. Shewing.<BR>	 3. Appearance.<BR>	 4.<BR>Meeting.<BR>	 5. Regard, consideration.<BR> E. सम् completely, दर्शन seeing;<BR>or सम् before दृश् to see, causal. v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्शयत्
सन्दर्शयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Shewing, pointing out.<BR> E. सम् before दृश्<BR>to see, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दर्शित|संदर्शित
सन्दर्शित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Shewn, pointed out.<BR> E. सम् before दृश् to see, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दान|संदान|संदानं|सन्दानं|संदानः|सन्दानः
सन्दान n. (-नं) A rope, a cord, (for tying cattle especially.)<BR>	 m. (-नः) The<BR>elephant's temples, or part whence the ichorous fluid issues when<BR>the animal is in rut.<BR> E. सम् before दो to cut, aff. ल्युट्; or सम्<BR>with, दान the temporal juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दानित|संदानित|सन्दानितः
सन्दानित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bound, tied.<BR> E. सन्दान a rope, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दानिनी|संदानिनी
सन्दानिनी f. (-नी) A cow-house.<BR> E. सन्दान a rope for tying cattle, इनि and<BR>ङीप् affs; also सन्धानिनी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दामितक|संदामितक
सन्दामितक n. (-कं) A poem of three stanzas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दाव|संदाव|संदावः|सन्दावः
सन्दाव m. (-वः) Flight, retreat.<BR> E. सम् before दु to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्ध|संदिग्ध|सन्दिग्धः
सन्दिग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Doubted, questioned, doubtful.<BR>	 2. Enter-<BR>taining doubt, uncertain.<BR>	 3. Obscure, (as a passage.)<BR>	 4. Danger-<BR>ous, unsafe.<BR>	 5. Covered.<BR> E. सम् before दिह् to augment, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्धनिश्चय|संदिग्धनिश्चय
सन्दिग्धनिश्चय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Confident in a doubtful matter.<BR> E. सन्दिग्ध,<BR>and निश्चय certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्धमति|संदिग्धमति|सन्दिग्धमतिः
सन्दिग्धमति m. (-तिः) A sceptic, one who is uncertain or doubtful of the<BR>results of religious observances, &c.<BR> E. सन्दिग्ध doubted, doubting,<BR>मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्धलेख्य|संदिग्धलेख्य
सन्दिग्धलेख्य n. (-ख्यं) A writing or document of doubtful meaning or<BR>authority.<BR> E. सन्दिग्ध, and लेख्य a writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिग्धार्थ|संदिग्धार्थ|संदिग्धार्थः|सन्दिग्धार्थः
सन्दिग्धार्थ m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. A disputed debt, either in its amount or exis-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">Page757-a+ 60</a>]<BR>tence.<BR>	 2. Doubtful interpretation or meaning.<BR> E. सन्दिग्ध doubted,<BR>अर्थ property or meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दित|संदित|सन्दितः
सन्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bound, tied.<BR> E. सम् before दो to cut, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिदर्शयिषु|संदिदर्शयिषु
सन्दिदर्शयिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing to show.<BR> E. सम् before दृश् to see,<BR>causal form, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिशत्
सन्दिशत् mfn. (-शन्-शन्ती-शत्) Informing, telling.<BR> E. सम् before दिश् to show, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिष्ट|संदिष्ट|सन्दिष्टं|संदिष्टः
सन्दिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Told, communicated, related as news or<BR>information.<BR>	 2. Promised, agreed, engaged.<BR>	 3. Pointed out, assign-<BR>ed.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) News, tidings, information.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः) A messenger, a<BR>herald.<BR> E. सम् with, दिश् to show, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिष्टार्थ|संदिष्टार्थ|सन्दिष्टार्थः
सन्दिष्टार्थ m. (-र्थः) A herald, pursuivant, a royal messenger who com-<BR>municates oral instructions or orders.<BR> E. सन्दिष्ट communicated,<BR>अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिहान|सन्दिहानः
सन्दिहान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dubious, uncertain.<BR> E. सम् before दिह् to collect, aff. शानच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दिह्यमान
सन्दिह्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Doubtful, uncertain, obscure.<BR> E. सम् before<BR>दिह् to collect, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दी|संदी
सन्दी f. (-न्दी) A small bed or couch.<BR> E. सम् before दो to cut, aff. ड, and ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीपन|संदीपनः
सन्दीपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Inflaming, kindling.<BR>	 2. Exciting.<BR>	 m. (-नः) One of the<BR>five arrows of KĀMADEVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीप्त|संदीप्त
सन्दीप्त f. (-प्ता)<BR>	 1. Kindled, inflamed.<BR>	 2. Excited, instigated, encouraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दीप्य|संदीप्य|सन्दीप्यः
सन्दीप्य m. (-प्यः) A plant, (Celosia cristata.)<BR> E. सम + दीप्-स ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दूषण|संदूषणं
सन्दूषण n. (-णं) Corrupting, vitiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृष्ट|संदृष्ट
सन्दृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Seen, beheld.<BR>	 2. Foreseen, anticipated. E.<BR>सम् before दृश् to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दृश्यमान
सन्दृश्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being seen or looked at.<BR>	 2. Being fore-<BR>seen.<BR> E. सम् before दृश् to see, pass. v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देश|संदेश|संदेशः|सन्देशः
सन्देश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. News, tidings, information.<BR>	 2. Commission, com-<BR>mand.<BR> E. सम् together, दिश् to show, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देशवाच्|संदेशवाच्
सन्देशवाच् mf. (-वाक्) Communication of intelligence.<BR> E. सन्देश news, वाच् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देशहर|संदेशहर|संदेशहरः|सन्देशहरः
सन्देशहर m. (-रः) A messenger, an envoy, an ambassador.<BR> E. सन्देश tid-<BR>ings, हर who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देशहारक|संदेशहारक|संदेशहारकः|सन्देशहारकः
सन्देशहारक m. (-कः) A messenger, an envoy, an ambassador.<BR> E. सन्देश news, हारक who conveys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देशार्थ|संदेशार्थः
सन्देशार्थ m. (-र्थः) The subject of a message or communication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देह|संदेह|संदेहः|सन्देहः
सन्देह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>	 2. Risk, danger.<BR>	 3. Rhetorical<BR>doubt proceeding from the close resemblance of two objects.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before दिह् to collect, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्देहदोला
सन्देहदोला f. (-ला) The swing of uncertainty, a dilemma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्दोह|संदोह|संदोहः|सन्दोहः
सन्दोह m. (-हः) Assemblage, multitude, quantity.<BR>	 2. Milking.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, दुह् to fill, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्द्राव|संद्राव|संद्रावः|सन्द्रावः
सन्द्राव m. (-वः) Flight, retreat.<BR> E. सम् with, द्रु to go, to run, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध|संध
सन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>	 1. Possessing as an integrant part, intimately<BR>blended with.<BR>	 2. Holding, possessing, having placed in or on.<BR>	 3.<BR>Joined, united.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. Promise, assent, agreement.<BR>	 2. State,<BR>condition, the steady continuance in any state, steadiness, fixa-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Intimate union or association, identification.<BR>	 4. Twilight.<BR>5. Stipulation.<BR>	 6. Limit, boundary.<BR>	 7. Steadiness.<BR>	 8. Distillation.<BR>E. सम् together, धा to have or hold, aff. क, or अङ् and टाप्<BR>fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धातव्य|संधातव्य
सन्धातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be united or allied with, to be reconcil-<BR>ed, to be connected, &c.<BR> E. सम् before धा to have, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धान|संधान|संधानं|सन्धानं
सन्धान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Holding together, uniting, joining.<BR>	 2. Tying, binding.<BR>3. Fixing, (as an arrow.)<BR>	 4. Peace, alliance.<BR>	 5. Association, com-<BR>pany.<BR>	 6. Supporting, reception, receiving, sustaining.<BR>	 7. Mixing,<BR>joining, intimate union or combination.<BR>	 8. A relish, something eaten<BR>to excite thirst.<BR>	 9. Sourrice-gruel.<BR>	 10. Pickles, &c., acid preparation<BR>of the Bel and other fruits.<BR>	 11. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 12. Contracting<BR>the skin, &c. by astringent applications.<BR>	 13. A joint.<BR>	 nf.<BR>(-नं-नी) Distillation, distilling, the manufacture of spirituous<BR>liquors.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A braziery, a foundery, a place where the base<BR>metals are stored or wrought.<BR> E. सम् together, धा to hold, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानकरण|संधानकरण
सन्धानकरण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Who or what heals, re-unites, allies, con-<BR>necting, re-uniting, &c.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Uniting, combining.<BR>	 2. Heal-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Allying, making peace.<BR> E. सन्धान, and करण making, the act<BR>or instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानकर्त्तृ|सन्धानकर्तृ
सन्धानकर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-त्त्री-र्त्तृ) Uniting, connecting, healing, &c.<BR> E. सन्धान, कर्त्तृ what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानित|संधानित|सन्धानितः
सन्धानित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Bound, tied.<BR>	 2. Strung together.<BR> E. सन्धान<BR>holding together, aff. इतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धानिनी|संधानिनी
सन्धानिनी f. (-नी) A cow-house.<BR> E. सन्धान a binding, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धारण|संधारण|संधारणं
सन्धारण n. (-णं) Holding, observing, practising.<BR> E. सम् before धृ to hold,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धार्य्य|सन्धार्य|संधार्य
सन्धार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be observed or followed.<BR> E. सम् before धृ to hold, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धि|संधि|संधिः|सन्धिः
सन्धि m. (-न्धिः)<BR>	 1. Union, junction, connection, combination.<BR>	 2. Peace,<BR>making peace, pacification.<BR>	 3. A hole, a chasm.<BR>	 4. A hole made in<BR>a wall or underneath it to enter a building for hostile or felonious<BR>purposes, a breach, a mine, &c.<BR>	 5. Breaking, dividing.<BR>	 6. The vulva.<BR>7. A division of a drama, apparently applicable to each subject<BR>represented or sentiment excited, as considered severally and<BR>detached from the rest, though contributing to the connection of<BR>the whole; contrast of incident, change of situation, transition<BR>of passion or emotion, &c.<BR>	 8. An interval, a pause or rest.<BR>	 9. A<BR>joint, an articulation of the body.<BR>	 10. The union of letters, either<BR>at the end and beginning of different words, or in the middle of<BR>compound terms, to avoid dissonance or hiatus.<BR>	 11. A period at<BR>the expiration of each Yuga or age, or one-sixth of its duration,<BR>intervening before the commencement of the next; a Sandhi,<BR>also, of the same length as the Satya-Yuga, occurs at the end of<BR>each Manwantara and each Kalpa.<BR>	 12. Critical juncture, opportune<BR>moment.<BR>	 13. (In mensuration,) The connecting link of a per-<BR>pendicular.<BR> E. सम together, धा to have or hold, aff. कि of either<BR>the act, condition or instrument; whence the word becomes<BR>applicable to a chasm, &c., as to an interval, which whilst it<BR>divides, also connects, two parts or places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिका|संधिका
सन्धिका f. (-का) Distillation.<BR> E. सम् together, धा to have, aff. क, and कन्<BR>added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिचौर|संधिचौर|सन्धिचौरः
सन्धिचौर m. (-रः) A housebreaker.<BR> E. सन्धि a breach, चौर a thief. “सिंँधेल” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिजीवक|संधिजीवक|संधिजीवकः|सन्धिजीवकः
सन्धिजीवक m. (-कः) One who seeks for wealth by dishonest means, espe-<BR>cially as a go-between.<BR> E. सन्धि union, (of others,) जीवक who<BR>lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धित|संधित|सन्धितः
सन्धित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Tied, bound, strung, fastened together.<BR>	 2. Alli-<BR>ed, united, reconciled.<BR>	 3. Pickled.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Pickles and preparations<BR>of various fruits.<BR>	 2. Spirituous liquor.<BR> E. सन्धा union, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धित्सु|संधित्सु
सन्धित्सु mfn. (-त्सुः-त्सुः-त्सु) Wishing to be at peace or in alliance with.<BR>E. सम् before धा to have, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिदूषण
सन्धिदूषण n. (-णं) The violation of a treaty or alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिनी|संधिनी
सन्धिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A cow with calf, or one which has taken the bull.<BR>2. One who is milked unseasonably.<BR> E. सन्धा joining, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिबन्ध|संधिबन्ध|सन्धिबन्धः
सन्धिबन्ध m. (-न्धः) A flower, (Kæmpferia rotunda.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिबन्धन|संधिबन्धन|संधिबंधन|सन्धिबन्धनं
सन्धिबन्धन n. (-नं) A tendon, a nerve, a ligament.<BR> E. सन्धि a joint, बन्धन binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिरन्ध्रका|संधिरन्ध्रका
सन्धिरन्ध्रका f. (-का) A hole or breach in a wall.<BR> E. सन्धि a breach, रन्ध्र a<BR>hole, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिला|संधिला
सन्धिला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A river.<BR>	 2. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 3. A hole in a wall, a<BR>breach.<BR>	 4. A chasm, a pit, a mine.<BR> E. सन्धि a hole, &c., लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिविग्रहाधिकार|संधिविग्रहाधिकार
सन्धिविग्रहाधिकार m. (-रः) War ministry, charge of peace and war. E.<BR>सन्धि, विग्रह war, अधिकार office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिविग्रहाधिकारिन्|संधिविग्रहाधिकारिन्
सन्धिविग्रहाधिकारिन् m. (-री) Chief political minister.<BR> E. इनि added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिविचक्षण|संधिविचक्षण|संधिविचक्षणः
सन्धिविचक्षण m. (-णः) An able negociator.<BR> E. सन्धि and विचक्षण skilled;<BR>also similar compounds, as सन्धिकुशल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिविद्|संधिविद्
सन्धिविद् m. (-वित्) A negociator, a minister.<BR> E. सन्धि, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिवेला|संधिवेला
सन्धिवेला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A particular period, and one which connects the part<BR>of the day or fortnight, as morning, noon, and evening, new moon,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">Page758-a+ 60</a>]<BR>the first or thirteenth day of the fortnight and full moon.<BR>	 2. Twi-<BR>light.<BR> E. सन्धि union, वेला time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धिहारक|संधिहारक|संधिहारकः|सन्धिहारकः
सन्धिहारक m. (-कः) A housebreaker.<BR> E. सन्धि a breach, हारक who carries away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धुक्षण|संधुक्षणं
सन्धुक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Kindling, inflaming.<BR>	 2. Exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धुक्षित|संधुक्षित
सन्धुक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Lighted, inflamed, kindled.<BR>	 2. Excited.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before धुक्ष् to kindle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्धेय|संधेय
सन्धेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be joined, united, &c.<BR>	 2. To be reconciled<BR>or at peace with.<BR>	 3. To be allied, connected, &c., what or who<BR>may or ought to be allied, &c.<BR> E. सम् before धा to have, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्या|संध्या
सन्ध्या f. (-न्ध्या)<BR>	 1. Twilight, either morning or evening.<BR>	 2. The period<BR>that elapses between the expiration of one Yuga or age, and the<BR>commencement of another.<BR>	 3. A period of time, forenoon, after<BR>moon or mid-day.<BR>	 4. Religious abstraction, meditation, repetition<BR>of Mantras, sipping water, &c., to be performed by the three first<BR>classes of Hindus, at stated periods in the course of every<BR>day, especially at sunrise, sunset, and at noon.<BR>	 5. Reflection.<BR>6. Promise, assent.<BR>	 7. Boundary, limit.<BR>	 8. Joining, union.<BR>	 9.<BR>A flower; according to some the tuberose, to others, the<BR>jasmine.<BR>	 10. Twilight, personified as the daughter of BRAHMĀ,<BR>and wife of ŚIVA.<BR>	 11. The name of a river.<BR> E. सन्धि a joint,<BR>(of the day,) and यत् aff.; or सम् + ध्यै-अङ् सन्धौ भवः यत् वा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यांश|संध्यांश|संध्यांशः|सन्ध्यांशः
सन्ध्यांश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Twilight.<BR>	 2. The period at the end of each Yuga. E.<BR>सन्ध्या as above, and अंश portion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यांशु|संध्यांशु|संध्यांशुः
सन्ध्यांशु m. (-शुः) Twilight.<BR> E. सन्ध्या, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याकाल|संध्याकाल|संध्याकालः
सन्ध्याकाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Twilight.<BR>	 2. The intervals of a Yuga.<BR> E. सन्ध्या, काल<BR>time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याचल|संध्याचल|सन्ध्याचलः
सन्ध्याचल m. (-लः) The name of a mountain.<BR> E. सन्ध्या twilight, अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यात्रय|संध्यात्रय
सन्ध्यात्रय n. (-यं) The three periods of the day.<BR> E. सन्ध्या, and त्रय triad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यानाटिन्|संध्यानाटिन्
सन्ध्यानाटिन् m. (-टी) ŚIVA.<BR> E. सन्ध्या evening twilight, नाटिन् who dances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याबल|संध्याबल|संध्याबलः|सन्ध्याबलः
सन्ध्याबल m. (-लः) An imp, a Rākshasa.<BR> E. सन्ध्या evening, बल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याबलि|संध्याबलि|संध्याबलिः|सन्ध्याबलिः
सन्ध्याबलि m. (-लिः) Any image of NANDĪ, the bull of ŚIVA, either of<BR>clay, wood, or stone, placed in a temple of the deity.<BR> E. सन्ध्या even-<BR>ing, (when ŚIVA is worshipped,) बलि an offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याभ्र|संध्याभ्र|सन्ध्याभ्रं
सन्ध्याभ्र n. (-भ्रं)<BR>	 1. A sort of red chalk.<BR>	 2. An evening cloud.<BR> E. सन्ध्या twilight, अभ्र talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याराग|संध्याराग|सन्ध्यारागं|संध्यारागः
सन्ध्याराग n. (-गं) Red-lead.<BR> E. सन्ध्या twilight, and राग the colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्याराम|संध्याराम|संध्यारामः|सन्ध्यारामः
सन्ध्याराम m. (-मः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. सन्ध्या the daughter of the deity, of whom<BR>he become enamoured, and आङ् before रम् to sport, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्ध्यासमय|संध्यासमय|संध्यासमयः
सन्ध्यासमय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Evening twilight.<BR>	 2. The period after each Yuga.<BR>E. सन्ध्या, and समय time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न|सन्नः
सन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Shrunk, diminished.<BR>	 2. Lost, gone.<BR>	 3. Still,<BR>motionless.<BR>	 4. Dispirited.<BR>	 5. Adjacent.<BR>	 6. Sunk down.<BR>	 n. (-न्नं) A<BR>little, a small quantity.<BR>	 m. (-न्नः) The Piyāla tree.<BR> E. षद् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नक|सन्नकः
सन्नक m. (-कः) A tree, commonly Piyāla: see सन्नकद्रु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नकण्ठ
सन्नकण्ठ mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं) Choking, choked, scarcely able to articulate.<BR>E. सन्न gone, कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नकद्रु|सन्नकद्रुः
सन्नकद्रु m. (-द्रुः) A tree, commonly Piyāla, (Buchanania latifolia, Rox.)<BR>E. सन्नक said to mean here, sharp, hot, and द्रु a tree; also सन्नक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नत|संनत
सन्नत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bent, bowed down.<BR> E. सम्, and नत bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नति|संनति|संनतिः|सन्नतिः
सन्नति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Reverence, obeisance, reverential salutation.<BR>	 2.<BR>Humiliating.<BR>	 3. Sound.<BR> E. सम् before नम् to bow, and क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नद्ध|संनद्ध|सन्नद्धः
सन्नद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Armed, mailed, accoutred.<BR>	 2. Arranged, array-<BR>ed, prepared for battle.<BR>	 3. Bound, girdled on.<BR>	 4. Harnessed.<BR>	 5.<BR>Prevalent.<BR>	 6. Murderous, felonious, provided with arms for the<BR>destruction of others.<BR>	 7. Wearing amulets, provided with charms,<BR>&c.<BR>	 8. Near, at hand.<BR> E. सम् before नह् to bind, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नय|संनय|संनयः|सन्नयः
सन्नय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Multitude, number, quantity.<BR>	 2. Rear, rearguard. E.<BR>सम् together, नी to get or guide, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नहर्ष
सन्नहर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं) Destitute of joy, distressed.<BR> E. सन्न gone, हर्ष joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नहन|संनहनं
सन्नहन n. (-नं) Arming, equipping.<BR>	 2. Industry, exertion.<BR>	 3. Binding<BR>tightly.<BR> E. सम् + नह्-ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नाह|संनाह|संनाहः|सन्नाहः
सन्नाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Armour, mail, either of iron or thick quilted cotton.<BR>2. Arming for battle.<BR> E. सम् before नह् to bind, aff. घञ् । “संँजोया ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नाह्य|संनाह्य|संनाह्यः|सन्नाह्यः
सन्नाह्य m. (-ह्यः) A war-elephant.<BR> E. सन्नाह armour, यत् aff. of fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकर्ष|संनिकर्ष|संनिकर्षः|सन्निकर्षः
सन्निकर्ष mf. (-र्षः-र्षा)<BR>	 1. Proximity, nearness.<BR>	 2. Bring or drawing near.<BR>3. Connection, relation.<BR>	 4. Connection of an organ of sense with<BR>its object, (in Nyāya philosophy.)<BR> E. सम् together, नि before कृष् to<BR>attract, aff. अच्, fem. aff. टाप्, or घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकर्षण|संनिकर्षण|संनिकर्षणं|सन्निकर्षणं
सन्निकर्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Proximity.<BR>	 2. Approximation, approximating,<BR>bringing or approaching near to.<BR> E. सम् and नि before कृष् to make<BR>furrows, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निकृष्ट|संनिकृष्ट|सन्निकृष्टः
सन्निकृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Near, proximate.<BR>	 n. (-ष्टं) Vicinity.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>नि prefixed to कृष् to make furrows, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निक्षार|संनिक्षार
सन्निक्षार m. (-रः) The Piyāl tree, (Buchanania latifolia.)<BR> E. सम् and नि<BR>before क्षर् to ooze, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निचय|संनिचय|संनिचयः
सन्निचय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Collected.<BR> E. सम् with, निचय heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निध|संनिध|सन्निधं
सन्निध n. (-धं) Proximity.<BR> E. सम् and नि before धा to have, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधातृ|संनिधातृ
सन्निधातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Receiving, keeping in deposit or near to,<BR>who or what places near to, &c.<BR>	 2. A receiver of stolen goods.<BR>	 3.<BR>An officer who introduces people at court.<BR> E. सम् and नि before धा<BR>to have, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधान|संनिधान|संनिधानं|सन्निधानं
सन्निधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Proximity.<BR>	 2. Appearance, perceptibility.<BR>	 3. Placing,<BR>depositing.<BR>	 4. Receiving, taking charge of.<BR>	 5. A receptacle.<BR>	 6.<BR>Placing down together.<BR> E. सम् and नि before धा to have ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधाय
सन्निधाय Ind. Having placed or placed near at hand.<BR> E. सम्, नि before<BR>धा to have, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निधि|संनिधि|संनिधिः|सन्निधिः
सन्निधि f. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Proximity, approximation.<BR>	 2. Perceptibility,<BR>presence, appearance, becoming or being visible or perceptible.<BR>3. Placing.<BR>	 4. Receiving.<BR>	 5. A receptacle.<BR> E. सम् and नि before धा<BR>to have, and कि aff.; also सन्निध and सन्निधान ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपतित|संनिपतित|सन्निपतितः
सन्निपतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Assembled, collected.<BR>	 2. Mixed, blended.<BR>3. Alighted, descended.<BR>	 4. Come, arrived.<BR> E. सम् and नि before पत्<BR>to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपात|संनिपात|संनिपातः|सन्निपातः
सन्निपात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Collection, assemblage, multitude.<BR>	 2. Union,<BR>junction, contact.<BR>	 3. Mixture, miscellaneous collection.<BR>	 4. Morbid<BR>state of the three humours of the body producing fever and<BR>dangerous illness.<BR>	 5. Alighting, descending, falling down.<BR>	 6.<BR>Arrival.<BR>	 7. A kind of musical tune or measure.<BR> E. सम् and नि<BR>before पत् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निपातक|संनिपातक|संनिपातकः
सन्निपातक m. (-कः) Dangerous illness.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबद्ध|संनिबद्ध|सन्निबद्धः
सन्निबद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Bound firmly, fast tied or fettered.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>नि intensitives, बद्ध bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबन्ध|संनिबन्ध|सन्निबंध|संनिबंधः|संनिबन्धः
सन्निबन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Binding, tying.<BR>	 2. Connection, consequence.<BR>	 3.<BR>Effectiveness.<BR> E. सम् completely, or सत् good, निबन्ध fastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निबन्धन|संनिबन्धन|सन्निबन्धनं
सन्निबन्धन n. (-नं) Binding or tying fast.<BR> E. सम् नि intens., वन्धन tying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निभ|संनिभ|सन्निभः
सन्निभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Like, similar.<BR> E. सम्, and निभ like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निमग्न|संनिमग्न
सन्निमग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं)<BR>	 1. Immersed, plunged in.<BR>	 2. Asleep, sleeping.<BR>E. सम्, and निमग्न immersed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निमित्त|संनिमित्त
सन्निमित्त n. (-त्तं) For a good cause, for the sake of the good.<BR> E. सत्, निमित्त cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियुक्त|संनियुक्त
सन्नियुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Appointed, employed.<BR>	 2. Attached to, con-<BR>nected with.<BR> E. सम् and नि before युज् to join, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नियोग|संनियोग|संनियोगः
सन्नियोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Attachment or application to, connection or union<BR>with.<BR>	 2. Deputation, appointment.<BR> E. सम् and नि before युज् to join,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निरुद्ध|संनिरुद्ध
सन्निरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Stopped, obstructed, checked.<BR> E. सम् and नि be-<BR>fore रुध् to oppose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निरोध|संनिरोध|संनिरोधः
सन्निरोध m. (-धः) Hindrance, check, obstruction, suppression.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>नि before रुध् to hinder, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निविष्ट|संनिविष्ट|सन्निविष्टः
सन्निविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Near, present, at hand.<BR>	 2. Entered into.<BR>	 3.<BR>Collected, assembled.<BR>	 4. Neighbouring.<BR> E. सम् and नि before विश् to<BR>enter, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवृत्त|संनिवृत्त
सन्निवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Ceasing, forbearing.<BR>	 2. Stopped, ceased.<BR>	 3.<BR>Returned, coming back.<BR> E. सम् and नि before वृत् to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवृत्ति|संनिवृत्ति|संनिवृत्तिः|सन्निवृत्तिः
सन्निवृत्ति f. (-त्त्रिः)<BR>	 1. Restraint, forbearance, avoiding, forsaking.<BR>	 2. Re-<BR>turning, coming back.<BR> E. सम्, and निवृत्ति desisting, stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निवेश|संनिवेश|संनिवेशः|सन्निवेशः
सन्निवेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. An open space, either in a town or its vicinity<BR>where the people take exercise or diversion.<BR>	 2. Vicinity,<BR>proximity, neighbourhood.<BR>	 3. Fabrication, manufacture, construc-<BR>tion, preparation.<BR>	 4. Putting in, causing to enter.<BR>	 5. Union, junc-<BR>tion.<BR>	 6. Assemblage, collection.<BR>	 7. Situation, position, posture.<BR>	 8.<BR>The collective form or figure of an asterism.<BR> E. सम् and नि before<BR>विश् to enter, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निषण्ण|संनिषण्ण
सन्निषण्ण mfn. (-ण्णः-ण्णा-ण्णं) Stationary, seated, halted.<BR> E. सम् and नि before षद् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निहित|संनिहित|सन्निहितं
सन्निहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate, at hand, present.<BR>	 2. Stay-<BR>ing, being.<BR>	 3. Deposited, fixed, laid up.<BR>	 4. Ready, prepared.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, निहित placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्निहितापाय|संनिहितापाय
सन्निहितापाय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Transient, brief. Adj. Fleeting, liable to<BR>destruction, transitory.<BR> E. सन्निहित, and अपाय loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मान|सन्मानः
सन्मान n. (-नं) Respect for the good.<BR> E. सत्, and मान respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मार्ग
सन्मार्ग m. (-र्गः) Good or virtuous conduct.<BR> E. सत्, and मार्ग a way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यसन|संन्यसन|संन्यसनं
सन्न्यसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Abandonment of the world.<BR>	 2. Entrusting to.<BR> E. सम्<BR>and नि before अस् to throw, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यस्त|संन्यस्त|सन्न्यस्तः
सन्न्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Abandoned, deserted.<BR>	 2. Entrusted or deli-<BR>vered to.<BR>	 3. Laid down.<BR> E. सम् and नि before अस् to throw, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यस्य
सन्न्यस्य Ind.<BR>	 1. Having left or abandoned.<BR>	 2. Having consigned or deli-<BR>vered to.<BR> E. सम् and नि before अस् to throw, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यास|संन्यास|संन्यासः|सन्न्यासः
सन्न्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Abandonment of all worldly affections and possess-<BR>ions.<BR>	 2. Abandonment in general.<BR>	 3. Deposit, trust, or relinquish-<BR>ment to.<BR>	 4. Sudden death.<BR>	 5. A stake in game.<BR>	 6. Indian spike-<BR>nard.<BR> E. सम् and नि before अस् to throw, to cast off, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न्यासिन्|संन्यासिन्
सन्न्यासिन् m. (-सी)<BR>	 1. The Brāhman of the fourth order, the religious<BR>mendicant.<BR>	 2. An ascetic, a devotee.<BR>	 3. One who lays down or<BR>deposits.<BR> E. सन्न्यास abandonment of the world, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपक्ष|सपक्षः
सपक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Winged.<BR>	 2. Having a side or party.<BR>	 3. Like,<BR>similar.<BR>	 4. Containing the major term or subject.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>partisan, a follower, an adherent, one of the same side or party.<BR>2. An instance of the same side.<BR> E. स for समान same, पक्ष party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्न|सपत्नः
सपत्न m. (-त्नः) An enemy, an adversary.<BR>	 f. (-त्नी) A woman whose<BR>husband has other wives.<BR> E. स for समान the same, पति a husband,<BR>ङीष् aff. and नुक् augment; अच् added for the masc. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्नारि|सपत्नारिः
सपत्नारि m. (-रिः) A sort of bamboo, (Bambusa spinosa.) “वेडवांँश ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्नीक
सपत्नीक f. (-का) Accompanied with a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्रकृत
सपत्रकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Distressed, afflicted.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A wounded deer<BR>or other animal.<BR> E. स for सह with, पत्र the leaf, the barb of the<BR>arrow, and कृत made; also सपत्राकृत, &c., being metaphorically<BR>applied to distress or pain in general: see the next:<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्राकरण|सपत्त्राकरणं|सपत्राकरणं
सपत्राकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Wounding so that the feathered part of the arrow<BR>enters the body.<BR>	 2. Excessive pain: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्राकृति|सपत्त्राकृतिः|सपत्राकृतिः
सपत्राकृति f. (-तिः) Agony, affliction, excessive pain or distress: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपदि
सपदि Ind.<BR>	 1. Instantly, in a moment, at the moment.<BR>	 2. Quickly,<BR>swiftly.<BR> E. सह् before पद् to go, इन् aff. and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्य्या|सपर्या
सपर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) Worship, reverence.<BR> E. सपर Kandwādi root, said to<BR>imply worship, यक् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपाद|सपादः
सपाद f. (-दा) Having a fourth part, increased by one-fourth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिण्ड|सपिंड|सपिंडः|सपिण्डः
सपिण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A kinsman, especially one connected by the offering<BR>of the funeral cake to either or all of the manes of the father,<BR>grandfather, and great-grandfather, and their wives respectively,<BR>as sprung from them in directly collateral lines; the relationship<BR>stops with every fourth person, as the fifth cannot perform the offer-<BR>ing of a cake to the father even of the deceased. The following are<BR>enumerated as Sapiṇḍās:--the son, son's son, and son's grandson;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">Page759-b+ 60</a>]<BR>widow, daughter and daughter's son; the father, the mother, the<BR>brother, brother's son, and brother's grandson; father's daughter's<BR>son; father's brother's son and grandson; paternal grandfather's<BR>daughter's son; paternal grandfather; paternal grandmother,<BR>paternal grandfather's brother, brother's son and grandson; and<BR>lastly the great grandfather's daughter's son: these all<BR>present oblations in which the deceased is either included,<BR>or may participate: other enumerations, including the oblations<BR>he was bound to offer, &c. extend the connection of Sapiṇḍa to<BR>seven persons both in an ascending or descending line.<BR> E. स for<BR>ससान common, and पिण्ड ball of meat, &c., offered to the manes<BR>of the deceased ancestors, at the Śrāddhas performed in honour<BR>of them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिण्डीकरण|सपिंडीकरणं|सपिण्डीकरणं
सपिण्डीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Offering food to the deceased relatives called<BR>Sapiṇḍas: to be performed at the end of a full year after the<BR>death of a relative; but can be performed on the twelfth day<BR>after death by Brāhmins only, on some special occasions.<BR>	 2.<BR>Investing a person with the rights of relationship, indicated by<BR>offering the funeral cake.<BR> E. सपिण्ड, करण making, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिण्डीकृत
सपिण्डीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Comprehended in the relationship of<BR>Sapiṇḍa or offering of a common cake.<BR> E. सपिण्ड, कृत made,<BR>च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपीति|सपीतिः
सपीति f. (-तिः) Drinking together.<BR> E. स for सह with, पा to drink, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तक|सप्तकः
सप्तक mfn. (-कः-का or की-कं)<BR>	 1. Seven.<BR>	 2. Seventh.<BR>	 3. Containing seven.<BR>n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A collection of seven stanzas of the Rig Vedas.<BR>	 2. A<BR>collection of any seven things.<BR>	 f. (-की) A woman's girdle.<BR> E. सप्तन्<BR>seven, (string, &c.) and कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तजिह्व|सप्तजिह्वः
सप्तजिह्व m. (-ह्वः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. सप्त seven, जिह्वा a tongue or flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तज्वाल|सप्तज्वालः
सप्तज्वाल m. (-लः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. सप्त seven, ज्वाला flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ततन्तु|सप्ततन्तुः
सप्ततन्तु m. (-न्तुः) A sacrifice, an offering or oblation.<BR> E. सप्त seven,<BR>(prayers, or the tongues of AGNI,) तन् to spread, aff. तुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तति|सप्ततिः
सप्तति f. Sing. (-तिः) Seventy. Du. (-तौ) Two seventies. Plu. (-तयः)<BR>Many seventies.<BR> E. सप्तन् seven, डति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तातितम
सप्तातितम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) The seventieth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तदश|सप्तदशः
सप्तदश mfn. (-शः-शी-शं) Seventeenth.<BR> E. सप्त seven, दशन् ten, aff. डट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तदशन्
सप्तदशन् mfn. Plu. (-शं) Seventeen.<BR> E. सप्तन् seven and दशन् ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तदीधिति|सप्तदीधितिः
सप्तदीधिति m. (-तिः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. सप्त seven, दीधिति a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तद्वीपा
सप्तद्वीपा (-पा) An epithet of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तधा
सप्तधा Plu. In seven ways.<BR> E. सप्तन् seven, धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तधातु
सप्तधातु m. (-तुः) The seven parts of the body, or chyle, blood, flesh,<BR>adeps, marrow, bone, and semen.<BR> E. सप्त seven, and धातु element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तन्
सप्तन् mfn. Plural only, (सप्त) Seven.<BR> E. षप् to be collected, Unādi aff.<BR>कनिन् and तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तनाडीचक्र|सप्तनाडीचक्रं
सप्तनाडीचक्र n. (-क्रं) An astrological diagram supposed to foretell rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तपदी
सप्तपदी f. (-दी) The ceremony of walking together round the nuptial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तपर्ण|सप्तपर्णं|सप्तपर्णः
सप्तपर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Seven-leaved.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) A tree, (Alstonia<BR>scholaris.)<BR>	 n. (-र्णं) A sort of sweetmeat, made of the expressed<BR>juice of the grape, pomegranate and date, with sugar, spices,<BR>honey, and Ghee.<BR> E. सप्त seven, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तपुत्त्रसू
सप्तपुत्त्रसू f. (-सूः) The mother of seven children.<BR> E. सप्त seven, पुत्त्र a child, सू mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तप्रकृति|सप्तप्रकृतिः
सप्तप्रकृति Plu. (-तयः) The seven constituent parts of a kingdom, or<BR>prince, ministers, fortress, territory, treasure, force, and ally or<BR>friend.<BR> E. सप्त, and प्रकृति constituent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तभद्र|सप्तभद्रः
सप्तभद्र m. (-द्रः) The Sirisha tree, (Acacia Sirisa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तभूमिक
सप्तभूमिक Adj. Seven stories high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तम|सप्तमः
सप्तम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Seventh.<BR>	 f. (-मी)<BR>	 1. The seventh day of a lunar<BR>fortnight.<BR>	 2. The locative case, (in gram.)<BR> E. सप्तन् seven, डतम् aff.;<BR>or सप्तानां पूरणः मट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तरक्त|सप्तरक्तं|सप्तरक्तः
सप्तरक्त m. Plu. (-क्ताः) The seven external parts of the body of a red<BR>colour, or the palms of the hands, the soles of the feet, the cor-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">Page760-a+ 60</a>]<BR>ners of the eyes, the tongue, the palate, the lips and nails.<BR> E. सप्त<BR>seven, and रक्त red or blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तरात्र
सप्तरात्र n. (-त्रं) A period of seven nights.<BR> E. सप्त, रात्र for रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तर्षि
सप्तर्षि m. Plu. (-र्षयः)<BR>	 1. The constellation Ursa Major, the seven stars of<BR>which are the seven great saints, viz:--MARĪCI, ATRI, ANGIRAS,<BR>PULASTYA, PULAHA, KRATU, and VAAISHṬHA.<BR>	 2. The seven sages<BR>themselves.<BR> E. सप्त seven, and ऋषि a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तला
सप्तला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Double jasmine, (J. zambac fl. multiplicatis.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>plant, commonly Charmakasā.<BR>	 3. Trumpet flower, (Bignonia<BR>suave-olens.)<BR>	 4. A shrub, (Abrus precatorius.)<BR> E. सप्त seven, (leaves,<BR>&c.) ला to get or have, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तशती
सप्तशती f. (-ती) An aggregate of seven hundred verses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तसप्ति|सप्तसप्तिः
सप्तसप्ति m. (-प्तिः) The sun.<BR> E. सप्त seven, सप्ति a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तहस्त
सप्तहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Of seven cubits.<BR>	 2. Having seven hands, &c.<BR>E. सप्त, हस्त a hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तांशुपुङ्गव|सप्तांशुपुंगव|सप्तांशुपुङ्गवः
सप्तांशुपुङ्गव m. (-वः) The planet SATURN.<BR> E. सप्त seven, अंशु a ray of light,<BR>पुङ्गव eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ताङ्ग
सप्ताङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Having seven members or parts.<BR> E. सप्त, अङ्ग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तार्च्चिस्|सप्तार्चिस्
सप्तार्च्चिस् mfn. (-र्च्चिः) Evil-eyed, fierce eyed.<BR>	 m. (-र्च्चिः)<BR>	 1. AGNI or fire.<BR>2. The planet SATURN.<BR> E. सप्त seven, and अर्च्चिस् a flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ताश्व|सप्ताश्वः
सप्ताश्व m. (-श्वः) The sun.<BR> E. सप्त seven, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तास्र
सप्तास्र n. (-स्रं) A heptagon.<BR> E. सप्त, and अस्र an angle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ताह|सप्ताहः
सप्ताह n. (-हं) A week.<BR> E. सप्त and अह for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ति|सप्तिः
सप्ति m. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. A yoke.<BR> E. षप् to be collected, (in a troop,) ति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफर|सफरः
सफर mf. (-रः-री) A small glistening fish, commonly Punthi, a sort of<BR>carp, (Cyphores-ophore, HAM:) see शफर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफल|सफलं
सफल mfn. (-लः-ला or ली-लं) Productive, fruitful, bearing fruit, yielding<BR>a profit, &c.<BR> E. स for सह with, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबधूक
सबधूक m. (-कः) A man with his wife.<BR> E. स with, बधू a wife, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबन्धु|सबंधु|सबन्धुः
सबन्धु m. (-न्धुः) A Kinsman, a relation. Adj. Possessed of a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबलि|सबलिः
सबलि m. (-लिः) Evening twilight.<BR> E. स for सह with, बलि offering of<BR>food to evil spirits; the proper hour for such ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबाध|सबाधः
सबाध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>	 1. Painful, hurtful.<BR>	 2. Oppressive, extortionary.<BR>E. स with, बाधा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सब्रह्मचर्य्य|सब्रह्मचर्य|सब्रह्मचर्यं
सब्रह्मचर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Studying together, being disciples of one teacher.<BR>E. स with, ब्रह्मचर्य्य studentship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सब्रह्मचारिन्
सब्रह्मचारिन् m. (-री) A fellow student, one engaged in the same studies<BR>and observing the same austerities.<BR> E. स for सह with and ब्रह्मचारिन्<BR>the religious student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभय
सभय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fearing, fearful.<BR> E. स with, भय fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभर्त्तृका|सभर्तृका
सभर्त्तृका f. (-का) A woman whose husband is alive.<BR> E. स with, भर्त्तृ a<BR>husband, कन् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभा
सभा f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. An assembly. a meeting.<BR>	 3. A Court of<BR>Justice.<BR>	 4. A gambling-house.<BR>	 5. A much frequented place.<BR> E. स<BR>for सह together, भा to shine, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाज्
सभाज् r. 10th cl. (सभाजयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To serve, to gratify by service.<BR>	 2. To<BR>please or satisfy.<BR>	 3. To show.<BR>	 4. To beautify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाजन|सभाजनं
सभाजन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Courtesy, politeness, civility in receiving or taking<BR>leave of a friend.<BR>	 2. Thanks.<BR>	 3. Congratulation.<BR> E. सभाज् to please<BR>or gratify, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाजित
सभाजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Treated with courtesy, gratified, pleased.<BR> E. सभाज् to please, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभापति|सभापतिः
सभापति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The keeper of a gaming-house.<BR>	 2. The president of<BR>an assembly.<BR> E. सभा an assembly, (of gamblers, &c.) पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभावशकर
सभावशकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Influencing or fascinating an assembly.<BR>E. सभा, वशकर what subdues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभासद्
सभासद् m. (-सत् or सद्) One of a company, an assistant at an assembly<BR>or meeting; (in law, an assessor.)<BR> E. सभा an assembly, सद् who<BR>goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभास्तार|सभास्तारः
सभास्तार m. (-रः) An assistant at an assembly, one of a company. E.<BR>सभा an assembly, स्तृ to cover, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभिक|सभिकः
सभिक m. (-कः) The keeper of a gaming-house.<BR> E. सभा an assembly, ठन्<BR>aff; also with the penultimate vowel made long, सभीक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभीक|सभीकः
सभीक m. (-कः) The keeper of a gaming-house: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभोचित|सभोचितः
सभोचित m. (-तः) A Paṇḍit, a learned Brāhman or teacher.<BR> E. सभा an<BR>assembly, and उचित fit, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्य|सभ्यः
सभ्य mfn. (-भ्यः-भ्या-भ्यं)<BR>	 1. Trusted, confidential, faithful.<BR>	 2. Relating to<BR>an assembly, fit for or suitable to it.<BR>	 3. Polite.<BR>	 4. Civilized.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-भ्यः)<BR>	 1. An assistant at an assembly.<BR>	 2. An assessor.<BR>	 3. A person<BR>of honourable parentage.<BR>	 4. The keeper of a gambling-house.<BR>	 5.<BR>A servant of the keeper of a gaming-house.<BR> E. सभा an assembly,<BR>&c., यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्यतम
सभ्यतम m. (-मः) A distinguished person, one who is an ornament of<BR>society.<BR> E. सभ्य, and तमप् affix of superlative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्यता
सभ्यता f. (-ता) Politeness, refinement in manners.<BR> E. सभ्य, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्
सम् Ind. A particle and prefix implying:--1. Union, junction, (with,<BR>together.)<BR>	 2. Assemblage, collection.<BR>	 3. Beauty or perfection.<BR>	 4.<BR>Intensity. As a prefix it corresponds to con, co, com, &c. Before a<BR>consonant the final of this word is changed to Anuswara, and is<BR>written सं.<BR> E. सो-वा० कमु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम|समः
सम mfn. Pron. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. All, whole, entire. (Adj.)<BR>	 1. Like, similar.<BR>2. Good, virtuous.<BR>	 3. Full, complete.<BR>	 4. Same, even, equal.<BR>	 5. In-<BR>different, impartial.<BR>	 6. Mean.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A year.<BR>	 2. Even,<BR>plain, level.<BR>	 3. Same.<BR>	 4. Equal.<BR>	 5. Convenient.<BR>	 6. Straight.<BR>	 7.<BR>Indifferent, impartial, fair.<BR>	 8. Common.<BR>	 9. Like, similar.<BR>	 10. Free<BR>from emotion.<BR>	 11. Good, virtuous.<BR>	 12. Honest, just.<BR>	 13. Full,<BR>complete, &c.: see समा: n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. A figure of rhetoric, identity or<BR>sameness of objects compared to one another.<BR>	 2. (In geometry), A<BR>mean; a fourth proportional to the two perpendiculars and the<BR>link or segment.<BR> E. सम् to be confused or unconfused, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समकन्या
समकन्या f. (-न्या) A girl fit to be married.<BR> E. सम complete, कन्या a virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समकर्ण|समकर्णः
समकर्ण mn. (-र्णः-र्णं) An equidiagonal tetragon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समकाल|समकालः
समकाल n. (-लं) The same time, the same moment.<BR> E. सम and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समकालीन
समकालीन Adj. Contemporary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समकोल|समकोलः
समकोल n. (-लं) A snake, a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्न|समक्नः
समक्न mfn. (-क्नः-क्ना-क्नं) Going or moving equally, kept equal or<BR>together.<BR> E. सम् together, अञ्च् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्षम्
समक्षम् Ind. Before, in presence or sight of, visible.<BR> E. सम् with, अक्षि<BR>the eye, aff. टच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्षेत्र
समक्षेत्र n. (-त्रं) An epithet of a particular division of the Nakshatras, in astronomy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समखात|समखातः
समखात m. (-तः) An oblong excavation, thence also a parallelopipedon,<BR>(in geometry.)<BR> E. सम equal, खात dug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समगन्धक|समगन्धकः
समगन्धक m. (-कः) Compounded perfume.<BR> E. सम same, even, गन्ध smell, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समग्र|समग्रः
समग्र mfn. (-ग्रः-ग्रा-ग्रं) All, entire, whole, full, complete.<BR> E. सम the<BR>whole, ग्रह् to take, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समङ्गा|समंगा
समङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>	 1. Bengal madder, (Rubia manjith.)<BR>	 2. A sort of fern,<BR>(Lycopodium imbricatum.)<BR>	 3. A sort of sensitive plant.<BR> E. सम् to-<BR>gether, अगि to go or grow, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समचतुरस्र
समचतुरस्र mn. (-स्रः-स्रं) An equilateral tetragon. Adj. Equally quadrangular, square.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समचतुर्भुज|समचतुर्भुजः
समचतुर्भुज mn. (-जः-जं) A rhombus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समचित्त|समचित्तं
समचित्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Indifferent, unattached.<BR>	 2. Equable, even-<BR>tempered.<BR> E. सम, and चित्त the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समचितत्व
समचितत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Indifference.<BR>	 2. Equanimity.<BR> E. त्व added to the<BR>last; also with तल्, समचित्तता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज|समजं|समजः
समज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A multitude of beasts or birds.<BR>	 2. A number of block-<BR>heads.<BR>	 n. (-जं) A forest, a wood.<BR> E. सम alike, जन् to be born, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज्ञा
समज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) Fame, reputation.<BR> E. सम all, ज्ञा to know, क and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज्या
समज्या f. (-ज्या)<BR>	 1. An assembly, a meeting.<BR>	 2. Fame, celebrity.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, अज् to go, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समञ्जस|समंजस|समञ्जसं|समञ्जसः
समञ्जस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Proper, right, fit.<BR>	 2. Exercised, experienced.<BR>3. Correct, accurate, true.<BR>	 4. Virtuous, good.<BR>	 n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Propriety,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">Page761-a+ 60</a>]<BR>fitness.<BR>	 2. Correct evidence.<BR> E. सम् with, together with, अञ्जसा truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समण्ठ|समण्ठः
समण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) A potherb, a sort of cucumber. “गण्डीरे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समता
समता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Sameness, similarity, equality.<BR>	 2. Equanimity.<BR>	 3. Right<BR>decision.<BR>	 4. Perfectness.<BR> E. सम equal, like, तल् aff.: also समत्व n. (-त्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रम|समतिक्रमः
समतिक्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Deviating from, transgressing.<BR>	 2. Going over or<BR>beyond.<BR> E. सम् and अति before क्रम् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रान्त
समतिक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Surpassed, exceeded.<BR>	 2. Gone over or<BR>beyond.<BR>	 3. Transgressed.<BR> E. सम्, and अति before क्रम् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिरिक्त|समतिरिक्तं
समतिरिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Much, exceeding, abundant.<BR> E. सम् with,<BR>and अतिरिक्त much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतीत
समतीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Past, gone.<BR> E. सम्, and अतीत past.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्रिभुज|समत्रिभुजः
समत्रिभुज m. (-जः) An equilateral triangle.<BR> E. सम, and त्रिभुज triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्विष्
समत्विष् mfn. (-तिट्) Equally bright or lovely.<BR> E. सम, and त्विष् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्सर
समत्सर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Envious, jealous.<BR> E. स with, मत्सर envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समदर्शिन्
समदर्शिन् m. (-र्शी) Impartial, equally viewing both sides.<BR> E. सम, and<BR>दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समदुःख
समदुःख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Sympathizing, feeling for another's woe.<BR> E. सम् and दुःख pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिक|समधिकः
समधिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Exceeding, abundant, plentiful.<BR> E. सम् intensi-<BR>tive, and अधिक more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिगमन|समधिगमनं
समधिगमन n. (-नं) Surpassing, overcoming.<BR> E. सम्, and अधि before गम् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधृत
समधृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Equal or equivalent to.<BR> E. सम, and धृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समध्व
समध्व mfn. (-ध्वः-ध्वा-ध्वं) Travelling in company.<BR> E. सम् same, अध्वन् a<BR>road, the final dropped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससनुज्ञात
ससनुज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Assented or agreed to, permitted, allowed. E.<BR>सम् and अनु before ज्ञा to know, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञान|समनुज्ञानं
समनुज्ञान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Permitted, allowed.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Assent, concurr-<BR>ence, permission.<BR> E. सम् and अनु before ज्ञा to know, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुव्रत
समनुव्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Entirely devoted to.<BR> E. सम्, अनुव्रत devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्त|समंत|समन्तः
समन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) All, entire, universal.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः) Limit, term,<BR>boundary, end.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्ततस्
समन्ततस् Ind.<BR>	 1. All round, on every side.<BR>	 2. Wholly, altogether.<BR> E. सम्<BR>with, अन्त end, term, तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्तदुग्धा
समन्तदुग्धा f. (-ग्धा) The milk hedge-plant, (Euphorbia tirucalli, &c.) E.<BR>समन्त every way, दुग्ध milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्तपञ्चक|समंतपंचक|समन्तपञ्चकं
समन्तपञ्चक n. (-कं) Name of a holy place near Kurukshetra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्तभद्र|समंतभद्र|समन्तभद्रः
समन्तभद्र m. (-द्रः) A Jina or Buddha.<BR> E. समन्त every way, and भद्र<BR>auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्तभुज्|समंतभुज्
समन्तभुज् m. (-भुक्) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. समन्त universally, भुज् what eats or consumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्तात्
समन्तात् Ind. All around, on every side.<BR> E. समन्त in the fifth case,<BR>used as a particle, आति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्यु|समन्युः
समन्यु mfn. (-न्युः-न्युः-न्यु) Fierce, angry, enraged.<BR>	 m. (-न्युः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. स for<BR>सह with, मन्यु wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वय|समन्वयः
समन्वय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Connected consequence.<BR>	 2. Natural succession or<BR>order.<BR>	 3. Conjunction, copulation.<BR> E. सम्, and अन्वय order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वित|समन्वितः
समन्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Possessed of, endowed with, possessing, affected<BR>by, full of.<BR> E. सम् intensitive or conjunctive, अन्वित endowed with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समपाद|समपादं
समपाद n. (-दं) An attitude in shooting, standing with the feet even. E.<BR>सम even, पाद the foot; also read समपद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समबुद्धि
समबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Philosophical, stoical, looking on all things<BR>alike, calm, indifferent.<BR> E. सम, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभाव|समभावः
समभाव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Of like nature or property.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Equa-<BR>bility.<BR>	 2. Sameness.<BR> E. सम, and भाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिप्लुत
समभिप्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Overwhelmed.<BR> E. सम्, अभि before प्लु to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिव्याहार|समभिव्याहारः
समभिव्याहार m. (-रः) Mentioning together.<BR>	 2. Proximity or association<BR>with a word whose meaning is well understood.<BR>	 3. Company, asso-<BR>ciation.<BR> E. सम + अभि + वि + आ + ह-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिसरण|समभिसरणं
समभिसरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Seeking, wishing, endeavouring to gain.<BR>	 2.<BR>Approaching, going to or against.<BR> E. सम्, and अभि before सृ to go,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिहरण
समभिहरण n. (-णं) Taking, seizing.<BR> E. सम्, and अभि before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिहार|समभिहारः
समभिहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Repetition, reiteration.<BR>	 2. Excess, surplus.<BR> E. सम्<BR>with, अभि before हृ to take, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभूमि|समभूमिः
समभूमि f. (-मिः) Even ground.<BR> E. सम even, and भूमि ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभ्यर्च्चन|समभ्यर्चन|समभ्यर्चनं
समभ्यर्च्चन nf. (-नं-ना) Worshipping, reverencing.<BR> E. सम्, and अभि before<BR>अर्च्च् to worship, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभ्यर्च्चित|समभ्यर्चित
समभ्यर्च्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Honoured, worshipped.<BR> E. सम्, and अभि before<BR>अर्च्च् to respect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभ्याहार|समभ्याहारः
समभ्याहार m. (-रः) Association, accompaniment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समम्
समम् Ind. With, together with.<BR> E. षम् to be confused or unconfused,<BR>aff. अच्; or सम--अमु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सममण्डल|सममंडल
सममण्डल n. (-लं) The prime vertical line, (in astronomy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सममय
सममय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Of like origin, proceeding from the same cause,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सम same, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सममात्र
सममात्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं) Of the same size or measure.<BR> E. सम same, मात्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सममिति|सममितिः
सममिति f. (-तिः) Mean measure.<BR> E. सम, and मिति measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समय|समयः
समय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Time.<BR>	 2. Oath, affirmation by oath or ordeal.<BR>	 3.<BR>An established moral or ceremonial custom, rule, law.<BR>	 4. Demons-<BR>trated conclusion.<BR>	 5. Agreement, covenant, contract, bargain.<BR>	 6.<BR>Engagement, appointment.<BR>	 7. Order, precept, instruction.<BR>	 8. Sign,<BR>hint, indication.<BR>	 9. Religious obligation or observance.<BR>	 10. Leisure,<BR>interval, opportunity.<BR>	 11. Season, fit or proper time for anything.<BR>12. Speech, declaration.<BR>	 13. Limit, boundary.<BR>	 14. End of trouble<BR>or distress, (in dramatic action.)<BR>	 15. End, conclusion, termination.<BR>16. Convention.<BR>	 17. Poetical conventionality, (as the dance of pea-<BR>cocks on the appearance of clouds.)<BR>	 18. Success, prosperity.<BR>	 19.<BR>Condition, stipulation.<BR> E. स for सम with, मी to mete, to measure,<BR>aff. अच्; or सम alike, इण् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयकार|समयकारः
समयकार m. (-रः) Making an appointment or engagement, fixing a<BR>time.<BR> E. समय an agreement, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयपरिरक्षण
समयपरिरक्षण n. (-णं) Observance of an agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयभेद|समयभेदः
समयभेद m. (-दः) Breaking an agreement.<BR> E. समय, and भेद breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयव्यभिचार|समयव्यभिचारः
समयव्यभिचार m. (-रः) Violating or breaking an agreement.<BR> E. समय, and<BR>व्यभिचार improper conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समया
समया Ind.<BR>	 1. Near, (with an accusative.)<BR>	 2. Within, between, midst.<BR>3. At such a time, at a fixed or appointed time.<BR>	 4. Duly, season-<BR>ably, in due time or season.<BR> E. सम् alike, इण् to go, आ Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयाचार|समयाचारः
समयाचार m. (-रः) Conventional practice or usage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयाध्युषित
समयाध्युषित n. (-तं) Time at which neither the stars nor the sun is<BR>visible.<BR> E. समय time, अधि over, उषित abided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर|समरं|समरः
समर mn. (-रः-रं) War, battle, conflict.<BR> E. सम् with, together, ऋ to go, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरज्जु
समरज्जु f. (-ज्जुः) Mean string or so undings.<BR> E. सम, and रज्जु a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरभ|समरभः
समरभ m. (-भः) A particular mode of sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरमूर्द्धन्
समरमूर्द्धन् m. (-र्द्धा) The front or van of battle.<BR> E. समर, and मूर्द्धन् front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरूप्य|समरूप्यः
समरूप्य mfn. (-प्यः-प्या-प्यं) Of like or same source or origin.<BR> E. सम same,<BR>रूप्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्चन|समर्चनं|समर्च्चन
समर्चन n. (-नं) Worshipping, adoration.<BR> E. सम् before अर्च्च् to worship, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्च्चित|समर्चित
समर्च्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Worshipped, adored, honoured.<BR> E. सम् before<BR>अर्च्च् to worship, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्ण|समर्ण्ण
समर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Asked, solicited.<BR>	 2. Pained, wounded.<BR> E. सम्, अर्द्द् to ask, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थ|समर्थः
समर्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Strong, powerful.<BR>	 2. Connected in sense.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fit, proper, 4. Able, adequate to, capable.<BR>	 5. Allowed.<BR>	 m. (-र्थः)<BR>The coherence of words in a significant sentence.<BR> E. सम् with, अर्थ्<BR>to ask, aff. अच्, or अर्थ meaning, sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थक|समर्थकं
समर्थक n. (-कं) Aloe-wood, (Amyris agallocha.)<BR> E. समर्थ fit, (for perfume,) कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थता
समर्थता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Strength, power, prowess.<BR>	 2. Ability, capability,<BR>adequacy.<BR>	 3. Signification of terms.<BR> E. तल् aff. of the abstract,<BR>added to समर्थ; also समर्थत्व n. (-त्वं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थन|समर्थनं
समर्थन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Deliberation, deciding on the propriety or impropriety<BR>of anything; also समर्थना.<BR>	 2. Perseverance in an arduous under-<BR>taking, attempting difficulties or impossibilities.<BR>	 3. Reconciling<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">Page762-a+ 60</a>]<BR>differences, allaying a dispute.<BR>	 4. Objecting, objection.<BR>	 5. Potency,<BR>efficacy.<BR> E. सम् before अर्थ् to ask or request, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्द्धक
समर्द्धक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Granting a boon.<BR> E. सम् before ऋध् to augment, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्पण|समर्पणं|समर्प्पण
समर्पण n. (-णं) Delivering, consigning, presenting.<BR> E. सम्, अर्पण delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्पणीय|समर्प्पणीय
समर्पणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be delivered, presented, made over, &c. E.<BR>सम्, and अर्पणीय to be delivered; also समर्पयितव्य and समर्प्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्पित|समर्प्पित
समर्पित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Delivered, made over, consigned.<BR> E. सम्, and<BR>अर्पित delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्पितवत्|समर्प्पितवत्
समर्पितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Giving or making over, delivering.<BR> E. सम्,<BR>अर्पितवत् delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्य्याद|समर्याद|समर्यादः|समर्य्यादः
समर्य्याद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. Bounded, limited.<BR>	 3.<BR>Correct in conduct.<BR>	 4. Respectful.<BR> E. स for सह with, मर्य्यादा a limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समल|समलं
समल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Dirty, muddy, filthy, foul, impure.<BR>	 2. Sinful.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-लं) Fæces, ordure.<BR> E. स for सह with, मल dirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवकार|समवकारः
समवकार m. (-रः) A sort of dramatic entertainment.<BR> E. सम्, and अव<BR>before कृ to make, aff. घञ्; described, as that in which the chiefs<BR>are engaged in mutual conflict to contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवतार|समवतारः
समवतार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A descent into a river or sacred bathing place at a<BR>TIRTHA.<BR>	 2. A descent.<BR> E. सम् with, अव below, तृ to cross or pass<BR>over, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवनत
समवनत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bent, bowed.<BR> E. सम्, and अव before णम् to bow, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवर्ण|समवर्णः
समवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Of the same caste, colour, &c.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः) Com-<BR>munity of caste, &c.<BR> E. सम, and वर्ण caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवर्त्तिन्|समवर्तिन्
समवर्त्तिन् m. (-र्त्ती) YAMA, the ruler of Tartarus.<BR> E. सम् all, equal, वृत् to<BR>be or to select, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवश्यात
समवश्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone away, wasted, destroyed.<BR> E. सम्, and अव<BR>before श्यै to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवसर्ग्य
समवसर्ग्य mfn. (-र्ग्यः-र्ग्या-र्ग्यं) To be let go or let out.<BR> E. सम्, and अव before<BR>सृज् to loose, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्था
समवस्था f. (-स्था)<BR>	 1. State, condition.<BR>	 2. Similar state or condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाप्ति|समवाप्तिः
समवाप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Obtaining, getting.<BR> E. सम्, and अव before आप् to get,<BR>क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाय|समवायः
समवाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Multitude, assemblage, collection, aggregate, quan-<BR>tity.<BR>	 2. One of the categories or Padārthas of logic, intimate and<BR>constant relation, as of yarn and the cloth made of it.<BR>	 3. Connec-<BR>tion of species in a genus, or parts of a whole.<BR> E. सम् and अव before<BR>अय् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवायसम्बन्ध|समवायसंबन्धः
समवायसम्बन्ध m. (-न्धः) Inseparable relation, as of properties with subs-<BR>tances, material with manufacture, species with genus.<BR> E. समवाय,<BR>and सम्बन्ध connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवायिकारण
समवायिकारण n. (-णं) Inseparable cause or relation, as of material<BR>with produce, &c.<BR> E. समवायिन्, and कारण cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवायिन्
समवायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Multitudinous, aggregated.<BR>	 2. Connect-<BR>ed intimately.<BR>	 n. (-यि) Intimate and inseparable cause, as earth of<BR>pottery, thread of cloth, &c.<BR> E. समवाय, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवृत्ति|समवृत्तिः
समवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) Moderate, equable.<BR> E. सम and वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवेत|समवेतः
समवेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Mixed, mingled, blended.<BR>	 2. Collected, assem-<BR>bled.<BR>	 3. Connected with, related to, as properties with things.<BR>4. Comprised in one genus.<BR> E. सम् and अव before इण् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवेध|समवेधः
समवेध m. (-धः) Mean depth.<BR> E. सम and वेध perforation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समश्रुवान
समश्रुवान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Spreading over, pervading, extending through-<BR>out.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, अश् to pervade, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समष्टि|समष्टिः
समष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A collective aggregate, an aggregate which is viewed<BR>as constituted of parts of which each is consubstantially the same<BR>with the whole.<BR> E. सम + अश्-व्याप्तौ क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समष्ठिला
समष्ठिला f. (-ला) A sort of potherb, said to grow in watery places;<BR>according to some authorities, a kind of cucumber, to others a<BR>shrub, called commonly गांडरदूवी.<BR> E. सम् together, स्था to stay, इतच्<BR>aff., deriv. irr.; or सम with, अस्थि a bone, (a seed,) ला to get or<BR>have, aff. क; also समष्ठीला ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसन|समसनं
समसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Contracting, contraction.<BR>	 2. Combination, conjunction,<BR>formation of compound terms.<BR> E. सम् together, अस् to throw or<BR>direct, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसन्धि|समसंधि|समसंधिः
समसन्धि f. (-न्धिः) Alliance or peace on equal terms.<BR> E. सम, सन्धि union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसन्धित|समसंधित
समसन्धित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Allied on equal terms.<BR>	 2. Bound or connec-<BR>ted equally.<BR> E. सम, and सन्धित bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसुप्ति|समसुप्तिः
समसुप्ति f. (-प्तिः) The end of the Kalpa, and destruction of the<BR>universe.<BR> E. सम universal, सुप्ति sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्त|समस्तं
समस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. All, whole, entire, complete.<BR>	 2. Compound,<BR>compounded.<BR>	 3. Abridged, contracted.<BR>	 m. (-स्तः) A whole, the aggre-<BR>gate of all the parts.<BR> E. सम् together, अस् to throw or direct, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्थ|समस्थः
समस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Even, equal, level, uniform.<BR>	 2. Like, simi-<BR>lar.<BR> E. सम even, स्थ what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्थल
समस्थल nf. (-लं-ली) Level ground.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The Doab, the country<BR>between the Ganges and Jamunā rivers.<BR> E. सम level, स्थल soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्थलीकृत
समस्थलीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Levelled, made level, filled up, (as a marsh<BR>or river.)<BR> E. समस्थल and कृत made, च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्य
समस्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं)<BR>	 1. To be collected together.<BR>	 2. To be made<BR>entire or complete.<BR>	 f. (-स्या) Part of a stanza, proposed as a trial of<BR>skill to be completed.<BR> E. सम even or complete, क्यच् affix, and सुक्<BR>augment; or सम together, अस् to direct, क्यप् or ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्थार्था
समस्थार्था f. (-र्था) Part of a stanza to be completed as a trial of skill.<BR>E. समस्य to be completed, अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांश|समांशः
समांश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Entitled to an equal share.<BR>	 m. (-शः) An equal<BR>portion, a part.<BR> E. सम, अंश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांशहारिन्
समांशहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Sharing equally, a co-heir.<BR> E. समांश, हारिन्<BR>who takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांशिन्
समांशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) A co heir entitled to an equal share.<BR> E. सम<BR>same, अंश part or portion, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांसमीना
समांसमीना f. (-ना) A cow bearing a calf every year.<BR> E. समा year, in the<BR>second case, repeated, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समा
समा f. (-मा) Year; (according to AMARA'S lexicon this word is always<BR>used in the plural: PĀṆINI however, uses it in the singular.)<BR>Ind. With, together with.<BR> E. सम + अच्--टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकर्षिन्
समाकर्षिन् mfn. (-र्षी-र्षिणी-र्षि) Possessing a diffusive fragrance.<BR>	 m. (-र्षी)<BR>A scent spreading afar.<BR> E. सम, and आङ् before कृष् to draw, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकुल
समाकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Agitated, bewildered, confused.<BR>	 2. Crowded,<BR>thronged.<BR> E. सम्, and आङ् before कुल् to accumulate, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकुलत्व
समाकुलत्व n. (-त्वं) Agitation, anxiety.<BR> E. त्व added to the last; also<BR>with तल्, समाकुलता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्रान्त
समाक्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Pervaded, spread.<BR>	 2. Overcome, surpass-<BR>ed.<BR> E. सम, and आङ् before क्रम् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्या
समाख्या f. (-ख्या)<BR>	 1. Fame, reputation.<BR>	 2. Appellation.<BR> E. सम् all, आङ्<BR>before ख्या to tell or declare, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्यात
समाख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Famed, celebrated.<BR>	 2. Notorious, public.<BR>	 3.<BR>Reckoned up.<BR>	 4. Declared.<BR> E. सम्, and आङ् before ख्या to say, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागत|समागतः
समागत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Arrived, approached.<BR>	 2. Met, encountered.<BR>3. United, joined.<BR> E. सम् together, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागति|समागतिः
समागति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Arrival, approach.<BR>	 2. Union, joining.<BR>	 3. Encounter-<BR>ing, meeting.<BR>	 4. Similar condition or progress.<BR> E. सम् with, or सम्<BR>same, आङ् before गम् to go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागम|समागमः
समागम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Union, junction.<BR>	 2. Arrival, approach.<BR>	 3. Associa-<BR>tion, acquaintance, intercourse.<BR>	 4. Encountering, meeting.<BR>	 5. (In<BR>astronomy,) The occultation of a star.<BR> E. सम् with, आगम coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाघात|समाघातः
समाघात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Striking, beating, killing.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, आघात striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचर
समाचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who or what observes, practices, proceeds, &c.<BR>E. सम् and आङ् before चर् to go, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचरण|समाचरणं
समाचरण n. (-णं) Following, practising, observing, proceeding.<BR> E. सम्<BR>and आङ् before चर् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचरत्
समाचरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Following, practising, behaving, proceeding,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सम्, and आङ् before चर् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचार|समाचारः
समाचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Equal or like in virtuous conduct.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Proper practice or conduct.<BR>	 2. Proceeding, going.<BR>	 3. Information,<BR>tradition, news.<BR> E. सम्, and आङ् before चर् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाच्छन्न
समाच्छन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Covered with, involved in.<BR> E. सम्, आच्छन्न covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज|समाजः
समाज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A multitude, a number, (of anything except beasts.)<BR>2. An assembly, a meeting.<BR>	 3. A convivial meeting, a club.<BR>	 4. An<BR>elephant.<BR> E. सम् like, and अज् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाजिक|समाजिकः
समाजिक m. (-कः) A member of an assembly, a spectator: also सामाजिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज्ञा
समाज्ञा f. (-ज्ञा) Fame, reputation.<BR> E. सम् all, आङ् before ज्ञा to know,<BR>affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादर
समादर m. (-रः) Veneration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादान|समादानं
समादान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Receiving suitable donations.<BR>	 2. Taking.<BR>	 3. The daily<BR>observances of the Jaina sect.<BR> E. सम् with, आदान taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादाय
समादाय Ind.<BR>	 1. Having taken.<BR>	 2. Having accepted.<BR> E. सम्, and आङ्<BR>before दा to give, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादिष्ट
समादिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Enjoined, commanded.<BR> E. सम्, आदिष्ट enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादेय
समादेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Acceptable, to be selected or taken.<BR> E. सम्, and<BR>आङ् before दा to give, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादेश|समादेशः
समादेश m. (-शः) Advice, direction, command, order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधा
समाधा f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. The act of collecting or composing.<BR>	 2. Restraining<BR>the senses and fixing the mind in abstract contemplation on the<BR>true nature of spirit.<BR>	 3. Profound absorption.<BR>	 4. Contentment.<BR>	 5.<BR>Answering an objection, replying to the Purva Paksha, (in logic.)<BR>6. Agreeing, promising.<BR>	 7. A leading incident which unexpectedly<BR>gives rise to the whole plot; also समाधान.<BR> E. सम + आ + धा-अङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधान|समाधानं
समाधान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Religious meditation, restraining the mind from<BR>external objects, and fixing it in profound absorption.<BR>	 2. Promising,<BR>declaring.<BR>	 3. (In the drama,) The leading incident, that which<BR>gives rise sometimes unexpectedly to the whole plot.<BR> E. सम् in-<BR>tensitive, आङ् before धा to have or hold, aff. ल्युट्ः see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधाय
समाधाय Ind. Having fixed upon, (the mind,) being intent upon.<BR> E. सम्,<BR>and आङ् before धा to have, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधि|समाधिः
समाधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. Deep and devout meditation, restraining the senses<BR>and confining the mind to contemplation on the true nature of<BR>spirit, &c.<BR>	 2. A religious vow or obligation.<BR>	 3. Silence.<BR>	 4. Promise,<BR>assent, engagement.<BR>	 5. Composing or reconciling differences, put-<BR>ting a stop to a dispute.<BR>	 6. Requital, return, retaliation.<BR>	 7. At-<BR>tempting impossibilities; exertion or perseverance in extreme<BR>difficulties.<BR>	 8. Storing corn on account of a dearth.<BR>	 9. A Jaina<BR>saint of a future age.<BR>	 10. A figure of rhetoric; connection or<BR>proximity of two events accidentally connected, and expressed by<BR>a common verb and the government of the verb by a double<BR>nominative, as उत्कण्ठिता च कुलटा जगामास्तञ्च भानुमान् the disloyal<BR>woman went sorrowfully, and the sun (went) down.<BR>	 11. Collection,<BR>combination.<BR>	 12. Demonstrated conclusion.<BR>	 13. The joint of the<BR>neck.<BR>	 14. A tomb, a grave.<BR> E. सम् together, धा to have or hold,<BR>with आङ् prefix, and कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधिमत्|समाधिमन्त्
समाधिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Contemplative, engaged in meditation.<BR>2. Making a promise, announcing assent or permission.<BR> E. समाधि,<BR>and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधिस्थ|समाधिस्थः
समाधिस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Devoted to meditation.<BR> E. समाधि and स्थ<BR>who is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाध्मात
समाध्मात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Blown or puffed up, inflated.<BR> E. सम् and आङ्<BR>before ध्मा to blow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समान|समानं|समानः
समान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Like, similar.<BR>	 2. Good, virtuous.<BR>	 3. One,<BR>uniform, same.<BR>	 4. Honoured.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. One of the five vital airs,<BR>that which is considered essential to digestion and occupies the<BR>cavity of the navel.<BR>	 2. A corresponding letter of the alphabet, as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">Page763-b+ 60</a>]<BR>a long vowel to its short one, &c.<BR>	 3. A friend.<BR> E. सम all, अन् to<BR>breathe, aff. अण् or घञ्; or सम् and आङ् before णी to get, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानकालीन|समानकालीनः
समानकालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Occurring or produced at the same period.<BR>E. समान same, काल time, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानगोत्र
समानगोत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Of the same lineage or family: see सगोत्र.<BR> E. समान, गोत्र family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानजन्मन्
समानजन्मन् mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म) Of equal age.<BR> E. समान, and जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानजाति
समानजाति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Of a common tribe, sort, &c.<BR> E. समान, and<BR>जाति sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानजातीय
समानजातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of the same caste or species.<BR> E. समान, जातीय of a caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानता
समानता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Sameness, equality, likeness.<BR>	 2. Community of kind<BR>or quality.<BR> E. समान, and तल् aff.; also with त्व aff., समानत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानयत्
समानयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Making equal or like to.<BR>	 2. Leading,<BR>bringing.<BR> E. समान used as a verb, or सम् and आङ् before णी to<BR>get, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानयन|समानयनं
समानयन n. (-नं) Bringing, conducting.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before णी to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानयम|समानयमः
समानयम m. (-मः) The same pitch of voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानाधिकरण
समानाधिकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Common or generic property.<BR>	 2. A predicament<BR>or condition including several things or persons.<BR>	 3. Same location<BR>or predicament.<BR>	 m. (-णः) A generic character. Adj.<BR>	 1. Being in the<BR>same category or predicament, having a common substratum, (in<BR>phil.)<BR>	 2. Being in the same case or same government, (in gram.) E.<BR>समान, and अधिकरण possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानाधिकार|समानाधिकारः
समानाधिकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Similar or equal duty, office, or government.<BR>2. Generic character.<BR> E. समान, अधिकार office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानित
समानित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Taken, led, conducted.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before<BR>णी to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानीय
समानीय Ind. Having taken.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before णी to take, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानोदक|समानोदकः
समानोदक m. (-कः) A kinsman, one who when distinct from the<BR>Sapiṇḍa is next in order and succession, and is connected by<BR>oblations of water only, to the manes of common ancestors; this<BR>relationship extends to the fourteenth in descent, i. e. the seven<BR>first or Sapiṇḍas presenting water as well as the cakes, are also<BR>Samānodakas, whilst the seven next presenting water alone are<BR>Samānodakas only.<BR> E. समान common, उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानोदर्य्य|समानोदर्य|समानोदर्यः|समानोदर्य्यः
समानोदर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A brother of whole blood.<BR> E. समान same, उदर belly, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समान्त|समान्तः
समान्त n. (-न्तं) The end of a year.<BR> E. समा a year, and अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप|समापः
समाप m. (-पः) Sacrificing, offering oblations to the gods.<BR> E. सम् same,<BR>आप water; in which libations of water are made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापक|समापकः
समापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Filling, completing, finishing.<BR>	 2. Killing. E.<BR>सम् together, आप् to get, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापत्ति|समापत्तिः
समापत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Chance, accident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापन|समापनं
समापन n. (-नं) Conclusion, completion, finish.<BR>	 2. A section, a chapter, a<BR>division.<BR>	 3. Killing, destroying.<BR>	 4. Profound meditation.<BR>	 5. Gain,<BR>acquisition.<BR> E. सम् with, together with, आप् to obtain, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापन्न|समापन्नं
समापन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Finished, done, completed, concluded.<BR>	 2. Got,<BR>gained, obtained.<BR>	 3. Distressed, afflicted.<BR>	 4. Killed.<BR>	 5. Accom-<BR>plished, perfect, (in any branch of study.)<BR>	 6. Come, occurred.<BR>E. सम् implying completion, &c., आङ् before पद् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापित|समापितं
समापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Finished, done, concluded.<BR> E. सम् before आप् to<BR>get, aff. क्त, and इट् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्त|समाप्तः
समाप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Finished, done, concluded, completed.<BR>	 2. Clever.<BR>E. सम् before आप् to get, aff. क्त, without the augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्ति|समाप्तिः
समाप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. End, completion, perfection, conclusion, finish.<BR>	 2.<BR>Reconciling differences, putting an end to disputes, &c.<BR> E. सम्<BR>implying completion, आप् to get or gain, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्तिक|समाप्तिकः
समाप्तिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Finite, final, concluding, completing.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. One who has completed a course of holy study.<BR>	 2. A finisher,<BR>an ender.<BR> E. समाप्त, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्त्यर्था
समाप्त्यर्था f. (-र्था) Part of a stanza given as a task or trial of skill to be<BR>completed.<BR> E. समाप्ति completion, अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्लुत
समाप्लुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Drenched, drowned.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before प्लु<BR>to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाभाषण|समाभाषणं
समाभाषण n. (-णं) Conversing, speaking to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्नान|समाम्नानं
समाम्नान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Enumeration.<BR>	 2. Mention, repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्नाय|समाम्नायः
समाम्नाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Traditional repetition or mention.<BR>	 2. A traditional<BR>collection.<BR>	 3. Revelation.<BR>	 4. Enumeration, recitation.<BR>	 5. Totality,<BR>the aggregate.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before म्ना to remember, घञ् and<BR>युक् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाय|समायः
समाय m. (-यः) A visit, arrival.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before या to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायत
समायत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Lengthened, extended.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before<BR>यम् to restrain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायात
समायात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Come, arrived.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before या to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायुक्त
समायुक्त f. (-क्ता)<BR>	 1. Connected, united.<BR>	 2. Prepared, made ready.<BR>	 3.<BR>Charged, appointed.<BR>	 4. Provided, supplied.<BR>	 5. Devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायुत
समायुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Joined, connected, attached to or united<BR>with.<BR>	 2. Decorated, adorned.<BR>	 3. Endowed with.<BR>	 4. Collected,<BR>brought together.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before युत joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायोग|समायोगः
समायोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Union, junction, connection, association.<BR>	 2. Heap,<BR>multitude, assemblage.<BR>	 3. Cause, origin, motive, object.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>आङ् before युज् to join, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारब्ध
समारब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं) Begun, commenced.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before<BR>रभि to begin, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारम्भ|समारंभ|समारंभः|समारम्भः
समारम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Commencement, beginning.<BR>	 2. An undertaking.<BR>3. An unguent.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before रभि to commence, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाराधन|समाराधनं
समाराधन n. (-नं) Winning, satisfying, gratification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारूढ
समारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Ascended, gone up or upon.<BR>	 2. Mounted.<BR>	 3.<BR>Agreed to, determined.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before रुह् to grow, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोपण|समारोपणं
समारोपण n. (-णं) Placing or fixing in or on.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before रुह्<BR>to grow, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोपित
समारोपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Placed in or upon.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Caused to<BR>ascend.<BR>	 2. Planted.<BR>	 3. Delivered over.<BR>	 4. Strung, (as a bow.) E.<BR>सम् and आङ् before रुह् to grow, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोह|समारोहः
समारोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Going up, ascending.<BR>	 2. Mounting, riding upon.<BR>	 3.<BR>Agreeing.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before रुह् to rise, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समार्थिन्
समार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि)<BR>	 1. Desirous of equality.<BR>	 2. Seeking peace.<BR>E. सम् and अर्थिन् who asks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्बन|समालंबनं
समालम्बन n. (-नं) Resting upon, being supported by.<BR> E. सम् and आङ्<BR>before लवि to depend, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्भ|समालंभ|समालंभः|समालम्भः
समालम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Smearing the body with coloured perfumes, as with<BR>saffron, sandal, &c.<BR>	 2. Seizing, (as a victim for sacrifice.)<BR> E. सम्<BR>and आङ् before लभि to sound, aff. अच्; also with ल्युट् aff. समालम्भन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालम्भन|समालंभन|समालंभनं|समालम्भनं
समालम्भन n. (-नं) Smearing the body with coloured fragrant substances:<BR>see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाली
समाली f. (-ली) A collection of flowers, a nosegay, &c.<BR> E. स for सम् with,<BR>माला a garland, affs. अच् and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावर्त्तन|समावर्तन|समावर्तनं|समावर्त्तनं
समावर्त्तन n. (-नं) A pupil's return home after finishing his religious<BR>studies.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before वृत् to be, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावाय|समावायः
समावाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A multitude, a number, a heap or quantity.<BR>	 2.<BR>Association.<BR>	 3. Integral or inseparable aggregation.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>आङ् implying aggregation, अय् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावास|समावासः
समावास m. (-सः) Residence, abode.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before वस् to dwell,<BR>घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावासित
समावासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sojourning, taking up a residence.<BR> E. समावास, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाविष्ट
समाविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Entered or engrossed by, absorbed by,<BR>(feeling, passion, &c.) possessed by, (as an evil spirit.)<BR>	 2. Entered<BR>thoroughly.<BR>	 3. Entered, (as a mansion.)<BR>	 4. Seated, settled.<BR>	 5. Well-<BR>instructed.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् implying entireness, and विष्ट entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत|समावृतः
समावृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Surrounded, encompassed.<BR>	 2. Covered,<BR>enclosed, beset.<BR>	 3. Viewed.<BR>	 4. Protected.<BR>	 5. Shut out, excluded.<BR>E. सम् and आङ् before वृ to choose, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्त|समावृत्तः
समावृत्त m. (-त्तः) A pupil who has completed his studies and taken<BR>leave of his preceptor.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before वृत् to be, aff. क्त;<BR>also with कन् added, समावृत्तक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेद्य
समावेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) To be announced or communicated.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>आङ् before विद् to know, causal v., यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेश|समावेशः
समावेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Affection, passion, emotion.<BR>	 2. Possession by evil<BR>spirits.<BR>	 3. Entrance.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before विश् to enter, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेशित|समावेशितः
समावेशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Placed, fixed.<BR>	 2. Entered.<BR>	 3. Brought in<BR>or into.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before विश् to enter, causal v., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाशङ्कित
समाशङ्कित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Doubtful, fearing, apprehensive.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>आङ् before शकि to doubt, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रय|समाश्रयः
समाश्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Protection, refuge.<BR>	 2. Seeking protection.<BR>	 3. A<BR>dwelling place.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रित|समाश्रितः
समाश्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Protected, defended, cherished, refuged. E.<BR>सम् intensitive, and आश्रित refuged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रित्य
समाश्रित्य Ind.<BR>	 1. Depending upon, trusting to.<BR>	 2. Having engaged in,<BR>agreed to, &c.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before श्री to serve, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्लेष|समाश्लेषः
समाश्लेष m. (-षः) A close embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वस्त
समाश्वस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Trusting, confiding in.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before श्वस् to breathe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वास|समाश्वासः
समाश्वास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Trust, belief, confidence.<BR>	 2. Relief, encouragement.<BR>3. Recovering breath.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before श्वस् to breathe, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वासन|समाश्वासनं
समाश्वासन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Recreating, recreation.<BR>	 2. Consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्
समास् m. (-माः) A year.<BR> E. स for सह with, मास a month: see सम and समा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास|समासः
समास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Contraction, abridgment, conciseness.<BR>	 2. Composition<BR>of words, formation of compound terms, (in grammar.)<BR>	 3. Com-<BR>position of differences, reconciling quarrels.<BR>	 4. Aggregation.<BR>assemblage, collection.<BR>	 5. Whole.<BR> E. सम् together, अस् to throw or<BR>direct, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासक्त|समासक्तः
समासक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Joined, united.<BR>	 2. Reached, attained.<BR>	 3.<BR>Marked, affected by, &c.<BR>	 4. Combined, comprehended.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>आङ् before षञ्ज् to be in contact with, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासक्ति|समासक्तिः
समासक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Union.<BR>	 2. Comprehension, inclusion.<BR>	 3. Affection.<BR>E. सम् and आङ् before षञ्ज् to be in contact with, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासञ्जत्
समासञ्जत् mfn. (-ञ्जन्-ञ्जन्ती-ञ्जत्) Joining, or connecting with.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>आङ् before षञ्ज् to unite, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासञ्जन|समासंजन|समासंजनं|समासञ्जनं
समासञ्जन n. (-नं) Joining, uniting, union, combination, connection,<BR>contact.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before षञ्ज् to be in contact with, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासतस्
समासतस् Ind. Briefly, summarily.<BR> E. समास, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासन
समासन Ind. Succinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासन्न|समासन्नं
समासन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. Obtained, attained. E.<BR>सम् and आङ् implying union or contiguity, षद् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासभावना
समासभावना f. (-ना) Composition by the sum of the products.<BR> E. समास,<BR>and भावना contemplating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासर्जन|समासर्जनं
समासर्जन n. (-नं) Delivering, consigning, abandoning.<BR> E. सम् and आङ्<BR>before सृज् to leave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासवत्|समासवन्त्
समासवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Abridged, contracted.<BR>	 2. Compounded.<BR>m. (-वान्) The Tūn tree, (Cedrela Tunna.)<BR> E. समास, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासादन|समासादनं
समासादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Attaining, effecting, accomplishing.<BR>	 2. Finding,<BR>obtaining.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before षद् to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासादित|समासादितः
समासादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done, effected, attained, obtained, accom-<BR>plished.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before षद् to go, causal v., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासाद्य|समासाद्यं
समासाद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Attainable, what may be obtained or effec-<BR>ted. Ind. Having obtained, &c.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before षद् to go,<BR>aff. ण्यत् or ल्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासाध्याहार|समासाध्याहारः
समासाध्याहार m. (-रः) Supplying an ellipsis.<BR> E. समास, अध्याहार the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासार्थ
समासार्थ m. (-र्थः) The sense of a compound.<BR>	 f. (-र्था) Part of a stanza to<BR>be completed.<BR> E. समास connection, composition, अर्थ meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासीन
समासीन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Sitting, seated.<BR> E. सम् before अस् to sit, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासृष्ट
समासृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Left, abandoned, given, made over.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>आङ् before सृज् to leave, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासेवन
समासेवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Following, practising.<BR>	 2. Serving.<BR> E. सम् and आङ्<BR>before सेव् to serve, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासेवित
समासेवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Followed, practised.<BR>	 2. Served.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>आङ् before सेव् to serve, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासोक्ति|समासोक्तिः
समासोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) A protracted metaphor, (in rhetoric.)<BR> E. समास, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समास्या
समास्या f. (-स्या) Interview, colloquy.<BR> E. सम् together, अस् to be, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहत
समाहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Struck, wounded.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before हन् to<BR>strike, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहरण|समाहरणं
समाहरण n. (-णं) Uniting, combining, collecting, composition.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, आङ् before हृ to take, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहर्तृ
समाहर्तृ f. (-र्त्री) Adj. Habituated to acquire.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्ता) A collector of taxes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहार|समाहारः
समाहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Aggregation, collection, assemblage, either in fact<BR>or thought.<BR>	 2. Contraction, abridgment.<BR>	 3. Composition or words,<BR>(in grammar.)<BR>	 4. Conjunction of equal words or sentences, the<BR>power of the particle “and.” 5. A particular form of composition,<BR>a sub-division of the class Dwaṇḍa, in which several words are<BR>joined together, and the compound is a term in the neuter gen-<BR>der, as अहिनकुलं the snake and mongoose.<BR>	 6. The combination of<BR>two letters of the alphabet into a syllable, which designates all<BR>the letters intermediate between the two of which it consists.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, आङ् before हृ to take or convey, and घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहित|समाहितः
समाहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Promised, agreed or assented to.<BR>	 2. Absorbed<BR>in meditation, absent, abstracted or having the senses steadily<BR>held in subjection.<BR>	 3. Concluded, demonstrated, following from<BR>what has been said.<BR>	 4. Composed, reconciled, put an end to, (as<BR>a contest or dispute.)<BR>	 5. Placed, deposited, delivered.<BR>	 6. Pure,<BR>purified.<BR>	 7. Finished, completed.<BR>	 8. Cool, collected, firm.<BR>	 9.<BR>Assembled.<BR>	 n. (-तं) (In rhetoric,) The expression or description of<BR>attentiveness.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् implying collection or perfection, धा<BR>to have or hold, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृत|समाहृतः
समाहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Accepted, received, taken.<BR>	 2. Collected,<BR>assembled, combined.<BR>	 3. Compiled.<BR>	 4. Accumulated.<BR>	 5. Much,<BR>abundant.<BR>	 6. Abridged.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before हृत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृति|समाहृतिः
समाहृति f. (-तिः) Compilation, abridgment, an abridgment.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, आङ् before हृ to take, to bring, aff. क्तिन्: see समाहार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्व|समाह्वः
समाह्व mf. (-ह्वः-ह्वी)<BR>	 1. Calling out or to, mutual calling.<BR>	 2. Acclaim.<BR>	 3.<BR>Defiance, Challenge.<BR>	 f. (-ह्वा)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly Gojiwhā.<BR>	 2.<BR>Name.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before ह्वेञ् to call, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वय|समाह्वयः
समाह्वय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A match, a main, the conflict of animals or birds<BR>for sport, cockfighting, &c.<BR>	 2. War, battle.<BR>	 3. Calling out.<BR>	 4.<BR>Name, appellation.<BR> E. सम् and आङ् before ह्वेञ् to call, घ or अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वान|समाह्वानं
समाह्वान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Challenge.<BR>	 2. Calling together.<BR> E. समाह्व to call out,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिक|समिकं
समिक n. (-कं) A pike, a dart.<BR> E. सम even, ठक् aff.; or सम्--इण्--डि संज्ञायां कन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समित्
समित् f. (-मित्) War, battle.<BR> E. सम् together, इण् to go, aff. क्विप्, and तुक्<BR>final augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिता
समिता f. (-ता) Wheat-flour.<BR> E. सम् before इण् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिति|समितिः
समिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Assembly, company.<BR>	 3. Association,<BR>meeting, union.<BR>	 4. Sameness, likeness, equality.<BR> E. सम् with, इण् to<BR>go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिथ|समिथः
समिथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. War, battle.<BR> E. सम् together, इण् to go, थक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिद्ध|समिद्धः
समिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Lighted, kindled, set alight or on fire.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before इन्ध् to kindle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिध्
समिध् f. (-मित् or मिद्) Fuel, wood, grass, &c. so employed.<BR> E. सम् to-<BR>gether, इन्धि to kindle or inflame, क्विप् aff., and the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिध|समिधः
समिध m. (-धः) AGNI or fire, सम्, and इन्ध् to kindle, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिन्धन|समिंधनं|समिन्धनं
समिन्धन n. (-नं) Fuel.<BR> E. सम् with, इन्ध् to kindle, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिन्धान
समिन्धान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Augmenting, prospering.<BR> E. सम् before इधि to<BR>increase, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिर|समिरः
समिर m. (-रः) Wind, air.<BR> E. सम्, with, ईर् to go, aff. क, and the vowel made short; also समीर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक|समीकं
समीक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. A pike, a dart.<BR> E. षम् to be sad or<BR>confused, ईकक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीकरण|समीकरणं
समीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Assimilation, digestion.<BR>	 2. Equalizing, making<BR>equal to.<BR>	 3. Equation, (in algebra.)<BR> E. सम, and करण making, च्वि<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीकृत|समीकृतं
समीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Equalized, made even or equal.<BR>	 2. Imitated,<BR>done in like manner, &c.<BR>	 3. Added, summed up.<BR>	 4. Balanced,<BR>equipoised.<BR> E. सम् same even, and कृत made, with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्रिया
समीक्रिया f. (-या) (In arithmetic.) Equation.<BR> E. सम, क्रिया operation,<BR>च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्ष|समीक्षं|समीक्षः
समीक्ष n. (-क्षं)<BR>	 1. The Sānkhya system of philosophy.<BR>	 2. Complete,<BR>investigation.<BR>	 f. (-क्षा)<BR>	 1. Nature, essential nature, or according to<BR>the Sānkhya system, crude matter or any of its twenty-four<BR>essential parts.<BR>	 2. Understanding, intellect.<BR>	 3. Sight, seeing,<BR>inspection, looking.<BR>	 4. Effort.<BR>	 5. Search, investigation, thorough<BR>inspection.<BR>	 6. A book, a work supplementary to the Vedas,<BR>treating of the modes of sacrifice.<BR> E. सम् before ईक्ष् to see, affs.<BR>अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्षण|समीक्षणं
समीक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Search, looking for, investigation.<BR>	 2. Seeing, look-<BR>ing at.<BR> E. सम् intensitive prefix, ईक्षण seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्षित
समीक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Seen, looked at.<BR>	 2. Considered, investiga-<BR>ted.<BR> E. सम् before ईक्ष् to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीक्ष्यकारिन्
समीक्ष्यकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Acting after due deliberation.<BR> E. समीक्ष्य<BR>having inspected, कारिन् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीच|समीचः
समीच m. (-चः) The ocean.<BR>	 f. (-ची)<BR>	 1. A deer, a doe.<BR>	 2. Praise, eulogium.<BR>E. सम् before इण् to go, Unādi aff. चट्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीचक|समीचकः
समीचक m. (-कः) Copulation.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीचीन|समीचीनं
समीचीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. True.<BR>	 2. Right, correct.<BR>	 3. Fit, proper.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>Truth.<BR> E. सम्यक् true, aff. ख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीद|समीदः
समीद m. (-दः) Fine wheat-flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीन|समीनः
समीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Yearly, annual, relating to a year.<BR>	 2. Hired<BR>for a year.<BR>	 3. After a year, a year hence, &c.<BR> E. समा a year, aff. ख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीनिका
समीनिका f. (-का) A cow calving every year.<BR> E. समीन a year, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीप|समीपः
समीप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Near, contiguous, proximate, at hand.<BR>	 n. (-पं)<BR>Proximity, vicinity.<BR> E. सम् together, आप water, and ई sub-<BR>stituted for आ; analogous to the confluence of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीपग
समीपग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Approaching, going or gone near to.<BR> E. समीप,<BR>and ग who or what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीपतस्
समीपतस् Ind. Before, near.<BR> E. समीप, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीपता
समीपता f. (-ता) Proximity, contiguity.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also<BR>with त्व, समीपत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीभूत
समीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Equalised.<BR>	 2. Identified.<BR>	 3. Equipoised. E.<BR>सम same, भूत become, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीय|समीयः
समीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of like cause or origin.<BR> E. सम same, च्छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीयिवस्
समीयिवस् mfn. (-वान्-युषी-वः) Going to, arriving at, attaining.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before इण् to go, क्वसु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीर|समीरः
समीर m. (-रः) Air, wind.<BR> E. सम् every way, ईर् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीरण|समीरणः
समीरण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A plant, commonly Maruvaka.<BR>	 3. A<BR>traveller.<BR>	 n. (-णं) Throwing.<BR> E. सम् completely, ईर् to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीरित
समीरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Tossed, thrown.<BR>	 2. Gone.<BR>	 3. Sent.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before ईर् to send, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीहा
समीहा f. (-हा) Longing, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीहित
समीहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wished, desired.<BR>	 2. Undertaken.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Wish,<BR>desire.<BR> E. सम् before ईह् to wish, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुक्षण|समुक्षणं
समुक्षण n. (-णं) Shedding, effusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुख|समुखः
समुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं) Eloquent.<BR> E. स with, and मुख a mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुचित|समुचितः
समुचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Fit, right, proper.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, उचित proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चय|समुच्चयः
समुच्चय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Assemblage, collection, either in thought or fact.<BR>2. Conjunction of words or sentences, the power of the particle<BR>and, or also; but it implies the conjunction of different objects<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">Page766-a+ 60</a>]<BR>of one act or different acts with the same object, as ईश्वरं गुरुञ्च<BR>भजस्व worship GOD, and (or also) the Guru.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before<BR>चि to collect, aff. अच् or णच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चर|समुच्चरः
समुच्चर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Who or what goes about or up traverses, ascends,<BR>flies, &c.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before चर् to go, अच् aff.; also with घञ्,<BR>समुच्चार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्चरत्
समुच्चरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत) Going up or about.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before चर् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छेद|समुच्छेदः
समुच्छेद m. (-दः) Destroying, destruction.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before छिद् to<BR>cut, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्रय|समुच्छ्रयः
समुच्छ्रय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Opposition, enmity.<BR>	 2. Height, elevation.<BR> E. सम्,<BR>and उद् up, above, and श्रिञ् to serve, aff. अच् or णच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्राय|समुच्छ्रायः
समुच्छ्राय m. (-यः) Height, elevation.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before श्रि to serve,<BR>aff. णच्, and the vowel made long, or घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्रित|समुच्छ्रितः
समुच्छ्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) High, elevated, lofty.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before श्वि<BR>to serve, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्वसित|समुच्छ्वसितं
समुच्छ्वसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sighing.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A sigh.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before<BR>श्वस् to breathe, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुच्छ्वास|समुच्छ्वासः
समुच्छ्वास m. (-सः) Heavy expiration, sighing.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before श्वस्<BR>to breathe, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुञ्झित
समुञ्झित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Left, abandoned, quitted, resigned.<BR> E. सम् inten-<BR>sitive, and उञ्झित left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्कर्ष|समुत्कर्षः
समुत्कर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Setting one self up as being of high tribe.<BR>	 2. Exaltation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्क्रम|समुत्क्रमः
समुत्क्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Rise, ascent, going up.<BR>	 2. Transgressing proper<BR>bounds.<BR> E. सम् and उद् up, क्रम going, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्क्रोश|समुत्क्रोशः
समुत्क्रोश m. (-शः) A osprey.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, and उद् before क्रुश् to<BR>cry, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्तरत्
समुत्तरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Crossing, passing over or beyond.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>उद् before तृ to cross, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्तेजन
समुत्तेजन n. (-नं) Inflaming, inciting, irritating.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before<BR>तिज् to be sharp, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्तेजित
समुत्तेजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Inflamed, incited, excited, irritated.<BR> E. सम्<BR>and उद् before तिज् to be sharp, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्थ|समुत्थः
समुत्थ mfn. (-त्थः-त्था-त्थं)<BR>	 1. Rising, risen, getting or got up.<BR>	 2. Born,<BR>produced.<BR>	 3. Occasioned, occurring.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, उद् up, स्था<BR>to stand, क aff., the स is changed to थ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्थान|समुत्थानं
समुत्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Performance of work, occupation, effort, industry.<BR>	 2.<BR>Positive indication or symptom of disease.<BR>	 3. Rising, getting up.<BR>4. Common growth or increase, (as of size or wealth, &c.)<BR>	 5.<BR>Healing a wound or sore, cure or recovery from any injury.<BR>	 6.<BR>Occupation.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, उद् up, स्था to stay or be, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्थित|समुत्थितः
समुत्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Risen, got up.<BR>	 2. Increased.<BR>	 3. Derived or<BR>obtained from.<BR>	 4. Cured, healed.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before स्था to stay,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पतन|समुत्पतनं
समुत्पतन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going.<BR>	 2. Ascending.<BR>	 3. Making effort, energy,<BR>exertion.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before पत् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पतित
समुत्पतित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone, gone up, ascended.<BR>	 2. Exerted,<BR>vigorous.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before पत् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पत्ति|समुत्पत्तिः
समुत्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Origin, production, birth.<BR>	 2. Occurrence, incidence.<BR>E. सम् and उद् before पद् to go, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पन्न|समुत्पन्नः
समुत्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. Occurring, taking place. E.<BR>सम् and उद् before पद् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पाट|समुत्पाटः
समुत्पाट m. (-टः) Detaching, separating from, tearing from, &c.<BR> E. सम्<BR>and उद् before पट् to go, causal v., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पाटित
समुत्पाटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Detached or severed from, torn from. &c. E.<BR>सम् and उद् before पट् to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पादन|समुत्पादनं
समुत्पादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Producing, fabricating.<BR>	 2. Effecting.<BR> E. सम् and उद्<BR>before पद् to go, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पादित
समुत्पादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Produced, effected.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before पद्<BR>to go, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्पिञ्ज|समुत्पिंज|समुत्पिञ्जः
समुत्पिञ्ज mfn. (-ञ्जः-ञ्जा-ञ्जं) Excessively confused or confounded, bewildered,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">Page766-b+ 61</a>]<BR>lost, overcome.<BR>	 m. (-ञ्जः) An army in great disorder.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>उद् before पिजि to hurt, aff. अच्; also समुत्पिञ्जल, and simply पिञ्ज, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सर्ग|समुत्सर्गः
समुत्सर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. Leaving, abandoning.<BR>	 2. Giving.<BR>	 3. Evacuation of<BR>urine or fæces.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before सृज् to abandon, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सव|समुत्सवः
समुत्सव m. (-वः) Festivity.<BR> E. सम्, and उत्सव festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सारण|समुत्सारणं
समुत्सारण n. (-णं) Pursuing, hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सुक|समुत्सुकः
समुत्सुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Sorrowful, regretting, missing or grieving<BR>for any one absent, &c.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, उत्सुक sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुत्सेध|समुत्सेधः
समुत्सेध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Height, elevation.<BR>	 2. Fatness, thickness.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>उद् before षिध् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदक्त|समुदक्तं
समुदक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Drawn, raised, lifted or thrown up from a<BR>deep place.<BR> E. सम् with, and उद् up, अञ्च् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदय|समुदयं|समुदयः
समुदय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Multitude, number, heap or quantity.<BR>	 2. War,<BR>battle.<BR>	 3. Assent, rise.<BR>	 4. Rising, (as of the sun, &c.)<BR>	 5. Effort,<BR>exertion, perseverance.<BR>	 6. A day.<BR>	 7. The rear of an army.<BR>	 8.<BR>Revenue.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before इण् to go, aff. अच् or णच्; also<BR>समुदाय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदागम|समुदागमः
समुदागम m. (-मः) Knowledge.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before आगम knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाचार|समुदाचारः
समुदाचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Intention, purpose, design, motive.<BR>	 2. Proper or<BR>right usage.<BR> E. सम् with, उद and आङ् before चर् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाय|समुदायः
समुदाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Multitude, quantity, number, heap.<BR>3. Rise, ascent.<BR>	 4. The rear or reserve of an army.<BR> E. सम् and उद्<BR>up, इण् to go, aff. णच्; also समुदय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाहरण|समुदाहरणं
समुदाहरण n. (-णं) Declaring, uttering.<BR>	 2. An illustration.<BR> E. सम् and उद्<BR>before हृ to take, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदाहृत
समुदाहृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Declared.<BR>	 2. Illustrated.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before<BR>हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदित|समुदितः
समुदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Risen, ascended.<BR>	 2. Risen, (as the sun, &c.)<BR>3. Produced, excited, occasioned.<BR>	 5. Possessed of.<BR>	 6. Aggregated,<BR>united.<BR> E. सम्, and उदित risen; or सम and उद् before इण् to go,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीरण|समुदीरणं
समुदीरण n. (-णं) Repeating, declaring, speaking, reciting.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>उद् before इर् to say, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुदीरित
समुदीरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Said, spoken, declared, recited.<BR> E. सम् and उद्<BR>before ईर् to say, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ग|समुद्गः
समुद्ग mfn. (-द्गः-द्गा-द्गं)<BR>	 1. Who or what rises or goes up.<BR>	 2. Who or what<BR>pervades entirely.<BR>	 3. Having a cover or lid.<BR>	 4. Having beans.<BR>m. (-द्गः)<BR>	 1. A casket, a covered box.<BR>	 2. A stanza in which two or<BR>more of the PĀDAS correspond in sound, though in a different<BR>sense.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before गम् to go, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गक|समुद्गकः
समुद्गक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A casket, a covered box.<BR>	 2. A sort of stanza: one,<BR>each half of which consists of the very same words but in differ-<BR>ent acceptations, those of one half being respectively the<BR>attributives or adjectives to those of the other.<BR> E. सम् and उद्<BR>before गम् to go, aff. ड and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गम|समुद्गमः
समुद्गम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Rising, ascent.<BR>	 2. Birth, production.<BR>	 3. Arising,<BR>issuing, coming out.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before गम् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गयमक
समुद्गयमक n. (-कं) (In rhetoric,) The repetition of the same words in diff-<BR>erent PĀDAS of a stanza, but in a different sense.<BR> E. समुद्ग what<BR>goes completely, यमक alliteration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गिरण|समुद्गिरणं
समुद्गिरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. What is vomited or ejected.<BR>	 2. Lifting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गीत|समुद्गीतं
समुद्गीत n. (-तं) A loud song.<BR> E. सम and उद् before गै to sing, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्गीर्ण|समुद्गीर्णः
समुद्गीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Brought up, (as food,) vomited.<BR>	 2. Raised or<BR>lifted up, (from a depth, &c.)<BR>	 3. Uttered, exclaimed raised, (as a<BR>cry, &c.)<BR> E. सम् and उद् before गॄ to swallow, or sound, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्दिष्ट
समुद्दिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Pointed out, shown.<BR>	 2. Particularised,<BR>enumerated.<BR>	 3. Explained.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before दिश् to show, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्देश|समुद्देशः
समुद्देश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Describing.<BR>	 2. Pointing out.<BR>	 3. Particularising,<BR>explaining, enumerating.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before दिश् to show, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धत|समुद्धतः
समुद्धत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ill-mannered, behaving ill or improperly,<BR>conducting one's self discreditably.<BR>	 2. Raised or drawn up.<BR>	 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">Page767-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Upheld, supported.<BR>	 4. Arrogant, proud, puffed up with pride, &c.<BR>5. Impudent.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before हन् to hurt or kill, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धरण|समुद्धरणं
समुद्धरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Food vomited or thrown up.<BR>	 2. Drawing up, raising,<BR>lifting, (as water from a well, &c.)<BR>	 3. Eradicating a tree, &c. pull-<BR>ing up by the roots.<BR>	 4. Extricating, lifting out.<BR>	 5. Taking out<BR>from, as a part or share.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before हृ to take, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धर्त्तृ|समुद्धर्तृ
समुद्धर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ) Who or what lifts, raises, extricates, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-र्त्ता) A redeemer, a deliverer.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before हृ to take,<BR>तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धस्त
समुद्धस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Wiped off by the hand.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्धत|समुद्धतः
समुद्धत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ill-behaved.<BR>	 2. Thrown up, (as food, &c.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Raised or drawn up.<BR>	 4. Extricated, lifted out or from.<BR>	 5. Taken<BR>as a share, set apart, divided.<BR>	 6. Seized, possessed of.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>उद् before धृ to have, or हृ to take, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्भव|समुद्भवः
समुद्भव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Born or produced.<BR>	 m. (-वः) Production, origin. E.<BR>सम् and उद् before भव being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्भूत|समुद्भूतः
समुद्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Born, produced, derived.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before भू to be, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्यत
समुद्यत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ready, prepared.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, उद्यत active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्यम|समुद्यमः
समुद्यम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Commencement, onset.<BR>	 2. Effort, exertion.<BR>	 3. Lifting<BR>up.<BR> E. सम्, and उद्यम effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्योग|समुद्योगः
समुद्योग m. (-गः) Active exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्र|समुद्रः
समुद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं) Sealed, stamped.<BR>	 m. (-द्रः) A sea, an ocean.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before उन्दि to be wet, and रक् aff.; or स for सह with, and मुद्रा a<BR>seal; also thence signifying a limit, (i. e. bounded by conti-<BR>nents,) or a jewel, (the receptacle of gems,) or सम् with, उद्र an otter;<BR>or स with, मुद pleasure, or सम् together, उद water, and रा to give<BR>or have, aff. क, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रकफ|समुद्रकफः
समुद्रकफ m. (-फः) Cuttle-fish-bone.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, and कफ phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रकान्ता|समुद्रकांता
समुद्रकान्ता f. (-न्ता) A river.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, and कान्ता the mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रग|समुद्रगः
समुद्रग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Ocean-going, sea-faring.<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A trader by<BR>sea.<BR>	 2. A seaman.<BR>	 f. (-गा) A river.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, ग who goes to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रगृह|समुद्रगृहं
समुद्रगृह n. (-हं) A sort of pleasure or summer house, built in the<BR>midst of water, &c.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, and गृह house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रचुलुक|समुद्रचुलुकः
समुद्रचुलुक m. (-कः) The saint AGASTYA.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, चुलुक a pot;<BR>having drank up the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रतट
समुद्रतट n. (-टं) The sea-coast.<BR> E. समुद्र, and तट a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रतीर
समुद्रतीर n. (-रं) The sea-shore.<BR> E. समुद्र, and तीर a bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रदयिता
समुद्रदयिता f. (-ता) A river.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, and दयिता beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रनवनीत|समुद्रनवनीतं
समुद्रनवनीत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The beverage of immortality.<BR>	 2. The moon. E.<BR>समुद्र the ocean, and नवनीत butter: being produced or recovered<BR>by the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रफेन|समुद्रफेनः
समुद्रफेन m. (-नः) Cuttle-fish-bone.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, फेन froth or foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रमेखला
समुद्रमेखला f. (-ला) The earth.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, मेखला a zone; the sea-<BR>girt; surrounded by the ocean as by a girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रयान|समुद्रयानं
समुद्रयान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A sea-voyage.<BR>	 2. A vessel, a ship.<BR> E. समुद्र, यान going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रयायिन्
समुद्रयायिन् m. (-यी) A sailor, a navigator, a merchant trading by sea.<BR>E. समुद्र, and यायिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रयोषित्
समुद्रयोषित् f. (-षित्) A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्ररसना
समुद्ररसना f. (-ना) The earth.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, and रसना a zone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रलवण|समुद्रलवणं
समुद्रलवण n. (-णं) Sea-salt.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रवसना
समुद्रवसना f. (-ना) The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रवह्नि|समुद्रवह्निः
समुद्रवह्नि m. (-ह्निः) Submarine fire.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, and वह्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रविजय|समुद्रविजयः
समुद्रविजय m. (-यः) The father of the Jina or Jaina pontiff of the<BR>present era.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea. and विजय victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रवेला
समुद्रवेला f. (-ला) A wave of the sea.<BR> E. समुद्र, and वेला a wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रसुभगा
समुद्रसुभगा f. (-गा) The ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रान्त|समुद्रांत|समुद्रान्तं|समुद्रान्तः
समुद्रान्त n. (-न्तं)<BR>	 1. The nutmeg.<BR>	 2. The sea-shore.<BR>	 f. (-न्ता)<BR>	 1. A shrub,<BR>(Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>	 2. The cotton plant.<BR>	 3. A gramineous plant,<BR>(Trigonella corniculata.)<BR>	 4. The earth.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, and अन्त<BR>end or boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्राम्बरा
समुद्राम्बरा f. (-रा) The earth.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, and अम्बर vesture;<BR>clothed or invested by the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रारु|समुद्रारुः
समुद्रारु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A shark.<BR>	 2. A large fabulous fish, perhaps inten-<BR>ding the whole, hyperbolically described.<BR>	 3. RĀMA'S bridge. E.<BR>समुद्र the sea, ऋ to go, aff. उण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्रिय|समुद्रियः
समुद्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Marine, oceanic, maritime.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, aff.<BR>घ or छ; also समुद्रीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्वह|समुद्वहः
समुद्वह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Who or what lifts or bears up.<BR>	 2. Moving<BR>up and down.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before वह् to bear, अच् or घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्वहत्
समुद्वहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्)<BR>	 1. Lifting or raising up.<BR>	 2. Moving up and<BR>down.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before वह् to bear, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्वाह|समुद्वाहः
समुद्वाह m. (-हः) Nuptials, marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुद्वेग|समुद्वेगः
समुद्वेग m. (-गः) Fear, alarm, terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्दन|समुंदन|समुंदनं|समुन्दनं
समुन्दन n. (-नं) Wetness, damp, moisture.<BR> E. सम् before उन्दि to be moist<BR>or wet, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्न|समुन्नं
समुन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Wet, moist, moistened.<BR> E. सम् before उन्द् to be wet, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नत|समुन्नतः
समुन्नत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. High, lofty, elevated.<BR>	 2. Full, prominent.<BR>3. Exalted, dignified.<BR>	 4. Proud, arrogant.<BR>	 5. Lifted up, raised up.<BR>6. Just, upright.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before नम् to bow, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नति|समुन्नतिः
समुन्नति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Height, elevation, (physical and mental.)<BR>	 2. Conse-<BR>quence, rank, dignity, exaltation.<BR>	 3. Pride, loftiness.<BR>	 4. Lifting up.<BR>5. Increase, thriving, prosperity.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before नम् to bow,<BR>aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नद्ध|समुन्नद्धः
समुन्नद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Conceited of learning, thinking one's self<BR>learned.<BR>	 2. Proud, arrogant.<BR>	 3. Produced, born.<BR>	 4. Tied up or<BR>above.<BR>	 5. Supreme, lord or master.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before णह् to<BR>tie, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नय|समुन्नयः
समुन्नय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Occurrence, event.<BR>	 2. Gaining, attaining.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>उद् before णी to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नयत्
समुन्नयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Attaining, gaining.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before<BR>णी to get, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्मूलन|समुन्मूलनं
समुन्मूलन n. (-नं) Uprooting, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपक्षित
समुपक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Seen, beheld.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before ईक्ष् to see,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपगत
समुपगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Approached, approximated.<BR> E. सम्, and उप near, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपगम|समुपगमः
समुपगम m. (-मः) Approach, approximation, contact.<BR> E. सम् and उप<BR>before गम् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपचित
समुपचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Collected, heaped, accumulated.<BR> E. सम् and<BR>उप before चि to collect, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपजीषम्
समुपजीषम् Ind. Happily, fortunately.<BR> E. सम् and उप before जुष् to<BR>gratify, aff. अम्; also read उपजोषम् and उपयोषम् or समुपयोषम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपभोग|समुपभोगः
समुपभोग m. (-गः) Copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपविष्ट
समुपविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Seated, sat down.<BR> E. सम् and उप before विश् to enter, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपवेश|समुपवेशः
समुपवेश m. (-शः) Welcoming, entertaining, causing to sit down.<BR> E. सम्<BR>and उप before विश् to enter, causal v., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपवेशन|समुपवेशनं
समुपवेशन n. (-नं) A building, a habitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपवेशित
समुपवेशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Welcomed, made to sit or rest.<BR> E. सम् and उप<BR>before विश् to enter, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपस्था
समुपस्था f. (-स्था)<BR>	 1. Proximity, approach, approximation.<BR>	 2. Nearness.<BR>	 3.<BR>Happening, befalling.<BR> E. सम् and उप before ष्ठा to be, अङ् and<BR>टाप् affs.; also समुपस्थान and समुपस्थिति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपस्थित
समुपस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Attained, acquired.<BR>	 2. Brought or come<BR>near to, approximated.<BR> E. सम् and उप before ष्ठा to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपार्जन|समुपार्जनं
समुपार्जन n. (-नं) Reconciliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपेत
समुपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Come together, assembled.<BR>	 2. Arrived at.<BR>	 3.<BR>Endowed with.<BR> E. सम् and उप before इण् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपेयिवस्
समुपेयिवस् mfn. (-वान्-युषी-वत्) Going, proceeding.<BR> E. सम् and उप before<BR>इण् to go, क्वसु aff. of the present participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुपोढ
समुपोढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Suppressed, restrained.<BR>	 2. Gone upwards,<BR>risen.<BR>	 3. Increased, developed.<BR> E. सम् and उप before वह् to bear, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुल्लसत्
समुल्लसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्)<BR>	 1. Sporting, wantoning.<BR>	 2. Shining, beauti-<BR>ful.<BR> E. सम् and उद् before लस् to play, शतृ aff. of the present<BR>participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुल्लसित
समुल्लसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sportive, sporting.<BR>	 2. Brilliant, beautiful.<BR>E. सम् and उत् before लस् to play, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूढ|समूढः
समूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Heaped, accumulated, assembled, collected.<BR>2. Crooked, bent.<BR>	 3. Produced quickly.<BR>	 4. Accompanying, associated,<BR>a companion.<BR>	 5. Tamed, tranquillized.<BR>	 6. Married.<BR>	 7. Purified,<BR>cleansed.<BR>	 8. Led, conducted.<BR>	 9. Enveloped.<BR> E. सम् before वह् to bear,<BR>or ऊह् to reason, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूर|समूरः
समूर m. (-रः) A deer.<BR> E. सम् to be confused, aff. ऊर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूरु|समूरुः
समूरु m. (-रुः) A deer, one of the sorts of which the skin may be used<BR>as a student's seat, &c.<BR> E. षम् to be confused, ऊरु aff.; or सन्धिहीन-<BR>त्वात् ऊरु यस्य । also with कन् added समूरुक. According to some, this<BR>sort of deer is distinguished by a white mane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूल|समूलं
समूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Having a root, joined or in connection with the<BR>root.<BR> E. स with, मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूलघात
समूलघात n. (-तं) Utter destruction or eradication.<BR> E. समूल radical, घात killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूह|समूहः
समूह m. (-हः) Assemblage, aggregate in general, heap, number,<BR>multitude, quantity, &c.<BR> E. सम् together, ऊह् to reason, or वह्<BR>to bear, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूहकार्य्य|समूहकार्य
समूहकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Interests or business of a number, general affair. E.<BR>समूह, and कार्य्य affair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूहत्
समूहत् mfn. (-हन्-हन्ती-हत्) Collecting, gathering.<BR> E. सम् before वह् to bear, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूहन|समूहनं
समूहन n. (-नं) Collection, plenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूहनी
समूहनी f. (-नी) A broom.<BR> E. समूह heap, (of dirt,) णी to take, affs. डु and<BR>ङीष्; or सम + ऊह्--करणे ल्युट् ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समूह्य|समूह्यः
समूह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be assembled or collected.<BR>	 m. (-ह्यः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Sacrificial fire.<BR>	 2. A place prepared for the reception of a sacri-<BR>ficial fire. Ind. Having collected.<BR> E. सम् completely, वह् to bear, or<BR>ऊह् to reason, aff. क्यप्, ण्यत् or ल्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समृद्ध|समृद्धः
समृद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Happy, prosperous, thriving.<BR>	 2. Grown,<BR>increased, augmented.<BR>	 3. Flourishing.<BR>	 4. Full, entire.<BR>	 5. Accelera-<BR>ted.<BR> E. सम् completely, ऋध् to increase, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समृद्धवेग
समृद्धवेग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Very swift.<BR> E. समृद्ध, and वेग speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समृद्धि|समृद्धिः
समृद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Thriving, increase.<BR>	 2. Prosperity, success.<BR>	 3. Power,<BR>supremacy.<BR>	 4. Wealth.<BR> E. सम् completely, ऋध् to increase, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समेत|समेतः
समेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Near, approximated, approached.<BR>	 2. Agreed,<BR>covenanted.<BR>	 3. Collected, associated.<BR>	 4. Having, possessed of. E.<BR>सम् with, इत gone; or सम and आङ् before इण् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समेधित|समेधितः
समेधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Increased, augmented.<BR> E. सम् before एधित increa-<BR>sed; or सम + एध् + णिच्--क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समोदक|समोदकं
समोदक n. (-कं) A mixture of half butter milk and half water.<BR> E. सम<BR>equal, उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प|संपः|सम्पः
सम्प m. (-म्पः) Descending, falling, alighting.<BR>	 f. (-म्पा) Lightning.<BR> E. सम्, and पत् to fall, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पत्ति|संपत्ति|संपत्तिः|सम्पत्तिः
सम्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Prosperity, success, increase of wealth, power or<BR>happiness.<BR>	 2. Excellence of qualities.<BR>	 3. A sort of medicinal root.<BR>E. सम् implying perfection, पद् to go, aff. क्तिन्; also सम्पद् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पद्|संपद्
सम्पद् f. (-पत् or पद्)<BR>	 1. Success, prosperity, increase of any favourable<BR>kind, or of wealth, fame, power, &c.<BR>	 2. Advancement in good<BR>qualities, perfection, excellence.<BR>	 3. A necklace of pearls, &c.<BR>4. Treasure.<BR>	 5. Adornment.<BR>	 6. Blessing.<BR> E. सम् before पद् to<BR>go, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पद|संपद|सम्पदं
सम्पद n. (-दं) Standing with the feet even.<BR> E. सम् together, पद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पद्वर|संपद्वर|संपद्वरः|सम्पद्वरः
सम्पद्वर m. (-रः) A king, a prince.<BR> E. सम् before पद् to go, ष्वरच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पन्न|संपन्न|संपन्नः|सम्पन्नः
सम्पन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Accomplished, completed, effected, obtained.<BR>2. Prosperous, fortunate, thriving, happy.<BR>	 3. Possessed of, endow-<BR>ed with.<BR>	 4. Mature, full-grown.<BR>	 5. Perfectly acquainted with or<BR>performing, (duty, &c.)<BR>	 6. Right, correct.<BR>	 7. Made of, become.<BR>E. सम् with, पद् to go, aff. क्त; also with कन् aff. सम्पन्नक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पराय|संपराय|संपरायः|सम्परायः
सम्पराय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Calamity, adversity.<BR>	 2. Futurity.<BR>	 3. War, battle.<BR>4. A son.<BR> E. सम् and परा before इण् to go, अच् or णच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्परायक|संपरायक|संपरायकं|सम्परायकं
सम्परायक n. (-कं) War, battle.<BR> E. कन् added to the last; see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्परायिक|संपरायिक|संपरायिकं|सम्परायिकं
सम्परायिक n. (-कं) War, battle.<BR> E. सम्पराय war, ठन् aff.; also सम्परायक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्परिशोषण|संपरिशोषण
सम्परिशोषण n. (-णं) A withering or drying up.<BR> E. सम्, and परि implying<BR>entirely, शोषण drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पर्कं|सम्पर्क|संपर्क|संपर्कः|सम्पर्कः
सम्पर्कं m. (-र्कः)<BR>	 1. Mixture, mingling, contact, union, junction.<BR>	 2. Copu-<BR>lation.<BR> E. सम् with, पृच् to be in contact, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पर्किन्|सम्पर्क्किन्
सम्पर्किन् mfn. (-र्की-र्किणी-र्कि)<BR>	 1. Mixed, blended.<BR>	 2. Connected or united<BR>with.<BR>	 3. In contact with.<BR> E. सम् together, पृच् to be in contact,<BR>घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पर्कीय|संपर्कीय|सम्पर्कीयः|सम्पर्क्कीय
सम्पर्कीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Liable to come in contact, relating to contact<BR>or connection.<BR> E. सम्पर्कं, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पश्यत्
सम्पश्यत् mfn. (-श्यन्-श्यन्ती-श्यत्) Seeing, beholding.<BR> E. सम् before दृश् to see, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पा|संपा
सम्पा f. (-म्पा) Lightning. See शम्पा.<BR> E. सम्यक् अतर्कितं पतति पत-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पाक|संपाक|संपाकः|सम्पाकः
सम्पाक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Reasoning, a reasoner, a logician.<BR>	 2. Impu-<BR>dent, shameless.<BR>	 3. Small, little, low.<BR>	 4. Lecherous, libertine.<BR>	 5.<BR>Lustful, lewd.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A tree, (Casia fistula.)<BR> E. सम् completely,<BR>पाक ripening or maturing; also शम्पाक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पाट|संपाट|संपाटः|सम्पाटः
सम्पाट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A spindle.<BR>	 2. The intersection of the prolonged side<BR>of a triangle by the perpendicular.<BR> E. सम् before पट् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पात|संपात|संपातः|सम्पातः
सम्पात m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Descending, falling, coming down.<BR>	 2. Alighting, (as<BR>a bird.)<BR>	 3. A special mode of flight, (attributed to birds.)<BR>	 4. Being<BR>removed or displaced.<BR>	 5. Flying of arrows.<BR>	 6. Meeting.<BR>	 7. Con-<BR>currence, butting together.<BR>	 8. Going, moving.<BR>	 9. The son of<BR>GARUḌA.<BR> E. सम् before पत् to alight, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पाति|संपाति|संपातिः|सम्पातिः
सम्पाति f. (-तिः) The son of GARUḌA, a fabulous bird.<BR> E. सम्, पा intensi-<BR>tive, to cherish or drink, अति Unādi aff.; or सम् + पत्-णिच्-इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पातिक|संपातिक|संपातिकः|सम्पातिकः
सम्पातिक m. (-कः) The eldest son of GARUḌA, and like him a sort of<BR>fabulous and supernatural bird.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पाद|संपाद|संपादः
सम्पाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Completion, accomplishment.<BR>	 2. Obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पादक|संपादक|सम्पादकः
सम्पादक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what fulfils, accomplishes, &c.<BR>n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Effecting.<BR>	 2. Cleansing.<BR>	 3. Attaining, acquiring.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before पद् to go, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पादन|संपादन|संपादनं|सम्पादनं
सम्पादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gaining, acquiring, reaching, attaining.<BR>	 2. Accom-<BR>plishing, effecting.<BR> E. सम् before पद् to go, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पादित|संपादित|सम्पादितः
सम्पादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Attained, obtained, gained, gotten.<BR>	 2. Effec-<BR>ted, accomplished.<BR> E. सम् before पद् to go, causal form, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पिष्ट
सम्पिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Pounded, bruised, crushed, destroyed.<BR> E. सम्,<BR>and पिष्ट ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पीड|संपीड|संपीडः
सम्पीड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. Agitating, disturbing.<BR>	 2. Sending, driving, directing.<BR>3. Pain, torture.<BR>	 4. Castigation, punishment.<BR>	 5. Squeezing, Com-<BR>pression.<BR> E. सम् before पीड् to give pain to, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पीडन|संपीडन|संपीडनं|सम्पीडनं
सम्पीडन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Castigation, punishment.<BR>	 2. Agitation.<BR>	 3. Sending.<BR>4. Pressing, squeezing.<BR> E. सम् before पीड् to give pain, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पीडित|संपीडित
सम्पीडित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Pained, tortured.<BR>	 2. Punished.<BR>	 3. Agitated.<BR>4. Sent.<BR>	 5. Pressed, squeezed.<BR> E. सम् before पीड् to pain, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पीति|संपीति|संपीतिः|सम्पीतिः
सम्पीति f. (-तिः) Drinking in company.<BR> E. सम् together, पा to drink, क्तिन्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पुट|संपुट|संपुटः|सम्पुटः
सम्पुट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A casket, a covered box.<BR>	 2. Cavity.<BR>	 3. The Kuruvaka-<BR>flower.<BR> E. सम् together, पुट् to contract, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पुटक|संपुटक|सम्पुटकः
सम्पुटक m. (-कः) A casket.<BR> E. सम् with पुट् to contract, aff. क, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पूजन|संपूजन|संपूजनं
सम्पूजन n. (-नं) Treating with great respect.<BR> E. सम्, and पूज् to worship,<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पूजनीय
सम्पूजनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be, what may or ought to be respected,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सम्, and पूज् to respect, अनीयर् aff.; also सम्पूजितव्य and<BR>सम्पूज्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पूजित|संपूजित
सम्पूजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Honoured, respected.<BR> E. सम्, and पूजित worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पूर्ण|संपूर्ण|सम्पूर्णं|सम्पूर्णः
सम्पूर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Whole, entire.<BR>	 2. Complete, finished.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः)<BR>Any mode of music in which all the notes of the gamut are<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">Page769-a+ 60</a>]<BR>employed.<BR>	 n. (-र्णं) Ether, the etherial matter or atmosphere.<BR> E. सम्<BR>intensitive, and पूर् to fill, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पूणता
सम्पूणता f. (-ता) Fulness, completion.<BR> E. सम्पूर्ण and तल् aff.; also with त्व, सम्पूर्णत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्पृक्त|संपृक्त|सम्पृक्तः
सम्पृक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Mixed, blended, combined, inlaid, interspersed.<BR>2. Joined, united.<BR>	 3. Close to, in contact with.<BR> E. सम् together, पृच्<BR>to be in contact, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रकॢप्त
सम्प्रकॢप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Possessed of, having.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before कॢप्त made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रक्षालन|संप्रक्षालनं
सम्प्रक्षालन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Bathing.<BR>	 2. Inundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रणर्दित|सम्प्रणर्द्दित
सम्प्रणर्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bellowed.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before नर्द् to sound, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रणीत|संप्रणीत
सम्प्रणीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Brought, conveyed.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before णी to<BR>take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रणेतृ|संप्रणेतृ
सम्प्रणेतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what guides, leads, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ता) A judge,<BR>a ruler.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before णी to get, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतापन|संप्रतापन|संप्रतापनं
सम्प्रतापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Heating, burning.<BR>	 2. Afflicting.<BR>	 3. One of the<BR>twenty-one hells.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before तप् to heat, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रति|संप्रति|सम्प्रतिः
सम्प्रति Ind. Now, at present, at this time.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) A Jaina pontiff,<BR>of the last era.<BR> E. सम्, and प्रति with respect to, &c., conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतिपत्ति|संप्रतिपत्ति|संप्रतिपत्तिः|सम्प्रतिपत्तिः
सम्प्रतिपत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) Agreed, convened, consentient.<BR>	 f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Assent, concurrence.<BR>	 2. Admission, acknowledgment, confession.<BR>3. Agreement.<BR>	 4. Co-operation.<BR>	 5. Presence, company.<BR>	 6. Assault.<BR>7. Doing, performing, effecting.<BR>	 8. A particular kind of reply or<BR>defence, admission of a fact, (in law.)<BR> E. सम् together, प्रतिपत्ति,<BR>agreement, assent; or सम् + प्रतिपद्यते-क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतिपन्न|संप्रतिपन्न
सम्प्रतिपन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Done, performed.<BR>	 2. Come, arrived.<BR>	 3. Agreed,<BR>concurred.<BR>	 4. Attached.<BR> E. सम् and प्रति before पद् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतिरोधक|संप्रतिरोधक|संप्रतिरोधकं|सम्प्रतिरोधकं|संप्रतिरोधकः
सम्प्रतिरोधक m. (-कः) Durance, actual confinement or restraint, imprison-<BR>ment.<BR> E. सम्प्रति present, रोधक what restricts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतीक्षा|संप्रतीक्षा
सम्प्रतीक्षा f. (-क्षा) Expecting, awaiting.<BR> E. सम् and प्रति before ईक्ष् to see,<BR>अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रतीति|संप्रतीति|संप्रतीतिः|सम्प्रतीतिः
सम्प्रतीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Fame, notoriety.<BR>	 2. Compliance.<BR> E. सम् before प्रतीति, the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रत्यय|संप्रत्यय|संप्रत्ययः
सम्प्रत्यय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Agreement.<BR>	 2. Firm conviction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रदान|संप्रदान|संप्रदानं|सम्प्रदानं
सम्प्रदान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Gift, donation.<BR>	 2. The act of giving or handing over<BR>completely.<BR>	 3. Bestowing in marriage.<BR>	 4. The idea expressed by<BR>the fourth case, the dative case, (in grammar.)<BR> E. सम् and प्र<BR>before दा to give, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रदानीय|संप्रदानीय|संप्रदानीयं
सम्प्रदानीय n. (-यं) A gift, a donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रदाय|संप्रदाय|संप्रदायः|सम्प्रदायः
सम्प्रदाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Traditional doctrine, what has been transmitted<BR>from one teacher to another, and is established as of sacred<BR>authority.<BR>	 2. A sect, a schism, a peculiar doctrine and exclusive<BR>worship of one divinity.<BR>	 3. Custom, usage.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before दा<BR>to give, घञ् aff., युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रधान|संप्रधानं
सम्प्रधान n. (-नं) Consideration, ascertainment.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before धा to have, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रधारणा|संप्रधारणा
सम्प्रधारणा f. (-णा) Determination, deliberation, the determining on the<BR>propriety or impropriety of anything.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before धृ to<BR>have or hold, causal form, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रपद|संप्रपद|सम्प्रपदं|संप्रपदः
सम्प्रपद n. (-दं) Roaming, peregrination.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before पद् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रमीद
सम्प्रमीद m. (-दः) Excessive joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रमोष|संप्रमोष|संप्रमोषः
सम्प्रमोष m. (-षः) Loss, abstraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रयाण|संप्रयाण|संप्रयाणं
सम्प्रयाण n. (-णं) Departure.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before या to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रयुक्त|संप्रयुक्त
सम्प्रयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Acquainted or connected with.<BR>	 2. Joined,<BR>united with, &c.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before युज् to join, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रयोग|संप्रयोग|संप्रयोगः|सम्प्रयोगः
सम्प्रयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Connection, relation, mutual proportion, dependence<BR>or association.<BR>	 2. Order, natural and connected series or arrange-<BR>ment.<BR>	 3. Copulation.<BR>	 4. Union, joining.<BR>	 5. Magic.<BR> E. सम् and प्र<BR>before युज् to join, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रयोगिन्|संप्रयोगिन्
सम्प्रयोगिन् m. (-गी)<BR>	 1. A libertine, a lecher.<BR>	 2. A catamite.<BR>	 3. A joiner<BR>or uniter, any one who effects a union or connection.<BR>	 4. A conjuror.<BR>E. सम्प्रयोग union in general, or coition, aff. इनि or घिनुण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रवदन|संप्रवदनं
सम्प्रवदन n. (-नं) Conversation, talking together.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before वद्<BR>to speak, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रवृत्त|संप्रवृत्त
सम्प्रवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Passed, gone by.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before वृत्त been<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रवृष्ट|संप्रवृष्ट|संप्रवृष्टं
सम्प्रवृष्ट n. (-ष्टं) A rain-fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रश्न|संप्रश्न|संप्रश्नः
सम्प्रश्न m. (-श्नः) Asking, enquiring civilly.<BR> E. सम्, and प्रश्न asking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रसाद|संप्रसाद|संप्रसादः
सम्प्रसाद n. (-दं)<BR>	 1. Trust, confidence.<BR>	 2. Serenity.<BR>	 3. Favour, grace.<BR>	 4.<BR>The soul.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before सद् to go, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रसाधन|संप्रसाधन|संप्रसाधनं
सम्प्रसाधन n. (-नं) Effecting, accomplishing, performing well or com-<BR>pletely.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before साध् to accomplish, causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रसारण|संप्रसारण|संप्रसारणं|सम्प्रसारणं
सम्प्रसारण n. (-णं) The mutual substitution of the letters इ, उ, ऋ, ॡ,<BR>and their respective semi-vowels, य, व, र, and ल, (in gram.)<BR> E. सम्,<BR>and प्र before सृ to go, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रस्थान|संप्रस्थान|संप्रस्थानं
सम्प्रस्थान n. (-नं) Setting out on a journey.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before स्था to<BR>stay, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रस्थित
सम्प्रस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Set forth, gone on a journey.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before स्था to stay, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रहार|संप्रहार|संप्रहारः|सम्प्रहारः
सम्प्रहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. War, battle.<BR>	 2. Striking, killing.<BR>	 3. Mutual striking.<BR>4. Going, motion.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before हृ to take, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रहास|संप्रहास|संप्रहासः
सम्प्रहास n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Laughter.<BR>	 2. Joy.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before हस् to laugh, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्राप्त|संप्राप्त|सम्प्राप्तः
सम्प्राप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Attained, obtained, gotten.<BR>	 2. Effected,<BR>accomplished.<BR>	 3. Become.<BR>	 4. Arrived, come.<BR> E. सम् and प्राप्त obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्राप्ति|संप्राप्ति|संप्राप्तिः|सम्प्राप्तिः
सम्प्राप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Obtaining, getting, acquisition.<BR> E. सम् before प्राप्ति ob-<BR>taining; or सम + प्र + आप-क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रीत|संप्रीत
सम्प्रीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-pleased, delighted.<BR> E. सम्, and प्रीत liking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रीति|संप्रीति|संप्रीतिः
सम्प्रीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Attachment, affection.<BR>	 2. Delight, friendly regard.<BR>E. सम् before प्रीति affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेक्षण|संप्रेक्षण|संप्रेक्षणं
सम्प्रेक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Deliberating, considering, investigating.<BR>	 2. Looking<BR>at, seeing.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before ईक्ष् to see, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेक्षित
सम्प्रेक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Considered, investigated.<BR>	 3. Seen, beheld. E.<BR>सम् and प्र before ईक्ष् to see, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रेषित
सम्प्रेषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sent, ordered.<BR>	 2. Dismissed, sent away.<BR> E. सम् before प्रेषित sent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रैष|संप्रैष|संप्रैषः|सम्प्रैषः
सम्प्रैष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Order, command, direction.<BR>	 2. Dismissing, sending<BR>away.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before इष् to go, aff. घञ्; also सम्प्रेष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रोक्षण|संप्रोक्षण|संप्रोक्षणं
सम्प्रोक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkling.<BR>	 2. Consecrating, (a temple.)<BR> E. सम् and<BR>प्र before उक्ष् to sprinkle, ल्युट् aff.: see प्रोक्षण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्रोक्षित
सम्प्रोक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkled, wetted, (especially with holy<BR>water.)<BR>	 2. Consecrated.<BR> E. सम् and प्र before उक्ष् to sprinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्प्लव|संप्लव|संप्लवः
सम्प्लव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Falling in various directions.<BR>	 2. Submersion, inunda-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Subversion.<BR>	 4. Surge.<BR> E. सम्, and प्लु to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्फाल|संफाल|संफालः|सम्फालः
सम्फाल m. (-लः) A ram.<BR> E. सम् before फल् to bear fruit, aff. ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्फुल्ल|संफुल्ल|सम्फुल्लः
सम्फुल्ल mfn. (-ल्लः-ल्ला-ल्लं) Blown, blossomed, opened, (as a flower.)<BR> E. सम्<BR>completely, and फुल्ल blown, अच् being added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्फेट|संफेट|संफेटः
सम्फेट m. (-टः) (In dramatic language,) Wrathful encounter, defiance,<BR>combat, the incident of an angry and tumultuous conflict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्ब्|संब्
सम्ब् r. 1st cl. (सम्बति) To go, to move. r. 10th cl. (सम्बयति-ते) To unite,<BR>to join, to contact or collect; also षम्ब् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्ब|संब|संबं|सम्बं
सम्ब n. (-म्बं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. The second ploughing of a field.<BR> E. सम्ब् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बद्ध|संबद्ध|सम्बद्धः
सम्बद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Connected with, endowed with, possessing as<BR>a predicate or property.<BR>	 2. Bound, tied, attached.<BR> E. सम् with, बन्ध्<BR>to bind, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बन्ध|संबन्ध|संबंध|संबन्धः|सम्बन्धः
सम्बन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं)<BR>	 1. Able, capable.<BR>	 2. Fit, right, proper.<BR>	 3. Ad-<BR>junct, annexed or connected, inherent, &c.<BR>	 m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Prosperity,<BR>success.<BR>	 2. Fitness, propriety.<BR>	 3. Connection, natural or essential<BR>connection, as of a property with a substance, subject matter with<BR>a work, proper meaning with a word, &c.<BR>	 4. Connection by birth<BR>or marriage, relationship.<BR>	 5. The application of authority, as of the<BR>Upanishads to prove a theological assertion, &c.<BR>	 6. Mental associa-<BR>tion of objects, conceiving them in connection with each other.<BR>	 7.<BR>(In grammar,) The possessive case.<BR> E. सम् with, and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बन्धक|संबन्धक|संबंधक|संबन्धकः
सम्बन्धक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating to, concerning.<BR>	 2. Fit, suitable.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः)<BR>	 1. A kind of alliance.<BR>	 2. A friend.<BR>	 3. A relation by birth or<BR>marriage.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बन्धिन्|संबन्धिन्|संबंधिन्
सम्बन्धिन् mfn. (-न्धी-न्धिनी-न्धि)<BR>	 1. Possessing good qualities, learned,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">Page770-a+ 60</a>]<BR>amiable, liberal, &c.<BR>	 2. Having adjoined or connected with,<BR>inherent.<BR>	 3. Related to, a relation, connection.<BR>	 4. Connected with,<BR>belonging or relating to.<BR> E. सम्बन्ध connection, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बर|संबर|सम्बरं|संबरः|सम्बरः
सम्बर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Restraint, forbearance, self-control.<BR>	 3. A<BR>religious observance of the Bauddhas.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The name of a<BR>demon or Daitya slain by KĀMA.<BR>	 2. A deer.<BR>	 3. A sort of fish.<BR>4. A mountain.<BR>	 5. A Jina, one of the pontiffs of the future age.<BR>6. A kind of dramatic entertainment.<BR>	 7. A bridge, a dam, a cause-<BR>way.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Asparagus racemosus.)<BR>	 2. A medicinal<BR>plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR> E. सम्ब् to accumulate, अरन् aff.; ङीप्<BR>added in the fem. form; also शम्बर and संवर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बल|संबल|संबलं|संबलः
सम्बल mn. (-लः-लं) Provender or stock for travelling expenses.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>Water.<BR> E. सम्ब् to go, aff. कलच्; or सम्यक् बलो यतो वा; also शम्बल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाकृत|सम्बाकृतं
सम्बाकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Twice-ploughed.<BR> E. सम्ब a second ploughing, कृत<BR>made, डाच् augment; also शम्बाकृत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाध|संबाध|संबाधः|सम्बाधः
सम्बाध Adj.<BR>	 m. only, but having the three genders when the last term<BR>of a compound adjective. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Narrow, contracted, impassible,<BR>either from being naturally confined, or from being blocked up or<BR>crowded.<BR>	 2. Crowded. Subst.<BR>	 1. The vulva.<BR>	 2. The road to tartarus<BR>or hell.<BR>	 3. Fear, dread.<BR> E. सम् before बाध् to impede, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाधक|संबाधक
सम्बाधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Crowding, contracting, pressing upon.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before बाध् to obstruct, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बाधन|संबाधन|संबाधनं|सम्बाधनं
सम्बाधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A gate, a barrier.<BR>	 2. The point of a stake or spit.<BR>3. A doorkeeper.<BR>	 4. Obstructing, opposing.<BR>	 5. The vulva.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before बाध् to impede, aff. ल्यु or ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बुद्ध|संबुद्ध|संबुद्धः|सम्बुद्धः
सम्बुद्ध m. (-द्धः) A Jaina deified sage.<BR> E. सम् implying perfection, बुद्ध wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बुद्धि|संबुद्धि|संबुद्धिः|सम्बुद्धिः
सम्बुद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Calling or calling to.<BR>	 2. An epithet.<BR>	 3. Perfect<BR>knowledge or perception.<BR>	 4. Consciousness.<BR>	 5. The vocative case.<BR>E. सम् with बुध् to know, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बोध|संबोध|संबोधः|सम्बोधः
सम्बोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Explaining, instructing, informing.<BR>	 2. Throwing,<BR>sending, 3. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 4. Right perception.<BR> E. सम् completely,<BR>बुध् to know, causal form, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्बोधन|संबोधन|संबोधनं|सम्बोधनं
सम्बोधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Calling, addressing, calling to.<BR>	 2. The vocative case,<BR>(in grammar.)<BR> E. सम्, and बुध् to know, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भली|संभली
सम्भली f. (-ली) A bawd, a procuress.<BR> E. सम् with, भल् to speak, affs. अच्<BR>and ङीष्; also शम्भली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भव|संभव|संभवः|सम्भवः
सम्भव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Cause, origin, motive.<BR>	 2. Birth, production.<BR>	 3. Mixing,<BR>union, combination.<BR>	 4. Capacity, appropriateness, adaptation,<BR>the conformity of the receptacle to the thing received, or<BR>supporter to the thing supported.<BR>	 5. Agreement, engagement.<BR>6. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 7. Acquaintance, intimacy.<BR>	 8. Possibility.<BR>9. Ability, adequacy.<BR>	 10. Consistency, compatibility.<BR>	 11. The<BR>third Jina of the present age.<BR> E. सम् implying perfection or co-<BR>existence, भू to be, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भव्य|संभव्य|संभव्यः|सम्भव्यः
सम्भव्य m. (-व्यः) The wood-apple, (Feronia elephantium.)<BR> E. सम् with, भव being, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भार|संभार|संभारः|सम्भारः
सम्भार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Multitude, number, quantity, heap, assemblage.<BR>2. Maintaining, supporting.<BR>	 3. Provision, preparation, getting<BR>everything ready or complete.<BR>	 4. Fulness, completion.<BR>	 5. Appara-<BR>tus, necessaries, things required for any act or affair.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before भृ to maintain, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भार्य्य|सम्भार्य|संभार्य
सम्भार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं) To be nourished, a dependent.<BR> E. सम्, and भृ to nourish, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भावन|संभावन|संभावनं|सम्भावनं
सम्भावन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Considering, reflecting.<BR>	 2. Fame, celebrity.<BR>3. Fitness, suitableness.<BR>	 4. Adequacy, competency, ability.<BR>	 5. Poss-<BR>ibility.<BR>	 6. Worship, honour.<BR>	 7. (In grammar,) The sense of the<BR>potential mood.<BR>	 8. (In rhetoric,) The use of the verb in the imper-<BR>ative or potential mood.<BR>	 9. (In Logic,) Doubt.<BR>	 10. Thought.<BR>	 11.<BR>Love.<BR> E. सम् before भू to be, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भावित|संभावित|सम्भावितः
सम्भावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Equal or adequate to, suited to or fit for.<BR>2. Possible.<BR>	 3. Considered, reflected.<BR>	 4. Satisfied or occupied with.<BR>5. Honoured.<BR> E. सम् with, भू to be, &c., causal form, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भावितात्मन्
सम्भावितात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म) Noble-minded.<BR> E. सम्भावित equal, आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाव्य|संभाव्य
सम्भाव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Suitable, to be adapted to, made, or fit for.<BR>E. सम्, and भू to be, causal v., यत् aff.; also सम्भावनीय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषण|संभाषण|संभाषणं|सम्भाषणं
सम्भाषण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Conversation, discourse.<BR>	 2. War-cry, watch-word.<BR>E. सम् together, भाषण speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषा|संभाषा
सम्भाषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. War-cry, watch-word.<BR>	 2. Conversation, discourse.<BR>	 3.<BR>Contract, agreement.<BR>	 4. Greeting.<BR>	 5. A criminal connection.<BR> E. सम्<BR>together, भाषा speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भाषित|संभाषित
सम्भाषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Said, spoken to, addressed.<BR> E. सम् before भाष् to speak, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भिन्न|संभिन्न|संभिन्नः|सम्भिन्नः
सम्भिन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Shaken, agitated.<BR>	 2. Divided, broken.<BR>	 3.<BR>Combined or united with.<BR> E. सम्, and भिन्न broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भु|संभु|सम्भुः
सम्भु m. (-म्भुः) A parent, a progenitor.<BR> E. सम् with, भू to be, डु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भुग्न
सम्भुग्न mfn. (-ग्नः-ग्ना-ग्नं) Bent, curved.<BR> E. सम्, and भुग्न aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूत|संभूत|सम्भूतः
सम्भूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Born, produced.<BR>	 2. Equal, adequate.<BR>	 3. Com-<BR>bined with, being together.<BR> E. सम् with, भू to be, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूतविजय|संभूतविजय|सम्भूतविजयः
सम्भूतविजय m. (-यः) A sacred person peculiar to the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूति|संभूति|संभूतिः
सम्भूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Birth, production.<BR>	 2. Combination.<BR>	 3. Power.<BR>	 4.<BR>Fitness.<BR> E. सम्, and भू to be, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूय|संभूय
सम्भूय Ind. Having united or combined.<BR> E. सम् together, भू to be, ल्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूयकारिन्|संभूयकारिन्
सम्भूयकारिन् m. (-री) A co-adjutor, co-partner, or colleague.<BR> E. सम्भूय, and<BR>कारिन् who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भूयसमुत्थान|सम्भूयसमुत्थानं
सम्भूयसमुत्थान n. (-नं) Partnership, association in trade, joint execution of<BR>work or conduct of business.<BR> E. सम्भूय, समुत्थान performance of work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृत|संभृत|सम्भृतः
सम्भृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Collected, assembled.<BR>	 2. Gained, got, possessed<BR>of.<BR>	 3. Filled, full.<BR>	 4. Complete, ready, prepared.<BR>	 5. Nourished<BR>maintained.<BR>	 6. Carried.<BR> E. सम् before भृ to nourish, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृति|संभृति|संभृतिः|सम्भृतिः
सम्भृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Nourishment, support.<BR>	 2. Plentitude, fulness.<BR>	 3.<BR>Preparation, provision.<BR> E. सम्, भृ to possess, aff. क्तिन्: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भृत्य|संभृत्य
सम्भृत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) To be nourished.<BR> E. सम्, भृ to nourish, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भेद|संभेद|संभेदः|सम्भेदः
सम्भेद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The confluence of two or more rivers, or the junction<BR>of a river with the sea.<BR>	 2. Breaking, splitting, bursting.<BR>	 3. Union,<BR>junction.<BR> E. सम् with, भिद् to break, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोग|संभोग|संभोगः|सम्भोगः
सम्भोग n. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Enjoyment, pleasure, delight.<BR>	 2. Coition, copulation.<BR>3. A Jaina or Bauddha Śāsana or edict, &c.<BR>	 4. One branch of<BR>the Śringāra-rasa, or sentiment of love, happy or successful<BR>love, meeting or union of lovers.<BR>	 5. A catamite.<BR>	 6. Use,<BR>occupation, employment.<BR> E. सम् with, भोग enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोगिन्|संभोगिन्
सम्भोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि)<BR>	 1. Sensual, sensualist, &c.<BR>	 2. Enjoying, as<BR>pleasure or property.<BR>	 m. (-गी) A catamite.<BR> E. सम्भोग, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भोजन|संभोजन|संभोजनं
सम्भोजन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Convivial, friendly, (as a dinner, &c.)<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>A meal, &c. partaken together, a convivial party.<BR> E. सम् together,<BR>भुज् to enjoy, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्रम|संभ्रम|संभ्रमः|सम्भ्रमः
सम्भ्रम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Haste, hurry.<BR>	 2. Fear, terror.<BR>	 3. Flurry, confusion,<BR>haste or hurry arising from joy, fear, &c.<BR>	 4. Error, ignorance.<BR>5. Turning round, whirling about, revolving.<BR>	 6. Respect, reverence.<BR>E. सम् before भ्रम् to revolve, &c., aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्भ्रान्त|संभ्रांत|संभ्रान्त
सम्भ्रान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Bewildered, agitated.<BR>	 2. Flurried, confused.<BR>E. सम्, and भ्रम् to err, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मत|संमत
सम्मत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Assented or agreed to, concurred in 2. Con-<BR>formable to.<BR>	 3. Attached to.<BR>	 4. Liked, beloved.<BR>	 5. Honoured,<BR>respected.<BR>	 6. Thought, considered.<BR> E. सम्, मन् to mind, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मति|संमति|संमतिः|सम्मतिः
सम्मति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Wish, desire.<BR>	 2. Order, command.<BR>	 3. Agreement,<BR>assent, similarity of opinion, or purpose.<BR>	 4. Approbation.<BR>	 5. Self<BR>or real knowledge.<BR>	 6. Regard, affection, love.<BR>	 7. Respect, homage.<BR>E. सम् implying union or perfection, मति mind, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मद|संमद|संमदः|सम्मदः
सम्मद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Happy, glad.<BR>	 m. (-दः) Happiness, joy, pleasure.<BR>E. सम् with, मद् to delight, aff. अप् or घञर्थे क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्द|संमर्दः|सम्मर्द्द|सम्मर्द्दः
सम्मर्द m. (-र्दः)<BR>	 1. Trampling or treading on, thronging together.<BR>	 2.<BR>Friction, rubbing.<BR>	 3. War, battle.<BR> E. सम्, मृद् to trample, aff. घञ्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मर्दिन्|संमर्दिन्|सम्मर्द्दिन्
सम्मर्दिन् mfn. (-र्दी-र्दिनी-र्दि)<BR>	 1. Trampling.<BR>	 2. Rubbing.<BR> E. सम्मर्द, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मातुर|संमातुर
सम्मातुर m. (-रः) The son of a virtuous woman.<BR> E. सत् good, मातृ a<BR>mother, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्माद|संमाद|संमादः|सम्मादः
सम्माद m. (-दः) Frenzy, intoxication.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, मद् to be mad, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मान|संमान|संमानः|सम्मानः
सम्मान m. (-नः) Respect, homage.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Measure.<BR> E. सम्, and मन् to<BR>respect, with घञ् aff., or मा to measure, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मानन|संमानन|संमाननं
सम्मानन n. (-नं) Worship, homage.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, मन् to respect,<BR>causal form, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मानित|संमानित|सम्मानितः
सम्मानित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Treated with reverence or respect.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before मन् to respect, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मान्य|संमान्य
सम्मान्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Respectable, honourable.<BR> E. सम्मन् to respect, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्जक|संमार्जक|संमार्जकः|सम्मार्ज्जकः
सम्मार्जक m. (-कः) A sweeper.<BR> E. सम् completely, मृज् to clean, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मार्जन|संमार्जन|संमार्जनं|सम्मार्ज्जनं
सम्मार्जन n. (-नं) Sweeping, brushing, cleaning.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A broom.<BR> E. सम्<BR>before मृज् to clean, aff. ल्यु; ङीप् being added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मित|संमित|संमितं|सम्मितः
सम्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Like, similar, same.<BR>	 2. Of equal measure or<BR>extent.<BR>	 3. Commensurate, conformable, corresponding.<BR>	 4. Furnished<BR>or provided with.<BR>	 5. Meted, measured out.<BR> E. सम् with, मित measured,<BR>compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मिश्र|संमिश्र|सम्मिश्रः
सम्मिश्र mfn. (-श्रः-श्रा-श्रं) Mixed, mingled, blended, joined.<BR> E. सम् together, मिश्र mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मीलन|संमीलन|संमीलनं
सम्मीलन n. (-नं) Closing up, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुख|संमुख|सम्मुखः
सम्मुख mfn. (-खः-खा or -खी-खं) Encountering, facing, in front of.<BR> E. सम् with, मुख the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुखिन्|संमुखिन्
सम्मुखिन् m. (-खी) A mirror.<BR> E. सम् with, मुख the face, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुखीन|संमुखीन|सम्मुखीनः
सम्मुखीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Before, in front or in face of.<BR> E. सम्मुख, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मुग्ध|संमुग्ध
सम्मुग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Fascinated, bewildered.<BR>	 2. Stupified,<BR>astounded.<BR>	 3. Beautiful.<BR> E. सम् before मुह् to fascinate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूढ|संमूढ|सम्मूढः
सम्मूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Heaped, accumulated.<BR>	 2. Produced rapidly.<BR>	 3.<BR>Broken.<BR>	 4. Foolish, ignorant, senseless.<BR>	 5. Bewildered, beguiled.<BR>	 6.<BR>Stupified, astounded.<BR> E. सम् entirely, मुह् to be foolish, and क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूढचेतस्
सम्मूढचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः) Foolish, infatuated.<BR> E. सम्मूढ, चेतस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूर्छन|सम्मूर्च्छनं|संमूर्छन|संमूर्छनं
सम्मूर्छन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Uniform or universal expansion or permeation, per-<BR>vading, co-extension.<BR>	 3. Height, elevation.<BR>	 3. Fainting, insensibility.<BR>4. Increasing, augmenting.<BR>	 5. Congealing, becoming dense. E.<BR>सम् before मूर्च्छ् to faint, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मूर्च्छनोद्भव
सम्मूर्च्छनोद्भव m. (-वः) A fish or aquatic animal.<BR> E. सम्मूर्च्छन insensibility, उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृत|संमृत
सम्मृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dead, deceased.<BR> E. सम्, and मृत dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मृष्ट|संमृष्ट|सम्मृष्टः
सम्मृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Strained, filtered.<BR>	 2. Cleaned, cleansed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Well-swept.<BR> E. सम् completely, मृष्ट cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मेलन|संमेलनं
सम्मेलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Meeting together.<BR>	 2. Mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोद|संमोद|संमोदः|सम्मोदः
सम्मोद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Pleasure, delight.<BR> E. सम् intensitive, मुद् to be happy aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोह|संमोह|संमोहः
सम्मोह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Ignorance.<BR>	 2. Folly.<BR>	 3. Beguilement, fascination.<BR>	 4.<BR>Stupefaction.<BR>	 5. Fainting.<BR> E. सम् before मुह् to be foolish, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्मोहित
सम्मोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Beguiled, fascinated.<BR>	 2. Enraptured, over-<BR>come with delight, &c.<BR> E. सम्, मुह् to be foolish, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यक्
सम्यक् Ind.<BR>	 1. All, wholly.<BR>	 2. Duly.<BR>	 3. By honourable means.<BR>	 4. Distinctly.<BR>5. With, together with.<BR>	 6. Properly, fitly: see सम्यच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यकत्व
सम्यकत्व n. (-त्वं) Accuracy, totality.<BR> E. सम्यक्, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यक्दण्डन
सम्यक्दण्डन n. (-नं) Inflicting the penalty of the law, punishing in a<BR>legal manner.<BR> E. सम्यक् properly, according to the Shāstras, and<BR>दण्डन punishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यगुक्त
सम्यगुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Of equal weight or authority, (a precept.)<BR> E. सम्यक् proper, उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यग्वर्त्तमान|सम्यग्वर्तमान
सम्यग्वर्त्तमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Continuing in the discharge of duty, &c. E.<BR>सम्यक्, वर्त्तमान being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यग्वृत्ति|सम्यग्वृत्तिः
सम्यग्वृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Steady and regular discharge of prescribed duties.<BR> E. सम्यक्, वृति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यच्
सम्यच् or सम्यञ्च् mfn. (-सम्यङ्-समीची-सम्यक्)<BR>	 1. True, right.<BR>	 2. Accompany-<BR>ing, going with.<BR>	 3. Pleasant, agreeable.<BR>	 4. Same, common, iden-<BR>tical, uniform.<BR>	 5. Accurate, correct.<BR>	 6. All, entire.<BR> E. सम् with,<BR>अञ्च् to go, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यञ्च्|सम्यंच्
सम्यच् or सम्यञ्च् mfn. (-सम्यङ्-समीची-सम्यक्)<BR>	 1. True, right.<BR>	 2. Accompany-<BR>ing, going with.<BR>	 3. Pleasant, agreeable.<BR>	 4. Same, common, iden-<BR>tical, uniform.<BR>	 5. Accurate, correct.<BR>	 6. All, entire.<BR> E. सम् with,<BR>अञ्च् to go, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्राज्
सम्राज् m. (-राट्) A paramount sovereign, one who rules over other<BR>princes, and has performed the Rāja-sūya sacrifice.<BR> E. सम् all, राजृ<BR>to rule, aff. क्विप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सय्
सय् r. 1st cl. (सयते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयत्न
सयत्न mfn. (-त्नः-त्ना-त्नं) Endeavouring, taking pains.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-त्नं) Vigor-<BR>ously, assiduously.<BR> E. स with, यत्न effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयूथ्य|सयूथ्यः
सयूथ्य m. (-थ्यः) One of the same tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयोनि|सयोनिः
सयोनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. Proximity to a wife.<BR>	 3. A pair of nip-<BR>pers for cutting betel-nut.<BR>	 4. Uterine brother. Adj. Having the<BR>same womb.<BR> E. स for सह with, or सम् like, योनि pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर|सरं|सरः
सर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Who or what goes, occurring chiefly in composi-<BR>tion, as अनुसर, अवसर, &c.<BR>	 2. Cathartic, purgative.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The thick part or coagulum of curds or milk, cream, &c.<BR>2. Going, motion.<BR>	 3. An arrow.<BR>	 4. Saltness, salt.<BR>	 5. A string.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A lake, a pool.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 mf. (-रः-रा or -री) A cascade,<BR>a water-fall; also शर.<BR> E. सृ to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरःकाक|सरःकाकः
सरःकाक m. (-कः) A gander.<BR>	 f. (-की) A goose.<BR> E. सरस् a pool, काक a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरक|सरकं|सरकः
सरक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Going, moving, proceeding.<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. Spiri-<BR>tuous liquor, especially distilled from sugar, rum.<BR>	 2. Drinking<BR>spirits.<BR>	 3. A drinking vessel.<BR>	 4. Distribution of liquor.<BR>	 5. A continu-<BR>ous line of road.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A lake, a pool.<BR>	 2. Heaven, sky.<BR>	 3.<BR>Going.<BR> E. सृ to go, Unādi aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरघा
सरघा f. (-घा) A bee.<BR> E. सर one who is going, हन् to injure, aff. ड, the radical final changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरङ्ग|सरंग|सरंगः|सरङ्गः
सरङ्ग mf. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A quadruped.<BR>	 2. A bird.<BR> E. सृ to go, अङ्गच् aff; ङीष्<BR>added in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरज|सरजं
सरज n. (-जं) Fresh butter.<BR> E. सर cream, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरजस्
सरजस् f. (-जाः) A woman during menstruation.<BR> E. स for सह with, रजस्<BR>the menses; also सरजस्का ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरट्
सरट् m. (-रट्)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. (In the language of the Vedas,)<BR>A bee.<BR>	 4. A lizard, a chameleon.<BR> E. सृ to go, अटि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरट|सरटः
सरट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A lizard, a chameleon, a guana, &c.<BR>	 2. A crow.<BR>	 3.<BR>Wind.<BR> E. सृ to go, अटन् aff.; also शरट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटि|सरटिः
सरटि m. (-टिः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR> E. सृ to go, अटिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटु|सरटुः
सरटु m. (-टुः) A lizard, a chameleon, &c.<BR> E. सृ to go, अटु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण|सरणं
सरण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Going, moving, who or what goes or moves.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-णं)<BR>	 1. Oxidized iron, either in the state of rust or filings.<BR>	 2. Go-<BR>ing.<BR>	 f. (-णा or -णी)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Pæderia fetida.)<BR>	 2. A sort of Teori.<BR>E. सृ to go, aff. युच् or ल्युट्, fem. aff. टाप् or ङीष्; also शरण, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरणि|सरणिः
सरणि f. (-णिः-णी) A road, a path, a way.<BR>	 2. A straight or continuous<BR>line.<BR>	 3. A disease of the throat.<BR>	 4. Deposition of things.<BR> E. सृ to<BR>go, Unādi aff. अनि, and ङीष् optionally added; also शरणि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्ड|सरंड|सरंडः|सरण्डः
सरण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 2. A sort of ornament.<BR>	 3. A bird.<BR>4. A lover.<BR>	 5. A lizard.<BR> E. सृ to go, Unādi aff. अण्डच्; also शरण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्यु|सरण्युः
सरण्यु m. (-ण्युः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. A cloud.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR>	 4. The spring.<BR>5. Fire.<BR> E. सृ to go, अन्यु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्
सरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Going, proceeding.<BR> E. सृ to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्
सरत् m. (-रत्) Thread.<BR> E. सृ to go, अति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्नि|सरत्निः
सरत्नि mf. (-त्निः-त्रिः) A short cubit-measure.<BR> E. सृ to go, कत्निच् aff.; more<BR>commonly रत्नि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरथ|सरथः
सरथ m. (-थः) A warrior riding in a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरपत्रिका
सरपत्रिका f. (-का) The new leaf of a lotus.<BR> E. सरे जले पत्रमस्त्यस्याः ठन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरभस
सरभस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Quick, speedy.<BR>	 2. Delighted.<BR>	 3. Agitated,<BR>distressed.<BR>	 4. Passionate.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-सं) Quick, delightedly,<BR>agitatedly, &c.<BR> E. स with, रभस speed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरमा
सरमा f. (-मा) The wife of RĀVAṆA'S brother, VIBHĪSAṆA.<BR>	 2. The bitch<BR>of the gods.<BR>	 3. One of the daughter of DAKṢA.<BR> E. सृ to go, अम<BR>aff.; or स with, रम sport, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरयु|सरयुः
सरयु m. (-युः) Air, wind.<BR>	 f. (-युः-यू) The Sarayu-river.<BR> E. सृ to go, अयु Unādi aff.: also शरयु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरल|सरलः
सरल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Honest, sincere, candid, upright.<BR>	 2. Straight.<BR>3. Guileless.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A sort of pine, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>bird, (Pavo bicalcarata.)<BR>	 f. (-ला) A variety of the plant called Teori.<BR>E. सृ to go, (to spread fragrance abroad, &c.,) अलच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरलद्रव|सरलद्रवः
सरलद्रव m. (-वः) A fragrant resin, the exudation of the Saral or pine<BR>tree.<BR> E. सरल as above, द्रव what exudes. “तारपीन” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरलयायिन्
सरलयायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Going in a straight line.<BR>	 2. Upright,<BR>honest.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A plant with an upright stem.<BR> E. सरल, and यायिन्<BR>who or what goes or grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरव्य|सरव्यं
सरव्य n. (-व्यं) A butt or mark for shooting at.<BR> E. सर an arrow, व्येञ् to cover, aff. ड; also शरव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्
सरस् nf. (-रः-सी)<BR>	 1. A large pond or pool.<BR>	 2. A piece of water in which<BR>the lotus grows or may grow.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Water.<BR> E. सृ to go, (into, to<BR>bathe or drink,) असुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस|सरसं
सरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Tasty, juicy, sapid.<BR>	 2. Comprising the express-<BR>ion of the poetical Rasas or sentiments, (a work, &c.)<BR>	 3. Impass-<BR>ioned.<BR>	 4. Beautiful, charming.<BR>	 5. Agreeable.<BR>	 n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. A tank, a<BR>pond, a lake.<BR>	 2. Alchemy.<BR>	 f. (-सा) A sort of Teori.<BR>	 f. (-सी) A lake,<BR>a pond.<BR> E. स with, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसम्प्रत|सरसंप्रत|सरसम्प्रतं
सरसम्प्रत n. (-तं) A sort of Euphorbia, commonly Tekāntā-Sij.<BR> E. सम + प्र + तन्-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसिक|सरसिकः
सरसिक m. (-कः) The Indian crane.<BR> E. सरस a pool, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसिज|सरसिजं
सरसिज n. (-जं) A lotus.<BR> E. सरस a pool, (seventh case,) and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसीरुह|सरसीरुहं|सरसीरुहः
सरसीरुह m. (-हः) A lotus.<BR> E. सरसी a pool, and रुह what grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्तीर
सरस्तीर n. (-रं) The bank of a lake or pond.<BR> E. सरस्, and तीर bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्वत्|सरस्वन्त्
सरस्वत् mfn. (-स्वान्-स्वती-स्वत्)<BR>	 1. Juicy, sapid.<BR>	 2. Elegant.<BR>	 3. Sentimental.<BR>m. (-स्वान्)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A male river.<BR>	 3. A buffalo.<BR>	 4. A lake.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-स्वती)<BR>	 1. The wife of BRAHMĀ, the goddess of speech and eloquence,<BR>the patroness of music and the arts, and the inventress of the<BR>Sanskrit language and Devanāgari letters.<BR>	 2. Speech, the faculty<BR>or its exercise.<BR>	 3. A river, the SARASWATY, which rises in the<BR>mountains bounding the north-east part of the province of Delhi,<BR>whence it runs in a south-westerly direction, and is lost in the<BR>sands of the great desart in the country of the Bhatti: according<BR>to the Hindus the river only disappears in this place, and<BR>continuing its course under ground, joins the Ganges and Jamunā<BR>at Āllāhābād.<BR>	 4. A river in general.<BR>	 5. An excellent woman.<BR>6. A cow.<BR>	 7. The wife of a Muni.<BR>	 8. A female divinity, peculiar<BR>to the Jainas.<BR>	 9. The moon-plant, (Asclepias acida.)<BR>	 10. An<BR>epithet of DURGĀ.<BR> E. सरस् a lake, and मतुप् poss. aff.; or स with,<BR>रस flavour, taste, and the same aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराग
सराग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Coloured, tinted.<BR>	 2. Impassioned, passionate.<BR>E. स with, राग colour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराव|सरावः
सराव f. (-वा) Adj. Sounding.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. A lid, a cover.<BR>	 2. A shallow<BR>cup or saucer, used as one: see शराव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरि|सरिः
सरि mf. (-रिः-री) A water-fall.<BR> E. सृ to go, इन् aff.; also सर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिका
सरिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A drug, commonly Hingu-patri.<BR>	 2. Going, proceed-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. A woman going, or moving.<BR> E. सृ to go, वुन aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्
सरित् f. (-रित्)<BR>	 1. A river in general.<BR>	 2. Thread.<BR> E. सृ to go, इति<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिताम्पति|सरितांपति|सरिताम्पतिः
सरिताम्पति m. (-तिः) The ocean.<BR> E. सरित् a river, (second case plural,) पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्पति|सरित्पतिः
सरित्पति m. (-तिः) The ocean.<BR> E. सरित् a river, and पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्वत्|सरित्वन्त्
सरित्वत् m. (-त्वान्) The ocean.<BR> E. सरित् a river, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्सुत|सरित्सुतः
सरित्सुत m. (-तः) BHISHMA, the son of GANGĀ.<BR> E. सरित् the river, सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिद्वरा
सरिद्वरा f. (-रा) The Ganges.<BR> E. सरित् a river, and वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिन्नाथ|सरिन्नाथः
सरिन्नाथ m. (-थः) The ocean.<BR> E. सरित् a river, and नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिन्मुख
सरिन्मुख n. (-खं) The source of a river.<BR> E. सरित्, मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिमन्
सरिमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Going, proceeding.<BR>	 2. Motion.<BR>	 3. Air, wind.<BR> E. सृ<BR>to go, इमनिन् Unādi aff.; also सरीमन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिल|सरिलं
सरिल n. (-लं) Water. E. See सलिल, the ल being changed to र; or सृ-इलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिषप|सरिषपः
सरिषप m. (-पः) Mustard, (Sinapis dichotoma.)<BR> E. सर्षप + पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरीसृप|सरीसृपः
सरीसृप m. (-पः) A snake.<BR> E. सृप् to go, irr. reiterative form, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरु|सरुः
सरु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु) Thin, small, fine, minute.<BR>	 m. (-रुः) The hilt or<BR>handle of a sword, &c.<BR> E. सृ to go, उन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरूप|सरूपः
सरूप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Like, resembling.<BR> E. स for समान like, same, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरूपता
सरूपता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Likeness, resemblance.<BR>	 2. One of the four states of<BR>MUKTI.<BR> E. सरूप like, तल् aff. of the abstract; also सरूपत्व n. (-त्वं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोग
सरोग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Sick, diseased.<BR> E. स, and रोग sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोगिता
सरोगिता f. (-ता) Sickness, disease.<BR> E. स, and रोगिता sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोज|सरोजं|सरोजः
सरोज n. (-जं) A lotus.<BR>	 m. (-जः) A foot of six long instants, (in Prosody.)<BR>E. सरस् a pond, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजन्मन्
सरोजन्मन् n. (-न्म) A lotus.<BR> E. सरस् a pond, जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजल
सरोजल n. (-लं) The water of a pond or lake.<BR> E. सरस् a pond, जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजिन्
सरोजिन् m. (-जी) BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 f. (-जिनी)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. A pond abounding<BR>in lotuses.<BR>	 3. A multitude of lotuses.<BR> E. सरोज a lotus, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोत्सव|सरोत्सवः
सरोत्सव m. (-वः) The Indian crane.<BR> E. सर water, उत्सव pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोध|सरोधः
सरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Loss, destruction.<BR>	 2. Opposition, obstruction.<BR> E. स for<BR>सह with, रोध hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोरुह्
सरोरुह् n. (-रुट्) A lotus.<BR> E. सरस् a pond, रुह् what grows; also with a final vowel सरोरुह n. (-हं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोरुहासन|सरोरुहासनः
सरोरुहासन m. (-नः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. सरोरुह a lotus, and आसन a seat; first<BR>appearing from the interior of a lotus in order to create the world;<BR>the flower is supposed to have sprung from the navel of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोवर|सरोवरः
सरोवर m. (-रः) A lake or large pond, any piece of water deep enough<BR>for the lotus to grow.<BR> E. सरस् a pool, वर best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोष
सरोष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं) Angry, wrathful.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-षं) Angrily.<BR> E. स with, रोष wrath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्क|सर्कः
सर्क m. (-र्कः)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. The mind.<BR> E. सृ to go, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ग|सर्गः
सर्ग m. (-र्गः)<BR>	 1. Nature, natural property or disposition.<BR>	 2. Tendency of<BR>a thing.<BR>	 3. Creation.<BR>	 4. Effort, perseverance.<BR>	 5. Assent, agreement.<BR>6. Relinquishment, abandoning, letting go or getting rid of.<BR>	 7.<BR>Voiding, as excrement.<BR>	 8. A chapter, a book, a section.<BR>	 9. Cer-<BR>tainty, ascertainment.<BR>	 10. Resolution, determination.<BR>	 11. Loss of<BR>consciousness, fainting.<BR>	 12. Nature, universe.<BR>	 12. Onset, advance,<BR>rush.<BR> E. सृज् to quit, &c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्गक्रम|सर्गक्रमः
सर्गक्रम m. (-मः) The order of creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्गबन्ध|सर्गबंध|सर्गबन्धः
सर्गबन्ध m. (-न्धः) A principal or great poem, one comprising many<BR>Sargas or Cantos.<BR> E. सर्ग a section, and बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्ज्|सर्ज्
सर्ज्ज् r. 1st cl. (सर्ज्जति) To gain or get, to earn by labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्ज|सर्ज|सर्जः|सर्ज्जः
सर्ज्ज m. (-र्ज्जः)<BR>	 1. The Sāl tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR>	 2. Another tree,<BR>(Pentaptera arjuna.)<BR>	 3. The resinous exudation of the Sāl tree. E.<BR>सृज् to quit, aff. अच्, and the final consonant unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जक|सर्जक|सर्जकः|सर्ज्जकः
सर्ज्जक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The Pentaptera arjuna.<BR>	 2. The Sāl tree.<BR>	 f. (-र्ज्जिका)<BR>1. Natron, alkali.<BR>	 2. Borax.<BR> E. सृज् to quit, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जगन्धा|सर्जगन्धा
सर्ज्जगन्धा f. (-न्धा) A plant, commonly Rāsnā, supposed to be the<BR>serpent Ophioxylon.<BR> E. सर्ज्ज the Sāl tree, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जन|सर्जन|सर्जनं|सर्ज्जनं
सर्ज्जन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The reserve or rear of an army.<BR>	 2. Abandoning,<BR>quitting.<BR>	 3. Voiding, as excrement.<BR>	 4. Making, creating.<BR> E. सृज् to<BR>abandon, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जमणि|सर्जमणि|सर्जमणिः|सर्ज्जमणिः
सर्ज्जमणि m. (-णिः) Resin in general, or the resinous exudation of the<BR>Śāl tree.<BR> E. सर्ज्ज the Śāl, and मणि a jewel. “धुना” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जरस|सर्जरस|सर्जरसः|सर्ज्जरसः
सर्ज्जरस m. (-सः) Resin in general, or the resinous exudation of the Sāl<BR>tree.<BR> E. सर्ज्ज the Sāl, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जि|सर्जि|सर्जिः|सर्ज्जिः
सर्ज्जि f. (-र्ज्जिः or र्ज्जी) Natron, alkali.<BR> E. सृज् to abandon, इन् or ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जिका|सर्जिका
सर्ज्जिका f. (-का) Natron, alkali, or the impure carbonate of soda,<BR>commonly termed Sājimāti, and used in India as a soap for<BR>cleaning linen, &c.<BR> E. सर्ज्जि the same, and कन् added, fem form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जिकाक्षार|सर्जिकाक्षार|सर्जिकाक्षारः|सर्ज्जिकाक्षारः
सर्ज्जिकाक्षार m. (-रः) Impure carbonate of soda, alkali, natron. E.<BR>सर्ज्जिका the same, and क्षार ashes; also स्वर्ज्जिकाक्षार । “साजिमाटि” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्जू|सर्जू
सर्ज्जू m. (-र्ज्जूः) A trader.<BR>	 f. (-र्ज्जूः)<BR>	 1. Lightning.<BR>	 2. A necklace.<BR>	 3.<BR>Going, following.<BR> E. सर्ज्ज् to gain, Unādi aff. ऊ; also सर्ज्जु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्प|सर्पः
सर्प m. (-र्पः)<BR>	 1. A snake, a serpent.<BR>	 2. Gentle or twining motion,<BR>gliding, flowing, creeping.<BR>	 f. (-र्पी) The female of the snake.<BR> E. सृप्<BR>to go, to glide, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पकङ्काली
सर्पकङ्काली f. (-ली) A plant, commonly SĀMP-KANKĀLI or serpent's<BR>skeleton.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, कङ्काल a skeleton, fem. aff. of diminutive-<BR>ness or comparison, ङीष्; also with कन् added सर्पकङ्कालिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पगन्धा
सर्पगन्धा f. (-न्धा) A plant, perhaps the same as the serpent ophioxylon.<BR>E. सर्प a snake, and गन्ध fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पघातिनी
सर्पघातिनी f. (-नी) A plant: see सर्पकङ्काली.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, and घातिनी destructress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पच्छत्र|सर्पछत्र|सर्प्पछत्र
सर्पच्छत्र n. (-त्रं) A mushroom.<BR> E. सर्प, and छत्र an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पण|सर्पणं|सर्प्पण
सर्पण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Going, gliding.<BR>	 2. The slow flight of an arrow nearly<BR>parallel to the ground.<BR> E. सृप् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पत्|सर्प्पत्
सर्पत् mfn. (-र्पन्-र्पन्ती-र्पत्) Going, gliding, creeping.<BR> E. सृप् to go, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पतृण|सर्पतृणः
सर्पतृण m. (-णः) An ichneumon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पदंष्ट्र|सर्पदंष्ट्रः
सर्पदंष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>	 1. A snake's tooth.<BR>	 2. A plant, commonly Danti, (Croton<BR>polyandrum.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्ट्रा) A plant, (Tragia involucrata.)<BR> E. सर्प, दंष्ट्र a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पफण
सर्पफण(णि)ज m. (-जः) The snake-stone, a gem or pearl said to resemble<BR>in form the berry of the Abrus precatorius, and to be found in<BR>the head of the snake.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, फण hood, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पभुज्
सर्पभुज् m. (-भुक्)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2. A crane.<BR>	 3. A large snake.<BR> E. सर्प a<BR>snake, भुज who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पमणि|सर्पमणिः
सर्पमणि m. (-णिः) The snake-stone or carbuncle, or a jewel said to be<BR>found in the head of a snake, possessing also alexipharmic proper-<BR>ties.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पमाला
सर्पमाला f. (-ला) A plant, commonly SARPA-KANKĀLI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पराज|सर्पराजः
सर्पराज m. (-जः) VĀSUKI, sovereign of the serpent race, inhabiting<BR>Pātāla or the regions under the earth.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, राज a sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पसत्रिन्
सर्पसत्रिन् m. (-त्री) A name of the prince JANAMEJAYA, the son of<BR>PARIKSHIT.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, and सत्र a sacrifice, इनि aff.; having<BR>compelled by Mantras all the snakes to be present at a sacrifice<BR>performed for their destruction, in retaliation of the death of his<BR>father who was killed by the bite of a snake; all were destroyed<BR>on this occasion except a few of the chiefs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पसहा
सर्पसहा f. (-हा) A plant: see सर्पकङ्काली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पहन्
सर्पहन् m. (-हा) An ichneumon, a mungoose.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, हन् who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पाक्ष|सर्पाक्षं
सर्पाक्ष n. (-क्षं) The seed of the Elæocarpus.<BR>	 f. (-क्षी) A plant, commonly<BR>Kankālikā.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पाख्य|सर्पाख्यः
सर्पाख्य m. (-ख्यः) A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR> E. सर्प a snake, आख्या an appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पाङ्गी
सर्पाङ्गी f. (-ङ्गी) A plant, Sarpa-kankāli or a variety of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पाराति|सर्पारातिः
सर्पाराति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. GARUḌA.<BR>	 2. An ichneumon.<BR>	 3. A peacock.<BR> E. सर्प<BR>a snake, अराति an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पारि|सर्पारिः
सर्पारि m. (-रिः) An ichneumon.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, and अरि an enemy;<BR>equally applicable to the peacock, &c.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पावास|सर्पावासं|सर्पावासः
सर्पावास n. (-सं) The sandal tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पाशन|सर्पाशनः
सर्पाशन m. (-नः) A peacock.<BR> E. सर्प a snake and अशन food: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिन्
सर्पिन् mfn. (-र्पी-र्पिणी-र्पि) Going gently or tortuously, gliding, winding,<BR>creeping.<BR>	 f. (-र्पिणी)<BR>	 1. A female serpent.<BR>	 2. A small medicinal<BR>shrub.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, or going, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिष्मत्|सर्पिष्मन्त्
सर्पिष्मत् Adj. Seasoned with clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिस्
सर्पिस् n. (-र्पिः) Ghee, clarified butter.<BR> E. सृप् to flow, इस् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिस्समुद्र
सर्पिस्समुद्र m. (-द्रः) The sea of clarified butter, one of the seven seas. E.<BR>सर्पिस् Ghee, समुद्र the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पेष्ट|सर्पेष्टं
सर्पेष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ब्ब्|सर्ब्
सर्ब्ब् r. 1st cl. (सर्ब्बति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ब्ब|सर्ब
सर्ब्ब mfn. (-र्ब्बः-र्ब्बा-र्ब्बं) All, whole, entire.<BR> E. षर्ब्ब् to go, aff. अच्; as<BR>differently read, with a final semivowel, सर्व्वं q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ब्बंसह
सर्ब्बंसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Patient, enduring.<BR>	 2. All-sustaining.<BR> E. सर्ब्ब<BR>all, सह to bear, खच् aff.; see सर्व्वंसह below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्म्म|सर्म|सर्मः
सर्म्म m. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Sky, heaven.<BR>	 2. Going, motion.<BR> E. सृ to go, मन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्व्|सर्व्
सर्व्व् r. 1st cl. (सर्व्वति) To hurt, to injure, to kill; more commonly<BR>षर्व्व q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्व|सर्व|सर्वः|सर्व्वः
सर्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वा-र्व्वं) All, whole, complete, universal, entire.<BR>	 m. (-र्व्वः)<BR>1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सृ to go, to pervade, (the world,) वन् Unādi<BR>aff.; also according to some authorities preferable, सर्ब्ब as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वंसह|सर्वंसह
सर्व्वंसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Patient, enduring.<BR>	 2. All-sustaining.<BR>	 f. (-हा)<BR>The earth.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, (men,) सह् to bear or suffer, aff. खश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वक|सर्वक|सर्व्वकः
सर्व्वक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) All, every.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकर्त्तृ|सर्वकर्तृ|सर्वकर्त्तृ
सर्व्वकर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, (things,) कर्त्तृ maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकर्म्मन्|सर्वकर्मन्
सर्व्वकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) All or every act.<BR>	 m. (-र्म्मा) A man of all work.<BR> E. सर्व्व, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकर्म्मीण|सर्वकर्मीण|सर्व्वकर्म्मीणः
सर्व्वकर्म्मीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Performing or conversant with every business,<BR>pervading every action, &c.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, कर्म्म act, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकारिन्|सर्वकारिन्
सर्व्वकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) The maker of all things.<BR> E. सर्व्व, कारिन् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकाल|सर्वकाल
सर्व्वकाल n. (-लं) All seasons or times.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकालीन|सर्वकालीन
सर्व्वकालीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Of all times or seasons.<BR> E. सर्व्वकाल, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वके|सर्वके
सर्व्वके Ind. Every where, universally.<BR> E. सर्व्व in all, and अकच् inserted<BR>before the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वकेशिन्|सर्वकेशिन्
सर्व्वकेशिन् m. (-शी) An actor, a dancer, a mime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वचार
सर्व्वचार m. (-रः) Any substance of an alkaline or soapy naure, as impure<BR>soda, pearl ash or potash, &c., which may be used in cleaning<BR>clothes.<BR> E. सर्व्व all क्षार impure alkali or alkaline salt or ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वग|सर्वग|सर्वगः|सर्व्वगं|सर्व्वगः
सर्व्वग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Going every where, all-pervading.<BR>	 n. (-गं) Water.<BR>m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. Soul, spirit.<BR>	 4. Air, wind.<BR>	 f. (-गा)<BR>A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, ग what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वगत|सर्वगत
सर्व्वगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Omnipresent, universally diffused.<BR> E. सर्व्व, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वगन्ध|सर्वगन्ध|सर्व्वगन्धं
सर्व्वगन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. A class of four aromatics, or kakkol, cloves, agallo-<BR>chum, and gum benjamin.<BR>	 2. A perfume in general.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, and<BR>गन्ध fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वग्रन्थिक|सर्वग्रन्थिक|सर्व्वग्रन्थिकं
सर्व्वग्रन्थिक n. (-कं) The root of long-pepper.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, ग्रन्थि a knot, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वङ्कष|सर्वङ्कष|सर्वंकषः
सर्व्वङ्कष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. All-pervading, diffused, extended.<BR>	 2. All-destroy-<BR>ing.<BR>	 m. (-षः) A rogue, a wicked man.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and कष् to go, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वचर्म्मीण|सर्वचर्मीण|सर्व्वचर्म्मीणः
सर्व्वचर्म्मीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Made of every kind of skin or leather.<BR> E. सर्व्व<BR>all, चर्म्म skin, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वजगत्|सर्वजगत्
सर्व्वजगत् f. (-त्) The universe, the whole world.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and जगत् world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वजनीन|सर्वजनीन|सर्व्वजनीनः
सर्व्वजनीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Belonging or relating to all men, fit for all,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, जन mankind, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वजित्|सर्वजित्
सर्व्वजित् mfn. (-जित्)<BR>	 1. All-subduing, irresistible.<BR>	 2. All-surpassing,<BR>excellent, incomparable.<BR>	 m. (-जित) The twenty-first year of the<BR>cycle.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, जित् who subdues or surpasses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वज्ञ|सर्वज्ञ|सर्व्वज्ञः
सर्व्वज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Omniscient, all-wise.<BR>	 m. (-ज्ञः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A Jina<BR>or Buddha, or deified sage peculiar to those sects.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, and<BR>ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वज्ञत्व|सर्वज्ञत्व
सर्व्वज्ञत्व n. (-त्वं) Omniscience.<BR> E. त्व added to the last; also with तल्, सर्व्वज्ञता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतःशुभा|सर्वतःशुभा
सर्व्वतःशुभा f. (-भा) A plant, (Priyangu.)<BR> E. सर्व्वतस् wholly, शुभ auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतन्त्र|सर्वतन्त्र|सर्वतन्त्रः|सर्व्वतन्त्रः
सर्व्वतन्त्र m. (-न्त्रः) A man who has studied the Tantra-Shāstras.<BR> E. सर्व्व all,<BR>तन्त्र a Tantra, properly with an affix of derivation, &c., as ठक्, and<BR>that again rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतस्|सर्वतस्
सर्व्वतस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Every way, all-round.<BR>	 2. Wholly, entirely.<BR>	 3. From<BR>every body.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतापन|सर्वतापन|सर्वतापनः|सर्व्वतापनः
सर्व्वतापन m. (-नः) Love or the deity KĀMA.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, तापन inflamer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतेजस्|सर्वतेजस्
सर्व्वतेजस् n. (-जः) All-splendour or power.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and तेजस् light, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतेजोमय|सर्वतेजोमय
सर्व्वतेजोमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made, comprising or consisting of all<BR>splendour or power.<BR> E. सर्व्वतेजस्, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतोभद्र|सर्वतोभद्र|सर्वतोभद्रः|सर्व्वतोभद्रं|सर्व्वतोभद्रः
सर्व्वतोभद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं) Every where auspicious.<BR>	 mn. (-द्रः-द्रं) A temple<BR>or palace of a square form, with an entrance opposed to each<BR>point of the compass.<BR>	 m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. The Nimba-tree, (Melia<BR>azadirachta.)<BR>	 2. The carriage of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A bamboo.<BR>	 4. A form<BR>of military array.<BR>	 5. A square mystical diagram, to be painted on<BR>the cloth which on particular occasions covers a sort of altar<BR>erected to VIṢṆU.<BR>	 6. A kind of charade, in which the same word<BR>answers several questions.<BR>	 7. A whimsical form of verse, so con-<BR>trived that the sams meanings and words occur, whether the<BR>line be read back-wards or forwards, or in several other directions.<BR>f. (-द्रा)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR>	 2. An actress or the wife of<BR>an actor or dancer, &c.<BR>	 3. A sort of yam, (Dioscorea.)<BR> E. सर्व्वतस्<BR>on every side, भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वतोमुख|सर्वतोमुख|सर्वतोमुखः|सर्व्वतोमुखं|सर्व्वतोमुखः
सर्व्वतोमुख n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Sky, heaven.<BR>	 m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>3. Soul, spirit.<BR>	 4. A Brāhman.<BR>	 5. Svarga, the heaven of INDRA.<BR>6. Agni.<BR> E. सर्व्वतस् on every side, मुख countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वत्र|सर्वत्र
सर्व्वत्र Ind.<BR>	 1. Every where, in all places.<BR>	 2. Always, at all times. र्व्व<BR> E. स all, त्रल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वत्रग|सर्वत्रग|सर्वत्रगः|सर्व्वत्रगः
सर्व्वत्रग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) All-pervading, going every where.<BR>	 m. (-गः) Air,<BR>wind.<BR> E. सर्व्वत्र every where, गम् to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वत्रगामिन्|सर्वत्रगामिन्
सर्व्वत्रगामिन् m. (-मी) Air, wind.<BR> E. सर्व्वत्र always, गामिन् going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वथा|सर्वथा
सर्व्वथा Ind.<BR>	 f. (-था)<BR>	 1. In all ways, by all means.<BR>	 2. Assuredly,<BR>certainly.<BR>	 3. Exceeding, mostly.<BR>	 4. Always.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, थाल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदमन|सर्वदमन|सर्व्वदमनः
सर्व्वदमन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) All-subduing, irresistible.<BR>	 m. (-नः) BHARATA,<BR>the son of ŚAKUNTALĀ.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, दमन taming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदर्शिन्|सर्वदर्शिन्
सर्व्वदर्शिन् mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि) All-seeing.<BR>	 m. (-र्शी) A Buddha in general.<BR>E. सर्व्व all, and दर्शिन् seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदा|सर्वदा
सर्व्वदा Ind. Always, at all times.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, and दाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदुःखक्षय|सर्वदुःखक्षय|सर्वदुःखक्षयः|सर्व्वदुःखक्षयः
सर्व्वदुःखक्षय m. (-यः) Final emancipation from transmigration.<BR> E. सर्व्व all,<BR>दुःख pain, and क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदेवमय|सर्वदेवमय|सर्वदेवमयः
सर्व्वदेवमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of or comprising all the gods.<BR> E. सर्व्वदेव, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वदेवमुख|सर्वदेवमुख|सर्वदेवमुखः|सर्व्वदेवमुखः
सर्व्वदेवमुख m. (-खः) A name of AGNI or fire.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, देव a deity, and<BR>मुख mouth; being the medium of oblations to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वधन|सर्वधन
सर्व्वधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Whole wealth or property.<BR>	 2. (In arithmetic,) Total<BR>of a sum in progression.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वधर्म्मविद्|सर्वधर्मविद्
सर्व्वधर्म्मविद् m. (-विद् or वित्) One who knows the duties of all tribes and<BR>classes.<BR> E. सर्व्व, धर्म्म duty, विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वधारी|सर्वधारी
सर्व्वधारी f. (-री) The twenty-second year of the cycle.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, धृ to<BR>hold, अण् and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वधुरावह|सर्वधुरावह|सर्व्वधुरावहः
सर्व्वधुरावह m. (-हः) An ox fit for any sorts of carriage.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, धुर a<BR>burden, आङ् before वह् to bear, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वधुरीण|सर्वधुरीण|सर्वधुरीणः|सर्व्वधुरीणः
सर्व्वधुरीण m. (-णः) An ox, &c. fit for any carriage or draught.<BR> E. सर्व्व all,<BR>धुर a burden, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वनामता|सर्वनामता
सर्व्वनामता f. (-ता) The quality or condition of a pronoun.<BR> E. सर्व्वनाम and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वनामन्|सर्वनामन्
सर्व्वनामन् n. (-म) A pronoun.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and नामन् name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वनाश|सर्वनाश
सर्व्वनाश m. (-शः) Total destruction, destruction of all.<BR> E. सर्व्व, नाश destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वन्दम|सर्वन्दम|सर्वंदमः|सर्व्वन्दमः
सर्व्वन्दम m. (-मः) BHARATA.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, दम् to tame or subdue, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वपथ|सर्वपथ
सर्व्वपथ m. (-थः) Every way, every direction. सर्व्व, पथ for पथिन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वपथीन|सर्वपथीन
सर्व्वपथीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) In or of every road or direction, (moving,<BR>passing, &c.)<BR> E. सर्व्वपथ, and ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वपा|सर्वपा
सर्व्वपा f. (-पा) The wife of the Daitya BALI.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, पा to drink, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वपूर्णत्व|सर्वपूर्णत्व|सर्वपूर्णत्वं|सर्व्वपूर्णत्वं|सर्व्वपूर्ण्णत्व
सर्व्वपूर्णत्व n. (-त्वं) Entire completion or fulness, complete preparation<BR>or provision.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, and पूर्णत्व fulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वप्रिय|सर्वप्रिय|सर्व्वप्रियः
सर्व्वप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Generally or universally beloved.<BR>	 2.<BR>Generally friendly, loving all.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, and प्रिय dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभक्ष|सर्वभक्ष|सर्वभक्षः
सर्व्वभक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Omnivorous, eating all or any thing.<BR>	 f. (-क्षा) A<BR>female goat.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, and भक्ष who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभक्ष्य|सर्वभक्ष्य
सर्व्वभक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Eating any thing or all things, (a child.)<BR>2. All-devouring, omnivorous.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and भक्ष्य edible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभाव|सर्वभाव|सर्वभावः
सर्व्वभाव m. (-वः) Whole disposition, all one's thoughts and purpose. E.<BR>सर्व्व, and भाव disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभूत|सर्वभूत
सर्व्वभूत n. Plu. (-तानि)<BR>	 1. All the elements.<BR>	 2. All created things.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, भूत an element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभूतकृत्|सर्वभूतकृत्
सर्व्वभूतकृत् mn. (-कृत्)<BR>	 1. The maker of all things.<BR>	 2. The cause of all<BR>elements or beings.<BR> E. सर्व्वभूत, and कृत् who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभूतमय|सर्वभूतमय
सर्व्वभूतमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Comprising or comprehending all elementary<BR>matter.<BR>	 m. (-यः) The supreme pervading spirit.<BR> E. सर्व्वभूत, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभूतस्थ|सर्वभूतस्थ
सर्व्वभूतस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Present in all elements or beings.<BR> E. सर्व्व<BR>all, भूत an element, and स्थ what stays; also सर्व्वभूतस्थित, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभूतात्मन्|सर्वभूतात्मन्
सर्व्वभूतात्मन् m. (-त्मा) Universal, all-pervading spirit.<BR> E. सर्व्वभूत an<BR>element, and आत्मन् soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभृत्|सर्वभृत्
सर्व्वभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Cherishing or supporting all.<BR> E. सर्व्व, भृत् who or what supports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभोगिन्|सर्वभोगिन्
सर्व्वभोगिन् mfn. (-गी-गिणी-गि) Enjoying all.<BR> E. सर्व्व, भोगिन् who enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वभोगीण|सर्वभोगीण
सर्व्वभोगीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Good or beneficial for all, to be enjoyed or<BR>possessed by all.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and भोग enjoyment, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वमङ्गला|सर्वमङ्गला|सर्वमंगला
सर्व्वमङ्गला f. (-ला) DURGĀ.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, मङ्गल auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वमय|सर्वमय|सर्व्वमयः
सर्व्वमय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) General, universal, comprehensive, comprehen-<BR>ding.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वमही|सर्वमही
सर्व्वमही f. (-ही) The whole earth.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and मही earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वमूल्य|सर्वमूल्य|सर्व्वमूल्यं
सर्व्वमूल्य n. (-ल्यं) A Cowrie or small coin represented by it.<BR> E. सर्व्व all,<BR>(of all things,) मूल्य price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वमूषक|सर्वमूषक|सर्वमूषकः|सर्व्वमूषकः
सर्व्वमूषक m. (-कः) Time.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, (things,) मूष् to steal, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वरस|सर्वरस|सर्वरसः|सर्व्वरसः
सर्व्वरस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Resin, the exudation of the pine or Sāl.<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>of musical instrument, a kind of lute.<BR>	 3. A learned man.<BR>	 4. Saltness,<BR>salt, saline flavour or taste.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, रस taste, real or figurative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वरसोत्तम|सर्वरसोत्तम|सर्व्वरसोत्तमः
सर्व्वरसोत्तम m. (-मः) The saline flavour, saltness, salt.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, रस a<BR>flavour, उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वरात्र|सर्वरात्र|सर्व्वरात्रः
सर्व्वरात्र m. (-त्रः) The whole night.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, रात्रि night, अच् substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वरीकर
सर्व्वरीकर m. (-रः) The moon.<BR> E. सर्व्वरी for शर्व्वरी night, कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वर्त्तिका
सर्व्वर्त्तिका f. (-का) A plant, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वर्त्तुपरिवर्त्त|सर्वर्तुपरिवर्त|सर्वर्तुपरिवर्तः|सर्वर्त्तुपरिवर्त्त|सर्व्वर्त्तुपरिवर्त्तः
सर्व्वर्त्तुपरिवर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A year.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, ऋतु a season, परिवर्त्त a revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वला|सर्वला
सर्व्वला f. (-ला) An iron club. “तोमरास्त्रे”<BR> E. सर्व्व all, ला to take, affs. अङ्<BR>and टाप्; also read शर्व्वला and सर्व्वली ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वलिङ्गिन्|सर्वलिङ्गिन्|सर्वलिंगिन्
सर्व्वलिङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी) A heretic, an impostor; one who not belonging to<BR>the orthodox faith, wears the dress, and assumes the character<BR>of an ascetic.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, लिङ्क mark, (of sect or caste,) इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वलोक|सर्वलोक|सर्वलोकः
सर्व्वलोक m. (-कः) The universe.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वलोह|सर्वलोह|सर्वलोहः|सर्व्वलोहः
सर्व्वलोह m. (-हः) An iron arrow.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववल्लभा|सर्ववल्लभा
सर्व्ववल्लभा f. (-भा) A disloyal or unchaste woman.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, and वल्लभा a mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वविद्|सर्वविद्
सर्व्वविद् mfn. (-वित्) Omniscient, all-wise.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and विद् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववेद|सर्ववेद|सर्ववेदः|सर्व्ववेदः
सर्व्ववेद m. (-दः) A Brāhman who has read the four Vedas.<BR> E. सर्व्व all,<BR>वेद the Veda, and अण् or ठक् aff.; the effects of the aff. being<BR>subsequently rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववेदस्|सर्ववेदस्
सर्व्ववेदस् m. (-दाः) A man who gives away all his property to the<BR>priests who have been employed by him at particular sacrifices, of<BR>which such a destination of the principal's whole wealth is an<BR>essential part.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, विद् to gain, causal form, aff. असुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववेदिन्|सर्ववेदिन्
सर्व्ववेदिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Omniscient.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and वेदिन् who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्ववेशिन्|सर्ववेशिन्
सर्व्ववेशिन् m. (-शी) An actor, a dancer.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, वेश dress, &c. इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वशस्|सर्वशस्
सर्व्वशस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Wholly, universally.<BR>	 2. On all sides.<BR> E. सर्व्व, शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वशान्तिकृत्|सर्वशान्तिकृत्
सर्व्वशान्तिकृत् m. (-कृत्) The sovereign of India. BHARATA.<BR> E. सर्व्व all,<BR>शान्ति tranquillity, and कृत् who effects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वशेष|सर्वशेष
सर्व्वशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. What remains of the whole.<BR>	 2. What is to<BR>continue or to be added to all.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and शेष remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसङ्गत|सर्वसङ्गत|सर्वसंगतः|सर्व्वसङ्गतः
सर्व्वसङ्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) United or meeting with universally.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>A sort of rice of quick growth.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, (by all,) सङ्गत known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसङ्ग्रह|सर्वसङ्ग्रह|सर्वसंग्रहः|सर्व्वसंग्रह
सर्व्वसङ्ग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A general or universal collection.<BR>	 2. Any<BR>collection.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and सङ्ग्रह collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसन्नहन|सर्वसन्नहन
सर्व्वसन्नहन n. (-नं) Assembling a complete army.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, (the parts,<BR>or elephants, chariots, horse, and foot,) सन्नहन arming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसन्नाह|सर्वसन्नाह|सर्वसंनाहः|सर्व्वसन्नाहः
सर्व्वसन्नाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The universal and pervading spirit.<BR>	 2. Arming or<BR>assembling a complete army.<BR> E. सर्व्व, सन्नाह arming, accoutring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसमता|सर्वसमता
सर्व्वसमता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Sameness or identity with all things.<BR>	 2. Equani-<BR>mity, equal regard for all.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and समता sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसह|सर्वसह|सर्वसहः|सर्व्वसहः
सर्व्वसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) All-enduring, bearing all things with patience<BR>and firmness.<BR>	 m. (-हः) Bdellium. “गुग्गुलौ” f. (-हा) The earth.<BR> E. सर्व्व<BR>all, सह् to suffer, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसिद्धार्थ|सर्वसिद्धार्थ
सर्व्वसिद्धार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Having every object attained, every wish<BR>gratified, &c.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and सिद्ध accomplished, अर्थ object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वसिद्धि|सर्वसिद्धि|सर्वसिद्धिः|सर्व्वसिद्धिः
सर्व्वसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Universal success or accomplishment of all.<BR>	 m. (-द्धि.)<BR>A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR> E. सर्व्व all, सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वस्व|सर्वस्व|सर्व्वस्वं
सर्व्वस्व n. (-स्वं)<BR>	 1. Whole property or possessions.<BR>	 2. Substance, whole<BR>essence of anything.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and स्व own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वस्वदण्ड|सर्वस्वदण्ड
सर्व्वस्वदण्ड mfn. (-ण्डः-ण्डा-ण्डं) Fined in all one's property.<BR>	 n. (-ण्डं)<BR>Confiscation of property.<BR> E. सर्व्वस्व, and दण्ड punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वस्वहरण|सर्वस्वहरण
सर्व्वस्वहरण n. (-णं) Confiscation of a whole property.<BR> E. सर्व्वस्व, and हरण<BR>taking; also सर्व्वस्वहार, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वस्वामिन्|सर्वस्वामिन्
सर्व्वस्वामिन् m. (-मी)<BR>	 1. A universal monarch.<BR>	 2. The owner or master<BR>of all.<BR> E. सर्व्व, स्वामिन् a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वहार|सर्वहार|सर्वहारः
सर्व्वहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Total confiscation.<BR>	 2. Seizing the whole.<BR> E. सर्व्व,<BR>हार taking; also सर्व्वहरणं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाङ्ग|सर्वाङ्ग|सर्वाङ्गः|सर्व्वाङ्गं
सर्व्वाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. The whole body.<BR>	 2. The Angas or portions of divine<BR>knowledge collectively.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, अङ्ग a limb, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाङ्गीण|सर्वाङ्गीण|सर्वांगीण|सर्व्वाङ्गीणः
सर्व्वाङ्गीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Spreading throughout the body, diffusive,<BR>pervading.<BR>	 2. Relating or belonging to the Angas, or parts of<BR>science collectively.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, अङ्ग member, स्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाणी|सर्वाणी
सर्व्वाणी f. (-णी) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. सर्व्व ŚIVA, ङीष् aff, and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वात्मक|सर्वात्मक
सर्व्वात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) All-pervading.<BR> E. सर्व्व and आत्मन् self, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वात्मन्|सर्वात्मन्
सर्व्वात्मन् m. (-त्मा)<BR>	 1. The supreme or universal spirit.<BR>	 2. All beings<BR>collectively.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and आत्मन् self or spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वात्मभूति|सर्वात्मभूति
सर्व्वात्मभूति f. (-तिः) All beings collectively.<BR> E. सर्व्वात्म, and भूति being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाधिकार|सर्वाधिकार
सर्व्वाधिकार m. (-रः) General control or superintendance.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and<BR>अधिकार office.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाधिकारिन्|सर्वाधिकारिन्
सर्व्वाधिकारिन् m. (-री) A general or head superintendent.<BR> E. सर्व्वाधिकार, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वानुभूति|सर्वानुभूति|सर्व्वानुभूतिः
सर्व्वानुभूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A Jina of the last era.<BR>	 2. One of the future era.<BR>3. A plant, commonly Teori, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR> E. सर्व्व<BR>all, अनुभूति perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वान्नभक्षक|सर्वान्नभक्षक|सर्व्वान्नभक्षकः
सर्व्वान्नभक्षक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Eating every thing or every where.<BR> E. सर्व्व<BR>all, अन्न food, and भक्षक who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वान्नभोजिन्|सर्वान्नभोजिन्
सर्व्वान्नभोजिन् mfn. (-जी-जिनी-जि) Eating all sorts of food.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, अन्न<BR>food, भुज् to eat, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वान्नीन|सर्वान्नीन|सर्व्वान्नीनः
सर्व्वान्नीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Eating all sorts of food.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, अन्न food, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाभिसन्धक|सर्वाभिसन्धक
सर्व्वाभिसन्धक m. (-कः) A railer, a cynic, one who abuses all.<BR> E. सर्व्व, and<BR>अभिसन्धक who calumniates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाभिसन्धिन्|सर्वाभिसन्धिन्
सर्व्वाभिसन्धिन् m. (-न्धी) A cynic, a calumniator or reviler.<BR> E. सर्व्व all,<BR>अभि and सम् before धा to have, क affix, and इनि possess. added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाभिसार|सर्वाभिसार|सर्वाभिसारः|सर्व्वाभिसारः
सर्व्वाभिसार m. (-रः) Assembling a complete army.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, and अभि<BR>before सृ to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वार्थ|सर्वार्थ
सर्व्वार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Having every object or sense.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-र्थम्)<BR>For or on account of all.<BR>	 m. Plu. (-र्थाः) All objects, &c.<BR> E. सर्व्व,<BR>and अर्थ an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वार्थसिद्ध|सर्वार्थसिद्ध|सर्वार्थसिद्धः|सर्व्वार्थसिद्धः
सर्व्वार्थसिद्ध m. (-द्धः) Buddha, the founder of the Bauddha faith.<BR> E. सर्व्व,<BR>all, अर्थ object, and सिद्ध perfect: his father's wishes being all<BR>fulfilled by his birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वावसर|सर्वावसर|सर्वावसरः|सर्व्वावसरः
सर्व्वावसर m. (-रः) Midnight.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, (things,) अवसर interval or cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाशिन्|सर्वाशिन्
सर्व्वाशिन् mfn. (-शी-शिनी-शि) Eating all things.<BR> E. सर्व्व, अशिन् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाश्रमिन्|सर्वाश्रमिन्
सर्व्वाश्रमिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Belonging or common to every order. E.<BR>सर्व्व, आश्रमिन् belonging to an Āshrama or order of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाश्रय|सर्वाश्रय|सर्वाश्रयः
सर्व्वाश्रय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Giving shelter or protection to all.<BR> E. सर्व्व, आश्रय asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वास्त्रा|सर्वास्त्रा
सर्व्वास्त्रा f. (-स्त्रा) One of the sixteen Vidyā-Devis, or goddesses of<BR>learning, according to the Jainas.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, अस्त्र a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वाह्ण|सर्वाह्ण|सर्व्वाह्णः
सर्व्वाह्ण m. (-ह्णः) The whole day.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वीय|सर्वीय|सर्व्वीयः
सर्व्वीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating or belonging to all, suitable or fit for<BR>all, &c.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वेश|सर्वेश|सर्वेशः
सर्व्वेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Supreme or universal monarch.<BR>	 2. The Supreme Being.<BR> E. सर्व्व, ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वेश्वर|सर्वेश्वर|सर्वेश्वरः|सर्व्वेश्वरः
सर्व्वेश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A universal monarch.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वौघ|सर्वौघ|सर्वौघः|सर्व्वौघः
सर्व्वौघ m. (-घः)<BR>	 1. Assembling a complete army.<BR>	 2. Great speed or<BR>dispatch.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, and ओघ a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वौषधिगण|सर्वौषधिगण|सर्व्वौषधिगणः
सर्व्वौषधिगण m. (-णः) A class of certain principal drugs, consisting of<BR>Murā, Valeriana Jatāmānsi, Orris root, Benzoin, Zedoary, Kurk,<BR>or Costus speciosus, red saunders, and Cyperus.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, औषधि<BR>a drug, and गण a class; also with वर्ग the same, सर्व्वौषधिवर्ग m. (-र्गः) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्वौषधिरस|सर्वौषधिरस
सर्व्वौषधिरस m. (-सः) The juice or infusion of a number of plants as<BR>used at a royal inauguration.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, औषधि herb, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षप|सर्षपः
सर्षप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A sort of mustard, (Sinapis dichotoma.)<BR>	 2. A kind of<BR>poison.<BR>	 3. A small measure of weight, a mustard seed so con-<BR>sidered.<BR>	 f. (-पी) A small bird.<BR> E. सृ to go, अप् Unādi aff, सुक् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षपतैल|सर्षपतैलं
सर्षपतैल n. (-लं) Mustard oil.<BR> E. सर्षप mustard, and तैलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्
सल् r. 1st cl. (सलति) To go, to move; more properly षल् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल|सलं
सल n. (-लं) Water.<BR> E. षल् to go, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलज्ज|सलज्जः
सलज्ज mfn. (-ज्जः-ज्जा-ज्जं) Bashful, modest, ashamed.<BR> E. स with, लज्जा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिल|सलिलं
सलिल n. (-लं) Water.<BR> E. षल् to go, इलच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलकुन्तल|सलिलकुन्तलः
सलिलकुन्तल m. (-लः) An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria octandra.) “शैवाले”<BR>E. सलिल water, and कुन्तल hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलक्रिया
सलिलक्रिया f. (-या) The funeral rite of washing the corpse.<BR> E. सलिल, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलज|सलिलजं
सलिलज n. (-जं) A lotus.<BR> E. सलिल water, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलनिधि|सलिलनिधिः
सलिलनिधि m. (-धिः) The ocean.<BR> E. सलिल, and निधि store.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलरय|सलिलरयः
सलिलरय m. (-यः) Current, stream.<BR> E. सलिल, रय speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलराशि|सलिलराशिः
सलिलराशि m. (-शिः)<BR>	 1. Ocean.<BR>	 2. Any piece of water.<BR> E. सलिल, राशि heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलेन्धन|सलिलेंधन|सलिलेन्धनः
सलिलेन्धन m. (-नः) Submarine fire.<BR> E. सलिल water, and इन्धन inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलील|सलीलः
सलील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Wanton, sportive.<BR> E. स for सह with, लीला sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलोकता
सलोकता f. (-ता) Residence in the same heaven with a particular deity,<BR>(one of the four stages of mukti.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्लकी
सल्लकी f. (-की) The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR> E. सल् to<BR>go, वुन् aff., and the ल doubled; also शल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव|सवं|सवः
सव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>	 2. Offspring, progeny.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>4. The moon.<BR>	 n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. The juice or honey of flowers.<BR>	 3.<BR>Sprinkling the juice of the acid Asclepias.<BR> E. षू to bear, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवन|सवनं
सवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Bathing, as a religious exercise, or preparatory to a sac-<BR>rifice, purificatory ablution in general.<BR>	 2. A sacrifice in general.<BR>3. Extracting and drinking the juice of the acid Asclepias.<BR>	 4.<BR>Bearing as children, bringing forth young.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The moon.<BR> E. ष<BR>to bear young, &c., Unādi aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवपुष
सवपुष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Embodied, having a body or form.<BR> E. स with, वपुस्<BR>body, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवयस्
सवयस् mfn. (-याः-याः-यः) Contemporary, of similar age or duration.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-याः) A friend, a contemporary.<BR>	 f. (-याः) A woman's female friend.<BR>E. स for समान equal, like, and वयस् age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर|सवरः
सवर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. A name of ŚIVA; more properly शवर, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्ण|सवर्णः
सवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Like, resembling.<BR>	 2. Of the same tribe or class.<BR>3. Of the same kind, homogeneous.<BR>	 f. (-र्णा)<BR>	 1. A name of CHHĀYĀ,<BR>one of the wives of the sun.<BR>	 2. Belonging to the same class of<BR>letters, i. e. requiring the same effort in pronunciation.<BR> E. स for<BR>समान like, same, वर्ण tribe, colour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवहा
सवहा f. (-हा) A plant, commonly Teori, (Convolvulus Turpethum;) also read सुवहा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवास
सवास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Scented, perfumed.<BR>	 2. Having a dwelling. E.<BR>स with, वास abode, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवासस्
सवासस् mfn. (-साः-साः-सः) Clothed, dressed.<BR> E. स with, वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकल्पक
सविकल्पक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Admitting of an alternative or choice.<BR>2. Doubtful.<BR>	 f. (-का) Adj. (In Vedānta philosophy,) Recognizing<BR>distinctions: namely those of subject and object, (as opposed to<BR>निर्विकल्प.)<BR> E. स with, विकल्प option, कप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकाश|सविकाशः
सविकाश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Expanded, extended, extensive.<BR>	 2. Budded,<BR>blown.<BR> E. स for सह with, विकाश expansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविग्रह
सविग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Embodied, having body or form.<BR>	 2. Having,<BR>meaning, importing.<BR>	 3. Quarrelling.<BR> E. स with, विग्रह body, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितर्कम्
सवितर्कम् Ind. Thoughtfully, with reasoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृ
सवितृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Indra.<BR>	 3. Śiva.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) Adj. Producer,<BR>giver.<BR> E. सु to send or cast, (his rays,) तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृदैवत|सवितृदैवतः
सवितृदैवत m. (-तः) The constellation HASTĀ, the thirteenth of the lunar<BR>asterisms.<BR> E. सवितृ the sun, and दैवत godhead; the sun being the<BR>ruling deity of this asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृल|सवितृलः
सवितृल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Belonging or relating to the sun.<BR> E. सवितृ the sun, and ल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्र|सवित्रं
सवित्र n. (-त्रं) Cause or instrument of production or generation.<BR> E. षू<BR>to bear, aff. इत्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्रिय|सवित्रियः
सवित्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating or belonging to the sun.<BR> E. सवितृ the sun, घ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्री
सवित्री f. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. A mother.<BR>	 2. A cow.<BR> E. षू to bring forth young, तृच्<BR>aff., ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविद्य
सविद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Learned, wise, versed in science.<BR> E. स with, विद्या knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविध|सविधः
सविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. Of the same kind.<BR>	 n. (-धं)<BR>Proximity.<BR> E. स for समान common, same, विध manner, sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविनय
सविनय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Modest, well-behaved.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Modestly, respect-<BR>fully.<BR> E. स with, विनय propriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविलास
सविलास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Wanton, sportive.<BR> E. स with, विलास sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेष
सविशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. Excellent, superior.<BR>	 2. Having characteristic<BR>qualities.<BR>	 3. Discriminative.<BR>	 4. Peculiar.<BR> E. स with, विशेष excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषण
सविशेषण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Distinguished, marked, individualised by<BR>marks or properties.<BR> E. स with, विशेषण distinguishing property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषतस्
सविशेषतस् Ind. Particularly, excellently.<BR> E. स with, विशेषतस् especially.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविस्मय|सविस्मयः
सविस्मय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Astonished, surprised.<BR> E. स for सह with, विस्मय<BR>astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवृद्धिक
सवृद्धिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Bearing interest.<BR> E. स with, वृद्धि interest, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवेश|सवेशः
सवेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. Ornamented decorated. E.<BR>स for समान common, or सह with, and वेश entrance, decoration, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवेष
सवेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. Near, proximate.<BR>	 2. Decorated, dressed.<BR> E. स<BR>for सह with, &c., and वेष entrance or decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्य|सव्यः
सव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Left, left hand.<BR>	 2. Right, right hand.<BR>	 3.<BR>South, southern.<BR>	 4. Reverse, contrary, backward.<BR>	 m. (-व्यः) VIṢṆU.<BR>E. सू to send, यत् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यथ
सव्यथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Suffering pain.<BR> E. स with, व्यथा pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यपेक्ष
सव्यपेक्ष f. (-क्षा) Having connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यभिचार|सव्यभिचारः
सव्यभिचार m. (-रः) A reason or argument that is locally incompatible<BR>with the conclusion to be drawn from it; a HETU that is too<BR>general, (in logic.)<BR> E. स with, व्यभिचार irrelevancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यसाचिन्
सव्यसाचिन् m. (-ची) A name of ARJUNA.<BR> E. सव्य left, षच् to be joined or<BR>attached, aff. णिनि; drawing the bow with his left hand, as well<BR>as his right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्याज
सव्याज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Cunning, plausible, pretending.<BR>	 2. Fraudu-<BR>lent.<BR> E. स with, व्याज pretext.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येष्ठ|सव्येष्ठः
सव्येष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) A charioteer.<BR> E. सव्ये on the left, and स्थ who stands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येष्ठृ
सव्येष्ठृ m. (-ष्ठा) A charioteer.<BR> E. सव्ये on the left, स्था to stand, ऋन्<BR>Unādi aff., with the effect of ड; स and थ changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्रीड
सव्रीड mfn. (-डः-डा-डं) Modest, ashamed.<BR> E. स with, व्रीडा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशङ्क
सशङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Fearful, doubtful.<BR> E. स with, शङ्का fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशल्क|सशल्कः
सशल्क mfn. (-ल्कः-ल्का-ल्कं) Scaly, (as a fish, &c.)<BR> E. स, and शल्क scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशल्य
सशल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Troublesome, difficult.<BR>	 2. Pierced by a thorn<BR>or dart.<BR> E. स with, शल्य a thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशूक|सशूकः
सशूक m. (-कः) A believer, one who believes the existence of GOD, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशोक
सशोक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Sorrowful, sad.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-कं) Sorrowfully.<BR> E. स<BR>with, शोक sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्मश्रु|सश्मश्रुः
सश्मश्रु f. (-श्रुः) A woman with a beard.<BR> E. स for सह with, श्मश्रु a beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्रम
सश्रम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Wearied, fatigued.<BR> E. स with, श्रम fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्रोक
सश्रोक f. (-का) Having prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्
सस् r. 2nd cl. (सस्ति) To sleep; also षस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंशय
ससंशय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Doubtful, uncertain.<BR> E. स with, संशय doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससत्व
ससत्व f. (-त्वा)<BR>	 1. Pregnant.<BR>	 2. Possessing energy or vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससत्वा
ससत्वा f. (-त्वा) A pregnant woman.<BR> E. स for सह with, सत्व a living being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससन|ससनं
ससन n. (-नं) Immolation, offering a living victim.<BR> E. सस् to sleep, &c.,<BR>aff. ल्युट्; also शसन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससम्पद
ससम्पद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Happy, delighted.<BR> E. स with, सम्पद pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससाध्वस
ससाध्वस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Frightened, alarmed.<BR> E. स with, साध्वस fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससौष्ठव
ससौष्ठव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं)<BR>	 1. Quick, fleet.<BR>	 2. Excellent.<BR> E. स with, सौष्ठव<BR>speed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्तर
सस्तर m. (-रः) A bed of leaves, &c.<BR> E. स for समान common, स्तर spreading, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्पृह
सस्पृह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Desirous, wishing for.<BR> E. स with, स्पृहा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्मित|सस्मितः
सस्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Smiling, laughing.<BR> E. स for सह with, स्मित a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्य|सस्यं
सस्य n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Fruit.<BR>	 2. Corn, grain.<BR>	 3. A weapon.<BR>	 4. A quality, an<BR>excellence.<BR> E. सस् to sleep, यत् Unādi aff; also शस्य, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यक|सस्यकः
सस्यक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sort of precious stone, described as of the colour<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">Page776-b+ 60</a>]<BR>of the inner fruit of the cocoanut.<BR>	 2. A sword.<BR>	 f. (-का) Adj.<BR>Possessed of good qualities.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यमारिन्
सस्यमारिन् Adj. Corn-destroying.<BR>	 m. (-रीः) A kind of rat or mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यसंवर|सस्यसंवरः
सस्यसंवर m. (-रः) The Śal tree, (Shorea robusta.)<BR> E. सस्य fruit, संवर<BR>a covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्याद्
सस्याद् mfn. (-द्) Fructivorous, granivorous, eating grain or fruit. E.<BR>सस्य, अद् to eat, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्येष्टि|सस्येष्टिः
सस्येष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Sacrifice offered on the ripening of new grain.<BR> E. सस्य, इष्टि sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्वेद
सस्वेद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Perspiring, exuding.<BR>	 f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. A virgin deflowered.<BR>2. A girl who has committed a breach of chastity.<BR> E. स with,<BR>स्वेद perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्त्रि
सस्त्रि mfn. (-स्त्रिः-स्त्रिः-स्त्रि) Who or what goes.<BR> E. सृ to go, इ aff., v. redup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह|सहं|सहः
सह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Patient, enduring, suffering, bearing.<BR>	 m. (-हः) The<BR>month Agrahāyaṇa.<BR>	 mn. (-हः-हं) Strength, power.<BR>	 f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. The<BR>earth.<BR>	 2. The Aloe plant.<BR>	 3. A sort of bean, commonly Mudga-<BR>parni.<BR>	 4. A drug, commonly Nakhi.<BR>	 5. A plant; also Daṇḍotpalā.<BR>6. Barleria, (the white sort.)<BR>	 7. The ichneumon plant or Rāsnā.<BR>8. A medicinal sort of moon plant. Ind.<BR>	 1. With, together with;<BR>a particle implying association, connection.<BR>	 2. Union, junction.<BR>	 3.<BR>Increase, addition.<BR>	 4. Presence, present time.<BR>	 5. Completeness,<BR>entireness.<BR>	 6. Resemblance, &c.<BR>	 7. Simultaneously.<BR> E. षह् to have<BR>patience, aff. अच्, fem. aff. टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकार|सहकारः
सहकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A fragrant sort of mango.<BR>	 2. Co-operation.<BR> E. सह<BR>with, कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकारिता
सहकारिता f. (-ता) Co-operation, assistance.<BR> E. सहकारिन् and तल् aff.; also सहकारित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकारिन्
सहकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) An implement, an assistant or associate,<BR>that or who, by which or whom, any object is effected, &c.<BR> E. सह<BR>with, कृ to make, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकृत्
सहकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Assisting, an assister.<BR> E. सह, कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकृत्वन्
सहकृत्वन् mfn. (-त्वा-त्वा-त्वं) Co-operating, assisting.<BR> E. सह with, कृ to do, क्वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहगत
सहगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Accompanied, associated.<BR> E. सह with, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहगमन
सहगमन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going with, accompanying.<BR>	 2. A woman's burning<BR>herself on the funeral pile with her deceased husband.<BR> E. सह<BR>with, गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहगामिन्
सहगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Going with, accompanying.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A<BR>woman who burns herself with her husband's body.<BR> E. सह with,<BR>गामिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचर|सहचरः
सहचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Accompanying, going or associating with, &c.<BR>mf. (-रः-री) Yellow Barleria.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A companion, a follower.<BR>2. A surety.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A wife.<BR>	 2. A woman's female friend or con-<BR>fidante.<BR> E. सह with, चर् to go, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचरत्
सहचरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Accompanying, attending.<BR> E. सह with, चर् to go, शुतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचरित
सहचरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Who or what accompanies, attends, associates<BR>with, &c.<BR> E. सह with, चर् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचार|सहचारः
सहचार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Harmony, agreement.<BR>	 2. The accompaniment of the<BR>middle term by the major, (in logic.)<BR> E. सह + चर-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचारिन्
सहचारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) A companion, an attendant.<BR> E. सह, चारिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहज|सहजः
सहज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. Co-existent, cognate, born or produced toge-<BR>ther.<BR>	 2. Innate, inherent, natural.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A brother of whole<BR>blood.<BR>	 2. The natural state or disposition.<BR> E. सह with, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजमित्र|सहजमित्रं
सहजमित्र m. (-त्रः) A friend by birth; as a sister's son, &c.<BR> E. सहज<BR>cognate, मित्र friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजारि|सहजारिः
सहजारि m. (-रिः) A natural enemy, one hostile by birth; as the son<BR>of the same father by another mother, the son of a paternal uncle,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सहज cognate, अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजेतर
सहजेतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Incidental, accidental, not inherent or innate,<BR>(in the dual it may imply both innate and adventitious.)<BR> E. सहज,<BR>and इतर other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजोदासीन|सहजोदासीनः
सहजोदासीन m. (-नः) A person, unconnected by birth, born neither an<BR>enemy nor friend.<BR> E. सहज cognate, उदासीन a stranger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहत्व|सहत्वं
सहत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Sufferance, endurance.<BR>	 2. Association, union.<BR> E. सह<BR>patient, or with, त्व aff.; also तल्, सहता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहदार
सहदार Adj Married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहदेव|सहदेवः
सहदेव m. (-वः) The youngest of the five Pāṇḍava princes, begotten on<BR>MĀDRI by the younger Aświn. He was proficient in astrology<BR>and is considered as the beau ideal of masculine beauty.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>	 1.<BR>A plant, a sort of Sida.<BR>	 2. A twining shrub, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>3. Another plant, also Daṇḍotpala.<BR>	 f. (-बी)<BR>	 1. A sort of Sida.<BR>	 2.<BR>A shrub, bearing a fragrant seed, Priyangu.<BR> E. सह with, देव who<BR>or what sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहधर्म्म|सहधर्म|सहधर्मः
सहधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Community of duty, law, property, &c.<BR> E. सह with, धर्म्म duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहधर्म्मिन्|सहधर्मिन्
सहधर्म्मिन् mfn. (-र्म्मी-र्म्मिणी-र्म्मि)<BR>	 1. Following the same law, acknowled-<BR>ging the same obligations.<BR>	 2. Possessing same or like properties.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णी) A woman married according to the ritual of the Vedas. E.<BR>सह with. धर्म्म the law, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहन|सहनं|सहनः
सहन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Patient, enduring.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Bearing, enduring,<BR>patience.<BR> E. सह् to bear, युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहनर्त्तन|सहनर्तन|सहनर्त्तनं
सहनर्त्तन n. (-नं) Dancing together in a circle, &c.<BR> E. सह् together, and नर्त्तन dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपांशुकिल|सहपांशुकिलः
सहपांशुकिल m. (-लः) A contemporary and friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपान|सहपानं
सहपान n. (-नं) Drinking together or equally.<BR> E. सह with, &c., पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहभाविन्
सहभाविन् m. (-वी) A friend, a companion, an adherent or partizan. E.<BR>सह with, भाव quality, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहभोजन|सहभोजनं
सहभोजन n. (-नं) Eating in company.<BR> E. सह together, भोजन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहमरण|सहमरणं
सहमरण n. (-णं) Concremation, a widow's burning herself with the corpse<BR>of her husband.<BR> E. सह with, मरण dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहयुध्वन्
सहयुध्वन् mfn. (-ध्वा-ध्वा-ध्व) Fighting with or along with.<BR>	 m. (-ध्वा) A<BR>brother-in-arms.<BR> E. सह, युध् to fight, क्वनिप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहयुध्वान
सहयुध्वान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fighting with.<BR> E. सह, युध्वान fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहरसा
सहरसा f. (-सा) A sort of bean: see मुद्गपर्णी.<BR> E. सह with, रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहरि|सहरिः
सहरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A bull. Ind. Resembling HARI or VIṢṆU.<BR>E. स for सह with, or समान same, हरि the deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहर्ष|सहर्षः
सहर्ष m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Envy, emulation.<BR>	 2. Pleasure, delight.<BR> E. स with, हर्ष pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्
सहस् m. (-हाः)<BR>	 1. The month Agrahāyaṇa, (Nov.-Dec.)<BR>	 2. The winter<BR>season.<BR>	 n. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Strength, power.<BR>	 2. Light.<BR> E. सह् to bear, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसा
सहसा Ind. Quickly, precipitately, inconsiderately, without considera-<BR>tion or pause.<BR> E. षह् to bear, असा aff.; or सह + सो-डा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसादृष्ट|सहसादृष्टः
सहसादृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Seen quickly.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टः) An adopted son. E.<BR>सहसा quickly, दृष्ट seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसान|सहसानः
सहसान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Patient, enduring.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A peacock.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sacrifice, oblation.<BR> E. षह् to bear, असानच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्य|सहस्यः
सहस्य m. (-स्यः) The month Pausha, (Dec. Jan.)<BR> E. सह् to bear, यत् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्र|सहस्रं
सहस्र n. (-स्रं) A thousand.<BR> E. समानं हसति हस्-र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रकाण्डा|सहस्रकांडा
सहस्रकाण्डा f. (-ण्डा) The white DŪRVĀ grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रकिरण|सहस्रकिरणः
सहस्रकिरण m. (-णः) The sun.<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand, and किरण a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रकृत्वस्
सहस्रकृत्वस् Ind. Repeatedly, reiteratedly, a thousand or many times. E.<BR>सहस्र and कृत्वसुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रद|सहस्रदः
सहस्रद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Liberal, giving by thousands.<BR> E. सहस्र, and द who gives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रदंष्ट्र|सहस्रदंष्ट्रः
सहस्रदंष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A sort of sheat fish, (Silurus pelorius, BUCH.) E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, दंष्ट्र tooth. “पाठीन मत्स्ये” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रदंष्ट्रिन्
सहस्रदंष्ट्रिन् m. (-ष्ट्री) A sheat fish: see the last. “वोयालमाछ ।”<BR> E. सहस्र, दंष्ट्र<BR>a tooth, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रदृश्
सहस्रदृश् m. (-दृक्) INDRA.<BR> E. सहस्र, दृश् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रदोस्
सहस्रदोस् m. (-दोः) KĀRTAVĪRYA, a prince so named.<BR> E. सहस्र, दोस् the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रधा
सहस्रधा Ind. In a thousand ways.<BR> E. सहस्र, धाच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रधार|सहस्रधारः
सहस्रधार m. (-रः) The discus of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand, धार an edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रनयन|सहस्रनयनः
सहस्रनयन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. An owl.<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand, नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रनेत्र|सहस्रनेत्रः
सहस्रनेत्र m. (-त्रः) INDRA.<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand, नेत्र the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रपति
सहस्रपति m. (-तिः) The governor of a district, or of a thousand villages.<BR>E. सहस्र, पति chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रपत्र|सहस्रपत्रं
सहस्रपत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. The indian crane.<BR> E. सहस्र, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रपाद्
सहस्रपाद् m. (-त् or -द्) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. सहस्र, and पाद् for पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रपाद|सहस्रपादः
सहस्रपाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. A sort of duck.<BR> E. सहस्र<BR>a thousand, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रभुज|सहस्रभुजः
सहस्रभुज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. An epithet of the demon BĀṆA.<BR>	 2. KĀRTAVIRYA.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रयुग
सहस्रयुग m. (-गः) A period of a thousand ages.<BR> E. सहस्र, and युग an age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्ररश्मि|सहस्ररश्मिः
सहस्ररश्मि m. (-श्मिः) The sun.<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand, and रश्मि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्ररोमन्
सहस्ररोमन् n. (-म) A blanket.<BR> E. सहस्र and रोमन् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवदन|सहस्रवदनः
सहस्रवदन m. (-नः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand, and वदन a face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवीर्य्या|सहस्रवीर्या
सहस्रवीर्य्या f. (-र्य्या) A bent grass, (Panicum dactylon, the Agrostis<BR>linearis of LINNÆUS.)<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand, वीर्य्य splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवेध|सहस्रवेधं
सहस्रवेध n. (-धं) Sorrel. “काञ्जिके” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवेधिन्
सहस्रवेधिन् n. (-धि) Asafœtida.<BR>	 m. (-धी) A sort of cane, (Calamus fasci-<BR>culatus.)<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand. वेधिन् what pierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशस्
सहस्रशस् Ind. By a thousand or thousands, thousand-fold.<BR> E. सहस्र, शसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशिखर|सहस्रशिखरः
सहस्रशिखर m. (-रः) The Vindhya mountain.<BR> E. सहस्र, शिखर a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रहर्य्याश्व|सहस्रहर्याश्व|सहस्रहर्य्याश्वः
सहस्रहर्य्याश्व m. (-श्वः) The car of INDRA.<BR> E. सहस्र, हरि green, अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रांशु|सहस्रांशुः
सहस्रांशु m. (-शुः) The sun.<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand, and अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्राक्ष|सहस्राक्षः
सहस्राक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षी-क्षं) Thousand-eyed; used figuratively, vigilant,<BR>all-perceiving, all-inspecting, all-powerful.<BR>	 m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>2. An owl.<BR>	 3. BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand, and अक्ष the<BR>eye: INDRA having been covered over with marks resem-<BR>bling the female organ, in consequence of a curse of GAUTAMA;<BR>those marks were changed subsequently to eyes by the<BR>relenting saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्राधिपति|सहस्राधिपतिः
सहस्राधिपति m. (-तिः) The governor of a district or chief over a<BR>thousand villages.<BR> E. सहस्र, अधिपति ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रार|सहस्रारः
सहस्रार n. (-रं) The top of the head, the seat of the soul.<BR> E. सहस्र, and अर a spoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रावर|सहस्रावरः
सहस्रावर m. (-रः) A fine from five hundred to a thousand Paṇas. E.<BR>सहस्र, and अवर below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रिन्
सहस्रिन् mfn. (-स्री-स्रिणी-स्रि) Having a thousand.<BR>	 m. (-स्री)<BR>	 1. A body of<BR>a thousand men, &c.<BR>	 2. Commander or prefect of a thousand. E.<BR>सहस्र a thousand, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्वत्|सहस्वन्त्
सहस्वत् f. (-स्वती) Adj. Powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहा
सहा f. (-हा) The earth.<BR> E. सह् to bear, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहाचर|सहाचरः
सहाचर m. (-रः) A yellow sort of Barleria, (B. prionitis.)<BR> E. सह with<BR>आङ् before चर् to go, aff. अच्; also सहचर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहाय|सहायः
सहाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A companion, a follower.<BR>	 2. A patron, a helper.<BR>	 3. A<BR>sort of drug and perfume, commonly Ghantāpātali.<BR>	 4. The ruddy<BR>goose.<BR>	 5. An adherent.<BR>	 6. An ally.<BR>	 7. Śiva.<BR> E. सह with, इण् to<BR>go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायता
सहायता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A multitude of companions, a company of associates<BR>or followers.<BR>	 2. Association, assistance, friendship.<BR> E. सहाय a<BR>companion, तल् aff. of number, or the abstract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायत्व|सहायत्वं
सहायत्व n. (-त्वं) Fellowship, companionship, friendship.<BR> E. सहाय a<BR>companion, त्व aff. of the quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायवत्|सहायवन्त्
सहायवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Befriended, assisted, accompanied.<BR> E. सहाय,<BR>मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार|सहारः
सहार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The mango tree.<BR>	 2. Universal dissolution.<BR> E. षह् to<BR>bear, आरन् Unādi aff.; or सह्-ऋ-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहारोग्य|सहारोग्यः
सहारोग्य mfn. (-ग्यः-ग्या-ग्यं) Well, convalescent.<BR> E. सह with, आरोग्य health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार्थ|सहार्थः
सहार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Having one object.<BR>	 2. Synonymous, having<BR>the same meaning.<BR> E. सह with, अर्थ object, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार्द्द|सहार्द|सहार्द्दः
सहार्द्द mfn. (-र्द्दः-र्द्दा-र्द्दं) Tender, affectionate.<BR> E. स with, हार्द्द affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहासन
सहासन n. (-नं) Sitting on the same seat.<BR> E. सह with, आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित|सहितः
सहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Accompanied by, in company with, associated<BR>with, &c.<BR>	 2. Borne, endured.<BR>	 3. Sincerely.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-तं) With,<BR>together with.<BR> E. सह with, इतच् aff.; or षह् to bear, क्त aff., with इट्<BR>augment; or स with, हित useful, right, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहितृ
सहितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Bearing, enduring.<BR> E. षह् to bear, तृच् or इट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित्र|सहित्रं
सहित्र n. (-त्रं) Patience, endurance.<BR> E. षह् to suffer, and इत्र aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=777-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्ठ
सहिष्ठ f. (-ष्ठा) Adj. Mightiest, very powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णु|सहिष्णुः
सहिष्णु mfn. (-ष्णुः-ष्णुः-ष्णु) Patient, enduring, resigned.<BR> E. षह् to bear, इष्णुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णुता
सहिष्णुता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Patience, resignation.<BR>	 2. Ability to support.<BR> E. तल्<BR>affix of the abstract, added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहुरि|सहुरिः
सहुरि m. (-रिः) The sun.<BR>	 f. (-रिः) The earth.<BR> E. षह् to bear, उरिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृदय|सहृदयः
सहृदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Good-hearted.<BR>	 2. Sincere.<BR>	 3. Appreciative.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-यः)<BR>	 1. A Pandit, a learned man.<BR>	 2. A man of taste, a critic.<BR> E. स<BR>with, हृदय a heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृल्लेख|सहृल्लेखं
सहृल्लेख f. (-खा) Questionable.<BR>	 n. (-खं) Questionable food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहेल
सहेल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Sportive, playing.<BR> E. स with, हेल sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोक्ति|सहोक्तिः
सहोक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. A figure of rhetoric; either the employment of a word<BR>in a double meaning, or connecting different circumstances in one<BR>sentence by the use of the term सह with, along with.<BR>	 2. Speaking<BR>at the same time.<BR> E. सह with, उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोटज|सहोटजः
सहोटज m. (-जः) A hut of leaves, &c., inhabited by ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोढ|सहोढः
सहोढ m. (-ढः)<BR>	 1. The son of a woman pregnant at the time of her<BR>marriage.<BR>	 2. A thief caught with stolen property.<BR> E. सह with, ऊढा<BR>a bride; or स with, होढ stolen goods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोढज|सहोढजः
सहोढज m. (-जः) The son of a woman pregnant at the time of marriage.<BR>E. स with, ऊढा a bride, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोदर|सहोदरः
सहोदर m. (-रः) A brother of whole blood, one by the same father and<BR>mother.<BR> E. सह with, उदर the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोदित
सहोदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Said or declared, comprehensively or collective-<BR>ly.<BR> E. सह with, उदित said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोबल|सहोबलं
सहोबल n. (-लं) Violence, aggression.<BR> E. सहस् and बल, both meaning power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोर|सहोरः
सहोर m. (-रः) A saint, a pure or pious man.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Good.<BR> E. सह, ओरन्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोषित
सहोषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dwelling or abiding with, being together with,<BR> E. सह, उषित abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्य|सह्यं|सह्यः
सह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. To be borne or suffered.<BR>	 2. Equal or adequate<BR>to.<BR>	 3. Sweet, agreeable.<BR>	 4. Powerful, strong.<BR>	 n. (-ह्यं)<BR>	 1. Health,<BR>convalescence.<BR>	 2. Assistance.<BR>	 m. (-ह्यः) One of the seven principal<BR>ranges of the mountains of India; the mountainous country on<BR>north-west side of the Peninsula or towards Poonah, &c., and<BR>in which the river Godāvari takes its rise.<BR> E. षह् to bear, aff. यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सा
सा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. A name of LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. The goddess GAURĪ.<BR>	 3. She, (the<BR>third personal feminine pronoun or the feminine inflection of तद्<BR>that, &c.)<BR> E. षो to destroy, &c., aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांख्य|साङ्ख्य|सांख्यं|सांख्यः|साङ्ख्यः
सांख्य mfn. (-ख्यः-ख्यी-ख्यं) See साङ्ख्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयात्रिक|सांयात्रिकः
सांयात्रिक m. (-कः) A voyaging merchant, one who trades by sea, &c.<BR>E. संयात्रा travelling together, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयुगीन|सांयुगीनः
सांयुगीन m. (-नः) An able leader, a soldier skilled in war.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Warlike.<BR> E. संयुग war, खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांराविण|सांराविणं
सांराविण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Shout, acclamation, the calling out of a number<BR>of people together.<BR>	 2. Crying or complaining aloud.<BR> E. सम् together,<BR>राविन् who calls or cries, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सर|सांवत्सरः
सांवत्सर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Annual, perennial.<BR>	 m. (-रः) An astrologer. E.<BR>संवत्सर a year, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सरिक|सांवत्सरिकः
सांवत्सरिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Yearly, annual, relating to a year, produced<BR>in a year, &c.<BR> E. संवत्सर a year, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवादिक|सांवादिकः
सांवादिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A logician.<BR>	 2. A controversialist.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Con-<BR>troversial.<BR>	 2. Colloquial.<BR> E. सांवाद dispute, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवृत्तिक
सांवृत्तिक f. (-की) Phenomenal, illusory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांशयिक|सांशयिकः
सांशयिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Dubious, doubtful.<BR>	 2. Uncertain, irresolute,<BR>in doubt.<BR> E. संशय doubt, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसारिक
सांसारिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Worldly, of or belonging to the world.<BR> E. संसार, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसिद्धिक
सांसिद्धिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Spontaneous, effected naturally.<BR>	 2. Innate.<BR>3. Effected by supernatural means.<BR> E. संसिद्धि perfection, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्थानिक|सांस्थानिकः
सांस्थानिक m. (-कः) A countryman, an inhabitant or native of the same<BR>place.<BR> E. सम् together, स्थान place, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्राविण|सांस्राविणं
सांस्राविण n. (-णं) A general stream or flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांहननिक
सांहननिक f. (-की) Relating to the body, corporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकम्
साकम् Ind.<BR>	 1. With, together with.<BR>	 2. Simultaneously.<BR> E. स for सह<BR>with, अक् to go, अम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकल्य|साकल्यं
साकल्य n. (-ल्यं) The whole, the entire, all.<BR> E. सकल all, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकाङ्क्ष|साकांक्ष
साकाङ्क्ष mfn. (-ङ्क्षः-ङ्क्षा-ङ्क्षं) Wishing, desirous.<BR> E. स with, आकाङ्क्षा desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकार|साकारः
साकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Having form or shape.<BR> E. स with, आकार form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूत
साकूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Significant.<BR>	 2. Wanton.<BR> E. स with, आकूत mean-<BR>ing, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूतस्मित
साकूतस्मित n. (-तं) A wanton glance.<BR> E. साकूत, and स्मित a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेत|साकेतं
साकेत n. (-तं) The city Ayodhyā, or ancient Oudh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्तुक|साक्तुकं|साक्तुकः
साक्तुक m. (-कः) Barley.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A quantity of fried grain, &c.<BR> E. सक्तु<BR>fried or parched grain ground, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्
साक्षात् Ind.<BR>	 1. Before, in presence, in sight.<BR>	 2. As, like.<BR>	 3. Actually in<BR>person.<BR>	 4. Evidently, manifestly, directly.<BR> E. स for सह with, अक्ष<BR>the eye, अत् to go or to be, aff. क्विप्; or सह अक्षति अक्ष्-आति सादेशः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्कार|साक्षात्कारः
साक्षात्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Causing to be visibly present.<BR>	 2. Making evident<BR>to the senses.<BR>	 3. Actual feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिता
साक्षिता f. (-ता) Evidence, testimony.<BR> E. साक्षिन्, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, साक्षित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिन्
साक्षिन् mfn. (-क्षी-क्षिणी-क्षि)<BR>	 1. Witnessing, seeing, an eye-witness.<BR>	 2.<BR>Attesting, testifying, evidence.<BR>	 m. (-क्षी) A witness, (in law.)<BR> E. स<BR>for सह with, (in presence of,) अक्षि the eye, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिपरीक्षा
साक्षिपरीक्षा f. (-क्षा) Examination of a witness' credibility.<BR> E. साक्षिन्,<BR>and परीक्षा trial; also साक्षिपरीक्षणं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिभावित
साक्षिभावित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made known by testimony.<BR> E. साक्षिन्, and<BR>भावित caused to be perceived or known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिमत्|साक्षिमन्त्
साक्षिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Having or requiring evidence.<BR> E. साक्षिन्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिलक्षण
साक्षिलक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Defined or proved by testimony.<BR> E. साक्षिन्,<BR>and लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष्य|साक्ष्यं
साक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं) Testimony, evidence.<BR> E. साक्षिन्, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष्यभाव
साक्ष्यभाव m. (-वः) Absence or deficiency of witnesses or testimony. E.<BR>साक्षिन्, and अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साखेय|साखेयः
साखेय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Friendly, amicable.<BR> E. सखि a friend, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साख्य|साख्यं
साख्य n. (-ख्यं) Friendship.<BR> E. सखि a friend, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागर|सागरः
सागर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. A sort of deer.<BR>	 3. The number “four.”<BR>4. The number “seven”.<BR> E. सगर a king and अण् aff.; to bathe the<BR>bones of SAGARA'S 60,000 sons the Ganges is said to have been led by<BR>BHAGĪRATHA, his great-great-grandson, to the ocean, at the place<BR>now called Gangā-Sāgar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरगामिनी
सागरगामिनी f. (-नी) A river in general.<BR> E. सागर the ocean, गामिनी going to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरनेमि|सागरनेमिः
सागरनेमि f. (-मिः) The earth.<BR> E. सागर the sea, and नेमि a circumference;<BR>surrounding the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरमेखला
सागरमेखला f. (-ला) The earth.<BR> E. सागर the ocean, and मेखला a zone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागराम्बरा|सागरांबरा
सागराम्बरा f. (-रा) The earth.<BR> E. सागर the ocean, अम्बर vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरालय|सागरालयः
सागरालय m. (-यः) VARUṆA, deity of the water.<BR> E. सागर the ocean, आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरोत्थ|सागरोत्थं
सागरोत्थ n. (-त्थं) Sea-salt.<BR> E. सागर the sea, उत्थ produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्निक|साग्निकः
साग्निक m. (-कः) A householder who maintains a sacred fire.<BR> E. स with,<BR>अग्नि fire, कप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कर्य्य|साङ्कर्य|सांकर्य|सांकर्यं
साङ्कर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Mixture, blending.<BR>	 2. The concurrence of various<BR>properties in one subject.<BR> E. सङ्कर mixing, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कल|सांकल|साङ्कलं
साङ्कल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Effected or produced by addition, collection,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सङ्कल collection, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्कुर|सांकुर
साङ्कुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Budding, in bud.<BR> E. स with, अङ्कुर a bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्केतिक|सांकेतिक
साङ्केतिक f. (-की) Conventional, indicatory, symbolical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्क्षेपिक|सांक्षेपिक|साङ्क्षेपिकः
साङ्क्षेपिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Short, summary, concise, contracted, abrid-<BR>ged.<BR> E. सङ्क्षेप abridgment, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ख्य|सांख्य|सांख्यं|सांख्यः|साङ्ख्यः
साङ्ख्य mfn. (-ङ्ख्यः-ङ्ख्यी-ङ्ख्यं)<BR>	 1. Numeral, relating to number.<BR>2. Deliberating, reasoning.<BR>	 3. Rational, discriminative.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-ङ्ख्यः)<BR>	 1. The Sānkhya system of philosophy, ascribed<BR>originally to the Muni KAPILA, and so called as enumera-<BR>ting twenty-five Tatwas or true principles; its object is<BR>to effect the final liberation of the twenty-fifth Tatwa, viz.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">Page779-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Purusha, (the soul,) from the fetters of the phenomenal crea-<BR>tion by conveying a correct knowledge of the twenty-four<BR>other Tatwas; the Sānkhya system agrees with Vedāntism in<BR>being synthetical, so differing from the analytical Nyāya; its<BR>great point of divergence from the Vedānta is its maintaining<BR>two principles, which the Vedānta denies.<BR>	 2. A follower of the<BR>Sānkhya system of philosophy.<BR> E. सङ्ख्या number, &c., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ग|सांग
साङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा or ङ्गी-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Having all the members.<BR>	 2. Comprising<BR>all the sub-divisions.<BR> E. स with, अङ्ग a limb or part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गतिक|सांगतिक|सांगतिकः
साङ्गतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Social, associating, relating or derived from<BR>encounter or society.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A visitor, a guest, a newcomer.<BR>E. सङ्गति acquaintance, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गम|सांगम|सांगमः|साङ्गमः
साङ्गम m. (-मः) Union, meeting.<BR> E. सङ्गम the same, अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ग्रामिक|सांग्रामिक|सांग्रामिकः|साङ्ग्रामिकः
साङ्ग्रामिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Warlike, martial, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A commander,<BR>a general.<BR> E. सङ्ग्राम war, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचि
साचि Ind. Crookedly, awry, bent, obliquely.<BR> E. षच् to collect, इण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिविलोकित
साचिविलोकित n. (-तं) A side glance.<BR> E. साचि, and विलोकित looked at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिव्य|साचिव्यं
साचिव्य n. (-व्यं)<BR>	 1. Ministry, administration.<BR>	 2. Friendship, fellowship.<BR>E. सचिव a friend, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिस्थित
साचिस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Crooked.<BR>	 2. Standing or placed unevenly.<BR> E. साचि, स्थित stood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचीकृत|साचीकृतं
साचीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made crooked.<BR>	 2. Seen crookedly or tortuously,<BR>distorted, misrepresented.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Prejudice, distortion or<BR>perversion of mind.<BR> E. साचि, च्वि aff., कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साजात्य|साजात्यं
साजात्य n. (-त्यं)<BR>	 1. Community of genus, homogeneousness.<BR>	 2. Sameness of tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साञ्जन|सांजनः|साञ्जनः
साञ्जन m. (-नः) A lizard, a chameleon.<BR> E. स with, अञ्जन unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साट्
साट् r. 10th cl. (साटयति-ते) To make visible, to show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साटोप
साटोप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Proud, haughty, consequential.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-पं)<BR>Arrogantly, consequentially.<BR> E. स with, आटोप pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्
सात् r. 10th cl. (सातयति-ते) To give pleasure; according to some it is a Sautra root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्
सात् Ind. A Tadhita affix which, when put after a word, denotes either<BR>a total change of anything into the thing expressed by that word,<BR>or complete control.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्
सात् n. (-सात्) BRAHMĀ, GOD.<BR> E. साति to cause happiness, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात|सातं
सात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Given.<BR>	 2. Destroyed.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Pleasure, delight.<BR>E. षण् to give, or षो to destroy, aff. क्त, form irr.; see सित; or more<BR>properly सात् to give pleasure, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातत्य|सातत्यं
सातत्य n. (-त्यं) Continuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातय|सातयः
सातय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Who or what causes pleasure.<BR> E. साति a Sautra<BR>root in the causal form, to cause pleasure, श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातला
सातला f. (-ला) A shrub, commonly Charmakasā.<BR> E. सात pleasure, and<BR>ला to give, affs. अङ् and टाप्; also शातला ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातवाहन|सातवाहनः
सातवाहन m. (-नः) The sovereign SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR> E. सात a Gandharba,<BR>changed according to the legend to a lion, on which this prince<BR>was discovered riding when a child, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साति|सातिः
साति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. End, conclusion, cessation of action.<BR>	 2. Destruction.<BR>3. Gift, giving.<BR>	 4. Sharp pain.<BR>	 5. Gaining, acquisition.<BR> E. षो to des-<BR>troy, or षण् to give, क्तिन् or क्तिच् aff.; also read सति and सन्ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिसार|सातिसारः
सातिसार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Dysenteric, afflicted with dysentery.<BR> E. स for<BR>सह with, अतिसार dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातीलक|सातीलकः
सातीलक m. (-कः) Pease; also सातीनक सतीलक, and सतीनक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यकि|सात्यकिः
सात्यकि m. (-किः) A hero of the Yādava family who acted as charioteer<BR>to Krishṇa and was a staunch adherent of the Pāndavas in the<BR>great war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यवत|सात्यवतः
सात्यवत m. (-तः) The poet and sage VYĀSA.<BR> E. सत्यवती the mother of<BR>the bard, and अण् aff.; also with ढक् aff. सात्यवतेय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वत्|सात्वन्त्
सात्वत् m. (-त्वान्)<BR>	 1. A worshipper, a follower.<BR>	 2. A man of the Yādava<BR>tribe.<BR> E. साति to cause happiness, वतु participial aff.; or सात्-क्विप्-मतुप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वत|सात्वतः
सात्वत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. BALADEVA.<BR>	 m. Plu. (-ताः) The people<BR>of one of the countries of midland India, apparently inhabiting<BR>a district in the vicinity of the Pārijātra mountains, said to be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">Page779-b+ 60</a>]<BR>descendants from outcaste Vaiśyas.<BR>	 f. (-ती)<BR>	 1. One of the four<BR>great divisions of the drama, described as the representation of<BR>gentle and amiable sentiments or passions.<BR>	 2. The mother of ŚIŚU-<BR>PĀLA.<BR> E. सत्वत a proper name, &c., अण् aff.; or सत्यमेव सात्वम तत्तनोति तन्-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्विक
सात्विक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Spontaneous, sincere, (as applied to the<BR>actions or signs of the Sātwika-Bhāva.)<BR>	 2. Relating to or pro-<BR>ceeding from the Satwa quality; honest, true, good, gentle, ami-<BR>able, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. BRĀHMAṆA.<BR>	 2. One of the Bhāvas or classes<BR>into which the affections of the mind or their expression, are<BR>distinguished, in poetry and the drama: this class holds a middle<BR>place between the Sthāyi, and Vyabhichāri-Bhāvas, and implies<BR>the honest and spontaneous indication of strong feeling, as<BR>evinced especially in eight acts, viz:--inability to move whilst the<BR>faculties or limbs are unaffected, perspiration, horripilation,<BR>inarticulate speech, trembling or tremor, change of colour, tears,<BR>and mental absorption or indifference, approaching to loss of<BR>sense, to every object but one which engrosses the attention.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-की) DURGĀ.<BR> E. सत्व the Satwa-Guṇa or quality, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद|सादः
साद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Purity, cleanness.<BR>	 2. Lassitude, weariness, exhaustion.<BR>3. Perishing, decay.<BR>	 4. Leanness, thinness, emaciation.<BR>	 5. Cessation,<BR>stoppage.<BR>	 6. Pain.<BR> E. षद् to decay, to be weary, &c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादन|सादनं
सादन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A house, a dwelling.<BR>	 2. Dispelling.<BR>	 3. Destroying.<BR>	 4.<BR>Wearying, exhausting.<BR>	 5. Exhaustion, decay.<BR> E. षद् to go, causal<BR>v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादयत्
सादयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Destroying.<BR>	 2. Exhausting.<BR>	 3. Expelling,<BR>removing, extracting.<BR> E. षद् to go, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादयितव्य
सादयितव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be destroyed.<BR> E. षद् to go, causal v., तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादर
सादर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Respectful.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-रं) Respectfully.<BR> E. स with,<BR>आदर respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादि|सादिः
सादि m. (-दिः)<BR>	 1. A charioteer.<BR>	 2. A warrior.<BR>	 3. Exhausted.<BR>	 4. Wind.<BR>E. षद् to be weary, &c., इण् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादित|सादितः
सादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Destroyed, exterminated.<BR>	 2. Wearied, exhaus-<BR>ted, harassed.<BR>	 3. Wasted, decayed.<BR>	 4. Broken, cut.<BR>	 5. Drawn,<BR>dragged.<BR> E. षद् to go, &c., aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिन्
सादिन् m. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A horseman, a cavalier.<BR>	 2. One who rides on an<BR>elephant.<BR>	 3. One who rides on or is mounted in a car.<BR>	 f. (-दिनी)<BR>Destroying.<BR> E. षद् to go, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादृश्य|सादृश्यं
सादृश्य n. (-श्यं)<BR>	 1. Resemblance, similarity.<BR>	 2. A likeness, an image, a<BR>portrait.<BR> E. सदृश like, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यस्क|साद्यस्कः
साद्यस्क mfn. (-स्कः-स्का-स्कं) Quick, instantaneous.<BR> E. सद्यस्, and वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्
साध्(उ)साधु r. 4th cl. (साध्यति-ते) To be completed. (औ) साधौ r. 5th cl.<BR>(साध्नोति)<BR>	 1. To finish, to perfect, to complete, or accomplish.<BR>	 2. To<BR>conquer. r. 10th cl. (साधयति-ते) To go, to depart; also षाध् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधक|साधकः
साधक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Completing, perfecting, finishing, who or what<BR>effects or completes.<BR>	 f. (-धका or धिका)<BR>	 1. Fulfilling.<BR>	 2. Effecting by<BR>magic.<BR>	 3. Skilful, adept.<BR>	 4. Aiding, helping.<BR> E. साध् to finish, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधन|साधनं
साधन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Accomplishing, effecting.<BR>	 2. Matter, materials, that<BR>of which any thing is composed or consists.<BR>	 3. Thing, substance.<BR>4. Means, expedient.<BR>	 5. Instrument, agent.<BR>	 6. Authority.<BR>	 7. The<BR>premises leading to a conclusion.<BR>	 8. Cause.<BR>	 9. Going, motion.<BR>	 10.<BR>Following.<BR>	 11. Killing, destroying.<BR>	 12. Obsequies, ceremonies<BR>observed after the death of a relative.<BR>	 13. Drug, medicament.<BR>	 14.<BR>Wealth.<BR>	 15. An army.<BR>	 16. The penis.<BR>	 17. Friendship.<BR>	 18. Enforce-<BR>ment of the delivery of any thing, especially juridically, as the<BR>infliction and levy of a fine, &c.<BR>	 19. Killing metals, depriving<BR>them (especially mercury,) by oxidation, &c., of their metallic<BR>properties, for medicinal or alchemical purposes.<BR>	 20. Good works, or<BR>the observance of the moral and ceremonial parts of the Hindu<BR>religion, as secondary means of obtaining purity and emancipation.<BR>21. Proof, substantiation.<BR>	 22. Penance, self-mortification.<BR>	 23.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">Page780-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Profit, advantage.<BR>	 24. Subduing.<BR>	 25. Subduing by charms.<BR>	 26.<BR>Conciliating, worshipping.<BR>	 27. Killing.<BR>	 28. Setting out.<BR>	 29. Aid,<BR>assistance.<BR>	 30. A bodily organ.<BR>	 31. An udder.<BR>	 32. Implement,<BR>utensil, apparatus.<BR>	 33. The instrumental case, (in gram.)<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>Effecting.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Accomplishment, completion.<BR>	 2. Propitiation,<BR>worship.<BR> E. षाध् to accomplish, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनत्व|साधनत्वं
साधनत्व n. (-त्वं) State or condition of being a means to a desired end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधननिर्देश|साधननिर्देशः|साधननिर्द्देश
साधननिर्देश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Production or indication of proof, (in law.)<BR>2. Establishment of premises, leading to a conclusion.<BR> E. साधन<BR>proof, &c., and निर्देश pointing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनीय
साधनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Perfective, to be perfected, accomplished,<BR>proved.<BR> E. षाध् to complete, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधन्त|साधंत|साधंतः|साधन्तः
साधन्त m. (-न्तः) A beggar, a mendicant.<BR> E. षाध् to accomplish, Unādi aff. झच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधयत्
साधयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Perfecting, accomplishing.<BR>	 2. Purifying.<BR>3. Proving.<BR>	 4. Recovering, (as a debt.)<BR> E. षध् to accomplish, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधर्म्म्य
साधर्म्म्य n. (-र्म्म्यं)<BR>	 1. Community, equality, (of duty, office, property, &c.)<BR>2. Sameness of nature.<BR> E. सधर्म्म of one duty, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण|साधारणः
साधारण mfn. (-णः-णा or णी-णं)<BR>	 1. Like, similar.<BR>	 2. Common, belonging<BR>to all or many.<BR>	 3. Generic.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. A common rule or precept,<BR>one applicable to many persons or things.<BR>	 2. A specific or generic<BR>character, one common to all the individuals of a species, or<BR>all the species of a genus, &c.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A small bolt or bar.<BR> E. स for<BR>सह with, धारण having, aff. अण् or ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणधर्म्म|साधारणधर्म|साधारणधर्मः|साधारणधर्म्मः
साधारणधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Common or universal duty, conduct to be obser-<BR>ved by all castes or orders, as humanity, &c.<BR> E. साधारण general,<BR>and धर्म्म merit, duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणस्त्री
साधारणस्त्री f. (-स्त्री) A whore.<BR> E. साधारण common, and स्त्री a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण्य|साधारण्यं
साधारण्य n. (-ण्यं) Community, universality.<BR> E. साधारण, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिका
साधिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Deep or sound sleep.<BR>	 2. An accomplished woman. E.<BR>षाध् to finish, aff. वुन्, fem. form.; or सिध्-णिच् ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधित|साधितः
साधित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Amerced, fined, punished by fine, (as the<BR>culprit.)<BR>	 2. Awarded, (as the thing or fine.)<BR>	 3. Awarded to or<BR>in favour of, (as the person to whom the fine is to be paid.)<BR>	 4.<BR>Recovered, (as a debt.)<BR>	 5. Accomplished, finished.<BR>	 6. Discharged,<BR>fulfilled.<BR>	 7. Conferred, bestowed, enabled to procure or effect.<BR>	 8.<BR>Made to pay.<BR>	 9. Subdued.<BR>	 10. Substantiated, proved.<BR>	 11. Settled.<BR>12. Achieved.<BR> E. षाध् to accomplish, क्त aff., with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिदैव
साधिदैव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) One with supreme divinity.<BR> E. स with, अधिदैव<BR>superintending godhead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिभूत
साधिभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Identified or one with elementary essence. E.<BR>स with, अधिभूत essential matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिमन्
साधिमन् m. (-मा) Goodness, perfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधियज्ञ
साधियज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) One with the Supreme Being.<BR> E. स with,<BR>अधियज्ञ the object of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिष्ठ
साधिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Very hard.<BR>	 2. Very fit, proper, or right. E.<BR>साधु good, or considered as irregularly substituted for वाढ heavy,<BR>इष्ठन् aff. of the irr. superlative; also with ईयसुन aff. साधीयस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधीयस्
साधीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. Very right or proper.<BR>	 2. Very hard or<BR>firm.<BR>	 3. Very handsome. E. See the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधु|साधुः
साधु Ind.<BR>	 1. Well, well indeed.<BR>	 2. Enough, away with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधु|साधुः
साधु mfn. (-धुः-धुः or ध्वी-धु)<BR>	 1. Pleasing, beautiful.<BR>	 2. Well-born, of honour-<BR>able descent.<BR>	 3. Right, fit, proper.<BR>	 4. Good, virtuous, pious, pure.<BR>5. Pure, classical, (as applied to language.)<BR>	 6. Excellent, good.<BR>7. Eminent.<BR>	 m. (-धुः)<BR>	 1. A Muni, a saint, a sage in general, one of<BR>subdued passions and contemplative habits.<BR>	 2. A Jina, a deified<BR>saint venerated by the Jainas.<BR>	 3. A usurer.<BR>	 4. A good or honest<BR>man.<BR>	 5. A merchant.<BR>	 6. A derivative or inflected noun.<BR>	 f. (-धुः or -ध्वी)<BR>1. A virtuous wife.<BR>	 2. Name of a particular root.<BR> E. साध् to accom-<BR>plish or perfect, Unādi aff. उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुक|साधुकः
साधुक m. (-कः) A low or degraded tribe.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुज|साधुजः
साधुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Well-born, of respectable family or descent. E.<BR>साधु the same, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुत्व|साधुत्वं
साधुत्व n. (-त्वं) Goodness, correctness.<BR> E. त्व added to साधु; also with तल्, साधुता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुधी
साधुधी f. (-धी) A wife's or husband's mother.<BR> E. साधु pious, धा to have,<BR>affs. क and ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुपुष्प|साधुपुष्पं
साधुपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) A flower, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR> E. साधु pure, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुम्मन्य|साधुंमन्य
साधुम्मन्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Thinking one's self pure or virtuous.<BR> E. साधु,<BR>and मन् to think, खश् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवाद|साधुवादः
साधुवाद m. (-दः) A cry of approbation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवाहिन्
साधुवाहिन् m. (-ही) A well trained horse.<BR> E. साधु agreeable, pleasing, वाह bearing, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृक्ष|साधुवृक्षः
साधुवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea Cadamba.)<BR> E. साधु<BR>handsome or excellent, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृत्त|साधुवृत्तः
साधुवृत्त m. (-त्तः) A virtuous or pious person.<BR>	 n. (-त्तं) Virtue, piety. Adj.<BR>Well-conducted, upright.<BR> E. साधु, and वृत्त practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृत्ति|साधुवृत्तिः
साधुवृत्ति mfn. (-त्तिः-त्तिः-त्ति) Virtuous.<BR>	 f. (-त्तिः) The institutes or moral<BR>and ritual observances of the Hindus.<BR> E. साधु excellent, वृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुशील
साधुशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Virtuous, righteous, wisely or virtuously<BR>inclined.<BR> E. साधु, and शील disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुशीलत्व
साधुशीलत्व n. (-त्वं) Virtuous or righteous inclination or disposition. E.<BR>साधुशील, and त्व aff.; also with तल्, साधुशीलता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधूक्त
साधूक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Said or declared by the good.<BR> E. साधु, उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधृत|साधृतं
साधृत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The flock of peacocks.<BR>	 2. A stall, a shop.<BR>	 3. An<BR>umbrella or parasol.<BR> E. स for सह with, आधृत held.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्य|साध्यः
साध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. To be perfected or accomplished.<BR>	 2. Accom-<BR>plishable, attainable.<BR>	 3. To be inferred or concluded, (in logic.)<BR>	 4.<BR>To be proved or demonstrated.<BR>	 5. To be cured, curable, (in medi-<BR>cine.)<BR>	 6. To be substantiated or made good.<BR>	 7. To be subdued<BR>or mastered.<BR>	 8. To be destroyed.<BR>	 m. (-ध्यः)<BR>	 1. An inferior deity or<BR>demigod, one of a class of twelve.<BR>	 2. A deity in general.<BR>	 3. The<BR>twenty-second astronomical Yoga.<BR>	 4. Name of a particular mantra.<BR>n. (-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Accomplishment, perfection.<BR>	 2. (In law,) The matter in<BR>debate, the thing to be proved.<BR>	 3. (In logic,) The subject of the<BR>proposition, the major term in a syllogism.<BR> E. साध् to accomplish,<BR>ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यता
साध्यता f. (-ता) Practicableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यतावच्छेदक|साध्यतावच्छेदकं
साध्यतावच्छेदक n. (-कं) The characteristic property of the major term, (in logic.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यमान
साध्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being subjected to, or capable, or in course<BR>of proof.<BR>	 2. Being in course of accomplishment.<BR>	 3. Being proceeded<BR>against, (at law.)<BR> E. षाध् to accomplish, pass. v. शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यवत्|साध्यवन्त्
साध्यवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Comprehending that which is to be proved.<BR>m. (-वान्) (In law,) The party on whom rests the onus probandi.<BR>E. साध्य, and मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसाधन
साध्यसाधन n. (-नं) Effecting what is to be or may be done, &c.<BR> E. साध्य, साधन accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसिद्धि|साध्यसिद्धिः
साध्यसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Proof, conclusion, the establishing of that which<BR>was to be proved.<BR>	 2. Completion, accomplishment, fulfilment. E.<BR>साध्य to be effected, &c., and सिद्धि perfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसिद्धिपाद|साध्यसिद्धिपादः
साध्यसिद्धिपाद m. (-दः) The fourth stage or division of a suit at law,<BR>judgment or decision.<BR> E. साध्य to be proved, सिद्धि conclusion, and<BR>पाद division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्याभाव|साध्याभावः
साध्याभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Absence of the thing to be proved.<BR>	 2. Absence of<BR>the subject of a proposition.<BR>	 3. Impossibility of cure.<BR> E. साध्य, and<BR>अभाव nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वनिन्दित
साध्वनिन्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Unreproached, irreproachable.<BR> E. साधु the<BR>pious, अनिन्दित not reproved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वस|साध्वसं
साध्वस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Fear, terror.<BR>	 2. Perturbation.<BR>	 3. Torpor.<BR> E. साधु a pious<BR>man, अस् to throw or disperse, aff. अङ् or अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वाचार
साध्वाचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Virtuous.<BR> E. साधु, and आचार observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानन्द|सानंद|सानन्दः
सानन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Happy, delighted, enjoying and endowed with<BR>happiness.<BR> E. स with, आनन्द happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानल|सानलः
सानल m. (-लः) The resinous exudation of the Śāl tree.<BR> E. स with, अनल fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानसि|सानसिः
सानसि m. (-सिः) Gold.<BR> E. षण् to give, Unādi aff. असि, and the radical<BR>vowel made long; or सन्-इण्-असुक् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानिका
सानिका f. (-का) A flute, a pipe.<BR> E. षण् to give, (pleasure,) ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानु|सानुः
सानु mn. (-नुः-नु)<BR>	 1. Table-land, level ground on the top or edge of a<BR>mountain.<BR>	 2. A wood.<BR>	 3. A road.<BR>	 4. A gale of wind.<BR>	 5. Point,<BR>end, top.<BR>	 6. A sage, a learned man or Paṇḍit.<BR>	 7. A shoot, a<BR>sprout.<BR>	 8. The sun.<BR> E. षण् to give, (pleasure,) Unādi aff. ञुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुकम्प|सानुकंप
सानुकम्प mfn. (-म्पः-म्पा-म्पं) Sympathizing.<BR> E. स with, अनुकम्पा kindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुक्रोश
सानुक्रोश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Compassionate.<BR> E. स with, अनुक्रोश compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुनय
सानुनय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Willing, civil, kind.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Kindly, civilly.<BR> E. स<BR>with, अनुनय assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुमत्|सानुमन्त्
सानुमत् m. (-मान्) A mountain.<BR> E. सानु a summit, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुराग
सानुराग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Attached, passionate.<BR> E. स with, अनुराग affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानेयिका
सानेयिका f. (-का) A flute, or pipe.<BR> E. कन् added to सानेयी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानेयी
सानेयी f. (-यी) A flute, a pipe, a fife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तपन|सांतपन|सांतपनं|सान्तपनं
सान्तपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A sort of penance; the lighter kind is feeding on a<BR>mixture of curds, &c. for one day and fasting the next; the<BR>severer is feeding six successive days, severally, on the same<BR>articles, or on cow's urine, cow's ordure, milk, curds, Ghee, and<BR>water in which Kuśa grass has been steeped, and fasting on the<BR>seventh.<BR> E. सम् completely, तपन austerity, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तर|सांतर|सान्तरं
सान्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. With intervals, or interstices.<BR>	 2. Open in<BR>texture.<BR> E. स for सह with, अन्तर between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तराल
सान्तराल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Separated, distinct from, apart.<BR> E. स with,<BR>अन्तराल interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तानिक|सांतानिक|सान्तानिकः
सान्तानिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Expansive, (as a shrub, &c.)<BR>	 2. Rela-<BR>ting to descendants, posterity, &c.<BR>	 3. Relating to the heavenly tree<BR>Santāna.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A Brāhman intending to marry for the sake of<BR>issue.<BR> E. सन्तान, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्व्|सांत्व्
सान्त्व् r. 10th. cl. (सान्त्वयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To appease, to conciliate.<BR>	 2. To comfort; also षान्त्व्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्व|सांत्व|सान्त्वं|सांत्वः|सान्त्वः
सान्त्व mn. (-न्त्वः-न्त्वं)<BR>	 1. Conciliation, reconciling, appeasing.<BR>	 2. Pleasing<BR>and conciliatory language.<BR>	 3. Cleverness, dexterity.<BR>	 4. Mildness.<BR>5. Friendly salutation.<BR> E. सान्त्व् to console or appease, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्वन|सांत्वन|सांत्वनं|सान्त्वनं
सान्त्वन n. (-नं) Conciliation, reconcilement.<BR>	 nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Friendly or<BR>affectionate salutation and enquiry.<BR>	 2. Speaking in a kindly and<BR>conciliatory manner.<BR> E. सान्त्व् to console, &c., aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्वयत्
सान्त्वयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Consoling, appeasing.<BR> E. सान्त्व् to console, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्ववाद|सान्त्ववादः
सान्त्ववाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Speaking in a kindly and affectionate manner.<BR>E. सान्त्व affection, and वाद speech, (whose.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्दीपनि|सांदीपनि|सांदीपनिः|सान्दीपनिः
सान्दीपनि m. (-निः) A sage who was the preceptor of KṚṢṆA and BALARĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्दृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिकं|सान्दृष्टिकं
सान्दृष्टिक n. (-कं) Immediate consequence.<BR>	 f. (-की) Relating to present<BR>perception.<BR> E. सम् with, दृष्टि sight, present perception, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्र|सांद्र|सान्द्रं|सान्द्रः
सान्द्र mfn. (-न्द्रः-न्द्रा-न्द्रं)<BR>	 1. Thick, coarse, gross.<BR>	 2. Soft, smooth, bland.<BR>3. Pleasing, agreeable.<BR>	 4. Much, abundant.<BR>	 5. Unctuous, viscid,<BR>oily.<BR>	 6. Close, compact, not having interstices.<BR>	 7. Stout, robust.<BR>	 8.<BR>Clustering, collected.<BR>	 9. Excessive, vehement.<BR>	 n. (-न्द्रं)<BR>	 1. A wood,<BR>a thicket.<BR>	 2. A heap, a cluster.<BR> E. स for सह with, together, अदि<BR>to bind, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्रता
सान्द्रता f. (-ता) Thickness, grossness, viscidity.<BR> E. सान्द्र, and तल् added; with त्व, सान्द्रत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्रपुष्प|सान्द्रपुष्पः
सान्द्रपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) Beleric myrobalan.<BR> E. सान्द्र thick, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्रस्निग्ध|सान्द्रस्निग्धः
सान्द्रस्निग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं) Thick and unctuous.<BR> E. सान्द्र thick, स्निग्ध<BR>unctuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्धिक|सांधिक|सांधिकः|सान्धिकः
सान्धिक m. (-कः) A distiller.<BR> E. सन्धा distilling, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्धिविग्रहिक|सांधिविग्रहिक|सांधिविग्रहिकः
सान्धिविग्रहिक m. (-कः) A minister of peace and war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्ध्य|सांध्य|सान्ध्यः
सान्ध्य mfn. (-न्ध्यः-न्ध्यी-न्ध्यं) Produced at or relating to the evening, &c. E.<BR>सन्ध्या twilight, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्नहनिक|सांनहनिक|सांनहनिकः|सान्नहनिकः
सान्नहनिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Calling to arms, sounding, (as an alarum,<BR>&c.)<BR>	 2. Bearing or putting on armour.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A squire, an armour-<BR>bearer.<BR> E. सन्नाहन arming, ठक् aff., implying relation or causation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्नाय्य|सांनाय्य|सान्नाय्यं|सांनाय्यः
सान्नाय्य n. (-य्यं) Any substance mixed with clarified butter and offered<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">Page781-b+ 60</a>]<BR>as a burnt offering.<BR> E. सम् before णी to bring, (to the sacrificial<BR>fire,) ण्यत् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्निध्य|सांनिध्य|सांनिध्यं|सान्निध्यं
सान्निध्य n. (-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Proximity, vicinity.<BR>	 2. Presence, attendance.<BR> E. सन्निध near, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्निध्यतस
सान्निध्यतस Ind. From near, from the presence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्निपातिक|सांनिपातिक|सान्निपातिकः
सान्निपातिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Complicated, (as disease,) relating to the<BR>morbid state of the three humours collectively.<BR>	 2. Miscellaneous,<BR>promiscuous, collective.<BR> E. सन्निपात collection, mixture, aff. ठञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्न्यासिक|सांन्यासिक|सांन्यासिकः|सान्न्यासिकः
सान्न्यासिक m. (-कः) A beggar, a Brāhman of the fourth or mendicant<BR>order.<BR> E. सन्न्यास abandonment, (of the world,) ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्वय
सान्वय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Related or of kin to.<BR>	 2. In connection with<BR>family or descendants.<BR>	 3. In order or succession.<BR> E. स with, अन्वय<BR>descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न
सापत्न f. (-त्नी) Born from a rival wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न्य|सापत्न्यं|सापत्न्यः
सापत्न्य m. (-त्न्यः)<BR>	 1. An enemy.<BR>	 2. The children of the different wives of<BR>the same husband.<BR>	 n. (-त्न्यं)<BR>	 1. Plurality of wives, or the condition<BR>of the wife of one who has other wives.<BR>	 2. Ambition, rivalry. E.<BR>सपत्नी a fellow-wife, or सपत्न an enemy, ष्यञ् pleonasm or aff. of the<BR>abstract, or यञ् or अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्य|सापत्यः
सापत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Having progeny.<BR> E. स with, अपत्य offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापराध
सापराध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Faulty, offending.<BR> E. स with, अपराध fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापिण्ड्य|सापिंड्य|सापिंड्यं|सापिण्ड्यं
सापिण्ड्य n. (-ण्ड्यं) Consanguinity, kindred, connection by presenting<BR>obsequial offerings to the same persons.<BR> E. सपिण्ड, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपदीन|साप्तपदीनं
साप्तपदीन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Friendship.<BR>	 2. Circumambulation of the nuptial fire<BR>by the bride and bridegroom in seven steps, (after which the mar-<BR>riage is complete.)<BR> E. सप्त seven, पद a step or pace, and खञ् aff.; to<BR>be formed with any with whom seven paces are walked together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपौरुष
साप्तपौरुष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Extending to seven generations, &c.<BR> E. सप्त<BR>seven, पुरुष male, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साफल्य|साफल्यं
साफल्य n. (-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Productiveness, fruitfulness.<BR>	 2. Advantage.<BR>	 3. Success.<BR> E. स with, फल fruit, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साब्दी
साब्दी f. (-ब्दी) A sort of grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभ्यसूय
साभ्यसूय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Envious, malicious.<BR> E. स with, अभ्यसूया malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्
साम् r. 10th cl. (सामयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To conciliate, to appease.<BR>	 2. To pacify,<BR>to tranquillize; more properly षाम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामक|सामकं|सामकः
सामक n. (-कं) The principal of a debt, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A whet-stone.<BR> E. सम<BR>equal, अण् or वुञ् aff.; or साम्-ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग|सामगः
सामग m. (-गः) A Brāhman who chants or recites the Sāma-Veda.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-गी) The wife of a Sāma-Vedi Brāhman.<BR> E. साम the Sāma-Veda,<BR>गै to sing, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग्री
सामग्री f. (-ग्री)<BR>	 1. Collection or assemblage of materials, apparatus.<BR>	 2.<BR>Provision. E. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग्र्य|सामग्र्यं
सामग्र्य nf. (-ग्र्यं-ग्री)<BR>	 1. Entireness, wholeness, the whole.<BR>	 2. Train,<BR>retinue.<BR>	 3. Implements, instruments, apparatus.<BR>	 4. Stock, effects.<BR>E. समग्र all, whole, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामज|सामजः
सामज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Producing from or produced by the Sāma-Veda.<BR>m. (-जः) An elephant.<BR> E. साम the Veda, ज born; also सामजात, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामञ्जस्य|सामंजस्य|सामंजस्यं|सामञ्जस्यं
सामञ्जस्य n. (-स्यं) Fitness, accordance, propriety.<BR> E. समञ्जस, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्
सामन् n. (-म)<BR>	 1. The Sāma-Veda, the prayers of which composed in<BR>metre, are always sung or chanted: the Chāndogya Upanishad<BR>belongs to this Veda.<BR>	 2. Conciliation, reconciling, appeasing.<BR>	 3.<BR>Calming, tranquillizing.<BR>	 4. Speaking kindly or tenderly.<BR>	 5. Gentle-<BR>ness.<BR>	 6. Negociation, (one of the four means of success against<BR>an enemy.)<BR>	 f. (-नी) A rope, for tying cattle.<BR> E. षो to destroy,<BR>(sin,) Unādi aff. मनिन्, and ङीष् added for the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्त|सामंत|सामन्तः
सामन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Limitative, boundary, bounding.<BR>	 2. Bordering,<BR>neighbouring.<BR>	 3. Universal.<BR>	 m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. The chief of a district.<BR>	 2. A<BR>neighbour.<BR>	 3. An attendant or companion of a chieftain.<BR>	 4. A<BR>leader, a captain, a champion.<BR>	 5. A neighbouring prince.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं)<BR>Neighbourhood.<BR> E. समन्त end, term, अण् aff. of relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्तवासिन्
सामन्तवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Dwelling in the borders, bordering,<BR>neighbouring.<BR> E. समन्त, वासिन् who abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=781-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्य|सामन्यः
सामन्य m. (-न्यः) A Brāhman conversant with the Sāma Veda.<BR> E. सामन्,<BR>and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामय
सामय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Sick, diseased.<BR> E. स with, आमय sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयिक|सामयिकः
सामयिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Seasonable, punctual, observing time or<BR>season.<BR>	 2. Precise, exact.<BR>	 3. Stipulated, according to agreement.<BR>	 4.<BR>Conventional, customary.<BR>	 5. Periodical.<BR>	 6. Temporary.<BR> E. समय<BR>time or engagement, ठञ् or ठक् aff. of relation or possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयिकाभाव|सामयिकाभावः
सामयिकाभाव m. (-वः) Temporary, nonexistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयोनि|सामयोनिः
सामयोनि mfn. (-निः-निः-नि) Born from or produced by the SĀMA.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-निः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. An elephant.<BR> E. सामन् the Veda, and योनि<BR>place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्थ्य|सामर्थ्यं
सामर्थ्य n. (-र्थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Power, force, ability, fortitude, strength.<BR>	 2. Fitness,<BR>suitableness.<BR>	 3. Capacity, adequacy.<BR>	 4. (In grammar,) Mutual<BR>relation of words.<BR>	 5. Sense or force of words.<BR>	 6. Wealth.<BR>	 7. Interest,<BR>advantage.<BR>	 8. Sameness of aim or object.<BR> E. समर्थ्य able, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्ष
सामर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं) Enraged, in wrath.<BR> E. स with, अमर्ष anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवायिक|सामवायिकः
सामवायिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A principal minister or counsellor.<BR>	 2. The chief<BR>of a company or corporation.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Belonging to an assembly.<BR>2. Relating to intimate connection, (in logic.)<BR> E. समवाय an<BR>assembly, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामसङ्गायक
सामसङ्गायक m. (-कः) A chanter of the Sāma-Veda.<BR> E. साम, सङ्गायक chanter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामाजिक|सामाजिकः
सामाजिक m. (-कः) An assistant or spectator at an assembly, &c. E.<BR>समाज an assembly, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामानाधिकरण्य|सामानाधिकरण्यं
सामानाधिकरण्य n. (-ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Common office, function of government, &c.<BR>2. The receptacle or substratum of common properties. E.<BR>समानाधिकरण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्य|सामान्यं
सामान्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Common, general, generic, universal.<BR>	 n. (-न्यं)<BR>1. Kind, sort, specific or generic property or character.<BR>	 2. Common<BR>property, generality, community.<BR>	 3. Public affairs or business.<BR>4. Totality, entireness.<BR>	 5. A figure of rhetoric, the connection of<BR>different objects by common properties.<BR>	 6. A general proposition.<BR>f. (-न्या) A female who is common to all men, a harlot.<BR> E. समान<BR>common, (to many individuals,) ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यज्ञान
सामान्यज्ञान n. (-नं) The perception of common or generic properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यतस्
सामान्यतस् Ind. Generally, commonly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यलक्षण
सामान्यलक्षण n. (-णं) A generic or specific definition or character. E.<BR>सामान्य, and लक्षण mark or description.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यशासन|सामान्यशासनं
सामान्यशासन n. (-नं) A general edict or enactment.<BR> E. सामान्य common,<BR>and शासन a grant, an edict, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामासिक
सामासिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Compounded, composite.<BR>	 2. Comprehensive,<BR>collective.<BR>	 3. Brief, summary.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The aggregate of compounds.<BR>E. समास, and ठक् aff. of relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामि
सामि Ind.<BR>	 1. Half, unfinished.<BR>	 2. Blamably.<BR>	 3. Vile, despised.<BR> E. षाम् for<BR>षान्त्व to appease, अच् added, इ substituted for the final; or साम्-इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिकृत|सामिकृतः
सामिकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Halved, divided.<BR> E. सामि half, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिभुक्त|सामिभुक्तः
सामिभुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Half eaten.<BR> E. सामि half, and भुक्त eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिपीत|सामिपीतः
सामिपीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Half-drank.<BR> E. सामि half, and पीत drank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिधेनी
सामिधेनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A prayer used on adding fuel to the sacrificial fire.<BR>2. Fuel.<BR>	 3. A kind of deer.<BR> E. सम्-इन्ध-करणे ल्युट् नि० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीची
सामीची f. (-ची) Praise, panegyric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीप्य|सामीप्यं|सामीप्यः
सामीप्य n. (-प्यं) Proximity, nearness.<BR>	 m. (-प्यः) A neighbour.<BR> E. समीप<BR>near, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्र|सामुद्रं|सामुद्रः
सामुद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्री-द्रं) Marine, sea-born, &c.<BR>	 n. (-द्रं)<BR>	 1. A spot or mark<BR>on the body.<BR>	 2. Sea-salt.<BR>	 3. Cuttle-fish-bone.<BR>	 m. (-द्रः) A mariner,<BR>a voyager.<BR> E. समुद्र the sea, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रिक|सामुद्रिकः
सामुद्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating to spots on the body, supposed<BR>to indicate good or ill fortune.<BR>	 2. Oceanic.<BR>	 m. (-कः) An interpreter<BR>of spots on the body.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Palmistry.<BR> E. समुद्र a spot or mole,<BR>ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामोद
सामोद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Fragrant, odoriferous.<BR> E. स with, आमोद fragrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्नी
साम्नी f. (-म्नी) A sort of metre, one of the classes occurring in the<BR>Vedas.<BR> E. सामन the Sāma-Veda, and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्पराय|सांपराय|सांपरायः
साम्पराय f. (-यी)<BR>	 1. Warlike.<BR>	 2. Relating to the other world.<BR>	 mn. (-यः-यं)<BR>1. Conflict.<BR>	 2. The future.<BR>	 3. Means of attaining a future world.<BR>4. Investigation.<BR>	 5. Uncertainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्परायिक|सांपरायिक|साम्परायिकं|सांपरायिकः
साम्परायिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Future, of or in a future state of being.<BR>2. Calamitous.<BR>	 3. Relating to war or battle.<BR>	 n. (-कं) War, battle.<BR>m. (-कः) A war-chariot.<BR> E. सम्पराय futurity, &c., and ठक् or ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्परायिककल्प|सांपरायिककल्प|सांपरायिककल्पः
साम्परायिककल्प m. (-ल्पः) Military form, strategic array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रत|साम्प्रतं
साम्प्रत f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Fit, proper.<BR>	 2. Relevant, pertinent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रतम्|सांप्रतम्
साम्प्रतम् Ind.<BR>	 1. Now, at this time.<BR>	 2. Fitly, properly.<BR> E. सम् and प्र<BR>before तन् to spread, aff. डम्; the first vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रतिक|सांप्रतिक
साम्प्रतिक f. (-की)<BR>	 1. Belonging to the present time or occasion.<BR>	 2. Fit,<BR>proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्प्रदायिक|सांप्रदायिक
साम्प्रदायिक f. (-की) Belonging to traditional doctrine, handed down by tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्ब्
साम्ब् r. 10th cl. (साम्बयति-ते) To join, to connect, to assemble; also षाम्ब ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बर|सांबरं|साम्बरं
साम्बर n. (-रं) The sambhar-salt.<BR> E. सम्बर the country, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बरी|सांबरी
साम्बरी f. (-री) A female juggler. E. See शाम्बरी; the श being changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्भवी|सांभवी
साम्भवी f. (-वी) Red Lodh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्भस्|सांभस्
साम्भस् mfn. (-म्भाः-म्भाः-म्भः) Having or being united with water.<BR> E. स with, अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्य|साम्यं
साम्य n. (-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Equality, sameness.<BR>	 2. Likeness, similarity.<BR>	 3.<BR>Indifference.<BR> E. सम same, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्यता
साम्यता f. (-ता) Equality, sameness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व, साम्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्राज्य|साम्राज्यं
साम्राज्य n. (-ज्यं) Imperial rule, dominion, empire.<BR>	 m. (-ज्यः) The des-<BR>cendant of a prince or man of the military tribe.<BR> E. सम्राज् an<BR>emperor, ष्यञ् aff. of the abstract, or ण्य patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साय|सायं|सायः
साय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Evening, close of day.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. End, termination.<BR>close in general.<BR> E. षो to end or destroy, &c., घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायंकाल
सायंकाल m. (-लः) Eventide, evening.<BR> E. सायम् evening, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायक|सायकः
सायक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An arrow.<BR>	 2. A sword.<BR>	 f. (-यिका) Standing in order.<BR>E. षो to destroy, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायकपुङ्ख|सायकपुंख|सायकपुङ्खः
सायकपुङ्ख mf. (-ङ्खः-ङ्खा) The feathered end of an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायन|सायनं
सायन n. (-नं) The longitude of a planet reckoned from the vernal<BR>equinoctial point.<BR> E. स with, अयन the equinoctial period.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायन्तन|सायंतन|सायन्तनः
सायन्तन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Belonging to the evening, vespertine.<BR> E. साय<BR>evening, ट्युल् aff., तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायम्
सायम् Ind. Evening, close of the day, in the evening.<BR> E. सो-ञमु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायमण्डन
सायमण्डन n. (-नं) The place or time of sunset.<BR> E. साय, मण्डन embellishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायाह्न|सायाह्नः
सायाह्न m. (-ह्नः) The evening, eventide.<BR> E. सायम् evening, and अहन् day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायिन्
सायिन् m. (-यी) A horseman, a groom.<BR> E. स for सह with, अय् to go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायुज्य|सायुज्यं
सायुज्य n. (-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. Likeness, similarity.<BR>	 2. Identification, intimate<BR>union, (especially with the Deity, considered as one of the four<BR>grades of mukti.)<BR> E. स with, युज् what joins, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साये
साये Ind. In the evening, at the close of the day.<BR> E. साय evening, the<BR>seventh case, used as a particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार|सारं|सारः
सार r. 10th cl. (सारयति-ते) To become weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार|सारं|सारः
सार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Best, excellent.<BR>	 2. Irrefragable, (as an argument.)<BR>mn. (-रः-रं)<BR>	 1. The pith or sap of trees, &c.<BR>	 2. Strength, vigour.<BR>	 3.<BR>The essence of anything, the essential or vital part of it.<BR>	 4. The subs-<BR>tance or material part, (of a speech, book, message, &c.)<BR>	 5. Marrow.<BR>6. Air, wind.<BR>	 7. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 8. Firmness, hardness.<BR>	 9. The<BR>coagulum of curds, &c., cream.<BR>	 10. Fresh butter.<BR>	 11. Prowess,<BR>valour, heroism.<BR>	 12. Nectar.<BR>	 13. Wealth, riches.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A man<BR>at chess, backgammon, &c.<BR>	 2. Worth, excellence.<BR>	 3. Compedium,<BR>summary.<BR>	 4. Impure carbonate of soda.<BR>	 5. Climax, (in rhetoric.)<BR>	 n.<BR>(-रं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. Wealth.<BR>	 3. Propriety, fitness.<BR>	 4. Steel.<BR>	 5.<BR>Wood, thicket.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Essential.<BR>	 2. Best.<BR>	 3. Strong,<BR>vigorous.<BR>	 4. Genuine, true.<BR>	 5. Thoroughly proved 6. Durbā-<BR>grass.<BR>	 f. (-री) The Shālika or Sārikā, (Turdus salica,<BR>BUCH.)<BR> E. सृ to go, aff. घञ्; or सार्-अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=782-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारक|सारकः
सारक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Purgative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारगन्ध|सारगंध|सारगन्धः
सारगन्ध m. (-न्धः) Sandal wood.<BR> E. सार essence, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारघ|सारघं
सारघ n. (-घं) Honey.<BR> E. सरघा a bee, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारङ्ग|सारंग|सारङ्गः
सारङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Variegated, of a variegated colour.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1.<BR>Variegated colour.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR>	 3. An elephant.<BR>	 4. The spotted deer.<BR>5. The Chātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>	 6. The Kokila or Indian<BR>cuckoo.<BR>	 7. A large kind of crane, (Ardea Sarunga, CAREY.)<BR>	 8. A<BR>peacock.<BR>	 9. A cloud.<BR>	 10. A tree.<BR>	 11. A parasol.<BR>	 12. A garment,<BR>cloth, clothes.<BR>	 13. Hair.<BR>	 14. A lotus.<BR>	 15. A flower.<BR>	 16. A conch-<BR>shell.<BR>	 17. A jewel.<BR>	 18. Gold.<BR>	 19. A bow.<BR>	 20. KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 21.<BR>Sandal.<BR>	 22. Camphor.<BR>	 23. The earth.<BR>	 24. Night.<BR>	 25. Light.<BR>	 26.<BR>A large bee.<BR>	 27. A kind of musical instrument.<BR>	 28. An ornament.<BR>29. Śiva.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी)<BR>	 1. A sort of fiddle.<BR>	 2. A kind of spotted deer.<BR>E. सृ to go, अङ्गच् Unādi aff., or सार strength, &c., गम् to go,<BR>खच् aff.; also शारङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारङ्गिक|सारंगिक|सारंगिकः|सारङ्गिकः
सारङ्गिक m. (-कः) A bird or deer-catcher.<BR> E. सारङ्ग as above, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारज|सारजं
सारज n. (-जं) Fresh butter.<BR> E. सार cream, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारण|सारणं|सारणः
सारण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. Dysentery, diarrhœa.<BR>	 2. Hog-plum, (Spondias mangi-<BR>fera.)<BR>	 3. A counsellor and ambassador from RĀVAṆA to RĀMA.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-णी)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Pæderia fetida.)<BR>	 2. A canal, a small river.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-णं) A kind of perfume.<BR>	 f. (-णी) Adj. Causing to grow or flow. E.<BR>सृ to go, (causal form,) ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणा
सारणा f. (-णा) A particular process to which mineral substances are subjected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणि|सारणिः
सारणि f. (-णिः-णी)<BR>	 1. A small river.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Pæderia fetida.)<BR>	 3. A<BR>canal or water-pipe.<BR> E. सृ to go, causal form, अनि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणिक|सारणिकः
सारणिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Travelling, way-faring, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A<BR>traveller.<BR> E. सरणि a road, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणिकघ्न|सारणिकघ्नः
सारणिकघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A robber.<BR> E. सारणिक a traveller, and घ्न who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारण्ड|सारंड|सारंडः|सारण्डः
सारण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A snake's egg.<BR> E. सृ to go, (causal form,) अण्डन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारतरु|सारतरुः
सारतरु m. (-रुः) The plantain tree, (Musa sapientum.)<BR> E. सार sap, तरु a<BR>tree, having no timber in the stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारतस्
सारतस् Ind.<BR>	 1. By or with vigour or essence, vigorously, essentially.<BR>2. According to wealth.<BR> E. सार, तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारता
सारता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Strength, substance.<BR>	 2. Essence.<BR> E. सार, तल् aff.; also with त्व, सारत्वं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथि|सारथिः
सारथि m. (-थिः) A charioteer.<BR> E. सृ to go, (causal form,) अथिण् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथ्य|सारथ्यं
सारथ्य n. (-थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Charioteering, driving, 2. Conveyance.<BR> E. सारथि, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारदा
सारदा f. (-दा)<BR>	 1. A name of SARASWATĪ.<BR>	 2. A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. सार<BR>essence, (of wisdom and eloquence,) दा to give, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारभङ्ग|सारभङ्गः
सारभङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Void of pith, substance, real strength, &c.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-ङ्गं) Destroying vigour, overcoming strength, &c.<BR> E. सार, and भङ्ग<BR>breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारभाण्ड|सारभाण्डं
सारभाण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A natural vessel, as the bag or skin in which musk<BR>is sold, &c.<BR>	 2. A bale of goods.<BR>	 3. Implements.<BR> E. सार essence, and<BR>भाण्ड a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारमेय|सारमेयः
सारमेय m. (-यः) A dog.<BR>	 f. (-यी) A bitch.<BR> E. सरमा a bitch, ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारयोग
सारयोग m. (-गः) Possession or application of the essence of anything.<BR>E. सार, and योग union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारलोह|सारलोहं
सारलोह n. (-हं) Steel.<BR> E. सार and लोह iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारल्य|सारल्यं
सारल्य n. (-ल्यं) Straightness, (lit. and fig.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारव|सारवः
सारव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Belonging or relating to the river Sarayu.<BR> E. सरयु<BR>the river, अण् aff., special form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारवत्|सारवन्त्
सारवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Substantial, having pith, substance, strength,<BR>&c.<BR>	 2. Fertile.<BR> E. सार, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारवर्ज्जित|सारवर्जित|सारवर्ज्जितः
सारवर्ज्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Pithless, sapless.<BR> E. सार substance, and वर्ज्जित deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस|सारसं|सारसः
सारस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Relating or belonging to a lake or pond, &c.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-सं)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. A woman's zone.<BR>	 mf. (-सः-सी) The Sāras or<BR>Indian crane, male and female, (Ardea Sibirica.)<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>moon.<BR>	 2. A bird in general.<BR> E. सरस् a pond, a lake, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारसन|सारसनं
सारसन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A woman's zone or girdle, formed of twenty-five<BR>strings.<BR>	 2. A military belt or girdle worn round the waist or chest,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">Page783-b+ 60</a>]<BR>upon the coat of mail, to bind it to the body.<BR> E. सार strength, and<BR>षण् to give, aff. अच्, or अस् to diffuse, aff. ल्युट्; also सारशन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस्वत|सारस्वतः
सारस्वत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं)<BR>	 1. Relating to the goddess SARASWATĪ, or to<BR>the river, &c.<BR>	 2. Eloquent, learned.<BR>	 m. Plu. (-ताः)<BR>	 1. The people of<BR>the Sāraswata country, or the north-west part of the province of<BR>Delhi.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A staff of the Vilwa tree.<BR>	 2. The north-west part<BR>of the province of Delhi or part of the Punjāb.<BR>	 3. A saint, sprung<BR>according to the legend, indirectly from the personified river<BR>Sarasvatī.<BR>	 4. A Brāhman of a particular family, called Sāraswata,<BR>from his coming from that country or supposed descent from the<BR>sanctified person last mentioned.<BR>	 5. A particular ceremonial used in<BR>the worship of Sarasvatī.<BR> E. सरस्वती the goddess, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साराल|सारालः
साराल m. (-लः) Sesamum. “तिलवृक्षे.”<BR> E. सारमालाति आ + ला-क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारासार
सारासार m. (-रः) Strength and weakness, substance and emptiness,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सार, and असार want of vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारि|सारिः
सारि mf. (-रिः-री)<BR>	 1. A man at chess or backgammon, &c.<BR>	 2. A kind<BR>of bird.<BR> E. सृ to go, causal form, इन् aff.; also शारि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिका
सारिका f. (-का) A kind of bird, (Turdus Salica, BUCH.) but applied also<BR>to the Mainā, (Gracula religiosa.)<BR> E. सृ to go, aff. ण्वुल्; also<BR>शारिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिन्
सारिन् f. (-रिणी) Adj.<BR>	 1. Going in front.<BR>	 2. Having the essence or<BR>substance of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिवा
सारिवा f. (-वा) A creeping plant, (Echites frutescens.) E. See शारिवा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारूप्य|सारूप्यं
सारूप्य n. (-प्यं)<BR>	 1. Identity of form.<BR>	 2. Close resemblance.<BR>	 3. Assimilation<BR>to or identification with the deity, (one of the four grades of<BR>mukti.)<BR>	 4. (In drama,) Surprise at seeing an object or its like-<BR>ness previously seen elsewhere.<BR> E. स with, रूप form, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्गल
सार्गल f. (-ला) Adj. Prevented, barred, impeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थ|सार्थः
सार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Opulent, wealthy.<BR>	 2. Of like meaning or<BR>purport.<BR>	 3. Significant importing, having meaning.<BR>	 m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>multitude of similar animals.<BR>	 2. A company of traders, a caravan,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. A number or multitude in general.<BR>	 4. A wealthy man.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-र्था)<BR>	 1. Having an object.<BR>	 2. Useful, serviceable.<BR> E. सृ to go, causal<BR>form, थन् Unādi aff.; or स for सह, &c., and अर्थ wealth or meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थक|सार्थकः
सार्थक f. (-का) Adj. Having meaning.<BR>	 2. Serviceable, advantageous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थज
सार्थज Adj. Reared in a caravan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थवत्|सार्थवन्त्
सार्थवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Meaning, intending.<BR>	 2. Having a meaning.<BR>3. Numerous in company.<BR> E. सार्थ, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थवाह|सार्थवाहः
सार्थवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A merchant, a trader.<BR>	 2. The leader of a caravan.<BR>E. सार्थ a company, a caravan, and वह् to bear, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थिक|सार्थिकः
सार्थिक m. (-कः) A merchant, a trader.<BR> E. सार्थ, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्द्र|सार्द्रं
सार्द्र mfn. (-र्द्रः-र्द्रा-र्द्रं) Wet, moist, damp.<BR> E. स for सह with, आर्द्र wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्द्ध
सार्द्ध mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धी-र्द्धं) Joined with half, (used chiefly in composi-<BR>tion, as सार्द्धशत a hundred and a half, i. e. fifty.)<BR> E. स with, अर्द्ध half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्द्धम्
सार्द्धम् Ind. With, together with. स for सह with, ऋद्ध increased, अमु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्प|सार्पः|सार्प्प
सार्प mfn. (-र्पः-र्पी-र्पं) Relating to a snake.<BR>	 f. (-र्पी) The ninth lunar<BR>asterism, of which the serpents (Aśleshā) are the presiding<BR>deities.<BR> E. सर्प a snake, and अण् aff.; also read सार्प्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष|सार्पिषः
सार्पिष mfn. (-षः-षी-षं) Dressed, &c. with Ghee or clarified butter. E.<BR>सर्पिस् Ghee, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष्क|सार्पिष्कं
सार्पिष्क mfn. (-ष्कः-ष्का-ष्कं) Cooked or dressed with Ghee.<BR> E. सर्पिस Ghee, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्व|सार्व|सार्वः|सार्व्वः
सार्व्व mfn. (-र्व्वः-र्व्वी-र्व्वं) Suitable to or fit for all, relating to all, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-र्व्वः) A Jaina deified sage.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, (knowledge, &c.), अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वकामिक|सार्वकामिक
सार्व्वकामिक f. (-की) Satisfying every wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वकालिक|सार्वकालिक
सार्व्वकालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Of all times or seasons.<BR> E. सर्व्वकाल, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वजनिक|सार्वजनिक|सार्व्वजनिकः
सार्व्वजनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging, fit or suited to all<BR>men.<BR> E. सर्व्वजन all men, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वजनीन|सार्वजनीन|सार्व्वजनीनः
सार्व्वजनीन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Belonging or relating, fit or suited to all<BR>men, &c.<BR>	 2. Public, universal.<BR> E. सर्व्वजन all men, खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वज्ञ|सार्वज्ञ|सार्वज्ञं
सार्व्वज्ञ n. (-ज्ञं) Omniscience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=783-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वत्रिक|सार्वत्रिक
सार्व्वत्रिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Suited to, or belonging to every place. E.<BR>सर्व्वत्र every where, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वदैवत्य|सार्वदैवत्य
सार्व्वदैवत्य mfn. (-त्यः-ती-त्यं) Presided over by, or sacred to all the gods.<BR>E. सर्व्व, देवता a god, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वधातुक|सार्वधातुक
सार्व्वधातुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Applicable to the whole of a radical term,<BR>(an affix, &c.,) or to the complete form of the verbal base after<BR>the conjugational characteristics are affixed, i. e. to the four conju-<BR>gational or special tenses, (in gram.)<BR>	 n. (-कं) Name of the verbal<BR>terminations of the four special tenses.<BR> E. सर्व्व, धातु a root, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वभौतिक|सार्वभौतिक
सार्व्वभौतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Belonging or relating to all elements,<BR>beings, &c.<BR>	 2. Comprising all animated beings.<BR> E. सर्व्वभूत, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वभौम|सार्वभौम|सार्वभौमः|सार्व्वभौमः
सार्व्वभौम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं) Relating to or consisting of the whole earth,<BR>known throughout the earth, &c.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The elephant of<BR>KUVERA, as regent of the north.<BR>	 2. An emperor, a universal<BR>monarch.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, भूमि earth, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वलौकिक|सार्वलौकिक|सार्व्वलौकिकः
सार्व्वलौकिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Universally known, prevailing throughout<BR>the universe.<BR> E. सर्व्व all, लोक a world, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्ववर्णिक|सार्ववर्णिक
सार्व्ववर्णिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Of every kind or sort.<BR>	 2. Belonging or<BR>relating to every tribe, &c.<BR> E. सर्व्ववर्ण, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्वविभक्तिक|सार्वविभक्तिक
सार्व्वविभक्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Applicable or belonging to all the cases<BR>of a noun, (in gram.)<BR> E. सर्व्व, विभक्ति inflection, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्ववेदस|सार्ववेदस|सार्ववेदसः
सार्व्ववेदस n. (-सः) One who gives away all his wealth at a sacred rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व्ववेद्य|सार्ववेद्य|सार्व्ववेद्यः
सार्व्ववेद्य m. (-द्यः) A Brāhman conversant with all the Vedas.<BR> E. सर्व्व<BR>all, वेद Veda, and यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्षप|सार्षपः
सार्षप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Mustard, made of or from mustard.<BR>	 n. (-पं)<BR>Mustard-oil.<BR> E. सर्षप, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्टि
सार्ष्टि Adj. Possessing the same rank or condition, having the same power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्टिता
सार्ष्टिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Equality in rank, condition, power, &c.<BR>	 2. Equality<BR>with the supreme being in power and all the divine attributes,<BR>(considered as the fourth grade of mukti.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल|सालः
साल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A wall surrounding a building, &c.<BR>	 2. A tree in<BR>general.<BR>	 3. The Śal tree, (Shoroa robusta.)<BR>	 4. A fish, (Ophioce-<BR>phalus Wrahl, HAM.)<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. A rampart; more<BR>usually शाला.<BR> E. षल् to go, घञ् aff.; also शाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालग्राम
सालग्राम n. (-मं) A stone, a species of ammonite common in the<BR>Gandaka river, and worshipped by the Vaishnavas, as a type of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR> E. स with, अर a ring, ग्राम multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालन|सालनः
सालन m. (-नः) The resin of the Sāl tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालनिर्य्यास|सालनिर्यास|सालनिर्यासः
सालनिर्य्यास m. (-सः) The resinous exudation of the Sāl tree.<BR> E. साल, निर्य्यास exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालपर्णी
सालपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum;) also शालपर्णी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालपुष्प|सालपुष्पं
सालपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) A shrub, (Hibiscus mutabilis.) “स्थलपद्मे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालभञ्जिका|सालभंजिका
सालभञ्जिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A doll, a puppet.<BR>	 2. A harlot.<BR> E. साल the Śal tree<BR>or its wood, भञ्ज् to rub, ण्वुल् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालरस|सालरसः
सालरस m. (-सः) The resinous juice of the Śal tree.<BR> E. साल the Sāl, and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालवाहन|सालवाहनः
सालवाहन m. (-नः) The sovereing SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR> E. साल the Sāl tree,<BR>and वाहन a vehicle: see शालवाहन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालवेष्ट|सालवेष्टः
सालवेष्ट m. (-ष्टः) Turpentine, or the resinous exudation of the Sāl tree,<BR>E. साल the tree, वेष्ट exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालशृङ्ग|सालशृंग|सालशृङ्गं
सालशृङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) The upper part or coping of a wall.<BR> E. साल a wall, शृङ्ग horn or summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साला
साला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A house.<BR>	 2. A rampart. E. See शाला ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालाकारी
सालाकारी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A female overcome or won in battle.<BR>	 2. A house-<BR>worker.<BR> E. साला a house, कृ to make, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालातुरीय|सालातुरीयः
सालातुरीय m. (-यः) A name of PĀNĪNI. E. See शालातुरीय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालार|सालारं
सालार n. (-रं) A pin, a bracket, or shelf, projecting from a wall. E.<BR>साल a wall, ऋ to go, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालावृक|सालावृकः
सालावृक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A dog.<BR>	 2. A wolf.<BR>	 3. A jackal.<BR>	 4. A hyena.<BR>	 5. A<BR>cruel man.<BR> E. साला a house and वृक a wolf; more usually शालावृक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालूर|सालूरः
सालूर m. (-रः) A frog.<BR> E. षल् to go, ऊरच् aff.; the first vowel made<BR>long, and the initial changed; also शालूर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालेय|सालेयं|सालेयः
सालेय m. (-यः) A sort of fennel or dill, (Anethum sowa.) E. See शालेय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालोक्य|सालोक्यं
सालोक्य n. (-क्यं)<BR>	 1. The being in the same sphere or world with another.<BR>2. Residence in the same heaven with any particular deity.<BR> E. स<BR>with, लोक world, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालोक्यता
सालोक्यता f. (-ता) Habitation, state of abiding or dwelling.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्व|साल्वः
साल्व mfn. (-ल्वः-ल्वी-ल्वं) Belonging to the Sālwa country: more usually<BR>read शाल्व.<BR>	 m. (-ल्वः)<BR>	 1. The name of a demon, the enemy of VIṢṆU.<BR>2. The name of a country, or place.<BR>	 m. Plu. (-ल्वाः) The people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्वहन्
साल्वहन् m. (-हा) A name of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. साल्व a demon, हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्विक|साल्विकः
साल्विक m. (-कः) The sārikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साव|सावः
साव m. (-वः) A libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावक|सावकः
सावक mfn. (-कः-विका-कं)<BR>	 1. Generative, productive, causing birth,<BR>parturient, &c.<BR>	 2. Obstetric.<BR>	 f. (-विका) A midwife.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The<BR>young of any animal, (in this sense for शावक ।)<BR> E. षू to bear<BR>young, causal form, षुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावकाश
सावकाश f. (-शा) Having leisure, at leisure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावग्रह
सावग्रह f. (-हा) Having the grammatical mark called Avagraha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावज्ञ
सावज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं) Despising, disdainful.<BR> E. स with, अवज्ञा disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावद्य|सावद्यं
सावद्य n. (-द्यं) One of the three kinds of power attainable by an ascetic,<BR>(the other two being निरवद्य and सूक्ष्म ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधान|सावधानः
सावधान mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Careful, cautious.<BR>	 2. Diligent.<BR> E. स with, अवधान care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधि
सावधि Adj.<BR>	 1. Having a bound.<BR>	 2. Finite, defined, circumscribed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावन|सावनं|सावनः
सावन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Natural, (in astronomy;) as Sāvana-Dina, a<BR>natural-day, from sunrise to sunrise.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The conclusion of a<BR>sacrifice, the ceremonies by which it is terminated.<BR>	 2. An employ-<BR>er of priests for a sacrifice.<BR>	 3. The deity VARUṆA.<BR>	 4. A month of<BR>thirty solar days.<BR> E. षू to bear or produce, aff. ल्युट् and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावयव
सावयव f. (-वा) Composed of parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर|सावरः
सावर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The Lodh tree.<BR>	 2. Sin.<BR>	 3. Fault, offence. E. See शावर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावरण
सावरण f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. Clandestine, secret.<BR>	 2. Closed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण|सावर्णः
सावर्ण m. (-र्णः) The eighth Manu.<BR>	 f. (-र्णी) Relating to one of the same<BR>colour, tribe or caste.<BR> E. सवर्ण the wife of sun, his mother, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णलक्ष्य|सावर्णलक्ष्यं
सावर्णलक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. The skin.<BR>	 2. Mark of the sameness of colour or caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णि|सावर्णिः
सावर्णि m. (-र्णिः)<BR>	 1. The eighth Manu.<BR>	 2. A name applied to the 8th,<BR>9th, 10th, 11th, and 12th Manu or Brahma-Sāvarni, Daksha-<BR>Sāvarni, &c.<BR> E. सवर्ण, his mother, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण्य|सावर्ण्यं
सावर्ण्य n. (-र्ण्यं)<BR>	 1. Identity of caste, class, &c.<BR>	 2. Sameness of colour.<BR>	 3.<BR>The age presided over by the eighth MANU.<BR> E. सवर्ण, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावलेप
सावलेप f. (-पा) Full of pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावशेष
सावशेष mfn. (-षः-षा-षं)<BR>	 1. Imperfect, incomplete.<BR>	 2. Leaving a residue<BR>or remainder.<BR> E. स with, अवशेष remains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावष्टम्भ|सावष्टंभ
सावष्टम्भ f. (-म्भा) Possessing self-dependence, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावहेल
सावहेल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Despising, disdaining.<BR> E. स with, अवहेल disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्र|सावित्रं|सावित्रः
सावित्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. A Brāhman.<BR>	 2. Śiva.<BR>	 3. A Vasu or demigod so<BR>named.<BR>	 4. The sun.<BR>	 5. The embryo or fœtus.<BR>	 6. Karna.<BR>	 f. (-त्री)<BR>	 1. Umā,<BR>wife of Śiva.<BR>	 2. The holy verse of the Vedas, the repetition of<BR>which forms an essential part of the ceremonies, enjoined to the<BR>Brāhman, as daily observances: the prayer is personified as the<BR>wife of BRAHMĀ, and mystical mother of the Hindu classes,<BR>which are regenerated by investiture with the sacrificial string.<BR>3. The wife of SATYAVĀNA.<BR>	 4. A beam of light, a cluster of solar<BR>rays.<BR>	 5. Descended from the sun, belonging to the solar dynasty.<BR>n. (-त्रं) The sacrificial string, (so called owing to the repetition of<BR>the Gāyatri which forms a principal part of the ceremony of wear-<BR>ing the sacred thread.)<BR> E. सवित्र the sun, and अण् aff. of reference:<BR>the prayer is in fact addressed to that luminary, and the deities,<BR>&c. are manifestations of the planet or prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीपतित|सावित्रीपतितः
सावित्रीपतित m. (-तः) A man of the three first classes, not invested at<BR>the proper time with the sacrificial cord.<BR> E. सावित्री, पतित fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्ट|सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्टः
सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A man of the three first classes, not invested<BR>with the string at the proper season.<BR> E. सावित्री, and परिभ्रष्ट broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=784-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीव्रत|सावित्रीव्रतं
सावित्रीव्रत n. (-तं) A particular fast kept by Hindu woman on the last<BR>three days, or the last day of the bright-half of Jyaishtha to avert<BR>widowhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीसूत्र|सावित्रीसूत्रं
सावित्रीसूत्र n. (-त्रं) The sacrificial or characteristic cord of the three<BR>first classes.<BR> E. सावित्री the sacred text, (the repetition of which forms<BR>part of the ceremony of investiture,) सूत्र a thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साविष्कार
साविष्कार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Proud, haughty.<BR>	 2. Manifest.<BR> E. स with,<BR>आविष्कार manifestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशंस
साशंस f. (-सा) Full of desires or passion, hopeful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशङ्क|साशंक
साशङ्क f. (-ङ्का) Disheartened, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशयन्दक|साशयंदक|साशयंदकः|साशयन्दकः
साशयन्दक m. (-कः) A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशूक|साशूकः
साशूक m. (-कः) A blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्चर्य्य|साश्चर्य
साश्चर्य्य n. Adv. (-र्य्यं) With surprise.<BR> E. स with, आश्चर्य्य astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्र
साश्र f. (-श्रा)<BR>	 1. Having angles or corners.<BR>	 2. Tearful, weeping. See सास्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्रुधी
साश्रुधी f. (-धी) A wife's or husband's mother, a mother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साष्टाङ्गम्|साष्टांगम्
साष्टाङ्गम् Ind. Prostrating the eight limbs or members of the body: see प्रणाम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास
सास f. (-सा) Having a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासहि
सासहि mfn. (-हिः-हिः-हि) Able to bear much.<BR> E. सह् to bear, intens. v., कि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासुसू
सासुसू Adj. Having arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासूय
सासूय f. (-या) Adj. Envious, disdainful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्थिताम्रार्द्ध|सास्थिताम्रार्द्धं
सास्थिताम्रार्द्ध n. (-र्द्धं) Bell-metal.<BR> E. स with, अस्थि substance, ताम्र copper, अर्द्ध a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्ना
सास्ना f. (-स्रा) The dewlap of an ox or cow.<BR> E. सस् to sleep, न Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्र
सास्र mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं)<BR>	 1. Weeping, in tears.<BR>	 2. Cornered, angular. E.<BR>स with, अस्र a tear, or an angle; also साश्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहङ्कार|साहंकार
साहङ्कार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Proud, arrogant.<BR>	 2. United with the prin-<BR>ciple of egotism.<BR> E. स with, अहङ्कार pride, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहचर्य्य|साहचर्य|साहचर्यं|साहचर्य्यं
साहचर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Company, association, society, fellowship.<BR> E. सह with, चर going, aff. ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहन|साहनं
साहन n. (-नं) Sufference, endurance.<BR> E. षह् to bear, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहय|साहयः
साहय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Causing or enabling to endure.<BR> E. षह् to bear,<BR>causal form, साहि, and श aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहयक
साहयक n. (-कं) Friendship, fellowship.<BR> E. साहय a friend, aff. वुञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस|साहसं|साहसः
साहस n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Punishment, chastisement, fine, (also masculine in<BR>this sense.)<BR>	 2. Violence, the perpetration of any act of rapine<BR>or aggression.<BR>	 3. Oppression, cruelty.<BR>	 4. Hatred.<BR>	 5. Rape,<BR>ravishment.<BR>	 6. Boldness, daring.<BR>	 7. Rashness.<BR>	 8. Oblation with<BR>fire.<BR> E. सहस् strength, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसाङ्क|साहसांक|साहसाङ्कः
साहसाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIKRAMĀDITYA.<BR>	 2. Name of a poet.<BR>	 3.<BR>An epithet of a lexicographer.<BR> E. साहस violence, अङ्क a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसाध्यवसायिन्
साहसाध्यवसायिन् Adj. Acting with inconsiderate haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिक|साहसिकः
साहसिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Castigatory, inflicted as punishment.<BR>	 2.<BR>Perpetrated by violence.<BR>	 3. Violent, felonious, rapacious, brutal,<BR>cruel.<BR>	 4. Impetuous, rash.<BR>	 5. Bold, daring.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A robber, a<BR>free-booter.<BR>	 2. A desperado.<BR> E. साहस violence, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिन्
साहसिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>	 1. Violent, ferocious.<BR>	 2. Rash.<BR>	 3. Daring,<BR>bold.<BR> E. साहस, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसैकरसिक
साहसैकरसिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Intent on violence, brutal, ferocious. E.<BR>साहस, एक alone, रस taste, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस्र|साहस्रं|साहस्रः
साहस्र mfn. (-स्रः-स्री-स्रं)<BR>	 1. Bought with a thousand.<BR>	 2. Paid per thou-<BR>sand, as interest, duty, &c.<BR>	 3. Relating or belonging to a thousand.<BR>m. (-स्रः) An army or detachment, a thousand strong.<BR>	 n. (-स्रं) The<BR>aggregate of a thousand.<BR> E. सहस्र a thousand, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहायक|साहायकं
साहायक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Assistance, aid.<BR>	 2. Fellowship.<BR>	 3. A number of<BR>associates.<BR>	 4. Auxiliary troops.<BR> E. सहाय, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहाय्य|साहाय्यं
साहाय्य n. (-य्यं)<BR>	 1. Friendship.<BR>	 2. Help succour.<BR>	 3. Alliance.<BR> E. सहाय a friend, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहित्य|साहित्यं
साहित्य nf. (-त्य-ती) Society, association, connection, combination.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-त्यं) Poetry, belles-lettres, literary composition.<BR> E. सहित with,<BR>together with, aff. ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्य|साह्यं
साह्य n. (-ह्यं) Society, conjunction.<BR>	 2. Aid, assistance.<BR> E. सह with,<BR>together with, aff. of the abstract ष्यञ् or ण्यत् aff; or सह्य-अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्यकृत्
साह्यकृत् m. (-कृत्) A companion.<BR> E. साह्य society, कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्वय|साह्वयः
साह्वय m. (-यः) Fighting animals, (as cocks, &c.) for sport or money. E.<BR>स with, आह्वय challenging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सि
सि r. 5th cl. (सिनोति) r. 9th cl. (सिनाति) To bind, to ensnare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंह|सिंहः
सिंह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. LEO, the sign of the zodiac.<BR>	 3. (In com-<BR>position,) Pre-eminent.<BR>	 f. (-ही)<BR>	 1. The egg-plant, (Solanum Melon-<BR>gena.)<BR>	 2. A shrub, (Justicia.)<BR>	 3. A prickly nightshade.<BR>	 4. The<BR>mother of RĀHU.<BR>	 5. A lioness.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, क Unādi aff., ह<BR>substituted for the final, and नुम् inserted; or हिसि to injure or kill,<BR>अच् aff., and the radical consonants transposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहकेलि|सिंहकेलिः
सिंहकेलि m. (-लिः) A Bauddha saint, also named MANJUGHOSHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहकेशर|सिंहकेशरः
सिंहकेशर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A lion's mane.<BR>	 2. The Bakula tree, (Mimusops<BR>elengi.)<BR> E. सिंह a lion, केशर a mane, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहतल|सिंहतलः
सिंहतल n. (-लं) The open hands joined.<BR> E. सिंह a lion, तल the open palm; also read संहततल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहतुण्ड|सिंहतुंड|सिंहतुण्डः
सिंहतुण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A kind of fish.<BR>	 2. The Sehunda tree.<BR> E. सिंह, तुण्ड face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहद्वार|सिंहद्वारं
सिंहद्वार n. (-रं) A gate, an entrance, especially the chief gate of a man-<BR>sion or palace.<BR> E. सिंह chief, and द्वार a door-way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहध्वनि|सिंहध्वनिः
सिंहध्वनि m. (-निः)<BR>	 1. The roar or sound of a lion.<BR>	 2. A war-cry.<BR> E. सिंह,<BR>ध्वनि sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहनर्दिन्|सिंहनर्द्दिन्
सिंहनर्दिन् mfn. (-र्दी-र्दिनी-र्दि) Roaring like a lion.<BR> E. सिंह, नर्दिन् who or what sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहनाद|सिंहनादः
सिंहनाद m. (-दः) A war-cry, war-hoop, shouting or roaring upon making<BR>an onset.<BR> E. सिंह a lion, and नाद cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहनादक|सिंहनादकः
सिंहनादक m. (-कः) The roar or yelp of a lion.<BR>	 2. War-cry.<BR>	 f. (-दिका) A<BR>plant, (Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR> E. सिंह a lion, नाद sounding, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहपर्णी
सिंहपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda.)<BR> E. सिंह a lion, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहपुच्छी
सिंहपुच्छी f. (-च्छी) A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR> E. सिंह a lion,<BR>पुच्छ tail; also with कन् added, सिंहपुच्छिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहयाना
सिंहयाना f. (-ना) DURGĀ.<BR> E. सिंह a lion, यान a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहरथा
सिंहरथा f. (-था) The goddess DURGĀ.<BR> E. सिंह, रथ a vehicle, mounted on that animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहल|सिंहलं|सिंहलः
सिंहल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Tin.<BR>	 2. Brass.<BR>	 3. Cassia bark.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Ceylon. E.<BR>सिंह a lion, &c., ला to give or get, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहलास्थान|सिंहलास्थानः
सिंहलास्थान m. (-नः) A tree, apparently a sort of palm.<BR> E. सिंहला Ceylon, स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहलील|सिंहलीलः
सिंहलील m. (-लः) A kind of sexual union thus defined:--<BR>“लिङ्गोपरि स्थिता नारी कान्तोरुस्थपदद्वया ।<BR>हृदये दत्तहस्ता चेत् सिंहलीलः प्रकीर्त्तितः ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहविक्रान्त|सिंहविक्रान्तः
सिंहविक्रान्त m. (-न्तः) A horse.<BR> E. सिंह a lion, and विक्रान्त valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहसंहनन|सिंहसंहननः
सिंहसंहनन Adj. As strong as a lion.<BR>	 n. (-नं) The killing of a lion.<BR>	 mfn.<BR>(-नः-ना-नं) Handsome and well-shaped.<BR> E. सिह the beast, संहनन<BR>rivalling or surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाढ्य
सिंहाढ्य mfn. (-ढ्यः-ढ्या-ढ्यं) Abounding with lions.<BR> E. सिंह, आढ्य wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहान|सिंहानं
सिंहान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Rust of iron.<BR>	 2. The mucus of the nose.<BR> E. शघि to<BR>smell, आनक् aff., form irr; also शिङ्घाण, सिंहाण, सिङ्घाण, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहावलोकनन्याय
सिंहावलोकनन्याय m. (-यः) The maxim of the lion's glance; it is used to<BR>denote the connection of a thing with the preceding and the<BR>following, just as the lion constantly pauses and casts his glance<BR>backward and forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहासन|सिंहासनं|सिंहासनः
सिंहासन n. (-नं) A throne.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A kind of coitus thus defined:--<BR>“स्वजङ्घाद्वयबाहु च कृत्वा योषापदद्वये ।<BR>स्तनौ धृत्वा रमेत् कामी बन्धः सिहासना मतः ॥”<BR>E. सिंह a lion, (supported by lions, &c. wrought in gold,) and आसन a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहास्य|सिंहास्यः
सिंहास्य m. (-स्यः) A plant, (Justicia adhenatoda, &c.)<BR> E. सिंह a lion, आस्य<BR>the face; to which the flowers are compared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहिका
सिंहिका f. (-का) The mother of RĀHU.<BR> E. सिंही a lioness, कन् aff. of comparison, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहिकासूनु|सिंहिकासूनुः
सिंहिकासूनु m. (-नुः) The personified ascending node.<BR> E. सिंहिका the<BR>mother of RĀHU, and सूनु son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्
सिक्(सेकति) To sprinkle; Sautra root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकता
सिकता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Sandy soil.<BR>	 2. Gravel or stone, (the disease.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Sugar.<BR>	 f. Plu. (-ताः) Sand.<BR> E. सिकि Sautra root, to sprinkle,<BR>Unādi aff. अतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतामय|सिकतामयं
सिकतामय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Sandy.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A sand bank, or an island<BR>with sandy shores.<BR> E. सिकता sand, मयट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=785-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतावत्|सिकतावन्त्
सिकतावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Sandy, (in general.)<BR> E. सिकता sand, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतिल|सिकतिलः
सिकतिल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Sandy as a soil or country.<BR> E. सिकता sand,<BR>aff. इलच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्त|सिक्तः
सिक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkled.<BR>	 2. Wetted.<BR>	 3. Impregnated.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्त्वा
सिक्त्वा Ind. Having sprinkled, effused, &c.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्थ|सिक्थं|सिक्थः
सिक्थ m. (-क्थः)<BR>	 1. A handful of boiled rice.<BR>	 2. Boiled rice.<BR>	 n. (-क्थं)<BR>1. Bee's-wax.<BR>	 2. Indigo.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, Unādi aff. थक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्थक|सिक्थकं
सिक्थक n. (-कं) Bee's-wax.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्य|सिक्यं
सिक्य n. (-क्यं) A sling made of ropes.<BR> E. सिक-यत् aff. “सिके इतिभाषा” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्ष्य|सिक्ष्यः
सिक्ष्य n. (-क्ष्यं) Crystal, glass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिङ्घाण|सिंघाण|सिंघाणं|सिङ्घाणं
सिङ्घाण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. The mucus of the nose.<BR>	 2. Rust of iron.<BR> E. शिघि to<BR>smell, Unādi aff. आनक्, and the last syllable of the aff. optionally<BR>rejected; also सिङ्घाणक n. (-कं): see सिंहान ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिङ्घिनी
सिङ्घिनी f. (-नी) The nose.<BR> E. शिघि to smell, affs. इनि and ङीप्, the initial changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिच्
सिच् f. (-सिक्) Clothes.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिचय|सिचयः
सिचय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Cloth, clothes.<BR>	 2. Old or ragged raiment.<BR> E. षिचि to<BR>cause to sprinkle, aff. श ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिच्यमान
सिच्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being sprinkled.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्चत्
सिञ्चत् mfn. (-ञ्चन्-ञ्चन्ती-ञ्चत्) Sprinkling, throwing water.<BR> E. षिच् to<BR>sprinkle, शतृ aff. of the present participle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्चिता|सिंचिता
सिञ्चिता f. (-ता) Long-pepper.<BR> E. सिच्-इतच्-पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिञ्जा|सिंजा
सिञ्जा f. (-ञ्जा) The sound of metallic ornaments, jingling, ringing, tink-<BR>ling; more usually शिञ्जा, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सित|सितं|सितः
सित mfn. (-तः-ता or ती-तं)<BR>	 1. White.<BR>	 2. Bound, tied.<BR>	 3. Finished, des-<BR>troyed.<BR>	 4. Completed, concluded.<BR>	 5. Known.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. White,<BR>(the colour.)<BR>	 2. The light-half of a lunar month.<BR>	 3. The planet<BR>VENUS.<BR>	 4. An arrow.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Silver.<BR>	 2. Sandal.<BR>	 3. Radish.<BR>f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Clayed or candied sugar.<BR>	 2. Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 3.<BR>A sort of Clitoria.<BR>	 4. Bent grass with white blossoms.<BR>	 5.<BR>Moon-light.<BR>	 6. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 7. A handsome or well made<BR>woman.<BR> E. षि to tie or bind, aff. क्त; or षो to destroy, क्त aff., and इ<BR>substituted for the radical vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितकर|सितकरः
सितकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितकुञ्जर|सितकुञ्जरः
सितकुञ्जर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. INDRA'S elephant.<BR> E. सित white, कुञ्जर an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितचिह्न|सितचिह्नः
सितचिह्न m. (-ह्नः) A sort of fish, (Lacerta scincus.)<BR> E. सित, चिह्न a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितच्छत्र|सितच्छत्रं|सितछत्र
सितच्छत्र n. (-त्रं) A white umbrella, especially as one of the emblems of<BR>royalty.<BR>	 f. (-त्री) A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR> E. सित white,<BR>छत्र an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितच्छद|सितच्छदः|सितछद
सितच्छद m. (-दः) A goose.<BR>	 f. (-दा) White Durbā grass.<BR> E. सित white, च्छद a feather or leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितदीधिति|सितदीधितिः
सितदीधिति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. सित white, and दीधिति a ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितदूर्व्वा|सितदूर्वा
सितदूर्व्वा f. (-र्व्वा) A bent grass with white blossoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितद्रु|सितद्रुः
सितद्रु m. (-द्रुः) A plant, commonly Morata.<BR> E. सित white, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितधातु|सितधातुः
सितधातु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. Chalk.<BR>	 2. Silver.<BR> E. सित white, and धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितपक्ष|सितपक्षः
सितपक्ष m. (-क्षः) A goose.<BR> E. सित white, पक्ष a feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितपुष्प|सितपुष्पं|सितपुष्पः
सितपुष्प n. (-ष्पं) A sort of grass, (Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>	 m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. A sort<BR>of tree, the Tagara tree.<BR>	 2. A kind of grass, (Saccharum spontane-<BR>um.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पा) Arabian jasmine.<BR> E. सित white, and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितमरिच|सितमरिचं
सितमरिच n. (-चं) White pepper.<BR> E. सित white, मरिच pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितमाष|सितमाषः
सितमाष m. (-षः) A sort of bean, (Dolichos catjang.)<BR> E. सित white, माष pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितरञ्जन|सितरञ्जनः
सितरञ्जन m. (-नः) Yellow, (the colour.)<BR> E. सित white, and रञ्जन colouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितरश्मि|सितरश्मिः
सितरश्मि m. (-श्मिः) The moon.<BR> E. सित white, and रश्मि a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितवाजिन्
सितवाजिन् m. (-जी) An epithet of ARJUNA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितशर्करा
सितशर्करा f. (-रा) Candied sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितशिम्बिक|सितशिम्बिकः
सितशिम्बिक m. (-कः) Wheat.<BR> E. सित white, and शिम्बिका an awn; also<BR>read शितशिम्बिक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितशिव|सितशिवं
सितशिव n. (-वं) Rock-salt.<BR> E. सित white, शिब auspicious; also सितशिवं, and सितसिवं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितशूक|सितशूकः
सितशूक m. (-कः) Barley.<BR> E. शित white, an शूक and awn or ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितसप्ति|सितसप्तिः
सितसप्ति m. (-प्तिः) A name of ARJUNA.<BR> E. सित white, and सप्ति a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितसर्षप|सितसर्षपः
सितसर्षप m. (-पः) White mustard.<BR> E. सित white, and सर्षप mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितसिन्धु|सितसिन्धुः
सितसिन्धु f. (-न्धुः) The Ganges.<BR> E. सित white, सिन्धु a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितसिव
सितसिव n. (-वं) Rook-salt.<BR> E. सित white, सिव for शिव auspicious: see सितशिव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताशु
सिताशु m. (-शुः) The moon.<BR> E. सित, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताखण्ड|सिताखण्डः
सिताखण्ड m. (-ण्डः) Clayed sugar, (prepared from honey.)<BR> E. सित white, आखण्ड sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताग्र|सिताग्रः
सिताग्र m. (-ग्रः) A thorn.<BR> E. सित white, and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताङ्क|सिताङ्कः
सिताङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A king of fish, (Laceria scincus.) “वेले माछ” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितादि|सितादिः
सितादि m. (-दिः) Treacle, molasses.<BR> E. सिता sugar, before दा to give, aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितानन|सिताननः
सितानन m. (-नः) GARUḌA, the bird of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सित white, आनन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितापाङ्ग|सितापांग|सितापाङ्गः
सितापाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A peacock.<BR> E. सित white, अपाङ्ग the angle of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताब्ज|सिताब्जं
सिताब्ज n. (-ब्जं) The white lotus.<BR> E. सित white, and अब्ज a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताभ|सिताभः
सिताभ m. (-भः) Camphor.<BR> E. सित white आङ् before भा to shine, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताभ्र|सिताभ्रः
सिताभ्र mn. (-भ्रः-भ्रं) Camphor.<BR> E. सित white, and अभ्र a cloud; also with<BR>कन् added, सिताभ्रक n. (-कं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताम्बर|सिताम्बरः
सिताम्बर m. (-रः) An ascetic wearing white garments.<BR> E. सित white, and अम्बर vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताम्भोज|सिताम्भोजं
सिताम्भोज n. (-जं) A white lotus.<BR> E. सित white, अम्भोज a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितार्जक|सितार्जकः|सितार्ज्जकः
सितार्जक m. (-कः) White basil.<BR> E. सित white, अर्जक basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितालता
सितालता f. (-ता) Durbā grass with white blossoms.<BR> E. सित, लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितालिका
सितालिका f. (-का) A cockle.<BR> E. सित white, आलि a line, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिताश्व|सिताश्वः
सिताश्व m. (-श्वः) ARJUNA.<BR> E. सित white, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितासित|सितासितः
सितासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) White and black.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A name of BALA-<BR>DEVA.<BR> E. सित white, (skin,) and असित black, (raiment.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिति|सितिः
सिति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति)<BR>	 1. White.<BR>	 2. Black.<BR> E. सि to bind, aff. क्ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितिकण्ठ|सितिकंठ|सितिकण्ठः
सितिकण्ठ Adj.<BR>	 1. Having a white throat.<BR>	 2. Dark-necked.<BR>	 m. (-ण्ठः) ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितिमन्
सितिमन् m. (-मा) Whiteness.<BR> E. सिति white, and इमनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितिवासस्
सितिवासस् m. (-साः) BALADEVA.<BR> E. सिति black, and वासस् vesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितेतर|सितेतरः
सितेतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Black.<BR> E. सित white, इतर reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितेतरगति|सितेतरगतिः
सितेतरगति m. (-तिः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. सितेतर black, (smoke,) गति going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितोदर|सितोदरः
सितोदर m. (-रः) KUVERA.<BR> E. सित white, and उदर the belly; the deity<BR>is properly of a black colour, but is whitened by a leprous taint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितोद्भव|सितोद्भवं
सितोद्भव n. (-वं) White sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितोपल|सितोपलं|सितोपलः
सितोपल n. (-लं) Chalk, or mineral substance of similar appearance<BR>considered as a variety.<BR>	 m. (-लः) Crystal.<BR>	 f. (-ला) Clayed or candied<BR>sugar.<BR> E. सित white, and उपला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितोष्णवारण
सितोष्णवारण n. (-णं) A white umbrella.<BR> E. सित, and उष्णवारण keeping off the heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्ध|सिद्धं|सिद्धः
सिद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं)<BR>	 1. Accomplished, effected, completed.<BR>	 2. Libera-<BR>ted, emancipated.<BR>	 3. Always, eternal.<BR>	 4. Celebrated, famous.<BR>	 5. Judg-<BR>ed, decided, terminated, (as a lawsuit.)<BR>	 6. Valid, (in law.)<BR>	 7. Adept<BR>initiated, in alchemy or magic.<BR>	 8. Demonstrated, proved, (in logic.)<BR>9. Finished.<BR>	 10. Cooked, dressed.<BR>	 11. Prepared, compounded, (in<BR>medicine.)<BR>	 12. Shining, splendid.<BR>	 13. Discharged, (as a debt.)<BR>	 14.<BR>Obtained, acquired.<BR>	 15. Succeeded, successful.<BR>	 16. Settled, estab-<BR>lished.<BR>	 17. Admitted to be true or right.<BR>	 18. Paid, liquidated,<BR>(as a debt.)<BR>	 19. Ready, (as money.)<BR>	 20. Concocted, (as drugs.)<BR>	 21.<BR>Matured, ripened.<BR>	 22. Subdued, (by magical power.)<BR>	 23. Tho-<BR>roughly skilled, (in any art.)<BR>	 24. Perfected or sanctified, (by pen-<BR>ance or austerities.)<BR>	 25. Endowed with supernatural faculties<BR>or powers.<BR>	 26. Sacred, pious.<BR>	 27. Divine, immortal.<BR>	 m. (-द्धः)<BR>1. A divine personage of undefined attributes or character;<BR>a sort of demigod or spirit, inhabiting with the Vidyādharas,<BR>Munis, &c. in the middle air, or the region between the earth and<BR>sun.<BR>	 2. An inspired or prophetic writer, as VYĀSA and others, or<BR>one to whom the past, present, and future, are supposed to be<BR>known, a sage, a seer.<BR>	 3. The twenty-first of the astronomical<BR>Yogas.<BR>	 4. An adept, a magician, one who by the performance of<BR>certain mystical and magical rites has acquired superhuman<BR>powers.<BR>	 5. An ascetic, who by mystical and austere practices has<BR>effected one or all of five purposes, viz:--the affluence, the form<BR>or the society of the gods, residence in the divine Lokas or<BR>identification with a deity.<BR>	 6. A lawsuit, a judicial<BR>trial.<BR>	 7. A sort of hard sugar.<BR>	 n. (-द्धं) Sea-salt.<BR>	 f. (-द्धा) A medi-<BR>cinal root, commonly Riddhi.<BR> E. षिध् to effect, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=786-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धगङ्गा|सिद्धगंगा
सिद्धगङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) The Ganges of heaven.<BR> E. सिद्ध a spirit of mid-heaven,<BR>गङ्गा the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धग्रह|सिद्धग्रहः
सिद्धग्रह m. (-हः) Name of a particular kind of madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धजल|सिद्धजलं
सिद्धजल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Sour rice-gruel.<BR>	 2. Water of boiled rice.<BR> E. सिद्ध<BR>perfect, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धता
सिद्धता f. (-ता) Perfection, completion; also with त्व, सिद्धत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धदेव|सिद्धदेवः
सिद्धदेव m. (-वः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. सिद्ध a saint, देव deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धधातु|सिद्धधातुः
सिद्धधातु m. (-तुः) Quicksilver.<BR> E. सिद्ध adept, (in alchemy,) धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धपक्ष|सिद्धपक्षः
सिद्धपक्ष m. (-क्षः) The established or logical side of an argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धप्रयोजन|सिद्धप्रयोजनः
सिद्धप्रयोजन n. (-नं) White mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धरस|सिद्धरसः
सिद्धरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Mineral, metallic, &c.<BR>	 m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Quicksilver.<BR>2. An alchemist.<BR> E. सिद्ध perfect, or perfected by alchemical opera-<BR>tion, रस fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धविद्या
सिद्धविद्या f. (-दा) The ten goddesses of the Tantra Shāstra: see महाविद्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसङ्कल्प
सिद्धसङ्कल्प Adj. One who has accomplished his wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसङ्घ|सिद्धसंघ
सिद्धसङ्घ m. (-ङ्घः) A company of saints or the beings called Siddhas. E.<BR>सिद्ध, and सङ्घ a company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसलिल|सिद्धसलिलं
सिद्धसलिल n. (-लं) Sour rice-gruel.<BR> E. सिद्ध perfect, and सलिल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाधन|सिद्धसाधनं|सिद्धसाधनः
सिद्धसाधन m. (-नः) White mustard.<BR>	 n. (-नं) The performance of magical<BR>rites, &c. or the materials employed in magical or alchemical pro-<BR>cesses.<BR> E. सिद्ध perfect, adept, &c., and साधन accomplishing, (the<BR>act or instrument.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाध्य|सिद्धसाध्यः
सिद्धसाध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Effected, proved.<BR>	 2. Having done what<BR>was to be done.<BR>	 n. (-ध्यं) Demonstrated proof or conclusion. E.<BR>सिद्ध, and साध्य to be proved, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसिन्धु|सिद्धसिंधु|सिद्धसिन्धुः
सिद्धसिन्धु f. (-न्धुः) The Ganges.<BR> E. सिद्ध a divine being or sage, and सिन्धु a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसेन|सिद्धसेनः
सिद्धसेन m. (-नः) The deity of war, KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. सिद्ध a divine being,<BR>and सेना an army; commanding the hosts of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धस्थाली
सिद्धस्थाली f. (-ली) The pot of a Seer, (fabled as a vessel gifted with<BR>the property of overflowing with any kind of food at the wish of<BR>the possessor.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धान्त|सिद्धांत|सिद्धान्तः
सिद्धान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. Demonstrated conclusion, established truth: it may<BR>be either the result of an argument in which one opinion is refuted<BR>and another undeniably established; or the concurrent doctrine<BR>of all the authorities on any subject similarly interpreted.<BR>	 2.<BR>Any fixed or established text-book resting on conclusive argu-<BR>ments.<BR> E. सिद्ध completed, perfect, and अन्त end, conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धान्तकोटि|सिद्धांतकोटि
सिद्धान्तकोटि f. (-टी) The point in an argument which is regarded as a<BR>logical conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धान्तिन्|सिद्धांतिन्
सिद्धान्तिन् m. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A follower of the Mimānsā philosophy.<BR>	 2. A<BR>demonstrator, one who establishes his conclusions.<BR> E. सिद्धान्त<BR>demonstrated conclusion, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धान्न
सिद्धान्न n. (-न्नं) Dressed food, cooked victuals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धापगा
सिद्धापगा f. (-गा) The Ganges.<BR> E. सिद्ध a divine being, अपगा a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धायिका
सिद्धायिका f. (-का) One of the tutelary goddesses of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धार्थ|सिद्धार्थः
सिद्धार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Successful, prosperous.<BR>	 m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. The father of<BR>the last and most celebrated Jina or Jaina teacher of the present<BR>era.<BR>	 2. White mustard.<BR>	 3. A name of Sākya-sinha or Buddha.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-र्था) The mother of the fourth Jina.<BR> E. सिद्ध complete, &c., and अर्थ<BR>meaning or wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धासन
सिद्धासन n. (-नं) A particular posture in religious meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धि|सिद्धिः
सिद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. Fulfilment, accomplishment, the entire completion<BR>of any undertaking or attainment of any object.<BR>	 2. A Yoga,<BR>either the sixteenth of the astronomical periods termed Yogas, or<BR>the nineteenth of the twenty-eight astrological Yogas.<BR>	 3. Final<BR>emancipation from existence, supreme felicity.<BR>	 4. Pros-<BR>perity, success.<BR>	 5. Knowledge, understanding.<BR>	 6. Accuracy, cor-<BR>rectness, indisputable conclusion or position.<BR>	 7. Validity, (in<BR>law.)<BR>	 8. Acquittance, discharge, (of a debt.)<BR>	 9. Concealment,<BR>secreting, covering.<BR>	 10. The result or fruit of the adoration<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">Page787-b+ 60</a>]<BR>of the gods or of ascetic severities.<BR>	 11. The supposed acquirement<BR>of supernatural powers by the completion of magical, mystical,<BR>or alchemical rites and processes.<BR>	 12. A wooden shoe or<BR>slipper, especially one over which some mystical formulæ have<BR>been repeated, and which will then, it is supposed, convey the<BR>wearer every where safely and rapidly.<BR>	 13. A medicinal root; also<BR>Riddhi.<BR>	 14. Settlement, establishment.<BR>	 15. Certainty, truth.<BR>	 16.<BR>Decision, (of a lawsuit.)<BR>	 17. The solution of a problem.<BR>	 18. Pre-<BR>paration, cooking.<BR>	 19. Readiness.<BR>	 20. Complete sanctification.<BR>	 21.<BR>Beatitude.<BR>	 22. Marvellous skill or capability.<BR>	 23. Making oneself<BR>invisible.<BR> E. षिध् to accomplish, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धियोग|सिद्धियोगः
सिद्धियोग m. (-गः) A particular auspicious conjunction of the planets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिली
सिद्धिली f. (-ली) A small ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्म|सिध्मं
सिध्म n. (-ध्मं) A blotch, a scab, leprosy.<BR>	 f. (-ध्मा)<BR>	 1. A leprous spot.<BR>	 2.<BR>Leprosy.<BR> E. षिध् to go, (on the body,) मन् aff.; also सिध्मन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मन्
सिध्मन् n. (-ध्म) A blotch, a scab.<BR> E. षिध् to go, मनिन् aff.: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मल|सिध्मलः
सिध्मल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Scabby.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Dried or salt fish.<BR>	 2.<BR>A scab.<BR>	 3. A sort of leprosy.<BR> E. सिध्मन् a scab, लच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मवत्|सिध्मवन्त्
सिध्मवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Scabby, pocky.<BR> E. सिध्म a blotch, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्य|सिध्यः
सिध्य m. (-ध्यः) The asterism Pushyā, stars in Cancer.<BR> E. षिध् to accom-<BR>plish or to be accomplished, क्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्र|सिध्रः
सिध्र m. (-ध्रः)<BR>	 1. A pious or virtuous man.<BR>	 2. A tree.<BR> E. षिध् to be perfect, रक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्रका
सिध्रका f. (-का) A plant, so named.<BR> E. कन् added to the preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्रकावण|सिध्रकावणं
सिध्रकावण n. (-णं) A garden of the gods.<BR> E. सिध्रका a plant, and वन a<BR>wood, न changed to ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन|सिनं|सिनः
सिन mf. (-नः-नी) One-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A morsel, a mouthful, or such a<BR>quantity bound together.<BR>	 2. A village.<BR> E. षि to bind, नक् Unādi<BR>aff. or क्त aff. in this particular application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिनी
सिनी f. (-नी) A woman with a white complexion.<BR> E. सित + ङीप्, तस्य नश्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिनीवाली
सिनीवाली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. The day preceding that of new-moon, or that on<BR>which the moon rises scarcely visible.<BR>	 2. The goddess UMĀ.<BR> E. सा<BR>good fortune, इनि aff., fem. form, सिनी a digit of the moon, वल् to<BR>contain, aff. अण्, fem. aff. ङीप्; several other etymologies occur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दुक|सिंदुक|सिंदुकः|सिन्दुकः
सिन्दुक m. (-कः) A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR> E. स्यन्द् to ooze, aff. उ,<BR>कन् added; the semivowel of the root changed to इ; also सिन्धुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दुवार|सिंदुवार|सिंदुवारः|सिन्दुवारः
सिन्दुवार m. (-रः) A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR> E. सिन्द oozing, (as<BR>before,) वृ to screen or choose, aff. अण्: see सिन्धुवार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूर|सिंदूर|सिन्दूरं|सिंदूरः|सिन्दूरः
सिन्दूर n. (-रं) Red lead, minium.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A sort of tree.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Red<BR>cloth or clothes.<BR>	 2. Rochani, (a sort of Crinum.)<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>(Lythrum fruticosum.)<BR> E. स्यन्द to ooze, Unādi aff. ऊरन्; also सिन्दुर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूरकारण|सिन्दूरकारणं
सिन्दूरकारण n. (-णं) Lead.<BR> E. सिन्दूर minium, and कारण origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूरतिलक|सिन्दूरतिलकः
सिन्दूरतिलक m. (-कः) An elephant.<BR>	 f. (-का) A woman whose forehead is<BR>marked with minium.<BR> E. सिन्दूर red lead, and तिलक the mark on<BR>the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूरिका|सिंदूरिका
सिन्दूरिका f. (-का) Red lead.<BR> E. सिन्दूर, कन् added, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्दूरित|सिंदूरित
सिन्दूरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Reddened, made red.<BR> E. सिन्दूर, and इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धु|सिंधु|सिंधुः|सिन्धुः
सिन्धु m. (-न्धुः)<BR>	 1. The ocean, the sea.<BR>	 2. The Indus.<BR>	 3. The country<BR>along the INDUS or SINDH.<BR>	 4. The juice that exudes from an ele-<BR>phant's temples.<BR>	 5. An elephant.<BR>	 6. A division of a Rāga or musical<BR>mode.<BR>	 7. A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR>	 f. (-न्धुः) A river in general.<BR>E. स्यन्द् to trickle or flow, उ Unādi aff., the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुक|सिंधुक|सिंधुकः|सिन्धुकः
सिन्धुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Marine.<BR>	 2. Born or produced in Sindh.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR> E. कन् added to the last,<BR>implying place of origin or production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुकफ|सिन्धुकफः
सिन्धुकफ m. (-फः) Cuttle-fish-bone.<BR> E. सिन्धु the sea, कफ phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुखेल|सिन्धुखेलः
सिन्धुखेल m. (-लः) The country of Sindh.<BR> E. सिन्धु the Indus, खिल् to go<BR>or sport, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुज|सिंधुज|सिन्धुजं|सिन्धुजः
सिन्धुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं)<BR>	 1. River or sea-born, marine, aquatic.<BR>	 2. Born<BR>or produced in Sindh.<BR>	 n. (-ज) Rock-salt.<BR>	 f. (-जा) The goddess<BR>LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 m. (-जः) The moon.<BR> E. सिन्धु the country or river, &c., ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=787-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुजन्मन्
सिन्धुजन्मन् m. (-न्मा) The moon.<BR>	 n. (-न्म) Rock-salt.<BR> E. सिन्धु the sea, &c.,<BR>जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुनन्दन|सिन्धुनन्दनः
सिन्धुनन्दन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. सिन्धु the ocean, and<BR>नन्दन the son; being produced at the churning of the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुनाथ|सिन्धुनाथः
सिन्धुनाथ m. (-थः) The ocean.<BR> E. सिन्धु a river, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुपुत्त्र
सिन्धुपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. A sort of ebony.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. सिन्धु the sea, &c., पुत्त्र offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुपुष्प|सिन्धुपुष्पः
सिन्धुपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A conch.<BR> E. सिन्धु the sea, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुमन्थज|सिन्धुमन्थजं
सिन्धुमन्थज n. (-जं) Rock-salt.<BR> E. सिन्धुमन्थ the ocean-churning, (a mountain,) ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुर|सिंधुर|सिंधुरः|सिन्धुरः
सिन्धुर m. (-रः) An elephant.<BR> E. स्यन्द् to ooze, the (ichor from his<BR>temples.) उरच् aff., and the form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुरद्वेषिन्
सिन्धुरद्वेषिन् m. (-षी) A lion.<BR> E. सिन्धुर an elephant, and द्वेषिन् enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुलवण|सिन्धुलवणं
सिन्धुलवण n. (-णं) Rock-salt.<BR> E. सिन्धु Sindh, and लवण salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुवार|सिंधुवार|सिंधुवारः|सिन्धुवारः
सिन्धुवार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A horse of a good breed, brought probably from<BR>Sindh or the borders of India and Persia.<BR>	 2. A small tree, (Vitex<BR>negundo.)<BR> E. सिन्धु the country or the sea, वृ to choose or screen. aff.<BR>घञ्; also सिन्दुवार in the second sense; with कन् added. सिन्धुवारक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुवारित|सिन्धुवारितः
सिन्धुवारित m. (-तः) A small tree, (Vitex negundo.)<BR> E. सिन्धु the sea,<BR>and वारित selected or chosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुवेषण|सिन्धुवेषणः
सिन्धुवेषण m. (-णः) A plant, (Gmelina arborea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुशयन|सिन्धुशयनः
सिन्धुशयन m. (-नः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सिन्धु the ocean, and शयन a couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धुसङ्गम|सिन्धुसंगम|सिन्धुसङ्गमः
सिन्धुसङ्गम m. (-मः) The mouth of a river, or its point of junction with<BR>the sea.<BR> E. सिन्धु the sea, सङ्गम confluence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धूद्भव|सिन्धूद्भवं
सिन्धूद्भव n. (-वं) Rock-salt.<BR> E. सिन्धु Sindh, and उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्धूपल|सिंधूपल|सिन्धूपलं
सिन्धूपल n. (-लं) Rock-salt.<BR> E. सिन्धु Sindh, and उपला a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन्व्
सिन्व् r. 1st cl. (सिन्वति) To wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिप्र|सिप्रं|सिप्रः
सिप्र m. (-प्रः)<BR>	 1. Perspiration, sweat.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 f. (-प्रा)<BR>	 1. The Siprā,<BR>a river near Oujein.<BR>	 2. A woman's zone.<BR>	 3. A female buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम|सिमः
सिम m. (-मः) All, entire.<BR>	 f. (-मा) Adj. Every.<BR> E. षि to bind, मन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम्बा|सिंबा
सिम्बा f. (-म्बा-म्बिः or -म्बी) A legume, a pod: see शिम्बा, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिम्बिका
सिम्बिका f. (-का) Grain in pods, as pulse, &c.<BR> E. सिम्बा a pod, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिर|सिरः
सिर m. (-रः) The root of long-pepper.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Any tubular vessel of<BR>the body, or one so considered, as a nerve, a vein, an artery, a<BR>tendon, &c.<BR>	 2. A bucket.<BR> E. षि to bind, aff. रक्, form irr.; also शिर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिराजाल
सिराजाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A plexus of vessels.<BR>	 2. Enlargement of the<BR>vessels of the eye.<BR> E. सिरा, and जाल a net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिरामोक्ष|सिरामोक्षः
सिरामोक्ष m. (-क्षः) Venesection.<BR> E. सिरा a vein, and मोक्ष loosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिराव्यध|सिराव्यधः
सिराव्यध m. (-धः) Venesection.<BR> E. सिरा, व्यध piercing; also सिराव्यधनं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिराहर्ष
सिराहर्ष m. (-र्षः) Flow of discoloured tears.<BR> E. सिरा, हर्ष joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिरोत्पात|सिरोत्पातः
सिरोत्पात m. (-तः) Redness and inflammation of the eyes.<BR> E. सिरा, उत्पात affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिल्लकी
सिल्लकी f. (-की) The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.) E. See<BR>सल्लकी, the इ being substituted for अ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिवर|सिवरः
सिवर m. (-रः) An elephant.<BR> E. सि-क्वरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषङ्ग्रामयिषु|सिषंग्रामयिषु
सिषङ्ग्रामयिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Wishing or intending to make war. E.<BR>सङ्ग्राम to make war, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषाधयिषा
सिषाधयिषा f. (-षा) Wish or purpose to effect, prove, &c.<BR> E. षाध् to<BR>accomplish, desid. form, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषाधयिषु
सिषाधयिषु mfn. (-षुः-षुः-षु) Desirous to accomplish, to prove, &c.<BR> E. षाध्<BR>to accomplish, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसृक्षा
सिसृक्षा f. (-क्षा) Wish or purpose to create.<BR> E. सृज् to create, desid. v., अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसृक्षु
सिसृक्षु mfn. (-क्षुः-क्षुः-क्षु) Wishing or purposing to create.<BR> E. सृज् to<BR>create, desid. v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिहुण्ड|सिहुंड|सिहुंडः|सिहुण्डः
सिहुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The milk-hedge plant, (Euphorbia antiquorum;) also सीहुण्ड and सेहुण्ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्ण
सिह्ण m. (-ह्णः) Incense, gum Benjamin or Olibanum, &c.<BR> E. ष्णिह् to be<BR>affectionate, to love, लक aff., form irr.; also with कन् added,<BR>सिह्णक m. (-कः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्णकी
सिह्णकी f. (-की) The Olibanum tree.<BR> E. सिह्ण incense, कन् added and ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्णभूमिका
सिह्णभूमिका f. (-का) The Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR> E. सिह्ण<BR>incense, भूमि place, site, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीक्
सीक् r. 1st cl. (सीकते)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle, to scatter in drops.<BR>	 2. To go, to<BR>move. r. 10th. cl. (सीकयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be impatient.<BR>	 2. To be patient.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">Page788-b+ 60</a>]<BR>3. To touch.<BR>	 4. To be angry. (ऋ) सीकृ r. 1st cl. (सीकति).<BR>	 1. To<BR>sprinkle, to shed or shower.<BR>	 2. To bear.<BR>	 3. To touch.<BR>	 4.<BR>To be angry.<BR>	 5. To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीकर|सीकरः
सीकर m. (-रः) Thin drizzling rain.<BR> E. सीक् to scatter, (as water,) अरन् aff.; also शीकर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीता
सीता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A furrow, the track of the plough-share.<BR>	 2. The<BR>daughter of JANAKA and wife of RĀMACHANDRA, so named<BR>because fabled to have sprung from a furrow made by<BR>Janaka while ploughing the ground to prepare it for a<BR>sacrifice instituted by him to obtain progeny.<BR>	 3. One of the<BR>four great branches into which the Ganges, after having fallen on<BR>mount Meru, is fabled to divide: the eastern branch, flowing<BR>into the Varṣa Bhadrāswa.<BR>	 4. The goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 5. UMĀ,<BR>the wife of ŚIVA.<BR>	 6. A goddess, wife of Indra, presiding over fruits,<BR>&c., an Indian FLORA or POMONA.<BR>	 7. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 8. Husban-<BR>dry.<BR> E. षि to bind, (the earth,) क्त aff., form irr; it is then appli-<BR>cable to the princess as having been turned up in the soil<BR>by a plough-share; and to the goddesses, as they may be sup-<BR>posed to have been incarnate in the wife of RĀMĀ; also, as<BR>differently derived शीता, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीताद्रव्य
सीताद्रव्य n. Plu. (-व्याणि) The implements of husbandry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतापति|सीतापतिः
सीतापति f. (-तिः) The hero RĀMA.<BR> E. सीता the princess, पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीताफल|सीताफलः
सीताफल m. (-लः) The custard-apple tree.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The custard-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतायाःपति|सीतायाःपतिः
सीतायाःपति m. (-तिः) RĀMA.<BR> E. सीता in the poss. case, पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतीनक|सीतीनकः
सीतीनक m. (-कः) Pease: see सतीलक, सतीनक, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्कार|सीत्कारः
सीत्कार n. (-रं) Uttering an inarticulate sound, such as is made with<BR>the lips when a person shivers with cold, or in fainting, sighing,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सीत् imitative sound, and कार making; also सीत्कृत n. (-तं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्कृत|सीत्कृतं
सीत्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uttered as an inarticulated sound.<BR>	 n. (-तं) An<BR>inarticulate sound: see the last.<BR> E. सीत्, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्य|सीत्यं
सीत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Ploughed, tilled.<BR>	 n. (-त्यं) Corn, grain, rice, &c.<BR>E. सीता a furrow, यत् aff.; also शीत्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीदत्
सीदत् mfn. (-दन्-दन्ती-दत्)<BR>	 1. Sorrowing, grieving, desponding.<BR>	 2. Decaying.<BR>3. Suffering from, distressed or pained by.<BR>	 4. Going.<BR> E. षद् to<BR>wane, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीद्य|सीद्यं
सीद्य n. (-द्यं) Slothfulness, idleness, indolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधु|सीधुः
सीधु m. (-धुः) Spirit, distilled from molasses, rum. E. See शीधु, the<BR>sibilant being changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुगन्ध|सीधुगंध|सीधुगन्धः
सीधुगन्ध m. (-न्धः) The Bakula tree, (mimusops elengi.)<BR> E. सीधु rum, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुप
सीधुप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Drinking spirits.<BR> E. सिधु, and पा to drink, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुपुष्प|सीधुपुष्पः
सीधुपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. The Kadamba tree.<BR>	 2. The Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुरस|सीधुरसः
सीधुरस m. (-सः) The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीध्र|सीध्रं
सीध्र n. (-ध्रं) The anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीप|सीपः
सीप m. (-पः) A sacrificial vessel in the shape of a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्
सीमन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A boundary, a limit, a landmark, or mound, &c. serving<BR>to fix the limits of estates, &c.<BR>	 2. A field.<BR>	 3. The nape of the neck.<BR>4. The scrotum.<BR> E. षिञ् to bind, इमनिन्, Unādi aff.; also with the<BR>aff. डाष्, or a final vowel, fem. form, सीमा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्त|सीमंत|सीमंतः|सीमन्तः
सीमन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A separation of the hair on each side, so as to leave a<BR>distinct line on the top of the head.<BR>	 2. A boundary line.<BR>	 mn. (-न्तः-न्तं)<BR>The head.<BR> E. सीमन् limit, (of the hair,) and अन्त end, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तक|सीमंतक|सीमन्तकं|सीमंतकः|सीमन्तकः
सीमन्तक m. (-कः) An infernal being.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Red lead, a mark with which<BR>is sometimes made along the division of the hair.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तित|सीमंतित
सीमन्तित f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Marked by a line.<BR>	 2. Parted, (as hair.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तिनी|सीमंतिनी
सीमन्तिनी f. (-नी) A woman in general.<BR> E. सीमन्त the separation of the<BR>hair, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तोन्नयन|सीमंतोन्नयन|सीमन्तोन्नयनं
सीमन्तोन्नयन n. (-नं) One of the Sanskāras or a purificatory and sacrificial<BR>ceremony, observed by women in the fourth, sixth, or eighth<BR>month of their pregnancy.<BR> E. सीमन्त partition of the hair, and<BR>उन्नयन arranging; this forming an essential part of the rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=788-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्त्यमान
सीमन्त्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being parted or divided.<BR> E. सीमन्त used as a<BR>passive verb, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमा
सीमा f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A boundary, a limit.<BR>	 2. A field.<BR>	 3. A bank, a shore.<BR>4. Rectitude observance of due bounds in morals, &c.<BR>	 5. The nape<BR>of the neck.<BR>	 6. The scrotum.<BR>	 7. A mound or ridge serving to mark<BR>the boundary of a field. village, &c.<BR>	 8. A landmark.<BR>	 9. The horizon.<BR>10. A suture, (of a skull.)<BR>	 11. The utmost limit, last degree, (fig.)<BR>E. सीमन् + ढाप्: see सीमन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमानिश्चय|सीमानिश्चयः
सीमानिश्चय m. (-यः) A legal decision with respect to boundaries, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमान्त|सीमांत|सीमान्तः
सीमान्त m. (-न्तः) A frontier line, a border.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमालिङ्ग|सीमालिंग
सीमालिङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A land or boundary-mark.<BR> E. सीमा, and लिङ्ग mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमावाद|सीमावादः
सीमावाद m. (-दः) A dispute about boundaries; also सीमाविवाद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमाविवाद|सीमाविवादः
सीमाविवाद m. (-दः) Litigation or dispute respecting boundaries.<BR> E. सीमा<BR>and विवाद dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमावृक्ष|सीमावृक्षः
सीमावृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A tree serving as a boundary-mark.<BR> E. सीमा, वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमासन्धि|सीमासंधि|सीमासंधिः
सीमासन्धि m. (-न्धिः) The meeting of two boundaries.<BR> E. सीमा, सन्धि junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमीक
सीमीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A kind of tree.<BR>	 2. An ant-hill.<BR>	 3. An ant or any<BR>similar small insect.<BR> E. ष्यम् to sound, and कीकन् Unādi aff., य<BR>changed to इ, and that made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीर|सीरः
सीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A plough.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. The Arka plant.<BR> E. षि to bind,<BR>Unādi aff. रन्, and the vowel made long; also शीर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरक|सीरकः
सीरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A porpoise.<BR>	 2. A plough.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 4. The Arka plant.<BR>E. सीर a plough, कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरध्वज|सीरध्वजः
सीरध्वज m. (-जः) An epithet of JANAKA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरपाणि|सीरपाणिः
सीरपाणि m. (-णिः) BALADEVA.<BR> E. सीर a plough, and पाणि the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरयोग|सीरयोगः
सीरयोग m. (-गः) The yoking of cattle to a plough, or a team so yoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरिन्
सीरिन् m. (-री) BALARĀMA.<BR> E. सीर a plough, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीलन्द|सीलंद
सीलन्द m. (-न्दः) A kind of fish; also read सीलन्ध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीवन|सीवनं
सीवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sewing, stitching.<BR>	 2. A seam, a suture.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The<BR>frenum of the prepuce.<BR>	 2. A needle.<BR> E. षिव् to sew, ल्युट् aff.; also सेवन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीस|सीसं
सीस n. (-सं) Lead.<BR> E. षि to bind, क्विप् aff.; or षो to destroy, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीसक|सीसकं
सीसक n. (-कं) Lead.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीसपत्रक|सीसपत्रकं
सीसपत्रक n. (-कं) Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीहुण्ड|सीहुंड|सीहुंडः|सीहुण्डः
सीहुण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The milk-hedge plant, (Euphorbia antiquorum, &c.)<BR>E. सी for सिद्ध complete, and हुण्ड a heap, from हुडि to collect, aff.<BR>घञ्, form irr. “स्नुही वृक्षे” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
सु r. 1st cl. (सवति)<BR>	 1. To bring forth, as young.<BR>	 2. To possess power.<BR>3. To go: see षु and षू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सु
सु Ind. A particle and prefix analogous to good, well, or the Greek<BR>Eu, and implying:--1. Reverence, worship, honour.<BR>	 2. Assent.<BR>3. Increase, prosperity.<BR>	 4. Excess, exceeding.<BR>	 5. Pain, distress.<BR>6. Pleasure, delight.<BR>	 7. With ease.<BR>	 8. Beauty.<BR> E. षु to go, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकण्टका
सुकण्टका f. (-का) The Aloe-plant.<BR> E. सु good or much, कण्टक thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकण्डु|सुकंडु|सुकण्डुः
सुकण्डु m. (-ण्डुः) Psora, itch, scab.<BR> E. सु much, कण्डु the same disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकन्द|सुकंद|सुकन्दः
सुकन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. The onion.<BR>	 2. A yam.<BR>	 3. A sort of grass, (Scirpus<BR>kyssoor.)<BR>	 4. An esculent root, (Arum campanulatum.)<BR> E. सु good,<BR>excellent, and कन्द a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकन्दक|सुकंदक|सुकन्दकः
सुकन्दक m. (-कः) An onion.<BR> E. सु good, कन्द a root, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकर|सुकरः
सुकर mfn. (-रः-रा or -री-रं)<BR>	 1. Easy, practicable, attainable.<BR>	 2. Doing well<BR>or becomingly.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Doing good to, charity, benevolence.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-रा) A tractable cow.<BR> E. सु pleasure, कृ to make or confer, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकर्णिका
सुकर्णिका f. (-का) A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR> E. सु good, कर्ण an ear,<BR>कन्, aff. of comparison, and fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकर्म्मन्|सुकर्मन्
सुकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, good, acting virtuously, doing<BR>what is right and fit.<BR>	 2. Active, diligent.<BR>	 m. (-र्म्मा)<BR>	 1. The artist or<BR>architect of the gods.<BR>	 2. One of the astronomical Yogas.<BR> E. सु<BR>good, कर्म्मन् act, action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकल|सुकलः
सुकल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Liberal, both in giving and using.<BR> E. सु good, कल् to call, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकाण्डिन्|सुकांडिन्
सुकाण्डिन् m. (-ण्डी) A bee. Adj. Having good stems or stocks, beauti-<BR>fully joined.<BR> E. सु good, काण्ड a shrub, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकालिन्
सुकालिन् m. (-ली) A progenitor of a particular class considered as those<BR>of the Śūdra tribe.<BR> E. सु good, काल time, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकालुका
सुकालुका f. (-का) The Dodi shrub.<BR> E. सु + कल उण् स्वार्थे क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकुन्दक|सुकुंदक|सुकुन्दकः
सुकुन्दक m. (-कः) An onion.<BR> E. सु + कुदि-ण्वुल्; also सुकन्दक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकुमार|सुकुमारः
सुकुमार mfn. (-रः-रा or -री-रं)<BR>	 1. Soft, smooth, tender.<BR>	 2. Youthful,<BR>young.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A variety of the sugar-cane.<BR>	 2. A sort of the grain,<BR>(Panicum colonum, &c.)<BR>	 3. A wild kind of Champaka.<BR>	 4. The name<BR>of a Daitya.<BR>	 5. A beautiful young man.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Double jasmine.<BR>2. Great-flowered jasmine.<BR>	 3. The plantain.<BR>	 4. The name of a river.<BR>E. सु very, exceedingly, कुमार soft, young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकुमारक|सुकुमारकः
सुकुमारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A beautiful young man.<BR>	 2. Rice.<BR>	 n. (-कं) The leaf<BR>of Tamāla-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकृत्
सुकृत् mfn. (-कृत्)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, pious.<BR>	 2. Fortunate, well-fated.<BR> E. सु well, कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकृत|सुकृतं
सुकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, pious.<BR>	 2. Befriended, assisted, treated<BR>with kindness.<BR>	 3. Fortunate, auspicious.<BR>	 4. Done well, properly,<BR>ably, &c.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Virtue, moral merit.<BR>	 2. Fortune, auspiciousness.<BR>3. Kindness, bounty, friendly aid or assistance.<BR>	 4. Any kind or<BR>friendly act.<BR>	 5. Reward, recompense, especially heaven as the<BR>reward of virtue.<BR> E. सु well, and कृत made or done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकृति|सुकृतिः
सुकृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Virtue, well-doing.<BR>	 2. Kindness, acting in a friendly<BR>or kindly manner.<BR>	 3. The practice of religious austerities, &c. E.<BR>सु good, and कृति action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकृतिन्
सुकृतिन् mfn. (-ती-तिनी-ति)<BR>	 1. Fortunate, well-fated.<BR>	 2. Virtuous, pious,<BR>good.<BR>	 3. Benign, benevolent.<BR>	 4. Learned, wise.<BR> E. सुकृत auspicious-<BR>ness, &c., इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकेसर|सुकेसरः
सुकेसर m. (-रः) The citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकोली
सुकोली f. (-ली) A medicinal root, commonly Kṣira-kākoli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुक्रतु|सुक्रतुः
सुक्रतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. AGNI or fire.<BR>	 2. INDRA.<BR>	 3. VARUṆA.<BR>	 4. MITRA.<BR>	 5. SOMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुक्रिया
सुक्रिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. A good action, a good work, a moral or religious<BR>observance.<BR> E. सु, and क्रिया act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख|सुखं
सुख r. 10th cl. (सुखयति-ते) To make happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख|सुखं
सुख mfn. (-खः-खा-खं)<BR>	 1. Happy, joyful, delighted.<BR>	 2. Virtuous, pious.<BR>3. Easy, practicable.<BR>	 4. Agreeable, sweet, comfortable.<BR>	 5. Suitable.<BR>n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. Happiness, pleasure, delight.<BR>	 2. Heaven, paradise.<BR>	 3.<BR>Water.<BR>	 4. Prosperity.<BR>	 5. Ease, alleviation.<BR>	 6. Easiness.<BR>	 f. (-खा) The<BR>capital of VARUṆA.<BR> E. सु good, ख an organ of sense; or सुख-अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखकर|सुखकरः
सुखकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Conferring happiness.<BR>	 2. Doing any thing<BR>easily.<BR>	 3. Done easily.<BR> E. सुख, and कर who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखङ्घुण|सुखंघुण|सुखंघुणः|सुखङ्घुणः
सुखङ्घुण m. (-णः) A kind of weapon or staff with which ŚIVA is armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखचार|सुखचारः
सुखचार m. (-रः) An excellent horse.<BR> E. सुख pleasure, चर् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखच्छेद्य|सुखछेद्य
सुखच्छेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Easily to be cut or destroyed.<BR> E. सुख, and च्छेद्य<BR>to be cut or cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखजात|सुखजातः
सुखजात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Happy, taking pleasure.<BR>	 2. Born or produced<BR>easily.<BR> E. सुख, जात born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखद|सुखदं|सुखदः
सुखद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Conferring or affording pleasure, &c.<BR>	 f. (-दा) A<BR>courtezan of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>	 n. (-दं) The seat of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सुख<BR>pleasure, दा to give, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखदोह्या
सुखदोह्या f. (-ह्या) A cow easily milked.<BR> E. सुख (with,) pleasure, दोह्य to be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखप्रतीक्ष
सुखप्रतीक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं) Hoping or expecting happiness.<BR> E. सुख, and<BR>प्रति before ईक्ष् to see, ण aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखभाग
सुखभाग m. (-गः) Happiness, good fortune.<BR> E. सुख, and भाग share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखभागिन्
सुखभागिन् mfn. (-गी-गिनी-गि) Happy, delighted.<BR> E. सुखभाग, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखभेद्य
सुखभेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) Easily broken or disunited.<BR> E. सुख, and भेद्य to<BR>be broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखमय
सुखमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Full or consisting of happiness, delightful.<BR> E. सुख, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखवर्च्चक|सुखवर्चक|सुखवर्चकः|सुखवर्च्चकः
सुखवर्च्चक m. (-कः) Natron, alkali.<BR> E. सुख pleasure, वर्च्च् to shine, aff. क्वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखवासन|सुखवासनः
सुखवासन m. (-नः) Perfume for the mouth.<BR> E. सुख pleasure, and वासन<BR>perfuming; also मुखवासन and शुभवासन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखवेदन
सुखवेदन n. (-नं) Consciousness of pleasure.<BR> E. सुख, वेदन knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखसन्दुह्या|सुखसंदुह्या
सुखसन्दुह्या f. (-ह्या) A tractable and gentle cow. E. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=789-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखसन्दोह्या|सुखसंदोह्या
सुखसन्दोह्या f. (-ह्या) A tractable cow, one easily and quickly milked. E.<BR>सुख pleasure, सम् before दुह् to milk, ण्यत् aff.; also with क्यप् aff.<BR>सुखसन्दुह्या as above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखसाध्य
सुखसाध्य mfn. (-ध्यः-ध्या-ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Easy of accomplishment or attainment.<BR>2. Easy of cure.<BR>	 3. Easy to be discomfited.<BR> E. सुख, and साध्य to be<BR>broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखस्पर्श
सुखस्पर्श mfn. (-र्शः-र्शा-र्शं) Gratifying, agreeable to the touch or feelings.<BR> E. सुख, स्पर्श touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखाधार|सुखाधारः
सुखाधार m. (-रः) Svarga, the heaven of INDRA, and paradise of the<BR>Hindus.<BR> E. सुख pleasure, and आधार a receptacle or reservoir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखानुभव
सुखानुभव m. (-वः) Anticipation or consciousness of pleasure.<BR> E. सुख and<BR>अनुभव perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखान्त
सुखान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Wishing well, friendly, attached.<BR>	 2. Sub-<BR>versive of happiness.<BR> E. सुख, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखायत|सुखायतं|सुखायतः
सुखायत m. (-तः) An excellent and well-trained horse.<BR> E. सुख pleasure, आयत restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखायन|सुखायनः
सुखायन m. (-नः) A good horse.<BR> E. सुख pleasure, and अयन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखार्थ|सुखार्थः
सुखार्थ n. Adv. (-र्थं) For the sake of ease, happiness, &c.<BR> E. सुख, and<BR>अर्थम् on account of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखार्थिन्
सुखार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Seeking or wishing for happiness.<BR> E. सुख, अर्थिन् seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखालोक
सुखालोक Adj. Charming, pleasant-looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखावतीश्वर|सुखावतीश्वरः
सुखावतीश्वर m. (-रः) A deified teacher of the Bauddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखावह|सुखावहः
सुखावह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Conferring pleasure, delighting, pleasing. E.<BR>सुख pleasure, आङ् before वह् to convey, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखाश|सुखाशः
सुखाश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. VARUṆA, deity of water.<BR>	 2. A cucumber, (Cucumbis<BR>sativus.)<BR>	 2. Eating with pleasure, feeding on dainties, &c.<BR> E. सुख<BR>pleasure, अश् to eat, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखाशक|सुखाशकः
सुखाशक m. (-कः) The common cucumber.<BR> E. सुखाश the same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखासीन
सुखासीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Seated or sitting at ease.<BR> E. सुख, आसीन seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखास्वाद|सुखास्वादः
सुखास्वाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं)<BR>	 1. Well-flavoured.<BR>	 2. Delightful, agreeable.<BR>m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Enjoyment.<BR>	 2. A pleasant flavour.<BR> E. सुख, आस्वाद taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखाहर
सुखाहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Conferring pleasure, agreeable, delightful. E.<BR>सुख and आङ् before हृ to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखिन्
सुखिन् mfn. (-खी-खिनी-खि) Happy, pleasant, possessing happiness or<BR>pleasure.<BR>	 m. (-खी) A yati or religious ascetic.<BR> E. सुख pleasure, इनि<BR>poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखिस्वभाव
सुखिस्वभाव m. (-वः) A happy or contented disposition.<BR> E. सुखिन्, and स्वभाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखेच्छा
सुखेच्छा f. (-च्छा) Hope or desire of happiness.<BR> E. सुख, and इच्छा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखैषिन्
सुखैषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Wishing well to, seeking another's happiness.<BR>E. सुख, and एषिन् who wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोत्सव|सुखोत्सवः
सुखोत्सव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Pleasure-festival, jubilee.<BR>	 2. A husband.<BR> E. सुख pleasure, उत्सव a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोदक|सुखोदकं
सुखोदक n. (-कं) Warm water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोदय|सुखोदयः
सुखोदय m. (-यः) Realization or occurence of pleasure.<BR> E. सुख, उदय arising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोदर्क
सुखोदर्क mfn. (-र्कः-र्का-र्कं) Yielding or leading to happiness or pleasure.<BR>E. सुख, and उदर्क consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोद्य
सुखोद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं) To be uttered easily or agreeably.<BR> E. सुख, उद्य to be spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोपविष्ट
सुखोपविष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Seated comfortably or at ease.<BR> E. सुख, and<BR>उपविष्ट seated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुखोपसर्प्य
सुखोपसर्प्य mfn. (-र्प्यः-र्प्या-र्प्यं) Easy of access.<BR> E. सुख, and उपसर्प्य to be approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख्यात
सुख्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Celebrated, famous.<BR> E. सु, and ख्यात renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुख्याति
सुख्याति f. (-तिः) Fame, celebrity.<BR> E. सु, and ख्याति fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग|सुगं|सुगः
सुग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Graceful, elegant.<BR>	 2. Going well or elegantly.<BR>3. Well rid of.<BR>	 4. Plain, intelligible.<BR>	 5. Easy of access.<BR>	 n. (-गं)<BR>Fæces, ordure.<BR> E. सु well, good, गम् to go, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगण्
सुगण् mfn. (-गण्) Counting well, a ready reckoner, or of easy calcu-<BR>lation.<BR> E. सु well, easily, गण् to number, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगणित
सुगणित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Easily or accurately calculated.<BR> E. स, and गणित counted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगत|सुगतः
सुगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Passed, gone.<BR>	 2. Well-bestowed.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A<BR>Buddha in general, one of the generic terms for a deified sage,<BR>and teacher of the Bauddha sect.<BR> E. सु well, and गत gone or<BR>known, (by whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्ध|सुगंध|सुगन्धं|सुगन्धः
सुगन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Fragrant, sweet-smelling.<BR>	 n. (-न्धं)<BR>	 1. Small<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">Page790-b+ 60</a>]<BR>cummin seed.<BR>	 2. A fragrant grass; also कुत्तृण.<BR>	 3. The blue lotus.<BR>4. Sandal.<BR>	 m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Fragrance, ordour.<BR>	 2. Sulphur.<BR>	 3. A sort of<BR>Morinda.<BR>	 4. A trader, a dealer.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. The ichneumon plant.<BR>2. Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>	 3. A fragrant grass.<BR>	 4. A sort<BR>of lime.<BR>	 5. Holy basil, (Ocymum sanctum.)<BR>	 6. Jasmine, (of vari-<BR>ous sorts.)<BR> E. सु good, and गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धक|सुगंधक|सुगन्धकः
सुगन्धक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Sulphur.<BR>	 2. The orange.<BR>	 3. A sort of gourd,<BR>(Momordica mixta.)<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धि|सुगंधि|सुगन्धिः
सुगन्धि mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि)<BR>	 1. Fragrant, sweet-smelling.<BR>	 2. Virtuous,<BR>pious.<BR>	 m. (-न्धिः)<BR>	 1. A fragrance.<BR>	 2. A fragrant sort of mango.<BR>	 3.<BR>The supreme being.<BR>	 n. (-न्धि)<BR>	 1. A drug and perfume, commonly<BR>Elabāluka.<BR>	 2. The root of long-pepper.<BR>	 3. A fragrant grass,<BR>(Cyperus rotundus.)<BR>	 4. Another sort, (Scirpus kyssoor.)<BR>	 5. Corian-<BR>der seed.<BR> E. सु good, well, गन्ध smell, and इ substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिक|सुगंधिक|सुगन्धिकं|सुगन्धिकः
सुगन्धिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A large sort of rice.<BR>	 2. Incense.<BR>	 3. Sulphur.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>The white lotus.<BR> E. सु pleonasm, गन्ध smell, ठक् aff.; also सौगन्धिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिकुसुम|सुगन्धिकुसुमः
सुगन्धिकुसुम m. (-मः) A sort of Nerium with yellowish flowers.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>A plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR> E. सुगन्धि fragrant, कुसुम flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिता
सुगन्धिता f. (-ता) Fragrance, pleasing scent, such as is produced by the<BR>trituration of perfumes.<BR> E. सुगन्धि fragrant, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिमूल|सुगन्धिमूलं
सुगन्धिमूल n. (-लं) The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>	 f. (-ला) Rāsnā,<BR>the ichneumon plant.<BR> E. सुगन्धि fragrant, मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगन्धिमूषिका
सुगन्धिमूषिका f. (-का) The musk rat or shrew.<BR> E. सुगन्धि fragrant, मूषिका a mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगम|सुगमः
सुगम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Accessible, good, (as a road.)<BR>	 2. Easy, practi-<BR>cable.<BR>	 3. Plain, intelligible.<BR> E. सु well, ready, and गम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगहन|सुगहनः
सुगहन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Thick, close, impervious.<BR>	 f. (-ना) An enclosure<BR>round a place of sacrifice, to exclude profane access or sight.<BR> E. सु<BR>well, much or thoroughly, गह् to be thick, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगुप्त
सुगुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Secret, well-hidden or kept secret.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-प्तं)<BR>Secretly, privily.<BR> E. सु, and गुप्त hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगुप्ति
सुगुप्ति f. (-प्तिः) Closeness, secrecy.<BR> E. सु, and गुप्ति secrecy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगृह|सुगृहः
सुगृह m. (-हः) The tailor bird, (Sylvia sutoria.)<BR>	 f. (-ही) Adj. Having<BR>a beautiful abode.<BR> E. सु handsome or good, and गृह a house or nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगृहीत|सुगृहीतः
सुगृहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Held fast or firmly, seized, grasped.<BR>	 2. Taken<BR>or applied properly or auspiciously.<BR> E. सु well, and गृहीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुगृहीतनामन्
सुगृहीतनामन् m. (-मा) An epithet of YUDHIṢṬHIRA, and others, whose<BR>names it is auspicious to invoke early in the morning.<BR> E. सु auspi-<BR>cious, and गृहीत taken, and नामन् a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग्रास|सुग्रासः
सुग्रास m. (-सः) A dainty morsel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग्राह्य
सुग्राह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) Easily apprehensible, easy to be laid hold of, &c.<BR> E. सु, ग्राह्य to be taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग्रीव|सुग्रीवः
सुग्रीव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Handsome-necked.<BR>	 m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. One of the horses of<BR>of KṚṢṆA'S car.<BR>	 2. A monkey-king, the son of the sun, and<BR>sovereign of Kishkindhyā, and friend and confederate of RĀMA<BR>CHANDRA.<BR>	 3. The father of the ninth Jina of the present age.<BR>4. ŚIVA.<BR>	 5. INDRA.<BR>	 6. A goose.<BR>	 7. A hero.<BR>	 8. A piece of water.<BR>9. The name of a mountain.<BR>	 10. A sort of weapon.<BR>	 11. The<BR>countenance of a friend.<BR>	 12. A serpent of Pātāla.<BR> E. सु handsome,<BR>and ग्रीवा a neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग्रीवेश|सुग्रीवेशः
सुग्रीवेश m. (-शः) RĀMA.<BR> E. सुग्रीव the monkey king, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुग्ल|सुग्लः
सुग्ल mfn. (-ग्लः-ग्ला-ग्लं) Very weary.<BR> E. सु very, ग्लै to be weary, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुघटित
सुघटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well-contrived or devised, well-arranged or<BR>managed.<BR>	 2. Well-joined or united.<BR>	 3. Brought into agreeable<BR>contract.<BR> E. सु, and घटित contrived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुघोर
सुघोर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Hideous, terrific.<BR> E. सु very, घोर fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुघोष|सुघोषः
सुघोष m. (-षः) A pleasant sound.<BR> E. सु, and घोष sound or cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचक्षुस्
सुचक्षुस् m. (-क्षुः)<BR>	 1. The glomerous fig-tree.<BR>	 2. A wise or learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचरित
सुचरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well-conducted, well-behaved.<BR>	 2. Well-man-<BR>aged or pursued.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Good conduct.<BR> E. सु, and चरित gone, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचरित्र
सुचरित्र n. (-त्रं) Good or virtuous course of life.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा) A devoted and<BR>virtuous wife.<BR> E. सु good, चरित्र conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=790-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचारु|सुचारुः
सुचारु mfn. (-रुः-रुः or -र्व्वी-रु)<BR>	 1. Very beautiful.<BR>	 2. Pleasing, delightful.<BR>E. सु very, चारु lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचारुस्वन
सुचारुस्वन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Melodious, mellifluous.<BR> E. सुचारु, and स्वन<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचित्रक|सुचित्रकः
सुचित्रक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A king-fisher.<BR>	 2. A kind of peckled snake.<BR> E. सु much, चित्रक variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिन्तन
सुचिन्तन n. (-नं) Deliberate consideration.<BR> E. सु, चिति to think, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिन्ता|सुचिंता
सुचिन्ता f. (-न्ता) Deep reflection or consideration.<BR> E. सु, चिन्ता thinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिन्तित
सुचिन्तित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-weighed, well-considered.<BR> E. सु well, चिति<BR>to think. क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिरम्
सुचिरम् Ind. Very long, (a time.)<BR> E. सु much, चिरम् long time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचिरायुस्
सुचिरायुस् m. (-युः) A god, a divinity.<BR> E. सु very, चिर a long time, आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचुटी
सुचुटी f. (-टी) A pair of nippers or tongs, &c.<BR> E. सु well, चट् to cut, aff.<BR>क, and ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुचेलक|सुचेलकः
सुचेलक m. (-कः) Cloth or fine cloth.<BR> E. सु excellent, चेल cloth, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुच्छत्री
सुच्छत्री f. (-त्री) The river Sutlej.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजन|सुजनः
सुजन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, good, respectable.<BR>	 2. Kind, benevo-<BR>lent.<BR>	 m. (-नः) The charioteer of INDRA.<BR> E. सु good, and जन person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजनता
सुजनता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Goodness, benevolence.<BR>	 2. A number of respectable<BR>persons.<BR> E. सुजन, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजनत्व
सुजनत्व n. (-त्वं) Kindness, benevolence.<BR> E. त्व added to सुजन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजन्मन्
सुजन्मन् mfn. (-न्मा-न्मा-न्म) Legitimate, of respectable birth.<BR> E. सु, जन्मन् birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजल|सुजलं
सुजल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Having clear or sweet water.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Good<BR>water.<BR>	 2. A lotus.<BR> E. सु, and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजल्प|सुजल्पः
सुजल्प m. (-ल्पः) A good speech; it is thus defined:--<BR>“यत्रार्जवात् सगाम्भीर्य्यं सदैन्यं सहचापलम् ।<BR>सोत्कण्ठञ्च हरिः स्पृष्टः स सुजल्पो निगद्यते ॥”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजाति
सुजाति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Of a good tribe or species.<BR> E. सु, जाति tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजीर्ण
सुजीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Well-digested.<BR>	 2. Decayed, worn out.<BR> E. सु,<BR>and जीर्ण digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुजीवित
सुजीवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Lived well or to some purpose.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A lucky<BR>or happy life.<BR> E. सु well जीवित living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुट्ट
सुट्ट r. 10th cl. (सुट्टयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To disregard, to despise.<BR>	 2. To be low, small, or shallow; also षुट्ट ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत|सुतः
सुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A prince.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A daughter.<BR>	 2. A plant,<BR>(Hedysarum alhagi.)<BR>	 f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Poured out.<BR>	 2. Extracted.<BR>	 3.<BR>Begotten, brought forth.<BR> E. षु to bear or bring forth, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतक
सुतक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Birth.<BR>	 2. Impurity from child-birth or mis-carriage:<BR>see सूतक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतङ्गम|सुतंगम|सुतंगमः
सुतङ्गम m. (-मः) The father of a son.<BR> E. सुत, गम् to obtain, खच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुज्ञात
सुज्ञात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well or easily known.<BR> E. सु, and ज्ञात known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतनिर्विशेषम्
सुतनिर्विशेषम् Ind. Just like a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतनु|सुतनुः
सुतनु mfn. (-नुः-नुः or -न्वी-नु)<BR>	 1. Very thin or delicate.<BR>	 2. Extremely fine.<BR>f. (-नुः or -न्वी) A beautiful woman.<BR> E. सु excellent, तनु thin; also सुतनू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतपस्
सुतपस् m. (-पाः)<BR>	 1. A hermit, an ascetic.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 n. (-पः) Severe<BR>penance. Adj.<BR>	 1. One who practises severe penance.<BR>	 2. Having<BR>great heat.<BR> E. सु very, profoundly, तपस् religious austerity, or तप्<BR>to heat, असि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतप्त
सुतप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Hot, very hot.<BR> E. सु, and तप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतराम्
सुतराम् Ind.<BR>	 1. Better, more excellently.<BR>	 2. Consequently, of course.<BR>3. Exceedingly.<BR>	 4. More positively.<BR> E. सु good, तराम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतर्द्दन|सुतर्दन|सुतर्दनः|सुतर्द्दनः
सुतर्द्दन m. (-नः) The Indian cuckoo.<BR> E. सु much, तृद् or तर्द्द् to hurt, aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतल|सुतलः
सुतल mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. A division of the lower regions, the sixth in<BR>descent.<BR>	 2. Immense depth.<BR>	 m. (-लः) The basement or foundation<BR>of a large building.<BR> E. सु well, and तल deep, profound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतवत्|सुतवन्त्
सुतवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having children.<BR>	 m. (-वान्)<BR>	 1. A drinker of<BR>the Asclepias juice.<BR>	 2. The father of a son.<BR> E. सुत, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतवस्करा
सुतवस्करा f. (-रा) The mother of seven children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतश्रेणी
सुतश्रेणी f. (-णी) A plant, (Salvinia cucullata.)<BR> E. सुत offspring, श्रेणी a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतस्नेह|सुतस्नेहः
सुतस्नेह m. (-हः) Paternal affection.<BR> E. सुत, and स्वेह affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतात्मज|सुतात्मजः
सुतात्मज m. (-जः) A grandson.<BR>	 f. (-जा) A grand-daughter.<BR> E. सुत a son,<BR>or सुता a daughter, and आत्मजा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतारका
सुतारका f. (-का) A sort of tutelar goddess peculiar to the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतार्थिन्
सुतार्थिन् mfn. (-र्थी-र्थिनी-र्थि) Desirous of having a son.<BR> E. सुत, अर्थिन् who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुति|सुतिः
सुति f. (-तिः) Extraction of the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतिक्तक|सुतिक्तकः
सुतिक्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A kind of gentian, (Gentiana cherayta.)<BR>	 2. The coral<BR>tree.<BR> E. सु very, तिक्त bitter, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतिन्
सुतिन् m. (-ती) A father, one who has a son.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A mother, the<BR>mother of a son.<BR> E. सुत, and इनि aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतीक्ष्ण|सुतीक्ष्णः
सुतीक्ष्ण mfn. (-क्ष्णः-क्ष्णा-क्ष्णं)<BR>	 1. Verp sharp.<BR>	 2. Very pungent.<BR>	 3. Acutely<BR>painful.<BR>	 m. (-क्ष्णः) A tree, (Hypernathera morunga.)<BR> E. सु exceed-<BR>ingly, and तीक्ष्ण sharp, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतीर्थ|सुतीर्थः
सुतीर्थ n. (-र्थं) A good preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतुङ्ग|सुतुंग|सुतुङ्गः
सुतुङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Very lofty or tall.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) The cocoanut tree.<BR> E. सु very, तुङ्ग tall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतुस्
सुतुस् Adj. Well-sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतेजस्
सुतेजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः)<BR>	 1. Very bright, splendid.<BR>	 2. Potent.<BR>	 m. (-जाः)<BR>One of the Jinas of the last age.<BR> E. सु much, तेजस् light or glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतोत्पत्ति|सुतोत्पत्तिः
सुतोत्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Birth of a son.<BR> E. सुत, उत्पत्ति birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्या
सुत्या f. (-त्या)<BR>	 1. Religious bathing.<BR>	 2. Extraction of the Soma juice.<BR>	 3.<BR>Parturition.<BR> E. षु to bear, क्यप् aff., form irr.; more usually सूत्या ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्रामन्
सुत्रामन् m. (-मा) INDRA.<BR> E. सु good, त्र to preserve, (the world,) मनिन्<BR>aff.; also सूत्रामन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्वन्
सुत्वन् m. (-त्वा)<BR>	 1. A student who has performed his ablutions subsequent,<BR>or according to some, preparatory to a sacrifice.<BR>	 2. A drinker of<BR>the Asclepias juice.<BR>	 3. An offerer of the same.<BR> E. षु to bring<BR>forth, क्वनिप् aff., तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुद
सुद(सुन्दति) 1. To beautify.<BR>	 2. To light. सौ० प० सक० सेट् इदित् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदक्षिण
सुदक्षिण m. (-णः) A sovereign of VIDARBHA.<BR>	 f. (-णा) The wife of<BR>DILĪPA. Adj.<BR>	 1. Very sincere or upright.<BR>	 2. Liberal in sacrificial<BR>gifts.<BR> E. सु very, दक्षिण clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदण्ड|सुदंड|सुदण्डः
सुदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदत्|सुदन्त्
सुदत् mfn. (-दन्-दती or -दन्ती-दत्) Having handsome teeth.<BR> E. सु handsome, and दतृ for दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदत्त
सुदत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Well or properly given.<BR> E. सु, and दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदन्त|सुदंत|सुदन्तः
सुदन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. An actor, a dancer.<BR>	 2. A good tooth.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती) The<BR>female elephant presiding over the N. W. quarter.<BR> E. सु good,<BR>handsome, and दन्त a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदम
सुदम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Easy to be subdued.<BR> E. सु, and दम taming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदर्शन|सुदर्शनं|सुदर्शनः
सुदर्शन mfn. (-नः-ना or -नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Handsome, good looking.<BR>	 2. Easily<BR>seen.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The discus of KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 2. Mount Meru.<BR>	 3. The<BR>rose apple, (Eugenia jambu.)<BR>	 4. The father of the eighteenth<BR>Jaina pontiff of the present era.<BR>	 5. One of the nine Suklabalas<BR>or BALARĀMAS of the Jainas.<BR>	 6. A vulture.<BR>	 nf. (-नं-नी) The city<BR>of INDRA.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A drug.<BR>	 2. Order, command.<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>(Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>	 4. A woman, a handsome woman. E.<BR>सु good, दर्शन sight or appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदा
सुदा Adj. Very bountiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदान्त|सुदान्तः
सुदान्त m. (-न्तः) A follower of ŚĀKYA MUNI, the teacher of the Baud-<BR>dhas.<BR> E. सु well, and दान्त tamed, (whose passions.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदामन्
सुदामन् m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. A mountain.<BR>	 3. INDRA'S elephant.<BR>	 4. The<BR>name of a cowherd.<BR>	 5. The sea.<BR>	 6. A poor Brāhman raised to<BR>wealth and honours by KṚṢṆA. Adj. One who gives liberally. E.<BR>सु good, excellent, and दामन् a cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदाय|सुदायः
सुदाय m. (-यः) A special gift, as alms to a student at his initiation,<BR>a nuptial present, &c.<BR> E. सु auspicious, and दाय a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदारु|सुदारुः
सुदारु m. (-रुः) The Pāryātra mountains, part of the Vindhya range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदि
सुदि Ind. In the light-half of a lunar month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदिन|सुदिनं
सुदिन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A fine day, fine weather.<BR>	 2. An auspicious day.<BR> E. सु, and दिन a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदिनाह|सुदिनाहं
सुदिनाह n. (-हं)<BR>	 1. A fine day.<BR>	 2. An auspicious day.<BR> E. सुदिन fair<BR>weather, and अह for अहन् a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदिव
सुदिव mfn. (-वः-वा-वं) Passing pleasant days.<BR> E. सु, दिव a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदीर्घ|सुदीर्घः
सुदीर्घ mfn. (-र्घः-र्घा-र्घं) Very long, (in space or time.)<BR>	 f. (-र्घा) A kind of<BR>cucumber.<BR> E. सु very, दीर्घ long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=791-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदीर्घधर्म्मा|सुदीर्घधर्मा
सुदीर्घधर्म्मा f. (-र्म्मा) A plant, (Marsilia quadrifolia.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुराचार
सुदुराचार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Very wicked, abandoned or profligate.<BR> E. सु very, दुराचार bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुरारुह
सुदुरारुह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Inaccessible.<BR> E. सु and दुर with आङ् before रुह्<BR>to mount, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुर्जय
सुदुर्जय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Difficult to be overcome.<BR> E. सु very, दुर्जय difficult to be conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुर्दर्श|सुदुर्द्दर्श
सुदुर्दर्श mfn. (-शः-र्शा-र्शं) Difficult to be beheld.<BR> E. सु very, दुर्दर्श difficult<BR>to be seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुर्लभ|सुदुर्ल्लभः
सुदुर्लभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Difficult to be attained, unattainable, impracti-<BR>cable.<BR> E. सु very, दुर्लभ difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुश्चर|सुदुश्चरः
सुदुश्चर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Very arduous or painful, difficult to be per-<BR>formed or attained.<BR> E. सु very, दुश्चर arduous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुष्कर|सुदुष्करः
सुदुष्कर mfn. (-रः-रा or -री-रं) Very difficult.<BR> E. सु very, दुष्कर difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुस्तर|सुदुस्तरः
सुदुस्तर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Impassable, difficult to be passed or crossed. E.<BR>सु very, दुर् difficult, तॄ to cross, टच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदुस्मह
सुदुस्मह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Very difficult to be endured.<BR> E. सु very, दुस्सह unendurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदूर
सुदूर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Very distant.<BR> E. सु very, and दूर remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदृश्
सुदृश् mfn. (-दृक्) Having handsome eyes.<BR>	 f. (-दृक्) A pretty woman. E.<BR>सु excellent, and दृश् sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदृढ|सुदृढं
सुदृढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Solid, firm.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-ढं) Very hard or firm.<BR> E. सु very, and दृढ hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधन्वन्
सुधन्वन् m. (-न्वा)<BR>	 1. An archer, a bowman.<BR>	 2. VIŚHWAKARMAN, the artist<BR>of the gods.<BR>	 3. A prince so named. Adj. Having an excellent bow.<BR>E. सु good, धनुस् a bow, अनङ् substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधन्वाचार्य्य|सुधन्वाचार्य|सुधन्वाचार्यः|सुधन्वाचार्य्यः
सुधन्वाचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) The son of an outcaste Vaiśya by a woman of the same class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधर्म्म|सुधर्म|सुधर्म्मः
सुधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) One of the principal disciples of MAHĀVIRA, the last<BR>Jina of the present age; he survived his master, and the different<BR>ascetics or candidates for holiness are traced from him in regular<BR>succession; none of the other ten disciples of Mahāvira having left<BR>successors.<BR>	 f. (-र्म्मी) A council of the gods.<BR> E. सु excellent, and<BR>धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधर्म्मन्|सुधर्मन्
सुधर्म्मन् mf. (-र्म्मा) The council or assembly of the gods.<BR>	 m. (-र्म्मा) A man<BR>attentive to the proper maintenance of his family.<BR> E. सु excellent,<BR>धर्म्म virtue, अनिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधा
सुधा f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. Nectar, the beverage of immortality and sustenance of<BR>the gods.<BR>	 2. The nectar or honey of flowers.<BR>	 3. Juice.<BR>	 4. Plaster,<BR>mortar.<BR>	 5. A brick.<BR>	 6. The Ganges.<BR>	 7. Water.<BR>	 8. Lightning.<BR>	 9.<BR>The milk-hedge plant, (Euphorbia antiquorum, &c.)<BR>	 10. A plant,<BR>(Aletris Hyacinthoides.)<BR>	 11. Emblic myrobalan.<BR>	 12. Yellow myro-<BR>balan.<BR> E. सु pleasure, धे to drink, or धा the have, to support, (life,)<BR>अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधांशु|सुधांशुः
सुधांशु m. (-शुः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. सुधा nectar, and अंशु a ray<BR>of light: the moon being the supposed repository of the beverage<BR>of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधांशुतैल|सुधांशुतैलं
सुधांशुतैल n. (-लं) Camphorated oil.<BR> E. सुधांशु Camphor, and तैल oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधांशुरत्न|सुधांशुरत्नं
सुधांशुरत्न n. (-त्नं) A pearl.<BR> E. सुधांशु the moon, and रत्न a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाकर|सुधाकरः
सुधाकर m. (-रः) The moon.<BR> E. सुधा nectar, आकर a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाङ्ग|सुधाङ्गः
सुधाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. सुधा nectar, अङ्ग body or substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाजीविन्
सुधाजीविन् m. (-वी) A bricklayer, a plasterer.<BR> E. सुधा plaster, and जीविन्<BR>who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाद्रव|सुधाद्रवः
सुधाद्रव m. (-वः) A nectar-like fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाधवलित
सुधाधवलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) White-washed, stuccoed, plastered.<BR> E. सुधा, and धवलित whitened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाधार|सुधाधारः
सुधाधार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. सुधा nectar, आधार a<BR>receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधानिधि|सुधानिधिः
सुधानिधि m. (-धिः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. सुधा nectar, and निधि a receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधापाणि|सुधापाणिः
सुधापाणि m. (-णिः) The divine physician, DHANWANTARI.<BR> E. सुधा nectar,<BR>पाणि hand, bearing in his hands the beverage of immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभवन
सुधाभवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A stuccoed house.<BR>	 2. The fifth Muhūrta or hour<BR>after noon.<BR> E. सुधा, and भवन mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभित्ति|सुधाभित्तिः
सुधाभित्ति f. (-त्तिः)<BR>	 1. A plastered wall.<BR>	 2. A brick-well.<BR>	 3. The fifth<BR>muhūrta or hour after noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधामुज्
सुधामुज् m. (-भुक्) A deity, an immortal.<BR> E. सुधा nectar, भुज् to enjoy, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभृति|सुधाभृतिः
सुधाभृति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. सुधा nectar, and<BR>भृति cherishing; also सुधासूति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधामय|सुधामयः
सुधामय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं)<BR>	 1. Made of plaster, &c.<BR>	 2. Consisting of nectar.<BR>n. (-यं) A palace, a mansion, a brick or stone building.<BR> E. सुधा<BR>mortar or a brick, and मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावर्ष|सुधावर्षः
सुधावर्ष m. (-र्षः) A shower of ambrosia.<BR> E. सुधा, and वर्ष rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावर्षिन्
सुधावर्षिन् m. (-र्षी)<BR>	 1. A Buddha or deified sage of the Bauddha religion.<BR>2. BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. सुधा nectar, and वर्षिन् raining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावास|सुधावासः
सुधावास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR>	 f. (-सा) A kind of cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावृष्टि
सुधावृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A shower of ambrosia.<BR> E. सुधा, and वृष्टि rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधासित
सुधासित Adj.<BR>	 1. White as mortar.<BR>	 2. Bright as nectar.<BR>	 3. Bound by nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधासूति|सुधासूतिः
सुधासूति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>	 3. A lotus. E.<BR>सुधा nectar, सूति birth, production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधास्यन्द
सुधास्यन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दी-न्दं) Shedding ambrosia.<BR> E. सुधा, स्यन्द what sheds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधास्यन्दिन
सुधास्यन्दिन Adj. Mellifluous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधास्रवा
सुधास्रवा f. (-वा) Uvula or soft palate.<BR> E. सुधा nectar or honey. स्रु to distil, अप् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाहर|सुधाहरः
सुधाहर m. (-रः) GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सुधा<BR>nectar, and हर who steals; having on one occasion stolen the<BR>moon for the sake of the Amrita which was to be communicated<BR>to the serpent children of KADRU, in consideration of which his<BR>mother VINATĀ was to be released from a state of servitude to<BR>KADRU, the wife, as well as herself, of the sage KAŚYAPA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाहृत्
सुधाहृत् m. (-हृत्) GARUḌA.<BR> E. सुधा nectar, and हृत् taking, stealing: see<BR>the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधिति|सुधितिः
सुधिति mf. (-तिः-तिः) An axe.<BR> E. सु well, धि to hold, क्तिन् aff.; more correctly स्वधितिः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधी
सुधी m. (-धीः)<BR>	 1. A Paṇḍit, a learned man or teacher.<BR>	 2. An intelligent<BR>person.<BR> E. सु well, ध्यै to think, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधूम
सुधूम m. (-मः) A kind of incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधोद्भव|सुधोद्भवः
सुधोद्भव m. (-वः) DHANWANTARI, the physician of Svarga.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>Chebulic myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula.)<BR> E. सुधा nectar, and<BR>उद्भव produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनन्द|सुनन्दं|सुनन्दः
सुनन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं) Pleasing, delighting.<BR>	 n. (-न्दं) The club of<BR>BALARĀMA.<BR>	 f. (-न्दा)<BR>	 1. The goddess UMĀ.<BR>	 2. A sort of pigment and<BR>drug: see गोरोचना.<BR>	 3. A woman.<BR>	 4. One of UMĀ'S female<BR>companions.<BR>	 5. A plant, (Aristolochia Indica.)<BR> E. सु well,<BR>thoroughly, नदि to please, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनय|सुनयः
सुनय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Policy.<BR>	 2. Good conduct.<BR> E. सु, and णी to take, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनयन|सुनयनः
सुनयन m. (-नः) A deer.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A woman.<BR>	 2. A woman having<BR>beautiful eyes.<BR> E. सु good excellent, नयन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनाकृत|सुनाकृतः
सुनाकृत m. (-तः) Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनाभ|सुनाभः
सुनाभ m. (-भः) The MAINĀKA mountain; part of the ranges of southern<BR>India, personified as the son of Himālaya, and Menā.<BR>	 f. (-भा)<BR>1. Having a good nave or centre.<BR>	 2. Having a beautiful navel. E.<BR>सु well, नाभि the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनार|सुनारः
सुनार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The udder of a bitch.<BR>	 2. The egg of a snake.<BR>	 3. A sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनालक|सुनालकः
सुनालक m. (-कः) A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनासीर|सुनासीरः
सुनासीर m. (-रः) INDRA.<BR> E. सु good, excellent, नासीर the van of an army,<BR>the leader of the celestial hosts; also सुनाशीर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिग्रह
सुनिग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Easily restrained.<BR> E. सु, and निग्रह confinement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिद्रा
सुनिद्रा f. (-द्रा) Sound sleep.<BR> E. सु, and निद्रा sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिभृत
सुनिभृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Very lonely or private.<BR> E. सु, and निभृत lonely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिभृतम्
सुनिभृतम् Ind. Privately, very secretly.<BR> E. सु, and निभृतम् privately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिरूपित
सुनिरूपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-observed or inspected.<BR> E. सु, निरूपित seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिश्चित|सुनिश्चितः
सुनिश्चित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ascertained, determined.<BR>	 2. Commended,<BR>approved.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A deified sage, according to the Jainas or<BR>Bauddhas.<BR> E. सु well, thoroughly, and निश्चित ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिषण्णक|सुनिषण्णकं|सुनिषण्णकः
सुनिषण्णक n. (-कं) A potherb, (Marsilia quadrifolia.) “सुसुनि शाक” ।<BR> E. सु<BR>well, निषण्ण depression of spirits or drowsiness, कन् aff.; also<BR>without the final, सुनिषण्ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनिष्टप्त|सुनिष्टप्तः
सुनिष्टप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Burnished.<BR> E. सु well, thoroughly, निष्टप्त heated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=792-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनीत
सुनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well-behaved.<BR>	 2. Politic.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Good<BR>conduct.<BR>	 2. Policy, prudence.<BR> E. सु well, णी to guide, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनीति|सुनीतिः
सुनीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Propriety of behaviour, good manners.<BR>	 2. Good policy.<BR>3. The mother of DHRUVA.<BR> E. सु good, नीति morals or manners.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनीथ|सुनीथः
सुनीथ mfn. (-थः-था-थं) Virtuous, moral, good, of proper disposition or<BR>conduct.<BR>	 m. (-थः) A Brāhmana. सु well, नी to obtain, aff. थक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनील|सुनीलं|सुनीलः
सुनील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Very black or blue, dark.<BR>	 m. (-लः) The pome-<BR>granate tree.<BR>	 n. (-लं) The root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला) Common flax.<BR> E. सु much, नील blue or black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनीलक|सुनीलकः
सुनीलक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The blue shrike.<BR>	 2. The emerald or sapphire.<BR> E. सु<BR>very, नील blue or black, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनेत्र
सुनेत्र f. (-त्रा) Beautiful-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्दर|सुंदर|सुन्दरं|सुन्दरः
सुन्दर mfn. (-रः-रा or -री-रं) Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 m. (-रः) KĀMADEVA.<BR>f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A handsome woman.<BR>	 2. A small timber tree, (Heritiera<BR>minor.)<BR>	 3. Turmeric.<BR>	 4. A species of metre.<BR> E. सु good, excellent,<BR>दृ to respect, aff. अप्; or सु with उन्दि to moisten, aff. अरन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्वत्|सुन्वन्त्
सुन्वत् mfn. (-न्वत्-न्वन्ती-न्वत्) Sacrificing.<BR> E. षुञ् to sacrifice, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपक्व|सुपक्वः
सुपक्व mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं)<BR>	 1. Ripe, mature.<BR>	 2. Well-cooked.<BR>	 m. (-क्वः) A sort of<BR>fragrant mango.<BR> E. सु well, thoroughly, पक्व ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपच
सुपच mfn. (-चः-चा-चं) Food easily digested.<BR> E. सु easily, पच् to digest, aff. खल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपत्री
सुपत्री f. (-त्री) A woman having a good husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपत्र|सुपत्रं|सुपत्रः
सुपत्र n. (-त्रं) The leaf of the Laurus cassia.<BR> E. सु good, and पत्र leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपथ|सुपथः
सुपथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. A good road.<BR>	 2. Good conduct.<BR>	 3. Good course.<BR> E. सु<BR>good, पथिन् a road, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपथिन्
सुपथिन् m. (-थाः)<BR>	 1. A good road.<BR>	 2. A country, &c., having good roads.<BR> E. सु good, पथिन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपद्मा
सुपद्मा f. (-द्मा) Orris root.<BR> E. सु + पद्-म ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपरीक्षण
सुपरीक्षण n. (-णं) Examining or trying well or thoroughly.<BR> E. सु, and परीक्षण trying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपरीक्षित
सुपरीक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-examined or tried.<BR> E. सु, परीक्षित tried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्ण|सुपर्णः
सुपर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A tree,<BR>(Cassia fistula.)<BR>	 3. A cock.<BR>	 4. A being of a superhuman character,<BR>as GARUḌA, and other birds of an equally fanciful description;<BR>one of those classes first created by the BRAHMĀDIKAS, and<BR>included in the daily presentation of water to deceased ancestors,<BR>&c.<BR>	 5. A ray of the sun.<BR>	 f. (-र्णा or -र्णी)<BR>	 1. Name of the mother of<BR>GARUḌA.<BR>	 2. A number of lotuses, or a pool abounding with them.<BR>Adj.<BR>	 1. Well-winged.<BR>	 2. Having beautiful leaves.<BR> E. सु handsome,<BR>and पर्ण a leaf or feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्णक|सुपर्णकः
सुपर्णक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A kind of Cassia, (C. fistula.)<BR>	 2. A small tree,<BR>(Echites scholaris.)<BR>	 3. A bird of superhuman character: see the<BR>last.<BR> E. सु good, पर्ण a wing, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्णकेतु|सुपर्णकेतुः
सुपर्णकेतु m. (-तुः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सुपर्ण GARUḌA, केतु symbol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्णाख्य
सुपर्णाख्य m. (-ख्यः) A plant, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR> E. सुपर्ण Cassia, आख्य appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्णीतनय|सुपर्णीतनयः
सुपर्णीतनय m. (-यः) GARUḌA.<BR> E. सुपर्णी a name of VINATĀ, तनय a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्य्याप्त|सुपर्याप्त
सुपर्य्याप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं)<BR>	 1. Extensive, vast.<BR>	 2. Comprehensive.<BR>	 3. Well<BR>laid out, (as a place with all sorts of buildings.)<BR> E. सु, पर्य्याप्त<BR>complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपर्व्वन्|सुपर्वन्
सुपर्व्वन् m. (-र्व्वा)<BR>	 1. A god, a deity.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. A bamboo.<BR>	 4. A<BR>lunar day, in which religious ceremonies are particularly perform-<BR>ed, as the new moon, and the eighth and the fourteenth days of<BR>each fortnight.<BR>	 5. Smoke. Adj. Well-jointed.<BR> E. सु good or much,<BR>and पर्व्वन् a knot or joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपलायित
सुपलायित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Completely fled or run away.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A total<BR>rout or retreat.<BR> E. सु, and पलायित fled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपात्र|सुपात्रं
सुपात्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. An able or clever man.<BR>	 2. A vessel of earthen ware,<BR>&c.<BR>	 3. Any suitable vessel.<BR> E. सु good, and पात्र a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपाद्
सुपाद् mfn. (-पात्-पाद् or -पदी) Having a handsome foot.<BR> E. सु, and पाद् for<BR>पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपान|सुपानः
सुपान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Drinking well, easily or deeply.<BR> E. सु well, पा to drink, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपार्श्व|सुपार्श्वः
सुपार्श्व m. (-र्श्वः)<BR>	 1. The seventh Jina or Jaina deified teacher of the<BR>present era.<BR>	 2. The waved-leaf fig-tree: see प्लक्ष ।<BR> E. सु good, पार्श्व side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपार्श्वक|सुपार्श्वकः
सुपार्श्वक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The third Jina of the future era.<BR>	 2. The veined-<BR>leaf fig, (Ficus venosa.)<BR> E. सु good. पार्श्व a side, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपीडन
सुपीडन n. (-नं) Rubbing and kneading the hands and feet.<BR> E. सु<BR>pleasantly or intensely, पीड् to pain, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपीत|सुपीतं|सुपीतः
सुपीत n. (-तं) A carrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपुंसी
सुपुंसी f. (-सी) A woman having a good husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपुत्त्र
सुपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) An excellent son.<BR> E. सु, and पुत्त्र a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपुष्प|सुपुष्पं|सुपुष्पः
सुपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. The coral tree.<BR>	 2. The Śirīṣa tree, (Mimosa Sirisha.)<BR>n. (-ष्पं)<BR>	 1. Cloves.<BR>	 2. The menstrual excretion.<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी)<BR>	 1. The plantain-<BR>tree.<BR>	 2. A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa and panmorium.)<BR>	 3.<BR>A flower, (Clitoria ternatea, the white sort.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पा or -ष्पी) Adj.<BR>Having beautiful flowers.<BR> E. सु excellent, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपूर|सुपूरः
सुपूर m. (-रः) A sort of lime or citron.<BR> E. सु well, and पूर what is full, (of seeds.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुपूरक|सुपूरकः
सुपूरक m. (-कः) A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्त|सुप्तं|सुप्तः
सुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्त)<BR>	 1. Sleeping, asleep.<BR>	 2. Senseless, numbed.<BR>	 n. (-प्तं)<BR>Sleep, deep or sound sleep.<BR> E. ष्वप् to sleep, क्त aff., and the semi-<BR>vowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तघातक|सुप्तघातकः
सुप्तघातक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Mischievous, murderous.<BR> E. सुप्त asleep, and घातक killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तजन|सुप्तजनः
सुप्तजन m. (-नः) Midnight.<BR> E. सुप्त asleep, and जन mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तज्ञान|सुप्तज्ञानं
सुप्तज्ञान n. (-नं) Dreaming, a dream.<BR> E. सुप्त asleep, and ज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तत्वच्
सुप्तत्वच् mfn. (-त्वक्) Benumbed, paralytic.<BR> E. सुप्त, त्वच् the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तविज्ञान|सुप्तविज्ञानं
सुप्तविज्ञान n. (-नं) A dream, dreaming.<BR> E. सुप्त sleeping, विज्ञान knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्ति|सुप्तिः
सुप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Sleep, sleeping.<BR>	 2. Numbness, insensibility, paralysis.<BR>3. Drowsiness, sleepiness.<BR>	 4. Trust, confidence.<BR> E. ष्वप् to sleep,<BR>aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रकाश
सुप्रकाश (-शः-शा-शं) 1. Manifest, apparent.<BR>	 2. Public.<BR> E. सु very, प्रकाश apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतर्क|सुप्रतर्कः
सुप्रतर्क m. (-र्कः) A sound judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतिभा
सुप्रतिभा f. (-भा) Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतिष्ठा
सुप्रतिष्ठा f. (-ष्ठा)<BR>	 1. Consecration, erection, (as of a temple or idol.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Fame.<BR>	 3. A form of metre, a stanza of four lines, containing five<BR>syllables each. Adj.<BR>	 1. Standing well.<BR>	 2. Famous.<BR> E. सु and प्रति<BR>intensitives, ष्ठा to stay or be, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतिष्ठित|सुप्रतिष्ठितः
सुप्रतिष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Consecrated.<BR>	 2. Celebrated.<BR> E. सु, and<BR>प्रतिष्ठा to consecrate, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतिष्णात
सुप्रतिष्णात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Certain, ascertained.<BR> E. सु and प्रति before ष्णा to bathe, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रतीक|सुप्रतीकः
सुप्रतीक (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Well-made, handsome.<BR>	 2. Having a beautiful<BR>trunk.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The elephant of the north-east quarter.<BR>	 2.<BR>KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 3. ŚIVA.<BR> E. सु handsome, प्रतीक form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रपाण
सुप्रपाण n. (-णं) A good tank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रभ|सुप्रभः
सुप्रभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Splendid, brilliant, glorious.<BR>	 m. (-भः) One of the<BR>nine Śuklabalas or BALARĀMAS of the Jainas.<BR>	 f. (-भा) One of the<BR>seven tongues of fire.<BR> E. सु excellent or excessive, and प्रभा light,<BR>lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रभात|सुप्रभातं
सुप्रभात n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. An auspicious dawn.<BR>	 2. The earliest dawn.<BR> E. सु, and प्रभात shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रयुक्त|सुप्रयुक्तः
सुप्रयुक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Joined, closely connected or in contact.<BR>	 2.<BR>Well-managed, as an instrument or weapon.<BR> E. सु well, प्रयुक्त joined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रयोग|सुप्रयोगः
सुप्रयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Dexterity, expertness.<BR>	 2. Contact, approximation.<BR>E. सु well, प्रयोग junction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रयोगविशिख|सुप्रयोगविशिखः
सुप्रयोगविशिख m. (-खः) A good archer.<BR> E. सु well, प्रयोग possessing,<BR>managing, and विशिख an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रलम्भ|सुप्रलम्भः
सुप्रलम्भ mfn. (-म्भः-म्भा-म्भं) Easy of attainment.<BR> E. सु well, प्र before लभ to get, खल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रलाप|सुप्रलापः
सुप्रलाप m. (-पः) Eloquence, elegant discourse, speaking or discoursing<BR>well.<BR> E. सु well, and प्रलाप speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रसन्न|सुप्रसन्नः
सुप्रसन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Well-pleased, favouring, favourable.<BR>	 m. (-न्नः)<BR>KUVERA.<BR> E. सु well, and प्रसन्न pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रसाद|सुप्रसादः
सुप्रसाद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Kind, complacent, auspicious.<BR>	 m. (-दः) ŚIVA. E.<BR>सु well, good, and प्रसाद favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रात
सुप्रात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dawning finely, (as the day.)<BR> E. सु, प्रातर dawn, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्रिय|सुप्रियः
सुप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Agreeable, pleasant, liked, loved.<BR>	 m. (-यः) (In<BR>prosody,) A foot of two short syllables, a Pyrrhic.<BR> E. सु, प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=793-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुफल|सुफलः
सुफल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Bearing good fruit, (literally or figuratively.)<BR>	 m.<BR>(-लः)<BR>	 1. The wood apple, (Feronia elephantium.)<BR>	 2. The pome-<BR>granate.<BR>	 3. Jujube.<BR>	 4. A sort of bean, (Phaseolus Mungo.)<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>1. Colocynth.<BR>	 2. A pumpkin-gourd.<BR>	 3. The plantain.<BR>	 4. The brown<BR>grape.<BR> E. सु good, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुफेन|सुफेनः
सुफेन n. (-नं) Cuttle-fish-bone.<BR> E. सु good, फेन froth or foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबन्ध|सुबंध|सुबन्धः
सुबन्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Well-secured, having a good binding.<BR>	 m. (-न्धः)<BR>Sesamum.<BR> E. सु, and बन्ध binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबुद्धि
सुबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Wise, clever, intelligent.<BR> E. सु, बुद्धि intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबोध|सुबोधः
सुबोध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं)<BR>	 1. Easily taught.<BR>	 2. Of easy apprehension.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-धः)<BR>	 1. Knowledge.<BR>	 2. Waking.<BR> E. सु, and बोध making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुब्रह्मण्य|सुब्रह्मण्यः
सुब्रह्मण्य m. (-ण्यः)<BR>	 1. KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 2. Name of one of the sixteen priests<BR>employed at a sacrifice.<BR> E. सु good, and ब्रह्मण्य the Brāhmanical<BR>order, of whom he is the special guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभग|सुभगः
सुभग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Pleasing to the eye, grateful to the site.<BR>	 2.<BR>Beloved, liked.<BR>	 3. Fortunate, auspicious.<BR>	 m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Borax.<BR>	 2.<BR>The Asoka tree.<BR>	 3. The champaka, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 4. Red<BR>amaranth.<BR>	 f. (-गा)<BR>	 1. A woman beloved by her husband, a<BR>favourite wife.<BR>	 2. A respectable and auspicious mother.<BR>	 3. A<BR>wild variety of Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 4. Turmeric.<BR>	 5. Holy basil.<BR>	 6.<BR>A shrub, (Hedysarum Gangeticum.)<BR>	 n. (-गं) Good fortune.<BR> E. सु<BR>good, excellent, and भग fortune, beauty, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभगम्भावुक|सुभगंभावुक
सुभगम्भावुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Become pleasant or agreeable.<BR> E. सुभग, भू<BR>to be, खुकञ् aff., मुम् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभगासुत|सुभगासुतः
सुभगासुत m. (-तः) The son of an auspicious mother.<BR> E. सुभगा as above, सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभङ्ग|सुभंग|सुभङ्गः
सुभङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) Separating or dividing easily.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) The<BR>cocoanut-tree.<BR> E. सु, and भङ्ग breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभट|सुभटः
सुभट m. (-टः) A champion, a warrior.<BR> E. सु, and भट a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभद्र|सुभद्रः
सुभद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं) Propitious, auspicious, fortunate.<BR>	 m. (-द्रः) A<BR>name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 f. (-द्रा)<BR>	 1. The sister of JAGANNĀTH whose<BR>image is worshipped with those of that deity and his brother<BR>BALARĀMA, and carried in procession with them in the Ratha-<BR>Yātrā, or annual movement of the car of JAGANNĀTH; she is the<BR>wife of ARJUNA.<BR>	 2. A creeper, (Echites frutescens.)<BR>	 3. A plant,<BR>commonly Ghṛta-mandā.<BR> E. सु exceedingly, भद्र auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभद्रक|सुभद्रकः
सुभद्रक n. (-कं) A car of the gods.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभद्राणी
सुभद्राणी f. (-णी) A plant and drug, commonly Trāyamāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभद्रेश|सुभद्रेशः
सुभद्रेश m. (-शः) A name of ARJUNA.<BR> E. सुभद्रा the sister of JAGANNĀTH, ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभर
सुभर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Heavily burthened.<BR> E. सु, भर bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभाञ्जन|सुभाञ्जनः
सुभाञ्जन m. (-नः) A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga;) a various reading of शोभाञ्जन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभाषित|सुभाषितः
सुभाषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Spoken well or eloquently.<BR>	 2. Well-spoken,<BR>speaking or discoursing well.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Eloquence.<BR>	 2. A witty<BR>saying, an apophthegm.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A deified sage, according to the<BR>Bauddhas.<BR> E. सु good, excellent, भाषा speech, इतच् aff., or भाष् to<BR>speak, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभिक्ष|सुभिक्षः
सुभिक्ष n. (-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Good alms, successful begging.<BR>	 2. Abundance of food.<BR>f. (-क्षा) A tree, (Grislea tomentosa.)<BR> E. सु well, भिक्ष् to beg, or<BR>obtain by begging, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभीरक्
सुभीरक् m. (-कः) The Palāsha tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभूम|सुभूमः
सुभूम m. (-मः) A name of KĀRTAVĪRYA, as the eighth Chakravarti, or<BR>universal emperor, according to the Jainas.<BR> E. सु good, भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभृत
सुभृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Cherished, protected.<BR> E. सु well, भृत nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभृश्
सुभृश् mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Much, exceeding.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-शं) Much, excessive.<BR>E. सु insensitive prefix, and भृश much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभोगीन
सुभोगीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Desirable, fit to be enjoyed.<BR> E. सु, भोग enjoyment, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभैरव
सुभैरव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Very fearful, terrific.<BR> E. सु, and भैरव fearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुभ्रु|सुभ्रुः
सुभ्रु f. (-भ्रुः or -भ्रू) A woman. Adj. Having beautiful eyebrows; the<BR>voc. of this word is सुभ्रूः, but सुभ्रु often occurs in classics.<BR> E. सु<BR>handsome, and भ्रु or भ्रू eyebrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम|सुमं|सुमः
सुम n. (-मं) A flower.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR>	 3. Sky.<BR> E. सु<BR>excellent, मा the goddess LAKṢMĪ; prized by her; or मक् aff.:<BR>see कुसुम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमङ्गल
सुमङ्गल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Very fortunate or auspicious.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A plant,<BR>commonly Ghrita-maṇḍā.<BR> E. सु very, मङ्गल auspicious. “माकडहाता” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमत|सुमतः
सुमत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Friendly, well or kindly disposed.<BR> E. सु well, मन्<BR>to mind, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमति|सुमतिः
सुमति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The fifth Jina or Jaina teacher of the present era.<BR>2. One of the Jainas of the past era.<BR>	 f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Friendship, kind-<BR>ness, good disposition.<BR>	 2. Favour of the gods, blessing.<BR>	 3. Hymn,<BR>prayer.<BR>	 4. Desire.<BR> E. सु good, मति intelligence or understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमद
सुमद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Very drunk, mad, or empassioned.<BR> E. सु, मद<BR>madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमदन|सुमदनः
सुमदन m. (-नः) The mango-tree.<BR> E. सु + मद--निच्--ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमदात्मजा
सुमदात्मजा f. (-जा) An Apsaras or courtezan or INDRA'S heaven.<BR> E. सु<BR>much, मद intoxication, and आत्मजा a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमधुर|सुमधुरं
सुमधुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Pleasant, gentle, soothing, (speech or discourse.)<BR>2. Sweet, saccharine.<BR> E. सु very, and मधुर sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमध्य
सुमध्य f. (-ध्या) Slender-waisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमध्यमा
सुमध्यमा f. (-मा) A woman with a handsome waist.<BR> E. सु, मध्यम middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमन|सुमनः
सुमन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Handsome, beautiful.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Wheat.<BR>	 2. The<BR>thorn-apple, (Datura metel.)<BR>	 f. (-ना) Great-flowered jasmine.<BR> E. सु<BR>good, मन् to think, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनःफल|सुमनःफलं|सुमनःफलः
सुमनःफल m. (-लः) Elephant or wood-apple, (Feronia elephantium.) E.<BR>सुमनस् a flower, and फल fruit. “कत्बेल” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनस्
सुमनस् m. (-नाः)<BR>	 1. A god, an immortal.<BR>	 2. A Paṇḍit, a learned man<BR>or teacher.<BR>	 3. A student of the Vedas, and supplementary<BR>sciences.<BR>	 4. A plant, (Cæsalpinia Bonducella.)<BR>	 5. Wheat.<BR>	 6. The<BR>Nimba-tree.<BR>	 mn. (-नाः-नः) or fem., but then always plur., even in<BR>the singular acceptation. (-सः) A flower in general.<BR>	 f. sing. (-नाः)<BR>Great-flowered jasmine. Adj.<BR>	 1. Good-minded.<BR>	 2. Well-pleased. E.<BR>सु well, excellent, मन् to think, असि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनोभर
सुमनोभर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Ornamented with or having flowers.<BR> E. सुमनस्, and भर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनोरजस्
सुमनोरजस् n. (-जः) The pollen of a flower.<BR> E. सुमनस् a flower, रजस् dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमनोहर
सुमनोहर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Very agreeable, pleasing, beautiful, &c.<BR> E. सु,<BR>and मनोहर grateful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमन्तु|सुमन्तुः
सुमन्तु m. (-न्तुः) A saint and legislator so named.<BR> E. सु + मन--तुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमन्त्रित
सुमन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well or wisely counselled, well-advised.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>Wise counsel.<BR> E. सु, and मन्त्रित advised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमहत्|सुमहन्त्
सुमहत् mfn. (-हन्-हती-हत्) Very large or abundant.<BR> E. सु, महत् great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमित्र|सुमित्रः
सुमित्र m. (-त्रः) The father of the twentieth Jina of the present era.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-त्रा) One of the wives of DAŚARATHA, and the mother of LAKSH-<BR>MAṆA.<BR> E. सु good, and मित्र a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमित्रभू
सुमित्रभू m. (-भूः)<BR>	 1. SAGARA, as one of the Chakravartis or emperors of<BR>the Jainas.<BR>	 2. The twentieth Jina of the present period.<BR> E. सुमित्रं a<BR>proper name, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमित्राभू
सुमित्राभू m. (-भूः) LAKSHMAṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमुख|सुमुखं|सुमुखः
सुमुख mfn. (-खः-खा or -खी-खं)<BR>	 1. Pleasing, agreeable.<BR>	 2. Lovely, hand-<BR>some-faced.<BR>	 m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. The son of GARUḌA.<BR>	 2. One of the serpents<BR>of Pātāla.<BR>	 3. A kind of potherb.<BR>	 4. A Paṇḍit, a learned man or<BR>teacher.<BR>	 5. GANEŚA.<BR>	 n. (-खं) The mark or scratch of a finger-<BR>nail.<BR>	 f. (-खी) A species of the Triṣṭubh-metre.<BR>	 f. (-खा or -खी)<BR>1. A handsome woman.<BR>	 2. A mirror.<BR> E. सु excellent, मुख countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमुखसू
सुमुखसू m. (-सूः) GARUḌA.<BR> E. सुमुख his son, and सू producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमू
सुमू mfn. (-मूः-मूः-मु) Who or what binds well.<BR> E. सु, मू to bind, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमेधस्
सुमेधस् mfn. (-धाः-धाः-धः) Sensible, intelligent, of good capacity or<BR>understanding.<BR>	 f. (-धाः) Heart-pea.<BR> E. सु good, मेधस् apprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमेरु|सुमेरुः
सुमेरु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु) Best, excellent.<BR>	 m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. The sacred mountain<BR>Meru: see मेरु.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR> E. सु excellent, मि to shed or scatter,<BR>(radiance,) रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=794-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्नयु|सुम्नयुः
सुम्नयु m. (-युः) A chanter of hymns.<BR> E. सुम्न a particular hymn, used as a<BR>verb, उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्पलुण्ठ|सुम्पलुण्ठः
सुम्पलुण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) Zedoary, (Curcuma Zerumbet.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्भ|सुम्भः
सुम्भ m. (-म्भः) A country so named; also read सुह्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयन्त्रित
सुयन्त्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-governed or regulated.<BR> E. सु, यन्त्रित restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयवस
सुयवस n. (-सं) Beautiful grass, good pasturage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयामुन|सुयामुनः
सुयामुन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A name of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. A prince, sovereign of<BR>Kośāmbi; also named VATSA-RĀJ.<BR>	 3. A palace.<BR>	 4. A mountain. E.<BR>सु well, यमुना the river, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयुद्ध
सुयुद्ध n. (-द्धं) A well fought war or battle.<BR> E. सु, and युद्ध war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयोधन|सुयोधनः
सुयोधन m. (-नः) A name of DURYODHANA, the chief of the Kuru family.<BR>E. सु well, or with pleasure, युध् to combat, युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुर्
सुर् r. 6th cl. (सुरति)<BR>	 1. To possess superhuman power.<BR>	 2. To shine; also षुर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुर|सुरः
सुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A god, a deity.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. A sage, a learned man.<BR>4. The number “thirty-three”.<BR>	 f. (-रा or री)<BR>	 1. Spirituous liquor in<BR>general personified: also as a nymph, produced at the churning<BR>of the ocean.<BR>	 2. A drinking vessel.<BR>	 3. A snake.<BR>	 4. Water.<BR> E. षु<BR>to possess power, Unādi aff. रक्; or षुर् to be radiant, क affix;<BR>or सुरा wine, (whose, that falling to the share of the gods;) or सु<BR>excellent, राज् to shine, aff. ड, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरकारु|सुरकारुः
सुरकारु m. (-रुः) An epithet of Viśhwakarman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरकार्मुक
सुरकार्मुक n. (-कं) A rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरक्त|सुरक्तः
सुरक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं)<BR>	 1. Deeply or well-coloured or dyed.<BR>	 2. Deep red,<BR>crimson.<BR>	 3. Strongly affected or impassioned.<BR> E. सु well, रञ्ज् to dye,<BR>&c., aff. क्त्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरक्तक|सुरक्तकः
सुरक्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A variety of red chalk, that called golden.<BR>	 2. A fruit-<BR>tree, apparently a sort of mango, bearing a small red fruit. E.<BR>सुरक्त very red, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरक्षण
सुरक्षण n. (-णं) Taking good care of, protecting, preserving.<BR> E. सु, रक्षण preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरक्षित
सुरक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-preserved or protected.<BR> E. सु well, रक्षित<BR>preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरगण|सुरगणः
सुरगण m. (-णः) A class or company of divinities.<BR> E. सुर, गण a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरगुरु|सुरगुरुः
सुरगुरु m. (-रुः) VṚHASPATI, regent of Jupiter and preceptor of the<BR>gods.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and गुरु spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरग्रामणी
सुरग्रामणी m. (-णीः) INDRA, the ruler of Svarga.<BR> E. सुर a god, ग्रामणी leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरङ्ग|सुरंग|सुरङ्गं|सुरंगः|सुरङ्गः
सुरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. The orange.<BR>	 2. Bright or good colour or dye.<BR>	 3. A<BR>hole cut in a wall.<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. Red sanders.<BR>	 2. Vermilion.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>1. A hole cut in a wall to break into a house, &c.; see सुरुङ्गा.<BR>	 2.<BR>A subterranean passage.<BR>	 3. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.)<BR>	 4.<BR>Crystal.<BR> E. सु well, and रङ्ग colour; or सृ-अङ्गच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरङ्गद|सुरङ्गदं
सुरङ्गद n. (-दं) Red sanders.<BR> E. सुरङ्ग good colour, द what yields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरङ्गवातु
सुरङ्गवातु m. (-तुः) Red chalk.<BR> E. सुरङ्ग good or much colour, धातु a mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरङ्गयुज्
सुरङ्गयुज् m. (-युक्) A housebreaker.<BR> E. सुरङ्ग a hole in a wall, and युज्<BR>who joins or makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरजःफल|सुरजःफलः
सुरजःफल m. (-लः) The jack-fruit tree.<BR> E. सुरजस् abundant farina, and फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरजनी
सुरजनी f. (-नी) Night.<BR> E. सु well, रजनी night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरज्येष्ठ|सुरज्येष्ठः
सुरज्येष्ठ m. (-ष्ठः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and ज्येष्ठ elder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरञ्जन|सुरंजन|सुरञ्जनः
सुरञ्जन m. (-नः) The betel-nut tree, (Areca faufel or catechu.)<BR> E. सु well,<BR>and रञ्जन pleasing, affecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरत|सुरतं
सुरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Compassionate, tender.<BR>	 2. Playful.<BR>	 3. Much<BR>enjoyed.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Copulation, coition.<BR>	 2. Great enjoyment.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ता) Godhead, divinity.<BR> E. सु well, रम् to sport or play, aff. क्त; or<BR>सुर a deity, and तल् aff. of state or condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरतताली
सुरतताली f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. A female messenger, a go-between.<BR>	 2. A chaplet,<BR>a garland for the head.<BR> E. सुरत coition, and ताल tune, &c., aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरतप्रसङ्ग|सुरतप्रसंग
सुरतप्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Addiction to amorous pleasures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरति|सुरतिः
सुरति f. (-तिः) Great enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरतोषक|सुरतोषकः
सुरतोषक m. (-कः) The jewel worn by KṚṢṆA on his breast.<BR> E. सुर a<BR>deity, तुष् to please, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरदारु
सुरदारु n. (-रु) A sort of Pine, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR> E. सुर a deity, दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरदीर्घिका
सुरदीर्घिका f. (-का) The Ganges of heaven.<BR> E. सुर a god, दीर्घिका a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरद्रुम|सुरद्रुमः
सुरद्रुम m. (-मः) The Deodar Pine.<BR> E. सुर, and द्रुम a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरद्विप|सुरद्विपः
सुरद्विप m. (-पः) An elephant of the gods, either that of INDRA or of<BR>either of the other rulers of the different quarters.<BR> E. सुर god, and<BR>द्विप an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरद्विष्
सुरद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) An Asura, an infernal being, the natural enemy of the<BR>gods.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and द्विष् an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरधनुस्
सुरधनुस् n. (-नुः) The rainbow.<BR> E. सुर a god, धनुस् a bow; the bow of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरधूप|सुरधूपः
सुरधूप m. (-पः) Resin, turpentine.<BR> E. सुर a god, and धूप incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरन
सुरन(ण)दी f. (-दी) The Ganges of heaven.<BR> E. सुर a god, and नदी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरनिम्नगा
सुरनिम्नगा f. (-गा) The Ganges.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and निम्नगा a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरन्दला
सुरन्दला f. (-ला) A river so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपति|सुरपतिः
सुरपति m. (-तिः) INDRA, sovereign of the gods.<BR> E. सुर a deity, पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपथ|सुरपथं
सुरपथ n. (-थं) Sky, heaven.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and पथिन् a path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपर्ण|सुरपर्णं
सुरपर्ण n. (-र्णं) A drug, probably a leaf, commonly called Māchi-parṇi<BR>and described as pungent and bitter, anthelmintic, stomachic,<BR>and a remover of phlegm and catarrh.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपर्णिका
सुरपर्णिका f. (-का) A tree, (Rottleria tinctoria.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपर्वत|सुरपर्वतः
सुरपर्वत m. (-तः) The mount MERU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरपुरी
सुरपुरी f. (-री) The capital of INDRA.<BR> E. सुर a god, and पुरी a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरप्रिय|सुरप्रियः
सुरप्रिय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. VṚHASPATI, the preceptor of the gods.<BR>	 3.<BR>The Elœocarpus.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and प्रिय beloved by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभि|सुरभिः
सुरभि mfn. (-भिः-भिः or -भी-भि)<BR>	 1. Fragrant, sweet-smelling.<BR>	 2. Pleasing,<BR>beloved.<BR>	 3. Friendly, a friend.<BR>	 4. Celebrated, famous.<BR>	 5. Wise,<BR>learned.<BR>	 6. Handsome.<BR>	 7. Good, virtuous.<BR>	 m. (-भिः)<BR>	 1. A fragrance,<BR>a perfume, a sweet-smelling substance.<BR>	 2. The Michelia Champaca.<BR>3. Nutmeg.<BR>	 4. The month Chaitra, (March-April.)<BR>	 5. Resin.<BR>	 6.<BR>The Śamī-tree.<BR>	 7. The Kadamba-tree.<BR>	 8. A kind of<BR>fragrant grass.<BR>	 f. (-भिः or भी)<BR>	 1. The gum Olibanum tree,<BR>(Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>	 2. Murā, a sort of drug and perfume.<BR>	 3.<BR>One of the divine Mātṛs.<BR>	 4. A cow.<BR>	 5. A fabulous cow, the cow<BR>of plenty, granting every wish.<BR>	 6. Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 7. The earth.<BR>8. The holy basil.<BR>	 9. Jasmine, of several sorts.<BR>	 n. (-भि)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2.<BR>Sulphur.<BR>	 3. Fragrance.<BR> E. सु well, excellently, रभ् to begin, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिका
सुरभिका f. (-का) A sort of plantain. “चांँपाकला” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिगन्धि|सुरभिगन्धिः
सुरभिगन्धि mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि) Fragrant, sweet-smelling.<BR> E. सुरभि fragrant,<BR>गन्ध smell, इ substituted for the final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभित
सुरभित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Perfumed, rendered fragrant.<BR> E. सुरभि, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभित्वच्
सुरभित्वच् n. (-त्वक्) Large cardamoms.<BR> E. सुरभि fragrant, त्वच् bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिपत्रा
सुरभिपत्रा f. (-त्रा) The rose-apple, (Eugenia jambu.)<BR> E. सुरभि fragrant,<BR>पत्रा leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिवल्कल|सुरभिवल्कलं
सुरभिवल्कल n. (-लं) The Laurus Cassia, or its bark.<BR> E. सुरभि fragrant, वल्कल bark. “दारुचिनि” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिवाण
सुरभिवाण m. (-णः) KĀMA.<BR> E. सुरभि a fragrance, (a flower,) वाण an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभिस्रवा
सुरभिस्रवा f. (-वा) The gum Olibanum tree.<BR> E. सुरभि a fragrance, स्रव<BR>what distils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभीरसा
सुरभीरसा f. (-सा) The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.) E.<BR>सुरभी fragrant, रस juice, टाप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरभूय
सुरभूय n. (-यं) The condition of a deity, deification, apotheosis.<BR> E. सुर, भूय becoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरर्षि|सुरर्षिः
सुरर्षि m. (-र्षिः) A Ṛṣi, or sage of divine order, as NĀRADA, &c.<BR> E. सुर<BR>a deity, and ऋषि a saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरला
सुरला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. The Ganges.<BR>	 2. Another river so named.<BR> E. सुर a deity,<BR>and ला to get or have, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरलासिका
सुरलासिका f. (-का) A flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरलोक|सुरलोकः
सुरलोक m. (-कः) Svarga, the heaven of INDRA and residence of the<BR>celestials.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरवर्त्मन्
सुरवर्त्मन् n. (-र्त्मं) Heaven, sky, ether, atmosphere.<BR> E. सुर a divinity, वर्त्मन् a road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरविद्विष्
सुरविद्विष् m. (-द्विट्) An Asura, a titan.<BR> E. सुर, विद्विष् foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरवैरिन्
सुरवैरिन् m. (-री) An Asura, an infernal spirit.<BR> E. सुर a deity, वैरिन् an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरशत्रु|सुरशत्रुः
सुरशत्रु m. (-त्रुः) An Asur, an infernal spirit.<BR> E. सुर a deity, शत्रु an<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=795-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरस|सुरसं|सुरसः
सुरस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Sweet.<BR>	 2. Well-flavoured, sapid, juicy.<BR>	 3. Elegant,<BR>(as a composition.)<BR>	 m. (-सः) A plant, (Vitex trifolia.)<BR>	 nf. (-सं-सा)<BR>Holy-basil.<BR>	 f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. The mother of the Nāgas.<BR>	 2. A plant,<BR>commonly Rāsnā, a kind of Ophiorrhiza, (Ophiorrhiza mangos.)<BR>3. A sort of fennel, (Anethum sowa.)<BR>	 4. The moon-plant,<BR>(Asclepias acida.)<BR>	 5. A name of DURGĀ.<BR>	 6. A species of the<BR>Atidhriti-metre.<BR>	 n. (-सं)<BR>	 1. Gum-myrrh.<BR>	 2. Cassia bark.<BR>	 3. Fragrant<BR>grass.<BR> E. सु excellent, रस juice or flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसङ्घ|सुरसंघ
सुरसङ्घ m. (-ङ्घः) A company, a number of gods.<BR> E. सुर, सङ्घ a troop, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसद्मन्
सुरसद्मन् n. (-द्म) The heaven of INDRA.<BR> E. सुर a deity, सद्मन् a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसमिति
सुरसमिति f. (-तिः) An assemblage of the gods.<BR> E. सुर, समिति assembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसरित्
सुरसरित् f. (-रित्) The Ganges.<BR> E. सुर deity, and सरित् a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसाष्ट|सुरसाष्टः
सुरसाष्ट m. (-ष्टः) A class of eight plants, viz:--<BR>“निर्गुण्डी तुलसी ब्राह्मी वृहती कण्टकारिका ।<BR>पुनर्नवेति मुनिभिः सुरसाष्टः प्रकीर्त्तितः ॥”<BR>E. सुरसा a juicy plant, and अष्ट eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसिन्धु|सुरसिंधु|सुरसिन्धुः
सुरसिन्धु f. (-न्धुः) The river Ganges.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and सिन्धु a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरसुन्दरी|सुरसुंदरी
सुरसुन्दरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. An Apsarā or courtezan of heaven.<BR>	 2. A name of<BR>DURGĀ.<BR> E. सुर a deity, सुन्दरी a beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराकर|सुराकरः
सुराकर m. (-रः) The cocoanut-tree.<BR> E. सुरा vinous spirit or Toddy, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराग्रह|सुराग्रहः
सुराग्रह m. (-हः) A vessel for taking liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराङ्गना|सुरांगना
सुराङ्गना f. (-ना) An Apsarā or courtezan of heaven, a nymph, a sylph,<BR>a fairy.<BR> E. सुर, and अङ्गना a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराचार्य्य|सुराचार्य|सुराचार्यः|सुराचार्य्यः
सुराचार्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) VṚHASPATI, regent of JUPITER, and preceptor of the<BR>gods.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and आचार्य्य a spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराजक|सुराजकः
सुराजक m. (-कः) A plant, (Eclipta prostrata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराजा
सुराजा m. (-जा) A divinity.<BR> E. सु particle of eminence, राज् to shine, affs. टाप् and अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराजीव|सुराजीवः
सुराजीव m. (-वः) A distiller.<BR> E. सुरा, and आजीव livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराजीविन्
सुराजीविन् m. (-वी) A distiller.<BR> E. सुरा spirits, and जीविन् who lives by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरात्रि
सुरात्रि f. (-त्रिः) A fine night.<BR> E. सु, and रात्रि night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराधिप|सुराधिपः
सुराधिप m. (-पः) INDRA.<BR> E. सुर, and अधिप chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराध्वज|सुराध्वजः
सुराध्वज n. (-जं) A tavern flag or sign.<BR> E. सुरा, and ध्वज a flag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराप|सुरापः
सुराप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Drinking spirits. (-पः-पा-पं)<BR>	 1. Wise.<BR>	 2. Pleasant,<BR>agreeable.<BR>	 3. Preserving spirits.<BR> E. सुरा vinous liquor, or सुर a<BR>deity, पा to drink or cherish, with or without the prefix आङ्,<BR>and ठक् or क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापगा
सुरापगा f. (-गा) The Ganges.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and अपगा a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापाण|सुरापाणं
सुरापाण m. Plu. (-णाः) The inhabitants of eastern India.<BR> E. सुरा vinous<BR>liquor, and पान drinking; the final changed to णः see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापान|सुरापानं
सुरापान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Drinking spirituous liquors.<BR>	 2. Eating any thing to<BR>excite thirst and promote drinking.<BR> E. सुरा spirits, पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापिन्
सुरापिन् mfn. (-पी-पिणी-पि) Drinking wine.<BR> E. सुरा, पा to drink, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापीत
सुरापीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Drinking wine.<BR> E. सुरा, and पीत drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराभाग|सुराभागः
सुराभाग m. (-गः) Yeast, barm.<BR> E. सुरा spirits, and भाग a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराभाजन
सुराभाजन n. (-नं) A wine-cup.<BR> E. सुरा, and भाजन a vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरामण्ड|सुरामंड|सुरामण्डः
सुरामण्ड m. (-ण्डः) The upper part or froth of vinous liquor during<BR>fermentation, yeast, barm.<BR> E. सुरा, wine, and मण्ड scum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरारि|सुरारिः
सुरारि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. An Asura, an infernal being opposed to the gods.<BR>2. A spirit, a goblin, a Pisācha or Yakṣa.<BR>	 3. The chirp of the<BR>cricket.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and अरि an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरार्च्चन|सुरार्चन
सुरार्च्चन n. (-नं) Worshipping.<BR> E. सुरा, and अर्च्चन worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरार्ह|सुरार्हं
सुरार्ह n. (-र्हं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR> E. सुर a god, and अर्ह worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरालय|सुरालयः
सुरालय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. The sacred mountain Meru, the extremity of the<BR>world's axis, and residence of the gods.<BR>	 2. Svarga or paradise.<BR>	 3.<BR>A tavern.<BR> E. सुर a deity, or सुरा spirituous liquor, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराष्ट्र|सुराष्ट्रः
सुराष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) A country on the western side of India, Surat.<BR> E. सु<BR>good, and राष्ट्र district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराष्ट्रज|सुराष्ट्रजं|सुराष्ट्रजः
सुराष्ट्रज nf. (-जं-जा) A fragrant earth.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. A sort of bean, a<BR>black variety of the Phaseolus Mungo.<BR>	 2. A kind of poison. E.<BR>सुराष्ट्र Surat, ज born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरासन्धान
सुरासन्धान n. (-नं) The distilling of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरासव|सुरासवः
सुरासव n. (-वं) Spirituous liquor, the produce of rapid distillation. E.<BR>सुरा, आसव spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराह्व|सुराह्वः
सुराह्व n. (-ह्वं) A kind of Pine, (Pinus Devadaru.)<BR> E. सुर a deity, and<BR>आह्व appellation; being generally called the tree or timber of the<BR>gods, or देवद्रु, देवदारु; also सुराह्वय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरुङ्ग|सुरुङ्गः
सुरुङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गा) A hole made<BR>under ground or through the walls of a building, for military or<BR>felonious purposes; a mine, a breach, &c.<BR> E. सु well, रञ्ज् to be<BR>intent on, aff. अच्, and उ substituted for the radical vowel; or<BR>सु + रुज्-अङ्गच्-पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरुङ्गाहि|सुरुङ्गाहिः
सुरुङ्गाहि m. (-हिः) A housebreaker.<BR> E. सुरुङ्गा a hole in the wall, and अहि a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरुज
सुरुज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Sick, unwell.<BR> E. सु much, रुज sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरूढ
सुरूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Prominent, standing well up or out.<BR> E. सु, रूढ ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरूप|सुरूपं|सुरूपः
सुरूप mfn. (-पः-पा or -पी-पं)<BR>	 1. Handsome, well-formed.<BR>	 2. Wise, learned.<BR>E. सु excellent, and रुप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरूहक|सुरूहकः
सुरूहक m. (-कः) A horse of the colour of an ass.<BR> E. सु well, रुह् to mount,<BR>क्वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेज्य|सुरेज्यः
सुरेज्य m. (-ज्यः) VṚHASPATI, teacher of the gods.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and इज्य preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेन्द्र|सुरेन्द्रः
सुरेन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A name of INDRA.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and इन्द्र chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेन्द्रजित्
सुरेन्द्रजित् m. (-जित्) GARUḌA.<BR> E. सुरेन्द्र INDRA, and जित victor; having<BR>beaten off that deity, when pursued by him to recover the nectar<BR>which GARUḌA had stolen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेन्द्रलोक
सुरेन्द्रलोक m. (-कः) The heaven of INDRA.<BR> E. सुरेन्द्र, and लोक a region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेभ|सुरेभं|सुरेभः
सुरेभ n. (-भं) Tin.<BR> E. सु well, रेभ् to sound, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेवट|सुरेवटः
सुरेवट m. (-टः) A sort of betel-nut tree, (Areca gracilis or triandra.)<BR> E. सु + रेव्-अटन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेश्वर|सुरेश्वरः
सुरेश्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA, or a personification of him, especially as one of<BR>the eleven Rudras.<BR>	 2. INDRA.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. The Ganges of heaven.<BR>	 2.<BR>A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and ईश्वर lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरेष्ट|सुरेष्टः
सुरेष्ट m. (-ष्टः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Sesbana grandiflora.)<BR>	 2. The Sāl tree.<BR>	 3. A<BR>kind Punnāg or Rottleria.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा) The moon-plant, (Asclepias<BR>acida.)<BR> E. सुर a deity, and इष्ट wished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरै
सुरै mf. (-राः) An opulent person.<BR> E. सु very, रै wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरोत्तम|सुरोत्तमः
सुरोत्तम m. (-मः) The sun.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरोत्तर|सुरोत्तरः
सुरोत्तर m. (-रः) Sandal-wood.<BR> E. सुर a deity, and उत्तर excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरोद|सुरोदः
सुरोद m. (-दः) The sea of spirituous liquor.<BR> E. सरा wine, and उद water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलक्षण
सुलक्षण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Ascertaining, determining.<BR>	 2. A good mark or charac-<BR>teristic.<BR>	 f. (-णा) One of DURGĀ'S female companions. Adj. Having<BR>beautiful or auspicious marks.<BR> E. सु good, लक्षण a mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलक्षित
सुलक्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-determined or ascertained.<BR> E. सु, लक्षित marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलभ|सुलभः
सुलभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं)<BR>	 1. Easy, feasible, attainable, of easy acquisition or<BR>attainment, not difficult to be obtained or effected.<BR>	 2. Suitable,<BR>natural to.<BR> E. सु ready, लभ acquiring; opposed to दुर्लभ or difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुललित
सुललित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sporting gracefully.<BR>	 2. Pleased, happy.<BR>	 n.<BR>Adv. (-तं) Delightedly, easily.<BR> E. सु, and ललित sported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलोचन|सुलोचनः
सुलोचन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Fine-eyed.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A deer.<BR>	 2. DURYODHANA.<BR>f. (-ना) A handsome woman.<BR> E. सु excellent, and लोचन an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलोहक|सुलोहकं
सुलोहक n. (-कं) Brass.<BR> E. सु good, लोह iron, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुलोहित
सुलोहित mfn. (-तः-ता or -हिणी-तं) Very red.<BR>	 f. (-ता) One of the seven<BR>tongues of AGNI or fire.<BR> E. सु very, लोहित red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवचन|सुवचनं
सुवचन n. (-नं) Eloquence, speaking well or elegantly.<BR> E. सु good, वचन speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवचस्
सुवचस् mfn. (-चाः-चाः-चः) Speaking much, and eloquently or well.<BR> E. सु<BR>good, वचस् speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवन|सुवनः
सुवन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. The moon.<BR> E. षु to produce, Unādi aff. क्युन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्च्चक|सुवर्चक|सुवर्चकः|सुवर्च्चकः
सुवर्च्चक mf. (-कः-र्च्चका or र्च्चिका) Natron,<BR> E. सु well, वर्च्च् to shine, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्च्चला|सुवर्चला
सुवर्च्चला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A wife of the sun.<BR>	 2. Linseed, (Linum utilatissimum.)<BR>m. (-लः) A country so named.<BR> E. सु well, वर्च्च् to shine, कलच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्ण|सुवर्णं|सुवर्णः|सुवर्ण्ण
सुवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Of a good tribe or caste.<BR>	 2. Brilliant, bright.<BR>3. Of a good colour.<BR>	 4. Praiseworthy.<BR>	 n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. A sort<BR>of Sandal-wood.<BR>	 3. A kind of red chalk or ochre.<BR>	 4. Wealth,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">Page797-a+ 60</a>]<BR>property.<BR>	 5. A weight of gold equal to sixteen Māshas, or<BR>about 175 grains troy.<BR>	 m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A sort of sacrifice.<BR>	 f. (-र्णा)<BR>	 1. Aloe-wood, the black kind.<BR>	 2.<BR>Turmeric.<BR>	 3. A bitter gourd. (Colocynth.)<BR>	 4. Sida, (Cordifolia, &c.)<BR>E. सु excellent, वर्ण tribe or colour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=796-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णक|सुवर्णकं|सुवर्णकः
सुवर्णक m. (-कः) A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Lead.<BR>	 2. Brass, bell-<BR>metal.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णकदली
सुवर्णकदली f. (-ली) A sort of plantain-tree bearing a bright yellow fruit.<BR>E. सुवर्ण gold, and कदली the plantain. “चापाकला” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णकर्त्तृ|सुवर्णकर्तृ
सुवर्णकर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) A goldsmith.<BR> E. सवर्ण, and कर्त्तृ who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णकार|सुवर्णकारः
सुवर्णकार m. (-रः) A goldsmith.<BR> E. सुवर्ण gold, and कार a workman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णकृत्
सुवर्णकृत् m. (-कृत्) A goldsmith.<BR> E. सुवर्ण gold, कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णगणित
सुवर्णगणित n. (-तं) (In arithmetic,) Medial allegation.<BR> E. सुवर्ण, गणित<BR>calculation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णगैरिक|सुवर्णगैरिकं
सुवर्णगैरिक n. (-कं) A variety of red chalk, a sort of ochre.<BR> E. सुवर्ण gold, गैरिक red chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णचौर
सुवर्णचौर m. (-रः) A stealer of gold.<BR> E. सुवर्ण gold, and चौर thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णपुष्पित
सुवर्णपुष्पित Adj. Abounding in gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णबिन्दु|सुवर्णबिन्दुः|सुवर्ण्णबिन्दु
सुवर्णबिन्दु m. (-न्दुः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सुवर्ण gold, and विन्दु, a dot or spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णयूथी
सुवर्णयूथी f. (-थी) Yellow jasmine.<BR> E. सुवर्ण gold, and यूथी jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णवत्|सुवर्णवन्त्
सुवर्णवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Golden, having or being of gold.<BR>	 2.<BR>Beautiful, handsome. Ind. (-वत्) Like gold.<BR> E. सुवर्ण, and मतुप् or वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णवर्णा
सुवर्णवर्णा f. (-र्णा) Turmeric.<BR> E. सुवर्ण gold, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णसिद्ध|सुवर्णसिद्धः
सुवर्णसिद्ध m. (-द्धः) An adept who has acquired gold by magical means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णस्तेय
सुवर्णस्तेय n. (-यं) Stealing gold.<BR> E. सुवर्ण, and स्तेय theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवर्णाख्य|सुवर्णाख्यः
सुवर्णाख्य m. (-ख्यः) A flower, (Mesua ferrea.)<BR> E. सुवर्ण gold, and आख्या<BR>appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवल्लि|सुवल्लिः
सुवल्लि f. (-ल्लिः-ल्ली) A shrub, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR> E. सु excellent,<BR>and वल्लि a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवस्
सुवस् mfn. (-वः) What covers or clothes well.<BR> E. सु, वस् to clothe, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवसन्त|सुवसन्तः
सुवसन्त m. (-न्तः) The day of full-moon in the month of Chaitra, a<BR>festival in honour of KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. सु well, वसन्त spring; being in<BR>March-April.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवसन्तक|सुवसन्तकः
सुवसन्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A large creeper, (Cærtnera racemosa.)<BR>	 2. A festival<BR>in honour of KĀMA-DEVA in the month of Chaitra.<BR> E. सु excellent,<BR>वसन्त the spring, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवह|सुवहः
सुवह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं)<BR>	 1. Bearing or conveying well or pleasantly.<BR>	 2.<BR>Pleasant of burden, to be borne with pleasure.<BR>	 3. Patient,<BR>enduring.<BR>	 f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. A flower, (Nyctanthes tristis.)<BR>	 2. A shrub,<BR>(Mimosa octandra.)<BR>	 3. Rāsnā, conjectured to be the ichneumon<BR>plant, (Ophiorrhyza mangos.)<BR>	 4. A scandent shrub, (Cissus<BR>pedata.)<BR>	 5. The gum Olibanum tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR>	 6. A<BR>Vinā, or lute.<BR>	 7. A medicinal plant, commonly Teori, (Convolvu-<BR>lus turpethum.)<BR> E. सु well, much, or pleasantly, and वह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवास|सुवासः
सुवास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A pleasant or reputable dwelling.<BR>	 2. An agreeable<BR>perfume.<BR> E. सु good, and वास abode, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवासिन्
सुवासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Dwelling in a comfortable or respectable<BR>abode.<BR>	 f. (-सिनी)<BR>	 1. A woman married or unmarried, residing in<BR>her father's house.<BR>	 2. A term of courtesy for a respectable woman<BR>whose husband is alive.<BR> E. सु well, वास abode, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविक्रम
सुविक्रम m. (-मः) Prowess, valour.<BR> E. सु, and विक्रम power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविक्रान्त|सुविक्रांत|सुविक्रान्तः
सुविक्रान्त m. (-न्तः) A hero.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं) Heroism, prowess.<BR> E. सु, and विक्रान्त valiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविचक्षण
सुविचक्षण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Very clever.<BR> E. सु, and विचक्षण intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविचार
सुविचार m. (-रः) Deliberate or due consideration.<BR> E. सु, विचार consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविचारित
सुविचारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-weighed, deliberately considered.<BR> E. सु,<BR>and विचारित considered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविद्
सुविद् m. (-विद्) A Paṇḍit, a learned man.<BR>	 f. (-विद्) A shrewd or clever<BR>woman.<BR> E. सु, well, विद् to know, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविद|सुविदः
सुविद m. (-दः) An attendant on the women's apartments.<BR> E. सु well,<BR>विद् to know, aff. क; also सौविद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविदत्
सुविदत् m. (-दत्) A king.<BR> E. सुविद् a Paṇḍit, अत् to associate with, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविदत्र
सुविदत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Related, of kin, a kinsman, &c.<BR> E. सु well, विद्<BR>to know, कत्रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविदल्ल|सुविदल्लं|सुविदल्लः
सुविदल्ल n. (-ल्लं) A harem, a seraglio.<BR>	 m. (-ल्लः) An attendant to a harem.<BR>f. (-ल्ला) A married woman.<BR> E. सुविदत् a king, ला to be or have, aff.<BR>ड, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविदित
सुविदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-known or understood.<BR> E. सु well, विदित<BR>known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविध
सुविध mfn. (-धः-धा-धं) Of a good kind, in a good or easy way.<BR> E. सु, विध kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविधि|सुविधिः
सुविधि m. (-धिः) The ninth Jaina deified teacher of the present age. E.<BR>सु good, and विधि a precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविनीत
सुविनीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well trained, properly behaved.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A<BR>tractable cow.<BR> E. सु exceeding, and विनात well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविलय
सुविलय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Easily fusible, liquefying.<BR> E. सु and वि before<BR>ली to melt, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविश्वस्त
सुविश्वस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Trusty, confidential.<BR> E. सु, and विश्वस्त trusted in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविस्तर
सुविस्तर n. Adv. (-रं) Fully, at length.<BR> E. सु, and विस्तर expansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविस्तीर्ण
सुविस्तीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Well-spread or laid out.<BR>	 2. Very broad. E.<BR>सु, and विस्तीर्ण spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुविहित
सुविहित f. (-ता) Adj.<BR>	 1. Well-placed.<BR>	 2. Well-furnished, well-supplied.<BR>3. Well-done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवीज|सुवीजः
सुवीज f. (-जा) Adj. Having good seed.<BR>	 m. (-जः) The poppy.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Good seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवीरक|सुवीरकं
सुवीरक n. (-कं) A collyrium, prepared from the Amomum anthorhizon.<BR>E. सु well, वीर power, efficacy, and कन् added, or ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवीराम्ल|सुवीराम्लं
सुवीराम्ल n. (-म्लं) Sour rice-gruel.<BR> E. सु very, वीर essence, अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवीर्य्य|सुवीर्य|सुवीर्य्यं
सुवीर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Great vigour.<BR>	 2. The fruit of the jujube.<BR>	 f. (-र्य्या)<BR>Wild-cotton.<BR> E. सु good, and वीर्य्य essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवृत्त|सुवृत्तः
सुवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं)<BR>	 1. Virtuous, good.<BR>	 2. Well or handsomely<BR>round.<BR>	 m. (-त्तः) A kind of esculent root.<BR>	 f. (-त्ता) Grape.<BR> E. सु, and<BR>वृत्त practised, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवेल|सुवेलः
सुवेल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Bowed, bent, stooping.<BR>	 2. Tamed, humble,<BR>quiet.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A mountain; also called Trikuta.<BR> E. सु well, and<BR>वेल् to move or shake, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवेश|सुवेशः
सुवेश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Well-dressed.<BR> E. सु, and वेश attire; also सुवेष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुवेषिन्
सुवेषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Well-dressed, ornamented, decorated.<BR> E. सु,<BR>excellent, वेश ornament, decoration, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुव्यक्त
सुव्यक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Plain, manifest.<BR>	 n. Adv. (-क्तं) Evidently, clearly.<BR>E. सु, and व्यक्त manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुव्यस्त
सुव्यस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Dispersed.<BR> E. सु, and व्यस्त scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुव्रत|सुव्रतः
सुव्रत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Virtuous, strict, rigidly observing any religious<BR>vow or obligation.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The twentieth Jina of the present<BR>age; also named Munisuvrata.<BR>	 2. One of the Jainas of the future<BR>era.<BR>	 3. The religious student.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The mother of the fifteenth<BR>Jaina of the present age.<BR>	 2. A cow easily milked, one of a trac-<BR>table and gentle disposition.<BR>	 3. A virtuous wife.<BR> E. सु well, good,<BR>व्रत a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशंस
सुशंस f. (-सा) Adj. Well-spoken, praiseworthy, glorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशक
सुशक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Easily made or done.<BR> E. सु, and शक able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशर्म्मन्|सुशर्मन्
सुशर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Exquisitely happy.<BR>	 m. (-र्म्मा) The name of a<BR>prince.<BR> E. सु exceeding, शर्म्मन् pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशल्य|सुशल्यः
सुशल्य m. (-ल्यः) Khadira, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशवी
सुशवी f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A kind of gourd, (Momordica charantia.) “कारवेल्ल”.<BR>	 2.<BR>A sort of a spice, (Nigella Indica.) “कृष्णजीरक”.<BR> E. सु well, शव् to<BR>go, affs. अच् and ङीष्; also सुषवी, सुसवी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशासित
सुशासित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-governed.<BR> E. सु and शासित governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशिक्षित
सुशिक्षित f. (-ता) Well-disciplined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशिख|सुशिखः
सुशिख m. (-खः) AGNI or fire.<BR>	 f. (-खा)<BR>	 1. A peacock's crest.<BR>	 2. A cock's<BR>comb.<BR> E. सु handsome, and शिखा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशिरस्
सुशिरस् mfn. (-राः-राः-रः) Having a fine head.<BR> E. सु, and शिरस् head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीत|सुशीतं|सुशीतः
सुशीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Very cold or cooling.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A yellow fragrant<BR>sort of Sandal-wood.<BR> E. सु very, शीत cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=797-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीतल|सुशीतलं
सुशीतल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Very cold or cooling, frigid, freezing.<BR>	 n. (-लं) A<BR>fragrant sort of grass; also कुत्तृण.<BR> E. सु very, शीतल cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीम|सुशीमः
सुशीम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Cold, frigid.<BR>	 m. (-मः) Cold, coldness.<BR> E. सु much,<BR>श्यै to go, aff. मक; more usually read सुषीम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशील|सुशीलः
सुशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Well-disposed, of good temper or disposition.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ला)<BR>	 1. The wife of YAMA.<BR>	 2. Name of one of KṚṢṆA'S eight<BR>favourite wives.<BR> E. सु well, and शील nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीलता
सुशीलता f. (-ता) Natural amiability, excellence of temper or disposition.<BR>E. तल् added to the last; also सुशीलत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुशीविका
सुशीविका f. (-का) A sort of yam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्रुत|सुश्रुतः
सुश्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well-heard.<BR>	 2. Versed in the Vedas.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>Name of the author of a system of medicine, and son of VISHWĀ-<BR>MITRA. His work, named after him, together with that of CHARAKA,<BR>is regarded as the oldest medical authority in India.<BR> E. सु well, श्रुत<BR>heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्लिष्ट
सुश्लिष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Closely united or adhering to.<BR>	 2. Well fitted.<BR> E. सु, श्लिष्ट united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्लेष|सुश्लेषः
सुश्लेष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. Close or intimate union.<BR>	 2. A close embrace.<BR> E. सु, and<BR>श्लेष embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषम|सुषमः
सुषम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Beautiful, handsome, pleasing.<BR>	 2. Same, even,<BR>all.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Exquisite beauty.<BR>	 2. Great refulgence.<BR>	 3. A period<BR>of time peculiar to the Jainas, the second division of a large<BR>period, containing six such portions, and that in which steady<BR>happiness is enjoyed by mankind: (the word however more usually<BR>occurs written सुखमा, as derived from सुख pleasure.)<BR> E. सु handsome,<BR>सम even, all, and the स changed after this particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषवी
सुषवी f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. A sort of gourd, (Momordica charantia.)<BR>	 2. Black<BR>cumin-seed, generally confounded with Kalonji, (Nigella Indica.)<BR>3. Cumin-seed.<BR> E. सु well, षु to send or direct, aff. अच्, fem. aff.<BR>ङीष्; also सुशवी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषामन्
सुषामन् mfn. (-मा-मा-म) Sweetly or kindly spoken.<BR> E. सु, सामन् calming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषि|सुषिः
सुषि f. (-षिः)<BR>	 1. A hole.<BR>	 2. Drying.<BR>	 3. A tube or pipe.<BR> E. शुष्-इन्-पृषो०: स<BR>substituted for श; see शुषिर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषिर|सुषिरं
सुषिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Perforated, pierced.<BR>	 2. Having apertures or<BR>holes.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A hole, an opening.<BR>	 2. A wind-instrument.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>Nalukā, a perfume.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Fire.<BR> E. स substituted for श: see शुषिर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषीम|सुषीमः
सुषीम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Cold, frigid.<BR>	 2. Pleasant, agreeable.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>1. Cold.<BR>	 2. A sort of snake.<BR>	 3. The moon-gem.<BR> E. सु well, सीमा a<BR>limit; also read सुषिम and सुशीम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुप्त|सुषुप्तं
सुषुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Fast asleep.<BR> E. सु well, ष्वप् to sleep, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषिप्ति
सुषिप्ति f. (-प्तिः)<BR>	 1. Deep sleep, profound repose, entire insensibility.<BR>	 2.<BR>Spiritual ignorance.<BR> E. सु well, ष्वप् to sleep, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुप्सु
सुषुप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Wishing to sleep.<BR> E. ष्वप् to sleep, desid, v., उ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषुम्णा
सुषुम्णा f. (-म्णा) A particular artery of the body lying between the<BR>vessels called IDĀ and PINGALĀ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषेण|सुषेणः
सुषेण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A fruit, (Carissa Carondas) “करम्चा” 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3.<BR>The physician of the monkey chief SUGRĪVA.<BR>	 4. A cane or reed, the<BR>ratan.<BR>	 f. (-णी) A plant, commonly Teori, (Convolvolus turpethum.)<BR>E. सु excellent, सेना a host or cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुषेणिका
सुषेणिका f. (-का) Black Teori, (Convolvulus turpethum.)<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुष्ठु
सुष्ठु Ind.<BR>	 1. Much, very much.<BR>	 2. Well, excellently.<BR>	 3. Truly.<BR> E. सु<BR>well, स्था to stay, aff. कु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुश्म
सुश्म n. (-श्मं) A rope, a cord.<BR> E. सु-मक्-सुक् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंगृहीत|सुसङ्गृहीत
सुसंगृहीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well-kept or preserved.<BR>	 2. Well-abridged.<BR> E. सु, संगृहीत taken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंस्कृत|सुसंस्कृतं
सुसंस्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Dressed, seasoned, prepared with condi-<BR>ments, sauces, &c.<BR>	 2. Entirely perfected, very highly finished,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सु well, संकृत made perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसंस्थित
सुसंस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Well-situated or placed.<BR>	 2. Being or doing<BR>well.<BR>	 3. Circumscribed, well-defined.<BR> E. सु and सम् before स्था to<BR>stay, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसहत
सुसहत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-compacted or united, well-kuit.<BR> E. सु, and संहत collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसन्नत
सुसन्नत f. (-ता) Adj. Well-directed, (as an arrow.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसवी
सुसवी f. (-वी) A sort of pungent seed, either a black species of cumin-<BR>seed or the Nigella Indica: see सुषवी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसम्पद्|सुसंपद्
सुसम्पद् f. (-म्पद्-म्पत्) Fortune, prosperity.<BR> E. सु good, सम्पद् prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसह|सुसहः
सुसह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Easily borne or suffered.<BR>	 2. Bearing or enduring<BR>well.<BR> E. सु well, and सह suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसार|सुसारः
सुसार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The red sort of Khayer, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>	 2. Good<BR>essence or substance.<BR>	 3. Competence.<BR> E. सु good, सार essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसारवत्|सुसारवन्त्
सुसारवत् n. (-वत्) Crystal.<BR> E. सु excellent, सार essence, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसीमा
सुसीमा f. (-मा) The mother of the sixth Jaina teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुसेवित
सुसेवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Assiduously served or attended upon 2.<BR>Much addicted to.<BR> E. सु and सेवित served.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थ|सुस्थः
सुस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Well, healthy.<BR>	 2. Happy, faring or living<BR>well.<BR> E. सु well, and स्थ being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थता
सुस्थता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Health.<BR>	 2. Welfare, happiness.<BR> E. सुस्थ being well, तल aff. of condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थयत्
सुस्थयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Setting at rest, appeasing, consoling. E.<BR>सुस्थ being well, used as a verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थित
सुस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Living well or happily.<BR>	 2. Being well,<BR>in health or condition.<BR> E. सु, and स्थित who or what stays in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थिति|सुस्थितिः
सुस्थिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Well-being, welfare.<BR>	 2. Health, convalescence.<BR> E. सु,<BR>and स्थिति staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्थिर|सुस्थिरः
सुस्थिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Firm, steady, stable.<BR>	 2. Resolute.<BR>	 3. Cool.<BR> E. सु well, स्थिर steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्ना
सुस्ना m. (-स्ना) A sort of pease. “खेंँसारी”.<BR> E. सु + स्नै-क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्नात|सुस्नातः
सुस्नात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-bathed.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A student, who has<BR>performed his ablutions preparatory or subsequent to a sacrifice.<BR>E. सु auspiciously, स्नात bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्मित
सुस्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Smiling.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A woman with a pleasing or<BR>smiling countenance.<BR> E. सु well, pleasant, and स्मित smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्मूर्षमाण
सुस्मूर्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Wishing or trying to recollect.<BR> E. स्मृ to<BR>remember, desid. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुस्वप्न
सुस्वप्न n. (-प्नं) A lucky or good dream.<BR> E. सु, and स्वप्न a dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहसानन
सुहसानन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Having a cheerful or smiling face.<BR> E. सु, हस्<BR>laughing, आनन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहस्ति
सुहस्ति m. (-स्तिः) One of the ten persons called Purbadharas by the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहित|सुहितः
सुहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Satiated, satisfied.<BR>	 2. Fit, right, suitable.<BR>	 3.<BR>Kindly, friendly.<BR>	 4. Salutary, beneficial.<BR>	 f. (-ता) One of the seven<BR>tongues of AGNI or fire.<BR> E. सु well, हित placed, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृत्तम
सुहृत्तम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Friendly, cordial, kind.<BR> E. सुहृत् a friend, तमप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृत्ता
सुहृत्ता f. (-त्ता) Friendship, affection.<BR> E. सुहृत्, and तल् aff.; also सुहृत्व ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृद्
सुहृद् m. (-हृद् or हृत्)<BR>	 1. A friend.<BR>	 2. An ally.<BR> E. सु good, kind, हृद् heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृदय|सुहृदयः
सुहृदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Good hearted.<BR> E. सु excellent, हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृद्बल
सुहृद्बल n. (-लं) The army of an ally.<BR> E. सुहृद्, बल an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृद्भेद
सुहृद्भेद m. (-दः) The separation of friends.<BR> E. सुहृद्, and भेद division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुहृद्वाक्य
सुहृद्वाक्य n. (-क्यं) A friend's advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सू
सू f. (-सूः)<BR>	 1. Sending ordering, dispatching.<BR>	 2. Bearing, parturition.<BR>3. Birth.<BR>	 4. A mother.<BR> E. षू to bear or send, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक|सूकः
सूक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Air, wind.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. A lotus.<BR> E. षू to bring forth,<BR>क्विप् affix, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुकर|सुकरः
सुकर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A hog.<BR>	 2. A potter.<BR>	 3. A sort of deer, (the hog-deer.)<BR>f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A sort of moss, (Lycopodium imbricatum.)<BR>	 2. A sow.<BR>E. स substituted for श; see शूकर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्त|सूक्तं
सूक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Well or properly said.<BR>	 n. (-क्तं)<BR>	 1. A hymn in the<BR>Rig-Veda.<BR>	 2. A good or wise saying.<BR>	 f. (-क्ता) The Shārika or<BR>Mainā.<BR> E. सु well, उक्त spoken, (by which.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ति|सूक्तिः
सूक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Friendly speech.<BR>	 2. Correct exposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्षण
सूक्षण n. (-णं) Disrespect.<BR> E. सूर्क्ष् to disrespect, aff. ल्युट्; the र rejected; also सूर्क्षण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्म|सूक्ष्मं|सूक्ष्मः
सूक्ष्म mfn. (-क्ष्मः-क्ष्मा-क्ष्मं)<BR>	 1. Little, small.<BR>	 2. Minute, atomic.<BR>	 3. Fine,<BR>delicate.<BR>	 4. Ingenious, subtle.<BR>	 5. Sharp, acute.<BR>	 6. Crafty,<BR>artful.<BR>	 7. Exact, precise, accurate.<BR>	 8. Deteriorated, declined.<BR>m. (-क्ष्मः)<BR>	 1. An atom.<BR>	 2. Clearing-nut plant, (Strychnos pota-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">Page799-a+ 60</a>]<BR>torum.)<BR>	 n. (-क्ष्मं)<BR>	 1. The Supreme Soul, the subtle and invisible<BR>spirit that pervades all existence.<BR>	 2. Fraud, cheating.<BR>	 3. Fine<BR>thread, &c.<BR>	 4. A figure of rhetoric, the delicate or subtle<BR>expression of act or intention.<BR>	 5. Subtlety, ingenuity, craft.<BR>	 6.<BR>Minuteness.<BR>	 7. One of the three kinds of power attainable by an<BR>ascetic.<BR>	 f. (-क्ष्मा)<BR>	 1. A kind of jasmine, (Jasminum auriculatum.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR>	 3. A perfume, consisting of a substance in<BR>small grains: see Elabāluka.<BR> E. सूच् to inform or make known,<BR>मन् Unādi aff., सुक् च नेट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=798-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मतण्डुल|सूक्ष्मतंडुल|सूक्ष्मतण्डुलः
सूक्ष्मतण्डुल m. (-लः) The poppy. “खस्खस्”.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Long-pepper.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sort of grass, (Andropogon muricatum.)<BR> E. सूक्ष्म fine, तण्डुल grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मत्व
सूक्ष्मत्व n. (-त्वं) Fineness, subtilty.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म, त्व aff.; also with तल्, सूक्ष्मता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मदर्शिता
सूक्ष्मदर्शिता f. (-ता) Quick-sightedness, wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मदर्शिन्
सूक्ष्मदर्शिन् mfn. (-र्शी-र्शिनी-र्शि)<BR>	 1. Acute, quick, sharp-sighted, intelligent.<BR>2. Acute discernment.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म small, fine, and दर्शिन् who sees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मदारु
सूक्ष्मदारु m. (-रुः) A thin plank of wood.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म fine, small, दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मपत्र|सूक्ष्मपत्रः
सूक्ष्मपत्र m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. Coriander-seed.<BR>	 2. A wild-kind of cumin.<BR>	 3. A sort<BR>of mustard.<BR>	 4. A red sort of sugar-cane.<BR>	 5. The gum Arabic tree,<BR>(Mimosa Arabica.)<BR> E. सूक्ष्म fine, small, and पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मपर्णी
सूक्ष्मपर्णी f. (-र्णी) Rāmadūti, a kind of basil.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म small, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मफला
सूक्ष्मफला f. (-ला) A fruit, (Flacourtia cataphracta.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मबुद्धि|सूक्ष्मबुद्धिः
सूक्ष्मबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि)<BR>	 1. Sharp, shrewd, intelligent, acute.<BR>	 f. (-द्धिः)<BR>Mental acumen.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्ममक्षिका
सूक्ष्ममक्षिका f. (-का) A musquito, a gnat.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म small, मक्षिका a fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्ममान
सूक्ष्ममान n. (-न) Exact measurement, precise computation, as opposed<BR>to स्थूलमान or rough calculation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्षमवस्त्र
सूक्षमवस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) Fine cloth.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म fine, वस्त्र cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मशरीर
सूक्ष्मशरीर n. (-रं) The subtle body invested by and the archetype of the<BR>grosser and perceptible frame.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म, and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मशर्करा
सूक्ष्मशर्करा f. (-रा) Small gravel, sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मशालि|सूक्ष्मशालिः
सूक्ष्मशालि m. (-लिः) A small and fine kind of rice.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म small and शालि rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मषट्चरण|सूक्ष्मषट्चरणः
सूक्ष्मषट्चरण m. (-णः) A sort of tick or louse breeding at the roots of<BR>the eyelashes.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म small, and षट्चरण an insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मीकृत
सूक्ष्मीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made thin or minute.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म, कृत made, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूक्ष्मीभूत
सूक्ष्मीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Become fine, subtle, minute.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म, भूत<BR>become, and च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्
सूच् r. 10th cl. (सूचयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To give information.<BR>	 2. To espy.<BR>	 3. To<BR>trace out, to ascertain.<BR>	 4. To indicate by gesture.<BR>	 5. To betray,<BR>to reveal, to inform against.<BR>	 6. To point out, to suggest.<BR>	 7. To<BR>pierce. With अभि, To indicate. With सम्, To foreshadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच|सूचः
सूच m. (-चः) A pointed shoot or blade of the Kuśa grass.<BR>	 f. (-ची) A<BR>needle: see सूचि.<BR>	 f. (-चा)<BR>	 1. Gesticulation.<BR>	 2. Sight, seeing.<BR>	 3. Pier-<BR>cing.<BR> E. सिव् to sew, चट् Unādi aff., and ऊ substituted for the<BR>final; or सूच् to make known, affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचक|सूचकः
सूचक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A spy, an informer.<BR>	 2. A teacher, an instructor.<BR>	 3.<BR>A needle, a piercer, any instrument for perforating.<BR>	 4. A dog.<BR>	 5.<BR>A crow.<BR>	 6. A cat.<BR>	 7. A scoundrel, a villain.<BR>	 8. The manager or<BR>chief actor of a company.<BR>	 9. A Buddha.<BR>	 10. A Siddha.<BR>	 11. A<BR>demon, an imp or goblin.<BR>	 12. A kind of fine rice.<BR>	 f. (-चिका)<BR>	 1.<BR>Indicating, proving.<BR>	 2. Betraying, informing.<BR> E. सूच् to make<BR>known, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचकवाक्य
सूचकवाक्य n. (-क्यं) The information given by a spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचन|सूचनं
सूचन nf. (-नं-ना)<BR>	 1. Information, informing.<BR>	 2. Teaching, showing,<BR>describing.<BR>	 3. Perforation.<BR>	 4. Indication.<BR>	 5. Hint.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Pier-<BR>cing.<BR>	 2. Wickedness.<BR>	 3. Gesture, gesticulation, conveying any<BR>intimation by signs.<BR>	 4. Sight, seeing.<BR> E. सूच् to make known,<BR>aff. युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचि|सूचिः
सूचि mf. (-चिः-ची)<BR>	 1. A needle.<BR>	 2. Piercing, perforating.<BR>	 3. Indication of<BR>a passion or feeling by signs, gesture, gesticulation.<BR>	 4. A mode of<BR>dancing.<BR>	 5. A mode of array, a sharp file or column.<BR>	 6. A tri-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">Page799-b+ 60</a>]<BR>angle formed by the sides of a trapezium produced to the point<BR>of meeting.<BR>	 7. A cone, a pyramid.<BR>	 8. (In astronomy,) The earth's<BR>disc in computing eclipses.<BR>	 9. An index, a catalogue.<BR>	 10. The<BR>pointed blade of Kuśa grass.<BR>	 11. The sharp point of anything.<BR>12. The point of a bud.<BR>	 13. Dramatic action.<BR> E. सूच् to make<BR>known, aff. इन्, and ङीप् optionally added; or सिव् to sew, &c.,<BR>Unādi aff. चट्: see सूच ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिक|सूचिकः
सूचिक m. (-कः) A tailor.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. An elephant's trunk.<BR>	 2. A needle.<BR>E. सूचि a needle, ठक् aff., or कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिकटाहन्याय|सूचिकटाहन्यायः
सूचिकटाहन्याय m. (-यः) The maxim of the needle and the boiler. It is<BR>used to denote that, when two matters, (one easy and another diffi-<BR>cult,) require attention, the simple one should be despatched first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिकाधर|सूचिकाधरः
सूचिकाधर m. (-रः) An elephant.<BR> E. सूचिका a trunk, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिकासुख
सूचिकासुख n. (-खं) A shell, a conch.<BR> E. सूचिका a needle, मुख a mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिखात|सूचिखातः
सूचिखात m. (-तः) An sharp pyramid or pyramidal excavation.<BR> E. सूचि,<BR>and खात a pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचित|सूचितः
सूचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Communicated, told, made known.<BR>	 2. Ascer-<BR>tained.<BR>	 3. Hinted.<BR>	 4. Pierced.<BR> E. सूच to make known, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिता
सूचिता f. (-ता) Needle-work.<BR> E. सूचि a needle, तल aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिन्
सूचिन् mfn. (-ची-चिनी-चि)<BR>	 1. Spying, informing.<BR>	 2. Piercing.<BR>	 3. Pointing.<BR>4. Informing against.<BR>	 m. (-ची) A spy, an informer: see सूचि.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नी)<BR>	 1. A needle.<BR>	 2. Night.<BR> E. सूच् to make known, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिपत्रक|सूचिपत्रकः
सूचिपत्रक m. (-कः) A kind of herb.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A paper of contents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिपुष्प|सूचिपुष्पः
सूचिपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A flower, (Pandanus odoratissimus.)<BR> E. सूचि a needle,<BR>and पुष्प a flower; also सूचीपुष्प ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिभिन्न
सूचिभिन्न Adj.<BR>	 1. Divided into needles.<BR>	 2. Bursting open at the points<BR>of the buds; also सूचीभिन्न ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिमुख|सूचिमुखः
सूचिमुख n. (-खं) The diamond.<BR>	 m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A bird.<BR>	 2. The white Kuśa<BR>grass.<BR>	 3. A particular position of the hands.<BR> E. सूचि a needle or a<BR>beak, and मुख mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिरोमन्
सूचिरोमन् m. (-मा) A hog.<BR> E. सूचि a needle, (a bristle,) रोमन् hair; also सूचीरोमन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिवत्|सूचिवन्त्
सूचिवत् m. (-वान्) GARUḌA.<BR> E. सूचि a needle, (a beak,) मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचिवदन|सूचिवदनः
सूचिवदन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The mungoose.<BR>	 2. A musquito.<BR> E. सूचि a needle,<BR>(a sharp nose or proboscis,) and वदन face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूचीभेद्य
सूचीभेद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Palpable, tangible.<BR>	 2. To be pierced, or<BR>penetrated by a needle.<BR>	 3. Gross, dense.<BR> E. सूची, भेद्य to be pierced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्य
सूच्य mfn. (-च्यः-च्या-च्यं) Informable, communicable.<BR> E. सूच् to inform, यत्<BR>aff.; also सूचनीय and सूचितव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्यग्र
सूच्यग्र n. (-ग्रं) The point of a needle.<BR> E. सूची, and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्यग्रस्थूलक|सूच्यग्रस्थूलकः
सूच्यग्रस्थूलक m. (-कः) A sort of grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.) “उलुखड”.<BR>E. सूचि a needle, अग्र a point, and स्थूलक thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूच्यास्य|सूच्यास्यः
सूच्यास्य m. (-स्यः) A rat.<BR> E. सूची a needle, and आस्य face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्
सूत् Ind. An imitative sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत|सूतः
सूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Born, engendered.<BR>	 2. Sent, dispatched.<BR>	 3. Drank.<BR>	 4.<BR>Gone, departed.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A charioteer.<BR>	 2. A carpenter.<BR>	 3. A man<BR>of a mixed race, descended from a Kṣatriya father, and mother<BR>of the sacerdotal tribe; his occupation is managing horses<BR>and driving cars.<BR>	 4. A bard, an encomiast.<BR>	 5. The sun.<BR>	 6. Name<BR>of a pupil of VYĀSA.<BR>	 mn. (-तः-तं) Quicksilver.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A woman<BR>lying-in or recently delivered.<BR> E. षू to bring forth, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतक|सूतकं|सूतकः
सूतक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Birth, production.<BR>	 2. Impurity from child-birth or<BR>miscarriage.<BR>	 mn. (-कः-कं) Quicksilver.<BR>	 f. (-का-तिका) A woman<BR>recently delivered.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतपुत्त्र
सूतपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः) A name of KARṆA.<BR> E. सूत the sun, and पुत्र son; also<BR>सूतपुत्त्रक and similar compounds, as सूततनय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूति|सूतिः
सूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Birth, production, delivery, parturition, bringing-<BR>forth.<BR>	 2. Offspring, progeny.<BR>	 3. Sewing.<BR>	 4. Source.<BR>	 5. A place<BR>where Soma-juice is extracted.<BR> E. षू to bring forth, (as young,) or<BR>सिव् to sew, क्तिच् aff.; in the letter ऊ is substituted for the finals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतिका
सूतिका f. (-का) A woman recently delivered.<BR> E. सू-क्त स्वार्थे क अत इत्त्वम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=799-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतिकागृह|सूतिकागृहं
सूतिकागृह n. (-हं) A part of a house appropriated to the women, or to<BR>a lying-in woman especially.<BR> E. सूतका or सूतिका a lying-in woman,<BR>and गृह house or room; hence also सूतकागृह n. (-हं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतिकाभवन|सूतिकाभवनं
सूतिकाभवन n. (-नं) The lying-in chamber: see the last.<BR> E. सूतिका a<BR>lying-in woman, and भवन a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतिकारोग|सूतिकारोगः
सूतिकारोग m. (-गः) Puerperal sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रिकाषष्ठी
सूत्रिकाषष्ठी f. (-ष्ठी) A particular goddess worshipped on the sixth day<BR>after child-birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतिगृह|सूतिगृहं
सूतिगृह n. (-हं) The lying-in chamber: see सूतिकागृह.<BR> E. सूति delivery,<BR>child-birth, गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतीगृह|सूतीगृहं
सूतीगृह n. (-हं) The lying-in chamber.<BR> E. सूति delivery गृह a house, the<BR>vowel made long: see सूतिकागृह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूतीमास
सूतीमास m. (-सः) The last month of pregnancy.<BR> E. सूति delivery, मास month; also सूतिमास ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूकार
सूकार n. (-रं) Snorting, roaring, any sound expressive of impatience<BR>or aversion.<BR> E. सूत् imitative sound, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्तर
सूत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Superior.<BR>	 2. Northern.<BR> E. सु very, उत्तर beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूयान
सूयान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Dexterous, clever.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Good effort or exertion.<BR>E. सु well, उत्थान exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्पर|सूत्परं
सूत्पर n. (-रं) Distilling spirits.<BR> E. सु + उत् + पृ-अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्या
सूत्या f. (-त्या)<BR>	 1. Religious bathing, ablution, preparatory or subsequent<BR>to a sacrifice.<BR>	 2. Drinking the juice of the acid Asclepias at a<BR>sacrifice.<BR> E. सू to bear, (fruit or offspring,) क्यप् aff., तुक् augment,<BR>and टाप् fem. aff.; also सुत्या ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्याशौच|सूत्याशौचं
सूत्याशौच n. (-चं) Impurity from child-birth, continuing for ten days,<BR>or if in consequence of a miscarriage, for as many days as months<BR>have passed since conception.<BR> E. सूति child-bearing, अशौच impure-<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्र|सूत्रं
सूत्र r. 10th cl. (सूत्रयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To bind, to thread, to string.<BR>	 2. To write<BR>in the form of a concise rule.<BR>	 3. To plan, to systematize.<BR>	 4. To<BR>unbind. to loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्र|सूत्रं
सूत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. A thread in general.<BR>	 2. A rule, a precept, in morals or<BR>science; a short, obscure, and technical sentence, enjoying some<BR>observance in law or religion, or intimating some rule in<BR>grammar, logic, &c.; in each case it is the fundamental and<BR>primitive part of Hindu learning, and is the form in which the<BR>works of the early and supposed inspired writers appear; the<BR>ingenuity and labour of subsequent authors having expanded and<BR>explained the original Sūtras in various commentaries and<BR>glosses.<BR>	 3. An opinion or decree, (in law.)<BR>	 4. A string, a collection<BR>of threads, as that worn by the three first classes, &c.<BR>	 5. The<BR>string or wire of a puppet.<BR>	 6. A fibre.<BR> E. षिव् to sew, ष्ट्रन् Unādi<BR>aff., and इव changed to ऊ; or सूत्र to string, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूवकण्ठ
सूवकण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>	 1. A Brāhman.<BR>	 2. A wagtail.<BR>	 3. A dove, a pigeon. E.<BR>सूव a thread, and कण्ठ throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रकर्मन्
सूत्रकर्मन् n. (-र्म) Carpentry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रकोण|सूत्रकोणः
सूत्रकोण m. (-णः) A small hour-glass-shaped drum, struck by a string<BR>and button fastened to it.<BR> E. सूत्र a string, and कोण corner; also<BR>with कन् added, सूत्रकोणक m. (-कः) । “डमरु ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रगण्डिका|सूत्रगंडिका
सूत्रगण्डिका f. (-का) A stick used in spinning the threads to be employed in weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रग्रह
सूत्रग्रह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Who holds thread, &c.<BR> E. सूत्र, ग्रह् to take, अच्<BR>aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रग्राह
सूत्रग्राह mfn. (-हः-ही-हं) Who or what takes, but does not hold thread, &c.<BR> E. सूत्र, ग्रह् to take, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रचरण
सूत्रचरण n. (-णं) Name of a class of charanas or Vedic schools that<BR>introduced various Sūtra works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रण|सूत्रणं
सूत्रण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Arranging, putting in order.<BR>	 2. Stringing.<BR>	 3. Arrang<BR>ing in aphorisms.<BR> E. सूत्र used as a verb, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रतन्तु|सूत्रतन्तुः
सूत्रतन्तु m. (-न्तुः) A thread.<BR> E. सूत्र a thread, तन्तु the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रतकुटी
सूत्रतकुटी f. (-टी) A distaff, a spindle.<BR> E. सूत्र a thread, तर्कुटी a spindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रदरिद्रता
सूत्रदरिद्रता f. (-ता) Pancity of fibres or threads.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रधर|सूत्रधरः
सूत्रधर m. (-रः) A stage-manager: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रधार|सूत्रधारः
सूत्रधार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The principal actor or manager of a company, and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">Page800-b+ 60</a>]<BR>chief interlocutor in the prologue or prelude to a drama.<BR>	 2. A<BR>carpenter.<BR>	 3. The author of a set of rules or axioms.<BR>	 4. INDRA. E.<BR>सूत्र a rule, &c., and धार who holds; also सूत्रधर and सूत्रभृत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रपिटक|सूत्रपिटकः
सूत्रपिटक m. (-कः) Name of one of the three collections of Buddhistic<BR>writings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रपुष्प|सूत्रपुष्पः
सूत्रपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) The cotton-plant.<BR> E. सूत्र thread, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रभिद्
सूत्रभिद् m. (-भिद् or -भित्) A tailor.<BR> E. सूत्र thread, भिद् who breaks or cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रमध्यभू
सूत्रमध्यभू m. (-भूः) Incense.<BR> E. सूत्र thread, मध्य amidst, and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रयन्त्र|सूत्रयंत्र|सूत्रयन्त्रं
सूत्रयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A shuttle, a thread-machine.<BR>	 2. A weaver's loom.<BR>E. सूत्र a thread, and यन्त्र a machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रला
सूत्रला f. (-ला) A spindle or distaff.<BR> E. सूत्र thread, ला to get, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रवीणा
सूत्रवीणा f. (-णा) A sort of lute.<BR> E. सूत्र a thread, and वीणा a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रवेष्टन|सूत्रवेष्टनं
सूत्रवेष्टन n. (-नं) A weaver's shuttle.<BR> E. सूत्र thread, वेष्टन surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रात्मन्
सूत्रात्मन् m. (-त्मा) The soul. Adj. Having the nature of a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रामन्
सूत्रामन् m. (-मा) INDRA.<BR> E. सु well, त्रै to preserve, मनिन् aff., and the<BR>vowel of the prefix optionally made long; also सुत्रामन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्राली
सूत्राली f. (-ली) A necklace or chain worn round the neck.<BR> E. सूत्र a<BR>thread, आली a line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रिका
सूत्रिका f. (-का) A kind of dish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रित
सूत्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Arranged, methodised.<BR>	 2. Ruled, directed in<BR>Sūtras.<BR>	 3. Strung.<BR> E. सूत्र used as a vest, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूत्रिन्
सूत्रिन् mfn. (-त्री-त्रिणी-त्रि) Having threads, rules, &c.<BR>	 m. (-त्री) A crow.<BR>E. सूत्र a thread, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूद|सूदः
सूद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A cook.<BR>	 2. Sauce, seasoning.<BR>	 3. A made dish, anything<BR>seasoned.<BR>	 4. Split pease.<BR>	 5. Mud, mire.<BR>	 6. Destroying, massacre.<BR>7. Distilling.<BR>	 8. A well, a spring.<BR>	 9. Sin, fault.<BR> E. षूद् to leak or<BR>distil, affs. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदकर्मन
सूदकर्मन n. (-र्म) Cookery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदत्त
सूदत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Well or entirely given.<BR> E. सु, दत्त given, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदन|सूदनं
सूदन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Destructive, destroyer.<BR>	 2. Dear, beloved.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>1. Destroying, killing.<BR>	 2. Assenting to, promising.<BR>	 3. Ejecting,<BR>throwing away.<BR> E. षूद् to injure or kill, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदशाला
सूदशाला f. (-ला) A kitchen.<BR> E. सूद a cook, शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदाध्यक्ष|सूदाध्यक्षः
सूदाध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) Superintendent of the kitchen.<BR> E. सूद a cook, अध्यक्ष<BR>superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूदित
सूदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Destroyed, killed.<BR> E. षूद् to destroy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदितृ
सदितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Destroyer, destroying.<BR> E. षूद्, तृन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून|सूनं|सूनः
सून mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Blown, budded, (as a flower.)<BR>	 2. Empty, vacant,<BR>(probably for शून or शून्य in this sense.)<BR>	 3. Born, produced.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-नं)<BR>	 1. Bringing forth, (as young,) parturition.<BR>	 2. A flower.<BR>	 3.<BR>A bud.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. A daughter.<BR>	 2. The uvula.<BR>	 3. A shambles,<BR>a slaughter-house.<BR>	 4. A place or utensil in a house, where,<BR>or by which, insects may be killed, as the hearth, the slab, the<BR>pestle and mortar, the broom, and the water-pot: see पञ्चसूना.<BR>5. Hurting, injuring.<BR>	 6. Inflammation of the glands of the neck.<BR>7. A zone, a girdle.<BR>	 8. A ray.<BR>	 9. A river.<BR>	 10. Mumps.<BR>	 11. The<BR>sale of flesh.<BR> E. षू to bear, &c., aff. क्त; or षु the same, न Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनरी
सूनरी f. (-री) A respectable woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनवत्
सूनवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Budding.<BR>	 2. Bearing.<BR> E. षू to bear, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनिन्
सूनिन् m. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A butcher.<BR>	 2. A hunter, one who practises the death<BR>of animals.<BR> E. सूना a slaughter-house, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनु|सूनुः
सूनु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A son.<BR>	 2. A younger brother.<BR>	 3. The sun.<BR>	 4. A<BR>daughter's son.<BR>	 5. A child, offspring.<BR>	 6. The Arka-plant.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-नुः or -नू) A daughter.<BR> E. षू to bear, (as children,) नुक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूनृत|सूनृतं
सूनृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. True and agreeable.<BR>	 2. Fortunate, auspicious.<BR>3. Dear to, beloved by.<BR>	 4. Kind, sincere, gentle.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Agreeable<BR>discourse or speech, but also true.<BR> E. सु well, नृत् to dance, (or<BR>excel,) घञ् aff., and the vowel of the prefix made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून्मद|सून्मदः
सून्मद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Mad, crazy, insane.<BR> E. सु much, उन्मद mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सून्माद|सून्मादः
सून्माद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Mad, insane.<BR> E. सु much, उन्माद madness, (whose.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=800-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूप|सूपः
सूप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Sauce, condiment.<BR>	 2. Soup, broth.<BR>	 3. A cook.<BR>	 4. A vessel.<BR>5. An arrow.<BR> E. षु to bear, प Unādi aff.; the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपकार|सूपकारः
सूपकार m. (-रः) A cook.<BR> E. सूप sauce, कार maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपत्
सूपत् Ind. Excellently,^1 well.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260701. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपधूपन|सूपधूपनं
सूपधूपन n. (-नं) Asafœtida.<BR> E. सूप sauce, सूपन perfuming; also सूपधूपक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपपर्णी
सूपपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A sort of bean, (Phaseolus trilobus.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपसदन
सूपसदन f. (-ना) Adj. Easy to be approached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपस्कर
सूपस्कर f. (-रा) Adj. Furnished with good instruments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूपाङ्ग|सूपाङ्गं
सूपाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) Asafœtida.<BR> E. सूप sauce, and अङ्ग member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूम|सूमं|सूमः
सूम mn. (-मः-मं)<BR>	 1. Sky, heaven.<BR>	 2. Milk.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR> E. षू to bring forth,<BR>मक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्
सूर् (ई) सूरी r. 4th cl. (सूर्य्यते)<BR>	 1. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 2. To be stupid or dull.<BR>	 3. To make firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर|सूरः
सूर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The father of the 17th Jaina of the present<BR>era.<BR>	 3. Paṇḍit.<BR>	 4. A hero.<BR>	 5. A king.<BR>	 6. The Soma.<BR>	 7. The Arka<BR>plant.<BR>	 f. (-री) Black mustard.<BR> E. षू to bring forth, क्रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरचक्षुस्
सूरचक्षुस् Adj. Radiant as the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरण|सूरणः
सूरण m. (-णः) An esculent root, (Arum campanulatum.)<BR> E. सूर् to hurt, aff. ल्युट्; also शूरण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरत|सूरतः
सूरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Compassionate, tender.<BR>	 2. Tranquil, calm.<BR> E. सु<BR>well. रम् to sport or rest, क्त Unādi aff., and the vowel of the prefix<BR>made long; also सुरत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरसुत|सूरसुतः
सूरसुत m. (-तः) An epithet of Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरसूत|सूरसूतः
सूरसूत m. (-तः) ARUṆA, the personification of the dawn, as the<BR>charioteer of the sun.<BR> E. सूर the sun, and सूत charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरि|सूरिः
सूरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. A Paṇḍit, a learned man.<BR>	 2. A title commonly<BR>given to Jaina teachers.<BR>	 3. KṚṢṆA.<BR>	 4. The sun.<BR>	 5. A priest.<BR>6. A worshipper.<BR> E. षू to bear, Unādi aff. क्रिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरिन्
सूरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Wise, learned.<BR>	 m. (-री) A Paṇḍit, a scholar,<BR>a learned man.<BR> E. सूर् to injure, to dispel, (ignorance, &c.) णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूरी
सूरी f. (-री) Name of the wife of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्
सूर्क्ष् r. 1st cl. (सूर्क्षति) To disregard; more properly षूर्क्ष्; also सूर्क्ष्य्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्षण|सूर्क्षणं
सूर्क्षण n. (-णं) Disrespect, contumely, contempt.<BR> E. षूर्क्ष् to treat with<BR>disrespect, ल्युट् aff.; also सूर्क्ष्यण and सूक्षण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्य्
सूर्क्ष्य् r. 1st cl. (सूर्क्ष्यति)<BR>	 1. To envy, to be impatient of another's success.<BR>2. To be intolerant; also षूर्क्ष्य् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्क्ष्य|सूर्क्ष्यः
सूर्क्ष्य m. (-र्क्ष्यः) A kind of bean, (Phaseolus radiatus.)<BR> E. सूर्क्ष् to disrespect, यत् aff.; also सूर्क्ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्ण
सूर्ण f. (-र्णा) Adj. Hurt, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्प्प|सूर्प|सूर्पः
सूर्प्प mn. (-र्प्पः-र्प्पं)<BR>	 1. A winnowing basket.<BR>	 2. A measure of two DRONAS.<BR>E. सूर्प्प् to measure, aff. घञ्; or शृ to injure, प Unādi aff., and the<BR>vowel and initial changed: this word and its compounds<BR>are hence more usually written शूर्प्प, &c. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्पणखा
सूर्पणखा f. (-खा) The sister of RĀVAṆA.<BR> E. सूर्प, नख a nail.; also शूर्पणखा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्म्मि|सूर्मि|सूर्मिः
सूर्म्मि f. (-र्म्मिः-र्म्मी)<BR>	 1. An image of metal, chiefly of iron.<BR>	 2. The pillar of a<BR>house.<BR>	 3. Brightness, radiance.<BR> E. श changed to सः : see शूर्म्मी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्य|सूर्य|सूर्यः|सूर्य्यः
सूर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. Gigantic swallow wort, (Asclepias gigantea.)<BR>3. The son of BALI.<BR>	 f. (-र्य्या)<BR>	 1. The wife of the sun.<BR>	 2. A bitter-<BR>gourd.<BR>	 3. A new bride.<BR> E. सृ to go, (in the heavens,) क्यप् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यकान्त|सूर्यकान्त|सूर्यकांत|सूर्यकान्तः|सूर्य्यकान्तः
सूर्य्यकान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. The sun-gem, sometimes applied to crystal, but usually<BR>to a stone of fabulous existence and properties.<BR>	 2. A tree,<BR>(Hibiscus phœniceus,) the red sort.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, कान्त a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यकान्वि
सूर्य्यकान्वि f. (-न्तिः)<BR>	 1. The flower of the Sesamum.<BR>	 2. sun-shine.<BR> E. सूर्य्य<BR>the sun, and कान्ति lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यकाल|सूर्यकाल|सूर्यकालः|सूर्य्यकालः
सूर्य्यकाल m. (-लः) Day.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यकालानलचक्र|सूर्यकालानलचक्र|सूर्य्यकालानलचक्रं
सूर्य्यकालानलचक्र n. (-क्रं) A kind of astrological diagram for indicating good or bad fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यग्रह|सूर्यग्रह|सूर्यग्रहः|सूर्य्यग्रहः
सूर्य्यग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. An eclipse of the sun.<BR>	 3. The personi-<BR>fied ascending and descending node, or RĀHU and KETU.<BR>	 4. The<BR>bottom of a water-jar.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and ग्रह a planet; or<BR>seizing, laying hold of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यग्रहण|सूर्यग्रहण|सूर्य्यग्रहणं
सूर्य्यग्रहण n. (-णं) A solar eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यज|सूर्यज|सूर्यजः|सूर्य्यजः
सूर्य्यज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The monkey SUGRĪVA.<BR>	 2. The hero KARṆA.<BR>	 3. SATURN.<BR>f. (-जा) The river Yamunā.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यतनय|सूर्यतनय|सूर्यतनयः|सूर्य्यतनयः
सूर्य्यतनय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. KARṆA.<BR>	 2. SUGRĪVA.<BR>	 f. (-या) The river Yamunā.<BR>E. सूर्य्य the sun, तनय child; also similar compounds, सूर्य्यपुत्त्र, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यतेजस्|सूर्यतेजस्
सूर्य्यतेजस् n. (-जः) The radiance or heat of the sun.<BR> E. सूर्य्य, तेजस् light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यनक्षत्र|सूर्यनक्षत्र
सूर्य्यनक्षत्र n. (-त्रं) That of the twenty-seven constellations in which the<BR>sun happens to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यपर्वन्|सूर्यपर्वन्
सूर्य्यपर्वन् n. (-र्व) A solar festival, on the days of the solstices, equinoxes, eclipses, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यपुत्त्र|सूर्यपुत्र|सूर्यपुत्रः|सूर्य्यपुत्त्रः|सूर्य्यपुत्र
सूर्य्यपुत्त्र m. (-त्त्रः)<BR>	 1. VARUṆA.<BR>	 2. ŚANI or Saturn.<BR>	 3. YAMA.<BR>	 f. (-त्त्री)<BR>	 1.<BR>Lightning.<BR>	 2. The river Yamunā.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and पुत्त्र the<BR>child; applicable also to KARṆA, SUGRĪVA, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यप्रभव|सूर्यप्रभव
सूर्य्यप्रभव Adj. Sprung from the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यफणिचक्र|सूर्यफणिचक्र|सूर्य्यफणिचक्रं
सूर्य्यफणिचक्र n. (-क्रं) A kind of astrological diagram for indicating good or bad fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यभक्त|सूर्यभक्त|सूर्यभक्तः|सूर्य्यभक्तः
सूर्य्यभक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Devoted to, or worshipping the sun.<BR>	 m. (-क्तः)<BR>A flower, (Pentapetes phœnicea.)<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, भक्त attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यभक्तक|सूर्यभक्तक|सूर्य्यभक्तकः
सूर्य्यभक्तक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A flower, (Pentapetes phœnicea.)<BR>	 2. A worshipper<BR>of the sun.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यमणि|सूर्यमणि|सूर्यमणिः|सूर्य्यमणिः
सूर्य्यमणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Hibiscus phœniceus.)<BR>	 2. The sun-stone, a<BR>crystal lens or a fabulous sort of gem.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यमण्डल|सूर्यमण्डल|सूर्यमंडल|सूर्य्यमण्डलं
सूर्य्यमण्डल n. (-लं) The orb or disc of the sun.<BR> E. सूर्य्य and मण्डल circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्ययन्त्र|सूर्ययन्त्र|सूर्ययंत्र
सूर्य्ययन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A representation of the sun, used in worshipping<BR>that divinity.<BR>	 2. An instrument used in taking solar observation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यरश्मि|सूर्यरश्मि|सूर्यरश्मिः
सूर्य्यरश्मि m. (-श्मिः) A ray of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यलता|सूर्यलता
सूर्य्यलता f. (-ता) A plant, (Cleome viscosa.)<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and लता a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यलोक|सूर्यलोक|सूर्यलोकः|सूर्य्यलोकः
सूर्य्यलोक m. (-कः) The heaven of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यवल्ली|सूर्यवल्ली
सूर्य्यवल्ली f. (-ल्ली) A plant, (Cleome pentaphylla.)<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and वल्ली a pedicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यविलोकन|सूर्यविलोकन
सूर्य्यविलोकन n. (-नं) The ceremony of taking a child out to see the<BR>sun when four months old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यसङ्क्रम|सूर्यसङ्क्रम|सूर्यसंक्रमः
सूर्य्यसङ्क्रम m. (-सः) The passage of the sun from one sign to another.<BR>E. सूर्य्य, and सङ्क्रम going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यसङ्क्रान्ति|सूर्यसङ्क्रान्ति|सूर्यसंक्रांति
सूर्य्यसङ्क्रान्ति f. (-न्तिः) The sun's entrance into a new sign.<BR> E. सूर्य्य, सङ्क्रान्ति transit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यसंज्ञ|सूर्यसञ्ज्ञ|सूर्य्यसंज्ञं
सूर्य्यसंज्ञ n. (-ज्ञं) Saffron.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and संज्ञ appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यसारथि|सूर्यसारथि|सूर्यसारथिः|सूर्य्यसारथिः
सूर्य्यसारथि m. (-थिः) The charioteer of the sun, ARUṆA or the personi-<BR>fied dawn.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and सारथि a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यहृदय|सूर्यहृदय|सूर्य्यहृदयं
