सूर्य्यार्घ
सूर्य्यार्घ n. (-र्घं) The presentation of an offering to the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यालोक|सूर्यालोक|सूर्यालोकः|सूर्य्यालोकः
सूर्य्यालोक m. (-कः) Sun-shine.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and आलोक light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यावर्त्त|सूर्यावर्त|सूर्यावर्तः|सूर्य्यावर्त्तः
सूर्य्यावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Cleome viscosa.)<BR>	 2. A sun-flower, (Helian-<BR>thus indicus.)<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and आवर्त्त revolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यावेक्षण|सूर्यावेक्षण
सूर्य्यावेक्षण n. (-णं) Looking at the sun.<BR> E. सूर्य्य, and अवेक्षण looking at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्याश्मन्|सूर्याश्मन्
सूर्य्याश्मन् m. (-श्मा) The sun-gem.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्याश्व|सूर्याश्व|सूर्याश्वः|सूर्य्याश्वः
सूर्य्याश्व m. (-श्वः) A horse of the sun.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्यास्त|सूर्यास्त|सूर्य्यास्तं
सूर्य्यास्त n. (-स्तं) Sun-set.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun अस्त setting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्याह्व|सूर्याह्व|सूर्याह्वः|सूर्य्याह्वं|सूर्य्याह्वः
सूर्य्याह्व n. (-ह्वं) Copper.<BR>	 m. (-ह्वः) Gigantic swallow-wort.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्येन्दुसङ्गम|सूर्येन्दुसङ्गम|सूर्येंदुसंगम|सूर्येन्दुसंगमः|सूर्य्येन्दुसङ्गमः
सूर्य्येन्दुसङ्गम m. (-नः) Day of new-moon, when the moon rises invisible.<BR>E. सूर्य्य the sun, इन्दु the moon, सङ्गम conjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्योढ|सूर्योढ|सूर्योढः|सूर्य्योढः
सूर्य्योढ m. (-ढः)<BR>	 1. An evening guest, one who claims hospitality after<BR>sunset.<BR>	 2. The time of sunset.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and ऊढ borne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूर्य्योदय|सूर्योदय|सूर्योदयः|सूर्य्योदयः
सूर्य्योदय m. (-यः) Sunrise.<BR> E. सूर्य्य the sun, and उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूष्
सूष् r. 1st cl. (सूषति) To bring forth, to bear, to beget; also षूष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सषणा
सषणा f. (-णा) A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सूष्यती
सूष्यती f. (-ती) A woman who is parturient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृ
सृ r. 1st cl. (सरति) r. 3d cl. (ससर्त्ति) To go, r. 1st cl. (सरति or धावति)<BR>	 1.<BR>To go fast, to run, (धै being substituted for the root.)<BR>	 2. To pro-<BR>ceed.<BR>	 3. To approach.<BR>	 4. To flow.<BR>	 5. To blow. With अनु prefixed., 1.<BR>To follow.<BR>	 2. To conform to.<BR>	 3. To go to.<BR>	 4. To return to. With<BR>अप, To go back, to withdraw or remove. With अभि, 1. To spread<BR>out or abroad.<BR>	 2. To go to or with, to accompany or attend, or<BR>to meet upon appointment.<BR>	 3. To attack. With उप, 1. To<BR>approach, to advance.<BR>	 2. To visit. With निर्, To go forth or out.<BR>With प्र, 1. To proceed.<BR>	 2. To extend.<BR>	 3. To project, 4. To pass-<BR>away, (as time.)<BR>	 5. To be prevalent.<BR>	 6. To predominate. With वि,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">Page802-a+ 60</a>]<BR>1. To go separately or apart.<BR>	 2. To come or arrive.<BR>	 3. To spread.<BR>4. To forego, to quit or leave. With प्रति, 1. To go towards, to<BR>assail.<BR>	 2. To go back. With सम्, To obtain. With निस्, 1. To slip.<BR>	 2.<BR>To depart.<BR>	 3. To ooze out. With परि, 1. To flow round.<BR>	 2.<BR>To go round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=801-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक|सृकः
सृक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A lotus.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>	 3. An arrow.<BR>	 4. A thunder-<BR>bolt.<BR> E. सृ to go, कक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृकण्डु|सृकंडु|सृकण्डुः
सृकण्डु f. (-ण्डुः) Itch, psora, scab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृकाल|सृकालः
सृकाल m. (-लः) A jackal.<BR> E. सृ to go, कालन् aff., कुक् augment; also सृगाल, शृकाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृक्कन्
सृक्कन् n. (-क्क) The corner of the mouth.<BR> E. सृज् to quit, (saliva,) कनिन्<BR>aff., form irr.; this word has various forms, as with a final vowel<BR>सृक्क n. (-क्कं) with क्वन्, or क्वनिन्, सृक्व n. (-क्वं) or सृक्वन् n. (-क्व); with क्कि or<BR>क्वि aff.: सृक्कि n. (-क्कि) or सृक्वि n. (-क्वि); with इनि, सृक्किन् n. (-क्कि) or<BR>सृक्विन् n. (-क्वि) and with ङीष् added, fem. form, सृक्विणी, सृक्विणी, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृग|सृगः
सृग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A sort of arrow, thrown with the hand or shot through<BR>a tube.<BR>	 2. A sling.<BR> E. सृ to go, aff. गक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृगाल|सृगालः
सृगाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A jackal.<BR>	 2. A Daitya or demon.<BR> E. सृज् to let go,<BR>कालन् aff; more usually शृगाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृङ्का|सृंका
सृङ्का f. (-ङ्का) A kind of garland made of jewels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज्
सृज् r. 4th cl. (सृज्यते) r. 6th cl. (सृजति)<BR>	 1. To leave, to quit.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be left or abandoned.<BR>	 3. To create, to make.<BR>	 4. To let loose.<BR>5. To shed.<BR>	 6. To throw.<BR>	 7. To place on, to apply.<BR>	 8. To<BR>beget.<BR>	 9. To send away. With अति, 1. To leave.<BR>	 2. To give.<BR>3. To remit. With अभि, To give. With अव, 1. To let loose.<BR>	 2. To<BR>cast. With उद्, 1. To shed.<BR>	 2. To let loose.<BR>	 3. To abandon.<BR>	 4. To<BR>shoot.<BR>	 5. To throw away.<BR>	 6. To dismiss.<BR>	 7. To return.<BR>	 8. To repu-<BR>diate.<BR>	 9. To decline. With उप, 1. To pour out or on, to make an<BR>oblation.<BR>	 2. To join.<BR>	 3. To oppress.<BR>	 4. To eclipse. With नि, To<BR>deliver, to set free. With प्र, 1. To abandon.<BR>	 2. To injure. With वि,<BR>1. To shed.<BR>	 2. To abandon.<BR>	 3. To drop.<BR>	 4. To send.<BR>	 5. To let fall.<BR>6. To repudiate.<BR>	 7. To utter.<BR>	 8. To give. With उत् or वि prefixed,<BR>To abandon, to quit, to reject. With सम्, To unite, to be in<BR>alliance or contact with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज्
सृज् m. (-सृक् or सृग्-सृट् or सृड्) A Creator.<BR> E. सृज् to create, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृजिकाक्षार|सृजिकाक्षारः
सृजिकाक्षार m. (-रः) Natron, alkali. E. See सर्ज्जिकाक्षार ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृज्यमान
सृज्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being made or created.<BR> E. सृज् to create, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृणि|सृणिः
सृणि m. (-णिः)<BR>	 1. An enemy.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 mf. (-णिः or -णिः-णी) A<BR>hook used to drive an elephant.<BR> E. सृ to go, नि Unādi aff., and<BR>the vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृणिका
सृणिका f. (-का) Saliva.<BR> E. सृ to go, नि added, and कन् aff.; or सृ as<BR>before, with ईकन् Unādi aff., and नुम् augment, सृणीका f. (-का ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृत|सृतः
सृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone.<BR> E. सृ to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृति|सृतिः
सृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A road, a path, a way.<BR>	 2. Going, gliding, proceeding.<BR>3. Hurting, injuring.<BR> E. सृ to go, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृत्वर|सृत्वरः
सृत्वर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Going, moving.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A stream, a river.<BR>	 2. A<BR>mother.<BR> E. सृ to go, क्वरप् aff., तुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृदर|सृदरः
सृदर m. (-रः) A snake.<BR> E. सृ to go, दर Unādi aff.; or सृ-अरक् दुक् च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृदाकु|सृदाकुः
सृदाकु m. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. Air, wind.<BR>	 3. INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>	 4. The<BR>disc or orb of the sun.<BR>	 f. (-कुः) A river in general.<BR> E. सृ to go, काकु<BR>Unādi aff., and दुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्
सृप् (ऌ) सृपॢ r. 1st. cl. (सर्पति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To creep, to crawl.<BR>With अप, 1. To go from, to depart.<BR>	 2. To deviate from.<BR>	 3. To<BR>espy. With उप, 1. To go near.<BR>	 2. To undergo.<BR>	 3. To go forth.<BR>	 4.<BR>To move. With अनु, To approach. With उद्, To rise, to overflow.<BR>With परि, To move to and fro. With प्र, 1. To proceed, to come<BR>forth.<BR>	 2. To prevail, to spread. With वि, 1. To sneak about,<BR>to fly about.<BR>	 2. To march, to proceed.<BR>	 3. To spread.<BR>	 4. To fall, to<BR>flow.<BR>	 5. To disperse.<BR>	 6. To wind.<BR>	 7. To run away. With सम्, 1. To<BR>flow.<BR>	 2. To glide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृपाट|सृपाटः
सृपाट mf. (-टः-टी) A kind of measure.<BR> E. सृ to go, पाट aff.; or सृप्-काटन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृपाटिका
सृपाटिका f. (-का) The beak of a bird.<BR> E. सृ to go, पाट aff., कन् added,<BR>fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्त
सृप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Gone, going.<BR> E. सृप् to go, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्र|सृप्रः
सृप्र m. (-प्रः) The moon.<BR> E. सृप् to go, रक् Unādi aff.; or सृप्-क्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृभ्
सृभ् r. 1st cl. (सर्भति) इ, सृभि (सृम्भति) To injure or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृमर|सृमरः
सृमर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Going, going well or quickly.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A kind of<BR>animal; according to some authorities, a young deer.<BR> E. सृ to go,<BR>क्मरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्ट|सृष्टं
सृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Created, made.<BR>	 2. Much, many.<BR>	 3. Ascertained.<BR>4. Joined, attached, connected.<BR>	 5. Ornamented, adorned.<BR>	 6. Left,<BR>abandoned.<BR>	 7. Poured out.<BR> E. सृज् to create, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्टवत्
सृष्टवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Creating, making.<BR> E. सृज् to create, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्टि|सृष्टिः
सृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Creation, creating.<BR>	 2. Nature, natural property or<BR>disposition.<BR>	 3. The absence of properties.<BR>	 4. The existence of<BR>properties or qualities.<BR>	 5. Giving away, gift.<BR>	 6. Letting loose. E.<BR>सृज् to create or abandon, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृष्ट्वा
सृष्ट्वा Ind. Having created.<BR> E. सृज् to create, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सॄ
सॄ r. 9th cl. (सृणाति) To hurt, to injure, to kill.; also षॄ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्
सेक् (ऋ) (सेकृ) r. 1st cl. (सेकते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक|सेकः
सेक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Sprinkling, aspersion, as of a fluid, or of Ghee on the<BR>sacrificial fire, &c.<BR>	 2. Seminal effusion.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेकपात्र|सेकपात्रं
सेकपात्र n. (-त्रं) A bucket, a baling vessel.<BR> E. सेक sprinkling, पात्र vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेकिम|सेकिमं
सेकिम n. (-मं) A radish.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, इमच् aff.; or सेक् वा डिम ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्तृ
सेक्तृ mfn. (-क्ता-क्त्री-क्तृ) Sprinkling, aspergent, who or what sprinkles.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-क्ता) A husband.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्त्र|सेक्त्रं
सेक्त्र n. (-क्त्रं) A bucket.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, aff. ष्ट्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचक|सेचकः
सेचक mfn. (-क्रः-का-कं) Sprinkling, a sprinkler.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A cloud.<BR> E. षिच्<BR>to sprinkle, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचन|सेचनं
सेचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sprinkling, aspersion.<BR>	 2. Dripping, oozing.<BR>	 nf. (-नं-नी)<BR>A bucket, a baling vessel.<BR> E. षिच् to sprinkle, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेटु|सेटुः
सेटु m. (-टुः)<BR>	 1. The water-melon.<BR>	 2. A kind of cucumber, (Cucumis<BR>Madraspatanus.)<BR> E. षिट् to disregard, उन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतु|सेतुः
सेतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. A mound, a bank, a causeway, dyke, an elevated piece of<BR>ground separating fields, and serving, during their inundation in<BR>the rains, for the passage of travellers, &c.<BR>	 2. A bridge.<BR>	 3. A pass,<BR>a defile, a road practised in mountainous countries, and places of<BR>difficult access.<BR>	 4. A land-mark.<BR>	 5. A boundary.<BR>	 6. A barrier, an<BR>obstruction of any kind.<BR>	 7. A fixed rule or law.<BR>	 8. An epithet of<BR>the sacred syllable “Om.” 9. A tree, (Tapia cratæva.)<BR> E. षि to bind,<BR>तुन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुक|सेतुकः
सेतुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Tapia cratæva.)<BR>	 2. A causeway, a pass.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुबन्ध|सेतुबंध|सेतुबन्धः
सेतुबन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. The ridge of rocks extending from the south extre-<BR>mity of the Coromandel coast towards the island of Ceylon, sup-<BR>posed to have been formed by HANUMĀN by command of RĀMA,<BR>as a bridge for the passage of his forces, when going against<BR>RĀVAṆA.<BR>	 2. Any dyke or dam, &c.<BR> E. सेतु a bridge, बन्ध a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुभेदिन्
सेतुभेदिन् m. (-दी) A plant, commonly Danti, (Croton polyandrum.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुवृक्ष|सेतुवृक्षः
सेतुवृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A tree, (Tapia craræva.)<BR> E. सेतु the same, वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेत्र|सेत्रं
सेत्र n. (-त्रं) A ligament, a fetter.<BR> E. षि to bind, ष्ट्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेदिवस्
सेदिवस् f. (-दुषी) Sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधा
सेधा f. (-धा) A porcupine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन
सेन f. (-ना) Adj. Having a lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेना
सेना f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. An army.<BR>	 2. A goddess, commonly known by<BR>DEVA-SENĀ, the personified armament of the gods, the wife of<BR>KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 3. The mother of the third Jaina pontiff of the present<BR>era.<BR> E. षि to bind, नक् and टाप् aff.; or स with, इन a lord or leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाग्रग
सेनाग्रग m. (-गः) The leader of an army.<BR> E. सेनाग्र the front of an army,<BR>ग who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाङ्ग|सेनांग|सेनाङ्गं
सेनाङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं) A component part or member of an army, as elephants,<BR>chariots, cavalry or infantry.<BR> E. सेना an army, अङ्ग limb or member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=802-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाचर|सेनाचरः
सेनाचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) A soldier, a camp-follower, &c., one belonging<BR>to or who accompanies an army.<BR> E. सेना an army, चर् to go, ट aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनानिवेश|सेनानिवेशः
सेनानिवेश m. (-शः) The camp of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनानी
सेनानी m. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A general, the commander of an army.<BR>	 2.<BR>KĀRTIKEYA, the military deity of the Hindus.<BR> E. सेना an army, णी<BR>to lead, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापति|सेनापतिः
सेनापति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A general, the commander of an army.<BR>	 2.<BR>KĀRTIKEYA.<BR> E. सेना an army and पति master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापतित्व
सेनापतित्व n. (-त्वं) Generalship.<BR> E. त्व added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापृष्ठ
सेनापृष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) The rear of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाभङ्ग|सेनाभंग|सेनाभङ्गः
सेनाभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The breaking of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनामुख|सेनामुखं
सेनामुख n. (-खं)<BR>	 1. A division of an army or battalion, consisting<BR>of three elephants, three chariots, nine horses, and fifteen<BR>foot.<BR>	 2. A mound or covered way in front of a city-gate.<BR> E. सेना<BR>an army, and मुख commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनायोग|सेनायोगः
सेनायोग m. (-गः) The equipment of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनारक्ष|सेनारक्षः
सेनारक्ष m. (-क्षः) A guard, a picket, a sentinel, &c.<BR> E. सेना an army, and<BR>रक्ष what protects or guards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेफ|सेफः
सेफ m. (-फः) The penis.<BR> E. श changed to स; see शेफ, शेफम्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेर|सेरः
सेर m. (-रः) A kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेरराह
सेरराह m. (-हः) A horse of a milk-white colour: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेराह|सेराहः
सेराह m. (-हः) A horse of a milk-white colour; also सेरराह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेरु|सेरुः
सेरु mfn. (-रुः-रुः-रु) Binding, tying.<BR> E. षि to bind, रु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेल्
सेल् (ऋ) सेऌ r. 1st cl. (सेलति) To go or move; preferably षेल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेलु|सेलुः
सेलु m. (-लुः) A tree, (Cordia myxa:) see शेलु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्
सेव् (ऋ) सेवृ r. 1st cl. (सेवते)<BR>	 1. To serve, to gratify by service.<BR>	 2.<BR>To follow.<BR>	 3. To use, to enjoy.<BR>	 4. To attend to, to cultivate, to<BR>perform.<BR>	 5. To enjoy, (sexually.)<BR>	 6. To dwell in, to frequent.<BR>	 7. To<BR>watch over. With आ, 1. To enjoy.<BR>	 2. To practise. With उप, 1. To<BR>apply oneself to.<BR>	 2. To perform.<BR>	 3. To enjoy.<BR>	 4. To serve. With<BR>नि, 1. To pursue.<BR>	 2. To practise.<BR>	 3. To employ.<BR>	 4. To enjoy.<BR>	 5. To<BR>inhabit.<BR>	 6. To observe.<BR>	 7. To attend. With परि, To take;<BR>preferably षेवृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवक|सेवकः
सेवक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Servile, dependent.<BR>	 2. Practising.<BR>	 3. Serving.<BR>m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A sack.<BR>	 2. A servant.<BR>	 3. A votary.<BR> E. षेव् to serve, or<BR>विव् to sew, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवकाल
सेवकाल m. (-लः) A plant, commonly Dugdha-peyā; also सेवकालुः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवधि|सेवधिः
सेवधि m. (-धिः) A divine treasure, a substance considered as the trea-<BR>sure of KUVERA.<BR> E. सेव service, धा to have, aff. कि; also शेवधि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवन|सेवनं
सेवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sewing, darning, stitching.<BR>	 2. A sack.<BR>	 3. Service,<BR>worship.<BR>	 4. Using, practising, following, being addicted to, or<BR>fond of.<BR>	 5. Enjoying sexually.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A needle.<BR>	 2. (In anatomy,)<BR>A peculiar union of parts, of which seven instances occur in the<BR>body: viz:--the five sutures of the cranium, the frenum of the<BR>tongue, and that of the glans penis.<BR>	 3. A seam.<BR> E. षिव् to sew,<BR>or षेव् to serve, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवनीय
सेवनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be served, waited on, or honoured.<BR>	 2. To<BR>be followed or practised.<BR> E. सेव् to serve, अनीयर् aff.; also सेवितव्य<BR>and सेव्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवन्ती
सेवन्ती f. (-न्ती) The Indian white rose, (Rosa alba;) also सेवती ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवमान
सेवमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Serving, attending on.<BR>	 2. Pursuing, practi-<BR>sing, being addicted to.<BR> E. सेव, and शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवा
सेवा f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. Service, servitude.<BR>	 2. Worship, homage.<BR>	 3. Addition<BR>to.<BR>	 4. Use, practise, employment.<BR>	 5. Resorting to, frequenting. E.<BR>षेव् to serve, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवाकाकु|सेवाकाकुः
सेवाकाकु f. (-कुः) Change of voice in service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवाधर्म|सेवाधर्मः
सेवाधर्म m. (-र्मः)<BR>	 1. The functions of service.<BR>	 2. The duty or rule of service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवि
सेवि n. (-वि)<BR>	 1. The jujube.<BR>	 2. An apple.<BR> E. सेव-कर्मणि इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवित|सेवितः
सेवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Served, obeyed, honoured, worshipped,<BR>adored.<BR>	 2. Protected, preserved.<BR>	 3. Pursued, practised, used.<BR>	 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">Page803-b+ 60</a>]<BR>Infested or frequented by, inhabited.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The jujube.<BR>	 2. An<BR>apple.<BR> E. षेवृ to gratify by service, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवितृ
सेवितृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ)<BR>	 1. Who or what serves, worships, &c.<BR>	 2. Addic-<BR>ted or devoted to.<BR> E. सेवृ to serve, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवित्व
सेवित्व n. (-त्वं) Serving, devotion.<BR> E. सेविन् who serves, त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेविन्
सेविन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि)<BR>	 1. Serving, obeying.<BR>	 2. Pursuing, practising,<BR>using.<BR>	 3. Dwelling.<BR>	 m. (-वी) A servant.<BR> E. षेव् to serve, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्य|सेव्यं|सेव्यः
सेव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be served or obeyed, to be worshipped or<BR>honoured.<BR>	 2. What ought or may be practised, used, &c.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>taken care of.<BR>	 4. To be employed.<BR>	 5. To be enjoyed.<BR>	 n. (-व्यं) The<BR>root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>	 m. (-व्यः) A plant, (Barring-<BR>tonia acutangula.)<BR>	 f. (-व्या) A parasite plant.<BR> E. षेवृ to gratify by<BR>service, ण्यत् or यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्यता
सेव्यता f. (-ता) Rank, eminence.<BR> E. सेव्य, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, सेव्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्यमान
सेव्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Being served, waited, attended on.<BR>	 2. Being<BR>practised or used.<BR> E. सेव् to serve, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सै
सै r. 1st cl. (सायति) To waste, to decline; also षै ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंह|सैंहः
सैंह mfn. (-हः-ही-हं) Belonging to a lion, leonine, lion-like.<BR> E. सिंह a lion, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहली
सैंहली f. (-ली) Adj. Belonging to or produced in CEYLON.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहिक|सैंहिकः
सैंहिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging to a lion, leonine.<BR>	 m. (-कः) RĀHU, the<BR>personified ascending node.<BR> E. सिंह, and ठक् aff.; or सिंहिका the<BR>mother of RĀHU, (by adoption,) and अण् patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहिकेय|सैंहिकेयः
सैंहिकेय m. (-यः) A metronymic of RĀHU, the personified ascending<BR>node.<BR> E. सिंहिका the reputed mother of this being, ढन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकत|सैकतं|सैकतः
सैकत mfn. (-तः-ती-तं) Sandy in general.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. A sand-bank or an<BR>island with sandy shores.<BR> E. सिकता sandy soil, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतिक|सैकतिकं|सैकतिकः
सैकतिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Living in doubt and error.<BR>	 2. Belonging<BR>or relating to a sand-bank.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A religious mendicant,<BR>an ascetic.<BR>	 n. (-कं) A thread worn round the wrist or neck, &c.,<BR>to secure good fortune.<BR> E. सिकता sand, &c., ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतेष्ट|सैकतेष्टं
सैकतेष्ट n. (-ष्टं) Ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैतवाहिनी
सैतवाहिनी f. (-नी) The river Bāhudā.<BR> E. सित white, अण् aff., वाहिनी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैद्धान्तिक|सैद्धांतिक|सैद्धान्तिकः
सैद्धान्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Connected with or relating to a demonstra-<BR>ted truth, one who knows the truth, &c.<BR> E. सिद्धान्त an established<BR>conclusion, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनापत्य|सैनापत्यं
सैनापत्य n. (-त्यं) The command of an army, the dignity or duty of a general.<BR> E. सेनापति a general, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनिक|सैनिकः
सैनिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or belonging to an army, drawn up as<BR>an army, &c.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A guard, a sentinel, a picket.<BR>	 2. A body<BR>of forces in array.<BR> E. सेना an array, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धव|सैंधव|सैन्धवं|सैन्धवः
सैन्धव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Produced or born in Sindh.<BR>	 2. Marine, aquatic,<BR>ocean or river-born.<BR>	 m. (-वः) A horse, (bred in Sindhu.)<BR>	 mn. (-वः-वं)<BR>Rock-salt.<BR>	 n. (-वं) In dramatic literature, musical expression of<BR>disappointment with Prākrit words.<BR>	 f. (-वी) One of the Rāginis.<BR>E. सिन्धु a river, &c. अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धवक|सैंधवक|सैन्धवकः
सैन्धवक m. (-कः) A miserable inhabitant of Sindhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धवघन|सैंधवघन|सैन्धवघनः
सैन्धवघन m. (-नः) A lump of salt.<BR> E. सैन्धव, and घन thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धवशिला|सैंधवशिला
सैन्धवशिला f. (-ला) A kind of rock or fossil-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्धी|सैंधी
सैन्धी f. (-न्धी) A kind of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्य|सैन्यं|सैन्यः
सैन्य n. (-न्यं) An army.<BR>	 m. (-न्यः)<BR>	 1. A soldier under arms, one drawn<BR>up in array.<BR>	 2. A guard, a sentinel.<BR> E. सेना an army, ण्य or ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्याधिपति
सैन्याधिपति m. (-तिः) A general.<BR> E. सैन्य, and अधिपति ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैन्याध्यक्ष
सैन्याध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) A commander, a general.<BR> E. सैन्य, अध्यक्ष supervisor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैमन्तिक|सैमंतिक|सैमंतिकं|सैमन्तिकं
सैमन्तिक n. (-कं) Red-lead.<BR> E. सीमन्त the parting of the hair, (where a<BR>red mark is often made with minium,) and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरन्ध्र|सैरंध्र|सैरंध्रः|सैरन्ध्रः
सैरन्ध्र m. (-न्ध्रः)<BR>	 1. A menial servant.<BR>	 2. The son of a DASYU by an<BR>AYOGAVA female: also सैरिन्ध्र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरन्ध्री|सैरंध्री
सैरन्ध्री f. (-न्ध्री)<BR>	 1. A female artist.<BR>	 2. A name of DRAUPADĪ: see सैरिन्द्री ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिक|सैरिकः
सैरिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Relating or belonging to a plough, &c.<BR>	 2.<BR>Having furrows.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plough-man.<BR>	 2. A plough-ox, &c.<BR>E. सीर a plough, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=803-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिन्ध्र|सैरिंध्र|सैरिंध्रः|सैरिन्ध्रः
सैरिन्ध्र m. (-न्धः) A menial servant, one employed to dress and decorate<BR>the person and perform all servile offices; also who may be<BR>employed in the chase, snaring animals, &c. the offspring of a<BR>Dasyu by an Ayogava female.<BR>	 f. (-न्ध्री)<BR>	 1. An independent female<BR>artizan working in another person's house.<BR>	 2. A female attendant<BR>in the women's apartments.<BR>	 3. A woman of one of the mixed<BR>and degraded classes.<BR>	 4. DRAUPADĪ, the wife of the PĀṆḌU<BR>princes, and who upon the temporary servitude of her husbands,<BR>became workwoman in the house of the Rāja of Virāta.<BR> E. सीर<BR>a plough, धृ to hold or take, aff. क, and मुक् augment, अण् added<BR>and the penultimate vowel changed optionally to इ; whence also<BR>सैरन्ध्री, or स्वैर independent, धृ to hold or be, aff. कन्, fem. aff. ङीष्,<BR>and form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरिभ|सैरिभः
सैरिभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A buffalo.<BR>	 2. Svarga, INDRA'S heaven or paradise.<BR>E. सीर the plough or the sun, इभ an elephant, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरीय|सैरीयः
सैरीय m. (-यः) A plant, (Barleria cristata.)<BR> E. सीर a plough, अण् aff.,<BR>सैर relating to a plough, (turned up by it, &c.) and छ added; also<BR>with कन् added सैरीयक, and with ढक् aff. सैरेय or सैरेयक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरीयक|सैरीयकः
सैरीयक m. (-कः) Barleria: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैरेय|सैरेयः
सैरेय m. (-यः) A shrub, (Barleria cristata:) see सैरीय; also with कन् added सैरेयक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैवाल|सैवालं
सैवाल n. (-लं) Name of an aquatic plant: see शैवाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैसक
सैसक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Leaden, of lead.<BR> E. सीसक, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सो
सो f. (-सोः) PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. षो to destroy aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोढ|सोढः
सोढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं)<BR>	 1. Borne, suffered, endured.<BR>	 2. Patient, enduring.<BR>E. सह् to bear, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोढृ
सोढृ mfn. (-ढा-ढ्री-ढृ)<BR>	 1. Patient, enduring.<BR>	 2. Able, powerful.<BR> E. सह् to bear, &c., aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्क
सोत्क f. (-त्का)<BR>	 1. Ardently longing.<BR>	 2. Regretful.<BR>	 3. Bewailing; also सोत्कण्ठ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्कण्ठ|सोत्कंठ|सोत्कण्ठः
सोत्कण्ठ mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठा-ण्ठं)<BR>	 1. Regretting, bewailing, grieving.<BR>	 2.<BR>Impatiently eager.<BR> E. स with, उत्कण्ठा sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्प्रास|सोत्प्रासं|सोत्प्रासः
सोत्प्रास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं)<BR>	 1. Excessive, much, violent.<BR>	 2. Exaggerated.<BR>3. Ironical.<BR>	 m. (-सः) A horselaugh.<BR>	 mn. (-सः-सं) Irony, sarcasm,<BR>sneering praise and covert censure.<BR> E. स with, उत्प्रास excess or<BR>effort; उद् + प्र अस्-घञ् । it is also read सोत्प्राश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्सव
सोत्सव f. (-वा) Festive, making merry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्साह
सोत्साह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Vigorous, energetic, persevering.<BR> E. स with, उत्साह effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्सुक
सोत्सुक f. (-का) Regretful, repining, anxious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोत्सेध
सोत्सेध f. (-धा) Raised, lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोदक
सोदक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Having or containing water.<BR> E. स with, उदक water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोदय|सोदयं
सोदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Accumulated, augmented, with interest, with<BR>profit.<BR> E. स for सह with, उदय increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोदर|सोदरः
सोदर m. (-रः) A brother of whole blood.<BR>	 f. (-रा) Uterine sister.<BR> E. स for<BR>समान common, same, उदर belly, or womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोदर्य्य|सोदर्य|सोदर्यः|सोदर्य्यः
सोदर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) A brother of whole blood.<BR> E. स for समान same or<BR>common, उदर belly, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोद्योग
सोद्योग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Active, diligent, persevering.<BR> E. स with, उद्योग- effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोद्वेग
सोद्वेग f. (-गा) Sorrowful, anxious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोनह|सोनहः
सोनह m. (-हः) Garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोन्माद|सोन्मादः
सोन्माद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Mad, insane.<BR> E. स with, उन्माद madness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपकरण|सोपकरणं
सोपकरण f. (-णा) Provided with requisite implements, properly equipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपकार|सोपकारः
सोपकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Equipped, stocked, furnished or provided<BR>with necessary means or implements.<BR>	 2. Assisted, abetted,<BR>befriended.<BR> E. स with, उपकार an instrument or assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपद्रव
सोपद्रव f. (-वा) Visited with calamities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपध|सोपधं
सोपध f. (-धा) Full of fraud or deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपधिम्
सोपधिम् Ind. Fraudulently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपप्लव|सोपप्लवः
सोपप्लव m. (-वः) The sun or moon in eclipse.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. Afflicted with<BR>great calamities.<BR>	 2. Over-run by enemies.<BR>	 3. Eclipsed, (as the sun<BR>or moon.)<BR> E. स with, उपप्लव a portent, an eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपरोध
सोपरोध f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. Obstructed, impeded.<BR>	 2. Favoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपवास|सोपवासः
सोपवास mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Fasting, keeping a fast.<BR> E. स with, उपवास fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपसर्ग
सोपसर्ग f. (-र्गा)<BR>	 1. Afflicted with misfortune.<BR>	 2. Possessed by an evil<BR>spirit.<BR>	 3. Preceded by a prepositional prefix, (in gram.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपहास
सोपहास f. (-सा) Accompanied with derisive laughter, sarcastic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपाक|सोपाकः
सोपाक m. (-कः) A man of a degraded caste, the son of a Chāṇḍāla<BR>by a Pukkasī female, and only to be employed as a public<BR>executioner, &c. E. See श्वपाक; the sibilants being irregularly<BR>transposed, व changed to उ, and that to the usual Guṇa letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपाधिक
सोपाधिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Restricted, limited, qualified, special.<BR>	 f. (-की)<BR>1. Restricted by conditions or limitations, qualified by parti-<BR>cular characteristics, (in phil.)<BR>	 2. Having some particular attri-<BR>butes; also सोपाधि ।<BR> E. स with, उपाधि discrimination, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपान|सोपानं
सोपान n. (-नं) Stairs, steps or a stair-case.<BR> E. स with, उप above, up,<BR>and अन a going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोपानमार्ग
सोपानमार्ग m. (-र्गः) A flight of steps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोभाञ्जन|सोभाञ्जनः
सोभाञ्जन m. (-नः) A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga:) see शोभाञ्जन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोम|सोमं|सोमः
सोम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. KUVERA.<BR>	 3. A monkey chief.<BR>	 4. Air,<BR>wind.<BR>	 5. YAMA.<BR>	 6. One of the demi-gods called VASUS.<BR>	 7. ŚIVA.<BR>8. The moon-plant, (Asclepias acida, or Sarcostema viminalis.)<BR>	 9.<BR>The acid juice of the Sarcostema.<BR>	 10. A drug of supposed magi-<BR>cal properties.<BR>	 11. Water.<BR>	 12. Nectar, the liquor of immortals.<BR>13. Camphor.<BR>	 14. A deified progenitor.<BR>	 15. A mountain or moun-<BR>tainous range, the mountains of the moon.<BR>	 16. The best, chief, (as<BR>the last member of a compound.)<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Rice-water or gruel.<BR>2. Heaven, sky, æther.<BR> E. षू to bear, (as young,) or to sprinkle,<BR>Unādi aff. मन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमकान्त|सोमकांत|सोमकान्तः
सोमकान्त m. (-न्तः) The moon-gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमक्षय|सोमक्षयः
सोमक्षय m. (-यः) The disappearance of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमगर्भ|सोमगर्भः
सोमगर्भ m. (-र्भः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सोम the moon, गर्भ embryo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमज|सोमजं|सोमजः
सोमज m. (-जः) The planet MERCURY.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Milk.<BR> E. सोम the moon, ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमतीर्थ|सोमतीर्थं
सोमतीर्थ m. (-र्थः) A place of pilgrimage in the west of India.<BR> E. सोम<BR>the moon, and तीर्थ a holy place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमदैवत्य
सोमदैवत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) Presided over by SOMA.<BR> E. सोम, and दैवत्य deification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमधारा
सोमधारा f. (-रा) Sky, heaven.<BR> E. सोम the moon, धारा having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमन्
सोमन् m. (-मा) The moon.<BR> E. षू to bring forth, (as young,) मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमनाथ|सोमनाथः
सोमनाथ m. (-थः)<BR>	 1. Name of a celebrated Linga destroyed by Mahmud<BR>of Gazni.<BR>	 2. The place where this Linga was set up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमप|सोमपः
सोमप m. (-पः) The performer of a sacrifice, or a sacrificer, who drinks<BR>the juice of the acid Sarcostema.<BR> E. सोम the plant, प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपति|सोमपतिः
सोमपति m. (-तिः) INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपत्र|सोमपत्रः
सोमपत्र n. (-त्रं) A sort of grass, (Saccharum cylindricum.)<BR> E. सोम the Sarcostema, पत्न a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपा
सोमपा m. (-पाः)<BR>	 1. A drinker of the juice of the acid Sarcostema.<BR>	 2.<BR>A Pitṛ or progenitor of a certain class, or those who are espe-<BR>cially the Pitṛs of the Brahmans.<BR> E. सोम the acid Sarcostema,<BR>and पा to drink, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपान
सोमपान n. (-नं) Drinking the juice of the acid Sarcostema, an essential<BR>part of sacrifices according to the Veda-ritual.<BR> E. सोम, पान drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमपीतिन्
सोमपीतिन् m. (-ती) A drinker of the juice of the acid Sarcostema. E.<BR>सोम the juice of the plant, पीति beverage, इनि aff.; it is also read<BR>सोमपीथिन् and सोमपीविन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमप्रवाक|सोमप्रवाकः
सोमप्रवाक m. (-कः) A person commissioned to engage Śrotriyas for a Soma-sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमबन्धु|सोमबंधु|सोमबन्धुः
सोमबन्धु n. (-न्धु) The white water-lily.<BR> E. सोम the moon, बन्धु friend;<BR>expanding at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमभू
सोमभू m. (-भूः)<BR>	 1. One of the persons called VĀSUDEVAS, by the<BR>Jainas.<BR>	 2. The son of SOMA, BUDHA, the regent of MERCURY, and<BR>supposed founder of the lunar dynasty.<BR> E. सोम the moon, and<BR>भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमयाग|सोमयागः
सोमयाग m. (-गः) Offering or sacrifice in which the acid Sarcostema<BR>juice is drank.<BR> E. सोम, and याग sacrifice; also सोमयज्ञ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमयाजिन्
सोमयाजिन् m. (-जी) A sacrificer who drinks at the ceremony the juice<BR>of the acid Sarcostema.<BR> E. सोम plant, यज् to sacrifice, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=804-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमयोनि|सोमयोनिः
सोमयोनि m. (-निः) A sort of sandal of yellow colour and great fra-<BR>grance.<BR> E. सोम the moon, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमराजिन्
सोमराजिन् m. (-जी) A medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.) E.<BR>सोम the moon. राज् to shine, aff. णिनि; or with अच् and ङीष् added,<BR>सामराजी; and again with कन् added, सोमराजिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमराजी
सोमराजी f. (-जी)<BR>	 1. A medicinal plant: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमरोग|सोमरोगः
सोमरोग m. (-गः) A particular disease of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमलता
सोमलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The moon-plant or acid Sarcostema, (S. viminalis.)<BR>2. The river Godāvari.<BR> E. सोम, and लता a creeper; also सोमवल्लरी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवंश|सोमवंशः
सोमवंश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A name of YUDHIṢṬHIRA.<BR>	 2. The lunar dynasty,<BR>or series of princes supposed to descend through BUDHA the<BR>son of SOMA, or the moon.<BR> E. सोम, and वंश family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवत्|सोमवन्त्
सोमवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Lunar, having the moon.<BR>	 2. Having the<BR>Sarcostema-juice.<BR> E. सोम, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवत्|सोमवन्त्
सोमवत् Ind. Like the moon.<BR> E. सोम, and वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवल्क
सामवल्क m. (-ल्कः)<BR>	 1. A white kind of Khayer, (Mimosa catechu.)<BR>	 2.<BR>A medicinal plant, commonly Kāyaphal.<BR>	 3. A plant, (Guilandina<BR>bonduccella.)<BR> E. सोम the moon, and वत्क bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवल्लरि|सोमवल्लरिः
सोमवल्लरि f. (-रिः-री) The moon-plant, (Sarcostema viminalis.)<BR> E. सोम<BR>the moon, and वल्लरि a creeper; also सोमलता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवल्ली
सोमवल्ली f. (-ल्ली)<BR>	 1. A twining plant, (Menispermum glabrum.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>medicinal plant, (Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR>	 3. The moon-plant. E.<BR>साम the moon, and वल्ली a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवार|सोमवारः
सोमवार m. (-रः) Monday.<BR> E. सोम, and वार a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमविक्रयिन्
सोमविक्रयिन् m. (-यी) A vendor of the juice of acid Sarcostema.<BR> E. सोम<BR>the plant, विक्रय selling, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमवृक्ष|सोमवृक्षः
सोमवृक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A medicinal plant, (Kāyaphal.)<BR>	 2. A shrub,<BR>(Serratula anthelmintica.)<BR> E. सोम the moon, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसंज्ञ
सोमसंज्ञ n. (-ज्ञं) Camphor.<BR> E. सोम the moon, and संज्ञ appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसद्
सोमसद् m. (-सद्) A Pitṛ or progenitor of a peculiar class, the<BR>progenitor of the celestial beings called Sādhyas.<BR> E. सोम, and सद्<BR>who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसार|सोमसारः
सोमसार m. (-रः) The white Khadira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसिद्धान्त|सोमसिद्धान्तः
सोमसिद्धान्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. One of the Buddhas.<BR>	 2. A rationalist of a sect<BR>of Śaivas.<BR>	 3. A particular doctrine, a system of theological<BR>philosophy, followed by a branch of the worshippers of ŚIVA. E.<BR>सोम the moon, (as the teacher of the doctrine,) and सिद्धान्त truth,<BR>(whose.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसिद्धान्तिन्
सोमसिद्धान्तिन् m. (-न्ती) A follower of a branch of the Śaivas.<BR> E. सोमसिद्धान्त the doctrine, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसिन्धु|सोमसिंधु|सोमसिन्धुः
सोमसिन्धु m. (-न्धुः) VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसुत्
सोमसुत् m. (-सुत्) A priest or sacrificer who sprinkles the juice of the<BR>acid Sarcostema at a sacrifice.<BR> E. सोम the plant, षु to sprinkle, aff.<BR>क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसुता
सोमसुता f. (-ता) The river Narmadā.<BR> E. सोम the moon, सुता daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसुत्वत्
सोमसुत्वत् mfn. (-त्वान्-त्वती-त्वत्) Having sprinklers of Soma-juice,<BR>(a hermitage, a sacrifice, &c.)<BR> E. सोमसुत्, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमसूत्र|सोमसूत्रं
सोमसूत्र n. (-त्रं) A channel for conveying water from a Śiva-Linga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामसूत्रप्रदक्षिणा
सामसूत्रप्रदक्षिणा f. (-णा) Circumambulation around a Śiva-Linga in such<BR>a way as that the Soma-sūtra shall not be crossed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमाख्य|सोमाख्यं
सोमाख्य n. (-ख्यं) The red lotus.<BR> E. सोम the moon, and आख्या appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमाल|सोमालः
सोमाल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Soft, bland.<BR> E. सोम the moon, अल् to resemble,<BR>aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमिन्
सोमिन् m. (-मी)<BR>	 1. A performer of Soma-sacrifice.<BR>	 f. (-मिनी) Performing the Soma-sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमोद्भवा
सोमोद्भवा f. (-वा) The river Narmadā.<BR> E. सोम the moon, (for the<BR>lunar race,) and उद्भव born; or सोम nectar, उद्भव production, (from it,)<BR>by conferring paradise on those who bathe in it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोम्य
सोम्य f. (-म्या)<BR>	 1. Worthy of Soma.<BR>	 2. Offering Soma.<BR>	 3. Soft, good, amiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोराष्ट्रिक
सोराष्ट्रिक m. (-कः) A sort of poison.<BR> E. सुराष्ट्र Surāt, ठक् aff.; also सौराष्ट्रिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्लुण्ठ|सोल्लुंठ|सोल्लुंठः|सोल्लुण्ठः
सोल्लुण्ठ m. (-ण्ठः) Irony, ridicule: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्लुण्ठन|सोल्लुंठन|सोल्लुंठनं|सोल्लुण्ठनं
सोल्लुण्ठन n. (-नं) Apparent praise and covert censure, irony.<BR> E. स with, उल्लुण्ठन the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोष्मन्
सोष्मन् m. (-ष्मा) An aspirated letter. Adj.<BR>	 1. Warm.<BR>	 2. Aspirated, (in<BR>gram.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर|सौकरः
सौकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Hoggish, swinish.<BR>	 2. Relating to a hog.<BR> E. सूकर a hog, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकरिक|सौकरिकः
सौकरिक m. (-कः) A hunter.<BR> E. सूकर a boar, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर्य्य|सौकर्य|सौकर्यं|सौकर्य्यं
सौकर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Facility, ease of effecting anything.<BR>	 2. Easy an<BR>extempore composition, or preparation of food or medicine.<BR>	 3.<BR>Hoggishness, swinishness, the condition or qualities of a hog.<BR>	 4.<BR>Adroitness.<BR> E. सुकर doing easily, or सूकर a hog, aff. ष्यञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकुमार्य्य|सौकुमार्य|सौकुमार्यं
सौकुमार्य्य n. (-र्य्य)<BR>	 1. Youthfulness.<BR>	 2. Delicacy, tenderness.<BR> E. सुकुमारष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौक्ष्म्य|सौक्ष्म्यं
सौक्ष्म्य n. (-क्ष्म्यं) Minuteness, subtilty.<BR> E. सूक्ष्म small, fine, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखशायनिक|सौखशायनिकः
सौखशायनिक m. (-कः) One who asks another whether he has slept well<BR>also सौखशायि क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखसुप्तिक|सौखसुप्तिकः
सौखसुप्तिक m. (-कः) A bard, a minstrel, one whose duty is to waken the<BR>prince in the morning with music.<BR> E. सुखसुप्त sleeping pleasantly,<BR>and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखिक|सौखिकः
सौखिक f. (-की) Relating to pleasure; also सौखोय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौख्य|सौख्यं
सौख्य n. (-ख्यं) Pleasure, happiness, felicity.<BR> E. सुख happiness, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगत|सौगतः
सौगत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A Saugata, a heretic, an atheist.<BR>	 2. A Bauddha. E.<BR>सुगत the supposed teacher of these doctrines, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगतिक|सौगतिकः
सौगतिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A Bauddha mendicant.<BR>	 2. The mendicant<BR>Brāhman.<BR>	 3. Doubt, unbelief, scepticism.<BR>	 4. An atheist, an<BR>unbeliever.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Atheism.<BR> E. सुयत the founder of the sect, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्ध|सौगंध|सौगन्धं|सौगन्धः
सौगन्ध n. (-न्धं)<BR>	 1. A fragrant grass: see कत्तृण.<BR>	 2. Fragrance.<BR>	 f. (-न्धी)<BR>Sweet-scented.<BR> E. सुगन्ध fragrant, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्धिक|सौगंधिक|सौगन्धिकं|सौगन्धिकः
सौगन्धिक mfn. (-कः-का or -की-कं) Fragrant, odorous.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The white<BR>water-lily, (Nymphæa lotus.)<BR>	 2. A fragrant grass: see कत्तृण. 3<BR>A ruby.<BR>	 4. The blue lotus.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Sulphur.<BR>	 2. A dealer in<BR>perfumes.<BR> E. सु pleasant, गन्ध smell, and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्ध्य|सौगंध्य|सौगंध्यं|सौगन्ध्यं
सौगन्ध्य n. (-न्ध्यं) Sweetness of odour, fragrance.<BR> E. सुगन्ध, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौचि|सौचिः
सौचि m. (-चिः) A tailor.<BR> E. सूची a needle, इञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौचिक|सौचिकः
सौचिक m. (-कः) A tailor.<BR> E. सूची a needle, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौजन्य|सौजन्यं
सौजन्य n. (-न्य)<BR>	 1. Kindness, clemency, compassion.<BR>	 2. Friendship.<BR>	 3.<BR>Goodness, generosity.<BR> E. सुजन, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौण्डी|सौंडी
सौण्डी f. (-ण्डी) Long-pepper. “गजपिप्पल्याम्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्य|सौत्यं
सौत्य n. (-त्य) The office of a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्र|सौत्रः
सौत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्री-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Preceptive, formulary, according to rule or<BR>precept.<BR>	 2. Relating to or having a thread.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः)<BR>	 1. Brāhman.<BR>	 2.<BR>A radical, the only application of which is to form derivative nouns.<BR>and not like other roots, capable of conversion into a verb.<BR> E. सूत्र<BR>a thread, a rule, &c., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्रान्तिक|सौत्रांतिक
सौत्रान्तिक m. Plu. (-काः) Name of one of the four great schools of BUDDHISM<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्रामणी
सौत्रामणी f. (-णी) The east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदामनी
सौदामनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Lightning.<BR>	 2. A courtezan of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>	 3.<BR>Part of the Śudāman mountain. E. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदामिनी
सौदामिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Lightning.<BR>	 2. One of the Apsarasas or nymphs of<BR>Svarga.<BR>	 3. A particular sort of lightning.<BR>	 4. A city so named. E.<BR>सुदामन् a cloud, a mountain, or INDRA'S elephant, अण् and ङीष्<BR>affs. with the augment इक्; also omitting the augment, सौदामनी,<BR>and dropping the penultimate vowel, सौदाम्नी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदाम्नी
सौदाम्नी f. (-म्नी) Lightning: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदायिक|सौदायिकं
सौदायिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Received by a woman at her marriage from<BR>her father or mother or any relative as a mark of regard, and<BR>thence her own property.<BR> E. मुदाय a nuptial gift, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौध|सौधः
सौध n. (-ध)<BR>	 1. A mansion, a palace.<BR>	 2. Silver.<BR>	 3. Opal.<BR>	 f. (-धी)<BR>	 1.<BR>Relating to nectar.<BR>	 2. Plastered.<BR> E. सुधा plaster, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधार|सौधारः
सौधार m. (-रः) One of the fourteen parts of a drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधाल|सौधालं
सौधाल n. (-लं) A temple of ŚIVA, or in the form of Īśāna.<BR> E. सौध a<BR>palace, अल् to be equal to, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौन|सौनः
सौन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Belonging or relating to a slaughter-house., &c.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-नं) Butcher's meat.<BR> E. सना, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=805-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनधर्म्य
सौनधर्म्य n. (-र्म्य) A state of deadly hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनन्द|सौनंद|सौनंदं|सौनन्दं
सौनन्द n. (-न्दं) The club of BALARĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनन्दिन्|सौनंदिन्
सौनन्दिन् m. (-न्दी) BALARĀMA, the brother of KṚṢṆA.<BR> E. सौनन्द his club, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनिक|सौनिकः
सौनिक m. (-कः) A vendor of the flesh of beasts or birds.<BR> E. सून a place<BR>of slaughter, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौन्दर्य्य|सौन्दर्य|सौंदर्य|सौंदर्यं|सौन्दर्य्यं
सौन्दर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Beauty, loveliness.<BR> E. सुन्दर handsome, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपर्ण|सौपर्णं
सौपर्ण n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Dry ginger.<BR>	 2. The emerald.<BR> E. सुपर्ण GARUḌA, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपर्णेय|सौपर्णेयः
सौपर्णेय m. (-यः) GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. सुपर्णा the<BR>mother of this being, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौप्तिक|सौप्तिकं
सौप्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Connected with or relating to sleep, somnolent,<BR>somniferous, &c.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Nocturnal combat, an attack on sleeping<BR>men.<BR> E. सुप्त sleep, (or the hour of sleep,) and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौबल|सौबलः
सौबल m. (-लः) An epithet of ŚAKUNI.<BR>	 f. (-ली) An epithet of GĀNDHĀRI,<BR>the wife of DHRITARĀSHTRA; also सौबलेयी in the last sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभ|सौभं
सौभ n. (-भं) The city of HARIŚCHANDRA suspended in mid-air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभग|सौभगं
सौभग n. (-गं)<BR>	 1. Good luck.<BR>	 2. Prosperity, wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभद्र|सौभद्रः
सौभद्र m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. The son of SUBHADRĀ.<BR>	 2. A war occasioned by the<BR>carrying off of SUBHADRA.<BR> E. सुभद्रा sister to KṚṢṆA, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभद्रेय|सौभद्रेयः
सौभद्रेय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Beleric myrobalan.<BR>	 2. ABHIMANYU, the son of<BR>SUBHADRĀ.<BR> E. सुभद्रा the sister of KṚṢṆA, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभागिनेय|सौभागिनेयः
सौभागिनेय m. (-यः) The son of an auspicious mother.<BR> E. सुभगा an auspi-<BR>cious mother, ढक् aff., and इनङ् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्य|सौभाग्यं
सौभाग्य n. (-ग्यं)<BR>	 1. Auspiciousness, good fortune.<BR>	 2. Blessednes.<BR>	 3.<BR>Beauty, grace, charm.<BR>	 4. Auspicious state of wife-hood, (as opposed<BR>to widow-hood.)<BR>	 5. Congratulation.<BR>	 6. The fourth of the astronomical<BR>Yogas.<BR>	 7. Borax.<BR>	 8. Red-lead.<BR> E. सुभग auspicious, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यतन्तु|सौभाग्यतंतु|सौभाग्यतन्तुः
सौभाग्यतन्तु m. (-न्तुः) Marriage-string, (cast round the neck of the<BR>bride by the bridegroom at the time of wedding and worn till<BR>widow-hood.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यतृतीया
सौभाग्यतृतीया f. (-या) The third day of the light-half of Bhādrapada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यदेवता
सौभाग्यदेवता f. (-ता) A tutelary deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यवत्|सौभाग्यवन्त्
सौभाग्यवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Auspicious, fortunate.<BR> E. सौभाम्य, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यवत्ता
सौभाग्यवत्ता f. (-त्ता) Auspiciousness, prosperity.<BR> E. तल्, added to the<BR>last: also with त्व, सौभाग्यवत्त्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यवायन
सौभाग्यवायन n. (-नं) An auspicious offering of sweetmeat, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाञ्जन|सौभाञ्जनः
सौभाञ्जन m. (-नः) A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga:) see शोभाञ्जन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभिक|सौभिकः
सौभिक m. (-कः) A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभ्रात्र|सौभ्रात्रं
सौभ्रात्र n. (-त्रं) Brotherhood, fraternity.<BR> E. सु good, भ्रातृ a brother, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस
सौमनस mfn. (-सः-सा or -सी-सं)<BR>	 1. Floral, flowery, relating to flowers.<BR>	 2.<BR>Agreeable, pleasing.<BR>	 n. (-स)<BR>	 1. Benevolence.<BR>	 2. Pleasure.<BR> E. सुमनस्<BR>content, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनसा
सौमनसा f. (-सा) The outer skin of the nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्य|सौमनस्यं
सौमनस्य n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Enjoyment, satisfaction.<BR>	 2. A particular offering of<BR>flowers made at a ŚRĀDDHA.<BR> E. सुमनस् content, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्यायनी
सौमनस्यायनी f. (-नी) The blossom of the great-flowered jasmine.<BR> E. सुमनस<BR>the plant, फक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमायन|सौमायनः
सौमायन m. (-नः) An epithet of BUDHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमिक
सौमिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Lunar, relating to SOMA or the moon.<BR>	 2.<BR>Performed with the Sarcostema juice, relating to it, &c.<BR>	 f. (-की) A<BR>sacrifice performed on the day of full-moon.<BR> E. सोम the moon, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमित्र|सौमित्रः
सौमित्र m. (-त्रः) LAKSHMANA, the younger brother of RĀMA.<BR> E. सुमित्रा<BR>the wife of DAŚARATHA, and mother of this prince, and अण् aff.;<BR>also with इञ् aff., सौमित्रि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेचक|सौमेचकं
सौमेचक n. (-कं) Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेधिक|सौमेधिकः
सौमेधिक m. (-कः) A sage, a seer, one possessing supernatural know-<BR>ledge or power.<BR> E. सु excellent, मेधा apprehension, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेरुक|सौमेरुकं
सौमेरुक n. (-कं) Gold.<BR>	 f. (-की) Born or produced from SUMERU.<BR> E. सुमेरु<BR>the mountain, with कन् added, and अण् aff. of origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्य|सौम्यः
सौम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या or -मी-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Handsome, pleasing.<BR>	 2. Mild, gentle,<BR>placid.<BR>	 3. Sacred or belonging to SOMA or the moon, 4. Auspi-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">Page806-b+ 60</a>]<BR>cious.<BR>	 m. (-म्यः)<BR>	 1. BUDHA, regent of MERCURY, and son of SOMA<BR>or the moon.<BR>	 2. One of the nine Khaṇḍas or divisions of the<BR>known continent.<BR>	 3. A term applied to a pupil when addressing<BR>instruction to one.<BR>	 4. (In anatomy,) The blood before it receives<BR>the red particles, the serum.<BR>	 5. The gastric juice.<BR>	 m. plu. (-म्याः)<BR>1. Name of a class of Pitṛs or Manes.<BR>	 2. Name of the five stars in<BR>Orion's head.<BR>	 f. (-म्या)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Heart-pea.<BR>	 3. The Abrus precatorius.<BR>	 4. The moon-plant, (Sarcos-<BR>tema acida.)<BR>	 5. Zedoary, Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>	 6. Arabian jasmine.<BR>E. सोम the moon, ण्यत् or यत् aff., or ड्यण् aff., when the word takes<BR>ङीप् in the feminine form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यकृच्छ्र|सौम्यकृच्छ्रः
सौम्यकृच्छ्र mn. (-च्छ्रः-च्छ्रं) A religious penance, subsisting for five days,<BR>severally, on sesamum after expression, the water of boiled-rice,<BR>butter-milk mixed with water, water, and parched grain, and fast-<BR>ing on the sixth day.<BR> E. सौम्य relating to the moon, कृच्छ्र penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यगन्धी|सौम्यगंधी
सौम्यगन्धी f. (-न्धी) The Indian white rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यग्रह|सौम्यग्रहः
सौम्यग्रह m. (-हः) An auspicious planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यत्व
सौम्यत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Beauty.<BR>	 2. Gentleness, placidity.<BR> E. त्व added to सौम्य;<BR>also with तल्, सौम्यता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यधातु|सौम्यधातुः
सौम्यधातु m. (-तुः) Phlegm, the phlegmatic humour.<BR> E. सौम्य lunar, and धातु element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यनामन्
सौम्यनामन् Adj. Having an agreeable name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यवार|सौम्यवारः
सौम्यवार m. (-रः) Wednesday; also सौम्यवासर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौर|सौरः
सौर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Solar.<BR>	 2. Celestial.<BR>	 3. Spirituous.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>The planet SATURN.<BR>	 2. A month, consisting of thirty rising and<BR>settings of the sun, a solar month.<BR>	 3. A solar day, whilst the sun<BR>is in one degree of the ecliptic.<BR>	 4. A worshipper of the sun.<BR>	 f. (-री)<BR>The wife of the sun.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Name of a collection of hymns,<BR>(taken from the Rig-Veda,) addressed to ŚURYA.<BR> E. सुर a deity, &c.,<BR>or सूर the sun, अण् aff.; or सूर्य्य the sun, ङीष् aff. for the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरथ|सौरथः
सौरथ m. (-थः) A hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरनक्त|सौरनक्तं
सौरनक्त n. (-क्तं) A particular religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ|सौरभं
सौरभ n. (-भं)<BR>	 1. Fragrance.<BR>	 2. Saffron.<BR>	 3. Myrrh.<BR>	 f. (-भी) Fragrant. E.<BR>सुरभि fragrant, अच् or अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभेय|सौरभेयः
सौरभेय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. An ox.<BR>	 f. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A cow.<BR>	 2. The daughter of Surabhi;<BR>also सौरभी.<BR> E. सुरभी the cow of plenty, (the parent cow,) and ढक्<BR>aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ्य|सौरभ्यं|सौरभ्यः
सौरभ्य n. (-भ्यं)<BR>	 1. Pleasingness, agreeableness, beauty.<BR>	 2. Fragrance,<BR>odour.<BR>	 3. Fame, character, reputation of learning or other merit.<BR>m. (-भ्यः) KUVERA.<BR> E. सुरभि fragrant, pleasing, and ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरमास|सौरमासः
सौरमास m. (-सः) A solar month, (consisting of thirty risings and<BR>settings of the sun.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसेय|सौरसेयः
सौरसेय m. (-यः) A name of SKANDA.<BR> E. सुरसा DURGĀ, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसैन्धव|सौरसैंधव|सौरसैन्धवः
सौरसैन्धव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Gangetic, relating or belonging to the river<BR>Ganges.<BR>	 m. (-वः) A horse of the sun.<BR> E. सुरसिन्धु the river of the<BR>gods, and अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराज्य|सौराज्यं
सौराज्य n. (-ज्यं) Good government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्र|सौराष्ट्रः
सौराष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः) Surāt.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ट्री) A fragrant sort of earth.<BR>	 n. (-ष्ट्रं)<BR>Bell metal.<BR>	 f. (-ष्ट्रा or -ष्ट्री) Relating to the district of SURĀSHTRA.<BR>E. सु good or much, राष्ट्र dominion, अञ् aff.; or सुराष्ट्र the same,<BR>अण् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रक|सौराष्ट्रकं|सौराष्ट्रकः
सौराष्ट्रक n. (-कं) A sort of white or bell metal.<BR> E. सौराष्ट्र Surāt, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रिक|सौराष्ट्रिकं
सौराष्ट्रिक n. (-कं) A sort of poison, (that of a kind of snake according<BR>to some, but according to others, a vegetable or mineral.)<BR> E. सुराष्ट्र<BR>the country, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरि|सौरिः
सौरि m. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. SATURN.<BR>	 2. The Asana tree.<BR>	 3. KARṆA.<BR>	 4. SUGRĪVA. E.<BR>सूर the sun, and इञ् aff. of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरिक|सौरिकः
सौरिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Celestial.<BR>	 2. Spirituous, vinous.<BR>	 3. Due for<BR>spirits, (such as money.)<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Heaven, paradise.<BR>	 2. A<BR>vendor of spirituous liquor.<BR>	 3. SATURN.<BR> E. सुर a deity, or सुरा wine,<BR>and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=806-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरिरत्न|सौरिरत्नं
सौरिरत्न n. (-त्नं) Sapphire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरीय|सौरीयं
सौरीय f. (-यी) Adj.<BR>	 1. Solar.<BR>	 2. Suitable to the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौर्य्य|सौर्य
सौर्य्य f. (-र्य्या) Adj. Solar, belonging to the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालभ्य
सालभ्य n. (-भ्य)<BR>	 1. Easiness of attainment.<BR>	 2. Feasibility, facility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौल्विक|सौल्विकः
सौल्विक m. (-कः) A copper-smith; more usually शौल्विक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौव|सौवं
सौव n. (-वं) An edict, &c., in general.<BR>	 f. (-वी)<BR>	 1. Relating to one's own<BR>property.<BR>	 2. Belonging to heaven.<BR> E. स्व own, proper, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवग्रामिक|सौवग्रामिकं
सौवग्रामिक Adj. Belonging to one's own village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर|सौवरं
सौवर, mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Produced or existing in a note of music, relating<BR>to it, &c.<BR>	 2. Treating of accents.<BR>	 3. Relating to sound.<BR> E. स्वर a<BR>note, &c., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्च्चल|सौवर्चल|सौवर्च्चलं
सौवर्च्चल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. Sachal-salt.<BR>	 2. Natron, alkali.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Coming from<BR>the Suvarchala country.<BR> E. सुवर्च्चल a district, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्ण|सौवर्णं|सौवर्णः
सौवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्ण)<BR>	 1. Golden, made or consisting of gold.<BR>	 2.<BR>Weighing a Suvarṇa.<BR> E. सुवर्ण gold, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्णभेदिनी
सौवर्णभेदिनी f. (-नी) A plant, commonly Priyangu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवस्तिक|सौवस्तिकः
सौवस्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Salutatory, benedictory.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A family<BR>Brāhman or priest.<BR> E. स्वस्ति a term of salutation, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवाध्यायिक
सौवाध्यायिक f. (-की) Belonging to sacred study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवास्तव|सौवास्तवः
सौवास्तव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं) Pleasantly situated, erected on a good site. E.<BR>सु good, वास्तु a site, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौविद|सौविदः
सौविद m. (-दः) A guard or attendant of the women's apartments. E.<BR>सुविद the same, and अण् pleonasm; or सुविद् a woman, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौविदल्ल|सौविदल्लः
सौविदल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A guard or attendant of the woman's apartments. E.<BR>सुविद्ल्ला a female, अण् aff.; or सुविदन् a king, ला to get or have,<BR>सुविदल्ल a harem, and अण् aff.; also with कन् added, सौविदल्लक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीर|सौवीरं|सौवीरः
सौवीर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The fruit of the jujube.<BR>	 2. Antimony.<BR>	 3. Sour-gruel.<BR>m. (-रः) A district, in the west of India, connected with the<BR>country along the Indus.<BR>	 m. plu. (-राः) The people of SUVIRA. E.<BR>सुवीर the country so called, and अण् pleonasm or aff. of derivation;<BR>also with यञ् aff. सीवीर्य्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीरक|सौवीरकं|सौवीरकः
सौवीरक m. (-कः) The jujube tree.<BR>	 n. (-कं) Sour barley-gruel.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीराञ्जन|सौवीरांजन|सौवीराञ्जनं
सौवीराञ्जन n. (-नं) A kind of antimony or collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीर्य्य|सौवीर्य|सौवीर्यं
सौवीर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Great heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौशील्य|सौशील्यं
सौशील्य n. (-लं) Excellence of disposition, good morals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौश्रवस|सौश्रवसं
सौश्रवस n. (-स) Celebrity, renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौष्ठव|सौष्ठवं
सौष्ठव n. (-वं)<BR>	 1. Excess, exceedingness, much.<BR>	 2. Excellence.<BR>	 3. A<BR>part of a drama.<BR>	 4. Lightness, fleetness, suppleness.<BR>	 5. Cleverness.<BR>E. सुष्ठु excellent, &c., and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौस्नातिक|सौस्नातिकः
सौस्नातिक m. (-कः) One who asks whether an ablution has been auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहार्द्द|सौहार्द|सौहार्दः|सौहार्द्दं|सौहार्द्दः
सौहार्द्द n. (-र्द्दं) Friendship.<BR>	 m. (-र्द्दः) The son of a friend.<BR> E. सुहृद् a<BR>friend, अण् aff., both vowels changed; also सौहार्द्य. E. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहार्द्य|सौहार्द्यं
सौहार्द्य n. (-र्द्यं) Friendship.<BR> E. सुहृद् a friend, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहित्य|सौहित्यं
सौहित्य n. (-त्य)<BR>	 1. Satiety, satisfaction.<BR>	 2. Fulness, completion.<BR>	 3.<BR>Kindness.<BR> E. सुहित satisfied, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृद|सौहृदं
सौहृद n. (-दं) Friendship.<BR> E. सुहृद a friend, अण् aff.; also from सुहृदय,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृद्य|सौहृद्यं
सौहृद्य n. (-द्यं) Friendship.<BR> E. सुहृद् a friend, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कद्
स्कद् (इ) स्कदि r. 1st cl. (-स्कन्दते)<BR>	 1. To leap, to jump.<BR>	 2. To inundate.<BR>	 3.<BR>To lift up.<BR>	 4. To shed or spill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द्|स्कंद्
स्कन्द् (इर) स्कन्दिर r. 1st cl. (स्कन्दति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To be dry or<BR>arid.<BR>	 3. To effuse or emit.<BR>	 4. To jump.<BR>	 5. To ascend.<BR>	 6. To<BR>burst out.<BR>	 7. To fall, to drop 8. To perish. With अव prefixed, To<BR>assail, to assault, to besiege. With आ, To assail. With परि, To<BR>spring about. With प्र, To spring forward. r. 10th cl. (स्कन्दयति-ते)<BR>To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्द|स्कंद|स्कंदः|स्कन्दः
स्कन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. SKANDA, or KĀRTIKEYA, the son of ŚIVA, and<BR>military deity of the Hindus.<BR>	 2. A king, a prince.<BR>	 3. The body.<BR>	 4.<BR>The bank of a river.<BR>	 5. A clever or learned man.<BR> E. स्कन्द् to go,<BR>(to fly before whom; the enemies of the gods,) and अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दक|स्कंदक|स्कंदकः|स्कन्दकः
स्कन्दक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. One who leaps.<BR>	 2. A soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दन|स्कंदन|स्कंदनं|स्कन्दनं
स्कन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Going, moving.<BR>	 2. Purging, looseness.<BR>	 3. Effusion.<BR>4. Suppressing bleeding by cold applications.<BR>	 5. Drying up. E.<BR>स्कन्द् to go, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दयत्
स्कन्दयत् mfn. (-यत्-यन्ती-यत्)<BR>	 1. Going.<BR>	 2. Effusing, pouring out.<BR> E. स्कन्द् to effuse, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दषष्ठी|स्कंदषष्ठी
स्कन्दषष्ठी f. (-ष्ठी) A festival in honour of Kārtikeya held on the sixth<BR>day of Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्दित
स्कन्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Going.<BR>	 2. Effused, shed, emitted.<BR> E. स्कन्द् to emit, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्ध|स्कंध|स्कंधः|स्कन्धः
स्कन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. The shoulder, the head of the humerus.<BR>	 2. The body.<BR>3. The trunk of a tree.<BR>	 4. A king, a prince.<BR>	 5. A sort of metre.<BR>	 6.<BR>A multitude, a quantity.<BR>	 7. War, battle.<BR>	 8. Any article essential<BR>to the coronation of a king, as a jar filled with holy water, a<BR>parasol, a Chowri, &c.<BR>	 9. Part of an army or a form of array.<BR>	 10.<BR>Any one of five branches of human or mundane knowledge, or<BR>objects of understanding.<BR>	 11. A road, a way.<BR>	 12. A heron.<BR>	 13. An<BR>engagement, an agreement.<BR>	 14. A wise old man.<BR>	 15. A learned<BR>man, a teacher.<BR>	 16. Match or equality in the humps of a pair of<BR>draft oxen.<BR>	 17. The five objects of sense, or form, taste, smell, &c.<BR>18. A book, a section, a chapter.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. A branch.<BR>	 2. A creeper.<BR>E. क the head, and धा to hold, aff. क, and सुट् initial augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धचाप|स्कंधचाप|स्कन्धचापः
स्कन्धचाप m. (-पः) A sort of yoke for carrying burdens by a sling<BR>attached to either end.<BR> E. स्कन्ध the shoulder, and चाप a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धज|स्कन्धजः
स्कन्धज m. (-जः) A tree which grows from a principal stem.<BR> E. स्कन्ध the<BR>trunk of a tree, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धतरु|स्कंधतरु|स्कन्धतरुः
स्कन्धतरु m. (-रुः) The cocoanut-tree.<BR> E. स्कन्ध a stem, and तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धदेश|स्कंधदेश|स्कन्धदेशः
स्कन्धदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. The withers of an elephant, or part where the<BR>rider sits.<BR>	 2. The shoulder.<BR> E. स्कन्ध the shoulder, देश part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धनिर्वाण|स्कंधनिर्वाण
स्कन्धनिर्वाण n. (-णं) The annihilation of the elements of being, (with<BR>Buddhists.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धफल|स्कंधफल|स्कन्धफलः
स्कन्धफल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. The cocoanut tree.<BR>	 2. The Vilwa or Bel.<BR>	 3. The<BR>glomerous-fig.<BR> E. स्कन्ध the trunk, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धबन्धना|स्कंधबंधना
स्कन्धबन्धना f. (-ना) A sort of fennel, (Anethum panmorium.)<BR> E. स्कन्ध the<BR>stem, बन्धन a binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धमल्लक|स्कंधमल्लक|स्कन्धमल्लकः
स्कन्धमल्लक m. (-कः) A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धरुह|स्कंधरुह|स्कन्धरुहः
स्कन्धरुह m. (-हः) The Indian fig-tree.<BR> E. स्कन्ध a principal stem, रुह what-grows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धवाह|स्कंधवाह|स्कन्धवाहः
स्कन्धवाह m. (-हः) An ox of burden.<BR> E. स्कन्ध the shoulder, वाह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धवाहक|स्कंधवाहक|स्कन्धवाहकः
स्कन्धवाहक m. (-कः) An ox of burden, a pack-bullock.<BR> E. कन् added to<BR>the last; or स्कन्ध the shoulder, with वह् to bear, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धशाखा|स्कंधशाखा
स्कन्धशाखा f. (-खा) The forked or principal branch, (which issues from<BR>the upper stem,) of a tree.<BR> E. स्कन्ध the trunk, and शास्वा a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धशृङ्ग|स्कंधशृंग|स्कन्धशृङ्गः
स्कन्धशृङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A buffalo.<BR> E. स्कन्ध the shoulder, and शृङ्ग the horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धस्|स्कंधस्
स्कन्धस् n. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. The shoulder.<BR>	 2. The trunk of a tree.<BR> E. स्कदि to go<BR>or collect, aff. असुन्, and द changed to ध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धस्कन्ध|स्कंधस्कंध|स्कन्धस्कन्धः
स्कन्धस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) Every shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धाग्नि|स्कन्धाग्निः
स्कन्धाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) The fire on the stem of a tree in consequence<BR>attrition.<BR> E. स्कन्ध the trunk of a tree, and अग्नि fire: see the next<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धानल|स्कन्धानलः
स्कन्धानल m. (-लः) The fire on the stem of a tree or any large piece<BR>timber in consequence of attrition.<BR> E. स्कन्ध the trunk of a tree, अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धावार|स्कंधावार|स्कन्धावारः
स्कन्धावार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. An army, or a division of it attached to the person<BR>of the king.<BR>	 2. A royal capital.<BR>	 3. A camp.<BR> E. स्कन्ध a king or an<BR>army, and आङ् before वृ to screen or guard, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धिक|स्कंधिक|स्कंधिकः|स्कन्धिकः
स्कन्धिक m. (-कः) An ox of burden.<BR> E. स्कन्ध the shoulder, and ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धिन्|स्कंधिन्
स्कन्धिन् m. (-न्धी)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. An ox of burden.<BR>	 f. (-न्धिनी)<BR>	 1. Having<BR>shoulders.<BR>	 2. Having branches.<BR> E. स्कन्ध a stem, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धोपनेय
स्कन्धोपनेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be carried on the shoulders.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>form of peace-offering, in which fruit or grain is presented as<BR>mark of submission.<BR> E. स्कन्ध, and उपनेय to be conveyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्न|स्कन्नं
स्कन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं)<BR>	 1. Fallen, fallen down or from.<BR>	 2. Oozed, trickled<BR>out or down.<BR>	 3. Emitted, sprinkled.<BR>	 4. Gone.<BR>	 5. Dried up.<BR> E. स्कन्द्<BR>to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कभ्
स्कभ् (इ) स्कभि r. 1st cl. (स्कम्भते) r. 9th and 5th cls. (स्कभ्राति-स्कभ्रीते-स्कभो-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">Page808-a+ 60</a>]<BR>स्कम्नुते)<BR>	 1. To stop or hinder, to impede, to block, to obstruct, &c.<BR>2. To be dull or stupid.<BR>	 3. To create.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=807-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कम्भ|स्कंभ|स्कंभः|स्कम्भः
स्कम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. Support, prop.<BR>	 2. The Supreme being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कम्मन
स्कम्मन n. (-नं) The act of supporting, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कान्द|स्कांद|स्कान्दं
स्कान्द f. (-न्दी) Adj.<BR>	 1. Relating to SKANDA.<BR>	 2. Relating to Śiva.<BR>	 n. (-न्दं)<BR>The Skanda-Purāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कु
स्कु r. 9th and 5th cls. (स्कुनाति-स्कुनीते-स्कुनोति-स्कुनुते)<BR>	 1. To go by leaps.<BR>	 2.<BR>To cover.<BR>	 3. To raise or lift.<BR>	 4. To approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुद्
स्कुद् (इ) स्कुदि r. 1st cl. (स्कुन्दते)<BR>	 1. To jump, to go by leaps or jumps.<BR>	 2.<BR>To raise, to lift up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुम्भ्|स्कुंभ्
स्कुम्भ् (उ) स्कुम्भु r. 5th and 9th cls. (स्कुभ्नोति-स्कुभ्राति)<BR>	 1. To stop or hinder.<BR>2. To be dull or insensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कोटिका
स्कोटिका f. (-का) A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खद्
स्खद् r. 1st cl. (स्खदते)<BR>	 1. To defeat, to discomfit.<BR>	 2. To cut.<BR>	 3. To make<BR>firm.<BR>	 4. To destroy, to hurt or kill.<BR>	 5. To fatigue, to exhaust.<BR>	 6.<BR>To eat, to taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खदन|स्खदनं
स्खदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Defeating, discomfiting.<BR>	 2. Injuring, hurting, killing.<BR>3. Cutting.<BR>	 4. Harassing.<BR> E. स्खद् to defeat, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खल्
स्खल् r. 1st cl. (स्खलति)<BR>	 1. To move, to go.<BR>	 2. To slip, to stumble or fall.<BR>3. To gather, to collect.<BR>	 4. To totter, to waver.<BR>	 5. To fall or<BR>deviate from the right course.<BR>	 6. To err, to blunder.<BR>	 7. To<BR>stammer, to falter, to lisp.<BR>	 8. To drip, to trickle.<BR>	 9. To disappear.<BR>With प्र, To jolt, to jostle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलत्
स्खलत् mfn. (-लन्-लन्ती-लत्) Stumbling, tripping, (either in motion,<BR>conduct, or speech.)<BR> E. स्खल् to stumble, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलद्वाक्य
स्खलद्वाक्य mfn. (-क्यः-क्या-क्यं) Blundering, making mistakes in speaking.<BR>E. स्खलत्, वाक्य speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलन्मति
स्खलन्मति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Erring in judgment, foolish.<BR> E. स्खलत्, मति understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलन|स्खलनं
स्खलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Stumbling, slipping, tripping.<BR>	 2. Stumbling or falling<BR>from virtue.<BR>	 3. Tripping in speech, making a mistake or blunder<BR>in speech or pronunciation.<BR>	 4. Knocking or falling together,<BR>shock, collision.<BR>	 5. Striking or rubbing one thing against another.<BR>6. Dropping, dripping.<BR> E. स्खल् to go, to drop, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलित|स्खलितं
स्खलित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Slipped, fallen.<BR>	 2. Gone.<BR>	 3. Shaken, agitated,<BR>disturbed.<BR>	 4. Shaking, wavering, unsteady, (literally or figurative-<BR>ly.)<BR>	 5. Drunk.<BR>	 6. Stuttering, hesitating, (in speech.)<BR>	 7. Dropped,<BR>effused, emitted.<BR>	 8. Trickling down.<BR>	 9. Interrupted, stopped.<BR>	 10.<BR>Confounded.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Circumvention, stratagem, (in war.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Falling, tumbling.<BR>	 3. Falling or deviating from virtue or truth.<BR>4. Fault, error, sin.<BR>	 5. Deceit, treachery.<BR> E. स्खल् to go, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलितसुभगम्
स्खलितसुभगम् Ind. Dashing or flowing along in a charming manner,<BR>(said of a stream.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्
स्तन् r. 1st cl. (स्तनति) r. 10th cl. (-स्तनयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sound, to reverberate.<BR>2. To groan, to sigh, to breathe hard.<BR>	 3. To thunder, to roar<BR>aloud. With नि, 1. To sigh.<BR>	 2. To bewail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन|स्तनः
स्तन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The female bosom or breast.<BR>	 2. An udder or dug of any<BR>female animal.<BR> E. स्तन् to sound, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनकुद्मल
स्तनकुद्मल n. (-लं) The female breast.<BR> E. स्तन, and कुद्मल a bud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनतट|स्तनतटः
स्तनतट mn. (-टः-टं) The slope of the breasts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनन|स्तननं
स्तनन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sound, noise in general.<BR>	 2. The grumbling of clouds.<BR>3. Breathing hard, groaning, (as a person in pain.)<BR> E. स्तन् to sound,<BR>aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्धय
स्तन्धय mf. (-यः-या- or यी) An infant, one at the breast.<BR>	 m. (-यः) An<BR>infant, a suckling.<BR>	 f. (-यी) Sucking at the breast.<BR> E. स्तन the<BR>breast, धेट् to drink, aff. खश्, मुम् aug. |<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तप
स्तप mf. (-पः-पा) An infant at the breast.<BR> E. स्तन the breast, and प who drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनपान
स्तनपान n. (-नं) Sucking of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभर
स्तभर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A man with a breast like a woman's 2. Heaviness<BR>or bulk of the female breasts.<BR> E. स्तन a pap, भर who possesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तण्डल
स्तण्डल n. (-लं) The female breast.<BR> E. स्तन, and मण्डल a globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनमुख|स्तनमुखः
स्तनमुख n. (-खं) A nipple.<BR> E. स्तन the breast, and मुख point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनयित्नु|स्तनयित्नुः
स्तनयित्नु m. (-त्नुः)<BR>	 1. A cloud.<BR>	 2. Thunder, the muttering of clouds.<BR>3. Lightning.<BR>	 4. Sickness.<BR>	 5. Death.<BR>	 6. A kind of grass.<BR> E. स्तन् to<BR>sound, in the tenth cl., इत्नुच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनवृन्त|स्तनवृंत|स्तनवृन्तः
स्तनवृन्त m. (-न्तः) A nipple.<BR> E. स्तन the breast, and कृन्त a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनशिखा
स्तनशिखा f. (-खा) A nipple.<BR> E. स्तन the breast, and शिखा the crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनांशुक
स्तनांशुक n. (-कं) A cloth covering the bosom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनाग्र|स्तनाग्रं|स्तनाग्रः
स्तनाग्र n. (-ग्रं) A nipple. स्तन the breast, and अग्र point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनाङ्गराग|स्तनांगराग|स्तनाङ्गरागः
स्तनाङ्गराग m. (-गः) Paint or pigment on the breasts of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनान्तर|स्तनांतर|स्तनान्तरं
स्तनान्तर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. The heart, or its site, placed however immediately<BR>under the centre bone of the sternum.<BR>	 2. The space between the<BR>two breasts.<BR>	 3. A mark on the breast, indicative of future widow-<BR>hood.<BR> E. स्तन the breast, अन्तर interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनाभोग|स्तनाभोगः
स्तनाभोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. A man with a large bosom, or one like a female's.<BR>2. The circumference or orb of the breast.<BR>	 3. Fulness of the<BR>breast.<BR> E. स्तन a breast, and भोग who enjoys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनित|स्तनितं
स्तनित n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The rattling of thunder, the rumbling of thundering<BR>clouds.<BR>	 2. The noise of clapping the hands.<BR> E. स्तन् to sound, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्य|स्तन्यं
स्तन्य n. (-न्य) Milk, mother's milk.<BR> E. स्तन a breast, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्यत्याग|स्तन्यत्यागः
स्तन्यत्याग m. (-गः) Leaving off the mother's milk, weaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तबक|स्तबकः
स्तबक m. (-कः) Bunch, cluster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्ध|स्तब्धः
स्तब्ध mfn. (-ब्धः-ब्धा-ब्धं)<BR>	 1. Stopped, blocked, or shut up.<BR>	 2. Firm, hard,<BR>stiff, rigid.<BR>	 3. Stupid, dull, insensible.<BR>	 4. Paralyzed.<BR>	 5. Obstinate,<BR>stubborn, hard-hearted.<BR>	 6. Coarse.<BR> E. स्तभि to stop, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धकर्ण
स्तब्धकर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णी-र्णं) Having the ears erect, pricking up the ears.<BR>E. स्तब्ध, and कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धता
स्तब्धता f. (-ता) Rigidity, stupor, stubbornness; also with त्व, स्तब्धत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धरोमन्
स्तब्धरोमन् m. (-मा) A hog.<BR> E. स्तब्ध firm, रोमन् hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धलोचन
स्तब्धलोचन Adj. Having fixed or unwinking eyes, (as an, epithet of gods.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धि|स्तब्धिः
स्तब्धि f. (-ब्धिः or -ब्धी)<BR>	 1. Fixedness, hardness, rigidity.<BR>	 2. Firmness,<BR>immobility.<BR>	 3. Stupor, numbness.<BR>	 4. Obstinacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धीकरण
स्तब्धीकरण n. (-णं) Stiffening, making rigid, paralyzing.<BR> E. स्तब्ध, करण making, चिव aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धीकृत
स्तब्धीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stiffened, rigid, paralyzed.<BR> E. स्तब्ध, and कृत<BR>made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभ|स्तभः
स्तभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A goat.<BR>	 2. A ram. E. See स्तुभ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्ब|स्तंब|स्तंबः|स्तम्बः
स्तम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. A shrub, a plant that has no particular or decided<BR>stem.<BR>	 2. A clump of grass, a sheaf of corn, &c.<BR>	 3. The post to<BR>which an elephant is tied.<BR>	 4. A mountain.<BR>	 5. A bush, a thicket.<BR>6. Stupefaction, insensibility, (probably for स्तम्भ in this sense.)<BR>	 n.<BR>(-म्बं)<BR>	 1. A post, a pillar in general.<BR>	 2. Stupidity, insensibility.<BR>E. ष्ठा to stand or abide, अम्बच् Unādi aff., किच्च ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बकरि|स्तंबकरि|स्तम्बकरिः
स्तम्बकरि m. (-रिः) Corn or rice. Adj. Forming into cluster.<BR> E. स्तम्ब a<BR>cluster, कृ to make, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बकरिता|स्तंबकरिता
स्तम्बकरिता f. (-ता) Luxuriant growth, the state of thickening into sheaves or clusters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बकार|स्तम्बकारः
स्तम्बकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Making or forming a heap or cluster.<BR> E. स्तम्ब a<BR>cluster, कृ to make, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बघन|स्तंबघन|स्तम्बघनः
स्तम्बघन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A small hoe for weeding or eradicating clusters of<BR>gramineous plants.<BR>	 2. A sickle or instrument for cutting corn.<BR>3. A basket for holding the heads of wild-rice, &c., when cut. E.<BR>स्तम्ब a cluster, (of stalks,) a sheaf, हन् to destroy, अप् aff.; also<BR>with कच् aff., स्तम्बघ्न; in each case घ being substituted for ह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बघ्न|स्तंबघ्न|स्तम्बघ्नः
स्तम्बघ्न mfn. (-घ्नः-घ्नी-घ्नं) Turf-destroying.<BR>	 m. (-घ्नः) A hoe or sickle, &c.:<BR>see the last; also स्तम्बघात ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बपुर्
स्तम्बपुर् f. (-पूः) A city so named; also known as TĀMRALIPTA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बहनन|स्तम्बहननः
स्तम्बहनन nf. (-नं-नी) A hoe or sickle for eradicating weeds, cutting or<BR>reaping corn, &c.: see स्तम्बघन.<BR> E. स्तम्ब a cluster, a sheaf, and<BR>हनन destroying; also स्तम्बहन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बेरम|स्तंबेरम|स्तंबेरमः|स्तम्बेरमः
स्तम्बेरम mf. (-मः-मा) An elephant.<BR> E. स्तम्बे in a clump, (of high grass,) रम् to sport, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भ्|स्तंभ्
स्तम्भ् (उ) स्तम्भु r. 5th. cl. (स्तभ्नोति) r. 9th. cl. (स्तभ्नाति)<BR>	 1. To stop, to<BR>block, to hinder.<BR>	 2. To be stupid or insensible; also उम्भ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=808-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भ|स्तंभ|स्तंभः|स्तम्भः
स्तम्भ m. (-म्भः)<BR>	 1. A post, a pillar, a column.<BR>	 2. A stalk, a stem.<BR>	 3.<BR>Stupidity, insensibility.<BR>	 4. Stupefaction from fear, joy, grief, &c.<BR>5. Coldness, (corporeally,) want of feeling or excitability, paraly-<BR>sis.<BR>	 6. The suppression of any faculty by magical means.<BR>	 7.<BR>Hindrance, obstruction.<BR>	 8. Fixedness, rigidity.<BR>	 9. Prop, support,<BR>fulcrum.<BR>	 10. Suppressing, curbing.<BR> E. ष्टभि to stop, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकर|स्तंभकर|स्तम्भकरः
स्तम्भकर m. (-रः) A fence, a railing, &c. Adj.<BR>	 1. Paralyzing.<BR>	 2. Obstruct-<BR>ing.<BR> E. स्तम्भ opposing, and कर making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकरण|स्तंभकरण
स्तम्भकरण n. (-णं) Cause of obstruction or impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकिन्|स्तंभकिन्
स्तम्भकिन् m. (-की) A musical instrument, covered with leather.<BR> E. स्तम्भक<BR>stopping, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भन|स्तंभन|स्तंभनं|स्तम्भनं|स्तम्भनः
स्तम्भन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Stopping, hindering, obstruction.<BR>	 2. Suppression of<BR>any of the bodily faculties by magical incantations.<BR>	 3. Stopping<BR>the flow of blood, &c.<BR>	 4. Any article so employed, a styptic,<BR>an astringent.<BR>	 5. Stunning, benumbing.<BR>	 6. Propping, supporting.<BR>m. (-नः) An epithet of one of the five arrows of KĀMADEVA. E.<BR>ष्टभि to stop, aff. युच् or ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भपूजा|स्तंभपूजा
स्तम्भपूजा f. (-जा) Worship of the posts of the temporary pavilions erect-<BR>ed for marriages or other festive occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भित|स्तंभित|स्तम्भितः
स्तम्भित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Stupefied, paralyzed.<BR> E. स्तम्भ् to be stupid, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भोत्कीर्ण|स्तंभोत्कीर्ण
स्तम्भोत्कीर्ण Adj. Carved out of a post or wood, (as a statue.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तर|स्तरः
स्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Who or what spreads, extends, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>layer, a stratum.<BR>	 2. A bed.<BR> E. स्तृ to spread, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरण|स्तरणं
स्तरण n. (-णं) The act of spreading or strewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरि
स्तरि(री)मन् m. (-मा) A bed, a couch.<BR> E. स्तृ to spread, इमनिच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरी
स्तरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. Smoke, vapour.<BR>	 2. A heifer.<BR>	 3. A barren cow.<BR> E. स्तृ to<BR>cover, Unādi aff. ई ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तव|स्तवः
स्तव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Praise, eulogium, panegyric.<BR>	 2. Celebrating as a hero<BR>or hymning as a deity.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवक|स्तवकः
स्तवक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A cluster of blossoms, a nosegay.<BR>	 2. A multitude in<BR>general.<BR>	 3. Praise, eulogium.<BR>	 4. A panegyrist, a praiser.<BR>	 5. The<BR>chapter of a book.<BR>	 f. (-विका) Praising.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, aff. वुन्; or<BR>स्था to stay, अवक Unādi aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवकाचित
स्तवकाचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) In blossom, covered with blossoms.<BR> E. स्तवक, आचित heaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवन|स्तवनं
स्तवन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Praising, praise.<BR>	 2. A hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवरक|स्तवरकः
स्तवरक m. (-कः) A fence, a railing, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवेय्य|स्तवेय्यः
स्तवेय्य m. (-य्यः) INDRA.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, एय्य Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ताव|स्तावः
स्ताव m. (-वः) Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तावक|स्तावकः
स्तावक m. (-कः) A praiser, a panegyrist.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमित|स्तिमितः
स्तिमित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Wet, moist.<BR>	 2. Unsteady, shaking, wavering,<BR>(literally or figuratively.)<BR>	 3. Still, steady, rigid, dull.<BR>	 4. Benumbed,<BR>paralyzed.<BR>	 5. Tender, soft.<BR>	 6. Gratified, pleased.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Moisture.<BR>E. ष्टिम् to be moist, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमितत्व|स्तिमितत्वं
स्तिमितत्व n. (-त्वं) Absence of motion, stillness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमितवायु|स्तिमितवायुः
स्तिमितवायु m. (-युः) Still air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिम्भि|स्तिम्भिः
स्तिम्भि m. (-म्भिः)<BR>	 1. The ocean.<BR>	 2. Air.<BR>	 3. An obstacle, an impediment. E.<BR>स्तम्भ् to stop, Unādi aff. इ, and the radical vowel changed to इ; or<BR>ष्टिम् to moist, इन् aff., भुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तीर्व्वि|स्तीर्वि|स्तीर्विः|स्तीर्व्विः
स्तीर्व्वि m. (-र्व्विः)<BR>	 1. A priest versed in the Yajur-Veda.<BR>	 2. Grass.<BR>	 3. Sky.<BR>4. Water.<BR>	 5. Blood.<BR>	 6. INDRA.<BR> E. स्तॄ to cover, Unādi aff. क्विन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुक|स्तुकः
स्तुक m. (-कः) A collection of hair, a knot.<BR>	 f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A knot or braid<BR>of hair.<BR>	 2. A bunch of curly hair between the horns of a bull.<BR>	 3.<BR>Hip, thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत|स्तुतः
स्तुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Praised, panegyrised, hymned, glorified.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुति|स्तुतिः
स्तुति f. (-तिः) Praise, eulogy.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिपद
स्तुतिपद n. (-दं) An object of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिपाठक|स्तुतिपाठकः
स्तुतिपाठक m. (-कः) A bard, one who accompanies a chief or an army, to<BR>recite the titles and praises of the one, and to inspire the other<BR>by chanting martial exploits, &c.<BR> E. स्तुति praise, पाठक a reader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिवाद|स्तुतिवादः
स्तुतिवाद m. (-दः) A laudatory speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिव्रत|स्तुतिव्रतः
स्तुतिव्रत m. (-तः) A bard, a herald: see the last.<BR> E. स्तुति praise, and व्रत<BR>observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत्य|स्तुत्यः
स्तुत्य mfn. (-त्यः-त्या-त्यं) To be praised, laudable, praise-worthy.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, aff. क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुनक|स्तुनकः
स्तुनक m. (-कः) A goat.<BR> E. ष्ट्रु to praise, नकक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभ|स्तुभः
स्तुभ m. (-भः) A he-goat.<BR> E. ष्टुभ् to stop, aff. क; also read स्तभ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुम्भ्|स्तुंभ्
स्तुम्भ् (उ) स्तुम्भु r. 5th cl. (स्तुभ्रोति) r. 9th cl. (स्तुभ्राति)<BR>	 1. To stop.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>stupid.<BR>	 3. To expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुपेप्य
स्तुपेप्य n. (-प्यं) Excellence, preferableness, (in the language of the<BR>Vedas.)<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, क्सेप्य Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूप्
स्तूप् r. 4th cl. (स्तूप्यति) r. 10th cl. (स्तूपयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To heap, to pile, to<BR>collect.<BR>	 2. To erect; the form ष्टूप् is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूप|स्तूपः
स्तूप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. A heap, a pile of earth, &c.<BR>	 2. A funeral pile.<BR>	 3. A<BR>Buddhistic construction for keeping holy relics.<BR> E. ष्टूप् to heap,<BR>aff. अच्; or ष्टु to praise, पक् Unādi aff., and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूयमान
स्तूयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being praised.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृंह
स्तृंह r. 6th cl. (-स्तृंहति) To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
स्तृ r. 5th cl. (स्तृणीति स्तृणुते)<BR>	 1. To cover, to clothe, to spread on or<BR>over, to strew.<BR>	 2. To kill. (-स्तृणोति)<BR>	 1. To love.<BR>	 2. To protect. With<BR>वि prefixed, 1. To spread widely, to extend.<BR>	 2. To diffuse or<BR>prolix.<BR>	 3. To cover. With उप, To arrange. With परि, 1. To spread.<BR>2. To cover.<BR>	 3. To arrange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृक्ष्
स्तृक्ष् r. 1st. cl. (स्तृक्षति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृणत्
स्तृणत् mfn. (-णन्-णती-णत्) Strewing, spreading over or upon, covering.<BR> E. स्तृ to strew, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृति|स्तृतिः
स्तृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Expansion.<BR>	 2. Covering, clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृह्
स्तृह् (ऊ) स्तॄहू r. 6th cl. (-स्तृहति) To hurt, to kill; also स्तॄह् and ष्टृह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄ
स्तॄ r. 9th cl. (-स्तृणाति स्तृणीते) To clothe, to cover, to spread on or over<BR>more properly ष्टॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄह्
स्तॄह् (ऊ) स्तॄहू r. 6th cl. (स्तॄहति) To hurt or kill: see स्तृह् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेन्
स्तेन् r. 10th cl. (स्तेनयति-ते) To steal, to rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेन|स्तेनं|स्तेनः
स्तेन m. (-नः) A thief.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Thieving, stealing.<BR> E. स्तेन् to steal, aff. अच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेननिग्रह|स्तेननिग्रहः
स्तेननिग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. The restraining or punishment of thieves.<BR>	 2.<BR>Suppression of theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेप्
स्तेप् r. 10 cl. (-स्तेपयति-ते) To throw; also ष्टेप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेम|स्तेमः
स्तेम m. (-मः) Wetness, moisture.<BR> E. ष्टिम् to be wet, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेय|स्तेयं
स्तेय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. Theft, robbery.<BR>	 2. Anything stolen or liable to be<BR>stolen.<BR>	 3. Anything private.<BR> E. स्तेन् to steal, यत् aff.; the final न<BR>rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेयिन्
स्तेयिन् m. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A goldsmith.<BR>	 2. A thief.<BR> E. स्तेय theft, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैन|स्तैनं
स्तैन n. (-नं) Theft, robbery.<BR> E. स्तेन a thief, अण् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैन्य|स्तैन्यं|स्तैन्यः
स्तैन्य n. (-न्यं) Theft, robbery.<BR>	 m. (-न्यः) A thief.<BR> E. स्तेन् to steal, ष्यञ् or ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैमित्य|स्तैमित्यं
स्तैमित्य n. (-त्यं) Rigidity, numbness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोक|स्तोकः
स्तोक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Little, small.<BR>	 2. Low.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. The Chātaka.<BR>(Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR>	 2. A drop of water.<BR>	 3. A small portion.<BR>n. Adv. (-कं) A little.<BR> E. ष्टुच् to be clear or bright, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकक|स्तोककः
स्तोकक m. (-कः) The Chātaka, (Cuculus melanoleucos.)<BR> E. स्तोक<BR>drop of water, and कै to sound or cry, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोककाय
स्तोककाय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Diminutive, dwarfish.<BR> E. स्तोक, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकनम्र
स्तोकनम्र Adj. Slightly bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकशस्
स्तोकशस् Ind. Sparingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतव्य
स्तोतव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be praised, deserving or requiring praise.<BR>E. ष्टु to praise, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतृ
स्तोतृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Praising, a praiser, a panegyrist.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्र|स्तोत्रं
स्तोत्र n. (-त्रं) Praise, eulogium.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise, aff. ष्ट्रन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्रिय|स्तोत्रियः
स्तोत्रिय mf. (-यः-या) A particular kind of verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोभ|स्तोभं|स्तोभः
स्तोभ m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. Stopping, obstructing.<BR>	 2. Disrespect, contumely.<BR>	 3.<BR>A division of the Sāma-Veda.<BR>	 4. A stop, a pause.<BR>	 5. Hymn,<BR>praise.<BR> E. ष्टुभ् to stop, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम्
स्तोम् r. 10th cl. (स्तोमयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To praise, to eulogise.<BR>	 2. To flatter, to<BR>wheedle, to coax.<BR>	 3. To boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम|स्तोमः
स्तोम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Crooked, bent.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A heap, a number,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">Page810-a+ 60</a>]<BR>a multitude, a quantity.<BR>	 2. Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>	 3. A Soma libation.<BR>	 4.<BR>Praise, eulogium.<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. The head.<BR>	 2. Wealth.<BR>	 3. Grain, corn.<BR>4. Praise.<BR>	 5. A stick or staff bound with iron.<BR> E. ष्टु to praise,<BR>मन् Unādi aff.; or स्तोम् to praise, &c., aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=809-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम्य
स्तोम्य f. (-म्या) Laudable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौपिक|स्तौपिकं
स्तौपिक n. (-कं) The small broom carried by a Jaina ascetic.<BR> E. स्तूप a heap, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यान|स्त्यानं|स्त्यानः
स्त्यान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Bland, soft, unctuous, smooth.<BR>	 2. Thick,<BR>bulky, gross.<BR>	 3. Collecting into a mass.<BR>	 4. Sounding.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1.<BR>Thickness, grossness, massiveness.<BR>	 2. Idleness, sloth.<BR>	 3. Echo.<BR>	 4.<BR>Unctuousness.<BR>	 5. Nectar.<BR> E. स्त्यै to sound, क्त aff.; त changed to न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यायन|स्त्यायनं
स्त्यायन n. (-नं) Crowding together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यैन
स्त्यैन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A thief.<BR>	 2. Amrita, nectar.<BR> E. स्त्यै to sound, &c., इनच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यै
स्त्यै 1st cl. (-स्त्यायति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To spread about.<BR>	 3. To collect,<BR>to crowd; the form ष्ट्यै is irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्री
स्त्री f. (-स्त्री)<BR>	 1. A woman or female in general.<BR>	 2. A wife.<BR> E. स्त्यै to sound,<BR>ड्रट् Unādi aff., ङीप् fem. aff.; or ष्टु to praise, ड्रट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकाम|स्त्रीकामः
स्त्रीकाम m. (-मः) Desire of intercourse with women, fondness for women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकार्य्य|स्त्रीकार्य
स्त्रीकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Attendance on women, or women's apartments.<BR>	 2.<BR>The business of women.<BR> E. स्त्री, and कार्य्य business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकुमार
स्त्रीकुमार n. (-रं) A woman and child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकुसुम
स्त्रीकुसुम n. (-मं) The menstrual excretion in women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीक्षीर
स्त्रीक्षीर n. (-रं) Mother's milk.<BR> E. स्त्री, and क्षीर milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीगवी
स्त्रीगवी f. (-वी) A milch cow.<BR> E. स्त्री a female, गो a cow, and ङीप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीगृह
स्त्रीगृह n. (-हं) An apartment in a house dedicated to women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीघोष|स्त्रीघोषः
स्त्रीघोष m. (-षः) Dawn, daybreak.<BR> E. स्त्री a woman, and घोष sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीघ्न|स्त्रीघ्नः
स्त्रीघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A woman's murderer.<BR> E. स्त्री, and घ्न who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचरित
स्त्रीचरित n. (-तं) The doings of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचित्तहारिन्
स्त्रीचित्तहारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Pleasing or delightful to the female<BR>sex.<BR>	 m. (-री) A tree, (Hyperanthera morunga.)<BR> E. स्त्री a woman,<BR>चित्त heart or mind, हारिन् what takes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचिह्न|स्त्रीचिह्नं
स्त्रीचिह्न n. (-ह्नं)<BR>	 1. The vulva or womb.<BR>	 2. The female breast.<BR>	 3. Any<BR>mark or characteristic of the female sex.<BR> E. स्त्री a female, चिह्न mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचौर|स्त्रीचौरः
स्त्रीचौर m. (-रः) A libertine.<BR> E. स्त्री a woman, चौर a thief; also स्त्रीचोर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीजननी
स्त्रीजननी f. (-नी) The mother of a daughter.<BR> E. स्त्री, and जननी mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीजित|स्त्रीजितः
स्त्रीजित m. (-तः) A henpecked husband.<BR> E. स्त्री a woman or wife, and<BR>जित overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीतमा
स्त्रीतमा f. (-मा) A thorough woman.<BR> E. स्त्री and तमप् aff.; also with तरप् aff., स्त्रीतरा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीता
स्त्रीता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Womanhood, wifehood.<BR>	 2. Effeminacy, feminineness.<BR>E. स्त्री a woman, तल् aff.; also with त्व aff., स्त्रीत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधन|स्त्रीधनं
स्त्रीधन n. (-नं) Woman's separate property, which is held to be of six<BR>kinds; viz:--1. Adhyagnikam, what is given before the sacrificial<BR>fire; 2. Adhyavahanikam, what is presented during the bridal pro-<BR>cession; 3. Adhivedanikam, what is given on her husband's<BR>marrying another wife; 4. Pritidattam, what is given through<BR>affection; 5. Sulkam, her dower allowed or perquisites made<BR>during marriage; 6. Anwādheyam, a gift from her own or<BR>husband's relatives after marriage. Other varieties are enumera-<BR>ted, as the pitri, mātri, suta, bhrātridattam, what is given by<BR>her parents, son, or brother; bandhudattam, what is given by<BR>her kindred; and some enumerate acceptance generally, and in-<BR>heritance, amongst a woman's titles to property.<BR> E. स्त्री, धन wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्म्म|स्त्रीधर्म|स्त्रीधर्मः|स्त्रीधर्म्मः
स्त्रीधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः)<BR>	 1. Duty of woman.<BR>	 2. The laws concerning women.<BR>	 3.<BR>The menstrual excretion.<BR> E. स्त्री a woman, धर्म्म peculiar property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्म्मयोग|स्त्रीधर्मयोग
स्त्रीधर्म्मयोग n. (-गं) Laws or institutes concerning women.<BR> E. स्त्रीधर्म्म, and<BR>योग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्म्मिणी|स्त्रीधर्मिणी
स्त्रीधर्म्मिणी f. (-णी) A woman during menstruation.<BR> E. स्त्रीधर्म्म menstruation, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधव|स्त्रीधवः
स्त्रीधव m. (-वः) A man, a male.<BR> E. स्त्री a woman, and धव a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीनाथ
स्त्रीनाथ Adj. Protected by a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीनिबन्धन|स्त्रीनिबंधन
स्त्रीनिबन्धन n. (-नं) A woman's peculiar province or domestic duty,<BR>housewifery.<BR> E. स्त्री, and निबन्धन conferring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपण्योपजीविन्
स्त्रीपण्योपजीविन् m. (-वी)<BR>	 1. One who lives by his wife.<BR>	 2. One who lives<BR>by keeping women for prostitution; also स्त्र्याजीव ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपर|स्त्रीपरः
स्त्रीपर m. (-रः) A libertine, a woman-lover, a lecher.<BR> E. स्त्री a woman, पर intent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपिशाची
स्त्रीपिशाची f. (-ची) A fiend-like wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुधर्म्म
स्त्रीपुधर्म्म m. (-र्म्मः) Reciprocal duty of husband and wife, or man and<BR>woman.<BR> E. स्त्री, and पुम् male, धर्म्म law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुंसलक्षणा
स्त्रीपुंसलक्षणा f. (-णा) A hermaphrodite. “पोटायाम्” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुमन्
स्त्रीपुमन् m. (-मा) A woman who has become a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीप्रत्यय|स्त्रीप्रत्ययः
स्त्रीप्रत्यय m. (-यः) A feminine affix, (in grammar.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीप्रसङ्ग|स्त्रीप्रसंग|स्त्रीप्रसंगः
स्त्रीप्रसङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Intercourse with woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीप्रिय|स्त्रीप्रियः
स्त्रीप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Liked or loved by women.<BR>	 m. (-यः) The mango-<BR>tree.<BR> E. स्त्री a female, and प्रिय dear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीबाध्य|स्त्रीबाध्यः
स्त्रीबाध्य m. (-ध्यः) One who suffers himself to be distressed by a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीबुद्धि|स्त्रीबुद्धिः
स्त्रीबुद्धि f. (-द्धिः)<BR>	 1. The female understanding.<BR>	 2. The counsel of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीभोग|स्त्रीभोगः
स्त्रीभोग m. (-गः) Sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीमत्|स्त्रीमन्त्
स्त्रीमत् m. (-मान्) A husband, a wedded man.<BR> E. स्त्री, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीमन्त्र|स्त्रीमंत्र|स्त्रीमन्त्रः
स्त्रीमन्त्र m. (-न्त्रः) A female stratagem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीयन्त्र|स्त्रीयंत्र
स्त्रीयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) A woman who works like a machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीरञ्जन|स्त्रीरंजन|स्त्रीरञ्जनं
स्त्रीरञ्जन n. (-नं) Pān, the mixture of betel-nut, Pān-leaf, &c., chewed<BR>by the Hindus and by women especially.<BR> E. स्त्री a woman, and रञ्जन<BR>delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीरत्न
स्त्रीरत्न n. (-त्नं) An excellent woman.<BR> E. स्त्री and रत्न a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीराज्य
स्त्रीराज्य n. (-ज्यं) The kingdom of women, a country placed by some in<BR>the direction of Bhot.<BR> E. स्त्री, राज्य kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीलिङ्ग|स्त्रीलिंग
स्त्रीलिङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Feminine gender, (in gram.)<BR>	 n. (-ङ्गं) The female<BR>organ.<BR> E. स्त्री, लिङ्ग mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीवश|स्त्रीवशः
स्त्रीवश m. (-शः) Subjection to women.<BR> E. स्त्री, and वश subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीविधेय
स्त्रीविधेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Uxorious.<BR> E. स्त्री, and विधेय to be ruled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीविवाह|स्त्रीविवाहः
स्त्रीविवाह m. (-हः) Marrying a woman.<BR> E. स्त्री, and विवाह marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीवृत
स्त्रीवृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Attended by women.<BR> E. स्त्री, and वृत surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंग्रहण
स्त्रीसंग्रहण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Adultery, seduction.<BR>	 2. The act of embracing a<BR>woman, (rare in use.)<BR> E. स्त्री, and संग्रहण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंसर्ग|स्त्रीसंसर्गः
स्त्रीसंसर्ग m. (-र्गः) Female society.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंस्थान
स्त्रीसंस्थान Adj. Having a female shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसभ
स्त्रीसभ n. (-भं) An assembly of women, a number of females.<BR> E. स्त्री a<BR>woman, सभा an assembly, neuter in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसम्बन्ध|स्त्रीसंबन्ध|स्त्रीसंबंध|स्त्रीसंबन्धः
स्त्रीसम्बन्ध m. (-न्धः)<BR>	 1. Marriage.<BR>	 2. Connection by marriage.<BR>	 3. Relation<BR>or reference to women.<BR> E. स्त्री, and सम्बन्ध union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसेवा
स्त्रीसेवा f. (-वा) Libertinism.<BR> E. स्त्री, and सेवा addiction to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीस्वभाव|स्त्रीस्वभावः
स्त्रीस्वभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. An attendant of the women's apartments, a eunuch.<BR>2. The nature of women.<BR> E. स्त्री female, स्वभाव nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहत्या
स्त्रीहत्या f. (-त्या) Murder of a woman.<BR> E. स्त्री, and हत्या killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहन्तृ
स्त्रीहन्तृ m. (-न्ता) A woman's murderer.<BR> E. स्त्री, हन्तृ who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहरण
स्त्रीहरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Carrying off a woman, ravishment.<BR>	 2. Rape.<BR> E. स्त्री,<BR>हरण taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहारिन्
स्त्रीहारिन् m. (-री) A ravisher, one who carries off a woman.<BR> E. स्त्री, and हृ to take, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैण|स्त्रैणं|स्त्रैणः
स्त्रैण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं)<BR>	 1. Female, feminine.<BR>	 2. Being among women.<BR>3. Suited to or good for women.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Woman-hood.<BR>	 2. The<BR>nature of a woman.<BR>	 3. The Female sex.<BR>	 4. A multitude of women.<BR>E. स्त्री a woman, and अण् or नञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैणता
स्त्रैणता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Effiminacy.<BR>	 2. Addiction to woman.<BR> E. स्त्रैण, तल् aff.; also with त्व, स्त्रैणत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्र्याजीव|स्त्र्याजीवः
स्त्र्याजीव m. (-वः) One who lives by his wife's labours or prostitution.<BR>E. स्त्री, and आजीव subsistence: see स्त्रीपण्योपजीविन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्र्याभिगमन
स्त्र्याभिगमन n. (-नं) Sexual intercourse.<BR> E. स्त्री, and अभिगमन going to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थ|स्थः
स्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Staying, abiding, what or who is or stays.<BR> E. ष्ठा<BR>to stay or stand, aff. क; this deriv. most usually occurs in<BR>composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थकर|स्थकरं
स्थकर n. (-रं) A betel-nut; also read स्थगर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग्
स्थग् (ए) स्थगे r. 1st cl. (स्थगति) To cover, to veil, to hide; also ष्ठग् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग|स्थगः
स्थग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं)<BR>	 1. Fraudulent, dishonest, a rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 2.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">Page811-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Shameless, abandoned.<BR>	 m. (-गः) A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 f. (गी) A<BR>betel-box.<BR> E. स्थग् to cover or hide, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=810-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगन|स्थगनं
स्थगन n. (-नं) Covering, concealment.<BR> E. स्थग् to cover, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगर|स्थगरं|स्थगरः
स्थगर n. (-रं) A betel-nut; also read स्थकर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगिका
स्थगिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A courtesan.<BR>	 2. The office of betel-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगित|स्थगितं
स्थगित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Covered, hidden, concealed.<BR> E. स्थग् to cover,<BR>क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगु|स्थगुः
स्थगु m. (-गुः) A hump or protuberance on the back, &c.<BR> E. स्थग् to cover, aff. उन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिल|स्थंडिल|स्थंडिलं|स्थण्डिलं
स्थण्डिल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A level square piece of ground, prepared for a sacri-<BR>fice.<BR>	 2. A boundary, a land-mark.<BR>	 3. A barren field.<BR>	 4. A heap of<BR>clods.<BR> E. ष्ठल् to be situated, इलच् aff., नुक् aug.; ल changed to ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलशायिन्|स्थंडिलशायिन्
स्थण्डिलशायिन् m. (-यी) A devotee who, as an act of mortification or<BR>penance, sleeps on the ground which has been prepared for sacri-<BR>ficial purposes.<BR> E. स्थण्डिल as above, शी to sleep, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलसितक|स्थंडिलसितक|स्थण्डिलसितकं
स्थण्डिलसितक n. (-कं) An altar.<BR> E. स्थण्डिल levelled ground for a sacrifice,<BR>षो to destroy, aff. क्त, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलेशय|स्थंडिलेशय|स्थण्डिलेशयः
स्थण्डिलेशय m. (-यः) An ascetic sleeping on the ground: see स्थण्डिल-<BR>शायिन्.<BR> E. स्थण्डिल on the ground, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपति|स्थपतिः
स्थपति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Chief, best, principal.<BR>	 m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The performer<BR>of the VṚHASPATI-sacrifice.<BR>	 2. A guard or attendant of the<BR>women's apartments.<BR>	 3. A sovereign, a chief.<BR>	 4. An architect, a<BR>master-carpenter or builder.<BR>	 5. A carpenter, a wheel-wright.<BR>	 6. A<BR>charioteer.<BR>	 7. KUVERA.<BR> E. स्थ who is or who is placed, and पति<BR>master, lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपुट|स्थपुटः
स्थपुट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Distressed, living in difficulty or distress.<BR>	 2.<BR>Bent with pain, &c.<BR>	 f. (-टा)<BR>	 1. Being in contracted or difficult<BR>circumstances.<BR>	 2. Unevenly raised, elevated and depressed.<BR> E. स्थ<BR>what stands, or is, पुट् to contract, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपुटगत
स्थपुटगत Adj. Being in contracted and uneven places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थल्
स्थल् E. 1st cl. (-स्थलति) To stand, to be firm; according to some it is a<BR>different root from ष्ठल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थल|स्थलं
स्थल nf. (-लं-ली)<BR>	 1. Place, site, soil, dry or firm ground.<BR>	 2. A natural<BR>spot, forest-land.<BR>	 nf. (-लं-ला) A spot of dry ground prepared by<BR>art or drained and raised, &c., (as opposed to स्थली,) which is<BR>naturally so.)<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A tent, a house of cloth.<BR>	 2. A mound, a<BR>hillock.<BR>	 3. Point, case, topic, subject, (of a description or discussion.)<BR>4. Part, (as of a book.)<BR>	 5. Firm or dry ground.<BR>	 6. Shore, strand,<BR>beach.<BR>	 7. Place, spot, soil, (in general.)<BR>	 8. Field, tract, district.<BR>9. Station.<BR> E. ष्ठल् to be firm, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलचर
स्थलचर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who or what goes on land, terrene.<BR> E. स्थल, चर what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलच्युत
स्थलच्युत Adj. Fallen or removed from a place or position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलज
स्थलज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Terrene, terrestrial, what is produced on land.<BR>E. स्थल, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलदेवता
स्थलदेवता f. (-ता) A local or rural deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलपद्म|स्थलपद्मं|स्थलपद्मः
स्थलपद्म n. (-द्मं) A shrub, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR> E. स्थल dry ground, and पद्म a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलपद्मिनी
स्थलपद्मिनी f. (-नी) A shrub, (Hibiscus mutabilis.)<BR> E. स्थल dry ground,<BR>and पद्मिनी a cluster of lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलमञ्जरी
स्थलमञ्जरी f. (-री) A plant, (Achyranthes aspera.)<BR> E. स्थल dry ground,<BR>मञ्जरी a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलमार्ग|स्थलमार्गः
स्थलमार्ग m. (-र्गः) A road by land; also similar compounds, as स्थलवर्त्मन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलविग्रह|स्थलविग्रहः
स्थलविग्रह m. (-हः) Battle on plain or level ground.<BR> E. स्थल, विग्रह war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलशुद्धि|स्थलशुद्धिः
स्थलशुद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Purification or clearance of a place from impurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलशृङ्गाट|स्थलशृङ्गाटः
स्थलशृङ्गाट m. (-टः) A plant, (Tribulus lanuginosus.)<BR> E. स्थल, dry ground,<BR>शृङ्गाट a sort of trapa; with कन् added स्थलशृङ्गाटक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलसीमन्
स्थलसीमन् m. (-मा) A boundary, a land-mark.<BR> E. स्थल dry ground, सीमन् a boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलान्तर|स्थलांतर
स्थलान्तर n. (-रं) Another place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलीरूढ
स्थलीरूढ Adj. Alighted on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलीदेवता
स्थलीदेवता f. (-ता) A terrestrial demigod, as a faun, a dryad, &c.<BR> E. स्थली<BR>the dry land, देवता a divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलीय
स्थलीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating or belonging to dry ground.<BR> E. स्थल, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलेशय|स्थलेशयः
स्थलेशय m. (-यः) An amphibious animal, as the tortoise, otter, &c. Adj.<BR>Sleeping on dry ground.<BR> E. स्थले on dry ground, शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थवि|स्थविः
स्थवि m. (-विः)<BR>	 1. A weaver.<BR>	 2. Heaven.<BR> E. स्था to stay, Unādi aff. क्विन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविर|स्थविरं|स्थविरः
स्थविर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Old, aged.<BR>	 2. Fixed, firm, steady.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1.<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. An old man.<BR>	 3. A beggar.<BR>	 f. (-रा) An old woman. E.<BR>ष्ठा to stay or stand, (a long time, &c.) किरच् Unādi aff., and स्थव<BR>substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविष्ठ|स्थविष्ठः
स्थविष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं)<BR>	 1. Very fat or corpulent.<BR>	 2. Createst.<BR> E. स्थ्ल<BR>bulky, इष्ठन् superlative affix, the final of the adjective dropped,<BR>and vowel changed; also with ईयसुन् aff., स्थवीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणु|स्थाणुः
स्थाणु mfn. (-णुः-णः-णु) Firm, fixed, steady, stable.<BR>	 m. (-णुः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2.<BR>A stake, a pin.<BR>	 3. A post.<BR>	 4. A spear, a dart.<BR>	 5. A nest of white<BR>ants.<BR>	 6. The gnomon of a dial.<BR>	 7. JIVAKA, the drug and perfume.<BR>mn. (-णुः-णु)<BR>	 1. The trunk of a tree of which the branches have<BR>been lopped off.<BR>	 2. The branchless trunk or stem of any tree. E.<BR>ष्ठा to stand, Unādi aff. नु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणुच्छेद|स्थाणुच्छेदः|स्थाणुछेद
स्थाणुच्छेद m. (-दः) One who cuts down or clears timber.<BR> E. स्थाणु, and छेद who cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणुभ्रम|स्थाणुभ्रमः
स्थाणुभ्रम m. (-मः) Mistaking anything for a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाण्डिल|स्थांडिल|स्थांडिलः|स्थाण्डिलः
स्थाण्डिल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. An ascetic sleeping on the bare ground, or ground<BR>prepared for a sacrifice.<BR>	 2. A mendicant, a religious beggar. E.<BR>स्थण्डिल ground, &c., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थातव्य|स्थातव्यं
स्थातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं)<BR>	 1. To be placed or fixed.<BR>	 2. To be appointed or<BR>determined, to be ordained or agreed upon.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थातृ
स्थातृ mfn. (-ता-त्री-तृ) Who or what stays or stands.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay, aff. तृन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थान|स्थानं
स्थान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Place, spot, site, situation.<BR>	 2. Stay, staying, continu-<BR>ance, being fixed or stationary and exempt, from increase or<BR>diminution.<BR>	 3. Likeness, resemblance.<BR>	 4. Leisure, interval.<BR>	 5. An<BR>open place in a town, a green, a plain, a square.<BR>	 6. A house, a<BR>dwelling.<BR>	 7. A section, a chapter, a book.<BR>	 8. One of the three<BR>objects of government, the middle state, as neither loss nor gain,<BR>nor discomfiture nor success, nor expenditure nor accumulation,<BR>&c.<BR>	 9. A town, a city.<BR>	 10. Office, appointment.<BR>	 11. Degree,<BR>station.<BR>	 12. Halt.<BR>	 13. Firmness of troops, keeping in array.<BR>	 14.<BR>The act of standing firm so as to resist a charge.<BR>	 15. State,<BR>condition.<BR>	 16. The stamina of a kingdom, regarded as consisting<BR>of four parts, viz:--Army, treasury, city, and territory.<BR>	 17.<BR>Proper or right place.<BR>	 18. Country, region, district.<BR>	 19. Any<BR>place or sphere assigned after death to men according as they<BR>do their duty or neglect it.<BR>	 20. A holy place.<BR>	 21. An altar.<BR>	 22.<BR>An open place in a town.<BR>	 23. The part or character of an actor.<BR>24. An object.<BR>	 25. A worthy or proper object.<BR>	 26. Object, point,<BR>place.<BR>	 27. A modulation of voice, note, tone.<BR>	 28. Intimation,<BR>indication.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay, to be fixed, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानक|स्थानकं
स्थानक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. A basin or trench dug for water at the root of a<BR>tree.<BR>	 2. A town, a city.<BR>	 3. A bubble or a bead on spirits or wine<BR>4. Position, situation.<BR>	 5. A particular point or situation in drama-<BR>tic action.<BR>	 6. A mode of recitation.<BR>	 7. A division or section of the<BR>Taittirīya branch of the Yayur-Veda.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानचञ्चला
स्थानचञ्चला f. (-ला) A plant, (Ocimum pilosum.)<BR> E. स्थान place, चञ्चला<BR>trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानचिन्तक|स्थानचिंतक|स्थानचिन्तकः
स्थानचिन्तक m. (-कः) A quarter-master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानतस्
स्थानतस् Ind.<BR>	 1. According to place or situation.<BR>	 2. In regard to the<BR>place or organ of utterance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानपाल|स्थानपालः
स्थानपाल m. (-लः) A guard, a keeper, a watchman.<BR> E. स्थान a place, पाल who protects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानभ्रष्ट|स्थानभ्रष्टः
स्थानभ्रष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Displaced, out of place, fallen or removed<BR>from the natural or usual situation.<BR> E. स्थान place, and भ्रष्ट fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानमाहात्म्य
स्थानमाहात्म्य n. (-त्म्यं) The greatness or glory of any place, a kind of<BR>divine virtue supposed to be inherent in a sacred spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानयोग|स्थानयोगः
स्थानयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Assignment of suitable places.<BR>	 2. Proper mode or<BR>place for preserving articles.<BR> E. स्थान, and योग application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=811-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानाध्यक्ष|स्थानाध्यक्षः
स्थानाध्यक्ष m. (-क्षः) The superintendent or governor of a place or post.<BR>E. स्थान a place, अध्यक्ष superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानासेध|स्थानासेधः
स्थानासेध m. (-धः) Confinement to a place, imprisonment, arrest.<BR> E. स्थान, आसेध durance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिक|स्थानिकः
स्थानिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Local, belonging to place or site.<BR>	 2.<BR>That which takes the place of any thing or is substituted for it,<BR>(in gram.)<BR>	 m. (-कः) The governor or superintendent of any place<BR>or district.<BR> E. स्थान a place, and ढक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिन्
स्थानिन् mfn. (-नी-निनी-नि)<BR>	 1. Having place or fixation, placed, abiding,<BR>permanent, &c.<BR>	 2. Having a substitute.<BR>	 m. (-नी)<BR>	 1. The original<BR>form or primitive element.<BR>	 2. That which has a place.<BR> E. स्थान<BR>place, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानीय|स्थानीयं
स्थानीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Relating or suitable to any place, fit for or<BR>belonging to it, &c.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A city, a town.<BR> E. स्थान place. छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाने
स्थाने Ind.<BR>	 1. Properly, suitably, fitly.<BR>	 2. Because, on account of.<BR>	 3.<BR>Like, resembling, similarly.<BR>	 4. Truly.<BR>	 5. In lieu of, instead of.<BR>E. स्थान place, in the seventh case; or स्था-ने ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापक|स्थापकः
स्थापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Placing, fixing, regulating, ordering.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>1. The director of the stage-business, a stage-manager.<BR>	 2. A<BR>founder, the erector of a temple or image, &c.<BR> E. ष्ठा to be or<BR>stand, causal form, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापत्य|स्थापत्यः
स्थापत्य m. (-त्यः) A guard of the women's apartments.<BR>	 n. (-त्यं) Archi-<BR>tecture, building.<BR> E. स्था who stays, (in the harem, such as the<BR>wife or concubine of a man of rank,) पति master, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापन|स्थापनं
स्थापन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Placing, founding, fixing, erecting.<BR>	 2. Ordering,<BR>directing.<BR>	 3. Fixing or concentrating the thoughts upon the<BR>object of meditation, abstraction, mental control.<BR>	 4. A ceremony<BR>performed in the month of utero-gestation.<BR>	 5. A dwelling, a habi-<BR>tation.<BR>	 f. (-ना)<BR>	 1. Ordering or arranging as a drama, stage-manage-<BR>ment.<BR>	 2. Placing, fixing.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A plant, (Cissampelos hexandra.)<BR>E. ष्ठा to stay or stand, causal form, aff. ल्युट् or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापयत्
स्थापयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Fixing, placing, establishing.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay,<BR>causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापयित्वा
स्थापयित्वा Ind. Having placed, fixed, erected, &c.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay, causal v., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापित|स्थापितं
स्थापित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Deposited, placed.<BR>	 2. Ordered, directed.<BR>	 3.<BR>Established, ascertained.<BR>	 4. Firm, steady.<BR>	 5. Set up, erected.<BR>	 6.<BR>Founded, endowed.<BR>	 7. Placed in a post or situation.<BR> E. ष्ठा to<BR>stay or be, causal form, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापितवत्
स्थापितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Placing, having placed.<BR> E. स्था to place, causal. v., क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाप्य|स्थाप्यः
स्थाप्य f. (-प्या)<BR>	 1. To be placed or deposited.<BR>	 2. To be fixed or<BR>established.<BR>	 n. (-प्यं) A deposit, a pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाप्यापहरण
स्थाप्यापहरण n. (-णं) The stealing or embezzling of a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थामन्
स्थामन् n. (-म)<BR>	 1. Strength, power, stamina.<BR>	 2. Fixity, stability.<BR> E. ष्ठा<BR>to stand or stay, Unādi aff. मनिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिन्
स्थायिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि)<BR>	 1. Steady, firm, unchangeable, invariable.<BR>	 2.<BR>Who or what stays, or is, &c.<BR>	 f. (-यिनी)<BR>	 1. Standing, staying.<BR>	 2.<BR>Abiding, living.<BR>	 3. Enduring, continuing, lasting.<BR>	 n. (-यि) Any-<BR>thing lasting, a permanent state or condition.<BR>	 m. (-यी) A class of<BR>those feelings or passions which are the objects of poetic descrip-<BR>tion: see the next.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay, णिनि aff., युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिभाव|स्थायिभावः
स्थायिभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Fixed or permanent condition.<BR>	 2. A feeling or<BR>passion which is the object of poetical or dramatic description,<BR>and is classed sometimes as one of three, but more usually as one<BR>of two orders of such objects; this order being opposed especially<BR>to the Vyabhichāri-Bhāvas: the feelings or conditions termed<BR>Sthāyi are eight; viz.:--desire, mirth, sorrow, heroism, anger,<BR>fear, aversion, and astonishment.<BR> E. स्थायिन् fixed, and भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायुक|स्थायुकः
स्थायुक mfn. (-कः-का) or -की-कं)<BR>	 1. Stationary.<BR>	 2. Steady, firm.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>The overseer of a village.<BR> E. ष्टा to stand or be, उकञ् aff., युक् aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाल|स्थालं
स्थाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A caldron.<BR>	 2. A plate or dish.<BR>	 3. Any culinary<BR>utensil.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. An earthen pot or boiler.<BR>	 2. A particular vessel<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">Page812-b+ 60</a>]<BR>used in the preparation of SOMA.<BR>	 3. The trumpet flower, (Bignonia<BR>suave olens.)<BR> E. ष्ठा to stand, Unādi aff. आलच्; or स्थल-घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालरूप
स्थालरूप n. (-पं) The form or representation of a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीपक्व|स्थालीपक्वं
स्थालीपक्व mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं) Boiled, dressed in a pot or boiler.<BR> E. स्थाली<BR>a pot, पक्व cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीपाक|स्थालीपाकः
स्थालीपाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A particular religious act performed by a house-<BR>holder.<BR>	 2. Rice, &c., boiled for presentation to gods and manes:<BR>see चरु for the last sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीपुरीष
स्थालीपुरीष n. (-षं) The sediment or dirt sticking to a kettle or cooking pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीपुलाक|स्थालीपुलाकः
स्थालीपुलाक m. (-कः) Boiled-rice in a cooking-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीपुलाकन्याय
स्थालीपुलाकन्याय m. (-यः) The maxim of the cooking-pot and the boiled-<BR>rice. In a cooking-pot all the grains are equally moistened by the<BR>heated water and so when one knows that one grain is well-cooked<BR>he can draw the same inference as regards all others. From this<BR>fact the maxim is applied to cases where the condition of the whole<BR>is inferred from that of a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीबिल|स्थालीबिलं
स्थालीबिल n. (-लं) The interior or hollow of a boiler.<BR> E. स्थाली a pot, बिल vacuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीबिलीय|स्थालीबिलीयः
स्थालीबिलीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Rice, &c., fit to be boiled or dressed. E.<BR>स्थालीबिल the interior of a pot, छ aff.; also with यत् aff., स्थालीबिल्य ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावर|स्थावरं|स्थावरः
स्थावर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Fixed, stationary, stable, immovable, (as<BR>opposed to जङ्गम.)<BR>	 2. Regular, established.<BR>	 3. Inactive, slow, inert.<BR>m. (-रः) A mountain.<BR>	 n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A bow-string.<BR>	 2. Immovable<BR>property, land or houses.<BR>	 3. Family property, jewels, &c., which<BR>have been long in a family, and which ought not to be sold or<BR>given away.<BR>	 4. Any stationary or inanimate object, (considered to<BR>be the seventh creation of BRAHMĀ.)<BR>	 5. A heir-loom.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stand,<BR>वरच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरास्थावर
स्थावरास्थावर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Movable and immovable property.<BR>	 2. Things<BR>animate and inanimate; also similar compounds, as स्थावरजङ्गम, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाविर|स्थाविरं
स्थाविर n. (-रं) Old oge, any time after seventy in men, and fifty in<BR>women.<BR>	 f. (-रा or -री) Thick, firm.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay, (a long time,)<BR>किरच् Unādi aff., and युक् augment; or स्थविर-अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासक|स्थासकः
स्थासक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Perfuming the person, smearing the body with<BR>fragrant unguents, as of Sandal, &c.<BR>	 2. A bubble of water or any<BR>fluid.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay, स aff., and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासु
स्थासु n. (-सु) Bodily strength or capability.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay or be, सु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थास्नु|स्थास्नुः
स्थास्नु mfn. (-स्नुः-स्नुः-स्नु)<BR>	 1. Disposed to stand, immovable, firm, stable.<BR>2. Durable, permanent, eternal.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay, स्नु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थास्नुता
स्थास्नुता f. (-ता) Firmness, stability.<BR> E. स्थास्नु, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिक|स्थिकः
स्थिक m. (-कः) A buttock; probably a corruption of स्फिक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थित|स्थितः
स्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Steady, firm, immovable.<BR>	 2. Stayed, stopped.<BR>3. Determined, resolved, decreed, established.<BR>	 4. Upright, virtu-<BR>ous, steady in conduct.<BR>	 5. Agreed, engaged, contracted, promised.<BR>6. Risen, got up.<BR>	 7. Standing.<BR>	 8. Being, situated, living, existing.<BR>9. Being close, at hand, ready.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A word standing by itself.<BR>E. ष्ठा to stay or be, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितधी
स्थितधी mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि) Firm, unmoved, calm.<BR> E. स्थित, धी intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितपाठ्य
स्थितपाठ्य n. (-ठ्यं) Ricitation in Prākrit by a standing woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितप्रज्ञ|स्थितप्रज्ञः
स्थितप्रज्ञ mfn. (-ज्ञः-ज्ञा-ज्ञं)<BR>	 1. Calm, content, free from desire.<BR>	 2. Firm<BR>in judgment or wisdom, free from fancies or hallucinations. E.<BR>स्थित, and प्रज्ञा wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितप्रेमन्
स्थितप्रेमन् m. (-मा) A faithful friend.<BR> E. स्थित established, प्रेमन् affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितवत्|स्थितवन्त्
स्थितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Staying, abiding, stationary.<BR>	 2. Waiting,<BR>attending.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay, क्तवतु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिति|स्थितिः
स्थिति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Stay, staying, being fixed or stationary.<BR>	 2. Correct-<BR>ness of conduct, continuance in the path of duty.<BR>	 3. Limit, boun-<BR>dary, term.<BR>	 4. Stop, cessation, pause.<BR>	 5. Determination, order,<BR>decree.<BR>	 6. Honour, dignity.<BR>	 7. Duration of an eclipse, (in<BR>astronomy.)<BR>	 8. Stay, residence.<BR>	 9. Continuance in one state,<BR>stopping.<BR>	 10. Any situation, state, position.<BR>	 11. Natural state,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">Page813-a+ 60</a>]<BR>habit.<BR>	 12. Good condition, welfare.<BR>	 13. High station, rank.<BR>	 14.<BR>Consistency.<BR>	 15. Establishment of good order, (in a government.)<BR>16. Settled rule, axiom, maxim.<BR>	 17. Inertia, resistance to<BR>motion, (in phil.)<BR>	 18. One of the three states through which the<BR>system of created things has to pass, viz.:--that of preservation.<BR>E. ष्ठा to stay or stand, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=812-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिमत्|स्थितिमन्त्
स्थितिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Firm, stable.<BR>	 2. Steady, (in purpose,<BR>or conduct,) upright, firm, virtuous.<BR> E. स्थिति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिस्थापक|स्थितिस्थापकः
स्थितिस्थापक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Who or what fixes, places, &c.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>Elasticity.<BR>	 m. (-कः) The capability of placing in or recovering a<BR>previous position or condition. Adj. Having elastic properties. E.<BR>स्थिति, and स्थापक what causes to stay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थित्वा
स्थित्वा Ind. Having stayed, stood, stopped, been, &c.<BR> E. स्था to stay, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिर|स्थिरः
स्थिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Firm, fixed, steady, immovable.<BR>	 2. Hard, solid.<BR>3. Permanent, durable, lasting.<BR>	 4. Firm, steady, (morally,) unin-<BR>fluenced by pleasure or pain, &c.<BR>	 5. Cool, collected.<BR>	 6. Constant,<BR>faithful.<BR>	 7. Sure, certain.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A deity, an immortal.<BR>	 2.<BR>KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 3. A mountain.<BR>	 4. A tree.<BR>	 5. Final emancipation<BR>from existence.<BR>	 6. The planet SATURN.<BR>	 7. A bull.<BR>	 8. ŚIVA.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>1. The earth.<BR>	 2. A shrub, (Hedysarum gangeticum.)<BR>	 3. A medi-<BR>cinal root, commonly Kākoli.<BR>	 4. Silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay<BR>or be, Unādi aff. किरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरकुट्टक|स्थिरकुट्टकः
स्थिरकुट्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A steady pulverizer.<BR>	 2. A common divisor, (in algebra.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरगन्ध|स्थिरगंध|स्थिरगन्धः
स्थिरगन्ध m. (-न्धः) The Champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 f. (-न्धा)<BR>	 1. The<BR>Pandanus odoratissimus.<BR>	 2. Trumpet flower.<BR> E. स्थिर lasting, and<BR>गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरचक्र|स्थिरचक्रः
स्थिरचक्र m. (-क्रः) A Bauddha saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरचेतस्
स्थिरचेतस् mfn. (-ताः-ताः-तः) Firm, resolute, steady, constant.<BR> E. स्थिर, firm, चेतस् the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरच्छद|स्थिरच्छदः
स्थिरच्छद m. (-दः) The Bhurja-patra or birch-tree of the Himālaya<BR>mountains.<BR> E. स्थिर firm, and च्छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरच्छाय|स्थिरच्छायः
स्थिरच्छाय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A tree by the road side, &c., giving shelter to<BR>travellers or persons passing.<BR>	 2. A tree in general.<BR> E. स्थिर lasting,<BR>and छाया shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरजिह्व|स्थिरजिह्वः
स्थिरजिह्व m. (-ह्वः) A fish.<BR> E. स्थिर immovable, and जिह्वा the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरजीविता
स्थिरजीविता f. (-ता) The silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. स्थिर lasting, (a long time,)<BR>and जीवित alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरतर|स्थिरतरः
स्थिरतर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Firm, fixed, stationary.<BR>	 2. Permanent, dura-<BR>ble, eternal.<BR> E. स्थिर firm, तरप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरता
स्थिरता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Stability, firmness.<BR>	 2. Moral firmness, fortitude.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fearlessness.<BR> E. स्थिर with स्थिर with तल् added; also with त्व, स्थिरत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरदंष्ट्र|स्थिरदंष्ट्रः
स्थिरदंष्ट्र m. (-ष्ट्रः)<BR>	 1. A snake.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU in the boar-Avatār.<BR> E. स्थिर<BR>hard, and दंष्ट्र a tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरधी
स्थिरधी Adj. Firm-minded, resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरपच
स्थिरपच m. (-त्रः) The marshy-date-tree.<BR> E. स्थिर lasting, पत्र a leaf. “हिन्ताल वृक्षे ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरपुष्प|स्थिरपुष्पः
स्थिरपुष्प m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. The Champaca, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 2. The Bakul,<BR>(Mimusops elengi.)<BR> E. स्थिर lasting, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरप्रतिज्ञ
स्थिरप्रतिज्ञ Adj.<BR>	 1. Persisting in an assertion, pertinacious.<BR>	 2. Faithful to a promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरप्रतिबन्ध|स्थिरप्रतिबंध
स्थिरप्रतिबन्ध Adj. Obstinate, firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरमति|स्थिरमतिः
स्थिरमति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Steady, firm, deliberate.<BR> E. स्थिर, मति mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरयोनि|स्थिरयोनिः
स्थिरयोनि m. (-निः) A large tree, one that gives shade and shelter. E.<BR>स्थिर firm, lasting, and योनि place of production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरयौवन|स्थिरयौवनः
स्थिरयौवन m. (-नः) A Vidyādhara, a peculiar kind of demigod. Adj.<BR>Ever youthful.<BR> E. स्थिर perpetual, यौवन youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिररङ्गा
स्थिररङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा)<BR>	 1. Indigo.<BR>	 2. Dāru-haridrā, a sort of Curcuma. E.<BR>स्थिर lasting, रङ्ग colour or dye; also स्थिररागा in the last sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरधी
स्थिरधी Adj. Having permanent, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरसगर
स्थिरसगर Adj. Faithful to a promise, true, veracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरस्थायिन्
स्थिरस्थायिन् Adj. Remaining firm or steady, keeping perfectly still,<BR>(as in meditation.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिराङ्घ्रिप|स्थिराङ्घ्रिपः
स्थिराङ्घ्रिप m. (-पः) The marshy-date-tree. “हिन्ताल वृक्षे” ।<BR> E. स्थिर hard or lasting, अंह्रिप tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरात्मन्
स्थिरात्मन् mfn. (-त्मा-त्मा-त्म)<BR>	 1. Firm, resolute, unmoved.<BR>	 2. Stable<BR>steady.<BR> E. स्थिर, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरानुराग
स्थिरानुराग Adj. Constant in affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरायु|स्थिरायुः
स्थिरायु m. (-युः) The silk-cotton tree, (Bombax heptaphyllum.)<BR> E. स्थि<BR>lasting long, and आयु or आयुस् life; whence also स्थिरायुस् m. (-युः ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुड्
स्थुड् r. 6th cl. (स्थुडति) To clothe or cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुरिन्
स्थुरिन् m. (-री) A pack-horse, a horse carrying loads: see स्थौरिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुल
स्थुल n. (-लं) A sort of long tent; more properly स्थूल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूणा
स्थूणा f. (-णा)<BR>	 1. The post or pillar of a house.<BR>	 2. Any post or pillar.<BR>	 3.<BR>An iron image, a statue.<BR>	 4. An anvil.<BR>	 5. A disease.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay<BR>or stand, नक् Unādi aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूम|स्थूमः
स्थूम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Light.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूर|स्थूरः
स्थूर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A man.<BR>	 2. A bull.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stay, ऊरन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूरिन्
स्थूरिन् m. (-री) A pack-horse or one carrying loads on his back.<BR> E. स्थूल<BR>bulk, size, इनि affix, and ल changed to र; or स्था-उरन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूल्
स्थूल् r. 10th cl. (स्थूलयति-ते) To increase, to become big or bulky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूल|स्थूलं|स्थूलः
स्थूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं)<BR>	 1. Fat, corpulent, bulky.<BR>	 2. Stupid, dull<BR>ignorant, thick-headed.<BR>	 3. Large, great.<BR>	 4. Coarse.<BR>	 5. Clumsy.<BR>	 6.<BR>Not exact.<BR>	 7. Solid.<BR>	 8. Strong, powerful.<BR>	 9. Big, huge.<BR>	 n. (-लं)<BR>	 1.<BR>A heap, a quantity.<BR>	 2. A tent.<BR>	 3. The top or summit of a moun-<BR>tain.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A sort of pepper, (Pothos officinalis.)<BR>	 2. A<BR>pumpkin-gourd.<BR>	 m. (-लः) The jack-fruit tree.<BR> E. स्थूल् to be large<BR>or fat, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलक|स्थूलकः
स्थूलक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Large, bulky.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A sort of grass or reed<BR>E. स्थूल the same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकङ्गु|स्थूलकङ्गुः
स्थूलकङ्गु m. (-ङ्गुः) A wild sort of kidney-bean. “वोरक धान्ये” ।<BR> E. स्थूरु large, कङ्गु coix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकण्टिका
स्थूलकण्टिका f. (-का) The silk-cotton tree.<BR> E. स्थूल large, कण्ट a thorn, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकन्द|स्थूलकन्दः
स्थूलकन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. An esculent root, (Arum colocasia.)<BR>	 2. Anothe<BR>sort, (Arum Indicum.)<BR> E. स्थूल large, and कन्द a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकाय
स्थूलकाय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Large-bodied, corpulent.<BR> E. स्थूल, and काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकाष्ठदह्
स्थूलकाष्ठदह् m. (-धक्) The trunk of a tree or any piece of timber of<BR>fire.<BR> E. स्थूल large, काष्ठ wood, दह burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलकाष्ठाग्नि|स्थूलकाष्ठाग्निः
स्थूलकाष्ठाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) A large piece of wood on fire.<BR> E. स्थूल large, काष्ठ wood, अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलक्ष्वेड|स्थूलक्ष्वेडः
स्थूलक्ष्वेड m. (-डः) An arrow.<BR> E. स्थूल large, and क्ष्वेड a bamboo-rod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलचाप|स्थूलचापः
स्थूलचाप m. (-पः) A large bow-like instrument used in cleaning cotton<BR>E. स्थूल large, चाप a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलजीरक|स्थूलजीरकः
स्थूलजीरक m. (-कः) Kalonji, (Nigella Indica.) “कालजीरा” इति भाषा ।<BR> E. स्थूल large, जीरक cumin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलता
स्थूलता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Coarseness, bulkiness.<BR>	 2. Dulness, stupidity.<BR> E. त<BR>added to स्थूल; also with त्व, स्थूलत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलदण्ड|स्थूलदण्डः
स्थूलदण्ड m. (-ण्डः) A sort of reed, (Arundo.) “देवनले” ।<BR> E. स्थूल large<BR>दण्ड a stick or stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलदर्भ|स्थूलदर्भः
स्थूलदर्भ m. (-र्भः) A kind of grass, (Saccharum munja.)<BR> E. स्थूल large दर्भ Poa cynosuroides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलदला
स्थूलदला f. (-ला) The Aloe-plant.<BR> E. स्थूल large, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलधी
स्थूलधी mfn. (-धीः-धीः-धि) Dull, stupid.<BR> E. स्थूल, and धौ understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलनाल|स्थूलनालः
स्थूलनाल m. (-लः) A large kind of reed.<BR> E. स्थूल large, and नाल a stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलनास|स्थूलनासं|स्थूलनासः
स्थूलनास m. (-सः) A hog.<BR> E. स्थूल large, and नास for नासिका nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलनासिक|स्थूलनासिकः
स्थूलनासिक m. (-कः) A hog, a boar. Adj. Thick-nosed.<BR> E. स्थूल large<BR>नासिका the nose, made masc. in this compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलपट|स्थूलपटः
स्थूलपट mn. (-टः-टं) Coarse cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलपट्ट|स्थूलपट्टः
स्थूलपट्ट m. (-ट्टः) Cotton.<BR>	 n. (-ट्टं) Coarse cloth.<BR> E. स्थूल, पट्ट cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलपट्टाक|स्थूलपट्टाकः
स्थूलपट्टाक m. (-कः) Coarse cloth.<BR> E. स्थूल large, पट्ट cloth, अक् to be, aff अच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलपाद|स्थूलपादः
स्थूलपाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. An elephant.<BR>	 2. A man with elephantiasis. Adj<BR>Having swelled legs.<BR> E. स्थूल large, and पाद a foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलपुष्प|स्थूलपुष्पः
स्थूलपुष्प m. (-ष्पः) A tree, (Æschynomene grandiflora.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पा) A flower<BR>a sort of mountain Clitorea.<BR> E. स्थूल large, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलबुद्धि
स्थूलबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Stupid, dull.<BR> E. स्थूल, and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलभद्र|स्थूलभद्रः
स्थूलभद्र m. (-द्रः) One of the sacred personages called Śrutā Kevalis by<BR>the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलमरिच|स्थूलमरिचं
स्थूलमरिच n. (-चं) A fragrant medicinal berry, commonly Kakkol. E.<BR>स्थूल large, मरिच black-pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=813-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलमान
स्थूलमान n. (-नं) Gross or rough measure, rough computation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलमूल|स्थूलमूलं
स्थूलमूल n. (-लं) A kind of radish. “चाणक्य मूले ।”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूललक्ष|स्थूललक्षः
स्थूललक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Munificent, liberal.<BR>	 2. Learned, well-read.<BR>3. Remembering both benefits and offences.<BR> E. स्थूल large, much,<BR>and लक्ष mark or note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूललक्ष्य|स्थूललक्ष्यः
स्थूललक्ष्य mfn. (-क्ष्यः-क्ष्या-क्ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Munificent, liberal.<BR>	 2. Dealing profusely<BR>or indiscriminately.<BR>	 2. Rocollecting benefits and injuries.<BR>	 4. Taking<BR>careless aim.<BR> E. स्थूल a heap, (of wealth,) लक्ष्य to be remarked or seen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूललक्ष्यत्व
स्थूललक्ष्यत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Liberality.<BR>	 2. Aiming carelessly.<BR>	 3. Retentiveness<BR>of benefits.<BR> E. स्थूललक्ष्य, and त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलवर्त्मकृत्
स्थूलवर्त्मकृत् m. (-कृत्) A plant, (Siphonanthus Indica.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलवल्कल|स्थूलवल्कलः
स्थूलवल्कल m. (-लः) Red Lodh, a tree, the bark of which is used as an<BR>astringent in tanning, &c.<BR> E. स्थूल thick, and वल्कल bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशङ्खा|स्थूलशंखा
स्थूलशङ्खा f. (-ङ्खा) A woman having a large vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशरीर
स्थूलशरीर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Large-bodied.<BR>	 n. (-रं) The external or material<BR>body, (as opposed to सूक्ष्मशरीर).<BR> E. स्थूल, शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशाटक|स्थूलशाटकः
स्थूलशाटक mf. (-टकः-टका or -टिका) Thick or coarse cloth.<BR> E. स्थूल thick, शाटक cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशाटि|स्थूलशाटिः
स्थूलशाटि m. (-टिः) Coarse cloth.<BR> E. स्थूल large, and शाटि cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशिरस्
स्थूलशिरस् mfn. (-राः-राः-रः) Large-headed.<BR>	 n. (-रः) A large head or<BR>summit.<BR> E. स्थूल bulky, and शिरस् the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलशीर्षिका
स्थूलशीर्षिका f. (-का) A small ant having a large head in proportion to<BR>its size.<BR> E. स्थूल large, शीर्ष the head, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलषट्पद|स्थूलषट्पदः
स्थूलषट्पद m. (-दः) A wasp. “वोल्ता” इति भाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलस्कन्ध|स्थूलस्कंध|स्थूलस्कन्धः
स्थूलस्कन्ध m. (-न्धः) The Lakucha tree. “मान्दार” इति भाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलहस्त|स्थूलहस्तः
स्थूलहस्त n. (-स्तं) An elephant's trunk.<BR> E. स्थूल large, and हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलान्त्र|स्थूलांत्र
स्थूलान्त्र n. (-न्त्रं) The larger intestine near the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलास्य|स्थूलास्यः
स्थूलास्य m. (-स्यः) A snake.<BR> E. स्थूल large, and आस्य face or head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलिन्
स्थूलिन् m. (-ली) A camel.<BR> E. स्थूल large, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलीभूत
स्थूलीभूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Thick, bulky.<BR>	 2. Stupid.<BR> E. स्थूल, भूत become, with च्वि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलोच्चय|स्थूलोच्चयः
स्थूलोच्चय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Incompleteness, deficiency, defect.<BR>	 2. The middle<BR>pace of an elephant, neither quick nor slow.<BR>	 3. An eruption of<BR>pimples on the face.<BR>	 4. A hill at the foot of a mountain, or a<BR>rocky fragment detached from its primitive site and forming a<BR>separate projection or promontory.<BR>	 5. A hollow at the root of the<BR>elephant's tusks.<BR> E. स्थूल large, and उच्चय lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेमन्
स्थेमन् m. (-मा) Fixedness, firmness, stability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेय|स्थेयः
स्थेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be fixed or determined.<BR>	 2. To be placed.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-यः)<BR>	 1. A judge, on arbitrator, one who decides upon a dispute<BR>between two parties.<BR>	 2. A domestic priest.<BR> E. ष्ठा to stand, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेयस्
स्थेयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः)<BR>	 1. More firm, stable, fixed.<BR>	 2. Eternal, per-<BR>manent.<BR> E. स्थिर firm, ईयसुन् aff. of the superlative, and स्था substi-<BR>tuted for the adjective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेष्ठ|स्थेष्ठः
स्थेष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very firm, stable, fixed, durable.<BR> E. स्थिर firm,<BR>इष्ठन् aff. of the superlative, and स्था substituted for the primitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थैर्य्य|स्थैर्य|स्थैर्यं|स्थैर्य्यं
स्थैर्य्य n. (-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. Firmness, stability.<BR>	 2. Firmness of mind, resolution,<BR>fortitude.<BR>	 3. Continuance.<BR>	 4. Patience.<BR>	 5. Hardness, solidity. E.<BR>स्थिर, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थोरिन्
स्थोरिन् m. (-री) A pack-horse: see स्थौरिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौणेय|स्थौणेयं|स्थौणेयः
स्थौणेय n. (-यं) A sort of perfume, commonly Ganthiala.<BR> E. स्थूणा an<BR>image, &c., ढक् or ढकञ् aff.; also with कन् added, स्थौणेयक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौर|स्थौरं
स्थौर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Strength, power.<BR>	 2. A sufficient load for a horse or an<BR>ass, &c.<BR> E. स्थूल large, bulky, अण् aff., and ल changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौरिन
स्थौरिन m. (-री)<BR>	 1. A pack-horse, one that carries burdens on his back<BR>like an ox or ass.<BR>	 2. A strong horse.<BR> E. स्थौर strength, इनि aff.; or<BR>according to some authorities स्थुरा a pack-saddle, इनि aff., deriv.<BR>irr.; it is also read स्थूरिन्, स्थूरिन्, and स्थोरिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौलशीर्ष|स्थौलशीर्षं
स्थौलशीर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं) Large-headed, having or relating to a large<BR>head or summit.<BR> E. स्थूल large, शिरस् the head, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौल्य|स्थौल्यं
स्थौल्य n. (-ल्यं) Bulkiness, bigness, coarseness, largeness.<BR> E. स्थूल, and ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थ्यम
स्थ्यम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. Light, lustre.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नपन|स्नपनं
स्नपन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Bathing, ablution.<BR>	 2. Washing, sprinkling, wetting.<BR>E. ष्णा to bathe or purify by bathing, causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नपित|स्नपितः
स्नपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sprinkled, wetted, bathed, washed.<BR> E. णा to<BR>bathe, causal form, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नव|स्नवः
स्नव m. (-वः) Oozing, dripping, trickling.<BR> E. णु to distil or ooze, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नसा
स्नसा f. (-सा) A tendon, a muscle.<BR> E. णस् to eject, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नस्त
स्नस्त f. (-स्ता) A tendon, a muscle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात्
स्नात् mfn. (-स्नान्-स्नान्ती-स्नात्) Bathing, performing ablution.<BR> E. णा to bathe, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात|स्नातः
स्नात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bathed, washed, purified, (by ablution.)<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>An initiated householder: see the next.<BR> E. णा to bathe, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नातक|स्नातकः
स्नातक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An initiated householder, a man of the three first<BR>classes, who having completed the term prescribed for his stu-<BR>dies becomes a housekeeper: if at the end of this period, he has<BR>not acquired a knowledge of the Veda, he is called Vrata-snātaka;<BR>if he has acquired that knowledge earlier, he is termed Vidyā-<BR>snātaka, and if he finishes his regular studies at the same time<BR>that the period of study expires, he is named Ubhaya-snātaka.<BR>2. A Brāhmana who has performed the ceremony of ablution,<BR>required to be performed on his finishing his first ĀŚHRAMA.<BR>	 3.<BR>A Brāhman who is a Bhikshu or beggar for any religious object.<BR>E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात्वा
स्नात्वा Ind. Having bathed.<BR> E. ष्णा to bathe, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नान|स्नानं
स्नान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Bathing, ablution.<BR>	 2. Purification by bathing, religious<BR>or ceremonial ablution.<BR>	 3. Anything proper for ablution, viz.:--<BR>water, perfumed powder for the body, &c.<BR> E. ष्णा to bathe, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानतृण|स्नानतृणं
स्नानतृण n. (-णं) Kuśa grass.<BR> E. स्नान ablution, and तृण grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानद्रोणी
स्नानद्रोणी f. (-णी) A bathing tub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानयात्रा
स्नानयात्रा f. (-त्रा) The festival held on the day of full-moon in the<BR>month of Jyeshtha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानवस्त्र
स्नानवस्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) A cloth put on at or after bathing.<BR> E. स्नान, वस्त्र clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानविधि|स्नानविधिः
स्नानविधि m. (-धिः) The rules of ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानशील
स्नानशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Bathing, performing ablution, (especially in<BR>sacred waters.)<BR> E. स्नान, and शील practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानीय|स्नानीयं
स्नानीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Ablutionary, fit or proper for bathing in, or to<BR>be used at bathing, as perfumed powders, &c.<BR>	 n. (-यं) Water or<BR>any other article, (such as unguents, perfumes, &c.) proper for<BR>bathing.<BR> E. स्नान ablution, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नापक|स्नापकः
स्नापक m. (-कः) A servant who brings water, or who applies it in bath-<BR>ing.<BR> E. ष्णा to bathe, causal v., ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नापन|स्नापनं
स्नापन n. (-नं) The act of causing to bathe or attending a person while bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नाविन्
स्नाविन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) A bather, a performer of ablutions.<BR> E. ष्णा to<BR>bathe, णिनि aff., युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायु|स्नायुः
स्नायु f. (-युः)<BR>	 1. A tendon, a muscle, described as a tubular vessel<BR>attached to the bones at either end, and carrying vital air.<BR>	 2. The<BR>string of a bow.<BR> E. ष्णा to bathe, उण् Unādi aff., and युक् augment;<BR>also with कन् added, स्नायुक; or स्नाति-शुध्यति दोषोऽनया ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नाय्वर्मन्|स्नाय्वर्म्मन्
स्नाय्वर्मन् n. (-र्म) A kind of disease of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नाव|स्नावः
स्नाव m. (-वः) A tendon, a muscle; also स्नावन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्ध|स्निग्धं|स्निग्धः
स्निग्ध mfn. (-ग्धः-ग्धा-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Oily, unctuous, greasy.<BR>	 2. Amiable, kind,<BR>affectionate.<BR>	 3. Coarse, dense, thick.<BR>	 4. Cooling, emollient.<BR>	 5.<BR>Sticky, cohesive, adhesive.<BR>	 6. Smooth.<BR>	 7. Glossy, shining, res-<BR>plendent.<BR>	 8. Moist, wet.<BR>	 9. Attached, loving, tender, friendly,<BR>(generally with a locative.)<BR>	 10. Lovely, agreeable.<BR>	 m. (-ग्धः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>friend.<BR>	 2. The red castor-oil-plant.<BR>	 3. A sort of pine, (Pinus Deva-<BR>dāru.)<BR>	 4. Another kind, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>	 f. (-ग्धा)<BR>	 1. Marrow.<BR>	 2.<BR>The scum of boiled-rice.<BR>	 n. (-ग्धं)<BR>	 1. Bee's-wax.<BR>	 2. Light, lustre.<BR>3. Thickness, coarseness.<BR>	 4. Oil.<BR> E. ष्णिह् to be unctuous, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धजन|स्निग्धजनः
स्निग्धजन m. (-नः) An affectionate or friendly person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धतण्डुल|स्निग्धतंडुल|स्निग्धतण्डुलः
स्निग्धतण्डुल m. (-लः) Rice of quick growth.<BR> E. स्निग्ध oily, तुण्डल grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धता
स्निग्धता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Affection, kindness.<BR>	 2. Unctuousness oiliness, 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">Page815-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Blandness.<BR>	 4. Tenderness.<BR> E. स्निग्ध affectionate, तल् aff. of the<BR>abstract; also with त्व, स्निग्धत्व n. (-त्वं) ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=814-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धदारु|स्निग्धदारुः
स्निग्धदारु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. A pine, (Pinus longifolia.)<BR>	 2. Another kind,<BR>(Pinus Devadāru.)<BR> E. स्निग्ध unctuous, दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धपन
स्निग्धपन mf. (-त्रः-त्रा) The jujube, (zizyphus jujube.)<BR> E. स्निग्ध unctuous, पत्र a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निट्
स्निट् r. 10th cl. (स्नेटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be greasy or unctuous.<BR>	 2. To fuse or melt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
स्नु mn. (-स्नुः-स्नु)<BR>	 1. Table-land, the level summit or edge of a mountain.<BR>2. Top, surface in general; this word has no forms for the first<BR>five cases; according to Vopadeva it is an optional substitute<BR>for सानु.<BR>	 f. (-स्नुः) A sinew, tendon, muscle.<BR> E. ष्णु to trickle, (the<BR>water or snow from it,) डु aff.; or ष्णा to bathe, कु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुत|स्नुतः
स्नुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Flowing, dropping, oozing, trickling, distilled. E.<BR>ष्णु to ooze, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुषा
स्नुषा f. (-षा)<BR>	 1. A daughter-in-law.<BR>	 2. The milk-hedge-plant.<BR> E. ष्णु to distil, Unādi aff. सक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुह्
स्नुह् f. (-स्नुक्) The milk-hedge-plant, (Euphorbia antiquorum. &c.) E.<BR>स्नुह् to vomit, (its milk being used as an emetic,) aff. क्विप्; also<BR>with टाप् added, स्नुहा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुहि|स्नुहिः
स्नुहि f. (-हिः-ही) A plant, (Euphorbia antiquorum.)<BR> E. ष्णुह् to vomit:<BR>(see the last,) कि aff., and ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेह|स्नेहः
स्नेह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Affection, kindness.<BR>	 2. Oil, unguent, grease, any<BR>unctuous or greasy substance.<BR>	 3. Oiliness, lubricity, viscidity,<BR>(one of the twenty-four Gunas of the Vaiśeshikas.)<BR>	 4. Moisture.<BR>5. A fluid of the body.<BR> E. ष्णिह् to be unctuous, &c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहच्छेद|स्नेहच्छेदः|स्नेहछेद
स्नेहच्छेद m. (-दः) Cessation or loss of regard, breach of friendship. E.<BR>स्नेह, च्छेद severing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहन्
स्नेहन् m. (-हा)<BR>	 1. A friend.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. A disease.<BR> E. ष्णिह् to be<BR>affectionate, &c., कनिन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहन|स्नेहनं
स्नेहन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Unctuousness, being or becoming oily, &c.<BR>	 2. Anoint-<BR>ing, unction, rubbing with unguents, oil, &c.<BR>	 3. An emollient,<BR>an unguent or liniment.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Adj.<BR>	 1. Anointing, lubricating.<BR>	 2.<BR>Destroying.<BR>	 m. (-नः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. ष्णिह् to be unctuous, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहपक्व
स्नेहपक्व mfn. (-क्वः-क्वा-क्वं) Dressed with oil.<BR> E. स्नेह, and पक्व cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहपूर्वम्
स्नेहपूर्वम् Ind. Affectionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहप्रिय|स्नेहप्रियः
स्नेहप्रिय m. (-यः) A lamp. Adj. Fond of oil.<BR> E. स्नेह oil, प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहभू
स्नेहभू m. (-भूः) The Phlegmatic humour, rheum.<BR> E. स्नेह oily substance,<BR>and भू born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहभूमि|स्नेहभूमिः
स्नेहभूमि m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. An object of affection.<BR>	 2. Any substance yielding<BR>oil or grease.<BR> E. स्नेह, and भूमि site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहरङ्ग|स्नेहरंग|स्नेहरङ्गः
स्नेहरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Sesamum.<BR> E. स्नेह oil, रङ्ग colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहवत्|स्नेहवन्त्
स्नेहवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Affectionate.<BR>	 2. Unctuous, oily.<BR> E. स्नेह, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहवस्ति|स्नेहवस्तिः
स्नेहवस्ति f. (-स्तिः) Injection of oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहविद्ध|स्नेहविद्धं|स्नेहविद्धः
स्नेहविद्ध m. (-द्धः) A sort of pine, (Pinus Devadāru.)<BR> E. स्नेह oil, विद्ध pierced, impregnated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहव्यक्ति|स्नेहव्यक्तिः
स्नेहव्यक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Display of friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहाक्त
स्नेहाक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Oiled, greased, lubricated.<BR> E. स्नेह, and अक्त<BR>anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहानुवृत्ति|स्नेहानुवृत्तिः
स्नेहानुवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Affectionate or friendly intercourse.<BR> E. स्नेह, अनुवृत्ति practice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहाश|स्नेहाशः
स्नेहाश m. (-शः) A lamp.<BR> E. स्नेह oil, and अश what consumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहित|स्नेहितः
स्नेहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Kind, affectionate.<BR>	 2. Beloved, the object of<BR>affection.<BR>	 3. Anointed.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A friend.<BR> E. स्नेह affection, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहिन्
स्नेहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिनी-हि)<BR>	 1. Affectionate, friendly.<BR>	 2. Oily, unctuous.<BR>3. Fat.<BR>	 m. (-ही)<BR>	 1. A friend.<BR>	 2. A painter.<BR>	 3. A smearer.<BR> E. स्नेह<BR>affection, &c., इनि aff.; or ष्णिह् to love, &c., णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहु|स्नेहुः
स्नेहु m. (-हुः)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR> E. ष्णिह् to be unctuous,<BR>उन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नैग्ध
स्नैग्ध n. (-ग्ध्यं)<BR>	 1. Oiliness, smoothness, lubricity.<BR>	 2. Affectionateness.<BR> E. स्निग्ध, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पद्
स्पद् (इ) स्पदि r. 1st cl. (स्पन्दते)<BR>	 1. To quake, to shake, to tremble slight-<BR>ly, to throb, to beat, to palpitate.<BR>	 2. To go, to move. With परि,<BR>To tremble. With वि, To struggle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्द|स्पंद|स्पंदः|स्पन्दः
स्पन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Throbbing, throb.<BR>	 2. Tremor, motion, vibration.<BR> E. स्पदि to shake, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दन|स्पंदन|स्पंदनं|स्पन्दनं
स्पन्दन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Beating, throbbing, pulsation, quivering, palpitation,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">Page815-b+ 60</a>]<BR>throbbing.<BR>	 2. The quickening of a child in the womb.<BR>	 3. Going.<BR>E. स्पदि to throb, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पन्दमान
स्पन्दमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Throbbing, beating.<BR>	 2. Going.<BR> E. स्पदि to beat, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्प्रन्दित
स्प्रन्दित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Throbbing, beating.<BR>	 2. Gone.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A pulsa-<BR>tion.<BR> E. स्पदि to throb, क्त्व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्परितृ
स्परितृ m. (-ता) The agent or active cause of pain or distress, as an<BR>enemy, an oppressor, a disease, &c.<BR> E. स्प्र to breathe, aff. तृच्,<BR>with इट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्ध्
स्पर्द्ध् r. 1st cl. (स्पर्द्धते)<BR>	 1. To vie, to envy, to desire another's reduction.<BR>2. To rival.<BR>	 3. To defy. With प्रति, To bid defiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्ध
स्पर्द्ध mfn. (-र्द्धः-र्द्धा-र्द्धं) Envious, emulous.<BR> E. स्पर्द्ध् to envy, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्धता
स्पर्द्धता f. (-ता) Enviousness, emulation.<BR> E. स्पर्द्ध, and तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्धा
स्पर्द्धा f. (-र्द्धा)<BR>	 1. Emulation, rivalry.<BR>	 2. Equality, sameness.<BR>	 3. Success-<BR>ive elevation.<BR>	 4. Jealousy, envy.<BR>	 5. Defiance.<BR> E. स्पर्द्ध् to envy or<BR>vie with, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्धित्
स्पर्द्धित् mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Vied or contended with, defied.<BR> E. स्पर्द्ध् to vie with, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्द्धिन्
स्पर्द्धिन् mfn. (-र्द्धी-र्द्धिनी-र्द्धि)<BR>	 1. Emulous, envious.<BR>	 2. Superb, gorgeous.<BR>3. Proud.<BR> E. स्पर्द्धा, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्श्
स्पर्श् r. 10th cl. (स्पर्शयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To take.<BR>	 2. To unite, to join.<BR>	 3. To embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्श|स्पर्शः
स्पर्श m. (-र्शः)<BR>	 1. Touch, contact.<BR>	 2. The thing touching or feeling.<BR>	 3.<BR>Gift, donation.<BR>	 4. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 5. Morbid heat.<BR>	 6. A conso-<BR>nant of either of the five first classes of the alphabet.<BR>	 7. An<BR>enemy, a disease, &c., the agent or instrument of pain, trouble,<BR>or distress.<BR>	 8. Air, wind.<BR>	 9. Sexual union.<BR>	 10. Collision, conflict,<BR>encounter.<BR>	 11. Contact, (in astronomy.)<BR>	 12. The quality of tangiti-<BR>lity.<BR>	 13. Feeling, sensation.<BR>	 14. Anything which touches or comes<BR>in contact.<BR>	 15. A spy.<BR>	 f. (-र्शा) A wanton, an unchaste woman. E.<BR>स्पृश् to touch, aff. घञ्; or स्पर्श् to take, &c., अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शक|स्पर्शकः
स्पर्शक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Touching, toucher, that which touches or is in<BR>contact with.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शतन्मात्र
स्पर्शतन्मात्र n. (-त्रं) The subtile element of tangibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शन|स्पर्शनं|स्पर्शनः
स्पर्शन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Touch, contact.<BR>	 2. Gift, donation.<BR>	 3. Organ of sense,<BR>sense of touch.<BR>	 m. (-नः) Air, wind.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Adj.<BR>	 1. Touching,<BR>handling.<BR>	 2. Acting upon, affecting.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शनक|स्पर्शनकं
स्पर्शनक n. (-कं) A term for the skin, (in Sānkhya philosophy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शनीय
स्पर्शनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) What is to be or may be touched, sensible,<BR>tangible.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शमणि|स्पर्शमणिः
स्पर्शमणि m. (-णिः) A stone, the philosopher's stone, converting every<BR>thing it touches to gold.<BR> E. स्पर्श touch, मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शमणिप्रभव|स्पर्शमणिप्रभवं
स्पर्शमणिप्रभव n. (-वं) Gold.<BR> E. स्पर्शमणि the stone, and प्रभव production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शलज्जा
स्पर्शलज्जा f. (-ज्जा) A sensitive plant, (Mimosa pudica.)<BR> E. स्पर्श the touch,<BR>and लज्जा ashamed. “लज्जावती लता” इति भाषा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शवत्|स्पर्शवन्त्
स्पर्शवत् Adj.<BR>	 1. Having tangibility.<BR>	 2. Smooth, soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शवेद्य
स्पर्शवेद्य Adj. Apprehended by touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शशुद्धा
स्पर्शशुद्धा f. (-द्धा) A plant, (Asparagus recemosus.) “शतमूल्याम्” ।<BR> E. स्पर्श<BR>touch, शुद्धा pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शस्नान
स्पर्शस्नान n. (-नं) Ablution at the ingress of the sun or moon into an eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शस्पन्द|स्पर्शस्पंद|स्पर्शस्पन्दः
स्पर्शस्प(स्य)न्द m. (-न्दः) A frog.<BR> E. स्पर्श the touch, स्पन्द who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शानन्दा
स्पर्शानन्दा f. (-न्दा) One of the Apsarasas.<BR> E. स्पर्श touch, आनन्द delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शोदय
स्पर्शोदय Adj. Following by a consonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ष्
स्पर्ष् r. 1st cl. (स्पर्षते) To become wet or moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ष्टृ
स्पर्ष्टृ m. (-र्ष्टा)<BR>	 1. Morbid heat.<BR>	 2. The agent or instrument of bodily<BR>pain.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, aff. तृच्; also स्प्रष्टृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश्
स्पश् r. 1st cl. (स्पशति-ते)<BR>	 1. To obstruct, to oppose.<BR>	 2. To string toge-<BR>ther.<BR>	 3. To touch.<BR>	 4. To make evident or clear.<BR>	 5. To inform.<BR>	 6.<BR>To perform.<BR>	 7. To see, to perceive clearly, to spy. r. 10th cl.<BR>(स्पाशयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To take.<BR>	 2. To unite, to connect, to join.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश|स्पशः
स्पश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A spy, a secret agent or emissary.<BR>	 2. War, battle.<BR>	 3.<BR>Fighting with a dangerous animal, as a tiger, a buffalo, &c., for<BR>reward.<BR> E. स्पश् to inform, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=815-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्ट|स्पष्टं
स्पष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Evident, manifest, apparent.<BR>	 2. Clear, easy,<BR>intelligible.<BR>	 3. True, real.<BR> E. स्पश् to make clear, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टगर्भा
स्पष्टगर्भा f. (-र्भा) A woman evidently pregnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टप्रतिपत्ति|स्पष्टप्रतिपत्तिः
स्पष्टप्रतिपत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Clear perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टम्
स्पष्टम् Ind.<BR>	 1. Clearly, distinctly.<BR>	 2. Openly, boldly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टार्थ
स्पष्टार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Clear, perspicuous, intelligible.<BR> E. स्पष्ट, अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टीकरण
स्पष्टीकरण n. (-णं) Making clear or intelligible.<BR> E. स्पष्ट, करण making, च्वि aug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टीकृत|स्पष्टीकृतं
स्पष्टीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Explained, expounded, elucidated, made<BR>clear, and intelligible.<BR>	 2. Made manifest, revealed, exposed. E.<BR>स्प्रष्ट easy, clear, च्वि augment, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पाशित
स्पाशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Caused to be stopped, hindered, &c.<BR> E. स्पश् to<BR>stop, causal v., क्त aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृ
स्पृ r. 5th cl. (स्पृणोति)<BR>	 1. To please, to gratify.<BR>	 2. To cherish, to protect.<BR>	 3. To breathe, to live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृक्का
स्पृक्का f. (-क्का) A gramineous plant, (Trigonella corniculata.)<BR> E. स्पृश् to<BR>touch, कक् aff., and श changed to क, form irr.; also पृक्का ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्
स्पृश् r. 6th cl. (स्पृशति)<BR>	 1. To touch, to take with the hand.<BR>	 2. To<BR>cleave to, to cling to.<BR>	 3. To came in contact with.<BR>	 4. To act upon,<BR>to affect.<BR>	 5. To accept.<BR>	 6. To reach, to attain.<BR>	 7. To sprinkle, to<BR>wash. With उप, 1. To tread upon.<BR>	 2. To bathe, to sip water, &c.<BR>3. To touch. With अप, To rinse one's mouth. With परि, To touch.<BR>With सम् 1. To touch.<BR>	 2. To sprinkle with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्
स्पृश् mfn. (-स्पृक्) Who or what touches.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृशत्
स्पृशत् mfn. (-शन्-शती or -शन्ती-शत्) Touching.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृशा
स्पृशा f. (-शा) A plant, commonly Kankālīkā.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, अङ् and<BR>टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृशी
स्पृशी f. (-शी) A prickly-nightshade, (Solanum Jacquini.)<BR> E. स्पृश् to<BR>touch, क and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्य
स्पृश्य mfn. (-श्यः-श्या-श्यं) What may be or is to be felt or touched.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्ट|स्पृष्टः
स्पृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Touched, felt.<BR>	 f. (-ष्टा) Adj.<BR>	 1. Touched, defiled.<BR>2. Handled.<BR>	 3. Formed by the contact of the organs of utterance.<BR>E. स्पृश् to touch, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टव्य
स्पृष्टव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) What is to be or may be touched, felt, &c.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टि|स्पृष्टिः
स्पृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) Touch, feeling, contact.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टिका
स्पृष्टिका f. (-का) Touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्ट्वा
स्पृष्ट्वा Ind. Having felt or touched.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृह्
स्पृह् r. 10th cl. (स्पृहयति-ते) To wish, to desire, to long for, (with a dative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहण|स्पृहणं
स्पृहण n. (-णं) The act or desiring or wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहणीय|स्पृहणीयं
स्पृहणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Desirable, to be wished.<BR> E. स्पृह् to wish, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहणीयशोभ
स्पृहणीयशोभ Adj. Having desirable beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयमाण
स्पृहयमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Desiring, wishing.<BR> E. स्पृह् to desire, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयालु|स्पृहयालुः
स्पृहयालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Wishing, desiring, cupidinous.<BR> E. स्पृह् to wish,<BR>आलुच् aff., and युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहा
स्पृहा f. (-हा) Wish, desire.<BR> E. स्पृह् to wish, अङ् and टाप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृह्य|स्पृह्यः
स्पृह्य mfn. (-ह्यः-ह्या-ह्यं) To be wished, desirable.<BR>	 m. (-ह्यः) A large kind<BR>of lime, the wild-citron tree.<BR> E. स्पृह् to wish, aff. यत् or क्यप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पॄ
स्पॄ r. 9th cl. (स्पृणाति) To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्प्रष्टृ
स्प्रष्टृ mfn. (-ष्टा-ष्ट्री-ष्टृ) Who or what touches, &c.<BR>	 m. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. Morbid<BR>heat.<BR>	 2. The agent or instrumental cause of pain or distress, as<BR>an enemy, a disease, &c.<BR> E. स्पृश् to touch, तृच् aff., and the first ऋ<BR>converted to र; also स्पर्ष्टृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फट्
स्फट् r. 1st cl. (स्फटति)<BR>	 1. To open, to unfold, to burst.<BR>	 2. To break or<BR>divide.<BR> E. (इ)स्फटि r. 1st cl. (स्फण्टति) To expand. r. 10th cl. (स्फण्टयति-ते)<BR>To jest or joke with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फट|स्फटः
स्फट mf. (-टः-टा) A snake's expanded neck or hood f. (-टिः or -टी) Alum.<BR>E. स्फुट् to swell, aff. क, and the vowel changed to अ; or स्फट्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटि
स्फटि(टी)क m. (-कः) Crystal, quartz.<BR>	 f. (-की) Alum.<BR> E. स्फुट् to expand,<BR>क्वुन् aff., and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकप्रभ
स्फटिकप्रभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Crystalline, transparent.<BR> E. स्फटिक, and प्रका light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकमय
स्फटिकमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of crystal.<BR> E. स्फटिक, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकाचल|स्फटिकाचलः
स्फटिकाचल m. (-लः) Mount Kailāsa.<BR> E. स्फटिक Crystal, अचल a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकाद्रिभिद|स्फटिकाद्रिभिदः
स्फटिकाद्रिभिद m. (-दः) Camphor.<BR> E. स्फटिकाद्रि Kailāsa, and भिह what<BR>breaks, what shames, being whiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकारि|स्फटिकारिः
स्फटिकारि f. (-रिः) Sulphate of alumina. “फट्किरि”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकाश्मन्
स्फटिकाश्मन् m. (-श्मा) Crystal.<BR> E. स्फटिक the same, and अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फड्
स्फड् (इ) स्फडि r. 1st and 10th cls. (स्फण्डति स्फण्डयति-ते) To jest or joke<BR>with, to smile or laugh at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फर्
स्फर् r. 6th cl. (स्फरति)<BR>	 1. To throb, to beat, to tremble.<BR>	 2. To move.<BR>	 3. To be manifest: see स्फुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फरण|स्फरणं
स्फरण n. (-णं) Throbbing, trembling.<BR> E. स्फर् to throb, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फल्
स्फल् r. 6th cl. (स्फलति)<BR>	 1. To throb, to beat, to tremble.<BR>	 2. To move.<BR>3. To be manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटक|स्फाटकं|स्फाटकः
स्फाटक m. (-कः) A drop of water.<BR> E. स्फट् to break, वुञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटिक|स्फाटिकं
स्फाटिक mfn. (-कः-की-क) Crystalline, made, &c. of crystal.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>Crystal.<BR> E. स्फटिक the same, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटिकोपल|स्फाटिकोपलः
स्फाटिकोपल n. (-लं) Crystal.<BR> E. स्फाटिक the same, and उपल a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटित
स्फाटित f. (-ता) Expanded, made to gape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटीक|स्फाटीकं
स्फाटीक n. (-कं) Crystal. E. See स्फटिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फात|स्फातः
स्फात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Swollen, enlarged.<BR> E. स्फायी to increase, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाति|स्फातिः
स्फाति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Increase, growth.<BR>	 2. Swelling, intumescence.<BR> E. स्फाय्<BR>to increase, क्तिन् aff., and the final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाय्
स्फाय् (ई) स्फायी r. 1st cl. (स्फायत)<BR>	 1. To grow, to increase, to become<BR>large or bulky.<BR>	 2. To expand.<BR>	 3. To smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फार|स्फारं|स्फारः
स्फार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Large, great.<BR>	 2. Loud.<BR>	 3. Increased, expanded.<BR>m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Throbbing, quivering.<BR>	 2. A bubble or flaw in gold, &c.<BR>3. Twanging as of a bow-string.<BR>	 4. Swelling, increase.<BR>	 5. A pro-<BR>tuberance.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Plenty, abundance.<BR> E. स्फर् to throb, aff. घञ्; or<BR>स्फाय् to swell, रक् Unādi aff., and the radical final rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फारण|स्फारणं
स्फारण n. (-णं) Throbbing, shaking, trembling.<BR> E. स्फर् to throb, causal<BR>form, aff. ल्युट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाल|स्फालः
स्फाल m. (-लः) Throbbing, quivering, trembling, shaking.<BR> E. स्फल् to shake, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फालन|स्फालनं
स्फालन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Shaking, quivering.<BR>	 2. Rubbing, friction.<BR>	 3. Rubbing<BR>or patting, (as a horse.)<BR> E. स्फल् to shake, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फावयत्
स्फावयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Increasing, augmenting.<BR> E. स्फाय् to<BR>increase, शतृ aff., वङ् inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिग्घातनक
स्फिग्घातनक m. (-कः) A medicinal plant, commonly Kāyaphal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिच्
स्फिच् f. Du. (-चौ) The buttocks.<BR> E. स्फाय् to swell, डिच् aff.; or स्फिट् to<BR>hurt, aff. क्विप्, form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिट्
स्फिट् r. 10th cl. (स्फेटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure, or kill.<BR>	 2. To cover.<BR>3. To despise.<BR>	 4. To love: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिट्ट्
स्फिट्ट् r. 10th cl. (स्फिट्टयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure, to kill.<BR>	 2. To dwell.<BR>3. To give.<BR>	 4. To be strong: see स्फिट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिर|स्फिरं
स्फिर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Much, many.<BR>	 2. Vast, capacious.<BR> E. स्फाय् to<BR>swell, किरच् aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फीत|स्फीतः
स्फीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Much, many.<BR>	 2. Swollen, enlarged.<BR>	 3. Suc-<BR>cessful, prosperous, risen in rank or fortune.<BR>	 4. Affected by here-<BR>ditary disease.<BR> E. स्फायी to swell, aff. क्त; also स्फात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फीति|स्फीतिः
स्फीति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Increase, enlargement.<BR>	 2. Prosperity.<BR>	 3. Plenty. E.<BR>स्फाय् to swell, क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट्
स्फुट् r. 1st cl. (स्फीटते) r. 6th cl. (स्फुटति)<BR>	 1. To blow, to blossom, to open<BR>as a bud or flower.<BR>	 2. To become manifested.<BR>	 3. To run away.<BR>4. To burst, to split open. r. 10th cl. (स्फोटयति-ते or with आङ्<BR>prefixed, आस्फोटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To hurt.<BR>	 2. To divide; also (इर) स्फुटिर्<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्फोटति) and (इ) स्फुटि r. 1st cl. (स्फुण्टति)<BR>	 1. To divide,<BR>to break, to tear, to pierce.<BR>	 2. To hurt or kill.<BR>	 3. To expand.<BR>स्फुटि r. 10th cl. (स्फुण्टयति-ते) To laugh at or with, to jest, to joke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट|स्फुटः
स्फुट mfn. (-टः-टा-टं)<BR>	 1. Blown, opened, expanded, (as a flower.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Apparent, manifest, evident.<BR>	 3. Known, understood.<BR>	 4. Plain, dis-<BR>tinct.<BR>	 5. Spread, diffused.<BR>	 6. White, bright.<BR>	 7. Burst, broken.<BR>	 8.<BR>Rent, torn.<BR>	 9. Loud.<BR>	 10. (In astronomy,) True or apparent,<BR>as स्फुटसूर्य्यगतिः true or apparent motion of the sun.<BR>	 f. (-टा) The<BR>expanded hood of a snake.<BR> E. स्फुट् to blow, as a flower, &c., aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=816-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटत्
स्फुटत् mfn. (-टन्-टन्ती or -टती-टत्)<BR>	 1. Bursting, blowing.<BR>	 2. Becoming<BR>manifest or clear.<BR>	 3. Evolving.<BR> E. स्फुट् to blow, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटता
स्फुटता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Manifestation, evidence.<BR>	 2. Blossoming.<BR> E. स्फुट, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटतार
स्फुटतार Adj. Bright with stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटन|स्फुटनं
स्फुटन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Tearing, rending.<BR>	 2. Opening, expanding.<BR> E. स्फुट् to<BR>blow, ण्फुट् aff., and the vowel unchanged; also सफोटन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटफल
स्फुटफल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. (In geometry,) Distinct or precise area of a triangle.<BR>2. The clear result of any calculation, (in geometry).<BR> E. स्फुट and<BR>फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटम्
स्फुटम् Ind. Distinctly, certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटवत्कली
स्फुटवत्कली f. (-ली) Heart-pea.<BR> E. वफुट burst, and वल्कल bark or rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटसार|स्फुटसारः
स्फुटसार m. (-रः) The true latitude of a star or planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटार्थ
स्फुटार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं) Intelligible, obvious, significant.<BR> E. स्फुट, अर्थ sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटि|स्फुटिः
स्फुटि f. (-टिः-टी)<BR>	 1. Kibe, swelling of the feet.<BR>	 2. A sort of melon,<BR>(Cucumis momordica, Rox.) “फुटि” इति भाषा ।<BR> E. स्फुट् to open or<BR>break, and कि aff., with ङीष् optionally added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटिका
स्फुटिका f. (-का) A small bit broken off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटित|स्फुटितः
स्फुटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Budded, blown.<BR>	 2. Broken, burst.<BR>	 3. Made<BR>clear.<BR>	 4. Torn, destroyed.<BR>	 5. Laughed at.<BR> E. स्फुट् to blow, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटितचरण
स्फुटितचरण Adj. Splay-footed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट्ट्
स्फुट्ट् r. 10th cl. (स्फुट्टयति-ते) To disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुड्
स्फुड् r. 6th cl. (स्फुडति) To clothe, to cover. (इ) स्फुडि r. 1st and 10th cls.<BR>(स्फुण्डते स्फुण्डयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To expand.<BR>	 2. To laugh at, to jest, to joke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुत्
स्फुत् Ind. An imitative sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुत्कर|स्फुत्करः
स्फुत्कर m. (-रः) Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुत्कार|स्फुत्कारः
स्फुत्कार m. (-रः) Crackling, burning.<BR> E. स्फुत् imitative sound, and कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्
स्फुर् r. 6th cl. (स्फुरति)<BR>	 1. To throb, to beat.<BR>	 2. To move.<BR>	 3. To swell.<BR>	 4.<BR>To struggle.<BR>	 5. To start, to dart.<BR>	 6. To spring back, to rebound.<BR>7. To break forth.<BR>	 8. To start into view.<BR>	 9. To flash, to scintillate.<BR>10. To shine.<BR>	 11. To flash on the mind.<BR>	 12. To go tremulously.<BR>13. To bruise, to destroy. With अभि, 1. To expand.<BR>	 2. To become<BR>known. With प्र, 1. To tremble.<BR>	 2. To expand.<BR>	 3. To spread wide.<BR>With वि, 1. To tremble.<BR>	 2. To struggle.<BR>	 3. To glitter.<BR>	 4. To draw,<BR>to twang, (as a bow.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर|स्फुरः
स्फुर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A shield.<BR>	 2. Throbbing, trembling.<BR>	 3. Swelling.<BR> E. स्फुर्<BR>to shake, &c., aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरण|स्फुरणं
स्फुरण nf. (-णं-णा)<BR>	 1. Trembling, throbbing, pulsation.<BR>	 2. Quivering of<BR>the lips, throbbing of the eyes, &c.<BR>	 3. Expansion of mind.<BR>	 4.<BR>Springing on memory.<BR>	 5. Springing or breaking forth, starting<BR>into view.<BR>	 6. Flashing, twinkling.<BR> E. स्फुर् to shake, aff. ल्युट् or युच्,<BR>and the radical vowel unchanged; also स्फोरण n. (-णं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरत्
स्फुरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्)<BR>	 1. Quivering, trembling, shaking, throbbing.<BR>2. Expanding, swelling.<BR>	 3. Going, moving.<BR>	 4. Going tremulously.<BR>5. Darting.<BR> E. स्फुर् to swell, &c., aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरदुल्का
स्फुरदुल्का f. (-ल्का) A shooting meteor, aerolite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरित|स्फुरितं
स्फुरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Shaken, agitated.<BR>	 2. Trembling, heaving,<BR>throbbing, palpitating.<BR>	 3. Flashing.<BR>	 4. Swelled, swollen.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>1. Trembling or throbbing of the eyelids.<BR>	 2. A throb, tremor.<BR>	 3.<BR>Emotion of the mind.<BR> E. स्फुर् to move or swell, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्च्छ्
स्फुर्च्छ् (आ) स्फुर्च्छा r. 1st cl. (स्फूर्च्छति)<BR>	 1. To spread, to expand, to extend.<BR>2. To forget; also स्वुर्च्छ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्ज्ज|स्फुर्ज
स्फुर्ज्ज r. 1st cl. (स्फुर्ज्जति)<BR>	 1. To thunder, to clash, to explode.<BR>	 2. To<BR>burn, to glitter. With वि, 1. To resound.<BR>	 2. To roar, (as wind.)<BR>	 3.<BR>To increase.: more properly स्फूर्ज्ज् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्ज्जक|स्फुर्जक|स्फुर्ज्जकः
स्फुर्ज्जक m. (-कः) A sort of ebony, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR> E. स्फुर्ज्ज् to<BR>make a noise like thunder, (on being burnt,) aff. वुन्; also स्फूर्ज्जक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्ज्जथु|स्फुर्जथु|स्फुर्जथुः
स्फुर्ज्जथु m. (-थुः) A clap of thunder.<BR> E. स्थुर्ज्ज् to sounds as thunder, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुल्
स्फुल् r. 6th cl. (स्फुलति)<BR>	 1. To throb, to vibrate.<BR>	 2. To heap, to collect.<BR>3. To be manifest or apparent.<BR>	 4. To dart forth.<BR>	 5. To go or<BR>move.<BR>	 6. To kill, to slay.<BR>	 7. To expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुल|स्फुलं
स्फुल n. (-लं) A tent.<BR> E. स्फुल् to expand, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलन|स्फुलनं
स्फुलन n. (-नं) Throbbing.<BR> E. स्फुर् to shake, aff. ल्युट्, and ल substituted for र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिङ्ग|स्फुलिंग|स्फुलिंगं|स्फुलिंगः|स्फुलिङ्गः
स्फुलिङ्ग mfn. Subst. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गा-ङ्गं) A spark of fire.<BR> E. स्फु for स्फुत् imitative<BR>sound, लिगि to go, aff. अच्; or स्फुल् to kill, इङ्गच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिङ्गिनी|स्फुलिंगिनी
स्फुलिङ्गिनी f. (-नी) One of the seven tongues of AGNI or fire.<BR> E. स्फुलिङ्ग<BR>a spark, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्ज्|स्फूर्ज्
स्फूर्ज्ज् (ओ आ) ओस्फूर्ज्जा r. 1st cl. (स्फूर्ज्जति) To thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्ज|स्फूर्ज|स्फूर्जः
स्फूर्ज्ज m. (-र्ज्जः)<BR>	 1. INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>	 2. The clashing sound of a<BR>thunder clap.<BR>	 3. Sudden burst.<BR>	 4. First union of lovers charac-<BR>terized by some joy in the beginning and fear in the end, (in<BR>dramaturgy.)<BR> E. स्फूर्ज्ज् to sound as thunder, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्जक|स्फूर्जक|स्फूर्जकः
स्फूर्ज्जक m. (-कः) A sort of ebony, (Diospyros glutinosa.)<BR> E. स्फूर्ज्ज् to sound<BR>like thunder, (in the fire, from its abounding with resin,) वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्जथु|स्फूर्जथु|स्फूर्जथुः
स्फूर्ज्जथु m. (-थुः) A clap of thunder, the sound of falling thunder, or<BR>that immediately following a stroke of lightning.<BR> E. स्फूर्ज्ज् to sound<BR>as thunder, अथुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्जन|स्फूर्जन|स्फूर्जनं
स्फूर्ज्जन n. (-नं) Thundering.<BR> E. स्फूर्ज्ज, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्ज्जावत्|स्फूर्जावत्|स्फूर्जावन्त्
स्फूर्ज्जावत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Thundering.<BR> E. स्फूर्ज्ज, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्त्ति|स्फूर्ति|स्फूर्तिः|स्फूर्त्तिः
स्फूर्त्ति f. (-र्त्तिः)<BR>	 1. Throbbing, palpitating, shaking.<BR>	 2. Blooming, open-<BR>ing.<BR>	 3. Poetical genius, “प्रतिभा”.<BR> E. स्फुर् to shake, &c., aff. क्तिन्, and<BR>the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्त्तिमत्|स्फूर्तिमत्|स्फूर्तिमन्त्
स्फूर्त्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्)<BR>	 1. Kind-hearted.<BR>	 2. Tremulous, agitated.<BR>E. स्फूर्त्ति agitation, मतुप् aff., and the म retained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेयस्
स्फेयस् mfn. (-वान्-वसी-यः) Very much or many.<BR> E. स्फिर many, ईयसुन् aff.<BR>of the comparative; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेष्ठ|स्फेष्ठः
स्फेष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very much or many.<BR> E. स्फिर much, इष्ठन् aff. of the superlative; form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोट|स्फोटः
स्फोट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. A boil, a tumour.<BR>	 2. Breaking, bursting.<BR>	 3. Revealing,<BR>disclosure, (as in नर्मस्फोट.)<BR>	 4. The idea which bursts out or flashes<BR>on the mind when a sound is uttered.<BR>	 f. (-टा) The hood of the<BR>snake.<BR> E. स्फुट् to break or open, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटक|स्फोटकः
स्फोटक m. (-कः) A boil, a tumour.<BR>	 f. (-टिका) A sort of bird.<BR> E. स्फुट् to burst, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटन|स्फोटनं|स्फोटनः
स्फोटन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Tearing, rending.<BR>	 2. The act of rending suddenly,<BR>splitting, cracking.<BR>	 3. Fidgetting with the hand, cracking the<BR>finger-joints, snapping the fingers, &c.<BR>	 4. Winnowing grain.<BR>	 5.<BR>The separation of the letters of a double consonant.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>Separated utterance of a close combination of consonants.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>Adj. Disclosing, making clear.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A gimlet, an auger. E.<BR>स्फुट् to open, (as a flower, &c.) causal form, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटवीजक
स्फोटवीजक m. (-कः) The marking-nut-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटा
स्फोटा f. (-टा) The expanded hood of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटायन|स्फोटायनः
स्फोटायन m. (-नः) A Muni so named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटित
स्फोटित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Torn, rent.<BR>	 2. Made to open or burst.<BR> E. स्फुट्<BR>to break, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फ्य|स्फ्यं
स्फ्य n. (-स्फ्यं) An implement used in sacrifices, a piece of wood<BR>shaped like a sword, for stirring the boiled-rice, or according to<BR>some for trimming the mound used as an alter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फ्यवर्त्तनि|स्फ्यवर्तनि|स्फ्यवर्तनिः
स्फ्यवर्त्तनि m. (-निः) The furrow or line made by the said implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्बॄ
स्बॄ r. 9th cl. (स्बृणाति)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to injure.<BR>	 2. To kill; more properly स्वृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्म
स्म Ind.<BR>	 1. An expletive.<BR>	 2. A particle which added to verbs in the<BR>present tense gives them a past sense, as हन्तिस्म रावणं रामः RĀMA<BR>killed (instead of kills) RĀVAṆA. It is often added to the<BR>prohibitive particle मा and used with the aorist or imperfect. E.<BR>षो to end or destroy ङ्म aff.; or ष्मिङ् to smile, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मय|स्मयः
स्मय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 2. Surprise, astonishment.<BR> E. स्मि to<BR>smile, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर|स्मरः
स्मर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. KĀMADEVA, the deity of love.<BR>	 2. Recollection.<BR> E. स्मृ to remember, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरकर्म्मन्|स्मरकर्मन्
स्मरकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Lasciviousness, wanton pleasures.<BR> E. स्मर, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरकूपक|स्मरकूपकः
स्मरकूपक mf. (-पकः-पिका) Pudendum muliebre.<BR> E. स्मर KĀMA, कूप a well,<BR>and कन् aff. of comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरगुरु|स्मरगुरुः
स्मरगुरु m. (-रुः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. स्मर love, गुरु the spiritual or natural father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=817-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरगृह|स्मरगृहं
स्मरगृह n. (-हं) The vulva.<BR> E. स्मर KĀMA, and गृह mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरच्छत्र|स्मरच्छत्रं
स्मरच्छत्र n. (-त्रं) The clitoris.<BR> E. स्मर love, छत्र an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरण|स्मरणं
स्मरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Recollecting, remembering.<BR>	 2. Memory, recollection.<BR>	 3.<BR>Regretting, remembering with regret, anxious thought.<BR>	 4. Tradi-<BR>tion, traditional precept.<BR>	 5. Name of a figure of speech.<BR>	 6. Mental<BR>recitation of the name of a deity.<BR> E. स्पृ to remember, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणपदवी
स्मरणपदवी f. (-वी) Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणानुग्रह|स्मरणानुग्रहः
स्मरणानुग्रह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. Kind remembrance.<BR>	 2. The favour of remembrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणापत्यतर्पक|स्मरणापत्यतर्पकः
स्मरणापत्यतर्पक m. (-कः) A turtle, a tortoise.<BR> E. स्मरण memory, आपत्य<BR>offspring, तर्पक who pleases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणीय
स्मरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fit or proper to be remembered.<BR> E. स्पृ to remember, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरत्
स्मरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Remembering, recollecting, considering.<BR> E. स्पृ<BR>to remember, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरदशा
स्मरदशा f. (-शा) State of the body produced by being in love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरध्वज|स्मरध्वजं|स्मरध्वजः
स्मरध्वज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Any musical instrument.<BR>	 2. The penis.<BR>	 3. A sort of<BR>fabulous fish or marine monster, the emblem of KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-जं) The vulva.<BR>	 f. (-जा) A bright moon-light night.<BR> E. स्मर KĀMA,<BR>and ध्वज emblem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरप्रिया
स्मरप्रिया f. (-या) RATI, the wife of KĀMA.<BR> E. स्मर the deity of love, and प्रिया wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरभासित
स्मरभासित Adj. Inflamed by love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरमन्दिर|स्मरमन्दिरं
स्मरमन्दिर n. (-रं) Pudendum muliebre.<BR> E. स्मर love, and मन्दिर abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरमोह|स्मरमोहः
स्मरमोह m. (-हः) Passion, love.<BR> E. स्मर, मोह fascination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरमोहित
स्मरमोहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Overcome by love or passion.<BR> E. स्मर, मोहित bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरलेखनी
स्मरलेखनी f. (-नी) The Sālika, (Turdus salica,) or Mainā, (Gracula<BR>religiosa.)<BR> E. स्मर love, लेखनी a pen, a writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरवल्लभ|स्मरवल्लभः
स्मरवल्लभ m. (-भः) ANIRUDDHA.<BR> E. स्मर KĀMA, and वल्लभ beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरवीथिका
स्मरवीथिका f. (-का) A harlot.<BR> E. स्मर love, वीथि a shop, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरसख|स्मरसखः
स्मरसख m. (-खः) The moon.<BR> E. स्मर CUPID, and सख a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरस्तम्भ|स्मरस्तम्भः
स्मरस्तम्भ m. (-म्भः) The penis.<BR> E. स्मर CUPID, स्तम्भ post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरस्मर्य्य|स्मरस्मर्य|स्मरस्मर्यः|स्मरस्मर्य्यः
स्मरस्मर्य्य m. (-र्य्यः) An ass, a donkey.<BR> E. स्मर KĀMA, स्मर्य्य to be remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरहर|स्मरहरः
स्मरहर m. (-रः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. स्मर the deity of love, हर destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मराकुल
स्मराकुल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) In love.<BR> E. स्मर, आकुल overcome; also स्मराकुलित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरामार
स्मरामार n. (-रं) The vulva.<BR> E. स्मर love, आगार abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मराङ्कुश|स्मरांकुश|स्मराङ्कुशः
स्मराङ्कुश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. A finger-nail.<BR>	 2. A lover, a lecher.<BR> E. स्मर love, and<BR>अङ्कुश a goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरातुर
स्मरातुर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Overcome with love or passion.<BR> E. स्मर, आतुर perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरान्ध|स्मरांध
स्मरान्ध mfn. (-न्धः-न्धा-न्धं) Infatuated with passion.<BR> E. स्मर, and अन्ध blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरार्त्त|स्मरार्त
स्मरार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Overcome or agitated by love, pining with love.<BR>E. स्मर, and आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरासव|स्मरासवः
स्मरासव m. (-वः) Saliva.<BR> E. स्मर love, आसव wine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरोत्सुक
स्मरोत्सुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Devoted to love.<BR> E. स्मर, and उत्सुक fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्त्तव्य|स्मर्तव्य
स्मर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Fit or proper to be remembered.<BR> E. स्मृ to<BR>remember, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्य्यमाण|स्मर्यमाण
स्मर्य्यमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Being remembered.<BR> E. स्मृ to remember, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार
स्मार f. (-रा) Adj. Relating to love.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारक
स्मारक f. (-रिका) Adj. Reminding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारण|स्मारणं
स्मारण n. (-णं) Calling to mind, reminding, causing to remember. E.<BR>स्मृ to remember, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारित
स्मारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Called to memory, caused to remember.<BR> E. स्मृ<BR>to remember, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्त्त|स्मार्त|स्मार्तः|स्मार्त्तं|स्मार्त्तः
स्मार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ती-र्त्तं)<BR>	 1. Legal, canonical, according to the doctrines<BR>of the Smṛtis or inspired codes of law.<BR>	 2. Following or professing<BR>the doctrine of the law-books.<BR>	 3. Memorial, relating to memory.<BR>4. Within memory, what may be remembered.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्तः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>Brāhman following the revealed law.<BR>	 2. One who knows the tra-<BR>ditional law.<BR>	 3. Name of a peculiar sect.<BR> E. स्मृति law collectively,<BR>and अण् aff. of reference, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्त्तकाल|स्मार्तकाल|स्मार्तकालः
स्मार्त्तकाल m. (-लः) Time to which memory may extend; according to<BR>the jurists, as far as a century.<BR> E. स्मार्त्त, and काल time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मि
स्मि r. 10th cl. (स्माययते) To slight, to disregard. (स्माययति) To astonish.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">Page818-b+ 60</a>]<BR>r. 1st cl. (स्मयते)<BR>	 1. To smile.<BR>	 2. To expand, to bloom. With उद्,<BR>To smile. With वि, 1. To be surprised.<BR>	 2. To admire.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>proud. Caus. (स्माययति-ते, स्मापयते)<BR>	 1. To cause to laugh.<BR>	 2. To mock.<BR>3. To astonish, (in this sense only स्मापयत). Also ष्मिङ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मिट्
स्मिट् r. 10th cl. (स्मेटयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To slight, to disregard, to disrespect.<BR>	 2.<BR>To love.<BR>	 3. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मित|स्मितं
स्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Smiling.<BR>	 2. Blown, (as a flower.)<BR>	 n. (-तं) A smile,<BR>a gentle laugh.<BR> E. ष्मि to smile, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितदृश्
स्मितदृश् f. (-दृक्) A handsome woman.<BR> E. स्मित, and दृश् the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितपूर्वम्
स्मितपूर्वम् Ind. Smilingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितशालिन्
स्मितशालिन् mfn. (-ली-लिनी-लि) Smiling, laughing.<BR> E. स्मित, शालिन् having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मील्
स्मील् r. 1st cl. (स्मीलति) To wink, to twinkle, to blink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृ
स्मृ r. 1st cl. (स्मरति)<BR>	 1. To remember, to recollect, to call to mind.<BR>	 2.<BR>To remember with regret, to miss, (with a genitive.)<BR>	 3. To record<BR>in a Smṛti.<BR>	 4. To recite mentally the name of a deity. r. 5th cl.<BR>(स्मृणोति)<BR>	 1. To please or delight.<BR>	 2. To guard, to protect, to<BR>cherish.<BR>	 3. To breathe or live. With वि prefixed, To forget. With<BR>सम्, To remember. With अप, To forget. With अनु, To remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत|स्मृतः
स्मृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Recollected, remembered, called to mind.<BR> E. स्मृ to<BR>remember, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृति|स्मृतिः
स्मृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Recollection, remembrance, memory.<BR>	 2. Law, the<BR>body of law, (civil and religious,) as delivered originally by MANU-<BR>YĀJNAWALKYA and other inspired legislators, to their respective<BR>pupils, and committed by them from recollection to writing,<BR>(as opposed to श्रुति or revelation.)<BR>	 3. A law-book, a code of laws.<BR>4. Wish, desire.<BR>	 5. Understanding.<BR> E. स्मृ to remember, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिपथ|स्मृतिपथः
स्मृतिपथ m. (-थः) Scope or object of memory, (used with गम or नी to<BR>mean “to be deceased”); also स्मृतिविषय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिप्रत्यवमर्ष
स्मृतिप्रत्यवमर्ष m. (-र्षः) Retentiveness of memory, accuracy of recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिप्रबन्ध|स्मृतिप्रबंध|स्मृतिप्रबन्धः
स्मृतिप्रबन्ध m. (-न्धः) A legal composition or work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिभ्रंश|स्मृतिभ्रंशः
स्मृतिभ्रंश m. (-शः) Loss of memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिमत्|स्मृतिमन्त्
स्मृतिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Remembering, recollecting, having a good<BR>memory.<BR> E. स्मृति memory, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिरोध|स्मृतिरोधः
स्मृतिरोध m. (-धः) Temporary interruption of memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविभ्रम|स्मृतिविभ्रमः
स्मृतिविभ्रम m. (-मः) Confusion of memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविरुद्ध|स्मृतिविरुद्धः
स्मृतिविरुद्ध mfn. (-द्धः-द्धा-द्धं) Illegal, unjust, contrary to law.<BR> E. स्मति<BR>jurisprudence, and विरुद्ध opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविरोध|स्मृतिविरोधः
स्मृतिविरोध m. (-धः)<BR>	 1. Opposition to law, illegality, impropriety.<BR>	 2.<BR>Disagreement between two or more codes of law.<BR> E. स्मति, and विरीध<BR>opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविषय|स्मृतिविषयः
स्मृतिविषय m. (-यः) Object of memory: see स्मृतिपथ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिशास्त्र|स्मृतिशास्त्रं
स्मृतिशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A work on law, a code, a digest, &c., as the Manu-<BR>Sanhitā, the Mitāksharā, &c.<BR>	 2. Legal science.<BR> E. स्मृति law, and<BR>शास्त्र an inspired treatise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिशेष
स्मृतिशेष Adj. Deceased, defunct, (as a person.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिसाध्य
स्मृतिसाध्य Adj. Capable of being proved by law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिसिद्ध
स्मृतिसिद्ध Adj. Established by law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिहेतु|स्मृतिहेतुः
स्मृतिहेतु m. (-तुः) The proximate cause of recollection, the act of the<BR>mind by which any thing is called to memory, association of<BR>ideas, recollection.<BR> E. स्मृति memory, and हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत्यन्तर|स्मृत्यंतर
स्मृत्यन्तर n. (-रं) Another law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत्यपेत|स्मृत्यपेतः
स्मृत्यपेत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Illegal, unjust.<BR>	 2. Forgotten.<BR>	 3. Inconsistant<BR>with Smṛti.<BR> E. स्मृति law, or memory, अप implying reverse, इत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत्युक्त
स्मृत्युक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Enjoined, prescribed, laid down in codes of<BR>law.<BR> E. स्मृति, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेर|स्मेरः
स्मेर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Smiling, laughing.<BR>	 2. Blown, opened, expanded,<BR>(as a flower.)<BR>	 3. Evident, apparent.<BR>	 m. (-रः) Manifestation,<BR>appearance.<BR> E. ष्मि to smile, रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेरमुख
स्मेरमुख mfn. (-खः-खी-खं) Having a smiling look.<BR> E. स्मेर, and मुख face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेरविष्किर|स्मेरविष्किरः
स्मेरविष्किर m. (-रः) A peacock.<BR> E. स्मेर smiling, विष्किर a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=818-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यद|स्यदः
स्यद m. (-दः) Speed, velocity.<BR> E. स्यन्द् to go, घञ् aff., the nasal rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्
स्यन् r. 10th cl. (स्यनयति-ते) To think, to consider, to reflect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्द्|स्यंद्
स्यन्द् (ऊ) स्यन्दू r. 1st cl. (स्यन्दते)<BR>	 1. To sprinkle, to drop, to ooze or distil.<BR>2. To go.<BR>	 3. To run, to flee. With अनु prefixed, अनुष्यन्दते or अनुस्यन्दते<BR>to drop, &c. With अभि, 1. To rain out.<BR>	 2. To be melted. With<BR>नि, To flow; the sibilant being optionally changed after this and<BR>other prepositions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्द|स्यंद|स्यंदः|स्यन्दः
स्यन्द m. (-न्दः)<BR>	 1. Oozing, trickling.<BR>	 2. Going, moving.<BR>	 3. A car, a<BR>chariot.<BR> E. स्यन्द् to go, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दन|स्यंदन|स्यन्दनं|स्यन्दनः
स्यन्दन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Quick, expeditious.<BR>	 2. Going quickly.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-नः)<BR>	 1. A war-chariot.<BR>	 2. A tree, (Dalbergia ougeinensis.) “तिनिश<BR>वृक्षे” । 3. A Jina of the past era.<BR>	 4. Air, wind.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Dropping,<BR>oozing, trickling.<BR>	 2. Water.<BR>	 3. Going swiftly.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Saliva. E.<BR>स्यन्द् to go, युच् or ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनद्रुम|स्यन्दनद्रुमः
स्यन्दनद्रुम m. (-मः) A timber tree, (Dalbergia ougeinensis.)<BR> E. स्यन्दन a<BR>car, and द्रुम a tree; the wood being used to make wheels, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनारूढ
स्यन्दनारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Mounted on or riding in a car.<BR> E. स्यन्दन, and<BR>आरूढ ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनारोह|स्यंदनारोह|स्यन्दनारोहः
स्यन्दनारोह m. (-हः) A warrior who fights in a car.<BR> E. स्यन्दन a war-<BR>chariot, and आरोह who ascends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनि|स्यन्दनिः
स्यन्दनि m. (-निः) A tree, (Dalbergia ougeinensis.)<BR> E. स्यन्दन a car, ञि aff.; or स्यन्द्, अनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनिका|स्यंदनिका
स्यन्दनिका f. (-का) A drop of saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दिन्|स्यंदिन्
स्यन्दिन् mfn. (-न्दी-न्दिनी-न्दि)<BR>	 1. Oozing, trickling, dropping.<BR>	 2. Going,<BR>moving.<BR>	 f. (-न्दिनी)<BR>	 1. Saliva.<BR>	 2. A cow bearing twins.<BR> E. स्यन्द् to<BR>drop or flow, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्न|स्यन्नः
स्यन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Flowing, dropping, or trickling.<BR> E. स्यन्द to drop, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यम्
स्यम् r. 1st cl. (स्यमति) To sound. r. 10th cl. (स्यमयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sound, to<BR>cry aloud, to shout.<BR>	 2. To go.<BR>	 3. To consider. (स्यामयति-ते) To think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमन्तक|स्यमंतक|स्यमंतकः|स्यमन्तकः
स्यमन्तक m. (-कः) The gem worn by KṚṢṆA. Formerly the gem was<BR>given to SATRĀJIT by the sun, and transferred by him to his<BR>brother PRASENA, from whom it was taken by JĀMBAVAT. After<BR>much fighting it was appropriated by KṚṢṆA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमिका
स्यमिका f. (-का) Indigo. E. See the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमीक|स्यमीकः
स्यमीक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An ant-hill.<BR>	 2. A kind of tree.<BR>	 3. Time.<BR>	 4. A cloud.<BR>f. (-का) Indigo.<BR> E. स्यम् to sound, कन् Unādi aff. with ईट् augment;<BR>or स्यम्-ईकक् aff.; also with इट्, स्यमिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यात्
स्यात् Ind. It may be perhaps, perchance, &c.; implying doubt, as स्यादस्ति,<BR>स्यान्नास्ति it may be, it may not be. E. The verbal conditional form<BR>used as a particle, or third person singular of the potential of अस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्याद्वाद|स्याद्वादः
स्याद्वाद m. (-दः) An assertion of probability, (in philosophy.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्याद्वादिक
स्याद्वादिक m. (-कः) A sceptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्याल|स्यालः
स्याल m. (-लः) A wife's brother.<BR> E. स्यम् to consider, aff. अच्, and म<BR>changed to ल; more properly श्याल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्युम्र
स्युम्र n. (-म्रं) Happiness, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूत|स्यूतः
स्यूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sewn, stitched.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A sack.<BR> E. षिव् to sew, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूति|स्यूतिः
स्यूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Sewing, stitching, working with needle and thread.<BR>2. Offspring, lineage.<BR>	 3. A sack, a bag.<BR> E. षिव् to sew, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यून|स्यूनः
स्यून m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR>	 3. A sack, a bag.<BR> E. षिव् to<BR>sew, Unādi aff. नक्, and यूच् substituted for the last two radical<BR>letters; also with the vowel of the augment changed स्योन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूम|स्यूमं|स्यूमः
स्यूम m. (-मः) A ray of light.<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Water.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR> E. षिव<BR>to sew, मक् Unādi aff., and यूच् substituted for the radical finals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योत|स्योतः
स्योत m. (-तः) A sack, a coarse canvas-bag.<BR> E. षिव् to sew, क्त aff., यूच्<BR>substituted for the finals, and the vowel changed; also स्यूत ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योन|स्योनः
स्योन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. A ray of light.<BR>	 3. A coarse canvas bag or<BR>sack.<BR>	 n. (-नं) Happiness, pleasure.<BR>	 f. (-ना) Adj.<BR>	 1. Beautiful.<BR>	 2.<BR>Auspicious.<BR> E. विव् to sew, Unādi aff. न, and यूच् substituted for<BR>the radical finals, and the vowel changed.: see स्यून ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंस्
स्रंस् (उ) स्रंसु r. 1st cl. (स्रंसते)<BR>	 1. To fall down, to drop, to slip down or<BR>off, to tumble.<BR>	 2. To fall asunder.<BR>	 3. To hang down.<BR>	 4. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंस|स्रंसः
स्रंस m. (-स्रः) Falling, slipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसन|स्रंसनं
स्रंसन n. (-नं) The act of bringing down.<BR> E. स्रंस्, ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसमान
स्रंसमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Falling, dropping, slipping off or down.<BR>	 2.<BR>Fainting.<BR> E. स्रस् to fall, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसिन्
स्रंसिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि)<BR>	 1. Falling or hanging down.<BR>	 2. Pendulous,<BR>depending.<BR>	 3. Being loosened.<BR>	 m. (-सी) A tree, commonly Pilu,<BR>and applied to several sorts, (as to Careya arborea, and Salvadora<BR>Persica, &c.)<BR> E. स्रंस् to fall down, aff. णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसिनीफल|स्रंसिनीफलः
स्रंसिनीफल m. (-लः) A tree, (Mimosa Sirisha.)<BR> E. स्रंसिनी pendulous, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंह्
स्रंह् r. 1st cl. (स्रङ्कते) To trust, to confide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रक्
स्रक् (इ) स्रकि r. 1st cl. (म्रङ्कते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्दाम
स्रग्दाम n. (-मं) The fillet or tie of a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्धर
स्रग्धर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Wearing a garland.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A species of the<BR>Prakriti metre, a stanza of four lines of 21 syllables, and each<BR>line divided into three portions of seven syllables each.<BR> E. स्रज्<BR>a chaplet, and धर who has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्विन्
स्रग्विन् mfn. (-वी-विनी-वि) Bearing a chaplet, &c.<BR>	 f. (-विनी) A species of<BR>Jagati metre.<BR> E. स्रज् a garland, विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्
स्रज् f. (-स्रक् or -स्रग्)<BR>	 1. A chaplet, a wreath of flowers worn over the<BR>forehead.<BR>	 2. Any garland or string of flowers.<BR> E. सृज् to quit, क्तिन्<BR>aff., and the vowel changed to its congener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रजिष्ठ|स्रजिष्ठः
स्रजिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Covered with garlands, profusely decorated<BR>with chaplets, &c.<BR> E. स्नग्विन् having a garland, इष्ठन् aff. of the irr.<BR>superlative and the possessive termination dropped; also with<BR>ईयसुन् aff. of the same, स्रजीयस् mfn. (-यान्-यसी-यः ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्वा
स्रज्वा f. (-ज्वा) A rope, a string, a cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रद्धू
स्रद्धू f. (-द्धूः) A fart.<BR> E. शृध् to fart, ऊ aff.; more properly शर्द्ध ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रम्भ्|स्रंभ्
स्रम्भ् (उ) स्नम्भु r. 1st cl. (स्रम्भते) To trust, to have faith or confidence in.<BR>With वि, 1. To entrust.<BR>	 2. To be careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रव|स्रवः
स्रव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Oozing, dropping, trickling, flowing, the gradual<BR>issue or progress of any fluid.<BR>	 2. A drop.<BR>	 3. A fountain.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>A plant, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR> E. स्रु to flow or drop, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवण|स्रवणं
स्रवण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Oozing, flowing, trickling.<BR>	 2. Sweat, perspiration.<BR>	 3.<BR>Piss, urine.<BR> E. स्रु to ooze, aff. ल्यु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवत्
स्रवत् mfn. (-वान्-वन्ती-वत्)<BR>	 1. Oozing.<BR>	 2. Dropping, distilling.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1.<BR>A river in general.<BR>	 2. The situation of the spleen, the left<BR>hypochondriac region.<BR>	 3. A drug.<BR> E. स्नु to drop, participial aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवत्स्वेदजल
स्रवत्स्वेदजल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Perspiring much, covered with perspira-<BR>tion.<BR> E. स्रवत्, स्वेदजल perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवद्गर्भा
स्रवद्गर्भा f. (-र्भा) A woman or cow miscarrying by accident.<BR> E. स्नवत् falling, गर्भ the fœtus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवद्रङ्ग|स्रवद्रङ्गः
स्रवद्रङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A fair, a market.<BR> E. स्रवत् moving, रङ्ग an assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रष्टृ
स्रष्टृ m. (-ष्टा)<BR>	 1. A creator, a maker.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. ŚIVA.<BR> E. सृज् to<BR>create, तृच् aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्त|स्रस्तं
स्रस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं)<BR>	 1. Fallen down, off, or from.<BR>	 2. Separated, dis-<BR>joined.<BR>	 3. Loosened, relaxed, given way.<BR>	 4. Hanging down. E.<BR>स्रंस् to fall, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तर|स्रस्तरः
स्रस्तर m. (-रं) A couch or sofa for reclining.<BR> E. स्रंस्-रिच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तहस्त
स्रस्तहस्त mfn. (-स्तः-स्ता-स्तं) Letting go, relaxing one's hold.<BR> E. स्रस्त, हस्त the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्ताङ्ग|स्रस्तांग
स्रस्ताङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Having the limbs relaxed, swooning, fainting,<BR>falling.<BR> E. स्रस्त, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राक्
स्राक् Ind. Quickly, instantly.<BR> E. स्रै to cook or ripen, क्विप् aff.; or स्रा<BR>maturity, अक् to obtain, क्विप् aff.; or स्रु-डाकु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राव|स्रावः
स्राव m. (-वः) Oozing, flowing, dropping.<BR> E. स्रु to go or flow, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रावक|स्रावकं
स्रावक n. (-कं) Black-pepper.<BR>	 f. (-विका) Adj. Exuding, letting flow. E.<BR>स्रु to ooze, causal form, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिभ्
स्रिभ् (उ) स्रिभु r. 1st cl. (स्रेभति) To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिम्भ्|स्रिंभ्
स्रिम्भ् (उ) स्रिम्भु r. 1st cl. (स्रिम्भति) To hurt or kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिव्
स्रिव् (उ) स्रिवु r. 4th cl. (स्रीव्यति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To become dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रु|स्रुः
स्रु r. 1st cl. (स्रवति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To flow.<BR>	 3. To drop, to distil,<BR>to ooze.<BR>	 4. To trickle away.<BR>	 5. To transpire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=819-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुग्दारु
स्रुग्दारु m. (-रुः) A plant, (Flacourtia.)<BR> E. स्नुच् a sacrificial ladle, दारु wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुध्नी
स्रुध्नी f. (-ध्नी) Natron, alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुच्
स्रुच् f. (-स्नुक् or -स्नुग्) A sort of ladle or long spoon, generally made of<BR>Vikankata-wood, and used to pour Ghee or clarified butter upon<BR>the sacrificial fire.<BR> E. स्नु to drop, (Ghee,) क्विप् aff., and चिट् final<BR>augment; also with टाप्, स्नुचा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुत|स्रुतं
स्रुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Flowing, dropping, falling, (as a fluid.)<BR>	 f. (-ता) A<BR>drug, commonly Hingupatri.<BR> E. स्नु to flow, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुति|स्रुतिः
स्रुति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Oozing.<BR>	 2. A stream.<BR>	 3. Exudation, resin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुव|स्रुवः
स्रुव mf. (-वः-वा) A ladle with a double extremity, or two oval collateral<BR>excavations made of Khadira-wood, and used to pour Ghee upon<BR>the sacrificial fire.<BR>	 f. (-वा)<BR>	 1. A shrub, (Sanseviera zeylanica.)<BR>	 3. A<BR>tree, (Boswellia thurifera.)<BR> E. स्नु to drop or ooze, (from or by it,) aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवावृक्ष|स्रुवावृक्षः
स्रुवावृक्ष m. (-क्षः) A plant, (Flacourtia aspida, Rox.)<BR> E. स्नुवा a sacri-<BR>ficial ladle, and वृक्ष a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रू
स्रू f. (-स्रूः)<BR>	 1. A sacrificial ladle: see स्नुव.<BR>	 2. A cascade.<BR> E. स्नु to drop,<BR>(Ghee from it,) Unādi aff. क्विप्, and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रेक्
स्रेक् (ऋ) स्रेकृ r. 1st cl. (स्रेकते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रै
स्रै r. 1st cl. (स्रायति)<BR>	 1. To boil or melt; also श्रै and श्रा.<BR>	 2. To cook or ripen.<BR>	 3. To sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोत|स्रोतं|स्रोतः
स्रोत n. (-तं) A natural or rapid stream: see स्रोतस्.<BR> E. स्नु-तन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतईश|स्रोतईशः
स्रोतईश m. (-शः) The ocean.<BR> E. स्रोतस a stream, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्
स्रोतस् n. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A current, a natural or rapid stream.<BR>	 2. A river in<BR>general.<BR>	 3. The flow or course of water.<BR>	 4. Water.<BR>	 5. A spring.<BR>	 6.<BR>A wave.<BR>	 7. An organ of sense.<BR>	 8. The trunk of an elephant.<BR> E. स्नु-<BR>तसि aff.; or स्नु to flow, Unādi aff. असुन्, and तुट् augment; also<BR>with a final vowel स्रोत, and palatial sibilant श्रोतस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्य|स्रोतस्यः
स्रोतस्य m. (-स्यः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A thief.<BR> E. स्रोतस् a stream, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्वती
स्रोतस्वती f. (-ती) A river.<BR> E. स्रोतस् a current, मतुप् poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्विनी
स्रोतस्विनी f. (-नी) A river.<BR> E. स्रोतस् a current, and विनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोञ्जन|स्रोतोञ्जनं
स्रोतोऽञ्जन n. (-नं) Antimony.<BR> E. स्रोतस् a stream, and अञ्जन collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोरन्ध्र|स्रोतोरंध्र
स्रोतोरन्ध्र n. (-न्ध्रं) The aperture of the trunk of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोवह
स्रोतोवह mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Flowing like a stream or river.<BR>	 f. (-हा) A river<BR>in general.<BR> E. स्रोतस् a stream, and वह bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्व|स्वं|स्वः
स्व Pron.<BR>	 mfn. (-स्वः-स्वा-स्वं) Own. Subst.<BR>	 m. (-स्वः)<BR>	 1. A kinsman.<BR>	 2.<BR>The soul.<BR>	 3. Wealth.<BR>	 4. Self-identity, individuality.<BR>	 mn. (-स्वः-स्वं)<BR>1. Wealth, property.<BR>	 2. (In algebra,) Plus, or affirmative quantity.<BR>f. (-स्वा) Pron. Adj.<BR>	 1. Belonging to oneself.<BR>	 2. Of one's own tribe<BR>or family.<BR>	 3. Natural, original.<BR> E. स्वन् to sound, aff. ड; or वू<BR>to send or order, व aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक|स्वकं|स्वकः
स्वक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Own, proper, peculiar.<BR> E. स्व as above, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकम्पन|स्वकंपन|स्वकम्पनः
स्वकम्पन m. (-नः) Air, wind.<BR> E. स्व self, कम्पन agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्म्मकृत्|स्वकर्मकृत्
स्वकर्म्मकृत् m. (-कृत्) An independent workman, one doing business on<BR>his own account.<BR> E. स्व own, कर्म्म business, and कृत् who does.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्म्मन्|स्वकर्मन्
स्वकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Own act, business, duty, conduct, &c.<BR> E. स्व, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्म्मवश|स्वकर्मवश
स्वकर्म्मवश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Suffering the consequences of one's own acts.<BR>E. स्वकर्म्म, and वश subject to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्म्मस्थ|स्वकर्मस्थ
स्वकर्म्मस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Who or what adheres to its own business<BR>or duty.<BR> E. स्वकर्म्म, स्थ staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकार्य्य|स्वकार्य
स्वकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) Own business or duty.<BR> E. स्व, and कार्य्य act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकीय|स्वकीयः
स्वकीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. Of one's own family.<BR>	 2. Own in general, as<BR>property, &c.<BR> E. स्व own, छ aff., and कुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकुटुम्ब
स्वकुटुम्ब n. (-म्बं) Own family.<BR> E. स्व, and कुटुम्ब family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकुल
स्वकुल n. (-लं) Own family or race.<BR> E. स्व, and कुल race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकुलक्षय|स्वकुलक्षयः
स्वकुलक्षय m. (-यः) A fish.<BR> E. स्व own, कुल race, क्षय destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकृत
स्वकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Done or made by one's self-performed.<BR> E. स्व, कृत done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक्ष
स्वक्ष mfn. (-क्षः-क्षा) or -क्षी-क्षं)<BR>	 1. Handsome-eyed.<BR>	 2. Acute, sensitive, having<BR>keen organs.<BR> E. सु good, अक्षि the eye, or अक्ष an organ of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वग्
स्वग् (इ) स्वगि r. 1st cl. (स्वङ्गति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगत|स्वगतं
स्वगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Kept to one's self, apart, aside.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Aside, (in<BR>theatrical language.)<BR> E. स्व self, गत gone, got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगुप्त
स्वगुप्त mfn. (-प्तः-प्ता-प्तं) Self-defended or preserved.<BR>	 f. (-प्ता) Cowach,<BR>(Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. स्व self, गुप्त preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगृह|स्वगृहः
स्वगृह m. (-हः) A small bird, (Loxia Philippensis.) “कलिकार स्वगे”.<BR>n. (-हं) Own house.<BR> E. स्व own, गृह house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वङ्ग|स्वंग|स्वंगः|स्वङ्गः
स्वङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Handsome and well-shaped.<BR>	 m. (-ङ्गः) An<BR>embrace.<BR> E. सु excellent, अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छ|स्वच्छं|स्वच्छः
स्वच्छ mfn. (-च्छः-च्छा-च्छं)<BR>	 1. Healthy, sound, convalescent.<BR>	 2. White.<BR>3. Pure, free from stain or soil.<BR>	 4. Transparent, pellucid.<BR>	 m. (-च्छः)<BR>1. Pearl.<BR>	 2. Quartz.<BR> E. सु exceedingly, and अच्छ clean, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छता
स्वच्छता f. (-ता) Purity, transparency, &c.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also<BR>with त्व, स्वच्छत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छन्द|स्वच्छंद|स्वच्छन्दः|स्वछन्द
स्वच्छन्द mfn. (-न्दः-न्दा-न्दं)<BR>	 1. Unrestrained, uncontrolled, self-willed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Spontaneous.<BR>	 2. Uncultivated.<BR>	 m. (-न्दः) Own fancy, own choice,<BR>independence.<BR> E. स्व own, and छन्द inclination; also स्वच्छन्दक mfn.<BR>(-कः-का-कं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छन्दम्|स्वच्छंदम्
स्वच्छन्दम् Ind. Voluntarily, wantonly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छपत्र|स्वच्छपत्रं
स्वच्छपत्र n. (-त्रं) Talc.<BR> E. स्वच्छ transparent, and पत्र a leaf, a layer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छमणि|स्वच्छमणिः
स्वच्छमणि m. (-णिः) Crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज|स्वजं|स्वजः
स्वज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Self-born, produced in or by one's self.<BR>	 m. (-जः)<BR>1. A son.<BR>	 2. Sweat, perspiration.<BR>	 n. (-जं) Blood.<BR>	 f. (-जा) A daughter.<BR>E. स्व own, self, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजन|स्वजनः
स्वजन m. (-नः) A distant kinsman.<BR> E. स्व own, जन man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजाति|स्वजातिः
स्वजाति f. (-तिः) Own caste, tribe, or species.<BR> E. स्व, and जाति sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजातीय
स्वजातीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Of one's own tribe, caste, species, &c.<BR> E. स्व,<BR>and जातीय of a caste, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज्ञाति|स्वज्ञातिः
स्वज्ञाति f. (-तिः) Kindred, kin.<BR>	 m. (-तिः) A kinsman.<BR> E. स्व, and ज्ञाति kin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वठ्
स्वठ् r. 10th cl. (स्वठयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To finish.<BR>	 2. To leave unfinished.<BR>	 3. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतन्त्र|स्वतंत्र|स्वतन्त्रः
स्वतन्त्र mfn. (-न्त्रः-न्त्रा-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. Unrestrained, uncontrolled, self-willed.<BR>	 2.<BR>Independent, free.<BR>	 3. Full-grown, of age, no longer subject to<BR>the authority of parents, &c.<BR> E. स्व own, तन्त्र inclination, will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतन्त्रता
स्वतन्त्रता f. (-ता) Independence, wilfulness.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतस्
स्वतस् Ind.<BR>	 1. Of itself, by one's self.<BR>	 2. Own, peculiar.<BR> E. स्व self, तसिल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्र|स्वत्रः
स्वत्र mfn. (-त्रः-त्रा-त्रं) Self-preserving.<BR>	 m. (-त्रः) A blind man.<BR> E. स्व self,<BR>and त्र who preserves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्व|स्वत्वं
स्वत्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Self-existence, independent being or condition.<BR>	 2. Own<BR>right or property, ownership, proprietary right, (in law.)<BR> E. स्व<BR>own, and त्व aff. of the abstract; also स्वत्ता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वनिवृत्ति|स्वत्वनिवृत्तिः
स्वत्वनिवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Cessation or loss of proprietary right.<BR> E. स्वत्व, निवृत्ति cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वबोधन
स्वत्वबोधन n. (-नं) Indication or proof of ownership.<BR> E. स्वत्व, and बोधन<BR>making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वव्यभिचारित्व
स्वत्वव्यभिचारित्व n. (-त्वं) Doubt or uncertainty of ownership.<BR> E. स्वत्व, and<BR>व्यभिचारित्व want of steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वहानि|स्वत्वहानिः
स्वत्वहानि f. (-निः) Loss or forfeiture of proprietary title or right.<BR> E. स्वत्व, हानि loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वहेतु|स्वत्वहेतुः
स्वत्वहेतु m. (-तुः) Ground or cause of proprietary right.<BR> E. स्वत्व, हेतु cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वाभाव
स्वत्वाभाव m. (-वः) Nonexistence of proprietary right.<BR> E. स्वत्व, and अभाव<BR>nonexistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वावगम
स्वत्वावगम m. (-मः) Determination or ascertainment of ownership.<BR> E. स्वत्व, अवगम certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वास्पद
स्वत्वास्पद n. (-दं) The subject or thing in which proprietary right is<BR>vested.<BR> E. स्वत्व, आस्पद site.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वोत्पत्ति
स्वत्वोत्पत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Origin or production of proprietary right.<BR> E. स्वत्व, उत्पत्ति production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वद्
स्वद् r. 1st cl. (स्वदते)<BR>	 1. To be pleasant to the taste, to be liked, (with<BR>a dative.)<BR>	 2. To taste, to eat, to relish.<BR>	 3. To please. r. 10th cl.<BR>(स्वादयति-ते) To sweeten, to make sweet; also ष्वद् and स्वाद् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदन|स्वदनं
स्वदन n. (-नं) Eating, tasting.<BR> E. स्वद् to taste, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदारनिरत
स्वदारनिरत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uxorious, devoted to a wife.<BR> E. स्व own, दार<BR>wife, निरत attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदित
स्वदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Eaten, well-eaten, tasted.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The term used<BR>after presenting food to the manes, asking if they are satisfied. E.<BR>स्वद् to taste, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदेश|स्वदेशः
स्वदेश m. (-शः)<BR>	 1. Native country, home.<BR>	 2. Own or proper place.<BR> E. स्व, देश country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=820-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदणपरिधि
स्वदणपरिधि m. (-धिः) Circumference of a circle of longitude in any<BR>place that has latitude.<BR> E. स्वदेश, and परिधि circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदेशमध्यपरिधि
स्वदेशमध्यपरिधि m. (-धिः) Circumference of the terrestrial equator. E.<BR>स्वदेश, मध्य centre, and परिधि circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म्म|स्वधर्म|स्वधर्मः|स्वधर्म्मः
स्वधर्म्म mn. (-र्म्मः-र्म्मं)<BR>	 1. Peculiar duty or occupation, as praying of a<BR>Brāhman, fighting of a soldier, &c.<BR>	 2. Property, peculiarity.<BR> E. स्व<BR>own, धर्म्म virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म्मच्युत|स्वधर्मच्युत
स्वधर्म्मच्युत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Neglecting one's duty.<BR> E. स्वधर्म्म, च्युत fallen from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म्मत्याग|स्वधर्मत्याग
स्वधर्म्मत्याग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Neglect of duty.<BR>	 2. Apostasy.<BR> E. स्वधर्म्म, त्याग<BR>abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म्मस्खलन|स्वधर्मस्खलन
स्वधर्म्मस्खलन n. (-नं) Neglecting or disregarding duty.<BR> E. स्वधर्म्म, and स्खलन slipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्म्मस्थ|स्वधर्मस्थ
स्वधर्म्मस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) Attached to or performing one's peculiar<BR>duty.<BR> E. स्वधर्म्म, and स्थ who or what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वघा
स्वघा Ind. (Aptote noun.) An exclamation used on presenting an<BR>oblation to the Manes.<BR>	 f. (-धा)<BR>	 1. A personification of Māyā or<BR>worldly illusion, the self-contained associate of the Creator.<BR>	 2. A<BR>nymph, the food of the Manes personified, and sometimes<BR>represented as the wife of AGNI or fire.<BR>	 3. Spontaneity.<BR>	 4. Self-<BR>will.<BR>	 5. The food offered to deceased ancestors.<BR> E. ष्वद् to taste, आ<BR>aff., and द changed to ध; or स्व self, धा to hold, affs. अ and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाकार|स्वधाकारः
स्वधाकार m. (-रः) Pronouncing the exclamation Swadhā.<BR> E. स्वधा, and<BR>कार making; also स्वधाकर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाप्रिय|स्वधाप्रियः
स्वधाप्रिय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Black sesamum.<BR>	 2. AGNI or fire.<BR> E. स्वधा the<BR>exclamation used in making oblations to the Manes, प्रिय fond of<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाभुज्
स्वधाभुज् m. (-भुक्)<BR>	 1. A divine or deified ancestor.<BR>	 2. A deity.<BR> E. स्वधा<BR>the food of the Manes, भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधिति|स्वधितिः
स्वधिति mf. (-तिः-ती) An axe.<BR> E. स्व self, धा to hold, क्तिच् aff.; with ङीप्<BR>added, स्वधिती; also read श्वधिति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधितिहेतिक|स्वधितिहेतिकः
स्वधितिहेतिक m. (-कः) A soldier armed with an axe.<BR> E. स्वधिति an axe, हेतिक armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधीत
स्वधीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well read, versed in.<BR> E. सु, and अधीत read.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन्
स्वन् r. 1st cl. (स्वनति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To sing. Caus. (स्वनयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>make to resound.<BR>	 2. To sound.<BR>	 3. To dress, to adorn, (in this sense<BR>more usually स्वानयति-ते). With वि or अव prefixed, in a limited<BR>sense, the initial is changed, (अवष्वणति or विष्वणति) To make a<BR>noise whilst eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन|स्वनः
स्वन m. (-नः) Sound in general.<BR> E. स्वन् to sound, aff. अप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनगर
स्वनगर n. (-रं) Own or native town.<BR> E. स्व, and नगर city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनत्
स्वनत् mfn. (-नन्-नन्ती-नत्) Sounding.<BR> E. स्वन् to sound, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनवत्|स्वनवन्त्
स्वनवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Sounding, thundering.<BR> E. स्वन sound, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनाश
स्वनाश m. (-शः) Self-destruction.<BR> E. स्व, and नाश loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनि|स्वनिः
स्वनि m. (-निः) Sound, noise.<BR> E. स्वन् to sound, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनिक
स्वनिक m. (-कः) One who clasps his hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनित|स्वनितं
स्वनित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sounded, sounding, making a noise.<BR>	 n. (-तं) The<BR>noise of thunder.<BR> E. स्वन् to sound, aff. क्त; or स्वन sound, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनुष्ठित
स्वनुष्ठित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well or duly observed, practised, performed,<BR>&c.<BR> E. सु well, अनुष्ठित followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनोत्साह|स्वनोत्साहः
स्वनोत्साह m. (-हः) A rhinoceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपत्
स्वपत् mfn. (-पन्-पन्ती-पत्) Sleeping.<BR> E. ष्वप् to sleep, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपन|स्वपनं
स्वपन n. (-नं) Sleep, sleeping.<BR> E. ष्वप् to sleep, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपरमण्डल|स्वपरमंडल
स्वपरमण्डल n. (-लं) One's own and an enemy's country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्न|स्वप्नः
स्वप्न m. (-प्नः)<BR>	 1. Sleep.<BR>	 2. Dreaming, a dream.<BR>	 3. Indolence, sleepi-<BR>ness.<BR> E. ष्वप् to sleep, न Unādi aff., तन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नकृत्
स्वप्नकृत् mfn. (-कृत्) Narcotic, producing sleep.<BR>	 n. (-कृत्) A potherb,<BR>(Marsilea quadrifolia.) “सुसुनि शाक” इति भाषा.<BR> E. स्वप्न sleep, कृत् making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नगृह
स्वप्नगृह n. (-हं) A bed-chamber.<BR> E. स्वप्न, and गृह a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नज्
स्वप्नज् mfn. (-प्नक्) Sleeping, sleepy, asleep.<BR> E. ष्वप् to sleep, नजिङ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नदोष|स्वप्नदोषः
स्वप्नदोष n. (-षं) Pollutio nocturna.<BR> E. स्वप्न, दोष fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नधीगम्य
स्वप्नधीगम्य Adj. Perceptible by the intellect (only) in a state of sleep-like abstraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्ननिकेतन
स्वप्ननिकेतन n. (-नं) A bed-chamber.<BR> E. स्वप्न, निकेतन a dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नप्रपञ्च|स्वप्नप्रपंच|स्वप्नप्रपञ्चः
स्वप्नप्रपञ्च m. (-ञ्चः) The illusions of sleep, the world as represented in a dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नविचार|स्वप्नविचारः
स्वप्नविचार m. (-रः) Interpretation of dreams.<BR> E. स्वप्न, विचार investigation<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नविचारिन्
स्वप्नविचारिन् m. (-री) An interpreter of dreams.<BR> E. स्वप्न a dream, an<BR>विचारिन् who investigates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नशील
स्वप्नशील mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Sleepy, drowsy.<BR> E. स्वप्न, and शील having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नसृष्टि|स्वप्नसृष्टिः
स्वप्नसृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) The creation of dreams or illusions in sleep<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नावस्था
स्वप्नावस्था f. (-स्था) State of dreaming, applied especially to life or<BR>ignorance of worldly illusion.<BR> E. स्वप्न, and अवस्था state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नोपम
स्वप्नोपम Adj.<BR>	 1. Resembling a dream.<BR>	 2. Transitory, evanescent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्रकाश
स्वप्रकाश Adj. Self-evident, self-luminous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्रयोगात्
स्वप्रयोगात् Ind. By means of one's own exertions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभट|स्वभटः
स्वभट m. (-टः) One's own warrior, body-guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभाजन|स्वभाजनं
स्वभाजन n. (-नं) Civility, courtesy, welcome or adieu.<BR> E. स्व self, भज् to<BR>serve, causal form, aff. ल्युट्; also सभाजन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभाव|स्वभावः
स्वभाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Nature, natural state, property or disposition.<BR>	 2.<BR>Purpose, intention.<BR> E. स्व own, and भाव property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावज
स्वभावज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Innate, natural, produced from, or by the<BR>natural disposition.<BR> E. स्वभाव, and ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावतस्
स्वभावतस् Ind. From or according to natural property or disposition. E.<BR>स्वभाव, and तसि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावदौर्जन्य
स्वभावदौर्जन्य n. (-न्यं) Natural or innate wickedness.<BR> E. स्वभाव, and दौर्जन badness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावद्वेष
स्वभावद्वेष m. (-षः) Natural or inherent enmity.<BR> E. स्वभाव, and द्वेष hate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावोक्त
स्वभावोक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Uttered or declared naturally or spontane-<BR>ously.<BR> E. स्वभाव, and उक्त said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावोक्ति
स्वभावोक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Spontaneous declaration.<BR>	 2. Description of living<BR>objects by circumstances or acts suited to their character, (in<BR>rhetoric.)<BR> E. स्वभाव, and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभू
स्वभू m. (-भूः)<BR>	 1. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. KĀMA.<BR> E. स्व self, भु born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभूमि
स्वभूमि f. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. Own land or estate.<BR>	 2. Native country.<BR> E. स्व, भूमि land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंग्रह
स्वयंग्रह m. (-हः) The taking for one's self, (without leave.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंवर|स्वयंवरः
स्वयंवर m. (-रः) The public choice of a husband by a princess, from a<BR>number of suitors assembled for the purpose.<BR>	 f. (-रा) A girl<BR>choosing her husband.<BR> E. स्वयम् of herself, वर selecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंशीर्ण
स्वयंशीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Fallen or dropped spontaneously.<BR> E. स्वयम्,<BR>and शीर्ण decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयङ्कुत
स्वयङ्कुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Self-formed, natural, spontaneous.<BR>	 2. Done<BR>to one's self.<BR>	 3. Done by or for one's self.<BR> E. स्वयम् self, कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयङ्गुप्ता|स्वयंगुप्ता
स्वयङ्गुप्ता f. (-प्ता) Cowach, (Carpopogon pruriens.)<BR> E. स्वयम् self, गुप्त<BR>preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयन्दत्त|स्वयंदत्त|स्वयन्दत्तः|स्वयंदत्तः
स्वयन्दत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Self-given.<BR>	 m. (-त्तः) A child who has given<BR>himself to adoptive parents.<BR> E. स्वयम् self, and दत्त given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्
स्वयम् Ind. Self, spontaneously, of one's own self or own accord, (this<BR>word is applicable to all persons, such as myself, thyself, itself,<BR>herself, &c., and is sometimes used emphatically with other<BR>pronouns.)<BR> E. सु auspiciously, अय् to go, अम् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमुक्ति|स्वयमुक्तिः
स्वयमुक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Voluntary declaration.<BR>	 2. (In law,) Information,<BR>deposition.<BR> E. स्वयम्, उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्प्रभ|स्वयंप्रभ|स्वयंप्रभः
स्वयम्प्रभ m. (-भः) A Jaina of the future era.<BR> E. स्वयम् self, प्रभ illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भु|स्वयंभु|स्वयम्भुः
स्वयम्भु m. (-म्भुः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. स्वयम् + भू-डु aff.: see स्वयम्भू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भुव|स्वयंभुव|स्वयम्भुवः
स्वयम्भुव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. The first MANU.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 3. Śiva.<BR> E. स्वयम् self,<BR>भू to be or exist, aff. क; or स्वयम्भ BRAHMĀ, and अण् pleonasm or<BR>patronymic aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भू|स्वयंभू
स्वयम्भू m. (-म्भूः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. A Jina or Jaina deified sage.<BR>	 3. An<BR>emperor of the world according to the Jainas.<BR>	 4. KĀLA, the deity<BR>presiding over time.<BR>	 5. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 6. ŚIVA.<BR>	 7. The god of love.<BR>	 8.<BR>The female breast.<BR> E. स्वयम् self, भू to exist, क्विप् aff., the self-<BR>existent; also read with a short final स्वयम्भु m. (-म्भुः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयोनि
स्वयोनि mfn. (-निः-निः-नि) Of kin, related by the mother's side.<BR>	 mf.<BR>(-निः-निः) Own womb, one's own place of birth.<BR>	 f. (-निः) A sister or<BR>near female relative.<BR> E. स्व, योनि place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
स्वर् r. 10th cl. (स्वरयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To blame, to censure, to reprove.<BR>	 2. To sound.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">Page822-a+ 60</a>]<BR>(Ind. (Aptote noun.)<BR>	 1. Heaven, paradise, the residence of INDRA<BR>and the celestials, (considered as the temporary abode of the<BR>virtuous after death.)<BR>	 2. Sky, ether.<BR>	 3. Splendour, beauty.<BR>	 4. One<BR>of the divisions of the universe, the space between the sun and the<BR>polar star and region of the planets and constellations; in this<BR>sense, this word is one of the three mystical words, to be repeated<BR>daily at the morning ceremonies, &c., with the holy Gāyatri.<BR>E. स्वृ to sound, to be in pain, विच् aff., and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=821-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर|स्वरः
स्वर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A Vedic accent, (of which there are three, viz: --उदात,<BR>अनुदात्त and स्वरित.)<BR>	 2. A vowel.<BR>	 3. A note of the musical scale or<BR>gamut.<BR>	 4. Air breathed through the nostrils.<BR>	 5. Snoring.<BR>	 6. Voice.<BR>7. Sound in general.<BR>	 8. A symbolical expression for the number<BR>“seven.”<BR> E. स्वर् to sound, अच् aff.; or स्वृ to sound, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरग्राम|स्वरग्रामः
स्वरग्राम m. (-मः) The musical scale, gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरपत्तन|स्वरपत्तनं
स्वरपत्तन n. (-नं) The Sāma-Veda.<BR> E. स्वर an accent, पत्तन a city: this<BR>Veda is chanted according to a peculiar rhythm, and the efficacy<BR>of its prayers depends chiefly on their accurate accentuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरबद्ध
स्वरबद्ध Adj. Composed in musical measure, adapted to musical time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभक्ति|स्वरभक्तिः
स्वरभक्ति f. (-क्तिः) A vowel-sound phonetically inserted in the pronun-<BR>ciation of र् or ल् when these letters are followed by a sibilant,<BR>(as वर्ष pronounced as वरिष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभङ्ग|स्वरभंग|स्वरभङ्गः
स्वरभङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Fluttering of the voice, &c., as indicative of agitation<BR>or feeling.<BR> E. स्वर a sound or note, भङ्ग a breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभङ्गिन्
स्वरभङ्गिन् m. (-ङ्गी) A kind of bird.<BR> E. स्वर a note, भङ्गिन् who breaks or divides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरमण्डलिका|स्वरमंडलिका
स्वरमण्डलिका f. (-का) A kind of stringed musical instrument.<BR> E. स्वर a<BR>note of a gamut, मण्डल a region, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरलासिका
स्वरलासिका f. (-का) A flute, a pipe.<BR> E. स्वर a note, लस् to be skilled, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरवत्|स्वरवन्त्
स्वरवत् Adj.<BR>	 1. Sonorous.<BR>	 2. Vocal.<BR>	 3. Accentuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरशून्य
स्वरशून्य mfn. (-न्यः-न्या-न्यं) Unmelodious, unmusical.<BR> E. स्वर, शून्य devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसंयोग|स्वरसंयोगः
स्वरसंयोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. The junction of vowels.<BR>	 2. Intonation, voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरस|स्वरसः
स्वरस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Expressed or extracted juice.<BR>	 2. Sediment of oil, &c.,<BR>ground on a stone.<BR>	 3. Proper or peculiar flavour.<BR>	 4. Proper or<BR>peculiar taste or sentiment in composition.<BR> E. स्व own, रस flavour, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसङ्क्रम|स्वरसंक्रमः
स्वरसङ्क्रम m. (-मः) A transition or succession of notes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसन्धि|स्वरसंधिः
स्वरसन्धि m. (-न्धिः) The junction or coalition of vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरांश|स्वरांशः
स्वरांश m. (-शः) A half or quarter tone in music.<BR> E. स्वर a note, अंश a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वराज्
स्वराज् m. (-राट्)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ or supreme spirit.<BR>	 2. A form of metre<BR>used in the Vedas, a verse of three lines, two containing eight<BR>syllables each, and one ten.<BR>	 3. A variety of the same containing<BR>four lines.<BR> E. स्व self, राज् to shine, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरान्तर|स्वरांतर
स्वरान्तर n. (-रं) The interval between two vowels, hiatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरापगा
स्वरापगा f. (-गा) The Ganges.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, आपगा river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरारूढ
स्वरारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Ascended to heaven.<BR> E. स्वर्, and आरूढ ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वराष्ट्र
स्वराष्ट्र n. (-ष्ट्रं) Own country or principality.<BR> E. स्व, and राष्ट्र country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरित|स्वरितः
स्वरित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Accented.<BR>	 2. Articulated.<BR>	 3. Sounded as<BR>a note, pitched.<BR>	 4. Circumflexed.<BR>	 m. (-तः) The third or circumflex<BR>accent, the mixed tone between high and low.<BR> E. स्वर a note or<BR>accent, इतच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरु|स्वरुः
स्वरु m. (-रुः)<BR>	 1. INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>	 2. An arrow.<BR>	 3. A sacrifice.<BR>	 4.<BR>Shavings of the wood of which a sacrificial post is made.<BR>	 5. Sun-<BR>shine.<BR>	 6. A kind of scorpion.<BR> E. स्वृ to sound, Unādi aff. उ; also<BR>with उसि aff., स्वरुस् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरुचि|स्वरुचिः
स्वरुचि mfn. (-चिः-चिः-चि) Wilful, self-willed, uncontrolled.<BR> E. स्व own,<BR>रुचि inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरुस्
स्वरुस् m. (-रुः) INDRA'S thunderbolt, &c.: see स्वरु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूप|स्वरूपं|स्वरूपः
स्वरूप mfn. (-पः-पा or -पी-पं)<BR>	 1. Wise, learned.<BR>	 2. Pleasing, handsome.<BR>	 3.<BR>Similar, like.<BR>	 4. Of like purport or character.<BR>	 n. (-पं)<BR>	 1. Natural<BR>state or condition, nature.<BR>	 2. Natural and obvious purpose or<BR>conclusion.<BR>	 3. True constitution, natural character.<BR>	 4. One's own<BR>form or shape.<BR>	 5. Peculiar aim.<BR>	 6. Kind, sort.<BR> E. स्व own, रूप form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूपगत
स्वरूपगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Having a like object or character.<BR> E. स्वरूप<BR>and गत obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूपता
स्वरूपता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Natural state.<BR>	 2. Handsomeness.<BR>	 3. Identity.<BR> E. तल्<BR>added to the last; also with त्व, स्वरूपत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूपासिद्धि
स्वरूपासिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) A form of fallacious proof, (in Nyāya phil.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरेणु|स्वरेणुः
स्वरेणु f. (-णुः) One of the wives of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ग|स्वर्गः
स्वर्ग m. (-र्गः) Heaven, INDRA'S paradise, and the residence of deified<BR>mortals and the inferior gods.<BR> E. सु happiness, ऋज् to go, or<BR>obtain, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गगत
स्वर्गगत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Gone to heaven.<BR> E. स्वर्ग, and मत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गगमन
स्वर्गगमन n. (-नं) Going to heaven.<BR> E. स्वर्ग, गमन going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गगामिन्
स्वर्गगामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Who or what goes to heaven.<BR> E. रुवर्ग, गमिन् who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गगिरि|स्वर्गगिरिः
स्वर्गगिरि m. (-रिः) The mountain SUMERU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गङ्गा|स्वर्गंगा
स्वर्गङ्गा f. (-ङ्गा) The Ganges of heaven.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, गङ्गा the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गजित्
स्वर्गजित् mfn. (-जित्) Obtaining or ensuring paradise.<BR> E. स्वर्ग heaven, and<BR>जित् what conquers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गत
स्वर्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Gone to heaven.<BR>	 2. Dead.<BR> E. स्वर्, and गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गात
स्वर्गात f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Going to heaven, future felicity.<BR>	 2. Death.<BR> E. स्वर्<BR>and गति going; also similar compounds, as स्वर्गमन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गद्वार
स्वर्गद्वार n. (-र) Heaven's gate, entrance into heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गपति|स्वर्गपतिः
स्वर्गपति m. (-तिः) INDRA.<BR> E. स्वर्ग paradise, पति lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गपर
स्वर्गपर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Desirous of INDRA'S heaven.<BR> E. स्वर्ग, पर intent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गबधू
स्वर्गबधू f. (-धूः) An Apsaras, a nymph or courtezan of INDRA'S heaven.<BR>E. स्वर्ग paradise, and बधू woman or wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गभर्त्तृ|स्वर्गभर्तृ
स्वर्गभर्त्तृ m. (-र्त्ता) INDRA.<BR> E. स्वर्ग, and भर्त्त sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गलाक
स्वर्गलाक m. (-कः) Paradise, the celestial region.<BR> E. स्वर्ग, लोक world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गलाकेश
स्वर्गलाकेश m. (-शः) INDRA.<BR> E. स्वर्गलोक, and ईश lord; the paradise of<BR>INDRA, being appropriated to corporeal felicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गापगा
स्वर्गापगा f. (-गा) The celestial Ganges.<BR> E. स्वर्ग heaven, and आपगा a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गारोहण
स्वर्गारोहण n. (-णं) Ascending to heaven.<BR> E. स्वर्ग, and आरोहण going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गारूढ
स्वर्गारूढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Gone to heaven.<BR> E. स्वर्ग, and आरूढ ascended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिगिरि|स्वर्गिगिरिः
स्वर्गिगिरि m. (-रिः) Mount SUMERU.<BR> E. स्वर्गि a god, गिरि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिन्
स्वर्गिन् m. (-र्गा)<BR>	 1. A god, a celestial.<BR>	 2. (In law,) Dead.<BR> E. स्वर्ग, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिबधू
स्वर्गिबधू f. (-धूः) A nymph of paradise.<BR> E. स्वगि a celestial, and बधू wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिरि|स्वर्गिरिः
स्वर्गिरि m. (-रिः) Mount SUMERU.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, and गिरि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गीय
स्वर्गीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Heavenly, divine, relating to Svarga.<BR> E. स्वर्ग, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गीकस्
स्वर्गीकस् m. (-काः) A god, a deity.<BR> E. स्वर्ग paradise, and ओकस् abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ग्य|स्वर्ग्यः
स्वर्ग्य mfn. (-र्ग्यः-र्ग्या-र्ग्यं)<BR>	 1. Heavenly, paradisiacal.<BR>	 2. Procuring a place<BR>in heaven.<BR> E. स्वर्ग heaven, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ण|स्वर्णं
स्वर्ण n. (-र्णं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. A gold coin.<BR> E. सु excellent, ऋण् to go or be, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णक
स्वर्णक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Golden, of gold.<BR> E. स्वर्ण, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णकाय|स्वर्णकायः|स्वर्ण्णकाय
स्वर्णकाय m. (-यः) GARUḌA, the bird and vehicle of VIṢṆU.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold,<BR>काय body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णकार|स्वर्णकारः
स्वर्णकार m. (-रः) A goldsmith.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, and कार maker, worker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णकृत्
स्वर्णकृत् m. (-कृत्) A goldsmith.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, and कृत् who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णक्षीरी
स्वर्णक्षीरी f. (-री) A medicinal kind of moon-plant, said to be brought<BR>from the Himālaya mountains.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, (like or yellow,) क्षीर<BR>milk, or milky sap, ङीष् fem. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णगैरिक|स्वर्णगैरिकं
स्वर्णगैरिक n. (-कं) A kind of ochre, golden ochre.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold. and गैरिक chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णचूड|स्वर्णचूडः
स्वर्णचूड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. The blue jay.<BR>	 2. A cock.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, चूडा a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णज|स्वर्णजं
स्वर्णज n. (-जं) Tin.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णदी
स्वर्णदी f. (-दी) The Ganges of heaven.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, नदी a river; the<BR>न changed to ण; also स्वर्नदी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णदीधिति|स्वर्णदीधितिः
स्वर्णदीधिति m. (-तिः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, दीधिति a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णद्रु|स्वर्णद्रुः
स्वर्णद्रु m. (-द्रुः) A tree with yellow blossoms.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, and द्रु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णपक्ष|स्वर्णपक्षः
स्वर्णपक्ष m. (-क्षः) GARUḌA.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, and पक्ष a wing or feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णपद्मा
स्वर्णपद्मा f. (-द्मा) The Ganges of heaven.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, पद्म lotus; bearing<BR>golden lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णपुष्प|स्वर्णपुष्पः
स्वर्णपुष्प mf. (-ष्पः-ष्पी) The Cassia fistula.<BR>	 m. (-ष्पः) The Champaca.<BR>(Michelia champaca.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पा) The gum Arabic tree, (Mimosa<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">Page823-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Arabica.)<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी) A medicinal sort of moon-plant.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold,<BR>and पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=822-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णबणिज्
स्वर्णबणिज् m. (-णिक्) A particular fallen caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णभृङ्गार|स्वर्णभृंगार|स्वर्णभृङ्गारः
स्वर्णभृङ्गार m. (-रः) A golden vase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णमाक्षिक|स्वर्णमाक्षिकं
स्वर्णमाक्षिक n. (-कं) A particular mineral substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णयूथी
स्वर्णयूथी f. (-थी) Yellow jasmine.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, and यूथी jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णरेखा
स्वर्णरेखा f. (-खा) A streak of gold.<BR> E. स्वर्ण, रेखा a line; also स्वर्णलेखा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णवर्णा
स्वर्णवर्णा f. (-र्णा) Turmeric.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णबल्कल
स्वर्णबल्कल m. (-लः) A plant, (Bignonia Indica.)<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, वल्कल bark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णविन्दु
स्वर्णविन्दु m. (-न्दुः)<BR>	 1. A spot of yellow or gold.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold,<BR>and विन्दु a spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णशीफालिका
स्वर्णशीफालिका f. (-का) A tree, (Cassia fistula.)<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, and शेफालिका Nyctanthes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णारि|स्वर्णारिः
स्वर्णारि m. (-रिः) Sulphur.<BR> E. स्वर्ण gold, and अरि hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्त्त्|स्वर्त्
स्वर्त्त् r. 10th cl. (स्वर्त्तयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To be miserable or distressed.<BR>	 2. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्द्द्|स्वर्द्
स्वर्द्द् r. 1st cl. (स्वर्द्दते)<BR>	 1. To taste.<BR>	 2. To be pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्नदी
स्वर्नदी f. (-दी) The Ganges of heaven.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, and नदी a river,<BR>and the न unchanged; also स्वर्णदी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्बधू
स्वर्बधू f. (-धूः) An Apsaras.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, and बधू wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्भानव|स्वर्भानवः
स्वर्भानव m. (-वः) A kind of precious stone, called GOMEDHA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्भानु|स्वर्भानुः
स्वर्भानु m. (-नुः) RĀHU, the personified ascending node.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, भानु shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्भाध्य
स्वर्भाध्य n. (-ध्यं) The zenith or the central point of the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्यात|स्वर्यातः
स्वर्यात mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Dead, deceased.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, and जात gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्लोक|स्वर्लोकः
स्वर्लोक m. (-कः) Heaven.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, and लोक a world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वापी|स्वर्व्वापी
स्वर्वापी f. (-पी) The Ganges.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, वापी a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वेश्या|स्वर्व्वेश्या
स्वर्वेश्या f. (-श्या) A nymph of heaven.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, and वेश्या a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वैद्य|स्वर्वैद्यः
स्वर्वैद्य m. DU. (-द्यौ) The twin sons of the sun by the nymph Aświni,<BR>and physicians of Svarga.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, and वैद्य a physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्
स्वल् r. 1st cl. (स्वलति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्प|स्वल्पः
स्वल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पा-ल्पं)<BR>	 1. Very small.<BR>	 2. Very few.<BR> E. सु very, अल्प little or few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पक
स्वल्पक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Very little.<BR>	 2. Few.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पकङ्क|स्वल्पकंक|स्वल्पकङ्कः
स्वल्पकङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) A small kind of heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पकेशिन्
स्वल्पकेशिन् m. (-शी) Root of sweet flag.<BR> E. स्वल्प little, few, केश a filament, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पपत्रक|स्वल्पपत्रकः
स्वल्पपत्रक m. (-कः) A kind of Mahuwā tree, (Bassia,) with small leaves.<BR>E. स्वल्प small, पत्र a leaf, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पबल
स्वल्पबल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Weak, feeble.<BR> E. स्वल्प, बल strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पविषय|स्वल्पविषयः
स्वल्पविषय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A small matter or object.<BR>	 2. A small part.<BR> E. स्वल्प, विषय object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पव्यय|स्वल्पव्ययः
स्वल्पव्यय m. (-यः) Niggardliness, little expenditure.<BR> E. स्वल्प, व्यय expense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पव्रीड
स्वल्पव्रीड mfn. (-डः-डा-डं) Shameless, impudent.<BR> E. स्वल्प, and व्रीडा shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पाहार
स्वल्पाहार Adj. Most abstemious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पिष्ठ
स्वल्पिष्ठ Adj. Most insignificant or minute. E. Superlative of स्वल्प ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पीयस्
स्वल्पीयस् Adj. More insignificant. E. Comparative of स्वल्प ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वव्
स्वव् r. 1st cl. (स्ववति) To revile, to abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववश
स्ववश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं) Self-subdued, self-controlled.<BR> E. स्व, and वश<BR>subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववहित
स्ववहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Alert, active.<BR>	 2. Automatous.<BR> E. स्व, and वहित impelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववासिनी
स्ववासिनी f. (-नी) A woman, (whether married or unmarried,) who con-<BR>tinues to dwell after maturity in her father's house.<BR> E. स्व her own,<BR>(family,) वासिन् abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववीज
स्ववीज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. The soul.<BR>	 2. A son.<BR> E. स्व self, वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववृत्ति
स्ववृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Own, or peculiar duty or occupation.<BR> E. स्व, and वृत्ति profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वशरीर
स्वशरीर n. (-रं) Own body.<BR> E. स्व, and शरीर body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वशरीरवत्
स्वशरीरवत् Ind. Like or as one's self.<BR> E. स्वशरीर, वति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसंवृत
स्वसंवृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Self-defended, on one's guard.<BR> E. स्व, and संवृत covered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसंस्था
स्वसंस्था f. (-स्था) Self-possession, absorption in one's own self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसिद्धवाद
स्वसिद्धवाद m. (-दः) The doctrine that the universe was produced and<BR>is sustained by the natural and necessary action of substances<BR>according to their inherent properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसृ
स्वसृ f. (-सा) A sister.<BR> E. सु before अस् to be or live, Unādi aff. ऋन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसृत्
स्वसृत् Adj. Going or moving at one's own will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्क्
स्वस्क् r. 1st cl. (स्वस्कते) To go, to move; more generally read ष्वष्क् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तरु|स्वस्तरुः
स्वस्तरु m. (-रुः) The tree of paradise.<BR> E. स्वर्, तरु a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्ति
स्वस्ति Ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of benediction.<BR>	 2. An auspicious particle.<BR>3. A term of sanction or approbation, meaning “so be it,”<BR>“may it be well with you”, “amen,” “hail”, “adieu”, &c., (used<BR>with a dative.)<BR> E. सु well, अस्व् to be, aff. क्तिच् or ति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिक|स्वस्तिकः
स्वस्तिक mn. (-कः-कं)<BR>	 1. A temple or mansion of a particular form with<BR>a portico in front.<BR>	 2. A particular mode of sitting practised by<BR>Yogins.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. Any lucky or auspicious object.<BR>	 2. The meeting<BR>of four roads.<BR>	 3. A building or place of a peculiar shape, described<BR>as surrounded by a terrace, or portico, on the north, west, and<BR>south sides, and having the door or entrance on the east.<BR>	 4. A<BR>kind of mystical figure, the inscription of which on any person or<BR>thing is generally considered to be lucky; and amongst the<BR>Jainas is the emblem of the seventh deified teacher of the present<BR>era.<BR>	 5. The crossing of the arms, as resembling the preceding.<BR>	 6.<BR>A kind of cake.<BR>	 7. A particular symbol made with ground-rice<BR>and shaped like a triangle.<BR>	 8. A libertine.<BR>	 9. Garlic.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिभाव|स्वस्तिभावः
स्वस्तिभाव m. (-वः) An epithet of ŚIVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिमत्|स्वस्तिमन्त्
स्वस्तिमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Happy, auspicious.<BR> E. स्वस्ति, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिमुख|स्वस्तिमुखः
स्वस्तिमुख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. A letter, a note.<BR>	 2. A Brāhman.<BR>	 3. A panegyrist.<BR>E. स्वस्ति, and मुख beginning or the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिवाचन|स्वस्तिवाचनं
स्वस्तिवाचन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. A religious rite, preparatory to a sacrifice or any<BR>important observance, in which the Brāhmans strew boiled rice<BR>on the ground, and invoke the blessings of the gods on the<BR>ceremony about to commence.<BR>	 2. An offering of flowers, sweet-<BR>meat, &c., to any one intended to secure good wishes and blessings.<BR>E. स्वस्ति inceptive and benedictory particle, वाचन uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिवाच्य
स्वस्तिवाच्य n. (-च्यं) Congratulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्त्ययन
स्वस्त्ययन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Auspicious, propitious.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The aversion<BR>of evil by the recitation of Mantras.<BR>	 2. The benediction of a<BR>Brāhmana after presentation of offerings.<BR>	 3. A means of attaining<BR>prosperity.<BR> E. स्वस्ति good, and अयन coming or bringing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थ|स्वस्थः
स्वस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं)<BR>	 1. Confident, resolute, firm, relying upon one's<BR>self.<BR>	 2. Well, at ease, in health.<BR>	 3. Self-sufficient.<BR>	 4. Contented. E.<BR>स्व self, and स्थ staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थम्
स्वस्थम् Ind. Composedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थान
स्वस्थान n. (-नं) One's own place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्रीय|स्वस्रीयः
स्वस्रीय m. (-यः) A sister's son.<BR>	 f. (-या) A sister's daughter.<BR> E. स्वसृ a<BR>sister, and छ aff.; also with घ aff. स्वस्रिय mf. (-यः-या) or with ढक्<BR>aff. स्वस्रेय mf. (-यः-यी ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहस्तिका
स्वहस्तिका f. (-का) An axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहित
स्वहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Good for one's self.<BR> E. स्व, and हित good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहितैषिन्
स्वहितैषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Seeking one's own welfare.<BR> E. स्वहित, and<BR>एषिन् seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाकार
स्वाकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Having one's own form.<BR> E. स्व, and आकार form;<BR>also स्वाकृति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाक्षपाद|स्वाक्षपादः
स्वाक्षपाद m. (-दः) A follower of the Nyāya system of philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वागत|स्वागतं
स्वागत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Welcome, salutation.<BR>	 2. Happy arrival; (in greeting<BR>this word is generally used with the dative of the person greeted.)<BR>f. (-ता) A species of the Trishtubh metre.<BR> E. सु well, and आगत come.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाङ्किक|स्वांकिक|स्वांकिकः|स्वाङ्किकः
स्वाङ्किक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A drummer.<BR>	 2. A kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाच्छन्द्य|स्वाच्छंद्य|स्वाच्छंद्यं|स्वाच्छन्द्यं|स्वाछन्द्य
स्वाच्छन्द्य n. (-न्द्य) Wilfulness, independence.<BR> E. स्वच्छन्द self-willed, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाच्छन्द्यतस्|स्वाच्छंद्यतस्
स्वाच्छन्द्यतस् Ind. Voluntarily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वातन्त्र्य|स्वातंत्र्य|स्वातंत्र्यं|स्वातन्त्र्यं
स्वातन्त्र्य n. (-न्त्र्यं) Wilfulness, independence.<BR> E. स्वतन्त्र self-willed, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाति|स्वातिः
स्वाति f. (-तिः-ती)<BR>	 1. One of the wives of the sun.<BR>	 2. The star Arcturus,<BR>or fifteenth lunar asterism, consisting of but one star.<BR>	 3. An<BR>auspicious constellation.<BR>	 4. A sword.<BR>	 5. A bird.<BR> E. सु well,<BR>auspiciously, अत् to go or be, aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्
स्वाद् r. 1st cl. (स्वादते)<BR>	 1. To taste, to relish.<BR>	 2. To please.<BR>	 3. To be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">Page824-a+ 60</a>]<BR>liked, (with a dative.) r. 10th cl. (स्वादयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sweeten.<BR>	 2. To<BR>cover; also स्वद् and ष्वद् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=823-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद|स्वादः
स्वाद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Taste, flavour.<BR>	 2. Tasting, either food or drink, eating,<BR>drinking.<BR>	 3. Liking, relishing, enjoyment.<BR> E. स्वाद् to taste, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादन|स्वादनं
स्वादन n. (-नं) Tasting, either as food or drink, eating, drinking.<BR> E. स्वाद्<BR>to taste, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादित|स्वादितः
स्वादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Tasted, touched with the lips.<BR> E. स्वाद् to taste, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादिमन्
स्वादिमन् m. (-मा) Savouriness, sweetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादिष्ठ
स्वादिष्ठ f. (-ष्ठा) Adj. Very sweet. E. Superlative of स्वादु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादीयस्
स्वादीयस् f. (-सौ) Adj. More sweet. E. Comparative of स्वादु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादु|स्वादुः
स्वादु mfn. (-दुः-दुः or -द्वी-दु)<BR>	 1. Sweet.<BR>	 2. Agreeable, desired.<BR>	 3. Hand-<BR>some.<BR>	 4. Grateful to the palate, dainty, delicate.<BR>	 m. (-दुः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>sweet taste or flavour, sweetness.<BR>	 2. Treacle, molasses.<BR>	 3. A<BR>medicinal root and perfume commonly Jivaka.<BR>	 f. (-द्वी or -दुः) A<BR>grape.<BR> E. ष्वद् to taste or to be pleasing, उण् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुकण्टक|स्वादुकण्टकः
स्वादुकण्टक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A plant, (Flacourtia sapida.)<BR>	 2. A sort of creeper,<BR>(Tribulus lanuginosus.)<BR> E. स्वादु sweet, and कण्टक a thron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुकार
स्वादुकार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Delicate in taste, dainty.<BR> E. स्वादु, कार who acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुखण्ड|स्वादुखंड|स्वादुखण्डः
स्वादुखण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. Molasses, raw sugar.<BR>	 2. A piece of any sweet<BR>substance.<BR> E. स्वादु sweet, खण्ड a fragment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुगन्धा
स्वादुगन्धा f. (-न्धा) A creeper, (Convolvulus paniculatus,) the dark sort.<BR>E. स्वादु sweet, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुधन्वन्
स्वादुधन्वन् m. (-न्वा) KĀMA.<BR> E. स्वादु sweet, (flowers,) धन्वन् a bowyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुफल|स्वादुफलं
स्वादुफल n. (-लं) The fruit of the jujube.<BR>	 f. (-ला) The jujube tree.<BR> E. स्वादु<BR>sweet, फल fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुमज्जन्
स्वादुमज्जन् m. (-ज्जा) A sort of tree, a Pilu growing in the hills.<BR> E. स्वादु sweet, मज्जन् sap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुमूल|स्वादुमूलं
स्वादुमूल n. (-लं) A carrot. “गाजर” इति भाषा.<BR> E. स्वादु sweet, मूल a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुरसा
स्वादुरसा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. A medicinal root, commonly, Kākoli.<BR>	 2. The fruit<BR>of the hog-plum.<BR>	 3. Vinous liquor.<BR>	 4. A grape.<BR>	 5. The Śatāvari<BR>plant.<BR> E. स्वादु sweet, &c., and रस juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुशीत
स्वादुशीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sweet and cool.<BR> E. स्वादु, and शीत cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुशुद्ध|स्वादुशुद्धं
स्वादुशुद्ध n. (-द्धं) Rock or river salt.<BR> E. स्वादु sweet, and शुद्ध pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्वन्न
स्वाद्वन्न n. (-न्नं) Dainties, delicacies, choice food.<BR> E. स्वादु, and अन्न food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्वम्ल|स्वाद्वम्लः
स्वाद्वम्ल m. (-म्लः) The pomegranate tree.<BR> E. स्वादु sweet, and अम्ल sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधिकार|स्वाधिकारः
स्वाधिकार m. (-रः) Own or peculiar office or station.<BR> E. स्व, अधिकार duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधिपत्य
स्वाधिपत्य n. (-त्यं) Supreme sway, royalty, sovereignty.<BR> E. स्व, and<BR>आधिपत्य supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधिष्ठान|स्वाधिष्ठानं
स्वाधिष्ठान n. (-नं) One of the six CHAKRAS or mystical circles of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीन|स्वाधीनः
स्वाधीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Independent, uncontrolled.<BR>	 2. One's own<BR>dependent.<BR> E. स्व self, अधीन dependent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीनकुशल
स्वाधीनकुशल Adj. Having prosperity in one's own power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीनता
स्वाधीनता f. (-ता) Independence.<BR> E. तल् added to the last; also with त्व,<BR>स्वाधीनत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीनपतिका
स्वाधीनपतिका f. (-का) A woman independent of her husband or lover.<BR>E. स्वाधीन independent, पति husband, कन् fem. form added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीनभर्त्तृका|स्वाधीनभर्तृका
स्वाधीनभर्त्तृका f. (-का) A woman who is independent of her lover or<BR>husband.<BR> E. स्व self, अधीन subservient, and भर्त्तृ a husband, कन्<BR>added; keeping her husband in subjection or dependence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्याय|स्वाध्यायः
स्वाध्याय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. Inaudible reading or muttering of prayers.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Vedas or scripture.<BR>	 3. Perusal or study of the Vedas.<BR> E. स्व one's<BR>self, अध्याय reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्यायवत्|स्वाध्यायवन्त्
स्वाध्यायवत् m. (-वान्) A student of the Vedas.<BR> E. स्वाध्याय perusing the Vedas, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्यायिन्
स्वाध्यायिन् m. (-यी)<BR>	 1. A tradesman, a citizen and dealer.<BR>	 2. A student<BR>of the Vedas.<BR> E. स्वाध्याय muttering, &c., इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वान|स्वानः
स्वान m. (-नः) Sound, noise.<BR> E. स्वन् to sound, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानुभूति|स्वानुभूतिः
स्वानुभूति f. (-तिः) One's own experience, self-enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानुरूप
स्वानुरूप mfn. (-पः-पी-पं) Natural, inherent, innate.<BR> E. स्व, अनुरूप conformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वान्त|स्वांत|स्वान्तं
स्वान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Sounded, making a noise.<BR>	 n. (-न्तं)<BR>	 1. The mind,<BR>the faculty of thought and feeling.<BR>	 2. A cave, a cavern.<BR> E. स्वन्<BR>to sound, क्त aff., deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाप|स्वापः
स्वाप m. (-पः)<BR>	 1. Sleep, sleeping.<BR>	 2. Sleepiness, sloth.<BR>	 3. Paralysis, palsy,<BR>loss of sensation.<BR>	 4. Ignorance.<BR>	 5. Dreaming, a dream.<BR>	 6. Tem-<BR>porary and partial palsy from pressure on a nerve, numbness, the<BR>sleep of a limb, &c.<BR> E. ष्वप् to sleep, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापतेय|स्वापतेयं
स्वापतेय n. (-यं) Wealth, property.<BR> E. स्व own, पति master, ढञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापद|स्वापदः
स्वापद m. (-दः) A wild beast.<BR> E. स substituted for श: see श्वापद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभाविक|स्वाभाविकः
स्वाभाविक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Natural, peculiar, inherent.<BR>	 m. Plu. (-काः)<BR>A sect of Buddhists who accounted for all things by the law of<BR>nature.<BR> E. स्वभाव natural property or nature, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिकार्य्य|स्वामिकार्य
स्वामिकार्य्य n. (-र्य्यं) The business of a prince or master.<BR> E. स्वामिन्, कार्य्य affair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिजङ्घिन्
स्वामिजङ्घिन् m. (-ङ्घी) PARAŚURĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिता
स्वामिता f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Ownership.<BR>	 2. Sovereignty.<BR> E. स्वामिन्, तल् aff.; also<BR>with त्व, स्वामित्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामित्व|स्वामित्वं
स्वामित्व n. (-त्वं)<BR>	 1. Ownership, mastership.<BR>	 2. Sovereignty, &c.<BR> E. त्व<BR>added to स्वामिन्; also with तल्, स्वामिता ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिन्
स्वामिन् mfn. (-मी-मिनी-मि) Owner, proprietor, master or mistress, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-मी)<BR>	 1. A master, a lord.<BR>	 2. A sovereign, a prince, a monarch.<BR>	 3.<BR>A husband, a lover.<BR>	 4. A spiritual preceptor.<BR>	 5. A learned Brāh-<BR>man or Paṇḍiṭ.<BR>	 6. An ascetic or religious man of the highest order,<BR>(in this sense generally an addition to proper names.)<BR>	 7.<BR>KĀRTIKEYA.<BR>	 8. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 9. ŚIVA.<BR>	 10. The Muni VĀTSYĀYANA.<BR>11. A name of GARUḌA.<BR> E. स्व own, आमिनच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिपाल|स्वामिपालः
स्वामिपाल m. DU. (-लौ) The owner and the tender, (of cattle.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिमूल
स्वामिमूल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Depending upon, or originating from the<BR>master, husband, or lord.<BR> E. स्वामिन्, and मूल root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिसद्भाव|स्वामिसद्भावः
स्वामिसद्भाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Existence of a master or owner.<BR>	 2. Amiability of<BR>a master or lord.<BR> E. स्वामि, and सत् being, or good, भाव existence<BR>or property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिसेवा
स्वामिसेवा f. (-वा) Attention to a master, husband, &c.<BR> E. स्वामिन्, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाम्य|स्वाम्यं
स्वाम्य n. (-म्यं)<BR>	 1. Mastership, ownership.<BR>	 2. Right or title to property.<BR>3. Rule, supremacy.<BR> E. स्वामिन्, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वावाम्युपकारक
स्वावाम्युपकारक m. (-कः) A horse.<BR> E. स्वामिन् a master, उपकार assistance, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायत्त
स्वायत्त Adj. Depending upon oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायम्भुव|स्वायंभुव|स्वायंभुवः|स्वायम्भुवः
स्वायम्भुव mfn. (-वः-वी-वं)<BR>	 1. Relating to SWAYAMBHŪ.<BR>	 2. Derived from<BR>the self-born.<BR>	 m. (-वः) An epithet of the first MANU, the son of<BR>SWAYAMBHŪ.<BR> E. स्वयम्भू, and अण् aff.; also स्वायम्भू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारसिक
स्वारसिक f. (-का) Possessing inherent flavour or sweetness, (said of a poem.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारस्य|स्वारस्यं
स्वारस्य n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. The possessing natural savouriness or excellence.<BR>	 2.<BR>Propriety, (of a word.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्
स्वाराज् m. (-राट्) INDRA.<BR> E. स्वर् heaven, राज ruler; the first र rejected,<BR>and the vowel made long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्य|स्वाराज्यं|स्वाराज्यः
स्वाराज्य n. (-ज्यं)<BR>	 1. Final felicity, union with BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. INDRA'S<BR>heaven.<BR> E. स्वराज्, and ष्यञ् aff.; or स्वाराज् and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारोचिष|स्वारोचिषः
स्वारोचिष m. (-षः) The second MANU.<BR> E. स्वरोचिस्, and अञ् affix of descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थ|स्वार्थः
स्वार्थ mfn. (-र्थः-र्था-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Pleonastic.<BR>	 2. Having a plain or literal<BR>meaning, or similar force or sense.<BR>	 3. Having one's own object.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-र्थं)<BR>	 1. Property, substance.<BR>	 2. Same effect or meaning, a<BR>pleonasm.<BR>	 3. Own object or desire.<BR>	 m. (-र्थः)<BR>	 1. Self-interest.<BR>	 2. Own<BR>meaning.<BR> E. स्व own, and अर्थ wealth or sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थपरायण
स्वार्थपरायण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Selfish.<BR> E. स्वार्थ, and परायण diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थलिप्सु
स्वार्थलिप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Desirous of having one's own way, self-<BR>seeking.<BR> E. स्वार्थ, and लिप्सु desirous of getting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थविघात
स्वार्थविघात m. (-तः) The frustration of one's own object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थसिद्धि
स्वार्थसिद्धि f. (-द्धिः) Accomplishment of one's object, attainment of the<BR>thing desired.<BR> E. स्वार्थ, and सिद्धि completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थानुमान
स्वार्थानुमान n. (-नं) (In logic,) A particular process of induction, (as<BR>opposed to परार्थानुमान.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थिक
स्वार्थिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Expressing its own or literal meaning.<BR>	 2.<BR>Having one's own object.<BR>	 3. Done with one's own wealth, &c. E.<BR>स्वार्थ, and ठण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=824-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वालक्षण्य|स्वालक्षण्यं
स्वालक्षण्य n. (-ण्यं) Peculiar characteristic, natural disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाल्प
स्वाल्प mfn. (-ल्पः-ल्पी-ल्पं)<BR>	 1. Small.<BR>	 2. Few.<BR>	 n. (-ल्पं)<BR>	 1. Littleness.<BR>	 2.<BR>Paucity.<BR> E. स्वल्प, and अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाशित
स्वाशित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Well-fed.<BR> E. सु, and आशित eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वास्तीर्ण
स्वास्तीर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Well-spread.<BR> E. सु, and आस्तीर्ण spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वास्थ्य|स्वास्थ्यं
स्वास्थ्य n. (-स्थ्यं)<BR>	 1. Health.<BR>	 2. Content, happiness, complacency. satisfac-<BR>tion.<BR>	 3. Fortitude, firmness, self-dependence.<BR>	 4. Prosperity, com-<BR>fortableness, competence.<BR> E. स्व self, स्थ who is or stays, ष्यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहा
स्वाहा Ind. An exclamation uttered at the time of making an offering<BR>to the gods, (used with a noun in the dative.)<BR>	 f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. A personi-<BR>fication of the preceding, as the wife of fire, and goddess presiding<BR>over burnt offerings.<BR>	 2. An oblation made to Gods indiscrimi-<BR>nately.<BR>	 3. A female divinity, peculiar to the Bauddhas. E.<BR>सु well, auspiciously, आङ् before ह्वेञ् to call, to invoke, (the<BR>gods,) and डा aff.; or स्वाद् to taste, aff. आ, and द changed to ह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाकार|स्वाहाकारः
स्वाहाकार m. (-रः) Utterance of the term Swāhā.<BR> E. स्वाहा, कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहापति|स्वाहापतिः
स्वाहापति m. (-तिः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. स्वाहा the goddess, and पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाप्रिय|स्वाहाप्रियः
स्वाहाप्रिय m. (-यः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. स्वाहा the goddess, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाभुज्
स्वाहाभुज् m. (-भुक्) A deity.<BR> E. स्वाहा the oblation, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वित्
स्वित् Ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of questioning, (hey, what ?)<BR>	 2. An exclama-<BR>tion of doubt or surprise.<BR>	 3. An expletive. It is added to interro-<BR>gative pronouns and adverbs to impart to them the sense of<BR>indefiniteness; (used generally after आहो or किम्, &c., and is trans-<BR>latable by “whether.”)<BR> E. सु well, इण् to go, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विदित|स्विदितः
स्विदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Sweated, melted.<BR>	 2. Sweating, perspiring. E.<BR>ष्विद् to be unctuous, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विन्न|स्विन्नः
स्विन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Sweating, perspiring.<BR> E. ष्विद् to perspire, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकरण|स्वीकरणं
स्वीकरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Assenting, agreeing.<BR>	 2. Promising.<BR>	 3. Marriage,<BR>wedding.<BR> E. स्व own, करण making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकरणीय
स्वीकरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं)<BR>	 1. To be promised.<BR>	 2. To be admitted, con-<BR>sented, or agreed to.<BR> E. स्व before कृ to make, अनीयर् aff., च्वि aug-<BR>ment; also स्वीकर्त्तव्य and स्वीकृत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकार|स्वीकारः
स्वीकार n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. Promise.<BR>	 2. Assent, agreement.<BR> E. स्व own, कार making, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकाररहित
स्वीकाररहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Not agreed or assented to.<BR> E. स्वीकार, and<BR>रहित void. of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकारान्त
स्वीकारान्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ता-न्तं) Agreed to, (consequent upon a promise or assent.)<BR> E. स्वीकार, अन्त end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृत
स्वीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Agreed, assented to.<BR>	 2. Promised.<BR> E. स्व, कृत<BR>made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृत्य
स्वीकृत्य Ind. Having agreed or promised.<BR> E. स्व, and कृत्य having made, च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीय|स्वीयः
स्वीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Own, relating or belonging to one.<BR>	 f. (-या) A virtu-<BR>ous woman, one attached solely to her husband.<BR> E. स्व own, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वुर्च्छ्
स्वुर्च्छ् r. 1st cl. (स्वुर्च्छति)<BR>	 1. To spread, to extend.<BR>	 2. To forget; also स्फुर्च्छ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वृ
स्वृ r. 1st cl. (-स्वरति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To be diseased.<BR>	 3. To pain or<BR>torture.<BR>	 4. To praise. With सम् prefixed, in an intransitive sense,<BR>the verb becomes deponent, (संस्वरते) It sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वृ
स्वृ r. 9th cl. (स्वृणाति) To hurt, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेक्
स्वेक् (ऋ,) स्वेकृ r. 1st cl. (स्वेकते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेच्छा
स्वेच्छा f. (-च्छा) Wilfulness, following one's own, purpose or inclina-<BR>tion, self-will.<BR> E. स्व own, इच्छा wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेच्छामृत्यु|स्वेच्छामृत्युः
स्वेच्छामृत्यु m. (-त्युः) BHĪṢMA.<BR> E. स्वेच्छा self-will, मृत्यु death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेच्छाहार
स्वेच्छाहार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Omnivorous, eating anything at pleasure. E.<BR>स्वेच्छा and आहार food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेद|स्वेदः
स्वेद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Warm, perspiring.<BR>	 m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. Warmth, heat.<BR>	 2.<BR>Perspiration, sweat.<BR>	 3. Vapour, steam.<BR> E. ष्विद् to perspire, &c.,<BR>aff. घञ्, or causal verb, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदचूषक|स्वेदचूषकः
स्वेदचूषक m. (-कः) A pleasant and cooling breeze.<BR> E. स्वेद perspiration,<BR>चूष् to suck or imbibe, aff. वुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदच्छिद्|स्वेदछिद्
स्वेदच्छिद् mfn. (-च्छित्) Cooling, allaying perspiration.<BR> E. स्वेद, and छिद् what cuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदज|स्वेदजः
स्वेदज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Engendered by heat and damp, as insects and<BR>worms.<BR> E. स्वेद sweat or vapour, and ज produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदजल
स्वेदजल n. (-लं) Perspiration.<BR> E. स्वेद and जल water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदन|स्वेदनं
स्वेदन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Perspiration, sweat.<BR>	 2. Sweating, causing to perspire.<BR>3. A diaphoretic, a sudorific.<BR> E. ष्विद् to be unctuous or sweaty<BR>ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनिका
स्वेदनिका f. (-का) An iron plate or pan used as a cooking utensil. E.<BR>स्वेदन sweat, ङीष् aff., and कन् fem. form added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनी
स्वेदनी f. (-नी) An iron plate or pan used as a frying pan, &c.<BR> E. ष्विद्<BR>to perspire, ल्युट् and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदमलोञ्झितदेह
स्वेदमलोञ्झितदेह m. (-हः) A holy or sainted teacher of the Jainas. E.<BR>स्वेद perspiration, मल excrement, उञ्झित abandoned, and देह body<BR>whose body is no longer subject to its original impurities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदविन्दु
स्वेदविन्दु f. (-न्दुः) A drop of perspiration.<BR> E. स्वेद, विन्दु a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदविप्रुष्
स्वेदविप्रुष् f. (-प्रट्) A drop of perspiration.<BR> E. स्वेद sweat, विप्रुष् a drop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदित
स्वदित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Sweated, heated.<BR> E. ष्विद् to sweat, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदोदक
स्वेदोदक n. (-कं) Perspiration.<BR> E. स्वेद and उदक water; also स्वेदोद ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैर|स्वैरः
स्वैर mfn. (-रः-री-रं)<BR>	 1. Self-willed, unrestrained.<BR>	 2. Slow, lazy.<BR>	 3.<BR>Voluntary, optional.<BR>	 4. Going.<BR>	 n. (-रं) Following one's own<BR>inclination.<BR> E. स्व self, ईर् to go or be, aff. अण् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरता
स्वैरता f. (-ता) Wilfulness, independence.<BR> E. स्वैर self-willed, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरम्
स्वैरम् Ind.<BR>	 1. Of one's own accord.<BR>	 2. Lowly, indistinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरवृत्त
स्वैरवृत्त mfn. (-त्तः-त्ता-त्तं) Acting or living as one likes.<BR> E. स्वैर, वृत्त practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिता
स्वैरिता f. (-ता) Wilfulness.<BR> E. स्वैरिन् self-willed, तल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवैरिन्
सवैरिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-प्रि) Uncontrolled, self-willed.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. An<BR>unchaste wife, an adulteress.<BR>	 2. A wanton woman.<BR> E. स्व self, ईर् to<BR>go, णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोदय|स्वोदयः
स्वोदय m. (-यः) The rising of a sign or heavenly body at any particular place<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोपधि|स्वोपधिः
स्वोपधि m. (-धिः) A fixed star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोपार्जित|स्वोपार्ज्जितः
स्वोपार्जित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Self-got, self-acquired, (as wealth, &c.)<BR> E. स्व self, उपार्जित obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोरस|स्वोरसः
स्वोरस m. (-सः) Sediment of oil, &c., ground with a stone and muller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोवश्वीय
स्वोवश्वीय n. (-यं) Happiness, prosperity; more preferably श्वोवसीयस ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
ह The thirty-third and last consonant of the Deva-Nāgari alphabet<BR>the letter “H.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
ह Subst.<BR>	 mfn. (-हः-हा-हं) Laughter. Adj. Mad, drunk.<BR>	 m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>2. Water.<BR>	 3. A cypher.<BR>	 4. Meditation.<BR>	 5. Auspiciousness.<BR>	 6. Sky<BR>heaven.<BR>	 7. Paradise.<BR>	 8. Blood.<BR>	 9. Dying.<BR>	 10. Fear.<BR>	 11. Know-<BR>ledge.<BR>	 12. The moon.<BR>	 13. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 14. War, battle.<BR>	 15. Horripila<BR>tion.<BR>	 16. A horse.<BR>	 17. Pride.<BR>	 18. A physician.<BR>	 19. Cause, motive<BR>f. (-हा)<BR>	 1. A bandoning, leaving.<BR>	 2. Coition.<BR>	 3. A lute.<BR>	 n. (-हं)<BR>	 1.<BR>GOD, the supreme soul.<BR>	 2. Pleasure, delight.<BR>	 3. Calling, calling<BR>to 4. A weapon.<BR>	 5. The sparkling of a gem.<BR>	 6. The sound of a lute.<BR>Ind.<BR>	 1. An expletive.<BR>	 2. A vocative particle, (ho ! holla !)<BR>	 3. A<BR>term or rejection or disdain.<BR>	 4. A particle of abuse or reproach<BR>see हा, ही &c.<BR>	 5. An emphatic particle laying stress on the prece-<BR>ding word and equivalent to “varily,” “indeed,” “evidently.” E.<BR>हा to abandon, or हन् to strike, &c., aff. क or ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंस|हंसः
हंस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. A goose, a gander, a flamingo, a swan. The descrip<BR>tion of this bird as found in sanskrit poetry is rather poetical<BR>than real; swans are considered to fly to the MĀNASA-LAKE when<BR>monsoon sets in; they are also represented as being the vehicle<BR>of BRAHMĀ; there is a convention among poets that this bird is<BR>gifted with the power of separating milk from water.<BR>	 2. BRAHMĀ<BR>the supreme soul.<BR>	 3. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 4. The sun.<BR>	 5. A liberal or moderate<BR>prince, one not covetous nor ambitious.<BR>	 6. A sort of ascetic<BR>or devotee.<BR>	 7. A particular Mantra, or mystical or magical pray-<BR>er.<BR>	 8. A horse.<BR>	 9. One of the vital airs.<BR>	 10. Envy, malice.<BR>	 11.<BR>ŚIVA.<BR>	 12. (In composition,) Best excellent.<BR>	 13. Preceding, before,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">Page826-a+ 60</a>]<BR>in front.<BR>	 14. A spiritual preceptor.<BR>	 15. A mountain.<BR>	 16. A<BR>buffalo.<BR>	 17. KĀMA.<BR>	 18. The individual soul.<BR>	 f. (-सी) A goose.<BR> E. हन्<BR>to hurt or kill, Unādi aff. स; also this word is curiously derived<BR>by native philologists, viz:--भवेद् वर्णागमाद् हंसः i. e. it is derived<BR>from हस् by the insertion of a nasal; also with कन् added, हंसक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=825-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसक|हंसकः
हंसक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An ornament for the feet, described as being made<BR>like a goose's foot.<BR>	 2. The flamingo.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकान्ता|हंसकांता
हंसकान्ता f. (-न्ता) A female goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकीलक|हंसकीलकः
हंसकीलक m. (-कः) A particular form of sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकूट|हंसकूटः
हंसकूट m. (-टः) The hump on the shoulder of the Indian ox.<BR> E. हंस a<BR>goose, कूट a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगति
हंसगति Adj. Having a swan's gait.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगद्गदा
हंसगद्गदा f. (-दा) A woman speaking sweetly or pleasantly.<BR> E. हंस a<BR>goose, गद् to sound, reiterated, affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगामिनी
हंसगामिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A woman having a graceful gait.<BR>	 2. An epithet<BR>of Brahmāni.<BR> E. हंस a goose, (or swan,) गामिनी who goes, (like.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसतूल|हंसतूलः
हंसतूल mn. (-लः-लं) The soft feathers of a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसदाहन|हंसदाहनं
हंसदाहन n. (-नं) Agallochum.<BR> E. हंस a goose, दाहन burning, exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसनाद|हंसनादः
हंसनाद m. (-दः) Cackling, the cry or noise of a goose.<BR> E. हंस, नाद sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसनादिन्
हंसनादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Cackling, making a noise like a goose.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-दिनी) An elegant woman, one of slender waist and large<BR>posteriors, with the gait of an elephant and voice of a Kokila. E.<BR>हंस a goose, नाद cry, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हपदी
हपदी f. (-दी)<BR>	 1. A scandent shrub, (Cissus pedata.)<BR>	 2. Another<BR>plant, perhaps Clitoria ternata.<BR> E. हंस a goose, and पद foot; from<BR>a fancied resemblance between it and the flower; also हंसपादी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसपाद|हंसपादं
हंसपाद n. (-दं) Vermilion.<BR>	 f. (-दी) A shrub, (Clitoria ternata.)<BR> E. हंस a<BR>goose, पाद a foot, (to which they are compared in colour, form,<BR>&c.:) see the last; also in the fem. form, कन् added, हंसपादिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसमाला
हंसमाला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. A duck.<BR>	 2. A flight or flock or wild geese.<BR>	 3. A<BR>kind of metre.<BR> E. हंत a goose, माला a garland or wreath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसरथ|हंसरथः
हंसरथ m. (-थः) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. हंस a goose, and रय vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसलोमश|हंसलोमशं
हंसलोमश n. (-शं) Sulphate of iron. “कासीसे”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसलोहक|हंसलोहकं
हंसलोहक n. (-कं) Brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसवती
हंसवती f. (-ती) A creeper, (Cissus pedata.)<BR> E. हंस a goose, (its foot,) and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसवाहन|हंसवाहनः
हंसवाहन m. (-नं) BRAHMĀ.<BR> E. हंस a goose, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसवीज
हंसवीज n. (-जं) The egg of a goose.<BR> E. हंस, वीज seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाङ्घ्रि|हंसाङ्घ्रिः
हंसाङ्घ्रि m. (-ङ्घ्रिः) Vermilion.<BR> E. हंस a goose, and अङ्घ्रि the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसाधिरूढा
हसाधिरूढा f. (-ढा) An epithet of SARASWATĪ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाभिख्य|हंसाभिख्यं
हंसाभिख्य n. (-ख्यं) Silver.<BR> E. हंस a goose, अभिख्या beauty; being of similar colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसिका
हंसिका f. (-का) A female goose.<BR> E. हंसो the female goose, and कन् added;<BR>or हन् to kill, सिकन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंहो
हंहो Ind.<BR>	 1. An interjection of calling, (ho, hollo!)<BR>	 2. A particle of<BR>haughtiness or arrogance.<BR>	 3. An arrogantly interrogative particle.<BR>In drama it is found used as a form of address in speeches<BR>assigned to characters of the middling class.<BR> E. हं and हो both<BR>vocative particles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हक्क|हक्कः
हक्क m. (-क्कः) The calling of elephants.<BR> E. हक् imitative sound, कै to utter, ड aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हक्कार|हक्कारः
हक्कार m. (-रः) Calling, calling to.<BR> E. हक् sound of calling, कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जा|हंजा
हञ्जा Ind. (In theatrical language,) A vocative particle used in calling<BR>to a female attendant.<BR> E. हिडि to treat with disrespect or<BR>contempt, aff. आ, and the deriv. irr.; also with ए aff. हञ्जे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जि|हञ्जिः
हञ्जि m. (-ञ्जिः)<BR>	 1. Hunger.<BR>	 2. Sneezing.<BR> E. हमित्यव्यक्तं जयति जि-डि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हञ्जे|हंजे
हञ्जे Ind. (In theatrical language,) A vocative particle to be used in<BR>addressing a female attendant. E. See हञ्जा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्
हट् r. 1st cl. (हटति) To shine, to be bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्ट|हट्टः
हट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A market, a movable market, a fair.<BR>	 f. (-ट्टी) A petty<BR>market or fair.<BR> E. हट् to shine, ट aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्टचौरक|हट्टचौरकः
हट्टचौरक m. (-कः) A thief, one stealing at fairs and markets.<BR> E. हट्ट a<BR>market, and चौर a theif, कन् pleonasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्टविलासिनी
हट्टविलासिनी f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A sort of perfume.<BR>	 2. A whore.<BR>	 3. Turmeric.<BR> E. हट्ट<BR>a market, विलस् to wanton or delight, णिनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ्
हठ् r. 1st cl. (हठति)<BR>	 1. To leap or jump.<BR>	 2. To be wicked.<BR>	 3. To treat<BR>with violence, to oppress.<BR>	 4. To bind to a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ|हठः
हठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. Violence.<BR>	 2. Oppression.<BR>	 3. Rapine.<BR>	 mf. (-ठः-ठी) An<BR>aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. हठ् to treat with violence,<BR>aff. अच् । The instrumental and ablative singulars, “हठेन” and<BR>“हठात्” are used as indeclinables in the sense of “forcibly,”<BR>“violently,” “suddenly.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ|हठः
हठ (ट) पर्णी f. (-र्णी) An aquatic plant, (Vallisneria ocatandra.)<BR> E. हठ Pistia, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठयोग|हठयोगः
हठयोग m. (-गः) A particular mode of YOGA, or abstract contemplation<BR>difficult to practise, and as such distinguished from RĀJA-YOGA,<BR>which is an easy mode of abstraction. It is performed in various<BR>ways, such as standing on one leg, holding up the arms, inhaling<BR>smoke with the head inverted, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठविद्या
हठविद्या f. (-द्या) The science of forced meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठालु|हठालुः
हठालु m. (-लुः) An aquatic plant, (Pistia stratiotes.)<BR> E. हठ Pistia, आलु<BR>a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हडि|हडिः
हडि m. (-डिः) A sort of stocks or wooden fetters. “हाडिकाठ” इति भाषा ।<BR> E. हठ्-इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हडिक|हडिकः
हडिक m. (-कः) A sweeper, a servant of the lowest caste and meanest<BR>function.<BR> E. हठ् to be wicked, इकक् aff.; also हड्डिक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्ड|हड्डं
हड्ड n. (-ड्डं)<BR>	 1. A bone.<BR>	 2. A sweeper: see the last.<BR> E. हठ्-ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डक|हड्डकः
हड्डक m. (-कः) A sweeper, a Mehter.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डज|हड्डजं
हड्डज n. (-जं) The marrow of the bones.<BR> E. हड्ड a bone, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डा|हंडा
हण्डा f. (-ण्डा) A large earthen pot. Ind. An interjection of calling to<BR>a low female: see हण्डे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डिका|हंडिका
हण्डिका f. (-का) A earthen pot or boiler; also हण्डी and हण्डा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डिकासुत|हण्डिकासुतः
हण्डिकासुत m. (-तः) A small earthen pot.<BR> E. हण्डिका, सुत son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हण्डे|हंडे
हण्डे Ind. A vocative particle to be addressed in theatrical language<BR>to a female of inferior rank.<BR> E. हिडि to treat with contempt or<BR>disrespect, aff. ए, and the form irr.; also with आ aff., हण्डा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत|हतः
हत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Struck, hurt, killed.<BR>	 2. Destroyed.<BR>	 3. Departed,<BR>lost.<BR>	 4. Ended.<BR>	 5. Deprived of, devoid of.<BR>	 6. Disappointed.<BR>	 7.<BR>Multiplied, (in arithmetic.)<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. Multiplication.<BR>	 2. Hurting,<BR>killing.<BR> E. हन् to strike or hurt, aff. क्त. It is often used at the<BR>beginning of compounds in the sense of “miserable,” “worthless.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतक|हतकः
हतक m. (-कः) A coward, a poltroon.<BR>	 f. (-का) Adj. Miserable, ill-bred,<BR>(generally used at the end of compounds.)<BR> E. हत slain, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतकण्टक|हतकंटक
हतकण्टक Adj.<BR>	 1. Freed from thorns, (lit.)<BR>	 2. Freed from enemies, (fig.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतचित
हतचित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Bewildered, astounded, bereft of sense.<BR> E. हत,<BR>चित mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतजीवित
हतजीवित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Deprived of life or hope, overcome with<BR>despair.<BR>	 n. (-तं) Despair.<BR> E. हत, and जीवित living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतताप
हतताप mfn. (-पः-पा-पं) Cool after great heat.<BR> E. हत, and ताप heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतदैव
हतदैव n. (-वं) Ill-starred, ill fated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतसम्पद
हतसम्पद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Reduced to poverty.<BR> E. हत, and सम्पद property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतसाध्वस
हतसाध्वस mfn. (-सः-सा-सं) Fearless, free from fear.<BR> E. हत, साध्वस fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हताधिमन्थ
हताधिमन्थ m. (-न्थः) Loss of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हताश|हताशः
हताश mfn. (-शः-शा-शं)<BR>	 1. Cruel, merciless.<BR>	 2. Desponding, despairing.<BR>3. Vile, wicked.<BR>	 4. Barren.<BR>	 5. Weak, powerless.<BR> E. हत destroyed,<BR>आशा hope, (in or by whom.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हताश्व
हताश्व mfn. (-श्वः-श्वा-श्वं) Having the horses killed.<BR> E. हत, अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हति|हतिः
हति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Striking, a stroke.<BR>	 2. Killing.<BR>	 3. Defect, flaw.<BR>	 4.<BR>Multiplication, (in arithmetic.)<BR> E. हन्, causal v., क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतौजस्
हतौजस् mfn. (-जाः-जाः-जः) Debilitated, weak.<BR>	 m. (-जाः) A kind of fever,<BR>fever with debility.<BR> E. हत, and ओजस् vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्नु|हत्नुः
हत्नु m. (-त्नुः)<BR>	 1. Sickness, disease.<BR>	 2. A weapon.<BR> E. हन् to kill or hurt, कत्नुच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्या
हत्या f. (-त्या) Killing, slaying, (used chiefly in criminal killing, as in<BR>ब्रह्महत्या the murder of a Brāhman, गोहत्या killing a cow, &c.<BR> E. हन्<BR>to kill, क्यप् aff., and न changed to त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=826-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्वा
हत्वा Ind. Having struck or killed.<BR> E. हन् to hurt, &c., क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्थ
हत्थ m. (-थः) A man dejected or in low spirits.<BR> E. हन् to hurt, क्थन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हद्
हद् r. 1st cl. (हदते) To evacuate as fæces, to discharge excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हदन|हदनं
हदन n. (-नं) The act of voiding excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्
हन् r. 2nd cl. (हन्ति pl. घ्नन्ति)<BR>	 1. To hurt, to strike, to injure, to do any<BR>act which tends to the destruction of life, to kill.<BR>	 2. To over-<BR>come, to overthrow, to conquer.<BR>	 3. To remove, to take away.<BR>	 4.<BR>To obstruct.<BR>	 5. To put an end to in any manner.<BR>	 6. To multiply,<BR>(in math.)<BR>	 7. To go, to move, (not used in classical literature; in<BR>a few places where it is found so used poeticians have held the<BR>use to be faulty.) With अप, 1. To destroy, to ward off.<BR>	 2. To<BR>lesson. With अव, 1. To strike, to hit.<BR>	 2. To thresh, to winnow,<BR>(as corn.) With आ, (Atm.)<BR>	 1. To strike at.<BR>	 2. To beat, (as a<BR>drum.) With उद्, 1. To elevate.<BR>	 2. To become haughty or vain.<BR>With उप, 1. To destroy.<BR>	 2. To vex. With नि, 1. To strike.<BR>	 2. To<BR>beat, (as a drum.)<BR>	 3. To kill.<BR>	 4. To frustrate, to render void.<BR>	 5.<BR>To neglect.<BR>	 6. To cure, (as a disease.) With परा, 1. To strike down<BR>or back.<BR>	 2. To assail.<BR>	 3. To drive back. With वि, 1. To strike vio-<BR>lently.<BR>	 2. To oppose, to impede.<BR>	 3. To reject, to deny.<BR>	 4. To kill.<BR>With अभि, 1. To sound a musical instrument.<BR>	 2. To strike, to<BR>beat.<BR>	 3. To inflict injury on. With आङ्, To smite. With नि or<BR>परि, To destroy entirely. With प्र, 1. To strike.<BR>	 2. To slay.<BR>	 3. To<BR>beat, (as a drum.)<BR>	 4. To place upon. With प्रति, 1. To refute or ds-<BR>troy, (an opposite argument.)<BR>	 2. To keep off, to strike back.<BR>	 3.<BR>To repel.<BR>	 4. To resist.<BR>	 5. To remove. With वि and आङ्, To obstruct,<BR>to prevent, to hinder. With सम्, 1. To slaughter.<BR>	 2. To join or<BR>unite closely.<BR>	 3. To collect.<BR>	 4. To diminish, to contract. (घन् or घ्न<BR>is substituted for the radical letters of this verb in many of its<BR>inflections and derivatives; the root also takes most of the<BR>prefixes with little or no variation of the sense)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन|हनः
हन m. (-नः) A killer, a slayer.<BR> E. हन् to kill, अच् aff.; also with क्विप् aff.,<BR>हन् m. (-हा ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनन|हननं|हननः
हनन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Killing, destroying.<BR>	 2. Injuring, hurting, striking.<BR>	 3.<BR>(In arithmetic,) Multiplication.<BR> E. हन् to hurt or kill, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हननीय
हननीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) What may be or ought to be struck, beaten,<BR>killed.<BR> E. हन् to kill, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनु|हनुः
हनु mfn. (-नुः-नुः or नूः-नु)<BR>	 1. The jaw.<BR>	 2. The chin.<BR>	 f. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. A drug and<BR>perfume: see हट्टविलासिनी.<BR>	 2. A weapon.<BR>	 3. Sickness.<BR>	 4. Death, dying.<BR>5. A prostitute.<BR> E. हन् to hurt or kill, aff. उत्; also with ऊङ्, हनू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुग्रह|हनुग्रहः
हनुग्रह m. (-हः) Locked jaw.<BR> E. हनु, and ग्रह seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुमत्|हनुमन्त्
हनुमत् m. (-मान्)<BR>	 1. The monkey chief HANUMĀN, the son of ANJANĀ,<BR>by PAVANA or the wind, the friend, ally and spy of RĀMACHANDRA,<BR>in his invasion of LANKĀ.<BR>	 2. A particular sort of monkey, (Simia<BR>sinica.)<BR> E. हनु the jaw, and मतुप् aff.; also with हनू, हनूमत् m. (-मान्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुमूल
हनुमूल n. (-लं) The root of the jaw or chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुस्तम्भ|हनुस्तम्भः
हनुस्तम्भ m. (-म्भः) Locked jaw.<BR> E. हनु, and स्तम्भ stiffness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनूष्
हनूष् m. (-षः) A goblin, a demon.<BR> E. हन् to kill, ऊषन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्त|हंत
हन्त Ind.<BR>	 1. An inceptive particle.<BR>	 2. An exclamation of grief, (ah,<BR>alas !)<BR>	 3. Of pity.<BR>	 4. Of pleasure.<BR>	 5. Of hurry or haste.<BR>	 6. Of joy.<BR>7. Of surprise.<BR> E. हन् to kill, त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तकार|हंतकार|हन्तकारः
हन्तकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Rice or any offering to be given to a guest.<BR>	 2. The<BR>exclamation “हन्त”.<BR> E. हन्त, कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तव्य
हन्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) What may be, or ought to be struck, killed, &c.<BR> E. हन्, तव्य aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तु|हंतुः|हन्तुः
हन्तु m. (-न्तुः)<BR>	 1. Death.<BR>	 2. A bull.<BR> E. हन् to kill, तुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तृ|हंतृ
हन्तृ m. (-न्ता)<BR>	 1. A murderer, a slayer.<BR>	 2. A thief, a robber.<BR>	 3. A measure<BR>of food, four times four double handfuls.<BR>	 f. (-न्त्री)<BR>	 1. Who or what<BR>strikes or kills.<BR>	 2. One who destroys or removes.<BR> E. हन् to kill, तृच्<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तोक्ति|हंतोक्ति|हन्तोक्तिः
हन्तोक्ति f. (-क्तिः) Tenderness, compassion.<BR> E. हन्त alas! and उक्ति saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्न|हन्नं|हन्नः
हन्न mfn. (-न्नः-न्ना-न्नं) Passed as ordure.<BR> E. हद् to void fæces, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्यमान|हन्यमानः
हन्यमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being killed or struck.<BR> E. हन् to hurt or kill,<BR>pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्
हम् Ind.<BR>	 1. An interjection of wrath.<BR>	 2. An expression of courtesy or respect.<BR> E. हा, डमु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्भा|हंभा
हम्भा f. (-म्भा) The lowing of kine.<BR> E. हम् imitative sound, भा to shine,<BR>affs. अङ् and टाप्; also हम्बा and हम्मा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्भारवविराविन्
हम्भारवविराविन् mfn. (-वी-विणी-वि) Lowing, bellowing.<BR> E. हम्भा, रव sound, विराविन् uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्म्
हम्म् r. 1st. cl. (हम्मति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हय्
हय् r. 1st cl. (हयति)<BR>	 1. To move.<BR>	 2. To worship.<BR>	 3. To sound.<BR>	 4. To be weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हय|हयः
हय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. A man of a particular class.<BR>	 3. The<BR>number “seven.” 4. INDRA'S horse.<BR>	 5. The Yak.<BR>	 6. (In prosody,)<BR>A foot of four short syllables, a proceleusmaticus.<BR>	 f. (-यी) A mare.<BR>f. (-या) A plant: see अश्वगन्धा ।<BR> E. हय् to go, or हि to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयकोविद
हयकोविद Adj. Skilled in the science of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयगन्ध|हयगन्धं
हयगन्ध n. (-न्धं) Black salt.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा) A plant, (Physalis flexuosa.)<BR> E. हय a horse, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयग्रीव|हयग्रीवः
हयग्रीव m. (-वः) A prince of the Daityas, who during BRAHMA'S sleep<BR>at the end of a KALPA stole the Vedas; in the recovery of them,<BR>he was slain by VIṢṆU, after his descent as the MATSYA or fish<BR>Avatār.<BR> E. हय a horse, and ग्रीवा neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयग्रीवहन्
हयग्रीवहन् m. (-हा) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. हयग्रीव the Daitya, and हन् slayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयङ्कष|हयंकष|हयंकषः|हयङ्कषः
हयङ्कष m. (-षः)<BR>	 1. A driver, a charioteer.<BR>	 2. INDRA'S charioteer.<BR> E. हय<BR>a horse, or INDRA'S horse, and कष् to hurt, aff. खच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयज्ञ|हयज्ञः
हयज्ञ m. (-ज्ञः) A horse-dealer, a groom, a jockey, one who is a judge<BR>of the qualities of a horse.<BR> E. हय, and ज्ञ who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयज्ञता
हयज्ञता f. (-ता) Horsemanship, knowledge of horses and their manage-<BR>ment.<BR> E. तल् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयद्विषत्|हयद्विषन्त्
हयद्विषत् m. (-षन्) The buffalo.<BR> E. हय, and द्विषत् foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयन|हयनं|हयनः
हयन n. (-नं) A covered carriage.<BR>	 m. (-नः) A year.<BR> E. हय् to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयपुच्छ
हयपुच्छ m. (-च्छः) A horse's tail.<BR>	 f. (-च्छी) A leguminous plant, (Glycine<BR>debilis.)<BR> E. हय a horse, पुच्छ the tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयप्रिय|हयप्रियः
हयप्रिय m. (-यः) Barley.<BR>	 f. (-या) The Kharjūrī tree.<BR> E. हय a horse, प्रिय fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयमारक|हयमारकः
हयमारक m. (-कः) A shrub, the fragrant oleander, (Nerium odorum.)<BR>E. हय a horse, मारक killer; also with मार the same, हयमार m. (-रः ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयमारण|हयमारणः
हयमारण m. (-णः) The holy-fig tree, (Ficus religiosa.)<BR> E. हय, मारण killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयमेध|हयमेधः
हयमेध m. (-धः) The sacrifice of a horse: see अश्वमेध.<BR> E. हय, and मेध<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयवाहन|हयवाहनः
हयवाहन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The son of SŪRYA.<BR>	 2. KUVERA.<BR> E. हय a horse, वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयवाहनसङ्कर|हयवाहनसंकर
हयवाहनसङ्कर m. (-रः) Mountain-ebony, the red sort. “रक्तकाञ्चने” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयशाला
हयशाला f. (-ला) A stable for horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयशास्त्र
हयशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) The art or science of training and managing horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयसङ्ग्रहण
हयसङ्ग्रहण n. (-णं) The restraining or curbing of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयानन्द|हयानन्दः
हयानन्द m. (-न्दः) Kidney-bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR> E. हय horse, आनन्द delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयारि|हयारिः
हयारि m. (-रिः) A shrub, (Nerium odorum.)<BR> E. हय a horse, अरि inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयारूढ|हयारूढः
हयारूढ m. (-ढः) A horseman, a rider.<BR> E. हय, and आरूढ mounted on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयारोह|हयारोहः
हयारोह m. (-हः) Riding, horsemanship.<BR> E. हय, and आरोह mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयाशना
हयाशना f. (-ना) The gum Olibanum tree.<BR> E. हय a horse, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयेष्ट|हयेष्टः
हयेष्ट m. (-ष्टः) Barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयोत्तम|हयोत्तमः
हयोत्तम m. (-मः) An excellent horse.<BR> E. हय a horse, and उत्तम best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर|हरः
हर mfn. (रः-रा or -री-रं) Who or what takes or seizes, carries or<BR>conveys, divides, removes, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. AGNI.<BR>	 3. An<BR>ass.<BR>	 4. (In Arithmetic,) A divisor; also the denominator of a<BR>fraction.<BR> E. हृ to take, aff. अप्, अच् or टच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरक|हरकः
हरक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A rogue, a cheat.<BR>	 2. A person of reflection.<BR>	 3. A<BR>taker, a conveyer, a seizer.<BR>	 4. (In Arithmetic,) A divisor; also<BR>division.<BR>	 5. SĪVA.<BR> E. हृ to take, वुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरगौरी
हरगौरी f. (-री) One of the forms of ŚIVA and PĀRVATĪ conjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरचूडामणि|हरचूडामणिः
हरचूडामणि m. (-णिः) The moon.<BR> E. हर ŚIVA, चूडा the crest, मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरण|हरणं
हरण n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Taking, (either in a good or bad sense,) accepting,<BR>receiving, seizing, stealing, dividing, carrying off or away.<BR>	 2. A<BR>special gift, as a nuptial present, alms to a student at his<BR>initiation, &c.<BR>	 3. The arm.<BR>	 4. Semen virile.<BR>	 5. Gold.<BR>	 6. A Kowri.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">Page828-a+ 60</a>]<BR>7. Boiling water.<BR>	 8. (In Arithmetic,) Dividing, division.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>The hand.<BR> E. हृ to take, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=827-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरणीय
हरणीय mfn. (-यः-या-य) To be taken, seized, accepted, &c.<BR> E. हृ to take, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरत्
हरत् mfn. (-रन्-रन्ती-रत्) Taking, seizing.<BR> E. हृ to take, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरतेजस्
हरतेजस् n. (-जः) Quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरनेत्र|हरनेत्रं
हरनेत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA'S eye.<BR>	 2. The number “three,” (in mathematics.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरवीज
हरवीज n. (-जं) Quicksilver.<BR> E. हर ŚIVA, and वीज semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरशेखरा
हरशेखरा f. (-रा) The Ganges.<BR> E. हर ŚIVA, and शेखर crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरसूनु|हरसूनुः
हरसूनु m. (-नुः)<BR>	 1. SKANDA.<BR>	 2. GANESA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरहूरा
हरहूरा f. (-रा) A grape; also हारहूरा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हराद्रि|हराद्रिः
हराद्रि m. (-द्रिः) Mount Kailāsa, the favourite resort of ŚIVA.<BR> E. हर ŚIVA, अद्रि mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरि|हरिः
हरि mfn. (-रिः-रिः-रि)<BR>	 1. Green, greenish.<BR>	 2. Tawny.<BR>	 3. Yellow.<BR>	 m. (-रिः)<BR>1. VIṢṆU, or as considered to be the same deity, with KṚṢṆA.<BR>2. YAMA.<BR>	 3. Air, wind.<BR>	 4. INDRA.<BR>	 5. The moon.<BR>	 6. The sun.<BR>	 7. A<BR>lion.<BR>	 8. A ray of light 9. A horse.<BR>	 10. A parrot.<BR>	 11. An ape.<BR>	 12. A<BR>snake.<BR>	 13. A frog.<BR>	 14. ŚIVA.<BR>	 15. One of the nine VARSHAS into<BR>which the known continent is divided.<BR>	 16. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 17. Fire.<BR>18. The Kokila or Indian cuckoo.<BR>	 19. A goose.<BR>	 20. A peacock.<BR>21. Green, (the colour.)<BR>	 22. Tawny, (the colour.)<BR>	 23. A golden<BR>colour, or yellow.<BR>	 24. A horse of INDRA.<BR>	 25. A name of the poet<BR>BHARTRIHARI.<BR>	 26. A learned man.<BR> E. हृ to take, to seize, (the<BR>world or men's hearts, &c.,) Unādi aff. इन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिक|हरिकः
हरिक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A horse of a yellowish blue tint.<BR>	 2. A thief.<BR>	 3. A<BR>gambler.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिकान्त|हरिकांत
हरिकान्त Adj.<BR>	 1. Dear to INDRA.<BR>	 2. Beautiful as a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिकेलीय|हरिकेलीयः
हरिकेलीय m. (-यः) Bengal.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, केलि sport, and छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिकेश|हरिकेशः
हरिकेश m. (-शः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, क BRAHMĀ, and ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिगन्ध|हरिगंध
हरिगन्ध n. (-न्धं) A sort of Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिगृह|हरिगृहं
हरिगृह n. (-हं) A city and district, also Sambhapūr.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, गृह abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिचन्दन|हरिचंदन|हरिचन्दनं|हरिचन्दनः
हरिचन्दन mn. (-नः-नं)<BR>	 1. A yellow and fragrant sort of Sandal wood.<BR>2. One of the five trees of paradise, (the other four being, पारिजात,<BR>मन्दार, सन्तान and कल्प.)<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Saffron.<BR>	 2. Moon-light.<BR>	 3. The<BR>filament or farina of a lotus.<BR>	 4. The person of a lover or mistress.<BR>E. हरि VIṢṆU, or yellow, and चन्दन Sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिण|हरिणः
हरिण mfn. (-णः-णी-णं) Yellowish white.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A deer.<BR>	 2. Pale,<BR>yellowish white, (the colour.)<BR>	 3. White.<BR>	 4. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 5. ŚIVA.<BR>	 6. The<BR>sun.<BR>	 7. A goose.<BR>	 8. A minor division of the world.<BR>	 f. (-णी)<BR>	 1. A<BR>doe.<BR>	 2. A golden image.<BR>	 3. A woman, one of the four kinds, the<BR>same as the CHITRINI, or female of the man termed MRIGA.<BR>	 4. A<BR>form of metre, a variety of the class termed Atyashti or verse of<BR>four lines of 17 syllables each.<BR>	 5. Green: see हरित.<BR>	 6. Yellow<BR>jasmine.<BR>	 7. A female deer.<BR> E. हृ to take, Unādi aff. इनन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणक|हरिणकः
हरिणक m. (-कः) A deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणकलङ्क|हरिणकलंक|हरिणकलङ्कः
हरिणकलङ्क m. (-ङ्कः) The moon.<BR> E. हरिण a deer, कलङ्क a spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणनयन
हरिणनयन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Deer-eyed.<BR> E. हरिण, नयन the eye; also<BR>हरिणलोचन, हरिणाक्षि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणनर्त्तक|हरिणनर्तक|हरिणनर्तकः|हरिणनर्त्तकः
हरिणनर्त्तक m. (-कः) A chorister of INDRA'S heaven.<BR> E. हरिण a deer, नर्त्तक a dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणप्लुता
हरिणप्लुता f. (-ता) A stanza having eleven syllables in every first and<BR>third PĀDA, and twelve in every second and fourth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणहृदय|हरिणहृदयः
हरिणहृदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Fearful, timid.<BR> E. हरिण a deer, हृदय heart;<BR>deer-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाक्ष|हरिणाक्षः
हरिणाक्ष Adj. Deer-eyed, fawn-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाक्षी
हरिणाक्षी f. (-क्षी)<BR>	 1. A perfume, commonly Hatta-vilaśinī.<BR>	 2. A woman<BR>with handsome eyes.<BR> E. हरिण a deer, अक्षि the eye, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाङ्क|हरिणांक|हरिणाङ्कः
हरिणाङ्क m. (-ङ्कः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. हरिण a deer, अङ्क mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित्
हरित् mfn. (-रित्)<BR>	 1. Green, of a green colour.<BR>	 2. Yellowish.<BR>	 m. (-रित्)<BR>1. Green, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. A swift horse.<BR>	 3. A horse of the sun.<BR>4. Kidney-bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR>	 5. A lion.<BR>	 6. The sun.<BR>	 7.<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR>	 mn. (-रित्) Grass.<BR>	 f. (-रित्)<BR>	 1. A quarter or region, a<BR>point of the compass.<BR>	 2. Turmeric.<BR> E. हृ to take, Unādi aff. इति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित|हरितं|हरितः
हरित mn. (-तः-ता or -रिणी-तं)<BR>	 1. Green, of a green colour.<BR>	 2. Grassy,<BR>verdant.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. Green, (the colour.)<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR>	 3. A kind of<BR>grass.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. Bent grass.<BR>	 2. Turmeric.<BR>	 3. A brown or tawny<BR>grape.<BR> E. हृ to take, इतच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितक|हरितकं
हरितक m. (-कः) A potherb.<BR> E. हरित green, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितच्छद|हरितछद
हरितच्छद mfn. (-दः-दा-दं) Green-leaved.<BR> E. हरित, छद a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितायत्
हरितायत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Becoming green.<BR> E. हरित used a verb, शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताल|हरितालं|हरितालः
हरिताल n. (-लं) Yellow orpiment.<BR>	 f. (-ली)<BR>	 1. Bent grass, (Panicum<BR>dactylon.)<BR>	 2. A streak or line in the sky, the milky way.<BR>	 3. A sort<BR>of creeper.<BR>	 4. A kind of pigeon.<BR> E. हरित green, अल् to possess or<BR>adorn, aff. अण्, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालक|हरितालकं|हरितालकः
हरितालक m. (-कः) The green pigeon.<BR>	 n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. Theatrical decoration.<BR>painting the person.<BR>	 2. Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. हरताल orpiment, कन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालिका
हरितालिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. A sort of grass, (Panicum dactylon, Rox.)<BR>	 2.<BR>The fourth lunar day of the month of Bhādrapada.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to हरिताल, fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताश्मन्
हरिताश्मन् n. (-श्म)<BR>	 1. Blue vitriol, sulphate of copper.<BR>	 2. An emerald.<BR>E. हरित green, अश्मन् a stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितीकृत
हरितीकृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Made verdant or green, coloured green, &c.<BR>E. हरित, and कृत made, with च्वि augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितुरङ्गम|हरितुरंगमः
हरितुरङ्गम m. (-मः) A name of INDRA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित्पर्ण|हरित्पर्णं
हरित्पर्ण n. (-र्णं) A radish. “मूलके” ।<BR> E. हरित् green, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदश्व|हरिदश्वः
हरिदश्व m. (-श्वः)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The Arka plant.<BR> E. हरित् green, अश्व a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदास|हरिदासः
हरिदास m. (-सः) A worshipper of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदिन
हरिदिन n. (-नं) A particular day sacred to VIṢṆU: see हरिवासर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदेव|हरिदेवः
हरिदेव m. (-वः) The asterism ŚRAVANĀ.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, देब presiding<BR>deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्गर्भ|हरिद्गर्भः
हरिद्गर्भ m. (-र्भः) Green Kuśa grass with broad leaves; also हरिदर्भ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रव|हरिद्रवः
हरिद्रव m. (-वः) The pollen of the blossoms of the Mesua ferrea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रा
हरिद्रा f. (-द्रा) Turmeric, (either the plant or the powdered root) E.<BR>हरित् green, द्रु to flow or ooze, aff. ड; or हरि VIṢṆU, &c., दृ to be<BR>regarded, aff. क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राक्त
हरिद्राक्त mfn. (-क्तः-क्ता-क्तं) Smeared or stained with turmeric.<BR> E. हरिद्रा, अक्त anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राङ्ग|हरिद्राङ्गः
हरिद्राङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A yellow bird.<BR> E. हरिद्रा turmeric, and अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राभ|हरिद्राभः
हरिद्राभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Of a yellow colour.<BR>	 m. (-भः)<BR>	 1. A tree,<BR>(Pentaptera tomentosa.)<BR>	 2. Zedoary, (Curcuma zerumbet.)<BR>	 3.<BR>Yellow, (the colour.)<BR> E. हरिद्रा turmeric, आभ resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राराग|हरिद्रारागः
हरिद्राराग mfn. (-गः-गा-गं) Fickle, capricious, unsteady, in affection or<BR>attachment.<BR> E. हरिद्रा turmeric, and राग colour, in opposition to<BR>the नीलराग or true blue; also with कन् added, हरिद्रारागक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रु|हरिद्रुः
हरिद्रु m. (-द्रुः)<BR>	 1. A tree.<BR>	 2. A plant, (Curcuma zanthorrhizon.)<BR> E. हरि<BR>a monkey, द्रु to go, Unādi aff. कु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्वार|हरिद्वारं
हरिद्वार n. (-रं) The town of HARIDWĀR. where the Ganges descends<BR>into the level land of HINDUSTHAN, the sacred bathing-place of<BR>the Hindus.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, and द्वार gate; being the road to<BR>VAIKUṆṬHA or VIṢṆU'S heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिनामन्
हरिनामन् m. (-मा) A kidney-bean, (Phaseolus mungo.)<BR> E. हरि the<BR>same, and नामन् appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिनेत्र|हरिनेत्रं|हरिनेत्रः
हरिनेत्र m. (-त्रः) An owl.<BR>	 n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. The white lotus.<BR>	 2. The eye of<BR>VIṢṆU.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, &c., and नेत्र an eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिन्मणि|हरिन्मणिः
हरिन्मणि m. (-णिः) An emerald.<BR> E. हरित् green, and मणि a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिपर्ण|हरिपर्णं
हरिपर्ण n. (-र्णं) A radish.<BR> E. हरि green, and पर्ण a leaf; also हरित्पर्ण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिप्रिय|हरिप्रियं|हरिप्रियः
हरिप्रिय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Liked or loved by VIṢṆU, &c.<BR>	 m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. A<BR>tree, (Nauclea Kadamba.)<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3. A fool, a block-head.<BR>	 4.<BR>Armour, mail.<BR>	 n. (-य)<BR>	 1. A dark sort of Sandal wood.<BR>	 2. The fra-<BR>grant root of the Andropogon muricatum.<BR>	 3. A conch-shell.<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>1. LAKṢMĪ, the wife of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. TULASĪ or basil.<BR>	 3. The twelfth<BR>day of the lunar fortnight.<BR>	 4. The earth.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, and प्रिय<BR>beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिबालुक|हरिबालुकं
हरिबालुक n. (-कं) A perfume and drug, commonly Elabālukā.<BR> E. हरि tawny, बालुका sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=828-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिभद्र|हरिभद्रं
हरिभद्र n. (-द्रं) A sort of perfume, commonly Elabālukā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिभुज्
हरिभुज् m. (-भुक्) A snake.<BR> E. हरि a frog, and भुज् what eats, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्
हरिमन् m. (-मा) Time.<BR> E. हृ to take, इमनिच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्थ|हरिमन्थः
हरिमन्थ m. (-न्थः)<BR>	 1. A tree, (Premna longifolia.)<BR>	 2. Chick-pea.<BR> E. हरि<BR>fire or a horse, &c., and मन्थ agitating or churning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्थक|हरिमन्थकः
हरिमन्थक m. (-कः) Chick-pea, (Cicer arietinum.)<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्थज|हरिमन्थजः
हरिमन्थज m. (-जः)<BR>	 1. Chick-pea.<BR>	 2. The black sort of kidney-bean.<BR>E. हरि a horse, &c., मन्थ churning, chewing, मन् to produce, aff. ड ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिय|हरियः
हरिय m. (-यः) A horse of a yellowish colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिले
हरिले Ind. A term of calling in theatrical language, addressed to a female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिलोचन|हरिलोचनः
हरिलोचन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A crab.<BR>	 2. An owl.<BR> E. हरि green, लोचन the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवत्|हरिवन्त्
हरिवत् m. (-वान्) INDRA.<BR> E. हरि a horse, मतुप् aff.; more properly हरिवात् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवर्ष|हरिवर्षं|हरिवर्षः
हरिवर्ष n. (-र्षं) A division of the old or known continent; the country<BR>between the NISHADHA and HEMAKŪTA mountains.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU,<BR>and वर्ष a division of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवल्लभा
हरिवल्लभा f. (-भा)<BR>	 1. LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. The holy basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवात्
हरिवात् m. (-वान्) INDRA.<BR> E. हरि the horse of INDRA, वात् to go, aff. शतृ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवासर|हरिवासरं|हरिवासरः
हरिवासर m. (-रः) The eleventh day of a lunar fortnight; also हरिदिन ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवाहन|हरिवाहनः
हरिवाहन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. GARUḌA.<BR>	 2. INDRA.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, or the horse of<BR>INDRA, and वाहन a vehicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिबीज
हरिबीज n. (-जं) Yellow orpiment.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, and वीज seamen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवृष|हरिवृषं
हरिवृष n. (-षं) A division of the known continent: see हरिवर्ष ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिशर|हरिशरः
हरिशर m. (-रः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, शर an arrow; VIṢṆU having<BR>served him as the shaft which set the cities of TRIPURA on fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिश्चन्द्र|हरिश्चंद्रः|हरिश्चन्द्रः
हरिश्चन्द्र m. (-न्द्रः) A sovereign, the twenty-eighth of the solar dynasty<BR>in the second age, celebrated for his piety and liberality, and who<BR>on those accounts was elevated, together with his subjects, to<BR>heaven: having been insidiously induced by NĀRADA, to relate<BR>his actions with unbecoming pride, he descended from Svarga, a<BR>stage at each sentence, till stopping in time, and doing homage to<BR>the gods, he was fixed with his capital in mid-air.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU,<BR>चन्द्र the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिश्चन्द्रपुर|हरिश्चन्द्रपुरं
हरिश्चन्द्रपुर n. (-रं) The city of HARIŚCHANDRA: see the last.<BR> E. हरिश्चन्द्र the sovereign, पुर city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिषेण|हरिषेणः
हरिषेण m. (-णः) The tenth of the twelve universal emperor<BR>enumerated by the Jainas.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, &c., सेना a host.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिसख|हरिसखः
हरिसख m. (-खः) A GANDHARVA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिसङ्कीर्त्तन|हरिसङ्कीर्तन|हरिसङ्कीर्त्तनं
हरिसङ्कीर्त्तन n. (-नं) The act of repeating the name of VIṢṆU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिसुत|हरिसुतः
हरिसुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. One of the emperors of the Jainas; also named<BR>HARISHEṆA.<BR>	 2. ARJUNA.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU, or INDRA, सुत the son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहय|हरिहयः
हरिहय m. (-यः)<BR>	 1. INDRA.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. हरि green, and हय a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहर|हरिहरः
हरिहर m. (-रः) A particular form of deity consisting of VIṢṆU and<BR>ŚIVA conjointly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहरात्मक|हरिहरात्मकः
हरिहरात्मक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. GARUD A.<BR>	 2. The bull of ŚIVA.<BR> E. हरि VIṢṆU,<BR>and हर ŚIVA, आत्मन् self, same, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहेति|हरिहेतिः
हरिहेति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. The disc of VIṢṆU.<BR>	 2. The rain-bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरीतकी
हरीतकी f. (-की) Yellow or Chebulic myrobalan, (Terminalia chebula:)<BR>seven varieties of this are distinguished.<BR> E. हरि green, (colour,) इत<BR>gone, got, कन् added, fem. aff. ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेणु|हरेणुः
हरेणु f. (-णुः)<BR>	 1. A drug and perfume, commonly Reṇukā.<BR>	 2. A<BR>reputable woman.<BR>	 3. Pulse, pease.<BR>	 4. A deer of a copper colour.<BR>E. हृ to take, एणु Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्त्तव्य|हर्तव्य
हर्त्तव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be seized, taken, accepted, &c.<BR> E. हृ to take, तव्यर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्त्तृ|हर्तृ
हर्त्तृ mfn. (-र्त्ता-र्त्त्री-र्त्तृ) Taking, seizing, conveying, who takes or<BR>receives.<BR>	 m. (-र्त्ता)<BR>	 1. A thief.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. हृ to take or convey,<BR>aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्मन्|हर्मन्
हर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म) Gaping, yawning.<BR> E. हृ to take, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्मित|हर्मित|हर्म्मितं
हर्म्मित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Thrown, cast, sent.<BR>	 2. Burnt.<BR>	 3. Yawned.<BR> E. हर्मन्-इत्रच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्म्य
हर्म्म्य n. (-र्म्म्यं)<BR>	 1. A palace, a mansion, the habitation of a man of<BR>wealth or rank.<BR>	 2. A fire place, a hearth.<BR>	 3. The nether world.<BR>E. हृ to take, (the mind,) यत् aff., and मुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्य्|हर्य्
हर्य्य् r. 1st cl. (हर्य्यति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To desire.<BR>	 3. To be weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्यक्ष|हर्यक्ष|हर्यक्षः|हर्य्यक्षः
हर्य्यक्ष m. (-क्षः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. KUVERA.<BR> E. हरि tawny or green, अक्षि the<BR>eye, षच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्यत|हर्यत|हर्यतः|हर्य्यतः
हर्य्यत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A horse.<BR>	 2. A steed fit for an Aśwa-medha.<BR> E. हृ to take, अतच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्यश्व|हर्यश्व|हर्यश्वः|हर्य्यश्वः
हर्य्यश्व m. (-श्वः) INDRA.<BR> E. हरि green, अश्व a horse; also हरिहय &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्ष|हर्षः
हर्ष mfn. (-र्षः-र्षा-र्षं) Happy, delighted.<BR>	 m. (-र्षः)<BR>	 1. Joy, pleasure, delight,<BR>happiness, glee, rapture, exultation.<BR>	 2. Joy, considered as one of<BR>the thirty-three minor feelings, (in rhetoric.)<BR>	 3. Bristling, erection,<BR>(of the hair.)<BR> E. हृष् to be pleased, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षक|हर्षकः
हर्षक mfn. (-कः-र्षका or -र्षिका-कं) Delighting, pleasing, delightful.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः) The name of a mountain.<BR> E. हृष् to be pleased, aff. खुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षकर
हर्षकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Causing delight, gratifying, delighting.<BR> E. हर्ष,<BR>and कर who or what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षण|हर्षणं|हर्षणः
हर्षण mfn. (-णः-णा or -णी-णं) Causing delight, delighting, delightful,<BR>pleasurable, pleasant, &c.<BR>	 m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A cause of pleasure, any<BR>thing which confers pleasure.<BR>	 2. The fourteenth of the astrono-<BR>mical Yogas.<BR>	 3. A morbid affection of the eyes.<BR>	 4. A deity presi-<BR>ding over Śrāddhas.<BR>	 5. A kind of Śrāddha.<BR>	 6. An epithet of one<BR>of the five arrows of KĀMADEVA.<BR>	 n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Pleasing, making<BR>happy.<BR>	 2. Rejoicing, being happy.<BR> E. हृंष् to be pleased, aff. ल्युट्<BR>or युच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षमाण|हर्षमाणः
हर्षमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Joyful, cheerful, happy.<BR> E. हष् to be pleased, शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षयित्नु|हर्षयित्नुः
हर्षयित्नु mfn. (-त्नुः-त्नुः-त्नु) Causing delight, delighting.<BR>	 m. (-त्नुः) A son,<BR>a child.<BR>	 n. (-त्नु) Gold.<BR> E. हृष् to be pleased, Unādi aff. इत्नुच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षविह्वल
हर्षविह्वल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Overjoyed.<BR> E. हर्ष, and विह्वल agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षसमन्वित
हर्षसमन्वित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Joyful.<BR> E. हर्ष, समन्वित possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षस्वन|हर्षस्वनः
हर्षस्वन m. (-नः) A cry expressing joy or pleasure.<BR> E. हर्ष gladness, स्वन sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षित|हर्षितः
हर्षित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Happy, delighted, gladdened, made glad or<BR>happy.<BR> E. हर्ष, इतच् aff.; or हृष् to be pleased, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षुल|हर्षुलः
हर्षुल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A deer.<BR>	 2. A lover.<BR> E. हृष् to be pleased, उलच् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षोत्कर्ष|हर्षोत्कर्षः
हर्षोत्कर्ष m. (-र्षः) Great happiness.<BR> E. हर्ष, उत्कर्ष eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षोदय|हर्षोदयः
हर्षोदय m. (-यः) Appearance or occurrence of happiness.<BR> E. हर्ष, उदय rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्
हल् r. 1st cl. (हलति) To plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल|हलं|हलः
हल n. (-लं) A plough.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Vinous liquor.<BR>	 2. The earth.<BR>	 3.<BR>Water.<BR>	 4. A female friend: see हला.<BR> E. हल् to plough, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलधर|हलधरः
हलधर mfn. (-रः-रा-री-रं) Holding or having a plough.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A name<BR>of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. हल, and धर who holds or has.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलभूति|हलभूतिः
हलभूति f. (-तिः) Agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलभृत्
हलभृत् mfn. (-भृत्) Having a plough.<BR>	 m. (-भृत्)<BR>	 1. A ploughman.<BR>	 2. A<BR>name of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. हल, भृत् possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलभृति|हलभृतिः
हलभृति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Agriculture.<BR>	 2. A saint so named.<BR> E. हल a plough, भृति having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलहति
हलहति f. (-तिः) Ploughing, furrowing.<BR> E. हल, and हति striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलहलाशब्द
हलहलाशब्द m. (-ब्दः) Noise, tumult.<BR> E. हलहला imitative sound, (as in<BR>halloo, hallooing,) and शब्द sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हला
हला Ind. A vocative particle, addressed in theatrical language to a<BR>female friend.<BR> E. हल् to plough, आ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलायुध|हलायुधः
हलायुध m. (-धः) A name of BALARĀMA.<BR> E. हल a plough, आयुध a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलाह|हलाहः
हलाह m. (-हः) A horse of mixed colour; also read हालाह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलाहल|हलाहलं|हलाहलः
हलाहल mn. (-लः-लं)<BR>	 1. A sort of deadly poison produced at the<BR>churning of the ocean.<BR>	 2. A poison in general.<BR>	 m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A kind<BR>of snake.<BR>	 2. A Jaina or Bauddha deified saint.<BR>	 3. A sort of lizard<BR>or newt.<BR> E. हल् to plough, अच् aff., अ negative, and हल the same;<BR>also हलहल, हालहल, हालाहल, हहल, हाहल and हाहाल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलि|हलिः
हलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. A furrow.<BR>	 2. Agriculture.<BR> E. हल् to plough, इन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलिन्
हलिन् m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. BALADEVA.<BR>	 2. A ploughman, a cultivator.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1.<BR>A plant, commonly Lāngaliya.<BR>	 2. A number of ploughs.<BR> E. हल a<BR>plough, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलिप्रिय|हलिप्रियः
हलिप्रिय m. (-यः) The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea Kadamba.)<BR>	 f. (-या)<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR> E. हलि BALARĀMA, and प्रिय beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलीन|हलीनः
हलीन m. (-नः) The teak tree. “शेगुन.”<BR> E. हल a plough, ख aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=829-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलीम
हलीम(स)क n. (-कं) A sort of jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलीशा
हलीशा f. (-शा) The handle of a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्य|हल्यं
हल्य mfn. (-ल्यः-ल्या-ल्यं)<BR>	 1. Ploughed, tilled.<BR>	 2. Arable.<BR>	 3. Ugly.<BR>	 f. (-ल्या)<BR>A multitude of ploughs.<BR>	 m. (-ल्यः) Ploughing.<BR> E. हल a plough, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्ल्
हल्ल् r. 1st cl. (हल्लति) To expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लक|हल्लकं
हल्लक n. (-कं) The red lotus. “हेलाफुल.”<BR> E. हल्ल् to expand, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लन|हल्लनं
हल्लन n. (-नं) Rolling or tossing as in sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीष|हल्लीषं
हल्लीष n. (-षं)<BR>	 1. One of the eighteen minor dramatic entertainment,<BR>chiefly of singing and dancing by one male and eight or ten<BR>female performers, a ballet.<BR>	 2. A dance performed by women in a<BR>circle.<BR> E. हेला wanton sport, लष् or लस् to be skilful, aff. अच्, deriv.<BR>irr.; or properly हल्-क्विप्-लष्-अच् पृषो० कर्म० । also हल्लीस, and हल्लीश ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीषक|हल्लीषकं
हल्लीषक n. (-कं) Dancing in a ring as performed by woman.<BR> E. कन् added<BR>to हल्लीस, हल्लीष, or हल्लीश; whence it is also read हल्लीसक and हल्लीशक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीस
हल्लीस n. (-सं) A dramatic entertainment, &c.: see हल्लीष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव|हवः
हव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Sacrifice, oblation.<BR>	 2. Call, calling.<BR>	 3. Order, command.<BR>4. Challenging, defying.<BR>	 5. Invocation, prayer.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice,<BR>or ह्वे to call, अप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवङ्ग
हवङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) Eating rice and curds from a cup of bell-metal.<BR> E. हव<BR>sacrifice, गम् to go, aff. खश् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवन|हवनं|हवनः
हवन m. (-नः) Sacrifice, offering, oblation.<BR>	 n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The act of offer-<BR>ing an oblation with fire.<BR>	 2. An oblation so offered.<BR>	 3. Invocation.<BR>4. Calling.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A hole made in the ground for receiving<BR>a sacrificial fire.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice, ल्युट् or युच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवनायुस्
हवनायुस् m. (-युः) Fire.<BR> E. हवन burnt-offering, and आयुस् life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवनीय|हवनीयं
हवनीय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be offered with fire, fit for an oblation, &c.<BR>n. (-यं) Ghee.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice, अनीयर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवा
हवा or हवाव Ind. A term implying undoubtedly, certainly: see हि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवाव
हवा or हवाव Ind. A term implying undoubtedly, certainly: see हि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविःशेष
हविःशेष m. (-षः) The residue of an oblation of Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>E. हविस्, and शेष rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवित्री
हवित्री f. (-त्री) A hole made in the ground for containing a sacrificial<BR>fire.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice, इत्रन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविरशन|हविरशनः
हविरशन m. (-नः) Fire.<BR>	 n. (-नं) The act of devouring clarified butter.<BR> E. हविस् Ghee, अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविर्गन्धा|हविर्गंधा
हविर्गन्धा f. (-न्धा) The Sāmī tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविर्गेह|हविर्गेहं
हविर्गेह n. (-हं) A room in which a burnt-offering is made, a place of<BR>sacrifice.<BR> E. हविस् Ghee, and गेह a house or apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविर्भुज्
हविर्भुज् m. (-भुक्) Fire.<BR> E. हविस्, and भुज् who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविर्याजिन्
हविर्याजिन् m. (-जी) A priest.<BR> E. हविस्, and याजिन् who offers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्मत्|हविष्मन्त्
हविष्मत् Adj. Possessed of oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्य|हविष्यं
हविष्य n. (-ष्यं)<BR>	 1. Clarified butter.<BR>	 2. Rice mixed with Ghee.<BR>	 3. Any<BR>thing fit for an oblation.<BR> E. हविस् an oblation, यत् aff. of fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्यभुज्
हविष्यभुज् m. (-भुक्) Fire.<BR> E. हविष्य and भुज् who eats; also हविष्याशिन्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्यान्न|हविष्यान्नं
हविष्यान्न n. (-न्नं) Food fit to be eaten during certain holy days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविस्
हविस् n. (-विः)<BR>	 1. Clarified butter.<BR>	 2. An intended oblation, the article<BR>to be so offered, usually clarified butter.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR> E. हु to offer<BR>in oblation, असि Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्य|हव्यं
हव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) Fit or proper to be offered in oblations.<BR>	 n. (-व्यं)<BR>1. An offering to the gods, (opposed to कव्य.)<BR>	 2. Ghee.<BR>	 3. An<BR>oblation in general.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्यकव्य
हव्यकव्य n. (-व्यं) The oblations to the gods and to the spirits of deceased ancestors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्यपाक|हव्यपाकः
हव्यपाक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An oblation dressed for the deities.<BR>	 2. The vessel<BR>in which it is prepared.<BR> E. हव्य an offering to the gods, पाक cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्यवाह|हव्यवाहः
हव्यवाह m. (-हः) Fire.<BR> E. हव्य an oblation, and वाह who bears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्यवाहन|हव्यवाहनः
हव्यवाहन m. (-नः) Fire.<BR> E. हव्य an oblation, and वाहन bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्याश|हव्याशः
हव्याश m. (-शः) Fire.<BR> E. हव्य an oblation, and अश who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्याशन|हव्याशनः
हव्याशन m. (-नः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. हव्य a burnt-offering, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्
हस् (ए) हसे r. 1st cl. (हसति)<BR>	 1. To smile.<BR>	 2. To laugh at, to ridicule:<BR>(this root does not take the middle voice when it implies recipro-<BR>cal action, as व्यतिहसन्ति they laugh at each other.)<BR>	 3. To open, to<BR>blow.<BR>	 4. To joke.<BR>	 5. To resemble.<BR>	 6. To brighten up. With अप, To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">Page830-b+ 60</a>]<BR>deride. With परि, 1. To joke.<BR>	 2. To laugh at. With प्र, 1. To<BR>mock.<BR>	 2. To laugh. With वि, 1. To smile.<BR>	 2. To laugh at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस|हसः
हस m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Laughter, laughing, laugh.<BR>	 2. Mirth, merriment, joy.<BR>3. Derision.<BR> E. हस् to laugh, aff. अप्; also with घञ, हास m. (-सः ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसत्
हसत् mfn. (-सन्-सन्ती-सत्) Laughing, smiling.<BR>	 f. (-न्ती)<BR>	 1. A portable<BR>firepan, a small furnace.<BR>	 2. Arabian jasmine.<BR>	 3. A Śakini or female<BR>spirit attendant on DURGĀ.<BR> E. हस् to laugh, aff. शतृ; or हस्-झ-ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसन|हसनं
हसन n. (-नं) Laughter, the act of laughing.<BR>	 f. (-नी) A portable<BR>fireplace or pan.<BR> E. हस् to laugh, aff. ल्युट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसनीमणि|हसनीमणिः
हसनीमणि m. (-णिः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. हसनी a fireplace, and मणि a jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसन्तिका|हसंतिका
हसन्तिका f. (-का) A portable fire-pan.<BR> E. कन् added to हसन्तीः see हसत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसिका
हसिका f. (-का) Laughter.<BR> E. हस् to laugh, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसित|हसितं|हसितः
हसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Blown, budded, (as a flower.)<BR>	 2. Smiling.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं)<BR>	 1. Laughter.<BR>	 2. Smiling.<BR>	 3. Jesting.<BR>	 4. The bow of KĀMA-<BR>DEVA.<BR> E. हस् to laugh, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त|हस्तं|हस्तः
हस्त m. (-स्तः)<BR>	 1. The hand.<BR>	 2. An elephant's trunk.<BR>	 3. The thirteenth<BR>lunar asterism, designated by a hand, and containing five stars.<BR>4. A cubit measured by the hand and arm, or from the elbow to<BR>the tip of the middle finger, (equal to about eighteen inches.)<BR>5. (In prosody,) An anapæst.<BR>	 6. Possession, (figuratively.)<BR>	 7. Hand-<BR>writing, signature.<BR>	 8. Abundance, mass; (in this sense it is<BR>used only at the end of compounds and implies “excellence,”<BR>“abundance,” &c., as केशहस्त means, “A head of hair,” or “Abundance<BR>of hair,” &c.)<BR>	 n. (-स्तं) A bellows.<BR>	 f. (-स्ता) The thirteenth lunar<BR>asterism.<BR> E. हस् to laugh, Unādi aff. तन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तकमल
हस्तकमल n. (-लं) A lotus-like hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तकौशल
हस्तकौशल n. (-लं) Manual dexterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तगत
हस्तगत Adj. Fallen into one's possession, gained, secured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तच्छेदन|हस्तछेदन
हस्तच्छेदन n. (-नं) Cutting off the hand.<BR> E. हस्त, and छेदन cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ततल
हस्ततल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. The palm of the hand.<BR>	 2. The hand.<BR>	 3. The tip of an<BR>elephant's trunk.<BR> E. हस्त, and तल surface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तताल|हस्ततालः
हस्तताल m. (-लः) Clapping the hands together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तदोष|हस्तदोषः
हस्तदोष m. (-षः) A slip of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तधारण|हस्तधारणं
हस्तधारण n. (-णं) Warding off a blow, stopping, resisting, (in a conflict.)<BR>E. हस्त the hand, धारण restraining; also हस्तवारण ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तपुच्छ|हस्तपुच्छं
हस्तपुच्छ n. (-च्छं) The hand below the wrist.<BR> E. हस्त the hand, पुच्छ tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तपृष्ठ
हस्तपृष्ठ n. (-ष्ठं) The back of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तमणि|हस्तमणिः
हस्तमणि m. (-णिः) A jewel worn on the wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तलाघव
हस्तलाघव n. (-वं) Manual readiness, legerdemain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तवर्त्तिन्|हस्तवर्तिन्
हस्तवर्त्तिन् mfn. (-र्त्ती-र्त्तिनी-र्त्ति) In hand, seized, held, caught hold of. E.<BR>हस्त, वर्त्तिन् what abides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तवारण|हस्तवारणं
हस्तवारण n. (-णं) Resisting an assault, warding off a blow.<BR> E. हस्त, वारण prohibiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तविम्ब
हस्तविम्ब n. (-म्बं) Perfuming the person.<BR> E. हस्त the hand, विम्ब a red fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तसिद्धि|हस्तसिद्धिः
हस्तसिद्धि f. (-द्दिः)<BR>	 1. Manual labour.<BR>	 2. Hire, wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तसूत्र
हस्तसूत्र n. (-त्रं) A bracelet, worn on the wrist.<BR> E. हस the hand, सूत्र a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तस्थ
हस्तस्थ mfn. (-स्थः-स्था-स्थं) In hand, held.<BR> E. हस्त, स्थ what stays or is.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तस्थित
हस्तस्थित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Held, in hand.<BR> E. हस्त, and स्थित staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ताक्षर
हस्ताक्षर n. (-रं) Signature, hand-writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ताग्र
हस्ताग्र n. (-ग्रं) The fingers.<BR> E. हस्त, अग्र point, extremity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ताङ्कुलि
हस्ताङ्कुलि f. (-लिः) Any finger of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तामलक|हस्तामलकं
हस्तामलक n. (-कं)<BR>	 1. The fruit of the myrobalan held in the hand,<BR>(literally.)<BR>	 2. Any thing clearly seen or understood, (figuratively.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तावाप|हस्तावापः
हस्तावाप m. (-पः) A finger-guard used by archers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ताहस्ति
हस्ताहस्ति Ind. Hand to hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिक|हस्तिकं
हस्तिक n. (-कं) A multitude of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकक्ष्य|हस्तिकक्ष्यः
हस्तिकक्ष्य m. (-क्ष्यः)<BR>	 1. A lion.<BR>	 2. A tiger.<BR> E. हस्तिन्, कश् to hurt, स aff., यत् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकन्द|हस्तिकन्दः
हस्तिकन्द m. (-न्दः) A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकर्ण|हस्तिकर्णः
हस्तिकर्ण m. (-र्णः)<BR>	 1. The castor-oil tree.<BR>	 2. The Butea frondosa.<BR>	 3. A<BR>demi-god of a particular class.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant, कर्ण the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकर्णक|हस्तिकर्णकः
हस्तिकर्णक m. (-कः) A tree, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=830-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकर्णदल|हस्तिकर्णदलः
हस्तिकर्णदल m. (-लः) A sort of Kiṃśuka, (Butea frondosa.)<BR> E. हस्तिन् an<BR>elephant, कर्ण the ear, and दल a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकोलि|हस्तिकोलिः
हस्तिकोलि m. (-लिः) A sort of jujube.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant, कोलि jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिगिरि|हस्तिगिरिः
हस्तिगिरि m. (-रिः) The city KĀNCHI, a place of pilgrimage in the<BR>peninsula.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant, गिरि a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिघोषा
हस्तिघोषा f. (-षा) A kind of creeper.<BR> E. हस्तिन्, घोषा the generic name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिघ्न|हस्तिघ्नः
हस्तिघ्न m. (-घ्नः) A man.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant, घ्न who kills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिचारिन्
हस्तिचारिन् m. (-री) An elephant-driver.<BR> E. हस्तिन्, चारिन् who drives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिदन्त|हस्तिदंत|हस्तिदन्तं|हस्तिदन्तः
हस्तिदन्त m. (-न्तः)<BR>	 1. A pin or bracket projecting from a wall to hang<BR>any thing upon.<BR>	 2. The tusk of an elephant.<BR>	 mn. (-न्तः-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Ivory.<BR>2. A radish.<BR> E. हस्तिन्, दन्त a tooth; also with कन् added हस्तिदन्तक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिधयस
हस्तिधयस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) As big as an elephant, gigantic, elephantine.<BR>E. हस्तिन् an elephant, इयसच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिन्
हस्तिन् m. (-स्ती) An elephant, (four kinds of elephants are enumerated,<BR>viz:--भद्र, मन्द, मृग and मिश्र.)<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A female elephant.<BR>	 2. A<BR>female; one of the four kinds into which they are classed,<BR>and described as of low stature, corpulent habits, curly hair,<BR>dark complexion, libidinous appetite, thick lips, thick hips, thick<BR>fingers, large breasts and furious passions.<BR>	 3. A drug and<BR>perfume; also हट्टविलासिनी.<BR>	 f. (-नी) Adj.<BR>	 1. Having hands.<BR>	 2.<BR>Having a trunk.<BR> E. हस्त a trunk, and इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनख|हस्तिनखः
हस्तिनख n. (-खं) A sort of covered way, a raised place of earth or<BR>masonry, covering the access to the gate of a city or fort.<BR> E. हस्तिन्<BR>an elephant, and नख nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ति
हस्ति (न) नापुर n. (-रं) Ancient Delhi, the capital of YUDHIṢṬHIRA and<BR>his brethren, the city founded by king HASTINA, the remains of<BR>which still exist, about 57 miles north-east of the modern city,<BR>on the banks of the old channel of the Ganges.<BR> E. हस्तिन् the<BR>name of a king, (its founder,) and पुर city; also हस्तिनीपुर, गजाह्वय,<BR>नामसाह्वय, नागाह्व, हास्तिन, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिप|हस्तिपः
हस्तिप m. (-पः) An elephant-driver, or keeper.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant,<BR>पाल् to cherish, or rear, aff. क; also with कन्, हस्तिपक m. (-कः ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिपर्णी
हस्तिपर्णी f. (-र्णी)<BR>	 1. A plant, commonly MORATĀ.<BR>	 2. A sort of gourd,<BR>(Momordica mixta.)<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant, पर्ण a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिमद|हस्तिमदः
हस्तिमद m. (-दः) The juice that exudes from an elephant's temples<BR>when in rut.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant, and मद the frontal juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिमल्ल|हस्तिमल्लः
हस्तिमल्ल m. (-ल्लः)<BR>	 1. GĀṆRŚA.<BR>	 2. ŚANKHA, the eighth of the chief<BR>Nāgas or serpents of the infernal regions.<BR>	 3. AIRĀVATA, the<BR>elephant of INDRA.<BR>	 4. A heap of ashes.<BR>	 5. A shower of dust.<BR>	 6.<BR>Frost, cold.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant, and मल्ल a wrestler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तियूथ|हस्तियूथः
हस्तियूथ mn. (-थः-र्थं) A herd of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिवर्चस्
हस्तिवर्चस् n. (-र्चः) The magnificence of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिवाह|हस्तिवाहः
हस्तिवाह m. (-हः)<BR>	 1. A goad.<BR>	 2. An elephant-driver.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an<BR>elephant, वाह what bears, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिशाला
हस्तिशाला f. (-ला) A stall for elephants.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant, शाला a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिसुण्डा
हस्तिसुण्डा f. (-ण्डा or -ण्डी)<BR>	 1. An elephant's trunk.<BR>	 2. A flower,<BR>(Heliotropium Indicum.)<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant, शुण्डा the trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिस्यान
हस्तिस्यान n. (-नं) The bathing of an elephant; it is figuratively used to<BR>indicate any useless occupation, from the elephant's throwing<BR>dirt over his body in the very act of bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिहस्त|हस्तिहस्तः
हस्तिहस्त m. (-स्तः) An elephant's trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तेकरण|हस्तेकरणं
हस्तेकरण n. (-णं) Marriage.<BR> E. हस्त the hand, in the seventh case, करण making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्य
हस्य mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं)<BR>	 1. Given with the hand.<BR>	 2. Done with the hand,<BR>manual.<BR> E. हस्त the hand, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्यायुर्वेद|हस्त्यायुर्वेदः|हस्त्यायुर्व्वेदः
हस्त्यायुर्वेद m. (-दः) A work treating of the diseases of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्याराह
हस्त्याराह m. (-हः) An elephant-rider or driver.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant,<BR>आरोह who mounts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्र|हस्रः
हस्र mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं) Stupid, ignorant.<BR> E. हम् to laugh at, or deride, रक् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहल|हहलं
हहल n. (-लं) A sort of deadly poison; also हाहल and हाहाल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहा
हहा m. (-हा) A Gandharba or chorister of heaven; also हाहा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा r. 3rd cl. (ओ, क) ओहाक् (जहाति) 1. To quit, to leave, to abandon.<BR>2. To wander or deviate.<BR>	 3. To let fall.<BR>	 4. To resign.<BR>	 5. To<BR>neglect. With परि, 1. To relinquish.<BR>	 2. To omit, to neglect. With प्र,<BR>1. To give up.<BR>	 2. To let go. With अप, To abandon. With वि, To<BR>give up. (ओ, ङ) ओहाङ् (जिहीते) 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To attain.<BR>With उद्, 1. To go up, to rise.<BR>	 2. To revive, to come to life.<BR>	 3.<BR>To spring up.<BR>	 4. To rise, (as the sun or moon.)<BR>	 5. To depart.<BR>	 6.<BR>To raise. With उप, To come down. With सम्, To attain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा Ind.<BR>	 1. An interjection of pain, weariness, “ah,” “alas.” 2. Of<BR>sorrow.<BR>	 3. An exclamation of pleasure or surprise, “oh” “ha.” 4.<BR>A term of anger or reproach. In the sense of “woe be to” हा is<BR>used with the accusative of the object of reproach.<BR> E. हा to<BR>abandon, aff. का ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाङ्गर|हांगर|हांगरः|हाङ्गरः
हाङ्गर m. (-रः) A shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटक|हाटकं
हाटक mfn. (-कः-का or -की-कं) Golden, of gold, (as a weight or coin.)<BR>	 n.<BR>(-कं) Gold.<BR> E. हट् to shine, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटकगिरि|हाटकगिरिः
हाटकगिरि m. (-रिः) An epithet of mount MERU.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटकमय|हाटकमयं
हाटकमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of gold, golden.<BR> E. हाटक gold, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हातव्य|हातव्यं
हातव्य mfn. (-व्यः-व्या-व्यं) To be abandoned.<BR> E. हा to abandon, तव्यर् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हात्न
हात्न n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. Wages, hire.<BR>	 2. Death.<BR> E. हन् to hurt, ष्ट्रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान|हानं
हान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The act of abandoning or relinquishing.<BR>	 2. Prowess,<BR>valour.<BR> E. हा to leave, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानि|हानिः
हानि f. (-निः)<BR>	 1. Loss.<BR>	 2. Abandonment.<BR>	 3. Deficiency, decrease.<BR>	 4.<BR>Neglect.<BR> E. हा to leave, Unādi aff. नि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानुक|हानुकः
हानुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Mischievous, hurting, killing.<BR> E. हन् to hurt or kill, उकञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान्द्र|हान्द्रं
हान्द्र n. (-न्द्रं) Death, dying.<BR> E. हन् to kill, ष्ट्रन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापुत्रिका
हापुत्रिका f. (-का) A bird, (a wagtail.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापुत्री
हापुत्री f. (-त्री) A wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाफिका
हाफिका f. (-का) Gaping, yawning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायन|हायनं|हायनः
हायन mn. (-नः-नं) A year.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. A flame, a ray.<BR>	 2. A sort of<BR>rice.<BR> E. हा to go or like, ल्युट् aff., युक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार|हारं|हारः
हार mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Who or what takes, &c.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A porter, a<BR>carrier.<BR>	 2. Taking, conveying.<BR>	 3. Abstraction, deprivation.<BR>	 4. A<BR>necklace, a string of pearls, &c.<BR>	 5. War, battle.<BR>	 6. (In prosody,)<BR>A long syllable.<BR>	 7. (In Arithmetic,) A divisor, also the<BR>denominator of a fraction.<BR> E. हृ to seize, (the mind, &c.,) and घञ्<BR>aff., or causal form, with अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारक|हारकः
हारक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A theif.<BR>	 2. A rogue.<BR>	 3. Science.<BR>	 4. A gambler.<BR>	 5. A<BR>tree, (Trophis aspera.)<BR>	 6. A plunderer, a ravisher, one who carries<BR>off any thing.<BR>	 7. A kind of prose composition.<BR>	 8. A string of<BR>pearls.<BR>	 9. (In Arithmetic,) A divisor.<BR> E. हृ to take, aff. ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारगुटिका
हारगुटिका f. (-का) The bead of a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारयष्टि|हारयष्टिः
हारयष्टि f. (-ष्टिः) A necklace.<BR> E. हार, यष्टि a staff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारहूर|हारहूरः
हारहूर n. (-रं) Vinous liquor.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. Wine.<BR>	 2. A kind of grape;<BR>also हारहारा in the last sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारावली
हारावली f. (-ली) A string of pearls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारि|हारिः
हारि mfn. (-रिः-रिः or -री-रि) Handsome, charming.<BR>	 f. (-रिः)<BR>	 1. Defeat,<BR>discomfiture, either in war or gambling, &c.<BR>	 2. A traveller's<BR>progeny or family.<BR>	 3. A caravan.<BR>	 f. (-री) A pearl.<BR> E. हृ to take or<BR>steal, causal v., aff. इन्; ङीष् added optionally in the fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिकण्ठ|हारिकंठ|हारिकण्ठः
हारिकण्ठ mfn. (-ण्ठः-ण्ठी-ण्ठं) Wearing or having a necklace.<BR>	 m. (-ण्ठः)<BR>The Kokila.<BR> E. हारि for हार a necklace, कण्ठ the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिण
हारिण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Relating to deer, (flesh, skin, &c.)<BR> E. हरिण, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिणिक|हारिणिकः
हारिणिक m. (-कः) A hunter, a deer-killer.<BR>	 f. (-की) A species of the<BR>Atyashti metre.<BR> E. हरिण a deer, ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारित|हारितः
हारित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Lost, relinquished, made way with.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The<BR>green or wood pigeon.<BR>	 2. Green, (the colour.)<BR> E. हृ to take, causal<BR>v., क्त aff.; or हरित् green, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारितक|हारितकं|हारितकः
हारितक n. (-कं) A potherb.<BR> E. हरित the same, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिद्र|हारिद्रः
हारिद्र mfn. (-द्रः-द्रा-द्रं)<BR>	 1. Stained, dyed or coloured with turmeric.<BR>	 2.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">Page832-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Yellow.<BR>	 m. (-द्रः)<BR>	 1. The Kadamba tree, (Nauclea Kadamba.)<BR>	 2.<BR>Yellow, (the colour.)<BR> E. हरिद्रा turmeric, and अण् or अञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=831-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिन्
हारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि)<BR>	 1. Taking, getting, who takes or gets.<BR>	 2.<BR>Disturbing, seizing.<BR>	 3. Having a necklace.<BR>	 4. Pleasant, agreeable.<BR>E. हृ to take, aff. इनि or णिनि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारीत|हारीतः
हारीत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The green or wood pigeon, (Columba hariala, BUCH.)<BR>2. A Muni and legislator.<BR>	 3. A rogue, a cheat.<BR> E. हार a necklace,<BR>or हारि defeat, and इत gone, got; or हरित green, अण् aff., and<BR>the vowel made long; or हृ-णिच् वा० ईतच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्द्द|हार्द|हार्दं|हार्द्दं
हार्द्द n. (-र्द्दं)<BR>	 1. Affection, love.<BR>	 2. Kindness.<BR>	 3. Intention, meaning. E.<BR>हृद् the heart, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्य्य|हार्य|हार्यः|हार्य्यः
हार्य्य mfn. (-र्य्यः-र्य्या-र्य्यं)<BR>	 1. To be taken, to be taken away.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>shaken, to be unsettled.<BR>	 3. To be attracted, to be influenced.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-र्य्यः)<BR>	 1. Beleric myrobalan.<BR>	 2. A serpent.<BR>	 3. The dividend, (in<BR>math.)<BR> E. हृ to take, aff. ण्यत् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाल|हालः
हाल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. BALARĀMA.<BR>	 2. A name of SĀLIVĀHANA.<BR>	 3. A plough.<BR>f. (-ला) Spirituous liquor.<BR>	 f. (-ली) A wife's younger sister.<BR> E. हाल a<BR>plough, aff. अण्; or हल् to plough, aff. घञ्. In fem. हल्-इण्-ङीष् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालक|हालकः
हालक m. (-कः) A horse of a yellowish-brown, or tawny colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालहल|हालहलं
हालहल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A sort of deadly poison.<BR>	 2. A poison in general:<BR>see the next.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालहाल|हालहालं
हालहाल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A sort of deadly poison.<BR>	 2. A poison in general;<BR>also variously read, हलाहल, हलहल, हालहल, हालाहल हाहाल, and हाहल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाह|हालाहः
हालाह m. (-हः) A piebald horse; also read हलाह ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहल|हालाहलं|हालाहलः
हालाहल n. (-लं)<BR>	 1. A sort of deadly poison produced at the churning<BR>of the ocean and quaffed by ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A poison in general.<BR>	 f. (-ला)<BR>A small mouse.<BR>	 f. (-ली) Wine, spirituous liquor.<BR>	 m. (-लः) A sort<BR>of worm or insect, a kind of newt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहलधर|हालाहलधरः
हालाहलधर m. (-रः) A small black and venomous snake.<BR> E. हालाहल poison, धर having.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिक|हालिकः
हालिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Belonging or relating to a plough, as a<BR>ploughman, cattle, &c.<BR> E. हल a plough, ठञ् or ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिनी
हालिनी f. (-नी) A sort of large lizard.<BR> E. हल-णिनि aff., ङीष् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालु|हालुः
हालु m. (-लुः) A tooth.<BR> E. हल् to plough, उण् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाव|हावः
हाव m. (-वः)<BR>	 1. Any feminine act of amorous pastime, or tending to<BR>excite amorous sensations, coquetry, blandishment, dalliance.<BR>	 2.<BR>Calling.<BR> E. ह्वेञ् to call, (to incite passion,) aff. घञ्; or हु, घञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास|हासः
हास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Laughing, laughter.<BR>	 2. Joy, merriment.<BR>	 3. One of the<BR>eight sentiments in poetry.<BR>	 4. Derision.<BR>	 5. Blowing, opening. E.<BR>हस् to laugh, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासक|हासकः
हासक m. (-कः) A buffoon.<BR> E. हस to laugh, causal v., वन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासकर
हासकर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Laughing, laughing at.<BR>	 2. Causing laughter,<BR>merry, ridiculous.<BR> E. हास, कर what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासस्
हासस् m. (-साः) The moon, (in the language of the Vedas.)<BR> E. हस् to<BR>laugh, causal verb, असुन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासिका
हासिका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Laughter.<BR>	 2. Mirth.<BR> E. हस् to laugh, ण्वुल् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासिन्
हासिन् mfn. (-सी-सिनी-सि) Laughing, smiling.<BR> E. हस् to laugh, घिनुण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिक|हास्तिकं|हास्तिकः
हास्तिक n. (-कं) A herd of elephants.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A rider on an elephant,<BR>an elephant-driver, &c.<BR> E. हस्तिन् an elephant, वुण् or ठक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिन|हास्तिनं
हास्तिन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Elephantine, large, as big as an elephant, &c.<BR>n. (-नं) Hastināpur, or ancient DELHI.<BR> E. हस्तिन् a sovereign, (founder<BR>of the city,) or an elephant, अण् aff. or derivation or abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिनपुर|हास्तिनपुरं
हास्तिनपुर n. (-रं) HASTINĀPUR.<BR> E. हास्तिन, पुर a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्य|हास्यं|हास्यः
हास्य mfn. (-स्यः-स्या-स्यं) Laughable, ridiculous.<BR>	 n. (-स्यं)<BR>	 1. Laughter.<BR>laughing, mirth.<BR>	 2. Ridicule, derision.<BR> E. हस् to laugh, ण्यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यपदवी
हास्यपदवी f. (-वी) Ridicule, laughter, (used with या, गम, &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यरस|हास्यरसः
हास्यरस m. (-सः) The sentiment of humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्यास्पद
ह्यस्यास्पद n. (-दं) A laughing-stock.<BR> E. हास्य, आस्पद an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहल|हाहलं
हाहल n. (-लं) A sort of deadly poison: also हाहाल, &c.: see हलाहल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहस्
हाहस् m. (-हाः) A Gandharba. E. see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहा
हाहा m. (-हाः) A Gandharba, a demi-god of an inferior order, atten-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">Page832-b+ 60</a>]<BR>dant on KUVERA and the other gods, and especially the chanter<BR>of their praises. Ind. An interjection of surprise, grief, or pain.<BR>E. हा alas, interjection of sorrow, हा to abandon, क्विप् aff.; or हा<BR>interjection repeated; also with असि or असुन् aff., हाहस् m. (-हाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहाकार|हाहाकारः
हाहाकार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The noise or uproar of battle 2. A great lamenta-<BR>tion or wailing, sound of grief or pity.<BR> E. हाहा interjection of<BR>pain, कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहाल|हाहालं
हाहाल n. (-लं) A sort of deadly poison; also हाहल, &c.: see हलाहल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
हि r. 5th cl. (हिनीति)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To send.<BR>	 3. To grow or increase.<BR>	 4.<BR>To be in pain.<BR>	 5. To Throw.<BR>	 6. To excite, to urge.<BR>	 7. To promote,<BR>to further.<BR>	 8. To please, to gratify. With प्र, 1. To discharge, to<BR>throw.<BR>	 2. To send forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
हि Ind. A particle expressing:--1. Because, for, on account of.<BR>	 2.<BR>Assuredly, certainly, (assertion.).<BR>	 3. Indeed, surely, (interrogation.)<BR>4. For instance.<BR>	 5. Only, alone.<BR>	 6. A particle, implying difference<BR>or distinction.<BR>	 7. An expletive.<BR>	 8. Ah, alas.<BR>	 9. An interjection of<BR>envy or contempt.<BR>	 10. An interjection of hurry.<BR> E. हि to go, विच्<BR>aff; or हा to abandon, or हि to go, डि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसक|हिंसकः
हिंसक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Mischievous, malignant, ferocious, savage.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-कः)<BR>	 1. A beast of prey.<BR>	 2. An enemy.<BR>	 3. A Brāhman, who has<BR>studied the Atharva-Veda.<BR> E. हिसि to injure, वुञ् aff.; or हिन्स्-ण्वुल् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसन|हिंसनं
हिंसन n. (-नं) Injuring, hurting, killing.<BR> E. हिसि to hurt, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसा
हिंसा f. (-सा)<BR>	 1. Injury, mischief, hurt, harm, &c.; it is usually<BR>distinguished as of three sorts,:--mental, (as malice,) verbal, (as<BR>abuse,) personal, (as striking, wounding, &c.)<BR>	 2. Slaughter, killing,<BR>slaying.<BR>	 3. Robbery.<BR> E. हिस्रि to hurt or kill, affs. अङ् and टाप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसाकर्म्मन्|हिंसाकर्मन्
हिंसाकर्म्मन् n. (-र्म्म)<BR>	 1. Incantation to destroy, or the practice of magic,<BR>or employment of mystical texts for malevolent and injurious pur-<BR>poses.<BR>	 3. Any mischievous act.<BR> E. हिंसा injury, कर्म्मन् act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसात्मक
हिंसात्मक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Injurious.<BR> E. हिंसा, आत्मक self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसारु|हिंसारुः
हिंसारु m. (-रुः) A tiger.<BR> E. हिंसा injury, ऋ to go, or affect, aff. उण्; or हिन्स् आरु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसालु|हिंसालुः
हिंसालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु)<BR>	 1. Mischievous, hurtful.<BR>	 2. Murderous.<BR>	 m. (-लुः)<BR>A savage dog.<BR> E. हिंसा injury, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसालुक|हिंसालुकः
हिंसालुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Mischievous, hurtful.<BR>	 m. (-कः) A<BR>mischievous or savage dog.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसीर|हिंसीरः
हिंसीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A tiger.<BR>	 2. A wretch, a villain.<BR>	 3. A bird.<BR> E. हिसि to<BR>hurt or kill, Unādi aff. ईरन् or ईरच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्य
हिंस्य f. (-स्या) Adj. Liable to be hurt or killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्र|हिंस्रः
हिंस्र mfn. (-स्रः-स्रा-स्रं)<BR>	 1. Mischievous, hurtful, injurious.<BR>	 2. Murderous.<BR>3. Terrible.<BR>	 4. Fierce, cruel, savage.<BR>	 m. (-स्रः)<BR>	 1. BHIMA.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR>	 3.<BR>A beast of prey.<BR>	 4. A destroyer.<BR>	 f. (-स्रा)<BR>	 1. Spikenard, (Valeriana<BR>Jatāmansi.)<BR>	 2. A vein, a nerve.<BR> E. हिसि to hurt, Unādi aff. रक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रक|हिंस्रकः
हिंस्रक m. (-कः) A beast of prey.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रपशु|हिंस्रपशुः
हिंस्रपशु m. (-शुः) A beast of prey.<BR> E. हिंस्र, mischievous, पशु an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रयन्त्र|हिंस्रयंत्र
हिंस्रयन्त्र n. (-न्त्रं)<BR>	 1. A trap.<BR>	 2. A mystical text used for injurious<BR>purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिक्क्
हिक्क् r. 1st cl. (हिक्कति-ते)<BR>	 1. To sound inarticulately.<BR>	 2. To hiccough.<BR>r. 10th cl. (हिक्कयते) To hurt or injure, to kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिक्का
हिक्का f. (-क्का)<BR>	 1. Hiccough.<BR>	 2. An indistinct sound.<BR> E. हिक्क् to hic-<BR>cough, affs. अङ् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्कार|हिंकार|हिंकारः|हिङ्कारः
हिङ्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. A tiger.<BR>	 2. A kind of low roar.<BR> E. हिं imitative sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गु|हिंगु
हिङ्गु mn. (-ङ्गुः-ङ्गु) Asafœtida, (the gum and plant respectively.)<BR> E. हि<BR>to go, deriv. irr., or हिम frost, गम् to go, डु aff., form irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुनिर्य्यास|हिङ्गुनिर्यास|हिंगुनिर्यास|हिङ्गुनिर्यासः
हिङ्गुनिर्य्यास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. The Nimba tree.<BR>	 2. Asafœtida, (the gum.) E.<BR>हिङ्गु asafœtida, and निर्य्यास exudation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुपत्र|हिंगुपत्त्र|हिङ्गुपत्रः
हिङ्गुपत्र m. (-त्रः) The Ingudi plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुपर्णी
हिङ्गुपर्णी f. (-र्णी) A plant, commonly Bansa-patri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुल|हिंगुल|हिंगुलं|हिंगुलः|हिङ्गुलः
हिङ्गुल mn. (-लः-लं) Vermilion.<BR>	 f. (-ली) The egg-plant, (Solanum melon-<BR>gena.)<BR> E. हिङ्गु asafœtida, ला to take or give, aff. क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुलि|हिंगुलि|हिंगुलिः|हिङ्गुलिः
हिङ्गुलि m. (-लिः) Vermilion.<BR> E. हिङ्गु asafœtida. -ला to take or give. aff. कि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=832-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुलिका|हिंगुलिका
हिङ्गुलिका f. (-का) A prickly night-shade, (Solanum Jacquini.)<BR> E. हिङ्गुली<BR>the egg-plant, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुलु|हिंगुलु|हिङ्गुलुः
हिङ्गुलु mn. (-लुः-लु) Vermilion.<BR> E. हिङ्गु asafœtida, ला to give or take, aff. डु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गुशि
हिङ्गुशि(सि)फा(रा)टिका f. (-का) A plant, commonly Bansa-patrī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिङ्गूल|हिङ्गूलं
हिङ्गूल n. (-लं) An esculent root, a sort of yam. “आलु” ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिज्ज|हिज्जः
हिज्ज m. (-ज्जः) A plant, (Barringtonia acutangula:) see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिज्जल|हिज्जलः
हिज्जल m. (-लः) A plant, commonly Hijjal, (Barringtonia acutangula.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिञ्जीर|हिंजीर|हिंजीरः|हिञ्जीरः
हिञ्जीर m. (-रः) A rope or chain for fastening an elephant's foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिड्
हिड् (इ) हिडि r. 1st cl. (हिण्डते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To wander.<BR>	 3.<BR>To disregard or disrespect. With आ, To wander about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडि
हिडि (ड) म्ब m. (-म्बः) A prince of the Rākshasas slain by BHĪMA.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-म्बा) The sister of HIḌIMBA carried off by BHĪMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिम्बजित्|हिडिंबजित्
हिडिम्बजित् m. (-जित्) BHĪMA, the second of the PĀNDUS.<BR> E. हिडिम्ब a<BR>Rākshasa, and जित् conqueror; also similar compounds, as<BR>हिडिम्बनिसूदनः, हिडिम्बभिद्, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिम्बभिद्|हिडिंबभिद्
हिडिम्बभिद् m. (-भित् or भिद् BHĪMA: see the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिम्बापति|हिडिम्बापतिः
हिडिम्बापति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. HANUMĀNA.<BR>	 2. BHĪMA.<BR> E. हिडिम्बा a female<BR>Rākshasa, पति husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिम्बारमण|हिडिम्बारमणः
हिडिम्बारमण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. HANUMĀNA, the monkey friend and ally of<BR>RĀMA.<BR>	 2. BHĪMA.<BR> E. हिडिम्बा a female Rākshasa, रमण husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डन|हिंडन|हिंडनं|हिण्डनं
हिण्डन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Wandering, roaming.<BR>	 2. Copulation.<BR>	 3. Writing. E.<BR>हिडि to go, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डिक|हिंडिकः|हिण्डिकः
हिण्डिक m. (-कः) An astrologer.<BR> E. हिडि to go, aff. अच्, and ठक् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डिर|हिंडिर|हिंडिरः|हिण्डिरः
हिण्डिर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Cuttle-fish-bone.<BR>	 2. A male.<BR>	 3. The egg-plant.<BR>	 4.<BR>A tonic.<BR> E. हिडि to go, or despise, aff. इरन्; also with ईरन्, हिण्डीर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डी|हिंडी
हिण्डी f. (-ण्डी) A name of DURGĀ.<BR> E. हिडि to go or despise, (the<BR>Asuras,) इन् aff., and ङीप् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डीप्रियतम|हिण्डीप्रियतमः
हिण्डीप्रियतम m. (-मः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. हिण्डी DURGĀ, and प्रियतम dearest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिण्डीर|हिंडीर|हिंडीरः|हिण्डीरः
हिण्डीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Cuttle-fish-bone, considered to be the indurated<BR>foam of the sea.<BR>	 2. A man, a male.<BR>	 3. The egg-plant, (Solanum<BR>melongena.)<BR>	 4. A tonic or stomachic.<BR> E. हिडि to go, or despise,<BR>aff. ईरन्; also with इरन्, हिण्डिर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित|हितं|हितः
हित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Suitable, proper, fit, worthy, right, (generally<BR>with a dative.)<BR>	 2. Gone, proceeded.<BR>	 3. Held, taken, seized.<BR>	 4. Put,<BR>placed.<BR>	 5. Advantageous, profitable, salutary, wholesome.<BR>	 6. (In<BR>medicine,) Proper, as diet or menstrua, suitable to the case or<BR>the medicines taken.<BR>	 7. Friendly, affectionate, kind to, (often with<BR>a locative.)<BR>	 8. Useful.<BR>	 m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. A good, a benefit.<BR>	 2. A<BR>benefactor, an adviser.<BR>	 n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. An advantage.<BR>	 2. Anything<BR>proper or suitable.<BR>	 f. (-ता) A causeway, a dike.<BR> E. धा to have or<BR>hold, क्त aff; or हि to go, &c., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितक|हितकः
हितक m. (-कः) A child.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकर|हितकरः
हितकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Friendly, kind, favourable.<BR>	 m. (-रः) A bene-<BR>factor.<BR> E. हित, कर who makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकाम
हितकाम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Wishing well to, kind or friendly to.<BR> E. हित, काम desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकाम्या
हितकाम्या f. (-म्या) Desire for another's welfare.<BR> E. हित, काम्या desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितप्रणी
हितप्रणी m. (-णीः) A spy, a secret emissary.<BR> E. हित, प्रणी who instructs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितप्रेप्सु
हितप्रेप्सु mfn. (-प्सुः-प्सुः-प्सु) Benevolent, benign.<BR> E. हित, प्रेप्सु wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितबुद्धि
हितबुद्धि mfn. (-द्धिः-द्धिः-द्धि) Well-disposed to, wishing well to.<BR> E. हित<BR>and बुद्धि understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितवत्|हितवन्त्
हितवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Friendly, favourable, doing good to.<BR> E. हित, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितवाक्य
हितवाक्य n. (-क्यं) Friendly advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितवादिन्
हितवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Giving good counsel, directing or advising<BR>what is right.<BR>	 m. (-दी) A director, an adviser, a friendly coun-<BR>sellor.<BR> E. हित proper, वादिन् speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितानुकारिन्
हितानुकारिन् mfn. (-री-रिणी-रि) Kind.<BR> E. हित, अनुकारिन् who acts conformably to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित्रान्वेषिन्
हित्रान्वेषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Seeking another's welfare.<BR> E. हित, अन्वेषिन्<BR>who seeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिताहित
हिताहित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Good and evil, beneficial and disadvantageous.<BR> E. हित, अहित bad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितेच्छा
हितेच्छा f. (-च्छा) Good wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितैषिन्
हितैषिन् mfn. (-षी-षिणी-षि) Wishing well to.<BR> E. हित, एषिन् who desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितोक्ति|हितोक्तिः
हितोक्ति f. (-क्तिः)<BR>	 1. Compassion, clemency. tenderness.<BR>	 2. Good or<BR>friendly advice.<BR> E. हित kind, उक्ति speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितोपदेश|हितोपदेशः
हितोपदेश m. (-शः) Friendly or proper advice.<BR> E. हित proper, उपदेश advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित्वा
हित्वा Ind. Having left or abandoned.<BR> E. हा to leave, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्ताल|हिंताल|हिंतालः|हिन्तालः
हिन्ताल m. (-लः) The marshy-date tree, (Phœnix or Elate paludosa.) E.<BR>हीन defective, i. e. small, ताल the palm, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दु|हिंदुः|हिन्दुः
हिन्दु m. (-न्दुः) A particular caste, the Hindus. Prof. TĀRĀNĀTH thus<BR>defines this word in his Vāchaspatya:--हीनं दूषयति-दुष + डु पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोल|हिंदोल|हिंदोलः|हिन्दोलः
हिन्दोल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A swing.<BR>	 2. The swing-festival held in the light-<BR>half of the month ŚRĀVAṆA.<BR>	 3. One of the Rāgas or personified<BR>musical modes.<BR>	 f. (-ला) A swing.<BR> E. हि particle, दुल् to shake,<BR>घञ् aff., deriv. irr.; also with कन्, हिन्दोलक m. (-कः ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिम|हिमं|हिमः
हिम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं) Cold, frigid.<BR>	 n. (-म)<BR>	 1. Frost, hoar-frost.<BR>	 2. Ice,<BR>snow.<BR>	 3. Cold.<BR>	 4. Sandal.<BR>	 5. Fresh butter.<BR>	 6. Tin.<BR>	 7. A pearl.<BR>	 8. A<BR>lotus.<BR>	 m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. The Sandal tree.<BR>	 2. The moon.<BR>	 3. Camphor.<BR>	 4.<BR>The Himālaya mountain.<BR>	 5. Winter.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. Small carda-<BR>moms.<BR>	 2. RENŪKĀ, a perfume.<BR>	 3. A fragrant grass, (Cyperus.) E.<BR>हन् to hurt, मक् Unādi aff., and हि substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमकर|हिमकरः
हिमकर mfn. (-रः-री-रं) Frigorific, cold.<BR>	 m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2.<BR>Camphor.<BR> E. हिम cold, and कर who makes, or a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमकूट|हिमकूटः
हिमकूट m. (-टः)<BR>	 1. The wintry season.<BR>	 2. The Himālaya mountain. E.<BR>हिम frost or cold, and कूट a quantity, or a summit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमगु|हिमगुः
हिमगु m. (-गुः) The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमज|हिमजः
हिमज mfn. (-जः-जा-जं) Produced by cold, in the Himālaya, &c.<BR>	 m.<BR>(-जः)<BR>	 1. The mountain MAINĀKA.<BR>	 f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. PĀRVATĪ.<BR>	 2. Zedoary-<BR>E. हिम the Himālaya personified, ज born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमज्झटि|हिमज्झटिः
हिमज्झटि f. (-टिः) Mist, dew, fog.<BR> E. हिम cold, झट् to be entangled, इन् aff.; also हिमझण्टि ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमतैल|हिमतैलं
हिमतैल n. (-लं) A kind of camphor-ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमदीधिति|हिमदीधितिः
हिमदीधिति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमदुर्द्दिन|हिमदुर्दिन|हिमदुर्दिनं
हिमदुर्द्दिन n. (-नं) Cold and bad weather.<BR> E. हिम cold, दुर्द्दिन bad weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमद्युति|हिमद्युतिः
हिमद्युति m. (-तिः) The moon.<BR> E. हिम cold, cooling, and द्युति radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमद्रुम|हिमद्रुमः
हिमद्रुम m. (-मः) The Nimba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमद्रुह
हिमद्रुह m. (-ध्रुक्-ग्-ट्-ड्) The sun.<BR> E. हिम frost, द्रुह् to hurt, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमप्रस्थ|हिमप्रस्थः
हिमप्रस्थ m. (-स्थः) The Himālaya mountain.<BR> E. हिम cold, प्रस्थ abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमबालुक
हिमबालुक mf. (-कः-का) Camphor.<BR> E. हिम cold, and बालुका sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमभास्
हिमभास् m. (-भाः) The moon.<BR> E. हिम, भास् to shine, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमवत्|हिमवन्त्
हिमवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Cold, freezing, chilly, frosty.<BR>	 m. (-वान्) The<BR>Himālaya range.<BR> E. हिम cold, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमवत्कुक्षि|हिमवत्कुक्षिः
हिमवत्कुक्षि m. (-क्षिः) A valley of the Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमवत्पुर
हिमवत्पुर n. (-रं) Oshadhiprastha, the capital of Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमवत्सुत|हिमवत्सुतः
हिमवत्सुत m. (-तः)<BR>	 1. The mountain Maināka.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1. The Ganges.<BR>2. PĀRVATĪ.<BR> E. हिमवत् the Himālaya, and सुत son, or सुता daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमशीतल
हिमशीतल mfn. (-लः-ला-लं) Very cold, frosty, freezing.<BR> E. हिम, शीतल cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमशैलजा
हिमशैलजा f. (-जा)<BR>	 1. The goddess DURGĀ or PĀRVATĪ.<BR>	 2. The Ganges.<BR>E. हिमशैल the Himālaya mountain and जा daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमश्रथ|हिमश्रथः
हिमश्रथ m. (-थः) The moon.<BR> E. हिम, and श्रथि to shed, अच aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमसंहति|हिमसंहतिः
हिमसंहति f. (-तिः) Ice and snow.<BR> E. हिम cold, संहति assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमसरस्
हिमसरस् n. (-रः) Cold-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमहानकृत्
हिमहानकृत् m. (-कृत्) Fire.<BR> E. हिम, हान loss, कृत् what makes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमहासक|हिमहासकः
हिमहासक m. (-कः) The marshy-date tree.<BR> E. हिम cold, or winter, हासक<BR>smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमांशु|हिमांशुः
हिमांशु m. (-शुः)<BR>	 1. The moon.<BR>	 2. Camphor.<BR> E. हिम cold, अंशु a ray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमांश्वभिख्य|हिमांश्वभिख्यं
हिमांश्वभिख्य n. (-ख्यं) Silver.<BR> E. हिमांशु the moon, अभिख्या beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमागम|हिमागमः
हिमागम m. (-मः) The cold season “हेमन्ते”.<BR> E. हिम cold, आगम arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाद्रि|हिमाद्रिः
हिमाद्रि m. (-द्रिः) The snowy range of mountains, skirting the north of<BR>India, the Imaus or Emodus.<BR> E. हिम cold, and अद्रि a mountain;<BR>also similar compounds, as हिमाचल, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमानिल|हिमानिलः
हिमानिल m. (-लः) A frosty or cold wind.<BR> E. हिम, अनिल wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=833-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमानी
हिमानी f. (-नी) Ice and snow.<BR> E. हिम cold, ङीष् aff., and आनुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाब्ज|हिमाब्जं
हिमाब्ज n. (-ब्जं) A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाभ
हिमाभ mfn. (-भः-भा-भं) Like frost and snow.<BR> E. हिम, आभ resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाम्ब्
हिमाम्ब् n. (-म्ब) Dew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाम्भस्|हिमांभस्
हिमाम्भस् n. (-म्भः) Dew.<BR> E. हिम, अम्भस् water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाराति|हिमारातिः
हिमाराति m. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR> E. हिम cold, अराति the enemy;<BR>also similar compounds, as हिमारि, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमार्त्त|हिमार्त
हिमार्त्त mfn. (-र्त्तः-र्त्ता-र्त्तं) Chilly, cold, suffering from cold.<BR> E. हिम, आर्त्त pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमालय|हिमालयः
हिमालय m. (-य) The Himālaya range of mountains,<BR>which bounds India on the north, and separates it from Tartary;<BR>the Imaus and Emodus of the ancients, giving rise to the Ganges,<BR>and Indus, and many other considerable rivers, and containing<BR>the highest elevations in the world: in mythology, the mountain<BR>is personified as the husband of MENAKĀ, and the father of<BR>GANGĀ or the Ganges, and DURGĀ or UMĀ in her descent as<BR>PĀRVATĪ, the mountain nymph, to captivate ŚIVA, and withdraw<BR>him from a course of ascetic austerity practised in those regions.<BR>E. हिम cold, or frost and snow, and आलय abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमावती
हिमावती f. (-ती) A sort of moon-plant; also स्वर्णक्षीरी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाह्व|हिमाह्वः
हिमाह्व m. (-ह्वः) Camphor.<BR> E. हिम snow, आह्व appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाह्वय|हिमाह्वयः
हिमाह्वय m. (-यः) Camphor.<BR>	 n. (-यं) A lotus.<BR> E. हिम cold, आह्वय appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमिका
हिमिका f. (-का) Hoar-frost.<BR> E. हिम frost, कन् aff., fem. form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमेलु|हिमेलुः
हिमेलु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Suffering from cold, chilly, frozen.<BR> E. हिम cold, एलु aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिम्य|हिम्यः
हिम्य mfn. (-म्यः-म्या-म्यं) Frozen, snowy, cold, frigid.<BR> E. हिम frost and<BR>snow, and यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरङ्गु|हिरंगुः|हिरङ्गुः
हिरङ्गु m. (-ङ्गुः) The personified ascending node.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरणु
हिरणु n. (-णं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Semen.<BR>	 3. A cowrie: see हिरण्य ।<BR> E. हृ to take,<BR>ल्युट् aff., and इ substituted for the antepenultimate vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्मय|हिरण्मयं|हिरण्मयः
हिरण्मय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Made of gold, golden.<BR>	 m. (-यः) BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-यं) One of the Varṣas or divisions of the continent; the part<BR>between the mountainous ranges Śweta and Śringavān.<BR> E. हिरण्<BR>for हिरण gold, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्य|हिरण्यं
हिरण्य n. (-ण्य)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Either of the precious metals, crude bullion,<BR>unwrought gold or silver.<BR>	 3. Silver, crude or wrought.<BR>	 4. Any<BR>precious metal.<BR>	 5. A measure.<BR>	 6. A cowrie.<BR>	 7. Semen virile.<BR>	 8.<BR>Imperishable matter, that which is eternal.<BR>	 9. Thing, substance.<BR>10. Wealth, property.<BR>	 11. The Dhattūra plant.<BR> E. हृ to take,<BR>Unādi aff. कन्यन्, and किरच् substituted for the radical letters; or<BR>हिरण, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकशिपु|हिरण्यकशिपुः
हिरण्यकशिपु m. (-पुः) A Daitya, the father of PRAHLĀDA, for whose<BR>destruction, VIṢṆU, descended in the fourth or NARASINHA-<BR>Avatār.<BR> E. हिरण्य gold, and कशिपु clothing, or food and clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकशिपुहन्
हिरण्यकशिपुहन् m. (-हा) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. हिरण्यकशिपु a Daitya, हन् destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकोश|हिरण्यकोशः
हिरण्यकोश(ष) m. (-शः or -षः) Gold and silver, (wrought or unwrought.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यगर्भ|हिरण्यगर्भः
हिरण्यगर्भ m. (-र्भः)<BR>	 1. BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 2. VIṢṆU.<BR>	 3. The soul invested by the<BR>subtile body, “सूक्ष्मशरीर”.<BR> E. हिरण्य gold, गर्भ embryo; or the mundane<BR>egg floating on the water at creation, of that metal, or of similar<BR>colour, from which the deity issued, according to some legends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यद|हिरण्यदः
हिरण्यद m. (-दः) The ocean.<BR>	 f. (-दा) The earth. Adj. Giving or granting<BR>gold.<BR> E. हिरण्य gold, and द what gives of yields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यनाभ|हिरण्यनाभः
हिरण्यनाभ m. (-भः) The mountain Maināka.<BR> E. हिरण्य gold, नाभ navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यबाहु|हिरण्यबाहुः
हिरण्यबाहु m. (-हुः)<BR>	 1. The river Śona.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR> E. हिरण्य, बाहु an arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यय
हिरण्यय f. (-यी) Adj. Golden.<BR> E. हिरण्य, मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यरेतस्
हिरण्यरेतस् m. (-ताः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. The sun.<BR>	 3. ŚIVA.<BR>	 4. The Arka-plant. E.<BR>हिरण्य gold, and रेतस् semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यव|हिरण्यवः
हिरण्यव m. (-वः) A divine treasure.<BR> E. हिरण्य gold, व possessive aff. in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यवर्णा
हिरण्यवर्णा f. (-र्णा) A particular river.<BR> E. हिरण्य gold, and वर्ण colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यवाह|हिरण्यवाहः
हिरण्यवाह m. (-हः) The river Śona.<BR> E. हिरण्य gold, वह् to bear, aff. अण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्याक्ष|हिरण्याक्षः
हिरण्याक्ष m. (-क्षः) The name of a demon, killed by VIṢṆU.<BR> E. हिरण्य,<BR>and अक्ष for अक्षि the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरुक्
हिरुक् Ind.<BR>	 1. Without, except.<BR>	 2. In the midst of, amongst.<BR>	 3. Near.<BR>4. Vile.<BR> E. हि to go, रुकक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्
हिल् r. 6th cl. (हिलति) To express amorous inclination, to dally, to<BR>wanton, to sport amorously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिलमोचि|हिलमोचिः
हिलमोचि f. (-चिः-ची) A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.) “हेलेञ्चा” इति भाषा ।<BR>E. हिल sporting, मुच् to loosen, इन् aff., ङीप् optionally added; also<BR>with कन् added, fem. form, हिलमोचिका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्ल|हिल्लः
हिल्ल m. (-ल्लः) A kind of bird, (Turdus ginginianus.)<BR> E. हिल् to dally, लक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्लोल्
हिल्लोल् r. 10th cl. (हिल्लोलयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To wave.<BR>	 2. To swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्लोल|हिल्लोलः
हिल्लोल m. (-लः) A wave, a surge.<BR>	 2. Swinging.<BR>	 3. A particular mode<BR>of sexual enjoyment, thus described:--<BR>“हृदि कृत्वा स्त्रियः पादौ कराभ्यां धारयेत् करौ ।<BR>यथेष्टं ताडयेद् योनिं बन्धो हिल्लोलसंज्ञकः ॥”<BR> E. हिल्लोल्-अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्वला
हिल्वला f. Plu. (-लाः) Name of the five small stars in the head of the<BR>constellation “MRIGASIRAS.”<BR> E. इल्वला + पृषो० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिव्
हिव् (इ) हिवि r. 5th cl. (हिन्वति)<BR>	 1. To be satisfied.<BR>	 2. To satisfy or please.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिस्
हिस् (इ) हिसि r. 10th cl. (-हिंसयति-ते) r. 7th cl. (हिंनस्ति) To hurt, to<BR>injure, to do anything tending to the prejudice of another in<BR>word, thought, or deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिहि
हिहि Ind. An interjection of surprise or merriment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ही
ही Ind.<BR>	 1. An exclamation or interjection of surprise.<BR>	 2. Of fatigue or<BR>despondence.<BR>	 3. Of sorrow.<BR>	 4. A particle implying reason or cause,<BR>(therefore, so.)<BR> E. हन् to hurt, डी aff., हि substituted for the root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीन|हीनः
हीन mfn. (-नः-ना-नं)<BR>	 1. Deficient, defective.<BR>	 2. Blamable, mean, base,<BR>vile, bad.<BR>	 3. Left, abandoned, quitted.<BR>	 4. Wasted, worn, decayed.<BR>5. Void of, free from.<BR>	 6. Lower, less.<BR>	 m. (-नः) An insufficient or<BR>objectionable witness.<BR> E. हा to quit, aff. क्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनकर्म्मन्|हीनकर्मन्
हीनकर्म्मन् mfn. (-र्म्मा-र्म्मा-र्म्म) Neglecting, or not performing the custo-<BR>mary rites, &c.<BR> E. हीन, कर्म्मन act; also हीनक्रिय, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनजाति|हीनजातिः
हीनजाति mfn. (-तिः-तिः-ति) Outcaste, vile, degraded.<BR> E. हीन abandoned, जाति caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवर्ण|हीनवर्णः
हीनवर्ण mfn. (-र्णः-र्णा-र्णं) Of a low caste, outcaste, vile.<BR> E. हीन, वर्ण caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवाद|हीनवादः
हीनवाद m. (-दः) Prevarication, contradictory evidence.<BR> E. हीन, वाद speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवादिन्
हीनवादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि)<BR>	 1. Dumb, speechless.<BR>	 2. Inadmissible, (as<BR>a witness.)<BR>	 3. Contradictory, prevaricating.<BR> E. हीन left, or defec-<BR>tive, वाद speech, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसख्य|हीनसख्यं
हीनसख्य n. (-ख्यं) Keeping low company, associating with persons of<BR>degraded castes and occupations.<BR> E. हीन an outcaste, and सख्य<BR>friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसन्धि|हीनसंधि|हीनसन्धिः
हीनसन्धि mfn. (-न्धिः-न्धिः-न्धि) Destitute of peace or reconciliation.<BR> E. हीन, सन्धि alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसेवा
हीनसेवा f. (-वा) Serving or attending on low persons, associating with<BR>them.<BR> E. हीन, and सेवा service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनाङ्ग|हीनांग|हीनाङ्गः
हीनाङ्ग mfn. (-ङ्गः-ङ्गी-ङ्गं) Crippled, maimed, defective.<BR>	 f. (-ङ्गी) An ant.<BR>E. हीन deficient, अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीन्ताल|हींताल|हींतालः|हीन्तालः
हीन्ताल m. (-लः) The marshy-date tree: see हिन्ताल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीर|हीरं|हीरः
हीर m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. ŚIVA.<BR>	 2. A snake.<BR>	 3. A necklace.<BR>	 4. A lion.<BR>	 5. Name<BR>of the father of SRIHARSHA, the author of Naishadha-Kāvyam.<BR>n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A diamond.<BR>	 2. INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>	 f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. The<BR>goddess LAKṢMĪ.<BR>	 2. A cockroach.<BR>	 3. An ant.<BR> E. हृ to take, क<BR>aff., and ईरु substituted for the radical finals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरक|हीरकः
हीरक m. (-कः) The diamond.<BR> E. कन् added to the last.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीराङ्ग|हीरांग|हीराङ्गः
हीराङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) The thunderbolt of INDRA.<BR> E. हीर the diamond, and अङ्ग substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हील|हीलं
हील n. (-लं) Semen virile.<BR> E. ही, ला to give, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीलुक|हीलुकं
हीलुक n. (-कं) Rum, spirits distilled from molasses,<BR> E. हिल-उक पृषी० ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीही
हीही Ind.<BR>	 1. An interjection of surprise, (ah, ha!)<BR>	 2. An interjection<BR>of laughter, (hee, hee!)<BR> E. ही the interjection repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हु
हु r. 3rd cl. (जुहोति)<BR>	 1. To sacrifice, to offer in oblation, (sometimes<BR>with the accusative of the deity honoured.)<BR>	 2. To eat.<BR>	 3. To take.<BR>4. To please or satisfy.<BR>	 5. To throw or cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हु
हु(हू)ङ्कार m. (-रः) Uttering a menacing sound, roaring, bellowing.<BR> E. हुन,<BR>and कार making; also similar compounds, as हुङ्कृति, हुङ्कृत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=834-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुङ्कृत|हुंकृत|हुंकृतं
हुङ्कृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Uttered or pronounced as an incantation.<BR>	 n.<BR>(-तं)<BR>	 1. An incantation.<BR>	 2. The roar or grunt of the wild boar.<BR>	 3.<BR>Any roar.<BR> E. हुम् a mystical monosyllable, and कृत made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुड्
हुड् r. 6th cl. (हुडति) To heap together, to collect or accumulate. (ऋ)<BR>हुडृ r. 1st cl. (होडते) To go or move. (इ) हुडि r. 1st cl. (हुण्डते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>heap, &c.<BR>	 2. To accept, to agree, to assent.<BR>	 3. To take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुड|हुडः
हुड m. (-डः)<BR>	 1. A ram.<BR>	 2. An iron club.<BR>	 3. An iron stake for keeping<BR>out thieves.<BR> E. हुड् to collect, क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडु|हुडुः
हुडु m. (-डः) A ram.<BR> E. हुड् to assemble, aff. कु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुक्क|हुडुक्कः
हुडुक्क m. (-क्कः)<BR>	 1. A gallinule.<BR>	 2. A drunken man.<BR>	 3. A small hour-<BR>glass-shaped drum.<BR>	 4. A stick or staff, one bound with iron.<BR>	 5.<BR>The bolt or bar of a door.<BR>	 6. A kind of bird, “दात्यूह”.<BR> E. हुडुक्<BR>an imitative sound, कै to utter, aff. क; or हुड्, उक्क aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुत
हुडुत n. (-तं)<BR>	 1. The noise of a bull.<BR>	 2. Any indistinct noise.<BR> E. हुड्-उति aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुम्ब|हुडुम्बः
हुडुम्ब m. (-म्बः) Flattened rice fried on fire.<BR> E. हुड्, उम्ब aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्ड|हुंड|हुंडः|हुण्डः
हुण्ड m. (-ण्डः)<BR>	 1. A tiger.<BR>	 2. A village-hog.<BR>	 3. A blockhead.<BR>	 4. An<BR>imp, a goblin.<BR>	 5. A ram.<BR> E. हुडि to collect, अच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुत|हुतं|हुतः
हुत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Offered with fire, burnt as an oblation.<BR>	 f. (-ता)<BR>	 1.<BR>Sacrificed.<BR>	 2. One to whom an oblation is offered.<BR>	 n. (-तं) An<BR>oblation.<BR>	 m. (-तः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतजातवेदस्
हुतजातवेदस् Adj. One who has made an oblation to fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतभुक्प्रिया
हुतभुक्प्रिया f. (-या) SWĀHĀ, the wife of AGNI.<BR> E. हुतभुज् AGNI, प्रिया the wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतभुज्
हुतभुज् m. (-भुक्) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. हुत an oblation, भुज् to eat, क्विप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतवह|हुतवहः
हुतवह m. (-हः) AGNI or fire.<BR> E. हुत an oblation, and वह who carries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतहोम|हुतहोमः
हुतहोम m. (-मः) A Brāhman who has offered an oblation.<BR>	 n. (-मं) An<BR>oblation.<BR> E. हुत, and होम sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताग्नि
हुताग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Fire with which oblation is made. Adj. Who has<BR>offered oblations to fire.<BR> E. हुत, अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताश|हुताशः
हुताश m. (-शः) Fire or its deity AGNI.<BR> E. हुत an oblation, अश who eats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताशन|हुताशनः
हुताशन m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. Fire or its deity AGNI.<BR>	 2. ŚIVA.<BR> E. हुत burnt-<BR>offering, and अशन food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताशनी
हुताशनी f. (-नी) The full-moon-day in the month of FĀLGUNA: होलाका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुति|हुतिः
हुति f. (-तिः) Finding, capture.<BR> E. हु to take, &c., क्तिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुत्वा
हुत्वा Ind. Having offered in oblation.<BR> E. हु to offer, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुम्
हुम् Ind.<BR>	 1. An interjection of remembering, (ha, ah!)<BR>	 2. Of repulse<BR>or reproach, (away!)<BR>	 3. Interrogation, (hey?)<BR>	 4. Assent, (yes.)<BR>5. Doubt.<BR>	 6. A mystical syllable of frequent occurrence in incan-<BR>tations.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice, डुमि or डुम् aff.: see हूम् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुयमान
हुयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being offered in oblation.<BR> E. हु to offer, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुर्च्छ्
हुर्च्छ् r. 1st cl. (हूर्च्छति)<BR>	 1. To be crooked, (literally.)<BR>	 2. To be fraudulent,<BR>(figuratively.)<BR>	 3. To retreat, to hide or abscond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुल्
हुल् r. 1st cl. (होलति)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To kill.<BR>	 3. To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुलहुली
हुलहुली f. (-ली) Inarticulate sounds made by women, especially a sort<BR>of Ululatus, though apparently employed upon pleasurable and<BR>not sorrowful occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुहु|हुहुः
हुहु m. (-हुः) A Gandharba.<BR> E. ह्वेञ् to call, डु aff., form irr.: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुहू
हुहू m. (-हूः) A Gandharba or chorister of heaven.<BR> E. ह्वेञ् to call, डु<BR>aff., form irr.; it is also read हुहु, हूहु, and हूहू ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हू
हू Ind. An interjection of calling, of contempt, of pride, and of grief or weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूङ्कार|हूंकार|हूङ्कारः
हूङ्कार m. (-रः)<BR>	 1. Uttering the sound “Hum.” 2. Uttering a menacing<BR>sound, roaring: see हुङ्कार.<BR> E. हूम्, कार making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूड्
हूड् (ऋ) हूडृ r. 1st cl. (-हूडते) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूण|हूणः
हूण m. (-णः)<BR>	 1. A barbarian, a Hūn.<BR>	 2. A kind of gold coin current<BR>in the country of the Hūnas; also read. हून.<BR> E. ह्वेञ् to call, नक<BR>Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूत|हूतं
हूत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Called, summoned, invited, invoked.<BR> E. ह्वेञ् to call, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूति|हूतिः
हूति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Calling, inviting.<BR>	 2. Calling to in defiance, challenging.<BR>E. ह्वेञ् to call, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूम्
हूम् Ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of doubt or consideration (humph, ha.)<BR>	 2. An<BR>interrogatory particle, (hey, indeed.)<BR>	 3. A particle of assent, (yes,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-b" target="_blank">Page835-b+ 60</a>]<BR>well, so be it, amen.)<BR>	 4. An interjection of anger.<BR>	 5. Of fear.<BR>6. Of reproach, or contempt, (equivalent to be silent, tush,<BR>pish.)<BR>	 7. Of aversion, repulse, or dislike, &c.<BR>	 8. A magical<BR>or mystical monosyllable.<BR>	 9. An imitative sound.<BR> E. ह्वेञ् to call,<BR>aff. डूमि or डूम्ः see हुम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूयमान
हूयमान mfn. (-नः-ना-नं) Being offered in oblation.<BR> E. हु to offer, pass. v.,<BR>शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूरव|हूरवः
हूरव m. (-वः) A Jackal.<BR> E. हू a cry of fear or wrath, and ख sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूर्च्छन
हूर्च्छन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Crookedness, (literal.)<BR>	 2. Craft, cunning, (figurative.)<BR>E. हुर्च्छ् to be crooked, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूहु|हूहुः
हूहु m. (-हुः) A Gandharba: see हुहू; also read हूहू m. (-हूः ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृ
हृ r. 1st cl. (ज) हृज् r. 1st cl. (हरति ते)<BR>	 1. To convey.<BR>	 2. To take or<BR>accept.<BR>	 3. To steal.<BR>	 4. To destroy or annual.<BR>	 5. To deprive of 6.<BR>To captivate, to charm, to influence.<BR>	 7. To remove. With अधि<BR>and आ, To supply an ellipsis. With अनु prefixed, 1. To imitate,<BR>(Par.)<BR>	 2. To take after the parents, (Atm.) With अप, 1. To<BR>remove, to take away or apart.<BR>	 2. To plunder, to steal.<BR>	 3. To<BR>attract, to influence.<BR>	 4. To leave behind. With अभि and अव, To eat.<BR>With आ, 1. To fetch, to carry.<BR>	 2. To perform, (as a sacrifice.)<BR>	 3.<BR>To get.<BR>	 4. To procreate.<BR>	 5. To recover, to bring back.<BR>	 6. To<BR>assume.<BR>	 7. To attract.<BR>	 8. To withdraw.<BR>	 9. To eat. With उद्, 1. To<BR>take out or up.<BR>	 2. To make an extract from.<BR>	 3. To raise, to extricate.<BR>4. To eradicate, to destroy.<BR>	 5. To deduct. With उप and आ, To bring.<BR>With निस्, 1. To carry out a dead body.<BR>	 2. To extract, to draw<BR>out from. With प्र, 1. To throw, to hurl, to fling, (with a dative<BR>or accusative.)<BR>	 2. To attack, to strike.<BR>	 3. To wound, to injure,<BR>(with a locative.)<BR>	 4. To seize upon. With वि, 1. To remove, to<BR>destroy.<BR>	 2. To pass, (as time.)<BR>	 3. To sport.<BR>	 4. To say. With सम्,<BR>1. To collect.<BR>	 2. To withdraw.<BR>	 3. To suppress, to restrain.<BR>	 4. To<BR>kill, to annihilate, (opposed to सृज्).<BR>	 5. To contract, to abridge<BR>With सम and आ, 1. To bring.<BR>	 2. To make reparation for.<BR>	 3. To<BR>draw.<BR>	 4. To destroy.<BR>	 5. To collect. With अभि, To assault. With<BR>अभि and आङ्, To reason. With अभि and उत्, To deliver. With<BR>अभि, वि, and आङ्, To utter, to pronounce. With अव, 1. To regain.<BR>2. To punish or fine. With उत्, 1. To raise, to lift or take up.<BR>	 2.<BR>To expel. With उद् and आङ्.<BR>	 1. To say or tell.<BR>	 2. To illustrate, to<BR>exemplify. With उप, 1. To bring near to.<BR>	 2. To give. With उप<BR>and सम्, To withhold. With नि changed to नी, To freeze. With<BR>निर्, To show disrespect. With निर् and आङ्, To fast. With परि,<BR>1. To reproach, to abuse or censure.<BR>	 2. To leave, to shun, to<BR>abandon.<BR>	 3. To resist.<BR>	 4. To remove, to destroy.<BR>	 5. To extract.<BR>With प्रति changed to प्रती, To keep watch. With प्रति and आङ्, To<BR>think abstractedly by restraining the organs of sense. With प्रति<BR>and सम्, To disregard, to abandon. With वि, 1. To sport, to ramble<BR>for pleasure.<BR>	 2. To pass, (as time.)<BR>	 3. To remove.<BR>	 4. To destroy.<BR>With वि and आङ्, To say, to utter, to speak. With वि and अव,<BR>1. To deal in transactions, (with a genitive.)<BR>	 2. To litigate.<BR>With सम् and आङ्, To collect, to assemble. With सम्, अभि,<BR>वि and आङ्, To speak in concert. With सम्, उत् and आङ्, To<BR>relate. With सम् and उप, 1. To give.<BR>	 2. To assemble, to collect.<BR>With सम् and प्र, To fight. With वि and अति prefixed and implying<BR>reciprocity (व्यतिहरते) To steal or plunder mutually. In the first<BR>sense “to convey” this verb governs two accusatives, as भारं हरति<BR>ग्रागं he takes the load (to) the village. Caus. (हारयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To<BR>cause to carry.<BR>	 2. To make to lose. With अप, To cause to take<BR>away. With अभि and अव, To feed. With आ, To cause to bring. With<BR>उद्, To cause to take out. r. 3rd cl. (जहर्त्ति) To take by violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृच्छय|हृच्छयः
हृच्छय m. (-यः) KĀMADEVA.<BR> E. हृत् the heart, and शय who sleeps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृच्छोक|हृच्छोकः
हृच्छोक m. (-कः) A pang.<BR> E. हृत् the heart, शोक grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणिया
हृणिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Shame, modesty.<BR>	 2. Censure, reproach.<BR>	 3. Pity. E.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">Page836-a+ 60</a>]<BR>हृणीङ् Kaṇḍwādi root, to be ashamed, यक् aff., and the vowel<BR>made short; otherwise read हृणीया ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=835-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणी
हृणी (हृणीयते) To feel ashamed. A kaṇḍwādi root; य is always added<BR>on the base in the case of this root: see ह्रिणी ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणीया
हृणीया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Censure, reproach.<BR>	 2. Shame, bashfulness.<BR>	 3. Pity. E.<BR>हृणीय, अ aff.: see हृणिया; also read ह्रिणीया ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्
हृत् Adj. Taking away, seizing, attracting, &c., (at the end of compounds only.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत|हृतं
हृत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Taken, taken away.<BR>	 2. Seized.<BR>	 3. Accepted.<BR>	 4.<BR>Captivated.<BR>	 5. Divided.<BR> E. हृ to take, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतसर्व्वस्व|हृतसर्वस्व
हृतसर्व्वस्व mfn. (-स्वः-स्वा-स्वं) Robbed or stripped of all, entirely ruined.<BR> E. हृत, सर्व्वस्व all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृताधिकार
हृताधिकार mfn. (-रः-रा-रं)<BR>	 1. Neglecting one's duty.<BR>	 2. Deprived of an<BR>office, turned out.<BR>	 3. Barred or deprived of one's right.<BR> E. हृत,<BR>and अधिकार superintendence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृति|हृतिः
हृति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Seizure.<BR>	 2. Robbing.<BR>	 3. Destruction.<BR> E. हृ to take, क्तिन् aff.; also ह्रिति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतोत्तर
हृतोत्तर mfn. (-रः-रा-रं) Left without a reply.<BR> E. हृत, and उत्तर answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्कम्प|हृत्कंप|हृत्कम्पः
हृत्कम्प m. (-म्पः) Tremor of the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्पिण्ड|हृत्पिंड|हृत्पिण्डः
हृत्पिण्ड n. (-ण्डं) The heart.<BR> E. हृत्, and पिण्ड lump of flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्वा
हृत्वा Ind. Having taken, seized, accepted, &c.<BR> E. हृ to take, क्त्वा aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्स्थ
हृत्स्थ mfn. (-त्स्थः-त्स्था-त्स्थं) Seated in the heart.<BR> E. हृत्, स्थ what stays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्
हृद् n. (-हृत् or हृद्) The heart, the mind, the faculty or seat of<BR>thought and feeling.<BR> E. हृ to take, aff. क्विप्, and तुक् added;<BR>This word has no forms for the first five cases; according to some<BR>it is not a separate word but an optional substitute for हृदय ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदय|हृदयं
हृदय n. (-यं)<BR>	 1. The mind, the seat or faculty of thought and feeling.<BR>2. Knowledge.<BR>	 3. Science.<BR>	 4. The essence of anything.<BR> E. हृ to<BR>take, कयन् Unādi aff., दुक् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयग्राहिन्
हृदयग्राहिन् mfn. (-ही-हिणी-हि) Captivating, engaging the affections.<BR> E. हृदय, ग्राहिन् taking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयङ्गम|हृदयंगम|हृदयङ्गमं
हृदयङ्गम mfn. (-मः-मा-मं)<BR>	 1. Apposite and proper, (as speech.)<BR>	 2. Affect-<BR>ing, touching, thrilling.<BR>	 3. Dear, beloved.<BR>	 4. Pleasing.<BR> E. हृदय the<BR>heart, गम् to go, खश् aff., मुम् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयचौर
हृदयचौर m. (-रः) One who steals the heart or affections.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयवत्|हृदयवन्त्
हृदयवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Good-hearted, kind, humane.<BR> E. हृदय the heart, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयवृत्ति
हृदयवृत्ति f. (-त्तिः) Disposition of the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयस्थ
हृदयस्थ Adj. Cherished or being in the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हदयस्थान
हदयस्थान n. (-नं) The breast, the chest.<BR> E. हृदय the heart, स्थान place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयात्मन
हृदयात्मन m. (-त्मा) A heron.<BR> E. हृदय the heart, and आत्मन् self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयालु|हृदयालुः
हृदयालु mfn. (-लुः-लुः-लु) Good-hearted.<BR> E. हृदय the heart, and आलुच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयाविध्
हृदयाविध् mfn. (-त् or द्) Heart-piercing.<BR> E. हृदय, and आविध् what pierces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयिक|हृदयिकः
हृदयिक mfn. (-कः-का-कं) Good-hearted.<BR> E. हृदय the heart, ठन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयिन्
हृदयिन् mfn. (-यी-यिनी-यि) Good-hearted.<BR> E. हृदय the heart, इनि poss. aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयेश|हृदयेशः
हृदयेश m. (-शः) A husband.<BR>	 f. (-शा)<BR>	 1. A wife.<BR>	 2. A mistress: see the<BR>next.<BR> E. हृदय the heart, ईश lord; also हृदयेश्वर, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयेश्वरी
हृदयेश्वरी f. (-री)<BR>	 1. A wife.<BR>	 2. A mistress.<BR> E. हृदय the heart, ईश्वरी<BR>governess; also with ईशा, हृदयेशा ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयोदङ्क|हृदयोदङ्कः
हृदयोदङ्क mfn. (-ङ्कः-ङ्का-ङ्कं) Heart-heaving, distressing.<BR> E. हृदय, उत् up, अङ्क what goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदावर्त्त|हृदावर्त|हृदावर्तः|हृदावर्त्तः
हृदावर्त्त m. (-र्त्तः) A curl or lock of hair on a horse's neck, or breast<BR>E. हृद् the heart, आवर्त्त a twist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदिकात्मज
हृदिकात्मज m. (-जः) KRITAVARMAN.<BR> E. हृदिक the YĀDAVA-king, आत्मज son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदिस्पृश्
हृदिस्पृश् mfn. (-स्पृक्)<BR>	 1. Dear, beloved.<BR>	 2. Attractive, beautiful.<BR>	 3.<BR>Touching the heart.<BR> E. हृदि in the heart, and स्पृश् what affects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्गत
हृद्गत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Conceived, come to mind, designed.<BR> E. हृद्, गत gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्गोल|हृद्गोलः
हृद्गोल m. (-लः) The name of a mountainous district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्गोलीय|हृद्गोलीयः
हृद्गोलीय m. Pl. (-याः) The military inhabitants of the Hridgola moun-<BR>tains.<BR> E. हृद्गोल, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्देश|हृद्देशः
हृद्देश m. (-शः) The heart or the region of it.<BR> E. हृद्, देश place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्य|हृद्यं|हृद्यः
हृद्य mfn. (-द्यः-द्या-द्यं)<BR>	 1. Dear, beloved cherished, desired.<BR>	 2. Grateful,<BR>pleasant, agreeable.<BR>	 3. Produced in or from the heart.<BR>	 4. Affec-<BR>tionate, kind.<BR>	 m. (-द्यः) A Mantra of the Vedas for effecting any<BR>one's subjection or fascination.<BR>	 f. (-द्या) Vriddhi, a medicinal root,<BR>so named.<BR>	 n. (-द्यं) Cassia bark.<BR> E. हृद् the heart, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्यगन्ध|हृद्यगन्धं|हृद्यगन्धः
हृद्यगन्ध m. (-न्धः) The Bel tree, (Ægle marmelos.)<BR>	 n. (-न्धं)<BR>	 1. Small<BR>cardamoms.<BR>	 2. Sachal-salt.<BR>	 f. (-न्धा) Great-flowered jasmine.<BR> E. हृद्य<BR>agreeable, गन्ध smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्यता
हृद्यता f. (-ता) Agreeableness, delightfulness.<BR> E. हृद्य, and तल् aff.; also with त्व, हृद्यत्वं ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्रोग|हृद्रोगः
हृद्रोग m. (-गः)<BR>	 1. Heart-burn.<BR>	 2. Any disease of the heart.<BR>	 3. Sorrow,<BR>grief, anguish.<BR>	 4. Love.<BR>	 5. The sign Aquarius of the zodiac, (in<BR>this sense more properly of Greek origin: see ह्रद्रोग.)<BR> E. हृद् the<BR>heart, रोग disease; also हृदयरोग ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्रोगवैरिन्
हृद्रोगवैरिन् m. (-री) A tree, (Pentaptera Arjuna.)<BR> E. हृद्रोग the heartburn, वैरिन् hostile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्वण्टक|हृद्वंटक|हृद्वण्टकः
हृद्वण्टक m. (-कः) The stomach.<BR> E. हृद् the heart, वण्टक a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृल्लास|हृल्लासः
हृल्लास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Hiccough.<BR>	 2. Disquietude, grief.<BR> E. हृद्, लस् to sport, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृल्लेख|हृल्लेखः
हृल्लेख m. (-खः)<BR>	 1. Knowledge.<BR>	 2. Reasoning.<BR>	 f. (-खा) Regret, sorrow<BR>for any object absent or missing, anxiety.<BR> E. हृद् the heart, लिख्<BR>to write, aff. अच् or घञ्; also हृदयलेख ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्
हृष् (इर, उ) इरहृषु r. 4th cl. (हृष्यति)<BR>	 1. To rejoice, to exult, to be pleased.<BR>2. To stand erect, (as the hair of the body, &c.) With प्र, 1.<BR>To be glad.<BR>	 2. To stand erect. With सम्, To rejoice. (उ) हृषु r.<BR>1st cl. (हर्षति)<BR>	 1. To lie, to affirm falsely.<BR>	 2. To be pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषित|हृषितं
हृषित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Astonished, surprised.<BR>	 2. Pleased.<BR>	 3. Exqui-<BR>sitely delighted, having the hair of the body erect with pleasure.<BR>4. Disappointed, deceived.<BR>	 5. Bent, bowed.<BR>	 6. Armed, accoutred.<BR>E. हृष् to be pleased, or to lie, aff. क्त, with the augment इट् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषीक|हृषीकं
हृषीक n. (-कं) Any organ of sense.<BR> E. हृष् to affirm falsely, ईकक् Unādi<BR>aff, and the radical vowel unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषीकेश|हृषीकेशः
हृषीकेश m. (-शः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. हृषीक an organ of sense, ईश lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्ट|हृष्टः
हृष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं)<BR>	 1. Pleased, glad, delighted.<BR>	 2. Laughing, smiling.<BR>3. Having the hair of the body erect with pleasure.<BR>	 4. Asto-<BR>nished, surprised.<BR>	 5. Disappointed.<BR> E. हृष् to be pleased, or to<BR>affirm falsely, aff. क्तः see हृषित ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टपुष्ट
हृष्टपुष्ट mfn. (-ष्टः-ष्टा-ष्टं) Well-conditioned, well-fed and happy.<BR> E. हृष्ट, पुष्ट nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टमानस|हृष्टमानसः
हृष्टमानस mfn. (-सः-सी-सं) Happy, glad.<BR> E. हृष्ट pleased, मानस the mind,<BR>अण् aff.; also similar compounds, as हृष्टचित्त ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टरोमन्
हृष्टरोमन् mfn. (-मा-मा-म) Having the hair of the body on end.<BR> E. हृष्ट<BR>delighted, रोमन् the down or bristles of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टहृदय
हृष्टहृदय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) Happy, light-hearted.<BR> E. हृष्ट, हृदय the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टि|हृष्टिः
हृष्टि f. (-ष्टिः)<BR>	 1. Delight, pleasure, happiness.<BR>	 2. Pride, arrogance.<BR>	 3.<BR>Knowledge.<BR> E. हृष् to be pleased, aff. क्तिन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हे
हे Ind.<BR>	 1. A vocative particle.<BR>	 2. A particle of calling out to, or<BR>challenging.<BR>	 3. An interjection, expressing envy or malice.<BR> E. हि<BR>to go, or हा to go, aff. डे ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेक्का
हेक्का f. (-क्का) Hiccough.<BR> E. हिक्क् to hiccough, aff. अच्, and the vowel changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेट्
हेट् r. 1st cl. (हेटते) To resist, to oppose; more properly हेठ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठ्
हेठ् r. 1st cl. (हेठति)<BR>	 1. To resist, to oppose. r. 6th cl. (हेठति)<BR>	 1. To be<BR>produced.<BR>	 2. To purify. (ऋ) हेठृ r. 1st cl. (हेठते)<BR>	 1. To oppress.<BR>	 2.<BR>To annoy.<BR>	 3. To resist, to contend with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठ|हेठः
हेठ m. (-ठः)<BR>	 1. Obstruction, opposition, hindrance.<BR>	 2. Injury, hurt. E.<BR>हेठ् to annoy or oppose, aff. अच् or घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेड्
हेड् r. 1st cl. (हेडति) To surround, to encompass. (ऋ) हेड r. 1st cl.<BR>(हेडते) To disregard, to neglect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडज|हेडजः
हेडज m. (-जः) Passion, anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडावुक्क|हेडावुक्कः
हेडावुक्क m. (-क्कः) A horse-dealer; also read हेलावुक्क and हेलावुक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेढ्
हेढ् r. 9th cl. (हेढ्णाति)<BR>	 1. To be past birth.<BR>	 2. To produce young.<BR>	 3. To purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेति|हेतिः
हेति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. A weapon.<BR>	 2. A ray of the sun.<BR>	 3. Light, splendour.<BR>	 4.<BR>Flame.<BR> E. हि to go, or हन् to kill, aff. क्तिन्; the form is irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतु|हेतुः
हेतु m. (-तुः)<BR>	 1. Cause, object, motive.<BR>	 2. The reason or argument for<BR>an inference or deduction.<BR>	 3. Reasoning, logic.<BR>	 4. Means, instru-<BR>ment.<BR>	 5. Source, origin.<BR>	 6. A figure of speech. The instantive,<BR>ablative and locative singulars of this word, viz:--“हेतुना,” “हेतो”<BR>and “हेतौ,” are used as indeclinables in the sense of “on account<BR>of,” “because of,” “by reason of.”<BR> E. हि to go, Unādi aff. तुन् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=836-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुक|हेतुकः
हेतुक mfn. (-कः-का-कं)<BR>	 1. Causal, instrumental.<BR>	 2. Relating or<BR>belonging to the cause or motive.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An active cause, an<BR>instrument or agent.<BR>	 2. A logician.<BR>	 f. (-का) Causing, producing,<BR>(at the end of compounds.)<BR> E. हेतु cause, and कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुता
हेतुता f. (-ता) Causation, cause, causativeness, the abstract existence<BR>of cause or motive.<BR> E. हेतु cause, तल् aff.; also with त्व, हेतुत्व n. (-त्वं ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुमत्|हेतुमन्त्
हेतुमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Having a cause, proceeding from one,<BR>acknowledging one, &c.<BR>	 n. (-मत्) An effect.<BR> E. हेतु, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुवाद|हेतुवादः
हेतुवाद m. (-दः) Disputation.<BR> E. हेतु, and वाद dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतशास्त्र
हेतशास्त्र n. (-स्त्रं) Any heretical work calling in question the authority of Śruti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतौ
हेतौ Ind. By reason or cause of.<BR> E. हेतु in the seventh case, used as a<BR>particle: see हेतु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेत्वाभास|हेत्वाभासः
हेत्वाभास m. (-सः) (In logic,) Fallacious semblance of reason or argu-<BR>ment, assignment of proof or cause which can be shown to be<BR>incorrect, the faulty reasoning for an inference; it is of five kinds,<BR>viz:--BYABHICHĀRA, VIRUDDHATĀ, ASIDDHI, SATPRATIPAK<BR>SHATĀ, and BĀDHA.<BR> E. हेतु, and आभास semblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेम|हेमं|हेमः
हेम m. (-मः)<BR>	 1. A horse of a dark colour.<BR>	 2. The planet MERCURY.<BR>	 3.<BR>A weight of gold, equal to a MĀSHĀ.<BR>	 n. (-मं)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. The<BR>Nāgakeśara flower.<BR>	 3. The Dhattūra.<BR>	 f. (-मा)<BR>	 1. An Apsarasas or<BR>courtezan of heaven.<BR>	 2. A handsome woman.<BR> E. हि to go, मन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकन्दल|हेमकंदल|हेमकन्दलः
हेमकन्दल m. (-लः) Coral. “प्रबाले.”<BR> E. हेम gold, and कन्दल a shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकार|हेमकारः
हेमकार m. (-रः) A goldsmith.<BR> E. हेमन् gold, and कार who makes or<BR>works; also हेमकर, हेमकारक and हेमकर्त्तृ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकिञ्जल्क|हेमकिंजल्क|हेमकिञ्जल्कं
हेमकिञ्जल्क n. (-ल्कं) The Nāgakeśara flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकूट|हेमकूटः
हेमकूट m. (-टः) One of the ranges of mountains dividing the known<BR>continent into nine Varṣas; this range is the second south of<BR>Illāvrita, or the central division, and is immediately to the north<BR>of the Himālaya, forming with it the boundaries of the Kinnara<BR>Varṣam.<BR> E. हेम gold or golden, and कूट a peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकेलि|हेमकेलिः
हेमकेलि m. (-लिः)<BR>	 1. Fire.<BR>	 2. The Chitraka tree.<BR> E. हेम gold, and केलि who sports.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकेश|हेमकेशः
हेमकेश m. (-शः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. हेम gold, केश hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमक्षीरी
हेमक्षीरी f. (-री) A medicinal sort of moon-plant.<BR> E. हेम gold, क्षीरी a name of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमगन्धिनी|हेमगंधिनी
हेमगन्धिनी f. (-नी) Renūkā, a perfume.<BR> E. हेम golden, गन्धिनी a perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमगिरि|हेमगिरिः
हेमगिरि m. (-रिः) The mountain Sumeru; also हेमपर्व्वत, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमगौर|हेमगौरः
हेमगौर m. (-रः) The Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमज्वाल|हेमज्वालः
हेमज्वाल m. (-लः) Fire.<BR> E. हेम gold, and ज्वाला flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमतरु|हेमतरुः
हेमतरु m. (-रुः) Dhattūra or thorn-apple.<BR> E. हेम, तरु tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमतार|हेमतारं
हेमतार n. (-रं) Blue vitriol.<BR> E. हेम gold, तृ to pass, aff. घञ, or causal v., अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमदुग्ध|हेमदुग्धः
हेमदुग्ध m. (-ग्धः) The glomerous-fig tree.<BR>	 f. (-ग्धी) A medicinal sort of<BR>moon-plant.<BR> E. हेम gold, दुग्ध milk; also with कन् added, हेमदुग्धक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमदुग्धक|हेमदुग्धकः
हेमदुग्धक m. (-कः) The glomerous-fig tree, (Ficus glomerata.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्
हेमन् n. (-म)<BR>	 1. Gold.<BR>	 2. Dhattūra.<BR>	 3. The Nāgakeśara flower.<BR>	 4. Snow.<BR>m. (-मा)<BR>	 1. The planet MERCURY.<BR>	 2. Winter.<BR> E. हि to go, मनिन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्त|हेमंत|हेमंतं|हेमंतः|हेमन्तः
हेमन्त mn. (-न्तः-न्तं) The cold season, winter, the two months, Agra-<BR>hāyana and Pausha, or about November-December.<BR> E. हन् to<BR>hurt, झच् Unādi aff., हि substituted for the root, and मुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्तनाथ|हेमन्तनाथः
हेमन्तनाथ m. (-थः) Elephant or wood-apple.<BR> E. हेमन्त winter, नाथ lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमपर्व्वत|हेमपर्वत|हेमपर्वतः|हेमपर्व्वतः
हेमपर्व्वत m. (-तः) The mountain Meru.<BR> E. हेम gold, पर्व्वत mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमपुष्प|हेमपुष्पं|हेमपुष्पः
हेमपुष्प n. (-ष्पं)<BR>	 1. The Aśoka tree, (Jonesia Asoca.)<BR>	 2. The China rose.<BR>the flower.<BR>	 m. (-ष्पः)<BR>	 1. The Champaka, (Michelia champaca.)<BR>2. The Lodh tree.<BR>	 f. (-ष्पी) Begal madder.<BR> E. हेम golden, पुष्प a flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमपुष्पक|हेमपुष्पकः
हेमपुष्पक m. (-कः) The Champaka.<BR>	 f. (-का) Yellow jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमफला
हेमफला f. (-ला) A kind of plantain. “चांँपाकला” इति भाषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेममाला
हेममाला f. (-ला) The wife of YAMA.<BR> E. हेम gold, माला a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेममालिन्
हेममालिन् m. (-ली)<BR>	 1. The sun.<BR>	 2. The Arka plant.<BR> E. हेम, माला a garland, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमयूथिका
हेमयूथिका f. (-का) The yellow Jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमरत्नमय
हेमरत्नमय mfn. (-यः-यी-यं) Full of gold and gems.<BR> E. हेम, and रत्न a gem. मयट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमरागिणी
हेमरागिणी f. (-णी) Turmeric.<BR> E. हेम gold, राग colour, इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमल|हेमलः
हेमल m. (-लः)<BR>	 1. A goldsmith.<BR>	 2. A touch-stone.<BR>	 mf. (-लः-ला or ली)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">Page837-b+ 60</a>]<BR>A chameleon, a lizard.<BR> E. हेम gold, ला to have or take, aff. क;<BR>ङीष् added in the feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमवल|हेमवलं
हेमवल n. (-लं) A pearl.<BR> E. हेम gold, वल surrounding; also read हिमबल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमशङ्ख|हेमशंख|हेमशङ्खः
हेमशङ्ख m. (-ङ्खः) VIṢṆU.<BR> E. हेम gold, and शङ्ख a shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमशिखा
हेमशिखा f. (-खा) A medicinal sort of moon-plant.<BR> E. हेम gold, शिखा crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमशृङ्ग|हेमशृंग
हेमशृङ्ग n. (-ङ्गं)<BR>	 1. A golden horn.<BR>	 2. A golden peak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमसार
हेमसार n. (-रं) Blue vitriol.<BR> E. हेम, सृ to remove, causal v., अण् aff.; also read हेमतर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमसूत्रक|हेमसूत्रकं
हेमसूत्रक n. (-कं) A kind of necklace.<BR> E. हेम gold, सूत्र a string, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाङ्ग|हेमांग|हेमाङ्गः
हेमाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. GARUḌA.<BR>	 2. A lion.<BR>	 3. The mountain Sumeru.<BR>	 4.<BR>BRAHMĀ.<BR>	 5. The Champaka.<BR>	 6. VIṢṆU.<BR> E. हेम gold, अङ्ग body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाङ्गद|हेमांगद
हेमाङ्गद n. (-दं) A gold-bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाद्रि|हेमाद्रिः
हेमाद्रि m. (-द्रिः) The mountain Sumeru.<BR> E. हेम gold, अद्रि mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाह्व|हेमाह्वः
हेमाह्व m. (-ह्वः) The wild-champaka tree.<BR>	 2. The Dhattūra plant.<BR>	 3.<BR>The Nagakeśara tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेय|हेयः
हेय mfn. (-यः-या-यं) To be left, abandoned, avoided, &c.<BR> E. हा to quit, यत् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेर|हेरं
हेर n. (-रं)<BR>	 1. A sort of crown or tiara.<BR>	 2. Turmeric.<BR>	 3. The illusion of<BR>a demon.<BR> E. हि to go, रक् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरम्ब|हेरंब|हेरंबः|हेरम्बः
हेरम्ब m. (-म्बः)<BR>	 1. GAṆEŚA.<BR>	 2. A buffalo.<BR>	 3. A hero inflated with his<BR>own valour and prowess.<BR>	 4. A Buddha or Bauddha deity.<BR> E. हे<BR>calling or defying, रवि to sound, aff. अच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरम्बजननी|हेरंबजननी
हेरम्बजननी f. (-नी) DURGĀ.<BR> E. हेरम्ब GAṆEŚA, and जननी mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरम्बहट्ट|हेरम्बहट्टः
हेरम्बहट्ट m. (-ट्टः) A country included in the enumeration of the pro-<BR>vinces of the Dakshin.<BR> E. हेरम्ब GAṆEŚA, and हट्ट fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरिक|हेरिकः
हेरिक m. (-कः) A spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR> E. हि to go, इक् Unādi<BR>aff., रुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरुक|हेरुकः
हेरुक m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. An attendant on MAHĀKĀLA, or ŚIVA in that form.<BR>2. An inferior divinity of the Bauddhas.<BR> E. हि to go, उक Unādi<BR>aff., रुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलञ्ची
हेलञ्ची f. (-ञ्ची) A potherb, (Hingtsha repens.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलन|हेलनं
हेलन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Disrespect, disregard, contempt.<BR>	 2. Wantoning,<BR>dalliance.<BR> E. हिल् to disregard, aff. ल्युट्; also with अन, हेलना ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेला
हेला f. (-ला)<BR>	 1. Wanton sport, dalliance, lascivious endearment.<BR>	 2.<BR>Disrespect, contempt.<BR>	 3. Facility, ease.<BR>	 4. Moonlight.<BR> E. हिल् to<BR>dally, affs. अच् and टाप्; or हेड् to disregard, अच् aff., ड changed<BR>to ल ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलावुक्क|हेलावुक्कः
हेलावुक्क m. (-क्कः) A horse-dealer; also read हेलावुक and हेडावुक्क ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलि|हेलिः
हेलि m. (-लिः) The sun.<BR>	 f. (-लिः) Dalliance, wanton sport.<BR> E. हिल् to<BR>dally, Unādi aff. इन्; also with णिनि, हेलिन् m. (-ली ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेवाक|हेवाकः
हेवाक m. (-कः) Fondness, eagerness. A word of doubtful origin, probably<BR>Arabic, and found only in later writers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेवाकिन्
हेवाकिन् f. (-किनी) Fond, eager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेष्
हेष् (ऋ) हेषृ r. 1st cl. (हेषते) To neigh, (as a horse,) to bray, to roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषा
हेषा f. (-षा) Neighing, (as a horse,) braying, (as an ass.)<BR> E. हेष् to<BR>neigh, to bray, affs. अच् and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषिन्
हेषिन् m. (-षी) A horse.<BR> E. हेषा neighing, and णिनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेहे
हेहे (है) Ind.<BR>	 1. A particle of addressing, a vocative particle.<BR>	 2. An<BR>interjection of calling aloud.<BR> E. हे, &c., the same, repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

है
है Ind.<BR>	 1. A vocative particle.<BR>	 2. An interjection of calling.<BR> E. ह्वे to<BR>call, डै aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैतुक|हैतुकः
हैतुक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Causal, causative.<BR>	 2. Argumentative, rational-<BR>istic.<BR>	 m. (-कः)<BR>	 1. A follower of the Mīmānsā doctrines.<BR>	 2. A<BR>sceptic, a causalist.<BR>	 3. A reasoner, an arguer.<BR> E. हेतु cause, ठण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैम|हैमं|हैमः
हैम mfn. (-मः-मी-मं)<BR>	 1. Golden.<BR>	 2. Frigid, freezing, cold.<BR>	 n. (-मं) Hoar-<BR>frost, dew.<BR>	 f. (-सा or मी) Yellow jasmine.<BR>	 m. (-मः) ŚIVA.<BR> E. हेमन्<BR>gold, or हिम frost, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन|हैमनं|हैमनः
हैमन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं)<BR>	 1. Cold, wintry.<BR>	 2. Growing in winter.<BR>	 3.<BR>Suitable to winter.<BR>	 4. Made of gold.<BR>	 m. (-नः)<BR>	 1. The month<BR>Mārgaśīrsha.<BR>	 2. The winter season.<BR> E. हेमन्त winter, अण् aff., and<BR>the final optionally rejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन्त|हैमन्तं
हैमन्त mfn. (-न्तः-न्ती-न्तं)<BR>	 1. Wintry, cold.<BR>	 2. Growing in winter, &c.<BR>	 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">Page838-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Suitable to the winter, (as abode or clothing, &c.)<BR>	 n. (-न्तं) The<BR>winter season.<BR> E. हेमन्त winter, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=837-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन्तिक|हैमंतिक|हैमन्तिकं
हैमन्तिक mfn. (-कः-की-कं)<BR>	 1. Wintry, freezing, frigid.<BR>	 2. Growing in winter.<BR> E. हेमन्त, ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमल|हैमलः
हैमल m. (-लः) Winter.<BR> E. हिमल cold, अण् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमवत|हैमवतं|हैमवतः
हैमवत n. (-तं) BHĀRATA-VARSHA or India.<BR>	 m. (-तः) A sort of poison.<BR>	 f.<BR>(-ती)<BR>	 1. PĀRVATĪ.<BR>	 2. Chebulic myrobalan.<BR>	 3. A medicinal kind of<BR>moon-plant.<BR>	 4. A white kind of Orris root.<BR>	 5. A tawny grape.<BR>	 6.<BR>The Ganges.<BR>	 f. (-ती) Adj.<BR>	 1. Flowing from the Himālaya mountain.<BR>2. Bred in or belonging to the Himālaya mountain.<BR>	 3. Snowy. E.<BR>हिमबत् the snowy mountains skirting India, अण् aff., fem. aff. ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैयङ्गवीन|हैयंगवीन|हैयंगवीनं|हैयङ्गवीनं
हैयङ्गवीन n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Clarified butter prepared a day before it is used.<BR>2. Clarified butter prepared from the milking of the previous day.<BR>E. ह्यम् yesterday, गोदोह milk, हियङ्ग substituted for them, खञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरिक|हैरिकः
हैरिक m. (-कः) A thief.<BR> E. हि-र हेरः तत्र प्रसूतः ठक् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैहय|हैहयः
हैहय m. (-यः) KĀRTAVĪRYA, a sovereign: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैहेय|हैहेयः
हैहेय m. (-यः) A prince; also KĀRTAVĪRYA, who was slain by PARAŚURĀMA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हो
हो Ind.<BR>	 1. A vocative particle.<BR>	 2. An interjection of calling out to, or<BR>challenging.<BR> E. ह्वेञ् to call, डो aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होड्
होड् (ऋ) होडृ r. 1st cl. (होडते)<BR>	 1. To go, to move.<BR>	 2. To disregard, to disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होड|होडः
होड m. (-डः) A raft, a float, a boat.<BR> E. होड् to go, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होडृ
होडृ m. (-डा) A robber, a footpad or highway robber.<BR> E. हुड् to collect, तृच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होढ|होढं
होढ mfn. (-ढः-ढा-ढं) Stolen.<BR>	 n. (-ढं) Stolen goods.<BR> E. हुड् to steal, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होतृ
होतृ m. (-ता)<BR>	 1. A priest who at a sacrifice recites the prayers of the<BR>Rig-Veda; one conversant with the Veda.<BR>	 2. A sacrificer.<BR>	 f. (-त्री)<BR>Adj. Sacrificing, offering oblation into fire.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice,<BR>Unādi aff. तृच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्र|होत्रं
होत्र n. (-त्रं)<BR>	 1. An article intended or fit for offering with fire, generally<BR>clarified butter.<BR>	 2. Burnt-offering, oblation with fire.<BR>	 f. (-त्रा) Praise.<BR>E. हु to sacrifice, ष्ट्रन् aff., टाप् added in the feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रीय|होत्रीयं|होत्रीयः
होत्रीय n. (-यं) A place where oblations are offered.<BR>	 m. (-यः) A priest<BR>offering an oblation.<BR> E. होत्र an offering, छ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होम|होमः
होम m. (-मः) Burnt-offering, the casting of clarified butter, &c., into<BR>the sacred fire, as an offering to the gods, accompanied with<BR>prayers or invocations, according to the object of the sacrifice. E.<BR>हु to sacrifice, मन् Unādi aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमकुण्ड|होमकुंड|होमकुण्डं
होमकुण्ड n. (-ण्डं) A hole in the ground or an altar, for receiving the<BR>fire for an oblation.<BR> E. होम burnt-offering, and कुण्ड a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमतुरङ्ग|होमतुरङ्गः
होमतुरङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः) A sacrificial horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमधान्य|होमधान्यं
होमधान्य n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. Sesamum.<BR>	 2. Barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमधूम|होमधूमः
होमधूम m. (-मः) The smoke of a burnt-offering, or of sacrificial fire.<BR> E. होम, धूम smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमभस्मन्
होमभस्मन् n. (-स्म) The ashes of a burnt-offering.<BR> E. होम, भस्मन् ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमवत्|होमवन्त्
होमवत् mfn. (-वान्-वती-वत्) Having performed sacrifice.<BR> E. होम, मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमवेला
होमवेला f. (-ला) The time of offering an oblation to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमाग्नि|होमाग्निः
होमाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) Sacrificial fire.<BR> E. होम an oblation, अग्नि fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमि|होमिः
होमि m. (-मिः)<BR>	 1. Clarified butter.<BR>	 2. Fire.<BR>	 3. Water.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice,<BR>मिन् aff., or इन aff, and मुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमिन्
होमिन् m. (-मी) The offerer of an oblation.<BR> E. हु to sacrifice, मिनि Unādi aff.; or होम, इनि aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होम्य|होम्यं
होम्य f. (-म्या) Belonging to or fit for an oblation.<BR> E. होम, यत् aff.; also<BR>होमीय f. (-या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होरा
होरा f. (-रा)<BR>	 1. The rising of a sign of the zodiac.<BR>	 2. Part of the<BR>duration of a sign, the twenty-fourth part of a day, an hour.<BR>	 3.<BR>A mark, a line.<BR>	 4. A science or work in science, (on astrology.) E.<BR>होड् to go, to proceed, affs. अच् and टाप्, and ड changed to र ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होलाका
होलाका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. The spring-festival held at the approach of the<BR>vernal season, the ceremony of throwing a red powder called Phāg,<BR>(held during the ten days preceding the full-moon-day of the<BR>month of Fālguna.)<BR>	 2. The full-moon-day in the month of<BR>Fālguna; also read होली f. (-ली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होहौ
होहौ Ind.<BR>	 1. An interjection of calling.<BR>	 2. An exclamation of<BR>challenging or defiance.<BR> E. हो, and हौ both the same.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौ
हौ Ind.<BR>	 1. An interjection of defiance or challenge.<BR>	 2. A vocative<BR>particle.<BR> E. ह्वेञ् to call, डौ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौड्
हौड् (ऋ) हौडृ r. 1st cl. (हौडते)<BR>	 1. To go.<BR>	 2. To disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौतृक|हौतृकः
हौतृक mfn. (-कः-की-कं) Relating or appertaining to the Hotṛ or<BR>priest so named.<BR> E. होतृ a priest, and ठञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौत्र|हौत्रं
हौत्र n. (-त्रं) The office of a Hotṛ-priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौम्य|हौम्यं
हौम्य n. (-म्यं) Clarified butter.<BR> E. होम burnt-offering, यञ् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौम्यधान्य|हौम्यधान्यं
हौम्यधान्य n. (-न्यं) Sesamum.<BR> E. हौम्य relating to burnt-offering, and धान्य grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नु
ह्नु r. 2nd cl. (ह्नुते)<BR>	 1. To take away, to rob.<BR>	 2. To withhold, to conceal.<BR>3. To hide from any one, (with a dative.) With अप prefixed, To<BR>conceal, to hide. With नि, 1. To conceal.<BR>	 2. To deny before any<BR>one, (with a dative.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नुति|ह्नुतिः
ह्नुति f. (-तिः)<BR>	 1. Concealment.<BR>	 2. Denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्मल्
ह्मल् r. 1st cl. (ह्मलति) To move, to shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्
ह्यस् Ind. Yesterday.<BR> E. अहन् a day, deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्तन|ह्यस्तनं
ह्यस्तन mfn. (-नः-नी-नं) Of yesterday, produced or occurred yesterday. E.<BR>ह्यस् yesterday, ट्युल् aff., तुट् augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्त्य|ह्यस्त्यः
ह्यस्त्य mfn. (-स्त्यः-स्त्या-स्त्यं) Of yesterday: see the last.<BR> E. ह्यस् yesterday, and त्यप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रग्
ह्रग् (ए) ह्रगे r. 1st cl. (ह्रगति) To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रणिया
ह्रणिया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Censure, reproach.<BR>	 2. Shame.<BR> E. हृणीङ् Kandwādi<BR>root, to feel ashamed, यक् aff., form irr.: see ह्रिणीया ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रद|ह्रदः
ह्रद m. (-दः)<BR>	 1. A deep lake, a large or deep piece of water.<BR>	 2. A ray<BR>of light.<BR> E. ह्राद् to sound, aff. अच्, and the deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रदग्रह|ह्रदग्रहः
ह्रदग्रह m. (-हः) An alligator, a crocodile.<BR> E. ह्नद a lake, and ग्रह abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रदिनी
ह्रदिनी m. (-नी)<BR>	 1. A river in general.<BR>	 2. Lightning.<BR> E. ह्रद deep water,<BR>इनि and ङीप् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रद्रोग|ह्रद्रोगः
ह्रद्रोग m. (-गः) The sign Aquarius of the zodiac: see हृद्रोग. The word is of Greek origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रप्
ह्रप् r. 10th cl. (ह्नापयति-ते) To speak articulately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्
ह्रस् r. 1st cl. (ह्रसति)<BR>	 1. To sound.<BR>	 2. To be small or few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसित
ह्रसित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made little, diminished.<BR>	 2. Sounded.<BR> E. ह्रस्<BR>to sound, &c., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसिमन्
ह्रसिमन् m. (-मा) Smallness, shortness.<BR> E. ह्रस्व short, small, इमनिच् aff., and ह्रस substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसिष्ठ|ह्रसिष्ठः
ह्रसिष्ठ mfn. (-ष्ठः-ष्ठा-ष्ठं) Very short or small.<BR> E. ह्रस्व short, aff. of the<BR>irr. superlative इष्ठन्, form irr.; also with ईयसुन् aff., ह्रसीयस् mfn.<BR>(-यान्-यसी-यः ।)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्व|ह्रस्वं|ह्रस्वः
ह्रस्व mfn. (-स्वः-स्वा-स्वं)<BR>	 1. Short, low in stature.<BR>	 2. Short, as a vowel.<BR>	 3.<BR>Small, little.<BR>	 m. (-स्वः) A dwarf.<BR> E. ह्रस् to be small, and वन् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वगर्भ|ह्रस्वगर्भः
ह्रस्वगर्भ m. (-र्भः) The Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वगवेधुका
ह्रस्वगवेधुका f. (-का) A plant, (Hedysarum lagopodioides.)<BR> E. ह्रस्व short,<BR>गवेधुका coix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वदर्भ|ह्रस्वदर्भः
ह्रस्वदर्भ m. (-र्भः) A short kind of Kuśa grass, the white sort.<BR> E. ह्रस्व short, दर्भ Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वपत्रक|ह्रस्वपत्रकः
ह्रस्वपत्रक m. (-कः) A sort of Bassia.<BR> E. ह्रस्व short, पत्र a leaf, कन् added.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वशाखाशिफ|ह्रस्वशाखाशिफः
ह्रस्वशाखाशिफ m. (-फः) A bush, a shrub.<BR> E. ह्रस्व short, शाखा a branch,<BR>and शिफा a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वाग्नि|ह्रस्वाग्निः
ह्रस्वाग्नि m. (-ग्निः) The gigantic Asclepias, (A. gigantea.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वाङ्ग|ह्रस्वांग|ह्रस्वाङ्गः
ह्रस्वाङ्ग m. (-ङ्गः)<BR>	 1. A medicinal root, commonly Jivaka.<BR>	 2. A dwarf.<BR>E. ह्रस्व short, and अङ्ग the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्राद्
ह्राद् r. 1st cl. (ह्रादते) To sound inarticulately, to roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्राद|ह्रादः
ह्राद m. (-दः) Noise, sound.<BR> E. ह्राद् to sound, aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रादिन्
ह्रादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Sounding, making a sound or noise.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>1. Lightning.<BR>	 2. INDRA'S thunderbolt.<BR>	 3. A river in general.<BR>	 4.<BR>The Olibanum tree: see ह्लादिनी.<BR> E. ह्राद् to sound inarticulately, affs.<BR>इनि and ङीप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रास|ह्रासः
ह्रास m. (-सः)<BR>	 1. Sound, noise.<BR>	 2. Decline, decrease, deterioration.<BR> E. ह्रस् to sound, &c., aff. घञ् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिणी
ह्रिणी (ह्रिणीयते) To feel ashamed. A Kandwādī root: see हृणी, य is<BR>always added on the base in the case of this root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिणीया
ह्रिणीया f. (-या)<BR>	 1. Censure, abuse.<BR>	 2. Shame.<BR> E. हृणीङ् to be ashamed,<BR>aff. यक्, the vowel changed to रि; otherwise हृणीया; or ह्रिणीङ्-यक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रित|ह्रितः
ह्रित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Ashamed, modest, bashful.<BR>	 2. Divided,<BR>portioned.<BR>	 3. Taken, conveyed.<BR>	 n. (-तं) A portion, a share.<BR> E. ह्री<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">Page839-a+ 31</a>]<BR>to be ashamed, क्त aff., and the vowel made short; or हृ to take,<BR>aff. क्त, and रि substituted for ऋ ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=838-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिति|ह्रितिः
ह्रिति f. (-तिः) Taking, conveying.<BR> E. रि substituted for ऋः see हृति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रियमाण
ह्रियमाण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं)<BR>	 1. Being taken or seized.<BR>	 2. Being captivated,<BR>attracted, &c.<BR> E. हृ to take, pass. v., शानच् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिवेर|ह्रिवेरं
ह्रिवेर n. (-रं) A perfume. E. see ह्रीवेर ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्री
ह्री r. 3rd cl. (-जिह्रेति) To be modest, to blush.<BR>	 2. To be ashamed of, (with an ablative or genitive.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्री
ह्री f. (-ह्रीः) Shame, bashfulness.<BR> E. ह्री to be ashamed, aff. क्विप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीका
ह्रीका f. (-का)<BR>	 1. Modesty, shame, shyness.<BR>	 2. Fear, terror, timidity. E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, Unādi aff. कक्; also र changed to ल, ह्लीका ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीकु|ह्रीकुः
ह्रीकु mfn. (-कुः-कुः-कु) Ashamed, modest.<BR>	 m. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. Lac.<BR>	 2. Tin.<BR> E. ह्री<BR>to be ashamed, Unādi aff. उन्, कुक् augment: see ह्लीकु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीच्छ्|ह्रीछ्
ह्रीच्छ् r. 1st cl. (ह्रीच्छति) To be modest or ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीजित|ह्रीजितः
ह्रीजित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Modest, ashamed.<BR> E. ह्री shame, and, जित overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीण|ह्रीणः
ह्रीण mfn. (-णः-णा-णं) Ashamed, bashful.<BR> E. ह्री to be ashamed, aff. क्त,<BR>and त changed to ण; deriv. irr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीत|ह्रीतः
ह्रीत mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Ashamed, bashful, modest.<BR> E. ह्री to be ashamed, aff. क्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीनिरास|ह्रीनिरासः
ह्रीनिरास m. (-सः) Shamelessness.<BR> E. ह्री, and निरास throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीमत्|ह्रीमन्त्
ह्रीमत् mfn. (-मान्-मती-मत्) Bashful, modest, ashamed.<BR> E. ह्री, and मतुप् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीयन्त्रणा|ह्रीयंत्रणा
ह्रीयन्त्रणा f. (-णा) The constraint of bashfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीवेर|ह्रीवेरं
ह्रीवेर n. (-रं) A drug and perfume, Commonly Bālā.<BR> E. ह्री shame, and<BR>वेर saffron: see the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीवेल|ह्रीवेलं
ह्रीवेल n. (-लं) A drug and perfume: see the last.<BR> E. ह्रीवेर as before, र<BR>changed to ल; also with कन् added, ह्रीवेलक ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रुड्
ह्रुड् (ऋ) ह्रुडृ r. 1st cl. (ह्रोडते)<BR>	 1. To collect.<BR>	 2. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रूड्
ह्रूड् (ऋ) ह्रूडृ r. 1st cl. (ह्रूडति)<BR>	 1. To collect.<BR>	 2. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेप्
ह्रेप् (ऋ) ह्रेपृ r. 1st cl. (ह्रेपते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेपण|ह्रेपणं
ह्रेपण n. (-ण) Putting to shame, excelling, surpassing.<BR> E. ह्री to be ashamed, causal v., ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेपयत्
ह्रेपयत् mfn. (-यन्-यन्ती-यत्) Putting to shame, outvieing, surpassing. E.<BR>ह्री to be ashamed, causal v., शतृ aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीपित
ह्रीपित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं)<BR>	 1. Made ashamed, put to shame.<BR>	 2. Excelled,<BR>surpassed.<BR> E. ह्री to be ashamed, causal v., क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेष्
ह्रेष् (ऋ) ह्रेषृ r. 1st cl. (ह्रेषते)<BR>	 1. To sound inarticulately, to neigh, (as<BR>horse.)<BR>	 2. To go, to move.<BR>	 3. To creep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेषा
ह्रेषा f. (-षा) Neighing as a horse.<BR> E. ह्रेष् to neigh, affs. अ and टाप् see हेषा; also read ह्लेषा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रोड्
ह्रोड् (ऋ) ह्रोडृ r. 1st cl. (ह्रोडति) To go, to move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रौड्
ह्रौड् (ऋ) हौडृ r. 1st cl. (ह्रौडते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लग्
ह्लग् (ए) ह्णगे r. 1st cl. (ह्लगति) To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लप्
ह्लप् r. 10th cl. (ह्लापयति-ते) To speak, to speak articulately: also ह्रप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लस्
ह्लस् r. 1st cl. (ह्लसति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लाद्
ह्लाद् (ई) ह्लादी r. 1st cl. (ह्लादते)<BR>	 1. To gladden, to delight.<BR>	 2. To be glad<BR>or delighted.<BR>	 3. To sound, especially as a musical instrument.<BR>With आ, To be delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लाद|ह्लादः
ह्लाद m. (-दः) Pleasure, joy.<BR> E. ह्लाद् to be glad, aff. अच् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादन|ह्लादनं
ह्लादन n. (-नं) Joy, delight.<BR> E. ह्लाद् to be glad, and ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादित
ह्लादित mfn. (-तः-ता-तं) Delighted, happy.<BR> E. ह्लाद् to be happy, क्त aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादिन्
ह्लादिन् mfn. (-दी-दिनी-दि) Happy, glad.<BR>	 f. (-नी)<BR>	 1. Lightning.<BR>	 2. INDRA'S<BR>thunderbolt.<BR>	 3. A river in general.<BR>	 4. The Olibanum tree: see<BR>ह्रादिनी.<BR> E. ह्लाद् pleasure, इनि and ङीष् affs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लीका
ह्लीका f. (-का) Shame, modesty.<BR> E. ह्री to be ashamed, कन् Unādi aff. र changed to ल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लीकु|ह्लीकुः
ह्लीकु mfn. (-कुः-कुः-कु) Ashamed, modest.<BR>	 m. (-कुः)<BR>	 1. Lac.<BR>	 2. Tin.<BR> E. ह्री<BR>to be ashamed, aff. कुक्, र changed to ल; otherwise read ह्रीकु ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लेषा
ह्लेषा f. (-षा) Neighing, (as a horse,) braying, (as an ass, &c.)<BR> E. ह्लेष् for<BR>ह्रेष् to neigh, &c., affs. अ and टाप् ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वल्
ह्वल् r. 1st cl. (-ह्वलति)<BR>	 1. To move.<BR>	 2. To shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वान|ह्वानं
ह्वान n. (-नं)<BR>	 1. The act of calling.<BR>	 2. A cry.<BR> E. ह्वे to call, ल्युट् aff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वृ
ह्वृ r. 1st cl. (ह्वरति)<BR>	 1. To bend, to curve, to make crooked.<BR>	 2. To be<BR>crooked in conduct, to deceive.<BR>	 3. To be injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वे
ह्वे r. 1st cl. (ह्वयति-ते)<BR>	 1. To call.<BR>	 2. To invoke, to call upon.<BR>	 3. To<BR>challenge.<BR>	 4. To name.<BR>	 5. To ask, to beg.<BR>	 6. To emulate, to vie<BR>with, to wish to overcome or surpass.<BR>	 7. To struggle or contend<BR>with. With आ, To call, to invite. With सम्, To call out together.<BR>With उप, नि, वि or सम्, the verb is deponent, (उपह्वयते); also with<BR>आङ् if rivalry be signified, (आह्वयते) He challenges.<BR>THE END.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=SHS&page=839-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=shs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

